window.BAHR_DATA=window.BAHR_DATA||{};window.BAHR_DATA["search"]=[{"kind":"passage","id":"preface","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"Author’s preface preface","anchor":"unit-preface"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-1","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم (وصلى الله على سيدنا محمد وعلى آله وصحبه وسلّم) قال الشيخ الإمام الحبر الهمام، العارف الرباني والقطب الصمداني، قدوة السالكين ومنار الواصلين، بحر العرفان، ومشرق شمس العيان، مهيع الطريقة، الجامع بين الشريعة وبحر الحقيقة، أبو العباس أحمد بن محمد بن عجيبة الحسنى- رضى الله عنه وأرضاه- آمين:","anchor":"ar-preface-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-2","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"نحمدك يا من تجلّى لعباده فى كلامه، بكمال بهائه وجماله، وفتق ألسنة العلماء النحارير لاستخراج درره ولآلئه، وفجّر قلوبهم بينابيع الحكم المؤيدة بأصوله ومبانيه، واستفادوا عند غوصهم فى تياره من فرائده ومثانيه، فدحضوا بآياته الباهرة، وحججه الظاهرة القاهرة شبه من يناويه ويعانيه، والكلّ معترف بالتقصير، مغترف على حسب الفهم والتيسير، من بحر أسراره ومعانيه، فهو البحر الطام الذي لا يدرك له قعر، والروض المونق الذي لا يعدم منه زهر ولا نور، وكيف لا، وهو كلام مولانا العالم بالخفيات، وبما كان وما هو الآن وما هو آت؟!.","anchor":"ar-preface-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-3","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"والصلاة والسلام على سيدنا ومولانا محمد، مظهر الرحمات، المبعوث بخوارق العادات ولوامع البينات، وعلى آله وأصحابه أولى النّدى والسماحة، وجبال اليقين فى اشتداد الأزمات وتفاقم المعضلات.","anchor":"ar-preface-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-4","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"وبعد ... فإن علم تفسير القرآن من أجلّ العلوم، وأفضل ما ينفق فيه نتائج الأفكار وقرائح الفهوم، ولكن لا يتقدم لهذا الخطر الكبير إلا العالم النّحرير، الذي رسخت أقدامه فى العلوم الظاهرة، وجالت أفكاره فى معانى القرآن الباهرة، بعد أن تضلّع من العلم الظاهر، عربية وتصريفا ولغة وبيانا، وفقها وحديثا وتاريخا، يكون أخذ ذلك من أفواه الرجال، ثم غاص فى علوم التصوف ذوقا وحالا ومقاما، بصحبة أهل الأذواق من أهل الكمال، وإلا فسكوته عن هذا الأمر العظيم أسلم، واشتغاله بما يقدر عليه من علم الشريعة الظاهرة أتم.","anchor":"ar-preface-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-5","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"واعلم أن القرآن العظيم له ظاهر لأهل الظاهر، وباطن لأهل الباطن، وتفسير أهل الباطن لا يذوقه إلا أهل الباطن، لا يفهمه غيرهم ولا يذوقه سواهم، ولا يصح ذكره إلا بعد تقرير الظاهر، ثم يشير إلى علم الباطن بعبارة رقيقة وإشارة دقيقة، فمن لم يبلغ فهمه لذوق تلك الأسرار فليسلّم، ولا يبادر بالإنكار فإنّ علم الأذواق من وراء طور العقول، ولا يدرك بتواتر النقول.","anchor":"ar-preface-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-6","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"قال في لطائف المنن: اعلم أن تفسير هذه الطائفة- يعنى الصوفية- لكلام الله وكلام رسوله صلى الله عليه وسلّم بالمعاني الغريبة ليس إحالة للظاهر عن ظاهره، ولكن ظاهر الآية مفهوم منه ما جاءت الآية له ودلت عليه فى حرف اللسان،","anchor":"ar-preface-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-7","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"وثمّ أفهام باطنة تفهم عند الآية والحديث لمن فتح الله قلبه، وقد جاء أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- قال: «لِكلِّ آيةٍ ظَاهرٌ وبَاطِنٌ وحدّ ومُطلع» . فلا يصدّنك عن تلقى المعاني الغريبة منهم أن يقول لك ذو جدل ومعارضة: هذا إحالة لكلام الله- عزّ وجل- وكلام رسوله صلى الله عليه وسلّم فليس بإحالة، وإنما يكون إحالة لكلام الله لو قالوا: لا معنى للآية إلا هذا، وهم لا يقولون ذلك. بل يقرّون الظواهر على ظواهرها ومراداتها وموضوعاتها، ويفهمون عن الله ما أفهمهم. هـ.","anchor":"ar-preface-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-8","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"وقال سعد الدين فى شرح عقائد النسفي- بعد إبطال الإلحاد-: (وأمّا ما يذهب إليه بعض المحققين من أن النصوص على ظواهرها، ومع ذلك ففيها إشارات خفية إلى حقائق تنكشف لأرباب السلوك، يمكن التطبيق بينها وبين الظواهر المرادة، فهو من كمال الإيمان ومحض العرفان) وقوله: يمكن التطبيق ... إلخ، أي: يمكن أن يشار إليها فى باطن الخطاب بحيث لا ينبو عنها سرّ الخطاب، ولا يبعد اللفظ عنها كل البعد حتى يكون تحريفا.","anchor":"ar-preface-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-9","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"وقال الشيخ زرّوق رضى الله عنه: نظر الصوفي أخص من نظر المفسر وصاحب فقه الحديث، لأن كلا منهما يعتبر الحكم والمعنى ليس إلا وهو يزيد بطلب الإشارة بعد إثبات ما أثبتاه. وإلّا فهو باطني خارج عن الشريعة فضلا عن المتصوفة. والله أعلم. هـ.","anchor":"ar-preface-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-10","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"وقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لِكلِّ آيةٍ ظَاهرٌ وبَاطِنٌ وحدّ ومُطلع» فالظاهر لمن اعتنى بظاهر اللفظ، كالنحاة وأهل اللغة والتصريف، والباطن لمن اعتنى بمعنى اللفظ، وما دلّ عليه الكلام من الأمر والنهى والقصص والأخبار والتوحيد، وغير ذلك من علوم القرآن، وهو نظر المفسرين. والحدّ لمن اعتنى باستنباط الأحكام منه، وهم الفقهاء، فهم ينتهون إلى ما يدل عليه اللفظ وسيق لأجله، دون زيادة عليه. والمطّلع لأهل الحقائق من أكابر الصوفية، لأنهم يطلعون من ظاهر الآية إلى باطنها، فيكشف لهم عن أسرار وعلوم وغوامض، تتجلى لهم عند استعمال الفكرة فيها.","anchor":"ar-preface-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-11","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"قال فى الصّحاح: فى الحديث: «من هول المطّلع» ، شبّه ما أشرف عليه من أمر الآخرة بالمطّلع وهو المأتى.","anchor":"ar-preface-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-12","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"يقال: أين مطلع هذا الأمر؟ أي: مأتاه، وهو موضع الاطلاع من إشراف إلى انحدار. هـ لأن أهل الحقائق يشرفون من ظاهر الآية إلى أسرار باطنها، ويغوصون فى لجج بحرها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-preface-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-13","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"هذا ... وقد ندبنى شيخى العارف الرباني سيدي محمد البوزيدي الحسني، وكذلك شيخه القطب الجامع شيخ المشايخ مولاي العربي الدرقاوي الحسني، أن أضع تفسيرا يكون جامعا بين تفسير أهل الظاهر وإشارة أهل الباطن، فأجبت سؤالهم وأسعفت طلبتهم، رجاء أن يعمّ به الانتفاع، ويكون ممتعا للقلوب والأسماع. مقدّما في كل آية ما يتعلق بمهمّ العربية واللغة، ثم بمعاني الألفاظ الظاهرة، ثم بالإشارات الباطنة. متوسطا فى ذلك بين الإطناب","anchor":"ar-preface-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-14","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"والاختصار. منتظرا فى ذلك كله ما يفتح علىّ من خزائن الكريم الغفار.. وسميته (البحر المديد في تفسير القرآن المجيد) نسأل الله أن يكسوه جلباب القبول، وأن يبلغ فيه القصد المأمول، إنه على ما يشاء قدير، وبالإجابة جدير، ولا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله العلي العظيم. وصلى الله على سيدنا محمد وآله وصحبه وسلم.","anchor":"ar-preface-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-preface-15","r":"preface","title":"Author’s preface","text":"وقد ذكرت في تفسير الفاتحة الكبير عشر مقدمات تتعلق بأصول العلوم وتفاريعها، وعلوم القرآن وأصل منابعها، فلينظرها من أرادها. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-preface-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-preface-s1","r":"preface","title":"The transmitted opening","text":"In the Name of God, the Compassionate, the Merciful. God bless our master Muḥammad, his family and his Companions, and grant them peace. The shaykh, imam, eminent and resolute scholar, God-knowing master and divinely sustained pole, exemplar of wayfarers and beacon of those who have arrived, ocean of gnosis and dawning-place of the sun of direct vision, broad highway of the Path, who unites the Sacred Law with the ocean of Reality—Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAjība al-Ḥasanī, may God be pleased with him and grant him His good pleasure, amen—said: [P01]","anchor":"en-preface-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-preface-s2","r":"preface","title":"The divine speech and the sciences of interpretation","text":"We praise You, O You who disclose Yourself to Your servants in Your speech, in the perfection of Your splendour and beauty; who loose the tongues of consummate scholars to bring forth its pearls and precious gems, and cause springs of wisdom to gush from their hearts, sustained by its principles and foundations. As they dive into its current, they draw benefit from its unique treasures and reiterated teachings. With its dazzling signs and its manifest, overwhelming proofs, they refute the doubts of those who oppose and resist it. Yet all acknowledge their inadequacy, each drawing from the ocean of its mysteries and meanings according to the understanding and facility granted him. It is the surging ocean whose bottom cannot be reached, the delightful garden never without blossom or flower. And how could it be otherwise, when it is the speech of our Master, who knows hidden things, what has been, what now is, and what is to come? Blessings and peace be upon our master and patron Muḥammad, the manifestation of mercies, sent with wonders that breach the customary order ( خوارق العادات ) and the radiance of clear proofs; and upon his family and Companions, the possessors of generosity and open-handedness, mountains of certainty amid intensifying crises and ever more difficult perplexities. To proceed: the science of interpreting the Qurʾān ( علم تفسير القرآن ) is among the noblest sciences, and among the best pursuits upon which to expend the fruits of reflection and the inventive powers of understanding. Yet none should advance to this momentous undertaking except the consummate scholar whose feet are firmly planted in the outward sciences ( العلوم الظاهرة ) and whose thought has ranged through the Qurʾān’s resplendent meanings. He must first have drunk deeply of outward learning: Arabic grammar, morphology, lexicography and rhetoric, jurisprudence, hadith and history—having received these from the mouths of men. He must then have plunged into the sciences of Sufism ( علوم التصوف ), in tasting, state and station ( ذوقًا وحالًا ومقامًا ), through the companionship of perfected people of spiritual tasting ( أهل الأذواق ). Otherwise, silence concerning this tremendous matter is safer for him, and occupation with whatever he can manage of the outward Sacred Law is more fitting. Know that the mighty Qurʾān has an outward aspect ( ظاهر ) for the people of the outward and an inward aspect ( باطن ) for the people of the inward. The interpretation offered by the people of the inward is tasted only by the people of the inward: others neither understand it nor taste it. Nor is it sound to set it forth before establishing the outward meaning. Thereafter one may indicate inward knowledge through a delicate expression and a subtle allusion ( إشارة ). Let anyone whose understanding does not reach the tasting of those mysteries yield assent, rather than hasten to deny them. For the knowledge of spiritual tastings ( علم الأذواق ) lies beyond the compass of discursive intellects and is not attained through the successive transmission of reports. [P02]","anchor":"en-preface-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-preface-s3","r":"preface","title":"The inward sense does not abolish the outward sense","text":"He says in Laṭāʾif al-minan : “Know that this community’s interpretation”—meaning the Sufis—“of the speech of God and of His Messenger, God bless him and grant him peace, through unfamiliar meanings is not a diversion of the outward sense from its outward meaning. Rather, the outward aspect of the verse conveys what the verse was revealed for and what it indicates in the language’s expression. “There are also inward understandings apprehended on hearing a verse or a hadith by those whose hearts God has opened. It has been related that he, blessings and peace be upon him, said: ‘Every verse has an outward aspect, an inward aspect, a limit, and a point of ascent ( ظاهر وباطن وحدّ ومطّلع ).’ Do not let a contentious opponent turn you away from receiving unfamiliar meanings from them by saying, ‘This diverts the speech of God, mighty and majestic, and the speech of His Messenger, God bless him and grant him peace.’ It is no such diversion. It would be a diversion of God’s speech only were they to say, ‘The verse has no meaning except this.’ They do not say that. Rather, they confirm the outward senses in their outward meanings, intentions and proper applications, and understand from God what He has enabled them to understand.” End of quotation. [P03] Saʿd al-Dīn says in his commentary upon al-Nasafī’s Creed , after refuting impious distortion ( الإلحاد ): “As for the view of certain realized authorities that scriptural texts retain their outward meanings, while also containing hidden allusions to realities unveiled to the people of wayfaring, which can be reconciled with the intended outward senses, this is of the perfection of faith and pure gnosis.” [XVI-N001] His words “can be reconciled,” and what follows, mean that these realities may be indicated within the inward dimension of the discourse in such a way that the discourse’s secret sense does not reject them, and the wording is not wholly remote from them, which would amount to distortion ( تحريف ). Shaykh Zarrūq, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Sufi’s consideration is more particular than that of the exegete and the interpreter of hadith: each of those considers the ruling and the meaning, and no more, whereas the Sufi adds the search for the allusion after affirming what they have affirmed. Otherwise he is an esotericist ( باطني ), outside the Sacred Law, let alone the Sufis. And God knows best.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-preface-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-preface-s4","r":"preface","title":"Outward aspect, inward aspect, limit and point of ascent","text":"Concerning his saying, blessings and peace be upon him, “Every verse has an outward aspect, an inward aspect, a limit, and a point of ascent”: the outward aspect belongs to those concerned with the wording’s outward form, such as the grammarians, lexicographers and morphologists. The inward aspect belongs to those concerned with the wording’s meaning and what the discourse indicates of command, prohibition, narratives, reports, the affirmation of divine unity ( التوحيد ), and the other sciences of the Qurʾān. This is the exegetes’ consideration. The limit ( الحدّ ) belongs to those concerned to derive rulings from it—the jurists—who stop at what the wording indicates and the purpose for which it is expressed, without adding to it. The point of ascent ( المطّلع ) belongs to the people of realities ( أهل الحقائق ), the great Sufis: they look through the verse’s outward aspect into its inward aspect, and mysteries, sciences and subtle matters are unveiled to them, disclosed when they exercise contemplative reflection ( الفكرة ) upon it. [P04] He says in al-Ṣiḥāḥ : “In the report, ‘from the terror of the place of arrival ( المطّلع ),’ the affairs of the Hereafter upon which one is about to look are likened to a muṭṭalaʿ , that is, a place of approach. One says, ‘Where is the muṭṭalaʿ of this affair?’ meaning, ‘Where is its point of approach?’ It is the place from which one looks down from a height.” End of quotation. For the people of realities look from the verse’s outward aspect into the mysteries of its inward aspect, and dive into the surging depths of its ocean. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-preface-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-preface-s5","r":"preface","title":"The commission and arrangement of this commentary","text":"Now my shaykh, the God-knowing, divinely nurtured master Sīdī Muḥammad al-Būzīdī al-Ḥasanī, and likewise his shaykh, the all-embracing pole, master of masters, Mawlāy al-ʿArabī al-Darqāwī al-Ḥasanī, charged me to compose a commentary uniting the interpretation of the people of the outward with the allusion of the people of the inward. I answered their request and fulfilled their wish, hoping that its benefit would extend widely, and that it would delight hearts and ears. For each verse I place first the important matters of Arabic expression and language, then the outward meanings of its words, and then the inward allusions, steering a middle course between prolixity and excessive brevity. In all this I await whatever is opened to me from the treasuries of the Generous, the All-Forgiving. I have called it al-Baḥr al-madīd fī tafsīr al-Qurʾān al-majīd — The Vast Ocean: An Interpretation of the Glorious Qurʾān . We ask God to clothe it in the robe of acceptance and bring to fulfilment the purpose for which it is hoped. He has power over whatever He wills and is worthy to answer. There is no power and no strength except through God, the Most High, the Tremendous. God bless our master Muḥammad, his family and his Companions, and grant them peace. In my larger commentary upon al-Fātiḥa I have set out ten introductions concerning the principles of the sciences and their branches, and the sciences of the Qurʾān and the sources from which they spring. Let anyone who desires them consult them there. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-preface-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"fatiha","r":"fatiha","title":"Sūrat al-Fātiḥa — introduction, names and background","text":"Sūrat al-Fātiḥa — introduction, names and background Introductory discussion","anchor":"unit-fatiha"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha-1","r":"fatiha","title":"Sūrat al-Fātiḥa — introduction, names and background","text":"سورة الفاتحة","anchor":"ar-fatiha-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha-2","r":"fatiha","title":"Sūrat al-Fātiḥa — introduction, names and background","text":"مكية. ولها عشرة أسماء: الفاتحة والوافية والكافية والشافية، والسبع المثاني لأنها سبع آيات عند الشافعي منها البسملة، وأسقطها مالك وجعل السابعة: غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ الآية، أو تثنى فى كل صلاة، أو لاشتمالها على الثناء على الله. وأمّ القرآن لأنها مفتتحه ومبدؤه، أو لأنها اشتملت على ما فيه إجمالا على ما يأتى، وسورة الحمد والشكر، وسورة تعليم المسألة، وسورة الصلاة لتكريرها فيها، وأساس القرآن لأنها أصله ومبدؤه ويبنى سائره عليها.","anchor":"ar-fatiha-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha-4","r":"fatiha","title":"Sūrat al-Fātiḥa — introduction, names and background","text":"واتفقت المصاحف على افتتاحها ب","anchor":"ar-fatiha-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha-s1","r":"fatiha","title":"Introduction: names and verse-counting","text":"I:52 It is Meccan. It has ten names: the Opening ( الفاتحة ); the Complete ( الوافية ); the Sufficient ( الكافية ); the Healing ( الشافية ); and the Seven Oft-Repeated ( السبع المثاني ). It is called the Seven Oft-Repeated because, according to al-Shāfiʿī, it consists of seven verses with the basmala counted among them, whereas Mālik does not count the basmala and makes “not those upon whom wrath has fallen, nor those who are astray” the seventh verse; or because it is repeated in every prayer; or because it contains praise of God ( الثناء ), with an evident play upon the name al-mathānī. It is also called the Mother of the Qurʾān ( أم القرآن ), because it is the Qurʾān's opening and beginning, or because it contains in summary what the Qurʾān contains, as will be explained; the Sūrah of Praise and Thanksgiving; the Sūrah of Teaching How to Ask; the Sūrah of Prayer, because it is repeatedly recited therein; and the Foundation of the Qurʾān, because it is its root and beginning, upon which the rest is built.","anchor":"en-fatiha-s1"},{"kind":"passage","id":"fatiha_1","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary 1:1","anchor":"unit-fatiha_1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-1","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ واختلف الأئمة فيها، فقال مالك: ليست آية لا من الفاتحة ولا من غيرها إلا من النمل خاصة، وقال الشافعي: هى آية من الفاتحة فقط، وقال ابن عباس: هي آية من كل سورة.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-2","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"فحجة مالك: ما فى الصحيح عنه صلى الله عليه وسلّم قال: «أنزلت علىّ سورة ليس في التوراة ولا في الإنجيل ولا في الفرقان مثلها، ثم قال: الحمد لله رب العالمين) ولم يذكر البسملة. وكذلك ما ورد فى الصحيح أيضا أن الله يقول: «قسمت الصّلاة بينى وبين عبدى نصفين. يقول العبد: الحمد لله رب العالمين» فبدأ بها دون البسملة.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-3","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"وحجة الشافعي: ما ورد فى الصحيح «إن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم كان يقرأ بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم. الحمد لله رب العالمين» . وحجة ابن عباس: ثبوت البسملة مع كل سورة فى المصحف، مع تحرّى الصحابة ألا يدخلوا فى المصحف غير كلام الله، وقالوا: ما بين الدفّتين كلام الله.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-4","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"وإذا ابتدأت أوّل سورة بسملت إلا براءة، وسيأتى الكلام عليها. وإذا ابتدأت جزء سورة فأنت مخير عند الجمهور.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-5","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"وإذا أتممت سورة وابتدأت أخرى فاختلف القرّاء فى البسملة وتركها.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-6","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"وأما حكمها فى الصلاة، فقال مالك: مكروهة فى الفرض دون النفل، وقال الشافعي: فرض تبطل الصلاة بتركها، فيبسمل- عنده- جهرا فى الجهر وسرا فى السر، وعند أبى حنيفة كذلك إلا أنه يسرّها مطلقا، وحجة مالك أنها ليست بآية: ما فى الحديث الصحيح عن أنس أنه قال: (صلّيت خلف النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم وأبى بكر وعمر وعثمان، فكانوا يستفتحون بالحمد لله رب العالمين) لا يذكرون البسملة أصلا. وحجة الشافعي أنها عنده آية: ما ورد فى الحديث من قراءتها كما تقدم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-7","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"ولم تكن البسملة قبل الإسلام، فكانوا يكتبون: باسمك اللهم، حتى نزلت بِسْمِ اللَّهِ مَجْراها فكتبوا بِسْمِ اللَّهِ حتى نزل: ... أَوِ ادْعُوا الرَّحْمنَ فكتبوا: بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمنِ حتى نزل: ... وَإِنَّهُ بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ، فكتبوها.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-8","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"وحذفت الألف لكثرة الاستعمال، والباء متعلقة بمحذوف، اسم عند البصريين، أي: ابتدائى كائن بسم الله، فموضعها رفع. وفعل عند الكوفيين، أي: أبدأ أو أتلو. فيقدّر كل واحد ما جعلت البسملة مبدأ له، فموضعها نصب، ويقدر مؤخرا لإفادة الحصر والاختصاص. وهو مشتق من السّموّ عند البصريين، فلامه محذوفة، وعند الكوفيين من السّمة، أي: العلامة، ففاؤه محذوفة، ودليل البصريين: التصغير والتكسير، فقالوا: أسماء، ولم يقولوا أوسام، وقالوا:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-9","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"سمى، ولم يقولوا: وسيم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-10","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"و (الله) علم على الذات الواجبة الوجود، المستحق لجميع المحامد، وهل هو مشتق أو مرتجل؟ قولان يأتى الكلام عليهما فى (الحمد لله) ، وكذلك (الرحمن الرحيم) .","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_1-11","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:1 — commentary","text":"قال الحق جل جلاله:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_1-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_1-s1","r":"fatiha_1","title":"The basmala: Qurʾānic status and evidence","text":"The written copies of the Qurʾān agree in opening it with “In the Name of God, the Compassionate, the Merciful.” The imams disagree concerning this formula. Mālik said that it is not a verse of al-Fātiḥa or of any other sūrah, except in al-Naml alone. Al-Shāfiʿī said that it is a verse of al-Fātiḥa alone. Ibn ʿAbbās said that it is a verse of every sūrah. Mālik's evidence is the authentic report in which the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A sūrah has been sent down to me whose like is not in the Torah, the Gospel, or the Criterion.” He then said, “Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds,” without mentioning the basmala. There is likewise the authentic report that God says: “I have divided the prayer between Myself and My servant into two halves. The servant says, ‘Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds.’” He thus begins with this, without the basmala. Al-Shāfiʿī's evidence is the authentic report that the Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite: “In the Name of God, the Compassionate, the Merciful. Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds.” Ibn ʿAbbās's evidence is that the basmala is written with every sūrah in the written copy of the Qurʾān, despite the Companions' care not to introduce anything into it other than God's speech. They said: “What is between the two covers is God's speech.”","anchor":"en-fatiha_1-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_1-s2","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Recitation and prayer rulings","text":"When you begin at the opening of a sūrah, recite the basmala, except in Barāʾa [al-Tawba], which will be discussed in its place. When you begin within a sūrah, the majority give you a choice. When you complete one sūrah and begin another, the Qurʾānic readers differ over whether to recite or omit the basmala. As for its ruling in prayer, Mālik said that it is disliked in obligatory prayer, but not in voluntary prayer. Al-Shāfiʿī said that it is obligatory and that omitting it invalidates the prayer. According to him, therefore, one recites it aloud in audible prayer and silently in silent prayer. With Abū Ḥanīfa it is likewise, except that he recites it silently in every case. Mālik's evidence that it is not a verse is the authentic report from Anas, who said: “I prayed behind the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān, and they used to begin with ‘Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds,’” not mentioning the basmala at all. Al-Shāfiʿī's evidence that it is a verse, in his view, is the report of its recitation already mentioned.","anchor":"en-fatiha_1-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_1-s3","r":"fatiha_1","title":"History of the written formula","text":"I:53 The basmala was not in use before Islam. People used to write, “In Your Name, O God,” until “In the Name of God is its sailing” [11:41] was revealed, whereupon they wrote, “In the Name of God.” Then “or call upon the All-Merciful” [17:110] was revealed, and they wrote, “In the Name of God, the All-Merciful.” Finally, “and it is: In the Name of God, the All-Merciful, the Ever-Merciful” [27:30] was revealed, and they wrote it in this form.","anchor":"en-fatiha_1-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_1-s4","r":"fatiha_1","title":"Grammar and derivation of the basmala","text":"The alif of ism in bism is omitted because of frequent usage. The preposition bāʾ is connected to an elided governing element ( متعلِّقة بمحذوف ). According to the Basrans, the ellipsis is nominal: “My beginning is [made] in the Name of God” ( ابتدائي كائن بسم الله ), so its syntactic locus is nominative ( موضعها الرفع ). According to the Kufans, the ellipsis is verbal: “I begin” or “I recite,” so each speaker supplies the action for which the basmala is made the beginning, and its syntactic locus is accusative ( موضعها النصب ). The omitted element is understood after the basmala in order to convey restriction ( الحصر ) and exclusive specification ( الاختصاص ). According to the Basrans, ism (“name”) is derived ( مشتق ) from sumuww (“elevation”), with the final radical - the lām of the root ( لام الكلمة ) - omitted. According to the Kufans it is derived from sima (“mark, sign”; السِّمة، أي العلامة ), with the first radical - the fāʾ of the root ( فاء الكلمة ) - omitted. The Basrans appeal to the diminutive ( التصغير ) and the broken plural ( التكسير ): one says asmāʾ, not awsām, and sumayy, not wusaym. “God” ( الله ) is a proper name ( عَلَم ) for the Essence that is Necessary in Existence ( الذات الواجبة الوجود ) and deserving of every praise. Whether the name is derived ( مشتق ) or independently coined ( مرتجل ) is disputed. The two positions will be discussed under “Praise belongs to God,” as will the names al-Raḥmān and al-Raḥīm. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says:","anchor":"en-fatiha_1-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"fatiha_2","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary 1:2–4","anchor":"unit-fatiha_2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-1","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ (2) الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ (3) مالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ (4)","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-2","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"قلت: (الحمد) مبتدأ، و (لله) خبر، وأصله النصب، وقرئ به، والأصل: أحمد الله حمداً، وإنما عدل عنه إلى الرفع ليدل على عموم الحمد وثباته، دون تجدده وحدوثه، وفيه تعليم اللفظ مع تعريض الاستغناء. أي: الحمد لله وإن لم تحمدوه. ولو قال (أحمد الله) لما أفاد هذا المعنى، وهو من المصادر التي تُنْصَب بأفعال مضمرة لا تكاد تذكر معها. والتعريف للجنس أي: للحقيقة من حيث هي، من غير قيد شيوعها، ومعناه: الإشارة إلى ما يَعْرِفه كل أحد أن الحمد ما هو. أو للاستغراق إذ الحمد في الحقيقة كُلُّه لله إذ ما من خير إلا وهو مُولِيهِ بواسطة وبغير واسطة. كما قال: وَما بِكُمْ مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ فَمِنَ اللَّهِ وقيل: للعهد، والمعهودُ حمدُه تعالى نفسه في أزله.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-3","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وقُرِئ (الحمد لله) بإتباع الدال للام(1)، وبالعكس(2)، تنزيلاً لهما من حيث إنهما يستعملان معاً منزلة كلمة واحدة.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-4","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"ومعناه في اللغة: الثناءُ بالجميل على قصد التعظيم والتبجيل، وفي العُرف: فعل يُنبئ عن تعظيم المُنعم بسبب كونه منعماً. والشكر في اللغة: فعل يُشعر بتعظيم المنعم، فهو مرادف للحمد العرفي، وفي العرف: صرف","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-5","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"العبد جميعَ ما أنعم الله عليه من السمع والبصر إلى ما خُلِقَ لأجله وأعطاه إياه. وانظر شرحنا الكبير للفاتحة في النَّسَبِ التي بيناها نظماً ونثراً.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-6","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"و (الله) اسم مُرْتَجَلٌ جامد، والألف واللام فيه لازمة لا للتعريف، قال الواحدي: اسم تفرِّد به الباري- سبحانه- يجري في وصفه مجرى الأسماء الأعلام، لا يُعرف له اشتقاق، وقال الأقْلِيشي: إن هذا الاسم مهما لم يكن مشتقّاً كان دليلاً على عين الذات، دون أن يُنظر فيها إلى صفة من الصفات، وليس باسمٍ مشتق من صفة، كالعالِم والحق والخالق والرازق، فالألف واللام على هذا في (الله) من نفس الكلمة، كالزاي من زيد، وذهب إلى هذا جماعة، واختاره الغزالي وقال: كل ما قيل في اشتقاقه فهو تعسُّف.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-7","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وقيل: مشتق من التَّأَلُّهِ وهو التعبد، وقيل: من الوَلَهَان، وهو الحيرة لتحيُّر العقول في شأنه. وقيل: أصله:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-8","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"الإلهُ، ثم حذفت الهمزة ونقلت حركتها إلى اللام، ثم وقع الإدغام وفُخمت للتعظيم، إلا إذا كان قبلها كسر.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-9","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"و (رب) نعت (لله) ، وهو في الأصل: مصدر بمعنى التربية، وهو تبليغ الشيء إلى كماله شيئاً فشيئاً، ثم وُصف به للمبالغة كالصوم والعدل.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-10","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وقيل: هو وصفٌ من رَبِّه يَرُبُّهُ، وأصله: رَبَبَ ثم أُدغم، سُمي به المالكُ لأنه يحفظ ما يملكه ويربيه، ولا يطلق على غيره تعالى إلا بقيد كقوله تعالى: ارْجِعْ إِلى رَبِّكَ. قال ابن جُزَيّ: ومعانيه أربعة: الإله والسيد والمالك والمصلح، وكلها تصلح في رب العالمين، إلا أن الأرجح في معناه: الإله لاختصاصه بالله تعالى.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-11","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"و (العالمين) جمع عالَم، والعالَمُ: اسم لما يُعْلَمُ به، كالخاتم لما يُختم به، والطابع لما يطبع به. غلب فيما يُعلم به الصانع. وهو كل ما سواه من الجواهر والأعراض، فإنها لإمكانها وافتقارها إلى مُؤثِرٍ واجبٍ لذاته، تدل على وجوده، وإنما جُمع ليشمل ما تحته من الأجناس المختلفة، وغلب العقلاء منهم فجُمِعَ بالياء والنون كسائر أوصافهم، فهو جمع، لا اسم جمع، خلافاً لابن مالك.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-12","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وقيل: اسم وضع لذوي العلم من الملائكة والثقلين، وتناولُه لغيرهم على سبيل الاستتباع، وقيل: عنى به هذا الناس، فإن كل واحد منهم عالَمٌ، حيث إنه يشتمل على نظائر ما في العالم الكبير، ولذا سوّى بين النظر فيهما فقال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-13","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وَفِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ أَفَلا تُبْصِرُونَ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-14","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"قلت: وإليه يشير قول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-15","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"يا تَائهاً في مَهْمَهٍ عَنْ سِرِّه ... انْظُرْ تجِدْ فِيكَ الوُجُودُ بأَسْره","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-16","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"أنْتَ الكمَالُ طَرِيقَةً وحَقِيقَةً ... يا جَامِعاً سِرَّ الإلّهِ بأسره","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-17","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"والرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ اسمان بُنيا للمبالغة، من رَحِمَ، كالغضبان من غضب، والعليم من علم، والرحمة في اللغة: رَقَّةُ القلب، وانعطافٌ يقتضي التفضل والإحسان، ومنه الرَّحِم لانعطافها على ما فيها. وأسماء الله تعالى إنما تُؤخذ باعتبار الغايات، التي هي أفعال، دون المبادئ التي هي انفعالات. و (الرحمن) أبلغ من (الرحيم) لأن زيادةَ المبنى تدل على زيادة المعنى، كقَطَّعَ وقَطَعَ، وذلك إنما يُؤخذ تارة باعتبار الكمية، وأخرى باعتباره الكيفية.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-18","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"فعلى الأول: قيل: يا رحمنَ الدنيا لأنه يَعُمُّ المؤمنَ والكافر، ورحيمَ الآخرة لأنه يختص بالمؤمن، وعلى الثاني قيل: يا رحمن الدنيا والآخرة ورحيم الدنيا لأن النعم الأخروية كلها جِسَام، وأما النعم الدنيوية فجليلة وحقيرة.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-19","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وإنما قدّم (الرحمن) - والقياس الترقي من الأدنى إلى الأعلى- لتقدُّم رحمة الدنيا، ولأنه صار كالعَلَم من حيث إنه لا يُوصف به غيره لأن معناه المنعم الحقيقي البالغُ في الرحمة غايتَها، وذلك لا يصدُق على غيره تعالى.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-20","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"انظر البيضاوي. وسيأتي الكلام عليهما في المعنى.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-21","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"و (مَلِكَ) نِعت لما قبله، قراءةُ الجماعة بغير ألف من (المُلك) بالضم، وقرأ عاصم والكسائي بالألف، من (المِلك) بالكسر، والتقدير على هذا: مالك مجئ يوم الدين، أو مالك الأمر يوم الدين. وقراءةُ الجماعة أرجح، لثلاثة أوجه:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-22","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"الأول: أن الملك أعظم من مالك، إذ قد يوصف كل أحد بالمالك لماله، وأما المَلِكُ فهو سيد الناس، والثاني: قوله:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-23","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وَلَهُ الْمُلْكُ يَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ، والثالث: أنها لا تقتضي حذفا، والحذف خلاف الأصل(1).","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-24","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"و (يوم الدين) ظرف مضاف إلى ما قبله على طريق الاتساع، وأُجري الظرف مجرى المفعول به، والمعنى على الظرفية، أي: الملك في يوم الدين، أو ملك الأمر يوم الدين، فيكون فيه حذف. وقد رُويت القراءتان- أي:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-25","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"القصر والمد- عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-26","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وقد قرئ (ملك) بوجوه كثيرة تركنا ذكرها لشذوذها. فإن قيل: ملك ومالك نكرة لأن إضافة اسم الفاعل لا تُخصص، وكيف ينعت به (الرحمن الرحيم) وهما معرفتان؟ قلت: إنما تكون إضافةُ اسم الفاعل لا تخصص إذا كان بمعنى الحال أو الاستقبال لأنها حينئذٍ غيرُ مَحْضَةٍ، وأما هذا فهو مستمر دائماً، فإضافته محضة. قاله ابن جزي.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-27","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله معلما لعباده كيف يُثْنُونَ عليه ويعظمونه ثم يسألونه: يا عبادي قولوا: الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ أي: الثناء الجميل إنما يستحقه العظيم الجليل، فلا يستحق الحمدَ سواه، إذ لا منعم على الحقيقة إلا الله، وَما بِكُمْ مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ فَمِنَ اللَّهِ. أو جميعُ المحامدِ كلُّها لله، أو الحمدُ المعهودُ في الأذهان هو حمدُ الله تعالى نفسَه في أزله، قبل أن يُوجِدَ خلقّه، فلما أوجد خلقه قال لهم: الحمد لله، أي: احمدونى بذلك الحمد المعهود في الأزل.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-28","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وإنما استحق الحمد وحده لأنه رَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ، وكأن سائلاً سأله: لم اختصصت بالحمد؟ فقال: لأني ربُّ العالمين، أنا أوجدتُهم برحمتي، وأمددتهم بنعمتي، فلا منعم غيري، فاستحققت الحمد وحدي، مِنِّي كان الإيجاد وعليَّ توالي الإِمْدَاد، فأنا ربُّ العباد، فالعوالم كلها- على تعدد أجناسها واختلاف أنواعها- في قبضتي وتحت تربيتي ورعايتي.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-29","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"قال بعضهم: خلق الله ثمانيةَ عَشرَ ألف عالَم، نصفها في البر ونصفها في البحر. وقال الفخرُ الرازي: رُوِيَ أن بني آدم عُشْرُ الجن، وبنو آدم والجنُ عُشْرُ حيوانات البر، وهؤلاء كلُّهم عشر الطيور، وهؤلاء كلهم عشر حيوانات البحار، وهؤلاء كلهم عشر ملائكة الأرض الموكلين ببني آدم، وهؤلاء كلهم عشر ملائكة سماء الدنيا، وهؤلاء كلهم عشر ملائكة السماء الثانية، ثم على هذا الترتيب إلى ملائكة السماء السابعة، ثم الكلُّ في مقابلة الكرسي نَزْرٌ قليل، ثم هؤلاء عشر ملائكة السُّرَادِق الواحد من سُرادقات العرش، التي عددُها: مائةُ ألف، طول كل سرادق وعرضُه- إذا قُوبلتْ به السموات والأرض وما فيهما وما بينهما- يكون شيئاً يسيراً ونَزْراً قليلاً. وما من موضع شِبْرٍ إلا وفيه مَلَكٌ ساجد أو راكع أو قائم، وله زَجَل بالتسبيح والتهليل. ثم هؤلاء كلهم في مقابلة الذين يَجُولُون حول العرش كالقطرة في البحر، ولا يَعلم عددهم إلا الله تعالى: وَما يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-30","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"وقال وَهْبُ بن منبه: (قوائم العرش ثلاثُمائةٍ وست وستون قائمة، وبين كل قائمة وقائمة ستون ألف صحراء، وفي كل صحراء ستون ألف عالم، وكل عالم قَدْرُ الثقلين) .","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-30"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-31","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"فهذه العوالم كلها في قبضة الحق وتحت تربيته وحفظه، يوصل المدد إلى كل واحد وهو في مستقرِّه ومستودعه، إما إلى روحانيته من قوة العلوم والمعارف، وإما إلى بشريته من قوة الأشباح، من العرش إلى الفرش،","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-31"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-32","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"كلها مقدَّرة أرزاقها محصورة آجالها، محفوظة أشباحها، معلومة أماكنها، لا يخفى عليه شيء في الأرض ولا في السماء وهو السميع العليم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-32"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-33","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"ثم هذه التربية التي ربى سبحانه بها خلقه إنما هي رحمة منه وإحسان، لا لزوم عليه وإيجاب، ولذلك وصلَه بقوله الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ، أي: الرحمن بنعمة الإيجاد، الرحيم بنعمة الإمداد. «نعمتان ما خلا موجود عنهما، ولا بد لكل مُكَوَّنَ منهما: نعمة الإيجاد ونعمة الإمداد، أنعم أولاً بالإيجاد، وثنى بتوالي الإمداد» . كما في (الحِكَم)(1). فاسمُه (الرحمن) يقتضي إيجادَ الأشياء وإبرازها، واسمه (الرحيم) يقتضي تربيتَها وإمدادها. ولذلك لا يجوز إطلاق اسم (الرحمن) على أحد، ولم يَتَسَمَّ أحد به إذ الإيجاد لا يصح من غيره تعالى، بخلاف اسمه (الرحيم) فيجوز إطلاقه على غيره تعالى لمشاركة صدور الإمداد في الظاهر من بعض المخلوقات مجازاً وعاريةً.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-33"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-34","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"أو: الرحمن في الدنيا والآخرة، والرحيم في الآخرة لأن رحمة الآخرة خاصة بالمؤمنين. أو الرحمن بجلائل النِعم والرحيم بدقائقها، فجلائل النعم مثل: نعمة الإسلام والإيمان والإحسان، والمعرفة والهداية، وكشف الحجاب وفتح الباب والدخول مع الأحباب، ودقائقُ النعم مثل: الصحة والعافية والمال الحلال، وغير ذلك مما يأتي ذكره في المُنْعَم عليهم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-34"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-35","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"ثم من تحقق منه الإيجادُ والإمداد استحق أن يكون ملكاً لجميع العباد، ولذلك ذكرَهِ بِأَثَره فقال: مَلِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ أي: المتصرف في عباده كيف شاء، لا راد لما قضى ولا مانع لما أعطى، فهو ملكُ الملوك رب الأرباب في هذه الدار وفي تلك الدار. وإنما خصّ يوم الدين- وهو يوم الجزاء- بالملكية لأن ذلك اليوم يظهرُ فيه المُلْكُ لله عيَاناً لجميع الخلق، فإن الله تعالى يتجلّى لفصل عباده، حتى يراه المؤمنون عياناً، بخلاف الدنيا فإن تصرفه تعالى لا يفهمه إلا الكَمَلَةُ من المؤمنين، ولذلك ادَّعى كثير من الجهلة الملكَ ونسبوه لأنفسهم. ويوم القيامة ينفرد الملك لله عند الخاص والعام، قال تعالى: لِمَنِ الْمُلْكُ الْيَوْمَ لِلَّهِ الْواحِدِ الْقَهَّارِ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-35"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-36","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"الإشارة: لمّا تجلّى الحقّ سبحانه من عالَم الجبروت إلى عالم الملكوت، أو تقول: من عالم الغيب إلى عالم الشهادة، حمد نفسه بنفسه، ومجَّد نفسه بنفسه، ووحَّد نفسه بنفسه، ولله دَرُّ الهَرَوِيّ، حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-36"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-37","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"مَا وَحَّدَ الواحِدَ مِنْ واحِدِ ... إِذْ كُلُّ مَنْ وحّده جاحد","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-37"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-38","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"توحيدُ مَنْ ينطقُ عَنْ نَعْتِهِ ... عاريةُ أَبْطَلَهَا الواحِدُ","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-38"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-39","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"توحيدُه إِيّاه توحيدُه ... ونعتُ من يَنْعَتُه لاَحِدُ(1)","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-39"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-40","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"فقال في توحيد نفسه بنفسه مترجماً عن نفسه بنفسه: (الحمد لله رب العالمين) ، فكأنه يقول في عنوان كتابه وسر خطابه: أنا الحامد والمحمود، وأنا القائم بكل موجود، أنا رب الأرباب، وأنا مسبب الأسباب لمن فهم الخطاب، أنا رب العالمين، أنا قيوم السموات والأرَضين، بل أنا المتوحِّدُ في وجودي، والمتجلِّي لعبادي بكرمي وجودي، فالعوالم كلها ثابتة بإثباتي، مَمْحُوَّةٌ بأحدية ذاتي.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-40"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-41","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"قال رجل بين يدي الجنيد: (الحمد لله) ولم يقل: (رب العالمين) ، فقال له الجنيد: كَمِّلْهَا يا أخي، فقال الرجل: وأيّ قَدْر للعالمين حتى تُذكر معه؟! فقال الجنيد: قُلها يا أخي فإن الحادث إذا قُرن بالقديم تلاشى الحادث وبقي القديم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-41"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-42","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"يقول سبحانه: يا مَن هو مني قريب، تَدبر سِرِّي فإنه غريب، أنا المحبُ، وأنا الحبيب، وأنا القريب، وأنا المجيب، أنا الرحيم الرحمن، وأنا الملك الديّان، أنا الرحمن بنعمة الإيجاد، والرحيمُ بتوالي الإمداد. منِّي كان الإيجاد، وعليَّ دوام الإمداد، وأنا رب العباد، أنا الملك الديَّان، وأنا المجازي بالإحسان على الإحسان، أنا الملك على الإطلاق، لولا جهالة أهل العناد والشقاق، الأمر لنا على الدوام، لمن فهم عنا من الأنام.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-42"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-43","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"قال في الرسائل الكبرى(2): لا عبرة بظواهر الأشياء، وإنما العبرة بالسر المكنون، وليس ذلك إلا بظهور أمر الحق وارتفاع غَطَائه وزوال أستاره وخفائه، فإذا تحقق ذلك التجلّي والظهور، واستولى على الأشياء الفناءُ والدُّثُور، وانقشعت الظلمات بإشراق النور، فهناك يبدو عين اليقين ويَحِقُّ الحق المبين، وعند ذلك تبطل دعوى المدعين، كما يفهم العامة بطلان ذلك في يوم الدين، حين يكون الملك لله رب العالمين، وليت شعري أيُّ وقت كان الملكُ لسواه حتى يقع التقييد بقوله: الْمُلْكُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِلَّهِ وقوله: وَالْأَمْرُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِلَّهِ؟! لولا الدعاوَى العريضة من القلوب المريضة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-43"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_2-44","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:2–4 — commentary","text":"ثم تنزل لبيان العبودية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_2-44"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s1","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-ḥamd: syntax, definiteness and readings","text":"I say: “Praise” ( الحمد ) is the subject ( مبتدأ ), and “belongs to God” ( لله ) is the predicate ( خبر ). Its underlying construction is accusative ( النصب ), and it has in fact been recited that way; the underlying expression is “I praise God with praise” ( أحمد الله حمداً ). It was shifted from the accusative to the nominative ( الرفع ) in order to signify the universality and abiding stability of praise, rather than its renewed occurrence and origination. The form also teaches the very words to be uttered while intimating God's independence of their praise: praise belongs to God even if you do not praise Him. Had He said, “I praise God,” this meaning would not have been conveyed. Ḥamd is one of those verbal nouns ( المصادر ) that are put in the accusative by implicit verbs ( أفعال مضمرة ) which are scarcely ever expressed alongside them. The definite article ( التعريف ) may be generic ( للجنس ): it then denotes the reality as such, without making its universal extension a condition, and points to what everyone already recognises praise to be. Or it may be exhaustive ( للاستغراق ): in reality every praise belongs to God, since there is no good that He does not bestow, either through an intermediary or without one, as He says, “Whatever blessing you have is from God” [16:53]. Or it may be referential ( للعهد ), the referent being God's praise of Himself in His beginningless eternity. “Praise belongs to God” has also been recited with the vowel of the dāl made to follow that of the lām, and conversely ( بإتباع الدال للام وبالعكس ), treating the two, because of their habitual conjunction, as though they were a single word.","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s2","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Praise and thanksgiving: technical meanings","text":"I:53–54 In the language ( في اللغة ), praise ( الحمد ) is commendation of what is beautiful, intended as magnification and reverence. In technical usage ( في العرف ), it is an act that discloses magnification of a benefactor precisely insofar as he is a benefactor. Thanksgiving ( الشكر ), in the language, is an act that signifies magnification of the benefactor and is therefore synonymous with ḥamd in that technical sense. In technical usage, however, shukr is the servant's directing everything God has bestowed upon him - hearing, sight, and the rest - toward the purpose for which it was created and bestowed. See our larger commentary on al-Fātiḥa for the relations ( النِّسَب ) among these meanings, which we set out there in verse and prose.","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s3","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Allāh: the name and its derivation","text":"I:54 “God” ( الله ) is, on this view, an independently coined ( مرتجل ), underived ( جامد ) name; the alif and lām are integral to the word and are not the definite article. Al-Wāḥidī said: “It is a name with which the Creator - glory be to Him - is uniquely named; in describing Him it functions as a proper name, and no derivation is known for it.” Al-Uqlīshī said: “If this name is not derived, it signifies the very Essence without considering in it any particular attribute. It is not a name derived from an attribute, like the Knowing, the Real, the Creator, or the Provider.” On this account the alif and lām in Allāh belong to the word itself, just as the zāʾ belongs to Zayd. A number of scholars held this view; al-Ghazālī preferred it and said that everything proposed by way of derivation is strained. It has also been said that Allāh is derived from taʾalluh ( التألّه ), worship or devotion; or from walahān ( الولهان ), bewilderment, because intellects are bewildered concerning Him. Another view is that its original form was al-ilāh: the hamza was omitted, its vowel transferred to the lām, assimilation ( الإدغام ) then occurred, and the lām was pronounced emphatically in magnification, except when preceded by kasra.","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s4","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Rabb: nurture, lordship and meaning","text":"“Lord” ( ربّ , rabb) is an adjective qualifying ( نعت ) “God.” In origin it is a verbal noun ( مصدر ) meaning nurture or bringing-up ( التربية ): bringing a thing to its perfection little by little. It is then used descriptively for intensification, as are ṣawm (“fasting”) and ʿadl (“justice”). It is also said to be a descriptive form from rabbahu yarubbuhu, “he tended it / nurtured it”; its original form is rabab, after which assimilation ( الإدغام ) occurs. An owner is called rabb because he preserves what he owns and nurtures it. The term is not applied to anyone other than God without qualification, as in “Return to your lord” [12:50]. Ibn Juzayy said: “It has four meanings: deity, master, owner, and one who sets things right. All four are suitable in ‘Lord of the worlds,’ though the strongest meaning is ‘deity,’ because that is peculiar to God Most High.”","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s5","r":"fatiha_2","title":"ʿĀlam: the cosmos as a sign of its Maker","text":"“The worlds” ( العالمين ) is the plural of ʿālam ( عالَم ). Ibn ʿAjība explains the word morphologically: al-ʿālam is “a noun for that by which something is known” ( اسم لما يُعلَم به ), just as khātam is that by which something is sealed and ṭābiʿ that by which something is stamped. The term came to be used predominantly for that by which the Maker is known ( ما يُعلَم به الصانع ): everything other than Him, comprising substances ( الجواهر ) and accidents ( الأعراض ). Because they are contingent or possible ( لإمكانها ) and stand in need of an efficient cause ( مؤثِّر ) that is Necessary in Itself ( واجب لذاته ), they signify His existence. Thus the cosmos functions as a sign ( علامة ) of its Maker, although Ibn ʿAjība's wording here is literally “that by which [He] is known.” The plural is used to include the differing genera contained beneath the term. Rational beings are given grammatical precedence, so it is pluralised with yāʾ and nūn like their other descriptions. It is therefore a true plural ( جمع ), not a collective noun ( اسم جمع ), contrary to Ibn Mālik. It is also said that the term was coined for beings possessed of knowledge - the angels and the two weighty species ( الثقلان ), humankind and jinn - and that it includes other beings only by concomitant extension ( على سبيل الاستتباع ). Another view is that humankind is intended here: every human being is a world ( عالَم ), since he contains counterparts of what exists in the greater world ( العالم الكبير ). Hence revelation places contemplation of the two on the same footing: “And in your own selves - do you not see?” [51:21]. I:55 I say: to this the poet alludes: O you who wander in a wilderness, estranged from your own secret, look: you will find all existence within yourself. You are perfection, in the Way and in the Reality, you who gather within yourself the divine secret in its entirety.","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s6","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Al-Raḥmān and al-Raḥīm: form and meaning","text":"Al-Raḥmān ( الرَّحمن , “the Compassionate”) and al-Raḥīm ( الرَّحيم , “the Merciful”) are two intensive forms ( اسمان بُنيا للمبالغة ) derived from raḥima, “to have mercy,” as ghaḍbān is formed from ghaḍiba and ʿalīm from ʿalima. In ordinary language, mercy ( الرحمة ) is tenderness of heart and an inclination that entails graciousness and beneficence; from the same root comes raḥim, “womb,” because of its tender enclosing of what is within it. The divine Names, however, are taken with regard to their ends ( الغايات ), which are acts, not their beginnings ( المبادئ ), which in creatures would be passive affections ( انفعالات ). Al-Raḥmān ( الرَّحمن ) is more intensive than al-Raḥīm ( الرَّحيم ), because increase in morphological form indicates increase in meaning ( زيادة المبنى تدل على زيادة المعنى ), as with qaṭṭaʿa and qaṭaʿa. This increase may be understood quantitatively or qualitatively. Quantitatively one says: “Compassionate in this world,” because that mercy encompasses believer and unbeliever, “and Merciful in the hereafter,” because that mercy is particular to believers. Qualitatively one says: “Compassionate in this world and the hereafter, and Merciful in this world,” because all blessings of the hereafter are immense, while worldly blessings include both great and small. Al-Raḥmān is placed first, although the normal progression ( الترقي ) would be from the lesser to the greater, because the mercy of this world comes first and because al-Raḥmān has become like a proper name ( كالعَلَم ), inasmuch as none other is described by it. Its meaning is the true Benefactor whose mercy reaches its utmost limit, and this is true of none but God Most High. See al-Bayḍāwī. The two Names will be discussed again in the running interpretation.","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s7","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Malik and mālik: readings and annexation","text":"“King” ( مَلِك , malik) is an adjective ( نعت ) qualifying what precedes. The majority recite it without alif, from mulk ( المُلك , sovereignty), with ḍamma; ʿĀṣim and al-Kisāʾī recite mālik ( مالِك , master/owner) with alif, from milk ( المِلك , possession), with kasra. On the latter reading the ellipsis is understood as “Master of the coming of the Day of Recompense,” or “Master of the affair on the Day of Recompense.” Ibn ʿAjība prefers the majority reading for three reasons: first, a king is greater than an owner, for anyone may be called owner of his property whereas the king is master of the people; second, “His is the sovereignty on the day the Trumpet is blown” [6:73]; and third, the reading malik requires no ellipsis ( حذف ), whereas ellipsis is contrary to the default ( خلاف الأصل ). “The Day of Recompense” ( يوم الدين ) is an adverbial expression ( ظرف ) annexed ( مضاف ) to what precedes by an extended construction ( على طريق الاتساع ). The adverbial is treated syntactically like a direct object ( مفعول به ), while the meaning remains adverbial: “the King on the Day of Recompense.” Or, on the mālik reading, the sense is “Master of the affair on the Day of Recompense,” in which case an ellipsis ( حذف ) is posited. Both readings - the short form malik and the long form mālik - are transmitted from the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace. I:56 Malik has been recited in several other ways which Ibn ʿAjība omits because they are anomalous ( شاذة ). If one objects: “Malik and mālik are indefinite ( نكرة ), because an active participle's annexation ( إضافة اسم الفاعل ) does not make it specific; how then can either qualify al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm, which are definite ( معرفة )?” The answer is that an active participle's annexation fails to specify only when it denotes present or future time, for then the annexation is non-pure ( إضافة غير محضة ). Here the meaning is continuously and eternally true, so the annexation is pure ( إضافة محضة ). This is Ibn Juzayy's explanation.","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s8","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Praise and lordship","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, teaches His servants how to praise and magnify Him and then to ask of Him: “My servants, say: ‘Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds.’” That is: beautiful praise is deserved only by the Magnificent, the Majestic. None other deserves praise, since in reality there is no benefactor but God: “Whatever blessing you have is from God” [16:53]. Or: all praises whatsoever belong to God. Or: the praise already known to the mind is God's praise of Himself in His beginningless eternity, before He brought His creation into existence. When He brought His creation into existence, He said to them, “Praise belongs to God”: that is, “Praise Me with that praise already known in beginningless eternity.” He alone deserves praise because He is “Lord of the worlds.” It is as though someone asked Him, “Why does praise belong exclusively to You?” and He answered: “Because I am Lord of the worlds. I brought them into existence through My mercy and sustain them through My bounty. There is no benefactor but Me, and so I alone deserve praise. From Me comes their being brought into existence, and upon Me rests their continually renewed sustenance. I am the Lord of the servants. All the worlds, with their many genera and differing species, are in My grasp and under My nurture and care.”","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s9","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Reports on the worlds and the angelic hosts","text":"Some have said that God created eighteen thousand worlds, half on land and half in the sea. Fakhr al-Dīn al-Rāzī said: “It has been related that the children of Adam are one tenth of the jinn; the children of Adam and the jinn together are one tenth of the land animals; all these are one tenth of the birds; all these are one tenth of the sea animals; all these are one tenth of the angels of the earth charged with the children of Adam; all these are one tenth of the angels of the lowest heaven; and all these are one tenth of the angels of the second heaven. This progression continues to the angels of the seventh heaven. “All of these, in comparison with the Footstool, are very few. These in turn are one tenth of the angels of a single pavilion among the hundred thousand pavilions of the Throne. Were the heavens and the earth, and all within and between them, compared with the length and breadth of one pavilion, they would be a very small and trifling thing. There is not a handspan of space without an angel prostrating, bowing, or standing, with a resounding voice glorifying God and declaring His unity. Then all these, in comparison with those who move around the Throne, are like a drop in the sea. None but God Most High knows their number: ‘None knows the hosts of your Lord but He’ [74:31].” Here ends the quotation. Wahb ibn Munabbih said: “The Throne has three hundred and sixty-six supports. Between each pair of supports are sixty thousand deserts; in each desert are sixty thousand worlds; and each world is the size of the two weighty kinds.” I:56–57 All these worlds are in the grasp of the Real, beneath His nurture and preservation. He conveys sustaining influx ( المدد ) to each in its settled abode and place of deposit: to its spiritual dimension through the strength of sciences and gnoses ( العلوم والمعارف ), and to its bodily dimension through the strength of corporeal forms ( الأشباح ). From the Throne to the earth, their provisions are apportioned, their lifespans delimited, their bodily forms preserved, and their locations known. Nothing on earth or in heaven is hidden from Him; He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s10","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Mercy, origination and sustaining influx","text":"I:57 This nurture ( التربية ) by which He nurtures His creation is mercy and beneficence from Him, not something binding or obligatory upon Him. Hence He joins to “Lord of the worlds” the words al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm: the Compassionate through the blessing of bringing-into-existence ( نعمة الإيجاد ), the Merciful through the blessing of sustaining influx ( نعمة الإمداد ). As the Ḥikam says: “Two blessings no existent is without, and every originated being must have them: the blessing of being brought into existence and the blessing of sustaining influx. He first favoured you with existence, then followed it with successive sustaining influx.” His Name al-Raḥmān entails the bringing of things into existence and their manifestation ( الإيجاد والإبراز ); His Name al-Raḥīm entails their nurture and sustaining influx ( التربية والإمداد ). Hence the Name al-Raḥmān may not be applied to anyone else, and no one has been named by it, because bringing into existence is not truly possible from other than Him. Al-Raḥīm differs: it may be applied to another, since the issuing of sustaining assistance from some creatures appears, metaphorically and by borrowed attribution, to be shared. Or: He is al-Raḥmān in this world and the hereafter, and al-Raḥīm in the hereafter, because the mercy of the hereafter is particular to believers. Or: al-Raḥmān with respect to the great blessings ( جلائل النعم ) and al-Raḥīm with respect to their subtleties ( دقائقها ). The great blessings include Islam, faith ( الإيمان ), spiritual excellence ( الإحسان ), gnosis ( المعرفة ), guidance, unveiling the veil, opening the door, and entrance among the beloved; subtler blessings include health, well-being, lawful wealth, and the other things to be mentioned under “those upon whom You have bestowed favour.”","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s11","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Sovereignty on the Day of Recompense","text":"He from whom bringing into existence and sustaining truly proceed deserves to be King over all the servants. This is therefore mentioned immediately afterwards: “King of the Day of Recompense.” He disposes of His servants as He wills: none can repel what He decrees, and none can withhold what He gives. He is King of kings and Lord of lords in this abode and the next. Sovereignty is associated particularly with the Day of Recompense, the day of requital, because on that day God's sovereignty becomes plainly manifest to all creation. God Most High discloses Himself to judge between His servants, so that believers see Him directly. In this world, by contrast, His disposal of affairs is understood only by the perfected among the believers. Many of the ignorant have therefore claimed sovereignty and attributed it to themselves. On the Day of Resurrection, God's sole sovereignty is evident to both the elect and the common people. God Most High says: “Whose is the sovereignty today? God's, the One, the All-Subduing” [40:16].","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_2-s12","r":"fatiha_2","title":"Divine self-disclosure and self-praise","text":"When the Real, glory be to Him, disclosed Himself ( تجلّى ) from the realm of jabarūt ( عالم الجبروت ) into the realm of malakūt ( عالم الملكوت ) - or, one may say, from the realm of the unseen into the realm of witnessing - He praised Himself by Himself, glorified Himself by Himself, and declared His own unity by Himself. How fine are al-Harawī's words: I:57–58 No one has declared the One to be One, for everyone who declares Him One is a denier. The tawḥīd of one who speaks from his own description is a borrowed thing annulled by the One. His declaring Himself One is His tawḥīd; the description of whoever describes Him deviates. I:58 Thus, affirming His own unity by Himself, and expressing Himself by Himself, He said: “Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds.” It is as though He says in the heading of His Book and the secret of His address: “I am the Praiser and the Praised. I sustain every existent. I am Lord of lords and, for whoever understands the address, the Cause of causes. I am Lord of the worlds, Sustainer of the heavens and the earths. Indeed, I am alone in My existence, disclosing Myself to My servants through My generosity and bounty. All the worlds are established through My establishing them, and effaced through the absolute oneness of My Essence.” A man said in al-Junayd's presence, “Praise belongs to God,” without adding “Lord of the worlds.” Al-Junayd said to him, “Complete it, my brother.” The man replied, “What standing do the worlds have, that they should be mentioned with Him?” Al-Junayd said: “Say it, my brother. When that which has come to be is placed alongside the Beginningless, that which has come to be vanishes, and the Beginningless remains.” He says, glory be to Him [in this spiritual interpretation]: “O you who are near to Me, ponder My secret, for it is wondrous. I am the Lover and I am the Beloved; I am the Near and I am the Answerer. I am the Ever-Merciful, the All-Merciful; I am the King, the Requiter. I am All-Merciful through the blessing of bringing into existence, and Ever-Merciful through the succession of sustaining gifts. From Me comes the bringing into existence, and upon Me rests continual sustaining. I am Lord of the servants. I am the King, the Requiter, rewarding goodness with goodness. I am King without qualification — were it not for the ignorance of the people of obstinacy and dissension! For those of humankind who understand Us, command belongs to Us perpetually.” He says in the Greater Epistles: “What counts is not the outward appearances of things, but the hidden secret. This consists in the manifestation of the affair of the Real, the lifting of its covering, and the removal of its veils and concealment. When that self-disclosure and manifestation are realised, when effacement and passing away overcome things, and darkness is dispersed by the shining of the light, there the eye of certainty appears and the manifest Truth stands established. Then the claims of the claimants are nullified, just as ordinary people understand their nullity on the Day of Recompense, when sovereignty belongs to God, Lord of the worlds. Would that I knew at what time sovereignty belonged to another, so that it should be qualified by His saying, ‘Sovereignty on that day belongs to God’ [22:56], or ‘Command on that day belongs to God’ [82:19]! Were it not for the vast claims of diseased hearts!” Here ends the quotation. I:59 He then descended to the exposition of servanthood ( العبودية ), saying:","anchor":"en-fatiha_2-s12"},{"kind":"passage","id":"fatiha_3","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary 1:5","anchor":"unit-fatiha_3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-1","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ (5)","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-2","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"قلت: (إياك) مفعول (نعبد) ، وقُدِّم للتعظيم والاهتمام به، والدلالة على الحصر، ولذلك قال ابن عباس:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-3","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"(نعبُدك ولا نعبد معك غيرَك) ، ولتقديم ما هو مقدَّمٌ في الوجود وهو الملك المعبود، وللتنبيه على أن العابدَ ينبغي أن يكون نظرُه إلى المعبود أولاً وبالذات، ومنه إلى العبادة، لا من حيث إنها عبادةٌ صدَرتْ عنه، بل من حيث إنها نِسْبَةٌ شريفة إليه، وَوُصْلَةٌ بينه وبين الحق، فإن العارف إنما يحقّ وصوله إذا استغرق في ملاحظة جناب القدس، وغاب عما عداه، حتى إنه لا يلاحظ نفسَه ولا حالاً من أحوالها إلا من حيث إنها تَجَلٍّ من تجلياته ومظهرٌ لربوبيته، ولذلك فُضِّلَ ما حكى اللَّهُ عن حبيبه حين قال: لاَ تَحْزَنْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَنا، على ما حكاه عن كليمه حيث قال: إِنَّ مَعِي رَبِّي سَيَهْدِينِ أي: حيث صرّح بمطلوبه، و (إياك) مفعول (نستعين) وقدّم أيضاً للاختصاص والاهتمام، كما تقدم في إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ. وكرّر الضمير ولم يقل: إياك نعبد ونستعين لأن إظهارَه أبلغ في إظهار الاعتماد على الله، وأقطعُ في إحضار التعلق بالله والإقبال على الله وأمدحُ، ألا ترى أن قولك: بك أنتصر وبك أحتمي وبك أنال مطالبي- أبلغ وأمدح من قولك: بك أنتصر وأحتمي ... الخ؟.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-4","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"وَقَدَّمَ العبادة على الاستعانة ليتوافق رءوس الآي، وليُعلمَ منه أن تقديم الوسيلة على طلب الحاجة أَدْعَى إلى الإجابة، فإن مَنْ تَلبَّس بخدمة الملك وشرع فيها بحسب وُسْعَه، ثم طلب منه الإعانة عليها أجيب إلى مطلبه، بخلاف من كلّفه الملكُ بخدمته، فقال: أعطني ما يعينُني عليها، فهو سوء أدب، وأيضاً: من استحضر الأوصافَ العِظام ما أمكنه إلا المسارعةُ إلى الخضوع والعبادة، وأيضاً: لمّا نسبَ المتكلمُ العبادةَ إلى نفسه أوْهَمَ ذلك تبجحاً واعتداداً منه بما يصدُر عنه فعقَّبه بقوله: وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ، دفعاً لذلك التوهم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-5","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"والعبادة: أقصى غاية الخضوع والتذلل، ومنه طريق مُعَبَّدٌ، أي: مُذَلل، والاستعانة: طلب المعونة، والمراد طلب المعونة في المُهمات كُلِّها، أو في أداء العبادات.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-6","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"والضمير المستتر فى الفعلين للقارىء ومن معه من الحفظة وحاضري صلاة الجماعة، أو له ولسائر الموجودين.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-7","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"أدْرَجَ عبادته في تضاعيف عبادتهم وخلط حاجته بحاجتهم لعلها تُقبل ببركتها ويُجاب إليها، ولهذا شرعت الجماعة. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-8","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، تتميماً لتعليم عباده: فإذا أثنيتمُ عليَّ ومجدتموني وعظمتموني فأقِرُّوا لي بالربوبية، وأظهروا من أنفسكم العبودية، واطلبوا مني العون في كل وقت وقولوا: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ، وكأنه- جلّ جلاله- لَمّا ذكر أنه مستحق للمحامد كلها قديمها وحديثها لأنه رب العوالِم وقيومها، أصل الأصول وفروعها، أنعم عليها أولاً بالإيجاد، وثانياً بتوالي الإمداد، فهو مالكها على الإطلاق، ذكر أنه لا يستحق أن يُعبد سواه إذ لا مُنعمَ على الحقيقة إلا الله، فهو أحقُّ أن يُعبد، وأولى أن يفرد بالوجهة والقصد، لأنه مُسْتَبِدٌ وغير مُسْتَمدّ، والمادة من عَيْنِ الجود، فإذا انقطعت المادة انعدم الوجود.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-9","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"قال البيضاوي: ثم إنه لما ذكر الحقيق بالحمد، ووصف بصفات عظام تميَّز بها عن سائر الذوات، تعلَّق العلمُ بمعلوم معين، خوطب بذلك، أي: يا من هذا شأنه نخصُّك بالعبادة والاستعانة، ليكون أدلّ على الاختصاص، وللترقي من الغَيْبة إلى الشهود، وكأن المعلومَ صار عياناً، والمعقولَ مُشاهَداً، والغيبة حضوراً. بَنَى أول الكلام على ما هو مبادئ حالِ العارفِ من الذكر والفكر والتأمل في أسمائه، والنظر في آلائه، والاستدلال بصنائعه على عظيم شأنه وباهر سلطانه، ثم قفَّى بما هو منتهى أمرِه، وهو أن يخوض لُجَّةَ الوصول، ويصير من أهل المشاهدة، فيراه عياناً ويناجيه شِفاها. اللهم اجعلنا من الواصلين إلى العين دون التابعين للأثر. ومن عادة العرب التفنن في الكلام والعدول عن أسلوبٍ إلى آخر، تَطْريَةً وتنشيطاً للسامع، فَتَعْدِل من الخطاب إلى الغيبة، ومن الغيبة إلى التكلم، كقوله: حَتَّى إِذا كُنْتُمْ فِي الْفُلْكِ وَجَرَيْنَ بِهِمْ بِرِيحٍ ... ولم يقل (بكم) وقوله أَرْسَلَ الرِّياحَ فَتُثِيرُ سَحاباً فَسُقْناهُ إِلى بَلَدٍ ... أي: ولم يقل: فساقه.. انظر تمام كلامه.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-10","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"والالتفات هنا في قوله: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ ولم يقل: إياه نعبد لأن الظاهر من قبل الغيبة، وحسنه أن الموصوف تعيَّن وصار حاضراً.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-11","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"قال الأقليشي: فهذه الآية هي التي قال فيها النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «فإذا قال العبد: إياك نعبد وإياك نستعين، يقول الله تعالى: هذه بيني وبين عَبْدِي ولعَبْدِيَ مَا سَأَلَ» . معناه: أيُّ عبد توجَّه إليَّ بالعبادة وسألني العون عليها فعبادته متقبلة، والعون مني له عليها حاصل حتى يُوقعها على وجهها، فالعبادة وصف العبد، والعون من الله تعالى للعبد، فلهذا قال: «فهذه بيني وبين عبدي» .","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-12","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"قال ابن جُزَي: أي نطلب العون منك على العبادة وعلى جميع أمورنا، وفي هذا دليل على بطلان قول القدَرية والجبرية، وأنَّ الحق بين ذلك.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-13","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"الإشارة: لمّا تجلى الحق جل جلاله من عالم الجبروت إلى عالم الملكوت، وحَمِدَ نفسه بنفسه، تجلّى أيضاً وتنزَّل من عالم الملكوت إلى عالم المُلك بقدرته وحكمته لإظهار آثار أسمائه وصفاته، فأظهر العبودية وأخفى الربوبية، أظهر الحكمة وأبطن القدرة، فجعلَ عالَم الحكمة يخاطبُ عالمَ القدرة، ويخضع له، ويتعبّد ويستمد، منه الإعانة والهداية، ويتحرز من طريق الضلالة والغواية.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-14","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"فعالَمً الحكمة محلُّ التكليف، وعالم القدرة محل التصريف، عالم الحكمة عالم الأشباح، وعالم القدرة عالم الأرواح، فإياك نعبد لأهل عالم الحكمة، وإياك نستعين لأهل عالم القدرة. ولذلك قال الشيخ أبو العباس المرسي رضى الله عنه: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ شريعة، وإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ حقيقة، إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ إسلاما، وإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ إحساناً، إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ عبادة، وإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ عبودية، إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ فرق إِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ جَمْعٌ. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-15","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"وإن شئت قلت: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ لأهل العمل لله وهم المخلصون، وإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ لأهل العمل بالله وهم الموحِّدون، العمل لله يوجب المثوبة، والعمل بالله يوجب القُرْبَة، العمل لله يوجب تحقيق العبادة، والعمل بالله يوجب تصحيح الإرادة، العمل لله نعتُ كُلِّ عابد، والعمل بالله نعت كل قاصد، العمل لله قيامٌ بأحكام الظواهر، والعمل بالله قيام بإصلاح الضمائر. قاله القشيري.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-16","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"ثم إنَّ الناسَ في شهود القدرة والحكمة على ثلاثة أقسام: قسم حُجبوا بالحكمة عن شهود القدرة، وهم أهل الحجاب من أهل الغفلة، وقفوا مع قوله: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ، وقسم حُجبوا بشهود القدرة عن الحكمة، وهم أهل الفناء، وقفوا مع قوله: إِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ، وقسم لم يحجبوا بالحكمة عن القدرة ولا بالقدرة عن الحكمة، أَعْطَوا كُلَّ ذي حق حقَّه وَوَفَّوْا كل ذي قسط قسطه، وهم أهل الكمال من أهل البقاء، جمعوا بين قوله: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_3-17","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:5 — commentary","text":"ثم بيّن المقصود الأعظم وما هو المطلوب الأهم، وهو طلب الهداية والتوفيق إلى عين التحقيق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_3-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_3-s1","r":"fatiha_3","title":"The fronting of iyyāka and the worshipper’s orientation","text":"I say: “You alone” ( إياك , iyyāka) is the direct object ( مفعول ) of “we worship” ( نعبد ). It is fronted ( قُدِّم ) for magnification and special attention, and to indicate restriction or exclusivity ( الحصر ); hence Ibn ʿAbbās said: “We worship You and worship none other with You.” Its fronting also places first what is first in existence: the Sovereign who is worshipped ( الملك المعبود ). It alerts the worshipper that his regard should be directed first and essentially to the One worshipped ( المعبود ), and only from Him to the worship - not considering it merely as an act that proceeds from himself, but as a noble relation ( نسبة شريفة ) to Him and a bond ( وصلة ) between himself and the Real. The gnostic's arrival ( وصول العارف ) becomes true only when he is absorbed in attending to the Holy Presence and absent from everything besides It, so that he observes neither himself nor any state of himself except insofar as it is a self-disclosure ( تجلٍّ ) from His self-disclosures and a locus manifesting His Lordship ( مظهر لربوبيته ). For this reason what God relates of His Beloved - “Do not grieve; God is with us” [9:40] - is superior to what He relates of His interlocutor Moses - “Indeed, my Lord is with me; He will guide me” [26:62] - insofar as the latter explicitly states the object sought. Likewise, “You alone” ( إياك ) is the direct object ( مفعول ) of “we seek help” ( نستعين ), and it too is fronted for exclusive specification ( الاختصاص ) and attention. The pronoun is repeated instead of saying, “You alone we worship and seek help,” because making it explicit a second time is stronger in manifesting reliance upon God, more decisive in bringing attachment and turning to God into presence, and more perfect in praise. Thus “Through You I prevail, through You I seek protection, and through You I attain my aims” is more forceful and laudatory than “Through You I prevail and seek protection,” and so forth.","anchor":"en-fatiha_3-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_3-s2","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Why worship precedes asking for help","text":"Worship is placed before seeking help so that the endings of the verses correspond, and to make it known that putting forward the means of approach before asking for one’s need is more conducive to receiving an answer. One who has entered the king’s service and begun to perform it to the extent of his capacity, then asks the king’s assistance in it, receives what he asks. This differs from one whom the king charges with his service and who says, “Give me what will help me perform it”: that is discourtesy. Moreover, one who brings those mighty attributes to mind cannot but hasten to submission and worship. Again, when the speaker ascribes worship to himself, this might suggest boasting and self-congratulation over what proceeds from him. He therefore follows it with “and You alone we ask for help,” to dispel that suggestion.","anchor":"en-fatiha_3-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_3-s3","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Worship, assistance and the plural “we”","text":"Worship ( العبادة , ʿibāda) is the utmost limit of submission and self-abasement; hence ṭarīq muʿabbad means “a road made low and submissive [by being trodden].” Seeking help ( الاستعانة , istiʿāna) is requesting assistance. What is intended is assistance in all important affairs, or specifically assistance in performing acts of worship. The pronoun implicit in the two verbs refers to the reciter together with the guardian angels accompanying him and those present at the congregational prayer; or to him together with all other existing beings. He incorporates his worship into the midst of theirs, and mingles his need with theirs, in the hope that his worship will be accepted through its blessing and his need answered. It is for this reason that congregational prayer was prescribed. So said al-Bayḍāwī. Source comparison: Cairo I:59 reads لسائر الموجودين , “all other existing beings.” The inspected electronic text of al-Bayḍāwī, Anwār al-tanzīl , I:29, on Q1:5, instead has لسائر الموحدين , “all other affirmers of God’s unity.” The difference changes the proposed scope of the plural “we”: Cairo gives a wider company than this source witness. The translation follows Cairo; establishing whether the difference arose in Ibn ʿAjība’s adaptation or in transmission requires further textual evidence.","anchor":"en-fatiha_3-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_3-s4","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Worship and dependence upon God","text":"I:60 The Real, glorious is His majesty, says, completing His instruction of His servants: “When you have praised Me, glorified Me, and magnified Me, acknowledge My lordship, manifest servanthood in yourselves, and ask My assistance at every moment. Say: ‘You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help.’” It is as though, when He mentioned that He deserves all praise, from eternity and in time, because He is the Lord and Sustainer of the worlds, the origin of all roots and their branches, who first bestowed existence upon them and then a continuous supply of support, and who therefore possesses them absolutely, He went on to declare that none besides Him deserves worship. For there is in reality no benefactor but God. He therefore has the greatest claim to be worshipped, and is most worthy to be made the sole object of orientation and intent. He is wholly independent and draws support from no other. The sustaining supply comes from the very fountain of munificence; were that supply cut off, existence would cease.","anchor":"en-fatiha_3-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_3-s5","r":"fatiha_3","title":"The shift to direct address and spiritual presence","text":"Al-Bayḍāwī said: “When the One truly deserving praise had been mentioned and described with mighty attributes by which He is distinguished from all other essences, knowledge became attached to a determinate object of knowledge. He was therefore addressed directly: ‘O You whose affair is thus, we single You out for worship and for seeking help.’ This more strongly indicates exclusive specification ( الاختصاص ), and it marks an ascent from absence/third-person reference ( الغيبة ) to witnessing ( الشهود ): as though what had been known became directly seen, what had been intellectually apprehended became witnessed, and absence became presence. The opening of the discourse is built upon the beginnings of the gnostic's state: remembrance ( الذكر ), reflection ( الفكر ), contemplation of His Names, consideration of His favours, and inference from His works to the greatness of His affair and the splendour of His sovereignty. It is then followed by the culmination of his affair: that he plunge into the sea of arrival ( لجة الوصول ), become one of the people of witnessing ( أهل المشاهدة ), see Him directly, and converse intimately with Him face to face. O God, make us among those who arrive at the Reality itself ( العين ), not those who merely follow the trace ( الأثر ).” Source comparison: Cairo I:60 has دون التابعين للأثر , “rather than those who follow the trace.” The inspected electronic text of al-Bayḍāwī, Anwār al-tanzīl , I:29, on Q1:5, reads دون السامعين للأثر , “rather than those who hear of the trace.” Both contrast arrival with an indirect relation to its evidence, but the source witness specifies hearing where Cairo specifies following. The translation retains Cairo’s wording and records the difference without choosing an unverified authorial reading. “It is the Arabs’ custom to vary their speech and pass from one mode of expression to another, refreshing and enlivening the hearer. Thus they move from direct address to the third person, and from the third person to the first, as in His saying, ‘Until, when you are in ships and they sail with them upon a wind …’ [10:22]. He did not say ‘with you.’ And in His saying, ‘He sent the winds, which stir up clouds, and We drove them to a land …’ [35:9]”: that is, He did not say, “and He drove them.” Consult his discussion in full. The rhetorical shift ( الالتفات , iltifāt) here occurs in “You alone we worship.” He did not say “Him alone we worship,” although the apparent continuation of the preceding discourse would have been in the third person ( الغيبة ). The beauty of the shift lies in the fact that the One described has now become determinate and present.","anchor":"en-fatiha_3-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_3-s6","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Divine aid and human action","text":"Al-Uqlīshī said: “This is the verse concerning which the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace, said: ‘When the servant says, “You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help,” God Most High says, “This is between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks.”’ Its meaning is: ‘Whichever servant turns to Me in worship and asks My assistance in it, his worship is accepted, and My assistance in it is assured to him, so that he may perform it as it should be performed.’ Worship is the servant’s attribute, and assistance is from God Most High to the servant. For this reason He said, ‘This is between Me and My servant.’” Ibn Juzayy said: “That is, we ask Your assistance in worship and in all our affairs. This is evidence of the falsity of the positions of the Qadariyya and the Jabriyya, and that the truth lies between the two.”","anchor":"en-fatiha_3-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_3-s7","r":"fatiha_3","title":"Wisdom and power; effacement and subsistence","text":"I:61 When the Real, glorious is His majesty, disclosed Himself from the realm of jabarūt ( عالم الجبروت ) to the realm of malakūt ( عالم الملكوت ), and praised Himself by Himself, He also disclosed Himself and descended from the realm of malakūt to the realm of mulk ( عالم الملك ) through His power ( القدرة ) and wisdom ( الحكمة ), in order to manifest the traces of His Names and Attributes. He manifested servanthood ( العبودية ) and concealed Lordship ( الربوبية ); He manifested wisdom and concealed power. He thus made the realm of wisdom ( عالم الحكمة ) address the realm of power ( عالم القدرة ), submit to it, worship, draw from it assistance and guidance, and seek protection from the path of error and misguidance. The realm of wisdom ( عالم الحكمة ) is the locus of legal-moral responsibility ( محل التكليف ), while the realm of power ( عالم القدرة ) is the locus of divine disposal ( محل التصريف ). The realm of wisdom is the realm of bodily forms ( عالم الأشباح ), and the realm of power the realm of spirits ( عالم الأرواح ). “You alone we worship” belongs to the people of the realm of wisdom; “from You alone we seek help” to the people of the realm of power. Hence Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mursī, may God be pleased with him, said: “‘You alone we worship’ is Sacred Law ( شريعة ); ‘from You alone we seek help’ is Reality ( حقيقة ). ‘You alone we worship’ is islām; ‘from You alone we seek help’ is iḥsān. ‘You alone we worship’ is worship ( عبادة ); ‘from You alone we seek help’ is servanthood ( عبودية ). ‘You alone we worship’ is distinction/separation ( فرق ); ‘from You alone we seek help’ is gathering/unification ( جمع ).” Or, if you wish: “‘You alone we worship’ belongs to those who act for God ( العمل لله ), the sincere; ‘from You alone we seek help’ belongs to those who act through God ( العمل بالله ), the people of tawḥīd. Acting for God brings reward; acting through God brings nearness. Acting for God brings realisation of worship; acting through God brings rectification of the will. Acting for God is the attribute of every worshipper; acting through God is the attribute of every seeker. Acting for God is standing by the rulings governing outward things; acting through God is standing by the rectification of inward consciences.” So said al-Qushayrī. People are three classes with respect to witnessing power ( شهود القدرة ) and wisdom ( الحكمة ). One class is veiled by wisdom from witnessing power: these are the veiled among the heedless, who stop with “You alone we worship.” A second class is veiled by witnessing power from wisdom: these are the people of effacement ( أهل الفناء ), who stop with “from You alone we seek help.” A third class is veiled neither by wisdom from power nor by power from wisdom: they give every possessor of a right his right and every possessor of a share his due. These are the perfected among the people of subsistence ( أهل البقاء ), who combine “You alone we worship” with “from You alone we seek help.” Success is through God. He then explained the greatest aim and the most important thing sought: asking for guidance ( الهداية ) and divine enabling ( التوفيق ) to the very essence of realisation ( عين التحقيق ). He said:","anchor":"en-fatiha_3-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"fatiha_4","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary 1:6","anchor":"unit-fatiha_4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-1","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ (6)","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-2","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"قلت: الهدايةُ في الأصل: الدلالة بلطف، ولذلك تُستعمل في الخير، وقوله: فَاهْدُوهُمْ إِلى صِراطِ الْجَحِيمِ على التهكم، والفعل منه (هَدَى) بالفتح، وأصله أن يُعدى باللام، أو «إلى» ، فَعْومل هنا معاملة:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-3","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"وَاخْتارَ مُوسى قَوْمَهُ. والصراط لغة: الطريق، مشتق من سَرَط الطعامَ إذا ابتلعه، فكأنها تبتلع السابلةَ أي","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-4","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"المارَّة به، وَقُلِبَتْ السين صاداً لتطابق الطاء في الإطباق، وقد تُشَمُّ زاياً لقرب المَخرج، و (المستقيم) : الذي لا عوج فيه، والمراد به طريق الحق المُوصَّلة إلى الله.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-5","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: معلما لعباده كيف يطلبونه، وما ينبغي لهم أن يطلبوا، أي: قُولوا (اهدنا) أي: أَرشِدْنا إلى الطريق المستقيم، الموصلة إلى حضرة النعيم، والطريقُ المستقيم هو السيرُ على الشريعة المحمدية في الظاهر، والتبرِّي من الحول والقوة في الباطن، أو تقول: هو أن يكون ظاهرُك شريعةً وباطنك حقيقة، ظاهرك عبودية وباطنك حرية، الفرق على ظاهرك موجود والجمع في باطنك مشهود، وفي الحكم: «متى جَعَلَك في الظاهر ممتثلاً لأمره وفي الباطن مستسلماً لقهره، فقد أعظم المِنَّة عليك» .","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-6","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"فالصراط المستقيم الذي أمرَنَا الحقُّ بطلبه هو: الجمع بين الشريعة والحقيقة، والمفهوم من قوله: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ، ولذلك وصلَه به، فكأن الحق- سبحانه- يقول: يا عبادي احمدوني ومجدوني وأفردوني بالقصد وخُصُّوني بالعبادة، وكونوا في ظاهركم مشتغلين بعبادتي، وفي باطنكم مستعينين بحولي وقوتي، أو كونوا في ظاهركم متأدبين بخدمتي، وفي باطنكم مشاهدين لقدرتي وعظمة ربوبيتي.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-7","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"وقال سيدنا علي- كَرَّمَ الله وجهه-: (الصراط المستقيم هنا القرآن) . وقال جابر رضي الله عنه: (هو الإسلام) يعني الحنيفية السمحاء، وقال سهل بن عبد الله: (هو طريق محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم) . يعني اتباعَ ما جاء به. وحاصله ما تقدم من إصلاح الظاهر بالشريعة والباطن بالحقيقة، فهذا هو الطريق المستقيم الذي من سلكه كان من الواصلين المقربين مع النبيين والصدِّيقين.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-8","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"فإن قلتَ: إذا كان العبدُ ذاهباً على هذا المنهاج المستقيم، فكيف يطلب ما هو حاصل؟ فالجواب: أنه طلب التثبيت على ما هو حاصل، والإرشاد إلى ما هو ليس بحاصل، فأهل مقام الإسلام يطلبون الثبات على الإسلام، الذي هو حاصل، والترقي إلى مقام الإيمان الذي ليس بحاصل، على طريق الصوفية، الذين يخصون العمل الظاهر بمقام الإسلام، والعمل الباطن بمقام الإيمان، وأهلُ الإيمان يطلبون الثبات على الإيمان الذي هو حاصل، والترقي إلى مقام الإحسان الذي ليس بحاصل، وأهل مقام الإحسان يطلبون الثبات على الإحسان، والترقي إلى مالا نهاية له من كشوفات العرفان وَفَوْقَ كُلِّ ذِي عِلْمٍ عَلِيمٌ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-9","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"وقال الشيخ أبو العباس المرسي رضي الله عنه: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ بالتثبيت فيما هو حاصل، والإرشاد فيما ليس بحاصل، ثم قال: عمومُ المؤمنين يقولون: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ أي: بالتثبيت فيما هو","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-10","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"حاصل، والإرشاد لما ليس بحاصل، فإنه حصل لهم التوحيد وفاتَهُم درجات الصالحين، والصالحون يقولون:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-11","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ معناه: نسألك التثبيت فيما هو حاصل والإرشاد إلى ما ليس بحاصل، فإنهم حصل لهم الصلاح وفاتهم درجات الشهداء، والشهداءُ يقولون: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ أي بالتثبيت فيما هو حاصل والإرشاد إلى ما ليس بحاصل، فإنهم حصلت لهم الشهادة وفاتهم درجات الصديقين، والصديقون يقولون: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ أي: بالتثبيت فيما هو حاصل والإرشاد إلى ما ليس بحاصل، فإنهم حَصل لهم درجات الصديقين وفاتهم درجات القطب. والقطبُ يقول: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ بالتثبيت فيما هو حاصل والإرشاد إلى ما ليس بحاصل، فإنه حصل له رتبة القطبانية، وفاته علم ما إذا شاء الله أن يطلعه عليه أطلعه. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-12","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"وقال بعضهم: الهدايةُ إما للعين وإما للأثرِ الدالَّ على العين، ولا نهاية للأولى. قلت: فالأولى لأهل الشهود والعِيان، والثانية لأهل الدليل والبرهان، فالهداية للعين هي الدلالةُ على الله. والهداية للأثر هي الدلالة على العمل، «مَنْ دَلَّكَ على الله فقد نصحك، ومَن دلَّك على العمل فقد أتعبك» . وإنما كانت الأولى لا نهاية لها لأن الترقي بعد المعرفة لا نهاية له. بخلاف الدلالة على الأثر فنهايتها الوصول إلى العين، إن كان الدالُّ عارفاً بالطريق.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-13","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"قال البيضاوي: وهداية الله تتنوَّعُ أنواعاً لا يحصيها عد وَإِنْ تَعُدُّوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّهِ لا تُحْصُوها لكنها تنحصر في أجناس مترتبة:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-14","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"الأول: إِفاضَةُ الُقُوَى التي بها يتمكنُ المرء من الاهتداء إلى مصالحه، كالقوة العقلية والحواس الباطنة والمشاعر الظاهرة.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-15","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"الثاني: نَصْبُ الدلائل الفارقة بين الحق والباطل والصلاح والفساد، وإليه الإشارة بقوله: وَهَدَيْناهُ النَّجْدَيْنِ، وقال: فَهَدَيْناهُمْ فَاسْتَحَبُّوا الْعَمى عَلَى الْهُدى.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-16","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"الثالث الهدايةُ بإرسال الرسل وإنزال الكُتُب، وإياها عني بقوله: وَجَعَلْناهُمْ أَئِمَّةً يَهْدُونَ بِأَمْرِنا، وقوله:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-17","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"إِنَّ هذَا الْقُرْآنَ يَهْدِي لِلَّتِي هِيَ أَقْوَمُ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-18","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"الرابع: أن يكشف عن قلوبهم السرائر ويُرِيَهُمْ الأشياءَ كما هي بالوحي والإلهام والمنامات الصادقة. وهذا يختص بِنَيْله الأنبياءُ والأولياءُ، وإياه عني بقوله: أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ هَدَى اللَّهُ فَبِهُداهُمُ اقْتَدِهْ، وَالَّذِينَ جاهَدُوا فِينا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنا.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-19","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"فالمطلوب: إما زيادةُ ما مُنحوه من الهدى والثباتُ عليه، أو حصولُ المراتب المترتبة عليه، فإذا قال العارفُ الواصل عَنَى بقوله: أرشدنا طريق السير فيك، لتمحُوَ عنا ظلماتِ أحوالنا، وتُمِيطَ غواشِيَ أبداننا، لنستضيء بنور قدسك فنراكَ بنورك. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-20","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"قلت: قوله الرابع ... الخ، في عبارته قَلَقٌ واختصار، والصواب أن يقول: الرابع- أن يكشف عن قلوبهم الظُّلَمَ والأغيار، ويُشرق عليها الأنوار والأسرار، ويُريهم الأشياء كما هي بالوحي والإلهام، وباستعمال الفكرة في عظمةِ الملك العلاَّم، حتى تستولي أنوارُ المعاني على حِسِّ الأواني، ثم يقول: وهذا قسم يختصّ بنيله الأنبياء والأولياء.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-21","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"وقوله: فإذا قال العارف.. الخ، الصواب أن يقول: فإذا قاله المريد السائر لأن الواصل انمحت عنه الظلماتُ كلها والغواشي وسائرُ الأكدار لأن الله تعالى غطَّى وصفه بوصفه ونعته بنعته، فلم يَبْقَ له وصفٌ ظُلماني. وأيضاً قوله: [أرشدنا إلى طريق السير] إنما يناسب السائر دون الواصل لأن الواصل ما بَقِيَ له إلا الترقي، ولا يُسمى في اصطلاح الصوفية [السير] إلا قبلَ الوصول. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_4-22","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:6 — commentary","text":"ثم فسرّ الطريق المستقيم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_4-22"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_4-s1","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Guidance and the straight path: language and readings","text":"I:61–62 I say: Guidance ( الهداية , hidāya) originally means indicating or directing with gentleness ( الدلالة بلطف ), and for that reason it is normally used of what is good. “Guide them to the path of Hell” [37:23] is therefore ironic or derisive ( على التهكم ). The verb is hadā ( هدى ). Its normal construction takes the preposition li- or ilā; here it governs a direct object without a preposition, by analogy with “Moses chose his people” [7:155]. Ṣirāṭ ( الصراط ), in the language, means “road.” It is derived from saraṭa al-ṭaʿām, “he swallowed the food,” as though the road swallowed its travellers, those passing along it. The sīn was changed to ṣād to harmonise with the emphatic ṭāʾ ( الإطباق ); it may also be pronounced with an admixture of zāy because their points of articulation are close. Mustaqīm ( المستقيم ) means “having no crookedness.” What is intended is the path of the Real ( طريق الحق ) that brings one to God.","anchor":"en-fatiha_4-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_4-s2","r":"fatiha_4","title":"The straight path: Sacred Law and Reality","text":"I:62 The Real, glorious is His majesty, says, teaching His servants how to seek Him and what they ought to seek: Say, “Guide us” - direct us to the straight path that brings one to the Presence of bliss ( حضرة النعيم ). The straight path is outwardly to travel according to the Muḥammadan Sacred Law ( الشريعة المحمدية ), and inwardly to divest oneself of any claim to power or strength of one's own ( التبرّي من الحول والقوة ). Or say: it is that your outward be Sacred Law ( شريعة ) and your inward Reality ( حقيقة ); your outward servanthood ( عبودية ) and your inward freedom ( حرية ); distinction ( الفرق ) present outwardly, and gathering ( الجمع ) witnessed inwardly. In the Ḥikam: “When He makes you outwardly obedient to His command and inwardly surrendered to His overpowering might, He has bestowed an immense favour upon you.” The straight path that the Real commands us to seek is the conjunction of Sacred Law and Reality ( الجمع بين الشريعة والحقيقة ), understood from “You alone we worship, and from You alone we seek help.” Hence He joins the petition for guidance directly to those words. It is as though the Real, glorified is He, says: “My servants, praise Me and glorify Me, make Me alone your aim, and single Me out in worship. Outwardly occupy yourselves with My worship; inwardly seek assistance through My power and strength. Or outwardly observe the courtesies of My service; inwardly witness My power and the majesty of My Lordship.” Our master ʿAlī, may God ennoble his countenance, said: “The straight path here is the Qurʾān.” Jābir, may God be pleased with him, said: “It is Islam,” meaning the generous, upright religion ( الحنيفية السمحاء ). Sahl ibn ʿAbd Allāh said: “It is the path of Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace,” meaning following what he brought. The substance of these statements is what preceded: rectifying the outward through Sacred Law ( الشريعة ) and the inward through Reality ( الحقيقة ). This is the straight path; whoever travels it is among those who arrive and are brought near ( الواصلين المقربين ), together with the prophets and the utterly truthful.","anchor":"en-fatiha_4-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_4-s3","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Why the guided continue to ask for guidance","text":"If you ask: when the servant is already proceeding upon this straight way, how can he ask for what he already possesses? The answer is that he asks for firmness in what he has attained and guidance to what he has not attained. The people of the station of islām ask for steadfastness in the islām already attained and ascent ( الترقي ) to the station of īmān not yet attained. This follows Sufi usage, which assigns outward action specifically to the station of islām and inward action to the station of īmān. The people of īmān ask for steadfastness in the īmān attained and ascent to the station of iḥsān not yet attained. The people of iḥsān ask for steadfastness in iḥsān and ascent into the endless unveilings of gnosis ( كشوفات العرفان ): “Above every possessor of knowledge is one more knowing” [12:76]. I:62–63 Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mursī, may God be pleased with him, said: “‘Guide us upon the straight path’: by making us firm in what is attained, and directing us towards what is not attained.” Then he said: “The generality of believers say, ‘Guide us upon the straight path,’ meaning: by making us firm in what is attained and directing us towards what is not attained. They have attained the affirmation of unity, but the degrees of the righteous have escaped them. The righteous say, ‘Guide us upon the straight path,’ meaning: we ask You to make us firm in what is attained and direct us towards what is not attained. They have attained righteousness, but the degrees of the martyrs have escaped them. The martyrs say, ‘Guide us upon the straight path,’ meaning: by making us firm in what is attained and directing us towards what is not attained. They have attained martyrdom, but the degrees of the utterly truthful have escaped them. The utterly truthful say, ‘Guide us upon the straight path,’ meaning: by making us firm in what is attained and directing us towards what is not attained. They have attained the degrees of the utterly truthful, but the degrees of the Pole have escaped them. The Pole says, ‘Guide us upon the straight path’: by making him firm in what is attained and directing him towards what is not attained. He has attained the rank of the Pole, but there remains knowledge which, if God wills to acquaint him with it, He acquaints him with.” Here ends the quotation. I:63 Someone said: “Guidance is either to the Reality itself ( العين ) or to the trace ( الأثر ) that indicates the Reality; the first has no end.” I say: the first belongs to the people of witnessing and direct vision ( أهل الشهود والعيان ), the second to the people of proof and demonstration ( أهل الدليل والبرهان ). Guidance to the Reality itself is direction to God; guidance to the trace is direction to works. “Whoever directs you to God has counselled you sincerely; whoever directs you to works has wearied you.” The first has no end because ascent ( الترقي ) after gnosis ( المعرفة ) has no end. Direction to the trace is otherwise: its end is arrival ( الوصول ) at the Reality itself, provided the guide knows the path.","anchor":"en-fatiha_4-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_4-s4","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Al-Bayḍāwī’s four kinds of guidance","text":"Al-Bayḍāwī said: “God’s guidance takes forms beyond numbering: ‘If you count God’s blessing, you will not enumerate it’ [14:34]. Yet these fall within successively ordered kinds: “The first is the bestowal of the faculties through which a person is enabled to find his way to what benefits him, such as the intellectual faculty, the internal senses, and the external organs of perception. “The second is the establishment of indications distinguishing truth from falsehood, and soundness from corruption. This is indicated by His saying, ‘We guided him upon the two high ways’ [90:10], and ‘We guided them, but they preferred blindness to guidance’ [41:17]. “The third is guidance by sending messengers and sending down scriptures. This is meant by His saying, ‘We made them leaders, guiding by Our command’ [21:73], and ‘This Qurʾān guides towards that which is most upright’ [17:9]. “The fourth is that He should uncover the mysteries from their hearts and show them things as they are, through revelation, inspiration, and true dreams. The attainment of this is particular to the prophets and the saints. This is meant by His saying, ‘Those are they whom God guided; so follow their guidance’ [6:90], and ‘Those who strive in Us, We shall surely guide them upon Our ways’ [29:69]. I:64 “What is sought is therefore either an increase in the guidance already bestowed upon them and steadfastness in it, or the attainment of the degrees consequent upon it. When the gnostic who has arrived says it, he means by his words: ‘Direct us upon the path of journeying in You, that You may efface from us the darknesses of our states and remove the coverings of our bodies, so that we may be illumined by the light of Your holiness and see You through Your light.’” Here ends the quotation.","anchor":"en-fatiha_4-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_4-s5","r":"fatiha_4","title":"Ibn ʿAjība’s clarification: journeying, arrival and ascent","text":"I say: His wording under “the fourth” is awkward ( في عبارته قلق ) and overly compressed. The sounder expression would be: “The fourth is that He unveil from their hearts the darknesses and all other-than-God ( الظُّلَم والأغيار ), cause lights and mysteries ( الأنوار والأسرار ) to shine upon them, and show them things as they are through revelation and inspiration, and through employing reflection upon the majesty of the all-knowing King, until the lights of the meanings ( أنوار المعاني ) dominate the sensible aspect of the vessels ( حسّ الأواني ).” Then one should say: “This is a kind whose attainment is particular to prophets and saints.” As for his words, “When the gnostic who has arrived says it...,” the sounder wording is: “When the disciple who is journeying ( المريد السائر ) says it.” For from one who has arrived ( الواصل ), all darknesses, coverings, and other turbidity have been effaced: God Most High has covered his description with His Description and his attribute with His Attribute, so no dark attribute remains to him. Moreover, “Direct us to the path of journeying ( طريق السير )” suits the traveller ( السائر ), not one who has arrived. The one who has arrived has nothing left but ascent ( الترقي ); in Sufi technical usage ( اصطلاح الصوفية ), “journeying” ( السير ) is used only for what precedes arrival ( الوصول ). God Most High knows best. He then explained the straight path, saying:","anchor":"en-fatiha_4-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"fatiha_5","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary 1:7","anchor":"unit-fatiha_5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-1","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"صِراطَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا الضَّالِّينَ (7)","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-2","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"قلت: (صراط) بدل من الأول- بدل الكل من الكل- وهو في حكم تكرير العامل من حيث إنه المقصود بالنسبة، وفائدته: التوكيد والتنصيص على أن طريق المسلمين هو المشهود عليه بالاستقامة، على آكد وجه وأبلغه لأنه جعله كالتفسير والبيان له، فكأنه من البيِّن الذي لا خفاء فيه، وأن الصراط المستقيم ما يكون طريق المؤمنين، وغَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ بدل من (الذين) على معنى أن المنعم عليهم هم الذين سَلِمُوا من الغضب والضلال.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-3","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"أو صفة له مُبيَّنة أو مقيدة على معنى أنهم جمعوا بين النعمة المطلقة، وهي نعمة الإيمان، وبين السلامة من الغضب والضلال، وذلك إنما يصح بأحد تأويلين: إجراء الموصول مجرى النكرة، إذ لم يُقصد به معهود كالمعرَّف في قوله:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-4","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"ولَقَد أَمُرُ علُى اللئيم يَسُبنّي(1) ...","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-5","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"أو يُجعل (غير) مَعْرِفةً لأنه أُضيف إلى مآلَهُ ضدٍّ واحد، وهو المنعمُ عليه، فيتعينُ تَعيُّن الحركة غير السكون، وإلا لزِم عليه نعت المعرفة بالنكرة. فتأملْهُ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-6","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"والغضبُ: ثَوَرانُ النفس إرادةَ الانتقام، فإذا أسند إلى الله تعالى أريد غايته وهو العقوبة، و (عليهم) نائب فاعل، و (لا) مَزيدة لتأكيد ما في (غير) من معنى النفي، فكأنه قال: ولا المغضوب عَلَيْهِم وَلاَ الضآلين، وقرأ عمر رضي الله عنه (وغير الضالين) والضلال: العدول عن الطريق السوي عمداً أو خطأً، وله عرض عَريضٌ والتفاوت بين أدناه وأقصاه كبير. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-7","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وإنما أَسند النعمة إلى الله والغضبَ إلى المجهول تعليماً للأدب، مَّآ أَصابَكَ مِنْ حَسَنَةٍ فَمِنَ اللَّهِ ... الآية.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-8","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في تفسير الطريق المستقيم: هو طريق الذين أنعمتُ عليهم بالهداية والاستقامة، والمعرفة العامة والخاصة، من النبيين والصديقين والشهداء والصالحين، والمُنعَم عليهم في الآية مطلق، يصدق بكل منعَم عليه بالمعرفة والاستقامة في دينه، كالصحابة وأضرابِهِمْ. وقيل: المراد بهم أصحاب سيدنا موسى عليه السلام قبل التحريف. وقيل: أصحاب سيدنا عيسى قبل التغيير. والتحقيق أنه عام.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-9","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"قال البيضاوي: ونِعَمُ الله وإن كانت لا تُحصى كما قال الله: وَإِنْ تَعُدُّوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ لا تُحْصُوها تنحصر في جنسين: دنيوي وأخروي.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-10","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"فالأول: وهو الدنيوي- قسمان: موهبي وكَسْبِي، والموهبي قسمان: رُوحاني، كنفخ الروح فيه وإشراقه بالعقل وما يتبعه من القوي، كالفهم والفكر والنطق، وجسماني: كتخليق البدن بالقوة الحالة فيه والهيئات العارضة له من الصحة وكمال الأعضاء. والكسبي: كتزكية النفس عن الرذائل، وتحليتها بالأخلاق الحسنة والملكات الفاضلة، وتزيين البدن بالهيئات المطبوعة والحُلي المستحسنة، وحصول الجاه والمال.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-11","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"والثاني: وهو الأُخروي-: أن يغفر له ما فَرَطَ منه ويرضى عنه ويبوئه في أعلى علِّيين، مع الملائكة المقربين أبد الآبدين، والمراد القسمُ الأخير، وما يكون وُصْلة إلى نيله من القسم الأول، وأما ما عدا ذلك فيشترك فيه المؤمن والكافر. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-12","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"قال ابن جُزَيّ: النعم التي يقع عليها الشكر ثلاثة أقسام، دنيوية: كالصحة والعافية والمال الحلال. ودينية:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-13","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"كالعلم والتقوى والمعرفة. وأخرويةٌ: كالثواب على العمل القليل بالعطاء الجزيل. وقال أيضاً: والناس في الشكر على مقامين: منهم مَن يشكر على النعم الواصلة إليه، الخاصة به، ومنهم مَن يشكر الله عن جميع خلقه على النعم الواصلة إلى جميعهم. والشكر على ثلاث درجات: فدرجة العوام: الشكر على النِّعم، ودرجة الخواص: الشكر على النِّعم والنقم وعلى كل حال، ودرجة خواص الخواص: أن يغيب عن رؤية النعمة بمشاهدة المُنعم. قال رجل","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-14","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"لإبراهيم بن أدهم رضى الله عنه: الفقراء إذا أُعْطُوا شَكَرُوا وإذا مُنعوا صبروا، فقال إبراهيم: هذه أخلاقُ الكلاب، ولكن القومَ إذا مُنِعوا شكروا وإذا أُعْطُوا آثروا. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-15","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"ثم احترس من الطريق غير المستقيمة، فقال: غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ أي: غير طريق الذين غضبت عليهم، فلا تهدنا إليها ولا تسلك بنا سبيلها، بل سلَّمنَا من مواردها. والمراد بهم: اليهود، كذا فسرها النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم، ويَصْدُقُ بحسب العموم على كل من غضب الله عليهم، وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ أي: ولا طريق الضالين، أي: التالفين عن الحق، وهم النصارى كما قال صلى الله عليه وسلّم. والتفسيران مأخوذان من كتاب الله تعالى. قال تعالى في شأن اليهود:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-16","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"فَباؤُ بِغَضَبٍ عَلى غَضَبٍ، وقال في حق النصارى: قَدْ ضَلُّوا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَأَضَلُّوا كَثِيراً وَضَلُّوا عَنْ سَواءِ السَّبِيلِ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-17","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"واعلم أن الحق- سبحانه- قسم خلقه على ثلاثة أقسام: قسم أعدَّهم للكرم والإحسان، ليظهر فيهم اسمه الكريم أو الرحيم، وهم المنعم عليهم بالإيمان والاستقامة. وقسم أعدَّهم للانتقام والغضب، ليُظهر فيهم اسمه المنتقم أو القهار، وهم المغضوب عليهم والضالون عن طريق الحق عقلاً أو عملاً، وهم الكفار، وقسم أعدَّهم الله للحِلْم والعفو، ليُظهر فيهم اسمه تعالى الحليم والعفو، وهم أهل العصيان من المؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-18","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"فمن رَامَ أن يكونَ الوجودُ خالياً من هذه الأقسام الثلاثة، وأن يكون الناس كلهم سواء في الهداية أو ضدها، فهو جاهل بالله وبأسمائه إذ لا بد من ظهور آثار أسمائه في هذا الآدمي، من كرم وقهرية وحِلْم وغير ذلك. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-19","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"الإشارة: الطريق المستقيم التي أمرنا الحق بطلبها هي: طريق الوصول إلى الحضرة، التي هي العلم بالله على نعت الشهود والعيان، وهو مقام التوحيد الخاص، الذي هو أعلى درجات أهل التوحيد، وليس فوقه إلا مقامُ توحيد الأنبياء والرسل، ولا بد فيه من تربية على يد شيخ كامل عارف بطريق السير، قد سلك المقامات ذوقاً وكشفاً، وحاز مقام الفناء والبقاء، وجمع بين الجذب والسلوك لأن الطريق عويص، قليلٌ خُطَّارُهُ، كثيرٌ قُطَّاعُه، وشيطان هذه الطريق فَقِيهٌ بمقاماته ونوازِله، فلا بد فيه من دليل، وإلا ضلّ سالكها عن سواء السبيل، وإلى هذا المعنى أشار ابن البنا، حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-20","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وَإِنَّمَا القَوْمُ مُسَافِرُونَ ... لِحَضْرَةِ الْحَقِّ وَظَاعِنُونَ","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-21","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"فَافْتَقَرُوا فِيهِ إلَى دَلِيل ... ذِي بَصَرٍ بالسَّيْرِ وَالْمَقِيلِ","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-22","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"قَدْ سَلَكَ الطَّرِيقَ ثُمَّ عَادَ ... لِيُخْبِرَ الْقَوْمَ بِمَا اسْتَفَادَ","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-23","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وقال في لطائف المنن: (مَن لم يكن له أستاذ يصله بسلسلة الأتباع، ويكشف له عن قلبه القناع، فهو في هذا الشأن لَقيطٌ لا أب له، دعي لا نسب له، فإن يكن له نور فالغالب غلبة الحال عليه، والغالب عليه وقوفه مع ما يرد من الله إليه، لم تَرْضْهُ سياسةُ التأديب والتهذيب، ولم يقده زمام التربية والتدريب) ، فهذا الطريق الذي ذكرنا هو الذي يستشعره القارئ للفاتحة عند قوله: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ مع الترقي الذي ذكره الشيخ أبو العباس المرسي رضى الله عنه المتقدم، وإذا قرأ صِراطَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ استشعر، أَيْ: أنعمتَ عليهم بالوصول والتمكين في معرفتك.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-24","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وقال الورتجبي: اهدنا مُرَادَك مِنَّا لأن الصراط المستقيم ما أراد الحق من الخلق، من الصدق والإخلاص في عبوديته وخدمته. ثم، قال: وقيل: اهدنا هُدَى العِيَانِ بعد البيان، لنستقيم لك حسب إرادتِك. وقيل: اهدنا هُدَى مَنْ يكون منك مبدؤه ليكون إليك منتهاه. ثم قال: وقال بعضهم: اهدنا، أي: ثبِّتْنا على الطريق الذي لا اعوجاج فيه، وهو الإسلام، وهو الطريق المستقيم والمنهاج القويم صِراطَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ أي: منازل الذين أنعمت عليهم بالمعرفة والمحبة وحسن الأدب في الخدمة. ثم قال: غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ يعني: المطرودين عن باب العبودية، وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ يعني المُفْلِسين عن نفائس المعرفة هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-25","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"قلت: والأحسن أن يقال: غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ هم الذين أَوْقَفَهُمْ عن السير اتباعُ الحظوظ والشهوات، فأوقعهم في مَهَاوِي العصيان والمخالفات، وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ هم الذين حبسهم الجهل والتقليد، فلم تنفُذْ بصائرهم إلى خالص التوحيد، فنكصوا عن توحيد العيان إلى توحيد الدليل والبرهان، وهو ضلال عند أهل الشهود والعِيان، ولو بلغ في الصلاح غايةَ الإمكان.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-26","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وقال في الإحياء: إذا قلت بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ فافْهَمْ أن الأمور كلها بالله، وأن المراد هاهنا المُسمَّى، وإذا كانت الأمورُ كلها بالله فلا جرَم أنَّ الحمد كله لله، ثم قال: وإذا قلت: الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ فأحضرْ في قلبك أنواعَ لطفه لتتفتحَ لك رحمتُه فينبعث به رجاؤُك، ثم استشعر من قلبك التعظيم والخوف من قولك: يَوْمِ الدِّينِ. ثم قال: ثم جَدَّد الإخلاص بقولك: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ. وجدَّد العجز والاحتياج والتبرِّيَ من الحوْل والقوة بقولك: وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ، ثم اطلب اسم حاجتك، وقل: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ الذي يسوقنا إلى جوارك ويُفضي بنا إلى مرضاتك، وزِدْهُ شرحاً وتفصيلاً وتأكيداً، واستشهد بالذين أفاض عليهم نعم الهداية من النبيين والصديقين والشهداء والصالحين، دون الذين غضب عليهم من الكفار والزائغين واليهود والنصارى والصابئين.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-27","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"هـ. ملخصاً.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-28","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وقال القشيري: قوله تعالى: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ الأمر في هذه الآية مضمر، أي: قولوا: اهدنا.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-29","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"والصراط المستقيم: طريق الحق، وهو ما عليه أهل التوحيد، أي: أرشدْنا إلى الحق لئلا نتكل على وسائط المعاملات، فيقعَ على وجه التوحيد غُبَارُ الظنون والحسابات لتكون دليلنا عليك. ثم قال: صِراطَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ أي: الواصلين بك إليك، ثم قال: غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ بنسيان التوفيق والتَّعامِي عن رؤية التأييد، وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ عن شهودِ سابقِ الاختيار، وجريان تصاريف الأقدار. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-31","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"تتمات:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-31"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-32","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"الأولى: هذه السورة جمعت معانى القرآن كلّها، فكأنها نسخة مختصرة منه، ولذلك سميت أمّ القرآن، فالإلهيات حاصلة من قوله: الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ. الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ، والدار الآخرة من قوله: مَلِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ، والعبادات كلّها من الاعتقادات والأحكام الظاهرة التي تقتضيها الأوامر والنواهي، من قوله: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ والمقامات وأسرار المعاملات الباطنة- تخلية وتحلية- من قوله: اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ والأنبياء وغيرهم من قوله: الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ وذكر طوائف الكفار من قوله: غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-32"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-33","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وقال الشيخ ابن أبي جمرة رضى الله عنه فى بيان تضمنها لكتاب الله: إن لفظ (الحمد) يتضمن كل ما في كتاب الله من الحمد والشكر لأن الحمد أعمّ من الشكر، وأتى بالعام ليدل على الصفتين. ولفظة (الله) تدل على ما فى الكتاب العزيز من أسماء الترفيع والتعظيم لأنه قيل: أنه اسم الله الأعظم، ولفظ: رَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ يدل على ما فيه من أسماء الله، سبحانه، وعلى العوالم وعلى اختلافها وخالقها والمتصرف فيها. ولفظ: الرَّحْمنِ الرَّحِيمِ يتضمن كل ما فى الكتاب من المغفرة والرحمة والإنعام والعفو والإفضال، ولفظ مَلِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ يدل على ما فيه من ذكر الآخرة وما فيه من الأهوال، ولفظ إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ يتضمن ما فيه من التعبّدات وإفراده بالألوهية، ولفظ إِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ يدل على ما فيه من طلب الاستعانة وذكر الاضطرار، ولفظ اهْدِنَا الصِّراطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ يتضمن ما فيه من طلب الهداية إلى سبيل الخير، ولفظ: صِراطَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ يتضمن ما فيه من ذكر الخصوص والمرضىّ عنهم والمعفوّ عنهم وأهل السعادة، ولفظ غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ يتضمن ما فيه من أنواع الكفر والمخالفات ومساوئهم ومآلهم فاستحقّت أن تسمى أمّا. هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-33"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-34","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وعن عليّ- كرّم الله وجهه- قال: (شرح موسى عليه السّلام التوراة فى سبعين سفرا، ولو أذن لى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم لأوقرت على الفاتحة سبعين بعيرا) . قلت: قوله (سبعين) تقريبا، وإلا فهى قابلة لأكثر من ذلك، وتفصيل ذلك يطول، وقد ذكرنا أصول علومها فى شرحنا الكبير عليها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-34"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-35","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"الثانية: قال ابن جزىّ: قولنا: الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ أفضل عند المحققين من (لا إله إلا الله) لوجهين:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-35"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-36","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"أحدهما: ما أخرج النّسائيّ: عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم «أنه مَن قال: لا إله إلا الله، كتبت له عشرون حسنة، ومن قال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-36"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-37","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"الحمد لله رب العالمين، كتبت له ثلاثون حسنة» . والثاني: أن التوحيد الذي تقتضيه (لا إله إلا الله) ، حاصل فى قولك: (رب العالمين) وزادت بقولك: الحمد لله، وفيه من المعاني ما قدّمنا. وأما قوله صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «أفضل ما قلته أنا والنبيون من قبلى: لا إله إلا الله» فإنما ذلك للتوحيد الذي تقتضيه، وقد شاركتها (الحمد لله رب العالمين) فى ذلك وزادت عليها. وهذا لمؤمن حقّق إيمانه وطلب الثواب، وأما لمن دخل فى الإسلام فيتعيّن «لا إله إلا الله» . هـ.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-37"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-38","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"قلت: والتحقيق أن كل ما يدل على التوحيد من الألفاظ يكفى فى الدخول فى الإسلام، كما قال البنانىّ فى حاشيته.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-38"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-39","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"الثالثة: قراءة الفاتحة فى الصلاة واجبة عند مالك والشافعي خلافاً لأبي حنيفة، وقد ذكرنا فى الشرح الكبير منشأ الخلاف.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-39"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-40","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"الرابعة: التأمين عند ختم الفاتحة مطلوب للدعاء الذي فيها، قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «ما حسدتكم اليهود على شىء ما حسدتكم على السّلام والتّأمين» . رواه ابن ماجة. وقال أيضا صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «إن الله أعطانى خصالا ثلاثة:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-40"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-41","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"أعطانى صلاة الصّفوف وأعطانى التحية، وإنها لتحية أهل الجنة، وأعطانى التأمين، ولم يعطه أحدا من النبيين قبلى، إلا أن يكون الله أعطاه هارون، يدعو موسى ويؤمن هارون» رواه ابن خزيمة. وسمع عليه الصلاة والسلام رجلا يدعو ويلح فقال: «أوجب إن ختم» فقال بعض القوم: بأيّ شىء يختم؟ فقال: «يؤمن فإنه إن ختم بآمين فقد أوجب» . قال أبو زهير- راوى الحديث- فإن آمين مثل الطّابع على الصحيفة. ولعلّه مرفوع إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم، رواه أبو داود.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-41"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-42","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"ولفظ آمِّينَ بالمدّ والقصر مخففا. وتشديد الميم لغة. قيل: هو اسم من أسماء الله تعالى.. وقيل معناه: اللهم استجب، أو كذلك فافعل، أو كذلك فليكن. قاله المنذرى فى الترغيب. قال البيضاوي: بنى على الفتح كأين لالتقاء الساكنين، وجاء مدّ ألفه وقصرها. قال:","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-42"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-43","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"ويرحم الله عبدا قال آمينا(1)","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-43"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-44","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"وليس من القرآن اتفاقا، ولكن يسنّ ختم السورة به لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «علّمنى جبريل عليه السّلام آمين عند فراغى من قراءة الفاتحة» . وقال: إنّه كالختم على الكتاب.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-44"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-45","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"ويقوله الإمام ويجهر به فى الجهرية، لما روى عن وائل بن حجر «أنه عليه الصلاة والسلام كان إذا قرأ: وَلَا الضَّالِّينَ قال: آمين، رفع بها صوته» وعن أبى حنيفة- رحمه الله- أنه لا يقوله. والمشهور عنه أنه يخفيه كما رواه عبد الله بن مُغفل وأنس. قلت: ومشهور مذهب مالك أن الإمام لا يقوله فى الجهرية.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-45"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-fatiha_5-46","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Al-Fātiḥa 1:7 — commentary","text":"ثم قال: والمأموم يؤمن معه لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «إذا قال الإمام ولا الضالين، فقولوا: آمين، فإن الملائكة تقول: آمين، فمن وافق تأمينه تأمين الملائكة غُفِر لَه ما تقدَم من ذنبه» . وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق. وصلّى الله على سيدنا ومولانا محمد عين الحق والتحقيق، وعلى آله وصحبه المطهرين بعده، أعلام الطريق، وسلّم تسليما.","anchor":"ar-fatiha_5-46"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s1","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Substitution, qualification and negation","text":"I say: the second “path” ( صراط ) is a substitute ( بدل ) for the first - specifically, substitution of the whole for the whole ( بدل الكل من الكل ). It is, in effect, like repeating the grammatical governor ( العامل ), since the substitute is what is ultimately intended by the syntactic relation ( المقصود بالنسبة ). Its function is confirmation ( التوكيد ) and explicit specification ( التنصيص ), in the strongest and most emphatic manner, that the path of the Muslims is the path attested to be straight. He makes the second phrase an explanation and clarification of the first, as though this were self-evident and without obscurity: the straight path is the path of the believers. “Not those upon whom wrath has fallen” ( غير المغضوب عليهم ) may itself be a substitute ( بدل ) for “those” ( الذين ), meaning that those blessed are precisely those kept safe from wrath and error. Or it may be an explanatory or restrictive adjective ( صفة مبيِّنة أو مقيِّدة ): they combine the unrestricted blessing - the blessing of faith - with safety from wrath and error. This grammatical analysis is sound only on one of two interpretations: either the relative expression ( الموصول ) is treated like an indefinite ( النكرة ), since no previously identified group ( معهود ) is intended, as with the formally definite expression in the poet's words, “Indeed, I pass by the base fellow who reviles me...” Or ghayr ( غير , “other than/not”) is treated as definite ( معرفة ) because it is annexed to something having a single contrary - namely, the one blessed - and so it becomes determinate in the way “motion, other than rest” is determinate. Otherwise the construction would require a definite noun ( المعرفة ) to be qualified by an indefinite adjective ( النكرة ). Reflect upon it. I:65 Wrath ( الغضب ) is the soul's agitation with the will to take vengeance. When attributed to God Most High, what is intended is its end-result ( غايته ): punishment. “Upon them” ( عليهم ) stands as the deputy subject ( نائب فاعل ) of the passive participle al-maghḍūb. The lā in “nor” is pleonastic/additional ( مزيدة ) for strengthening the negation already contained in ghayr, as though He had said: “neither those upon whom wrath has fallen nor those who are astray.” ʿUmar, may God be pleased with him, recited, “and other than those who are astray.” Error ( الضلال ) is turning aside from the even path, deliberately or mistakenly. It has a very broad extension, and the distance between its lowest and highest degrees is great. So said al-Bayḍāwī. The bestowal of favour is ascribed to God, whereas wrath is expressed in the passive, to teach courtesy: “Whatever good befalls you is from God …” [4:79], and the rest of the verse.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s2","r":"fatiha_5","title":"The recipients of divine favour","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says, explaining the straight path: “It is the path of those upon whom I have bestowed favour through guidance, uprightness, and general and special gnosis: the prophets, the utterly truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous.” “Those upon whom favour has been bestowed” is unrestricted in the verse. It applies to everyone favoured with gnosis and uprightness in his religion, such as the Companions and their like. It has been said that the followers of our master Moses, peace be upon him, before the distortion are intended. It has also been said that the followers of our master Jesus before the alteration are intended. The sound determination is that its meaning is general.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s3","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Kinds of blessings","text":"Al-Bayḍāwī said: “Although God’s blessings are innumerable, as God says, ‘If you count God’s blessing, you will not enumerate it’ [14:34], they fall into two kinds: worldly and otherworldly. “The first, the worldly, has two divisions: bestowed and acquired. The bestowed has two divisions. One is spiritual: the breathing of the spirit into a person and his illumination by the intellect and the faculties consequent upon it, such as understanding, thought, and speech. The other is bodily: the formation of the body with the power inhering in it and the conditions that come upon it, such as health and completeness of its members. Acquired blessings include purifying the soul of vices, adorning it with good character and virtuous dispositions, embellishing the body with pleasing appearances and comely ornaments, and acquiring standing and wealth. “The second, the otherworldly, is that He should forgive a person’s previous faults, be pleased with him, and give him a dwelling in the highest heights, with the angels brought near, for ever and ever. It is this last division that is intended, together with whatever in the first division serves as a means of attaining it. In other things, believers and unbelievers share.” Here ends the quotation.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s4","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Degrees of thanksgiving","text":"I:65–66 Ibn Juzayy said: “The blessings for which thanksgiving ( الشكر ) is rendered are of three kinds: worldly, such as health, well-being, and lawful wealth; religious, such as knowledge, reverent fear, and gnosis ( المعرفة ); and otherworldly, such as abundant reward for little work.” He also said: “People occupy two stations in thanksgiving. Some give thanks for blessings that reach them personally and belong especially to them; others thank God on behalf of all His creatures for blessings reaching them all. Thanksgiving has three degrees: the common people give thanks for blessings; the elect give thanks for blessings and afflictions, in every state; the elect of the elect become absent from seeing the blessing through witnessing the Benefactor ( مشاهدة المنعم ).” A man said to Ibrāhīm ibn Adham, may God be pleased with him: “When the spiritual poor are given, they give thanks; when they are denied, they are patient.” Ibrāhīm replied: “Those are the manners of dogs! Our people give thanks when denied, and when given, prefer others to themselves.”","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s5","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Wrath and straying","text":"I:66 He then guarded against the path that is not straight, saying, “not those upon whom wrath has fallen”: that is, not the path of those with whom You are angry. Do not guide us to it or lead us along its way, but keep us safe from the places to which it leads. The Jews are intended; thus the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace, explained it. In its general application it holds of all those with whom God is angry. “Nor those who are astray”: that is, nor the path of those who are astray, who have lost the truth. These are the Christians, as he, God bless him and grant him peace, said. Both explanations are taken from the Book of God Most High. He says concerning the Jews, “They incurred wrath upon wrath” [2:90], and concerning the Christians, “They went astray before, led many astray, and strayed from the even way” [5:77].","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s6","r":"fatiha_5","title":"The divine Names and the three classes of creation","text":"Know that the Real, glorified is He, has divided His creatures into three classes. One class He prepared for generosity and beneficence, to manifest in them His Name the Generous or the Ever-Merciful. These are those favoured with faith and uprightness. Another class He prepared for retribution and wrath, to manifest in them His Name the Avenger or the Overpowering. These are those upon whom wrath has fallen and who stray from the path of truth in understanding or in action: the unbelievers. A third class God prepared for forbearance and pardon, to manifest in them His Names the Forbearing and the Pardoner. These are the disobedient among the believers. Whoever wishes existence to be free of these three classes, and all people to be alike in guidance or in its opposite, is ignorant of God and His Names. For the effects of His Names must appear in the human being: generosity, overpowering might, forbearance, and the rest. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s7","r":"fatiha_5","title":"The path of arrival and spiritual guidance","text":"The straight path that the Real commands us to seek is the path of arrival ( طريق الوصول ) at the Presence ( الحضرة ): knowledge of God in the mode of witnessing and direct vision ( العلم بالله على نعت الشهود والعيان ). This is the station of the special tawḥīd ( مقام التوحيد الخاص ), the highest degree of the people of tawḥīd; above it is only the tawḥīd of the prophets and messengers. It necessarily requires spiritual formation at the hands of a perfected shaykh who knows the path of journeying ( طريق السير ), has traversed the stations through tasting ( ذوقاً ) and unveiling ( كشفاً ), has attained the stations of effacement and subsistence ( الفناء والبقاء ), and has combined attraction and wayfaring ( الجذب والسلوك ). The path is difficult, its travellers few and its highwaymen many; the devil of this path is learned in its stations and the occurrences that arise in them ( نوازله ). A guide is therefore indispensable, otherwise the traveller will stray from the even way. Ibn al-Bannāʾ alluded to this meaning: The folk are travellers, journeying toward the Presence of the Real. Upon this way they therefore need a guide, one with insight into travel and the resting-place, who has travelled the path and then returned to tell the people what he gained. I:67 In Laṭāʾif al-minan it is said: “Whoever has no master to connect him with the chain of following ( سلسلة الأتباع ) and lift the covering from his heart is, in this affair, a foundling without a father and a claimant without lineage. If he possesses light, the usual case is that the spiritual state overwhelms him, and that he stops with whatever comes to him from God. The governance of discipline and refinement ( سياسة التأديب والتهذيب ) has not trained him, nor have the reins of formation and exercise ( التربية والتدريب ) led him.” This path is what the reciter of al-Fātiḥa should inwardly call to mind at “Guide us upon the straight path,” together with the ascent ( الترقي ) mentioned earlier by Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mursī. At “the path of those whom You have blessed,” he should inwardly apprehend: those whom You blessed with arrival ( الوصول ) and firm establishment ( التمكين ) in gnosis of You.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s8","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Guidance, deprivation and fulfilment","text":"Al-Wartajbī said: “Guide us to what You desire of us; the straight path is what the Real desires from creation: truthfulness and sincerity in His servanthood ( عبوديته ) and service.” Then: “It has been said: ‘Guide us with the guidance of direct vision ( هدى العيان ) after clear exposition ( البيان ), so that we may stand straight before You according to Your will.’ It has also been said: ‘Guide us with the guidance of one whose beginning is from You, so that his end may be unto You.’” He then quotes someone who said: “‘Guide us’ means: make us firm upon the path in which there is no crookedness, namely Islam, the straight path and upright way. ‘The path of those whom You have blessed’: the stations of those whom You blessed with gnosis, love, and beautiful courtesy in service.” He then said: “‘Not those upon whom wrath has fallen’: those expelled from the gate of servanthood. ‘Nor those who are astray’: those bankrupt of the precious treasures of gnosis.” I say: it is better to say that “not those upon whom wrath has fallen” are those whom following their egoic shares and appetites ( الحظوظ والشهوات ) has halted from journeying ( السير ), casting them into the abysses of disobedience and opposition. “Nor those who are astray” are those whom ignorance and imitation ( الجهل والتقليد ) have imprisoned, so that their inner sights ( بصائرهم ) do not penetrate to pure tawḥīd. They have recoiled from the tawḥīd of direct vision ( توحيد العيان ) to the tawḥīd of proof and demonstration ( توحيد الدليل والبرهان ). Among the people of witnessing and direct vision ( أهل الشهود والعيان ), this is a kind of error, even if a person reaches the utmost possible degree of righteousness.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s9","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Inward attentiveness when reciting al-Fātiḥa","text":"In the Iḥyāʾ it is said: “When you say, ‘In the Name of God, the All-Merciful, the Ever-Merciful,’ understand that all affairs are through God, and that what is intended here is the One named. If all affairs are through God, it necessarily follows that all praise belongs to God.” Then he said: “When you say, ‘The All-Merciful, the Ever-Merciful,’ bring the forms of His gentleness into your heart, so that His mercy may open to you and your hope may be stirred by it. Then let your heart feel magnification and fear at your words, ‘the Day of Recompense.’” Then he said: “Renew sincerity with your saying, ‘You alone we worship,’ and renew helplessness, need, and the disclaiming of strength and power with your saying, ‘and You alone we ask for help.’ Then ask for your need by name, and say, ‘Guide us upon the straight path,’ which leads us to Your proximity and brings us to Your good pleasure. Add explanation, detail, and confirmation to it, and invoke the testimony of those upon whom He poured the blessings of guidance: the prophets, the utterly truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, as distinct from those upon whom His wrath fell among the unbelievers, the deviating, the Jews, the Christians, and the Sabians.” Here ends the abridged quotation. I:68 Al-Qushayrī said: “In ‘Guide us upon the straight path,’ the imperative is implicit ( الأمر مضمر ): that is, ‘Say: Guide us.’ The straight path is the path of the Real, the way of the people of tawḥīd. That is: ‘Direct us to the Real, lest we rely upon the intermediary means of our dealings ( وسائط المعاملات ) and the dust of suppositions and reckonings fall upon the face of tawḥīd; be Yourself our guide to You.’ ‘The path of those whom You have blessed’ means those who arrive through You unto You. ‘Not those upon whom wrath has fallen’: through forgetting divine enabling ( التوفيق ) and deliberately blinding themselves to divine support ( التأييد ). ‘Nor those who are astray’: from witnessing the antecedence of divine choice ( سابق الاختيار ) and the unfolding dispositions of the decrees ( تصاريف الأقدار ).”","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s10","r":"fatiha_5","title":"1. Al-Fātiḥa as a summary of the Qurʾān","text":"This sūrah gathers all the meanings of the Qurʾān, as though it were an abridged copy of it. For this reason it is called the Mother of the Qurʾān. Matters concerning divinity are contained in His saying, “Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds, the All-Merciful, the Ever-Merciful”; the abode of the hereafter in His saying, “King of the Day of Recompense”; all forms of worship, comprising beliefs and the outward ordinances entailed by commands and prohibitions, in His saying, “You alone we worship”; the spiritual stations and the mysteries of inward dealings, through purification and adornment [of the soul], in His saying, “Guide us upon the straight path”; the prophets and others in His saying, “those upon whom You have bestowed favour”; and the mention of the classes of unbelievers in His saying, “not those upon whom wrath has fallen, nor those who are astray.” Shaykh Ibn Abī Jamra, may God be pleased with him, said, explaining how it comprises the Book of God: “The word ‘praise’ includes everything in the Book of God relating to praise and thanksgiving, for praise is more general than thanksgiving: the more general term was used to indicate both attributes. The word ‘God’ indicates what is in the Mighty Book of Names of exaltation and magnification, since it has been said to be God’s Greatest Name. The phrase ‘Lord of the worlds’ indicates what it contains of the Names of God, glorified is He, and of the worlds, their differences, their Creator, and the One who disposes their affairs. ‘The All-Merciful, the Ever-Merciful’ includes everything in the Book relating to forgiveness, mercy, the bestowal of blessings, pardon, and munificence. ‘King of the Day of Recompense’ indicates its mention of the hereafter and its terrors. ‘You alone we worship’ includes its acts of worship and the singling of Him out as God. ‘You alone we ask for help’ indicates its requests for assistance and its mention of utter need. ‘Guide us upon the straight path’ includes its requests for guidance upon the way of good. ‘The path of those upon whom You have bestowed favour’ includes its mention of the elect, those with whom God is pleased, those who are pardoned, and the people of felicity. ‘Not those upon whom wrath has fallen’ includes its kinds of unbelief and transgression, the evil qualities of those concerned, and their final end. It therefore deserves to be called a Mother.” Here ends the quotation. I:69 It is related from ʿAlī, may God ennoble his countenance, that he said: “Moses, peace be upon him, expounded the Torah in seventy volumes. If the Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace, gave me leave, I would load seventy camels with an exposition of al-Fātiḥa.” I say: his mention of “seventy” is approximate, for it admits of more than that. The detail would be lengthy. We have mentioned the foundations of its sciences in our greater commentary upon it. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s11","r":"fatiha_5","title":"2. Praise, tawḥīd and entering Islam","text":"Ibn Juzayy said: “According to the discerning scholars, our saying, ‘Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds,’ is superior to ‘There is no god but God,’ for two reasons. The first is what al-Nasāʾī related from the Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace: ‘Whoever says, “There is no god but God,” has twenty good deeds recorded for him, and whoever says, “Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds,” has thirty good deeds recorded for him.’ The second is that the affirmation of unity entailed by ‘There is no god but God’ is contained in your saying, ‘Lord of the worlds,’ while the phrase adds your words, ‘Praise belongs to God,’ with the meanings we have already explained. As for his saying, God bless him and grant him peace, ‘The best thing that I and the prophets before me have said is: There is no god but God,’ this is because of the affirmation of unity which it entails. ‘Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds’ shares that affirmation and adds something to it. This applies to a believer who has made his faith firm and seeks reward. For one entering Islam, however, ‘There is no god but God’ is specifically required.” Here ends the quotation. I say: The sound determination is that any expression indicating the affirmation of unity suffices for entering Islam, as al-Bannānī said in his gloss.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s12","r":"fatiha_5","title":"3. Reciting al-Fātiḥa in prayer","text":"Reciting al-Fātiḥa in prayer is obligatory according to Mālik and al-Shāfiʿī, contrary to Abū Ḥanīfa. We have explained the origin of the disagreement in the greater commentary.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s13","r":"fatiha_5","title":"4. Saying Āmīn: reports and practice","text":"Saying Āmīn upon completing al-Fātiḥa is called for because of the supplication it contains. The Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews have envied you for nothing as they have envied you for the greeting of peace and for saying Āmīn.” Ibn Mājah related it. He also said, God bless him and grant him peace: “God has granted me three distinctions: He granted me prayer in rows; He granted me the greeting, which is indeed the greeting of the people of Paradise; and He granted me the saying of Āmīn. He gave it to none of the prophets before me, unless God gave it to Aaron: Moses would supplicate and Aaron would say Āmīn.” Ibn Khuzayma related it. He, blessings and peace be upon him, heard a man supplicating insistently and said: “He has made it assured, if he seals it.” Some of those present asked, “With what should he seal it?” He replied: “He should say Āmīn; if he seals it with Āmīn, he has made it assured.” Abū Zuhayr, the transmitter, said: “Āmīn is like the seal ( الطابع ) upon the sheet.” Ibn ʿAjība adds that this last statement may itself be traceable to the Prophet. Abū Dāwūd related the report.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s14","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Āmīn: pronunciation, grammar and meaning","text":"Āmīn may be pronounced with its initial vowel long or short ( بالمد والقصر ), with an ungeminated mīm; gemination of the mīm is also an attested linguistic form. It has been said to be one of the Names of God Most High. It has also been explained as “O God, answer,” “thus, do [it],” or “thus, let it be.” Al-Mundhirī mentions this in al-Targhīb. Al-Bayḍāwī said: “It is indeclinable with final fatḥa ( مبني على الفتح ), like ayna, because of the meeting of two quiescent consonants ( لالتقاء الساكنين ). Its alif is transmitted both long and short.” The poet said: “May God have mercy upon a servant who says Āmīn.”","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-fatiha_5-s15","r":"fatiha_5","title":"Āmīn in congregational prayer","text":"I:70 “By agreement, it is not part of the Qurʾān. It is, however, a sunna to conclude the sūrah with it, because of his saying, blessings and peace be upon him: ‘Gabriel, peace be upon him, taught me Āmīn when I finished reciting al-Fātiḥa.’ He said that it is like the seal upon a letter. “The imam says it, and says it aloud in prayers recited aloud, because of the report from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr that when he, blessings and peace be upon him, recited ‘nor those who are astray,’ he would say Āmīn, raising his voice with it. It is related from Abū Ḥanīfa, may God have mercy upon him, that the imam does not say it. The well-known position related from him is that the imam says it quietly, as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mughaffal and Anas reported.” I say: the well-known position of Mālik’s school is that the imam does not say it in prayers recited aloud. Then he said: “The person praying behind the imam says Āmīn with him, because of his saying, blessings and peace be upon him: ‘When the imam says, “nor those who are astray,” say Āmīn, for the angels say Āmīn. Whoever’s saying of Āmīn coincides with the angels’ saying of Āmīn will have his previous sins forgiven.’” Success is through God, and He guides to the even way. May God bless our master and patron Muḥammad, the very reality of truth and realisation, and his family and his Companions, purified after him, the standards of the path, and grant them abundant peace.","anchor":"en-fatiha_5-s15"},{"kind":"passage","id":"intro2","r":"intro2","title":"Al-Baqara: introduction and excellence","text":"Al-Baqara: introduction and excellence intro2","anchor":"unit-intro2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro2-1","r":"intro2","title":"Al-Baqara: introduction and excellence","text":"سورة البقرة","anchor":"ar-intro2-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro2-2","r":"intro2","title":"Al-Baqara: introduction and excellence","text":"قال سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه-: (أول سورة نزلت بالمدينة سورة البقرة)(1). وفيها ستة آلاف ومائة وإحدى وعشرون كلمة، ومائتان وست وثمانون آية، وقيل: سبع وثمانون. قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «لكلّ شيء سنام، وإنّ سنام القرآن سورة البقرة. من قرأها فى بيته نهارا لم يدخله شيطان ثلاثة أيام، ومن قرأها فى بيته ليلا لم يدخله شيطان ثلاث ليال، وفيها سيّدة آي القرآن، وهى آية الكرسي» . وإنما كانت سنام القرآن، أي ذروته لأنها اشتملت على جملة ما فيه من أحوال الإيمان وفروع الإسلام.","anchor":"ar-intro2-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro2-3","r":"intro2","title":"Al-Baqara: introduction and excellence","text":"وقال صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «أعطيت سورة البقرة من الذكر الأول، وأعطيت طه والطواسين من ألواح موسى، وأعطيت فاتحة الكتاب، وخواتيم البقرة من تحت العرش» .","anchor":"ar-intro2-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro2-4","r":"intro2","title":"Al-Baqara: introduction and excellence","text":"ثم افتتح السورة برموز رمز بها بينه وبين حبيبه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-intro2-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-intro2-s1","r":"intro2","title":"Revelation, extent and excellence of the sūrah","text":"Our master ʿAlī, may God ennoble his countenance, said: “The first sūrah revealed in Medina was Sūrat al-Baqara [CP11] .” It contains six thousand, one hundred and twenty-one words, and two hundred and eighty-six verses—or, it is said, two hundred and eighty-seven. [B001] Source comparison: Al-Thaʿlabī, al-Kashf wa-l-bayān , I:135, independently transmits this sentence through ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī from ʿIkrima. His preceding heading mentions ʿAlī in connection with Kūfan verse enumeration, whereas the chain for the first Medinan sūrah ends with ʿIkrima. This directly inspected parallel supports the Cairo editor’s existing caution about the attribution. The English preserves Ibn ʿAjība’s attribution to ʿAlī; the source comparison establishes an attribution discrepancy rather than authenticating the reported revelation chronology. The Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Everything has a summit, and the summit of the Qurʾān is Sūrat al-Baqara. Whoever recites it in his house by day, no devil will enter it for three days; whoever recites it in his house by night, no devil will enter it for three nights. Within it is the foremost verse of the Qurʾān: the Throne Verse.” It is the summit of the Qurʾān—that is, its highest point—because it embraces a compendium of the Qurʾān’s teachings concerning the states of faith and the branches of Islam. [B002] He also said, God bless him and grant him peace: “I was given Sūrat al-Baqara from the First Remembrance; Ṭā Hā and the Ṭawāsīn from the tablets of Moses; and the Opening of the Book and the concluding verses of al-Baqara from beneath the Throne.” [B003]","anchor":"en-intro2-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-intro2-s2","r":"intro2","title":"","text":"He then opens the sūrah with symbols exchanged between Himself and His Beloved, saying:","anchor":"en-intro2-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-1","r":"q2-1","title":"2:1 · The opening letters and the descent of revelation","text":"2:1 · The opening letters and the descent of revelation 2:1","anchor":"unit-q2-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-1-1","r":"q2-1","title":"2:1 · The opening letters and the descent of revelation","text":"الم (1)","anchor":"ar-q2-1-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-1-2","r":"q2-1","title":"2:1 · The opening letters and the descent of revelation","text":"وقد حارت العقول في رموز الحكماء، فكيف بالأنبياء؟ فكيف بالمرسلين؟ فكيف بسيد المرسلين؟، فكيف يطمع أحد في إدراك حقائق رموز رب العالمين؟! قال الصديق رضى الله عنه: (في كل كتاب سر وسر، القرآن فواتح السور) . هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-1-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-1-3","r":"q2-1","title":"2:1 · The opening letters and the descent of revelation","text":"فمعرفة أسرار هذه الحروف لا يقف عليها إلا الصفوة من أكابر الأولياء. وكل واحد يلمع له على قدر صفاء شربه.","anchor":"ar-q2-1-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-1-4","r":"q2-1","title":"2:1 · The opening letters and the descent of revelation","text":"وأقرب ما فيها أنها أشياء أقسم الله بها لشرفها. فقيل: إنها مختصرة من أسمائه تعالى، فالألف من الله، واللام من اللطيف، والميم من مهيمن أو مجيد. وقيل: من أسماء نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلّم فالميم مختصرة إما من المصطفى، ويدل عليه زيادة الصاد فى المص، أو من المرسل، ويدل عليه زيادة الراء فى المر. والر مختصرة من الرسول. فكأن الحق تعالى يقول: يا أيها المصطفى، أو يا أيها الرسول","anchor":"ar-q2-1-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-1-s1","r":"q2-1","title":"The mysteries of the opening letters","text":"If intellects are bewildered by the symbols of sages, what then of prophets? What of messengers? What of the master of the messengers? How, then, could anyone aspire to grasp the realities of the symbols of the Lord of the worlds? Al-Ṣiddīq, may God be pleased with him, said: “Every book has a secret, and the secret of the Qurʾān is the opening of its sūrahs.” End of quotation. Knowledge of the mysteries of these letters is accessible only to the elect among the greatest saints ( الأولياء ). A gleam of it appears to each according to the purity of his draught ( صفاء شربه ). [B004] The most plausible explanation is that they are things by which God swears because of their nobility. Thus it has been said that they are abbreviated from His Names: the alif from Allāh, the lām from al-Laṭīf, and the mīm from Muhaymin or Majīd. Others say they are abbreviated from the names of His Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace: the mīm from al-Muṣṭafā , as the additional ṣād in Alif Lām Mīm Ṣād indicates, or from al-Mursal , as the additional rāʾ in Alif Lām Mīm Rāʾ indicates. Alif Lām Rāʾ is abbreviated from al-Rasūl . It is as though the Real Most High were saying, “O Chosen One,” or “O Messenger: ‘That is the Book, in which there is no doubt,’” or “‘A Book sent down to you,’” or the like. The fact that the address is directed to him, God bless him and grant him peace, after these symbols supports this interpretation. Kāf Hā Yā ʿAyn Ṣād is abbreviated from al-Kāfī, al-Hādī, al-Walī, al-ʿĀlim and al-Ṣādiq; Ṭā Hā from ṭāhir, “pure”; Ṭā Sīn from “O Pure One, O Master,” with “O Muḥammad” added in Ṭā Sīn Mīm ; and so forth.","anchor":"en-q2-1-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-1-s2","r":"q2-1","title":"Letters, divine Names and the realms of manifestation","text":"According to the people of allusion, the Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Alif: devote your innermost secret ( سرّك ) exclusively to Me, as the alif stands apart from the other letters. Lām: make your limbs pliant in My worship. Mīm: abide with Me through the effacement of your outlines and attributes ( محو رسومك وصفاتك ), and I shall adorn you with the purity of intimacy and nearness to Me.” This is reported by al-Thaʿlabī. I say: more evidently, these letters point to the three realms ( العوالم الثلاثة ). Alif signifies the oneness of the Essence in the realm of jabarūt ( عالم الجبروت ); lām, the appearance of its mysteries in the realm of malakūt ( عالم الملكوت ); mīm, the pervasion of its sustaining influxes in the realm of raḥamūt ( عالم الرحموت ); and ṣād, the manifestation of its governance in the realm of mulk ( عالم الملك ). [B005] Each of these symbolic letters indicates the appearance of the Essence’s effect in the realm of witnessing ( عالم الشهادة ). Alif points to the pervasion of oneness in the manifestations of created things; lām, to the overflowing of the lights of malakūt from the ocean of jabarūt; and mīm, to the King’s governance in the realm of mulk. It is as though the Real Most High were saying: “This Book which you recite, O Muḥammad, flows from the ocean of jabarūt into the realm of malakūt, and from malakūt into raḥamūt. The Trustworthy Spirit then brought it down to the realm of mulk and witnessing. One ought not, therefore, to doubt it.” Hence He follows these letters with His words: “That is the Book, in which there is no doubt.”","anchor":"en-q2-1-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-1-s3","r":"q2-1","title":"Doubt and tranquillity","text":"I say: rayb ( الريب ) is the heart’s movement and agitation through doubts and imaginings. Its opposite is tranquillity ( الطمأنينة ), through abiding rest in the Real. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “O chosen Messenger and elect Prophet, that Book which We have sent down to you from the jabarūt of Our holiness and the malakūt of Our might—there is no doubt that it is from Us. Whoever doubts it or attributes it to another has merited distance from the precinct of Our mercy and incurred the severity of Our retribution. Whoever realizes that it is from Us and believes in the one who has brought it from Us has merited entry into the Presence of Our holiness, until he hears from Us and speaks through Us: ‘When I love him, I am his; through Me he hears, through Me he sees, and through Me he speaks …’”—the hadith. [B006] Thus he becomes one of the utterly truthful brought near ( الصديقين المقربين ), with the prophets and messengers, and reaches the summit of the degrees of those who are mindful of God ( المتقين ), who are guided by the clear Qurʾān’s guidance. He points to this in His words:","anchor":"en-q2-1-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-2","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation 2:2","anchor":"unit-q2-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-1","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"ذلِكَ الْكِتابُ لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ أوهذا كِتابٌ أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ أو غير ذلك، ويدل على هذا توجيه الخطاب إليه صلى الله عليه وسلّم بعد هذه الرموز. وكهيعص مختصرة من الكافي والهادي والولي والعالم والصادق، وطه من طاهر، وطس من يا طاهر يا سيد، ويا محمد في طسم، إلى غير ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-2","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"وعند أهل الإشارة يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ألف: أفْرِدْ سِرَّك إِلّيَّ، انفراد الألف عن سائر الحروف، واللام: لَيِّنْ جوارحك لعبادتي، والميم: أقم معي بمحو رسومك وصفاتك، أزينك بصفاء الأنس والقرب مني. قاله الثعلبي.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-3","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"قلت: والأظهر أنها حروف تشير للعوالم الثلاثة، فالألف لوحدة الذات في عالم الجبروت، واللام لظهور أسرارها في عالم الملكوت، والميم لسريان أمدادها في عالم الرحموت، والصاد لظهور تصرفها في عالم الملك.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-4","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"وكل حرف من هذه الرموز يدل على ظهور أثر الذات في عالم الشهادة، فالألف يشير إلى سريان الوحدة في مظاهر الأكوان، واللام: يشير إلى فيضان أنوار الملكوت من بحر الجبروت، والميم يشير إلى تصرف الملك في عالم الملك، وكأن الحق تعالى يقول: هذا الكتاب الذي تتلو يا محمد- هو فائض من بحر الجبروت إلى عالم الملكوت، ومن عالَم الملكوت إلى الرحموت، ثم نَزَلَ به الروح الأمين إلى عالم الملك والشهادة، فلا ينبغي أن يرتاب فيه، ولذلك رتب عليه قوله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q2-2-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-5","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"ذلِكَ الْكِتابُ لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-2-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-6","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"قلت: الريب: تحرُّك القلب واضطرابه بالشكوك والأوهام، وتقابله الطمأنينة بالسكون إلى الحق على الدوام.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-7","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أيها الرسول المصطفى والنبيّ المجتبى ذلِكَ الْكِتابُ الذي أنزلناه عليك من جبروت قدسنا وملكوت عزِّنا لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ أنه من عندنا. فمن ارتاب فيه، أو نسبه إلى غيرنا، فقد استحق البعد من ساحة رحمتنا، وحلّت عليه شدائد نقمتنا، ومن تحقق به أنه من لدنا، وآمن بمن جاء به من عندنا، فقد استحق دخول حضرة قدسنا حتى يسمع منا ويتكلم بنا، فإذا أحببته كنت له، فبي يسمع، وبي يبصر، وبي يتكلم ... الحديث.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-8","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"فيكون من الصديقين المقربين مع النبيين والمرسلين، وكان في ذروة درجات المتقين، الذين يهتدون بهدي القرآن المبين، كما أشار إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-2-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-10","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"... هُدىً لِلْمُتَّقِينَ (2)","anchor":"ar-q2-2-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-11","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"قلت: (هدى) خبر عن مبتدأ مضمر، أو مبتدأ بتقديم الخبر. أي: هو هاد للمتقين، أو فيه الهدى لهم. والهدى:","anchor":"ar-q2-2-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-12","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"هو الإرشاد والبيان، ومعناه: الدلالة الموصلة إلى الحق. والمتقي: من جعل بينه وبين مقت الله وقاية، وله ثلاث درجات:","anchor":"ar-q2-2-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-13","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"حفظ الجوارح من المخالفات، وحفظ القلوب من المساوئ والهفوات، وحفظ السرائر من الوقوف مع المحسوسات،","anchor":"ar-q2-2-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-14","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"فالأولى لمقام الإسلام، وإليه توجه الخطاب بقوله: فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ، والثانية لمقام الإيمان، وإليه توجه الخطاب بقوله: فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ يا أُولِي الْأَلْبابِ، والثالثة لمقام الإحسان، وإليه توجه الخطاب بقوله: اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقاتِهِ.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-15","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ذلِكَ الْكِتابُ الذي لا يقرب ساحتَه شكٍّ ولا ارتياب، هو عين الهداية لأهل التقى من ذوي الألباب، فلا يزالون يَتَرَقَّوْنَ به في المقامات والأحوال حتى يسمعوه من الكبير المتعال، بلا واسطة تبليغ ولا إرسال، قد انمحت في حقهم الرسوم والأشكال، وهذه غاية الهداية، وتحقيق سابق العناية.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-16","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"قال جعفر الصادق: (والله لقد تجلّى الله تعالى لخلقه في كلامه ولكن لا يشعرون) وقال أيضاً- وقد سألوه عن حالة لحقَته في الصلاة حتى خَرّ مغشيًّا عليه، فلما سُرِّيَ عنه، قيل له في ذلك فقال-: (ما زلت أردد الآية على قلبي حتى سمعتها من المتكلم بها، فلم يثبت جسمي لمعاينة قدرته) .","anchor":"ar-q2-2-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-18","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"فدرجات القراءة ثلاث:","anchor":"ar-q2-2-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-19","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"أدناها: أن يقرأ العبد كأنه يقرأ على الله تعالى واقفاً بين يديه، وهو ناظر له ومستمع منه، فيكون حاله السؤال والتملُّق والتضرّع والابتهال.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-20","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"والثانية: أن يشهد بقلبه كأن الله تعالى يُخاطبه بألفاظه، ويُناجيه بإنعامه وإحسانه، فمقامه الحياء والتعظيم، والإصغاء والفهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-21","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"والثالثة: أن يرى في الكلام المتكلِّم، فلا ينظر إلى نفسه ولا إلى قراءته، بل يكون فانيّا عن نفسه، غائباً في شهود ربه، لم يبق له عن نفسه إخبار ولا مع غير الله قرار.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-22","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"فالأولى لأهل الفناء في الأفعال، والثانية لأهل الفناء في الصفات، والثالثة لأهل الفناء في شهود الذات، رضى الله عنهم، وحشرنا على منهاجهم.. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-2-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-2-23","r":"q2-2","title":"2:2 · Guidance, God-consciousness and the degrees of recitation","text":"ثم وصف المتقين، الذين خصوا بهداية كتابه المبين، بثلاثة أوصاف، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-2-23"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-2-s1","r":"q2-2","title":"The grammar of guidance and the degrees of taqwā","text":"I say: “guidance” ( هدى ) is either the predicate ( خبر ) of an implicit subject ( مبتدأ مضمر ), or itself the subject with its predicate placed before it: “It is a guide for those mindful of God,” or “Within it is guidance for them.” Guidance ( الهدى ) is direction and clear explanation ( الإرشاد والبيان ); its meaning is an indication that brings one to the Real ( الدلالة الموصلة إلى الحق ). The person mindful of God ( المتقي ) is one who places a safeguard ( وقاية ) between himself and God’s displeasure. This has three degrees: guarding the limbs against disobedience; guarding hearts against defects and lapses; and guarding the innermost secrets against stopping with sensible things. The first belongs to the station of Islam ( مقام الإسلام ), to which the address “Be mindful of God as far as you are able” [64:16] is directed. The second belongs to the station of faith ( مقام الإيمان ), to which “Be mindful of God, O possessors of understanding” [65:10] is directed. The third belongs to the station of excellence ( مقام الإحسان ), to which “Be mindful of God as He ought to be regarded” [3:102] is directed.","anchor":"en-q2-2-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-2-s2","r":"q2-2","title":"From guidance to hearing the Speaker","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “That Book, whose precinct neither doubt nor uncertainty approaches, is guidance itself for the God-conscious possessed of understanding.” Through it they continue to ascend in stations and states ( المقامات والأحوال ) until they hear it from the Great, the Most High, without an intermediary conveying or transmitting it. Outlines and forms ( الرسوم والأشكال ) have been effaced for them. This is guidance’s utmost attainment and the realization of antecedent providential care ( سابق العناية ). Jaʿfar al-Ṣādiq said: “By God, God Most High has disclosed Himself to His creatures in His speech, but they do not perceive it.” He also said, when asked about a state that overtook him in prayer until he fell unconscious, and then recovered: “I continued repeating the verse upon my heart until I heard it from the One who speaks it. My body could not withstand the direct vision of His power.”","anchor":"en-q2-2-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-2-s3","r":"q2-2","title":"The three degrees of recitation","text":"The degrees of recitation ( درجات القراءة ) are three. The lowest is for the servant to recite as though he were reciting before God Most High, standing in His presence while He looks upon him and listens to him. His state is then one of petition, humble entreaty, supplication and imploring. The second is to witness in his heart as though God Most High were addressing him with His words and speaking intimately to him through His bounty and beneficence. His station is modesty, magnification, attentive listening and understanding. The third is to behold the Speaker in the speech, looking neither to himself nor to his recitation. Rather, he is effaced from himself ( فانيًا عن نفسه ), absent in witnessing his Lord: no report of himself remains to him, nor any resting with other than God. The first belongs to the people of effacement in acts ( الفناء في الأفعال ); the second to the people of effacement in attributes ( الفناء في الصفات ); and the third to the people of effacement in witnessing the Essence ( الفناء في شهود الذات ). May God be pleased with them and gather us upon their way. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-2-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-2-s4","r":"q2-2","title":"","text":"He then describes those mindful of God, singled out for the guidance of His clear Book, by three qualities, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-2-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-3","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending 2:3","anchor":"unit-q2-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-1","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَيُقِيمُونَ الصَّلاةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْناهُمْ يُنْفِقُونَ (3)","anchor":"ar-q2-3-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-2","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"قلت: هذه الأوصاف تتضمن ثلاثة أعمال: الأول: عمل قلبي وهو الإيمان، والثاني: عمل بدني، وهو الصلاة، والثالث: عمل مالي، وهو الإنفاق في سبيل الله، وهذه الأعمال هي أساس التقوى التي تدور عليها.","anchor":"ar-q2-3-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-3","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"أما العمل القلبي: فهو الإيمان أولاً، والمعرفة ثانياً، فما دام العبد محجوبا بشهود نفسه، محصوراً في الأكوان وفي هيكل ذاته فهو مؤمن بالغيب، يؤمن بوجود الحق تعالى، وبما أخبر به من أمور الغيب، يستدل بوجود أثره عليه، فإذا فني عن نفسه وتلطفت دائرة حسه، وخرجت فكرته عن دائرة الأكوان، أفضى إلى الشهود والعيان، فصار الغيب عنده شهادة، والملك ملكوتاً، والمستقبل حالاً، والآتي واقعاً، وقد قلتُ في ذلك:","anchor":"ar-q2-3-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-4","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"فَلا تَرْضى بغَيْرِ الله حِبّاً ... وكُنْ أبداً بعِشْقٍ واشْتِيَاقِ","anchor":"ar-q2-3-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-5","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"تَرَى الأمْرَ المغيّب ذا عيان ... وتحظى بالوصُولِ وبالتَّلاَقِي","anchor":"ar-q2-3-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-6","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"وفي الحكم: «لو أشرق نور اليقين في قلبك لرأيت الآخرة أقرب من أن ترحل إليها، ولرأيت بهجة الدنيا وكسوة الفناء ظاهرة عليها» . وقال في التنوير: ولو انْهَتَكَ حجاب الوهم لوقع العيان على فقد الأعيان، ولأشرق نور الإيقان فغطّى وجود الأكوان. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-3-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-7","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"وإنما اقتصر الحق تعالى على الإيمان بالغيب لأنه هو المكلف به إذ هو الذي يطيقه جلّ العباد، بخلاف المعرفة الخاصة فلا يطيقها إلا الخصوص، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-3-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-8","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"وأما العمل البدني: فهو إقامة الصلاة، والمراد بإقامتها إتقان شروطها وأركانها وخشوعها، وحفظ السر فيها، قال الشيخ أبو العباس المرسى رضى الله عنه: (كل موضع ذكر فيه المصلّون في معرض المدح فإنما جاء لمن أقام الصلاة، إما بلفظ الإقامة، وإما بمعنى يرجع إليها، قال تعالى: الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَيُقِيمُونَ الصَّلاةَ، وقال تعالى: أَقِمِ الصَّلاةَ، وَالْمُقِيمِي الصَّلاةِ، ولما ذكر المصلّين بالغفلة قال: فَوَيْلٌ لِلْمُصَلِّينَ الَّذِينَ هُمْ عَنْ صَلاتِهِمْ ساهُونَ ولم يقل: فويل للمقيمين الصلاة) .","anchor":"ar-q2-3-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-9","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"وأما العمل المالي فهو الإنفاق في سبيل الله واجباً أو مندوباً، وهو من أفضل القربات، يقول الله- تبارك وتعالى-: «يا ابن آدم أَنفق، أنفقْ عليك» ، وفي حديث آخر: «أنفِقْ ولا تخَفْ من ذي العرش إقلالا» ، وقال صلى الله عليه وسلّم:","anchor":"ar-q2-3-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-10","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"«إنّ في الجنة غُرَفاً يُرى ظَاهِرُهَا مِنْ باطنها وباطِنَها مِنْ ظَاهِرهَا. قيل لِمَنْ هِي يا رسولَ الله؟ قال: لِمَنْ أطْعَمَ الطعَامَ، وأفْشَى السلام، وصَلى باللَّيْلِ والناسُ نِيام» . وقال أيضا صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «إن الله- عزّ وجل- ليُدْخلُ باللقمةِ مِن الخبز والقبضةِ مِن التمْر ومثله ممَّا ينتفع به المسكين ثلاثةً، الجنةَ: رَب البيتِ الآمرَ به، والزوجة تصلحه، والخادمَ","anchor":"ar-q2-3-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-11","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"الذي يناولهُ المسْكِين» . وقال أيضا: صلى الله عليه وسلّم «إنّ الصدقةَ لتسُدُّ سَبعينَ باباً من السوء» . وقال أيضا صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «صنائِع المعْرُوف تقي مَصارعَ السُّوءِ، وصدقةُ السِّر تُطفِئ غَضَبَ الربِّ، وصِلةُ الرَّحِم تزيدُ في العمرِ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-3-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-12","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"الإشارة: يا من غرق في بحر الذات وتيار الصفات (ذلك الكتاب) الذي تسمعه من أنوار ملكوتنا، وأسرار جبروتنا (لا ريب فيه) أنه من عندنا، فلا تسمعه من غيرنا، (فإذا قرأناه فاتبعْ قرآنه) ، فهو هاد لشهود ذاتنا، ومرشد للوصول إلى حضرتنا، لمن اتقى شهود غيرِنا، وغرق في بحر وحدتنا، الذي يؤمن بغيب غيبنا، وأسرار جبروتنا، التي لا تُحيط بها العلوم، ولا تسمو إلى نهايتها الأفكار والمفهوم، الذي جمع بين مشاهدة الربوبية، والقيام بوظائف العبودية، إظهاراً لسر الحكمة بعد التحقق بشهود القدرة، فهو على صلاته دائم، وقلبه في غيب الملكوت هائم، ينفق مما رزقه الله من أسرار العلوم ومخازن الفهوم، فهو دائماً ينفق من سعة علمه وأنوار فيضه، فلا جرم أنه على بينة من ربه.","anchor":"ar-q2-3-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-3-13","r":"q2-3","title":"2:3 · Faith, prayer and spending","text":"ولما ذكر الحق تعالى من آمن من العرب، ذكر مَن آمن مِن أهل الكتاب، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-3-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-3-s1","r":"q2-3","title":"The three kinds of action","text":"I say: these qualities embrace three kinds of action. The first is an action of the heart: faith. The second is a bodily action: prayer. The third is an action involving wealth: spending in God’s path. These actions are the foundations upon which God-consciousness ( التقوى ) turns.","anchor":"en-q2-3-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-3-s2","r":"q2-3","title":"From faith in the unseen to direct witnessing","text":"As for the heart’s action, it is first faith ( الإيمان ) and then gnosis ( المعرفة ). So long as the servant is veiled by witnessing himself, confined within created things and the structure of his own person, he believes in the unseen: he believes in the existence of the Real Most High and in what He has reported of unseen matters, inferring Him from the existence of His effects. When he is effaced from himself, his sphere of sensible apprehension is subtilized, and his reflection passes beyond the circle of created things, he reaches witnessing and direct vision ( الشهود والعيان ). The unseen then becomes witnessed for him, mulk becomes malakūt, the future becomes present, and what is to come becomes actual. Concerning this I have said: Take none but God as your beloved; remain forever in ardent love and longing. You shall see the hidden matter face to face, and win arrival and encounter. The Ḥikam says: “Were the light of certainty to shine in your heart, you would see the Hereafter nearer than that you should journey to it; and you would see the world’s splendour with the garment of passing-away manifest upon it.” In al-Tanwīr he says: “Were the veil of imagining ( الوهم ) torn away, direct vision would fall upon the disappearance of individual entities ( فقد الأعيان ), and the light of certainty would shine forth, covering the existence of created things.” End of quotation. [B007] The Real Most High mentions only faith in the unseen because that is what is required of people: it is within the capacity of the great majority of servants. Special gnosis ( المعرفة الخاصة ), by contrast, is within the capacity only of the elect. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-3-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-3-s3","r":"q2-3","title":"Establishing prayer","text":"The bodily action is establishing prayer ( إقامة الصلاة ). Establishing it means performing its conditions, pillars and reverent attentiveness ( شروطها وأركانها وخشوعها ) with care, and guarding the innermost secret ( السر ) within it. Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mursī, may God be pleased with him, said: “Wherever those who pray are mentioned by way of praise, the reference is to those who establish prayer—either through the actual expression ‘establishing’ or through a meaning that returns to it. God Most High says, ‘Those who believe in the unseen and establish prayer’; ‘Establish prayer’; and ‘those who establish prayer’ [22:35]. But when He mentions worshippers in connection with heedlessness, He says, ‘Woe, then, to those who pray, who are heedless of their prayer’ [107:4–5]. He does not say, ‘Woe to those who establish prayer.’”","anchor":"en-q2-3-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-3-s4","r":"q2-3","title":"Spending in God’s path","text":"Action involving wealth is spending in God’s path, whether obligatory or recommended ( واجبًا أو مندوبًا ), and it is among the best acts of drawing near. God, blessed and exalted, says: “Son of Adam, spend, and I shall spend upon you.” In another hadith: “Spend, and do not fear impoverishment from the Possessor of the Throne.” [B008] He said, God bless him and grant him peace: “In the Garden are chambers whose outside can be seen from within and whose inside can be seen from without.” He was asked, “For whom are they, Messenger of God?” He replied: “For those who feed others, spread the greeting of peace, and pray by night while people sleep.” He also said, God bless him and grant him peace: “Through a morsel of bread, a handful of dates, or the like from which a poor person benefits, God, mighty and majestic, brings three people into the Garden: the master of the house who orders it, the wife who prepares it, and the servant who hands it to the poor person.” He also said, God bless him and grant him peace: “Charity closes seventy doors of evil.” And he said, God bless him and grant him peace: “Acts of kindness protect against evil ends; secret charity extinguishes the Lord’s wrath; and maintaining kinship ties increases one’s lifespan.” [B009]","anchor":"en-q2-3-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-3-s5","r":"q2-3","title":"Witnessing lordship and fulfilling servanthood","text":"O you who are immersed in the ocean of the Essence and the current of the attributes: “That Book,” which you hear from the lights of Our malakūt and the mysteries of Our jabarūt—“there is no doubt” that it is from Us, so do not hear it from another. “When We recite it, follow its recitation” [75:18]. It guides to witnessing Our Essence and directs to arrival at Our Presence, for one who guards against witnessing other than Us and is immersed in the ocean of Our oneness; who believes in the unseen of Our unseen ( غيب غيبنا ) and the mysteries of Our jabarūt, which sciences cannot encompass and whose utmost reaches neither thought nor understanding attains. Such a person unites witnessing lordship ( مشاهدة الربوبية ) with the performance of the duties of servanthood ( وظائف العبودية ), manifesting the secret of wisdom after realizing the witnessing of power ( شهود القدرة ). He is constant in his prayer, while his heart wanders in the unseen of malakūt. He spends from the mysteries of the sciences and the treasuries of understanding God has provided him, ever giving from the amplitude of his knowledge and the lights of his effusion. No wonder, then, that he stands upon clear evidence from his Lord.","anchor":"en-q2-3-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-3-s6","r":"q2-3","title":"","text":"After mentioning the believers among the Arabs, the Real Most High mentions those who believe among the People of the Book, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-3-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-4-5","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success 2:4–5","anchor":"unit-q2-4-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-4-5-1","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"وَالَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ وَما أُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ وَبِالْآخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوقِنُونَ (4) أُولئِكَ عَلى هُدىً مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ (5)","anchor":"ar-q2-4-5-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-4-5-2","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"قلت: الموصول مبتدأ، و (أولئك) خبره، أو عطف على (المتقين) ، وحذف المنزل عليه في جانب الكتب المتقدمة، فلم يقُلْ: وما أنزل على مَن قبلك إشارة إلى أن الإيمان بالكتب المتقدمة دون معرفة أعيان المنزل عليهم كاف، إلا من ورد تعيينُه في الكتاب والسنة فلابد من الإيمان به، أما القرآن العظيم فلابد من الإيمان أنه منزل على نبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم، فمن اعتقد أنه منزل على غيره كالروافض فإنه كافر بإجماع، ولذلك ذكر المتعلق بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-4-5-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-4-5-3","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-4-5-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-4-5-4","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالَّذِينَ يصدقون بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ يا محمد من الأخبار الغيبية والأحكام الشرعية، والأسرار الربانية والعلوم اللدنية وَما أُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ من الكتب السماوية، والأخبار القدسية، وهم يُوقِنُونَ بالبعث والحساب والرجوع إلينا والمآب، على نعتٍ ما أخبرتُ به في كتابي وأخبار أنبيائي، أُولئِكَ راكبون على مَتْنِ الهداية، مُسْتَعْلون على محمل العناية، محفوفون بجيش النصر والرعاية، وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الظافرون بكل مطلوب، الناجون من كل مخوف ومرهوب، دون من عداهم ممن","anchor":"ar-q2-4-5-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-4-5-5","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"سبق له الخذلان، فلم يكن له إيمان ولا إيقان، فلا هداية له ولا نجاح، ولا نجاة له ولا فلاح، نسأل الله العصمة بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-4-5-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-4-5-6","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"الإشارة: قلت: كأن الآية الأولى في الواصلين، والثانية في السائرين، لأن الأولين وصفهم بالإنفاق من سعة علومهم، وهؤلاء وصفهم بالتصديق في قلوبهم، فإن داموا على السير كانوا مفلحين فائزين بما فاز به الأولون.","anchor":"ar-q2-4-5-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-4-5-7","r":"q2-4-5","title":"2:4–5 · Revelation, certainty and success","text":"فأهل الآية الأولى من أهل الشهود والعيان، وأهل الثانية من أهل التصديق والإيمان. أهل الأولى ذاقوا طعم الخصوصية، فقاموا بشهود الربوبية وآداب العبودية، وأهل الثانية صدقوا بنزول الخصوصية ودوامها، واستنشقوا شيئاً من روائح أسرارها وعلومها، فهم يوقنون بوجود الحقيقة، عالمون برسوم الطريقة، فلا جرم أنهم على الجادة وطريق الهداية، وهم مفلحون بالوصول إلى عين العناية. دون الفرقة الثالثة التي هى بالإنكار موسومة، ومن نيل العناية محرومة، التي أشار إليها الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-4-5-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-4-5-s1","r":"q2-4-5","title":"The relative construction and belief in revelation","text":"I say: the relative expression ( الموصول ) is a subject ( مبتدأ ), and “those” ( أولئك ) introduces its predicate ( خبر ); alternatively, it is coordinated with “those mindful of God” ( المتقين ). In referring to earlier scriptures, He leaves the recipient of revelation unmentioned: He does not say, “what was sent down to those before you.” This indicates that belief in earlier scriptures suffices without knowing the individual recipients, except where someone is specifically named in the Book or the Sunna: belief in that person is then indispensable. As for the mighty Qurʾān, one must believe that it was sent down to our Prophet Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace. Anyone who believes it was sent down to someone else—as [he alleges of] the Rāfiḍa—is an unbeliever by consensus. Hence He states the object of the relation ( المتعلَّق ) in His words, “what has been sent down to you.” [B010]","anchor":"en-q2-4-5-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-4-5-s2","r":"q2-4-5","title":"Guidance and the protection of providence","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Those who affirm what has been sent down to you, O Muḥammad,” of reports concerning the unseen, rulings of the Sacred Law, lordly mysteries and divinely bestowed sciences ( العلوم اللدنية ), “and what was sent down before you” of heavenly scriptures and sacred tidings, and who are certain of resurrection, reckoning, return to Us and the final homecoming, just as I have described them in My Book and the reports of My prophets—“those” ride upon the back of guidance, raised high upon the conveyance of providential care ( العناية ), surrounded by a host of help and protection. “Those are” the ones who win every object sought and escape everything feared and dreaded, unlike those others for whom abandonment ( الخذلان ) has already been decreed, who possess neither faith nor certainty, neither guidance nor success, neither deliverance nor prosperity. We ask God for protection by His grace and generosity.","anchor":"en-q2-4-5-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-4-5-s3","r":"q2-4-5","title":"Those who have arrived and those still journeying","text":"I say: it is as though the first verse [2:3] concerns those who have arrived ( الواصلين ), and the second [2:4] those who are journeying ( السائرين ). He describes the former as spending from the amplitude of their sciences, and the latter as affirming the truth in their hearts. If they persevere in journeying, they will prosper, winning what the former have won. The people of the first verse are the people of witnessing and direct vision ( الشهود والعيان ); those of the second, the people of assent and faith ( التصديق والإيمان ). The former have tasted special election ( الخصوصية ), and so uphold the witnessing of lordship and the courtesies of servanthood ( آداب العبودية ). The latter affirm the descent and continuance of special election and have breathed something of the fragrance of its mysteries and sciences. They are certain of the existence of Reality ( الحقيقة ) and know the observances of the Path ( رسوم الطريقة ). No wonder they stand upon the highway and the way of guidance, prospering through arrival at the very source of providential care. Not so the third group, marked by denial and deprived of attaining that care, to whom the Real Most High alludes in His words:","anchor":"en-q2-4-5-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-6-7","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power 2:6–7","anchor":"unit-q2-6-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-1","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا سَواءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ أَأَنْذَرْتَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تُنْذِرْهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ (6) خَتَمَ اللَّهُ عَلى قُلُوبِهِمْ وَعَلى سَمْعِهِمْ وَعَلى أَبْصارِهِمْ غِشاوَةٌ وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ عَظِيمٌ (7)","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-2","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"قلت: (سواء) خبر مقدم، و (أنذرتهم) مبتدأ لسبك همزة التسوية، أي: الإنذار وعدمه سواء في حق هؤلاء الكفرة، والجملة خبر إن، و (غشاوة) مبتدأ، والجار قبله خبره، والغشاوة: ما يغشى الشيء ويغطيه، كنى به عن مانع قهرهم عن الإيمان.","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-3","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا محمد إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بما أنزل إليك جهراً، وسبقت لهم مني الشقاوة سرّاً، لا ينفع فيهم الوعظ والإنذار، ولا البشارة والتذكار، فإنذارك وعدمه في حقهم سواء، لما سبق لهم مني الطرد والشقاء، فالتذكير في حقهم عناء، والغيبة عن أحوالهم راحة وهناء، لأني ختمتُ على قلوبهم بطابع الكفران، فلا يهتدون إلى إسلام ولا إيمان، ومنعت أسماعهم أن تصغي إلى الوعظ والتذكير، فلا ينجع فيهم تخويف ولا تحذير، وغشيت أبصارهم بظلمة الحجاب فلا يبصرون الحق والصواب، قد أعددتُهم لعذابي ونقمتي، وطردتهم عن ساحة رحمتي ونعمتي.","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-4","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"وإنما أمرتك بإنذارهم لإقامة الحجة عليهم، وإني وإن حكمت عليهم أنهم من أهل مخالفتي وعنادي فإني لا أظلم أحداً من خلقي وعبادي، قُلْ فَلِلَّهِ الْحُجَّةُ الْبالِغَةُ فَلَوْ شاءَ لَهَداكُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ. فما ظلمتُهم لأني بعثتُ الرسلَ مبشرين ومنذرين، ولكن ظلموا أنفسهم فكانوا هم الظالمين، فحكمتى اقتضت الإنذار، وقدرتي اقتضت","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-5","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"القهر والإجبار، فالواجب عليك أيها العبد أن تكون لك عينان: عين تنظر لحكمتي وشريعتي فتتأدب، وعينٌ تنظر لقدرتي وحقيقتي فتُسلم، وتكون بين الأمن والرّهْب، فلا تأمَنْ مَكْرِي وإن أمَّنتُك، ولا تيأس من حلمي وإن أبعدتك، فعلمي لا يحيط به محيط، إلا من هو بكل شيء محيط.","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-6","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"الإشارة: إن الذين أنكروا وجود الخصوصية، وجحدوا أهل مشاهدة الربوبية من أهل التربية النبوية، لا ينفع فيهم الوعظ والتذكير، بما سبق لهم في علم الملك القدير، فسواء عليهم أأنذرتهم وبال القطيعة والحجاب، أم لم تنذرهم لعدم فتح الباب، قد ختم الله على قلوبهم بالعوائد والشهوات، أو حلاوة الزهد والطاعات، أو تحرير المسائل والمشكلات، وعلى سمع قلوبهم بالخواطر والغفلات، وجعل على أبصارهم غشاوة الحجاب، فلا يبصرون إلا المحسوسات، غائبون عن أسرار المعاني وأنوار التجليات، بخلاف قلوب العارفين، فإنها ترى من أسرار المعاني مالا يُرى للناظرين، وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-7","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"قلوبُ العَارفِينَ لَهَا عُيُونٌ ... ترى مالا يُرى للناظرينا","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-8","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"وألسنةٌ بأسْرارٍ تُنَاجِي ... تغيبُ عَنَ الكِرَام الكَاتِبِينَا","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-9","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"وأجنحةٌ تَطِيرُ بِغَيْرِ ريشٍ ... إلَى ملكُوتٍ ربِّ العَالَمِينَا(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-10","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"فسبحان من حجب العالمين بصلاحهم عن مصلحهم، وحجب العلماء بعلمهم عن معلومهم، واختصّ قوماً بنفوذ عزائمهم إلى مشاهدة ذات محبوبهم، فهم في رياض ملكوته يتنزهون، وفي بحار جبروته يسبحون، لِمِثْلِ هذا فَلْيَعْمَلِ الْعامِلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-6-7-11","r":"q2-6-7","title":"2:6–7 · Sealed hearts and the two perspectives of wisdom and power","text":"ولمَّا ذكر الحق- جل جلاله- من أعلن بالإنكار، ذكر من أسَرَّ بالجحود وأظهر الإقرار، فقال جل وعلا:","anchor":"ar-q2-6-7-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-6-7-s1","r":"q2-6-7","title":"Indifference to warning and the covering over sight","text":"I say: “the same” ( سواء ) is a fronted predicate ( خبر مقدّم ), while “whether you warn them” supplies the subject ( مبتدأ ), the hamza of equivalence ( همزة التسوية ) allowing the expression to be construed as a verbal noun. That is, warning and not warning are equal in the case of these unbelievers. The entire clause is the predicate of inna ( خبر إنّ ). “A covering” ( غشاوة ) is a subject, with the preceding prepositional phrase as its predicate. A ghishāwa is something that envelops and covers another thing; it is used here figuratively for a barrier that forcibly prevents their believing.","anchor":"en-q2-6-7-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-6-7-s2","r":"q2-6-7","title":"Warning, predetermination and responsibility","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “O Muḥammad, those who outwardly disbelieve in what has been sent down to you, for whom wretchedness has already been determined by Me in secret, gain nothing from exhortation and warning, glad tidings or reminders. Your warning and its absence are alike for them, because banishment and wretchedness have already been determined for them by Me. Reminding them brings weariness; being absent from concern with their states brings repose and ease. For I have sealed their hearts with the stamp of unbelief, so they find no way to Islam or faith. I have prevented their hearing from attending to exhortation and remembrance, so neither alarm nor warning avails them. I have covered their eyes with the darkness of the veil, so they see neither truth nor rightness. I have prepared them for My punishment and retribution and expelled them from the precinct of My mercy and bounty. “I commanded you to warn them only to establish the proof against them. Although I have decreed that they belong to those who oppose and resist Me, I wrong none of My creatures or servants. ‘Say: to God belongs the conclusive proof; had He willed, He would have guided you all’ [6:149]. I have not wronged them, for I sent the messengers bearing glad tidings and warnings; rather, they wronged themselves, and it was they who did wrong. My wisdom ( حكمتي ) required the warning, while My power ( قدرتي ) required overpowering and compulsion ( القهر والإجبار ). “Your duty, O servant, is therefore to have two eyes: one that looks to My wisdom and My Sacred Law, so that you observe due courtesy; and one that looks to My power and My Reality, so that you submit. Remain between security and fear. Do not feel secure from My hidden devising ( مكري ), even if I assure you of safety; and do not despair of My forbearance, even if I keep you distant. None encompasses My knowledge except He who encompasses all things.”","anchor":"en-q2-6-7-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-6-7-s3","r":"q2-6-7","title":"Veils formed from habits, accomplishments and knowledge","text":"Those who deny the existence of special election ( الخصوصية ) and reject the people who witness lordship through prophetic spiritual formation ( التربية النبوية ) gain nothing from exhortation and reminders, because of what has already been established concerning them in the knowledge of the all-powerful King. It is the same for them whether you warn them of the evil consequence of severance and veiling ( القطيعة والحجاب ), or do not warn them, since the door has not been opened. God has sealed their hearts with habits and appetites, or with the sweetness of asceticism and acts of obedience, or with the precise formulation of questions and difficult problems. He has sealed their hearts’ hearing with passing thoughts and heedlessness, and placed the covering of the veil over their sight. They perceive only sensible things, absent from the mysteries of meanings and the lights of divine self-disclosures ( أنوار التجليات ). Not so the hearts of the gnostics: they see mysteries of meaning invisible to ordinary observers. Concerning this the poet says: The hearts of the gnostics have eyes that see what other eyes do not; and tongues that converse in mysteries hidden from the noble recording angels; and wings that fly without feathers to the malakūt of the Lord of the worlds. Glory be to Him who veils people by their righteousness from the One who makes them righteous, and scholars by their knowledge from the One they would know; who singles out a people whose resolves penetrate to witnessing the Essence of their Beloved. They roam the gardens of His malakūt and swim the seas of His jabarūt. “For the like of this, let those who act perform their deeds” [37:61].","anchor":"en-q2-6-7-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-6-7-s4","r":"q2-6-7","title":"","text":"After mentioning those who proclaim their denial, the Real, glorious is His majesty, mentions those who conceal rejection and profess acknowledgement, saying, exalted is He:","anchor":"en-q2-6-7-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-8-10","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart 2:8–10","anchor":"unit-q2-8-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-1","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَقُولُ آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَبِالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَما هُمْ بِمُؤْمِنِينَ (8) يُخادِعُونَ اللَّهَ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَما يَخْدَعُونَ إِلاَّ أَنْفُسَهُمْ وَما يَشْعُرُونَ (9) فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ مَرَضٌ فَزادَهُمُ اللَّهُ مَرَضاً وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ بِما كانُوا يَكْذِبُونَ (10)","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-2","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"قلت: (من) موصوفة مبتدأ، والخبر مقدم، أي: ومن الناس ناس يقولون كذا، والمخادعة: إظهار خلاف ما يخفي من المكروه، وأصل الخدع: الإخفاء، ومنه المخدع للبيت الذي يخبأ فيه المتاع. وقيل: الفساد لأن المنافقين","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-3","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"يفسدون إيمانهم بما يُخْفُون، وجملة (وما يشعرون) حالية، أي: غير شاعرين، والشعور: التفطن، وفعله من باب كَرُمَ ونَصَرَ. وليت شعري: أي: ليت فطنتي تدرك هذا، وجملة (في قلوبهم مرض) تعليلية للمخادعة، والمرض:","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-4","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"الضعف والفتور، وهو هنا مرض القلوب بالشك والنفاق. والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-5","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمِنَ النَّاسِ منهم مغموص عليهم بالنفاق كبعض اليهود والمنافقين، يقولون بألسنتهم ما ليس في قلوبهم، يقولون: آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَبِالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وما هُم في عداد المؤمنين، يُخادِعُونَ بزعمهم اللَّهَ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بما يُظهرون من الإيمان، وَما يَخْدَعُونَ في الحقيقة إِلَّا أَنْفُسَهُمْ لأن وبال خداعهم راجع إليهم، وَما يَشْعُرُونَ أن خداعهم وبال عليهم، وإنما حصلت لهم هذه المخادعة لأن فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ مرضاً من الشك والحسد، فقلوبهم مذبذبة، وأنفسهم مغمومة، فَزادَهُمُ اللَّهُ مَرَضاً على مرضهم بما ينزل عليهم من الآيات التي تفضحهم، وَلَهُمْ في الآخرة- إذا قدموا على الله- عَذابٌ موجع بسبب تكذيبهم رسول الله أو كذبهم على الله. هذا مُضَمَّنُ الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-6","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"افتتح الحق- جلّ جلاله- بذكر الذين أخلصوا دينهم لله وواطأت فيه قلوبهم ألسنتهم، ثم ثنى بالكافرين الذين محضوا الكفر ظاهراً وباطناً، ثم ثلث بالمنافقين الذين آمنوا بأفواههم ولم تؤمن قلوبهم، وهم أخبث الكفرة لأنهم خلطوا بالكفر استهزاء وخداعاً، ولذلك كانوا في الدرك الأسفل من النار.","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-7","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"الإشارة: ومن الناس مَن يترامى بالدعوى على الخصوصية، ويدعي تحقيق مشاهدة الربوبية، وهو في الدرك الأسفل من العمومية، يظهر خلوص الإيمان وتحقيق العرفان، وهو في أودية الشكوك والخواطر حيران، وفي فيافي القطيعة والفَرْقِ ظمآن، لسانه منطلق بالدعوى، وقلبه خارب من الهدي، يخادع الله بالرضا عن عيوبه ومساوئه، ويخادع المسلمين بتزيين ظاهره، وباطنه معمور بحظوظه ومهاويه، يتزيه بِزِيِّ العارفين ويتعامل معاملة الجاهلين، ويصدق عليه قول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-8","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"أمَّا الخِيَامُ فَإنَّها كخِيَامهمْ ... وأَرَى نِسَاءَ الحيِّ غَيْرَ نِسَائِهَا(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-9","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"وما يخادع في الحقيقة إلا نفسه، حيث حرمها الوصول، وتركها في أودية الأكوان تجول، قلبه بمرض الفرق والقطيعة سقيم، وهو يظن أنه في عداد مَن يأتي الله بقلب سليم، فزاده الله مرضاً على مرضه حيث رضي بسقمه وعيبه، وله عذاب الحرص والتعب في ضيق الحجاب والنصب بسبب كذبه على الله، وإنكاره على أولياء الله، فجزاؤه البعد والخذلان، وسوء العاقبة والحرمان، عائذاً بالله من المكر والطغيان.","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-8-10-10","r":"q2-8-10","title":"2:8–10 · Hypocrisy, self-deception and the diseased heart","text":"ثم ذكر أقوالهم الشنيعة، وأحوالهم الفظيعة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-8-10-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-8-10-s1","r":"q2-8-10","title":"Deception, perception and sickness","text":"I say: man ( مَن ) is an indefinite qualified expression ( موصوفة ), functioning as the subject ( مبتدأ ), with the predicate placed first: “Among people are people who say such-and-such.” Deception ( المخادعة ) is displaying the opposite of the disagreeable thing one conceals. The root meaning of khadʿ ( الخدع ) is concealment; hence mikhdaʿ ( المخدع ), a room where possessions are hidden. It is also said to mean corruption, because the hypocrites corrupt their faith by what they conceal. The clause “without perceiving it” ( وما يشعرون ) is circumstantial ( حالية ): “being unaware.” Perception ( الشعور ) is noticing or becoming aware ( التفطّن ); the verb is conjugated according to the patterns of karuma and naṣara . “Would that I knew” ( ليت شعري ) means, “Would that my awareness grasped this.” The clause “in their hearts is a sickness” explains the cause ( تعليلية ) of their deception. Sickness ( المرض ) is weakness and languor; here it is the sickness of hearts through doubt and hypocrisy. In God is refuge.","anchor":"en-q2-8-10-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-8-10-s2","r":"q2-8-10","title":"The concealed condition of the hypocrites","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: among people are those charged with hypocrisy, such as some of the Jews and the hypocrites. They say with their tongues what is not in their hearts: “We believe in God and in the Last Day,” but they are not numbered among the believers. Through their profession of faith they imagine they deceive God and those who believe; in reality they deceive only themselves, for the evil consequence of their deception returns upon them. They do not perceive that their deception is to their own harm. This deception arises because their hearts harbour the sickness of doubt and envy: their hearts waver and their souls are troubled. God increases their sickness through the verses He sends down that expose them. In the Hereafter, when they come before God, they will suffer painful punishment because they denied the Messenger of God, or because they lied against God. This is the substance of the verse. [B011] The Real, glorious is His majesty, opens by mentioning those who make their religion sincerely God’s and whose hearts accord with their tongues. He then mentions the unbelievers, whose unbelief is unalloyed both outwardly and inwardly. Third come the hypocrites, who believe with their mouths but not with their hearts. These are the most corrupt of the unbelievers, because they mix unbelief with mockery and deception. Hence they occupy the lowest depth of the Fire.","anchor":"en-q2-8-10-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-8-10-s3","r":"q2-8-10","title":"Claiming realization without possessing it","text":"Among people are those who lay presumptuous claim to special election ( الخصوصية ) and profess to have realized the witnessing of lordship ( مشاهدة الربوبية ), while remaining in the lowest depth of ordinary, unillumined existence ( العمومية ). They display purity of faith and realized gnosis, yet wander bewildered in the valleys of doubts and passing thoughts, thirsting in the deserts of severance and separation ( القطيعة والفَرْق ). Their tongues run freely with claims, while their hearts are desolate of guidance. They seek to deceive God, content with their own faults and misdeeds, and deceive Muslims by adorning their outward appearance while their inward being is filled with egoic shares and inclinations. They dress in the garb of gnostics but act as the ignorant do. The poet’s words apply to them: The tents are like their tents, indeed; but the women of this encampment are not its women. In truth such a person deceives only himself, depriving his soul of arrival and leaving it to wander in the valleys of created things. His heart is sick with separation and severance, while he supposes himself to be among those who come to God with a sound heart. God increases his sickness because he is content with his disease and defect. He suffers the punishment of anxious grasping and weariness within the constriction of the veil and its toil, because he lies against God and rejects God’s friends. His recompense is distance and abandonment, an evil end and deprivation. In God we seek refuge from hidden devising and transgression.","anchor":"en-q2-8-10-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-8-10-s4","r":"q2-8-10","title":"","text":"He then mentions their abominable words and appalling states, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-8-10-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-11-12","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform 2:11–12","anchor":"unit-q2-11-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-1","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُمْ لا تُفْسِدُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ قالُوا إِنَّما نَحْنُ مُصْلِحُونَ (11) أَلا إِنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْمُفْسِدُونَ وَلكِنْ لا يَشْعُرُونَ (12)","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-2","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"قلت: «إذا» ظرف خافض لشرطه منصوب بجوابه، أي: قالوا نحن مصلحون، وقت قول القائل لهم: لا تفسدوا، والجملة بيان وتقرير لخداعهم، أو معطوفة على (من يقول آمنا) ، أي: ومن الناس فرقة إِذا قيلَ لهم:","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-3","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"لا تفسدوا، قالوا: إنما نحن مصلحون.","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-4","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا قِيلَ لهؤلاء المنافقين: لا تُفْسِدُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ بالمعاصي والتعويق عن الإيمان، وإغراء أهل الكفر والطغيان على أهل الإسلام والإيمان، وتهييج الحروب والفتن، وإظهار الهرج والمرج والمحن، وإفشاء أسرار المسلمين إلى أعدائهم الكافرين، فإن ذلك يؤدي إلى فساد النظام، وقطع مواد الإنعام، قالُوا في جوابهم الفاسد: إِنَّما نَحْنُ مُصْلِحُونَ في ذلك، فلا تصح مخاطبتنا بذلك، فإن من شأننا الإصلاح والإرشاد، وحالنا خالص من شوائب الفساد، قال تعالى: أَلا إِنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْمُفْسِدُونَ هنالك، ولكن لا شعور لهم بذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-5","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"قلت: فردّ الله ما ادعوه من الانتظام في سلك المصلحين بأقبح رد وأبلغه، من وجوه الاستئناف الذي في الجملة، والاستفتاح بالتنبيه، والتأكيد بإن وضمير الفعل، وتعريف الخبر، والتعبير بنفي الشعور، إذ لو شعروا أدنى شعور لتحققوا أنهم مفسدون.","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-6","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"وهذه الآية عامة لكل مَن اشتغل بما لا يعنيه، وعوق عن طريق الخصوص، ففيه شعبة من النفاق، وفي صحيح البخاري: «ثلاث من كن فيه كان مُنَافِقاً خالِصاً: إذا حدّث كذب، وإذا وعد أخلف، وإذا أؤتمن خان» .","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-7","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"الإشارة: وإذا قيل لمن يشتغل بالتعويق عن طريق الله والإنكار على أولياء الله: أقصر من هذا الإفساد، وارجع عن هذا الغي والعناد، فقد ظهرت معالم الإرشاد لأهل المحبة والوداد. قال: إنما أنا مصلح ناصح، وفي أحوالي كلها صالح، يقول له الحق جلّ جلاله: بل أفسدت قلوب عبادي، ورددتهم عن طريق محبتي وودادي، وعوقتهم عن دخول حضرتي، وحرمتهم شهود ذاتي وصفاتي، سددت بابي في وجه أحبابي، آيستهم من وجود التربية، وتحكمت على القدرة الأزلية، ولكنك لا تشعر بما أنت فيه من البلية.","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-8","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"ولقد صدق مَن سبقت له العناية، وأُتحف بالرعاية والهداية، حيث يقول(1):","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-9","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"فَهَذِهِ طريقَةُ الإشْرَاقِ ... كَانَتْ وتَبْقَى ما الوُجُودُ بَاقِ","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-10","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"وقال أيضاً:","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-11","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"وأَنْكَرُوهُ مَلاٌ عَوَامٌ ... لَمْ يَفْهَمُوا مَقْصُودَهُ فَهَامُوا","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-12","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"فتب أيها المنكر قبل الفوات، واطلب من يأخذ بيدك قبل الممات، لئلا تلقى الله بقلب سقيم، فتكون في الحضيض الأسفل من عذابه الأليم، فسبب العذاب وجود الحجاب، وإتمام النعيم النظر لوجهه الكريم، منحنا الله منه الحظ الأوفى في الدنيا والآخرة. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-11-12-13","r":"q2-11-12","title":"2:11–12 · Corruption disguised as reform","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى استهزاءهم بالإسلام وامتناعهم منه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-11-12-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-11-12-s1","r":"q2-11-12","title":"The conditional expression","text":"I say: idhā ( إذا ) is an adverbial expression ( ظرف ) that places its conditional clause in a genitival relation and is itself governed in the accusative by the response ( خافض لشرطه منصوب بجوابه ). That is: they say, “We put things right,” at the time someone tells them, “Do not cause corruption.” The sentence explains and confirms their deception; alternatively, it is coordinated with “those who say, ‘We believe.’” The sense is: among people is a group who, when told not to cause corruption, say, “We are only putting things right.”","anchor":"en-q2-11-12-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-11-12-s2","r":"q2-11-12","title":"The emphatic rejection of a false claim","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when these hypocrites are told not to corrupt the earth through disobedience, obstructing faith, inciting unbelievers and transgressors against the people of Islam and faith, stirring up wars and dissension, provoking disorder, confusion and affliction, or divulging Muslims’ secrets to their unbelieving enemies—for that disrupts the order of things and cuts off the means of beneficence—they make the corrupt reply, “We are only putting things right by this. It is therefore improper to address us in that fashion, for reform and guidance are our concern, and our state is free of any taint of corruption.” God Most High replies: surely it is they who cause corruption there, though they have no perception of it. I say: God rejects their claim to belong among those who put things right with the most devastating and eloquent rejection, in several ways: the sentence’s independent opening ( الاستئناف ), its initial call to attention ( التنبيه ), emphasis through inna and the separating pronoun ( ضمير الفصل ) [Translator’s note: Cairo I:79 prints ḍamīr al-fiʿl ( ضمير الفعل , “the pronoun of the verb”). The nominal clause contains the separating pronoun hum ; the closely parallel emphatic-device lists in al-Bayḍāwī’s Anwār al-tanzīl (I:46) and al-Nasafī’s Madārik , both on Q2:12, explicitly identify faṣl . The correction to ḍamīr al-faṣl remains a conjecture about the letters of this passage, and the origin of Cairo’s reading is unestablished.], the definite form of the predicate ( تعريف الخبر ), and the expression denying them perception. Had they the least perception, they would recognize that they were corrupters. [B012] This verse applies generally to anyone who occupies himself with what does not concern him and obstructs the way of the elect. Such a person has a branch of hypocrisy within him. In al-Bukhārī’s Ṣaḥīḥ : “Three qualities, if present in someone, make him a complete hypocrite: when he speaks, he lies; when he promises, he breaks his promise; and when he is entrusted with something, he betrays the trust.” [B013]","anchor":"en-q2-11-12-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-11-12-s3","r":"q2-11-12","title":"Obstructing the path of divine love","text":"When one who occupies himself with obstructing God’s path and rejecting God’s friends is told, “Desist from this corruption and turn back from this error and obstinacy: the signs of right guidance have become manifest to the people of love and affection,” he says, “I am only a reformer and sincere adviser, upright in all my states.” The Real, glorious is His majesty, says to him: “Rather, you have corrupted My servants’ hearts, turned them back from the path of My love and affection, hindered them from entering My Presence, and deprived them of witnessing My Essence and attributes. You have shut My door in the faces of My beloveds, made them despair of the existence of spiritual formation ( التربية ), and presumed to pass judgement upon eternal power ( القدرة الأزلية ). Yet you do not perceive the calamity in which you stand.” How truly has one whom antecedent providential care embraced, and who was favoured with protection and guidance, said: This is the path of illumination: it has been, and will remain while existence remains. He also says: A crowd of common people denied it; they did not understand its purpose, and wandered astray. [B014] Repent, then, O denier, before the opportunity passes. Seek someone to take you by the hand before death, lest you meet God with a diseased heart and fall into the lowest depth of His painful punishment. For the cause of punishment is the presence of the veil, while the fulfilment of bliss is beholding His noble Face. May God grant us the fullest share of that in this world and the Hereafter. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-11-12-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-11-12-s4","r":"q2-11-12","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then mentions their mockery of Islam and refusal to enter it, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-11-12-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-13","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility 2:13","anchor":"unit-q2-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-1","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُمْ آمِنُوا كَما آمَنَ النَّاسُ قالُوا أَنُؤْمِنُ كَما آمَنَ السُّفَهاءُ أَلا إِنَّهُمْ هُمُ السُّفَهاءُ وَلكِنْ لا يَعْلَمُونَ (13)","anchor":"ar-q2-13-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-2","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"قلت: الكاف من كَما آمَنَ صفة لمصدر محذوف، و (ما) مصدرية. أي: إذا قيل لهم آمنوا إيماناً خالصاً من النفاق مثل إيمان المسلمين، أو من أسلم من جلدتهم، والسفه: خفة وطيش في العقل، يقال: ثوب سفيه، أي: خفيف.","anchor":"ar-q2-13-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-3","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا قِيلَ لهؤلاء المنافقين من المشركين واليهود: اتركوا ما أنتم عليه من الكفر والجحود، وراقبوا الملك المعبود، وطهروا قلوبكم من الكفر والنفاق، وأقصروا مما أنتم فيه من البعاد والشقاق وآمِنُوا إيماناً خالصاً مثل إيمان المسلمين، لتكونوا معهم في أعلى عليين، «مَنْ أحَبَّ قَوْماً حُشرِ مَعهم» . «المَرْءُ مَعَ مَنْ أَحَبَّ» ، قالُوا مترجمين عما في قلوبهم من الكفر والنفاق: أَنُؤْمِنُ كَما آمَنَ السُّفَهاءُ الذين لا عقل لهم، إذ جُلهم فقراء ومَوَالي.","anchor":"ar-q2-13-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-4","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"قال الحق تعالى في الرد عليهم وتقبيح رأيهم: أَلا إِنَّهُمْ هُمُ السُّفَهاءُ لا غيرهم، حيث تركوا ما هو السبب في الفوز العظيم بالنعيم المقيم، وارتكبوا ما استوجبوا به الخلود في الدرك الأسفل من الجحيم وَلكِنْ لاَّ","anchor":"ar-q2-13-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-5","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"يَعْلَمُونَ، وَسَيَعْلَمُ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا أَيَّ مُنْقَلَبٍ يَنْقَلِبُونَ، عبَّر الحق في هذه الآية ب لا يَعْلَمُونَ وفي الأولى ب لاَ يَشْعُرُونَ لأن الفساد في الأرض يدرك بأدنى شعور، بخلاف الإيمان والتمييز بين الحق والباطل فيحتاج إلى زيادة تفكر واكتساب علم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-13-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-6","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"الإشارة: وإذا قيل لأهل الإنكار على أهل الخصوصية، القاصدين مشاهدة عظمة الربوبية، قد تجرّدوا عن لباس العز والاشتهار، ولبسوا أطمار الذل والافتقار، آمنوا بطريق هؤلاء المخصوصين، وادخلوا معهم كي تكونوا من المقربين. قالوا: (أنؤمن كما آمن السفهاء) ونترك ما نحن عليه من العز والكبرياء، قال الله تعالى فِى تسفيه رأيهم وتقبيح شأنهم: (ألا إنهم هم السفهاء) حيث تعززوا بعز يفنى، وتركوا العز الذي لا يفنى، قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-13-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-7","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"تَذَلَّلْ لِمَنْ تَهْوَى لِتَكْسِبَ عِزةً ... فكم عزة قد نالها المرء بِالذُّلِّ","anchor":"ar-q2-13-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-8","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"إِذَا كَانَ مَنْ تَهْوى عَزِيزاً، وَلَمْ تَكُنْ ... ذَلِيلاً لَهُ، فَاقْرَ السَّلامَ على الوَصْلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-13-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-9","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"فلو علموا ما في طيّ الذل من العز، وما في طي الفقر من الغنى، لجالدوا عليه بالسيوف، ولكن لا يعلمون.","anchor":"ar-q2-13-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-13-10","r":"q2-13","title":"2:13 · Faith, folly and the dignity of humility","text":"ثم بين الحق تعالى ما أضمروه من النفاق وأظهروه من الوفاق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-13-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-13-s1","r":"q2-13","title":"Comparison and the meaning of folly","text":"I say: the kāf in “as they have believed” ( كما آمن ) qualifies an omitted verbal noun ( صفة لمصدر محذوف ), and mā is nominalizing ( مصدرية ). The sense is: when they are told, “Believe with a faith free of hypocrisy, like the faith of the Muslims,” or of those from their own people who have embraced Islam. Folly ( السفه ) is lightness and rashness of intellect; one says of a thin garment that it is safīh .","anchor":"en-q2-13-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-13-s2","r":"q2-13","title":"The inversion of wisdom and folly","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when these hypocrites among the associators and Jews are told, “Leave your unbelief and denial; be watchful of the King who is worshipped; purify your hearts from unbelief and hypocrisy; desist from your estrangement and discord; and believe with a pure faith like that of the Muslims, so that you may be with them in the highest heights”—for “Whoever loves a people will be gathered with them,” and “A person is with those he loves”—they give expression to the unbelief and hypocrisy in their hearts by saying, “Shall we believe as the foolish have believed, those without intelligence?” For most of them are poor people and clients ( موالي ). [B015] Refuting them and exposing the ugliness of their judgement, the Real Most High says: “Surely it is they who are foolish,” not the others, because they abandon what brings the tremendous success of abiding bliss and commit what makes them deserve perpetual residence in the lowest depth of Hell. “But they do not know.” “Those who do wrong shall know to what place of return they will return” [26:227]. In this verse the Real says, “They do not know,” whereas in the preceding verse He says, “They do not perceive.” For corruption on earth can be grasped by the slightest perception; faith and discrimination between truth and falsehood, by contrast, require further reflection and the acquisition of knowledge. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-13-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-13-s3","r":"q2-13","title":"Humility as the road to abiding dignity","text":"When those who reject the people of special election—who seek to witness the majesty of lordship, have stripped themselves of the garments of dignity and renown, and donned the rags of lowliness and need—are told, “Believe in the path of these specially favoured ones and enter it with them, so that you may be among those brought near,” they answer, “Shall we believe as the foolish have believed, and abandon the dignity and grandeur we possess?” Exposing the folly of their judgement and the ugliness of their condition, God Most High says: “Surely it is they who are foolish,” because they seek might in a dignity that passes away and abandon the dignity that does not pass away. The poet says: Humble yourself before the one you love, to gain dignity: how much dignity has a man attained through lowliness! If the one you love is mighty and you will not be lowly before him, bid farewell to union. Were they to know the dignity folded within lowliness and the riches folded within poverty, they would fight for it with swords. But they do not know.","anchor":"en-q2-13-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-13-s4","r":"q2-13","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then makes clear the hypocrisy they conceal and the agreement they display, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-13-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-14-16","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path 2:14–16","anchor":"unit-q2-14-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-1","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"وَإِذا لَقُوا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قالُوا آمَنَّا وَإِذا خَلَوْا إِلى شَياطِينِهِمْ قالُوا إِنَّا مَعَكُمْ إِنَّما نَحْنُ مُسْتَهْزِؤُنَ (14) اللَّهُ يَسْتَهْزِئُ بِهِمْ وَيَمُدُّهُمْ فِي طُغْيانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُونَ (15) أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ اشْتَرَوُا الضَّلالَةَ بِالْهُدى فَما رَبِحَتْ تِجارَتُهُمْ وَما كانُوا مُهْتَدِينَ (16)","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-2","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"قلت: اللقاء: المصادفة بلا قصد، والخلو بالشيء أو معه: الانفراد به، ضمنه هنا معنى رجع، ولذلك تعدَّى بإلى، و (الشيطان) فَيْعَالٌ، من شَطَنَ، إذا بعد، أو فَعْلاَن من شاط، إذا بطل، والاستهزاء بالشيء: الاستخفاف بحقه، والعَمَهُ في البصيرة كالعمى في البصر.","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-3","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في وصف المنافقين تقريراً لنفاقهم: إنهم كانوا إِذا لَقُوا الصحابة أظهروا الإيمان، وإذا رجعوا إِلى شَياطِينِهِمْ أي: كبرائهم المتمردين في الكفر والطغيان، قالُوا إِنَّا مَعَكُمْ لم","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-4","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"نخرج عن ديننا إِنَّما نَحْنُ مُسْتَهْزِؤُنَ بهم، ومستسخرون بشأنهم. نزلت في عبد الله بن أُبَيّ- رأس المنافقين- كان إذا لقي سعداً قال: نعم الدين دين محمد، وإذا خلا برؤساء قومه من أهل الكفر، قال: شدوا أيديكم على دين آبائكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-5","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"وخرج ذات يوم مع أصحابه فاستقبلهم نفر من الصحابة- رضوان الله عليهم- فقال عبدُ الله لأصحابه: انظروا كيف أرد هؤلاء السفهاء عنكم، فأخذ بيد أبى بكر رضى الله عنه فقال: مرحباً بالصدِّيق سيد بني تيم، وشيخ الإسلام، وثانى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم في الغار، الباذل نفسه وماله لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم، ثم أخذ بيد عمر، فقال: مرحباً بسيد بني عدي بن كعب، الفاروق، القوي في دين الله، الباذل نفسه وماله لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم، ثم أخذ بيد عَلِيّ فقال: مرحباً بابن عم رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم وخِتِنِه(1)، سيد بني هاشم، ما عدا رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم، فقال على رضى الله عنه: يا عبد الله، اتق الله ولا تنافق، فإن المنافقين شرُّ خليقة الله، فقال عبد الله: مهلاً يا أبا الحسن، أنى تقول هذا؟ والله إن إيماننا كإيمانكم، وتصديقنا كتصديقكم، فنزلت الآية(2).","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-6","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"ثم ردّ الله تعالى عليهم فقال: اللَّهُ يَسْتَهْزِئُ بِهِمْ أي: يفعل بهم فعل المستهزئ بأن يفتح لهم باباً إلى الجنة وهم في النار، ويطلع المؤمنين عليهم، فيقول لهم: ادخلوا الجنة، فإذا جاءوا يستبقون إليها وطمعوا في الدخول، سُدَّتْ عليهم ورجعوا إلى النار، فَالْيَوْمَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مِنَ الْكُفَّارِ يَضْحَكُونَ الآية. وَيَمُدُّهُمْ أي: يمهلهم فِي كفرهم، وطُغْيانِهِمْ يتحيرون إلى يوم يبعثون لأنهم اشْتَرَوُا الضَّلالَةَ بِالْهُدى أي: استبدلوا بها رأس مالهم، فضلاً عن الربح، إذ الإيمان رأس المال، وأعمال الطاعات ربح، فإذا ذهب الرأس فلا ربح ولذلك قال تعالى فَما رَبِحَتْ تِجارَتُهُمْ، بل خسرت صفقتهم، وَما كانُوا مُهْتَدِينَ إلى أسباب الربح أبداً، لاستبدالهم الهدى- التي هي رأس المال- بالضلالة- التي هي سبب الخسران. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-7","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"وهاهنا استعارات وبلاغات يطول سردها، إذ مرادنا تربية اليقين بكلام رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-8","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"الإشارة: الناس في طريق الخصوص على أربعة أقسام:","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-9","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"قسم: سبقت لهم من الله العناية، وهَبَّتْ عليهم ريحُ الهداية، فصدقوا ودخلوا فيها، وبذلوا أنفسهم وأموالهم في سبيل الله، فَتَجِرُوا فيه وربحوا، فعوّضهم الله تعالى جنة المعارف، يتبوءون منها حيث شاءوا، فإذا قدموا عليه أدخلهم جنة الزخارف، يسرحون فيها حيث شاءوا، وأتحفهم فيها بالنظر إلى وجهه الكريم.","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-10","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"وقسم: سبقت لهم من الله الهداية، وحفتهم الرعاية، فصدقوا وأقروا، ولكنهم ضعفوا عن الدخول، ولم تتعلق همتهم بالوصول، فبقوا في ضعفاء المسلمين لَيْسَ عَلَى الضُّعَفاءِ وَلا عَلَى الْمَرْضى وَلا عَلَى الَّذِينَ لا يَجِدُونَ ما يُنْفِقُونَ حَرَجٌ إِذا نَصَحُوا لِلَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ ما عَلَى الْمُحْسِنِينَ مِنْ سَبِيلٍ....","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-11","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"وقسم: أنكروا وأظهروا وجحدوا وكفروا، فتجروا وخسروا، «مَنْ عادى لي وليّاً فقد آذنْتُهُ بالْحَربِ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-12","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"وقسم رابع: هم مذبذبون بين ذلك إذا لقوا أهل الخصوصية قالوا: آمنا وصدقنا فأنتم على الجادة، وإذا رجعوا إلى أهل التمرد من المنكرين- طعنوا وجحدوا، وقالوا: إنما كنا بهم مستهزئين، اللَّهُ يَسْتَهْزِئُ بِهِمْ بما يظهر لهم من صور الكرامات والاستدراجات، ويمدهم في تعاطي العوائد والشهوات، وطلب العلو والرئاسات، متحيرين في مهامه الخواطر والغفلات، أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ اشْتَرَوُا الضَّلالَةَ عن طريق الخصوص من أهل الوصول، بِالْهُدى الذي كان بيدهم، لو حصل لهم التصديق والدخول، فما ربحوا في تجارتهم، وما كانوا مهتدين إلى بلوغ المأمول. قال بعض العارفين: (التصديق بطريقتنا ولاية، والدخول فيها عناية، والانتقاد عليها جناية) . وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-14-16-13","r":"q2-14-16","title":"2:14–16 · Mockery, spiritual commerce and four responses to the Path","text":"ثم ضرب مثل المنافقين، زيادة فى توبيخهم وتقبيح شأنهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-14-16-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-14-16-s1","r":"q2-14-16","title":"Meeting, withdrawal and the devil","text":"I say: meeting ( اللقاء ) is an unplanned encounter. Being alone with a thing or someone ( الخلوّ به أو معه ) means being apart with it or him. Here the verb includes the meaning “return,” and is therefore followed by ilā ( إلى ). “Devil” ( الشيطان ) has either the pattern fayʿāl ( فَيْعَال ), from shaṭana , “to be distant,” or faʿlān ( فَعْلان ), from shāṭa , “to perish or come to nothing.” Mocking a thing is treating its due standing lightly. Bewildered blindness ( العَمَه ) in inward sight is like blindness ( العمى ) in bodily sight. [B016]","anchor":"en-q2-14-16-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-14-16-s2","r":"q2-14-16","title":"Duplicity towards the believers","text":"Describing the hypocrites and confirming their hypocrisy, the Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when they met the Companions, they displayed faith; but when they returned to their devils—that is, their leaders obstinate in unbelief and transgression—they said, “We are with you; we have not departed from our religion. We were merely mocking them and making sport of their affairs.” This was revealed concerning ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy, the leader of the hypocrites. Whenever he met Saʿd, he said, “What an excellent religion is Muḥammad’s!” But when alone with the unbelieving leaders of his people, he said, “Hold firmly to the religion of your forefathers.” One day he went out with his associates and met a group of the Companions, may God be pleased with them. ʿAbd Allāh told his associates, “Watch how I keep these fools away from you.” Taking Abū Bakr’s hand, he said: “Welcome to al-Ṣiddīq, chief of Banū Taym, elder of Islam, the Messenger of God’s companion in the cave, who gives his life and wealth for the Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace!” He then took ʿUmar’s hand: “Welcome to the chief of Banū ʿAdī ibn Kaʿb, al-Fārūq, strong in God’s religion, who gives his life and wealth for the Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace!” Then he took ʿAlī’s hand: “Welcome to the cousin and son-in-law of the Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace, chief of Banū Hāshim apart from the Messenger of God!” ʿAlī, may God be pleased with him, replied: “ʿAbd Allāh, fear God and do not be hypocritical: the hypocrites are the worst of God’s creatures.” ʿAbd Allāh said: “Gently, Abū al-Ḥasan! How can you say this? By God, our faith is like yours, and our assent is like yours.” The verse was then revealed. [B017]","anchor":"en-q2-14-16-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-14-16-s3","r":"q2-14-16","title":"Mockery returned and the loss of spiritual capital","text":"God Most High then answers them: “God mocks them”—that is, He treats them as a mocker would. While they are in the Fire He opens a door to the Garden, allows the believers to look upon them, and says to them, “Enter the Garden.” When they race towards it, hoping to enter, it is closed against them and they return to the Fire. “So today those who believe laugh at the unbelievers” [83:34]. He prolongs their respite as they wander bewildered in their unbelief and transgression until the day they are raised. For they “purchased error at the price of guidance”: they exchanged away their capital, to say nothing of profit. Faith is the capital and acts of obedience are the profit; once the capital is gone, there is no profit. Hence God Most High says, “Their trade has brought no profit”—rather, their transaction has incurred loss—“and they were not guided” to the means of profit at all, because they exchanged guidance, their capital, for error, the cause of loss. And success is through God. There are metaphors and eloquent devices here whose enumeration would be lengthy. Our purpose, however, is to nurture certainty ( تربية اليقين ) through the speech of the Lord of the worlds.","anchor":"en-q2-14-16-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-14-16-s4","r":"q2-14-16","title":"Four kinds of response to the way of the elect","text":"People fall into four groups with regard to the way of the elect ( طريق الخصوص ). The first are those for whom God’s providential care has preceded and over whom the breeze of guidance has blown. They believe in the Path and enter it, giving their lives and wealth in God’s way. They trade therein and profit. God Most High gives them in exchange the garden of gnoses ( جنة المعارف ), in which they settle wherever they wish. When they come before Him, He admits them to the Garden of adornments ( جنة الزخارف ), where they roam wherever they wish, and favours them there with the sight of His noble Face. The second are those for whom God’s guidance has preceded and whom His protection surrounds. They believe and acknowledge, but are too weak to enter, and their spiritual aspiration ( الهمة ) does not attach itself to arrival. They remain among the weak Muslims: “There is no blame upon the weak, the sick, or those unable to find anything to spend, provided they are sincere towards God and His Messenger. There is no ground for reproach against those who do good” [9:91]. The third openly deny, reject and disbelieve. They trade and lose: “Whoever shows enmity to a friend of Mine, I declare war upon him.” The fourth waver between these. On meeting the people of special election, they say, “We believe and affirm; you are upon the right highway.” But when they return to obstinate deniers, they disparage and reject, saying, “We were only mocking them.” God mocks them through the semblances of miraculous favours and gradual enticements ( صور الكرامات والاستدراجات ) that He displays to them, and prolongs their immersion in habits and appetites, the pursuit of eminence and leadership, bewildered in the wildernesses of passing thoughts and heedlessness. [B018] These have purchased estrangement from the special path of those who have arrived, at the price of the guidance that would have been theirs had they believed and entered. Their trade has brought them no profit, nor are they guided to attain what they hoped for. One of the gnostics said: “Believing in our path is friendship with God ( ولاية ); entering it is providential care ( عناية ); and attacking it is an offence ( جناية ).” And success is through God; He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q2-14-16-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-14-16-s5","r":"q2-14-16","title":"","text":"He then sets forth a likeness of the hypocrites, further rebuking them and exposing the ugliness of their condition, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-14-16-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-17-18","r":"q2-17-18","title":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light","text":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light 2:17–18","anchor":"unit-q2-17-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-17-18-1","r":"q2-17-18","title":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light","text":"مَثَلُهُمْ كَمَثَلِ الَّذِي اسْتَوْقَدَ ناراً فَلَمَّا أَضاءَتْ ما حَوْلَهُ ذَهَبَ اللَّهُ بِنُورِهِمْ وَتَرَكَهُمْ فِي ظُلُماتٍ لا يُبْصِرُونَ (17) صُمٌّ بُكْمٌ عُمْيٌ فَهُمْ لا يَرْجِعُونَ (18)","anchor":"ar-q2-17-18-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-17-18-2","r":"q2-17-18","title":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light","text":"قلت: (استوقد) يحتمل أن تكون للطلب، أو زائدة بمعنى أوقد، و (لما) شرطية، وذَهَبَ جواب، وإذا كان لفظ الموصول مفرداً واقعاً على جماعة، يصح في الضمير مراعاة لفظه فيفرد، ومعناه فيجمع، فأفرد في الآية أولاً، وجمع ثانياً. ويقال: أضاء يضئ إضاءة، وضَاء يضُوء ضَوْءاً.","anchor":"ar-q2-17-18-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-17-18-3","r":"q2-17-18","title":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: مثل هؤلاء المنافقين من اليهود كَمَثَلِ رجل في ظلمة، تائه في الطريق، فاستوقد ناراً ليبصر طريق القصد فَلَمَّا اشتعلت وأَضاءَتْ ما حَوْلَهُ فأبصر الطريق، وظهرت له معالم التحقيق، أطفأ الله تلك النار وأذهب نورها، ولم يبق إلا جمرها وحرّها. كذلك اليهود كانوا في ظلمة الكفر والمعاصي ينتظرون ظهور نور النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم ويطلبونه، فلما قدم عليهم، وأشرقت أنواره بين أيديهم كفروا به، فأذهب الله عنهم نوره، وَتَرَكَهُمْ فِي ظُلُماتٍ الكفر والشك والنفاق، لاَّ يُبْصِرُونَ ولا يهتدون، صُمٌّ عن سماع الحق،","anchor":"ar-q2-17-18-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-17-18-4","r":"q2-17-18","title":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light","text":"بُكْمٌ عن النطق به عُمْيٌ عن رؤية نوره، فَهُمْ لا يَرْجِعُونَ عن غيّهم، ولا يقصرون عن ضلالتهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-17-18-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-17-18-5","r":"q2-17-18","title":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light","text":"الإشارة: مَثَلُ مَنْ كان في ظلمات الحجاب قد أحاطت به الشكوك والارتياب، وهو يطلب من يأخذ بيده ويهديه إلى طريق رشده، فلما ظهرت أنوار العارفين، وأحدقت به أسرار المقربين، حتى أشرقت من نورهم أقطارُ البلاد، وحَيِيَ بهم جلّ العباد، أنكرهم وبعد منهم، فتصامم عن سماع وعظهم، وتباكَمَ عن تصديقهم، وعَمِيَ عن شهود خصوصيتهم، فلا رجوع له عن حظوظه وهواه، ولا انزجار له عن العكوف على متابعة دنياه، مثله كمن كان في ظلمات الليل ضالاً عن الطريق، فاستوقد ناراً لتظهر له الطريق، فلما اشتعلت وأضاءت ما حوله أذهب الله نورها، وبقي جمرها وحرّها، وهذه سنة ماضية: لا ينتفع بالولي إلا مَن كان بعيداً منه. وفي الحديث: «أزْهَدُ النَّاسِ في العَالِم جيرانُه» ، وقد مَثَّلُوا الولي بالنهر الجاري كلما بَعُدَ جَرْيُه عَمَّ الانتفاعُ به، ومثَّلوه أيضاً بالنخلة لا تُظِلُّ إلا عن بُعْد. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-17-18-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-17-18-6","r":"q2-17-18","title":"2:17–18 · The extinguished light","text":"ثم ضرب لهم مثلا آخر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-17-18-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-17-18-s1","r":"q2-17-18","title":"Kindling and the shift from singular to plural","text":"I say: the prefix in istawqada ( استوقد ) may signify seeking [to kindle], or it may be additional, giving the meaning of awqada , “kindled.” Lammā ( لمّا ) is conditional, and “God takes away” ( ذهب ) is its response ( جواب ). When a relative pronoun is singular in form but applies to a group, a subsequent pronoun may agree with its form and be singular, or with its meaning and be plural. The verse first uses the singular and then the plural. One says aḍāʾa, yuḍīʾu, iḍāʾatan , and ḍāʾa, yaḍūʾu, ḍawʾan , of giving light.","anchor":"en-q2-17-18-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-17-18-s2","r":"q2-17-18","title":"The light awaited and then rejected","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the likeness of these hypocrites among the Jews is that of a man lost on a road in darkness, who kindles a fire to see the right way. When it burns and lights up his surroundings, so that he sees the road and the landmarks of sure guidance become clear, God puts out the fire and takes away its light, leaving only its embers and heat. Likewise, the Jews were in the darkness of unbelief and disobedience, awaiting and seeking the appearance of the Prophet’s light, God bless him and grant him peace. When he came to them and his lights shone before them, they disbelieved in him. God therefore removed his light from them and left them in the darknesses of unbelief, doubt and hypocrisy, neither seeing nor finding guidance. They are deaf to hearing truth, dumb in speaking it, and blind to seeing its light. They do not return from their error or desist from their going astray.","anchor":"en-q2-17-18-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-17-18-s3","r":"q2-17-18","title":"Rejecting the guide when he appears","text":"Consider one who lives in the darknesses of the veil, surrounded by doubts and uncertainty, seeking someone to take him by the hand and guide him to the way of right direction. When the lights of the gnostics appear, and the mysteries of those brought near surround him, until the land’s regions shine with their light and the greater part of the servants is revived through them, he rejects them and stays distant. He makes himself deaf to their exhortation, dumb in affirming them, and blind to witnessing their special election. He will not return from his egoic shares and desires, nor desist from clinging to the pursuit of his worldly life. His likeness is that of someone lost from the road in the darkness of night who kindles a fire to reveal the way. Once it burns and lights his surroundings, God takes away its light, leaving only embers and heat. This is an established pattern: only those at a distance from a saint benefit from him. In the hadith: “Those who value a scholar least are his neighbours.” They have likened the saint to a flowing river: the farther it flows, the more widely it benefits others. They also liken him to a date-palm, which casts its shade only at a distance. And God Most High knows best. [B019]","anchor":"en-q2-17-18-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-17-18-s4","r":"q2-17-18","title":"","text":"He then sets forth another likeness of them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-17-18-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-19-20","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance 2:19–20","anchor":"unit-q2-19-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-19-20-1","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"أَوْ كَصَيِّبٍ مِنَ السَّماءِ فِيهِ ظُلُماتٌ وَرَعْدٌ وَبَرْقٌ يَجْعَلُونَ أَصابِعَهُمْ فِي آذانِهِمْ مِنَ الصَّواعِقِ حَذَرَ الْمَوْتِ وَاللَّهُ مُحِيطٌ بِالْكافِرِينَ (19) يَكادُ الْبَرْقُ يَخْطَفُ أَبْصارَهُمْ كُلَّما أَضاءَ لَهُمْ مَشَوْا فِيهِ وَإِذا أَظْلَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ قامُوا وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَذَهَبَ بِسَمْعِهِمْ وَأَبْصارِهِمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (20)","anchor":"ar-q2-19-20-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-19-20-2","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"قلت: (أو) للتنويع، أو بمعنى الواو، و (الصيب) : المطر، فَيْعِلٌ، من صاب المطر إذا نزل، وهو على حذف مضاف، أي: أو كذي صيب، وأصله: صيوب، كسيد، قلبت الواو ياء وأدغمت، ولا يوجد هذا إلا في المعتل كميت وهين وضيق وطيب. و (الرعد) : الصوت الذي يخرج من السحاب، و (البرق) : النور الذي يخرج منه. قال ابن عزيز: رُوِيَ عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم أنه قال: «إِنَّ اللهَ عزّ وجلّ ينشئ السَّحَابَ فَتنطِقُ أحْسَنَ النطْق، وتَضْحَكُ أحسَنُ الضحك، فنطقها الرعدُ، وضَحِكُها البَرْقُ» . وقال ابن عباس: (الرعدُ مَلَكٌ يسوقُ السَّحابَ، والبرقُ سَوْطٌ مِنْ نُورٍ يَزْجُرُ بهِ السَّحَاب) . هـ. والصواعق: قطعة من نار تسقط من المخراق الذي بيد سائق السحاب، وقيل: تسقط من نار بين السماء والأرض، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-19-20-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-19-20-3","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ومثل المنافقين أيضاً كأصحاب مطر غزير فِيهِ ظُلُماتٌ وَرَعْدٌ وهدير أصابهم في ليلة مظلمة وقفراء مُدْلهمة. فيه بَرْقٌ يلمع، وصاعقة تقمع، إذا ضرب الرعد وعظم صوته جعلوا أَصابِعَهُمْ فِي آذانِهِمْ من الهول والخوف حذراً من موت أنفسهم، وقد ماتت أرواحهم وقلوبهم، وإذا ضرب البرق كاد أن يَخْطَفُ أَبْصارَهُمْ، فإذا لمع أبصروا الطريق، ومَشَوْا فِيهِ، وَإِذا أَظْلَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ قامُوا متحيرين حائدين عن عين التحقيق، وَاللَّهُ مِنْ وَرائِهِمْ مُحِيطٌ. وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَذَهَبَ بِسَمْعِهِمْ بصوت ذلك الرعد، وَأَبْصارِهِمْ بلمعان ذلك البرق، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ لا يعجزه شيء.","anchor":"ar-q2-19-20-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-19-20-4","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"هذا مثلهم في تحيّرهم واضطرابهم، فيحتمل أن يكون من التشبيه المركب، وهو تشبيه الجملة بالجملة، أو من المفَصَّل، فيكون المطر مثالاً للقرآن، وفيه ذكر الكفر والنفاق المُشَبَّهَيْن بالظلمات، والوعد عليه والزجر المشبّه بالرعد، والحُجج الباهرة التي تكاد أحياناً تبهرهم المشبهة بالبرق، وتخوفهم، وروعُهم هو جَعْل أصابعهم في آذانهم، لئلا يسمعوا فيميلوا إلى الإيمان، وفَضْحُ نفاقهم وتكاليفُ الشرع التي يكرهونها هي الصواعق. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-19-20-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-19-20-5","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"الإشارة: أهل الخصوصية إذا ظهروا بين العموم بأحوال غريبة وعلوم وَهْبية، وأسرار ربانية وأذكار نورانية، دهشوا منهم وتحيّروا في أمرهم، وخافوا على أنفسهم، فإذا سمعوا منهم علوماً لدنية وأسراراً ربانية فرّوا منها، وجعلوا أصابعهم في آذانهم، خوفاً على نفوسهم أن تفارق عوائدها وهواها، وإذا خاصمهم أحد من العموم ألجموه بالحجة، فتكاد تلك الحجة تخطفه إلى الحضرة، كلما لمع له شيء من الحق مشى إلى حضرته، وإذا كرّت عليه الخصوم والخواطر، وأظلم عليه الحال، وقف في الباب حيران، ولو شاء الله لذهب بعقله وسمعه وبصره، فيبصر به إلى حضرته. مَن استغرب أن يُنقذه الله من شهوته، وأن يُخرجه من وجود غفلته، فقد استعجز القدرة الإلهية وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُقْتَدِراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-19-20-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-19-20-6","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"فالصِّيَّب الذي نزل من السماء كِنَايةٌ عن الواردات والأحوال التي ترد على قلوب العارفين، ويظهر أثرها على جوارحهم، والظلمات التي فيها كناية عن اختفاء بعضها عن أهل الشريعة فينكرونها، والرعد كناية عن اللهج بذكر الله جهراً في المحافل والحلق، والبرق كناية عن العلوم الغريبة التي ينطقون بها والحجج التي يحتجون بها على الخصوم، فإذا سمعها العوام اشمأزت قلوبهم عن قبولها، فإذا وقع منهم إنصاف تحققوا صحتها فمالوا إلى جهتها، ومَشَوْا إلى ناحيتها، فإذا كَرَّت عليهم الخصوم قاموا منكرين، ولو شاء ربك لهدى الناس جميعاً وَلا يَزالُونَ مُخْتَلِفِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-19-20-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-19-20-7","r":"q2-19-20","title":"2:19–20 · The storm: fear, bewilderment and flashes of guidance","text":"ولما ذكر الحق من تخلق بالإيمان ظاهراً وباطناً، ومن تحلّى به كذلك، ومن أخفى الكفر وأظهر الإيمان، دعا الكل إلى توحيده وعبادته، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-19-20-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-19-20-s1","r":"q2-19-20","title":"Rain, thunder and lightning","text":"I say: “or” ( أو ) distinguishes different kinds of likeness ( للتنويع ), or has the sense of “and.” Ṣayyib ( الصيّب ) means rain, on the pattern fayʿil ( فَيْعِل ), from ṣāba , said when rain descends. A governing noun is omitted ( حذف مضاف ): “or like those caught in a downpour.” Its underlying form is ṣaywib , as with sayyid : the wāw is changed to yāʾ and assimilated ( الإدغام ). This form occurs only in weak-rooted words ( المعتلّ ), such as mayyit , hayyin , ḍayyiq and ṭayyib . Thunder ( الرعد ) is the sound that comes from clouds, and lightning ( البرق ) the light that comes from them. Ibn ʿAzīz says: “It is related from the Messenger of God, God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: ‘God, mighty and majestic, brings clouds into being; they speak most beautifully and laugh most beautifully. Their speech is thunder and their laughter lightning.’ Ibn ʿAbbās said: ‘Thunder is an angel driving the clouds, and lightning a whip of light with which he urges them on.’” End of quotation. Thunderbolts ( الصواعق ) are pieces of fire that fall from the whip in the hand of the clouds’ driver. It is also said that they fall from a fire between heaven and earth. And God Most High knows best. [B020]","anchor":"en-q2-19-20-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-19-20-s2","r":"q2-19-20","title":"The structure of the storm simile","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the hypocrites are also like people caught by heavy rain, darkness and roaring thunder on a dark night in a pitch-black wilderness. Lightning flashes in it and thunderbolts strike. When thunder resounds with a mighty voice, they put their fingers in their ears in terror, fearing the death of their persons, though their spirits and hearts are already dead. When lightning flashes, it almost snatches away their sight. Its flash reveals the road, and they walk; when darkness returns, they stand bewildered, swerving from the very reality of sure guidance. God encompasses them from beyond them. Had He willed, He could have taken away their hearing through the thunder’s sound and their sight through the lightning’s flash. God has power over every thing; nothing defeats Him. This is their likeness in bewilderment and agitation. It may be a composite simile ( التشبيه المركّب ), comparing one whole situation with another; or it may be a detailed comparison ( المفصّل ). In that case, rain represents the Qurʾān, within which unbelief and hypocrisy are mentioned, likened to darkness. The announcement of their requital and the rebuke are likened to thunder; the dazzling proofs that almost overwhelm them at times are likened to lightning. Their fear and alarm are represented by putting their fingers in their ears, lest they hear and incline towards faith. The exposure of their hypocrisy and the obligations of the Sacred Law that they dislike are the thunderbolts. And God Most High knows best. [B021]","anchor":"en-q2-19-20-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-19-20-s3","r":"q2-19-20","title":"Spiritual influxes and resistance to transformation","text":"When the people of special election appear among ordinary people with unfamiliar states, bestowed sciences ( علوم وهبية ), lordly mysteries and luminous invocations, the latter are astonished and perplexed, and fear for themselves. On hearing divinely bestowed sciences and lordly mysteries from them, they flee and put their fingers in their ears, fearing that their souls will be parted from accustomed habits and desires. If someone among the ordinary people disputes with them, they silence him with a proof that almost carries him into the Presence. Whenever something of the truth flashes for him, he walks towards that Presence. But when opponents and passing thoughts return against him and his state darkens, he stands bewildered at the door. Had God willed, He would have taken away his own intellect, hearing and sight, so that through Him he might see his way into His Presence. “Whoever deems it strange that God should rescue him from his appetite and bring him out of his heedlessness has deemed the divine power incapable.” “God has power over all things” [18:45]. [B022] The downpour from the sky alludes to the spiritual influxes and states ( الواردات والأحوال ) that come upon the hearts of gnostics and show their effects upon their limbs. Its darknesses allude to the hiddenness of some of these from the people of the Sacred Law, who consequently deny them. Thunder alludes to persistence in invoking God aloud in assemblies and circles; lightning, to the unfamiliar sciences they express and the proofs they bring against opponents. When ordinary people hear these, their hearts recoil from accepting them. If they exercise fairness, they recognize their soundness, incline towards them and walk in their direction. When opponents return upon them, however, they stand in denial. Had your Lord willed, He would have guided everyone, “but they continue to differ” [11:118].","anchor":"en-q2-19-20-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-19-20-s4","r":"q2-19-20","title":"","text":"After mentioning those formed by faith outwardly and inwardly, those likewise adorned with it, and those concealing unbelief while displaying faith, the Real calls them all to affirm His oneness and worship Him, saying: [B023]","anchor":"en-q2-19-20-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-21-22","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence 2:21–22","anchor":"unit-q2-21-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-1","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اعْبُدُوا رَبَّكُمُ الَّذِي خَلَقَكُمْ وَالَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ (21) الَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْأَرْضَ فِراشاً وَالسَّماءَ بِناءً وَأَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّماءِ ماء فَأَخْرَجَ بِهِ مِنَ الثَّمَراتِ رِزْقاً لَكُمْ فَلا تَجْعَلُوا لِلَّهِ أَنْداداً وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (22)","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-2","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"قلت: جملة الترجي حال من الواو في (اعْبُدُوا) ، أي: اعبدوا ربكم راجين أن تنخرطوا في سلك المتقين الفائزين بالهدي والفلاح، المستوجبين جوار الله تعالى، نبّه به على أن التقوى منتهى درجات السالكين وهو التبري من كل شيء سوى الله تعالى- إلى الله تعالى.","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-3","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"و (الَّذي جَعَلَ) صفة للرب، و (فَلا تَجْعَلُوا) معطوف على (اعْبُدُوا) على أنه نهي، أو منصوب بأن، جواب له، و (الأنداد) جمع نِدِّ، بكسر النون. وهو الشبه والمثل، و (أَنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ) حال من ضمير (فَلاَ تَجْعَلُوا) أي: فلا تجعلوا لله أنداداً والحال أنكم من أهل العلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-4","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا عبادي اعبدوني بقلوبكم بالتوحيد والإيمان، وبجوارحكم بالطاعة والإذعان، وبأرواحكم بالشهود والعيان، فأنا الذي أظهرتكم من العدم- أنتم ومَن كان قبلكم- وأسبلت عليكم سوابغ النعم، الأرض تقلكم والسماء تظلكم، والجهات تكتنفكم، وأنزلت من السماء ماء فأخرجت به أصنافاً مِنَ الثَّمَراتِ رِزْقاً لَكُمْ، فأنتم جوهرة الصدق، تنطوي عليكم أصداف مكوناتي، وأنتم الذين أطلعتكم على أسرار مكنوناتي، فكيف يمكنكم أن تتوجهوا إلى غيري؟ وقد أغنيتكم بلطائف إحساني وبري، أنعمت عليكم أولاً بالإيجاد، وثانياً بتوالي الإمداد، خصصتكم بنور العقل والفهم، وأشرقت عليكم نبذة من أنوار القِدم، فبي عرفتموني، وبقدرتي عبدتموني، فلا شريك معي ولا ظهير، ولا احتياج إلى معين ولا وزير.","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-5","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"الإشارة: توجه الخطاب إلى العارفين الكاملين فى الإنسانية الذين يعبدون الله تعظيماً لحق الربوبية، وقياماً بوظائف العبودية، وفيهم قال صاحب العينية(1):","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-6","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"هُم الناسُ فالزمْ إنْ عَرفْتَ جَنَابَهُمْ ... فَفِيهِم لِضُرِّ العالمين منافع","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-7","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"وقال قبل ذلك:","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-8","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"همُ الْقَصْدُ للملهوفِ والكنزُ والرجَا ... وَمِنهُمْ يَنَالُ الصَّبُّ مَا هُوَ طامعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-9","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"بهِم يَهْتَدي للعينِ مَن ضَلَّ فِي العَمَى ... بهِم يُجذَبُ العُشَّاقُ، والرَّبْعُ شاسعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-10","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"هُمُ القَصْدُ والمطلوبُ والسؤلُ والمنَى ... واسْمُهُم لِلصَّبِّ فِي الحبِّ شَافعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-11","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"فعبادة العارفين: بالله ومن الله وإلى الله، وعبادة الجاهلين: بأنفسهم ومن أنفسهم ولأنفسهم، عبادة العارفين حمد وشكر، وعبادة الغافلين اقتضاء حظ وأجر، عبادة العارفين قلبية باطنية، وعبادة الغافلين حسية ظاهرية، يا أيها الناس المخصوصون بالأنس والقرب دوموا على عبادة القريب، ومشاهدة الحبيب، فقد رَفَعْتُ بيني وبينكم الحجب والأستار، وأشهدتكم عجائب الألطاف والأسرار، أبرزتكم إلى الوجود، وأدخلتكم من باب الكرم والجود، ومنحتكم بفضلي غاية الشهود، لعلكم تتقون الإنكار والجحود، وتعرفونني في كل شاهد ومشهود.","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-12","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"فقد جعلت أرض نفوسكم مهادا لعلوم الشريعة، وسماء قلوبكم سقفاً لأسرار الحقيقة، وأنزلت من سماء الملكوت ماء غيبياً تحيا به أرض النفوس، وتهتز بواردات حضرة القدوس، فتخرج من ثمرات العلوم اللدنية، والأسرار الربانية، والأحوال المرضية، ما تتقوت به عائلة المستمعين، وتنتعش به أسرار السائرين، فلا تشهدوا معي غيري، ولا تميلوا لغير إحساني وبري، فقد علمتم أني منفرد بالوجود، ومختص بالكرم والجود، فكيف يرجى غيري وأنا ما قطعت الإحسان؟! وكيف يلتفت إلى ما سواي وأنا بذلت عادة الأمتنان؟! مني كان الإيجاد، وعليَّ دوام الإمداد، فثقوا بي كفيلاً، واتخذوني وكيلاً، أعطكم عطاء جزيلاً، وأمنحكم فخراً جليلاً.","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-21-22-13","r":"q2-21-22","title":"2:21–22 · Worship, creation and sustaining providence","text":"ولما أمر عباده بعبادته وتوحيده، أمرهم بتصديق كلامه والإيمان برسوله، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-21-22-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-21-22-s1","r":"q2-21-22","title":"Worship and the hope of taqwā","text":"I say: the clause expressing hope ( جملة الترجّي ) is circumstantial ( حال ), relating to the plural subject-marker in “worship” ( اعبدوا ). That is: worship your Lord, hoping to join the ranks of those mindful of God, who win guidance and prosperity and deserve nearness to God Most High. He thereby indicates that taqwā is the utmost degree of the wayfarers: renouncing everything other than God Most High in turning to God Most High. “Who made” ( الذي جعل ) qualifies “Lord.” “So do not set up” ( فلا تجعلوا ) is coordinated with “worship” if understood as a prohibition; alternatively, its verb is in the subjunctive through an implicit an ( أن ), as the response to that command. “Rivals” ( الأنداد ) is the plural of nidd , with a kasra on the nūn: a likeness or equal. “When you know” ( وأنتم تعلمون ) is a circumstantial clause relating to the subject of “do not set up”: do not set up rivals to God while you are people possessed of knowledge.","anchor":"en-q2-21-22-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-21-22-s2","r":"q2-21-22","title":"Creation, reason and the succession of divine gifts","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “My servants, worship Me with your hearts through the affirmation of unity and faith; with your limbs through obedience and submission; and with your spirits through witnessing and direct vision. I am He who brought you forth from nonexistence—you and those before you—and spread over you abundant favours. Earth bears you, sky shelters you, and the directions surround you. I sent down water from the sky and brought forth through it various fruits as provision for you. “You are the precious pearl of truth, enclosed within the shells of My created things; you are those to whom I have disclosed the mysteries of My hidden things. How, then, can you turn towards another, when I have enriched you through the subtleties of My beneficence and kindness? I favoured you first by bringing you into existence ( الإيجاد ), and then by the succession of sustaining gifts ( الإمداد ). I singled you out with the light of intellect and understanding, and shone upon you a glimmer from the lights of beginninglessness ( القِدَم ). Through Me you knew Me, and by My power you worshipped Me. There is no partner or supporter beside Me, and no need of helper or minister.”","anchor":"en-q2-21-22-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-21-22-s3","r":"q2-21-22","title":"Worship through God, from God and towards God","text":"The address is directed to the gnostics perfected in humanity, who worship God out of magnification of the right of lordship and fulfilment of the duties of servanthood. Concerning them the author of the ʿAyn-rhymed ode says: They are the people: hold to their side, if you recognize them; within them lie remedies for the world’s afflictions. Before that he says: They are the destination of the distressed, the treasure and the hope; from them the ardent lover gains what he desires. Through them the one lost in blindness finds the very Source; through them lovers are drawn, though the dwelling lies far away. They are the aim, the object sought, the petition and the wish; their name intercedes for the ardent one in love. [B024] The worship of the gnostics is through God, from God and towards God; the worship of the ignorant is through themselves, from themselves and for themselves. The gnostics’ worship is praise and thanksgiving; the heedless worship in pursuit of a personal share and reward. The gnostics’ worship is inward, of the heart; that of the heedless is sensible and outward. “O people singled out for intimacy and nearness, persevere in worshipping the Near One and witnessing the Beloved. I have lifted the veils and curtains between Me and you and made you witness wondrous subtleties and mysteries. I brought you forth into existence, admitted you through the gate of generosity and open-handedness, and granted you, by My bounty, the utmost witnessing, so that you might guard against denial and rejection and recognize Me in every witness and everything witnessed. “I have made the earth of your souls a resting-place for the sciences of the Sacred Law, and the sky of your hearts a roof for the mysteries of Reality. From the sky of malakūt I have sent down unseen water through which the earth of souls comes alive and stirs with the influxes of the Presence of the All-Holy. It yields fruits of divinely bestowed sciences, lordly mysteries and approved states, nourishing the household of those who listen and reviving the innermost secrets of the wayfarers. “So witness no other alongside Me, and incline towards no beneficence or kindness but Mine. You know that I alone possess existence, and that generosity and open-handedness belong especially to Me. How can another be hoped in when I have not cut off beneficence? How can attention turn to what is other than Me when I have freely bestowed the customary gifts of grace? From Me came bringing-into-existence, and upon Me rests the continuance of sustaining influx. Trust in Me as guarantor and take Me as your trustee: I shall give you richly and grant you glorious distinction.”","anchor":"en-q2-21-22-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-21-22-s4","r":"q2-21-22","title":"","text":"Having commanded His servants to worship Him and affirm His oneness, He commands them to affirm His speech and believe in His Messenger, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-21-22-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-23-25","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful 2:23–25","anchor":"unit-q2-23-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-1","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِي رَيْبٍ مِمَّا نَزَّلْنا عَلى عَبْدِنا فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِنْ مِثْلِهِ وَادْعُوا شُهَداءَكُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (23) فَإِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوا وَلَنْ تَفْعَلُوا فَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجارَةُ أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكافِرِينَ (24) وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ أَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ كُلَّما رُزِقُوا مِنْها مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِزْقاً قالُوا هذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَأُتُوا بِهِ مُتَشابِهاً وَلَهُمْ فِيها أَزْواجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ وَهُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (25)","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-2","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"فإن قلت: الريب في القرآن قد وقع من الكفار قطعاً، فكيف عبّر بإن الدالة على الشك والتردد؟","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-3","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"قلت: (إن) جازمة للفظ الشرط أو محله، موضوعة للشك في الشرط. و «إذا» لا تجزم في اللفظ، وتدل على الجزم في المعنى، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-4","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"أنا إنْ شَككتُ وجدْتُموني جَازِماً ... وإذا جَزمتُ فإنني لَمْ أجزمِ","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-5","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"فإن قلت: الريب في القرآن قد وقع من الكفار قطعاً، فكيف عبر بإن الدالة على الشك والتردد؟ قلت: لما كان ريبهم واقعاً في غير محله- إذ لو تأملوا أدنى تأمل لزال ريبهم لوضوح الأمر وسطوع البرهان- كان ريبهم كأنه مشكوك فيه ومتردد في وقوعه، و (الشهداء) جمع شهيد بمعنى الحاضر، أو القائم بالشهادة، أو الناصر، أُطْلِقَ على الأصنام لأنهم يزعمون أنها تشهد لهم، ومعنى (دون) : أدنى مكان من الشيء، ثم استعير للرُّتَب فقيل: زيد دون عمرو أي: في الشرف، ثم اتسع فيه فاستعير لكل تجاوزِ حدّ إلى حد، وتخطّي أمرٍ إلى آخر.","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-6","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ يا معشر الكفار فِي شك مِمَّا نَزَّلْنا عَلى محمد عَبْدِنا ورسولنا المختار لِسِرّ وحينا، فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِنْ جنسه في البلاغة والفصاحة، مشتملة على علوم وأسرار ومغيبات كما اشتمل عليه كتابي، وَادْعُوا من استطعتم ممن تنتصرون به على ذلك الإتيان، مِن آلهتكم التي تزعمون أنها تشهد لكم يوم القيامة، أو من حضركم من البلغاء والفصحاء ممن تنتصرون به مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في أنها تنفعكم. فَإِنْ لَمْ تقدروا أن تَفْعَلُوا ذلك وَلَنْ تقدروا ابداً فأسلموا وأقرُّوا بالحق، فَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجارَةُ أي: حجارة الكبريت، فَهُمَا حطبُها ووقودها أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكافِرِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-7","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"وَبَشِّرِ يا محمد ويا مَن يصلح منه التبشير الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بالله ورسولِه، وَعَمِلُوا ما كلفوا به من الأعمال الصَّالِحاتِ أَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ أي: من تحت قصورها، وهي أنهار من ماء، وأنهار من عسل، وأنهار من لبن، وأنهار من خمر لذة للشاربين. كُلَّما رُزِقُوا مِنْها مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِزْقاً أي: صنفاً، قالُوا هذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنا مِنْ قَبْلُ في دار الدنيا، فإن الطباع تميل إلى المألوف، فالصفة متفقة والطعم مختلف. أو في الجنة، قيل: هذا لما روى عنه صلى الله عليه وسلّم أنه قال: «والذي نفسُ محمدٍ بيدِه إنَّ الرجلَ مِنْ أهلِ الجنةِ لَيتَناولُ الثمرة لِيأكلهَا فما هي واصِلةٌ إلى جَوفِه حتى يبدل الله تعالى مكانها مِثلَها» ، فلعلهم إذا رأوها على الهيئة الأولى قالوا","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-8","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"ذلك، لفرط استغرابهم، وتبجحهم بما وجدوا من التفاوت العظيم في اللذة والتشابه البليغ في الصورة، وَلَهُمْ فِيها أَزْواجٌ أي: حور مُطَهَّرَةٌ من الحيض، وسائر الأدناس، ومن الأخلاق المذمومة، والشيم الذميمة، وَهُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ فإن النعيم إذا كان يعقُبه الفناء تنغّص على صاحبه، كما قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-9","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"لا خيرَ في العيش مادامت مُنغَّصَةً ... لَذاتُه بادِّكارِ الموتِ والهَرَمِ","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-10","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"الإشارة: وإن كنتم يا معشر العوام في شك مما خصصنا به ولينا من الأنوار، وما أنزلنا على قلبه من المعارف والأسرار، وما ظهر عليه من البهجة والأنوار، وما اهتدى على يديه من الصالحين والأبرار، فأتوا أنتم بشئ من ذلك، وانتصروا بما قدرتم من دون الله إن كنتم صادقين في المعارضة. قال القشيري: وكما أن كيد الكافرين يَضْمَحِلُّ في مقابلة معجزات الرسول، فكذلك دعاوى المُلْبِسين تتلاشى عند ظهور أنوار الصديقين. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-11","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"فإن لم تفعلوا ما ذكرنا من المعارضة، ولن تقدروا على ذلك أبداً، فأَذْعنوا، واخْضعوا، واتقوا نار القطيعة والحظوظ، والطمع والهلع، التي مادتها النفوس والفلوس إذ بهما هلك مَن هلك وفاز مَن فاز، أُعدت تلك النار للمنكرين الخصوصية، الجاحدين لوجود التربية النبوية.","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-12","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"وبَشِّر المصدقين بوجود الخصوصية، المنقادين لأهلها، أن لهم جنات المعارف في الدنيا، وجنات الزخارف في الآخرة، تجري من تحت قلوب أهلها أنوار العلوم والمعارف، فإذا كشف لهم يوم القيامة عن أسرار ذاته، قالوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-13","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"هذا الذي عرفناه من قبل في دار الدنيا، إذ الوجود واحد والمعرفة متفاوتة، وأتُوا بأرزاق المعارف متشابهة لأن مَنْ عَرَفه في الدنيا عرفه في الآخرة، ومَن أنكره هنا أنكره يوم القيامة، إلا في وقت مخصوص على وجه مخصوص، ولهم في جنات المعارف عرائس المعارف والكشوفات، مطهرات من أدناس الحس وعبث الهوى والشهوات، وهم بعد تمكنهم من شهود الذات، خالدون في عُشّ الحضرة، فيها يسكنون وإليها يأوون.","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-14","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"وقال القشيري: كما أن أهل الجنة يجدد لهم النعيم في وقت، فالثاني عندهم على ما يظنون كالأول، فإذا ذاقوه وجدوه غير ما تقدم، كذلك أهل الحقائق: أحوالهم في الزيادة أبداً، فإذا رقي أحدهم عن محله، توهم أن الذي سيلقاه في هذا النَّفس مثل ما تقدم، فإذا ذاقه وجده فوق ذلك بأضعاف، كما قال قائلهم:","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-15","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"مازلت أنزلُ مِنْ وِدادِكَ مَنْزِلاً ... تَتحَيرُ الألبابُ عِندَ نُزُولهِ(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-23-25-16","r":"q2-23-25","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","text":"ولما ضرب الله الأمثال في القرآن للمنافقين وغيرهم تكلم في ذلك بعض الكفار والملحدين، بينّ الحق تعالى وجه ذلك فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-23-25-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-23-25-s1","r":"q2-23-25","title":"Conditional doubt and the force of the challenge","text":"Should you ask, “The unbelievers’ doubt concerning the Qurʾān certainly occurred; why, then, is it expressed through in ( إن ), which indicates doubt and uncertainty?”—I say: in makes the conditional verb jussive, either in its expressed inflection or in its grammatical position ( جازمة للفظ الشرط أو محله ), and is assigned to uncertainty about the condition. Idhā ( إذا ), by contrast, does not make the verb jussive in its expressed inflection, but indicates certainty in meaning. Hence the saying: When I doubt with in , you find me making jussive; when I am certain with idhā , I do not make jussive. Should you ask, “The unbelievers’ doubt concerning the Qurʾān certainly occurred; why, then, use in , which indicates doubt and uncertainty?”—I say: their doubt was misplaced. Had they reflected in the least, it would have disappeared, so clear is the matter and so radiant the proof. Their doubt is therefore treated as though its occurrence were itself doubtful and uncertain. [B025] Shuhadāʾ ( الشهداء ) is the plural of shahīd , meaning one present, one who bears witness, or a supporter. It is applied to the idols because their worshippers claim that they testify for them. Dūn ( دون ) originally denotes a place nearer than another thing. It was then borrowed for ranks: “Zayd is below ʿAmr,” that is, in honour. Its use was subsequently extended to any passing from one limit to another or crossing from one affair to another. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-02] ]","anchor":"en-q2-23-25-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-23-25-s2","r":"q2-23-25","title":"A challenge beyond their power","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: if you unbelievers doubt what We have sent down upon Muḥammad—Our servant and Messenger, chosen to receive the mystery of Our revelation—then bring a sūrah of its kind in eloquence and lucid expression, containing sciences, mysteries and disclosures of the unseen such as My Book contains. Summon everyone whose support you can obtain in producing it: the gods that you claim will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection, or the eloquent and accomplished speakers present among you whose assistance you seek apart from God, if you are truthful in claiming that they can benefit you. If you cannot do this—and you never will—then submit and acknowledge the truth. Guard yourselves against the Fire whose fuel is people and stones, meaning sulphur stones: these two are its firewood and fuel. It has been prepared for the unbelievers.","anchor":"en-q2-23-25-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-23-25-s3","r":"q2-23-25","title":"The renewed delight of Paradise","text":"Muḥammad—and anyone fit to convey good tidings—give good tidings to those who believe in God and His Messenger and perform the righteous works required of them: theirs are gardens beneath which rivers flow, that is, beneath their palaces. These are rivers of water, honey, milk, and wine delightful to those who drink it. Whenever they are provided with a kind of fruit from them, they say, “This is what we were provided with before,” in the earthly abode. Natural dispositions incline to the familiar: the appearance agrees, while the taste differs. Alternatively, “before” refers to an earlier provision in Paradise. This is explained by the report from the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace: “By Him in whose hand is Muḥammad’s soul, a man in Paradise takes a fruit to eat, and before it has reached his stomach God Most High replaces it with another like it.” Perhaps, then, on seeing it in its former shape, they say this in astonishment and delight at the immense difference in flavour alongside the close resemblance of appearance. There they have spouses—that is, houris—purified of menstruation and every other defilement, and of blameworthy dispositions and ignoble traits. There they abide for ever, since a delight followed by extinction is embittered for its possessor. As the poet says: There is no good in life while its pleasures are embittered by remembering death and decrepit age.","anchor":"en-q2-23-25-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-23-25-s4","r":"q2-23-25","title":"The challenge addressed to those who deny spiritual election","text":"If you ordinary people doubt the lights with which We have specially favoured Our friend, the forms of knowledge and mysteries We have sent down upon his heart, the splendour and lights manifested upon him, and the righteous and good who have found guidance at his hands, then produce something of this yourselves. Seek all the support you can apart from God, if you are truthful in your opposition. Al-Qushayrī says: “Just as the unbelievers’ plotting dwindles away before the Messenger’s miracles, so the claims of pretenders vanish when the lights of the utterly truthful appear.” End of quotation. If you do not accomplish the opposition We have mentioned—and you will never be able to do so—then yield and submit. Guard yourselves against the fire of severance, egoic shares, covetousness and anxious grasping, whose substance is souls and money ( النفوس والفلوس ). Through these two those who perish have perished, and those who triumph have triumphed. That fire is prepared for those who deny special election and reject the existence of Prophetic spiritual formation ( التربية النبوية ). Give good tidings to those who affirm the existence of special election and submit to its people: theirs are gardens of gnosis in this world and gardens of adornment in the next. Beneath their inhabitants’ hearts flow the lights of sciences and forms of knowledge. When the mysteries of His Essence are unveiled to them on the Day of Resurrection, they say, “This is what we knew before in the earthly abode,” for existence ( الوجود ) is one, while knowledge of it differs in degree. They are given resembling provisions of gnosis, because one who knew Him here knows Him in the Hereafter; one who denied Him here denies Him on the Day of Resurrection, except at a particular time and in a particular manner. [B026] In the gardens of gnosis they have bridal forms of knowledge and unveiling, purified of the defilements of sense perception and the frivolity of caprice and desires. Once firmly established in witnessing the Essence, they abide in the nest of the Presence: there they dwell, and to it they take refuge. Al-Qushayrī says: “Just as the people of Paradise receive renewed delight at each moment, imagining the second to be like the first but, on tasting it, finding it unlike what preceded, so the states of the people of realities continually increase. When one rises beyond his station, he imagines that what he will meet in this breath is like what preceded; when he tastes it, he finds it many times greater.” As one of them says: Ever I alight at a dwelling-place of Your love whose approach leaves minds bewildered.","anchor":"en-q2-23-25-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-23-25-s5","r":"q2-23-25","title":"","text":"When God set forth parables in the Qurʾān concerning the hypocrites and others, some unbelievers and deniers spoke against them. The Real Most High therefore explained their purpose, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-23-25-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-26-27","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom 2:26–27","anchor":"unit-q2-26-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-1","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَسْتَحْيِي أَنْ يَضْرِبَ مَثَلاً ما بَعُوضَةً فَما فَوْقَها فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا فَيَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فَيَقُولُونَ ماذا أَرادَ اللَّهُ بِهذا مَثَلاً يُضِلُّ بِهِ كَثِيراً وَيَهْدِي بِهِ كَثِيراً وَما يُضِلُّ بِهِ إِلاَّ الْفاسِقِينَ (26) الَّذِينَ يَنْقُضُونَ عَهْدَ اللَّهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مِيثاقِهِ وَيَقْطَعُونَ ما أَمَرَ اللَّهُ بِهِ أَنْ يُوصَلَ وَيُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ أُولئِكَ هُمُ الْخاسِرُونَ (27)","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-2","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"قلت: الحياء: خُلُق كريم يمنع صاحبه من ارتكاب ما يعاب به، وفي الحديث: «إنَّ الله حَيِيٌ كَريم» ، و (مثلاً) مفعول، و (ما) نكرة، صفته، و (بعوضة) بدل، والبعوضة: الذباب. وفي الحديث: «لوْ كَانَتِ الدُّنيَا تُسَاوِي عندَ الله جَنَاحَ بعُوضَةٍ مَا سَقَى الكافرَ منها جَرْعَة ماءٍ» ، وقيل: صِغَار البَقِّ، أي: إن الله لا يترك أن يضرب مثلاً- أيّ مثل كان- بعوضة فما فوقها. أو (بعوضة) مفعول أول، و (مثلاً) مفعول ثانٍ، من باب جعل، و (ماذا) إما مبتدأ وخبرِ، على أن (ذا) موصولة، أو مفعولة بأراد على أنها مركبة، و (مثلاً) حال أو تمييز. والفسق: الخروج، يقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-3","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"فسقت الرطبة إذا خرجت عن قشرها.","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-4","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يترك ترك المستحيي أَنْ يَضْرِبَ مَثَلًا بالخسيس والكبير كالذباب والعنكبوت وغير ذلك. فأما المؤمنون فيتيقَّنُون أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ، وحكمته: إبراز المعاني اللطيفة في قوالب المحسوسات ليسهل الفهم، وأما الكفار فيعترضون ويقولون: مَاذَا أَرادَ اللَّهُ بهذه الأمثال؟ فإن الله منزه عن ضرب الأمثال بهذه الأشياء الخسيسة، قال الله تعالى فِى الرد عليهم: أراد بهذا إضلال قوم بسبب إنكارها، وهداية آخرين بسبب الإيمان بها، وَما يُضِلُّ بذلك المثل إلا الخارجين عن طاعته، الَّذِينَ نقضوا العهد الذي أُخذ عليهم في عالم الذَّرِّ، أو مطلق العهد، وَيَقْطَعُونَ مَا أَمَرَ اللَّهُ بِهِ أَنْ يُوصَلَ من الأنبياء والرسل والأرحام وغيرها، وَيُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ بالمعاصي والتعويق عن الإيمان، أُولئِكَ هُمُ الْخاسِرُونَ الكاملون في الخسران، نعوذ بالله من الخذلان.","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-5","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"الإشارة: إن الله لا يترك أن يظهر مثلاً من أنوار قدسه بارزاً بقدرته، مرتدياً برداء حكمته، ملتبساً بأسرار ذاته، مَكسُوّاً بأنوار صفاته من الذرة إلى مالا نهاية له، فالمتجلِّي في النملة هو المتجلي في الفيلة، فأما الذين صَدَّقُوا بتجلي الذات في أنوار الصفات، فيقولون: إنه الحق فائضٌ من نور الربوبية، محتجباً برداء الكبرياء وسبحات الألوهية. وأما الجاحدون لظهور نور ذات الربوبية فينكرونه في حال ظهوره، ويقولون: ماذا أراد الله بهذه العوالم الظاهرة؟ فيقول الحق تعالى: أردت ظهور قدرتي وعجائب حكمتي، ليظهر سر ربوبيتي في مظاهر عبوديتي.","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-6","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"قال الشيخ أبو الحسن رضى الله عنه: «العبودية جوهرة أظهر بها الربوبية» وقيل لأبي الحسن النُّورِي: ما هذه الأماكن والمخلوقات الظاهرة؟ فقال: عز ظاهر وملك قاهر، ومخلوقات ظاهرة به، وصادرة عنه، لا هي متصلة به ولا منفصلة عنه، فرغ من الأشياء ولم تفرغ منه، لأنها تحتاج إليه وهو لا يحتاج إليها. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-7","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"فأراد الله بظهور هذا الكون أن يضل به قوماً فيقفون مع ظاهر غرَّتِه، ويهدي به قوماً فينفذون إلى باطن عبرته. وما يضل به إلا الفاسقين الخارجين عن دائرة الشهود، المنكرين لتجليات الملك المعبود، الذين ينقضون عهد الله، وهو معرفة الروح التي حصلت لها وهي في عالم الذر، ويقطعونَ ما أمر اللهُ به أن يوصل من الشيوخ العارفين، الذين أَهَّلَهُمَ الله للتربية والترقية، وهم لا ينقطعون ما دامت المِلَّةُ المحمدية، ويفسدون في الأرض بالإنكار والتعويق عن طريق الخصوص، بتضييعهم الأصولَ، وهي صحبة العارفين، والتأدب لهم، والتعظيم لحرمتهم. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-26-27-8","r":"q2-26-27","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","text":"ثم عجّب الحقّ تعالى خلقه من خفائه بعد شدة ظهوره، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-26-27-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-26-27-s1","r":"q2-26-27","title":"Modesty, the parable and transgression","text":"I say: modesty ( الحياء ) is a noble disposition that prevents its possessor from committing something for which he would be reproached. The hadith says, “God is modest and generous.” Mathalan ( مثلاً ) is an object ( مفعول ); mā ( ما ) is an indefinite word qualifying it; and baʿūḍatan ( بعوضة ) is an apposition ( بدل ). Baʿūḍa is a fly. The hadith says, “Were this world worth the wing of a gnat in God’s sight, He would not give an unbeliever a draught of water from it.” It is also said to mean the smallest biting insects. Thus: God does not refrain from setting forth a parable—whatever sort it may be—of a gnat or anything beyond it. [B027] Alternatively, baʿūḍatan is the first object and mathalan the second, on the pattern of jaʿala , “to make.” Mādhā ( ماذا ) is either a subject and predicate, with dhā a relative expression, or the object of “intends,” when the two form a compound interrogative. Mathalan is a circumstantial accusative or an accusative of specification ( حال أو تمييز ). Transgression ( الفسق ) means going out: one says, “The ripe date fasaqat ,” when it comes out of its skin.","anchor":"en-q2-26-27-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-26-27-s2","r":"q2-26-27","title":"The purpose of sensible parables","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: God does not refrain, as a modest person might, from setting forth a parable through something lowly or something great—a fly, a spider, or anything else. Believers are certain that it is the truth from their Lord. Its wisdom lies in displaying subtle meanings in sensible forms so that understanding becomes easy. Unbelievers, however, object: “What does God intend by these parables? God is too exalted to strike parables through such lowly things.” In answer, God Most High says: He intends thereby to lead one people astray through their rejection, and to guide others through their faith in them. Through such a parable He leads astray only those who depart from obedience to Him: those who break the covenant taken from them in the world of the primordial particles ( عالم الذر ), or covenant in its unrestricted sense; who sever what God commanded to be joined—prophets, messengers, ties of kinship and other bonds—and corrupt the earth through disobedience and obstructing faith. These are the losers, complete in their loss. We seek refuge in God from abandonment.","anchor":"en-q2-26-27-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-26-27-s3","r":"q2-26-27","title":"Self-disclosure in the smallest and greatest things","text":"God does not refrain from manifesting a similitude of the lights of His holiness, brought forth by His power, clad in the robe of His wisdom, invested with the mysteries of His Essence and clothed in the lights of His attributes—from the smallest particle to that which has no limit. He who discloses Himself in the ant is He who discloses Himself in the elephant. Those who affirm the Essence’s self-disclosure in the lights of the attributes say: it is the Real, flowing forth from the light of lordship, veiled in the robe of majesty and the splendours of divinity. Those who deny the manifestation of the light of the Essence of lordship reject it in its manifestation and say, “What did God intend by these manifest worlds?” The Real Most High replies: “I intended the manifestation of My power and the wonders of My wisdom, so that the mystery of My lordship might appear in the loci of My servanthood.” Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan, God be pleased with him, said: “Servanthood is a jewel through which He manifested lordship.” Abū al-Ḥasan al-Nūrī was asked, “What are these places and manifest creatures?” He replied: “Manifest might, overpowering dominion, and creatures made manifest through Him and issuing from Him: neither connected to Him nor separated from Him. He has finished with things, but they have not finished with Him, for they need Him while He does not need them.” End of quotation. By manifesting this cosmos, God intends that one people be led astray through it, stopping at its outward allure, and another be guided through it, penetrating to the inward lesson it offers. None is led astray through it except those who transgress beyond the circle of witnessing and deny the self-disclosures of the worshipped King; those who break God’s covenant, namely the spirit’s knowledge acquired while it was in the world of the primordial particles; and those who sever the bond God commanded to be maintained with the knowing shaykhs whom He qualified for spiritual formation and elevation. Such shaykhs will not cease to exist as long as the Muḥammadan religion remains. These people corrupt the earth through denial and obstruction of the path of the elect, neglecting its foundations: companionship with the gnostics, observing proper courtesy towards them, and honouring their sanctity. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q2-26-27-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-26-27-s4","r":"q2-26-27","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then calls His creatures to wonder at His hiddenness despite His overwhelming manifestation, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-26-27-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-28","r":"q2-28","title":"2:28 · Life, death and return","text":"2:28 · Life, death and return 2:28","anchor":"unit-q2-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-28-1","r":"q2-28","title":"2:28 · Life, death and return","text":"كَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَكُنْتُمْ أَمْواتاً فَأَحْياكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيكُمْ ثُمَّ إِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ (28)","anchor":"ar-q2-28-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-28-2","r":"q2-28","title":"2:28 · Life, death and return","text":"قلت: (كيف) حال لأنها وقعت قبل كلام تام.","anchor":"ar-q2-28-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-28-3","r":"q2-28","title":"2:28 · Life, death and return","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: كَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وتجحدون نعمه المتوالية، وَالحالة أنكم كُنْتُمْ أَمْواتاً نطفاً في الأرحام، فَأَحْياكُمْ بنفخ الروح في أجسادكم، ثُمَّ يُمِيتُكُمْ عند انقضاء آجالكم، ثُمَّ يُحْيِيكُمْ عند البعث لحسابكم، ثم يسكنكم دار القرار، إمّا إلى الجنة وإمّا إلى النار. فهذه الآثار دالّة على باهر قدرته وتمام حكمته، فقد وضح الحق وظهر، فَمَنْ شاءَ فَلْيُؤْمِنْ وَمَنْ شاءَ فَلْيَكْفُرْ.","anchor":"ar-q2-28-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-28-4","r":"q2-28","title":"2:28 · Life, death and return","text":"الإشارة: كيف تنكرون ظهور نور الحق في الأكوان، وتبعدون عن حضرة الشهود والعيان، وقد كنتم أمواتاً بالغفلة وغم الحجاب، فأحياكم باليقظة والإياب، ثم يميتكم بالفناء عن شهود ما سواه، ثم يحييكم بالرجوع إلى شهود أثره بالله، ثم إليه ترجعون في كل شيء لشهود نوره في كل شيء، وقبل كل شيء، وبعد كل شيء، وعند كل شيء «كان الله ولا شيء معه، وهو الآن على ما عليه كان» .","anchor":"ar-q2-28-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-28-5","r":"q2-28","title":"2:28 · Life, death and return","text":"ولمَّا ذكر نعمة الإيجاد أتبعها بنعمة الإمداد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-28-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-28-s1","r":"q2-28","title":"The circumstantial force of “how”","text":"I say: “How” ( كيف ) has the force of a circumstantial expression ( حال ), because it precedes a complete statement.","anchor":"en-q2-28-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-28-s2","r":"q2-28","title":"The successive gifts of life","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: how can you disbelieve in God and deny His successive blessings, when you were lifeless—drops in the wombs—and He gave you life by breathing the spirit into your bodies? Then He causes you to die when your appointed terms expire; then He gives you life at the resurrection for your reckoning. Thereafter He settles you in the enduring abode, either Paradise or the Fire. These effects indicate His dazzling power and perfect wisdom. The truth has become clear and manifest: “Whoever wills, let him believe; and whoever wills, let him disbelieve” [18:29].","anchor":"en-q2-28-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-28-s3","r":"q2-28","title":"Awakening, effacement and renewed witnessing","text":"How can you deny the manifestation of the Real’s light in created things and remain distant from the presence of witnessing and direct vision, when you were dead through heedlessness and the gloom of the veil, and He gave you life through awakening and return? Then He causes you to die through effacement from witnessing anything other than Him; then He gives you life through returning, by God, to witness His effect. Then to Him you return in everything, witnessing His light in everything, before everything, after everything and with everything: “God was, and nothing was with Him; and He is now as He was.” [B028]","anchor":"en-q2-28-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-28-s4","r":"q2-28","title":"","text":"After mentioning the blessing of bringing into existence ( الإيجاد ), He follows it with the blessing of sustaining provision ( الإمداد ), saying:","anchor":"en-q2-28-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-29","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations 2:29","anchor":"unit-q2-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-1","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"هُوَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ لَكُمْ ما فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعاً ثُمَّ اسْتَوى إِلَى السَّماءِ فَسَوَّاهُنَّ سَبْعَ سَماواتٍ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (29)","anchor":"ar-q2-29-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-2","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"قلت: جَمِيعاً حال مؤكدة من ما، وثُمَّ للترتيب الذكري لا الخارجي(1) لأن دحو الأرض مؤخر عن خلق السماء، إلا أن يكون العطف على معنى الجملة، والتقدير: هُوَ الذى خَلَقَ لَكُمْ الأرض مشتملة على جميع منافعكم، ثم استوى إلى السماء فخلقهن سبعاً، ثم دحا الأرض وبسطها.","anchor":"ar-q2-29-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-3","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"والتسوية: خلق الأشياء سالمة من العوج والخلل، و (سبع) : بدل من الضمير، أو بيان له، وجملة وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ تعليل لِما قبله. أي: ولكونه عالماً بكنه الأشياء كلها خلق ما خلق على هذا النمط الأكمل والوجه الأنفع.","anchor":"ar-q2-29-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-4","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله على لسان الواسطة: هُوَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ لأجلكم ما استقر فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعاً تنتفعون به في الظاهر قوتاً لأشباحكم، ودواء لأبدانكم، ومتعة لنفوسكم، وتنتفعون به في الباطن بالتفكر والاعتبار، وزيادة في إيمانكم وقوة لإيقانكم، ثم قصد إِلَى السَّماءِ قصد إرادة، فخلقهن سَبْعَ سَماواتٍ مستوية تامة، ليس فيها تفاوت ولا خلل، تظلكم بجرمها، وتضيء عليكم بشمسها وقمرها وكواكبها، وقد أحاط علمه بالأشياء كلها، فلذلك خلقها على هذا النمط الغريب والإتقان العجيب.","anchor":"ar-q2-29-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-5","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"الإشارة: يا عبادي خلقتُ الأشياء كُلَّها من أجلكم، الأرض تُقلكم، والسماء تُظلكم، والجهات تَكْتَنِفُكُمْ والحيوانات تخدُمكم، والنباتات تنفعكم، وخلقتكم من أجلي، فكيف تميلون إلى غيري، وتنسَوْن إحساني وبرِّي؟!! الأشياء كلها عبيدكم وأنتم عبيد الحضرة، «أنت مع الأكوان ما لم تشهد المكون، فإذا شهدت المكون كانت الأكوان معك» .","anchor":"ar-q2-29-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-6","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"وفي بعض الكتب المنزلة يقول الله تعالى: (يا عبدي إنما منحتك صفاتي لتعرفني بها، فإن ادعيتها لنفسك سلبتُك الولاية، ولم أسلبك صفاتي، يا عبدي: أنت صفتي وأنا صفتك، فارجع إليَّ أرجع إليك، يا عبدي: فيك للعلوم باب مفتاحه أنا، وفيك للجهل باب مفتاحه أنت، فاقصد أيّ البابين شئت، يا عبدي: قربي منك بقدر بعدك عن نفسك وبعدي عنك بقدر قربك من نفسك، فقد عرفتك الطريق، فاترك نفسك تصل إليَّ في خطرة واحدة، يا عبدي: كل ما جمعك علي فهو مني، وكل ما فرقك عني فهو منك، فجاهد نفسك تصل إليّ، وإني لغني عن العالمين، يا عبدي: إن منحتني نفسك رددتها إليك راضية مرضية، وإن تركتها عندك فهي أعظم بلية، فهي أعدى الأعادي إليك فجاهدها تَعُدْ بالفوائد إليك) .","anchor":"ar-q2-29-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-7","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"وفي بعض الآثار المروية عن الله تعالى: «يا عبدي: أنا بُدُّك اللازم فالزم بُدَّك»(1). ويمكن أن يشار بالأرض إلى أرض العبودية، وبالسماء إلى سماء الحقيقة، وبالسبع سموات إلى سبع مقامات وهي الصبر والشكر والتوكل والرضى والتسليم والمحبة والمعرفة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-29-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-29-8","r":"q2-29","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","text":"ولما ذكر خلق العالم العلوي والسفلي، ذكر كيفية ابتداء من عمَّر العالم السفليَّ من جنس الآدمي، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-29-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-29-s1","r":"q2-29","title":"The order of mention and the order of creation","text":"I say: “all” ( جميعاً ) is an emphatic circumstantial expression ( حال مؤكدة ) referring to “what.” “Then” ( ثم ) indicates order in the account, not necessarily order in external occurrence ( الترتيب الذكري لا الخارجي ), because the spreading of the earth came after the creation of heaven. An alternative is that the coordination refers to the sentence’s sense, giving the reconstruction: He it is who created the earth for you, containing all your benefits; then He turned to heaven and created the seven; then He spread and extended the earth. Fashioning or setting in order ( التسوية ) means creating things free from crookedness and defect. “Seven” ( سبع ) is an apposition to the pronoun or an explanatory specification of it ( بدل أو بيان ). “He knows all things” explains what precedes: because He knows the inmost reality of all things, He created what He created according to this most perfect pattern and most beneficial manner.","anchor":"en-q2-29-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-29-s2","r":"q2-29","title":"Outward benefit and inward reflection","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says through the tongue of the intermediary: He created for your sake everything established on earth. Outwardly you benefit from it as sustenance for your bodies, medicine for your physical frames and enjoyment for your souls; inwardly you benefit through reflection and taking heed, an increase of faith and strengthening of certainty. He then directed Himself towards the heaven with the intention of His will and created them as seven heavens, well-formed and complete, without disparity or defect. Their mass overshadows you, and their sun, moon and stars give you light. His knowledge encompasses all things; hence He created them according to this wondrous pattern and marvellous perfection.","anchor":"en-q2-29-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-29-s3","r":"q2-29","title":"Created things serve you; you belong to the Presence","text":"My servants, I created all things for your sake. The earth bears you, heaven overshadows you, the directions encompass you, animals serve you and plants benefit you. I created you for My sake: how, then, can you incline to another and forget My kindness and beneficence? All things are your servants, while you are servants of the Presence. “You are with created things so long as you do not witness their Creator; when you witness the Creator, created things are with you.” In one of the revealed books, God Most High says: “My servant, I only bestowed My attributes upon you so that you might know Me through them. If you claim them for yourself, I deprive you of friendship with Me, though I do not deprive you of My attributes. My servant, you are My attribute, and I am your attribute: return to Me and I return to you. My servant, within you is a gate to the sciences whose key is I; and within you is a gate to ignorance whose key is you. Seek whichever gate you wish. My servant, My nearness to you is in proportion to your distance from yourself, and My distance from you is in proportion to your nearness to yourself. I have shown you the way: leave yourself and reach Me in a single movement of thought. My servant, whatever gathers you unto Me comes from Me; whatever scatters you away from Me comes from you. Strive against yourself and reach Me: I have no need of the worlds. My servant, if you grant Me your soul, I return it to you content and well-pleasing; if you keep it with yourself, it is your greatest affliction and your most hostile enemy. Strive against it, and it returns to you bringing benefits.” [B029] Among the reports transmitted from God Most High is: “My servant, I am your indispensable need: cleave, then, to that without which you cannot be.” The earth may also allude to the earth of servanthood, heaven to the heaven of reality, and the seven heavens to seven stations: patience, thankfulness, reliance, contentment, surrender, love and gnosis ( الصبر والشكر والتوكل والرضى والتسليم والمحبة والمعرفة ). And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-29-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-29-s4","r":"q2-29","title":"","text":"Having mentioned the creation of the upper and lower worlds, He recounts how the human kind that populated the lower world first began, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-29-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-30-33","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge 2:30–33","anchor":"unit-q2-30-33"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-1","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"وَإِذْ قالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلائِكَةِ إِنِّي جاعِلٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً قالُوا أَتَجْعَلُ فِيها مَنْ يُفْسِدُ فِيها وَيَسْفِكُ الدِّماءَ وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ قالَ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ (30) وَعَلَّمَ آدَمَ الْأَسْماءَ كُلَّها ثُمَّ عَرَضَهُمْ عَلَى الْمَلائِكَةِ فَقالَ أَنْبِئُونِي بِأَسْماءِ هؤُلاءِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (31) قالُوا سُبْحانَكَ لا عِلْمَ لَنا إِلاَّ مَا عَلَّمْتَنا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ (32) قالَ يَا آدَمُ أَنْبِئْهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ فَلَمَّا أَنْبَأَهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ قالَ أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَأَعْلَمُ ما تُبْدُونَ وَما كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ (33)","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-2","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"لمّا أراد الله تعالى عمارة الأرض، بعد أن عمر السموات بالملائكة، أخبر الملائكة بما هو صانع من ذلك تنويهاً بآدم وتشريفاً لذريته، وتعليما لعباده أمر المشاورة، فقال لهم: إِنِّي جاعِلٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً يخلفني في أرضي وتنفيذ أحكامي، قالُوا على وجه الاستفهام، أو من الإدلال، إِن كَانَ مِنَ المقربين، بعد أن رأوا الجن قد أفسدوا وسفكوا الدماء: أَتَجْعَلُ فِيها مَنْ يُفْسِدُ فِيها، وشأن الخليفة الإصلاح، وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ، أي: نسبح ملتبسين بحمدك، وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ، أي: نطهر أنفسنا لأجلك، أو ننزهك عما لا يليق بجلال قدسك، فنحن أحق بالخلافة منهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-3","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"قال الحقّ جلّ وعلا: إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ..... ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ فإني أعلم أنه يكون منهم رسل وأنبياء وأولياء، ومن يكون مثلكم أو أعظم منكم، ولما ألقى الخليل في النار ضجت الملائكة وقالت: «يا رب هذا خليلك يحرق بالنار» .","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-4","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"فقال لهم: «إن استغاث بكم فأغيثوه» . فلما رفع همَّتَه عنهم قال الحق تعالى: أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ ما لا تعلمون.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-5","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"ثم وَجَّهَ الحق تعالى استحقاقه للخلافة وهو تشريفه بالعلم، فقال: وَعَلَّمَ آدَمَ الْأَسْماءَ كُلَّها، أي: مسميات الأسماء بأن ألقى في رُوعه ما تحتاج إليه ذريته من اللغات والحروف، وخواص الأشياء ومنافعها، ثم عرض تلك المسميات على الملائكة، إظهاراً لعجزهم، وتشريفاً لآدم بالعلم، فَقالَ: أخبروني بِأَسْماءِ هؤُلاءِ المسميات إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في ادعائكم استحقاق الخلافة، فلما عجزوا عن معرفة تلك الأسماء قالُوا سُبْحانَكَ أي: تنزيهاً لك عن العبث، لا عِلْمَ لَنا إِلَّا مَا عَلَّمْتَنا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَلِيمُ بكل شيء، الْحَكِيمُ لإتقانك كل شيء، وهذا اعتراف منهم بالقصور والعجز، وإشعار بأن سؤالهم كان استفهاماً وطلباً لتفسير ما أشكل عليهم، ولم يكن اعتراضاً.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-6","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"قال الحق جلّ جلاله: يَا آدَمُ أَنْبِئْهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ، وعيِّن لهم اسم كل مسمى، فلما أخبرهم بذلك بحيث قال مثلاً: هذا فرس وهذا جمل، وعين ذلك لهم، وظهرت ميزته عليهم بالعلم حتى استحق الخلافة، قال الحقّ تعالى: أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ أي: ما غاب، وأعلم ما تظهرونه من قولكم:","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-7","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"أَتَجْعَلُ فِيها.. الخ، وما تكتمونه من استحقاقكم الخلافة، وقولكم: لن يخلق الله تعالى أحداً أعلم منا لتقدمنا، والفضل لمن صدق لا لمن سبق.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-8","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"قال البيضاوي: اعلم أن هذه الآيات تدل على شرف الإنسان، ومزية العلم وفضله على العبادة، وأنه شرط في الخلافة، بل العمدة فيها، وأن التعليم يصح إطلاقه عليه تعالى، وإن لم يصح إطلاق المعلم عليه لاختصاصه بمن يحترف به، وأن اللغات توقيفية- علمها الله بالوحي-، وأن آدم عليه السلام أفضل من هؤلاء الملائكة لأنه أعلم منهم، والأعلم أفضل لقوله تعالى: هَلْ يَسْتَوِي الَّذِينَ يَعْلَمُونَ وَالَّذِينَ لاَ يَعْلَمُونَ، وأن الله يعلم الأشياء قبل حدوثها. هـ. باختصار.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-9","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"وقال في تفسير الملائكة: إنهم أجسام لطيفة قادرة على التشكل، وهي منقسمة على قسمين: قسم شأنهم الاستغراق في معرفة الحق والتنزه عن الاشتغال بغيره، - وهم العليِّون، والملائكة المقربون- وقسم يدبرون الأمر مِنَ","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-10","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"السماء إلى الأرض على ما ثبت به القضاء وجرى به القلم الإلهي، وهم المدبرات أمراً، فمنهم سماوية، ومنهم أرضية. هـ. مختصراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-11","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الروح القائمة بهذا الآدمي هي قطعة من الروح الأعظم التي هي المعاني القائمة بالأواني، وهي آدم الأكبر والأب الأقدم، وفي ذلك يقول ابن الفارض:","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-12","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"وإنِّي وإنْ كنتُ ابن آدمَ صُورةً ... فلِي فِيه مَعْنىً شاهدٌ بأُبوَّتِي","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-13","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"فلما أراد الحق تعالى أن يستخلف هذا الروح في هذه البشرية لتدبرها وتصرفها فيما أريد منها، قالت الملائكة بلسان حالها: كيف تجعل فيها من يفسد فيها بالميل إلى الحظوظ والشهوات، ويسفك الدماء بالغضب والحميات، ونحن نسبحك وننزهك عما لا يليق بك؟ رأت الملائكة ما يصدر من بعض الأرواح من الميل إلى الحضيض الأسفل، ولم تر ما يصدر من بعضها من التصفية والترقية، فقال لهم الحق تعالى: إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ فإن منها من تعرج إلى عرش الحضرة، وتعبدني بالفكرة والنظرة، وتستولي على الوجود بأسره، وتنكشف لها عند ذلك أسرار الذات وأنوار الصفات وأسماء المسميات.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-14","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"فيقول الحق تعالى للملائكة: هل فيكم من كشف له عن هذا السر المكنون، والاسم المصون، فقالوا: سُبْحانَكَ لا عِلْمَ لَنا إِلَّا ما عَلَّمْتَنا من علم الصفات دون أسرار الذات إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ يقول الحق تعالى لروح العارف التي نفذت إلى بحر وحدة الذات وتيار الصفات: أنبئهم بما غاب عنهم من أسرار الجبروت، وأسماء الملكوت، فلما أعلمهم بما كوشف له من الأسرار، وانفلق له من الأنوار، أقروا بشرف الآدمي، وسجدوا لطلعة آدم عليه السلام فقال الحق لهم: أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ؟ أي: ما غاب في سماء الأرواح من الأسرار وفي أرض النفوس من الأنوار، وأعلم ما تظهرونه من الانقياد، وما تكتمونه من الاعتقاد، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-30-33-15","r":"q2-30-33","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","text":"ولما تبينّ شرف آدم عليه السلام وبان فضله أمرهم بالسجود له، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-30-33-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-30-33-s1","r":"q2-30-33","title":"The angels’ question and the purpose of vicegerency","text":"When God Most High willed to populate the earth, having populated the heavens with angels, He informed the angels of what He would do, to extol Adam, honour his offspring, and teach His servants the practice of consultation. He told them: “I am placing on earth a vicegerent ( خليفة ) who represents Me there and executes My judgements.” They replied by way of inquiry—or with the intimacy of confidence, if the speaker was among those brought near—after seeing the jinn corrupt and shed blood: “Will You place there one who causes corruption,” when a vicegerent’s task is to put things right, “while we glorify You with praise,” that is, glorify You accompanied by praising You, “and sanctify ourselves for You,” purifying ourselves for Your sake or declaring You free of whatever does not befit Your holy majesty? Thus: we are more entitled to vicegerency than they are. The Real, exalted and sublime, replied: “I know what you do not know.” I know that among them will be messengers, prophets and friends of God, and those who are your equals or greater than you. When the Friend, Abraham, was cast into the fire, the angels cried out, “Lord, this is Your friend being burned!” He told them, “If he seeks your help, help him.” When Abraham raised his aspiration beyond them, the Real Most High said, “Did I not tell you that I know what you do not know?”","anchor":"en-q2-30-33-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-30-33-s2","r":"q2-30-33","title":"The names, humility and the priority of knowledge","text":"The Real Most High then disclosed the ground of Adam’s entitlement to vicegerency: his ennoblement through knowledge. “He taught Adam all the names,” that is, the things named. He cast into Adam’s heart the languages and letters, and the properties and benefits of things, that his descendants would require. He then displayed these named things to the angels, revealing their inability and honouring Adam through knowledge. He said: tell Me the names of these things, if you are truthful in your claim to deserve vicegerency. When they could not recognize those names, they replied, “Glory be to You”—we declare You free from purposeless action—“we have no knowledge except what You taught us. You are the Knowing,” of everything, “the Wise,” in Your perfect ordering of everything. This acknowledges their limitation and inability and indicates that their question was an inquiry seeking explanation of what they found difficult, not an objection. The Real, glorious is His majesty, said: “Adam, tell them their names,” specifying for them the name of each named thing. When he told them—for example, “This is a horse, and this a camel”—and distinguished these things for them, his excellence over them in knowledge became evident, establishing his entitlement to vicegerency. The Real Most High said: “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and earth”—what is hidden—and know what you reveal in saying, “Will You place there…?” and what you conceal concerning your own entitlement to vicegerency, and your saying, “God will not create anyone more knowledgeable than us, since we came before”? Excellence belongs to the one who is true, not simply to the one who came first. Al-Bayḍāwī says: “Know that these verses indicate the dignity of the human being, the distinction of knowledge and its superiority to worship, and that knowledge is a condition of vicegerency—indeed, its principal foundation. They indicate that ‘teaching’ may be predicated of God, although He may not be called ‘a teacher’ ( المعلّم ), since that designation belongs particularly to someone who practises it as a profession; that languages are divinely instituted ( توقيفية ), taught by God through revelation; and that Adam, peace be upon him, is superior to these angels because he knows more than they do. The more knowledgeable is superior, according to His words, ‘Are those who know equal to those who do not know?’ [39:9]. They also indicate that God knows things before they occur.” End of the abridged quotation. [B030] In explaining the angels, he says: “They are subtle bodies ( أجسام لطيفة ) capable of assuming forms and are divided into two classes. One is wholly absorbed in knowing the Real and free from occupying itself with anything else: these are the exalted ones and the angels brought near. The other administers affairs from heaven to earth according to the established decree and the course of the divine Pen: these are those who govern affairs. Among them are heavenly and earthly angels.” End of the abridged quotation. Source comparison: In the fuller passage of al-Bayḍāwī, Anwār al-tanzīl , I:67, on Q2:30, the view that angels are subtle bodies is attributed to most Muslims. He then introduces the philosophers’ account of angels as immaterial substances and places the twofold division under that account. Ibn ʿAjība’s abridgement, Cairo I:94–95, joins the subtle-bodies description directly to the two classes. The translation follows that abridgement; the fuller source distinguishes views whose transition has been omitted here. Abū al-Suʿūd, I:80, preserves the same distinction.","anchor":"en-q2-30-33-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-30-33-s3","r":"q2-30-33","title":"The human spirit and the disclosure of the names","text":"Know that the spirit subsisting in this human being is a portion of the Supreme Spirit ( الروح الأعظم ), which is the meanings subsisting in the vessels ( المعاني القائمة بالأواني ). It is the Greater Adam and most ancient father. Concerning this Ibn al-Fāriḍ says: Though in form I am Adam’s son, within him I have a meaning that witnesses to my fatherhood. [B031] When the Real Most High wished to appoint this spirit as vicegerent within human embodiment, to govern it and dispose of it as intended, the angels said through the tongue of their state ( بلسان حالها ): how can You place within it one who corrupts it by inclining to egoic shares and desires, and sheds blood through anger and partisan passions, while we glorify You and declare You free from what does not befit You? The angels saw some spirits incline to the lowest depth, but did not see the purification and ascent of others. The Real Most High told them, “I know what you do not know.” Among them are spirits that ascend to the Throne of the Presence, worship Me through contemplation and vision, embrace the whole of existence, and have the mysteries of the Essence, the lights of the attributes and the names of the named things unveiled to them. The Real Most High says to the angels: has any of you had this concealed mystery and guarded Name unveiled to him? They reply, “Glory be to You! We have no knowledge except what You have taught us”—knowledge of the attributes, not the mysteries of the Essence—“You are the Knowing, the Wise.” The Real Most High says to the gnostic’s spirit, which has penetrated to the ocean of the Essence’s unity and the current of the attributes: acquaint them with what is hidden from them of the mysteries of the jabarūt and the names of the malakūt. When it informs them of the mysteries unveiled to it and the lights opened before it, they acknowledge the human being’s dignity and prostrate before Adam’s appearance, peace be upon him. The Real says to them: “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and earth?”—the mysteries hidden in the heaven of spirits and the lights hidden in the earth of souls. I know the obedience you display and the belief you conceal. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-30-33-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-30-33-s4","r":"q2-30-33","title":"","text":"Once Adam’s dignity was disclosed and his excellence became clear, He commanded them to prostrate before him, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-30-33-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-34","r":"q2-34","title":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief","text":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief 2:34","anchor":"unit-q2-34"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-34-1","r":"q2-34","title":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief","text":"وَإِذْ قُلْنا لِلْمَلائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلاَّ إِبْلِيسَ أَبى وَاسْتَكْبَرَ وَكانَ مِنَ الْكافِرِينَ (34)","anchor":"ar-q2-34-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-34-2","r":"q2-34","title":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief","text":"قلت: (إذ) ظرف للماضي، ضد إذا، وهي معمولة لفعل مقدر، يفسره قوله تعالى: وَاذْكُرُوا إِذْ كُنْتُمْ، فحيثما وردت في القرآن فيقدر له «اذكر» ، والاستثناء متصل إذا قلنا إبليس من الملائكة، ومنقطع إذا قلنا من الجن. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-34-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-34-3","r":"q2-34","title":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر إِذْ قُلْنا لِلْمَلائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ، لما تبينت فضيلة، آدم أمرهم بالسجود، فقال لهم: اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ سجود انحناء، فَسَجَدُوا كلهم، لأنهم شهدوا الجمع ولم يشهدوا الفرق، فرأوا آدم قِبْلَةً، أو نوراً من أنوار عظمته، إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ أي: امتنع حيث نظر الفرق بحكمة الواحد القهار، فاستكبر وَكانَ من جملة الْكافِرِينَ. وكفره باعتراضه على الله وتسفيه حكمه، لا بامتناعه إذ مجرد المعصية لا تكفر. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-34-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-34-4","r":"q2-34","title":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief","text":"الإشارة: إذا كمل تصفية الروح، وظهر شرفها، خضع لها كل شيء، وتواضع لها كل شيء، وانقاد لأمرها مَن سبقت له العناية، وهبت عليه ريح الهداية، لأنها صارت آدم الأكبر، إلا من إبلسته المشيئة، وطردته القدرة، فاستكبر عن تحكيم جنسه على نفسه، وكان من الكافرين لوجود الخصوصية، فجزاؤه حرمان شهود طلعة الربوبية، وهبوطه إلى حضيض العمومية.","anchor":"ar-q2-34-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-34-5","r":"q2-34","title":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى دخول آدم الجنة، ونزوله إلى الخلافة التي أخبر الحق تعالى بها قبل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-34-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-34-s1","r":"q2-34","title":"The past-time particle and the exception","text":"I say: idh ( إذ ) is an adverbial expression for past time, the opposite of idhā ( إذا ). It is governed by an implied verb, explained by His words “Remember when you were…”: wherever it occurs in the Qurʾān, “remember” is supplied. The exception ( الاستثناء ) is connected if we say Iblīs was one of the angels, and disconnected if we say he belonged to the jinn. And God Most High knows best. [B032]","anchor":"en-q2-34-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-34-s2","r":"q2-34","title":"The cause of Iblīs’s unbelief","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when We told the angels to prostrate before Adam. Once Adam’s excellence was apparent, He commanded their prostration, telling them, “Prostrate before Adam,” with a prostration of bowing. They all prostrated because they witnessed gathering ( الجمع ), not distinction ( الفرق ): they saw Adam as a direction of prayer or a light among the lights of His greatness. Iblīs alone refused, looking to distinction, by the wisdom of the One, the All-Subduing. He grew proud and belonged among the unbelievers. His unbelief lay in objecting to God and declaring His judgement foolish, not simply in refusing, since bare disobedience does not constitute unbelief. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-34-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-34-s3","r":"q2-34","title":"A purified spirit and the refusal to submit","text":"When the spirit’s purification is complete and its dignity becomes manifest, everything bows and humbles itself before it. Whoever has been embraced by antecedent providence and touched by the breeze of guidance submits to its command, for it has become the Greater Adam. The exception is one made an Iblīs by the divine will and driven away by power: he is too proud to submit himself to the judgement of another of his own kind, and becomes one of those who deny the existence of special election. His recompense is deprivation of witnessing the appearance of lordship and descent to the low ground of the ordinary condition.","anchor":"en-q2-34-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-34-s4","r":"q2-34","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then mentions Adam’s entry into Paradise and his descent to the vicegerency of which He had spoken earlier, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-34-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-35-37","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency 2:35–37","anchor":"unit-q2-35-37"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-1","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"وَقُلْنا يا آدَمُ اسْكُنْ أَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ وَكُلا مِنْها رَغَداً حَيْثُ شِئْتُما وَلا تَقْرَبا هذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُونا مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ (35) فَأَزَلَّهُمَا الشَّيْطانُ عَنْها فَأَخْرَجَهُما مِمَّا كانا فِيهِ وَقُلْنَا اهْبِطُوا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ وَلَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَمَتاعٌ إِلى حِينٍ (36) فَتَلَقَّى آدَمُ مِنْ رَبِّهِ كَلِماتٍ فَتابَ عَلَيْهِ إِنَّهُ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ (37)","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-2","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"قلت: (رغداً) : صفة لمصدر محذوف، أي: أكلا رغداً واسعاً، و (تكونا) : منصوب، جواب الأمر، أو معطوف على (تقرباً) ، و (أزلهما) : أوقعهما في الزلل بسبب الأكل، أو أذهبهما عن الجنة، ويدل عليه قراءة حمزة:","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-3","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"«فأزالهما» ، وجملة (بعضكم لبعض عدو) : حالية، أي: متعادين.","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-4","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقُلْنا يَا آدَمُ حين سجدت له الملائكة ودخل الجنة: اسْكُنْ أَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ حواء الْجَنَّةَ، وكانت خلقت من ضلعه الأيسر، وَكُلا من ثمار الجنة حَيْثُ شِئْتُما وَلا تَقْرَبا هذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ: العنب أو التين أو الحنطة فَتَكُونا إن أكلتما منها مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ لنفسيكما. فدخل إبليس خفية أو في فم الحية(1)، فتكلم مع آدم عليه السلام فقال له آدمُ عليه السلام: ما أحسن هذه الحالة لو كان الخلود. فحفظها إبليس، ووجد فيها مدخلاً من جهة الطمع، فقال له: هَلْ أَدُلُّكَ عَلى شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لاَّ يَبْلى فدلّه على أكل الشجرة، وقال: مَا نَهاكُما رَبُّكُما عنها إِلَّا كراهية أَنْ تَكُونا مَلَكَيْنِ أَوْ تَكُونا مِنَ","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-5","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"الْخالِدِينَ وَقاسَمَهُما إِنِّي لَكُما لَمِنَ النَّاصِحِينَ. وأكلت حواء أولاً، ثم قالت له: قد أكلتُ ولم يضرني، ثم أكل آدم عليه السلام من جنس الشجرة، لا من عينها، متأوّلاً، فطار التاج واللباس، وأخرجهما مِمَّا كانا فِيهِ من رغد العيش والهناء، وأهبطهما إلى الأرض، للتعب والعناء، ليكون خليفة على ما سبق به القضاء.","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-6","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"فقال لهم الحق تعالى: اهْبِطُوا آدم وحواء وإبليس والحية، بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ وَلَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ استقرار وتمتع إِلى حِينٍ وفاتكم، فتقدمون علي فيجازي المحسن بإحسانه، والمسيء بإساءته، فَتَلَقَّى أي أخذ آدَمُ مِنْ رَبِّهِ كَلِماتٍ وهي: رَبَّنا ظَلَمْنا أَنْفُسَنا وَإِنْ لَمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنا وَتَرْحَمْنا لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْخاسِرِينَ، فَتابَ الحق تعالى عليه واجتباه لحضرته، فإنه توّاب كثير التوبة على عباده، رحيم بهم، أرحم من أبيهم وأمهم، اللهم ارحمنا رحمة تعصمنا بها عن رؤية السّوي، إِنك على كل شيءٍ قدير.","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-7","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للروح، إذا كمل تهذيبها، وتمت تربيتها: اسكن أنت وبشريتك التي تزوجتها- قال تعالى: وَإِذَا النُّفُوسُ زُوِّجَتْ- جنة المعارف، وَكُلا من ثمار أذواقها وأنهار علومها، وتبوَّءًا من قصور ترقياتها، أكلاً واسعاً ما دمتما متحليين بالأدب، ولا تقربا شجرة المعصية وسوء الأدب (فتكونا من الظالمين) ، فلما سكنت جنة الخلود، وشَرهَتْ إلى الخلود، أهبطها الله إلى أرض العبودية، وردها إلى البقاء لتستحق الخلافة، وتقوم بحقوق الربوبية، بسبب ما ارتكبه من المعصية، وهي الشَّرهُ إلى دوام الحرية، «أكْرِمْ بها معصية أورثت الخلافة!» ، فكل ما ينزل بالروح إلى قهرية العبودية، فهو سبب إلى الترقي لشهود نور الربوبية، وربما قضى عليك بالذنب فكان سبب الوصول، فلما أراد الحق تعالى أن ينزلها إلى أرض العبودية بالسلوك بعد الجذب، قال لها ولمن يحاربها من الشيطان والهوى والدنيا وسائر الحظوظ: اهبطوا بعضكم لبعض عدو، ولكم- أيها العارفون بعد جهاد أعدائكم- في أرض العبودية، استقرار وتمتعٌ بتجليات أنوار الربوبية، إلى حين الملاقاة الحقيقية. فتلقت الروح من ربها كلمات الإنابة، وهبَّ عليها، نسيم الهداية، بما سبق لها من عين العناية، فتاب عليها، وقرَّبها إلى حضرة الشهود، ومعاينة طلعة الملك الودود، إنه تواب رحيم جواد كريم.","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-35-37-8","r":"q2-35-37","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","text":"ثم كرّر الحق تعالى أمرهم بالهبوط، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-35-37-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-35-37-s1","r":"q2-35-37","title":"Abundant eating and the cause of the lapse","text":"I say: “freely” ( رغداً ) qualifies an omitted verbal noun: “eat an abundant, ample eating.” “Become” ( تكونا ) is subjunctive as the response to the injunction, or coordinated with “approach” ( تقربا ). “He caused them to slip” ( أزلهما ) means that he made them fall into error through eating, or removed them from the Garden. Ḥamza’s reading, “he removed them” ( فأزالهما ), supports the latter. “Enemies to one another” is a circumstantial clause: “being mutually hostile.” [B033]","anchor":"en-q2-35-37-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-35-37-s2","r":"q2-35-37","title":"The temptation and the words of return","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: after the angels prostrated before Adam and he entered the Garden, We said, “Adam, dwell with your spouse Eve in the Garden.” She had been created from his left rib. “Eat of the Garden’s fruits wherever you wish, but do not approach this tree”—the vine, fig, or wheat—“lest,” by eating from it, “you wrong yourselves.” Iblīs entered secretly or in the serpent’s mouth and spoke with Adam, peace be upon him. Adam said, “How excellent this state would be, were it everlasting!” Iblīs remembered this and found in covetousness an opening. He said, “Shall I lead you to the tree of everlasting life and a dominion that never decays?” [20:120]. He directed him to eat from the tree, saying: “Your Lord only forbade you it lest you become two angels or become immortal”; and he swore to them, “I am a sincere adviser to you both” [7:20–21]. Eve ate first, then said, “I have eaten and it has not harmed me.” Adam then ate from the kind of tree, not the particular tree itself, acting on an interpretation. The crown and clothing flew away. Satan brought them out of the ease and happiness they had enjoyed, and they were sent down to earth, to toil and hardship, so that Adam might become vicegerent according to the antecedent decree. [B034] The Real Most High told them—Adam, Eve, Iblīs and the serpent—“Go down, enemies to one another. On earth you shall have residence and enjoyment until your deaths; then you come before Me, and the doer of good is recompensed for his goodness and the evildoer for his wrongdoing.” Adam received, that is, took, words from his Lord: “Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves. If You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we shall surely be among the losers” [7:23]. The Real Most High turned towards him and chose him for His Presence, for He continually turns towards His servants and is merciful to them, more merciful than their fathers and mothers. God, grant us a mercy that protects us from seeing other-than-You: You have power over all things.","anchor":"en-q2-35-37-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-35-37-s3","r":"q2-35-37","title":"The return from attraction to servanthood","text":"When the spirit’s refinement is complete and its formation perfected, the Real, glorious is His majesty, tells it: dwell, with the human embodiment you have married—He says, “When souls are paired” [81:7]—in the garden of gnosis. Eat of the fruits of its spiritual tastings and the rivers of its sciences, and take up residence in the palaces of its ascents, eating freely so long as you remain adorned with courtesy. Do not approach the tree of disobedience and ill courtesy, lest you become wrongdoers. When it dwelt in the garden of permanence and greedily desired to remain there, God sent it down to the earth of servanthood and returned it to subsistence ( البقاء ), so that it might deserve vicegerency and fulfil the claims of lordship, through the disobedience it committed: greedy desire for perpetual freedom. “How noble a disobedience that bequeathed vicegerency!” Everything that brings the spirit down into the compelling condition of servanthood becomes a means of ascent to witnessing the light of lordship. He may decree a sin for you, and it becomes the means of arrival. [B035] When the Real Most High wished to bring it down to the earth of servanthood through wayfaring after attraction ( السلوك بعد الجذب ), He told it and its adversaries—Satan, caprice, the world and the other egoic shares—“Go down, enemies to one another.” After striving against your enemies, you gnostics have in the earth of servanthood a dwelling and enjoyment of the self-disclosures of the lights of lordship until the true meeting. The spirit receives from its Lord words of turning back. The breeze of guidance blows over it through the providence already bestowed upon it; He turns towards it and brings it near to the presence of witnessing and the direct vision of the loving King’s appearance. He is the Ever-Relenting, Merciful, Munificent, Generous.","anchor":"en-q2-35-37-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-35-37-s4","r":"q2-35-37","title":"","text":"The Real Most High repeats His command that they descend, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-35-37-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-38-39","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization 2:38–39","anchor":"unit-q2-38-39"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-38-39-1","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"قُلْنَا اهْبِطُوا مِنْها جَمِيعاً فَإِمَّا يَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِنِّي هُدىً فَمَنْ تَبِعَ هُدايَ فَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (38) وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَكَذَّبُوا بِآياتِنا أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (39)","anchor":"ar-q2-38-39-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-38-39-2","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"قلت: (إن) : شرط، و (ما) زيدت لتقوية الشرط، ولذلك دخلت نون التوكيد، وعبر بإن دون (إذا) ، مع تحقق مجيئ الهدى لأنه غير واجب عقلاً، وجملة الشرط الثاني وجوابه، الشرط الأول، و (جميعاً) حال مؤكدة أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-38-39-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-38-39-3","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"اهبطوا أنتم أجمعون، ولذلك لا يقتضى اجتماعهم على الهبوط في زمان واحد.","anchor":"ar-q2-38-39-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-38-39-4","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"ولما أمر الحقّ جلا جلاله آدم أولاً بالهبوط من الجنة، جعل يبكي ويتضرّع ويقول: ألم تخلقني بيدك؟ ألم تسجد لي ملائكتك؟ ألم تدخلني جنتك؟ ثم ألهم الكلمات التي تلقاها من ربه، فتاب عليه ورحمه، فطمع آدم حين سمع من ربه قبول توبته في البقاء في الجنة، فقال له الحق جلّ جلاله: يا آدم لا يجاورني من عصاني، وقد سبقت كلمتي بهبوطك إلى الأرض لتكون خليفتي بذريتك، فكرّر عليه الأمر بالهبوط ثانياً. فقال: اهْبِطُوا مِنْها جَمِيعاً أنتما بما اشتملتما عليه من ذريتكما. فمهما يَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِنِّي هُدىً أي: بيان وإرشاد إلى توحيدي ومعرفتي، على يد رسول أو نائب عنه، فَمَنْ تَبِعَ ذلك الإرشاد، واهتدى إلى معرفتي وتوحيدي، وعمل بطاعتي وتكاليفي، فَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ من لحوق مكروه وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ من فوات محبوب، لأني أَصرف عنهم جميع المكاره، وأجلب لهم المنافع، وَالَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا بِآياتِنا الدالة على قدرتنا المنزلة على رسلنا، واستكبروا عن النظر فيها، أو عن الخضوع لمن جاء بها، أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-38-39-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-38-39-5","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"الإشارة: إذا سكنت الأرواح في عُشِّ الحضرة، وتمكنت من الشهود والنظرة، أمرها الحق تعالى بالنزول إلى سماء الحقوق أو أرض الحظوظ، فتنزل بالإذن والتمكين، والرسوخ في اليقين، لا لطلب جزاء أو لقضاء شهوة، بل تنزل بالله ومن الله وإلى الله، فمن نزل منها على هذا الهدى الحسن فَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ، ومن ركب بحر التوحيد مع غير رئيس عارف، ولم يأوِ إلى سفينة الشريعة، واستكبر عن الخضوع إلى تكاليفها لعبت به الأمواج، فكان من المغرقين. أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ لأن مَن تحقق ولم يتشرّع فقد تزندق، ومن تشرع ولم يتصوف فقد تفسّق، ومَن جمع بينهما فقد تحقق، جعلنا الله ممن تحقّق بهما. وسلك على منهاجهما إلى الممات، آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-38-39-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-38-39-6","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"ولما ذكر الحق تعالى شرف كتابه، ونفى وجود الريب عن ساحته، ثم دعا إلى توحيده، وبرهن على وجوده، بابتداء خلق العالم من عرشه إلى فرشه، وذكر كيفية ابتداء عمارته، خاطب بني إسرائيل لأنهم أهل العلم بالأخبار المتقدمة، وقد سمعوا هذه الأخبار من نَبِي أُمِّي لم يُعْهَدْ بقراءةٍ ولا تعلم، فقامت الحجة عليهم، وتحققوا أنه من عند الله. وما منعهم من الإسلام إلا الحسد وحب الرئاسة، فلذلك أطال الحق الكلام معهم، تارةً يُقرِّعَهم على عدم","anchor":"ar-q2-38-39-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-38-39-7","r":"q2-38-39","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","text":"الإيمان وما فعلوا مع أنبيائهم، وتارة يذكرهم النِعَم التي أنعم الله على أسلافهم، فقال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q2-38-39-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-38-39-s1","r":"q2-38-39","title":"The condition and the gift of guidance","text":"I say: in ( إن ) is conditional; mā is added to strengthen the condition, and for this reason the emphatic nūn enters the verb. In , rather than idhā , is used although the coming of guidance is certain, because it is not rationally obligatory. The second conditional sentence, with its response, supplies the response to the first condition. “All together” ( جميعاً ) is an emphatic circumstantial expression: “descend, every one of you.” It therefore does not require their descending at one and the same time. [B036]","anchor":"en-q2-38-39-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-38-39-s2","r":"q2-38-39","title":"Repentance does not annul the appointed vicegerency","text":"When the Real, glorious is His majesty, first commanded Adam to leave the Garden, he wept and implored: “Did You not create me with Your hand? Did You not make Your angels prostrate before me? Did You not admit me to Your Garden?” He was then inspired with the words he received from his Lord, who turned towards him and had mercy on him. Hearing that his repentance had been accepted, Adam hoped to remain in the Garden. The Real, glorious is His majesty, told him: “Adam, one who has disobeyed Me does not remain My neighbour. My word has already gone forth that you descend to earth to be My vicegerent through your offspring.” He therefore repeated the command to descend: “Go down from it, all of you”—the two of you together with the offspring contained in you. Whenever guidance comes to you from Me—explanation and direction towards affirming My unity and knowing Me, at the hands of a messenger or his deputy—whoever follows that direction, is guided to My knowledge and unity, and observes My obedience and obligations shall have no fear of harm overtaking him or grief over losing something beloved. I turn every harm away from them and bring benefits to them. Those who deny Our signs, which demonstrate Our power and are sent down upon Our messengers, and are too proud to consider them or submit to their bearer, are the companions of the Fire; there they abide for ever.","anchor":"en-q2-38-39-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-38-39-s3","r":"q2-38-39","title":"Descending with permission and remaining in the ship of the Law","text":"When spirits dwell in the nest of the Presence and become established in witnessing and vision, the Real Most High commands them to descend to the heaven of rightful obligations or the earth of allotted enjoyments ( سماء الحقوق أو أرض الحظوظ ). They descend by permission and firm establishment, rooted in certainty—not to seek recompense or gratify desire. Rather, they descend by God, from God and unto God. Those who descend upon this beautiful guidance have no fear and do not grieve. But whoever sails the ocean of unity without a knowing captain, does not take refuge in the ship of the Sacred Law, and is too proud to submit to its obligations is tossed by the waves and drowned. Such are the companions of the Fire, abiding therein. For whoever pursues realization without observing the Law falls into heresy; whoever observes the Law without Sufi purification falls into transgression; and whoever unites the two attains realization. May God make us among those who realize both and follow their way until death. Amen. [B037]","anchor":"en-q2-38-39-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-38-39-s4","r":"q2-38-39","title":"","text":"Having declared His Book’s dignity and excluded doubt from its precincts, then summoned people to His unity and demonstrated His existence through the beginning of the world’s creation, from its throne to its carpet, and described how it first became inhabited, the Real Most High addresses the Children of Israel. They possess knowledge of the earlier accounts and have heard these accounts from an unlettered Prophet not known for reading or instruction. The proof has therefore been established against them, and they recognize that it comes from God. Nothing prevents their embracing Islam but envy and love of leadership. For this reason the Real speaks to them at length: sometimes rebuking their failure to believe and their treatment of their prophets, sometimes reminding them of the blessings He bestowed upon their forebears. He says:","anchor":"en-q2-38-39-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-40-43","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant 2:40–43","anchor":"unit-q2-40-43"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-1","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَوْفُوا بِعَهْدِي أُوفِ بِعَهْدِكُمْ وَإِيَّايَ فَارْهَبُونِ (40) وَآمِنُوا بِما أَنْزَلْتُ مُصَدِّقاً لِما مَعَكُمْ وَلا تَكُونُوا أَوَّلَ كافِرٍ بِهِ وَلا تَشْتَرُوا بِآياتِي ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً وَإِيَّايَ فَاتَّقُونِ (41) وَلا تَلْبِسُوا الْحَقَّ بِالْباطِلِ وَتَكْتُمُوا الْحَقَّ وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (42) وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكاةَ وَارْكَعُوا مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ (43)","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-2","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"قلت: (إسرائيل) : هو يعقوب بن إسحاق بن إبراهيم الخليل- عليهم الصلاة والسلام- وهو اسم عجمي، وبنو تميم تقول: «إسرائين» بالنون، (وإسرا) بالعبرانية: عبد، و (إيل) : اسم الله تعالى، فمعناه: عبد الله، وبنو إسرائيل:","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-3","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"هم أولاد يعقوب عليه السلام، و (بعهدي) من إضافة المصدر إلى فاعله، وبِعَهْدِكُمْ إلى مفعوله، و (إياي) منصوب بفعل مضمر، يُقدر مؤخراً. أي: أياي ارهبوا فارهبون. وحذف مفعول (ارهبون) لرءوس الآي، وكذا قوله: (وإياي فاتقون) ، والرهبة: خوف مع تحرُّز، و (تكتموا) : معطوف على (تلبسوا) ، أو منصوب بأن مضمرة بعد النهي، و (أنتم تعلمون) : جملة حالية.","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-4","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ التي خصصتُكم بها، بأن فضلتكم على أهل زمانكم، وجعلت فيكم أنبياء ورسلاً، كلما انقرض نبيّ بعثت نبيّاً آخر، وجعلتكم ملوكاً وحكاماً على الناس، قبل أن تفسدوا في الأرض بقتل الأنبياء، فتكفروا بهذه النعم، فإن الإنسان حسود غيور بالطبع، فإذا نظر إلى ما أنعم الله على غيره حمله الحسد والغيرة على السخط والكفران، وإذا نظر إلى ما أنعم الله به عليه حمله حب النعمة على الرضا والشكر. فاذكروا ما أنعمتُ به عليكم، وقيدوه بالشكر، وَأَوْفُوا بِعَهْدِي الذي عهدت إليكم، وهو أنكم إن أدركتم محمدا صلى الله عليه وسلّم لتؤمنن به ولتنصرنه، ولتبينن صفته التي في كتابكم، ولا تكتمونها، أُوفِ بِعَهْدِكُمْ بأن أدخلكم جنتي، وأبيح لكم النظر إلى وجهي، وأحل عليكم رضواني في جملة عبادي، ولا ترهبوا أحداً غيري، فإنه لا فاعل غيري.","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-5","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"وبادروا إلى الإيمان بِما أَنْزَلْتُ على محمد رسولي، من كتابي، الذي هو مصدق لِما مَعَكُمْ من التوراة، ومهيمن عليه، وَلا تَكُونُوا أَوَّلَ فريق كافِرٍ بِهِ، فتبوءوا بإثمكم وإثم من تبعكم، ولا تستبدلوا الإيمان الذي هو سبب الفوز في الدارين، بالعرضِ الفاني الذي تأخذونه من سفلتكم، فإنه ثمن قليل يعقبه عذاب جليل وخزي كبير. ولا تخشوا أحداً سواي فإن النفع والضرر بيدي، ولا تخلطوا الْحَقَّ الذي هو ذكر","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-6","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم وصفته التي في كتابكم، بِالْباطِلِ الذي تريدونه تحريفاً وتأويلا، وَلا تَكْتُمُوا الْحَقَّ الذي عندكم من ذكر محمد وصحة رسالته، وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ أنكم محرفون، ولابسون عناداً وحسداً، فيحل عليكم غضبي وعقابي، وَمَنْ يَحْلِلْ عَلَيْهِ غَضَبِي فَقَدْ هَوى. فإذا حصلتم أصول الدين، وهو الإيمان، فاشتغلوا بفروعه، وهي الصلاة والزكاة وغيرهما، فأدوهما على منهاج المسلمين. واجعلوا صلاتكم في جماعة المؤمنين فإنَّ صلاة الجماعة تُفضلُ غيرها بسبعٍ وعشرين درجة، مع سريان الأسرار واقتباس الأنوار من الصالحين والأبرار، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-7","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"الإشارة: إذا توجَّه الخطاب إلى طائفة مخصوصة، حمله أهل الفهم عن الله على عمومه لكل سامع، فإن الملك إذا عاتب قوماً بمحضر آخرين، كان المراد بذلك تحذير كل مَن يسمع، فكأن الحق جل جلاله يقول: يا بني آدم اذكروا نعمتي التي أنعمت عليكم، وتفكروا في أصولها وفروعها، واشكروني عليها بنسبتها إليَّ وحدي، فإنه لا منعم غيري، فمن شكرني شكرته، ومن فيض إحساني وبري مددته، ومن كفر نعمتي سلبته، وعن بابي طردته، وأوفوا بعهدي بالقيام بوظائف العبودية، أوف بعهدكم بأن أطلعكم على أسرار الربوبية.","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-8","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"أو: أوفوا بعهدي بالقيام برسوم الشريعة، أوفِ بعهدكم بالهداية إلى منار الطريقة، أو: أوفوا بعهدي بسلوك منهاج الطريقة، أوفِ بعهدكم بالإيصال إلى عين الحقيقة، أو: أوفوا بعهدي بالاستغراق في بحر الشهود، أوفِ بعهدكم بالترقي أبدا إلى الملك الودود، وخصّوني بالرهب والرغب، وتوجهوا إليّ في كل سؤال وطلب، أعطف عليكم بعنايتي وودي، وأمنحكم من عظيم إحساني ورفدي، وآمنوا بما أنزلت على قلوب أوليائى، من مواهب أسراري وآلائي، تصديقاً لما أتحفت به رسلي وأنبيائي، فكل ما ظهر على الأولياء فهو معجزة للأنبياء وتصديق لهم، ولا تبادروا بالإنكار على أوليائي، فتكونوا سبباً في طرد عبادي عن بابي، ولا يمنعكم حب الرئاسة والجاه عن الخضوع إلى أوليائي، ولا ترقبوا أحداً غيري، فإني أمنعكم من شهود سري.","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-9","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"ولا تلبسوا الحق بالباطل، فتظهروا شعار الصالحين وتبطنوا أخلاق الفاسقين، تتزيوا بزى الأولياء، وتفعلوا فعل الأغوياء، وإذا تحققتم بخصوصية أحد من عبادي، فلا تكتموها عن أهل محبتي وودادي، وأقيموا صلاة القلوب بالخضوع تحت مجاري الأقدار، وأدّوا زكاة النفوس بالذل والانكسار، وكونوا مع الخاشعين، واركعوا مع الراكعين، أمنحكم معونتي ونصري، وأفيض عليكم من بحر إحساني وبري، أنا عند المنكسرة قلوبُهم من أجلى.","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-40-43-10","r":"q2-40-43","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","text":"ثم وبّخ الحق تعالى من عرف الحق وحرم نفسه منه من أهل الكتاب وغيرهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-40-43-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-40-43-s1","r":"q2-40-43","title":"Israel, the covenant and the fronted pronoun","text":"I say: Israel is Jacob, son of Isaac, son of Abraham the Friend, peace and blessings be upon them. It is a non-Arabic name; the Banū Tamīm pronounce it Isrāʾīn , with nūn. In Hebrew, isrā means servant and īl is a name of God Most High, so its meaning is “servant of God.” The Children of Israel are Jacob’s descendants. [B038] “My covenant” is an annexation of the verbal noun to its agent ( إضافة المصدر إلى فاعله ), while “your covenant” annexes it to its object. “Me alone” ( إياي ) is accusative through an implied verb, reconstructed after it: “Me fear—so fear Me.” The object of “fear Me” is omitted for the verse-endings, as also in “be mindful of Me alone.” Fear ( الرهبة ) here is fear accompanied by self-guarding. “Conceal” ( تكتموا ) is coordinated with “clothe” ( تلبسوا ), or subjunctive through an implicit an after the prohibition. “While you know” is circumstantial.","anchor":"en-q2-40-43-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-40-43-s2","r":"q2-40-43","title":"Gratitude, truthfulness and worship","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember the blessing with which I distinguished you: I preferred you over the people of your time and appointed prophets and messengers among you; whenever a prophet passed away, I sent another. I made you kings and governors over people before you corrupted the earth by killing the prophets and denied these blessings. Human beings are naturally prone to envy and rivalry: looking at what God gives another inclines them to resentment and ingratitude, whereas looking at what He gives them inclines them, through love of the blessing, to contentment and thanks. Remember My benefactions and secure them with gratitude. Fulfil the covenant I made with you: should you live to encounter Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, you must believe in him, support him, and disclose rather than hide the description of him in your Book. I shall fulfil My covenant with you by admitting you to My Garden, permitting you to behold My Face, and bestowing My good pleasure upon you among My servants. Fear none but Me, for there is no agent other than Me. Hasten to believe in My Book sent down upon My Messenger Muḥammad, confirming the Torah you possess and standing as its guardian. Do not be the first group to disbelieve in it, bearing both your own sin and that of your followers. Do not exchange faith—the means of success in both abodes—for the passing worldly gain you take from your lower ranks. It is a paltry price followed by mighty punishment and great disgrace. Fear none but Me, for benefit and harm are in My hand. Do not mix the truth—the mention of Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, and his description in your Book—with the falsehood you intend through distortion and tendentious interpretation. Do not conceal the truth you possess about Muḥammad and the soundness of his mission, knowing that you distort and confuse through obstinacy and envy, lest My wrath and punishment fall upon you: “He upon whom My wrath falls has indeed fallen” [20:81]. Once you possess the foundations of religion—faith—occupy yourselves with its branches: prayer, almsgiving and the rest. Perform them according to the Muslims’ way and join the believers in congregational prayer. Congregational prayer surpasses other prayer by twenty-seven degrees, together with the circulation of spiritual mysteries and the receiving of lights from the righteous and good. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-40-43-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-40-43-s3","r":"q2-40-43","title":"The successive fulfilments of the covenant","text":"When an address is directed to a particular group, those who understand from God take its meaning as general for every hearer. When a king reproaches one people before others, his purpose is to warn everyone who hears. It is as though the Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Adam, remember My blessing upon you; reflect on its roots and branches, and thank Me by attributing it to Me alone, for none bestows blessings but I. Whoever thanks Me, I thank and sustain from the overflow of My kindness and beneficence. Whoever denies My blessing, I deprive and drive from My door. Fulfil My covenant by discharging the duties of servanthood, and I fulfil yours by disclosing to you the mysteries of lordship. Or: fulfil My covenant by observing the forms of the Sacred Law, and I fulfil yours by guiding you to the beacon of the Path. Or: fulfil My covenant by travelling the Path, and I fulfil yours by bringing you to the very reality. Or: fulfil My covenant by immersion in the ocean of witnessing, and I fulfil yours through unceasing ascent towards the loving King. Direct fear and desire to Me alone, turning to Me in every request and need. I embrace you with My care and love and grant you immense beneficence and support. Believe in the gifts of My mysteries and blessings that I send down upon My friends’ hearts, confirming what I bestowed on My messengers and prophets. Everything that appears upon the friends of God is a miracle of the prophets and a confirmation of them. Do not hasten to deny My friends and so become the cause of driving My servants from My door. Do not let love of leadership and rank prevent your submission to My friends; do not watch for another besides Me, lest I withhold from you the witnessing of My mystery. Do not clothe truth in falsehood, displaying the marks of the righteous while concealing the character of transgressors, wearing the garb of God’s friends while acting as the misguided do. Once you recognize special election in one of My servants, do not hide it from the people of My love and affection. Establish the prayer of hearts by submission beneath the unfolding decrees; render the alms of souls through humility and brokenness. Be with the humble and bow with those who bow: I grant you My aid and victory and pour upon you from the ocean of My kindness and goodness. “I am with those whose hearts are broken for My sake.” [B039]","anchor":"en-q2-40-43-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-40-43-s4","r":"q2-40-43","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then rebukes those among the People of the Book and others who know the truth but deprive themselves of it, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-40-43-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-44","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself 2:44","anchor":"unit-q2-44"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-1","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"أَتَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبِرِّ وَتَنْسَوْنَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ تَتْلُونَ الْكِتابَ أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ (44)","anchor":"ar-q2-44-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-2","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"قلت: البر، بالكسر: يجمع وجوه الخير وأنواع الطاعات، والنسيانُ: الترك.","anchor":"ar-q2-44-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-3","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله فى توبيخ أحبار اليهود، كانوا إذا استرشدهم أحد من العرب دلّوه على الإسلام، وقالوا له: دين محمد حق، وهم يمتنعون منه، وقيل: كانوا يأمرون الناس بالصدقة وهم يبخلون، فقال لهم: كيف تَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبِرِّ والإحسان، وتتركون أَنْفُسَكُمْ في الكفر والعصيان، وأنتم تدرسون التوراة الصحيح، وتعلمون أن ذلك من أقبح القبيح؟، أفلا عقل لكم يزجركم عن هذه الخصلة الذميمة؟ فإن من شأن العقل التمييز بين القبيح والحسن والنافع والضار، فكل من تقدم لما فيه ضرره فلا عقل له.","anchor":"ar-q2-44-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-4","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن أشار إلى مقام لم يبلغْ قدمه إليه، فهذا التوبيخ متوجِّهُ إليه، وكل مَن ذكر غيره بعيب لم يتخلص منه، قيل له: أتأمر الناس بالبر وتنسى نفسك خالية منه، فلا يسلم من توبيخ هذه الآية من أهل التذكير إلا الفرد النادر من أهل الصفاء والوفاء.","anchor":"ar-q2-44-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-5","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"وقال البيضاوي: (المراد بها حثّ الواعظ على تزكية النفس، والإقبال عليها بالتكميل لتُقَوم فيُقَيِّم، لا منع الفاسق عن الوعظ، فإن الإخلال بأحد الأمرين المأمور بهما لا يوجب الإخلال بالآخر) . فانظره. وتأمل قول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-44-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-6","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"يا أيهَا الرجلُ المعلِّمُ غيرَه ... هلاَّ لنفسِك كانَ ذا التعليمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-44-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-7","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"تَصِف الدواءَ لِذي السقامِ وذي الضنَا ... ومِن الضَّنَا وجَواهُ أنتَ سقيمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-44-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-8","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"وأراكَ تلقحُ بالرشادِ عقُولَنا ... نُصْحاً، وأنت مِن الرشادِ عديمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-44-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-9","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"ابدأ بنفسِك فانْهَهَا عَن غَيَّها ... فإذا انتهتْ عنه فأنتَ حكيمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-44-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-10","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"فَهُناك يُقْبَلُ إن وعظتَ، ويُقتدَى ... بالقول منكَ، وينفعُ التعليمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-44-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-11","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"لا تَنْهَ عن خُلقٍ وتأتيَ مثلَه ... عارٌ علَيكَ إذا فعلتَ عظيمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-44-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-12","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"لكن مَنْ حصل له بعض الصفاء، ذكر غيره ونفسه معهم، وكان بعض أشياخنا يقول حين يذكر الفقراء: نحن إنما ننبح على نفوسنا.","anchor":"ar-q2-44-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-44-13","r":"q2-44","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","text":"ثم أشار الحق تعالى إلى الدواء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-44-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-44-s1","r":"q2-44","title":"Righteousness and forgetting","text":"I say: righteousness ( birr , البر ), with kasra, embraces every form of goodness and kind of obedience. Forgetting ( النسيان ) means leaving aside.","anchor":"en-q2-44-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-44-s2","r":"q2-44","title":"A rebuke to those who know but do not act","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says in reproach to the Jewish learned men: when an Arab sought their direction, they directed him to Islam, saying that Muḥammad’s religion was true, while themselves abstaining from it. Alternatively, they commanded others to give charity but were themselves miserly. He says: how do you enjoin righteousness and beneficence upon people and leave yourselves in unbelief and disobedience, although you study the authentic Torah and know this to be among the ugliest acts? Have you no understanding to restrain you from this blameworthy quality? The rational intellect distinguishes ugly from beautiful and beneficial from harmful; one who deliberately approaches what harms him does not act with understanding.","anchor":"en-q2-44-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-44-s3","r":"q2-44","title":"The admonisher’s responsibility to his own soul","text":"Whoever points towards a station his own foot has not reached is addressed by this rebuke. Whoever reminds another of a fault from which he has not freed himself is told: do you enjoin righteousness upon others and forget that your own soul is empty of it? Among those who give reminders, only the rare individual possessed of purity and fidelity escapes this verse’s reproach. Al-Bayḍāwī says: “Its purpose is to urge the admonisher to purify his soul and turn to its perfection, so that it is set right and he can set others right—not to prevent a transgressor from admonishing. Neglecting one of two commanded duties does not necessitate neglecting the other.” Consider his words. Reflect also upon the poet’s saying: You who teach another, why was this instruction not for yourself? You prescribe medicine for the sick and wasted, while you yourself are sick with wasting and its pain. I see you implant guidance in our minds as counsel, while yourself devoid of guidance. Begin with yourself: restrain it from its error; once it desists, you are indeed wise. Then, when you admonish, it is accepted; your words are followed, and instruction benefits. Do not forbid a trait and then perform its like: great is your shame if you do so. Yet one who possesses some purity may remind others and include himself among them. One of our shaykhs, when reminding the spiritual poor, used to say: “We are only barking at our own souls.”","anchor":"en-q2-44-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-44-s4","r":"q2-44","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then points to the remedy, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-44-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-45-46","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God 2:45–46","anchor":"unit-q2-45-46"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-1","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"وَاسْتَعِينُوا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلاةِ وَإِنَّها لَكَبِيرَةٌ إِلاَّ عَلَى الْخاشِعِينَ (45) الَّذِينَ يَظُنُّونَ أَنَّهُمْ مُلاقُوا رَبِّهِمْ وَأَنَّهُمْ إِلَيْهِ راجِعُونَ (46)","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-2","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"قلت: الصبر: هو حبس القلب على حكم الرب، فيحتمل أن يُراد به ظاهره، أو يراد به هنا الصوم، لأن فيه الصبر عن الشهوات. والخشوع فى الجوارح: سكونها وذُلها، والخضوع في القلب: انقياده لحكم الرب.","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-3","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا مَن ابتلي بالرئاسة والجاه، واستكبر عن الانقياد لأحكام الله التي جاءت بها الرسل من عند الله، استعن على نفسك بِالصَّبْرِ على قطع المألوفات، وترك الحظوظ والشهوات، وأصل فروعها حب الرئاسة والجاه، فمن صبر على تركهما فاز برضوان الله. وفي الحديث: «وفي الصبر على ما تكره خير كثير» . وقال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-4","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"والصَّبْرُ كالصْبرِ مُرٌ في مذَاقَتِه ... لَكِنْ عَواقِبُه أحلَى مِن العسلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-5","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"أو: وَاسْتَعِينُوا بالصوم وَالصَّلاةِ، فإن في الصوم كَسْرَ الشَّهْوَةِ وتصفية النفس، فإذا صفت النفس من الرذائل تحلت بأنواع الفضائل، كالتواضع والإنصاف، والخشوع وسائر سني الأوصاف، وفي الصلاة أنواع من العبادات النفسية والبدنية، كالطهارة، وستر العورة، وصرف المال فيهما، والتوجه إلى الكعبة، والعكوف للعبادة، وإظهار الخشوع بالجوارح، وإخلاص النية بالقلب، ومجاهدة الشيطان، ومناجاة الرحمن وقراءة القرآن، وكف النفس عن الأطْيَبَيْنِ(1)، وفي الصلاة قضاء المآرب وجبر المصائب، ولذلك كان- عليه الصلاة والسلام- إذا حزبه أمر فزع إلى الصلاة، وَإِنَّها لَكَبِيرَةٌ أي: شاقة على النفس لتكريرها في كل يوم، ومجيئها وقت حلاوة النوم، إِلَّا عَلَى الْخاشِعِينَ الذين سكنت حلاوتها في قلوبهم، وتناجوا فيها مع ربهم، حتى صارت فيها قُرَّة عينهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-6","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"الذين يتيقنون أَنَّهُمْ مُلاقُوا رَبِّهِمْ فيتنعمون بالنظر إلى وجهه الكريم، ويتيقنون أيضاً أنهم راجعون إلى ربهم بالبعث والحشر للثواب والعقاب، وإنما عبَّر الحق تعالى هنا بالظن في موضع اليقين إبقاء على المذنبين، وتوفراً على العاصين، الذين ليس لهم صفاء اليقين إذ لو ذكر اليقين صرفاً لخرجوا من الجملة، فسبحانه من رب حليم، وجواد كريم. اللهم امنن علينا بصفاء المعرفة واليقين، حتى لا يختلج قلوبنا وَهْمٌ ولا ريب، يا رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-7","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"الإشارة: يا من رام الدخول إلى حضرة الله، تذلل وتواضع لأولياء الله، وتجرّع الصبر في ذلك كي يدخلوك حضرة الله، كما قال القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-8","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"تَذللْ لِمنْ تَهْوَى فَلَيْسَ الْهَوى سَهْلُ(2) ... إِذَا رَضِيَ المحبوبُ صَحّ لَكَ الوَصْلُ","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-9","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"فإن منعك من ذلك حب الرئاسة والجاه، فاستعن على ذلك بالصبر والصلاة، فإن الصبر عنوان الظفر، والصلاة تنهى عن الفحشاء والمنكر. فأدمن قرع الباب حتى تدخل مع الأحباب، فالإدمان على عبادة الصلاة أمره كبير، إلا مَن خلص إلى مناجاة العلي الكبير، وتحقق بملاقاة الشهود والعيان، ورجع إلى مولاه في كل أوان، فإن الصلاة حينئذٍ تكون له من قرّة العين. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-45-46-10","r":"q2-45-46","title":"2:45–46 · Patience, prayer and certainty of meeting God","text":"ولما أمرهم بالأصول والفروع، ذكَّرهم بالنعم، وخوفهم بالوعيد على عدم شكرها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-45-46-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-45-46-s1","r":"q2-45-46","title":"Patience, fasting and humility","text":"I say: patience ( الصبر ) is holding the heart fast to the Lord’s judgement. The word may retain its outward meaning, or here denote fasting, since fasting involves patience in abstaining from desires. Humility of the limbs ( الخشوع ) is their stillness and abasement; submission in the heart ( الخضوع ) is its yielding to the Lord’s judgement. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-03] ]","anchor":"en-q2-45-46-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-45-46-s2","r":"q2-45-46","title":"The disciplines that overcome love of rank","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: you who are afflicted by leadership and rank, and are too proud to submit to God’s judgements brought by His messengers, seek help against your own soul through patience in cutting off familiar habits and abandoning egoic shares and desires. At the root of their branching growth lies love of leadership and rank; whoever patiently abandons these wins God’s good pleasure. The hadith says, “In patience over what you dislike is much good.” The poet says: Patience is like aloes: bitter to the taste, but its consequences are sweeter than honey. Alternatively: seek help through fasting and prayer. Fasting breaks desire and purifies the soul; when purified of vices, the soul is adorned with virtues such as humility, fairness, reverence and the other noble qualities. Prayer contains spiritual and bodily forms of worship: purification, covering one’s nakedness, spending money on both, facing the Kaʿba, remaining devoted to worship, displaying humility with the limbs, making the heart’s intention sincere, striving against Satan, conversing intimately with the All-Merciful, reciting the Qurʾān, and withholding oneself from the two pleasures. [B040] Through prayer needs are fulfilled and afflictions repaired. Hence, when a matter troubled the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace, he took refuge in prayer. It is burdensome to the soul because it recurs each day and comes at the hour when sleep is sweet—except for the humble, in whose hearts its sweetness has settled. They converse with their Lord in it until it becomes the delight of their eyes. They are certain that they will meet their Lord and delight in beholding His noble Face; they are also certain of returning to Him through resurrection and gathering, for reward and punishment. The Real Most High here uses expectation ( الظن ) where certainty is intended out of consideration for sinners and indulgence towards the disobedient, who lack certainty’s purity. Had He mentioned unmixed certainty, they would have been excluded. Glory be to such a forbearing Lord, such a munificent, generous One! God, favour us with pure gnosis and certainty, so that no illusion or doubt stirs in our hearts, Lord of the worlds.","anchor":"en-q2-45-46-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-45-46-s3","r":"q2-45-46","title":"Persevering at the door of the Presence","text":"You who seek entry into God’s Presence, abase and humble yourself before His friends. Swallow the bitterness of patience in this so that they may bring you into His Presence. As the poet says: Humble yourself before the one you love: love is not easy. When the beloved is pleased, union is assured. Should love of leadership and rank prevent you, seek help through patience and prayer. Patience is the sign of victory, and prayer restrains indecency and wrongdoing. Keep knocking at the door until you enter with the beloveds. Perseverance in prayer is a weighty matter, except for one who reaches intimate converse with the Most High, the Great, realizes the meeting of witnessing and direct vision, and returns to his Master at every moment. Prayer then becomes the delight of his eye. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q2-45-46-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-45-46-s4","r":"q2-45-46","title":"","text":"Having commanded the foundations and branches, He reminds them of His blessings and warns them of the threatened consequence of failing to give thanks, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-45-46-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-47-48","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence 2:47–48","anchor":"unit-q2-47-48"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-1","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَنِّي فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى الْعالَمِينَ (47) وَاتَّقُوا يَوْماً لا تَجْزِي نَفْسٌ عَنْ نَفْسٍ شَيْئاً وَلا تُقْبَلُ مِنْها شَفاعَةٌ وَلا يُؤْخَذُ مِنْها عَدْلٌ وَلا هُمْ يُنْصَرُونَ (48)","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-2","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"قلت: العدل بالفتح: الفداء، وبالكسر: الحمل، وجملة لا تَجْزِي: صفة ليوم، والعائد محذوف، أي: لا تجزي فيه.","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-3","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ على آبائكم بالهداية وبعث الرسل، وَأَنِّي فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى الْعالَمِينَ: أهل زمانكم، فاذكروا هذه النعم واشكروني عليها بأن تتبعوا هذا النبيّ الجليل، الذي تجدونه مكتوباً عندكم في التوراة والإنجيل.","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-4","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"وخافوا يَوْماً لا تَقْضي فيه نَفْسٌ عَنْ نَفْسٍ شَيْئاً بحيث لا تجلِب لها نفعاً، ولا تدفع عنها ضرراً، ولا تقبل مِنْها شَفاعَةٌ إن وقعت الشفاعة فيها، ولا يؤخذ منها فداء، إن أرادت الفداء عنها، ولا تنتصر في دفع العذاب، إن أرادت الانتصار بعشيرتها. فانتفى عنها وجوه الامتناع من العذاب بأي وجه أمكن فإن الإنسان إذا أُخذ للنكال احتال على نفسه إما بالشفاعة، أو بالفداء إن لم تقبل الشفاعة فيه، أو بالانتصار بأقاربه، والآيةُ في الكفار، فلا حجةَ لمن ينفِي الشفاعة في عُصَاة المؤمنين، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-5","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"الإشارة: قد يتوجَّهُ العتاب إلى أهل الرئاسة والجاه، من العلماء والصالحين، وكل من خُصَّ بشرف أو خصوصية، فيقول لهم الحق تعالى: اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ بالعلم أو السيادة أو الصلاح، وبأن فضلتكم على أهل زمانكم، وخصصتكم من أبناء جنسكم فقد رُوِيَ: «أنَّ العبد يُحاسب على جاهه كما يُحاسب على ماله» . فمن صرفه في طاعة الله، وتواضع لعباد الله، وسعى في حوائجهم، وأبلغ الجهد في قضاء مآربهم، كان ذلك شكراً لنعمة الجاه فقد رُوِيَ في الحديث: «مَنْ سَعَى في حَاجَةِ أخيهِ المسْلِم، قُضِيتْ أو لَم تُقْضَ، غُفِر لَه ما تقدَم مِنْ ذنبه، وكُتب له براءتان: براءة من النار وبراءة من النفاق» .","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-6","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"ولا يأخذ على ذلك أجراً ولا جُعلاً فإنَّ ذلك سحت وربا، ومن تكبّر به وطغى، أو أخذ على ذلك أجراً، قيل له يوم القيامة: قد استوفيت أجرك فلا حظ لك عندنا، فلا تنفعه شفاعة، ولا يقبل منه فداء، ولا يقدر أن ينتصر من موارد الهوان والردى، ففي بعض الأخبار: يقول الله تعالى للفقراء الذين يعظمون في الدنيا لأجل فقرهم: ألم أرخص لكم الأسعار؟ ألم أوسع لكم المجالس؟ ألم أُعطِّف عليكم عبادي؟ فقد أخذتم أجركم في الدنيا. أو كما قال.","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-7","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-47-48-8","r":"q2-47-48","title":"2:47–48 · Gratitude for distinction and accountability for influence","text":"ثم ذكّر الحق تعالى بنى إسرائيل بنعمة أخرى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-47-48-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-47-48-s1","r":"q2-47-48","title":"Ransom and the omitted resumptive","text":"I say: ʿadl ( عَدل ), with fatḥa, is ransom; ʿidl ( عِدل ), with kasra, is a load. “No soul can avail…” qualifies “a day,” with the resumptive omitted: “on which no soul can avail another.”","anchor":"en-q2-47-48-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-47-48-s2","r":"q2-47-48","title":"The limits of intercession in this verse","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember My blessing upon your fathers through guidance and the sending of messengers, and My favouring you above the worlds—the people of your own time. Remember these blessings and thank Me by following this illustrious Prophet, whom you find recorded with you in the Torah and Gospel. Fear a day when one soul cannot discharge anything for another, neither securing it benefit nor warding off harm. No intercession is accepted on its behalf, should intercession be attempted; no ransom is taken, should ransom be offered; and it cannot obtain help against punishment by appealing to its clan. Every possible means of resisting punishment is thus excluded. When a person is seized for chastisement, he contrives to escape through intercession; if that is not accepted, through ransom; or through the support of relatives. The verse concerns unbelievers and therefore supplies no proof to those who deny intercession for sinful believers. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-47-48-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-47-48-s3","r":"q2-47-48","title":"The blessing and danger of social standing","text":"This reproach may be directed at scholars, righteous people and others possessing leadership, rank, honour or special distinction. The Real Most High tells them: remember My blessing of knowledge, precedence or righteousness, My preferring you over the people of your time and distinguishing you from your fellows. It is reported: “The servant is called to account for his standing as he is called to account for his wealth.” Whoever uses it in obedience to God, humbles himself before God’s servants, attends to their needs and strives to fulfil their purposes has given thanks for the blessing of influence. A hadith is reported: “Whoever strives to fulfil his Muslim brother’s need, whether it is fulfilled or not, has his past sins forgiven and receives two certificates of freedom: from the Fire and from hypocrisy.” [B041] He takes no wage or payment for this, for such gain is illicit consumption and usury. Whoever grows proud and tyrannical through his influence, or takes payment for it, is told on the Day of Resurrection: “You have already received your wage; you have no share with Us.” Intercession will not benefit him, no ransom will be accepted, and he cannot defend himself against the inroads of humiliation and ruin. In one report, God Most High says to the spiritual poor honoured in this world for their poverty: “Did I not lower prices for you? Did I not make room for you in assemblies? Did I not incline My servants kindly towards you? You have received your reward in the world”—or words to that effect. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-47-48-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-47-48-s4","r":"q2-47-48","title":"","text":"The Real Most High reminds the Children of Israel of another blessing, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-47-48-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-49","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age 2:49","anchor":"unit-q2-49"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-49-1","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"وَإِذْ نَجَّيْناكُمْ مِنْ آلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُومُونَكُمْ سُوءَ الْعَذابِ يُذَبِّحُونَ أَبْناءَكُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيُونَ نِساءَكُمْ وَفِي ذلِكُمْ بَلاءٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ عَظِيمٌ (49)","anchor":"ar-q2-49-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-49-2","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"قلت: (إذ) : معمول لا ذكروا، و (فرعون) : اسم لكل من ملك القبط، كما أن قيصر اسم لمن ملك الروم، وكسرى اسم لمن ملك الفرس، واسم (فرعون) الذي كان في زمن موسى عليه السلام: «مصعب بن ريان» ، وقيل: ابنه الوليد.","anchor":"ar-q2-49-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-49-3","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"وسَام يسُوم: طلب وبغى، يقال: سامه خسفاً إذا أولاه ظلماً، وجملة (يسومونكم) : حال من (آل فرعون) ، وجملة (يذبحون) : بيان لها. وسوء العذاب: أفظعه وأقبحه.","anchor":"ar-q2-49-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-49-4","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا بني إسرائيل اذكروا نعمة أخرى أنعمت بها على أسلافكم، وأنتم عالمون بها، وذلك حين أنجيناكم من عذاب فرعون ورهطه، يولونكم أقبحَ العذاب وأشنعَه، كانوا يستعبدون رجالكم ونساءكم في مشاق الخدمة والمهنة، ولمّا أخبره الكهان أنه سيخرج منكم ولد يُخَرِّب ملكه، جعل يذبح ذكوركم ويترك نساءكم، وفي ذلكم محنة مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وابتلاء عَظِيمٌ، أو في ذلك الإنجاء اختبار من ربكم عظيم، فاذكروا هذه النعمة، وتحصنوا بالإيمان بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم من محنة أخرى، ولا ينفع حذرٌ من قدر، وَكانَ أَمْرُ اللَّهِ قَدَراً مَقْدُوراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-49-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-49-5","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-49-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-49-6","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"الإشارة: لكل زمان فراعين وجبابرة يقطعون الناس عن الانقطاع إلى الله والدخول إلى حضرة الله، (ضَلَّ سَعْيُهُمْ فِى الحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَهُمْ يَحْسَبُونَ أنهم يُحسنون صنعا) ، يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للذين تخلصوا منهم: اذكروا نعمتي التي أنعمت عليكم بها حيث أنجيتكم من فراعين زمنكم، يسومونكم سوء العذاب وهو البقاء في غم الحجاب، والانقطاع عن الأحباب، يقتلون ما ربيتم من اليقين في قلوبكم والمعرفة في أسراركم، ويستحيون","anchor":"ar-q2-49-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-49-7","r":"q2-49","title":"2:49 · Deliverance from Pharaoh and the tyrannies of every age","text":"شهواتكم وحظوظكم، (وفي ذلكم بلاء من ربكم عظيم) . قال تعالى: وَإِنْ تُطِعْ أَكْثَرَ مَنْ فِي الْأَرْضِ يُضِلُّوكَ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ إِنْ يَتَّبِعُونَ إِلَّا الظَّنَّ.... وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-49-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-49-s1","r":"q2-49","title":"Pharaoh and the infliction of torment","text":"I say: idh ( إذ ), “when,” is governed by “remember.” Pharaoh is the title of anyone who ruled the Copts, just as Caesar designates the ruler of the Romans and Chosroes the ruler of the Persians. The Pharaoh in Moses’s time was named Muṣʿab ibn Rayyān, or, according to another account, his son al-Walīd. [B042] Sāma, yasūmu ( سام يسوم ) means to seek or pursue. One says, “He subjected him to abasement,” when he treated him unjustly. “Subjecting you” is circumstantial in relation to “Pharaoh’s people,” and “slaughtering” explains it. Grievous torment is its most appalling and ugly form.","anchor":"en-q2-49-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-49-s2","r":"q2-49","title":"A trial in affliction or in deliverance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember another blessing upon your forebears, known to you: We rescued you from the torment of Pharaoh and his people, who inflicted the ugliest and most terrible suffering upon you. They enslaved your men and women in arduous service and menial work. When the soothsayers told him that a child from among you would destroy his kingdom, he began slaughtering your males and sparing your women. In that was an affliction and mighty trial from your Lord; alternatively, the mighty trial lay in that deliverance. Remember this blessing and fortify yourselves through belief in Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, against another affliction. Caution does not avail against destiny: “God’s command is a determined decree” [33:38]. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-49-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-49-s3","r":"q2-49","title":"Those who obstruct the way to God","text":"Every age has pharaohs and tyrants who prevent people from severing attachments for God’s sake and entering His Presence: “Their striving goes astray in worldly life, while they suppose they do good work” [18:104]. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says to those freed from them: remember My blessing when I rescued you from the pharaohs of your time. They subjected you to grievous torment—remaining in the gloom of the veil and severance from the beloveds. They kill the certainty you have cultivated in your hearts and the gnosis in your innermost selves, while keeping alive your desires and egoic shares. “In that is a great trial from your Lord.” He says, “If you obey most of those on earth, they will lead you astray from God’s path; they follow only conjecture…” [6:116]. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q2-49-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-50","r":"q2-50","title":"2:50 · The divided sea and liberation from desire","text":"2:50 · The divided sea and liberation from desire 2:50","anchor":"unit-q2-50"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-50-1","r":"q2-50","title":"2:50 · The divided sea and liberation from desire","text":"وَإِذْ فَرَقْنا بِكُمُ الْبَحْرَ فَأَنْجَيْناكُمْ وَأَغْرَقْنا آلَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ (50)","anchor":"ar-q2-50-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-50-2","r":"q2-50","title":"2:50 · The divided sea and liberation from desire","text":"ثم ذكَّرهم الحق تعالى نعمة أخرى وهي فلق البحر وإغراق العدو، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-50-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-50-3","r":"q2-50","title":"2:50 · The divided sea and liberation from desire","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا أيضاً حين فَرَقْنا بسببكم الْبَحْرَ، حين فررتم من عدوكم، فسلكتم فيه اثنيْ عشر مسلكاً يابساً، حتى خلصتم إلى الشام، فلما أدرككم عدوُّكم، واسْتَتَمَّ دخولهُ فيه، أطبقنا عليهم البحر فَأَنْجَيْناكُمْ وَأَغْرَقْنا آلَ فِرْعَوْنَ وأنتم تعاينون غرقهم وهلاكهم، فاشكروا هذه النعم التي أنعمت بها على أسلافكم، واتبعوا أحسن ما أنزل إليكم من ربكم على نبي أُمي، لم يكن له علم بهذا، حتى علمه بالوحي من ربكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-50-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-50-4","r":"q2-50","title":"2:50 · The divided sea and liberation from desire","text":"الإشارة: قال بعض الحكماء: (الهوى بحر لا ساحل له إلا الموت) . فلا يقطع بحر الحظوظ والعوائد، إلا الخواص، الذين منَّ الله عليهم بسلوك الطريقة، والغرق في بحر الحقيقة، على يد رجال جمعوا بين الشريعة والحقيقة، فيقول الحق- جلّ جلاله- لمن تخلَّص من بحر هواه، وأفضى إلى مشاهدة مولاه: اذكروا نعمتي التي أنعمت عليكم حيث خلصتكم من بحر الشهوات والعوائد، وأطلعتكم على أسرار العلوم وذخائر الفوائد، وأغرقنا فيه من تكبر وطغى، وأنت تنظرون ما فيه الناس من غم الحجاب وسوء الحساب، في بحر لجى يغشاه موج الذنوب، من فوقه موج الحظوظ، من فوقه سحاب الأثر، إذا أخرج يده لم يكد يراها ومن لم يجعل اللهُ لَهُ نُورًا فَمَا له من نورٍ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-50-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-50-5","r":"q2-50","title":"2:50 · The divided sea and liberation from desire","text":"ثم ذكّرهم نعمة التوراة التي أنزلها على موسى، وفى ضمنه التوبيخ على عبادة العجل، فقال جل جلاله:","anchor":"ar-q2-50-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-50-s1","r":"q2-50","title":"Deliverance witnessed","text":"The Real Most High reminds them of another blessing: the dividing of the sea and drowning of the enemy. He says: The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember also when We divided the sea for your sake as you fled your enemy. You travelled through twelve dry pathways until you escaped towards Syria. When your enemy overtook you and had fully entered, We closed the sea upon them, delivering you and drowning Pharaoh’s people while you watched their drowning and destruction. Give thanks for these blessings upon your forebears and follow the best of what your Lord has sent down to you upon an unlettered Prophet. He had no knowledge of this until your Lord taught him through revelation.","anchor":"en-q2-50-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-50-s2","r":"q2-50","title":"Crossing the sea of customary attachments","text":"One of the sages said: “Caprice is an ocean whose only shore is death.” Only the elect cross the sea of egoic shares and habitual attachments: those whom God has favoured with travelling the Path and immersion in the ocean of Reality, at the hands of men who unite the Sacred Law and Reality. To one freed from the sea of his caprice and brought to witnessing his Master, the Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember My blessing when I freed you from the sea of desires and habits, disclosed to you the mysteries of the sciences and treasures of benefits, and drowned in it those who grew proud and transgressed. You see people suffering the gloom of the veil and an evil reckoning, in a deep sea covered by the wave of sins, above it the wave of egoic shares, and above that the cloud of created effects. When one stretches out his hand, he can scarcely see it: “He for whom God appoints no light has no light” [24:40]. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-50-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-50-s3","r":"q2-50","title":"","text":"He then reminds them of the blessing of the Torah sent down upon Moses, including within this a rebuke for worshipping the calf, saying, glorious is His majesty:","anchor":"en-q2-50-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-51-53","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence 2:51–53","anchor":"unit-q2-51-53"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-1","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"وَإِذْ واعَدْنا مُوسى أَرْبَعِينَ لَيْلَةً ثُمَّ اتَّخَذْتُمُ الْعِجْلَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ وَأَنْتُمْ ظالِمُونَ (51) ثُمَّ عَفَوْنا عَنْكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ذلِكَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ (52) وَإِذْ آتَيْنا مُوسَى الْكِتابَ وَالْفُرْقانَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ (53)","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-2","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"قلت: (أربعين) : مفعول لواعدنا، لا ظرف، و (العجل) : مفعول أول، والثاني محذوف، أي: اتخذتموه إلها، و (الفرقان) : معطوف على (الكتاب) .","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-3","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا أيضاً حين واعَدْنا مُوسى أن يصوم أَرْبَعِينَ لَيْلَةً بأيامها متواصلة، وذلك حين طلبتم منه أن ينزل عليه الكتاب فيه بيان الأحكام، ثم لما صامها، وهي: ذو القعدة وعشر ذي الحجة، وأتى إلى المناجاة، كفرتم، واتَّخَذْتُمُ الْعِجْلَ الذي صاغه السامِريُّ من الحُليّ، الذي أخذته نساء بني إسرائيل من القبط عارية، ففرّوا به ظنّاً منهم أنه حلال، فقال لهم هارون عليه السلام: لا يحل لكم، فطرحوه في حفرة، فصاغ منه السامري صورة العجل، وألقى في جوفه قبضة أخذها من تحت حافر فرس جبريل عليه السلام حين عبر معهم البحر، فجعل يخور، فقال السامري: هذا إِلهُكُمْ وَإِلهُ مُوسى، وَأَنْتُمْ ظالِمُونَ في عبادته، ثُمَّ عَفَوْنا عَنْكُمْ بالتوبة وقتل النفس على ما يأتي، لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ، فلا تعصون بنعمة، وَاذكروا أيضاً إِذْ آتَيْنا مُوسَى الْكِتابَ الذي طلبتم، وهو التوراة، وهو الْفُرْقانَ الذي فرقنا فيه بين الحق والباطل، كي تهتدوا إلى الصواب فتنجوا من العذاب.","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-4","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"الإشارة: ما زالت الأشياخ والأولياء الأقدمون ينتحلون طريق سيدنا موسى عليه السلام في استعمال هذه الأربعين، ينفردون فيها إلى مولاهم، مؤانسة ومناجاة، وفي ذلك يقول ابن الفارض رضى الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-5","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"وصِرْتُ مُوسَى زَمَاني ... مذ صارَ بَعْضِيَ كُلِّي","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-6","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"وقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-7","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"صارتْ جِبالِيَ دكًا ... مِنْ هَيْبَةِ المُتَجَلِّي","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-8","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"فيفارقون عشائرهم وأصحابهم في مناجاة الحبيب، والمؤانسة بالقريب، فمن أصحابهم مَن يبقى على عهده في حال غيبة شيخه، من المجاهدة والمشاهدة، ومنهم مَن تسرقه العاجلة فيرجع إلى عبادة عجل حظه وهواه فيظلم نفسه بمتابعة دنياه، فإن بادر بالتوبة والإقلاع، ورجع إلى حضرة شيخه بالاستماع والاتباع، وقع عنه العفو والغفران، ورجا ما كان يؤمله من المشاهدة والعيان، وإلا باء بالعقوبة والخسران، وكل مَن اعتزل عن الأحباب والعشائر والأصحاب، طالباً جمع قلبه، ورضى ربه، فلا بد أن ترد عليه أسرار ربانية ومواهب لدنية، من لدن حكيم عليم، يظهر بها الحق، ويدفع بها الباطل، فيفرق بين الحق والباطل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-51-53-9","r":"q2-51-53","title":"2:51–53 · The forty nights and fidelity during the guide’s absence","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى كيفية توبة من عبد العجل منهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-51-53-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-51-53-s1","r":"q2-51-53","title":"The appointed period and the omitted object","text":"I say: “forty” ( أربعين ) is the object of “We appointed,” not an adverbial expression. “The calf” is the first object, while the second is omitted: “you took it as a god.” “The Criterion” is coordinated with “the Book.”","anchor":"en-q2-51-53-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-51-53-s2","r":"q2-51-53","title":"The calf and the gift of the Torah","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when We appointed for Moses forty consecutive nights, with their days, to fast. This followed your request that a Book explaining the judgements be sent down upon him. When he had fasted them—Dhū al-Qaʿda and ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijja—and came to intimate converse, you disbelieved and took the calf for worship. Al-Sāmirī had fashioned it from jewellery borrowed by the Israelite women from the Copts. They fled with it, supposing it lawful. Aaron, peace be upon him, told them, “It is not lawful for you,” so they cast it into a pit. Al-Sāmirī shaped it into a calf and cast into its hollow a handful taken from beneath the hoof of Gabriel’s horse when he crossed the sea with them. It began to low. Al-Sāmirī said, “This is your god and Moses’s god” [20:88]. You wronged yourselves by worshipping it. Then We pardoned you through repentance and the killing that will be explained, so that you might give thanks and not use a blessing to disobey. Remember also when We gave Moses the Book you requested, the Torah: it is the Criterion by which We distinguished truth from falsehood, so that you might be guided to what is right and escape punishment.","anchor":"en-q2-51-53-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-51-53-s3","r":"q2-51-53","title":"Forty-day withdrawal and the disciple’s fidelity","text":"The early shaykhs and friends of God have continued to follow our master Moses’s path in observing these forty days, withdrawing to their Master in intimacy and converse. In this connection Ibn al-Fāriḍ, God be pleased with him, says: I became the Moses of my time when my part became my whole. And: My mountains became level dust in awe of the One disclosing Himself. [B043] They leave their families and companions to converse with the Beloved and find intimacy with the Near One. Some companions remain faithful in their shaykh’s absence, continuing their striving and witnessing. Others are stolen away by the immediate world and return to worshipping the calf of their own share and desire, wronging themselves through following worldly life. If such a person hastens to repent and desist, returning to his shaykh’s presence with listening and obedience, pardon and forgiveness come to him, and he may hope again for the witnessing and direct vision he sought. Otherwise he incurs punishment and loss. Whoever withdraws from beloveds, family and companions, seeking the gathering of his heart and his Lord’s pleasure, necessarily receives divine mysteries and directly bestowed gifts from a Wise and Knowing One. Through these he manifests truth, repels falsehood, and distinguishes the two. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-51-53-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-51-53-s4","r":"q2-51-53","title":"","text":"The Real Most High explains how those who worshipped the calf repented, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-51-53-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-54","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self 2:54","anchor":"unit-q2-54"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-1","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وَإِذْ قالَ مُوسى لِقَوْمِهِ يا قَوْمِ إِنَّكُمْ ظَلَمْتُمْ أَنْفُسَكُمْ بِاتِّخاذِكُمُ الْعِجْلَ فَتُوبُوا إِلى بارِئِكُمْ فَاقْتُلُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ ذلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ عِنْدَ بارِئِكُمْ فَتابَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِنَّهُ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ (54)","anchor":"ar-q2-54-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-2","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"قلت: البارئ هو: المقدر للأشياء والمظهر لها.","anchor":"ar-q2-54-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-3","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا يا بني إسرائيل حين قالَ موسى لِقَوْمِهِ لما رجع من الطور، ووجدهم قد عبدوا العجل: يَا قَوْمِ إِنَّكُمْ ظَلَمْتُمْ أَنْفُسَكُمْ وبخستموها بِاتِّخاذِكُمُ الْعِجْلَ إلاهكم، فَتُوبُوا إِلى خالقكم الذي صوركم في أحسن تقويم، فَاقْتُلُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ بهدم هذه البنية التي ركبتها في أحسن صورة، فبخستموها، ولم تعرفوا قدرها، فعبدتم أبلد الحيوان، الذي هو البقرة. من لم يعرف حق النعمة فحقيق أن تُسترد منه.","anchor":"ar-q2-54-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-4","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"فذلكم القتل والمبادرة إلى التوبة خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ عِندَ خالقكم، لأنه يفضي إلى الحياة الدائمة والبهجة السرمدية، فلما صعب عليكم القتل للشفقة على الأخ أو القريب، ألقينا عليكم ضبابة حتى أظلم المكان، فاقتتلتم من الغداة إلى العشي، فدعا موسى وهارون- عليهما السلام- بالكشف عنهم، فرفعت السحابة، وقد قُتل سبعون ألفاً، ففعلتم ذلك القتل، فتاب الحق تعالى عليكم، فقبل توبة مَن بقي منكم، وعفا عمن مات إِنَّهُ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ أي: كثير التوفيق للتوبة، أو كثير قبولها، الرحيم بعباده المؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q2-54-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-5","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"الإشارة: ما قاله سيدنا موسى عليه السلام لقومه، يقال مثله لمن عبد هواه، وعكف على متابعة دنياه: يا من بخس نفسه بإرخاء العنان في متابعة هواها، حتى حرمها من مشاهدة جمال مولاها، تُب إلى ربك، وانتبه من غفلتك، واقتل نفسك بمخالفة هواها، فلعلها تحيا بمشاهدة مولاها، فما دامت النفس موجودة، وحظوظها لديها مشهودة، وآمالها ممدودة، كيف تطمع أن تدخل حضرة الله، وتتمتع بشهود جماله وسناه؟!","anchor":"ar-q2-54-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-6","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"إنْ تُرِدَ وَصْلَنَا فَمَوْتكَ شَرْطٌ ... لا يَنَالُ الوِصَالَ مَنْ فيهِ فَضْلَهْ(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-54-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-7","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وقال الحلاجُ في هذا المعنى:","anchor":"ar-q2-54-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-8","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"لَمْ أُسْلِم النفسَ للأسقامِ تُتْلِفُها ... إلاَّ لِعِلْمِي بأَنَّ الوصْلَ يُحْيِيهَا","anchor":"ar-q2-54-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-9","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وقال أيضاً:","anchor":"ar-q2-54-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-10","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"أُقتُلوني يا ثقاتي ... إِنَّ في قَتْلِي حَياتِي","anchor":"ar-q2-54-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-11","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وحَيَاتي في مَماتِي ... وممَاتي في حَياتي","anchor":"ar-q2-54-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-12","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"أنا عندي: مَحْوُ ذَاتي ... من أجَلِّ المكْرُمَاتِ","anchor":"ar-q2-54-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-13","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وبَقَائِي في صِفاتي ... مِنْ قبيح السيّئات","anchor":"ar-q2-54-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-14","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وقال أيضاً:","anchor":"ar-q2-54-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-15","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"إنْ كان سَفْكُ دَمي أقْصَى مُرادِكُمُ ... فَمَا غَلَتْ نظرةٌ مِنكُم بِسَفْك دَمِي","anchor":"ar-q2-54-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-16","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وقال الشيخ أبو العباس المرسي رضى الله عنه: (لا يدخل على الله إلا من بابين، أحدهما: الموت الحسي، وهو الموت الطبيعي، والآخر: الموت الذي تعنيه هذه الطائفة) . هـ. وهو موت النفوس، فمن لم تمت نفسه لم تَحْيَى روحه.","anchor":"ar-q2-54-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-17","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"وقال بعض العارفين: (لا يحصل الدخول على الله حتى يموت أربع موتات: موت أحمر، وموت أسود، وموت أبيض، وموت أخضر. أما الموت الأحمر فهو مخالفة الهوى، وأما الموت الأسود فهو تحمل الأذى، وأما الموت الأبيض فهو الجوع- أي: المتوسط- وأما الموت الأخضر فهو لبس المرقعات، وطرح الرقاع بعضها على بعض) .","anchor":"ar-q2-54-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-18","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"قلت: ورأس الهوى وعنصره هو حب الجاه وطلب الرئاسة. فمن نزل إلى أرض الخمول، وخرق عوائد نفسه فيه، انخرقت له الحجب، ولاحت له الأنوار، وأشرقت عليه الأسرار في مدة قريبة، وبالله التوفيق وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-54-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-54-19","r":"q2-54","title":"2:54 · Repentance and the four deaths of the lower self","text":"ثم وبخهم الحق تعالى على طلب الرؤية قبل إبانها، وقبل تحصيل شروطها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-54-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-54-s1","r":"q2-54","title":"The Maker","text":"I say: the Maker ( البارئ ) is He who determines things and brings them forth.","anchor":"en-q2-54-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-54-s2","r":"q2-54","title":"The prescribed repentance in Moses’s community","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember when Moses returned from the Mount, found his people worshipping the calf, and told them: “My people, you have wronged and debased yourselves by taking the calf as your god. Repent to your Creator, who fashioned you in the finest form, and kill one another”—destroying this bodily structure I fashioned so beautifully, but which you debased by failing to recognize its worth and worshipping the dullest animal, the cow. One who fails to recognize the right of a blessing deserves to have it withdrawn. That killing and haste to repent are better for you in your Creator’s sight, because they lead to everlasting life and perpetual joy. When killing became difficult through compassion for brother or kinsman, We cast a mist over you until the place grew dark. You fought one another from morning to evening. Moses and Aaron, peace be upon them, prayed that the cloud be lifted; it was raised when seventy thousand had been killed. You carried out the killing, and the Real Most High turned towards you, accepting the repentance of those remaining and pardoning the dead. He is the Ever-Relenting—abundant in enabling repentance or accepting it—and merciful towards His believing servants.","anchor":"en-q2-54-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-54-s3","r":"q2-54","title":"Dying to caprice, not destroying the body","text":"What our master Moses told his people is likewise said to someone who worships his caprice and persists in following his worldly desire: you who have debased your soul by giving it free rein to follow its inclination, depriving it of witnessing its Master’s beauty, repent to your Lord and awaken from heedlessness. Kill your lower self by opposing its desire, so that it may live through witnessing its Master. So long as the lower self remains present, its shares held in view and its hopes extended, how can you expect to enter God’s Presence and delight in witnessing His beauty and radiance? [B044] If you desire union with Us, your death is the condition: one in whom a remnant remains does not attain union. Al-Ḥallāj says in this sense: I only surrendered the soul to consuming sicknesses because I knew that union would revive it. And also: Kill me, my trusted friends: in my killing lies my life. My life is in my death, and my death is in my life. The effacing of my self, to me, is among the greatest acts of generosity; my remaining in my own attributes is among the ugly wrongs. He also says: If shedding my blood is your utmost desire, a glance from you is not dearly bought by shedding it. Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mursī, God be pleased with him, says: “God is entered upon through only two doors: sensory death, which is natural death, and the death intended by this company.” End of quotation. It is the death of the lower selves: one whose lower self has not died has no living spirit. One of the gnostics said: “Entry unto God is not attained until one has died four deaths: red, black, white and green. Red death is opposing caprice; black death is enduring injury; white death is hunger”—meaning moderate hunger—“and green death is wearing patched garments, laying patches one upon another.” I say: the head and root of caprice is love of rank and pursuit of leadership. Whoever descends to the earth of obscurity and breaks his soul’s customary habits there has the veils torn apart, the lights disclosed, and the mysteries shine upon him in a short time. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q2-54-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-54-s4","r":"q2-54","title":"","text":"The Real Most High rebukes them for demanding the vision before its time and before fulfilling its conditions, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-54-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-55-56","r":"q2-55-56","title":"2:55–56 · The thunderbolt and revival after effacement","text":"2:55–56 · The thunderbolt and revival after effacement 2:55–56","anchor":"unit-q2-55-56"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-55-56-1","r":"q2-55-56","title":"2:55–56 · The thunderbolt and revival after effacement","text":"وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَا مُوسى لَنْ نُؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّى نَرَى اللَّهَ جَهْرَةً فَأَخَذَتْكُمُ الصَّاعِقَةُ وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ (55) ثُمَّ بَعَثْناكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَوْتِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ (56)","anchor":"ar-q2-55-56-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-55-56-2","r":"q2-55-56","title":"2:55–56 · The thunderbolt and revival after effacement","text":"قلت: (جهرة) : مصدر نرى لأنه نوع منه، أي: نرى الله رؤية عيان، أو حال من الفاعل أي: نراه معاينين له، أو من المفعول أي: نراه معاينة.","anchor":"ar-q2-55-56-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-55-56-3","r":"q2-55-56","title":"2:55–56 · The thunderbolt and revival after effacement","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا أيضاً، يا بني إسرائيل، حين قلتم لموسى عليه السلام لما رجع من الطور، ووجدكم قد عبدتم العجل، فأخذ منكم سبعين رجلاً ممن لم يعبد العجل، وذهب يعتذر، فلما سمعتم كلامي أنكرتموه وحرفتموه، وقلتم: لَنْ نُؤْمِنَ لَكَ أن هذا كلام الله حَتَّى نَرَى اللَّهَ جَهْرَةً فَأَخَذَتْكُمُ الصَّاعِقَةُ بسبب طلبكم ما لا طاقة لكم به، فغبتم عن إحساسكم، وذهبت أرواحكم، وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ ما فعل بكم، فاستشفع فيكم موسى عليه السلام وقال: يا رَبِّ لَوْ شِئْتَ أَهْلَكْتَهُمْ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَإِيَّايَ أَتُهْلِكُنا بِما فَعَلَ السُّفَهاءُ مِنَّا، كيف أرجع إلى قومي بغير هؤلاء؟ ثُمَّ بَعَثْناكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَوْتِكُمْ، وعشتم زماناً بعد ذلك لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ هذه النعمة، وتقومون بحسن الخدمة، فتقروا بربوبيتي، وتصدقوا برسلي، فلم تفعلوا.","anchor":"ar-q2-55-56-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-55-56-4","r":"q2-55-56","title":"2:55–56 · The thunderbolt and revival after effacement","text":"الإشارة: من شأن الأرواح الطيبة التشوق إلى الحضرة، والتشوف إلى العيان والنظرة، فلا يحصل لها كمال التصديق والإيقان إلا بعد الشهود والعيان، فلما علم الحق سبحانه من بعض الأرواح صدق الطلب، رفع عنها الحجاب، وفتح لها الباب، فأخذتها صاعقة الدهشة والحيرة، ولم تطق صدمة المشاهدة والنظرة، فغابت عن الأشكال والرسوم في مشاهدة أنوار الحي القيوم، ثم مَنَّ عليها بالبعث من موت الفناء إلى حياة البقاء، فأمنت من الشقاء، فحصلت لها الحياة الدائمة والسعادة السرمدية. فالصاعقة عند أهل الفن هي عبارة عن الغيبة عن النفس، وفناء دائرة الحس، وهي شهود عدمك لوجود الحق، والبعث منها هو مقام البقاء، وهو شهود الأثر بالله. وهو مقام حق اليقين. وحاصله: شهود وجود الحق وحده، لا عدمك ولا وجودك، «كان الله ولا شيء معه، وهو الآن على ما عليه كان» . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-55-56-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-55-56-5","r":"q2-55-56","title":"2:55–56 · The thunderbolt and revival after effacement","text":"ثم ذكّرهم الحق لطفه بهم فى حال التيه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-55-56-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-55-56-s1","r":"q2-55-56","title":"Open vision","text":"I say: “openly” ( جهرة ) functions as the verbal noun of “we see,” because it denotes one kind of seeing: “we see God with direct vision.” Alternatively, it is a circumstantial expression referring to the agent—seeing Him face to face—or to the object—seeing Him openly presented to vision.","anchor":"en-q2-55-56-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-55-56-s2","r":"q2-55-56","title":"The demand for sight and Moses’s intercession","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember what you told Moses after he returned from the Mount and found you worshipping the calf. He chose seventy men who had not worshipped it and went to offer an apology. When you heard My speech, you denied and distorted it, saying, “We shall not believe your claim that this is God’s speech until we see God openly.” The thunderbolt seized you because you demanded what you lacked the capacity to bear. You lost sensory awareness and your spirits departed while you witnessed what was done to you. Moses interceded for you: “Lord, had You willed, You could have destroyed them and me before. Will You destroy us for what the foolish among us have done?” [7:155]. How could he return to his people without them? We then raised you after your death, and you lived for a time thereafter, so that you might thank Us for this blessing and render good service, acknowledging My lordship and affirming My messengers. But you did not.","anchor":"en-q2-55-56-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-55-56-s3","r":"q2-55-56","title":"Effacement and the truth of certainty","text":"Pure spirits naturally long for the Presence and yearn for direct sight and vision. They attain complete affirmation and certainty only after witnessing and direct vision. When the Real—glory be to Him—knows the sincerity of some spirits’ seeking, He raises the veil and opens the door. The thunderbolt of amazement and bewilderment seizes them: unable to bear the shock of witnessing and vision, they are absent from forms and outward traces in witnessing the lights of the Living, the Self-Subsisting. He then favours them with resurrection from the death of effacement ( الفناء ) to the life of subsistence ( البقاء ). Secure from misery, they attain enduring life and everlasting felicity. For the people of this art, the thunderbolt signifies absence from the self and the passing away of the sphere of sense perception: witnessing your non-being before the existence of the Real. Resurrection from it is the station of subsistence, witnessing the created effect through God. This is the station of the truth of certainty ( حق اليقين ): its outcome is witnessing the existence of the Real alone, neither your non-being nor your being. “God was, and nothing was with Him; He is now as He was.” Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-55-56-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-55-56-s4","r":"q2-55-56","title":"","text":"The Real reminds them of His kindness during their wandering, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-55-56-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-57","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit 2:57","anchor":"unit-q2-57"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-1","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"وَظَلَّلْنا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمامَ وَأَنْزَلْنا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوى كُلُوا مِنْ طَيِّباتِ ما رَزَقْناكُمْ وَما ظَلَمُونا وَلكِنْ كانُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُونَ (57)","anchor":"ar-q2-57-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-2","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"قلت: (الغّمّامّ) : السحاب الرقيق، و (المَنِّ) هنا: العسل، و (والسّلوى) قيل: اللحم، والأصح: أنه اسم طائر كالسماني.","anchor":"ar-q2-57-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-3","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في تذكير بني إسرائيل ما أنعم به عليهم في حال التيه: وَقد ظَلَّلْنا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمامَ يقيكم من الحر في أيام التيه، وَأَنْزَلْنا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وهو عسل كان ينزل على الشجر من الفجر إلى الطلوع، فيغرفون منه ما شاءوا، وَأنزلنا عليكم السَّلْوى، وهو طير كانت تحشره الجنوب، فينزل عليهم، فياخذون منه ما شاءوا، ولا يمتنع منهم، فيذبحون ويأكلون لحماً طريّاً، فقلنا لهم: كُلُوا مِنْ طَيِّباتِ ما رَزَقْناكُمْ وَما ظَلَمُونا بمخالفتهم أمْرَ نبيهم وسوء أدبهم معه، حيث قالوا: فَاذْهَبْ أَنْتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقاتِلا إِنَّا هاهُنا قاعِدُونَ، فعاقبهم بالتيه أربعين سنة، يتيهون في مقدار خمسة فراسخ أو ستة. وَلكِنْ ظلموا أنفسهم حيث أوقعوها في البلاء والمحنة.","anchor":"ar-q2-57-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-4","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"رُوِيَ أنهم لما أُمروا بجهاد الجبارين، جبنوا وقالوا تلك المقالة، فدعا عليهم سيدنا موسى عليه السلام فوقعوا في التيه بين مصر والشام، فكانوا يمشون النهار فيبيتون حيث أصبحوا، ويمشون الليل فيصبحون حيث أمسوا، فقالوا","anchor":"ar-q2-57-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-5","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"لموسى عليه السلام: من لنا بالطعام؟ فأنزل الله عليهم المنّ والسلوى، قالوا: كيف بحر الشمس؟ فظلل عليهم الغمام، قالوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-57-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-6","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"بم نستصبح بالليل؟ فضرب لهم عمود نور في وسط محلتهم، قالوا: من لنا بالماء؟ فأمر موسى عليه السلام بضرب الحجر، فقالوا: من لنا باللباس؟ فأعطوا ألا يَبْلى لهم ثوب، ولا يَخْلَق، ولا يَدْرن، وأن ينمو بنمو صاحبه، وقيل:","anchor":"ar-q2-57-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-7","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"كساهم مثل الظفر، وَاللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ.","anchor":"ar-q2-57-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-8","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"الإشارة: لما انفصلت الأرواح من عالم الجبروت، كانت على الطهارة الأصلية، والنزاهة الأزلية، عالمة بأسرار الربوبية وعظمة الألوهية، لكن لم يكن لها إلا جنة الحرية، دون جنة العبودية، فلما أراد الحق تعالى أن يمتعها بجنتين عن يمين وشمال، أمرها بالنزول إلى أرض العبودية، في ظلل من غمام البشرية، فمنَّ عليها بحلاوة المشاهدات وسلوان المناجاة، وقال لها: كلوا مِنْ طَيِّباتِ ما رَزَقْناكُمْ من طرائف العلوم، وفواكه الفهوم، هذا لمن اعتنى بروحه فاستكمل فضيلتها، وخالف هواها، فنفذت من عالم الأشباح إلى عالم الأرواح، فلم تنحجب بسحب الآثار إلى نفوذ شهود الأنوار، بل غابت عن شهود الآثار بشهود الأنوار. أما من حجبت عن شهود الأنوار بالوقوف مع الآثار، ووقعت في شبكة الحظوظ والشهوات، وربطت بعقال الأسباب والعادات، فقد ظلمت نفسها، وبخست حقها من مشاهدة مولاها، حتى اتسعت عليها دائرة الحس، ولم تنفذ إلى المشاهدة والأنس. وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-57-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-9","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"كَمِّلْ حقيقتك التي لم تكمُلِ ... والجسمَ ضَعْهُ في الحضِيض الأسفلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-57-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-10","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"أَتُكَمِّلُ الفَانِي وَتَتْرُك باقياً ... هَمَلاً، وأَنت بأمرِه لم تحفلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-57-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-11","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"فالجسمُ للنفس النفيسةِ آلةٌ ... ما لَمْ تُحَصِّلْه بها لم يحْصُلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-57-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-12","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"يَفْنَى، وتَبقى دائماً في غِبْطةٍ ... أو شِقْوةٍ وندامة لا تنْجَلِي","anchor":"ar-q2-57-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-13","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"أعطيت جسمك خادما فخدمته ... أَتُمَلِّكُ المفضولَ رِقَّ الأفضلِ؟","anchor":"ar-q2-57-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-14","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"شَرَكٌ كثيفٌ أنتَ في أحباله ... مادام يُمكنك الخَلاصَ فَعَجِّلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-57-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-15","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"مَنْ يستطيعُ بلوغَ أَعْلَى مَنزلٍ ... ما بالَهُ يرضَى بأدنَى منزل!","anchor":"ar-q2-57-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-57-16","r":"q2-57","title":"2:57 · Manna, quails and the two gardens of the spirit","text":"ثم وبَّخهم على ما وقع منهم من المخالفة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-57-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-57-s1","r":"q2-57","title":"Cloud, manna and quails","text":"I say: ghamām ( الغمام ) is thin cloud. Manna ( المنّ ) here is honey. Salwā ( السلوى ) is said to mean meat; more correctly, it is the name of a bird resembling the quail.","anchor":"en-q2-57-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-57-s2","r":"q2-57","title":"Provision in the wandering","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, reminds the Children of Israel of His blessings during the wandering: We shaded you with clouds to protect you from the heat, and sent down manna, honey descending on the trees from dawn until sunrise, from which you scooped as much as you wished. We sent down salwā , birds gathered by the south wind and brought down upon you. You took as many as you wished, without their resisting, slaughtering them and eating fresh meat. We said: “Eat of the good things We have provided.” They did not wrong Us by disobeying their prophet and behaving discourteously towards him, saying, “Go, you and your Lord, and fight; we are sitting here” [5:24]. He punished them with forty years of wandering within five or six parasangs. They wronged themselves, bringing their own souls into affliction and trial. It is related that, when commanded to fight the tyrants, they grew cowardly and made that reply. Our master Moses prayed against them and they fell into the wandering between Egypt and Syria. They walked by day but spent the night where they had begun the morning; they walked by night but reached morning where they had begun the evening. They asked Moses, “Who will provide our food?” God sent manna and quails. “What of the sun’s heat?” He shaded them with clouds. “How shall we have light at night?” A pillar of light was set in the middle of their encampment. “Who will give us water?” Moses was commanded to strike the stone. “Who will provide clothing?” They were granted garments that neither wore out, grew old nor became dirty, and that grew with their wearers. Alternatively, they were clothed in a covering like a fingernail. God has power over all things.","anchor":"en-q2-57-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-57-s3","r":"q2-57","title":"Freedom, servanthood and the body’s rightful place","text":"When the spirits separated from the world of the jabarūt, they possessed original purity and primordial freedom from defilement, knowing the mysteries of lordship and the greatness of divinity. They had only the garden of freedom, however, not the garden of servanthood. When the Real Most High wished them to enjoy two gardens, to right and left, He commanded them to descend to the earth of servanthood beneath the clouds of human embodiment. He favoured them with the sweetness of witnessing and the solace of intimate converse, telling them: eat of the good things We have provided—the rare treasures of sciences and fruits of understanding. This applies to one who cares for his spirit, perfects its excellence, and opposes its caprice, so that it penetrates from the world of bodily forms to the world of spirits. The clouds of created effects do not prevent it from penetrating to witness the lights; rather, in witnessing the lights it is absent from witnessing effects. [Translator’s note: Cairo I:110 prints فلم تنحجب بسحب الآثار إلى نفوذ شهود الأنوار. The connection made by إلى (“to”) within this negative clause is unclear. The following contrast establishes the intended opposition between witnessing lights and being veiled by effects. Ibn ʿAjība’s Īqāẓ al-himam (ed. al-Kayyālī, 1437/2016, p. 230, ḥikma 110) likewise describes the clouds of effects clearing so that light shines and the heart is absent from forms. This supports the contextual English, but does not explain the exact preposition or establish an emendation.] A spirit veiled from the lights by stopping at effects, caught in the net of egoic shares and desires, and tethered by secondary causes and habits has wronged itself and diminished its rightful share of witnessing its Master. The sphere of sense perception expands over it, and it does not penetrate to witnessing and intimacy. The following verses are recited: Perfect your reality, still imperfect, and put the body in the lowest place. Will you perfect what passes away and leave what endures neglected, taking no heed of its concern? The body is an instrument for the precious soul: what you do not acquire through it is not acquired. It perishes, while you remain for ever in joy, or misery and unrelenting regret. You were given your body as a servant, yet served it: will you give the inferior mastery over the superior? It is a thick net, and you are in its cords: while escape is possible, hasten! One capable of reaching the highest dwelling— why is he content with the lowest?","anchor":"en-q2-57-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-57-s4","r":"q2-57","title":"","text":"He then rebukes their disobedience, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-57-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-58-59","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility 2:58–59","anchor":"unit-q2-58-59"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-1","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"وَإِذْ قُلْنَا ادْخُلُوا هذِهِ الْقَرْيَةَ فَكُلُوا مِنْها حَيْثُ شِئْتُمْ رَغَداً وَادْخُلُوا الْبابَ سُجَّداً وَقُولُوا حِطَّةٌ نَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ خَطاياكُمْ وَسَنَزِيدُ الْمُحْسِنِينَ (58) فَبَدَّلَ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا قَوْلاً غَيْرَ الَّذِي قِيلَ لَهُمْ فَأَنْزَلْنا عَلَى الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا رِجْزاً مِنَ السَّماءِ بِما كانُوا يَفْسُقُونَ (59)","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-2","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"قلت: (حِطة) : خبر مبتدأ مضمر، أي: أمرنا حطة، أي: تواضع وانحطاط، وقال هنا: (فكلوا) ، وفي الأعراف بالواو لأن الأكل مرتب على الدخول، بخلاف السكنى، فإنها تفارق الأكل، فكأنه مأمور به.","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-3","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا يا بني إسرائيل حين قلنا لأسلافكم بعد أن خرجوا من التيه: ادْخُلُوا هذِهِ الْقَرْيَةَ أعني بيت المقدس، أو أريحا، بعد أن تُجاهدوا أهلها، فَكُلُوا من نعم ما فيها أكلاً واسعاً لأنها مخصبة، وَادْخُلُوا باب القرية راكعين، تواضعاً وشكراً، وَقُولُوا في دخولكم: شأننا حِطَّةٌ، أي: شأننا الانحطاط والتواضع لله، فإن فعلتم ذلك نَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ خَطاياكُمْ، وَسَنَزِيدُ من امتثل أمرنا، وأحسن الأدب معنا، خيراً كثيراً، في الدنيا والآخرة، فَبَدَّلَ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا منهم قولا غيْر الَّذِي أمروا به، وقالوا مكان حطة: حنطة، حبة في شعرة، فَأَنْزَلْنا عَلَى الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا رِجْزاً عذاباً مِنَ السَّماءِ قيل: هو الطاعون، فمات منهم سبعون ألفاً في يوم واحد، بسبب فسقهم وتعديهم الحدود.","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-4","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق سبحانه للأرواح، لما كمل تطهيرها من البقايا، وتكاملت فيها المزايا: ادخلوا هذه الحضرة المقدسة، وتنعموا فيها حيث شئتم بالمشاهدة، والمكالمة، والمواجهة، والمساورة، والمفاتحة، والمناجاة، وادخلوا بابها أذلاء صاغرين، فلا دخول للحضرة المقدسة إلا من باب الذل والافتقار، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-5","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"ومَا رُمتُ الدخولَ عليهِ حتَّى ... حَلَلْتُ مَحَلَّةَ العبدِ الذليلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-6","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"وأَغمضْتُ الجفُونَ على قَذَاها ... وصُنْت النَّفْسَ عن قالٍ وقيلِ(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-7","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"وقيل لأبي يزيد: يا أبا يزيد، خزائننا معمورة بالخدمة، ائتني من كُوّة الذل والافتقار. وفي رواية قيل له: يا أبا يزيد: تقرب إلينا بما ليس عندنا، فقال: يا رب وما الذي ليس عندك؟ فقال: الذل والافتقار. هـ. وقال شيخ المشايخ القطب الجيلاني رضى الله عنه (أتيت الأبواب كلها، فوجدت عليها الزحام، فأتيت من باب الذل والافتقار، فوجدته خالياً، فدخلت منه، وقلت: هلموا) . أو كما قال. وقال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-8","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"تذلَّلْ لمَن تَهْوَى فَلَيْسَ الْهَوى سَهْلُ(2) ... إِذَا رَضِيَ المحبوبُ صَحّ لكَ الوّصْلُ","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-9","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"وقولوا عند دخولكم الحضرة: شأننا حطة أي: شأننا السفليات دون العلويات، فالسلوك من باب السفليات واجب، وإلا فلا وصول، فكل مَن سلك من باب السفليات طهر من البقايا، وتكاملت فيه المزايا، فيصلح لدخول الحضرة،","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-10","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"وينخرط في سلك أهل الشهود والنظرة، فيكون من المحسنين المقربين، فلا جرم أن الله يزيده ترقياً في العلوم والأسرار، في هذه الدار، وفي تلك الدار، بخلاف مَن خالف ما أُمر به من سلوك طريق السفليات، وتعاطي الأمور العلويات، قبل كمال التربية فإنه يرجع إلى غم الحجاب، وسوء الحساب بسبب خروجه عن طريق الأحباب، وسلوكه طريق أهل الغفلة والارتياب. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-58-59-11","r":"q2-58-59","title":"2:58–59 · Entering through humility","text":"ثم ذكَّرهم بنعمة الماء الذي سقاهم فى التيه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-58-59-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-58-59-s1","r":"q2-58-59","title":"Ḥiṭṭa and the relation between entering and eating","text":"I say: ḥiṭṭa ( حطة ) is the predicate of an implied subject: “Our affair is abasement,” that is, humility and lowering ourselves. Here He says “then eat” with fā , whereas in al-Aʿrāf He uses wāw : eating follows upon entering, unlike dwelling, which can occur apart from eating, so eating is as though independently commanded. [B045]","anchor":"en-q2-58-59-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-58-59-s2","r":"q2-58-59","title":"Courtesy in receiving a blessing","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember when, after your forebears left the wandering, We told them: enter this town—Jerusalem or Jericho—after fighting its people, and eat abundantly of its blessings, for it is fertile. Enter its gate bowing in humility and gratitude. On entering, say, “Our affair is ḥiṭṭa ”: our condition is to lower and humble ourselves before God. If you do so, We forgive your offences and add much good in this world and the Hereafter for those who obey Our command and show good courtesy towards Us. The wrongdoers among them substituted another saying: instead of ḥiṭṭa , they said ḥinṭa , “wheat,” and “a grain in a hair.” We sent down upon the wrongdoers a scourge, a punishment from heaven, said to have been plague. Seventy thousand died in a single day because of their transgression and exceeding the limits.","anchor":"en-q2-58-59-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-58-59-s3","r":"q2-58-59","title":"The unfrequented door of need","text":"Once spirits are fully purified of residual selfhood and their excellences complete, the Real—glory be to Him—says: enter this holy Presence and delight as you wish in witnessing, discourse, face-to-face encounter, musāwara [a figurative encounter whose precise force remains uncertain], opening address and secret converse [Translator’s note: Cairo I:111 reads al-musāwara . Ibn ʿAjība also includes the word in Īqāẓ al-himam (ed. al-Kayyālī, 1437/2016, p. 384, ḥikma 203) among figurative expressions for what spirits perceive and inward selves taste of the Real’s greatness and majesty. This confirms the term, but does not define it individually. Ibn Manẓūr’s Lisān al-ʿArab , s.v. سور, glosses sāwarahu musāwaratan as assailing or springing at another. Neither “intimate drawing near” nor a more forceful mystical equivalent is established as Ibn ʿAjība’s precise meaning here. The technical word is therefore retained; no emendation to musārara or musāmara is warranted.] ( المشاهدة والمكالمة والمواجهة والمساورة والمفاتحة والمناجاة ). Enter its gate abased and humble: there is no entrance to the holy Presence except through humility and need. The following is recited: I did not seek entry unto Him until I took the station of the lowly servant, closed my eyelids over their discomfort, and guarded the soul from gossip and disputation. Abū Yazīd was told: “Our treasuries are full of service: come to Me through the aperture of humility and need.” Another account says: “Abū Yazīd, draw near to Us with what We do not possess.” He asked, “Lord, what do You not possess?” He replied: “Humility and need.” End of quotation. The shaykh of shaykhs, the Pole al-Jīlānī, God be pleased with him, said: “I approached every door and found crowds. I came to the door of humility and need and found it empty; I entered through it and called, ‘Come!’”—or words to that effect. The poet says: Humble yourself before the one you love: love is not easy. When the beloved is pleased, union is assured. On entering the Presence say, “Our affair is ḥiṭṭa ”: our concern is lowliness, not loftiness. Travelling through the door of lowly conditions is necessary; otherwise there is no arrival. Whoever travels by that door is purified of residues and perfected in excellences, becoming fit for entry into the Presence and inclusion among the people of witnessing and vision. He belongs to the excellent, those brought near; necessarily God increases his ascent in sciences and mysteries, in this abode and the next. By contrast, one who disobeys the command to follow lowly conditions and assumes lofty concerns before his formation is complete returns to the gloom of the veil and an evil reckoning, because he has left the beloveds’ road for the path of heedlessness and doubt. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q2-58-59-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-58-59-s4","r":"q2-58-59","title":"","text":"He reminds them of the blessing of the water He gave them during the wandering, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-58-59-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-60","r":"q2-60","title":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts","text":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts 2:60","anchor":"unit-q2-60"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-60-1","r":"q2-60","title":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts","text":"وَإِذِ اسْتَسْقى مُوسى لِقَوْمِهِ فَقُلْنَا اضْرِبْ بِعَصاكَ الْحَجَرَ فَانْفَجَرَتْ مِنْهُ اثْنَتا عَشْرَةَ عَيْناً قَدْ عَلِمَ كُلُّ أُناسٍ مَشْرَبَهُمْ كُلُوا وَاشْرَبُوا مِنْ رِزْقِ اللَّهِ وَلا تَعْثَوْا فِي الْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ (60)","anchor":"ar-q2-60-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-60-2","r":"q2-60","title":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts","text":"قلت: اسْتَسْقى: طلب السقي، و «ال» في الْحَجَرَ للعهد، وهو الحجر الذي فرَّ بثوبه، أو حجر خفيف مربع مثل رأس الرجل، أُمر أن يحمله معه، فكان يضعه في مخلاته، فإذا احتاج الماء ضربه، قيل: كان من رخام، وقيل: كان كذَّان(1)، كان فيه اثنتا عشرة حفرة، تنبع من كل حفرة عين ماء عذب، على عدد الأسباط، فإذا أراد حمله ضربه فجفّ الماء منه، وقيل: للجنس، فكان يضرب أيَّ حجر وجد، فتنفجر منه عيوناً، ثم تسير كل عين في جدول إلى سبط، فقالوا: إن أفضينا إلى أرض لا حجارة فيها عطشنا، فأوحى إليه: أن كلِّمْهُ يَطِعْك لعلهم يعتبرون.","anchor":"ar-q2-60-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-60-3","r":"q2-60","title":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts","text":"وفَانْفَجَرَتْ: معطوف على محذوف أي: فضرب فانفجرت، والعُثو: أشد الفساد، عثا يعثو عثواً، وعثى يعثِي عثِياً، وعاث يعيث عيثا، ومُفْسِدِينَ: حال مؤكدة لعاملها، أو مقيدة، إن قلنا: إن العثو أعم من الفساد، لصدقه على القصاص، فإنه عثو غير فساد. انظر البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-60-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-60-4","r":"q2-60","title":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا يا بني إسرائيل حين عطشتم في التيه، فطلبتم من موسى السقي، فاستسقى لكم، فَقُلْنَا له: اضْرِبْ بِعَصاكَ التي أخذتها من شعيب عليه السلام، وكانت من آس الجنة، وورثت عن آدم عليه السلام، فيها عشرة أذرع، فضرب فَانْفَجَرَتْ مِنْهُ اثْنَتا عَشْرَةَ عَيْناً على عدد أسباطكم، فكل عين تجري إلى سبط قَدْ عَلِمَ كُلُّ أُناسٍ مَشْرَبَهُمْ مُعَيناً، لا يعدو أحد على أحد، فقلنا لهم: كُلُوا من المن والسلوى، وَاشْرَبُوا من الماء الذي رزقناكم، ولا تطغوا بالنعم فتفسدوا في الأرض بالمعاصي والذنوب، فيكون ذلك كفراً مستوجباً للسلب بعد العطاء، رُوِيَ أنهم كانوا ستمائة ألف، وسعة المعسكر اثنا عشر ميلاً. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-60-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-60-5","r":"q2-60","title":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الأرواح إذا تطهرت من الأكدار، وتحررت من الأغيار، وأشرقت عليها الأنوار والأسرار، وكمل تطهيرها، وتمت تصفيتها، كان صاحبها آية من آيات الله، وحجة من حجج الله، إذا ضرب بعصا همته القلوب القاسية أو الأنفس الأبية، لانت وانفجرت بالعلوم القدسية، كل واحد بما يليق به، فمنها من تنبع بالعلوم الوهبية، ومنها من تنبع بالعلوم الرسمية، ومنها من تنبع بالكرامات وخوارق العادات، ومنها من تنبع منها المكاشفات والاطلاعات، قد علم كل أناس مشربهم، على حسب ما سبق لهم، فيقول الحق تعالى لهم: كلوا من ثمرات ما اجتنيتم من العلوم والمعارف التي أوليناكم، واشربوا من مناهل المنازل التي فيها أقمناكم، أو كلوا من ثمرات المعرفة ما تتقوى به معانيكم، واشربوا من خمر الحبيب ما تغيبوا به عن وجودكم، ولا تتعدوا أطواركم من القيام بوظائف العبودية، ومعرفة عظمة الربوبية، فتكونوا لسلب ما أولاكم متعرضين، ولعقوبته مستحقين، عائذاً بالله من السلب بعد العطاء. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-60-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-60-6","r":"q2-60","title":"2:60 · The twelve springs and the diversity of spiritual gifts","text":"ولما سئموا من المن والسلوى، استبدلوا غيرهما، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق تعالى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-60-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-60-s1","r":"q2-60","title":"The stone and the meaning of corruption","text":"I say: seeking water ( الاستسقاء ) is requesting a supply of drink. The article in “the stone” specifies a known object: either the stone that fled with his garment, or a light, square stone, the size of a man’s head, which he was commanded to carry. He kept it in his bag and struck it when water was needed. It is said to have been marble, or soft porous stone ( kadhdhān , كذّان ). It contained twelve hollows, each producing a fresh spring, according to the number of tribes. When he wanted to carry it, he struck it and the water dried up. Alternatively, the article denotes the kind: he struck any stone he found, and springs burst out, each flowing in a channel to a tribe. They said, “If we reach a land without stones, we shall thirst.” He was inspired: “Speak to it and it will obey you, so that they may take heed.” [B046] “Then they gushed forth” is coordinated with an omitted clause: “he struck, and they gushed forth.” ʿUthūw ( العُثو ) is the most intense corruption. The verbal forms are ʿathā–yaʿthū–ʿuthūwan , ʿathiya–yaʿthī–ʿithiyyan , and ʿātha–yaʿīthu–ʿaythan . “Corrupting” ( مفسدين ) is a circumstantial expression emphasizing its governing verb; alternatively, it restricts its meaning if ʿuthūw is taken more broadly than corruption, applying also to lawful retaliation, which is destructive action without corruption. See al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q2-60-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-60-s2","r":"q2-60","title":"A drinking-place for every tribe","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember when you thirsted in the wandering and asked Moses for water. He sought it for you, and We told him: strike with the staff received from Shuʿayb, peace be upon him. It was of Paradise’s myrtle, inherited from Adam and ten cubits long. He struck, and twelve springs gushed forth, according to your tribes, each flowing to one tribe. Every group knew its appointed drinking-place, none encroaching upon another. We told them: eat the manna and quails and drink the water We have provided. Do not grow insolent through blessings and corrupt the earth with sins and disobedience: that is ingratitude deserving deprivation after bestowal. It is related that they numbered six hundred thousand and their camp extended twelve miles. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-60-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-60-s3","r":"q2-60","title":"The shaykh’s aspiration and the disciples’ differing receptivities","text":"Know that, when spirits are purified of impurities, freed from other-than-God, illuminated by lights and mysteries, and perfected in purification, their possessor becomes one of God’s signs and proofs. If he strikes hard hearts or resistant souls with the staff of his aspiration ( الهمة ), they soften and burst forth with holy sciences, each according to its capacity. Some yield bestowed sciences; others, formal disciplines; others, saintly wonders and extraordinary acts; others, unveilings and disclosures. Every people knows its drinking-place according to its prior allotment. The Real Most High tells them: eat the fruits you have gathered of the sciences and forms of knowledge We bestowed, and drink from the watering-places of the stations in which We established you. Or: eat fruits of gnosis that strengthen your inward meanings, and drink the Beloved’s wine through which you become absent from your own existence. Do not exceed your bounds in fulfilling the duties of servanthood and recognizing the greatness of lordship, thereby exposing yourselves to the withdrawal of His gifts and deserving punishment. In God we take refuge from deprivation after bestowal. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-60-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-60-s4","r":"q2-60","title":"","text":"When they tired of manna and quails, they sought something else instead, as the Real Most High indicates:","anchor":"en-q2-60-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-61","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision 2:61","anchor":"unit-q2-61"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-1","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَا مُوسى لَنْ نَصْبِرَ عَلى طَعامٍ واحِدٍ فَادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنا مِمَّا تُنْبِتُ الْأَرْضُ مِنْ بَقْلِها وَقِثَّائِها وَفُومِها وَعَدَسِها وَبَصَلِها قالَ أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنى بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ اهْبِطُوا مِصْراً فَإِنَّ لَكُمْ ما سَأَلْتُمْ وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ وَالْمَسْكَنَةُ وَباؤُ بِغَضَبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ ذلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ كانُوا يَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ وَيَقْتُلُونَ النَّبِيِّينَ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ ذلِكَ بِما عَصَوْا وَكانُوا يَعْتَدُونَ (61)","anchor":"ar-q2-61-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-2","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"قلت: المراد بالطعام الواحد: هو المنّ والسلوى. ووحَّده لأنه لا يختلف ولا يتبدل، كقولهم: طعام مائدة الأمير واحد، والبقل: جميع الخضر، كالنجم والكرنب والكراث وغير ذلك. والقثاء: جمع قثاءة، وهي الخيار والفقوس والبطيخ وغير ذلك من الفواكه التي تستنبت، والفوم قيل: الحنطة، والأصح أنه الثوم. قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-61-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-3","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"وأنتم أُناسٌ لِئامُ الأُصولِ ... طعامُكُم الفومُ والحَوقَلُ","anchor":"ar-q2-61-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-4","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"أراد: الثوم والبصل. والعرب تعاقب بين الفاء والثاء فتقول: معافير ومعاثير، وتقول للقبر: جدث وجدف.","anchor":"ar-q2-61-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-5","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"والعدس: معلوم، روى علي- كرم الله وجهه- عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم أنه قال: «عليكم بالعدس، فإنه مبارك مقدس، وإنه يرقق القلب، ويكثر الدمعة، وإنه بارك فيه سبعون نبيا، آخرهم عيسى بن مريم»(1).","anchor":"ar-q2-61-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-6","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا أيضاً حين قُلْتُمْ يَا مُوسى لَنْ نَصْبِرَ عَلى طَعامٍ واحِدٍ حين مللتم من العسل واللحم، وملتم إلى عَكَرِكُمْ السوء، أي: مألوفكم وشهواتكم السيئة، لأنهم كانوا فلاحين، فقلتم: فَادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنا مِمَّا تُنْبِتُ الْأَرْضُ، أي: من جنس ما ينبت الله فيها من البقل والقثاء والعدس والفوم والبصل، قال موسى عليه السلام: أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنى وأخس من الثوم والبصل وغيرهما، بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ من اللحم والعسل، اهْبِطُوا إلى مصر من الأمصار، تجدوا ما تشتهون، إذ لا يوجد ذلك إلا في القرى والأمصار، أو اهْبِطُوا مِصْراً التي كنتم فيها أذلاء مستعبدين، تجدوا حظوظكم وشهواتكم لأن الحظوظ والشهوات منوطة بالذل والهوان، وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ وَالْمَسْكَنَةُ، أي: ألزموها لزوم الدرهم المضروب لضربه ونقشه، فالذلة: ضرب الجزية، والمسكنة: فقر النفس وإن كان موسراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-61-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-7","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"وإنما ضُربت عليهم الذلة والمسكنة لأنهم لم يرضوا بتدبير الحق، ولم يقنعوا برزقه، فكل مَن لم يقنع بقسمته وسلم من اتحاد رزقه، خيف عليه من ضرب الذل والمسكنة، وانقلبوا أيضاً بِغَضَبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ حيث نقضوا العهود، وتعدوا الحدود، فكفروا وطغوا وقتلوا الأنبياء بغير حق، وسبب ذلك: تمردهم في العصيان، فإن المعاصي تجر بعضها إلى البعض حتى تنتهي إلى الكفر، والعياذ بالله من سخطه وغضبه.","anchor":"ar-q2-61-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-8","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن لم يقنع بالقسمة الأزلية، ولم يقم حيث أقامته القدرة الإلهية، بل جنح إلى حظوظه وهواه، وحرص على تحصيل أغراضه ومناه، قيل له: أتستبدل تدبيرك- الذي هو أدنى- بتدبير الحق- الذي هو خير-؟","anchor":"ar-q2-61-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-9","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"أتترك تدبير الحكيم العليم، الرؤوف الرحيم، إلى تدبير عقلك الضعيف الجاهل الخسيس اللئيم؟! فعسى أن تدبر شيئاً يكون لك فإذا هو عليك. وعسى أن تأتيك المسار من حيث تعتقد المضار، وتأتيك المضار من حيث ترتجي المسار.","anchor":"ar-q2-61-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-10","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"ولله درّ القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-61-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-11","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"وكَم رُمْتُ أَمْراً خِرْتَ لي في انْصِرَافِهِ، ... فَلاَ زلْتَ لي مِني أبَرَّ وأَرْحَمَا","anchor":"ar-q2-61-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-12","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"عَزَمْتُ عَلَى ألاّ أُحِسَّ بِخَاطِرٍ ... عَلى القلْبِ إلاَّ كُنْتَ أَنْتَ المُقَدَّمَا","anchor":"ar-q2-61-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-13","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"وألا تَرَانِي عِنْدَ مَا قَدْ نَهيْتَني ... لِكَونَك(1) في قَلْبِي كَبيراً معظّما","anchor":"ar-q2-61-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-14","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"يا مَن لم يقنع بتدبير مولاه، ومال إلى نيل حظه وهواه، اهبط إلى أرض الحظوظ والشهوات تجد فيها ما ألفته نفسك من عوائدك السيئات. يا مَن أخلدت نفسه إلى الهوى ومتابعة الشيطان، كيف تستبدل العز الدائم بالذل والهوان؟! وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-61-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-15","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"لاَ تتبع النفس في هواها ... إنَّ اتِّبَاعَ الْهَوَى هَوَانُ(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-61-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-16","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"قال في التنوير: (فائدة) اعلم إن بني إسرائيل لمَّا دخلوا التيه، ورُزقوا المنّ والسلوى، واختار الله لهم ذلك رزقاً، رزقهم إياه، يبرز من عين المنة، من غير تعب منهم ولا نصب، فرجعت نفوسهم الكثيفة لوجود، العادة، والغيبة عن شهود تدبير الله، إلى طلب ما كانوا يعتادونه، فقالوا: فَادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنا مِمَّا تُنْبِتُ الْأَرْضُ الآية. قالَ أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنى بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ. اهْبِطُوا مِصْراً فَإِنَّ لَكُمْ ما سَأَلْتُمْ. وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ وَالْمَسْكَنَةُ وَباؤُ بِغَضَبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ، وذلك لأنهم تركوا ما اختار الله لهم، مائلين لما اختاروا لأنفسهم. فقيل لهم عن طريق التوبيخ: أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنى بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ؟ فظاهر التفسير: أتستبدلون الفوم والعدس والبصل بالمنّ والسلوى؟ وليس النوعان سواء في اللذة ولا فى سقوط المشقة وسر الاعتبار، أتستبدلون مرادكم لأنفسكم بمراد الله تعالى لكم؟ أَتَسْتَبْدِلُونَ الَّذِي هُوَ أَدْنى وهو ما أردتموه، بِالَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ، وهو ما أراده الله لكم؟ اهْبِطُوا مِصْراً فإن ما اشتهيتموه لا يليق إلا أن يكون في الأمصار، وفي سر الخطاب: اهبطوا عن سماء التفويض وحسن التدبير منا لكم، إلى أرض التدبير والاختيار منكم لأنفسكم، موصوفين بالذل والمسكنة لاختياركم مع اختيار الله، وتدبيركم لأنفسكم مع تدبير الله. هـ المراد منه.","anchor":"ar-q2-61-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-61-17","r":"q2-61","title":"2:61 · Rejecting the allotted provision","text":"ولما ذَكَّرَهُمْ الحق تعالى بالنعمة، ووبَّخَهم على ارتكاب الآثام، رغّبهم فى الإسلام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-61-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-61-s1","r":"q2-61","title":"The foods named in the verse","text":"I say: “one kind of food” means manna and quails. It is called one because it did not vary or change, as when one says that a prince’s table always offers one meal. Herbs ( البقل ) embraces all greens: low-growing herbs, cabbage, leeks and others. Qiththāʾ ( القثّاء ), plural of qiththāʾa , includes cucumbers, snake-cucumbers, melons and other cultivated fruits. Fūm ( الفوم ) is said to be wheat; more correctly, it is garlic. The poet says: You are a people of base origins: your food is garlic and onions. He means garlic by fūm and onions by ḥawqal . The Arabs interchange fāʾ and thāʾ : they say maʿāfīr and maʿāthīr , and call a grave jadath or jadaf . Lentils are well known. ʿAlī—God ennoble his face—relates from the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace: “Take lentils, for they are blessed and holy; they soften the heart and increase tears. Seventy prophets blessed them, the last being Jesus son of Mary.” [B047]","anchor":"en-q2-61-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-61-s2","r":"q2-61","title":"Discontent and the preference for familiar habits","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when you said, “Moses, we cannot endure one food,” tiring of honey and meat and inclining towards your own bad sediment—that is, your familiar practices and bad desires, since they had been agricultural people. You said: ask your Lord to bring forth some of what He grows on earth: greens, cucumbers, lentils, garlic and onions. Moses asked: do you exchange the better—meat and honey—for the lower and baser—garlic, onions and the rest? Go down to any town and you will find your cravings, for these foods occur in villages and towns. Alternatively: return to Egypt, where you were humiliated and enslaved, and find your egoic shares and desires, for such shares and desires are bound to humiliation and abasement. Abasement and poverty were imposed upon them, clinging as a struck coin retains its impression and engraving. Abasement is the imposition of the tribute-tax ( الجزية ); poverty is poverty of the soul, even when materially wealthy. These were imposed because they were not content with the Real’s ordering or satisfied with His provision. Whoever is discontent with his allotted share and tires of the sameness of his sustenance [Translator’s note: Cairo I:114 prints وسلم , “and was free/safe,” apparently a corruption of وسئم , “and grew tired.” The rendering follows the latter conjecture, supported by the passage’s opening reference to weariness with manna and quails.] is in danger of abasement and poverty being imposed upon him. [B048] They also incurred God’s wrath by breaking covenants and transgressing limits: they disbelieved, grew insolent and killed the prophets without right. The cause was their rebellious persistence in disobedience, for sins draw one another on until they end in unbelief. In God is refuge from His displeasure and wrath.","anchor":"en-q2-61-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-61-s3","r":"q2-61","title":"Your own planning and the divine ordering","text":"Whoever is not content with the eternal allotment and does not remain where divine power has stationed him, but inclines to his own shares and caprice and avidly pursues his aims and wishes, is asked: will you exchange the Real’s ordering, which is better, for your own planning, which is lower? Will you leave the ordering of the Wise, Knowing, Compassionate and Merciful for that of your weak, ignorant, paltry and ignoble intellect? You may plan something to your benefit, only to find it against you. Joy may come from where you expected harm, and harm from where you hoped for joy. How excellent the poet’s saying: How often I sought a thing whose turning away You chose for me: You have ever been kinder and more merciful to me than I. I resolved that no thought should stir within the heart unless You were placed first; and that You should not see me where You forbade me, so great and honoured are You in my heart. You who are discontent with your Master’s ordering and incline to attaining your own desire, descend to the earth of shares and appetites: there you will find the bad habits familiar to your soul. You whose soul clings to caprice and follows Satan, how can you exchange enduring dignity for humiliation and abasement? The following is recited: Do not follow the soul in its caprice: following caprice is abasement. In al-Tanwīr : “A beneficial observation. When the Children of Israel entered the wandering and were provided manna and quails, God had chosen that provision for them. It issued from pure favour, without toil or labour on their part. Their gross souls, through ingrained habit and absence from witnessing God’s ordering, returned to demanding what they had been accustomed to. They said, ‘Pray to your Lord for us to bring forth what the earth grows…’ He said, ‘Do you exchange the better for the inferior? Go down to a town, and you will have what you asked.’ Abasement and poverty were imposed upon them, and they incurred God’s wrath because they abandoned what God chose for them, inclining instead to their own choice. “They were therefore reproached: ‘Do you exchange the better for the inferior?’ The outward explanation is: do you exchange manna and quails for garlic, lentils and onions? The two are unequal in pleasure and freedom from toil. The inward lesson is: do you exchange God’s will for you for your will for yourselves? The inferior is what you desire; the better is what God desires for you. ‘Go down to a town’: what you crave belongs only in towns. The mystery of the address is: descend from the heaven of entrusting yourselves and Our good ordering for you to the earth of your own planning and choice, marked by abasement and poverty because you choose alongside God’s choice and plan for yourselves alongside His ordering.” End of the relevant passage.","anchor":"en-q2-61-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-61-s4","r":"q2-61","title":"","text":"Having reminded them of His blessing and rebuked their sins, the Real Most High encourages them towards Islam, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-61-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-62","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care 2:62","anchor":"unit-q2-62"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-1","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَالَّذِينَ هادُوا وَالنَّصارى وَالصَّابِئِينَ مَنْ آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَعَمِلَ صالِحاً فَلَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (62)","anchor":"ar-q2-62-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-2","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"قلت: (إن) : ناصبة مؤكدة، وخبرها: جملة (مَن آمن) أو (فلهم أجرهم) . و (من آمن) : بدل من اسمها، أو محذوف، والموصول: مبتدأ أي: إن الذين آمنوا بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم لا خوف عليهم ولا هم يحزنون، والذين هادوا كذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-62-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-3","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"و (هادوا) : تهودوا، أي: دخلوا في اليهودية. وسمّوا يهوداً إما نسبة لأبيهم الأكبر (يهوذا بن يعقوب) ، أو مِنْ هَادَ، إذَا تَابَ لأنهم تابوا من عبادة العجل.","anchor":"ar-q2-62-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-4","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"والنصارى: جمع نصران، وسُموا بذلك إما لنصرهم المسيح عليه السلام، أو لسكناهم معه في قرية يقال لها:","anchor":"ar-q2-62-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-5","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"(نصران) ، والصابئون: طائفة من أهل الكتاب، خرجوا عن دين اليهودية وعبدوا الكواكب، يقال: صبا يصبو، إذا مال وخرج من دين إلى دين.","anchor":"ar-q2-62-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-6","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم والذين آمنوا بموسى، والذين آمنوا بعيسى- عليهما السلام-، والذين خرجوا عن دينهم وصبوا، مَنْ آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وتبع محمداً صلّى الله عليه وسلّم وعمل بشريعته، فَلَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ إذا قدموا عليه بالنعيم المقيم، والنظر إلى وجهه الكريم، وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ حين يخاف الكفار، وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ حين يحزن المفرطون والأشرار إذ لا يلحقهم وبال ولا يفوتهم نوال. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-62-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-7","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"الإشارة: إنَّ الذين آمنوا إيماناً لا يختلجه وهم، ولا يطرق ساحته شك ولا ريب، إما عن برهان قاطع، أو عن شهود ساطع، والذين تابوا عن هواجس الخواطر وغفلات الضمائر، والذين نصروا الدين، وشيّدوا منار شريعة المسلمين، والذين صبوا إلى الحبيب، ومالوا عن كل بعيد وقريب، فهؤلاء الذين سبقت لهم من الله العناية، وهَبَّتْ عليهم ريحُ الهداية، جمعوا بين تزيين البواطن بأنوار الإيقان، وتزيين الظواهر بأنواع الطاعة والإذعان، فلا جرم أنهم، إذا قدموا على ربهم، أجلَّ منصبهم، وأجزل ثوابهم، وأعلى مقامهم، فأولئك أولياء الله الذين لا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-62-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-8","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"فالمخصوصون بالعناية أربعة: قوم أقامهم الحق تعالى لتنمية الإيمان وتربية الإيقان، إما عن دليل وبرهان- وهم أهل النظر والاعتبار، - وإما عن شهود وعيان- وهم أهل الشهود والاستبصار-، وقوم أقامهم الحق تعالى لتصفية نفوسهم وتزكية أحوالهم بالتوبة، والإقلاع عن كل وصف مذموم، وهم السائرون والطالبون، وقوم أقامهم لنصرة الدين وإظهار شريعة المسلمين، إما بتقرير قواعده أو جهاد معانده، وهم العلماء والمجاهدون، وقوم أقامهم لخدمته، وملأ قلوبهم بهيبته، وهم العُباد والزهاد، مالوا عن الشهوات وتأنسوا به في الخلوات، هجروا الأوطان وفارقوا الأحباب والإخوان، صبوا إلى محبة الحبيب وتلذذوا بمناجاة القريب، فهؤلاء المخصوصون بعين العناية، المحفوظون بغاية الرعاية، لا يخافون إذا خاف الناس، ولا يحزنون إذا حزن الناس. حققنا الله بمقام الجميع بمنِّه وكرمه. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-62-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-62-9","r":"q2-62","title":"2:62 · Faith, righteous action and four forms of divine care","text":"ثم وبّخهم على نقض العهود، وعدم الوقوف مع الحدود، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-62-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-62-s1","r":"q2-62","title":"The conditional qualification and the communities named","text":"I say: inna is emphatic and assigns the accusative to its noun. Its predicate may be the sentence beginning “whoever believes,” or “theirs is their reward,” with “whoever believes” an apposition to its noun. Alternatively, the predicate is omitted and the following relative expression begins a new nominal sentence: those who believe in Muḥammad have no fear and do not grieve; those who are Jews likewise. “Those who became Jews” ( هادوا ) means those who entered Judaism. They are called Jews either after their great ancestor Judah son of Jacob, or from hāda , “to repent,” because they repented of worshipping the calf. Naṣārā ( النصارى ) is the plural of naṣrān . They are so called either because they supported ( نصروا ) the Messiah, peace be upon him, or because they lived with him in a village called Naṣrān. The Sabians are a group of the People of the Book who left Judaism and worshipped the stars. One says ṣabā–yaṣbū when someone inclines and passes from one religion to another. [B049]","anchor":"en-q2-62-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-62-s2","r":"q2-62","title":"The commentator’s interpretation of the promised reward","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those who believe in Muḥammad, those who believed in Moses or Jesus, peace be upon them, and those who left their religion and inclined away—whoever believes in God and the Last Day, follows Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, and acts according to his Law, has his reward with his Lord upon coming before Him: abiding bliss and the vision of His noble Face. They do not fear when unbelievers fear, nor grieve when the negligent and wicked grieve: no evil consequence reaches them, and no bounty escapes them. Through God is success. [B050]","anchor":"en-q2-62-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-62-s3","r":"q2-62","title":"Four groups specially embraced by providence","text":"Those who believe with a faith untouched by illusion, doubt or uncertainty, whether through decisive proof or radiant witnessing; those who repent of whispering thoughts and inward heedlessness; those who support religion and build high the beacon of the Muslims’ Law; and those who incline towards the Beloved, turning from every near or distant other—these are those whom God’s antecedent care embraces and the breeze of guidance visits. They unite adorning the inward being with certainty’s lights and the outward being with obedience and submission. Necessarily, when they come before their Lord, He honours their standing, makes their reward abundant, and raises their station. These are God’s friends, upon whom is no fear and who do not grieve. Those specially embraced by providence form four groups. One He establishes to nurture faith and cultivate certainty, through evidence and proof—the people of reflection and consideration—or through witnessing and direct vision—the people of witnessing and insight. Another He establishes to purify their souls and refine their states through repentance and abandoning every blameworthy quality: these are wayfarers and seekers. Another He establishes to support religion and manifest the Muslims’ Law, through expounding its principles or striving against its adversaries: these are scholars and fighters in God’s path. Another He establishes in His service, filling their hearts with awe: these are worshippers and ascetics. They turn from desires, find intimacy with Him in retreat, abandon homelands and part from beloveds and brethren. They incline towards the Beloved’s love and delight in conversing with the Near One. These are singled out by providential care and protected with the utmost solicitude. They neither fear when people fear nor grieve when people grieve. May God realize us in all their stations through His favour and generosity. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-62-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-62-s4","r":"q2-62","title":"","text":"He rebukes their breaking of covenants and failure to remain within the limits, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-62-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-63-66","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath 2:63–66","anchor":"unit-q2-63-66"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-1","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"وَإِذْ أَخَذْنا مِيثاقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنا فَوْقَكُمُ الطُّورَ خُذُوا ما آتَيْناكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ وَاذْكُرُوا ما فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ (63) ثُمَّ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ذلِكَ فَلَوْلا فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ لَكُنْتُمْ مِنَ الْخاسِرِينَ (64) ","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-2","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْتُمُ الَّذِينَ اعْتَدَوْا مِنْكُمْ فِي السَّبْتِ فَقُلْنا لَهُمْ كُونُوا قِرَدَةً خاسِئِينَ (65) فَجَعَلْناها نَكالاً لِما بَيْنَ يَدَيْها وَما خَلْفَها وَمَوْعِظَةً لِلْمُتَّقِينَ (66)","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-4","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"قلت: (لولا) : حرف امتناع لوجود ، تلزم الدخول على المبتدأ، وخبرها واجب الحذف عند سيبويه، أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-5","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"لولا فضل الله عليكم ورحمته موجودان، وقال الكوفيون: فاعل بمحذوف: أي: لولا أن ثبت فضل الله عليكم ورحمته، و (لكنتم) : جوابها.","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-6","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا يا بني إسرائيل حين أَخَذْنا مِيثاقَكُمْ أن تقبلوا تكاليف التوراة، وكانت شاقة عليهم، فلما أبيتم قبولها، قلعنا الطور، ورفعناه فوقكم على مقدار عسكركم، كالظلة، وقلنا لكم:","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-7","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"خُذُوا ما آتَيْناكُمْ من التوراة بجد واجتهاد، وَاذْكُرُوا ما فِيهِ من الوعظ والتذكير لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ الله، فتفوزون بالخير الكثير، فقبلتم ذلك كرهاً ثُمَّ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ وأعرضتم بعد ذلك، فسفكتم الدماء، وقتلتم الأنبياء، فَلَوْلا فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ بتوفيقكم للتوبة، وَرَحْمَتُهُ بقبولها منكم، لخسرتم الدنيا والآخرة.","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-8","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْتُمُ ما جرى للذين اعْتَدَوْا مِنْكُمْ فِي السَّبْتِ في زمن داود عليه السلام، وذلك في قرية يقال لها: «أيْلة» ، كانت على شاطىء البحر، وقد نُهوا عن الاصطياد يوم السبت، فكانت الحيتان تخرج يوم السبت شُرَّعاً، فتُخْرِج خراطيمها للبر، فإذا كان يوم الأحد دخلت في البحر، فحفروا حياضا، وشرعوا إليها جداول، فكانت الحيتان تدخلها يوم السبت فيصطادونها يوم الأحد، فلمَّا لمْ يُعاقبوا على ذلك أحلُّوا يوم السبت، فانقسمت القرية على ثلاث فرق: قوم نهوا، وقوم سكتوا، وقوم اصطادوا، فمُسِخ من اصطاد قردة وخنازير الشُّبان قردة، والشيوخ خنازير، فبقوا ثلاثة أيام وماتوا. فجعلنا تلك الفعلة التي فعلنا بهم- نَكالًا وزجراً لِما بَيْنَ يَدَيْها في زمانها، وما خلفها من يأتي بعدها، وَمَوْعِظَةً: وتذكيراً لِلْمُتَّقِينَ من أمة محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلّم.","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-9","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن المريدين إذا دخلوا في يد شيخ، وأخذوا عنه العهد، حملهم من أعباء التكليف وخرق العوائد ما تموت به نفوسهم، وتحيا به قلوبهم، كذبح النفوس وحط الرؤوس ودفع الفلوس، فإذا هموا بالتقصير، ظلل عليهم جبل همته، وأدار عليهم يد حفظه ورعايته، ولذلك قال الشيخ أبو الحسن: (والله لا يكون الشيخ شيخاً حتى تكون يده مع الفقير أينما ذهب) . والمراد باليد: الهمة والحفظ، ولا يزال الشيخ يراسلهم بهذه التكاليف، ويحضّهم على الأخذ بها، والاجتهاد في العمل بها، حتى تموت نفوسهم وتحيا قلوبهم، وترسخ معرفتهم، وتكمل تربيتهم، فحينئذٍ ينتقلون إلى روح وريحان في جنات الشهود والعيان.","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-10","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"قلت: وقد كان شيخنا يرسل لنا البطاقات في حال البدايات، فما كنت أفتحها حتى ترتعد نفسي مما فيها، لأنها تعلم أنه ما يُرسل لها إلا ما فيه موتها، فلولا فضل الله علينا ورحمته- حتى قوانا على العمل بما فيها- لكنا من الخاسرين، ولقد أخطأت العناية قوماً، فتعدوا حدود الشيوخ، أو خرجوا عن دائرتهم قبل كمال تربيتهم، فمسخت قلوبهم، وانمحت من ديوان الولاية رسومهم، جعل الله ذلك عبرة لغيرهم، وزاجراً لمن حذا حذوهم، نعوذ بالله من السلب بعد العطاء، وكفران النعم وحرمان الرضى، وبالله التوفيق وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-63-66-11","r":"q2-63-66","title":"2:63–66 · The covenant, the raised Mount and the Sabbath","text":"ثم وبّخهم بما فعل أسلافهم من قتل النفس والتشغيب على نبيهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-63-66-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-63-66-s1","r":"q2-63-66","title":"Lawlā and the unfulfilled consequence","text":"I say: lawlā ( لولا ) is a particle signifying that one thing fails to occur because another exists ( حرف امتناع لوجود ). It necessarily precedes a subject, whose predicate, according to Sībawayh, must be omitted: “had God’s bounty and mercy towards you not been existent…” The Kufans take what follows as the subject of an implied verb: “had God’s bounty and mercy not been established…” “You would have been” is its response.","anchor":"en-q2-63-66-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-63-66-s2","r":"q2-63-66","title":"Accepting the obligation and subsequently turning away","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember when We bound you to accept the Torah’s obligations, which were burdensome to you. When you refused, We uprooted the Mount and raised it above you like a canopy, covering the extent of your camp. We told you: take the Torah We have given with seriousness and effort, and remember its admonitions and reminders, so that you may fear God and attain abundant good. You accepted unwillingly, then turned away, shedding blood and killing prophets. Were it not for God’s favour in enabling your repentance and His mercy in accepting it, you would have lost both this world and the Hereafter. You knew what befell those who violated the Sabbath in David’s time, peace be upon him, in a coastal town called Ayla. They had been forbidden to fish on the Sabbath. On that day the fish appeared openly, extending their snouts towards the shore; on Sunday they returned to sea. The people dug pools and cut channels leading to them. Fish entered on Saturday and were caught on Sunday. When no punishment followed, they made fishing on the Sabbath lawful for themselves. The town divided into three groups: those who forbade, those who remained silent, and those who fished. Those who fished were transformed into apes and swine: the young into apes, the old into swine. They remained three days and died. We made that act a chastisement and deterrent for those present at its time and those who came after, and an admonition for the God-conscious of Muḥammad’s community, God bless him and grant him peace. [B051]","anchor":"en-q2-63-66-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-63-66-s3","r":"q2-63-66","title":"The guide’s protective aspiration","text":"When disciples enter a shaykh’s hand and take the covenant from him, he places upon them burdens and breaks their customary habits in ways that cause their lower selves to die and their hearts to live: slaughtering selfhood, lowering their heads, and parting with money. If they incline to neglect, he overshadows them with the mountain of his aspiration and surrounds them with the hand of his protection and care. Hence Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan said: “By God, a shaykh is not a shaykh until his hand accompanies the spiritual poor wherever he goes.” The hand means aspiration and protection, not the bodily hand. The shaykh continues to send these disciplines, urging them to take them up and work diligently with them, until their lower selves die, their hearts live, their knowledge becomes rooted and their formation complete. They then pass to repose and fragrant ease in the gardens of witnessing and direct vision. I say: our shaykh used to send us written slips in the beginning. Before opening one my lower self would tremble at its contents, knowing that he sent only what would cause its death. Were it not for God’s bounty and mercy, strengthening us to act upon them, we would have been losers. Some were missed by providential care: they exceeded their shaykhs’ limits or left their circle before completing their formation. Their hearts were transformed and their inscriptions erased from the register of friendship with God. God made this a lesson to others and a restraint upon those following their example. We seek refuge in God from deprivation after bestowal, ingratitude for blessings and loss of good pleasure. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q2-63-66-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-63-66-s4","r":"q2-63-66","title":"","text":"He rebukes what their forebears did in killing a soul and disputing with their prophet, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-63-66-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-67-71","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning 2:67–71","anchor":"unit-q2-67-71"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-67-71-1","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"وَإِذْ قالَ مُوسى لِقَوْمِهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَنْ تَذْبَحُوا بَقَرَةً قالُوا أَتَتَّخِذُنا هُزُواً قالَ أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِنَ الْجاهِلِينَ (67) قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا ما هِيَ قالَ إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ لا فارِضٌ وَلا بِكْرٌ عَوانٌ بَيْنَ ذلِكَ فَافْعَلُوا ما تُؤْمَرُونَ (68) قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا ما لَوْنُها قالَ إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ صَفْراءُ فاقِعٌ لَوْنُها تَسُرُّ النَّاظِرِينَ (69) قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا ما هِيَ إِنَّ الْبَقَرَ تَشابَهَ عَلَيْنا وَإِنَّا إِنْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَمُهْتَدُونَ (70) قالَ إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ لا ذَلُولٌ تُثِيرُ الْأَرْضَ وَلا تَسْقِي الْحَرْثَ مُسَلَّمَةٌ لا شِيَةَ فِيها قالُوا الْآنَ جِئْتَ بِالْحَقِّ فَذَبَحُوها وَما كادُوا يَفْعَلُونَ (71)","anchor":"ar-q2-67-71-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-67-71-2","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"قلت: الفارض: المسنة التي لا تلد، يقال: فرضت البقرة تفرض فروضاً، إذا أسنت. والبكر: الصغيرة التي لم تلد، العوان: المتوسطة بين المسنة والصغيرة، والفاقع: الناصع الصفرة، يقال: أصفر فاقع، وأسود حالك: أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-67-71-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-67-71-3","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"شديد السواد. وأصل شية: وِشْيَة، كعدة، حذفت فاؤها وعوض عنها التاء، والوشي: الرقم.","anchor":"ar-q2-67-71-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-67-71-4","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا يا بني إسرائيل حين قالَ مُوسى لِقَوْمِهِ لما تخاصموا إليه في قتيل وجد في قرية ولم يدر قاتله، وذلك أن رجلاً فقيراً من بني إسرائيل قتل قريباً له كان موسراً ليرثه، ثم رماه في قرية أخرى، ثم ذهب يطلب دمه، فترافعوا إلى موسى عليه السلام فقال لهم بوحي: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَنْ تَذْبَحُوا بَقَرَةً، وأبهم الأمر عليهم، قالُوا أَتَتَّخِذُنا هُزُواً أي: مهزوءاً بنا، حيث نسألك عن بيان القاتل وأنت تأمرنا أن نذبح بقرة، وهذا من تعنتهم وسوء أدبهم. قالَ أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِنَ الْجاهِلِينَ إذ لا يستهزئ بأمر الدين إلا الجاهل.","anchor":"ar-q2-67-71-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-67-71-5","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"فلما رأوا جدَّه قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا مَا هِيَ، هل هي كبيرة أو صغيرة أو متوسطة؟ قالَ إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ لاَّ فارِضٌ أي: كبيرة، وَلا بِكْرٌ أي: ولا صغيرة، عَوانٌ متوسطة بين ما ذكر من الصغر والكبر، فَافْعَلُوا مَا تُؤْمَرُونَ، فإن الله يُبين لكم القاتل، قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا ما لَوْنُها، أهي حمراء أو سوداء أو صفراء؟ قالَ إِنَّهُ تعالى يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ صَفْراءُ فاقِعٌ لَوْنُها ناصع صفرتها تَسُرُّ النَّاظِرِينَ لسمنها وبهجة لونها، قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا ما هِيَ، فإن البقر الصفر كثير، وقد تشابه علينا أمرها؟ قالَ إِنَّهُ تعالى يقول: إنها مسلمة من العمل ليست ذلولاً، أي: مذللة بالعمل لا تُثِيرُ أي: تقلب الْأَرْضَ وَلا تَسْقِي الْحَرْثَ بالسانية . مُسَلَّمَةٌ من العيوب كلها، لاَّ شِيَةَ فِيها أي: لا رقم فيها يخالف الصفرة.","anchor":"ar-q2-67-71-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-67-71-6","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"فلما تبين لهم الأمر قالُوا الْآنَ جِئْتَ بِالْحَقِّ الواضح، فوجدوها عند شاب كان بيد أمه، قد استودعها له أبوه في غيضة ، فاشتروها منه بملء جلدها ذهباً، أو بوزنها، فَذَبَحُوها، وضربوا القتيل بجزء منها، فجلس وعروقه تسيل دماً، وقال: قتلني ابن عم لي، ثم رجع، وَما كادُوا يَفْعَلُونَ لكثرة ترددهم، أو لفحش غلوها. قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لو ذبحوا أدنى بقرة لكفتهم لكن شددوا فشدد الله عليهم» .","anchor":"ar-q2-67-71-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-67-71-7","r":"q2-67-71","title":"2:67–71 · The cow and the burden of needless questioning","text":"ثم ذكر أول القصة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-67-71-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-67-71-s1","r":"q2-67-71","title":"The cow’s age, colour and markings","text":"I say: fāriḍ ( فارض ) is an old cow that no longer bears young; faraḍat al-baqara–tafriḍu–furūḍan means it has grown old. Bikr is a young cow that has not calved. ʿAwān is intermediate between old and young. Fāqiʿ means brilliantly yellow; one says “vivid yellow” and “pitch black,” the latter meaning intensely black. Shiya ( شية ) derives from wishya ( وِشية ), like ʿida from its root: the first radical is dropped and compensated by the final tāʾ. Washy is a coloured pattern.","anchor":"en-q2-67-71-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-67-71-s2","r":"q2-67-71","title":"The murder, the questions and the eventual obedience","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember when Moses spoke to his people after they disputed before him about a slain man found in a village, whose killer was unknown. A poor Israelite had killed a wealthy relative to inherit from him, cast his body into another village, and gone to demand vengeance for him. They brought their case before Moses, who told them through revelation: God commands you to slaughter a cow. The command left its description unspecified. They asked, “Do you make us objects of mockery?” We ask you to disclose the killer, and you command us to slaughter a cow! This was obstinacy and ill courtesy. He replied, “I seek refuge in God from being among the ignorant,” for only an ignorant person mocks a matter of religion. Seeing his seriousness, they asked: pray to your Lord to explain whether it is old, young or intermediate. He replied: He says it is neither old nor young, but midway between the two. Do what you are commanded, and God will disclose the killer. They asked: pray to your Lord to explain its colour—is it red, black or yellow? He replied: He says it is yellow, brilliant in yellowness, pleasing those who look through its plumpness and the beauty of its colour. They asked again what it was, since yellow cows were numerous and the matter seemed confused. He replied: He says it is free of labour, not broken to work. It does not turn the earth in ploughing or water crops by drawing water. It is sound, free of every defect, with no marking differing from its yellow colour. When the matter became clear, they said, “Now you have brought the clear truth.” They found it with a young man under his mother’s care; his father had placed it in safekeeping for him in a thicket. They bought it for its hide full of gold, or for its weight in gold. They slaughtered it and struck the dead man with part of it. He sat up, blood flowing from his veins, and said, “A paternal cousin of mine killed me,” then returned to death. They had nearly failed to do it, through their repeated hesitation or its exorbitant price. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Had they slaughtered the least cow, it would have sufficed; but they made things difficult, so God made them difficult for them.” [B052]","anchor":"en-q2-67-71-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-67-71-s3","r":"q2-67-71","title":"","text":"He then recounts the beginning of the story, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-67-71-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-72-73","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference 2:72–73","anchor":"unit-q2-72-73"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-1","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"وَإِذْ قَتَلْتُمْ نَفْساً فَادَّارَأْتُمْ فِيها وَاللَّهُ مُخْرِجٌ ما كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ (72) فَقُلْنا اضْرِبُوهُ بِبَعْضِها كَذلِكَ يُحْيِ اللَّهُ الْمَوْتى وَيُرِيكُمْ آياتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ (73)","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-2","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"قلت: حق هذه الآية أن تتقدم قبل قوله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ ... وإنما أخَّرها الحق تعالى ليتوجه العتاب إليهم مرتين على ترك المسارعة لامتثال أمر نبيهم، وعلى قتل النفس، ولو قدمها لكانت قصة واحدة بتوبيخ واحد.","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-3","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاذكروا إِذْ قَتَلْتُمْ نَفْساً حرصاً على الدنيا فَادَّارَأْتُمْ أي: تدافعتم في شأنها، كل قرية تدفع عنها، وَاللَّهُ تعالى مُخْرِجٌ ومبين مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ من القتل، ومن قتله، فَقُلْنا","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-4","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":": اضربوا القتيل أو قبره بِبَعْضِها","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-5","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"قيل: اللسان، وقيل: القلب، وقيل: الفخذ أو الذنب، فضربوه فحيى، وأخبر بقاتله كما تقدم، كَذلِكَ","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-6","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"أي: كما أحيا هذا القتيل، يُحْيِ اللَّهُ الْمَوْتى","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-7","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"من قبورها وَيُرِيكُمْ آياتِهِ","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-8","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"الدالة على قدرته، لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-9","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"فتعلمون أنَّ مَن قَدَر على إحياء نفس واحدة يقدر على إحياء الأنفس كلها.","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-10","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"واستدلت المالكية بالقصة على التدمية الحمراء ، وهي قبول قول القتيل قبل موته بأن فلاناً قتله، وفيه نظر لأن هذا حيى بعد موته فلا يتطرقه الكذب، واستدلت أيضاً على حرمان القاتل من الإرث، وفيه نظر لأن هذه شريعة من قبلنا يتطرقها النسخ، لكن ثبت في الحديث أنه لا يرث. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-11","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"الإشارة: إذا أمر الشيخ المريدين بذبح نفوسهم بخرق عوائدها، فمن تردد منهم في فعل ما تموت به نفسه، كان ذلك دليلاً على قلة صدقه وضعف نهايته، ومن بادر منهم إلى قتلها دلّ ذلك على صدقه وفلاحه ونجح نهايته، فإذا ماتت النفس بالكلية حييت روحه بالمعرفة والمشاهدة الدائمة، فلا موت بعدها أبداً، قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-12","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"لا يَذُوقُونَ فِيهَا الْمَوْتَ إِلَّا الْمَوْتَةَ الْأُولى، وأما الموت الطبيعي فإنما هو انتقال من مقام إلى مقام، ومن وطن ضيق إلى وطن واسع، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-13","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"لا تظُنُّوا الموتَ موتاً إنهُ ... لَحَيَاةٌ، وَهْو غايةُ المنَى","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-14","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"لا تَرُعْكُم هَجْمَةُ الموتِ فَما ... هُو إلا انْتِقَالٌ مِنْ هنَا","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-15","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"فاخلعوا الأجساد من أنفسكم ... تُبْصِرُوا الحقَّ عيَاناً بَيِّنَا","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-16","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"قلت: والسيف الذي يُجْهز على النفس ويسرع قتلها هو الذل والفقر، فمن ذلّ نفسه بين أبناء جنسه، وخرق عوائد نفسه، وزهد في الدنيا، ماتت نفسه في طرفة عين، وحيِيَتْ روحه، وظفر بِقُرَّةِ العين، وهي معرفة مولاه، والغيبة عما سواه.","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-17","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"وكمال الوقت في ذبح النفس أن تكون متوسطة بين الصغر والكبر، فإن الصغيرة جدّاً لا يؤمن عليها الرجوع، والكبيرة جدّاً قد يصعب عليها النزوع، كاملة الأوصاف بحسن الزهد والعفاف، تسر الناظرين لبهجة منظرها وحسن طلعتها، وكذلك مَن كان من أهل الشهود والنظرة، تسحر مشاهدته القلوب، ويسوقها بسرعة إلى حضرة علام الغيوب، لما أقيم به من مشاهدته الملكوت، حتى إن من لا حظه تناسى أحوال البشرية، واستولت عليه أنوار الروحانية، وغاب في ذكر الحبيب عن البعيد والقريب، كما في الحديث: «أولياء اللَّهِ مَنْ إِذا رُؤوا ذُكر الله» وتكون أيضاً هذه النفس غير مذللة بطلب الدنيا والحرص عليها، مسلمة لا عيب فيها، ولا رِقَّ لشيء من الأثر عليها، فحينئذٍ تصلح للحضرة، وتتمتع بنعيم الشهود والنظرة، لم يبق لخصم الفَرْقِ معها تدارؤٌ ولا نزاع، بل أقر الخصم وارتفع النزاع.","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-72-73-18","r":"q2-72-73","title":"2:72–73 · The slain man restored and the limits of legal inference","text":"ثم وبّخهم على عدم تأثير هذه المعجزة فى قلوبهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-72-73-18"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-72-73-s1","r":"q2-72-73","title":"Why the beginning of the story is placed afterwards","text":"I say: in narrative sequence this verse belongs before “God commands you…” The Real Most High postpones it so that the reproach reaches them twice: for failing to hasten to obey their prophet, and for killing a soul. Had it been placed first, there would have been one story and one rebuke.","anchor":"en-q2-72-73-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-72-73-s2","r":"q2-72-73","title":"The sign of resurrection","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when you killed a soul through greed for worldly gain, then disputed concerning it, each village repelling the accusation. God brings out and makes clear what you concealed of the killing and its perpetrator. We said: strike the dead man—or his grave—with part of the cow, said to be its tongue, heart, thigh or tail. They struck him; he revived and named his killer, as already mentioned. Just as He revived this slain man, God gives life to the dead from their graves and shows you the signs of His power, so that you may understand: He who can revive one soul can revive them all.","anchor":"en-q2-72-73-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-72-73-s3","r":"q2-72-73","title":"A dying accusation and the killer’s inheritance","text":"The Mālikīs adduce this story for the bloodied victim’s accusation ( التدمية الحمراء ), accepting the victim’s statement before death that a particular person killed him. This requires examination, because this man revived after death, and lying could not enter his statement. They also use it to establish that the killer is deprived of inheritance. This too requires examination, because it is the law of those before us, which may be subject to abrogation. The rule that he does not inherit is, however, established in hadith. And God Most High knows best. [B053]","anchor":"en-q2-72-73-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-72-73-s4","r":"q2-72-73","title":"The death of selfhood and the fitness of the soul","text":"If a shaykh commands disciples to slaughter their lower selves by breaking customary habits, hesitation over what brings the lower self’s death indicates scant sincerity and a weak final attainment. Haste to overcome it indicates sincerity, success and a sound end. When the lower self dies entirely, the spirit lives through knowledge and perpetual witnessing, with no death thereafter: “They taste no death therein except the first death” [44:56]. Natural death is only a passage from station to station, from a narrow home to a spacious one. The following is recited: Do not think death is death: it is life, the utmost of desire. Do not fear death’s assault: it is only passage from here. Put bodily forms off from your selves, and behold the Real in clear direct vision. I say: the sword that finishes the lower self swiftly is humility and poverty. Whoever humbles himself among his fellows, breaks his own habits and renounces the world finds his lower self dead in the blink of an eye and his spirit alive. He gains the delight of the eye: knowledge of his Master and absence from all else. The best time for this slaughter is when the lower self is between youth and age. If too young, one fears its return; if too old, its withdrawal may be difficult. It should be complete in qualities through beautiful renunciation and restraint, pleasing to behold through its comely appearance. Likewise, seeing a person of witnessing and vision captivates hearts and carries them swiftly into the Presence of the Knower of unseen things, through his established witnessing of the malakūt. Whoever beholds him forgets ordinary human conditions, is overtaken by spiritual lights, and becomes absent from near and far in remembrance of the Beloved. As the hadith says: “God’s friends are those whose sight brings God to remembrance.” This lower self must also be unbroken by pursuit of worldly gain and greed, sound and free of blemish, with no created thing holding it in bondage. It then becomes fit for the Presence and delights in witnessing and vision. The adversary of separation ( الفرق ) no longer contests or disputes with it: the adversary has acknowledged the truth, and the dispute is lifted.","anchor":"en-q2-72-73-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-72-73-s5","r":"q2-72-73","title":"","text":"He rebukes the failure of this miracle to affect their hearts, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-72-73-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-74","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance 2:74","anchor":"unit-q2-74"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-1","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"ثُمَّ قَسَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ذلِكَ فَهِيَ كَالْحِجارَةِ أَوْ أَشَدُّ قَسْوَةً وَإِنَّ مِنَ الْحِجارَةِ لَما يَتَفَجَّرُ مِنْهُ الْأَنْهارُ وَإِنَّ مِنْها لَما يَشَّقَّقُ فَيَخْرُجُ مِنْهُ الْماءُ وَإِنَّ مِنْها لَما يَهْبِطُ مِنْ خَشْيَةِ اللَّهِ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ (74)","anchor":"ar-q2-74-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-2","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"قلت: القسوة والقساوة: هي الصلابة واليبوسة، كالشقوة والشقاوة، يقال حجر قاس، أي: يابس. قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-74-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-3","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"وَلاَ أرَى أثراً لِلذِّكرِ في جَسدِي ... والحَبلُ في الجَبَل القاسِي لهُ أثرُ","anchor":"ar-q2-74-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-4","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"و (أو) للإضراب، أو بمعنى الواو، أو للتنويع، فبعضها كالحجارة وبعضها أشد.","anchor":"ar-q2-74-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-5","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ثُمَّ قَسَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ يا معشر اليهود، ويبست فلم تلن ولم تخشع، مع ما رأت من الآيات كانفجار الحجر بالماء في التيه، وإنزال المنّ والسلوى، وتظليل الغمام، وإحياء الميت وغير ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-74-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-6","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"قال الكلبي: (أنكروا بعد ما رأوا ذلك، وقالوا: ما قتلنا، فما كانوا قط أعمى قلباً، ولا أشد تكذيباً منهم لنبيهم عند ذلك) فقلوبهم كالحجارة، بل أشد، أو إن شَبَّهْتم قلوبهم بالحجارة أصبتم، وبما هو أشد أصبتم، بل في الحجارة فضل عليها في اللين، فإن منها ما تتفجر مِنْهُ الْأَنْهارُ الكبار، ومنها ما تشقق فَيَخْرُجُ مِنْهُ العيون الجارية، ومنها ما تهبط من رأس الجبل مِنْ خَشْيَةِ اللَّهِ. وفي بعض الأخبار: «كل حجر تَرَدَّى من رَأسِ جبلٍ فهو من خشية الله» ، وقلوبكم يا معشر اليهود لا تلين ولا تخشع ولا تأتي بخير. نسأل الله السلامة بمنَّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-74-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-7","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"الإشارة: كل من أساء الأدب مع أستاذه، أو خرج عن دائرته إلى غيره، قسا قلبه، وذهب حاله ولُبه، فإن رجع قريباً واستدرك ما فات، لان قلبه ونهض حاله، وإلا وقع في مهاوي القطيعة، ولم يأت منه شيء. وللقلب القاسي علامات: منها جمود العين، وطول الأمل، وعدم الحزن على ما فاته من الطاعات وما صدر منه من السيئات، وعدم الفرح بما يصدر منه من الطاعات، فإن المؤمن تسره حسناته وتسيئه سيئاته، ودواؤه: صحبة الفقراء الذاكرين الخاشعين، والجلوس بين يدي العارفين الكاملين، وتعاهد الصيام، والصلاة بالليل والناس نيام، والتضرّع إلى الحي القيوم الذي لا ينام، وللشافعي رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-74-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-8","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"ولَمَا قَسَا قَلبي وَضَاقَت مَذَاهِبِي ... جَعَلتُ الرَجَا منِّي لِعَفْوكَ سُلَّمَا","anchor":"ar-q2-74-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-9","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"تَعَاظَمَني ذَنبِي فَلَمَّا قَرَنتُهُ ... بِعفوكَ رَبِّي كَانَ عفوك أَعْظَمَا","anchor":"ar-q2-74-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-10","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"قوله تعالى: وَإِنَّ مِنَ الْحِجارَةِ لَما يَتَفَجَّرُ مِنْهُ الْأَنْهارُ كذلك القلوب القاسية إذا لانت بالإنابة إلى ربها، والرجوع عن مألوفاتها، تتفجر منها أنهار العلوم، وتشقق منها أسرار الحِكَم، ومنها من تذوب من هيبة المتجلي لها، فتندك جبالها، وتزلزل أرض نفوسها، كما قال القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-74-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-11","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"لَو عَايَنتْ عَينَاكَ يومَ تزلزلتْ ... أَرضْ النفُوس ودُكَّتِ الأجْبَالُ","anchor":"ar-q2-74-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-12","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"لَرأَيتَ شَمسَ الحقِّ يسطعُ نورُها ... حِينَ التزَلْزلِ، والرجَالُ رجالُ","anchor":"ar-q2-74-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-13","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-74-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-74-14","r":"q2-74","title":"2:74 · Hardness of heart and the rivers released by repentance","text":"ثم آيس المؤمنين من الطمع فى إيمان من كان هذا وصفه فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-74-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-74-s1","r":"q2-74","title":"Hardness and the senses of “or”","text":"I say: qaswa and qasāwa mean hardness and dryness, just as shaqwa and shaqāwa are variant forms of misery. One calls a stone hard, meaning dry. The poet says: I see no effect of remembrance upon my body, though a rope leaves its mark upon the hard mountain. “Or” ( أو ) marks a transition of emphasis, means “and,” or distinguishes kinds: some hearts are like stones, others harder.","anchor":"en-q2-74-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-74-s2","r":"q2-74","title":"Stones that answer while hearts remain unmoved","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: then your hearts, Jewish people, hardened and grew dry, neither softening nor humbling themselves, despite the signs they saw: the stone gushing with water in the wandering, manna and quails descending, clouds providing shade, the dead revived, and the rest. Al-Kalbī says: “After seeing this, they denied it and said, ‘We did not kill him.’ Never were their hearts blinder or their denial of their prophet more intense.” Their hearts are like stones—indeed, harder. Or: compare their hearts to stones and you are right; compare them to something harder and you are right. Stones possess a softness surpassing theirs: great rivers burst from some, flowing springs emerge from others, and others fall from mountain-tops in fear of God. A report says: “Every stone that falls from a mountain-top falls through fear of God.” Your hearts, however, neither soften nor humble themselves nor produce good. We ask God for safety through His favour and generosity.","anchor":"en-q2-74-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-74-s3","r":"q2-74","title":"Symptoms and treatment of the hardened heart","text":"Whoever behaves discourteously towards his teacher or leaves his circle for another becomes hard-hearted, losing his spiritual state and inner substance. If he returns soon and makes good what was lost, his heart softens and his state rises; otherwise he falls into the depths of severance and nothing comes of him. Signs of a hard heart include dry eyes, long hopes, no sorrow over missed acts of obedience or committed sins, and no joy in the obedience one performs. A believer is pleased by his good deeds and distressed by his wrongs. Its remedy is companionship with the humble spiritual poor who remember God, sitting before the perfected gnostics, regularly fasting, praying at night while people sleep, and imploring the Living, Self-Subsisting One who never sleeps. Al-Shāfiʿī, God be pleased with him, says: When my heart hardened and my ways grew narrow, I made my hope a ladder to Your pardon. My sin seemed immense, but when I set it beside Your pardon, Lord, Your pardon was greater. His words, “Among stones are those from which rivers burst forth,” likewise apply to hardened hearts. When they soften through turning to their Lord and abandoning familiar habits, rivers of knowledge burst forth and mysteries of wisdom open within them. Some melt in awe of the One disclosing Himself, their mountains levelled and the earth of their lower selves shaken. As one says: Had your eyes seen the day the earth of souls was shaken and the mountains levelled, you would have seen the sun of the Real pour out its light amid the shaking, while the men remained men. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-74-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-74-s4","r":"q2-74","title":"","text":"He then removes the believers’ expectation of faith from those characterized in this way, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-74-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-75-77","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge 2:75–77","anchor":"unit-q2-75-77"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-75-77-1","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"أَفَتَطْمَعُونَ أَنْ يُؤْمِنُوا لَكُمْ وَقَدْ كانَ فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ يَسْمَعُونَ كَلامَ اللَّهِ ثُمَّ يُحَرِّفُونَهُ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما عَقَلُوهُ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ (75) وَإِذا لَقُوا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قالُوا آمَنَّا وَإِذا خَلا بَعْضُهُمْ إِلى بَعْضٍ قالُوا أَتُحَدِّثُونَهُمْ بِما فَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكُمْ لِيُحَاجُّوكُمْ بِهِ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ (76) أَوَلا يَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُ ما يُسِرُّونَ وَما يُعْلِنُونَ (77)","anchor":"ar-q2-75-77-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-75-77-2","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"قلت: ضمن الإيمان معنى الإذعان والإقرار ولذلك عداه باللام، وجملة (قد كان) حال من فاعل الإيمان، و (إذا لقوا) عطف على (كان) ، والتقدير: أفتطمعون في إيمانهم والحالة أن مَن سلف منهم كانوا يُحرفون كلام الله، ومن حضر منهم الآن ينافقونكم في دين الله، فلا مطمع في إيمان مَنْ هذا وصفه.","anchor":"ar-q2-75-77-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-75-77-3","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلاّ جلاله: أَفَتَطْمَعُونَ يا معشر المسلمين أن يذعن لكم أهل الكتاب ويصدقوكم وَقَدْ كانَ فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ، وهم السبعون الذين ذهبوا مع موسى للاعتذار، يَسْمَعُونَ كَلامَ اللَّهِ حين كلّمهم وكلّفهم بمشاق التوراة، فحرفوا وقالوا: قال افعلوا ما استطعتم، فإذا لم يحصل لهم الإيمان مع سماع الكلام بلا واسطة، فكيف يؤمن لكم هؤلاء، وهم إنما يسمعونه بواسطة الرسالة؟ أو يَسْمَعُونَ كَلامَ اللَّهِ في التوراة ثم يحرفونه، محواً أو تأويلاً، كصفة سيدنا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم وآية الرجم وغير ذلك، مِنْ بَعْدِ ما فهموه وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ أنه كلام الله، أو وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ أنهم محرفون ومغيرون لكلام الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-75-77-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-75-77-4","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"وكيف تطمعون أيضاً في إيمانهم وهم منافقون؟ إِذا لَقُوا المؤمنين قالُوا آمَنَّا، وصفة نبيكم مذكورة في كتابنا، وَإِذا خَلا بَعْضُهُمْ إِلى بَعْضٍ لامهم مَن لم ينافق، وقالُوا أَتُحَدِّثُونَهُمْ بِما فَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكُمْ من علم التوراة فتطلعونهم عليه لِيُحَاجُّوكُمْ بِهِ أي: يغلبوكم بالحجة عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ في الدنيا والآخرة، فيقولون: كنتم عالمين بنبوة نبينا فجحدتم وعاندتم، أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ حتى تطلعوهم على ما فتح الله به عليكم. أو يقول الحق تعالى: أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ يا معشر المسلمين فتطمعون في إيمانهم بعد هذه الخصال التي فيهم، قال الحقّ جلّ جلاله:","anchor":"ar-q2-75-77-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-75-77-5","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"أَوَلا يَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّ اللَّهَ لا يخفى عليه شيء، بل يَعْلَمُ ما يُسرونه وما يُعلنونه، فيجازيهم على ما أخفوا وما أعلنوا.","anchor":"ar-q2-75-77-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-75-77-6","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"الإشارة: مَن سبقت له المشيئة بالخذلان، وحكم عليه القدر والقضاء بالحرمان، يرجع إلى الدليل والبرهان، بعد الاستشراف على الشهود والعيان، فيرجع إلى مشاهدة الآثار والرسوم، وينسى ما كان يعهده من دقائق العلوم، سبب ذلك كلَّه: الإخلال بالأدب مع المشايخ والأصحاب، أو مفارقة الإخوان، وعدم مواصلة أهل العرفان، وضم إلى ذلك الإنكار على أولياء الله، وتحريف ما سمعه منهم من مواهب الله، فلا مطمع في رجوعه وإيابه، وقد بَعُد من الفتح وأسبابه، لا سيما إذا اتصف بالنفاق، إذا لقي أهل النسبة أظهر الوفاق، وإذا خلا إلى العامة أظهر الشقاق، فمِثلُ هذا لا يرجى له فلاح، ولا يَسعد بصلاح ونجاح. نعوذ بالله من ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-75-77-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-75-77-7","r":"q2-75-77","title":"2:75–77 · Distortion after understanding and the concealment of knowledge","text":"ولما ذكر الحق تعالى رؤساء اليهود أتبعهم بذكر أتباعهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-75-77-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-75-77-s1","r":"q2-75-77","title":"Believing as acknowledgement and submission","text":"I say: believing here includes the sense of submission and acknowledgement; hence it takes the preposition lām . “A group of them used to…” is circumstantial relative to the subject of “believe.” “When they meet…” is coordinated with “used to.” The sense is: do you hope for their faith when their predecessors distorted God’s speech and those now present dissemble before you in God’s religion? There is no ground for such hope in one characterized this way.","anchor":"en-q2-75-77-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-75-77-s2","r":"q2-75-77","title":"Knowing distortion and concealed acknowledgement","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Muslims, do you hope that the People of the Book will submit to you and affirm you, when a group of them—the seventy who accompanied Moses to offer an apology—heard God’s speech as He addressed them and imposed the Torah’s arduous requirements, then distorted it, saying, “He said, ‘Do what you can’”? If hearing the speech without an intermediary did not bring them faith, how will these believe you when they hear only through the mediation of a messenger? Alternatively, they heard God’s speech in the Torah and distorted it by erasure or interpretation, such as the description of our master Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, the stoning verse, and other matters, after understanding it, knowing it was God’s speech—or knowing that they were changing and distorting His speech. How can you hope for their belief while they dissemble? On meeting believers, they say, “We believe; your prophet’s description is mentioned in our Book.” Alone together, those who did not dissemble blame the others: “Do you tell them what God disclosed to you of the Torah’s knowledge, revealing it so that they may overcome you with an argument before your Lord, in this world and the next? They will say: you knew our prophet’s prophethood but denied it obstinately. Have you no understanding, that you disclose what God has opened to you?” Alternatively, the Real Most High says, “Have you no understanding, Muslims, that you hope for their faith despite these qualities?” The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: do they not know that nothing is hidden from God, that He knows their secret and public acts and recompenses both?","anchor":"en-q2-75-77-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-75-77-s3","r":"q2-75-77","title":"The danger of repudiating a knowledge once approached","text":"One whom the prior will assigns to abandonment and decree condemns to deprivation returns to evidence and demonstration after approaching witnessing and direct vision. He returns to seeing effects and forms, forgetting the subtle sciences he once knew. The cause is failure in courtesy towards shaykhs and companions, parting from the brethren and ceasing to maintain contact with the people of gnosis, compounded by denial of God’s friends and distortion of the divine gifts heard from them. There is no expectation of his return when he has become so distant from opening and its means—especially if he adds hypocrisy, displaying agreement when meeting people of the spiritual affiliation and discord when alone with the general public. No success or joyful attainment is expected for one like this. We seek refuge in God from it.","anchor":"en-q2-75-77-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-75-77-s4","r":"q2-75-77","title":"","text":"Having mentioned the Jewish leaders, the Real Most High follows with their followers, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-75-77-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-78","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge 2:78","anchor":"unit-q2-78"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-1","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"وَمِنْهُمْ أُمِّيُّونَ لا يَعْلَمُونَ الْكِتابَ إِلاَّ أَمانِيَّ وَإِنْ هُمْ إِلاَّ يَظُنُّونَ (78)","anchor":"ar-q2-78-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-2","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"قلت: أماني: جمع أمنية، وهي في الأصل: ما يُقَدِّرُهُ الإنسان في نفسه من مُنى إذا قدَّر، ولذلك تطلق على الكذب، وعلى ما يتمنى وما يقرأ ، قاله البيضاوي. والاستثناء منقطع، أي: لكن أكاذيب، ويقال: تمنى الرجل، إذا كذب واختلق الحديث، ومنه قول عثمان رضى الله عنه: (والله ما تَمنَّيْتُ ولا تَغَنَّيْتُ منذُ أَسْلَمْتُ) .","anchor":"ar-q2-78-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-3","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمِنْهُمْ أي: من اليهود عوام أُمِّيُّونَ لا يقرءون الكتاب ولا يفهمونه، لكن يسمعون من أحبارهم أَمانِيَّ كاذبة، وأشياء يظنونها من الكتاب، ولا علم لهم بصحتها، كتغيير صفته صلّى الله عليه وسلّم","anchor":"ar-q2-78-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-4","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"وغير ذلك، أو مواعيد فارغة، ومطامع خاوية، سمعوها منهم، من أن الجنة لا يدخلها إلا هم، وأن النار لا تمسهم إلا أياماً معدودة، وغير ذلك من أمنيتهم الفارغة وأمانيهم الباطلة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-78-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-5","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن المنكرين على أهل الخصوصية ثلاث فرق: أهل الرئاسة المتكبرون، والفقهاء المتجمدون، والعوام المقلدون، يصدق عليهم قوله تعالى: وَمِنْهُمْ أُمِّيُّونَ لا يَعْلَمُونَ الْكِتابَ إِلَّا أَمانِيَّ إذ لا علم عندهم يُميزون به المحق من المبطل، وإنما هم مقلدون، فوزرهم على مَن حرمهم بركة الاعتقاد، وأدخلهم في شؤم الانتقاد، ولقد أحسن «ابن البنا» حيث قال في شأن أهل الإنكار:","anchor":"ar-q2-78-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-6","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"واعلمْ رعاكَ اللهُ مِنْ صَديقِ ... أنَّ الورَى حَادُوا عن التحقيق","anchor":"ar-q2-78-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-7","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"إذْ جَهِلُوا النفوسَ والقلوبَ ... وطلبُوا مَا لم يكُنْ مَطلُوبَا","anchor":"ar-q2-78-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-8","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"واشْتَغَلُوا بعالم الأبدان ... فالكلّ ناء منْهمُ ودَانِ","anchor":"ar-q2-78-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-9","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"وأنكَرُوا مَا جَهِلوا وزَعموا ... أنْ لَيسَ بعدَ الجسمِ شَيْءٌ يُعلمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-78-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-10","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"وكفَّرُوا وزندقُوا وبدَّعُوا ... إذَا دَعَاهُم اللَّبِيبُ الأوْرَعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-78-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-11","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"كلٍّ يرى أنْ لَيسَ فوقَ فَهْمِهِ ... فَهْمٌ ولاَ عِلْمٌ وراءَ عِلْمِهِ","anchor":"ar-q2-78-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-12","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"مُحْتَجِباً عَنْ رؤيةِ المَراتبْ ... عَلّ يُسْمَى عَالماً وَطالبِ","anchor":"ar-q2-78-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-13","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"هَيْهَاتَ هذا كُلَّه تقْصِيرُ ... يأنَفُهُ الحَاذقُ والنّحرير","anchor":"ar-q2-78-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-78-14","r":"q2-78","title":"2:78 · Uncomprehending imitation and the limits of one’s own knowledge","text":"ثم توعّد أهل التحريف من الأحبار، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-78-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-78-s1","r":"q2-78","title":"The range of amāniyy","text":"I say: amāniyy ( أمانيّ ) is the plural of umniyya . Originally it means what a person forms within himself, from manā , “to determine or conceive.” It is therefore applied to falsehood, what one wishes for, and what one recites. Al-Bayḍāwī says this. The exception is disconnected: “but [they know] falsehoods.” One says a man tamannā when he lies and invents a report. Thus ʿUthmān, God be pleased with him, said: “By God, since embracing Islam I have neither fabricated tales nor sung.”","anchor":"en-q2-78-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-78-s2","r":"q2-78","title":"Unexamined notions about Scripture","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: among the Jews are unlettered common people who neither read nor understand the Book. They hear false notions from their learned men, supposing things to belong to Scripture without knowing their truth—for example, the alteration of the Prophet’s description, God bless him and grant him peace, and other matters. Or they hear empty promises and groundless hopes: that none but they will enter Paradise, that the Fire will touch them for only a few days, and their other empty wishes and false expectations. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-78-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-78-s3","r":"q2-78","title":"Mistaking the limits of one’s understanding for the limits of reality","text":"Those who deny the people of special election are of three kinds: arrogant people of leadership, rigid jurists and imitative commoners. His words apply to them: “Among them are unlettered people who know the Book only through notions,” since they lack knowledge to distinguish the person in truth from the person in error and merely imitate. Their burden falls upon those who deprive them of the blessing of trusting acknowledgement and lead them into the ill fortune of hostile criticism. Ibn al-Bannāʾ expresses the condition of deniers well: Know, my friend—may God protect you— that people have turned away from realization. They knew not souls and hearts, and sought what was not to be sought. They occupied themselves with the world of bodies, all of them, near and far. They denied what they did not know, claiming that nothing beyond the body could be known. They accused him of unbelief, heresy and innovation when the intelligent, scrupulous man invited them. Each thinks that no understanding exceeds his own, and no knowledge lies beyond his knowledge, veiled from seeing the degrees, perhaps called a scholar or a seeker. Far from it! All this is shortcoming which the skilful and discerning reject.","anchor":"en-q2-78-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-78-s4","r":"q2-78","title":"","text":"He then threatens the learned men who distort, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-78-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-79","r":"q2-79","title":"2:79 · Writing falsehood for worldly gain","text":"2:79 · Writing falsehood for worldly gain 2:79","anchor":"unit-q2-79"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-79-1","r":"q2-79","title":"2:79 · Writing falsehood for worldly gain","text":"فَوَيْلٌ لِلَّذِينَ يَكْتُبُونَ الْكِتابَ بِأَيْدِيهِمْ ثُمَّ يَقُولُونَ هَذَا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ لِيَشْتَرُوا بِهِ ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً فَوَيْلٌ لَهُمْ مِمَّا كَتَبَتْ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَوَيْلٌ لَهُمْ مِمَّا يَكْسِبُونَ (79)","anchor":"ar-q2-79-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-79-2","r":"q2-79","title":"2:79 · Writing falsehood for worldly gain","text":"قلت: (ويل) : كلمة يستعملها كل واقع في هلكة، وأصلها العذاب والهلكة، وهو في الأصل مصدر لا فعل له، وسوغ الابتداء به الدعاء، وقال أبو سعيد الخدري عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «الويلُ وادٍ في جَهنَّم» [لو سيرت فيه جبال الدنيا لانماعت] .","anchor":"ar-q2-79-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-79-3","r":"q2-79","title":"2:79 · Writing falsehood for worldly gain","text":"يقول الحق جلاّ جلاله: فَوَيْلٌ لِلَّذِينَ يَكْتُبُونَ الْكِتابَ بِأَيْدِيهِمْ تحريفاً لكتاب الله، ويَقُولُونَ هَذَا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ خوفاً من أن تزول رئاستهم، وينقطع عنهم ما كانوا يأخذونه من سفلتهم، نزلت في أحبار اليهود لما قدم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم المدينة، خافوا أن تزول رئاستهم، فاحتالوا في تعويق اليهود عن الإسلام، وكانت صفة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم فى التوراة: «حسن الوجه، حسن الشعر، أكحل العينين، ربعة» ، فغيروها، وكتبوا: طوالاً، أزرق، سبط الشعر، فَوَيْلٌ لَهُمْ مِمَّا كَتَبَتْ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَوَيْلٌ لَهُمْ مِمَّا يَكْسِبُونَ، ويأخذون من سفلتهم، فهو وإن كان كثيرا فى الحس فهو، بالنسبة إلى ما استوجبوه من العذاب الأليم، قليل.","anchor":"ar-q2-79-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-79-4","r":"q2-79","title":"2:79 · Writing falsehood for worldly gain","text":"الإشارة: ينزجر بهذه الآية صنفان: أحدهما: علماء الأحكام، إذا أفتوا بغير المشهور، رغبة فيما يقبضون على الفتوى من الحطام الفاني، وكذلك القضاة إذا حكموا بالهوى، رغبة فيما يقبضون من الرشا، أو يحصلونه من الجاه، فَوَيْلٌ لَهُمْ مِمَّا كَتَبَتْ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَوَيْلٌ لَهُمْ مِمَّا يَكْسِبُونَ الثاني: أهل الرئاسة والجاه من أولاد الصالحين وغيرهم، فإنهم إذا رأوا أحداً قام بولاية أو نسبة خافوا على زوال رئاستهم، فيحتالون على الناس بالتعويق عن الدخول في طريقته، فيكتبون في ذلك سفسطات وترهات، يُنفِّرون الناس عن اتباع الحق، وَيَأْبَى اللَّهُ إِلَّا أَنْ يُتِمَّ نُورَهُ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكافِرُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-79-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-79-5","r":"q2-79","title":"2:79 · Writing falsehood for worldly gain","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى بعض أمانيهم الفارغة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-79-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-79-s1","r":"q2-79","title":"The cry of woe","text":"I say: wayl ( ويل ) is an expression used by someone falling into destruction. Its basic sense is punishment and ruin. Originally it is a verbal noun without a corresponding verb; its supplicatory force permits it to begin a nominal sentence. Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī relates from the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace: “Wayl is a valley in Hell.” [Were the mountains of this world made to travel through it, they would melt.] [B054] [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-01] ]","anchor":"en-q2-79-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-79-s2","r":"q2-79","title":"Distortion to preserve authority","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: woe to those who write the Book with their hands, distorting God’s Book, and say, “This is from God,” fearing the loss of their leadership and the payments they receive from their lower ranks. The verse was revealed concerning the Jewish learned men: when the Prophet came to Medina, they feared losing their authority and devised means to prevent Jews from embracing Islam. His description in the Torah was: beautiful in face and hair, dark-rimmed of eye, of medium stature. They changed it to: tall, blue-eyed and straight-haired. Woe for what their hands wrote and what they earn and take from their lower ranks. However great it appears to the senses, it is little compared with the painful punishment it incurs.","anchor":"en-q2-79-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-79-s3","r":"q2-79","title":"Corrupt rulings and inherited spiritual authority","text":"Two groups should be restrained by this verse. First are scholars of legal judgements who issue opinions contrary to the established position ( المشهور ) out of desire for the perishable gain received for their fatwās; likewise judges who decide according to desire, seeking bribes or status. Woe to them for what their hands write and what they earn. Second are people of leadership and rank, including descendants of the righteous. When they see someone established in friendship with God or a spiritual affiliation, they fear losing their authority and plot to prevent people entering his path. They write sophistries and nonsense that repel people from following truth. “But God will only perfect His light, though the unbelievers dislike it” [9:32].","anchor":"en-q2-79-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-79-s4","r":"q2-79","title":"","text":"The Real Most High mentions some of their empty wishes, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-79-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-80-82","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession 2:80–82","anchor":"unit-q2-80-82"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-1","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"وَقالُوا لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ إِلاَّ أَيَّاماً مَعْدُودَةً قُلْ أَتَّخَذْتُمْ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ عَهْداً فَلَنْ يُخْلِفَ اللَّهُ عَهْدَهُ أَمْ تَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ مَا لا تَعْلَمُونَ (80) بَلى مَنْ كَسَبَ سَيِّئَةً وَأَحاطَتْ بِهِ خَطِيئَتُهُ فَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (81) وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ الْجَنَّةِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (82)","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-2","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"قلت: (بلى) : حرف جواب كنعم، والفرق بينهما أن (بلى) لا يقع إلا في جواب النفي ويصير إثباتاً، تقول: ألم يأت زيد؟ فتقول بلى. أي: أتى، ومثله: قالُوا لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ فقال تعالى: (بلى) أي تمسكم، بخلاف نعم فإنها لتقرير ما قبلها نفياً أو إثباتاً، فإذا قيل: ألم يأت زيد؟ فقلت: نعم، أي لم يأت، وإذا قيل: هل أتى زيد فقلت:","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-3","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"نعم، أي أتى. وقد نظم ذلك بعضهم فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-4","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"«نعَمْ» لتقرير الذي قبلها ... إثباتاً أو نفياً، كذا قرَّرُوا","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-5","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"«بلى» جواب النفي لكنه ... يصير إثباتاً، كذا حرَّرُوا","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-6","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقالُوا أي: بنو إسرائيل في أمانيهم الباطلة: لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ إِلَّا أَيَّاماً مَعْدُودَةً أربعين يوماً مقدار عبادة العجل، ثم يخلفنا فيها المسلمون. قال الحق جل جلاله: قُلْ لهم يا محمد: أَتَّخَذْتُمْ بذلك عهداً عند الله فَلَنْ يُخْلِفَ اللَّهُ عَهْدَهُ أَمْ تَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ مَا لا تَعْلَمُونَ- بَلى تمسكم النار وتخلدون فيها لأن مَنْ كَسَبَ سَيِّئَةً أي: كفراً ومات عليه، وَأَحاطَتْ بِهِ خَطِيئَتُهُ أي: أحدقت به، واستولت عليه، فَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ- وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بما نُزِّل على محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلّم وَعَمِلُوا بشريعته المطهرة الأعمال الصَّالِحاتِ أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ الْجَنَّةِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ هذه عادته تعالى إذا ذكر فريقاً شفع بضده ترغيباً وترهيباً وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-7","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن كثيرا من الناس يعتمدون على صحبة الأولياء، ويُطلقون عنان أنفسهم في المعاصي والشهوات، ويقولون: سمعنا من سيدي فلان يقول: مَن رآنا لا تمسه النار. وهذا غلط وغرور، وقد قال- عليه الصلاة والسّلام- لابنته: «يا فاطمةَ بنتَ مُحمَّد، لا أُغْنِي عَنْكِ مِنَ اللهِ شيئاً، اشترِيِ نفسك من الله» . وقال للذي قال: ادع الله أن أكون رفيقك في الجنة فقال له: «أعِنِّي عَلَى نَفْسِكَ بكَثْرةِ السُّجُود» . نعم، هذه المقالة: إن صدرت من ولي متمكن مع الله فهي حق، لكن بشرط العمل ممن رآه بالمأمورات وترك المحرمات، فإن المأمول من فضل الله، ببركة أوليائه، أن يتقبل الله منه أحسن ما عمل، ويتجاوز عن سيئاته، فإن الأولياء المتمكنين اتخذوا عند الله عهداً فلن يخلف الله عهده وهو أن من تعلق بهم وتمسك بالشريعة شفعوا فيه.","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-8","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"والغالب على مَن صَحِبَ أولياء الله المتمكنين- الحفظ وعدم الإصرار، فمن كان كذلك لا تمسه النار، وفي الحديث: «إذا أحب الله عَبْداً لَمْ يضرُّه ذَنْب» ، يعني: يُلهم التوبة سريعاً، كما قيل لأهل بدر: «افعلوا ما شئتم فقد غَفَرتْ لَكُم» . ولا يتخذ عند الله العهد إلا أهل الفناء والبقاء، لأنهم بالله فيما يقولون، فليس لهم عن أنفسهم إخبار، ولا مع غير الله قرار، وأما من لم يبلغ هذا المقام فلا عهد له لأنه بنفسه، فمن تعلّق بمثل هذا فهو على خطر، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-9","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"قوله تعالى: بَلى مَنْ كَسَبَ سَيِّئَةً، من اقتنى حب الدنيا أحاطت به أشغالها وعلائقها، فهو في نار القطيعة مقيم، أحاط به سرادق الهموم والأكدار، تلدغه عقارب الشكوك والأغيار، بخلاف من أشرقت عليه أنوار الإيمان، وصحب أهل الشهود والعيان، فإنه في رَوْح وريحان وجنة ورضوان، متعنا الله بذلك فى الدارين. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-80-82-10","r":"q2-80-82","title":"2:80–82 · False assurance and the conditions of saintly intercession","text":"ثم قرّعهم على نقض العهد الذي أُخذ عليهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-80-82-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-80-82-s1","r":"q2-80-82","title":"Balā and naʿam","text":"I say: balā ( بلى ) is a response particle like naʿam ( نعم ), but the two differ. Balā answers a negative and turns it into an affirmation. If asked, “Did Zayd not come?” one replies balā : he did come. Likewise, they said, “The Fire will not touch us,” and God replied balā : it will touch you. Naʿam , however, confirms the preceding statement, negative or affirmative. Asked “Did Zayd not come?” naʿam confirms that he did not. Asked “Did Zayd come?” it confirms that he came. Someone has put this into verse: Naʿam confirms what goes before, affirmation or negation: so they teach. Balā replies to a negative, but makes it affirmative: so they explain.","anchor":"en-q2-80-82-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-80-82-s2","r":"q2-80-82","title":"The offence that encompasses its possessor","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the Children of Israel utter their false wish that the Fire will touch them for only a few numbered days—forty, the period of calf-worship—after which the Muslims will replace them there. The Real tells Muḥammad to ask: have you taken a covenant from God to that effect, which He will not break, or do you speak about Him without knowledge? Rather, the Fire will touch you and you will remain there, for whoever acquires an evil deed—unbelief—and dies upon it, his offence surrounding and mastering him, belongs among the companions of the Fire, abiding therein. Those who believe what was revealed to Muḥammad and perform righteous works according to his purified Law are the companions of Paradise, abiding therein. It is His customary manner, when mentioning one group, to follow it with its opposite, for encouragement and warning. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-80-82-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-80-82-s3","r":"q2-80-82","title":"Companionship is not permission to disobey","text":"Know that many rely upon companionship with God’s friends while giving their souls free rein in disobedience and desires. They say, “We heard our master so-and-so say: whoever sees us is not touched by the Fire.” This is error and delusion. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, told his daughter: “Fāṭima daughter of Muḥammad, I cannot avail you against God: purchase your own soul from God.” To the man who asked, “Pray that I may be your companion in Paradise,” he said, “Help me against your own soul through abundant prostration.” [B055] Certainly, if this saying comes from a friend of God firmly established with Him, it is true—but on condition that the person who sees him obeys the commands and abandons forbidden things. What may be hoped from God’s bounty, through His friends’ blessing, is that He accepts the best of that person’s deeds and overlooks his wrongs. The firmly established friends have taken a covenant with God, which He will not break: they intercede for someone who attaches himself to them while adhering to the Sacred Law. The usual condition of one who accompanies firmly established friends of God is protection and non-persistence in sin. Such a person is not touched by the Fire. In the hadith: “When God loves a servant, sin does not harm him”—meaning that He inspires swift repentance—as the people of Badr were told, “Do what you wish: I have forgiven you.” Only the people of effacement and subsistence take this covenant, because they are through God in what they say. They report nothing from their own selves and find no abiding place with other-than-God. Someone who has not reached this station has no such covenant, because he remains through himself. One attached to such a person is in danger. Through God is success. His words, “Rather, whoever earns evil…”: whoever acquires love of the world is surrounded by its occupations and attachments. He remains in the fire of severance, encompassed by the enclosure of cares and impurities, stung by the scorpions of doubts and other-than-God. By contrast, one upon whom faith’s lights shine and who accompanies the people of witnessing and direct vision enjoys repose, fragrance, a garden and good pleasure. May God give us that enjoyment in both abodes. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-80-82-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-80-82-s4","r":"q2-80-82","title":"","text":"He rebukes their breach of the covenant taken from them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-80-82-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-83","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence 2:83","anchor":"unit-q2-83"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-1","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"وَإِذْ أَخَذْنا مِيثاقَ بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ لا تَعْبُدُونَ إِلاَّ اللَّهَ وَبِالْوالِدَيْنِ إِحْساناً وَذِي الْقُرْبى وَالْيَتامى وَالْمَساكِينِ وَقُولُوا لِلنَّاسِ حُسْناً وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكاةَ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ إِلاَّ قَلِيلاً مِنْكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ مُعْرِضُونَ (83)","anchor":"ar-q2-83-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-2","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"قلت: (لا تعبدون) : خبر في معنى النهي، كقوله تعالى: وَلا يُضَارَّ كاتِبٌ وَلا شَهِيدٌ، وهو أبلغ من صريح النهي، لما فيه من إيهام أن المنهي سارع إلى الانتهاء، وقيل: حُذفت «أن» ، وارتفع المضارع، وهو على حذف القول، أي: وقلنا لهم: لا تعبدون، وقرأ ابن كثير وحمزة والكسائي بالغيب.","anchor":"ar-q2-83-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-3","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكروا إذ أخذنا الميثاق على بني إسرائيل وقلنا لهم: لا يتصوّر منكم شرك معي ولا ميل إلى غيري، فلا تعبدوا إلا إياي، وأحسنوا بِالْوالِدَيْنِ إحسانا كاملا، وأحسنوا بِذِي الْقُرْبى نسباً وديناً، وأحسنوا باليتامى وَالْمَساكِينِ، بالمواساة والملاطفة، وَقُولُوا لِلنَّاسِ قولاً حُسْناً أو ذا حسن، وهو ما لا لغو فيه، ولا تأثيم بل ما فيه نصح وإرشاد، وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ بإتقان شروطها وكمال آدابها، وأدوا الزَّكاةَ لمستحقها، ثُمَّ بعد ذلك تَوَلَّيْتُمْ، وأعرضتم إِلَّا قَلِيلًا ممن أسلم مِنْكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ مُعْرِضُونَ عن الحق بعد ظهوره.","anchor":"ar-q2-83-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-4","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"ذكر الحق تعالى في هذا العهد أربعة أعمال: عمل خاص بالقلب، وهو التوحيد، وعمل خاص بالبدن، وهو الصلاة، وعمل خاص بالمال، وهو الزكاة، وعمل عام وهو الإحسان، ورتَّبها باعتبار الأهم فالأهم، فقدّم الوالدين لتأكيد حقهما الأعظم، ثم القرابة لأن فيهم أجر الإحسان وصلة الرحم، ثم اليتامى لقلّة حيلتهم، ثم المساكين لضعفهم، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-83-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-5","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"الإشارة: كل عهد أخذ على بني إسرائيل يؤخذ مثله على الأمة المحمدية، وهذا حكمة ذكر قصصهم لنا، وسرد مساوئهم علينا لنتحرز من الوقوع فيما وقعوا فيه، فنهلك كما هلكوا، وكل عهد أخذ على العموم باعتبار","anchor":"ar-q2-83-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-6","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"الظاهر يؤخذ مثله على الخصوص باعتبار الباطن، فقد أخذ الحق سبحانه العهد على المتوجهين إليه ألا تتوجه همتهم إلا إليه، ولا يعتمدون بقلوبهم إلا عليه، وأن يتخلقوا بالإحسان، مع الأقارب والأجانب وكافة الإخوان، وخصوصاً الوالدين من قِبل البشرية أو الروحانية، وهم أهل التربية النبوية، فحقوق أب الروحانية تُقدم على أب البشرية، لأنَّ أب البشرية كان سبباً في خروجه إلى دار الفناء والهوان، وأب الروحانية كان سببًا في دخوله إلى رَوْحٍ وريحان.","anchor":"ar-q2-83-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-7","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"وأخذ العهد على المتوجهين أن يكلموا الناس بالملاطفة والإحسان، ويرشدوهم إلى الكريم المنان، ويقيموا الصلاة بالجوارح والقلوب، ويؤدوا زكاة نفوسهم بتطهيرها من العيوب، فمن تولّى بعد ذلك فأولئك هم الفاسقون، وعن دائرة الولاية خارجون.","anchor":"ar-q2-83-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-83-8","r":"q2-83","title":"2:83 · The covenant of worship and beneficence","text":"ثم وبّخهم على نقض عهد آخر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-83-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-83-s1","r":"q2-83","title":"A prohibition expressed as a statement","text":"I say: “You do not worship” ( لا تعبدون ) is a declarative expression with prohibitive meaning, like “No scribe or witness shall be harmed” [2:282]. It is more emphatic than an explicit prohibition, suggesting that those forbidden have already hastened to desist. Alternatively, an is omitted and the imperfect consequently nominative. A verb of saying is also omitted: “We told them, ‘You do not worship…’” Ibn Kathīr, Ḥamza and al-Kisāʾī read the verb in the third person.","anchor":"en-q2-83-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-83-s2","r":"q2-83","title":"Four forms of obedience and the order of their claims","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when We bound the Children of Israel by covenant and told them: association of another with Me or inclination to another should not be conceivable from you, so worship Me alone. Show complete goodness to parents, and goodness to relatives by lineage and religion. Treat orphans and the needy with generosity and gentleness. Speak good words to people, free of empty talk and sin, containing sincere counsel and direction. Establish prayer with its conditions perfected and its courtesies complete, and give the alms to those entitled. Yet you subsequently turned away, except the few among you who embraced Islam, averting yourselves from truth after its manifestation. The Real mentions four works in this covenant: one proper to the heart, affirming divine unity; one to the body, prayer; one to wealth, almsgiving; and one comprehensive, beneficence. He orders its recipients by priority: parents first because of their greatest and most binding right; then relatives, since kindness to them unites the reward of beneficence and maintaining kinship; then orphans because of their scant resources; then the needy because of their weakness. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-83-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-83-s3","r":"q2-83","title":"The inward covenant and spiritual parenthood","text":"A covenant like every covenant taken from the Children of Israel is taken from the Muḥammadan community. This is the wisdom of recounting their stories and faults: we should guard against falling into what destroyed them. Corresponding to each outward covenant taken from the generality, an inward covenant is taken from the elect. The Real binds those turning towards Him to direct their aspiration only to Him and rely in their hearts only upon Him; to adopt beneficence towards relatives, strangers and all the brethren, especially parents, whether of bodily or spiritual parenthood. The latter are those who practise Prophetic formation. The rights of the spiritual father take precedence over those of the bodily father: bodily fatherhood occasioned entry into the abode of passing-away and humiliation, whereas spiritual fatherhood occasioned entry into repose and fragrance. [B056] Those turning towards Him are bound to speak gently and kindly, guide people to the Generous Bestower, establish prayer through limbs and hearts, and give their souls’ alms by purifying them of faults. Whoever turns away after this is a transgressor, outside the circle of friendship with God.","anchor":"en-q2-83-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-83-s4","r":"q2-83","title":"","text":"He reproaches their violation of another covenant, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-83-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-84-85","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture 2:84–85","anchor":"unit-q2-84-85"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-1","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"وَإِذْ أَخَذْنا مِيثاقَكُمْ لا تَسْفِكُونَ دِماءَكُمْ وَلا تُخْرِجُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ مِنْ دِيارِكُمْ ثُمَّ أَقْرَرْتُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ تَشْهَدُونَ (84) ثُمَّ أَنْتُمْ هؤُلاءِ تَقْتُلُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَتُخْرِجُونَ فَرِيقاً مِنْكُمْ مِنْ دِيارِهِمْ تَظاهَرُونَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِالْإِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوانِ وَإِنْ يَأْتُوكُمْ أَسْرَى تفدوهم وَهُوَ مُحَرَّمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ إِخْراجُهُمْ أَفَتُؤْمِنُونَ بِبَعْضِ الْكِتابِ وَتَكْفُرُونَ بِبَعْضٍ فَما جَزاءُ مَنْ يَفْعَلُ ذلِكَ مِنْكُمْ إِلاَّ خِزْيٌ فِي الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا وَيَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ يُرَدُّونَ إِلى أَشَدِّ الْعَذابِ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ (85)","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-2","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"قلت: (ثُمَّ أَنتُمْ هَؤُلاء) «أنتم» : مبتدأ، و «هؤلاء» : خبر، و «تَقْتُلُون» : حال، كقولك: أنت ذلك الرجل الذي فعلت كذا وكذا، أو «هَؤُلاءِ» : بدل، و «تَقْتُلُونَ» : خبر أو منادي، أي: يا هؤلاء، أو منصوب على الاختصاص، والْعُدْوَانِ: الإفراط في الظلم، و «أسارى» حال، جمع أسير، ويجمع على أًسرى، وقرئ به أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-3","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"مأسورين، و «هُوَ» ضمير الشأن، و «مُحَرَّمٌ» خبر، و «إِخْرَاجُهُمْ» مبتدأ مؤخر، أو ضمير الإخراج فيكون مبتدأ، و «مُحَرَّمٌ» خبره، و «إِخْرَاجُهُمْ» بدل من الضمير، وهذه الجملة متصلة بقوله: وَتُخْرِجُونَ فَرِيقاً مِنْكُمْ مِنْ دِيارِهِمْ تَظاهَرُونَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِالْإِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوانِ، وما قبلها اعتراض.","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-4","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاذكروا أيضا إِذْ أَخَذْنا مِيثاقَكُمْ وقلنا لكم لا تَسْفِكُونَ دِماءَكُمْ أي: لا يسفك بعضكم دم بعض، وَلا تُخْرِجُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ مِنْ دِيارِكُمْ أي: لا يخرج أحدكم أخاه من داره","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-5","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"ويجليه عنها، وجعلهم الحق نفسا واحدة، وكذلك هو في الحقيقة، وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-6","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"عُنْصُرُ الأنفاسِ مِنَّا واحِدٌ ... وكّذا الأجْسَامُ جِسْمٌ عَمَّنَا","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-7","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"ثُمَّ أَقْرَرْتُمْ بهذا العهد والتزمتموه لأنفسكم وَأَنْتُمْ تَشْهَدُونَ على أنفسكم بذلك، ثُمَّ أَنْتُمْ يا هؤُلاءِ اليهود تَقْتُلُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ أي: يقتل بعضكم بعضاً، وَتُخْرِجُونَ فَرِيقاً مِنْكُمْ مِنْ دِيارِهِمْ إجلاءً عنها، تتغالبون عَلَيْهِمْ بالظلم والطغيان، وَإِنْ يَأْتُوكُمْ مأسورين تفدوهم بمالكم، وذلك الإخراج محرم عليكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-8","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"وحاصل الآية: أن الله تعالى أخذ على بني إسرائيل العهد في التوراة ألا يقتل بعضهم بعضاً، ولا يخرج بعضهم بعضاً من ديارهم، وأيّما عبدٍ أو أمَةٍ وجدتموه من بني إسرائيل أسيراً فاشتروه بما كان من ثمنه واعتقوه، فكانت قريظة حلفاء الأوس، والنضير حلفاء الخزرج، وكانوا يقتتلون في الحرب فيُعين بنو قريظة حلفاءهم الأوس، فيقاتلون بني النضير في قتالهم مع الخزرج، فإذا غلبوا خربوا ديارهم وأخرجوهم منها، فإذا أسر رجل من الفريقين جمعوا له حتى يفدوه، فعيرتهم العرب، فقالوا: تقاتلونهم وتفدونهم؟! فيقولون: قد أمرنا أن نفديهم وحُرم علينا قتالهم، قالوا: فلم تقاتلونهم؟ فقالوا: إنا نسْتحي أن يُذَل حلفاؤنا، فوبخهم الله على ذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-9","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"أَفَتُؤْمِنُونَ بِبَعْضِ الْكِتابِ وهو الفداء وَتَكْفُرُونَ بِبَعْضٍ وهو القتل والإخراج؟ فَما جَزاءُ مَنْ يَفْعَلُ ذلِكَ مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا خِزْيٌ أي: ذل وهوان فِي الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا، وهو السبي والقتل لبني قريظة، والجلاء والإخراج من الوطن لبني النضير، أو الذل والجزية للفريقين إلى يوم القيامة، وَيَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ يُرَدُّونَ إِلى أَشَدِّ الْعَذابِ. وليس ما أصابهم تكفيراً لذنوبهم، بل نقمة وغضباً عليهم، وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-10","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"الإشارة: الناس على قسمين: قوم ضعفاء تمسكوا بظاهر الشريعة ولم ينفذوا إلى باطنها، ولم يقدروا على قتل نفوسهم، ولا على الخروج من وطن عوائدهم، فيقول لهم الحق جلّ جلاله: لا تسفكون دماءكم في محبتي لأنكم لا تقدرون على ذلك، ولا تخرجون أنفسكم من دياركم في سياحة قلوبكم، فقد أقررتم بعجزكم وضعفكم، ويقول للأقوياء: ثم أنتم يا هؤلاء تقتلون أنفسكم في طلب معرفتي، وتخرجون فريقاً منكم من ديار عوائدهم في طلب مرضاتي، تتعاونون على نفوسكم بالقهر والغلبة، وكذلك ورد في بعض الأخبار: (أول ما يقول الله للعبد: اطلب العافية والجنة والأعمال وغير ذلك، فإن قال: لا، ما أريد إلا أنت، قال له: من دخل في هذا معي فإنما يدخل بإسقاط الحظوظ، ورفع الحدث، وإثبات القدم، وذلك يوجب العدم) وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-11","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"منْ لَم يَكُن فَانِياً عَنْ حَظِّهِ ... وَعِنِ الفَنَا والأُنسِ بالأحْبَابِ","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-12","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"فلأَنَّهُ بَيْنَ المنَازِل واقفٌ ... لِمنَالِ حَظّ أَوْ لُحُسْنِ مَآبِ","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-13","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"ويقول أيضاً للأقوياء الذين قتلوا أنفسهم وخرجوا عن عوائدهم: وإن يأتوكم أسارى في أيدي نفوسهم وعوائدهم، أو في طلب الدنيا وشهواتها، تفدوهم من أسرهم، وتفكوهم من قيودهم، وتدخلوهم في حضرة مولاهم، وفي بعض الآثار: (طالب الدنيا أسير، وطالب الآخرة أجير، وطالب الحق أمير) هـ. والأمير هو الذي يفك الأسارى من أيدي العدو، لأجل ما ملكه الله من القوة والاستعداد، فإذا انفك العبد من هواه، دخل في حضرة مولاه، فمن رام إخراجه منها بعد دخوله يقال له: وهو محرم عليكم إخراجهم، فكيف تؤمنون بظاهر الشريعة وتنكرون علم الطريقة، وأنوار الحقيقة؟ فما جزاء من يفعل ذلك منكم إلا خزي في الحياةِ الدنيا وهو الحرص والطمع، والخوف والجزع وطول الأمل، وعدم النهوض إلى العمل، (ويوم القيامة يردون إلى أشد العذاب) ، وهو غم الحجاب وسوء الحساب، (وما الله بغافل عما يعملون) .","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-84-85-14","r":"q2-84-85","title":"2:84–85 · Killing, expulsion and selective fidelity to Scripture","text":"ثم بين الحق تعالى وصفهم وذكر ما أعد لهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-84-85-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-84-85-s1","r":"q2-84-85","title":"The demonstrative and the pronoun of the affair","text":"I say: in “then you, these…” ( ثم أنتم هؤلاء ), “you” is the subject, “these” its predicate, and “killing” a circumstantial expression, as when one says, “You are that man, having done such-and-such.” Alternatively, “these” is an apposition and “killing” the predicate; or “these” is vocative, “you people”; or accusative through specification ( الاختصاص ). Aggression ( العدوان ) is excess in wrongdoing. “Captives” ( أسارى ) is circumstantial, the plural of asīr , also pluralized asrā , as in another reading: “being captives.” Huwa ( هو ) is the pronoun of the affair ( ضمير الشأن ), “forbidden” a predicate, and “their expulsion” a delayed subject. Alternatively, huwa refers to expulsion and is the subject, “forbidden” its predicate, with “their expulsion” an apposition to the pronoun. This sentence connects with “you expel a group from their homes, supporting one another against them in sin and aggression”; the intervening words are a parenthesis.","anchor":"en-q2-84-85-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-84-85-s2","r":"q2-84-85","title":"A people treated as one soul","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when We bound you by covenant and told you not to shed your blood—that is, not to shed one another’s blood—or expel yourselves from your homes: no one should drive his brother out of his dwelling and banish him. The Real makes them one soul, which in reality they are. As the poet says: The source of our breaths is one; our bodies too are one body encompassing us. You acknowledged this covenant, committed yourselves to it and bore witness against yourselves. Yet you Jewish people kill one another and expel a group from their homes, prevailing over them through injustice and tyranny. If they come to you as captives, you ransom them with your wealth, though that expulsion is forbidden to you. The verse’s substance is that God bound the Children of Israel in the Torah not to kill or expel one another, and to purchase and free any Israelite man or woman found enslaved, whatever the price. Qurayẓa were allies of the Aws, and al-Naḍīr of the Khazraj. When war broke out, Qurayẓa supported the Aws against al-Naḍīr fighting with the Khazraj. The victors destroyed their opponents’ homes and expelled them. If a man from either side was captured, they collected money to ransom him. The Arabs reproached them: “You fight them and then ransom them?” They replied, “We are commanded to ransom them and forbidden to fight them.” “Why, then, fight?” “We are ashamed to see our allies humiliated.” God rebuked them: do you believe in the portion of the Book commanding ransom and disbelieve in the portion forbidding killing and expulsion? Those who do this have no recompense but disgrace—humiliation and abasement—in worldly life: captivity and killing for Qurayẓa, exile from their homeland for al-Naḍīr; or abasement and tribute for both until the Day of Resurrection. Then they are returned to the severest punishment. What befell them is not expiation of sins, but vengeance and wrath. God is not unaware of what you do.","anchor":"en-q2-84-85-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-84-85-s3","r":"q2-84-85","title":"Different capacities and freeing the captives of desire","text":"People are of two kinds. The weak hold to the Sacred Law’s outward aspect without penetrating its inward reality. They cannot put their lower selves to death or leave the homeland of their habits. The Real tells them: do not shed your blood in My love, for you cannot bear it; do not leave your homes through the journeying of your hearts, since you have acknowledged your weakness and inability. He tells the strong: you people put your lower selves to death in seeking My knowledge and bring a group of you out of their accustomed homes in seeking My good pleasure, helping one another overcome your lower selves. Thus one report says: “God first tells the servant to seek well-being, Paradise, works and other things. If he says, ‘No, I desire only You,’ He tells him: whoever enters this with Me enters only by relinquishing allotted shares, removing the originated and affirming the eternal ( رفع الحدث وإثبات القدم ); that entails non-being.” The following is recited: One not effaced from his own share, from effacement itself and intimacy with beloveds, remains standing between the stations, seeking a share or a beautiful destination. He also tells the strong who have overcome their lower selves and left their habits: if others come captive in the hands of their lower selves and habits, or in pursuit of the world and its desires, ransom them from captivity, free their bonds and admit them to their Master’s Presence. In one report: “The seeker of the world is a captive; the seeker of the Hereafter a hired worker; the seeker of the Real a prince.” A prince frees captives from the enemy’s hands through the strength and preparedness God grants him. When the servant is freed from caprice, he enters his Master’s Presence. Anyone seeking to expel him after entry is told: their expulsion is forbidden to you. How can you believe in the Sacred Law’s outward aspect while denying the science of the Path and the lights of Reality? Whoever does this receives disgrace in worldly life: greed, covetousness, fear, anxiety, long hopes and failure to rise to action. On the Day of Resurrection they return to the severest punishment: the gloom of the veil and an evil reckoning. God is not unaware of what they do.","anchor":"en-q2-84-85-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-84-85-s4","r":"q2-84-85","title":"","text":"The Real Most High states their character and what He has prepared for them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-84-85-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-86","r":"q2-86","title":"2:86 · The exchange of the lasting for the passing","text":"2:86 · The exchange of the lasting for the passing 2:86","anchor":"unit-q2-86"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-86-1","r":"q2-86","title":"2:86 · The exchange of the lasting for the passing","text":"أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ اشْتَرَوُا الْحَياةَ الدُّنْيا بِالْآخِرَةِ فَلا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذابُ وَلا هُمْ يُنْصَرُونَ (86)","anchor":"ar-q2-86-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-86-2","r":"q2-86","title":"2:86 · The exchange of the lasting for the passing","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أُولئِكَ الناقضون للعهود المتعدون الحدود اشْتَرَوُا الْحَياةَ الدُّنْيا وزخارفها الغرارة بِالْآخِرَةِ الباقية الدائمة، فَلا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذابُ ساعة فى الدنيا بالذل والهوان، وفي الآخرة بدخول النيران، وَلا هُمْ يُنْصَرُونَ بالامتناع منه في كل أوان.","anchor":"ar-q2-86-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-86-3","r":"q2-86","title":"2:86 · The exchange of the lasting for the passing","text":"الإشارة: أولئك الذين نظروا إلى غرة ظاهر الأكوان، ولم ينفذوا إلى عبرة باطنها، فلا ينقطع عنهم عذاب الوهم والحجاب، ولا هم يُنصرون من أليم العذاب.","anchor":"ar-q2-86-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-86-4","r":"q2-86","title":"2:86 · The exchange of the lasting for the passing","text":"ثم وبّخهم الحق تعالى على تكذيب الرسل وقتلهم إياهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-86-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-86-s1","r":"q2-86","title":"The price of a broken covenant","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: these covenant-breakers and transgressors of the limits have bought worldly life and its deceptive adornments at the price of the enduring, everlasting Hereafter. Their punishment is not lightened for an hour: humiliation and abasement in this world, entry into the fires in the next. Nor are they helped to ward it off at any time.","anchor":"en-q2-86-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-86-s2","r":"q2-86","title":"The outward lure and the inward lesson","text":"These looked at the deceptive outward appearance of created things without penetrating their inward lesson. The torment of illusion and the veil therefore does not cease, nor are they rescued from painful punishment.","anchor":"en-q2-86-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-86-s3","r":"q2-86","title":"","text":"The Real Most High rebukes their denying and killing the messengers, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-86-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-87","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call 2:87","anchor":"unit-q2-87"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-1","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنا مُوسَى الْكِتابَ وَقَفَّيْنا مِنْ بَعْدِهِ بِالرُّسُلِ وَآتَيْنا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ الْبَيِّناتِ وَأَيَّدْناهُ بِرُوحِ الْقُدُسِ أَفَكُلَّما جاءَكُمْ رَسُولٌ بِما لا تَهْوى أَنْفُسُكُمُ اسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ فَفَرِيقاً كَذَّبْتُمْ وَفَرِيقاً تَقْتُلُونَ (87)","anchor":"ar-q2-87-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-2","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"قلت: (قفينا) : أتبعنا، و (عيسى) عجمي معدول عن أيشوع في لغة السريانية، وهو غير منصرف للعلمية والعجمة، و (مريم) : بمعنى الخادم، ووزنه: مَفْعَل لا فعيل، و (أيدناه) أي: قويناه ونصرناه، و (روح القدس) هنا جبريل عليه السلام أي: الروح المقدسة- من إضافة الموصوف إلى الصفة-، سمي به لطهارته من كدر الحس.","anchor":"ar-q2-87-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-3","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنا مُوسَى التوراة، فما قمتم بحقها ولا عملتم بما فيها، واتبعنا بعده الرسل كلما مات رسول بعثنا بعده آخر اعتناء بكم، وَآتَيْنا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ المعجزات الواضحات كإحياء الموتى، وإبراء الأكمه والأبرص، والإخبار بالمغيبات، والإنجيل، وَأَيَّدْناهُ بجبريل عليه السلام كان يسير معه حيث سار، ورفعه إلى السماء حين أردتم يا معشر اليهود قتله، أَفَكُلَّما جاءَكُمْ رَسُولٌ بِما لا تَهْوى أَنْفُسُكُمُ من مشاق الطاعات وترك الحظوظ والشهوات، اسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ وامتنعتم من الإيمان به فَفَرِيقاً منهم كذبتموه كعيسى وسليمان ومحمد- عليهم السلام-، وَفَرِيقاً تقتلونه كزكريا ويحيى- عليهما السلام-؟ قال القشيري:","anchor":"ar-q2-87-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-4","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"أصْغَوْا إلى الداعين بسمع الهوى، فصار معبودهم صفاتهم وهواهم. هـ-.","anchor":"ar-q2-87-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-5","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"الإشارة: كل ما قاله الحقّ جلّ جلاله لبني إسرائيل في فحوى الخطاب يقوله لهذه الأمة في سرّ الخطاب، فلقد آتانا الكتاب، وبيَّن فيه الرشد والصواب، وقفَّى بعد إنزاله بعلماء أتقياء، وأولياء أصفياء، يحكمون بحكمه، ويهدون بهديه، فإذا أمروا بالزهد في الدنيا وترك الحظوظ والهوى رفضوهم وكذبوهم، وربما كفَّروهم وقتلوهم، واستكبروا عن الأذعان لهم والانقياد لقولهم، ففريقاً كذبوا وفريقاً يقتلون.","anchor":"ar-q2-87-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-6","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"وفى الحديث قال صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: «لَتَتبعُنَّ سَنَنَ مَنْ قَبْلكم شِبْراً بشِبرٍ وذَراعاً بذراعٍ، حَتَّى لَوْ دَخلُوا جُحْر ضَبٍّ لدَخَلْتُموه، فقالوا: مَن يا رسول الله اليهودُ والنصارى؟ قالَ: نعم.. ومَنْ إذن؟» أي: ومَن تتبعون إلا هم؟. فالدعاة إلى الله لا ينقطعون ما دام الدين قائماً، فقوم يدعون إلى أحكام الله، وقوم يدعون إلى معرفة الله، فالأول: العلماء، والثاني:","anchor":"ar-q2-87-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-7","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"الأولياء، فإذا أمروا بالخروج عن العوائد والشهوات، رموهم بسهام العتاب والمخالفات، إذ لم يأت أحد بمثل ما جاءوا به إلا عودي، إلا من خصته سابق العناية، وهبت عليه ريح الهداية، فيتبع آثارهم، وقليلٌ ما هم.","anchor":"ar-q2-87-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-87-8","r":"q2-87","title":"2:87 · Messengers, the Holy Spirit and opposition to the divine call","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى مقالتهم الشنيعة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-87-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-87-s1","r":"q2-87","title":"Jesus, Mary and the Holy Spirit","text":"I say: “We sent after” ( قفّينا ) means We caused to follow. ʿĪsā is a non-Arabic name adapted from Syriac Īshūʿ, declining without full inflection because it is a foreign proper name. Maryam means a servant, and its pattern is mafʿal , not faʿīl . “We strengthened him” means We fortified and supported him. The Holy Spirit ( روح القدس ) here is Gabriel, peace be upon him: the holy spirit, an annexation of the qualified noun to its attribute. He is called this because he is pure of the turbidity of sense perception. [B057]","anchor":"en-q2-87-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-87-s2","r":"q2-87","title":"Rejection prompted by desire","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: We gave Moses the Torah, but you did not fulfil its right or act upon its contents. In care for you We sent messengers after him, another whenever one died. We gave Jesus son of Mary clear miracles: reviving the dead, healing congenital blindness and leprosy, reporting unseen things, and the Gospel. We supported him with Gabriel, who accompanied him wherever he went and raised him to heaven when you sought to kill him. Whenever a messenger brought what your souls disliked—arduous obedience and abandonment of egoic shares and desires—did you grow proud and refuse belief, denying some, such as Jesus, Solomon and Muḥammad, peace be upon them, and killing others, such as Zechariah and John, peace be upon them? Al-Qushayrī says: “They listened to the callers with the ear of caprice, so their own attributes and desires became what they worshipped.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q2-87-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-87-s3","r":"q2-87","title":"The continuing callers to God","text":"Everything the Real tells the Children of Israel in the manifest purport of the address He tells this community in its inward mystery. He gave us the Book, showing right guidance, and after its revelation sent reverent scholars and pure friends of God, judging by its judgement and guiding by its guidance. When they command renunciation of the world and abandonment of shares and desires, people reject and deny them, sometimes declaring them unbelievers and killing them, too proud to yield and accept their words. Some they deny; others they kill. The hadith says: “You will follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, so that if they entered a lizard’s hole, you would enter it.” They asked, “Who, Messenger of God—the Jews and Christians?” He replied, “Yes; who else?” That is: whom would you follow but them? [B058] Callers to God do not cease while the religion remains. Some call to His judgements, others to His knowledge: the first are scholars, the second His friends. When they command departure from habits and desires, people shoot at them the arrows of reproach and opposition. No one has brought the like of what they bring without being opposed—except that one singled out by antecedent care and visited by guidance’s breeze follows their traces. Few are such people.","anchor":"en-q2-87-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-87-s4","r":"q2-87","title":"","text":"The Real Most High mentions their appalling assertion, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-87-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-88","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline 2:88","anchor":"unit-q2-88"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-88-1","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"وَقالُوا قُلُوبُنا غُلْفٌ بَلْ لَعَنَهُمُ اللَّهُ بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَقَلِيلاً ما يُؤْمِنُونَ (88)","anchor":"ar-q2-88-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-88-2","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"قلت: (غلف) : جمع أغلف، كأحمر وحُمْر، وأصفر وصُفْر، وهو الذي عليه غشاوة، أي: هي في غلاف فلا تفقه ما تقول، بمنزلة الأغلف، وهو غير المختون، وقيل: أصله (غُلُف) بضم اللام، وبه قرأ ابن محيصن.","anchor":"ar-q2-88-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-88-3","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"فيكون جمع غلاف، كحجاب وحجب، وكتاب وكتب، ومعناه: قلوبنا أوعية لكل علم فلا نحتاج إلى علمك وكتابك.","anchor":"ar-q2-88-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-88-4","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"و (قليلاً) صفة لمحذوف أي: فإيماناً قليلاً، أو عدداً قليلاً يؤمنون، أو ظرف لأنه من صفة الأحيان، والعامل فيه ما يليه، و (ما) لتأكيد القلة، أي: في قليل من الأحيان يؤمنون، أو حال من الواو في (يؤمنون) أي: فيؤمنون في حال قلتهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-88-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-88-5","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قالت اليهود استهزاء بما تدعوهم إليه: قُلُوبُنا مغلفة ومغشاة فلا نفقه ما تقول، أو أوعية للعلوم فلا تحتاج إلى علمك، قال الله تعالى: بَلْ لا غطاء على قلوبهم حساً، بل هي على الفطرة لكن لَعَنَهُمُ اللَّهُ وطردهم وخذلهم بسبب بِكُفْرِهِمْ فأبطل استعدادها للعلم، فَقَلِيلًا مَّا يُؤْمِنُونَ أي: فإيماناً قليلاً يؤمنون كإيمانهم ببعض الكتاب، أو فلا يؤمن إلا قليل منهم كعبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-88-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-88-6","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"الإشارة: إذا أمر الدعاة إلى الله أهل الدنيا بذبح النفوس وحط الرءوس ودفع الفلوس، ليتأهلوا به لدخول حضرة القدوس، أو أمروهم بخرق العوائد، لتخرق لهم العوائد ، أنفوا وعنفوا وقالوا: قلوبنا في أكنة مما تدعونا إليه، فيقال لهم: بل سبق لكم من الله البعد والحرمان، فأنكرتم أسباب الشهود والعيان، لكن مَن سبقت له من الله العناية، وهبَّ عليه نسيم الهداية، فلا تضره الجناية، فقد يلتحق بالخصوص، وإن كان من أعظم اللصوص، وهو قليل بالنسبة إلى من جاهد نفسه في طلب السبيل، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُقْتَدِراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-88-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-88-7","r":"q2-88","title":"2:88 · Covered hearts and the refusal of discipline","text":"ثم وبخهم ولعنهم على عدم الإيمان بالقرآن مع إقرارهم به قبل الإتيان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-88-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-88-s1","r":"q2-88","title":"Covered hearts or repositories of knowledge","text":"I say: ghulf ( غُلْف ) is the plural of aghlaf ( أغلف ), as ḥumr is of aḥmar and ṣufr of aṣfar . It means something upon which there is a covering: our hearts are in a sheath and do not understand what you say, like the aghlaf , the uncircumcised person. Alternatively, its original form is ghuluf ( غُلُف ), with the lām vowelled u , as Ibn Muḥayṣin reads it. It would then be the plural of ghilāf , “container,” like ḥijāb/ḥujub and kitāb/kutub : our hearts are repositories of every kind of knowledge, so we have no need of your knowledge or your Book. “Little” ( قليلاً ) qualifies an omitted expression: they believe with little faith, or a small number believe. Alternatively, it is adverbial, since it qualifies periods of time, governed by the following verb; mā emphasizes the paucity: on few occasions do they believe. Or it is a circumstantial expression relating to the plural subject of “believe”: they believe while few in number.","anchor":"en-q2-88-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-88-s2","r":"q2-88","title":"The original disposition and its frustration","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the Jews said, mocking what you invite them to, “Our hearts are enclosed and covered, so we do not understand what you say”; or, “They contain the sciences and have no need of yours.” God Most High says: rather, there is no material covering over their hearts; they are constituted upon the original disposition ( الفطرة ). But God has cursed, expelled and forsaken them because of their unbelief, thus frustrating their receptivity to knowledge. They believe with little faith, as when they believe in part of the Book; or only a few believe, such as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his companions. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-88-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-88-s3","r":"q2-88","title":"Breaking habits and the antecedent gift of guidance","text":"When those who summon people to God tell the worldly to slaughter their lower selves, lower their heads and part with their money, that they may become fit to enter the presence of the All-Holy—or tell them to break their habitual patterns, so that ordinary patterns may be broken for them—they take offence, become harsh, and say, “Our hearts are enclosed against what you invite us to.” [B059] They are told: rather, distance and deprivation have preceded you from God, so you deny the means of witnessing and direct vision. Yet one for whom divine care has preceded, and upon whom the breeze of guidance blows, is not ultimately barred by his wrongdoing: he may join the elect even if he has been among the greatest thieves. Such a case is rare in comparison with those who struggle against themselves in seeking the way. “God has power over everything” [18:45].","anchor":"en-q2-88-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-88-s4","r":"q2-88","title":"","text":"He rebukes and curses them for failing to believe in the Qurʾān, although they acknowledged it before its coming, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-88-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-89","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects 2:89","anchor":"unit-q2-89"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-1","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"وَلَمَّا جاءَهُمْ كِتابٌ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ مُصَدِّقٌ لِما مَعَهُمْ وَكانُوا مِنْ قَبْلُ يَسْتَفْتِحُونَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فَلَمَّا جاءَهُمْ ما عَرَفُوا كَفَرُوا بِهِ فَلَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَى الْكافِرِينَ (89)","anchor":"ar-q2-89-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-2","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"قلت: (لمَّا) حرف وجود لوجود إذا وليها الماضي، ولها شرط وجواب، وهو هنا محذوف دلّ عليه جواب (لما) الثانية، أي: ولما جاءهم كتاب من عند الله كفروا به، أو (لما) الثانية تأكيد للأولى. والجواب: (كفروا به) ، أو فلما وجوابها جواب الأولى، كقوله فَإِمَّا يَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِنِّي هُدىً فَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ ... الآية، و (يستفتحون) ينتصرون، وفي الحديث: «أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم كان يَستَفْتِحُ بِصعَالِيكِ المُهَاجِرينَ» ، الذين لا مال لهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-89-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-3","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَمَّا جاءَهُمْ أي: اليهود، القرآن مصدقاً لِما مَعَهُمْ من التوراة، أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-89-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-4","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"موافقاً له وشاهداً له بالصحة، وقد كانوا قبل ظهوره يستنصرون على أعدائهم بالنبيّ الذي جاء به، فيقولون: اللهم انصرنا عليهم بالنبيّ المبعوث في آخر الزمان، الذي نجد نعته في التوراة، وكانوا يقولون لأعدائهم من المشركين:","anchor":"ar-q2-89-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-5","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"(قد أظلَّ زمانُ نبيّ يخرج بتصديق ما قلنا، فنقتلكم معه قتل عاد وإرَم) ، فلما ظهر وعرفوه كفروا به فَلَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ عليهم، فوضع الظاهر موضع المضمر للدلالة على أنهم لُعنوا لكفرهم، فاللام في الْكافِرِينَ للعهد، وهم كفار اليهود، أو للجنس، فتكون اللعنة عامة لكل كافر، ويدخلون فيها دخولا أولياء، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-89-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-6","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"الإشارة: ترى كثيراً من الناس إذا ذكر لهم الأولياء المتقدمون أقروهم وصدقوهم، وإذا ذكر لهم أولياء أهل زمانهم أنكروهم وجحدوهم، مع كونهم يستنصرون بأهل زمانهم في الجملة. فهذه نزعة يهودية، آمنوا ببعض وكفروا ببعض.","anchor":"ar-q2-89-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-7","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"والناس في إثبات الخصوصية ونفيها على ثلاثة أقسام: قسم أثبتوها للمتقدمين، ونفوها عن المتأخرين، وهم أقبح العوام، وقسم أقروها قديماً وحديثاً، وقالوا: إنهم أخفياء في زمانهم، فحرمهم الله بركتهم، وقوم أقروا الخصوصية في أهل زمانهم، وعرفوهم وظفروا بهم وعظموهم، وهم السعداء الذين أراد الله أن يوصلهم إليه ويقربهم إلى حضرته.","anchor":"ar-q2-89-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-8","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"وفي الحكم: «سبحان مَن لم يجعل الدليل على أوليائه إلا من حيث الدليل عليه، ولم يوصل إليهم إلا مَن أراد أن يوصله إليه» . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-89-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-89-9","r":"q2-89","title":"2:89 · Recognizing what one subsequently rejects","text":"ثم أشار الحق تعالى إلى تسفيه رأى اليهود حيث استبدلوا الإيمان بالكفر، والربح بالخسران، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-89-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-89-s1","r":"q2-89","title":"Lammā and seeking victory","text":"I say: when followed by a past verb, lammā ( لمّا ) is a particle indicating the occurrence of one thing upon the occurrence of another. It has a conditional clause and a response. Here the response is omitted, indicated by that of the second lammā : when a Book came to them from God, they disbelieved in it. Alternatively, the second lammā confirms the first, and “they disbelieved in it” is the response; or the second lammā with its response answers the first, as in “When guidance comes to you from Me, then whoever follows…” [2:38]. “They sought an opening” ( يستفتحون ) means they sought victory. In the hadith: “The Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek victory through the impoverished Emigrants”—those without possessions.","anchor":"en-q2-89-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-89-s2","r":"q2-89","title":"Prior expectation and subsequent unbelief","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when the Qurʾān came to the Jews, confirming the Torah they possessed—that is, agreeing with it and bearing witness to its truth—they had previously sought victory over their enemies through the Prophet who brought it. They would say, “O God, give us victory over them through the Prophet sent at the end of time, whose description we find in the Torah.” To their polytheist enemies they used to say, “The time of a prophet is now near: he will emerge confirming what we have said, and with him we shall slay you as ʿĀd and Iram were slain.” But when he appeared and they recognized him, they disbelieved in him. God’s curse is therefore upon them. An explicit noun replaces the expected pronoun to indicate that they were cursed for unbelief. The article in “the unbelievers” is either referential, indicating the unbelieving Jews in question, or generic: the curse then encompasses every unbeliever, and they are included first and foremost. [B060] And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-89-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-89-s3","r":"q2-89","title":"Recognizing the friends of God in one’s own time","text":"You see many people acknowledge and affirm the friends of God of earlier times when they are mentioned, yet deny and reject the friends of God of their own time—even though in a general way they seek victory through contemporaries. This is a tendency resembling the Jews’ conduct: believing in some and disbelieving in others. People fall into three classes concerning the affirmation and denial of special election ( الخصوصية ). One class affirms it for the earlier generations and denies it to the later; these are the worst of the common people. Another acknowledges it in both earlier and later times, but says that its possessors are hidden in their own time: God deprives them of their blessing. A third acknowledges special election in people of its own time, recognizes, finds and reveres them. These are the fortunate whom God wishes to bring to Himself and draw near to His presence. In the Ḥikam : “Glory to Him who has made the indication of His friends arise only from the indication of Himself, and who brings to them only those whom He wishes to bring to Himself.” Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-89-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-89-s4","r":"q2-89","title":"","text":"The Real Most High points to the foolishness of the Jews’ judgement in exchanging faith for unbelief and profit for loss, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-89-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-90-91","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality 2:90–91","anchor":"unit-q2-90-91"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-1","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"بِئْسَمَا اشْتَرَوْا بِهِ أَنْفُسَهُمْ أَنْ يَكْفُرُوا بِما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ بَغْياً أَنْ يُنَزِّلَ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ عَلى مَنْ يَشاءُ مِنْ عِبادِهِ فَباؤُ بِغَضَبٍ عَلى غَضَبٍ وَلِلْكافِرِينَ عَذابٌ مُهِينٌ (90) وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُمْ آمِنُوا بِما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ قالُوا نُؤْمِنُ بِما أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنا وَيَكْفُرُونَ بِما وَراءَهُ وَهُوَ الْحَقُّ مُصَدِّقاً لِما مَعَهُمْ قُلْ فَلِمَ تَقْتُلُونَ أَنْبِياءَ اللَّهِ مِنْ قَبْلُ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ (91)","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-2","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"قلت: بئس ونعم: فعلان جامدان مختصان بالدخول على ما يدل على العموم، إما نكرة، فتنصب على التمييز المفسر للضمير الفاعل، أو معرف بأل الجنسية، فيرتفع على الفاعلية، تقول: بئس رجلاً زيدٌ، وبئس الرجل زيد، ويذكر بعد ذلك المخصوص: إما خبر عن مبتدأ مضمر، أو مبتدأ والخبر مقدم. وإنما اخْتُصَّتَا بالدخول على ما يدل على العموم لأن (نعم) مستوفية لجميع المدح، و (بئس) مستوفية لجميع الذم. فإذا قلت: نعم الرجل زيد، فكأنك قلت: استحق زيدٌ المدحَ الذي يكون في سائر جنسه، وكذلك تقول في بئس.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-3","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"و (ما) المتصلة ببئس ونعم: نكرة منصوبة على التمييز، أي: بئس شيئاً اشتروا به أنفسهم، وهو كفرهم، أو معرفة تامة مرفوعة على الفاعل، أي: بئس الشيء شيء اشتروا به أنفسهم. و (اشتروا) هنا بمعنى باعوا، كشَروا على خلاف الأصل، وقد يمكن ان يبقى على أصله، على ما يأتي في بيان المعنى.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-4","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"و (بغيا) مفعول من اجله ليكفروا، و (يكفرون) حال من الفاعل في (قالوا) ، و (وراء) في الأصل: مصدر جُعل ظرفاً، ويضاف إلى الفاعل ويراد به ما يتوارى به وهو خلفه، وإلى المفعول فيراد به ما يواريه وهو قدامه، ولذلك عد من الأضداد، قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-5","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في شأن اليهود: بئس شيئاً باعوا به حظ أنفسهم، وهو كفرهم بما أنزل الله، أو بِئْسَمَا اشْتَرَوْا بِهِ أَنْفُسَهُمْ بحسب ظنهم، فإنهم ظنوا أنهم خلّصوا أنفسهم من العذاب بما فعلوا، وهو كفرهم بما أنزل الله على محمد نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلّم بغياً وحسداً أن يكون النبيّ من غيرهم، فانقلبوا بِغَضَبٍ عَلى غَضَبٍ للكفر والحسد لمن هو أفضل الخلق، أو لكفرهم بمحمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- بعد عيسى عليه السلام، أو لتضييعهم التوراة، وكفرهم بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم، وَلِلْكافِرِينَ عَذابٌ مُهِينٌ أي: يذلهم ويخزيهم في الدنيا والآخرة، بخلاف عذاب العاصي فإنه كفارة لذنوبه.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-6","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"وَإِذا قِيلَ لهؤلاء اليهود: آمِنُوا بِما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ على محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم قالُوا نُؤْمِنُ بِما أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنا من التوراة، وهم يَكْفُرُونَ بِما وَراءَهُ أي: بما سواه، وهو القرآن، حال كونه مُصَدِّقاً لِما مَعَهُمْ من التوراة ومهيمناً عليه. قُلْ لهم يا محمد: فَلِمَ تَقْتُلُونَ أَنْبِياءَ اللَّهِ مِنْ قَبْلُ هذا الزمان، وهو محرم عليكم في التوراة، إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ به؟ فهذا يبطل دعواكم الإيمان بالتوراة إذ الإيمان بالكتاب يقتضي العمل به، وإلاَّ كان دعوى، وإن فعله أسلافكم فأنتم راضون به وعازمون عليه.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-7","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن قاعدة تفسير أهل الإشارة هي أن كل عتاب توجه لمن ترك طريق الإيمان، وأنكر على أهله يتوجه مثله لمن ترك طريق مقام الإحسان، وأنكر على أهله. وكل وعيد توعد به أهل الكفران يتوعد به مَن ترك السلوك لمقام الإحسان، غير أن عذاب أهل الكفر حسي بدني، وعذاب أهل الحجاب معنوي قلبي.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-8","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"فنقول فيمن رضي بعيبه وأقام على مرض قلبه وأنكر الأطباء ووجود أهل التربية: بئسما اشتروا به أنفسهم، وهو كفرهم بما أنزل الله من الخصوصية على قلوب أوليائه بغياً وحسداً، أو جهلاً وسوء ظن، أن ينزل الله من فضله على","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-9","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"من يشاء من عباده، فباءوا بغضب الحجاب على غضب البعد والارتياب، أو بغضب سقم القلوب على غضب الإصرار على المساوئ والعيوب. (من لم يتغلغل في علمنا هذا مات مُصرًا على الكبائر وهو لا يشعر) كما قال الشاذلي رضي الله عنه، ولا يصح التغلغل فيه إلا بصحبة أهله. وللكافرين بالخصوصية عذاب الطمع وسجن الأكوان، وهما شجرة الذل والهوان.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-10","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"وإذا قيل لهم: آمنوا بما أنزل الله من أسرار الحقيقة وأنوار الطريقة، قالوا: نؤمن بما أنزل علينا من ظواهر الشريعة، ويكفرون بما وراءه من أسرار الحقيقة، ككشف أسرار الذات وأنوار الصفات، وهو- أي: علم الحقيقة- الحق لأنه خالص لب الشريعة، ولله در صاحب المباحث الأصلية حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-11","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"هل ظاهِرُ الشرع وعلمُ الباطِنْ ... إلا كجِسمٍ فيه رُوحٌ سَاكِنْ؟","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-12","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"وقال أيضاً:","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-13","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"ما مَثلُ المعقولِ والمنقولِ ... إلا كَدُرِّ زاخرٍ مَجْهُولِ","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-14","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"حتى إذا أخْرَجَهُ الغِوَّاصُ ... لم يكُ لِلدُرِّ إذن خلاص","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-15","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"وإنما خَلاصُهُ في الكَشْفِ ... عن الغِطَاءِ حيثُ لا يسْتَخْفِي","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-16","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"فَالصّدَفُ الظاهرُ ثم الدرُّ ... مَعْقولُه والجهلُ ذاك البحْرُ","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-17","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"وكان الشيخ عز الدين بن عبد السلام يقول: (هل ثَمَّ شيءٌ غيرُ ما فهمناه من الكتاب والسنة؟) ، كان يقول ذلك إذا قيل له: إن الشيخ الشاذلي فاض اليوم بعلوم وأسرار، فلما التقى بالشيخ وأخذ بيده، قال: (أي والله.. ما قعد على قواعد الشريعة التي لا تنهدم إلا الصوفية) . ويقال لمن ادعى التمسك بالشريعة وأنكر ما وراءها: فلم تشتغل بجمع الدنيا واحتكارها وتخاف من الفقر، وتهتم بأمر الرزق وتجزع من المصائب، والشريعة تنادي عليك بذم ذلك كله إن كنت مؤمناً؟!! وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-90-91-18","r":"q2-90-91","title":"2:90–91 · Envy of divine favour and the relation of Law to Reality","text":"ثم نعى عليهم عبادة العجل بعد ما رأوا من الآيات البينات، إبطالا لدعواهم الإيمان بالتوراة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-90-91-18"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-90-91-s1","r":"q2-90-91","title":"The comprehensive force of praise and blame","text":"I say: biʾsa and niʿma ( بئس، نعم ) are invariable verbs restricted to expressions indicating generality. This may be an indefinite noun, accusative as a specification ( تمييز ) explaining the pronominal agent, or a noun with the generic article, nominative as the agent ( فاعل ). Thus: biʾsa rajulan Zaydun , “What a bad man Zayd is”; or biʾsa al-rajulu Zaydun . The particular person praised or blamed follows, either as the predicate of an implied subject or as a subject with its predicate preceding. These verbs are restricted to general expressions because niʿma exhausts every aspect of praise, and biʾsa every aspect of blame. “What an excellent man Zayd is” is as though you said: Zayd deserves the praise belonging to his whole kind. The corresponding explanation applies to biʾsa . The mā attached to biʾsa or niʿma is an indefinite expression, accusative as specification: “What a wretched thing it is for which they sold their souls”—their unbelief. Or it is a complete definite expression, nominative as the agent: “Wretched is the thing—the thing for which they sold their souls.” Here ishtaraw means “sold,” as sharaw does, contrary to its usual meaning. It may, however, retain its usual meaning, “bought,” as will appear in the exposition. “Out of envy” ( بغياً ) is an accusative of purpose explaining their unbelief. “They disbelieve” is circumstantial, relating to the subject of “they said.” Warāʾ ( وراء ) was originally a verbal noun made into an adverb. When annexed to the agent, it denotes that by which he is hidden, lying behind him; when annexed to the object, it denotes what hides it, lying before it. Hence it is counted among expressions bearing opposite meanings. So al-Bayḍāwī explains.","anchor":"en-q2-90-91-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-90-91-s2","r":"q2-90-91","title":"Faith professed but contradicted in practice","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says concerning the Jews: wretched is the thing for which they sold their souls’ portion—unbelief in what God sent down. Alternatively, wretched is that by which, as they imagined, they purchased their souls’ deliverance: they supposed that their action saved them from punishment. Their action was to disbelieve in what God revealed to His Prophet Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, through transgression and envy that the Prophet should come from a people other than themselves. They returned with wrath upon wrath: for unbelief and envy towards the best of creation; or for disbelieving in Muḥammad after Jesus, peace be upon them; or for neglecting the Torah and disbelieving in Muḥammad. The unbelievers have a humiliating punishment, abasing and disgracing them in this world and the next, unlike the punishment of a disobedient believer, which expiates his sins. When these Jews are told to believe what God revealed to Muḥammad, they say that they believe the Torah revealed to them, while disbelieving what lies beyond it—the Qurʾān—which confirms and stands as guardian over the Torah they possess. Say to them, Muḥammad: why did you kill God’s prophets before this time, when the Torah forbids it, if you believe in that Book? This invalidates your claim: believing a Book entails acting upon it; otherwise it is merely a claim. Although your forefathers committed the deed, you approve it and resolve upon the same course.","anchor":"en-q2-90-91-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-90-91-s3","r":"q2-90-91","title":"The rule of allusive interpretation","text":"Know that the rule of those who interpret by allusion is this: every reproach addressed to those who abandon the way of faith and deny its people is addressed correspondingly to those who abandon the way of the station of spiritual excellence ( الإحسان ) and deny its people. Every threat directed at unbelievers is correspondingly directed at those who abandon the journey to the station of spiritual excellence. But the unbelievers’ punishment is sensible and bodily, whereas the punishment of the veiled is inward and belongs to the heart. [B061] Thus we say of those content with their faults, persisting in the sickness of their hearts, denying the physicians and the existence of masters of formation: wretched is that for which they have sold their souls—denial of the special election God bestows upon His friends’ hearts, through envy and transgression, or ignorance and bad opinion, that God should bestow His bounty upon whomsoever He wills. They incur the wrath of veiling upon that of distance and uncertainty, or the wrath of sick hearts upon that of persistence in faults and defects. As al-Shādhilī, God be pleased with him, said: “Whoever does not penetrate this science of ours dies persisting in grave sins without knowing it.” One cannot properly penetrate it without accompanying its people. Those who deny special election suffer the punishment of covetousness and the prison of created things: these are the tree of abasement and humiliation. When told to believe in the secrets of Reality ( الحقيقة ) and lights of the Path ( الطريقة ) that God has bestowed, they say, “We believe in the outward ordinances of the Sacred Law revealed to us,” while denying what lies beyond them: the secrets of Reality, such as the unveiling of the Essence’s mysteries and the lights of the Attributes. Yet the science of Reality is the truth, because it is the pure kernel of the Sacred Law. How fine are the words of the author of al-Mabāḥith al-aṣliyya : Are the outward Law and inward science anything but a body in which a spirit dwells? He also says: The intelligible and the transmitted are like a pearl in an unknown, overflowing sea. Even when the diver brings it forth, the pearl is not yet free. It is freed only by uncovering it, removing the covering, so it lies concealed no more. The shell is the outward, the pearl its intelligible meaning; ignorance is that sea. Shaykh ʿIzz al-Dīn ibn ʿAbd al-Salām used to say, “Is there anything besides what we have understood from the Book and the Sunna?” He said this when told that Shaykh al-Shādhilī had that day poured forth sciences and mysteries. But when he met the shaykh and took his hand, he said: “Yes, by God! None but the Sufis are established upon the indestructible foundations of the Sacred Law.” To someone claiming adherence to the Sacred Law while denying what lies beyond it, one says: why occupy yourself with amassing and hoarding the world, fear poverty, worry about provision and panic at calamities, when the Sacred Law proclaims its condemnation of all this—if you are a believer? Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-90-91-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-90-91-s4","r":"q2-90-91","title":"","text":"He reproaches them for worshipping the calf after seeing the clear signs, invalidating their claim to believe the Torah, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-90-91-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-92","r":"q2-92","title":"2:92 · Clear signs and the idol of desire","text":"2:92 · Clear signs and the idol of desire 2:92","anchor":"unit-q2-92"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-92-1","r":"q2-92","title":"2:92 · Clear signs and the idol of desire","text":"وَلَقَدْ جاءَكُمْ مُوسى بِالْبَيِّناتِ ثُمَّ اتَّخَذْتُمُ الْعِجْلَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ وَأَنْتُمْ ظالِمُونَ (92)","anchor":"ar-q2-92-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-92-2","r":"q2-92","title":"2:92 · Clear signs and the idol of desire","text":"قلت: جملة: وَأَنْتُمْ ظالِمُونَ حال من (اتخذتم) .","anchor":"ar-q2-92-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-92-3","r":"q2-92","title":"2:92 · Clear signs and the idol of desire","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَقَدْ جاءَكُمْ مُوسى بالمعجزات الواضحات: كالعصا واليد وفلق البحر، ثم لم ينجح ذلك فيكم، فاتخذتم العجل إلهاً تعبدونه من بعد ذهابه إلى الطور وَأَنْتُمْ ظالِمُونَ في ذلك، فأين دعواكم الإيمان بالتوراة؟","anchor":"ar-q2-92-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-92-4","r":"q2-92","title":"2:92 · Clear signs and the idol of desire","text":"الإشارة: ويقال لمن أقام على عيبه، ورضي بمرض قلبه، حتى لقي الله بقلب سقيم: لقد جاءتكم أوليائي بالآيات الواضحات، ولو لم يكن إلا شفاء المرضى على أيديهم- أعني مرضى القلوب- لكان كافياً، ثم اتخذتم الهوى إلهكم، وعبدتم العاجلة بقلوبكم، وعزَّتْ عليكم نفوسكم وفلوسكم، وأنتم ظالمون في الإقامة على مساوئكم وعيوبكم، مع وجود الطبيب لمن طلب الشفاء، وحسّن الظن وشهد الصفاء. (كن طالباً تجد مرشداً) وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-92-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-92-5","r":"q2-92","title":"2:92 · Clear signs and the idol of desire","text":"ثم عدّد الحق تعالى عليهم مساوئ تقدمت لأسلافهم تبطل دعوى إيمانهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-92-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-92-s1","r":"q2-92","title":"The circumstantial clause","text":"I say: “while you were wrongdoers” ( وأنتم ظالمون ) is a circumstantial clause relating to “you took.”","anchor":"en-q2-92-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-92-s2","r":"q2-92","title":"Signs that did not bear fruit","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Moses came to you with manifest miracles, such as the staff, the hand and the parting of the sea. Yet they did not produce their effect in you: after he went to the Mount you took the calf as a god to worship, doing wrong. Where, then, is your claim to believe the Torah?","anchor":"en-q2-92-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-92-s3","r":"q2-92","title":"The available physician and the refusal of healing","text":"One also says to a person who persists in his fault and accepts the sickness of his heart until he meets God with a sick heart: My friends came to you with clear signs. Even if they did no more than heal the sick—I mean those whose hearts are sick—that would suffice. Yet you made desire your god and worshipped the immediate world with your hearts. Your selves and your money were too dear to you, and you wronged yourselves by persisting in your defects when the physician was present for whoever sought healing, thought well and witnessed purity. “Be a seeker and you will find a guide.” Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-92-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-92-s4","r":"q2-92","title":"","text":"The Real Most High recounts earlier faults of their forefathers that invalidate their claim to faith, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-92-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-93","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf 2:93","anchor":"unit-q2-93"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-93-1","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"وَإِذْ أَخَذْنا مِيثاقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنا فَوْقَكُمُ الطُّورَ خُذُوا ما آتَيْناكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ وَاسْمَعُوا قالُوا سَمِعْنا وَعَصَيْنا وَأُشْرِبُوا فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ الْعِجْلَ بِكُفْرِهِمْ قُلْ بِئْسَما يَأْمُرُكُمْ بِهِ إِيمانُكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ (93)","anchor":"ar-q2-93-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-93-2","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"قلت: (إن كنتم) : شرط حُذف جوابه، أي: إن كنتم مؤمنين فبئس ما يأمركم به إيمانكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-93-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-93-3","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاذكروا أيضاً إِذْ أَخَذْنا مِيثاقَكُمْ أن تعملوا بالتوراة فأبيتم وَرَفَعْنا فَوْقَكُمُ جبل الطُّورَ وقلنا: خُذُوا ما آتَيْناكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ واجتهاد وَاسْمَعُوا ما أقول لكم فيه قالُوا بلسان حالهم: سَمِعْنا قولك وعَصَيْنا أمرك، حيث لم يمتثلوا، أو بلسان المقال لسوء أدبهم، وَأُشْرِبُوا فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ حب الْعِجْلَ حتى صبغ فيها ورسخ رسوخ الصبغ في الثوب، لأنهم كانوا مُجَسِّمَةً، ولم يروا منظراً أعجب من العجل الذي صنعه السامري، (قل) لهم يا محمد: بِئْسَما يَأْمُرُكُمْ بِهِ إِيمانُكُمْ بالتوراة الذي ادعيتموه، إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ، لكن الإيمان لا يأمر بهذا فلستم مؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q2-93-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-93-4","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لمن ادعى كمال الإيمان، وهو منكر على أهل الإحسان، مع إقامته على عوائد نفسه، وكونه محجوباً بشهود حسه: وإذ أخذنا ميثاقكم، بأن تجاهدوا نفوسكم، وتخرقوا عوائدكم لتدخلوا حضرة","anchor":"ar-q2-93-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-93-5","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"ربكم، ورفعنا فوق رؤوسكم سيوف التخويف، أو جبال التشويق، وأوضحنا لكم سواء الطريق، وقلنا لكم: خذوا ما آتيناكم من خرق العوائد، واكتساب الفوائد، بجد واجتهاد، فأبيتم وعزَّت عليكم نُفوسكم، وقلتم بلسان حالكم:","anchor":"ar-q2-93-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-93-6","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"سمعنا وعصينا، وأشربت قلوبكم حب العاجلة، وآثرتم الدنيا على الآخرة، بئسما يأمركم به إيمانكم إن كنتم مؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q2-93-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-93-7","r":"q2-93","title":"2:93 · The heart imbued with love of the calf","text":"ومن جملة ما ادعاه اليهود اختصاصهم بالجنة، فردَّ الله عليهم بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-93-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-93-s1","r":"q2-93","title":"The omitted conditional response","text":"I say: “if you are” is a conditional clause whose response is omitted: if you are believers, wretched is what your faith commands you.","anchor":"en-q2-93-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-93-s2","r":"q2-93","title":"Love fixed in the heart like dye in cloth","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember also when We bound you to act according to the Torah, but you refused. We raised the Mount above you and said: hold firmly and earnestly to what We have given you, and hear what I tell you in it. They said through the tongue of their state, by failing to comply, “We have heard Your speech and disobeyed Your command”; or they said it aloud, through bad comportment. Their hearts drank in love of the calf until it coloured them and became fixed as dye becomes fixed in cloth. For they were corporealists ( مجسّمة ) and had never seen a sight more wonderful than the calf fashioned by al-Sāmirī. Say to them, Muḥammad: wretched is what your alleged faith in the Torah commands you, if you are believers. Faith, however, does not command this, so you are not believers.","anchor":"en-q2-93-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-93-s3","r":"q2-93","title":"The covenant to struggle against habitual patterns","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says to someone claiming perfect faith while denying the people of spiritual excellence, persisting in his soul’s habits and veiled by witnessing sensible things: We took your covenant to struggle against your lower selves and break your habits, so that you might enter your Lord’s presence. We raised above your heads the swords of warning or the mountains of longing, made the level way clear, and told you to take earnestly what We gave you of breaking habits and acquiring benefits. But you refused: your selves were too dear to you. Through the tongue of your state you said, “We hear and disobey.” Your hearts drank in love of the immediate world, and you preferred this world to the next. Wretched is what your faith commands you, if you are believers.","anchor":"en-q2-93-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-93-s4","r":"q2-93","title":"","text":"Among the Jews’ claims was that Paradise belonged exclusively to them. God refuted them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-93-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-94-95","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God 2:94–95","anchor":"unit-q2-94-95"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-1","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"قُلْ إِنْ كانَتْ لَكُمُ الدَّارُ الْآخِرَةُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ خالِصَةً مِنْ دُونِ النَّاسِ فَتَمَنَّوُا الْمَوْتَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (94) وَلَنْ يَتَمَنَّوْهُ أَبَداً بِما قَدَّمَتْ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِالظَّالِمِينَ (95)","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-2","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"قلت: (خالصة) خبر كان، و (عند) متعلق بكان على الأصح.","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-3","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد لبني إسرائيل الذين ادعوا أن الجنة خاصة بهم: إِنْ كانَتْ لَكُمُ الدَّارُ الْآخِرَةُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ أي: في غيبه، خالِصَةً لكم مِنْ دُونِ سائر النَّاسِ، أو من دون المسلمين، فَتَمَنَّوُا الْمَوْتَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في اختصاصكم بها، فإن العبد إذا تحقق أنه صائر إليها اشتاق إلى الموت الذي يوصل إليها، كما قال عمار رضي الله عنه عند موته:","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-4","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"الآنَ ألاقِي الأحِبَّهْ ... مُحَمَّداً وحِزْبَه","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-5","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"وقال حذيفة رضي الله عنه حين احتضر: (جَاءَ حَبِيبٌ عَلَى فَاقَة، لاَ أَفْلَحَ مَنْ نَدِم) . أي: على التمني، أو على الدنيا.","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-6","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"قال تعالى: وَلَنْ يَتَمَنَّوْهُ أَبَداً بسبب بِما قَدَّمَتْ أَيْدِيهِمْ من الكفر والعصيان، فما تمناه أحد منهم قط، قال ابن عباس: (لو أن اليهود تمنوا الموت لماتوا ورأوا مقاعدهم في النار) . وقال فى الإحياء:","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-7","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"(دعا- عليه الصلاة والسلام- اليهود إلى تمني الموت، وأخبرهم بأنهم لا يتمنونه، فحيل بينهم وبين النطق بذلك) . وذكر غيره: أن بعضهم تمناه، فما جاءت العشاء حتى أخذته الدّبحة في حلقه فمات .","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-8","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِالظَّالِمِينَ، فيه تهديد لهم وتنبيه على أنهم ظالمون في دعوى ما ليس لهم، ونفيه عمن هو لهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-9","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"الإشارة: في هذه الآية ميزان صحيح توزن به الأعمال والأحوال ويتميز به المدعون من الأبطال، فكل عمل يهدمه الموت فهو مدخول، وكل حال يهزمه الموت فهو معلول، وكل من فرّ من الموت فهو في دعواه المحبة كذاب، فمن ادعى الخصوصية على الناس يختبر بهذه الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-10","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"والناس في حب البقاء في الدنيا على أربعة أقسام:","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-11","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"رجل أحب البقاء في الدنيا لاغتنام لَذَّاته ونيل شهواته، قد طرح أخراه، وأكبَّ على دنياه، واتخذ إلهه هواه، فأصمه ذلك وأعماه، إن ذُكر له الموت فرّ عنه وشرد، وإن وعِظَ أنِف وعَنَدَ، عمره ينقص، وحرصه يزيد، وجسمه يبلى، وأمله جديد، وحتفه قريب، ومطلبه بعيد، فهذا إن لم تكن له عناية أزلية، وسابقة أولية فيمسك عليه الإيمان، ويختم له بالإسلام، وإلا فقد هلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-12","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"ورجل قد أزيل عن عينه قذاها، وأبصر نفسه وهواها، وزجرها ونهاها، قد شمر ليتلافى ما فات، ونظر فيما هو آت، وتأهب لحلول الممات، والانتقال إلى محلة الأموات، ومع هذا فإنه يكره الموت أن يشاهد وقائعه، أو يرى طلائعه، وليس يكره الموت لذاته، ولا لأنه هَادِمْ لَذَّاتِهِ، لكنه يخاف أن يقطعه عن الاستعداد ليوم المعاد، ويكره أن تطوى صحيفةِ عَمَلِهِ قبل بلوغ أمله، وأن يبادر بأجله قبل صلاح خلله، فهو يريد البقاء في هذه الدار لقضاء هذه الأوطار، فهذا ما أفضل حياته: وأطيب مماته! لا يدخل تحت قوله صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: «مَنْ كَرِهَ لِقَاءَ اللهِ كره اللهُ لِقَاءَه» .","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-13","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"ورجل آخر قد عرف الله تعالى بأسمائه الحسنى، وصفاته العليا، وشهد ما شهد من كمال الربوبية، وجمال حضرة الألوهية، فملأت عينه وقلبه، وأطاشت عقله ولبّه، فهو يحن إلى ذلك المشهد، ويستعجل إنجاز ذلك الموعد، قد علم أن الحياة الدنيوية حجابٌ بينه وبين محبوبه، وسترٌ مُسدل بينه وبين مطلوبه، فهذا من المحبين العشاق، قد حنّ إلى الوصال والتلاق، أحب لقاء الله فأحب الله لقاءه، فما أحسن حياته ولقاءه! ورجل آخر قد شهد ما شاهد ذلك، وربما زاد على ما هنالك، لكنه فوّض الأمر إلى خالقه، وسلّم الأمر لبارئه، فلم يرض إلا ما رضي له، ولم يرد إلا ما أريد به، وما اختار إلا ما حكم به فيه، إن أبقاه في هذه الدار أبقاه، وإن أخذه فهو بغيته ومناه، فهذا من العارفين المقربين. جعلنا الله منهم بمنِّه وكرمه. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-94-95-15","r":"q2-94-95","title":"2:94–95 · Longing for the meeting with God","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى ما يبطل دعواهم أن الجنة خالصة لهم؛ وهو حرصهم على البقاء في هذه الدار، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-94-95-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-94-95-s1","r":"q2-94-95","title":"Exclusivity and the predicate","text":"I say: “exclusively” ( خالصة ) is the predicate of kāna . On the sounder view, “with” ( عند ) is attached to kāna .","anchor":"en-q2-94-95-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-94-95-s2","r":"q2-94-95","title":"An exclusive claim put to the test","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: tell the Children of Israel who claim that Paradise is theirs alone: if the abode of the Hereafter with God—that is, in His unseen knowledge—belongs exclusively to you, apart from everyone else or apart from the Muslims, wish for death, if your claim is true. For when a servant is certain that he is going to Paradise, he longs for the death that brings him there. As ʿAmmār, God be pleased with him, said when dying: Now I meet the beloved ones: Muḥammad and his company. Ḥudhayfa, God be pleased with him, said at the approach of death: “A beloved friend has come at a time of need. May whoever regrets it not prosper”—meaning regret for wishing for it, or regret over the world. [B062] God Most High says: they will never wish for it, because their hands have sent ahead unbelief and disobedience. None of them ever wished for it. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “Had the Jews wished for death, they would have died and seen their places in the Fire.” In the Iḥyāʾ : “He, peace and blessings be upon him, invited the Jews to wish for death and told them they would not wish for it: they were prevented from uttering it.” Another writer mentions that one of them did wish for it, and before nightfall a choking inflammation took him in the throat and he died. “God knows the wrongdoers” threatens them and indicates their wrongdoing in claiming what is not theirs and denying it to those to whom it belongs.","anchor":"en-q2-94-95-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-94-95-s3","r":"q2-94-95","title":"Four attitudes towards remaining in this world","text":"This verse contains a sound balance in which deeds and states are weighed and pretenders distinguished from true champions. Every deed that death demolishes is adulterated; every state that death defeats is defective. Whoever flees death lies in claiming love. A person claiming special election above others is tested by this verse. People fall into four classes in their love of remaining in this world. One loves to remain in order to seize its pleasures and satisfy his desires. He casts aside his Hereafter, bends over his world and takes his desire as his god; this deafens and blinds him. Mention death and he flees; admonish him and he takes offence and resists. His lifespan diminishes while his avidity grows; his body wears out while his expectations renew themselves. His death is near, his aspirations remote. Unless eternal care and an antecedent gift preserve his faith and seal his life with Islam, he is lost. [Translator’s note: Cairo I:138 prints إن لم تكن له عناية أزلية ... فيمسك عليه الإيمان ... وإلا فقد هلك: “if there is no eternal care,” followed by preservation of faith and “otherwise he has perished.” The corresponding passage in ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq al-Ishbīlī’s al-ʿĀqiba (ed. Khiḍr Muḥammad Khiḍr, 1406/1986, p. 29) has the same difficult negative conditional, with dual pronouns for its preceding two classes. A public manuscript facsimile of that earlier work (Wikisource file al-ʿĀqiba fī aḥwāl al-ākhira kh. , PDF image 7, visible folio numeral 4) omits this entire conditional and the following supplication. It supplies no variant particle and does not settle the difficulty. The English expresses the contextual warning; the exact syntax and authorial wording remain unresolved.] Another has had the mote removed from his eye: he perceives his soul and its desires, restrains and forbids it, girds himself to make good what has passed, considers what is coming, and prepares for death and departure to the dwelling of the dead. Yet he dislikes witnessing death’s events or seeing its advance guard. He dislikes it neither for its own sake nor because it destroys his pleasures, but fears being cut off from preparation for the Day of Return. He dislikes having his record of deeds rolled up before attaining his hope, or his term arriving before he has put his defects right. He wishes to remain here to fulfil these purposes. How excellent his life, how good his death! He is not included in the saying, “Whoever dislikes meeting God, God dislikes meeting him.” A third knows God through His most beautiful Names and highest Attributes. He has witnessed something of the perfection of Lordship and the beauty of the presence of Divinity; it fills his eyes and heart and carries away his reason and understanding. He yearns for that vision and hastens towards fulfilment of that promise. He knows that worldly life is a veil between him and his Beloved, a hanging curtain between him and what he seeks. Such a person is among the passionate lovers, longing for union and encounter. He loves meeting God, and God loves meeting him. How beautiful his life and his meeting! A fourth has witnessed what the third witnessed, perhaps more. But he entrusts the matter to his Creator and surrenders it to his Maker. He approves only what is approved for him, desires only what is desired for him, and chooses only what is decreed concerning him. If God keeps him here, He keeps him; if He takes him, that is his desire and hope. He is among the gnostics brought near. May God make us among them through His favour and generosity. Amen. The Real Most High then mentions what refutes their claim that the Garden belongs exclusively to them: their eagerness to remain in this abode. He says:","anchor":"en-q2-94-95-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-96","r":"q2-96","title":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience","text":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience 2:96","anchor":"unit-q2-96"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-96-1","r":"q2-96","title":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience","text":"وَلَتَجِدَنَّهُمْ أَحْرَصَ النَّاسِ عَلى حَياةٍ وَمِنَ الَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا يَوَدُّ أَحَدُهُمْ لَوْ يُعَمَّرُ أَلْفَ سَنَةٍ وَما هُوَ بِمُزَحْزِحِهِ مِنَ الْعَذابِ أَنْ يُعَمَّرَ وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ (96)","anchor":"ar-q2-96-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-96-2","r":"q2-96","title":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience","text":"قلت: (ومن الذين أشركوا) : على حذف مضاف، أي: وأحرص من الذين أشركوا، فيوقف عليه، و (لو يعمر) مصدرية، أي: يود أحدهم تعمير ألف سنة. و (أن يعمر) فاعل لمزحزحه، أي: وما هو بمزحزحه من العذاب تعميره.","anchor":"ar-q2-96-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-96-3","r":"q2-96","title":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولتجدن يا محمد اليهود أَحْرَصَ النَّاسِ على البقاء في هذه الدار الدنية، فكيف يزعمون أنهم أولى الناس بالجنة، ولتجدنهم أيضاً أحرص من المشركين على البقاء، مع كونهم لا يقرون بالجزاء، فدلَّ ذلك على أنهم صائرون إلى النار، فلذلك كرهوا اللقاء وحرصوا على البقاء، يتمنى أحدهم لو يعيش أَلْفَ سَنَةٍ وليس ذلك بِمُزَحْزِحِهِ أي: مبعده من العذاب ، بل زيادة له في العقاب وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ: تهديد وتخويف.","anchor":"ar-q2-96-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-96-4","r":"q2-96","title":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience","text":"الإشارة: يفهم من سر الخطاب إن كل من قصر أمله، وحسن عمله، وطيب نفسه للقاء الحبيب، واشتغل في هذه اللحظة القصيرة بما يقربه من القريب، كان قربه من الله بقدر محبته للقائه، وكل من طوّل أمله، وحرص على البقاء في هذه الدار الفانية، كان بُعده من الله بقدر محبته للبقاء، إلا من أحب البقاء لزيادة الأعمال، أو الترقي في المقامات والأحوال، فلا بأس به، ويفهم منه أيضاً أن مَن اشتد حرصه على الحياة الفانية كانت فيه نزعة يهودية.","anchor":"ar-q2-96-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-96-5","r":"q2-96","title":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience","text":"واعلم أن الناس، في طول الأمل وقصره، على قسمين: منهم من طوّل في أمله فازداد في كسله، ودخله الوهن في عمله، وآخر قد قصر أملُه وجعل التقوى بضاعته، والعبادة صناعته، ولم يتجاوز بأمله ساعته، ومثل هذا قد رفع التوفيق عليه لواءه، وألبسه رداءه، وأعطاه جماله وبهاءه، فانظر رحمك الله أيّ الرجلين تريد أن تكون، وأي العملين تريد أن تعمل، وبأى الرداءين تريد أن تشتمل؟ فلست تلبس هناك إلا ما تلبس هنا. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-96-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-96-6","r":"q2-96","title":"2:96 · Lengthy expectations and present obedience","text":"ومن أشنع كفر بنى إسرائيل وأقبح مساوئهم، بغضهم لجبريل عليه السّلام وإلى ذلك أشار الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-96-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-96-s1","r":"q2-96","title":"The omitted comparison and the infinitival construction","text":"I say: “and of those who associate partners” involves an omitted comparative: “and more eager than those who associate partners”; one therefore pauses after this phrase. Law in “that he might live long” is infinitival ( مصدرية ): each desires a lifespan of a thousand years. “That he should live long” is the agent of “removing”: his longevity would not remove him from punishment.","anchor":"en-q2-96-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-96-s2","r":"q2-96","title":"A life prolonged does not secure deliverance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Muḥammad, you will find the Jews most eager to remain in this lowly abode. How then do they claim greatest entitlement to Paradise? You will find them more eager to remain than the polytheists, although the latter do not acknowledge requital. This indicates that they are destined for the Fire; hence their aversion to the meeting and eagerness to remain. Each wishes to live a thousand years, but this would not remove or distance him from punishment; rather, it would increase his requital. “God sees what they do” is a warning and a threat.","anchor":"en-q2-96-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-96-s3","r":"q2-96","title":"The garment worn here and hereafter","text":"The inward import of the address teaches that whoever shortens his expectations, improves his deeds, makes his soul ready to meet the Beloved, and fills this brief moment with what brings him near the Near One, draws near to God in proportion to his love of meeting Him. Whoever extends his expectations and eagerly clings to this perishable abode is distant from God in proportion to his love of remaining—except one who desires further life to increase his deeds or rise through spiritual stations and states; there is no harm in this. The address also implies that extreme eagerness for perishable life contains a tendency resembling that of the Jews described here. Know that people are of two kinds concerning lengthy and brief expectations. One lengthens his hopes, increases his idleness and admits weakness into his works. Another shortens his hopes, makes mindfulness his merchandise and worship his craft, and lets his expectation reach no further than the present hour. Divine enabling ( التوفيق ) raises its banner over such a person, clothes him in its robe and bestows its beauty and splendour. Consider, God have mercy on you, which man you wish to be, which deeds you wish to perform, and which robe you wish to wear. There you will wear only what you wear here. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-96-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-96-s4","r":"q2-96","title":"","text":"Among the most odious forms of the Children of Israel’s unbelief and their worst faults was hatred of Gabriel, peace be upon him. The Real points to it, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-96-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-97-98","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures 2:97–98","anchor":"unit-q2-97-98"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-1","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"قُلْ مَنْ كانَ عَدُوًّا لِجِبْرِيلَ فَإِنَّهُ نَزَّلَهُ عَلى قَلْبِكَ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ مُصَدِّقاً لِما بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَهُدىً وَبُشْرى لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ (97) مَنْ كانَ عَدُوًّا لِلَّهِ وَمَلائِكَتِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَجِبْرِيلَ وَمِيكالَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَدُوٌّ لِلْكافِرِينَ (98)","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-2","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"قلت: (من) شرطية وجوابها محذوف، أي: فليمت غيظاً، أو (فإنه نزله) على معنى: مَن عادى منهم جبريل فقد خلع ربقة الإنصاف، أو كفر بما معه من الكتاب لأنه نزل بكتاب مصدقاً لما قبله من الكتب، وجبريل فيه ثماني لغات، أربع قرئ بهن. وهي: جَبْرَئِيل كسلسبيل. وجَبْرَئِل كجحْمرش، وجَبْريل- بفتح الجيم- بلا همز، وجِبْرِيل بكسرها، وأربع شواذ: جِبْرَالُ، وجَبْرَائِيل، وجَبْرِائل، وجَبْرين بالنون، ومعناه: عبد الله. وفي ميكائيل أربع لغات: ميكائيل ممدود، وميكائل مقصور، وميكئل مهموز مقصور، وميكال على وزن ميعاد.","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-3","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في الرد على اليهود، كابن صُوريا وغيره، حيث قالوا للنبيّ صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: من الذي يأتيك بالوحي؟ فقال: جبريل، فقالوا: ذلك عدونا من الملائكة لأنه ينزل بالشدة والعذاب، ولو كان ميكائيل لاتبعناك لأنه ينزل بالخصب والسلم، فقال تعالى: مَنْ كانَ عَدُوًّا لِجِبْرِيلَ فليمت غيظاً، فإنه هو الذي نزَّل القرآن عَلى قَلْبِكَ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ مُصَدِّقاً لِما بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ من الكتب، وهداية وَبُشْرى لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ، فإن كان ينزل بالشدة والعذاب على الكافرين، فإنه ينزل بالهداية والبشارة على المؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-4","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"ومن كان عدواً لجبريل فإنه عدو لله، إذ هو رسوله للأنبياء، وصفيه من الملائكة، وعدو أيضاً لميكائيل فإنه وزيره، وللرسل أيضاً فإنه سفيرهم، ومَنْ كانَ عَدُوًّا لِلَّهِ وَمَلائِكَتِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَجِبْرِيلَ وَمِيكالَ فإن الله عدو له.","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-5","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"وعطف جبريل وميكائيل من عطف الخاص على العام لزيادة شرفهما. ووضع الظاهر موضع الضمير في قوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-6","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"عَدُوٌّ لِلْكافِرِينَ ولم يقل: لهم، تسجيلاً عليهم بالكفر، وبيان أن الله إنما عاداهم لكفرهم، وأن عداوة الملائكة والرسل كفر، عصمنا الله من موارد الردى. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-7","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"الإشارة: إذا كانت معاداة الملائكة والرسل هي معاداة الله، فكذلك معاداةُ أوليائه هي معاداة الله أيضاً، ولذلك قال تعالى: «مَنْ عادى لي وليّاً فقد آذنني بالحَرْب» . فالبعض هو الكل، ويؤخذ بالمفهوم أن محبة الملائكة والرسل هي محبة الله. وكذلك محبة أولياء الله هي محبة الله، وكذلك أيضاً محبة عباد الله هي محبة الله، ومعاداتهم معاداة الله. «الخَلقُ عِيَالُ اللَّهِ، وأحبُّ الخَلْقِِِ إلى اللَّهِ أَنفَعُهُم لِعيَاله» . وكل مَن ادعى أنه يحب الله وفي قلبه عداوة لمسلم فهو كاذب، وكل مَن ادعى أنه يعرف الله وفي قلبه إنكار على مخلوق فهو في دعواه أيضاً كاذب، فالواجب على العبد أن يُحب جميع العباد، من كان طائعاً فظاهر. ومَن كان عاصياً أحب له التوبة والإنابة، ومَن كان كافراً أحب له الإسلام والهداية، ولا يكره من العبد إلا فعله، ولله دَر القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-8","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"ارْحَمْ بُنَيَّ جَميعَ الخلقِ كُلِّهمُ ... وانْظُرْ إليْهمْ بعين الحِلمِ والشّفَقَهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-9","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"وَقَّرْ كَبيرَهُم وارْحَمْ صغِيرَهُمْ ... وَراع في كلّ خلق حقّ مَنْ خَلَقَهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-10","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-97-98-11","r":"q2-97-98","title":"2:97–98 · Gabriel, revelation and love of God’s creatures","text":"ولما قال ابن صوريا للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: يا محمد ما جئت بشئ نعرفه، وما أنزل الله عليك من آية بينة فنتبعك لها فنزل قوله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q2-97-98-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-97-98-s1","r":"q2-97-98","title":"The conditional response and the angels’ names","text":"I say: “whoever” ( من ) is conditional, with an omitted response: let him die in his rage. Or “it is he who brought it down” is the response, meaning: whoever among them opposes Gabriel has cast off the bond of fairness, or disbelieved in the Book he possesses, for Gabriel brought a Book confirming the earlier Books. Gabriel’s name has eight forms, four occurring in the readings: جَبْرَئِيل , patterned like salsabīl ; جَبْرَئِل , like jaḥmarish ; جَبْريل with an a on the jīm and no hamza; and جِبْرِيل with an i . Four are anomalous: جِبْرَال، جَبْرَائِيل، جَبْرِائل، جَبْرين , the last with nūn. Its meaning is “servant of God.” Michael has four forms: ميكائيل with lengthening, ميكائل shortened, ميكئل with hamza and shortening, and ميكال on the pattern of mīʿād . [B063]","anchor":"en-q2-97-98-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-97-98-s2","r":"q2-97-98","title":"Dividing between the messengers","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, replies to Jews such as Ibn Ṣūriyā and others who asked the Prophet, “Who brings you revelation?” He answered, “Gabriel.” They said, “That is our enemy among the angels, for he brings severity and punishment. Were it Michael, we would follow you, because he brings fertility and peace.” God Most High says: whoever is Gabriel’s enemy, let him die in his rage, for Gabriel brought the Qurʾān down upon your heart by God’s permission, confirming the preceding Books and bringing guidance and good tidings to believers. If he descends with severity and punishment upon unbelievers, he descends with guidance and good tidings upon believers. An enemy of Gabriel is an enemy of God, for Gabriel is His messenger to the prophets and His chosen one among the angels. Such a person is also an enemy of Michael, Gabriel’s companion in ministry, and of the messengers, whose envoy Gabriel is. Whoever is an enemy to God, His angels and His messengers, Gabriel and Michael, has God as his enemy. The addition of Gabriel and Michael after “angels” is the conjunction of the particular to the general ( عطف الخاص على العام ), enhancing their honour. In “an enemy to the unbelievers,” the explicit expression replaces “to them,” registering their unbelief and showing that God opposes them because of it, and that enmity towards angels and messengers is unbelief. May God preserve us from the paths of ruin. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-97-98-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-97-98-s3","r":"q2-97-98","title":"Love of all servants, hatred of the wrongful act","text":"If hostility to angels and messengers is hostility to God, hostility to His friends is likewise hostility to God. Thus He says: “Whoever opposes a friend of Mine has declared war against Me.” The part here is the whole. Conversely, love of angels and messengers is love of God, as is love of His friends. Love of God’s servants is also love of God, and hostility to them hostility to Him: “Creation are God’s dependants, and the most beloved creatures to God are those most beneficial to His dependants.” [B065] Whoever claims to love God while harbouring enmity towards a Muslim is lying; whoever claims to know God while harbouring rejection of a creature is likewise lying in his claim. The servant must love all servants. In the case of the obedient this is evident; for the disobedient he loves repentance and return; for the unbelieving he loves Islam and guidance. Nothing should be hated in the servant but his act. How fine are these words: My son, have mercy on every creature; regard them with forbearance and compassion. Honour their elders, be merciful to their young; in every creature observe the right of its Creator. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-97-98-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-97-98-s4","r":"q2-97-98","title":"","text":"When Ibn Ṣūriyā told the Prophet, “Muḥammad, you have brought nothing we recognize, and God has sent down no clear sign to you that we should follow you for it,” these words were revealed:","anchor":"en-q2-97-98-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-99","r":"q2-99","title":"2:99 · Manifest signs and inward recognition","text":"2:99 · Manifest signs and inward recognition 2:99","anchor":"unit-q2-99"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-99-1","r":"q2-99","title":"2:99 · Manifest signs and inward recognition","text":"وَلَقَدْ أَنْزَلْنا إِلَيْكَ آياتٍ بَيِّناتٍ وَما يَكْفُرُ بِها إِلاَّ الْفاسِقُونَ (99)","anchor":"ar-q2-99-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-99-2","r":"q2-99","title":"2:99 · Manifest signs and inward recognition","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَقَدْ أَنْزَلْنا إِلَيْكَ يا محمد آياتٍ واضحات، مشتملة على علوم غيبية، وأخبار نبوية، وشرائع محكمة، وأنوار قدسية، وأسرار جبروتية، وما يجحدها ويكفر بها إلا المتمرد في الكفر والطغيان، الخارج عن الطاعة والإيمان، فالفسق، إذا استعمل في نوع من المعاصي، دلّ على أعظمه وأقبحه، وهو هنا الكفر، والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q2-99-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-99-3","r":"q2-99","title":"2:99 · Manifest signs and inward recognition","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن العبد إذا سبقت له من الله العناية، ألقى الله في قلبه التصديق والهداية، من غير أن يحتاج إلى علامة ولا آية، بل يكشف له الحق تعالى عن سر الخصوصية وأنوارها، فيشهد سره لصاحبها بالتقويم، وتخضع له روحه بالتعظيم، فتبدو له أنوار الإيمان وتشرق عليه شموس العرفان، من غير توقف على دليل ولا برهان، بخلاف من سبق له الحرمان، فلا ينجح فيه دليل ولا برهان، والعياذ بالله من الخذلان.","anchor":"ar-q2-99-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-99-4","r":"q2-99","title":"2:99 · Manifest signs and inward recognition","text":"ولما ذَكّر النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم اليهود في شأن العهد الذي أخذه الله عليهم فيه، قال مالك بن الصيف: والله ما عهد إلينا في محمد عهدٌ ولا ميثاق، نزل:","anchor":"ar-q2-99-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-99-s1","r":"q2-99","title":"The scope of the clear signs","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: We have sent down to you, Muḥammad, manifest signs containing knowledge of the unseen, prophetic accounts, firmly established ordinances, holy lights and mysteries of the realm of Divine Omnipotence ( الجبروت ). None rejects them and disbelieves in them but those rebellious in unbelief and tyranny, outside obedience and faith. When “transgression” ( فسق ) is employed of a particular kind of disobedience, it indicates its greatest and worst form: here, unbelief. In God is refuge.","anchor":"en-q2-99-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-99-s2","r":"q2-99","title":"Recognition bestowed before an external proof","text":"Know that when divine care has preceded for a servant, God casts affirmation and guidance into his heart without need of a sign or miracle. The Real unveils to him the mystery and lights of special election. His secret bears witness to its possessor’s rectitude; his spirit bows in reverence. Faith’s lights appear and the suns of gnosis shine upon him without dependence on a proof or demonstration. The opposite holds for one for whom deprivation has preceded: neither proof nor demonstration benefits him. We seek refuge in God from abandonment.","anchor":"en-q2-99-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-99-s3","r":"q2-99","title":"","text":"When the Prophet reminded the Jews of the covenant God had taken concerning him, Mālik ibn al-Ṣayf said, “By God, no undertaking or covenant concerning Muḥammad has been made with us.” Then there was revealed:","anchor":"en-q2-99-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-100","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority 2:100","anchor":"unit-q2-100"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-1","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"أَوَكُلَّما عاهَدُوا عَهْداً نَبَذَهُ فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ (100)","anchor":"ar-q2-100-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-2","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"قلت: الهمزة للإنكار، والواو للعطف على محذوف تقديره: أَكفروا بالآيات وكلما عاهدوا عهدا، وكُلَّما منصوب على الظرفية، وهي متضمنة معنى الشرط فتفتقر للجواب، وهو العامل فيها. والنبذ: الطرح، لكنه يغلب فيما ينسى، قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-100-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-3","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في شأن اليهود والإنكار عليهم: أَوَكُلَّما أعطوا عهداً وعقدوه على أنفسهم طرحه فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ؟ فقد أعطوا العهد أنهم إن أدركوا محمدا صلّى الله عليه وسلّم ليؤمنن به ولينصرنه، فلما أدركوه نبذوا ذلك العهد ونسوه. وكذلك أعطوا العهد للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلّم ألا يعاونوا المشركين عليه، فنبذه بنو قريظة والنضير، ولم ينقضه جميعهم بل فريق منهم، وهم الأكثر، ولذلك قال: بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ، فالأكثر هم الناقضون للعهود، المجاوزون للحدود. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-100-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-4","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"الإشارة: نقض العهد مع الله أو مع عباده من علامة النفاق، ومن شيم أهل البعاد والشقاق، والوفاء بالعهد من علامة الإيمان، ومن شيم أهل المحبة والعرفان. قال تعالى في صفة المفلحين: وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ لِأَماناتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ راعُونَ، ولا سيما عهود الشيوخ أهل التمكين والرسوخ. فمن أخذ عقد الصحبة مع الشيخ الذي هو أهل للتربية فليحذر مِنْ حَلّ العقدة بينه وبينه، فإنَّ ذلك يقطع الإمداد، ويوجب الطرد والبعاد، والالتفات إلى غيره تسويس لبذرة الإرادة، وموجب لقطع الزيادة والإفادة، ثم إن الانجماع على الشيخ، وقطع النظر والالتفات إلى غيره هو سبب للكون- كذلك- مع الله، فبقدر الانقطاع إلى الشيخ يحصل الانقطاع إلى الله، وبقدر ترك الاختيار وسلب الإرادة مع الشيخ يحصل كذلك مع الله، وبقدر الوفاء بعهود شيوخ التربية يحصل الوفاء بعهود حقوق الربوبية. فمن كانت غيبته في الشيخ أقوى، وانحياشه أليه أكثر، وجمعه عليه أدوم، كان كذلك مع ربه، وكذلك التعظيم والأدب، والله يعامل العبد على حسب ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-100-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-5","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"قال الشيخ زرّوق رضي الله عنه: (ولا تنتقلْ عنه، ولو رأيت من هو أعلى منه، فتحرمَ بركة الأول والثاني) ، ولذلك كان المشايخ يمنعون أصحابهم من صحبة غيرهم، بل من زيارتهم، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-100-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-6","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"خُذْ مَا تَراهُ ودَعْ شَيْئاً سَمِعتَ بِهِ ... في طلْعَةِ البدرِ ما يُغنيكَ عن زُحَلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-100-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-7","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"وحاصل أمر الزيارة لغير شيخه أن فيه تفصيلاً: فمن كَمُل صدقه، وتوفر عقله، بحيث إذا زار لا يستنقص شيخه، ولا الذي زاره، جازله أن يزور من شاء، ومن لم يكمل صِدقُهُ وعقله، بحيث إذا زار: إما يستنقص شيخه، أو الشيخ الذي زاره، فليكف عن زيارة غير شيخه. وقال محيي الدين بن العربي: ويجب على المريد أن يعتقد في شيخه أنه عالم بالله، ناصح لخلق الله، ولا ينبغي له أن يعتقد في شيخه العصمة. وقد قيل للجنيد: أيزني العارف؟","anchor":"ar-q2-100-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-8","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"فقال: وَكانَ أَمْرُ اللَّهِ قَدَراً مَقْدُوراً. وصحب تلميذ شيخاً، فرآه يوماً قد زنا بامرأة، فلم يتغير من خدمته، ولا أخلّ في شيء من مرسومات شيخه، ولا ظهر منه نقص في احترامه. وقد عرف الشيخ أنه رآه، فقال له يوماً:","anchor":"ar-q2-100-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-9","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"يا بني قد عَرَفْتُ أنك رأيتني حين فسقتُ بتلك المرأة، وكنت أنتظر فراقك عني من أجل ذلك، فقال له التلميذ:","anchor":"ar-q2-100-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-10","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"يا سيدي الإنسان معرض لمجاري أقدار الله عليه، وإني من الوقت الذي دخلت فيه إلى خدمتك ما خدمتك على أنك معصوم، وإنما خدمتك على أنك عارف بطريق الله تعالى، عارف بكيفية السلوك عليه الذي هو طلبي، وكونك تعصي أو لا تعصي شيء بينك وبين الله عز وجل، لا يرجع من ذلك شيء عَلَيَّ، فما وقع منك يا سيدي شيء لا يوجب نفاري وزوالي عنك، وهذا هو عَقْدي، فقال له الشيخ: وفقت وسعدت هكذا وإلا فلا ... فربح ذلك التلميذ، وجاء منه ما تَقَرُّ بِهِ العينُ من حسن الحال وعُلوِّ المقام . هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-100-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-100-11","r":"q2-100","title":"2:100 · Fidelity to covenants and the limits of a guide’s authority","text":"ولما وسمهم الحق تعالى بنقض العهود، ذكر جزئية من ذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-100-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-100-s1","r":"q2-100","title":"The interrogative and repeated condition","text":"I say: the hamza expresses disapproval. The wāw connects with an omitted clause: have they disbelieved in the signs, and whenever they make a covenant…? “Whenever” ( كلما ) is accusative as an adverbial expression. It includes conditional meaning and requires a response, which governs it. Nabdh ( نبذ ) is casting away, most often used of what is forgotten, according to al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q2-100-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-100-s2","r":"q2-100","title":"A group, not every member","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, reproaches the Jews: whenever they give an undertaking and bind themselves by it, does a group cast it away? They undertook that, if they lived to see Muḥammad, they would believe in and support him; when they did see him, they cast aside and forgot the undertaking. They also promised the Prophet not to assist the polytheists against him, but Banū Qurayẓa and al-Naḍīr cast it aside. Not all broke it, but a group—the majority. Hence He says, “Rather, most of them do not believe.” The majority are those who break undertakings and overstep limits. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-100-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-100-s3","r":"q2-100","title":"The covenant of companionship","text":"Breaking a covenant with God or His servants is a sign of hypocrisy and a trait of estrangement and division. Keeping it is a sign of faith and a trait of love and gnosis. Describing the successful, God says, “Those who guard their trusts and their covenant” [23:8]. This applies especially to undertakings made with shaykhs of firm establishment and deep rootedness. Whoever enters the bond of companionship with a shaykh qualified for spiritual formation should beware of undoing it. That cuts off assistance and brings expulsion and distance. Turning to someone else lets the worm into the seed of aspiration and cuts off increase and benefit. Gathering oneself upon the shaykh, without looking or turning elsewhere, is a means to being so with God. In proportion to one’s exclusive orientation to the shaykh comes one’s exclusive orientation to God; in proportion to abandoning choice and surrendering self-will with the shaykh comes the same with God; in proportion to fidelity to the masters of formation comes fidelity to the rights of Lordship. One whose absorption in the shaykh is stronger, whose sheltering with him is greater, and whose collectedness upon him is more constant, is likewise with his Lord. The same applies to reverence and courtesy, and God deals with the servant accordingly. Shaykh Zarrūq, God be pleased with him, says: “Do not move away from him, even if you see one higher than him, lest you be deprived of the blessing of both the first and the second.” Hence the shaykhs used to prohibit their companions from accompanying others, even from visiting them. They recited: Take what you see, and leave what you have only heard about; the full moon’s appearance dispenses with Saturn. Visiting a shaykh other than one’s own nevertheless calls for distinction. Someone whose sincerity is complete and judgement abundant, so that a visit leads him to belittle neither his own shaykh nor the one visited, may visit whom he wishes. Someone whose sincerity and judgement are incomplete, so that a visit leads him to belittle either one, should refrain from visiting another shaykh.","anchor":"en-q2-100-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-100-s4","r":"q2-100","title":"Recognition does not imply infallibility","text":"Muḥyī al-Dīn Ibn al-ʿArabī says: a disciple must believe his shaykh to know God and sincerely counsel God’s creatures; he should not believe his shaykh infallible ( العصمة ). Al-Junayd was asked, “Can a gnostic commit fornication?” He answered, “God’s command is a decree determined” [33:38]. [B064] A disciple accompanied a shaykh and one day saw him commit fornication with a woman. He did not change his service, neglect any of his shaykh’s prescribed practices, or diminish his respect. The shaykh knew that he had seen him and said one day: “My son, I know that you saw me transgress with that woman. I expected you to leave me for that reason.” The disciple replied: “Master, a human being is exposed to the courses of God’s decrees. From the time I entered your service, I did not serve you on the assumption that you were infallible, but because you knew God’s way and how to travel it, which is what I seek. Whether you disobey or not is between you and God Most High; none of it falls upon me. What happened on your part is not something that requires me to recoil and leave you. This is my conviction.” The shaykh said: “You have been enabled and made fortunate: it is thus, or not at all.” The disciple prospered, and from him appeared what delighted the eye: a beautiful state and a lofty station. Thus ends the quotation. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-04] ]","anchor":"en-q2-100-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-100-s5","r":"q2-100","title":"","text":"Having characterized them by breach of covenants, the Real mentions a particular instance, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-100-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-101","r":"q2-101","title":"2:101 · Casting the Book behind one’s back","text":"2:101 · Casting the Book behind one’s back 2:101","anchor":"unit-q2-101"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-101-1","r":"q2-101","title":"2:101 · Casting the Book behind one’s back","text":"وَلَمَّا جاءَهُمْ رَسُولٌ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ مُصَدِّقٌ لِما مَعَهُمْ نَبَذَ فَرِيقٌ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ كِتابَ اللَّهِ وَراءَ ظُهُورِهِمْ كَأَنَّهُمْ لا يَعْلَمُونَ (101)","anchor":"ar-q2-101-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-101-2","r":"q2-101","title":"2:101 · Casting the Book behind one’s back","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَمَّا جاءَهُمْ يعني اليهود رَسُولٌ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم مُصَدِّقٌ لِما مَعَهُمْ من التوراة بموافقته له في بعض الأخبار نَبَذَ فَرِيقٌ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ، وهم من كفر من أحبار يهود، كِتابَ اللَّهِ: التوراة، وَراءَ ظُهُورِهِمْ، حيث لم يعملوا بما فيه من الأمر بالإيمان بالنبيّ صلّى الله عليه وسلّم، وغيروا صفته التي فيه، وكتموها، فكأنهم طرحوه وراء ظهورهم، وكأنهم لا علم لهم بشئ من ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-101-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-101-3","r":"q2-101","title":"2:101 · Casting the Book behind one’s back","text":"قال البيضاوي: اعلم أن الحق تعالى دل بالآيتين على أن حال اليهود أربع فرق: فرقة آمنوا بالتوراة وقاموا بحقوقها كمؤمني أهل الكتاب، وهم الأقلون المدلول عليهم بقوله: بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ، وفرقة جاهروا بنبذ عهودها، وتخطي حدودها، تمرداً وفسوقاً، وهم المعنيون بقوله تعالى: نَبَذَهُ فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ، وفرقة لم يجاهروا بنبذها، ولكن نبذوا لجهلهم بها، وهم الأكثرون، وفرقة تمسكوا بها ظاهراً، ونبذوها خفية، عالمين بالحال بَغْياً وعناداً، وهم المتجاهلون. هـ. قلت: ولعلهم المنافقون منهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-101-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-101-4","r":"q2-101","title":"2:101 · Casting the Book behind one’s back","text":"ولما نبذوا كتاب الله اشتغلوا بكتب السحر مكانه، كما أبان ذلك الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-101-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-101-s1","r":"q2-101","title":"Four responses to the Torah","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when a messenger from God—Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace—came to the Jews, confirming the Torah they possessed by agreeing with some of its accounts, a group of those given the Book, the unbelieving Jewish learned men, cast God’s Book, the Torah, behind their backs. They did not act upon its command to believe in the Prophet; they altered and concealed his description in it. It was as though they threw it behind their backs and knew nothing of this. Al-Bayḍāwī says: know that through these two verses the Real indicates four classes among the Jews. One believes the Torah and fulfils its rights, like the believers among the People of the Book. These are the minority indicated by “Rather, most of them do not believe.” Another openly casts aside its covenants and oversteps its limits through rebellion and transgression: these are meant by “a group of them casts it aside.” A third does not openly reject it, but abandons it through ignorance of it: these are the majority. A fourth adheres to it outwardly but secretly abandons it, knowingly, through transgression and obstinacy. These feign ignorance. Thus ends his statement. I say: perhaps the last are their hypocrites.","anchor":"en-q2-101-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-101-s2","r":"q2-101","title":"","text":"When they cast aside God’s Book, they occupied themselves instead with books of sorcery, as the Real makes clear in His words:","anchor":"en-q2-101-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-102-103","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world 2:102–103","anchor":"unit-q2-102-103"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-1","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"وَاتَّبَعُوا ما تَتْلُوا الشَّياطِينُ عَلى مُلْكِ سُلَيْمانَ وَما كَفَرَ سُلَيْمانُ وَلكِنَّ الشَّياطِينَ كَفَرُوا يُعَلِّمُونَ النَّاسَ السِّحْرَ وَما أُنْزِلَ عَلَى الْمَلَكَيْنِ بِبابِلَ هارُوتَ وَمارُوتَ وَما يُعَلِّمانِ","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-3","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":" مِنْ أَحَدٍ حَتَّى يَقُولا إِنَّما نَحْنُ فِتْنَةٌ فَلا تَكْفُرْ فَيَتَعَلَّمُونَ مِنْهُما مَا يُفَرِّقُونَ بِهِ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَزَوْجِهِ وَما هُمْ بِضارِّينَ بِهِ مِنْ أَحَدٍ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَيَتَعَلَّمُونَ ما يَضُرُّهُمْ وَلا يَنْفَعُهُمْ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمُوا لَمَنِ اشْتَراهُ ما لَهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلاقٍ وَلَبِئْسَ مَا شَرَوْا بِهِ أَنْفُسَهُمْ لَوْ كانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ (102) وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا وَاتَّقَوْا لَمَثُوبَةٌ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ لَوْ كانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ (103)","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-4","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"قلت: عَلى مُلْكِ سُلَيْمانَ على حذف مضاف، أي: على عهد ملك سليمان، أو «عَلَى» بمعنى «في» ، وقوله: «وَمَا أُنزِل» عطفٌ على السحر، عَطْفَ تفسير، والفتنة في الأصل: الاختبار، تقول: فتنت الذهب والفضة إذا أدخلتهما النار لتعلم جودتهما من رداءتهما، وقوله «لَمَثُوبَةٌ» جواب «لَّوْ» ، والأصل: لأثِيبوا، ثم عَدَلَ إلى الجملة الاسمية لتدل على الثبوت.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-5","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في شأن اليهود: ولما جاءهم كتاب من عند الله نبذوه وَاتَّبَعُوا ما تقرأ الشَّياطِينُ على الناس من السحر عَلى عهد مُلْكِ سُلَيْمانَ، وذلك أن الشياطين كانوا يسترقون السمع ويضمون إلى ما سمعوا أكاذيب، ويلقونها إلى الكهنة، وهم يدونونها ويعلمونها الناس، وفَشَا ذلك في عهد سليمان حتى قيل: إن الجن يعلم الغيب، وإن ملك سليمان إنما قام بهذا، وأنه به سخر الجن والإنس والريح، فجمع سليمان ما دُوِّن منه ودفنه، فاستخرجته الشياطين بعد موته، فردَّ الله تعالى قولهم بقوله: وَما كَفَرَ سُلَيْمانُ باستعمال السحر لأنه تعظيم غير الله بالتقرب للشيطان، والنبيّ معصوم، وَلكِنَّ الشَّياطِينَ هم الذين كَفَرُوا باستعماله يُعَلِّمُونَ النَّاسَ السِّحْرَ إغواء وإضلالاً، ويعلمون مَا أُنْزِلَ عَلَى الْمَلَكَيْنِ في بلد بابل من سواد الكوفة، وهما هارُوتَ وَمارُوتَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-6","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"كانا ملكين من أعبد الملائكة، ولما رأت الملائكة ما يصعد إلى السماء من أعمال بني آدم الخبيثة في زمن إدريس عليه السلام عيروهم بذلك، وقالوا: يا ربنا هؤلاء الذين جعلتهم خليفة في الأرض يعصونك؟ فقال الله تعالى: لو أنزلتكم إلى الأرض، وركَّبْتُ فيكم ما ركبت فيهم لارتكبتم ما ارتكبوا، قَالُواْ: سُبْحَانَكَ مَا كَانَ ينبغي لنا أن نعصيك.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-7","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"فقال الله تعالى: فاختاروا ملكين من خِياركم أُهبطهما إلى الأرض. فاختاروا هاروت وماروت، وكانا من أعبد","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-8","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"الملائكة، فركّب الله تعالى فيهما الشهوة، وأمرهما أن يحكما في الأرض بين الناس بالحق، ونهاهما عن الشرك والقتل بغير الحق، والزنا وشرب الخمر، فكانا يقضيان بين الناس يومهما، فإذا أمسيا ذكرا اسم الله الأعظم وصعدا إلى السماء، فاختصمت إليهما ذات يوم امرأة يقال لها الزهرة: وكانت من أجمل النساء من أهل فارس، فأخذت بقلبيهما، فراوداها عن نفسها، فأبت، ثم عاودت في اليوم الثاني، ففعلا مثل ذلك فأبت، وقالت: إلا أن تعبدا ما أعبد، وتصليا لهذا الصنم، وتقتلا النفس وتشربا الخمر، فأبيا هذه الأشياء، وقالا: إن الله نهانا عنها، فانصرفت، ثم عادت فى اليوم الثالث، فراوداها، فعرضت عليهما ما قالت بالأمس، فقالا: الصلاة لغير الله ذنب عظيم، وأهونُ الثلاثة شرب الخمر، فشربا، وانتشيا، ووقعا بالمرأة، فلما فرغا رآهما إنسان فخافا أن يظهر عليهما فقتلاه.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-9","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"وفي رواية عن سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه- أنه قال: (قالت لهما: لن تدركاني حتى تخبراني بالذي تصعدان به إلى السماء، فقالا: باسم الله الأعظم، فعلماها ذلك، فتكلمت به، وصعدت إلى السماء فمسخها الله كوكباً) . ولذلك كان عليه الصلاة والسلام إذا رأى سهيلاً قال: «لَعَنَ اللهُ سُهيلاً كَانَ عَشَّاراً بِاليمن، ولَعَنَ اللهُ الزهْرةَ، وقال: إِنَها فتنت ملكين» .","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-10","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"قلت: قصة هاروت وماروت ذكرها المنذري في شرب الخمر، وقال في حديثها: رواه أحمد وابن حبان في صحيحه من طريق زهير بن محمد، وقد قيل: إن الصحيح وقفه على كعب. هـ. وقال ابن حجر: قصة هاروت وماروت جاءت بسند حسن، خلافاً لمن زعم بطلانها كعياض ومن تبعه.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-11","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"وتمام قصتهما: أنهما لما قارفا الذنب وجاء المساء همّا بالصعود، فلم تطاوعهما أجنحتهما، فعلما ما حلّ بهما، فقصدا إدريس عليه السلام، فأخبراه، وسألاه الشفاعة إلى الله تعالى فشفع فيهما، فخيّرهما الله تعالى بين عذاب الدنيا وعذاب الآخرة، فاختارا عذاب الدنيا لانقطاعه، فهما يعذبان في بئر ببابل، منكسان معلقان بالسلاسل من أرجلهما، مزرقة أعينهما، ليس بينهما وبين الماء إلا قدر أربعة أصابع، وهما يعذبان بالعطش . هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-12","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"فإن قلت: الملائكة معصومون فكيف يصح هذا من هاروت وماروت؟ قلنا: لما ركب الله فيهما الشهوة انسلخا من حكم المَلَكيَّة إلى حكم البشرية ابتلاء من الله تعالى لهما، فلم يبق لهما حكم الملائكة من العصمة.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-13","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"وَما يُعَلِّمانِ مِنْ أَحَدٍ السحر حتى ينصحاه ويقولا: إِنَّما نَحْنُ فِتْنَةٌ لكم، واختبار من الله تعالى لعباده، ليظهر من يصبر عنه ومن لا يصبر، وكان تعلمه في ذلك الوقت كفراً. فيقولان له فَلا تَكْفُرْ بتعلُّمه، فكانوا يتعلمون مِنْهُما مَا يُفَرِّقُونَ بِهِ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَزَوْجِهِ وَما هُمْ بِضارِّينَ بِهِ مِنْ أَحَدٍ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وقدرته، فلا تأثير لشئ إلا بإذن الله، ويتعلمون منهما مَا يَضُرُّهُمْ يوم القيامة وَلا يَنْفَعُهُمْ، ولقد علم بنو إسرائيل أن من اشتراه واستبدله بكتاب الله والعمل بما فيه مَا لَهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنْ نصيب، وَلَبِئْسَ ما باعوا به حظ أنفسهم من النعيم لَوْ كانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ، لكن لما لم يعملوا بعلمهم كانوا كمن لا علم عنده.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-14","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا بالله ورسوله وَاتَّقَوْا الكفر والسحر، لأثيبوا ثواباً كبيراً، وكان ذلك خيراً لهم مما استوجبوه من العقاب لَوْ كانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-15","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"الإشارة: كل من أكَبُّ على دنياه وتتبع حظوظه وهواه، وترك العمل بما جاء من عند الله، يصدق عليه أنه نبذ كتاب الله، واشتغل بما سواه مِن حب الدنيا والرئاسة والجاه، فالدنيا سحارة غرارة، تسحر القلوب وتغيبها عن حضرة علاّم الغيوب وفي الحديث: «اتَقُوا الدُّنْيَا فإنْهَا أسْحَرُ مِنْ هَارُوتَ وَمَارُوتَ» ، ولا شك أنها تفرق بين الأحباب وبين العشائر والأصحاب. ولقد علم من أخذ الدنيا ونعيمها، وأكب عليها ما له في الآخرة من نصيب، فبقدر ما يأخذ من نعيم الدنيا وشهواتها ينقص له من نعيم الآخرة. وَلَبِئْسَ مَا شَرَوْاْ بِهِ أنفسهم- حيث آثروا الحياةَ الدنيا على الآخرة- لو كانوا يعلمون. ولو أنهم آمنوا بالله، واتقوا كل ما يشغل عن الله لكانوا من أولياء الله، وتلك المثوبة- التي صاروا إليها- خير لو كانوا يعلمون.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-16","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"قال عبد الواحد بن زيد: سمعت أن جارية مجنونة في خراب الأُبُلَّةِ تنطق بالحِكَم، فطلبتها حتى وجدتها، وهي محلوقة الرأس، وعليها جبة صوف، فلما رأتنى قالت: مَرحباً بك يا عبد الواحد، ثم قالت: يا عبد الواحد ما جاء بك؟","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-17","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"فقلت: تعظينني، فقالت: واعجبا لواعظ، يوعظ، يا عبد الواحد.. اعلم أن العبد إذا كان في كفاية، ومال إلى شيء من الدنيا، سلبه الله حلاوة الزهد، وظل حيراناً وَلِهاً، فإن كان له عند الله نصيب عاتبه وَحْياً في سره، فيقول له:","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-18","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"عبدي أردت رفع قدرك عند ملائكتي، وأجعلك دليلاً لأوليائي، ومرشداً لأهل طاعتي، فملت إلى عرض الدنيا وتركتني، فأورثك ذلك الوحشة بعد الأنس، والذل بعد العز، والفقر بعد الغنى، ارجع إلى ما كنت عليه أُرجع إليك ما كنت تعرفه من نفسك. ثم انصرفت عني وتركتني وبقيت حسرتها في قلبي. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-102-103-19","r":"q2-102-103","title":"2:102–103 · Sorcery, trial and the enchantment of the world","text":"ولما كان المسلمون يقولون للرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: راعنا يا رسول الله وأرْعِنا سَمْعَكَ، يَعْنُون من المراعاة والانتظار، وهي عند اليهود سب من الرعونة، ففرحت اليهود، وقالوا: كنا نسب محمداً سرّاً، فأعلنوا له بالشتم، فكانوا يقولون: يا محمد راعنا ويضحكون، نهى الله تعالى المسلمين عن هذه اللفظة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-102-103-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-102-103-s1","r":"q2-102-103","title":"Trial and the promise of lasting reward","text":"I say: “over Solomon’s kingdom” involves an omitted expression: “during the time of Solomon’s reign”; or ʿalā means fī , “in.” “What was sent down” is conjoined to “sorcery” as an explanatory conjunction ( عطف تفسير ). Fitna ( فتنة ) originally means testing. You say that you test gold or silver when you put it into the fire to distinguish its good quality from its bad. “A reward” answers law , “had”: originally, “they would have been rewarded.” The expression shifts to a nominal sentence to indicate permanence.","anchor":"en-q2-102-103-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-102-103-s2","r":"q2-102-103","title":"Solomon’s vindication and the two angels","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says concerning the Jews: when a Book came to them from God, they cast it aside and followed the sorcery that devils recited to people during Solomon’s reign. The devils used to eavesdrop, combine what they heard with lies, and pass it to the soothsayers, who recorded it and taught it to people. This spread in Solomon’s time until it was said that the jinn knew the unseen, and that Solomon’s kingship depended upon this, through which he subjected jinn, human beings and wind. Solomon collected the written material and buried it; the devils dug it up after his death. God refutes their claim: Solomon did not disbelieve by practising sorcery—for sorcery magnifies another besides God through drawing near to Satan, and the prophet is protected from sin ( معصوم ). Rather, the devils disbelieved through practising it, teaching people sorcery to seduce and mislead them, and teaching what was sent down to the two angels in Babylon, in the cultivated region of Kūfa: Hārūt and Mārūt. [B066] They were two of the most devoted angels. When the angels saw the foul deeds of Adam’s children ascending to heaven in the time of Idrīs, peace be upon him, they reproached them: “Our Lord, do these whom You made vicegerents upon earth disobey You?” God said: “Were I to send you to earth and constitute you as I constituted them, you would commit what they commit.” They replied: “Glory to You! It would not be fitting for us to disobey You.” God told them to choose two of their best whom He would send down. They chose Hārūt and Mārūt, among the most devoted angels. God implanted desire in them, commanded them to judge truly among people on earth, and forbade association, unjust killing, fornication and drinking wine. They judged between people by day; in the evening they pronounced God’s greatest Name and ascended to heaven. One day a woman called al-Zuhara, among the most beautiful women of Persia, brought a dispute before them. She captured their hearts, and they solicited her, but she refused. She returned the second day; they repeated their approach, and she refused unless they would worship what she worshipped, pray to the idol, kill a person and drink wine. They refused, saying that God had forbidden these things. She left and returned on the third day. When they solicited her, she repeated the conditions. They said: praying to another besides God is a great sin, and the lightest of the three is drinking wine. They drank, became intoxicated and lay with the woman. Afterwards someone saw them; fearing exposure, they killed him. A report from our master ʿAlī, God ennoble his face, says: “She told them, ‘You will not have me until you tell me how you ascend to heaven.’ They said, ‘Through God’s greatest Name,’ and taught it to her. She uttered it, ascended to heaven, and God transformed her into a star.” Thus, when he, peace and blessings be upon him, saw Suhayl, he used to say: “God curse Suhayl: he was a tax-collector in Yemen. God curse al-Zuhara: she tempted two angels.” I say: al-Mundhirī mentions the story of Hārūt and Mārūt in his discussion of drinking wine. Concerning its hadith he says: Aḥmad and Ibn Ḥibbān in his Ṣaḥīḥ transmit it through Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad; it has been said that the correct version stops at Kaʿb. Thus ends his statement. Ibn Ḥajar says: the story of Hārūt and Mārūt comes through a fair chain ( سند حسن ), contrary to those who consider it invalid, such as ʿIyāḍ and his followers. The story continues: after committing the sin, they wished to ascend at evening, but their wings did not obey them. They recognized what had befallen them, went to Idrīs, told him, and asked him to intercede with God. He did so, and God offered them the choice of punishment in this world or the next. They chose this world’s punishment because it comes to an end. They are punished in a well in Babylon, suspended upside down by chains from their feet, their eyes blue, only four fingers’ breadth from the water, yet tormented by thirst. Thus ends the account. Should you ask, “Angels are protected from sin: how can this be true of Hārūt and Mārūt?” we reply: when God implanted desire in them, they passed from the condition of angels to that of humanity, as a trial from Him. They no longer possessed the angels’ condition of protection.","anchor":"en-q2-102-103-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-102-103-s3","r":"q2-102-103","title":"Knowledge that harms and effects permitted by God","text":"They teach sorcery to no one without counselling him: “We are only a trial for you, a test from God for His servants, so that those who refrain and those who do not may become manifest.” Learning it was unbelief at that time; therefore they say, “Do not disbelieve through learning it.” People learned from them what separates a man and his wife. Yet they could harm no one except by God’s permission and power: nothing produces an effect except by His permission. They learned what would harm them on the Day of Resurrection and not benefit them. The Children of Israel knew that whoever purchased it, exchanging God’s Book and obedience to it for sorcery, would have no portion in the Hereafter. Wretched was that for which they sold their souls’ share of bliss, had they known. But because they did not act on their knowledge, they were like people who had none. Had they believed in God and His Messenger and guarded against unbelief and sorcery, they would have received a great reward, better than the punishment they incurred, had they known.","anchor":"en-q2-102-103-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-102-103-s4","r":"q2-102-103","title":"The world’s enchantment","text":"Whoever bends over his worldly life, follows his desires and private portions, and abandons what comes from God, may truly be said to have cast aside God’s Book and occupied himself with something else: love of the world, leadership and prestige. The world is an enchanting deceiver, bewitching hearts and drawing them away from the presence of the Knower of unseen things. In the hadith: “Beware the world: it is more bewitching than Hārūt and Mārūt.” [B067] It certainly divides lovers, kindred and companions. Whoever takes the world and its delights and bends over it knows that he has no share in the Hereafter: his heavenly bliss diminishes in proportion to the worldly delights and desires he takes. Wretched is that for which they sold their souls, preferring worldly life to the next, had they known. Had they believed in God and guarded against everything that distracts from Him, they would have become His friends. That reward to which they would have come is better, had they known. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Zayd said: I heard of a girl called mad, living in the ruins of al-Ubulla, who uttered wisdom. I sought her and found her, head shaven, wearing a woollen gown. Seeing me, she said, “Welcome, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. What brings you?” I said, “That you may admonish me.” She answered: “How strange—a preacher being preached to! Know, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, that when a servant has enough and inclines to something worldly, God takes away the sweetness of renunciation and he remains bewildered and distraught. If he has a portion with God, He reproaches him through an inspiration in his secret: ‘My servant, I wished to raise your rank among My angels and make you a guide to My friends and a director of those who obey Me. But you inclined to worldly goods and left Me. This bequeathed estrangement after intimacy, humiliation after honour, and poverty after wealth. Return to what you were, and I shall restore what you knew in yourself.’” She then turned away and left me, and sorrow at her departure remained in my heart.","anchor":"en-q2-102-103-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-102-103-s5","r":"q2-102-103","title":"","text":"The Muslims used to say to the Messenger, “Rāʿinā, Messenger of God; lend us your ear,” intending consideration and waiting. Among the Jews it served as an insult derived from foolishness ( الرعونة ). They rejoiced and said, “We used to insult Muḥammad secretly,” then openly uttered the insult, saying “Muḥammad, rāʿinā,” and laughing. God forbade the Muslims this expression, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-102-103-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-104","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"2:104 · Courtesy in address 2:104","anchor":"unit-q2-104"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-1","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَقُولُوا راعِنا وَقُولُوا انْظُرْنا وَاسْمَعُوا وَلِلْكافِرِينَ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ (104)","anchor":"ar-q2-104-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-2","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"قلت: يقال راعى الشيء يراعيه مراعاة: انتظره أو التفت إليه. ويقال: رَعَى إلى الشيء، وراعاه وأرعاه: إذا أصغى إليه واستمعه.","anchor":"ar-q2-104-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-3","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَقُولُوا للرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: راعِنا أي: انتظرنا أو أمهل علينا لأن في ذلك ذريعة لسب اليهود، أو قلة أدب، وقولوا: انْظُرْنا أي: انتظرنا وَلِلْكافِرِينَ المؤذين لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ أي: موجع.","anchor":"ar-q2-104-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-4","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"الإشارة: حسنُ الخطاب من تمام الآداب، وتمام الآداب هو السبب الموصل إلى عين الصواب، فمن لا أدب له لا تربية له، ومن لا تربية له لا سَيْر له، ومن لا سير له لا وصول له، فمن لا يتربى على أيدي الرجال لا يُربى الرجال، وقد قالوا: من أساء الأدب مع الأحباب طُرد إلى الباب، ومن أساء الأدب في الباب طرد إلى سياسة الدواب. وقالوا أيضاً: اجعل عَمَلك مِلْحاً، وأدبك دقيقاً. وقال آخر: إن الإنسان ليبلغ بالخلق وحسن الأدب إلى عظيم الدرجات وهو قليل العمل، ومن حرم الأدب حُرم الخيرَ كله، ومن أُعطي الأدب فقد مُكن من مفاتيح القلوب.","anchor":"ar-q2-104-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-5","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"قال أبو عثمان رضي الله عنه: الأدب عند الأكابر وفي مجالس السادات من الأولياء يبلغ بصاحبه إلى الدرجات العلا والخير في الدنيا والعقبى. وقال أبو حفص الحداد رضي الله عنه: التصوف كله آداب، لكل وقت أدب، ولكل حال أدب، ولكل مقام أدب، فمن لازم الأدب بلغ مبلغ الرجال، ومن حرم الأدب فهو بعيد من حيث يظن القرب، مردود من حيث يرجو الوصول. وقال ذو النون المصري رضي الله عنه: (إذا خرج المريد عن استعمال الأدب فإنه يرجع من حيث جاء) .","anchor":"ar-q2-104-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-6","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"وقيل: من لم يتأدب لوقت فوقته مقت. وقيل: من حَبَسه النسب أطلقه الادب، ومن قل أدبه كثر شغبه. وقيل:","anchor":"ar-q2-104-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-7","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"الأدب سند الفقراء، وزينة الأغنياء. هـ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-104-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-104-8","r":"q2-104","title":"2:104 · Courtesy in address","text":"ومن مساوئ اليهود أيضا الحسد والغل، وإليه أشار الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-104-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-104-s1","r":"q2-104","title":"Choosing an unambiguous form of address","text":"I say: to rāʿā something is to wait for it or attend to it. Raʿā ilā , rāʿā and arʿā also mean to incline one’s ear and listen. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: believers, do not tell the Messenger, “Rāʿinā”—wait for us or give us time—for it supplies a means for the Jews’ insult, or constitutes a lack of courtesy. Say instead, “Unẓurnā”: wait for us. The unbelievers who hurt God’s Messenger have a painful, distressing punishment.","anchor":"en-q2-104-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-104-s2","r":"q2-104","title":"Courtesy as the condition of formation","text":"Good address belongs to complete courtesy ( الأدب ), and complete courtesy is the means of reaching what is truly right. Without courtesy there is no formation; without formation, no journey; without a journey, no arrival. Whoever has not been formed at the hands of realized people cannot form others. It is said: whoever behaves badly with the beloved is expelled to the door; whoever behaves badly at the door is expelled to tending the beasts. It is also said: make your works salt and your courtesy flour. [B068] Another said: through good character and courtesy a person reaches great degrees despite few works. Whoever is deprived of courtesy is deprived of all good; whoever is given it is entrusted with the keys of hearts. Abū ʿUthmān, God be pleased with him, says: courtesy with the great and in the gatherings of the masters among God’s friends brings its possessor to lofty degrees and goodness in this world and the next. Abū Ḥafṣ al-Ḥaddād says: Sufism is entirely courtesy. Every time, state and station has its courtesy. Whoever adheres to courtesy attains the rank of realized people; whoever lacks it is distant precisely where he supposes himself near, rejected precisely where he hopes to arrive. Dhū al-Nūn al-Miṣrī says: when a disciple abandons the practice of courtesy, he returns from where he came. It is said: whoever fails to observe the courtesy of his time finds his time hateful. Whom lineage confines, courtesy releases. Whoever has little courtesy causes much disturbance. Courtesy is the support of the poor and the adornment of the rich. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-104-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-104-s3","r":"q2-104","title":"","text":"Envy and rancour are also among the Jews’ faults. The Real points to them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-104-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-105","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy 2:105","anchor":"unit-q2-105"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-1","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"ما يَوَدُّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ وَلا الْمُشْرِكِينَ أَنْ يُنَزَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَاللَّهُ يَخْتَصُّ بِرَحْمَتِهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ (105)","anchor":"ar-q2-105-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-2","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"قلت: الود: محبة الشيء مع تمنيه، و «مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ» بيانية كقوله: «لَمْ يَكُنِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ» ، و «أَن يُنَزَّلَ» معمول يود، و «مِّنْ خَيْرٍ» صلة، و «مِّن رَّبكُمْ» ابتدائية.","anchor":"ar-q2-105-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-3","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ما يتمنى الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ إنزال خير عليكم مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ ولا المشركون حسداً منهم، بل يتمنون أن تبقوا على ضلالتكم وذُلِّكُمْ، وَاللَّهُ يَخْتَصُّ بِرَحْمَتِهِ كالنبوة والولاية مَنْ يَشاءُ من عباده. فلا يجب عليه شيء ولا يمتنع عليه ممكن، وَاللَّهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ، فَيَمُنُّ بالنبوة أو الولاية على مَن يشاء فضلاً وإحساناً.","anchor":"ar-q2-105-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-4","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"الإشارة: في الآية تنبيهان: أحدهما: أن من كان يحسد أهل الخصوصية وينكر عليهم، فيه نزعة يهودية، وخصلة من خصال المشركين، والثاني: أن حسد أهل الخصوصية والإنكار عليهم أمر شائع وسنة ماضية، فليوطن المريد نفسه على ذلك، وليعلم انه ما يقال له إلا ما قيل لمن قبله، وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لِسُنَّةِ اللَّهِ تَبْدِيلًا، وما من نعمة إلا وعليها حسود.","anchor":"ar-q2-105-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-5","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"وقال حاتم الطائي:","anchor":"ar-q2-105-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-6","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"ومِنْ حَسَدٍ يَجُورُ عَلَيَّ قَومي ... وأيُّ الدهر ذُو لَمْ يَحْسُدُوني","anchor":"ar-q2-105-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-7","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-105-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-105-8","r":"q2-105","title":"2:105 · Divine mercy is not subject to envy","text":"ومن مساوئهم أيضا إنكار النسخ للأحكام، فردَّ الله عليهم بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-105-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-105-s1","r":"q2-105","title":"Three uses of min","text":"I say: wudd ( ودّ ) is love of a thing together with wishing for it. “Among the People of the Book” is explanatory, like the corresponding expression in 98:1. “That there should be sent down” is governed by “wish.” The min in “any good” is supplementary; in “from your Lord” it indicates origin.","anchor":"en-q2-105-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-105-s2","r":"q2-105","title":"Bounty freely bestowed","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the unbelieving People of the Book and the polytheists do not wish good to descend upon you from your Lord, through envy. Rather, they wish you to remain in error and humiliation. God singles out whom He wills of His servants for His mercy, such as prophethood and friendship with Him. Nothing is obligatory upon Him, and no possible thing is impossible for Him. He possesses tremendous bounty, granting prophethood or friendship to whom He wills through favour and beneficence.","anchor":"en-q2-105-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-105-s3","r":"q2-105","title":"Prepare for the envy that accompanies a gift","text":"The verse contains two admonitions. First, whoever envies and denies the people of special election has a tendency resembling that of the Jews and a trait of the polytheists. Second, envy and denial of special election are widespread and follow an established pattern. Let the disciple prepare himself for this and know that nothing is said to him but what was said to his predecessors: “You will find no alteration in God’s customary way” [33:62]. No blessing lacks someone who envies it. Ḥātim al-Ṭāʾī said: Through envy my people wrong me; what age has passed in which they did not envy me? Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-105-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-105-s4","r":"q2-105","title":"","text":"Another of their faults was denying the abrogation of rulings. God refuted them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-105-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-106-107","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends 2:106–107","anchor":"unit-q2-106-107"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-1","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"مَا نَنْسَخْ مِنْ آيَةٍ أَوْ نُنْسِها نَأْتِ بِخَيْرٍ مِنْها أَوْ مِثْلِها أَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (106) أَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَما لَكُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ مِنْ وَلِيٍّ وَلا نَصِيرٍ (107)","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-2","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"قلت: النسخ في اللغة يُطلق على معنيين أحدهما: التغيير والتحويل، يقال: مسخه الله قرداً ونسخه. قال الفراء: ومنه نسخ الكتاب، والثاني: بمعنى رفع الشيء وإبطاله. يقال: نَسَخَتِ الشمسُ الظلَّ، أي: ذهبت به وأبطلته، وهو المراد هنا.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-3","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"والإنساء هو الترك والإذهاب، والنساء هو التأخر. و «ما» شرطية منصوبة بشرطها مفعولاً به. و «نَأْتِ» جوابها.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-4","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: في الرد على اليهود حيث قالوا: انظروا إلى محمد يأمر أصحابه بأمر ثم ينهاهم عنه، فأجاب الله عنهم بقوله: مَا نَنْسَخْ مِنْ آيَةٍ أي: نزيل لفظها أو حكمها أو هما معاً، نَأْتِ بِخَيْرٍ مِنْها في","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-5","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"الخفة أو في الثواب، أَوْ نُنْسِها من قلب النبي- عليه الصلاة والسلام- بإذن الله، أو نتركها غير منسوخة، أو نؤخر إنزالها أو نسخها. باعتبار القراءات، نَأْتِ بِخَيْرٍ مِنْها أَوْ مِثْلِها أَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ يا محمد أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ لا يعجزه نسخ ولا غيره أَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ يتصرف فيهما كيف يشاء، لا راد لما قضى ولا مُعقِّب لما حكم به وأمضى، ينسخ من شرائع أحكامه ما شاء، ويثبت فيها ما شاء، بحسب مصالح العباد، وما تقتضيه الرأفة والوداد.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-6","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"وهو جائز عقلاً وشرعاً، فكما نسخت شريعتهم ما قبلها نسخها ما بعدها، فمن تحكم على الله، أو رد على أصفياء الله ممن اصطفاهم لرسالته، فليس له مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ مِنْ وَلِيٍّ يمنع من عذاب الله، وَلا نَصِيرٍ ينصره من غضب الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-7","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"والنسخ إنما يكون في الأوامر والنواهي دون الأخبار، لأنه يكون كذباً، ومعنى النسخ: انتهاء العمل بذلك الحكم، ونقل العباد من حكم إلى حكم لمصلحة، فلا يلزم عليه البَدَاءُ كما قالت اليهود، والنسخ عندنا على ثلاثة أقسام: نسخ اللفظ والمعنى: كما كان يُقْرَأُ: «لا ترغبوا عن آبائكم فإنه كفر» ، ثم نُسخ، ونسخ اللفظ دون المعنى: «كالشيخ والشيخة إذا زنيا فارجموهما البتة» ، ثم نسخ لفظه، وبقي حكمه وهو الرجم، ونسخ المعنى دون اللفظ: كآية السيف بعد الأمر بالمهادنة مع الكفار. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-8","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"الإشارة: قال الشيخ أبو العباس المرسى رضي الله عنه في تفسيرها: ما نذهب من بدل إلا ونأت بخير منه أو مثله. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-9","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"ومعناه: ما نذهب بولي إلا ونأت بخير منه أو مثله إلى يوم القيامة، وبهذا يُرَدّ على مَن زعم أن شيخ التربية انقطع فإن قدرة الله عامة، وملك الله قائم، والأرض لا تخلو ممن يقوم بالحجة حتى يأتي أمر الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-10","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"قال في لطائف المنن: وقد سئل بعضُ العارفين عن أولياء المدد: أينقصون في زمن؟ فقال: لو نقص منهم واحد ما أرسلت السماء قطرها، ولا أبرزت الأرض نباتها، وفساد الوقت لا يكون بذهاب أعدادهم، ولا بنقص إمدادهم، ولكن إذا فسد الوقت كان مراد الله وقوع اختفائهم مع وجود بقائهم، ثم قال: وقد قال علي- كرم الله وجهه- في مخاطبته لكميل:","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-11","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"اللهم لا تخلو الأرض من قائم لك بحجتك، أولئك الأقلون عدداً، الأعظمون عند الله قدراً، قلوبهم معلقة بالمحل الأعلى.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-12","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"أولئك خلفاء الله في بلاده وعباده، وا شوقاه إلى رؤيتهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-13","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"وروى الترمذي الحكيم عن ابن عمر رضي الله عنه يرفعه إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم قال: «أمتي كالمَطَرِ لا يُدْرَى أَولهُ خيرٌ أم آخره» . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-106-107-14","r":"q2-106-107","title":"2:106–107 · Abrogation and the continuing presence of God’s friends","text":"ولما سأل رافع بن حريملة اليهودي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم أن يريه آية، كتفجير ماء أو غيره، نزل قوله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q2-106-107-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-106-107-s1","r":"q2-106-107","title":"Removal, forgetting and postponement","text":"I say: naskh ( نسخ ) has two lexical meanings. One is alteration or transfer: one says, “God transformed him into an ape,” using either masakha or nasakha . Al-Farrāʾ says that copying a book belongs to this meaning. The second is removing and cancelling something: “The sun removed the shadow”—made it disappear. This is the meaning here. Insāʾ ( إنساء ) is leaving or making something depart; nasāʾ ( نساء ) is postponement. Mā is conditional, accusative as the object of its conditional verb, and “We bring” is its response.","anchor":"en-q2-106-107-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-106-107-s2","r":"q2-106-107","title":"The end of a ruling’s period of application","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, replies to the Jews’ remark, “Look at Muḥammad: he commands his companions something and then forbids it.” God answers: whatever verse We abrogate—removing its wording, its ruling or both—We bring one better in lightness or reward. “Or cause it to be forgotten” means removed from the Prophet’s heart by God’s permission; alternatively, We leave it unabrogated, or postpone its revelation or abrogation, according to the different readings. We bring something better or similar. Do you not know, Muḥammad, that God has power over everything? Neither abrogation nor anything else incapacitates Him. His is the kingdom of heaven and earth; He disposes of both as He wills. None rejects His decree or reverses what He decides and establishes. He abrogates or confirms the rulings of His revealed ordinances as He wills, according to His servants’ interests and what tenderness and love require. Abrogation is possible both rationally and according to revelation. As their Law abrogated what preceded it, what followed abrogated it. Whoever dictates to God or objects to His chosen messengers has no protector against His punishment and no helper against His anger. Abrogation concerns commands and prohibitions, not reports, since the latter would imply falsehood. It means the end of acting upon a ruling and the transfer of servants from one ruling to another for a benefit. It does not entail the emergence of previously unknown knowledge ( البداء ), as the Jews claim. For us abrogation is of three kinds: removal of both wording and meaning, as in the former recitation, “Do not turn away from your fathers, for that is unbelief”; removal of wording but not meaning, as in “The elderly man and elderly woman, when they commit adultery, stone them outright,” whose wording was abrogated but whose ruling—stoning—remained; and removal of meaning but not wording, as in the sword verse following the command to maintain a truce with unbelievers. [B069] And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-106-107-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-106-107-s3","r":"q2-106-107","title":"Successors among the friends of God","text":"Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mursī interprets it: “We remove no substitute saint ( بدل ) without bringing one better or like him.” That is, no friend of God is taken away without another better or similar being brought, until the Day of Resurrection. This refutes anyone who claims that masters of formation have ceased. God’s power is universal, His kingdom endures, and the earth does not lack someone who upholds the proof until God’s command arrives. In Laṭāʾif al-minan : a gnostic was asked whether the saints through whom assistance comes ever diminish. He replied: were one of them to be missing, heaven would not send its rain and earth would not bring forth its plants. The corruption of an age does not come from a reduction in their number or assistance. Rather, when an age is corrupt, God wills that they be hidden although they remain. He then cites ʿAlī’s words to Kumayl: “O God, the earth is not without someone who stands for You with Your proof. They are fewest in number, greatest in worth with God; their hearts are attached to the highest abode. They are God’s vicegerents in His lands and among His servants. How I long to see them!” Al-Tirmidhī al-Ḥakīm transmits from Ibn ʿUmar, as a saying of the Messenger: “My community is like rain: one does not know whether its beginning or its end is better.” [B070] Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-106-107-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-106-107-s4","r":"q2-106-107","title":"","text":"When Rāfiʿ ibn Ḥuraymila, the Jew, asked God’s Messenger to show him a sign, such as causing water to burst forth, these words were revealed:","anchor":"en-q2-106-107-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-108","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood 2:108","anchor":"unit-q2-108"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-1","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"أَمْ تُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَسْئَلُوا رَسُولَكُمْ كَما سُئِلَ مُوسى مِنْ قَبْلُ وَمَنْ يَتَبَدَّلِ الْكُفْرَ بِالْإِيمانِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَواءَ السَّبِيلِ (108)","anchor":"ar-q2-108-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-2","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"قلت: (أم) للإضراب بمعنى بل وهو على قسمين: إما إضراب عن المعنى السابق، أو لفظه فقط كما هنا، انظر تفسير ابن عطية، وإضافة الرسول إليهم باعتبار ما في نفس الأمر. وهو نص في إرساله إليهم كما أرسل إلى غيرهم. والضلال: التلف. وسَواءَ السَّبِيلِ: وسط الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-108-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-3","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أتريدون يا معشر اليهود أن تقترحوا على نبيكم الذي أرسلت إليكم، وإلى كافة الخلق من غيركم الآيات، وتسألوه أن يريكم المعجزات، كما سألتم موسى من قبل فقلتم: أَرِنَا اللَّهَ جَهْرَةً تشغيباً وتعنتاً، وأبيتم عن الإيمان، واستبدلتموه بالكفر والعصيان، وَمَنْ يَتَبَدَّلِ الْكُفْرَ بِالْإِيمانِ فقد تلف عن طريق الحق والسداد، ومأواه جهنم وبئس المهاد.","anchor":"ar-q2-108-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-4","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"الإشارة: لا يُشترط في الولي ظهور الكرامة، وإنما يشترط فيه كمال الاستقامة، ولا يشترط فيه أيضا هداية الخلق على يديه إذ لم يكن ذلك للنبي فكيف يكون للولي؟ قال تعالى: أَفَأَنْتَ تُكْرِهُ النَّاسَ حَتَّى يَكُونُوا مُؤْمِنِينَ وقد سَرَى في طبع العوام ما سَرَى في طبع الكفار، قالوا: لَنْ نُؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّى تَفْجُرَ لَنا مِنَ الْأَرْضِ يَنْبُوعاً الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-108-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-5","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"فكثير من العوام لا يقرون الولي حتى يروا له آية أو كرامة، مع أن الولي كلما رسختْ قدمه في المعرفة قلَّ ظهور الكرامة على يديه لأن الكرامة إنما هي معونة وتأييد وزيادة إيقان. والجبل الراسي لا يحتاج إلى عماد.","anchor":"ar-q2-108-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-6","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"والحق هو ما قاله الشيخ أبو الحسن الشاذلي رضي الله عنه: (وإنهما كرامتان جامعتان محيطتان: كرامة الإيمان بمزيد الإيقان على نعت الشهود والعيان، وكرامة العمل على السنة والمتابعة، ومجانبة الدعاوى والمخادعة، فمن أُعْطِيَهُمَا ثم اشتاق إلى غيرهما فهو مفتر كذاب، أو ذو خطأ في العلم والفهم، كمن أكرم بشهود الملك على نعت الرضى والكرامة، ثم جعل يشتاق إلى سياسة الدواب وخِلَعِ الرضا) أو كما قال رضي الله عنه.","anchor":"ar-q2-108-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-7","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"وقال شيخنا رضي الله عنه: (الكرامة الحقيقية هي الأخلاق النبوية والعلوم اللدنية) . فمن أنكر أولياء أهل زمانه وطلب منهم الدليل غير ما تقدم فقد ضل سواء السبيل، وبقي مربوطاً في سجن البرهان والدليل. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-108-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-108-8","r":"q2-108","title":"2:108 · A miracle is not the condition of sainthood","text":"ولما ظهر حسد اليهود واجتهادهم فى الرد على الإسلام، أمر الحق تعالى المسلمين بالعفو والصفح حتى يأذن فى قتالهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-108-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-108-s1","r":"q2-108","title":"A transition in the address","text":"I say: am ( أم ) indicates transition ( الإضراب ), in the sense of bal , “rather.” This is of two kinds: departure from the preceding meaning, or only from its wording, as here; consult Ibn ʿAṭiyya’s commentary. Calling him “your messenger” corresponds to the reality of the matter and explicitly establishes that he was sent to them as to others. Going astray is losing the way; sawāʾ al-sabīl is the middle of the road.","anchor":"en-q2-108-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-108-s2","r":"q2-108","title":"Demanding signs through obstinacy","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Jewish people, do you wish to prescribe signs to your Prophet, whom I sent to you and to all other creatures, asking him to show miracles, as you formerly asked Moses, “Show us God openly” [4:153], through contentiousness and obstinacy? You refused faith and exchanged it for unbelief and disobedience. Whoever makes that exchange is lost from the way of truth and rectitude. His abode is Hell: an evil resting place.","anchor":"en-q2-108-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-108-s3","r":"q2-108","title":"Two comprehensive graces","text":"The appearance of an extraordinary grace ( كرامة ) is not a condition of being God’s friend; complete uprightness ( الاستقامة ) is. Nor is it a condition that people be guided through him: that was not guaranteed even to the prophet, so how could it be to the friend? God says, “Will you compel people until they become believers?” [10:99]. A tendency has entered the common people like that which entered the unbelievers who said, “We will not believe you until you make a spring burst from the earth for us” [17:90]. Many will not acknowledge a friend of God until they see a sign or wonder. Yet the more firmly his foot is rooted in gnosis, the fewer the wonders appearing at his hands. A wonder is assistance, confirmation and an increase in certainty; a firmly established mountain needs no support. The truth is what Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan al-Shādhilī said: “There are two comprehensive, all-encompassing graces: the grace of faith with increasing certainty in witnessing and direct vision, and the grace of action according to the Sunna and following the Prophet, avoiding pretension and deception. Whoever receives these and longs for something else is a fabricating liar, or mistaken in knowledge and understanding—like someone honoured by seeing the king in approval and dignity, who then longs to tend the beasts and receive robes of favour.” Or words to that effect. Our shaykh said: “The true extraordinary grace is Prophetic character and divinely bestowed knowledge.” Whoever denies the friends of God of his own time and demands proof from them other than what has been described has strayed from the level way and remains bound in the prison of demonstration and proof. Through God is success; He guides to the level way.","anchor":"en-q2-108-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-108-s4","r":"q2-108","title":"","text":"When the Jews’ envy and efforts to oppose Islam became manifest, the Real commanded the Muslims to pardon and overlook until He permitted fighting them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-108-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-109-110","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents 2:109–110","anchor":"unit-q2-109-110"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-1","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"وَدَّ كَثِيرٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ لَوْ يَرُدُّونَكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ إِيمانِكُمْ كُفَّاراً حَسَداً مِنْ عِنْدِ أَنْفُسِهِمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْحَقُّ فَاعْفُوا وَاصْفَحُوا حَتَّى يَأْتِيَ اللَّهُ بِأَمْرِهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (109) وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكاةَ وَما تُقَدِّمُوا لِأَنْفُسِكُمْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ تَجِدُوهُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ (110)","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-2","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"قلت: لَوْ مصدريةٌ مفعول «وَدَّ» ، وكُفَّاراً: مفعول ثان، وحَسَداً: مفعول له، علة لود، أو حال من الواو، ومِنْ عِنْدِ متعلق بود، أي: يتمنوا ذلك من عند أنفسهم وتَشهِّيهم، أو بقوله: «حسداً» ، فالوقف على قوله كُفَّاراً، أي: حسداً حاصلاً من تلقاء أنفسهم، لم يستندوا فيه إلى شبهة ولا دليل، والعفو: ترك العقوبة بالذنب. والصفح: الإعراض عن المذنب، كأنه يولي عنه صفحة عنقه، فهو أبلغ من العفو.","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-3","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في التحذير من اليهود وغيرهم من الكفار: تمنّى الذين كفروا من أهل الكتاب وغيرهم لو يصرفونكم عن دينكم ويَرُدُّونَكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ إِيمانِكُمْ بنبيكم كُفَّاراً ضالين، كما كنتم قبل الدخول فيه، وذلك حَسَداً مِنْ تلقاء أَنْفُسِهِمْ غيرة أن تكون النبوة في غيرهم، وذلك مِنْ بَعْدِ ما تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْحَقُّ وعرفوه كما يعرفون أبناءهم، فَاعْفُوا عن عتابهم، وأعرضوا عن تشغيبهم حَتَّى يَأْتِيَ اللَّهُ بِأَمْرِهِ فيهم بالقتل والجلاء. إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ، واشتغلوا بما كلفكم به من أداء حقوق العبودية، والقيام بوظائف الربوبية، كإتقان الصلاة وأداء الزكاة، واعلموا أن الله لا يضيع من أعمالكم شيئاً، فما تقدموا لأنفسكم ليوم فقركم تجدوه عند الله خيرا وأعظم أجراً، إن الله لا يخفى عليه شيء من أعمالكم وأحوالكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-4","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"نزلت الآية في عمار بن ياسر وحذيفة بن اليمان، أتيا بيت المِدْرَاس ، فألانوا لهم الكلام، فطمعوا في صرفهما عن دينهما، ففضحهم الله ورد كيدهم في نحرهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-5","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"الإشارة: من جملة ما دَبَّ إلى بعض الطوائف المتجمدين على تقليد أشياخهم: التعصب والحمية على طريق أشياخهم، ولو ظهر الحق عند غيرهم، وخصوصاً أولاد الصالحين منهم، فإذا رأوا أحداً ظهرت عليه أنوار الولاية،","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-6","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"وأسرار الخصوصية، تمنَّوْا أن يردوهم عن طريق الحق، ويصرفوهم إلى مخالطة الخلق، حسداً من عند أنفسهم من بعد ما تبيّن لهم الحق، فيقال لمن توجه إلى الحق: فاعفوا واصفحوا حتى يظهر الحق، ولا تلتفتوا إلى تشغيبهم، ولا تشتغلوا قط بعيبهم فتكونوا أقبح منهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-7","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"قال بعض العارفين: (لا تشتغل قط بمَن يؤذيك واشتغل بالله يرده عنك، وقد غلط في هذا الأمر خلق كثير، اشتغلوا بمن يؤذيهم فطال الأذى مع الإثم. ولو أنهم رجعوا إلى مولاهم لكفاهم أمرهم.) . بل ينبغي لمن يُحْسَدُ أو يُؤْذَى أن يغيب عن الحاسد وكيده، ويشتغل بما هو مكلف به من حقوق العبودية وشهود عظمة الربوبية، فإن الله لا يضيع مَن التجأ إليه، ولا يخيب مقصود من اعتمد عليه. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-109-110-8","r":"q2-109-110","title":"2:109–110 · Pardon, worship and freedom from preoccupation with opponents","text":"ومن جملة أمانى اليهود الفارغة: ادعاء اختصاصهم بالجنة، كما أبان ذلك الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-109-110-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-109-110-s1","r":"q2-109-110","title":"Pardoning and overlooking","text":"I say: law is infinitival, forming the object of “wish.” “Unbelievers” is the second object of “turn back.” “Out of envy” is an accusative of purpose explaining “wish,” or circumstantial with respect to its plural subject. “From themselves” attaches either to “wish”—they wish it from themselves and their own inclination—or to “envy,” in which case one pauses after “unbelievers”: an envy arising from within, supported by neither a semblance of proof nor a demonstration. Pardoning ( العفو ) is refraining from punishing an offence; overlooking ( الصفح ) is turning away from the offender, as though showing him the side of one’s neck. It is therefore more emphatic than pardoning.","anchor":"en-q2-109-110-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-109-110-s2","r":"q2-109-110","title":"Fulfil the duties entrusted to you","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, warns against the Jews and other unbelievers: the unbelieving People of the Book and others wish to turn you from your religion and make you unbelievers again after faith in your Prophet, astray as before entering it. This arises from their own envy that prophethood should be among others, after the truth has become clear and they know it as they know their sons. Refrain from reproaching them and turn away from their contentiousness until God brings His command concerning them, through killing and expulsion. [B071] God has power over everything. Occupy yourselves with what He has entrusted to you: rendering the rights of servanthood and performing the duties owed to Lordship, such as perfecting prayer and paying the alms. Know that God loses none of your works. Whatever you send ahead for your day of need, you will find with Him, better and greater in reward. None of your deeds or states is hidden from Him. The verse was revealed concerning ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir and Ḥudhayfa ibn al-Yamān, who visited the house of study ( بيت المدراس ). Its people spoke gently to them and hoped to divert them from their religion. God exposed them and turned their plot back upon them. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-109-110-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-109-110-s3","r":"q2-109-110","title":"Partisanship towards one’s teachers","text":"Among the things that have crept into groups rigidly attached to imitating their shaykhs are partisanship and zeal for their shaykhs’ way, even when truth appears with others—especially among descendants of the righteous. When they see someone upon whom the lights of friendship with God and the secrets of special election have appeared, they wish to turn him from the way of truth back to mingling with people, through envy from within, after truth has become clear. Those turning towards the Real are told: pardon and overlook until truth appears. Do not attend to their contentiousness or occupy yourselves with their faults, lest you become worse than they. A gnostic said: “Never occupy yourself with someone who harms you; occupy yourself with God and He will turn that person from you. Many have erred here: they occupied themselves with those who harmed them, and the harm lasted, accompanied by sin. Had they returned to their Master, He would have sufficed them.” Someone envied or harmed should instead become absent from the envier and his plot and attend to the rights of servanthood and witnessing the grandeur of Lordship. God does not abandon one who takes refuge with Him, nor frustrate the aim of one who relies upon Him. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-109-110-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-109-110-s4","r":"q2-109-110","title":"","text":"Another of the Jews’ empty wishes is their claim to exclusive possession of Paradise, as the Real makes clear:","anchor":"en-q2-109-110-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-111-112","r":"q2-111-112","title":"2:111–112 · Empty claims and genuine surrender","text":"2:111–112 · Empty claims and genuine surrender 2:111–112","anchor":"unit-q2-111-112"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-111-112-1","r":"q2-111-112","title":"2:111–112 · Empty claims and genuine surrender","text":"وَقالُوا لَنْ يَدْخُلَ الْجَنَّةَ إِلاَّ مَنْ كانَ هُوداً أَوْ نَصارى تِلْكَ أَمانِيُّهُمْ قُلْ هاتُوا بُرْهانَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (111) بَلى مَنْ أَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهُ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ فَلَهُ أَجْرُهُ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِ وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (112)","anchor":"ar-q2-111-112-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-111-112-2","r":"q2-111-112","title":"2:111–112 · Empty claims and genuine surrender","text":"قلت: وَقالُوا عطف على وَدَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا، والضمير يعود على أهل الكتاب من اليهود والنصارى، أي: وقالت اليهود: لن يدخل الجنة إلا من كان هوداً، وقالت النصارى: لن يدخل الجنة إلا من كان نصارى، وهُوداً: جمع هائد، كبازل وبُزْل وحائل وحول، والأمانى: جمع أمنية، وهي ما يتمنى المرء ويشتهيه، وأصله أمْنُوية كأضْحُوكَة وأعجوبة، فقلبت الواو ياء وأدغمت، وهاتُوا: اسم فعل بمعنى الأمر، ومعناه آتٍ، وأهمل ماضيه ومضارعه، وأَسْلَمَ معناه: استسلم وخضع، والخوف مما يتوقع، والحزن على ما وَقع.","anchor":"ar-q2-111-112-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-111-112-3","r":"q2-111-112","title":"2:111–112 · Empty claims and genuine surrender","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وقالت اليهود: لَنْ يَدْخُلَ الْجَنَّةَ إلا مَن كان يهوديّاً، أي: على دينهم، وقالت النصارى: لن يدخل الجنة إلا مَن كان نصرانيّاً، وهذه دعاوى باطلة، وأماني فارغة ليس عليها بينة، بل مجرد أمانيهم الكاذبة، قُلْ لهم يا محمد: هاتُوا بُرْهانَكُمْ أنكم مختصون بالجنة إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في هذه الأمنية، بل يدخلها غيركم من أهل الإسلام والإحسان، فإن مَنْ أَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهُ لِلَّهِ أي: انقاد بكليته إليه وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ في أفعاله واعتقاده، فَلَهُ أَجْرُهُ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِ وهو دخول النعيم والنظر إلى وجهه الكريم، وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ من مكروه يُتوقع وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ على فوات شيء يحتاجون إليه لأنهم في ضيافة الكريم تُساق إليهم المسار وتدفع عنهم المضار، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-111-112-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-111-112-4","r":"q2-111-112","title":"2:111–112 · Empty claims and genuine surrender","text":"الإشارة: من جملة ما دخل على بعض الفقراء أنهم يَخُصون الخصوصية بهم وبمن تبع شيخهم، وينفونها عن غيرهم، وهذه نزعة يهودية، وتحكم على القدرة الإلهية، فيقال لهم: تلك أمانيكم الفارغة، بل ينالها غيركم، فمن قصد الله صادقاً وجده، وأنجز بالوفاء موعده، فمن خضع لله وانقاد لأولياء الله، فله أجره عند ربه، وهو المعرفة به، ولا خوف عليه من القطيعة، ولا يحزن على فوات نصيبه من المعرفة. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-111-112-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-111-112-5","r":"q2-111-112","title":"2:111–112 · Empty claims and genuine surrender","text":"ولما قدم نصارى نجران على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم سمعت بهم اليهود، فجاءوا إليهم، وتناظروا حتى تسابوا، وكفر اليهود بعيسى وبملّته والإنجيل، وكفر النصارى بموسى وبالتوراة، فأنزل الله فى شأنهم:","anchor":"ar-q2-111-112-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-111-112-s1","r":"q2-111-112","title":"Two claims compressed into one sentence","text":"I say: “they said” is conjoined to “those who disbelieved wished.” [Translator’s note: Cairo I:152 prints وَدَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا here; the preceding verse, 2:109, reads “many of the People of the Book wished.” The printed phrase is retained.] The pronoun refers to Jews and Christians: the Jews said that only Jews would enter Paradise, and the Christians that only Christians would enter it. Hūd ( هود ) is the plural of hāʾid , as buzl is of bāzil and ḥūl of ḥāʾil . Amānī ( أماني ) is the plural of umniyya , what someone wishes for and desires. Its original form is umnūya , like uḍḥūka and uʿjūba : wāw became yāʾ and was assimilated. Hātū ( هاتوا ) is an imperative verbal expression ( اسم فعل ): “bring!” Its past and imperfect forms are unused. To aslama is to submit and humble oneself. Fear concerns what is anticipated; grief concerns what has occurred.","anchor":"en-q2-111-112-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-111-112-s2","r":"q2-111-112","title":"Surrender of the whole person","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the Jews claimed that none but a Jew, someone of their religion, would enter Paradise; the Christians made the corresponding claim for a Christian. These are false claims and empty wishes without evidence, merely their lying aspirations. Tell them, Muḥammad: bring your proof of exclusive entitlement to Paradise, if this wish is truthful. Rather, others enter it—people of surrender and excellence ( الإسلام والإحسان ). Whoever surrenders his face to God, yielding to Him in his entirety, and excels in conduct and belief, has his reward with his Lord: entry into bliss and vision of His noble Face. They fear no anticipated harm and grieve for no needed thing missed. As guests of the Generous One, joys are brought to them and harms repelled. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-111-112-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-111-112-s3","r":"q2-111-112","title":"Special election is not a school’s monopoly","text":"Among the errors that have entered some spiritual aspirants is restricting special election to themselves and those following their shaykh, denying it to others. This is a tendency resembling the Jews’ claim and an attempt to dictate to divine power. They are told: those are your empty wishes; others attain it. Whoever sincerely seeks God finds Him, and He fulfils His promise faithfully. Whoever humbles himself to God and submits to His friends has his reward with his Lord—knowledge of Him. He need not fear severance or grieve over missing his portion of gnosis. Through God is success; He guides to the level way.","anchor":"en-q2-111-112-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-111-112-s4","r":"q2-111-112","title":"","text":"When the Christians of Najrān came to the Prophet, the Jews heard of them and came. They debated until they exchanged insults: the Jews denied Jesus, his religion and the Gospel; the Christians denied Moses and the Torah. God revealed concerning them:","anchor":"en-q2-111-112-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-113","r":"q2-113","title":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency","text":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency 2:113","anchor":"unit-q2-113"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-113-1","r":"q2-113","title":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency","text":"وَقالَتِ الْيَهُودُ لَيْسَتِ النَّصارى عَلى شَيْءٍ وَقالَتِ النَّصارى لَيْسَتِ الْيَهُودُ عَلى شَيْءٍ وَهُمْ يَتْلُونَ الْكِتابَ كَذلِكَ قالَ الَّذِينَ لا يَعْلَمُونَ مِثْلَ قَوْلِهِمْ فَاللَّهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ فِيما كانُوا فِيهِ يَخْتَلِفُونَ (113)","anchor":"ar-q2-113-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-113-2","r":"q2-113","title":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله إخباراً عن مقالات اليهود والنصارى وتقبيحاً لصنيعهم: وَقالَتِ الْيَهُودُ في الرد على النصارى: لَيْسَتِ النَّصارى عَلى شَيْءٍ يعتد به، وَقالَتِ النَّصارى في سَبِّ اليهود: لَيْسَتِ الْيَهُودُ عَلى شَيْءٍ يعتمد عليه، والحالة أنهم يَتْلُونَ الْكِتابَ، فاليهود يتلون التوراة وفيها البشارة بعيسى عليه السلام، والنصارى يتلون الإنجيل، وفيه تقرير شريعة التوراة وصحة نبوة موسى عليه السلام، فقد كفرت كلُّ فرقة بكتابها غضباً وتعصباً، ومثل مقالتهم هذه قالَ الَّذِينَ لا يَعْلَمُونَ، وهم المشركون، فقالوا: ليس المسلمون على شيء، فَاللَّهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ فِيما كانُوا فِيهِ يَخْتَلِفُونَ فيدخل أهل الحق الجنة وأهلَ الباطل النار. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-113-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-113-3","r":"q2-113","title":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency","text":"الإشارة: كل ما قصه الحق تعالى علينا من مساوئ غيرنا فالمقصود به التنفير والتحذير من مثل ما ارتكبوه، والتخلق بضد ما فعلوه، فكل من تراه ينقص الناس ويصغّرهم فهو أصغرهم، وكل من تراه يقول: أصحاب سيدي فلان ليسوا على شيء، وأصحاب سيدي فلان ليس عندهم شيء، فليس هو على شيء، وقد ابتلي بعض المتصوفة بهذا الوصف الذميم، ينصب الميزان على الناس، فيسقط قوما ويرفع آخرين، وهو يتلو كتاب الله، ويسمع قوله تعالى: وَلا تَجَسَّسُوا وَلا يَغْتَبْ بَعْضُكُمْ بَعْضاً ... الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-113-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-113-4","r":"q2-113","title":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency","text":"وأكثر ما تجد هذا الوصف في بعض الفقهاء المتجمدين على ظاهر الشريعة، يعتقد ألا علم فوق علمه، ولا فهم فوق فهمه، كيف؟ والله تعالى يقول: وَما أُوتِيتُمْ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا، وَفَوْقَ كُلِّ ذِي عِلْمٍ عَلِيمٌ، وقد قال إمام الحرمين: (لإِنْ أُدْخلَ ألْفَ كَافرٍ في الإسْلامِ بِشُبْهَةٍ خَيْرٌ مِنْ إِخراجِ واحدٍ منْه بشُبْهة) .","anchor":"ar-q2-113-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-113-5","r":"q2-113","title":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency","text":"فالواجب على مَن أراد السلامة أن يُحسن الظن بجميع المسلمين، ويعتقد فيهم أنهم كلهم صالحون، ففي الحديث: «خَصْلَتَان لَيْسَ فوقهما شيء من الخير: حُسْن الظنِّ بالله، وحُسْن الظن بعباد الله، وخصلتان ليس فوقهما شيء من الشرِّ: سُوءُ الظن بِالله، وسوء الظن بعباد الله» . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-113-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-113-6","r":"q2-113","title":"2:113 · Mutual denigration and the presumption of one’s own sufficiency","text":"ثم وبّخ الحق- تعالى- النصارى على منع الناس من بيت المقدس وإيذاء مَن يصلي فيه، وطرح الأقذار فيه، مع زعمهم أنهم على الحق دون غيرهم، قاله ابن عباس، أو كفار قريش حيث منعوا المسلمين من الصلاة فيه، وصدوا رسول الله عن الوصول إليه، قاله ابن زيد، والتحقيق: أن الحق تعالى وبخ الجميع، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-113-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-113-s1","r":"q2-113","title":"A dispute that contradicts the books they read","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, reports the Jews’ and Christians’ statements and condemns their conduct. The Jews reply to the Christians, “They stand upon nothing worth considering”; the Christians insult the Jews, “They stand upon nothing reliable.” Yet they recite Scripture: the Jews read the Torah, which foretells Jesus, and the Christians the Gospel, which confirms the Torah’s Law and Moses’ prophethood. Each party thus disbelieves in its own Book through anger and partisanship. Those without knowledge—the polytheists—make the same assertion: the Muslims stand upon nothing. God will judge their disputes on the Day of Resurrection, admitting the people of truth to Paradise and the people of falsehood to the Fire. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-113-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-113-s2","r":"q2-113","title":"Do not make yourself the measure of everyone","text":"Everything the Real recounts of others’ faults is intended to deter and warn us against committing the same, and to have us cultivate the opposite. Whoever belittles and diminishes others is himself the smallest. Whoever says, “The companions of master so-and-so stand upon nothing; those of master so-and-so possess nothing,” himself stands upon nothing. Some Sufis have been afflicted by this blameworthy trait: setting up a scale over people, bringing some down and raising others, while reading God’s Book and hearing His words, “Do not spy, and do not backbite one another” [49:12]. You find this especially among jurists rigidly fixed upon the outward Sacred Law, imagining no knowledge above theirs and no understanding beyond theirs. How can this be, when God says, “You have been given but little knowledge” [17:85], and “Above every possessor of knowledge is one more knowing” [12:76]? The Imām al-Ḥaramayn said: “To admit a thousand unbelievers into Islam on a doubtful ground is better than to expel one person from it on a doubtful ground.” [B072] Whoever desires safety must think well of all Muslims and believe them all righteous. In the hadith: “Two traits have no goodness above them: thinking well of God and thinking well of God’s servants. Two traits have no evil above them: thinking ill of God and thinking ill of His servants.” Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-113-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-113-s3","r":"q2-113","title":"","text":"The Real next reproaches the Christians for preventing people from the sanctuary in Jerusalem, harming those praying there and casting filth into it, while claiming that they alone follow truth: this is Ibn ʿAbbās’s explanation. Or He reproaches the unbelieving Quraysh for preventing Muslims from praying in the sanctuary and barring the Messenger’s access: this is Ibn Zayd’s view. The sound conclusion is that He reproaches them all, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-113-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-114","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within 2:114","anchor":"unit-q2-114"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-1","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ مَنَعَ مَساجِدَ اللَّهِ أَنْ يُذْكَرَ فِيهَا اسْمُهُ وَسَعى فِي خَرابِها أُولئِكَ ما كانَ لَهُمْ أَنْ يَدْخُلُوها إِلاَّ خائِفِينَ لَهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيا خِزْيٌ وَلَهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ عَذابٌ عَظِيمٌ (114)","anchor":"ar-q2-114-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-2","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"قلت: مَنْ مبتدأ، وأَظْلَمُ خبر، وأَنْ يُذْكَرَ إما منصوب على إسقاط الخافض وتسلط الفعل عليه، أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-114-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-3","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"من أن يذكر، أو بدل اشتمال من مَساجِدَ، أو مجرور بالحرف المحذوف، قاله سيبويه. وخائِفِينَ حال من الواو.","anchor":"ar-q2-114-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-4","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لا أحَد أكثرُ جُرْماً ولا أعظم ظلماً مِمَّنْ يمنع مَساجِدَ اللَّهِ من أَنْ يُذْكَرَ اسم الله فيها، جماعة أو فرادى، في صلاة أو غيرها، وَسَعى فِي خَرابِها حيث عطل عمارتها، أُولئِكَ ما كانَ ينبغي لَهُمْ أَنْ يَدْخُلُوها إلا بخشية وخشوع، فكيف يجترءون على تخريبها؟ أو ما كان الواجب أن يدخلوها إلا خائفين من المؤمنين أن يبطشوا بهم فضلاً عن أن يمنعوهم منها، أو ما كانَ لَهُمْ في علم الله وقضائه أَنْ يَدْخُلُوها إِلَّا خائِفِينَ، فيكون وعداً أنجزه الله لهم، وقد فتح الله لهم مكة والشام، فكان لا يدخل بيت الله الحرام كافر إلا خفية، خائفاً من القتل، ولا يدخل نصراني بيت المقدس إلا خائفاً من المسلمين، فنالهم فِي الدُّنْيا خِزْيٌ وهو قتل الحربي، وضرب الجزية على الذمي، وخزي المشركين قتلهم يوم الفتح، وإذلالهم بدخولها عليهم عنوة، ولمن مات على الكفر فِي الْآخِرَةِ عَذابٌ عَظِيمٌ.","anchor":"ar-q2-114-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-5","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"وهذه الآية- وإن نزلت في الكفار- فهي عامة لكل من يمنع الناس من الذكر في المساجد، كيفما كان قياماً أو قعوداً، جماعة أو فرادى. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-114-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-6","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"الإشارة: مساجدُ الله هي حضرة القلوب وحضرة الأرواح وحضرة الأسرار، فحضرة القلوب لأهل المراقبة من أهل الإيمان، وحضرة الأرواح والأسرار لأهل المشاهدة والمكالمة من أهل الإحسان، فمن منع نفسه من الدخول في هذه الحضرات الثلاث، وسعى في خراب باطنه باتباع الحظوظ والشهوات، ومال إلى الدنيا وزخارفها الغرارات، فلا أحد أظلم منه نفساً، ولا أبخس منه صفقةً. فلا ينجعُ في هؤلاء إلا خوف مُزعج أو شوقٍ مقلق. فإن لم يكن أحد من هذين بقي على غيّه حتى مخايل الموت، فيحن إلى الدخول فيها خائفاً، ولا ينفع حينئذٍ الندم، وقد زلّت به القدم، له في الدنيا ذلك الفقر والجزع، وله في الآخرة غم الحجاب وسوء الحساب وحسرة العتاب، نسأل الله العافية في الدارين. آمين، بمنه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-114-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-7","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"وقال القشيري: نفْسُ العابدِ وَطَنُ العبادة، وقلب العارف وطن المعرفة، وروح الواجد وطن المحبة، وسر الموحِّد وطن المشاهدة، ولا أظلم ممن سعى في خراب وطن العابد بالشهوات، وفي وطن المعرفة بالمُنى والعلاقات، وفي وطن المحبة بالحظوظ والمساكنات، وفي وطن الموحد بالالتفات إلى القربات. هـ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-114-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-114-8","r":"q2-114","title":"2:114 · The sanctuaries of worship and the sanctuaries within","text":"ولمَّا ذكر الحق تعالى تعطيل بعض المساجد والمنع من الصلاة فيها، وسع على عباده فى الصلاة حيث شاءوا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-114-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-114-s1","r":"q2-114","title":"The construction of prevention","text":"I say: “who” is the subject and “more unjust” its predicate. “That His name should be remembered” is either accusative after the preposition is omitted and the verb governs it directly—“prevents from its being remembered”; or an apposition of inclusion ( بدل اشتمال ) to “places of worship”; or genitive through the omitted preposition, according to Sībawayh. “In fear” is circumstantial, relating to the plural subject of “enter.”","anchor":"en-q2-114-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-114-s2","r":"q2-114","title":"Preventing remembrance in God’s mosques","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: no one commits a greater crime or injustice than one who prevents God’s name from being remembered in His mosques, in groups or individually, in prayer or otherwise, and strives to ruin them by obstructing their flourishing. Such people should enter only with reverence and humility: how dare they destroy them? Alternatively, they ought to enter only fearing that the believers might seize them, far less prevent the believers from entering. Or, in God’s knowledge and decree, they were to enter only in fear: this is then a promise He fulfilled. God opened Mecca and Syria to the believers. Thereafter no unbeliever entered the Sacred House except secretly, fearing death, and no Christian entered the sanctuary in Jerusalem except in fear of the Muslims. They thus suffered worldly disgrace: the killing of a belligerent unbeliever and the imposition of the poll-tax on a protected non-Muslim. The polytheists’ disgrace was their being killed on the day of the conquest and humiliated by the city’s forcible entry. Whoever died in unbelief has a tremendous punishment in the Hereafter. [B073] Although revealed concerning unbelievers, the verse applies generally to anyone preventing people from remembrance in mosques, however performed: standing or sitting, together or alone. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-114-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-114-s3","r":"q2-114","title":"The presences of hearts, spirits and secrets","text":"God’s mosques are the presence of hearts, the presence of spirits and the presence of secrets. The presence of hearts belongs to the people of watchfulness among those of faith; the presences of spirits and secrets belong to those of witnessing and divine converse among the people of spiritual excellence. Whoever bars himself from these three presences, strives to ruin his inward being through private portions and desires, and inclines towards the world’s deceptive adornments, is unsurpassed in injustice to himself and loss in his bargain. Only a fear that shakes him or a longing that unsettles him can benefit such a person. Without either, he persists in error until death’s signs appear. Then he longs to enter, afraid; but remorse no longer helps, and his foot has slipped. In this world he has poverty and panic; in the next, the anguish of veiling, an evil reckoning and the sorrow of reproach. We ask God for well-being in both abodes, through His favour and generosity. Amen. Al-Qushayrī says: the worshipper’s self is the homeland of worship; the gnostic’s heart, the homeland of knowledge; the ecstatic’s spirit, the homeland of love; and the unifier’s secret, the homeland of witnessing. None is more unjust than one who ruins the worshipper’s homeland through desires, that of knowledge through wishes and attachments, that of love through private portions and settling into repose, and that of the unifier through attending to acts of drawing near themselves. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-114-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-114-s4","r":"q2-114","title":"","text":"Having mentioned the obstruction of some mosques and prevention of prayer there, the Real gives His servants breadth to pray where they may, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-114-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-115","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face 2:115","anchor":"unit-q2-115"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-1","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"وَلِلَّهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ فَأَيْنَما تُوَلُّوا فَثَمَّ وَجْهُ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ واسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ (115)","anchor":"ar-q2-115-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-2","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"قلت: (أينما) شرطية، و (تولوا) شَرْطُها، وجملة (فثم) جوابها، و «وَلْي» يستعمل بمعنى أدبر وبمعنى أقبل، تقول: وليت عن كذا أو كذا، والوجه هنا بمعنى الجهة، تقول: سافرت في وجه كذا، أي في جهة كذا. قاله ابن عطية.","anchor":"ar-q2-115-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-3","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلِلَّهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ، والجهات كلها له، لا يختص ملكه بمكان دون آخر، فإذا مُنعتم من الصلاة في المساجد ففي أي مكان كنتم ووليتم وجهكم إلى القبلة التي أمرتم بالتوجه إليها فثم جهته التي أمر بها، أو فثم ذاته المقدسة، أي: عالم مطلع على ما يفعل فيه، إِنَّ اللَّهَ واسِعٌ بإحاطته بالأشياء، أو برحمته يريد التوسعة على عباده، عَلِيمٌ بمصالحهم وأعمالهم في الأماكن كلها.","anchor":"ar-q2-115-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-4","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"وعن ابن عمر: أنها نزلت في صلاة المسافر على الراحلة حيثما توجهت به، وقيل: في قوم عميت عليهم القبلة فصلوا إلى أنحاء مختلفة، فلما أصبحوا تبينوا خطأهم، وعلى هذا: لو أخطأ المجتهد ثم تبين له الخطأ، لم يلزمه التدارك. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-115-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-5","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الأماكن والجهات، وكل ما ظهر من الكائنات، قائمة بأنوار الصفات، ممحوة بأحدية الذات، «كان الله ولا شيء معه، وهو الآن على ما عليه كان» إذ لا وجود لشئ مع الله، فَأَيْنَما تُوَلُّوا فَثَمَّ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-6","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"وَجْهُ اللَّهِ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-7","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"، محق الآثار بأفلاك الأنوار، وانمحت الأنوار بأحدية الأسرار، وانفرد بالوجود الواحد القهار، ولله درّ القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-115-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-8","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"مُذْ عَرفْتُ الإِلَهَ لَمْ أَرَ غَيْراً ... وكَذّا الْغَيْرُ عندنا ممنوع","anchor":"ar-q2-115-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-9","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"مُذْ تَجَمَّعْتْ مَا خَشيتُ افْتِراقًا ... فأَنّا اليَوْمَ وَاصلٌ مجموع","anchor":"ar-q2-115-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-10","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"وقال آخر:","anchor":"ar-q2-115-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-11","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"فالكلُّ دونَ اللهِ إنْ حَققتَهُ ... عَدم عَلَى التفصيلِ والإجمالِ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-12","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"مَن لاَ وجُودَ لذاتهِ مِنْ ذاتِهِ ... فوجُودُهُ لولاهُ عينُ مُحَالِ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-13","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"وقال صاحب العينية:","anchor":"ar-q2-115-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-14","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"تَجلَّى حَبِيبي فِي مَرَائِي جَمَالِهِ ... فَفِي كُلِّ مَرْئِيّ لِلْحَبِيبِ طَلاَئِعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-15","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"فَلَمَّا تَبَدَّى حُسْنُه مُتَنوعاً ... تَسمَّى بأسْماءٍ فهُنَّ مَطالِعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-16","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"وقال الششتري:","anchor":"ar-q2-115-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-17","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"مَحْبوبي قدْ عَمَّ الوجودْ ... وقدْ ظهرَ في بيضٍ وسُودْ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-18","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"قال بعض السلف: (دخلت ديرا فجاء وقت الصلاة، فقلت لبعض النصارى: دُلني على بقعة طاهرة أصلي فيها، فقال لي: طهر قلبك عما سواه، وقف حيث شئت، قال: فخَجِلت منه) . ويحكى عن أبى يزيد رضي الله عنه أنه كان يصلي إلى أي جهة شاء، ويتلو هذه الآية، فالوجه عند أهل التحقيق هو عين الذات، يعني أسرار الذات وأنوار الصفات. قال تعالى: كُلُّ شَيْءٍ هالِكٌ إِلَّا وَجْهَهُ أي: كل شيء فانٍ ومستهلك في الحال والاستقبال إلا ذاته المقدسة، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-115-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-19","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"فالعارِفُون فَنَوْا بأَن لَمْ يَشْهَدُوا ... شَيْئاً سِوَى المُتَكَبِّرِ المتَعالِي","anchor":"ar-q2-115-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-20","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"ورَأوْا سواهُ عَلَى الحقيقةِ هَالِكاً ... فِي الحالِ وَالْمَاضِي والاستقبال","anchor":"ar-q2-115-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-21","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"وقلت في تائيتي الخمرية في وصف الخمرة الأزلية:","anchor":"ar-q2-115-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-22","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"تنزهت عن حكم الحلول في وصفها ... فليس لها في سوى شَكْلهِ حَلَّتِ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-23","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"تجلت عروسا في مرائي جمالها ... وأرخت ستور الكبرياء بِعزَّةِ","anchor":"ar-q2-115-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-24","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"فمَا ظَهَر في الكون غير بهائها ... وما احتجبت إلا لحجب سريرة","anchor":"ar-q2-115-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-115-25","r":"q2-115","title":"2:115 · Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face","text":"ولما قالت اليهود: عزير ابن الله، وقالت النصارى: الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ الله، وقالت المشركون: الملائكة بنات الله، رد الله تعالى عليهم بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-115-25"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-115-s1","r":"q2-115","title":"Turning and direction","text":"I say: “wherever” ( أينما ) is conditional, “you turn” its condition, and “there is…” its response. The verb wallā can mean either to turn away or to turn towards: one says wallaytu ʿan kadhā or wallaytu kadhā . Here wajh , “face,” means direction: “I travelled in the direction of such-and-such.” So Ibn ʿAṭiyya explains. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-05] ]","anchor":"en-q2-115-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-115-s2","r":"q2-115","title":"God’s possession of every direction","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: east and west belong to God, as do all directions. His dominion is not restricted to one place rather than another. If prevented from praying in mosques, wherever you are and turn towards the prayer-direction you have been commanded to face, there is His appointed direction. Or there is His holy Essence: that is, He knows and observes what is done there. God is encompassing in His knowledge of things, or in His mercy, wishing breadth for His servants; He knows their interests and their deeds in every place. Ibn ʿUmar relates that the verse concerns a traveller’s prayer on his mount, whichever way it turns. Another explanation concerns people unable to determine the prayer-direction, who prayed facing different ways and discovered their mistake in the morning. On that interpretation, one who has exercised judgement and subsequently discovers an error need not make the prayer up. Thus al-Bayḍāwī. [B074]","anchor":"en-q2-115-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-115-s3","r":"q2-115","title":"The Face, the lights and the secrets","text":"Know that places, directions and every manifested existent stand through the lights of the Attributes and are effaced by the unicity of the Essence ( أحدية الذات ). “God was, and nothing was with Him; He is now as He was.” Nothing has existence alongside God. “Wherever you turn, there is God’s Face.” The traces are effaced by the orbits of lights, the lights effaced by the unicity of secrets, and the One, the All-Subduing, alone possesses existence. How fine are these words: Since knowing God, I have seen no other; “other” is inadmissible with us. Since being gathered, I have feared no parting: today I have arrived, gathered into unity. Another says: All beside God, when truly examined, is nothing, in detail and in sum. What has no existence of itself from itself— its existence, were it not for Him, is sheer impossibility. The author of the ʿAyniyya says: My Beloved disclosed Himself in the mirrors of His beauty; in everything seen, the Beloved’s advance signs appear. When His beauty appeared in diverse forms, He took names, and they are its places of rising. Al-Shushtarī says: My Beloved has encompassed existence and appeared in white and black. One of the predecessors said: “I entered a monastery when prayer-time came and asked a Christian to show me a pure place to pray. He said, ‘Purify your heart of other-than-Him, and stand where you will.’ I was ashamed before him.” It is related that Abū Yazīd used to pray in whatever direction he wished and recite this verse. [B074] For the people of realization, the Face is the Essence itself: the mysteries of the Essence and the lights of the Attributes. God says, “Everything is perishing except His Face” [28:88]: everything is passing away and consumed, now and in the future, except His holy Essence. They recited: The gnostics passed away from themselves, seeing nothing but the Supremely Great, the Exalted. They saw all else truly perishing, in present, past and future. In my Tāʾiyya on wine, describing the eternal wine, I said: In her description she transcends indwelling; [there is no other in whose form she dwells]. A bride, she disclosed herself in mirrors of her beauty, and in might let fall the curtains of majesty. Nothing appears in the cosmos but her splendour; she is hidden only by veils within the heart. [B075] [Translator’s note: Cairo I:157 reads فليس لها في سوى شكله حلت. Ibn ʿAjība quotes the same couplet again at Cairo II:22, on Q5:17, with the order فليس لها سوى في شكله حلت, “there is no other in whose form she dwells.” There the preceding prose expressly explains that the eternal wine is beyond indwelling and union because there is no second entity in which it could dwell or with which it could unite. This establishes the intended sense and pronoun references: “her/she” is the wine, and “his/its form” belongs to the hypothetical other. The bracketed English follows that internal parallel. I:157’s different word order is preserved in the Arabic companion; the full poem’s independent manuscript text has not been established.]","anchor":"en-q2-115-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-115-s4","r":"q2-115","title":"","text":"When the Jews said, “ʿUzayr is God’s son,” the Christians, “The Messiah is God’s son,” and the polytheists, “The angels are God’s daughters,” God Most High refuted them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-115-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-116-117","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God 2:116–117","anchor":"unit-q2-116-117"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-1","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"وَقالُوا اتَّخَذَ اللَّهُ وَلَداً سُبْحانَهُ بَلْ لَهُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ كُلٌّ لَهُ قانِتُونَ (116) بَدِيعُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَإِذا قَضى أَمْراً فَإِنَّما يَقُولُ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ (117)","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-2","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"قلت: هذه الجملة معطوفة على قوله: وَقالَتِ الْيَهُودُ ... الخ، ومن قرأ بغير واو جعلَها مستأنفة، و (بديع) :","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-3","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"بمعنى مُبدِع، والإبداع: اختراع الشيء من غير تقدم شيء. وقوله: (كن فيكون) ، قدّره سيبويه: فهو يكون، وقرأ ابن عامر بنصب المضارع، ولَحَّنه بعضُهم لأن المنصوبَ في جواب الأمر لا بد أن يصلح جواباً لشرطه، تقول:","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-4","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"اضرب زيداً فيستقيم، أي: إن تضربه يستقيم، ولا يصلح أن تقول هنا: إن يكن يكن، وقد يجاب بحمله على المعنى، والتقدير: إن قلت كن يكن.","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-5","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وقالت اليهود والنصارى والمشركون: اتَّخَذَ اللَّهُ وَلَداً تعالى الله عن قولهم، وتنزه عن ذلك لأنه يقتضي الجنسية والمشابهة والاحتياج، والحق منزَّهٌ عن ذلك. بل كل ما استقر في السموات السبع والأرَضين السبع ملكه وعبيده، فكيف يكون العبد ولداً لمالكه؟. وأيضاً كل ما ظهر في الوجود كله قانت، أي: خاضع ومطيع لله، وعابد له، ومقهور تحت حكمه ومشيئته، وذلك مُنافٍ لحال البُنوة.","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-6","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"وأيضاً: كل ما دخل عالم التكوين فهو مُبْدَع ومَخترَع لله، ومصنوع من مصنوعات الله، فلا يصح أن يكون ولداً، وأيضاً: الولد يحتاج إلى صاحبة ومعالجة ومهلة، والحق تعالى أمره بين الكاف والنون، بل أسرع من لحظ العيون، فإِذا قَضى أَمْراً أي: أراده، فَإِنَّما يَقُولُ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ، ولا يتوقف على لفظة كُنْ، وإنما هو كناية عن سرعة الاقتدار.","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-7","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"قال البيضاوي: واعلم أن السبب في هذه الضلالة أن أرباب الشرائع المتقدمة كانوا يطلقون الأب على الله تعالى، باعتبار أنه السبب الأول، حتى قالوا: إن الأب هو الرب الأصغر، والله تعالى هو الرب الأكبر، ثم ظنّ الجهلة منهم أن المراد به معنى الولادة، فاعتقدوا ذلك تقليداً، ولذلك كفر قائله ومنع منه مطلقاً حسماً لمادة الفساد. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-8","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أنك إذا نظرت بعين البصيرة، أو بحق البصيرة، إلى الوجود بأسره، وجدته ذاتاً واحدة، ونسبته من الحق نسبة واحدة، أنوار ظاهرة، وأسرار باطنة، حكمته ظاهرة، وقدرته باطنة حسن ظاهر، ومعنى باطن، عبودية ظاهرة، وأسرار معاني الربوبية باطنة إذ لا قيام للعبودية إلا بأسرار معاني الربوبية، قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-9","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُمْسِكُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضَ أَنْ تَزُولا، وقال تعالى: اللَّهُ نُورُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ، وقال في الحكم: «الأكوان ظاهرها غرة وباطنها عبرة، فالنفس تنظر إلى ظاهر بهجتها، والقلب ينظر إلى باطن عبرتها» . فأهل الفَرْقِ يثبتون الأشياء مستقلة مع الله، وربما تغالى بعضهم فأشركها معه في الألوهية، فتعالى الله عن ذلك علوًّا كبيراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-10","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"قال محيي الدين الحاتمي: من رأى الخلق لا فعلَ لهم فقد فاز، ومن رآهم لا حياة لهم فقد جاز، ومن رآهم بعين العدم فقد وصل. هـ. قلت: ومن أثبتهم بالله فقد تمكن وصاله، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-11","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"مَن أبصرَ الخلقَ كالسرابِ ... فقَد تَرقَّى عن الحجابِ","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-12","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"إِلى وُجودٍ تراهُ رَتْقاً ... بِلاَ ابتعادٍ ولا اقْتِرابِ","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-13","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"ولم تُشَاهِدْ به سواهُ ... هناك تهدى إلى الصوابِ","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-14","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"فَلا خِطابَ بِه إليهِ ... وَلا مُشِيرَ إلى الخطابِ. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-116-117-15","r":"q2-116-117","title":"2:116–117 · Origination without dependence and creation subsisting through God","text":"ولما قال رافع بن حريملة- من أحبار يهود- للرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: أسمعنا كلام الله إن كنت رسوله، أو أرنا آية تصدقك، ردّ الله تعالى عليه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-116-117-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-116-117-s1","r":"q2-116-117","title":"The response to the command “Be”","text":"I say: this sentence is conjoined to “The Jews said…” [2:113]. In the reading without wāw, it begins independently. Badīʿ ( بديع ) means mubdiʿ , an originator; origination ( الإبداع ) is bringing something into being without anything preceding it. Sībawayh understands “Be, and it is” as “and so it is.” Ibn ʿĀmir reads the imperfect verb in the subjunctive ( النصب ). Some declared his reading grammatically faulty: a subjunctive answering a command must also work as the response to its conditional equivalent. “Strike Zayd, that he may become upright” means “if you strike him, he becomes upright,” whereas “if it is, it is” does not work here. One may reply by considering the meaning: “If I say ‘Be,’ it is.” [B076]","anchor":"en-q2-116-117-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-116-117-s2","r":"q2-116-117","title":"Why divine sonship is denied","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the Jews, Christians and polytheists claimed that God took a child. Exalted is He beyond their assertion. Sonship implies a common kind, resemblance and need; the Real transcends these. Everything in the seven heavens and seven earths is His possession and servant: how could a servant be his owner’s child? Everything manifest in existence is also obedient—submissive, compliant and worshipping God, constrained by His decree and will. This is incompatible with sonship. Everything entering the world of formation ( التكوين ) is originated, invented and made by God; it cannot therefore be His child. A child also requires a consort, a process and a period of time. The Real’s command is between kāf and nūn, the two letters of “Be”—indeed, swifter than the blink of an eye. When He decrees, that is wills, a thing, He only says “Be,” and it is. This does not depend on uttering the word “Be”; the expression alludes to the swiftness of His power. Al-Bayḍāwī says: the cause of this error was that adherents of earlier revealed Laws used “Father” of God as the first cause, even saying that a father was the lesser lord and God the greater Lord. The ignorant then supposed that literal generation was intended and adopted that belief through imitation. For that reason one who says it is judged unbelieving, and the expression is prohibited altogether to close the source of corruption. Thus ends his explanation.","anchor":"en-q2-116-117-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-116-117-s3","r":"q2-116-117","title":"Effacement followed by affirmation through God","text":"Know that when you regard all existence with the eye of insight ( عين البصيرة ), or with the truth of insight ( حق البصيرة ), you find it one reality ( ذاتاً واحدة ), standing in one relation to the Real: outward lights and inward secrets; His wisdom outward and His power inward; outward beauty and inward meaning; outward servanthood and the secrets of Lordship’s meanings inward. Servanthood stands only through the secrets of Lordship’s meanings. [B077] God says, “God holds the heavens and earth lest they pass away” [35:41], and “God is the Light of the heavens and earth” [24:35]. In the Ḥikam : “Created things are outwardly a delusion, inwardly a lesson. The lower self looks at their outward splendour; the heart looks at their inward lesson.” The people of separation ( الفرق ) affirm things as independent alongside God. Some go so far as to associate them with Him in divinity. Exalted is God far beyond that. Muḥyī al-Dīn al-Ḥātimī says: whoever sees creatures as having no action has succeeded; whoever sees them as having no life has crossed over; whoever sees them with the eye of non-existence has arrived. I say: whoever affirms them through God has become firmly established in his arrival. They recited: Whoever sees creation like a mirage has risen beyond the veil, to existence seen as undivided, without distance or proximity. There you witness none but Him; there you are guided to what is right. No address is directed there to Him, nor any pointer to that address.","anchor":"en-q2-116-117-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-116-117-s4","r":"q2-116-117","title":"","text":"When Rāfiʿ ibn Ḥuraymila, one of the Jewish learned men, told the Messenger, “Let us hear God’s speech if you are His messenger, or show us a sign confirming you,” God replied:","anchor":"en-q2-116-117-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-118-119","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing 2:118–119","anchor":"unit-q2-118-119"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-1","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"وَقالَ الَّذِينَ لا يَعْلَمُونَ لَوْلا يُكَلِّمُنَا اللَّهُ أَوْ تَأْتِينا آيَةٌ كَذلِكَ قالَ الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِثْلَ قَوْلِهِمْ تَشابَهَتْ قُلُوبُهُمْ قَدْ بَيَّنَّا الْآياتِ لِقَوْمٍ يُوقِنُونَ (118) إِنَّا أَرْسَلْناكَ بِالْحَقِّ بَشِيراً وَنَذِيراً وَلا تَسْأَلْ عَنْ أَصْحابِ الْجَحِيمِ (119)","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-2","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"قلت: هذه المقالة صدرت من بعض اليهود والمشركين، قالوا ذلك تعنتاً وعناداً، لا طلباً لليقين، فلذلك نفى الله عنهم العلم رأساً، والمقصود في هذه الآيات كلها توبيخ اليهود.","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-3","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقالَ الَّذِينَ لا علم عندهم: هلا يُكَلِّمُنَا اللَّهُ حتى نسمع منه أنك رسوله، أَوْ تَأْتِينا آيَةٌ ظاهرة، نراها جهرة تدل على رسالتك، كما كانت لموسى- عليه السلام-.","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-4","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"وهذه المقالة التي صدرت من اليهود، تَعنتاً وعناداً، قد صدرت ممن قبلهم من أسلافهم، فقالوا: أَرِنَا اللَّهَ جَهْرَةً، ومن النصارى فقالوا: هَلْ يَسْتَطِيعُ رَبُّكَ أَنْ يُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنا مائِدَةً مِنَ السَّماءِ، ومن المشركين فقالوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-5","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"لَنْ نُؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّى تَفْجُرَ لَنا مِنَ الْأَرْضِ يَنْبُوعاً، أَوْ تَكُونَ لَكَ جَنَّةٌ مِنْ نَخِيلٍ وَعِنَبٍ فَتُفَجِّرَ الْأَنْهارَ خِلالَها تَفْجِيراً الآية. فقد تماثلت قلوبهم في الكفر والعناد، وتشابهت في العتو والفساد، قد أوضحنا لك الآيات البينات، تحقق رسالتك وتقرر اصطفائيتك، لمن طلب مزيد الإيقان، وكشف البيان على نعت العيان، فأعظمُها القرآن، ثم ما أوضحته من شرائع الأحكام، وما بينته من الحلال والحرام، ثم ما أخبرت به من الغيوب، وما كشفته عن القلوب من الكروب، ثم نطق الجمادات والأحجار، كحنين الجذع وانقياد الأشجار، وتسبيح الحصى، وتسليم الحجر، وقد نبع الماء من بين أصابعه وانهمر، إلى ما لا يعد ولا يحصى.","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-6","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"فقد أَرْسَلْناكَ بِالْحَقِّ، أي: متلبساً بالحق ومبيناً له، بَشِيراً لمن صدقك واتبعك بالنعيم المقيم، ونَذِيراً لمن خالفك بعذاب الجحيم. فلا تسأل عن حالهم إذا أفضوا إليه، فإنه أعظم من أن يذكر، وأفظع من أن يسمع، إذ لا يمكن تفسير حالهم، ولا يستطيع أحد سماع أهوالهم، فالله يعصمنا من موارد الردى، ويوفقنا لاتباع الحق والهدى، أو لا يسألك ربك عنهم فهو أعلم بحالهم، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-7","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"الإشارة: طلب الكرامات وظهور الآيات من طبع أهل الجهل والعناد، وليس هو من شيم أهل الهداية والاسترشاد. فالطريق واضح لمن طلب السبيل، والحق لائح لمن أبصر الدليل، فمن كَحل عين بصيرته بإثمد التوحيد الخاص، لم يقع بصره إلا على الحق، ولا يعرف إلا إياه، ورأى الأشياء كلها قائمة بالله، بل لا وجود لها مع الله، ومن فتح الله سمع قلبه لم يسمع إلا من الحق، ولا يسمع إلا به، كما قال القائل: أنا بالله أنطق ومن الله أسمع.","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-8","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"وقال الجنيد رضي الله عنه: (لي أربعون سنة أُناجي الحق، والناس يَروْن أني أناجى الخلق) . فالخلق محذوفون عند أهل العلم بالتحقيق، مُثْبَتُونَ عند أهل الجهل والتفريق. يقولون: لولا يكلمنا الله أو تأتينا آية، مع أنه يكلمهم في كل","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-9","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"وقت وساعة، كذلك قال مَن شاركهم في الجهل بالله، مع وضوح الآيات لمن عرف الله. والله يقول الحق وهو يهدي السبيل.","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-118-119-10","r":"q2-118-119","title":"2:118–119 · Signs, certainty and the opening of the heart’s hearing","text":"ولمَّا قالت اليهود والنصارى لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم: اجعل بيننا وبينك هُدْنة نتبعك بعدها، وأضمَرُوا في نفوسهم أنهم لا يتبعونه حتى يتبع ملتهم، فضحهم الله تعالى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-118-119-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-118-119-s1","r":"q2-118-119","title":"Obstinacy is not a search for certainty","text":"I say: this statement came from some Jews and polytheists through obstinacy and resistance, not a search for certainty. God therefore denies them knowledge altogether. All these verses aim to reproach the Jews. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those without knowledge ask why God does not speak to them, so that they may hear from Him that you are His messenger, or why a manifest sign does not come, visible openly, indicating your messengership as Moses had. The Jews’ obstinate statement had precedents: their forefathers said, “Show us God openly” [4:153]; Christians said, “Can your Lord send down a table from heaven for us?” [5:112]; and polytheists said, “We will not believe you until you make a spring burst from the earth for us, or possess a garden of palms and vines and make rivers flow abundantly through it” [17:90–91]. Their hearts are alike in unbelief and resistance, comparable in insolence and corruption. We have made clear the signs establishing your messengership and election for those seeking increased certainty and disclosure in direct vision. The greatest sign is the Qurʾān; then the ordinances you have clarified and the lawful and forbidden you have explained; then the unseen matters you have reported and the distresses you have lifted from hearts; then the speech of inanimate things and stones, the palm-trunk’s yearning, trees’ obedience, pebbles’ glorification and the stone’s greeting. Water also sprang abundantly from between his fingers, besides countless other signs. We sent you with the truth, clothed in it and making it clear, bringing the abiding bliss as good news to those who affirm and follow you, and warning opponents of the punishment of the Fire. Do not ask about their condition when they reach it: it is too great to recount, too dreadful to hear. Their state cannot be explained, nor can anyone bear to hear its terrors. May God preserve us from ruin and enable us to follow truth and guidance. Alternatively, your Lord will not question you about them: He knows their condition best. [B078] Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-118-119-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-118-119-s2","r":"q2-118-119","title":"Hearing from the Real","text":"Demanding wonders and manifest signs belongs to the disposition of the ignorant and obstinate, not to those seeking guidance and direction. The road is clear for one who seeks the way, and truth evident for one who perceives its indication. Whoever anoints his inner eye with the antimony of the special realization of unity ( التوحيد الخاص ) sees none but the Real and knows none but Him. He sees all things standing through God—indeed, having no existence alongside Him. Whoever has the hearing of his heart opened by God hears only from the Real and only through Him. As someone said, “Through God I speak; from God I hear.” Al-Junayd said: “For forty years I have conversed intimately with the Real, while people suppose I converse with creation.” Creation is effaced for those possessing realized knowledge, but affirmed as separate by the ignorant and divisive. They ask why God does not speak to them or a sign come, although He speaks to them at every time and hour. Those sharing their ignorance of God say the same, despite the clarity of the signs to those who know Him. God speaks the truth and guides to the way.","anchor":"en-q2-118-119-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-118-119-s3","r":"q2-118-119","title":"","text":"When Jews and Christians told the Messenger, “Make a truce between us and yourself, after which we will follow you,” while concealing the intention not to follow him until he followed their religion, God exposed them, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-118-119-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-120","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people 2:120","anchor":"unit-q2-120"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-120-1","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"وَلَنْ تَرْضى عَنْكَ الْيَهُودُ وَلا النَّصارى حَتَّى تَتَّبِعَ مِلَّتَهُمْ قُلْ إِنَّ هُدَى اللَّهِ هُوَ الْهُدى وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ أَهْواءَهُمْ بَعْدَ الَّذِي جاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ ما لَكَ مِنَ اللَّهِ مِنْ وَلِيٍّ وَلا نَصِيرٍ (120)","anchor":"ar-q2-120-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-120-2","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"قلت: الملّة هي الشريعة، وهي ما شرع الله على لسان أنبيائه ورسله، من أمللت الكتاب وأمليته، إذا قرأته.","anchor":"ar-q2-120-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-120-3","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"والهوى: رأى يتبع الشهوة.","anchor":"ar-q2-120-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-120-4","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لرسوله صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: وَلَنْ تَرْضى عَنْكَ الْيَهُودُ وتتبع دينك أبداً، وَلَا النَّصارى كذلك حَتَّى تَتَّبِعَ مِلَّتَهُمْ على فرض المحال، والمقصود قطعُ رجائه من إسلامهم باختيارهم لأن اتباعه ملتهم محال، وكذلك إسلامهم. ولعله في قوم مخصوصين. ثم زاد في التنفير من اتباعهم فقال: وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ أَهْواءَهُمْ الباطلة فرضاً وتقديراً بَعْدَ الَّذِي جاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ بالله وبأحكامه على المنهاج القويم، ما لَكَ مِنَ اللَّهِ مِنْ وَلِيٍّ يمنعك منا، وَلا نَصِيرٍ ينصرك من غيرنا، أي: لا ولي ولا نصير لك إلا نحن حيث واليتنا، وأحببتنا، وأظهرت ملتنا، فنحن لك على ما تحب وترضى.","anchor":"ar-q2-120-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-120-5","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"الإشارة: التماس رضى الناس من علامة الإفلاس، ولن يرضى عنك الناس حتى تتبع أهواءهم، ولئن اتبعت أهواءهم بعد ما تحققت ما هم فيه، إنك إذاً لمن الظالمين، فمن التمس رضى الناس وقع في سخط الله، ومن التمس رضى الله قطع يأسه من الناس. ولذلك قال بعضهم: كل ما سقط من عين الخلق عظم في عين الحق، وكل ما عظم في عين الخلق سقط من عين الحق، وقال آخر: إن الذي تكرهون مني هو الذي يشتهيه قلبي. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-120-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-120-6","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"وقال بعض الصالحين: (لقيتُ بعض الأبدال، فقلت له: دُلَّني على الطريق؟ فقال: لا تخالط الناس فإن مخالطتهم ظلمة، فقلت: لا بد من مخالطتهم وأنا بين أظهرهم؟ فقال لا تعاملهم، فإن معاملتهم خسران. قلت: لا بد من معاملتهم؟ فقال: لا تركن إليهم، فإن في الركون إليهم هلكة، فقلت: هذا لعله يكون؟ فقال: يا هذا، أتخالط البطالين، وتعامل الجاهلين، وتركن إلى الهلكى، وتحب أن يكون قلبك مع الله؟ هيهات.. هذا لا يكون أبدًا، ثم غاب عني ولم أره) .","anchor":"ar-q2-120-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-120-7","r":"q2-120","title":"2:120 · Seeking approval from people","text":"ولما عاتب الله بني إسرائيل ووبخهم استثنى من آمن منهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-120-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-120-s1","r":"q2-120","title":"Religion and desire","text":"I say: milla ( ملّة ) is a revealed Law, what God ordains upon the tongues of His prophets and messengers. It derives from amlaltu al-kitāba or amlaytuhu : I recited the written text. Desire ( الهوى ) is an opinion that follows appetite.","anchor":"en-q2-120-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-120-s2","r":"q2-120","title":"An impossible hypothesis and a particular group","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, tells His Messenger: the Jews will never be pleased with you and follow your religion, nor the Christians, until you follow theirs—on the supposition of an impossibility. The aim is to cut off his hope that they will embrace Islam of their own choice: as his following their religion is impossible, so too is their conversion. Perhaps this concerns a particular group. He further deters following them: were you, hypothetically, to follow their false desires after receiving knowledge of God and His judgements upon the straight method, you would have no protector against Us and no helper from any other. You have no protector or helper but Us, because you have befriended and loved Us and manifested Our religion; We are therefore for you as you love and approve.","anchor":"en-q2-120-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-120-s3","r":"q2-120","title":"Approval as a form of dependence","text":"Seeking people’s approval is a sign of spiritual bankruptcy. People will not be pleased with you until you follow their desires; were you to follow them after recognizing their condition, you would be among the wrongdoers. Whoever seeks people’s approval falls into God’s displeasure; whoever seeks God’s approval cuts off expectation from people. Hence someone said: whatever falls in creation’s estimation rises in the Real’s estimation, and whatever rises in creation’s estimation falls in the Real’s. Another said, “What you dislike in me is what my heart desires.” A righteous man said: “I met one of the substitute saints and asked him to show me the way. He replied, ‘Do not mingle with people: mingling with them is darkness.’ I said, ‘I must mingle with them, since I live among them.’ He said, ‘Do not transact with them: dealing with them is loss.’ I said, ‘I must deal with them.’ He replied, ‘Do not rely upon them: such reliance is ruin.’ I said, ‘Perhaps that is possible.’ He answered, ‘Man, you mingle with the idle, deal with the ignorant, rely on the ruined, and wish your heart to be with God? Far from it: that can never be.’ Then he disappeared from me, and I never saw him again.”","anchor":"en-q2-120-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-120-s4","r":"q2-120","title":"","text":"After reproaching and admonishing the Children of Israel, God excepts those among them who believe, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-120-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-121","r":"q2-121","title":"2:121 · Reading the Book as it should be read","text":"2:121 · Reading the Book as it should be read 2:121","anchor":"unit-q2-121"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-121-1","r":"q2-121","title":"2:121 · Reading the Book as it should be read","text":"الَّذِينَ آتَيْناهُمُ الْكِتابَ يَتْلُونَهُ حَقَّ تِلاوَتِهِ أُولئِكَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِهِ وَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِهِ فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْخاسِرُونَ (121)","anchor":"ar-q2-121-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-121-2","r":"q2-121","title":"2:121 · Reading the Book as it should be read","text":"قلت: جملة (يتلونه) حال، و (أولئك) خبر الموصول.","anchor":"ar-q2-121-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-121-3","r":"q2-121","title":"2:121 · Reading the Book as it should be read","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الَّذِينَ آتَيْناهُمُ الْكِتابَ، كعبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه، حالتهم يَتْلُونَهُ حَقَّ تِلاوَتِهِ غير محرّفين له، ولا كاتمين ما فيه، أُولئِكَ هم الذين يُؤْمِنُونَ بِهِ حقيقة، وأما غيرهم ممن حرف وكتم صفة الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم فقد كفر به، وَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِهِ فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْخاسِرُونَ أي: الكاملون في الخسران، حيث بخسوا أنفسهم من عَزِّ الدارين.","anchor":"ar-q2-121-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-121-4","r":"q2-121","title":"2:121 · Reading the Book as it should be read","text":"الإشارة: ما قيل في التوراة وأصحابه يقال مثله في القرآن وأهله فمن آتاه الله القرآن، وتلاه حق تلاوته، بحيث جَوَّدَ حروفه وتَدبَّر معانيه، وعمل بما فيه، فأولئك هم المؤمنون به حقا، والفائزون بثمار معانيه حلاوة وذوقاً، ومن ترك التدبر في معانيه فقد حرم نفسه ثمار حلاوته، وذلك عين الخسران عند أهل الإيقان. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-121-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-121-5","r":"q2-121","title":"2:121 · Reading the Book as it should be read","text":"ثم رجع الحقّ تعالى إلى تذكيرهم بالنعم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-121-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-121-s1","r":"q2-121","title":"A circumstantial clause and the delayed predicate","text":"I say: “they recite it” is a circumstantial clause, and “those…” is the predicate of the relative expression.","anchor":"en-q2-121-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-121-s2","r":"q2-121","title":"Recitation without concealment","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those to whom We gave the Book, such as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his companions, recite it properly, neither distorting it nor concealing its contents. They truly believe it. Those who alter and conceal the Messenger’s description have disbelieved it; whoever disbelieves it is utterly a loser, having deprived himself of honour in both abodes.","anchor":"en-q2-121-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-121-s3","r":"q2-121","title":"The fruits of attentive recitation","text":"What is said of the Torah and its people applies correspondingly to the Qurʾān and its people. Those to whom God gives the Qurʾān, who recite it properly—perfecting its letters, contemplating its meanings and acting upon it—truly believe it and win the fruits of its meanings in sweetness and taste. Whoever abandons contemplation of its meanings deprives himself of the fruits of its sweetness. For the people of certainty, that is loss itself. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-121-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-121-s4","r":"q2-121","title":"","text":"The Real returns to reminding them of His blessings, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-121-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-122-123","r":"q2-122-123","title":"2:122–123 · Gratitude for favour and fear of the final day","text":"2:122–123 · Gratitude for favour and fear of the final day 2:122–123","anchor":"unit-q2-122-123"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-122-123-1","r":"q2-122-123","title":"2:122–123 · Gratitude for favour and fear of the final day","text":"يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَنِّي فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى الْعالَمِينَ (122) وَاتَّقُوا يَوْماً لا تَجْزِي نَفْسٌ عَنْ نَفْسٍ شَيْئاً وَلا يُقْبَلُ مِنْها عَدْلٌ وَلا تَنْفَعُها شَفاعَةٌ وَلا هُمْ يُنْصَرُونَ (123)","anchor":"ar-q2-122-123-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-122-123-2","r":"q2-122-123","title":"2:122–123 · Gratitude for favour and fear of the final day","text":"قلت: جملة (لا تجزي) : نعت ليوم، وحذف العائد، أي: لا تجزي فيه نفس، قال المرادي: (إذا نعت بالجملة اسم زمان جاز حذف عائده) ثم استدل بالآية. وهل حذف برمته أو بالتدريج؟ قولان.","anchor":"ar-q2-122-123-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-122-123-3","r":"q2-122-123","title":"2:122–123 · Gratitude for favour and fear of the final day","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ بأن جعلت الأنبياء تسوسكم، والملوك منكم يدبرون أموركم، وفَضَّلْتُكُمْ على عالم زمانكم، فاشكروا هذه النعم بالإيمان بالرسول الذي أرسلته إليكم، وخافوا أهوال يوم القيامة، الذي لا تغنى فيه نَفْسٌ عَنْ نَفْسٍ شَيْئاً وَلا يُقْبَلُ مِنْها فداء إن أرادت الفداء، وَلا تَنْفَعُها شَفاعَةٌ","anchor":"ar-q2-122-123-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-122-123-4","r":"q2-122-123","title":"2:122–123 · Gratitude for favour and fear of the final day","text":"شافع، ولا يدفع عنها أهوال ذلك اليوم ولي ولا ناصر، إلا من اتخذ يداً عند الملك القادر، وبالله التوفيق. وتقدمت إشارة هذه الآية في الآية الأولى.","anchor":"ar-q2-122-123-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-122-123-5","r":"q2-122-123","title":"2:122–123 · Gratitude for favour and fear of the final day","text":"وَلَمَّا أراد الحقُّ تعالى أن ينسخ القبلة ويردها إلى بيت الله الحرام بعد أن كانت إلى بيت المقدس، ذكر خصوصيةَ مَنْ بناه، وكيفية بنائه، وفي ضمن ذلك ذكر شرفه ليكون ذلك داعياً إلى الامتثال، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-122-123-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-122-123-s1","r":"q2-122-123","title":"Omitting the resumptive pronoun","text":"I say: “no soul can avail…” qualifies “a day.” Its resumptive expression is omitted: “a day in which no soul can avail…”. Al-Murādī says that when a temporal noun is qualified by a sentence, its resumptive may be omitted, citing this verse. Was the whole expression omitted at once or in stages? There are two views.","anchor":"en-q2-122-123-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-122-123-s2","r":"q2-122-123","title":"The favour of prophets and kings","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember My blessing: I appointed prophets to guide you and kings from among you to manage your affairs, and favoured you above the people of your time. Thank Me by believing the messenger I sent to you. Fear the terrors of the Day of Resurrection, when no soul can avail another, no ransom is accepted should it offer one, and no intercessor benefits it. No protector or helper repels that day’s terrors, except for one who has established a claim of favour with the Powerful King. Through God is success. The spiritual allusion of this verse has already appeared at its first occurrence [2:47–48].","anchor":"en-q2-122-123-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-122-123-s3","r":"q2-122-123","title":"","text":"When the Real wished to change the prayer-direction from Jerusalem back to God’s Sacred House, He mentioned the special distinction of its builder and the manner of its building. Within this He set forth its honour, encouraging compliance, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-122-123-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-124","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership 2:124","anchor":"unit-q2-124"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-1","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"وَإِذِ ابْتَلى إِبْراهِيمَ رَبُّهُ بِكَلِماتٍ فَأَتَمَّهُنَّ قالَ إِنِّي جاعِلُكَ لِلنَّاسِ إِماماً قالَ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِي قالَ لا يَنالُ عَهْدِي الظَّالِمِينَ (124)","anchor":"ar-q2-124-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-2","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"قلت: (ابتلى) اختبر، و (إبراهيم) مفعول، وفيه أربع لغات: إبراهام وإبراهوم وإبراهيم وبالقصر، و (ربه) فاعل، وقدم المفعول للاهتمام، ولئلا يعود الضمير على ما بعده لفظاً ورتبة، و (عهدي) فاعل، و (الظالمين) مفعول.","anchor":"ar-q2-124-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-3","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر يا محمد، أو اذكروا يا بني إسرائيل، حين اختبر إِبْراهِيمَ رَبُّهُ بِكَلِماتٍ أن يعمل بها، وهي: تسليم بدنه للنيران، وولده للقربان، وطعامه للضَّيفان، أو عشر خصال: خمس في الرأس:","anchor":"ar-q2-124-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-4","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"المضمضة، والاستنشاق، وقصّ الشارب، والسواك، وفرق الرأس. وقيل: وإعفاء اللحية، وخمس في الجسد: تقليم الظفر، وحلق العانة، ونتف الإبط، والاستنجاء بالماء، والاختتان. أو مناسك الحج أو الخصال التي امتحن بها وهي:","anchor":"ar-q2-124-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-5","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"الكوكب، والقمر، والشمس، والنار. والهجرة، والذبح، والأحسن أنها ثلاث: الهجرة من وطنه، ورمي ولده بمكة، وذبح الآخر حين بلغ أن يسعى معه . فَأَتَمَّهُنَّ أي: وَفَّى بهن، فلما وَفَّى بهن (قال) الله تعالى له: إِنِّي جاعِلُكَ لِلنَّاسِ إِماماً، أي: قدوة بك في التوحيد، أو في الأصول والفروع، إذ لم يبعث بعده نبي إلا كان من ذريته، ومأمور باتباعه.","anchor":"ar-q2-124-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-6","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"ولمّا جعله الله إماماً طلب ذلك لأولاده فقال: وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِي فاجعل أئمة، قالَ الحق تعالى: لا يَنالُ عَهْدِي أي: لا يلحق عهدي بالإمامة الظَّالِمِينَ منهم، إذ لا يصلح للإمامة إلا البررة الأتقياء، لأنها أمانة من الله وعهد، والظالم لا يصلح لها، وفيه تنبيه على أنه قد يكون من ذريته ظلمة لا يستحقون الإمامة، وفيه دليل على عصمة الأنبياء قبل البعثة، وأن الفاسق لا يصلح للإمامة. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-124-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-7","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"الإشارة: إذا أراد الله تعالى أن يجعل وليّاً من أوليائه إماماً يُقتدى به، وداعياً يدعو إليه، ابتلاه، فإن صبر ورضي اصطفاه، ولحضرته اجتباه، فيكون إماماً يُقتدى به، وداعياً يُهتدى به، وهذه سُنَّة الله تعالى في أصفيائه","anchor":"ar-q2-124-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-8","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"يبتليهم الله تعالى بتسليط الخلق عليهم وأنواع من البلايا، فإذا نقوا من البقايا، وتكلمت فيهم المزايا، أظهرهم للخلق داعين إلى الله ومرشدين إلى طريق الله، وقد تبقى الإمامة فى ذريتهم إن ساروا على هديهم، ومَن لم يسلك به هذا المسلك فلا يصلح للإمامة، وإن توجه إليها كان ناقصّا في الدعوة، ولذلك قال بعضهم: (من ادّعى شهود الجمال قبل تأدُّبه بالجلال، فارفضه فإنه دجال) . هـ. وكل من اتصف بشئ من ظلم العباد لا ينال عهد الإمامة في طريق الإرشاد، وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-124-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-124-9","r":"q2-124","title":"2:124 · Abraham’s testing and the trust of leadership","text":"ثم ذكر شرف البيت الذي هو المقصود، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-124-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-124-s1","r":"q2-124","title":"The test, the agent and the object","text":"I say: to ibtalā ( ابتلى ) is to test. “Abraham” is the object; his name has four forms: Ibrāhām, Ibrāhūm, Ibrāhīm and a shortened form. “His Lord” is the agent. The object precedes for emphasis and to avoid a pronoun referring to something following it both in wording and grammatical rank. “My covenant” is the agent of “reaches,” and “the wrongdoers” its object.","anchor":"en-q2-124-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-124-s2","r":"q2-124","title":"The commands Abraham fulfilled","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember, Muḥammad—or remember, Children of Israel—when Abraham’s Lord tested him with words to carry out. These were surrendering his body to the fires, his son to sacrifice, and his food to guests. Alternatively, they were ten practices: five concerning the head—rinsing the mouth, drawing water into the nose, trimming the moustache, using the tooth-stick and parting the hair, or, in another account, letting the beard grow—and five concerning the body: clipping the nails, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpits, cleansing with water after relieving oneself, and circumcision. Or they were the rites of pilgrimage; or the trials of the star, moon, sun, fire, migration and sacrifice. The preferable explanation is three trials: migration from his homeland, leaving his son in Mecca, and sacrificing the other when he reached the age to work alongside him. [B079] He fulfilled them all. God then said: I am making you a leader whom people follow in affirming unity, or in both principles and particular ordinances. Every prophet subsequently sent was of his descendants and commanded to follow him. When God made him a leader, he asked the same for his children: make leaders from my descendants too. The Real said: My covenant of leadership does not reach the wrongdoers among them. Only the righteous and mindful are suited to leadership, for it is a trust and covenant from God. A wrongdoer is not fit for it. The verse indicates that some descendants would be wrongdoers undeserving of leadership. Al-Bayḍāwī says it also proves the prophets’ protection before their mission and the unfitness of a transgressor for leadership.","anchor":"en-q2-124-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-124-s3","r":"q2-124","title":"Formation through majesty before leadership","text":"When God wishes to make one of His friends a leader to follow and a summoner to Himself, He tests him. If he is patient and content, He chooses and draws him to His presence, making him an exemplar and guide. This is God’s customary way with His chosen: He tests them by allowing creatures power over them and through various afflictions. When the remnants of self are purified and their excellences speak, He brings them before creation as callers to God and guides upon His way. Leadership may remain in their descendants if they follow their guidance. Someone not taken through this course is not fit for leadership; should he assume it, his calling is deficient. Hence the saying: “Whoever claims to witness Beauty before being disciplined by Majesty—reject him, for he is an impostor.” Whoever wrongs God’s servants in any way does not obtain the covenant of leadership in spiritual direction. Through God is success; He guides to the level way.","anchor":"en-q2-124-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-124-s4","r":"q2-124","title":"","text":"He then mentions the honour of the House, the principal subject here, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-124-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-125","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart 2:125","anchor":"unit-q2-125"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-1","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"وَإِذْ جَعَلْنَا الْبَيْتَ مَثابَةً لِلنَّاسِ وَأَمْناً وَاتَّخِذُوا مِنْ مَقامِ إِبْراهِيمَ مُصَلًّى وَعَهِدْنا إِلى إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ أَنْ طَهِّرا بَيْتِيَ لِلطَّائِفِينَ وَالْعاكِفِينَ وَالرُّكَّعِ السُّجُودِ (125)","anchor":"ar-q2-125-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-2","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"قلت: (المثابة) : المرجع الذي يثُوب الناس إليه كل سنة، و (اتخذوا) : على قراءة الأمر، محكي بقول محذوف، أي: وقلنا اتخذوا، وعلى قراءة الماضي: معطوف على (جعلنا) ، أي: جعلناه مثابة، واتخذه الناس مُصلَّى.","anchor":"ar-q2-125-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-3","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: (و) اذكر يا محمد إِذْ جَعَلْنَا الْبَيْتَ الحرام، أي: الكعبة، مرجعاً للناس يرجعون لزيارته والطواف به كل سنة، وجعلناه محل أمن، كل من دخله كان آمناً من عقوبة الدنيا والآخرة، إما في الدنيا فإنَّ الناس يُتَخطفون من حوله، وأهلُه آمنون، وأما فى الآخرة فلأن الحج يَجُبُّ ما قبله، وهذا يدل على شرف البيت وحرمته.","anchor":"ar-q2-125-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-4","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"وقلنا لهم: اتَّخِذُوا مِنْ مَقامِ إِبْراهِيمَ، وهو الحجر الذي فيه أثر قدميه، مُصَلًّى تصلون إليه، وهو الذي يصلون خلفه ركعتي الطواف، وَعَهِدْنا أي: أوحينا إِلى إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ ولده، بأن قلنا لهما:","anchor":"ar-q2-125-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-5","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"طَهِّرا بَيْتِيَ من الأدناس والأرجاس والأصنام والأوثان، لِلطَّائِفِينَ به وَالْعاكِفِينَ أي: المقيمين فيه، والمصلين فيه الراكعين الساجدين. فكان البيت مطهراً في زمانهما وبعدهما زماناً، ثم أدخلت فيه [الأصنام] فطهّره نبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم، وتبقى طهارته حتى يأتي أمر الله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-125-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-6","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"الإشارة: القلب هو بيت الرب، يقول الله تبارك وتعالى لبعض أنبيائه: «طهر لي بيتًا أسكنه، فقال: يا رب أي بيت يسعك؟ فقال له: لن تسعني أرضي ولا سمائي، ووسعني قلب عبدي المؤمن» . فإذا تطهر القلب من الأغيار","anchor":"ar-q2-125-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-7","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"وملئ بالأنوار، وتمكنت فيه المعارف والأسرار، كان مرجعاً وملجأ للعباد، كل مَن وصل إليه، وطاف به، كان آمنا من الزيغ والعناد، ومن خواطر السوء وسوء الاعتقاد، ومن دخله بالمحبة والوداد، أَمِن من الطرْد والبعاد، وكان عند الله من أفضل العباد. ومقام إبراهيم- عليه السلام- هو الاستغراق في عين بحر الشهود، ورفع الهمة عن ما سوى الملك المعبود.","anchor":"ar-q2-125-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-8","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"وهذا المقام هو الذي اتخذه العارفون كعبة لصلاة قلوبهم، وغاية لمنتهى قصودهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-125-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-9","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"عِبارَاتُهُم شَتَّى، وحُسْنُكَ واحِدٌ، ... وكُلٌّ إلى ذاك الجَمالِ يُشِيرُ","anchor":"ar-q2-125-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-10","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"وقد عهد الله تعالى إلى أنبيائه وأصفيائه أن يطهروا قلوبهم من الأغيار، ويرفضوا كل ما سواه من الأكدار، لتتهيأ بذلك لطواف الواردات والأنوار، ولعكوف المعارف والأسرار، وتخضع لهيبتها ظواهرُ الأشباح، وتنقاد لجمال بهجتها القلوبُ والأرواح، وما ذلك على الله بعزيز.","anchor":"ar-q2-125-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-125-11","r":"q2-125","title":"2:125 · The House as return, security and purified heart","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى دعاء إبراهيم الخليل لمكان البيت، زيادة فى تشريفه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-125-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-125-s1","r":"q2-125","title":"A place to which people return","text":"I say: mathāba ( مثابة ) is a place of return to which people come back every year. On the imperative reading, “take” is reported after an omitted “We said.” On the past-tense reading it is conjoined to “We made”: We made it a place of return, and people took it as a place of prayer.","anchor":"en-q2-125-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-125-s2","r":"q2-125","title":"Purification of the Sacred House","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember, Muḥammad, when We made the Sacred House—the Kaʿba—a place to which people return yearly for visitation and circumambulation. We made it a place of security: whoever enters is safe from punishment in this world and the next. Here, people are snatched away around it while its inhabitants are secure; hereafter, pilgrimage erases what preceded it. This indicates the House’s honour and sanctity. We told them to take Abraham’s station—the stone bearing his footprints—as a place towards which to pray, behind which they perform the two units after circumambulation. We covenanted with Abraham and his son Ishmael, revealing to them: purify My House of dirt, defilement, idols and images for those who circle it, reside in it and pray there, bowing and prostrating. It was purified in their time and for a period afterwards. Then idols were brought in, until our Prophet Muḥammad purified it. Its purity remains until God’s command comes. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-125-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-125-s3","r":"q2-125","title":"The heart as the Lord’s House","text":"The heart is the Lord’s House. God Most High says to one of His prophets: “Purify a house for Me to dwell in.” He asks, “Lord, what house can contain You?” God replies, “Neither My earth nor My heaven contains Me, but the heart of My believing servant contains Me.” [B080] When the heart is purified of others, filled with lights and firmly established in knowledge and mysteries, it becomes a refuge and place of return for servants. Whoever reaches and circles it is safe from deviation and resistance, evil suggestions and wrong belief. Whoever enters it through love and affection is safe from rejection and distance, and is among the best servants with God. Abraham’s station is absorption in the very sea of witnessing and the lifting of aspiration above everything but the worshipped King. The gnostics take this station as the Kaʿba for their hearts’ prayer and the final goal of their purposes: Their expressions differ, but Your beauty is one; each points towards that Beauty. God covenants with His prophets and chosen ones to purify their hearts of others and discard every impurity of other-than-Him, preparing them for the circling of inspirations and lights, the abiding of knowledge and mysteries. Outward bodies bow before their awe; hearts and spirits submit to their radiant beauty. That is not difficult for God.","anchor":"en-q2-125-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-125-s4","r":"q2-125","title":"","text":"The Real recounts Abraham the Intimate’s prayer for the place of the House, further honouring it:","anchor":"en-q2-125-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-126","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers 2:126","anchor":"unit-q2-126"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-126-1","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"وَإِذْ قالَ إِبْراهِيمُ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ هذا بَلَداً آمِناً وَارْزُقْ أَهْلَهُ مِنَ الثَّمَراتِ مَنْ آمَنَ مِنْهُمْ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ قالَ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَأُمَتِّعُهُ قَلِيلاً ثُمَّ أَضْطَرُّهُ إِلى عَذابِ النَّارِ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيرُ (126)","anchor":"ar-q2-126-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-126-2","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"قلت: الإشارة تعود إلى المكان، أو البلد، أي: اجعل هذا المكان بلداً ذا أمن، قال بعضهم: نكَّرَ البلد هنا، وعرَّفه في سورة إبراهيم، لان هذا الدعاء وقع قبل أن يكون بلداً، وفي سورة إبراهيم وقع بعد أن كان بلداً فلذلك عرَّفه، وفيه نظر من جهة التاريخ، وسيأتي تمامه هناك إن شاء الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-126-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-126-3","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"وقوله: (مَن آمَن) : بدل من (أهله) ، بدل البعض للتخصيص، و (مَن كفر) : معطوف على (مَن آمَن) ، على حذف المضارع، أي: وارزق من كفر.","anchor":"ar-q2-126-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-126-4","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاذكر إِذْ قالَ إِبْراهِيمُ في دعائه لمكة لما أنزَل ابنَه بها بوادٍ غير ذي زرع، وتركه في يد الله تعالى: رَبِّ اجْعَلْ هذا المكان بَلَداً آمِناً يأمن فيه كل من يأوي إليه، وَارْزُقْ أَهْلَهُ مِنَ أنواع الثَّمَراتِ، كالحبوب وسائر الفواكه، مَنْ آمَنَ مِنْهُمْ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ قالَ الحق جلّ جلاله: بل وأرزق أيضاً مَنْ كَفَرَ في الدنيا، فَأُمَتِّعُهُ زمناً قَلِيلًا، أو تمتيعاً قليلاً. ثُمَّ ألجئه إِلى عَذابِ النَّارِ وبئس المرجع مصيره.","anchor":"ar-q2-126-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-126-5","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"قاس إبراهيم الخليل الرزق على الإمامة، فنبَّه سبحانه وتعالى أن الرزق رحمة دنيوية، تعم المؤمن والكافر، بخلاف الإمامة، والتقدم في الدين، فإنها سبب النعيم الأخروي، ولا ينالها إلا أهلُ الإيمان والصلاح.","anchor":"ar-q2-126-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-126-6","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"الإشارة: دعاء الأنبياء عليهم السلام، كما يصدقُ بالحس يصدق بالمعنى، فيشمل دعاء الخليل القلوبَ التي هي بلد الإيمان، والأرواح التي هي معدن الأسرار والإحسان، فتكون آمنة من طوارق الشيطان، ومحفوظة من الوقوف مع رؤية الأكوان، آمنة من الأكدار، محفوظة من رؤية الأغيار، فيرزقها الله من ثمرة العلوم، ويفتح لها من مخازن الفهوم، من آمن منهم بالشريعة الظاهرة، وجاهد نفسه في عمل الطريقة الباطنة، حتى أشرقت عليه أنوار الحقيقة العيانية، وأما من كفر بطريق الخصوص، ووقف مع ظواهر النصوص، فإنما يُمَتَّع بعلم الرسوم الذي حدُّ حلاوته اللسان، ثم يلجأ إلى عذاب الحجاب، وسوء الحساب، ولم يُفْضِ إلى حلاوة الشهود والعيان، التي يمتع بها الجَنَانُ حتى يُفْضي إلى نعيم الجنَان، فيتم النعيم بالنظر إلى وجهه الكريم، منحنا الله من ذلك حظا وافرا بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-126-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-126-7","r":"q2-126","title":"2:126 · Provision for believers and unbelievers","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى كيفية بناء البيت، وما كان شعارهما فى حالة بنائه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-126-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-126-s1","r":"q2-126","title":"The town and the particularization of its people","text":"I say: the demonstrative refers to the place or town: make this place a town possessing security. Someone explains that “town” is indefinite here but definite in Sūrat Ibrāhīm [14:35], because this prayer preceded its becoming a town, whereas that prayer followed it. This raises a chronological difficulty; its fuller discussion will come there, God willing. “Those who believe” is an apposition of the part to “its people,” particularizing them. “Whoever disbelieves” is conjoined to “those who believe,” with an omitted imperfect: “and I shall provide for whoever disbelieves.”","anchor":"en-q2-126-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-126-s2","r":"q2-126","title":"Provision differs from religious leadership","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember Abraham’s prayer for Mecca after settling his son there in an uncultivated valley and leaving him in God’s care. “My Lord, make this place a secure town, where whoever takes shelter is safe. Provide its inhabitants with fruits of every kind, grain and all other produce—those believing in God and the Last Day.” The Real says: I also provide for the unbeliever in this world, granting him a brief time or scant measure of enjoyment, then compelling him to the Fire. What an evil place to return! Abraham the Intimate compared provision with leadership. God teaches that provision is a worldly mercy encompassing believer and unbeliever, unlike leadership and precedence in religion, which occasion heavenly bliss and are attained only by people of faith and righteousness.","anchor":"en-q2-126-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-126-s3","r":"q2-126","title":"The fruits of the sciences","text":"The prophets’ prayers apply to inward meanings as to sensible realities. Abraham’s prayer thus includes hearts, the towns of faith, and spirits, the mines of mysteries and excellence. They become safe from Satan’s assaults and protected from stopping at the sight of created things; secure from impurities, protected from seeing others. God gives them the fruits of the sciences and opens the treasuries of understanding: those who believe the outward Law and struggle in the inward practice of the Path until the lights of directly witnessed Reality shine upon them. But someone who denies the special path and stops at the outward texts enjoys only formal learning ( علم الرسوم ), whose sweetness extends no further than the tongue. He is then driven to the punishment of veiling and an evil reckoning. He has not reached the sweetness of witnessing and direct vision that delights the heart ( الجَنان ) until it reaches the bliss of the gardens ( الجِنان ), perfected by looking upon His noble Face. May God grant us an abundant share through His favour and generosity.","anchor":"en-q2-126-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-126-s4","r":"q2-126","title":"","text":"The Real describes the House’s construction and what its builders uttered while building:","anchor":"en-q2-126-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-127","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence 2:127","anchor":"unit-q2-127"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-127-1","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"وَإِذْ يَرْفَعُ إِبْراهِيمُ الْقَواعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ وَإِسْماعِيلُ رَبَّنا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ (127)","anchor":"ar-q2-127-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-127-2","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"قلت: (القواعد) جمع قاعدة، وهي الأساس، وكأنه مأخوذ من القعود بمعنى الثبات، وأما القواعد من النساء، فجمع قاعد، بلا تاء، لأنه وصف خاص بالنساء، فلا يحتاج إلى تمييز التاء، و (ربنا) منصوب على النداء محكي بحال محذوفة، أي: حال كونهم قائلين ربنا ... الخ.","anchor":"ar-q2-127-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-127-3","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر وقت رفع إِبْراهِيمُ الْقَواعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ وَإِسْماعِيلُ، وبنائهما له، بعد أن درس بالطوفان، وكان بناء آدم عليه السلام لما أُهبط إلى الأرض بإعلام الملائكة. كان إبراهيم عليه السلام يبني، وإسماعيلُ يُناوله الحجارة، فنسب البناء لهما لتعاونهما، وقيل: كانا يبنيان كُلٍّ في ناحية، حال كونهما قَائِلَيْنِ:","anchor":"ar-q2-127-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-127-4","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"رَبَّنا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا عملنا هذا، إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ السَّمِيعُ لدعائنا، الْعَلِيمُ بنياتنا وسرائرنا.","anchor":"ar-q2-127-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-127-5","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"الإشارة: ينبغي للعبد أن يرفع قواعد إسلامه، ويشيد دعائمه بتحقيق أركانه، كإتقان الشهادتين بتحقيق معانيها، وإتقان الصلاة بإتقان أركانها الظاهرة والباطنة، وإتقان الزكاة بإخلاص أدائها، وإتقان الصيام بتحصيل آدابه، وإتقان الحج بتحصيل مناسكه بعد وجوبه، ويرفع أيضاً قواعد إيمانه بتحقيق أركانه، وهي: الإيمان بالله وملائكته وكتبه ورسله واليوم الآخر، وبالقدر خيره وشره، حُلْوِه ومُره، اعتقاداً وذوقاً، ويرفع أيضاً قواعد إحسانه،","anchor":"ar-q2-127-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-127-6","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"بتحصيل مراتبه، كتحقيق المشاهدة، وهو أن يعبد الله كأنه يراه، فإن لم يستطع فليعبده كأن الله يراه، وإن شئت قلت: رفعُ قواعد الإسلام يكون بتحقيق التوبة والتقوى والاستقامة، ورفع قواعد الإيمان يكون بتحقيق الإخلاص والصدق والطمأنينة، ورفع قواعد الإحسان يكون بالمراقبة والمشاهدة والمعرفة، كما قال الساحلى- رحمه الله-.","anchor":"ar-q2-127-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-127-7","r":"q2-127","title":"2:127 · Raising the foundations of surrender, faith and excellence","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى دعاءهم بعد البناء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-127-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-127-s1","r":"q2-127","title":"Foundations and the omitted circumstantial expression","text":"I say: qawāʿid ( قواعد ) is the plural of qāʿida , a foundation, apparently derived from sitting in the sense of stability. By contrast, qawāʿid said of women [24:60] is the plural of qāʿid without a feminine ending: the description is particular to women and needs no tāʾ to distinguish the gender. “Our Lord” is accusative as a vocative, reported after an omitted circumstantial phrase: “while saying, ‘Our Lord…’”.","anchor":"en-q2-127-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-127-s2","r":"q2-127","title":"Building and praying for acceptance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when Abraham and Ishmael raised the House’s foundations, rebuilding it after the Flood had effaced it. Adam had built it when sent down to earth, instructed by the angels. Abraham built while Ishmael handed him stones; their cooperation permits attributing the construction to both. Alternatively, each built a different side. They said: our Lord, accept this deed from us; You hear our prayer and know our intentions and inward secrets.","anchor":"en-q2-127-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-127-s3","r":"q2-127","title":"The three sets of foundations","text":"The servant should raise the foundations of his surrender and strengthen its supports by realizing its pillars: perfect the two testimonies by realizing their meanings; perfect prayer through its outward and inward pillars; perfect almsgiving through sincere payment; fasting through its courtesies; and pilgrimage, when obligatory, through its rites. He should also raise faith’s foundations by realizing its pillars: belief in God, His angels, Books, messengers, the Last Day and the decree, good and evil, sweet and bitter—in conviction and in taste. He should likewise raise the foundations of spiritual excellence, attaining its degrees: realize witnessing, worshipping God as though seeing Him; if unable, worship as though God sees him. [B081] Or say: surrender’s foundations are raised through repentance, mindfulness and uprightness; faith’s through sincerity, truthfulness and tranquillity; excellence’s through watchfulness, witnessing and gnosis. Thus al-Sāḥilī, God have mercy on him.","anchor":"en-q2-127-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-127-s4","r":"q2-127","title":"","text":"The Real recounts their prayer after the building:","anchor":"en-q2-127-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-128-129","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger 2:128–129","anchor":"unit-q2-128-129"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-1","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"رَبَّنا وَاجْعَلْنا مُسْلِمَيْنِ لَكَ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِنا أُمَّةً مُسْلِمَةً لَكَ وَأَرِنا مَناسِكَنا وَتُبْ عَلَيْنا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ (128) رَبَّنا وَابْعَثْ فِيهِمْ رَسُولاً مِنْهُمْ يَتْلُوا عَلَيْهِمْ آياتِكَ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ (129)","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-2","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"قلت: قال ابن عباس رضي الله عنه: لما فرغ إبراهيم وإسماعيل من بناء البيت، دَعَوَا بهذا الدعاء، فقالا: (ربنا واجعلنا مسلمين لك) أي: منقادين لأوامرك الظاهرة ولأحكامك القهرية.","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-3","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"واجعل مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِنا أُمَّةً أي: جماعة مُسْلِمَةً لَكَ. عَلِمَا- بوحي أو إلهام- أنه يكون من ذريتهما من يكفر بالله، وَأَرِنا أي: عرفنا وعلمنا مَناسِكَنا في الحج. والنُّسُك في الأصل: غاية العبادة، وشاع في الحج لما فيه من المشاق والكلفة، والبعد عن العادة. وَتُبْ عَلَيْنا مما لا يليق بحالنا، فحسنات الأبرار سيئات المقربين، فلكل مقام ما ينقصه وإن كان كاملاً. ولهذا كان عليه الصلاة والسلام يستغفر في المجلس سبعين مرة. إذ ما من مقام إلا وقبله ما فيه نقص، فإذا ترقى عنه استغفر منه، إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ أي: كثير القبول والإقبال على التائبين.","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-4","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"رَبَّنا وَابْعَثْ فِيهِمْ أي: في الذرية رَسُولًا مِنْهُمْ وهو مولانا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-:","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-5","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"«أنا دعوة أبي إبراهيم، وبشارة عيسى» ، حال كونه يَتْلُوا عَلَيْهِمْ أي: يبلغهم آياتِكَ الدالة على توحيدك وصدق رسالتك، وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتابَ أي: القرآن وَالْحِكْمَةَ أي: الشريعة أو السنة. وقال مالك: هي الفقه في الدين والفهم فيه، أو نور يضعه في قلب من شاء من عباده، وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ أي: يطهرهم من لوث المعاصي وكدر الحس، إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَزِيزُ الغالب في حكمه وسلطانه، الْحَكِيمُ في صنعه وإتقانه، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-6","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"الإشارة: تضمن دعاؤهما عليهما السلام ثلاثة أمور يُطلب التماسها والتحقق بها من كل أحد أولها:","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-7","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"الانقياد لله في الظاهر والباطن، بامتثال أمره والاستسلام لقهره، حتى يسري ذلك من الأصل إلى فرعه، وهي غاية المِنَّة، قال في الحكم: «متى جعلك في الظاهر ممتثلاً لأمره، وفي الباطن مستسلماً لقهره، فقد أعظم منته","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-8","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"عليك» . والثاني: معرفة الطريق، والسلوك على جادتها، كارتكاب مشاق الطاعات، ومعانقة مخالفة الهوى والشهوات، ورؤية التقصير في ذلك، وطلب التوبة مما هنالك، وهذه هي مناسك حج القلوب، والطريق الموصل إلى عَرَفَةِ حَضْرَةِ الغيوب، والثالث: الظفر بالداعي إلى الله والدال عليه، وهو المعلم الأكبر، صحبته تطهر من العيوب، ورؤيته تغني القلوب، وتدخلها إلى حضرة الغيوب، ظاهره قائم بوظائف الحكمة، وباطنه مشاهد لتصاريف القدرة، وهذا هو القائم بالتربية النبوية. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-128-129-9","r":"q2-128-129","title":"2:128–129 · The prayer for surrender, rites and a purifying messenger","text":"ولما قرر شرف إبراهيم عليه السّلام وجعله إماما يقتدى به، حذر من ترك دينه والرغبة عن ملته، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-128-129-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-128-129-s1","r":"q2-128-129","title":"Surrender and repentance appropriate to one’s station","text":"I say: Ibn ʿAbbās relates that when Abraham and Ishmael finished building the House, they prayed: our Lord, make us surrendered to Your outward commands and Your overpowering decrees. Make from our descendants a community surrendered to You. Through revelation or inspiration they knew that some descendants would disbelieve. Show us—that is, acquaint us with and teach us—our pilgrimage rites. Nusuk ( نسك ) originally means the utmost in worship; it became common for pilgrimage because of its hardships, burdens and distance from ordinary habits. Turn towards us in mercy for what is unfitting to our state. The good deeds of the righteous are the shortcomings of those brought near: every station has something that diminishes it, however complete. Hence he, peace and blessings be upon him, asked forgiveness seventy times in a gathering. No station lacks a preceding one containing deficiency; upon rising from it, he sought forgiveness for it. You are the Ever-Returning, the Merciful, abundant in acceptance and turning towards the repentant. Our Lord, raise among the descendants a messenger of their own—our master Muḥammad, who said: “I am the prayer of my father Abraham and the good tidings of Jesus.” He will recite and convey Your signs of unity and the truth of Your messengership, teaching them the Book—the Qurʾān—and wisdom: the Sacred Law or Sunna. Mālik says wisdom is understanding and discernment in religion, or a light God places in the heart of whichever servant He wills. He purifies them of the stain of disobedience and the turbidity of sensible fixation. You are Mighty, prevailing in judgement and dominion, Wise in fashioning and perfecting. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-128-129-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-128-129-s2","r":"q2-128-129","title":"Three things to seek and realize","text":"Their prayer contains three things everyone should seek and realize. First is outward and inward surrender to God: obeying His command and yielding to His irresistible decree, until it passes from the root to its branches. This is the utmost favour. In the Ḥikam : “When He makes you outwardly obedient to His command and inwardly surrendered to His overpowering decree, He has bestowed an immense favour upon you.” Second is knowing the way and travelling its clear course: undertaking the hardships of obedience, embracing opposition to desire and appetite, seeing one’s shortcomings and seeking repentance for them. These are the rites of the hearts’ pilgrimage, the road to the ʿArafa of the unseen presence. Third is finding one who summons to God and points to Him: the great teacher, whose companionship purifies faults, whose sight enriches hearts and brings them into the unseen presence. Outwardly he fulfils the duties of wisdom; inwardly he witnesses the dispositions of power. He is the one undertaking Prophetic formation. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-128-129-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-128-129-s3","r":"q2-128-129","title":"","text":"Having established Abraham’s honour and made him a leader to follow, the Real warns against abandoning his religion and turning from his way:","anchor":"en-q2-128-129-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-130-132","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender 2:130–132","anchor":"unit-q2-130-132"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-1","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"وَمَنْ يَرْغَبُ عَنْ مِلَّةِ إِبْراهِيمَ إِلاَّ مَنْ سَفِهَ نَفْسَهُ وَلَقَدِ اصْطَفَيْناهُ فِي الدُّنْيا وَإِنَّهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ (130) إِذْ قالَ لَهُ رَبُّهُ أَسْلِمْ قالَ أَسْلَمْتُ لِرَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ (131) وَوَصَّى بِها إِبْراهِيمُ بَنِيهِ وَيَعْقُوبُ يا بَنِيَّ إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفى لَكُمُ الدِّينَ فَلا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلاَّ وَأَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ (132)","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-2","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"قلت: (من) : استفهامية إنكارية، فيها معنى النفي، مبتدأ، و (يرغب) وما بعده خبر، و (إلا) إبطال لنفيها الذي تضمنته، و (مَن سَفِه) بدل من ضمير (يرغب) على المختار، و (نفسه) مفعول «سَفِه» لتضمنه معنى جهل أو أهلك، قاله الزجاج، أو على التمييز قاله الفراء لأن الضمير فيه معنى الشيوع الذي في (مَن) فلم يكسب التعريف، أو على إسقاط الجارّ وإيصال الفعل إليه، كقولهم: ضرب فلان الظهر والبطن. و (إذ) معمول لاصطفيناه، وأوصى ووصى: لغتان، إلا أن وصى فيه معنى التكثير. وضمير (بها) يعود على كلمة (أسلمت) ، أو الملة، و (يعقوب) معطوف على «إبراهيم» ، و (بني) محكي بحال محذوفة، أي: قائلين يا بني، أو مبتدأ، والخبر محذوف، أي: قال يا بني ... الخ، فيوقف على (بنيه) .","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-3","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ هذا الذي يَرْغَبُ عَنْ مِلَّةِ إِبْراهِيمَ الواضحة إِلَّا من جهل قدر نَفْسَهُ وبخسها حقها؟ أو إلا من خف رأيه وسفهت نفسه؟ وكيف يرغب عاقل عنها وقد اخترناه إماماً فِي الدُّنْيا يقتدي به أهل الظاهر والباطن؟ وَإِنَّهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ لحضرتنا، والساكنين في جوارنا.","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-4","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"وإنما اخترناه لذلك لأنه حين قالَ لَهُ رَبُّهُ: استسلم لحكمنا، وانقد لأمرنا، قال سريعاً: أَسْلَمْتُ وجهي لِرَبِّ الْعالَمِينَ، وانقدْتُ بكُلّيتي إليه. وَوَصَّى بهذه الكلمة أو الملة إِبْراهِيمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-5","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"، عند موته، بَنِيهِ، وكانوا أربعة: إسماعيل وإسحاق ومدين ومدان. وكذلك حفيده يَعْقُوبُ أوصى بهذه الكلمة بنيه. وكانوا اثني عشر، على ما يأتي في الأسباط، قائلين في تلك الوصية: يا بَنِيَّ إِنَّ اللَّهَ اختار لكم الدِّينَ الحنيف الواضح المنيف، فتمسكوا به ما عِشْتُّم، ولا تموتن إِلَّا وَأَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ متمسكون به.","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-6","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"الإشارة: ملة أبينا إبراهيم عليه السلام هي رفع الهمة عن الخلق، وإفراد الوجهة للملك الحق، ورفض الوسائط والأسباب، والتعلق بربّ الأرباب، وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر، وهو الششتري:","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-7","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"فَرَفْضُ السّويَ فَرْضٌ علينا لأنَّنا ... بملةِ محْوِ الشّركِ والشَّكِّ قدْ دِنَّا","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-8","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"ومِنْ ملته أيضاً: تركُ التدبير والاختيار، والاستسلام لأحكام الواحد القهار، فمن تمسك بهذه الخصال على التمام، ووصى بها من لقيه من الأنام، جعله الله في الدنيا إماماً يقتدي بأقواله ويهتدي بأنواره، وإنه في الآخرة لمن الصالحين المقربين مع النبيين والمرسلين، وأما من رَغِبَ عن هذه الملة الحنيفية فقد خسر الدنيا والآخرة. نسأل الله الحفظ بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-130-132-9","r":"q2-130-132","title":"2:130–132 · Abraham’s religion and the testament of surrender","text":"ولما ادّعت اليهود أن اليهودية هى ملة إبراهيم عليه السلام كذّبهم الله تعالى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-130-132-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-130-132-s1","r":"q2-130-132","title":"Safiha nafsahu and the testament","text":"I say: “who” is a disapproving interrogative containing a negative sense, the subject of which “turns away…” is the predicate. “Except” overturns that implicit negation. On the preferred analysis, “one who makes a fool…” is an apposition to the subject-pronoun of “turns away.” “Himself” ( نفسه ) is the object of safiha , which includes the meaning “does not know” or “destroys,” according to al-Zajjāj. Al-Farrāʾ takes it as specification: its pronoun retains the indefiniteness of “who” and does not make it definite. Or it follows an omitted preposition, with the verb made directly transitive, like “He struck so-and-so the back and belly.” “When” is governed by “We chose him.” Awṣā and waṣṣā both mean to enjoin, though the latter suggests repetition. “This” refers to the declaration “I have surrendered” or to the religion. “Jacob” is conjoined to “Abraham,” and “My sons” is quoted after an omitted “while saying.” Alternatively, “Jacob” is a new subject whose predicate is omitted: “Jacob said, ‘My sons…’”; on that reading one pauses after “his sons.”","anchor":"en-q2-130-132-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-130-132-s2","r":"q2-130-132","title":"The immediate response to the divine command","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: who would turn from Abraham’s clear religion except someone ignorant of his own worth and withholding its due, or one whose judgement is light and whose soul is foolish? How could a rational person turn from it when We chose him as a worldly leader followed by people of outward and inward knowledge, and in the Hereafter he is among those fit for Our presence and dwelling near Us? We chose him because, when his Lord commanded surrender to Our judgement and obedience to Our command, he replied immediately: I surrender my face to the Lord of the worlds and yield myself wholly to Him. At death, Abraham enjoined this declaration or religion upon his four sons: Ishmael, Isaac, Midian and Midan. [B082] His grandson Jacob likewise enjoined it upon his twelve sons, described below among the Tribes. They said: my sons, God has chosen for you the upright, clear and exalted religion. Hold to it throughout your lives; die only in surrender, adhering to it.","anchor":"en-q2-130-132-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-130-132-s3","r":"q2-130-132","title":"Aspiration lifted above created supports","text":"The religion of our father Abraham is lifting aspiration above creation, directing oneself exclusively to the True King, relinquishing intermediaries and causes, and attaching oneself to the Lord of lords. Al-Shushtarī says: To renounce other-than-Him is our obligation, for we profess the way that effaces association and doubt. His religion also includes abandoning self-direction and choice, and surrendering to the decrees of the One, the All-Subduing. Whoever fully holds these qualities and enjoins them upon those he meets is made a leader in this world: his words are followed and his lights guide. In the Hereafter he is among the righteous brought near, with prophets and messengers. Whoever turns from this upright religion loses both worlds. We ask God’s protection through His favour and generosity.","anchor":"en-q2-130-132-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-130-132-s4","r":"q2-130-132","title":"","text":"When the Jews claimed that Judaism was Abraham’s religion, God declared their claim false, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-130-132-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-133-134","r":"q2-133-134","title":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds","text":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds 2:133–134","anchor":"unit-q2-133-134"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-133-134-1","r":"q2-133-134","title":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds","text":"أَمْ كُنْتُمْ شُهَداءَ إِذْ حَضَرَ يَعْقُوبَ الْمَوْتُ إِذْ قالَ لِبَنِيهِ ما تَعْبُدُونَ مِنْ بَعْدِي قالُوا نَعْبُدُ إِلهَكَ وَإِلهَ آبائِكَ إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ إِلهاً واحِداً وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُسْلِمُونَ (133) تِلْكَ أُمَّةٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ لَها ما كَسَبَتْ وَلَكُمْ ما كَسَبْتُمْ وَلا تُسْئَلُونَ عَمَّا كانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ (134)","anchor":"ar-q2-133-134-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-133-134-2","r":"q2-133-134","title":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds","text":"قلت: (أم) منقطعة، والاستفهام فيها للإنكار، أي: ما كنتم حاضرين حين حضر يعقوب الموت، وقال لبنيه ما قال، فكيف تدعون اليهودية عليه، و (إلهاً واحداً) بدل من (إله آبائك) ، وفائدته التصريح بالتوحيد، ونفى التوهم الناشئ عن تكرير المضاف، لتعذر العطف على المجرور، والتأكيد، أو نصب على الاختصاص أو الحال، وعد إسماعيل من الآباء تغليباً، أو لأنه كالأب لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «عَمُّ الرُجلِ صِنْوُ أبيه» وقال في العباس: «هذا بقية آبائي» . قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-133-134-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-133-134-3","r":"q2-133-134","title":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في توبيخ اليهود على زعمهم أن اليهودية كانت ملة إبراهيم، وأن يعقوب عليه السلام أوصى بها عند موته، فقال: هل كنتم حاضرين عند يعقوب حين حضرته الوفاة حتى أوصى بما زعمتم؟ وإنما كانت وصيته أن قال لبنيه: ما تَعْبُدُونَ مِنْ بَعْدِي أيْ: أيّ شيء تعبدونه؟ أراد به تقريرهم على التوحيد وأخذ ميثاقهم على الثبات عليه، (قالوا) في جوابه: نَعْبُدُ إِلهَكَ المتفق على وجوب وجوده وثبوت ألوهيته الذي هو إِلهَكَ وَإِلهَ آبائِكَ من قبلك إِبْراهِيمَ وولده إِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ الذي هو إلهٌ واحد. ونحن منقادون لأحكامه، مستسلمون لأمره إلى مماتنا، فلم يوص يعقوب إلا بما سمعتم، فانتسابكم يا معشر اليهود إليهم لا يوجب انتفاعكم بأعمالهم، وإنما تنتفعون بموافقتهم واتباعهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-133-134-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-133-134-4","r":"q2-133-134","title":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds","text":"فتلك أُمَّةٌ أي: جماعة قَدْ خَلَتْ لَها ما كَسَبَتْ من الخير، وَلَكُمْ ما كَسَبْتُمْ أنتم، وَلا تُسْئَلُونَ عَمَّا كانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ فلا تؤاخذون بسيئاتهم، كما لا تثابون بحسناتهم. وهذا كما قال صلّى الله عليه وسلّم لقريش: «لا يأتيني الناسُ بأعمَالهِم وتَأتُوني بأنْسَابِكُم» .","anchor":"ar-q2-133-134-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-133-134-5","r":"q2-133-134","title":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds","text":"الإشارة: يقال لمن حصرَ الخصوصية في أسلافه، ونفاها عن غيرهم: هل حضرتم معهم حين أوصوا بذلك؟ بل ما كانوا يوصون إلا بإخلاص العبودية، وتوحيد الألوهية، ومشاهدة عظمة الربوبية، فمن حصّل هذه الخصال كانت الخصوصية معه أينما كان، ومَن حاد عنها ومال إلى متابعة الهوى انتقلت إلى غيره، ويقال له: إن أسلافه قد جَدُّوا ووجَدُوا، وأنت لا تنتفع بأعمالهم في طريق الخصوصية، (تلك أمة قد خلت لها ما كسبت ولكم ما كسبتم ... ) الآية. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-133-134-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-133-134-6","r":"q2-133-134","title":"2:133–134 · The fathers’ religion and responsibility for one’s own deeds","text":"ولما أمر اليهود والنصارى المسلمين باتباع دينهم، لأنه أقدم، ردّ الله عليهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-133-134-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-133-134-s1","r":"q2-133-134","title":"One God, not several","text":"I say: am is disconnected ( منقطعة ), its interrogative expressing denial: you were not present at Jacob’s death when he spoke to his sons, so how can you attribute Judaism to him? “One God” is an apposition to “the God of your fathers.” It explicitly affirms unity, removes any misconception caused by repeating the annexed noun—which is necessary because one cannot here conjoin directly to the genitive pronoun—and reinforces the sense. Alternatively, it is accusative through specification or as a circumstantial expression. Ishmael is counted among the fathers by giving the predominant class’s designation to the whole ( التغليب ), or because he is like a father: the Prophet said, “A man’s paternal uncle is the counterpart of his father,” and of al-ʿAbbās, “This is what remains of my fathers.” Thus al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q2-133-134-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-133-134-s2","r":"q2-133-134","title":"A covenant of unity, not an inherited claim","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, reproaches the Jews for claiming that Judaism was Abraham’s religion and Jacob’s dying testament. Were you there to hear the testament you allege? He actually asked his sons what they would worship after him, confirming them in unity and taking their covenant of steadfastness. They answered: we worship your God, whose necessary existence and divinity are acknowledged, the God of your fathers Abraham and his sons Ishmael and Isaac—one God. We yield to His judgements and surrender to His command until death. Jacob enjoined only what you have heard. Your descent from them does not let you profit from their deeds; only conforming to and following them does. That community has passed: it has the good it earned, and you have what you earned. You are not questioned about their acts: neither punished for their wrongs nor rewarded for their good. This resembles the Prophet’s words to Quraysh: “Do not let people come to me with their deeds while you come with your lineages.”","anchor":"en-q2-133-134-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-133-134-s3","r":"q2-133-134","title":"Ancestry does not replace realization","text":"Someone restricting special election to his forefathers and denying it elsewhere is asked: were you present when they enjoined such a claim? They enjoined only sincere servanthood, the unity of Divinity and witnessing Lordship’s grandeur. Whoever realizes these qualities possesses special election wherever he is. If he deviates and follows desire, it passes to another. He is told: your forefathers strove and found; their deeds do not benefit you in the path of special election. “That community has passed; theirs is what they earned, yours what you earned.” Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-133-134-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-133-134-s4","r":"q2-133-134","title":"","text":"When Jews and Christians told the Muslims to follow their older religion, God replied:","anchor":"en-q2-133-134-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-135","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God 2:135","anchor":"unit-q2-135"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-135-1","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"وَقالُوا كُونُوا هُوداً أَوْ نَصارى تَهْتَدُوا قُلْ بَلْ مِلَّةَ إِبْراهِيمَ حَنِيفاً وَما كانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ (135)","anchor":"ar-q2-135-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-135-2","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"قلت: الضمير في (قالوا) لأهل الكتاب، و (أو) للتفصيل، أي: قالت اليهود: كونوا هودا، وقالت النصارى:","anchor":"ar-q2-135-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-135-3","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"كونوا نصارى. و (تهتدوا) جواب الأمر، و (ملة) منصوب بفعل محذوف، على حذف مضاف، أي: بل نكون أهل ملة إبراهيم، أو نتبع او نلزم ملة إبراهيم، و (حنيفاً) حال من المضاف إليه، لأنه كجزئه، أي: مائلاً عن الباطل إلى الحق.","anchor":"ar-q2-135-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-135-4","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وقالت اليهود للمسلمين: كُونُوا معنا هوداً تَهْتَدُوا فإن ديننا أقدم، وقالت النصارى لهم أيضاً: كونوا نَصارى معنا تَهْتَدُوا فإن ديننا أصوب، قُلْ لهم يا محمد: بَلْ نلزم مِلَّةَ إِبْراهِيمَ الذي كان مائلاً عن الباطل متبعاً للحق، ومشاهداً له وحده. ولم يكن من المشركين كما أشركتم بعُزير وعيسى وغيرهما، تعالى الله عن قولكم علواً كبيراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-135-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-135-5","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"الإشارة: قد سرى هذا الطبع في بعض المنتسبين، يُرَغِّبُون الناس في طريقهم، ويحرصون على اتباعهم والدخول معهم، وينقصون طريق غيرهم، وهو وصف مذموم، بل الواجب أن ينظر الإنسان بعين البصيرة، فمن وجده يدل على الله ويغيب عما سواه، ينهض حاله ويدل على الله مقاله، اتبعه وحطَّ رأسه له، ولزم ملته وطريقه أينما كان، وكيفما كان. ومن وجده على غير هذا الوصف، أعرض عنه، والتمس غيره، وليس من شأن الدعاة إلى","anchor":"ar-q2-135-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-135-6","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"الله الحرص على الناس، أو الترغيب في اتباعهم، بل هم أزهد الناس في الناس، من أتاهم دلّوه على الله، ومن لقيهم نصحوه في الله، هم على قدَم الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم وقد قال له الحقّ تعالى: أَفَأَنْتَ تُكْرِهُ النَّاسَ حَتَّى يَكُونُوا مُؤْمِنِينَ. لَسْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِمُصَيْطِرٍ.، لَعَلَّكَ باخِعٌ نَفْسَكَ أَلَّا يَكُونُوا مُؤْمِنِينَ، فكان صلّى الله عليه وسلّم بعد ذلك يدل على الله وينظر ما يفعل الله. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-135-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-135-7","r":"q2-135","title":"2:135 · Following the guide who points to God","text":"ثم بيَّن الحق تعالى كيفية الإيمان الذي يجب اتباعه، وأبطل ما سواه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-135-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-135-s1","r":"q2-135","title":"The two claims and the upright inclination","text":"I say: “they said” refers to the People of the Book; “or” distributes the statement: the Jews say “be Jews,” the Christians “be Christians.” “You will be guided” is the response to the command. “Religion” is accusative through an omitted verb and, on one analysis, an omitted annexed noun: rather, we become adherents of Abraham’s religion; or, we follow or adhere to his religion. “Inclining wholly” ( حنيفاً ) is circumstantial with respect to the second term of the annexation, since the first is like part of it: inclining from falsehood towards truth.","anchor":"en-q2-135-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-135-s2","r":"q2-135","title":"The religion free of association","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the Jews tell Muslims to join them and be guided because their religion is older; the Christians tell them to join theirs because it is more correct. Say, Muḥammad: rather, we adhere to Abraham’s religion. He inclined away from falsehood, followed truth and witnessed Him alone. He was not an associator, as you associated ʿUzayr, Jesus and others. Exalted is God far above your assertions.","anchor":"en-q2-135-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-135-s3","r":"q2-135","title":"Spiritual calling without recruitment and rivalry","text":"This disposition has spread among some affiliated to spiritual paths. They entice people to their own way, eagerly seek followers and belittle other paths: a blameworthy trait. Instead, one must look with insight. Whoever points to God and makes one absent from other-than-Him, whose state raises one and whose speech directs one to God—follow him, lower your head before him and adhere to his way, wherever and however he may be. Turn from anyone lacking this quality and seek another. Those who call to God are not characterized by grasping after people or enticing them to become followers. They are the least attached to people. Whoever comes, they direct to God; whoever meets them, they counsel for God. They stand upon the Messenger’s footing. The Real told him, “Will you compel people until they become believers?” [10:99]; “You are not a controller over them” [88:22]; and “Perhaps you would destroy yourself because they do not believe” [26:3]. Thereafter he pointed to God and watched what God would do. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-135-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-135-s4","r":"q2-135","title":"","text":"The Real explains the faith that must be followed and invalidates what differs from it:","anchor":"en-q2-135-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-136-138","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye 2:136–138","anchor":"unit-q2-136-138"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-1","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"قُولُوا آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْنا وَما أُنْزِلَ إِلى إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْباطِ وَما أُوتِيَ مُوسى وَعِيسى وَما أُوتِيَ النَّبِيُّونَ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ لاَ نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُسْلِمُونَ (136) فَإِنْ آمَنُوا بِمِثْلِ ما آمَنْتُمْ بِهِ فَقَدِ اهْتَدَوْا وَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَإِنَّما هُمْ فِي شِقاقٍ فَسَيَكْفِيكَهُمُ اللَّهُ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ (137) صِبْغَةَ اللَّهِ وَمَنْ أَحْسَنُ مِنَ اللَّهِ صِبْغَةً وَنَحْنُ لَهُ عابِدُونَ (138)","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-2","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"قلت: الأسباط: الأحفاد، والسِّبطُ في بني إسرائيل بمنزلة القبيلة في ولد إسماعيل، والباء في (بمثل) : يحتمل أن تكون زائدة كقوله تعالى: وجَزاءُ سَيِّئَةٍ بِمِثْلِها، أو (مثل) مُقْحَم، أي: فإن آمنوا بما آمنتم به، كقوله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-3","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"وَشَهِدَ شاهِدٌ مِنْ بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ عَلى مِثْلِهِ. والشقاق: المخالفة، كأنَّ كل واحد من المتخالفين في شق غير شق الآخر، و (صبغة الله) : مصدر مؤكد لآمنا لأن الإيمان ينصبغ في القلوب، ويظهر أثره على الجوارح ظهور الصبغ على المصبوغ، ويتداخل في قلوبهم تداخل الصبغ للثوب. أي: آمنا وصبغنا الله به صبغة.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-4","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"وهي فطرةَ الله التي فطر الناس عليها، وعبَّر عنها بالصبغ للمشاكلة فإن النصارى كانوا يغمسون أولادهم في ماء أصفر يسمونه المعمودية، ويقولون: هو تطهير لهم، وبه تحق نصرانيتهم، فردَّ الله تعالى عليهم بأن صبغة، الله أحسن من صبغتهم وقيل: نصب على البدل من (ملة إبراهيم) ، أو على الإغراء، أي: الزموا صبغة الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-5","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُولُوا يا معشر المسلمين في تحقيق إيمانكم: آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ أي: صدقنا بوجوده متصفاً بصفة الكمال، منزّهاً عن النقائص، وَبما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْنا وهو القرآن، وَبما أُنْزِلَ من الصحف إِلى إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ ولد إسحاق، وَالْأَسْباطِ أولاد يعقوب عليه السلام وهم: روبيل وشمعون ولاوى ويهوذا وربالون ويشحُرْ، ودنية بنته، وأمهم لَيَا، ثم خلف على أختها راحيل، فولدت له يوسف وبنيامين، وَوُلد له من سرِّيَّتينِ: دان ونفتالى وجاد وآشر.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-6","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"قال ابن حجر: اختلف في نبوتهم، فقيل: كانوا أنبياء، وقيل: لم يكن فيهم نبيّ، وإنما المراد بالأسباط قبائل من بني إسرائيل، فقد كان فيهم من الأنبياء عدد كثير. هـ. وممن صرّح بنفي نبوتهم عياض وجمهور المفسرين.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-7","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"انظر: المحشي الفاسي.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-8","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"وقولوا: آمنا بما أنزل إلى مُوسى وهو التوراة، وَعِيسى وهو الإنجيل، وبما أُوتِيَ النَّبِيُّونَ كلهم مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ من عرفنا منهم ومن لم نعرف، لاَ نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ واحد مِنْهُمْ كما فرقت اليهود والنصارى، فقد آمنا بالله وبجميع أنبيائه وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُسْلِمُونَ أي: منقادون لأحكامه الظاهرة والباطنة.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-9","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"قال الحق جلّ جلاله: فَإِنْ آمَنُوا أي: أهل الكتاب إيماناً مثل إيمانكم، فَقَدِ اهْتَدَوْا إلى الحق والصواب، وإن أعرضوا عن ذلك فاتركهم حتى نأمرك فيهم، فَإِنَّما هُمْ فِي شِقاقٍ وخلاف لك، فلا تهتم بشأنهم، فَسَيَكْفِيكَهُمُ اللَّهُ أي سيكفيك شرهم وينصرك عليهم، وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ لدعائكم، الْعَلِيمُ بإخلاصكم، فالزموا صِبْغَةَ اللَّهِ التي صُبغتم بها، وهى الإيمان بما ذكرت لكم فإنه لا أحسن صبغة من صبغة الله، وَقولوا: نَحْنُ لَهُ عابِدُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-10","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"الإشارة: كما أوجب الله تعالى الإيمان بجميع الرسل في طريق العموم، كذلك أوجب الله التصديق بكل من ثبتت ولايته في طريق الخصوص، فمن فرق بينهم فقد كفر بطريقهم، ومن كفر بطريقهم طُرد عن بابهم، ومن طرد عن بابهم طرد عن باب الله، لأن إسقاطه من الولاية إيذاء له ، ومن آذى وليًا فقد آذن الله بالحرب، فالواجب، على مَن أراد أن يرد مناهلهم، أن يصدق بجميعهم، ويعظم من انتسب إليهم، حتى تنصبغ في قلبه حلاوة الإيمان، وتشرق عليه شموس العرفان، فمن فعل هذا فقد اهتدى إلى الحق والصواب، واستحق الدخول مع الأحباب، ومن أعرض عن هذا فإنما هو في شقاق، وربما يخاف عليه من شؤم الكفر والنفاق، فسيكفي الله أولياءه سوءَ شره، والله غالب على أمره.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-11","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"قال القشيري: فللقلوب صبغة، وللأرواح صبغة، وللسرائر صبغة، وللظواهر صبغة، فصبغة الأشباح والظواهر بآثار التوفيق، وصبغة الأرواح والسرائر بأنوار التحقيق. هـ. وقال الورتجبي: صبغة الله: صفته الخاصة","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-12","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"التي خلق آدم عليها، وأورثت ذلك في أرواح ذريته من الأنبياء والأولياء. ثم قال: وسقاها من شراب الزلفة، وألهمها خصائص علوم الربوبية، فاستنارت بنور المعرفة، وخاضت في بحر الربوبية، وخرجت منها تجليات أسرار الوحدانية، وتكوّنت بصبغ الصفات. هـ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-136-138-13","r":"q2-136-138","title":"2:136–138 · Faith in all the messengers and the divine dye","text":"ولمَّا ادعت اليهود والنصارى أنهم أولى الناس بالله من غيرهم لتقدم دينهم، رد الله عليهم ووبخهم فقال: (قل أتحاجوننا ... ) الآية. وقيل: إن اليهود قالوا للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: الأنبياء كلهم منا، فلو كنت نبيا لكنت منا، فردَّ الله عليهم بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-136-138-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-136-138-s1","r":"q2-136-138","title":"Tribes, opposition and the dye of faith","text":"I say: the asbāṭ ( أسباط ) are descendants; a sibṭ among the Children of Israel is like a tribe among Ishmael’s descendants. The bāʾ in bi-mithli may be supplementary, as in “the recompense of an evil deed is its like” [10:27]; or mithl itself is inserted for reinforcement: if they believe what you believe, as in “a witness from the Children of Israel testified to its like” [46:10]. Opposition ( شقاق ) is disagreement, as though each opponent occupies a different side ( شقّ ). “God’s dye” ( صبغة الله ) is a verbal noun reinforcing “we believe,” for faith dyes hearts and shows its effect upon the limbs as dye upon a dyed object, penetrating hearts as dye penetrates cloth: we believe, and God dyes us with it. It is the original disposition upon which God created people. “Dye” is used through verbal correspondence ( المشاكلة ), since Christians immersed children in yellow water called baptism, regarding it as purification establishing their Christianity. God replies that His dye is better. [B083] Alternatively, it is an apposition to “Abraham’s religion,” or an accusative of exhortation: hold to God’s dye.","anchor":"en-q2-136-138-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-136-138-s2","r":"q2-136-138","title":"The prophets and the descendants of Jacob","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Muslims, declare in realization of your faith: we believe in God—His existence, perfection and transcendence beyond defects; in the Qurʾān revealed to us; and in the scrolls revealed to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob son of Isaac, and the Tribes, Jacob’s sons. These are Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Zebulun and Issachar, with their sister Dinah, whose mother was Leah. He subsequently married Leah’s sister Rachel, who bore Joseph and Benjamin. Two concubines bore Dan, Naphtali, Gad and Asher. Ibn Ḥajar says their prophethood is disputed: some hold that they were prophets; others that none was a prophet, and that “the Tribes” means the tribes of Israel, among whom many prophets arose. ʿIyāḍ and the majority of commentators expressly deny their prophethood: consult the glossator al-Fāsī. [B084] Say: we believe what was given to Moses—the Torah—and Jesus—the Gospel—and all prophets by their Lord, those we know and those we do not. We distinguish none by rejection, as Jews and Christians did. We believe God and all His prophets and surrender to His outward and inward judgements. The Real says: if the People of the Book believe with faith like yours, they have reached truth and correctness. If they turn away, leave them until We command you concerning them. They are in opposition and disagreement; do not be troubled by them. God will suffice against their evil and grant you victory. He hears your prayer and knows your sincerity. Hold to the divine dye with which you were coloured—faith in all I have mentioned—for none is better. Say: we worship Him alone.","anchor":"en-q2-136-138-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-136-138-s3","r":"q2-136-138","title":"Affirming every established friend of God","text":"Just as God requires faith in all messengers on the general path, so He requires affirmation of everyone whose friendship with Him is established on the special path. Whoever divides between them denies their way; whoever denies their way is expelled from their door, and whoever is expelled from their door is expelled from God’s. To strip a friend of his friendship is to hurt him; whoever hurts God’s friend declares war against God. Anyone wishing to drink at their watering places must affirm them all and honour those affiliated to them, until faith’s sweetness dyes his heart and the suns of gnosis shine upon him. Whoever does this reaches truth and deserves admission among the beloved. Whoever turns away is in opposition; one may fear for him the ill omen of unbelief and hypocrisy. God will suffice His friends against his evil, and God prevails in His purpose. Al-Qushayrī says: hearts have a dye, spirits a dye, secrets a dye and outward forms a dye. Bodies and outward forms are dyed with the effects of divine enabling; spirits and secrets with the lights of realization. Al-Wartajbī says: “God’s dye is His special attribute upon which He created Adam, inherited in the spirits of Adam’s prophetic and saintly descendants.” He then said: “He gave them the wine of nearness and inspired them with the special sciences of Lordship. They shone with gnosis’s light, plunged into Lordship’s sea, and from them came disclosures of the mysteries of unity; they were formed through the dye of the Attributes.” Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-136-138-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-136-138-s4","r":"q2-136-138","title":"","text":"When Jews and Christians claimed greater proximity to God than others because their religion was older, He rebuked them: “Say, do you dispute with us…”. Another account says the Jews told the Prophet, “All prophets are from us; were you a prophet, you would be from us.” God replied:","anchor":"en-q2-136-138-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-139-141","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people 2:139–141","anchor":"unit-q2-139-141"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-1","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"قُلْ أَتُحَاجُّونَنا فِي اللَّهِ وَهُوَ رَبُّنا وَرَبُّكُمْ وَلَنا أَعْمالُنا وَلَكُمْ أَعْمالُكُمْ وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُخْلِصُونَ (139) أَمْ تَقُولُونَ إِنَّ إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْباطَ كانُوا هُوداً أَوْ نَصارى قُلْ أَأَنْتُمْ أَعْلَمُ أَمِ اللَّهُ وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ كَتَمَ شَهادَةً عِنْدَهُ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ (140) تِلْكَ أُمَّةٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ لَها ما كَسَبَتْ وَلَكُمْ ما كَسَبْتُمْ وَلا تُسْئَلُونَ عَمَّا كانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ (141)","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-2","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"قلت: الذي يظهر أن (أم) منقطعة، بمعنى بل، على قراءة الخطاب والغيبة لأن المقصود إنكار وقوع الأمرين معاً، لا أحدهما.","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-3","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد لأهل الكتاب: أتخاصموننا فِي اللَّهِ وتقولون: أنتم أولى به منا وَهُوَ رَبُّنا وَرَبُّكُمْ، لا يختص به واحد دون آخر، وَلَنا أَعْمالُنا نتقرب بها إليه، وَلَكُمْ أَعْمالُكُمْ تتقربون بها أيضاً، فكيف تختصون به دوننا وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُخْلِصُونَ في أعمالنا وقلوبنا دونكم فإنكم أشركتم به غيره، فإن قلتم: إن الأنبياء كلهم منكم وعلى ملتكم فقد كذبتم، أتقولون إِنَّ إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وأولاده الْأَسْباطَ كانُوا هُوداً على دينكم يا معشر اليهود، أَوْ نَصارى على ملتكم يا معشر النصارى.","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-4","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"قُلْ لهم يا محمد: أَأَنْتُمْ أَعْلَمُ أَمِ اللَّهُ وقد نفى الأمرين معاً عن إبراهيم فقال: مَا كانَ إِبْراهِيمُ يَهُودِيًّا وَلا نَصْرانِيًّا وَلكِنْ كانَ حَنِيفاً مُسْلِماً وقال: وَما أُنْزِلَتِ التَّوْراةُ وَالْإِنْجِيلُ إِلَّا مِنْ بَعْدِهِ، وهؤلاء المعطوفون عليه: أتباعه في الدين، فليسوا يهوداً ولا نصارى، فكيف تدعون أنهم كلهم منكم، وعلى دينكم، وأنتم تشهدون أنهم لم يكونوا على دينكم؟ وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ كَتَمَ شَهادَةً عِنْدَهُ مِنَ اللَّهِ، وهي شهادة الحق","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-5","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"لإبراهيم بالحنيفية، والبراءة من اليهودية والنصرانية، أي: لا أحد أظلم منه، وليس الله تعالى بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ، بل يجازيكم على النقير والقطمير، فإن اعتمدتم على نسبكم إليهم فقد اغتررتم.","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-6","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"تِلْكَ أُمَّةٌ قد مضت، لَها ما كَسَبَتْ لا ينتفع به غيرها، وَلَكُمْ ما كَسَبْتُمْ لا ينفعكم غيره، ولا تسألون عن عملهم كما لا يسألون عن أعمالكم. قال البيضاوي: كرره للمبالغة في التحذير، والزجر عما استحكم في الطباع من الافتخار بالآباء، والاتكال عليهم، وقيل: الخطاب فيما سبق لهم، وفي هذه الآية لنا، تحذيراً عن الاقتداء بهم، وقيل: المراد بالأمة في الأولى الأنبياء، وفي الثانية أسلاف اليهود والنصارى. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-7","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"الإشارة: كل من أقامه الحقّ في وجهة، ووجهه إليها، فهو عامل لله فيها، قائم بمراد الله منها، وما اختلفت الأعمال إلا من جهة المقاصد، وما تفاوت الناس إلا من جهة الإخلاص. فالخلق كلهم عبيد للملك المجيد، وما وقع الاختصاص إلا من جهة الإخلاص. فمن كان أكثر إخلاصاً لله كان أولى من غيره بالله، وبقدر ما يقع للعبد من الصفاء يكون له من الاصطفاء، فالصوفية والعلماء والعباد والزهاد وأهل الأسباب على اختلاف أنواعهم كلهم عاملون لله، ليس أحد منهم بأولى من غيره بالله إلا من جهة الإخلاص وإفراد القلب لله، فمن ادعى الاختصاص بالله من غير هذه الوجهة فهو كاذب، ومن اعتمد على عمل غيره فهو مغرور، يقال له: تِلْكَ أُمَّةٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ لَها ما كَسَبَتْ وَلَكُمْ ما كَسَبْتُمْ وَلا تُسْئَلُونَ عَمَّا كانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-139-141-8","r":"q2-139-141","title":"2:139–141 · Sincerity, not occupation or ancestry, distinguishes people","text":"ولمّا أراد الله تعالى أن ينسخ القبلة من جهة الشام ويردها إلى الكعبة، أخبر أنه سينكرها قومٌ خَفَّتْ أحلامُهم، وفسدت بالتقليد الردي عقولُهم، وهم أحبار اليهود والمنافقون والمشركون، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-139-141-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-139-141-s1","r":"q2-139-141","title":"Disapproval of both claims","text":"I say: am appears to be disconnected, meaning “rather,” whether the verb is read in the second or third person. The intention is to reject both things, not merely one of them.","anchor":"en-q2-139-141-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-139-141-s2","r":"q2-139-141","title":"Neither precedence nor ancestry secures a monopoly","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Muḥammad, ask the People of the Book whether they dispute concerning God, claiming greater entitlement to Him, when He is our Lord and yours, not restricted to one rather than another. We have deeds by which we draw near, and you have yours, by which you too draw near. How can you monopolize proximity when we are sincere to Him in deeds and hearts, whereas you associate another with Him? If you claim all prophets belonged to you and your religion, you have spoken falsely. Do you claim that Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob and his sons, the Tribes, were Jews according to your religion, Jewish people, or Christians according to yours, Christian people? Ask them: do you know better, or God? He denied both of Abraham: “Abraham was neither Jew nor Christian, but upright in surrender” [3:67]; “The Torah and Gospel were sent down only after him” [3:65]. Those mentioned with him followed his religion, so were neither Jews nor Christians. How can you claim them all for your religion when you bear witness otherwise? None is more unjust than one concealing God’s testimony that Abraham was upright and free of Judaism and Christianity. God is not unaware of your acts: He requites even the tiniest thing. Reliance on descent from them is delusion. That community has passed. Its deeds belong to it and do not benefit others; yours belong to you and nothing else benefits you. You are not questioned about their deeds, nor they about yours. Al-Bayḍāwī says the repetition intensifies warning against the deeply rooted habit of boasting in fathers and relying upon them. Another view takes the earlier address as directed to them and this one to us, warning against imitation. Another takes the first “community” as the prophets and the second as the Jewish and Christian ancestors.","anchor":"en-q2-139-141-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-139-141-s3","r":"q2-139-141","title":"The equality of callings before the criterion of sincerity","text":"Whoever the Real establishes in an occupation and directs towards it works for God there and fulfils God’s purpose in it. Works differ through intentions; people differ in degree through sincerity. All creatures are servants of the Glorious King. Special distinction arises only through sincerity: whoever is more sincere to God is nearer to Him than another. In proportion to the servant’s purity comes his election. Sufis, scholars, worshippers, renunciants and those engaged in worldly occupations of every kind all work for God. None has greater entitlement to Him than another except through sincerity and the heart’s exclusive devotion to Him. Whoever claims distinction with God on any other basis is lying. Whoever relies on another’s work is deluded and is told: “That community has passed; theirs is what they earned, yours what you earned; you will not be questioned about what they did.”","anchor":"en-q2-139-141-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-139-141-s4","r":"q2-139-141","title":"","text":"When God wished to change the prayer-direction from Syria towards the Kaʿba, He announced that people of light judgement and minds corrupted by bad imitation—the Jewish learned men, hypocrites and polytheists—would object, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-139-141-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-142","r":"q2-142","title":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean","text":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean 2:142","anchor":"unit-q2-142"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-142-1","r":"q2-142","title":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean","text":"سَيَقُولُ السُّفَهاءُ مِنَ النَّاسِ ما وَلاَّهُمْ عَنْ قِبْلَتِهِمُ الَّتِي كانُوا عَلَيْها قُلْ لِلَّهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشاءُ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ (142)","anchor":"ar-q2-142-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-142-2","r":"q2-142","title":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: سَيَقُولُ السُّفَهاءُ مِنَ النَّاسِ الذين لا عقل لهم ولا دين، حين تحول القبلة من بيت المقدس إلى الكعبة: ما صرفهم عَنْ قِبْلَتِهِمُ الَّتِي كانُوا عَلَيْها، فلو دام عليها لاتبعناه. قُلْ لهم يا محمد:","anchor":"ar-q2-142-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-142-3","r":"q2-142","title":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean","text":"لِلَّهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ لا يختص ملكه بمكان دون مكان بخاصية ذاتية تمنع من إقامة غيره مقامه، بل الأماكن عند الله سواء: والخلق في حقه سواء، يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشاءُ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ، ويضل من يشاء عن المنهاج القويم لاَ يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُونَ، والصراط المستقيم: ما ترتضيه الحكمة وتقتضيه المصلحة من التوجه إلى بيت المقدس تارة، والكعبة أخرى، وفائدة تقديم الإخبار به: توطين النفس وإعداد الجواب. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-142-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-142-4","r":"q2-142","title":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean","text":"قال بعض العارفين: (لي أربعون سنة ما أقامني الحق في شيء فكرهته، ولا نقلني إلى غيره فسخطته) .","anchor":"ar-q2-142-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-142-5","r":"q2-142","title":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean","text":"بخلاف السفهاء من الجهال، فشأنهم الإنكار عند اختلاف الأحوال، فمن رأوه تجرد عن الأسباب وانقطع إلى الكريم الوهاب، قالوا: ما ولاَّه عن حاله الذي كان عليه؟ وأكثروا من الاعتراض والانتقاد عليه، وكذلك من رأوه رجع إلى الأسباب بعد الكمال، قالوا: قد انحط عن مراتب الرجال. وهو إنما زاد في مراتب الكمال. فالملك كله لله، يهدي مَن يشاء إلى صراط مستقيم، ويضل من يشاء بعدله الحكيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-142-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-142-6","r":"q2-142","title":"2:142 · Changing directions and the community of the just mean","text":"ثم شهد الحق تعالى لهذه الأمة بالعدالة والفضل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-142-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-142-s1","r":"q2-142","title":"The disposition of places belongs to God","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when the prayer-direction changes from Jerusalem to the Kaʿba, the foolish, lacking sound judgement and religion, will ask what has turned them from their former direction, saying, “Had he remained with it, we would have followed him.” Tell them, Muḥammad: east and west belong to God. His dominion is not restricted to a place by an intrinsic property preventing another from replacing it. Places are equal before God, as creatures are equal in relation to Him. He guides whom He wills to a straight path and leads whom He wills away from the sound road: “He is not questioned about what He does, but they are questioned” [21:23]. The straight path is what wisdom approves and benefit requires: facing Jerusalem at one time and the Kaʿba at another. Announcing the objection in advance prepares the soul and readies the answer. Thus al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q2-142-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-142-s2","r":"q2-142","title":"Neither withdrawal nor return to occupations is judged by appearances","text":"A gnostic said: “For forty years, the Real has never placed me in something I disliked or transferred me to something else with which I was discontent.” The ignorant foolish are otherwise: they object whenever states change. If they see someone withdraw from ordinary means and turn entirely to the Generous Bestower, they ask what turned him from his former condition and multiply objections. If they see someone return to ordinary means after perfection, they say he has fallen from the ranks of realized people, though he has only increased in perfection. All dominion belongs to God: He guides whom He wills to a straight path and leads whom He wills astray through His wise justice. The Real then attests this community’s justice and excellence: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:143a وَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا Thus We made you a community of the just mean, that you may be witnesses over people and the Messenger a witness over you.","anchor":"en-q2-142-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-142-s3","r":"q2-142","title":"The mean between excess and deficiency","text":"I say: wasaṭ ( وسط ) means just, good and excellent. Originally it names a place equally distant from its surrounding sides; it is then borrowed for praiseworthy qualities lying between excess and deficiency, such as generosity between extravagance and miserliness, or courage between recklessness and cowardice. It then denotes someone possessing these qualities, unchanged for singular and plural, masculine and feminine. Thus al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q2-142-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-142-s4","r":"q2-142","title":"The community as witness","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: just as We guided you to the straight path and made your prayer-direction the best, We made you the best community—chosen, just and purified through knowledge and action—fit to bear witness over others on the Day of Resurrection. Your Prophet attests your integrity. Al-Bayḍāwī relates: the communities on the Day of Resurrection deny that their prophets conveyed the message. God, though knowing their state, requires evidence to establish the argument against the deniers. Muḥammad’s community is brought to testify. Asked how they know, they reply: God informed us in His Book, spoken upon His truthful Prophet’s tongue. Muḥammad is then brought and questioned about his community, and attests their justice. Although this testimony is in their favour, “over” is used because the Messenger watches and oversees his community; the phrase’s position emphasizes their particular distinction in having him as witness over them.","anchor":"en-q2-142-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-142-s5","r":"q2-142","title":"Knowledge, purification and the authority to attest","text":"Excellence among people depends on knowledge and state. Whoever is stronger in knowledge of God is greater in worth before Him. The knowledge conferring honour is knowledge of His Essence, Attributes and Names, and knowledge of His rulings when joined to knowledge of Him. The more the heart’s veil is lifted, the nearer it is to its Lord. Unveiling corresponds to emptying and adorning ( التخلية والتحلية ): as the heart relinquishes vices, withdraws from obstacles and distractions, and acquires virtues, its veil lifts and it enters among the beloved. As distracting thoughts and occupations accumulate and defects enter it, distance from God grows and the servant is expelled from His door. Many deeds do not establish perfection; lofty aspiration and state do. Aspiration corresponds to certainty, certainty to gnosis, gnosis to orientation and purification, and orientation follows the eternal allotment. Such is God’s bounty, given to whom He wills. Scholars of God’s rulings without unveiling of His Essence are a proof against God’s servants. Those knowing God, to whom His Essence has been unveiled in witnessing and direct vision, are a proof against the scholars of His rulings. As the Muḥammadan community testifies over people and the Messenger attests it, so scholars testify over people and friends of God over scholars, validating those who deserve validation and rejecting those who do not. Gnostics know the states and stations of outward scholars; outward scholars neither know the friends’ stations nor smell their fragrance. As someone said: We left the overflowing seas behind us; how should people know where we have turned? Al-Qushayrī says: God made this community the best of communities and this company the best within it—the best of the best. As the community witnesses over other communities at the Resurrection, this company is the pivot and pole through whom God preserves the whole community. Whoever their hearts accept is accepted; whoever they reject is rejected. Their discernment judges truly, their judgement is sound and their vision correct. He protects the whole community from agreeing upon error, and this company from error in perception, judgement, acceptance and rejection. Yet their affair rests upon the Messenger’s Sunna: anyone not following him is rejected among them and counts for nothing. [B085] Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-142-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-142-s6","r":"q2-142","title":"","text":"The Real explains the wisdom of changing the prayer-direction:","anchor":"en-q2-142-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-143-144","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy 2:143–144","anchor":"unit-q2-143-144"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-1","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"وَكَذلِكَ جَعَلْناكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطاً لِتَكُونُوا شُهَداءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيداً ...","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-2","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"قلت: (الوسط) هو العدل الخيّر الفاضل، وهو في الأصل اسم للمكان الذي تستوي إليه المساحة من الجوانب، ثم استعير للخصال المحمودة لوقوعها بين طرفي إفراط وتفريط، كالجود بين الإسراف والبخل، والشجاعة بين التهور والجبن، ثم أطلق على المتصف بها مستويا فيه الواحد والجمع، والمذكر والمؤنث. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-3","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وكما جعلناكم مهتدين إلى الصراط المستقيم، وجعلنا قبلتكم أفضل الجهات، جعلناكم أمة أفضل الأمم، خياراً عدولاً مزكَّين بالعلم والعمل، لتصلحوا للشهادة على غيركم، فتكونوا يوم القيامة شُهَداءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ، ويزكيكم نبيكم فيشهد بعدالتكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-4","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"قال البيضاوي: رُوِيَ (أن الأمم يوم القيامة يجحدون تبليغ الأنبياء، فيُطالبُهم الله ببينة التبليغ وهو أعلم بهم، إقامة للحجة على المنكرين، فيُؤتَى بأمة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم فيشهدُون، فتقُول الأمم: مِنْ أَيْنَ عرفتُمْ؟ فيقولُون: عَلِمْنَا ذلك بإخْبَار الله في كِتَابِهِ النَّاطِقِ عَلَى لسانِ نبيه الصَّادِقِ. فيُؤتى بمحمَّدٍ صلى الله عليه وسلّم فَيُسألُ عن حَالِ أُمته فَيشْهَدُ بعَدَالتِهمْ) .","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-5","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"وهذه الشهادة، وإن كانت لهم، لكن لمّا كان الرسول كالرقيب المهيمن على أمته عُدّيِ بِعَلَى، وقُدِّمت الصلة للدلالة على اختصاصهم بكون الرسول شهيداً عليهم. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-6","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"الإشارة: التفاضل بين الرجال إنما يكون بالعلم والحال، فمن قَويَ علْمُه بالله كان أعظم قدراً عند الله، والعلم الذي به الشرف عند الله هو العلم بذات الله وبصفاته وأسمائه، وكذا العلم بأحكام الله إذا حصل معه العلم بالله، فكلما انكشف الحجاب عن القلب كان أقرب إلى الرب، وانكشاف الحجاب يكون على قدر التخلية والتحلية، فبقدر ما يتخلّى القلب عن الرذائل، ويبعد عن القواطع والشواغل، ويتحلّى بأنواع الفضائل، ينكشف عنه الحجاب ويدخل مع","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-7","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"الأحباب، وبقدر ما يتراكم على القلب من الخواطر والشواغل، ويدخل عليه من المساوئ والرذائل، يقع البعد عن الله، ويطرد العبد عن باب الله، فلا يدل على كمال العبد كثرة الأعمال، وإنما يدل على كماله علو الهمة والحال، وعلو الهمة على قدر اليقين، وقدر اليقين على قدر المعرفة، والمعرفة على قدر التوجه والتصفية، والتوجه تابع للقسمة الأزلية. وذلك فضل الله يؤتيه مَن يشاء.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-8","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"ثم إن العلماء بأحكام الله إذا لم يحصل لهم الكشف عن ذات الله يكونون حجة على عباد الله. والعلماء بالله الذين حصل لهم الكشف عن ذات الله حتى حصل لهم الشهود والعيان يكونون حجة على العلماء بأحكام الله. فكما أن الأمة المحمدية تشهد على الناس، والرسول يشهد عليهم ويزكيهم، فكذلك العلماء يشهدون على الناس، والأولياء يشهدون على العلماء، فيزكون من يستحق التزكية، ويردون مَن لا يستحقها لأن العارفين بالله عالمون بمقامات العلماء أهل الظاهر، لا يخفى عليهم شيء من أحوالهم ومقاماتهم، بخلاف العلماء، لا يعرفون مقامات الأولياء، ولا يشمون لها رائحة، كما قال القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-9","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"تَرَكْنَا البُحُورَ الزاخِراتِ ورَاءنَا ... فَمِنْ أَينَ يَدْرِِي الناسُ أينَ توجَّهْنَا","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-10","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"قال القشيري: (جعل هذه الأمة خيار الأمم، وجعل هذه الطائفة خيار هذه الأمة، فهم خيار الخيار. وكما أن هذه الأمة شهداء على الأمم في القيامة فهذه الطائفة هم المدار وهم القطب، وبهم يحفظ الله جميع الأمة. وكل مَن قبلته قلوبهم فهو المقبول، ومن ردَّته قلوبهم فهو المردود. فالحكم الصادق لفراستهم، والصحيح حكمهم، والصائب نظرهم، عصم جميع الأمة من الاجتماع على الخطأ، وعصم هذه الطائفة من الخطأ في النظر والحكم والقبول والرد، ثم إن بناء أمرهم مستند إلى سنة الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم، فكل مَن لا يكون له اقتداء بالرسول فهو عندهم مردود، وصاحبه كلا شيء) . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-11","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى حكمة نسخ القبلة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-13","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"... وَما جَعَلْنَا الْقِبْلَةَ الَّتِي كُنْتَ عَلَيْها إِلاَّ لِنَعْلَمَ مَنْ يَتَّبِعُ الرَّسُولَ مِمَّنْ يَنْقَلِبُ عَلى عَقِبَيْهِ وَإِنْ كانَتْ لَكَبِيرَةً إِلاَّ عَلَى الَّذِينَ هَدَى اللَّهُ وَما كانَ اللَّهُ لِيُضِيعَ إِيمانَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِالنَّاسِ لَرَؤُفٌ رَحِيمٌ (143)","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-14","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"قلت: (جعل) تصييرية، و (القبلة) مفعول أول، و (التي) صفة للمفعول الثاني المحذوف، أي: وما جعلنا القبلة الجهة التي كنت عليها وهي بيت المقدس، ثم وجهناك إلى الكعبة إلا لنعلم الثابت على الإيمان من غيره، أو: وما صيّرنا القبلة الجهة التي كنت عليها بمكة وهي الكعبة، فإنه كان- عليه الصلاة والسلام- يصلي إليها بمكة.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-15","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"وقيل: كان يستقبل بيت المقدس ويجعل الكعبة بينه وبينها، كما قال ابن عباس، و (إن) مخففة، واللام فارقة.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-16","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"أي: وإنه، أي: الأمر والشأن: كانت التحويلة لشاقة على الناس، والرأفة: شدة العطف، فهي أبلغ من الرحمة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-17","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وما نسخنا حكم القبلة وجعلناها الجهة التي كنت عليها بمكة دون التي كانت بالمدينة، وهي بيت المقدس، إِلَّا لِنَعْلَمَ علم ظهور وشهادة مَنْ يَتَّبِعُ الرَّسُولَ فى التحول إليها مِمَّنْ يَنْقَلِبُ عَلى عَقِبَيْهِ لضعف إيمانه وقلة إيقانه، فإن التحويلة عن القبلة الأولى والرجوع عنها إلى الثانية شاق على النفوس، إلا مَن سبقت له الهداية وحفت به الرعاية، فإنه يدور مع مراد الله أينما دار، ويتبع رسوله أينما سار. ومن مات قبل التحويل إلى الكعبة فإن الله لا يضيع أجر عمله وَما كانَ اللَّهُ لِيُضِيعَ إِيمانَكُمْ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-18","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"صلاتكم إلى بيت المقدس إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِالنَّاسِ لَرَؤُفٌ رَحِيمٌ.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-19","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"الإشارة: الخروج عن العادات وترك الأمور المألوفات كلاهما شاق على النفوس، إلا على الذين هدى الله، ولذلك كان خرق العوائد هو الفصل بين الخصوص والعموم، ومفتاح لمخازن العلوم والفهوم. فمن لم يخرق عوائد نفسه فلا يطمع أن يدخل حضرة قدسه. (كيف يخرق لك العوائد وأنت لم تخرق من نفسك العوائد) . وهو الميدان الذي تحقق به سير السائرين. (لولا ميادينُ النفوس ما تحقق سير السائرين) . وهو عند شيوخ التربية ميزان يتميز به من يتبع الرسول ويلزم طريقه إلى الوصول، ممن ينقلب على عقبيه، فمن رأوه خرق عوائد نفسه، وزهد في ملبسه وجنسه، تحققوا بدخوله حضرة قدسه، إلاّ مَن سبق له الحرمان والعياذ بالله من الخذلان، ومن رأوه وقف مع العادات، وركن إلى المألوفات، ومال إلى الرُّخَص والتأويلات، علموا أن مقامه مقام أهل الحجاب، يأخذ أجره من وراء الباب، ولا نصيب له في الدخول مع الأحباب.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-20","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"وأيضاً عند تخالف الآثار وتنقلات الأطوار، يظهر الإقرار من الإنكار. أهلُ الإقرار عارفون في كل حال، يدورون مع رياح الأقدار حيث سارت، ويسيرون معها حيث سارت، وأهل الإنكار جاهلون بالله في كل حال، معترضون عليه عند اختلاف الأحوال، نعوذ بالله من الضلال.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-21","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى كيفية ابتداء نسخ القبلة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-22","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"قَدْ نَرى تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّماءِ فَلَنُوَلِّيَنَّكَ قِبْلَةً تَرْضاها فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-23","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"قلت: التقلب: التردد، وولَّيْت كذا: جعلته والياً له، والشَّطْر هنا: الجهة.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-24","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لنبيه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- حين تمنى أن يُحَول إلى الكعبة، لأنها قبلة أبيه إبراهيم وأدْعى إلى إسلام العرب، وهي أقدم القبلتين، فكان ينظر إلى السماء، ويقلب وجهه فيها انتظاراً لنزول الوحْي، وهذا من كمال أدبه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- حيث انتظر ولم يطلب، فقال له الحق تعالى: قَدْ نَرى أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-25","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"ربما نرى تردد وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّماءِ انتظاراً للوحي، فلنعطينك ما تمنيت، ونوجهك إلى قبلة تَرْضاها وتحبها لمقاصد دينية وافقت المشيئة، واقتضتها الحكمة، فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ أي: اجعله موالياً شَطْرَ أي: جهة الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ. وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ أيها المؤمنون أي في أي مكان كنتم فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ جهته.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-26","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"وإنما ذكر الحق تعالى شطر المسجد، أي: جهته، دون عين الكعبة لأنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- كان في المدينة، والبعيد يكفيه مراعاة الجهة، فإن استقبال عينها حَرجٌ عليه، بخلاف القريب، فإنه يسهل عليه مسامتة العين ، وقيل: أن جبريل- عليه السلام- عيّنها له بالوحي فسميت قبلة وحْي.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-27","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"رُوِيَ أنه صلّى الله عليه وسلّم قدم المدينة فصلّى نحو بيت المقدس ستة عشر شهراً، ثم وُجِّه إلى الكعبة في رجب بعد الزوال قبل قتال بدر بشهرين، وقد صلّى بأصحابه في مسجد بني سلمة ركعتين من الظهر، فتحوّل في الصلاة، واستقبل الميزاب، وتبادل الرجال والنساء صفوفهم، فسُمي مسجد القبلتين. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-28","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"الإشارة: في الآية إشارة إلى أن ترك التصريح من كمال الأدب، وفي الحكم: «ربما دلهم الأدب على ترك الطلب، كيف يكون دعاؤك اللاحق سبباً في قضائه السابق؟! جل حكم الأزل أن يضاف إلى العلل» . فإذا تمنيت شيئاً وتوقفت على أمر فاصبر وتأدب واقتد بنبيك- عليه الصلاة والسلام- حتى يعطيك ما ترضى، أو يعوضك منها مقام الرضا. وفي المسألة كلام، والتحقيق أن ينظر إلى ما ينشرح به صدره في الوقت، فإن انشرح للدعاء دعا، وإن انقبض عن الدعاء سكت. والله يرزق من يشاء بغير حساب ولا علّة ولا أسباب.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-29","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"وإن شئت قلت: قد نرى فكرتك أيها العارف في سماء المعاني، غائباً في شهود الأواني، فلنولينك قبلة ترضاها، وتتلذذ بشهود جمالها وسناها، وهي الحضرة المطهرة التي هي صلاة القلوب، فولّ وجهك ووجهتك إلى تلك الحضرة، وحيثما كنت فولّ وجهك شطره، ودم على صلاة الفكرة والنظرة، فهي صلاة العارفين، ومنتهى أمل القاصدين، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-30","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"ولمّا تحوّلت القبلة إلى الكعبة غضبت اليهود، حيث ترك قبلتهم، مكابرة وعناداً، وقالوا: لو بقي على قبلتنا لرجونا أن يكون هو النبي المبعوث في آخر الزمان فنتبعه، فردَّ الله عليهم وكذبهم فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-30"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-143-144-32","r":"q2-143-144","title":"2:143–144 · The trial of a changed direction and the Prophet’s courtesy","text":"... وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ لَيَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُونَ (144)","anchor":"ar-q2-143-144-32"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-143-144-s1","r":"q2-143-144","title":"The appointed direction and the emphatic construction","text":"I say: jaʿala means to make one thing into another. “The prayer-direction” is its first object; “which you used to face” qualifies an omitted second object: We made the prayer-direction the direction you formerly faced—Jerusalem—then turned you to the Kaʿba, only to distinguish those steadfast in faith from others. Or: We made it the direction you faced in Mecca, the Kaʿba, for he prayed towards it there. Another account, from Ibn ʿAbbās, says he faced Jerusalem with the Kaʿba between him and it. In ( إن ) is the lightened emphatic particle; the lām distinguishes it from the negative. The sense is: the matter is that the change was hard for people. Tenderness ( الرأفة ) is intense compassion and therefore more emphatic than mercy. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-143-144-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-143-144-s2","r":"q2-143-144","title":"Knowledge made manifest and worship not lost","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: We changed the ruling of the prayer-direction back to the one you faced in Mecca rather than the Medinan direction, Jerusalem, only that We might know with a knowledge of manifestation and witnessing who follows the Messenger in the change and who turns back through weak faith and scant certainty. Moving from the first direction to the second is hard upon souls, except those for whom guidance has preceded and care surrounds them. They turn with God’s will wherever it turns and follow His Messenger wherever he goes. For anyone who died before the change to the Kaʿba, God does not lose the reward of his deeds. “God would not let your faith go to waste” means your prayer towards Jerusalem. God is deeply tender and merciful towards people.","anchor":"en-q2-143-144-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-143-144-s3","r":"q2-143-144","title":"Breaking habits as a test of following","text":"Leaving habits and familiar things is hard upon souls, except those whom God guides. Hence breaking habits distinguishes the elect from the generality and opens the treasuries of knowledge and understanding. Whoever has not broken his own habits should not hope to enter the holy presence. “How should ordinary patterns be broken for you when you have not broken your own habitual patterns?” This is the arena in which wayfarers’ journeys become real: “Were it not for the arenas of the lower selves, the wayfarers’ journey would not be realized.” For masters of formation it is a balance distinguishing one who follows the Messenger and adheres to his path of arrival from one who turns back. When they see someone break his soul’s habits and renounce attachment to his dress and his own social kind, they recognize his entry into the holy presence—unless deprivation has preceded for him; in God is refuge from abandonment. Whoever stops at habits, settles into familiar things and inclines to dispensations and accommodating interpretations remains among the veiled, receiving his wage from behind the door with no share in entering among the beloved. Changing effects and shifting conditions also distinguish affirmation from denial. Those who affirm know God in every state, turning and travelling with the winds of destiny. Those who deny remain ignorant in every state, objecting when conditions change. We seek God’s protection from error. The Real describes how the change of direction began: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:144a قَدْ نَرَىٰ تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّمَاءِ فَلَنُوَلِّيَنَّكَ قِبْلَةً تَرْضَاهَا فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ We have indeed seen your face turning towards heaven; We shall turn you towards a prayer-direction pleasing to you. Turn your face towards the Sacred Mosque. Wherever you are, turn your faces towards it.","anchor":"en-q2-143-144-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-143-144-s4","r":"q2-143-144","title":"Facing the direction of the House","text":"I say: turning ( التقلب ) is repeated movement. Wallaytuhu kadhā means I made him face it; shaṭr here means direction. The Real, glorious is His majesty, addresses His Prophet when he wished to turn towards the Kaʿba, the direction of his father Abraham, more conducive to the Arabs’ accepting Islam and older than Jerusalem’s direction. He looked towards heaven, turning his face in expectation of revelation. His waiting without asking is perfect courtesy. The Real says: We see, at times, your face turning towards heaven awaiting revelation. We shall grant what you desire and direct you to a prayer-direction you love for religious purposes agreeing with the divine will and required by wisdom. Turn your face towards the Sacred Mosque. Believers, wherever you may be, turn towards it. God mentions the mosque’s direction rather than the exact structure of the Kaʿba because the Prophet was in Medina. For someone distant, observing the direction suffices: exact alignment with the building would be burdensome, unlike for someone near. Another explanation says Gabriel identified it precisely through revelation, hence “a revealed prayer-direction.” It is related that after coming to Medina he prayed towards Jerusalem for sixteen months, then was turned to the Kaʿba after noon in Rajab, two months before Badr. He had prayed two units of the noon prayer with his companions in the mosque of Banū Salima when he turned during prayer, facing the waterspout; men and women exchanged rows. It was therefore named the Mosque of the Two Prayer-Directions. Thus al-Bayḍāwī. [B086]","anchor":"en-q2-143-144-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-143-144-s5","r":"q2-143-144","title":"Asking, waiting and the guidance of the moment","text":"The verse suggests that refraining from explicitly asking belongs to perfect courtesy. In the Ḥikam : “Courtesy may lead them to refrain from asking. How could your subsequent prayer cause His preceding decree? Exalted is the eternal judgement beyond attribution to causes!” When you wish for something or await an affair, be patient, observe courtesy and imitate your Prophet until God gives what pleases you or replaces it with the station of contentment. The question admits discussion. The precise approach is to consider what one’s breast opens to at the moment: if it opens to prayer, pray; if it contracts from prayer, remain silent. God provides whom He wills without reckoning, ground or means. Or say: We see your contemplation, gnostic, in the heaven of meanings, in a state of absence in the witnessing of vessels. [Translator’s note: Cairo I:178 reads غائباً في شهود الأواني, with fī (“in”), not ʿan (“from”). Ibn ʿAjība defines sensible forms as the vessels of inward meanings in Miʿrāj al-tashawwuf (ed. al-Khayyālī, p. 61). Absence can denote self-forgetful absorption, so witnessing such vessels need not be mere attachment to their outward forms. His discussions of Q6:103 (II:153) and Q7:143 (II:257) describe witnessing meanings behind the vessels and becoming absent from vessels by witnessing meanings. These clarify his vocabulary but do not settle the different local construction with “in.” The local sentence, however, does not explicitly say what the gnostic is absent from or how that absence relates to the vessels. The literal wording is retained; neither a different preposition nor substitution of “lights” is established.] [B088] We shall direct you towards a prayer-direction pleasing to you, delighting you through the sight of its beauty and radiance: the purified presence which is the hearts’ prayer. Turn your face and aspiration towards it wherever you are, and persist in the prayer of contemplation and vision. This is the gnostics’ prayer and the seekers’ ultimate hope. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-143-144-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-143-144-s6","r":"q2-143-144","title":"","text":"When the direction changed to the Kaʿba, the Jews angrily and obstinately objected to his leaving theirs: “Had he remained, we might have hoped he was the Prophet sent at the end of time, and followed him.” God refuted their assertion, saying:","anchor":"en-q2-143-144-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-145-147","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed 2:145–147","anchor":"unit-q2-145-147"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-1","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"وَلَئِنْ أَتَيْتَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ بِكُلِّ آيَةٍ مَّا تَبِعُوا قِبْلَتَكَ وَما أَنْتَ بِتابِعٍ قِبْلَتَهُمْ وَما بَعْضُهُمْ بِتابِعٍ قِبْلَةَ بَعْضٍ وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ أَهْواءَهُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ إِنَّكَ إِذاً لَمِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ (145) الَّذِينَ آتَيْناهُمُ الْكِتابَ يَعْرِفُونَهُ كَما يَعْرِفُونَ أَبْناءَهُمْ وَإِنَّ فَرِيقاً مِنْهُمْ لَيَكْتُمُونَ الْحَقَّ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ (146) الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ فَلا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِينَ (147)","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-2","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"قلت: (ولئن) اللام موطِّئة للقسم، و (إن) شرطية، و (أتيت) فعل الشرط، و (ما تبعوا) جواب القسم المحذوف سد مسد جواب الشرط. قال في الألفية:","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-3","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"واحذِف لَدَى اجتماع شرطٍ وقسمْ ... جوابَ ما أَخَّرْتَ فَهْوَ مُلْتَزَمْ","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-4","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ مِن أحبار اليهود لَيَعْلَمُونَ أن التحول إلى الكعبة حق مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ لِمَا يجدون في كتابهم أنه يصلي إلى القبلتين، وأن عادته تعالى تخصيص كل أمة بشريعة، وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُونَ من التعنت والعناد، وإنما يمهلهم ليوم المعاد، والله لئن أتيتهم بكل حجة وبرهان على صحة التوجه إلى الكعبة ما تَبِعُوا قِبْلَتَكَ لأنهم ما تركوا قبلتك لشبهة تُزيلُها الحجة، وإنما خالفوك مكابرة وعناداً. وقد طمعوا أن ترجع إلى قبلتهم، ولست بِتابِعٍ قِبْلَتَهُمْ أبداً، بل لهم قبلتهم صخرة بيت المقدس، وللنصارى قبلتهم مطلع الشمس، وليس بعضهم بِتابِعٍ قِبْلَةَ بَعْضٍ لتصلب كل حزب بما هو فيه، وإن كان على خطأ وفساد لأن مفارقة العوائد هنا صعب على النفوس إلا مَن سبقت له العناية.","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-5","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ أَهْواءَهُمْ الباطلة وآراءهم الزائفة فَرْضاً وتقديراً مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ الواضح والوحي الصحيح إِنَّكَ إِذاً لَمِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ، لكنك معصوم، فلا يتصور اتباعك لهم أبداً.","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-6","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"الَّذِينَ آتَيْناهُمُ الْكِتابَ أي: اليهود يَعْرِفُونَهُ أي: الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- وإن لم يتقدم ذكره لدلالة الكلام عليه أو القرآن أو التحويل، كَما يَعْرِفُونَ أَبْناءَهُمْ لا يشكُّون في صحة رسالته كما لا يشكون في معرفة أبنائهم. وعن عمر رضي الله عنه أنه سأل عبد الله بن سلام عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم فقال: (أنا أعلَمُ بِه مِنِّي بِابني، قال له: ولِمَ؟ قال: لأنِّي لستُ أشُكُّ في محمدٍ أنه نبيُّ الله. وأمَا ولَدِي فلعلَّ والدتَهُ قدْ خَانَتْ) .","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-7","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"وبعد حصول هذه المعرفة لهم جحدوه وكتموا صفته، إلاَّ مَن عصمه الله بالإيمان كعبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه- فقد كتم فريق منهم الحق وهم أحبارهم، وهم يعلمون أنه حق حسداً وعناداً.","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-8","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"هذا الذي أنت عليه يا محمد هو الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ، فَلا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِينَ أي: من الشاكين في أنه الحق، أو في كتمانهم الحق عالمين به. والخطاب مصروف للسامعين لا للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلّم لأنه غير متوقع منه، وإنما المراد تحقيق الأمر، وإنه بحيث لا يشك فيه ناظر، أو أمر الأمة باكتساب المعارف المزيحة للشك على الوجه الأبلغ. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-9","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"الإشارة: مما جرت به سُنة الله تعالى في خلقه أن أهل الحقيقة منكورون عند أهل الشريعة، أو تقول: علماء الباطن منكورون عند علماء الظاهر، يقابلونهم بالإذاية والإنكار، مع أنهم يعلمون أن الحقيقة حق من ربهم، وأن علم الباطن حق لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «إن من العلم كهيئة المكنون، لا يعلمه إلا العلماء بالله، فإذا سمعه أهل الغرة بالله أنكروه عليهم» . أو كما قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، وقال صلى الله عليه وسلّم: «لِكلِّ آيةٍ ظَاهرٌ وبَاطِنٌ وحَدٍّ ومَطْلَع» .","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-10","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُونَ فجزاؤهم الحرمان عن لذة الشهود والعيان، فيقال لأهل الباطن: ولئن أتيتهم بكل آية وبرهان ما تبعوا وجهتك التي توجهت إليها لأنها مَنُوطة بموت النفوس وحط الرؤوس ودفع الفلوس، وخرق العوائد لاكتساب الفوائد، ومفارقة الأوطان والغيبة عن الأهل والولدان، وما أنت أيها المريد بتابع وجهتهم التي توجهوا إليها، ولئن اتبعت أَهْوَاءَهُم مِّن بَعْدِ مَا ظهر لك من علم التحقيق: إنك إذاً لمن الظالمين لنفوسهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-11","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"الذين آتيناهم الكتابَ مِن علماء الشريعة يعرفون علم الحقيقة، كما يعرفون أبناءهم، أي: يقرون به في الجملة وينكرون وجود أهله مخصوصين، وقد يتحققون به ويكتمون الحق حسداً، وهم يعلمون وجود خصوصيته، فيقال","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-12","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"للعارف: هذا الذي أنت عليه من سلوك جادة الطريق، وعلم التحقيق، هو الحق من ربك فلا تكونن من الممترين إنك على الحق المبين.","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-145-147-13","r":"q2-145-147","title":"2:145–147 · Knowledge resisted and truth concealed","text":"ثم بين الحق تعالى قبلة من بعد عن مكة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-145-147-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-145-147-s1","r":"q2-145-147","title":"When an oath and condition coincide","text":"I say: in wa-laʾin , the lām prepares for an oath, in is conditional, “you brought” its verb, and “they would not follow” answers the omitted oath, also sufficing for the conditional response. In the Alfiyya : When condition and oath meet together, omit the response of whichever comes later: this is required.","anchor":"en-q2-145-147-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-145-147-s2","r":"q2-145-147","title":"A sign cannot remove deliberate resistance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the Jewish learned men know that the change to the Kaʿba is truth from their Lord, since their Book describes the Prophet praying towards two directions, and God habitually appoints a distinct Law for each community. God is not unaware of their resistance; He only gives them respite until the Day of Return. By God, if you brought them every argument and proof of the correctness of facing the Kaʿba, they would not follow it. They have not abandoned your direction through a doubt removable by evidence, but through obstinacy. They hoped you would return to theirs, but you never will. Theirs is Jerusalem’s rock, the Christians’ the sunrise; neither follows the other’s direction, each party rigidly fixed in its own position, however mistaken. Leaving habits is hard upon souls unless divine care has preceded. Were you hypothetically to follow their false desires and corrupt opinions after receiving clear knowledge and sound revelation, you would be among the wrongdoers. But you are protected, so following them is inconceivable. Those given the Book recognize him—the Messenger, although not expressly named beforehand, since the context indicates him—or the Qurʾān, or the change of direction—as they recognize their sons. They no more doubt his true messengership than their knowledge of their sons. ʿUmar asked ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām about the Messenger, and he replied: “I know him better than my son.” Asked why, he said: “I have no doubt that Muḥammad is God’s prophet, whereas my son’s mother might have been unfaithful.” After attaining this knowledge they denied him and concealed his description, except those whom God protected through faith, such as Ibn Salām and his companions. A group—their learned men—knowingly concealed truth through envy and resistance. What you follow, Muḥammad, is truth from your Lord; do not doubt its truth or their knowing concealment. The address actually turns to the hearers, not the Prophet, from whom doubt is not expected. Its purpose is to establish the matter as beyond a discerning person’s doubt, or most emphatically to command the community to acquire knowledge that dispels uncertainty. Thus al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q2-145-147-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-145-147-s3","r":"q2-145-147","title":"The cost of following inward realization","text":"God’s customary way is that people of Reality are denied by people restricted to the Law—or say, inward scholars by outward scholars—who meet them with harm and denial, although knowing Reality and inward knowledge to be true. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Some knowledge is like a hidden treasure, known only to those who know God; when people deluded about God hear it, they deny its possessors”—or words to that effect. He also said: “Every verse has an outward, an inward, a limit and a point of ascent.” [B087] God is not unaware of what they do. Their recompense is deprivation of the sweetness of witnessing and direct vision. Inward people are told: even if you brought every sign, they would not follow your orientation, for it depends on the death of the lower selves, lowering heads, relinquishing money, breaking habits to gain benefits, leaving homelands and becoming absent from family and children. Nor, disciple, will you follow their orientation. Were you to follow their desires after the knowledge of realization has appeared to you, you would wrong yourself. The scholars of the Law given the Book know the science of Reality as they know their sons: they acknowledge it generally while denying particular possessors. They may recognize it fully but conceal the truth through envy, knowing its special distinction exists. The gnostic is told: what you follow—the clear course and the knowledge of realization—is truth from your Lord. Do not doubt that you stand upon manifest truth.","anchor":"en-q2-145-147-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-145-147-s4","r":"q2-145-147","title":"","text":"The Real explains the direction for someone far from Mecca:","anchor":"en-q2-145-147-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-148-149","r":"q2-148-149","title":"2:148–149 · Every direction and the race towards good","text":"2:148–149 · Every direction and the race towards good 2:148–149","anchor":"unit-q2-148-149"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-148-149-1","r":"q2-148-149","title":"2:148–149 · Every direction and the race towards good","text":"وَلِكُلٍّ وِجْهَةٌ هُوَ مُوَلِّيها فَاسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْراتِ أَيْنَ مَا تَكُونُوا يَأْتِ بِكُمُ اللَّهُ جَمِيعاً إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (148) وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ وَإِنَّهُ لَلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ (149)","anchor":"ar-q2-148-149-1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-148-149-s1","r":"q2-148-149","title":"The one who turns and the one who is directed","text":"I say: the nunation of “each” substitutes for an omitted expression: each community has a prayer-direction, or each group of Muslims has a direction and side of the Kaʿba. “A direction” is the subject; the preceding prepositional phrase is its predicate. “He” is a subject and “turns towards it” its predicate, with an underlying shortened form. Wallā takes two objects, one omitted here: he turns his face towards it, if “he” refers to the omitted community or group. Alternatively, it refers to God: God directs it towards that person, making it face him when he faces its direction. Ibn ʿĀmir reads the passive huwa muwallāhā ( هو مُوَلّاها ). Its deputy-agent is a pronoun referring to “he,” originally the first object; the second becomes the attached genitive for lightness. The sense is “he is directed towards it.”","anchor":"en-q2-148-149-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-148-149-s2","r":"q2-148-149","title":"Good deeds before the arrival of death","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: each group of Muslims has a side of the Kaʿba to face wherever it may be. Multiply prayers and hasten towards good before the destroyer of pleasures descends. Wherever you are, in the earth’s east or west, death comes and brings you to the gathering barefoot and naked. Only righteous deeds and good acts sent ahead benefit you then. God has power over everything: neither resurrecting servants nor gathering them from the earth’s depths and distant regions incapacitates Him. Knowing that each people has a direction, wherever you set out from or settle, turn your face towards the Sacred Mosque. By God, this is truth from your Lord, so hasten to obey. God is not unaware of good or evil deeds and requites each for what he sent ahead. The Real repeats the command for another reason: wherever you set out from, face the Sacred Mosque, and wherever you settle, turn towards it. Al-Bayḍāwī says the ruling is repeated because its reasons are multiple. Three are given for the change: honouring the Messenger by seeking what pleases him; the divine custom of assigning every religious community and bearer of a mission a distinguishing direction; and removing opponents’ arguments. Each reason is joined to its corresponding ruling. Moreover, the prayer-direction is weighty, and abrogation can occasion trial and doubt; emphatic repetition is therefore fitting.","anchor":"en-q2-148-149-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-148-149-s3","r":"q2-148-149","title":"","text":"He states the third reason, removing opponents’ arguments:","anchor":"en-q2-148-149-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-150","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction 2:150","anchor":"unit-q2-150"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-1","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-150-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-2","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"قلت: التنوين فى (لكل) تنوين العوض، أي ولكل أمة قبلة، أو لكل قوم من المسلمين جهة وجانب من الكعبة، و (وجهة) مبتدأ، والخبر: المجرور قبله. و (هو) مبتدأ، و (موليها) خبر مقصور، و (ولّى) يتعدى إلى مفعولين، وهو هنا محذوف، أي: موليها وجهه إن كان الضمير يعود على المضاف المحذوف، ويحتمل أن يعود على الله تعالى، أي: الله تعالى موليها إياه، أي: يجعلها موالية له إن استقبل جهتها.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-3","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"وقرأ ابن عامر: (هو مُوَلاَّها) بالبناء للمفعول، فالنائب ضمير يعود على (هو) ، وهو المفعول الأول، والثاني:","anchor":"ar-q2-150-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-4","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"المضاف إليه تخفيفا، وأصله: مولى إياها، أي مصروفاً إليها.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-5","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولكل فريق من المسلمين جهة من الكعبة يستقبلها ويوليها وجهه، أينما كان وحيثما حل، فأكثروا من الصلوات، واستقبلوا الخيرات قبل هجوم هادم اللذات، أَيْنَما تَكُونُوا في مشارق الأرض ومغاربها، يأتكم الممات، ويأت بكم إلى المحشر حُفاة عراة، ولا ينفعكم حينئذ إلا صالح عمل قدمتوه، أو فعل خير أسلفتموه، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ","anchor":"ar-q2-150-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-6","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"، فلا يعجزه بعث العباد، ولا جمعهم من أعماق الأرض وأقطار البلاد. وإذا علمت أن لكل قوم جهة يستقبلونها، فمن حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ وفي أي مكان حللت فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ، والله إِنَّهُ لَلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ فبادر إلى امتثاله، وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ من خير أو شر، فيجازي كل واحد على ما أسلف.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-7","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"ثم كرّر الحق تعالى الأمر بالتوجه إلى الكعبة لعلة أخرى سيذكرها، فقال: وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ وحيثما حللتم فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ. قال البيضاوي: كرر هذا الحكم لتعدد علله، فإنه تعالى ذكر للتحول ثلاث علل: تعظيم الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم بابتغاء مرضاته، وَجَرت العادة الإلهية على أن يُولِّي أهل كل ملة وصاحب دعوة وجهة يستقبلها ويتميز بها، ودفع حجج المخالفين على ما بينه، وقرن كل علة بمعلولها، مع أن القبلة لها شأن، والنسخ من مظان الفتنة والشبهة، فبالحَرِيِّ أن يُؤكد أمرها ويعاد ذكرها مرة بعد أخرى. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-8","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"ثم ذكر العلّة الثالثة وهي دفع حجج المخالفين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-150-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-10","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"... لِئَلاَّ يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَيْكُمْ حُجَّةٌ إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا مِنْهُمْ فَلا تَخْشَوْهُمْ وَاخْشَوْنِي وَلِأُتِمَّ نِعْمَتِي عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ (150)","anchor":"ar-q2-150-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-11","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"قلت: الاستثناء من (الناس) أي: لئلا يكون لأحد من الناس حجة عليكم إلا المعاندين منهم، و (لأتم) متعلق بمحذوف، أي: ولإتمام نعمتي عليكم وإرادة اهتدائكم أمرتكم بالتحول، أو معطوف على محذوف أي: واخشوني لأحفظكم ولأتم نعمتي عليكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-12","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وإنما أمرتكم بالتوجه إلى الكعبة دون الصخرة لتدفع حجج الناس، فإن اليهود ربما قالوا: المنعوت في التوراة قبلته الكعبة، وهذا يستقبل الصخرة، أو إن محمداً يخالف ديننا ويستقبل قبلتنا. والمشركون ربما قالوا: يدعي ملّة إبراهيم ويخالف قبلته، فأمرتكم باستقبال القبلة دفعاً لحجج الناس، إلا المعاندين منهم فلا ينقطع شغبهم، فإنهم يقولون: ما تحول إلى الكعبة إلا مَيلاً إلى دين قومه، وحبّاً لبلده، أو بَدَا له فرجع إلى قبلة آبائه، ويوشك أن يرجع إلى دينهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-13","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"فلا تخافوهم ولا تلتفتوا إلى مَطاعنهم، فإنها لا تضركم، وَاخْشَوْنِي أكْفكم شرهم، فإن مَن خافني خاف منه كل شيء، ومَن لم يخشني خاف من كل شيء، وأمرتكم أيضاً بالتوجه إلى قبلة جدكم لِأُتِمَّ نِعْمَتِي عَلَيْكُمْ بإقرار عين نبيكم، وإرادة اهتدائكم، فاشكروا ما أوليتكم، واذكروا ما به أنعمت عليكم أزدكم من فضلي وإحساني، وأسبغ عليكم إنعامي وامتناني.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-14","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"الإشارة: من حكمة المدبر الحكيم أن دبر ملكه العظيم، ووجه كل فرقة بوجهة من مصالح عباده، أفناه فيها وولاه إياها. فقوم اختصهم لمحبته واصطفاهم لحضرته وهم العارفون، وقوم أقامهم لخدمته وأفناهم في عبادته","anchor":"ar-q2-150-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-15","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"وهم العباد والزهاد، وقوم أقامهم لحمل شريعته وتمهيد دينه وهم العلماء العاملون، وقوم أقامهم لحفظ كتابه رسماً وتلاوة وتفهماً وهم القرّاء والمفسرون، قال تعالى: إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَحافِظُونَ، وقوم أقامهم لتسكين الفتن ودفع المظالم والمحن وهم الحكام ومَن يستعان بهم في تلك الوجهة، وقوم أقامهم لحفظ نظام الحكمة وهم القائمون بالأسباب الشرعية على اختلاف أنواعها وتعدد فروعها، وقوم أعدهم لظهور حلمه وعفوه فيهم وهم أهل المعاصي والذنوب، وقوم أعدهم للانتقام وظهور اسمه القهار وهم أنواع الكفار.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-16","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"فكل وجهة من هؤلاء توجهت لحق شرعي أقامتها القدرة فيه، وحَكم بها القضاء والقدر، إلا أن القسمين الأخيرين لا تقررهما الشريعة. فلو حسنت المقاصد لكان الكل عُمالاً لله، فيقال لهم: اسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْراتِ","anchor":"ar-q2-150-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-17","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"بتحسين المقاصد والنيات، وبادروا إلى الطاعات قبل هجوم هادم اللذات، أينما تكونوا يجمعكم للحساب، وتُعاينوا جزاء ما أسلفتم من عذاب أو ثواب، ومن حيث خرجت أيها العارف فولّ وجهتك وكليتك لمسجد الحضرة باستعمال الفكرة والنظرة، فإنها حق وما سواها باطل، كما قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-150-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-18","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"ألا كُلُّ شيء ما خلا الله باطل ... وكل نعيم لا مَحَالَةَ زائلُ","anchor":"ar-q2-150-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-19","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"وحيثما كنتم أيها العارفون فولّوا وجوهكم إلى قبلة تلك الحضرة، واعبدوا ربكم بعبادة الفكرة، فإنها صلاة القلوب، ومفتاح ميادين الغيوب، وفي ذلك يقول القائل :","anchor":"ar-q2-150-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-20","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"يَا قِبْلَتِي في صَلاَتِي ... إذَا وقَفْتُ أصَلِّي","anchor":"ar-q2-150-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-21","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"جَمَالُكم نُصْبَ عَيْنِي ... إليهِ وَجَّهْتُ كُلِّي","anchor":"ar-q2-150-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-22","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"فإذا تحققتم بهذه الحضرة، وتحصنتم بحصن الشهود والنظرة، انقطع عنكم حجج خصيم النفس والجنس، وتنزهتم في رياض القرب والأنس، إلا الخواطر التي تحوم على القلوب، فلا تقدح في مشاهدة الغيوب، فلا تخافوا غيري، ولا تتوجه همتكم إلا لإحساني وبرَّي فإني أتم عليكم نعمتي، وأرشدكم إلى كمال معرفتي، وأتحفكم بنصري ومعونتى.","anchor":"ar-q2-150-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-150-23","r":"q2-150","title":"2:150 · The many callings and the one inward direction","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى نعمة الواسطة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-150-23"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-150-s1","r":"q2-150","title":"The exception and the implied purpose","text":"I say: the exception is from “people”: let no one have an argument except the obstinate. “That I may complete” is attached to an omitted expression: I commanded the change to complete My blessing and will your guidance. Or it is conjoined to an omitted clause: fear Me that I may protect you and complete My blessing. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-06] ]","anchor":"en-q2-150-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-150-s2","r":"q2-150","title":"Arguments removed, obstinacy remaining","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: I commanded you to face the Kaʿba rather than the rock to remove people’s arguments. The Jews might say that the Prophet described in the Torah faces the Kaʿba, whereas this man faces the rock; or that Muḥammad opposes their religion but faces their direction. The polytheists might say that he claims Abraham’s religion while opposing his direction. Thus I commanded the change, except that the obstinate do not cease their contentiousness. They say he turned only from inclination towards his people’s religion and love of his homeland, or that he changed his mind and returned to his fathers’ direction and might soon return to their religion. Do not fear them or attend to their attacks: they do not harm you. Fear Me, and I will suffice you against them. Whoever fears Me is feared by everything; whoever does not fear Me fears everything. I also commanded your forefather’s direction to complete My blessing by delighting your Prophet and willing your guidance. Thank Me for what I have granted and remember My blessings: I will increase My favour and beneficence and pour My gifts upon you.","anchor":"en-q2-150-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-150-s3","r":"q2-150","title":"Different offices within the divine governance","text":"The Wise Governor’s wisdom includes ordering His great kingdom and assigning each group a service benefiting His servants, absorbing it in that work and entrusting it to it. Some He chooses for His love and presence: the gnostics. Some He establishes in service, absorbed in worship: the worshippers and renunciants. Some He establishes to bear His Law and consolidate His religion: the practising scholars. Some preserve His Book in writing, recitation and understanding: the reciters and commentators. “We sent down the Remembrance, and We preserve it” [15:9]. Some quiet disturbances and repel oppression and hardship: rulers and those assisting their work. Some preserve the order of wisdom: those undertaking lawful occupations in all their kinds and branches. Some are prepared for His forbearance and pardon to appear in them: the disobedient and sinful. Some are prepared for requital and the manifestation of His Name the All-Subduing: the different unbelievers. Each of these orientations is directed towards a task under the Sacred Law in which divine power has established it and which decree and destiny have determined, though the Sacred Law does not approve the last two categories. [B089] Were intentions good, all would be workers for God. They are told: vie in good by improving purposes and intentions, and hasten to obedience before death. Wherever you are, He gathers you for reckoning, and you see the punishment or reward for what you sent ahead. Wherever you set out from, gnostic, turn your orientation and whole being to the mosque of the Presence through contemplation and vision. It is truth, and what is other is false, as the poet says: Everything except God is false; every delight must inevitably pass away. Wherever you are, gnostics, turn towards that Presence’s direction and worship through contemplation: the prayer of hearts and key to the fields of unseen realities. As someone says: O my direction in prayer, when I stand to pray: Your beauty is before my eyes; towards it I turn my whole being. When you realize this presence and fortify yourselves in witnessing and vision, the arguments of the adversaries—the lower self and your own kind—are cut off. You walk in gardens of nearness and intimacy. Thoughts still hovering around hearts do not impair witnessing of unseen realities. Fear none but Me; direct your aspiration only towards My kindness and beneficence. I will complete My blessing, guide you to perfect knowledge of Me, and favour you with victory and assistance.","anchor":"en-q2-150-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-150-s4","r":"q2-150","title":"","text":"The Real mentions the blessing of the intermediary:","anchor":"en-q2-150-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-151-152","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance 2:151–152","anchor":"unit-q2-151-152"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-1","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"كَما أَرْسَلْنا فِيكُمْ رَسُولاً مِنْكُمْ يَتْلُوا عَلَيْكُمْ آياتِنا وَيُزَكِّيكُمْ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ الْكِتابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمْ ما لَمْ تَكُونُوا تَعْلَمُونَ (151) فَاذْكُرُونِي أَذْكُرْكُمْ وَاشْكُرُوا لِي وَلا تَكْفُرُونِ (152)","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-2","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"قلت: (كما) متعلق بأتم، أي: ولأتم نعمتي عليكم في شأن القبلة كما أتممتها عليكم بإرسال الرسول. أو باذكروني، أي: كما ذكرناكم بالإرسال، فاذكروني بالمقال والحال. وقدم هنا التزكية على التعليم، باعتبار القصد لأن القصد من الإرسال والتعليم هو التطهير، وأخره في دعوة إبراهيم باعتبار الفعل، لأن الإرسال والتعليم مقدم على التطهير، وأعاد العامل في قوله: وَيُعَلِّمُكُمْ ما لَمْ تَكُونُوا تَعْلَمُونَ إيذاناً بأنه جنس آخر شرفاً له.","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-3","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا عبادي اذكروا برّي وإحساني فقد أتممت عليكم نعمى وآلائي بإسعافكم في تحويل القبلة، كما أتممتها عليكم بأعظم النعم وأجلها، وهو إرسال من يعلمكم رَسُولًا مِنْكُمْ يَتْلُوا عَلَيْكُمْ آياتِنا الموصلة إلى حضرتنا، ويطهركم من المساوئ والعيوب، وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ الْكِتابَ المشتمل على علم الغيوب ودواء القلوب، ويعلمكم الْحِكْمَةَ وهي الشريعة المطهرة والسنّة النبوية، وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ علوماً غيبية لم يكن لكم بها علم ولا معرفة، فَاذْكُرُونِي بالطاعة والإحسان أَذْكُرْكُمْ بالثواب ونعيم الجنان. قال صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: «مَن أطَاعَ الله فقدْ ذكَرَ الله، وإنْ قَلَّتْ صَلاتُه وصيَامُهُ وتِلاوتُه القرآن. ومَنْ عَصيَ اللهَ فَقَدْ نَسِيَ الله، وإنْ كَثُرتْ صَلاتُهُ وصَيَامُهُ وتِلاوَتُه» .","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-4","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"أو فاذكروني بالجَنَانِ أذكركم بنعمة الشهود والعيان، أو فاذكروني بالقلوب أذكركم بكشف الحجب، أو فاذكروني بالتوحيد والإيمان أذكركم بالدرجات في الجنان. قال الصّديق رضي الله عنه: (كفَى بالتوحيدِ عبَادةً، وكَفَى بالجنةِ ثَواباً) . أو فاذكروني بالشكر أذكركم بالزيادة، أو فاذكروني على ظهر الأرض أذكركم في بطنها. قال الأصمعي:","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-5","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"(رأيت أعرابيّاً واقفاً يوم عرفة بعرفات، وهو يقول: إلهي عَجَّتْ لكَ الأصْواتُ بضُروب اللغات يسألونك الحَاجَات، وحاجَتي إليكَ أنْ تَذْكُرني عندَ البلاَءِ إذا نَسِيَني أهلُ الدنيا) .","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-6","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"أو: فاذكروني في الدنيا أذكركم في العقبى، أو: فاذكروني بالطاعات أذكركم بالمعافاة، يعني يحييه حياة طيبة. أو: فاذكروني في الخلاء والملأ أذكركم في أفضل الملأ، دليله الحديث: «أنا عِندَ ظنِّ عبدي بي فليُظنَّ بي","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-7","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"مَا شاء، وأنا معه إذا ذكَرني، فمن ذَكَرَنيِ في نَفْسِه ذَكَرْتُه في نَفْسِي. ومن ذَكَرَنِي في مَلأ ذَكرْتُه في مَلأ خير من مَلَئِهِ..» الحديث.","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-8","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"أو: فاذكروني في النعمة والرخاء أذكركم في الشدة والبلاء، أو: فاذكروني بالتسليم والرضا أذكركم بحسن التدبير ولطف القضاء، وَمَنْ يَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ فَهُوَ حَسْبُهُ أو: فاذكروني بالشوق والمحبة أذكركم بالوصال والقربة. أو: فاذكروني بالتوبة أذكركم بغفران الحوبة، أو: فاذكروني بالدعاء أذكركم بالعطاء، أو: فاذكروني بالسؤال أذكركم بالنوال، إلى غير ذلك مما لا ينحصر.","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-9","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"واعلم أن الذكر ثلاثة أنواع: ذكر اللسان فقط وهو ذكر الغافلين ، وذكر اللسان والقلب وهو ذكر السائرين، وذكر القلب فقط، وهو ذكر الواصلين، والذكر هو أفضل الأعمال كما تقتضيه الأحاديث النبوية والآيات القرآنية، وهو أقرب الطرق الموصلة إلى الله تعالى، إذا كان بشيخ كامل، واعلم أن الذكر على أنواع كثيرة من تهليل وتكبير وتسبيح وحَمْدَلَةٍ وحَسْبَلَةٍ وحوقلة وصلاة على رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم، ولكلِّ خاصيةٌ وثمرة، وتجتمع في ذكر المفرد، وهو:","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-10","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"الله، الله. فإن ثمرته الفناء في الذات، وهي الغاية والمنتهى. انظر ابن جزي.","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-11","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"قال الحقّ تعالى: واشكروا لي ما أوليتكم من إحساني وبرّي بأن تنسبوها لي لا لغيري، ولا تجحدوا إحساني فأسلبكم ما خولتكم من إنعامي.","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-12","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"الإشارة: كما أنعم الله على الأمة المحمدية بأن بعث فيهم رسولاً منهم يعلمهم الشريعة النبوية، ويطهرهم من شهود الغيرية، ويعلمهم العلوم اللدنية، كذلك منَّ الله تعالى على عباده من هذه الأمة في كل زمان، ببعث شيوخ التربية يطهرون الناس من العيوب، ويدخلونهم حضرة الغيوب، ويطلعونهم على شهود القدرة الأزلية والحكمة الإلهية، ويعلمهم من غرائب العلوم، ويفتح لهم مخازن الفهوم، فَيَطَّلعون على السر المصون، ويعلمون ما لم يكونوا يعلمون، فيقول لهم الحقّ جلّ جلاله: اذكروني بأرواحكم وأسراركم، أذكركم بالغيبة عن رؤية أشباحكم، اذكروني بالفكرة والنظرة أمتعكم بدوام شهود الحضرة، واشكروا لي آلائي وبرّي، ولا تكفروا بالركون إلى غيري فإني أسلبكم من مزيد معونتى ونصرى.","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-151-152-13","r":"q2-151-152","title":"2:151–152 · The messenger’s teaching and the degrees of remembrance","text":"ولمّا أمر عباده بالشكر أمرهم بمقام الصبر لأنه أخوه في ضده إذ الشكر في النعمة والصبر فى البلية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-151-152-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-151-152-s1","r":"q2-151-152","title":"Purification as purpose and as result","text":"I say: “just as” is attached to “complete”: I complete My blessing in the prayer-direction as I completed it by sending the Messenger. Or it attaches to “remember Me”: as We remembered you through sending, remember Us through speech and state. Purification precedes teaching here according to the intended purpose, since purification is the aim of sending and teaching. It follows teaching in Abraham’s prayer [2:129] according to the order of execution, since sending and teaching precede purification. The governing verb is repeated in “teaches you what you did not know” to indicate and honour a different kind of knowledge.","anchor":"en-q2-151-152-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-151-152-s2","r":"q2-151-152","title":"The many correspondences of remembrance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: My servants, remember My kindness and beneficence. I completed My gifts by granting the change of direction, just as I completed them through the greatest blessing: sending a messenger of your own to teach you. He recites Our signs leading to Our presence, purifies faults, teaches the Book containing knowledge of unseen things and medicine for hearts, teaches wisdom—the purified Law and Prophetic Sunna—and teaches unseen sciences previously unknown to you. Remember Me through obedience and beneficence; I remember you through reward and the bliss of gardens. The Prophet said: “Whoever obeys God remembers Him, even with little prayer, fasting and Qurʾān recitation; whoever disobeys Him forgets Him, even with much prayer, fasting and recitation.” [B090] Or: remember Me with your inward heart, and I remember you through witnessing and direct vision; remember Me with hearts, and I unveil the curtains; remember Me through unity and faith, and I remember you through degrees in Paradise. Al-Ṣiddīq said: “Unity suffices as worship; Paradise suffices as reward.” Or: remember Me with gratitude, and I remember you with increase; remember Me upon the earth, and I remember you within it. Al-Aṣmaʿī saw a Bedouin standing at ʿArafāt on the Day of ʿArafa, saying: “My God, voices cry to You in different tongues, asking their needs. My need is that You remember me in affliction when the people of the world forget me.” Or: remember Me in this world, and I remember you in the next; remember Me through obedience, and I remember you through well-being—a good life. Remember Me in solitude and in company, and I remember you in a better company. The proof is the hadith: “I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let him think as he will. I am with him when he remembers Me. If he remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself; if he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a better gathering.” Or: remember Me in blessing and ease, and I remember you in hardship and affliction; remember Me through surrender and contentment, and I remember you through good ordering and a gentle decree: “Whoever relies on God, He suffices him” [65:3]. Remember Me through longing and love, and I remember you through union and nearness; through repentance, and I forgive offences; through prayer, and I give; through asking, and I bestow—besides correspondences without limit.","anchor":"en-q2-151-152-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-151-152-s3","r":"q2-151-152","title":"Three modes and many forms of remembrance","text":"Know that remembrance is of three kinds: tongue alone, the remembrance of the heedless; tongue and heart, that of wayfarers; and heart alone, that of those who have arrived. Remembrance is the best of deeds, as Prophetic hadiths and Qurʾānic verses indicate, and the nearest path leading to God when practised with a perfected shaykh. It has many forms: declaring unity ( التهليل ), magnifying God ( التكبير ), glorifying Him ( التسبيح ), praising Him ( الحمدلة ), declaring His sufficiency ( الحسبلة ), declaring that power and strength are only through Him ( الحوقلة ), and blessing the Messenger. Each has a property and fruit. They are gathered in remembrance of the single Name ( ذكر المفرد ): “God, God” ( الله، الله ). Its fruit is effacement in the Essence, the final end. Consult Ibn Juzayy. The Real says: thank Me for My kindness and beneficence by attributing them to Me, not another. Do not deny My goodness, lest I withdraw the gifts I entrusted to you.","anchor":"en-q2-151-152-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-151-152-s4","r":"q2-151-152","title":"The continuing work of Prophetic formation","text":"As God blessed the Muḥammadan community with a messenger of its own who teaches Prophetic Law, purifies them of witnessing otherness and imparts divinely bestowed sciences, so in every time He favours this community with masters of formation. They purify faults, bring people into the unseen presence, disclose witnessing of eternal power and divine wisdom, teach wondrous sciences and open treasuries of understanding. People perceive the guarded secret and learn what they did not know. The Real tells them: remember Me through spirits and secrets; I remember you through absence from seeing your bodily forms. Remember Me through contemplation and vision; I give abiding witnessing of the Presence. Thank Me for My gifts and kindness; do not deny Me by resting upon another, lest I withdraw increased assistance and victory.","anchor":"en-q2-151-152-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-151-152-s5","r":"q2-151-152","title":"","text":"Having commanded gratitude, He commands patience, its companion in the opposite condition: gratitude in blessing, patience in affliction.","anchor":"en-q2-151-152-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-153-157","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God 2:153–157","anchor":"unit-q2-153-157"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-1","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اسْتَعِينُوا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلاةِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ (153) وَلا تَقُولُوا لِمَنْ يُقْتَلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْواتٌ بَلْ أَحْياءٌ وَلكِنْ لا تَشْعُرُونَ (154) وَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ بِشَيْءٍ مِنَ الْخَوْفِ وَالْجُوعِ وَنَقْصٍ مِنَ الْأَمْوالِ وَالْأَنْفُسِ وَالثَّمَراتِ وَبَشِّرِ الصَّابِرِينَ (155) الَّذِينَ إِذا أَصابَتْهُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ قالُوا إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّا إِلَيْهِ راجِعُونَ (156) أُولئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ صَلَواتٌ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْمُهْتَدُونَ (157)","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-2","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"قلت: (أحياء) و (أموات) خبران عن مبتدأ مضمر، والابتلاء هو الاختبار، حيثما ورد في القرآن، ومعناه في حقه تعالى: أنه يظهر في الوجود ما في علمه لتقوم الحجة على العبد، وليس كاختبار الناس بعضهم بعضاً لأن الله علم ما كان وما يكون، والصلاة هنا المغفرة والتطهير، والرحمة: اللطف والإحسان.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-3","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اسْتَعِينُوا على نيل رضواني وبرِّي وإحساني بِالصَّبْرِ على مشاق الطاعات وترك المعاصي والهفوات، وبالصلاة التي هي أم العبادات، ومحل المناجاة ومعدن المصافاة، فيها تشرق شوارق الأنوار، وتتسع ميادين الأسرار، وهي معراج أرواح المؤمنين ومناجاة رب العالمين، فإن تجرعتم مرارة الصبر فإن اللَّهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ، وأعظم مواطن الصبر عند مفارقة الأحباب، وذهاب العشائر والأصحاب، فإن كان موتهم في الجهاد فلا ينبغي لأجلهم أسف ولا نكاد لأنهم أَحْياءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ، وكذلك من ألحق بهم من ذي هَدْم وغَرَق وحرق ونفاسٍ وطاعون، فلا تقولوا لمن يقتل فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ من هؤلاء: هم أَمْواتٌ، بَلْ هم أَحْياءٌ حياة روحانية لا بشرية، وَلكِنْ لا تَشْعُرُونَ بحياتهم لأنهم مجرد أرواح، وأنتم قد لبستم طلسم الأشباح، فاختفى عنكم مقام الأرواح، وكذلك أرواح المؤمنين كلهم أحياء.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-4","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"وإنما خصّ الشهداء لمزيد بهجة وكرامة. وإجراء رزقهم عليهم دون غيرهم، ففي الحديث: «أرْواحُ الشُّهَداءِ في حَواصِل طَيرٍ خضرٍ تَعَلقُ من ورق الجنة» . أي: تأكل، وفي حديث آخر: «يَخْلُقُ اللهُ الشهداءَ جُسوماً على صُورةٍ طيرٍ خُضرٍ، فتكونُ في حَواصِلهَا، فَتسْرحُ بِها في الجَنة، وتأكلُ مِنْ ثمارِها، وتنالُ مِنْ خَيراتِها ونَعِيمها، حتى تُحشرَ مِنها يومَ القِيامَةِ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-5","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"ولا يدخل الجنة أحد غيرهم إلى ميقاتها إلا الصدِّيقون، وهم العارفون، فهم أعظم من الجميع لمزيد تصرف وإدراك وسعة روح وريحان، وتحقق شهود وعيان، فهم في نعيم الجنان كالشهداء، لكن الصديقين غير محصورين في حواصل الطيور، بل لهم هياكل وصور سرحوا بها حيث شاءوا. وكذلك من فوقهم من الأنبياء والرسل، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-6","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"ثم قال الحق جلّ جلاله: ولنختبركم يا معشر المسلمين بِشَيْءٍ قليل مِنَ الْخَوْفِ لهيجان العدو وصولة الكفار، وَالْجُوعِ لغلاء الأسعار وقلة الثمار، وَنَقْصٍ مِنَ الْأَمْوالِ بموت الحيوان وتعذر التجارة أو الخسران، وَالْأَنْفُسِ بالموت في الجهاد، وَالثَّمَراتِ بذهابها بالجوائح.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-7","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"وعن الشافعي رضي الله عنه (الخوفُ خوفُ الله، والجوعُ صومُ رمضان، والنقصُ من الأموال بالزكوات والصدقات، ومن الأنفسُ بالأمراض، ومن الثمرات مَوتُ الأولاد) . وعن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «إذا ماتَ ولَدُ العبد قال اللهَ للملائكةِ:","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-8","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"أقَبَضْتُمْ ولَدَ عَبدي؟ فيقولون: نَعَم. فيقولُ اللهُ تعالى: أقبضتم ثمرة قلبه؟ فيقولون: نعم. فيقول اللهُ تعالى: ماذا قال؟","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-9","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"فيقولون: حَمِدَك واستَرْجَع، فيقول الله تعالى: ابْنُوا لعَبْدِي بَيْتاً في الجَنَّةِ وسَمُّوه بَيْتَ الحمدِ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-10","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"وَبَشِّرِ الصَّابِرِينَ يا من تتأتَّى منه البشارة الَّذِينَ إِذا أَصابَتْهُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ في بدن أو أهل أو مال أو صاحب قالُوا إِنَّا لِلَّهِ ملكاً وعبيداً يحكم فينا بما يريد، وَإِنَّا إِلَيْهِ راجِعُونَ فيجازينا بما لا عين رأت، ولا أُذن سمعت، ولا خطر على قلب بشر، فتغيب مصائب الدنيا في جانبه.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-11","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"وفي الحديث: «من أصابته مُصيبةٌ فقال: إنَّا لله وإنّا إليه راجعُون. اللهم أجُرْنِي في مُصيبَتِي واخْلُفْ لي خَيْراً منها، إلا أَخْلَفَ الله له خيراً مما أصابه» قالت أم سَلَمَة: فلما ماتَ زوجي أبو سَلَمَة قلتَ ذلك، فأبدلني الله برسوله صلّى الله عليه وسلّم.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-12","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"أُولئِكَ الصابرون الراجعون إلى الله عَلَيْهِمْ صَلَواتٌ أي: مغفرة وتطهير مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-13","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"عطف ولطف وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْمُهْتَدُونَ لكل خير في الدنيا والآخرة.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-14","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"الإشارة: يا أيها الذين آمنوا بطريق الخصوص استعينوا على سلوك طريق حضرتنا ومشاهدة أنوار قدسنا بالصبر على ما تكره النفوس من ترك الحظوظ والشهوات، والميل إلى العادات والمألوفات، وبالصلاة الدائمة وهي صلاة القلوب بالعكوف في حضرة الغيوب. إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ بالمعونة والتأييد، وإشراق أنوار التوحيد، ولا تقولوا لمن ترونه قتل نفسه بالذل والافتقار، وخرق العوائد وخلع العذار: إنه قد مات، بل هو حي لا يموت، قال","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-15","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"الله تعالى: لا يَذُوقُونَ فِيهَا الْمَوْتَ إِلَّا الْمَوْتَةَ الْأُولى فإذا ماتت نفس المريد. واستوى عنده الذل والعز والمدح والذم، والغنى والفقر، والموت والحياة، فقد حييت روحه واتسع عليها فضاء الشهود، وتمتعت بالنظرة إلى الملك المعبود. فلا يزيدها الموت الحسيّ إلا اتصالاً وتمتعاً وشهوداً، فهي في الترقي أبداً سرمداً، ولكن لا تشعرون بما هم فيه في هذه الدار وفي تلك الدار.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-16","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"ويقال لهم عند إرادة سلوكهم الطريق إلى عين التحقيق: والله لنبلونكم يا معشر المريدين بشيء من إذاية الخلق وتضييق الرزق، وذهاب الأموال، وضعف الأبدان بالمجاهدة، وتأخير الفتح بظهور ثمرة المشاهدة ليظهر الصادق في الطلب بالثبوت في أحكام العبودية، حتى تشرق عليه أنوار الربوبية، من الكاذب بالرجوع إلى العوائد والشهوات، والركون إلى الرخص والتأويلات، وَبَشِّرِ الصَّابِرِينَ الثابتين في الطلب، بالظفر بكل ما أمَّلُوا، وبالوصول إلى ما إليه رحلوا، الذين إذا أصابتهم نكبة أو وقفة تحققوا بضعف العبودية، وتعلقوا بقوة الربوبية، فرجعوا إلى الله في كل شيء، فآواهم إليه من كل شيء، أولئك عليهم تَحنُّنٌ من ربهم وتقريب، وهم المهتدون إلى جوار الحبيب.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-17","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"قال ابن جزي: (فائدة) وَرَدَ ذكر الصبر في القرآن في أكثر من سبعين موضعاً وذلك لعظم موقعه في الدين، قال بعض العلماء: كل الحسنات لها أجر معلوم إلا الصبر، فإنه لا يحصر أجره لقوله تعالى: إِنَّما يُوَفَّى الصَّابِرُونَ أَجْرَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ. وذكر الله للصابرين ثمانياً من الكرامات:","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-18","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"أولها: المحبة، قال: وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الصَّابِرِينَ، والثاني: النصر: قال: إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ، والثالث: غرفات الجنة، قال: يُجْزَوْنَ الْغُرْفَةَ بِما صَبَرُوا، والرابع: الأجر الجزيل، قال: إِنَّما يُوَفَّى الصَّابِرُونَ أَجْرَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ والأربعة الأخرى المذكورة في هذه الآية، فمنها البشارة قال: وَبَشِّرِ الصَّابِرِينَ، والصلاة والرحمة والهداية قال: أُولئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ صَلَواتٌ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْمُهْتَدُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-19","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"والصبر على أربعة أوجه: صبر على البلاء، وهو منع النفس عن التسخط والهلع والجزع، وصبر على النعم، وهو تقييدها بالشكر وعدم الطغيان والتكبّر بها، وصبر على الطاعة بالمحافظة والدوام عليها، وصبر على المعاصي بكف النفس عنها. وفوق الصبر التسليم، وهو ترك الاعتراض والتسخط ظاهراً، وترك الكراهية باطناً، وفوق التسليم الرضا بالقضاء، وهو سرور النفس بفعل الله، وهو صادر عن المحبة، وكل ما يفعل المحبوب محبوب. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-153-157-20","r":"q2-153-157","title":"2:153–157 · Patience, the life of the martyrs and return to God","text":"ولما ذكر الحق تعالى الكعبة، وأمر بالتوجه إليها، ناسب أن يذكر الصفا والمروة لقربهما منها ومشاركتهما لها في أمر الدين. وذلك أن الصحابة تحرجوا أن يطوفوا بهما لأن الصفا كان عليه صنم يقال له إِسَاف، وعلى المروة صنم يقال له نائلة، فخافوا أن يكون الطواف بينهما تعظيماً لهما، فرفع الله ذلك فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-153-157-20"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-153-157-s1","r":"q2-153-157","title":"Testing makes manifest what divine knowledge already encompasses","text":"I say: “alive” and “dead” are predicates ( خبران ) of an implied subject ( مبتدأ مضمر ). Wherever trial ( الابتلاء ) occurs in the Qurʾān it means testing. In relation to God Most High, its meaning is that He manifests in existence what is in His knowledge, so that the proof stands against the servant. It is not like people testing one another, for God knows what has been and what will be. Blessing ( الصلاة ) here means forgiveness and purification; mercy means gentleness and beneficence.","anchor":"en-q2-153-157-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-153-157-s2","r":"q2-153-157","title":"Prayer, perseverance and the life beyond bodily death","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: believers, seek help in attaining My good pleasure, kindness and beneficence through patience in the difficulties of obedience and in abandoning disobedience and lapses, and through prayer, the mother of acts of worship, the place of intimate converse and the mine of pure communion. In it the dawning lights shine and the fields of spiritual secrets expand. It is the ascent of believers’ spirits and their intimate converse with the Lord of the worlds. When you drink patience’s bitterness, God is with the patient. Among the greatest occasions for patience are parting from loved ones and losing kin and companions. If their death occurs in holy struggle, there should be neither sorrow nor distress on their account, for “they are alive with their Lord, provided for” [3:169]. The same applies to those joined to their rank: those who die beneath a collapsed building, through drowning or burning, in childbirth or of plague. Do not call those among them killed in God’s way dead: rather, they are alive with a spiritual, not an ordinary bodily, life. You do not perceive their life because they are spirits alone, whereas you are clothed in the talisman of bodily forms, and the station of spirits is hidden from you. Likewise all believers’ spirits are alive. Martyrs are singled out because of their additional joy and honour and the provision made to flow to them, unlike others. A report says: “The martyrs’ spirits are in the crops of green birds, feeding upon the leaves of the Garden”—that is, eating them. Another report says: “God creates for the martyrs bodies in the form of green birds. They are in their crops and range with them through the Garden, eating its fruits and enjoying its good things and delight, until they are raised from them on the Day of Resurrection.” [B091] No one else enters the Garden before its appointed time, except the utterly truthful ( الصديقون ), who are the gnostics. They are greater than all the others through their additional freedom of action and perception, their expansive repose and refreshment, and their realized witnessing and direct vision. Like the martyrs, they enjoy the Gardens’ bliss; unlike them, however, they are not confined within the crops of birds. They have forms and bodies in which they range wherever they wish. So too those above them, the prophets and messengers. And God Most High knows best. The Real then says: We shall test you, company of Muslims, with a little fear from the enemy’s rising and the unbelievers’ assault; hunger from high prices and scarce produce; loss of property through livestock dying, trade becoming difficult or business losses; loss of lives through death in holy struggle; and loss of fruits through disasters destroying them. Al-Shāfiʿī is reported to have said: “Fear means fear of God; hunger, the Ramadan fast; loss of property, obligatory and voluntary alms; loss of lives, illnesses; and loss of fruits, children’s deaths.” The Prophet is reported to have said: “When a servant’s child dies, God asks the angels, ‘Have you taken My servant’s child?’ They answer, ‘Yes.’ God asks, ‘Have you taken the fruit of his heart?’ They answer, ‘Yes.’ God asks, ‘What did he say?’ They answer, ‘He praised You and said that he belongs to You and returns to You.’ God says, ‘Build My servant a house in the Garden, and name it the House of Praise.’” [B092] Give glad tidings—you who can convey them—to the patient: those who, when calamity befalls their body, family, property or companion, say, “We belong to God,” as His possession and servants, over whom He rules as He wills; “and to Him we return,” so that He may reward us with what no eye has seen, no ear has heard and no human heart has conceived. Beside that reward, worldly afflictions disappear. A report says: “Whenever someone afflicted by a calamity says, ‘We belong to God, and to Him we return. O God, reward me in my calamity and replace it for me with something better,’ God gives him something better in its place.” Umm Salama said: “When my husband Abū Salama died, I said this, and God gave me His Messenger in his place.” [B093] Upon these patient ones, returning to God, are blessings—meaning forgiveness and purification—from their Lord, and mercy—meaning tenderness and gentleness. They are guided to every good in this world and the next.","anchor":"en-q2-153-157-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-153-157-s3","r":"q2-153-157","title":"The dying of self-will and the spirit’s abiding life","text":"You who believe in the path of the elect, seek help in travelling to Our presence and witnessing the lights of Our holiness through patience with what the lower selves dislike: abandoning their shares and desires, and their inclination to habits and familiar things. Seek help also through unceasing prayer, the prayer of hearts abiding in the presence of the unseen. God is with the patient through help, confirmation and the shining lights of unity. Do not say of someone whom you see put his lower self to death through abasement and need, breaking customary patterns and casting off restraint, “He has died.” Rather, he is alive and does not die. God Most High says: “They taste no death there except the first death” [44:56]. When the aspirant’s lower self dies, and abasement and honour, praise and blame, wealth and poverty, death and life become equal to him, his spirit comes alive. The space of witnessing opens wide before it, and it enjoys beholding the worshipped King. Bodily death only increases its union, enjoyment and witnessing. It ascends for ever and ever, though you do not perceive what these people experience in this abode or the other. [B094] When they intend to travel the path to the very source of realization, they are told: by God, We shall test you, company of aspirants, with something of people’s harm, restricted provision, loss of wealth, bodily weakness through spiritual struggle, and delay in the opening and the appearance of witnessing’s fruit. This distinguishes the one sincere in seeking—steadfast in the requirements of servanthood until lordship’s lights shine upon him—from the liar who returns to habits and desires and rests in concessions and accommodating interpretations. Give glad tidings to those patient and steadfast in seeking: they shall attain all they hoped for and arrive at that towards which they travelled. When a setback or standstill befalls them, they realize servanthood’s weakness and cling to lordship’s strength. They turn back to God in everything, and He shelters them with Himself from everything. Upon them are tenderness and nearness from their Lord; they are guided to the Beloved’s neighbourhood.","anchor":"en-q2-153-157-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-153-157-s4","r":"q2-153-157","title":"Four forms of patience, surrender and contentment","text":"Ibn Juzayy says, by way of a useful observation: patience is mentioned in the Qurʾān in more than seventy places because of its great importance in religion. A scholar said that all good deeds have a known reward except patience, whose reward cannot be bounded: “The patient will be paid their reward without reckoning” [39:10]. God mentions eight honours for the patient. The first is love: “God loves the patient” [3:146]. The second is support: “God is with the patient” [2:153]. The third is the Garden’s lofty chambers: “They are rewarded with the chamber because they were patient” [25:75]. The fourth is abundant reward: “The patient will be paid their reward without reckoning.” The remaining four occur in this passage: glad tidings, “Give glad tidings to the patient”; blessing, mercy and guidance, “Upon them are blessings and mercy from their Lord; it is they who are rightly guided.” Patience has four forms. Patience with affliction prevents the soul from resentment, panic and anguish. Patience with blessings binds them with gratitude and prevents arrogance and self-exaltation through them. Patience in obedience consists in preserving and continually practising it. Patience against sins restrains the self from them. Above patience is surrender ( التسليم ): abandoning outward objection and resentment, and inward aversion. Above surrender is contentment with the decree ( الرضا بالقضاء ), the soul’s joy in God’s action. This arises from love, for whatever the beloved does is beloved. Here ends his statement.","anchor":"en-q2-153-157-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-153-157-s5","r":"q2-153-157","title":"","text":"Having mentioned the Kaʿba and commanded people to face it, the Real appropriately mentions al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa, near it and joined to it in religious observance. The Companions hesitated to go between them because an idol named Isāf stood upon al-Ṣafā and another named Nāʾila upon al-Marwa. They feared that going between them might honour the idols. God removed that apprehension:","anchor":"en-q2-153-157-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-158","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion 2:158","anchor":"unit-q2-158"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-158-1","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"إِنَّ الصَّفا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعائِرِ اللَّهِ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ أَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِما وَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْراً فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ شاكِرٌ عَلِيمٌ (158)","anchor":"ar-q2-158-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-158-2","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"قلت: (الصفا) في أصل الوضع: جمع صفاة، وهي الصخرة الصلبة الملساء، يقال: صفاة وصفا، كحصاة وحصى، وقطاة وقطا، ونواة ونوى. وقيل: مفرد، وتثنيته: صفوان، وجمعه: أصفاء، و (المروة) مَا لاَنَ من الحجارة وجمعه مرو ومروات، كتمرة وتمر وتمرات. والمراد هنا جَبَلانِ بمكة، و (شعائر الله) : أعلام دينه، جمع شعيرة أو شعارة، والشعيرة: كل ما كان معلماً لقربان يُتقرب به إلى الله تعالى، من دعاء أو صلاة أو أداء فرض أو ذبيحة.","anchor":"ar-q2-158-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-158-3","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"والحج في اللغة: القصد، والعمرة: الزيارة، ثم غلباً شرعاً في العبادتين المخصوصتين.","anchor":"ar-q2-158-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-158-4","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"وقرأ الأخَوَان وخلف: (يَطّوعْ) بلفظ المضارع، مجزوم اللفظ، وهو مناسب لقوله (أن يطوف) ، أصله: يتطوع، أُدغمت التاء في الطاء لقرب المخرج، والباقون بلفظ الماضي، مجزوم المحل، وهو مناسب لقوله: (فمن حج البيت) . و (الجُناح) : الإثم، من جَنَحَ إذا مال، كأن صاحب الإثم مال عن الحق إلى الباطل، و (خيراً) : صفة لمصدر محذوف، أو على إسقاط الخافض.","anchor":"ar-q2-158-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-158-5","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الطواف بين الصَّفا وَالْمَرْوَةَ من معالم دينه ومناسك حجه، فَمَنْ قصد الْبَيْتَ للحج أو العمرة فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَطَّوَّفَ بينهما، ولا يضره الصنمان اللذان كانا عليهما في الجاهلية فإن الله محا ذلك بالإسلام، وَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ لله بخير من حج أو عمرة أو صلاة أو غير ذلك، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يشكر فعله ويجزل ثوابه. واختلف في حكمه، فقال مالك والشافعي: ركن لا يُجبر بالدم، وقال أبو حنيفة: فرض يجبر بالدم، وقال أحمد: سنة، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-158-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-158-6","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"الإشارة: الصفا والمروة إشارة إلى الروح الصافية والنفس اللينة الطيبة، فالاعتناء بتطهيرهما وتصفيتهما من معالم الطريق، وبهما يسلك إلى عين التحقيق، فمن قصد بيت الحضرة لحج الروح بالفناء في الذات، أو عمرة النفس بالفناء في الصفات، فلا جناح عليه أن يطوف بهما ويشرب من كأسهما، حتى يغيب عن حسّهما، ومن تطوّع خيراً ببذل روحه لله، والغيبة عنها في شهود مولاه، فإن الله يشكر فعله، وينشر فضله ويظهر خيره، ويتولى أمره، والله ذو الفضل العظيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-158-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-158-7","r":"q2-158","title":"2:158 · Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa: the rites and their inward allusion","text":"ولما ذكر الحق تعالى نسخ القبلة ردا على اليهود، والمنكرين للنسخ، رجع إلى معاتبتهم على كتمان الحق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-158-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-158-s1","r":"q2-158","title":"The two hills, ritual signs and voluntary goodness","text":"I say: al-ṣafā ( الصفا ), in its original usage, is the plural of ṣafāt , a hard, smooth rock: ṣafāt/ṣafā , like ḥaṣāt/ḥaṣā (“pebble/pebbles”), qaṭāt/qaṭā (“sandgrouse”) and nawāt/nawā (“date-stone/date-stones”). It is also said to be singular, with the dual ṣafwān and plural aṣfāʾ . Marwa means soft stone; its plurals are marw and marwāt , like tamra/tamr/tamarāt (“date/dates”). Here the two names denote two hills in Mecca. “God’s ritual signs” ( شعائر الله ) means the distinguishing marks of His religion. Shaʿāʾir is the plural of shaʿīra or shiʿāra . A shaʿīra is anything marking an offering by which one draws near to God: supplication, prayer, performance of an obligation or a sacrificial animal. In language, pilgrimage ( الحج ) means intending or making for something; the lesser pilgrimage ( العمرة ), visiting. In revealed usage they came predominantly to denote the two particular acts of worship. The two brothers and Khalaf read yaṭṭawwaʿ , an imperfect verb jussive in its expressed form ( مجزوم اللفظ ), corresponding to “that he go between them.” Its original form is yataṭawwaʿ : the tāʾ is assimilated to the ṭāʾ because their points of articulation are close. The others read a past tense, jussive in syntactic position ( مجزوم المحل ), corresponding to “whoever makes pilgrimage to the House.” [B095] Blame ( الجناح ) means sin, from janaḥa , “to incline,” as though the sinner inclined from truth to falsehood. “Good” qualifies an omitted verbal noun, or stands in the accusative through omission of a preposition ( إسقاط الخافض ).","anchor":"en-q2-158-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-158-s2","r":"q2-158","title":"A rite of pilgrimage and disagreement over its legal status","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: going between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa belongs to the signs of His religion and the rites of His pilgrimage. Whoever makes for the House for the greater or lesser pilgrimage incurs no blame in going between them. The two idols formerly upon them in pagan times do not harm him, for God effaced that through Islam. Whoever freely performs something good for God—a greater or lesser pilgrimage, prayer or another act—God appreciates his action and makes his reward abundant. There is disagreement over this rite’s ruling. Mālik and al-Shāfiʿī call it an integral pillar ( ركن ), not repairable by a sacrificial offering. Abū Ḥanīfa calls it an obligation ( فرض ) repairable by an offering. Aḥmad calls it a Sunna. And God Most High knows best. [B096]","anchor":"en-q2-158-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-158-s3","r":"q2-158","title":"Purifying spirit and soul","text":"Al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa allude to the pure spirit and the gentle, wholesome soul. Attending to their purification and refinement is among the Path’s signs; through them one travels to the very source of realization. Whoever makes for the House of the presence, for the spirit’s pilgrimage through effacement in the Essence or the soul’s lesser pilgrimage through effacement in the Attributes, incurs no blame in going round them and drinking their cup until he is absent from sensing them. Whoever freely does good by offering his spirit to God and becoming absent from it in witnessing his Master—God appreciates his action, spreads his excellence, manifests his goodness and takes charge of his affairs. God possesses tremendous bounty.","anchor":"en-q2-158-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-158-s4","r":"q2-158","title":"","text":"Having spoken of changing the prayer-direction in answer to the Jews and others denying abrogation, the Real returns to reproaching them for concealing the truth:","anchor":"en-q2-158-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-159-162","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge 2:159–162","anchor":"unit-q2-159-162"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-1","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْتُمُونَ ما أَنْزَلْنا مِنَ الْبَيِّناتِ وَالْهُدى مِنْ بَعْدِ ما بَيَّنَّاهُ لِلنَّاسِ فِي الْكِتابِ أُولئِكَ يَلْعَنُهُمُ اللَّهُ وَيَلْعَنُهُمُ اللاَّعِنُونَ (159) إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ تابُوا وَأَصْلَحُوا وَبَيَّنُوا فَأُولئِكَ أَتُوبُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَأَنَا التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ (160) إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَماتُوا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ أُولئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ وَالْمَلائِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِينَ (161) خالِدِينَ فِيها لا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذابُ وَلا هُمْ يُنْظَرُونَ (162)","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-2","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"قلت: الضمير في (فيها) : يعود على اللعنة أو النار، وإضمارها قبل الذكر تفخيماً لشأنها، وتهويلاً لأمرها.","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-3","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في شأن أحبار اليهود حيث كتموا صفة الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْتُمُونَ ما أنزلناه عليهم في كتابهم من صفة محمد- عليه الصلاة السلام- من الآيات الواضحات في شأنه، وبيان صفته وبلده وشريعته، وما يهدي إلى وجوب اتباعه، والإيمان به، مِنْ بَعْدِ ما بَيَّنَّاهُ لِلنَّاسِ في التوراة، أُولئِكَ الكاتمون يَلْعَنُهُمُ اللَّهُ ويطردهم عن ساحة رحمته، وَيَلْعَنُهُمُ الجن والإنس، وكل من يتأتى منه اللعن، كالملائكة وغيرهم. إِلَّا الَّذِينَ تابُوا من الكتمان، وكل ما يجب أن يتاب منه، وَأَصْلَحُوا ما أفسدوا من الدين بالتدارك، وَبَيَّنُوا ما كتموا فَأُولئِكَ أَتُوبُ عَلَيْهِمْ وأرحمهم وَأَنَا التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ أي: المبالغ في قبول التوبة وإفاضة الرحمة، وأما مَن مات على الكفر ولم يتب فأولئك عَلَيْهِمْ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ، ومن يُعْتَدّ بلعنته من الْمَلائِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِينَ خالدين في اللعنة أو في النار لا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذابُ ساعة، ولا هم يمهلون عنه، أو لا ينتظرون للاعتذار أو الفداء.","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-4","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"الإشارة: ما قيل في أحبار اليهود يقال مثله في علماء السوء من هذه الأمة، الذين ملكتهم جيفة الدنيا، وأسرهم الهوى، الذين يقبضون الرّشَا على الأحكام، فيكتمون المشهور الواضح، ويحكمون بشهوة أنفسهم، فأولئك يلعنهم اللاعنون، وفي ذلك يقول ابن المبارك- رحمه الله-:","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-5","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"وهل أفسد الدين إلا الملوك ... وأحبار سوء ورهبانها","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-6","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"وباعُوا النفوسَ ولم يَرْبَحُوا ... ولم تغْلُ في البَيْع أثْمَانُهَا","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-7","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"لقدْ رتعَ القومُ في جِيفَةٍ ... يَبِينُ لذِي العَقْلِ إنْتَانُهَا","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-8","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"وكان يحيى بن معاذ الرازي رضي الله عنه يقول لعلماء وقته: (يا معْشرَ العلماء، ديارُكم هَامَانيَّة، وملابِسُكُم قَارُونية، ومَرَاكِبُكُم فرعونية وولائمُكُمْ جالوتية، فأين السنّةُ المحمدية؟) . إلا مَن تاب وأصلح ما أفسد، وبيَّن ما كتم، فأولئك يتوب الله عليهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-9","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"تنبيه: العلم باعتبار وجوب إظهاره وكتمه على ثلاثة أقسام:","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-10","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"قسم يجب إظهاره، ومَنْ كَتَمَه دخل في وعيد الآية، وهو علم الشريعة الظاهرة، إذا تعيَّن على المسئول بحيث لم يُوجَد من يُفتِي في تلك النازلة.","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-11","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"وقسم يجب كتمه، وهو علم سرّ الربوبية، أعني التوحيدَ الخاص، فهذا لا يجوز إفشاؤه إلا لأهله، وهو من بذل نَفْسَه وفَلْسَهُ وخَرقَ عوائد نفسه، فهذا لا يحل كتمه عنه إذا طلبه.","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-12","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"وقسم يُستحب كتمه، وهو أسرار القدَر المُغَيَّبَات، فهذا من باب الكرامات يستحب كتمها ولا يجب، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-13","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"هنا انتهى العتاب لبني إسرائيل والكلام معهم، وابتداؤه من قوله تعالى: يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَوْفُوا بِعَهْدِي أُوفِ بِعَهْدِكُمْ..،. وإنما تخلَّل الكلامَ ذكرُ إبراهيم وبنيه توطئةً لنسخ القبلة الذي أنكروه، فذكر بناء الكعبة وبيان شرفها، وانجر الكلام إلى ذكر الصفا والمروة لقرب المناسبة والجوار.","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-159-162-14","r":"q2-159-162","title":"2:159–162 · Concealing revealed guidance and the responsibilities of knowledge","text":"فلما فرغ من عتابهم دلَّهم على التوحيد، وشاركهم فى ذلك غيرهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-159-162-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-159-162-s1","r":"q2-159-162","title":"The antecedent of “therein”","text":"I say: the pronoun in “therein” refers to the curse or to the Fire. Referring to the latter before mentioning it magnifies its importance and the terror of its affair.","anchor":"en-q2-159-162-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-159-162-s2","r":"q2-159-162","title":"Repentance requires repairing and disclosing","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, speaks of the Jewish scholars who concealed the Messenger’s description: those who conceal what We sent down in their Book concerning Muḥammad—God bless him and grant him peace—the clear signs about him, the account of his qualities, city and revealed law, and the guidance showing that following him and believing in him is obligatory, after We made it plain to people in the Torah: God curses these concealers and drives them from the court of His mercy. Jinn, human beings and all who can curse, including angels and others, curse them. Except those who repent of concealment and everything requiring repentance, repair the religion they corrupted by making good what was lost, and disclose what they concealed. To them I turn in mercy and show compassion: I abundantly accept repentance and pour forth mercy. But those who die in unbelief without repenting bear God’s curse and that of all whose curse counts, angels and human beings. They abide in the curse or in the Fire. Their punishment is not lightened for an hour, nor are they reprieved from it, or given time to offer excuses or ransom.","anchor":"en-q2-159-162-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-159-162-s3","r":"q2-159-162","title":"Corrupt scholars and repentance from venal judgement","text":"What is said of the Jewish scholars may likewise be said of this community’s evil scholars: those possessed by the carrion of this world and captive to desire, who take bribes for judgements, conceal the well-established and manifest ruling, and judge according to their own appetites. Those who curse curse them. Concerning this Ibn al-Mubārak says: What corrupted religion but kings, evil scholars and its monks? They sold their souls, yet gained no profit; their price in the sale was not high. The people have grazed upon carrion whose stench is plain to anyone of reason. Yaḥyā ibn Muʿādh al-Rāzī used to tell the scholars of his time: “Scholars! Your houses are Hāmān’s, your garments Qārūn’s, your mounts Pharaoh’s and your banquets Goliath’s. Where, then, is the Muḥammadan Sunna?” Except those who repent, repair what they corrupted and disclose what they concealed: God turns to them in mercy.","anchor":"en-q2-159-162-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-159-162-s4","r":"q2-159-162","title":"When knowledge must be disclosed or concealed","text":"Knowledge, considered with respect to the obligation to disclose or conceal it, falls into three divisions. One must be disclosed: concealing it brings one under the verse’s warning. This is knowledge of the outward Sacred Law when answering becomes individually incumbent upon the person asked, because no one else is available to give a ruling on that occurrence. Another must be concealed: knowledge of lordship’s secret ( سر الربوبية ), meaning the elect’s realization of unity ( التوحيد الخاص ). It must not be divulged except to its people: one who has surrendered self and money and broken the lower self’s habits. From such a person it is unlawful to withhold it when he requests it. A third is preferably concealed: the hidden secrets of destiny. These belong to extraordinary graces ( الكرامات ); concealing them is recommended, not obligatory. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-159-162-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-159-162-s5","r":"q2-159-162","title":"","text":"Here the reproach addressed to the Children of Israel and the discourse with them ends. It began at “Children of Israel, remember My favour which I bestowed upon you, and fulfil My covenant; I shall fulfil yours” [2:40]. Abraham and his sons were mentioned within it to prepare for the change of prayer-direction that they denied. The building of the Kaʿba and its honour were therefore explained; the discussion then led to al-Ṣafā and al-Marwa because of their close connection and proximity. Having finished reproaching them, He points them to unity, including others with them in the address:","anchor":"en-q2-159-162-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-163-164","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization 2:163–164","anchor":"unit-q2-163-164"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-1","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"وَإِلهُكُمْ إِلهٌ واحِدٌ لاَ إِلهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الرَّحْمنُ الرَّحِيمُ (163) إِنَّ فِي خَلْقِ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَاخْتِلافِ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهارِ وَالْفُلْكِ الَّتِي تَجْرِي فِي الْبَحْرِ بِما يَنْفَعُ النَّاسَ وَما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ مِنَ السَّماءِ مِنْ ماءٍ فَأَحْيا بِهِ الْأَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِها وَبَثَّ فِيها مِنْ كُلِّ دَابَّةٍ وَتَصْرِيفِ الرِّيحِ وَالسَّحابِ الْمُسَخَّرِ بَيْنَ السَّماءِ وَالْأَرْضِ لَآياتٍ لِقَوْمٍ يَعْقِلُونَ (164)","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-2","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"قلت: إِلهُكُمْ إِلهٌ واحِدٌ مبتدأ وخبر، وجملة لاَ إِلهَ إِلَّا هُوَ: تقرير لها وتأكيد، والرَّحْمنُ الرَّحِيمُ: خبران آخران، أو عن مبتدأ مضمر، وأنث الْفُلْكِ لأنه بمعنى السفينة، ومِنَ السَّماءِ ابتدائية، ومِنْ ماءٍ بيانية، وبَثَّ: عطف على أَنْزَلَ أو فَأَحْيا لأن الحيوانات تنمو بنزول المطر والخصب، والبث: النشر والتفريق وتَصْرِيفِ الرِّياحِ: هبوبها من الجهات المختلفة.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-3","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِلهُكُمْ يا معشر العباد الذي يستحق أن يُعبد إِلهٌ واحِدٌ لا شريك له، ولا نظير، ولا ضد له ولا ند، لاَ إِلهَ إِلَّا هُوَ، إذ لا يستحق العبادة غيره، إذ هو الرَّحْمنُ بنعمة الإيجاد الرَّحِيمُ بنعمة الإمداد، فكل ما سواه مُكونٌ مخلوق، إما مُنْعَم عليه أو نعمة، فلم يستحق العبادة غيره.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-4","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"ثم برهن على وجوده، وثبوت وحدانيته بثمانية أمور، فقال: إِنَّ فِي خَلْقِ السَّماواتِ طباقاً متفاصلة مرفوعة بغير عمد، وما اشتملت عليه من الكواكب والبروج والمنازل، وفي الْأَرْضِ وما اشتملت عليه من الجبال والبحار والأنهار والأشجار وأنواع الثمار، وفي اخْتِلافِ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهارِ بالطول والقصر، أو تعاقبهما بالذهاب والمجيء، (و) في الْفُلْكِ الَّتِي تَجْرِي فِي الْبَحْرِ بقدرته مع إمكان رسوبها إلى الأسفل، متلبسة بِما يَنْفَعُ النَّاسَ من التجارة وغيرها. وقال البيضاوي: القصد الاستدلال بالبحر وأحواله، وتخصيص الفلك بالذكر لأنه سبب الخوض فيه والاطلاع على عجائبه ولذلك قَدَّمه على ذكر المطر والسحاب، لأن منشأهما منه في الغالب. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-5","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"(و) في ما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ مِنَ السَّماءِ مِنْ ماءٍ من غير ظهور مادة سابقة، بل تُبرزه القدرة من عالم الغيب قريب عهد بالله، ولذلك (كان عليه الصلاة والسلام يَتَمَطَّر) أي: يَنْصُبُ وجهه للمطر إذا نزل تبركاً به، فَأَحْيا الحقّ تعالى بذلك المطر الْأَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِها ويُبْسِها، بالنبات والأزهار وأصناف النّوار والثمار، وفيما نشر فِيها مِنْ كُلِّ دَابَّةٍ من النملة إلى الفيلة، (و) في تَصْرِيفِ الرِّياحِ وهبوبها من جهات مختلفة، وهي الجهات الأربع وما بينها بصفات مختلفة، مُلَقِّحَةٍ للشجر وعقيم وصرِ ، وللنصر والهلاك، (و) في السَّحابِ الْمُسَخَّرِ أي: المذلَّل بَيْنَ السَّماءِ وَالْأَرْضِ لا يسقط ولا يرتفع، مع أن الطبع يقتضي أحدهما، أو مسخر للرياح تُقَلِّبه في جو السماء بمشيئة الله لَآياتٍ لِقَوْمٍ يَعْقِلُونَ. أي: تلك المخلوقات آيات دالة على وحدانيته تعالى وباهر قدرته، ولَوْ كانَ فِيهِما آلِهَةٌ إِلَّا اللَّهُ لَفَسَدَتا.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-6","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"وفي الآية حَضٍّ على التفكر، ولذلك قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «ويلٌ لِمَنْ قَرأَ هَذهِ الآيةِ فَمَجَّ بِها» ،. أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-7","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"لم يتفكر فيها، وفيها دلالة على شرف علم التوحيد العام والخاص. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-8","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"الإشارة: قال الجنيد: (التوحيد معنى تضْمَحِل فيه الرسوم وتندرج فيه العلوم، ويكونُ الله كما لم يزل) . قلت:","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-9","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"وهذا هو التوحيد الخاص، أعني توحيد أهل الشهود والعيان. ثم قال: (وأصولُه خمسة أشياء: رفعُ الحدَث، وإثبات","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-10","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"القدم، وهُجْران الإخُوان، ومفارقةُ الأوطان، ونسيان ما عَلِم وجَهِل) . هـ. قلت: قوله: (وهجران الإخوان) ، يعني:","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-11","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"غيرَ من يستعين بهم على السير، وأما من يستعين بهم فلا يستغني عنهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-12","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"واعلم أن توحيد الخلق لله تعالى على ثلاث درجات:","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-13","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"الأولى: توحيد العامة: وهو الذي يعصِمُ النفس والمال، وينجو به من الخلود في النار، وهو نَفْيُ الشركاء والأنداد، والصاحبةِ والأولاد، والأشباه والأضداد.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-14","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"الثانية: توحيد الخاصة: وهو أنْ يَرى الأفعال كلها صادرة من الله وحده، ويشاهد ذلك بطريق الكشف لا بطريق الاستدلال، فإنَّ ذلك حاصل لكل مؤمن، وإنما مَقامُ الخاصة يقينٌ في القلب بعلم ضروري لا يحتاج إلى دليل، وثمرة هذا العلم الانقطاعُ إلى الله، والتوكل عليه وحده، فلا يرجو إلا الله، ولا يخاف أحداً سواه، إذ ليس يرى فاعلا إلا الله، فيطرح الأسباب، وينبذ الأرباب.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-15","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"الدرجة الثالثة: ألا يرى في الوجود إلا الله، ولا يشهد معه سواه، فيغيبَ عن النظر إلى الأكوان في شهود المكون، وهذا مقام الفناء، فإن رُدّ إلى شهود الأثر بالله سُمي مقام البقاء. هـ. قال بعضَه ابنُ جُزَيّ باختصار.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-16","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"قلت: وفي التحقيق أنهما مقامان مقام أهل الدليل والبرهان، وهو المذكور في الآية، لأنه هو الذي يطيقه جميع العباد، ومقام أهل الشهود والعيان، وهو خاص بالأفراد الذين بذلوا مهجهم في طلب الله، باعوا أنفسهم وأموالهم في سبيل الله، فعوّضهم الله في الدنيا جنة المعارف، وزادهم في الآخرة جنة الزخارف.","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-17","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"(أهل الدليل والبرهان عموم عند أهل الشهود والعيان) لأن أهل الشهود والعيان قدسوا الحقّ تعالى عن أن يحتاج إلى دليل، فكيف يُعرف بالمعارف مَن به عرفت المعارف؟ كيف يستدل عليه بما هو في وجوده مفتقر إليه؟ أيكون لغيره من الظهور ما ليس له؟ - متى غاب حتى يحتاج إلى دليل عليه؟ ومتى بَعُدَ حتى تكون الآثار هي التي توصل إليه؟ - ولله در القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-18","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"لَقَدْ ظهرتَ فَمَا تَخْفَى على أحدٍ ... إلا على أَكْمَهِ لا يُبْصِرُ القمرَا","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-19","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"لَكِنْ بَطَنْتَ بِما أَظْهَرْتَ مُحْتَجِبا ... وكيفَ يُبْصَرُ مَن بالعزةِ استترَا؟","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-20","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"وقال آخر :","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-21","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"ما لِلحِجَابِ مَكَانٌ في وجُودِكُمُ ... إِلا بِسِرِّ حُروفِ (انظُرْ إلى الجَبَلَ)","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-22","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"أنتُم دلَلْتُمُ عليكُم مِنكُمُ ولكُمْ ... دَيمُومَةٌ عبَّرتْ عَنْ غاَمِضِ الأزلِ","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-23","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"عَرَّفْتُم بكُم هذا الخبيرَ بِكُم ... أنتُمْ هُمُ يا حياةَ القلْبِ يا أمَلِي","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-163-164-24","r":"q2-163-164","title":"2:163–164 · The signs of unity and the degrees of its realization","text":"ولما كانت المحبة تزيد وتنقص باعتبار شهود الوحدانية، فكلما قَويَ التوحيدُ في القلب قويت المحبة لانحصارها في واحد، ذكرها بأثر التوحيد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-163-164-24"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-163-164-s1","r":"q2-163-164","title":"Predicates, prepositions and the scattering of life","text":"I say: “your God” is the subject and “one God” its predicate. “There is no god but He” confirms and reinforces the statement. “The Compassionate, the Merciful” are two further predicates, or predicates of an implied subject. Fulk ( الفلك ), ships, is treated as feminine because it means safīna , a vessel. Min in “from heaven” marks the starting point; in “of water” it explains the kind. “He scattered” is coordinated with “sent down” or “revived,” since animals flourish with rain and fertility. Scattering ( البث ) means spreading and dispersing. “The shifting of the winds” is their blowing from different directions. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-07] ]","anchor":"en-q2-163-164-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-163-164-s2","r":"q2-163-164","title":"Eight considerations leading to knowledge of the One","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: servants, your God, who deserves worship, is one God. He has no partner, peer, opposite or equal; no god but He exists, for none besides Him deserves worship. He is the Compassionate through the blessing of bringing into existence ( الإيجاد ), the Merciful through the blessing of sustaining ( الإمداد ). Everything besides Him is originated and created, either a recipient of blessing or a blessing; none but He therefore merits worship. He then establishes His existence and unity through eight considerations: the creation of the heavens as distinct, separated layers raised without pillars, with their stars, zodiacal divisions and lunar stations; the earth, with its mountains, seas, rivers, trees and kinds of fruit; the difference of night and day in length and shortness, or their alternation as one departs and another arrives; and the ships sailing the sea through His power, though they could sink beneath it, carrying what benefits people through trade and otherwise. Al-Bayḍāwī says that the intention is to reason from the sea and its conditions. Ships are particularly mentioned because they provide the means of venturing upon it and observing its marvels. They therefore precede rain and clouds, whose origin is generally from it. Consider also the water God sends from heaven without a prior material becoming visible: power brings it forth from the unseen realm, newly come from God. Hence the Prophet used to expose himself to rain, turning his face towards it when it fell to receive its blessing. Through it the Real revives the earth after death and dryness, with vegetation, blossoms, varieties of flowers and fruit; and He scatters upon it every kind of creature, from ant to elephant. [B097] Consider the winds’ shifting and blowing from different directions—the four quarters and between them—with different qualities: fertilizing trees, barren or intensely cold, bringing victory or destruction. Consider the clouds subjected between heaven and earth, neither falling nor rising although natural inclination would require one of these, or subjected to the winds, which turn them about in heaven’s air as God wills. In these created things are signs of His unity and resplendent power for people who understand: “Had there been gods in them other than God, both would have fallen into ruin” [21:22]. The verse urges reflection. Hence the Prophet is reported to have said: “Woe to whoever reads this verse and casts it away”—that is, does not reflect upon it. It also indicates the nobility of the knowledge of unity, both general and particular. And God Most High knows best. [B098]","anchor":"en-q2-163-164-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-163-164-s3","r":"q2-163-164","title":"Unity through proof and unity through witnessing","text":"Al-Junayd said: “Unity is a meaning in which traces disappear and sciences are enfolded, and God is as He has ever been.” I say: this is the particular realization of unity, the unity of those possessing witnessing and direct vision. He then said: “Its foundations are five: setting aside temporal origination, affirming eternity, leaving companions, parting from homelands, and forgetting what one knew and did not know.” I say: “leaving companions” means those who do not help one travel. As for companions who help one, one cannot dispense with them. Know that creatures’ affirmation of God’s unity has three degrees. First is the generality’s unity, which protects life and property and delivers one from abiding for ever in the Fire: denying partners and equals, consort and children, likenesses and opposites. Second is the elect’s unity: seeing every action issue from God alone and witnessing this through unveiling, not inference. Inference is available to every believer; the elect’s station is certainty in the heart through immediate knowledge ( علم ضروري ) requiring no proof. Its fruit is exclusive devotion to God and trust in Him alone. One hopes only in God and fears none besides Him, seeing no agent but God, discarding means and casting aside other lords. The third degree is to see none in existence but God, and to witness no other with Him: one becomes absent from looking at created things through witnessing their Creator. This is the station of effacement ( الفناء ). If one is returned to witnessing the effect through God, it is called the station of subsistence ( البقاء ). Some of this is from Ibn Juzayy, abridged. I say: precisely considered, there are two stations: that of people of proof and demonstration, mentioned in the verse because it is within all servants’ capacity; and that of people of witnessing and direct vision, particular to rare individuals who have offered their very lives in seeking God. They sold their selves and wealth in God’s way, and He gave them in this world the garden of gnoses, adding in the next the garden of adornments. “People of proof and demonstration are the generality in relation to people of witnessing and direct vision.” For those of witnessing and vision hold the Real too holy to need a proof. How should He be known through items of knowledge when through Him those items are known? How can one infer Him from what depends upon Him for its existence? Does anything other than He possess a manifestation He lacks? When was He absent, that a proof of Him should be needed? When was He distant, that effects should lead to Him? How excellent the poet’s words: You have appeared, hidden from no one except one born blind, who cannot see the moon. Yet You are inward, veiled by what You have made appear; how is He seen who is concealed by might? Another said: No place for a veil exists within Your being, except through the secret in the words, “Look at the mountain.” You point to Yourself, from Yourself; Yours is a permanence expressing hidden eternity. Through Yourself You taught this knower of You: You are they, O life of the heart, O my hope! [B099]","anchor":"en-q2-163-164-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-163-164-s4","r":"q2-163-164","title":"","text":"Love increases and decreases with the witnessing of unity. The stronger unity becomes in the heart, the stronger love grows, confined to the One. He therefore mentions love immediately after unity:","anchor":"en-q2-163-164-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-165-167","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments 2:165–167","anchor":"unit-q2-165-167"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-1","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَتَّخِذُ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ أَنْداداً يُحِبُّونَهُمْ كَحُبِّ اللَّهِ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَشَدُّ حُبًّا لِلَّهِ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-2","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"قلت: ويُحتمل في وجه المناسبة، أن يكون الحق تعالى لمّا ذكر دلائل التوحيد ذكّر من أعرض بعد وضوحها فأشرك معه، ليرتب بعد ذلك ما أعدَّ له من العذاب، والأنداد: جمع نِدْ وهو المِثْل، والمراد هنا الأصنام أو الرؤساء، والإضافة في كَحُبِّ اللَّهِ من إضافة المصدر إلى مفعوله، والحُب: ميل القلب إلى المحبوب، وسيأتي في الإشارة، إن شاء الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-3","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَتَّخِذُ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ أشباهاً وأمثالاً من الأصنام والرؤساء يُحِبُّونَهُمْ، وينقادون إليهم، كما يحبون الله تعالى، فيُسَوَّون في المحبة بين الله تعالى العلي الكبير، وبين المصنوع الذليل الحقير، وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بالله ووحدوه أَشَدُّ حُبًّا لِلَّهِ لأن المؤمنين لا يلتفتون عن محبوبهم في الشدة ولا في الرخاء، بخلاف الكفار فإنهم يعبدونهم في وقت الرخاء، فإذا نزل البلاء التجئوا إلى الله. قال تعالى: ثُمَّ إِذا مَسَّكُمُ الضُّرُّ فَإِلَيْهِ تَجْئَرُونَ الآية، وأيضاً: المؤمنون يعبدون الله بلا واسطة، والكفار يعبدونه بواسطة أصنامهم مَا نَعْبُدُهُمْ إِلَّا لِيُقَرِّبُونا إِلَى اللَّهِ زُلْفى وأيضا المؤمنون يعبدون ربّاً واحداً فاتحدت محبتهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-4","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"قال سعيد بن جبير: (إن الله تعالى يأمر يوم القيامة مَنْ عبد الأصنام أن يدخلوا النار مع أصنامهم، فيمتنعون لعلمهم بالخلود فيها، ثم يقول للمؤمنين بين يدي الكفار: إن كنتم أحبائي فادخلوا، فيقتحم المؤمنون النار، وينادي مُنَأدٍ مِنْ تحت العرش: وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَشَدُّ حُبًّا لِلَّهِ. وفي ذلك يقول ابن الفارض:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-5","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"أحباي أَنتُم، أَحْسَنَ الدَّهرُ أم أَسا ... فَكُونُوا كما شِئتُمُ، أَنا ذَلك الخِل","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-6","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وقال أيضاً:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-7","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"لَو قالَ تِيهاً: قِف عَلَى جَمْرِ الغَضَا ، ... لوقفتُ مُمْتثلاً ولَمْ أَتَوقَّفِ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-8","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وقال آخر:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-9","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"ولَو عَذَّبْتَني في النارِ حتْماً ... دخلتُ مُطاوعاً وسْطَ الجَحِيمِ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-10","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"إذا كَانَ الجَحِيمُ رِضَاك عَنِّي ... فَمَا ذاكَ الجَحِيمُ سِوَى نَعِيمِ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-11","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"الإشارة: المحبةُ: مَيلٌ دائم بقلب هائم، أو مراقبة الحبيب في المشهد والمغيب، أو مواطأةُ القلب لمراد الرب، أو خوف ترك الخدْمة مع إقامة الحُرْمة، أو اسْتِقْلالُ الكثير من نفسك واستكثارُ القليل مِنْ حبيبك، أو معانقة الطاعة ومباينة المخالفة، وقال الشِّبْلِي: (أن تَغَار على المحبوب أن يحبه مثلك) والمحب على الحقيقة من لا سلطان على قلبه لغير محبوبه، ولا مشيئة له غير مشيئته، وقال الشيخ أبو الحسن رضي الله عنه: (المحبة أخذة من الله لقلب عبده المؤمن عن كل شيء سواه، فترى النفس مائلة لطاعته، والعقل متحصّناً بمعروفه، والروح مأخوذة في حضرته، والسر مغمورا في مشاهدته، والعبد يستزيد من محبته فيزداد، ويفاتح بما هو أعذب من لذيذ مناجاته، فيكسي حلل التقريب على بساط القربة، ويمس أبكار الحقائق وثيبات العلوم، فمن أجل ذلك قالوا: أولياء الله عرائس، ولا يَرَى العرائسَ المجرمون ... ) الخ كلامه.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-12","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"واعلم أن محبة العبد لمولاه سببُها شيئان:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-13","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"أحدهُما: نظر العبد لإحسان الله إليه وضروب امتنانه عليه، وجُبِلَت القلوبُ على حب من أحسن إليها، وهذا هو المسمى بحب الهوى، وهو مكتسب، لأن الإنسان مغمور بإحسانات الله إليه، ومتمكن من النظر فيها، فكلما طالَع منةً مِنْ مِنَن الله التي لا تقبل الحصر ولا العدَّ، كان ذلك كحَبة زُرعت في أرض قلبه الطيب الزكي، فلا يزال يطالع مِنّةً بعد منّة، وكلُّ منّة أعظم من التي قبلها، لأنه كلما طالع المنن تنور قلبه وازداد إيماناً، وكشف من دقائق المنن ما لم يكن يُكشف له قبلُ، وظهر له خفايا المنن، وعظمت محبته.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-14","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"الثاني: كشْف الحجب، وإزالة الموانع عن ناظر القلب، حتى يرى جمال الحقّ وكماله، والجمال محبوب بالطبع، وهذان هما اللذان قصدت رابعة العدوية- رضى الله عنها-:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-15","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"أُحِبُّكَ حُبَّين: حُبَّ الهَوَى ... وحُبّاً لأنك أهلٌ لِذَاكَ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-16","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"فأمّا الذي هو حُبُّ الهَوى ... فَشُغْلي بِذِكْرِك عمَّن سِوَاكَ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-17","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وأمَّا الذي أنتَ أهلٌ لهُ ... فكَشْفُكِ لِلْحُجْبِ حتى أراكَ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-18","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"فَلا الحمدُ في ذَا ولا ذَاك لي ... ولَكِنْ لكَ الحَمْدُ في ذَا وذاكَ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-19","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وإنما خَصَّصَتْ الحُبَّ الناشئ عن شهود الجمال بالأهلية دون الأول، وإن كان أهلاً للجميع لأن هذا منه إليه، لا كسب للعبد فيه، والآخر فيه كسب، وعمل العبد معلول، وقولها: (فَشُغْلي بِذِكْرِك عمَّن سِوَاكَ) من باب التعبير بالمسبب عن السبب، والأصل: فثمرته شغلي بذكرك عمن سواك، فهو مسبب عن المحبة لأنفسنا، وقولها أيضاً (كشفك للحجب حتى أراك) ، من باب التعبير بالسبب عن المسبب، والأصل، فبسببه كشفك للحجب حتى رأيتك بعينَيْ قلبي. وقولها: (فلا الحمد ... ) الخ، إخبار منها بأن الحُبَّيْن معاً منه وإليه وبه في الحقيقة، لا كسب لها في واحد منهما باعتبار الحقيقة، بل هو الحامد والمحمود، وإدراك التفاوت بين المقامين، - أعْني بين المحبة الناشئة عن شهود الإحسان، والناشئة عن شهود الجمال- ضروري عند كل ذائق، وأن الثانية أقوى. قاله في شرح الشريشية .","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-20","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"قال ابن جُزَيّ: اعلم أن محبة العبد لربه على درجتين أحدهما: المحبة العامة، التي لا يخلو منها كل مؤمن، وهي واجبة، والأخرى: المحبة الخاصة التي ينفرد بها العلماء الربَّانيون والأولياء والأصفياء، وهي أعلى المقامات، وغاية المطلوبات، فإنَّ سائر مقامات الصالحين: كالخوف والرجاء والتوكل، وغير ذلك، مَبْنِيَةٌ على حظوظ النفس، ألا ترى أن الخائف إنما يخاف على نفسه، والراجي إنما يرجو منفعة نفسه، بخلاف المحبة، فإنها من أجل المحبوب فليست من المعاوضة.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-21","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"واعلم أن سببَ محبةِ الله: معرفتُه، فتقوى المحبة على قدر المعرفة، وتضعف على قدر ضعف المعرفة، فإن الموجب للمحبة أحد أمرين أو كلاهما إذا اجتمعا، ولا شك أنهما اجتمعا في حق الله تعالى على غاية الكمال","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-22","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"فالموجب الأول: الحسن والجمال، والآخر الإحسان والإجمال، فأما الجمال فهو محبوب بالطبع، فإن الإنسان بالضرورة يحب كل ما يُستحسن، ولا جمالَ مثلُ جمال الله تعالى، في حكمته البالغة وصنائعه البديعة، وصفاته الجميلة الساطعة الأنوار، التي تَرُوق العقول وتبهج القلوب، وإنما يُدْرَك جمالُه تعالى بالبصائر لا بالأبصار.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-23","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وأما الإحسان فقد جبلت القلوب على حب من أحسن إليها، وإحسان الله إلى عباده متواتر، وإنعامُه عليهم باطن وظاهر، وَإِنْ تَعُدُّوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ لا تُحْصُوها، ويكفيك أنه يُحسن إلى المطيع والعاصي، وإلى المؤمن والكافر، وكل إحسان ينسب إلى غيره فهو في الحقيقة منه وحدَه، فهو المستحق للمحبة وحده.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-24","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"واعلم أن محبة الله إذا تمكنت من القلب ظهرت آثارها على الجوارح، من الجد في طاعته، والنَّشَطِ لخدمته، والحرص على مرضاته والتلذذ بمناجاته، والرضا بقضائه، والشوق إلى لقائه، والأُنْس بذكره، والاسْتِيحَاش مِنْ غيره، والفرار من الناس، والانفراد في الخلوات، وخروج الدنيا من القلب، ومحبة كل ما يحب الله، وكل من يحب الله، وإيثار الله على كل ما سواه.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-25","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"قال الحارث المحاسبي: (المحبة ميلك إلى المحبوب بِكُلِّيتِكَ، ثم إيثارك له على نفسك ورُوحك، ثم موافقته سرّاً وجهراً، ثم علمك بتقصيرك في حبه) .","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-26","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"قلت: ظاهره أن المحبة أعلى من المعرفة، والتحقيق أن المعرفة أعلى من جميع المقامات لأنها لا تبقى معها بقية من الحجاب أصلاً، بخلاف المحبة، فإنها تكون مع بقية الحجاب، ألا ترى أن المحب يستوحش من الخلق، والعارف لا يستوحش من شيء لمعرفته في كل شيء.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-27","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"قال في الحِكَم: (إنما استوحشَ العُبَّاد والزهاد من كل شيء لغيبتهم عن الله في كل شيء، ولو عرفوا الله في كل شيء ما استوحشوا من شيء) . وأيضاً: العارف أكمل أدباً من المحب لأن المعرفة إنما تحصُل بعد كمال التهذيب والتدريب، وقد تحصل المحبة قبل كمال التهذيب، مع أن المعرفة هي غاية المحبة ونهايتها، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-28","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"ثم ذكر الحقّ وعيدَ مَنْ أشرك مع الله في عبادته أو محبته، بعد وضوح برهان وحدانيته، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-29","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"... وَلَوْ تَرَى الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا إِذْ يَرَوْنَ الْعَذابَ أَنَّ الْقُوَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعاً وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعَذابِ (165) إِذْ تَبَرَّأَ الَّذِينَ اتُّبِعُوا مِنَ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوا وَرَأَوُا الْعَذابَ وَتَقَطَّعَتْ بِهِمُ الْأَسْبابُ (166) وَقالَ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوا لَوْ أَنَّ لَنا كَرَّةً فَنَتَبَرَّأَ مِنْهُمْ كَما تَبَرَّؤُا مِنَّا كَذلِكَ يُرِيهِمُ اللَّهُ أَعْمالَهُمْ حَسَراتٍ عَلَيْهِمْ وَما هُمْ بِخارِجِينَ مِنَ النَّارِ (167)","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-30","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"قلت: لَوْ شرطية، وتَرَى شرطها، قرأ نافع وابن عامر ويعقوب بالخطاب للنبيّ صلّى الله عليه وسلّم أو لكل سامع، والباقون بالغيب وإسناده إلى الظالم، لأنه المقصود بالوعيد والتهديد، وإِذْ ظرف للرؤية، وموضع يَرَوْنَ خفض بالإضافة، قرأ ابن عامر بضم الياء، على البناء للمفعول، والفاعلُ الحقيقي هو الله تعالى، بدليل يُرِيهِمُ اللَّهُ، والباقون بالفتح على البناء للفاعل، على حد: وَإِذا رَأَى الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا الْعَذابَ. وأَنَّ الْقُوَّةَ معمول للجواب المحذوف، تعظيماً لشأنه، والتقدير: لو ترى يا محمد، أو يا مَنْ يسمَع، الذين ظلموا حين يرون العذاب، أو يريهم الله العذاب، لرأيت أمرا فظيعا وخطبا جسيماً، ولعلمت أن القوة لله جميعا.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-30"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-31","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وجَمِيعاً حال، أي: أن القوة ثابتة في حال اجتماعها، وقرأ أبو جعفر ويعقوب (إنَّ) بالكسر في الموضعين على الاستئناف، و (إذ تبرأ) بدل من (إذ يرون) ، والأسباب: العهود والوُصَل التي كانت بينهم في الدنيا يتوادُّون عليها، وأصل السبب: كل شيء يتوصل به إلى شيء، ومنه قيل للحبل الذي يُصعد به: سبب، وللطريق:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-31"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-32","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"سبب، قال الشاعر :","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-32"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-33","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"ومَنْ هَابَ أَسْبابَ المَنِيِّةِ يلْقَها ... ولَوْ رَامَ أسْبَابَ السماء بسُلَّم","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-33"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-34","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"و (حسَرات) : حال، إن كانت بصرية، على مذهب أهل السنة، أو مفعول ثالث إن كانت عِلمية على مذهب المعتزلة القائلين بعدم تشخص الأعمال.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-34"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-35","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَوْ تَرَى يا محمد، أو كل مَن يتأتى منه الرؤية، حالَ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا باتخاذهم الأنداد والأوثان، بعد وضوح الأدلة وسُطوع البرهان، حيث يَرَوْنَ الْعَذابَ محيطاً بهم، والزبانيةُ تَغْلِبُهم، والنار تلتقطهم، لرأيت أمرا فظيعا، وخطبا جسيماً، ولعلمت أَنَّ الْقُوَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعاً، أو لو يرى الذين ظلموا العذاب الذي أعد لهم بسبب شركهم، لرأوا أمراً عظيماً، ولتيقنوا أَنَّ الْقُوَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعاً وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعَذابِ.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-35"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-36","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وذلك حين يتبرأ المتبوعون- وهم الرؤساء-، من الأتباع- وهم القلّة الضعفاء- والحالة أنهم رَأَوُا الْعَذابَ الفظيع، وَتَقَطَّعَتْ بِهِمُ الْأَسْبابُ أي: أسباب المودة والوُصْلات التي كانت بينهم في الدنيا، وصارت مودتهم عداوة، وَقالَ حينئذٍ الضعفاء الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوا شياطينهم في الكفر والضلال: لَوْ أَنَّ لَنا كَرَّةً أي: رجعة للدنيا فَنَتَبَرَّأَ مِنْهُمْ أي: من كبرائهم كَما تَبَرَّؤُا مِنَّا اليوم. كَذلِكَ أي: مثل ذلك الإبراء الفظيع يُرِيهِمُ اللَّهُ أَعْمالَهُمْ حَسَراتٍ وندامات عَلَيْهِمْ فيدخلون النار على سبيل الخلود، وَما هُمْ بِخارِجِينَ مِنَ النَّارِ.","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-36"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-37","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"الإشارة: يا من أقبل على مولاه، وجعل محبة سيده بُغْيته ومُناه، فلم يُشرك في محبة حبيبه سواه، لو رأيت من ظلم نفسه باتباع هواه، وأشرك مع الله في محبته سواه، باتباع حظوظ دنياه، وذلك حين يرون ما هم فيه من الانحطاط والبعاد، وما أعدّ الله لأهل المحبة والوداد من الفوز بالقرب من الحبيب، ومشاهدة جمال القريب، لرأيت أمراً عظيماً وخطباً جسيماً، ولعلمت أن القوة كلها لله، قَرّبَ مَنْ شاء بفضله ورحمته، وأبعد من شاء بعدله وحكمته، وذلك حين يتبرأ الأكابر فى الجرم من الأصاغر، ويقع التفريق بين الأصحاب والعشائر، إلا من اجتمعوا على محبة الحبيب، وتعاونوا على طاعة القريب المجيب، الْأَخِلَّاءُ يَوْمَئِذٍ بَعْضُهُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ إِلَّا الْمُتَّقِينَ. لا تصحب من لا يُنْهِضُكَ حاله، ولا يَدُلُّكَ على الله مقاله- فكل من صحب أهل الغفلة أو رَكَنَ إلى أهل الدنيا فلابد أن يرى ذلك حسرات يوم القيامة، يوم لا ينفع الندم وقد زلّ القدم. ولله دَرُّ صاحب العينية رضي الله عنه حيث يقول:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-37"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-38","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وَقَاطِعْ لِمَنْ وَاصَلْتَ أيَّامَ غفلة ... فما واصل العذال إلاَّ مُقَاطِعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-38"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-39","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"وَجَانِب جَنَابَ الأجنبي لو أنه ... لقرب انتساب في المنام مضاجع","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-39"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-40","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"فللنفس من جلاسها كل نسبة ... ومن خلة للقلب تِلكَ الطَّبَائعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-40"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-165-167-41","r":"q2-165-167","title":"2:165–167 · Undivided love and the severing of false attachments","text":"ولما حذَّر الحقّ تعالى من الشرك الجلي والخفي، حذَّر من متابعة المشركين في التحريم والتحليل بلا حكم شرعي فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-165-167-41"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s1","r":"q2-165-167","title":"Rivals and the relation between knowledge and love","text":"I say: another possible connection is that, having mentioned the proofs of unity, the Real mentions those who turn away after their clarity and associate others with Him, to introduce what He has prepared for them of punishment. Rivals ( الأنداد ) is the plural of nidd , an equal; here it means idols or leaders. “As God is loved” annexes the verbal noun to its object ( إضافة المصدر إلى مفعوله ). Love is the heart’s inclination towards the beloved; it will be discussed under the spiritual allusion, God willing.","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s2","r":"q2-165-167","title":"A love that does not change with adversity","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: some people take likenesses and equals apart from God—idols and leaders—loving and obeying them as they love God. They thus place the Most High, the Great, and a lowly, contemptible manufactured thing on equal terms in love. Those who believe in God and affirm His unity are stronger in love for Him. Believers do not turn from their Beloved in hardship or ease. Unbelievers, by contrast, worship their objects in ease but take refuge in God when affliction descends: “Then, when harm touches you, to Him you cry” [16:53]. Believers also worship God without an intermediary, whereas unbelievers worship Him through idols: “We worship them only that they may bring us nearer to God” [39:3]. Moreover, believers worship one Lord, and their love is consequently united. Saʿīd ibn Jubayr said: “On the Day of Resurrection God commands those who worshipped idols to enter the Fire with their idols. Knowing that they will remain there, they refuse. Then, before the unbelievers, He tells the believers, ‘If you are My beloved, enter!’ They plunge into the Fire, and a caller beneath the Throne calls, ‘Those who believe are stronger in love for God.’” Concerning this Ibn al-Fāriḍ says: [B100] You are my beloved, whether time deals well or ill; be as you wish: I remain that faithful friend. He also says: Were he, in proud disdain, to say, “Stand upon the glowing embers,” I would stand in obedience, without hesitation. Another said: Were You to decree my punishment in Fire, I would enter willingly into its midst. If Hell meant Your good pleasure with me, that Hell would be nothing but bliss.","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s3","r":"q2-165-167","title":"Definitions of love and the heart seized by God","text":"Love ( المحبة ) is an enduring inclination of an enraptured heart; or watching over the Beloved in presence and absence; or the heart’s agreement with the Lord’s will; or fearing to abandon service while maintaining reverence; or counting much from oneself as little and little from one’s Beloved as much; or embracing obedience and separating from opposition. Al-Shiblī said: “It is to be jealous for the Beloved that someone like you should love Him.” The true lover is one over whose heart none but the Beloved has authority, and who has no will apart from His. Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan said: “Love is God’s seizure of His believing servant’s heart away from everything besides Him. You see the soul inclined to obey Him, the intellect fortified by knowledge of His goodness, the spirit seized in His presence, and the innermost secret submerged in witnessing Him. The servant asks for increased love and is increased, and is opened to what is sweeter than the delight of intimate converse. He is clothed in robes of nearness upon the carpet of nearness, and touches the virgin realities and the previously known sciences. Hence it is said: God’s friends are brides, and criminals do not see the brides …” Here ends the quoted portion of his words. [B101]","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s4","r":"q2-165-167","title":"Love through beneficence and love through unveiled beauty","text":"Know that the servant’s love for his Master has two causes. The first is considering God’s beneficence towards him and the many kinds of grace bestowed upon him. Hearts are naturally fashioned to love whoever treats them well. This is called love of inclination ( حب الهوى ), and is acquired: a person is immersed in God’s beneficences and can reflect upon them. Each grace among God’s innumerable, uncountable graces that he beholds is like a seed planted in his good, pure heart. He continues to behold grace after grace, each greater than the preceding one. For as he considers the graces, his heart is illuminated and his faith increases; subtleties of grace previously hidden are unveiled, their concealed aspects appear, and his love grows. The second cause is the lifting of veils and removal of obstacles from the heart’s eye, until it sees the Real’s beauty and perfection. Beauty is naturally loved. These are the two intended by Rābiʿa al-ʿAdawiyya: I love You with two loves: love of inclination, and a love because You are worthy of it. As for the love of inclination, it is my occupation with remembering You to the exclusion of others. As for the love of which You are worthy, it is Your lifting the veils until I see You. No praise in this or that is mine; Yours is the praise in this and that. She reserves worthiness for love arising from witnessing beauty, although He is worthy of both, because this love proceeds from Him to Him without the servant’s acquisition. The other involves acquisition, and the servant’s action is subject to defect. “My occupation with remembering You to the exclusion of others” expresses an effect in place of its cause ( التعبير بالمسبب عن السبب ): its full sense is “its fruit is my occupation with remembering You to the exclusion of others.” This is an effect of love for our own sake. “Your lifting the veils until I see You” expresses a cause in place of its effect ( التعبير بالسبب عن المسبب ): its expanded sense is “its cause is Your lifting the veils until I saw You with the eyes of my heart.” [Translator’s note: Cairo I:195 prints فبسببه (“through/because of it”). The cited commentary, Aḥmad b. Yūsuf al-Fāsī’s commentary on the Rāʾiyya (Cairo, 1316 AH), p. 154, reads فسببه ومنشؤه, “its cause and origin.” The translation follows the cited source’s clear causal construction; the different Cairo reading is expressly recorded.] [B102] “No praise …” tells us that both loves in reality proceed from Him, are directed to Him and are through Him. Considered in reality, she acquires neither; He is both the Praiser and the Praised. Everyone possessing spiritual taste necessarily apprehends the difference between these stations—love arising from witnessing beneficence and love arising from witnessing beauty—and knows that the second is stronger. This is stated in the commentary on the Sharīshiyya . Ibn Juzayy says: know that the servant’s love for his Lord has two degrees. The first is the general love of which no believer is altogether devoid; it is obligatory. The second is the particular love belonging to divinely instructed scholars, friends of God and the purified. It is the highest station and the ultimate object sought. The righteous people’s other stations—fear, hope, trust and so forth—rest upon the lower self’s shares. One who fears fears for himself; one who hopes hopes for his own benefit. Love, by contrast, is for the Beloved’s sake, and is not an exchange. Know that love of God is caused by knowledge of Him. It strengthens in proportion to knowledge and weakens as knowledge weakens. One or both of two things brings love about; in God Most High both are certainly united with utmost perfection. The first is loveliness and beauty; the second, beneficence and gracious treatment. Beauty is naturally loved: a person necessarily loves whatever he finds beautiful. No beauty resembles God’s beauty in His consummate wisdom, wondrous handiwork and beautiful, radiantly luminous Attributes, which enchant intellects and gladden hearts. His beauty is perceived by inward insight, not bodily sight. As for beneficence, hearts naturally love whoever does good to them. God’s beneficence towards His servants is unceasing, His blessings outward and inward: “If you count God’s blessing, you will not enumerate it” [14:34; 16:18]. It suffices that He does good to the obedient and disobedient, believer and unbeliever. Every beneficence attributed to another is in reality from Him alone; He alone therefore deserves love. When love of God takes firm hold in the heart, its effects appear upon the limbs: diligence in obedience, eagerness for service, care to please Him, delight in intimate converse, contentment with His decree, longing to meet Him, intimacy with His remembrance, estrangement from others, flight from people, solitude in retreats, the world’s departure from the heart, love for whatever and whomever God loves, and preference for Him over all besides Him. Al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāsibī said: “Love is your inclining wholly towards the Beloved, then preferring Him to your self and spirit, then agreeing with Him secretly and openly, then knowing your shortcoming in loving Him.”","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s5","r":"q2-165-167","title":"Ibn ʿAjība’s qualification: gnosis is beyond love with a remaining veil","text":"I say: the apparent implication is that love is higher than gnosis ( المعرفة ). Precisely considered, however, gnosis is higher than every station, since with it no remnant of the veil remains at all. Love may coexist with a remaining veil. Do you not see that the lover feels estranged from creation, whereas the gnostic feels estranged from nothing, knowing Him in everything? The Ḥikam says: “Worshippers and renunciants feel estranged from everything only because they are absent from God in everything. Had they known God in everything, they would have felt estranged from nothing.” The gnostic also possesses more perfect courtesy than the lover, for gnosis is attained only after refinement and training have become complete, whereas love may arise before refinement is complete. Nevertheless, gnosis is love’s goal and culmination. And God Most High knows best. The Real then mentions the threat against one who, after the clarity of the proof of His unity, associates another with God in worship or love: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:165b وَلَوْ تَرَى الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا إِذْ يَرَوْنَ الْعَذَابَ أَنَّ الْقُوَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعًا وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعَذَابِ If you could see the wrongdoers when they see the punishment, [you would know] that power belongs wholly to God and that God is severe in punishment!","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s6","r":"q2-165-167","title":"An omitted consequence and deeds made visible","text":"I say: law is conditional; tarā is its protasis. Nāfiʿ, Ibn ʿĀmir and Yaʿqūb read the verb as an address to the Prophet or every listener, “if you saw.” The others read it in the third person, referring it to the wrongdoer, the intended recipient of the threat and warning. Idh is an adverbial expression qualifying the seeing, and yarawna occupies the genitive position through annexation ( خفض بالإضافة ). Ibn ʿĀmir reads the verb passively, with initial ḍamma: “when they are shown.” God is the true agent, as “God shows them” indicates. The others read the active form, with initial fatḥa, like “when the wrongdoers see the punishment” [16:85]. “That power …” is governed by an omitted consequence ( الجواب المحذوف ), suppressed to magnify its importance: if you, Muḥammad—or you who listen—saw the wrongdoers when they see the punishment, or God shows it to them, you would see something dreadful and a tremendous affair, and know that power belongs wholly to God. “Wholly” is a circumstantial qualifier ( حال ): power belongs to Him in its entirety. Abū Jaʿfar and Yaʿqūb read inna with kasra in both places as a fresh statement. “When those who were followed disown …” substitutes for “when they see.” The bonds ( الأسباب ) are the covenants and connections upon which their worldly affection depended. Originally a sabab is anything through which something is reached: a rope used to ascend is so called, as is a road. The poet says: Whoever fears the means of death will meet it, though he seek the pathways of heaven by a ladder. “Regrets” ( حسرات ) is a circumstantial qualifier if “shows” means bodily seeing, according to the People of the Sunna; or a third object if it means causing to know, according to the Muʿtazila, who deny deeds’ taking concrete form. [B103]","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s7","r":"q2-165-167","title":"Followers and leaders disown one another","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: if you, Muḥammad—or anyone capable of seeing—saw the condition of those who wronged themselves by taking equals and idols after clear evidence and radiant proof, when punishment surrounds them, its guardians overpower them and the Fire snatches them up, you would see something dreadful and a tremendous affair, and know that power belongs wholly to God. Or: if the wrongdoers saw the punishment prepared for their association of others with God, they would behold a tremendous affair and be certain that power belongs wholly to God and His punishment is severe. This occurs when those followed—the leaders—disown their followers, the weak and insignificant, while beholding the dreadful punishment. The bonds of affection and connection that joined them in this world are severed, and their affection turns to enmity. Those weak people who followed their devils in unbelief and error say, “If only we could return to the world, we would disown our leaders as they have disowned us today.” In a manner like that terrible showing, God shows them their deeds as regrets and remorse. They enter the Fire abidingly and never emerge from it.","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s8","r":"q2-165-167","title":"Companionship whose consequences appear at the end","text":"You who turn towards your Master, making your Lord’s love your aim and hope and associating no other with your Beloved in love: if you saw those who wrong themselves by following desire and joining another to God in love through pursuing worldly shares, when they see their own abasement and distance, and what God has prepared for people of love and affection—nearness to the Beloved and witnessing the beauty of the Near—you would see a tremendous affair. You would know that all power belongs to God: He brings whom He wills near through His bounty and mercy, and sets whom He wills far through His justice and wisdom. The great in wrongdoing then disown the lesser; companions and kin are separated, except those joined in love of the Beloved and helping one another obey the Near, Responsive One: “Close friends that day will be enemies to one another, except the God-fearing” [43:67]. “Do not accompany one whose state does not raise you and whose speech does not direct you to God.” Whoever accompanies the heedless or rests upon worldly people must see this as regrets on the Resurrection Day, when remorse is useless and the foot has slipped. How excellent the author of the ʿAyniyya : Part from those you joined in heedless days; only one severed [from the Beloved] keeps company with reproachers. Avoid the stranger’s company, even if close kinship makes him your bedfellow in sleep. From its companions the soul takes every affinity; from the heart’s friendship come these dispositions. [B104]","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-165-167-s9","r":"q2-165-167","title":"","text":"Having warned against manifest and hidden association, the Real warns against following the associators in declaring things forbidden or permitted without a ruling of the Sacred Law:","anchor":"en-q2-165-167-s9"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-168-169","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary 2:168–169","anchor":"unit-q2-168-169"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-1","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ كُلُوا مِمَّا فِي الْأَرْضِ حَلالاً طَيِّباً وَلا تَتَّبِعُوا خُطُواتِ الشَّيْطانِ إِنَّهُ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُبِينٌ (168) إِنَّما يَأْمُرُكُمْ بِالسُّوءِ وَالْفَحْشاءِ وَأَنْ تَقُولُوا عَلَى اللَّهِ ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ (169)","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-2","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"قلت: حَلالًا حال، أو مفعول به، وطَيِّباً نعت له، والخطوات جمع خطوة، وهي بالفتح- مصدر خطا يخطو، وبالضم- اسم لمسافة ما بين القدمين، ويُكَسَّر على خطاً، ويُصَحَّح على خطوات، مثلث الطاء، أعني:","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-3","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"الضم على الإتباع، كغرفات وقربات، قال ابن مالك:","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-4","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"والسَّالمَ العَيْنِ الثُّلاثي اسْما أَنِلْ ... إتْبَاعَ عَيْنٍ فَاءَهُ بما شُكِلُ","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-5","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"والسكون على الأصل في المفرد، والفتح تخفيفاً، قال في الألفية:","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-6","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"وسكَّنِ التالِيَ غيرَ الفتحِ أوْ ... خفِّفْهُ بالفَتْحِ فكُلاَّ قدْ رووا","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-7","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"وقرئ فى المتواتر بالضم والإسكان، وفي الشاذِّ بالفتح.","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-8","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"قال الخليل: (خطوات الشيطان: آثاره وطرقه، يقول: لا تقتدوا به) . هـ. وأصل السوء: كل ما يَسُوء صاحبه ويُحزنه. والفحشاء: ما قبحُ من القول والفعل، مصدر فحش كالبأساء والضراء واللأوَاء.","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-9","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"قال ابن عباس: (الفحشاءُ: ما فيه حد، والسوء: ما لا حَدَّ فيه) ، وقال مقاتل: (كل ما في القرآن من ذكر الفحشاء فإنه الزنا، إلا قوله: الشَّيْطانُ يَعِدُكُمُ الْفَقْرَ وَيَأْمُرُكُمْ بِالْفَحْشاءِ فإنه البخل) . قال البيضاوي: السوء والفحشاء: ما أنكره العقل واستقبحه الشرع، والعطف لاختلاف الوصفين، فإنه سوءٌ لاغتمام العاقل به، وفحشاء باستقباحه إياه، وقيل: السوء يعمُ القبائح، والفحشاء ما تجاوَز الحدَّ في القبح. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-10","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ كُلُوا من جميع ما خلقنا لكم في الأرض من نباتها مما يُستطاب أكله، وحيواناتها إلا ما حرمناه عليكم، حالة كون ذلك حَلالًا قد انحلَّت عنه التبِعَات، وزالت عنه الشبهات، طَيِّباً مُستلَذاً يستلِذُّه الطبع، ويستحسنه الشرع، وَلا تَتَّبِعُوا طرق الشَّيْطانِ فتُحَرِّموا برأيكم ما أحلَّ الله لكم، كالبَحِيرة والسائبة والوَصِيلة والحام، وبعض الحرث الذي جعلتموه للأصنام، فإن ذلك من تزيين الشيطان، وهو لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُبِينٌ. ومن شأن العدو الخِدَاع والغرور، فإنما يأمركم بما يَسُوء وجوهَكم من الذنوب، وما يُرديكم من قبائح المعاصي والعيوب، وَأَنْ تَقُولُوا عَلَى اللَّهِ ما لا علم لكم به من تحلِيل الحرام، أو تحريم الحلال، أو ادعاء الولد أو الصاحبة في جانب الكبير المتعال.","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-11","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الحق تعالى جعل للبشرية قُوتاً ونعيماً تتنعم به، وجعل للروح قوتاً ونعيماً تتلذذ به، فقُوت البشرية الطعام والشراب، ونعيمُها: الملابس والمَناكح والمَراكب. وقوت الروح: اليقين والعلوم والأنوار، ونعيمها:","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-12","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"الشهود والاستبصار، والترقي في المعارف والأسرار، فكما أن النفس تأكُل مما في الأرض حلالاً طيباً، كذلك الروح تأكل مما في الأرض حلالاً طيباً، إلا أن أكل النفس حِسّي، وأكل الروح معنوي، وهو التفكر والاعتبار، أو الشهود والاستبصار، وفي ذلك يقول المجذوب رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-13","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"الخَلْقُ نَوَّارٌ ... وَأَنا رَعَيْتُ فيهمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-14","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"هُمُ الحجابُ الأكبَرُ ... والمَدخَلُ فِيهم","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-15","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"وقال الششتري رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-16","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"عَينُ الزِّحامِ هُوَ ... المَسِيرُ لِحَيّنَا","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-17","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"وكان شيخ شيوخنا سيدي علي رضي الله عنه يقول: (من أراد أن يذوق فليذهب إلى السوق) . وذلك لأنه مظنة الزحام، وفيه عند الأقوياء الربح التام، فيقال لهم: يا أيها الناس الكاملون في الإنسانية كلوا مما في الأرض بأرواحكم وأسراركم، شهوداً واعتباراً، حلالاً طيّباً، ولا تتبعوا خطوات الشيطان، فتقفوا مع ظواهر الأكوان، فتُحجبوا عن الشهود والعيان، فإنه لكم في صورة العدو المبين، لكنه في الحقيقة يحوشكم إلى الرسوخ والتمكين، لأنه كلما حرككم بنزغه فزعتم إلى ربكم في دفعه، حتى يمكنكم من حضرته، فإنما يأمركم بما يسوء وجوهكم ويغُم قلوبكم، من مفارقة شهود الأحباب، والوقوف مِنْ وراء الباب، وأن تقولوا على الله ما ليس بحق ولا صواب، كثبوت السَّوي، أو الالتفات إلى الهوى. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-168-169-18","r":"q2-168-169","title":"2:168–169 · Lawful nourishment and the footsteps of the adversary","text":"ثم أعلمنا الحق تعالى أن بعض من سبق عليه الشقاء لا يخرج عن هواه، ولا يجيب من دعاه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-168-169-18"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-168-169-s1","r":"q2-168-169","title":"The plural khuṭuwāt and the meanings of evil","text":"I say: “lawful” is a circumstantial qualifier or direct object; “wholesome” qualifies it. Footsteps ( الخطوات ) is the plural of khuṭwa . With fatḥa, khaṭwa is the verbal noun of stepping; with ḍamma, it names the distance between the feet. Its broken plural is khuṭā , its sound plural khuṭuwāt . The ṭāʾ admits three vowels: ḍamma by vowel-following ( الإتباع ), as in ghurufāt and qurubāt . Ibn Mālik says: In a triliteral noun whose middle radical is sound, make the middle radical follow the first in its vowel. The consonant may be quiescent, preserving its form in the singular, or carry fatḥa for ease. The Alfiyya says: Make quiescent the consonant following a vowel other than fatḥa, or lighten it with fatḥa: both have been transmitted. The mutawātir readings have ḍamma or sukūn, and an anomalous reading has fatḥa. [B105] Al-Khalīl said: “Satan’s footsteps are his traces and paths: do not imitate him.” Evil ( السوء ) originally means anything that distresses and saddens its possessor. Indecency ( الفحشاء ) is what is ugly in speech or deed, a verbal noun from faḥusha , like baʾsāʾ , ḍarrāʾ and laʾwāʾ . Ibn ʿAbbās said that indecency is what incurs a prescribed penalty ( حد ), and evil what does not. Muqātil said every mention of indecency in the Qurʾān means illicit intercourse except “Satan promises you poverty and commands you to indecency” [2:268], where it means miserliness. Al-Bayḍāwī says evil and indecency are what reason rejects and revealed law judges ugly. They are coordinated because their descriptions differ: an act is evil through the distress it causes a rational person and indecent through his finding it ugly. Another view makes evil embrace all ugly acts and indecency those exceeding the ordinary degree of ugliness.","anchor":"en-q2-168-169-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-168-169-s2","r":"q2-168-169","title":"Neither invent prohibitions nor attribute them to God","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: people, eat from all We created for you upon the earth—its plants that are pleasant to eat and its animals except those We forbade—provided it is lawful, released from liabilities and free of doubts, and wholesome, agreeable to nature and approved by the Sacred Law. Do not follow Satan’s paths by forbidding through your own opinion what God permitted: the baḥīra , sāʾiba , waṣīla and ḥām , and crops assigned to idols. Satan makes this attractive; he is your manifest enemy, and deception and delusion are an enemy’s business. [B106] He commands only sins that disfigure your faces, ugly acts and faults that bring you to ruin, and speech about God without knowledge: permitting the forbidden, forbidding the permitted, or claiming a child or consort for the Most Great, Most High.","anchor":"en-q2-168-169-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-168-169-s3","r":"q2-168-169","title":"The body’s food and the spirit’s nourishment","text":"Know that the Real has appointed nourishment and enjoyment for human bodily nature, and nourishment and delight for the spirit. Bodily nourishment is food and drink; its enjoyment is clothing, marriage and mounts. The spirit’s nourishment is certainty, knowledge and lights; its enjoyment is witnessing, insight and ascent in gnoses and secrets. As the lower self eats what is lawful and wholesome upon earth, so does the spirit. The former’s eating is sensory; the latter’s is inward: reflection and taking heed, or witnessing and insight. Al-Majdhūb says: Creation is blossom, and I have grazed among them. They are the greatest veil; among them is the entrance. Al-Shushtarī says: The very press of the crowd is the road to our quarter. Our masters’ master, Sīdī ʿAlī, used to say: “Whoever wishes to taste should go to the market.” Crowding is to be expected there, and for the strong therein lies complete gain. They are told: people perfected in humanity, eat of what is upon earth with your spirits and secrets, through witnessing and reflection, lawfully and wholesomely. Do not follow Satan’s footsteps by stopping at created things’ outward appearances and being veiled from witnessing and direct vision. He appears to you as a manifest enemy, but in reality drives you towards rootedness and establishment: whenever his prompting stirs you, you flee to your Lord to repel him, until He establishes you in His presence. Satan commands only what distresses your faces and saddens your hearts: departing from witnessing the beloved and standing behind the door, and saying about God what is neither true nor right, such as affirming an other or turning towards desire. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-168-169-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-168-169-s4","r":"q2-168-169","title":"","text":"The Real informs us that some whose wretchedness has preceded do not leave their desire or answer one who calls them:","anchor":"en-q2-168-169-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-170","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance 2:170","anchor":"unit-q2-170"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-170-1","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُمُ اتَّبِعُوا ما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ قالُوا بَلْ نَتَّبِعُ ما أَلْفَيْنا عَلَيْهِ آباءَنا أَوَلَوْ كانَ آباؤُهُمْ لا يَعْقِلُونَ شَيْئاً وَلا يَهْتَدُونَ (170)","anchor":"ar-q2-170-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-170-2","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"قلت: الضمير في (لهم) يعود على (من يتخذ مِن دُونِ الله أَندَاداً) ، أو على (الناس) ، من قوله: (يا أيها الناس) ، أو على (اليهود) المتقدمين قبلُ، وألفى: بمعنى وجد، يتعدّى إلى مفعولين، وهما هنا: (آباءنا) والجار والمجرور، أي: نتبع في الدين ما وجدنا آباءنا كائنين عليه.","anchor":"ar-q2-170-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-170-3","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا قِيلَ لهؤلاء المشركين من كفار العرب: اتَّبِعُوا ما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ على رسوله من التوحيد، وترك الأنداد له والأمثال، وتحريم الحرام وتحليل الحلال، قالُوا بَلْ نَتَّبِعُ ما وجدنا عَلَيْهِ آباءَنا من عبادة الأصنام، وارتكاب المعاصي والآثام، قال الحق جلّ جلاله: أيتبعونهم تقليداً وعَمى، ولو كان آباؤهم جهلة لا يَعْقِلُونَ شَيْئاً من الدين، ولا يتفكرون في سبيل المهتدين؟! وقال ابن عباس- رضى الله عنهما-: دعا النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم اليهودَ إلى الإسلام، ورغبهم فيه، فقال له رافع بن خارجة ومالك بن عوف:","anchor":"ar-q2-170-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-170-4","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"بل نتبعُ ما وجدنا عليه آباءنا، فهم كانوا خيراً وأعلم منا، فأنزل الله تعالى هذه الآية. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-170-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-170-5","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"الإشارة: وإذا قيل لمن أكَبَّ على دنياه، واتخذ إلهه هواه، فأشرك في محبة الله سواه: أقلعْ عن حظوظك وهواك، وأفرد الوجهة إلى مولاك، واتبع ما أنزل الله من وجوب مخالفة الهوى ومحبة المولى، قال: بل أتبع ما وجدتُ عليه الآباء والأجداد، وأكبَّ عليه جلُّ العباد، فيقال له: أتتبعهم في متابعة الهوى، ولو كانوا لا يعقلون شيئا","anchor":"ar-q2-170-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-170-6","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"من طرق الهدى؟ وقد قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «لاَ يُؤْمِنُ أَحَدُكُمْ حَتَّى يَكُونَ هَواهُ تَبعاً لِمَا جئت به» . هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-170-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-170-7","r":"q2-170","title":"2:170 · Inherited custom and the refusal of guidance","text":"ثم ضرب الحق مثلا لمن تبع هواه، فأصمّه وأعماه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-170-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-170-s1","r":"q2-170","title":"The antecedent and the two objects of alfa","text":"I say: “them” refers to those taking rivals apart from God, or to the people addressed by “O people,” or to the Jews mentioned earlier. Alfā means found and takes two objects: here “our fathers” and the prepositional phrase, meaning “we follow in religion that upon which we found our fathers established.”","anchor":"en-q2-170-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-170-s2","r":"q2-170","title":"Ancestry does not establish the truth of a practice","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when these associators among the Arab unbelievers are told to follow what God revealed to His Messenger—unity, abandoning equals and likenesses for Him, forbidding the forbidden and permitting the lawful—they reply: rather, we follow what we found our fathers following, worshipping idols and committing sins. The Real says: do they follow them blindly and imitatively even though their fathers were ignorant, understanding nothing of religion and not reflecting upon the rightly guided path? Ibn ʿAbbās reports that the Prophet called the Jews to Islam and encouraged them to accept it. Rāfiʿ ibn Khārija and Mālik ibn ʿAwf replied: “Rather, we follow what we found our fathers following: they were better and more knowledgeable than we are.” God then revealed this verse.","anchor":"en-q2-170-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-170-s3","r":"q2-170","title":"Inherited desire and the obligation to oppose it","text":"When someone absorbed in worldly life, taking desire as his god and joining another to God in love, is told, “Leave your shares and appetites, direct yourself wholly towards your Master, and follow God’s revelation requiring opposition to desire and love of the Master,” he replies: “Rather, I follow what I found my fathers and ancestors following, and what most people pursue.” He is asked: will you follow them in pursuing desire even though they understood nothing of the paths of guidance? The Prophet is reported to have said: “None of you believes until his desire follows what I have brought.” [B107]","anchor":"en-q2-170-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-170-s4","r":"q2-170","title":"","text":"The Real sets forth a likeness for one whom following desire has deafened and blinded:","anchor":"en-q2-170-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-171","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it 2:171","anchor":"unit-q2-171"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-1","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"وَمَثَلُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا كَمَثَلِ الَّذِي يَنْعِقُ بِما لا يَسْمَعُ إِلاَّ دُعاءً وَنِداءً صُمٌّ بُكْمٌ عُمْيٌ فَهُمْ لا يَعْقِلُونَ (171)","anchor":"ar-q2-171-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-2","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"قلت: (ومثل) إلخ، يحتمل أن يكون على حذف مضاف، أي: مثَلُ واعظِ الذين كفروا، أو لا يحتاج إلى تقدير. وسيأتى بيانه، ونَعَقَ، كضرب، ينعق نعقاً ونعيقاً، إذا صاح وزجر.","anchor":"ar-q2-171-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-3","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَثَلُ واعظ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وداعيهم إلى الله كَمَثَلِ الراعي الذي يرعَى البهائم، وينعق عليها ليزجرها، أو يدعوها فإذا سمعَت النداء رفعت رءوسها ولم تعقِلْه، ثم عادت إلى مراعيها، فلا تسمع من الراعي يزجرها إِلَّا دُعاءً وَنِداءً، ولا تفقه ما يقول لها، كذلك الكفار المنهمكون في الكفر، إذا دعاهم أحد إلى التوحيد لا يلتفتون إليه، ولا يفقهون ما يقول لهم، كالبهائم أو أضل.","anchor":"ar-q2-171-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-4","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"أو مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا في انهماكهم في التقليد والجهل، مع مَنْ يدعوهم إلى الله كَمَثَلِ بهائم الذي ينعق ويصيح عليها صاحبها فلا تسمع إِلَّا دُعاءً وَنِداءً ولا تفقه ما يقول لها، أو مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا في دعائهم الأصنام التي لا تسمع ولا تعقل، كمثل الناعق بغنمه، فلا ينتفع من نعيقه بشيء، غير أنه في عناء وتعب من دعائه وندائه، ثم وصفهم بالصمم والبكم والعمى مجازاً، أي: هم صُمٌّ عن سماع الحق فلا يعقلونه، بُكْمٌ عن النطق به، عُمْيٌ عن النظر إلى أسبابه، أو عن الهدى فلا يبصرونه، فَهُمْ لا يَعْقِلُونَ شيئاً ولا يتدبرون.","anchor":"ar-q2-171-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-5","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"الإشارة: إذا تمكن الهوى من القلوب عَزَّ دواؤه وشقّ علاجه، وعظم على الأطباء عناؤه، فالمنهمكون في الغفلة لا ينفَع فيهم التذكير، ولا ينجح فيهم التخويف والتحذير، فالواعظ لهم كالناعق بالبهائم التي لا تسمع إلا دعاء ونداء، قد أعماهم الهوى، وأصمهم عن سماع أسباب الهدى.","anchor":"ar-q2-171-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-6","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"(إنَّ الهَوَى مَا تَولَّى يُصْمِ أو يَصِمِ)","anchor":"ar-q2-171-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-7","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"فلا يُقلع الهوى من قلوبهم إلا بسابق العناية، أو هبوب ريح الهداية، فتثير في قلوبهم خوفاً مُزْعِجاً، أو شوقاً مُقْلِقًا، أو نُوراً خارقاً وَما ذلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ بِعَزِيزٍ.","anchor":"ar-q2-171-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-171-8","r":"q2-171","title":"2:171 · Hearing a call without understanding it","text":"ولما فرغ من تذكير الكفار وتخويفهم ذكّر المؤمنين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-171-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-171-s1","r":"q2-171","title":"An omitted term or an unexpressed relation","text":"I say: “the likeness …” may involve an omitted annexed noun ( حذف مضاف ): “the likeness of the admonisher of those who disbelieve.” Or no such supplied term is needed, as will be explained. Naʿaqa —patterned like ḍaraba , with verbal nouns naʿq and naʿīq —means to cry out or drive away by shouting.","anchor":"en-q2-171-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-171-s2","r":"q2-171","title":"Three explanations of the shepherd’s likeness","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the likeness of one admonishing unbelievers and calling them to God is that of a shepherd tending animals and shouting to drive or call them. They hear the call, lift their heads without understanding it, then return to grazing. They hear only a call and a shout, not comprehending what he says. Similarly, those immersed in unbelief neither attend to a caller to unity nor comprehend his words: like animals, or more astray. Alternatively, the likeness of unbelievers immersed in imitation and ignorance, together with one calling them to God, is that of the animals of a person shouting to them: they hear only a call and a shout and do not comprehend his words. Or unbelievers calling upon idols, which neither hear nor understand, resemble one shouting to sheep and gaining nothing from his cries but the fatigue and trouble of calling. He then describes them figuratively as deaf, dumb and blind: deaf to hearing truth, so they do not understand it; dumb concerning speaking it; blind to observing its means, or to guidance, so they do not see it. They understand and reflect upon nothing.","anchor":"en-q2-171-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-171-s3","r":"q2-171","title":"When desire makes admonition ineffective","text":"When desire establishes itself in hearts, its cure becomes difficult, its treatment arduous and the physicians’ trouble great. Admonition does not benefit those immersed in heedlessness; warning and intimidation do not succeed with them. Their admonisher resembles one calling animals that hear only a call and a shout. Desire blinds them and deafens them to hearing the means of guidance: Desire, wherever it rules, kills or brands with disgrace. Only preceding divine care or the blowing wind of guidance removes desire from their hearts, stirring within them a fear that shakes them, a longing that troubles them, or a light that pierces through. “That is not difficult for God” [14:20; 35:17].","anchor":"en-q2-171-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-171-s4","r":"q2-171","title":"","text":"Having finished admonishing and warning unbelievers, He admonishes believers:","anchor":"en-q2-171-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-172-173","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity 2:172–173","anchor":"unit-q2-172-173"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-1","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُلُوا مِنْ طَيِّباتِ ما رَزَقْناكُمْ وَاشْكُرُوا لِلَّهِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ إِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُونَ (172) إِنَّما حَرَّمَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَيْتَةَ وَالدَّمَ وَلَحْمَ الْخِنْزِيرِ وَما أُهِلَّ بِهِ لِغَيْرِ اللَّهِ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ غَيْرَ باغٍ وَلا عادٍ فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (173)","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-2","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"قلت: أصل اضْطُرَّ: اضتُرِرَ، على وزن افتعل، من الضرر، أُبدلت التاء طاءً لقرب مخرج التاء من الطاء، قال فى الألفية:","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-3","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"طاتا افْتِعَالٍ رُدَّ إثْرَ مُطْبقِ ثم أدغمت الراء في الراء بعد ذهاب حركتها، وقرأ أبو جعفر: بكسر الطاء حيث وقع. ووجهُه: نقل حركة الراء إلى الطاء، وأصل البغي: قصد الفساد، يقال: بغي الجرح بغياً، إذا ترامى إلى الفساد، ومنه قيل للزنا: بِغاء، وللزانية:","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-4","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"بَغِيّ، وأصل العدوان: الظلم ومجاوزة الحد، يقال: عدا يعدو عُدواناً وعَدْواً.","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-5","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُلُوا من لذيذ طَيِّباتِ ما رَزَقْناكُمْ وقفوا عند ما حلَّ لكم ولا تحرموا برأيكم ما أحللنا لكم، كما فعل مَنْ سَلَفَ قبلكم، وَاشْكُرُوا نعمة الله عليكم الظاهرة والباطنة إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تخصُّونه بعبادتكم، فقد أحلّلْنا لكم جميع ما خلقنا لكم على وجه الأرض التي تُقِلكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-6","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"إِنَّما حرمنا عَلَيْكُمُ ما فيه ضررُكم كالميتة لخُبْثها، وَالدَّمَ لأنه يقسي قلوبكم، وَلَحْمَ الْخِنْزِيرِ لأنه يُورث عدم الغيرة، وما ذكر عليه غير اسم الله، وهو الذي أُهِلَّ بِهِ لِغَيْرِ اللَّهِ أي: رُفع الصوت عند ذبحه لغير الله، وهو الصنم فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ وألجئ إلى شيء من هذه المحرمات، غَيْرَ باغٍ أي: ظالم بأكلها اختياراً، وَلا عادٍ متعدّ يتعدى الحلالَ إلى الحرام، فيأكلها وهو غني عنها فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ، أو غَيْرَ باغٍ غير قاطع للطريق، وَلا عادٍ: مفارق للأمة خارج عن الجماعة، فمن خرج يقطع الرحم، أو يُخيف ابنَ السبيل، أو يُفسد في الأرض، أو أَبَق من سيده، أو فرَّ من غريمه أو عاصياً بسفره، واضطر إلى شيء من هذه، فلا تحلُّ له حتى يتوب ويأكل، إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ. وقال سهل بن عبد الله: غَيْرَ باغٍ: غير مفارق للجماعة وَلا عادٍ:","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-7","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"مبتدع مخالف للسنّة، فلم يرخص للمبتدع تناول المحرمات عند الضرورات.","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-8","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"الإشارة: يا أيها الذين آمنوا إيمانَ أهل العِرْفان، كلوا من طيبات ما رزقناكم من حلاوة الشهود والعيان، واشكروا الله الكريم المنَّان، إن كنتم تخصونه بالعبادة والإحسان، أو: يا أيها الذين آمنوا إيمان أهل الصفاء، ووقفوا مع الحدود وقوف أهل الوفاء، كلوا من طيبات ما رزقناكم من ثمرات بساتين العلوم، واشكروا لله يزدكم من المواهب والفهوم، إن كنتم تعبدون الحيّ القيوم، إنما حرَّم عليكم ما يعوقكم عن هذه المواهب، أو ينزلكم عن منابر تلك المراتب، كالميل إلى جيفة الدنيا، أو الركون إلى متابعة الهوى، أو تأخذون منها ما قُصد به غيرُ الله، أو تقبضونها من يد غير الله. فمن اضطر إلى أخذ شيء من نجاستها، فأخَذَ القدر الذي احتاج إليه منها، دون التشوُّف إلى ما زاد عليه، غير قاصد بذلك شهوة ولا متعة، فلا إثم عليه، إن الله غفور رحيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-9","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"قال شيخ شيوخنا سيدي علي الجمل رضي الله عنه لما تكلم على الغَنِيَّ بالله، قال: (علامته هو الذي ترك الدنيا للخلق، حتى لا يكون له فيها حق معهم، إلا ما فَضَل عنهم من بعد اضطراره واحتياجه، ويترك الآخرة لمولاه، حتى لا يكون له فيها حق إلا النظر في وجه الله، ويترك أيضاً نفسه لله حتى لا يكون فيها حق إلا حق مولاه، ولا إرادة له إلا ما أراد مولاه، ويكون كالغصن الرطب أينما مالت به الريح يلين ويميل معها، ولا ينكر على الخلق حالاً من أحوالهم) . هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-172-173-10","r":"q2-172-173","title":"2:172–173 · Gratitude, prohibited foods and necessity","text":"ومن جملة ما ألحق بهذه المحرمات الرّشا وأكل أموال الناس بالباطل، ولذلك ذكره الله تعالى بإثر ما أحلّه للمؤمنين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-172-173-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-172-173-s1","r":"q2-172-173","title":"Compulsion, wrongdoing and transgression","text":"I say: uḍṭurra ( اضطر ), “is compelled,” was originally uḍturira , on the pattern iftaʿala , from harm ( الضرر ). The tāʾ becomes ṭāʾ because their articulation is close. The Alfiyya says: Change the tāʾ of iftiʿāl to ṭāʾ after an emphatic consonant. The first rāʾ then loses its vowel and is assimilated to the second. Abū Jaʿfar reads the ṭāʾ with kasra wherever the word occurs, transferring the rāʾ’s vowel to it. Wrongful seeking ( البغي ) originally means aiming at corruption: baghā al-jarḥ means a wound deteriorated. Hence illicit intercourse is called bighāʾ , and a prostitute baghiyy . Transgression ( العدوان ) originally means injustice and crossing the limit, from ʿadā, yaʿdū , with verbal nouns ʿudwān and ʿadw .","anchor":"en-q2-172-173-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-172-173-s2","r":"q2-172-173","title":"The lawful gift and the limits of a necessity-based concession","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: believers, eat of the delightful good things We have provided. Stop at what is lawful for you; do not prohibit by your own opinion what We permitted, as earlier peoples did. Thank God for His outward and inward blessing if you worship Him exclusively. We have permitted everything We created upon the earth that carries you. We have forbidden only what harms you: carrion because of its foulness, blood because it hardens your hearts, swine’s flesh because it produces a loss of protective jealousy, and that over which another name than God’s has been pronounced. The last means that the voice was raised at slaughter for another than God—an idol. [B108] Whoever is driven and compelled to one of these prohibited things, without wrongdoing by freely choosing to eat it and without crossing from lawful to forbidden while having no need of it, incurs no sin. Alternatively, “neither seeking wrongdoing” means not a highway robber; “nor transgressing,” not someone separating from the community and rebelling against its united body. Thus someone travelling to sever kinship, frighten travellers or spread corruption, or an enslaved person fleeing his master, a debtor fleeing his creditor, or anyone disobedient through his journey, cannot lawfully eat these things under necessity until he repents and then eats. God is Forgiving, Merciful. Sahl ibn ʿAbd Allāh interprets “neither seeking wrongdoing” as not departing from the community, and “nor transgressing” as not an innovator opposing the Sunna. He thus grants the innovator no concession to consume prohibited things in necessity. [B109]","anchor":"en-q2-172-173-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-172-173-s3","r":"q2-172-173","title":"Necessity without attachment to the world","text":"You who believe with the faith of people of gnosis, eat the good things We have provided—the sweetness of witnessing and direct vision—and thank the Generous, Gracious God, if you single Him out in worship and excellence. Or: you who believe with the faith of the pure and observe the limits like people of fidelity, eat what We have provided from the gardens of knowledge. Thank God, and He will increase you in gifts and understanding, if you worship the Living, the Self-Subsisting. He forbids you only what obstructs these gifts or lowers you from the platforms of those ranks: inclining to the world’s carrion, resting in the pursuit of desire, taking from the world what was intended for another than God, or receiving it from another hand than God’s. Whoever is compelled to take something of its impurity, taking only what he needs without looking towards more, intending neither appetite nor enjoyment, incurs no sin. God is Forgiving, Merciful. Our masters’ master, Sīdī ʿAlī al-Jamal, speaking of one enriched through God, said: “His mark is that he leaves the world to creation, claiming no right alongside them except what remains after them when necessity and need compel him. He leaves the hereafter to his Master, claiming no right there except looking upon God’s Face. He leaves his own self to God, claiming in it no right except his Master’s right, with no will except what his Master wills. He is like a supple branch: wherever the wind bends it, it yields and bends with it. He objects to no condition of creatures.”","anchor":"en-q2-172-173-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-172-173-s4","r":"q2-172-173","title":"","text":"Among things joined to these prohibitions are bribes and consuming people’s wealth falsely. God therefore mentions this after what He has permitted believers:","anchor":"en-q2-172-173-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-174-176","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart 2:174–176","anchor":"unit-q2-174-176"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-1","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْتُمُونَ ما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الْكِتابِ وَيَشْتَرُونَ بِهِ ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً أُولئِكَ ما يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ إِلاَّ النَّارَ وَلا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ اللَّهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ وَلا يُزَكِّيهِمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ (174) أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ اشْتَرَوُا الضَّلالَةَ بِالْهُدى وَالْعَذابَ بِالْمَغْفِرَةِ فَما أَصْبَرَهُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ (175) ذلِكَ بِأَنَّ اللَّهَ نَزَّلَ الْكِتابَ بِالْحَقِّ وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ اخْتَلَفُوا فِي الْكِتابِ لَفِي شِقاقٍ بَعِيدٍ (176)","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-2","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"قلت: (ما) تعجبية، مبتدأ، وهي نكرة، وسوَّغَ الابتداء معنى التعجب، وجملة (أصبرهم) خبر، أي: أيُّ شيء عظيم صيَّرهم صابرين، أو استفهامية، أي: أيُّ شيء حملهم على الصبر على النار؟.","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-3","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في رؤساء اليهود وعلمائهم، كانوا يُصيبون من سفلتهم الهدايا والخَرَاج، ويدَّعون أن النبيّ المبعوث منهم، فلما بعث نبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم خافوا ذهاب مأكلتهم ورئاستهم، فأنزل الله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْتُمُونَ ما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ في التوراة من صفة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم، ويحرفونها في المعنى ويَنْزِعُونها مِنَ الْكِتابِ أي: التوراة، وَيَشْتَرُونَ بذلك التحريف ثَمَناً قَلِيلًا أي: عِوَضاً حقيراً يذهب ويفنَى في زمان قليل، أُولئِكَ الذين يكتمون ويأكلون ذلك العوض الحقير- ما يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ إلا نار جهنم لأنها مآلهم وعقوبة أكلهم، وَلا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ اللَّهُ إهانة وغضباً عليهم حين يُكلم أولياءه ويسلم عليهم، وَلا يُزَكِّيهِمْ أي: لا يطهرهم من دنَس ذنوبهم حتى يتأهلوا للحضرة، وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ مُوجع. أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ استبدلوا الضَّلالَةَ بِالْهُدى أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-4","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"باعوا الهدى واشتروا به الضلالة، واستبدلوا الْعَذابَ بِالْمَغْفِرَةِ التي كانت لهم لو آمنوا وبيّنوا، فما أجرأهم على اقتحام النار باقتحام أسبابها، أو فما أبقاهم في النار، أو ما الذي أصبرهم على النار حتى تركوا الحق ومالوا إلى الباطل؟! استفهام توبيخي.","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-5","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"ذلِكَ العذاب الذي استحقوه وتجرءوا عليه بسبب أن اللَّهَ تعالى نَزَّلَ الْكِتابَ القرآن ملتبساً بِالْحَقِّ، فاختلفوا فيه فآمنوا ببعض وكفروا ببعض، وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ اخْتَلَفُوا فِي الْكِتابِ لَفِي شِقاقٍ بَعِيدٍ أي: لفي خلاف وضلال بعيد.","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-6","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"الإشارة: كل من كتم علمه، ولم ينشرْه إلا في مقابلة حظ دنيوي، صَدَق عليه قولُه تعالى: وَيَشْتَرُونَ بِهِ ثَمَناً قَلِيلًا أُولئِكَ ما يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ إِلَّا النَّارَ. رُوِيَ أن بعض الصحابة كان يُقرئ أهل الصُّفّة، فأَهْدَى له أحدُهم قوساً، فأتى به النبي صلى الله عليه وسلّم، فقال: يا رسول الله: كنت أُعلِّمُ أهلَ الصفة فأهدى لي فلان قوساً، وقال: هو لله، فقال له- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «لقدْ تقلدتَ قَوسْاً مِنْ نَارِ جَهنم» . أو كما قال صلّى الله عليه وسلّم، وأمره بردِّه. ولعل هذا من باب الورع، فأراد عليه السلام أن يرفع همة ذلك الصحابي، وإلا فقد ورد في الحديث: «أَحَقُّ ما أَخَذْتُمْ علَيْهِ الأجرَ كتَابُ اللهِ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-7","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"فمن ملَكَتْه نفسه، وأسره الهوى، فقد اشترى الضلالة بالهدى، اشترى الضلالة عن طريق أولياء الله، بالهدى الذي كان له لو ملَكَ نفسه وهواه، وعذابَ القطيعة والحجاب، بالمغفرة والدخول مع الأحباب، فما أصبرهم على غم الحجاب وسوء الحساب، سبب ذلك اختلاف قلبه، وتفريق همه ولُبَّه، وقد قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «اقْرَءوا القُرْآنَ ما ائْتَلَفَتْ عليه قلوبكم، فَإِذَا اخْتَلَفْتُمْ فَقُومُوا» . أو كما قال.","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-8","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"وسبب تفرق القلب وعدم حضوره، حبُّ الدنيا فقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «مَنْ كَانَت الدُّنيا هَمَّهُ فَرَّقَ اللهُ عَلَيْه أمْرَه، وَجَعَلَ فَقْرَهُ بَيْنَ عَيْنَيْهِ ولَمْ يَأتِهِ مِنَ الدُّنْيا إلا ما قُسِمَ لَهُ، ومَن كَانَتِ الآخرةُ نيته، جَمَعَ اللهُ عليه أمْرَهُ، وَجَعَلَ غِنَاهُ في قَلْبه، وأتتْهُ الدُنيَا وَهِيَ رَاِغِمةً» .","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-9","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"والقلب الذي اختلَف في فهم الكتاب وتشتَّت عنه في شقاق بعيد عن الحضرة لأن عُنْوان صحة القلب: جمعُه على كلام الله وتدبر خطابه والتلذذ بسماعه، وقد تقدم في أول السورة درجات القراءة. فانظره إن شئت. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-174-176-10","r":"q2-174-176","title":"2:174–176 · Trading revelation for gain and the divided heart","text":"ولما ادّعت اليهود والنصارى أن البرّ خاص بقبلتهم، لأنها قبلة الأنبياء، رد الله تعالى عليهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-174-176-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-174-176-s1","r":"q2-174-176","title":"An expression of wonder or a reproachful question","text":"I say: mā is exclamatory ( تعجبية ), an indefinite subject whose use at the beginning is licensed by the sense of wonder. The clause aṣbarahum is its predicate: what a tremendous thing has made them so enduring! Or it is interrogative: what has induced them to endure the Fire?","anchor":"en-q2-174-176-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-174-176-s2","r":"q2-174-176","title":"What is gained by concealment becomes punishment","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, speaks about Jewish leaders and scholars. They received gifts and levies from the common people and claimed that the awaited prophet would arise from among them. When our Prophet Muḥammad was sent, they feared losing their livelihood and leadership. God therefore revealed: those who conceal the description of Muḥammad that God sent down in the Torah, distort its meaning and remove it from the Book, exchanging this distortion for a small price—a contemptible compensation that soon passes away—eat nothing but Hellfire in their bellies. This is their eventual destination and the punishment for their eating. God does not speak to them, to abase them and manifest anger against them, when He speaks to His friends and greets them. He does not purify them from their sins’ pollution so that they may become fit for the presence. They have a painful, grievous punishment. They sold guidance to buy error, and exchanged the forgiveness they would have received through believing and explaining for punishment. How bold they are in plunging into the Fire by plunging into its causes! Or: how long they remain in it! Or: what has made them endure it, abandoning truth and inclining to falsehood? This is a reproachful question. They deserve that punishment, and have dared approach it, because God sent down the Book—the Qurʾān—clothed in truth, but they disagreed about it, believing some and rejecting some. Those who differ concerning the Book are far gone in opposition and error.","anchor":"en-q2-174-176-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-174-176-s3","r":"q2-174-176","title":"Teaching, compensation and the dispersal of concern","text":"Whoever conceals knowledge and spreads it only in exchange for a worldly share falls under “they exchange it for a small price” and “consume nothing in their bellies but fire.” It is related that a Companion taught the People of the Bench and received a bow as a gift from one of them. He brought it to the Prophet, saying: “Messenger of God, I taught the People of the Bench, and so-and-so gave me a bow, saying it was for God.” The Prophet replied: “You have hung a bow of Hellfire about yourself,” or words to that effect, and commanded its return. Perhaps this belongs to scrupulousness ( الورع ): he wished to raise that Companion’s aspiration. Otherwise, a report states: “The thing for which you have the greatest right to take payment is God’s Book.” [B110] One possessed by his lower self and captive to desire has bought error at the price of guidance: deviation from the path of God’s friends in exchange for the guidance he would have possessed had he mastered self and desire; the punishment of severance and veiling in exchange for forgiveness and entrance among the beloved. How enduring they are of the distress of veiling and the evil reckoning! The cause is division within the heart and dispersal of its concern and understanding. The Prophet said: “Read the Qurʾān while your hearts agree upon it; when you differ, rise and leave it,” or words to that effect. The cause of the heart’s dispersion and lack of presence is love of the world. The Prophet said: “Whoever makes the world his concern, God scatters his affairs, sets his poverty between his eyes, and nothing of the world comes to him except what was allotted. Whoever makes the hereafter his intention, God gathers his affairs, places his wealth in his heart, and the world comes to him unwillingly.” [B111] A heart divided in understanding the Book and dispersed away from it is in discord far from the presence. The sign of a sound heart is its gathered attention upon God’s speech, reflection on His address and pleasure in hearing it. The degrees of recitation were discussed at the sūrah’s beginning; consult them. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-174-176-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-174-176-s4","r":"q2-174-176","title":"","text":"When the Jews and Christians claimed that righteousness belonged particularly to their prayer-direction because it was the prophets’ direction, God answered them:","anchor":"en-q2-174-176-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-177","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life 2:177","anchor":"unit-q2-177"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-1","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"لَيْسَ الْبِرُّ أَنْ تُوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ قِبَلَ الْمَشْرِقِ وَالْمَغْرِبِ وَلكِنِ الْبِرُّ مَنْ آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَالْمَلائِكَةِ وَالْكِتابِ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ وَآتَى الْمالَ عَلى حُبِّهِ ذَوِي الْقُرْبى وَالْيَتامى وَالْمَساكِينَ وَابْنَ السَّبِيلِ وَالسَّائِلِينَ وَفِي الرِّقابِ وَأَقامَ الصَّلاةَ وَآتَى الزَّكاةَ وَالْمُوفُونَ بِعَهْدِهِمْ إِذا عاهَدُوا وَالصَّابِرِينَ فِي الْبَأْساءِ وَالضَّرَّاءِ وَحِينَ الْبَأْسِ أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ صَدَقُوا وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْمُتَّقُونَ (177)","anchor":"ar-q2-177-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-2","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"قلت: لمَّا ذكر الحق تعالى التوحيد وبراهينه الذي هو رأس الدين، وحذَّرَ من الشرك وفروعه، ذكر هنا بقية أركان الدين، وهى الإيمان والإسلام، فذكر في هذه الآية قواعد الإيمان وبعض قواعدِ الإسلام وهي الصلاة والزكاة، ثم ذكر بعد ذلك الصيام وأحكامه، ثم ذكر الحج وأركانه، ثم ذكر الجهاد والنكاح والطلاق والعِدَّة، ثم ذكر البيوع وما يتعلق بها من الربا، ثم الشهادات والرهَان، وبها ختم السورة.","anchor":"ar-q2-177-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-3","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"لكن الحديث ذو شُجون، والكلام يَجُرُّ بعضُه بعضاً، فقوله: لَيْسَ الْبِرَّ أَنْ تُوَلُّوا: اسم ليس وخبرها، وكلاهما مُعَرَّفَتان، الأول بأل والثاني بالإضافة، إذ التقدير: توليةُ وجوهكم، فمن رجَّح تعريف الألف واللام، جعل (البر) اسمها، و (أن تولوا) خبرها، وبه قرأ الأكثر، ومن رجح الإضافة جعل (البر) خبرها مقدماً، والمصدر اسمها مؤخراً، وبه قرأ حمزة وحفص.","anchor":"ar-q2-177-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-4","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"وقوله: وَلكِنَّ الْبِرَّ مَنْ خَفَّفَ جعلها عاطفة الجملة، والْبِرَّ مبتدأ، و (من آمن) خبر على حذف مضاف، أَيْ: بِرُّ من آمن إذ لا يُخْبَرُ بالذات عن المعنى، أو قصد المبالغة، ومن شدَّد نصب بها، لوقوعها بين","anchor":"ar-q2-177-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-5","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"جملتين، وهى استدراكية، وعَلى حُبِّهِ حال من المال، والصَّابِرِينَ نصب على المدح، ولم يعطفه بالرفع لفضل الصبر وشرفه.","anchor":"ar-q2-177-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-6","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في الرد على أهل الكتاب: لَيْسَ الْبِرَّ محصوراً في شأن القبلة، وَلكِنَّ الْبِرَّ الذي ينبغي أن يُعتنى بشأنه هو الإيمان بالله، وما يجب له من الكمالات، وباليوم الآخر وما بعده، وبالملائكة وما يجب أن يعتقد في شأنهم، والكتاب المنزل من السماء كالقرآن وغيره، والنَّبِيِّينَ وما يجب لهم وما يستحيل في حقهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-177-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-7","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"فالبر هو بر من اعتقد في قلبه هذه الأشياء، وأظهر على جوارحه ما يصدق صحة اعتقادها، وذلك كالاتصاف بالسخاء والكرم، فأعطى المال على محبته له، أي: مع حبه، فقد سئل- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «أىّ الصّدقة أفضل؟ فقال: أن تَتَصَدَّقَ وأَنْتَ صَحِيحٌ شَحِيحٌ، تأمُلُ الْغِنَى وتَخشَى الفقر» . وَآتَى الْمالَ على حب الله، لا جزاءً ولا شكوراً، فأعطى ذلك المال ذوي قرابته المحَاويج، وقدَّمهم لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-:","anchor":"ar-q2-177-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-8","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"«صَدَقَتُك على المَساكينِ صَدَقَةٌ، وعَلَى ذَوِي القُربى اثنتان صَدَقَةٌ وصِلَةٌ» . وأعطى الْيَتامى لإهمالهم، وأعطى الْمَساكِينَ الذين أسكنهم الفقر في بيوتهم، وَابْنَ السَّبِيلِ وهو المسافر الغريب، كأن الطريق وَلَدْته، أو الضيف وَالسَّائِلِينَ ألجأتهم الحاجة إلى السؤال. وفي الحديث: «أَعْطِ السائِلَ ولو على فَرَسِه» . وقال أيضاً صلّى الله عليه وسلّم: «هَدِيَّةُ اللهِ إلى المؤمن السائلُ على بَابِه» . وأعطى في فك الرِّقابِ من الرق أو الأسر.","anchor":"ar-q2-177-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-9","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"وَأَقامَ الصَّلاةَ المفروضة، وَآتَى الزَّكاةَ المعلومة. ومن أهل البر أيضاً: الْمُوفُونَ بِعَهْدِهِمْ فيما بينهم وبين الله، وفيما بينهم وبين الناس إِذا عاهَدُوا الله أو عباده، فإذا وعدوا أنجزوا، وإذا حلفوا أو نذروا أوفوا، وإذا قالوا صدقوا، وإذا ائتمنوا أدَّوْا، وأخُصُّ من أهل البر الصَّابِرِينَ فِي الْبَأْساءِ كالفقر والذل وإذاية الخلق، والضَّرَّاءِ كالمرض والزَّمَانة ، أو (البأساء) : الأهوال، و (الضراء) في الأنفس، والصابرين حِينَ الْبَأْسِ أي: الحرب والجهاد، أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ صَدَقُوا في طلب الحق، وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْمُتَّقُونَ لكل ما يقطع عن الحق، أو يشغل عنه. فقد اشتملت هذه الآية على كمالات الإنسان بأسرها لاشتمالها على ما يَزِين البواطنَ من الاعتقادات وما يزين الظواهر من المعاملات، وما يُزَكِّي النفوس من الرذائل ويُحَلِّيها بالمحاسن والكمالات. ولذلك","anchor":"ar-q2-177-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-10","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"وُصف المتصف بها بالصدق والتقى، اللذين هما أساسُ الطريقة ومبنَى أسرار التحقيق، وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-177-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-11","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"الإشارة: ليس المطلوب من العبد أن يَتَوجَّه إلى الحق بجِهَةٍ مخصوصة، كما إذا توجه إليه بالظاهر وأهملَ الباطن، أو توجه بالباطن وأهمل الظاهر، ولكن المطلوب منه أن يُزين باطنه بأنوار الإيمان واليقين، ويزين ظاهره بسائر وظائف الدين، ويزكي نفسه من الرذائل كالشح والبخل والغش والخيانة والكذب والخَوْف والجزَع، ويحليها بأنواع الفضائل كالسخاء والكرم والوفاء بالعهد والأمانة، والصبر والشجاعة، والعفة والقناعة، وسائر أنواع الفضائل، فإذا تخلّى عن الرذائل وتحلّى بأضدادها من الفضائل استحق الدخول مع الأبرار، وكان من العارفين الكبار، أولئك الذين ظفروا بصدق الطلب فنالوا الغاية من كل مطلب، وأولئك هم المتقون حق التقاة، فنالوا أعلى الدرجات، منحنا الله من ذلك الحظ الوافر بمنّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-177-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-177-12","r":"q2-177","title":"2:177 · Righteousness as the perfection of inward and outward life","text":"ولمّا مدح الله تعالى الصبر والجرأة فى الحرب، أمر بالقصاص لئلا يتسع الناس فى إطلاق الجرأة، حتى يتجرءوا على قتل المسلم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-177-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-177-s1","r":"q2-177","title":"The pillars of religion and the verse’s constructions","text":"I say: having mentioned unity and its proofs, the head of religion, and warned against association and its branches, the Real now mentions the remaining pillars: faith ( الإيمان ) and Islam. This verse gives the foundations of faith and some foundations of Islam, prayer and the purifying alms. Afterwards He mentions fasting and its rulings, pilgrimage and its pillars, then holy struggle, marriage, divorce and the waiting period, then sales and their connected question of usury, and finally testimony and pledges, with which the sūrah concludes. Discourse, however, branches out, one matter drawing another after it. “Righteousness” and “that you turn” are the subject and predicate of laysa . Both are definite, the first through the article and the second through annexation, since the latter means “your turning your faces.” Whoever gives priority to definiteness through the article makes “righteousness” the subject and “that you turn” the predicate: this is the majority reading. Whoever gives priority to annexation makes “righteousness” the fronted predicate and the verbal-noun clause the postponed subject: this is the reading of Ḥamza and Ḥafṣ. In “but righteousness,” whoever lightens lakin makes it a conjunction joining clauses. “Righteousness” is then a subject and “one who believes” its predicate, with an omitted annexed term: “the righteousness of one who believes,” since an entity is not predicated of an abstract meaning. Alternatively, the expression is intentionally emphatic. Whoever doubles the nūn makes lākinn govern the accusative, occurring between two clauses with corrective force ( استدراكية ). “Despite loving it” is a circumstantial qualifier of the wealth. “Those patient” is accusative in praise ( النصب على المدح ), not coordinated in the nominative, because of patience’s excellence and nobility.","anchor":"en-q2-177-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-177-s2","r":"q2-177","title":"Faith, generosity, fidelity and endurance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, answers the People of the Book: righteousness is not confined to the prayer-direction. What deserves attention is faith in God and the perfections necessary to Him; the Last Day and what follows it; the angels and what must be believed about them; the Book sent from heaven, the Qurʾān and other scriptures; and the prophets, what is necessary to them and what is impossible concerning them. Righteousness belongs to one who believes these matters in his heart and manifests upon his limbs what confirms that belief’s soundness. Thus he possesses generosity and liberality, giving wealth while loving it. Asked what charity is best, the Prophet answered: “That you give while healthy and reluctant to part with it, hoping for wealth and fearing poverty.” Or he gives wealth out of love for God, seeking neither repayment nor thanks. [B112] He gives to needy relatives, placed first because the Prophet said: “Your charity to the needy is charity; to relatives it is two things: charity and maintaining kinship.” He gives to orphans because they lack care, to the needy whom poverty has made remain in their homes, and to the wayfarer—the traveller away from home, as though the road had borne him—or the guest. He gives to those whom need drives to ask. A report says: “Give to the beggar even if he is upon his horse.” Another says: “God’s gift to the believer is the beggar at his door.” He gives to free people from slavery or captivity. [B113] He establishes obligatory prayer and gives the known purifying alms. Among the righteous are those fulfilling their covenants with God and with people. When they promise, they perform; when they swear or vow, they fulfil; when they speak, they tell the truth; when trusted, they discharge the trust. I especially praise the patient in adversity—poverty, abasement and people’s harm—and affliction—illness and chronic disability. Or the first means terrors, and the second bodily afflictions. They are patient at the time of battle and holy struggle. They are truthful in seeking the Real and guard against whatever cuts them off from Him or distracts them from Him. This verse encompasses all human perfections: what adorns the inward life through beliefs, what adorns the outward life through dealings, and what purifies souls from vices and clothes them in good qualities and perfections. Hence those possessing these qualities are described as truthful and God-fearing, the two foundations of the Path and the basis of realization’s secrets. Through God is success; He guides to the sound road.","anchor":"en-q2-177-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-177-s3","r":"q2-177","title":"Neither the outward nor the inward may be neglected","text":"The servant is not asked to turn towards the Real in one particular respect alone, as by turning outwardly while neglecting the inward, or inwardly while neglecting the outward. Rather, he must adorn his inward life with the lights of faith and certainty and his outward life with religion’s various duties. He must purify his soul from vices—greed, miserliness, fraud, betrayal, lying, fear and anguish—and adorn it with virtues: generosity, liberality, fidelity to covenants, trustworthiness, patience, courage, chastity, contentment and every other virtue. When he empties himself of vices and adorns himself with their opposite virtues, he deserves entrance among the righteous and becomes one of the great gnostics. These have attained sincerity in seeking and thus the goal of every quest. They truly fear God and attain the highest degrees. May God grant us an abundant share through His grace and generosity.","anchor":"en-q2-177-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-177-s4","r":"q2-177","title":"","text":"Having praised patience and courage in battle, God commands just retaliation, lest people extend courage’s scope and dare kill a Muslim:","anchor":"en-q2-177-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-178-179","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life 2:178–179","anchor":"unit-q2-178-179"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-1","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِصاصُ فِي الْقَتْلى الْحُرُّ بِالْحُرِّ وَالْعَبْدُ بِالْعَبْدِ وَالْأُنْثى بِالْأُنْثى فَمَنْ عُفِيَ لَهُ مِنْ أَخِيهِ شَيْءٌ فَاتِّباعٌ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَأَداءٌ إِلَيْهِ بِإِحْسانٍ ذلِكَ تَخْفِيفٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ فَمَنِ اعْتَدى بَعْدَ ذلِكَ فَلَهُ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ (178) وَلَكُمْ فِي الْقِصاصِ حَياةٌ يا أُولِي الْأَلْبابِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ (179)","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-2","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"قلت: (عفا) لازمٌ يتعدى بالحرف: بعَنْ إلى الجناية، وباللام إلى الجاني، فيقال: عفوت لفلان عن جنايته و (اتباع) خبر عن مضمر، أي: فالأمر اتباع، و (حياة) مبتدأ، و (في القصاص) خبره، و (لكم) خبر ثان، أو صلة له، أو حال من الضمير المستكِنْ فيه. وفيه من البلاغة والفصاحة ما لا يخفى، جعل الشيء محيي ضده، وعرّف القصاص ونكْر الحياة ليدل على التعظيم والتعميم، أي: ولكم نوع من الحياة عظيم، وذلك لأن العلم به يَرْدَع القاتل عن القتل، فيكون سببَ حياةِ نَفْسَيْن، ولأنهم كانوا يقتلون غير القاتل، والجماعة بالواحد، فتثور الفتنة بينهم، فإذا اقتُصّ من القاتل سَلِم الباقون، ويصيرُ ذلك سبباً لحياتهم. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-3","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أيها المؤمنون كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِصاصُ فِي شأن الْقَتْلى في العَمْد، فاستسلِموا للقصاص، فالحُر يُقتل بِالْحُرِّ، ولا يقتل بالعبد. بل يغرم قيمته لسيده، ودليله قوله- عليه الصلاة","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-4","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"والسلام-: «لا يُقتل مسلمٌ بكافرٍ ولا حرٌ بعبدٍ» ، والعبد يقتل بالعبد، إن أراد سيد المقتول قتله، فإن استحياه خُيِّر سيدُه بين إسلامه وفدائه بقيمة العبد. وكذلك إن قُتل الحر خُيّر أولياؤُه بين قتله أو استرقاقه، فإن استحيَوْه خُيِّر سيدُه بين إسلامه وفدائه بِدِيَةِ الحر العَمْد، والأنثى تُقتل بالأنثى والذكر، والذكر يقتل بالأنثى.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-5","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"وتخصيصُ الآية بالمُساوي، قال مالك: (أحسنُ ما سمعتُ في هذه الآية: أنه يُراد بها الجنسُ- أي: جنس الحر- والذكر والأنثى فيه سواء. وأعيدَ ذِكْرُ الأنثى تأكيداً وتهمُّمَا بإذهاب أمر الجاهلية) . هـ. يعني أن (أل) في الحر:","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-6","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"للجنس، تشمل الذكر والأنثى. وأعاد ذكر الأنثى اهتماماً بردِّ ما كان يفعله الجاهلية من عدم القَودَ فيها.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-7","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"ثم قال الحق جلّ جلاله: فَمَنْ عُفِيَ لَهُ مِنْ دم أخيه شَيْءٌ ولو قَلَّ، فقد سقط القتل، فالواجب اتباعٌ للقاتل بالدية بِالْمَعْرُوفِ من غير تعنيف ولا تعنيت، وأَداءٌ من القاتل بِإِحْسانٍ من غير مطل ولا بَخس.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-8","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"ذلِكَ- الذي شرعْتُ لكم من أمر العفو والديّة- تَخْفِيفٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ بكم، وقد كُتب على اليهود القصاص وحده، وعلى النصارى العفو مطلقاً. وخيَّركم أيها الأمة المحمدية بين أخذ الديّة والقصاص. فَمَنِ اعْتَدى بعد أخذ الديّة وقَتَل فَلَهُ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ في الدنيا والآخرة، في الدنيا: بأن يُقتل لا محالة لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «لا أُعَافِي أحَداً قَتَلَ بَعْدَ أَخْذِ الدِّيَة» .","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-9","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"وَلَكُمْ يا معشر المسلمين فِي تشريع الْقِصاصِ حَياةٌ عظيمة في الدنيا، لانزجار القاتل إذا علَم أنه يُقتص منه، وقد كانوا يَقتُلون الجماعةَ في الواحد، فسلِموا من القتل بشروع القصاص، أو في الآخرة، فإن القاتل إذا اقتُصَّ منه في الدنيا لم يؤخذْ به في الآخرة، فاعتُبِروا يا أُولِي الْأَلْبابِ أي: العقول الكاملة، ما في حكمة القصاص من استبقاء الأرواح وحفظ النفوس، لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ الله في المحافظة على القصاص، والحكم به والإذعان له، أو تَكُفُّون عن القتل خوفاً من الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-10","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"الإشارة: كما جعل الله القصاص في الجناية الحسيّة، جعل القصاصَ في الجناية المعنوية، وهي الجنايةُ على النفس بسوء الأدب مع الله، فكل من صدر منه هفوةٌ أو زَلَّة، اقْتصَ الحقّ تعالى منه في دار الدنيا، إن كانت له من الله عناية، الكبيرة بالكبيرة والصغيرة بالصغيرة. وتأمَّلْ قضية الرجل الذي كان يطوف بالكعبة، فنظر إلى امرأة، فلطَمْته كَفٍّ من الهوى، وذهبت عينه، فقال: آه، فقيل له: لطمة بنظرة، وإن زدت زدنا. هـ. وقضية أبي تراب النخشبي: قال رضي الله عنه: ما تمنت نفسي شهوةً من الشهوات إلا مرة واحدة، تمنيت خبزاً وبيضاً وأنا في سفر، فعدلت إلى قرية، فقام واحد، وتعلّق بي، وقال: هذا رأيته مع اللصوص، فضربوني سبعين درة، ثم عرفني رجلٌ منهم، وحملني إلى منزله، وقدَّم لي خبزاً وبيضاً. فقلت في نفسي: كُلْ بعد سبعين درة.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-11","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"وقضية أبى الخير العسقلاني: اشتهى السمك فلما مد يده ليأكل أخذت شوكة من عظامها إصبعَه، فذهبت في ذلك يده. وقضية إبراهيم بن شيبان: قال: (اشتهيت شبعة من الخبز والعدس، فاتفق ذلك، فأكلت حتى شبعت، ثم رأيت منكرا، فغيرته، فأخذونى وضربونى مائة خشبة، وطرحونى فى السجن أربعة أشهر، حتى شفع فىّ شيخى، فخرجت، وقال: أخذتها مجانا) ، أي: حيث عوقبت فى ظاهرك دون باطنك.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-12","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"وقضية خير النسّاج: قال: (عاهدت الله وعقدت ألا آكل الرطب فغلبتني نفسى، فأخذت نصف رطل، فلما أكلت واحدة إذا برجل نظر إلىّ وقال: يا خير، أين هربت منى؟ وكان له عبد اسمه خير، فوقع علىّ شبهه- قال:","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-13","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"فبقيت معه عدة أشهر أنسج له الكرباس- وهو القطن الأبيض-، ثم تبت فزال عنى الشّبه) .","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-14","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"فمن عفى له عن شىء من هذه الجناية، بعد الأدب أو قبله، فليشكر الله، ويتبع ما أمره به، ويؤدى ما فرضه عليه بالمعروف، من غير إسراف، ولا تقصير، ذلك تخفيف من الله عنه، ورحمة به، فمن اعتدى بعد ذلك، ورجع إلى ما تاب عنه فله عذاب أليم، وهو الطرد عن حضرة الأحباب، إلى الوقوف بالباب أو سياسة الدواب، إلا من تاب وعمل صالحا فإن الله يتوب على من تاب. ولكم فى القصاص فى دار الدنيا- حياة عظيمة لأرواحكم وأسراركم لأن ذلك اعتناء بكم يا أولى الألباب، لعلكم تتقون كل ما يشغلكم عن مولاكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-178-179-15","r":"q2-178-179","title":"2:178–179 · Just retaliation, mercy and the preservation of life","text":"ولمّا ذكر القصاص وهو مظنّة الموت، والموت من أسباب الوصية ذكرها بإثره، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-178-179-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-178-179-s1","r":"q2-178-179","title":"A consequence opposite to its apparent cause","text":"I say: ʿafā is intransitive and takes a preposition: ʿan introduces the offence, and li- the offender. One says, “I pardoned so-and-so for his offence.” “Pursuit” is the predicate of an implied subject: the required course is pursuit according to what is right. “Life” is a subject, “in retaliation” its predicate; “for you” is a second predicate, a complement of the first, or a circumstantial qualification of its implicit pronoun. The eloquence and rhetorical force are evident: He makes something bring about its opposite, makes retaliation definite and life indefinite to signify greatness and generality—there is for you a tremendous kind of life. Knowledge of retaliation deters a killer from killing and thus preserves two lives. Previously people killed someone other than the killer, or a group for one person, setting strife ablaze. Retaliation against the killer spares the rest and becomes a cause of their life. Thus al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q2-178-179-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-178-179-s2","r":"q2-178-179","title":"Retaliation, remission and compensation","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: believers, retaliation concerning deliberate killing is prescribed for you; submit to it. A free person is killed for a free person, not for an enslaved person; in the latter case he pays the person’s value to the owner. Its proof is the reported saying: “A Muslim is not killed for an unbeliever, nor a free person for an enslaved person.” An enslaved person is killed for another enslaved person if the slain person’s owner demands it. If he spares the killer, the killer’s owner chooses between surrendering him and redeeming him for the value of the slain person. Likewise, if an enslaved person kills a free person, the latter’s heirs choose between killing and enslaving him. If they spare him, his owner chooses between surrendering him and redeeming him with the compensation for a free person deliberately killed. A woman is killed for a woman or a man, and a man for a woman. [B114] Concerning the verse’s specification of equivalents, Mālik said: “The best explanation I have heard is that the kind is intended—the kind ‘free person’—in which male and female are equal. The woman is mentioned again for emphasis and out of concern to abolish pagan practice.” That is, the article in “the free” denotes the kind, embracing male and female. The woman is repeated particularly to reject the pre-Islamic refusal of retaliation for her. The Real then says: whoever has anything, however little, remitted concerning his brother’s blood, the execution falls away. The duty is then to pursue the killer for compensation according to what is right, without harshness or unreasonable pressure; and the killer must pay with goodness, without delay or short payment. This legislation of remission and compensation is a lightening from your Lord and a mercy to you. The Jews were prescribed retaliation alone, the Christians unconditional pardon, while you, the Muḥammadan community, are given the choice between compensation and retaliation. [B115] Whoever transgresses after receiving compensation and then kills faces painful punishment in this world and the next. In this world he is necessarily executed, according to the reported saying: “I shall not spare anyone who kills after taking compensation.” Muslims, in legislating retaliation there is tremendous life for you in this world: a would-be killer is deterred by knowing that retaliation will be exacted. People previously killed a group for one person and were spared this through retaliation’s institution. Or there is life in the hereafter: a killer against whom retaliation is carried out here is not taken to account for it there. People of complete understanding, consider the preservation of spirits and protection of lives within this wisdom, so that you fear God in maintaining retaliation, judging by it and submitting to it—or refrain from killing out of fear of God.","anchor":"en-q2-178-179-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-178-179-s3","r":"q2-178-179","title":"Correction of inward offences","text":"As God appoints retaliation for sensory offences, He appoints it for inward offences: injuring one’s own soul through discourtesy towards God. Whoever commits a lapse or slip receives recompense from the Real in this world, if divine care attends him: a great offence for a great one, a small for a small. Consider the man circumambulating the Kaʿba who looked at a woman. A hand struck him from the air and his eye was lost. He cried out and was told, “A blow for a glance; if you increase, We increase.” Consider Abū Turāb al-Nakhshabī: “My soul desired an appetite only once. Travelling, I desired bread and eggs and turned aside to a village. Someone seized me, saying he had seen me with thieves, and they struck me seventy times. A man then recognized me, took me home and served bread and eggs. I told myself: eat—after seventy blows.” [B116] Consider Abū al-Khayr al-ʿAsqalānī: he desired fish, and when he reached to eat, a fishbone pierced his finger; his hand was lost through it. Ibrāhīm ibn Shaybān said: “I desired my fill of bread and lentils, and when they became available I ate until full. Then I saw a wrong and sought to change it. They seized me, beat me a hundred times with a stick and imprisoned me for four months, until my shaykh interceded. When I emerged, he said, ‘You received it cheaply’”—that is, punishment touched his outward, not his inward, condition. Khayr al-Nassāj said: “I covenanted with God not to eat fresh dates. My soul overcame me and I took half a raṭl. When I ate one, a man looked at me and said, ‘Khayr, where have you escaped from me?’ He owned a slave named Khayr, and I had been made to resemble him. I remained with him several months weaving kirbās , white cotton cloth. Then I repented, and the resemblance left me.” Whoever receives pardon for any such offence, before or after correction, should thank God, follow His command and perform His obligations according to what is right, without excess or neglect. This is a lightening and mercy from God. Whoever transgresses thereafter and returns to what he repented of has painful punishment: expulsion from the beloved’s presence to stand at the door or tend the animals—except one who repents and acts rightly, for God accepts repentance. In recompense in this world there is tremendous life for your spirits and secrets, people of understanding, for it is care for you, so that you guard against all that distracts you from your Master.","anchor":"en-q2-178-179-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-178-179-s4","r":"q2-178-179","title":"","text":"Retaliation is an occasion of death, and death an occasion for a bequest. Having mentioned the former, He follows it with the latter:","anchor":"en-q2-178-179-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-180-182","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge 2:180–182","anchor":"unit-q2-180-182"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-1","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذا حَضَرَ أَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ إِنْ تَرَكَ خَيْراً الْوَصِيَّةُ لِلْوالِدَيْنِ وَالْأَقْرَبِينَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُتَّقِينَ (180) فَمَنْ بَدَّلَهُ بَعْدَ ما سَمِعَهُ فَإِنَّما إِثْمُهُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ يُبَدِّلُونَهُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ (181) فَمَنْ خافَ مِنْ مُوصٍ جَنَفاً أَوْ إِثْماً فَأَصْلَحَ بَيْنَهُمْ فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (182)","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-2","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"قلت: إِذا حَضَرَ ظرف، العامل فيه: كُتِبَ، أي: توجَّهَ إيجابُ الوصية عليكم إذا حضر الموت. أو مصدر محذوف يفهم من الوصية، أي: كتب عليكم الإيصاء إذا حضر الموت، والْوَصِيَّةُ","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-3","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"نائب فاعل كُتِبَ، ولا يصح أن تعمل في (إذا) لتقدمه عليها لأن المصدر لا يعمل في ما قبله، إلا على مذهب الأخفش. اللهم إلا أن يتوسع في الظروف، وجواب الشرطين محذوف، أي: إذا حضر أحدكم الموت، إن ترك خيراً، فقد كُتبت عليه الوصية.","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-4","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"والجنَف: الميل عن الصواب، فإن كان خطأ فهو جَنَفٌ بلا إثم، وإن كان عمداً فهو جنَف إثم.","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-5","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: كتب الله عَلَيْكُمْ أن تُوصوا للوالدين والأقربين إِذا حَضَرَ أَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ، إِنْ تَرَكَ المستحضر خَيْراً أي: مالاً، قال سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه-: (ألف درهم فصاعداً، فلا وصية في أقل) .","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-6","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"وقال النخعي: (خمسمائة درهم لا أقل) . وقال الزُّهْرِي: (تجب فيما قلّ وكَثُر) ، وعن عائشة- رضى الله عنها-:","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-7","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"(أن رجلاً أراد أن يوصي، فسألته: كم مالُك؟ فقال: ثلاثة آلاف. فقالت: كم عِيالك؟ فقال: أربعة، فقالت: لا، إنما قال الله تعالى إِنْ تَرَكَ خَيْراً وإن هذا لشيء يسير، فاتركْه لعيالك) .","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-8","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"وتكون تلك الوصية بِالْمَعْرُوفِ، أي: بالعدل، فلا يُفضل الذكور، ولا يتجاوز الثلث. قد حَقَّ الله ذلك حَقًّا واجباً عَلَى الْمُتَّقِينَ، فمَن غيَّره من الأوصياء أو الشهود بَعْدَ ما سَمِعَهُ وعلمه، فَإِنَّما إِثْمُهُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ يُبَدِّلُونَهُ من الأوصياء أو الشهود، لأنه هو الذي خالف الشرع وغيَّر دون الميت، إِنَّ اللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ فلا يخفى عليه مَنْ بدَّل أو غيَّر، فهو حسيبُه ومُعاقبه، فَمَنْ خافَ أي: علِم مِنْ مُوصٍ جَنَفاً أي: ميلاً بالخطأ في الوصية، أَوْ إِثْماً تعمداً للجنف، فَأَصْلَحَ بين المُوصَى لهم وبين الورثة، بأن أجراهم على منهاج الشرع، أو نقص للموصَى لهم، أو زاد لمصلحة رآها فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ لأنه تبديل لمصلحة. والتبديل الذي فيه الإثم إنما هو تبديل الهوى، إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ فيغفر للمبدِّل لمصلحةٍ ويرحمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-9","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"وهذه الآية منسوخة في وصية الوالدين، مُحْكَمة في الأقربين غير الوارثين، بقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام- فى الحديث المشهور: «إنَّ اللهَ أعْطَى كل ذي حق حقه. فلا وَصِيَّةَ لِوَارثٍ» ، فإذا كان الوالدان غيرَ وارثيْن كالكافرَيْن أو العبدَيْن فهي مُحْكَمة، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-10","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن المريد إذا منع نفسه من الشهوات، وحفظ قلبه من الخطَرَات، وصان سرّه من الغَفَلات- وأعظمُ الشهوات حبُّ الرئاسة والجاه، فإذا قتل نفسه ونزل بها إلى السُّفْليات حتى حَضرها الموت، وانقطع عنها الخواطر والخيالات- فإنها تفيض بالعلوم والواردات، فالواجب من طريق الجزم أن يقيد تلك العلوم، أو يوصي مَنْ يقيدها لينتفع بها الوالدان وهما الأشياخ، والأقربون وهم الإخوان. فإن الحكمة تَرِدُ في حال التجلي كالجبَل، فإن لم يقيدها وأهملها رجعت كالجمل، فإن أهملها رجعت كالكبش، فإن أهملها رجعت كالطير، ثم ترجع كالبَيْضة ثم تذهب. هكذا كان يقول شيخ شيوخنا سيدي علي الجمل رضي الله عنه، وكان شيخه سيدي العربي بن عبد الله يقول له:","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-11","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"(إن ورد عليك واردٌ فقَيِّدْه وأعطني منه نسخة) . وهكذا كان أشياخنا يأمروننا بتقييد الواردات، فَمنْ قَيَّدَ وارداً","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-12","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"أو سمعه من غيره، فلا يُغيرْه بمجرد رأيه وهواه. فإن تحقق منه نقصاً أو ميلاً عن منهاج الطريقة والحقيقة، فأصلحه، فلا إثم عليه، إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ.","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-180-182-13","r":"q2-180-182","title":"2:180–182 · Bequests, correction and the preservation of inspired knowledge","text":"ولما ذكر في الآية المتقدمة قاعدتين من قواعد الإسلام في قوله: وَأَقامَ الصَّلاةَ وَآتَى الزَّكاةَ، بعد أن ذكر قواعد الإيمان، ذكر هنا القاعدة الثالثة، وهي الصيام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-180-182-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-180-182-s1","r":"q2-180-182","title":"The governing expression and two forms of deviation","text":"I say: “when death approaches” is an adverbial expression governed by “is prescribed”: the obligation of a bequest is directed to you when death approaches. Alternatively its governor is an omitted verbal noun understood from “bequest”: making a bequest when death approaches is prescribed for you. “Bequest” is the passive subject ( نائب فاعل ) of “is prescribed.” It cannot itself govern “when,” which precedes it, because a verbal noun does not govern what comes before it, except according to al-Akhfash—or unless latitude is allowed with adverbial expressions. The consequences of both conditions are omitted: when death approaches one of you, if he leaves wealth, a bequest is prescribed for him. Deviation ( الجنف ) is inclining from what is right. If mistaken, it is deviation without sin; if deliberate, sinful deviation.","anchor":"en-q2-180-182-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-180-182-s2","r":"q2-180-182","title":"Bequests to relatives and alteration for a legitimate purpose","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: God prescribed that you make bequests to parents and near relatives when death approaches, if the dying person leaves good—that is, wealth. Our master ʿAlī said: “A thousand dirhams or more; no bequest below that.” Al-Nakhaʿī said five hundred dirhams, not less. Al-Zuhrī held it obligatory for little or much. ʿĀʾisha is reported to have asked a man wishing to make a bequest how much wealth he had. He answered, “Three thousand.” She asked how many dependants he had; he answered, “Four.” She said, “No. God says only, ‘if he leaves good.’ This is little; leave it for your dependants.” The bequest must accord with what is right: justice, without favouring males or exceeding one-third. God has established this as a binding duty upon the God-fearing. If an executor or witness changes it after hearing and knowing it, the sin rests upon those changing it, not upon the deceased, for they oppose revealed law. God is Hearing, Knowing: no alteration is hidden from Him; He calls its author to account and punishes him. Whoever fears—that is, knows—mistaken partiality or deliberate sinful deviation in a testator, and reconciles the beneficiaries with the heirs by bringing them into conformity with revealed law, reducing what the beneficiaries receive or increasing it for a perceived legitimate benefit, incurs no sin. This is alteration for benefit. Sinful alteration is that arising from desire. God is Forgiving, Merciful, forgiving and showing mercy to one who alters for a proper benefit. This verse is abrogated concerning bequests to parents but remains operative for non-inheriting relatives, by the well-known report: “God has given everyone entitled his right; there is no bequest to an heir.” If the parents do not inherit, as when they are unbelievers or enslaved, the verse remains operative. And God Most High knows best. [B117]","anchor":"en-q2-180-182-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-180-182-s3","r":"q2-180-182","title":"Writing down the inspirations before their force diminishes","text":"Know that when the aspirant restrains his lower self from appetites, preserves his heart from passing thoughts and guards his secret from heedlessness—the greatest appetites being leadership and rank—and puts the self to death, lowering it into humble conditions until death approaches it and thoughts and imaginings cease, knowledge and inspirations flow abundantly. He must firmly undertake to record this knowledge or charge someone to record it, so that the parents—the shaykhs—and near relatives—the brethren—may benefit. Wisdom arrives in self-disclosure like a mountain. If neglected and not recorded, it becomes like a camel; neglected further, like a ram; then like a bird, then an egg, then disappears. Thus our masters’ master, Sīdī ʿAlī al-Jamal, used to say. His shaykh, Sīdī al-ʿArabī ibn ʿAbd Allāh, would tell him: “When an inspiration comes to you, record it and give me a copy.” Our shaykhs likewise instructed us to record inspirations. Whoever records one, or hears it from another, must not change it by mere opinion and desire. If he establishes that it contains a deficiency or deviation from the Path and Reality and corrects it, he incurs no sin. God is Forgiving, Merciful.","anchor":"en-q2-180-182-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-180-182-s4","r":"q2-180-182","title":"","text":"After the foundations of faith, the earlier verse mentioned two pillars of Islam—“establishes prayer and gives the purifying alms.” Here He mentions the third, fasting:","anchor":"en-q2-180-182-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-183-185","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention 2:183–185","anchor":"unit-q2-183-185"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-1","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الصِّيامُ كَما كُتِبَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ (183) أَيَّاماً مَعْدُوداتٍ فَمَنْ كانَ مِنْكُمْ مَرِيضاً أَوْ عَلى سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ وَعَلَى الَّذِينَ يُطِيقُونَهُ فِدْيَةٌ طَعامُ مِسْكِينٍ فَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْراً فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَهُ وَأَنْ تَصُومُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (184) شَهْرُ رَمَضانَ الَّذِي أُنْزِلَ فِيهِ الْقُرْآنُ هُدىً لِلنَّاسِ وَبَيِّناتٍ مِنَ الْهُدى وَالْفُرْقانِ فَمَنْ شَهِدَ مِنْكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ وَمَنْ كانَ مَرِيضاً أَوْ عَلى سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ بِكُمُ الْيُسْرَ وَلا يُرِيدُ بِكُمُ الْعُسْرَ وَلِتُكْمِلُوا الْعِدَّةَ وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا اللَّهَ عَلى ما هَداكُمْ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ (185)","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-2","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"قلت: (أياماً) منصوب على الظرفية، واختُلِف في العامل فيه، والأحسنُ أنه الصيام، ولا يضره الفصل لأن الظرف يُتوسع فيه ما لا يتوسع في غيره، و (معدودات) نعت له، و (عدة) مبتدأ أي: فَعَليْهِ عِدَّةٌ. و (أُخر) ممنوع من الصرف للعدل عن الألف واللام والوصف. و (شهر رمضان) إما خبر عن مضمر، أو مبتدأ، والخبر: (فمن شهد) ، أو بدل من (الصيام) ، على حذف مضاف، أي: صيام شهر رمضان.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-3","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"و (رمضان) مصدر رمَض إذا احترق، وأضيف إليه الشهر، وجُعل عَلَما، ومُنع من الصرف للعلَمية والألف والنون. وسَمَّوْه بذلك إما لارتماض القلب فيه من حر الجوع والعطش، أو لارتماض الذنوب فيه، أو وافق الحرَّ حين نقلوا الشهور عن اللغة القديمة. و (الشهر) ظرف، لقوله: (شهد) أي: حضر، وقوله (ولتكملوا ... ) الآية، هذه ثلاثُ عِللَ لثلاثة أحكام على سبيل اللفّ والنَّشْرِ المعكوس، أي: ولتكملوا العدة أمرتُكم بقضاء عدة أيام أخر، ولتكبروا الله عند تمام الشهر أمرتُكم بصيام الشهر كله، ولعلكم تشكرون أردتُ بكم اليسر دون العسر.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-4","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا فُرض عليكم الصِّيامُ كما فرض عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ من الأنبياء وأممهم من لدن آدم، فلكم فيهم أسوة، فلا يشق عليكم لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ المعاصي، فإن الصوم يكسر الشهوة. ولذلك قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «مَنْ اسْتَطَاعَ منْكُمُ البَاءَةَ فَلْيَتَزَوَّجْ، ومَنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَعَليْه بالصَّوْمِ، فَإِنَّه لَهُ وِجَاء» .","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-5","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"وذلك الصيام إنما هو في أيام قلائل مَعْدُوداتٍ، فلا يهولكم أمره، فَمَنْ كانَ مِنْكُمْ مَرِيضاً يشق عليه الصيام، أَوْ عَلى سَفَرٍ فأفطر فعليه صيام عدة ما أفطر مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ بعد تمام الشهر، وَعَلَى الَّذِينَ يُطِيقُونَهُ بلا مشقة، إن أرادوا أن يفطروا فِدْيَةٌ وهى: طَعامُ مَساكِين: مُدٍّ لكل يوم. وفي قراءة فِدْيَةٌ طَعامُ مِسْكِينٍ أي: وهي طعام مسكين لكل يوم. وقيل: نصف صاع. فَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ بزيادة المُد، أو أطعم مسكينَينْ عن يوم، فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَهُ وأعظم أجراً، وَأَنْ تَصُومُوا أيها المطيقون للصيام، خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ ما في الصيام من الأسرار، والخير المدرار، ثم نسخ بقوله: فَمَنْ شَهِدَ مِنْكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-6","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"وذلك الصيام الذي أُمرتم به هو شَهْرُ رَمَضانَ المبارك الَّذِي أُنْزِلَ فِيهِ الْقُرْآنُ أي: ابتداء نزوله فيه.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-7","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"أو إلى سماء الدنيا، حالة كونه هُدىً لِلنَّاسِ أي: هادياً لهم إلى طريق الوصول، وآيات واضحات مِنَ الْهُدى وَالْفُرْقانِ الذي يفرق بين الحق والباطل. وإن شئتَ قلتَ: فيه هدى للناس إلى مقام الإسلام، وَبَيِّناتٍ، أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-8","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"حججاً واضحة تهدي إلى تحقق الإيمان، وإلى تحقق الفرق بين الحق والباطل، وهو ما سوى الله، فيتحقق مقام الإحسان.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-9","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"فَمَنْ حضر منكم في الشَّهْرَ ولم يكن مسافراً فَلْيَصُمْهُ وجوباً، وكان في أول الإسلام على سبيل التخيير لأنه شق عليهم حيث لم يألفُوه، فلما ألفوه واستمروا معه، حتّمه عليهم في الحضور والصحة. وَمَنْ كانَ مَرِيضاً يشق عليه الصيام، أَوْ عَلى جَناح سَفَرٍ، بحيث شرَع فيه قبل الفجر فأفطر فيه، فعليه فَعِدَّةٌ مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ بِكُمُ الْيُسْرَ والتخفيف، حيث خفّف عنكم،. وأباح الفطر في المرض والسفر، وَلا يُرِيدُ بِكُمُ الْعُسْرَ إذ لم يجعل عليكم في الدين من حرج، وإنما أمركم بالقضاء لِتُكْمِلُوا الْعِدَّةَ التي أمركم بها، وهي تمام الشهر، وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا اللَّهَ عَلى ما هَداكُمْ، أمركم بصيامه فتكبروا عند تمامه.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-10","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"ووقت التكبير عند مالك: من حين يخرج إلى المُصَلَّى، بعد الطلوع، إلى مجيء الإمام إلى الصلاة. ولفظُه المختار: (الله أكبر، الله أكبر، لا إله إلا الله، الله أكبر ولله الحمد على ما هدانا، اللهم اجعلنا من الشاكرين) لجمعه","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-11","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"بين التهليل والتكبير والشكر، امتثالاً لقوله: وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ على ما أوليناكم من سابغ الإنعام، وسهَّلنا عليكم في شأن الصيام.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-12","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"الإشارة: كُتب عليكم الصيام عن الحظوظ والشهوات، كما كتب على مَن سلك الطريق قبلكم من العارفين الثقات، في أيام المجاهدة والرياضات، حتى تنزلوا بساحة حضرة المشاهدات، لعلكم تتقون شهود الكائنات، ويكشف لكم عن أسرار الذات، فمن كان فيما سلف من أيام عمره مريضاً بحب الهوى، أو على سفر في طلب الدنيا، فليبادِرْ إلى تلافِي ما ضاع في أيام أُخر، وعلى الأقوياء الذين يُطيقون هذا الصيام، إطعام الضعفاء من قُوت اليقين ومعرفة رب العالمين. فمَنْ تطوع خيراً بإرشاد العباد إلى ما يُقوِّي يقينهم، ويرفع هممهم فهو خير له.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-13","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"وأَنْ تَدُوموا أيها الأقوياء على صومكم عن شهود السَّوَى، وعن مخالطة الحس بعد التمكين، فهو خير لكم وأسلم، إن كنتم تعلمون ما في مخالطة الحس من تفريق القلب وتوهين الهمم، إذ في وقت هذا الصيام يتحقق وحي الفهم والإلهام، وتترادف الأنوار وسواطعُ العرفان. فمن شهد هذا فَلْيَدُمْ على صيامه، ومن لم يَقْدِر عليه فَلْيَبْكِ على نفسه في تضييع أيامه.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-14","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"واعلم أن الصيام على ثلاث درجات: صوم العوام، وصوم الخواص، وصوم خواص الخواص.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-15","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"أما صوم العوام: فهو الإمساك عن شهوتَي البطن والفَرْج، وما يقوم مقامَهما من الفجر إلى الغروب، مع إرسال الجوارح في الزلاَّت، وإهمال القلب في الغفلات. وصاحبُ هذا الصوم ليس له من صومه إلا الجوع، لقوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «مَنْ لم يَدَعْ قولَ الزُور والعملَ به فليس لله حاجةٌ في أنْ يدع طعامَه وشرابَه» . وأما صوم الخواص: فهو إمساك الجوارح كلَّها عن الفَضول، وهو كل ما يشغل العبد عن الوصول، وحاصلُه: حفظ الجوارح الظاهرة والباطنة عن الاشتغال بما لا يَعْنِي. وأما صوم خواص الخواص: فهو حفظ القلب عن الالتفات لغير الرب، وحفظ السر عن الوقوف مع الغير، وحاصله: الإمساك عن شهود السَّوى، وعكوفُ القلب في حضرة المولَى. وصاحب هذا صائم أبداً سرمداً. فأهل الحضرة على الدوام صائمون، وفي صلاتهم دائمون، نفعنا الله بهم وحشرنا معهم. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-183-185-16","r":"q2-183-185","title":"2:183–185 · Fasting, the month of revelation and three degrees of abstention","text":"ولمّا كان الصيام يرقّق القلب فيحصل به القرب من الحق، ذكره بإثر الصيام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-183-185-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-183-185-s1","r":"q2-183-185","title":"Time, derivation and reverse-order correspondence","text":"I say: “days” is accusative as an adverbial expression ( منصوب على الظرفية ). Its governor is disputed; the best view makes it “fasting.” The intervening words do no harm, since adverbial expressions admit latitude not allowed elsewhere. “Numbered” qualifies it. “An equal number” is a subject: an equal number is incumbent upon him. Ukhar ( أخر ), “other,” is a diptote ( ممنوع من الصرف ) because of adjectival force and deviation from a form with the definite article. “The month of Ramadan” may be the predicate of an implied subject, a subject whose predicate is “whoever is present …,” or a substitution for “fasting,” with an omitted annexed noun: the fasting of Ramadan’s month. Ramaḍān is a verbal noun of ramiḍa , to burn. “Month” is annexed to it; it becomes a proper name, prevented from full declension because of proper-name status and its additional alif and nūn. They so named it because hearts burn with hunger and thirst, sins are burnt away, or the season was hot when the months were transferred from the old language. “The month” is an adverbial complement of “is present.” “So that you complete …” gives three reasons for three rulings, in reverse-order unfolding ( اللف والنشر المعكوس ): to complete the number, I commanded you to make up an equal number of other days; to magnify God at the month’s completion, I commanded fasting the whole month; and that you might give thanks, I desired ease for you rather than hardship.","anchor":"en-q2-183-185-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-183-185-s2","r":"q2-183-185","title":"The prescribed fast and its concessions","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: believers, fasting is imposed upon you as upon earlier prophets and communities from Adam onwards. They are an example for you, so it should not be hard, that you may guard against sins: fasting breaks appetite. Hence the Prophet said: “Whoever among you can afford marriage should marry; whoever cannot should fast, for it is a restraint for him.” [B118] This fasting is only for a few numbered days; do not be daunted. Whoever is ill so that fasting is difficult, or travelling, and breaks the fast, must fast an equal number of other days after the month. Those able to fast without difficulty, should they wish to break it, owe a ransom: food for needy people (masākīn), one mudd for each day. A variant reading has “a ransom, food for a needy person,” meaning such food for each day; another view prescribes half a ṣāʿ. Whoever gives more than a mudd or feeds two needy people for a day does better and earns greater reward. For those capable of fasting, fasting is better, if they know its secrets and abundant good. This was then abrogated by “whoever among you is present during the month shall fast it.” [B119] The commanded fast is the blessed month of Ramadan, in which the Qurʾān’s descent began, or in which it descended to the lowest heaven: a guidance leading people towards arrival, with clear signs of guidance and discernment distinguishing truth from falsehood. Alternatively: it guides people to the station of Islam, provides clear proofs leading to the realization of faith, and realizes discernment between the Real and falsehood—that is, whatever is other than God—thus realizing the station of spiritual excellence ( الإحسان ). Whoever is present in the month, not travelling, must fast. At Islam’s beginning a choice was given, since people were unused to fasting and found it difficult. Once accustomed to it and continuing in it, they were required to fast when resident and healthy. Whoever is ill with difficulty in fasting, or on a journey begun before dawn, and breaks the fast, owes an equal number of other days. God desires ease and lightening, permitting breaking the fast in illness and travel. He desires no hardship, having placed no constriction in religion. Making up the fast completes the prescribed number, the whole month. He commanded it so that you magnify Him at its completion for His guidance. According to Mālik, the time of magnification ( التكبير ) runs from setting out for the prayer-ground after sunrise until the imam comes to prayer. The preferred wording is: “God is greater, God is greater; there is no god but God; God is greater, and to God belongs praise for guiding us. O God, make us among the thankful.” It unites the profession of unity, magnification and thanks, fulfilling “that you might give thanks” for Our abundant blessings and the ease We granted in fasting.","anchor":"en-q2-183-185-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-183-185-s3","r":"q2-183-185","title":"Abstention from desire and from witnessing an other","text":"Fasting from personal shares and appetites is prescribed for you, as for trustworthy gnostics who travelled before you: during days of struggle and discipline, until you alight in the court of witnessing’s presence, that you guard against witnessing created beings and the Essence’s secrets be unveiled to you. Whoever spent earlier days of life sick with love of desire or travelling in pursuit of the world should hasten to recover in other days what was lost. Those strong enough for this fast must feed the weak with certainty and knowledge of the Lord of the worlds. Whoever freely guides servants to what strengthens certainty and raises aspiration does better for himself. Strong ones, continuing your fast from witnessing an other and from mingling with sensory things after establishment is better and safer, if you know how sensory engagement disperses hearts and weakens aspirations. During this fast the inspiration of understanding becomes real, and lights and radiant gnosis follow one another. Whoever witnesses this should continue fasting; whoever cannot should weep over wasting his days. Know that fasting has three degrees: the fast of the generality, the elect and the elect of the elect. The first abstains from the appetites of stomach and sexual organ, and what stands in their place, from dawn to sunset, while releasing the limbs into lapses and neglecting the heart in heedlessness. Such a faster gains only hunger: “Whoever does not abandon false speech and acting upon it, God has no need of his abandoning food and drink.” The elect’s fast restrains every limb from superfluities—whatever distracts the servant from arrival. In sum, it guards outward and inward faculties from what does not concern them. The elect of the elect guard the heart from turning towards other than the Lord and the secret from stopping with an other. In sum, they abstain from witnessing otherness and keep the heart abiding in the Master’s presence. Such a person fasts for ever: people of the presence fast continually and are constant in prayer. May God benefit us through them and gather us with them. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-183-185-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-183-185-s4","r":"q2-183-185","title":"","text":"Fasting softens the heart and brings nearness to the Real; He therefore mentions this immediately afterwards:","anchor":"en-q2-183-185-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-186","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place 2:186","anchor":"unit-q2-186"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-1","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"وَإِذا سَأَلَكَ عِبادِي عَنِّي فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌ أُجِيبُ دَعْوَةَ الدَّاعِ إِذا دَعانِ فَلْيَسْتَجِيبُوا لِي وَلْيُؤْمِنُوا بِي لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْشُدُونَ (186)","anchor":"ar-q2-186-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-2","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: في جواب رجل سأل: هل قريب ربنا فنناجيَه، أو بعيد فنناديه؟ فنزل: وَإِذا سَأَلَكَ عِبادِي عَنِّي. فقل لهم: فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌ إليهم من أرواحهم لأشباحهم، ومن وَسْواس قلوبهم لقلوبهم، عِلْماً وقدرة وإحاطة، أجيب دعوة الداعي إذا دَعَانِ، سرّاً أو جهراً، ليلاً أو نهاراً، على ما يليق بحاله في الوقت الذي نريد، لا في الوقت الذي يريد، فَلْيَسْتَجِيبُوا لِي إذا دعوتُهم للإيمان والطاعة، أَسْلُك بهم طريق المعرفة، وَلْيُؤْمِنُوا بِي إني قريب منهم فَيَسْتَحْيُوا مني، حياءَ مَنْ يرى أني معه حيث كان، لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْشُدُونَ إلى سلوك طريقتي ودوام محبتي.","anchor":"ar-q2-186-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-3","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"قال البيضاوي: اعلم أنه، تعالى، لما أمرهم بصوم الشهر، ومراعاة العدة على القيام بوظائف التكبير والشكر، عقَّبه بهذه الآية الدالّة على أنه خبير بأحوالهم، سميع لأقوالهم مجيب لدعائهم، مجازيهم على أعمالهم، تأكيداً وحثّاً عليه. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-186-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-4","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"الإشارة: قُرْب الحقّ تعالى من عباده هو قرب المعاني من المحسوسات، أو قرب الصفات من الذات، أو الذات من الصفات. فإذا تحقق المحو والاضمحلال، وزال البَيْن، وثبت الوصال، لم يبقَ قرب ولا بعد ولا بَينٌ ولا انفصال. قال الشيخ القطبُ العارف الكبير سيدي عبد السلام بن مشيش رضي الله عنه لأبى الحسن رضي الله عنه: حدِّدْ بصرَ الإيمان تَجد الله في كل شيء وعند كل شيء، ومع كل شيء، وقبل كل شيء، وبعد كل شيء، وقريباً من كل شيء، ومحيطاً بكل شيء، بقُرب هو وصَفْهُ، وبحيطة هي نعتُه، وَعَدّ عن الظرفية والحدود، وعن الأماكن والجهات، وعن الصحبة والقرب في المسافات، وعن الدَّوْر بالمخلوقات، وامْحَق الكلَّ بوصفه الأول والآخر والظاهر والباطن، «كان الله ولا شيء معه، وهو الآن على ما عليه كان» .","anchor":"ar-q2-186-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-5","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"وقال بعض العارفين: الحق تعالى منزّه عن الأين والجهة والكيف والمادة والصورة. ومع ذلك لا يخلو منه أين ولا مكان، ولا كم ولا كيف، ولا جسم، ولا جوهر ولا عرض، لأنه للطفه سارٍ في كل شيء، ولنوريته ظاهر في كل شيء، ولإطلاقه وإحاطته متكيّف بكل كيف، غير متقيد بذلك، فمن لم يعرف هذا ولم يذقه ولم يشهده فهو أعمى البصيرة، محروم من مشاهدة الحق تعالى. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-186-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-6","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"وهذه الإشارات لا يفهمها إلا أهل الذَّوْق من أهل المعاني، فاصحب الرجال أهلَ المعاني تِذُقْ أسرارهم، وتفهم إشاراتهم. وإلا فحسبُك أن تعتقد كمال التنزيه، وبطلان التشبيه، وتَمَسَّكْ بقوله تعالى: لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهِ شَيْءٌ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْبَصِيرُ، وسلَّمْ للرجال في كل حال.","anchor":"ar-q2-186-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-7","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"إِنْ لم تَر الهلالَ فسَلِّم ... لأناس رأوه بالأبْصَار","anchor":"ar-q2-186-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-8","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"وإذا تحققت أن الحقّ قريب منك كفاك لسانُ الحال عن طلب المقال، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-186-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-186-9","r":"q2-186","title":"2:186 · Divine nearness, answered prayer and transcendence beyond place","text":"ثم تمّم الحق تعالى بقية أحكام الصوم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-186-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-186-s1","r":"q2-186","title":"The answer in the time God wills","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says, in answer to a man asking, “Is our Lord near, so that we converse quietly with Him, or distant, so that we call aloud?”: when My servants ask you about Me, tell them I am nearer to them, in knowledge, power and encompassing, than their spirits to their bodies and the whispers of their hearts to their hearts. I answer the caller, secretly or aloud, by night or day, in the way fitting his condition and at the time We will, not the time he wills. Let them answer Me when I call to faith and obedience, and I shall lead them on gnosis’s path. Let them believe I am near, feeling shame before Me as one who sees that I am with him wherever he is, so that they are directed to travel My path and persist in loving Me. Al-Bayḍāwī says: after commanding the month’s fast, observing its count and performing the duties of magnification and thanks, God follows with this verse. It shows that He knows their conditions, hears their words, answers their prayers and repays their deeds, reinforcing and encouraging the command.","anchor":"en-q2-186-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-186-s2","r":"q2-186","title":"Nearness without spatial proximity","text":"The Real’s nearness to His servants is the nearness of meanings to sensory things, or Attributes to Essence, or Essence to Attributes. When effacement and disappearance are realized, separation removed and union established, neither nearness nor distance, between-ness nor separation remains. The great gnostic and pole, Sīdī ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Mashīsh, told Abū al-Ḥasan: “Sharpen faith’s vision and you will find God in everything, at everything, with everything, before everything, after everything, near everything and encompassing everything—with a nearness that is His attribute and an encompassing that is His quality. Pass beyond containment and limits, places and directions, companionship and nearness measured by distances, and circling among created things. Efface everything through His attributes ‘the First, the Last, the Outward, the Inward.’ God was, and nothing was with Him; He is now as He was.” [B120] A gnostic said: “The Real transcends where, direction, how, matter and form. Yet no where or place, quantity or quality, body, substance or accident is empty of Him. Through His subtlety He pervades everything; through His luminosity He appears in everything; through His absoluteness and encompassing He assumes every modality without being restricted by it. Whoever has neither known, tasted nor witnessed this is blind in inward sight, deprived of witnessing the Real.” Only people of spiritual taste and inward meanings understand these allusions. Accompany the men of meanings, and you will taste their secrets and understand their allusions. Otherwise it suffices to affirm perfect transcendence and the falsity of assimilation, holding to “Nothing is like Him, and He is the Hearing, the Seeing” [42:11], and yielding to these men in every state. If you have not seen the crescent, yield to people who have seen it with their eyes. When you realize that the Real is near, the tongue of the state ( لسان الحال ) suffices in place of verbal petition. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-186-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-186-s3","r":"q2-186","title":"","text":"The Real completes the remaining rules of fasting:","anchor":"en-q2-186-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-187","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat 2:187","anchor":"unit-q2-187"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-1","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"أُحِلَّ لَكُمْ لَيْلَةَ الصِّيامِ الرَّفَثُ إِلى نِسائِكُمْ هُنَّ لِباسٌ لَكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ لِباسٌ لَهُنَّ عَلِمَ اللَّهُ أَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَخْتانُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ فَتابَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَعَفا عَنْكُمْ فَالْآنَ بَاشِرُوهُنَّ وَابْتَغُوا ما كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ وَكُلُوا وَاشْرَبُوا حَتَّى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمُ الْخَيْطُ الْأَبْيَضُ مِنَ الْخَيْطِ الْأَسْوَدِ مِنَ الْفَجْرِ ثُمَّ أَتِمُّوا الصِّيامَ إِلَى اللَّيْلِ وَلا تُبَاشِرُوهُنَّ وَأَنْتُمْ عاكِفُونَ فِي الْمَساجِدِ تِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ فَلا تَقْرَبُوها كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ آياتِهِ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُونَ (187)","anchor":"ar-q2-187-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-2","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"قلت: الرفَث: مُحَرِّك الجِماع، والفُحْش كالرفوث، وكلام النساء في الجماع. قاله في القاموس، وقال الأزهري اللغوي: الرفَث: كلمة جامعة لكل ما يريد الرجل من امرأته، وضمَّنه هنا الإفضاء، فعدَّاه بإلى.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-3","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في نسخ ما كان في أول الإسلام من تحريم الجِماع في رمضان بعد العشاء أو النوم، ثم إن عمر رضي الله عنه باشر امرأته بعد العشاء، فندم وأتى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يعتذر إليه، فقام رجال فاعترفوا بما صنعوا بعد العشاء فنزل قوله: أُحِلَّ لَكُمْ لَيْلَةَ الصِّيامِ قبل الفجر، الإفضاءُ إِلى نِسائِكُمْ بالجماع. وعبَّر بالرفث تقبيحاً لما ارتكبوه.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-4","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"ثم علَّل التحليل بقوله: هُنَّ لِباسٌ لَكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ لِباسٌ لَهُنَّ، أي: وإنما أبحتُ لكم الجماع لقلّة صبركم عليهن، حتى تعانقوهن ويعانقنكم، فيشتمل بعضُكم على بعض، كاشتمال اللباس على صاحبه، كما قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-187-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-5","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"إذَا مَا الضَّجِيعَ ثَنَى عِطْفَهَا ... تَثَنَّتْ فكَانَتْ عَلَيْهِ لِبَاسَا","anchor":"ar-q2-187-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-6","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"وهذه الحالة يقلُّ فيها الصبرُ عن الوقَاع، عَلِمَ اللَّهُ أَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَخْتانُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ أي تَخُونُونها فَتُعرِّضُونها للعقاب، وتَحْرمُونها من الثواب، فَتابَ عَلَيْكُمْ لَمّا تُبْتُم واعترفتم بما اقْتَرَفْتُم، وعفا عنكم فمحا ذنوبكم، فَالْآنَ بَاشِرُوهُنَّ. والمباشرة: إلصاق البَشْرة بالبشرة، كنايةً عن الجماع، وَابْتَغُوا ما كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ","anchor":"ar-q2-187-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-7","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"من النسل، فلا تباشروهن لمجرد قضاء الشهوة، بل اطلبوا ما قدَّر الله لكم، وأثْبتَه في اللوح المحفوظ من الولد، لأنه هو المقصود من تشريع النكاح، وخلق الشهوة، لا مجرد قضاء الوطر. وفي الحديث: «إِذَا مَاتَ العبدُ انْقَطَعَ عَمَلُه إِلاَّ مَن ثَلاثٍَ: صَدَقَةٍ جَاريَةٍ، وعِلْمٍ بثَّه في صُدور الرِّجالِ، وولدٍ صالح يدعو لَهُ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-187-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-8","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"وفي حديث طويل عن عائشة- رضي الله عنها- في قصة الحَوْلاء- امرأة من الأنصار-، قال لها رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: ما من امرأة حمَلَت من زوجها حين تَحْمِل، إلا لها من الأجْر مثل القائم ليلَة الصائم نهارَه، والغازي في سبيل الله، وما من امرأة يأتيها الطَلْقُ، إلا كان لها بكل طَلْقةٍ عِتْق نسمةٍ، وبكل رَضْعة عتق رقبة، فإذا فَطَمت ولَدها ناداها مُنادِ من السماء: قد كُفيتِ العملَ فيما مضى، فاستأنفي العمل فيما بقي. قالت عائشة- رضي الله عنها-: قد أُعْطِي النساءُ خيراً كثيراً، فما لكم يا معشر الرجال؟. فضحك النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ثم قال: ما من رجل مؤمن أخذ بيد امرأتِه يُرَاوِدُها، إلا كتب الله له حسنة، وإنْ عانقها فعشْر حسنات، وإن ضاجعها فعشرون حسنةٌ، وإن أتاها كان خيراً من الدنيا وما فيها، فإذا قام ليغتسل لم يمر الماء على شعرة من جسده إلا مُحِيَ عنه سيئة، ويُعطى له درجة، وما يعطى بغسله خير من الدنيا وما فيها، وإن الله تعالى يباهي الملائكة فيقول: انظروا إلى عبدي قام في ليلة قَرَّة يغتسل من الجنابة، يتيقن بأني ربه، اشهدوا أني قد غفرت له» . هـ. من الثعلبي.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-9","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"ثم أباح الحق تعالى الأكلَ والشرب، ليلة الصيام إلى الفجر، فقال: وَكُلُوا وَاشْرَبُوا حَتَّى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمُ الْخَيْطُ الْأَبْيَضُ مِنَ الْخَيْطِ الْأَسْوَدِ شبَّه أول ما يبدو من الفجر المعترِض في الأفق، بالخيط الأبيض، وما يمتد معه من غَبَشِ الليل، بالخيط الأسود.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-10","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"ولم ينزل قوله تعالى: مِنَ الْفَجْرِ إلا بعد مدة، فحمله بعض الصحابة على ظاهره، فعمد إلى خيطٍ أبيض وخيط أسود فجعلهما تحت وِسادته، فجعل يأكل وينظر إليهما، فلم يتبيَّنا، ومنهم عَديُّ بنُ حاتم، قال: فغدوتُ إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فأخبرته فضحِك، وقال: «إِنك لَعَرِيضُ القَفا، إِنَّمَا ذلِكَ بَيَاضُ النَّهَارِ وسَوَادُ اللَّيْلِ» ، والحديث ثابت في البخاري وغيرِه. واعترضه الزمخشري بأن فيه تأخير البيان عن وقت الحاجة، وذلك لا يجوز، لما فيه من التكليف بما لا يطاق.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-11","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"وأُجيب بأنه ليس فيه تأخير البيان عن وقت الحاجة، وإنما فيه تأخير البيان لوقت الحاجة، وهو جائز. وبيان ذلك أنه لمّا نزل قوله تعالى: حَتَّى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمُ الْخَيْطُ الْأَبْيَضُ مِنَ الْخَيْطِ الْأَسْوَدِ فهم رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم والمؤمنون مُرادَ الله منهما، واستمر عملهم على ذلك، فكانت الآية مُبينة في حقهم لا مُجْمَلة. وأما عَدِيّ بن حاتم فكان بَدَوِيّاً مُشتغلاً بالصيد، ولم يكن فيه حُنْكَة أهل الحاضرة، فحمل الآية على ظاهرها ولذلك قال له رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: «إنك لَعِرَيضُ القَفا» . فنزلت الآية تُبين لعدي مُرادَ الله عند الحاجة إلى البيان. مع أن السيوطي ذكر في التوشيح خلاف هذا ونصه:","anchor":"ar-q2-187-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-12","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"قال بعضهم: كأنَّ عديّاً لم يسمع هذه اللفظة من الآية لأنها نزلت قبل إسلامه بمدة، وذلك أن إسلامه كان في السنة التاسعة أو العاشرة، بعد نزول الآية بمدة، قال: علَّمنِي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم الصلاة والصيام، فقال: «صلّ كذا، وصم كذا، فإن غابت الشمس فَكُلْ حتى يتبين لك الخيط الأبيض من الخيط الأسود، فأخذ الخيطين ... » .","anchor":"ar-q2-187-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-13","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"الحديث. فقال له- عليه الصلاة والسلام: «ألم أقل لك من الفجر؟» فتبين أن قوله في الحديث: «فأنزل الله مِنْ الفجر» من تصرُّف الرواة. هـ. مختصراً، فهذا صريح في أن الآية نزلت بتمامها مبينة فلم يكن فيها تأخير، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-14","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"ثم بيَّن الحق تعالى غاية الصوم، فقال: ثُمَّ أَتِمُّوا الصِّيامَ إِلَى اللَّيْلِ فمن أفطر مع الشك في الغروب، فعليه الكفارة، بخلاف الشك في الفجر للاستصحاب. ولما كان الاعتكاف من لوازم الصوم ذكر بعض أحكامه بإثره فقال: وَلا تُبَاشِرُوهُنَّ أي: النساء وَأَنْتُمْ عاكِفُونَ فِي الْمَساجِدِ، فالمباشرة للمعتكف حرام، وتُفسد الاعتكاف. كانت المباشرة في المسجد أو خارجَه. وكان الرجل يكون معتكفاً فيخرج فيصيب زوجَه ثم يرجع، فنزلت الآية- تِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ قد حدها لكم، فَلا تَقْرَبُوها فضلاً عن أن تعتدوها، كَذلِكَ أي: مثل هذا البيان التام، يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ آياتِهِ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُونَ محارمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-15","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"الإشارة: قد تقدم أن صوم الخواص، وخواص الخواص، هو الإمساك عن الفُضول، وعن كل ما يقطع عن الوصول. أو الإمساك عن شهود الأغيار، وعن كل ما يوجب الأكدار. فإن عزَمَت النفس على هذا الصوم وعقَدَت النيّة عليه، حلَّ لها أن تُباشر أَبْكارَ العلوم اللدنية الوهبية، والحقائق العرفانية، وتفضي إلى ثَيبات العلوم الرَّسْمية الكسبية. العلوم اللدنية الوهبية شِعارُها، والعلومُ الرسمية دِثارها . العلوم اللدنية لباس باطنها، والعلوم الرسمية لباس ظاهرها.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-16","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"قال أبو سليمان الداراني: إذا اعتادت النفوس على ترك الآثام جالت في الملكوت، ثم عادت إلى صاحبها بطرائف العلوم، من غير أن يؤدي إليها عالمٌ عِلْماً. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-17","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"قال الحقّ تعالى: عَلِمَ اللَّهُ أَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَخْتانُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ بدنس الهفوات، فمنعكم من مباشرة تلك العلوم الوهبيات، فلما عقدْتُم التوبة، وعزمتم على تركها، تاب عليكم وعفا عنكم، فالآن باشروها، وابتغوا ما كتب الله لكم، من الوصول إلى معرفته، والعكوف في حضرة قُدسه، وكلوا من ثمرات تلك العلوم، واشربوا من خمرة الحيّ القيّوم، حتى يَطْلُعَ عليكم فجرُ الكشف والبيان، وتُشرق على قلوبكم شمسُ نهار العرفان، فحينئذٍ تَضْمَحِلُّ تلك العلوم، وتمحى تلك المعالم والرسوم. ولم يبقَ إلا الاستغراق في مشاهدة الحيّ القيّوم، فلا تباشروها وأنتم عاكفون في تلك المساجد. فمشاهدةُ وجهِ الحبيب تُغنْي عن مطالعة المعالم والمشاهد. تلك حدود الله فلا تقربوها، أي: لا تقفوا مع تلك العلوم وحلاوة تلك الرسوم فإنها تمنعكم من مشاهدة الحىّ القيوم. كذلك يُبين الله آياته الموضَّحة لطريق وصوله للناس، لعلهم يتقون مشاهدة ما سواه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-187-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-187-18","r":"q2-187","title":"2:187 · The nights of fasting, the dawn’s discernment and retreat","text":"ولما أراد الحقّ أن يتكلم على الحج قدَّم الكلام على الأموال لأنها سببٌ في وجوبه، والوصول إليه في الغالب، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-187-18"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-187-s1","r":"q2-187","title":"Rafath and intimate approach","text":"I say: rafath ( الرَّفَث ), pronounced with consecutive fatḥas, means intercourse and indecent speech, like rufūth , and talk with women about intercourse, as stated in the Qāmūs . The lexicographer al-Azharī calls it a comprehensive term for everything a man desires of his wife. Here it includes the meaning of intimate approach ( الإفضاء ), and therefore takes the preposition ilā . [B121]","anchor":"en-q2-187-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-187-s2","r":"q2-187","title":"A concession after an earlier prohibition","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, speaks in abrogation of the initial prohibition of intercourse during Ramadan after the night prayer or sleep. ʿUmar had relations with his wife after the night prayer, regretted it and came to the Messenger apologetically. Other men rose and admitted what they had done after that prayer. Then came the revelation: on the nights of fasting before dawn, approaching your wives in intercourse is permitted. The expression rafath marks the ugliness of their earlier act. He explains the permission: “They are a garment for you, and you a garment for them.” I permitted intercourse because you have little patience apart from them: you embrace one another, each enveloping the other as clothing envelops its wearer. The poet says: When the bedfellow bends her side towards him, she bends and becomes his garment. In that condition patience in abstaining is slight. God knew you betrayed yourselves, exposing yourselves to punishment and depriving yourselves of reward. When you repented and acknowledged your acts, He turned to you and pardoned, effacing your sins. Now approach them. Mubāshara literally brings skin against skin and is a euphemism ( كناية ) for intercourse. Seek what God has written for you of offspring: do not approach merely to satisfy appetite, but seek the child God has decreed and recorded on the Preserved Tablet. This, not merely satisfying desire, is the intention behind instituting marriage and creating appetite. A report says: “When the servant dies, his action ceases except for three: continuing charity, knowledge spread in people’s breasts and a righteous child praying for him.” In a lengthy report from ʿĀʾisha concerning al-Ḥawlāʾ [CP16] , a woman of the Helpers, the Messenger tells her: “Whenever a woman conceives by her husband, from conception she has the reward of one standing in prayer at night, fasting by day and fighting in God’s way. Every labour pang brings the reward of freeing a person, and every nursing that of freeing a slave. When she weans her child, a caller from heaven says: your previous deeds have been taken care of; begin anew for what remains.” ʿĀʾisha said: “Women have been given much good; what is there for you men?” The Prophet laughed and said: “Whenever a believing man takes his wife’s hand to court her, God writes him a good deed; embracing her brings ten; lying with her twenty; and intercourse is better than the world and all it contains. When he rises to bathe, water passes over no hair on his body without a sin being effaced and a degree bestowed. What he receives for bathing is better than the world and all it contains. God glories before the angels: ‘Look at My servant, rising on a cold night to bathe from major ritual impurity, certain that I am his Lord. Bear witness that I have forgiven him.’” From al-Thaʿlabī. [B122]","anchor":"en-q2-187-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-187-s3","r":"q2-187","title":"The two threads and the timing of clarification","text":"The Real permits eating and drinking on the fasting night until dawn: “Eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread.” The first light of dawn appearing horizontally across the horizon is likened to a white thread, and the darkness of night stretching beside it to a black thread. “Of dawn” was not revealed until some time later. Some Companions took the words literally, putting a white and black thread beneath their pillow and continuing to eat while looking at them, unable to distinguish them. Among them was ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim. He said: “I went early to the Messenger and told him. He laughed and said, ‘You are indeed broad in the nape! It means the whiteness of day and the blackness of night.’” The report is established in al-Bukhārī and elsewhere. Al-Zamakhsharī objected that this postpones clarification beyond the time of need ( تأخير البيان عن وقت الحاجة ), which is impermissible because it imposes what cannot be performed. The answer given is that clarification was delayed until, not beyond, the time of need, which is permissible. When the two-thread passage was revealed, the Messenger and believers understood God’s intention and acted accordingly. For them it was clear, not indeterminate ( مجملة ). ʿAdī, a Bedouin occupied with hunting and lacking settled people’s experience, took it literally; hence “broad in the nape.” The verse then clarified God’s intention for him when clarification became necessary. Yet al-Suyūṭī states otherwise in the Tawshīḥ : someone said ʿAdī apparently had not heard this part of the verse, which descended long before his conversion in year nine or ten. He said: “The Messenger taught me prayer and fasting: ‘Pray thus and fast thus; when the sun sets, eat until the white thread becomes distinct from the black.’ I took the two threads …” The Prophet asked him, “Did I not say, ‘of dawn’?” This shows that “then God revealed ‘of dawn’” in the report results from the narrators’ handling of it. Here ends the abridged quotation. [XVI-N002] This explicitly makes the verse clear and complete upon revelation, with no delay. And God Most High knows best. [B123]","anchor":"en-q2-187-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-187-s4","r":"q2-187","title":"The end of fasting and intercourse during retreat","text":"The Real specifies the fast’s limit: “Then complete the fast until night.” Whoever breaks it while doubtful whether sunset has occurred owes expiation, unlike doubt about dawn, because the preceding state is presumed to continue ( الاستصحاب ). [B124] Since retreat ( الاعتكاف ) is connected with fasting, He follows with part of its rulings: do not have relations with women while in retreat in the mosques. Intercourse is forbidden to one in retreat and invalidates it, whether inside or outside the mosque. A man would go out from retreat, have relations with his wife and return; the verse was revealed. These are limits God has set for you: do not approach them, much less cross them. With such complete explanation God clarifies His signs, so that people avoid His prohibitions.","anchor":"en-q2-187-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-187-s5","r":"q2-187","title":"Gifted knowledge, acquired learning and witnessing beyond both","text":"The fast of the elect and elect of the elect has been explained: abstaining from superfluities and whatever prevents arrival, or from witnessing others and whatever produces turbidity. When the soul resolves upon this fast and forms its intention, it may approach the virgin, divinely bestowed sciences and gnostic realities, and the previously possessed formal, acquired sciences. Gifted knowledge ( العلوم اللدنية الوهبية ) is its inner garment; formal knowledge its outer cloak. The first clothes its inward life, the second its outward life. Abū Sulaymān al-Dārānī said: “When souls become accustomed to abandoning sins, they range through the dominion and return to their possessor with wondrous knowledge, without a scholar conveying knowledge to them.” The Real says: God knew that you betrayed yourselves through the pollution of lapses and prevented your approaching these gifted sciences. Once you resolved upon repentance and abandoning the lapses, He accepted and pardoned you. Now approach the sciences, seeking the arrival at His knowledge and abiding in His holy presence that He wrote for you. Eat their fruits and drink the wine of the Living, Self-Subsisting until unveiling’s dawn rises and the day of gnosis shines upon your hearts. Then those sciences disappear and their landmarks and traces are effaced; nothing remains but absorption in witnessing the Living, Self-Subsisting. Do not approach them while abiding in those mosques. Seeing the Beloved’s Face dispenses with contemplating landmarks and scenes. These are God’s limits: do not stop with those sciences and the sweetness of their traces, for they prevent witnessing the Living, Self-Subsisting. Thus God clarifies His signs showing people the path of arrival, so that they guard against witnessing other than He. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-187-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-187-s6","r":"q2-187","title":"","text":"Before speaking of pilgrimage, the Real mentions wealth, generally a condition of its obligation and of reaching it:","anchor":"en-q2-187-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-188","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver 2:188","anchor":"unit-q2-188"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-1","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"وَلا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوالَكُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ بِالْباطِلِ وَتُدْلُوا بِها إِلَى الْحُكَّامِ لِتَأْكُلُوا فَرِيقاً مِنْ أَمْوالِ النَّاسِ بِالْإِثْمِ وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (188)","anchor":"ar-q2-188-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-2","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"قلت: أصل الإدلاء: إرسالُ الدَّلْو في الماء ليتوصل به إلى أخذ الماء من البئر، ثم أُطلق في كل ما يتوسل به إلى شيء، يقال: أدلَى بمالِه إلى الحكام، أي: دفعه رِشْوة، ليتوصل بذلك إلى أخذ أكثر منه، وهو المراد هنا، وفي القاموس: أدلى برَحمِه: توسَّل، وبحُجَّتِه: أحضرَها، وإليه بمالهِ: دفَعه. ومنه: (وتُدْلوا بها إلى الحكام) . هـ. و (تدلوا) معطوف على (تأكلوا) ، مَنْهِي عنهما معاً.","anchor":"ar-q2-188-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-3","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلا تَأْكُلُوا يا معشر المسلمين أَمْوالَكُمْ أي: أموال بعضكم بعضاً، بِالْباطِلِ أي: بغير حقّ شرعي إما بغير حق أصلا كالغصب والسرقة والخيانة والخَدْع والتطفيف والغش وغير ذلك. أو بحق باطل كما يؤخذ في السحر والكهانة والفأل والقِمار والجاه، وهَدِية المِدْيان ، وهدية القرض، والضمان،","anchor":"ar-q2-188-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-4","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"والرشوة، والربا، وغير ذلك مما نهى الشارعُ عنه. ولا يدخل في ذلك التمائم والعزائم إذا كان بالقرآن أو السنّة وغلَب الشفاء، وكذلك لا يدخل أيضاً الغَبْن، إذا كان البائعُ عالماً بالمَبِيع.","anchor":"ar-q2-188-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-5","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"أو وَلا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوالَكُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ بِالْباطِلِ بأن تُنفقوها في المَلاهي والزنا والشرب واللواط، وغير ذلك من المحرمات، ولا تُدْلُوا أي: تتوسلوا بها، أي: بدفعها إِلَى الْحُكَّامِ رشوة لِتَأْكُلُوا فَرِيقاً مِنْ أَمْوالِ النَّاسِ بأن يحكم لكم بها القاضي، تأخذونها متلبسين بِالْإِثْمِ أي: بالمعصية وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ أنها لغيركم فإنَّ حُكْمَ الحاكِم لا يُحِلُّ حراماً.","anchor":"ar-q2-188-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-6","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم قال: «إنَّما أنا بَشرٌ مثلُكُم، ولعلَّ بعضَكُمْ أن يكون الْحَنَ بحُجَّتِهِ مِنْ بَعضٍ فأقضي لهُ، فمن قَضَيتُ له بشيء من مال أخيه فإنَما أقَطَعُ له قطعةً من النارِ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-188-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-7","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"الإشارة: الباطلُ كلُّ ما سوى الحقّ، فكل من كان يأخذ من يد الخلق ولا يشاهد فيهم الحقّ فإنما يأخذ أموال الناس بالباطل. قال في الحكم: «لا تمدن يديك إلى الأخذ من الخلائق إلا أن ترى أن المعطي فيهم مولاك، فإذا كنت كذلك فخذ ما وافقك العلم» . ويحتاج العامل بهذا إلى عَسةٍ كبيرةٍ، وشُهودٍ قَوِي، حتى يَفْنَى عَنْ نظرهِ مشاهدةُ الخلق في شهود الملك الحق. وكان بعضهم يطلب مَنْ هذا وصْفُه فيعطي للفقير العطاء، ويقول: خذ، لا لك، فلا يسمع من أحد شيئاً، حتى أعطَى لبعض الفقراء، وقال: خذ، لا لك، فقال: أقبضُ لا منك. هـ. قلت: الوصول إلى الحكام على شأن الدنيا أو للانتصار للنفس حرام في طريق الخصوص، بل يصبر حتى يحكم الله بينه وبين خصمه، وهو خير الحاكمين، فإن اضطُرَّ إلى شيء ولم يجد بُدّاً منه فليُوكِّلْ، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-188-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-188-8","r":"q2-188","title":"2:188 · Unjust wealth, judicial judgement and the hand of the Giver","text":"وَلَمَّا أراد الحقُّ تعالى أن يتكلم على أحكام الحج، قدَّم الكلام على الهلال لأنه معتبر فى الحج، أداء وقضاء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-188-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-188-s1","r":"q2-188","title":"Lowering a bucket and presenting a bribe","text":"I say: idlāʾ ( الإدلاء ) originally means lowering a bucket into water to draw from a well, then anything used to attain something. “He offered his wealth to the judges” means paying a bribe to obtain more; that is intended here. The Qāmūs gives: he invoked his kinship as a means; presented his proof; and offered his wealth to someone, meaning handed it over. Hence “offer it to judges.” The verb is coordinated with “consume,” and both are prohibited.","anchor":"en-q2-188-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-188-s2","r":"q2-188","title":"A court’s decision does not make the forbidden lawful","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Muslims, do not consume one another’s wealth falsely, without a valid right under the Sacred Law. This may mean no right at all—usurpation, theft, betrayal, deception, short measure, fraud and the like—or a false claim to a right, as with payments for sorcery, soothsaying, omens, gambling, influence, a debtor’s gift, gifts connected with loans, guarantees, bribes, usury and other things forbidden by the Lawgiver. This does not include amulets and invocations based upon Qurʾān or Sunna when healing is predominant, nor disproportion in an exchange when the seller knows the thing sold. [B125] Or: do not consume wealth falsely by spending it on diversions, illicit intercourse, drinking, sodomy and other prohibitions. Do not use it as a means by paying bribes to judges, so that a judge awards you a portion of others’ property which you take sinfully while knowing it belongs to another. A judge’s judgement does not make an unlawful thing lawful. The Prophet said: “I am only a human being like you. Perhaps one of you presents his argument more eloquently than another and I judge in his favour. Whoever I award something of his brother’s wealth, I award him only a piece of the Fire.” [B126]","anchor":"en-q2-188-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-188-s3","r":"q2-188","title":"Receiving through creation without forgetting God","text":"Falsehood is everything besides the Real. Whoever receives from creation’s hand without witnessing the Real in them takes people’s wealth falsely. The Ḥikam says: “Do not stretch your hands to receive from creatures unless you see that the Giver through them is your Master. When you are thus, take what knowledge permits you.” Acting upon this requires great vigilance and strong witnessing, until the sight of creation disappears from one’s gaze in witnessing the True King. Someone sought a person of this quality. Giving to a poor man, he would say, “Take—not for you,” but heard no answer. Finally he gave to one of the poor and said, “Take—not for you.” The man replied, “I receive—not from you.” I say: approaching rulers over worldly matters or to vindicate oneself is forbidden in the path of the elect. Rather, one waits patiently until God judges between oneself and one’s opponent; He is the best of judges. If compelled by an unavoidable need, one should appoint an agent. Through God is success. [B127]","anchor":"en-q2-188-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-188-s4","r":"q2-188","title":"","text":"Before the rulings of pilgrimage, the Real speaks of the crescent, considered in both performing and making up pilgrimage:","anchor":"en-q2-188-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-189","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door 2:189","anchor":"unit-q2-189"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-1","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"يَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْأَهِلَّةِ قُلْ هِيَ مَواقِيتُ لِلنَّاسِ وَالْحَجِّ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-189-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-2","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"قلت: الذي سأله معاذُ بن جبل وثعلبةُ بن غنمة ، فقالا: يا رسول الله: ما بال الهلال يبدو رقيقاً كالخيط، ثم لا يزال يزيد حتى يستوي، ثم لا يزال ينقص حتى يرجع كالخيط؟ فقال الحق جل جلاله: يَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْأَهِلَّةِ","anchor":"ar-q2-189-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-3","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"أي: عن حكمة اختلاف الأهلة بالزيادة والنقص، قُلْ لهم يا محمد: هِيَ مَواقِيتُ لِلنَّاسِ يُوقِّتُون بها دُيونهم، ويعرفون بها أوقات زَرْعهم، وعِدَدَ نسائهم وصيامهم. وهي أيضاً مواقيتُ للحج، يعرفون بذلك وقت دخوله وخروجه، فيعرفون الأداء من القضاء، فلو كانت على حالة واحدة لم يعرفوا ذلك. أجابهم الحق تعالى بغير ما ينتظرون إشارة إلى أن السؤال عن سر الاختلاف، ليس فيه منفعة شرعية، وإنما ينبغي الاهتمام بما فيه منفعة دينية.","anchor":"ar-q2-189-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-4","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"قال أهل الهيئة: إن نوره من نُور الشمس، وجِرْمه أَطْلَس، فكلما بعد من مُسَامتة الشمس قابَله نورُها، فإذا قرب منها لم يقابله من نورها إلا بعض جِرمه، فإذا دخل تحتها في الفلك كان ظَهره كله إليها، فلم يقابله شيء من نورها، فإذا خرج من تحتِها قابله بقدر ذلك، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-189-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-5","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"الإشارة: إذا ظهر هلال السعادة في أفق الإرادة، وهبَّت ريح الهداية من ناحية سابق العناية، دخل وقت حج القلوب إلى حضرة علام الغيوب، فهلال الهداية للسائرين، وهم أرباب الأحوال أهل التلوين، يزداد نوره بزيادة اليقين، وينقص بنقصانه، على حسب ضعف حاله وقوته، حتى يتحقق الوصال، ويُرزق صفة الكمال. وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-189-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-6","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"كُلَّ يومٍ تَتَلَوَّنْ ... غيرُ هذا بِكَ أَجْمَلْ","anchor":"ar-q2-189-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-7","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"فصاحب التلوين بين الزيادة والنقصان، إلى أن تطلع عليه شمس العرفان، فإذا طلعت شمس العرفان فليس بعدها زيادة ولا نقصان، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-189-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-8","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"طَلَعَتْ شمسُ مَنْ أُحِبُّ بلَيْلٍ ... واستضاءتْ فَمَا تَلاَهَا غُرُوبُ","anchor":"ar-q2-189-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-9","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"إنَّ شَمْسَ النَّهارِ تَغْربُ باللي ... ل وشَمْسَ القُلوب لَيْسَتْ تَغيبُ","anchor":"ar-q2-189-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-10","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"بخلاف صاحب التمكين فإنه أبداً في ضياء معرفته، متمكن في بُرج سعادته، لا يلحق شمسَه كسوف ولا حجابٌ، ولا يستر نورَها ظلمةٌ ولا سحاب، فلو طلب الحجاب لم يُجَبْ. قال بعض العارفين: (لو كُلفت أن أرى غيره لم أستطع، فإنه لا غير معه حتى أشهده) .","anchor":"ar-q2-189-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-11","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"ثم حذَّر الحق تعالى مما ابتدعه المشركون في الحج، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-189-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-12","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"... وَلَيْسَ الْبِرُّ بِأَنْ تَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ ظُهُورِها وَلكِنِ الْبِرُّ مَنِ اتَّقى وَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ أَبْوابِها وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ (189)","anchor":"ar-q2-189-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-13","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"قلت: كانت الأنصار إذا حَجُّوا أو اعتمروا، يقولون: لا يَحُول بيننا وبين السماء سَقْفٌ، حتى يدخلوا بيوتهم، فإذا رجعوا تسوَّرُوا الجُدْران، أو نَقَبُوا في ظهور بيوتهم، فجاء رجل منهم فدخل من الباب، فَعُيِّر بذلك، فأنزل الحقّ جلّ جلاله: وَلَيْسَ الْبِرُّ أي: الطاعة، بِأَنْ تَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ ظُهُورِها فتتسوروها، أو تنقُبوا من أعلاها، وَلكِنَّ الْبِرَّ مَنِ اتَّقى المحارم وخالف الشهوات.","anchor":"ar-q2-189-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-14","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"أو: ليس البر بأن تعكسوا مسائلكم بأن تسألوا عما لا نفع لكم فيه، وتتركوا مسائل العلم التي تنفعكم في العاجل والآجل. وَلكِنَّ الْبِرَّ مَنِ اتَّقى ذلك، وَأْتُوا بيوت العلم من أبوابها، فتُحسنون السؤال وتتأدبون في المقال، وتقدمون الأهم فالأهم، والأنفع فالأنفع. وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فلا تُغيروا أحكامه، ولا تعترضوا على أفعاله، لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ بتوفيقه وهدايته.","anchor":"ar-q2-189-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-15","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن البيوت التي يدخلها المريد ثلاثة: بيت الشريعة وبيت الطريقة وبيت الحقيقة، ولكل واحد أبواب فمن أتى البيت من بابه دخل. ومن أتاه من غيره طُرد.","anchor":"ar-q2-189-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-16","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"فبيت الشريعة له ثلاثة أبواب: الباب الأول: التوبة، فإذا دخل هذا الباب، وحقَّق التوبة بأركانها وشروطها، استقبله باب الاستقامة، وهي: متابعة الرسول في أقواله وأفعاله وأحواله، فإذا دخله، وحقق الاستقامة، استقبله باب التقوى بأقسامها. فإذا حقق التقوى ظاهراً وباطناً، دخل بيت الشريعة المطهرة، وتنزه في محاسنه ومعانيه، ثم يروم دخول بيت الطريقة، وله ثلاثة أبواب:","anchor":"ar-q2-189-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-17","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"الباب الأول: الإخلاص وهو: إفراد العمل لله من غير حرف ولا حظ، فإذا حقق الإخلاص استقبله باب التخلية وهى التطهير من العيوب الباطنة، وهي لا تنحصر، لكن من ظفر بالشيخ أطلعه عليها، وعلّمه أدويتها، فإذا حقق التخلية استقبله باب التحلية، وهي: الاتصاف بأنواع الفضائل كالصبر والحلم والصدق والطمأنينة والسخاء والإيثار، وغير ذلك من أنواع الكمالات. فإذا حقق الإخلاص والتخلية والتحلية فقد حقق بيت الطريقة، ثم يستقبله بيت الحقيقة.","anchor":"ar-q2-189-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-18","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"فأول ما يقرع باب المراقبة، وهي: حفظ القلب والسر من الخواطر الردية، فإذا تطهر القلب من الخواطر الساكنة، استشرف على باب المشاهدة، وهى: محو الرسوم في مشاهدة أنوار الحي القيّوم، أو تلطيف الأواني عند ظهور المعاني، فإذا دخل باب المشاهدة، وسكن فيها، استقبله باب المعرفة، وهي محلّ الرسوخ والتمكين، وهي الغاية والمنتهى، فبيت الحقيقة هو مسجد الحضرة الربانية. وما بقي بعدها إلا الترقي في المقامات، وزيادة المعارف والكشوفات أبداً سرمداً، منحنا الله من ذلك حظا وافرا بمنّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-189-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-189-19","r":"q2-189","title":"2:189 · The crescents and entering each house by its door","text":"ولمّا كان البيت الحرام عند فرض الحج معمورا بالكفار، أمرهم بجهادهم ليتمكن المسلمون من الحج، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-189-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-189-s1","r":"q2-189","title":"The useful answer to a question about the moon","text":"I say: Muʿādh ibn Jabal and Thaʿlaba ibn Ghanama asked him: “Messenger of God, why does the crescent appear thin as a thread, then increase until full, then diminish until it returns to a thread?” The Real said: they ask you about the crescents, about the wisdom of their increase and decrease. Tell them, Muḥammad: they mark times for people’s debts, cultivation, women’s waiting periods and fasting. They also mark pilgrimage’s times, its beginning and end, distinguishing timely performance from making it up. Were the moon always in one condition, these would not be known. The Real answers differently from what they expected, indicating that asking about the secret of the change yields no benefit under revealed law; attention should be given to what benefits religion. Astronomers say that its light is from the sun and its body smooth. As it moves away from alignment with the sun, the sun’s light faces it. When near the sun, only part of its body receives that light. When it passes beneath the sun in the sphere, its whole back faces the sun and none of its [visible face] receives the light. As it emerges from beneath, it receives light to that extent. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-189-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-189-s2","r":"q2-189","title":"The crescent of changing states and the sun of establishment","text":"When happiness’s crescent appears on the horizon of aspiration and guidance’s wind blows from preceding divine care, the time arrives for hearts to make pilgrimage to the presence of the Knower of unseen things. Guidance’s crescent belongs to travellers, possessors of states and changing coloration ( التلوين ). Its light grows as certainty grows and diminishes as certainty diminishes, according to the strength or weakness of the state, until union is realized and perfection granted. They recite: Every day you change your colour; something other than this would become you better. One subject to changing states passes between increase and decrease until gnosis’s sun rises. Once it rises there is no subsequent increase or decrease. They recite: The sun of the one I love rose by night, shining with no sunset to follow. The daytime sun sets in the night, but the sun of hearts never disappears. The one established ( صاحب التمكين ), by contrast, remains always in gnosis’s radiance, fixed in happiness’s constellation. Neither eclipse nor veil touches his sun; darkness and clouds do not obscure its light. Were he to ask for a veil, his request would not be granted. A gnostic said: “Were I charged to see another than He, I could not, for no other is with Him for me to witness.” The Real then warns against what the associators innovated in pilgrimage: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:189b وَلَيْسَ الْبِرُّ بِأَنْ تَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ ظُهُورِهَا وَلَكِنِ الْبِرُّ مَنِ اتَّقَى وَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ أَبْوَابِهَا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ Righteousness is not that you enter houses from their backs; righteousness is in one who fears God. Enter houses by their doors, and fear God, so that you may prosper.","anchor":"en-q2-189-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-189-s3","r":"q2-189","title":"Ritual custom and the courtesy of asking","text":"I say: when the Helpers made the greater or lesser pilgrimage, they would say that no roof should intervene between them and heaven until they entered their houses. On returning they climbed walls or opened holes in the backs of their houses. One man entered by the door and was reproached. The Real revealed: righteousness—obedience—is not entering from behind, climbing over or opening a hole above. Righteousness belongs to one avoiding prohibitions and opposing appetites. Alternatively, righteousness is not reversing the proper order of your questions, asking what does not benefit you and abandoning matters of knowledge useful now and hereafter. It belongs to one avoiding this. Enter the houses of knowledge by their doors: ask well, speak courteously, and put first what matters most and benefits most. Fear God: do not alter His rulings or object to His acts, so that you prosper through His enabling and guidance.","anchor":"en-q2-189-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-189-s4","r":"q2-189","title":"The three houses and their nine doors","text":"Know that the aspirant enters three houses: Sacred Law ( الشريعة ), Path ( الطريقة ) and Reality ( الحقيقة ). Each has doors. Whoever comes by the door enters; whoever comes otherwise is expelled. The house of Sacred Law has three doors. First is repentance. Once entered and realized with its pillars and conditions, the door of uprightness ( الاستقامة ) meets him: following the Messenger in words, acts and states. Upon realizing it, he meets God-fearing vigilance ( التقوى ) in its divisions. Realizing this outwardly and inwardly, he enters the purified Sacred Law’s house and ranges through its beauties and meanings. He then seeks the Path’s house, also with three doors. First is sincerity ( الإخلاص ): directing action to God alone without reservation or personal share. Once realized, the door of emptying ( التخلية ) meets him: purification from inward faults, which are innumerable. Whoever finds a shaykh is shown them and taught their remedies. Then comes adornment ( التحلية ): patience, forbearance, truthfulness, tranquillity, generosity, preferring others and every other perfection. Realizing sincerity, emptying and adornment, he has realized the Path’s house. [B128] The house of Reality then meets him. First he knocks at watchfulness ( المراقبة ): guarding heart and secret from bad thoughts. Once the heart is purified of thoughts settled within it, it overlooks the door of witnessing ( المشاهدة ): effacing traces in witnessing the lights of the Living, Self-Subsisting, or rendering vessels subtle when meanings appear. Entering and settling there, he meets the door of gnosis ( المعرفة ), the place of rootedness and establishment, the goal and end. The house of Reality is the mosque of the divine presence. Beyond it remains only ascent in stations and increasing gnoses and unveilings, for ever and ever. May God grant us an abundant share through His grace and generosity.","anchor":"en-q2-189-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-189-s5","r":"q2-189","title":"","text":"When pilgrimage was prescribed, unbelievers occupied the Sacred House. He therefore commands struggle against them so that Muslims may make pilgrimage:","anchor":"en-q2-189-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-190-195","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles 2:190–195","anchor":"unit-q2-190-195"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-1","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"وَقاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ الَّذِينَ يُقاتِلُونَكُمْ وَلا تَعْتَدُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِينَ (190) وَاقْتُلُوهُمْ حَيْثُ ثَقِفْتُمُوهُمْ وَأَخْرِجُوهُمْ مِنْ حَيْثُ أَخْرَجُوكُمْ وَالْفِتْنَةُ أَشَدُّ مِنَ الْقَتْلِ وَلا تَقْتُلُوهُمْ عِنْدَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ حَتَّى يَقْتُلُوكُمْ فِيهِ فَإِنْ قَتَلُوكُمْ فَاقْتُلُوهُمْ كَذلِكَ جَزاءُ الْكافِرِينَ (191) فَإِنِ انْتَهَوْا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (192) وَقاتِلُوهُمْ حَتَّى لا تَكُونَ فِتْنَةٌ وَيَكُونَ الدِّينُ لِلَّهِ فَإِنِ انْتَهَوْا فَلا عُدْوانَ إِلاَّ عَلَى الظَّالِمِينَ (193) الشَّهْرُ الْحَرامُ بِالشَّهْرِ الْحَرامِ وَالْحُرُماتُ قِصاصٌ فَمَنِ اعْتَدى عَلَيْكُمْ فَاعْتَدُوا عَلَيْهِ بِمِثْلِ مَا اعْتَدى عَلَيْكُمْ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِينَ (194)","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-2","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"وَأَنْفِقُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَلا تُلْقُوا بِأَيْدِيكُمْ إِلَى التَّهْلُكَةِ وَأَحْسِنُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ (195)","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-3","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"قلت: (التهلكة) : مصدر هلك- بتشديد اللام- قاله ابن عطية. وضمن (تُلْقُوا) معنى تفضوا، أو تنتهوا، فعدَّاه بإلى، أي: ولا تفضوا بأنفسكم إلى التهلكة. ولا يحتاج إلى زيادة الباء.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-4","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"وسبب نزول الآية: أن المشركين صَدُّوا رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عام الحديبية، وصالحوه على أن يرجع في قابل، فيخلوا له البيت ثلاثة أيام، فرجع لعمرة القضاء، وخاف المسلمون ألا يفوا لهم، فيقاتِلُوا في الحرم والشهر الحرام، وكرهوا ذلك، فنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-5","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وإعلاء كلمته الَّذِينَ يُقاتِلُونَكُمْ أي: يبدءونكم بالقتال، وَلا تَعْتَدُوا فتقاتلوهم قبل أن يبدءوكم إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِينَ لا ينصرهم ولا يؤيدهم. ثم نسخ هذا بقوله: وَقاتِلُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ كَافَّةً ... الآية. وَاقْتُلُوهُمْ حَيْثُ ثَقِفْتُمُوهُمْ أي: وجدتموهم، ولا تتحرجوا من قتالهم في الحرم، فإنهم هم الذين صدوكم وبدأوكم بالإذاية، وَأَخْرِجُوهُمْ من مكة حَيْثُ أَخْرَجُوكُمْ منها، وَالْفِتْنَةُ أي: الكفر الذي هم فيه، أَشَدُّ مِنَ الْقَتْلِ لهم في الحرم، وَلا تُقاتِلُوهُمْ عِنْدَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ ابتداءً حَتَّى يُقاتِلُوكُمْ فِيهِ، فَإِنْ قاتَلُوكُمْ فيه فَاقْتُلُوهُمْ فيه، وفي غيره، كَذلِكَ جَزاءُ الْكافِرِينَ يفعل بهم ما فعلوا بغيرهم، فَإِنِ انْتَهَوْا عن الشرك وأسلموا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ لهم رَحِيمٌ بهم.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-6","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"وَقاتِلُوهُمْ حَتَّى لا تَكُونَ فِتْنَةٌ أي: شرك وَيَكُونَ الدِّينُ خالصاً لِلَّهِ بحيث لا يبقى في جزيرة العرب إلا دين واحد، فَإِنِ انْتَهَوْا عن قتالكم، فلا تعتدوا فإنه فَلا عُدْوانَ إِلَّا عَلَى الظَّالِمِينَ إذ لا يحسن أن يظلم إلا من ظلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-7","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"القتال الصادر منكم لهم في الشَّهْرُ الْحَرامُ في مقابلة الصد الذي صدر منهم لكم في الشهر الحرام، وَالْحُرُماتُ قِصاصٌ يقتص بعضها من بعض، فكما انتهكوا حرمة الشهر الحرام، بمنعكم من البيت، فانتهكوا حرمتهم بالقتل فيه. فَمَنِ اعْتَدى عَلَيْكُمْ بالقتال في الأشهر الحُرُم، أو في الحرَم فَاعْتَدُوا عَلَيْهِ بِمِثْلِ مَا اعْتَدى عَلَيْكُمْ، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فلا تنتصروا لنفوسكم، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِينَ بالحفظ والتأييد.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-8","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"وَأَنْفِقُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ في جهاد عدوكم، ولا تمسكوا عن الإنفاق فيه فتلقوا بِأَيْدِيكُمْ أي: بأنفسكم إِلَى التَّهْلُكَةِ أي: الهلكة فيستولي عليكم عدوكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-9","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"رُوِيَ عن أبي أيوب الأنصاري (أنه كان على القسطنطينية، فحمل رجل على عسكر العدو، فقال قوم: ألقى بيده إلى التهلكة، فقال أبو أيوب: لا، إن هذه الآية نزلت في الأنصار، قالوا- لما أعز الله الإسلام وكثر أهله-: لو رجعنا إلى أهلينا وأموالنا نقيم فيها ونصلحها، فأنزل الله فينا وَلا تُلْقُوا بِأَيْدِيكُمْ إِلَى التَّهْلُكَةِ، وأما هذا فهو الذي قال فيه الله تعالى: وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَشْرِي نَفْسَهُ ابْتِغاءَ مَرْضاتِ اللَّهِ....)","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-10","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"أو: ولا تنفقوا كل أموالكم فتتعرضوا للهلكة، أو الطمع في الخلق، ولكن القصد، وهو الوسط. وَأَحْسِنُوا بالتفضل على المحاويج والمجاهدين إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ فيحفظهم، ويحفظ عقبهم إلى يوم القيامة.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-11","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن أعداء الإنسان التي تقطعه عن حضرة ربه أربعة: النفس والشيطان والدنيا والناس.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-12","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"فمجاهدة النفس: بمخالفة هواها، وتحميلها ما يَثقُل عليها حتى ترتاض، ومجاهدة الشيطان: بعصيانه، والاشتغال بالله عنه، فإنه يذوب بذكر الله، ومجاهدة الدنيا: بالزهد فيها، والقناعة بما تيسر منها، ومجاهدة الناس: بالغيبة عنهم والإعراض عنهم في الإقبال والإدبار. فيقول الحق جلّ جلاله للمتوجهين إليه: وَقاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ الَّذِينَ يُقاتِلُونَكُمْ ويصدونكم عن حضرته، ولا تعتدوا فتشتغلوا بهم عن ذكري، والإقبال عليّ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِينَ. بل اقتلوهم حيث تعرضوا لكم فقط، فإذا ظهرت صورة النفس أدبها، ثم غاب في الله عنها، وكذلك بقية القواطع.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-13","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"وكان شيخ شيوخنا سيدي علي الجمل رضي الله عنه يقول: (عداوة العدو حقاً هي اشتغالك بمحبة الحبيب حقا، وأما إذا اشتغلت بعداوة العدو فاتتك محبة الحبيب،، ونال العدو مراده منك) . هـ. وأخرجوهم من قلوبكم من حيث أخرجوكم من حضرة ربكم، يعني: كما أخرجوكم من الحضرة في أيام الغفلة، أخرجوهم من قلوبكم في أيام اليقظة. والفتنة بالاشتغال بهم أشد من القتل لهم، ولا تقاتلوهم عند مسجد الحضرة وحال الغيبة في الله، فإن ذلك التفات إلى غير الله، كمن كان مقبلاً عليه حبيبه فجعل يلتفت إلى مَن يكلمه ويشغله عنه. وذلك في غاية الجفاء، حتى يقاتلوكم فيه، ويريدون أن يخرجوكم منه بوسوستهم، فإن قاتلوكم، وخطر على بالكم شيء من وسوستهم، فاقتلوهم بذكر الله، والتعوّذ منهم، فإن الله يكفيكم أمرهم، وينهزمون عنكم، كذلك جزاء الكافرين. فإن انتهوا عنكم، وانقطع عنكم خواطرهم، فغيبوا عنهم فإن الله يستركم عنهم، وقاتلوهم على الدوام حتى لا تكون في قلوبكم فتنة منهم، ويكون التوجه كله لله، لا ينازعه شيء مما سواه، فإن انتهوا عنكم فلا تتعرضوا لهم فإن ذلك عدوان وظلم، فَلا عُدْوانَ إِلَّا عَلَى الظَّالِمِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-14","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"فإن جَنَحَتْ نفسُك إلى حرمة الطاعة الظاهرة كتدريس علم أو جهاد أو صلاة أو غيرها، وأرادت أن تخرجك من حرمة الحضرة القدسية وهي الفكرة والشهود والمعاينة، فقاتلها وأخرجها من حرمة تلك الطاعة، فالحرمات قصاص. فكما أخرجتك من حضرة ربك القدسية أخرِجْها من حضرة الطاعة الحسية إلى الطاعة القلبية. فإن الذرة من أعمال القلوب أفضل من أمثال الجبال من أعمال الجوارح.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-15","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"فمَن اعتدى عليكم، في زمن البطالة، فاعتدوا عليه في زمن اليقظة بمثل ما اعتدى عليكم. وكان شيخنا البوزيدى رضي الله عنه يقول: جوروا على نفوسكم بقدر ما جارت عليكم. هـ. أي: اقتلوها بقدر ما قتلتكم بالبعد عن ربكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-16","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"وكان أيضاً يقول: (جوروا على الوهم قبل أن يجور عليكم) . هـ. واتقوا الله فإن الله يعينكم عليها، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِينَ. وأنفقوا أنفسكم ومهجكم في سبيل الله، بأن تطرحوها في يد الله يفعل بها ما يشاء. وَلا تُلْقُوا بِأَيْدِيكُمْ إِلَى التَّهْلُكَةِ فتدبروا لها، وتختاروا لها، وتعتنوا بشئونها، فإن ذلك غفلة عن ربكم. وَأَحْسِنُوا أي: ادخلوا في مقام الإحسان بأن تعبدوا الله كأنكم ترونه إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ أي: يقربهم إلى حضرته، ويصطفيهم إلى محبته ومعرفته، خرطنا الله في سلكهم بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-190-195-17","r":"q2-190-195","title":"2:190–195 · Conflict, sacred limits and the struggle against inward obstacles","text":"ثم أمر الحق تعالى بإتمام النسك الذي دخل فيه، وحض على الإخلاص فيه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-190-195-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-190-195-s1","r":"q2-190-195","title":"Destruction and the return after al-Ḥudaybiya","text":"[Translator’s note: Cairo I:222 prints three forms of qatala (“kill”) in the heading of 2:191; the following exposition uses qātala (“fight”). The translation preserves this distinction. The bracketed “some of” makes the collective plural address explicit.] I say: destruction ( التهلكة ) is the verbal noun of hallaka , with doubled lām, according to Ibn ʿAṭiyya. “Cast” includes the meaning of bringing or leading to, hence it takes ilā : do not bring yourselves to destruction. There is no need to regard the bāʾ as redundant. The occasion was the associators’ barring the Messenger in the year of al-Ḥudaybiya, then making peace on condition that he return the following year and have the House vacated for three days. When he returned for the lesser pilgrimage in fulfilment of the agreement, Muslims feared that the others would break it, leading to fighting in the sanctuary and sacred month. They disliked this, and the passage was revealed.","anchor":"en-q2-190-195-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-190-195-s2","r":"q2-190-195","title":"Fighting, restraint and reciprocal limits","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: fight in God’s way, raising His word, those who begin fighting you. Do not transgress by beginning before they do. God neither loves, supports nor strengthens transgressors. This was then abrogated by “fight the associators all together” [9:36]. [B129] Kill them wherever you find them and do not hesitate over fighting in the sanctuary, for they barred you and initiated harm. Expel them from Mecca as they expelled you. The fitna —their unbelief—is more grievous than killing them in the sanctuary. Do not initiate fighting at the Sacred Mosque until they fight you there; if they do, kill them there and elsewhere. Such is their recompense: they are treated as they treated others. If they abandon association and embrace Islam, God forgives and shows mercy to them. Fight until there is no association and religion belongs purely to God, so that only one religion remains in the Arabian Peninsula. If they cease fighting you, do not transgress: aggression is only against wrongdoers, for it is not fitting to wrong anyone except one who has wronged. [B130] Your fighting them in the sacred month corresponds to their barring you in a sacred month. Sanctities are reciprocally requited: as they violated the month’s sanctity by keeping you from the House, violate their immunity by fighting in it. Whoever transgresses against you through fighting in sacred months or the sanctuary, respond in equal measure. Fear God and do not act merely to vindicate yourselves. Know that God protects and strengthens the God-fearing. Spend in God’s way in struggle against the enemy. Do not withhold spending and cast yourselves into destruction, allowing the enemy to overpower you. Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī is reported to have been at Constantinople when a man charged the enemy’s army. Some said he had cast himself into destruction. Abū Ayyūb replied: “No. This verse concerned the Helpers. When God strengthened Islam and its followers multiplied, we said, ‘Let us return to our families and properties, remain there and put them in order.’ God revealed to us, ‘Do not cast yourselves into destruction.’ This man, however, is described by ‘Among people is one who sells himself seeking God’s good pleasure’ [2:207].” [B131] Alternatively: do not spend all your wealth, exposing yourselves to destruction or dependence upon people. Keep to moderation, the middle course. Do good by generously assisting the needy and those struggling in God’s way. God loves the good-doers and preserves them and their descendants until the Resurrection Day.","anchor":"en-q2-190-195-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-190-195-s3","r":"q2-190-195","title":"Four enemies and the danger of becoming occupied with them","text":"Know that four enemies cut a person off from his Lord’s presence: the lower self, Satan, the world and people. Struggle against the lower self opposes its desires and makes it bear what it finds heavy until disciplined. Struggle against Satan disobeys him and becomes occupied with God instead, for remembrance melts him away. Struggle against the world renounces it and is content with what comes easily. Struggle against people becomes absent from them and turns aside from their coming and going. The Real tells those turning to Him: fight in God’s way those fighting you and barring you from His presence, but do not transgress by becoming occupied with them instead of remembering and turning towards Me. God does not love transgressors. Strike them only where they confront you. When the form of the lower self appears, discipline it, then become absent from it in God; likewise with the remaining obstacles. Our masters’ master, Sīdī ʿAlī al-Jamal, said: “True enmity towards the enemy is being truly occupied with love of the Beloved. If you become occupied with hating the enemy, you lose love of the Beloved, and the enemy gains his intention.” Expel these obstacles from your hearts as they expelled you from your Lord’s presence: as they expelled you in heedless days, expel them in days of wakefulness. Being tried through occupation with them is more grievous than putting them to death. Do not fight them at the mosque of the presence while absent in God: that would turn towards other than God, like someone whose Beloved faces him while he turns towards another speaking and distracting him—utter discourtesy. Only when they fight there, trying to drive you out through whisperings, should you act. When their whisperings enter your thoughts, overcome them by remembering God and seeking refuge. God suffices you and they flee. Such is the recompense of unbelievers. If their thoughts cease, become absent from them, and God screens you from them. Persist in struggling until no disturbance from them remains in your hearts and all orientation belongs to God, uncontested by anything else. If they desist, do not provoke them: that would be transgression and wrongdoing. There is no aggression except against wrongdoers. If your lower self inclines to the sanctity of outward obedience—teaching, struggle, prayer or another act—and tries to remove you from the holy presence’s sanctity, reflection, witnessing and direct vision, resist it and draw it from that outward observance to inward obedience. Sanctities are reciprocally requited. An atom of the heart’s works surpasses mountains of bodily works. [B132] Whoever transgressed against you in idle days, respond in wakeful days with equal measure. Our shaykh al-Būzīdī said: “Be hard upon your lower selves in proportion to their hardness upon you”—put them to death in proportion to their having killed you through distance from your Lord. He also said: “Overcome imagination before it overcomes you.” Fear God, and He will assist you against them; He is with the God-fearing. Spend your selves and very lives in God’s way, placing them in God’s hand to do with as He wills. Do not cast yourselves into destruction by planning, choosing and attending to their affairs, for that is heedlessness of your Lord. Do good: enter the station of excellence, worshipping God as though you see Him. He loves the good-doers, bringing them near, electing them for His love and knowledge. May He include us among them through His grace and generosity.","anchor":"en-q2-190-195-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-190-195-s4","r":"q2-190-195","title":"","text":"The Real commands completion of the rite once entered and urges sincerity in it:","anchor":"en-q2-190-195-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-196","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self 2:196","anchor":"unit-q2-196"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-1","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"وَأَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلَّهِ فَإِنْ أُحْصِرْتُمْ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ وَلا تَحْلِقُوا رُؤُسَكُمْ حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ الْهَدْيُ مَحِلَّهُ فَمَنْ كانَ مِنْكُمْ مَرِيضاً أَوْ بِهِ أَذىً مِنْ رَأْسِهِ فَفِدْيَةٌ مِنْ صِيامٍ أَوْ صَدَقَةٍ أَوْ نُسُكٍ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-196-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-2","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"قلت: المشهور في اللغة أن أحصر الرباعي: بالمرض، وحصر الثلاثي: بالعدو، وقيل: بالعكس، وقيل: هما سواء. و (ما استيسر) : خبر أو مبتدأ، أي: فالواجب ما استيسر، أو: فعليه ما استيسر.","anchor":"ar-q2-196-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-3","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَأَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ الذي دخلتم فيه، وَالْعُمْرَةَ وجوباً كالصلاة والصوم، ويكون ذلك لِلَّهِ لا رياء ولا سمعة، وإنما خصّ الحج والعمرة بالحض على الإخلاص، لما يسرع إليهما من الخلل أكثر من غيرهما، فمن أفسدهما وجب عليه قضاؤهما، فَإِنْ أُحْصِرْتُمْ ومنعتم من إتمامهما فتحللوا منهما، وعليكم فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ، وذلك شاة وَلا تَحْلِقُوا رُؤُسَكُمْ أي: لا تتحللوا حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ الْهَدْيُ مَحِلَّهُ، أي: حيث يحل ذبحه، وهو محل الإحصار عند الشافعي، فيذبح فيه بنية التحلل ويُفرق، ومِنَى أو مكة عند مالك، فيُرسله فإذا تحقق أنه وصل وذُبح حل وحلق.","anchor":"ar-q2-196-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-4","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"ويحرم على المُحْرِم إزالة الشعث، ولبس المخيط بالعضو، فمن كان مَرِيضاً أَوْ بِهِ أَذىً صُداع أو نحوه، فحلق رأسه، أو لبس ثيابه، فعليه فدية مِنْ صِيامٍ ثلاثة أيام، أَوْ صَدَقَةٍ على ستة مساكين، مُدَّان لكل مسكين، أَوْ نُسُكٍ بشاة فأعلى، فهو مخير بين الثلاثة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-196-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-5","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"الإشارة: إذا عقد المريد مع ربه عُقْدةً، فالواجب عليه إتمامها حتى يَجْني ثمرتَها، فإذا عقد عقدة المجاهدة فليجاهد نفسه حتى يجني ثمرتها، وهي المشاهدة، وإذا عقد مع الشيخ عقدة الصحبة، فليلزم خدمته حتى يدخله إلى بيت الحضرة، ويشهد له بالترشيد. وهكذا كل من عقد مع الله عقدة يجب عليه إتمامها، فإن أُحصر ومُنع من إتمامها فليفعل ما استيسر من ذبح نفسه وحط رأسه، ولا يُكَلِّفُ اللَّهُ نَفْساً إِلَّا ما آتاها، ولا ينبغي أن يستعجل الفتح قبل إِبَّانِه، فلعلَّه يُعاقَب بحرمانه، فكم من مريد طلب من شيخه أَنْ يُطلعه على سر الربوبية قبل بلوغ محله، فكان ذلك سبب عطبه، فيقال له: ولا تحلق رأسك من شهود السوى حتى يبلغ هَديُ نفسك محله فيذبح، فإذا ذُبِحت النفس وأُجهِز عليها حلق رأسه حينئذٍ من شهود السِّوى، وفي ذلك يقول الششتري رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-196-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-6","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"إنْ تُرِدَ وَصْلَنَا فَمَوْتكَ شَرْطٌ ... لا يَنَالُ الوِصَالَ مَنْ فِيهِ فَضْلَهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-196-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-7","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"فمن كان مريضاً بضعف عزمه، أو به أذى بعدم نهوض حاله، بحيث لم تُسعفْه المقادير في مجاهدة نفسه، فليشتغل بالنسك الظاهر من صيام أو صدقة أو قراءة أو غير ذلك، حتى يَمنَّ عليه العليمُ الحكيمُ. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-196-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-8","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"ولما ذكر الحق تعالى هدى الإحصار وفديَة الأذى، ذكر هدى التمتع، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-196-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-9","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"... فَإِذا أَمِنْتُمْ فَمَنْ تَمَتَّعَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الْحَجِّ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ فَمَنْ لَمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيامُ ثَلاثَةِ أَيَّامٍ فِي الْحَجِّ وَسَبْعَةٍ إِذا رَجَعْتُمْ تِلْكَ عَشَرَةٌ كامِلَةٌ ذلِكَ لِمَنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ أَهْلُهُ حاضِرِي الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقابِ (196)","anchor":"ar-q2-196-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-10","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فإذا حصل لكم الأمن من المرض أو العدو، وأردتم الحج فَمَنْ تَمَتَّعَ منكم بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الْحَجِّ بأن قدَّم العمرة في أشهر الحج، ثم حجّ من عامه، فالواجب عليه فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ شاة فأعلى لكونه تمتَّعَ بإسقاط أحد السَّفَرَيْن ولم يُفرِد لكل عبادة سفراً مخصوصاً. فَمَنْ لَمْ يَجِدْ الهدي، ولم يقدِر على شرائه، فعليه فَصِيامُ ثَلاثَةِ أَيَّامٍ فِي زمن الْحَجَّ، وهو زمنُ إحرامه إلى وقوفه بعرفة، فإن لم يصم في ذلك الزمان صام أيام التشريق. ثم يصوم سبعة أيام إذا رجَع إلى مكة أو إلى بلده. فتلك عَشَرَةٌ أيام كامِلَةٌ، ولا تتوهموا أن السبعة بدل من الثلاثة، فلذلك صرّح الحقّ تعالى بفَذْلَكة الحساب .","anchor":"ar-q2-196-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-11","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"وهذا الهَدْي أو الصيام إنما يجب على المتمتع إذا لم يكن ساكناً بأهله في مكة أو ذي طَوى، وأما مَن كان (أهلُه حاضري المسجد الحرام) فلا هَدى عليه لأنه يُحرم بالحج من مكة فلم يسقط أحد السفرين، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ في امتثال أوامره، وخصوصاً مناسك الحج لكثرتها وتشعب فروعها، ولذلك أُفردت بالتأليف، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقابِ لمن ترك أوامرَه وارتكب نواهيه. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-196-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-12","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق جلّ جلاله على طريق الإشارة للمتوجهين إليه: فإذا أمنتُمْ من أعدائكم الذين يقطعونكم عن الوصول إلى حضرتنا، أو أمِنْتُم من الرجوع بعد الوصال، أو من السلب بعد العطاء، وذلك بعد التمكين من شهود أسرار الذات، وأنوار الصفات، إذ الكريم إذا أعطى لا يرجع، فإذا حصل لكم الأَمْن، فمن تمتع بأنوار الشريعة إلى أسرار الحقيقة فعليه ما استطاع من الهدي والسمت الحسَن والخلُق الحَسن لأنه إذ ذاك قد اتصف بصفة الكمال وتصدَّر لتربية الرجال، فمن لم يجد ذلك فليرجع إلى ما تيسر من المجاهدة حتى يتمكن من ذلك الهَدْي الحسن والخلق الحسن، هذا لمن لم يتمكن في الحضرة الأزلية، وأما مَن كان مقيماً بها، عاكفاً في شهود أنوارها، فلا كلام عليه، لأنه قد تولاّه مولاه، وغيَّبَه عن شهود نفسه وهواه، فَأمْرُه كله بالله وإلى الله. جعلنا الله فيهم بمنّه وكرمه،","anchor":"ar-q2-196-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-13","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"لكن لا يغفُل عن التقوى لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام: «أنا أعرفُكُم بالله، وأنا أتقاكم له» . وقالوا: «من علامة النهايات الرجوعُ إلى البدايات» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-196-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-196-14","r":"q2-196","title":"2:196 · Completing pilgrimage and the offering of the self","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى ميقات الحج الزمانى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-196-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-196-s1","r":"q2-196","title":"Being prevented from completing the rites","text":"I say: the well-known linguistic distinction makes the four-letter form aḥṣara refer to illness and the three-letter form ḥaṣara to an enemy’s obstruction. Some reverse this, and some make them equivalent. “Whatever is within reach” is a predicate or subject: the obligation is what is within reach, or what is within reach is incumbent upon him.","anchor":"en-q2-196-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-196-s2","r":"q2-196","title":"Completion, obstruction and compensation for removing hair","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: complete the greater and lesser pilgrimage you have begun, as an obligation like prayer and fasting. Do so for God, not display or reputation. They are particularly urged to sincerity because corruption enters them more readily than other acts. Whoever invalidates either must make it up. If prevented from completion, leave the consecrated state and owe whatever offering is available: a sheep. Do not shave—that is, do not leave consecration—until the offering reaches the place where it may be slaughtered. According to al-Shāfiʿī this is the place of obstruction: it is slaughtered there with the intention of leaving consecration and distributed. According to Mālik the place is Minā or Mecca: the offering is sent, and once its arrival and slaughter are established, the pilgrim leaves consecration and shaves. [B133] One in consecration may not remove dishevelment or wear clothing sewn to fit a bodily member. Whoever is ill or suffers a headache or similar affliction and shaves or puts on ordinary clothing owes a ransom: fasting three days, giving two mudds to each of six needy persons, or sacrificing a sheep or larger animal. He chooses among the three. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-196-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-196-s3","r":"q2-196","title":"Completing a covenant and not forcing an opening","text":"When an aspirant binds himself to his Lord by a commitment, he must complete it until he harvests its fruit. Having committed to struggle, he must struggle against his self until witnessing results. Having covenanted for companionship with a shaykh, he must continue serving until the shaykh admits him to the house of the presence and attests his maturity. Every covenant with God must be completed. If obstructed from completion, do whatever is possible of sacrificing the self and lowering the head: “God charges no soul beyond what He has given it” [65:7]. Do not hasten an opening before its season, lest deprivation be the punishment. Many an aspirant asked his shaykh to disclose lordship’s secret before its proper time and thereby met ruin. He is told: do not shave your head of witnessing an other until your self’s offering reaches its place and is slaughtered. Only when the self is fully sacrificed is the head shaved of witnessing otherness. Al-Shushtarī says: If you desire union with us, your death is a condition; one in whom a remnant remains does not attain union. Whoever is ill through weak resolve or afflicted by a state that will not rise, destiny not assisting his struggle, should occupy himself with outward devotion—fasting, charity, recitation or another act—until the Knowing, Wise grants His favour. Through God is success; He guides to the sound road. After the obstruction-offering and compensation for affliction, the Real mentions the offering for combining the two pilgrimages: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:196b فَإِذَا أَمِنْتُمْ فَمَنْ تَمَتَّعَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الْحَجِّ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ When you are secure, whoever enjoys the lesser pilgrimage until the greater shall offer whatever sacrificial animal is within reach.","anchor":"en-q2-196-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-196-s4","r":"q2-196","title":"Tamattuʿ and the complete count of ten","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when secure from illness or enemy and intending pilgrimage, whoever performs the lesser pilgrimage in the pilgrimage months, then the greater in the same year, owes an available offering, a sheep or larger animal. He enjoyed the benefit of dispensing with one of two journeys, not assigning each act its own journey. Whoever finds no offering and cannot buy one must fast three days in pilgrimage’s period, from consecration to standing at ʿArafa. If he does not fast then, he fasts the days of Tashrīq. He then fasts seven when he returns to Mecca or his homeland. These are ten complete days: do not suppose the seven replace the three. Hence the explicit summation ( فذلكة الحساب ). The offering or fast applies only when the pilgrim’s household does not reside in Mecca or Dhū Ṭuwā. A resident at the Sacred Mosque owes no offering, since he enters consecration for pilgrimage from Mecca and has not dispensed with a journey. Fear God in obeying His commands, especially the many, ramifying pilgrimage rites, which accordingly receive separate treatises. Know His punishment is severe for abandoning commands and committing prohibitions. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-196-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-196-s5","r":"q2-196","title":"Good bearing after security in realization","text":"The Real tells those turning to Him by way of allusion: when secure from enemies cutting you off from Our presence, from returning after union, or from loss after a gift—after establishment in witnessing the Essence’s secrets and the Attributes’ lights, for the Generous does not withdraw His gift—whoever enjoys the Sacred Law’s lights unto Reality’s secrets must offer what he can of right conduct, good bearing and good character ( الهدي والسمت الحسن والخلق الحسن ). He has attained perfection and taken his place forming men. Whoever does not possess this should return to whatever struggle is possible until established in good bearing and character. [B134] This concerns one not established in the eternal presence. One residing there, abiding in witnessing its lights, lies beyond such discussion: his Master has taken charge of him and removed him from witnessing self and desire. His affair is wholly through God and towards God. May God place us among them through His grace and generosity. Yet he must not neglect God-fearing vigilance: the Prophet said, “I am the most knowing of God among you and the most God-fearing.” They say: “A sign of the endings is returning to the beginnings.” And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-196-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-196-s6","r":"q2-196","title":"","text":"The Real specifies pilgrimage’s appointed time:","anchor":"en-q2-196-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-197","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage 2:197","anchor":"unit-q2-197"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-1","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"الْحَجُّ أَشْهُرٌ مَعْلُوماتٌ فَمَنْ فَرَضَ فِيهِنَّ الْحَجَّ فَلا رَفَثَ وَلا فُسُوقَ وَلا جِدالَ فِي الْحَجِّ وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يَعْلَمْهُ اللَّهُ وَتَزَوَّدُوا فَإِنَّ خَيْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوى وَاتَّقُونِ يا أُولِي الْأَلْبابِ (197)","anchor":"ar-q2-197-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-2","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"قلت: (الحج) : مبتدأ، على حذف مضاف، أي: إحرامُ الحج أو فعلُ الحج، و (أشهر) : خبر، وإذا وقع الزمان خبراً عن اسم معنى فإن كان ذلك المعنى واقعاً في كل ذلك الزمان أو جُلِّه تعيَّن رفعُه عند الكوفيين، وترجح عند البصريين إذا كان الزمان نكرة، نحو: السفر يوم. إن كان السفر واقعاً في جميع ذلك اليوم أو في جُلِّه لأنه باستغراقه إياه صار كأنه هو، ويصح: السفر يوماً، أو في يوم. وإن كان ذلك المعنى واقعاً في بعض ذلك الزمان تعيَّن نصبه أو جرّه ب (في) ، نحو: السفر يوم الجمعة، أو في يوم الجمعة وقد يرفع نادراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-197-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-3","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"قال في التسهيل: ويُغني- أيْ: ظرف الزمان- عن خبر اسم معنى مطلقاً، فإن وقع في جميعه، أو في أكثره، وكان نكرة، رُفع غالباً، ولا يمتنع نصبه ولا جره بفي خلافاً للكوفيين. وربما رُفع خبرُ الزمان المُوقَع في بعضه. هـ. ومن ذلك: الْحَجُّ أَشْهُرٌ مَعْلُوماتٌ فإن جلّها تصلح للإحرام.","anchor":"ar-q2-197-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-4","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وقتُ إحرام الحج أَشْهُرٌ مَعْلُوماتٌ: شوال وذو القعدة وذو الحجة، فمن أحرم قبلها كره عند مالك، وبطل عند الشافعي، فَمَنْ فَرَضَ على نفسه فِيهِنَّ الْحَجَّ فيلزم الأدب والوقار، ويجانبْ شهوة النساء، (فَلا) يقع منه رَفَثَ أي: جماع أو كلام فُحْش، وَلا فُسُوقَ أي: ذنوب، وَلا جِدالَ فِي زمان الْحَجُّ ولو مع المكاري أو الخُدّام، ولا غيره من أنواع الخصام فإنه في حضرة الملك العلاّم.","anchor":"ar-q2-197-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-5","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ كحِلْم وصبر وحُسن خلق يَعْلَمْهُ اللَّهُ فاستبقوا الخيرات، وتزودوا قبل هجوم الممات، واتقوا الله حق تقاته فَإِنَّ خَيْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوى. أو تزودوا لسفر الحج، ولا تسافروا كلّا على الناس","anchor":"ar-q2-197-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-6","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"فَإِنَّ خَيْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوى عن الطمع في الخلق، وَاتَّقُونِ يا أُولِي الْأَلْبابِ، وأفرِدُوني في سركم حتى أفتح لكم الباب، وأدخلَكم مع الأحباب.","anchor":"ar-q2-197-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-7","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"الإشارة: معاملة الأبدان مؤقتة بالأماكن والأزمان، ومعاملة القلوب أو الأرواح غير مؤقتة بزمان مخصوص، ولا مكان مخصوص، فحجَ القلوب، الأزمنةُ كلها له ميقات، والأماكن كلها عرفات، حج القلوب هو العكوف في حضرة علاّم الغيوب، وهي مُسَرْمَدَةٌ على الدوام على مَرِّ الليالي والأيام، فكل وقت عندهم ليلة القدر، وكل مكان عندهم عرفةُ المشرَّفةُ القدر، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-197-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-8","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"لولا شهودُ جمالكم في ذاتي ... ما كنتُ أَرْضَى ساعة بِحَياتي","anchor":"ar-q2-197-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-9","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"ما ليلةُ القدرُ الْمُعَظَّمُ شأنُها ... إلاَّ إذا عَمَرَتْ بكُم أوقَاتِي","anchor":"ar-q2-197-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-10","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"إنَّ المحبَّ إذا تمكَّنَ في الهَوَى ... والحب لم يَحْتَجْ إلى ميقاتِ","anchor":"ar-q2-197-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-11","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"وقال آخر :","anchor":"ar-q2-197-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-12","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"كُلُّ وقتٍ مِنْ حَبيبيِ ... قدره كألف حجة","anchor":"ar-q2-197-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-13","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"فازَ مَنْ خلَّى الشَّوَاغِلْ ... وَلِموْلاَه تَوَجَّهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-197-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-14","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"فمَنْ فَرض على قلبه حجَّ الحضرة فليلتزم الأدب والنظرة، والسكوتَ والفكرة، قال تعالى وَخَشَعَتِ الْأَصْواتُ لِلرَّحْمنِ فَلا تَسْمَعُ إِلَّا هَمْساً فلا رفث ولا فسوقَ ولا جدال ولا مراء، إذ مبنى طريقهم على التسليم والرضى، وما تفعلوا من خير فليس على الله بخفي. وتزودوا بتقوى شهود السَّوَى، فَإِنَّ خَيْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوى، وجِمَاعُ التقوى هي مخالفة الهَوى، ومحبة المولَى، فهذه تقوى أولي الألباب الذين صفَتْ مِرآة قلوبهم، فأبصروا الرشد والصواب. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-197-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-197-15","r":"q2-197","title":"2:197 · Pilgrimage’s months and the heart’s perpetual pilgrimage","text":"ثم أباح الحق تعالى التجارة فى مواسم الحج، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-197-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-197-s1","r":"q2-197","title":"A period of time predicated of an abstract noun","text":"I say: “pilgrimage” is a subject with an omitted annexed noun: entering consecration for pilgrimage, or performing pilgrimage. “Months” is its predicate. When time is predicated of an abstract noun ( اسم معنى ), and the event occupies all or most of that time, the Kufans require the nominative. The Basrans prefer it when the time-expression is indefinite: “the journey is a day,” if travel fills all or most of it. By occupying the whole period, the event is as though identical with it. “The journey [takes] a day” in the accusative, or “is in a day,” is also valid. If the event occupies only part of the time, the accusative or genitive with fī is required: “the journey [occurs on] Friday” or “on Friday,” though the nominative occurs rarely. The Tashīl says: a temporal adverb can stand in place of the predicate of an abstract noun without restriction. If the event occurs in all or most of the time and the expression is indefinite, it is generally nominative, but, contrary to the Kufans, neither accusative nor genitive with fī is prohibited. Sometimes a time-expression containing the event only partly is nominative. Such is “pilgrimage is known months,” since most of them are suitable for consecration.","anchor":"en-q2-197-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-197-s2","r":"q2-197","title":"Courtesy and provision for the journey","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the time for entering pilgrimage’s consecration is known months: Shawwāl, Dhū al-Qaʿda and Dhū al-Ḥijja. Earlier consecration is disliked according to Mālik and invalid according to al-Shāfiʿī. Whoever imposes pilgrimage upon himself in them must maintain courtesy and dignity and avoid desire for women: neither intercourse or indecent speech, nor sins, nor disputation—even with a hired carrier or servants—or other quarrels should occur. He stands in the presence of the All-Knowing King. God knows whatever good you do: forbearance, patience and good character. Race towards good deeds and take provision before death overtakes you. Fear God as He deserves, for the best provision is God-fearing vigilance. Or: take provision for the pilgrimage journey, not travelling as a burden upon people, for the best provision is guarding against coveting what creatures possess. Fear Me, people of understanding, and single Me out in your secret, so that I open the door and admit you among the beloved.","anchor":"en-q2-197-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-197-s3","r":"q2-197","title":"Every time a Night of Power, every place an ʿArafa","text":"Bodily dealings are assigned places and times. The dealings of hearts and spirits have no particular appointed time or place. For the pilgrimage of hearts, every season is appointed and every place an ʿArafa. Their pilgrimage is abiding in the presence of the Knower of unseen things, eternally continuous through passing nights and days. Every time is for them a Night of Power, every place an ʿArafa of exalted worth. They recite: But for witnessing Your beauty within me, I would not be content with one hour of life. The Night of Power, exalted in worth, is only when my times are filled with You. The lover established in ardour and love needs no appointed season. Another said: Every moment from my Beloved is worth a thousand years. Successful is one who leaves distractions and turns towards his Master. Whoever undertakes the presence’s pilgrimage in his heart should maintain courtesy and contemplation, silence and reflection: “Voices are humbled before the Compassionate; you hear only a whisper” [20:108]. No indecent speech, wrongdoing, disputation or contention: their path rests upon surrender and contentment. No good you do is hidden from God. Take provision by guarding against witnessing otherness, for the best provision is God-fearing vigilance. Its sum is opposing desire and loving the Master. Such is the vigilance of people of understanding whose heart-mirrors are purified, so that they perceive guidance and right judgement. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q2-197-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-197-s4","r":"q2-197","title":"","text":"The Real permits trading during pilgrimage’s seasons:","anchor":"en-q2-197-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-198-199","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument 2:198–199","anchor":"unit-q2-198-199"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-1","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُناحٌ أَنْ تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلاً مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-2","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"قلت: (أن تبتغوا) : على إسقاط حرف الجر، أيْ: في أن تبتغوا، وسبب نزول الآية: أن عُكاظاً ومَجَنّة وذا المجاز- أسماء مواضع- كانت أسواقاً في الجاهلية يعمرونها في مواسم الحج، وكانت معايشهم منها، فلما جاء الإسلام تأثَّمُوا وتحرجوا أن يتجروا فيها، فقال لهم الحق جلّ جلاله: لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُناحٌ أي: إثم أو ميل","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-3","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"عن الصواب، في أَنْ تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلًا مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ أي: عطاء ورزقاً تستفيدونه من التجارة في مواسم حجكم، إذا خلَصَتْ نيتكم، وغلب قصدُ الحج على التجارة.","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-4","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"وهاهنا قاعدةٌ ذكرها الغزالي في الإحياء، وحاصلها: أن العمل إذا تمحَّض لغير الله فهو سبب المقت والعقاب، وإذا تمحض لله خالصاً فهو سبب القرب والثواب، وإذا امتزج بشوْب من الرياء أو حظوظ النفس فينظر إلى الغالب وقوة الباعث فإن كان باعث الحظ أغلب، سقط، وكان إلى العقوبة أقرب، لكن عقوبته أخف ممن تجرد لغير الله، وإن كان باعث التقرب أغلب، حُط منه بقدر ما فيه من باعث الحظ، وإن تساويا تقاوما وتساقطا وصار العمل لا له ولا عليه.","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-5","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"ثم قال: ويشهد لهذا إجماعُ الأمة على أن مَنْ خرج حاجّاً ومعه تجارة صحَّ حجه وأُثيب عليه. ثم قال:","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-6","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"والصواب أنْ يقال: مهما كان الحج هو المحرّك الأصلي، وكان غرضُ التجارة كالتابع، فلا ينفك نفس السفر عن ثواب، ثم طُرِّد هذا الاعتبار في الجهاد باعتبار الغنيمة، يعني: يُنْظر لغالب الباعث وخُلوص القصد، وكذلك الصوم للحِمْية والثواب، ينظر لغالب الباعث.","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-7","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"قلت: وتطَّرد هذه القاعدة في المعاملات كلها، وجميع الحركات والسكنات والحِرَف وسائر الأسباب، فالخالص من الحظوظ مقبول، والمتمحض للحظوظ مردود، والمَشُوب يُنظر للغالب كما تقدم.","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-8","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"وقد ذكر شيخ المشايخ سيدي أبو الحسن الشاذلى رضي الله عنه قاعدة أخرى أدقّ من هذه فقال: إذا أكرم الله عبداً في حركاته وسكناته، نصَب له العبودية لله وستر عنه حظوظ نفسه، وجعله يتقلّب في عبوديته، والحظوظ عنه مستورة، مع جَرْي ما قُدِّر له، ولا يلتفت إليها لأنها في معزل عنه، وإذا أهان الله عبداً في حركاته وسكناته، نصب له حظوظ نفسه، وستر عنه عبوديته، فهو يتقلّب في شهواته، وعبودية الله عنه بمعزلِ، وإن كان يجري عليه شيء منها في الظاهر، قال: وهذا باب من الولاية والإهانة. وأما الصِّدِّيقية العظمى، والولاية الكبرى، فالحظوظ والحقوق كلها سواء عند ذوي البصيرة لأنه بالله فيما يأخذ ويترك. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-9","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"الإشارة: العبد لا يستغني عن طلب الزيادة، ولو بلغ من الكمال غاية النهاية، فالقناعة من الله حرمان، واعتقاد بلوغ النهاية نقصان، فليس عليكم جناح أيها العارفون أَن تَبْتَغُواْ فَضْلاً مِّن ربكم زيادة في إيقانكم، وترَقِّياً في معانيكم، إذ كمالات الحق لا نهاية لها، وأسرار الذات لا إحاطة بها، قال تعالى: وَلا يُحِيطُونَ بِهِ عِلْماً. والله وليّ التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-10","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى الوقوف بعرفة، والرجوع إلى المزدلفة والمشعر الحرام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-198-199-11","r":"q2-198-199","title":"2:198–199 · Seeking bounty during pilgrimage; ʿArafāt and the Sacred Monument","text":"... فَإِذا أَفَضْتُمْ مِنْ عَرَفاتٍ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ عِنْدَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرامِ وَاذْكُرُوهُ كَما هَداكُمْ وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ لَمِنَ الضَّالِّينَ (198) ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفاضَ النَّاسُ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللَّهَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (199)","anchor":"ar-q2-198-199-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-198-199-s1","r":"q2-198-199","title":"Trade during pilgrimage","text":"I say: “That you seek” ( أن تبتغوا ) follows the omission of a preposition ( إسقاط حرف الجر ): that is, “in your seeking.” The occasion of this verse’s revelation was that ʿUkāẓ, Majanna and Dhū al-Majāz—names of places—were markets in the Age of Ignorance. People frequented them in the pilgrimage seasons and drew their livelihoods from them. When Islam came, they felt that trading there was sinful and were reluctant to do so. The Real, glorious is His majesty, therefore told them: there is no blame upon you—no sin or departure from what is right—in seeking bounty from your Lord: a gift and provision obtained through trade in your pilgrimage seasons, provided your intention is sincere and your purpose of pilgrimage predominates over trade.","anchor":"en-q2-198-199-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-198-199-s2","r":"q2-198-199","title":"Mixed motives and the predominant impulse","text":"Here there is a rule mentioned by al-Ghazālī in the Iḥyāʾ . Its substance is that an act done entirely for something other than God causes divine loathing and punishment; one done wholly and sincerely for God causes nearness and reward. When it is mixed with ostentation ( الرياء ) or the lower self’s interests ( حظوظ النفس ), consideration is given to what predominates and to the strength of the motive. If the motive of self-interest predominates, the act falls short and is nearer to punishment, although its punishment is lighter than that of an act done wholly for something other than God. If the motive of drawing near to God predominates, the reward is reduced in proportion to the self-interested motive. If the two are equal, they oppose and cancel one another: the act counts neither for nor against its doer. He then says: “The community’s agreement that someone who sets out on pilgrimage while conducting trade has a valid pilgrimage and receives reward for it bears witness to this.” He continues: “The correct position is to say that whenever pilgrimage is the original impulse and the commercial aim merely follows it, the journey itself is not without reward.” He then applies this consideration to fighting in God’s path in relation to booty: one considers the predominant motive and the sincerity of purpose. Likewise, when fasting is undertaken for a regimen and for reward, one considers the predominant motive. [B135] I say: this rule applies to all dealings, movements and rests, crafts and other means of livelihood. What is free of self-interested aims is accepted; what is wholly directed to such aims is rejected; and in a mixed act one considers what predominates, as already explained. The master of masters, my lord Abū al-Ḥasan al-Shādhilī, God be pleased with him, stated another rule, subtler than this: “When God honours a servant in his movements and rests, He sets servanthood to God ( العبودية لله ) before him and conceals his own interests from him. He moves within his servanthood while his interests remain hidden, although what has been decreed for him continues to run its course. He does not attend to those interests, for they are apart from him. When God abases a servant in his movements and rests, He sets the servant’s own interests before him and conceals his servanthood. He moves within his desires, while servanthood to God is apart from him, although something of it may occur outwardly.” He says: “This is one aspect of sainthood and abasement. As for the greatest veracity ( الصديقية العظمى ) and the greater sainthood ( الولاية الكبرى ), personal interests and duties are all alike for the person of insight, because he is through God in what he takes and leaves.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q2-198-199-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-198-199-s3","r":"q2-198-199","title":"No final limit to increase in knowledge of God","text":"The servant cannot dispense with seeking increase, even though he attain the furthest extremity of perfection. To be content with one’s portion from God is deprivation; to believe one has reached the end is deficiency. There is therefore no blame upon you, gnostics, for seeking bounty from your Lord: increase in your certainty and ascent in your inward realities. The Real’s perfections have no end, and the mysteries of the Essence cannot be encompassed. He says: “They do not encompass Him in knowledge” [20:110]. God is the guardian of success. The Real then mentions standing at ʿArafa and returning to Muzdalifa and the Sacred Monument: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:198b–199 فَإِذَا أَفَضْتُمْ مِنْ عَرَفَاتٍ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ عِنْدَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ وَاذْكُرُوهُ كَمَا هَدَاكُمْ وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ لَمِنَ الضَّالِّينَ ۝ ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ النَّاسُ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللَّهَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ When you pour forth from ʿArafāt, remember God at the Sacred Monument. Remember Him because He has guided you, although before that you were among those astray. Then pour forth from where the people pour forth, and ask God’s forgiveness. God is Forgiving, Merciful.","anchor":"en-q2-198-199-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-198-199-s4","r":"q2-198-199","title":"Pouring forth, ʿArafāt and the reason for remembrance","text":"I say: afaḍtum ( أفضتم ) means “you moved forth.” The original meaning of ifāḍa is a forceful outpouring, from water’s gushing strongly; it was then used, by way of intensification, for movement forth generally. ʿArafāt permits both full declension and its absence ( الصرف وعدمه ), like Adhriʿāt . It was named ʿArafāt because Abraham the Friend said to Gabriel, when Gabriel taught him the rites, “I have understood” ( ʿaraftu ), or because Adam recognized Eve there. The kāf in “as He guided you” ( كما هداكم ) gives the reason ( تعليلية ), and mā is infinitival ( مصدرية ): remember Him on account of His guidance of you. In in “although you were” ( إن كنتم ) is the lightened form ( مخففة ), and the lām distinguishes it [from the negative]. “Or more intense” [in 2:200] qualifies an omitted verbal noun ( نعت لمصدر محذوف ): “or a remembrance more intense,” and so forth. [B136]","anchor":"en-q2-198-199-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-198-199-s5","r":"q2-198-199","title":"Standing with the people and remembering God","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when you have stood at ʿArafa and poured forth from it, descend to Muzdalifa and spend the night there. After praying the dawn prayer while it is still dark, stand at the Sacred Monument, a mountain at the end of Muzdalifa. Remember God there by declaring His unity, magnifying Him and reciting the pilgrimage response ( التهليل والتكبير والتلبية ), until daylight spreads. This is what the Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, did. Remember Him because He has guided you to the landmarks of His religion, the rites of His pilgrimage and its other observances; or remember Him with a good remembrance, just as He guided you with a good guidance. Before this guidance you were among those astray. Quraysh used not to stand with the people, considering themselves above them, but stood at Muzdalifa. The Real commanded them to stand with the people: then pour forth, company of Quraysh, from where the people pour forth—completing [the rites] with them and departing from where they depart. Ask God’s forgiveness for your alteration of Abraham’s and Ishmael’s rites. God is Forgiving towards you, Merciful to you, if you repent, return and follow your Messenger.","anchor":"en-q2-198-199-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-200-202","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray 2:200–202","anchor":"unit-q2-200-202"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-1","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"فَإِذا قَضَيْتُمْ مَناسِكَكُمْ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَذِكْرِكُمْ آباءَكُمْ أَوْ أَشَدَّ ذِكْراً ...","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-2","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"قلت: (أفضتُم) : دفعتم، وأصل الإفاضة: الدفع بقوة، من فاض الماء إذا نبَع بقوة، ثم استُعمل في مطلق الاندفاع على سبيل المبالغة. و (عرفات) فيها الصرف وعدمه، كأذرعات. وسمى عرفات لقول إبراهيم الخليل عليه السلام لجبريل حين علَّمه المناسك: قد عرفتُ. أو لمعرفة آدم حواءَ فيها. والكاف في (كما هداكم) تعليلية، و (ما) مصدرية، أي: واذكروه لأجل هدايته لكم. و (إن كنتم) مخففة، واللام فارقة، وقوله: (أو أشد) نعت لمصدر محذوف، أي: أو ذكراً أشد ... الخ.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-3","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فإذا وقفتم بعرفة، وأفضتم منها، فانزلوا المزدلفة وبيِتُوا بها، فإذا صليتم الصبح بغلس فقفوا عند الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرامِ، وهو جبل في آخر المزدلفة، واذكروا الله عنده بالتهليل والتكبير والتلبية إلى الإسفار، هكذا فعل الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، وَاذْكُرُوهُ لأجل ما هداكم إليه من معالم دينه ومناسك حجه، وغير ذلك من شعائر الدين، أو فاذكروه ذكرا حسنا كما هداكم هداية حسنة، وقد كنتم من قبل هذه الهداية لَمِنَ الضَّالِّينَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-4","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"وكانت قريش لا تقف مع الناس ترفعاً عليهم، بل تقف بالمزدلفة، فأمرهم الحق جلّ جلاله بالوقوف مع الناس، فقال لهم: ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا يا معشر قريش مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفاضَ النَّاسُ بأن تَقْضُوا معهم، وتفيضوا من حيث أفاضوا، وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللَّهَ في تغييركم مناسك إبراهيم وإسماعيل- عليهما السلام- إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ لكم، رَحِيمٌ بكم إن تبتم ورجعتم واتبعتم رسولكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-6","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"فَإِذا قَضَيْتُمْ مَناسِكَكُمْ وفرغتم من حجكم فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ ذكراً كثيراً كَذِكْرِكُمْ آباءَكُمْ أو ذكراً أَشَدَّ ذِكْراً منهم، حيث كنتم تَذْكُرونهم عند فراغ حجكم بالمفاخَرة، وكانوا إذا فرغوا من حجهم وقَفُوا بِمنى، بين المسجد والجبل، فيذكرون مفاخر آبائهم، ومحاسن أيامهم، فأُمِرُوا أن","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-7","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"يُبدلوا ذلك بذكر الله، وذكر إحسانه إليهم، وشكر ما أسداه إليهم من مفاخر الدنيا والآخرة، إن آمنوا واتبعوا رسوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-8","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"الإشارة: إذا وقَفَت القلوبُ على جَبل عرفة المعارف، وتمكنت من شهود جمال معاني تلك الزخارف، حتى صارت تلك المعاني هي روحَها وسرَّها، وإليها مآلها ومسيرُها، أُمرتْ بالنزول إلى أرض العبودية، والقيام بوظائف الربوبية، شكراً لما هداها إليه من معالم التحقيق، وما أبان لها من منار الطريق، وإن كانت من قبله لمن الضالين عن الوصول إلى رب العالمين. ثم يؤمرون بمخالطة الناس بأشباحهم، وانفرادهم عنهم بأرواحهم. أشباحُهم مع الخلق تسعى، وأرواحهم في الملكوت ترعى، فإذا وقع منهم ميل أو سكون إلى حِسّ فليستغفروا الله إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ. ثم يقال لهم: فإذا قضيتم مناسككم، بأن جمعتم بين مشاهدة الربوبية في باطنكم، والقيام بوظائف العبودية في ظاهركم، فاذكروا الله على كل شيء، وعند كل شيء، وقبل كل شيء، وبعد كل شيء، حتى لا يبقى من الأثر شيء، كما كنتم تذكرون آباءكم وأبناءكم، في حال غفلتكم، بل أشد ذكراً وأعظم وأتم، والله ذو الفضل العظيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-9","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"ثم بين الحق تعالى مقاصد الناس، وهممهم في طلبهم وسعيهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-10","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"... فَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَقُولُ رَبَّنا آتِنا فِي الدُّنْيا وَما لَهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلاقٍ (200) وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَقُولُ رَبَّنا آتِنا فِي الدُّنْيا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنا عَذابَ النَّارِ (201) أُولئِكَ لَهُمْ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا كَسَبُوا وَاللَّهُ سَرِيعُ الْحِسابِ (202)","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-11","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في بيان مقاصد الناس وهممهم في طلبهم في الحج وغيره: فَمِنَ النَّاسِ من قصرت نيته وانحطت همته، يَقُولُ رَبَّنا آتِنا فِي الدُّنْيا ما تشتهيه نفوسنا من حظوظها وشهواتها، وليس له فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلاقٍ أي: نصيب، لأنه عجَّل نصيبه في الدنيا. «إن الله يرزق العبدَ على قدر نيته» وَمِنْهُمْ من أراد كرامة الدنيا وشرف الآخرة يَقُولُ رَبَّنا آتِنا فِي الدُّنْيا حالة حَسَنَةً كالمعرفة، والعافية، والمال الحلال، والزوجة الحسنة، وجميع أنواع الجمال، وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً كالنظرة، والحُور العين، والقصور، وجميع أنواع النعيم، وَقِنا عَذابَ النَّارِ بالعفو والمغفرة، وقال سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه-: (الحسنة في الدنيا: المرأة الصالحة، وفي الآخرة: الحَوْرَاء. وعذاب النار في الدنيا: المرأة السوء) وقال الحسن: (الحسنة في الدنيا: العلم والعبادة، وفي الآخرة: الجنة) . وَقِنا عَذابَ النَّارِ: احفظنا من الشهوات والذنوب المؤدية إلى النار، وهذه كلها أمثلة للحالة الحسنة.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-12","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"أُولئِكَ الذين طلبوا خيرَ الدارَيْن لَهُمْ نَصِيبٌ وحظٍّ من الجزاء الوافر من أجلْ ما كسبوا من الأعمال الصالحات، وَاللَّهُ سَرِيعُ الْحِسابِ يحاسب عباده على كثرتهم، وكثرة أعمالهم، في مقدار لَمْحة. قيل لعليّ رضي الله عنه: كيف يُحاسب اللهُ عباده في ساعة واحدة؟ فقال: كما يرزقهم في ساعة واحدة. هـ. أو يوشك أن يقيم القيامة ويحاسب عباده؛ فبادِرُوا إلى اغتنام الطاعات، واكتساب الحسنات، قبل هجوم الممات.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-13","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"الإشارة: الناس ثلاثة: صاحب همة دَنِيَّة، وذو همة متوسطة، وصاحب همة عالية، أما صاحب الهمة الدنية فهو الذي أنزل همته على الدنيا الدنية، وأكبَّ على جمع حطامها الفانية، فقلبُ هذا خالٍ من حب الحبيب، فما له في الآخرة من نصيب. وأما صاحب الهمة المتوسطة فهو الذي طلب سلامة الدارين، وصلاح الحالين، قد اشتغل في هذه الدار بما ينفعه في دار القرار، ولم ينسَ نصيبه من الدنيا لِيقْضِي ما له فيها من الأوطار، فهذا له في الدنيا حسنة، وهي الكفاية والغنى، وفي الآخرة حسنة، وهي النعمة والسرور والهنا.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-14","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"وأما صاحب الهمة العالية فهو الذي رفع همته عن الكونَيْن، وأغمض طَرْفَه عن الالتفات إلى الدارين، بل علَّق همته بمولاه، ولم يقنع بشيء سواه، قد ولّى عن هذه الدار مُغضياً، وأعرض عنها مُولياً، ولم يشغله عن الله شيء، يقول بلسان المقال إظهارا لعبوديته للكبير المتعال: رَبَّنا آتِنا فِي الدُّنْيا حَسَنَةً وهي النظرة والشهود، ورضا الملك الودود، وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وهي اللحوق بأهل الرفيق الأعلى، من المقربين والأنبياء، في حضرة الشهود المؤبد فِي مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ مَلِيكٍ مُقْتَدِرٍ. أتحفَنَا الله من ذلك بحظٍّ وافر، بمنِّه وكرمه، نحن وأحباءَنا أجمعين، آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-200-202-15","r":"q2-200-202","title":"2:200–202 · Remembrance after the rites and the aspirations of those who pray","text":"ثم تمّم الحق تعالى ما بقي من مناسك الحج وهى رمى الجمار أيام منى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-200-202-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-200-202-s1","r":"q2-200-202","title":"Replacing ancestral boasting with remembrance","text":"When you have completed your rites and finished your pilgrimage, remember God abundantly, as you remember your fathers, or with a remembrance more intense than your remembrance of them, when you used to boast of them after completing pilgrimage. On finishing their pilgrimage, they would stand at Minā between the mosque and the mountain, recounting their fathers’ boasts and the splendours of their former days. They were commanded to replace this with remembrance of God, His beneficence towards them, and gratitude for the distinctions He had bestowed upon them in this world and the Hereafter, should they believe and follow His Messenger, God bless him and grant him peace.","anchor":"en-q2-200-202-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-200-202-s2","r":"q2-200-202","title":"Returning from witnessing to servanthood","text":"When hearts stand on the mountain of the ʿArafa of gnoses, and become established in witnessing the beauty of the meanings within those adornments, until those meanings become their spirit and secret—their destination and the goal of their journey—they are commanded to descend to the ground of servanthood and undertake the duties owed to Lordship ( وظائف الربوبية ). This is gratitude for the landmarks of realization to which He has guided them and the beacons of the Path He has disclosed, although before this they were among those who had strayed from arrival at the Lord of the worlds. They are then commanded to mingle with people in their bodily forms while remaining apart in their spirits. Their forms move among created beings; their spirits pasture in the spiritual kingdom ( الملكوت ). If inclination towards, or repose in, sensory appearance occurs, let them ask God’s forgiveness: God is Forgiving, Merciful. They are then told: when you have completed your rites—uniting inward witnessing of Lordship with outward fulfilment of servanthood’s duties—remember God over everything, at everything, before everything and after everything, until no trace remains. Remember Him as you used to remember your fathers and children during your heedlessness, but with remembrance more intense, greater and more complete. God is possessed of immense bounty. The Real then explains people’s purposes and aspirations in what they seek and strive for: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:200b–202 فَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَقُولُ رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَمَا لَهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلَاقٍ ۝ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَقُولُ رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ ۝ أُولَئِكَ لَهُمْ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا كَسَبُوا وَاللَّهُ سَرِيعُ الْحِسَابِ Among people is one who says, “Our Lord, give us in this world”; he has no share in the Hereafter. Among them is one who says, “Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.” Those will have a share from what they have earned. God is swift in reckoning.","anchor":"en-q2-200-202-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-200-202-s3","r":"q2-200-202","title":"Seeking the good of both abodes","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says, explaining people’s purposes and aspirations in what they seek during pilgrimage and otherwise: among people is one whose intention is narrow and whose aspiration is low, who says, “Our Lord, give us in this world whatever our lower selves desire of their interests and appetites.” He has no share in the Hereafter, for his share has been hastened to him in this world. “God provides for a servant in proportion to his intention.” Among them is one who desires this world’s honour and the Hereafter’s nobility, who says, “Our Lord, give us a good condition in this world”: gnosis, well-being, lawful wealth, a good wife and every kind of beauty. “And good in the Hereafter”: the vision, the wide-eyed maidens, palaces and every kind of bliss. “Protect us from the punishment of the Fire” through pardon and forgiveness. Our master ʿAlī, God ennoble his face, said: “Good in this world is the righteous woman; in the Hereafter, the fair-eyed maiden. The punishment of fire in this world is the bad woman.” Al-Ḥasan said: “Good in this world is knowledge and worship; in the Hereafter, the Garden.” “Protect us from the punishment of the Fire” means preserve us from the desires and sins that lead to it. All these are examples of a good condition. [B137] Those who sought the good of both abodes will have a portion and share of abundant recompense because of the righteous works they earned. God is swift in reckoning: despite the multitude of His servants and their deeds, He reckons with them in the space of a glance. ʿAlī, God be pleased with him, was asked: “How does God reckon with His servants in a single hour?” He replied: “Just as He provides for them in a single hour.” End of quotation. Or [the phrase means] that He is about to establish the Resurrection and reckon with His servants. Hasten, therefore, to seize opportunities for obedience and acquire good deeds before death’s sudden onset.","anchor":"en-q2-200-202-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-200-202-s4","r":"q2-200-202","title":"Low, intermediate and high aspiration","text":"People are of three kinds: one with low aspiration, one with intermediate aspiration, and one with high aspiration ( الهمة ). The person of low aspiration has set his aim upon the lowly world and devoted himself to collecting its perishing debris. His heart is empty of love for the Beloved; he has no share in the Hereafter. The person of intermediate aspiration seeks safety in both abodes and soundness in both conditions. In this abode he occupies himself with what will benefit him in the abode of permanence. He has not forgotten his share of this world, so that he may accomplish his needs within it. His good in this world is sufficiency and freedom from want; his good in the Hereafter is blessing, happiness and delight. The person of high aspiration raises his aim above the two worlds and closes his eyes to turning towards either abode. He attaches his aspiration to his Master and is satisfied with nothing other than Him. He turns from this abode with lowered gaze, departs from it and turns away; nothing distracts him from God. With the tongue of utterance, manifesting his servanthood to the Great, the Exalted, he says: “Our Lord, give us good in this world”—vision and witnessing, and the approval of the Loving King—“and good in the Hereafter”: joining the company of the Highest Companion, the near ones and the prophets, in the presence of everlasting witnessing, “in a seat of truthfulness, in the presence of an all-powerful King” [54:55]. May God, by His generosity and bounty, bestow an abundant share of this upon us and all our loved ones. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-200-202-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-200-202-s5","r":"q2-200-202","title":"","text":"The Real then completes the remaining pilgrimage rites: casting the pebbles during the days at Minā.","anchor":"en-q2-200-202-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-203","r":"q2-203","title":"2:203 · The numbered days and the freedom to depart or remain","text":"2:203 · The numbered days and the freedom to depart or remain 2:203","anchor":"unit-q2-203"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-203-1","r":"q2-203","title":"2:203 · The numbered days and the freedom to depart or remain","text":"وَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ فِي أَيَّامٍ مَعْدُوداتٍ فَمَنْ تَعَجَّلَ فِي يَوْمَيْنِ فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ وَمَنْ تَأَخَّرَ فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ لِمَنِ اتَّقى وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ إِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُونَ (203)","anchor":"ar-q2-203-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-203-2","r":"q2-203","title":"2:203 · The numbered days and the freedom to depart or remain","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ فِي أَيَّامٍ مَعْدُوداتٍ وهي ثاني النَّحْر وثالثُه ورابعُه، وهي أيام التشريق وأيام منى، وأما الأيام المعلومات فهي يوم النحر وثانِيه وثالثُه. والمراد بالذِكْر: التكبيرُ عند الرمي، وذبحِ القَرَابين، وخَلْفَ الصلواتِ الخمس، وغير ذلك، فَمَنْ تَعَجَّلَ فِي يَوْمَيْنِ بحيث رمَى ثانيَ النحر وثالثه، ورجَع، فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ وَمَنْ تَأَخَّرَ لرمى رابع النحر، وهو ثالث أيام منى، فَلا إِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ، والقصد بنفي الإثم:","anchor":"ar-q2-203-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-203-3","r":"q2-203","title":"2:203 · The numbered days and the freedom to depart or remain","text":"التخيير والرد على الجاهلية، فإنَّ منهم مَن أَثم المتعجل، ومنهم من أثم المتأخر. هذا كله لِمَنِ اتَّقى الله في حجه، فَلَمْ يَرْفُثْ، وَلَمْ يَفْسُقْ، فإنه يخرج من ذُنُوبِه كَيَوْمِ وَلَدَتْهُ أمه، كما قال الصادق المصدوق، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ في جميع أموركم، فإنه ذكرٌ وشرفٌ لكم، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ إِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُونَ فتجازَوْن على ما أسلفتم من خير أو شر.","anchor":"ar-q2-203-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-203-4","r":"q2-203","title":"2:203 · The numbered days and the freedom to depart or remain","text":"الإشارة: الأيام المعدودات هي أيام الدنيا فإنها قلائل معدودة، وهي كلها كيوم واحد، وأيام البرزخ يومٌ ثانٍ، وأيام البعث وما بعده يوم ثالث، فمن تعجل في يومين، بحيث طوى في نظره أيام الدنيا وأيام البرزخ، وسكن بقلبه في يوم القيامة فلا إثم عليه، وهذا هو صاحب الهمة المتوسطة، ومن تأخر حتى زَهد فى الأيام الثلاثة، وعلق همته بمولاه، ولم يلتفت إلى ما سواه، فلا إثم عليه في ذلك التأخر، إن اتقى شهود السوى، وعلق همته بمحبة المولى، ثم حضّ سبحانه على هذه التقوى فقال: (واتقوا الله) فلا تشهدوا معه سواه، (واعلموا أنكم إليه تحشرون) فترَوْا ما فاز به المتقون.","anchor":"ar-q2-203-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-203-5","r":"q2-203","title":"2:203 · The numbered days and the freedom to depart or remain","text":"ولمّا أمر الحق سبحانه عباده بالتقوى ذكر من لم يرفع بذلك رأسا واتبع هواه، ومن امتثل أمره وباع نفسه لله فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-203-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-203-s1","r":"q2-203","title":"The days at Minā","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember God during numbered days. These are the second, third and fourth days counting from the Day of Sacrifice: the days of tashrīq , the days at Minā. The “known days” [22:28], by contrast, are the Day of Sacrifice and the second and third days counting from it. Remembrance here means magnifying God when casting the pebbles, slaughtering sacrificial offerings, after the five prayers and at other times. Whoever hastens to leave in two days, casting on the second and third days counting from the Day of Sacrifice and returning, incurs no sin. Whoever remains to cast on the fourth day counting from the sacrifice, which is the third day at Minā, likewise incurs no sin. Negating sin here intends to establish a choice and refute the people of the Age of Ignorance: some counted early departure sinful, while others counted remaining sinful. All this is for one who fears God during pilgrimage, engaging neither in sexual misconduct nor transgression. He leaves his sins as on the day his mother bore him, as the truthful and confirmed Messenger said. Fear God in all your affairs: it is remembrance and honour for you. Know that to Him you will be gathered and recompensed for whatever good or evil you sent before you. [B138]","anchor":"en-q2-203-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-203-s2","r":"q2-203","title":"The three days of the world, the interval and resurrection","text":"The numbered days are the days of this world, few and numbered. All of them are as one day; the days of the intermediate realm ( البرزخ ) are a second day; the days of resurrection and what follows it are a third. Whoever hastens in two days—folding away in his sight the days of this world and of the intermediate realm, and dwelling in his heart in the Day of Resurrection—incurs no sin. This is the person of intermediate aspiration. Whoever remains beyond them, renouncing all three days, attaching his aspiration to his Master and turning to nothing other than Him, incurs no sin in that remaining, provided he guards against witnessing anything other and attaches his aspiration to love of the Master. He then urges this Godfearingness: “Fear God”—witness no other with Him—“and know that to Him you will be gathered.” You will then see what the Godfearing have won.","anchor":"en-q2-203-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-203-s3","r":"q2-203","title":"","text":"When the Real, exalted is He, commanded His servants to fear Him, He mentioned one who paid it no heed but followed his desire, and one who obeyed His command and sold himself to God.","anchor":"en-q2-203-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-204-207","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God 2:204–207","anchor":"unit-q2-204-207"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-1","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُعْجِبُكَ قَوْلُهُ فِي الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا وَيُشْهِدُ اللَّهَ عَلى ما فِي قَلْبِهِ وَهُوَ أَلَدُّ الْخِصامِ (204) وَإِذا تَوَلَّى سَعى فِي الْأَرْضِ لِيُفْسِدَ فِيها وَيُهْلِكَ الْحَرْثَ وَالنَّسْلَ وَاللَّهُ لا يُحِبُّ الْفَسادَ (205) وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُ اتَّقِ اللَّهَ أَخَذَتْهُ الْعِزَّةُ بِالْإِثْمِ فَحَسْبُهُ جَهَنَّمُ وَلَبِئْسَ الْمِهادُ (206) وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَشْرِي نَفْسَهُ ابْتِغاءَ مَرْضاتِ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ رَؤُفٌ بِالْعِبادِ (207)","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-2","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"قلت: نزلت الآية في الأخنَسْ بن شريق الثقفي وصُهيب بن سنان الرومي، أما الأخنس فكان رجلاً حسن المنظر، حُلُو المنطق، كان يوالي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ويدَّعي الإسلام، ثم ارتد، ومرَّ على زرع وحُمر للمسلمين فقتلها وأفسد الزرع، قال ابن عطية: ولم يثبت أنه أسلم. قلت: بل ذكره في القاموس من الصحابة، فانظره، ولعله تاب بعد نزول الآية. وأما صهيب الرومي فأخذه المشركون وعذبوه ليرتد، فقال لهم: إني شيخ كبير لا أنفعكم إن كنت معكم، ولا أضركم إن كنت عليكم، فخلّوني وما أنا عليه، وخذوا مالي، فقبلوه منه، وأتى المدينة فلما رآه صلّى الله عليه وسلم قال له: «رَبِحْتَ يا أَبَا يَحْيى» .","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-3","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"وقيل: نزلت في المنافقين ومَنْ نحَا نحوهم، وفيمن باع نفسه لله في الجهاد وتغيير المنكر من المسلمين. و (في الحياة الدنيا) يتعلق بالقول، و (ألد الخصام) شديده، وفي الحديث: «أبْغَضُ الرِّجالِ إلى اللهِ الألدُّ الخَصِم» .","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-4","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"والخِصام: مصدر، أو جمع خصيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-5","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمِنَ النَّاسِ قوم حلو اللسان خرَاب الجَنَان، إذا تكلم في شأن الدنيا يُعْجِبُكَ قَوْلُهُ فيها لرونقه وفصاحته، وَيُشْهِدُ اللَّهَ أي: يحلف على أنه موافق لقلبه، وأن ظاهره موافق لباطنه، وهو شديد الخصومة والعداوة للمسلمين، أو أشد الخصوم، وَإِذا تَوَلَّى أي: أدبر وانصرف عنك، سَعى فِي الْأَرْضِ أي: مشى فيها بنية الإفساد لِيُفْسِدَ فِيها وَيُهْلِكَ الْحَرْثَ وَالنَّسْلَ كما فعل الأخنَسْ، أو كما فعله أهل الظلم، فيَحْبِسُ الله القَطْر، فَيَهْلِكَ الحرثُ والنسل بشؤم معاصيهم، وَاللَّهُ لا يُحِبُّ الْفَسادَ أي: لا يرتضيه، فاحذروا غضبه. وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُ اتَّقِ اللَّهَ وارجع عما أنت عليه من الفساد أَخَذَتْهُ الْعِزَّةُ أي: حملته الحمية والأنفة بسبب الإثم الذي ارتكبه، فلا ينزجر عن غَيِّه. أو حملَتْه الحمية على الإثم الذي يُؤمَر باتقائه. فَحَسْبُهُ جَهَنَّمُ أي: كَفَته عذاباً وعقاباً، وهي عَلَمٌ لدار العقاب، كالنار، وَلَبِئْسَ الْمِهادُ هي، أي: بئس الفراش الذي مهَّده لنفسه.","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-6","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"ونزل في مقابله، وهو صهيب، أو كل من بذل نفسه لله: وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَشْرِي نَفْسَهُ أي: يبيعُها ويبذلها لله في الجهاد وغيره، ابْتِغاءَ مَرْضاتِ اللَّهِ والوصول إلى حضرته وَاللَّهُ رَؤُفٌ بِالْعِبادِ الذين يفعلون مثل هذا، فيدرأ عنهم المضَارّ، ويجلبُ لهم المَسَار أينما حَلُّوا من الدارين.","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-7","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"الإشارة: الناس على قسمين: قسم زَيّنُوا ظواهرهم وخرَّبوا بواطنهم، ظاهرهم جميل وباطنُهم قبيح، إذا تكلموا في الدنيا أو في الحس، أعجبَك قولهم، وراقك منظرُهم، وإذا تكلموا في الآخرة، أو في المعنى، أخذتهم الحبْسةُ والدهشة. وفي بعض الكتب المنزلة: «إنَّ مِنْ عِبَاد الله قوماً ألْسنَتُهُم أحْلَى منَ العَسَلِ، وَقُلُوبُهُمْ أمرّ مِنْ الصَّبْرِ، يَلْبَسُونَ للنَّاس جُلُودَ الضَّأنِ مِن اللِّينِ، يَجْتَرُّون الدُّنْيَا بالدين، يَقُولُ الله تعالى: أبِي يَغْتَرُّونَ، وعليَّ يَجْترِئُون؟ حَلَفتْ لأُسلطنَّ عليهمْ فتْنةٌ تَدَعُ الْحَليم مِنْهُمْ حَيْرَانَ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-8","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"وقوله (يلبسون ... ) الخ. كناية عن إظهار اللين والسهول ليخدع ويغر الناس ليتوصل إلى حظ نفسه من الدنيا، ومع ذلك يدعي موافقة ظاهره لباطنه، وهو شديد الخصومة لأهل الله، وإذا تولى عنك اشتغل بالمعاصي والذنوب، ليُفسد في الأرض، ويهلك الحرث والنسل بشؤم معاصيه، وإذا ذُكِّر: أنِفَ واستكبر، وأخذته حمية الجاهلية، فحسبُه البُعد في نار القطيعة.","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-9","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"والقسم الثاني: قوم زَيَّنوا بواطنهم وخربوا ظواهرهم، عمّروا قلوبهم بمحبة الله، وبذلوا أنفسهم في مرضات الله، قلوبهم في أعلى عليين، وأشباحهم في أسفل سافلين، فأولئك المقربون مع النبيين والمرسلين. قال بعض العارفين:","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-10","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"كلما وضعت نفسك أرضاً أرضاً، سما قلبك سماء سماء، وكل ما نقص من حسك زاد في معناك. وفي الحديث:","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-11","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"«مَن تواضعَ دُون قَدْره رَفَعهُ الله فوقَ قَدْره» . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-204-207-12","r":"q2-204-207","title":"2:204–207 · Pleasing speech, destructive conduct and the self sold to God","text":"ثم دعا الحق، تعالى عباده، إلى التوغل فى الإسلام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-204-207-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-204-207-s1","r":"q2-204-207","title":"Al-Akhnas and Ṣuhayb","text":"I say: the verses were revealed concerning al-Akhnas ibn Sharīq al-Thaqafī and Ṣuhayb ibn Sinān al-Rūmī. Al-Akhnas was a man of handsome appearance and sweet speech. He professed friendship towards God’s Messenger, God bless him and grant him peace, and claimed Islam. He then apostatized and, passing Muslim crops and donkeys, killed the animals and ruined the crops. Ibn ʿAṭiyya says: “It has not been established that he embraced Islam.” I say: rather, the Qāmūs lists him among the Companions; consult it. Perhaps he repented after the verse’s revelation. As for Ṣuhayb al-Rūmī, the associators seized and tortured him to make him turn back. He told them: “I am an old man: I will not benefit you if I am with you or harm you if I am against you. Leave me and the faith I follow, and take my wealth.” They accepted. He came to Medina, and when the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, saw him, he said: “Your bargain has prospered, Abū Yaḥyā!” [B139] It is also said that the verses concern the hypocrites and those who follow their way, and Muslims who sell themselves to God in fighting in His path and changing what is wrong. “In worldly life” is attached to “speech.” “Fiercest in disputation” ( ألد الخصام ) means intensely contentious. The Tradition says: “The man most hated by God is the stubborn, contentious adversary.” Khiṣām is either a verbal noun ( مصدر ) or the plural of khaṣīm , an adversary.","anchor":"en-q2-204-207-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-204-207-s2","r":"q2-204-207","title":"Eloquence without inward soundness","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: among people are those whose tongues are sweet and whose hearts are ruined. When one speaks of worldly affairs, his speech pleases you through its polish and eloquence. He calls God to witness: he swears that it agrees with his heart and that his exterior agrees with his interior, although he is fiercely contentious and hostile towards Muslims—or the fiercest of adversaries. When he turns away, departing from you, he goes through the land intending corruption, to spread corruption in it and destroy crops and offspring, as al-Akhnas did; or as the unjust do, whereupon God withholds rain and crops and offspring perish through the ill consequence of their sins. God does not love corruption: He does not approve it. Beware of His wrath. When he is told, “Fear God and turn back from your corruption,” pride seizes him: indignation and disdain, because of the sin he has committed, prevent him from leaving his error. Or indignation drives him into the sin he is commanded to avoid. Hell suffices him as punishment and torment. Jahannam is a proper name ( عَلَم ) for the abode of punishment, like “the Fire.” What an evil resting place it is: an evil bed he has prepared for himself. Concerning his opposite—Ṣuhayb, or everyone who gives himself to God—it was revealed: among people is one who sells himself, offering himself to God in fighting in His path and otherwise, seeking God’s good pleasure and arrival in His presence. God is tender towards servants who act thus: He averts harms from them and brings them joys wherever they dwell in either abode.","anchor":"en-q2-204-207-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-204-207-s3","r":"q2-204-207","title":"Adorning the exterior or cultivating the heart","text":"People are of two kinds. One kind adorn their exteriors and ruin their interiors: outwardly beautiful, inwardly ugly. If they speak about the world or sensory appearances, their speech pleases you and their appearance delights you. If they speak of the Hereafter or inward meaning, they are seized by speechlessness and bewilderment. One of the revealed books says: “Among God’s servants are people whose tongues are sweeter than honey and whose hearts are more bitter than aloes. They dress before people in the softness of sheepskins and draw the world to themselves through religion. God Most High says: ‘Are they deceived about Me, and do they dare defy Me? I have sworn to set over them a trial that will leave even their forbearing ones bewildered.’” [B140] “Dress before people,” and the remainder, is an allusion ( كناية ) to displaying gentleness and easy manners in order to deceive and delude people and reach one’s own worldly interest. At the same time, such a person claims that his exterior agrees with his interior, although he is fiercely contentious towards God’s folk. When he turns away from you, he occupies himself with sins and disobedience, spreading corruption in the earth and destroying crops and offspring through his sins’ ill consequence. When reminded, he disdains and grows proud, seized by the indignation of ignorance. Distance in the fire of separation suffices him. The second kind adorn their interiors and lay their exteriors waste. They cultivate their hearts with God’s love and give themselves for His good pleasure. Their hearts are in the highest heights, their bodily forms in the lowest depths. They are the ones brought near, with the prophets and messengers. A gnostic said: “The more you lower yourself, earth upon earth, the higher your heart rises, heaven upon heaven. Whatever diminishes from your sensory appearance increases in your inward meaning.” The Tradition says: “Whoever humbles himself below his rank, God raises above his rank.” And success is through God. [B141]","anchor":"en-q2-204-207-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-204-207-s4","r":"q2-204-207","title":"","text":"The Real then calls His servants to enter deeply into Islam.","anchor":"en-q2-204-207-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-208-209","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission 2:208–209","anchor":"unit-q2-208-209"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-208-209-1","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا ادْخُلُوا فِي السِّلْمِ كَافَّةً وَلا تَتَّبِعُوا خُطُواتِ الشَّيْطانِ إِنَّهُ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُبِينٌ (208) فَإِنْ زَلَلْتُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْكُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ فَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ (209)","anchor":"ar-q2-208-209-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-208-209-2","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"قلت: (السلم) ، بالفتح والكسر: هو الاستسلام والانقياد، ويبعد هنا تفسيره بالصُّلْح. و (كافة) : حال من الواو والسلم معاً، كقوله تعالى: فَأَتَتْ بِهِ قَوْمَها تَحْمِلُهُ.","anchor":"ar-q2-208-209-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-208-209-3","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلم من أهل الكتاب ادْخُلُوا فِي شرائع الإسلام كَافَّةً بحيث لا تهملوا شيئاً منها، ولا تلتفتوا إلى غيرها. نزلت في عبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه، حيث دخلوا فى الإسلام، وأرادوا أن يُعظّموا السبت، وتحرجوا من لحوم الإبل. أو في المنافقين حيث أسلموا في الظاهر، ونافقوا في الباطن، فقال لهم الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا في الظاهر، ادخلوا في الإسلام كَافَّةً ظاهراً وباطناً. أو في المسلمين يأمرهم بالتمسك بشرائع الإسلام كلها، والبحث عن أحكامها وأسرارها، وَلا تَتَّبِعُوا خُطُواتِ الشَّيْطانِ أي: طُرُقَه الدالة على التفريق والتفرق إِنَّهُ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُبِينٌ أي: بيّن العداوة.","anchor":"ar-q2-208-209-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-208-209-4","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"فَإِنْ زَلَلْتُمْ عن طريق الجادَّة ففرقتم بين أجزاء الشريعة، أو التفتُّم إلى غير شريعتكم، مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْكُمُ الآيات الْبَيِّناتُ الدالة على صحة الدين ونبوة محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم، فَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ أي: غالب لا يُعجزه عقابكم، حَكِيمٌ في إمهاله إلى وقت معلوم.","anchor":"ar-q2-208-209-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-208-209-5","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"الإشارة: أمر الحق جل جلاله جميع عباده بالصلح معه والاستسلام لأحكامه، بحيث لا يَصْدُر منهم نِزَاعٌ لأحكامه، ولا اعتراض على أفعاله، بل يَنظرون ما يبرز من عنصر القدرة، فيتلقونه بالرضى والتسليم، أو الصبر والتصبر، سواء ظهرت هذه الأفعال على أيدي الوسائط أو بلا وسائط، إذ لا فاعل سواه، وكلٍّ من عند الله، فإن","anchor":"ar-q2-208-209-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-208-209-6","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"زللتم واعترضتم، أو سخطتم، من بعد ما جاءتكم الآيات البينات الدالة على وحدانية الحق في ذاته وصفاته وأفعاله، فاعلموا أن الله عزيز حكيم، لا يعجزه عقوبتكم وإبعادكم، لكنه من حكمته يُمهل ولا يهمل، والله غالب على أمره، ومن تاب تاب الله عليه.","anchor":"ar-q2-208-209-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-208-209-7","r":"q2-208-209","title":"2:208–209 · Entering wholly into submission","text":"ثم ذكر وعيد من خالف أمره، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-208-209-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-208-209-s1","r":"q2-208-209","title":"Submission and completeness","text":"I say: salm or silm ( السَّلْم، السِّلْم ), with either vowel, means surrender and compliance. Interpreting it here as a peace settlement is remote. Kāffatan ( كافة ), “wholly,” is a circumstantial expression ( حال ) relating both to the subject pronoun and to “submission,” as in His saying, “She brought him to her people, carrying him” [19:27]. [B142]","anchor":"en-q2-208-209-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-208-209-s2","r":"q2-208-209","title":"Entering all the ordinances of Islam","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: you People of the Book who have believed in Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, enter all the ordinances of Islam, neglecting none and turning to nothing else. It was revealed concerning ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his companions, who entered Islam but wished to venerate the Sabbath and felt reluctance to eat camel meat. Or it concerns the hypocrites, who submitted outwardly but harboured hypocrisy inwardly. The Real tells them: you who believe outwardly, enter Islam altogether, outwardly and inwardly. Or it concerns Muslims, whom He commands to adhere to all Islam’s ordinances and investigate their rulings and mysteries. Do not follow Satan’s footsteps: his paths leading to dividing and being divided. He is a manifest enemy to you, whose hostility is plain. If you slip from the straight road, dividing the parts of the Sacred Law or turning towards another law, after clear signs have come to you establishing the religion’s truth and Muḥammad’s prophethood, know that God is Mighty—prevailing, not unable to punish you—and Wise in granting respite until an appointed time.","anchor":"en-q2-208-209-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-208-209-s3","r":"q2-208-209","title":"Making peace with God’s decrees","text":"The Real commands all His servants to make peace with Him and surrender to His decrees, so that no contention with His rulings or objection to His acts issues from them. Rather, they look at what emerges from the source of power ( عنصر القدرة ) and receive it with contentment and surrender ( الرضى والتسليم ), or patience and the effort to be patient ( الصبر والتصبر ), whether those acts appear through intermediaries or without intermediaries. There is no agent other than He; all is from God. If you slip and object, or become displeased, after clear signs have come to you indicating the Real’s oneness in His Essence, attributes and acts, know that God is Mighty, Wise. Punishing and distancing you do not defeat Him; in His wisdom, however, He grants respite without neglecting. God prevails in His purpose. Whoever repents, God turns towards in mercy.","anchor":"en-q2-208-209-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-208-209-s4","r":"q2-208-209","title":"","text":"He then mentions the threat against whoever opposes His command.","anchor":"en-q2-208-209-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-210","r":"q2-210","title":"2:210 · The coming of God and the return of all affairs","text":"2:210 · The coming of God and the return of all affairs 2:210","anchor":"unit-q2-210"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-210-1","r":"q2-210","title":"2:210 · The coming of God and the return of all affairs","text":"هَلْ يَنْظُرُونَ إِلاَّ أَنْ يَأْتِيَهُمُ اللَّهُ فِي ظُلَلٍ مِنَ الْغَمامِ وَالْمَلائِكَةُ وَقُضِيَ الْأَمْرُ وَإِلَى اللَّهِ تُرْجَعُ الْأُمُورُ (210)","anchor":"ar-q2-210-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-210-2","r":"q2-210","title":"2:210 · The coming of God and the return of all affairs","text":"قلت: (الظُّلَل) : جمع ظُلَّه، وهي ما أظلَّك من فوق، و (الغَمام) : السحاب الرقيق الأبيض.","anchor":"ar-q2-210-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-210-3","r":"q2-210","title":"2:210 · The coming of God and the return of all affairs","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ما ينتظر هؤلاء الممتنعون من الدخول في شرائع الإسلام- إلا أن تقوم الساعة، ويأتيهم الله للفصل بين عباده فِي ظُلَلٍ مِنَ الْغَمامِ، بأن يتجلّى لعباده على ما يليق بجلاله إذ تجليات الحق لا تنحصر. وتأتيهم الْمَلائِكَةُ تحيط بهم وَقُضِيَ الْأَمْرُ بعذابهم، وَإِلَى اللَّهِ تُرْجَعُ الْأُمُورُ كلها، فهو المتصرف وحده. وقد ذكر المنذري حديث هذا التجلّي بطوله، وذكر فيه النزول والفصل بين عباده، والمرور على الصراط، والناس في أنوار إيمانهم. وذكره الفاسي في الحاشية بتمامه. ومن كَحل عين بصيرته بإثمد التوحيد الخاص(1)، لم يُسْتَصْعَبْ عليه فَهْمُ هذا الحديث وأمثاله لسعة دائرة معرفته. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-210-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-210-4","r":"q2-210","title":"2:210 · The coming of God and the return of all affairs","text":"الإشارة: في الآية تهديدٌ لأهل الحجاب الذين لم يتحققوا بالصلح مع الله، بل هم يخاصمون الله في مظاهر خلقه، ويعترضون على الله في قضائه وحكمه، فقال لهم الحق جلّ جلاله: هل ينتظر هؤلاء المنكرون عليَّ في أفعالي، المعترضون عليَّ في حكمي وإبرامي- إلا أن أتعرف لهم فِي ظُلَلٍ مِّنَ الْغَمَامِ، وهو سحب الآثار، فإذا أنكروني أخذتهم الملائكةُ، وقضي الأمر بهلاكهم، وإِلى الله تُرجع الأمورُ كلها، فليلتزم العبد الأدب مع مولاه، وليُسلم الأمور كلها إلى الله، إذ لا موجود سواه(2) ، فما برز من العباد: كله من الله، فمن اشتغل بعتابهم فاته الأدب مع الله، إلا ما أمرت به الشريعة، فليكن في ذلك كالعبد يُؤدب ابنَ سيده يده تؤدب وقلبه يعظم، والله تعالى أعلم وأرحم.","anchor":"ar-q2-210-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-210-5","r":"q2-210","title":"2:210 · The coming of God and the return of all affairs","text":"ثم هدّد بنى إسرائيل على عدم دخولهم فى الإسلام، أو على عدم تمسكهم بشرائعه كلها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-210-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-210-s1","r":"q2-210","title":"Canopies and cloud","text":"I say: ẓulal ( ظُلَل ) is the plural of ẓulla , whatever shades you from above. Ghamām ( الغمام ) is fine, white cloud.","anchor":"en-q2-210-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-210-s2","r":"q2-210","title":"Theophany and judgement","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those who refuse to enter Islam’s ordinances await only the Hour’s arising and God’s coming to decide between His servants in canopies of cloud. He discloses Himself to His servants in a manner befitting His majesty, for the Real’s self-disclosures ( تجليات الحق ) are not confined. The angels come and surround them; the matter is decided through their punishment. To God all affairs return: He alone disposes of them. Al-Mundhirī relates at length the Tradition concerning this self-disclosure, mentioning the descent, the judgement between His servants, and the crossing of the Bridge, with people in the lights of their faith. Al-Fāsī includes it in full in his gloss. One who has anointed the eye of inward sight with the antimony of the elect’s realization of unity ( التوحيد الخاص ) will not find this Tradition and its like difficult to understand, because of the breadth of his gnosis’s compass. And God Most High knows best. [B143]","anchor":"en-q2-210-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-210-s3","r":"q2-210","title":"Recognizing the Real without abandoning the Law","text":"The verse threatens the veiled who have not truly made peace with God, but dispute with Him in the manifestations of His creatures and object to His decree and judgement. The Real tells them: do those who deny Me in My acts and object to My ruling and determination await anything but My making Myself known to them in canopies of cloud—the clouds of created effects ( الآثار )? When they deny Me, the angels seize them and their destruction is decided. All affairs return to God. Let the servant therefore observe right comportment ( الأدب ) with his Master and entrust all affairs to God, for no existent is other than He. Whatever proceeds from servants is wholly from God. Whoever occupies himself with reproaching them misses right comportment with God—except in what the Sacred Law commands. There let him be like a servant disciplining his master’s son: his hand disciplines while his heart reveres. And God Most High knows best and is most merciful.","anchor":"en-q2-210-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-210-s4","r":"q2-210","title":"","text":"He then threatens the Children of Israel for not entering Islam, or for not adhering to all its ordinances.","anchor":"en-q2-210-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-211","r":"q2-211","title":"2:211 · Changing the blessing after receiving it","text":"2:211 · Changing the blessing after receiving it 2:211","anchor":"unit-q2-211"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-211-1","r":"q2-211","title":"2:211 · Changing the blessing after receiving it","text":"سَلْ بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ كَمْ آتَيْناهُمْ مِنْ آيَةٍ بَيِّنَةٍ وَمَنْ يُبَدِّلْ نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقابِ (211)","anchor":"ar-q2-211-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-211-2","r":"q2-211","title":"2:211 · Changing the blessing after receiving it","text":"قلت: (كم) خبرية، أو استفهامية، محلها نصب بفعل محذوف يُقدر مؤخراً للصدرية، أي: كم آياتنا آتيناهم، أو رفع بالابتداء، والعائد محذوف، أي: آتيناهموه.","anchor":"ar-q2-211-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-211-3","r":"q2-211","title":"2:211 · Changing the blessing after receiving it","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لرسوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أو لكل سامع: سَلْ بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ سؤال تقريع، وقل لهم: كَمْ آتَيْناهُمْ مِنْ آيَةٍ بَيِّنَةٍ أي: كثيراً ما آتيناهم من آية واضحة في شأنك، تدل على صدق رسالتك وعلو شأنك وفخامة أمرك، اعتناء بأمرهم، ونعمة على مَنْ أدرك زمانك منهم. ثم إنهم بدلوا نعمة الله كفرا، وجحدوا فكتموا تلك النعمة وكفروها، وَمَنْ يُبَدِّلْ نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ من بعد مجيئها إياه، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقابِ لمن كفر نعمه وجحد رسله، نعوذ بالله من السلب بعد العطاء، ومن كفران النعم، وحرمان الرضا.","anchor":"ar-q2-211-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-211-4","r":"q2-211","title":"2:211 · Changing the blessing after receiving it","text":"الإشارة: ما قيل لبني إسرائيل، يقال لمن تحقق بولاية وليّ من أولياء الله، ثم جحدها وكتمها، وحرّم نفسه بركة ذلك الولي، فمات على مرضه، فيقال له: وَمَنْ يُبَدِّلْ نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقابِ. وعقوبته: أن يلقى الله بقلب سقيم، فيُبعث مع عوام أهل اليمين، ويُحرم درجة المقربين، التي تلي درجة النبيين والمرسلين. عائذاً بالله من الحرمان، وشُؤمِ عاقبةِ الخذلان.","anchor":"ar-q2-211-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-211-5","r":"q2-211","title":"2:211 · Changing the blessing after receiving it","text":"ثم ذكر الحق جل جلاله سبب هذا الحرمان، وهو حب الدنيا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-211-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-211-s1","r":"q2-211","title":"The construction of “how many”","text":"I say: kam ( كم ) may be declarative or interrogative ( خبرية أو استفهامية ). It occupies an accusative position through an omitted verb understood after it, because it must stand initially ( الصدرية ): “How many [We gave]—We gave them.” Or it is nominative as the subject ( الابتداء ), with the resumptive pronoun ( العائد ) omitted: “We gave it to them.” Translator’s note: Cairo I:237 prints كم آياتنا آتيناهم . The closely parallel grammatical discussion in Ibn ʿAṭiyya’s al-Muḥarrar al-wajīz , at 2:211, reads كم آتينا آتيناهم . This makes explicit the supplied verb “We gave” required by the preceding explanation. The rendering follows that strongly supported reconstruction; the Cairo wording is recorded here, and no manuscript confirmation is claimed.","anchor":"en-q2-211-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-211-s2","r":"q2-211","title":"Signs received and then denied","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, tells His Messenger—or every hearer—to ask the Children of Israel a question of rebuke: how many clear signs We gave them! That is, many a manifest sign concerning you, indicating your message’s truth, your exalted rank and the greatness of your affair, through care for them and as a blessing to those among them who lived in your time. Yet they exchanged God’s blessing for unbelief, denied it, concealed that blessing and were ungrateful for it. Whoever changes God’s blessing after receiving it—God is severe in punishing one who denies His blessings and rejects His messengers. We seek refuge in God from withdrawal after giving, ingratitude for blessings and deprivation of His approval.","anchor":"en-q2-211-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-211-s3","r":"q2-211","title":"Depriving oneself of a saint’s blessing","text":"What was said to the Children of Israel is said to one who recognizes the sainthood of one of God’s saints, then denies and conceals it, deprives himself of that saint’s blessing and dies in his sickness. He is told: whoever changes God’s blessing after it has come to him—God is severe in punishment. His punishment is to meet God with an ailing heart and be raised among the ordinary people of the right hand, deprived of the rank of the near ones that follows the rank of the prophets and messengers. We seek refuge in God from deprivation and the evil outcome of abandonment.","anchor":"en-q2-211-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-211-s4","r":"q2-211","title":"","text":"The Real then identifies the cause of this deprivation: love of the world.","anchor":"en-q2-211-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-212","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart 2:212","anchor":"unit-q2-212"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-1","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"زُيِّنَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا الْحَياةُ الدُّنْيا وَيَسْخَرُونَ مِنَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَالَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا فَوْقَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ وَاللَّهُ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَشاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ (212)","anchor":"ar-q2-212-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-2","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"قلت: (زُين) مبني للمفعول، والفاعل هو الله، إذ لا فاعل سواه.","anchor":"ar-q2-212-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-3","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: زُيِّنَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا من أهل الكتاب وغيرهم، الْحَياةُ الدُّنْيا أي: حُسِّنَتْ في أعينهم، وأُشربت محبتها في قلوبهم، حتى تهالكوا عليها، واعرضوا عن غيرها، فلم تتفرغ قلوبهم للتفكر والاعتبار، ولم تستمع آذانهم للوعظ والتذكار، بل أعمتهم، وأصمّتهم، وقصروا عليها همتهم، حتى جعلوا يسخرون ممن أعرض عنها، كفقراء المسلمين وأهل الصفة، فكانوا يستهزئون بهم، حيث رفضوا الدنيا وأقبلوا على الله، فرفعهم الله","anchor":"ar-q2-212-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-4","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"في أعلى عليين، وخفض الكفار في أسفل سافلين. فهم يسخرون منهم في دار الدنيا وَالَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا فَوْقَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ لأنهم في عليين، والآخرون في أسفل سافلين. أو لأنهم في كرامة، والآخرون في مذلة. أو لأنهم يسخرون منهم يوم القيامة كما سخروا منهم في الدنيا.","anchor":"ar-q2-212-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-5","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"وعبَّر بالتقوى لأنها سبب رفعهم واستعلائهم. وأما استهزاؤهم بهم لأجل فقرهم، فإن الفقر شرف للعبد، والبسط فى الدنيا لا يدل على شرفه فقد يكون استدراجاً، وقد يكون عوناً، فالله يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَشاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ، أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-212-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-6","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"بغير تقدير، فيوسع في الدنيا استدراجاً وابتلاء، ويقتر على من يشاء اختباراً وتمحيصاً، لاَ يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-212-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-7","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن عمل أهل الباطن كله باطني قلبي، بين تفكر واعتبار، وشهود واستبصار، أو نقول: بين فكرة ونظرة وعكوف في الحضرة، فلا يظهرون من أعمالهم إلا المهم من الواجبات، ولذلك قال بعضهم: إذا وصل العمل إلى القلوب استراحت الجوارح، (ومعلوم أن الذرة من أعمال القلوب أفضل من أمثال الجبال من أعمال الجوارح(1)) لأن أعمال القلوب خفية، لا يطلع عليها ملك فيكتبها، ولا شيطان فيفسدها، الإخلاص فيها محقق.","anchor":"ar-q2-212-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-8","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"وأيضاً: «تفكر ساعة أفضل من عبادة ستين سنة» . وسئل- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «أيُّ الأَعْمَال أَفْضَلُ؟ قال:","anchor":"ar-q2-212-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-9","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"العلْمُ بالله. قيلَ: يا رسُولَ الله سَأَلْنَاكَ عن العَمَل؟ فقال: العلمُ بالله، ثم قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: إذا حَصَلَ العلمُ بالله كَفَى قلِيلُ العَملِ» . أو كما قال عليه الصلاة والسلام، فلما خفيت أعمال أهل الباطن سخر منهم أهل الظاهر، واستصغروا شأنهم حيث لم يروا عليهم من الأعمال ما رأوا على العُبَّاد والزُهاد. والذين اتقوا شهود ما سوى الله، أو كل ما يشغل عن الله، فوقهم يوم القيامة لأنهم من المقربين وغيرهم من عوام المسلمين، والله يرزق من يشاء في الدارين بغير حسابٍ، أي: بغير تقدير ولا حصر، فيرزق العلوم، ويفتح مخازن الفهوم على مَن توجه إلى مولاه، وفرغ قلبه مما سواه. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-212-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-212-10","r":"q2-212","title":"2:212 · Worldly adornment and the hidden works of the heart","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى حكمة بعثه الرسل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-212-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-212-s1","r":"q2-212","title":"The unexpressed agent","text":"I say: “Has been adorned” ( زُيّن ) is passive ( مبني للمفعول ). Its agent is God, for there is no agent other than He. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-08] ]","anchor":"en-q2-212-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-212-s2","r":"q2-212","title":"The poor mocked in this world","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: worldly life has been adorned for the disbelievers, whether People of the Book or others. It has been made beautiful in their eyes and its love made to permeate their hearts, until they throw themselves upon it and turn away from everything else. Their hearts find no leisure for reflection and taking heed; their ears do not listen to admonition and reminder. It blinds and deafens them, and they confine their aspiration to it, until they mock those who turn away from it, such as poor Muslims and the People of the Bench. They ridicule them for rejecting the world and turning towards God. God raises these to the highest heights and lowers the disbelievers to the lowest depths. They mock them in this world, but those who fear God will be above them on the Day of Resurrection: they are in the heights, the others in the lowest depths; or they are honoured, the others abased; or they will mock the others on the Day of Resurrection as the others mocked them in this world. He expresses their state by Godfearingness because it causes their elevation and superiority. As for being mocked for poverty, poverty is an honour to the servant. Worldly abundance does not prove his honour: it may be a gradual drawing on towards punishment ( استدراج ), or it may be an aid. God provides for whom He wills without reckoning—that is, without prescribed measure. He gives worldly abundance as a gradual drawing on and a trial, and constricts provision for whom He wills as a test and purification. “He is not questioned about what He does, but they are questioned” [21:23].","anchor":"en-q2-212-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-212-s3","r":"q2-212","title":"Inward work and outward incomprehension","text":"Know that the work of the inward folk ( أهل الباطن ) is wholly inward and of the heart: reflection and taking heed, witnessing and inward perception—or, we may say, contemplation, vision and abiding in the Presence. They display of their works only the necessary obligations. Hence someone said: “When work reaches the hearts, the limbs rest.” It is known that a particle of the heart’s works is better than mountains of bodily works, because the heart’s works are hidden: no angel sees them to record them, and no devil sees them to spoil them. Sincerity is realized in them. Moreover, “An hour’s reflection is better than sixty years’ worship.” The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, was asked: “Which works are best?” He replied: “Knowledge of God.” They said: “Messenger of God, we asked you about work.” He replied: “Knowledge of God,” and then said: “When knowledge of God is attained, little work suffices”—or as he said, blessings and peace be upon him. [B144] Because the inward folk’s works are hidden, the outward folk mock and belittle them, not seeing the works they see in worshippers and ascetics. Those who guard against witnessing anything other than God, or against everything that occupies them away from Him, will be above them on the Day of Resurrection: they are among the near ones, while the others are ordinary Muslims. God provides for whom He wills in both abodes without reckoning: without measure or restriction. He provides sciences and opens the treasuries of understanding to one who turns to his Master and empties his heart of everything else. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q2-212-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-212-s4","r":"q2-212","title":"","text":"The Real then mentions the wisdom of sending messengers.","anchor":"en-q2-212-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-213","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance 2:213","anchor":"unit-q2-213"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-1","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"كانَ النَّاسُ أُمَّةً واحِدَةً فَبَعَثَ اللَّهُ النَّبِيِّينَ مُبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنْذِرِينَ وَأَنْزَلَ مَعَهُمُ الْكِتابَ بِالْحَقِّ","anchor":"ar-q2-213-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-2","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"لِيَحْكُمَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ فِيمَا اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ وَمَا اخْتَلَفَ فِيهِ إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوهُ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ بَغْياً بَيْنَهُمْ فَهَدَى اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لِمَا اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ مِنَ الْحَقِّ بِإِذْنِهِ وَاللَّهُ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشاءُ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ (213)","anchor":"ar-q2-213-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-3","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"قلت: (فبعث) معطوف على محذوف، أي: فاختلفوا فبعث، و (بغياً) : مفعول له، و (من الحق) بيان (لما) .","anchor":"ar-q2-213-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-4","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: كانَ النَّاسُ في زمن آدم عليه السلام وما قرُب منه أُمَّةً واحِدَةً أي: جماعة واحدة، متفقة على التوحيد، والطاعة، فاختلفوا بعد ذلك في أمر التوحيد، فَبَعَثَ اللَّهُ النَّبِيِّينَ مُبَشِّرِينَ لأهل التوحيد والطاعة بالنعيم المقيم، وَمُنْذِرِينَ أي: مخوفين لأهل الكفر والعصيان بالعذاب الأليم.","anchor":"ar-q2-213-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-5","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"وَأَنْزَلَ مَعَهُمُ الْكِتابَ أي: جنس الكتب، فيشمل الكتب السماوية كلها، متلبساً ذلك الكتاب بِالْحَقِّ، ودالاً عليه لِيَحْكُمَ الحق تعالى على لسان الرسل بَيْنَ النَّاسِ في الأمر الذي اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ من أمر التوحيد وغيره. ثم اختلفوا أيضاً في الكتب المنزلة فبعضهم آمن، وبعضهم كفر بها أو ببعضها، وَمَا اخْتَلَفَ فِيهِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-213-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-6","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"في الكتاب المنزل، إِلَّا الَّذِينَ أُوتُوهُ حسداً أو كبراً فاليهود آمنوا بالتوراة وكفروا بالإنجيل، والنصارى آمنوا بالإنجيل وكفروا بالتوراة، مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُمُ: الآيات الواضحات في صحة ذلك الكتاب الذي كفروا به، والأمر بالإيمان به.","anchor":"ar-q2-213-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-7","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"وإنما وقع ذلك الكفر منهم بَغْياً وحسداً بَيْنَهُمْ، فأنزل الله العلم ليجمعهم ويؤلف بينهم على طاعته، فأمرهم أن يتألفوا بالعلم، فتحاسدوا، واختلفوا طلباً للرئاسة والجاه، فَهَدَى اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بمحمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- للأمر الذي اختلف فيه أهل الكتاب، وهو الحق الذي جاءت به الرسل، فآمنوا بالجميع، وتآلفوا على طاعة الله بِإِذْنِهِ وإرادته، وَاللَّهُ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشاءُ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ، ويضل من يشاء عن طريقه القويم، لاَ يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-213-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-8","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"الإشارة: الأصل في الأرواح كلها: الاتفاقُ والإقرار، وإنما حصل لها الخلاف والإنكار بعد دخولها في عالم الأشباح، وهبوطها من عالم الأرواح، فبعث الله النبيين يُذكْرون الناس العهدَ القديم، فمن سبقت له السعادة حصل له الإقرار، ومَن سبق له الشقاء حصل له الإنكار، ولذلك قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «كُلُّ مَوْلُودٍ يُولَد على الفِطْرَةِ، فَأَبَوَاهُ يُهَوِّدَانِهِ أَوْ يُنَصّرَانِهِ أوْ يُمَجِّسَانِهِ» . ثم بعث الله الحكماء، وهم العارفون بالله، يعالجون ما حصل","anchor":"ar-q2-213-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-9","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"للروح من الجهل والإنكار، فمن سبقت له العناية آمن بهم، وصدقهم، واستسلم بكليته إليهم، فحصل له الوصول، وبلغ كل المأمول، ومن سبق له الحرمان لم يحصل له بهم إيمان، وبقي دائماً في قلبه حيران.","anchor":"ar-q2-213-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-10","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"وما وقع هذا الإنكار في الغالب إلا من أهل الرئاسة والجاه، أو من كان عبداً لدنياه وهواه، بغياً وحسداً منهم، فهدى الله الذين آمنوا- وهم أهل الفطرة والنيّة- لما اختلفوا فيه من الحق بإذنه، فحصل لهم التصديق، ووصلوا إلى عين التحقيق، وَاللَّهُ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشاءُ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ وهو طريق الوصول إلى الحضرة القدسية التي كانت مقرّاً للأرواح الزكية، منها جاءت وإليها عادت. وفي ذلك يقول ابن البنا رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-213-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-11","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"وَهَذِهِ الحَقِيقَةُ النَّفْسِيَّةْ ... مَوْصُولةٌ بالحَضْرَةِ القُدْسِيَّهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-213-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-12","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"وَإِنَّمَا يَعْوقُهَا المَوْضُوعُ ... وَمِنْ هُنَا يُبْتَدأُ الطُّلُوعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-213-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-213-13","r":"q2-213","title":"2:213 · The one community, disagreement and prophetic guidance","text":"ولمّا كانت المحبة والهداية إلى أسبابها مقرونتين بالبلاء ذكره الحق تعالى بإثر الهداية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-213-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-213-s1","r":"q2-213","title":"An omitted disagreement and an expressed motive","text":"I say: “Then He sent” ( فبعث ) is coordinated with something omitted ( معطوف على محذوف ): “then they disagreed, so He sent.” “Out of aggression” ( بغياً ) is an accusative of purpose or cause ( مفعول له ). “Of the truth” ( من الحق ) explains the relative “that about which” ( ما ).","anchor":"en-q2-213-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-213-s2","r":"q2-213","title":"Revelation intended to unite, and knowledge turned into rivalry","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: in Adam’s time and the period near it, people were one community, one company agreeing upon unity and obedience. Afterwards they disagreed concerning divine unity. God then sent the prophets, bringing good news of abiding bliss to the people of unity and obedience, and warning the people of unbelief and disobedience of painful punishment. He sent down with them the Book: the kind denoted by “books,” encompassing all heavenly scriptures. That Book was clothed in truth and indicated it, so that the Real, through the messengers’ tongues, might judge between people concerning their disagreements about divine unity and other matters. They then also disagreed concerning the revealed books: some believed, while others disbelieved in them or in part of them. None disagreed concerning the revealed Book except those given it, through envy or pride. Thus the Jews believed in the Torah and disbelieved in the Gospel, and the Christians believed in the Gospel and disbelieved in the Torah, after clear signs had come to them establishing the truth of the Book they rejected and commanding faith in it. [B145] This unbelief arose only through mutual aggression and envy. God sent down knowledge to gather and unite them in His obedience, commanding them to come together through knowledge; they envied one another and disagreed in pursuit of leadership and standing. God then guided those who believed in Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, concerning what the People of the Book disputed: the truth the messengers brought. They believed in all of it and united in God’s obedience by His leave and will. God guides whom He wills to a straight path and leads whom He wills away from His upright way. “He is not questioned about what He does, but they are questioned” [21:23].","anchor":"en-q2-213-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-213-s3","r":"q2-213","title":"The spirits’ original acknowledgement and their return","text":"The original state of all spirits is agreement and acknowledgement. Disagreement and denial arise only after their entry into the world of bodily forms and their descent from the world of spirits. God sent the prophets to remind people of the ancient covenant. Those for whom happiness had preceded acknowledged it; those for whom wretchedness had preceded denied it. Hence the Prophet said: “Every newborn is born upon the original disposition ( الفطرة ); its parents make it a Jew, a Christian or a Magian.” God then sent the sages, the gnostics of God, to treat the ignorance and denial that had overtaken the spirit. Those for whom divine care preceded believed in them, affirmed them and surrendered wholly to them. They attained arrival and reached all they hoped for. Those for whom deprivation preceded did not attain faith in them and remained always bewildered in their hearts. This denial generally comes only from people of leadership and standing, or those enslaved to their world and desire, through their aggression and envy. God guided those who believed—the people of original disposition and intention—to the truth about which others disagreed, by His leave. They attained affirmation and reached realization itself. God guides whom He wills to a straight path: the path of arrival at the Holy Presence, which was the dwelling of pure spirits. From it they came, and to it they returned. Concerning this Ibn al-Bannā, God be pleased with him, says: This reality of the soul is joined to the Holy Presence; only its bodily substrate impedes it, and from here the ascent begins. [B146]","anchor":"en-q2-213-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-213-s4","r":"q2-213","title":"","text":"Since love and guidance to its means are joined to trial, the Real mentions trial immediately after guidance.","anchor":"en-q2-213-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-214","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help 2:214","anchor":"unit-q2-214"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-1","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَأْتِكُمْ مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ خَلَوْا مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ مَسَّتْهُمُ الْبَأْساءُ وَالضَّرَّاءُ وَزُلْزِلُوا حَتَّى يَقُولُ الرَّسُولُ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ مَتى نَصْرُ اللَّهِ أَلا إِنَّ نَصْرَ اللَّهِ قَرِيبٌ (214)","anchor":"ar-q2-214-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-2","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"قلت: «أم» منقطعة بمعنى بل، وتتضمن استفهاماً إنكاريّاً، و «حسب» تتعدى إلى مفعولين، أي: أظننتم دخول الجنة حاصلاً من غير أن يأتيكم؟. (لما) أصلها (لم) زيدت عليها «ما» : وهي تدل على توقع منفيها بخلاف لم.","anchor":"ar-q2-214-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-3","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"و (حتى يقول) يصح فيه النصب بتقدير (أن) لأن الزلزلة متقدمة على قول الرسول، والرفع على حكاية الحال، أي: وزلزلوا حتى حالتهم حينئذٍ أن الرسول ومن معه يقولون كذا وكذا. وفائدة الحكاية: فرض ما كان واقعاً في الزمان الماضي واقعاً في هذا الزمان، تصوّراً لتلك الحال العجيبة، واستحضاراً لصورتها في مشاهدة السامع، وإنما وجب رفعه عند إرادة الحال لأن نصبه يؤدي إلى تقدير (أن) ، وهي للاستقبال، والحال يُنافيه، ويصح في موضع «حتى» الداخلة على الحال الفاء السببية.","anchor":"ar-q2-214-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-4","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- والمؤمنين، تسلية لهم وتشجيعاً لقلوبهم: أظننتم أَن تَدْخُلُواْ الْجَنَّةَ ولمَّا يُصبكم مثلُ ما أصاب مَنْ قبلَكم من الأنبياء وأممهم، فقد مَسَّتْهُمُ الْبَأْساءُ في أموالهم بالغصب والنهب والموت وَالضَّرَّاءُ فى أبدانهم بالقتل في الحرب والمرض وأنواع البلاء، وَزُلْزِلُوا أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-214-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-5","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"ضُربوا بالمحن والشدائد، وطال عليهم البلاء، وتأخر عنهم النصر، حتى أفضى بهم الحال إلى أن قالوا: مَتى يأتينا نَصْرُ اللَّهِ؟ استبطاء لمجيئه مع شدة البلاء.","anchor":"ar-q2-214-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-6","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"قال الحق جل جلاله بشارةً لهم: أَلا إِنَّ نَصْرَ اللَّهِ قَرِيبٌ فلا تستعجلوا، وَاصْبِرُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ وَالْعاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-214-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-7","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"الإشارة: الجنة حفت بالمكاره، ولا فرق بين جنة الزخارف وجنة المعارف، فمن رام دخول جنة المعارف قبل أن يمسه شيء من المكاره، فقد رام المحال. قال أبو المواهب: من ادّعى شهود الجمال، قبل تأدُّبه بالجلال، فارفضه فإنه دجال. وقال بعض العارفين: [صيحة العدو سوط الله يزجر به قلوب أوليائه لئلا تسكن إلى غيره] . وفي الحِكَم: «إنما أجرى الأذى عليهم كي لا تكون ساكناً إليهم، أراد أن يُزْعِجَكَ عن كل شيء حتى لا تكون ساكناً إلى شيء» . وقال الشيخ أبو الحسن رضي الله عنه: [اللهم إنَّ القوم قد حكمت عليهم بالذل حتى عزُّوا، وحكمت عليهم بالفقْدِ حتى وَجَدُوا] . فتسليط الخلق على أولياء الله في بدايتهم سنة ماضية، وحكمة إلهية، وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لِسُنَّةِ اللَّهِ تَبْدِيلًا.","anchor":"ar-q2-214-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-8","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"حتى إذا تخلصوا من البقايا، وكملت فيهم المزايا، نشر فضيلتهم لعباده، فأقروهم ليُعرفُوهم الطريق إلى الله، ويدلوا العباد على الله، بعد أن كساهم حينئذٍ كُسوة الجمال وكسوة الجلال، فبكسوة الجمال يقع الائتلاف عليهم والعطف لهم، وبكسوة الجلال يقع الامتثال لأمرهم والاستماع لقولهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-214-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-214-9","r":"q2-214","title":"2:214 · Trial, trembling and the nearness of help","text":"ولما أمر الحق تعالى بالنفقة في الجهاد وغيره، سألوا ما الذي ينفقون؟، فبيَّن الله تعالى لهم المنفَق والمحل الذي تُدفع فيه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-214-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-214-s1","r":"q2-214","title":"Expectation and the vivid presentation of a past scene","text":"I say: am ( أم ) is discontinuous ( منقطعة ), meaning “rather,” and includes a reproachful question ( استفهام إنكاري ). Ḥasiba , “to suppose,” takes two objects: “Did you suppose entry into the Garden to be attainable without this coming upon you?” Lammā originally consists of lam with mā added. Unlike lam , it implies expectation of what it negates. “Until the messenger says” ( حتى يقول ) permits the subjunctive ( النصب ) through an understood an , because the shaking precedes the messenger’s speech. It also permits the indicative ( الرفع ), representing the situation as present ( حكاية الحال ): they were shaken until their condition then was that the messenger and those with him were saying such and such. The benefit of this representation is to present what occurred in past time as occurring now, depicting that astonishing situation and bringing its image before the hearer’s witnessing. The indicative is required when a present situation is intended, because the subjunctive would imply an , which points forward, whereas present occurrence is incompatible with that. The causal fāʾ ( الفاء السببية ) can stand where ḥattā introduces this present situation.","anchor":"en-q2-214-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-214-s2","r":"q2-214","title":"The trials of earlier believers","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says to the Messenger and believers, consoling and strengthening their hearts: did you suppose that you would enter the Garden before the like of what befell earlier prophets and their communities had befallen you? Hardship touched their wealth through seizure, pillage and loss; distress touched their bodies through killing in war, illness and varieties of affliction. They were shaken: struck by trials and hardships. Their affliction lasted, and help was delayed, until their condition brought them to say, “When will God’s help come to us?” They found its coming slow in the intensity of their trial. The Real gives them good news: indeed, God’s help is near. Do not be hasty; “be patient: God is with the patient” [8:46], and “the final outcome belongs to the Godfearing” [7:128].","anchor":"en-q2-214-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-214-s3","r":"q2-214","title":"Beauty reached through discipline under Majesty","text":"The Garden is surrounded by hardships. There is no difference in this between the Garden of adornments and the Garden of gnoses ( جنة الزخارف، جنة المعارف ). Whoever seeks entry into the Garden of gnoses before any hardship touches him seeks the impossible. Abū al-Mawāhib said: “Reject anyone who claims to witness Beauty before being disciplined by Majesty: he is an impostor.” A gnostic said: “The enemy’s cry is God’s whip, driving His saints’ hearts away from repose in anything other than Him.” The Ḥikam says: “He made injury reach you through them only so that you would not repose in them. He wished to dislodge you from everything, so that you would repose in nothing.” [Translator’s note: Cairo I, p. 241, reads عليهم (ʿalayhim, “upon them”). Ibn ʿAjība’s own Īqāẓ al-himam quotes the same construction and then explicitly explains that God makes the injury reach you على أيدي الخلق إليك , “through other people’s hands” (Dār al-Maʿārif, p. 488). The English follows this authorial explanation of the intended agency; the collated Arabic retains Cairo’s wording. The second sentence also retains Cairo’s distinct ending, “repose in nothing,” rather than the Īqāẓ / Ḥikam ending, “nothing distracts you from Him.”] Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan, God be pleased with him, said: “O God, You decreed abasement upon the folk until they became mighty, and loss upon them until they found.” [B147] Allowing creatures power over God’s saints at their beginnings is an established divine way and wisdom: “You will find no change in God’s way” [33:62]. When they are freed of the remnants and their excellences are completed, He spreads their merit among His servants. People acknowledge them so that they may make known the path to God and direct servants towards Him. By then He has clothed them in the garment of Beauty and the garment of Majesty. Through Beauty’s garment people come together around them and incline affectionately towards them; through Majesty’s garment people obey their commands and listen to their words. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-214-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-214-s4","r":"q2-214","title":"","text":"When the Real commanded expenditure in fighting in His path and elsewhere, they asked what they should spend. God explained what should be spent and where it should be given.","anchor":"en-q2-214-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-215","r":"q2-215","title":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self","text":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self 2:215","anchor":"unit-q2-215"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-215-1","r":"q2-215","title":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self","text":"يَسْئَلُونَكَ ماذا يُنْفِقُونَ قُلْ ما أَنْفَقْتُمْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلِلْوالِدَيْنِ وَالْأَقْرَبِينَ وَالْيَتامى وَالْمَساكِينِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ (215)","anchor":"ar-q2-215-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-215-2","r":"q2-215","title":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self","text":"قلت: (ماذا) إما مفعول (يُنفقون) ، أو مبتدأ وخبر بحذف العائد، أي: ما الذي ينفقونه، والسائل هو عمرو بن الجُموح، كان ذا مال فقال: يا رسول الله، ماذا ننفق من أموالنا، وأين نضعها؟ فنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-215-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-215-3","r":"q2-215","title":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يَسْئَلُونَكَ يا محمد ماذا يُنْفِقُونَ من أموالهم؟ قُلْ لهم: ما أَنْفَقْتُمْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ أيّ خير كان، ذهباً أو فضة أو طعاماً أو ثياباً أو حيواناً أو غير ذلك، فادفعوه للأهمّ فالأهم كالوالدين والأقربين لأن فيهم الصلة والصدقة، وَالْيَتامى الذين مات آباؤهم لهضم حالهم، وَالْمَساكِينِ لضعفهم، وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ لغربته واحتياجه إلى ما يُبلِّغه إلى وطنه، وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يجازيكم به الله، فلا يخفى عليه شيء من أحوالكم، وهذه النفقة غير الزكاة، فلا نسخ فى الآية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-215-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-215-4","r":"q2-215","title":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self","text":"الإشارة: الإنفاق على قسمين: حسىّ ومعنوى، الإنفاق الحسيّ هو بذل الأموال والفلوس، والإنفاق المعنوي هو بذل الأرواح والنفوس، فمن بذل أمواله لله عوضه الله جنة الزخارف، ومن بذل نفسه لله عوضه الله جنة المعارف، ومن دخل جنة المعارف لا يشتاق إلى جنة الزخارف، وكما أن لنفقة الأموال محلا تصرف فيه، كما ذكره الحقّ تعالى هنا، كذلك لنفقة النفوس محل تصرف فيه وهو خدمة الشيوخ العارفين بالله، والإخوان الذين يستعين بهم على الوصول إلى الله، وكذلك من احتاج إليه من اليتامى الذين لا شيخ لهم، فيرشدهم وينصحهم، والمساكين الضعفاء الذين لا قدرة لهم على مجاهدة نفوسهم، فيقويهم بحاله أو مقاله، والغريب الذي انفرد عن الإخوان، ولم يجد ما يستعين به على سيره فيرشده إلى الصحبة والاجتماع بأهل المحبة، وإلى هذا المنزع أشار الشيخ أبو مدين رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-215-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-215-5","r":"q2-215","title":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self","text":"وَبالتغنِّي عَلى الإخوَانِ جُدْ أبَدا ... حِسّاً ومعنىً، وغُضَّ الطَّرْفَ إنْ عَثَرَا","anchor":"ar-q2-215-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-215-6","r":"q2-215","title":"2:215 · Where to spend wealth and where to offer the self","text":"ولمَّا ذكر الحق جلّ جلاله قواعد الإسلام، وهي الصلاةُ والزكاة والصوم والحج، بعد أن أشار إلى كلمة التوحيد بقوله: وَإِلهُكُمْ إِلهٌ واحِدٌ، ذكر الجهاد- الذي هو حفظ نظامه- فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-215-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-215-s1","r":"q2-215","title":"What to give, and to whom","text":"I say: mādhā ( ماذا ) may be the object of “spend,” or a subject and predicate ( مبتدأ وخبر ) with the resumptive pronoun omitted: “What is it that they should spend?” The questioner was ʿAmr ibn al-Jamūḥ, a wealthy man, who asked: “Messenger of God, what should we spend from our wealth, and where should we place it?” The verse was revealed.","anchor":"en-q2-215-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-215-s2","r":"q2-215","title":"Priority among recipients","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: they ask you, Muḥammad, what they should spend from their wealth. Tell them: whatever good you spend—gold, silver, food, clothing, livestock or anything else—give it in order of greatest need and priority. Parents and close relatives come first, because giving to them combines maintaining kinship with charity; then orphans whose fathers have died, because their condition is diminished; the needy, because of their weakness; and the traveller, because he is away from home and needs what will enable him to return. Whatever good you do, God will recompense you for it: none of your conditions is hidden from Him. This expenditure is other than the obligatory alms ( الزكاة ); thus the verse is not abrogated. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-215-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-215-s3","r":"q2-215","title":"Expenditure in sense and meaning","text":"Expenditure is of two kinds: sensible and inward ( حسي ومعنوي ). Sensible expenditure is giving wealth and money; inward expenditure is giving spirits and selves. Whoever gives his wealth for God receives in exchange the Garden of adornments; whoever gives himself for God receives in exchange the Garden of gnoses. One who enters the Garden of gnoses does not yearn for the Garden of adornments. Just as expenditure of wealth has a place to be directed, as the Real mentions here, expenditure of selves has its place: serving shaykhs who know God, and brethren through whom one seeks aid in arriving at God. It also includes those who need one: orphans with no shaykh, whom one guides and counsels; the weak and needy who cannot struggle against their lower selves, whom one strengthens by one’s state or speech; and the stranger separated from the brethren, who finds nothing to assist his journey. One guides him towards companionship and gathering with the people of love. Shaykh Abū Madyan, God be pleased with him, points to this meaning: Be ever generous to the brethren, needing nothing from them, in sense and meaning; lower your gaze when one stumbles. [B148]","anchor":"en-q2-215-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-215-s4","r":"q2-215","title":"","text":"Having mentioned Islam’s pillars—prayer, obligatory alms, fasting and pilgrimage—after pointing to the declaration of unity with “Your God is One God,” the Real mentions fighting in His path, which preserves its order.","anchor":"en-q2-215-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-216","r":"q2-216","title":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good","text":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good 2:216","anchor":"unit-q2-216"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-216-1","r":"q2-216","title":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good","text":"كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌ لَكُمْ وَعَسى أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئاً وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ وَعَسى أَنْ تُحِبُّوا شَيْئاً وَهُوَ شَرٌّ لَكُمْ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنْتُمْ لا تَعْلَمُونَ (216)","anchor":"ar-q2-216-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-216-2","r":"q2-216","title":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good","text":"قلت: الكره- بالضم-: اسم لما يَشُقُّ على النفس، وبالفتح المَصْدَر.","anchor":"ar-q2-216-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-216-3","r":"q2-216","title":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فُرض عليكم الجهاد، وهو شاق عليكم، تكرهه نفوسكم، وفيه خير كبير لكم، وَعَسى أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئاً وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ، ففي الجهاد نصر دينكم، وإعلاء كلمة إسلامكم، والغنيمة والظّفْرُ بعدوكم، والأجر الكبير عند ربكم، من مات كان شهيداً، ومن عاش عاش سعيداً، وكذلك بقية التكاليف، فإن النفس تكره الإقدام عليها، وهي مَنَاط صلاحها، وسبب فلاحها، وَعَسى أَنْ تُحِبُّوا شَيْئاً وَهُوَ شَرٌّ لَكُمْ فقد تحبون الراحة وترك الجهاد وفي ذلك ذُلُّكُمْ، وظهورُ العدو عليكم، وفوات الأجر من ربكم، وحرمان درجة الشهادة عند ربكم. وكذلك جميع المنهيات فإن النفس تحبها بالطبع، وتَشْرَهُ إليها، وهي تُفضي بها إلى ذلها وهوانها، وعبَّر الحقّ سبحانه بعسى لأن النفس إذا ارتاضت انعكس الأمر عليها، فيخف عليها أمر الطاعة، ويصعب عليها أمر المخالفة، وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ ما فيه مصلحتكم، وَأَنْتُمْ لا تَعْلَمُونَ لجهلكم بعواقب أموركم.","anchor":"ar-q2-216-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-216-4","r":"q2-216","title":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good","text":"الإشارة: الجهاد على قسمين: جهاد أصغر وهو جهاد السيف، وجهاد أكبر وهو جهاد النفس، فيجاهدها أولاً في القيام بجميع المأمورات، وترك جميع المنهيات، ثم يجاهدها ثانياً في ترك العوائد والشهوات، ومجانبة الرخص والتأويلات، ثم يجاهدها ثالثاً في ترك التدبير والاختيار، والسكون تحت مجاري الأقدار، حتى لا تختار إلا ما اختار الحق تعالى لها، ولا تشتهي إلا ما يقضي الله عليها، فإن النفس جاهلة بالعواقب، فعسى أن تكره شيئاً وهو خير لها، وعسى أن تحب شيئاً وهو شر لها.","anchor":"ar-q2-216-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-216-5","r":"q2-216","title":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good","text":"فعسى أن تأتيها المسار من حيث تعتقد المضارّ، وعسى أن تأتيها المضار من حيث ترجو المسار، وعسى أن تنتفع على أيدي الأعداء، وعسى أن تضر على أيدي الأحباء، وعسى أن تكره الموت وهو خير لها، وعسى أن تحب الحياة وهي شر لها، فالواجب تسليم الأمور إلى خالقها، الذي هو عالم بمصالحها، وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنْتُمْ لا تَعْلَمُونَ، وهذا كله قبل تصفيتها وكمالها، وأما إذا تهذبت وكملت رياضتها، فالواجب اتباع ما يتجلى فيها، إذ لا يتجلى فيها إلا الحق، وهذا هو ثمرة الجهاد الأكبر، وأما الجهاد الأصغر فلا يحصل شيء من هذا، فلذلك كان مفضولا عند أهل الجهاد الأكبر(1) . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-216-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-216-6","r":"q2-216","title":"2:216 · What the self dislikes and what God knows to be good","text":"ولمَّا كان القتال محرماً في الأشهر الحرم في أول الإسلام، ووقع من بعض الصحابة، فندموا وتحرجوا، أزال الله ذلك الحرج عنهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-216-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-216-s1","r":"q2-216","title":"Hardship and aversion","text":"I say: kurh ( كُره ), with ḍamma , names what is hard upon the self; with fatḥa , karh , it is the verbal noun ( المصدر ).","anchor":"en-q2-216-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-216-s2","r":"q2-216","title":"Duties, desires and their outcomes","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: fighting in His path has been made obligatory for you. It is difficult for you and your selves dislike it, although it holds great good for you. You may dislike something that is good for you. Fighting brings victory for your religion, raises the word of your Islam, brings booty and victory over your enemy, and great reward with your Lord. Whoever dies is a martyr; whoever lives lives happily. So too with the other religious obligations ( التكاليف ): the self dislikes undertaking them, although its soundness depends upon them and they cause its flourishing. You may love something that is bad for you. You may love rest and abandoning the struggle, although this brings your abasement, the enemy’s ascendancy over you, loss of reward from your Lord and deprivation of martyrdom’s rank with Him. So too with all prohibited things: the self naturally loves and greedily desires them, although they lead to its abasement and humiliation. The Real uses “may” ( عسى ) because, when the self is disciplined, its condition is reversed: obedience becomes easy and disobedience difficult. God knows what serves your well-being, while you do not know, because you are ignorant of your affairs’ outcomes.","anchor":"en-q2-216-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-216-s3","r":"q2-216","title":"The successive struggles against the lower self","text":"Struggle ( الجهاد ) is of two kinds: the lesser struggle, with the sword, and the greater struggle, against the lower self. One first struggles against it to fulfil every command and abandon every prohibition. Secondly, one struggles to abandon habitual comforts and desires and avoid concessions and accommodating interpretations ( الرخص والتأويلات ). Thirdly, one struggles to abandon self-directed management and choice ( التدبير والاختيار ), resting beneath the flow of decrees until the self chooses only what the Real chooses for it and desires only what God decrees for it. The self is ignorant of outcomes: it may dislike what is good for it and love what is bad for it. Joys may come from where it expects harms, and harms from where it hopes for joys. It may benefit at enemies’ hands and suffer at loved ones’ hands. It may dislike death although death is good for it, and love life although life is bad for it. What is required is to entrust affairs to their Creator, who knows what benefits them. God knows, and you do not know. All this precedes the self’s purification and perfection. When it has been refined and its discipline completed, however, one must follow what discloses itself within it, for only the Real discloses Himself there. This is the fruit of the greater struggle. None of this is attained through the lesser struggle; hence it is surpassed in the eyes of the people of the greater struggle. And success is through God. [B149]","anchor":"en-q2-216-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-216-s4","r":"q2-216","title":"","text":"At the beginning of Islam, fighting was forbidden in the sacred months. Some Companions fought then, regretted it and felt distress; God removed that distress from them.","anchor":"en-q2-216-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-217-218","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith 2:217–218","anchor":"unit-q2-217-218"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-1","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"يَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ الشَّهْرِ الْحَرامِ قِتالٍ فِيهِ قُلْ قِتالٌ فِيهِ كَبِيرٌ وَصَدٌّ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَكُفْرٌ بِهِ وَالْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ وَإِخْراجُ أَهْلِهِ مِنْهُ أَكْبَرُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ وَالْفِتْنَةُ أَكْبَرُ مِنَ الْقَتْلِ وَلا يَزالُونَ يُقاتِلُونَكُمْ حَتَّى يَرُدُّوكُمْ عَنْ دِينِكُمْ إِنِ اسْتَطاعُوا وَمَنْ يَرْتَدِدْ مِنْكُمْ عَنْ دِينِهِ فَيَمُتْ وَهُوَ كافِرٌ فَأُولئِكَ حَبِطَتْ أَعْمالُهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (217) إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَالَّذِينَ هاجَرُوا وَجاهَدُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أُولئِكَ يَرْجُونَ رَحْمَتَ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (218)","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-2","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"قلت: (قتال) : بدل اشتمال من (الشهر الحرام) ، وقد وقع خبط في عطف (المسجد الحرام،) والصواب: ما قاله الزمخشري وابن عطية أنه عطف على (السبيل) إذ هو المتبادر من جهة المعنى، أي: وصد عن سبيل الله وعن المسجد الحرام أكبر جرماً من قتل السَّرِية في الشهر الحرام، والقواعد النحوية إنما هى أغلبية.","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-3","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يَسْئَلُونَكَ يا محمد عَنِ الشَّهْرِ الْحَرامِ أي: عن القتال فى الأشهر الحرم، قُلْ لهم: القتالُ في الشهر الحرام أمره كَبِيرٌ، لكن ما وقع من الكفار من صد الناس عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-4","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"منعهم من الإسلام والطاعة، وكذلك كفرهم بالله وصدهم المسلمين عن الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرامِ عام الحديبية، وإخراج المسلمين من مكة التي هي بلدهم- وَالْفِتْنَةُ التي هم فيها من الكفر، وافتتان الناس عن دينهم- أَكْبَرُ جرماً من القتال الذي وقع في الشهر الحرام تأويلاً وظنّاً أنه لم يدخل الشهر الحرام.","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-5","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"وذلك أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بعث سرية وأمّر عليها عبد الله بنَ جَحْش في آخر جُمَادى الآخِرَةِ، فَلَقُوا عمرو بن الحضرمي، مع أناس من قريش، بعد غروب الشمس من جمادى الآخرة، فرموا عمراً فقتلوه، وأخذوا الغنيمة، فقال لهم عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لم آمركم أن تقتلوا في الشهر الحرام» فندموا، وبعثت قريش بالعتاب للنبيّ صلّى الله عليه وسلم: كيف تستحل القتال في الشهر الحرام؟ فنزلت هذه الآية. ثم نسخ تحريم القتال في الأشهر الحرم بقوله تعالى: وَقاتِلُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ كَافَّةً كَما يُقاتِلُونَكُمْ كَافَّةً.","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-6","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"ثم قال الحق جلّ جلاله في التحذير من الكفار: وَلا يَزالُونَ يُقاتِلُونَكُمْ حَتَّى يَرُدُّوكُمْ عَنْ دِينِكُمْ إِنِ اسْتَطاعُوا، لكن لا يطيقون ذلك، وَمَنْ يَرْتَدِدْ مِنْكُمْ عَنْ دِينِهِ ويستمر عليه حتى يموت وَهُوَ كافِرٌ فَأُولئِكَ حَبِطَتْ أَعْمالُهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيا فلا حرمة له، ولا نصيب له في الفيء والغنيمة، وفي الْآخِرَةِ فلا يرى لها ثواباً، وَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-7","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"ومفهوم الآية: أنه إن رجع قبل الموت لا يحبَط عملُه، وهو قول الشافعي. وقال مالك: يحبط أجر كل ما عمل، ويعيد الحج، إن تقدم على الردة، ويقبل منه الإسلام إن رجع، فإنْ لم يرجع أمهل ثلاثة أيام، ثم يقتل.","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-8","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"ولمّا نزلت الآية في إسقاط الحرج، ظنوا أنه لا أجر لهم في ذلك الجهاد، فأنزل الحق جل جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَالَّذِينَ هاجَرُوا وَجاهَدُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أُولئِكَ يَرْجُونَ رَحْمَتَ اللَّهِ أي ثوابه، وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ لهم رَحِيمٌ بهم، فلا يضيع جهادهم في هذه السرِيَّة، وأعاد الموصول لتعظيم شأن الهجرة والجهاد، وعبَّر بالرجاء إشعاراً بأن العمل غير موجب للثواب، وإنما هو عبودية، والأمر بيد الله إن شاء أثاب وإن شاء عاقب، لاَ يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-9","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"الإشارة: تعظيم الزمان والمكان يكون بقدر ما يقع فيه من طاعة الملك الديان، فالزمان الذي تهب فيه نفحات القبول والإقبال، لا ينبغي أن يقع فيه ملاججة ولا قتال، وهو وقت حضرة الذكر، أو التذكير، أو الجلوس مع","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-10","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"العارفين أهل الإكسير، فسوء الأدب فيه أمره كبير، ومنع القاصدين من وصوله جُرمه كبير، وصد القلوب عن نفحات تلك الحضرة أكبر من كل كبير، ولا يزال قُطَّاع هذه الطريق يردون من أراد سلوكها على التحقيق، لكن من سبق له التأييد لا يرده عن الحق جبار ولا عنيد، ومن سبق له الحرمان، وحَكم عليه القضاءُ بالخذلان، رجع ولو بعد العيان، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-11","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"والله ما نَشْكُرْ خَلِيعْ ... وإنْ ثَمِلْ. وإن صَحَا","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-12","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"وإن ثَبَتْ، سَيْرٌ سَرِيعْ ... وإن شَرِبْ حَتَّى امْتَحا","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-13","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"حَتى يُقَطَّعْ في القَطيعْ ... ويَدُورْ دَوْرَ الرَحَا(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-14","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"إن الذين آمنوا وصدَّقُوا بطريق الله، وهاجروا أهواءهم في مرضاة الله، وجاهدوا نفوسهم في محبة الله، أولئك يرجون رحمة الله، فلا يُخيبهم الكريم لأنه غفور رحيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-217-218-15","r":"q2-217-218","title":"2:217–218 · Fighting in the sacred month, expulsion and steadfastness in faith","text":"ولمّا كان الخمر حلالاً في أول الإسلام، وكانوا يشربونه، ويتِّجُرون فيه، فيتصدقون بثمنه وبثمن القمار، بيَّن الحقّ تعالى ذلك، بعد الأمر بالإنفاق لئلا يقع التساهل في المعاملة بعلّة الصدقة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-217-218-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-217-218-s1","r":"q2-217-218","title":"An inclusive substitution and a disputed coordination","text":"I say: “Fighting” ( قتال ) is a substitution of inclusion ( بدل اشتمال ) for “the sacred month.” There has been confusion concerning the coordination ( العطف ) of “the Sacred Mosque.” The correct explanation is that of al-Zamakhsharī and Ibn ʿAṭiyya: it is coordinated with “the path,” since this is the meaning that immediately suggests itself—barring from God’s path and from the Sacred Mosque is a greater offence than the expedition’s killing during the sacred month. Grammatical rules describe what generally obtains; they are not without exceptions. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-09] ]","anchor":"en-q2-217-218-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-217-218-s2","r":"q2-217-218","title":"The expedition and the opponents’ greater wrongs","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: they ask you, Muḥammad, about the sacred month—that is, fighting during the sacred months. Tell them: fighting during the sacred month is a grave matter. Yet the disbelievers’ barring people from God’s path—preventing their entry into Islam and obedience—their unbelief in God, their barring Muslims from the Sacred Mosque in the year of al-Ḥudaybiya, and their expulsion of Muslims from Mecca, their own homeland, together with the fitna of their unbelief and turning people from their religion, are graver offences than the fighting that occurred in the sacred month through an interpretation and the supposition that the sacred month had not yet begun. The Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace, had sent an expedition under ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaḥsh at the end of Jumādā al-Ākhira. They encountered ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥaḍramī with a group of Quraysh after sunset on [the final day of] Jumādā al-Ākhira, shot ʿAmr, killed him and took the booty. The Prophet told them: “I did not command you to kill in the sacred month.” They regretted it. Quraysh sent a reproach to the Prophet: “How can you consider fighting in the sacred month lawful?” This verse was revealed. The prohibition of fighting during the sacred months was then abrogated by His saying, “Fight the associators all together, just as they fight you all together” [9:36]. [B150] The Real then warns against the disbelievers: they will continue fighting you until they turn you back from your religion, if they can—but they cannot accomplish that. Whoever among you turns back from his religion and persists until he dies an unbeliever, his works become void in this world: he has no protected standing and no share in revenue or booty. In the Hereafter he sees no reward for them. Such people are inhabitants of the Fire, remaining there. The verse’s implication ( مفهوم الآية ) is that, if he returns before death, his work does not become void. This is al-Shāfiʿī’s position. Mālik says that the reward of everything he did becomes void; he repeats pilgrimage if it preceded his apostasy. His Islam is accepted if he returns. If he does not return, he is allowed three days and then put to death. [B151]","anchor":"en-q2-217-218-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-217-218-s3","r":"q2-217-218","title":"Hope is not an entitlement earned against God","text":"When the verse removing blame was revealed, they thought they had no reward for that fighting. The Real therefore revealed: those who believe, and those who emigrate and strive in God’s path, hope for God’s mercy—His reward. God is Forgiving towards them, Merciful to them, and does not waste their striving in this expedition. The relative expression is repeated to magnify the standing of emigration and struggle. He uses hope to indicate that work does not make reward obligatory: it is servanthood. The affair rests with God; He rewards if He wills and punishes if He wills. “He is not questioned about what He does, but they are questioned” [21:23].","anchor":"en-q2-217-218-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-217-218-s4","r":"q2-217-218","title":"The sanctity of a gathering and the danger of turning back","text":"The honour of a time or place is measured by the obedience to the King, the Requiter, that occurs in it. A time when the breezes of acceptance and turning towards God blow should not be a time of wrangling or fighting. This is the time of a gathering for remembrance or reminder, or sitting with the gnostics, possessors of the elixir. Bad comportment there is grave; preventing those who seek it from reaching it is a grave offence; barring hearts from the breaths of that presence is graver still. The brigands of this path never cease turning back those who wish truly to follow it. Yet no tyrant or obstinate person can turn from the Real one for whom divine support has preceded. One for whom deprivation preceded and abandonment was decreed turns back, even after direct vision. They recite: By God, we praise no unbridled one, whether drunk or sober; even if firmly set upon a swift journey, even if he drinks until effaced— not until he is cut down within the flock and turns with the turning of a millstone. [B152] Those who believe and affirm God’s path, leave behind their desires to please God, and struggle against their selves in love of God—those hope for God’s mercy. The Generous One will not disappoint them, for He is Forgiving, Merciful.","anchor":"en-q2-217-218-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-217-218-s5","r":"q2-217-218","title":"","text":"Wine was lawful at the beginning of Islam. People drank and traded in it, giving its proceeds and gambling winnings in charity. After commanding expenditure, the Real clarifies this, so that charity does not become a pretext for laxity in dealings.","anchor":"en-q2-217-218-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-219","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure 2:219","anchor":"unit-q2-219"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-1","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"يَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ قُلْ فِيهِما إِثْمٌ كَبِيرٌ وَمَنافِعُ لِلنَّاسِ وَإِثْمُهُما أَكْبَرُ مِنْ نَفْعِهِما ...","anchor":"ar-q2-219-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-2","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"قلت: الخمر في اللغة: ما يستر الشيء ويغطيه، ومنه: خمار المرأة، وسُمِّي الخمر خمراً لستره العقلَ. وفي الاصطلاح: ما غَيّب العقل دون الحواس مع النَّشْوة والطرَب. وقال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: «كُلُّ مُسْكِرٍ خَمْرٌ وكُلُّ خَمْرٍ حَرَامٌ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-219-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-3","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"والميسر: قال ابن عباس والحسن: كل قمار ميسر، من شطرنج ونرْد ونحوه، حتى لَعِب الصبيان بالجَوْز والكِعَاب، إذا كان بالفُلوس، وسمي ميسراً ليُسْر صاحبه بالمال الذي يأخذه، وأما إذا كان بغير عِوض، إنما هو لَعِبٍّ فقط، فلا بأس.","anchor":"ar-q2-219-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-4","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"قاله ابن عرفة.","anchor":"ar-q2-219-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-5","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ حكم الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ قُلْ لهم: فِيهِما إِثْمٌ كَبِيرٌ أي: عظيم لما فى الميسر من أكل أموال الناس بالباطل، وما ينشأ عنه من العداوة والشحناء، وما في الخمر من إذهاب العقل والسباب والافتراء والإذاية، والتعدّي الذي يكون من شاربه. وقرأ حمزة والكسائي: كثير بالمثلثة، أي: آثام كثيرة لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لَعَنَ اللهُ الخَمْرَ، وَبَائِعِهَا، وَمُبْتَاعَهَا، والمُشتَرَاة لَهُ، وعَاصَرَهَا، والمعصورة له،","anchor":"ar-q2-219-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-6","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"وسَاقِيها، وشَاربهَا، وحَامِلهَا، والْمْحمُولة لَهُ، وآكل ثَمِنِها» . فهذه آثام، وفيها مَنافِعُ لِلنَّاسِ أي: منافع دنيوية ككسب المال بلا تعب، وإطعام الفقراء من كسبه، كما كانت تصنع العرب في الميسر، وفى الخمرة اللذة والنشوة، كما قال حسان رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-219-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-7","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"ونَشْرَبُها فَتَتْرُكنا مُلوكاً ... وأُسداً لا يُنهْنِهُنا اللقَاءُ(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-219-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-8","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"وَإِثْمُهُما أَكْبَرُ مِنْ نَفْعِهِما لأن منفعتهما دنيوية، وعقوبة إثمهما أُخروية، وهذه الآية نزلت قبل التحريم.","anchor":"ar-q2-219-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-9","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"رُويَ أنه لمّا نزل بمكة قوله تعالى: وَمِنْ ثَمَراتِ النَّخِيلِ وَالْأَعْنابِ تَتَّخِذُونَ مِنْهُ سَكَراً وَرِزْقاً حَسَناً، أخذ المسلمون يشربونها، ثم إن عمرَ ومعاذاً في نفر من الصحابة، قالوا: أفْتنا يا رسول الله في الخمر فإنها مُذهبة للعقل، فنزلت هذه الآية، فشربها قوم وتركها آخرون، ثم دعا عبدُ الرحمن بن عوف ناساً إلى داره، فشربوا وسكروا، ثم قام يصلي بهم فقرأ: (قل يا أيها الكافرون أعبدُ ما تعبدون) من غير نفي، فنزلت: ... لاَ تَقْرَبُوا الصَّلاةَ وَأَنْتُمْ سُكارى ... فاجتنبُوها في أوقات الصلاة. ثم دعا عتبانُ بنُ مالك سعدَ بن أبي وقاص في جماعة، فلما سكروا افتخروا وتناشدوا، فأنشد سعدُ شعراً فيه هجاء الأنصار، فضربه أنصارى بلخى بعير فشجَّه، فشكى إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فقال عمر: اللهم بيِّن لنا في الخمر بياناً شافياً. فنزلت إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ ... إلى قوله ... فَهَلْ أَنْتُمْ مُنْتَهُونَ فقال عمر: قد انتهينا يا رب. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-219-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-10","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"ولما شربها بعض الناس بعد التحريم، كان- عليه الصلاة والسلام- يضرب فيها بالنعال والجريد، ضرباً غير محدود، وضرب أبو بكر وعمر أربعين، وأول من حد فيها ثمانين سيدنا عثمان(2) ، لما تهافت الناس فيها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-219-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-11","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الحق تعالى جعل للعقل نوراً يُميز بين الحق والباطل، بين الضار والنافع، وبين الصانع والمصنوع، ثم إن هذا النور قد يتغطى بالظلمة الطينية وهي نشوة الخمر الحسية. وقد يتغطى أيضاً بالأنوار الباهرة من الحضرة الأزلية إذا فاجأته، فيغيب عن الإحساس في مشاهدة الأنوار المعنوية، وهي أسرار الذات الأزلية، فلا يرى إلا أسرار المعاني القديمة، وينكر الحوادث الحسية، فسمي الصوفية هذه الغيبة خمرة لمشاركتها للخمر في غيبوبة العقل، وتغنوا بها في أشعارهم ومواجيدهم، قال ابن الفارض رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q2-219-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-12","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"شَرِبْنَا على ذِكْر الحبيبِ مُدامَةً ... سَكرنَا بها من قبل أن يُخلَقَ الكَرْمُ(3)","anchor":"ar-q2-219-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-13","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"ثم قال:","anchor":"ar-q2-219-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-14","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"علَى نَفْسِه فَليبْكِ مَن ضاعَ عُمْرُه ... وليسَ لهُ مِنْها نَصِيبٌ ولا سَهْمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-219-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-15","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"وقلت في عينيتي:","anchor":"ar-q2-219-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-16","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"وَلِي لَوْعَةٌ بالرَّاحِ إِذْ فِيه رَاحِتِي ... وَرَوْحِي ورَيْحَانِي، وخيرٌ واسِعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-219-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-17","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"سَكرْنَا فهِمْنَا في بَهاءِ جَمَالِه ... فَغِبْنا عَن الإحساسِ، والنُورُ ساطعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-219-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-18","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"والميسر في طريق الإشارة: هو الغني الذي يحصل بهذه الخمرة، وهو الغني بالله عن كل ما سواه، (قل فيهما إثم كبير) أي: في تعاطيهما حرج كبير، ومنافع للناس بعد تعاطيهما، فيهما إثم كبير عند طالب الأجور، ومنافع للناس لمن طلب الحضور ورفع الستور. وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-219-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-19","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"لَوْ كَان لي مسعد بالراح يُسعِدُني ... لمَا انتظرتُ لشُربِ الراحِ إفطارا","anchor":"ar-q2-219-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-20","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"فالراحُ شيءٌ شَريفٌ أنتَ شَاربُه، ... فاشْرَب، ولو حَمَّلَتْكَ الراحُ أوْزارا","anchor":"ar-q2-219-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-21","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"يا مَنْ يلومُ على صَهْبَاءَ(1) صافيةٍ ... خُذ الجِنَانَ، ودَعْنِي أَسكنُ النَارا","anchor":"ar-q2-219-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-22","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"وقال ابن الفارض:","anchor":"ar-q2-219-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-23","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"وقالُوا: شَرِبْتَ الإثَم! كلاّ، وإنما ... شرِبْتُ التي في ترْكِها عنديَ الإثْمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-219-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-24","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"وقال آخر(2) :","anchor":"ar-q2-219-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-25","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"طابَ شُرْبُ المُدامِ في الخَلَواتْ ... اسْقِني يا نديمُ بالآنِيَاتْ","anchor":"ar-q2-219-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-26","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"خْمْرَةٌ تركُها علينا حرَامٌ، ... ليسَ فيها إثمٌ ولا شُبُهَاتْ","anchor":"ar-q2-219-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-27","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"عُتِّقَتْ في الدَّنان مِنْ قَبْلِ آدمْ ... أصلُها طيّبٌ من الطَّيِّبَاتْ","anchor":"ar-q2-219-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-28","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"أَفْتِ لي أيُّها الفقيهُ وقلْ لي: ... هل يجوزُ شُرْبُها على عَرَفاتْ؟","anchor":"ar-q2-219-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-29","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"فيهما إثم كبير عند أهل الحجاب، ونفع كبير عند ذوي الألباب، يعني: في الخمرة الأزلية والغنى بالله. وقوله تعالى: (وإثمهما أكبر من نفعهما) : خطاب على قدر ما يفهم الناس لأن إثمهما ظاهر للعوام، وهو ما يظهر على","anchor":"ar-q2-219-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-30","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"النشوان من خراب الظاهر، وصدور الأحوال الغريبة، ونفعهما خاص عند خواص الخواص، لا يفهمه إلا الخواص، بل يجب كتمه عن غير أهله. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-219-30"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-31","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"ثم وقع سؤال ثالث عن قدر المنفق، فأشار إليه الحقّ جل جلاله بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-219-31"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-219-32","r":"q2-219","title":"2:219 · Wine, gambling and the measure of expenditure","text":"... وَيَسْئَلُونَكَ مَاذَا يُنْفِقُونَ قُلِ الْعَفْوَ كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمُ الْآياتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ (219)","anchor":"ar-q2-219-32"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-219-s1","r":"q2-219","title":"What wine and gambling denote","text":"I say: in language, khamr ( الخمر ) is what conceals and covers something; from this comes a woman’s head-covering ( خمار ). Wine is called khamr because it covers the intellect. In technical usage, it is what makes the intellect absent, without eliminating the senses, together with exhilaration and delight. God’s Messenger said: “Every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is forbidden.” Concerning maysir ( الميسر ), Ibn ʿAbbās and al-Ḥasan said: every form of gambling is maysir , whether chess, backgammon or the like, even children’s games with nuts and knucklebones when money is staked. It is named maysir because of the player’s ease or enrichment ( يُسر ) through the money he takes. When there is no payment and it is merely play, however, there is no harm. Ibn ʿArafa states this. [B153] [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-10] ]","anchor":"en-q2-219-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-219-s2","r":"q2-219","title":"Benefits outweighed by sin","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: they ask you about the ruling on wine and gambling. Tell them: in them is great sin. Gambling involves consuming people’s wealth wrongfully and causes hostility and rancour. Wine removes intellect and leads to abuse, slander, injury and aggression from its drinker. Ḥamza and al-Kisāʾī read kathīr , with the three-dotted letter, “much” rather than kabīr , “great”: many sins. For the Prophet said: “God curses wine, its seller, its buyer, the person for whom it is bought, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its server, its drinker, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried and the consumer of its price.” These are sins. In them are benefits for people: worldly benefits such as acquiring money without toil and feeding the poor from the proceeds, as the Arabs did with gambling. Wine offers pleasure and exhilaration, as Ḥassān, God be pleased with him, says: We drink it, and it leaves us kings, and lions whom no encounter holds in check. Their sin is greater than their benefit, because their benefit is worldly, while the punishment for their sin belongs to the Hereafter. This verse was revealed before prohibition.","anchor":"en-q2-219-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-219-s3","r":"q2-219","title":"The stages of prohibition","text":"It is related that, when His saying was revealed in Mecca, “From the fruits of date-palms and vines you take intoxicant and good provision” [16:67], Muslims drank it. Then ʿUmar, Muʿādh and a group of Companions said: “Give us a ruling on wine, Messenger of God: it removes the intellect.” This verse was revealed. Some drank and others abstained. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf then invited people to his home. They drank and became intoxicated. He stood to lead them in prayer and recited: “Say, unbelievers, I worship what you worship,” without the negation. “Do not approach prayer while intoxicated” [4:43] was then revealed, and they avoided it at prayer times. ʿItbān ibn Mālik then invited Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ with a group. When intoxicated, they boasted and recited poetry to one another. Saʿd recited a poem satirizing the Helpers. A Helper struck him with a camel’s jawbone and wounded his head. He complained to God’s Messenger. ʿUmar said: “O God, give us a conclusive explanation concerning wine.” Then “Wine and gambling…” was revealed through “Will you then desist?” [5:90–91]. ʿUmar said: “We have desisted, our Lord.” End of report. When some people drank after the prohibition, the Prophet would strike them with sandals and palm stalks, without a fixed number of blows. Abū Bakr and ʿUmar gave forty. The first to prescribe eighty was our master ʿUthmān, when people rushed into drinking. And God Most High knows best. [B154]","anchor":"en-q2-219-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-219-s4","r":"q2-219","title":"The intellect covered by darkness or overwhelmed by light","text":"Know that the Real has given the intellect a light by which to distinguish truth from falsehood, harmful from beneficial, and Maker from made. This light may be covered by the darkness of clay: the intoxication of sensible wine. It may also be covered by dazzling lights from the Eternal Presence when they take it suddenly. It then becomes absent from sensory perception in witnessing inward lights, which are the mysteries of the Eternal Essence. It sees only the mysteries of eternal meanings and denies sensory, originated things. The Sufis call this absence “wine” because it shares with wine the intellect’s absence. They sing of it in their poems and ecstasies. [B155] Ibn al-Fāriḍ, God be pleased with him, says: We drank a wine in remembrance of the Beloved; with it we were drunk before the vine was created. He then says: Let him weep for himself whose life is lost, having no portion or share of it. I said in my poem rhyming in ʿayn : I burn with longing for the wine: in it are my rest, my refreshment, my sweet fragrance and abundant good. We grew drunk, then wandered in His beauty’s splendour; we vanished from sensation, while the light shone bright. In the mode of spiritual allusion, gambling is the wealth acquired through this wine: being rich through God, free of need for all other than Him ( الغنى بالله ). “Say: in them is great sin”: undertaking them entails great difficulty, yet there are benefits for people after undertaking them. In them is great sin for one who seeks wages, and benefits for people who seek presence and the lifting of veils. They recite: Had I a helper who would aid me with the wine, I would not wait for fast-breaking before drinking. Wine is a noble thing for you to drink; drink, though wine should load you with burdens. You who blame me for a pure red wine, take the gardens, and leave me to dwell in the fire. Ibn al-Fāriḍ says: They said: “You drank sin!” No: I drank that whose abandonment, to me, is sin. Another says: Sweet is the drinking of wine in solitude; cup-companion, give me drink in vessels. A wine whose abandonment is forbidden us, with neither sin nor doubtful thing within it; aged in jars before Adam, its origin good, among good things. Give me a ruling, jurist, and tell me: may it be drunk upon ʿArafāt? In them is great sin in the eyes of the veiled, and great benefit for possessors of understanding—meaning eternal wine and richness through God. “Their sin is greater than their benefit” addresses people according to their understanding. Their sin is apparent to ordinary people: what appears upon the intoxicated person of a ruined exterior and strange states. Their benefit is particular to the elect of the elect. Only the elect understand it; indeed, it must be concealed from those unqualified for it. And success is through God, who guides to the right way. A third question then arose concerning how much should be spent. The Real indicates it: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:219b وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ مَاذَا يُنْفِقُونَ قُلِ الْعَفْوَ كَذَلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمُ الْآيَاتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ They ask you what they should spend. Say, “What can be spared.” Thus God makes the signs clear to you, so that you may reflect.","anchor":"en-q2-219-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-219-s5","r":"q2-219","title":"What is easy to give, according to the giver","text":"I say: ʿafw ( العفو ) is the opposite of strain: what is easy. Easy ground is called ʿafw . The intention is to spend what can readily be given without going to the point of hardship. Grammatically it is a predicate or object ( خبر أو مفعول ): “it is what can be spared,” or “they spend what can be spared.” The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: they ask you what amount they should spend. Tell them: what can be spared, easily given without hardship or harm to the giver through its loss. It is related that a man came to the Prophet with gold the size of an egg and said: “Take it from me as charity.” The Prophet turned away until the man repeated his request several times. Angrily he said, “Bring it,” and threw it back so forcefully that it would have wounded him had it struck him. He said: “One of you brings all his wealth as charity and then sits begging from people! Charity should be given from a position of sufficiency.” Al-Bayḍāwī relates this in abbreviated form. I say: this differs according to certainty. The Truthful One, God be pleased with him, gave all his wealth, and ʿUmar gave half. The Prophet approved both while rejecting another person’s action. This shows that what can be spared differs between people according to their certainty. [B156] Thus God makes the signs clear to you: with an explanation like this, He explains the signs without leaving you perplexity or illusion, so that you may reflect with your intellects and adopt what returns benefit to you. Thus you reflect—","anchor":"en-q2-219-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-220","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans 2:220","anchor":"unit-q2-220"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-1","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-220-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-2","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"قلت: (العفو) : ضد الجهد، وهو السهل، ويقال للأرض السهلة: عفو، والمراد: أن يُنفق ما تيسر بذله، ولا يبلغ به الجَهد، وهو خبر، أو مفعول، أي: هو العفو، أو ينفقون العفو.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-3","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَيَسْئَلُونَكَ ما القدر الذي ينفقونه؟ قُلْ لهم: هو الْعَفْوَ أي: السهل الذي لا مشقة في إعطائه، ولا ضرر على المعطي في فقده، رُوِي أن رجلاً أتى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بقدر بَيْضة من الذهب، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-220-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-4","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"خُذها عني صَدقَة، فأعرض عنه، حتى كَرَّر مِرَاراً، فقال: هاتها، مُغْضَبَا، فحذفها حذفاً لو أصابه لشجَّه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-220-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-5","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"«يأتي أحدكم بماله كله يتصدّق به، ويجلس يتكفَّفُ الناس، إنما الصدقةُ عن ظَهْرِ غِنَى» . قاله البيضاوي مختصراً.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-6","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"قلت: وهذا يختلف باختلاف اليقين فقد تصدّق الصدّيق رضي الله عنه بماله كله، وعمر رضي الله عنه بنصف ماله، فأقرهما، ورَدّ فعلَ غيرهما، فدلَّ ذلك على أن العفو يختلف باختلاف الأشخاص، على حسب اليقين.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-7","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمُ الْآياتِ أي: مثل هذا التبيين الذي ذكرنا، (يُبين) لكم الآيات، حتى لا يترك لكم إشكالاً ولا وهماً، لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ بعقولكم، وتأخذون بما يعود نفعه عليكم، فتتفكرون","anchor":"ar-q2-220-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-9","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"فِي الدُّنْيا وسرعة ذهابها وتقلبها بأهلها، إذا أقبلت كانت فتنة، وإذا أدبرت كانت حسرة، لا يفي طالبُها بمقصوده منها ولو ملكها بحذافيرها، ضيقة الزمان والمكان، عمارتها إلى الخراب، وشأنها إلى انقلاب، سريعة الزوال، وشيكة الانتقال، فتزهدون فيها وترفعون همتكم عنها.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-10","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"وفى الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «مَالِي وللدُّنْيَا، إِنَّما مَثَلي ومثلُ الدنيا كرجلٍ سَافَرَ في يَوْمٍ صَائِفٍ، فاسْتَظَلَّ تَحْتَ شَجَرةٍ، ثم رَاحَ وَتَرَكَها» . وفي صُحف إبراهيم عليه السلام: «عجبت لمَن أيقن بالموت كيف يفرح، عجبت لمَن أيقن بالنار كيف يضحك، عجبت لمَن أيقن بالقدر كيف ينصب- أي: يتعب- عجبت لمَن رأى الدنيا وتقلُّبها بأهلها كيف يطمئن إليها» . وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-220-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-11","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"أَلاَ إنَّما الدنيا كأحْلاَمِ نَائِم ... وكُلُّ نعيمٍ ليسَ فيها بِدَائِم","anchor":"ar-q2-220-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-12","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"تَذَكَّرْ إذَا ما نِلْتَ بالأمْسِ لَذَّةً ... فأفْنَيْتَها هَلْ أنتَ إلا كَحَالِمِ","anchor":"ar-q2-220-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-13","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"وتتفكرون في (الآخرة) ودوام نعيمها، وسعة فضائها، وبهجة منظرها فترغبون في الوصول إليها، وتتأهبون للقائها، فتؤثرونها على هذه الدار الفانية. قال بعض الحكماء: لو كانت الدنيا من ذهب يفنى، والآخرة من طين يبقى، لكان ينبغي للعاقل أن يختار ما يبقى على ما يفنى، لا سيما والأمر بالعكس، الدنيا من طين يفنى، والآخرة من ذهب يبقى، فلا يختار هذه الدار إلاَّ أحمق خسيس الهمة، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-14","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"الإشارة: كما نهى الحقّ جلّ جلاله عن السرف فى الأموال، نهى عن السرف في الأحوال، فالسرف، من حيث هو، يؤدي إلى الملل والانقطاع، «أحبُ العملِ إلى اللهِ ما دَامَ عليه صاحبُه، وإنْ قَلَ» كما في الحديث، والله ما رأينا أحداً أسرف في الأحوال إلا مَلَّ، وضعف حاله، وفي الحديث: «لاَ يكْن أحَدُكُم كالمُنْبَتِّ- أي: المنقطع- لا أرضا قطع، ولا ظَهْراً أبقى» . وقال في المباحث:","anchor":"ar-q2-220-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-15","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"فاحْتلْ عَلَى النَّفْسِ فَرُبَّ حِيله ... أنفعُ في النُّصْرة مِن قَبِيله","anchor":"ar-q2-220-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-16","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"فلا يزال يُسايس نفسه شيئاً فشيئاً حتى يملكها، ويظفر بها، فإذا ظفر بها كانت له شبكة يصطاد بها العلوم والمعارف، فتتفكر في الدنيا فتراها فانية فترحل عنها، ثم تتفكر في الآخرة فتراها باقية، فإذا رامت السُّكْنَى فيها رأتْها كَوْناً مخلوقاً فرحلت إلى خالقها، فكشف الحقّ عنها الحجاب، وأدخلها مع الأحباب، فغابت عن الكونين في شهود المكون، فلم يبق لها دنيا ولا آخرة، بل هي الآن في بهجة ونضرة (إلى ربها ناظرة) ، حققنا الله بهذا المقام العلي. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-17","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"ثم سألوا أيضاً عن مخالطة اليتامى، فأجابهم الحقّ تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-220-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-18","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"... وَيَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْيَتامى قُلْ إِصْلاحٌ لَهُمْ خَيْرٌ وَإِنْ تُخالِطُوهُمْ فَإِخْوانُكُمْ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ الْمُفْسِدَ مِنَ الْمُصْلِحِ وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَأَعْنَتَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ (220)","anchor":"ar-q2-220-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-19","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"قلت: العنت: التعب والمشقة، أعنتكم: أتعبكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-20","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَيَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ مخالطة الْيَتامى أي: خَلْط مال اليتامى بمال الوصيّ، أو القائم به، فيأكلون جميعاً، قُلْ لهم: يفعلون ما هو إِصْلاحٌ لليتيم وأحفظ لماله، فإنْ كان خلط مال اليتيم مع","anchor":"ar-q2-220-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-21","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"مال الوصي أحفظُ لماله، وأوفر، فهو خير، فإنما هم إخوانكم في الدين، وإن كان عزل مالهم عن مالكم، وأكله وحده، أوفر لماله، فاعتزالهم خير، وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ من قصدُه الإفساد، ممن قصده الإصلاح، فيعامل كل واحد بقصده، وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لأمركم بعزلهم وحفظ مالهم مطلقاً، فيُحرجكم، ويشق عليكم، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ غالب، لا يُعجزه شيء، حَكِيمٌ لا يفعل شيئاً إلا لحكمة ومصلحة.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-22","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"ولمّا نزل قوله تعالى: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ أَمْوالَ الْيَتامى ظُلْماً ... الآية، تحرَّج الصحابة من مخالطة اليتامى، فسألوا رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-23","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن لا شيخ له في طريق القوم فهو يتيم، لا أبَ له، فإن ادعى شيئاً من الخصوصية سُمي عندهم لقيطاً أو دعياً، أي: منسوباً إلى غير أبيه، وما زالت الأشياخ تُحذِّر من مخالطة العوام، ومن مخالطة المتفقرة الجاهلة، أعني: الذين لا شيخ لهم يصلح للتربية، حتى قالوا: مخالطتهم سُم قاتل. وقال بعضهم: يجتنب المريد مخالطة ثلاثة أصناف من الناس: المتفقرة الجاهلين، والقراء المداهنين، والجبابرة المتكبرين.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-24","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"قلت: وكذلك الفروعية المتجمدين على ظاهر الشريعة، فصُحبتهم أقبحُ من الجميع، ومن ابتلى بمخالطة العوام فلينصحهم، ويرشدهم إلى مصالح دينهم، إنما هم إخوان في الدين، والله يعلم المفسد من المصلح، فمن خالطهم طمعاً في مالهم أو جاههم، أفسده الله، ومن خالطهم نُصحاً وإرشاداً أصلحه الله، ولو شاء الله لأمر الفقراء باعتزالهم بالكلية، وفي ذلك حرج ومشقة، ومِنْ حكمته تعالى أن جعلهم حجاباً لأهل الحجاب، ومدخلاً لذوي الألباب، حجاباً للضعفاء، ومدخلاً ومشهداً للأقوياء، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-220-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-220-25","r":"q2-220","title":"2:220 · Reflection upon the two abodes and care for orphans","text":"ولما فرغ الحق جل جلاله من ذكر بعضَ أمر الجهاد وما يتعلق به، شَرَع يتكلم على النكاح، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-220-25"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-220-s1","r":"q2-220","title":"The world’s passing and the Hereafter’s permanence","text":"—upon this world, how quickly it passes and changes for its people. When it approaches it is a trial; when it departs it is regret. Its seeker never fulfils his purpose in it, even if he possesses it entirely. Constricted in time and place, its prosperity ends in ruin, its affairs in reversal. Swift to disappear and soon to depart: thus you renounce it and raise your aspiration above it. The Tradition relates that the Prophet said: “What have I to do with this world? My likeness in relation to it is that of a man travelling on a hot day who takes shade beneath a tree, then moves on and leaves it.” The scrolls of Abraham say: “I marvel at one certain of death: how does he rejoice? I marvel at one certain of the Fire: how does he laugh? I marvel at one certain of destiny: how does he toil? I marvel at one who sees the world and its changes for its people: how does he find repose in it?” [B157] They recite: This world is only a sleeper’s dreams; none of its delights abides. Remember a pleasure you enjoyed yesterday and exhausted: are you anything but one who dreamed? You reflect upon the Hereafter, its enduring bliss, spacious expanse and delightful prospect. You desire arrival there and prepare to meet it, preferring it to this perishing abode. A sage said: “Were this world gold that perishes and the Hereafter clay that remains, the intelligent person should choose what remains over what perishes. How much more when the truth is the reverse: this world is clay that perishes, the Hereafter gold that remains. Only a fool of base aspiration chooses this abode.” And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q2-220-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-220-s2","r":"q2-220","title":"Moderation in states and the ascent beyond both worlds","text":"Just as the Real forbids excess in wealth, He forbids excess in spiritual states ( الأحوال ). Excess, as such, leads to weariness and interruption. “The work most beloved to God is that in which its doer perseveres, though little,” as the Tradition says. By God, we have seen no one excessive in states who did not grow weary and whose state did not weaken. The Tradition says: “Let none of you be like the overdriven traveller: he neither covers the ground nor preserves his mount.” [B158] The Mabāḥith says: Use skilful means with the self: many a stratagem avails more for victory than a tribe. One continues to manage the self gently, little by little, until one masters and gains it. Once gained, it becomes a net for catching sciences and gnoses. It reflects upon this world, sees it passing and departs from it. Then it reflects upon the Hereafter and sees it enduring. When it seeks to settle there, however, it sees that the Hereafter too is a created existence, and travels to its Creator. The Real removes its veil and admits it among the beloved. It becomes absent from the two worlds in witnessing their Maker; neither world nor Hereafter remains for it. It is now in delight and radiance, “looking towards its Lord” [75:23]. May God establish us in this exalted station. Amen. They also asked about sharing life with orphans. The Real answered: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:220b وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْيَتَامَى قُلْ إِصْلَاحٌ لَهُمْ خَيْرٌ وَإِنْ تُخَالِطُوهُمْ فَإِخْوَانُكُمْ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ الْمُفْسِدَ مِنَ الْمُصْلِحِ وَلَوْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ لَأَعْنَتَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ They ask you about orphans. Say, “Setting their affairs right is best.” If you share your lives with them, they are your brethren. God knows the one who corrupts from the one who sets right. Had God willed, He would have burdened you. God is Mighty, Wise.","anchor":"en-q2-220-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-220-s3","r":"q2-220","title":"Managing an orphan’s property for the orphan’s benefit","text":"I say: ʿanat ( العنت ) is toil and hardship; “He would have burdened you” means made things hard for you. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: they ask you about mixing with orphans—combining an orphan’s property with that of the testamentary guardian or caretaker so that they eat together. Tell them: do what sets the orphan’s affairs right and better preserves the property. If mixing it with the guardian’s property better preserves it and leaves more of it, that is best: they are only your brethren in religion. If separating their property from yours and having them eat on their own preserves more, separation is best. God knows whose purpose is corruption and whose purpose is reform, and deals with each according to his intention. Had God willed, He would have commanded you to keep them separate and preserve their property without qualification, putting you in difficulty and hardship. God is Mighty, prevailing, nothing defeating Him; Wise, doing nothing except for wisdom and benefit. When His saying was revealed, “Those who consume orphans’ wealth wrongfully…” [4:10], the Companions felt distress about sharing life with orphans. They asked God’s Messenger and this verse was revealed.","anchor":"en-q2-220-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-220-s4","r":"q2-220","title":"Those without a guide and the intention governing association","text":"In the folk’s path, everyone without a shaykh is an orphan without a father. If he claims any spiritual election ( الخصوصية ), they call him a foundling or a claimant to someone other than his father. Shaykhs have continually warned against association with ordinary people and ignorant pretenders to spiritual poverty: those without a shaykh qualified to train them. They have even said: “Association with them is a deadly poison.” Someone said: “The disciple should avoid three kinds of people: ignorant pretenders to poverty, dissembling reciters and arrogant tyrants.” I say: likewise the specialists in legal branches who are frozen upon the outward form of the Sacred Law. Companionship with them is worse than with all the others. Whoever is tried with associating with ordinary people should counsel them and guide them towards their religious good: they are brethren in religion. God knows the corrupter from the reformer. Whoever associates with them coveting wealth or status, God corrupts; whoever associates to counsel and guide, God sets right. Had God willed, He would have commanded the spiritually poor to withdraw from them altogether, but this entails difficulty and hardship. In His wisdom, He makes them a veil for the veiled and an entrance for people of understanding: a veil for the weak, an entrance and place of witnessing for the strong. And God Most High knows best. [B159]","anchor":"en-q2-220-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-220-s5","r":"q2-220","title":"","text":"After completing some matters of fighting in His path and their associated questions, the Real begins discussing marriage.","anchor":"en-q2-220-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-221","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship 2:221","anchor":"unit-q2-221"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-221-1","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"وَلا تَنْكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكاتِ حَتَّى يُؤْمِنَّ وَلَأَمَةٌ مُؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ مُشْرِكَةٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ وَلا تُنْكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ حَتَّى يُؤْمِنُوا وَلَعَبْدٌ مُؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ مُشْرِكٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَكُمْ أُولئِكَ يَدْعُونَ إِلَى النَّارِ وَاللَّهُ يَدْعُوا إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ وَالْمَغْفِرَةِ بِإِذْنِهِ وَيُبَيِّنُ آياتِهِ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ (221)","anchor":"ar-q2-221-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-221-2","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"قلت: بدأ الحقّ جلّ جلاله بذكر محل النكاح، وسيأتي في سورة النساء تمامه في قوله: حُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ أُمَّهاتُكُمْ ... الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-221-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-221-3","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولا تتزوجوا النساء الْمُشْرِكاتِ حَتَّى يُؤْمِنَّ، ونكاحهن حرام، بخلاف الكتابيات، كما في سورة المائدة. ونكاح أمة سوداء مُؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ نكاح مُشْرِكَةٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ حُسناً وحسباً ومالاً، أو: ولامرأةٌ مؤمنة أمة كانت أو حُرة خَيْرٌ من مشركة إذ النساء كلهن إماء الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-221-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-221-4","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"رُوِيَ أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- بعث مَرْثَداً الغَنَوي إلى مكة ليُخرج منها نَاساً من المسلمين فأَتتْه امرأة يقال لها: عناق، وكان يهواها في الجاهلية- فقالت: ألا تخلو؟ فقال: إن الإسلام حال بيننا، فقالت: هل لك أنْ تتَزَوج بي؟ فقال: نعم، ولكن أستشير رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فاستشاره، فنزلت الآية. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-221-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-221-5","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"ولا تُزوجوا المشركين وليَّتَكم، وهو حرام مطلقاً إذ الرجال قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النسآء، ولا تَسلُّطَ للكافر على المسلمة، فلا تُنكحوهم حَتَّى يُؤْمِنُوا، وَلَعَبْدٌ أسود مملوك مُؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ مُشْرِكٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَكُمْ حسباً ومالاً إذ لا حسب مع الكفر. وإنما حرَّم نكاح أهل الكفر لأنهم يَدْعُونَ إِلَى الكفر، وهو سبب النَّارِ، والصحبة توجب عقد المحبة، والطباع تُسْرق، فلا يَؤمنُ جانب الكفر أن يغلب على الإيمان، وَاللَّهُ تعالى إنما يَدْعُوا إِلَى سبب الْمَغْفِرَةِ، والتطهير من لَوث الكفر والمعاصي بِإِذْنِهِ وقدرته، فلا يأمر إلا بما يقوى عقد الإيمان واليقين، ويُنهض إلى الطاعات، وهو صحبة أهل الإيمان واليقين، وَيُبَيِّنُ آياتِهِ الدالّة على جمع عباده إليه لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ فيها، ويتعظون بتذكيرها ووعظها.","anchor":"ar-q2-221-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-221-6","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"الإشارة: لا ينبغي للفقير أن يعقد مع نفسه عقد الصحبة والمودة، أو ينظر إليها بعين الشفقة والرحمة، ما دامت مشركة بشهود السّوى، أو مائلة بطبعها إلى الهوى، ولأن تكون عندك نفس مؤمنة بعلم التوحيد، خير من نفس مشركة برؤية الغير، ولو أعجبتك في الطاعة، وظهور الاستقامة، فقد تُظْهر الطاعة والخدمة، وتُبطن مالها فيها من الحظوظ والمتعة، فليتهمها ما دامت مشركة، فإذا آمنت ووحدت الله تعالى، فلم تر معه سواه، فلا بأس بعقد النكاح معها، فإنها لا تأمره إلا بما يقوي شهودها وتوحيدها. وكذلك لا ينبغي أن يعقد نكاح نفسه، ويدفعها لمن يشهد السّوى شيخاً أو أخاً، ولو أعجبك طاعته واجتهاده، ولأن تصحب جاهلاً لا يرضى عن نفسه، خير من أن تصحب عالماً يرضى عن نفسه، أولئك أهل النفوس- يدعون إلى نار الشهوات والحظوظ العاجلة أو الآجلة، والله يدعو إلى التطهير من شهود الأغيار، والدخول في حضرة الأسرار، وهذا لا يكون إلا للعارفين الأبرار الذين تطهروا من الأكدار، وتخلصوا من شهود الأغيار، كذلك يُبين الله آياته للناس- الدالّة على وحدانيته- لعلهم يتعظون فينزجرون عن متابعة الهوى، أو رؤية وجود السوى. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-221-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-221-7","r":"q2-221","title":"2:221 · Marriage, belief and the formation of companionship","text":"ولمَّا بيَّن الحقُ تعالى ما يحرم في النكاح أصالَةً، بيَّن ما يحرم فيه عروضا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-221-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-221-s1","r":"q2-221","title":"Whom one may marry","text":"I say: the Real begins by mentioning those eligible for marriage. The account will be completed in Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, in “Forbidden to you are your mothers…” [4:23]. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: do not marry women who associate others with God until they believe. Marriage to them is forbidden, unlike marriage to women of the Book, as in Sūrat al-Māʾida. Marrying a black believing slave woman is better than marrying an associating woman, though the latter please you in beauty, ancestry or wealth. Or the meaning is: a believing woman, enslaved or free, is better than an associating woman, since all women are God’s female servants. It is related that the Prophet sent Marthad al-Ghanawī to Mecca to bring out some Muslims. A woman called ʿAnāq, whom he had loved in the Age of Ignorance, came to him and asked: “Will you not be alone with me?” He replied: “Islam has come between us.” She asked: “Would you marry me?” He said: “Yes, but I must consult God’s Messenger.” He consulted him, and the verse was revealed. Al-Bayḍāwī relates this. [B160] Do not give women under your guardianship in marriage to associators. This is forbidden without qualification, since men have responsibility over women ( قوامون على النساء ), and an unbeliever is to have no authority over a Muslim woman. Do not therefore marry them to such men until they believe. A black, enslaved believer is better than an associator, though the latter please you in ancestry and wealth: no ancestry counts alongside unbelief. Marriage with the people of unbelief is forbidden because they invite to unbelief, which causes the Fire. Companionship binds affection, and dispositions are imperceptibly borrowed ( الطباع تُسرق ); one cannot be secure that unbelief will not prevail over faith. God invites to the cause of forgiveness and purification from the stain of unbelief and sins, by His leave and power. He commands only what strengthens the bond of faith and certainty and arouses obedience: companionship with people of faith and certainty. He makes clear His signs that indicate His gathering His servants to Him, so that they may take heed, benefiting from their reminder and admonition.","anchor":"en-q2-221-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-221-s2","r":"q2-221","title":"Do not befriend the self while it witnesses another","text":"The spiritually poor person should not contract companionship and affection with his own self, or look upon it with compassion and mercy, while it associates others by witnessing what is other ( شهود السوى ), or naturally inclines towards desire. To possess a self believing through knowledge of unity is better than to possess a self associating through seeing another, even though its obedience and manifest uprightness please you. It may display obedience and service while concealing its own interests and enjoyment in them. Suspect it while it remains associating. When it believes and realizes God’s unity, seeing no other with Him, there is no harm in contracting marriage with it: it commands only what strengthens its witnessing and realization of unity. Likewise, one should not contract the marriage of one’s self and hand it to someone who witnesses otherness, whether a shaykh or a brother, even though his obedience and exertion please you. To accompany an ignorant person dissatisfied with himself is better than to accompany a learned person satisfied with himself. Those—the people ruled by their selves—invite to the fire of desires and interests, immediate or deferred. God invites to purification from witnessing others and entry into the presence of mysteries. This is only attained by the righteous gnostics, purified of turbidities and freed from witnessing others. Thus God explains His signs of oneness to people so that they may take heed and refrain from following desire or seeing the existence of anything other. And success is through God, who guides to the right way.","anchor":"en-q2-221-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-221-s3","r":"q2-221","title":"","text":"Having explained what is forbidden in marriage in itself, the Real explains what is forbidden in it because of a passing condition.","anchor":"en-q2-221-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-222-223","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation 2:222–223","anchor":"unit-q2-222-223"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-1","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"وَيَسْئَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْمَحِيضِ قُلْ هُوَ أَذىً فَاعْتَزِلُوا النِّساءَ فِي الْمَحِيضِ وَلا تَقْرَبُوهُنَّ حَتَّى يَطْهُرْنَ فَإِذا تَطَهَّرْنَ فَأْتُوهُنَّ مِنْ حَيْثُ أَمَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ التَّوَّابِينَ وَيُحِبُّ الْمُتَطَهِّرِينَ (222) نِساؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ وَقَدِّمُوا لِأَنْفُسِكُمْ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ مُلاقُوهُ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ (223)","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-2","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"قلت: المحيض: مصدر، كالمقيل والمعيش والمجيء، وهو الحيض.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-3","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَيَسْئَلُونَكَ يا محمد عَنِ قرب النساء بالجماع في زمن الْمَحِيضِ، قُلْ لهم: هُوَ أَذىً، أي: مُضِرٍّ، أو مُنتن مستقذر، لا يَرضى ذو همة أن يقربه، فَاعْتَزِلُوا مجامعة النِّساءَ فِي زمن الْمَحِيضِ وَلا تَقْرَبُوهُنَّ بالجماع في المحل حَتَّى يَطْهُرْنَ من الدم، بانقطاعه، ويغتسلن بالماء، فَإِذا تَطَهَّرْنَ بالماء فَأْتُوهُنَّ مِنْ حَيْثُ أَمَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ وهو الفرج، الذي أمركم باجتنابه في الحيض إذ هو محل زراعة النطفة. فمن غلبته نفسه حتى وطئ في الحيض، أو النفاس، فليبادر إلى التوبة، إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ التَّوَّابِينَ كلما أذنبوا تابوا.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-4","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"ولا تجب كفارة على الواطئ، على المشهور. وقال ابن عباس والأوزاعي: (من وطئ قبل الغسل تصدق بنصف دينار، ومن وطئ في حال سيلان الدم تصدق بدينار) . رواه أبو داود حديثاً. ومن صبر وتنزَّه عن ذلك فإن الله يُحِبُّ الْمُتَطَهِّرِينَ من الذنوب والعيوب كلها، وإنما أعاد العامل لأن محبته للمتنزهين أكثر.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-5","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"قال البيضاوي: رُوِيَ أن أهل الجاهلية كانوا لا يُسَاكنون الحائض ولا يُؤاكلونها، كفعل اليهود والمجوس، واستمر ذلك إلى أنْ سأل أبو الدحْداح، في نفر من الصحابة، عن ذلك، فنزلت. ولعله سبحانه- إنما ذكر «يسألونك» من غير واو، ثلاثاً، ثم بها ثلاثاً لأن السؤالات الأُوَل كانت في أوقات متفرقة، والثلاثة الأخيرة كانت في وقت واحد فلذلك ذكرها بحرف الجمع. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-6","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"ثم بيَّن الحق تعالى كيفية إتيان النساء بعد الطُهر، فقال: نِساؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ، أي: مواضع حرثكم، شبه ما يلقى في أرحامهن من النطف، بالبذر، والأرحام أرض لها، فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أي: محل حرثكم، وهو الفرج، أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ أي: من أي جهة شئتم.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-7","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"رُوِيَ أن اليهود كانوا يقولون: مَنْ جامع امرأته مِنْ خَلْفهَا في قُبُلِهَا جَاء الولُد أَحْولَ، فذُكر ذلك لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فنزلت. وقيل: إنَّ قُريشاً كانوا يأتون النساء من قُدَّام، مستلقية، والأنصار كانوا يأتوهن من خلف، باركة، فتزوج رجل من المهاجرين امراة من الأنصار، فأراد أن يفعل عادته، فامتنعت، وأرادت عادتها، فاختصما إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلّم، فنزلت الآية بالتخيير للرجل، مع الإتيان في المحل. وأما الإتيان في الدُّبُر فحرام، ملعونٌ فاعله، وقال في القوت: فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ أي: في أي وقت شئتم، ومن أي مكان شئتم، مع اتحاد المحل. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-8","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"ثم حذر الحق تعالى من متابعة شهوة النساء، والغفلة عن الله، فقال: وَقَدِّمُوا لِأَنْفُسِكُمْ ما تجدون ثوابه مُدخراً عنده، وهو ذكر الله في مظان الغفلة، قيل: التسمية قبل الوطء وقيل: طلب الولد، والتحقيق: أنه الحضور مع الحق عند هيجان الشهوة، قال بعض العارفين: إني لا أغيب عن الله ولو في حالة الجماع. هـ. وهذا شأن أهل الجمع، لا يفترقون عن الحضرة ساعة. وهذه التقوى التي أمر الله بها بقوله: وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ أي: لا تغيبكم عنه شهوةُ النساء، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ مُلاقُوهُ فترون وبال الغفلة وجزاء اليقظة، وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ بالقرب من رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-9","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"الإشارة: إذا سُئلت- أيها العارف- عن النفس في حال جنابتها بالغفلة، وحال تلبسها بنجاسة حب الدنيا، فقل:","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-10","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"هي أذى، أي: قذر ونجس، من قَرُب منها لطَّخته بنجاستها، فلا يحل القرب منه، أو الصحبة معها، حتى تطهر من جنابة الغفلة باليقظة، ومن نجاسة حب الدنيا بالزهد، ورفع الهمة عنها، فإذا تطهرت فاتها، وردها إلى حضرة مولاها، كما أمرك الله، إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ التَّوَّابِينَ، وقد تابت ورجعت إلى مولاها، وَيُحِبُّ الْمُتَطَهِّرِينَ، وقد تطهرت من جنابة الغفلة، وتنزهت عن نجاسة الدنيا برفع الهمة، فصارت لك أرضاً لزراعة حقوق العبودية، ومَنْبَتا لبذر شهود عظمة الربوبية، فأتوا حرثكم- أيها العارفون- أنى شئتم، أي: ازرعوا في أرض نفوسكم من أوصاف العبودية ما شئتم، وفي أي وقت شئتم.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-11","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"فبقدر ما تزرعون من العبودية تحصدون من الحرية. وبقدر ما تزرع فيها من الذل تحصده من العز، وبقدر ما تزرع فيها من الفقر تحصده من الغنى، وبقدر ما تزرع فيها من التواضع تحصده من الشرف والرفعة.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-12","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"والحاصل: بقدر ما تزرع فيها من السفليات تحصد ضده من العلويات. قال تعالى: وَنُرِيدُ أَنْ نَمُنَّ عَلَى الَّذِينَ اسْتُضْعِفُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَنَجْعَلَهُمْ أَئِمَّةً وَنَجْعَلَهُمُ الْوارِثِينَ. وَنُمَكِّنَ لَهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ. فإذا تركتها هَمَلاً، أنبتت لك الشوك والحنظل. وَقَدِّمُوا لِأَنْفُسِكُمْ من أوصاف العبودية ما تجدونه أمامكم من مشاهدة الربوبية، واتقوا الله فلا تشهدوا معه سواه، واعلموا أنكم ملاقوه حين تغيبون عن وجودكم وتفقدونه، وبشر المؤمنين الموقنين بشهود رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-222-223-13","r":"q2-222-223","title":"2:222–223 · Menstruation, purification and the field of cultivation","text":"ولما تكلم الحق جل جلاله على بعض أحكام النكاح، أراد أن يتكلم على الإيلاء، وهو الحلف على عدم مس المرأة وجماعها، وقدّم على ذلك النهي عن كثرة الحلف لأنه هو السبب في الوقوع فى الإيلاء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-222-223-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-222-223-s1","r":"q2-222-223","title":"The interval of abstention and purification","text":"I say: maḥīḍ ( المحيض ) is a verbal noun ( مصدر ), like maqīl , maʿīsh and majīʾ , meaning menstruation. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: they ask you, Muḥammad, about approaching women through intercourse during menstruation. Tell them: it is a hurt—harmful, or offensive and repellent, something a person of high aspiration would not consent to approach. Abstain from intercourse with women during menstruation. Do not approach them through intercourse in its place until they become clean through the blood’s cessation and wash with water. When they have purified themselves with water, approach them where God has commanded you: the vagina, which He commanded you to avoid during menstruation, since it is the place where the seed is planted. Whoever is overcome by his self and has intercourse during menstruation or postnatal bleeding should hasten to repent. God loves those who repeatedly repent: whenever they sin, they repent. According to the well-known position, no expiation ( كفارة ) is obligatory upon the man. Ibn ʿAbbās and al-Awzāʿī said: “Whoever has intercourse before washing gives half a dinar in charity; whoever does so while the blood is flowing gives a dinar.” Abū Dāwūd transmits it as a Tradition. Whoever remains patient and keeps clear of this—God loves those who purify themselves from all sins and faults. He repeats the governing verb ( العامل ) because His love for those who keep clear is greater. [B161] Al-Bayḍāwī says: “It is related that the people of the Age of Ignorance would neither share a dwelling nor eat with a menstruating woman, like the Jews and Magians. This continued until Abū al-Daḥdāḥ and a group of Companions asked about it, and the verse was revealed. Perhaps He mentions ‘they ask you’ three times without wāw , then three times with it, because the first questions occurred at separate times and the final three at one time; He therefore mentions the latter with the conjunction of combination.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q2-222-223-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-222-223-s2","r":"q2-222-223","title":"The field and the permitted place","text":"The Real then explains how to approach women after purification: your wives are a field for you—the place of your cultivation. He compares the drops of seed cast into their wombs to seed, and the wombs to its soil. Approach your field, the place of cultivation, namely the vagina, as you will: from whichever direction you will. It is related that the Jews used to say: whoever approaches his wife from behind into her vagina will have a cross-eyed child. This was mentioned to God’s Messenger, and the verse was revealed. It is also said that Quraysh approached women from in front, lying on their backs, while the Helpers approached them from behind, kneeling. An Emigrant married a woman of the Helpers and wished to follow his custom, but she refused and wished to follow hers. They brought their disagreement to God’s Messenger. The verse was revealed, giving the man a choice, provided he approached the proper place. Anal intercourse is forbidden, and its doer is cursed. The Qūt says: “Approach your field as you will: at whatever time and from whichever place you will, while the place [of intercourse] remains one.” End of quotation. [B162]","anchor":"en-q2-222-223-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-222-223-s3","r":"q2-222-223","title":"Presence at a moment of desire","text":"The Real then warns against following sexual appetite and forgetting God: send ahead for yourselves what you will find stored with Him in reward—remembrance of God at the places where heedlessness is likely. It is said to mean invoking God’s Name before intercourse; or seeking a child. The precise realization is presence with the Real when desire surges. A gnostic said: “I do not become absent from God even during intercourse.” End of quotation. This is the state of the people of gathering ( أهل الجمع ): they do not separate from the Presence for an hour. This is the Godfearingness commanded in “Fear God”: let not desire for women make you absent from Him. Know that you will meet Him and see heedlessness’s evil consequence and wakefulness’s reward. Give believers good news of nearness to the Lord of the worlds.","anchor":"en-q2-222-223-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-222-223-s4","r":"q2-222-223","title":"Cultivating servanthood in the purified self","text":"If you, gnostic, are asked about the self in its state of major impurity through heedlessness ( جنابة الغفلة ), clothed in the impurity of worldly love, say: it is a hurt, filth and impurity. Whoever approaches it is stained by it. Approaching it or keeping its companionship is not lawful until it is purified from heedlessness’s major impurity through wakefulness, and from worldly love’s impurity through renunciation and raising aspiration above it. When it is purified, approach it and return it to its Master’s presence as God has commanded you. God loves those who repeatedly repent: it has repented and returned to its Master. He loves those who purify themselves: it has cleansed itself of heedlessness’s major impurity and kept clear of the world’s impurity by raising aspiration. It has become for you soil in which to cultivate servanthood’s duties and a place to plant the seed of witnessing Lordship’s greatness. Approach your field, gnostics, as you will: plant in the soil of your selves whatever attributes of servanthood you will, whenever you will. In proportion to the servanthood you plant, you harvest freedom ( الحرية ). In proportion to the abasement you plant, you harvest might; to the poverty you plant, wealth; to the humility you plant, honour and elevation. In sum, in proportion to what you plant of lower qualities, you harvest their higher opposites. He says: “We wished to favour those oppressed in the land, to make them leaders and inheritors, and establish them in the land” [28:5–6]. Leave the self untended and it grows thorns and bitter colocynth for you. Send ahead for yourselves attributes of servanthood whose fruit you will find before you in witnessing Lordship. Fear God: witness none other with Him. Know that you will meet Him when you become absent from your existence and lose it. Give believers, certain in faith, good news of witnessing the Lord of the worlds.","anchor":"en-q2-222-223-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-222-223-s5","r":"q2-222-223","title":"","text":"After discussing some marriage rulings, the Real turns to the oath of abstention ( الإيلاء ): swearing not to touch one’s wife or have intercourse with her. He first prohibits frequent swearing, since it causes people to fall into such oaths.","anchor":"en-q2-222-223-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-224-225","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention 2:224–225","anchor":"unit-q2-224-225"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-1","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"وَلا تَجْعَلُوا اللَّهَ عُرْضَةً لِأَيْمانِكُمْ أَنْ تَبَرُّوا وَتَتَّقُوا وَتُصْلِحُوا بَيْنَ النَّاسِ وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ (224) لا يُؤاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمانِكُمْ وَلكِنْ يُؤاخِذُكُمْ بِما كَسَبَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ (225)","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-2","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"قل: العرضة: فُعلة، بمعنى مفعولة: أي: معرضاً منصوباً، لأيمانكم تحلفون به كثيراً، فيصير اسم الجلالة مبتذلاً بينكم. و (أن تبروا) : مفعول من أجله.","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-3","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلا تَجْعَلُوا اللَّهَ أي: اسم الجلالة، معرضاً لِأَيْمانِكُمْ، فتتبذلونه بكثرة الحلف، فتمتنعون من فعل الخير بسبب الحلف، كراهة أَنْ تَبَرُّوا أي: تفعلوا فعل البر، وهو الإحسان، وكراهة أن تَتَّقُوا أن تجعلوا بينكم وبين الله وقاية بفعل المعروف، وذلك أن يحلف الرجل ألا يصل رحمه، أو لا يسلم على فلان، أو لا يضمن أحداً، أو لا يبيع بدين، أو لا يسلف أحداً، أو لا يتصدق، فهذه الأمور كلها بر وتقوى، نهى الله تعالى عن الحلف على عدم فعلها، أو يحلف ألا يصلح بين الناس، فيجب على الحالف على ذلك أن يحنث، ويكفر عن يمينه. ولذلك قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «إنِّي لأَحْلِفُ عَلَى يَمِينٍ فَأَرَى خيْراً منْهَا، فأكفر عن يميني، وآتي الَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ» . وقال لابن سَمُرَة: «إذا حَلَفْتَ عَلَى يَمِينٍ، فَرأيْتَ غَيرهَا خَيْراً مِنْهَا، فاتِ الَّذِي هُوَ خَيْرٌ، وَكَفّرْ عَنْ يمِينِك» .","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-4","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"أو يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلا تَجْعَلُوا اللَّهَ معرضا لأيمانكم، تحلفون به كثيراً، نهيتكم عن ذلك، إرَادَةَ أنْ تكونوا أبراراً متقين، مصلحين بَيْنَ النَّاسِ فإن الحالف مجترئ على الله، والمجترئ لا يكون برّاً متقياً، ولا موثوقاً به في إصلاح ذات البين، وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ لأيمانكم، عَلِيمٌ بنياتكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-5","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"ثم رفع الحق تعالى الحرج عن يمين اللغو الذي لا قصد فيه- فقال: لا يُؤاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمانِكُمْ، وهو ما يجري على اللسان من غير قصد، كقول الرجل في مجرى كلامه: لا والله وبلى والله، قاله ابن عباس وعائشة- رضي الله عنهما-، وبه قال الشافعي.","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-6","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"وقال أبو هريرة والحسنُ وابنُ عباس- في أحد قوليه-: هو أن يحلف على ما يعتقد فيظهر خلافه. وبه قال مالك رضي الله عنه، والأول ألْيَق بقوله تعالى: وَلكِنْ يُؤاخِذُكُمْ بِما كَسَبَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ أي: بما عقدت عليه قلوبكم، وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ حيث لم يؤاخذكم باللغو، حَلِيمٌ حيث لم يعجل بالمؤاخذة على يمين الجدّ، تربصاً للتوبة.","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-7","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لا تَجْعَلُوا اللَّهَ عُرْضَةً لِأَيْمانِكُمْ، ولكن اجعلوه عرضة لتعظيم قلوبكم ومشاهدة لأسراركم، فإني ما أظهرت اسمي لتبتذلوه في الأيمان والجدال، وإنما أظهرت اسمي لتتلقَّوْه بالتعظيم والإجلال، فمن عظَّم اسمي فقد عظَّم ذاتي، ومن عظم ذاتي جعلته عظيماً في أرضي وعند أهل سمواتي، وجعلته برّاً تقيّاً، من أهل محبتي وودادي، وداعياً يدعو إلى معرفتي، ويصلح بيني وبين عبادي، فمن حلمي ورأفتي: أني لا أؤاخذ بما يجري على اللسان، وإنما أؤاخذ بما يقصده الجَنَان.","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-8","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"تنبيه: كثرة الحلف مذموم يدل على الخفة والطيش، وعدم الحلف بالكلية تعسف، وخيرُ الأمور أوسطها، كان عليه الصلاة والسلام يحلف في بعض أحيانه، يقول: «لاَ وَمُقَلِّبِ الْقُلُوبِ» ،: «والذي نفس محمد بيده» .","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-9","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-224-225-10","r":"q2-224-225","title":"2:224–225 · Oaths, doing good and the heart’s intention","text":"ثم أشار الحق تعالى إلى حكم الإيلاء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-224-225-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-224-225-s1","r":"q2-224-225","title":"Making the divine Name a target for oaths","text":"I say: ʿurḍa ( عُرضة ) is on the pattern fuʿla with the sense of the passive participle ( مفعولة ): something exposed and set up for your oaths. You swear by Him frequently until the Name of Majesty becomes commonplace among you. “That you do good” ( أن تبروا ) is an accusative of purpose or cause ( مفعول من أجله ).","anchor":"en-q2-224-225-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-224-225-s2","r":"q2-224-225","title":"Breaking an oath to do what is better","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: do not expose God—that is, the Name of Majesty—to your oaths, making it commonplace through frequent swearing. You then refrain from good because of an oath, out of aversion to doing good—that is, beneficence—or to fearing God by placing a protection between yourselves and Him through right action. A man might swear not to maintain kinship, greet someone, guarantee anyone, sell on credit, lend, or give charity. All these are goodness and Godfearingness; God forbids swearing not to do them. Or someone swears not to reconcile people: such a swearer must break his oath and expiate it. Hence the Prophet said: “I swear an oath, then see something better than it, so I expiate my oath and do what is better.” He told Ibn Samura: “When you swear an oath and see something else better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath.” Or the Real says: do not expose God to your oaths by swearing by Him often. I prohibit this so that you may be good, Godfearing people who reconcile others. The habitual swearer is presumptuous towards God. One presumptuous towards Him is neither good and Godfearing nor trustworthy in reconciling people. God hears your oaths and knows your intentions.","anchor":"en-q2-224-225-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-224-225-s3","r":"q2-224-225","title":"Two explanations of inadvertent oaths","text":"The Real then removes difficulty concerning the inadvertent oath ( يمين اللغو ), which lacks intention: God does not take you to task for inadvertence in your oaths. It is what passes upon the tongue without purpose, as when a man says in ordinary speech, “No, by God,” or “Yes, by God.” Ibn ʿAbbās and ʿĀʾisha, God be pleased with them, explain it thus, and al-Shāfiʿī adopts this position. Abū Hurayra, al-Ḥasan and Ibn ʿAbbās, in one of his two positions, say: it is swearing to what one believes, then discovering the contrary. Mālik adopts this position. The first better suits His saying: “But He takes you to task for what your hearts have earned”—what your hearts have firmly resolved. God is Forgiving in not taking you to task for inadvertence, Forbearing in not hastening to punish deliberate oaths, allowing time for repentance. [B163]","anchor":"en-q2-224-225-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-224-225-s4","r":"q2-224-225","title":"The Name received with reverence","text":"The Real says: do not make God a target for your oaths. Make Him instead the object of your hearts’ reverence and your secrets’ witnessing. I did not manifest My Name so that you would make it commonplace in oaths and disputes. I manifested it so that you would receive it with reverence and awe. Whoever reveres My Name reveres My Essence. Whoever reveres My Essence, I make great in My earth and among the inhabitants of My heavens. I make him good and Godfearing, one of the people of My love and affection, a caller who invites to knowledge of Me and sets right the relation between Me and My servants. Of My forbearance and tenderness is that I do not take to task for what passes upon the tongue, but for what the heart intends.","anchor":"en-q2-224-225-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-224-225-s5","r":"q2-224-225","title":"Neither habitual swearing nor artificial refusal","text":"Frequent swearing is blameworthy and indicates levity and rashness. Refusing to swear altogether is affectation. The best affairs are the middle ones. The Prophet would sometimes swear, saying, “No, by the Turner of hearts,” or “By Him in whose hand is Muḥammad’s soul.” And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-224-225-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-224-225-s6","r":"q2-224-225","title":"","text":"The Real then indicates the ruling on the oath of abstention.","anchor":"en-q2-224-225-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-226-227","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement 2:226–227","anchor":"unit-q2-226-227"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-226-227-1","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"لِلَّذِينَ يُؤْلُونَ مِنْ نِسائِهِمْ تَرَبُّصُ أَرْبَعَةِ أَشْهُرٍ فَإِنْ فاؤُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (226) وَإِنْ عَزَمُوا الطَّلاقَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ (227)","anchor":"ar-q2-226-227-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-226-227-2","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"قلت: (الإيلاء) : يمين زوج مكلَّف على عدم وطء زوجته، أكثر من أربعة أشهر. وآلى: بمعنى حلف، يتعدى بعلى، ولكن لما ضُمَّن هنا معنى البُعد من المرأة، عُدّي بمن، و (تربص) : مبتدأ، و «للذين يؤلون» : خبر.","anchor":"ar-q2-226-227-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-226-227-3","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لِلَّذِينَ يبعدون مِنْ نِسائِهِمْ ويحلفون ألاَّ يجامعوهن أكثر من أربعة أشهر، غضباً وقصداً للإضرار، تَرَبُّصُ أي: تمهل أَرْبَعَةِ أَشْهُرٍ، لا يُطالبُ فيهن بفيئة ولا حنث، فَإِنْ فاؤُ أي: رجعوا عما حلفوا عليه، وحنثوا وكفَّروا أيمانهم، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ لما قصدوا من الإضرار، بالفيئة التي هي كالتوبة، رَحِيمٌ بهم حَيث لم يعاجلهم بالعقوبة، وَإِنْ عَزَمُوا الطَّلاقَ أي: صمموا عليه، ولم يرجعوا عما حلفوا عليه، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ لطلاقهم، عَلِيمٌ بقصدهم ونيتهم. ومذهب مالك والشافعي: أن القاضي يُوقفه:","anchor":"ar-q2-226-227-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-226-227-4","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"إما أن يرجع بالوطء إن قدر، أو بالوعد إن عَجز، أو يُطلِّق عليه طلقة رجعية، عند مالك. ومذهب أبي حنيفة: أنها تَبِين بمجرد مُضي أربعة أشهر. وأحكام الإيلاء مقررة في كتب الفقه.","anchor":"ar-q2-226-227-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-226-227-5","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"الإشارة: لا ينبغي للعبد أن يصرف عمره كله في معاداة نفسه ومجانبتها، إذ المقصود هو الاشتغال بمحبة الحبيب، لا الاشتغال بعداوة العدو، فلمجاهدة نفسه ومجانبتها حد معلوم ووقت مخصوص، وهو ما دامت جموحة","anchor":"ar-q2-226-227-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-226-227-6","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"جاهلة بالله. فإن فاءت ورجعت إلى الله، وارتاضت لحضرة الله، وجبت محبتها والاصطلاح معها لأن النفس بها ربح مَنْ ربح، ومنها خسر من خسر، من عرف قدرها، واحتال عليها حتى ردها إلى ربها- ربح، ومن أهملها وجهل قدرها- خسر، وكان شيخ شيوخنا يقول: جزاها الله عنا خيراً والله ما ربحنا إلا منها، يعني نفسه. وفي بعض الآثار: (مَنْ عَرَفَ نَفْسَه عَرَفَ ربَه) . وإن عزموا الطلاق، يعني: العباد والزهاد عزموا ألا يرجعوا إلى أنفسهم أبداً، فإن الله سميع عليم بقصدهم هل قصدهم طلب الحظوظ أو محبة الحبيب، وأما العارفون فلا تبقى لهم معاداة مع أحد قط، قد اصطلحوا مع الوجود بأسره، فمكنهم الله من التصرف في الوجود بأسره. والله ذو الفضل العظيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-226-227-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-226-227-7","r":"q2-226-227","title":"2:226–227 · The oath of abstention and the limit of estrangement","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى عدة الطلاق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-226-227-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-226-227-s1","r":"q2-226-227","title":"The oath of abstention","text":"I say: īlāʾ ( الإيلاء ) is the oath of a legally responsible husband not to have intercourse with his wife for more than four months. Ālā means “swore” and takes the preposition ʿalā . Here, however, it includes the meaning of keeping away from the woman ( التضمين ), and therefore takes min . “A waiting period” ( تربص ) is the subject, and “for those who swear to abstain” its predicate. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those who distance themselves from their wives and swear not to have intercourse for more than four months, through anger and the intention to harm, have a waiting period of four months. During these they are not required to return or break the oath. If they return from what they swore, break and expiate their oaths, God forgives the harm they intended through their return, which is like repentance. He is Merciful to them in not hastening to punish them. If they resolve upon divorce, determining upon it and not returning from their oath, God hears their divorce and knows their purpose and intention. Mālik’s and al-Shāfiʿī’s position is that the judge puts the husband to a decision: he must return through intercourse if able, or through a promise if unable; otherwise, according to Mālik, the judge pronounces one revocable divorce against him. Abū Ḥanīfa’s position is that she becomes irrevocably separated merely through the passing of four months. The rulings of īlāʾ are set out in the books of jurisprudence. [B164]","anchor":"en-q2-226-227-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-226-227-s2","r":"q2-226-227","title":"Hostility to the self is a means, not the whole of life","text":"The servant should not spend his entire life opposing and avoiding his self. The purpose is to occupy himself with love of the Beloved, not hostility towards the enemy. Struggling against and avoiding the self therefore has a known limit and a particular time: while it remains refractory and ignorant of God. If it returns to God and becomes disciplined for His presence, loving it and making peace with it become obligatory. Through the self, those who gain have gained; through it, those who lose have lost. Whoever knows its worth and deals skilfully with it until returning it to its Lord gains. Whoever neglects it and fails to know its worth loses. Our shaykh’s shaykh used to say: “May God reward it well on our behalf! By God, we gained only through it”—meaning his self. Among the transmitted sayings is: “Whoever knows his self knows his Lord.” [B165] “If they resolve upon divorce”: worshippers and ascetics resolve never to return to their selves. God hears and knows their purpose: is it seeking their own interests or loving the Beloved? Gnostics, however, retain no hostility towards anyone at all. They have made peace with existence in its entirety; God therefore enables them to exercise disposal within existence in its entirety. God is possessed of immense bounty.","anchor":"en-q2-226-227-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-226-227-s3","r":"q2-226-227","title":"","text":"The Real then mentions the waiting period following divorce.","anchor":"en-q2-226-227-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-228","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self 2:228","anchor":"unit-q2-228"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-1","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"وَالْمُطَلَّقاتُ يَتَرَبَّصْنَ بِأَنْفُسِهِنَّ ثَلاثَةَ قُرُوءٍ وَلا يَحِلُّ لَهُنَّ أَنْ يَكْتُمْنَ ما خَلَقَ اللَّهُ فِي أَرْحامِهِنَّ إِنْ كُنَّ يُؤْمِنَّ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَبُعُولَتُهُنَّ أَحَقُّ بِرَدِّهِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ إِنْ أَرادُوا إِصْلاحاً ...","anchor":"ar-q2-228-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-2","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"قلت: القُرء هو الطهر الذي يكون بعد الحيض، عند مالك، وجمع القلة: أقراء، والكثرة: قروء، واستعمله هنا باعتبار كثرة المطلقات، و (ثلاثة) : مفعول مطلق، أو ظرف، و (بعولتهن) : جمع بعل، والتاء لتأنيث الجماعة.","anchor":"ar-q2-228-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-3","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالْمُطَلَّقاتُ يَتَرَبَّصْنَ أي: يمكثن عن التزوج، بِأَنْفُسِهِنَّ ثَلاثَةَ قُرُوءٍ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-228-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-4","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"أطهار، وتَعْتَدُّ بالطهر الذي طلقها فيه، فتحيض، ثم تطهر، ثم تحيض، ثم تطهر، فإذا رأت الحيضة الثالثة خرجت من العدة، هذا في غير الحامل، وأما الحامل فعدتها وضع حملها. وَلا يَحِلُّ لَهُنَّ أَنْ يَكْتُمْنَ ما خَلَقَ اللَّهُ فِي أَرْحامِهِنَّ من الولد استعجالاً لإتمام العدة، أو من الحيض استبقاءا لتمادي العدة، وتُصدق في ذلك كله، فإن كانت يُؤْمِنَّ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فلا يحل لها أن تكتم ما استؤمنت عليه، وَبُعُولَتُهُنَّ أي: أزواجهن، أَحَقُّ بِرَدِّهِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ التربص، إن كان الطلاق رجعيّاً، وإلا بانت منه، وينبغي للزوج أن يراجعها في العدة، إن أراد بذلك الإصلاح والمودة، لا الإضرار بها، وإلا حرم عليه ارتجاعها، إذ «لاَ ضَرَرَ ولا ضرار» ، كما قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-.","anchor":"ar-q2-228-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-5","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"الإشارة: إذا طُلّقَتْ النَّفْسُ، ووقع البعد منها حتى طهرت ثلاثة: الطهر الأول: من الإصرار على الذنوب والمخالفات، الطهر الثاني: من العيوب والغفلات، الطهر الثالث: من الركون إلى العادات والوقوف مع المحسوسات، دون المعاني وأنوار التجليات- حلَّتْ رجعتُها والاصطلاح معها، ولا يحل لهن أن يكتمن ما خلق الله في أرحامهن: من العلوم والمعارف والأنوار، وذلك إذا استشرفَتْ على حضرة الأسرار، فإنها تفيض بالعلوم والحكم،","anchor":"ar-q2-228-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-6","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"أو ما لا يحصى، فينبغي أن تطلع عليها من يقتدي بشأنها. وبعولتهن أحق بردهن، والصلح معهن، بعد تمام تطهيرهن، إن أرادوا بذلك إصلاحاً، وهو إدخالها في الحضرة، ونعيمها بالشهود والنظرة. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-228-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-7","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"ثم ذكر الحقّ جلّ جلاله حقوق الزوجية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-228-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-8","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"... وَلَهُنَّ مِثْلُ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَلِلرِّجالِ عَلَيْهِنَّ دَرَجَةٌ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ (228)","anchor":"ar-q2-228-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-9","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وللنساء حقوق على الرجال، كما أن للرجال حقوقاً على النساء، فحقوق النساء على الرجال: الإنفاق، والكسوة، والإعفاف، وحسن المعاشرة، وكان ابنُ عمر- رضي الله عنهما- يقول: إني لأُحِبُّ أن أتزيَّنَ للمرأة كما تتزين لي، ويقرأ هذه الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-228-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-10","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"وحقوق الرجل على المرأة: إصلاح الطعام والفراش، وطاعة زوجها في كل ما يأمرها به من المباح، وحفظ فرجها، وصيانة ماله الذي ائتمنت عليه- إلى غير ذلك من الحقوق، فللنساء حقوق على الرجال مِثْلُ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ من غير ضرر ولا ضرار. ولا تفريط ولا إفراط، وَلِلرِّجالِ عَلَيْهِنَّ دَرَجَةٌ أي: فضيلة لأن الرجال قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النسآء، ولهم فضل في الميراث، والقسمة، وكثير من الحقوق، فضلهم الله على النساء.","anchor":"ar-q2-228-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-11","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ لا يعجزه عقاب من خالف أمره، لكنه يمهل ولا يُهمل، حَكِيمٌ لا يفعل إلا لمصلحة ظاهرة أو خفية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-228-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-12","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"الإشارة: للنفس حقوق على صاحبها، كما له حقوق عليها، قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «إنَّ لنفْسك عَلَيْكَ حَقّاً، وَلزَوْجِكَ عَلَيْك حَقّاً، ولِربِكَ عليك حَقّاً، فأَعْطِ كُلّ ذِي حَقِ حَقَّهُ» . فالنفس مغرفة للسر، فإذا تعبت سقط منها السر، كذلك نفس الإنسان، إذا تحامل عليها حتى تعللت، ودخلها الوجع، تعذر عليها كثير من العبادات، لا سيما الفكرة، فلا بد من حفظ البشرية، وإنما ينبغي قتلها بالأمور التي لا تُخِلُّ بصحتها، فعليها طاعتك فيما تأمرها به، كما عليك حفظها مما تتضرر به. وللرجال الأقوياء عليها تسلطٌ وتصرف، فهي مملوكة في أيديهم، وهم غالبون عليها، والله غالب على أمره، وهو العزيز الحكيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-228-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-228-13","r":"q2-228","title":"2:228 · The waiting period, mutual rights and the care of the self","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى عدد الطلاق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-228-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-228-s1","r":"q2-228","title":"The courses and the husbands","text":"I say: according to Mālik, qurʾ ( القُرء ) is the interval of purity after menstruation. Its plural of paucity is aqrāʾ , and of multitude qurūʾ ( جمع القلة، جمع الكثرة ). The latter is used here with regard to the multitude of divorced women. “Three” is an absolute accusative or adverbial expression ( مفعول مطلق أو ظرف ). Buʿūlatuhunna ( بعولتهن ), “their husbands,” is the plural of baʿl ; the tāʾ marks the collective as feminine. [B166]","anchor":"en-q2-228-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-228-s2","r":"q2-228","title":"The waiting period and return for reconciliation","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: divorced women wait, refraining from marriage, by themselves for three courses—that is, intervals of purity. She counts the interval during which she was divorced, then menstruates, becomes clean, menstruates and becomes clean. When she sees the third menstruation she leaves the waiting period. This applies to one who is not pregnant; the pregnant woman’s waiting period ends when she gives birth. It is not lawful for them to conceal what God has created in their wombs: a child, to hasten completion of the waiting period, or menstruation, to keep the period going. Her word is accepted in all this. If she believes in God and the Last Day, it is not lawful to conceal what has been entrusted to her. Their husbands have the stronger right to take them back during this waiting period if the divorce is revocable; otherwise she is separated from him. The husband should take her back during the waiting period if he intends reconciliation and affection, not harm. Otherwise taking her back is forbidden, for “there is neither harming nor reciprocating harm,” as the Prophet said.","anchor":"en-q2-228-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-228-s3","r":"q2-228","title":"Three purifications before reconciliation","text":"When the self has been divorced and kept at a distance until purified three times, it may be taken back and peace made with it. The first purification is from persistence in sins and disobedience; the second from faults and heedlessness; the third from repose in habits and stopping with sensible forms rather than meanings and the lights of self-disclosure. It is not lawful for such selves to conceal what God has created in their wombs: sciences, gnoses and lights. When the self looks out upon the presence of mysteries, it overflows with sciences and wisdoms, or what cannot be counted. It should disclose these to one who follows its example. Their husbands have the stronger right to take them back and make peace after their purification is complete, if they intend reconciliation: bringing the self into the Presence and delighting it with witnessing and vision. And success is through God. The Real then mentions the rights of marriage, saying: [B167] Qurʾānic continuation · 2:228b وَلَهُنَّ مِثْلُ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَلِلرِّجَالِ عَلَيْهِنَّ دَرَجَةٌ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ Women have rights corresponding to their obligations, according to what is right; men have a degree over them. God is Mighty, Wise.","anchor":"en-q2-228-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-228-s4","r":"q2-228","title":"Reciprocal duties and the stated degree","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: women have rights over men, just as men have rights over women. Women’s rights over men are maintenance, clothing, sexual fulfilment and good companionship. Ibn ʿUmar, God be pleased with them both, used to say: “I like to adorn myself for the woman as she adorns herself for me,” and he would recite this verse. [B167] A man’s rights over a woman include preparing food and bedding, obeying her husband in every permitted thing he commands, guarding her chastity and preserving the wealth entrusted to her, together with other rights. Women therefore have rights over men corresponding to their obligations, according to what is right, without harming or reciprocating harm, neglect or excess. Men have a degree over them: a distinction, since men have responsibility over women, and an advantage in inheritance, allotment and many rights. God has preferred them over women. God is Mighty: punishing whoever disobeys His command does not defeat Him. He gives respite, however, without neglecting. He is Wise, acting only for a benefit, manifest or hidden. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-228-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-228-s5","r":"q2-228","title":"The self’s rights and the preservation of bodily health","text":"The self has rights over its owner, just as he has rights over it. The Prophet said: “Your self has a right over you, your spouse has a right over you, and your Lord has a right over you. Give everyone who possesses a right his right.” The self is a ladle carrying the secret: when it grows weary, the secret falls from it. So with a person’s self: if one burdens it until it sickens and pain enters it, many acts of worship become difficult, especially contemplation. Bodily human nature ( البشرية ) must therefore be preserved. The self should be “put to death” only through things that do not impair its health. It owes you obedience in what you command, just as you owe it protection from what harms it. Strong men have authority and disposal over it: it is owned in their hands, and they prevail over it. God prevails in His purpose; He is the Mighty, the Wise. [B168]","anchor":"en-q2-228-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-228-s6","r":"q2-228","title":"","text":"The Real then mentions the number of divorces.","anchor":"en-q2-228-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-229-230","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation 2:229–230","anchor":"unit-q2-229-230"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-1","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"الطَّلاقُ مَرَّتانِ فَإِمْساكٌ بِمَعْرُوفٍ أَوْ تَسْرِيحٌ بِإِحْسانٍ وَلا يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ أَنْ تَأْخُذُوا مِمَّا آتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ شَيْئاً إِلاَّ أَنْ يَخافا أَلاَّ يُقِيما حُدُودَ اللَّهِ فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلاَّ يُقِيما حُدُودَ اللَّهِ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما فِيمَا","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-2","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"افْتَدَتْ بِهِ تِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ فَلا تَعْتَدُوها وَمَنْ يَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَ اللَّهِ فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ (229) فَإِنْ طَلَّقَها فَلا تَحِلُّ لَهُ مِنْ بَعْدُ حَتَّى تَنْكِحَ زَوْجاً غَيْرَهُ فَإِنْ طَلَّقَها فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما أَنْ يَتَراجَعا إِنْ ظَنَّا أَنْ يُقِيما حُدُودَ اللَّهِ وَتِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ يُبَيِّنُها لِقَوْمٍ يَعْلَمُونَ (230)","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-3","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"قلت: (فإمساك بمعروف) : مبتدأ، والخبر: محذوف، أي: أحسن أو أمثل. أو خبر، أي: فالواجب إمساك بمعروف أو تسريح بإحسان.","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-4","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الطَّلاقُ الذي تقع الرجعة بعده- إنما هو مَرَّتانِ، فإن طلق ثالثة فلا رجعة بعدها، فإن طلق واحدة أو اثنتين فهو مُخير، فإما أن يمسكها ويرتجعها بحسن المعاشرة، والقيام بحقوق الزوجية بالمعروف. وإما أن يُسرِّحها حتى تنقضي عدتها بِإِحْسانٍ، من غير إضرار، ولا تطويل عدة. وَلا يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ، أيها الأزواج، أَنْ تَأْخُذُوا مِمَّا آتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ من الصداق شَيْئاً- خُلْعاً- إِلَّا أَنْ يَخافا أَلَّا يُقِيما حُدُودَ اللَّهِ بأن ظن الزوج أو الزوجة فساد العشرة بينهما، وعدم القيام بحقوق الزوجية، فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أيها الحكام، أو من ينوب عنهم، أَلَّا يُقِيما حُدُودَ اللَّهِ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما فِيمَا افْتَدَتْ بِهِ من العصمة، فيحل للزوج أن يأخذ منها الفداء، ولو بجميع ما تملك، إذا كان الضرر منها أو منهما. فإن انفرد بضررها، حُرِّمَ عليه أخذ الفداء، وطُلِّقَتْ عليه.","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-5","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"تِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ فَلا تَعْتَدُوها وَمَنْ يَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَ اللَّهِ فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ أي: هذه الأحكام التي ذكرنا من عدد الطلاق وأخذ الخُلْع على وجهه- هي حدود الله التي حدها لعباده، فمن تعداها فهو ظالم.","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-6","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"(فإن) طلق الزوجُ مرة ثالثة فَلا تَحِلُّ لَهُ مِنْ بَعْدُ حَتَّى تَنْكِحَ زَوْجاً غَيْرَهُ، ويدخل بها، من غير شرط التحليل، فَإِنْ طَلَّقَها الثاني، فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما أَنْ يَتَراجَعا بنكاح جديد إِنْ ظَنَّا أَنْ يُقِيما حقوق الزوجية، وحسن العشرة، وَتِلْكَ الأحكام المذكورة هي حُدُودُ اللَّهِ يُبَيِّنُها الحقُ تعالى لِقَوْمٍ يَعْلَمُونَ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-7","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"يفهمون ويتدبرون الأمور.","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-8","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"الإشارة: إذا طلَّق المريد الدنيا، ثم رجع إليها، ثم تاب وتوجه إلى الله، ثم رجع إليها، ثم تاب وتوجه مرة ثانية، قُبلت توبته، فإن رجع إليها بعد الطلقة الثانية، فلا يُرجى فلاحه في الغالب لأنه متلاعب، قال تعالى: (الطلاقُ","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-9","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"مَرَّتان) فإمساكُ لها بمعروف بأن يواسي بها من يحتاج إليها، أو تسريح لها من يده بإحسان من الله إليه، حتى يدخله في مقام الإحسان، فإن طلقها مرة ثالثة فلا تحل له أبداً حتى يأخذها من يد الله بالله، بعد أن كان يأخذها بنفسه، فكأنه أخذها بعصمة جديدة، فإن تمكن من الفناء والبقاء، فلا جُناح عليه أن يرجع إليها غنيّاً بالله عنها.","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-10","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-229-230-11","r":"q2-229-230","title":"2:229–230 · The limits of divorce and release by compensation","text":"ثم نهى الحقّ تعالى عن إمساك الزوجة، إضراراً، كما كانت تفعل الجاهلية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-229-230-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-229-230-s1","r":"q2-229-230","title":"Retention as a subject or a predicate","text":"I say: “Then retention in an honourable manner” ( فإمساك بمعروف ) may be a subject with an omitted predicate: “is better” or “more fitting.” Or it is a predicate: “what is required is retention in an honourable manner or release with kindness.”","anchor":"en-q2-229-230-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-229-230-s2","r":"q2-229-230","title":"Two revocable divorces and the prohibition of injury","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the divorce after which return is possible occurs only twice. If he divorces a third time, no return follows it. After one or two divorces, he has a choice: retain her, taking her back with good companionship and fulfilment of marital rights according to what is right; or release her until her waiting period expires, kindly, without injury or prolonging the waiting period. It is not lawful for you husbands to take anything from the dower you gave them as compensation for release ( الخُلع ), unless the two fear that they cannot keep God’s limits: husband or wife thinks their life together will be unsound and marital rights will not be fulfilled. If you judges, or those acting for them, fear that they cannot keep God’s limits, there is no blame upon either in what she gives to free herself from the marriage bond ( العصمة ). The husband may take compensation, even everything she owns, if the harm arises from her or from both of them. If he alone inflicts the harm, taking compensation is forbidden to him and divorce is pronounced against him. Those are God’s limits: do not overstep them. Whoever oversteps God’s limits is a wrongdoer. The rulings We mentioned concerning the number of divorces and taking compensation in its proper manner are the limits God set for His servants; whoever transgresses them wrongs.","anchor":"en-q2-229-230-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-229-230-s3","r":"q2-229-230","title":"The third divorce and a subsequent marriage","text":"If the husband divorces a third time, she is not lawful to him thereafter until she marries another husband and that husband consummates the marriage, without a condition of making her lawful to the first ( التحليل ). If the second husband divorces her, there is no blame upon the first two returning through a new marriage, if they think they can fulfil marital rights and live together well. These rulings are God’s limits, which the Real explains to people who know: who understand and consider matters. [B169]","anchor":"en-q2-229-230-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-229-230-s4","r":"q2-229-230","title":"Divorcing the world and returning through God","text":"If the disciple divorces the world, then returns to it, then repents and turns towards God, then returns to it, then repents and turns a second time, his repentance is accepted. If he returns after the second divorce, his flourishing is generally not to be hoped for, because he is playing. He says: divorce is twice. Then retain it honourably, sharing it with those who need it, or release it from one’s hand through God’s kindness towards one, until He admits one into the station of excellence ( الإحسان ). If he divorces it a third time, it is never lawful for him until he takes it from God’s hand through God, after formerly taking it through his own self. It is as though he takes it through a new bond. If he becomes established in effacement and subsistence ( الفناء والبقاء ), there is no blame in returning to it while rich through God and free of need for it. And God Most High knows best. [B170]","anchor":"en-q2-229-230-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-229-230-s5","r":"q2-229-230","title":"","text":"The Real then forbids retaining a wife to injure her, as the people of the Age of Ignorance used to do.","anchor":"en-q2-229-230-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-231","r":"q2-231","title":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs","text":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs 2:231","anchor":"unit-q2-231"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-231-1","r":"q2-231","title":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs","text":"وَإِذا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّساءَ فَبَلَغْنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ فَأَمْسِكُوهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوفٍ أَوْ سَرِّحُوهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوفٍ وَلا تُمْسِكُوهُنَّ ضِراراً لِتَعْتَدُوا وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ فَقَدْ ظَلَمَ نَفْسَهُ وَلا تَتَّخِذُوا آياتِ اللَّهِ هُزُواً وَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَما أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنَ الْكِتابِ وَالْحِكْمَةِ يَعِظُكُمْ بِهِ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (231)","anchor":"ar-q2-231-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-231-2","r":"q2-231","title":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs","text":"قلت: (ضراراً) : مفعول له، أو حال، أي: مُضَارِّين.","anchor":"ar-q2-231-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-231-3","r":"q2-231","title":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّساءَ فَقَرُبَ بلوغُ أَجَل عِدَّتِهِنَّ فَأَمْسِكُوهُنَّ بالرجعة متلبسين بالمعروف والإحسان إليها، أَوْ سَرِّحُوهُنَّ يتزوجن غيركم بِمَعْرُوفٍ لا إضرار فيه، وَلا تُمْسِكُوهُنَّ بنية طلاقهن ضِراراً أي: لأجل الضرر بتطويل عدتهن لِتَعْتَدُوا عليهن وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ فَقَدْ ظَلَمَ نَفْسَهُ.","anchor":"ar-q2-231-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-231-4","r":"q2-231","title":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs","text":"نزلت في رجل قال لامرأته: لا آويك، ولا أدعك تحلِّين لغيري. فقالت: كيف؟ فقال: أطلقك، فإذا دنا مُضِيُّ عِدَّتِك راجعتك، فَشَكَتْ ذلك لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فنزلت الآية. وكان بعضهم يطلق، ويعتق، ثم يرجع، ويقول: كُنت أهزأ بذلك وألعب، فنزل قوله تعالى: وَلا تَتَّخِذُوا آياتِ اللَّهِ هُزُواً أي: مهزوءاً بها، وفي الحديث: «ثَلاَثٌ هزْلُهُنَّ جدٌ: النّكَاحُ، والطَّلاقُ، والرَّجْعَةُ» . وَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ بالهداية وبعثة الرسول، وَما أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنَ الْكِتابِ فيه ما تحتاجون إليه ظاهراً وباطناً، وَالْحِكْمَةِ أي: السنة المطهرة، يَعِظُكُمْ بذلك ويزكيكم، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فيما يأمركم به، وينهاكم عنه، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ يَعْلَمُ سِرَّكُمْ وَجَهْرَكُمْ وَيَعْلَمُ ما تَكْسِبُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-231-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-231-5","r":"q2-231","title":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs","text":"الإشارة: يقال للمريدين المتجردين إذا طلقتم الدنيا، وآيستم أنفسكم من الرجوع إليها حتى تمكَّن اليقين من القلب بحيث انقطع الاهتمام بالرزق من القلب، وزالت عنه الشكوك والأوهام، فإذا رجعت إليه الدنيا، فإما أن يمسكها بمعروف بأَنْ تكون في يده لا في قلبه، أو يسرحها من يده، بسبب مقام الإحسان الذي عوضه الله عنها، ولا تمسكوا الدنيا، أيها الفقراء، قبل كمال اليقين، فإنها ضرر لكم، فقد أخذت الرجال لا سيما الأطفال. وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ فَقَدْ ظَلَمَ نَفْسَهُ حيث حرمها الوصول، وتركها في حيرة الأوهام تجول، فاحذروا لذيذ عاجلها، لكريه آجلها، وَلا تَتَّخِذُوا آياتِ اللَّهِ هُزُواً بالرخص والتأويلات، وَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ بالهداية إلى الطريق، وَما أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنَ الْكِتابِ: فيه بيان التحقيق وَالْحِكْمَةِ التي هي إصابة عين التوفيق، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ، فلا تركنوا إلى شيء سواه، فإن مالت قلوبكم إلى شيء من السِّوى، أو نزعت إلى محبة الهوى، فاعلموا أَنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ فيبعدكم بعد الوصول. ولا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله العلي العظيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-231-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-231-6","r":"q2-231","title":"2:231 · No retention for harm and no mockery of God’s signs","text":"ثم نهى الحقّ تعالى عن منع النساء من التزوج إضرارا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-231-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-231-s1","r":"q2-231","title":"Harm as intention or circumstance","text":"I say: “To cause harm” ( ضراراً ) is an accusative of purpose or cause ( مفعول له ), or a circumstantial expression ( حال ): “while inflicting harm.”","anchor":"en-q2-231-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-231-s2","r":"q2-231","title":"Ending the cycle of injurious revocation","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when you divorce women and the end of their waiting period draws near, retain them by taking them back while treating them honourably and kindly, or release them to marry others, honourably and without injury. Do not retain them with the intention of divorcing them again to cause harm, prolonging their waiting period and transgressing against them. Whoever does this wrongs himself. It was revealed concerning a man who told his wife: “I will neither shelter you nor let you become lawful to another.” She asked how. He said: “I divorce you; when your waiting period is nearly over, I take you back.” She complained to God’s Messenger and the verse was revealed. Some people would divorce or emancipate, then retract and say, “I was only joking and playing.” His saying was revealed: do not make a mockery of God’s signs. The Tradition says: “Three things are serious even in jest: marriage, divorce and taking a wife back.” [B171] Remember God’s blessing upon you through guidance and the sending of the Messenger, and the Book He sent down, containing what you need outwardly and inwardly, together with wisdom—the purified Sunna. With these He admonishes and purifies you. Fear God in what He commands and forbids, and know that God knows everything: He knows your secret and public conduct and what you earn.","anchor":"en-q2-231-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-231-s3","r":"q2-231","title":"The world in the hand, not in the heart","text":"Those disciples who have stripped themselves of attachments are told: when you divorce the world and make your selves despair of returning to it, until certainty becomes established in the heart, concern over provision is cut off and doubts and illusions disappear, then, if the world returns, either hold it honourably—in your hand, not your heart—or release it from your hand because of the station of excellence God has given in exchange for it. Do not hold the world, spiritually poor ones, before certainty is complete: it is harmful to you. It has captured grown men, let alone children. Whoever does this wrongs himself, depriving his self of arrival and leaving it to wander in the bewilderment of imaginings. Beware its immediate sweetness because of its bitter aftermath. Do not make a mockery of God’s signs through concessions and accommodating interpretations. Remember His blessing upon you in guiding you to the Path, and the Book He sent down, which explains realization, together with wisdom, which is hitting upon the very reality of success. Fear God; repose in nothing other than Him. If your hearts incline to something other, or are drawn towards desire’s love, know that God knows everything: He will distance you after arrival. There is no power and no strength except through God, the High, the Magnificent.","anchor":"en-q2-231-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-231-s4","r":"q2-231","title":"","text":"The Real then forbids preventing women from marrying in order to harm them.","anchor":"en-q2-231-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-232","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage 2:232","anchor":"unit-q2-232"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-232-1","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"وَإِذا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّساءَ فَبَلَغْنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ فَلا تَعْضُلُوهُنَّ أَنْ يَنْكِحْنَ أَزْواجَهُنَّ إِذا تَراضَوْا بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ ذلِكَ يُوعَظُ بِهِ مَنْ كانَ مِنْكُمْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ ذلِكُمْ أَزْكى لَكُمْ وَأَطْهَرُ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنْتُمْ لا تَعْلَمُونَ (232)","anchor":"ar-q2-232-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-232-2","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"قلت: العَضْل: المنع والتضييق والتعسير، يقال: أعضلت الدجاجةُ، إذا عسر بيضُها.","anchor":"ar-q2-232-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-232-3","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّساءَ فانقضت عدتهن فَلا تمنعوهن، أيها الأولياء، من أَنْ يَنْكِحْنَ أَزْواجَهُنَّ الذين كانوا يملكوهن ثم طلقوا، أو الخُطَّاب الأجانب، إِذا تَراضَوْا بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-232-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-232-4","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"بأن كانوا أكفاء لهن، وبذلوا من المهر ما يناسبهن، أو كانت رشيدة. ذلِكَ الذي ذكرنا لكم- يتعظ به، ويقف معه، من كان يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ لأنه هو الذي ينجع فيه الوعظ وينتفع بالتذكير، ذلِكُمْ أَزْكى لَكُمْ أي: أرفع لقدركم، إن تمسكتم به، وَأَطْهَرُ لكم من الذنوب والعيوب، وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ ما فيه صلاحكم، وَأَنْتُمْ لا تَعْلَمُونَ. نزلت الآية في مَعْقِلَ بنِ يَسَارٍ، زوَّج أُخْتَه ثم طلقها زوجُها، وأمهلها حتى انقضت عِدَّتُهَا، ثم جاء يَخْطُبُهَا، فقال مَعْقِلُ: تَرَكها حتى ملكت نفسها، ثم جاء يخطُبها، والله لا أُزوجها منه أبداً. والمرأة أرادت أن ترجع إليه، فنزلت الآية، فرجع معقل عن قسمه وزَوَّجَها.","anchor":"ar-q2-232-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-232-5","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"وفيه دليل أن المرأة لا تُزَوج نفسها، خلافاً لأبي حنيفة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-232-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-232-6","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"الإشارة: ينبغي للشيوخ إذا تحققوا من المريدين كمال اليقين، وظهر عليهم أمارات الرشد، ألا يمنعوهم من تعاطي الأسباب، وأخذ ما جاءهم من الدنيا، بلا استشراف ولا طمع، فقد يكون ذلك عوناً لهم على الدين، وعمارة لزاوية الذاكرين، فذلك أزكى لهم وأطهر لقلوبهم، (والله يعلم وأنتم لا تعلمون) .","anchor":"ar-q2-232-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-232-7","r":"q2-232","title":"2:232 · Do not obstruct a woman’s remarriage","text":"ثم ذكر تعالى حكم الرضاع، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-232-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-232-s1","r":"q2-232","title":"Obstruction and constraint","text":"I say: ʿaḍl ( العَضْل ) means preventing, constraining and making something difficult. One says aʿḍalat al-dajāja when a hen has difficulty laying her egg.","anchor":"en-q2-232-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-232-s2","r":"q2-232","title":"The guardian must not prevent an agreed marriage","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when you divorce women and their waiting period expires, do not prevent them, guardians, from marrying their husbands—those who previously held them in marriage and then divorced them—or other suitors, when they agree between themselves in a right manner: the men are suitable matches and offer a dower appropriate to the women, or the woman is of sound judgment in managing her affairs ( رشيدة ). The person who believes in God and the Last Day takes admonition from what We have mentioned and abides by it, for admonition is effective in him and he benefits from the reminder. This raises your standing, if you hold fast to it, and purifies you from sins and faults. God knows what is conducive to your well-being, and you do not know. The verse was revealed concerning Maʿqil ibn Yasār. He married his sister to a man, who divorced her and left her until her waiting period expired. The man then came to seek her hand again. Maʿqil said: “He left her until she became her own mistress, then came to seek her hand! By God, I shall never marry her to him.” The woman wanted to return to him. The verse was revealed, and Maʿqil withdrew from his oath and married her to the man. This provides evidence that a woman does not contract her own marriage, contrary to Abū Ḥanīfa. And God Most High knows best. [B172]","anchor":"en-q2-232-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-232-s3","r":"q2-232","title":"Mature disciples and the use of worldly means","text":"When shaykhs have ascertained the perfection of their disciples’ certainty and signs of sound judgment have appeared in them, they should not prevent them from engaging in means of livelihood or accepting what comes to them of this world, without looking eagerly for it or coveting it. This may assist them in religion and sustain the lodge of those who remember God. It is more wholesome for them and purer for their hearts: “God knows, and you do not know.”","anchor":"en-q2-232-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-232-s4","r":"q2-232","title":"","text":"God Most High then mentions the ruling on nursing.","anchor":"en-q2-232-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-233","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture 2:233","anchor":"unit-q2-233"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-233-1","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"وَالْوالِداتُ يُرْضِعْنَ أَوْلادَهُنَّ حَوْلَيْنِ كامِلَيْنِ لِمَنْ أَرادَ أَنْ يُتِمَّ الرَّضاعَةَ وَعَلَى الْمَوْلُودِ لَهُ رِزْقُهُنَّ وَكِسْوَتُهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ لا تُكَلَّفُ نَفْسٌ إِلاَّ وُسْعَها لا تُضَارَّ والِدَةٌ بِوَلَدِها وَلا مَوْلُودٌ لَهُ بِوَلَدِهِ وَعَلَى الْوارِثِ مِثْلُ ذلِكَ فَإِنْ أَرادا فِصالاً عَنْ تَراضٍ مِنْهُما وَتَشاوُرٍ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما وَإِنْ أَرَدْتُمْ أَنْ تَسْتَرْضِعُوا أَوْلادَكُمْ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذا سَلَّمْتُمْ ما آتَيْتُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ (233)","anchor":"ar-q2-233-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-233-2","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ويجب على الوالدات أن يُرْضِعْنَ أَوْلادَهُنَّ حَوْلَيْنِ كامِلَيْنِ إذا كُنَّ في العصمة، ولا شرف لهن لجرى العُرف بذلك، أو مطلقاتٍ، ولم يقبل الولد غيرهنَّ، هذا لِمَنْ أَرادَ أَنْ يُتِمَّ الرَّضاعَةَ، فإن اتفقا على فطامه قبلهما، جاز، كما يأتي. ويجب عَلَى الْمَوْلُودِ لَهُ وهو الأب، رزق أمهات أولاده، وَكِسْوَتُهُنَّ إذ هو الذي يُنسب المولود له، وذلك بِالْمَعْرُوفِ، لا يكلف الله نفسا إلا ما في وُسْعها وتُطيقه، فلا تُضَارَّ والِدَةٌ بِوَلَدِها، بحيث ترضعه وهي مريضة، أو انقطع لبنها. بل يجب على الأب أن يستأجر من يرضعه، ولا يضار مَوْلُودٌ لَهُ بِوَلَدِهِ، بحيث يكلف من الإنفاق والكسوة فوق جهده. فإن مات الأب وترك مالاً- فعلى الْوارِثِ الكبير مِثْلُ ذلِكَ من الكسوة والإنفاق، يُجريها من مال الأب، ويحسبها من حق الصبي، فإن لم يكن للأب مال- فعلى جماعة المسلمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-233-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-233-3","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"فَإِنْ أَرادا أي: الأب والمرضعة، فِصالًا أي: فطاماً للصبي قبل تمام الحولين، عَنْ تَراضٍ مِنْهُما وَتَشاوُرٍ بينهما، فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما، إن لم يخف على الولد ضعف. وَإِنْ أَرَدْتُمْ، أيها الأزواج، أَنْ تَسْتَرْضِعُوا أَوْلادَكُمْ عند غير الأم، برضاها، فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ في ذلك إِذا سَلَّمْتُمْ أي: أعطيتم للمراضع، ما آتَيْتُمْ أي: ما أردتم إيتاءه من الأجرة بِالْمَعْرُوفِ من غير مَطْلٍ ولا تقتير. والشرط إنما هو","anchor":"ar-q2-233-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-233-4","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"على وجه الكمال والإحسان، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فيما كُلفتم به من الحقوق، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ لا يخفى عليه شيء من أموركم فإنه بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ.","anchor":"ar-q2-233-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-233-5","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن تربية الولاية في قلب المريد، على نمط تربية الطفل الصغير، تنبت في قلب المريد وقت عقد الصحبة بينهما، ثم لا تزال تنمو، أو الشيخ يرضعه بلبن الإمداد حتى يتم أوان رضاعه، ولذلك قالوا: الثدي الميتة لا ترضع. هـ. يشيرون إلى أن الشيخ الميت لا يُربى، فلا يزال الشيخ يُربى الروح، ويمدها حتى تدخل بلد الإحسان، وتشتعل فكرتها. وهذا تمام الحولين في حقها، وهو أوان كمال الحقيقة والشريعة لمن أراد إتمامها، فتأكل الروح حينئذٍ من كل شيء، وتشرب من كل شيء، وتستمد من الأشياء كلها، ثم لا يزال يحاذيها بهمته حتى تَرشُد، فيطلق لها التصرف، فتصلح لتربية غيرها.","anchor":"ar-q2-233-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-233-6","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"وعلى الشيخ رزقُ المريدين من قوت القلوب وكسوتهم، تقيهم من إصابة الذنوب والعيوب، إلا ما سبق به القضاءُ في علم الغيوب، فليس في طَوْق أحدٍ دفعُه، لا تُكلف نفسٌ إلا وسعها، فإذا مات الشيخ، ووصَّى بمن يرث مقامه، فعلى الوارث مثلُ ذلك، فإن أراد المريد انفصالاً عن الشيخ، وتعمير بلد، أو تذكير عباد الله، عن تراض منهما وتشاور من الشيخ، فلا جناح عليهما، وإن أردتم، أيها الشيوخ، أن تسترضعوا أولادكم بإرسال منْ يُذكِّرُهم، ويمدهم، نائباً عنكم، فلا جناح عليكم إذا سلمتم لهم من الإمداد ما يمدهم به، واتقوا الله في شأن المريدين، في جبر كسرهم، وقبول عذرهم، واعلموا أن الله بما تعملون بصير.","anchor":"ar-q2-233-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-233-7","r":"q2-233","title":"2:233 · Nursing, mutual consultation and spiritual nurture","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى عدّة الوفاة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-233-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-233-s1","r":"q2-233","title":"Nursing, maintenance and the child’s welfare","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: mothers must nurse their children for two complete years when they remain in marriage and are not women of high social standing, since this is the customary practice; or when they are divorced and the child will accept no other nurse. This is for whoever desires to complete the nursing. If the two agree to wean the child earlier, it is permissible, as will follow. [B173] The father—the one to whom the child is ascribed—must provide the food and clothing of his children’s mothers, in a right manner. God charges no soul beyond what lies within its capacity and what it can bear. A mother is therefore not to be harmed on account of her child, by having to nurse while ill or when her milk has ceased; the father must instead hire someone to nurse the child. Nor is a father to be harmed on account of his child by being charged with maintenance and clothing beyond his means. If the father dies leaving property, the adult heir bears a like duty of clothing and maintenance, paying it out of the father’s property and reckoning it against the child’s share. If the father leaves no property, the duty falls upon the Muslim community. If the father and nursing woman desire to wean the child before the completion of two years, by mutual agreement and consultation, there is no blame upon them, provided that no weakening of the child is feared. If you, husbands, wish to have your children nursed by someone other than their mother, with her consent, there is no blame upon you, provided you give the nurses the payment you intend to give in a right manner, without delay or stinting. This condition is stated by way of perfection and good conduct. Be mindful of God concerning the rights with which you have been charged, and know that nothing in your affairs is hidden from God, for He sees what you do.","anchor":"en-q2-233-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-233-s2","r":"q2-233","title":"The growth of sainthood and the responsibility of the guide","text":"Know that the nurture of sainthood ( الولاية ) within the disciple’s heart follows the pattern of nurturing a little child. It takes root in his heart when the bond of companionship is established between him and the shaykh. It then continues to grow, while the shaykh nurses him with the milk of spiritual support ( الإمداد ), until his period of nursing is complete. Hence their saying: “A dead breast does not nurse.” They indicate by this that a deceased shaykh does not provide this formative nurture. [B174] The shaykh continues to nurture and sustain the spirit until it enters the country of spiritual excellence ( الإحسان ) and its contemplative thought is kindled. This is the completion of its two years: the time when Reality and Sacred Law are brought to perfection, for whoever desires their completion. The spirit then eats of everything, drinks of everything, and draws nourishment from all things. The shaykh continues to attend it with his spiritual aspiration ( الهمة ) until it reaches maturity. He then releases it to act, and it becomes fit to nurture another. The shaykh is responsible for feeding the disciples with the sustenance of hearts and clothing them in what protects them from sins and faults—except what the decree has already determined in the knowledge of the unseen, for no one has the power to repel that. “No soul is charged beyond its capacity.” If the shaykh dies and designates someone to inherit his station, the heir bears a like duty. If a disciple wishes to separate from the shaykh, establish a centre in another place or remind God’s servants, by mutual agreement and consultation with the shaykh, there is no blame upon them. If you, shaykhs, wish to have your children nursed by sending someone to remind and sustain them as your deputy, there is no blame upon you, provided you impart to him the spiritual support through which he can sustain them. Be mindful of God in the affairs of disciples: mend their brokenness and accept their excuses. Know that God sees what you do.","anchor":"en-q2-233-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-233-s3","r":"q2-233","title":"","text":"The Real then mentions the waiting period following a husband’s death.","anchor":"en-q2-233-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-234-235","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity 2:234–235","anchor":"unit-q2-234-235"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-1","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"وَالَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزْواجاً يَتَرَبَّصْنَ بِأَنْفُسِهِنَّ أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وَعَشْراً فَإِذا بَلَغْنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيما فَعَلْنَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ (234) وَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيما عَرَّضْتُمْ بِهِ مِنْ خِطْبَةِ النِّساءِ أَوْ أَكْنَنْتُمْ فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ عَلِمَ اللَّهُ أَنَّكُمْ سَتَذْكُرُونَهُنَّ وَلكِنْ لا تُواعِدُوهُنَّ سِرًّا إِلاَّ أَنْ تَقُولُوا قَوْلاً مَعْرُوفاً وَلا تَعْزِمُوا عُقْدَةَ النِّكاحِ حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ الْكِتابُ أَجَلَهُ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ فَاحْذَرُوهُ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ (235)","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-2","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"قلت: والَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ: مبتدأ، ويَتَرَبَّصْنَ: خبر، ولا بد من الحذف ليصح الإخبار، إما من الصدر أو من العَجزُ، أي: وأزواج الذين يتوفون، أو الذين يتوفون أزواجهن يتربصن.","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-3","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالَّذِينَ يموتون منكم، أيها المؤمنون، ويتركون أَزْواجاً، فلا يتزوجن حتى يَتَرَبَّصْنَ أي: يمكثن بِأَنْفُسِهِنَّ أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وعشرة أيام لأن الجنين يتحرك لثلاثة أشهر إن كان ذكراً، ولأربعة إن كان أنثى في الغالب(1) ، وزيد عشرةً، استظهاراً، هذا في غير الحامل، أما الحامل، فعدتها وضع حملها. فَإِذا بَلَغْنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ أي: انقضت عدتهن، فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ أيها الأولياء فِيما فَعَلْنَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِنَّ من التزين والتعرض للنكاح أو التزوج، بِالْمَعْرُوفِ، بحيث لا ينكره الشرع من تزين ونكاح، وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ فيجازيكم على ما فعلتم.","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-4","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"وَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ أيها الخُطَّاب فِيما عَرَّضْتُمْ بِهِ للمعتدات مِنْ خِطْبَةِ النِّساءِ كقول الرجل:","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-5","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"إني لراغب في صحبتكم، وإني أريد أن أتزوج في هذه الساعة. وإنك لنافقة(2)، أو لا يصلح لك أن تبقى بلا زوج، ونحو هذا، أَوْ أَكْنَنْتُمْ أي: أضمرتم فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ في زمن العدة من أمر التزوج دون تصريح، عَلِمَ اللَّهُ أَنَّكُمْ ستذكرون النساء المعتدات، وتتكلمون في نكاحهن، حرصاً وتمنياً، فعرّضُوا بذلك، وَلكِنْ لا تُواعِدُوهُنَّ سِرًّا أي: في الخلوة، أو لا تواعدوهن نكاحاً أو جماعاً، إِلَّا أَنْ تَقُولُوا قَوْلًا مَعْرُوفاً وهو التعريض بالألفاظ المتقدمة.","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-6","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"ولا تقطعوا عُقْدَةَ النِّكاحِ، وتعزموا على فعله، حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ كتاب المعتدة أَجَلَهُ، وتنقضى العدة، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُ ما فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ من الرغبة والحرص، فَاحْذَرُوهُ فإنَّ الحرص على الشيء، والرغبة فيه، قبل أوانه، ربما يعاقب صاحبه بحرمانه، وما قُدِّر لكَ لا يكون لغيرك، وما كان لغيرك لا يكون لك، ولو فعلت ما فعلت، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ لِمَا استعجلتم فإن الإنسان خُلق عجولاً، حَلِيمٌ فلا يعاجلكم ولا يفضح سرائركم.","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-7","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"الإشارة: إذا ماتت النفس عن الهوى، وتركت حظوظاً وشهوات، فلا ينبغي أن يردها إلى ذلك حتى تتربص مدة، ليظهر عليها آثارُ الزهد من السكون إلى الله، والتأنس بمشاهدة الله حتى تغيب عما سواه. فإذا بلغت هذا الوصف فلا جناح على المريد أن يسعفها فيما تفعل بالمعروف، من غير سَرَفٍ ولا ميل إلى هوى، لأن فعلها حينئذٍ بالله، ومن الله، وإلى الله، وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ لا يخفى عليه شيء من أمرها، ولا جناح عليكم، أيها المريدون، إن تزكت نفوسكم، وطهرت من الأغيار قلوبكم، فيما عرضتم به من خطبة أبكار الحقائق وثيبات العلوم، أو أكننتم في أنفسكم من المعارف والمفهوم، علم الله أنكم ستذكرون ذلك باللسان قبل أن يصل الذوق إلى الجَنَان، فلا تصرحوا بعلوم الحقائق مع كل الخلائق فإن ذلك من فعل الزنادق، إلا أن تقولوا قولاً معروفاً، إشارة أو تلويحاً، فعلمنا كله إشارة، فإذا صار عبارة خفي.","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-8","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"ولا تطلبوا علم الحقائق قبل بلوغ أجله، وهو موت النفوس، والزهد في الفلوس، وكمال التربية، وتمام التصفية، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُ ما فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ من الشرة إليها قبل أوانها، فَاحْذَرُوهُ أن يعاقبكم بحرمانها، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ لا يعاجلكم بحرمان قصدكم، إن صح مقصدكم، والله تعالى أعلم، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-234-235-9","r":"q2-234-235","title":"2:234–235 · Widowhood, guarded proposals and the time of spiritual maturity","text":"ثم ذكر الحقّ جلّ جلاله حكم الطلاق قبل المسيس، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-234-235-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-234-235-s1","r":"q2-234-235","title":"The necessary ellipsis","text":"I say: “Those who die” is the subject ( مبتدأ ), and “shall wait” the predicate ( خبر ). An ellipsis ( حذف ) must be supplied for the predication to be sound, either at the beginning or at the end: “The wives of those who die …,” or “Those who die—their wives shall wait …”.","anchor":"en-q2-234-235-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-234-235-s2","r":"q2-234-235","title":"The widow’s waiting period","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those of you who die, believers, and leave wives—the wives shall not marry until they have waited by themselves for four months and ten days. This is because a male foetus generally moves after three months, and a female after four; ten days are added as a precaution. This concerns the woman who is not pregnant. A pregnant woman’s waiting period ends when she gives birth. [B175] When their waiting period expires, there is no blame upon you, guardians, concerning their adorning themselves, making themselves available for marriage or marrying, in a right manner: an adornment or marriage not disapproved by the Sacred Law. God is aware of what you do and will recompense you for what you have done.","anchor":"en-q2-234-235-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-234-235-s3","r":"q2-234-235","title":"Allusion to marriage without a premature contract","text":"There is no blame upon you, suitors, for hinting at a proposal to women in their waiting period. A man might say: “I am desirous of your companionship”; “I wish to marry at this time”; “You are much sought after”; or “It is not fitting that you remain without a husband”—and similar expressions. Nor is there blame for concealing within yourselves during the waiting period a wish to marry, without declaring it openly. God knows that, out of eagerness and desire, you will mention women in their waiting period and discuss marrying them. You may therefore allude to this, but do not make promises to them in secret—that is, in private—or promise marriage or intercourse, except to speak in a right manner through the indirect expressions already mentioned. Do not conclude the marriage bond or determine to do so until the woman’s prescribed term has ended and the waiting period expired. Know that God knows your desire and eagerness, so beware of Him. Someone’s eagerness and desire for a thing before its time may be punished by being deprived of it. What has been allotted to you will not belong to another, and what belongs to another will not be yours, whatever you do. Know that God is Forgiving concerning your haste—for the human being was created hasty—and Forbearing: He does not hasten against you or expose your secrets.","anchor":"en-q2-234-235-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-234-235-s4","r":"q2-234-235","title":"Do not seek the sciences of Reality before their time","text":"When the self dies to desire and abandons its interests and appetites, it should not be returned to them until it has waited for a time, so that the effects of renunciation appear in it: resting in God and finding intimacy in witnessing Him, until it is absent from everything other than Him. When it attains this quality, there is no blame upon the disciple for allowing it what it does in a right manner, without excess or inclination towards desire. Its action is then through God, from God and towards God. God is aware of what you do: nothing concerning it is hidden from Him. There is no blame upon you, disciples, when your selves have been purified and your hearts cleansed of other things, for hinting at a proposal to the virgins of the realities and the previously wedded women of the sciences, or for concealing within yourselves gnoses and understanding. God knows that you will mention these with the tongue before their taste has reached the heart. Do not therefore declare the sciences of Reality openly to everyone, for that is the conduct of the heretics ( الزنادقة ), except to speak in a right manner, through indication or allusion. Our knowledge is all allusion ( إشارة ); when it becomes explicit expression ( عبارة ), it is concealed. [B176] Do not seek the knowledge of realities before its appointed time: the death of selves, renunciation of money, complete nurture and perfected purification. Know that God knows your eagerness for it before its time, so beware lest He punish you by withholding it. Know that God is Forgiving, Forbearing: He does not hasten to deprive you of your aim, if your purpose is sound. And God Most High knows best; and success is through God.","anchor":"en-q2-234-235-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-234-235-s5","r":"q2-234-235","title":"","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, then mentions divorce before consummation.","anchor":"en-q2-234-235-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-236-237","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity 2:236–237","anchor":"unit-q2-236-237"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-236-237-1","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"لا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِنْ طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّساءَ ما لَمْ تَمَسُّوهُنَّ أَوْ تَفْرِضُوا لَهُنَّ فَرِيضَةً وَمَتِّعُوهُنَّ عَلَى الْمُوسِعِ قَدَرُهُ وَعَلَى الْمُقْتِرِ قَدَرُهُ مَتاعاً بِالْمَعْرُوفِ حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُحْسِنِينَ (236) وَإِنْ طَلَّقْتُمُوهُنَّ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ تَمَسُّوهُنَّ وَقَدْ فَرَضْتُمْ لَهُنَّ فَرِيضَةً فَنِصْفُ ما فَرَضْتُمْ إِلاَّ أَنْ يَعْفُونَ أَوْ يَعْفُوَا الَّذِي بِيَدِهِ عُقْدَةُ النِّكاحِ وَأَنْ تَعْفُوا أَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوى وَلا تَنْسَوُا الْفَضْلَ بَيْنَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ (237)","anchor":"ar-q2-236-237-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-236-237-2","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"قلت: (ما) مصدرية ظرفية، وأَوْ تَفْرِضُوا معطوف على تَمَسُّوهُنَّ أي: لا تبعة عليكم ولا إثم إن طلقتم النساء قبل البناء، مدة كونكم لم تمسوهن ولم تفرضوا لهن مهرا، وإِلَّا أَنْ يَعْفُونَ مبني لاتصاله بنون النسوة، ووزنه: يفعُلن كقوله تعالى: السِّجْنُ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ مِمَّا يَدْعُونَنِي إِلَيْهِ وقوله وَالْقَواعِدُ مِنَ النِّساءِ اللَّاتِي لا يَرْجُونَ نِكاحاً، وحَقًّا مفعول مطلق.","anchor":"ar-q2-236-237-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-236-237-3","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لا حرج عليكم من إثم أو صداق، إِنْ طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّساءَ مدة كونكم لَمْ تَمَسُّوهُنَّ بالجماع، ولَم تَفْرِضُوا لَهُنَّ فَرِيضَةً من الصداق، فطلقوهن حينئذٍ، وَمَتِّعُوهُنَّ أي: أعطوهن ما يتمتعن به ويجبر كسرهن، على قدر حال الزوج عَلَى الْمُوسِعِ أي: الغنى، قَدَرُهُ من المتعة كأمة أو كسوة أو مال يليق بحاله، وَعَلَى الْمُقْتِرِ أي: الذي تقتر رزقَه، أي ضَيّق عليه، وهو الفقير، قَدَرُهُ ما يقدر عليه، فمتعوهن مَتاعاً بِالْمَعْرُوفِ من غير سَرَفٍ ولا تقتير، حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُحْسِنِينَ أي: حقّ ذلك عليهم حقّاً. حمل مالكُ الأمْرَ على الندب، وحمله غيره على الوجوب، وهو الظاهر.","anchor":"ar-q2-236-237-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-236-237-4","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"وإن طلقتموهن بعد المسيس فالصداق كامل، وَإِنْ طَلَّقْتُمُوهُنَّ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ تَمَسُّوهُنَّ وَقَدْ فَرَضْتُمْ لَهُنَّ صداقاً فَنِصْفُ ما فَرَضْتُمْ يجب عليكم، إِلَّا أَنْ يَعْفُونَ أي: النساء، عن نصف الصداق، أَوْ يَعْفُوَا الَّذِي بِيَدِهِ عُقْدَةُ النِّكاحِ، وهو الأب في ابنته البكر قاله مالك، أو الزوج بأن يدفعه كاملاً، قاله الشافعي، وَأَنْ تَعْفُوا أيها الأولياء عن الزوج، فلا تقبضوا منه شيئاً، أَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوى لأن المرأة لم يذهب لها شيء فسلُعتُها قائمة، وَلا تَنْسَوُا الْفَضْلَ والإحسان بَيْنَكُمْ، فتسامحوا يسمح لكم، إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ لا يخفى عليه شيء من أعمالكم، فيجازي المحسن بإحسانه، وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-236-237-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-236-237-5","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"الإشارة: من المريدين من تحصل له الغيبة عن نفسه، والجذب عنها، بعد أن يمسها بالمجاهدة والمكابدة، فحينئذٍ يمتعها بالشهود والعيان، وهذه طريق الجادة. ومنهم من تحصل له الغيبة عن نفسه والجذب عنها قبل أن يمسها، ويجاهدها، وهو نادر بالنسبة إلى الأول، فيقال لهؤلاء الفريق: لا جناح عليكم إن طلقتم أنفسكم، وغبتم عنها، من قبل أن تمسوها، وقبل أن تعرضوا عليها وظائف العبودية. ومتعوهن بالشهود والعيان على قدر وسعكم وقوة شهودكم، على الموسع قدره من لذة الشهود، وعلى المقتر- أي: المضيق عليه في المعرفة- قدره من لذة الشهود، حق ذلك حقا على المحسنين الذين حازوا مقام الإحسان، وفازوا بالشهود والعيان.","anchor":"ar-q2-236-237-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-236-237-6","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"وإن حصل لكم جذب العناية، وطلقتم أنفسكم قبل أن تمسوها، وقد كنتم وظفتم عليها أوراداً من وظائف العبودية فنصف ما فرضتم، وهو المهم منها لأن عبادتها صارت قلبية، فيكفيها من العبادة القالبية المهم، إلا أن تقوى على ذلك مع الشهود. أو يأمرها الذي بيده عقدة نكاحها، وهو الشيخ، فلا يضرها الاشتغال بها حيث كان بإذْن، وأن تعفوا، أيها الشيوخ، عن المريدين في العبادة الحسيّة، وتأمروهم بالعبادة القلبية، أقرب للتقوى الكاملة، وهي تقوى السَّوَى. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-236-237-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-236-237-7","r":"q2-236-237","title":"2:236–237 · Divorce before consummation, compensation and generosity","text":"ولما ذكر الحق تعالى شأن النساء، حذر من الاشتغال بهن عن العبادة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-236-237-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-236-237-s1","r":"q2-236-237","title":"The temporal construction and the feminine plural","text":"I say: mā ( ما ) is infinitival and temporal ( مصدرية ظرفية ). “Or assign” is coordinated with “touch”: you incur neither liability nor sin by divorcing women before consummation, during the period in which you have neither touched them nor assigned them a dower. “Unless they remit” ( إلا أن يعفون ) is indeclinable because of its attachment to the feminine plural nūn ( نون النسوة ). Its pattern is yafʿulna , like “Prison is dearer to me than that to which they invite me” ( يدعونني ) [12:33], and “The women past childbearing who do not hope for marriage” ( لا يرجون نكاحاً ) [24:60]. “A duty” ( حقاً ) is an absolute accusative ( مفعول مطلق ). [B177]","anchor":"en-q2-236-237-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-236-237-s2","r":"q2-236-237","title":"The compensatory gift and the assigned dower","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: there is no liability upon you in respect of sin or dower if you divorce women while you have neither touched them through intercourse nor assigned them a dower. You may then divorce them, but give them a provision: something from which they can benefit and which mends their brokenness, according to the husband’s circumstances. The affluent gives according to his means—a slave woman, clothing or money appropriate to his circumstances. The straitened man, whose livelihood has been restricted, gives what he can afford. Give them a provision in a right manner, without extravagance or stinting. It is a duty upon those who do good: it is truly due from them. Mālik understood the command as recommendation ( ندب ), while others understood it as obligation ( وجوب ); the latter is the apparent meaning. [B178] If you divorce them after consummation, the full dower is due. If you divorce them before touching them but have assigned them a dower, half of what you assigned is due from you, unless the women remit their half, or the one who holds the marriage bond remits it. According to Mālik, this is the father in the case of his virgin daughter. According to al-Shāfiʿī, it is the husband, by paying the whole dower. For you, guardians, to remit the husband’s payment and take nothing from him is nearer to reverence, since the woman has lost nothing and her “goods” remain intact. Do not forget generosity and kindness between you. Be forbearing, and forbearance will be shown to you. God sees what you do; none of your deeds is hidden from Him. He recompenses the one who does good for his goodness, and God loves those who do good. [B178]","anchor":"en-q2-236-237-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-236-237-s3","r":"q2-236-237","title":"Attraction before or after discipline","text":"Some disciples attain absence from their selves and attraction away from them ( الجذب ) after having touched them with struggle and endurance. They then allow them the enjoyment of witnessing and direct vision ( الشهود والعيان ). This is the usual path. Others attain absence from the self and attraction away from it before touching it or struggling against it; this is rare compared with the first. To this latter group it is said: there is no blame upon you for divorcing your selves and becoming absent from them before touching them and before imposing upon them the observances of servanthood ( وظائف العبودية ). Allow them the enjoyment of witnessing and direct vision according to your capacity and the strength of your witnessing. The one granted amplitude receives the delight of witnessing according to his capacity; the one whose gnosis remains restricted receives its delight according to his capacity. This is truly due from those who do good: those who have attained the station of spiritual excellence ( مقام الإحسان ) and gained witnessing and direct vision. If the attraction of divine care reaches you and you divorce your selves before touching them, having already imposed upon them litanies ( أوراد ) among the observances of servanthood, then retain half of what you imposed: the essential part. Their worship has become inward, of the heart ( قلبية ), and the essential bodily worship ( قالبية ) suffices them—unless they are strong enough to combine the whole with witnessing, or the one who holds their marriage bond, the shaykh, commands them to do so. Occupation with these observances does not harm them when undertaken with permission. For you, shaykhs, to remit some sensory worship from the disciples and direct them to worship of the heart is nearer to complete reverence: guarding against everything other than God ( تقوى السوى ). And God Most High knows best. [B179]","anchor":"en-q2-236-237-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-236-237-s4","r":"q2-236-237","title":"","text":"Having mentioned the affairs of women, the Real Most High warns against allowing them to distract one from worship.","anchor":"en-q2-236-237-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-238-239","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear 2:238–239","anchor":"unit-q2-238-239"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-1","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"حافِظُوا عَلَى الصَّلَواتِ وَالصَّلاةِ الْوُسْطى وَقُومُوا لِلَّهِ قانِتِينَ (238) فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ فَرِجالاً أَوْ رُكْباناً فَإِذا أَمِنْتُمْ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَما عَلَّمَكُمْ ما لَمْ تَكُونُوا تَعْلَمُونَ (239)","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-2","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: حافِظُوا أيضاً على أداء الصَّلَواتِ الخمس في أوقاتها بإتقان شروطها وأركانها وخشوعها وآدابها، ولا تشتغلوا عنها بشهوات النساء وتشغيب أحكامهن، ولا بغير ذلك، وحافظوا أيضاً على الصَّلاةِ الْوُسْطى وهى العصر عند الشافعي، وهو ظاهر الحديث، أو الصبح عند مالك لفضلها، أو لتوسطها بين صلاتي الليل والنهار. وما من صلاة إلا وقيل فيها الوسطى. وقيل: أخفيت كساعة الجمعة وليلة القدر.","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-3","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"وَقُومُوا لِلَّهِ في الصلاة قانِتِينَ أي: ساكتين، وكان، قبل نزول الآية، الكلام في الصلاة جائزاً، أو قيل: مطيعين. إذ القنوت في القرآن كله بمعنى الطاعة. فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ من عدو، أو سَبع، أو سَيْل، فصلُّوا قياماً على أرجلكم بالإيماء للسجود، أَوْ رُكْباناً على خيولكم بالإيماء للركوع والسجود، فَإِذا أَمِنْتُمْ في الصلاة، أو بعدها، فصلوا صلاة أمن، فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ في الصلاة، وصلوا كَما عَلَّمَكُمْ من الكيفية ما لَمْ تَكُونُوا تَعْلَمُونَ قبل ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-4","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"الإشارة: حافظوا على الصلوات الحسية قياماً بوظائف العبودية، وعلى الصلاة القلبية قياماً بشهود عظمة الربوبية وهي الصلاة الوسطى لدوامها في كل ساعة، قيل لبعضهم: هل للقلوب صلاة؟ قال: نعم، إذا سجد لا يرفع رأسه أبداً. هـ. أي: إذا خضع لهيبة العظمة لم يرفع أبداً، وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-5","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"فاسجُدْ لهيبةِ الجَلالِ ... عنْد التَّدَانِي","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-6","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"وَلْتَقْرَأ آيةَ الكَمالِ ... سَبْعَ المَثَانِي","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-7","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"وأشار بقوله «آية الكمال» لقوله تعالى: إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ ليجمع بين الشريعة والحقيقة، فسجود القلب حقيقة، وسجود الجوارح شريعة، وقوموا لله بآداب العبودية قانتين خاشعين، فإن خفتم ألا تصلوا إلى ربكم، قبل انقضاء أجلكم، فسيروا إليه رجالاً أو ركباناً، خفافاً أو ثقالاً، فإذا أمنتم من القطيعة- وذلك بعد التمكين- فاذكروا الله شكراً لأجل ما أطلعكم عليه، وعلَّمكم ما لم تكونوا تعلمون من عظمة الربوبية، وكمال آداب العبودية.","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-238-239-8","r":"q2-238-239","title":"2:238–239 · Guard the prayers, in security and in fear","text":"ثم رجع الحقّ تعالى إلى الكلام على النساء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-238-239-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-238-239-s1","r":"q2-238-239","title":"The appointed prayers and prayer in danger","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: guard also the performance of the five prayers at their appointed times, perfecting their conditions, essential acts, humility and proper manners ( شروطها وأركانها وخشوعها وآدابها ). Do not let desire for women, the troublesome disputes concerning their affairs, or anything else distract you from them. Guard especially the middle prayer. According to al-Shāfiʿī, it is the afternoon prayer, as the apparent meaning of the hadith indicates. According to Mālik, it is the dawn prayer, because of its excellence or its position between the two night prayers and the daytime prayers. Every prayer has been identified as the middle prayer. It is also said that it was concealed, like the hour of Friday and the Night of Power. [B180] Stand before God in prayer qānitīn ( قانتين ): silent. Before this verse was revealed, speaking in prayer was permissible. Alternatively, it means obedient, for qunūt throughout the Qurʾān signifies obedience. If you fear an enemy, a wild beast or a flood, pray standing on your feet, gesturing for prostration, or mounted on your horses, gesturing for bowing and prostration. When you become secure, during the prayer or afterwards, perform the prayer of security. Remember God in prayer and pray in the manner He taught you, which you did not previously know.","anchor":"en-q2-238-239-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-238-239-s2","r":"q2-238-239","title":"The prayer of the heart and the prayer of the limbs","text":"Guard the sensory prayers, fulfilling the observances of servanthood, and the prayer of the heart, witnessing the majesty of Lordship. The latter is the middle prayer because it continues at every hour. Someone was asked: “Do hearts have a prayer?” He replied: “Yes. When the heart prostrates, it never raises its head again.” That is, once it has bowed before the awe of divine majesty, it never rises. The poet says concerning this: Prostrate before the awe of Majesty at the drawing near; and recite the verse of perfection, the Seven Oft-Repeated. By “the verse of perfection,” he indicates: “You alone we worship, and from You alone we seek help,” joining Sacred Law and Reality. The prostration of the heart is Reality; the prostration of the limbs is Sacred Law. Stand before God observing the manners of servanthood, devoted and humble. If you fear that you will not reach your Lord before your allotted term expires, travel towards Him on foot or mounted, lightly or heavily laden. When you become secure from severance—and this is after firm establishment ( التمكين )—remember God in gratitude for what He has disclosed to you and taught you, which you did not know: the majesty of Lordship and the perfection of the manners of servanthood.","anchor":"en-q2-238-239-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-238-239-s3","r":"q2-238-239","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then returns to the discussion of women.","anchor":"en-q2-238-239-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-240","r":"q2-240","title":"2:240 · The widow’s provision and the preservation of spiritual knowledge","text":"2:240 · The widow’s provision and the preservation of spiritual knowledge 2:240","anchor":"unit-q2-240"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-240-1","r":"q2-240","title":"2:240 · The widow’s provision and the preservation of spiritual knowledge","text":"وَالَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزْواجاً وَصِيَّةً لِأَزْواجِهِمْ مَتاعاً إِلَى الْحَوْلِ غَيْرَ إِخْراجٍ فَإِنْ خَرَجْنَ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِي ما فَعَلْنَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِنَّ مِنْ مَعْرُوفٍ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ (240)","anchor":"ar-q2-240-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-240-2","r":"q2-240","title":"2:240 · The widow’s provision and the preservation of spiritual knowledge","text":"قلت: (وصية) : مبتدأ، والخبر محذوف، أي: عليهم وصية، ومَنْ نَصَبَ، فمفعول مطلق، أي: فليوصوا وصية، و (غير) : حال من الأزواج، أي: حَالَ كَوْنِهِنَّ غَيْرَ مُخْرَجَاتِ.","anchor":"ar-q2-240-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-240-3","r":"q2-240","title":"2:240 · The widow’s provision and the preservation of spiritual knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ ويتركون أَزْواجاً بعدهم، فيجب عليهم أن يوصوا لأزواجهم وصية يتمتعن بها من كسوة ونفقة وسكنى، إلى تمام الْحَوْلِ ما دام الأزواج لم يخرجن من مسكن الزوج، فَإِنْ خَرَجْنَ بأنفسهن، فلا نفقة ولا كسوة ولا سكنى عليكم أيها الأولياء، ولا حرج عليكم فِيما فَعَلْنَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِنَّ من التزين والتعرض للنكاح بعد تمام عدتهن، على ما هو معروف في الشرع، والوصية منسوخة بآية الميراث، وتربص الحول بآية أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وَعَشْراً المتقدمة المتأخرة في النزول(1)، وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ ينسخ ما يشاء، ويحكم ما يريد، باعتبار الحكمة والمصلحة.","anchor":"ar-q2-240-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-240-4","r":"q2-240","title":"2:240 · The widow’s provision and the preservation of spiritual knowledge","text":"الإشارة: والذين يُتوفون عن الحظوظ والشهوات، ويتركون علوماً وأسراراً، ينبغي لهم أن يوصوا بحفظها وتدوينها، كان الشيخ أبو الحسن الشاذلي رضي الله عنه إذا استغرق في الكلام وفاضت عليه المواهب، يقول: (هلاَّ رجلٌ يقيد عنا هذه العلوم) . هـ. ليقع التمتع بها للسائرين والطالبين، (غير إخراج) لغير أهلها، فإن قضى الوقت بخروجها، من غير قصد، فلا حرج، إما لغلبة وجد أو هداية مريد، (والله عزيز حكيم) ، فعزته اقتضت الغيرة على سره: أن يأخذه غير أهله، وحكمته اقتضت ظهوره في وقته لأهله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-240-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-240-5","r":"q2-240","title":"2:240 · The widow’s provision and the preservation of spiritual knowledge","text":"ثم كرر أمر المتعة تأكيدا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-240-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-240-s1","r":"q2-240","title":"The bequest and the circumstantial expression","text":"I say: in the nominative reading, “a bequest” ( وصية ) is the subject, with its predicate omitted: “A bequest is incumbent upon them.” In the accusative reading, it is an absolute accusative: “Let them make a bequest.” “Without being turned out” ( غير إخراج ) is a circumstantial expression ( حال ) referring to the wives: while they are not being expelled.","anchor":"en-q2-240-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-240-s2","r":"q2-240","title":"The year’s provision and the account of abrogation","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those of you who die and leave wives behind must make a bequest for their wives, by which they can enjoy clothing, maintenance and lodging until the completion of a year, so long as the wives do not leave the husband’s dwelling. If they leave of their own accord, no maintenance, clothing or lodging is due from you, guardians. Nor is there blame upon you concerning their adorning themselves and making themselves available for marriage after the completion of their waiting period, in a manner recognised by the Sacred Law. The bequest was abrogated by the inheritance verse, and the year’s waiting period by “four months and ten days,” which occurs earlier in the arrangement but was revealed later. God is Mighty, Wise: He abrogates what He wills and decrees what He desires, in accordance with wisdom and benefit. [B181]","anchor":"en-q2-240-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-240-s3","r":"q2-240","title":"Record the sciences, and guard their proper recipients","text":"Those who die to personal interests and desires, leaving sciences and mysteries behind, should enjoin their preservation and recording. When spiritual gifts poured upon Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan al-Shādhilī and he became absorbed in speaking, he would say: “Is there no man who will record these sciences from us?” This is so that travellers and seekers may benefit from them, “without being turned out”—not disclosed to those unfit for them. If the moment decrees that they emerge unintentionally, there is no blame: it may occur through an overpowering spiritual finding ( وجد ) or for a disciple’s guidance. “God is Mighty, Wise.” His might requires jealous protection of His mystery, lest one unfit for it receive it; His wisdom requires its appearance at its proper time to those fit for it. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-240-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-240-s4","r":"q2-240","title":"","text":"He then repeats the command to give a provision, for emphasis.","anchor":"en-q2-240-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-241-242","r":"q2-241-242","title":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship","text":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship 2:241–242","anchor":"unit-q2-241-242"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-241-242-1","r":"q2-241-242","title":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship","text":"وَلِلْمُطَلَّقاتِ مَتاعٌ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُتَّقِينَ (241) كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ آياتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ (242)","anchor":"ar-q2-241-242-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-241-242-2","r":"q2-241-242","title":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship","text":"قلت: إنما كرره لأن الأولى في غير المدخول بها، إذا طُلقت قبل الفرض، وهذه في المدخول بها، وعبَّر أولاً بالمحسن: لأن المتعة قبل الدخول لا يعطيها إلا أهل الإحسان لأن المطلق لم يحصل له تمتع بالزوجة، بخلاف الثاني، فمطلق المدخول بها، التقوى تحمله على الإمتاع.","anchor":"ar-q2-241-242-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-241-242-3","r":"q2-241-242","title":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship","text":"وقيل: لمّا نزلت الآية الأولى، قال رجل من المسلمين: إنْ أحسنتُ مَتَّعْتُ وإلاَّ تَركتُ، فنزلت الثانية تأكيداً.","anchor":"ar-q2-241-242-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-241-242-4","r":"q2-241-242","title":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship","text":"وقال: حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُتَّقِينَ الشرك، أي: على كل مؤمن، وحكمها: الندب، عند مالك، على تفصيل ذكره في المختصر، فقال عاطفاً على المندوب: والمتعة على قدر حاله، بعد العدة للرجعة، أو ورثتها، ككل مُطَلَّقة في نكاح لازم، لا في فَسْخ كلعَانٍ وملك أحد الزوجين، إلا من اختلعَتْ، أو فُرض لها وطُلقت قبل البناء، ومختارة لعتقِها أو لِعَيْبه أو مُخَيَّرَة أو مُمَلَّكة.","anchor":"ar-q2-241-242-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-241-242-5","r":"q2-241-242","title":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship","text":"الإشارة: كل من طلق نفسه وخالف هواها تمتع بحلاوة المعاملة مع ربه، فمن اتصل بشيخ التربية تمتع بحلاوة العبادة القلبية كالشهود والعيان، ومن لم يتصل بالشيخ تمتع بحلاوة العبادة الحسية. فالآية الأولى في المريدين والواصلين، وهذه الآية في العُبَّاد والزهاد، ولذلك عبّر في الأولى بالمحسنين، وفي الثانية بالمتقين، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-241-242-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-241-242-6","r":"q2-241-242","title":"2:241–242 · Provision for divorced women and the sweetness of worship","text":"ثم حذّر من الفرار من الموت، توطئة للترغيب فى الجهاد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-241-242-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-241-242-s1","r":"q2-241-242","title":"Why the command is repeated","text":"I say: He repeats it because the first verse concerns a woman divorced before consummation and before a dower has been assigned, whereas this concerns one whose marriage has been consummated. In the first, He speaks of “those who do good,” because only people of goodness give this provision before consummation: the divorcing man has received no enjoyment from his wife. In the second case, however, reverence moves the man who divorces a wife after consummation to provide for her. It is also said that when the first verse was revealed, a Muslim man said: “If I do good, I give her a provision; otherwise I leave it.” The second was therefore revealed as confirmation. It says: “A duty upon those who are mindful”—who guard against associating partners with God; that is, upon every believer. According to Mālik, its ruling is recommendation, with the distinctions mentioned in the Mukhtaṣar . There, in a list of recommended acts, he says: “The consolatory provision is according to his circumstances; in a revocable divorce, after the waiting period, or to her heirs—as for every woman divorced from a binding marriage, not a dissolution, such as mutual imprecation or one spouse’s acquisition of the other. Exceptions are the woman who obtains release by compensation; one assigned a dower and divorced before consummation; and one who chooses separation because of her emancipation, his defect, an option given to her or delegated power of divorce.” [B182]","anchor":"en-q2-241-242-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-241-242-s2","r":"q2-241-242","title":"Two kinds of sweetness","text":"Everyone who divorces his self and opposes its desire enjoys the sweetness of dealings with his Lord. One who has joined a shaykh of spiritual nurture enjoys the sweetness of inward worship, such as witnessing and direct vision. One who has not joined a shaykh enjoys the sweetness of sensory worship. The first verse thus concerns disciples and those who have arrived, and this verse worshippers and ascetics. Hence the first speaks of “those who do good” ( المحسنين ), and the second of “those who are mindful” ( المتقين ). And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-241-242-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-241-242-s3","r":"q2-241-242","title":"","text":"He then warns against flight from death, preparing the way for encouragement to struggle in His cause.","anchor":"en-q2-241-242-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-243","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement 2:243","anchor":"unit-q2-243"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-1","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا مِنْ دِيارِهِمْ وَهُمْ أُلُوفٌ حَذَرَ الْمَوْتِ فَقالَ لَهُمُ اللَّهُ مُوتُوا ثُمَّ أَحْياهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَلكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لا يَشْكُرُونَ (243)","anchor":"ar-q2-243-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-2","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"قلت: الاستفهام للتعجب والتشويق، والرؤية قلبية، والواو للحال، و (حَذَرَ) مفعول من أجله.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-3","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ألم تنظر يا محمد، بعين الفكر والاعتبار، إِلَى الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا مِنْ دِيارِهِمْ وَهُمْ أُلُوفٌ عشرة، أو ثلاثون، أو أربعون، أو سبعون، حذراً من الْمَوْتِ في زمن الطاعون.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-4","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"وكانوا في قرية يقال لها: (داوردان) فلما وقع بها الطاعون، خرجت طائفة هاربين، وبقيت أخرى، فهلك أكثر من بقي، وسلم الخارجون، ثم رجعوا، فقال الباقون: لو صنعنا مثلهم لبقينا، لئن أصابنا الطاعون مرة ثانية لخرجنا، فأصابهم من قابل، فهربوا كلهم، ونزلوا وادياً أفيح(1) ، فناداهم ملك من أسفل الوادي، وآخر من أعلاه، أن:","anchor":"ar-q2-243-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-5","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"موتوا، فماتوا كلهم أجمعون، ومرت عليهم مدة ثمانية أيام أو أكثر حتى انتفخوا، وقيل: صاروا عظاماً، فمرَّ عليهم نبيّ الله (حزقيل) ، فدعا الله تعالى، واستشفع فيهم، فأحياهم الله، وعاشوا دهراً، عليهم سيما الموت لا يلبسون ثوباً إلا عاد كالكفن، واستمر في أسباطهم. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-6","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"قال الأصمعي: لما وقع الطاعون بالبصرة، خرج رجل منها على حمار معه أهله، وله عبد يسوق حماره، فأنشأ العبد يقول:","anchor":"ar-q2-243-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-7","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"لن يُسبَقَ اللهُ على حِمار ... ولا على ذي مَشعَةٍ طيّار","anchor":"ar-q2-243-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-8","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"قد يصبح الله أمَامَ السارِي(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-243-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-9","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"فرجع الرجل بعياله.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-10","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"والآية تدل على أن الفرار من الطاعون حرام في تلك الشريعة، كما حرم في شرعنا، وروى عبد الرحمن ابن عوف أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: «إِذَا سَمِعْتُمْ هذا الوباء بِبلد فَلاَ تَقْدُمُوا عَلَيْهِ، وإذَا وَقَعَ بِبلد وَأَنْتُمْ فيه فَلاَ تَخْرُجُوا مِنْهُ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-243-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-11","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"قلت: وقد اختلف الأئمة في حكم الفرار والقدوم: فمنهم من شهر المنع فيهما تمسكاً بظاهر الحديث، ومنهم من شهر الكراهة. والمختار في الفرار: التحريم، وفي القدوم: التفصيل، فمن قوي يقينه، وصفا توحيده، حَلَّ له القدوم، ومن ضعف يقينه، بحيث إذا أصابه شيء نسب التأثير لغير الله حرم عليه القدوم.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-12","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"وفي حديث عائشة- رضي الله عنها- قلت: يا رسول الله، ما الطاعون؟ قال: «غدة كغدة البعير، المقيم فيه كالشهيد، والفارُّ منه كالفار من الزحْف» . قال ابن حجر: كون المقيم فيه له أجر شهيد إنما بشرط أن يعلم أنه لا يصيبه إلا ما كتب الله له، وأن يسلم إليه أمره ويرضى بقضائه، وأن يبقى في مكانه ولا يخرج منه بقصد الفرار، فإذا اتصف الجالس بهذه القيود حصل له أجر الشهادة. ودخل تحته ثلاث صور، الأولى: من اتصف بذلك فوقع له الطاعون ومات فهو شهيد. والثانية: من وقع به ولم يمت به فهو شهيد وإن مات بعد ذلك. والثالثة: من لم يقع به أصلاً ومات بغيره عاجلاً أو آجلاً فهو شهيد، إذا حصلت فيه القيود الثلاثة، ومن لم يتصف بالقيود الثلاثة فليس بشهيد، ولو مات بالطاعون. والله أعلم هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-13","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"وأما القدوم من بلد الطاعون إلى البلد السالمة منه فجائز. ولا يُمنع من الدخول، قاله الباجي وابن حجر والحطاب وغيرهم لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «لاَ عَدْوَى وَلاَ طِيَرَةَ» وأما قوله عليه الصلاة والسلام:","anchor":"ar-q2-243-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-14","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"«فِرَّ مِنَ المَجْذُومِ فِرَارَكَ مِنَ الأَسَدِ» ، وقوله: «لاَ يورد مُمْرِضٌ عَلَى مُصِحٍّ» ، فهو محمول على حسم المادة، وسد الذريعة لئلا يحدث للمخالط شيء من ذلك، فيظنه بسبب المخالطة، فيثبت العدوى التي نفاها الشارع، هذا المختار في الجمع بين الحديثين. والله تعالى أعلم. وإنما أطلت في المسألة لِمَسْ الحاجة لأن التأليف وقع في زمن الوباء، حفظنا الله من وبالها.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-15","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"وقيل: إن الذين خرجوا من ديارهم قوم من بني إسرائيل، أُمروا بالجهاد، فخافوا الموت بالقتل في الجهاد، فخرجوا من ديارهم فراراً من ذلك، فأماتهم الله ليعرفهم أنهم لا ينجيهم من الموت شيء، ثم أحياهم وأمرهم بالجهاد، بقوله: وَقاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ الآية. وقوله تعالى: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ حيث أنزل بهم رحمته، ففروا منها، ولم يعاقبهم، حيث أحياهم بعد موتهم، وَلكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لا يَشْكُرُونَ إذ لا يفهم النعم في طي النقم إلا القليل، فيشكروا الله في السراء والضراء.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-16","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"الإشارة: ألم ترَ أيها السامع إلى الذين خرجوا من ديار عوائدهم وأوطان شهواتهم، وهم جماعة أهل التجريد، القاصدين إلى صفاء التوحيد، والغرق في بحر التفريد، حذراً من موت أرواحهم بالجهل والفَرْقِ، فاصطفاهم الله لحضرته، وجذبهم إلى مشاهدة ذاته، فقال لهم الله: موتوا عن حظوظكم، وغيبوا عن وجودكم، فلما ماتوا عن حظوظهم، وغابوا عن وجودهم، أحياهم الله بالعلم والمعرفة، إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ حيث فتح لهم باب السلوك، وهيأهم لمعرفة ملك الملوك، وَلكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لا يَشْكُرُونَ حيث تجلّى لهم، وعرَّفهم به، وهم لا يشعرون، إلا من فتح الله بصيرتهم، وقليل ما هم.","anchor":"ar-q2-243-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-243-17","r":"q2-243","title":"2:243 · Flight from death, the plague and life after effacement","text":"ثم حرّض الحق تعالى المؤمنين على الجهاد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-243-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-243-s1","r":"q2-243","title":"A question that awakens wonder","text":"I say: the question expresses wonder and awakens interest. The seeing is of the heart ( رؤية قلبية ); the wāw introduces a circumstance ( واو الحال ); and “fearing” ( حذر ) is an accusative of purpose ( مفعول من أجله ).","anchor":"en-q2-243-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-243-s2","r":"q2-243","title":"Those who fled the plague","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: have you not looked, Muḥammad, with the eye of reflection and consideration, at those who left their homes in their thousands—ten, thirty, forty or seventy thousand—fearing death at a time of plague? They were in a village called Dāwardān. When plague struck, one group fled and another remained. Most of those who remained perished, while those who left escaped. The latter returned, and the survivors said: “Had we done as they did, we would have remained alive. If plague strikes us a second time, we shall leave.” It struck the following year. They all fled and descended into a broad valley. An angel called from its lower end, and another from its upper end: “Die!” They all died. Eight days or more passed until they swelled; it is also said that they became bones. God’s prophet Ḥizqīl passed them, prayed to God Most High and interceded for them. God brought them to life. They lived for a long time with the mark of death upon them: any garment they wore became like a shroud. This continued among their descendants. [B183] Al-Aṣmaʿī said: when plague struck Basra, a man left on a donkey with his family and a slave driving the donkey. The slave began to recite: God cannot be outstripped upon a donkey, nor upon a flying, shaggy-maned steed; God may already stand before the night-traveller. The man returned with his family.","anchor":"en-q2-243-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-243-s3","r":"q2-243","title":"The author’s discussion of flight, entry and contagion","text":"The verse indicates that flight from plague was forbidden in that dispensation, as it is forbidden in ours. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf related that the Prophet said: “When you hear of this epidemic in a land, do not enter it; when it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave it.” [B184] I say: the imams disagreed over flight and entry. Some regarded prohibition in both as the recognised position, holding to the apparent meaning of the hadith; others regarded disapproval as the recognised position. The preferred ruling for flight is prohibition. For entry, a distinction is made: someone whose certainty is strong and whose affirmation of unity is pure may enter; someone whose certainty is weak, so that if something befalls him he ascribes efficacy to other than God, may not enter. [B184] In ʿĀʾisha’s report, she says: “I asked, ‘Messenger of God, what is plague?’ He said: ‘A swelling like the swelling of a camel. One who remains in it is like a martyr, and one who flees from it is like one who flees the battle line.’” Ibn Ḥajar said: the person who remains receives a martyr’s reward only on condition that he knows nothing can befall him except what God has decreed for him, entrusts his affairs to Him and is content with His decree, and remains in his place without leaving in flight. When the person who stays fulfils these conditions, he receives the reward of martyrdom. This includes three cases. First, one who possesses these qualities, contracts plague and dies: he is a martyr. Second, one who contracts it but does not die of it: he is a martyr, even if he dies afterwards. Third, one who never contracts it and dies of something else, sooner or later: he is a martyr if these three conditions are fulfilled. One who lacks the three conditions is not a martyr, even if he dies of plague. And God knows best. Here his words end. [B185] As for coming from a plague-stricken land to one free from it, it is permissible, and the person is not prevented from entering. Al-Bājī, Ibn Ḥajar, al-Ḥaṭṭāb and others said this, on the basis of the Prophet’s words: “There is no contagion and no evil omen.” As for his words, “Flee from the leper as you flee from a lion,” and “Do not bring sick animals among healthy ones,” these are understood as cutting off the occasion and blocking the means ( سد الذريعة ), lest something similar occur to the person who mixes with the sick, and he suppose that it was caused by the mixing, thus affirming the contagion negated by the Lawgiver. This is the preferred reconciliation of the two reports. And God Most High knows best. I have prolonged this discussion only because the need is pressing: this work was composed at a time of epidemic. May God preserve us from its harm. [B184]","anchor":"en-q2-243-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-243-s4","r":"q2-243","title":"The alternative account and gratitude amid affliction","text":"It is also said that those who left their homes were Israelites commanded to fight. Fearing death in battle, they left their homes to escape it. God caused them to die so that they would know nothing could save them from death, then brought them to life and commanded them to fight in His words: “Fight in the path of God.” “God is indeed bountiful towards people”: He sent His mercy upon them, and they fled from it, yet He did not punish them, but brought them back to life after death. “But most people do not give thanks”: only a few understand the blessings folded within afflictions and therefore thank God in both ease and adversity.","anchor":"en-q2-243-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-243-s5","r":"q2-243","title":"Death to personal interests, life through gnosis","text":"Have you not considered, listener, those who left the homes of their habits and the homelands of their desires? They are the company of those stripped of attachments ( أهل التجريد ), seeking purity of the affirmation of unity ( التوحيد ) and immersion in the sea of singleness ( التفريد ), fearing that their spirits might die through ignorance and separation ( الفرق ). God chose them for His presence and drew them to witnessing His Essence. He said to them: “Die to your personal interests and become absent from your existence.” When they died to their interests and became absent from their existence, God brought them to life through knowledge and gnosis. God is indeed bountiful towards people: He opened for them the door of wayfaring and prepared them to know the King of kings. But most people do not give thanks. He discloses Himself to them and makes Himself known, while they are unaware—except those whose inward sight God opens, and few they are.","anchor":"en-q2-243-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-243-s6","r":"q2-243","title":"","text":"The Real then urges the believers to struggle in His cause.","anchor":"en-q2-243-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-244","r":"q2-244","title":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path","text":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path 2:244","anchor":"unit-q2-244"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-244-1","r":"q2-244","title":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path","text":"وَقاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ (244)","anchor":"ar-q2-244-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-244-2","r":"q2-244","title":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقاتِلُوا الكفار فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وإعلاء كلمة الله حتى يكون الدين كله لله، وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ لأقوالكم ودعائكم، عَلِيمٌ بنياتكم وإخلاصكم، فيجازي المخلصين، ويحرم المخلطين.","anchor":"ar-q2-244-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-244-3","r":"q2-244","title":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path","text":"الإشارة: وجاهدوا نفوسكم في طريق الوصول إلى الله، وأديموا السير إلى حضرة الله، فحضرة القدوس محرمة على أهل النفوس. قال الششتري:","anchor":"ar-q2-244-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-244-4","r":"q2-244","title":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path","text":"إنْ تُرِدَ وَصْلَنَا فَمَوْتكَ شَرْطٌ ... لا يَنَالُ الوِصَالَ مَنْ فِيه فَضْلَه","anchor":"ar-q2-244-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-244-5","r":"q2-244","title":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path","text":"ومجاهدة النفس هو تحميلها ما يثقل عليها، وبُعدها مما يخف عليها، حتى لا يثقل عليها شيء، ولا تشره إلى شيء، بل يكون هواها ما يقضيه عليها مولاها. قيل لبعضهم: [ما تشتهي؟ قال: ما يقضي الله] . واعلموا أيها السائرون أن الله سميع لأذكاركم، عليم بإخلاصكم ومقاصدكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-244-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-244-6","r":"q2-244","title":"2:244 · Striving in God’s path","text":"ولما كان الجهاد يحتاج إلى مؤنة التجهيز، وليس كل الناس يقدر على ذلك، رَغَّبَ الحق تعالى الأقوياء بالإنفاق على الفقراء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-244-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-244-s1","r":"q2-244","title":"The intention of struggle","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: fight the unbelievers in God’s path, raising God’s word, until religion belongs wholly to God. Know that God hears your words and prayers and knows your intentions and sincerity. He recompenses the sincere and deprives those whose motives are mixed.","anchor":"en-q2-244-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-244-s2","r":"q2-244","title":"Training the self until it accepts its Lord’s decree","text":"Struggle against your selves on the path of reaching God, and persist in travelling towards His presence, for the presence of the All-Holy is forbidden to those still possessed by their selves. Al-Shushtarī said: If you desire union with us, your death is a condition; one in whom a remnant remains does not attain union. [B186] Struggling against the self means making it bear what it finds burdensome and keeping it from what it finds easy, until nothing burdens it and it eagerly desires nothing. Its desire then becomes whatever its Master decrees for it. Someone was asked: “What do you desire?” He replied: “Whatever God decrees.” Know, travellers, that God hears your remembrances and knows your sincerity and purposes.","anchor":"en-q2-244-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-244-s3","r":"q2-244","title":"","text":"Since fighting requires the expense of preparation, and not everyone can afford it, the Real Most High encourages those with means to spend upon the poor.","anchor":"en-q2-244-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-245","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion 2:245","anchor":"unit-q2-245"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-1","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"مَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يُقْرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرْضاً حَسَناً فَيُضاعِفَهُ لَهُ أَضْعافاً كَثِيرَةً وَاللَّهُ يَقْبِضُ وَيَبْصُطُ وَإِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ (245)","anchor":"ar-q2-245-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-2","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"قلت: القرض هو القطع، أطْلِقَ على السلف لأن المُقْرِضَ يقطع قطعة من ماله ويدفعها للمستلف، والمراد بها الصدقة لأن المتصدق يدفع الصدقة فيردها الحق تعالى له بضعف أمثالها فأشبهت القرض في مطلق الرد.","anchor":"ar-q2-245-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-3","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: مَنْ هذا الذي يعامل الله تعالى ويقرضه قَرْضاً حَسَناً بأن يتصدق على عباده صدقة حسنة بنية خالصة، فيُكثرها الله تعالى له أَضْعافاً كَثِيرَةً بسبعمائة إلى ما لا نهاية له، ولا يحمله خوف الفقر على ترك الصدقة فإنَّ الله تعالى يقبض الرزق عمن يشاء ولو قل إعطاؤه، ويبسط الرزق على من يشاء ولو كثر إعطاؤه، بل يقبض على من قبض يده شحّاً وبخلاً، ويبسط على من بسط يده عطاءً وبذلاً، يقول: «يا ابن آدم أنفق أنفق عليك» ، «أُنْفِقْ ولا تَخْش من ذي العرش إقلالا» .","anchor":"ar-q2-245-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-4","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"ونسبة القرض إليه تعالى ترغيب وتقريب للإفهام، كما قال في الحديث القدسي: «يقول اللهُ تعالى يوم القيامة: يَا ابْنَ آدَمَ، مَرِضْتُ فَلَمْ تَعُدْني، قَالَ: يَا رَبّ! كَيْفَ أَعُودُكَ وأنت رب العالمين؟ قال: أَمَا عَلِمْتَ أَنَّ عَبْدِي فُلاَناً مَرِضَ فَلَمْ تَعُدْهُ. أَمَا إِنَكَ لَوْ عُدْتَهُ لوجدتنى عنده. يَا ابْنَ آدَم اسْتَطْعَمتُكَ فَلَمْ تُطْعِمني. قال:","anchor":"ar-q2-245-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-5","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"يَا رَبّ! كَيْفَ أُطْعِمُكَ وَأَنْتَ رب العالمين؟ قال: أما علمت أَنَّهُ اسْتَطْعَمَكَ عَبْدِي فُلاَنٌ فَلَمْ تُطْعمْه؟ أَمَا عَلِمْتَ أَنَّكَ لَوْ أَطْعَمْتَه لَوَجَدْتَ ذَلكَ عِنْدِي. يَا ابْنَ آدم استسقيتك فلم تسقنى. قال: يا رب كيف أَسْقِيك وَأَنْتَ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِينَ؟","anchor":"ar-q2-245-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-6","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"قال: اسْتَسْقَاكَ عَبْدِي فُلاَنٌ فَلَمْ تسْقِه. أَمَا عَلِمْتَ أَنَّكَ لَوْ سَقَيْتَهُ لوَجَدْتَ ذَلِكَ عِنْدِي» .","anchor":"ar-q2-245-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-7","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"الإشارة: من هذا الذي يقطع قلبه عن حب الدارين، ويرفع همته عن الكونين، فإن الله (يضاعفه له أضعافاً كثيرة) بأن يُمَلِّكَهُ الوجودَ بما فيه، «أنت مع الأكوان ما لم تشهد المكون، فإذا شهدت المكون كانت الأكوان","anchor":"ar-q2-245-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-8","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"معك» ، (والله يقبض ويبسط) فيقبض الوجود تحت حكمك وهمتك، إن رفعت همتك عنه، ويبسط يدك بالتصرف فيه، إن علقت همتك بخالقه. أو يقبض القلوب بالفقد والوحشة، ويبسطها بالإيناس والبهجة. أو يقبض الأرواح بالوفاة، ويبسطها بالحياة. والقبض والبسط عند أهل التصوف: حالتان تتعاقبان على القلوب تعاقب الليل والنهار، فإذا غلب حال الخوف كان مقبوضا، وإذا غلب حال الرجاء كان مبسوطاً، وهذا حال السائرين. أما الواصلون فقد اعتدل خوفهم ورجاؤهم، فلا يؤثر فيهم قبض ولا بسط، لأنهم مالكو الأحوالَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-245-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-9","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"قال القشيري: فإذا كاشف العبدَ بنعت جماله بسطَه، وإذا كاشفه بنعت جلاله قَبضه. فالقبض يوجب إيحاشَه، والبسط يُوجب إيناسه، واعلم أنه يَرُدُّ العبد إلى حال بشريته، فيقبضه حتى لا يُطيق ذَرَّة، ويأخذه مَرَّة عن نعوته، فيجد لحمل ما يَرِدُ عليه قدرة وطاقة، قال الشّبلى رضي الله عنه: (من عَرَفَ الله حمَل السموات والأرض على شَعرة من جَفْن عينه، ومن لم يعرف الله- جلّ وعلا- لو تعلق به جَناح بعوضة لضجَّ) .","anchor":"ar-q2-245-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-10","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"وقال أهل المعرفة: [إذا قَبض قَبض حتى لا طاقة، وإذا بسط بسط حتى لا فاقة، والكل منه وإليه] . ومن عرف أن الله هو القابض الباسط، لم يَعتِب أحداً من الخلق، ولا يسكن إليه في إقبال ولا إدبار، ولم ييأس منه في البلاء، ولا يسكن إليه في عطاء، فلا يكون له تدبير أبداً. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-245-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-11","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"ولكلٍّ من القبض والبسط آداب، فآداب القبض: السكون تحت مجاري الأقدار، وانتظار الفرج من الكريم الغفار.","anchor":"ar-q2-245-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-12","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"وآداب البسط: كف اللسان، وقبض العنان، والحياء من الكريم المنان. والبسط مَزَلَّة أقدام الرجال. قال بعضهم: (فُتح عليَّ بابٌ من البسط فزللتُ زَلَّة، فحُجِبْتُ عن مقامي ثلاثين سنة) . ولذلك قيل: قف على البساط وإياك والانبساطَ واعلم أن القبض والبسط فوق الخوف والرجاء، وفوق القبض والبسط: الهيبة والأنس فالخوف والرجاء للمؤمنين، والقبض والبسط للسائرين، والهيبة والأنس للعارفين، ثم المحو في وجود العين للمتمكنين، فلا هيبة لهم، ولا أنس، ولا علم، ولا حس. وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q2-245-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-13","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"فلو كُنْتَ مِنْ أَهلِ الوُجودِ حقيقةً ... لغبْتَ عَن الأكوانِ والعرشِ والكرسي","anchor":"ar-q2-245-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-14","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"وكُنْتَ بلا حالٍ مَع اللهِ واقفاً ... تُصان عَنْ التّذْكَارِ للجِن والإنس(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-245-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-245-15","r":"q2-245","title":"2:245 · The goodly loan, contraction and expansion","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى قصة من أمر بالجهاد فجبن عنه، ترهيبا من التشبه به، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-245-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-245-s1","r":"q2-245","title":"Why charity is called a loan","text":"I say: qarḍ ( القرض ) means cutting. It is applied to a loan because the lender cuts off a portion of his property and gives it to the borrower. Here it means charity: the donor gives it, and the Real Most High returns it to him multiplied many times. It thus resembles a loan in the general respect of being returned.","anchor":"en-q2-245-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-245-s2","r":"q2-245","title":"Giving to God through giving to His servants","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: who will deal with God Most High and lend Him a goodly loan by giving His servants a good charity with a sincere intention? God will multiply it for him many times: seven hundredfold and beyond, without end. Fear of poverty must not make him abandon charity. God restricts provision for whom He wills, even if that person gives little, and expands provision for whom He wills, even if he gives much. Rather, He restricts the one who withholds his hand through avarice and miserliness, and expands the one who opens his hand in giving and generosity. He says: “Son of Adam, spend, and I shall spend upon you”; and, “Spend, and do not fear impoverishment from the Possessor of the Throne.” [B187] Attributing the loan to God Most High encourages giving and brings the meaning within reach of understanding. Thus the sacred report ( حديث قدسي ) says: “God Most High will say on the Day of Resurrection: ‘Son of Adam, I was ill and you did not visit Me.’ He will reply: ‘Lord, how could I visit You when You are Lord of the worlds?’ He will say: ‘Did you not know that My servant so-and-so was ill, and you did not visit him? Had you visited him, you would have found Me with him. Son of Adam, I asked you for food and you did not feed Me.’ He will reply: ‘Lord, how could I feed You when You are Lord of the worlds?’ He will say: ‘Did you not know that My servant so-and-so asked you for food, and you did not feed him? Had you fed him, you would have found that with Me. Son of Adam, I asked you for drink and you did not give Me drink.’ He will reply: ‘Lord, how could I give You drink when You are Lord of the worlds?’ He will say: ‘My servant so-and-so asked you for drink, and you did not give him drink. Had you given him drink, you would have found that with Me.’” [B187]","anchor":"en-q2-245-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-245-s3","r":"q2-245","title":"Raising aspiration beyond the two worlds","text":"Who will cut his heart free from love of the two abodes and raise his aspiration beyond the two worlds? God will multiply this for him many times by granting him mastery over existence and all it contains. “You are with created things so long as you do not witness their Maker. When you witness their Maker, created things are with you.” “God contracts and expands”: He gathers existence beneath your judgment and aspiration if you raise your aspiration beyond it, and extends your hand to exercise disposal within it if you attach your aspiration to its Creator. Or He contracts hearts through loss and loneliness, and expands them through intimacy and joy. Or He contracts spirits through death and expands them through life.","anchor":"en-q2-245-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-245-s4","r":"q2-245","title":"The states of contraction and expansion","text":"Among the people of Sufism, contraction and expansion ( القبض والبسط ) are two states that alternate upon hearts as night and day alternate. When fear predominates, the heart is contracted; when hope predominates, it is expanded. This is the state of travellers. As for those who have arrived, their fear and hope are balanced. Neither contraction nor expansion affects them, for they have become masters of states. [B188] Al-Qushayrī said: when He unveils Himself to the servant through the quality of His beauty, He expands him; when He unveils Himself through the quality of His majesty, He contracts him. Contraction brings loneliness, and expansion brings intimacy. Know that He returns the servant to his human condition and contracts him until he cannot bear a speck; at another time He takes him away from his own attributes, and he finds power and capacity to bear whatever comes upon him. Al-Shiblī said: “One who knows God can carry the heavens and earth upon a hair of his eyelid. One who does not know God—majestic and exalted is He—would cry out if the wing of a gnat were attached to him.” The people of gnosis said: “When He contracts, He contracts until no capacity remains; when He expands, He expands until no need remains. All is from Him and to Him.” Whoever knows that God is the Contractor and Expander ( القابض الباسط ) reproaches no creature and rests in none, whether approaching or withdrawing. He does not despair of Him in affliction or settle into complacency with Him in a gift; he therefore never engages in self-directed planning. Here the quotation ends.","anchor":"en-q2-245-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-245-s5","r":"q2-245","title":"The proper conduct of each state","text":"Each of contraction and expansion has its proper manners ( آداب ). The manners of contraction are stillness beneath the courses of the decrees and awaiting relief from the Generous, the Forgiving. The manners of expansion are restraining the tongue, drawing in the reins and having modesty before the Generous Bestower. Expansion is a place where men’s feet slip. One of them said: “A door of expansion opened to me. I slipped once and was veiled from my station for thirty years.” Hence the saying: “Stand upon the carpet ( البساط ), but beware of overfamiliarity ( الانبساط ).” Know that contraction and expansion are above fear and hope; above contraction and expansion are awe and intimacy ( الهيبة والأنس ). Fear and hope belong to believers; contraction and expansion to travellers; awe and intimacy to gnostics. Then comes effacement within the existence of the very Reality ( المحو في وجود العين ), for those firmly established. They have neither awe nor intimacy, neither knowledge nor sensation. They recited: Had you truly been among the people of Being, you would have been absent from created things, the Throne and the Footstool; you would have stood with God, without a state, preserved from recollection of jinn and humankind.","anchor":"en-q2-245-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-245-s6","r":"q2-245","title":"","text":"The Real then relates the story of people commanded to fight who shrank from it, warning against resembling them.","anchor":"en-q2-245-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-246","r":"q2-246","title":"2:246 · A request to fight and the test of resolve","text":"2:246 · A request to fight and the test of resolve 2:246","anchor":"unit-q2-246"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-246-1","r":"q2-246","title":"2:246 · A request to fight and the test of resolve","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الْمَلَإِ مِنْ بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ مِنْ بَعْدِ مُوسى إِذْ قالُوا لِنَبِيٍّ لَهُمُ ابْعَثْ لَنا مَلِكاً نُقاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ قالَ هَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ إِنْ كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتالُ أَلاَّ تُقاتِلُوا قالُوا وَما لَنا أَلاَّ نُقاتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَقَدْ أُخْرِجْنا مِنْ دِيارِنا وَأَبْنائِنا فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتالُ تَوَلَّوْا إِلاَّ قَلِيلاً مِنْهُمْ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِالظَّالِمِينَ (246)","anchor":"ar-q2-246-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-246-2","r":"q2-246","title":"2:246 · A request to fight and the test of resolve","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أَلَمْ تَرَ يا محمد- فتعتبر- إِلَى قصة جماعة مِنْ بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ مِنْ بَعْدِ موت مُوسى حين طلبوا الجهاد، وقالوا لِنَبِيٍّ لَهُمُ يقال له: شمويل، وقيل: شمعون: ابْعَثْ لَنا مَلِكاً يَسوس أمرنا ونرجع إليه في رأينا إذ الحرب لا تستقيم بغير إمام نُقاتِلْ معه فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، قالَ لهم ذلك النبيّ: هَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ إِنْ كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتالُ أَلَّا تُقاتِلُوا أي: هل أنتم قريب من التولي والفرار إن كُتب عليكم القتال؟ والمعنى: أتوقع جُبْنكم عن القتال إنْ فُرض عليكم. والأصل: عساكم أن تجبنوا إن فرض عليكم، فأدخل (هل) على فعل التوقع، مستفهماً عما هو المتوقع عنده، تقريراً وتثبيتاً.","anchor":"ar-q2-246-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-246-3","r":"q2-246","title":"2:246 · A request to fight and the test of resolve","text":"قالُوا في جوابه: وَما لَنا أَلَّا نُقاتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أيْ: أيُّ مانع يمنعنا من القتال وقد وُجد داعيه؟ وهو تسلط العدو علينا فأخْرَجَنَا من ديارنا وأسَرَ أبناءَنا، وكان الله تعالى سلط عليهم جالوت ومن معه من العمالقة، كانوا يسكنون ساحل بحر الروم(1) بين مصر وفلسطين، وذلك لمَّا عصوا وسفكوا الدماء، فخرَّبَ بيت المقدس، وحرق التوراة، وأخذ التابوت الذي كانوا ينتصرون به، وسبي نساءهم وذراريهم(2) . رُوِيَ أنه سبي من أبناء ملوكهم أربعمائة وأربعين، فسألوا نبيهم أن يبعث لهم ملكاً يجاهدون معه، فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتالُ ويَسر لهم ملكاً يسوسهم وهو طالوت، جبنُوا وتولوا إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِنْهُمْ، وهم من عَبَرَ النهر مع طالوت، وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِالظَّالِمِينَ فيخزيهم ويُفسد رأيهم. نعوذ بالله من ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-246-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-246-4","r":"q2-246","title":"2:246 · A request to fight and the test of resolve","text":"الإشارة: ترى كثيراً من الناس يتمنون أن لو ظفروا بشيخ التربية، ويقولون: لو وجدناه لجاهدنا أنفسنا أكثر من غيرنا، فلما ظهر، وعُرف بالتربية، تولى ونكص على عقبيه، وتعلل بالإنكار وعدم الأهلية، إلا قليلاً ممن خصه الله بعنايته (وَاللَّهُ يَخْتَصُّ بِرحمَتِهِ مَن يَشَاءُ) . (واللَّهُ ذو الفضل العظيم) . سبحان مَن لم يجعل الدليل على أوليائه إلا من حيث الدليل عليه، ولم يوصل إليهم إلا مَن أراد أن يوصله إليه.","anchor":"ar-q2-246-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-246-5","r":"q2-246","title":"2:246 · A request to fight and the test of resolve","text":"ثم عيّن لهم الملك الذي طلبوا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-246-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-246-s1","r":"q2-246","title":"The request and the anticipated retreat","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: have you not considered, Muḥammad, and taken a lesson from the story of a group of Israelites after Moses’ death? They sought to fight and said to a prophet of theirs called Shumwīl, or, according to another account, Shamʿūn: “Appoint a king for us to govern our affairs and to whom we may refer our decisions, for warfare cannot be conducted properly without a leader. We shall fight with him in God’s path.” Their prophet said: “Might you, if fighting were prescribed for you, fail to fight?” Are you likely to turn away and flee if fighting is prescribed? That is, I anticipate that you will shrink from fighting if it is made obligatory. The underlying construction is: “You may shrink if it is made obligatory.” The interrogative hal ( هل ) is introduced before the verb of anticipation, questioning them about what he expects, to make them acknowledge and confirm their intention. They replied: “What should prevent us from fighting in God’s path when the cause that calls for it exists?” Their enemy had gained power over them, driven them from their homes and taken their children captive. God Most High had subjected them to Jālūt and the Amalekites with him, who inhabited the coast of the Sea of the Romans between Egypt and Palestine. This happened when they disobeyed and shed blood. He laid Jerusalem waste, burned the Torah, took the Ark through which they had obtained victory, and captured their women and children. It is related that he captured four hundred and forty sons of their kings. [B189] They therefore asked their prophet to appoint a king with whom they could fight. When fighting was prescribed and He provided them with a king to govern them, Ṭālūt, they grew afraid and turned away, except for a few: those who crossed the river with Ṭālūt. God knows the wrongdoers; He disgraces them and brings their counsels to ruin. We seek God’s protection from that.","anchor":"en-q2-246-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-246-s2","r":"q2-246","title":"The wish for a guide and the response when one appears","text":"You see many people wishing they could find a shaykh of spiritual nurture. They say: “If we found him, we would struggle against our selves more than others.” Yet when he appears and becomes known for spiritual nurture, the person turns away and retreats, making excuses through denial and allegations of unfitness—except a few whom God singles out for His care. “God singles out for His mercy whom He wills”; “God is possessed of immense bounty.” Glory to Him who has made the indication of His saints accessible only in the same manner as the indication of Himself, and who brings to them only those whom He wishes to bring to Himself.","anchor":"en-q2-246-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-246-s3","r":"q2-246","title":"","text":"He then identifies the king they had requested.","anchor":"en-q2-246-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-247","r":"q2-247","title":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage","text":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage 2:247","anchor":"unit-q2-247"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-247-1","r":"q2-247","title":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage","text":"وَقالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ بَعَثَ لَكُمْ طالُوتَ مَلِكاً قالُوا أَنَّى يَكُونُ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ عَلَيْنا وَنَحْنُ أَحَقُّ بِالْمُلْكِ مِنْهُ وَلَمْ يُؤْتَ سَعَةً مِنَ الْمالِ قالَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفاهُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَزادَهُ بَسْطَةً فِي الْعِلْمِ وَالْجِسْمِ وَاللَّهُ يُؤْتِي مُلْكَهُ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ (247)","anchor":"ar-q2-247-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-247-2","r":"q2-247","title":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ شمويل: إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ بَعَثَ لَكُمْ ملكاً، أي: عيَّنه لكم لتقاتلوا معه، وهو طالُوتَ وهو عَلَمٌ عِبْراني كدَاوُد، قالُوا تعنتاً وتشغيباً: أَنَّى يَكُونُ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ عَلَيْنا أي من أين يستأهل التملك علينا وليس من دار الملك؟ لأن المملكة كانت في أولاد يهوذا، وطالوت من أولاد بنيامين، والنبوة كانت في أولاد لاوى. وقالوا: نَحْنُ أَحَقُّ بِالْمُلْكِ مِنْهُ وراثة ومُكْنة، لأن دار المملكة فينا. وأيضاً هو فقير لَمْ يُؤْتَ سَعَةً مِنَ الْمالِ يتقوى به على حرب عدوه، وكان طالوت فقيراً راعياً أو سَقَّاءً أو دباغاً. قالَ لهم نبيهم- عليه السلام-: إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفاهُ عَلَيْكُمْ رغم أنفكم. قال وهب بن منبه: أوحى الله إلى نبيهم: إذا دخل عليك رجل فَنَش الدُهنَ(1) الذي في القرن(2) فهو ملكهم، فلما دخل طالوت نَشَّ الدهن.","anchor":"ar-q2-247-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-247-3","r":"q2-247","title":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage","text":"وقال السدي: أرسل الله إليه عَصا، وقال له: إذا دخل عليك رجل على طول هذه العصا فهو ملكهم، فكان ذلك طالوت فتبيَّن أن الله تعالى اصطفاه للملك، وَزادَهُ بَسْطَةً فِي الْعِلْمِ فكان أعلم بني إسرائيل بالتوراة وقيل:","anchor":"ar-q2-247-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-247-4","r":"q2-247","title":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage","text":"بالحروب وعلم السياسة. وزاده أيضاً بسطة في الْجِسْمِ، فكان أطولُ بني إسرائيل يبلغ إلى مَنْكبِهِ. وذلك ليكون أعظم خطَراً في القلوب، وأقوى على مقاومة العدو ومكابدة الحروب، (والله يؤتي ملكه من يشاء) لأنه ملك الملوك","anchor":"ar-q2-247-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-247-5","r":"q2-247","title":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage","text":"يضع مُلكه حيث شاء، (والله واسع) فيوسع على الفقير ويغنيه بلا سبب، (عليم) بمن يليق بالملك بسبب وبلا سبب.","anchor":"ar-q2-247-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-247-6","r":"q2-247","title":"2:247 · Kingship is not measured by wealth or lineage","text":"ثم ذكر آية أخرى تدل على ملكه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-247-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-247-s1","r":"q2-247","title":"God’s choice and the qualifications of the king","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: their prophet Shumwīl told them: “God has appointed a king for you”—designated him so that you may fight with him—namely Ṭālūt, a Hebrew proper name like Dāwūd. In obstinacy and contentiousness, they said: “How can he have kingship over us?” How is he entitled to rule us when he is not of the royal house? Kingship belonged to the descendants of Judah, whereas Ṭālūt descended from Benjamin; prophecy belonged to the descendants of Levi. They said: “We have a stronger right to kingship than he,” by inheritance and power, for the royal house is among us. Moreover, he is poor and has not been given wealth with which to strengthen himself against his enemy. Ṭālūt was a poor shepherd, water-carrier or tanner. [B189] Their prophet said: “God has chosen him over you,” despite your displeasure. Wahb ibn Munabbih said: God revealed to their prophet, “When a man enters your presence and the oil in the horn begins to seethe, he is their king.” When Ṭālūt entered, the oil seethed. Al-Suddī said: God sent him a staff and said, “When a man as tall as this staff enters, he is their king.” This proved to be Ṭālūt, and it became clear that God Most High had chosen him for kingship. “He increased him in knowledge”: he was the most knowledgeable Israelite in the Torah; or, according to another account, in warfare and the science of government. [B190] He also increased his bodily stature: the tallest Israelite reached only to his shoulder. This made his standing greater in people’s hearts and strengthened him to resist the enemy and endure warfare. “God grants His kingship to whom He wills,” for He is the King of kings, placing His kingship wherever He wills. God is All-Encompassing: He enriches and enlarges the poor man’s means without an intermediary cause. He knows who is fit for kingship, with or without such a cause.","anchor":"en-q2-247-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-247-s2","r":"q2-247","title":"","text":"He then mentions another sign indicating his kingship.","anchor":"en-q2-247-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-248","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election 2:248","anchor":"unit-q2-248"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-1","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"وَقالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ إِنَّ آيَةَ مُلْكِهِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَكُمُ التَّابُوتُ فِيهِ سَكِينَةٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَبَقِيَّةٌ مِمَّا تَرَكَ آلُ مُوسى وَآلُ هارُونَ تَحْمِلُهُ الْمَلائِكَةُ إِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ لَآيَةً لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ (248)","anchor":"ar-q2-248-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-2","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"قلت: قال الجوهري: أصل التابوت: تأبُوة، مثل تَرْقُوة وهي فَعْلُوةٌ، فلما سُكِّنتْ الواو، انقلبت هاء التأنيث تاءٌ، فلغة قريش بالتاء، ولغة الأنصار بالهاء.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-3","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ لَمَّا طلبوا منه الحجة على اصطفاء طالوت للملك: إِنَّ آيَةَ مُلْكِهِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَكُمُ التَّابُوتُ وهو صندوق من خشب الشمشار مُمَوَّه بالذهب، طوله ثلاثة أذرع في سعة ذراعين فِيهِ سَكِينَةٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ أي: فيه ما تسكن إليه قلوبكم وتثبت عند الحرب. وكانوا يُقدمونه أمامهم في الحروب فلا يفرون، ويُنصرون على عدوهم، وقيل: كان فيه صور الأنبياء من آدم عليه السلام إلى محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم. وقيل: كان فيه طَسْت من ذهب غُسلت به قلوب الأنبياء- عليهم السلام- وهى السكينة- وفيه بَقِيَّةٌ مِمَّا تَرَكَ آلُ مُوسى وهي رُضاض الألواح(1)، وعصا موسى، وثيابه، وعمامة هارون والآل: مقحم فيهما.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-4","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"تَحْمِلُهُ الْمَلائِكَةُ قال وهب: لما صار التابوت عند القوم الذين غلبوا بني إسرائيل- فوضعوه في كنيسة لهم فيها أصنام، فكانت الأصنام تُصبح مُنكسرة، فحملوه إلى قرية قوم، فأصاب أولئك القومَ أوجاعٌ، فقالوا: ما هذا إلا لهذا التابوت، فلنتركه إلى بني إسرائيل، فأخذوا عَجَلَةً فجعلوا التابوت عليها وربطوها ببقرتين، وأرسلوهما نحو بلاد بني إسرائيل، فبعث الله ملائكة تسوق البقرتين حتى دخلتا على بني إسرائيل، وهم في أمر طالوت فأيقنوا بالنصر.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-5","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"وقيل غير ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-6","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"وقوله تعالى: إِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ لَآيَةً لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ يحتمل أن يكون من كلام نبيهم، أو من كلام الحق تعالى لنبينا- عليه الصلاة والسلام-.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-7","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"الإشارة: من شأن غالب النفوس ألا تقبل الخصوصية عند أحد حتى تظهر علامتُها، ولذلك طالب الكفارُ الرسلَ بالمعجزات، وطالب العوامُ الأولياءَ بالكرامات، ويكفي في الولي استقامة ظاهره، وتحقيق اليقين في باطنه.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-8","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"قال الشيخ أبو الحسن رضي الله عنه: «إنما هما كرامتان جامعتان محيطتان: كرامة الإيمان بمزيد الإيقان ونعت العيان، وكرامة العمل على السنة والمتابعة، وترك الدعاوى والمخادعة، فَمنْ أُعطيهما ثم جعل يشتاق إلى غيرهما فهو مفتر كذاب، أو ذو خطأ في العلم والعمل ... » الخ كلامه رضي الله عنه.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-9","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"وقال في العوارف: وقد يكون مَنْ لا يُكَاشَفُ بشيء من معاني القَدَر أفضل ممن يكاشف بها، إذا كاشفه الله تعالى بصرف المعرفة، فالقدرة أثر من القادر، ومن أُهِّل لقرب القادر لا يستغرب ولا يستكثر شيئاً من القدرة، ويرى القدرة تتجلّى من سُحُب أجزاء عالم الحكمة. فالكرامة إنما تظهر للقلوب المضطربة والنفوس المتزلزلة، وأما من سكن قلبه باليقين واطمأنت نفسه بالعيان لم يحتج إلى دليل ولا برهان إذ الجبال الراسية لا تحتاج إلى دُعامة، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-10","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"وكل من طالب أهلَ الخصوصية بالكرامة الحسية ففيه نزعة إسرائيلية، حيث قالوا لنبيهم بعد أن عيَّن لهم مَنْ أكرمه الله بخصوصية الملك: (أَنَّى يَكُونُ لَهُ الملك عَلَيْنَا وَنَحْنُ أَحَقُ بِالْمُلْكِ منه) . ورد الحق تعالى عليهم بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-248-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-11","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"وَاللَّهُ يُؤْتِي مُلْكَهُ مَنْ يَشاءُ. وما أظهر لهم كرامة التابوت إلا بعد امتناعهم من الجهاد المُتَعَيَّنِ عليهم رحمةٌ بهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-248-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-248-12","r":"q2-248","title":"2:248 · The Ark, tranquillity and the signs of spiritual election","text":"ثم كمّل قصة خروجهم إلى العدو، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-248-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-248-s1","r":"q2-248","title":"The form of the word tābūt","text":"I say: al-Jawharī said that the original form of tābūt ( التابوت ) is tābuwa ( تابوة ), like tarquwa ( ترقوة ), on the pattern faʿluwa . When the wāw was made quiescent, the feminine hāʾ became a tāʾ . Quraysh’s usage has tāʾ , and the Helpers’ usage hāʾ . [B191]","anchor":"en-q2-248-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-248-s2","r":"q2-248","title":"The return of the Ark","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when they asked for proof that Ṭālūt had been chosen as king, their prophet told them: “The sign of his kingship is that the Ark will come to you.” It was a gilded chest of boxwood, three cubits long and two cubits broad. “In it is tranquillity from your Lord”: that through which your hearts find rest and remain firm in battle. They would place it before them in warfare, not flee, and receive victory over their enemy. It is said that it contained representations of the prophets from Adam to Muḥammad. Another account says that it contained a gold basin in which the prophets’ hearts had been washed, and that this was the tranquillity ( السكينة ). It also contained a remnant of what Moses’ family left: fragments of the Tablets, Moses’ staff and clothes, and Aaron’s turban. “Family” ( آل ) is inserted in both expressions. [B191] “The angels carry it.” Wahb said: when the Ark came into the possession of the people who had defeated Israel, they put it in a sanctuary containing idols. Each morning the idols were found broken. They carried it to another people’s village, but pains afflicted that people. They said: “This is only because of this Ark; let us return it to Israel.” They placed it on a cart, harnessed two cows to it and sent them towards Israel’s land. God sent angels to drive the cows until they entered among the Israelites while these were occupied with Ṭālūt’s affair. They then became certain of victory. Other accounts are also given. “In that is indeed a sign for you, if you are believers” may be the words of their prophet, or the words of the Real Most High to our Prophet.","anchor":"en-q2-248-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-248-s3","r":"q2-248","title":"The greatest wonders are certainty and faithful practice","text":"Most selves will not acknowledge spiritual election ( الخصوصية ) in someone until its sign appears. Hence the unbelievers demanded miracles from the messengers, and ordinary people demand extraordinary gifts ( كرامات ) from saints. Yet the saint’s outward uprightness and inward realization of certainty suffice. Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan said: “There are only two comprehensive, all-embracing extraordinary gifts: the gift of faith, through increased certainty and the quality of direct vision; and the gift of action in accordance with the Sunna and following the Prophet, abandoning claims and deception. Someone given these two who then longs for something else is a fabricating liar, or mistaken in knowledge and action …”—to the end of his words. [B192] In the ʿAwārif it is said: someone to whom nothing of the meanings of destiny ( القدر ) is unveiled may be better than one to whom they are unveiled, if God unveils to him pure gnosis. Power ( القدرة ) is an effect of the Powerful ( القادر ). One made fit for nearness to the Powerful finds nothing in power strange or excessive; he sees power disclosing itself through the clouds formed by the parts of the world of wisdom. Extraordinary gifts appear only for unsettled hearts and wavering selves. Someone whose heart rests in certainty and whose self is tranquil through direct vision needs neither evidence nor proof. Firmly rooted mountains need no supporting prop. And God Most High knows best. Everyone who demands a sensory wonder from people of spiritual election has an Israelite tendency in him. After their prophet had identified the person whom God honoured with the distinction of kingship, they said: “How can he have kingship over us when we have a stronger right to kingship than he?” The Real Most High answered them: “God grants His kingship to whom He wills.” He showed them the wonder of the Ark only after they refused the fighting incumbent upon them, as a mercy to them. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-248-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-248-s4","r":"q2-248","title":"","text":"He then completes the story of their march towards the enemy.","anchor":"en-q2-248-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-249","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire 2:249","anchor":"unit-q2-249"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-1","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"فَلَمَّا فَصَلَ طالُوتُ بِالْجُنُودِ قالَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مُبْتَلِيكُمْ بِنَهَرٍ فَمَنْ شَرِبَ مِنْهُ فَلَيْسَ مِنِّي وَمَنْ لَمْ يَطْعَمْهُ فَإِنَّهُ مِنِّي إِلاَّ مَنِ اغْتَرَفَ غُرْفَةً بِيَدِهِ فَشَرِبُوا مِنْهُ إِلاَّ قَلِيلاً مِنْهُمْ فَلَمَّا جاوَزَهُ هُوَ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ قالُوا لا طاقَةَ لَنَا الْيَوْمَ بِجالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ قالَ الَّذِينَ يَظُنُّونَ أَنَّهُمْ مُلاقُوا اللَّهِ كَمْ مِنْ فِئَةٍ قَلِيلَةٍ غَلَبَتْ فِئَةً كَثِيرَةً بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ (249)","anchor":"ar-q2-249-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-2","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"قلت: قال في القاموس: غرف الماء يغرفه: أخذه بيده، كاغْتَرَفه، والغَرْفَةُ للمَرَّة، وبالكسر: هيئة الغرف وبالضم: اسم للمفعول، كالغرافة، لأنك ما لم تغرفه لا تسميه غُرْفَة، ثم قال: والغُرْفَةُ، بالضم: العُلِّيَّة(1) .","anchor":"ar-q2-249-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-3","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولما اتفقوا على مُلك طالوت تجهز للخروج، وقال: لا يخرج معه إلا الشبابُ النشيط الفارغُ ليس وراءه علقة(2) ، فاجتمع ممن اختار ثمانون ألفا، وقيل: ثلاثون، فلما انفصل عن بلده بالجنود وساروا في البيداء، - وكان وقت الحرِّ والقيّظ- عطشوا، وسألوا طالوتَ أن يُجري لهم نهراً، فقال لهم بوحْي، أو بإلهام، أو بأمر نبيهم: إِنَّ اللَّهَ مُبْتَلِيكُمْ أي: مُختبركم بِنَهَرٍ بسبب اقتراحكم، فَمَنْ شَرِبَ مِنْهُ كَرْعاً بلا واسطة فَلَيْسَ مِنِّي أي: من جيشي، وَمَنْ لَمْ يَطْعَمْهُ أي: يَذْقه، فَإِنَّهُ مِنِّي إِلَّا مَنِ اغْتَرَفَ غُرْفَةً بِيَدِهِ فإنها تكفيه لنفسه ولفرسه، فالاستثناء من الجملة الأولى.","anchor":"ar-q2-249-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-4","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"فَشَرِبُوا مِنْهُ أي: كَرعُوا، وسقطوا على وجوههم، إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِنْهُمْ ثلاثُمائةٍ وأربعةَ عشر، على عدد أهل بدر، وقيل: ألفاً. رُوِيَ أن من اقتصر على الغَرفة كَفَتْه لشربه ودوابه، ومن لم يقتصر غلب عطشُه، واسودَّتْ شفتُه ولم يقدْر أن يمضيَ. وعن ابن عباس: أن القومَ شربوا على قدر يقينهم: فالكفار شربوا شُربَ الهيم، وشَرِب العاصي دون ذلك، وانصرف من القوم ستةٌ وسبعون ألفاً، وبقي بعضُ المؤمنين لم يشرب شيئاً، وأخذ بعضهم الغَرفة، فأما من شرب فاشتد به العطشُ وسقط، وأما من ترك الماءَ فحسن حالُه، وكان أجلَد ممن أخذ الغرفة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-249-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-5","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وحكمة هذا الامتحان: ليتخلص للجهاد المطيعون المخلصون، إذ لا يقع النصر إلاَّ بهم، فلما جاوز النهرَ طالوتُ ومن بقيَ معه ممن لم يشربْ قال بعضهم لبعض: لا طاقَةَ لَنَا الْيَوْمَ بِجالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ لكثرتهم وقلة عددنا، قالَ الَّذِينَ يَظُنُّونَ أي: يَتَيَقَّنْون أَنَّهُمْ مُلاقُوا اللَّهِ ويتوقعون ثوابَ الشهادة وهم الخُلْصُ من أهل البصيرة: لا تفزعوا من كثرة عددهم كَمْ مِنْ فِئَةٍ قَلِيلَةٍ غَلَبَتْ فِئَةً كَثِيرَةً بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وإرادته ومعونته، و «كم» للتكثير، وَاللَّهُ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ بالنصر والمعونة.","anchor":"ar-q2-249-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-6","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"الإشارة: قال بعض الحكماء: الدنيا كنهر طالوت، لا ينجو منها إلا من لم يشربْ أو اغترف غرفةً بيده، فمن أخذ منها قَدْرَ الضرورةِ كَفَتْه، ونَشَطَ لعبادة مولاه، ومن أخذ فوق الحاجة حُبس في سجنها، وكان أسيرا فى يدها.","anchor":"ar-q2-249-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-7","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وقال بعضهم: طالبُ الدنيا كشارب ماءِ البحر، كلما زاد شربه ازداد عطشه. هـ. وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم: «من أُشرب قلبه حُبَ الدنيا التاط(1) منها بثلاث: بشغل لا ينفد عناه، وأمل لا يبلغ منتهاه، وحرص لا يدرك مداه» وقال عيسى عليه السلام: الدنيا مزرعة لإبليس، وأهلها حراث له. هـ. وقال على رضي الله عنه: الدنيا كالحية: لَيِّن مسها، قاتل سمها، فكن احذر ما تكونُ منها، أَسَرَّ ما تكون بها فإن من سكن منها إلى إيناس أزاله عنها إيحاش.","anchor":"ar-q2-249-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-8","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «مِنْ هوان الدنيا على الله أنه لا يُعصى إلا فيها، ولا ينال ما عنده إلا بتركها» .","anchor":"ar-q2-249-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-9","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وقال سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه-: أول الدنيا عناء، وآخرها فناء، حلالها حساب، وحرامها عقاب، ومتشابهها عتاب، من استغنى فيها فُتن، ومن افتقر فيها حزن. هـ. وقيل: الدنيا تُقبل إقبال الطالب، وتُدبر إدبار الهارب، وتصل وصال الملول، وتُفارق فراق العجول، خيرها يسير، وعمرها قصير، ولذاتها فانية، وتبعاتها باقية.","anchor":"ar-q2-249-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-10","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وقال عيسى عليه السلام: تعملون للدنيا، وأنتم تُرزقون فيها بغير عمل، ولا تعملون للآخرة وأنتم لا ترزقون فيها إلا بالعمل. هـ. وقيل: أوحى الله إلى الدنيا: مَنْ خدَمني فاخدِميه، ومن خدمك فاستخدِميه.","anchor":"ar-q2-249-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-11","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وكان عمرُ بنُ عبد العزيز يتمثل بهذه الأبيات(2) :","anchor":"ar-q2-249-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-12","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"نهارك يا مغرورُ سهوٌ وغفلةٌ ... وليلُكَ نومٌ، والأسَى لك لازمٌ","anchor":"ar-q2-249-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-13","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"تُسَرُّ بما يفْنَى، وتفرحُ بالمُنَى ... كما سُرَّ باللذَّات في النومِ حالمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-249-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-14","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وشغلُك فيها سوف تكرَه غَبَّه ... كذلك في الدنيا تَعيِشُ البهائمُ","anchor":"ar-q2-249-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-15","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"وقال آخر(3) :","anchor":"ar-q2-249-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-16","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"هي الدارُ دَارُ الأذى والقذى ... ودارُ الفناءِ ودارُ الْغِيَرْ","anchor":"ar-q2-249-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-17","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"فلو نِلْتَها بحذافيرها ... لمِتَّ ولم تقض منها الوطرْ","anchor":"ar-q2-249-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-18","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"أيا مَنْ يؤملُ طولَ الخلودِ ... وطولُ الخلودِ عليه ضررْ","anchor":"ar-q2-249-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-19","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"إذا ما كبِرْتَ وفات الشبَابُ ... فلا خيرَ في العيش بعد الكبر","anchor":"ar-q2-249-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-249-20","r":"q2-249","title":"2:249 · The river’s test and the thirst of worldly desire","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى قصة جالوت وملك داود عليه السلام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-249-20"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-249-s1","r":"q2-249","title":"Gharfa, ghirfa and ghurfa","text":"I say: the Qāmūs states: gharafa al-māʾa yaghrifuhu means taking water with one’s hand, as does ightarafahu . Gharfa , with fatḥa , denotes a single act; ghirfa , with kasra , the manner of scooping; and ghurfa , with ḍamma , what is scooped, like ghurāfa , for before it is scooped one does not call it a ghurfa . It then says that ghurfa , with ḍamma , also means an upper chamber.","anchor":"en-q2-249-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-249-s2","r":"q2-249","title":"The testing of the army","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when they agreed to Ṭālūt’s kingship, he prepared to march, saying that only active young men, free from responsibilities and without ties left behind, should accompany him. Eighty thousand of those he selected assembled; another account says thirty thousand. When he departed his town with the forces and they travelled through the wilderness, in the heat of summer, they became thirsty and asked him to make a river flow for them. By revelation, inspiration or his prophet’s command, he told them: “God will test you with a river,” because of your request. “Whoever drinks from it”—lapping directly without an intervening vessel—“is not of me,” not of my army. “Whoever does not taste it is of me—except one who scoops a handful,” which will suffice him and his horse. The exception refers back to the first clause. They drank from it, lapping and falling upon their faces, except a few: three hundred and fourteen, corresponding to the people of Badr; or, according to another account, a thousand. It is related that those who restricted themselves to one handful found it sufficient for themselves and their animals. Those who did not became overwhelmed by thirst, their lips blackened, and they could not continue. [B193] Ibn ʿAbbās is reported to have said that they drank according to the measure of their certainty. The unbelievers drank like thirst-stricken camels, and the disobedient less than that. Seventy-six thousand turned back. Some believers remained who drank nothing, while others took a handful. Those who drank became intensely thirsty and collapsed; those who left the water fared well and were stronger than those who took a handful. The wisdom of this test was to single out the obedient and sincere for the struggle, since victory comes only through them. When Ṭālūt and those remaining with him who had not drunk crossed the river, some said to others: “We have no strength today against Jālūt and his forces,” because they are many and we are few. Those certain that they would meet God, expecting the reward of martyrdom—the pure people of inward sight—said: “Do not be alarmed by their numbers. How many a small company has overcome a large company by God’s leave,” His will and assistance. Kam ( كم ) expresses multitude here. God is with the steadfast through victory and assistance.","anchor":"en-q2-249-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-249-s3","r":"q2-249","title":"Take from the world only what is needed","text":"One of the sages said: this world is like Ṭālūt’s river. Only someone who does not drink, or scoops a handful, escapes it. Whoever takes only what is necessary finds it sufficient and becomes energetic in worshipping his Master. Whoever takes more than he needs is confined in its prison and held captive in its hand. Someone said: the seeker of the world resembles a drinker of seawater—the more he drinks, the thirstier he becomes. The Prophet is quoted as saying: “Someone whose heart is made to drink love of the world becomes attached through it to three things: occupation whose toil never ends, hope whose limit is never reached, and eagerness whose utmost extent is never attained.” Jesus said: “The world is Iblīs’s field, and its people are his cultivators.” [B194] ʿAlī said: “The world is like a snake: soft to touch, deadly in its venom. Be most wary of it when most delighted by it. Whoever rests in it through familiarity is driven from it through estrangement.” The Prophet is also quoted as saying: “A sign of the world’s insignificance before God is that He is disobeyed only within it, and what is with Him is attained only by abandoning it.” Our master ʿAlī, may God ennoble his face, said: “The world begins in toil and ends in passing away. Its lawful things entail an accounting; its unlawful things punishment; its doubtful things reproach. Whoever becomes wealthy in it is tried; whoever becomes poor in it grieves.” [B194] It is said: the world approaches like a seeker and retreats like a fugitive. It joins like someone easily bored, and separates like someone in haste. Its good is little, its life short, its pleasures passing and its consequences enduring. Jesus said: “You work for this world, although you are provided for in it without work. You do not work for the Hereafter, although you will receive no provision there except through work.” It is also said that God revealed to the world: “Serve whoever serves Me, and make whoever serves you serve you.” [B194] ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz used to cite these verses: Your day, deluded one, is heedlessness and neglect; your night is sleep, while sorrow clings to you. You delight in what passes and rejoice in wishes, as a dreamer delights in pleasures during sleep. The aftermath of your occupation with it you will hate: so do the beasts live in this world. Another said: This abode is an abode of hurt and irritation, an abode of passing away and change. Even were you to obtain it in its entirety, you would die without satisfying your desire for it. You who hope for prolonged abiding— prolonged abiding would harm you. When you have aged and youth has passed, there is no good in life after old age.","anchor":"en-q2-249-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-249-s4","r":"q2-249","title":"","text":"The Real then relates the story of Jālūt and the kingship of David.","anchor":"en-q2-249-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-250-252","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained 2:250–252","anchor":"unit-q2-250-252"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-1","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"وَلَمَّا بَرَزُوا لِجالُوتَ وَجُنُودِهِ قالُوا رَبَّنا أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنا صَبْراً وَثَبِّتْ أَقْدامَنا وَانْصُرْنا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكافِرِينَ (250) فَهَزَمُوهُمْ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَقَتَلَ داوُدُ جالُوتَ وَآتاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَهُ مِمَّا يَشاءُ وَلَوْلا دَفْعُ اللَّهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لَفَسَدَتِ الْأَرْضُ وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْعالَمِينَ (251) تِلْكَ آياتُ اللَّهِ نَتْلُوها عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَإِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ (252)","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-2","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولما برز طالوت بمَن معه لِجالُوتَ، أي: ظهر في البرَاز، ودنا بعضهم من بعض، تضرعوا إلى الله واستنصروه، وقالوا: رَبَّنا أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنا صَبْراً أي: أصْبُبْه علينا صبّاً، وَثَبِّتْ أَقْدامَنا عند اللقاء لئلا نَفِرّ، وَانْصُرْنا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكافِرِينَ. وفي دعائهم ترتيب بليغ سألوا أولاً إفراغ الصبر في قلوبهم الذي هو ملاك الأمر، ثم ثبات القدمِ في مَدَاحِضِ الحرب المُسببِ عنه، ثم النصرَ على العدو المرتب عليها غالباً.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-3","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"فهزم الله عدوَّهم وأجاب دعاءهم بإذنه وقدرته، وَقَتَلَ داوُدُ جالُوتَ. وقصة قتله: أن أصحاب طالوت كان فيهم بنو إيش، وهو أبو داود عليه السلام ستة أو سبعة، وكان داود صغيراً يرعى غنماً، فلما حضرت الحرب قال فى نفسه: لأذهبن لرؤية هذه الحرب، فمرَّ في طريقه، بحجر فناداه: يا داود خُذْني، فبي تقتل جالوت، ثم ناداه حجر آخر ثم آخر فأخذها، وجعلها في مخلاته وسار، فلما حضر البأس خرج جالوت يطلب البراز، وكاع الناس عنه(1)، أي: تأخروا خوفاً، حتى قال طالوت: من يبرز له ويقتله فأنا أزوجه ابنتي، وأُحَكِّمُهُ في مالي، فجاء داود، فقال له طالوت: اركب فرسي وخذ سلاحي، ففعل، وخرج في أحسن شكله، فلما مشى قليلاً رجع، فقال الناس: جَبُنَ الفتى، فقال داود: إن الله سبحانه لم يقتله ولم يُعنى عليه، لم ينفعني هذا الفرس ولا هذا السلاح، ولكني أحب أن أقاتله","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-4","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"على عادتي. وكان داود من أرمى الناس بالمقلاع، فنزل، وأخذ مخلاته فتقلدها، وأخذ مقلاعه فخرج إلى جالوت، وهو شاكٍ في السلاح(1)، فقال جالوت: أنت يا فتى تخرج إليّ! قال، نعم، قال: هكذا كما تخرج إلى الكلب! قال:","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-5","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"نعم، وأنت أهون، قال: لأطعمن لحمك اليوم الطير والسباع، ثم تدانيا فأدار داود فأخذ مقلاعه وأدخل يده إلى الحجارة، فروى أنها التأمت، وصارت حجراً واحداً، فأخذه ووضعه في المقلاع، وسَمَّى الله، وأداره، ورماه، فأصاب رأس جالوت فقتله، وجزّ رأسه، وجعله في مخلاته، واختلط الناس، وحمل أصحابُ طالوت فكانت الهزيمة.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-6","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"ثم إن داود جاء يطلب شرطه من طالوت، فقال: حتى تقتل مائتين من هؤلاء الجراجمة(2) الذين يؤذون الناس وتجيئني بسلبهم، فقتل داود منهم مائتين، وجاء بذلك، فدفع إليه امرأته وتخلّى له عن الملك(3) . ولما تمكن داود- عليه السلام- من الملك، أجلى من بقي من قوم جالوت إلى المغرب، فمن بقيتهم البرابرة من الشلوح وسائر الأرياف.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-7","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"فآتى اللهُ داود الْمُلْكَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وهي النبوة، وقيل: صنعة الدروع ومنطق الطير وَعَلَّمَهُ مِمَّا يَشاءُ من أنواع العلوم والمعارف والأسرار، وقد دفع الله بأس الكافرين ورد كيدهم في نحرهم، وَلَوْلا دَفْعُ اللَّهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لَفَسَدَتِ الْأَرْضُ أي: لولا أنَّ الله يدفع بعض الناس ببعض، فينصر المسلمين على الكافرين، ويكف فسادهم، لغلبوا وأفسدوا في الأرض. أو: لولا أن الله نصب السلطان، وأقام الحكام لينصفوا المظلوم من الظالم، ويردوا القوي عن الضعيف، لتواثب الخلق بعضهم على بعض، وأكل القوي الضعيفَ فيفسد النظام. أو: لولا أن الله يدفع بالشهود عن الناس في حفظ الأموال والنفوس والدماء والأعراض، لوقع الفساد في الأرض.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-8","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"أو: لولا أن الله يدفع بأهل الطاعة والإحسان عن أهل الغفلة والعصيان، لفسدت الأرض بشؤم أهل العصيان.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-9","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"وفى الخبر عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «إنَّ الله يَدْفَعُ بالمُصلِّي مِنْ أمَّتِي عَمَّنْ لا يصلى، وبمن يُزكيَّ عَمَّنْ لاَ يُزَكِّي، وبمن يصوم،","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-10","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"عَمَّنْ لاَ يَصُوم، وبمَنْ يَحُجُّ، عَمَّنْ لاَ يَحُجُّ، وبَمَّنْ يُجاهِدُ عَمَّنْ لاَ يُجَاهِدُ. وَلَوِ اجْتَمَعُوا عَلَى تَرْكِ هذِهِ الأشْياءِ ما أنْظَرَهُمُ الله طَرْفة عَيْنٍ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-11","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"وفي حديث آخر: «لولا عباد لله رُكَّع، وصبية رُضَّع، لصبَّ عَليكُمُ العَذَابُ صَبًّا» . ورَوى جابر رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «إن الله ليُصْلِحُ بصلاح الرجل- ولده وولد ولدهِ، وأهل دُوَيْرَتِه، ودويراتٍ حوله، ولا يزالون في حفظ الله مادام فيهم» . هـ. فهذا من فضل الله على عباده يصلح طالحهم بصالحهم، ويُشَفع خيارُهُم في شرارهم، ولولا ذلك لعوجلوا بالهلاك، وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْعالَمِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-12","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"تِلْكَ يا محمد، آياتُ اللَّهِ والإشارة إلى ما قصَّ من حديث الألوف، وتمليك طالوت، وإتيان التابوت، وانهزام الجبابرة أصحاب جالوت، نَتْلُوها أي: نقصها عليكم بِالْحَقِّ أي: بالوجه المطابق الذي لا يَشُك فيه أهل الكتاب وأرباب التواريخ، وَإِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ حيث أخبرتَ بها من غير تعرف ولا استماع ولم يعهد منك تعلم ولا اطلاع، فلا يشك أنه مِنْ عند الخبير العليم، إلا من طَبع اللهُ على قلبه. نعوذ بالله من ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-13","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"الإشارة: «من علامة النجح في النهايات الرجوع إلى الله في البدايات» ، فإذا برز المريد لجهاد أعدائه من النفس وَالهوى والشيطان وسائر القُطاع، واستنصر بالله وتبرأ من حوله وقوته، كان ذلك علامة على نصره وظفره بنفسه، وكان سبباً في نجح نهايته، فيملكه الله الوجود بأسره، ويفتح عليه من خزائن حكمته. قال أبو سليمان الداراني: (إذا اعتادت النفوس على ترك الآثام، جالت في الملكوت ثم عادت إلى صاحبها بطرائف الحكم من غير أن يؤدي إليها عالم علماً) . وفي الخبر: «من عَمِلَ بِمَا عَلِمَ أَوْرَثَهُ اللهُ علمَ مَا لم يعلمْ» . وكان حينئذٍ رحمة للعباد، يدفع الله بوجوده العذاب عمن يستحقه من عباده.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-14","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"وفي الحديث القدسي: «يقول الله عزّ وجلّ: إذا كان الغالبَ على عبدي الاشتغالُ بي جعلتُ همته ولذَّته في ذكري، ورفعتُ الحجابُ فيما بيني وبينه، لا يسهو إذا سَهَا الناسُ، أولئك كَلاَمُهُم كلام الأنبياءِ، أولئك الأبطالُ حقًا، أولئك الذين إذا أردتُ بأهلِ الأرضِ عقوبةً أو عذابًا ذكرتُهم فصرفتُه بهم عنهم» . حقَّقنا الله بمحبتهم وجعلنا منهم.. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-250-252-15","r":"q2-250-252","title":"2:250–252 · David’s victory and the good through which corruption is restrained","text":"ولمَّا ذكر في هذه السورة جملة من الأنبياء والرسل، وشهد لرسوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه من المرسلين ذكر تفضيل بعضهم على بعض في الجملة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-250-252-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-250-252-s1","r":"q2-250-252","title":"The ordered prayer for victory","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when Ṭālūt and those with him came forth against Jālūt, appearing in the open ground and drawing near one another, they humbly supplicated God and sought His victory: “Our Lord, pour steadfastness upon us”—pour it forth abundantly—“make our feet firm” at the encounter, lest we flee, “and grant us victory over the unbelieving people.” Their supplication has an eloquent order. First they ask that steadfastness be poured into their hearts, since it is the foundation of the affair; then for firmness of foot in the slippery places of battle, which results from it; then for victory over the enemy, which ordinarily follows these two. God routed their enemy and answered their prayer by His leave and power. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-11] ]","anchor":"en-q2-250-252-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-250-252-s2","r":"q2-250-252","title":"David and Jālūt","text":"“David killed Jālūt.” The account of his killing is this. Among Ṭālūt’s companions were six or seven sons of Īsh, David’s father. David was a young boy tending sheep. When battle approached, he said to himself: “I shall go and see this battle.” On his way he passed a stone, which called: “David, take me; through me you will kill Jālūt.” Another stone called, then another. He took them, put them in his bag and continued. When the fighting began, Jālūt came out demanding single combat. The men kāʿū ( كاعوا ): they drew back in fear. Ṭālūt said: “Whoever goes out to him and kills him, I shall marry to my daughter and give authority over my property.” David came forward. Ṭālūt told him to mount his horse and take his arms. He did so and went out in splendid form. After a short distance, however, he returned. The men said: “The youth has lost courage.” David replied: “Unless God Most High kills him and assists me against him, this horse and arms will not benefit me. I prefer to fight him in my customary manner.” David was among the most skilful men with a sling. He dismounted, slung his bag over himself, took his sling and went out against Jālūt, who was fully armed. Jālūt said: “You, boy, come out against me?” He replied: “Yes.” “Like this, as you would go out against a dog?” “Yes—and you are more contemptible.” Jālūt said: “Today I shall feed your flesh to birds and beasts.” They drew near. David took his sling and reached for the stones. It is related that they joined into a single stone. He put it into the sling, named God, swung it and released it. It struck Jālūt’s head and killed him. He cut off his head and put it in his bag. The forces became intermingled, Ṭālūt’s companions charged, and the rout followed. David then asked Ṭālūt to fulfil his promise. He replied: “Not until you kill two hundred of these Jarājima who harm people and bring me their spoils.” David killed two hundred and brought them. Ṭālūt gave him his bride and relinquished kingship to him. When David was established as king, he expelled the remaining people of Jālūt to the Maghrib. The Berbers—the Shlūḥ and the inhabitants of the other rural regions—are said here to be their remnant. [B195]","anchor":"en-q2-250-252-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-250-252-s3","r":"q2-250-252","title":"The means by which God repels corruption","text":"God gave David kingship and wisdom: prophecy; or, according to another explanation, the craft of making coats of mail and the speech of birds. He taught him of whatever He willed: kinds of sciences, gnoses and mysteries. God repelled the might of the unbelievers and turned their plotting back upon them. “Were God not to repel some people by means of others, the earth would be corrupted.” Were He not to give Muslims victory over unbelievers and restrain their corruption, the latter would prevail and spread corruption on earth. Alternatively, were God not to establish rulers and judges to give the oppressed justice against the oppressor and restrain the strong from the weak, people would spring at one another, the strong consume the weak, and the order of things collapse. Or, were God not to protect property, lives, blood and honour through witnesses, corruption would arise on earth. Or, were God not to repel affliction from the heedless and disobedient through the people of obedience and goodness, the earth would be corrupted through the ill effects of disobedience. A report from the Prophet says: “Through those of my community who pray, God repels affliction from those who do not pray; through those who give alms, from those who do not give alms; through those who fast, from those who do not fast; through those who make pilgrimage, from those who do not; and through those who fight in His cause, from those who do not. Were they all to abandon these things, God would not grant them respite for the blink of an eye.” Another report says: “Were it not for servants of God bowing in prayer and infants suckling, punishment would be poured upon you abundantly.” [B196] Jābir related that the Messenger of God said: “Through a man’s righteousness, God sets right his child, his child’s child, the people of his little household and the households around him. They remain in God’s protection so long as he is among them.” This is God’s bounty towards His servants: He sets right their corrupt through their righteous and accepts the intercession of their best for their worst. Otherwise destruction would be hastened upon them. “But God is bountiful towards all worlds.” [B196]","anchor":"en-q2-250-252-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-250-252-s4","r":"q2-250-252","title":"The recitation of the signs and the proof of messengership","text":"“These, Muḥammad, are God’s signs.” The reference is to the account of the thousands, Ṭālūt’s appointment as king, the Ark’s arrival and the defeat of the tyrants who followed Jālūt. We recite—that is, relate—them to you in truth: in a corresponding account about which the People of the Book and possessors of historical knowledge have no doubt. You are indeed one of the messengers, since you have reported them without investigation or hearing them from others; no study or acquaintance with such matters was previously known of you. None doubts that this comes from the All-Aware, the Knowing, except one whose heart God has sealed. We seek God’s protection from that. [B195]","anchor":"en-q2-250-252-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-250-252-s5","r":"q2-250-252","title":"Return to God at the beginning, and serve as a mercy at the end","text":"“A sign of success at the end is returning to God at the beginning.” When the disciple comes forth to struggle against his enemies—the self, desire, Satan and the other highwaymen—and seeks God’s assistance, disavowing his own power and strength, this is a sign of his victory and triumph over his self, and a cause of success at his journey’s end. Through God he gains mastery over all existence, and the treasuries of His wisdom are opened to him. Abū Sulaymān al-Dārānī said: “When selves become accustomed to abandoning sins, they roam through the kingdom of the unseen ( الملكوت ), then return to their owner with rare wisdoms, without any scholar having communicated knowledge to them.” A report says: “Whoever acts upon what he knows, God bequeaths to him knowledge of what he did not know.” He then becomes a mercy to the servants: through his existence, God repels punishment from those of His servants who deserve it. [B197] In a sacred report, God, mighty and majestic, is quoted as saying: “When occupation with Me predominates in My servant, I place his aspiration and delight in My remembrance and raise the veil between Me and him. He is not heedless when people are heedless. Their speech is the speech of prophets; they are the true champions. When I intend a punishment or affliction for the people of the earth, I remember them and turn it away from the people through them.” May God establish us in their love and make us among them. Amen. [B197]","anchor":"en-q2-250-252-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-250-252-s6","r":"q2-250-252","title":"","text":"Having mentioned a number of prophets and messengers in this sūrah and testified that His Messenger is one of them, He speaks in general of the preference given to some over others.","anchor":"en-q2-250-252-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-253","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement 2:253","anchor":"unit-q2-253"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-1","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"تِلْكَ الرُّسُلُ فَضَّلْنا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلى بَعْضٍ مِنْهُمْ مَنْ كَلَّمَ اللَّهُ وَرَفَعَ بَعْضَهُمْ دَرَجاتٍ وَآتَيْنا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ الْبَيِّناتِ وَأَيَّدْناهُ بِرُوحِ الْقُدُسِ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-253-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-2","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"قلت: (تلك) : مبتدأ، و (الرسل) : نعت، أو بدل منه، أو بيان، و (فضلنا) ، خبر، أو (الرسل) خبر، و (فضلنا) : خبر ثان، والإشارة إلى الجماعة المذكور قَصَصُها في السورة.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-3","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: تِلْكَ الرُّسُلُ الذين قصصناهم عليك، وذكرتُ لك أنك منهم، فَضَّلْنا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلى بَعْضٍ بخصائص ومناقب لم توجد في غيره. لكن هذا التفضيل إنما يكون في الجملة من غير تعيين المفضول، لأنه تنقيص في حقه وهو ممنوع. ولذلك قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لا تُخَيِّرُوا بَيْنَ الأَنبِيَاءَ» ، «ولا تفضلوني على يونس بن متى» فإن معناه النهي عن تعيين المفضول، لأنه غيبة وتنقيص، وقد صرح صلّى الله عليه وسلم بفضله على جميع الأنبياء بقوله: «أنَا سَيِّدُ وَلَدِ آدَمَ ولا فخر» . لكن لا يُعَيِّن أحداً من الأنبياء بالمفضولية لئلا يؤدي إلى نقصه، فلا تعارُضَ بين الحديثين.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-4","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"مِنْهُمْ مَنْ كَلَّمَ اللَّهُ وهو موسى عليه السلام في جبل الطور، وسيدنا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم حين كان قاب قوسين أو أدنى، وَرَفَعَ بَعْضَهُمْ دَرَجاتٍ وهو نبيّنا محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم فإنه خُصَّ بالدعوة العامة، والحُجَج المتكاثرة، والمعجزات المستمرة، والآيات المتعاقبة بتعاقب الدهر، والفضائل العلمية والعملية الفائتة للحصر. والإبهام لتفخيم شأنه، كأنه العلم المشهور المتعين لهذا الوصف المستغني عن التعيين. وقيل: إبراهيم، خصه بالخلة التي هي أعلى المراتب.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-5","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"قلت: بل المحبة أعلى منها(1) ، وقيل: إدريس لقوله: وَرَفَعْناهُ مَكاناً عَلِيًّا، وقيل: أولو العزم من الرسل، قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-6","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"وَآتَيْنا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ الْبَيِّناتِ أي: الآيات الواضحات، كإحياء الموتى، وإبراء الأكمه والأبرص، (وأيدناه بروح القدس) ، أي: جبريل عليه السلام كان معه أينما سار، وخصَّه بالتعيين لإفراط اليهود والنصارى في تحقيره وتعظيمه، فردَّهم إلى الصواب باعتقاد نبوته دون ربوبيته.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-7","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"الإشارة: كما فضَّل الله الرسل بعضهم على بعض، كذلك فضل الأولياء بعضهم على بعض، وإنما يقع التفضيل بكمال اليقين، والتغلغل في علم التوحيد الخاص، ذوقاً وكشفاً، والترقي في المعارف والأسرار. وذلك بخدمة الرجال وصحبة أهل الكمال، والتفرغ التام، والزهد الكامل في النفس والفَلْس والجنْس، فمنهم من تحصل له المشاهدة وتصحبها المكالمة، ومنهم من تحصل له المشاهدة دون المكالمة، ومنهم من تحصل له الكرامات الواضحة، ومنهم من لا يرى شيئاً من ذلك استغناءً عنها بكرامة المعرفة. وما قيل في الرسل من عدم تعيين المفضول، مثله يقال في حق الأولياء، وإلا وقع في الغيبة الشنيعة فإن لحوم الأولياء سموم، فليعتقد الكمال في الجميع، ولا يصرح بتعيين المفضول كما تقدّم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-8","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"ولما ذكر الحقّ تعالى أحوال الرسل، وتفاوتهم في العناية، ذكر أحوال أممهم وتفاوتهم في الهداية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-253-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-9","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"... وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ مَا اقْتَتَلَ الَّذِينَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ وَلكِنِ اخْتَلَفُوا فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ آمَنَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ كَفَرَ وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ مَا اقْتَتَلُوا وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يُرِيدُ (253)","anchor":"ar-q2-253-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-10","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"قلت: إذا وقع فعل المشيئة بعد (لو) فالغالب حذف مفعوله، كقوله: وَلَوْ شِئْنا لَرَفَعْناهُ بِها، أي: لو شئنا رفعه لرفعناه بها، وكقوله: وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ مَا اقْتَتَلَ ... ، أي: لو شاء هدايتهم ما اقتتلوا، وغير ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-11","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولما بعثتُ الرسلَ، وفضَّلتُ بعضَهم على بعض، اختلفت أممهم من بعدهم فاقتتلوا، وكل ذلك بإرادتي ومشيئتي، وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ هداية أممهم مَا اقْتَتَلَ الَّذِينَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُمُ المعجزات الواضحات في تحقيق رسالتهم وصحة نبوتهم، وَلكِنِ اخْتَلَفُوا بغياً وحسداً فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ آمَنَ بتوفيقه لاتباع دين الأنبياء، وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ كَفَرَ بمخالفتهم، فكان من الأشقياء، وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ جمعهم على الهدى مَا اقْتَتَلُوا، لكن حكمته اقتضت وجود الاختلاف ليظهر سر اسمه المنتقم والقهار واسمه الكريم والحليم، وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَفْعَلُ ما يُرِيدُ لاَ يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-12","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"وفي الآية دليل على أن الحوادث كلها بيد الله خيرها وشرها، وأن أفعال العباد كلها بقدرته تعالى، لا تأثير لشيء من الكائنات فيها. وهذا يردُّ قول المعتزلة القائلين بخلق العبد أفعاله، فما أبعدهم عن الله. نسأل الله العصمة بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-13","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"الإشارة: اختلاف الناس على الأولياء سُنة ماضية وحكمة أزلية، وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لِسُنَّةِ اللَّهِ تَبْدِيلًا، وَلا يَزالُونَ مُخْتَلِفِينَ، فمن رأيته من الأولياء اتفق الناسُ على تعظيمه في حياته فهو ناقص أو جاهل بالله إذ","anchor":"ar-q2-253-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-14","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"الداخل على الله منكور، والراجع إلى الناس مبرور، وهذا هو الغالب، والنادر لا حكم له، فلو كان الاتفاق محموداً لكان على الأنبياء أولى، فلما لم يقع للأنبياء والرسل، لم يقع للأولياء إذ هم على قدمهم، وقائمون بالوراثة الكاملة عنهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-253-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-253-15","r":"q2-253","title":"2:253 · The messengers’ distinctions and the mystery of human disagreement","text":"ثم حضّ على الصدقة فى سبيل الله لأنها برهان الإيمان وعنوان الهداية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-253-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-253-s1","r":"q2-253","title":"The demonstrative and its predicate","text":"I say: “Those” ( تلك ) is the subject; “messengers” is its adjective, substitute or explanatory apposition ( نعت، بدل، بيان ); and “We favoured” is the predicate. Alternatively, “messengers” is the predicate and “We favoured” a second predicate. The demonstrative refers to the company whose stories have been mentioned in the sūrah.","anchor":"en-q2-253-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-253-s2","r":"q2-253","title":"Preference without disparagement","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those messengers whom We have related to you, and among whom I have said that you belong—We favoured some over others through distinctive gifts and virtues not found in another. This preference, however, is expressed generally, without identifying a particular prophet as inferior, since that diminishes him and is forbidden. Hence the Prophet said: “Do not make distinctions of superiority among the prophets,” and, “Do not prefer me over Jonah son of Mattā.” These prohibit identifying someone as inferior, which is backbiting and diminution. The Prophet nevertheless stated his superiority over all the prophets: “I am the master of the children of Adam, without boasting.” But no individual prophet is to be designated inferior, lest this lead to diminishing him. Thus the two reports do not conflict. [B198] “Among them are those to whom God spoke”: Moses upon Mount Ṭūr, and our master Muḥammad when he was “two bows’ lengths away or nearer.” “He raised some by degrees”: our Prophet Muḥammad, distinguished by a universal mission, abundant proofs, enduring miracles, signs succeeding one another throughout time, and virtues of knowledge and action beyond enumeration. Leaving him unnamed magnifies his standing, as though he were the well-known figure uniquely marked by this description and needing no explicit identification. Another explanation identifies Abraham, distinguished by intimate friendship ( الخلة ), said to be the highest rank. I say: rather, love ( المحبة ) is higher than it. Another identifies Idrīs, because of “We raised him to a lofty place” [19:57]; another, the messengers of firm resolve ( أولو العزم ). Al-Bayḍāwī gives these explanations. “We gave Jesus son of Mary the clear proofs”: manifest signs, such as raising the dead and healing the person born blind and the leper. “We strengthened him with the Holy Spirit”: Gabriel, who accompanied him wherever he went. He is explicitly named because of the Jews’ and Christians’ excesses in belittling and magnifying him. God returns them to the right course: belief in his prophethood, not his Lordship.","anchor":"en-q2-253-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-253-s3","r":"q2-253","title":"Degrees among the saints","text":"As God favoured some messengers over others, He favoured some saints over others. The distinction lies in perfected certainty, penetration into the special knowledge of unity through taste and unveiling, and ascent in gnoses and mysteries. It comes through serving the men of the path, accompanying people of perfection, complete freedom for the pursuit, and full renunciation of self, money and kindred attachments ( النفس والفلس والجنس ). Some attain witnessing together with divine address ( المكالمة ); some attain witnessing without address; some receive manifest extraordinary gifts; and some see none of these, having no need of them because of the gift of gnosis. What was said about not identifying an inferior among the messengers applies likewise to the saints. Otherwise one falls into dreadful backbiting: the flesh of saints is poisonous. Let one believe in the perfection of them all and not explicitly designate anyone inferior, as already explained. And God Most High knows best. The Real Most High, having mentioned the messengers’ states and their differing degrees of divine care, then mentions their communities and their differing degrees of guidance. Qurʾānic continuation · 2:253b وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ مَا اقْتَتَلَ الَّذِينَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ وَلكِنِ اخْتَلَفُوا فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ آمَنَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ كَفَرَ وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ مَا اقْتَتَلُوا وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَفْعَلُ ما يُرِيدُ Had God willed, those who came after them would not have fought one another after the clear proofs came to them. But they differed: some believed and some disbelieved. Had God willed, they would not have fought one another; but God does whatever He desires.","anchor":"en-q2-253-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-253-s4","r":"q2-253","title":"The omitted object of willing","text":"I say: when a verb of willing follows law ( لو ), its object is usually omitted. Thus “Had We willed, We would have raised him through them” [7:176] means: had We willed to raise him, We would have raised him through them. Likewise, “Had God willed, they would not have fought one another” means: had He willed their guidance, they would not have fought—and similarly elsewhere.","anchor":"en-q2-253-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-253-s5","r":"q2-253","title":"Disagreement, divine will and the manifestation of the Names","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: when I sent the messengers and favoured some over others, their communities differed after them and fought. All this occurred through My will and desire. Had God willed the guidance of their communities, those who came after them would not have fought after receiving the clear miracles establishing their messengership and authenticating their prophethood. But they differed through transgression and envy. Some believed, through His granting them success in following the prophets’ religion; some disbelieved by opposing them and became among the wretched. Had God willed to unite them upon guidance, they would not have fought. His wisdom, however, required disagreement to exist so that the mystery of His Names the Avenger ( المنتقم ) and the Subduer ( القهار ), and the Generous ( الكريم ) and the Forbearing ( الحليم ), might appear. God does whatever He desires. “He is not questioned about what He does, but they are questioned” [21:23]. The verse proves that all events, good and evil, are in God’s hand, and that all the servants’ acts occur through His power. Nothing created exercises efficacy within them. This refutes the Muʿtazilites’ assertion that the servant creates his acts. How far they are from God! We ask God for protection through His grace and generosity. [B199]","anchor":"en-q2-253-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-253-s6","r":"q2-253","title":"Disagreement over the saints","text":"People’s disagreement over saints is an established way and an eternal wisdom. “You will find no alteration in God’s way” [33:62]; “They do not cease to differ” [11:118]. Any saint you see whom everyone agrees to honour during his lifetime is deficient or ignorant of God, for one entering upon God is denied, while one returning to people is honoured. This is the general rule; the rare exception does not determine the judgment. Were agreement praiseworthy, the prophets would have had the strongest claim to it. Since it did not occur for prophets and messengers, it does not occur for saints, who follow in their footsteps and stand in complete inheritance from them. And God Most High knows best. [B200]","anchor":"en-q2-253-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-253-s7","r":"q2-253","title":"","text":"He then urges charity in God’s path, for it is a proof of faith and a sign of guidance.","anchor":"en-q2-253-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-254","r":"q2-254","title":"2:254 · Spend before the day when worldly transactions cease","text":"2:254 · Spend before the day when worldly transactions cease 2:254","anchor":"unit-q2-254"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-254-1","r":"q2-254","title":"2:254 · Spend before the day when worldly transactions cease","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْفِقُوا مِمَّا رَزَقْناكُمْ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ يَوْمٌ لا بَيْعٌ فِيهِ وَلا خُلَّةٌ وَلا شَفاعَةٌ وَالْكافِرُونَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ (254)","anchor":"ar-q2-254-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-254-2","r":"q2-254","title":"2:254 · Spend before the day when worldly transactions cease","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْفِقُوا مِمَّا رَزَقْناكُمْ واجباً أو تطوعاً في وجوه الخير، وخصوصاً في الجهاد الذي نحن بصدد الحضّ عليه، وقدموا لأنفسكم ما تجدونه بعد موتكم مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ يَوْمٌ الحساب، واقتضاء الثواب، يوم ليس فيه بَيْعٌ ولا شراء، فيكتسب ما يقع به الفداء، وليس فيه خُلَّةٌ تنفعُ إلا خلة الأتقياء، وَلا شَفاعَةٌ ترجى إِلَّا مَنْ أَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمنُ وَرَضِيَ لَهُ قَوْلًا فأنفقوا مما خولناكم في سبيل الله، وجاهدوا الكافرين أعداء الله، فإن الكافرين هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ حيث وضعوا عبادتهم في غير محلها، ونسبوا الربوبية لغير مستحقيها، إذ لا يستحقها إلا الحي القيوم، الذي أشار إليه الحق جلّ جلاله:","anchor":"ar-q2-254-2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-254-s1","r":"q2-254","title":"Prepare through giving before the accounting","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: you who believe, spend from what We have provided you, obligatorily or voluntarily, upon good causes—particularly the fighting in His cause that We are now urging. Send ahead for yourselves what you will find after death, before the day of accounting and the rendering of recompense arrives. On that day there is no buying or selling through which one might acquire a ransom; no friendship avails except the friendship of the reverent; and no intercession may be hoped for except that of one to whom the All-Merciful gives permission and whose speech He approves. Spend, then, in God’s path from what We have entrusted to you, and struggle against the unbelievers, God’s enemies. The unbelievers are the wrongdoers: they have placed their worship where it does not belong and attributed Lordship to those unworthy of it. Only the Living, the Self-Subsisting, merits it, as the Real, glorious is His majesty, indicates in the following verse.","anchor":"en-q2-254-s1"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-255","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool 2:255","anchor":"unit-q2-255"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-1","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"اللَّهُ لاَ إِلهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ لا تَأْخُذُهُ سِنَةٌ وَلا نَوْمٌ لَهُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ مَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَشْفَعُ عِنْدَهُ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِهِ يَعْلَمُ ما بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَما خَلْفَهُمْ وَلا يُحِيطُونَ بِشَيْءٍ مِنْ عِلْمِهِ إِلاَّ بِما شاءَ وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضَ وَلا يَؤُدُهُ حِفْظُهُما وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيمُ (255)","anchor":"ar-q2-255-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-2","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"قلت: (الله) : مبتدأ، وجملة (لاَ إله إِلاَّ هُوَ) : خبره، والضمير المنفصل بدل من المستتر في الخبر، و (الحي) : إما خبر ثان، أو لمبتدأ مضمر، أو بدل من (الله) ، و (قيوم) فَيْعُول، مبالغة من القيام، ومعناه: القائم بنفسه المستغني عن غيره.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-3","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: اللَّهُ الواجب الوجود لا يستحق العبادة غيره، فمن عبد غيره فقد أتى بظلم عظيم الْحَيُّ أي: الدائم بلا أول، الباقي بلا زوال الذي لا سبيل عليه للموت والفناء، الْقَيُّومُ أي: دائم القيام بتدبير خلقه في إيصال المنافع ودفع المضار، وجلب الأرزاق وأنواع الارتقاء، لا تَأْخُذُهُ سِنَةٌ وَلا نَوْمٌ السنة:","anchor":"ar-q2-255-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-4","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"ما يتقدم النوم من الفتور، والنوم: حالة تعرض للإنسان من استرخاء أعصاب الدماغ من رطوبات الأبخرة المتصاعدة، فتقف الحواس الظاهرة عن الإحساس رأساً.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-5","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"وتقديم السنَة عليه، على ترتيب الوجود، كقوله تعالى: وَلا يُنْفِقُونَ نَفَقَةً صَغِيرَةً وَلا كَبِيرَةً، وجمع بينهما لأنه لو اقتصر على نفى السنّة عنه لتوهم أن النوم يغلبه لأنه أشد، ولو اقتصر على نفي النوم لتوهم أن السنة تلحقه لخفتها. والمراد تنزيهه تعالى عن آفات البشرية، وتأكيد كونه حيّاً قيوماً، فإن من أخذه نعاس أو نوم يكون مؤوف الحياة(1)، قاصراً في الحفظ والتدبير. ولذلك ترك العطف فيه وفي الجمل التي بعدَه لأنها كلها مقررة له، أي: للحيّ للقيّوم.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-6","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"وقد ورد أنه اسم الله الأعظم، وقال عليه الصلاة والسلام لفاطمة- رضي الله عنها: «ما مَنَعك أن تَسْمَعي ما أُوصِيك به تَقُولين إذا أصْبَحْتِ وإذا أمْسَيتِ يا حيّ يا قيوم، برحمتِكَ أستغيث أصْلحْ لي شأني كُلَّه، ولا تَكلْني إلى نفْسِي طَرْفَةَ عَيْنِ» . رواه النسائي. وأخرج مسلم عن أبى موسى رضي الله عنه قال: «قَامَ فِينَا رسُولُ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بخَمْسِ كلماتٍ قال: إنَّ الله عزّ وجل لا ينامُ، ولا يَنْبَغِي لَهُ أنْ يَنَام، يَخْفِضُ القِسطَ ويَرْفَعُهُ. يُرْفَعُ إلَيْهِ عَمَلُ اللَّيل قَبْلَ عَمَلِ النَّهَارِ وعَمَلُ النَّهَارِ قَبْلَ عَملِ اللَّيلِ، حِجَابُهُ النُّورُ- وفي رواية. النَّارُ- لَوْ كَشَفَهُ لأحرقت سُبحات وجهه ما أدركه بَصَرُهُ مِنْ خَلْقِهِ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-255-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-7","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"لَهُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ هذا تقرير لقيوميته تعالى، واحتجاج على تفرده في الألوهية.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-8","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"والمراد بما فيهما: ما هو أعمُّ من أجزائهما الداخلة فيهما ومن الأمور الخارجة عنهما، المتمكنة فيهما، من العقلاء وغيرهم، فهو أبلغ من (له السموات والأرض وما فيهن) ، يعني: أن الله يملك جميع ذلك من غير شريك ولا منازع، وعبر ب- (ما) تغليبا للغالب.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-9","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"مَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَشْفَعُ عِنْدَهُ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِهِ هذا بيان لكبرياء شأنه، وأنه لا يدانيه أحد ليقدر على تغيير ما يريده بشفاعة واستكانة، فضلاً عن أن يعاوقه عناداً أو مناصبة. والاستفهام إنكاري، أي: لا أحد يشفع عنده لمن أراد تعالى عقوبته، إلا بإذنه، وذلك أن المشركين زعموا أن الأصنام تشفع لهم، فأخبر تعالى أنه لا شفاعة عنده إلا بإذنه، يريد بذلك شفاعة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وبعض الأنبياء والأولياء والملائكة.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-10","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"يَعْلَمُ ما بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَما خَلْفَهُمْ أي: ما قبلهم وما بعدهم، أو بالعكس، لأنك تستقبل المستقبل وتستدبر الماضي وقيل: يَعْلَمُ ما بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ من الدنيا وَما خَلْفَهُمْ من الآخرة، وقيل: عكسه، لأنهم يقدمون ويُخَلِّفُون الدنيا وراءهم، وقيل: يعلم ما قدموه بين أيديهم من خير أو شر، وما خلفهم وما هم فاعلوه، أو عكسه.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-11","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"والمراد أنه سبحانه أحاط بالأشياء كلها، فلا يخفى عليه شيء وَلا يُحِيطُونَ بِشَيْءٍ مِنْ عِلْمِهِ إِلَّا بِما شاءَ أي: لا يحيطون بشيء من معلوماته تعالى إلا بما شاء أن يُطْلعهم عليه، وعطفه على ما قبله لأن مجموعه يدل على تفرده تعالى بالعلم الذاتي التام، الدال على وحدانيته تعالى في ذاته وصفاته.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-12","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضَ يقال: فلان يسَعُ الشيء سعة إذا احتمله وأطاقه وأمكنه القيامُ به. ويقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-255-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-13","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"وسع الشيءُ الشيء إذا أحاط به وغمره حتى اضمحلّ في جانبه، وهذا المعنى هو اللائق هنا. وأصل الكرسي في اللغة: من تَركّب الشيء بعضه على بعض، ومنه الكراسة، لتركب أوراقها بعضها على بعض، وفي العرف: اسم لما يُقعد عليه، سُمِّي به لتركب خشباته. واختلف فيه فقيل: العرش، وقيل: غيره.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-14","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"والصحيح أنه مخلوق عظيم أمام العرش، فوق السموات السبع دون العرش. يقال: إن السموات والأرض في جنب الكرسي كحلقة في فلاة. والكرسي في جانب العرش كحلقة في فلاة. وعن ابن عباس: (أن السموات في الكرسي كدراهم سبعة في تُرْسٍ) وقيل: كرسيه: علمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-15","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"قال البيضاوي: هو تصوير لعظمته تعالى وتمثيل مجرد، كقوله وَما قَدَرُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهِ وَالْأَرْضُ جَمِيعاً قَبْضَتُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ وَالسَّماواتُ مَطْوِيَّاتٌ بِيَمِينِهِ ولا كرسي في الحقيقة ولا قاعد(1) . وقيل: كرسيه مجاز عن","anchor":"ar-q2-255-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-16","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"علمه أو ملكه، مأخوذ من كرسي العلم والملك، وقيل: جسم بين يدي العرش محيط بالسماوات السبع لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «ما السموات السبع والأرضون السبع في الكرسي إلا كحلقة في فلاة، وفضل العرش على الكرسي كفضل تلك الفلاة على تلك الحلقة» ولعله الفلك المشهور بفلك البروج. هـ. قلت: وقد اعترض السيوطي في حاشيته عليه(1) . فالله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-17","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"وَلا يَؤُدُهُ أي: لا يُثْقله ولاَ يُشقُّ عليه حِفْظُهُما أي: حفظ السموات والأرض. وإنما لم يتعرض لذكر ما فيهما لأن حفظهما مُسْتَتْبع لحفظه، وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ أي: المتعالي عن الأشباه والأنداد، الْعَظِيمُ أي: عظيم الشأن، جليل القدر، الذي يستحقر كلُّ شيء دون عظمته.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-18","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"وهذه الآية مشتملة على أمهات المسائل الإلهية، فإنها دالّة على أنه تعالى موجود واحد في الألوهية، متصف بالحياة الذاتية، واجب الوجود لذاته، موجد لغيره إذ القيوم هو القائم بنفسه المقيم لغيره، منزه عن التحيز والحلول، مُبرَّأ عن التغير والفتور، لا يناسب الأشباح، ولا يعتريه ما يعتري الأرواح، مالك الملك والملكوت، مبدع الأصول والفروع، ذو البطش الشديد، الذي لا يشفع عنده إلا من أذن له. عالم بالأشياء كلها: جليّها وخفيّها، كلّيّها وجِزْئيَّها.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-19","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"واسع الملك والقدرة لكل ما يصح أن يملك ويقدر عليه، لا يشقُّ عليه شاقٌّ، ولا يشغله شأن عن شأن، مُتَعَالٍ عن تناول الأوهام، عظيمٌ لا تحيط به الأفهام، ولذلك تفردت عن أخواتها بفضائل رائعة وخواص فائقة، قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم:","anchor":"ar-q2-255-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-20","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"«أعظمُ آيةٍ في القرآنِ آية الكرسىّ» . وقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «مَنْ قَرَأَ آيَةَ الكُرْسيّ دُبر كل صلاة مكتوبة لم يَمْنَعْهُ من دُخُولِ الْجنَّة إلا الموتُ- وفي رواية- كانَ الذي يَتوَلَّى قَبْضَ رُوحِه ذُو الجَلاَل والإكْرَام- ولا يُوَاظِبُ عليها إلا صِدِّيقٌ أو عَابدْ، ومن قَرَأها إذا أخَذ مَضْجَعَه أمن على نفْسِه وَجارِه وَجارِ جَارِه، والأبيات حوله» .","anchor":"ar-q2-255-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-21","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"وقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «ما قُرئت هذه الآيةُ في بيْت إلا هَجَرَتْهُ الشياطينُ ثلاثين يَوْماً، ولا يدْخُله ساحرُ ولا ساحرةٌ أربعين يوماً، يا عليّ علِّمْها ولدَك وأهلكَ وجيرانَك، فما نزلَتْ آيةٌ أعظمُ منها» . قاله البيضاوي وأبو السعود، وتكلم السيوطي في بعض هذه الأحاديث. والفضائل يعمل فيها بالضعيف. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-22","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"الإشارة: يا أيها الذين آمنوا أيمان أهل الخصوصية- (أَنفِقُواْ مما رزقناكم) من سعة العلوم ومخازن الفهوم، من قبل أن يأتي يوم اللقاء، يوم تسقط فيه المعاملات وتغيب تلك الإشارات، لا ينفع فيه إلا الدخول من باب الكرم،","anchor":"ar-q2-255-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-23","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"فيلقى الله بالله دون شيء سواه، والجاحدون لهذا هم الظالمون لأنفسهم، حيث اعتمدوا على أعمالهم فلقُوا الله بالصنم الأعظم. والحيُّ القيوم الكبير المتعال غني عن الانتفاع بالأعمال. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-24","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"ومن عرف أنه الحي الذي لا يموت توكل عليه. قال تعالى: وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْحَيِّ الَّذِي لا يَمُوتُ. والتعلق به: استمداد حياة الروح بالعلم والمحبة الكاملة. ومن عرف أنه الحي القيّوم وثق به، ونسي ذكر كل شيء بذكره، ولم يشاهد غيره بمشاهدة قيوميته. والتعلق به استمداد معرفة قيوميته حتى يستريح من نكد التدبير، والتخلق به بأن تكون قائماً على ما كُلِّفْتَ به من أهْلٍ وَوَلَدٍ ونَفْسٍ ومَالٍ، وكُلِّ من تعلق بك من النساء والرجال.","anchor":"ar-q2-255-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-255-25","r":"q2-255","title":"2:255 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting: the Verse of the Footstool","text":"ولمَّا وصف الحيُّ تعالى نفسه بأوصاف الكمال من الكبرياء والعظمة والجلال، وكانت شواهد ذلك ظاهرة في خلقه حتى تبيَّن الحق من الباطل، بيّن ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-255-25"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s1","r":"q2-255","title":"The divine Name and its predicates","text":"I say: “God” is the subject, and the sentence “there is no god but He” its predicate. The separate pronoun “He” ( هو ) substitutes for the pronoun implicit in the predicate. “The Living” is either a second predicate, the predicate of an omitted subject, or a substitute for “God.” Qayyūm ( قيوم ) has the intensive pattern fayʿūl , from standing or subsisting ( القيام ). It means the One who subsists through Himself, independent of anything else.","anchor":"en-q2-255-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s2","r":"q2-255","title":"Life, subsistence and transcendence","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: God, the Necessarily Existent, alone deserves worship. Whoever worships another has committed a tremendous wrong. “The Living”: enduring without beginning, abiding without cessation, beyond the reach of death and passing away. “The Self-Subsisting”: continually attending to the governance of His creation, conveying benefits, repelling harms, bringing provisions and the various forms of advancement. “Neither slumber nor sleep overtakes Him.” Slumber ( السنة ) is the lassitude preceding sleep. Sleep is a condition that overtakes the human being when the nerves of the brain relax because of the moisture of ascending vapours, so that the outward senses cease altogether to perceive. [B201] Slumber precedes sleep here in the order in which they occur, as in “They spend no small or great expenditure” [9:121]. Both are mentioned because negating slumber alone might suggest that sleep overcomes Him, since it is stronger; negating sleep alone might suggest that slumber affects Him, since it is lighter. The purpose is to declare Him transcendent above human afflictions and confirm that He is Living and Self-Subsisting. Someone overtaken by drowsiness or sleep has life affected by a deficiency and is limited in preservation and governance. Hence there is no coordinating conjunction here or before the subsequent sentences: each confirms the description “Living, Self-Subsisting.”","anchor":"en-q2-255-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s3","r":"q2-255","title":"The invocation of the Living, the Self-Subsisting","text":"It has been transmitted that this is God’s Greatest Name. The Prophet said to Fāṭima: “What prevents you from listening to my counsel? Say morning and evening: ‘Living, Self-Subsisting One, through Your mercy I seek relief. Set all my affairs right for me, and do not entrust me to my self for the blink of an eye.’” Al-Nasāʾī related it. [B202] Muslim transmits from Abū Mūsā: “The Messenger of God stood among us and spoke five sayings: ‘God, mighty and majestic, does not sleep, and it is not fitting that He sleep. He lowers the balance and raises it. The work of the night is raised to Him before the work of the day, and the work of the day before the work of the night. His veil is light’—in another transmission, ‘fire’—‘and were He to unveil it, the splendours of His Face would burn everything of His creation reached by His sight.’” [B203]","anchor":"en-q2-255-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s4","r":"q2-255","title":"Sovereignty, intercession and knowledge","text":"“To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth.” This confirms His sustaining governance ( قيوميته ) and argues for His uniqueness in divinity. What is in them includes their constituent parts and the things distinct from those parts but situated within them, rational beings and others. It is therefore more comprehensive than “To Him belong the heavens, the earth and what is in them.” He owns all this without partner or rival. Mā ( ما ) is used because the non-rational is predominant. “Who can intercede with Him except by His permission?” This makes clear the grandeur of His standing. No one approaches His rank so as to change what He wills through intercession and entreaty, much less resist Him through opposition or hostility. The question negates the possibility: no one intercedes for someone He intends to punish except by His leave. The associators claimed that the idols would intercede for them. He therefore declares that intercession with Him occurs only by His permission—meaning the intercession of the Prophet and of certain prophets, saints and angels. “He knows what is before them and what is behind them”: what preceded and what follows them; or the reverse, since you face the future and leave the past behind. It is also said: what is before them of this world and behind them of the Hereafter; or conversely, since they advance and leave this world behind. Or He knows the good and evil they have sent before them and the deeds still to come—or the reverse. The meaning is that He encompasses all things, and nothing is hidden from Him. “They encompass nothing of His knowledge except what He wills”: they encompass none of the things He knows except what He wills to disclose to them. This is coordinated with the preceding statement because the two together establish His unique possession of complete, intrinsic knowledge ( العلم الذاتي التام ), indicating His oneness in Essence and attributes.","anchor":"en-q2-255-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s5","r":"q2-255","title":"The Footstool and its interpretations","text":"“His Footstool embraces the heavens and the earth.” One says that someone yasaʿu a thing when he can bear it, has power over it and can attend to it. One also says that a thing encompasses another when it surrounds and overwhelms it, so that the second becomes insignificant beside it. This is the appropriate meaning here. The linguistic root of kursī ( الكرسي ) concerns the joining of one part to another. Hence kurrāsa ( الكراسة ), a gathering of written sheets, because its leaves are joined one upon another. In ordinary usage it denotes something upon which one sits, so named from the joining of its pieces of wood. There is disagreement about it: some identify it with the Throne, others distinguish them. The correct view is that it is a tremendous created thing before the Throne, above the seven heavens and below the Throne. It is said that the heavens and earth beside the Footstool are like a ring in a desert, and the Footstool beside the Throne like a ring in a desert. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “The heavens within the Footstool are like seven dirhams upon a shield.” Another interpretation identifies His Footstool with His knowledge. [B204] Al-Bayḍāwī said: it is a portrayal of His majesty and a purely figurative representation, like “They have not measured God with His true measure; the entire earth will be His handful on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens folded in His right hand” [39:67]. There is in reality neither a seat nor someone seated. Alternatively, His Footstool is a metaphor for His knowledge or sovereignty, drawn from the seat of learning or kingship. Or it is a body before the Throne, encompassing the seven heavens, in accordance with the Prophet’s saying: “The seven heavens and seven earths in the Footstool are only like a ring in a desert; the superiority of the Throne over the Footstool is like that desert’s superiority over that ring.” Perhaps it is the sphere known as the sphere of the zodiac. Here his words end. I say: al-Suyūṭī objected to this in his marginal commentary. God Most High knows best. [B204] “Preserving them does not burden Him”: preserving the heavens and earth does not weigh upon Him or cause Him difficulty. Their contents are not separately mentioned because preserving the two entails preserving what is in them. “He is the High”: exalted above likenesses and equals. “The Tremendous”: immense in standing and majestic in worth, beside whose greatness everything is deemed insignificant.","anchor":"en-q2-255-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s6","r":"q2-255","title":"The principal divine questions gathered in the verse","text":"This verse contains the principal questions concerning God ( أمهات المسائل الإلهية ). It indicates that He exists and is one in divinity; possesses life intrinsically; is necessarily existent through Himself and brings others into existence, since the Self-Subsisting is the One who subsists through Himself and sustains another. He is transcendent above occupying a location and indwelling ( التحيز والحلول ), free from change and lassitude. He does not resemble bodily forms, nor is He subject to what affects spirits. He owns the visible dominion and the unseen kingdom ( الملك والملكوت ), originates roots and branches, and is possessed of mighty force. None intercedes with Him except one whom He permits. He knows all things, manifest and hidden, universal and particular. His sovereignty and power extend to everything that can be possessed and fall under power. No difficulty burdens Him; no affair distracts Him from another. He is exalted beyond the reach of imaginings, Tremendous beyond the comprehension of understandings.","anchor":"en-q2-255-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s7","r":"q2-255","title":"The verse’s excellence","text":"For this reason it is distinguished from its fellows by splendid virtues and exceptional properties. The Prophet said: “The greatest verse in the Qurʾān is the Verse of the Footstool.” He is also quoted as saying: “Whoever recites the Verse of the Footstool after each prescribed prayer is prevented from entering the Garden only by death”—and in another transmission: “The Possessor of Majesty and Generosity Himself undertakes the taking of his spirit.” Further: “Only one utterly truthful or devoted to worship persists in it. Whoever recites it upon taking to bed is made secure in himself, his neighbour, his neighbour’s neighbour and the houses around him.” [B205] He is also quoted as saying: “This verse is not recited in a house without the devils abandoning it for thirty days; no male or female sorcerer enters it for forty days. ʿAlī, teach it to your children, family and neighbours: no greater verse than it has been revealed.” Al-Bayḍāwī and Abū al-Suʿūd mention this. Al-Suyūṭī criticised some of these reports. Weak reports are acted upon concerning virtues. And God Most High knows best. [B205]","anchor":"en-q2-255-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s8","r":"q2-255","title":"Give knowledge, and meet God through God","text":"You who believe with the faith of spiritual election: “Spend from what We have provided you” of abundant sciences and treasuries of understanding, before the day of meeting comes. On that day transactions fall away and those allusions disappear. Nothing avails except entering through the door of generosity, so that one meets God through God, without anything else. Those who deny this wrong themselves: they rely upon their works and thus meet God with the greatest idol. The Living, the Self-Subsisting, the Great, the Exalted, is independent of benefiting from works. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q2-255-s8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s9","r":"q2-255","title":"Attachment and taking on the appropriate character","text":"One who knows that He is the Living who does not die relies upon Him: “Rely upon the Living who does not die” [25:58]. Attachment to this Name ( التعلق ) is seeking the spirit’s life through knowledge and perfect love. One who knows that He is the Living, the Self-Subsisting, trusts Him, forgets remembrance of everything through remembering Him, and witnesses no other through witnessing His sustaining governance. Attachment to this Name is seeking knowledge of His sustaining governance until one rests from the misery of self-directed planning. Taking on its appropriate character ( التخلق ) means attending to everything with which you have been charged: spouse, children, self, property, and all the women and men connected with you. [B206]","anchor":"en-q2-255-s9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-255-s10","r":"q2-255","title":"","text":"The Living Most High has described Himself through the attributes of perfection—grandeur, might and majesty. Their evidences are manifest in His creation, so that truth is distinguished from falsehood. He makes this clear in the following words.","anchor":"en-q2-255-s10"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-256","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold 2:256","anchor":"unit-q2-256"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-1","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"لا إِكْراهَ فِي الدِّينِ قَدْ تَبَيَّنَ الرُّشْدُ مِنَ الْغَيِّ فَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِالطَّاغُوتِ وَيُؤْمِنْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقى لا انْفِصامَ لَها وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ (256)","anchor":"ar-q2-256-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-2","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"قلت: (الرُشْد) : مصدر رَشُد، بالكسر والضم، رشداً ورشاداً، و (الغي) : مصدر غَوَى، إذا ضلّ فى مُعْتَقَدِه، و (الطاغوت) : فعلوت من الطغيان، وأصله: طغيوت، فقلبت لام الكلمة لعينها فصار طيغوت، ثم قلبت الياء ألفاً.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-3","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"وهو كل ما عُبد من دون الله راضياً بذلك، و (العروة) : ما تستمسك به اليد عند خوف الزل كالحبل ونحوه، ووثوقها: متانتها، وانفصامها أن تنفك عن موضعها، وأصل الفصم في اللغة: أن ينفك الخلخال ونحوه ولا يَبِين، فإذا بان فهو القَصْم- بالقاف- وهو هنا استعارة للدّين الصحيح.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-4","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في شأن رجلٍ من الأنصار، تَنَصَّر ولدَاه قبل البَعْثَة فلما جاء الإسلامُ قَدِمَا إلى المدينة فدعاهما أبوهما إلى الإسلام فامتنعا، فلزمهما أبوهما وقال: والله لا أدِعكما حتى تُسلما، فاختصموا إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فأنزل الله: لا إِكْراهَ فِي الدِّينِ، فهو خبر بمعنى النهي، أي: لا تُكرهوا أحداً على الدخول في الدين.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-5","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"وهو خاص بأهل الكتاب.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-6","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"قال البيضاوي: إذ الإكراه في الحقيقة هو: إلزام الغير فعلاً لا يرى فيه خيراً، ولكن قَدْ تَبَيَّنَ الرُّشْدُ مِنَ الْغَيِّ أي تميّز الإيمان من الكفر بالآيات الواضحة، ودلت الدلائل على أن الإيمان رشد يوصل إلى السعادة الأبدية، والكفر غيّ يوصل إلى الشقاوة السرمدية. والعاقل متى تبين له ذلك بادرت نفسُه إلى الإيمان طلباً للفوز بالسعادة والنجاة، ولم يحتج إلى الإكراه والإلجاء. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-7","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"فَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِالطَّاغُوتِ أي: يبعد عنها ويجحد ربوبيتها وَيُؤْمِنْ بِاللَّهِ أي: يصدق بوحدانيته، ويقر برسله، فَقَدِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقى أي: فقد تمسك بالدين المتين، لا انقطاع له أبداً، وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ بالأقوال، عَلِيمٌ بالنيات، فإنَّ الدين مشتمل على قول باللسان وعقد بالجَنَان، فحسن التعبير بصفة السمع والعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-8","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-9","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"الإشارة: قال في الحكم: «لا يخاف عليك أن تلتبس الطرق، إنما يخاف عليك من غلبة الهوى عليك» . وقال أحمد بن حضرويه: الطريق واضح، والحق لائح، والداعي قد أَسْمَع، ما التحير بعد هذا إلا من العمَى. هـ. فطريق السير واضحة لمَن سبقت له العناية، باقية إلى يوم القيامة، وكل ما سوى الله طاغوت، فمن أعرض عن السَّوَى، وعلق قلبه بمحبة المولى، فقد استمسك بالعروة الوثقى، التي لا انفصام لها على طول المدى. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-256-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-256-10","r":"q2-256","title":"2:256 · No compulsion in religion and the firmest handhold","text":"ثم بيَّن الحق تعالى حال أهل العناية من أهل الشقاوة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-256-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-256-s1","r":"q2-256","title":"Guidance, error and the handhold","text":"I say: rushd ( الرشد ) is the verbal noun of rashida or rashuda , alongside rashād . Ghayy ( الغي ) is the verbal noun of ghawā : to go astray in belief. Ṭāghūt ( الطاغوت ) has the pattern faʿalūt , from transgression ( الطغيان ). Its original form is ṭaghayūt . The final root-letter is transposed into the middle position, giving ṭayaghūt , and the yāʾ then becomes alif . It denotes anything worshipped besides God while consenting to that worship. The handhold ( العروة ) is what the hand grasps when one fears slipping, such as a rope. Its firmness is its strength; its breaking means becoming detached from its place. Originally faṣm ( الفصم ) means the cracking of an anklet or something similar without its parts separating. If they separate, it is qaṣm ( القصم ), with qāf . Here the handhold is a metaphor ( استعارة ) for sound religion.","anchor":"en-q2-256-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-256-s2","r":"q2-256","title":"The distinction of guidance from error","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, speaks concerning a man of the Helpers whose two sons became Christians before the prophetic mission. When Islam came, they visited Medina. Their father invited them to Islam, but they refused. He held them and said: “By God, I shall not leave you until you become Muslims.” They brought their dispute to the Messenger of God, and God revealed: “There is no compulsion in religion.” It is a statement conveying a prohibition: do not compel anyone to enter religion. It applies specifically to the People of the Book. [B207] Al-Bayḍāwī said: compulsion properly means obliging someone to perform an act in which he sees no good. But right guidance has become distinct from error: faith has been distinguished from unbelief through clear signs. The proofs establish that faith is guidance leading to everlasting happiness, while unbelief is error leading to perpetual wretchedness. Once this becomes clear to a rational person, his self hastens to faith, seeking happiness and salvation. He needs neither compulsion nor force. Here his words end. Whoever rejects false objects of worship—distances himself from them and denies their Lordship—and believes in God, affirming His oneness and acknowledging His messengers, has grasped the firmest handhold: adhered to the strong religion that never breaks. God hears words and knows intentions. Since religion includes the tongue’s confession and the heart’s conviction, the attributes of hearing and knowledge are fittingly mentioned. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-256-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-256-s3","r":"q2-256","title":"The clear path and the danger of desire","text":"The Ḥikam says: “What is feared for you is not that the paths become confused, but that desire overcome you.” Aḥmad ibn Khaḍrawayh said: “The path is clear, the Real manifest, and the caller has made himself heard. Bewilderment after this comes only from blindness.” The path of wayfaring is clear for someone preceded by divine care and remains until the Day of Resurrection. [B208] Everything other than God is a false object of worship. Whoever turns away from otherness ( السوى ) and attaches his heart to love of the Master has grasped the firmest handhold, which will not break throughout the ages. And success is through God; He guides to the level path.","anchor":"en-q2-256-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-256-s4","r":"q2-256","title":"","text":"The Real then distinguishes the condition of the people of divine care from that of the people of wretchedness.","anchor":"en-q2-256-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-257","r":"q2-257","title":"2:257 · From darkness into light","text":"2:257 · From darkness into light 2:257","anchor":"unit-q2-257"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-257-1","r":"q2-257","title":"2:257 · From darkness into light","text":"اللَّهُ وَلِيُّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا يُخْرِجُهُمْ مِنَ الظُّلُماتِ إِلَى النُّورِ وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَوْلِياؤُهُمُ الطَّاغُوتُ يُخْرِجُونَهُمْ مِنَ النُّورِ إِلَى الظُّلُماتِ أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (257)","anchor":"ar-q2-257-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-257-2","r":"q2-257","title":"2:257 · From darkness into light","text":"قلت: الولي: هو المحب الذي يتولى أمور محبوبه، أو الناصر الذي ينصر محبوبه، ولا يخذله بأن يكله إلى نفسه. وجملة (يخرجهم) : حال من الضمير المستتر في الخبر، أو من الموصول أو منهما، أو خبر ثان.","anchor":"ar-q2-257-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-257-3","r":"q2-257","title":"2:257 · From darkness into light","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: اللَّهُ وَلِيُّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أي: محبهم ومتولي أمورهم، يُخْرِجُهُمْ مِنَ ظلمات الكفر والجهل، ومتابعة الهوى وقبول الوسواس، والشبه المُشْكِلة في التوحيد- إلى نور الإيمان واليقين، وصحة التوحيد، ومتابعة الداعي إلى الله، وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَوْلِياؤُهُمُ أي: أحباؤهم الطَّاغُوتُ أي: الشياطين، أو المضلات من الهوى والشيطان وغيرهما، يُخْرِجُونَهُمْ مِنَ النُّورِ الذي مُنحوه بالفطرة الأصلية، أو يصدونهم من الدخول في الإيمان إلى ظلمات الكفر والجهل، والتقليد الرديء واتباع الهوى، أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ بسبب نِيَّاتهم البقاء على الكفر إلى الممات، ولم يذكر في جانب المؤمنين دخول الجنة لتكون عبادتهم عبودية، لا خوفاً ولا طمعاً. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-257-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-257-4","r":"q2-257","title":"2:257 · From darkness into light","text":"الإشارة: (الله ولي الذين آمنوا) حيث تولاهم بسابق العناية، وكلأهم بعين الرعاية، يخرجهم أولا من ظلمات الكفر إلى نور الإيمان، ثم من ظلمات الحس ورؤية الأكوان إلى نور المعاني بحصول الشهود والعيان، فافن","anchor":"ar-q2-257-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-257-5","r":"q2-257","title":"2:257 · From darkness into light","text":"عن الإحساس تر عبراً. «الكون كله ظلمة، وإنما أناره ظهورُ الحَقِّ فيه» . أو تقول: الكون كله ظلمة لأهل الحجاب، وأما عند أهل المعرفة فالكون عندهم كله نور، وإنما حجبه ظهور الحكمة فيه، «فمن رأى الكون ولم يشهد النور فيه، أو قبله، أو بعده، فقد أعوزه وجود الأنوار وحجبت عنه شموس المعارف بسحب الآثار» . والذين كفروا- وهم الذين سبق لهم الشقاء، وحكم عليهم بالبعد القدر والقضاء- أولياؤهم الطاغوت، وهم القواطع: من الهوى والشيطان والدنيا والناس، (يخرجونهم من النور إلى الظلمات) أي: يمنعونهم من شهود تلك الأنوار السابقة، إلى الوقوف مع تلك الظلمات المتقدمة، فهم متعاكسون مع مَن سبقتْ لهم العناية، فما خرج منه أهل العناية وقع فيه أهل الغواية. نسأل الله الحفظ والعافية فى الدنيا والآخرة.","anchor":"ar-q2-257-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-257-6","r":"q2-257","title":"2:257 · From darkness into light","text":"ثم بيَّن الحق تعالى حال مَن سبق له الشقاء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-257-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-257-s1","r":"q2-257","title":"The protecting friend","text":"I say: a walī ( الولي ) is the lover who takes charge of his beloved’s affairs, or the helper who assists his beloved and does not abandon him by entrusting him to himself. The sentence “He brings them out” is a circumstance referring to the pronoun implicit in the predicate, to the relative pronoun, or to both; alternatively, it is a second predicate.","anchor":"en-q2-257-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-257-s2","r":"q2-257","title":"Faith, original disposition and corrupt guidance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: God is the protecting friend of those who believe—their lover and the One who takes charge of their affairs. He brings them out of the darkness of unbelief, ignorance, following desire, accepting whisperings and troubling doubts about unity, into the light of faith, certainty, sound affirmation of unity and following the caller to God. As for those who disbelieve, their protecting friends—their beloved allies—are the false objects of worship: devils, or the misleading forces of desire, Satan and others. They bring them out of the light granted them through their original disposition ( الفطرة الأصلية ), or prevent them from entering faith, into the darkness of unbelief, ignorance, corrupt imitation and following desire. They are the people of the Fire, abiding therein, because they intend to remain in unbelief until death. On the believers’ side, entrance into the Garden is not mentioned, so that their worship may be servanthood, not fear or desire for gain. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-257-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-257-s3","r":"q2-257","title":"The world as darkness and as light","text":"“God is the protecting friend of those who believe”: He takes charge of them through prior divine care and guards them with the eye of solicitude. First He brings them from the darkness of unbelief into the light of faith; then from the darkness of sensation and seeing created things into the light of meanings, through the attainment of witnessing and direct vision. Become effaced from sensation, and you will see lessons. [B209] “The whole cosmos is darkness; only the manifestation of the Real within it illuminates it.” Or you may say: the whole cosmos is darkness for the veiled, whereas for the people of gnosis it is all light; the manifestation of wisdom within it is what veils it. “Whoever sees the cosmos without witnessing the light within it, before it or after it lacks the presence of lights; the suns of gnoses are veiled from him by the clouds of created effects.” Those who disbelieve—those preceded by wretchedness and sentenced to distance by destiny and decree—have false objects of worship as their protecting friends: the highwaymen of desire, Satan, the world and people. “They bring them out of light into darkness”: they prevent them from witnessing the lights just mentioned and hold them at the darkness described before. Their direction is the opposite of those preceded by divine care. What the people of divine care leave, the people of error fall into. We ask God for preservation and well-being in this world and the Hereafter.","anchor":"en-q2-257-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-257-s4","r":"q2-257","title":"","text":"The Real then illustrates the condition of someone preceded by wretchedness.","anchor":"en-q2-257-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-258","r":"q2-258","title":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship","text":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship 2:258","anchor":"unit-q2-258"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-258-1","r":"q2-258","title":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِي حَاجَّ إِبْراهِيمَ فِي رَبِّهِ أَنْ آتاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ إِذْ قالَ إِبْراهِيمُ رَبِّيَ الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ قالَ أَنَا أُحْيِي وَأُمِيتُ قالَ إِبْراهِيمُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْتِي بِالشَّمْسِ مِنَ الْمَشْرِقِ فَأْتِ بِها مِنَ الْمَغْرِبِ فَبُهِتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ وَاللَّهُ لا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ (258)","anchor":"ar-q2-258-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-258-2","r":"q2-258","title":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship","text":"قلت: (أن آتاه) : على حذف لام العلة، و (إذ قال) : ظرف ل- (حاجّ) ، أو بدل من (آتاه الله) .","anchor":"ar-q2-258-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-258-3","r":"q2-258","title":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله متعجباً من جهالة النمرود، والمراد تعجيب السامع: أَلَمْ تَرَ يا محمد، إِلَى جهالة الَّذِي حَاجَّ إِبْراهِيمَ أي: خاصمه فِي رَبِّهِ لأجْل أَنْ أعطاه اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ، أي: حمله على ذلك بطر الملك. وذلك أنه لما كسَّر إبراهيم الأصنام، سجنه أياماً، وأخرجه من السجن، وقال له: من ربك الذي تعبد؟ قالَ له إِبْراهِيمَ عليه السلام: رَبِّيَ الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ، أي: يخلق الأرواح في الأجسام، ويخرجها عند انقضاء آجالها، (قال) نمرود: أَنَا أُحْيِي وَأُمِيتُ، فدعا برجلين فقتل أحدهما، وعفا عن الآخر، فلما رأى إبراهيم عليه السلام غلطه وتشغيبه عدل له إلى حجة أخرى، لا مقدور للبشر على الإتيان بمثلها، فقال له: فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْتِي بِالشَّمْسِ مِنَ الْمَشْرِقِ فَأْتِ بِها أنت مِنَ الْمَغْرِبِ لأنك تدَّعي الربوبية، ومن شأن الربوبية أن تقدر على كل شيء، ولا يعجزها شيء، فَبُهِتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ أي: غُلب وصار مبهوتاً، وَاللَّهُ لا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ إلى قبول الهداية، أو إلى طريق النجاة، أو إلى محجة الاحتجاج.","anchor":"ar-q2-258-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-258-4","r":"q2-258","title":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship","text":"الإشارة: قال بعض الحكماء: للنفس سر، ظهر على فرعون والنمرود، حتى صرّحا بدعوى الربوبية. قلت:","anchor":"ar-q2-258-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-258-5","r":"q2-258","title":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship","text":"وهذا السر هو ثابت للروح في أصل نشأتها لأنها جاءت من عالم العز والكبرياء. انظر قوله تعالى: وَنَفَخْتُ فِيهِ مِنْ رُوحِي، وقال أيضاً: قُلِ الرُّوحُ مِنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّي أي: سر من أسراره، فلما ركبت في هذا القالب الذي هو قالب العبودية- طلبت الرجوع إلى أصلها. فجعل لها الحقّ جلّ جلاله باباً تدخل منه فترجع إلى أصلها وهو الذل والخضوع والانكسار والافتقار، فمن دخل من هذا الباب، واتصل بمن يعرّفه ربه، رجعت روحه إلى ذلك الأصل، وأدركت ذلك السر، فمنها من تتسع لذلك السر وتطيقه، ومنها من تضيق عن حمله وتبوح به، فتقتلها الشريعة، كالحلاج وأمثاله، ومن طلب الرجوع إلى ذلك الأصل من غير بابه، ورام إدراكه بالعز والتكبّر، طُرد وأُبعد، وهو الذي صدر من النمرود وفرعون وغيرهما ممن ادّعى الربوبية جهلاً. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-258-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-258-6","r":"q2-258","title":"2:258 · Abraham’s argument and the false claim to Lordship","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى من أدركته العناية، وفي قصته برهان على إحياء الموتى الذي احتج به إبراهيم- عليه السّلام- فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-258-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-258-s1","r":"q2-258","title":"The cause and the time of the dispute","text":"I say: “Because He gave him” ( أن آتاه ) has an omitted causal lām ( لام العلة ). “When Abraham said” ( إذ قال ) is an adverbial expression attached to “disputed,” or a substitute for “God gave him.”","anchor":"en-q2-258-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-258-s2","r":"q2-258","title":"Power over subjects is not power to create life","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, expresses wonder at Nimrod’s ignorance, intending to awaken the listener’s wonder: have you not considered, Muḥammad, the ignorance of the man who disputed with Abraham concerning his Lord because God had given him kingship? The arrogance engendered by kingship drove him to it. When Abraham broke the idols, Nimrod imprisoned him for some days, then brought him out and asked: “Who is your Lord whom you worship?” Abraham replied: “My Lord is He who gives life and causes death”—creates spirits in bodies and brings them out when their appointed terms expire. Nimrod said: “I give life and cause death.” He summoned two men, killed one and pardoned the other. When Abraham saw his error and sophistry, he turned to another proof whose like no human could produce: “God brings the sun from the east; then bring it from the west.” You claim Lordship, and Lordship must have power over everything, with nothing beyond it. The unbeliever was confounded: defeated and bewildered. God does not guide the wrongdoing people to accept guidance, to the path of salvation or to the clear way of argument.","anchor":"en-q2-258-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-258-s3","r":"q2-258","title":"Return through humility, not through arrogance","text":"One of the sages said: the self contains a mystery which appeared in Pharaoh and Nimrod until they openly claimed Lordship. I say: this mystery belongs to the spirit in its original arising, because it came from the world of might and grandeur. Consider: “I breathed into him of My spirit” [15:29]; and, “Say: the spirit is of my Lord’s command” [17:85]—a mystery among His mysteries. When it was placed in this bodily mould, the mould of servanthood, it sought to return to its origin. The Real, glorious is His majesty, made a door through which it could enter and return: lowliness, submission, brokenness and need. Whoever enters by this door and joins someone who makes his Lord known to him has his spirit returned to that origin and apprehends that mystery. Some spirits have room for it and can bear it; others lack the capacity to bear it and divulge it, whereupon the Sacred Law puts them to death—as with al-Ḥallāj and those like him. [B210] Whoever seeks to return to that origin by another door and attempts to apprehend it through might and arrogance is expelled and banished. This is what occurred with Nimrod, Pharaoh and others who ignorantly claimed Lordship. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-258-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-258-s4","r":"q2-258","title":"","text":"The Real then mentions someone reached by divine care. His story also supplies a demonstration of the raising of the dead with which Abraham argued.","anchor":"en-q2-258-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-259","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty 2:259","anchor":"unit-q2-259"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-1","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"أَوْ كَالَّذِي مَرَّ عَلى قَرْيَةٍ وَهِيَ خاوِيَةٌ عَلى عُرُوشِها قالَ أَنَّى يُحْيِي هذِهِ اللَّهُ بَعْدَ مَوْتِها فَأَماتَهُ اللَّهُ مِائَةَ عامٍ ثُمَّ بَعَثَهُ قالَ كَمْ لَبِثْتَ قالَ لَبِثْتُ يَوْماً أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ قالَ بَلْ لَبِثْتَ مِائَةَ عامٍ فَانْظُرْ إِلى طَعامِكَ وَشَرابِكَ لَمْ يَتَسَنَّهْ وَانْظُرْ إِلى حِمارِكَ وَلِنَجْعَلَكَ آيَةً لِلنَّاسِ وَانْظُرْ إِلَى الْعِظامِ كَيْفَ نُنْشِزُها ثُمَّ نَكْسُوها لَحْماً فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ قالَ أَعْلَمُ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (259)","anchor":"ar-q2-259-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-2","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"قلت: (أو) : عاطفة، و (كالذي) : معطوف على الموصول المجرور بإلى، أي: أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِي حَآجَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ فِى رَبِّهِ، وإلى مثل الذي مر على قرية. وإنما أدخل حرف التشبيه لأن المُنكر للإحياء كثيرٌ، والجاهل بكيفيته أكثر، بخلاف مدعي الربوبية فإنه قليل. وقيل: الكاف مزيدة، والتقدير: أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِي حاج وإلى الذي مرَّ، (أنَّى) :","anchor":"ar-q2-259-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-3","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"ظرف ليُحيي، بمعنى: متى، أو حال بمعنى كيف، و (يتسنه) بمعنى يتغير، وأصله: يتسنن، فأبدلت النون الثالثة حرف علة. قال في الكافية:","anchor":"ar-q2-259-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-4","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"وثَالِثَ الأمثَالِ أبدِلَنْه يا ... نحو (تَظَنَّى خالدٌ تَظَنِّيَا)","anchor":"ar-q2-259-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-5","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"فصار تَسَنَّى ثم حُذفت للجازم، وأتى بهاء السَّكْت، وقفا ووصلا، كالعِوض من المحذوف، وقيل: من السَّنة، وهو التغير، فالهاء أصلية، و (لنجعلك) : معطوف على محذوف، أي: لتعتبر ولنجعلك آية للناس.","anchor":"ar-q2-259-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-6","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ألم ترَ يا محمد أيضاً إلى مثل الذي مَرَّ عَلى قَرْيَةٍ، وهو عزير، حَبْرُ بني إسرائيل. - وقيل: غيره- مرَّ على بيت المقدس حين خربها بُختنصر وَهِيَ خاوِيَةٌ ساقطة حيطانها عَلى عُرُوشِها أي: سقفها، وذلك بعد مائة سنة حتى سقطت العروش، ثم سقطت الحيطان عليها، فلما رآها خالية، وعظام الموتى فيها بالية، قالَ في نفسه: أَنَّى يُحْيِي هذِهِ اللَّهُ بَعْدَ مَوْتِها أي: متى يقع هذا. اعترافاً بالقصور عن معرفة طريق الإحياء، واستعظاماً لقدرة المحيي، إن كان القائل عزيراً، أو استبعاداً إن كان كافراً، فَأَماتَهُ اللَّهُ مِائَةَ عامٍ أي: ألبثه ميتاً مائة عام، ثُمَّ بَعَثَهُ بالإحياء، فقال له على لسان الملك، أو بلا واسطة: كَمْ لَبِثْتَ ميتاً؟ قالَ لَبِثْتُ يَوْماً أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ، وذلك أنه مات ضحى وبعث بعد مائة عام قبل غروب الشمس، فقال قبل النظر إلى الشمس (يوماً) ، ثم التفت فرأى بقية منها، فقال: أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ على الإضراب، قال له الحق جلّ جلاله: بَلْ لَبِثْتَ مِائَةَ عامٍ.","anchor":"ar-q2-259-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-7","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"وذلك أن عزيراً ذهب ليخترف(1) لأهله فجعل على حماره سَلة عنب وجَرَّة عصير. فلما مرَّ بتلك القرية ربط حماره، وجعل يتعجب من خرابها وخلائها بعد عمارتها، فقال في نفسه ما قال، فلطف الله به، وأراه كيفية الأحياء عياناً، فأماته مائة عام، حتى بليت عظام حماره وبقي العصير والعنب كأنه حين جنى وعصر فقال له جلّ جلاله: فَانْظُرْ إِلى طَعامِكَ وهو العنب، وَشَرابِكَ وهو العصير، لَمْ يَتَسَنَّهْ، أي: لم يتغير بمرور الزمان وطول المدة، وَانْظُرْ إِلى حِمارِكَ كيف تفرقت أوصاله، وبليت عظامه، فعلنا ذلك بك لتشاهد قدرتنا، وَلِنَجْعَلَكَ آيَةً لِلنَّاسِ بعدك، وَانْظُرْ إِلَى الْعِظامِ أي: عظام حمارك، كَيْفَ نُنْشِرُها، أي: نحييها، من نَشَرَ الله الموتى: أحياها. أو: كَيْفَ نُنْشِزُها بالزاي- أي: نرفع بعضها، ونركبه عليه، ثُمَّ نَكْسُوها لَحْماً.","anchor":"ar-q2-259-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-8","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"فنظر إلى العظام، فقام كلُّ عَظْم إلى موضعه، ثم كسى لحماً وجلداً، وجعل ينهق، فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ ما كان استغربه وأُشكل عليه قالَ أَعْلَمُ علم اليقين أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ، أو فلما تبين له الحق، وهو قدرته تعالى على كل شيء، قال لنفسه: اعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ.","anchor":"ar-q2-259-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-9","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"رُوِيَ أنه أتى قومه على حماره، وقال أنا عزير، فكذبوه، فقرأ التوراة من حفظه، ولم يحفظها أحد قبله، فعرفوه بذلك، وقالوا: هو ابن الله- تعالى عن قولهم- وقيل: لما رجع إلى منزله- وكان شاباً- وجد أولاده شيوخاً، فإذا حدَّثهم بحديث قالوا: حديث مائة سنة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-259-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-10","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"الإشارة: في هذه الآية والتي بعدها، الإشارة إلى الأمر بتربية اليقين والترقي فيه من علم اليقين إلى عين اليقين، فإن الروح ما دامت محجوبة بالوقوف مع الأسباب والعوائد، وبرؤية الحس والوقوف مع الوسائط، لم تخل من طوارق الشكوك والخواطر، فإذا انقطعت إلى ربها، وخرقت عوائد نفسها، كشف لها الحق تعالى عن أستار غيبه، وأطلعها على مكنونات سره، وكشف لها عن أسرار الملكوت، وأراها سنا الجبروت، فنظرت إلى قدرة الحي الذي لا يموت، وتمتعت بشهود الذات وأنوار الصفات، في هذه الحياة وبعد الممات، فحينئذٍ ينقطع عنها الشكوك والأوهام، وتتطهر من طوارق الخواطر، وتزول عنها الأمراض والأسقام.","anchor":"ar-q2-259-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-11","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"قال في الحِكَم: «كيف تخرق لك العوائد وأنت لم تخرق من نفسك العوائد» . فانظر إلى عزير ... ما أراه الحق قدرته عياناً حتى خرق له عوائده فأماته ثم أحياه، فكذلك أنت أيها المريد لا تطمع أن تخرق لك العوائد، فتشاهد قدرة الحق أو ذاته عياناً، حتى تموت عن حظوظك وهواك، ثم تحيا روحك وسرك، فحينئذٍ تشاهد أسرار ربك، ويكشف الأستار عن عين قلبك. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q2-259-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-259-12","r":"q2-259","title":"2:259 · The ruined town, the hundred years and the renewal of certainty","text":"ثم ذكر الحقّ تعالى قصة خليله عليه السلام في طلبه رؤية عين القدرة في إحياء الموتى، ليترقى من علم اليقين إلى عين اليقين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-259-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-259-s1","r":"q2-259","title":"The comparison and the verb of change","text":"I say: “Or” is a coordinating conjunction, and “like the one” ( كالذي ) is coordinated with the relative expression governed by ilā in the preceding verse: have you not considered the man who disputed with Abraham concerning his Lord, and someone like the man who passed a town? The particle of comparison is introduced because those who deny resurrection are many, and those ignorant of its manner more numerous still; claimants to Lordship, by contrast, are few. Alternatively, the kāf is supplementary: have you not considered the man who disputed and the man who passed? Annā ( أنى ) is an adverb attached to “give life,” meaning “when,” or a circumstance meaning “how.” Yatasannah ( يتسنه ) means change. Its original form is yatasannan ( يتسنن ), the third nūn being replaced by a weak letter. The Kāfiya says: Replace the third of like consonants with a yāʾ, as in “Khālid conjectured”— taẓannā Khālidun taẓanniyā . It thus becomes tasannā . The weak letter is then removed by the jussive, and the pause- hāʾ ( هاء السكت ) is added in both pause and connected recitation, as though compensating for the deleted letter. Another explanation derives it from sana ( السنة ), conveying alteration with years; on this account the hāʾ is radical. “To make you” is coordinated with an omitted expression: so that you may take a lesson, and so that We may make you a sign for people. [B211]","anchor":"en-q2-259-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-259-s2","r":"q2-259","title":"The food preserved and the donkey restored","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: have you not also considered, Muḥammad, someone like the man who passed a town? He was ʿUzayr, the learned man of Israel, though another person is also proposed. He passed Jerusalem after Nebuchadnezzar had laid it waste. Its walls had fallen upon its roofs: a hundred years had passed, the roofs had fallen and the walls collapsed upon them. Seeing it deserted and the bones of the dead decayed within it, he said to himself: “When will God bring this to life after its death?” [B212] If the speaker was ʿUzayr, this acknowledged his inability to understand the manner of restoration and marvelled at the power of the Giver of life; if an unbeliever, it expressed doubt about its possibility. God kept him dead for a hundred years, then raised him to life. Through an angel, or without intermediary, He asked: “How long have you remained dead?” He replied: “A day, or part of a day.” He had died in the morning and was raised a hundred years later before sunset. Before looking at the sun, he said “a day”; turning and seeing some daylight remain, he corrected himself: “or part of a day.” The Real, glorious is His majesty, said: “Rather, you have remained a hundred years.” ʿUzayr had gone to gather fruit for his family, placing a basket of grapes and a jar of juice upon his donkey. Passing the town, he tied the donkey and marvelled at its ruin and emptiness after its former habitation, saying what he said inwardly. God dealt gently with him and showed him directly how He gives life. He caused him to die for a hundred years, until the donkey’s bones decayed, while the juice and grapes remained as though freshly pressed and gathered. He said: “Look at your food,” the grapes, “and your drink,” the juice: they have not changed through the passage of time and the long interval. Look at your donkey, whose joints have separated and bones decayed. We have done this so that you may witness Our power and become a sign for people after you. Look at the donkey’s bones: how We restore them to life, according to the reading nunshiruhā ( ننشرها ), from “God raised the dead”; or how We lift and assemble them, according to nunshizuhā ( ننشزها ), with zāy . Then We clothe them with flesh. [B211] He looked at the bones, and each bone stood in its place. They were clothed with flesh and skin, and the donkey began to bray. When what had seemed strange and difficult became clear to him, he said: “I know with certain knowledge that God has power over everything.” Alternatively, when the truth—His power over all things—became clear, he said to himself: “Know that God has power over everything,” according to the imperative reading. [B211] It is related that he returned to his people upon his donkey and said: “I am ʿUzayr.” They disbelieved him, so he recited the Torah from memory, which no one before him had memorised. They recognised him by this and said that he was God’s son—exalted is He above their saying. Another account says that he returned home as a young man and found his children elderly. Whenever he told them something, they said: “That is a story from a hundred years ago.” And God Most High knows best. [B212]","anchor":"en-q2-259-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-259-s3","r":"q2-259","title":"From knowledge of certainty to its direct vision","text":"This verse and the next indicate the command to cultivate certainty and ascend from knowledge of certainty ( علم اليقين ) to the eye of certainty ( عين اليقين ). So long as the spirit remains veiled by stopping with causes and customary patterns, seeing sensory forms and remaining with intermediaries, it is not free of invading doubts and thoughts. When it devotes itself entirely to its Lord and breaks through the customary habits of its self, the Real Most High uncovers for it the curtains of His unseen, reveals the hidden treasures of His mystery, unveils the secrets of the unseen kingdom and shows it the radiance of the world of divine omnipotence ( الجبروت ). It beholds the power of the Living who does not die and delights in witnessing the Essence and the lights of the attributes, in this life and after death. Doubts and imaginings then cease; it is purified of intrusive thoughts, and its illnesses and ailments disappear. The Ḥikam says: “How should customary patterns be broken for you while you have not broken the customary habits of your self?” Consider ʿUzayr: the Real did not show him His power directly until He broke customary patterns for him, causing him to die and then bringing him to life. Likewise, disciple, do not hope that customary patterns will be broken for you, so that you witness the Real’s power or Essence directly, until you die to your interests and desire. Then your spirit and secret come to life; you witness your Lord’s mysteries and the curtains are lifted from the eye of your heart. And success is through God; He guides to the level path.","anchor":"en-q2-259-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-259-s4","r":"q2-259","title":"","text":"The Real then relates His intimate friend’s request to see power itself in the raising of the dead, so as to ascend from knowledge of certainty to its direct vision.","anchor":"en-q2-259-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-260","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self 2:260","anchor":"unit-q2-260"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-1","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"وَإِذْ قالَ إِبْراهِيمُ رَبِّ أَرِنِي كَيْفَ تُحْيِ الْمَوْتى قالَ أَوَلَمْ تُؤْمِنْ قالَ بَلى وَلكِنْ لِيَطْمَئِنَّ قَلْبِي قالَ فَخُذْ أَرْبَعَةً مِنَ الطَّيْرِ فَصُرْهُنَّ إِلَيْكَ ثُمَّ اجْعَلْ عَلى كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِنْهُنَّ جُزْءاً ثُمَّ ادْعُهُنَّ يَأْتِينَكَ سَعْياً وَاعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ (260)","anchor":"ar-q2-260-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-2","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"قلت: رأى: البصرية، إنما تتعدى إلى مفعول واحد، فإذا أُدخلت عليها الهمزة تعدت إلى مفعولين. وعلقها هنا عن الثاني الاستفهام، (وصرهن) أي: أَمْلهُنَّ واضمُمْهن إليك. وفيه لغتان: صار يصير ويصور، ولذلك قرئ بكسر الصاد وضمها، و (سعيا) : حال، أي: ساعيات.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-3","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر يا محمد، أو أيها السامع، حين قالَ إِبْراهِيمُ عليه السلام: يا رَبِّ أَرِنِي كَيْفَ تُحْيِ الْمَوْتى أي: أبصرني كيفية إحياء الموتى، حتى أرى ذلك عياناً، أراد عليه السلام أن ينتقل من علم","anchor":"ar-q2-260-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-4","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"اليقين إلى عين اليقين، وقيل: لما قال للنمرود: رَبِّيَ الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ قال له: هل عاينت ذلك؟ فلم يقدر أن يقول: نعم. وانتقل إلى حجة أخرى، ثم سأل ربه أن يريه ذلك ليطمئن قلبه على الجواب، إن سئل مرة أخرى، فقال له الحق جل جلاله: أَوَلَمْ تُؤْمِنْ بأني قادر على الإحياء بإعادة التركيب والحياة؟ وإنما قال له ذلك، مع علمه بتحقيق إيمانه ليجيبه بما أجاب فيعلم السامعون غرضه، قالَ إبراهيم عليه السلام: بَلى آمنت إِنك على كل شيءٍ قدير، وَلكِنْ سألتك لِيَطْمَئِنَّ قَلْبِي إذ ليس الخبر كالعيان، وليس علم اليقين كعين اليقين، أراد أن يضم الشهود والعيان إلى الوحي والبرهان.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-5","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"قال له الحق جلّ جلاله: فَخُذْ أَرْبَعَةً مِنَ الطَّيْرِ طاووساً وديكاً وغراباً وحمامة، ومنهم من ذكر النسر بدل الحمام، فَصُرْهُنَّ إِلَيْكَ أي: اضممهن إليك لتتأملها وتعرف أشكالها، لئلا يلتبس عليك بعد الإحياء أشكالها، ثُمَّ اجْعَلْ عَلى كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِنْهُنَّ جُزْءاً أي: ثم جَزَّئهن، وفرق أجزاءهن على الجبال التي تحضرك. قيل: كانت أربعة وقيل: سبعة، ثُمَّ ادْعُهُنَّ وقل لهن: تعالين بإذن الله، يَأْتِينَكَ سَعْياً أي: ساعيات مسرعات، رُوِيَ أنه أمر أن يذبحها وينتف ريشها، ويقطعها ويخلط بعضها ببعض، ويوزعها على الجبال، ويمسك رءوسها عنده، ثم يناديها، ففعل ذلك، فجَعَل كل جزء يطير إلى الآخر ويلتئم بصاحبه حتى صارت جثثاً، ثم أقبل إليه فأعطى كل طير رأسه فطار في الهواء. فسبحان من لا يعجزه شيء، ولا يغيب عن علمه شيء، ثم نبّه إلى التفكر في عجائب قدرته وحكمته فقال: وَاعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ لا يعجزه شيء، حَكِيمٌ ذو حكمة بالغة فيما يفعل ويذر.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-6","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"الإشارة: من أراد أن تحيا رُوحُه الحياة الأبدية، وينتقل من علم اليقين إلى عين اليقين، فلا بد أن تموت نفسه أربع موتات:","anchor":"ar-q2-260-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-7","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"الأولى: تموت عن حب الشهوات والزخارف الدنيوية، التي هي صفة الطاووس.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-8","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"الثانية: عن الصولة والقوى النفسانية، التي هي صفة الديك.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-9","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"الثالثة: عن خسة النفس والدناءة وبعد الأمل، التي هي صفة الغراب.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-10","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"الرابعة: عن الترفع والمسارعة إلى الهوى المتصف بها الحمام.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-11","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"فإذا ذبح نفسه عن هذه الخصال حييتْ روحه، وتهذبت نفسه، فصارت طوع يده، كلما دعاها إلى طاعة أتت إليها مسرعة ساعية.","anchor":"ar-q2-260-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-12","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"وإلى هذا المعنى أشار الشيخ أبو الحسن الشاذلي بقوله في حزبه الكبير: (واجعل لنا ظهيراً من عقولنا ومهيمناً من أرواحنا، ومسخراً من أنفسنا، كي نسبحك كثيراً، ونذكرك كثيرًا، إِنكَ كنت بنا بصيراً) .","anchor":"ar-q2-260-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-260-13","r":"q2-260","title":"2:260 · Abraham’s four birds and the four deaths of the self","text":"ولما كانت حياة الروح متوقفة على أمرين: بذل النفوس، ودفع الفلوس وقدم الإشارة إلى الأول بقوله: وَقاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، أشار إلى الثاني بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-260-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-260-s1","r":"q2-260","title":"Seeing, showing and drawing near","text":"I say: raʾā , when it denotes visual seeing, governs one object. Introducing the causative hamza makes it govern two. Here the interrogative suspends its direct government of the second object ( التعليق بالاستفهام ). “Draw them to you” ( صرهن إليك ) means incline and gather them towards yourself. There are two verbal forms, ṣāra yaṣīru and ṣāra yaṣūru , hence the readings with kasra and ḍamma on the ṣād . “Swiftly” ( سعياً ) is a circumstantial expression: coming swiftly.","anchor":"en-q2-260-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-260-s2","r":"q2-260","title":"Adding direct witnessing to revelation and proof","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember, Muḥammad—or listener—when Abraham said: “My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead.” Let me see its manner directly. He wished to pass from knowledge of certainty to the eye of certainty. Another account says that when he told Nimrod, “My Lord is He who gives life and causes death,” Nimrod asked whether he had witnessed it. Unable to say yes, he moved to another proof. He then asked his Lord to show it to him, so that his heart would be at rest concerning his answer if questioned again. [B213] The Real, glorious is His majesty, asked: “Do you not believe that I can give life by restoring the composition and life?” Although He knew the reality of Abraham’s faith, He asked so that Abraham would give the answer he gave, making his purpose known to the listeners. Abraham replied: “Yes indeed, I believe that You have power over everything. I ask only that my heart may be at rest.” A report is not like direct vision, nor is knowledge of certainty like the eye of certainty. He wished to add witnessing and direct vision to revelation and demonstration ( الوحي والبرهان ). The Real said: “Take four birds”: a peacock, a cock, a raven and a pigeon; some name a vulture instead of the pigeon. Draw them to you, examine them and know their forms, so that their forms will not be confused for you after restoration. Then divide them and place portions upon the mountains near you—said to have been four, or seven. Call them, saying, “Come by God’s leave,” and they will come swiftly. It is related that he was commanded to slaughter them, pluck their feathers, cut them up, mix their parts, distribute them upon the mountains and retain their heads. Then he was to call them. He did so. Each part flew to another and joined its counterpart until bodies were formed. They approached him, and he gave each bird its head; it flew into the air. Glory to Him whom nothing defeats and from whose knowledge nothing is absent. He then directs attention to reflection upon the wonders of His power and wisdom: “Know that God is Mighty”—nothing defeats Him—“Wise,” possessed of consummate wisdom in what He does and leaves undone.","anchor":"en-q2-260-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-260-s3","r":"q2-260","title":"Four qualities to be overcome","text":"Whoever wishes his spirit to live the everlasting life and to pass from knowledge of certainty to the eye of certainty must have his self die four deaths. First, it must die to love of appetites and worldly adornments: the peacock’s quality. Second, to aggression and the powers of the lower self: the cock’s quality. Third, to baseness, lowliness of character and far-reaching hopes: the raven’s quality. Fourth, to self-exaltation and hastening towards desire: the pigeon’s quality. [B213] When he slaughters these qualities in his self, his spirit lives and his self becomes refined and obedient to his hand. Whenever he calls it to obedience, it comes swiftly and eagerly. Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan al-Shādhilī indicates this meaning in his Great Litany ( الحزب الكبير ): “Make our intellects a support for us, our spirits a guardian over us, and our selves subject to us, so that we may glorify You much and remember You much. You have ever seen us.”","anchor":"en-q2-260-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-260-s4","r":"q2-260","title":"","text":"The spirit’s life depends upon two things: offering up the self and giving away money. Having indicated the first through “Fight in the path of God,” He now indicates the second.","anchor":"en-q2-260-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-261-262","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury 2:261–262","anchor":"unit-q2-261-262"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-1","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ أَنْبَتَتْ سَبْعَ سَنابِلَ فِي كُلِّ سُنْبُلَةٍ مِائَةُ حَبَّةٍ وَاللَّهُ يُضاعِفُ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ (261) الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ثُمَّ لا يُتْبِعُونَ ما أَنْفَقُوا مَنًّا وَلا أَذىً لَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (262)","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-2","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"قلت: (مثل الذين) : مبتدأ، و (كمثل) : خبر، ولا بد من حذف مضاف، إما من المبتدأ أو الخبر، أي: مثل نفقة الذين ينفقون كمثل حبة، أو مثل الذين ينفقون كمثل باذر حبة ... الخ.","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-3","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في التحريض على النفقة في سبيل الله: مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أي: يتصدقون بها في سبيل الله، كالجهاد ونحوه، كَمَثَلِ زارع حَبَّةٍ أَنْبَتَتْ له سَبْعَ سَنابِلَ فِي كُلِّ سُنْبُلَةٍ مِائَةُ حَبَّةٍ، فالمجموع سبعمائة. وفى الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «الحسنة بعشر أمثالها، إلى سبعمائة إلى أضْعَافٍ كَثيرَةٍ» . وإسناد الإنبات إلى الحبة مجاز، والمنبت هو الله، وهذا مثال لا يقتضي الوقوع، وقد يقع في الذرة والدخن(1) في الأرض الطيبة، بحيث تخرج الحبة ساقاً يتشعب إلى سبع شعب، في كل شعبة سنبلة، وَاللَّهُ يُضاعِفُ تلك المضاعفة لِمَنْ يَشاءُ بفضله، على حسب حال المنفق من إخلاصه وتعبه، وبحسبه تتفاوت الأعمال في مقادير الثواب، وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ لا يضيق عليه ما يتفضل به من الثواب، عَلِيمٌ بنية المنفق وقدر إنفاقه.","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-4","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"ثم ذكر شرطَيْن آخرَيْن في قبول النفقة، فقال: الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ثُمَّ لا يُتْبِعُونَ ما أَنْفَقُوا مَنًّا وَلا أَذىً. المن: أن يعتد بإحسانه على من أحسن إليه بحيث يقول: أنا فعلت معه كذا، وكذا إظهاراً لميزته عليه. والأذى: أن يتطاول عليه بذلك. ويقول: لولا أنا لم يكن منك شيء، مثلاً. فمن فعل هذا فقد ذهبت صدقته هباءاً منثوراً، ومن سلم من ذلك، وأنفق ماله ابتغاء وجه الله ف- لا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-5","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"وقال زيد بن أسلم رضي الله عنه: إذا أعطيت أحداً شيئاً وظننت أن سلامَكَ يَثْقُلُ عليه فَكُفَ سلامَكَ عنه. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-6","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"قيل: إن الآية نزلت في عثمان وعبد الرحمن بن عوف- رضى الله عنهما أما عثمان فإنه جهز جيش العسرة بألف بعير بأقتابها وأحلاسها. وقال عبد الرحمن بن سمرة: جاء عُثْمَانُ بألْفِ دِينَارِ في جيش العُسْرَةِ، فصَبَها في حجر النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فرأيت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يُدخل يَده فيها، ويُقلِّبهَا ويقول: «ما ضَرَّ ابن عفَّان ما عَمِلَ بَعْدَ اليوم» .","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-7","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"زاد في رواية أبى سعيد: فرأيت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم رافعاً يدعو لعثمان، ويقول: «يا رب عثمان بن عفان، رضيتُ عنه فارض عنه» . وأما عبد الرحمن: فإنه أتى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بأربعة آلاف درهم، صدقة، وأمسك أربعة آلاف لعياله، فقال له النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «بارك الله لك فيما أعطيتَ وفيما أمسكتَ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-8","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"وإنما لم يدخل الفاء في قوله: لا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ، مع أن الموصول قد تضمن معنى الشرط، إيهاماً بأنهم أهلٌ لذلك، وإن لم يفعلوا، فكيف بهم إذا فعلوا. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-9","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"الإشارة: التقرُّب إلى الله تعالى يكون بالعمل البدني وبالعمل المالي، وبالعمل القلبي، أما العمل البدني، ويدخل فيه العمل اللساني، فقد ورد فيه التضعيف بعشر وبعشرين وبثلاثين وبخمسين وبمائة، وبأكثر من ذلك أو أقل، وكذلك العمل المالي: قد ورد تضعيفه إلى سبع مائة، ويتفاوت ذلك بحسب النيات والمقاصد، وأما العمل القلبي: فليس له أجر محصور، قال تعالى: إِنَّما يُوَفَّى الصَّابِرُونَ أَجْرَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ، فالصبر، والخوف، والرجاء، والورع، والزهد، والتوكل، والمحبة، والرضا، والتسليم، والمعرفة، وحسن الخلق، والفكرة، وسائر الأخلاق الحميدة، إنما جزاؤها: الرضا، والإقبال والتقريب، وحسن الوصال. قال تعالى: وَرِضْوانٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ أَكْبَرُ أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-10","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"أكبر من الجزاء الحسيّ الذي هو القصور والحور.","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-11","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"وأما قوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «تفكر ساعة أفضل من عبادة سبعين سنة» . فإنما هو كناية عن الكثرة والمبالغة، كقوله تعالى: إِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِينَ مَرَّةً فَلَنْ يَغْفِرَ اللَّهُ لَهُمْ. ومثله قول الشاعر(1) :","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-12","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"كُلُّ وَقتٍ مِنْ حَبيبيِ ... قَدْرُهُ كألفِ حجَّهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-13","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"أي: سَنَة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-261-262-14","r":"q2-261-262","title":"2:261–262 · The seven hundred grains and giving without injury","text":"ثم بيَّن الحقّ تعالى أن حسن الخلق ولين الجانب أفضل من الصدقة المشوبة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-261-262-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-261-262-s1","r":"q2-261-262","title":"The implied term in the comparison","text":"I say: “The likeness of those” is the subject, and “like a grain” the predicate. A term in a possessive construction must be supplied on one side or the other: the likeness of the expenditure of those who spend is like a grain; or the likeness of those who spend is like someone sowing a grain—and so forth.","anchor":"en-q2-261-262-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-261-262-s2","r":"q2-261-262","title":"The multiplication of sincere charity","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, encourages expenditure in His path: the likeness of those who spend their wealth in His path, giving charity for such purposes as fighting in His cause, is a sower whose grain produces seven ears, with a hundred grains in each: seven hundred altogether. The Prophet said: “A good deed is multiplied tenfold, up to seven hundredfold, and many times beyond.” [B214] Ascribing the growth to the grain is figurative ( مجاز ); the One who causes growth is God. This is an illustration, not a claim that such growth must actually occur, though it may occur with sorghum or millet in good soil: a grain produces a stalk branching into seven, each branch bearing an ear. God grants this multiplication through His bounty to whom He wills, according to the giver’s sincerity and effort. Accordingly, deeds differ in the amount of their recompense. God is All-Encompassing: what He bestows of recompense does not restrict Him. He knows the giver’s intention and the measure of his giving. He then mentions two further conditions for accepted expenditure: those who spend in God’s path must not follow it with reminders of their favour or injury ( منّ وأذى ). Reminding someone of a favour means counting one’s beneficence against its recipient, saying, “I did such-and-such for him,” to display one’s superiority. Injury means lording it over him because of it, saying, for example: “Without me, you would have amounted to nothing.” Whoever does this has made his charity scattered dust. Those free from it, who spend seeking God’s Face, shall have no fear and shall not grieve. Zayd ibn Aslam said: “If you give someone something and think that your greeting weighs upon him, withhold even your greeting from him.”","anchor":"en-q2-261-262-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-261-262-s3","r":"q2-261-262","title":"Generosity and the promised reward","text":"The verse is said to have been revealed concerning ʿUthmān and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf. ʿUthmān equipped the Army of Hardship with a thousand camels, complete with saddles and saddlecloths. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samura said: “ʿUthmān brought a thousand dinars for the Army of Hardship and poured them into the Prophet’s lap. I saw him put his hand among them and turn them over, saying: ‘Nothing Ibn ʿAffān does after today will harm him.’” Abū Saʿīd’s transmission adds: “I saw the Prophet raise his hands in prayer for ʿUthmān, saying: ‘Lord of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, I am pleased with him; be pleased with him.’” [B214] ʿAbd al-Raḥmān brought four thousand dirhams to the Prophet as charity and kept four thousand for his dependants. The Prophet said: “May God bless what you have given and what you have retained.” [B214] Although the relative expression contains a conditional meaning, the fāʾ is not introduced before “No fear shall be upon them.” This suggests that they deserve it even had they not acted thus—how much more when they do. Al-Bayḍāwī says this.","anchor":"en-q2-261-262-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-261-262-s4","r":"q2-261-262","title":"The unbounded recompense of inward acts","text":"Drawing near to God Most High occurs through bodily, financial and inward acts. Bodily acts include acts of the tongue. Their multiplication is reported as ten, twenty, thirty, fifty, a hundred, more or less. Financial acts are reported to be multiplied up to seven hundredfold. This varies according to intentions and purposes. Inward acts, however, have no circumscribed reward: “The steadfast are paid their reward without reckoning” [39:10]. Patience, fear, hope, scrupulousness, renunciation, reliance, love, contentment, surrender, gnosis, good character, contemplation and the other praiseworthy qualities receive divine good pleasure, turning towards the servant, drawing him near and beautiful communion. “God’s good pleasure is greater” [9:72]: greater than sensory recompense, such as palaces and heavenly companions. The saying attributed to the Prophet, “An hour’s contemplation is better than seventy years’ worship,” expresses abundance and intensification, as in “Even if you seek forgiveness for them seventy times, God will not forgive them” [9:80]. The poet’s words are similar: Every moment from my Beloved is worth a thousand ḥijjas— that is, years. And God Most High knows best. [B215]","anchor":"en-q2-261-262-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-261-262-s5","r":"q2-261-262","title":"","text":"The Real then explains that good character and gentleness are better than charity mixed with impurity.","anchor":"en-q2-261-262-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-263","r":"q2-263","title":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness","text":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness 2:263","anchor":"unit-q2-263"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-263-1","r":"q2-263","title":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness","text":"قَوْلٌ مَعْرُوفٌ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ صَدَقَةٍ يَتْبَعُها أَذىً وَاللَّهُ غَنِيٌّ حَلِيمٌ (263)","anchor":"ar-q2-263-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-263-2","r":"q2-263","title":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness","text":"قلت: (قول) : مبتدأ، و (خير) : خبر، والمسوِّغ الصفةُ.","anchor":"ar-q2-263-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-263-3","r":"q2-263","title":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قَوْلٌ جميل يقوله الإنسان للسائل في حال رده، حيث لم يجد ما يعطيه، خَيْرٌ وأفضل عند الله من الصدقة التي يتبعها المن والأذى، ومثال القول المعروف: الله يرزقنا وإياك رزقاً حسناً. والله يغنينا وإياك من فضله العظيم، وشبه ذلك من غير تعبيس ولا كراهية. وَمَغْفِرَةٌ للسائل والعفو عن جفوته وإلحاحه، خَيْرٌ أيضاً مِنْ صَدَقَةٍ يَتْبَعُها مَنٍّ، أو أَذىً للسائل، علم الحق جل جلاله أن الفقير إذا رُدَّ بغير نوال شقَّ عليه، فربما أطلق لسانه وأظهر الشكوى فأمر المسئول بالعفو والتواضع. ولو شاء الحقّ تعالى لأغنى الجميع، لكنه أعطى الأغنياء ليظهر شكرهم، وابتلى الفقراء لينظر كيف صبرهم، وَاللَّهُ تعالى غَنِيٌّ عن إنفاق يصحبه مَنٌ أو أذى، حَلِيمٌ عن معاجلة من يَمُنُّ أو يؤذي بالعقوبة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-263-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-263-4","r":"q2-263","title":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness","text":"الإشارة: يُفهم من الآية أن حسن الخلق، ولين الجانب، وخفض الجناح، وكف الأذى، وحمل الجفاء، وشهود الصفاء، من أفضل الأعمال وأزكى الأحوال وأحسن الخلال، وفي الحديث: «إنَّ حُسْن الخُلق يعدل الصيام والقيام» .","anchor":"ar-q2-263-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-263-5","r":"q2-263","title":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness","text":"وفي قوله: وَاللَّهُ غَنِيٌّ حَلِيمٌ: تربية للسائل والمسئول، فتربية السائل: أن يستغني بالغنيِّ الكبير عن سؤال العبد الفقير، ويكتفي بعلم الحال عن المقال، وتربية المسئول: أن يحلم عن جفوة السائل فيتلطف في الخطاب، ويحسن الرد والجواب. قال في شرح الأسماء: والتخلق بهذا الاسم- يعني الحليم- بالصفح عن الجنايات، والسمح فيما يقابلونه به من الإساءات، بل يجازيهم بالإحسان، تحقيقاً للحلم والغفران. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-263-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-263-6","r":"q2-263","title":"2:263 · A gracious word and forgiveness","text":"ثم حذَّر الحق تعالى من المن والأذى فى الصدقة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-263-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-263-s1","r":"q2-263","title":"An indefinite subject qualified by an adjective","text":"I say: “A word” is the subject and “better” the predicate. The adjective makes the indefinite subject admissible.","anchor":"en-q2-263-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-263-s2","r":"q2-263","title":"Gentleness towards the person who asks","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: a gracious word spoken to someone asking, when one has nothing to give and must turn him away, is better before God than charity followed by reminders and injury. Such words include: “May God provide us and you with a good provision”; “May God enrich us and you from His immense bounty”—and the like, without frowning or aversion. Forgiving the person who asks, overlooking his roughness and insistence, is also better than charity followed by reminders or injury. The Real knows that being sent away empty-handed is hard for the poor person. He may therefore loose his tongue and complain. The person asked is consequently commanded to pardon and show humility. Had the Real willed, He would have enriched everyone. He gives to the rich so that their gratitude may appear, and tests the poor to see how they endure. God is independent of expenditure accompanied by reminders or injury, and Forbearing in not hastening to punish those who remind or injure. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-263-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-263-s3","r":"q2-263","title":"The divine Names educate giver and petitioner","text":"The verse teaches that good character, gentleness, humility, refraining from harm, bearing rough treatment and witnessing purity are among the best deeds, purest states and finest qualities. The hadith says: “Good character equals fasting and standing in prayer.” [B216] “God is Independent, Forbearing” educates both the petitioner and the person asked. The petitioner is taught to find sufficiency in the Great, Independent One rather than ask a needy servant, and to be content with His knowledge of the situation instead of speaking. The person asked is taught to bear the petitioner’s roughness patiently, address him gently and make a gracious response. The commentary on the divine Names says: taking on the appropriate character of this Name—the Forbearing—means overlooking offences and being generous towards the wrongs people commit against one. Rather, one repays them with goodness, realizing forbearance and forgiveness. [B216]","anchor":"en-q2-263-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-263-s4","r":"q2-263","title":"","text":"The Real then warns against reminders and injury in charity.","anchor":"en-q2-263-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-264","r":"q2-264","title":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display","text":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display 2:264","anchor":"unit-q2-264"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-264-1","r":"q2-264","title":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تُبْطِلُوا صَدَقاتِكُمْ بِالْمَنِّ وَالْأَذى كَالَّذِي يُنْفِقُ مالَهُ رِئاءَ النَّاسِ وَلا يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَمَثَلُهُ كَمَثَلِ صَفْوانٍ عَلَيْهِ تُرابٌ فَأَصابَهُ وابِلٌ فَتَرَكَهُ صَلْداً لا يَقْدِرُونَ عَلى شَيْءٍ مِمَّا كَسَبُوا وَاللَّهُ لا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الْكافِرِينَ (264)","anchor":"ar-q2-264-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-264-2","r":"q2-264","title":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display","text":"قلت: (كالذي) : الكاف في محل نصب على المصدر، أي: إبطالاً كإبطال الذي ينفق ماله رئاء الناس. أو حال، أي: مشبَّهين بالذي ينفق رئاء. و (رئاء) مفعول له، والصفوان: الحجر الأملس، والصلد: البارز الذي لا تراب عليه، وجمع الضمير في قوله: (لا يقدرون) باعتبار معنى (الذي) لأنَّ المراد به الجنس.","anchor":"ar-q2-264-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-264-3","r":"q2-264","title":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تُبْطِلُوا أجر صدقتكم بسبب الْمَنِّ بها على المتصدَّقِ عليه، وَالْأَذى الذي يصدر منكم له، بأن تذكروا ذلك للناس، فتكون صدقتكم باطلة، كَالَّذِي يُنْفِقُ مالَهُ رِئاءَ النَّاسِ وَلا يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ، فإن أجره يوم القيامة يكون هباء منثوراً، فَمَثَلُهُ في انتفاعه بصدقته، وتستره بها في دار الدنيا، وافتضاحه يوم القيامة، كحجر أملس عَلَيْهِ تُرابٌ يستره، فيظن الرائي أنه أرض طيبة تصلح للزراعة، فَأَصابَهُ وابِلٌ أي: مطر غزير فَتَرَكَهُ صَلْداً حجراً يابساً خالياً من التراب، كذلك المراءون بأعمالهم، ينتفعون بها في الدنيا بثناء الناس عليهم وستر حالهم، فإذا قدموا يوم القيامة وجدوها باطلة، لا يَقْدِرُونَ عَلى الانتفاع ب شَيْءٍ مِمَّا كَسَبُوا وَاللَّهُ لا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الْكافِرِينَ إلى مراشدهم ومصالح دينهم. وفيه تعريض بأن الرياء والمن والأذى من صفة الكافر، ولا بد للمؤمن أن يتجنب عنها.","anchor":"ar-q2-264-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-264-4","r":"q2-264","title":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-264-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-264-5","r":"q2-264","title":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display","text":"الإشارة: تصفية الأعمال على قدر تصفية القلوب، وتصفية القلوب على قدر مراقبة علام الغيوب، والمراقبة على قدر المعرفة. والمعرفة على قدر المشاهدة. والمشاهدة تحصل على قدر المجاهدة، وَالَّذِينَ جاهَدُوا فِينا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنا. وفي الحكم: «حسن الأعمال من نتائج حسن الأحوال. وحسن الأحوال من التحقق بمقامات الإنزال» والحاصل أن من لم يتحقق بمقام الفناء لا تخلو أعماله من شوب الخلل، ومن تحقق بالزوال لم ير لنفسه نسبة في عطاء ولا منع، ولا حركة ولا سكون، ولم ير لغيره وجوداً حتى يرجو منه نفعاً ولا خيراً. وفي بعض الإشارات: يا من يرائي أَمْر مَنْ ترائِي بيد من تعصيه. هـ. وفي تمثيله بالحجر إشارة إلى قساوة قلبه ويبوسة طبعه، فلا يرجى منه خير قط. والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q2-264-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-264-6","r":"q2-264","title":"2:264 · The smooth rock and charity performed for display","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى ضد هؤلاء، وهم المخلصون، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-264-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-264-s1","r":"q2-264","title":"The comparison and the bare stone","text":"I say: the kāf in “like the one” is accusative as an expression qualifying an absolute accusative: a nullification like that of one who spends his wealth to be seen by people. Alternatively, it is circumstantial: resembling the one who spends for display. “To be seen” ( رئاء ) is an accusative of purpose. Ṣafwān ( صفوان ) is a smooth stone; ṣald ( صلد ), bare and uncovered by soil. The pronoun in “they gain nothing” is plural in accordance with the meaning of “the one,” which denotes the class.","anchor":"en-q2-264-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-264-s2","r":"q2-264","title":"A charitable appearance stripped away","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: you who believe, do not nullify the reward of your charity by reminding its recipient of it or injuring him—for example, by mentioning it to other people. Your charity would then be void, like that of someone who spends his wealth to be seen by people and does not believe in God and the Last Day. His recompense on the Day of Resurrection becomes scattered dust. His worldly benefit from charity, the concealment it affords him here and his exposure at the Resurrection resemble a smooth stone covered in soil. An observer supposes it to be good ground fit for cultivation. Then a heavy downpour strikes it and leaves it a dry, bare stone, free of soil. Likewise, those who make a display of their deeds benefit in this world through people’s praise and the concealment of their condition. When they arrive at the Resurrection, they find the deeds void and cannot benefit from anything they earned. God does not guide the unbelieving people to their right course and the well-being of their religion. This indirectly warns that display, reminders and injury are unbelieving characteristics, which the believer must avoid. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q2-264-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-264-s3","r":"q2-264","title":"The inward conditions of pure action","text":"The purification of deeds corresponds to the purification of hearts; the purification of hearts to watchfulness before the Knower of the unseen; watchfulness to gnosis; gnosis to witnessing; and witnessing is attained according to struggle. “Those who struggle for Us, We shall guide them to Our paths” [29:69]. The Ḥikam says: “Good deeds are the fruits of good states; good states come from realization in the stations of alighting ( مقامات الإنزال ).” In sum, someone who has not realized the station of effacement cannot have works altogether free from an admixture of defect. One who has realized passing away ascribes to himself neither giving nor withholding, movement nor stillness. Nor does he see another as existent, so as to hope for benefit or good from him. [B217] One of the allusive sayings declares: “You who act for show: the affairs of the person before whom you display yourself are in the hand of the One you disobey.” The comparison with a stone indicates hardness of heart and dryness of disposition. No good at all is to be expected from such a person. God is our refuge.","anchor":"en-q2-264-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-264-s4","r":"q2-264","title":"","text":"The Real then describes the opposite of these people: the sincere.","anchor":"en-q2-264-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-265","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground 2:265","anchor":"unit-q2-265"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-1","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"وَمَثَلُ الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمُ ابْتِغاءَ مَرْضاتِ اللَّهِ وَتَثْبِيتاً مِنْ أَنْفُسِهِمْ كَمَثَلِ جَنَّةٍ بِرَبْوَةٍ أَصابَها وابِلٌ فَآتَتْ أُكُلَها ضِعْفَيْنِ فَإِنْ لَمْ يُصِبْها وابِلٌ فَطَلٌّ وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ (265)","anchor":"ar-q2-265-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-2","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"قلت: الربوة- مثلثة الراء-: المكان المرتفع، والوابل: المطر الغزير، والطل: المطر الخفيف، وفي ذلك يقول الراجز:","anchor":"ar-q2-265-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-3","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"والطلُّ ما خفَّ من الأمْطَارِ ... والوابلُ الغزيرُ ذو أنْهِمَارِ","anchor":"ar-q2-265-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-4","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"و (ابتغاء مَرْضات الله) و (تثبيتاً) : حالان من الواو في: (ينفقون) ، أو مفعولان له. والتثبيت بمعنى التثبت، أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-265-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-5","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"التحقق، كقوله تعالى: وَتَبَتَّلْ إِلَيْهِ تَبْتِيلًا أي: تبتلاً.","anchor":"ar-q2-265-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-6","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمُ في سبيل الله ابْتِغاءَ مَرْضاتِ اللَّهِ وتحققاً مِنْ أَنْفُسِهِمْ بثواب الله، أو تحقيقاً من أنفسهم بالوصول إلى رضوان الله إن بذلوا أموالهم في طلب رضى الله، مَثَلُ نفقتهم في النمو والارتفاع كَمَثَلِ جَنَّةٍ أي: بستان بِرَبْوَةٍ بمكان مرتفع، فإن شجره يكون أحسن منظراً وأزكى ثمراً، أَصابَها وابِلٌ أي: مطر غزير فَآتَتْ أُكُلَها أي: ثمارها ضِعْفَيْنِ أي: مِثْلَيْ ما كانت تثمر في عادتها، أي: حملت في سَنَةٍ ما يحمل غيرها في سنتين، بسبب هذا المطر الذي نزل بها، فَإِنْ لَمْ يُصِبْها وابِلٌ فَطَلٌّ أي: فيصيبها طل، أي: مطر قليل يكفيها لطيب تربتها وارتفاع مكانها، فأقلُّ شيء يكفيها.","anchor":"ar-q2-265-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-7","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"والمراد: أن نفقات هؤلاء، لإخلاصهم وكمال يقينهم، كثيرة زاكية عند الله، وإن كانت قليلة في الحس فهي كثيرة في المعنى. وفي الحديث: «مَنْ تصدَّقَ ولو بلُقْمة وقعتْ في كَفٍّ الرحمن فيُرَبِّيها كما يُربى أحدُكُم فلُوَّهُ أو فَصِيله(1) ، حتى تكونَ مثل الجبل» . وفي قوله: وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ: تحذير من الرياء، وترغيب فى الإخلاص. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-265-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-8","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"الإشارة: تنمية الأعمال على قدر تصفية الأحوال، وتصفية الأحوال على قدر التحقق بمقامات الإنزال، أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-265-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-9","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"على قدر التحقق بالإنزال في مقامات اليقين، فكل من تحقق بالنزول في مقامات اليقين، ورسخت قدمه فيها، كانت أعماله كلها عظيمة، مضاعفة أضعافاً كثيرة، فتسبيحة واحدة من العارف، أو تهليلة واحدة، تعدل الوجود بأسره، ولا يزنها ميزان، وكذلك سائر أعمال العارف: كلها عظيمة مضاعفة لأنها بالله ومن الله وإلى الله، وما كان بالله ومن الله لا يطرقه نقص ولا يشوبه خلل، ولأجل هذا صارت أوقاتهم كلها ليلة القدر، وأماكنهم كلها عرفات، وأنفاسهم كلها زكيات، وصحبتهم كلها نفحات، ومخالطتهم كلها بركات. نفعنا الله بذكرهم وخرطنا في سلكهم. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-265-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-265-10","r":"q2-265","title":"2:265 · The garden on rising ground","text":"ثم حذَّر الحق تعالى من طوارق الخلل بعد تمام العمل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-265-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-265-s1","r":"q2-265","title":"The elevated garden and the two rains","text":"I say: rabwa ( ربوة ), whose rāʾ may take any of the three short vowels, is elevated ground. Wābil ( وابل ) is abundant rain; ṭall ( طل ), light rain. The poet in rajaz metre says: Ṭall is the light kind of rain; wābil is abundant, pouring rain. “Seeking God’s good pleasure” and “from firm conviction” are either circumstantial expressions referring to the subject of “spend,” or accusatives of purpose. Tathbīt ( تثبيت ) here means tathabbut ( تثبت ), being firmly convinced or assured, as “devote yourself to Him with complete devotion” [73:8] uses tabtīl where tabattul is meant.","anchor":"en-q2-265-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-265-s2","r":"q2-265","title":"The growth of a gift given with certainty","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the likeness of those who spend their wealth in God’s path seeking His good pleasure, inwardly certain of His reward—or assured that giving their wealth in pursuit of His approval leads to His good pleasure—is, in growth and increase, a garden upon rising ground. Its trees are more beautiful to behold and its fruit more abundant. A downpour strikes it, and it yields twice its ordinary produce: in one year it bears what another garden bears in two, because of the rain. If no downpour strikes it, light rain suffices because of its good soil and elevated position. The least thing is enough for it. The meaning is that, because of their sincerity and perfect certainty, these people’s gifts are abundant and fruitful before God. Though small in sensory measure, they are great in inward meaning. The hadith says: “Whoever gives in charity, even a morsel, it falls into the palm of the All-Merciful, who nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal or young camel, until it becomes like a mountain.” [B218] “God sees what you do” warns against display and encourages sincerity. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-265-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-265-s3","r":"q2-265","title":"The measure of action is the station from which it comes","text":"The growth of deeds corresponds to the purification of states, and the purification of states to realization in the stations of alighting: that is, realizing one’s alighting in the stations of certainty. Whoever is established in these stations, with firm footing in them, has all his deeds made great and multiplied many times. [B217] A single glorification or declaration of unity from a gnostic equals the whole of existence and cannot be weighed by a balance. So too all his other works are great and multiplied, for they are through God, from God and towards God. What is through God and from God is not visited by deficiency or mixed with defect. For this reason all their times become the Night of Power; all their places, ʿArafāt; all their breaths, pure; all their companionship, breaths of divine grace; all association with them, blessings. May God benefit us through remembering them and thread us into their company. Amen.","anchor":"en-q2-265-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-265-s4","r":"q2-265","title":"","text":"The Real then warns against the intrusion of defects after a work has been completed.","anchor":"en-q2-265-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-266","r":"q2-266","title":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most","text":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most 2:266","anchor":"unit-q2-266"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-266-1","r":"q2-266","title":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most","text":"أَيَوَدُّ أَحَدُكُمْ أَنْ تَكُونَ لَهُ جَنَّةٌ مِنْ نَخِيلٍ وَأَعْنابٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ لَهُ فِيها مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَراتِ وَأَصابَهُ الْكِبَرُ وَلَهُ ذُرِّيَّةٌ ضُعَفاءُ فَأَصابَها إِعْصارٌ فِيهِ نارٌ فَاحْتَرَقَتْ كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمُ الْآياتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ (266)","anchor":"ar-q2-266-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-266-2","r":"q2-266","title":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most","text":"قلت: الإعصار: عمود من ريح فيه عجاجة، يدور ويرتفع.","anchor":"ar-q2-266-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-266-3","r":"q2-266","title":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أيتمنى أحدكم أَنْ تَكُونَ لَهُ جَنَّةٌ أي: بستان مِنْ نَخِيلٍ وَأَعْنابٍ، هما الغالبان فيه لكثرة منافعهما، تَجْرِي مِنْ تحت تلك الأشجار الْأَنْهارُ إذ من كمال البستان أن يشتمل على الماء البارد والظل الممدود، ولَهُ فِيها أي: في تلك الجنة مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَراتِ زائدة على النخيل والأعناب، ثم أَصابَهُ الْكِبَرُ فضعف عن القيام بتلك الجنة، وَلَهُ ذُرِّيَّةٌ ضُعَفاءُ لا يستطيعون القيام بأنفسهم لصغرهم، فأصاب تلك الجنة إِعْصارٌ أي: ريح شديد فِيهِ نارٌ فَاحْتَرَقَتْ تلك الجنة، فلا تسأل عن حسرة صاحب هذا البستان، لخوفه من ضياع نفسه وعياله. وهذا مثال لمن يُكثر من أعمال البر، كالصلاة والصيام والصدقة والحج والجهاد وغير ذلك، ثم يُعجب به، ويفتخر وَيَمُنَّ بصدقته أو يؤذي، فتحبط تلك الأعمال وتذهب، فيتحسر عليها يوم القيامة، وهو أحوج ما يكون إليها. أو يعمل بالطاعة في أيام عمره، فإذا قرب الموت عمل بالمعاصي حتى ختم له بها فحبطت تلك الأعمال، والعياذ بالله كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمُ الْآياتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُونَ فيها فتعتبرون، وتخلصون في أعمالكم، وتخافون من سوء عاقبتكم. أعاذنا الله من ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q2-266-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-266-4","r":"q2-266","title":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most","text":"الإشارة: في الآية تخويف للمريد أن يرجع إلى عوائده، ويلتفت إلى عوالم حسه، فيشتغل بالدنيا بعد أن استشرف على جنة المعارف، تجري على قلبه أنهار العلوم، فينقُضُ العهد مع شيخه، أو يسيىء الأدب معه، ولم يتب حتى تيبس أشجار معارفه، وتلعب به ريح الهوى، فيحترق قلبه بنار الشهوات.","anchor":"ar-q2-266-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-266-5","r":"q2-266","title":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most","text":"قال البيضاوي: وأشبههم به من جال سره في عالم الملكوت، وترقى بفكره إلى جناب الجبروت، ثم نكص على عقبيه إلى عالم الزور، والتفت إلى ما سوى الحق وجعل سعيه هباء منثوراً. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-266-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-266-6","r":"q2-266","title":"2:266 · The garden destroyed when it is needed most","text":"ثم رغّب الحق تعالى فى الصدقة من الكسب الطيب، فرضا ونفلا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-266-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-266-s1","r":"q2-266","title":"The whirlwind","text":"I say: an iʿṣār ( إعصار ) is a column of wind containing dust, revolving and rising.","anchor":"en-q2-266-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-266-s2","r":"q2-266","title":"A lifetime’s works lost at its end","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: would any of you wish to have a garden of palms and vines—its predominant trees because of their many benefits—with rivers flowing beneath them? A perfect garden includes cool water and extended shade. Within it he has every kind of fruit besides palms and vines. Then old age overtakes him, weakening his ability to tend it, and he has young, weak children who cannot look after themselves. A strong whirlwind containing fire strikes the garden and burns it. Do not ask how great the owner’s grief would be, fearing ruin for himself and his dependants. This illustrates someone who performs abundant good works—prayer, fasting, charity, pilgrimage, fighting in God’s cause and others—then admires and boasts of them, or reminds recipients of his charity and injures them. The works become void and disappear, and he grieves over them at the Resurrection when he most needs them. Or he acts obediently throughout his life, then near death acts disobediently and ends in that state, so that the works are lost. God is our refuge. [B219] Thus God makes the signs clear so that you may reflect, take a lesson, act sincerely and fear an evil end. May God preserve us from that.","anchor":"en-q2-266-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-266-s3","r":"q2-266","title":"Returning to habit after approaching the garden of gnosis","text":"The verse warns the disciple against returning to his habitual ways and looking back towards the worlds of sensation, becoming occupied with the world after looking out upon the garden of gnoses, with rivers of knowledge flowing through his heart. He breaks the covenant with his shaykh or behaves improperly towards him, and does not repent until the trees of his gnosis wither. The wind of desire plays with him, and his heart burns in the fire of appetites. Al-Bayḍāwī said: the person who most resembles this is one whose secret roamed the unseen kingdom and whose thought ascended to the precinct of divine omnipotence, then turned back towards the world of falsehood, looked to other than the Real and made his striving scattered dust.","anchor":"en-q2-266-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-266-s4","r":"q2-266","title":"","text":"The Real then encourages giving charity from good earnings, whether obligatory or voluntary.","anchor":"en-q2-266-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-267","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state 2:267","anchor":"unit-q2-267"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-1","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْفِقُوا مِنْ طَيِّباتِ ما كَسَبْتُمْ وَمِمَّا أَخْرَجْنا لَكُمْ مِنَ الْأَرْضِ وَلا تَيَمَّمُوا الْخَبِيثَ مِنْهُ تُنْفِقُونَ وَلَسْتُمْ بِآخِذِيهِ إِلاَّ أَنْ تُغْمِضُوا فِيهِ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ حَمِيدٌ (267)","anchor":"ar-q2-267-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-2","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"قلت: (تيمموا) : أصله: تتيمموا، أي تقصدوا، وجملة (تنفقون) : حال مقدرة- من فاعل (تيمموا) ، و (منه) :","anchor":"ar-q2-267-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-3","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"يصح أن يتعلق ب- (تنفقون) أو ب- (الخبيث) ، أي: ولا تقصدوا الخبيث حال كونكم تنفقونه، أو لا تقصدوا الخبيث تنفقون منه، و (لستم بآخذيه) : حال أيضًا من فاعل (تنفقون) .","anchor":"ar-q2-267-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-4","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْفِقُوا مِنْ طَيِّباتِ ما كَسَبْتُمْ من الأموال في التجارة وغيرها، وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «يا معشرَ التُجار، أنتم فُجار إلا من اتقى وبَرَّ وصَدَق وَقَالَ بالمال(1) هكذا وهكذا» .","anchor":"ar-q2-267-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-5","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"وقوله مِنْ طَيِّباتِ ما كَسَبْتُمْ أي: من حلاله، أو من خياره، أما في الزكاة فعلى الوجوب، إذ لا يصح دفع الرديء فيها، وأما فى التطوع فعلى سبيل الكمال، وأنفقوا أيضاً من طيبات ما أَخْرَجْنا لَكُمْ مِنَ الْأَرْضِ من أنواع الحبوب والثمار والفواكه، وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «مَا مِنْ مُسْلِم يَغْرِسَ غَرْساً، أَوْ يَزرَعُ زَرْعاً، فَيَأكُلُ مِنهُ إنْسَانٌ ولا دَابَّةٌ ولاَ طَائِرٌ، إلاَّ كَانَت لَهُ صدقةً إلى يَوَمِ الِقِيَامِةِ» . ولا تقصدوا الْخَبِيثَ أي: الرديء من أموالكم، فتنفقون منه وأنتم لَسْتُمْ بِآخِذِيهِ في ديونكم إِلَّا أَنْ تُغْمِضُوا بصركم فيه، وتقبضونه حياء أو كرهاً أو مسامحة.","anchor":"ar-q2-267-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-6","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"نزلت في قوم كانوا يتصدقون بخبيث التمر وشراره، فنُهوا عنه، وأدبهم بقوله: وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عن إنفاقكم، وإنما أمركم به منفعة لكم، حَمِيدٌ بقبوله وإثابته، فهو فعيل بمعنى فاعل، مبالغة، أي: يحمد فعلكم ويشكره لكم، إن أحسنتم فيه، وفي الحديث عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «إِنَّ اللهَ قَسَم بينَكم أخلاقكم كما قسم أرزاقكم، وإن الله طيِّبٌ لا يقبلُ إلا طيباً، لا يكسبُ عبدٌ مالاً من حرام فيتصدقُ منه فيُقْبل منه، ولا ينفقُ منه فيبَارك له فيه، ولا يتركهُ خلفَ ظهره إلا كان زاده إلى النار، وإن الله لا يمحو السيّء بالسيىء ولكن يمحو السيء بالحسن، وإن الخبيث لا يمحوه الخبيث» .","anchor":"ar-q2-267-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-7","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"الإشارة: يا أيها الذين آمنوا إيمان الخصوص، أنفقوا العلوم اللدنية والأسرار الربانية، من طيبات ما كسبتم من تصفية أسراركم وتزكية أرواحكم، وأنفقوا أيضاً علوم الشريعة وأنوار الطريقة، مما أخرجنا لكم من أرض نفوسكم التي تزكت بالأعمال الصافية والأحوال المُرْضِية.","anchor":"ar-q2-267-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-8","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"ولا تيمموا العمل الخبيث أو الحال الخبيث، تريدون أن تنفقوا منه شيئاً من تلك العلوم، فإن ذلك لا يزيد النفس إلا جهلاً وبعداً، فكما أن الحبة لا تنبت إلا في الأرض الطيبة، كذلك النفس لا تُدفن إلا في الحالة المرضية، فلا تؤخذ العلوم اللدنية من النفس حتى تدفن في أرض الخُمول، وأرض الخمول هي الأحوال المرضية، الموافقة للقواعد الشرعية، وإليه الإشارة بقوله: وَلَسْتُمْ بِآخِذِيهِ أي: لستم بآخذي العلم اللدني من الحال الخبيث، إلا أن تغيبوا فيه عن حِسَّكم، ومن غلبه الحال لم يبق عليه مقال. وعليها تتخرج قصة لص الحَمَّام(2) ، فلا يقتدى به لغلبة الحال عليه، واعلموا أن الله غني حميد، لا يتقرب إليه إلا بما هو حميد. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-267-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-267-9","r":"q2-267","title":"2:267 · Give what is good, and seek knowledge through a sound spiritual state","text":"ثم حذّر من الشّحّ، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-267-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-267-s1","r":"q2-267","title":"Intention and the circumstantial clauses","text":"I say: tayammamū ( تيمموا ) originally has two initial tāʾs : tatayammamū , “intend” or “deliberately seek.” “You spend” is an anticipated circumstance ( حال مقدرة ) referring to its subject. “From it” ( منه ) may attach to “spend” or “the bad”: do not select the bad, intending to spend it; or do not select bad property from which to spend. “You would not accept it” is likewise a circumstance referring to the subject of “spend.”","anchor":"en-q2-267-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-267-s2","r":"q2-267","title":"Lawful earnings and acceptable quality","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: you who believe, spend from the good property you earn through trade and other means. The Prophet is quoted as saying: “Company of traders, you are sinful except those who are mindful of God, act uprightly, speak truthfully and distribute wealth this way and that.” [B220] “From the good things you have earned” means their lawful portion, or their good quality. In obligatory alms this is binding, since giving inferior goods is not valid; in voluntary charity it is a matter of perfection. Spend also from the good things We have brought forth from the earth: the different grains, crops and fruits. The Prophet said: “No Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop from which a human, animal or bird eats without it being a charity for him until the Day of Resurrection.” [B221] Do not deliberately select the bad—the inferior part of your property—to spend, when you would not accept it in payment of debts unless you closed your eyes to it and took it through embarrassment, reluctance or indulgence. The verse was revealed concerning people who gave bad and inferior dates in charity; they were forbidden to do so. He disciplines them with: “Know that God is Independent.” He needs none of your expenditure; He commands it only for your benefit. He praises you by accepting and rewarding it. Here ḥamīd ( حميد ), on the pattern faʿīl , has the intensive sense of an active participle: He commends and thanks you for your deed if you perform it well. The Messenger of God is quoted as saying: “God has apportioned your characters as He apportioned your provisions. God is good and accepts only what is good. A servant does not earn unlawful wealth and give charity from it with acceptance, nor spend from it with blessing. If he leaves it behind him, it becomes his provision for the Fire. God does not erase evil through evil, but erases evil through good; the impure does not erase the impure.” [B222]","anchor":"en-q2-267-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-267-s3","r":"q2-267","title":"A sound state is the soil of sound knowledge","text":"You who believe with the faith of the elect: spend the divinely bestowed sciences and lordly mysteries from the good fruits of purifying your secrets and refining your spirits. Spend also the sciences of Sacred Law and the lights of the Path, from what We have brought forth from the earth of your selves, purified by pure deeds and pleasing states. Do not seek an impure deed or impure state, intending to impart any of these sciences from it. That only increases the self’s ignorance and distance. As a seed grows only in good earth, so the self is to be buried only in an approved state. Divinely bestowed knowledge is not drawn from the self until it has been buried in the earth of obscurity ( أرض الخمول ). The earth of obscurity is the approved states that accord with the principles of the Sacred Law. This is indicated by “you would not accept it”: you do not receive divinely bestowed knowledge from an impure state, unless you have become absent within it from your sensory awareness. One overcome by a state is beyond reproach for that state. On this basis the story of the thief at the bathhouse is explained: he is not to be imitated, because a state had overcome him. [B223] Know that God is Independent, Praiseworthy; one draws near to Him only through what is praiseworthy. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-267-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-267-s4","r":"q2-267","title":"","text":"He then warns against avarice.","anchor":"en-q2-267-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-268","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace 2:268","anchor":"unit-q2-268"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-1","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"الشَّيْطانُ يَعِدُكُمُ الْفَقْرَ وَيَأْمُرُكُمْ بِالْفَحْشاءِ وَاللَّهُ يَعِدُكُمْ مَغْفِرَةً مِنْهُ وَفَضْلاً وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ (268)","anchor":"ar-q2-268-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-2","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"قلت: يقال: وعدته خيراً ووعدته شرّاً، هذا إن ذكر الخير أو الشر، وأما إذا لم يذكر فيقال في الخير: وعدته، وفى الشر: أوعدته، قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-268-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-3","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"وإنّيَ وإنْ أوْعَدْتُهُ أوْ وَعَدْتُهُ ... لمخلِفُ إيعادي ومنْجِزُ مَوْعدي(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-268-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-4","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"و (الفحشاء) هنا: البخل والشح.","anchor":"ar-q2-268-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-5","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الشَّيْطانُ يَعِدُكُمُ أي: يخوفكم الْفَقْرَ بسبب الإنفاق، ويقول في وسوسته: إن أعطيت مالك بقيت فقيراً تتكفف الناس، وَيَأْمُرُكُمْ بِالْفَحْشاءِ أي: ويأمركم بالبخل والشح، والعرب تسمي البخيل فاحشاً، وفي الحديث: «البخيلُ بعيدٌ من اللهِ، بعيدُ من الناسِ، بَعِيدٌ مِنَ الجَنَّةِ قَرِيبٌ من النَّارِ. والسخي قَرِيبٌ مِنَ اللهِ. قَرِيبٌ من النَّاس، قريبٌ من الجَنَّةِ، بَعِيدٌ من النارِ. ولجَاهلٌ سَخِيٌ أَحَبُ إلى الله من عابدٍ بخيل» .","anchor":"ar-q2-268-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-6","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"وفي حديث آخر: «إنَّ الله يأخذُ بيد السخيِّ كلما عثر» . وَاللَّهُ يَعِدُكُمْ في الإنفاق مَغْفِرَةً مِنْهُ لذنوبكم، وستراً لعيوبكم، وَفَضْلًا أي: خَلَفاً أفضل مما أنفقتم في الدنيا والآخرة، وَما أَنْفَقْتُمْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ فَهُوَ يُخْلِفُهُ، وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ الفضل والعطاء، عَلِيمٌ بما أنفقتم، ولماذا أنفقتم، وفيما أخلصتم، لا يخفى عليه شيء من أموركم.","anchor":"ar-q2-268-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-7","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"الإشارة: إذا توجه المريد إلى الله تعالى، وأراد سلوك طريق التجريد والزهد والانقطاع إلى الله تعالى، تعرض له الشيطان، اختباراً منه تعالى وابتلاء، إذ الحضرة محروسة بالقواطع ليظهر الصادق في الطلب من الكاذب، فيخوفه من الفقر، ويأمره بالوقوف مع الأسباب والعوائد، وهي أفحش المعاصي عند الخواص، إذ الهمة العالية تأنف عن الاشتغال بغير الحضرة الإلهية. والله يعدكم- أيها المتوجهون إليه- مغفرة لذنوبكم، وستراً لعيوبكم، فيغطي وصفكم بوصفه، ونعتكم بنعته، فيُوصلكم بما منه إليكم من الفضل والجود، لا بما منكم إليه من المجاهدة والمكابدة، وَلَوْلا فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ مَا زَكى مِنْكُمْ مِنْ أَحَدٍ أَبَداً، (والله واسع) الجود والإحسان، (عليم) بمن يستحق الفضل والامتنان.","anchor":"ar-q2-268-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-268-8","r":"q2-268","title":"2:268 · The threat of poverty and the promise of grace","text":"ومن نتائج الزهد والانقطاع: ورود الحكمة على لسان العبد وقلبه، كما أشار إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-268-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-268-s1","r":"q2-268","title":"Promise, threat and indecency","text":"I say: one says waʿadtuhu khayran , “I promised him good,” and waʿadtuhu sharran , “I threatened him with evil,” when the good or evil is specified. Without specifying it, waʿadtuhu denotes promising good, while awʿadtuhu denotes threatening evil. The poet says: Whether I threaten him or promise him, I fail to carry out my threat and fulfil my promise. “Indecency” ( الفحشاء ) here means miserliness and avarice.","anchor":"en-q2-268-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-268-s2","r":"q2-268","title":"The whispering that restrains generosity","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Satan threatens you with poverty because of expenditure. In his whispering he says: “If you give away your property, you will become poor, holding out your hand to people.” He commands you to miserliness and avarice; the Arabs call a miser fāḥish . A report says: “The miser is far from God, far from people, far from the Garden and near the Fire. The generous person is near God, near people, near the Garden and far from the Fire. An ignorant but generous person is dearer to God than a miserly worshipper.” Another says: “God takes the generous person by the hand whenever he stumbles.” [B224] God promises you, through expenditure, forgiveness for your sins, concealment of your faults and bounty: a replacement better than what you spent, in this world and the Hereafter. “Whatever you spend, He replaces it” [34:39]. God is expansive in bounty and giving. He knows what you spend, why you spend it and where your sincerity lies. Nothing in your affairs is hidden from Him.","anchor":"en-q2-268-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-268-s3","r":"q2-268","title":"The test on the path of detachment","text":"When a disciple turns towards God Most High and wishes to travel the path of detachment, renunciation and complete devotion to Him, Satan confronts him as a test and trial from God. The Presence is guarded by obstacles, so that the truthful seeker may be distinguished from the false. He frightens him with poverty and commands him to remain with causes and customary patterns—the most indecent disobedience in the eyes of the elect, for lofty aspiration disdains occupation with anything other than the divine Presence. God promises you who turn towards Him forgiveness of sins and concealment of faults. He covers your quality with His quality and your attribute with His attribute, bringing you to Himself through the bounty and generosity that come from Him to you, not through the struggle and endurance that come from you to Him. “Were it not for God’s bounty and mercy upon you, not one of you would ever become pure” [24:21]. God is expansive in generosity and goodness, knowing who is fit for bounty and grace.","anchor":"en-q2-268-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-268-s4","r":"q2-268","title":"","text":"One fruit of renunciation and complete devotion is the coming of wisdom upon the servant’s tongue and heart, as He indicates next.","anchor":"en-q2-268-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-269","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom 2:269","anchor":"unit-q2-269"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-1","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"يُؤْتِي الْحِكْمَةَ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَمَنْ يُؤْتَ الْحِكْمَةَ فَقَدْ أُوتِيَ خَيْراً كَثِيراً وَما يَذَّكَّرُ إِلاَّ أُولُوا الْأَلْبابِ (269)","anchor":"ar-q2-269-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-2","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"قال البيضاوي: الحكمة: تحقيق العلم وإتقان العمل. هـ. وقيل: هي سرعة الجواب وإصابة الصواب، وقيل:","anchor":"ar-q2-269-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-3","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"كل فضل جَزْلٍ من قول أو فعل.","anchor":"ar-q2-269-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-4","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، يُؤْتِي الحق تعالى الْحِكْمَةَ مَنْ يَشاءُ من عباده، وهي التفقّه في الدين والتبصر في الأمور. قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «مَنْ يُرد اللهُ به خيراً يُفقِّهْه في الدين، ويُلهمْه رُشْدَه» ، وقيل: الحكمة: الإصابة في الرأي. وقيل: الفهم في كتاب الله. وقيل: الفهم عن الله. وَمَنْ يُؤْتَ الْحِكْمَةَ أي: أعطيها، فَقَدْ أُوتِيَ خَيْراً كَثِيراً لأنه حاز خيرَ الدارَيْن، ولا شك أن مَن حقَّق العلم بالله وبأحكامه، وأتقنَ العملَ بما أمره الله به، فقد صفا قلبه، وتطهر سره، فصار من أولي الألباب ولذلك قال عقبه: وَما يَذَّكَّرُ إِلَّا أُولُوا الْأَلْبابِ.","anchor":"ar-q2-269-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-5","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"الإشارة: الحكمة هي: شهود الذات مرتديةً بأنوار الصفات، وهي حقيقة المعرفة، ومن عرف الله هابه، ولذلك قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «رأس الحكمة مخافة الله» . وقيل: هي تجريد السر لورود الإلهام، وقيل: هي النور المفرق بين الوسواس والإلهام، وقيل: شهود الحق تعالى في جميع الأحوال. والتحقيق: أن الحكمة هي إبداع الشيء وإتقانه حتى يأتي على غاية الكمال، ويجري ذلك في العلم والعمل والحال والمعرفة.","anchor":"ar-q2-269-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-6","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"وقال القُشَيْري: الحكمة: أن يَحكم عليك خاطر الحق لا داعي الباطل، وأن تحكم قواهر الحق لا زواجر الشيطان.","anchor":"ar-q2-269-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-7","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"ويقال: الحكمة: صواب الأمر، ويقال: هي ألا تغلب عليك رعونات البشرية، ومنْ لا حُكْم له على نَفْسِه لا حُكْمَ له على غيره. ويقال: الحكمة: موافقة أمر الله، والسفه: مخالفة أمره، ويقال: الحكمة شهود الحق، والسفه: شهود الغير.","anchor":"ar-q2-269-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-8","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"قاله المحشي.","anchor":"ar-q2-269-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-9","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"واعلم أن الصوفية، في اصطلاحهم، يُعبِّرون عن أسرار الذات بالقدرة، وعن أنوار الصفات- وهي ظهور آثارها- بالحكمة. فالوجودُ كله قائم بين الحكمة والقدرة، فالقدرة تُبرز الأشياء، والحكمة تَسترها. فربط الأشياء واقترانها بأسبابها تُسمى عندهم الحكمة، وإنفاذ الأمر وإظهاره يسمى القدرة، فمن وقف مع الحكمة حجب عن","anchor":"ar-q2-269-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-10","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"شهود القدرة، وكان محجوباً عن الله. ومن نفذ إلى شهود القدرة ولم يرتبط مع الأسباب والعوائد كان عارفاً محبوباً. فالعارف الكامل هو الذي جمع بين شهود القدرة وإقرار الحكمة، فأعطى كل ذي حق حقه، وَوَفَّى كلَّ ذي قسط قسطه، لكن يكون ذلك ذوقاً وكشفاً، لا علماً وتقليداً. وبالله تعالى التوفيق:","anchor":"ar-q2-269-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-269-11","r":"q2-269","title":"2:269 · Wisdom and the union of power with wisdom","text":"ثم رغّب فى الإخلاص، وحذّر من شوب الحظوظ فى النفقة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-269-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-269-s1","r":"q2-269","title":"Knowledge realized and action perfected","text":"Al-Bayḍāwī said: wisdom ( الحكمة ) is realizing knowledge and perfecting action. Other definitions are: readiness in answering and correctness in judgment; or every substantial excellence of speech or deed. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: He gives wisdom to whom He wills among His servants—understanding religion and seeing clearly into affairs. The Prophet said: “Whomever God desires good for, He gives understanding in religion and inspires with right guidance.” [B225] Wisdom is also explained as sound judgment, understanding God’s Book, or understanding from God. Whoever is given wisdom has received abundant good, for he has obtained the good of both abodes. One who realizes knowledge of God and His rulings and perfects the action He commands has surely purified his heart and cleansed his secret. He becomes one of those possessed of understanding ( أولو الألباب ). Hence the verse continues: “None takes heed except those possessed of understanding.”","anchor":"en-q2-269-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-269-s2","r":"q2-269","title":"Wisdom as perfected perception and conduct","text":"Wisdom is witnessing the Essence clothed in the lights of the attributes: the reality of gnosis. Whoever knows God stands in awe of Him. Hence the saying attributed to the Prophet: “The beginning of wisdom is fear of God.” Wisdom is also defined as stripping the secret free to receive inspiration; the light distinguishing satanic whispering from inspiration; or witnessing the Real Most High in every state. [B225] The precise account is that wisdom means bringing a thing into being and perfecting it until it reaches the utmost completeness. This applies to knowledge, action, spiritual state and gnosis. Al-Qushayrī said: wisdom is that an impulse from the Real should govern you, not a caller to falsehood; that the Real’s overpowering forces should rule, not Satan’s goads. Wisdom is also said to be correctness in affairs, or freedom from the dominance of human follies. Whoever has no rule over his own self has no rule over another. Wisdom is accord with God’s command, and folly is opposition to it. Wisdom is witnessing the Real, and folly is witnessing other than Him. The marginal commentator gives these sayings.","anchor":"en-q2-269-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-269-s3","r":"q2-269","title":"Power, wisdom and the complete gnostic","text":"Know that, in their technical usage, the Sufis call the mysteries of the Essence “power” ( القدرة ), and the lights of the attributes—the manifestation of their effects—“wisdom” ( الحكمة ). The whole of existence stands between wisdom and power. Power brings things forth; wisdom conceals them. [B226] The connection of things and their association with causes is what they call wisdom. The execution of the command and its manifestation is called power. Someone who remains with wisdom is veiled from witnessing power and is veiled from God. Someone who penetrates to witnessing power without remaining bound to causes and customary patterns is a beloved gnostic. The complete gnostic unites witnessing power with acknowledging wisdom. He gives everyone possessing a right his right and renders everyone possessing a portion his portion. This must, however, be through taste and unveiling, not merely knowledge and imitation. And success is through God Most High.","anchor":"en-q2-269-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-269-s4","r":"q2-269","title":"","text":"He then encourages sincerity and warns against mixing expenditure with personal interests.","anchor":"en-q2-269-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-270-271","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity 2:270–271","anchor":"unit-q2-270-271"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-1","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"وَما أَنْفَقْتُمْ مِنْ نَفَقَةٍ أَوْ نَذَرْتُمْ مِنْ نَذْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُهُ وَما لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنْصارٍ (270) إِنْ تُبْدُوا الصَّدَقاتِ فَنِعِمَّا هِيَ وَإِنْ تُخْفُوها وَتُؤْتُوهَا الْفُقَراءَ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ وَيُكَفِّرُ عَنْكُمْ مِنْ سَيِّئاتِكُمْ وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ (271)","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-2","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"قلت: النذْر: هو إلزَامُ المكلف نفسه ما لم يَجب، كقوله: لله عليَّ أن أتصدق بكذا، أو أصلي كذا، أو أن أصوم كذا، أو إن شفى الله مريضي فعليَّ كذا، فمن نطق بشيء من ذلك لزمه، ومن علق بشيء وحصل ذلك لزمه ما نطق به. و (نعما) أصلها: نِعم ما هي، فأدغمت الميم في الميم، وفي (نعم) : ثلاث لغات: «نعم» بفتح النون وكسر العين وهي الأصل، وبسكونها، وبكسر النون وسكون العين، فمن قرأ بكسر النون والعين، فعلى لغة كسر العين، وأتبع النون للعين، ومن اختلس، أشار إلى لغة السكون، ومن قرأ بفتح النون وكسر العين، فعلى الأصل وأدغم المثلين، ومن قرأ بفتح النون وسكون العين فعلى لغة (نعم) بالفتح والسكون، ثم أدغم، ولم يعتبر التقاء الساكنين لعروضه، أو لكون الثاني مُشدَّداً سهل ذلك. والله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-3","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"ومن قرأ: (ونكَّفرْ) ، بالجزم، فعطف على محل الجزاء، ومن قرأ بالرفع، فعلى الاستئناف، أي: ونحن نكفر، أو: فهو يكفر، على القراءتين.","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-4","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَما أَنْفَقْتُمْ مِنْ نَفَقَةٍ قليلة أو كثيرة، سرّاً أو علانية، في حق أو باطل، أَوْ نَذَرْتُمْ مِنْ نَذْرٍ بشرط أو بغير شرط، في طاعة أو معصية، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُهُ، فيجازيكم عليه، فمن أنفق في طاعة أو نذر قربة كان من المحسنين، ومن أنفق في معصية أو نذر معصية كان من الظالمين. وَما لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنْصارٍ ينصرونهم من عذاب الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-5","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"إِنْ تُظهروا الصَّدَقاتِ، مخلصين فيها، فَنِعِمَّا هِيَ أي: فنعم شيئاً إبداؤها، ولا سيما للمقتدى به، فهو أفضل في حقه، وَإِنْ تُخْفُوها وَتُؤْتُوهَا الْفُقَراءَ خفية فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ لأنه أقرب للإخلاص، وهذا","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-6","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"في التطوع، تفضل عَلانيتها بسبعين ضعفاً. وأما الفريضة ففيها تفصيل، فمن خاف على نفسه شوْبَ الرياء أخفى أو نَوّب، ومَنْ أَمِنَ أَظْهَر. فقد ورد أن علانية الفريضة تَفْضُلُ سرَّها بخمسة وعشرين ضعفاً، فإن فعلتم ما أُمرتم به في الوجهين، فقد أحسنتم، ونكفر عَنْكُمْ مِنْ سَيِّئاتِكُمْ أي: نستر عنكم بعض ذنوبكم، وقد ورد في صدقة السر أن صاحبها يُظله الله يوم لا ظِلَّ إِلا ظله وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ لا يخفى عليه مَن أَسَرَّ أو جَهَر، ومن أخلص أو خلط، ففيه ترغيب وترهيب. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-7","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"الإشارة: معاملة العبد مع مولاه: إما أن تكون لطلب الأجور، وإما لرفع الستور، فالأول يُعطي أجره من وراء الباب، والثاني يدخل مع الأحباب. وأما العامل للدنيا فهو ظالم لنفسه (وما للظالمين من أنصار) ، وفي بعض الآثار: طالب الدنيا أسير، وطالب الآخرة أجير، وطالب الحق أمير.","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-8","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"ثُم الناس في معاملة الحق على أقسام ثلاثة: قِسْمٍ يليق بهم الإخفاء والإسرار، وهم طالبو الإخلاص من المريدين السائرين. وقسْمٍ يليق بهم الإظهار وهم أهل الاقتداء من العلماء المخلصين. وقسْم لا يقفون مع ظهور ولا خفاء، بل مع ما يبرز في الوقت، وهم العارفون الكاملون. ولذلك قال الشيخ أبو العباس رضي الله عنه: (مَن أحبَّ الظهور فهو عبد الظهور، ومَن أحبّ الخفاء فهو عبد الخفاء، ومن كان عبد الله فسواء عليه أظهره أم أخفاه) .","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-270-271-9","r":"q2-270-271","title":"2:270–271 · Vows, open giving and hidden charity","text":"والهداية كلها بيد الله، ليس لغيره منها شىء، كما أبان ذلك الحقّ جلّ جلاله بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q2-270-271-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-270-271-s1","r":"q2-270-271","title":"Vows and the readings of niʿimmā","text":"I say: a vow ( النذر ) is a legally responsible person’s imposing upon himself something not already obligatory: “For God, I must give such-and-such in charity,” “pray such-and-such,” “fast such-and-such,” or “If God heals my sick person, such-and-such is due from me.” Whoever utters one of these is bound by it; whoever makes it conditional is bound when the condition occurs. Niʿimmā ( نعمّا ) is originally niʿma mā hiya , with one mīm assimilated into the other. The verb has three forms: naʿima , with fatḥa on the nūn and kasra on the ʿayn , the original form; naʿma , with quiescent ʿayn ; and niʿma , with kasra on the nūn and quiescent ʿayn . The reading with kasra on both consonants follows the form with kasra on the ʿayn , making the nūn conform to it. A reduced vowel ( اختلاس ) points towards the form with quiescence. The reading with fatḥa on the nūn and kasra on the ʿayn retains the original and assimilates the two identical consonants. The reading with fatḥa on the nūn and quiescent ʿayn follows naʿma and then assimilates, disregarding the meeting of two quiescent consonants because it is incidental, or because the second is doubled, making it easier. And God knows best. [B227] The jussive reading of “We efface” ( نكفّرْ ) is coordinated with the syntactic position of the conditional consequence. The indicative reading begins a new statement: “We efface,” or “He effaces,” according to the two pronominal readings.","anchor":"en-q2-270-271-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-270-271-s2","r":"q2-270-271","title":"The intention and manner of expenditure","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: whatever you spend, little or much, secretly or openly, rightly or wrongly; or whatever vow you undertake, conditionally or unconditionally, in obedience or disobedience—God knows it and will recompense you. Whoever spends in obedience or vows a pious act is among those who do good. Whoever spends in disobedience or vows disobedience is among the wrongdoers, who have no helpers to save them from God’s punishment. If you disclose your charities sincerely, how excellent their disclosure is—especially for someone whose example is followed, for whom it is preferable. If you conceal them and give to the poor secretly, that is better, being nearer to sincerity. This concerns voluntary charity: its secrecy surpasses its publicity seventyfold. Obligatory giving requires a distinction. Someone fearing an admixture of ostentation should conceal it or act through a deputy; someone secure from that should make it public. It is transmitted that the publicity of an obligatory gift surpasses its secrecy twenty-fivefold. [B228] If you do as commanded in either manner, you have acted well, and “We efface some of your evil deeds”: We conceal some of your sins. It is transmitted that the giver of secret charity is shaded by God on the day when there is no shade except His shade. God is aware of what you do. Neither the one who conceals nor the one who discloses escapes His knowledge, nor the sincere person or the one with mixed motives. The words therefore encourage and warn. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-270-271-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-270-271-s3","r":"q2-270-271","title":"Seeking wages, seeking unveiled communion","text":"The servant’s dealings with his Master are either to seek rewards or to lift veils. The first is given his wages from behind the door; the second enters with the beloved. Someone who works for this world wrongs himself, and the wrongdoers have no helpers. A transmitted saying declares: “The seeker of the world is a captive; the seeker of the Hereafter a hired worker; the seeker of the Real a prince.” People fall into three classes in their dealings with the Real. Concealment and secrecy befit disciples travelling in search of sincerity. Disclosure befits sincere scholars whose example is followed. A third class stops at neither disclosure nor concealment, but at what the moment brings forth: the complete gnostics. Hence Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās said: “Whoever loves to be seen is a servant of being seen. Whoever loves concealment is a servant of concealment. For someone who is God’s servant, it is the same whether He makes him manifest or conceals him.” [B229]","anchor":"en-q2-270-271-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-270-271-s4","r":"q2-270-271","title":"","text":"All guidance is in God’s hand; no other possesses any of it, as the Real, glorious is His majesty, explains next.","anchor":"en-q2-270-271-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-272","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver 2:272","anchor":"unit-q2-272"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-1","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"لَيْسَ عَلَيْكَ هُداهُمْ وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشاءُ ...","anchor":"ar-q2-272-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-2","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لنبيه عليه الصلاة والسلام: لَيْسَ عَلَيْكَ يا محمد هُداهُمْ أي: لا يجب عليك أن تخلق الهداية في قلوبهم، وليس من شأنك ذلك، إنما أنت نذير تدلُّ على الخير، كالنفقة وغيرها، وتنهى عن الشر كالمِّن والأذى، وإنفاق الخبيث، وغير ذلك من المساوئ وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشاءُ بفضله وإحسانه، فالأمور كلها بيد الله خيرها وشرها، ولكن من جهة الأدب مَّآ أَصابَكَ مِنْ حَسَنَةٍ فَمِنَ اللَّهِ وَما أَصابَكَ مِنْ سَيِّئَةٍ فَمِنْ نَفْسِكَ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-272-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-3","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"الإشارة: ما قيل في الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- يقال في ورثته من أهل التذكير، فليس بيدهم الهداية والتوفيق، وإنما شأنهم الإرشاد وبيان الطريق، فليس من شأن الدعاة إلى الله الحرص على هداية الخلق. وإنما من","anchor":"ar-q2-272-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-4","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"شأنهم بيان الحقّ. إِنْ تَحْرِصْ عَلى هُداهُمْ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يُضِلُّ. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-272-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-5","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"ثم رجع الحقّ تعالى إلى الترغيب في الصدقة والإخلاص فيها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-272-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-6","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"... وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلِأَنْفُسِكُمْ وَما تُنْفِقُونَ إِلاَّ ابْتِغاءَ وَجْهِ اللَّهِ وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يُوَفَّ إِلَيْكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ لاَ تُظْلَمُونَ (272)","anchor":"ar-q2-272-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-7","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"قلت: هذه ثلاث جمل كلها تدل على الترغيب في إنفاق الطيب وإخلاص النية.","anchor":"ar-q2-272-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-8","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ قليل أو كثير، فهو فَلِأَنْفُسِكُمْ لا ينتفع به غيركم، فإن كان طيباً فلأنفسكم، وإن كان خبيثاً فأجره لكم، وإن مننتم به أو آذيتم فقد ظلمتم أنفسكم، وإن أخلصتم فيه فلأنفسكم.","anchor":"ar-q2-272-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-9","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"وأيضاً إنكم تَدَّعُونَ أنكم ما تُنْفِقُونَ إِلَّا ابْتِغاءَ وَجْهِ اللَّهِ، فكيف تقصدون الخبيث، وتجعلونه لوجه الله؟ وكيف تَمُنُّونَ أو تؤذون بها وهى لوجه الله؟ هذا تكذيب للدعوى، وكل ما تنفقون من خيرٍ قليل أو كثير يُوَفَّ إِلَيْكُمْ جزاؤه يوم القيامة بسبعمائة إلى أضعاف كثيرة، ويخلفه لكم في الدنيا، وَأَنْتُمْ لا تُظْلَمُونَ شيئاً من أعمالكم إن أخلصتم أو أحسنتم. وستأتي إشارتها مع ما بعدها.","anchor":"ar-q2-272-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-272-10","r":"q2-272","title":"2:272 · Guidance belongs to God; the fruits of giving return to the giver","text":"ثم بيّن المصرف، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-272-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-272-s1","r":"q2-272","title":"The messenger indicates; God creates guidance","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says to His Prophet: their guidance is not your responsibility, Muḥammad. You are not required to create guidance in their hearts, nor is that your function. You are only a warner, pointing towards good, such as expenditure and other acts, and forbidding evil, such as reminders, injury, giving inferior things and other faults. God, however, guides whom He wills through His bounty and goodness. All affairs, good and evil, are in God’s hand. As a matter of proper manners, however: “Whatever good befalls you is from God, and whatever evil befalls you is from your self” [4:79]. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q2-272-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-272-s2","r":"q2-272","title":"The inheritors’ task is to make the path clear","text":"What is said concerning the Messenger applies to his inheritors among those who give reminders. Guidance and enabling success are not in their hands. Their task is direction and clarification of the path. Those who call to God should not be anxiously intent upon bringing creation to guidance; their task is to make the truth clear. “However eager you are for their guidance, God does not guide those He leaves astray” [16:37]. And God Most High knows best. The Real Most High then returns to encouraging charity and sincerity within it. Qurʾānic continuation · 2:272b وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلِأَنْفُسِكُمْ وَما تُنْفِقُونَ إِلَّا ابْتِغاءَ وَجْهِ اللَّهِ وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يُوَفَّ إِلَيْكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ لا تُظْلَمُونَ Whatever good you spend is for yourselves, and you spend only seeking God’s Face. Whatever good you spend will be repaid to you in full, and you will not be wronged.","anchor":"en-q2-272-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-272-s3","r":"q2-272","title":"The claim of sincerity and its demands","text":"I say: these three sentences all encourage giving what is good with a sincere intention. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: whatever good you spend, little or much, is for yourselves; its benefit accrues to you, not another. If it is good, it is for yourselves; if it is bad, its recompense is yours. If you remind the recipient or injure him, you wrong yourselves; if you act sincerely, it is for yourselves. [B230] Moreover, you claim that you spend only seeking God’s Face. How, then, can you deliberately select the bad and make it an offering for His Face? How can you remind or injure through a gift supposedly given for His Face? That belies the claim. Whatever good you spend, little or much, will be repaid in full at the Resurrection, seven hundredfold and many times beyond; He also replaces it for you in this world. You will be wronged in none of your deeds if you act sincerely or well. The spiritual allusion to this will follow together with the next verse.","anchor":"en-q2-272-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-272-s4","r":"q2-272","title":"","text":"He then identifies the recipients.","anchor":"en-q2-272-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-273","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God 2:273","anchor":"unit-q2-273"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-1","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"لِلْفُقَراءِ الَّذِينَ أُحْصِرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ لا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ ضَرْباً فِي الْأَرْضِ يَحْسَبُهُمُ الْجاهِلُ أَغْنِياءَ مِنَ التَّعَفُّفِ تَعْرِفُهُمْ بِسِيماهُمْ لا يَسْئَلُونَ النَّاسَ إِلْحافاً وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ (273)","anchor":"ar-q2-273-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-2","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"قلت: (للفقراء) : متعلق بمحذوف، أي: يعطي ذلك للفقراء، أو اجعلوا ما تنفقونه للفقراء، والإلحاف: هو الإلحاح في السؤال، وهو أن يلازم المسئول حتى يعطيه، وهو منصوب على المصدر أو الحال.","anchor":"ar-q2-273-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-3","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: تجعلون ما تنفقونه لِلْفُقَراءِ الَّذِينَ أُحْصِرُوا أي: حبسوا أنفسهم في سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وهو الجهاد، لا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ ضَرْباً فِي الْأَرْضِ أي: ذهاباً في الأرض للتجارة أو للأسباب، بل شغلهم الجهاد والتبتل للعبادة عن الأسباب، وهم أهل الصُّفَّة، كانوا نحواً من أربعمائة من فقراء المهاجرين، يسكنون صفة المسجد، يستغرقون أوقاتهم في العلم والذكر والعبادة، وكانوا يخرجون في كل سرية بعثها رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-273-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-4","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"قال ابن عباس رضي الله عنه: «وقف النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يوماً على أصحاب الصفة، فرأى فقرهم وجهدهم وطيب قلوبهم، فقال: «أبشروا يا أصحاب الصفة، فمن بقي من أمتي على النعت الذي أنتم عليه، راضياً بما فيه فإنه، من رفقائي» .","anchor":"ar-q2-273-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-5","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"وقيل: المراد الفقراء مطلقاً، حصرهم الفقر عن الضرب في الأرض للتجارة، يَحْسَبُهُمُ الْجاهِلُ بهم أَغْنِياءَ مِنَ التَّعَفُّفِ، أي: من أجل تعففهم عن السؤال، تَعْرِفُهُمْ بِسِيماهُمْ من الضعف ورثاثة الحال.","anchor":"ar-q2-273-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-6","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"الخطاب للرسول، أو لكل أحدٍ لا يَسْئَلُونَ النَّاسَ إِلْحافاً، أي: لا يسألون، وإن سألوا عن ضرورة لم يلحوا، وقيل: نفى للأمرين معا، أي: ليس لهم سؤال، فيقع فيه إلحاف، كقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q2-273-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-7","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"على لا حِبٍ لا يُهْتَدى بمنَارِه(1)","anchor":"ar-q2-273-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-8","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"وليس ثَمَّ لا حب ولا منار، وإنما المراد نفيهما، وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «منْ سأَلَ، وله أربعونَ دِرهماً، فَقَدْ سأل إلحافاً» .","anchor":"ar-q2-273-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-9","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ فيجازي على القليل والكثير، وهذا ترغيب في الإنفاق، وخصوصاً على هؤلاء.","anchor":"ar-q2-273-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-10","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"الإشارة: ما أفلح مَن أفلح، وخسر مَنْ خسر، إلا من نفسه وفلسه، فمن جاد بهما، أو بأحدهما، فقد فاز وأفلح وظفر بما قصد، والجود بالنفس أعظم، وهو يستلزم الجود بالفلس، والجود بالفلس، إن دام، يوصل إلى الجود بالنفس، والمراد بالجود بالنفس: إسلامها للشيخ يفعل بها ما يشاء، وتكون الإشارة فيها كافية عن التصريح، ومن بخل بهما أو بأحدهما، فقد خسر وخاب في طريق الخصوص، ومصرف ذلك هو الشيخ، أو الفقراء المنقطعون إلى الله الذين حصروا أنفسهم في سبيل الله، وهو الجهاد الأكبر.","anchor":"ar-q2-273-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-11","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"قال في القوت: وكان بعض الفضلاء يؤثر بالعطاء فقراء الصوفية دون غيرهم، فقيل له في ذلك، فقال: لأن هؤلاء همهم الله عزّ وجلّ، فإذا ظهر منهم فاقة تَشَتَّتَ قلبُ أحدِهم، فلأنْ أرد هِمة واحدٍ إلى الله أحب إليَّ من أن أعطي ألفاً من غيرهم ممن همه الدنيا. فذكر هذا الكلام لأبي القاسم الجنيد، فقال: هذا كلام وليّ من أولياء الله. ثم قال: ما سمعت كلاماً أحسنَ من هذا. وبلغني أن هذا الرجل اقتر حاله في أمر الدنيا","anchor":"ar-q2-273-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-12","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"حتى همّ بترك الحانوت فبعث إليه الجنيد بمال كان صرف إليه، وقال له: اجعل هذا في بضاعتك، ولا تترك الحانوت فإنَّ التجارة لا تضرُّ مثلك. ويقال: إن هذا لم يكن يأخذ من الفقراء ثمن ما يبتاعون منه. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q2-273-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-13","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"وكان عبد الله بن المبارك يصرف مصروفه لأهل العلم، ويقول: إني لا أعرف بعد النبوة أفضل من العلماء، فإذا اشتغل قلب أحدهم بالحاجة والعيلة لم يتفرغ للعلم، ولا يقبل على تعليم الناس، فرأيت أن أكفيهم أمر الدنيا لأفرغهم للعلم، فهو أفضل. هـ. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-273-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-273-14","r":"q2-273","title":"2:273 · The unobtrusive poor and support for those devoted to God","text":"ثم رغّب فى النفقة مطلقا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-273-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-273-s1","r":"q2-273","title":"The recipients and persistent asking","text":"I say: “For the poor” attaches to an omitted expression: this is given to the poor, or assign what you spend to the poor. Ilḥāf ( الإلحاف ) means insistence in asking: remaining with the person asked until he gives. It is accusative as an absolute accusative or a circumstance.","anchor":"en-q2-273-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-273-s2","r":"q2-273","title":"Those who cannot pursue a livelihood","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: assign what you spend to the poor who have confined themselves to God’s path—fighting in His cause—and cannot travel through the land for trade or means of livelihood. Fighting and exclusive devotion to worship have occupied them away from earning. These are the People of the Bench ( أهل الصفة ), about four hundred poor Emigrants who lived on the mosque’s covered platform. They devoted their time to knowledge, remembrance and worship, and went out with every expedition sent by the Messenger of God. [B231] Ibn ʿAbbās related: “The Prophet stood one day before the People of the Bench and saw their poverty, hardship and purity of heart. He said: ‘Rejoice, People of the Bench. Whoever of my community remains in the condition you are in, content with it, is among my companions.’” [B231] Another explanation takes the verse to concern the poor generally, whose poverty prevents travel for trade. Someone ignorant of their situation supposes them wealthy because of their restraint from asking. You recognise them by their marks: weakness and a shabby appearance. The address is to the Messenger or to everyone. “They do not ask people insistently”: they do not ask, or, if necessity makes them ask, they do not persist. Another explanation negates both asking and insistence: they make no request in which insistence could occur. It resembles the poet’s words: Upon a clear path by whose beacons one is not guided— where, according to this explanation, there is neither clear path nor beacon: both are negated. A report from the Prophet says: “Whoever asks while possessing forty dirhams has asked insistently.” [B231] Whatever good you spend, God knows it, recompensing little and much. This encourages expenditure, especially upon such people.","anchor":"en-q2-273-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-273-s3","r":"q2-273","title":"Giving oneself and one’s means","text":"Those who succeed and those who lose do so through their self and their money. Whoever gives both, or either, gains success and obtains his aim. Giving the self is greater and entails giving money. Giving money, if sustained, leads to giving the self. Giving the self means surrendering it to the shaykh, who acts upon it as he wills; a mere indication from him suffices without explicit instruction. Whoever withholds both or either loses and fails on the path of the elect. The recipients are the shaykh or the poor devoted entirely to God, who have confined themselves to His path: the greater struggle.","anchor":"en-q2-273-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-273-s4","r":"q2-273","title":"Supporting contemplatives and scholars","text":"The Qūt relates that a virtuous man preferred poor Sufis over others in giving. Asked why, he replied: “Their concern is God, mighty and majestic. When need appears, one of their hearts becomes scattered. Restoring one person’s aspiration to God is dearer to me than giving to a thousand others whose concern is the world.” These words were reported to Abū al-Qāsim al-Junayd, who said: “These are the words of one of God’s saints. I have heard no finer words.” It reached the author that this man’s worldly circumstances became so straitened that he considered closing his shop. Al-Junayd sent him money that had come to him, saying: “Put this into your stock and do not abandon the shop. Trade does not harm someone like you.” It is said that he would not take payment from the poor for what they bought from him. Here the quotation ends. ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak directed his expenditure towards scholars. He said: “After prophecy, I know nothing better than scholars. If one of their hearts becomes occupied with need and dependants, he cannot devote himself to knowledge or turn towards teaching people. I therefore thought it best to relieve them of worldly concerns and free them for knowledge.” And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-273-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-273-s5","r":"q2-273","title":"","text":"He then encourages expenditure generally.","anchor":"en-q2-273-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-274","r":"q2-274","title":"2:274 · Giving by night and day","text":"2:274 · Giving by night and day 2:274","anchor":"unit-q2-274"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-274-1","r":"q2-274","title":"2:274 · Giving by night and day","text":"الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ بِاللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهارِ سِرًّا وَعَلانِيَةً فَلَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (274)","anchor":"ar-q2-274-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-274-2","r":"q2-274","title":"2:274 · Giving by night and day","text":"قلت: الموصول مبتدأ، و (فلهم أجرهم) : خبر، والفاء للسببية، ولأن في الموصول معنى الشرط، وقيل: الخبر محذوف، أي: ومنهم الذين ينفقون الخ، و (فلهم) : استئناف بياني.","anchor":"ar-q2-274-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-274-3","r":"q2-274","title":"2:274 · Giving by night and day","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ بِاللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهارِ سِرًّا وَعَلانِيَةً، ويعمرون أوقاتهم بفعل الخيرات، فَلَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ إذا قدموا عليه، وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ من لحوق مكروه، وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ على فوات محبوب، بل وجدوا الله فأغناهم عن كل شيء.","anchor":"ar-q2-274-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-274-4","r":"q2-274","title":"2:274 · Giving by night and day","text":"قيل: نزلت في أبي بكر رضي الله عنه تصدَّق بأربعين ألف دينار، عشرة بالليل، وعشرة بالنهار، وعشرة بالسر، وعشرة بالعلانية، أو في علي- كرم الله وجهه- لم يملك إلا أربعة دراهم، فتصدق بدرهم ليلاً، ودرهم نهاراً، ودرهم سرّاً، ودرهم علانية. وهي عامة لمن فعل فعلهما.","anchor":"ar-q2-274-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-274-5","r":"q2-274","title":"2:274 · Giving by night and day","text":"الإشارة: أجر بذل الأموال هو إعطاء الثواب من وراء الباب، والأمن من العذاب وسوء المآب، وأجر بذل النفوس هو دخول حضرة القدوس، والأنس بالأحباب داخل الحجاب، فمن بذل نفسه لله على الدوام، أمنه من الحجبة في دار السلام، فلا خوف يلحقهم في الدارين، ولا يعتريهم حزن في الكونين. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q2-274-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-274-6","r":"q2-274","title":"2:274 · Giving by night and day","text":"ولما رغَّب في الصدقة، وكانت في الغالب لا يتوصل إليها إلا بتعاطي أسباب المال، وهو البيع والشراء حذر من الربا لئلا يتساهل الناس في المعاملة به، حرصاً على الصدقة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-274-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-274-s1","r":"q2-274","title":"The conditional force of the relative expression","text":"I say: the relative expression is the subject and “they have their reward” the predicate. The fāʾ expresses causation and appears because the relative expression contains a conditional meaning. Alternatively, the predicate is omitted: “Among them are those who spend …”; “they have” then begins an explanatory new sentence ( استئناف بياني ).","anchor":"en-q2-274-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-274-s2","r":"q2-274","title":"A life filled with good deeds","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those who spend their wealth by night and day, secretly and openly, filling their times with good deeds, have their reward with their Lord when they come to Him. They have no fear of something harmful overtaking them and do not grieve over a beloved thing lost. Rather, they have found God, who makes them independent of everything. The verse is said to concern Abū Bakr, who gave forty thousand dinars in charity: ten thousand by night, ten thousand by day, ten thousand secretly and ten thousand openly. Another account identifies ʿAlī, who possessed only four dirhams and gave one by night, one by day, one secretly and one openly. The verse applies generally to anyone who acts as they did. [B232]","anchor":"en-q2-274-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-274-s3","r":"q2-274","title":"Beyond reward at the door","text":"The reward of giving wealth is recompense from behind the door, and security from punishment and an evil return. The reward of giving the self is entrance into the presence of the All-Holy and intimacy with the beloved within the veil. Whoever continually gives his self to God is made secure from veiling in the Abode of Peace. No fear reaches them in either abode, and no grief befalls them in either world. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q2-274-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-274-s4","r":"q2-274","title":"","text":"Having encouraged charity, which is generally attained through the means of earning wealth—buying and selling—He warns against usury, lest eagerness to give charity make people lax about dealing in it.","anchor":"en-q2-274-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-275-279","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance 2:275–279","anchor":"unit-q2-275-279"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-1","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"الَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ الرِّبا لا يَقُومُونَ إِلاَّ كَما يَقُومُ الَّذِي يَتَخَبَّطُهُ الشَّيْطانُ مِنَ الْمَسِّ ذلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قالُوا إِنَّمَا الْبَيْعُ مِثْلُ الرِّبا وَأَحَلَّ اللَّهُ الْبَيْعَ وَحَرَّمَ الرِّبا فَمَنْ جاءَهُ مَوْعِظَةٌ مِنْ رَبِّهِ فَانْتَهى فَلَهُ ما سَلَفَ وَأَمْرُهُ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَمَنْ عادَ فَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (275) يَمْحَقُ اللَّهُ الرِّبا وَيُرْبِي الصَّدَقاتِ وَاللَّهُ لاَ يُحِبُّ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ أَثِيمٍ (276) إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ وَأَقامُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتَوُا الزَّكاةَ لَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (277) ","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-2","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"قلت: (الربا) في الأصل: هو الزيادة، رَبا المال يربو: زاد. وكتبت بالواو مراعاة للأصل، وهو المصدر، قال الفراء: إنما كتبوه بالواو لأن أهل الحجاز تعلموا الكتابة من أهل الحيرة، ولغتهم الربو، فعلموهم صورة الحروف، وكذلك قرأها أبو السمال العدوي، وقرأ الأخَوَان بالإمالة لمكان الكسرة، والباقون بالتفخيم.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-3","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"والربا في اصطلاح الشرع على قسمين: ربا الفضل وربا النِّسَاءِ، فأما ربا الفضل فهو التفاضل بين الطعامين أو النقدين في المبادلة من الجنس الواحد، فإن اختلفت الأجناس فلا حرج، وأما ربا النساء فهو بيع الطعامين أو النقدين بعضهما ببعض بالتأخير، وهذا حرام ولو اختلفت الأجناس.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-4","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ الرِّبا أي: يأخذونه، وإنما خص الأكل لأنه أعظم منافع المال، لا يَقُومُونَ من قبورهم يوم البعث إِلَّا كَما يَقُومُ المجنون الَّذِي يَتَخَبَّطُهُ الشَّيْطانُ مِنَ أجل الْمَسِّ الذي يمسه يقوم ويسقط، رُوِيَ أن بطونهم تكون أمامهم كالبيت الضخم، يقوم أحدهم فتميل به بطنه فيصرع، وعن أبى هريرة رضي الله عنه أنه قال: قال رسول الله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «لما أُسْرِيَ بِي إلى السماء رأيتُ رِجالاً بُطُونُهُمْ كَالبُيوتِ، فيهَا حَيَّاتٌ تُرى مِنْ خِارِجِ بُطُونِهمْ، فقلت: مَنْ هؤلاءِ يا جِبْرِيل؟ فقال: أكَلَةُ الرِّبا» .","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-5","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"ذلِكَ العذاب بسبب أنهم استحلُّوا الربا، وقالُوا إِنَّمَا الْبَيْعُ مِثْلُ الرِّبا فنظموا الربا والبيع في سلك واحد، وفيه عكس التشبيه. والأصل: إنما الربا مثل البيع، قصدوا المبالغة، كأنهم جعلوا الربا أصلاً وقاسوا عليه البيع.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-6","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"وذلك أن أهل الجاهلية كان أحدهم إذا حلّ ماله على غريمه يقول الغريم: زدني في الأجل أزدك في المال، فيفعلان، ويقولان: سواء علينا الزيادة في أول البيع بالربح أو عند محل الدين، هو مراضاة. فكذبهم الحقّ تعالى بقوله: وَأَحَلَّ اللَّهُ الْبَيْعَ وَحَرَّمَ الرِّبا لأن القياس مع وجود النص فاسد، والفرق ظاهر فإن من باع درهماً","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-7","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"بدرهمين ضيع درهماً من غير فائدة، بخلاف من اشترى سلعة بدرهم، وباعها بدرهمين، فلعل مساس الحاجة، والرغبة فيها، توقع رواجها فيجبر الغبن.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-8","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"فَمَنْ جاءَهُ مَوْعِظَةٌ مِنْ رَبِّهِ كالنهي عن الربا، فَانْتَهى وترك الربا فَلَهُ ما سَلَفَ قبل التحريم ولا يَرُدُّهُ، وَأَمْرُهُ إِلَى اللَّهِ لا إلى أحد منكم، فلا يتعرض له، وَمَنْ عادَ إلى تحليل الربا بعد بلوغه النهي فَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ لأنهم كفروا وسفهوا أمر الله. يَمْحَقُ اللَّهُ الرِّبا أي: يذهب بركته، ويُهلك المال الذي يدخل فيه وَيُرْبِي الصَّدَقاتِ أي: يضاعف ثوابها ويُبارك في المال الذي أخرجت منه، فقد رُوِيَ عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أنه قال: «ما نَقَصَ مالٌ مِنْ صَدقة» ، «وأنه يُربي الصدقةَ حتى تكونَ مثلَ الجبل» . قال يحيى بن معاذ: (ما أعرفُ حبةً تزن جبال الدنيا إلا الحبَّةَ من الصدقة) .","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-9","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"وَاللَّهُ لا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ أي: مُصِرٍّ على تحليل المحرمات، أَثِيمٍ أي: منهمك في ارتكاب المنهيات، أي: لا يرتضي حاله، ولا يحبه كما يحب التوابين.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-10","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"ثم ذكر مقابله فقال: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بالله، وصدَّقُوا بما جاء من عنده، وَعَمِلُوا الأعمال الصَّالِحاتِ وَأَقامُوا الصَّلاةَ أي: أتقنوها وَآتَوُا الزَّكاةَ أي: أدوها على التمام، فلهم أجرهم عند ربهم إذا قدموا عليه، وَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ من آت، وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ على ما فات، إذ لم يفتهم شيء حيث وجدوا الله.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-11","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"ثم أكد فى أمر الربا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-12","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَذَرُوا ما بَقِيَ مِنَ الرِّبا أي: اتركوا بقايا ما شرطتم على الناس من الربا، فلا تقبضوها منهم، إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ (278) . فإن دليل الإيمان: امتثال ما أمرتم به، رُوِيَ أنه كان لثقيف مال على بعض قريش، فطالبوهم عند الحَلِّ بالمال والربا، فنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-13","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"فَإِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوا وتتركوا ما نهيتم عنه، فَأْذَنُوا أي: فاعلموا بِحَرْبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ ومن قرأ:","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-14","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"فآذنوا بالمد، فمعناه: أعلموا بها غيركم، رُوِيَ أنها لمّا نزلت، قالت ثقيف: لا يَدَانِ لنا بحرب الله ورسوله(1).","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-15","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"وَإِنْ تُبْتُمْ من تعاطي الربا واعتقاد حله فَلَكُمْ رُؤُسُ أَمْوالِكُمْ لا تَظْلِمُونَ الغريم بأخذ الزيادة، وَلا تُظْلَمُونَ (279) بنقص رأس مالكم. مفهومه إن لم يتب فليس له شيء، لأنه مرتد. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-16","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"الإشارة: مدار صفاء المعاملة على تصفية اللقمة، فمن صفَّا طعمته صفت معاملته، ومن صفت معاملته أفضى الصفاء إلى قلبه، ومن خلط في لقمته تكدرت معاملته، ومن تكدرت معاملته تكدر قلبه، ولذلك قال بعضهم: (مَنْ أكَلَ الحلال أطاع الله، أحبَّ أم كَرِهَ، ومن أكل الحرام: عصى الله، أحبَّ أم كَرِه) وكذلك الواردات الإلهية، لا ترد إلا على من صفا مطعمه ومشربه، ولذلك قال بعضهم: (من لا يعرف ما يدخل بطنه لا يفرق بين الخواطر الربانية والشيطانية) .","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-17","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"وقال سيدى على الخواص رضي الله عنه: (اعلم أن المدد الذي لم يزل فياضاً على قلب كل إنسان يتلون بحسب القلب، والقلب يتلون بحسبه هو بحسب صلاح الطعمة وفسادها) . هـ. فالذين يأكلون الحرام كالربا وشبهه، لا يقومون إلى معاملتهم للحق إلا كما يقوم المجنون الذي يلعب به الشيطان، ولا يدري ما يقول ولا ما يقال له، فقد حُرم لذيذ المناجاة وحلاوة خلوص المعاملات، فإن احتج لنفسه واستعمل القياس لم يُرْجَ فلاحُه في طريق الخواص، فمن جاءه موعظة من ربه فانتهى، وطلب العفاف فقد عفا الله عما سلف. ومن عاد إلى ما خرج عنه من متابعة هواه، فنار القطيعة مثواه ومأواه.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-18","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"ومن شأن الحق جلّ جلاله مع عباده: أن من طلب الزيادة في حس ظاهره محق الله نور باطنه، ومن حسم مادة زيادة الحس في ظاهره قوي الله مدد الأنوار في باطنه، (يَمْحَقُ الله الربا ويربى الصدقات) ، أي: يُقَوِّي مدد ثواب الصدقات. (وَاللَّهُ لاَ يُحِبُّ كل كفّار أثيم) ، وإنما يحب كل مطيع منيب، وهو من آمن إيمان أهل التحقيق، وسلك مسلك أهل التوفيق. فلا جرم أنه ينخرط في سلك أهل العناية، ويسلك به مسلك أهل الولاية، (الذين لا خوف عليهم ولا هم يحزنون) .","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-19","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"(يا أيها الذين آمنوا اتقوا الله) حق تقاته، واتركوا ما بقي في باطنكم من بقايا الحس وأسبابه، إن كنتم طالبين إيمان أهل الشهود، والوصول إلى الملك المعبود. فإن لم تفعلوا ذلك فاعلموا أنكم في مقام البعد من حيث لا تظنون، معاندون وأنتم لا تشعرون. وإن رجعتم إلى ربكم فلكم رؤوس أموالكم، وهو نور التوحيد، لا تنقصون منه ولا تزيدون عليه، إلا إن أفردتم الوجهة إليه، وطلبتم الوصول منه إليه، فإن الله لا يُخيٍّب من أمَّل جُوده، ولا يردُّ من وقَف ببابه، بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-275-279-20","r":"q2-275-279","title":"2:275–279 · Usury, the lawful exchange and the purity of one’s sustenance","text":"ثم ذكر حال المعسر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-275-279-20"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-275-279-s1","r":"q2-275-279","title":"The root of ribā and its two kinds","text":"I say: ribā ( الربا ) originally means increase: property rabā yarbū when it increases. It is written with wāw in consideration of its original form as a verbal noun. Al-Farrāʾ said: they wrote it with wāw because the people of the Ḥijāz learned writing from the people of al-Ḥīra, whose usage was ribū . They taught them the letter-forms. Abū al-Sammāl al-ʿAdawī recited it thus. The two brothers recited it with vowel inclination ( الإمالة ), because of the kasra ; the others without inclination ( التفخيم ). [B233] In the technical usage of the Sacred Law, usury has two kinds: surplus usury ( ربا الفضل ) and deferred usury ( ربا النَّساء ). The first is an unequal exchange of foods or currencies within one genus; when the genera differ, there is no objection to inequality. The second is the exchange of foods or currencies with delayed delivery; this is forbidden even when the genera differ. [B233]","anchor":"en-q2-275-279-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-275-279-s2","r":"q2-275-279","title":"The inverted comparison","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: those who consume usury—that is, take it; consumption is specified because it is the greatest use of wealth—will rise from their graves at the Resurrection only as one bereft of reason whom Satan throws into confusion through his touch, rising and falling. It is related that their bellies will be before them like enormous houses, so that each time they rise their bellies incline and throw them down. Abū Hurayra related that the Messenger of God said: “When I was taken by night to heaven, I saw men with bellies like houses, containing snakes visible from outside. I asked, ‘Who are these, Gabriel?’ He replied, ‘Those who consume usury.’” [B233] This punishment is because they declared usury lawful and said: “Trade is only like usury,” placing both in one category. The comparison is inverted ( عكس التشبيه ). The expected form would be “Usury is like trade”; for emphasis, they make usury the original case and compare trade with it. In the age of ignorance, when a debt fell due, the debtor would say: “Extend my term, and I shall increase the sum.” They would do so, saying: “An increase as profit at the beginning of the sale and an increase when the debt falls due are the same; both rest upon mutual consent.” The Real Most High declares this false: “God has permitted trade and forbidden usury.” Analogy in the face of an explicit text is invalid, and the distinction is manifest. Someone who sells a dirham for two dirhams makes the other lose a dirham without benefit. Someone who buys merchandise for a dirham and sells it for two is different: pressing need, desire for the goods and the prospect of their marketability may compensate for the price disadvantage.","anchor":"en-q2-275-279-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-275-279-s3","r":"q2-275-279","title":"Desisting, persistence and the growth of charity","text":"Whoever receives an admonition from his Lord, such as the prohibition of usury, and desists, retains what preceded the prohibition and need not return it. His affair belongs to God, not any of you; he is not to be interfered with. Whoever returns to declaring usury lawful after the prohibition has reached him is among the people of the Fire, abiding therein, because he has disbelieved and treated God’s command as foolish. [B234] God diminishes usury: removes its blessing and destroys the wealth into which it enters. He causes charities to grow: multiplies their reward and blesses the wealth from which they were taken. It is reported that the Prophet said: “Wealth is not diminished by charity,” and that God nurtures charity until it becomes like a mountain. Yaḥyā ibn Muʿādh said: “I know no grain weighing as much as the mountains of the world except a grain given in charity.” [B234] God does not love any persistent rejecter—one who persists in declaring forbidden things lawful—or sinner, immersed in prohibited acts. He does not approve his condition or love him as He loves those who repent. He then describes their opposite: those who believe in God and affirm what comes from Him, do righteous deeds, perfect prayer and pay the alms completely have their reward with their Lord when they come to Him. They fear nothing to come and grieve over nothing past; they have missed nothing, having found God. He then reinforces the prohibition of usury: Qurʾānic continuation · 2:278–279 يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَذَرُوا ما بَقِيَ مِنَ الرِّبا إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ فَإِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوا فَأْذَنُوا بِحَرْبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَإِنْ تُبْتُمْ فَلَكُمْ رُؤُسُ أَمْوالِكُمْ لا تَظْلِمُونَ وَلا تُظْلَمُونَ You who believe, be mindful of God and abandon what remains of usury, if you are believers. If you do not, then be warned of war from God and His Messenger. If you repent, your principal is yours: you shall neither wrong nor be wronged.","anchor":"en-q2-275-279-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-275-279-s4","r":"q2-275-279","title":"Abandon the outstanding increment","text":"You who believe, be mindful of God and leave the outstanding usury you stipulated against people; do not collect it, if you are believers. The evidence of faith is compliance with what you are commanded. It is related that Thaqīf had money owed to them by some of Quraysh. When it fell due, they demanded the principal and usury, and the verse was revealed. If you do not abandon what you have been forbidden, know of war from God and His Messenger. The reading fa-ādhinū ( فآذنوا ), with lengthening, means inform others of it. When the verse was revealed, Thaqīf are reported to have said: “We have no power to wage war against God and His Messenger.” If you repent of taking usury and believing it lawful, your principal is yours. You do not wrong the debtor by taking an increment, and you are not wronged by a reduction in your principal. The implication is that one who does not repent has no entitlement, because he is an apostate. And God Most High knows best. [B234]","anchor":"en-q2-275-279-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-275-279-s5","r":"q2-275-279","title":"Purity of sustenance and purity of inward reception","text":"Pure dealings with God turn upon purifying one’s morsel. Whoever makes his food pure has pure dealings; their purity reaches his heart. Whoever mixes impurity into his morsel clouds his dealings, and that clouds his heart. Hence the saying: “Whoever eats lawful food obeys God, willingly or unwillingly; whoever eats unlawful food disobeys God, willingly or unwillingly.” Likewise, divine incoming inspirations ( الواردات الإلهية ) arrive only upon someone whose food and drink are pure. One of them said: “Someone who does not know what enters his belly cannot distinguish lordly impulses from satanic ones.” Sīdī ʿAlī al-Khawwāṣ said: “Know that spiritual support continually overflows upon every human heart and takes its colour according to the heart. The heart takes its colour accordingly, in keeping with the goodness or corruption of its sustenance.” [B235] Those who eat unlawful things, such as usury and its like, rise to their dealings with the Real only as a person bereft of reason with whom Satan plays, not knowing what he says or what is said to him. He is deprived of the delight of intimate converse and the sweetness of pure dealings. If he argues in his own defence and resorts to analogy, no success is to be hoped for him on the path of the elect. Whoever receives an admonition from his Lord, desists and seeks purity has his past pardoned. Whoever returns to following the desire he had abandoned has the fire of severance as his dwelling and refuge. The Real’s way with His servants is that when someone seeks an increase in the sensory dimension of his outward being, God diminishes the light of his inward being. When someone cuts off the supply feeding this outward sensory increase, God strengthens the inflow of lights within him. “God diminishes usury and causes charities to grow”: He strengthens the support conveyed by charity’s reward. God does not love any persistent rejecter and sinner, but every obedient one who returns to Him: someone who believes with the faith of realized people and follows those granted success. Such a person is necessarily threaded into the company of divine care and taken upon the path of protecting friendship ( الولاية ): those upon whom there is no fear and who do not grieve. You who believe, be mindful of God as He should be, and leave whatever traces of sensory attachment and its causes remain within you, if you seek the faith of direct witnessing and arrival at the worshipped King. If you do not, know that you remain distant without realising it, opposing without being aware. If you return to your Lord, your principal is yours: the light of unity. You neither diminish it nor add to it—unless you direct yourselves wholly towards Him and seek arrival through Him at Him. God does not disappoint one who hopes for His generosity or turn away one who stands at His door, through His grace and bounty.","anchor":"en-q2-275-279-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-275-279-s6","r":"q2-275-279","title":"","text":"He then mentions the debtor in hardship.","anchor":"en-q2-275-279-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-280-281","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return 2:280–281","anchor":"unit-q2-280-281"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-1","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"وَإِنْ كانَ ذُو عُسْرَةٍ فَنَظِرَةٌ إِلى مَيْسَرَةٍ وَأَنْ تَصَدَّقُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (280) وَاتَّقُوا يَوْماً تُرْجَعُونَ فِيهِ إِلَى اللَّهِ ثُمَّ تُوَفَّى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لا يُظْلَمُونَ (281)","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-2","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"قلت: (كان) : تامة بمعنى حضر، وقرأ أُبَيّ وابنُ مسعود: (ذا عسرة) فتكون ناقصة، و (نظرة) : مبتدأ، والخبر محذوف، أي: فعليكم نظرة، أو فالواجب نظرة. وهو مصدر بمعنى الإنظار، وهو الإمهال، و (ميسرة) : فيه لغتان:","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-3","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"الفتح والضم، وهي مَفْعَلة من اليسر، فالضم لغة أهل الحجاز، والفتح لغة تميم وقَيْس ونَجْد.","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-4","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وإن حضر الغريم وهو معسر، فعليكم إنظاره، أي: إمهاله إلى زمان يسره ولا يحل لكم أن تُضَيِّقُوا عليه، وتطالبوه بما ليس عنده إن أقام البيِّنَةَ على عسره وَأَنْ تَصَدَّقُوا عليه برؤوس أموالكم ولا تطالبوه بها خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ ما في ذلك من الخير الجزيل والذكر الجميل.","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-5","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"روى أبو هريرة رضي الله عنه أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: «مَنْ أَنْظَر مُعْسِراً، أو وَضَعَ عنه، أَظلَّه اللهُ في ظِلِّ عَرْشِه يوم لا ظِلَّ إِلا ظلّه» وقال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «من أَحَبَّ أن تُستجاب دعوته، وتُكشف كُربتُه، فليُيسِّرْ على المعسر» .","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-6","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم: «من أنْظَر معسراً كان له بكل يوم صدقةٌ بمثل ما أنظره به» . وقد ورد في فضل الدّين قوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إن الله مع المدين حتى يقضي دَيْنه، ما لم يكن فيما يكره الله» . فكان عبد الله(1) يقول: «إني أكره أن أبيت ليلة إلا والله تعالى معي، فيأمر غلامه أن يأخذ بدين» .","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-7","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"وقد ورد الترغيب أيضاً في الإسراع بقضاء الدين دون مطل، قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم «مَنْ مشَى إلى غَريمه بحقه، صلّت عليه دوابُّ الأرض ونُونُ الماء، وكتبت له بكل خُطوة شجرة في الجنة، وذنب يغفر له فإن لم يفعل ومطل فهو مُعْتَدِ» . وقال أيضا: «مطل الغَنِيِّ ظلم، وإذا أُتْبعَ أحدكم على مليىء فَلْيتْبَعْ» .","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-8","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"ثم قال تعالى: وَاتَّقُوا يَوْماً تُرْجَعُونَ فِيهِ إِلَى اللَّهِ، وهو يوم القيامة، فتأهبوا للمصير إليه بالصدقة وسائر الأعمال الصالحة، ثُمَّ تُوَفَّى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ جزاء ما أسلفت، وَهُمْ لا يُظْلَمُونَ بنقص ثواب أو تضعيف عقاب. قال ابن عباس: (هذه آخر آية نزل بها جبريل، فقال: ضعها في رأس المائتين والثمانين من البقرة، وعاش بعدها رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أحداً وعشرين يوماً) . وقيل: أحداً وثمانين، وقيل غير ذلك. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-9","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"الإشارة: وإن كان ذو عسرة من نور اليقين والمعرفة، فلينظر إلى أهل الغنى بالله، وليصحبهم ويتعلَّق بهم، وهم العارفون، فإنهم يغنونه بالنظر. وفي بعض الأخبار: إن لله رجالاً من نظر إليهم سعد سعادة لا يشقى بعدها أبداً. هـ. ولله رجال إذا نظروا أغنَوْا، وفي هذا المعنى يقول صاحب العينية:","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-10","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"فَشَمِّرْ، ولُذْ بالأَوْليَاءِ فَإنَّهُمْ ... لَهُمْ مِنْ كِتَابِ الله تلْكَ الوقَائعُ","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-11","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"هُمُ الذُّخْرُ لِلمَلهُوفِ، والكَنْزُ لِلرَّجَا ... وَمِنْهُمْ يَنَالُ الصَبُّ مَا هُوَ طامع","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-12","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"وقال الشيخ أبو العباس رضي الله عنه: والله ما بيني وبين الرجل إلاَّ أن أنظر إليه وقد أغنيته. وقال فيه شيخه: نعم الرجل أبو العباس، يأتيه البدويُّ يبول على ساقه، فلا يُمسي إلا وقد أوصله إلى ربه. وقال شيخ شيوخنا سيدي العربي بن عبد الله: لو أتاني يهودي أو نصراني، لَمْ يُمْسِ إلا وقد أوصلته إلى الله. هـ. وفي كل زمان رجال يُغْنُونَ بالنظر، وقد أدركتهم، وصحبتُهم والحمد لله. والإشارة بقوله: وَأَنْ تَصَدَّقُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إلى أهل الغنى بالله، يتصدقون على الفقراء بالنظرة والهمة، حتى يحصل لهم الغنى بالله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-280-281-13","r":"q2-280-281","title":"2:280–281 · Respite for the debtor and the final return","text":"ثم أمر الحق تعالى بتحصين الأموال بتقييد الديون والإشهاد عليها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-280-281-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-280-281-s1","r":"q2-280-281","title":"The complete and incomplete verb kāna","text":"I say: kāna ( كان ) is complete ( تامة ), meaning “be present.” Ubayy and Ibn Masʿūd read “one in hardship” in the accusative ( ذا عسرة ), making kāna incomplete ( ناقصة ). “A respite” is a subject whose predicate is omitted: “A respite is incumbent upon you,” or “What is obligatory is a respite.” It is a verbal noun meaning granting delay. Maysara ( ميسرة ) has two forms, with fatḥa or ḍamma on the sīn . It is formed from ease: ḍamma is the usage of the Ḥijāz, and fatḥa that of Tamīm, Qays and Najd.","anchor":"en-q2-280-281-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-280-281-s2","r":"q2-280-281","title":"Give time, or forgive the principal","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: if the debtor appears in hardship, you must grant him time until he has means. It is not lawful to constrain him or demand what he does not possess if he establishes his hardship by evidence. Giving him your principal as charity, without demanding it, is better for you, if you know the abundant good and beautiful remembrance that this brings. Abū Hurayra related that the Prophet said: “Whoever grants respite to someone in hardship or remits his debt, God shades him beneath His Throne on the day when there is no shade except His shade.” He is also quoted as saying: “Whoever wishes his prayer answered and distress relieved should make things easy for someone in hardship”; and, “Whoever grants respite to a debtor in hardship has, for every day, a charity equal to the sum he deferred.” [B236] Concerning debt, it is transmitted that the Prophet said: “God is with the debtor until he discharges his debt, provided it is not for something God dislikes.” ʿAbd Allāh would say: “I dislike passing a night without God Most High being with me,” and would instruct his servant to purchase on credit. [B236] Prompt repayment without delay is also encouraged. The Prophet is quoted as saying: “Whoever walks to his creditor with what is due has the animals of the earth and fish of the water pray for him. For every step, a tree in the Garden is recorded for him and a sin forgiven. If he does not do so but delays, he is a transgressor.” He also said: “Delay by someone with means is wrongdoing. If one of you is referred to a solvent debtor, let him accept the transfer.” [B236]","anchor":"en-q2-280-281-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-280-281-s3","r":"q2-280-281","title":"The final accounting","text":"“Be mindful of a day when you will be returned to God”: the Day of Resurrection. Prepare for your return through charity and all other good deeds. Every soul will then receive the full recompense of what it sent ahead, without diminished reward or increased punishment. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “This was the last verse Gabriel brought down. He said, ‘Place it after the first two hundred and eighty verses of al-Baqara.’ The Messenger of God lived twenty-one days after it.” Other accounts give eighty-one days or other intervals. And God Most High knows best. [XVI-N003] [B237]","anchor":"en-q2-280-281-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-280-281-s4","r":"q2-280-281","title":"The poverty that is relieved by a glance","text":"If someone is poor in the light of certainty and gnosis, let him look towards those rich through God, accompany them and attach himself to them: the gnostics, who enrich through a glance. A transmitted saying declares that God has men whom someone need only see to receive a happiness never followed by wretchedness. God has men who enrich by looking. The author of the poem rhyming in ʿayn says: Make ready and seek refuge with the saints: theirs are those encounters from God’s Book. They are provision for the distressed, a treasure for hope; from them the ardent lover gains what he desires. Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās said: “By God, between me and a man there is only my looking at him, and I have enriched him.” His shaykh said of him: “What an excellent man is Abū al-ʿAbbās! A rustic who urinates upon his own leg comes to him, and before evening he has brought him to his Lord.” Our teachers’ teacher, Sīdī al-ʿArabī ibn ʿAbd Allāh, said: “Were a Jew or Christian to come to me, evening would not fall before I had brought him to God.” In every age there are men who enrich through a glance. I have encountered and accompanied them, and praise belongs to God. [B238] “To remit as charity is better for you” addresses those rich through God: let them give to the poor through their glance and aspiration until the latter attain richness through God. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-280-281-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-280-281-s5","r":"q2-280-281","title":"","text":"The Real then commands the safeguarding of wealth by recording debts and having them witnessed.","anchor":"en-q2-280-281-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-282","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge 2:282","anchor":"unit-q2-282"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-1","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذا تَدايَنْتُمْ بِدَيْنٍ إِلى أَجَلٍ مُسَمًّى فَاكْتُبُوهُ وَلْيَكْتُبْ بَيْنَكُمْ كاتِبٌ بِالْعَدْلِ وَلا يَأْبَ كاتِبٌ أَنْ يَكْتُبَ كَما عَلَّمَهُ اللَّهُ فَلْيَكْتُبْ وَلْيُمْلِلِ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ وَلْيَتَّقِ اللَّهَ رَبَّهُ وَلا يَبْخَسْ مِنْهُ شَيْئاً فَإِنْ كانَ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ سَفِيهاً أَوْ ضَعِيفاً أَوْ لا يَسْتَطِيعُ أَنْ يُمِلَّ هُوَ فَلْيُمْلِلْ وَلِيُّهُ بِالْعَدْلِ وَاسْتَشْهِدُوا شَهِيدَيْنِ مِنْ رِجالِكُمْ فَإِنْ لَمْ يَكُونا رَجُلَيْنِ فَرَجُلٌ وَامْرَأَتانِ مِمَّنْ تَرْضَوْنَ مِنَ الشُّهَداءِ أَنْ تَضِلَّ إِحْداهُما فَتُذَكِّرَ إِحْداهُمَا الْأُخْرى ...","anchor":"ar-q2-282-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-2","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذا تَدايَنْتُمْ بِدَيْنٍ أي: داين بعضكم بعضاً فى بيع أو سلف، إِلى أَجَلٍ مُسَمًّى أي: معلوم بالأيام أو الأشهر، لا بالحصاد أو قدوم الحاج، إلا في السَّلمَ، فَاكْتُبُوهُ لأنه أوثق وأدفع للنزاع. والجمهور: أن الأمر للاستحباب، وَلْيَكْتُبْ بَيْنَكُمْ كاتِبٌ بِالْعَدْلِ لا يزيد ولا ينقص، ولا بد أن يكون عدلا حتى يجيىء مكتوبه موثوقاً به، وَلا يَأْبَ كاتِبٌ أَنْ يَكْتُبَ أي: ولا يمتنع كاتب من الكتابة كَما عَلَّمَهُ اللَّهُ فَلْيَكْتُبْ أي: فليكتب كما علمه الله من كتابة الوثائق، أو: لا يأب أن ينفع الناس بكتابته كما نفعه الله بتعليمها. وَلْيُمْلِلِ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ أي: وليكن المُملي مَنْ عليه الحق لأنه المُقر للشهود، يقال: أملل وأملى، إذا ذكر ما عنده أو ما عليه، وَلْيَتَّقِ اللَّهَ رَبَّهُ أي: المملي أو الكاتب، وَلا يَبْخَسْ مِنْهُ شَيْئاً أي: ولا ينقص من الحق الذي عليه شيئاً في الإملاء أو في الكتابة.","anchor":"ar-q2-282-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-3","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"فَإِنْ كانَ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ سَفِيهاً: ناقص العقل مُبذراً، أَوْ ضَعِيفاً شيخاً مخبلاً، أو صبيّاً صغيراً، أَوْ لا يَسْتَطِيعُ أَنْ يُمِلَّ هُوَ، لخرس أو جهل باللغة، فَلْيُمْلِلْ عنه وَلِيُّهُ بِالْعَدْلِ، من وَصِيٍّ أو وكيل، وَاسْتَشْهِدُوا على معاملتكم شَهِيدَيْنِ مِنْ رِجالِكُمْ المسلمين، فَإِنْ لَمْ يَكُونا رَجُلَيْنِ، بأن تعذر إحضارهما، فَرَجُلٌ وَامْرَأَتانِ فأكثر، تقوم مقام رجلين مِمَّنْ تَرْضَوْنَ مِنَ الشُّهَداءِ لعلمكم بعدالتهم، وإنما شرط تعدد النساء لأجل أَنْ تَضِلَّ إِحْداهُما فَتُذَكِّرَ إِحْداهُمَا الْأُخْرى أي: إن ضلت إحداهما الشهادة، ونسيتها، ذكرتها الأخرى لأنها ناقصة عقل ودين.","anchor":"ar-q2-282-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-4","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"ثم حذَّر الشهود من الامتناع عن تحمل الشهادة أو أدائها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-282-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-5","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"... وَلا يَأْبَ الشُّهَداءُ إِذا ما دُعُوا وَلا تَسْئَمُوا أَنْ تَكْتُبُوهُ صَغِيراً أَوْ كَبِيراً إِلى أَجَلِهِ ذلِكُمْ أَقْسَطُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ وَأَقْوَمُ لِلشَّهادَةِ وَأَدْنى أَلاَّ تَرْتابُوا إِلاَّ أَنْ تَكُونَ تِجارَةً حاضِرَةً تُدِيرُونَها بَيْنَكُمْ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُناحٌ أَلاَّ تَكْتُبُوها وَأَشْهِدُوا إِذا تَبايَعْتُمْ وَلا يُضَارَّ كاتِبٌ وَلا شَهِيدٌ وَإِنْ تَفْعَلُوا فَإِنَّهُ فُسُوقٌ بِكُمْ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ اللَّهُ وَاللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (282)","anchor":"ar-q2-282-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-6","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"قلت: السَّأَمُ هو: الملَلُ، و (لا يضار) يحتمل أن يكون مبنيّاً للفاعل، وأصله: يضارر بالكسر، أو للمفعول، فيكون الأصح بالفتح.","anchor":"ar-q2-282-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-7","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولا يمتنع الشُّهَداءِ من تحمل الشهادة إذا دعوا إليها، حيث تعيَّنت عليهم، وسُموا شهداء باعتبار المآل، وإنما تتعين إذا لم يوجد غيرهم. أو: من أدائها حيث لا ضرر، وَلا تَسْئَمُوا أَنْ تَكْتُبُوهُ أي: ولا تملوا من كتابة الحق إذا تكرر صَغِيراً كان أَوْ كَبِيراً، فقيدوا ذلك إِلى أَجَلِهِ، ذلِكُمْ أَقْسَطُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ أي: ذلك الكتاب والتقييد للحقوق، أكثر قسطاً عند الله لأنه أدفع للنزاع وأحفظ للحقوق، وَأَقْوَمُ لِلشَّهادَةِ أي: أثبتُ لها وأعون على أدائها، وَأَدْنى أَلَّا تَرْتابُوا أي: وأقرب لعدم الريب والشك في جنس الدين وقَدْره وأجلَه، لأنه إذا كتب جنسه وقدره وأجله لم يبق لأحد شك في ذلك، إِلَّا أَنْ تَكُونَ تِجارَةً حاضِرَةً لا أجَل فيها، تُدِيرُونَها بَيْنَكُمْ أي: تتعاملون فيها نقداً، فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُناحٌ أَلَّا تَكْتُبُوها لقلة النزاع فيها، وَأَشْهِدُوا إِذا تَبايَعْتُمْ مطلقاً بدين أو نقد لأنه أحوط، خوفاً من الإنكار، والأوامر في هذه الآية للاستحباب عند الأكثر.","anchor":"ar-q2-282-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-8","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"وَلا يُضَارَّ كاتِبٌ وَلا شَهِيدٌ بالتحريف والتغيير في الكتابة والشهادة، على البناء للفاعل، أو: ولا يضارا بأن يُعْجلا عن مهم، أو يكلفا الأداء من شقة بعيدة، أو يمنع من أجرته، وَإِنْ تَفْعَلُوا ذلك الضرار وما نهيتهم عنه فَإِنَّهُ فُسُوقٌ بِكُمْ أي: خروج بكم عن حد الاستقامة، وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ في مخالفة أمره ونهيه، وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ اللَّهُ العلوم اللدنية وَاللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ فلا يخفى عليه من اتقى الله ممن عصاه. وكرر لفظ الجلالة في الجمل الثلاث، لاستقلالها، فإن الأُولى حثٌّ على التقوى والثانية وعدٌ بتعليم العلم، والثالثة تعظيم لشأنه، ولأنه أدخل في التعظيم من الكناية. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-282-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-9","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"وأدخل الواو فى جواب الأمر ليقتضي أن تعليمه سبحانه لأهل التقوى ليس هو مسبباً عن التقوى، بل هو بمحض الفضل والكرم، والتقوى إنما هي طريق موصل لذلك الكرم، لا سبب فيه «جَلَّ حكم الأزل أن يضاف إلى العلل» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-282-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-282-10","r":"q2-282","title":"2:282 · Recording debts, truthful testimony and the gift of knowledge","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى حكم الرهان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-282-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-282-s1","r":"q2-282","title":"The term, the record and the debtor’s dictation","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: you who believe, when you contract a debt with one another through sale or loan, for a term specified by days or months—not by harvest or the pilgrims’ return, except in a forward purchase ( السَّلَم )—write it down. This is more secure and more effective in preventing dispute. The majority understand the command as recommendation. [B239] Let a scribe write between you justly, adding and omitting nothing. He must be upright ( عدل ), so that his document is trustworthy. No scribe should refuse to write as God has taught him. Let him write in accordance with what God has taught him about recording contracts; or let him not refuse to benefit people through writing as God benefited him by teaching it. Let the debtor dictate, since he is the one acknowledging the obligation before the witnesses. Amlala and amlā ( أملل، أملى ) both mean setting out what one holds or owes. Let him—the dictator or scribe—be mindful of God, his Lord, and diminish nothing of the debt in dictation or writing. If the debtor lacks sound judgment and is wasteful, or is weak—an elderly man whose mind has become impaired, or a young child—or cannot dictate because he cannot speak or does not know the language, let his guardian, testamentary guardian or agent dictate justly on his behalf. Call two Muslim men to witness the transaction. If two men cannot be brought, one man and two women or more take their place, from witnesses whose uprightness you approve. The plurality of women is stipulated so that if one loses track of the testimony and forgets, the other reminds her, since she is described here as deficient in intellect and religion. [B239] He then warns witnesses against refusing to undertake or give testimony. Qurʾānic continuation · 2:282b وَلا يَأْبَ الشُّهَداءُ إِذا ما دُعُوا وَلا تَسْئَمُوا أَنْ تَكْتُبُوهُ صَغِيراً أَوْ كَبِيراً إِلى أَجَلِهِ ذلِكُمْ أَقْسَطُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ وَأَقْوَمُ لِلشَّهادَةِ وَأَدْنى أَلَّا تَرْتابُوا إِلَّا أَنْ تَكُونَ تِجارَةً حاضِرَةً تُدِيرُونَها بَيْنَكُمْ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُناحٌ أَلَّا تَكْتُبُوها وَأَشْهِدُوا إِذا تَبايَعْتُمْ وَلا يُضَارَّ كاتِبٌ وَلا شَهِيدٌ وَإِنْ تَفْعَلُوا فَإِنَّهُ فُسُوقٌ بِكُمْ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ اللَّهُ وَاللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ Witnesses should not refuse when called. Do not tire of writing the debt down, small or great, with its term. That is more equitable before God, firmer for testimony and nearer to preventing doubt—unless it is immediate trade you conduct among yourselves; then there is no blame upon you for not writing it down. Take witnesses when you trade. No scribe or witness shall be harmed. If you do that, it is disobedience on your part. Be mindful of God; God teaches you; and God knows all things.","anchor":"en-q2-282-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-282-s2","r":"q2-282","title":"Weariness and the active or passive verb","text":"I say: saʾam ( السأم ) means weariness. “Shall not harm or be harmed” ( لا يضار ) may be active, originally yuḍārir with kasra , or passive, with fatḥa in the original unassimilated form. [B240]","anchor":"en-q2-282-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-282-s3","r":"q2-282","title":"Witnesses, immediate trade and the prevention of injury","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: witnesses must not refuse to undertake testimony when called, where the duty falls specifically upon them. They are called witnesses in view of what they will become. The duty becomes individual only if no others are available. Or the prohibition concerns refusing to deliver testimony where no harm is involved. Do not tire of writing down an obligation when it recurs, whether small or great. Record it with its term. Such recording is more equitable before God, since it better prevents dispute and safeguards rights; firmer for testimony, making it more established and easier to deliver; and nearer to preventing doubt about the debt’s kind, amount and term. Once these are written, no one remains uncertain about them. An exception is immediate trade, with no deferred term, conducted for ready payment among yourselves. There is no blame for not writing it because dispute is less likely. Take witnesses whenever you trade, whether on credit or for cash, as a precaution against denial. The majority regard the commands in this verse as recommendations. On the active construction, neither scribe nor witness should harm another by distorting or altering the document or testimony. On the passive construction, neither should be harmed by being hurried away from an important affair, required to give testimony from a far-off place or denied his fee. If you commit such injury and what you have been forbidden, it is departure from uprightness on your part. Be mindful of God by avoiding opposition to His commands and prohibitions. God teaches you the divinely bestowed sciences. God knows all things: the reverent and the disobedient alike are not hidden from Him.","anchor":"en-q2-282-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-282-s4","r":"q2-282","title":"Teaching is a gift, not an effect produced by reverence","text":"The divine Name is repeated in the three clauses because each is independent: the first urges reverence; the second promises teaching; the third magnifies His standing. Explicit naming also conveys greater magnification than a pronoun. Al-Bayḍāwī says this. The wāw is introduced in the response to the command to show that God’s teaching of the reverent is not an effect caused by their reverence, but pure bounty and generosity. Reverence is a path leading to that generosity, not a cause producing it. “The judgment of eternity is too exalted to be attributed to causes.” And God Most High knows best. [B240]","anchor":"en-q2-282-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-282-s5","r":"q2-282","title":"","text":"The Real then mentions the ruling on pledges.","anchor":"en-q2-282-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-283","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart 2:283","anchor":"unit-q2-283"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-1","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ عَلى سَفَرٍ وَلَمْ تَجِدُوا كاتِباً فَرِهانٌ مَقْبُوضَةٌ فَإِنْ أَمِنَ بَعْضُكُمْ بَعْضاً فَلْيُؤَدِّ الَّذِي اؤْتُمِنَ أَمانَتَهُ وَلْيَتَّقِ اللَّهَ رَبَّهُ وَلا تَكْتُمُوا الشَّهادَةَ وَمَنْ يَكْتُمْها فَإِنَّهُ آثِمٌ قَلْبُهُ وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ عَلِيمٌ (283)","anchor":"ar-q2-283-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-2","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"قلت: (فرهان) : خبر، أو مبتدأ، أي: فالمستوثق به رهان، أو فعليه رهان.","anchor":"ar-q2-283-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-3","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ عَلى جناح سَفَرٍ أي: مسافرين، وَلَمْ تَجِدُوا كاتِباً يكتب شهادة البيع أو الدين، فالمستوثق به عوضا من الإشهاد: فَرِهانٌ مَقْبُوضَةٌ. وليس السفر شرطاً فى صحة الارتهان، لأنه عليه الصلاة والسلام «رَهَنَ دِرْعَه عند يهودي بالمدينة في شَعِير» لكنّ لمّا كان السفر مَظنَّة إعواز الكتاب، ذكره الحق تعالى حكماً للغالب. والجمهور على اعتبار القبض فيه، فإن لم يقبض حتى حصل المانع، فلا يختص به في دينه، فَإِنْ أَمِنَ بَعْضُكُمْ بَعْضاً واستغنى بأمانته عن الارتهان، لوثوقه بأمانته فداينه بلا رهن، فَلْيُؤَدِّ الَّذِي اؤْتُمِنَ أَمانَتَهُ أي: دينه، وسماه أمانة لائتمانه عليه بلا ارتهان ولا إشهاد، وَلْيَتَّقِ اللَّهَ رَبَّهُ في أداء دينه وعدم إنكاره.","anchor":"ar-q2-283-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-4","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"وَلا تَكْتُمُوا الشَّهادَةَ أيها الشهود، أو أهل الدين، أي: شهادتهم على أنفسهم، وَمَنْ يَكْتُمْها منكم بأن يمتنع من أداء ما تحمل من الشهادة، أو من أداء ما عليه من الدين، فَإِنَّهُ آثِمٌ قَلْبُهُ حيث كتم ما علمه به، لأن الكتمان من عمل القلوب فتعلق الإثم به، ونظيره: «العين زانية وزناها النظر» ، أو أسنده إلى القلب، مبالغة لأنه رئيس الأعضاء، فإذا أثم قلبه فقد أثم كله، وكأنه قد تمكن الإثم منه فأخذ أشرف أجزائه، وفاق سائر ذنوبه، ثم هدد","anchor":"ar-q2-283-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-5","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"الكاتمين فقال: وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ عَلِيمٌ لا يخفى عليه ما تبدون وما تكتمون، روى عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «من كَتَمَ شهادةً إذا دُعِي- كَان كَمَنْ شَهِدَ بالزُّور» .","anchor":"ar-q2-283-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-6","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"الإشارة: كما أمر الله تعالى بتقييد الديون الدنيوية، والاعتناء بشأنها، أمر بتقييد العلوم اللدنية والواردات القدسية والاغتباط بأمرها، بل هي أولى لدوام ثمراتها وخلود نتائجها، فإن الحكمة ترد على القلب من عالم القدس عظيمة كالجبل، فإن أهملتها ولم تبادر إلى تقييدها، رجعت كالجمل، فإن أخرتها رجعت كالطير، ثم كالبيضة، ثم تمتحي من القلب، وفي هذا المعنى قيل:","anchor":"ar-q2-283-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-7","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"العلمُ صيدٌ والكتابةُ قَيْدُه ... قَيِّدْ صُيودَك بالحِبَالِ المُوثِقَهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-283-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-8","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"وَمِنَ الجَهَالة أن تصِيدَ حمامةً ... وتتركُها بَيْنَ الأوانِس مطلقهْ","anchor":"ar-q2-283-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-9","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"فإن لم يحسن الكتابة، فليملله على من يُحسنها، ولا يبخس منه شيئاً، بل يمُليه على ما ورد في قلبه، فإن كان ضعيف العبارة، فليملل عنه من يحسنها بالعدل، من غير زيادة ولا نقصان في المعنى، وليُشهد عليها رجال أهل الفن وهم العارفون، فإن لم يكونوا، فمن حضر من الفقراء المتمكنين لئلا يكون في تلك الحكمة شيء من الخلل لنقصان صاحبها، أو: وليُشْهِد على ذلك الوارد عدلين، وهما الكتاب والسنّة، فإن كان موافقاً لهما، قُبل، وإلا ردّ.","anchor":"ar-q2-283-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-10","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"قال الجنيد رضي الله عنه: إن النكتةَ لتقع في قلبي فلا أقبلها إلا بشهادة عَدْلَين: الكتاب والسنّة. هـ. وإن كنتم مستعجلين، ولم تجدوا كاتباً، فارتهنوها في قلوب بعضكم بعضاً، حتى تُقيد. ومن كتم الواردات عن شيخه أو إخوانه، فقد أثم قلبه لأنه نوع من الخيانة في طريق التربية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-283-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-283-11","r":"q2-283","title":"2:283 · Pledges, trust and recording the gifts of the heart","text":"ثم هدّد الحق تعالى عباده، على مخالفة ما أمرهم به، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-283-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-283-s1","r":"q2-283","title":"The implied predicate or subject","text":"I say: “A pledge” ( رهان ) may be predicate or subject: “The security is a pledge,” or “A pledge is incumbent upon him.”","anchor":"en-q2-283-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-283-s2","r":"q2-283","title":"Possession of security and honouring trust","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: if you are travelling and find no scribe to record testimony to a sale or debt, the security replacing formal witnessing is a pledge taken into possession. Travel is not a condition of a valid pledge: the Prophet “pledged his coat of mail with a Jew in Medina for barley.” Travel is mentioned as the usual circumstance in which scribes are unavailable. [B241] The majority require taking possession. If this has not occurred before an impediment arises, the creditor has no exclusive claim to the pledged asset against his debt. If one of you trusts another and dispenses with a pledge because he trusts his honesty, lending without security, let the one entrusted discharge his trust—that is, his debt. It is called a trust because he was trusted without pledge or witnesses. Let him be mindful of God, his Lord, by repaying and not denying the debt. Do not conceal testimony, witnesses—or debtors, concerning their acknowledgment against themselves. Whoever refuses to give the testimony he undertook, or to pay the debt he owes, has a sinful heart, concealing what it knows. Concealment is an act of hearts, so the sin is attached to the heart. A parallel is: “The eye commits fornication, and its fornication is looking.” Alternatively, the sin is ascribed to the heart for emphasis, since it is chief among the limbs. If the heart sins, the whole person sins: the sin has taken firm hold of his noblest part and surpassed his other sins. He then threatens those who conceal: “God knows what you do.” Neither what you reveal nor what you hide is concealed from Him. It is related that the Prophet said: “Whoever conceals testimony when called is like someone who gives false testimony.” [B241]","anchor":"en-q2-283-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-283-s3","r":"q2-283","title":"Record inspiration, then submit it to its witnesses","text":"As God commands the recording of worldly debts and care for them, He commands the recording of divinely bestowed sciences and sacred incoming inspirations, and rejoicing in them. These deserve it even more, for their fruits endure and their results abide. A wisdom may come to the heart from the world of holiness, immense as a mountain. If you neglect it and do not promptly record it, it shrinks to the size of a camel. Delay further and it becomes like a bird, then an egg, then is erased from the heart. In this sense it is said: Knowledge is game, and writing its tether; bind your catches with strong cords. It is ignorance to catch a dove and leave it loose among its companions. [B242] Someone unable to write should dictate it to someone who can, diminishing nothing but dictating as it came to his heart. If his expression is weak, let someone who expresses himself well dictate justly on his behalf, without adding or subtracting meaning. Let him call men skilled in this art—the gnostics—to witness it; failing them, whoever is present among firmly established spiritual poor, lest the wisdom contain a defect arising from its recipient’s deficiency. Or let him call two upright witnesses to the incoming inspiration: the Book and the Sunna. If it accords with them, it is accepted; otherwise it is rejected. Al-Junayd said: “A subtle point may fall into my heart, but I do not accept it without the testimony of two upright witnesses: the Book and the Sunna.” If you are in haste and find no scribe, entrust these inspirations as pledges within one another’s hearts until they can be recorded. Whoever conceals incoming inspirations from his shaykh or brothers has a sinful heart, for that is a kind of betrayal on the path of spiritual nurture. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-283-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-283-s4","r":"q2-283","title":"","text":"The Real then warns His servants against opposing His commands.","anchor":"en-q2-283-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-284","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within 2:284","anchor":"unit-q2-284"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-1","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"لِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ وَإِنْ تُبْدُوا ما فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ يُحاسِبْكُمْ بِهِ اللَّهُ فَيَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (284)","anchor":"ar-q2-284-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-2","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"قلت: من قرأ (فيغفر) بالجزم، فعلى العطف على الجواب، ومن قرأ بالرفع فعلى الاستئناف، أي: فهو يغفرُ.","anchor":"ar-q2-284-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-3","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ خلقا وملكاً وعبيداً، يتصرف فيهم كيف شاء يرحم من يشاء بفضله، ويعذب من يشاء بعدله، وَإِنْ تُبْدُوا أي: تظهروا ما فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ من السوء والعزم عليه، أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ في قلوبكم، يُحاسِبْكُمْ بِهِ اللَّهُ يوم القيامة فَيَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ مغفرته، وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشاءُ تعذيبه، وَاللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ لا يعجزه عذاب أحد ولا مغفرته. وعبّر الحق تعالى بالمحاسبة دون المؤاخذة، فلم يقل: يؤاخذكم به الله لأن المحاسبة أعم، فتصدق بتقرير الذنوب دون المؤاخذة بها، لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام: «يدنو المؤمن من ربه حتى يضع كنفه عليه، فيقرره بذنوبه، فيقول: هل تعرف","anchor":"ar-q2-284-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-4","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"كذا؟ فيقول: يا رب، أعرف، فيوقفه على ذنبه ذنباً، ذنباً فيقول الله تعالى: أنا الذي سترتها عليك في الدنيا، وأنا أغفرها لك اليوم» . فلله الفضل والمنّة، وله الحمد والشكر.","anchor":"ar-q2-284-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-5","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"الإشارة: (وإن تبدوا ما في أنفسكم) من الخواطر الردية والطوارق الشيطانية، أو تخفوه في قلوبكم، حتى يحول بينكم وبين شهود محبوبكم، (يحاسبكم به الله فيغفر لمن يشاء) فيمحو ظلمته من قلبه بإلهام التوبة والمبادرة إلى اليقظة، (ويعذب من يشاء) بتركه مع ظلمة تلك الأغيار، وخوضه في بحار تلك الأكدار، فما منع القلوب من مشاهدة الأنوار إلا اشتغالها بظلمة الأغيار، فرّغْ قلبك من الأغيار تملأه بالمعارف والأسرار، فإن أردت أن تكون عين العين، فامح من قلبك نقطة الغين، وهي نقطة السوى، ولله درّ القائل:","anchor":"ar-q2-284-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-6","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"إِنْ تَلاشَى الكونُ عَنْ عَيْنِ كشْفِي ... شاهَدَ السرُّ غَيْبَه في بَيَاني","anchor":"ar-q2-284-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-7","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"فاطْرح الكونَ عن عِيانِكَ وامْحُ ... نقطةَ الغَيْنِ إنْ أردتَ تَرَاني","anchor":"ar-q2-284-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-8","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"واعلم أن الخواطر أربعة: ملكي ورباني ونفساني وشيطاني، فالملكي والرباني لا يأمران إلا بالخير، والنفساني والشيطاني لا يأمران إلا بالشر، وقد يأمران بالخير إذا كان فيه دسيسة إلى الشر، والفرق بين النفساني والشيطاني:","anchor":"ar-q2-284-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-9","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"أن الخاطر النفساني ثابت لا يزول بتعوذ ولا غيره، إلا بسابق العناية، بخلاف الشيطاني: فإنه يزول بذكر الله، ويرجع مع الغفلة عن الله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q2-284-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-284-10","r":"q2-284","title":"2:284 · The reckoning of what is within","text":"ولمّا نزل قوله تعالى: وَإِنْ تُبْدُوا ما فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ ... الآية. شق ذلك على الصحابة- رضى الله عنهم- فجاء الصدِّيقُ والفاروق وعبدُ الرحمن ومعاذ، وناسُ من الأنصار، فَجَثَوْا على الرُّكَب، وقالوا: يا رسول الله، ما نزلت علينا آيةٌ أشد من هذه الآية وأنا إن أخذنا بما نُحَدِّثُ به أنفَسنا هَلَكْنَا! فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «هكذا نزلت» . فقالوا: كُلِّفنا من العمل ما لا نطيق، فقال- عليه الصلاة والسلام: «فلعلكم تقولون كما قالت بنو إسرائيل: سَمِعْنا وَعَصَيْنا، قولوا: سمعنا وأطعنا» ، فقالوا: سَمِعْنَا وَأَطَعْنَا، وذَلَّتْ بها أَلْسِنَتُهُمْ، فأَنْزَلَ اللهُ التخفيف، وحكى ما وقع لهم من الإيمان والإذعان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-284-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-284-s1","r":"q2-284","title":"Reckoning and its consequence","text":"I say: whoever reads “then He forgives” ( فيغفر ) in the jussive ( الجزم ) coordinates it with the conditional response ( الجواب ). Whoever reads it in the indicative ( الرفع ) takes it as a fresh statement ( الاستئناف ): that is, “He, then, forgives.”","anchor":"en-q2-284-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-284-s2","r":"q2-284","title":"Being called to account is not necessarily being punished","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth,” as His creation, possession and servants. He disposes of them as He wills, showing mercy to whom He wills by His bounty and punishing whom He wills by His justice. “Whether you disclose”—make manifest—“what is within yourselves” of evil and resolve to commit it, “or conceal it” in your hearts, “God will call you to account for it” on the Day of Resurrection. “He then forgives whom He wills” to forgive “and punishes whom He wills” to punish. “God has power over all things”: neither punishing nor forgiving anyone is beyond His power. The Real, exalted is He, expresses this by “calling to account” ( المحاسبة ), not by “holding culpable” ( المؤاخذة ): He did not say, “God will hold you culpable for it.” Calling to account is more general, and can be fulfilled by making sins acknowledged without exacting punishment for them. For the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “The believer draws near to his Lord until He places His shelter over him and makes him acknowledge his sins, saying, ‘Do you recognize such-and-such?’ He says, ‘My Lord, I recognize it.’ Thus He confronts him with his sins, one by one; then God, exalted is He, says, ‘I am the One who concealed them for you in the world, and I forgive them for you today.’” To God belong bounty and gracious favour, and to Him belong praise and thanksgiving. [B243]","anchor":"en-q2-284-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-284-s3","r":"q2-284","title":"Clearing the heart of otherness","text":"“Whether you disclose what is within yourselves” of evil incoming thoughts ( الخواطر الردية ) and satanic visitations, or conceal it in your hearts until it interposes between you and witnessing your Beloved, “God will call you to account for it. He then forgives whom He wills”: He effaces its darkness from that person’s heart by inspiring repentance and a swift return to wakefulness. “And He punishes whom He wills” by leaving him with the darkness of those other things, plunging into the seas of those troubles. Nothing prevents hearts from witnessing the lights but their occupation with the darkness of otherness ( الأغيار ). Empty your heart of otherness, and you will fill it with recognitions and mysteries. To become the very eye of the Eye ( عين العين ), efface from your heart the dot of the letter ghayn ( الغين ): it is the dot of all that is other ( السوى ). How excellent is the poet’s saying: [B244] When the cosmos vanishes from the eye of my unveiling, the inmost secret witnesses its unseen in my disclosure. Cast the cosmos from your direct vision, and erase the dot of ghayn, should you wish to see me. Know that incoming thoughts are of four kinds: angelic, lordly, from the lower self, and satanic ( ملكي، رباني، نفساني، شيطاني ). The angelic and the lordly command only good; those from the lower self and Satan command only evil. The latter may command good when a concealed means to evil lies within it. The difference between the thought arising from the lower self and the satanic thought is that the former persists: neither seeking refuge nor anything else removes it, except antecedent divine care. The satanic thought, by contrast, departs with remembrance of God and returns with heedlessness of God. And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q2-284-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-284-s4","r":"q2-284","title":"The Companions’ submission and the ensuing relief","text":"When His words, “Whether you disclose what is within yourselves …,” were revealed, they weighed heavily upon the Companions—God be pleased with them. Al-Ṣiddīq, al-Fārūq, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Muʿādh and some of the Anṣār came, sank to their knees and said: “Messenger of God, no verse more burdensome than this has been sent down to us. If we are taken to task for what we say within ourselves, we shall perish!” The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said, “Thus has it been revealed.” They said, “We have been charged with deeds beyond our power.” He said, blessings and peace be upon him: “Are you, then, perhaps saying what the Children of Israel said, ‘We hear and disobey’? Say, ‘We hear and obey.’” They said, “We hear and obey,” and their tongues yielded to these words. God then sent down relief and related their faith and submission, saying: [B245]","anchor":"en-q2-284-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q2-285-286","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication 2:285–286","anchor":"unit-q2-285-286"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-1","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"آمَنَ الرَّسُولُ بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَبِّهِ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ كُلٌّ آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ لاَ نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْ رُسُلِهِ وَقالُوا سَمِعْنا وَأَطَعْنا غُفْرانَكَ رَبَّنا وَإِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيرُ (285) لا يُكَلِّفُ اللَّهُ نَفْساً إِلاَّ وُسْعَها لَها مَا كَسَبَتْ وَعَلَيْها مَا اكْتَسَبَتْ رَبَّنا لا تُؤاخِذْنا إِنْ نَسِينا أَوْ أَخْطَأْنا رَبَّنا وَلا تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنا إِصْراً كَما حَمَلْتَهُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِنا رَبَّنا وَلا تُحَمِّلْنا ما لا طاقَةَ لَنا بِهِ وَاعْفُ عَنَّا وَاغْفِرْ لَنا وَارْحَمْنا أَنْتَ مَوْلانا فَانْصُرْنا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكافِرِينَ (286)","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-2","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"قلت: من قرأ: (لا نفرق) بالنون، فعلى حذف القول، أي: قالوا: لا نفرق، ومن قرأ بالياء فيرجع إلى الكل، أي: لا يفرق كل واحد منهم بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِّن رُّسُلِهِ، و (بين) : من الظروف النسبية، لا تقع إلا بين شيئين أو أشياء، تقول: جلست بين زيد وعمرو، وبين رجلين، أو رجال، ولا تقول بين زيد فقط، وإنما أضيف هنا إلى أحد لأنه في معنى الجماعة، أي: لا نفرق بين آحاد منهم كقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «ما أُحلَّت الغنائم لأحدٍ، سُودِ الرؤوس، غيركم» . و (غفرانك) : مفعول مطلق، أي: اغفر لنا غفرانك. أو: نطلب غفرانك، فيكون مفعولاً به.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-3","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: آمَنَ الرَّسُولُ بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَبِّهِ إيمان تحقيق وشهود، وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ كل على قدر إيقان، كُلٌّ واحد منهم آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ على ما يليق به من شهود وعيان، أو دليل وبرهان، وآمن بملائكته وأنهم عباد مكرمون لاَّ يَعْصُونَ اللَّهَ مَآ أَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُونَ ما يُؤْمَرُونَ، وَكُتُبِهِ وأنها كلام الله، مشتملة على أمر ونهى ووعد ووعيد وقصص وأخبار، ما عرف منها كالتوراة والإنجيل والزبور والفرقان، وجب الإيمان به بعينه، ومالم يعرف وجب الإيمان به في الجملة، وَرُسُلِهِ وأنهم بشر متصفون بالكمالات، منزّهون عن النقائص، كما يليق بحالهم، حال كون الرسول والمؤمنون قائلين لاَ نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْ رُسُلِهِ أو: (لا يفرق) كل منهم بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِّن رُّسُلِهِ بأن يصدقوا بالبعض، دون البعض كما فرقت اليهود والنصارى، وَقالُوا أي المؤمنين سَمِعْنا وَأَطَعْنا أي:","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-4","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"سمعنا قولك وأطعنا أمرك، نطلب غُفْرانَكَ يا ربنا وَإِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيرُ بالبعث والنشور، وهذا إقرار منهم بالبعث الذي هو من تمام أركان الإيمان.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-5","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"فلمّا تحقق إيمانُهم، وتيقن إذعانُهم، خفَّف الله عنهم بقوله: لا يُكَلِّفُ اللَّهُ نَفْساً إِلَّا وُسْعَها أي: إلا ما في طاقتها وتسعه قدرتها. وهذا يدل على عدم وقوع التكليف بالمحال ولا يدل على امتناعه. أما المحال العادي(1) فجائز التكليف به، وأما المحال العقلي(2) فيمتنع، إذ لا يتصور وقوعه، وإذا كلف الله عباده بما يطيقونه، فكل نفس لَها ما كَسَبَتْ من الخير فتوفى أجره على التمام، وَعَلَيْها مَا اكْتَسَبَتْ من الشر، فترى جزاءه، إلا أن يعفو ذو الجلال والإكرام.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-6","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"وعبر في جانب الخير بالكسب، وفي جانب الشر بالاكتساب، تعليماً للأدب في نسبة الخير إلى الله، والشر إلى العبد. فتأمله.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-7","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"ثم قالوا في تمام دعائهم: رَبَّنا لا تُؤاخِذْنا إِنْ نَسِينا أَوْ أَخْطَأْنا، أي: لا تؤاخذنا بما أدى بنا إلى نسيان أو خطأ من تفريط أو قلة مبالاة، وفي الحديث: «إن الله رفعَ عن أمتي الْخَطأَ والنِّسْيَانَ وما حدثتْ به نفسها» .","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-8","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"ويجوز أن يراد نفس الخطأ والنسيان إذ لا تمتنع المؤاخذة بهما عقلاً، فإن الذنوب كالسموم، فكما أن تناول السم يؤدى إلى الهلاك، وإن كان خطأ- فتعاطي الذنوب لا يبعد أن يفضي إلى العقاب، وإن لم يكن عزيمة، لكنه تعالى وعد التجاوز عنه رحمة وفضلاً. ويجوز أن يدعو به الإنسان، استدامة واعتداداً بالنعمة فيه. ويؤيد ذلك مفهوم قوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «رفع عن أمتي الخطأ والنِّسْيَانْ» ، أي: فإن غير هذه الأمة كانوا يؤاخذون به، فدلّ على عدم امتناعه. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-9","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"ثم قالوا: رَبَّنا وَلا تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنا إِصْراً أي: عهداً ثقيلاً يأصر ظهورنا، أي: يثقله، فتعذبنا بتركه وعدم حمله، كَما حَمَلْتَهُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِنا مثل اليهود في تكليفهم بقتل الأنفس في التوبة، وقطع موضع النجاسة، وغير ذلك من التكاليف الشاقة، رَبَّنا وَلا تُحَمِّلْنا ما لا طاقَةَ لَنا بِهِ من التكاليف التي لا تسعها طاقتنا، وهذا يدل على جواز التكليف بما لا يطاق عادة، وإلا لما سئل التخلص منه، وَاعْفُ عَنَّا أي: امح ذنوبنا، وَاغْفِرْ لَنا أي: استر عيوبنا، وَارْحَمْنا أي: تعطف علينا. اعْفُ عَنَّا الصغائر، وَاغْفِرْ لَنا الكبائر، وَارْحَمْنا عند الشدائد والحسرات، أَنْتَ مَوْلانا أي: سيدنا وناصرنا، فَانْصُرْنا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكافِرِينَ فإن من شأن المولى أن ينصر مواليه على الأعداء.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-10","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"قال البيضاوي: (رُوِيَ أنه عليه الصلاة والسلام- لمّا دعا بهذه الدعوات قيل له: فعلتُ) . وعنه عليه الصلاة والسلام: «أُنْزِلَ آيتان من كُنوز الجنة، كتبهما الرحمن بيده قبل أن يخلق الخلق بألفَيْ سنة، من قرأهما بعد العشاء الأخيرة أجْزَأتَاه عن قيام الليل» . وعنه عليه الصلاة والسلام: «من قرأ الأيَتينِ مِنْ آخِر سُورَةِ الْبَقَرةِ في لَيْلَة كَفَتَاهُ» . وهو يَرُدُّ قول من استكره أن يقال سورة البقرة، وقال: ينبغي أن يقال السورة التي يذكر فيها البقرة، كما قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «السورة التي يذكر فيها البقرة فسطاط القرآن فتعلموها فإنَّ تعلُّمها بَرَكَة، وَتَرْكَهَا حَسْرَة، ولن يَسْتَطِيعها البَطَلَةُ. قيل: وما البطلة؟ قال: السحرة(1)» .","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-11","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"الإشارة: يُفهم من سر الآية أن من شق عليه أمر من الأمور، أو عسرت عليه حاجة، أو نزلت به شدة أو بلية، فليرجع إلى الله، ولينطرح بين يدي مولاه، وليعتقد أن الأمور كلها بيده فإنَّ الله تعالى لا يخليه من معونته ورفده، فيخفف عنه ما نزل به، أو يقويه على حمله، فإن الصحابة- رضي الله عنهم- لما شق عليهم المحاسبة على الخواطر سلَّموا وأذعنوا لأمر مولاهم، فأنزل عليهم التخفيف، وأسقط عنهم في ذلك التكليف، وكل من رجع في أموره كلها إلى الله قضيت حوائجه كلها بالله. «من علامات النجح في النهايات الرجوع إلى الله في البدايات» .","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-12","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"وقوله تعالى: رَبَّنا وَلا تُحَمِّلْنا ما لا طاقَةَ لَنا بِهِ، قيل: هو الحب لله، فلا يسأل العبد من مولاه من حبه إلا ما يطيقه، وتأمل قضية الرجل الذي سأل سيدنا موسى عليه السلام أن يرزقه الله حبه، فلما سأل ربه موسى عليه السلام هام ذلك الرجل، وشق ثيابه، وتمزقت أوصاله حتى مات. فناجى موسى رضى الله عنه ربه في شأنه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-13","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"يا موسى، ألف رجل كلهم سألوني ما سأل ذلك الرجل، فقسمت جزءاً من محبتي بينهم، فنابه ذلك الجزء. أو كما قال سبحانه.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-14","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"وقال بعض الصالحين: حضرتُ مجلس ذي النون، في فسطاط مصر، فَحَزَرْت(1) في مجلسه سبعين ألفا، فتكلم ذلك اليوم في محبته تعالى فمات أحدَ عشرَ رجلاً في المجلس، فصاح رجل من المريدين فقال: يا أبا الفيض، ذكرْتَ محبة الله تعالى فاذكر محبة المخلوقين، فتأوّه ذو النون تأوّهاً شديداً، ومدّ يده إلى قميصه، وشقه اثنتين، وقال: آه! غلقت رهونهم، واستعبرت عيونهم، وحالفوا السُّهَاد، وفارقوا الرُّقاد، فليلُهم طويل، ونومهم قليل، أحزانهم لا تُنْفذ. وهمومهم لا تفقد، أمورهم عسيرة، ودموعهم غزيرة، باكية عيونهم، قريحة جفونهم، عاداهم الزمان والأهل والجيران.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-15","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"قلت: هذه حالة العباد والزهاد، أُولي الجد والاجتهاد، غلب عليهم الخوف المزعِج، أو الشوق المقلق، وأما العارفون الواصلون فقد زال عنهم هذا التعب، وأفضوا إلى الراحة بعد النصب، قد وصلوا إلى مشاهدة الحبيب، ومناجاة القريب، فعبادتهم قلبية، وأعمالهم باطنية، بين فكرة ونظرة، مع العكوف في الحضرة، قد سكن شوقهم وزال قلقهم، قد شربوا ورووا، وسكروا وصحوا، فلا تحركهم الأحوال، ولا تهيجهم الأقوال، بل هم كالجبال الرواسي، نفعنا الله بذكرهم، وجعلنا من حزبهم. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q2-285-286-16","r":"q2-285-286","title":"2:285–286 · Faith, capacity and the final supplication","text":"قوله تعالى: (واعف عنا) ، قال الورتجبي: أي: (واعف عنا) قلة المعرفة بك، (واغفر لنا) التقصير في عبادتك، (وارحمنا) بمواصلتك ومشاهدتك. هـ. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق، وسلام على المرسلين، والحمد لله رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q2-285-286-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-285-286-s1","r":"q2-285-286","title":"Collective reference and the plea for forgiveness","text":"I say: in the reading “we make no distinction” ( لا نفرق ), with nūn, a verb of saying is understood: “They say, ‘We make no distinction.’” In the reading with yāʾ, the reference is to “each”: each one of them makes no distinction “between any of His messengers.” “Between” ( بين ) is a relational adverb ( الظروف النسبية ), occurring only between two or more things. You say, “I sat between Zayd and ʿAmr,” “between two men,” or “between men,” but not “between Zayd” alone. Here it is annexed to “any one” ( أحد ) because that word has a collective meaning: “We make no distinction between individuals among them.” Compare the Prophet’s saying, blessings and peace be upon him, “Spoils were never made lawful to anyone—black-haired heads—other than you.” [B246] “Your forgiveness” ( غفرانك ) is an absolute accusative ( مفعول مطلق ): “Forgive us with Your forgiveness.” Alternatively, “[We seek] Your forgiveness,” in which case it is a direct object ( مفعول به ).","anchor":"en-q2-285-286-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-285-286-s2","r":"q2-285-286","title":"The degrees and objects of faith","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “The Messenger believes in what has been sent down to him from his Lord,” with the faith of realization and witnessing ( تحقيق وشهود ); “and the believers,” each according to his certainty. “Each” one of them “believes in God” as befits him: through witnessing and direct vision ( شهود وعيان ), or evidence and demonstration ( دليل وبرهان ). Each believes in His angels: that they are honoured servants, who “do not disobey God in what He commands them, and do what they are commanded” [66:6]. And in “His books”: that they are God’s speech, containing command and prohibition, promise and warning, narratives and reports. Those known by name—the Torah, Gospel, Psalms and Criterion—must be believed in individually; those not known must be believed in collectively. And in “His messengers”: that they are human beings endowed with perfections and free from defects in a manner appropriate to their condition. The Messenger and believers say, “We make no distinction between any of His messengers”; or, in the other reading, each one “makes no distinction between any of His messengers.” They do not affirm some and deny others, as the Jews and Christians made distinctions. “They say”—the believers—“We hear and obey”: we hear Your word and obey Your command. We seek “Your forgiveness, our Lord! To You is the return,” through resurrection and rising from the dead. This is their acknowledgement of resurrection, which completes the pillars of faith.","anchor":"en-q2-285-286-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-285-286-s3","r":"q2-285-286","title":"Capacity, acquisition and divine pardon","text":"When their faith was realized and their submission established, God lightened their burden by saying, “God charges no soul beyond its capacity”: only what lies within its strength and the extent of its ability. This indicates that imposing the impossible does not occur; it does not establish that such imposition is itself impossible. As for what is impossible according to ordinary custom ( المحال العادي ), imposing it is admissible; what is rationally impossible ( المحال العقلي ) cannot be imposed, since its occurrence is inconceivable. [B247] When God charges His servants with what they can bear, each soul has “to its credit what it has earned” of good, and is paid its reward in full; “and against it what it has acquired” of evil, whose recompense it will see, unless the Possessor of Majesty and Generosity pardons it. On the side of good He uses “earning” ( الكسب ), and on the side of evil “acquiring” ( الاكتساب ), teaching reverent propriety ( الأدب ) in attributing good to God and evil to the servant. So consider this. They then complete their supplication: “Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err.” That is, do not take us to task for the negligence or lack of concern that has led us into forgetfulness or error. The report says: “God has lifted from my community error, forgetfulness and what it says within itself.” [B248] Alternatively, the intended meaning is error and forgetfulness themselves. Punishment for these is not rationally impossible. Sins resemble poisons: just as taking poison leads to destruction even when it is taken in error, so committing sins might conceivably lead to punishment even without deliberate resolve. But He, exalted is He, has promised to overlook them in mercy and bounty. A person may continue to pray for this in order that the favour endure, and in acknowledgement of it. This is supported by the implication of the Prophet’s words, “Error and forgetfulness have been lifted from my community”: those outside this community were taken to task for them, which shows that such punishment is not impossible. So says al-Bayḍāwī. They then say, “Our Lord, do not lay upon us a burden”: a heavy covenant that weighs upon our backs, so that You punish us for abandoning it and failing to carry it; “such as You laid upon those before us.” An example is the Jews’ being required to kill themselves in repentance, cut away the place affected by impurity, and undertake other arduous obligations. “Our Lord, do not make us bear what we have no strength to bear”: obligations exceeding our capacity. This indicates the admissibility of imposing what is ordinarily beyond one’s capacity; otherwise, deliverance from it would not be requested. “Pardon us”: efface our sins. “Forgive us”: veil our faults. “Have mercy on us”: turn tenderly towards us. Or: pardon our lesser sins, forgive our greater sins, and have mercy upon us in hardships and regrets. “You are our Master,” our Lord and Helper: “give us victory over the unbelieving people,” for it is the master’s part to help those attached to him against their enemies.","anchor":"en-q2-285-286-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-285-286-s4","r":"q2-285-286","title":"The closing verses and the merit of al-Baqara","text":"Al-Bayḍāwī says: “It is related that when the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, made these supplications, he was told, ‘I have done so.’” It is also related from him: “Two verses were sent down from the treasures of Paradise, written by the All-Merciful with His hand two thousand years before He created creation. Whoever recites them after the final evening prayer, they suffice him in place of standing in prayer through the night.” And from him: “Whoever recites the two verses at the end of Sūrat al-Baqara in a night, they suffice him.” [B249] The latter report refutes the view of one who disliked saying “Sūrat al-Baqara,” maintaining that one should say, “The sūrah in which the cow is mentioned.” Compare his words, blessings and peace be upon him: “The sūrah in which the cow is mentioned is the pavilion of the Qurʾān. Learn it: learning it is a blessing, abandoning it a cause of regret, and the baṭala cannot withstand it.” When asked who the baṭala were, he answered, “Sorcerers.” [B250]","anchor":"en-q2-285-286-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-285-286-s5","r":"q2-285-286","title":"Returning to God in difficulty","text":"From the verse’s inward meaning it is understood that anyone for whom a matter becomes difficult, a need hard to obtain, or upon whom hardship or affliction descends, should return to God, cast himself down before his Master and believe that all affairs are in His hand. God, exalted is He, will not leave him without assistance and support: He will lighten what has befallen him, or strengthen him to bear it. When the Companions—God be pleased with them—found reckoning for incoming thoughts burdensome, they submitted and yielded to their Master’s command. He then sent relief upon them and removed the obligation in that respect. Whoever returns all his affairs to God has all his needs fulfilled through God. “Among the signs of success at the ends is returning to God at the beginnings.” [B251]","anchor":"en-q2-285-286-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q2-285-286-s6","r":"q2-285-286","title":"Love, overwhelming states and settled realization","text":"Regarding His words, “Our Lord, do not make us bear what we have no strength to bear,” it has been said that what is meant is love for God. A servant should therefore ask his Master for no more of His love than he can bear. Consider the story of the man who asked our master Moses, peace be upon him, to ask God to bestow His love upon him. When Moses asked his Lord, the man wandered distraught, rent his clothes, and his limbs were torn apart until he died. Moses privately addressed his Lord concerning him, and He said: “Moses, a thousand men all asked Me what this man asked. I divided a portion of My love among them, and that share fell to him”—or words to that effect from Him, exalted is He. [B252] One of the righteous said: “I attended Dhū l-Nūn’s gathering in Fusṭāṭ, Egypt. I estimated those present at seventy thousand. That day he spoke of love of God, and eleven men died in the gathering. A disciple cried, ‘Abū l-Fayḍ, you have spoken of love of God; speak now of the love of created beings.’ [XV-N004] Dhū l-Nūn gave a deep groan, reached towards his shirt, tore it in two, and said: ‘Ah! Their pledges are forfeit, their eyes overflow. They have allied themselves with sleeplessness and parted company with slumber. Their nights are long, their sleep little. Their sorrows do not run out, their cares do not depart. Their affairs are hard, their tears abundant, their eyes weeping, their eyelids sore. Time, family and neighbours have become their enemies.’” [B252] I say: this is the condition of worshippers and ascetics, people of strenuous effort and exertion, overcome by disturbing fear or unsettling longing. As for the gnostics who have arrived ( العارفون الواصلون ), this weariness has left them, and after toil they have passed into repose. They have reached the witnessing of the Beloved and intimate converse with the Near. Their worship is of the heart, their works inward: now contemplation, now vision, while abiding in the Presence. Their longing has grown still and their disquiet departed. They have drunk and been quenched, become intoxicated and returned to sobriety. States no longer move them, nor do words excite them; rather, they are like firmly rooted mountains. May God benefit us through their remembrance and make us of their company. Amen. On His words, “Pardon us,” al-Wartajbī says: “‘Pardon us’ our slight knowledge of You; ‘forgive us’ our shortcoming in worshipping You; and ‘have mercy on us’ through communion with You and witnessing You.” And success is through God. He guides to the even path. Peace be upon the messengers, and praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds.","anchor":"en-q2-285-286-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"intro3","r":"intro3","title":"Sūrat Āl ʿImrān — The Family of ʿImrān","text":"Sūrat Āl ʿImrān — The Family of ʿImrān Sūrah introduction","anchor":"unit-intro3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro3-1","r":"intro3","title":"Sūrat Āl ʿImrān — The Family of ʿImrān","text":"سورة آل عمران","anchor":"ar-intro3-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro3-2","r":"intro3","title":"Sūrat Āl ʿImrān — The Family of ʿImrān","text":"مدنية. وآياتها: مائتان، وقيل: مائة وسبع وثمانون. وكلماتها: ثلاثة آلاف وأربعمائة وثمانون كلمة، ومناسبتها لما قبلها: قوله تعالى فى أولها: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآياتِ اللَّهِ ... إلخ، فكأنه تتميم لقوله، فَانْصُرْنا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكافِرِينَ، وتفسير له.","anchor":"ar-intro3-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro3-3","r":"intro3","title":"Sūrat Āl ʿImrān — The Family of ʿImrān","text":"ومضمنها: توجيه العتاب لثلاث طوائف: للنصارى لغلوهم في عيسى عليه السلام، ولامتناعهم من الدخول فى الإسلام، وبسببهم نزلت السورة، أعنى نصارى نجران، ولليهود لتفريطهم فى اتباع النبي- عليه الصلاة والسلام- وللمسلمين لما وقع لهم من الفشل يوم أحد، ولذلك افتتح السورة بذكر الكتب الثلاثة، إذ لو قاموا بحقوقها ما توجه لهم عتاب، فقال:","anchor":"ar-intro3-3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-intro3-s1","r":"intro3","title":"Rebuke, revelation and the three communities","text":"It is Medinan. Its verses number two hundred; it has also been said, one hundred and eighty-seven. Its words number three thousand four hundred and eighty. [A001] Its connection with the preceding sūrah is His saying near its beginning, “Those who disbelieve in God’s signs …”: this is, as it were, a completion and explanation of “give us victory over the unbelieving people.” Its contents direct reproach towards three groups: the Christians, for their excess concerning Jesus, peace be upon him, and their refusal to enter Islam—it was on their account that the sūrah was revealed, namely the Christians of Najrān; the Jews, for their failure to follow the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him; and the Muslims, for the loss of resolve that befell them on the day of Uḥud. [A002] For this reason He opens the sūrah by mentioning the three books: had they fulfilled their obligations towards them, no reproach would have been directed at them. Thus He says:","anchor":"en-intro3-s1"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-1-3","r":"q3-1-3","title":"3:1–3 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting and the revealed books","text":"3:1–3 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting and the revealed books 3:1–3","anchor":"unit-q3-1-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-1-3-1","r":"q3-1-3","title":"3:1–3 · The Living, the Self-Subsisting and the revealed books","text":"الم (1) اللَّهُ لآَ إِلهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ (2) نَزَّلَ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ بِالْحَقِّ مُصَدِّقاً لِما بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَأَنْزَلَ التَّوْراةَ وَالْإِنْجِيلَ (3)","anchor":"ar-q3-1-3-1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-1-3-s1","r":"q3-1-3","title":"The opening letters","text":"I say: all the sūrahs’ opening letters are pronounced in pause and have no syntactic inflection ( الإعراب ), since that which would occasion and require it is absent. They are therefore paused upon with sukūn, as when one enumerates “one, two.” In the well-known recitation, the mīm here is given fatḥa only because the vowel of the following hamza is transferred to it. Consult al-Bayḍāwī. [A003] Ibn ʿAbbās—God be pleased with him—said: “Alif is His favours ( آلاؤه ), lām His gentleness ( لطفه ), and mīm His dominion ( ملكه ).” I say: perhaps each letter points to one of the groups to whom the reproach is directed. The favours are for those Christians who embraced Islam; the gentleness for those Jews who embraced it; and dominion for the Companions who embraced Islam—God’s good pleasure be upon them—for God gave them possession of the earth’s east and west. And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-1-3-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-1-3-s2","r":"q3-1-3","title":"The Qurʾān confirms the earlier revelation","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: O exalted sovereign, O magnified Messenger, convey to your people that God is One in His dominion. There is no deity beside Him, nor does He love that another be worshipped with Him. None deserves worship but the Living, the Self-Subsisting ( الحي القيوم ), whom intellects and the apprehensions of understanding cannot encompass. He attends to His servants’ affairs and disposes of them according to His will. He has left them without excuse through the messengers’ tongues and sent down books as clarification for those seeking guidance. Thus “He has sent down upon you the Book,” in instalments over twenty years, [A004] “in truth”: clothed in truth, so that “falsehood cannot come to it from before it or behind it” [41:42]; or clothed in proofs that repel every falsehood; or in justice, through which the oppression of every deviating person is removed. It is “confirming” the divine books that preceded it, agreeing with their narratives and reports, and so bearing witness to their truth and rectitude. “And He sent down the Torah and the Gospel …”","anchor":"en-q3-1-3-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-4","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers 3:4","anchor":"unit-q3-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-1","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"مِنْ قَبْلُ هُدىً لِلنَّاسِ وَأَنْزَلَ الْفُرْقانَ ...","anchor":"ar-q3-4-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-2","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"قلت: فواتح السور كلها موقوفة خالية عن الإعراب لفقدان مُوجبه ومقتضيه، فيوقف عليها بالسكون، كقولهم:","anchor":"ar-q3-4-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-3","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"واحد، اثنان. وإنما فَتَحَ الميم هنا في القراءة المشهورة لإلقاء حركة الهمزة عليها. انظر البيضاوي. قال ابن عباس رضي الله عنه: (الألف آلاؤه، واللام لطفه، والميم مُلكه) .","anchor":"ar-q3-4-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-4","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"قلت: ولعلَّ كل حرف يشير إلى فرقة ممن توجَّه العتاب إليهم، فالآلاء لِمنْ أسلم من النصارى، واللطف لمن أسلم من اليهود، والملك لمن أسلم من الصحابة- رضوان الله عليهم-، فقد ملكهم الله مشارق الأرض ومغاربها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-5","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"يقول الحق جل جلاله: أيها الملك المُعظَّم، والرسول المفخم، بلِّغ قومك أن الله واحد في ملكه، ليس معه إله، ولا يُحب أن يُعبد معه سواه إذ لا يستحق أن يعبد إلا الحيّ القيّوم، الذي تعجز عن إدراكه العقولُ ومدارك الفهوم، قائم بأمر عباده، متصرف فيهم، على وفق مراده، فأعذر إليهم على ألسنة المرسلين، وأنزل عليهم الكتب بياناً للمسترشدين، فنزَّل عَلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ مُنَجّماً في عشرين سنة، متلبساً بِالْحَقِّ، حتى لا يَأْتِيهِ الْباطِلُ مِنْ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَلا مِنْ خَلْفِهِ، أو متلبساً بالحجج التي تدفع كل باطل، أو بالعدل حتى ينتفي به جَوْر كل مائل، مُصَدِّقاً لما تقدم قبله من الكتب الإلهية إذ هو موافق لما فيها من القصص والأخبار، فكان شاهداً عليها بالصحة والإبرار.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-6","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"وَأَنْزَلَ التَّوْراةَ وَالْإِنْجِيلَ","anchor":"ar-q3-4-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-8","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"من قبله هادياً لمن كلف باتباعهما من الأنام، أو للجميع، إذا كان شرعُ منْ قبلنا شرعاً لنا- معشر أهل الإسلام-، ثم ختم الوحي بإنزال الْفُرْقانَ، وكلّف بالإيمان به الإنس والجان، فرَّق به بين الحق والباطل، واندفع به ظلمة كل كافر وجاهل وقدَّم ذكره على الكتب لعظم شرفه، وختم به آخراً لتأخر نزوله.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-9","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-10","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"الإشارة: لمّا أراد الحق جل جلاله أن يشير إلى وحدة الذات وظهور أنوار الصفات، قَدَّم قبل ذلك رموزاً وإشارات، لا يفهمها إلا من غاص في قاموس بحر الذات، وغرق في تيار الصفات، فيستخرج بفكرته من يواقيت العلوم وغوامض الفهوم، ما تحار فيه الأذهان، وتكِلُّ عنه عبارةُ اللسان، فحينئذ يفهم دقائق الرموز وأسرار الإشارات، ويطلع على أسرار الذات وأنوار الصفات، ويفهم أسرار الكتب السماوية، وما احتوت عليه من العلوم اللدنية، والمواهب الربانية، ويشرق في قلبه أنوار الفرقان، حتى يرتقي إلى تحقيق أهل الشهود والعيان. جعلنا الله منهم بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-11","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"ثم هدد من كفر بالفرقان، بعد وضوح سواطع البرهان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-4-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-12","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"... إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآياتِ اللَّهِ لَهُمْ عَذابٌ شَدِيدٌ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ ذُو انْتِقامٍ (4)","anchor":"ar-q3-4-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-13","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"قلت: الانتقام والنقمة: عقوبة المجرم. وفعله: نقم بكسر القاف وفتحها.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-14","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآياتِ اللَّهِ المنزلة على نبيه أو على سائر أنبيائه، أو الآيات الدالة على وحدانيته، لَهُمْ عَذابٌ شَدِيدٌ يوم يظهر نفوذ الوعد والوعيد، فينتقم الله فيه من المجرمين، ويتعطف على عباده المؤمنين، فإن اللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ لا يغلبه غالب، ولا يفُوته هارب، ذُو انْتِقامٍ كبير ولطف كثير. لطف الله بنا وبجميع المسلمين. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-15","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"الإشارة: ظهور أولياء الله لطف من آيات الله، فمن كفر بهم حُرم بركتهم، وبقي في عذاب الحجاب وسوء الحساب، تظهر عليه النقمة والمحنة، حين يرفع الله المقربين في أعلى عليين، ويكون الغافلون مع عوام المسلمين، (ذلك يوم التغابن) . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-4-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-4-16","r":"q3-4","title":"3:4 · Guidance, discernment and the warning to unbelievers","text":"ولما وصف الحق جل جلاله نفسه بالوحدانية والحياة والقيومية المقتضية للغنى المطلق، وصف نفسه أيضا بالعلم المحيط والقدرة النافذة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-4-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-4-s1","r":"q3-4","title":"The Criterion and the earlier books","text":"He sent them down before it, as guidance for those people charged with following them; or for all, on the principle that the Sacred Law of those before us is law for us, the community of Islam. He then sealed revelation by sending down “the Criterion” ( الفرقان ), charging humans and jinn with believing in it. Through it He distinguished truth from falsehood and dispelled the darkness of every unbeliever and ignorant person. He mentioned it before the other books because of its immense honour, and mentioned it last because it was the last to descend. And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-4-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-4-s2","r":"q3-4","title":"Understanding the mysteries of revelation","text":"When the Real, glorious is His majesty, wished to point to the unity of the Essence and the manifestation of the lights of the Attributes, He first set forth symbols and allusions understood only by one who has dived into the depths of the ocean of the Essence and been submerged in the current of the Attributes. Through his contemplation he brings out precious jewels of knowledge and subtle understandings at which minds stand bewildered and for which the tongue’s expression fails. Then he understands the subtleties of the symbols and the secrets of the allusions, and gains insight into the mysteries of the Essence and lights of the Attributes. He understands the mysteries of the heavenly books and the divinely bestowed sciences ( العلوم اللدنية ) and lordly gifts they contain. The lights of discernment shine in his heart until he rises to the realization of those possessed of witnessing and direct vision. May God make us among them through His gracious favour and generosity.","anchor":"en-q3-4-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-4-s3","r":"q3-4","title":"","text":"He then threatens those who disbelieve in the Criterion after the radiance of the proof has become clear, saying: Qurʾānic continuation · 3:4b إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآياتِ اللَّهِ لَهُمْ عَذابٌ شَدِيدٌ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ ذُو انْتِقامٍ Those who disbelieve in God’s signs will have a severe punishment. God is Mighty, Possessed of requital.","anchor":"en-q3-4-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-4-s4","r":"q3-4","title":"Requital","text":"I say: intiqām and niqma ( الانتقام والنقمة ) mean the punishment of an offender. The verb is naqima or naqama, with kasra or fatḥa on the qāf.","anchor":"en-q3-4-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-4-s5","r":"q3-4","title":"Might, punishment and gentleness","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Those who disbelieve in God’s signs,” sent down to His Prophet or to all His prophets, or in the signs indicating His oneness, “will have a severe punishment” on the day when promise and warning are seen to take effect. God will then exact requital from the offenders and turn tenderly towards His believing servants. For “God is Mighty”: no vanquisher overcomes Him and no fugitive escapes Him. He is possessed of great requital and abundant gentleness. May God show gentleness to us and to all Muslims. Amen.","anchor":"en-q3-4-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-4-s6","r":"q3-4","title":"The loss of the blessing of God’s friends","text":"The appearance of God’s friends is a gracious manifestation of God’s signs. Whoever rejects them is deprived of their blessing, remaining in the torment of the veil and an ill reckoning. Requital and affliction become manifest upon him when God raises those brought near into the highest heights, while the heedless remain with the ordinary Muslims. “That is the Day of Mutual Loss and Gain” [64:9]. And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-4-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-4-s7","r":"q3-4","title":"","text":"Having described Himself by oneness, life and self-subsistence—which entail absolute independence—the Real, glorious is His majesty, also describes Himself by encompassing knowledge and effectual power, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-4-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-5-6","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb 3:5–6","anchor":"unit-q3-5-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-5-6-1","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَخْفى عَلَيْهِ شَيْءٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلا فِي السَّماءِ (5) هُوَ الَّذِي يُصَوِّرُكُمْ فِي الْأَرْحامِ كَيْفَ يَشاءُ لاَ إِلهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ (6)","anchor":"ar-q3-5-6-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-5-6-2","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَخْفى عَلَيْهِ شَيْءٌ من أمر خلقه، إيماناً أو كفراناً، طاعة أو عصياناً، أحاط علمه بما فى السموات العلي وما في الأرضين السفلى، كليّاً كان أو جزئيّاً، حسيّاً أو معنوياً، يعلم عدد الحصى والرمال، ومكاييل المياه ومثاقيل الجبال، ويعلم حوادث الضمائر، وهواجس الخواطر، بعلم قديم أزلي، وله قدرة نافذة، وحكمة بالغة، فبقدرته صَوَّرَ النُّطَف في الأرحام كيف شاء سبحانه من نقص أو تمام، وأتقنها بحكمته، وأبرزها إلى ما يَسَّرَ لها من رزقه، سبحانه من مدبر عليم، عزيز حكيم، لا يعجزه شيء، ولا يخرج عن دائرة علمه شيء، لا موجود سواه، ولا نعبد إلا إياه، وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-5-6-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-5-6-3","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"الإشارة: مَنْ تحقق أن الله واحد في ملكه، لا شريك له في ذاته ولا في صفاته ولا أفعاله، وأنه أحاط به علماً وسمعاً وبصراً، وأن أمره بين الكاف والنون، (إِذَآ أَرَادَ شَيْئاً أَن يقولَ له كُن فيكون) - كيف يشكو ما نزل به منه إلى أحد سواه؟ أم كيف يرفع حوائجه إلى غير مولاه؟ أم كيف يعول هما، وسيدُه من خيره لا ينساه؟ من دبرك في ظلمة الأحشاء، وصوَّرك في الأرحام كيف يشاء، وآتاك كل ما تسأل وتشاء، كيف يَنْساكَ من بره وإحسانه؟ أم كيف يخرجك عن دائرة لطفه وامتنانه؟ وفي ذلك يقول لسان الحقيقة:","anchor":"ar-q3-5-6-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-5-6-4","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"تَذَكَّر جَمِيلِي فِيكَ إِذْ كُنْتَ نُطْفَةً ... وَلا تَنْسَ تَصْوِيرِي لشَخْصِكَ في الْحَشا","anchor":"ar-q3-5-6-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-5-6-5","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"وَكُنْ وَاثِقاً بِي في أُمُورِكَ كُلِّها ... سأَكْفِيكَ مِنْهَا ما يُخافُ ويُخْتَشَى","anchor":"ar-q3-5-6-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-5-6-6","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"وَسَلِّمْ ليّ الأمْرَ واعْلَمْ بأنني ... أُصَرِّفُ أحْكَامِي وأَفْعَلُ ما أشا","anchor":"ar-q3-5-6-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-5-6-7","r":"q3-5-6","title":"3:5–6 · Knowledge, power and formation in the womb","text":"ثم وصف كتابه الفرقان بأنه مشتمل على ما هو محكم واضح البيان، وعلى ما هو متشابه لا يعلمه إلا الله، والراسخون من أهل العرفان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-5-6-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-5-6-s1","r":"q3-5-6","title":"Nothing escapes His knowledge or power","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Nothing is hidden from God” concerning His creatures: belief or unbelief, obedience or disobedience. His knowledge encompasses whatever is in the high heavens and the lower earths, universal or particular, sensible or intelligible. He knows the number of pebbles and grains of sand, the measures of the waters and the weights of the mountains. He knows the occurrences of inward consciousness and the stirrings of thoughts, with beginningless, eternal knowledge. His power is effectual and His wisdom consummate. By His power He formed the drops in the wombs however He willed, with deficiency or completeness, perfected them through His wisdom, and brought them forth to the sustenance He had made available to them. Glory to the Disposer who is Knowing, Mighty and Wise! Nothing incapacitates Him and nothing falls outside the compass of His knowledge. There is no existent besides Him, and we worship none but Him. [A005] Success is through God, who guides to the even path.","anchor":"en-q3-5-6-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-5-6-s2","r":"q3-5-6","title":"Trust in the One who first formed you","text":"Whoever realizes that God is One in His dominion, without associate in His Essence, Attributes or acts; that He encompasses him in knowledge, hearing and sight; and that His command is between kāf and nūn—“when He wills a thing, He says to it, ‘Be,’ and it is” [compare 36:82]—how could he complain to anyone else of what descends upon him from Him? How could he raise his needs to other than his Master? How could he nurse anxiety, when his Master does not forget to bestow His goodness upon him? He who cared for you in the darkness of the inward parts, formed you in the wombs as He willed, and gave you all you ask and wish: how would He forget to show you His goodness and beneficence? How would He place you outside the compass of His gentleness and favour? Concerning this, the tongue of Reality ( لسان الحقيقة ) says: Remember My kindness to you when you were a drop; do not forget My forming your person in the womb. Trust Me in all your affairs: I shall suffice you against what is feared and dreaded. Surrender the affair to Me, and know that I dispose My decrees and do whatever I will.","anchor":"en-q3-5-6-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-5-6-s3","r":"q3-5-6","title":"","text":"He then describes His book, the Criterion, as containing what is decisive and clearly explained, and what is ambiguous, known only to God and to those firmly grounded among the people of gnosis, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-5-6-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-7-9","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge 3:7–9","anchor":"unit-q3-7-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-1","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"هُوَ الَّذِي أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ مِنْهُ آياتٌ مُحْكَماتٌ هُنَّ أُمُّ الْكِتابِ وَأُخَرُ مُتَشابِهاتٌ فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ زَيْغٌ فَيَتَّبِعُونَ ما تَشابَهَ مِنْهُ ابْتِغاءَ الْفِتْنَةِ وَابْتِغاءَ تَأْوِيلِهِ وَما يَعْلَمُ تَأْوِيلَهُ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَالرَّاسِخُونَ فِي الْعِلْمِ يَقُولُونَ آمَنَّا بِهِ كُلٌّ مِنْ عِنْدِ رَبِّنا وَما يَذَّكَّرُ إِلاَّ أُولُوا الْأَلْبابِ (7) رَبَّنا لا تُزِغْ قُلُوبَنا بَعْدَ إِذْ هَدَيْتَنا وَهَبْ لَنا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ (8) رَبَّنا إِنَّكَ جامِعُ النَّاسِ لِيَوْمٍ لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُخْلِفُ الْمِيعادَ (9)","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-2","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"قلت: (منه) : خبر مقدم، و (آيات) : مبتدأ، فيوقف على (الكتاب) ، وقيل: (منه) : نعت لكتاب، وهو بعيد.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-3","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"قال ابن السبكي: المحكَم: المتضح المعنى، والمتشابه: ما استأثر الله بعلمه، وقد يُطْلعُ عليه بعضَ أصفيائه.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-4","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"و (هن أم الكتاب) : جملة، وحق الخبر المطابقة فيقول: أمهات، وإنما أفرده على تأويل كل واحدة، أو على أن الكل بمنزلة آية واحدة. والزيغ: الميل عن الحق. و (الراسخون في العلم) : معطوف على (الله) ، أو مبتدأ إن فسر المتشابه بما استأثر الله بعلمه، كمدة بقاء الدنيا ووقت قيام الساعة، أو بما دلّ القاطع على أن ظاهره غير مراد. قاله البيضاوي. و (إذ هديتنا) : ظرف مجرور بالإضافة مسبوك بالمصدر، أي: بعد هدايتك إيانا.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-5","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إن الذي انفرد بالوحدانية والقيومية، ولا يخفى عليه شيء في العالم العلوي والسفلي هُوَ الَّذِي أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ المبين، فمنه ما هو آياتٌ مُحْكَماتٌ واضحات المعنى، لا اشتباه فيها ولا إجمال، هُنَّ أُمُّ الْكِتابِ أي: أصله، يرد إليها غيرها، وَمنه آيات أُخَرُ مُتَشابِهاتٌ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-6","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"محتملات، لا يتضح مقصودها لإجمال أو مخالفة ظاهر إلا بالفحص وجودة الفكر، ليظهر فضل العلماء النُقاد، ويزداد حرصهم على الاجتهاد في تَدبُرها وتحصيل العلوم المتوقف عليها استنباط المراد بها، فينال بها، وبإتعاب القرائح في استخراج معانيها، والتوفيق بينها وبين المحكمات، أعلى الدرجات وأرفع المقامات.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-7","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"قال في نوادر الأصول: لمّا تكلم على المتشابه قسّمه على قسمين منه ما طوى علمه إلاَّ على الخواص كعلم فواتح السور، ومنه ما لم يصل إليه أحد من الرسل فمَنْ دُونَهم، وهو سر القدر لا يستقيم لهم مع العبودية، ولو كُشِفَ لفسدت العبودية، فطواه عن الرّسل والملائكة لأنهم في العبودية، فإذا زالت العبودية احتملوها أي: أسرار القدر. هـ. ولمثل هذا يشير قول سهل: للألوهية سر- لو انكشف لبطلت النبوة، وللنبوة سر- لو انكشف لبطل العِلم، وللعلم سر لو انكشف لبطلت الأحكام. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-8","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"قلت: فَتَحَصَّل أن الكتاب العزيز مشتمل على المحكم والمتشابه. وأما قوله تعالى: كِتابٌ أُحْكِمَتْ آياتُهُ فمعناه: أنها حُفظت من فساد المعنى وركاكة اللفظ، وقوله تعالى: كِتاباً مُتَشابِهاً معناه: أنه يُشبه بعضُه بعضاً في صحة المعنى وجزالة اللفظ.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-9","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"ثم إن الناس في شأن المتشابه على قسمين: فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ زَيْغٌ: أي: شك، أو ميل عن الحق، كالمبتدعة وأشباههم، فَيَتَّبِعُونَ ما تَشابَهَ مِنْهُ، فيتعلقون بظاهره، أو بتأويل باطل، ابْتِغاءَ الْفِتْنَةِ أي: طلباً لفتنة الناس عن دينهم: بالتشكيك والتلبيس، ومناقضة المحكم بالمتشابه، وَابْتِغاءَ تَأْوِيلِهِ على ما يشتهون ليوافق بدعتهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-10","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"روى عن عائشة- رضي الله عنها-: أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم- قرأ هذه الآية فقال: «إِذَا رَأَيتُم الذِينَ يَسألُون عن المتشابه منه، ويجادلون فيه، فهم الذين عَنَا الله تعالى، فاحذروهم، ولا تجالسوهم» .","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-11","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"(وما يعلم تأويله) على الحقيقة (إلا الله) تعالى، وقد يُطلع عليه بعضَ خواص أوليائه، وهم (الراسخون) أي: الثابتون في العلم، وهم العارفون بالله أهل الفناء والبقاء، وهم أهل التوحيد الخاص ... فقد أطلعهم تعالى على أسرار غيبه، فلم يبق عندهم متشابه في الكتاب ولا في السنة، حال كونهم (يقولون آمنا به) ، وصدقنا أنه من كلامه، (كُلّ من عند ربنا) المحكم والمتشابه، وقد فهمنا مراده في القسمين، وهم أولو الألباب، ولذلك مدحهم فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-12","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"(وما يذكر إلا أولوا الألباب) أي: القلوب الصافية من ظلمة الهوى وغَبَش الحس.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-13","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"سئل عليه الصلاة والسلام: مَن الراسخون في العلم؟ فقال: «من برَّ يمينُه، وصدق لسانُه، واستقام قلبُه، وعفَّ بطنُه وفرجه، فذلك الراسخ في العلم» . وقال نافع بن يزيد: الراسخون في العلم: المتواضعون لله، المتذللون في طلب مرضات الله، لا يتعظمون على مَنْ فوقهم، ولا يحقرون من دونهم. هـ. وقيل: الراسخ في العلم: من وجُد فيه أربعة أشياء: التقوى بينه وبين الله، والتواضع بينه وبين الخلق، والزهد بينه وبين الدنيا، والمجاهدة بينه وبين نفسه. هـ. قلت: ويجمع هذه الأوصاف العارف بالله، فهو الراسخ في العلم كما تقدم.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-14","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"ويقولون أيضاً في تضرعهم إلى الله: رَبَّنا لا تُزِغْ قُلُوبَنا عن نهج الحق بالميل إلى اتباع الهوى، بَعْدَ إِذْ هَدَيْتَنا إلى طريق الوصول إلى حضرتك، وَهَبْ لَنا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً تجمع قلوبنا بك، وتضم أرواحنا إلى مشاهدة وحدانيتك، إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ تهب للمؤمل فوق ما يؤمل. رَبَّنا إِنَّكَ جامِعُ النَّاسِ لِيَوْمٍ الجزاء الذي لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ، فاجمعنا مع المقربين إنك لا تخلف الميعاد، فأنجز لنا ما وعدتنا في ذلك اليوم. وخلف الوعد في حقه تعالى مُحال. أما الوعد بالخير فلا إشكال، وأما الوعيد بالشر، فإن كان في مُعَيِّنٍ فلا يخلفه، وإن كان في الجملة فيخلفه بالعفو. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-15","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"وقال في النوادر أيضاً: لَمَّا رَدَّ الراسخون في العلم عِلْمَ المتشابه إلى عالمه، حيث قالوا: آمَنَّا بِهِ كُلٌّ مِنْ عِنْدِ رَبِّنا، خافوا شَرَه النفوس لطلبها فإنَّ العلم لذيذ، وفتنة تلك اللذة لها عتاب، ففزعوا إلى ربهم فقالوا: رَبَّنا لا تُزِغْ قُلُوبَنا بَعْدَ إِذْ هَدَيْتَنا وَهَبْ لَنا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ رَحْمَةً، علموا أن الرحمة تطفئ تلك الفتنة. ولما كان يوم القيامة ينكشف فيه سر القدر حنوا إليه فقالوا: رَبَّنا إِنَّكَ جامِعُ النَّاسِ ... الآية. سكنوا نفوسهم لمجيء ذلك اليوم الذي تَبْطُنِ فيه الحكمة، وتظهر فيه القدرة. هـ. بالمعنى.","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-16","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"الإشارة: إذا صفت القلوب، وسكنت في حضرة علاّم الغيوب، تنزلت عليها الواردات الإلهية والعلوم اللدنية، والمواهب القدسية، فمنها ما تكون محكمات المبنى، واضحات المعنى، ومنها ما تكون مجملة في حال ورودها،","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-17","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"وبعد الوعي يكون البيان، فَإِذا قَرَأْناهُ فَاتَّبِعْ قُرْآنَهُ ثُمَّ إِنَّ عَلَيْنا بَيانَهُ","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-18","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":". وقد تكون خارجة عن مدارك العقول. فأما أهل الزيغ والانتقاد فيتبعون المتشابه من تلك الواردات، ابتغاء فتنة العامة، وصرفهم عن طريق الخاصة، وابتغاء تأويله، ليقيم عليه حجة الشريعة، (وما يعلم تأويله إلا الله) ، أو من تحقق فناؤه في الله، وهم الراسخون في معرفة الله، يقولون: (آمنا به كل من عند ربنا) إذ القلوب المطهرة من الهوى لا تنطق عن الهوى، وهم أرباب القلوب يقولون: (ربنا لا تزغ قلوبنا) عن حضرة قدسك (بعد إذ هديتنا) إلى الوصول إليها، (وهب لنا من لدنك رحمة) تعصمنا من النظر إلى سواك، (إنك أنت الوهاب) ربنا إنك جامع الناس. وهم السائرون إليك ليوم لا ريب في الوصول إليه، وهو يوم اللقاء، (إنَّكَ لا تُخْلفُ المِيعادَ) فاجمع بيننا وبينك، وحل بيننا وبين من يقطعنا عنك (إِنك على كل شيءٍ قدير) .","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-7-9-19","r":"q3-7-9","title":"3:7–9 · The decisive, the ambiguous and those firmly grounded in knowledge","text":"ثم هدد أهل الزيغ والفساد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-7-9-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-7-9-s1","r":"q3-7-9","title":"Where the sentence ends","text":"I say: “In it” ( منه ) is a preceding predicate ( خبر مقدم ), and “verses” is the subject ( مبتدأ ); one therefore pauses at “the Book.” It has also been said that “in it” qualifies “a book,” but that is remote. Ibn al-Subkī says: “The decisive ( المحكم ) is that whose meaning is clear; the ambiguous ( المتشابه ) is that whose knowledge God reserves to Himself, although He may acquaint some of His chosen ones with it.” [A006] “They are the foundation of the Book” is a sentence. Normally the predicate should agree in number, giving “foundations” ( أمهات ). It is singular here either with the sense “each one [is a foundation],” or because the whole is treated as one verse. Zaygh ( الزيغ ) is deviation from truth. “Those firmly grounded in knowledge” ( الراسخون في العلم ) is coordinated with “God”; or it begins a new sentence, if the ambiguous is understood as that whose knowledge God reserves to Himself, such as how long the world will endure and when the Hour will arise, or that whose apparent meaning decisive proof shows not to be intended. So says al-Bayḍāwī. “When You guided us” ( إذ هديتنا ) is an adverbial expression in the genitive through annexation, construed as a verbal noun: “after Your guidance of us.” [A007]","anchor":"en-q3-7-9-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-7-9-s2","r":"q3-7-9","title":"The labour and rank of interpretation","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the One who alone possesses oneness and self-subsistence, from whom nothing in the higher or lower world is hidden, “is He who sent down upon you the clear Book.” Some of it consists of “decisive verses,” clear in meaning, without ambiguity or indeterminacy. “They are the foundation of the Book”: its root, to which the rest is referred. Some consists of “other ambiguous verses,” admitting possibilities: their intent is not clear, because of indeterminacy or an apparently conflicting sense, without examination and sound reflection. This is so that the excellence of discerning scholars may appear, and their eagerness to exert themselves in pondering these verses and acquiring the sciences necessary to derive their intent may increase. Through this, through tiring their minds in extracting their meanings and reconciling them with the decisive verses, they attain the highest degrees and loftiest stations. In Nawādir al-uṣūl , in discussing the ambiguous, its author divides it into two kinds. One is that whose knowledge is withheld except from the elect, such as the knowledge of the sūrahs’ opening letters. The other is that which none of the messengers, nor anyone beneath them, has attained: the mystery of predestination ( سر القدر ). This is not compatible with their servanthood: were it unveiled, servanthood would be impaired. He therefore concealed it from the messengers and angels, since they are in servanthood. When servanthood passes away, they will be able to bear it—that is, the mysteries of predestination. End of quotation. [A008] Sahl’s saying points to something of this kind: “Divinity has a mystery which, if disclosed, would nullify prophethood; prophethood has a mystery which, if disclosed, would nullify knowledge; and knowledge has a mystery which, if disclosed, would nullify the rulings.” End of quotation. I say: it follows that the Mighty Book contains the decisive and the ambiguous. As for His words, “A Book whose verses have been made firm” [11:1], they mean that the verses are preserved from corrupt meaning and feeble expression. His words “a mutually resembling Book” [39:23] mean that its parts resemble one another in soundness of meaning and strength of expression.","anchor":"en-q3-7-9-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-7-9-s3","r":"q3-7-9","title":"Deviation and steadfast understanding","text":"People’s relation to the ambiguous is of two kinds. “Those in whose hearts is deviation”—doubt or a turning from truth, such as innovators and their like—“follow what is ambiguous in it.” They attach themselves to its apparent sense, or to a false interpretation, “seeking discord”: seeking to turn people from their religion through doubt and deception, setting the ambiguous against the decisive. And “seeking its interpretation” according to their desires, so that it agrees with their innovation. It is related from ʿĀʾisha—God be pleased with her—that the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, recited this verse and said: “When you see those who ask about what is ambiguous in it and dispute concerning it, they are those whom God meant. Beware of them, and do not sit with them.” [A009] “None knows its interpretation” in reality “but God,” exalted is He. Yet He may acquaint some of His specially chosen friends with it: they are “those firmly grounded,” established “in knowledge,” the gnostics of God, the people of effacement and subsistence ( الفناء والبقاء ), the people of the distinctive realization of unity. He has acquainted them with the mysteries of His unseen, so that nothing ambiguous remains for them in the Book or the Sunna. They say, “We believe in it,” affirming that it is His speech. “All is from our Lord,” decisive and ambiguous alike, and we have understood His intention in both. These are those possessed of understanding, whom He praises by saying, “None takes heed but those possessed of understanding”: hearts purified of the darkness of desire and the haze of sense-perception. [A010] The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, was asked who the firmly grounded in knowledge were. He replied: “One whose oath proves true, whose tongue is truthful, whose heart is upright, and whose belly and private parts are chaste: that is one firmly grounded in knowledge.” [A011] Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd said: “Those firmly grounded in knowledge are those humble before God, abasing themselves in seeking God’s good pleasure. They do not exalt themselves against those above them, nor despise those beneath them.” End of quotation. It has also been said: one firmly grounded in knowledge is one in whom four things are found—godfearingness between himself and God, humility between himself and creatures, renunciation between himself and the world, and struggle between himself and his lower self. End of quotation. I say: the gnostic of God unites these qualities; he is therefore the one firmly grounded in knowledge, as stated above.","anchor":"en-q3-7-9-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-7-9-s4","r":"q3-7-9","title":"Mercy, steadfastness and the promised gathering","text":"In their supplication to God they also say: “Our Lord, do not cause our hearts to deviate” from the way of truth by inclining to follow desire, “after You have guided us” to the path of arrival in Your Presence. “Grant us mercy from Your presence,” gathering our hearts through You and joining our spirits to the witnessing of Your oneness. “You are indeed the Bestower”: You give the hopeful more than he hopes. “Our Lord, You will gather humankind for a day” of recompense “of which there is no doubt.” Gather us, then, with those brought near, for You “do not fail the promise.” Fulfil for us what You have promised on that day. Failure to fulfil a promise is impossible for Him, exalted is He. There is no difficulty concerning the promise of good. As for a threat of evil, if it concerns a specified individual, He does not fail to fulfil it; if it is general, He may forgo it through pardon. And God, exalted is He, knows best. [A012] The Nawādir also says: when those firmly grounded in knowledge referred knowledge of the ambiguous to the One who knows it, saying, “We believe in it; all is from our Lord,” they feared the souls’ avid appetite for seeking it. Knowledge is pleasurable, and the temptation of that pleasure incurs reproach. They therefore fled to their Lord, saying, “Our Lord, do not cause our hearts to deviate after You have guided us. Grant us mercy from Your presence,” knowing that mercy extinguishes that temptation. Since the mystery of predestination will be unveiled on the Day of Resurrection, they yearned towards it, saying, “Our Lord, You will gather humankind ….” They quieted their souls in expectation of that day, when wisdom will be inwardly concealed and power outwardly manifest. End of the passage, rendered in sense.","anchor":"en-q3-7-9-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-7-9-s5","r":"q3-7-9","title":"The understanding of inward visitations","text":"When hearts become pure and repose in the Presence of the Knower of unseen things, divine visitations ( الواردات الإلهية ), divinely bestowed sciences and holy gifts descend upon them. Some are decisive in construction and clear in meaning; others are indeterminate when first received, and clarification follows their assimilation: “When We recite it, follow its recitation; then its explanation rests upon Us” [75:18–19]. They may also lie beyond the intellects’ powers of apprehension. Those disposed to deviation and criticism follow what is ambiguous in these visitations, seeking to disturb ordinary people and turn them from the way of the elect, and seeking its interpretation in order to establish the Sacred Law’s case against it. “None knows its interpretation but God,” or one whose effacement in God has been realized: these are those firmly grounded in the knowledge of God. They say, “We believe in it; all is from our Lord,” for hearts purified of desire do not speak from desire. These are the masters of hearts. They say: “Our Lord, do not cause our hearts to deviate” from Your holy Presence “after You have guided us” to arrival there. “Grant us mercy from Your presence” to protect us from looking towards other than You. “You are indeed the Bestower.” [A010] “Our Lord, You will gather humankind”—those journeying towards You—“for a day” whose attainment admits no doubt: the day of meeting. “You do not fail the promise.” Join us to You, then, and interpose between us and whatever cuts us off from You. “You have power over all things.”","anchor":"en-q3-7-9-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-7-9-s6","r":"q3-7-9","title":"","text":"He then threatens the people of deviation and corruption, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-7-9-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-10-11","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace 3:10–11","anchor":"unit-q3-10-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-1","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَنْ تُغْنِيَ عَنْهُمْ أَمْوالُهُمْ وَلا أَوْلادُهُمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ شَيْئاً وَأُولئِكَ هُمْ وَقُودُ النَّارِ (10) كَدَأْبِ آلِ فِرْعَوْنَ وَالَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ كَذَّبُوا بِآياتِنا فَأَخَذَهُمُ اللَّهُ بِذُنُوبِهِمْ وَاللَّهُ شَدِيدُ الْعِقابِ (11)","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-2","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"قلت: (الوقود) بالفتح: الحطب، وبالضم: المصدر، (كدأب آل فرعون) خبر، أي: دأبهم كدأب آل فرعون.","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-3","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"والدأب: مصدر دأب، إذا دام، ثم نقل إلى الشأن والعادة، و (كذبوا) : حال بإضمار «قد» ، أو مستأنف، تفسير حالهم، أو خبر إن ابتدأت بالذين من قبلهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-4","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بما أنزلته، على نبينا محمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، إذا عاينوا العذاب لَنْ تُغْنِيَ عَنْهُمْ أَمْوالُهُمْ وَلا أَوْلادُهُمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ، أي: بدلاً من رحمته أو طاعته، أو بدلاً من عذابه، شَيْئاً، وأولئك هم حطب جهنم، فشأنهم كشأن آلِ فِرْعَوْنَ وَالَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ، قد كَذَّبُوا بِآياتِنا فَأَخَذَهُمُ اللَّهُ بِذُنُوبِهِمْ أي: أهلكهم، وشدد العقوبة عليهم، وَاللَّهُ شَدِيدُ الْعِقابِ لمن أعرض عنه وركن إلى غيره.","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-5","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"الإشارة: كل من جحد أهل الخصوصية، وفاته حظه من مشاهدة عظمة الربوبية، حتى حصل له الطرد والبعاد، وفاته مرافقة أهل المحبة والوداد، لن تغني عنه- بدلاً مما فاته- أموالُ ولا أولاد، واتصلت به الأحزان والأنكاد كما قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-6","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"مَنْ فَاتَه منكَ وصلٌ حَظُّه الندمُ ... ومَنْ تَكُنْ هَمِّه تَسْمُو به الهممُ","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-7","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"وقال آخر:","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-8","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"مَنْ فاتَهُ طَلَبُ الوُصُولِ وَنَيْلُهُ ... مِنْه، فقُلْ: ما الذِي هُوَ يَطلُبُ!","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-9","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"حَسْبُ المحِبِّ فناؤه عما سِوى ... مَحْبوبِهِ إنْ حاضِرٌ وَمُغَيَّبُ","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-10","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"وقال آخر:","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-11","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"لكل شيء إذا فارقْتَهُ عِوَضٌ ... وَلَيْسَ لله إنْ فارقْتَ مِنْ عَوِضِ","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-12","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"وفي الحكم: «ماذا وَجَدَ مَنْ فقدك؟ وما الذي فَقَدَ مَنْ وَجَدَك؟ لقد خاب مَنْ رَضِي دونك بدلاً، ولقد خسر من بغى عنك مُتحولاً» . فكل مَن وقف مع شيء من السِّوى، وفاته التوجه إلى معرفة المولى، فهو في نار القطيعة والهوى، مع النفوس الفرعونية، وأهل الهمم الدنية. نسأل الله تعالى العافية.","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-10-11-13","r":"q3-10-11","title":"3:10–11 · What wealth cannot replace","text":"ثم بدأ بعتاب اليهود، بعد أن قرر شأن كتابه العزيز وما اشتمل عليه من المحكم والمتشابه، توطئة للكلام معهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-10-11-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-10-11-s1","r":"q3-10-11","title":"Fuel and habitual conduct","text":"I say: waqūd ( الوقود ), with fatḥa, means firewood; with ḍamma, wuqūd, it is the verbal noun. “Like the way of Pharaoh’s people” is a predicate: their way is like that of Pharaoh’s people. Daʾb ( الدأب ) is the verbal noun of daʾaba, “to persist”; it was then transferred to mean one’s condition and habitual practice. “They denied” is either a circumstantial clause ( حال ), with qad understood, a fresh statement explaining their condition, or a predicate if “those before them” begins a new sentence.","anchor":"en-q3-10-11-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-10-11-s2","r":"q3-10-11","title":"Neither wealth nor children can ransom them","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Those who disbelieve” in what I have sent down upon our Prophet Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him—when they behold punishment, “their wealth and their children will avail them nothing” in place of God’s mercy or obedience to Him, or instead of His punishment. They are the firewood of Hell. Their condition is like that of Pharaoh’s people and those before them: “they denied Our signs, so God seized them for their sins,” destroying them and intensifying their punishment. “God is severe in punishment” towards whoever turns away from Him and relies on another.","anchor":"en-q3-10-11-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-10-11-s3","r":"q3-10-11","title":"No substitute for the Beloved","text":"Whoever rejects the people of spiritual election ( أهل الخصوصية ), losing his share in witnessing the grandeur of lordship, so that he suffers expulsion and remoteness and misses the companionship of the people of love and affection—neither wealth nor children will replace what he has lost. Sorrows and troubles adhere to him. As the poet says: Whoever misses communion with You has regret for his portion; whoever makes You his concern is raised by his aspirations. Another says: One who has missed seeking arrival and attaining it from Him—tell me, what is he seeking? It is enough for the lover to be effaced from all besides his Beloved, whether present or absent. And another: Everything you part with has a substitute; but part from God, and there is no substitute for Him. In the Ḥikam : “What has one found who has lost You? What has one lost who has found You? Disappointed indeed is one content with another as a substitute for You; at a loss indeed is one who seeks to turn away from You.” Everyone who stops with anything other than Him, failing to direct himself towards knowledge of the Master, is in the fire of estrangement and desire, with pharaonic souls and people of low aspiration. We ask God, exalted is He, for well-being.","anchor":"en-q3-10-11-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-10-11-s4","r":"q3-10-11","title":"","text":"He then begins reproaching the Jews, having set forth the nature of His Mighty Book and its decisive and ambiguous contents in preparation for addressing them, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-10-11-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-12-13","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory 3:12–13","anchor":"unit-q3-12-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-1","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"قُلْ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا سَتُغْلَبُونَ وَتُحْشَرُونَ إِلى جَهَنَّمَ وَبِئْسَ الْمِهادُ (12) قَدْ كانَ لَكُمْ آيَةٌ فِي فِئَتَيْنِ الْتَقَتا فِئَةٌ تُقاتِلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَأُخْرى كافِرَةٌ يَرَوْنَهُمْ مِثْلَيْهِمْ رَأْيَ الْعَيْنِ وَاللَّهُ يُؤَيِّدُ بِنَصْرِهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ إِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِأُولِي الْأَبْصارِ (13)","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-2","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"قلت: لمَّا رجع رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم من غزوة بدر غالباً منصوراً بالغنائم والأسارى، جمع اليهود في سوق بني قينقاع، وقال لهم: يا معشر اليهود، اتقوا الله وأسلموا، فإنكم تعلمون أني رسولُ الله حقا، واحذروا أن يُنزل الله بكم من نقمته ما أنزل على قريش يوم بدر، فقالوا: يا محمد، لا يغرّنّك أنك لقيت أغماراً لا علم لهم بالحرب، لئن قاتلتنا لتعلَمنَّ أنَّا نحن الناس. فأنزل الله فيهم هذه الآية.","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-3","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا من بني إسرائيل، أو مطلقاً: سَتُغْلَبُونَ إن قاتلتم المسلمين، وَتُحْشَرُونَ بعد الموت والهزيمة إِلى جَهَنَّمَ وَبِئْسَ الْمِهادُ ما مهدتم لأنفسكم من العذاب، وقد صدق وعده بقتل قريظة، وإجلاء بني النضير، وفتح خيبر، وضرب الجزية على من عداهم. فقد غُلِبوا أينما ثُقفوا، وحشروا إلى جهنم، إلا من أسلم منهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-4","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"ثم ندبهم للاعتبار بما وقع من النصر للمسلمين يوم بدر فقال لهم: قَدْ كانَ لَكُمْ يا معشر اليهود، آيَةٌ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-5","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"عبرة ظاهرة، ودلالة على صدق ما أقول لكم: إنكم ستغلبون، فِي فِئَتَيْنِ أي: جماعتين الْتَقَتا يوم بدر، وهم","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-6","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"المسلمون، وكانوا ثلاثمائة وأربعة عشر، والمشركون كانوا زهاء ألف، فِئَةٌ تُقاتِلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وهم المؤمنون، وَأُخْرى كافِرَةٌ، وهم المشركون، ترونهم مثليهم أي: ترون، يا معشر اليهود، الكفارَ مثلي عدد المسلمين رأي تحقيق، ومع ذلك أيدهم الله بالنصر والمدد حتى نصرهم على عدوهم، وكذلك يفعل بهم معكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-7","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"والرؤية، على هذا، علمية. ومن قرأ (بالياء) يكون الضمير راجعاً للكفار، أي: يرى الكفارُ المسلمين مثليهم، وذلك بعد أن قللهم الله في أعينهم حتى اجترءوا عليهم، وتوجهوا إليهم، فلما لاقوهم كثروا في أعينهم حتى غلبوا، مدداً من الله للمؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-8","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"أو: يرى المؤمنون المشركين مثلي المؤمنين، وكانوا ثلاثة أمثالهم، ليثبتوا لهم، ويتيقنوا بالنصر الذي وعدهم الله بقوله: إِنْ يَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ عِشْرُونَ صابِرُونَ يَغْلِبُوا مِائَتَيْنِ ... الآية. وَاللَّهُ يُؤَيِّدُ أي: يقوي بِنَصْرِهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ نصره، كما أيد أهل بدر، إِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِأُولِي الْأَبْصارِ المفتوحة. وذلك حين نصر الله قوماً لا عدد لهم ولا عدة، على قوم لهم عدد وعدة، فلم تغن عنهم من الله شيئاً.","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-9","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"الإشارة: إذا توجه القلب إلى مولاه تعرض له جندان، أحدهما: جند الأنوار، وهو جند القلب، والثاني: جند الأغيار، وهو جند النفس، فيلتحم بينهما القتال، فجند الأنوار يريد أن يرتقي بالروح إلى وطنها وهو حضرة الأسرار، وجند الأغيار يريد أن يهبط بالنفس إلى أرض الحظوظ والشهوات، فيحبسها في سجن الأكوان، فإذا أراد الله تعالى سعادة عبد، قوي له جند الأنوار، وضَعَّفَ عنه جند الأغيار، فينهزم عنه جند الأغيار، ويستولي على قلبه جند الأنوار، فلا تزال الأنوار تتوارد عليه حتى تشرق عليه أنوار المواجهة، فيدخل حضرة الأسرار، وهي حضرة الشهود، ويتحصن في جوار الملك الودود، وتناديه ألسنة الهواتف: أيها العارف، قل للذين كفروا، وهم جند الأغيار: ستغلبون وتحشرون إلى جهنم وبئس المهاد. وإذا أراد الله خذلان عبده، بعدله، قطع عنه مدد الأنوار، وقوي لديه جند الأغيار، فتستولي ظلمة النفس على نور القلب، فتحبسه في سجن الأكوان، وتسجنه في ظلمة هيكل الإنسان، (والله يويد بنصره من يشاء) . ففي التقاء جندي الأنوار والأغيار عبرة لأولى الأبصار.","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-12-13-10","r":"q3-12-13","title":"3:12–13 · Two armies and the sign of victory","text":"ثم بين الحق تعالى مدد جند الأغيار، والذي منع الأبصار من الاعتبار، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-12-13-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-12-13-s1","r":"q3-12-13","title":"The address at the market of Banū Qaynuqāʿ","text":"I say: when the Messenger of God, blessings and peace be upon him, returned from Badr victorious and helped, with spoils and prisoners, he gathered the Jews in the market of Banū Qaynuqāʿ. He said: “Jews, fear God and embrace Islam. You know that I am truly God’s Messenger. Beware lest God bring down upon you the requital He brought upon Quraysh at Badr.” They said: “Muḥammad, do not be deceived because you encountered inexperienced men with no knowledge of war. If you fight us, you will certainly learn that we are the men.” God then revealed this verse concerning them. [A013]","anchor":"en-q3-12-13-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-12-13-s2","r":"q3-12-13","title":"The perceived numbers at Badr","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Say,” Muḥammad, “to those who disbelieve,” among the Children of Israel or generally: “You will be overcome” if you fight the Muslims, “and gathered,” after death and defeat, “into Hell—an evil resting-place”: the punishment you have prepared for yourselves. His promise was fulfilled through the killing of Qurayẓa, the expulsion of Banū l-Naḍīr, the conquest of Khaybar, and the imposition of jizya upon the others. They were overcome wherever encountered and gathered into Hell, except those among them who embraced Islam. [A014] He then urges them to take a lesson from the Muslims’ victory at Badr: “You,” Jews, “have already had a sign”—a manifest lesson and indication of the truth of My saying that you will be overcome—“in two companies” that met on the day of Badr. These were the Muslims, numbering three hundred and fourteen, and the idolaters, numbering about a thousand. “One company fighting in God’s way” was the believers, “and another unbelieving” was the idolaters. In the reading with tāʾ, “you see them as twice their number,” you Jews see the unbelievers as twice the Muslims’ number, with certain perception. Nevertheless God strengthened the Muslims with victory and reinforcement until He made them prevail over their enemy. He will do the same for them against you. On this interpretation, “seeing” means knowing. [A015] In the reading with yāʾ, the pronoun may refer to the unbelievers: the unbelievers saw the Muslims as twice their own number. This occurred after God had made the Muslims appear few in their eyes, so that they dared to advance upon them. When they met them, however, the Muslims appeared numerous in their eyes until they were defeated: this was reinforcement from God for the believers. Alternatively, the believers saw the idolaters as twice the believers’ number, though they were three times as many, so that they might stand firm against them and be certain of the victory God had promised in His words, “If there are twenty steadfast among you, they will overcome two hundred …” [8:65]. “God strengthens”—fortifies—“with His help whom He wills” to help, as He strengthened the people of Badr. “In that is surely a lesson for those possessed of sight,” whose eyes are open: God helped a people with neither numbers nor equipment against a people possessing both, neither of which availed them anything against God.","anchor":"en-q3-12-13-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-12-13-s3","r":"q3-12-13","title":"The armies of light and otherness","text":"When the heart turns towards its Master, two armies present themselves to it: the army of lights ( جند الأنوار ), which is the heart’s army, and the army of otherness ( جند الأغيار ), which is the lower self’s army. Battle joins between them. The army of lights seeks to raise the spirit to its homeland, the Presence of mysteries; the army of otherness seeks to bring the lower self down to the earth of pleasures and appetites and confine it in the prison of created things. When God wills a servant’s happiness, He strengthens for him the army of lights and weakens the army of otherness. The latter is routed and the army of lights takes possession of his heart. Lights continue to descend upon him until the lights of face-to-face encounter shine upon him. He enters the Presence of mysteries—the Presence of witnessing—and finds protection in the neighbourhood of the Loving King. The voices of unseen callers address him: “Gnostic, say to those who disbelieve”—the army of otherness—“You will be overcome and gathered into Hell—an evil resting-place!” When God wills, in His justice, to abandon a servant to himself, He cuts off the reinforcement of lights and strengthens before him the army of otherness. The darkness of the lower self overcomes the heart’s light, confining it in the prison of created things and imprisoning it in the darkness of the human frame. “God strengthens with His help whom He wills.” Thus the meeting of the armies of light and otherness contains a lesson for those possessed of sight.","anchor":"en-q3-12-13-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-12-13-s4","r":"q3-12-13","title":"","text":"The Real, exalted is He, then explains the reinforcement of the army of otherness, which prevents eyes from taking heed, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-12-13-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-14","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit 3:14","anchor":"unit-q3-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-1","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"زُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ الشَّهَواتِ مِنَ النِّساءِ وَالْبَنِينَ وَالْقَناطِيرِ الْمُقَنْطَرَةِ مِنَ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ وَالْخَيْلِ الْمُسَوَّمَةِ وَالْأَنْعامِ وَالْحَرْثِ ذلِكَ مَتاعُ الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا وَاللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ حُسْنُ الْمَآبِ (14)","anchor":"ar-q3-14-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-2","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"قلت: (زُين) : بحذف الفاعل، وهو الله، حقيقة إذ لا فاعل سواه، أو الشيطان، شَريعَةً إذ هو منديل لمسح أوساخ الأقذار. والقنطار: المال الكثير، وقيل: مائة ألف دينار، وقيل: ملء مسك الثور. وروى عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أنه قال: «القنطار: ألف دينار» ، وفي رواية: «ألفا دينار» ، وفي عرفنا اليوم: ألف مثقال.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-3","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"والمقنطرة: المنضدة بعضها فوق بعض، وسمي الذهب ذهباً لذهابه وفنائه، أو لذهابه بالقلوب عن حضرة الغيوب، وسميت الفضة فضة لأنها تَنْفَضُّ أي: تنفرق، أو تفرق القلوب لمن اشتغل بها. والمسوَّمة: المعلمة أو الراعية أو المطهمة الحسان.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-4","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: زُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ الشَّهَواتِ والركون إلى المألوفات، حتى صرفهم ذلك عن النظر والاعتبار، أو الشهود والاستبصار، وذلك لمن وقف مع متعتها، وغرته شهوة لذتها، وأما من ذكرته نعيم الجنان، وأعانته على طاعة الملك الديان، فلم يقف مع متعتها، ولا التفت إلى عاجل شهوتها، بل نزل إليها بالإذن والتمكين، والرسوخ في اليقين، فلا يشمله تحذير الآية لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «حبب إلي من دنياكم ثلاث ... » الحديث.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-5","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"وقال بعض الأولياء: [كل شهوة تحجب القلب عن الله، إلا شهوة الجماع] يعني الحلال، وقال الورتجبي:","anchor":"ar-q3-14-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-6","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"ابتلاهم حتى يظهر الصادق بترك هذه الشهوات، من الكاذب بالشروع في طلبها، قيل: من اشتغل بهذه الأشياء قطعته عن طريق الحق، ومن استصغرها وأعرض عنها، عوض عليها السلامة منها، وفتح له الطريق إلى الحقائق. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-7","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"ثم بدأ برأس الشهوات فقال: مِنَ النِّساءِ وذلك لمن شُغف بهن فصرف عن ذكر الله، أو تناولهن على وجه الحرام. وفي الخبر عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «مَا تَرَكْتُ في الناس بَعْدِي فِتْنَةً أَضَرُّ عَلَى الرِّجَالِ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-14-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-8","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"وفي خبر آخر: «النظر إلى محاسن المرأة من سهام إبليس» . ومَنْ ثَمَّ جُعِلْنَ في القرآن عين الشهوات، قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-14-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-9","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"زُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ الشَّهَواتِ مِنَ النِّساءِ.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-10","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"وقال بعض العارفين: ما أيس الشيطانُ من إنسان قط إلا أتاه من قبل النساء. وقال على رضى الله عنه: أيها الناس، لا تطيعوا للنساء أمراً، ولا تَدَعُوهُنَّ يدبرن أمر عيش، فإنهن إن تُرِكْنَ وما يُرِدْن أفسدن الملك، وعصَين المالك، وجدناهن لا دين لهن في خلَواتهن، ولا ورع لهن عند شهواتهن، اللذة بهن يسيرة، والحيرة بهن كثيرة، فأما صوالحهن ففاجرات، وأما طوالحهن فعاهرات- أي: زانيات-، وأما المعصومات فهن المعدومات، يتظلمن وهن","anchor":"ar-q3-14-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-11","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"الظالمات، ويتمنعن وهن الراغبات، ويحلفن وهن الكاذبات، فاستعيذوا بالله من شرارهن، وكونوا على وجل من خيارهن، والسلام(1). هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-12","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"وَالْبَنِينَ: قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «إنهم لثمرة القلوب، وقُرَّةُ الأعيُن، وإنهم مع ذلك لَمَجْبَنَةٌ مَبْخَلَةٌ مَحْزَنَةٌ» . وَالْقَناطِيرِ الْمُقَنْطَرَةِ: أي: المجموعة المنضدة، مِنَ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ. وَالْخَيْلِ الْمُسَوَّمَةِ أي: المعلمة: وهي البلق، أو غيرها، وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «الخَيْلُ معقودٌ في نَواصِيها الخير إلى يوم القِيَامةِ، الأجرُ والمَغْنمُ» . وعن أنس قال: (لم يكن شيء أحب إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بعد النساء، من الخيل) . وعن أبي وهب الجشمي قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «ارتبطوا الخيل، وامسحوا بنواصيها، وقَلِّدُوها، ولا تقلدوها الأوتار، وعليكم بكل كُمَيْت(2) أغر مُحَجِّلِ، أو أشقر أغر محجل، أو أدهم أغر محجّل» . وعن خباب رضي الله عنه قال: قال رسول الله صلّى الله عليه وسلم:","anchor":"ar-q3-14-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-13","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"«الخيل ثلاثة: فرس للرحمن، وفرس للإنسان، وفرس للشيطان، فأما فرس الرحمن فما اتخذ لله في سبيل الله، وقوتل عليه أعداء الله، وأما فرس الإنسان فما استطرق عليه- أي: ركب عليه في طريق حوائجه، وأما فرس الشيطان فما روهن عليه، وقومر عليه» . وفي البخاري ما يشهد لهذا.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-14","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"ومما زُيِّن للناس أيضاً: حب الْأَنْعامِ، وهي الإبل والبقر والغنم، إن شغلته عن ذكر الله، ومنع منها حق الله، وَالْحَرْثِ أي: الزراعة والغراسة، ذلِكَ الذي ذكرت مَتاعُ الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا الفانية الزائلة، وَاللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ حُسْنُ الْمَآبِ، أي: المرجع في دار البقاء التي لا يفنى نعيمها، ولا تنقطع حياتها إلى أبد الأبد.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-15","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"الإشارة: كل ما يقطع القلبّ عن الشهود، أوُ يُفَتِّرُهُ عن السير إلى الملك المعبود، فهو شهوة، كائناً ما كان، أغياراً أو أنواراً، أو علوماً أو أحوالاً، أو غير ذلك، فالنساء الأغيار، والبنون الأنوار، والقناطير المقنطرة من الذهب علوم الطريقة، والفضة علوم الشريعة، والخيل المسومة هي الأحوال، والأنعام الأذكار، والحرث استعمال الفكرة.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-16","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"فكل مَنْ وقف مع حلاوة شيء من هذا، ولم يُفْضِ إلى راحة الشهود والعيان، فهي في حقه شهوة.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-17","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"وبعد أن ذكر الحق تعالى أنواعاً من الشهوات، زَهَّدَ فيها فقال: ذلِكَ مَتاعُ الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا وَاللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ حُسْنُ الْمَآبِ قال أبو هاشم الزاهد رضي الله عنه: وَسَمَ اللهُ الدنيا بالوحشة ليكون أنس المريد بربه دونها، وليقبل المطيعون بالإعراض عنها، وأهلُ المعرفة بالله من الدنيا مستوحشون، وإلى الله مشتاقون. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-18","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"وقد تعوذ النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم من شر فتنتها، غناها وفقرها. وأكثرُ القرآن مشتملٌ على ذمها، وتحذير الخلق منها، بل ما من داع يدعو إلى الله تعالى إلا وقد حذر منها، ورغَّب في الآخرة، بل هو المقصود بالذات من بيان الشرائع، وكيف لا- وهي عدوة الله لقطعها طريق الوصلة إليه، ولذلك لم ينظر إليها منذ خلقها. وعدوة لأوليائه لأنها تزينت بزينتها حتى تجرعوا مرارة الصبر في مقاطعتها، وعدوة لأعدائه لأنها استدرجتهم بمكرها، واقتنصتهم بشبكتها، فوثقوا بها، فخذلتهم أحوج ما كانوا إليها. كفانا الله شرّها بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q3-14-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-14-19","r":"q3-14","title":"3:14 · Desires and their proper limit","text":"ثم نبه الحق تعالى على ما هو المقصود الأهم لمن له عقل وافر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-14-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-14-s1","r":"q3-14","title":"Adornment, wealth and its names","text":"I say: “Adorned” ( زُيّن ) has its agent omitted. In reality ( حقيقة ), the agent is God, for there is no agent but He; according to the Sacred Law ( شريعة ), it is Satan, who serves as the cloth upon which the filth of impurities is wiped. [A016] A qinṭār is abundant wealth. It has been said to be a hundred thousand dinars, or the contents of a bull’s hide. It is related from the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, that he said, “A qinṭār is a thousand dinars”; another version says, “two thousand dinars.” In our usage today it is a thousand mithqāls. [A017] “Heaped-up” ( المقنطرة ) means arranged in piles one above another. Gold is called dhahab ( ذهب ) because it goes away and perishes, or because it carries hearts away from the Presence of unseen things. Silver is called fiḍḍa ( فضة ) because it disperses, or because it disperses the hearts of those occupied with it. “Marked” ( المسوّمة ) means bearing marks, grazing, or finely formed and beautiful. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-12] ]","anchor":"en-q3-14-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-14-s2","r":"q3-14","title":"Desire that distracts, and enjoyment received with permission","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Adorned for humankind is love of desires,” and reliance upon familiar pleasures, until this turns them from reflection and taking heed, or from witnessing and inward perception. This concerns those who stop at their enjoyment and are deceived by the appetite for their pleasure. Those reminded by them of the bliss of the Gardens and helped by them to obey the Requiting King do not stop at their enjoyment or turn towards their immediate pleasure. Rather, they descend to them with permission and firm establishment, grounded in certainty. The verse’s warning does not encompass them, in view of the Prophet’s saying, blessings and peace be upon him, “Three things from your world have been made dear to me ….” [A018] One of God’s friends said: “Every appetite veils the heart from God, except the appetite for intercourse”—meaning lawful intercourse. Al-Wartajbī says: “He tries them so that the truthful one, who leaves these appetites, may be distinguished from the false one, who embarks upon seeking them.” It has been said: whoever occupies himself with these things is cut off by them from the path of the Real. Whoever regards them as small and turns from them receives, in exchange, safety from them, and the way to the realities is opened to him. End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q3-14-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-14-s3","r":"q3-14","title":"Women, children and the danger of attachment","text":"He begins with the foremost of the desires, “women.” This concerns one captivated by them and thereby turned from God’s remembrance, or one who approaches them unlawfully. It is reported from the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him: “I have left after me no temptation more harmful to men than women.” Another report says: “Looking at a woman’s beauties is one of Satan’s arrows.” Thus they are represented in the Qurʾān as the very objects of appetite: “Adorned for humankind is love of desires: women ….” [A019] One of the gnostics said: “Whenever Satan has despaired of a person, he has approached him by way of women.” [A020] ʿAlī—God be pleased with him—is quoted as saying: “People, do not obey women’s commands or let them manage an affair of livelihood. If they are left to do as they wish, they ruin the domain and disobey its master. We have found them without religion in their seclusion and without scruple in their appetites. Pleasure with them is little; perplexity through them is great. Their righteous ones are sinful, their wicked ones promiscuous”—that is, adulteresses—“and those protected from fault are nonexistent. They complain of injustice while being unjust; they withhold themselves while desirous; they swear oaths while lying. Seek God’s protection from their wicked ones, and be apprehensive of their good ones. Peace.” End of quotation. [A021] “And sons”: the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “They are indeed the fruit of hearts and the delight of eyes, yet they are also a cause of cowardice, miserliness and sorrow.” [A022]","anchor":"en-q3-14-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-14-s4","r":"q3-14","title":"Horses, livestock and cultivation","text":"“And heaped-up stores”—collected and piled—“of gold and silver; and marked horses”: those with distinguishing marks, such as piebald horses, or others. It is reported from the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him: “Good is tied to horses’ forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils.” Anas said: “Nothing after women was dearer to the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, than horses.” [A023] Abū Wahb al-Jushamī reports the Prophet’s words: “Keep horses tethered; stroke their forelocks and put neck-bands upon them, but do not neck-band them with bowstrings. Choose a bay with a white forehead and white lower legs, or a chestnut with a white forehead and white lower legs, or a black horse with a white forehead and white lower legs.” Khabbāb—God be pleased with him—reports: “Horses are of three kinds: a horse for the All-Merciful, a horse for a human being, and a horse for Satan. The horse for the All-Merciful is kept for God, in God’s way, and used to fight God’s enemies. The horse for a human being is ridden upon the road”—in going about one’s needs. “The horse for Satan is staked in betting and gambling.” There is material in al-Bukhārī supporting this. [A024] Also adorned for people is love of “livestock”—camels, cattle, sheep and goats—when it occupies them away from God’s remembrance and they withhold God’s due from it; and “cultivated land,” farming and planting. “That” which has been mentioned “is the enjoyment of the life of this world,” perishing and passing away. “With God is the finest place of return”: the abode of permanence, whose bliss does not perish and whose life never ends, for ever and ever.","anchor":"en-q3-14-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-14-s5","r":"q3-14","title":"Even lights and spiritual states can become an appetite","text":"Everything that cuts the heart off from witnessing, or weakens its journey towards the worshipped King, is an appetite ( شهوة ), whatever it may be: otherness or lights, knowledge or states, or anything else. The women are otherness; the sons, lights; the heaped-up stores of gold, the sciences of the Path; silver, the sciences of the Sacred Law; marked horses, spiritual states; livestock, remembrances; and cultivated land, the exercise of contemplation. Whoever stops with the sweetness of any of these and fails to pass into the repose of witnessing and direct vision has made it an appetite for himself. Having mentioned kinds of desire, the Real, exalted is He, encourages detachment from them: “That is the enjoyment of the life of this world; with God is the finest place of return.” Abū Hāshim al-Zāhid—God be pleased with him—said: “God has marked the world with estrangement, so that the disciple’s intimacy may be with his Lord rather than with it, and the obedient may advance by turning away from it. Those who know God feel estranged from the world and long for God.” End of quotation. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, sought refuge from the evil of its trial, both its wealth and its poverty. Most of the Qurʾān contains censure of it and warnings against it. Indeed, every caller to God has warned against it and encouraged desire for the hereafter. This is the principal purpose in explaining the revealed laws. How could it be otherwise? The world is God’s enemy, because it cuts off the way of communion with Him; for that reason He has not looked at it since creating it. [A025] It is the enemy of His friends, adorning itself until they have to swallow the bitterness of patience in breaking with it. It is also the enemy of His enemies: it draws them on by its deception and captures them in its net. They trust it, and it abandons them when they most need it. May God suffice us against its evil through His gracious favour and generosity.","anchor":"en-q3-14-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-14-s6","r":"q3-14","title":"","text":"The Real, exalted is He, then points to the supremely important aim for anyone of ample intelligence, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-14-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-15-17","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them 3:15–17","anchor":"unit-q3-15-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-1","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"قُلْ أَأُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِخَيْرٍ مِنْ ذلِكُمْ لِلَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها وَأَزْواجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ وَرِضْوانٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِالْعِبادِ (15) الَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنا إِنَّنا آمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنا ذُنُوبَنا وَقِنا عَذابَ النَّارِ (16) الصَّابِرِينَ وَالصَّادِقِينَ وَالْقانِتِينَ وَالْمُنْفِقِينَ وَالْمُسْتَغْفِرِينَ بِالْأَسْحارِ (17)","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-2","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"قلت: (للذين) : خبر، و (جنات) : مبتدأ، وهو استئناف لبيان الخيرية، والرضوان فيه لغتان: الضم والكسر، كالعدوان والطغيان، و (الذين يقولون) : بدل من (الذين اتقوا) ، أو خبر عن مضمر، أو منصوب على المدح، أو بدل من العباد، و (الصابرين) وما بعده: نعت الموصول.","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-3","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد: أأخبركم بِخَيْرٍ من الذي ذكرتُ لكم من الشهوات الفانية واللذات الزائلة، وهو ما أعد الله للمتقين عند لقاء ربهم، وهو جَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تحت قصورها الأنهارُ من الماء واللبن والعسل والخمر، خالِدِينَ فِيها، لا كنعيم الدنيا الفاني، ولهم فيها أَزْواجٌ من الحور العين، مطهرات من الحيض والنفاس وسائر المستقذرات، وَرِضْوانٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ الذي هو (أكبر) النعم.","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-4","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"فانظر: كيف ذكر الحق- جل جلاله- أدنى النعيم وأوسطه وأعلاه؟ فأدناه: متاع الدنيا الذي زُين للناس، وأوسطه: نعيم الجنان، وأعلاه: رضي الرحمن. وفي الحديث الصحيح عنه صلى الله عليه وسلم: «يَقُولُ الله تعالى لأهِلْ الْجنَّةِ:","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-5","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"يَا أهْلَ الجَنَّةِ، فيقول أهْلَ الجَنَّةِ: لَبْيكَ رَبَّنَا وَسَعْدَيْكِ، والخير في يديك، فيقول: هَلْ رضِيتُم؟ فيقولون: ما لَنَا لا نَرضى وَقَد أعطيتنا ما لم تُعط أَحَداً مِنْ العالمين، فَيَقُولُ: ألا أعْطِيكُم أَفْضَلَ من ذلك؟ فيقُولون: يا ربنا، وأيُّ شَيء أَفْضَلُ مِنْ ذلك؟ قال: أُحل عليكم رضواني فلا أسخط عليكم أبدا» .","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-6","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِالْعِبادِ لا يخفى عليه شيء من أعمالهم، فيثيب المحسن، ويعاقب المسيء، أو: (بصير) بأحوال المتقين.","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-7","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"الَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنا إِنَّنا آمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنا ذُنُوبَنا وَقِنا عَذابَ النَّارِ. وفي ترتيب السؤال على مجرد الإيمان دليل على أنه كاف في استحقاق المغفرة والاستعداد لها.","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-8","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"ثم وصف المتقين بقوله: الصَّابِرِينَ على أداء الأمر واجتناب النهي، وفي البأساء والضراء وحين البأس، وَالصَّادِقِينَ في أقوالهم وأفعالهم وأحوالهم، فاستوى سرهم وعلانيتهم، وَالْقانِتِينَ أي: المطيعين، وَالْمُنْفِقِينَ أموالهم في سبيل الله، وَالْمُسْتَغْفِرِينَ بِالْأَسْحارِ لأن الدعاء فيها أقرب إلى الإجابة لأن العبادة حينئذٍ أشق، والنفس أصفى، والروح أجمع، وَلاَ سيما للمتهجدين.","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-9","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"قيل: إنهم كانوا يُصلُون إلى السحر، ثم يستغفرون ويدعون، وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: (إِنَّ اللهَ تعالى يقول: إني لأهُمُّ بأهل الأرض عذاباً، فإذا نظرت إلى عُمَّار بيوتي، وإلى المتهجدين، وإلى المتحابين فِيَّ، وإلى المستغفرين بالأسحار، صرفت عنهم العذاب) .","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-10","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"وقال سفيان: إن لله ريحاً يقال لها الصيحة، تهبُّ وقتَ السحر، تحمل الأذكار والاستغفار إلى الملك الجبار.","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-11","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"قال: وبلَغنا أنه إذا كان أول الليل، نادى مناد: ألا ليقم القانتون، فيقومون يُصلون إلى السحَر، فإذا كان وقت السحر، ينادي منادٍ: أين المستغفرون بالأسحار؟ فيستغفر أولئك، ويقوم آخرون، ويُصلون، فيلحقون بهم، فإذا طلع الفجر، نادى مناد: ألا ليقم الغافلون، فيقومون من فرشِهم كالموتى إذا نُشروا من قبورهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-15-17-12","r":"q3-15-17","title":"3:15–17 · The higher gifts and those who seek them","text":"الإشارة: للذين اتقوا شهودَ السّوى عند ربهم جنات المعارف، تجري من تحتها أنهار العلوم، وأصناف الحكم، مطهرة من العلل، منزهة من الخلل، تهب عليهم نسيم الرضوان، تحمل الرَّوُحَ والريحان، مخلدون في نعيم الشهود والعيان، والله بصير بعباده المخلصين، المنزَّهين من العيوب، المبرّئين من درن الذنوب، الصابرين على دوام المجاهدة، والصادقين في طلب المشاهدة، والقانتين لأحكام العبودية، والمنفقين أنفسَهُمْ ومُهَجَهم في طلب مشاهدة أنوار الربوبية، والمستغفرين من شهود الأغيار، وخصوصاً إذا هبّ نسيم الأسحار، فإن كثيراً من العباد والزهاد شغلتهم حلاوة نسيم الأسحار عن مطالعة أسرار الجبار، وهى أسرار التوحيد التي أشار إليها بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-15-17-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-15-17-s1","r":"q3-15-17","title":"The promise and its recipients","text":"I say: “For those” is the predicate, and “gardens” the subject. This begins a new statement explaining the superiority. Riḍwān ( الرضوان ) has two pronunciations, with ḍamma or kasra, like ʿudwān and ṭughyān. “Those who say” is an apposition ( بدل ) to “those who are mindful of God,” a predicate of an understood subject, an accusative of praise ( المدح ), or an apposition to “the servants.” “The steadfast” and what follows qualify the relative expression.","anchor":"en-q3-15-17-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-15-17-s2","r":"q3-15-17","title":"From worldly enjoyment to divine good pleasure","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Say,” Muḥammad, “Shall I tell you of something better” than the perishing desires and passing pleasures I have mentioned? It is what God has prepared for the godfearing when they meet their Lord: “gardens beneath” whose palaces “rivers flow”—water, milk, honey and wine—“abiding there,” unlike the perishing bliss of this world. They have “spouses” from among the wide-eyed maidens, purified of menstruation, childbirth bleeding and all that is repellent, “and good pleasure from God,” the greatest of blessings. Consider how the Real, glorious is His majesty, mentions the lowest, middle and highest bliss. The lowest is worldly enjoyment, adorned for people; the middle, the bliss of the Gardens; the highest, the good pleasure of the All-Merciful. In the sound report from the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him: “God says to the people of the Garden, ‘People of the Garden!’ They answer, ‘At Your service, our Lord, and gladly; good is in Your hands.’ He says, ‘Are you satisfied?’ They say, ‘How should we not be satisfied, when You have given us what You have given none of the worlds?’ He says, ‘Shall I give you something better than that?’ They say, ‘Our Lord, what could be better than that?’ He says, ‘I shall cause My good pleasure to rest upon you, and shall never be angry with you thereafter.’” [A026] “God sees His servants”: none of their deeds is hidden from Him, and He rewards the one who does well and punishes the one who does ill; or He sees the conditions of the godfearing, “those who say, ‘Our Lord, we believe: forgive us our sins and guard us from the punishment of the Fire.’” Basing the request upon faith alone indicates that faith suffices to merit forgiveness and to make one ready for it.","anchor":"en-q3-15-17-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-15-17-s3","r":"q3-15-17","title":"Truthfulness and the hours before dawn","text":"He then describes the godfearing as “the steadfast”: in performing commands, avoiding prohibitions, and bearing deprivation, adversity and the time of battle. “The truthful” in words, deeds and states, whose secret and public life agree. “The devoutly obedient”; “those who spend” their wealth in God’s way; and “those who seek forgiveness before dawn.” Supplication then is nearer to acceptance, because worship at that time is harder, the soul clearer and the spirit more collected, especially for those who keep night vigil. It is said that they used to pray until the time before dawn and then seek forgiveness and supplicate. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is reported to have said: “God, exalted is He, says, ‘I am about to punish the earth’s people; but when I look upon those who frequent My houses, those who keep night vigil, those who love one another for My sake, and those who seek forgiveness before dawn, I turn punishment away from them.’” [A027] Sufyān said: “God has a wind called the Cry, which blows before dawn, carrying remembrance and pleas for forgiveness to the Compelling King.” He said: “We have been told that at the beginning of the night a caller cries, ‘Let the devoutly obedient arise!’ They rise and pray until before dawn. Then a caller cries, ‘Where are those who seek forgiveness before dawn?’ Those people seek forgiveness, and others rise and pray, joining them. When dawn breaks a caller cries, ‘Let the heedless arise!’ They rise from their beds like the dead raised from their graves.” [A027]","anchor":"en-q3-15-17-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-15-17-s4","r":"q3-15-17","title":"The Gardens of recognition","text":"For those who guard against witnessing anything other than God there are, with their Lord, gardens of recognition, beneath which flow rivers of knowledge and varieties of wisdom, purified of defects and free from flaws. The breeze of good pleasure blows upon them, bearing repose and fragrance. They abide in the bliss of witnessing and direct vision. God sees His sincere servants, purified of faults and cleansed of the stain of sins: steadfast in continual struggle, truthful in seeking witnessing, obedient to the rulings of servanthood, expending themselves and their lifeblood in seeking to witness the lights of lordship, and asking forgiveness for witnessing otherness—especially when the breeze before dawn blows. For many worshippers and ascetics have been occupied by the sweetness of that breeze away from contemplating the mysteries of the Compeller: the mysteries of unity to which He points by saying:","anchor":"en-q3-15-17-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-18","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness 3:18","anchor":"unit-q3-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-1","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"شَهِدَ اللَّهُ أَنَّهُ لاَ إِلهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ وَالْمَلائِكَةُ وَأُولُوا الْعِلْمِ قائِماً بِالْقِسْطِ لاَ إِلهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ (18) إِنَّ الدِّينَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ الْإِسْلامُ ...","anchor":"ar-q3-18-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-2","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"قلت: (قائماً) : حال مِن (الله) ، وإنما جاز من بعض المعطوفات لعدم اللبس، كقوله: وَوَهَبْنا لَهُ إِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ نافِلَةً ... ، ولا يجوز: جاء زيد وعمرو راكباً لعدم القرينة، أو مِن (هو) ، والعامل الجملة لأنه حال مؤكدة، أي: تفرد قائماً، أو حقه قائماً، (بالقسط) أي: العدل، و (إن الدين) : جملة مستأنفة مؤكدة للأولى، أي: لا دين مرضى عند الله سوى الإقرار بالشهادة والدخول فيما جاء به محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، ومن قرأ بالفتح فهو بدل من (أنه) ، بدل الكل، إن فسر الإسلام بالإيمان، وبدل الاشتمال إن فسر بالشريعة.","anchor":"ar-q3-18-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-3","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: شَهِدَ اللَّهُ أَنَّهُ لاَ إِلهَ إِلَّا هُوَ أي: بيَّن وحدانيتَه بنصب الدلائل الدالة عليها، وإنزال الآيات الناطقة بها، أو بتدبيره العجيب وصنعته المتقنة وأموره المحكمة، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-18-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-4","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"يَا عَجَباً كيف يُعْصَى الإلهُ ... أم كيف يَجْحَدُه الجاحدُ؟!","anchor":"ar-q3-18-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-5","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"وللهِ في كل تحريكةٍ ... وتسكينةٍ أبداً شاهدُ","anchor":"ar-q3-18-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-6","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"وفي كُلِّ شَيءٍ له آيةٌ ... تَدُلُّ على أنَّه واحِدُ(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-18-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-7","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"وقيل لبعض العرب: ما الدليل على أن للعالم صانعاً؟ فقال: البعرة تدل على البعير، وآثار القدم تدل على المسير، فهيكل علوي بهذه اللطافة، ومركز سفلي بهذه الكثافة، أمَا يدلان على الصانع الخبير؟! وَشهدت الْمَلائِكَةُ أيضاً بالإقرار بالوحدانية والإخبار بها، وَأُولُوا الْعِلْمِ وهم: الأنبياء والعلماء بالله، بالإيمان بها والاحتجاج عليها، شبه ذلك في البيان والكشف بشهادة الشاهد. وفيه دليل شرف أهل العلم وفضلهم، حيث قرن شهادتهم بشهادته لأن العلم صفة الله العليا ونعمته العظمى، والعلماء أعلام الإسلام، والسابقون إلى دار السلام، وسُرج الأمكنة وحجج الأزمنة.","anchor":"ar-q3-18-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-8","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"وعن جابر قال: قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «ساعة من عالم يتّكىء على فِرَاشِهِ، ينظُرُ في علمهِ، خَيرٌ مِنْ عِبَادَة العَابِد سَبعينَ عاماً» . وعن معاذ قالَ: قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «تعلموا العلم فإن تعلمه لله خشيةٌ، ومدارستَه تسبيحٌ، والبحث فيه جهادٌ، وتعليمه مَنْ لا يعلمه صدقةٌ، وتذكُّره في أهله قُرْبَة» . ثم قال في آخر الحديث في فضل أهل العلم: «وتَرْغَبُ الملائكة في خُلتِهم، وبأجنحتها تمسحُهم، وفي صلاتها تستغفر لهم، وكلُّ رطب ويابس يستغفر لهم. حتى حيتان البحر وهوامه، وسباع الأرضين وأنعامها، والسماء ونجومها، ألا وإن العلم حياةُ القلوب من العمى، ونورُ الأبصار من الظلم، وقوة الأبدان من الضعف، يبلغ بالعبد منزل الأحرار ومجالسة الملوك، والفكر فيه يُعْدل بالصيام، ومدارسته بالقيام، وبه يُعرف الحلال والحرام، وبه تُوصلَ الأرحام، العلم إمام والعمل تابعه، يُلْهَمُه السعداء، ويحرمه الأشقياء» .","anchor":"ar-q3-18-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-9","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"حال كون الحقّ تعالى قائِماً بِالْقِسْطِ أي: مُدبراً لأمر خلقه بالعدل، فيما حكم وأبرم، لاَ إِلهَ إِلَّا هُوَ، كرر الشهادة للتأكيد، ومزيد الاعتبار بأمر التوحيد، والحكم به، بعد إقامته الدليل عليه. وقال جعفر الصادق:","anchor":"ar-q3-18-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-18-10","r":"q3-18","title":"3:18 · God’s testimony to His oneness","text":"(الأُولى وصف وتوحيد، والثانية رسم وتعليم) . أي: قولوا: لاَ إِلهَ إِلَّا هُوَ، أو ليرتب عليه قوله: الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ، فيعلم أنه الموصوف بهما، وقدَّم «العزيز» ليتقدم العلم بقدرته على العلم بحكمته.","anchor":"ar-q3-18-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-18-s1","r":"q3-18","title":"The circumstantial clause and the following affirmation","text":"I say: “Upholding” ( قائماً ) is a circumstantial qualifier ( حال ) of “God.” Its restriction to one of the coordinated elements is admissible because there is no confusion, as in “We bestowed upon him Isaac, and Jacob as an additional gift” [21:72]. One cannot say “Zayd and ʿAmr came riding,” with the singular qualifier, without an indication of which is meant. Alternatively, it qualifies “He” ( هو ), and the sentence governs it, because it is a confirmatory circumstantial qualifier ( حال مؤكدة ): He alone is God, upholding justice; or it is established of Him while He upholds justice. Qisṭ ( القسط ) means justice. “Indeed, the religion …” [3:19] is a new sentence confirming the first: no religion is pleasing to God except acknowledgement of the testimony and entering what Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, brought. In the reading with fatḥa, anna, it is apposition to “that He” ( أنه ): complete apposition ( بدل الكل ) if Islam is interpreted as faith, or apposition of inclusion ( بدل الاشتمال ) if it is interpreted as the Sacred Law. [A028] [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-13] ]","anchor":"en-q3-18-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-18-s2","r":"q3-18","title":"Signs, testimony and the honour of knowledge","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “God bears witness that there is no god but He”: He makes His oneness clear by setting up indications of it and sending down verses declaring it, or through His wondrous governance, perfected workmanship and well-ordered affairs. Concerning this the poet says: How astonishing that God should be disobeyed, or denied by one who denies! In every movement and every stillness there is always a witness to God. In everything He has a sign indicating that He is One. One of the Arabs was asked for the proof that the world has a Maker. He replied: “Dung points to a camel and footprints to a traveller. Do not a celestial structure of such subtlety and a lower centre of such density point to the All-Aware Maker?” [A029] “The angels” also bear witness, acknowledging and declaring oneness; and “those possessed of knowledge”—the prophets and those who know God—through believing it and adducing proof for it. In its clarification and disclosure, this is likened to a witness’s testimony. It indicates the honour and excellence of the people of knowledge, since He joins their testimony to His own. Knowledge is God’s exalted attribute and His greatest gift. Scholars are the standards of Islam, the foremost on the way to the Abode of Peace, the lamps of places and the proofs of their times. Jābir reports the Prophet’s words: “An hour in which a scholar reclines upon his bed considering his knowledge is better than a worshipper’s worship for seventy years.” Muʿādh reports: “Learn knowledge: learning it for God is reverent fear; studying it is glorification; investigating it is struggle; teaching it to one who does not know is charity; and recalling it among its people is a means of nearness.” At the end of the report he says of the people of knowledge: “The angels desire their friendship, stroke them with their wings and seek forgiveness for them in their prayers. Every moist and dry thing seeks forgiveness for them: the fish and creatures of the sea, the beasts and livestock of the earths, the heaven and its stars. Knowledge is the life of hearts from blindness, the light of sight from darkness, and the strength of bodies from weakness. It brings the servant to the rank of the free and the companionship of kings. Reflection upon it equals fasting, and studying it equals standing in prayer. Through it the lawful and unlawful are known, and kinship ties maintained. Knowledge is the leader; action follows it. The fortunate are inspired with it, and the wretched deprived of it.” [A030] The Real, exalted is He, is “upholding justice”: governing His creation with justice in what He decrees and settles. “There is no god but He.” He repeats the testimony for emphasis, further consideration of oneness, and affirmation of it after establishing its proof. Jaʿfar al-Ṣādiq says: “The first is description and affirmation of unity; the second is prescription and instruction”—that is, say, “There is no god but He.” Alternatively, it is repeated to attach to it “the Mighty, the Wise,” making clear that He is described by both. He places “the Mighty” first, so that knowledge of His power precedes knowledge of His wisdom.","anchor":"en-q3-18-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-19","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement 3:19","anchor":"unit-q3-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-1","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"إِنَّ الدِّينَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ الْإِسْلامُ أي: إن الدين المرضى عند الله هو الانقياد لأمر التوحيد والإذعان لمن جاء به. ورُوِيَ عن أنس رضي الله عنه قال: قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «من قرأَ هذه الآيةَ عند منامه خَلَقَ اللَّهَ تعالى سبعين ألف خَلْقٍ يستغفرون الله له إلى يوم القيامة(1)» . وهي أعظم شهادة في كتاب الله، «من قرأها إلى (الحكيم) وقال: وأنا أشهد بما شهد الله به، وأستودِعُ اللهَ هذه الشهادة، وهي لي عند الله وديعة، يقول الحق تعالى: إن لعبدي هذا عندي عهداً وأنا أحقُّ مَنْ وفى بالعهد، أدخِلوا عبدي الجنة(2)» .","anchor":"ar-q3-19-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-2","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"الإشارة: صدرُ الآية يشير إلى الفرق، وعَجُزُها يشير إلى الجمع، كما هي عادته تعالى في كتابه العزيز، يشرع أولاً، ويُحَقِّق ثانياً، فأثبت الحق- جلّ جلاله- شهادة الملائكة وأولى العلم مع شهادته لإثبات سر الشريعة، ثم محاها بقوله: (لاَ إله إِلاَّ هُوَ العزيز الحكيم) بحكم الحقيقة. فإثبات الرسوم شريعة، ومحوها حقيقة، فتوحيد أهل الرسوم والأشكال دلالة من وراء الحجاب، وتوحيد أهل المحو والاضمحلال شهادة من داخل الحجاب، وتوحيد أهل الرسوم دلالة وبرهان، وتوحيد أهل المحو شهادة وعيان، أهل الدليل والبرهان عموم عند أهل الشهود والعيان.","anchor":"ar-q3-19-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-3","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"إثبات الرسوم إسلام وإيمان، ومحوها شهود وإحسان، وكل توحيد لم تظهر ثمرته على الجوارح من الإذعان والانقياد لأحكام العبودية فهو مخدج(3) ، لقوله تعالى: إِنَّ الدِّينَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ الْإِسْلامُ أي، الانقياد والإذعان، ظاهراً وباطناً، لأحكام القهرية والتكليفية، فمن لا انقياد له لا دين له كاملاً.","anchor":"ar-q3-19-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-4","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"ثم ذكر من سبق له الخذلان بعد سطوع الدليل والبُرهان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-19-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-5","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"... وَمَا اخْتَلَفَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ إِلاَّ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا جاءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ بَغْياً بَيْنَهُمْ وَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ سَرِيعُ الْحِسابِ (19)","anchor":"ar-q3-19-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-6","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"قلت: (بغياً) : مفعول له، علة للاختلاف.","anchor":"ar-q3-19-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-7","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَا اخْتَلَفَ اليهود والنصارى في حقيقة الإسلام والتدين به، إِلَّا مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ أي: من بعد ما تمكنوا من العلم بصحته، وأن الدين عند الله هو الإسلام، فجحدوه ظلماً وحسداً.","anchor":"ar-q3-19-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-8","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"أو ما اختلف أرباب الكتب المتقدمة في دين الإسلام فأثبته قوم، وقال قوم: إنه مخصوص بالعرب، ونفاه آخرون مطلقاً، إلا من بعد ما ثبت لهم العلم بصحته وعموم الدعوة له. أو في التوحيد فثلث النصارى، وقالت اليهود:","anchor":"ar-q3-19-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-9","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"عزير ابن الله، بعد ما صح لهم العلم بالتوحيد فغيروا. وقال الربيع: إن موسى عليه السلام لما حضره الموت، دعا سبعين حبراً من قومه، فاستودعهم التوراة، فلما مضى القرن الأول والثاني والثالث وقعت بينهم الفرقة، وهم:","anchor":"ar-q3-19-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-10","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"الَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ الْكِتَابَ مِن أبناء السبعين، فأراقوا الدماء ووقع بينهم الشر والاختلاف.","anchor":"ar-q3-19-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-11","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"وذلك من بعد ما جاءهم العلم، يعني بيان ما في التوراة، (بغياً بينهم) أي: طلباً للملك والرئاسة والتحاسد، فسلّط عليهم الجبابرة، وَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ المنزلة على رسوله، أو الدالة على وحدانيته، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ سَرِيعُ الْحِسابِ لا يشغله شأن عن شأن، وفيه تهديد لأهل الاختلاف.","anchor":"ar-q3-19-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-12","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"الإشارة: الاختلاف على الصوفية، والإنكار عليهم، إن كان بغياً وحسداً وخوفاً على زوال رئاسة المنكر، فهذا معرض لمقت الله، فقد آذن بحرب الله، وبالُه سوء الخاتمة، والعياذ بالله، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-19-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-13","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"هممهم تقضى بحكم الوَقْتِ ... مُنِكِرُهُم مُعَرَّضٌ للمٌقْتِ","anchor":"ar-q3-19-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-14","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"وإن كان غيرة على الشريعة، وسدّاً لباب الذريعة، فهذا معذور أو مأجور إن صح قصده، وهو منخرط في سلك الضعفاء، قال تعالى: لَيْسَ عَلَى الضُّعَفاءِ وَلا عَلَى الْمَرْضى وَلا عَلَى الَّذِينَ لا يَجِدُونَ ما يُنْفِقُونَ حَرَجٌ إِذا نَصَحُوا لِلَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ، ولا ينكر على الفقير إلا المُحرَّم المجمع على تحريمه، وليس فيه تأويل، كالزنى بالمعينة، واللواط، وشبهه، والمؤمن يلتمس المعاذر، والمنافق يلتمس العيوب، وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-19-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-19-15","r":"q3-19","title":"3:19 · Submission, division and reverent disagreement","text":"ثم بين الحق تعالى الدواء فى أذى المنكر، وهو الإعراض عنه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-19-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-19-s1","r":"q3-19","title":"The religion pleasing to God","text":"“The religion with God is Islam”: the religion pleasing to Him is submission to the affirmation of unity and yielding to the one who brought it. Anas—God be pleased with him—reports the Prophet’s words: “Whoever recites this verse [3:18] when going to sleep, God creates seventy thousand creatures who seek forgiveness for him until the Day of Resurrection.” It is the greatest testimony in God’s Book. “Whoever recites it as far as ‘the Wise,’ then says, ‘I too bear witness to what God has borne witness to, and I entrust this testimony to God: it is a deposit for me with Him,’ the Real, exalted is He, says, ‘This servant of Mine has a covenant with Me, and I am most entitled to fulfil a covenant. Admit My servant to the Garden.’” [A031]","anchor":"en-q3-19-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-19-s2","r":"q3-19","title":"Distinction, gathering and obedience","text":"The opening of the verse [3:18] points to distinction ( الفرق ), and its conclusion to gathering ( الجمع ), as is His customary manner in His Mighty Book: He sets forth the Sacred Law first and realization second. The Real, glorious is His majesty, affirms the testimony of angels and people of knowledge alongside His testimony, establishing the mystery of the Sacred Law. He then effaces it with “There is no god but He, the Mighty, the Wise,” by the ruling of Reality. Affirming created outlines ( الرسوم ) is Sacred Law; effacing them is Reality. [A032] The unification of those concerned with outlines and forms is an indication from behind the veil. The unification of the people of effacement and disappearance is testimony from within the veil. The former is indication and demonstration; the latter testimony and direct vision. People of evidence and demonstration are ordinary people in relation to those of witnessing and direct vision. Affirmation of outlines is Islam and faith; their effacement is witnessing and spiritual excellence ( الإحسان ). Every affirmation of unity whose fruit fails to appear in the limbs as yielding and submission to the rulings of servanthood is deficient. For He says, “The religion with God is Islam”: outward and inward submission to the rulings of overpowering divine governance and of obligation. Whoever lacks submission lacks complete religion.","anchor":"en-q3-19-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-19-s3","r":"q3-19","title":"","text":"He then mentions those for whom abandonment was already decreed despite the radiance of evidence and demonstration, saying: Qurʾānic continuation · 3:19b وَمَا اخْتَلَفَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ إِلاَّ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا جاءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ بَغْياً بَيْنَهُمْ وَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ سَرِيعُ الْحِسابِ Those given the Book differed only after knowledge had come to them, through mutual rivalry. Whoever disbelieves in God’s signs—God is swift in reckoning.","anchor":"en-q3-19-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-19-s4","r":"q3-19","title":"The cause of division","text":"I say: “Through rivalry” ( بغياً ) is an accusative of purpose or cause ( مفعول له ), giving the cause of the disagreement.","anchor":"en-q3-19-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-19-s5","r":"q3-19","title":"Knowledge contradicted by rivalry","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: the Jews and Christians differed concerning the truth of Islam and adherence to it only after knowledge had come to them: after they had the means to know its soundness and that the religion with God is Islam. They denied it unjustly and enviously. Alternatively, the possessors of earlier books differed concerning Islam—some affirming it, others saying it was restricted to the Arabs, and others denying it altogether—only after knowledge of its truth and the universality of its summons had been established for them. Or they differed concerning unity: Christians asserted a trinity and Jews said, “ʿUzayr is God’s son,” changing what they had soundly known of unity. [A033] Al-Rabīʿ said: “When death approached Moses, peace be upon him, he called seventy learned men of his people and entrusted the Torah to them. After the first, second and third generations had passed, division arose among them: these were ‘those given the Book,’ the descendants of the seventy. They shed blood, and evil and disagreement arose among them.” This was after knowledge—the explanation contained in the Torah—had come to them, “through mutual rivalry”: seeking dominion and leadership and envying one another. He therefore gave tyrants power over them. “Whoever disbelieves in God’s signs,” revealed to His Messenger or indicating His oneness, “God is swift in reckoning”: one affair does not distract Him from another. This threatens the people of division.","anchor":"en-q3-19-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-19-s6","r":"q3-19","title":"Two motives for criticizing the Sufis","text":"Disagreement with the Sufis and repudiation of them, when arising from rivalry, envy or fear that the critic will lose his leadership, exposes him to God’s abhorrence. He has declared war against God, and its evil outcome is an ill ending—God protect us. Concerning this the poet says: Their aspirations give judgment according to the moment’s ruling; their repudiator exposes himself to abhorrence. But when criticism arises from protective concern for the Sacred Law and blocking the means to wrongdoing ( سد الذريعة ), its author is excused, or rewarded if his intention is sound. He is included among the weak: “There is no blame upon the weak, the sick, or those who find nothing to spend, provided they are sincere towards God and His Messenger” [9:91]. A spiritual pauper is to be censured only for what is unanimously prohibited and admits no interpretation, such as illicit intercourse with a specified woman, sodomy and the like. The believer seeks excuses; the hypocrite seeks faults. [A034] Success is through God, who guides to the even path.","anchor":"en-q3-19-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-19-s7","r":"q3-19","title":"","text":"The Real, exalted is He, then explains the remedy for the critic’s harm: turning away from him. He says:","anchor":"en-q3-19-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-20","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person 3:20","anchor":"unit-q3-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-1","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"فَإِنْ حَاجُّوكَ فَقُلْ أَسْلَمْتُ وَجْهِيَ لِلَّهِ وَمَنِ اتَّبَعَنِ وَقُلْ لِلَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ وَالْأُمِّيِّينَ أَأَسْلَمْتُمْ فَإِنْ أَسْلَمُوا فَقَدِ اهْتَدَوْا وَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَإِنَّما عَلَيْكَ الْبَلاغُ وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِالْعِبادِ (20)","anchor":"ar-q3-20-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-2","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"قلت: (ومن اتبعن) ، عطف على فاعل (أسلمت) الضمير(1) .","anchor":"ar-q3-20-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-3","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَإِنْ حَاجُّوكَ في الدين، وخاصموك فيه، بعد ما أقيمت الحجج على صحته، فَقُلْ لهم: أما أنا فقد أَسْلَمْتُ وَجْهِيَ لِلَّهِ، وانقدت بكليتي إليه، وتمسكت بدينه القويم، الذي قامت الحجج على حقيته، وكذلك من تبعني من المؤمنين. وخصّ الوجه بالانقياد لأنه أشرف الأعضاء ومحل ظهور المحاسن، فإذا انقاد الوجه فقد انقاد الكل.","anchor":"ar-q3-20-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-4","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"وَقُلْ لِلَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ من اليهود والنصارى، وَالْأُمِّيِّينَ الذين لا كتاب لهم من المشركين:","anchor":"ar-q3-20-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-5","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"أَأَسْلَمْتُمْ كما أسلمتُ، لما وضحت لكم من الحجة؟ أم أنتم على كفركم بغياً وحسداً؟ والاستفهام معناه الأمر، كقوله: فَهَلْ أَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ أي: أسلموا، فَإِنْ أَسْلَمُوا فَقَدِ اهْتَدَوْا وأنقذوا أنفسهم من الهلاك، وَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا وأعرضوا فَإِنَّما عَلَيْكَ الْبَلاغُ، ولا يضرك عنادهم، فقد بلغت ما أمرت به. وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِالْعِبادِ لا يخفى عليه مَن أسلم ممن تولى.","anchor":"ar-q3-20-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-6","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"رُوِيَ أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- قرأ عليهم هذه الآية، فقال لليهُود: «أتشهدون أن عزيراً عبد الله ورسوله وكلمته؟» فقالوا: معاذ الله، وقال للنصارى: «أتشهدون أن عيسى عبد الله ورسوله؟» فقالوا: معاذ الله أن يكون عيسى عبداً. فنزل قوله تعالى: وَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَإِنَّما عَلَيْكَ الْبَلاغُ الآية.","anchor":"ar-q3-20-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-7","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"الإشارة: لا يليق بالفقير، إذا توجه إليه الإنكار أو المجادلة والاستظهار، إلا السكوت والإقرار، والاستسلام بكليته لأحكام الواحد القهار، إذ لا يرى فاعلاً إلا الله، فلا يركن إلى شيء سواه. وفي الحِكَم: «إنما أجرى الأذى عليهم لئلا تكون ساكناً إليهم، أراد أن يُزْعِجَكَ عن كل شيء، حتى لا تكون ساكناً إلى شيء» . وقال بعض العارفين: لا تشتغل قط بمَن يؤذيك، واشتغل بالله يرده عنك، وقد غلط في هذا خلق كثير، اشتغلوا بمن يؤذيهم، فطال عليهم الأذى مع الإثم، ولو أنهم رجعوا إلى مولاهم لكفاهم أمرهم. هـ. بالمعنى. وبهذا يأمر الشيخ أتباعه، فإن انقادوا لأحكام الحق، فقد اهتدوا إلى طريق الوصول، وإن تولوا فإنما عليك البلاغ، والهداية بيد السميع البصير.","anchor":"ar-q3-20-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-20-8","r":"q3-20","title":"3:20 · The duty to convey and the surrender of the whole person","text":"ثم وبّخ اليهود بما وقع لأسلافهم من البغي والفساد، وهم راضون بذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-20-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-20-s1","r":"q3-20","title":"Those who follow","text":"I say: “Those who follow me” is coordinated with the pronominal subject of “I have submitted.”","anchor":"en-q3-20-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-20-s2","r":"q3-20","title":"Submission after the proof has been established","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “If they dispute with you” concerning religion, contesting it after the proofs of its truth have been established, say: as for me, “I have submitted my face to God.” I have yielded my entire being to Him and held fast to His upright religion, whose truth has been demonstrated; and so have the believers who follow me. The face is singled out for submission because it is the noblest limb and the place where beauties appear. When the face submits, the whole submits. “Say to those given the Book,” Jews and Christians, “and to the unlettered,” idolaters without a book: “Have you submitted,” as I have, now that the proof is clear? Or do you remain in unbelief through rivalry and envy? The interrogation has the sense of a command, like “Will you, then, submit?” [compare 11:14]: submit! “If they submit, they are guided” and have saved themselves from destruction. “If they turn away,” rejecting it, “your duty is only to convey.” Their obstinacy does not harm you: you have conveyed what you were commanded. “God sees His servants”: those who submit and those who turn away are not hidden from Him. It is related that the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, recited this verse to them and said to the Jews, “Do you testify that ʿUzayr is God’s servant, His messenger and His word?” They replied, “God forbid!” He said to the Christians, “Do you testify that Jesus is God’s servant and messenger?” They replied, “God forbid that Jesus should be a servant!” Then “If they turn away, your duty is only to convey …” was revealed. [A035]","anchor":"en-q3-20-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-20-s3","r":"q3-20","title":"Do not become occupied with the one who harms you","text":"When repudiation, disputation and attempts to prevail in argument are directed against the spiritual pauper, nothing befits him but silence, acknowledgement and the surrender of his entire being to the rulings of the One, the Subduer. He sees no agent but God and therefore relies upon nothing else. In the Ḥikam : “He caused harm to come to you through them only so that you would not rest in them. He wished to disturb you away from everything, so that you would not rest in anything.” One of the gnostics said: “Never occupy yourself with the one who harms you. Occupy yourself with God, and He will repel him from you. Many have erred here: they occupied themselves with their assailant, so their harm continued, together with sin. Had they returned to their Master, He would have sufficed them in their affair.” End of the passage, in sense. This is what the shaykh commands his followers. If they submit to the Real’s rulings, they are guided to the path of arrival. If they turn away, your duty is only to convey; guidance is in the hand of the All-Hearing, All-Seeing.","anchor":"en-q3-20-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-20-s4","r":"q3-20","title":"","text":"He then reproaches the Jews for the aggression and corruption committed by their predecessors, with which they are content, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-20-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-21-22","r":"q3-21-22","title":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice","text":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice 3:21–22","anchor":"unit-q3-21-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-21-22-1","r":"q3-21-22","title":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ وَيَقْتُلُونَ النَّبِيِّينَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ وَيَقْتُلُونَ الَّذِينَ يَأْمُرُونَ بِالْقِسْطِ مِنَ النَّاسِ فَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذابٍ أَلِيمٍ (21) أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ حَبِطَتْ أَعْمالُهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَما لَهُمْ مِنْ ناصِرِينَ (22)","anchor":"ar-q3-21-22-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-21-22-2","r":"q3-21-22","title":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice","text":"قلت: إنما دخلت الفاء في خبر إنَّ لتضمن اسمها معنى الشرط لعموم الموصول وإبهامه، وهو خاص بإنَّ، دون ليت ولعل لأن «إن» لا تغير معنى الابتداء، وإنما تؤكده. وقيل: الخبر: (أولئك..) الخ.","anchor":"ar-q3-21-22-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-21-22-3","r":"q3-21-22","title":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ أي: بحُججه الدالة على توحيده، وصحة نبوة رسله، أو بكلامه، وهم اليهود، وَيَقْتُلُونَ النَّبِيِّينَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ بل بغياً وَيَقْتُلُونَ الَّذِينَ يَأْمُرُونَ بالعدل وترك الظلم من الأحبار، فَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذابٍ أَلِيمٍ موجع، أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ حَبِطَتْ أَعْمالُهُمْ أي: بطلت، فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ فلا ينتفعون بها في الدارين، وَما لَهُمْ مِنْ ناصِرِينَ يمنعونهم من العذاب.","anchor":"ar-q3-21-22-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-21-22-4","r":"q3-21-22","title":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice","text":"وعن أبي عبيدة بن الجراح رضي الله عنه قال: سألت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أيُّ النَّاسِ أشَدُّ عَذَاباً يَوْمَ القيامة؟ قال: «رَجُلٌ قَتَلَ نَبِيّاً، أو رَجل أمَرَ بالمُنكَر ونَهَى عن المَعْرُوفِ، ثم قرأ النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وَيَقْتُلُونَ النَّبِيِّينَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ الآية، ثم قال: يا أبا عبيدة، قتلت بنو إسْرَائِيلَ ثلاثةً وأرْبَعِين نبيّاً أوَّل النَّهَار في سَاعَةٍ، فقام مائة وعشرون من عُبَّادِ بَني إسْرَائِيل فأَمرُوهم بالمَعرُوف ونَهوهُمْ عن المنكر، فقتلوهم جميعاً مِنْ آخِرِ النَّهارِ من ذلك اليوم، فهم الذين ذكرهم في كتابه، وأنزل الآية فيهم» . هـ. من الثعلبي.","anchor":"ar-q3-21-22-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-21-22-5","r":"q3-21-22","title":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice","text":"الإشارة: ذكر في الآية الأولى تشجيع المريدين، وأمرهم بالصبر والتسليم لإذاية المؤذين، وذكر هنا وبال المؤذين الجاحدين لخصوصية المقربين، فالأولياء والعلماء ورثة الأنبياء، فمن آذاهم فله عذاب أليم، في الدنيا بغم الحجاب وسوء المنقلب، وفي الآخرة بالبعد عن ساحة المقربين، وبالسقوط إلى دَرْكَ الأسفلين، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-21-22-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-21-22-6","r":"q3-21-22","title":"3:21–22 · Killing the prophets and those who command justice","text":"ومن مساوئ اليهود أيضا إعراضهم عن الحق إذا توجه إليهم، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق تعالى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-21-22-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-21-22-s1","r":"q3-21-22","title":"A predicate carrying conditional force","text":"I say: fāʾ enters the predicate of inna because its subject carries a conditional sense, owing to the generality and indeterminacy of the relative expression. This is peculiar to inna, not layta or laʿalla: inna does not alter the meaning of the initial nominal construction, but confirms it. Alternatively, the predicate is “They are those ….”","anchor":"en-q3-21-22-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-21-22-s2","r":"q3-21-22","title":"The consequence of violent rejection","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Those who disbelieve in God’s signs”—His proofs of oneness and the truth of His messengers’ prophethood, or His speech, namely the Jews—“kill the prophets without right,” rather through aggression, “and kill people who command justice,” the learned men who enjoin fairness and abandoning oppression: “give them tidings of a painful,” agonizing, “punishment.” They are those whose works are nullified in this world and the hereafter, benefiting them in neither abode. They have no helpers to protect them from punishment. Abū ʿUbayda ibn al-Jarrāḥ—God be pleased with him—said: “I asked the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, which people will suffer most severely on the Day of Resurrection. He replied, ‘A man who killed a prophet, or a man who commanded wrong and forbade right.’ He then recited ‘and kill the prophets without right …,’ and said, ‘Abū ʿUbayda, the Children of Israel killed forty-three prophets in a single hour at the beginning of a day. A hundred and twenty of their worshippers then stood up, commanding them to do right and forbidding them to do wrong. They killed them all by the end of that same day. These are those God mentioned in His Book, concerning whom He revealed the verse.’” End of the quotation from al-Thaʿlabī. [Translator’s note: Cairo I:337 reads “commanded wrong and forbade right” and “a hundred and twenty.” The electronic text of al-Thaʿlabī, al-Kashf wa-l-bayān III:36–37, shares the first wording but gives one hundred and twelve. Al-Baghawī, Maʿālim al-tanzīl II:21, instead describes a man who killed a prophet or someone who commanded right and forbade wrong, and likewise gives one hundred and twelve. The English retains Cairo. These source differences do not establish Ibn ʿAjība’s original wording or authenticate the report.] [A036]","anchor":"en-q3-21-22-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-21-22-s3","r":"q3-21-22","title":"The encouragement of disciples and the warning to persecutors","text":"The preceding verse encouraged disciples and commanded patience and submission before the harm inflicted by others. Here He mentions the evil outcome for those who harm and deny the spiritual election of those brought near. God’s friends and the scholars are the prophets’ heirs. Whoever harms them has a painful punishment: in this world, the distress of veiling and an ill return; in the hereafter, remoteness from the precinct of those brought near and descent to the lowest depth. And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-21-22-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-21-22-s4","r":"q3-21-22","title":"","text":"Another of the Jews’ faults is their turning away from truth when it is directed towards them, as the Real, exalted is He, indicates, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-21-22-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-23-25","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning 3:23–25","anchor":"unit-q3-23-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-1","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيباً مِنَ الْكِتابِ يُدْعَوْنَ إِلى كِتابِ اللَّهِ لِيَحْكُمَ بَيْنَهُمْ ثُمَّ يَتَوَلَّى فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ وَهُمْ مُعْرِضُونَ (23) ذلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قالُوا لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ إِلاَّ أَيَّاماً مَعْدُوداتٍ وَغَرَّهُمْ فِي دِينِهِمْ ما كانُوا يَفْتَرُونَ (24) فَكَيْفَ إِذا جَمَعْناهُمْ لِيَوْمٍ لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ وَوُفِّيَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لا يُظْلَمُونَ (25)","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-2","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"قلت: التنكير في (نصيب) يحتمل التحقير والتعظيم، والأول أقرب. وجملة: (وهم معرضون) حال من (فريق) لتخصيصه بالصفة.","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-3","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أَلَمْ تَرَ يا محمد، أو مَنْ تصح منه الرؤية، إِلَى الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيباً مِنَ الْكِتابِ وهم: اليهود، تمسكوا بشيء من التوراة، ولم يعملوا به كلّه، كيف يُدْعَوْنَ إِلى كِتابِ اللَّهِ القرآن لِيَحْكُمَ بَيْنَهُمْ فيما اختلفوا فيه من أمر التوحيد وصحة نبوته- عليه الصلاة والسلام، فأعرضوا عنه، أو المراد بكتاب الله: التوراة. قال ابن عباس رضي الله عنه: (دخل النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم على جماعة من اليهود، فَدَعاهُمْ إلى الله تعالى، فقال نُعَيْمُ بْنُ عَمِرْو والحَارِثُ بَنْ زَيْد: على أيِّ دين أنْتَ يا مُحَمَّدُ؟ قال: «على مِلَّةِ إبْرَاهِيم» قالا: إنَّ إبرَاهِيم كان","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-4","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"يَهُودِيّاً، فقال لهما النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «فَهَلمُّوا إلى التَّوراةِ فهي بَيْنَنَا وبينكم» فأبَيا عليه، فنزلت الآية) . وقيل: نزلت في الرجم، على ما يأتي في العقود.","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-5","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"ذلِكَ الإعراض بسبب اغترارهم وتسهيلهم أمر العقاب، فقالوا: لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ إِلَّا أَيَّاماً مَعْدُوداتٍ أربعين يوماً، قدر عبادتهم العجل، ثم يَخْلفهم المسلمون، وَغَرَّهُمْ فِي دِينِهِمْ ما كانُوا يَفْتَرُونَ بزعمهم الفاسد وطمعهم الفارغ.","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-6","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَكَيْفَ إِذا جَمَعْناهُمْ لِيَوْمٍ لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ، وهذا تهويل لشأنهم، واستعظام لما يحيق بهم، وَوُفِّيَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ من خير أو شر، وَهُمْ لا يُظْلَمُونَ أي: لا يبخسون من أعمالهم شيئاً، فلا ينقص من الحسنات، ولا يزاد على السيئات. وفيه دليل على أنَّ المؤمن لا يخلد في النار. قال ابن عباس: (أولُ رايةٍ تُرفع لأهل الموقف، ذلك اليوم، رايةُ اليهود، فيفضحهم الله تعالى على رءوس الأشهاد، ثم يؤمر بهم إلى النار) .","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-7","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"الإشارة: ترى كثيراً ممن ينتسب إلى العلم والدين ينطلق لسانه بدعوى الخصوصية، وأنه منخرط في سلك المقربين، فإذا دُعي إلى حق، أو وقف على عيب من عيوب نفسه، أعرض وتولى، وغرته نفسه، وغلبه الهوى، فجعل يحتج لنفسه بما عنده من العلم أو الدين، أو بمن ينتسب إليهم من الصالحين، فكيف يكون حاله إذا أقبل على الله بقلب سقيم، ورأى منازل أهل الصفا، الذين لقوا الله بقلب سليم، حين ترفع درجاتهم مع المقربين، ويبقى هو مع عوام أهل اليمين؟ قال تعالى: وَبَدا لَهُمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ مَا لَمْ يَكُونُوا يَحْتَسِبُونَ الآية.","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-23-25-8","r":"q3-23-25","title":"3:23–25 · The Book, false reassurance and the coming reckoning","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى نزع ملك أهل الكتاب، وسلب عزهم، وانتقاله إلى المسلمين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-23-25-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-23-25-s1","r":"q3-23-25","title":"The indefinite “share”","text":"I say: the indefinite form of “a share” ( نصيب ) may diminish or magnify it; the first is nearer. “While they are averse” ( وهم معرضون ) is a circumstantial clause qualifying “a group,” since the latter is specified by its qualification.","anchor":"en-q3-23-25-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-23-25-s2","r":"q3-23-25","title":"Refusing the judgment one professes to acknowledge","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Have you not seen,” Muḥammad—or anyone capable of seeing—“those given a share of the Book,” namely the Jews, who held to something of the Torah without acting upon all of it? See how they are summoned to God’s Book, the Qurʾān, to judge between them concerning their disagreement over unity and the truth of the Prophet’s mission, yet they turn away. Alternatively, God’s Book here is the Torah. Ibn ʿAbbās—God be pleased with him—said: “The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, entered among a group of Jews and called them to God. Nuʿaym ibn ʿAmr and al-Ḥārith ibn Zayd asked, ‘What religion do you follow, Muḥammad?’ He answered, ‘The way of Abraham.’ They said, ‘Abraham was a Jew.’ The Prophet said, ‘Come, then, to the Torah: let it stand between us and you.’ They refused, and the verse was revealed.” It is also said that it was revealed concerning stoning, as will be discussed in al-ʿUqūd. [A037] “That” aversion is caused by their self-deception and their making light of punishment: they say, “The Fire will touch us only for a limited number of days,” forty days, corresponding to their worship of the calf, after which the Muslims will take their place. “What they used to fabricate has deceived them in their religion,” through their false supposition and empty expectation. The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “How will it be when We gather them for a day of which there is no doubt?” This makes their situation terrifying and magnifies what will encompass them. “Every soul is paid in full what it has earned,” good or evil, “without being wronged”: nothing of its deeds is withheld, neither good deeds diminished nor evil deeds increased. This indicates that the believer does not remain eternally in the Fire. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “The first banner raised for the people standing that day is the Jews’ banner. God exposes them before all witnesses, then orders them into the Fire.” [A038]","anchor":"en-q3-23-25-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-23-25-s3","r":"q3-23-25","title":"Claims of election tested by correction","text":"You see many who claim affiliation to learning and religion readily asserting spiritual election and inclusion among those brought near. Yet when summoned to truth, or shown a fault of their own soul, they turn away. Their lower self deceives them and desire overcomes them. They defend themselves by appealing to their learning or religion, or to the righteous people to whom they claim affiliation. What will their condition be when they come before God with a sick heart and see the stations of the people of purity, who met Him with a sound heart? Those people’s degrees are raised among those brought near, while they themselves remain among the ordinary people of the right hand. He says: “There will appear to them from God what they had not reckoned upon” [39:47].","anchor":"en-q3-23-25-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-23-25-s4","r":"q3-23-25","title":"","text":"The Real, exalted is He, then mentions the removal of the People of the Book’s dominion, the stripping away of their might, and its transfer to the Muslims, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-23-25-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-26-27","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion 3:26–27","anchor":"unit-q3-26-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-1","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"قُلِ اللَّهُمَّ مالِكَ الْمُلْكِ تُؤْتِي الْمُلْكَ مَنْ تَشاءُ وَتَنْزِعُ الْمُلْكَ مِمَّنْ تَشاءُ وَتُعِزُّ مَنْ تَشاءُ وَتُذِلُّ مَنْ تَشاءُ بِيَدِكَ الْخَيْرُ إِنَّكَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (26) تُولِجُ اللَّيْلَ فِي النَّهارِ وَتُولِجُ النَّهارَ فِي اللَّيْلِ وَتُخْرِجُ الْحَيَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَتُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتَ مِنَ الْحَيِّ وَتَرْزُقُ مَنْ تَشاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ (27)","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-2","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"قلت: (اللهم) منادى مبني على الضم، حذفت منه الياء المتضمنة للفرق، وعوضت منها الميم المُؤْذِنة بالجمع، لئلا يبقى بين الداعي والمدعو فَرْقٌ(1) ، و (مالك) : نعت لمحل المنادي لأنه مفعول، ومنادى ثانٍ عند سيبويه، لأن الميم عنده تمنع الوصفية.","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-3","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلِ يا محمد في استنصارك على عدوك: اللَّهُمَّ يا مالِكَ الْمُلْكِ مُلك الدنيا وملك الآخرة، تُؤْتِي الْمُلْكَ والنصر مَنْ تَشاءُ وَتَنْزِعُ الْمُلْكَ مِمَّنْ تَشاءُ، فهب لنا ملك الدارين،","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-4","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"والنصر على الأعداء في كل أين، وانزع الملك من يد عدونا، وانقله إلينا وإلى من تبعنا إلى يوم الدين. قال قتادة:","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-5","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"(ذكر لنا أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم سأل ربه أن يجعل مُلك فارس والروم في أمته، فأنزل الله تعالى هذه الآية) .","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-6","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"وَتُعِزُّ مَنْ تَشاءُ بالإيمان والطاعة وَتُذِلُّ مَنْ تَشاءُ بالكفر والمعصية، أو تعز من تشاء بالمعرفة، وتذل من تشاء بالفكرة، أو تعز من تشاء بالقناعة والورع، وتذل من تشاء بالحرص والطمع، أو تعز من تشاء بالتوفيق والإذعان، وتذل من تشاء بالكسل والخذلان، بِيَدِكَ الْخَيْرُ كله، فأعطنا من خيرك الجزيل، وأجرنا من الشر الوبيل، فالأمور كلها بيدك.","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-7","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"قال البيضاوي: ذكر الخير وحده لأنه المقضى بالذات، والشر مقضى بالعرض إذ لا يوجد شر جزئي ما لم يتضمن خيراً كليّاً. أو لمراعاة الأدب في الخطاب، أو لأن الكلام وقع فيه، إذ رُوِيَ أنه عليه الصلاة والسلام- لَمَّا خَطَّ الخَنْدَقَ، وقَطَعَ لكل عَشَرَة أربعينَ ذِرَاعاً، وأخذوا يَحْفرُون، فظهر فيه صخْرَةٌ عظيمةٌ لم تَعْمَلْ فيها المَعَاوِلُ، فَوَجَّهُوا سلْمَانَ إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يخبره، فجاء عليه الصلاة والسلام، فأخذ المعْول منه، فَضَرب به ضَرْبَةً صدعَهَا، وَبَرَقَ منها برق أضَاءَ ما بَيْنَ لابَتَيْها(1) ، لكأن مصباحاً في جوْف بَيتِ مُظلم، فكَبَّرَ، وكَبَّرَ معه المسلمونَ، وقال: أضَاءَتْ لي مِنْهَا قُصُور الحيرة، كأنها أنيابُ الكلاب، ثم ضرب الثانية، فقال: أضَاءَتْ لي مِنْها القُصور الحمر من أرض الروم، ثم ضرب الثالثة، فقال: أضاءت لي منها قُصُورُ صَنعاء، وأخْبرَنِي جِبْريل أنَّ أُمَّتِي ظَاهرةٌ علَى كُلِّها، فأبشروا، فقال المنافقون: ألا تَعْجَبُون! يمنيكم ويعدكم الباطل، ويُخبركم أنه يبصر من يثرب قصور الحِيَرةِ، وأنَّها تُفْتحُ لَكُمْ، وأنتم إنما تَحْفُرون الخنْدَقَ مِنَ الفَرَق(2) فنزلت، أي: الآية. ونبّه على أن الشر أيضاً بيده بقوله: إِنَّكَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-8","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"ثم استدلّ على نفوذ قدرته بقوله: تُولِجُ اللَّيْلَ فِي النَّهارِ أي: تُدخل أحدَهما في الآخر بالتعقيب، أو بالزيادة أو النقص، فيولج الليلَ في النهارِ، إذا طال النهار حتى يكون خمس عشرة ساعة، وفي الليل تِسْعٌ، ويُولج النهارَ في الليل، إذا طال الليل كذلك، وفيه دلالة على أنَّ مَنْ قَدَر على ذلك قدر على معاقبة العز بالذل، والمُلك بنزعه. وَتُخْرِجُ الْحَيَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَتُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتَ مِنَ الْحَيِّ كالحيوانات من النُّطَف، وبالعكس، والنباتات من الحبوب، وبالعكس، أو المؤمن من الكافر والعالم من الجاهل، وبالعكس، وَتَرْزُقُ مَنْ تَشاءُ من الأقوات والعلوم والأسرار، بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ، ولا تقدير ولا حصر. اللهم ارزقنا من ذلك الحظ الأوفر، (إِنك على كل شيءٍ قدير) .","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-9","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"روى معاذ رضي الله عنه أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال له: «يا معاذُ، أتحبُّ أن يقضيَ اللهُ عنك دَيْنك؟» قال: نعم يا رسول الله، قال: «قل» (اللهم مالك الملك) إلى قوله: (بغير حساب) ، رحمان الدنيا والآخرة ورحيمهما، تعطي منهما ما تشاء، وتمنع منهما ما تشاء، اقضِ عني ديني، فلو كان عليك ملءُ الأرض ذهباً وفضة لأدَّاه الله عنك» .","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-10","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"وروى عن على رضي الله عنه أنه قال: الفاتحة، وآية الكرسي، و (شهد الله) ، و (قل اللهم مالك الملك ... ) إلى ( ... بغير حساب) ، لمّا أراد الله أن ينزلهن، تعلقن بالعرش وقلن: تهبطنا إلى دار الذنوب فقال الله عزّ وجلّ: وعزّتي وجلالي لا يقرؤكن عبد، دبر كل صلاة مكتوبة، إلا أسكنته حظيرة القدس، على ما كان فيه، وإلا نظرت إليه بعيني المكنونة في كل يوم سبعين نظرة، وقضيت له في كل يوم سبعين حاجة، وأعززته من كل عدو، نصرته عليه(1) ... »","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-11","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"الحديث . انظر الثعلبي.","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-12","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"الإشارة: من ملك نفسه وهواه فقد ملكه الله ملك الدارين، ومن ملكته نفسه وهواه فقد أذلّه الله فى الدارين، ومن ملك نفسه لله فقد مكنه الله من التصرف في الكون بأسره، وكان حرّاً حقيقة، وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-13","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"دَعَوْنِي لمُلْكِهم، فلمَّا أجبتُهم ... قالُوا: دَعَوْنَاك للمُلْك لا للمِلْكِ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-14","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"ومن أذلَّ نفسه لله فقد أعزّه الله، قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-15","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"تَذَلَّلْ لِمَنْ تَهْوَى لِتَكْسِبَ عِزةً ... فكم عزة قد نالها المرء بِالذُّلِّ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-16","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"إِذَا كَانَ مَنْ تَهْوى عَزِيزاً وَلَمْ تَكُنْ ... ذَلِيلاً لَهُ، فَاقْرَ السَّلامَ على الْوصْلِ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-17","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"قال ابن المبارك: (قلت لسفيان الثوري: من الناس؟ قال: الفقهاء، قلت: فمن الملوك؟ قال: الزهاد، قلت: فمن الأشراف؟ قال: الأتقياء، قلت فمن الغوغاء؟ قال: الذين يكتبون الحديث ليستأكلوا به أموال الناس، قلت: أخبرني ما السفلة؟ قال: الظلمة.) وقال الشبلي: (المُلك هو الاستغناء بالمكون عن الكونين) . وقال الوراق: (تُعز من تشاء بقهر النفس ومخالفة الهوى، وتذل من تشاء باتباع الهوى) . قلت: وفي ذلك يقول البرعى رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-18","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"لا تتبع النفس في هَوَاهَا ... إنَّ اتِّبَاعَ الْهَوَى هَوَانُ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-19","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"وقال وهب: «خرج الغِنَى والعز يجولان، فلقيا القناعة فاستقرا» . وقال عيسى عليه السلام لأصحابه: أنتم أغنى من الملوك، قالوا: يا روح الله كيف، ولسنا نملك شيئاً؟ قال: أنتم ليس عندكم شيء ولا تريدونها، وهم عندهم أشياء ولا تكفيهم هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-20","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"قال الشافعي رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-21","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"أَلاَ يا نفسُ إن ترضَيْ بِقُوتٍ ... فأنت عزيزةٌ أبداً غنيهْ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-22","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"دَعِي عنكِ المطامِعَ والأمانِي ... فكمْ أُمْنِيَّةٍ جَلبَتْ مَنِيهْ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-23","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"وقال آخر(1) :","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-24","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"أَفَادتني القناعةُ كلَّ عزٍّ ... وهَلْ عِزٍّ أعزُّ مِنْ القَنَاعَهْ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-25","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"فَصَيِّرْها لنفسِكَ رأسَ مالٍ ... وصَيِّرْ بعدها التَّقْوى بِضَاعَهْ","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-26","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"تَنَل عِزّاً وتَغْنَى عَنْ لَئِيمٍ ... وتَرْحَلْ للجِنَان بصبر ساعة","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-27","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"وقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «مِن أَصْبَحَ آمِناً فِي سِرْبِه، مُعَافى فِي بَدنه، عنده قوت يومه، فكأنما حيزت له الدنيا بحذافيرها» .","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-28","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"تولج ليل القبض في نهار البسط، وتولج نهار البسط في ليل القبض، وترزق من تشاء فيهما من العلوم والأسرار، بغير حساب ولا مقدار، أو تولج ليل العبودية في نهار الحرية، وتولج نهار الحرية فى ليل العبودية، فمن كان في نهار الحرية تاه على الوجود، ومن كان في ليل العبودية عطل ذله ذل اليهود، والعبد لا يخلو من هذين الحالين، يتعاقبان عليه تعاقب الليل والنهار. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-26-27-29","r":"q3-26-27","title":"3:26–27 · The Master of dominion","text":"ولما كان العز ينال بصحبة أهل العز، والذل ينال كذلك، حذر الحق تعالى من صحبة أهل الذل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-26-27-29"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s1","r":"q3-26-27","title":"The invocation Allāhumma","text":"I say: Allāhumma ( اللهم ) is a vocative ( منادى ), indeclinably built upon ḍamma. The vocative yāʾ, which contains a suggestion of separation ( الفرق ), has been omitted and replaced by mīm, intimating gathering ( الجمع ), so that no separation remains between caller and Called. [A039] “Master” ( مالك ) qualifies the syntactic position of the vocative, since the vocative is an object. According to Sībawayh it is a second vocative, because for him the mīm prevents an adjectival qualification.","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s2","r":"q3-26-27","title":"Dominion, exaltation and abasement","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Say,” Muḥammad, when seeking help against your enemy: “O God, Master of dominion,” the dominion of this world and the hereafter, “You give dominion,” and victory, “to whom You will, and take dominion from whom You will.” Grant us, then, the dominion of both abodes, and victory over enemies everywhere. Take dominion from our enemy’s hand and transfer it to us and to those who follow us until the Day of Recompense. Qatāda said: “We have been told that the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, asked his Lord to place the dominion of Persia and Byzantium in his community, and God revealed this verse.” “You exalt whom You will,” through faith and obedience, “and abase whom You will,” through unbelief and disobedience. Or: You exalt whom You will through gnosis and abase whom You will through reflection. [A040] Or: through contentment and scrupulousness, as against avidity and greed; or through divinely granted success and submission, as against laziness and abandonment. “In Your hand is good,” all of it. Give us, then, of Your abundant good, and shelter us from grievous evil, for all affairs are in Your hand.","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s3","r":"q3-26-27","title":"Good, evil and the promise at the Trench","text":"Al-Bayḍāwī says: “He mentions good alone because it is decreed in itself ( بالذات ), whereas evil is decreed incidentally ( بالعرض ): no particular evil exists without encompassing a universal good. Or it is out of reverent propriety in address, or because the discourse concerns good.” [A041] For it is related that when the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, marked out the Trench, allotting forty cubits to every ten men, they began digging and encountered a great rock upon which the picks made no impression. They sent Salmān to inform the Messenger. He came, took the pick from him and struck a blow that split it. A flash shone from it, lighting the space between the town’s two lava tracts like a lamp in a dark house. He proclaimed God’s greatness and the Muslims did likewise. He said, “The palaces of al-Ḥīra have been illuminated for me through it, like dogs’ fangs.” He struck again and said, “The red palaces in the land of Byzantium have been illuminated for me.” At the third blow he said, “The palaces of Ṣanʿāʾ have been illuminated for me, and Gabriel has told me that my community will prevail over them all. Receive the good tidings!” The hypocrites said: “Are you not astonished? He fills you with hopes and false promises, telling you that from Yathrib he sees al-Ḥīra’s palaces and that they will be conquered for you, while you are only digging the Trench out of fear!” The verse was then revealed. By “You have power over all things,” He draws attention to the fact that evil too is in His hand. End of al-Bayḍāwī’s passage. [A042]","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s4","r":"q3-26-27","title":"The alternation of life and its conditions","text":"He then adduces evidence for His effectual power: “You cause night to enter day,” one entering the other through succession, or increase and decrease. Night enters day when day lengthens to fifteen hours and night has nine; day enters night when night lengthens correspondingly. This indicates that One able to do this is able to replace might with abasement, and dominion with its removal. [A043] “You bring the living from the dead and the dead from the living”: animals from seminal drops and vice versa, plants from seeds and vice versa; or the believer from the unbeliever and the learned from the ignorant, and conversely. “You provide for whom You will,” with nourishment, knowledge and mysteries, “without reckoning,” measure or limit. O God, give us the fullest share of this: You have power over all things.","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s5","r":"q3-26-27","title":"Invocation, debt and the verses after prayer","text":"Muʿādh—God be pleased with him—reports that the Prophet said to him: “Muʿādh, would you like God to discharge your debt?” He answered, “Yes, Messenger of God.” He said: “Recite ‘O God, Master of dominion …’ as far as ‘without reckoning,’ then say, ‘All-Merciful and Ever-Merciful of this world and the hereafter, You give from them what You will and withhold from them what You will: discharge my debt.’ Even if you owed the earth’s fill of gold and silver, God would discharge it for you.” [A044] It is related from ʿAlī—God be pleased with him—that when God wished to send down al-Fātiḥa, the Throne Verse, “God bears witness …,” and “O God, Master of dominion …” as far as “without reckoning,” they clung to the Throne and said, “Will You send us down to the abode of sins?” God, mighty and majestic, replied: “By My might and majesty, no servant recites you after every prescribed prayer without My settling him in the holy precinct, whatever his condition; without My looking upon him with My hidden eye seventy times each day, fulfilling seventy needs for him each day, and strengthening him against every enemy and granting him victory over him ….” Consult al-Thaʿlabī for the report. [A045]","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s6","r":"q3-26-27","title":"Self-mastery, contentment and true sovereignty","text":"Whoever masters his lower self and desire has been given by God dominion over both abodes. Whoever is mastered by his lower self and desire has been abased by God in both abodes. Whoever masters himself for God is enabled by God to exercise disposal throughout the cosmos, and is truly free. Concerning this the poet says: They called me to their dominion; when I answered, they said, “We called you to sovereignty, not to possession.” [A046] Whoever abases himself before God is exalted by God. The poet says: Be humble before the one you love, to gain might: how much might a person has gained through humility! If the one you love is mighty and you will not be humble before him, bid farewell to communion. Ibn al-Mubārak said: “I asked Sufyān al-Thawrī, ‘Who are the people?’ He answered, ‘The jurists.’ ‘Who are the kings?’ ‘The ascetics.’ ‘Who are the noble?’ ‘The godfearing.’ ‘Who are the rabble?’ ‘Those who write down hadith in order to consume people’s wealth through it.’ ‘Tell me, who are the base?’ ‘The oppressors.’” Al-Shiblī said: “Sovereignty is being independent of both worlds through their Maker.” Al-Warrāq said: “You exalt whom You will by subduing the lower self and opposing desire, and abase whom You will by following desire.” I say: al-Buraʿī—God be pleased with him—says of this: Do not follow the soul in its desire: following desire is abasement. Wahb said: “Wealth and might went wandering, met contentment, and settled there.” Jesus, peace be upon him, told his disciples: “You are richer than kings.” They asked, “Spirit of God, how, when we possess nothing?” He answered: “You have nothing and desire nothing; they have things, and those things do not suffice them.” End of quotation. Al-Shāfiʿī—God be pleased with him—said: My soul, if you are content with sustenance, you are forever mighty and rich. Leave greed and wishful hopes aside: how many a hope has brought death! Another says: Contentment has given me every kind of might: what might is mightier than contentment? Make it your capital, then make godfearingness your merchandise. You will gain might, need no base person, and journey to the Gardens through an hour’s patience. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever awakens secure in his dwelling, sound in body, possessing that day’s sustenance, has, as it were, the whole world gathered for him.” [A047]","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s7","r":"q3-26-27","title":"Contraction, expansion, servanthood and freedom","text":"You cause the night of contraction ( القبض ) to enter the day of expansion ( البسط ), and the day of expansion to enter the night of contraction. In both You provide knowledge and mysteries to whom You will without reckoning or measure. Or You cause the night of servanthood to enter the day of freedom, and the day of freedom to enter the night of servanthood. Whoever is in freedom’s day exults above existence; whoever is in servanthood’s night is so humbled that his abasement eclipses that of the Jews. [A048] The servant is never without these two states: they alternate over him as night and day alternate. And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-26-27-s8","r":"q3-26-27","title":"","text":"Since might is acquired through the companionship of the mighty, and abasement likewise, the Real, exalted is He, warns against keeping company with the abased, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-26-27-s8"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-28-30","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure 3:28–30","anchor":"unit-q3-28-30"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-1","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"لا يَتَّخِذِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ الْكافِرِينَ أَوْلِياءَ مِنْ دُونِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ فَلَيْسَ مِنَ اللَّهِ فِي شَيْءٍ إِلاَّ أَنْ تَتَّقُوا مِنْهُمْ تُقاةً وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللَّهُ نَفْسَهُ وَإِلَى اللَّهِ الْمَصِيرُ (28) قُلْ إِنْ تُخْفُوا ما فِي صُدُورِكُمْ أَوْ تُبْدُوهُ يَعْلَمْهُ اللَّهُ وَيَعْلَمُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ وَاللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (29) يَوْمَ تَجِدُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا عَمِلَتْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ مُحْضَراً وَما عَمِلَتْ مِنْ سُوءٍ تَوَدُّ لَوْ أَنَّ بَيْنَها وَبَيْنَهُ أَمَداً بَعِيداً وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللَّهُ نَفْسَهُ وَاللَّهُ رَؤُفٌ بِالْعِبادِ (30)","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-2","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"قلت: (تُقاة) : مصدر تَقَى، على وزن فَعَل، وله مصدران آخران: تُقّى وتَقِيَّة- بتشديد الياء-، وبه قرأ يعقوب، وأصله: تُقِيَة، فقلبت الياء ألفاً لتحركها وانفتاح ما قبلها. و (يوم) : ظرف، والعامل فيه: اذكر، أو اتقوا، أو المصير، أو تود، و (ما عملت) : مبتدأ، و (تود) : خبر، أو معطوف على (ما عملت) الأولى، و (تود) : حال.","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-3","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، لقوم من الأنصار، كانوا يُوالون اليهود لقرابة أو صداقة تقدمت في الجاهلية: لا يَتَّخِذِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ الْكافِرِينَ أَوْلِياءَ، أي: أصدقاء، إذ الحب إنما يكون في الله والبغض في الله، أو لا تستعينوا بهم في غزو ولا غيره، فلا تودوهم مِنْ دُونِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إذ هم أحق بالمودة، ففيهم مَنْدُوحة عن موالاة الكفرة، وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ الاتخاذ فَلَيْسَ مِنَ ولاية اللَّهِ فِي شَيْءٍ إذ لا تجتمع ولاية الله مع ولاية عدوه. قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-4","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"تَوَدُّ عَدُوِّي ثُمِّ تَزْعُمُ أنَّني ... صَدِيقكَ، لَيْسَ النّوْك عَنْكَ بِعَازِبِ","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-5","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"والنُّوك- بضم النون-: الحُمْق.","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-6","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"فلا تُوالوا الكفار إِلَّا أَنْ تَتَّقُوا مِنْهُمْ تُقاةً أيْ: إلا أن تخافوا من جهتهم ما يجب اتقاؤه، فلا بأس بمداراتهم ظاهراً، والبعد منهم باطنا، كما قال عيسى عليه السلام: (كن وَسَطاً وامْشِ جانباً) . وقال ابن مسعود رضي الله عنه: خالطوا الناس وزايلوهم، وصافحوهم بما يشتهون، ودينكم لا تَثْلُموه. وقال جعفر الصادق: إني لأسمع الرجل يشتمني في المسجد، فأستتر منه بالسارية لئلا يراني. هـ. وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللَّهُ نَفْسَهُ أي: يخوفكم عذابه على موالاة الكفار ومخالفة أمره وارتكاب نهيه، تقول العرب: احذر فلاناً: أي: ضرره لا ذاته، وفي ذكر النفس زيادة تهديد يُؤذِن بعقاب يصدر منه بلا واسطة، وَإِلَى اللَّهِ الْمَصِيرُ فيحشر كل قوم مع مَن أحب.","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-7","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"قُلْ إِنْ تُخْفُوا ما فِي صُدُورِكُمْ من موالاة أعدائه، أَوْ تُبْدُوهُ يَعْلَمْهُ اللَّهُ فلا يخفى عليه ما تُكن الصدور من خير أو شر. وقدَّم في سورة البقرة الإبداء، وأخره هنا لأن المحاسبة لا ترتيب فيها بخلاف العلم، فإن الأشياء التي تبرز من الإنسان يتقدم إضمارها في قلبه ثم تبرز، فقد تعلق علم الله تعالى بها قبل أن تبرز، فلذلك قدَّم هنا الإخفاء لتقدم وجوده في الصدر، وأخره في البقرة، لأن المحاسبة لا ترتيب فيها، وَيَعْلَمُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ فلا يخفى عليه شيء، وَاللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ فيقدر على عقوبتكم إن لم تنتهوا، والآية بيان لقوله: وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللَّهُ نَفْسَهُ لأن الذات العالية متصفة بعلم محيط بجميع المعلومات، وبقدرة تحيط بجميع المقدورات، فلا تجسروا على عصيانه، فإنه ما من معصية إلا وهو مطلع عليها، قادرٌ على العقاب عليها يوم القيامة.","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-8","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"يَوْمَ تَجِدُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا عَمِلَتْ مِنْ خَيْرٍ مُحْضَراً بين يديها تنتفع به، وَما عَمِلَتْ مِنْ سُوءٍ تَوَدُّ لَوْ أَنَّ بَيْنَها وَبَيْنَهُ أَمَداً بَعِيداً، كَما بَيْن المشرقِ والمغرب، ولا ينفع الندم وقد زلَّت القدم. وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللَّهُ نَفْسَهُ، كرره للتأكيد وزيادة التحذير، وسيأتي في الإشارة حكمة تكريره، وَاللَّهُ رَؤُفٌ بِالْعِبادِ حيث حذرهم مما يضرهم، وأمرهم بما يقربهم، فكل ما يصدر منه- سبحانه- في غاية الكمال.","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-9","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"الإشارة: لا ينبغي للمريد الصادق أن يخالط أهل الغفلة، ولا يتودد معهم فإن ذلك يقطعه عن ربه، ويصده عن دواء قلبه، وفي ذلك يقول صاحب العينية:","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-10","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"وَقَاطِعْ لِمَنْ واصلت أيام غفلة ... فما وَاصَلَ العُذْالَ إلاَّ مُقَاطِعُ","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-11","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"وجانب جناب الأجنبي لو أنه ... لقرب انتساب في المنام مضاجع","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-12","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"فللنفس من جلاسها كل نسبة ... ومن خلة للقلب تلك الطبائع","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-13","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"إلا أن يتقي منهم تقية، بحيث تلجئه الضرورة إلى مخالطتهم، فيخالطهم بجسمه ويفارقهم بقلبه، وقد حذَّر الصوفية من صحبة أرْبَع طوائف: الجبابرة المتكبرون، والقراء المداهنون، والمتفقرة الجاهلون، والعلماء المتجمدون لأنهم مُولَعون بالطعن على أولياء الله، يرون ذلك قربة تُقربهم إلى الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-14","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"ثم قال: (ويحذركم الله نفسه) أن تقصدوا معه غيره، وهذا خطاب للسائرين بدليل تعقيبه بقوله: (وإلى الله المصير) أي: إليه ينتهي السير وإليه يكون الوصول، ثم شدد عليهم في المراقبة فقال: (إن تُخفوا ما في صدوركم) من الميل أو الركون إلى الغير أو الوقوف عن السير، (أو تبدوه يعلمه الله) فينقص عنكم المدد بقدر ذلك الميل، يظهر ذلك يوم الدخول إلى بلاد المشاهدة، (يَوْمَ تَجِدُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ) ما قدّمت من المجاهدة، فبقدر المجاهدة تكون المشاهدة. ثم خاطب الواصلين فقال: (ويحذركم الله نفسه) من أن تشهدوا معه سواه، فلو كُلّف الواصل أن يشهد غيره لم يستطع، إذ لا غير معه حتى يشهده. ويدل على أن الخطاب هنا للواصلين تعقيبه بالمودة والرأفة، اللائقة بالواصلين المحبوبين العارفين الكاملين. خرطنا الله في سلكهم بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-28-30-15","r":"q3-28-30","title":"3:28–30 · Allegiance, watchfulness and the day of disclosure","text":"ثم لا طريق للوصول إلى هذا كله إلا باتباع الرسول الأعظم، كما أشار إلى ذلك بقوله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-28-30-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-28-30-s1","r":"q3-28-30","title":"Precaution and the day of disclosure","text":"I say: tuqāt ( تقاة ) is a verbal noun of taqā, on the pattern faʿal. It has two other verbal nouns, tuqā and taqiyya ( تقيّة ), with doubled yāʾ; Yaʿqūb recites the latter. The original of tuqāt is tuqaya: yāʾ changes to alif because it is vocalized and preceded by fatḥa. “The day” is an adverbial expression governed by an understood “remember” or “beware,” or by “the return” or “will wish.” “Whatever it has done” is a subject, with “will wish” its predicate; alternatively, it is coordinated with the first “whatever it has done,” and “will wish” is a circumstantial clause. [A049]","anchor":"en-q3-28-30-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-28-30-s2","r":"q3-28-30","title":"Loyalty and outward accommodation under fear","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, addresses a group of the Anṣār who maintained bonds with Jews because of kinship or friendship dating from the pre-Islamic period: “Let not believers take unbelievers as awliyāʾ,” friends. Love should be for God and hatred for God. Or: do not seek their assistance in warfare or otherwise. Do not therefore love them “instead of believers,” who are more entitled to affection and provide an alternative to allegiance with unbelievers. Whoever does this has no share in God’s friendship, since friendship with God and friendship with His enemy cannot be combined. [A050] The poet says: You love my enemy, yet claim that I am your friend: foolishness has not departed from you. Nūk ( النُّوك ), with ḍamma, means foolishness. Do not ally yourselves with unbelievers “unless you guard yourselves against them as a precaution”: unless you fear something from their side that must be guarded against. Then there is no harm in outward accommodation while remaining inwardly distant. As Jesus, peace be upon him, said, “Be in the midst, but walk to the side.” Ibn Masʿūd—God be pleased with him—said: “Mix with people and remain distinct from them; meet them with what pleases them, but do not impair your religion.” Jaʿfar al-Ṣādiq said: “I may hear a man insulting me in the mosque and conceal myself behind a pillar so that he does not see me.” End of quotation. “God warns you of Himself”: He makes you fear His punishment for taking unbelievers as allies, opposing His command and committing what He forbids. Arabs say, “Beware of so-and-so,” meaning his harm, not his person. Mentioning “Himself” intensifies the threat, indicating punishment proceeding from Him without intermediary. “To God is the return”: each people will be gathered with those it loved.","anchor":"en-q3-28-30-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-28-30-s3","r":"q3-28-30","title":"The order of concealment and disclosure","text":"“Say: Whether you conceal what is in your breasts,” of allegiance to His enemies, “or disclose it, God knows it.” No good or evil concealed in breasts is hidden from Him. In al-Baqara [2:284] He puts disclosure first, whereas here He puts it last. Reckoning has no such order, unlike knowledge: what a person brings forth is first inwardly conceived in his heart, then appears. God’s knowledge is related to it before it appears. Thus concealment comes first here because it exists in the breast beforehand; it comes last in al-Baqara because reckoning has no such order. [A051] “He knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth”: nothing escapes Him. “God has power over all things,” and can therefore punish you if you do not desist. This verse explains “God warns you of Himself”: the Exalted Essence is characterized by knowledge encompassing everything knowable and power encompassing everything possible. Do not venture to disobey Him: there is no act of disobedience of which He is unaware, or which He is unable to punish on the Day of Resurrection. “On the day when every soul finds present whatever good it has done,” before it for its benefit, and whatever evil it has done, “it will wish there were a far distance between itself and it,” as between east and west. Regret does not avail after the foot has slipped. “God warns you of Himself”: repeated for emphasis and further warning; the wisdom of its repetition will be given in the allusion. “God is tender towards His servants,” warning them against what harms them and commanding what brings them near. Everything proceeding from Him, glory to Him, is of utmost perfection.","anchor":"en-q3-28-30-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-28-30-s4","r":"q3-28-30","title":"Companionship and the two warnings","text":"The sincere disciple should not mix with the heedless or cultivate their affection, for this cuts him off from his Lord and diverts him from his heart’s remedy. The author of the ʿAyniyya says: Break with those you kept company with in heedlessness: only one who severs communion keeps company with reproachers. Avoid the outsider’s side, even if through close kinship he shares your sleeping-place. The soul receives every affinity from its companions, and from friendship the heart receives those dispositions. The exception is necessary precaution, when need compels such association. He then mixes with them bodily and parts from them in his heart. The Sufis have warned against accompanying four groups: arrogant tyrants, compromising reciters, ignorant pretenders to spiritual poverty, and rigid scholars. These are addicted to attacking God’s friends, regarding it as a deed that brings them near to God. [A052] He then says, “God warns you of Himself”: against seeking another together with Him. This addresses the wayfarers, as is shown by the following words, “To God is the return”: in Him the journey ends, and to Him is arrival. He then intensifies the demand for watchfulness ( المراقبة ): “Whether you conceal what is in your breasts,” of inclination towards another, reliance upon another or halting on the journey, “or disclose it, God knows it.” Reinforcement is diminished in proportion to that inclination. This becomes manifest on the day of entering the lands of witnessing, “the day when every soul finds” what it has put forward of struggle: according to the struggle is the witnessing. He then addresses those who have arrived: “God warns you of Himself,” against witnessing another together with Him. Were the arrived one charged with witnessing another, he could not: there is no other with Him to witness. That this addresses those who have arrived is indicated by its being followed by affection and tenderness, appropriate to the beloved who have arrived, the perfected gnostics. May God include us in their company through His gracious favour and generosity.","anchor":"en-q3-28-30-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-28-30-s5","r":"q3-28-30","title":"","text":"There is no path to attaining all this except following the greatest Messenger, as He indicates in His words:","anchor":"en-q3-28-30-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-31-32","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger 3:31–32","anchor":"unit-q3-31-32"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-1","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"قُلْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُحِبُّونَ اللَّهَ فَاتَّبِعُونِي يُحْبِبْكُمُ اللَّهُ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوبَكُمْ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (31) قُلْ أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَالرَّسُولَ فَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ الْكافِرِينَ (32)","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-2","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"قلت: قد تقدّم الكلام على حقيقة المحبة عند قوله يُحِبُّونَهُمْ كَحُبِّ اللَّهِ. وقال البيضاوي هنا: المحبة ميلُ النفس إلى الشيء لإدراك كمال فيه، بحيث يحملها- أي الميل- إلى ما يقربها إليه، والعبد إذا علم أن الكمال الحقيقي ليس إلا لله، وأن ما يراه كمالاً من نفسه أو غيره فهو من الله وبالله وإلى الله، لم يكن حبه إلا لله وفي الله، وذلك يقتضي إرادة طاعته، فلذلك فُسرت المحبة بإرادة الطاعة، وجعلت مستلزمة لاتباع الرسول في عبادته، والحرص على مطاوعته. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-3","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"وقوله: (فإن تولوا) : فعل ماض مجزوم المحل، ولم يدغمه البَزِّي هنا، على عادته في الماضي، لعدم موجبه.","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-4","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد لمن يدّعي أنه يحب الله ولا يتبع رسوله: إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُحِبُّونَ اللَّهَ كما زعمتم، فَاتَّبِعُونِي في أقوالي وأفعالي وأحوالي، يُحْبِبْكُمُ اللَّهُ أي: يرضى عنكم ويقربكم إليه، وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوبَكُمْ أي: يكشف الحجاب عن قلوبكم بغفران الذنوب ومحو العيوب، فيقربكم من جناب عزه، ويبوئكم في جِوار قدسه، وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ لمن تحبب إليه بطاعته واتباع رسوله.","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-5","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"قُلْ أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ فيما يأمركم به وينهاكم عنه، وَالرَّسُولَ فيما يَسُنه لكم ويرغبكم فيه، فَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا وأعرَضوا عنه، فقد تعرضوا لمقت الله وغضبه بكفرهم به فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ الْكافِرِينَ أي: لا يرضى عنهم ولا يقبل عليهم، وإنما لم يقل: لا يحبهم لقصد العموم، والدلالة على أن التولي عن الرسول كفر، وأنه برئ من محبة الله، وأن محبته مخصوصة بالمؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-6","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"رُوِيَ أن نصارى نجران قالوا: إنما نعظم المسيح ونعبده، حباً لله وتعظيماً لله. فقال تعالى: (قل) يا محمد: إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُحِبُّونَ اللَّهَ تعالى فَاتَّبِعُونِي ... الآية. ولما نزلت الآية قال عبد الله بن أُبَيّ لأصحابه: إن محمداً يجعل طاعته كطاعة الله، ويأمرنا أن نحبه كما أحبت النصارى عيسى، فنزل قوله تعالى: قُلْ أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَالرَّسُولَ الآية. وقال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «من أطاعني فقد أطاع الله، ومن أَطَاعَ الإمامَ فَقدْ أطَاعَنِي، وَمَنْ عَصَانِي فَقَدْ عَصَى الله وَمَنْ عصَى الإمامَ فَقَدْ عَصَانِي» .","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-7","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"الإشارة: اتباع الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم رُكن من أركان الطريقة، وشرط في إشراق أنوار الحقيقة، فمن لا اتباع له لا طريق له، ومن لا طريق له لا وصول له، قال الشيخ زروق رضي الله عنه: (أصول الطريقة خمسة أشياء: تقوى الله في السر والعلانية، واتباع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم في الأقوال والأفعال، والإعراض عن الخلق في الإقبال والإدبار، والرجوع إلى الله في السراء والضراء، والرضى عن الله في القليل والكثير) .","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-8","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"فالرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- حجاب الحضرة وبَوَّابُها، فمن أتى من بابه بمحبته واتباعه، دخل الحضرة، وسكن فيها، ومن تنكب عنها طُرِد وأُبعد، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-9","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"وأنتَ بابُ الله، أيّ امرئ ... وافاه من غَيْرِكَ لاَ يدْخُلُ","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-10","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"وقال في المباحث:","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-11","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"تَبِعَهُ العَالِم في الأقوال ... والعابد الزاهد في الأفعال","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-12","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"وفيهما الصوفي في السباق ... لكنه قد زاد في الأخْلاَقِ","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-13","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"فمن ادّعى محبة الله أو محبة رسوله، ولم يطعهما، ولم يتخلق بأخلاقهما، فدعواه كاذبة، وفي ذلك يقول ابن المبارك(1) :","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-14","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"تَعْصِي الإله وأنت تظهر حبه ... هذَا محَالٌ في القِيَاسِ بديع","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-15","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"لو كان حبك صادقا لأطعته ... إن المحب لِمَنْ يُحِبُّ مُطِيعُ","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-31-32-16","r":"q3-31-32","title":"3:31–32 · Love proved by following the Messenger","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى بيان نشأة عيسى عليه السلام، وبيان أصله ونشأة أمه، توطئة للكلام مع النصارى والرد عليهم في اعتقادهم فيه. وقال البيضاوي: لما أوجب الله طاعة الرسل، وبيَّن أنها الجالبة لمحبة الله، عقَّب ذلك ببيان مناقبهم تحريضا عليها فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-31-32-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-31-32-s1","r":"q3-31-32","title":"Love, perfection and obedience","text":"I say: the reality of love has already been discussed at “they love them as God is loved” [2:165]. Al-Bayḍāwī says here: “Love is the soul’s inclination towards something because it perceives perfection in it, so that this inclination carries it towards what brings it near. When the servant knows that true perfection belongs only to God, and that whatever perfection he sees in himself or another is from God, through God and to God, his love can only be for God and in God. This entails the will to obey Him. Love is therefore interpreted as the will to obey, and is made to require following the Messenger in his worship and eagerly complying with him.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q3-31-32-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-31-32-s2","r":"q3-31-32","title":"“If they turn away”","text":"“If they turn away” ( فإن تولوا ) is a past verb occupying a jussive syntactic position. Al-Bazzī does not assimilate it here, in keeping with his treatment of the past tense, because the condition requiring assimilation is absent. [A053]","anchor":"en-q3-31-32-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-31-32-s3","r":"q3-31-32","title":"The claim of love and the lifting of the veil","text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: “Say,” Muḥammad, to those who claim to love God without following His Messenger: “If you love God,” as you assert, “follow me” in my words, deeds and states. “God will love you”: He will be pleased with you and bring you near. “He will forgive you your sins”: through forgiving sins and effacing faults, He will lift the veil from your hearts, bring you near the precinct of His might and settle you in His holy neighbourhood. “God is Forgiving, Merciful” to those who seek His love through obeying Him and following His Messenger. “Say: Obey God,” in what He commands and forbids, “and the Messenger,” in what he establishes for you and encourages you to do. “If they turn away,” rejecting him, they expose themselves to God’s abhorrence and anger through their unbelief in him. “God does not love the unbelievers”: He is neither pleased with them nor turns favourably towards them. He does not merely say, “He does not love them,” in order to generalize, show that turning away from the Messenger is unbelief and devoid of love for God, and indicate that His love belongs specifically to believers. It is related that the Christians of Najrān said: “We magnify and worship the Messiah only out of love and reverence for God.” He therefore said, “Say: If you love God, follow me ….” When the verse was revealed, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy told his companions: “Muḥammad makes obedience to himself like obedience to God and commands us to love him as the Christians loved Jesus.” Then “Say: Obey God and the Messenger …” was revealed. [A054] The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever obeys me obeys God; whoever obeys the imam obeys me. Whoever disobeys me disobeys God; whoever disobeys the imam disobeys me.” [A055]","anchor":"en-q3-31-32-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-31-32-s4","r":"q3-31-32","title":"Following the Prophet as a foundation of the Path","text":"Following the Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, is a pillar of the Path and a condition for the dawning of the lights of Reality. Whoever does not follow has no path; whoever has no path has no arrival. Shaykh Zarrūq—God be pleased with him—said: “The foundations of the Path are five: fear of God in private and public; following the Prophet in words and deeds; turning from creatures whether they approach or withdraw; returning to God in ease and hardship; and being content with God in little and much.” [A056] The Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, is the veil and doorkeeper of the Presence. Whoever comes through his door, loving and following him, enters the Presence and dwells there. Whoever turns aside from it is expelled and distanced. As the poet says: You are God’s door: whoever approaches Him other than through you does not enter. In the Mabāḥith : The scholar follows him in words, the worshipping ascetic in deeds. The Sufi races ahead in both, but adds the qualities of character. [A057] Whoever claims love for God or His Messenger, but does not obey them or take on their qualities of character, makes a false claim. Ibn al-Mubārak says of this: You disobey God while displaying love for Him: this is an impossibility, astonishing by every measure. Were your love truthful, you would obey Him: the lover obeys the one he loves.","anchor":"en-q3-31-32-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-31-32-s5","r":"q3-31-32","title":"","text":"The Real, exalted is He, then explains Jesus’ formation, his origin and his mother’s upbringing, preparing to address the Christians and refute their belief about him. Al-Bayḍāwī says: having made obedience to the messengers obligatory and shown that it brings God’s love, He follows it with an account of their excellences to encourage that obedience, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-31-32-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-33-37","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration 3:33–37","anchor":"unit-q3-33-37"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-1","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفى آدَمَ وَنُوحاً وَآلَ إِبْراهِيمَ وَآلَ عِمْرانَ عَلَى الْعالَمِينَ (33) ذُرِّيَّةً بَعْضُها مِنْ بَعْضٍ وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ (34) إِذْ قالَتِ امْرَأَتُ عِمْرانَ رَبِّ إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لَكَ ما فِي بَطْنِي مُحَرَّراً فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّي إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ (35) فَلَمَّا وَضَعَتْها قالَتْ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَضَعْتُها أُنْثى وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِما وَضَعَتْ وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنْثى وَإِنِّي سَمَّيْتُها مَرْيَمَ وَإِنِّي أُعِيذُها بِكَ وَذُرِّيَّتَها مِنَ الشَّيْطانِ الرَّجِيمِ (36) فَتَقَبَّلَها رَبُّها بِقَبُولٍ حَسَنٍ وَأَنْبَتَها نَباتاً حَسَناً وَكَفَلَها زَكَرِيَّاءُ كُلَّما دَخَلَ عَلَيْها زَكَرِيَّا الْمِحْرابَ وَجَدَ عِنْدَها رِزْقاً قالَ يا مَرْيَمُ أَنَّى لَكِ هذا قالَتْ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَشاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ (37)","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-2","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"قلت: (ذرية) : حال، أو بدل من الآلين، أو من نوح، أي: أنهم ذرية واحدة متشعبة بعضها من بعض.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-3","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"و (إذ قالت) : ظرف لعليم، أو بإضمار اذكر. و (محرراً) : حال، والتحرير: التخلص، يقال: حررت العبد، إذا خلصته من الرق، وحررت الكتاب، إذا أصلحته وأخلصته، ولم يبق فيه ما يحتاج إلى إصلاح، ورجل حُر، أي: خالص، ليس لأحد عليه متعلق، والطين الحُر، أي: الخالص من الحمأة. وقوله: (وإني سميتها مريم) : عطف على (إني وضعتها) ، وما بينهما اعتراض، من كلامها على قراءة التكلم، أو من كلام الله على قراءة التأنيث.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-4","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفى، آدَمَ بالخلافة والرسالة، وَنُوحاً بالرسالة والنِّذَارة، وَآلَ إِبْراهِيمَ بالنبوة والرسالة، وهم: إسحاق، ويعقوب والأسباط، وإسماعيل، وولده سيد ولد آدم نبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم بالنبوة والرسالة والمحبة الجامعة. وَآلَ عِمْرانَ، وهم موسى وهارون- عليهما السلام- وهو عمران بن يصهر","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-5","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"ابن فاهث بن لاوي بن يعقوب، أو المراد بعمران: عمران بن أشهم بن أموي، من ولد سليمان عليه السلام، وهو والد مريم أم عيسى عليه السلام، وقيل: المراد عمران بن ماثان، أحد أجداد عمران والد مريم. وإنما خصّ هؤلاء، لأن الأنبياء كلهم من نَسْلهم. وقيل: أراد إبراهيم وعمران أنفسهما. «وآل» مقحمة، كقوله: وَبَقِيَّةٌ مِمَّا تَرَكَ آلُ مُوسى وَآلُ هارُونَ أي: موسى وهارون، فقد فضل الحقّ- جلّ جلاله- هؤلاء الأنبياء بالخصائص الجسمانية والروحانية عَلَى الْعالَمِينَ أي: كلاً على عَالَمِي زمانه، وبه استدلّ على فضلهم على الملائكة. حال كونهم ذُرِّيَّةً متشعبة بَعْضُها مِنْ ولد بَعْضٍ في النسب والدين، وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ لأقوال العباد وأعمالهم، عَلِيمٌ بسرائرهم وعلانيتهم، فيصطفي من صفا قوله وعمله، وخلص سره، للرسالة والنبوة.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-6","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"ثم تخلًّص لذكر نشأة مريم، توطئة لذكر ولدها، فقال: واذكر إِذْ قالَتِ امْرَأَتُ عِمْرانَ وهي حنة بنت فاقوذا، جدة عيسى عليه السلام: رَبِّ إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لَكَ ما فِي بَطْنِي مُحَرَّراً لخدمة بيت المقدس، لا أشغله بشيء، أو مخلصاً للعبادة، فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّي إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ، وكان المحرر عندهم، إذا حُرر، جُعل في الكنيسة يقوم عليها وينكسها، ولا يبرح منها حتى يبلغ الحلم، ثم يُخَيَّر، فإن أحبَّ أقام أو ذهب حيث شاء، ولم يكن يحرر إلا الغلمان لأن الجارية لا تصلح للخدمة لما يصيبها من الحيض، فحررت أمُّ مريمَ حمْلَها ولم تَدْرِ ما هو.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-7","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"وقصة ذلك: أن زكريا وعمران تزوجا أختين، فتزوج زكريا أشياعَ بنت فاقوذا، وتزوج عمران حنة بنت فاقوذا، فكان عيسى ويحيى ابني الخالة(1) ، وكانت حنة عاقراً لا تلد، فبينما هي في ظل شجرة، بصُرت بطائر يطعم فرخاً، فتحركت لذلك نفسها للولد فدعت الله تعالى، وقالت: اللهم لك علي، إن رزقتني ولداً، أن أتصدق به على بيت المقدس، يكون من سدنته وخدمه، فحملت بمريم، فهلك عمران، وحنة حامل بمريم، فَلَمَّا وَضَعَتْها أي: النذيرة، أو ما في بطنها، قالت: رَبِّ إِنِّي وَضَعْتُها أُنْثى، قالت ذلك تحسّراً وتحزناً إلى ربها، لأنها كانت ترجو أن تلد ذكراً يصلح للخدمة، ولذلك نذرته.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-8","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"قال تعالى: وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِما وَضَعَتْ، تعظيماً لموضوعها وتنويهاً بشأنها، أو من كلامها- على قراءة التكلم- تسلية لنفسها، أي: ولعل لله فيه سرّاً، قال تعالى: وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنْثى أي: وليس الذكر الذي طلبت كالأنثى التي وهبت، أو من كلامها، أي: وليس الذكر والأنثى سيان فيما نذرتُ. ثم قالت: وَإِنِّي سَمَّيْتُها مَرْيَمَ راجية أن يطابق اسمُها فعلها، فإن مريم فى نعتهم هى العابدة الخادمة، وكانت مريم أجمل النساء في وقتها وأفضلهن، وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «حَسْبُكَ من نساءِ العالمين أربع: مريم بنت عمران، وآسية امرأة فرعون، وخديجة بنت خويلد، وفاطمة بنت محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم» .","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-9","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"ثم قالت حنة أم مريم: وَإِنِّي أُعِيذُها بِكَ أي: أحصنها بك وَذُرِّيَّتَها مِنَ الشَّيْطانِ الرَّجِيمِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-10","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"المرجوم بالشهب، أو المطرود، وفي الحديث: «مَا مِنْ مَوْلُودٍ يُولَدُ إلاَّ والشَّيْطَانُ يَمَسُّهُ حِينَ يُولَد فَيَسْتَهِلُّ مِنْ مَسِّهِ، إلاَّ مَرْيَمَ وابْنهَا» . ومعناه: أن الشيطان يطمع في إغواء كل مولود، بحيث يتأثر به، إلا مريم وابنها لمكان الاستعاذة، قلت: وكذا الأنبياء كلهم، لا يمسهم لمكان العصمة. والله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-11","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"فَتَقَبَّلَها رَبُّها أي: رَضِيَها في النذر مكان الذكَر، بِقَبُولٍ حَسَنٍ أي: بوجه حسن، وهو إقامتها مقام الذكر، وتسلمها للخدمة عقب ولادتها قبل أن تكبر وتصلح للسِّدانة(1) ، رُوِي: أن حنة لما ولدتها لفَّتْها في خرقة، وحملتها إلى المسجد، ووضعتها عند الأحبار، وقالت: دونكم هذه النذيرة، فتنافسوا فيها، لأنها كانت ابنة إمامهم، وصاحب قربانهم، فإن (بني ماثان) كانت رؤوس بني إسرائيل وملوكهم، فقال زكريا: أنا أحق بها، عندي خالتها، فأبوا إلا القرعة، وكانوا سبعة وعشرين، فانطلقوا إلى نهر، فألقوا فيه أقلامهم، فطفا قلم زكريا- أي: علا- على وجه الماء، ورسبت أقلامهم، فأخذها زكريا.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-12","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"وَأَنْبَتَها الله نَباتاً حَسَناً أي: رباها تربية حسنة، فكانت تشب في اليوم ما يشب المولود في العام، وكفلها زكريا أي: ضمها إليه وقام بأمرها. وقرأ عاصم- في رواية ابن عياش- بشدِّ الفاء، أي: وكفَّلها اللهُ زكريا، أي: جعله كافلاً لها وحاضناً. رُوِيَ: أنه لما ضمها إليه بنى لها بيتاً، واسترضع لها، فلما بلغت، بنى لها محراباً في المسجد، وجعل بابه في وسطه لا يرقى إليها إلا بسلم، ولا يصعد إليها غيره، وكان يأتيها بطعامها وشرابها كل يوم، وكان إذا خرج أغلق عليها سبعة أبواب.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-13","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"كُلَّما دَخَلَ عَلَيْها زَكَرِيَّا الْمِحْرابَ ليأتيها بطعامها، وَجَدَ عِنْدَها رِزْقاً أي: فاكهة في غير حينها، يجد فاكهة الشتاء في الصيف، وبالعكس، قالَ يا مَرْيَمُ أَنَّى لَكِ هذا أي: من أين لك هذا الرزق الآتي في غير أوانه، والأبواب مغلقة عليك؟ قالَتْ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ فلا يُستبعد، قيل: تكلمت صغيرة، وقيل: لم ترضع ثدياً قط، خلاف ما تقدم، وكان رزقها ينزل عليها من الجنة.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-14","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"ثم قالت: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَشاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ أي: بغير تقدير، أو بغير استحقاق تفضلاً منه، وقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-15","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"(كلما) : يقتضي التكرار، وفيه إشارة إلى أنَّ زكريا لم يَذَرْ تَعهُّدهَا، ولم يعتمد على ما كان يجد عندها، بل كان يتفقد حالها كل وقت، لأن الكرامات للأولياء ليس مما يجب أن تدوم قطعاً، بل يجوز أن يظهر ذلك عليهم دائماً وألا يظهر، فما كان زكريا معتمداً على ذلك، فيترك تفقد حالها، ثم كان يجدد السؤال بقوله: يا مَرْيَمُ أَنَّى لَكِ هذا، لجواز أن يكون الذي هو اليوم لا على الوجه الذي كان بالأمس، فإنه لا واجب على الله- سبحانه-. قاله القشيري.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-16","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"رَوى جابر بنُ عبد الله أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أقام أياماً لم يطعم الطعام، فقام في منازل أزواجه، فلم يصب عندهن شيئاً، فأتى فاطمة فقال: «يا بُنيةُ، هل عندك شيء؟» فقالت: لا والله، بأبي أنت وأمي، فلما خرج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، بعثت إليها جارتُها برَغِيفَيْن وبِضْعَة لَحْم، فبعثت حَسَناً وحسينا إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فجاء، فكشفت له الجفنة، فإذا الجفنة مملوءة خُبْزاً ولَحْماً، فَبُهِتَتْ، وعرفت أنَّهَا بَرَكَةٌ مِن اللهِ تعالى، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «من أين لك هذا يا بنيّة؟» قالت: هو مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَشاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ، فحمد الله تعالى، وقال: «الحمْدُ للهِ الَّذِي جَعلَك شَبِيهَةً بسَيِّدَةِ بَنِي إسْرَائِيل، فإنها كانت إذا رزقها الله شيئاً قالت: هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَشاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسابٍ ثم بعث النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم إلى علىّ رضي الله عنه. ثم أكل أهلُ البيت كلهم، وجميع أزواج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، وبقيت الجَفْنة كما هي، فأَوْسَعَتْ علَى الجيران، وجعل الله فيها بركة وخيراً. انتهى(1) .","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-17","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"الإشارة: (إن الله اصطفى آدم ونوحاً وآل إبراهيم وآل عمران على العالمين) ، إنما اصطفى الحق تعالى هؤلاء الرسل لكونهم قد أظهروا الدين بعد انطماس أنواره، وجددوه بعد خمود أسراره، هم أئمة الهدى ومقتبس أنوار الاقتداء، فكل من كان على قدمهم من هذه الأمة المحمدية، بحيث يجدد للناس دينهم، ويُبين للناس معالم الطريق وطريق السلوك إلى عين التحقيق، فهو ممن اصطفاه الله على عالمي زمانه.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-18","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"وفي الحديث: «إن الله يَبْعَثُ عَلَى رَأسِ كُلِّ مِائَةِ سَنَةٍ مَنْ يُجَدِّدُ لهذِه الأمة دِينَهَا» . قال الحريري: (مات الحسن البصري عشية جمعة- أي: بعد زوالها- فلما صلّى الناس الجمعة حملوه، فلم يترك الناس صلاة العصر في مسجد الجماعة بالبصرة منذ كان الإسلام، إلا يوم مات الحسن، واتبع الناس جنازته، فلم يحضر أحد في المسجد صلاة العصر، قال: وسمعت منادياً ينادي: (إن الله اصطفى آدم ونوحاً وآل إبراهيم وآل عمران على العالمين) ، واصطفى الحسن على أهل زمانه) . قلت: والحسن البصري هو الذي أظهر علم التصوّف، وتكلم فيه وهذبه. قال في القوت: وهو إمامنا في هذا العلم- يعني علم التصوف.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-19","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"وقوله تعالى: إِذْ قالَتِ امْرَأَتُ عِمْرانَ ... الآية. كُلُّ من نذر نفسه وحررها لخدمة مولاه، تقبلها الله منه بقبول حسن، وأنبت فيها المعرفة نباتاً حسناً، وكفلها بحفظه ورعايته، وضمها إليه بسابق عناية، ورزقها من طُرَفِ الحِكَم وفواكه العلوم، مما لا تحيط به العقول وغاية الفهوم، فإذا قال لنفسه: من أين لك هذا؟ (قالت هو من عند الله إن الله يرزق من يشاء بغير حساب) . وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-20","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"فَلاَ عَمَلٌ مِنِّي إليه اكْتَسَبْتُه ... سِوَى مَحْضِ فَضْلٍ، لا بشيءٍ يُعلَّلُ","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-21","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"وقال القشيري: قوله تعالى: (فتقبلها ربها بقبول حسن) ، يقال: منَ القبول الحسن أنه لم يطرح كَلَّهَا وشَغْلَهَا على زكريا، فكان إذا دخل عليها زكريا ليتعاهدها بطعام وجد عندها رزقاً، ليعلم العالمون أن الله- تعالى- لا يلقى شغل","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-22","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"أوليائه على غيره، ومن خدم وليّاً من أوليائه كان هو في رفق الولي، وهذه إشارة لمن يخدم الفقراء، يعلم أنه في رفقهم، لا أن الفقراء تحت رفقه. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-33-37-23","r":"q3-33-37","title":"3:33–37 · The chosen households and Mary’s consecration","text":"قال أهل التفسير: فلما رأى زكريا ما يأتي لمريم من الفواكه في غير أوانها، قال: إن الذي قدر على أن يأتي مريم بالفاكهة في غير وقتها، قادر على أن يصلح زوجتي، ويهب لي ولداً على الكبر. فطلب الولد، كما أشار الحق تعالى إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-33-37-23"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-33-37-s1","r":"q3-33-37","title":"“Offspring” and the meaning of dedication","text":"I say: “Offspring” ( ذُرِّيَّةً ) is an accusative of state ( حال ), or a substitute ( بدل ) for the two families, or for Noah: that is, they are one offspring, branching forth, some from others. “When the wife [of ʿImrān] said” ( إذ قالت ) is an adverbial expression ( ظرف ) governed by “Knowing” ( عليم ), or by an understood “remember” ( اذكر ). “Consecrated” ( محرَّرًا ) is an accusative of state ( حال ). Taḥrīr ( التحرير ) means setting free or purifying. One says “I freed the slave” when I released him from bondage; and “I revised [or purified] the writing” when I corrected it and made it sound, leaving nothing that still required amendment. A free man ( حُرّ ) is one unencumbered by another’s claim; pure clay is clay free of black mud. Her saying “I have named her Mary” ( وإني سميتها مريم ) is coordinated ( عطف ) with “I have given birth to her” ( إني وضعتها ); what intervenes is a parenthesis ( اعتراض ). On the reading in the first person, this is part of her speech; on the reading in the third-person feminine, it is speech from God. [XIV-N001]","anchor":"en-q3-33-37-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-33-37-s2","r":"q3-33-37","title":"The families singled out for divine election","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “God chose Adam”—through the vicegerency ( الخلافة ) and messengership ( الرسالة ); “and Noah”—through messengership and warning ( النذارة ); “and the family of Abraham”—through prophecy and messengership, including Isaac, Jacob, the tribes, Ishmael, and his descendant, our Prophet Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, the master of Adam’s offspring, distinguished by prophecy, messengership and love that gathers all [excellences]. “And the family of ʿImrān”: either Moses and Aaron—peace be upon them—their father being ʿImrān son of Yiṣhar son of Qāhith son of Levi son of Jacob; or ʿImrān son of Ashham son of Umawī, a descendant of Solomon, who was the father of Mary the mother of Jesus. It is also said that the reference is to ʿImrān son of Māthān, an ancestor of Mary’s father ʿImrān. These are singled out because the prophets descend from them. Some hold that Abraham and ʿImrān themselves are intended and the word āl (“family”) is inserted, as in “the relics left by the family of Moses and the family of Aaron” [2:248], meaning Moses and Aaron themselves. The Real, exalted is His majesty, favoured those prophets in bodily and spiritual characteristics “above the worlds”—each over the people of his own age. This has also been used as an argument for their superiority over angels. They are “offspring, some from others,” their lineages and their religion connected. “And God is All-Hearing” of the servants’ words and acts, “All-Knowing” of their outward and inward conditions; He therefore selects for prophecy and messengership those whose speech and works are pure and whose innermost secret is sincere.","anchor":"en-q3-33-37-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-33-37-s3","r":"q3-33-37","title":"Ḥanna’s vow and Mary’s birth","text":"He then turns to Mary’s upbringing as a preliminary to speaking of her son: “Remember when the wife of ʿImrān”—Ḥanna daughter of Fāqūdhā, Jesus’ grandmother—said, “My Lord, I have vowed to You what is in my womb, consecrated” ( محرَّرًا ) for the service of the Sacred House ( بيت المقدس ): I shall occupy this child with nothing else; or, wholly devoted to worship. “So accept it from me, for You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.” Among them, a child dedicated in this way was assigned to care for and sweep the place of worship; he did not leave it until puberty, when he could choose to remain or depart. Only boys were customarily dedicated, since girls were considered unsuitable for this service on account of menstruation. Mary’s mother made her vow without knowing what she carried. The account is that Zachariah and ʿImrān married two sisters: Zachariah married Ashyāʿ daughter of Fāqūdhā; ʿImrān married Ḥanna daughter of Fāqūdhā. Jesus and John were accordingly sons of maternal aunts. Ḥanna had been barren. One day in the shade of a tree she saw a bird feeding its young, and the sight stirred in her a longing for a child. She invoked God: “O God, should You grant me a child, I pledge to dedicate the child to the Sacred House as one of its custodians and servants.” She conceived Mary; ʿImrān died while Ḥanna was pregnant. “When she gave birth to her”—to the one she had vowed, or to what had been in her womb—she said, “My Lord, I have given birth to a female.” She spoke out of sorrow and disappointment before her Lord, for she had hoped for a boy suitable for service, which was why she had made the vow. “And God knew best what she had borne”: this magnifies the one born and draws attention to her rank. Alternatively, on the reading “and God knows best what I have borne” (with “I have borne” in the first person), it belongs to the mother’s words as consolation: perhaps God has placed a hidden purpose in this. “And the male is not like the female”: the boy she sought is not like the girl she was given. Alternatively, these are the mother’s words: a boy and a girl are not alike in the service she had vowed. She then said, “I have named her Mary,” hoping her conduct would accord with her name, which in their description signified one who worships and serves. Mary was the fairest and most excellent woman of her age. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is reported to have said: “Sufficient for you, among the women of all the worlds, are four: Mary daughter of ʿImrān, Āsiya the wife of Pharaoh, Khadīja daughter of Khuwaylid, and Fāṭima daughter of Muḥammad.” Ḥanna, Mary’s mother, continued: “I seek Your protection for her”—that is, I shelter her with You—“and her offspring from Satan the accursed,” either stoned with shooting stars or driven away. The Prophet is reported to have said: “No child is born without Satan touching him at birth, causing him to cry out by his touch, except Mary and her son.” Its meaning is that Satan seeks to mislead every newborn, so that the child is affected by him; Mary and her son are excepted by virtue of this invocation for protection. I say: likewise with all the prophets: he does not touch them on account of their protection from sin ( العصمة ). And God knows best. [XIV-N002] Translator’s note: Cairo I:346 prints وينكسها . The rendering “sweep” follows ويكنسها in al-Baghawī’s closely parallel account at3:35. The Cairo form appears to transpose two consonants; it is preserved in the Arabic transcription, and the reconstruction is disclosed here without claiming manuscript confirmation.","anchor":"en-q3-33-37-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-33-37-s4","r":"q3-33-37","title":"Acceptance, growth and Zachariah’s guardianship","text":"“Her Lord accepted her with a gracious acceptance”: He was satisfied to receive her in the fulfilment of the vow in place of a boy. The manner of this acceptance was beautiful: He put her in the boy’s position and received her into service immediately after her birth, before she had grown fit for custodianship ( السدانة ). It is related that Ḥanna wrapped the child in a cloth, carried her to the sanctuary, placed her before the learned custodians, and said: “Here is the child I have dedicated.” They vied to take charge of her, for she was the daughter of their leader and the man who presided over their offerings. The family of Māthān were leaders and kings among the Children of Israel. Zachariah said, “I have the strongest claim to her, for her maternal aunt is in my house.” They refused except by lot. All twenty-seven of them went to a river and cast their pens into it; Zachariah’s pen remained afloat on the water, while the others sank. So he took charge of her. [XIV-N003] “And caused her to grow with a beautiful growth”: God gave her a fine upbringing ( تربية حسنة ). She is said to have grown in a day as an ordinary infant grows in a year. “And Zachariah took her into his care” ( وَكَفَلَهَا زَكَرِيَّا ): he took her into his care and attended to her. In the reading transmitted from ʿĀṣim through Ibn ʿAyyāsh, the fāʾ is doubled ( كَفَّلَهَا ): God made Zachariah her guardian and fosterer. It is related that when he took her into his care, he built her a home and arranged for her to be nursed. When she came of age, he built her a sanctuary within the place of worship, its doorway partway up so that it could be reached only by a ladder. He alone could ascend to her. He brought her food and drink each day, locking seven doors when he left. “Whenever Zachariah entered the sanctuary to see her” and bring food, “he found provision with her”—fruit out of season: winter fruit in summer, and summer fruit in winter. “He said, Mary, whence is this for you?” How did such provision reach you out of season, with the doors locked? “She said, It is from God”; there is nothing unlikely in that. Some say she spoke while still a child; others that she was never suckled, contrary to the earlier account. Her provision, they say, descended from the Garden. “God provides for whomsoever He wills without reckoning” ( بغير حساب ): without measure or without anything being owed, solely through His grace. The expression “whenever” ( كلما ) implies repetition. It also indicates that Zachariah never abandoned his care of her or relied upon what he found: he continually inspected her circumstances. Extraordinary graces granted to God’s friends ( كرامات الأولياء ) are not bound to continue; they may be manifested constantly or may cease. Zachariah therefore did not cease looking after her. He kept asking “Mary, whence is this for you?” because what arrived today might have come in a different fashion from yesterday. Nothing is incumbent upon God—exalted is He. Thus al-Qushayrī. [XIV-N004]","anchor":"en-q3-33-37-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-33-37-s5","r":"q3-33-37","title":"Fāṭima’s provision","text":"Jābir son of ʿAbd Allāh relates that the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, went without food for several days. He visited the homes of his wives and found nothing, then went to Fāṭima and asked, “My daughter, do you have anything?” She replied, “No, by God—may my father and mother be your ransom.” After he left, a neighbour sent her two loaves and a piece of meat. She sent Ḥasan and Ḥusayn to fetch the Prophet. He arrived, and she uncovered the dish: it was full of bread and meat. She was astonished and knew it to be a blessing from God. He asked, “Whence is this for you, my daughter?” She answered, “It is from God. God provides for whomsoever He wills without reckoning.” He praised God and said, “Praise belongs to God who has made you like the foremost lady of the Children of Israel. Whenever God provided her with something, she said, ‘It is from God. God provides for whomsoever He wills without reckoning.’” The Prophet then sent for ʿAlī. The whole household and all the Prophet’s wives ate, yet the dish remained as before; she shared with the neighbours, and God bestowed abundant goodness and blessing in it. End of report. [XIV-N005]","anchor":"en-q3-33-37-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-33-37-s6","r":"q3-33-37","title":"The chosen renewers and consecration of the self","text":"“God chose Adam and Noah and the family of Abraham and the family of ʿImrān above the worlds.” The Real, exalted is He, chose these messengers because they made the religion visible again after its lights had become effaced, and renewed it after its mysteries had lain dormant. They are guides of right guidance and lamps from which the light of emulation is kindled. Whoever in this Muḥammadan community follows in their footsteps, renewing the religion for people, explaining the landmarks of the way and the path of spiritual travelling ( السلوك ) towards the very reality of realization ( عين التحقيق ), is among those whom God has chosen above the people of his own age. The hadith states: “At the head of every hundred years God sends one who renews this community’s religion.” Al-Ḥarīrī relates: “Al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī died on a Friday afternoon—that is, after the sun had passed its zenith. After the Friday prayer people carried him [to burial], and for the first time since Islam came to Basra, the congregational ʿaṣr prayer was not held in its mosque: all had followed his funeral procession. I heard a caller proclaiming, ‘God chose Adam and Noah and the family of Abraham and the family of ʿImrān above the worlds, and chose al-Ḥasan above the people of his age.’” I say: al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī was the one who made the science of Sufism ( علم التصوف ) manifest, spoke of it, and refined it. The Qūt says of him: “He is our imam in this science,” meaning Sufism. [XIV-N006] As for the verse “When the wife of ʿImrān said ...”: everyone who vows his self to God and sets it free ( حرّرها ) for the service of his Master is accepted graciously. God causes gnosis ( المعرفة ) to grow beautifully within him, assumes his protection and care, draws him near through preceding solicitude ( سابق العناية ), and provides him with rare insights of wisdom and fruits of knowledge beyond the scope of intellects and the utmost of understanding. When he asks himself, “Whence has this come to you?” his soul replies, “It is from God. God provides for whomsoever He wills without reckoning.” They recited: No work of mine earned it from Him; it came as sheer grace, whose gift no cause can explain. Al-Qushayrī says concerning “Her Lord accepted her graciously”: “Part of His gracious acceptance was that He did not place her entire burden and care upon Zachariah. Whenever Zachariah went to bring food, he found provision already there; thus those with knowledge might learn that God does not cast the burden of His friends upon others. Whoever serves one of His friends is himself under the friend’s kindly care: the friend is not under his.” This is an allusion for those who serve the poor [in the spiritual sense, الفقراء ], teaching them that they are within those servants’ care, not that the servants depend upon theirs. End of quotation. The commentators say: When Zachariah saw how fruits out of season came to Mary, he said to himself: The One who can bring fruit to Mary outside its season can restore my wife’s fertility and grant me a child in old age. So he sought a child, as the Real, exalted is He, indicates in what follows:","anchor":"en-q3-33-37-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-38-41","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John 3:38–41","anchor":"unit-q3-38-41"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-1","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"هُنالِكَ دَعا زَكَرِيَّا رَبَّهُ قالَ رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِنْ لَدُنْكَ ذُرِّيَّةً طَيِّبَةً إِنَّكَ سَمِيعُ الدُّعاءِ (38) فَنادَتْهُ الْمَلائِكَةُ وَهُوَ قائِمٌ يُصَلِّي فِي الْمِحْرابِ أَنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكَ بِيَحْيى مُصَدِّقاً بِكَلِمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَسَيِّداً وَحَصُوراً وَنَبِيًّا مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ (39) قالَ رَبِّ أَنَّى يَكُونُ لِي غُلامٌ وَقَدْ بَلَغَنِيَ الْكِبَرُ وَامْرَأَتِي عاقِرٌ قالَ كَذلِكَ اللَّهُ يَفْعَلُ ما يَشاءُ (40) قالَ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ لِي آيَةً قالَ آيَتُكَ أَلاَّ تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلاثَةَ أَيَّامٍ إِلاَّ رَمْزاً وَاذْكُرْ رَبَّكَ كَثِيراً وَسَبِّحْ بِالْعَشِيِّ وَالْإِبْكارِ (41)","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-2","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"قلت: (هنالك) : اسم إِشارة للبعيد، والكاف: حرف خطاب، يطابق المخاطب في التذكير والتأنيث والإفراد والجمع في الغالب. والمحراب: مفعال، من الحرب، وهو الموضع المعد للعبادة، كالمسجد ونحوه، سمي به، لأنه محل محاربة الشيطان.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-3","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"(والملائكة) : جمع تكسير، يجوز في فعله التذكير والتأنيث، وهو أحسن، تقول: قام الرجال وقامت الرجال، فمن قرأ: (فنادته الملائكة) ، فعلى تأويل الجماعة، ومن قرأ: (فناداه) ، أراد تنزيه الملائكة عن التأنيث، ردّاً على الكفار.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-4","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"والمراد هنا: جبريل عليه السلام كقوله: يُنَزِّلُ الْمَلائِكَةَ بِالرُّوحِ، وَإِذْ قالَتِ الْمَلائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ، و (بشر) : فيها لغتان: التخفيف، وهي لغة تهامة، تقول: بَشَرَ يَبْشُر- بضم الشين في المضارع، والتشديد، وهو أفصح، تقول بشّر يبشّر تبشيراً.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-5","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، مخبراً عن زكريا عليه السلام: هُنالِكَ أي: في ذلك الوقت الذي رأى ما رأى من الخوارق عند مريم، دَعا زَكَرِيَّا رَبَّهُ، فدخل المحراب، وغلق الأبواب، وقال في مناجاته: رَبِّ هَبْ لِي مِنْ لَدُنْكَ ذُرِّيَّةً طَيِّبَةً، كما وهبتها لحنَّة العجوز العاقر، إِنَّكَ سَمِيعُ الدُّعاءِ أي: مجيبه فاسمع دعائي يا","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-6","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"مجيب، فَنادَتْهُ الْمَلائِكَةُ، وهو جبريل، لأنه رئيس الملائكة، والعرب تنادي الرئيس بلفظ الجمع إذ لا يخلو من أصحاب، وَهُوَ قائِمٌ يُصَلِّي فِي الْمِحْرابِ رُوِيَ: أنه كان قائماً يصلّي في محرابه، فدخل عليه شاب، عليه ثياب بيض، ففزع منه، فناداه، وقال له: أَنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكَ بِيَحْيى، سمي به لأن الله تعالى أحيا به عقم أمه، أو لأن الله تعالى أحيا قلبه بمعرفته، فلم يهم بمعصية قط، أو لأنه استشهد، والشهداء أحياء.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-7","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"مُصَدِّقاً بِكَلِمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وهو عيسى، لأنه كان بكلمة: كُنْ، من غير سبب عادى، وَسَيِّداً أي: يسود قومه ويفوقهم، وَحَصُوراً، أي: مبالغاً في حبس النفس عن الشهوات والملاهي. رُوِيَ أنه مرَّ في صباه على صبيان، فدعوه إلى اللعب، فقال: ما للعب خلقت. أو عِنِّيناً، رُوِيَ: «أنه كان له ذَكَرٌ كالقذاة» رواه ابن عباس. وقال في الأساس: (رجل حصور: لا يرغب في النساء) . قيل: كان ذلك فضيلة في تلك الشريعة، بخلاف شريعة نبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم وفي الورتجبي: الحصور: الذي يملك ولا يملك. وقال القشيري: حَصُوراً: أي: مُعْتَقاً من الشهوات، مَكْفِيّاً أحكام البشرية، مع كونه مِن جملة البشر، وَنَبِيًّا مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ الذين صلحوا للنبوة وتأهلوا للحضرة.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-8","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"ولما سمع البشارة هزَّه الفرحُ فقال: يا رَبِّ أَنَّى يَكُونُ لِي غُلامٌ أي: من أين يكون لي غلام؟! قاله استعظاماً أو تعجباً أو استفهامًا عن كيفية حدوثه. هل مع كبر السن والعقم، أو مع زوالهما. وَقَدْ بَلَغَنِيَ الْكِبَرُ، وكان له تسع وتسعون سنة، وقيل: مائة وعشرون، وَامْرَأَتِي عاقِرٌ لا تلد، ولم يقل: عاقرة، لأنه وصف خاص بالنساء. قال له جبريل: كَذلِكَ اللَّهُ يَفْعَلُ ما يَشاءُ من العجائب والخوارق، فيخلق الولد من العاقر والشيخ الفاني، أو الأمر كذلك، أي: كما أخبرتك، ثم استأنف: اللَّهُ يَفْعَلُ ما يَشاءُ.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-9","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"ولما تحقق بالبشارة طلبَ العلامةَ، فقال: رَبِّ اجْعَلْ لِي آيَةً أعرف بها حمل المرأة، لاستقبله بالبشاشة والشكر، قالَ آيَتُكَ أَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلاثَةَ أَيَّامٍ أي: لا تقدر على كلام الناس ثلاثاً، فحبس لسانه عن الكلام دون الذكر والشكر، ليخلص المدة للذكر والشكر، إِلَّا رَمْزاً بيد أو رأس أو حاجب أو عين. وَاذْكُرْ رَبَّكَ كَثِيراً في هذه المدة التي حبِسْتَ فيها عن الكلام، وهو يُبين الغرض من الحبس عن الكلام. وتقييد الأمر بالكثرة يدل على أنه لا يفيد التكرار. وَسَبِّحْ بِالْعَشِيِّ أي: من الزوال إلى الغروب، أو من العصر إلى جزء الليل، وَالْإِبْكارِ من الفجر إلى الضحى، وقيل: كانت صلاتهم ركعتين في الفجر وركعتين في المغرب، ويؤيد هذا قولُه تعالى في الآية الأخرى: فَأَوْحى إِلَيْهِمْ أَنْ سَبِّحُوا بُكْرَةً وَعَشِيًّا. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-10","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"الإشارة: الأصلاب الروحانية كالأصلاب الجسمانية، منها ما تكون عقيمة مع كمالها، ومنها ما تكون لها ولد أو ولدان، ومنها ما تكون لها أولاد كثيرة، ويؤخذ من قضية السيد زكريا عليه السلام: طلب الولد إذا خاف الولي اندراس","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-11","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"علمه أو حاله بانقطاع نَسْله الروحاني، ولا شك في فضل بقاء النسل الحسيّ أو المعنوي، وقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إِذَا مَاتَ العبدُ انْقَطَعَ عَمَلُه إِلاَّ مَن ثَلاثٍَ: صَدَقَةٍ جَارِيَةٍ، أَوْ وَلَدٍ صالح يدعُو لَهُ، أوْ عِلَم يُنْتَفَعُ به» .","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-12","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"وشمل الولد البشري والروحاني، وقال عليه الصلاة والسلام لسيدنا علي- كَرّم الله وجهه-: «لأنْ يَهْدِيَ اللهُ بِكَ رَجُلاً وَاحِداً خَيْرٌ لكَ مِنْ حُمْر النَعَمِ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-13","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"وقال بعض الشعراء(1) :","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-14","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"وَالمَرْءُ في مِيزانِه أتْباعُهُ ... فاقْدرْ إِذَنُ قَدْرَ النبي مُحمَّد","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-15","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"وقد سلَك هذا المسلك القطب ابن مشيش في طلب الولد الروحاني، حيث قال في تصليته المشهورة: (اسمع ندائي بما سمعت به نداء عبدك زكريا) ، فأجابه الحق تعالى بشيخ المشايخ القطب الشاذلي. وغير واحد من الأولياء دخل محراب الحضرة، ونادى نداءً خفيّاً في صلاة الفكرة، فأجابته الهواتف في الحال، بلسان الحال أو المقال: إن الله يبشرك بمن يحيي علمك ويرث حالك، مصدقاً بكلمة من الله، وهم أولياء الله، وسيداً وحصوراً عن شواغل الحس، مستغرقاً في مشاهدة القرب والأنس، ينبئ بعلم الغيوب، ويصلح خلل القلوب، فإذا استعظم ذلك واستغربه، قيل له: الأمر كذلك، (الله يفعل ما يشاء إِذا قضى أمرًا فإِنما يقولُ له كن فيكون) ، فحسبك الاشتغال بذكر الله، والغيبة عما سواه. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-38-41-16","r":"q3-38-41","title":"3:38–41 · Zachariah’s prayer and the promise of John","text":"ثم ذكر اصطفائية مريم بالخصوص بعد العموم فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-38-41-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-38-41-s1","r":"q3-38-41","title":"“There,” the sanctuary, and the angelic announcement","text":"I say: “There” ( هنالك ) is a demonstrative ( اسم إشارة ) indicating something distant. The kāf is a particle of address ( حرف خطاب ) which ordinarily agrees with the addressee in gender and number. Miḥrāb ( المحراب ) follows the pattern mifʿāl and derives from ḥarb , warfare. It names a place set aside for worship, such as a mosque, because it is where Satan is fought. “The angels” ( الملائكة ) is a broken plural ( جمع تكسير ). Its verb may be masculine or feminine, though the latter is preferable; thus one may say qāma al-rijāl or qāmat al-rijāl , “the men arose.” The reading “the angels called to him” with a feminine verb construes them as a group ( الجماعة ); the masculine reading, “he [or they] called,” is intended to keep the angels free from feminine description, in reply to the unbelievers. What is intended here is Gabriel, as in “He sends down the angels with the Spirit” [16:2] and “When the angels said, O Mary ...” [3:42]. In bashshara , “he gave glad tidings,” two forms occur: the light, ungeminated form, the idiom of Tihāma, bashara yabshuru (with ḍamma on the shīn of the imperfect), and the geminated form bashshara yubashshiru , which is more eloquent. [XIV-N007]","anchor":"en-q3-38-41-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-38-41-s2","r":"q3-38-41","title":"A child from the barren and the aged","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says concerning Zachariah, upon him peace: “There”—at the time he witnessed the extraordinary provision with Mary—“Zachariah invoked his Lord.” He entered his sanctuary, shut its doors and said in intimate address: “My Lord, grant me, from Yourself, good offspring,” just as You granted a child to Ḥanna, the elderly barren woman; “You are the Hearer of prayer”—its Answerer. Hear my supplication, O Answerer! “The angels called him”—that is, Gabriel, the chief of angels. Arabs refer to a leader in the plural, since he is not ordinarily without companions—“while he was standing in prayer in the sanctuary.” It is related that as he prayed a youth wearing white entered, and Zachariah was alarmed. The visitor called out, “God gives you glad tidings of John” ( يحيى ). He was so called because God gave new life through him to his mother’s barrenness; or because God brought his heart to life through gnosis ( المعرفة ), so that he never inclined towards an act of disobedience; or because he died a martyr, and martyrs are alive. “Confirming a Word from God”: the Word is Jesus, who came to be by the divine command “Be!” ( كُنْ ), without the customary natural cause. “A lordly leader” ( سيّدًا ): he will surpass and preside over his people. “Restrained” ( حصورًا ): one who exercises exceptional restraint over the self’s desires and diversions. It is reported that children invited him to play in his youth, and he replied: “I was not created for play.” Or it has been interpreted as a man incapable of sexual intercourse. It is related that “he had a male organ like a mote”; Ibn ʿAbbās transmits this. The Asās defines a ḥaṣūr as “a man who has no desire for women.” It is said that this was an excellence under his religious law, unlike the law of our Prophet Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him. Al-Wartajbī explains: the ḥaṣūr is one who rules [his impulses] without being ruled by them. Al-Qushayrī says: “Restrained” means set free from passions, spared the compulsion of ordinary human appetites even while remaining human. “A prophet among the righteous”: those fitted for prophecy and worthy of the [divine] Presence. [XIV-N008] On hearing the glad tidings, joy stirred him, and he exclaimed: “My Lord, how shall I have a boy?”—How can a son come to me? He spoke in wonder or amazement, or to ask how the birth would occur: with old age and barrenness remaining, or after their removal? “Old age has overtaken me”: he was ninety-nine, some say a hundred and twenty; “and my wife is barren” ( عاقر ), unable to conceive. The text does not say ʿāqira , since the adjective in this usage is particular to women. Gabriel said to him: “Thus does God do whatever He wills”—wonders and extraordinary events, bringing forth a child from a barren woman and an aged man. Or the sense is “The matter is as I have told you,” followed by a new sentence, “God does whatever He wills.” Having become certain of the promise, he asked for its sign: “My Lord, appoint for me a sign” by which I shall know of my wife’s pregnancy and greet it with delight and gratitude. “Your sign is that you shall not speak to people for three days”: you will be incapable of ordinary conversation during those three days. His tongue was withheld from speech but not from remembrance and thanksgiving, so that the time might be devoted entirely to them; “except by gesture,” with hand, head, eyebrow or eye. “Remember your Lord abundantly” in those days of speechlessness: the instruction indicates the purpose of his inability to speak. Specifying abundance also indicates that the bare imperative does not, by itself, entail repeated performance. “And glorify Him in the evening” ( العشيّ ), either from noon until sunset or from the late afternoon into the beginning of night, “and in the early morning” ( الإبكار ), from dawn to the forenoon. Some say that their prayers consisted of two cycles at dawn and two at sunset, supported by “He signalled to them to glorify [God] morning and evening” [19:11]. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-38-41-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-38-41-s3","r":"q3-38-41","title":"Spiritual children and the transmission of the Path","text":"Spiritual lineages ( الأصلاب الروحانية ) resemble bodily lineages ( الأصلاب الجسمانية ). Some remain without offspring despite their own perfection; some have one or two, while some have many. Zachariah’s story teaches the appropriateness of seeking offspring when a friend of God ( وليّ ) fears that his knowledge or state may disappear with the interruption of his spiritual descent. There is unquestionably merit in the continuation of offspring, sensible or spiritual. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “When a servant dies, his work comes to an end except for three: ongoing charity, a righteous child praying for him, or knowledge from which people benefit.” [XIV-N009] The “child” includes the bodily and the spiritual. The Prophet said to our master ʿAlī, may God ennoble his face: “For God to guide one person through you is better for you than red camels.” A poet said: A man’s followers are weighed with him: estimate, then, the rank of the Prophet Muḥammad! The pole Ibn Mashīsh pursued this course in asking for spiritual offspring. In his well-known invocation of blessings he said: “Hear my call as You heard the call of Your servant Zachariah.” The Real, exalted is He, answered him through the shaykh of shaykhs, the pole al-Shādhilī. Many a friend of God has entered the sanctuary of the Presence ( محراب الحضرة ) and called secretly in the prayer of contemplation ( صلاة الفكرة ), only to receive an immediate response from unseen calls, by the tongue of state ( لسان الحال ) or that of utterance ( لسان المقال ): “God gives you glad tidings of one who will revive your knowledge and inherit your state, confirming a Word from God”—that is, [one of] God’s friends—“a leader, restrained” from the preoccupations of sensory existence, immersed in witnessing nearness and intimacy, making known the knowledge of hidden things and restoring disordered hearts. Should the seeker regard this as extraordinary or impossible, he will be told: “Thus it is. God does whatsoever He wills. When He decrees a thing, He only says to it ‘Be!’ and it is” [3:47]. Let it suffice you to occupy yourself with God’s remembrance and to be absent from all besides Him. And success is through God; He guides to the even path. He next speaks of Mary’s particular election after the general mention of election, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-38-41-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-42-43","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood 3:42–43","anchor":"unit-q3-42-43"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-1","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"وَإِذْ قالَتِ الْمَلائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفاكِ وَطَهَّرَكِ وَاصْطَفاكِ عَلى نِساءِ الْعالَمِينَ (42) يا مَرْيَمُ اقْنُتِي لِرَبِّكِ وَاسْجُدِي وَارْكَعِي مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ (43)","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-2","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر إِذْ قالَتِ الْمَلائِكَةُ أي: جبريل، أو جماعة، كلمتها شفاهاً كرامةً لها.","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-3","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"وفيه إثبات كرامة الأولياء، وليست نبية(2) للإجماع على أنه تعالى لم يستنبئ امرأة لقوله: وَما أَرْسَلْنا قَبْلَكَ إِلَّا رِجالًا نُوحِي إِلَيْهِمْ فقالوا لها: يا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفاكِ لخدمة بيته، ولم يقبل قبلك أنثى قط، وفرغك لعبادته، وأغناك برزقه عن رزق غيره، وَطَهَّرَكِ من الأخلاق الذميمة، ومما يستقذر من النساء، وَاصْطَفاكِ ثانياً بهدايته لك، وتخصيصك بتكليم الملائكة، وبالبشارة بالولد من غير أب، فقد اصطفاك عَلى نِساءِ الْعالَمِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-4","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"وفى الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «كَمُلَ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ كَثِيرٌ ولَمْ يَكْمُلْ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ إلا مَرْيَمَ ابنةَ عِمْرَانَ، وآسِيَةَ بنت مزاحِم وخديجة بنت خويلد» ... الحديث. قال ابن عزيز: أي: عالمي دهرها، كما فُضِّلَتْ خديجة وفاطمة بنت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم على نساء أمة محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم، بل قال أبو عمر: فاطمة فُضلت على جميع النساء، وهو واضح، لحديث:","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-5","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"سيدة نساء أهل الجنة، لكن جاء في حديث آخر استثناء مريم. فالله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-6","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"وفي الاستيعاب: عن عمران بن حصين: أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم عاد فاطمة، وهي مريضة، فقال: «كيف تجدك يا بُنَيَّةُ؟» فقالت له: إني لوجعة، وإنه ليزيدني أني مالي طعام آكله، فقال: «يا بُنَيِّةُ، أما ترضين أنك سيدة نساء العالمين» ، فقالت: يا أبت، فأين مريم بنت عمران؟ قال: «تلك سيدةُ نُساءِ عالمها، وأنت سيدة نساء عالمك، والله لقد زوجتك سيّداً في الدنيا والآخرة» هـ. من المحشي.","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-7","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"يا مَرْيَمُ اقْنُتِي لِرَبِّكِ أي: أطيلي الصلاة شكراً لما اختصك به، وَاسْجُدِي وَارْكَعِي مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-8","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"صلِّي مع المصلين، وقدَّم السجود على الركوع، إما لكونه كذلك في شرعهم، أو للتنبيه على أن الواو لا ترتب، أو ليقترن ارْكَعِي بالراكعين، للإيذان بأنَّ من ليس في صلاتهم ركوعٌ ليسوا بمصلين. وقيل: المراد بالقنوت: إدامة الطاعة، كقوله: أَمَّنْ هُوَ قانِتٌ آناءَ اللَّيْلِ ساجِداً وَقائِماً، وبالسجود: الصلاة، لقوله: وَأَدْبارَ السُّجُودِ، وبالركوع: الخشوع والإخبات. قاله البيضاوي. وقال الأوزاعي: لما قالت لها الملائكة ذلك، قامت في الصلاة حتى تورمت قدمها وسالت دماً وقَيْحاً.","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-42-43-9","r":"q3-42-43","title":"3:42–43 · Mary’s election and the stages of servanthood","text":"الإشارة: لا يصطفي الله العبدَ لحضرته إلا بعد تطهيره من الرذائل، وتحليته بأنواع الفضائل، وقطعه عن قلبه الشواغل، والقيام بوظائف العبودية، وبالآداب مع عظمة الربوبية، والخضوع تحت مجاري الأقدار، والتسليم لأحكام الواحد القهار، فأنفاس المريد ثلاثة: عبادة، ثم عبودية، ثم عبودة، ثم يترقى إلى مطالعة علم الغيوب، الذي أشار إليه الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-42-43-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-42-43-s1","r":"q3-42-43","title":"The two elections of Mary","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Remember when the angels said”—Gabriel, or a company of angels, addressing Mary directly as a grace ( كرامة ) bestowed upon her. This establishes extraordinary graces for God’s friends ( كرامات الأولياء ). Mary was not a prophet, because of the consensus that God did not appoint a woman to prophecy, as indicated by “We sent before you only men to whom We revealed” [21:7]. [Translator’s note: The assertion of consensus is the author’s. The Cairo editor directs the reader to Fatḥ al-bārī , 6:542, on the question of Mary’s prophethood.] The angels said: “Mary, God has chosen you” for service in His House; before you He had not accepted a female for that service. He has freed you for His worship and sufficed you with His provision, without needing that of anyone else. “He has purified you” of blameworthy qualities and of what is considered impure in women; “and has chosen you” again through guidance, through addressing you by the angels, and through the annunciation of a son without a father. Thus He has chosen you above the women of the worlds. [XIV-N010] The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is reported to have said: “Many among men have attained perfection; among women only Mary daughter of ʿImrān, Āsiya daughter of Muzāḥim, and Khadīja daughter of Khuwaylid attained perfection ...” Ibn ʿAzīz says that “the worlds” means the people of her age, just as Khadīja and Fāṭima daughter of the Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, were favoured above the women of Muḥammad’s community. Abū ʿUmar even maintained that Fāṭima was favoured above all women, pointing to the report that she is the foremost woman of Paradise; but another report excepts Mary. God knows best. In the Istīʿāb there is a report from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn that the Prophet visited Fāṭima when she was ill and asked how she was. She replied that she was in pain, made worse by having nothing to eat. He asked whether she would not be content to be the foremost woman of the worlds. She said, “Father, then where is Mary daughter of ʿImrān?” He replied that Mary was the foremost woman of her world, while Fāṭima was foremost in hers, and that he had married her to a master in this world and the next. End of note from the glossator. [XIV-N011]","anchor":"en-q3-42-43-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-42-43-s2","r":"q3-42-43","title":"Devotion, bowing and prostration","text":"“Mary, be devoutly obedient to your Lord” ( اقنتي ): prolong your prayer in gratitude for what He has singled you out to receive. “Prostrate and bow with those who bow”: pray with those who pray. The verse mentions prostration before bowing either because that was the sequence in their religious law, or to show that the conjunction wa- (و) does not itself impose an order, or so that “bow” may stand next to “those who bow,” indicating that those whose prayer does not include bowing are not among those who pray [in this sense]. It has also been said that qunūt is continual obedience, as in “one devout during the night, prostrating and standing” [39:9]; sujūd denotes prayer, as in “after prostrations” [50:40]; while rukūʿ signifies humility and lowliness. Thus al-Bayḍāwī. Al-Awzāʿī relates that when the angels had said this to Mary, she stood in prayer until her feet swelled and discharged blood and pus. [XIV-N012]","anchor":"en-q3-42-43-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-42-43-s3","r":"q3-42-43","title":"Purification, obedience and opening to the unseen","text":"God does not choose the servant for His Presence before purifying him of vices ( الرذائل ), adorning him with the various virtues ( الفضائل ), cutting off the heart’s distracting occupations, and establishing him in the tasks of servanthood ( وظائف العبودية ) and the appropriate adab before the majesty of Lordship ( الربوبية ). The servant bows beneath the courses of destiny and yields to the decrees of the One, the Overpowering. The aspirant ( المريد ) has three breaths [or phases]: worship ( عبادة ), then servanthood ( عبودية ), then utter servantness ( عبودة ); from there he ascends to the contemplation of knowledge of hidden things, to which the Real alludes in what follows:","anchor":"en-q3-42-43-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-44","r":"q3-44","title":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation","text":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation 3:44","anchor":"unit-q3-44"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-44-1","r":"q3-44","title":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation","text":"ذلِكَ مِنْ أَنْباءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوحِيهِ إِلَيْكَ وَما كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ إِذْ يُلْقُونَ أَقْلامَهُمْ أَيُّهُمْ يَكْفُلُ مَرْيَمَ وَما كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ إِذْ يَخْتَصِمُونَ (44)","anchor":"ar-q3-44-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-44-2","r":"q3-44","title":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، لحبيبه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: ذلِكَ القصص الذي أطلعتك عليه، هو مِنْ أخبار الْغَيْبِ الذي لم يكن لك به شعور، وما عرفته إلا بوحينا وإعلامنا، فلا يشك في نبوتك إلا مطموس أعمى، (و) أيضاً: ما","anchor":"ar-q3-44-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-44-3","r":"q3-44","title":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation","text":"كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ","anchor":"ar-q3-44-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-44-4","r":"q3-44","title":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation","text":"أي: عندهم، حين كانوا يُلْقُونَ أَقْلامَهُمْ لما اقترعوا، أَيُّهُمْ يَكْفُلُ مَرْيَمَ، وَما كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ إِذْ يَخْتَصِمُونَ في كفالتها، فتخبرهم عما شهدت، بل لم يكن شيء من ذلك، فتعين أن يكون وحيا حقيقا، لأنه عليه الصلاة والسلام- كان أمياً لم يطالع شيئاً من كتب الأخبار، ولا جلس إلى من طالعهم من الأحبار، بإجماع الخاص والعام. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-44-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-44-5","r":"q3-44","title":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الوحي على أربعة أقسام: وحي منام، ووحي إلهام، ووحي أحكام، ووحي إعلام، وشاركت الأولياءُ الأنبياءَ في ثلاثة: الإلهام والمنام والإعلام، إن كان بغير الملَك، ومعنى وحي إعلام: هو إطلاع الله النبيّ على أمور مغيبة، فإن كان بواسطة الملك، فهو مختص بالأنبياء، كما اختصت بوحي الأحكام، وأما إن كان بالإلهام أو بالمنام أو بالفهم عن الله، فيكون أيضاً للأولياء، إذ الروح إذا تصفت وتطهرت من دنس الحس أطلعها الله على غيبه في الجملة، وأما التفصيل فلا يعلمه إلا علاّم الغيوب. والله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-44-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-44-6","r":"q3-44","title":"3:44 · Unseen reports and four kinds of revelation","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى البشارة بعيسى عليه السلام، وهو المقصود الأعظم من هذه القصص ليتخلص للرد على النصارى فى زعمهم الفاسد فيه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-44-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-44-s1","r":"q3-44","title":"The story as a sign of prophecy","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says to His beloved, blessings and peace be upon him: “That” account, which I have enabled you to know, belongs to “the tidings of the unseen” ( أنباء الغيب ), of which you had no previous awareness and which you knew only through Our revelation and communication. None therefore doubts your prophecy except one whose inward vision has been utterly extinguished. “You were not with them”—present among them—when they “cast their pens” to draw lots for “which of them would take charge of Mary.” “Nor were you with them when they disputed” over her guardianship, so as to have reported something you witnessed. None of that happened. It must therefore have been a true revelation ( وحي ), since the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, was unlettered ( أميّ ): he had not studied historical books or sat with scholars acquainted with them, as both the learned and the public agreed. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-44-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-44-s2","r":"q3-44","title":"Dream, inspiration, legislation and disclosure","text":"Know that waḥy ( الوحي ) is of four kinds: revelation in a dream ( وحي منام ), revelatory inspiration ( وحي إلهام ), revelation of rulings ( وحي أحكام ), and revelation conveying information ( وحي إعلام ). God’s friends share with the prophets in three of them: inspiration, dreams, and disclosure of information—provided that the last does not come through an angel. The meaning of waḥy al-iʿlām ( وحي إعلام ) is God’s acquainting a prophet with concealed matters. If it comes through an angel it belongs especially to prophets, just as revelation of rulings belongs especially to them. If, however, it comes by inspiration, dream or direct understanding from God ( الفهم عن الله ), it can also occur to God’s friends: once the spirit is clarified and cleansed of sensory defilement, God may disclose something of the unseen to it in a general way. Its particulars, however, none knows except the Knower of unseen things. And God knows best. [XIV-N013] The Real then mentions the good news concerning Jesus, upon him peace—the chief purpose of this narrative, since it prepares the rebuttal to the Christians’ mistaken claim about him—saying:","anchor":"en-q3-44-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-45-51","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus 3:45–51","anchor":"unit-q3-45-51"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-1","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"إِذْ قالَتِ الْمَلائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكِ بِكَلِمَةٍ مِنْهُ اسْمُهُ الْمَسِيحُ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ وَجِيهاً فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ (45) وَيُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ فِي الْمَهْدِ وَكَهْلاً وَمِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ (46) قالَتْ رَبِّ أَنَّى يَكُونُ لِي وَلَدٌ وَلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِي بَشَرٌ قالَ كَذلِكِ اللَّهُ يَخْلُقُ ما يَشاءُ إِذا قَضى أَمْراً فَإِنَّما يَقُولُ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ (47) وَيُعَلِّمُهُ الْكِتابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَالتَّوْراةَ وَالْإِنْجِيلَ (48) وَرَسُولاً إِلى بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ أَنِّي قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِآيَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ أَنِّي أَخْلُقُ لَكُمْ مِنَ الطِّينِ كَهَيْئَةِ الطَّيْرِ فَأَنْفُخُ فِيهِ فَيَكُونُ طَيْراً بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَأُبْرِئُ الْأَكْمَهَ وَالْأَبْرَصَ وَأُحْيِ الْمَوْتى بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَأُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِما تَأْكُلُونَ وَما تَدَّخِرُونَ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ إِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ لَآيَةً لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ (49)","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-2","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"وَمُصَدِّقاً لِما بَيْنَ يَدَيَّ مِنَ التَّوْراةِ وَلِأُحِلَّ لَكُمْ بَعْضَ الَّذِي حُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَجِئْتُكُمْ بِآيَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ (50) إِنَّ اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوهُ هذا صِراطٌ مُسْتَقِيمٌ (51)","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-3","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"قلت: (إذ قالت) : بدل من (وإذ قالت) الأولى، ويبعد إبدالها من (إذ يختصمون) ، و (المسيح) وما بعده: أخبار عن اسمه، أو (عيسى) : خبر عن مضمر، و (ابن مريم) : صفته، و (المسيح) : فعيل بمعنى مفعول، لأنه مُسِحَ من الأقذار، أي: طهر منها، أو مسح بالبركة، أو كان مسيح القدم، لا أخمص له، أو مسحه جبريل بجناحه من الشيطان. أو بمعنى فاعل لأنه كان يمسح المرضى فيبرءون، أو يمسح عين الأعمى فيبصر، أو لأنه كان يسيح في الأرض ولا يقيم في مكان فتكون الميم زائدة.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-4","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"وأما المسيح الدجّال فإنه ممسوح إحدى العينين، أو لأنه يطوف الأرض ويمسحها، إلا مكة والمدينة، والحاصل:","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-5","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"أن عيسى مسيح الخير، والدجال مسيح الشر، ولذلك قيل: إن المسيح يقتل المسيح. و (وجيهاً) : حال من (كلمة) لتخصيصه بالصفة، و (في المهد وكهلاً) : حالان، أي: طفلاً وكهلاً، والمهد: ما يمهد للصبي. و (رسولاً) : مفعولٌ لمحذوف، أي: ونجعله رسولاً، و (مصدقاً) : عطف على (رسولاً) ، و (لأُحِلَّ) : متعلق بمحذوف، أي: وجئتكم لأُحل.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-6","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"أو معطوف على معنى مصدقاً، كقولهم: جئتك معتذراً، أو لأطيب قلبك.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-7","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: (و) اذكر أيضا إِذْ قالَتِ الْمَلائِكَةُ في بشارتهم لمريم: يا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكِ بِكَلِمَةٍ مِنْهُ، أي: بولد يتكوَّن بكلمة من الله كن فيكون، وقيل: إنما سمى كلمة لكونه مظهراً لكلمة التكوين، متحققاً ومتصرفاً بها. ولذلك كان يظهر عليه خوارق الأقدار أكثر من غيره من الأنبياء، اسْمُهُ الْمَسِيحُ، واسمه عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ، وإنما قال: ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ والخطاب لها، تنبيهاً على أنه يولد من غير أب إذ الأولاد إنما تنسب لأبائها إلا إذا فقد الأب. ثم وصف الولد بقوله: وَجِيهاً فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ أي: شريفاً في الدنيا بالنبوة والرسالة، وفي الآخرة بالشفاعة لمن تبعه. ويكون مِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ إلى الله تعالى في الدارين.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-8","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"وَيُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ طفلاً فِي الْمَهْدِ على وجه خَرْق العادة في تبرئة أمه، وَكَهْلًا إذا كمل عقله قبل أن يرفع، أو بعد الرفع والنزول، لأن الكهولة بعد الأربعين، والتحقيق: أنه بشرها بنبوة عيسى وكلامه في المهد، معجزةً، وفي الكهولة دعوة قبل الرفع وبعده، وما قارب الشيء يُعطي حكمه، وحال كونه مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ لحضرة رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-9","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"ولما سمعت البشارة دهشت وقالَتْ: يا رَبِّ أَنَّى يَكُونُ لِي وَلَدٌ وَلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِي بَشَرٌ، والخطاب لله، فانية عن الواسطة جبريل، والاستفهام تعجباً، أو عن الكيفية: هل يكون بتزوج أم لا؟ قالَ لها الملك: كَذلِكِ اللَّهُ يَخْلُقُ ما يَشاءُ. أو الأمر كذلك كما تقولين، لكن اللَّهُ يَخْلُقُ ما يَشاءُ لا يحتاج إلى وسائط ولا أسباب، بل إِذا قَضى أَمْراً فَإِنَّما يَقُولُ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ، وَيُعَلِّمُهُ الْكِتابَ أي: الكتابة والخط، وَالْحِكْمَةَ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-10","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"النبوة، أو الإصابة في الرأي، وَالتَّوْراةَ وَالْإِنْجِيلَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-11","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"(و) يجعله رَسُولًا إِلى بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ. وكان أول رسل بني إسرائيل يوسف، وآخرهم عيسى- عليهما السلام-، وقال: عليه الصلاة والسلام: «بُعثْتُ على إِثْرِ ثمانية آلاف نبيّ، أربعة آلاف من بني إسرائيل» . فإذا بعث إليهم قال: أَنِّي قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِآيَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ أي: بأني قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِآيَةٍ مِّن ربكم، قالوا: وما هي؟ قال:","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-12","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"أَنِّي أَخْلُقُ لَكُمْ مِنَ الطِّينِ كَهَيْئَةِ الطَّيْرِ كصورته، فَأَنْفُخُ فِيهِ فَيَكُونُ طَيْراً بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ، وكان يخلق لهم صورة الخفاش، لأنها أكمل الطير لأن لها ثدياً وأسناناً وتحيض وتطير، فيكون أبلغ في المعجزة، وكان يطير مادام الناس ينظرون إليه، فإذا غاب عنهم سقط ميتاً ليتميز فعل الحق من فعل الخلق.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-13","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"ثم قال لهم: ولي معجزة أخرى أني أُبْرِئُ الْأَكْمَهَ الذي ولد أعمى، فأحرى غيره، وَالْأَبْرَصَ الذي فيه وضح(1) . وخصهما لأنهما عاهتان معضلتان. وكان الغالب في زمن عيسى الطب، فأراهم المعجزة من جنس ذلك. رُوِي: أنه ربما اجتمع عليه من المرضى في اليوم الواحد ألوف، من أطاق منهم البلوغ(2) أتاه، ومن لم يطق أتاه عيسى عليه السلام، وإنما كان يداويهم بالدعاء على شرط الإسلام.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-14","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"وَأُحْيِ الْمَوْتى بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ لا بقدرتي دفعاً لتوهم الألوهية، فإن الإحياء ليس من طوق البشر. رُوِيَ أنه أحيا أربعة أنفس: (العازر) ، وكان صديقاً له، فأرسلت أخته إلى عيسى أن أخاك العازر يموت، فأتاه من مسيرة ثلاثة أيام فوجده مات، فقال لأخته: انطلقي بنا إلى قبره، وهو في صخرة مطبقة، فدعا الله تعالى، فقام العازر يقطر ودكه(3) ، فعاش وولد له. و (ابن العجوز) ، مُر بجنازته على عيسى عليه السلام فدعا الله تعالى، فجلس على سريره، ونزل عن أعناق الرجال، ولبس ثيابه، وحمل سريره على عنقه، ورجع إلى أهله، وبقي حتى وُلد له. و (ابنة العاشر) ، كان يأخذ العشور، قيل له: أتحييها، وقد ماتت أمس؟ فدعا الله تعالى، فعاشت وولد لها. و (سام بن نوح) ، دعا باسم الله الأعظم، فخرج من قبره، وقد شاب نصف رأسه، فقال: أقامت الساعة؟ قال: لا، لكني دعوت الله فأحياك، مالى أرى الشيب في رأسك، ولم يكن في زمانك؟ قال: سمعت الصيحة، فظننت أن الساعة قامت فشبت من هولها. قيل: كان يحيي الموتى ب يا حيّ يا قيوم.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-15","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"وَأُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِما تَأْكُلُونَ وَما تَدَّخِرُونَ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ، لما أبرأ الأكمه والأبرص قالوا: هذا سحر، أخبرنا بما نأكل وما ندخر؟ فكان يُخبر الرجل بما يأكل في غدائه وعشائه. ورُوِيَ أنه لمَّا كان في المكتب، كان يحدث الغلمان بما يصلح لهم آباؤهم من الطعام، فيقول للغلام: انطلق ... غداء أهلك كذا وكذا، فيقول أهله: من أخبرك بهذا؟ قال: عيسى، فحبسوا صبيانهم عنه، وقالوا: لا تلعبوا مع هذا الساحر، فجمعوهم في بيت، فجاء عيسى","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-16","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"يطلبهم، فقالوا: ليسوا هاهنا، قال: ماذا في البيت؟ قالوا: خنازير، قال عيسى: كذلك يكونون، ففتحوا الباب، فإذاهم خنازير، فهموا بقتله، فهربت به أمه إلى مصر. قاله السُّدي.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-17","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"ثم قال لهم: إِنَّ فِي ذلِكَ لَآيَةً لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ، فإن غير المؤمنين لا ينتفع بالمعجزات لعناده، وَمُصَدِّقاً لِما بَيْنَ يَدَيَّ مِنَ التَّوْراةِ أي: وجئتكم مصدقاً للتوراة، وشاهداً على صحتها، وَلِأُحِلَّ لَكُمْ بَعْضَ الَّذِي حُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ في شريعة موسى عليه السلام كالشحوم والثروب(1) ولحم الإبل والعمل في السبت. وهذا يدل على أنه ناسخ للتوراة، ولا يخل بكونه مصدقاً له، كما لا يخل نسخ القرآن بعضه لبعض بصحته. فإن النسخ في الحقيقة: بيان لانتهاء العمل بذلك الحكم. ثم قال لهم: (و) قد جِئْتُكُمْ بِآيَةٍ واضحة مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ، قد شاهدتموها بأعينكم، فما بقي إلا عنادكم، فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-18","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"ثم دعاهم إلى التوحيد بعد بيان الحجة فقال: إِنَّ اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوهُ ولا تعبدوا معه سواه، هذا صِراطٌ مُسْتَقِيمٌ لا عوج فيه. قال البيضاوي: أي: لما جئتكم بالمعجزات القاهرة والآيات الباهرة، فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ في المخالفة، وَأَطِيعُونِ فيما أدعوكم إليه، ثم شرع في الدعوة وأشار إليها بالقول المجمل، فقال: إِنَّ اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبُّكُمْ أشار إلى استكمال القوة النظرية بالاعتقاد الحق الذي غايتُه التوحيد، وقال: فَاعْبُدُوهُ إشارة إلى استكمال القوة العملية بملازمة الطاعة، التي هي الإتيان بالأوامر والانتهاء عن المناهي، ثم قرر ذلك بأن الجمع بين الأمرين هو الطريق المشهود له بالاستقامة، ونظيره: قوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «قُلْ آمَنْتُ بِاللهِ ثم اسْتَقِمْ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-19","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"الإشارة: كل من انقطع بكليته إلى مولاه، وصدف عن حظوظه وهواه، وأفنى شبابه في طاعة ربه، وجعل يلتمس في حياته دواء قلبه، تحققت له البشارة في العاجل والآجل، وحصل له التطهير من درن العيوب والرذائل، ورزقه من فواكه العلوم، ما تتضاءل دون إدراكه غاية الفهوم، هذه مريم البتول أفنت شبابها في طاعة مولاها، فقربها إليه وتولاها، وبشرها بالاصطفائية والتطهير، وأمرها شكراً بالجد والتشمير، ثم بشّرها ثانياً بالولد النزيه والسيد النبيه، روح الله وكلمة الله، من غير أب ولا سبب، ولا معالجة ولا تعب، أمره بأمر الله، يبرئ الأكمه والأبرص ويحيي الموتى بإذن الله، هذا كله ببركة الانقطاع وسر الاتباع.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-20","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «من انقطع إلى الله كَفَاه الله كلَّ مُؤْنة، ورَزقه من حيثُ لا يحتسب، ومن انقطع إلى الدنيا وكَلَه الله تعالى إليها» .","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-21","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"وقال بعضهم: صِدْقُ المجاهدة: الانقطاع إليه من كل شيء سواه. فالانقطاع إلى الله في الصغر يخدم على الإنسان في حال الكبر، ومعاصي الصغر تجر الوبال إلى الكبر، فكما أن عيسى عليه السلام كان يبرئ الأكمه والأبرص بإذن الله، كذلك من انقطع بكُلِّيته إلى الله أبرأ القلوبَ السقيمة بإذن الله، وأحيا موتى القلوب بذكر الله، وأخبر بالغيوب وما تدخره ضمائر القلوب، يدل على طاعة الله، ويدعو بحاله ومقاله إلى الله، يهدي الناس إلى الصراط المستقيم، ويوصل من اتبعه إلى حضرة النعيم. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-45-51-22","r":"q3-45-51","title":"3:45–51 · The annunciation, miracles and mission of Jesus","text":"ولما تمت البشارة بعيسى عليه السلام وظهر إلى الدنيا، وبلغ وقت الدعوة، بعثه الله إلى بنى إسرائيل، فكفروا به، فلما تحقق كفرهم طلب من ينصره إلى الله، كما أشار الحق تعالى إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-45-51-22"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-45-51-s1","r":"q3-45-51","title":"The Messiah, the Word, and the syntax of the annunciation","text":"I say: “When the angels said” ( إذ قالت ) is a substitute ( بدل ) for the earlier “when they said.” Taking it as a substitute for “when they disputed” is remote. “The Messiah” ( المسيح ), and what follows, gives information about the child’s name; alternatively “Jesus” ( عيسى ) is the predicate ( خبر ) of an omitted subject, “son of Mary” ( ابن مريم ) being its attribute ( صفة ). “Messiah” ( المسيح ) follows the pattern faʿīl with a passive sense ( mafʿūl ): he was wiped or cleansed of impurities and so purified; or he was anointed with blessing; or the sole of his foot was flat without an arch; or Gabriel wiped him with his wing to protect him from Satan. Or masīḥ has an active sense ( fāʿil ), because he passed his hand over the ill and they recovered, or over the blind person’s eyes and they saw; or because he travelled ( يسِيح ) through the earth, without settling in one place, in which case the initial mīm is additional. As for the Antichrist, al-masīḥ al-dajjāl , one of his eyes is effaced, or he traverses the earth save Mecca and Medina. In short, Jesus is the Messiah of good and the Antichrist the messiah of evil. It is therefore said, “The Messiah will slay the messiah.” [XIV-N014] “Distinguished” ( وجيهًا ) is an accusative of state ( حال ) modifying “Word,” which has been sufficiently specified by its qualification. “In the cradle” and “in maturity” ( في المهد وكهلًا ) are two circumstantial expressions: as an infant and as a mature man. The cradle ( mahd ) is the bedding prepared for an infant. “A messenger” ( رسولًا ) is the object of an omitted verb: “And We shall make him a messenger.” “Confirming” ( مصدقًا ) is coordinated ( عطف ) with “a messenger.” “So that I may make lawful” ( ولأحل ) depends upon an omitted verb, “I have come to make lawful,” or is coordinated with the implied meaning of “confirming,” as in the idiom “I came to you apologizing—or to please your heart.”","anchor":"en-q3-45-51-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-45-51-s2","r":"q3-45-51","title":"The Word, speech from the cradle, and the divine creative command","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Remember when the angels said” in giving Mary good news, “Mary, God gives you glad tidings of a Word from Him”—a son formed by God’s Word “Be!” ( كُنْ ) and thus brought into being. Some say he was called a “Word” because he manifested the creative Word ( كلمة التكوين ), realized it, and exercised effect through it. That is why extraordinary events appeared at his hands more often than at those of other prophets. “His name is the Messiah, Jesus son of Mary.” Although Mary herself is being addressed, he is called “son of Mary” to signal that he will be born without a father: children are ordinarily attributed to their fathers, except when the father is absent. “Distinguished in this world and the Hereafter”: noble in this world through prophecy and messengership, and in the Hereafter through intercession for his followers. “And one of those brought near” to God in both abodes. “He will speak to people in the cradle,” as an event that breaches the customary order ( خرق العادة ), vindicating his mother; “and in maturity,” after his understanding has become complete, before his being raised, or after his return, since maturity is after forty. The sound interpretation is that she was given tidings of Jesus’ prophecy and his speech in the cradle as a miracle, and of his mission of calling people in maturity before and after his being raised. What closely approaches a state may be treated under its ruling. He is “among the righteous”—those fit for the Presence of the Lord of the worlds. When Mary heard the good news, she was astonished. “She said, My Lord, how shall I have a son when no man has touched me?” She addressed God, having become absent from awareness of the intermediary Gabriel ( فانية عن الواسطة ), whether in wonder or inquiring how: through marriage or without it? The angel said, “Thus does God create whatever He wills”; or: “The matter is as you say, yet God creates whatever He wills.” He needs neither intermediaries nor causes ( الوسائط والأسباب ). “When He decrees a thing, He merely says to it ‘Be!’ and it is.” He will teach him “the Book”—writing and the script—“and Wisdom”—prophecy or sound judgment—“and the Torah and the Gospel.”","anchor":"en-q3-45-51-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-45-51-s3","r":"q3-45-51","title":"The signs granted to Jesus","text":"“And [He will make him] a messenger to the Children of Israel.” Joseph was the first of the messengers among the Children of Israel, Jesus the last—upon them peace. A report attributed to the Prophet says: “I was sent after eight thousand prophets, four thousand of them from the Children of Israel.” When Jesus was sent to them, he said, “I have come to you with a sign from your Lord.” They asked what it was. He replied: “I fashion for you from clay something in the form of a bird; then I breathe into it and it becomes a bird, by God’s leave .” He used to form for them the shape of a bat, because it is the most complete of birds: it has breasts and teeth, menstruates and flies, making the miracle more striking. It flew while people looked at it and fell dead when out of their sight, to distinguish the act of the Real from that of the creature. [Translator’s note: These are transmitted exegetical descriptions; their claims about natural history have not been independently established.] [XIV-N015] He then said: “And I heal the one born blind” ( الأكمه )—and all the more one whose blindness came later—“and the leper” ( الأبرص ), one afflicted with whitish skin disease. These two were singled out because they were considered especially difficult to cure. Medicine was predominant in Jesus’ age, so he displayed a miracle of that kind. It is related that at times thousands of sick people gathered around him in one day: those able to come to him did so, and he visited those unable to move. He healed through supplication, on condition that they enter Islam [i.e., submit to God]. “And I bring the dead to life by God’s leave ”—not by my own power, lest divinity be wrongly imputed to him, for the restoration of life lies beyond human capacity. It is related that he raised four people: Lazarus ( al-ʿĀzir ), his friend, after his sister sent word that he was dying. Jesus arrived after a journey of three days, only to find him dead. He went with the sister to the sealed rock-tomb, invoked God, and Lazarus stood up, his bodily fat dripping; he lived on and had children. The second was the son of an old woman whose funeral passed by Jesus. Through his prayer the young man sat up on the bier, descended from the men’s shoulders, dressed himself, carried the bier on his own shoulder and returned home, living long enough to have children. The third was the daughter of a collector of tithes: on being asked whether he could restore one who had died the day before, he prayed, and she lived and had offspring. The fourth was Shem son of Noah. Jesus invoked God by His Greatest Name, and Shem came out of his grave, half his head white-haired. He asked, “Has the Hour come?” Jesus said, “No, but I invoked God and He gave you life. Why is your hair grey when it was not so in your time?” He answered that hearing the cry he supposed the Hour had come, and terror turned his hair grey. It is said Jesus raised the dead by the invocation “O Living, O Self-Subsisting” ( يا حي يا قيوم ). [XIV-N016] “And I tell you what you eat and what you store in your homes.” After witnessing his cures, some said that these were sorcery and demanded to know what they ate and saved. He would tell a man what he had eaten for his morning and evening meals. It is related that when he attended school, he told the boys what food their parents had prepared: “Go—your family’s meal today is such and such.” Asked how they knew, they said Jesus had informed them. Their parents confined them and warned them not to play with “this sorcerer.” When Jesus came looking for them, they denied the boys were there. He asked what the house contained. They said “Pigs.” Jesus said: “Then so shall they be.” When the door was opened, the boys were pigs. The people then intended to kill him, and his mother fled with him to Egypt. So relates al-Suddī. [XIV-N017] “Surely in that is a sign for you, if you are believers.” Those stubborn in unbelief gain nothing from miracles. “Confirming what came before me of the Torah”: I have come as its confirmer, attesting its truth, “and to make lawful for you some of what was forbidden to you” under Moses’ law—such as certain fats and fatty parts, camel flesh, and work on the Sabbath. This shows that Jesus superseded certain Torah rulings ( ناسخ للتوراة ), without compromising his confirmation of the Torah’s truth, just as one Qurʾānic ruling’s supersession of another does not compromise the truth of either. In reality abrogation ( النسخ ) means clarifying that the operative period of a ruling has ended. “I have come to you with a clear sign from your Lord,” which your own eyes have witnessed. Nothing remains but your obstinacy. “So be mindful of God and obey me.”","anchor":"en-q3-45-51-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-45-51-s4","r":"q3-45-51","title":"Divine unity and the straight way","text":"He then calls them to divine unity ( التوحيد ) after establishing the evidence: “God is my Lord and your Lord; so worship Him,” and none besides Him. “This is a straight path,” without crookedness. Al-Bayḍāwī says: Having come with compelling miracles and manifest signs, “be mindful of God” by avoiding opposition “and obey me” in what I call you to. Jesus then begins his call, summed up in the words “God is my Lord and your Lord,” indicating the perfection of the theoretical power ( القوة النظرية ) through true belief, whose highest end is divine unity; and “so worship Him,” indicating the perfection of the practical power ( القوة العملية ) by persevering in obedience, performing commands and avoiding prohibitions. Uniting these two completes the path attested as straight. Its counterpart is the saying of the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him: “Say, ‘I believe in God,’ and then remain upright.” [XIV-N018]","anchor":"en-q3-45-51-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-45-51-s5","r":"q3-45-51","title":"Mary’s consecration and the healing of hearts","text":"Whoever turns wholly to his Master, withdrawing from his personal portions ( حظوظه ) and passions, spends his youth obeying his Lord and seeks throughout life the remedy of the heart, obtains the promised good in this world and the next, is purified of the stains of faults and vices, and is provided fruits of knowledge before whose comprehension the utmost reach of understanding dwindles. Mary the Virgin spent her youth obeying her Master. He drew her near, took charge of her, announced her election and purification, and commanded her to strive diligently out of gratitude. He then announced a second gift: an immaculate son, a distinguished master, the Spirit of God and the Word of God, with no father, ordinary cause, contrivance or toil. By God’s command he cured the blind and the leper and restored the dead by His leave. This was all through the blessing of complete devotion ( الانقطاع ) and the secret of following faithfully ( الاتباع ). The Prophet is reported to have said: “Whoever devotes himself wholly to God, God suffices him for every burden and provides him from whence he does not expect; whoever gives himself over to the world, God leaves him to it.” One of the masters said: “The truth of spiritual struggle ( صدق المجاهدة ) is turning to Him, leaving everything besides Him.” Devotion to God in youth serves a person in old age, while youthful acts of disobedience draw calamity into old age. Just as Jesus cured the blind and lepers by God’s leave, so the person wholly devoted to God cures sick hearts by God’s leave , gives life to dead hearts through God’s remembrance, and speaks of inwardly hidden matters and what the consciences of hearts conceal. He directs others to obedience and calls to God by state and speech, guides people to the straight path, and leads those who follow him into the Presence of bliss ( حضرة النعيم ). And success is through God; He guides to the straight way. Once the announcement of Jesus was complete, he entered the world and reached the time of his mission. God sent him to the Children of Israel; they disbelieved in him. When their unbelief became manifest, he sought those who would help him towards God, as the Real indicates:","anchor":"en-q3-45-51-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-52-54","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions 3:52–54","anchor":"unit-q3-52-54"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-1","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"فَلَمَّا أَحَسَّ عِيسى مِنْهُمُ الْكُفْرَ قالَ مَنْ أَنْصارِي إِلَى اللَّهِ قالَ الْحَوارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنْصارُ اللَّهِ آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَاشْهَدْ بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ (52) رَبَّنا آمَنَّا بِما أَنْزَلْتَ وَاتَّبَعْنَا الرَّسُولَ فَاكْتُبْنا مَعَ الشَّاهِدِينَ (53) وَمَكَرُوا وَمَكَرَ اللَّهُ وَاللَّهُ خَيْرُ الْماكِرِينَ (54)","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-2","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"قلت: (من أنصاري إلى الله) : الجار يتعلق بحال محذوفة، أي: ذاهباً إلى الله إلى نَصْر دينه، أو مُضيفاً نفسه إلى الله، أو ملتجئاً إلى الله، أو يتعلق ب- (أنصاري) مضمِّناً معنى الإضافة، أي: من يضيف نفسه إلى الله في نصره. وحوارى الرجل: خاصته، الذين يستعين بهم في نوائبه، وفى الحديث عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «لكلِّ نبي حَوَاري، وحَوارِيي: الزّبير» . وحواريو عيسى: أصحابه الذين نصروه، وسموا بذلك لخلوص نيتهم ونقاء سريرتهم. والحَوَرُ: البياض الخالص، وكل شيء بيَّضته فقد حوَّرْته، ويقال للبيضاء من النساء: حوارية. وقيل: كان الحواريون قًصَّارين(1) ، يُحَوِّرُون الثياب، أي: يبيضونها، وقيل: كانوا ملوكاً يلبسون البياض.","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-3","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَلَمَّا أَحَسَّ عِيسى من بني إسرائيل الْكُفْرَ، وتحققه تَحَقُّقَ ما يدرك بالحواس، بعد ما بُعث إليهم، وأرادوا قتله، فرَّ منهم واستنصر عليهم، وقالَ مَنْ أَنْصارِي ملجئاً إِلَى اللَّهِ، أو ذاهباً إلى نصر دينه، قالَ الْحَوارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنْصارُ اللَّهِ أي: أنصار دينه، آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَاشْهَدْ علينا بأننا مُسْلِمُونَ لتشهد لنا يوم القيامة، حين يشهد الرسل لقومهم، رَبَّنا آمَنَّا بِما أَنْزَلْتَ على نبيك من الأحكام، وَاتَّبَعْنَا الرَّسُولَ عيسى عليه السلام، فَاكْتُبْنا مَعَ الشَّاهِدِينَ بوحدانيتك، أو مع الذين يشهدون لأنبيائك","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-4","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"بالصدق، أو مع الأنبياء الذين يشهدون لأتباعهم، أو مع أمة محمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- فإنهم شهداء على الناس.","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-5","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"قال عطاء: سَلَمَتْ مريمُ عيسى إلى أعمال شتى، وآخر ما دفعته إلى الحواريين، وكانوا قصَّارين وصباغين، فأراد مُعلّم عيسى السفر، فقال لعيسى: عندي ثياب كثيرة مختلفة الألوان، وقد علمتك الحرفة فاصبغها، فطبخ جُبّاً واحداً، وأدخل فيه جميع الثياب، وقال لها: كوني على ما أريد، فقدم الحواريُ، والثياب كلها في الجب، فلما رآها قال: قد أفسدتها، فأخرج عيسى ثوباً أصفر، وأحمر، وأخضر، إلى غير ذلك، فعجب الحواري، وعلم أنَّ ذلك من الله تعالى، ودعا الناس إليه، وآمنوا به، ونصروه، فهم الحواريون.","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-6","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"ولما أخرجه بنو إسرائيل عاد إليهم مع الحواريين، وصاح فيهم بالدعوة، فهمُّوا بقتله، وتواطئوا عليه، وَمَكَرُوا أي: دبروا الحيل في قتله، وَمَكَرَ اللَّهُ بهم، أي: استدرجهم حتى قتلوا صاحبهم، ورُفع عيسى عليه السلام، فالمكر في الأصل: هو حيلة يجلب بها غيره إلى مضرة. ولا تُسند إلى الله إلا على حسب المقابلة والازدواج، كقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-7","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"يُخادِعُونَ اللَّهَ وَهُوَ خادِعُهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-8","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"، وقوله: اللَّهُ يَسْتَهْزِئُ بِهِمْ، وَاللَّهُ خَيْرُ الْماكِرِينَ. أي: أشدهم مكراً، وأقواهم على إيصال الضرر من حيث لا يحتسب، أو أفضل المجازين بالعقوبة لأنه لا أحد أقدر على ذلك منه.","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-9","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"تنبيه: قيل للجنيد رضى الله عنه: كيف رَضِيَ المكرَ لنفسه، وقد عابه على غيره؟ قال: لا أدري، ولكن أنشدني فلان للطبرانية:","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-10","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"فديتُك قد جُبِلْتُ على هواكَ ... ونفْسِي ما تَحِنُّ إلى سِوَاكَ","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-11","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"أُحِبّك، لا بِبَعْضِي بل بكلّى ... وإن لم يُبْقِ حُبُّكَ لي حِرَاكَا","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-12","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"وَيَقْبُحُ مِنْ سِوَاكَ الْفِعْلُ عِنْدي ... وتَفْعَلُهُ فَيَحْسُنُ مِنْكَ ذَاكَ(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-13","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"فقال له السائل: أسألُك عن القرآن، وتجيبني بشعر الطبرانية؟ قال: ويحك، قد أجبتك إن كنت تعقل. إنَّ تخليته إياهم مع المكرية، مكرٌ منه بهم. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-14","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"قلت: وجه الشاهد في قوله: (وتفعله فيحسن منك ذاك) ، ومضمن جوابه: أن فعل الله كله حسن في غاية الإتقان، لا عيب فيه ولا نقصان، كما قال صاحب العينية:","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-15","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"وَكلُّ قبِيح إنْ نَسَبْتَ لِحُسْنِهِ ... أَتَتْكَ مَعَانِي الْحُسْنِ فِيهِ تُسَارعُ","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-16","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"يُكَمِّلُ نُقصَانَ الْقَبِيحِ جَمَالُهُ ... فَما ثَمَّ نُقْصَانٌ وَلاَ ثَمَّ بَاشِعُ","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-17","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"وتخليته تعالى إياهم مع المكر، تسبب عنه الرفع إلى السماء، وإبقاء عيسى حيّاً إلى آخر الزمان، حتى ينزل خليفة عن نبينا- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، فكان ذلك في غاية الكمال والإتقان، لكن لا يفطن لهذا إلا أهل العرفان.","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-18","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"الإشارة: يجب على المريد الصادق الذي يطلب دواء قلبه، أن يفر من الوطن الذي يظهر فيه الإنكار، إلى الوطن الذي يكثر فيه الإقرار، يفر إلى من يعينه على نصر الدين من الأبرار المقربين، الذين جعلهم الله حواري الدين، ففي الحديث الصحيح: «خَيْرُ مالِ المُسْلِم غَنَمٌ يَتْبَعُ بها شَعَفَ(1) الجِبَالِ يَفِرُّ مِنَ الْفِتَنِ» . فالمؤمن يفر بدينه من شاهق جبل إلى شاهق جبل حتى يدركه الموت، وما زالت الأكابر تفر بنفسها إلى شواهق الجبال، يهربون من حس الدنيا وشغبها، ولا يرافقون إلا من يستعين بهم على ذكر الله، وهم أهل التجريد، الذين اصطفاهم الله لخالص التوحيد، فروا إلى الله فآواهم الله، قالوا: (آمنا بالله وأشهد بأنا مسلمون) منقادون لما تريد منا، (ربنا آمنا بما أنزلت) من الأحكام الجلالية والجمالية قد عرفناك في جميع الحالات، (فاكتبنا مع الشاهدين) لحضرتك، المنعمين بشهود ذاتك، ومن مكر بنا من القواطع الخفية فَغَيَّبنا عنه بشهود أنوارك القدسية، وانصرنا فإنك خير الناصرين، ولا تدعنا مع مكر الماكرين يا رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-52-54-19","r":"q3-52-54","title":"3:52–54 · The disciples, divine stratagem and the Path’s companions","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى رفع عيسى إلى السماء فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-52-54-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-52-54-s1","r":"q3-52-54","title":"“My helpers towards God” and “disciples”","text":"I say: in “Who are my helpers towards God?” ( من أنصاري إلى الله ), the preposition attaches to an omitted circumstantial expression ( حال ): “as one going to God,” that is, to the aid of His religion; or “as one attaching himself to God”; or “as one seeking refuge in God.” Alternatively it attaches to “my helpers,” understood in the sense of joining or attaching oneself: “Who will join himself to God in helping His religion?” A man’s ḥawārī ( حواري ) is one of his intimates upon whose assistance he relies in adversity. The Prophet said: “Every prophet has a ḥawārī ; my ḥawārī is al-Zubayr.” Jesus’ ḥawāriyyūn ( الحواريون ) were the companions who supported him. They were so called because of their pure intentions and unblemished innermost dispositions. The root ḥawar denotes pure whiteness: anything you whiten, you have ḥawwarta ; a fair-complexioned woman can be called ḥawāriyya . Some say they were launderers or fullers ( قصّارون ) who whitened cloth; others say they were kings dressed in white.","anchor":"en-q3-52-54-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-52-54-s2","r":"q3-52-54","title":"The disciples’ confession and the attempt upon Jesus","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “When Jesus sensed unbelief” among the Children of Israel—apprehending it with the certainty of something perceived by the senses—after his mission had begun and they intended to kill him, he fled and sought assistance against them. “He said: Who will help me, turning towards God?” Or: who will go to the aid of His religion? “The disciples replied: We are helpers of God,” meaning helpers of His religion. “We believe in God, and bear witness that we submit” ( مسلمون ), so that you may testify on our behalf on the Day of Resurrection, when messengers testify concerning their communities. “Our Lord, we believe in what You have sent down” of rulings upon Your prophet “and follow the Messenger,” Jesus—peace be upon him. “Write us among the witnesses”: witnesses to Your oneness ( وحدانيتك ); or among those who testify to the truthfulness of Your prophets; or with the prophets who bear witness for their followers; or among Muḥammad’s community, who are witnesses over people. ʿAṭāʾ relates that Mary handed Jesus over to learn various crafts, the last apprenticeship being with the disciples, who worked as cloth-finishers and dyers. When Jesus’ teacher was about to travel, he left him many garments of different colours to dye. Jesus heated a single vat, placed all the garments in it and bade them take the colours he wished. On the teacher’s return, the man feared that all had been ruined. Jesus took out yellow, red, green and other garments, each according to its intended colour. Amazed, the teacher knew that the act was from God, called people to him, and they believed and gave him support; hence they became disciples. [XIV-N019] After the Children of Israel expelled him, Jesus returned with the disciples and proclaimed his mission to them. They sought to kill him and conspired: “They plotted” ( مكروا ), contriving means to put him to death; “and God planned against them,” allowing them to kill one of their own party while Jesus was raised. In its original usage makr ( المكر ) is a device by which one draws another into harm. It is predicated of God only in response and correspondence ( على سبيل المقابلة والازدواج ), as in “They seek to deceive God, but He is their deceiver” [4:142] and “God mocks them” [2:15]. “God is the best of planners” means either the mightiest in strategic action, most able to bring about punishment from unsuspected quarters, or the best in recompensing wrongdoing, since none is more able than He.","anchor":"en-q3-52-54-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-52-54-s3","r":"q3-52-54","title":"Why “planning” is predicated of God","text":"Notice ( تنبيه ). Al-Junayd was asked: “How can He accept makr for Himself when He reproves it in others?” He answered, “I do not know—but so-and-so recited for me verses of al-Ṭabarāniyya”: For you I would give myself: I was fashioned in desire for you, and my soul yearns for none besides you. I love you not with one part, but with my whole being, though love for you should leave no movement in me. In another I find an act reprehensible; you do that very act, and from you it seems fair. The questioner protested: “I ask you about the Qurʾān and you answer with the poetry of al-Ṭabarāniyya?” Al-Junayd replied: “Alas for you! I have answered you, if you can understand. God’s letting them persist in their plotting was itself His makr against them.” End of quotation. I say: the relevant witness is “you do that very act, and from you it seems fair.” The answer implies that every act of God is good and perfectly accomplished, without deficiency or defect. The poet of the ʿAyniyya says: Whenever you trace the ugly thing to His beauty, meanings of beauty hasten forth within it. His beauty perfects what seemed defective; no deficiency is left, nor any ugliness. His leaving them to their intrigue resulted in Jesus’ being raised to heaven and preserved alive until the last age, when he descends as the deputy of our Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him. This was an act of the highest perfection and wisdom, although only the people of gnosis ( أهل العرفان ) discern it. [XIV-N020]","anchor":"en-q3-52-54-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-52-54-s4","r":"q3-52-54","title":"Fleeing denial and finding helpers on the Way","text":"The sincere aspirant who seeks a remedy for the heart ought to flee a land where denial prevails to one where affirmation is widespread; flee towards righteous ones brought near to God who help him defend the religion—the disciples of religion whom God has appointed. The sound hadith says: “The best wealth of a Muslim is sheep with which he follows the mountain peaks, fleeing tribulations.” The believer flees with his religion from one mountain summit to another until death overtakes him. The eminent masters, too, have withdrawn to the mountains, away from the sensible clamor of the world. They accompany only those who help them remember God: the people of detachment ( أهل التجريد ), chosen for pure divine unity ( خالص التوحيد ). They fled towards God, and He sheltered them. “We believe in God. Bear witness that we submit”—we yield to what You desire of us. “Our Lord, we believe in what You have sent down” in decrees of majesty and beauty ( الأحكام الجلالية والجمالية ); we have known You in every condition. “Write us among the witnesses”—those who witness Your Presence, graced with witnessing Your Essence ( شهود ذاتك ). Whatever hidden impediments ( القواطع الخفية ) plot against us, make us absent from them through witnessing Your holy lights. Help us, for You are the best of helpers; do not abandon us to the schemes of schemers, Lord of the worlds. The Real then mentions Jesus’ elevation to heaven:","anchor":"en-q3-52-54-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-55-58","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit 3:55–58","anchor":"unit-q3-55-58"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-1","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"إِذْ قالَ اللَّهُ يا عِيسى إِنِّي مُتَوَفِّيكَ وَرافِعُكَ إِلَيَّ وَمُطَهِّرُكَ مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَجاعِلُ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوكَ فَوْقَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا إِلى يَوْمِ الْقِيامَةِ ثُمَّ إِلَيَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَأَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ فِيما كُنْتُمْ فِيهِ تَخْتَلِفُونَ (55) فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فَأُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذاباً شَدِيداً فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَما لَهُمْ مِنْ ناصِرِينَ (56) وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ فَيُوَفِّيهِمْ أُجُورَهُمْ وَاللَّهُ لا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ (57) ذلِكَ نَتْلُوهُ عَلَيْكَ مِنَ الْآياتِ وَالذِّكْرِ الْحَكِيمِ (58)","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-2","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"قلت: (إذ قال) : ظرف لمقدر، أي: اذكر، أو وقع ذلك إذ قال، أو لمكروا، (متوفيك) أي: رافعك إليَّ وافياً تاماً، من قولهم: توفيت كذا واستوفيته: قبضته وافياً تامّاً، أو مميتك عن الشهوات العائقة عن العروج إلى عالم الملكوت، أو منيمك بدليل قوله تعالى: وَهُوَ الَّذِي يَتَوَفَّاكُمْ بِاللَّيْلِ، رُوِيَ أنه رُفع نائماً، والإجماع على أنه لم يمت،","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-3","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"قال تعالى: وَما قَتَلُوهُ وَما صَلَبُوهُ وَلكِنْ شُبِّهَ لَهُمْ، وقوله: (ذلك) مبتدأ، و (نتلوه) : خبر، و (من الآيات) :","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-4","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"حال، أو (من الآيات) : خبر، و (نتلوه) : حال، أو خبر بعد خبر.","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-5","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: اذكر إِذْ قالَ اللَّهُ لعيسى عليه السلام لما أراد رفعه: يا عِيسى إِنِّي مُتَوَفِّيكَ، أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-6","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"قابضك إليّ ببدنك تامّاً، وَرافِعُكَ إِلَيَّ أي: إلى محل كرامتي ومقر ملائكتي، وَمُطَهِّرُكَ مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أي: من مخالطة دنس كفرهم، وَجاعِلُ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوكَ ممن صدق بنبوتك من النصارى والمسلمين، وقال قتادة والشعبي والربيع: هم أهل الإسلام. هـ. فو الله ما اتبعه من ادعاه ربا، فمن تبع دينه حقا جعل فَوْقَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا به من اليهود إِلى يَوْمِ الْقِيامَةِ يغلبونهم بالحجة والسيف. وقد حقق الله فيهم هذا الأمر، فإن اليهود لم ترفع لهم راية قط، ولم يتفق لهم ملك ولا دولة إلى زمننا هذا(1) .","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-7","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"ثم قال تعالى: ثُمَّ إِلَيَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ بالبعث، فَأَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ فِيما كُنْتُمْ فِيهِ تَخْتَلِفُونَ من أمر الدين وأمر عيسى. فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فَأُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذاباً شَدِيداً فِي الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ أي: فأجمع لهم عذاب الآخرة لعذاب الدنيا الذي أصابهم فيها من القتل والسبي. وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ فَيُوَفِّيهِمْ أُجُورَهُمْ في الدارين بالنصر والعز في الدنيا، وبالرضا والرضوان في الآخرة، وَاللَّهُ لا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ لا يرضى فعلهم ولا يقربهم إليه.","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-8","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"ذلِكَ الذي ذكرت لك من نبأ عيسى ومريم ومن ذكر قبلهما، نَتْلُوهُ عَلَيْكَ مِنَ الْآياتِ أي: العلامات الدالة على صدقك، لأنها أخبار عن أمور لم تشاهدها ولم تقرأها في كتاب، بل هي من الذِّكْرِ الْحَكِيمِ، وهو القرآن المبين.","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-9","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن طَهَّر سره من الأكدار، وقدس روحه من دنس الأغيار، ورفع همته عن هذه الدار، عرج الله بروحه إلى سماء الملكوت، ورفع سره إلى مشاهدة سنا الجبروت، وبقي ذكره حيّاً لا يموت، وجعل من انتسب إليه في عين الرعاية والتعظيم، وفي محل الرفعة والتكريم، قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «هَاجِرُوا تكسبوا العز لأولادكم» ، فمن هاجر وطن الحظوظ والشهوات، والركون إلى العوائد والمألوفات، عرجت روحه إلى سماء القدس ومحل الأنس، وتمكن من العز الذي لا يفنى، ينسحب عليه وعلى أولاده ومن انتسب إليه إلى أن يرث الله الأرض ومَن عليها، (وهو خير الوارثين) . هذه سُنة الله في خلقه، لأنهم نصروا دين الله ورفعوا كلمة الله، فنصرهم الله، ورفعهم الله، قال تعالى: إِنْ تَنْصُرُوا اللَّهَ يَنْصُرْكُمْ، وقال تعالى: وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلى وَكَلِمَةُ اللَّهِ هِيَ الْعُلْيا. وفي الحكم: «إن أردت أن يكون لك عز لا يفنى، فلا تستعزن بعز يفنى» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-10","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"وقال القشيري: الإشارة فيه: إني متوفيك عنك وقابضك منك، ورافعك عن نعوت البشرية، ومطهرك عن إرادتك بالكلية، حتى تكون مصدقاً لنا بنا، ولا يكون لك من اختيارك شيء، وتكون إسبال التولي عليك قائماً، وبهذا الوصف كان يظهر على يده إحياء الموتى، وما كانت تلك الأحداث حاصلة إلا بالقدرة عليه. هـ. وقال الورتجبي:","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-11","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"متوفيك عن رسم الحدوثية، ورافعك إليَّ بنعت الربوبية، ومطهرك عن شوائب البشرية. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-55-58-12","r":"q3-55-58","title":"3:55–58 · Jesus’ elevation and the purification of the spirit","text":"ثم ذكر نشأة عيسى وخلقه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-55-58-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-55-58-s1","r":"q3-55-58","title":"The meanings of tawaffī and the demonstrative","text":"I say: “When He said” ( إذ قال ) is governed by something understood: “remember”; or, “that took place when He said”; or it depends on “they plotted.” “I shall take you fully” ( مُتَوَفِّيكَ ) may mean “I shall raise you to Me complete and intact”: one says tawaffaytu or istawfaytu something when one receives it in full. Or it means “I shall cause you to die to the desires that impede ascent to the world of malakūt” ( عالم الملكوت ). Or it means “I shall cause you to sleep,” as indicated by “He it is who takes you [in sleep] by night” [6:60]. It is related that he was raised while sleeping. Ibn ʿAjība states a consensus that Jesus did not die, citing “They did not kill him or crucify him, but it was made to appear so to them” [4:157]. [XIV-N021] “This” ( ذلك ) is the subject ( المبتدأ ) and “We recite it” ( نتلوه ) the predicate ( الخبر ); “from the signs” ( من الآيات ) may be an accusative of state ( حال ). Alternatively “from the signs” is the predicate and “We recite it” a circumstantial clause; or there are two predicates. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-14] ]","anchor":"en-q3-55-58-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-55-58-s2","r":"q3-55-58","title":"The raising, judgment and recompense","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Remember when God said” to Jesus, as He intended to raise him: “Jesus, I shall take you fully”—receive you to Myself, body and all, without diminution—“and raise you to Me,” to the place of My honour and the abode of My angels, “and purify you of those who disbelieve,” freeing you from companionship polluted by their unbelief. “I shall set those who follow you,” who believe in your prophethood, Christians and Muslims; though Qatāda, al-Shaʿbī and al-Rabīʿ say it means the Muslims. End of report. By God, whoever claims Jesus as Lord has not truly followed him. Those who really follow his religion are placed “above those who disbelieve” in him, the Jews, “until the Day of Resurrection,” overcoming them in argument and by the sword. He adds: This matter has been realised concerning them, for the Jews have not raised a standard, nor possessed kingship or a state, down to our own time. [XIV-N022] “Then to Me is your return” through resurrection, “and I shall judge between you concerning that in which you differed” over religion and Jesus. “Those who disbelieve, I shall punish with a severe punishment in this world and the Hereafter”—joining the punishment of the next world to the killing and captivity they endured here. “Those who believe and perform righteous deeds, He will give their rewards in full” in the two abodes: help and honour here, satisfaction and good pleasure in the next. “God loves not the wrongdoers”: He does not approve their acts or draw them near. “This” narrative that I have told you about Jesus, Mary and those before them “We recite to you from the signs,” indications of your truthfulness because they recount events you did not witness or read in books; indeed it is of “the Wise Remembrance” ( الذِّكْر الحكيم ), the clear Qurʾān.","anchor":"en-q3-55-58-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-55-58-s3","r":"q3-55-58","title":"Ascending beyond desires and enduring through transmission","text":"Whoever purifies the innermost secret ( السرّ ) of turbidity, sanctifies the spirit from the impurity of otherness ( الأغيار ), and lifts his aspiration beyond this abode, God causes his spirit to ascend to the heaven of malakūt and elevates his secret to the witnessing of the splendour of jabarūt ( مشاهدة سنا الجبروت ). His renown remains alive after death, and those attached to him enjoy care, reverence, dignity and honour. The Prophet is reported to have said: “Emigrate, and you will gain honour for your children.” Whoever leaves the homeland of personal portions and passions ( الحظوظ والشهوات ) and reliance upon habits and familiar comforts ascends in spirit to the heaven of holiness and the abode of intimacy; there he obtains honour that does not perish, extending to his offspring and associates until God inherits the earth and its inhabitants—He is the best of inheritors. [XIV-N023] This is God’s established way with His creation. For they supported His religion and raised His Word, so He helped and raised them. “If you help God, He will help you” [47:7]. “He made the word of those who disbelieved the lowest, while the Word of God is the highest” [9:40]. In the Ḥikam : “If you desire an honour that does not perish, do not seek honour through what perishes.” God Most High knows best. Al-Qushayrī says in allusion: “I shall take you away from yourself, seize you from yourself, raise you beyond human qualities, and purify you altogether of your self-will, until you attest to Us through Us. Nothing of your independent choice will remain, and the cloak of Our care shall rest upon you. It was in this state that the raising of the dead appeared at his hand; these events came about only through the Power governing him.” End of quotation. Al-Wartajbī says: “I shall take you away from the vestiges of contingent being ( رسم الحدوثية ), raise you to Me through the attribute of Lordship ( نعت الربوبية ), and purify you from the admixtures of human nature.” End of quotation. He then recounts Jesus’ coming to be and his creation:","anchor":"en-q3-55-58-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-59-60","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit 3:59–60","anchor":"unit-q3-59-60"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-1","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"إِنَّ مَثَلَ عِيسى عِنْدَ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ آدَمَ خَلَقَهُ مِنْ تُرابٍ ثُمَّ قالَ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ (59) الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ فَلا تَكُنْ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِينَ (60)","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-2","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ مَثَلَ عِيسى عِنْدَ اللَّهِ أي: إن شأنه الغريب في كونه وجد من غير أب (كمثل آدم) . ثم فسر شأن آدم فقال: خَلَقَهُ مِنْ تُرابٍ أي: خلق قالبه من تراب، ثُمَّ نفخ فيه الروح، وقالَ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ أي: فكان، فشأنه أغرب من شأن عيسى، لأنه وجد من غير أب ولا أم، بخلاف عيسى عليه السلام، فلا يستغرب حاله ويتغالى فيه إلا من طَبع اللهُ على قلبه، فاستعجز القدرة الإلهية، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُقْتَدِراً. هّذاَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ فَلا تَكُنْ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِينَ أي: الشاكين في مخلوقيته، وهذا خطاب للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم، على طريق التهييج لغيره، أو لكل سامع.","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-3","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"وسبب نزول الآية: أنَّ وفد نجران قالوا للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم: مالك تشتم صاحبنا، فتقول: إنه عبد؟ قال: أجل، هو عبد الله ورسوله، وكلمته ألقاها إلى مريم العذراء البتول، فغضبوا، وقالوا: هل رأيت إنساناً قط من غير أب؟ فإن كنت صادقاً فأرنا مثله. فنزلت: إِنَّ مَثَلَ عِيسى عِنْدَ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ آدَمَ. أي: فهو أعجب من عيسى، لكونه بلا واسطة أصلاً. رُوِيَ أن مريم حملت بعيسى وهي بنت ثلاث عشرة سنة، وأوحى الله إليه على رأس ثلاثين سنة، ورفعه إليه من بيت المقدس ليلة القدر، وهو ابن ثلاث وثلاثين سنة، وعاشت أمه بعد رفعه ست سنين.","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-4","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «أنا أولى الناس بعيسى ابن مريم لأنه لم يكن بيني وبينه نبيّ، فإنه نازل بأمتي وخليفتي فيهم، فإذا رأيتموه فاعرفوه، فإنه رجل مربوع إلى الحمرة والبياض، سبط الشعر، كأن شعره يقطر، وإن لم يصبه بلل، يدق الصليب، ويقتل الخنزير، ويفيض المال، وليسلكن الروحاء(1) ، حاجّاً أو معتمراً، أو ليَثْنِينَّهما جميعاً، ويقاتل الناس على الإسلام، حتى يُهلك الله في زمانه الملل كلها، ويهلك الله في زمانه مسيح الضلالة، الكذاب","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-5","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"الدجال، وتقع في الأرض الأمنة، حتى ترتع الأسد مع الإبل، والنمر مع البقر، والذئاب مع الغنم، ويلعب الغلمان بالحيات، ويلبث في الأرض أربعين سنة، ثم يتزوج ويولد له ثم يتوفى، ويصلي المسلمون عليه» . ويدفنونه في حجرة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-6","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الحق- جلّ جلاله- أظهر هذا الآدمي في شكل غريب، وسر عجيب، جمع فيه بين الضدين، وأودع فيه سر الكونين، نوراني ظلماني، روحاني جسماني، سماوي أرضي، ملكوتي ملكي، معنوي حسيّ، أودع فيه الروح نورانية لاهوتية في نطفة ناسوتية، فوقع التنازع بين الضدين، فالروح تحن إلى وطنها اللاهوتي، والنطفة الطينية تحن إلى وطنها الناسوتي، فمن غلبت روحانيته على طينته التحق بالروحانيين، وكان من المقربين في أعلى عليين، فصارت همته منصرفة إلى طاعة مولاه، والارتقاء إلى مشاهدة نوره وسناه، فانياً عن حظوظه وهواه، ومَن غلبت طينتُه على روحانيته التحق بالبهائم أو الشياطين، وانحط إلى أسفل سافلين، وكانت همته منصرفة إلى حظوظه وهواه، غائباً عن ذكر مولاه، قد اتخذ إلهه هواه.","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-7","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"وتأمل قضية السيد عيسى عليه السلام لمَّا لم ينشأ من نطفة أمشاجية، كيف غلبت روحانيته، حيث لم تجد ما يجذبها إلى الحضيض الطيني، فلم يلتفت إلى هذا العالم الظلماني أصلاً، وكذلك الأنبياء حيث طهروا من بقاياها في الأصالة، والأولياء حيث طهروها بالمجاهدة، كيف صارت أرواحهم لاتشتاق إلا إلى الأذكار والعلوم والأسرار، فانية في محبة الواحد القهار، حتى لحقت بوطنها، ورجعت إلى أصلها، محل المشاهدة والمكالمة والمناجاة والمساررة، هّذاَ هُوَ الحق مِنْ ربك فلا تكن من الممترين في إدراك الروح هذا المقام، إن لم يغلب عليها عالم الصلْصَال. والله- تعالى- أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-59-60-8","r":"q3-59-60","title":"3:59–60 · Jesus and Adam; the human composite and the ascent of spirit","text":"ولما قامت الحجة على النصارى، وتبيّن عنادهم، دعاهم إلى المباهلة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-59-60-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-59-60-s1","r":"q3-59-60","title":"Adam without parents and Jesus without a father","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Truly, the likeness of Jesus with God”—the wonder of his having come into existence without a father—“is as the likeness of Adam.” God then explains Adam’s case: “He created him from dust,” that is, fashioned his bodily frame from earth; then He breathed the spirit into him, and said to him “Be!”—“and he is,” meaning he came to be. Adam’s case is more extraordinary than Jesus’, since Adam existed without father or mother, whereas Jesus had a mother. Thus only one whose heart God has sealed, who regards divine power as incapable, finds Jesus’ case inexplicable and exalts him beyond proper measure. “God has power over everything” [18:45]. “That is the truth from your Lord: be not among the doubters”—those who doubt that Jesus is a created being. The address is directed to the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, to stir others to heed; or to every hearer. As the occasion of revelation it is related that the delegation from Najrān said to the Prophet, “Why do you insult our master by calling him a servant?” He replied: “Yes, he is God’s servant and His Messenger, His Word cast to Mary, the Virgin.” They grew angry and asked: “Have you ever seen a human being without a father? If you speak truth, show us another.” Then the verse was revealed: “The likeness of Jesus with God is as the likeness of Adam.” Adam is more remarkable, having come to be with no parental intermediary whatever. [XIV-N024] It is related that Mary conceived Jesus when she was thirteen; God revealed to him when he reached thirty, and raised him from Jerusalem on the Night of Power when he was thirty-three; his mother lived six years after his being raised. A lengthy report attributed to the Prophet says: “I am the closest of people to Jesus son of Mary, for no prophet came between him and me. He will descend among my community and act as my deputy in it. When you see him, recognize him: he is a man of medium stature, reddish and white in complexion, with straight hair, as though water dripped from it even when it was not wet. He will break the cross and kill the pig, and wealth will become abundant. He will pass through al-Rawḥāʾ as a pilgrim or performer of ʿumra, perhaps combining both. He will fight people for Islam, until God brings all other religions to an end in his time and destroys in his time the false Messiah, the lying Dajjāl. Peace will spread upon the earth, so lions will graze with camels, leopards with cattle and wolves with sheep, and children will play with snakes. He will remain on earth forty years; then he will marry, have offspring and die, and the Muslims will pray over him.” The narration adds that they will bury him in the Prophet’s chamber. [Translator’s note: Such statements belong to the transmitted report, and individual details require their own authentication.] [XIV-N025]","anchor":"en-q3-59-60-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-59-60-s2","r":"q3-59-60","title":"Spirit and clay in the human being","text":"Know that the Real, exalted is His majesty, manifested this human being in a wondrous form and with an extraordinary mystery. He joined two opposites in him and entrusted to him the mystery of two worlds: luminous and dark, spiritual and bodily, heavenly and earthly, of malakūt and of mulk, intelligible and sensible. Into a human ( ناسوتية ) drop He placed a luminous, divine ( لاهوتية ) spirit. Thus a conflict arose between the opposites: the spirit yearns for its divine home, while the clay-formed drop yearns for its human home. [XIV-N026] Whoever allows the spiritual nature to prevail over the clay joins the spiritual beings and becomes among those brought near in the highest heights. His aspiration is turned to obedience to his Master and ascent to the witnessing of His light and splendour, effaced from his personal portion and passion ( فانيًا عن حظوظه وهواه ). Whoever lets the clay nature prevail over the spirit resembles beasts or devils and falls to the lowest depths. His aspiration remains turned towards his pleasures and passions, absent from remembrance of his Master, having taken his passion as his god. Consider our master Jesus, peace upon him: because he did not originate from a mingled drop ( نطفة أمشاجية ), his spiritual nature prevailed; he had nothing drawing him towards the lowliness of clay, so he did not turn to this dark world at all. Likewise the prophets, who were purified of its residues from the outset, and the friends of God, who purified them through spiritual struggle ( المجاهدة ): their spirits desired only invocations, knowledge and mysteries, effaced in love of the One, the Overpowering, until they rejoined their home and returned to their origin—the station of witnessing ( المشاهدة ), intimate speaking ( المكالمة ), supplication ( المناجاة ) and mutual confidence ( المساررة ). “This is the truth from your Lord; do not be among those who doubt” that the spirit can attain this station, provided the realm of clay ( عالم الصلصال ) does not dominate it. And God Most High knows best. After the argument against the Christians had been established and their obstinacy exposed, he invited them to a mutual invocation of judgment ( mubāhala , المباهلة ), saying:","anchor":"en-q3-59-60-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-61-63","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master 3:61–63","anchor":"unit-q3-61-63"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-1","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"فَمَنْ حَاجَّكَ فِيهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ فَقُلْ تَعالَوْا نَدْعُ أَبْناءَنا وَأَبْناءَكُمْ وَنِساءَنا وَنِساءَكُمْ وَأَنْفُسَنا وَأَنْفُسَكُمْ ثُمَّ نَبْتَهِلْ فَنَجْعَلْ لَعْنَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَى الْكاذِبِينَ (61) إِنَّ هذا لَهُوَ الْقَصَصُ الْحَقُّ وَما مِنْ إِلهٍ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ (62) فَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ بِالْمُفْسِدِينَ (63)","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-2","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"قلت: أصل (تعالوا) : تَعالَيُوا، على وزن تفاعلوا، من العلو، فقلبت الياء ألفاً لتحركها، ثم حذفت، ومن قرأ بالضم نقل، وأصل معناها: ارتفع، ثم أطلق على الأمر بالمجيء. والابتهال: التضرّع والمبالغة في الدعاء.","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-3","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَمَنْ خاصمك يا محمد في شأن عيسى عليه السلام، وكان الذي خاصم في ذلك السيد والعاقب، لما قدموا مع نصارى نجران على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، قال لهما النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «أسلما» ، قالا: قد أسلمنا قبلك، قال: «كذبتما، يمنعكما من الإسلام دعاؤكما عيسى لله ولداً، وعبادتكما الصليب، وأكلكما الخنزير» ، قالا: إن","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-4","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"لم يكن عيسى ولداً لله فمن أبوه؟ فقال لهما النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: ألستم تعلمون أنه لا يكون ولد إلا وهو يشبه أباه؟ قالوا: بلى، قال: ألستم تعلمون أن ربنا حي لا يموت، وأن عيسى يأتي عليه الفناء؟ قالوا: بلى، قال: ألستم تعلمون أن ربنا قيِّم كل شيء، ويحفظه، ويرزقه؟ قالوا: بلى، قال: فهل ملك عيسى شيئاً من ذلك؟ فقالوا: لا. قال: ألستم تعلمون أن الله لا يخفى عليه شيء في الأرض ولا في السماء؟ قالوا: بلى، قال: فهل يعلم عيسى من ذلك إلا ما عُلِّم؟ قالوا: لا.","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-5","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"قال: فإن ربنا صوَّر عيسى في الرحم كيف شاء، وربنا لا يأكل ولا يشرب ولا يُحدث، قالوا: بلى. قال: ألستم تعلمون أن عيسى حملته أمه كما تحمل المرأة ثم وضعته كما تضع المرأة ولدها، ثم غُذِّي كما يُغَذّى الصبي، ثم كان يطعم ويشرب ويحدث؟ قالوا: بلى. قال: كيف يكون هذا كما زعمتم؟ فسكتوا ... فأنزل فيهم السورة إلى هنا.","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-6","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"فقال الحقّ لنبيه- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: فَمَنْ حَاجَّكَ فِيهِ أي: في عيسى من النصارى، مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ بعبوديته، فَقُلْ لهم: تَعالَوْا نَتَلاَعَنُ، أي: نلعن الكاذبَ منا نَدْعُ أَبْناءَنا وَأَبْناءَكُمْ وَنِساءَنا وَنِساءَكُمْ وَأَنْفُسَنا وَأَنْفُسَكُمْ أي: يدعو كل واحد منا نفسه وأعزة أهله وألصقهم بقلبه إلى المباهلة، وإنما قدَّمهم على النفس لأن الرجل يخاطر بنفسه دونهم، فكان تقديمهم أبلغ في الابتهال، ثُمَّ نَبْتَهِلْ، أي نجهد في الدعاء على الكاذب، فَنَجْعَلْ لَعْنَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَى الْكاذِبِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-7","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"فلما قرأ النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم هذه الآية على وفد نجران، ودعاهم إلى المباهلة، قالوا: حتى نرجع وننظر في أمرنا، فقالوا للعاقب- وكان ذا رأيهم-: ما ترى؟ فقال: والله لقد عرفتم يا معشر النصارى أن محمداً نبيّ مرسل، ولقد جاءكم بالفَصْل من أمر صاحبكم، والله ما لاعن قومٌ قط نبيّاً فعاش كبيرُهم، ولا نبت صغيرُهم، ولئن فعلتم ذلك لتهلكن، فوادِعُوا الرَّجُلَ. وانصرفوا، فأتوه وهو محتضنٌ الحسن آخذ بيد الحسين، وفاطمةُ تمشي خلفه، وعَلِيّ خلفها، وهو يقول لهم: «إِذَا دَعَوْتُ فَأمِّنُوا» ، فقال الأسقُف: يا معشر النصارى، إني لأرى وجُوهاً لو سألوا الله أن يُزيل جبلاً من مكانه لأزاله، فلا تتباهلوا فتهلكوا جميعاً إلى يوم القيامة. فقالوا: يا أبا القاسم، نرى ألا نلاعنك، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: أسْلِمُوا يَكُنْ لكم ما للمسلمين وعليكم ما عليهم، فأَبَوا، فقال: إنى أنابذكم، فقالوا: مالنا بحرب العرب طاقة، ولكنا نصالحك على ألا تغزونا ولا تَرُدَّنا عن ديننا، على أن نؤدي إليك في كل عام ألفَيْ حلة ألفاً في صَفَر، ألفا في رجب، وثلاثين درعاً من حديد.","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-8","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"فصالحهم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم على ذلك، فقال النبيّ: «والذي نفسي بيده لو تلاعنوا لمُسِخُوا قِرَدَة، وخَنَازِيرَ، ولأضْرَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ الوَادِي نَاراً، ولاستأصل اللهُ نَجْرَان وأهْلَهُ، ولَمَا حَالَ الحَوْلُ على النَّصَارى كلّهم حَتى هَلكوا» .","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-9","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"قال الله تعالى: إِنَّ هذا الذي أوحينا إليك لَهُوَ الْقَصَصُ الْحَقُّ وَما مِنْ إِلهٍ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، خلافاً لما يزعم النصارى من التثليث، وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيزُ في ملكه الْحَكِيمُ في صنعه، فلا أحد يساويه في قدرته التامة، ولا في حكمته البالغة، فَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا وأعرضوا عن الإيمان، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ بِالْمُفْسِدِينَ، الذين يعبدون غير الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-10","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"ووضع المظهر موضع الضمير، ليدل على أن التولي عن الحجج والإعراض عن التوحيد إفساد للدين، بل يؤدي إلى فساد العالم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-11","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"الإشارة: ينبغي للمريد، الذي تحقق بخصوصية شيخه، أن يلاعن من يخاصمه فيه، ويبعد عنه كل البعد، ولا يلين له لئلا يركبه، ويدفع عن شيخه ما استطاع، فإنَّ هذا من التعظيم الذي هو سببٌ في سعادة المريد، ولا يصغي إلى المفسدين الطاعنين في أنصار الدين. قلت: وقد جاءني بعض من ينتسب إلى العلم من أهل فاس، فقال لي: قد اتفقت علماء فاس على بدعة شيخكم، فقلت له: لو اتفق أهل السموات السبع والأرضين السبع، على أنه من أهل البدعة، لقلت أنا: إنه من أهل السنّة، لأني تحققت بخصوصيته، كالشمس في أفق السماء، ليس دونها سحاب. فالله يرزقنا حسن الأدب معهم والتعظيم إلى يوم الدين. آمين. فمن أعرض عن أولياء الله من المنكرين (فإن الله عليم بالمفسدين) .","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-61-63-12","r":"q3-61-63","title":"3:61–63 · The challenge of mutual invocation and devotion to the spiritual master","text":"ثم دعاهم إلى التوحيد الذي اتفقت عليه سائر الأديان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-61-63-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-61-63-s1","r":"q3-61-63","title":"The derivation of “come” and the meaning of mubāhala","text":"I say: the original of “Come!” ( تعالَوا , taʿālaw ) is taʿālayū , on the pattern tafāʿalū , from ʿuluww ( العلوّ ), height or elevation. The yāʾ changed to alif because it was vocalized; the alif was subsequently elided. In the reading with ḍamma, the vowel has been transferred [from the yāʾ to the lām]. Its original meaning was “rise up,” after which it became a general imperative meaning “come.” Mutual invocation ( ibtihāl , الابتهال ) means humbling oneself intensely and striving earnestly in prayer.","anchor":"en-q3-61-63-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-61-63-s2","r":"q3-61-63","title":"Najrān and the challenge of mubāhala","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Whoever disputes with you,” Muḥammad, “concerning him,” Jesus, after the knowledge concerning his servanthood has come to you ... Those who disputed are said to have been al-Sayyid and al-ʿĀqib, who came with the Christians of Najrān. The Prophet said to them, “Submit [become Muslims].” They answered, “We submitted before you.” He replied: “You speak falsely: your calling Jesus God’s son, worshipping the cross and eating pork prevents your submission.” They asked, “If Jesus is not God’s son, who is his father?” The Prophet then asked whether a child does not resemble its father; whether God is living and never dies, while Jesus is subject to passing away; whether God sustains, protects and provides for all things, while Jesus cannot exercise such sovereignty; and whether nothing in earth or heaven escapes God’s knowledge, whereas Jesus knows only what he has been taught. They acknowledged each point. He continued: “God formed Jesus in the womb as He willed. God neither eats, drinks nor expels waste. Was Jesus not borne by his mother, delivered as other children are, fed and nourished, and himself subject to eating, drinking and the needs of the body?” When they assented, he asked how Jesus could be as they claimed. They fell silent. The narrative says that the opening of this sūrah was then revealed down to the present passage. [XIV-N027] Thus God said to His Prophet: Whoever disputes with you over Jesus, “after knowledge has come to you,” say to them: “Come, let us invoke a curse upon the liar among us. Let us call our sons and your sons, our women and your women, ourselves and yourselves”—that is, each party should bring itself and the dearest members of its family, those most closely bound to its heart, for the mubāhala . They are named before the individual himself because a man will hazard his own safety sooner than theirs, making the summons a more forceful test. “Then let us earnestly pray” against the party who lies, “and place God’s curse upon the liars.” When the Prophet recited the verse and invited the delegation to mutual invocation, they requested time to consult. They asked al-ʿĀqib, their adviser, what he thought. He said: “You know that Muḥammad is a messenger, and that he has brought a decisive judgment concerning your master. No people who entered into mutual imprecation with a prophet ever had their elders survive or their children grow up. If you do so, you will perish; make peace with the man.” They then came to him while he held al-Ḥasan close, took al-Ḥusayn by the hand, and walked with Fāṭima behind him and ʿAlī behind her, telling them, “When I invoke, say ‘Amen.’” Their bishop is reported to have warned that these were faces whose prayer could move a mountain and that the delegation should not invoke destruction upon themselves. They declined the mubāhala . The Prophet invited them again to enter Islam and receive the rights and responsibilities of Muslims. When they refused, he said that he would oppose them. They answered that they could not wage war against the Arabs, but sought terms by which he would not attack them or compel them to leave their religion. The reported settlement required two thousand garments each year, one thousand in Ṣafar and one thousand in Rajab, together with thirty iron coats of mail. The narrative adds the Prophet’s warning that, had they undertaken mubāhala , they would have been transformed into monkeys and pigs, their valley consumed in fire, Najrān and its people uprooted, and no year would have elapsed before all the Christians perished. [Translator’s note: All these details are presented as reports in the source, not as independent archival proof of the encounter or treaty.] [XIV-N028] The Real says: “This” account revealed to you “is the true narration. There is no deity but God,” contrary to the Christian trinitarian claim as Ibn ʿAjība construes it. “God is the Mighty” in His kingship, “the Wise” in His creation. None equals Him in perfect power or consummate wisdom. “If they turn away” from faith, “God knows the corrupters,” those who worship other than Him. The explicit noun “the corrupters” stands in place of a pronoun to indicate that turning away from proofs and from divine unity ( التوحيد ) corrupts religion and leads to disorder in the world. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-61-63-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-61-63-s3","r":"q3-61-63","title":"Loyalty to one’s shaykh and the trial of denial","text":"The aspirant ( المريد ) who has become certain of his shaykh’s particular spiritual distinction ( خصوصية شيخه ), Ibn ʿAjība says, should engage in mutual imprecation with anyone who disputes with him about that shaykh, keep his distance from them, and not soften towards them, lest they gain mastery over him. He should defend his shaykh to the extent of his ability; this reverence is a cause of happiness upon the Path. He should not listen to those who disparage the helpers of religion. I say: Someone associated with learning in Fez came to me and said, “The scholars of Fez have agreed that your shaykh is an innovator.” I replied: “If all the inhabitants of the seven heavens and the seven earths agreed that he was an innovator, I would still say he belonged to the Sunna. For I have realized his particular spiritual distinction as clearly as the sun in the sky, unobscured by any cloud.” May God grant us excellent comportment ( حسن الأدب ) towards them and reverence until the Day of Judgment. Amen. Whoever of the deniers turns away from God’s friends: “God knows the corrupters.” [XIV-N029] He then calls them to the divine unity on which the religious traditions agree, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-61-63-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-64","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization 3:64","anchor":"unit-q3-64"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-1","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"قُلْ يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ تَعالَوْا إِلى كَلِمَةٍ سَواءٍ بَيْنَنا وَبَيْنَكُمْ أَلاَّ نَعْبُدَ إِلاَّ اللَّهَ وَلا نُشْرِكَ بِهِ شَيْئاً وَلا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنا بَعْضاً أَرْباباً مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ فَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُولُوا اشْهَدُوا بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ (64)","anchor":"ar-q3-64-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-2","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"قلت: (سواء) : مصدر، نعت للكلمة، والمصادر لا تثني ولا تجمع ولا تؤنث، فإذا فتحت السين مددت، وإذا ضمت أو كسرت قصرت، كقوله: مَكاناً سُوىً أي: مستوٍ. وسواء كل شيء: وسطه، قال تعالى: فَرَآهُ فِي سَواءِ الْجَحِيمِ، أي: وسطه.","anchor":"ar-q3-64-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-3","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد: يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ اليهود والنصارى، تَعالَوْا: هلموا إِلى كَلِمَةٍ سَواءٍ أي: عدل مستوية، بَيْنَنا وَبَيْنَكُمْ لا يختلف فيها الرسل والكتب والأمم، هي أَلَّا نَعْبُدَ إِلَّا اللَّهَ أي: نوحده بالعبادة، ونقر له بالوحدانية، وَلا نُشْرِكَ بِهِ شَيْئاً أي: لا نجعل غيره شريكاً له في استحقاق العبادة، وَلا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنا بَعْضاً أَرْباباً مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ أي: لا نقول عزير ابن الله، ولا المسيح ابن الله، ولا نطيع الأحبار فيما أحدثوا من التحريم والتحليل، لأنهم بشر مثلنا.","anchor":"ar-q3-64-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-4","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"ولمّا نزل قوله تعالى: اتَّخَذُوا أَحْبارَهُمْ وَرُهْبانَهُمْ أَرْباباً مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ ... قال عدي بن حاتم: ما كُنَّا نعبدهم يا رسول الله، قال: «أَلّيْس كانُوا يُحِلُّون لَكُمْ ويُحرِّمون، فتأخُذُون بقَوْلِهم؟ قال: بلى، قال: هُوَ ذَاكَ» فَإِنْ","anchor":"ar-q3-64-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-5","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"تَوَلَّوْا وأعرضوا عن التوحيد فَقُولُوا اشْهَدُوا بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ، فقد لزمتكم الحجة، فاعترفوا بأنا مسلمون دونكم، وأنتم كافرون بما نطقت به الكتبُ وتواطأت عليه الرسل.","anchor":"ar-q3-64-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-6","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"تنبيه: انظر ما في هذه الآية من المبالغة وحسن التدرج في الاحتجاج، بيِّن أولاً أحوال عيسى وما تطاور عليه من الأطوار المنافية للألوهية، ثم ذكر ما يحل عقدتهم ويزيح شبهتهم، فلما رأى عنادهم ولجاجهم دعاهم إلى المباهلة بنوع من الإعجاز، ثم لمّا أعرضوا عنها وانقادوا بعض الانقياد، عاد عليهم بالإرشاد، وسلك طريقاً أسهل وألزم، بأن دعاهم إلى ما وافق عليه عيسى وسائر الأنبياء والكتب، ثم لمّا لم يُجد ذلك فيهم شيئاً، وعلم أن الآيات والنذر لا تغني عنهم شيئاً أعرض عنهم، وقال: فَقُولُوا اشْهَدُوا بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-64-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-7","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"الإشارة: الطرق كثيرة والمقصد واحد، وهو التوحيد الخاص، أعني مقام الفناء والبقاء. فالداعُون إلى الله كلهم متفقون على الدعوة إلى هذا المقصد، فكل طريق لا توصل إلى هذا المقصد لا عبرة بها، وكل داع لا يُبلغ إلى هذا الجمال فهو دجال، فإنْ رضي بتعظيم الناس، ولم يَبْنِ طريقه على الأساس، فليس لصاحبه إلا الإفلاس، وكل مَن أطاع المخلوق في معصية الله فقد اتخذه ربّاً من دون الله، وكل مَن تولى عن طريق الإرشاد فقد استوجب لنفسه الطرد والبعاد، فيقول له الواصلون أو السائرون: (فإن تولوا فقولوا اشهدوا بأنا مسلمون) . وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-64-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-64-8","r":"q3-64","title":"3:64 · A common word; many paths and the single aim of realization","text":"ولما قدم وفدُ نجران المدينة، التقوا مع اليهود، فاختصموا في إبراهيم عليه السّلام فأتاهم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فقالوا: يا محمد إنا اختلفنا فى إبراهيم ودينه، فقالت النصارى: كان نصرانيّاً، وقالت اليهود: كان يهوديّاً، وهم أولى الناس به، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «كلا الفريقين برئ من إبراهيم، بل كان إبراهيم حنيفاً مسلماً، وأنا على دينه، فاتبعوا دينه الإسلام» . فأنزل الله:","anchor":"ar-q3-64-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-64-s1","r":"q3-64","title":"Sawāʾ: equity, levelness and the middle","text":"I say: “Equitable” ( سواء ) is a verbal noun ( مصدر ) used as an adjective ( نعت ) qualifying “word.” Verbal nouns [used in this way] are not put into the dual or plural, nor made feminine. With an a-vowel on the sīn, its ending is long: sawāʾ; with a u- or i-vowel, it is short: suwā or siwā, as in “a level place” ( مَكَانًا سُوًى ) [20:58], meaning an even place. The sawāʾ of anything is its middle. God Most High says, “He saw him in the midst of Hell” [37:55], that is, in its middle.","anchor":"en-q3-64-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-64-s2","r":"q3-64","title":"Worship, religious authority and the call to a common word","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Say,” Muḥammad, “O People of the Book”—Jews and Christians—“come,” that is, approach, “to a word equitable,” just and even-handed, “between us and you,” concerning which messengers, scriptures and communities do not differ. It is “that we worship none but God”: that we single Him out in worship and acknowledge His oneness; “associate nothing with Him”: assign no other being a share in the right to be worshipped; “and do not take one another as lords apart from God”: do not say that Ezra is God’s son or that the Messiah is God’s son, and do not obey the rabbis in the prohibitions and permissions they have newly introduced, for they are human beings like ourselves. When the words of God Most High, “They have taken their rabbis and monks as lords apart from God” [9:31], were revealed, ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim said: “We did not worship them, Messenger of God.” He replied: “Did they not declare things lawful and unlawful for you, and you accepted what they said?” He answered: “Yes.” He said: “That is it.” [XIV-N030] “If they turn away,” turning aside from the affirmation of God’s oneness, “say: ‘Bear witness that we submit to God.’” The proof has now become binding upon you; acknowledge, therefore, that we submit and you do not, and that you disbelieve what the scriptures have declared and the messengers have unanimously affirmed.","anchor":"en-q3-64-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-64-s3","r":"q3-64","title":"The successive stages of the argument","text":"Admonition ( تنبيه ): consider the force and skilful progression of the argument in this verse. First, He explained Jesus’ circumstances and the successive conditions he underwent that are incompatible with divinity. Then He set out what would unravel their difficulty and remove their doubt. When He saw their obstinate insistence, He invited them to the mutual invocation of a curse ( المباهلة ), involving a kind of miraculous challenge. When they declined it and yielded to some extent, He returned to guiding them and took an easier, more compelling route: He invited them to that upon which Jesus, the other prophets and the scriptures agreed. When this too availed them nothing, and He knew that the signs and warnings would not benefit them, He turned away from them, saying: “Say: ‘Bear witness that we submit to God.’” Thus al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q3-64-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-64-s4","r":"q3-64","title":"The paths are many; their aim is one","text":"The paths ( الطرق ) are many, but the aim is one: the special realization of divine oneness ( التوحيد الخاص ), by which I mean the station of effacement and subsistence ( الفناء والبقاء ). All who call to God agree in calling to this aim. A path that does not lead to it is of no account, and every caller who fails to bring one to this beauty is an impostor. If he is content to receive people’s veneration but has not built his path upon its foundation, his companion gains nothing but bankruptcy. Whoever obeys a created being in disobedience to God has taken that being as a lord apart from God. Whoever turns from the path of right guidance has brought expulsion and remoteness upon himself. Those who have arrived, or those still journeying, say to him: “If they turn away, say: ‘Bear witness that we submit to God.’” Success comes through God, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q3-64-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-64-s5","r":"q3-64","title":"","text":"When the delegation from Najrān came to Medina, they met the Jews and disputed about Abraham, peace be upon him. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, came to them. They said: “Muḥammad, we have disagreed about Abraham and his religion.” The Christians said he was Christian; the Jews said he was Jewish, and that they had the closest claim to him. The Prophet said: “Both parties are disassociated from Abraham. Rather, Abraham was a ḥanīf, one submitting to God, and I follow his religion. Follow, then, his religion: submission to God.” So God revealed: [XIV-N031]","anchor":"en-q3-64-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-65-68","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims 3:65–68","anchor":"unit-q3-65-68"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-65-68-1","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تُحَاجُّونَ فِي إِبْراهِيمَ وَما أُنْزِلَتِ التَّوْراةُ وَالْإِنْجِيلُ إِلاَّ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ (65) ها أَنْتُمْ هؤُلاءِ حاجَجْتُمْ فِيما لَكُمْ بِهِ عِلْمٌ فَلِمَ تُحَاجُّونَ فِيما لَيْسَ لَكُمْ بِهِ عِلْمٌ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنْتُمْ لا تَعْلَمُونَ (66) ما كانَ إِبْراهِيمُ يَهُودِيًّا وَلا نَصْرانِيًّا وَلكِنْ كانَ حَنِيفاً مُسْلِماً وَما كانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ (67) إِنَّ أَوْلَى النَّاسِ بِإِبْراهِيمَ لَلَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ وَهذَا النَّبِيُّ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَاللَّهُ وَلِيُّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ (68)","anchor":"ar-q3-65-68-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-65-68-2","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"قلت: (ها أنتم) : أصله: أنتم، دخلت عليه هاء التنبيه، وقال الأخفش: أصله: أأنتم، فقلبت الهمزة الأولى هاء، كقوله: هرقت. وتوجيه القراءات معلوم في محله، و (أنتم) : مبتدأ، و (هؤلاء) : خبره، و (حاججتم) : جملة مبينة للأولى، أو (حاججتم) : خبر، و (هؤلاء) : منادى بحذف النداء، و (حنيفاً) : حال، أي: مائلاً عن الأديان إلا دين الإسلام.","anchor":"ar-q3-65-68-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-65-68-3","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تُحَاجُّونَ فِي إِبْراهِيمَ، ويدعي كل فريق أنه كان على دينه، وَما أُنْزِلَتِ التَّوْراةُ وَالْإِنْجِيلُ إِلَّا مِنْ بَعْدِهِ، فكيف يكون يهوديّاً، ودينكم إنما حدث بعد إبراهيم بألف سنة؟! وكيف يكون نصرانيّاً، ودين النصرانية إنما ظهر بعد إبراهيم بألفي سنة؟! أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ فتدعون المحال، ها أَنْتُمْ يا هؤُلاءِ الحمقى حاجَجْتُمْ فِيما لَكُمْ بِهِ عِلْمٌ من أمر محمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- ونبوته، مما وجدتموه في التوراة والإنجيل، فأنكرتموه عناداً وحسداً، فَلِمَ تجادلون فيما لا علم لكم به، ولا ذكر في كتابكم من شأن إبراهيم؟ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ ما خاصمتم فيه، وَأَنْتُمْ لا تَعْلَمُونَ، بل أنتم جاهلون.","anchor":"ar-q3-65-68-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-65-68-4","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"ثم صرّح بتكذيب الفريقين فقال: ما كانَ إِبْراهِيمُ يَهُودِيًّا وَلا نَصْرانِيًّا وَلكِنْ كانَ حَنِيفاً مائلاً عن العقائد الزائفة، (مسلماً) منقاداً لأحكام ربه. وليس المراد أنه كان على ملة الإسلام، وإلا لكان مشترك الإلزام، لأن دين الإسلام مؤخر أيضاً، فكان إبراهيم إمام الموحدين، وَما كانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ كما عليه اليهود والنصارى والمشركون. ففيه تعريض بهم، ورد لادعائهم أنهم على ملته.","anchor":"ar-q3-65-68-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-65-68-5","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"ثم ذكر مَنْ أولى الناس به، فقال: إِنَّ أَوْلَى النَّاسِ بِإِبْراهِيمَ أي: أخصهم به وأقربهم منه، لَلَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ من أمته في زمانه، وَهذَا النَّبِيُّ محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لموافقتهم له في أكثر الأحكام، قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «لكُلِّ نَبيَ وُلاة مِنَ النَّبيِّينَ، وإنَّ وَلِيِّي منهم أبِي وَخَلِيل ربِّي» . يعني: إبراهيم عليه السلام، وَاللَّهُ وَلِيُّ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أي: ناصرهم على سائر الأديان، ومجازيهم بغاية الإحسان.","anchor":"ar-q3-65-68-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-65-68-6","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"الإشارة: ترى كثيراً من المتفقرة يخصون الكمال بطريقهم، ويخاصمون في طريق غيرهم، وهي نزعة أهل الكتاب، حائدة عن الرشد والصواب، فأولى بالحق من اتبع السنة المحمدية، وتخلق بالأخلاق المرضية، وزهد في الدارين، ورفع همته عن الكونين، ورفع حجاب الغفلة عن قلبه، حتى أشرقت عليه أنوار ربه، واتصل بأهل التربية النبوية، فزجوا به في بحار الأحدية، ثم ردوه إلى مقام الصحو والتكميل، فياله من مقام جليل، فهذه ملة إبراهيم الخليل، وبها جاء الرسول الجليل حبيب الرحمن، وقطب دائرة الزمان، سيد المرسلين، وإمام العارفين، ورسول رب العالمين، صلى الله عليه وسلم دائماً إلى يوم الدين.","anchor":"ar-q3-65-68-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-65-68-7","r":"q3-65-68","title":"3:65–68 · Abraham, submission and the limits of partisan claims","text":"ثم شرع فى معاتبة اليهود وذكر مساوئهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-65-68-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-65-68-s1","r":"q3-65-68","title":"The particles and predicates in “there you are”","text":"I say: the underlying form of hā antum ( ها أنتم ) is antum, to which the attention-calling hāʾ ( هاء التنبيه ) has been prefixed. Al-Akhfash says its underlying form is a-antum ( أأنتم ), with the first hamza changed into hāʾ, as in haraqtu ( هرقت ). The explanations of the variant readings are known in their proper place. Antum is the subject ( مبتدأ ), hāʾulāʾ its predicate ( خبر ), and ḥājajtum, “you disputed,” a clause explaining the first. Alternatively, ḥājajtum is the predicate and hāʾulāʾ is a vocative ( منادى ) with the particle of address omitted. “A ḥanīf” is a circumstantial accusative ( حال ), meaning one who turns away from all religions except the religion of submission to God.","anchor":"en-q3-65-68-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-65-68-s2","r":"q3-65-68","title":"Abraham precedes the later communal designations","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “O People of the Book, why do you dispute about Abraham,” each party claiming that he followed its religion, “when the Torah and the Gospel were sent down only after him?” How could he have been Jewish, when your religion arose only a thousand years after Abraham? How could he have been Christian, when Christianity appeared only two thousand years after Abraham? “Will you not reason,” instead of asserting what is impossible? [XIV-N032] “There you are,” you foolish people: “you have disputed about matters of which you have knowledge”—Muḥammad’s case and his prophethood, blessings and peace be upon him, which you found in the Torah and the Gospel, but denied out of obstinacy and envy. Why, then, do you dispute about something you do not know, concerning Abraham, for which your scripture contains no statement? “God knows” the matter you dispute, “and you do not know”; rather, you are ignorant. He then expressly declares both parties’ claims false: “Abraham was neither a Jew nor a Christian, but a ḥanīf,” turning away from false beliefs, “one submitting to God,” obedient to his Lord’s ordinances. It does not mean that he belonged to the [later] religious community of Islam ( ملّة الإسلام ); otherwise the same objection would apply, since the religion of Islam also came later. Abraham was the imam of those who affirm the One. “He was not one of those who associate partners with Him,” as do the Jews, Christians and polytheists. This indirectly rebukes them and refutes their claim to follow his religious way. [XIV-N033] He then states who has the closest claim to him: “Those with the closest claim to Abraham”—those most particularly related and nearest to him—“are surely those who followed him,” of his community in his own time, “this Prophet,” Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, “and those who believe,” since they agree with him in most ordinances. The Prophet said: “Every prophet has protecting friends among the prophets, and my protecting friend among them is my father and my Lord’s intimate friend,” meaning Abraham, peace be upon him. “God is the protecting friend of the believers”: He supports them against the other religions and recompenses them with the utmost beneficence.","anchor":"en-q3-65-68-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-65-68-s3","r":"q3-65-68","title":"Following the prophetic way rather than claiming exclusive perfection","text":"You see many who profess spiritual poverty ( المتفقرة ) confining perfection to their own path and disputing about the paths of others. This is a tendency of the People of the Book, departing from sound guidance and correctness. The one with the closest claim to the truth is he who follows the Muhammadan Sunna, acquires praiseworthy character, renounces the two abodes, lifts his aspiration beyond the two worlds, and removes the veil of heedlessness from his heart until his Lord’s lights shine upon him. He joins those who impart prophetic spiritual training ( التربية النبوية ); they cast him into the seas of absolute oneness ( الأحدية ), then return him to the station of sobriety and the perfecting of others ( الصحو والتكميل ). What an exalted station! This is the religious way of Abraham, the intimate friend, and it is what the noble Messenger brought: the beloved of the All-Merciful, the pole of the circle of time, the master of the messengers, the imam of the knowers, and the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds. God’s blessings and peace be upon him continually until the Day of Judgment.","anchor":"en-q3-65-68-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-65-68-s4","r":"q3-65-68","title":"","text":"He then began to rebuke the Jews and recount their faults, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-65-68-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-69-71","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status 3:69–71","anchor":"unit-q3-69-71"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-1","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"وَدَّتْ طائِفَةٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ لَوْ يُضِلُّونَكُمْ وَما يُضِلُّونَ إِلاَّ أَنْفُسَهُمْ وَما يَشْعُرُونَ (69) يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ وَأَنْتُمْ تَشْهَدُونَ (70) يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَلْبِسُونَ الْحَقَّ بِالْباطِلِ وَتَكْتُمُونَ الْحَقَّ وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (71)","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-2","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"قلت: (لو) : مصدرية، أي: تمنوا إضلالكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-3","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لبعض المسلمين- وهم حذيفة وعمار ومعاذ- دعاهم اليهود إلى دينهم وطمعوا فيهم:","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-4","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"وَدَّتْ طائِفَةٌ أي: تمنت طائفة مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ لَوْ يُضِلُّونَكُمْ أي: يفتنونكم عن دينكم، ويتلفونكم عن طريق الحق، وَما يُضِلُّونَ إِلَّا أَنْفُسَهُمْ لأن المسلمين لا يقبلون ذلك منهم، فرجع الضلال عليهم، وعاد وباله إليهم، وتضاعف عذابه عليهم، وَما يَشْعُرُونَ أن وباله راجع إليهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-5","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"ثم صرّح الحق تعالى بعتابهم، فقال: يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ المنزلة على نبيه محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم وتجحدون رسالته؟ وَأَنْتُمْ تَشْهَدُونَ أنها من عند الله، وأنه نبيّ الله، وهو منعوت عندكم في التوراة والإنجيل، والمراد أحبارهم، أو تشهدون أنه نبيّ الله بالمعجزات الواضحات. يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَلْبِسُونَ الْحَقَّ بِالْباطِلِ بالتحريف وإبراز الباطل في صورة الحق، حتى كتمتم نعت محمد وحرفتموه، وأظهرتم موضعه الباطل الذي سولت لكم أنفسكم؟ وَتَكْتُمُونَ الْحَقَّ نبوة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ أنه رسول الله حقّاً وأن دينه حق، أو:","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-6","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"وأنتم عالمون بكتمانكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-7","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"الإشارة: ترى كثيراً من أهل الرئاسة والجاه من أولاد الصالحين، وممن ينتسب لهم، إذا رأوا من ظهر بالخصوصية في زمانهم يتمنون إضلالهم وإطفاء أنوارهم، خوفاً على زوال رئاستهم، وما يضلون إلا أنفسهم وما يشعرون، (وَاللَّهُ مُتِمُّ نُورِهِ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الكافرون) ، وهذه نزعة يهودية سببها الحسد، والحسود لا يسود، وبعضهم يتحقق بخصوصية غيرهم، فيكتمها وهو يشهد بصحتها، فيقال لهم: لم تكفرون بآيات الله وأنتم تشهدون؟ ولم تلبسون الحق بالباطل، وتكتمون الحق وأنتم تعلمون؟.","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-69-71-8","r":"q3-69-71","title":"3:69–71 · Concealment, envy and the preservation of religious status","text":"ثم ذكر الحق- تعالى- خدع أهل الكتاب وحيلهم الفارغة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-69-71-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-69-71-s1","r":"q3-69-71","title":"Law introducing the content of a wish","text":"I say: law ( لو ) has the force of a verbal-noun clause ( مصدرية ): that is, they wished for your being led astray.","anchor":"en-q3-69-71-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-69-71-s2","r":"q3-69-71","title":"Knowing testimony and deliberate concealment","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, addresses certain Muslims—Ḥudhayfa, ʿAmmār and Muʿādh—whom the Jews had invited to their religion and hoped to win over: “A group,” that is, a party “among the People of the Book would like to lead you astray”: tempt you from your religion and ruin you by turning you from the way of truth. “But they lead none astray except themselves,” since the Muslims do not accept this from them: the misguidance recoils upon them, its evil consequence returns to them, and its punishment is multiplied against them. “They do not perceive” that its evil consequence returns to themselves. The Real Most High then expressly rebukes them: “O People of the Book, why do you disbelieve in God’s signs,” sent down to His Prophet Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, and deny his mission, “when you yourselves bear witness” that they come from God and that he is God’s prophet, described in your Torah and Gospel? Those meant are their rabbis. Alternatively, you bear witness through the clear miracles that he is God’s prophet. “O People of the Book, why do you mix truth with falsehood,” by alteration and by displaying falsehood in the form of truth, concealing and changing Muḥammad’s description and putting in its place the falsehood your souls have enticed you to devise? “And conceal the truth”—Muḥammad’s prophethood—“while you know” that he truly is God’s Messenger and that his religion is true; or, while you know that you are concealing it.","anchor":"en-q3-69-71-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-69-71-s3","r":"q3-69-71","title":"Envy of living spiritual distinction","text":"You see many people of leadership and standing, among the descendants of the righteous and those affiliated with them, who, when they see someone manifest special spiritual distinction ( الخصوصية ) in their own time, wish to lead him astray and extinguish his lights, fearing the loss of their own leadership. Yet they mislead only themselves and do not perceive it: “God will bring His light to completion, though the unbelievers dislike it” [61:8]. This is a Jewish tendency caused by envy; the envious man does not attain mastery. Some recognize the special distinction of others, yet conceal it while bearing witness inwardly to its truth. They are asked: Why do you disbelieve in God’s signs when you bear witness? Why do you mix truth with falsehood and conceal the truth while you know?","anchor":"en-q3-69-71-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-69-71-s4","r":"q3-69-71","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then mentioned the deceptions of the People of the Book and their futile stratagems, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-69-71-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-72","r":"q3-72","title":"3:72 · Calculated withdrawal and the instability of spiritual commitment","text":"3:72 · Calculated withdrawal and the instability of spiritual commitment 3:72","anchor":"unit-q3-72"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-72-1","r":"q3-72","title":"3:72 · Calculated withdrawal and the instability of spiritual commitment","text":"وَقالَتْ طائِفَةٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ آمِنُوا بِالَّذِي أُنْزِلَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَجْهَ النَّهارِ وَاكْفُرُوا آخِرَهُ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُونَ (72)","anchor":"ar-q3-72-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-72-2","r":"q3-72","title":"3:72 · Calculated withdrawal and the instability of spiritual commitment","text":"قال الحسن والسدي: تواطأ اثنا عشر رجلاً من يهود خيبر- يعني من أحبارهم- وقال بعضهم لبعض: ادخلوا في دين محمد أول النهار باللسان لا بالاعتقاد، واكفروا به آخره، وقولوا: نظرنا في كتبنا، وشاورنا علماءنا، فوجدنا محمداً ليس بذلك، وظهر لنا كذبه، وإنما نفعل ذلك حتى نشكك أصحابه. هـ. فحذَّر الله تعالى المسلمين من قولهم، فقال جلّ جلاله: وَقالَتْ طائِفَةٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ يعني: أحبارهم: (آمنوا بالذي أنزل على الذين آمنوا) وأظهروا الدخول في دينهم، وَجْهَ النَّهارِ وَاكْفُرُوا آخِرَهُ وقولوا: نظرنا في كتبنا، وشاورنا علماءنا، فلم نجد محمداً بالنعت الذي في التوراة، لعل أصحابه يشكون فيه- لعنهم الله وأضلّ سعيهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-72-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-72-3","r":"q3-72","title":"3:72 · Calculated withdrawal and the instability of spiritual commitment","text":"وقيل: نزلت في شأن الكعبة، فإنَّ كعب بن الأشرف ومالك بن الصيف- من اليهود- قالا لأصحابهما: صلّوا معهم إلى الكعبة أول النهار، ثم صلّوا إلى الصخرة آخره، لعلهم يقولون: هم أعلم منا، وقد رجعوا، فيرجعون، ففضحهم الله وأبطل حيلتهم الواهية.","anchor":"ar-q3-72-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-72-4","r":"q3-72","title":"3:72 · Calculated withdrawal and the instability of spiritual commitment","text":"الإشارة: ترى كثيراً من الناسَ يدخلون في طريق القوم، ثم تثقل عليهم أعباؤها، فيخرجون منها إما لضعفهم عن حملها، أو لكونهم دخلوا مختبرين لها، أو على حرف أو حيلة لغيرهم، فإذا رجع أحد منهم قال الناس: لو كانت صحيحة ما رجع فلان عنها، ويصدون الناس عن الدخول فيها والدوام عليها، وهذه نزعة إسرائيلية، قالوا: آمنوا وجه النهار واكفروا آخره لعلهم يرجعون وقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لتَسْلُكن سَنَنَ مَنْ قَبْلكم شِبراً بشبر، وذرَاعاً بِذرَاعٍ، حَتَّى لَوْ دَخلُوا جُحْر ضَبٍّ لدخلْتُموه، قالوا: اليَهُود والنًّصَارَى؟ قال: نعم، فَمنْ إذن» . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-72-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-72-5","r":"q3-72","title":"3:72 · Calculated withdrawal and the instability of spiritual commitment","text":"ثم ذكر الحق- تعالى- مقالة أخرى من مقالاتهم الشنيعة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-72-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-72-s1","r":"q3-72","title":"The stratagem of professing belief and then withdrawing","text":"Al-Ḥasan and al-Suddī said: twelve men among the Jews of Khaybar—that is, their rabbis—conspired together, saying to one another: “Enter Muḥammad’s religion at the beginning of the day in speech, not in conviction; reject it at the end. Say: ‘We examined our books and consulted our learned men, and found that Muḥammad is not the one described; his falsehood became clear to us.’ We shall do this only to make his companions doubt.” End of the quotation. [XIV-N034] God Most High therefore warned the Muslims against their statement. He, exalted is His majesty, said: “A group among the People of the Book”—their rabbis—“said: ‘Believe in what was sent down to those who believe,’” outwardly professing entry into their religion, “at the beginning of the day, and reject it at its end.” Say: “We examined our books and consulted our learned men, and did not find Muḥammad to have the description in the Torah,” so that his companions might come to doubt him. May God curse them and bring their endeavour to nothing. Another account says that the verse was revealed concerning the Kaʿba. Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf and Mālik ibn al-Ṣayf, who were Jews, told their companions: “Pray with them towards the Kaʿba at the beginning of the day; then pray towards the Rock at its end. Perhaps they will say, ‘These people know more than we do and have turned back,’ and they too will turn back.” God exposed them and nullified their feeble stratagem.","anchor":"en-q3-72-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-72-s2","r":"q3-72","title":"Entering the path without a settled commitment","text":"You see many people enter the path of the Folk ( طريق القوم ), only to find its burdens heavy and leave it: either because they lack the strength to bear them, or because they entered merely to test it, with a precarious commitment, or as a stratagem against others. When one of them withdraws, people say: “Had it been sound, so-and-so would not have left it.” They then deter people from entering it and persevering in it. This is an Israelite tendency: “Believe at the beginning of the day and reject it at its end, so that they may turn back.” The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “You will follow the ways of those before you, span for span and cubit for cubit, until, were they to enter a lizard’s hole, you would enter it.” They asked: “The Jews and Christians?” He said: “Yes; who else, then?” Success comes through God. [XIV-N035]","anchor":"en-q3-72-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-72-s3","r":"q3-72","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then mentioned another of their objectionable statements, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-72-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-73-74","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge 3:73–74","anchor":"unit-q3-73-74"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-1","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"وَلا تُؤْمِنُوا إِلاَّ لِمَنْ تَبِعَ دِينَكُمْ قُلْ إِنَّ الْهُدى هُدَى اللَّهِ أَنْ يُؤْتى أَحَدٌ مِثْلَ ما أُوتِيتُمْ أَوْ يُحاجُّوكُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ قُلْ إِنَّ الْفَضْلَ بِيَدِ اللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ (73) يَخْتَصُّ بِرَحْمَتِهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ (74)","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-2","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"قلت: يحتمل أن يكون قوله: (أن يؤتى) : مفعولاً ب- (تؤمنوا) ، و (قل إن الهدى هدى الله) : اعتراض، واللام في «لمن» صلة، (أو يحاجوكم) : عطف على (يؤتى) ، والتقدير: ولا تصدقوا أن يؤتى أحد مثل ما أوتيتم، إلا من كان على دينكم، ولا تصدقوا أن يحاجوكم عند ربكم، بل أنتم تحاجون غيركم. فردَّ الله عليهم (قل إن الهدى هدى الله) ، و (إن الفضل بيد الله) . ويحتمل أن يكون قوله: (أن يؤتى) مفعولاً لأجله، والعامل فيه محذوف، والتقدير: أدبَّرتم ما دبرتم كراهية أن يوتى أحد ما أوتيتم، ومخافة أن يحاجوكم عند ربكم؟.","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-3","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، حاكياً عن اليهود: (و) قالوا لا تُؤْمِنُوا أي: لا تقروا، أو تصدقوا أَنْ يُؤْتى أَحَدٌ مِثْلَ ما أُوتِيتُمْ من العلم والحكمة وفلق البحر وسائر الفضائل، إِلَّا لِمَنْ تَبِعَ دين اليهودية، وكان على دِينَكُمْ، ولا تؤمنوا أن يُحاجُّوكُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ لأنكم أصح ديناً منهم. قال الحق جل جلاله: قُلْ لهم: إِنَّ الْهُدى هُدَى اللَّهِ يهدي به مَن يشاء، وإِنَّ الْفَضْلَ بِيَدِ اللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ.","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-4","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"أو يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وقالوا: لا تصدقوا ولا تذعنوا إِلَّا لِمَنْ تَبِعَ دِينَكُمْ وكان من جلدتكم، فإن النبوة خاصة بكم. فكذبهم الحق بقوله: قُلْ إِنَّ الْهُدى هُدَى اللَّهِ، يخص بها مَن يشاء من عباده، فكيف تحصرونها فيكم؟ لأجل أَنْ يُؤْتى أَحَدٌ مِثْلَ ما أُوتِيتُمْ قلتم ما قلتم، ودبرتم ما دبرتم، حسداً وبغياً، (أو) خوفاً أن يُحاجُّوكُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ، يغلبوكم بالحجة لظهور دينهم، قُلْ يا محمد: إِنَّ الْفَضْلَ بِيَدِ اللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ فلا ينفع في رده حيلة ولا خدع.","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-5","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"أو يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، للمؤمنين، تثبيتاً لهم وتشجيعاً لقلوبهم: ولا تصدقوا يا معشر المؤمنين أن يعطي أحد مثل ما أوتيتم من الفضل والدين القويم إلا من تبع دينكم الحق، وجاء به من عند الحق، ولا تصدقوا أن يحاجوكم في دينكم عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ، أو يقدر أحد على ذلك، فإن الهدى هدى الله والفضل بيد الله، يُؤْتِيهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ الفضل والكرم، عَلِيمٌ بمن يستحق الخصوصية والفضل، يَخْتَصُّ بِرَحْمَتِهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ كالنبوة وغيرها، وَاللَّهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ لا حصر لفضله، كما لا حصر لذاته.","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-6","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق- جلت ذاته، وعظمت قدرته- لأهل الخصوصية: ولا تقروا بالخصوصية إلا لمن كان على دينكم وطريقكم، وتزيّاً بزيكم، وبذل نفسه وفلسه في صحبتكم، مخافة أن يؤتى أحد مثل ما أوتيتم من الخصوصية، وهو ليس أهلاً لها، فيأخذها علماً، فإما أن يتزندق أو يتفسق، أو يحاجوكم بالشريعة فيريق دماءكم كما وقع للحلاج رضي الله عنه وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-7","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"ومن شَهِدَ الحَقِيقَةَ فَلْيَصُنْهَا ... وإلا سوف يقتل بالسنان","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-8","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"كحلاج المحبة إذ تبدت ... له شمس الحقيقة بالتداني(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-9","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"وقال آخر:","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-10","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"بالسِّرِّ إنْ بَاحُوا تُبَاحُ دِمَاؤُهُمْ ... وكَذَا دماء البائحين تباح","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-11","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"وقل أيها العارف، لمن طلب الخصوصية قبل شروطها أو أنكر وجودها عند أهل شرطها: إن الهدى هُدَى اللهِ يهدي به مَن يشاء، والفضل بيد الله يُؤتيه مَن يشاء، والرحمة- التي هي الخصوصية- في قبضة الله، يخص بها مَن يشاء، (والله ذو الفضل العظيم) فمن أراد الخصوصية فليطلبها من معدنها، وهم العارفون بها، فيبذل نفسه وفلسه لهم حتى يُعرفوه بها. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-73-74-12","r":"q3-73-74","title":"3:73–74 · The distribution of divine bounty and the safeguarding of spiritual knowledge","text":"ثم ذكر الحق- تعالى- وصف اليهود بالخيانة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-73-74-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-73-74-s1","r":"q3-73-74","title":"The disputed construction of an yuʾtā and the parenthetical reply","text":"I say: “that anyone is given” ( أن يؤتى ) may be the object ( مفعول ) of “believe” ( تؤمنوا ), while “Say: ‘Guidance is God’s guidance’” is a parenthesis ( اعتراض ). The lām in li-man ( لمن ) is an additional linking particle ( صلة ), and “or that they might dispute with you” is coordinated with yuʾtā. The reconstructed sense ( التقدير ) is: do not believe that anyone is given the like of what you were given, except someone of your own religion; and do not believe that they can dispute with you before your Lord—rather, you are the ones who dispute with others. God answers them: “Say: ‘Guidance is God’s guidance,’” and “[Say:] ‘Bounty is in God’s hand.’” Alternatively, “that anyone is given” is an expression of purpose or cause ( مفعول لأجله ), governed by an omitted expression ( عامل محذوف ). The reconstructed sense is: did you devise what you devised because you disliked anyone being given what you were given, and feared that they might dispute with you before your Lord? [XIV-N036]","anchor":"en-q3-73-74-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-73-74-s2","r":"q3-73-74","title":"Three readings of the argument and its speakers","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, relates the Jews’ words: “And” they said, “do not believe”—do not acknowledge or credit—“that anyone is given the like of what you were given,” of knowledge, wisdom, the parting of the sea and other favours, “except one who follows” Judaism and belongs to “your religion.” Do not believe “that they might dispute with you before your Lord,” for your religion is sounder than theirs. The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Say” to them, “Guidance is God’s guidance”—by it He guides whom He wills—and “Bounty is in God’s hand; He gives it to whom He wills.” Alternatively, the Real, exalted is His majesty, says: they said, do not believe or submit “except to one who follows your religion” and is of your own people, for prophethood belongs exclusively to you. The Real refutes them: “Say: ‘Guidance is God’s guidance.’” He assigns it to whichever of His servants He wills. How, then, can you confine it to yourselves? Because “anyone might be given the like of what you were given,” you said what you said and contrived what you contrived, out of envy and transgression; “or” because you feared that “they might dispute with you before your Lord,” overcoming you in argument through the manifest ascendancy of their religion. “Say,” Muḥammad: “Bounty is in God’s hand; He gives it to whom He wills.” No device or deception can turn it back. Alternatively, the Real, exalted is His majesty, addresses the believers to make them steadfast and strengthen their hearts: do not believe, company of believers, that anyone is given the like of the bounty and upright religion you have been given, except someone who follows your true religion and brings it from the Real. Do not believe that they can dispute with you about your religion “before your Lord,” or that anyone is capable of this. Guidance is God’s guidance and bounty is in God’s hand: “He gives it to whom He wills. God is all-encompassing” in bounty and generosity, “knowing” who merits special distinction and bounty. “He singles out for His mercy whom He wills,” as with prophethood and other gifts. “God is the possessor of immense bounty”: His bounty has no limit, just as His Essence has no limit.","anchor":"en-q3-73-74-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-73-74-s3","r":"q3-73-74","title":"Preparation, confidentiality and the danger of disclosure without realization","text":"The Real—majestic is His Essence and mighty His power—says to the people of special distinction ( أهل الخصوصية ): acknowledge that distinction only to someone who shares your religion and path, has adopted your manner, and has expended himself and his means in your companionship. This is for fear that someone might be given the like of the distinction you have received without being qualified for it, and take it merely as knowledge; he might then fall into heresy or transgression. Or they might argue against you by the religious Law ( الشريعة ) and shed your blood, as happened to al-Ḥallāj, God be pleased with him. Concerning this the poet says: Whoever has witnessed the Reality, let him guard it, or he will be slain by the spear; like the Ḥallāj of love, when there appeared to him the sun of Reality through drawing near. [XIV-N037] Another says: If they divulge the secret, their blood is made forfeit; thus is the blood of those who divulge it made forfeit. Say, knower of God, to one who seeks special distinction before fulfilling its conditions, or denies its presence in those who do fulfil them: guidance is God’s guidance; by it He guides whom He wills. Bounty is in God’s hand; He gives it to whom He wills. Mercy—which here is special distinction—is in God’s grasp; He singles out whom He wills for it. “God is the possessor of immense bounty.” Whoever desires special distinction should seek it at its source: those who know it. Let him expend himself and his means in their service until they acquaint him with it. Success comes through God.","anchor":"en-q3-73-74-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-73-74-s4","r":"q3-73-74","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then mentioned the description of the Jews as betraying trusts, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-73-74-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-75-76","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption 3:75–76","anchor":"unit-q3-75-76"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-1","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"وَمِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ مَنْ إِنْ تَأْمَنْهُ بِقِنْطارٍ يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ إِنْ تَأْمَنْهُ بِدِينارٍ لا يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ إِلاَّ ما دُمْتَ عَلَيْهِ قائِماً ذلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قالُوا لَيْسَ عَلَيْنا فِي الْأُمِّيِّينَ سَبِيلٌ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ (75) بَلى مَنْ أَوْفى بِعَهْدِهِ وَاتَّقى فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِينَ (76)","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-2","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"قلت: الباء في (بقنطار) ، بمعنى على، و (يؤده) : جواب الشرط مجزوم بحذف الياء، ومن قرأ بإسكان الضمير فلأنه أقامه مقام المحذوف، فجزمه عوضاً عنه، وقال الفراء: مذهب بعض العرب: يسكنون الهاء إذا تحرك ما قبلها، يقولون: ضربته ضرباً شديداً.","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-3","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ من أسلم وآمن فصار من أهل الإيمان، إِنْ تَأْمَنْهُ على قنطار من المال أو أكثر أداه إليك، ولم يخن منه شيئاً. وفي الحديث: «من ائتمن على أمانة فأداها، ولو شاء لم يؤدها، زوجه الله من الحور العين ما شاء» . وَمِنْهُمْ من بقي على دينه من أهل الخيانة والخسران، إِنْ تَأْمَنْهُ على دينار فأقل لم يؤده إليك إِلَّا ما دُمْتَ عَلَيْهِ قائِماً على رأسه، مبالغاً في مطالبته. نزلت في عبد الله بن سلام، استودعه قرشي ألفاً ومائتي أوقية ذهباً، فأداها إليه، وفي فنحاص بن عازوراء اليهودي، استودعه قرشي آخر ديناراً، فجحده. وقيل: في النصارى واليهود، فإن النصارى: الغالب عليهم الأمانة، واليهود الغالب عليهم الخيانة.","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-4","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"وذلك الاستحلال بسبب أنهم قالُوا لَيْسَ عَلَيْنا فِي الْأُمِّيِّينَ سَبِيلٌ أي: ليس علينا في شأن من ليسوا أهل كتاب، ولم يكونوا على ديننا، حرج في أخذ مالهم وجحدها، ولا إثم، وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ أنهم كاذبون لأنهم استحلوا ظلم من خالفهم، وقالوا: لم يجعل لهم في التوراة حرمة.","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-5","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"وقيل: عامل اليهود رجالا من قريش، فلما أسلموا تقاضوهم، فقالوا: سقط حقكم حيث تركتم دينكم. وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم:","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-6","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"«كَذَبَ أَعْدَاءُ اللهِ، مَا مِنْ شَيءٍ فِي الجاهِلية إلاّ وَهُو تَحْتَ قَدَمَي، إِلاَّ الأمَانَةَ فإِنهَا مُؤداةٌ إلى الْبَر والفَاجِر» .","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-7","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"ثم كذَّبهم الحقّ- تعالى- فقال: بَلى عليهم في ذلك سبيل، فإن مَنْ أَوْفى بِعَهْدِهِ وَاتَّقى الشرك والمعاصي فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِينَ ومن أحبّه الله كيف يباح ماله وتسقط حرمته؟! بل من أسقط حرمته فقد حارب الله ورسوله، أو مَنْ أَوْفى، بعهد الله من أهل الكتاب، فآمن بمحمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- وَاتَّقى الخيانة، وأدى الأمانة، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِينَ. وأوقع المظهر موقع الضمير العائد إلى «من» لعمومه، فإن لفظ المتقين عام يصدق برد الودائع وغيره، إشعاراً بأن التقوى ملاك الأمر وسبب الحفظ. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-8","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"الإشارة: قد رأينا بعض الفقراء دخل بلد الحقيقة فسقطت من قلبه هيبة الشريعة، فتساهل في أموال الناس وسقطت لديه حرمة العباد، حتى لا تثق به في حفظ مال ولا أهل، فإذا أودعته شيئاً أو قارضته لا يرده إليك إلا ما دمت عليه قائماً. وهذه زندقة ونزعة إسرائيلية، لا يرضاها أدنى الناس، فما بالك بمن يدعي أنه أعلى الناس، وفي بعض الحكم: [كَمَالُ الديانة ترك الخيانة] ، وأعظم الإفلاس خيانة الناس، وفي الحديث: «ثَلاَثٌ مَنْ كُنَّ فيه فهُوَ مُنَافقٌ، وإن صَلَّى وإن صَامَ وزَعم أنه مؤمن، إذا حدّث كذب، وإذا وعد أخلف، وإذا ائتمن خَانَ» . فإذا احتج لنفسه الأمارة، وقال: لا سبيل علينا في متاع العوام، فقد خلع من عنقه ربقة الإسلام، واستحق أن يعلو مفرقه الحُسام. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-75-76-9","r":"q3-75-76","title":"3:75–76 · Trustworthiness, the rights of others and false claims of spiritual exemption","text":"ومن جملة الخيانة: أكل أموال الناس بالأيمان الفاجرة، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق- تعالى- فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-75-76-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-75-76-s1","r":"q3-75-76","title":"The preposition of entrusting and the jussive form yuʾaddihi","text":"I say: the bāʾ in bi-qinṭārin ( بقنطار ) has the meaning of ʿalā. “He will return it” ( يؤدّه ) is the response to the condition ( جواب الشرط ), made jussive ( مجزوم ) by deletion of the yāʾ. In the reading that leaves the pronoun unvowelled, the pronoun is put in the place of the deleted letter and made quiescent in compensation for it. Al-Farrāʾ says that some Arabs leave the hāʾ unvowelled when the preceding letter is vowelled; they say, for example, ḍarabtuh ḍarban shadīdan, “I struck him a severe blow.”","anchor":"en-q3-75-76-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-75-76-s2","r":"q3-75-76","title":"An entrusted deposit remains another person’s right","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Among the People of the Book” are those who have submitted and believed, becoming people of faith. If you entrust such a person with “a great sum” of money, or more, he returns it to you without betraying any part of it. A hadith states: “Whoever is entrusted with a trust and returns it, although he could have withheld it, God will marry him to as many of the wide-eyed maidens as he wishes.” Among them are also those who remain in their religion, people of treachery and loss: entrust such a person with “a single dinar,” or less, and “he will not return it to you unless you keep standing over him,” insistently demanding it. [XIV-N038] The verse was revealed concerning ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām: a Qurashī deposited twelve hundred ūqiyyas of gold with him, which he returned. It also concerned Finḥāṣ ibn ʿĀzūrāʾ, the Jew: another Qurashī deposited a dinar with him, which he denied. Another explanation takes the verse to concern Christians and Jews, saying that trustworthiness predominates among the Christians and treachery among the Jews. Their treating this as lawful arose because “they say: ‘We are not answerable concerning the unlettered.’” That is: with respect to people who are not People of the Book and do not share our religion, there is no blame or sin upon us in taking their property or denying it. “They knowingly speak falsehood against God”: they know they are lying, since they make it lawful to wrong those who differ from them and say that the Torah grants such people no inviolability. Another account says that Jews had dealings with some men of Quraysh. When those men became Muslim and demanded payment, they replied: “Your right has lapsed because you abandoned your religion.” The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “God’s enemies have lied. Everything belonging to the Age of Ignorance is beneath my feet, except a trust: it must be returned to the righteous and the unrighteous alike.” The Real Most High then declares them false: “Rather,” they are indeed answerable in this matter. “Whoever fulfils his covenant and is mindful of God,” avoiding association of partners and acts of disobedience—“God loves the God-fearing.” How could the property of someone God loves be made lawful to take, or his inviolability lapse? Rather, whoever abolishes his inviolability has made war upon God and His Messenger. Alternatively: whoever among the People of the Book fulfils God’s covenant, believes in Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, avoids treachery and returns the trust—“God loves the God-fearing.” He puts the explicit noun ( المظهر ) in the place of a pronoun referring back to “whoever” ( مَن ), to make the statement general. “The God-fearing” is a general expression applying to returning deposits and to other things, indicating that God-fearingness ( التقوى ) is the governing principle of the matter and the cause of preservation. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-75-76-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-75-76-s3","r":"q3-75-76","title":"Realization does not cancel the Law or people’s rights","text":"We have seen some of the spiritually poor enter the land of Reality ( الحقيقة ), whereupon reverence for the religious Law ( الشريعة ) falls away from their hearts. They become careless with people’s property, and the inviolability of God’s servants loses its hold upon them, until you cannot trust them to protect either property or family. Deposit something with such a person, or entrust him with capital in a profit-sharing investment ( قِراض ), and he will not return it unless you keep standing over him. This is heresy ( زندقة ), an Israelite tendency that even the lowest of people would not accept—how much less someone claiming to be the highest! [XIV-N039] Among the sayings of wisdom is: “The perfection of religious integrity is to abandon treachery.” The greatest bankruptcy is betraying people. A hadith states: “Three qualities make a person a hypocrite, even if he prays, fasts and claims to be a believer: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his promise, and when entrusted he betrays the trust.” If he argues on behalf of his soul that commands evil ( النفس الأمّارة ), saying, “We are not answerable concerning the possessions of ordinary people,” he has cast the bond of Islam from his neck and deserves the sharp sword to fall upon the crown of his head. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-75-76-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-75-76-s4","r":"q3-75-76","title":"","text":"One form of treachery is consuming people’s property through wicked oaths, as the Real Most High indicates, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-75-76-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-77","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits 3:77","anchor":"unit-q3-77"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-1","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَشْتَرُونَ بِعَهْدِ اللَّهِ وَأَيْمانِهِمْ ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً أُولئِكَ لا خَلاقَ لَهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ وَلا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ اللَّهُ وَلا يَنْظُرُ إِلَيْهِمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ وَلا يُزَكِّيهِمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ (77)","anchor":"ar-q3-77-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-2","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَشْتَرُونَ بِعَهْدِ اللَّهِ أي: يستبدلون بالوفاء بعهد الله كالإيمان بالرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- الذي أخذ على بني إسرائيل في التوراة وبيان صفته، وأداء الأمانة، فكتموا ذلك واستبدلوا به ثَمَناً قَلِيلًا حطاماً فانياً من الدنيا، كانوا يأخذونه من سفلتهم، فخافوا إن بيَّنوا ذلك زال ذلك عنهم، وكذلك الأيمان التي أخذها الله عليهم لئن أدركوا محمدا صلّى الله عليه وسلم ليؤمنن به ولينصرنه، فنقضوها، خوفاً من زوال رئاستهم، فاستبدلوا بالوفاء بها ثمناً قليلا فانياً، أُولئِكَ لا خَلاقَ لَهُمْ أي: لا نصيب لهم، فِي الْآخِرَةِ، وَلا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ اللَّهُ بما يسرهم، أو بشيء أصلاً، وإنما الملائكة تسألهم، وَلا يَنْظُرُ إِلَيْهِمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ نظرة رحمة، بل يعرض عنهم، غضباً عليهم وهواناً بهم، وَلا يُزَكِّيهِمْ لا يطهرهم من ذنوبهم، أو لا يُثني عليهم، وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ أي: موجع.","anchor":"ar-q3-77-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-3","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"قال عكرمة: نزلت في أبي رافع وكنانة بن أَبي الحقيق وحُيي بن أخطب، وغيرهم من رؤساء اليهود، كتموا ما عهد الله إليهم في التوراة في شأن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم من بيان صفته، فكتموا ذلك وكتبوا غيره، وحلفوا أنه من عند الله، لئلا يفوتهم الرشا من أتباعهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-77-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-4","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"وقال الكلبي: إن ناساً من علماء اليهود كانوا ذا حظ من علم التوراة، فأصابتهم سنة، فأتوا كعب بن الأشرف يستميرونه، أي: يطلبون منه الميرة- وهو الطعام-، فقال لهم كعب: هل تعلمون أن هذا الرجل رسول في كتابكم؟","anchor":"ar-q3-77-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-5","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"قالوا: نعم، أو ما تعلمه أنت؟ قال: لا، قالوا: فإنا نشهد أنه عبد الله ورسوله، قال كعب: لقد قدمتم عليَّ، وأنا أريد أن أميركم وأكسوكم، فَحَرَمَكُم الله خيراً كثيراً، قالوا: فإنه شُبه لنا، فرُوَيْداً حتى نلقاه، فانطلقوا، فكتبوا صفة غير صفته، ثم أتوا نبى الله- عليه الصلاة والسلام- فكلموه، ثم رجعوا إلى كعب، فقالوا: قد كنا نرى أنه رسول الله، فأتيناه فإذا هو ليس بالنعت الذي نُعت لنا، وأخرجوا الذي كتبوه، ففرح كعب، ومارهم. فنزلت الآية. قلت: انظر الطمع، وما يصنع بصاحبه! والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q3-77-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-6","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"وقيل: نزلت في رجل أقام سلعته في السوق، وحلف لقد أعطى فيها كذا وكذا، وقيل: نزلت في الأشعث بن قيس، كانت بينه وبين رجل خصومة، فتوجهت اليمين على الرجل، فأراد أن يحلف. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-77-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-7","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"الإشارة: قد أخذ الله العهد على الأرواح ألا يعبدوا معه غيره، ولا يميلوا إلى شيء سواه، فكل من مال إلى شيء أو ركن بالمحبة إلى غير الله، فقد نقض العهد مع الله، فلا نصيب له في مقام المعرفة، ولا تحصل له مشاهدة ولا مكالمة حتى يثوب ويتوجه بكليته إلى مولاه. والله- تعالى- أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-77-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-77-8","r":"q3-77","title":"3:77 · Selling the covenant; worldly inducement and the covenant of spirits","text":"ومن مساوئهم أيضا: تحريفهم لكتاب الله، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق- تعالى- بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-77-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-77-s1","r":"q3-77","title":"The paltry price of concealing a binding trust","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Those who exchange God’s covenant”—who barter away fidelity to it, such as belief in the Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, the covenant taken from the Children of Israel in the Torah, disclosure of his description, and the discharge of trusts. They concealed this and exchanged it for “a paltry price”: the perishing debris of this world that they received from their common followers. They feared that disclosing it would cost them these receipts. Likewise, they broke the oaths God had taken from them that, should they live to encounter Muḥammad, they would believe in him and support him, for fear of losing their leadership. In place of fidelity, they took a paltry, perishing price. “They have no share”—no portion—“in the Hereafter. God will not speak to them” with anything that pleases them, or will not speak to them at all: only the angels question them. He will not “look upon them on the Day of Resurrection” with a look of mercy, but will turn from them in anger and make them abased. He will not “purify them” of their sins, or praise them. “Theirs will be a painful,” grievous, “punishment.” ʿIkrima said: it was revealed concerning Abū Rāfiʿ, Kināna ibn Abī al-Ḥuqayq, Ḥuyayy ibn Akhṭab and other Jewish leaders. They concealed what God had entrusted to them in the Torah concerning disclosure of the Prophet’s description, wrote something else, and swore that it came from God, so that they would not lose their followers’ bribes. Al-Kalbī said: some Jewish scholars with a share of knowledge of the Torah were afflicted by a year of famine. They went to Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf to seek provisions—that is, food. Kaʿb asked them: “Do you know that this man is a messenger in your scripture?” They answered: “Yes. Do you not know it yourself?” He said: “No.” They replied: “We testify that he is God’s servant and Messenger.” Kaʿb said: “You came to me when I intended to provision and clothe you; God has now deprived you of much good.” They said: “We were confused about him. Give us a little time to meet him.” They went away and wrote a description different from his. Then they went to God’s Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, and spoke to him. Returning to Kaʿb, they said: “We used to think he was God’s Messenger, but when we visited him, he did not match the description given to us.” They produced what they had written, and Kaʿb rejoiced and supplied them with provisions. The verse was then revealed. I say: look at avarice and what it does to its possessor! In God we seek refuge. Another account says it was revealed concerning a man who displayed his merchandise in the market and swore that he had been offered such-and-such a price for it. Another says it concerned al-Ashʿath ibn Qays, who had a dispute with a man upon whom the oath then devolved; the man intended to swear it. And God Most High knows best. [XIV-N040]","anchor":"en-q3-77-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-77-s2","r":"q3-77","title":"The covenant that no other should share the heart’s devotion","text":"God took the covenant from the spirits ( الأرواح ) that they should worship none with Him and incline to nothing other than Him. Whoever inclines to a thing, or rests in love upon someone other than God, has broken his covenant with God. He has no portion in the station of knowledge of God ( المعرفة ), nor does witnessing ( المشاهدة ) or divine converse ( المكالمة ) come to him until he returns and turns in his entirety towards his Master. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-77-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-77-s3","r":"q3-77","title":"","text":"Another of their faults is altering God’s scripture, as the Real Most High indicates in His words:","anchor":"en-q3-77-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-78","r":"q3-78","title":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge","text":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge 3:78","anchor":"unit-q3-78"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-78-1","r":"q3-78","title":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge","text":"وَإِنَّ مِنْهُمْ لَفَرِيقاً يَلْوُونَ أَلْسِنَتَهُمْ بِالْكِتابِ لِتَحْسَبُوهُ مِنَ الْكِتابِ وَما هُوَ مِنَ الْكِتابِ وَيَقُولُونَ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ وَما هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ (78)","anchor":"ar-q3-78-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-78-2","r":"q3-78","title":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنَّ من أهل الكتاب لَفَرِيقاً، وهو كعب بن الأشرف، وحيي بن أخطب، ومالك بن الصيف، وأبو ياسر، وشعبة بن عامر، يَلْوُونَ أي: يفتلون أَلْسِنَتَهُمْ بِالْكِتابِ أي: التوراة عند قراءته، فيميلون عن المنزل إلى المُحرف، لِتَحْسَبُوهُ مِنَ الْكِتابِ أي: لتظنوا أن ذلك المحرف من التوراة، وَما هُوَ مِنَ الْكِتابِ وَيَقُولُونَ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ وَما هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ فيما نسبوا إليه، وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ أنه ليس من عند الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-78-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-78-3","r":"q3-78","title":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge","text":"قال ابن عباس: نزلت في اليهود والنصارى جميعاً، حرفوا التوراة والإنجيل، وألحقوا به ما ليس منه، وأسقطوا منه الدين الحنيف، فبيَّن الله كذبهم. وقيل: في الرجم، حيث كتموا الرجم، وألقى قارئ التوراة يده على آية الرجم، وقرأ ما حولها، فقال له ابنُ سلام: ارفع يديك، فإذا آية الرجم تلوح. والله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-78-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-78-4","r":"q3-78","title":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge","text":"الإشارة: هذه الآية تنسحب على علماء السوء، الذين يفتون بغير المشهور، لحظ يأخذونه من الدنيا، وعلى قضاة الجور الذين يحكمون بالهوى، ويعتمدون على الأقوال الواهية، ويقولون هو من عند الله، وما هو من عند الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-78-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-78-5","r":"q3-78","title":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge","text":"وكذلك بعض المنتسبين من الفقراء، يتصنعون إلى العامة، يطمعون فيما في أيديهم من الحطام، فيظهرون لهم علوماً ومعارف وحكماً، يلوون ألسنتهم بها وقلوبهم خاوية من معناها، فظاهر حالهم يُوهم أن ذلك موافق لقلوبهم، وأنهم عاملون بذلك، وباطنهم يكذبهم في ذلك، (وَاللَّهُ يهدي مَن يشاء إلى صراط مستقيم) .","anchor":"ar-q3-78-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-78-6","r":"q3-78","title":"3:78 · Distorting scripture, corrupt judgments and the imitation of spiritual knowledge","text":"ثم أبطل الله تعالى شبهة اليهود والنصارى فى عبادة عيسى وعزير وغيرهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-78-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-78-s1","r":"q3-78","title":"Presenting altered words as revealed scripture","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Among” the People of the Book “is a group”—Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf, Ḥuyayy ibn Akhṭab, Mālik ibn al-Ṣayf, Abū Yāsir and Shuʿba ibn ʿĀmir—“who twist,” that is, turn and contort, “their tongues with the scripture,” the Torah, when reciting it. They turn from what was revealed to what has been altered, “so that you might think it belongs to the scripture”: suppose that the altered material belongs to the Torah, “though it does not belong to the scripture.” They say, “‘It is from God,’ though it is not from God.” They “knowingly speak falsehood against God” in what they attribute to Him, knowing that it is not from Him. Ibn ʿAbbās said: it was revealed concerning both Jews and Christians, who altered the Torah and the Gospel, added what did not belong to them, and removed the upright religion; God made their falsehood clear. Another account concerns stoning: they concealed it, and the reader of the Torah put his hand over the verse on stoning while reciting what surrounded it. Ibn Salām told him to lift his hands, whereupon the verse on stoning was plainly visible. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-78-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-78-s2","r":"q3-78","title":"Worldly gain behind scholarly and spiritual appearances","text":"This verse extends to corrupt scholars who issue rulings contrary to the established predominant position ( المشهور ) for a worldly portion they receive, and to unjust judges who judge by desire and rely on unsound opinions, saying, “It is from God,” although it is not from God. [XIV-N041] So too with certain people affiliated with the spiritually poor: they put on a performance for the public, coveting the worldly debris in their hands. They display sciences, spiritual knowledge and words of wisdom, twisting their tongues around them, while their hearts are empty of their meaning. Their outward appearance suggests that these things correspond to their hearts and that they act upon them, but their inward state gives them the lie. “God guides whom He wills to a straight path.”","anchor":"en-q3-78-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-78-s3","r":"q3-78","title":"","text":"God Most High then refuted the misconception of the Jews and Christians concerning the worship of Jesus, Ezra and others, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-78-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-79-80","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation 3:79–80","anchor":"unit-q3-79-80"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-1","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"ما كانَ لِبَشَرٍ أَنْ يُؤْتِيَهُ اللَّهُ الْكِتابَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ ثُمَّ يَقُولَ لِلنَّاسِ كُونُوا عِباداً لِي مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَلكِنْ كُونُوا رَبَّانِيِّينَ بِما كُنْتُمْ تُعَلِّمُونَ الْكِتابَ وَبِما كُنْتُمْ تَدْرُسُونَ (79) وَلا يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَنْ تَتَّخِذُوا الْمَلائِكَةَ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ أَرْباباً أَيَأْمُرُكُمْ بِالْكُفْرِ بَعْدَ إِذْ أَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ (80)","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-2","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"قلت: البشر: اسم جمع لا مفرد له، يطلق على الجماعة والواحد. والرباني: هو الذي يُربي الناس ويؤدبهم ويُهذبهم بالعلم والعمل. وقال ابن عباس: (هو الذي يُربي الناس بصغار العلم قبل كباره) ، والنون فيه للمبالغة، كلحياني ورقباني. و (لا يأمركم) بالرفع، استئناف، وبالنصب: عطف على «يقول» ، و «لا» مزيدة،: أي ما كان لبشر أن يستنبئه الله، ثم يأمر بعبادة نفسه، ويأمر باتخاذ الملائكة أرباباً. أو غير مزيدة، والتقدير: ليس له أن يأمر بعبادته ولا باتخاذ الملائكة أرباباً.","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-3","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ما كانَ ينبغي لِبَشَرٍ أَنْ يُؤْتِيَهُ اللَّهُ الْكِتابَ وَالْحُكْمَ أي: الفصل بين العباد، وَالنُّبُوَّةَ أي: الوحي بالأحكام، ثُمَّ يَقُولَ بعد ذلك لِلنَّاسِ كُونُوا عِباداً لِي مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ أو مع الله، أو يرضى أن يعبد من دون الله، وَلكِنْ يقول لهم: كُونُوا رَبَّانِيِّينَ أي: علماء بالله، فقهاء في دينه، حلماء على الناس، تُربون الناس بالعلم والعمل والهمة والحال، بسبب بما كنتم تعلمون من كتاب الله وَبِما كُنْتُمْ تَدْرُسُونَ منه، أو بِما كُنْتُمْ تُعَلِّمُونَ الناس من الخير بكتاب الله، وما كنتم تدرسونه عليهم. ولمّا مات ابن عباس- رضى الله عنهما- قال محمد بن الحنفية: (مات ربَّاني هذه الأمة) .","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-4","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"ولا يأمركم ذلك البشر الذي خصه الله بالنبوة، أَنْ تَتَّخِذُوا الْمَلائِكَةَ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ أَرْباباً من دون الله، أَيَأْمُرُكُمْ بِالْكُفْرِ بَعْدَ إِذْ أَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ أي: منقادون لأحكام الله. قيل: سبب نزول الآية: أن نصارى نجران قالوا: يا محمد تريد أن نعبدك ونتخذك ربا؟ فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «معاذ الله أن نعبد غيرَ الله، أو نَأمُرَ بعبادة غيره» . وقيل: أن رجلاً قال: يا رسول الله: نُسلِّم عليك كما يُسلِّم بعضُنا على بعض، أفلا نسجُد لك؟ فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-5","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"«لا يَنْبَغِي ان يسجد احدٌ لأحدٍ من دُونِ اللهِ، ولكنْ أكْرِموا نَبِيَّكُمْ، واعْرِفُوا الحقَّ لأَهْلِه» .","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-6","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"الإشارة: ما زال الفقراء يعظمون أشياخهم، ويبالغون في ذلك حتى يُقبِّلون أرجلهم والترابَ بين أيديهم، ويجتهدون في خدمتهم(1) ، فإذا رءاهم الأشياخ فعلوا ذلك سكتوا عنهم، لأن ذلك هو ربحهم وسبب فتحهم، وفي ذلك قال القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-7","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"بذَبْح النفوس وحط الرءوس تصفى الكئوس","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-8","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"لكنهم يرشدونهم إلى الحضرة، حتى يفنوهم عن شهود الواسطة، فيكون تعظيمهم وحط رأسهم إنما هو لله لا لغيره، وحينئذٍ يكونون ربانيين، علماء بالله مقربين، وكان شيخنا يقول: لا تزوروني على أني شيخكم، ولكن اعرفوا فينا، وافنوا عن رؤية حسنا، حتى يكون التعظيم إنما هو لله ربنا. هـ. فدلالة الأشياخ للفقراء على التعظيم والأدب ليس ذلك مقصوداً لأنفسهم، وحاشاهم من ذلك. ما كان لبشر أن يؤتيه الله الخصوصية ثم يقول للناس كونوا عباداً لي من دون الله، ولكن يقول لهم: كونوا ربانيين عارفين بالله، حتى يكون تعظيمكم إنما هو لله، ولا يأمر أيضاً بالفرق حتى يتخذوا الأشياء أرباباً من دون الله، ولكن يأمر بالجمع حتى يغيبوا عما سوى الله، وكيف يأمرهم بالفرق، وهو إنما يدلهم على الجمع؟ أيأمرهم بالكفر بعد أن كانوا مسلمين. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-79-80-9","r":"q3-79-80","title":"3:79–80 · God-centred teachers; veneration, spiritual training and the limits of mediation","text":"ثم ذكر أخذ الميثاق على الأنبياء وأممهم في الإيمان بالنبي صلّى الله عليه وسلم فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-79-80-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-79-80-s1","r":"q3-79-80","title":"Bashar, rabbānī and the readings of “he commands you”","text":"I say: bashar ( البشر ) is a collective expression ( اسم جمع ) with no singular form of its own; it is applied to a group and to an individual. A rabbānī is someone who nurtures people, trains their conduct and refines them through knowledge and action. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “He is one who nurtures people through the elementary matters of knowledge before its major ones.” The nūn in it conveys intensification, as in liḥyānī and raqabānī. [XIV-N042] With the indicative ( الرفع ), “nor does he command you” ( ولا يأمركم ) begins a new statement ( استئناف ). With the subjunctive ( النصب ), it is coordinated with “say” ( يقول ), and lā is additional ( مزيدة ): it is not for a human being whom God makes a prophet then to command worship of himself and command the taking of angels as lords. Alternatively, lā is not additional, and the reconstructed sense is: he may neither command worship of himself nor the taking of angels as lords.","anchor":"en-q3-79-80-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-79-80-s2","r":"q3-79-80","title":"Teaching that directs worship to God rather than the teacher","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: it would not be fitting for “a human being to whom God gives scripture, judgment”—adjudication between His servants—“and prophethood”—revelation of ordinances—“then to say to people: ‘Be servants of me apart from God,’” or alongside God, or to consent to being worshipped apart from God. Rather, he tells them: “Be God-centred teachers ( ربّانيين )”: knowers of God, discerning in His religion and forbearing towards people, nurturing them through knowledge, action, spiritual aspiration ( الهمّة ) and spiritual state ( الحال ), by virtue of what you know of God’s scripture and what you study of it; or by virtue of the good you teach people through God’s scripture and what you rehearse to them. When Ibn ʿAbbās, God be pleased with him and his father, died, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyya said: “The rabbānī of this community has died.” [XIV-N043] “Nor does he command you”—that human being whom God has specially favoured with prophethood—“to take angels and prophets as lords” apart from God. “Would he command you to disbelieve after you have submitted to God,” that is, yielded to His ordinances? One account gives this occasion for the verse’s revelation: the Christians of Najrān said, “Muḥammad, do you want us to worship you and take you as a lord?” The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, answered: “God forbid that we worship anyone other than God, or command the worship of another.” Another says that a man asked: “Messenger of God, we greet you as we greet one another; should we not prostrate ourselves before you?” He answered: “No one should prostrate himself before anyone apart from God. Rather, honour your prophet and acknowledge the due of those to whom it belongs.”","anchor":"en-q3-79-80-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-79-80-s3","r":"q3-79-80","title":"Honouring the guide without making the intermediary the goal","text":"The spiritually poor have always venerated their shaykhs, going so far as to kiss their feet and the ground before them, and exerting themselves in their service. When the shaykhs see them doing so, they do not forbid them, because this is the disciples’ gain and a cause of their spiritual opening ( الفتح ). Of this someone has said: [XIV-N044] Through the slaughter of the lower selves and the lowering of heads, the cups are made clear. Yet the shaykhs guide them to the Presence ( الحضرة ), until they efface them from witnessing the intermediary ( الواسطة ). Their veneration and lowering of their heads are then for God, not another. At that point they become rabbānīs: knowers of God, brought near. Our shaykh used to say: “Do not visit me on the basis that I am your shaykh. Rather, recognize [God] in us and be effaced from seeing our sensible appearance, so that the veneration is for God, our Lord.” End of the quotation. [XIV-N045] Thus, when shaykhs direct the spiritually poor to veneration and right conduct ( الأدب ), they do not intend this for their own persons—far be it from them! It is not for a human being whom God gives special spiritual distinction then to tell people, “Be servants of me apart from God.” Rather, he tells them: “Be rabbānīs, knowers of God,” so that your veneration is for God alone. Nor does he command separation ( الفرق ), so that they take things as lords apart from God. Rather, he commands gathering in unity ( الجمع ), so that they become absent from all that is other than God. How could he command separation when he is pointing them to gathering? Would he command them to disbelieve after they had submitted? And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-79-80-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-79-80-s4","r":"q3-79-80","title":"","text":"He then mentioned the covenant taken from the prophets and their communities to believe in the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-79-80-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-81-82","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality 3:81–82","anchor":"unit-q3-81-82"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-1","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"وَإِذْ أَخَذَ اللَّهُ مِيثاقَ النَّبِيِّينَ لَما آتَيْتُكُمْ مِنْ كِتابٍ وَحِكْمَةٍ ثُمَّ جاءَكُمْ رَسُولٌ مُصَدِّقٌ لِما مَعَكُمْ لَتُؤْمِنُنَّ بِهِ وَلَتَنْصُرُنَّهُ قالَ أَأَقْرَرْتُمْ وَأَخَذْتُمْ عَلى ذلِكُمْ إِصْرِي قالُوا أَقْرَرْنا قالَ فَاشْهَدُوا وَأَنَا مَعَكُمْ مِنَ الشَّاهِدِينَ (81) فَمَنْ تَوَلَّى بَعْدَ ذلِكَ فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْفاسِقُونَ (82)","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-2","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"قلت: اللام في (لما) ، موطئة للقسم لأن أخذ الميثاق بمعنى الاستحلاف، و (ما) : يحتمل الشرطية، و (لتؤمنن) : جواب القسم، سد مسد الجواب، أي: مهما آتيناكم من كتاب وحكمة ثم جاءكم رسول الله لتؤمنن به.","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-3","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"ويحتمل الموصولية، و (لتؤمنن) : خبر عنه، وحذف شرط يدل عليه السياق أي: للذي آتيناكم من كتاب وحكمة، ثم إذا جاءكم رسول مصدق لما معكم لتؤمنن به. ومن قرأ بكسر اللام كان تعليلاً للأمر بالإيمان بالرسول، أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-4","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"لأجل الذي خصصتكم به إذا جاءكُمْ رسول مصدق لما معكم لتؤمنن به، وإذا كان أخذ الله الميثاق على الأنبياء كان على الأتباع أولى، أو استغنى بذكر الأنبياء عن ذكر أتباعهم لأنهم فى حكمهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-5","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر إِذْ أخذنا الميثاق على النبيين من لدن آدم عليه السلام إلى عيسى عليه السلام. وقلنا لهم: والله للذي خصصتكم به مِنْ كِتابٍ وَحِكْمَةٍ، ثم إن ظهر رسول مُصَدِّقٌ لِما مَعَكُمْ لَتُؤْمِنُنَّ بِهِ وَلَتَنْصُرُنَّهُ أنتم وأممكم، أو: لأجل الذي خصصتكم به مما تقدم لئن أدركتم محمداً لتؤمنن به ولتنصرنه. قال سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه-: (لم يبعث اللهُ نبياً، آدم ومن بعده، إلا أخذ عليه العهد في محمد، وأمره بأخذ العهد على قومه ليُؤْمنُنَّ به، ولئن بُعث وهم أحياءٌ لينْصُرُنَّه) .","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-6","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"قالَ الحق جلّ جلاله لمَن أخذ عليهم العهد: أَأَقْرَرْتُمْ بذلك وقبلتموه، وَأَخَذْتُمْ عَلى ذلِكُمْ إِصْرِي أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-7","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"عهدي وميثاقي؟ قالُوا أَقْرَرْنا وقبلنا، قالَ فَاشْهَدُوا على أنفسكم، أو ليشهدْ بعضكم على بعض بالإقرار، أو فاشهدوا يا ملائكتي عليهم، وَأَنَا مَعَكُمْ مِنَ الشَّاهِدِينَ، وفيه توكيد وتحذير عظيم، فَمَنْ تَوَلَّى بَعْدَ ذلِكَ الإقرار والشهادة، وأعرض عن الإيمان به، ونصره بعد ظهوره، فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْفاسِقُونَ الخارجون عن الإيمان المتمردون في الكفران.","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-81-82-8","r":"q3-81-82","title":"3:81–82 · The prophetic covenant and the inseparability of Law and Reality","text":"الإشارة: كما أخذ الله العهد على الأنبياء وأممهم في الإيمان به عليه الصلاة والسلام، أخذ الميثاق على العلماء وأتباعهم من العامة، لئن أدركوا وليّاً من أولياء الله، حاملاً لواء الحقيقة، مصدقا لما معهم من الشريعة، ليؤمنن به ولينصرنه، فمن تولى وأعرض عن الإذعان إليهم فأولئك هم الفاسقون الخارجون عن دائرة الولاية، محرومون من سابق العناية، فإن الحقيقة إنما هي لب الشريعة وخلاصتها، فإنما مثل الحقيقة والشريعة كالروح للجسد، فالشريعة كالجسد، والحقيقة كالروح، فالشريعة بلا حقيقة جسد بلا روح، والحقيقة بلا شريعة روح بلا جسد، فلا قيام لهذا إلا بهذا، فمن تشرَع ولم يتحقق فقد تفسق، ومن تحقق ولم يتشرّع فقد تزندق، ومَن جمع بينهما فقد تحقق، ومن خرج عنهما فقد خرج عن دين الله وطلب غيره. وإليه توجه الإنكار بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-81-82-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-81-82-s1","r":"q3-81-82","title":"Oath, condition and the binding covenant","text":"I say: the lām in la-mā ( لما ) prepares for an oath ( موطئة للقسم ), since taking the covenant has the force of exacting an oath ( الاستحلاف ). Mā may be conditional ( شرطية ); “you shall surely believe” ( لتؤمنن ) is the response to the oath ( جواب القسم ), also taking the place of the response to the condition. Thus: whatever scripture and wisdom We give you, then a messenger of God comes to you, you shall surely believe in him. [XIV-N046] Mā may instead be relative ( موصولية ), with “you shall surely believe” as its predicate ( خبر ). A condition indicated by the context has been omitted: with respect to the scripture and wisdom I have given you, then, if a messenger comes confirming what you have, you shall surely believe in him. In the reading with a kasra on the lām, the phrase supplies the reason for the command to believe in the messenger: because of what I have specially granted you, when a messenger comes confirming what you have, you shall surely believe in him. If God took the covenant from the prophets, it applies all the more to their followers; alternatively, mentioning the prophets suffices instead of mentioning their followers, since they fall under the same ruling.","anchor":"en-q3-81-82-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-81-82-s2","r":"q3-81-82","title":"Acknowledgment, support and mutual witness","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: remember when We took the covenant from the prophets, from Adam to Jesus, peace be upon them. We told them: by God, with respect to the scripture and wisdom with which I have specially favoured you, should a messenger appear “confirming what is with you, you shall surely believe in him and support him”—you and your communities. Alternatively: because of the favour already described, should you encounter Muḥammad, you shall surely believe in him and support him. Our master ʿAlī, God ennoble his face, said: “God sent no prophet, Adam or any after him, without taking his pledge concerning Muḥammad and commanding him to take his people’s pledge that they would believe in him, and that, should he be sent while they were alive, they would support him.” The Real, exalted is His majesty, said to those from whom He took the pledge: “Do you acknowledge” and accept it, “and accept My binding covenant ( إصري ) upon it”—My pledge and covenant? “They said: ‘We acknowledge’” and accept. He said: “Then bear witness” against yourselves, or let each bear witness to the others’ acknowledgment; or, bear witness against them, My angels. “I am with you among the witnesses.” This contains emphatic confirmation and a mighty warning. “Whoever turns away after” that acknowledgment and witnessing, refusing belief in him and support for him after his appearance, “it is they who are the transgressors”: departing from faith and rebelliously persisting in unbelief.","anchor":"en-q3-81-82-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-81-82-s3","r":"q3-81-82","title":"The religious Law as body and Reality as spirit","text":"Just as God took the pledge from the prophets and their communities to believe in him, blessings and peace be upon him, He took a covenant from the scholars and their ordinary followers: should they encounter one of God’s friends bearing the banner of Reality ( الحقيقة ), confirming the religious Law ( الشريعة ) they possess, they must believe in him and support him. Those who turn away and refuse to yield to them are the transgressors, outside the circle of friendship with God ( الولاية ) and deprived of antecedent divine care ( سابق العناية ). Reality is the very kernel and distillation of the Law. Their relation is that of spirit to body: the Law is like the body, Reality like the spirit. Law without Reality is a body without spirit; Reality without Law is a spirit without body. Neither can stand without the other. Whoever adheres to the Law without realizing Reality falls into transgression; whoever realizes Reality without adhering to the Law falls into heresy; whoever brings both together attains realization. Whoever departs from both has departed from God’s religion and sought another. To him is directed the reproach in His words:","anchor":"en-q3-81-82-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-83","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance 3:83","anchor":"unit-q3-83"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-1","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"أَفَغَيْرَ دِينِ اللَّهِ يَبْغُونَ وَلَهُ أَسْلَمَ مَنْ فِي السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ طَوْعاً وَكَرْهاً وَإِلَيْهِ يُرْجَعُونَ (83)","anchor":"ar-q3-83-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-2","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"قلت: (أفغير) : مفعول مقدم، و (يبغون) : معطوف على محذوف، أي: أتتولون فتبغون غير دين الله، وقدم المعمول لأنه المقصود بالإنكار، و (طوعاً وكرهاً) : حالان، أي: طائعين أو كارهين.","anchor":"ar-q3-83-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-3","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للنصارى واليهود، لمَّا اختصموا إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، وادعوا أن كل واحد على دين إبراهيم، فقال لهم- عليه الصلاة والسلام: «كِلاكما بَرِيءٌ مِنْ دِينه، وأنا على دِينه، فخذوا به» ، فغضبوا، وقالوا:","anchor":"ar-q3-83-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-4","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"والله لا نرضى بحكمك ولا نأخذ بدينك، فقال لهم الحق جل جلاله- منكرا عليهم-: أفتبغون غير دين الله الذي ارتضاه لخليله وحبيبه، وقد انقاد له تعالى مَنْ فِي السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ طائعين ومكرهين، فأهل السموات","anchor":"ar-q3-83-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-5","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"انقادوا طائعين، وأهل الأرض منهم من انقاد طوعاً بالنظر واتباع الحجة أو بغيرها، ومنهم من انقاد كرهاً أو بمعاينة ما يُلجئ إلى الإسلام كنتق الجبل وإدراك الغرق والإشراف على الموت، أو: «طوعاً» كالملائكة والمؤمنين، فإنهم انقادوا لما يراد منهم طوعاً، (وكرهاً) كالكفار فانقادوا لما يراد منهم كرهاً، وكلٍّ إليه راجعون، لا يخرج عن دائرة حكمه، أو راجعون إليه بالبعث والنشور. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-83-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-6","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الدين الحقيقي هو الانقياد إلى الله في الظاهر والباطن، أما الانقياد إلى الله في الظاهر فيكون بامتثال أمره واجتناب نهيه، وأما الانقياد إلى الله في الباطن فيكون بالرضى بحكمه والاستسلام لقهره.","anchor":"ar-q3-83-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-7","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"فكل من قصَّر في الانقياد في الظاهر، أو تسخط من الأحكام الجلالية في الباطن، فقد خرج عن كمال الدين، فيقال له: أفغير دين الله تبغون وقد انقاد له (من في السموات والأرض طوعاً وكرهاً) ، فإما أن تنقاد طوعاً أو ترجع إليه كرها. وفي بعض الآثار يقول الله تبارك وتعالى: «منْ لم يَرْضَ بقضائي ولم يَصْبِرْ على بَلائِي، فليخرجْ من تحت سَمَائي، وليتخذْ ربّاً سِوَاي» .","anchor":"ar-q3-83-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-8","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"وسبب تبرّم القلب عن نزول الأحكام القهرية مرضُه وضعف نور يقينه، فكل من استنكف عن صحبة الطبيب، فله من هذا العتاب حظ ونصيب، فالأولياء حجة الله على العلماء، والعلماء حجة الله على العوام، فمن لم يستقم ظاهره عُوتب على تفريطه في صحبة العلماء، ومن لم يستقم باطنه عاتبه الله تعالى على ترك صُحبة الأولياء، أعني العارفين. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-83-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-83-9","r":"q3-83","title":"3:83 · Willing and unwilling submission; outward obedience and inward acceptance","text":"ثم بين الحق- تعالى- حقيقة الإيمان والإسلام الذي يجب اتباعه على جميع الأنام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-83-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-83-s1","r":"q3-83","title":"The fronted object and the circumstantial expressions","text":"I say: “other than” ( أفغير ) is a fronted object ( مفعول مقدّم ). “They seek” ( يبغون ) is coordinated with an omitted expression: do you turn away and so seek a religion other than God’s? The governed expression ( المعمول ) is placed first because it is the target of the reproach. “Willingly and unwillingly” ( طوعاً وكرهاً ) are two circumstantial expressions ( حالان ): being willing or unwilling.","anchor":"en-q3-83-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-83-s2","r":"q3-83","title":"No creature stands outside God’s rule","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, addresses the Christians and Jews when they brought their dispute to the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, each claiming to follow Abraham’s religion. He told them: “You are both disassociated from his religion; I follow his religion, so take hold of it.” They grew angry and said: “By God, we will neither accept your judgment nor adopt your religion.” The Real, exalted is His majesty, rebukes them: do you seek a religion other than God’s, which He approved for His intimate friend and His beloved, when whoever is in the heavens and the earth has yielded to Him, willingly or under compulsion? The inhabitants of the heavens yield willingly. Of the inhabitants of the earth, some yield willingly through reflection and following proof, or by another means; others yield unwillingly, or through witnessing what compels submission, such as the raising of the mountain, being overtaken by drowning, or approaching death. Alternatively, “willingly” describes the angels and believers, who willingly submit to what is required of them; “unwillingly” describes the unbelievers, who unwillingly submit to what is willed concerning them. All return to Him: none stands outside the circle of His judgment. Alternatively, they return to Him through resurrection and the raising of the dead. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-83-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-83-s3","r":"q3-83","title":"The two forms of yielding and the physician of the heart","text":"Know that true religion is yielding to God outwardly and inwardly. Outward yielding consists in fulfilling His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Inward yielding consists in contentment with His judgment ( الرضا بحكمه ) and surrender to His overpowering might ( الاستسلام لقهره ). Whoever falls short in outward obedience or inwardly resents the majestic decrees ( الأحكام الجلالية ) has fallen short of the perfection of religion. He is asked: do you seek a religion other than God’s, when whoever is in the heavens and earth has yielded to Him, willingly or unwillingly? Either yield willingly or return to Him unwillingly. In certain transmitted reports, God—blessed and exalted—says: “Whoever is not content with My decree and does not patiently bear My trial, let him leave the shelter of My heaven and take a lord other than Me.” [XIV-N047] The reason the heart chafes at the descent of overpowering decrees is its sickness and the weakness of the light of its certainty ( اليقين ). Whoever disdains the physician’s companionship has a share in this reproach. God’s friends are His proof against the scholars; the scholars are His proof against ordinary people. Whoever’s outward conduct is not upright is reproached for neglecting the companionship of the scholars. Whoever’s inward state is not upright is reproached by God Most High for abandoning the companionship of the friends of God—that is, the knowers of Him. Success comes through God, and He guides to the even way.","anchor":"en-q3-83-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-83-s4","r":"q3-83","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then explained the reality of faith and submission that all people must follow, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-83-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-84","r":"q3-84","title":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God","text":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God 3:84","anchor":"unit-q3-84"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-84-1","r":"q3-84","title":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God","text":"قُلْ آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَما أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنا وَما أُنْزِلَ عَلى إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْباطِ وَما أُوتِيَ مُوسى وَعِيسى وَالنَّبِيُّونَ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ لاَ نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُسْلِمُونَ (84)","anchor":"ar-q3-84-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-84-2","r":"q3-84","title":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God","text":"قلت: (أُنزل) : يتعدى بإلى لأنه ينتهي إلى الرسل، ويتعدى بعلى، لأنه يأتي من ناحية العلو والاستعلاء، وفرَّق بعضهُم بين التعبير هنا بعلى وفي البقرة بإلى، فقال: لأن الخطاب هنا للرسول بالخصوص، وقد أنزل عليه الوحي مباشرة، وهناك الخطاب للمسلمين، وإنما أنزل الوحي متوجهاً إليهم بالواسطة، ولم يكن عليهم بالمباشرة.","anchor":"ar-q3-84-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-84-3","r":"q3-84","title":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-84-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-84-4","r":"q3-84","title":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد لأهل الكتاب الذين فرقوا في إيمانهم بين الرسل: أما نحن فقد آمنا بالذي أُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنا وَما أُنْزِلَ على جميع الأنبياء والرسل لاَ نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ كما فرَّقتم أنتم، فَضَلَلْتُم، وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُسْلِمُونَ أي: منقادون لأحكامه الظاهرة والباطنة، أو مخلصون في أعمالنا كلها، وقدَّم المنزل علينا على المنزل على غيرنا، لأنه عيار عليه ومُعَرَّفٌ به. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-84-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-84-5","r":"q3-84","title":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God","text":"الإشارة: ينبغي للفقير أن يبالغ في تعظيم شيخه، ويسوغ له التغالي في شأنه ما لم يخرجه عن طَوْر البشر، وما لم يؤد ذلك إلى إسقاط حُرمة غيره من الأولياء بالتنقيص أو غيره، فحرمة الأولياء كحرمة الأنبياء، فمن فرق بينهم حُرِم بركة جميعهم. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-84-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-84-6","r":"q3-84","title":"3:84 · Faith in all the prophets and respect for the friends of God","text":"ثم إن ملة الإسلام التي جاء بها نبينا- عليه الصلاة والسلام- هى التي أحرزت هذا الاعتقاد الصحيح، فكل من خرج عنها فقد ضل عن الحق الصريح، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-84-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-84-s1","r":"q3-84","title":"Revelation “upon” and “to” its recipients","text":"I say: unzila ( أُنزل ), “was sent down,” takes ilā because revelation reaches the messengers, and takes ʿalā because it comes from above, with the sense of being over them. Some distinguish the use of ʿalā here from ilā in al-Baqara [2:136]: here the address is specifically to the Messenger, and revelation was sent down upon him directly; there the address is to the Muslims, and revelation was directed to them through an intermediary, not sent down directly upon them. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-84-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-84-s2","r":"q3-84","title":"Acknowledging revelation without selective rejection","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Say,” Muḥammad, to the People of the Book who distinguish between messengers in their belief: as for us, we believe in what was sent down upon us and in what was sent down upon all the prophets and messengers. “We make no distinction between any of them,” as you have distinguished and so gone astray. “To Him we submit”: yield to His outward and inward ordinances; or, devote all our actions sincerely to Him. What was sent down upon us is placed before what was sent down upon others because it is the criterion by which the latter is measured and the means by which it is made known. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-84-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-84-s3","r":"q3-84","title":"Veneration without denigrating other saints","text":"The spiritually poor person should greatly venerate his shaykh. He may go far in esteeming him, so long as he does not raise him beyond the human condition or thereby violate the honour of other friends of God through disparagement or anything else. The inviolability of the friends of God is like that of the prophets: whoever discriminates between them is deprived of the blessing of them all. Success comes through God.","anchor":"en-q3-84-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-84-s4","r":"q3-84","title":"","text":"The Islamic religious way brought by our Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is the one that has secured this sound belief. Whoever departs from it has strayed from manifest truth, as the Real Most High indicates, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-84-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-85-86","r":"q3-85-86","title":"3:85–86 · Turning from recognized truth and the corruption of the primordial disposition","text":"3:85–86 · Turning from recognized truth and the corruption of the primordial disposition 3:85–86","anchor":"unit-q3-85-86"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-85-86-1","r":"q3-85-86","title":"3:85–86 · Turning from recognized truth and the corruption of the primordial disposition","text":"وَمَنْ يَبْتَغِ غَيْرَ الْإِسْلامِ دِيناً فَلَنْ يُقْبَلَ مِنْهُ وَهُوَ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنَ الْخاسِرِينَ (85) كَيْفَ يَهْدِي اللَّهُ قَوْماً كَفَرُوا بَعْدَ إِيمانِهِمْ وَشَهِدُوا أَنَّ الرَّسُولَ حَقٌّ وَجاءَهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ وَاللَّهُ لا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ (86)","anchor":"ar-q3-85-86-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-85-86-2","r":"q3-85-86","title":"3:85–86 · Turning from recognized truth and the corruption of the primordial disposition","text":"قلت: (وشهدوا) : عطف على ما في (إيمانهم) من معنى الفعل، والتقدير: بعد أن آمنوا وشهدوا.","anchor":"ar-q3-85-86-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-85-86-3","r":"q3-85-86","title":"3:85–86 · Turning from recognized truth and the corruption of the primordial disposition","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لرجال من الأنصار ارتدوا عن الإسلام ولحقوا بمكة، منهم الحارث بن سويد الأنصاري: وَمَنْ يطلب غَيْرَ الْإِسْلامِ دِيناً يتدين به فَلَنْ يُقْبَلَ مِنْهُ أبداً، وَهُوَ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنَ الْخاسِرِينَ لأنه أبطل الفطرة السليمة التي فطر الناس عليها، واستبدلها بالتقليد الرديء، بعد أن عاين سواطع البرهان، وشهدت نفسه بالحق والبيان، ولذلك وقع التعجب والاستبعاد من هدايته فقال: كَيْفَ يَهْدِي اللَّهُ قَوْماً كَفَرُوا بعد أن آمنوا، وَشَهِدُوا أَنَّ الرَّسُولَ حَقٌّ وَجاءَهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ أي: المعجزات الواضحات، فإن الحائد عن الحق بعد ما وضح، منهمك في الضلال، بعيد عن الرشاد، فقد ظلم نفسه وبخسها، وَاللَّهُ لا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ الذين ظلموا أنفسهم بالإخلال بالنظر، ووضعوا الكفر موضع الإيمان، ولعل هذا في قوم مخصوصين سبق لهم الشقاء.","anchor":"ar-q3-85-86-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-85-86-4","r":"q3-85-86","title":"3:85–86 · Turning from recognized truth and the corruption of the primordial disposition","text":"ثم ذكر جزاءهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-85-86-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-85-86-s1","r":"q3-85-86","title":"Coordination with the verbal meaning of a noun","text":"I say: “and they bore witness” ( وشهدوا ) is coordinated with the verbal meaning contained in “their belief” ( إيمانهم ). The reconstructed sense is: after they believed and bore witness.","anchor":"en-q3-85-86-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-85-86-s2","r":"q3-85-86","title":"Rejecting proof after acknowledging it","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, addresses some men of the Helpers who renounced Islam and went to Mecca, including al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd al-Anṣārī: whoever seeks “a religion other than Islam” to profess will never have it accepted from him; “in the Hereafter he will be among the losers.” He has nullified the sound primordial disposition ( الفطرة السليمة ) upon which people were created, exchanging it for corrupt imitation ( التقليد الرديء ), after beholding the blazing proofs and inwardly bearing witness to the truth and its clarity. Thus the question expresses astonishment at, and the remoteness of, his being guided: “How shall God guide a people who disbelieved” after believing, “bore witness that the Messenger is true, and received the clear proofs”—the manifest miracles? One who turns from truth after it becomes clear is immersed in error and far from right guidance. He has wronged and diminished his own soul. “God does not guide the wrongdoing people,” who wrong themselves by defective reflection and put unbelief in the place of faith. Perhaps this concerns a particular people whose wretchedness was already decreed.","anchor":"en-q3-85-86-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-85-86-s3","r":"q3-85-86","title":"","text":"He then mentioned their recompense, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-85-86-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-87-88","r":"q3-87-88","title":"3:87–88 · The consequence of rejection and the opening towards repentance","text":"3:87–88 · The consequence of rejection and the opening towards repentance 3:87–88","anchor":"unit-q3-87-88"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-87-88-1","r":"q3-87-88","title":"3:87–88 · The consequence of rejection and the opening towards repentance","text":"أُولئِكَ جَزاؤُهُمْ أَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ لَعْنَةَ اللَّهِ وَالْمَلائِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ أَجْمَعِينَ (87) خالِدِينَ فِيها لا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذابُ وَلا هُمْ يُنْظَرُونَ (88)","anchor":"ar-q3-87-88-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-87-88-2","r":"q3-87-88","title":"3:87–88 · The consequence of rejection and the opening towards repentance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أُولئِكَ المرتدون عن الإسلام- جَزاؤُهُمْ: أن تلعنهم الملائكة والناسُ أجمعون، مؤمنُهم وكافرهم، لأن الكافر يلعنُ من ترك دين الحق، وإنْ كان لا يشعر بمن هو على الحقّ. خالِدِينَ في اللعنة، أو في النار، لدلالة السياق عليها، أو في العقوبة. لا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذابُ ساعة، ولا هم يُمهلون عنها لحظة.","anchor":"ar-q3-87-88-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-87-88-3","r":"q3-87-88","title":"3:87–88 · The consequence of rejection and the opening towards repentance","text":"ثم إنَّ الحارث نَدِم، وأرسل إلى قومه أن اسألوا الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم، هل لي من توبة؟ فنزل قوله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-87-88-3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-87-88-s1","r":"q3-87-88","title":"The referent of “abiding therein”","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Their”—those who have renounced Islam—“recompense” is that the angels and all people curse them, believers and unbelievers alike. For the unbeliever curses whoever abandons the true religion, even if he does not recognize who actually follows the truth. They abide in the curse; or in the Fire, which the context indicates; or in the punishment. Their punishment is not lightened for an hour, nor are they given a moment’s respite from it.","anchor":"en-q3-87-88-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-87-88-s2","r":"q3-87-88","title":"","text":"Then al-Ḥārith regretted what he had done and sent to his people, asking them to ask the Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, whether repentance was open to him. Thereupon the following words of God Most High were revealed:","anchor":"en-q3-87-88-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-89","r":"q3-89","title":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship","text":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship 3:89","anchor":"unit-q3-89"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-89-1","r":"q3-89","title":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship","text":"إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ تابُوا مِنْ بَعْدِ ذلِكَ وَأَصْلَحُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (89)","anchor":"ar-q3-89-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-89-2","r":"q3-89","title":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إلا مَن تابَ من بعد الردة، فأسلم وأصلح ما أفسد، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ له فيما فعل، رَحِيمٌ به حيث تاب.","anchor":"ar-q3-89-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-89-3","r":"q3-89","title":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship","text":"ولمّا نزلت الآية حملها إليه رجلٌ من قومه وقرأها عليه، فقال الحارث: إنك والله فيما علمت لصدوق، وإن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم لأصدق منك، وإن الله- تعالى- لأصدق الثلاثة، فرجع الحارث إلى المدينة، فأسلم وحَسُن إسلامُه.","anchor":"ar-q3-89-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-89-4","r":"q3-89","title":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن ابتغى الخصوصية من غير أهلها، أو ادعاها ولم يأخذْها من معدنها، فلن تُقبل منه، وهو عند القوم من الخاسرين في طريق الخصوص، فكل مَن لا شيخ له في هذا الشأن فهو لقيط، لا أب له، دعي، لا نسب له.","anchor":"ar-q3-89-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-89-5","r":"q3-89","title":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship","text":"والمراد بأهلها: العارفون بالله، أهلُ الفناء والبقاء، أهل الجذب والسلوك، أهل السكر والصحو، الذين شربوا الخمر فسكروا ثم صحوا وتكملوا، فمعدنُ الخصوصية عند هؤلاء، فكل من لم يصحبهم ولم يشرب من خمرتهم، لا يُقتدى به، ولو بلغ من الكرامة ما بلغ، وأخسر من هذا مِنْ صحب أهل هذه الخمرة، وشهد بأن طريقهم حق، ثم رجع عنها، فهذا مغبون ملعون عند كافة الخلق، أي: مطرود عن شهود الحق، إلا مَن تاب ورجع إلى صحبتهم والأدب معهم، فإن الله غفور رحيم.","anchor":"ar-q3-89-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-89-6","r":"q3-89","title":"3:89 · Repentance, spiritual lineage and the return to companionship","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى من ارتدّ وبقي على كفره، حتى مات، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-89-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-89-s1","r":"q3-89","title":"Repentance joined to repair","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: except one who repents after renunciation, submits to God and repairs what he has corrupted. God forgives what he has done and has mercy upon him when he repents. When the verse was revealed, a man from al-Ḥārith’s people carried it to him and recited it. Al-Ḥārith said: “By God, I have known you to speak truth. The Prophet is more truthful than you, and God Most High is the most truthful of the three.” Al-Ḥārith returned to Medina, embraced Islam and became a good Muslim.","anchor":"en-q3-89-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-89-s2","r":"q3-89","title":"The source of spiritual distinction and the possibility of returning","text":"Whoever seeks special spiritual distinction ( الخصوصية ) from those who do not possess it, or claims it without receiving it from its source, will not have it accepted from him. Among the Folk he is one of the losers in the special path. Whoever has no shaykh in this matter is a foundling without a father, a pretender without a lineage. [XIV-N048] Those who possess it are the knowers of God: the people of effacement and subsistence ( الفناء والبقاء ), attraction and wayfaring ( الجذب والسلوك ), intoxication and sobriety ( السكر والصحو ), who drank the wine and became intoxicated, then returned to sobriety and attained completion. With them is the source of special spiritual distinction. Whoever has not accompanied them or drunk of their wine is not to be taken as a guide, however far his extraordinary gifts ( الكرامات ) extend. Still more bereft is one who accompanied the people of this wine, bore witness that their path is true, and then turned back from it. He has suffered loss and is accursed among all creatures—that is, driven away from witnessing the Real—except one who repents and returns to their companionship and to right conduct with them. God is forgiving, merciful.","anchor":"en-q3-89-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-89-s3","r":"q3-89","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then mentioned one who renounced belief and remained in unbelief until death, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-89-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-90","r":"q3-90","title":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse","text":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse 3:90","anchor":"unit-q3-90"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-90-1","r":"q3-90","title":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بَعْدَ إِيمانِهِمْ ثُمَّ ازْدادُوا كُفْراً لَنْ تُقْبَلَ تَوْبَتُهُمْ وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الضَّالُّونَ (90)","anchor":"ar-q3-90-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-90-2","r":"q3-90","title":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ ارتدوا عن الإيمان، ثُمَّ ازْدادُوا في الكفر، وقالوا: نتربص بمحمد ريب المنون، لَنْ تُقْبَلَ تَوْبَتُهُمْ أي: لا توبة لهم فتقبل، لأنه سبق لهم الشقاء، أو لأنهم لا يتوبون إلا عند الغرغرة، أو لَنْ تُقْبَلَ تَوْبَتُهُمْ ما داموا على كفرهم. وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الضَّالُّونَ المنهمكون في الضلالة.","anchor":"ar-q3-90-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-90-3","r":"q3-90","title":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse","text":"قيل: نزلت في أصحاب الحارث بن سويد المتقدم، وكانوا أحد عشر رجلاً، لما رجع الحارثُ قالوا: نقيم بمكة على الكفر ما بَدا لنا، فمتى أردنا الرجعة رجعنا، فلما افتتح النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مكة، دخل في الإسلام بعضُهم، فقُبلت توبته، وبقي من بقي على كفره، فنزلت الآية فيهم. وقيل: نزلت في اليهود، كفروا بعيسى بعد إيمانهم بأنبيائهم، ثم ازدادوا كفراً بكفرهم بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، وقيل: نزلت في النصارى كفروا بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلم بعد إيمانهم بعيسى، ثُمَّ ازْدادُوا كُفْراً بإصرارهم عليه. وقيل: نزلت في الفريقين معا، كفروا بنبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم بعد إيمانهم به قبل ظهوره، ثُمَّ ازْدادُوا كُفْراً بتمردهم فيه، وتماديهم على المعاصي. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-90-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-90-4","r":"q3-90","title":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن من دَخَل طريق التربية، وأخذ في تهذيب نفسه وتطهيرها من المساوئ وأوساخ الحس، ثم غلبته القهرية ورجع عنها، فإن تاب قريباً ورجع إليها سهل عليه الرجوع، ورجى نجحه وقبلت توبته، وإن استمر على رجوعه عنها حتى ألفت نفسه البطالة لن ترجى توبته وصار من الضالين، فمثله كآنية، فرَّغت منها لبناً أو عسلاً، وعَمَرْتها بالقطران، فإن بادرت بإهراقه منها قريباً سهل غسلها، وإن أمهلتها حتى صبغ فيها عسر غسلها، وتعذر زوال رائحته منها. [فإن مات على رجعته فلا يحشر في الآخرة مع أهل هذه الرفقة، ولو شفع فيه ألف عارف، بل من كمال المكر به أن يُلقي شَبَهَه في الآخرة على غيره، حتى يتوهم عارفوه من أهل المعرفة أنه هو، فلا يخطر بباله أنه يشفع فيه] . قاله القشيري.","anchor":"ar-q3-90-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-90-5","r":"q3-90","title":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse","text":"قال المحشي: وما ذكره ربما ينظر إلى قضية الخليل مع أبيه، حين يلقاه وعليه القترة، فيريد الشفاعة له، فيمسخ ذيخاً(1) متلطخاً- أي: خنزيراً- فينكره، كما في الحديث الصحيح، فتذكر واعتبر. هـ. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-90-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-90-6","r":"q3-90","title":"3:90 · Persistence in rejection, repentance and the danger of spiritual relapse","text":"ثم ذكر من مات على كفره، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-90-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-90-s1","r":"q3-90","title":"Several explanations of repentance that is not accepted","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: those who turn back from faith and then increase in unbelief, saying, “We shall wait for the turns of fortune to overtake Muḥammad”—“their repentance will not be accepted.” That is, they will have no repentance that could be accepted, because wretchedness has already been decreed for them; or because they repent only when the death-rattle comes; or their repentance will not be accepted for as long as they remain in their unbelief. “Those are the ones who have gone astray”: those who have plunged deeply into error. It is said that this was revealed concerning the companions of al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd mentioned above. They were eleven men. When al-Ḥārith returned, they said: “We shall remain in Mecca in unbelief for as long as it suits us; whenever we wish to return, we shall return.” When the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, conquered Mecca, some of them entered Islam and their repentance was accepted, while the others remained in unbelief. The verse was revealed concerning those who remained. It is also said that it was revealed concerning the Jews: they disbelieved in Jesus after believing in their prophets, then increased in unbelief by disbelieving in Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him. Or concerning the Christians: they disbelieved in Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, after believing in Jesus, then increased in unbelief by persisting in it. Or concerning both groups together: they disbelieved in our Prophet Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, after believing in him before his appearance, then increased in unbelief by obstinately rejecting him and persisting in acts of disobedience. And God Most High knows best. [XIV-N049]","anchor":"en-q3-90-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-90-s2","r":"q3-90","title":"Returning before an acquired habit becomes entrenched","text":"Know that someone may enter the path of spiritual training ( التربية ) and begin to discipline his soul and cleanse it of faults and the stains of sensible attachment ( الحس ), but then overpowering might ( القهرية ) prevails over him and he turns back from it. If he repents promptly and returns to the path, returning will be easy for him; his success may be hoped for, and his repentance will be accepted. But if he persists in abandoning it until his soul has grown accustomed to idleness, his repentance can no longer be hoped for, and he becomes one of those who have gone astray. He resembles a vessel from which you have poured out milk or honey and which you have filled with tar. If you promptly pour out the tar, the vessel is easy to wash. But if you leave it until it has stained the vessel, washing it becomes difficult and removing its smell becomes impracticable. “If he dies having turned back, he will not be gathered in the Hereafter with the people of this companionship, even if a thousand knowers intercede for him. Rather, the consummation of the hidden divine ruse ( المكر ) against him is that his likeness should be cast upon another in the Hereafter, so that those among the people of gnosis who knew him suppose that the other is he. Thus it does not occur to [the knower] to intercede for him.” So said al-Qushayrī. The glossator says: “What he mentions perhaps has in view the Friend’s encounter with his father, when he meets him covered in darkness and desires to intercede for him. His father is transformed into a filth-smeared dhīkh ( ذيخ )—that is, a pig—and he no longer recognizes him, as in the authentic report. So remember and take heed.” End of quotation. [Translator’s note: The gloss “a pig” is the quoted glossator’s; the Cairo editor defines dhīkh here as “a male hyena” (I:379, n. 1).] [XIV-N050] Success is through God, and He is the guide to the even path.","anchor":"en-q3-90-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-90-s3","r":"q3-90","title":"","text":"He then mentioned one who dies in unbelief, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-90-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-91","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness 3:91","anchor":"unit-q3-91"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-91-1","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَماتُوا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ فَلَنْ يُقْبَلَ مِنْ أَحَدِهِمْ مِلْءُ الْأَرْضِ ذَهَباً وَلَوِ افْتَدى بِهِ أُولئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ وَما لَهُمْ مِنْ ناصِرِينَ (91)","anchor":"ar-q3-91-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-91-2","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"قلت: (ذهباً) : تمييز، و (لو افتدى به) : محمول على المعنى، كأنه قيل: فلن يقبل من أحدهم فدية، ولو افتدى بملء الأرض ذهباً، أو عطف على محذوف، أي: فلن يقبل من أحدهم ملءُ الأرض ذهباً لو تقرب به في الدنيا، ولو افتدى به من العذاب في الآخرة. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-91-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-91-3","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا، واستمروا على كفرهم حتى ماتوا، لن يُقْبَلَ منهم فدية، ولو افتدوا بملء الأرض ذهباً، بل يحصل لهم الإياس من رحمة الله، أُولئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ فلا ينفعهم فداء منه ولا شفاعة ولا حميم، وَما لَهُمْ مِنْ ناصِرِينَ ينصروهم من عذاب رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-91-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-91-4","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «يُجَاءُ بالكَافِر يومَ القيامةِ، فيُقال له: أرأيتَ لو كان لكَ ملءُ الأرض ذهباً- أكنْتَ مفتدِياً به؟","anchor":"ar-q3-91-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-91-5","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"فيقولُ: نعم، نعم، فيُقال له: قد سُئلْتَ ما هو أيسرُ من ذلك» . يعني: لا إله إلا الله. ثبتنا الله عليها إلى الممات عالمين بها. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-91-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-91-6","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"الإشارة: كل من كفر بطريق أهل الخصوصية، وحرم نفسه من دخول الحضرة القدوسية، واستمر على كفرانه إلى الممات، فلا شك أنه يحصل له الندم وقد زلّت به القدم، لأنه مات مُصرًا على الكبائر وهو لا يشعر، فإذا حشر مع عوام المسلمين، وسَكَن في رَبضِ الجنة مع أهل اليمين، ثم رأى منازل المقربين في أعلى عليين، ندم وتحسر(1) ، وقد غلبه القدر، فلو اشترى المُقَام معهم بملء الأرض ذهباً ما نفعه ذلك، فيمكث في غمّ الحجاب وعذاب القطيعة هنالك، مقطوع عن شهود الأحباب على نعت الكشف والبيان، ممنوع عن الشهود والعيان. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-91-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-91-7","r":"q3-91","title":"3:91 · The ransom that cannot avail and the lost rank of nearness","text":"ولمّا حكم الحق تعالى بأن الفداء لا ينفع يوم القيامة ذكر أفضل ما يفتدى به العبد فى دار الدنيا لأنه ينفع فيها ذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-91-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-91-s1","r":"q3-91","title":"Specification and an understood ransom","text":"I say: “gold” ( ذهباً ) is an accusative of specification ( تمييز ). “Even if he offers it as a ransom” is construed according to the sense, as though it had been said: “No ransom will be accepted from any one of them, even if he ransoms himself with an earthful of gold.” Alternatively, the clause is coordinated with something omitted: “An earthful of gold will not be accepted from any one of them, whether he offered it to draw near [to God] in this world or offered it as a ransom from punishment in the Hereafter.” So said al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q3-91-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-91-s2","r":"q3-91","title":"No purchase of release after death","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: those who disbelieve and persist in their unbelief until they die will have no ransom accepted from them, even if they ransom themselves with an earthful of gold. Rather, despair of God’s mercy overtakes them. For them is a painful punishment: neither ransom, intercession nor an intimate friend will avail them against it. They have no helpers to defend them against the punishment of the Lord of the worlds. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “The unbeliever will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and asked: ‘Tell Me: had you possessed an earthful of gold, would you have offered it as a ransom?’ He will answer: ‘Yes, yes.’ He will be told: ‘You were asked for something easier than that.’” He means: “There is no god but God.” May God make us steadfast in this word until death, knowing its meaning. Amen. [XIV-N051]","anchor":"en-q3-91-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-91-s3","r":"q3-91","title":"Salvation distinguished from the station of the near ones","text":"Whoever denies the path of those possessed of special spiritual distinction ( أهل الخصوصية ), deprives himself of entry into the Holy Presence ( الحضرة القدوسية ), and persists in that denial until death will undoubtedly feel regret after his footing has slipped. For he has died persisting in grave sins without realizing it. When he is gathered with ordinary Muslims and dwells in the outskirts of Paradise with the people of the right hand, then sees the dwellings of those brought near in the highest ʿIlliyyūn, he regrets and grieves; but the decree has prevailed over him. Were he to purchase a station among them with an earthful of gold, it would not avail him. He remains there in the grief of the veil and the pain of separation, cut off from witnessing the beloved ones in unveiling and clarity ( الكشف والبيان ), deprived of witnessing and direct vision ( الشهود والعيان ). And success is through God. [XIV-N052]","anchor":"en-q3-91-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-91-s4","r":"q3-91","title":"","text":"After the Real Most High had ruled that ransom would not avail on the Day of Resurrection, He mentioned the best thing by which the servant may ransom himself in the abode of this world, where such a ransom does avail. He said:","anchor":"en-q3-91-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-92","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself 3:92","anchor":"unit-q3-92"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-1","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"لَنْ تَنالُوا الْبِرَّ حَتَّى تُنْفِقُوا مِمَّا تُحِبُّونَ وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ شَيْءٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ (92)","anchor":"ar-q3-92-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-2","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"قلت: البرّ: كمال الطاعة.","anchor":"ar-q3-92-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-3","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لَنْ تَنالُوا كمال الطاعة والتقرب حَتَّى تُنْفِقُوا مِمَّا تُحِبُّونَ، أو: لن تنالوا برَّ الله، الذي هو الرضى والرضوان، حَتَّى تُنْفِقُوا بعض ما تُحِبُّونَ من المال وغيره، كبذل الجاه في معاونة الناس، إن صحبه الإخلاص، وكبذل البدن فى طاعة الله، وكبذل المهج في سبيل الله. ولمّا نزلت الآية","anchor":"ar-q3-92-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-4","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"جاء أبو طلحة فقال: يا رسول الله، إن أحب أموالي إِليَّ بَيْرُحاء- وهو بستان كان خلف المسجد النبوي- وهو صدقة لله، أرجو برّها وذخرها، فقال له- عليه الصلاة والسلام- «بَخٍ بَخٍ ذَلَكَ مَالٌ رَابحٌ- أو رائح- وَإِنِّي أَرَى أَنْ تَجْعَلَهَا في الأَقْرَبينَ» . فقسمها أبو طلحة في أقاربه.","anchor":"ar-q3-92-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-5","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"وجاء زيدٌ بنُ حَارِثَةَ بفرسٍ كان يُحبها، فقال: هذه في سبيل الله، فحمل عليها رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أسامة ولده، فقال زيد: إنما أردت أن أتصدق بها، فقال- عليه الصلاة السلام-: «إنَّ اللَّهَ تعالى قَدْ قَبِلَهَا» . فدلّ ذلك على أن الصدقة على الأقارب أفضل. وأعتقت امرأةٌ جارية لا تملك غيرها، كانت تحبها، واشترطت عليها أن تقيم معها، فلما عُتِقَتْ، ذهبت، فقال لها عليه الصلاة والسلام: «دعيها فقد حجَبْتِك عن النار» .","anchor":"ar-q3-92-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-6","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"وأمر عمر بن الخطاب بشراء جارية من سبي العراق، فلما جيء بها، ورآها عمرُ أعجبْته غايةً، فقال: إن الله تعالى يقول: لَنْ تَنالُوا الْبِرَّ حَتَّى تُنْفِقُوا مِمَّا تُحِبُّونَ، فأعتقها. وذكر ابن عمر هذه الآية، فلم يجد عنده أحبَّ من جارية كانت عنده، يطؤها فأعتقها، وقال: لولا أني لا أعود في شيء جعلته لله لنكحتها. وكان الربيع يعطي للسائل إذا وقف في بابه السكر، فإذا قيل له في ذلك، قال: إن الربيع يحب السكر.","anchor":"ar-q3-92-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-7","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"ثم إن الله- تعالى- يقبل الصدقة من المحبوب أو غيره، ولذلك قال: وَما تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ شَيْءٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ فيجازيكم بحسبه.","anchor":"ar-q3-92-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-8","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"الإشارة: ليس للفقير شيء أحبّ إليه من نفسه التي بين جنبيه، بل عند جميع الناس، فمن بذل روحه في مرضاة الله نال رضوان الله ومعرفته، وهو غاية البر، فمن أذل نفسه لله أعزه الله، ومن أفقر نفسه لله أغناه الله، ومن تواضع لله رفعه، فبذل النفس لله هو تقديمها لشيخ التربية يفعل بها ما يشاء، فكل ما يشير به إليه بادر إليه بلا تردد، فمن فعل ذلك فقد نال غاية البر، وأنفق غاية ما يُحب، وكل من بذل نفسه بذل غيرها بالأحرى، إذ ليس أعز منها، وفي ذلك يقول ابن الفارض رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q3-92-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-9","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"مالى سِوَى رُوحِي، وباذل نَفْسه(1) ... في حُبّ من يَهْوَاهُ ليس بُمُسْرِفِ","anchor":"ar-q3-92-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-10","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"فَلَئِنْ رَضِيتَ بها فقد أسْعَفْتَني ... يا خَيْبَةَ الْمَسْعَى إذا لم تُسْعِفِ","anchor":"ar-q3-92-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-11","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"وقال الشيخ أبو عبد الله القرشي: حقيقة المحبة أن تهب كُلَّكَ لمن أحببته، حتى لا يبقى لك منك شيء. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-92-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-12","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"وقال الجنيد رضي الله عنه: لن تنالوا محبة الله حتى تسخُوا بأنفسكم لله. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-92-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-92-13","r":"q3-92","title":"3:92 · Spending what one loves: property, service and the gift of oneself","text":"ولما قال عليه الصلاة والسلام لليهود: «أنا على ملة إبراهيم» . - كما تقدم- قالوا: كيف تكون على ملة إبراهيم، وأنت تأكل لحوم الإبل وألبانها؟، وكان ذلك حراما على إبراهيم، فأنزل الله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-92-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-92-s1","r":"q3-92","title":"The meaning of birr","text":"I say: righteousness ( البرّ ) is the perfection of obedience.","anchor":"en-q3-92-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-92-s2","r":"q3-92","title":"Wealth, influence, bodily service and life itself","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: you will not attain perfection in obedience and drawing near until you spend of what you love. Or: you will not attain God’s goodness ( برّ الله ), namely His approval and good pleasure ( الرضى والرضوان ), until you spend some of what you love, whether wealth or something else. This includes giving the benefit of one’s influence to help people, provided it is accompanied by sincerity ( الإخلاص ); giving one’s bodily effort in obedience to God; and giving one’s very life in God’s path. When the verse was revealed, Abū Ṭalḥa came and said: “Messenger of God, the property dearest to me is Bayruḥāʾ”—a garden behind the Prophet’s mosque—“and it is a charitable gift for God. I hope for its goodness and its stored reward.” He, blessings and peace be upon him, replied: “Excellent, excellent! That is a profitable property”— rābiḥ ( رابح ), or rāʾiḥ ( رائح ), literally “going forth,” in the other wording—“and I consider that you should give it to your near relatives.” Abū Ṭalḥa therefore divided it among his relatives. [XIV-N053] Zayd ibn Ḥāritha brought a horse that he loved and said: “This is for God’s path.” The Messenger of God, blessings and peace be upon him, gave it to Zayd’s son Usāma to ride. Zayd said: “I only intended to give it in charity.” He, blessings and peace be upon him, replied: “God Most High has accepted it.” This indicates that charity to relatives is preferable. A woman freed an enslaved woman whom she loved and who was her only possession, on condition that she should remain with her. Once freed, the woman departed. He, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “Let her go: she has screened you from the Fire.” ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb ordered that an enslaved woman from among the captives of Iraq be purchased. When she was brought to him and he saw her, he found her exceedingly pleasing. He said: “God Most High says: ‘You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love,’” and he freed her. Ibn ʿUmar recalled this verse and found nothing he possessed dearer to him than an enslaved woman with whom he had sexual relations. He freed her and said: “Were it not that I do not take back anything I have given for God, I would marry her.” Whenever a beggar stood at al-Rabīʿ’s door, he would give him sugar. When questioned about this, he said: “Al-Rabīʿ loves sugar.” [XIV-N054] God Most High nevertheless accepts charity whether it consists of something loved or something else. Hence He says: “Whatever you spend, God knows it,” and He recompenses you accordingly.","anchor":"en-q3-92-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-92-s3","r":"q3-92","title":"The self as the dearest gift","text":"The spiritual wayfarer ( الفقير ) possesses nothing dearer to him than the self within him; indeed, this is true of all people. Whoever gives his spirit in seeking God’s pleasure attains God’s good pleasure and knowledge of Him, which is the utmost righteousness. Whoever humbles his self for God is ennobled by God; whoever makes his self poor for God is enriched by God; and whoever humbles himself before God is raised by Him. Giving the self to God means presenting it to a shaykh of spiritual training ( شيخ التربية ), who does with it what he wills. Whatever he directs the disciple to do, the disciple hastens to do without hesitation. Whoever does this has attained the utmost righteousness and spent the dearest thing he loves. Whoever gives his self will all the more readily give everything else, for nothing is dearer than it. [XIV-N055] Concerning this, Ibn al-Fāriḍ, may God be pleased with him, says: I have nothing but my spirit; one who gives himself for love of his beloved is no squanderer. If you are pleased with it, you have granted my desire; how fruitless the striving if you do not grant it! Shaykh Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Qurashī said: “The reality of love is to give your entire being to the one you love, until nothing of you remains for you.” End of quotation. Al-Junayd, may God be pleased with him, said: “You will not attain the love of God until you give yourselves generously to God.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q3-92-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-92-s4","r":"q3-92","title":"","text":"When he, blessings and peace be upon him, told the Jews, “I follow the religious way of Abraham,” as stated above, they said: “How can you follow the way of Abraham when you consume camels’ flesh and milk, although these were forbidden to Abraham?” Thereupon God Most High revealed:","anchor":"en-q3-92-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-93-95","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire 3:93–95","anchor":"unit-q3-93-95"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-1","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"كُلُّ الطَّعامِ كانَ حِلاًّ لِبَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ إِلاَّ ما حَرَّمَ إِسْرائِيلُ عَلى نَفْسِهِ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ تُنَزَّلَ التَّوْراةُ قُلْ فَأْتُوا بِالتَّوْراةِ فَاتْلُوها إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (93) فَمَنِ افْتَرى عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ مِنْ بَعْدِ ذلِكَ فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ (94) قُلْ صَدَقَ اللَّهُ فَاتَّبِعُوا مِلَّةَ إِبْراهِيمَ حَنِيفاً وَما كانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ (95)","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-2","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"قلت: (إسرائيل) : هو يعقوب عليه السلام.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-3","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: كُلُّ الطَّعامِ كانَ حلالاً على بني إسرائيل، كما كان حلالاً على الأنبياء كلهم، إِلَّا ما حَرَّمَ إِسْرائِيلُ أي: يعقوب، عَلى نَفْسِهِ، كلحوم الإبل وألبانها، قيل: كان به عرق النسا(1) ، فنذر:","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-4","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"إن شفاه الله لم يأكل أحب الطعام إليه، وكان ذلك أحب الطعام إليه. وقيل: فعل ذلك للتداوي بإشارة الأطباء، فترك ذلك بنوه ولم يحرم عليهم في التوراة، وإنما هو شيء حرموه على أنفسهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-5","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"فالطعام كله كان حلالاً على بني إسرائيل وعلى الأنبياء كلهم قبل نزول التوراة، فلما نزلت التوراة حرم الله عليهم أشياء من الطيبات لظلمهم وبغيهم، فإن ادعوا أن لحوم الإبل كانت حراماً على إبراهيم، وأن كل ما حرم عليهم كان حراماً على إبراهيم وعلى الأنبياء قبله، فقل لهم: كذبتم فَأْتُوا بِالتَّوْراةِ فَاتْلُوها هل تجدون ذلك فيها؟ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في قولكم: إنَّ كل شيء حرم عليكم كان حراماً على إبراهيم. رُوِيَ: أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- لما قال لهم ذلك بهتوا، ولم يجسروا أن يأتوا بالتوراة، فتبين افتراؤهم على الله فَمَنِ افْتَرى عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-6","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"بزعمه أن الله حرَّم لحوم الإبل وألبانها قبل نزول التوراة، مِنْ بَعْدِ ذلِكَ","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-7","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"البيان وإلزامهم الحجة، فَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الظَّالِمُونَ","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-8","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"المكابرون بالباطل بعد ما وضَح الحق.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-9","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"قُلْ لهم يا محمد: صَدَقَ اللَّهُ فيما أنزل، وكذبتم فيما قلتم، فتبين أن ملة إبراهيم هي الإسلام الذي جاء به محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم فأسلموا، واتبعوا مِلَّةَ إِبْراهِيمَ حَنِيفاً، فإن ملة الإسلام موافقة لملة إبراهيم، أو عينُها، فادخلوا فيه وتخلصوا من اليهودية التي اضطرتكم إلى التحريف والمكابرة، وألزمَتْكُم تحريمَ طيباتٍ أحلها الله لإبراهيم ومن تبعه، وقد خالفتم التوراة التي زعمتم أنكم متمسكون بها، وأشركتم مع الله عزيراً وغيره، وقد كان إبراهيم حنيفاً مسلماً وَما كانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-10","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"قال البيضاوي: فيه إشارة إلى أن اتَّبَاعَهُ- أي: إبراهيم- واجبٌ في التوحيد الصرف والاستقامةِ في الدين، والتجنب عن الإفراط والتفريط، وتعريض بشرك اليهود. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-11","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"الإشارة: إذا تحقق للفقير الإخلاص، وحصل على التوحيد الخاص، كان الطعام كله حلالاً له، لأنه يأخذه بالله، ويتناوله من يد الله ويدفعه لله، مع موافقة الشريعة، ولم يغض من أنوار الطريقة بحيث لا يصحبه شرهٌ ولا طمعٌ. وكان عبد الله بن عمر يقول: كُلْ ما شئت، والبس ما شئت، ما أخطأتك خصلتان: سرف أو مخيلة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-12","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"وإنما امتنعت العباد والزهَّادُ من تناول الشهوات المباحات خوفاً على أنفسهم أن تجمح بهم إلى تناول أسبابهما، فتعطلهم عن العبادة، وكذلك المريدون السائرون، ينبغي لهم التقلل من تناولها لئلا يتعلق قلبهم بشيء منها، فتعطلهم عن السير، وأما الواصلون العارفون، فقد تحقق فناؤهم وبقاؤهم، فهم يأخذون بالله من يد الله، كما تقدم.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-13","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"والحاصل: أن النفس ما دامت لم تُسلم ولم تنقد إلى مشاهدة ربها، وجب جهادها ومخالفتها، فإذا أسلمت وانقادت إلى ربها، وجب الصلح معها وموافقتها فيما يتجلى فيها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-93-95-14","r":"q3-93-95","title":"3:93–95 · Israel’s food prohibition, Abraham’s religious way and the discipline of desire","text":"ولمّا كانت اليهود لا تحجُّ بيت الله الحرام، الذي بناه خليل الله إبراهيم عليه السلام، مع زعمهم أنهم على ملته، ردَّ الله تعالى عليهم بقوله: إِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيْتٍ ... الخ، وقيل: تفاخر المسلمون واليهود، فقالت اليهود: بيت المقدس أفضل لأنه مهاجر الأنبياء، وقال المسلمون: الكعبة أفضل لأنه أول بيت وضع في الأرض، أنزل الله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-93-95-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-93-95-s1","r":"q3-93-95","title":"Israel is Jacob","text":"I say: “Israel” ( إسرائيل ) is Jacob, peace be upon him.","anchor":"en-q3-93-95-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-93-95-s2","r":"q3-93-95","title":"A personal abstention is not an original universal prohibition","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “All food was lawful to the Children of Israel,” just as it was lawful to all the prophets, “except what Israel”—that is, Jacob—“forbade himself,” such as camel meat and its milk. It is said that he suffered from sciatica ( عرق النسا ) and vowed that, if God healed him, he would no longer eat the food he loved most; camel meat and milk were dearest to him. It is also said that he abstained from them as a treatment at the physicians’ direction. His children continued to abstain, although those foods were not forbidden to them in the Torah: this was something they had forbidden themselves. [XIV-N056] Thus all kinds of food had been lawful to the Children of Israel, as to all prophets, before the Torah was sent down. When the Torah came down, God prohibited certain good things to them because of their wrongdoing and oppression. If, therefore, they claim that camel meat was forbidden to Abraham, and that everything later forbidden to them had already been forbidden to Abraham and the prophets before him, say to them: “You have lied. Bring the Torah and recite it.” Do you find such a prohibition there? Do so “if you are truthful” in claiming that everything forbidden to you was also forbidden to Abraham. It is related that when the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, challenged them in this way they were confounded and dared not produce the Torah, whereupon their fabrication against God became manifest. “Whoever fabricates a lie against God” by alleging that God had forbidden camel meat and milk before the Torah was sent down, “after that”—after this explanation and the argument that has been brought home to them—“it is they who are the wrongdoers,” stubbornly maintaining falsehood after the truth has become clear. [XIV-N057] Say to them, O Muḥammad: “God has spoken the truth” in what He has revealed, and you have lied in what you have asserted. It has thus become clear that Abraham’s religious way ( ملة إبراهيم ) is the submission ( الإسلام ) brought by Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him. Submit, then, and follow “the religious way of Abraham, inclining to the truth ( حنيفاً ).” The religious way of Islam agrees with Abraham’s way—or is that way itself. Enter it, and be rid of the Judaism which has led you into alteration and obstinate contention and has obliged you to prohibit good things God made lawful to Abraham and those who followed him. You have departed from the very Torah to which you profess adherence and associated Ezra and others with God, whereas Abraham was one who inclined to the truth, submitted to God, “and was not one of those who associate others with God.” Al-Bayḍāwī says: In this is an indication that following Abraham is obligatory in pure affirmation of divine unity ( التوحيد الصرف ), uprightness in religion, and avoidance of excess and deficiency; it also contains an indirect censure of Jewish associationism. End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q3-93-95-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-93-95-s3","r":"q3-93-95","title":"Permission, watchfulness and the differing states of the wayfarer and the knower","text":"When the spiritual poor one ( الفقير ) has attained sincerity ( الإخلاص ) and realized the particular affirmation of unity ( التوحيد الخاص ), all food becomes lawful to him, because he receives it through God, takes it from the hand of God, and expends it for God, while remaining in conformity with the revealed Law ( الشريعة ). His lights of the spiritual path ( الطريقة ) are not diminished; greed and covetousness do not accompany him. ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: “Eat what you wish and wear what you wish, so long as two things avoid you: extravagance ( سرف ) and vainglory ( مخيلة ).” Worshippers and ascetics refrained from permissible enjoyments because they feared that their souls would carry them into pursuing the means of those enjoyments and so interrupt their worship. Likewise, beginners travelling the path ( المريدون السائرون ) ought to take little of them, lest their hearts become attached to anything therein and thus be impeded in their journeying ( السير ). Those who have arrived and know God ( الواصلون العارفون ), however, have realized their effacement and subsistence ( الفناء والبقاء ); they take through God, from God’s hand, as stated above. In sum: so long as the soul has not submitted and yielded to the witnessing of its Lord ( مشاهدة ربها ), it must be struggled against and opposed. Once it has submitted and yielded to its Lord, reconciliation with it is required, and one must agree with it in what becomes manifest within it ( فيما يتجلى فيها ). And God Most High knows best. [XIV-N058]","anchor":"en-q3-93-95-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-93-95-s4","r":"q3-93-95","title":"","text":"Since the Jews did not perform pilgrimage to God’s Sacred House, built by Abraham the Friend of God, despite claiming to follow his religious way, God refuted them by saying, “Truly the first House ...” It is also said that the Muslims and the Jews disputed which sanctuary was superior. The Jews said that Jerusalem was superior because it was a place to which prophets migrated; the Muslims said that the Kaʿba was superior because it was the first House placed upon the earth. God Most High revealed:","anchor":"en-q3-93-95-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-96-97","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary 3:96–97","anchor":"unit-q3-96-97"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-1","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"إِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيْتٍ وُضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِي بِبَكَّةَ مُبارَكاً وَهُدىً لِلْعالَمِينَ (96) فِيهِ آياتٌ بَيِّناتٌ مَقامُ إِبْراهِيمَ وَمَنْ دَخَلَهُ كانَ آمِناً وَلِلَّهِ عَلَى النَّاسِ حَجُّ الْبَيْتِ مَنِ اسْتَطاعَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيلاً وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عَنِ الْعالَمِينَ (97)","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-2","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"قلت: (بكة) : لغة في مكة، والعرب تعاقب بين الباء والميم، تقول: ضربة لازم ولازب، وأغبَطَتْ عليه الحُمِّى وأغْمَطَتْ، وقيل: (مكة) بالميم: اسم للبلد كله، وبكة: اسم لموضع البيت، سميت بذلك لأنها تبك أعناق الجبابرة- أي: تدقها- فما قصدها جبّار قط بسوء إلا قصمه الله. و (مباركاً) : حال من الضمير في المجرور، والعامل فيه الاستقرار، أي: الذي استقر ببكة مباركاً، و (مقام إبراهيم) : مبتدأ، والخبر محذوف، أي: منها مقام إبراهيم، أو بدل من (آيات) ، بدل البعض من الكل، أو عطف بيان، على أن المراد بالآيات: أثر القدم في الصخرة الصّماء، وغوصها فيها إلى الكعبين، وتخصيصُها بهذه المزيَّة من بين الصخور، وإبقاؤه دون سائر آثار الأنبياء، وحفظه مع كثرة أعدائه ألوف سنة، فكان مقام إبراهيم، وإن كان مفرداً، في قوة الجمع، ويدل عليه أنه قرئ (آية) :","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-3","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"بالتوحيد.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-4","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"وقيل: (الآيات) : مقام إبراهيم، وأمْنُ من دخله، فعلى هذا يكون: (ومن دخله) ، عطفاً على (مقام) ، وعلى الأول: استئنافاً. و (حج البيت) مبتدأ، و (لله) : خبر، والفتح لغة الحجاز، والكسر لغة نجد، و (من استطاع) : بدل من (الناس) ، وقيل: فاعل.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-5","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيْتٍ وُضِعَ في الأرض لِلنَّاسِ للذي استقر بمكة، وبعده بيت المقدس، وبينهما أربعون سنة. بنت الأولَ الملائكة حيالَ البيت المعمور، وأمر اللهُ مَنْ في الأرض أن يطوفوا به كما يطوف أهل السماء بالبيت المعمور، ثم بُنِيَ الثاني. وقيل: بناهما آدم عليه السلام ثم جدَّد الأول إبراهيمُ. حال كونه مُبارَكاً لأنه يتضاعف فيه الحسنات، بكل واحدة مائة ألف، وتكفر فيه السيئات، وتنزل فيه الرحمات، وتتوارد فيه النفحات.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-6","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"فِيهِ آياتٌ بَيِّناتٌ واضحات، منها: الحجر الذي هو مَقامُ إِبْراهِيمَ، وهو الذي قام عليه حين رفع القواعد من البيت، فكان كلما طال البناء ارتفع به الحجر في الهواء، حتى أكمل البناء، وغرقت فيه قدمه كأنه طين، ومنها: أن الطير لا تعلوه، ومنها: إهلاك أهل الفيل وردُّ الجبابرة عنه، ونبع زمزم لهاجر بهمز جبريل عليه السلام، وحفر عبد المطلب لها بعد دُثُورها، وأن ماءها ينفع لما شُرب له، وَمَنْ دَخَلَهُ كانَ آمِناً من العقاب في الدارين لدعاء الخليل: رَبِّ اجْعَلْ هَذَا الْبَلَدَ آمِناً، فكان في الجاهلية كل من فعل جريمةً، ثم لجأ إليه لا يُهَاج(1) ولا يعاقب مادام به، وأما في الإسلام فإن الحرم لا يمنع من الحدود ولا من القصاص. وقال أبو حنيفة:","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-7","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"الحكم باق، وإن من وجب عليه حد أو قصاص فدخل الحرم لا يهاج،، لكن يُضيَّق عليه، فلا يطعم ولا يباع له حتى يخرج.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-8","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «مَنْ مَاتَ في أحد الحرمين بعثه اللهُ من الآمنين» . وقال أيضاً: «مَنْ حَجَّ هذَا البَيْتَ- فَلَمْ يَرْفُثْ، وَلَمْ يَفْسُقْ، خَرَجَ من ذُنُوبِه كَيَوْمِ وَلَدَتْهُ أُمُّه» .","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-9","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"وَلِلَّهِ عَلَى النَّاسِ حِجُّ الْبَيْتِ فرض عين على مَنِ اسْتَطاعَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيلًا بالقدرة على الوصول بصحة البدن، راجلاً أو راكباً مع الزاد المُبلِّغ، والأمن على النفس والمال والدين. وقيل: الاستطاعة: الزاد والراحلة.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-10","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"وَمَنْ تركه، وكَفَرَ به، كاليهود والنصارى، وكل من جحده، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عنه، وعَنِ حجه، وعن جميع الْعالَمِينَ، أو عبر بالكفر عن الترك، تغليظاً كقوله: «مَنْ تَرَكَ الصَّلاةَ فَقَدْ كَفَر» روى أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- لما نزل صدر الآية- جمع أرباب الملل، فخطبهم، وقال: «إن الله كتب عليكم الحج فحجوا» ، فآمنت به ملة واحدة، وكفرت به خمس ملل، فنزل وَمَنْ كَفَرَ ... إلخ.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-11","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"الإشارة: قد وضع الله للناس بيتين: أحدهما حسي، وهو الكعبة، والآخر معنوي، وهو القلب، الذي هو بيت الرب، فما دام بيت القلب خالياً من نور الرب اشتاق إلى حج البيت الحسي، فإذا تعمر البيت بنور ساكنه، صار قبلة لغيره، واستغنى عن الالتفات إلى غير نور ربه، بل صار كعبة تطوف به الواردات والأنوار، وتحفه المعارف والعلوم والأسرار، ثم يصير قطب دائرة الأكوان، وتدور عليه من كل جانب ومكان، فكيف يشتاق هذا إلى الكعبة الحسية(1) ، وقد طافت به دائرة الوفود الكونية؟ ولله در الحلاج رضي الله عنه حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-12","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"يَا لاَئِمِي لا تَلُمْني في هواه فَلَوْ ... عايَنْتَ منه الذي عاينْتَ لم تَلُمِ","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-13","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"للنَّاسِ حجٍّ ولي حجٍّ إلى سَكَنِي ... تُهْدَى الأضَاحِي، وأُهْدِي مُهْجِتِي ودَمِي","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-14","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"يطوفُ بالبيت قومٌ لا بجارحةٍ، ... بالله طافوا فأغنَاهم عن الحَرَمِ(2) .","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-15","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"في هذا البيت آيات واضحات، وهى إشراق شموس المعارف والأنوار، فى فضاء سماء الأرواح والأسرار، وسطوع أنوار قمر التوحيد في أرض التجريد والتفريد، وظهور أنوار نجوم العلم والحِكم، في أفق سماء ارتفاع الهمم، فهذا كان مقام إبراهيم، إمام الموحدين، فمن دخله كان آمناً من الطرد والبعاد إلى يوم الدين، ومن كفر وجوده فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عَنِ العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-16","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"قال في الحاشية في قوله: (ومن دخله كان آمنا) ، قيل: وهكذا من دخل في قلب وليٍّ من أوليائه، فإن قلب العارف حرم المراقبات والمشاهدات. هـ. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-96-97-17","r":"q3-96-97","title":"3:96–97 · Bakkah, the first House, the obligation of pilgrimage and the inner sanctuary","text":"ثم رجع الحقّ تعالى إلى معاتبة أهل الكتاب، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-96-97-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-96-97-s1","r":"q3-96-97","title":"Bakkah, the circumstantial accusative and the Station of Abraham","text":"I say: “Bakkah” ( بكة ) is a dialectal form of “Makkah”; Arabs interchange bāʾ and mīm, as when they say ḍarba lāzim and lāzib for a decisive blow, or aghbaṭat ʿalayhi al-ḥummā and aghmaṭat, concerning a fever. It is also said that “Makkah,” with mīm, names the whole town, whereas “Bakkah” names the location of the House. It was given that name because it “breaks” ( تبك ), that is, crushes, the necks of tyrants: no tyrant has intended it evil without God breaking him. [XIV-N059] “Blessed” ( مباركاً ) is a circumstantial accusative ( حال ) referring to the pronoun in the prepositional expression, with the implied state of being established or located ( الاستقرار ) as its governor ( العامل ): that is, “the one situated in Bakkah, being blessed.” “The Station of Abraham” ( مقام إبراهيم ) may be a subject ( مبتدأ ) whose predicate ( خبر ) is suppressed: “among them is the Station of Abraham.” Or it may be a part-for-whole substitute ( بدل البعض من الكل ) for “signs” ( آيات ), or an explicative apposition ( عطف بيان ), if the signs intend the impression of his foot in the solid rock, its sinking into it as far as the ankles, the rock’s being distinguished from other rocks by this property, the preservation of this impression rather than other prophets’ traces, and its survival for thousands of years despite his many enemies. Thus the Station of Abraham, though singular, has the force of a plural. Supporting this is a variant reading with the singular “a sign” ( آية ). [XIV-N060] It is also said that the “signs” are the Station of Abraham and the security of whoever enters. On this explanation, “whoever enters it” is coordinated with “the Station”; on the former interpretation it begins a new sentence ( استئناف ). “Pilgrimage to the House” ( حج البيت ) is a subject ( مبتدأ ), and “belongs to God” ( لله ) is its predicate ( خبر ). The vowel fatḥa [in ḥajj] is the idiom of the Ḥijāz and kasra [ḥijj] the idiom of Najd. “Whoever is able” ( من استطاع ) is an appositional substitute ( بدل ) for “the people” ( الناس ); it is also said to be the subject/agent ( فاعل ). [XIV-N060]","anchor":"en-q3-96-97-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-96-97-s2","r":"q3-96-97","title":"The Kaʿba, its signs and reported virtues","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Truly the first House” placed upon the earth “for humankind” was the one established at Makkah, followed by the House of Jerusalem, with forty years between them. The angels built the first facing the Inhabited House ( البيت المعمور ), and God commanded the inhabitants of earth to circumambulate it as the dwellers of heaven circumambulate the Inhabited House; then the second was built. It is also said that Adam built both, and that Abraham later renewed the first. It is “blessed,” because good deeds are multiplied there, each one by a hundred thousand; sins are expiated there, mercies descend, and spiritual gifts ( النفحات ) arrive in succession. [Translator’s note: These are explanations and reports transmitted by the commentator, not claims independently established here about construction chronology.] [XIV-N061] “In it are clear signs,” conspicuous proofs, including the stone that is “the Station of Abraham,” upon which Abraham stood while he raised the foundations of the House. Whenever the building grew higher, the stone rose with him into the air until he completed the building, and his foot sank into it as though it were clay. Other signs are said to include birds not passing above it, the destruction of the People of the Elephant, the repelling of tyrants, the emergence of Zamzam for Hagar through Gabriel’s striking it, its later rediscovery by ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib after it had been obscured, and the benefit of its water for whatever purpose it is drunk. [XIV-N061] “Whoever enters it is safe”: from punishment in the two abodes, through the Friend’s prayer, “My Lord, make this land secure” [14:35]. In the pre-Islamic period anyone who committed an offence and then took refuge there was neither attacked nor punished while within it. In Islam, however, the sacred precinct does not bar the prescribed penalties ( الحدود ) or retaliation ( القصاص ). Abū Ḥanīfa holds that the earlier rule remains: if someone liable to a prescribed penalty or retaliation enters the sacred precinct, he is not attacked, but pressure is applied to him—he is not fed or sold provisions—until he goes out. [XIV-N062] The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever dies in one of the two sanctuaries will be raised among those who are safe.” He also said: “Whoever performs pilgrimage to this House and neither commits obscenity nor transgresses comes forth from his sins like the day his mother gave birth to him.” [XIV-N063] “Pilgrimage to the House is a duty owed to God by people”: an individual obligation ( فرض عين ) upon “whoever is able to find a way to it,” meaning able to reach it with a healthy body, on foot or mounted, having the provisions needed to arrive there, and being secure in person, property and religion. Another explanation of ability ( الاستطاعة ) is provisions and a mount. “Whoever” abandons it and “disbelieves” in it—such as Jews, Christians, and anyone who denies its obligation—“God has no need” of that person, his pilgrimage, or any of the worlds; or “disbelief” is used for abandoning it as an intensification, as in the saying: “Whoever abandons prayer has disbelieved.” It is related that when the opening of the verse came down, the Prophet assembled the religious communities and said, “God has prescribed the pilgrimage for you; so perform it.” One community believed him and five denied him; so “whoever disbelieves ...” was revealed. [Translator’s note: The report is cited as a report, without independent authentication.] [XIV-N064]","anchor":"en-q3-96-97-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-96-97-s3","r":"q3-96-97","title":"The physical House and the heart as an inward sanctuary","text":"God has established two houses for humankind. One is sensible ( حسي ), the Kaʿba; the other is intelligible or spiritual ( معنوي ), the heart, which is the House of the Lord ( بيت الرب ). As long as the house of the heart is empty of the Lord’s light, it longs to make pilgrimage to the sensible House. But when the house has been built up with the light of its Indweller, it becomes a direction of orientation ( قبلة ) for others and ceases to turn towards anything other than the light of its Lord. Rather, it becomes a Kaʿba around which spiritual visitations ( الواردات ) and lights make their circumambulations, surrounded by gnoses, sciences and secrets. Then it becomes a pole ( قطب ) of the circle of existing things, around which they turn from every side and place. How could such a person long for the sensible Kaʿba when the circle of cosmic visitors revolves around him? [XIV-N065] How splendidly al-Ḥallāj, may God be pleased with him, put it: O you who blame me, blame me not for love of Him; had you beheld what I beheld, you would not blame. Other people have a pilgrimage, and I a pilgrimage to my Beloved, in whom I find rest: they offer sacrifices, while I offer my life-blood and blood. People circumambulate the House without bodily limb: they circumambulate through God, who makes them free of need for the Sanctuary. [Translator’s note: The printed سكني (sakanī) is retained. “My Beloved, in whom I find rest” draws on the sense of sakan defined by Ibn Fāris as a beloved in whom one finds repose (Maqāyīs al-lugha, root s-k-n, III:88), also attested in Ibn Manẓūr’s Lisān al-ʿArab. All three lines occur together in Ibn ʿArabī’s Muḥāḍarat al-abrār (II:147, electronic texts inspected), following two other verses about the Beloved. Their order there is pilgrimage, circumambulation, then blame; the circumambulation verse reads “through love” (bi-l-ḥubb) where Cairo has “through God” (bi-llāh). That passage gives the poem without an attribution to al-Ḥallāj. It establishes an earlier literary parallel. Al-Shībī’s Sharḥ Dīwān al-Ḥallāj , poem 48, pp. 487–488 (Jamal facsimile inspected), explicitly disputes the attribution: the cited Taqyīd introduction describes recitation from al-Ḥallāj, which does not establish composition. Al-Shībī assembles his seven-line text from several recensions; it is not a single continuous witness. The attribution here therefore remains Ibn ʿAjība’s, with this critical disagreement disclosed. The word also permits an echo of a dwelling or resting place; no Arabic emendation is proposed.] In this inward house are clear signs: the shining of the suns of gnosis and lights in the open heaven of spirits and secrets; the brightness of the moon of divine unity upon the earth of detachment and singleness ( التجريد والتفريد ); and the appearing of the stars of knowledge and wisdom in the horizon of exalted aspirations. This is the station of Abraham, the imam of those who affirm divine unity. Whoever enters it is secure from rejection and remoteness until the Day of Judgment. Whoever denies its existence—God is independent of all the worlds. It is said in the marginal commentary concerning “Whoever enters it is safe”: the same may be said of whoever enters the heart of one of God’s friends ( ولي ): the heart of the knower ( العارف ) is a sanctuary of watchful awareness and witnessing ( المراقبات والمشاهدات ). End of citation. Through God is success, and He is the Guide to the even way.","anchor":"en-q3-96-97-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-96-97-s4","r":"q3-96-97","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then returned to reproaching the People of the Book, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-96-97-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-98-99","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction 3:98–99","anchor":"unit-q3-98-99"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-1","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"قُلْ يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ شَهِيدٌ عَلى ما تَعْمَلُونَ (98) قُلْ يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَصُدُّونَ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ مَنْ آمَنَ تَبْغُونَها عِوَجاً وَأَنْتُمْ شُهَداءُ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ (99)","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-2","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"قلت: (تبغونها) : جملة حالية من الواو، أي: لِمَ تصدون عن السبيل باغين لها عوجاً. والعوج- بالكسر- في الدين والقول والعمل-، وبالفتح- في الجدار والحائط وكل شخص قائم.","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-3","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قُلْ يا محمد في عتابك لليهود: يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ السمعية والعقلية الدالة على صدق نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم فيما يدعوكم إليه من الإسلام؟ وَاللَّهُ شَهِيدٌ عَلى ما تَعْمَلُونَ مطلع على سرها وجهرها، فيجازيكم عليها، فلا ينفعكم التحريفُ ولا الإسرار.","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-4","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لِمَ تَصُدُّونَ عن طريق الله مَنْ آمَنَ بها، وتبع من جاء بها، تَبْغُونَها عِوَجاً أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-5","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"طالبين لها اعوجاجاً، بأن تلبسوا على الناس، وتُوهموا أن فيها عوجاً عن الحق، بزعمكم أن التوراة لا تُنْسخ، وبتغيير صفة الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام، أو بأن تحرشوا بين المسلمين لتختلف كلمتهم، ويختل أمر دينهم، وأنتم شهداء على أنها حق، وأن الصد عنها ضلال، أو: وأنتم عُدول عند أهل ملتكم، يثقون بأقوالكم، ويستشهدونكم في القضايا، وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ فلا بد ان يجازيكم على أعمالكم، فإنه يُمهل ولا يُهمل.","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-6","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"كرَّر الخطاب والاستفهام مرتين مبالغة في التقريع ونفي العذر، وإشعاراً بأن كل واحد من الأمرين مستقبح في نفسه، مستقل باستجلاب العذاب. ولمَّا كان المنكَر عليهم في الآية الأولى: كفرهم، وهم يجهرون به، ختم بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-7","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"وَاللَّهُ شَهِيدٌ عَلى ما تَعْمَلُونَ، ولمَّا كان في هذه الآية: صدهم المؤمنين عن الإسلام، وكانوا يخفونه ويحتالون فيه، قال: وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-8","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"الإشارة: كل من جحد وجود الخصوصية عند أهلها، وصد القاصدين للدخول فيها، استحق هذا العتاب بلا شك ولا ارتياب. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-98-99-9","r":"q3-98-99","title":"3:98–99 · Concealing the way of God and denying the presence of spiritual distinction","text":"ثم حذّر المؤمنين من الاستماع لهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-98-99-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-98-99-s1","r":"q3-98-99","title":"The circumstantial clause and two senses of crookedness","text":"I say: “Seeking to make it crooked” ( تَبْغُونَها ) is a circumstantial clause ( جملة حالية ) describing the state of the subject represented by the plural wāw; that is, “Why do you obstruct the path while seeking crookedness for it?” The noun ʿiwaj ( عِوَج ), with kasra, applies to religion, speech and action, while ʿawaj ( عَوَج ), with fatḥa, applies to a wall, boundary wall or other upright physical object.","anchor":"en-q3-98-99-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-98-99-s2","r":"q3-98-99","title":"Open rejection and concealed obstruction","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: Say, O Muḥammad, in reproaching the Jews, “O People of the Book, why do you disbelieve in God’s signs”—the transmitted and rational signs ( السمعية والعقلية ) that show the truthfulness of His Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, in what he summons you to of Islam? “God is witness to what you do”: He knows its concealed and manifest aspects and will requite you for it. Your alterations and secrecy therefore cannot profit you. “O People of the Book, why do you turn those who believe” in the signs and follow the messenger who brought them “away from God’s path, seeking to make it crooked?” That is, seeking to give the path a distortion: you confuse people and make them imagine that it deviates from the truth by claiming that the Torah cannot be abrogated ( النسخ ), by changing the Messenger’s description, or by stirring up discord among the Muslims so that their word becomes divided and their religious affairs disordered. And “you are witnesses” that this path is true and obstruction of it is error; or you are reputable upright witnesses ( عُدول ) in the eyes of your own community, who trust your testimony and summon you as witnesses in legal cases. “God is not heedless of what you do”: He must surely requite you for your deeds, for He grants respite but does not neglect. The address and question are repeated twice to heighten rebuke, remove excuse and indicate that each offence is reprehensible in itself and independently attracts punishment. Since the action denounced in the first verse is their unbelief, which they openly declare, it closes with “God is witness to what you do.” Since the second denounces the obstruction of believers from Islam, which they concealed and contrived secretly, it concludes with “God is not heedless of what you do.” Al-Bayḍāwī explains it thus. [XIV-N066]","anchor":"en-q3-98-99-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-98-99-s3","r":"q3-98-99","title":"Recognizing the special spiritual realization of one’s contemporaries","text":"Whoever denies the existence of special spiritual distinction ( الخصوصية ) among those who possess it, and obstructs seekers from entering it, undoubtedly merits this reproof. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-98-99-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-98-99-s4","r":"q3-98-99","title":"","text":"He then warned the believers against listening to them, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-98-99-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-100-102","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness 3:100–102","anchor":"unit-q3-100-102"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-1","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تُطِيعُوا فَرِيقاً مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ يَرُدُّوكُمْ بَعْدَ إِيمانِكُمْ كافِرِينَ (100) وَكَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ وَأَنْتُمْ تُتْلى عَلَيْكُمْ آياتُ اللَّهِ وَفِيكُمْ رَسُولُهُ وَمَنْ يَعْتَصِمْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ هُدِيَ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ (101) يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقاتِهِ وَلا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلاَّ وَأَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ (102)","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-2","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا، الخطاب عامٌ، والمراد: نفر من الأوس والخزرج، إِنْ تُطِيعُوا فَرِيقاً مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ، وهو شاسُ بن قيس اليهودي، كان شيخاً كبيراً، وكان عظيمَ الكفر شديد الضغن على المسلمين، مرَّ بنفر من الأوس والخزرج، جلوساً يتحدثون، وكان بينهما عداوة في الجاهلية، فغاظه تآلفهم واجتماعهم، وقال: قد اجتمع ملأ بني قَيْلَة بهذه البلاد، فما لنا معهم قرار، فأمر شاباً من اليهود أن يجلس بينهم ويُذكِّرهم يوم بعاث- وهو يوم حرب كان بينهم في الجاهلية- ويُنشدهم بعض ما قيل فيه، وكان الظفرُ في ذلك اليوم للأوس، ففعل، وتنازع القوم وتفاخروا وتغاضبوا، وقالوا: السلاحَ السلاحَ، واجتمع من القبيلتين خلق عظيم، فتوجه إليهم رسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم وأصحابه، فقال: «أبدعْوَى الجَاهِليةِ وأنا بَيْنَ أَظْهُرِكُمْ، بعدَ إذ أكْرَمَكْم اللهُ بالإسْلام، وقَطَعَ به عَنْكُم أمْرَ الجَاهِلِية، وألْفَ بَينكُم؟» فعلموا أنها نزغة من الشيطان وكيدٌ من عدوهم، فَأَلَقَوا السِّلاحَ، واستغفروا، وعانق بعضهم بعضاً، وانصرفوا مع الرسول- صلوات الله عليه وسلامه- فنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-3","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تُطِيعُوا فَرِيقاً من اليهود يَرُدُّوكُمْ بَعْدَ إِيمانِكُمْ كافِرِينَ يُبيح بعضكم دماء بعض، كما كنتم في الجاهلية. وَكَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ وَأَنْتُمْ تُتْلى عَلَيْكُمْ آياتُ اللَّهِ الدالة على تحريم الدماء والشحناء، وَفِيكُمْ رَسُولُهُ الهادي إلى الصراط المستقيم، وهو إنكار وتعجُّبٌ من كفرهم، بعد اجتماع الأسباب الداعية إلى الإيمان، الصارفة عن الكفران، وإنما خاطبهم الله بنفسه بعد ما أمر الرسولَ بأن يخاطب أهل الكتاب إظهاراً لجلالة قدرهم، وإشعاراً بأنهم الأحقاء بأن يخاطبهم الله ويكلمهم، دون أهل الكتاب لبعدهم عن استحقاق مواجهة الخطاب من الكريم الوهاب. وَمَنْ يَعْتَصِمْ بِاللَّهِ ويتمسك بدينه فَقَدْ هُدِيَ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ لا عوج فيه وأصل الاعتصام: التمنع.","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-4","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"ثم حَضَّ على التقوى الكاملة والدوام على الإسلام، تنفيراً من الاستماع لمن يخرج عنها، فقال: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقاتِهِ، قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «حق تقاته هو أن يُطاعَ فلا يُعْصَى طرفةَ عين، وأن يُذكر فلا يُنسى، وأن يُشكر فلا يُكفر» . ولما نزلت قالوا: يا رسول الله من يقوى على هذا؟ وشق عليهم، فنزلت: فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ، فنسختها. وقال مُقاتل: معناه: (اتقوا الله حق تقاته، فإن لم تستطيعوا فلا تموتن إلا وأنتم مسلمون) . وعن أنس ابن مالك، قال: (لا يتقي الله عبدٌ حق تقاته حتى يُخْزِن من لسانه) ، وقيل:","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-5","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"ليست بمنسوخة لأنَّ مَنْ جَانَبَ ما نهى الله عنه، وفعل من الطاعة ما استطاع، فقد اتقى الله حق تقاته، فمعناها واحد. وسيأتي تحديد ذلك في الإشارة، إن شاء الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-6","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"قال البيضاوي: وقيل: معنى (حق تقاته) : أن يُنزه الطاعة عن الالتفات إليها، وعن توقع المجازاة عليها، وفي هذا الأمر تأكيدٌ للنهي عن طاعة أهل الكتاب، وَلا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنْتُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ أي: لا تكونوا على حالةٍ سوى الإسلام، إلى أن يدرككم الموت. هـ. أماتنا الله على حسن الختام، مع السلامة والعافية على الدوام.","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-7","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"الإشارة: كما نهى الله عن طاعة من يرد عن الإيمان، نهى عن طاعة من يصد عن مقام الإحسان، كائناً ما كان، وكيف يرجع عن مقام التحقيق، وقد ظهرت معالم الطريق لمَن سبقت له العناية والتوفيق!. قال بعضهم:","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-8","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"والله ما رجع مَن رجع إلا من الطريق، وأما من وصل فلا يرجع أبدًا. إذ لا يمكن أن يرجع من عين اليقين إلى علمِ اليقين، أو من اليقين إلى الظن. ومن أراد الثبات على اليقين فليعتصم بحبل الله المتين، وهو صحبة العارفين، فمن اعتصم بهم فقد اعتصم بالله وَمَنْ يَعْتَصِمْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ هُدِيَ إِلى صِراطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ.","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-9","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"ثم خاطب أهل الإحسان فقال: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقاتِهِ بأن تغيبوا عما سواه، ولا تموتن إلا وأنتم منقادون لأحكام الربوبية، قائمون بوظائف العبودية. فهذه الآية خطاب لأهل الإحسان، وفَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ: خطاب لأهل الإسلام والإيمان. أو هذه لأهل التجريد، والثانية لأهل الأسباب، أو هذه لأهل الباطن،","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-10","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"والثانية لأهل الظاهر، فلكل آية أهل ومحل، فلا نسخ ولا تعارض. وقال الشيخ أبو العباس رضي الله عنه: من أراد الجمع بين الآيتين فليتق الله حق تقاته بباطنه، وليتق الله ما استطاع بظاهره. هـ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-100-102-11","r":"q3-100-102","title":"3:100–102 · Communal discord, holding fast to God and the degrees of Godfearingness","text":"ثم حضّ الحق جل جلاله على الاجتماع، ونهى عن الفرقة التي رام العدو منهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-100-102-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-100-102-s1","r":"q3-100-102","title":"An attempt to revive the feud between Aws and Khazraj","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “O you who believe.” The address is general but those intended are a group of the Aws and Khazraj. “If you obey a group of those who were given the Book”—namely Shās ibn Qays the Jew. He was an elderly man deeply entrenched in unbelief and intensely resentful of the Muslims. He passed some men of the Aws and Khazraj sitting together in conversation; there had formerly been enmity between the two clans during the pre-Islamic period ( الجاهلية ). Their affection and gathering angered him. He said: “The leading men of the Banū Qayla have gathered here; if they remain united we shall have no place among them.” He commanded a Jewish youth to sit with them, remind them of the Day of Buʿāth—a battle between them before Islam—and recite some of the verses composed about it. The Aws had prevailed on that day. The youth did as instructed; they began to dispute and boast, then became angry and shouted, “To arms! To arms!” Many from both clans assembled. The Messenger of God, blessings and peace be upon him, went out to them with his companions and said: “Do you call with the call of the Age of Ignorance while I am here among you, after God has honoured you with Islam, cut off from you the affair of ignorance, and brought you together?” They recognized it as an incitement from Satan and a stratagem of their enemy. They threw down their weapons, sought forgiveness, embraced one another, and returned with the Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him. Then the verse was revealed. [Translator’s note: This is the occasion-of-revelation narrative transmitted by Ibn ʿAjība; its historical details require separate assessment.] [XIV-N067] “O you who believe, if you obey a group” of Jews, “they will turn you back into disbelievers after your faith,” making one another’s blood licit again as in the Age of Ignorance. “How could you disbelieve while God’s signs”—which declare bloodshed and rancour forbidden—“are recited to you, and His Messenger is among you,” guiding you to the straight path? This is both repudiation and astonishment at the possibility of unbelief after all the causes inviting them to faith and diverting them from unbelief have been assembled. God now addresses the believers directly, after commanding the Messenger to address the People of the Book, in order to make manifest their exalted worth: they are more deserving that God should address and speak to them, unlike those distant from receiving the Generous Bestower’s direct address. “Whoever holds fast to God,” cleaving to His religion, “has indeed been guided to a straight path” without deviation. The basic sense of holding fast ( الاعتصام ) is taking protection against something ( التمنع ).","anchor":"en-q3-100-102-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-100-102-s2","r":"q3-100-102","title":"“As He should be feared” and the question of abrogation","text":"God then urged perfect Godfearingness ( التقوى الكاملة ) and constancy in submission, discouraging them from listening to anyone who would remove them from these. “O you who believe, be mindful of God as He is truly worthy of being regarded.” The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is reported to have said: “His true due is that He should be obeyed and not disobeyed for the blink of an eye, remembered and not forgotten, thanked and not denied.” When the verse came down, they asked, “Messenger of God, who can bear this?” It was difficult for them; then “Be mindful of God as far as you are able” [64:16] was revealed and abrogated it, according to this explanation. [XIV-N068] Muqātil said its meaning is: “Be mindful of God as He truly deserves; if you cannot, then do not die except as Muslims.” From Anas ibn Mālik it is related: “No servant is mindful of God as He truly deserves until he stores up [restrains] his tongue.” Others say that it is not abrogated: whoever avoids what God has forbidden and performs of obedience whatever he is able has been mindful of God as He truly deserves; the meaning of the two verses is therefore one. We shall explain its exact application in the spiritual allusion, God willing. Al-Bayḍāwī says: It is also said that the meaning of “as He truly deserves” is to purify obedience of looking at one’s obedience and of expecting recompense for it. The command reinforces the prohibition on obeying the People of the Book. “And do not die except while you are Muslims” means: remain in no state but Islam until death overtakes you. End of quotation. May God cause us to die with a good end, in abiding safety and wellbeing.","anchor":"en-q3-100-102-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-100-102-s3","r":"q3-100-102","title":"Holding fast through companionship and the certainty of realization","text":"Just as God forbade obedience to one who turns people back from faith ( الإيمان ), He forbade obedience to anyone who diverts them from the station of spiritual excellence ( مقام الإحسان ), whoever that person might be. How can anyone return from the station of realized certainty ( التحقيق ), once the signs of the path have appeared to one for whom divine care and success were decreed? Someone said: “By God, no one turns back except someone who was still on the road. As for one who has arrived, he never turns back,” for it is impossible to return from the eye of certainty ( عين اليقين ) to the knowledge of certainty ( علم اليقين ), or from certainty to conjecture ( الظن ). Whoever desires permanence in certainty should hold fast to God’s strong cord, which is companionship with the knowers ( صحبة العارفين ). Whoever holds fast to them has held fast to God: “Whoever holds fast to God has indeed been guided to a straight path.” Then He addressed the people of spiritual excellence ( أهل الإحسان ): “O you who believe, be mindful of God as He truly deserves,” by being absent to everything other than Him; “and do not die except while you are Muslims,” yielding to the determinations of Lordship ( أحكام الربوبية ) and fulfilling the functions of servanthood ( وظائف العبودية ). This verse, then, is addressed to the people of iḥsān, while “Be mindful of God as far as you are able” [64:16] is addressed to the people of Islam and faith. Or the former is for the people of detachment ( أهل التجريد ) and the latter for those occupied with secondary causes ( أهل الأسباب ); or the former is for the inward people ( أهل الباطن ) and the latter for the outward people ( أهل الظاهر ). Each verse has its people and its proper place: there is therefore no abrogation ( نسخ ) and no contradiction ( تعارض ). [XIV-N068] Shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās, may God be pleased with him, said: “Whoever wishes to reconcile the two verses should be mindful of God as He truly deserves inwardly ( بباطنه ), and mindful of Him as far as possible outwardly ( بظاهره ).” End of quotation. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q3-100-102-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-100-102-s4","r":"q3-100-102","title":"","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, then urged unity and forbade the division that their enemy had sought among them, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-100-102-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-103","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path 3:103","anchor":"unit-q3-103"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-1","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"وَاعْتَصِمُوا بِحَبْلِ اللَّهِ جَمِيعاً وَلا تَفَرَّقُوا وَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ كُنْتُمْ أَعْداءً فَأَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِكُمْ فَأَصْبَحْتُمْ بِنِعْمَتِهِ إِخْواناً وَكُنْتُمْ عَلى شَفا حُفْرَةٍ مِنَ النَّارِ فَأَنْقَذَكُمْ مِنْها كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ آياتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ (103)","anchor":"ar-q3-103-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-2","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"قلت: أصل الحبل في اللغة: السبب المُوصِّل إلى البغية، سمى به الإيمان أو القرآن لأنه يُوصل إلى السعادة السرمدية، و (شفا حفرة) أي: طرفها، وأصله: (شفو) ، فقلبت ألفاً في المذكر، وحذفت في المؤنث، فقالوا: شفة.","anchor":"ar-q3-103-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-3","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاعْتَصِمُوا أي: تمسكوا يا معشر المسلمين بِحَبْلِ اللَّهِ أي: الإيمان، أو كتاب الله، لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إنَّ هذا القرآن هو حَبْلُ الله المّتِين، وهو النورُ المُبِينُ، والشِّفَاءُ النافِعُ، عِصْمَةٌ لِمَنْ تَمَسَّكَ به ... » . الحديث. حال كونكم جَمِيعاً أي: مجتمعين عليه، وَلا تَفَرَّقُوا تفرقكم الجاهلي، أو لا تفرقوا عن الحق بوقوع الاختلاف بينكم كأهل الكتاب. قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إنَّ بَني إسْرائيلَ افتَرقَتْ على إحدى وسبعين فرقة، وإنَّ أُمَّتِي سَتَفْتَرِقُ على ثِنتَيْنِ وسَبْعِينَ فِرْقَةً، كُلّها في النار إلا واحدة، فقيل: يا رسول الله، ما هذه الواحدة؟ فقبض يده وقال: الجَمَاعَةُ، ثمَّ قرأ: وَاعْتَصِمُوا بِحَبْلِ اللَّهِ جَمِيعاً وَلا تَفَرَّقُوا.","anchor":"ar-q3-103-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-4","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"وَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ، التي من جملتها الهداية للإسلام المؤدِّي إلى التآلف وزوال الغِلِّ، إِذْ كُنْتُمْ أَعْداءً في الجاهلية، يقتل بعضُكم بعضاً، فَأَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِكُمْ بالإسلام، فَأَصْبَحْتُمْ بِنِعْمَتِهِ إِخْواناً متحابين مجتمعين على الأخوة فى الله. قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لا تَحَاسَدُوا، ولا تَبَاغَضُوا، ولا تَدَابَرُوا، وكُونُوا عبادَ الله إخوانا، المسلم أخو المسلمُ لا يَظْلِمُه ولا يَخْذُلُه» . الحديث. رُوي أن الأوس والخزرج كانوا أخَوَيْن لأبوين، فوقع بين أولادهما العداوة، وتطاولت الحرب بينهما مائة وعشرين سنة، حتى أطفأها الله بالإسلام، وألف بينهم برسوله عليه الصلاة والسلام- فنزلت فيهم هذه الآية.","anchor":"ar-q3-103-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-5","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"ثم قال لهم: وَكُنْتُمْ عَلى شَفا حُفْرَةٍ مِنَ النَّارِ أي: مُشرفين على نار جهنم، إذ لو أدرككم الموت لوقعتم في النار، فَأَنْقَذَكُمْ الله مِنْها برسوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-. رُوِيَ أن أعرابيّاً سمع ابن عباس يقرأ هذه الآية، فقال الأعرابي: والله ما أنقذهم منها وهو يريد أن يوقعهم فيها، فقال ابن عباس رضي الله عنه خذوها من غير فقيه. هـ. كَذلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ آياتِهِ أي: مثل هذا التبيين يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ آياتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ إلى الخير، وتزيدون ثباتاً فيه.","anchor":"ar-q3-103-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-6","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"الإشارة: المذاهب كلها وقع فيها الاختلاف والتفرق في الأصول والفروع، إلا مذاهب الصوفية فكلها متفقة بداية ونهاية، إذ بدايتهم مجاهدة، ونهايتهم مشاهدة، وإلى ذلك أشار في المباحث، حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-q3-103-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-7","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"مذاهبُ الناسِ على اخْتلاف ... ومَذْهَبُ القَوْمِ على ائْتِلاَف","anchor":"ar-q3-103-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-8","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"وإن وقع الاختلاف في بعض الطرق الموصلة إلى المقصود، فقد اتفقت في النهاية، بخلاف أهل الظاهر، لا تجدهم يتفقون إلا في مسائل قليلة، لأن مذهبهم مبني على غلبة الظن، ومذهب القوم مبني على التحقيق ذوقاً وكشفاً، وكذلك ائتلفت أيضاً قلوبهم وأرواحهم، إذ كلهم متخلقون بالشفقة والرأفة والمودة والألفة والصفا لأنهم دخلوا الجنة- أعني جنة المعارف- فتخلقوا بأخلاق أهل الجنة، قال تعالى: وَنَزَعْنا مَا فِي صُدُورِهِمْ مِنْ غِلٍّ إِخْواناً عَلى سُرُرٍ مُتَقابِلِينَ، فيقال لهم بعد الفتح: واذكروا نعمةَ الله عليكم، إذ كنتم أعداء قبل اتصالكم بالطبيب، فألف بين قلوبكم، فأصبحتم بنعمته أخواناً متحابين، وكنتم على شفا حفرة من نار القطيعة والحجاب فَأَنْقَذَكُمْ مِنْها. مثل هذا البيان يوضح الله آياته، أي: تجلياته، لعلكم تهتدون إلى مشاهدة ذاته في أنوار صفاته. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-103-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-103-9","r":"q3-103","title":"3:103 · The rope of God, the reconciliation of hearts and the unity of the spiritual path","text":"ثم أمرهم الحق تعالى بالأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر، ووجه اتصاله بما قبله: أنهم سكتوا حين حرّش بينهم اليهود حتى هموا بالقتال، ولم يأمرهم أحد بالإمساك عنه، فحذّرهم الله من نزغته، وحضّهم على الاجتماع، وأمرهم بالأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر إذا رأوا شيئا من ذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-103-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-103-s1","r":"q3-103","title":"The rope as a means of attaining the end","text":"I say: The original sense of “rope” ( الحبل ) in language is a means ( السبب ) by which one reaches the object sought; faith or the Qurʾān is so named because it leads to unending happiness. “The edge of a pit” ( شفا حفرة ) means its rim. Its original form is shafw ( شفو ), the wāw being changed into alif in the masculine and omitted in the feminine, whence the word shafa ( شفة ), “lip.”","anchor":"en-q3-103-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-103-s2","r":"q3-103","title":"God’s cord and the reversal of inherited enmity","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Hold fast,” O company of Muslims, that is, cling “to the rope of God,” meaning faith or God’s Book, according to the Prophet’s saying: “This Qurʾān is God’s strong rope, the manifest light, the beneficial healing, and a protection for whoever holds fast to it ...” and the remainder of the report. Do so “all together,” united upon it; “and do not divide” as you were divided in the Age of Ignorance, or do not part from the truth through discord among yourselves as the People of the Book did. [XIV-N069] The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said, as cited here: “The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and my community will split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except one.” Asked, “Messenger of God, which is the one?”, he clasped his hand and said: “The community ( الجماعة ).” Then he recited: “Hold fast, all together, to the rope of God, and do not divide.” [Translator’s note: The numbers and wording here must be kept distinct from Ibn ʿAjība’s other version of the report in his very next section.] [XIV-N069] “Remember God’s blessing upon you,” one of its forms being guidance to Islam, which brings about affection and removes rancour, “when you were enemies” in the Age of Ignorance, killing one another, “and He joined your hearts” through Islam, “so that by His blessing you became brothers,” loving one another and united in brotherhood for God’s sake. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “Do not envy one another, hate one another or turn your backs on one another; be, servants of God, brothers. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not wrong him or abandon him.” The remainder of the report follows. It is related that Aws and Khazraj were originally two full brothers whose descendants became enemies and warred for a hundred and twenty years, until God extinguished this through Islam and united them by His Messenger; the verse was revealed about them. [XIV-N070] He then says to them: “You were upon the brink of a pit of fire,” almost falling into Hell; had death overtaken you, you would have fallen in. “And He rescued you from it,” through His Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him. It is related that a Bedouin heard Ibn ʿAbbās reciting this verse and said: “By God, He did not rescue them from it in order to cast them into it.” Ibn ʿAbbās replied: “Take this from someone who is not a jurist.” End of report. “Thus God makes His signs clear to you,” in such a manner He explains them, “that you may be guided” to the good and increase in steadfastness upon it. [XIV-N070]","anchor":"en-q3-103-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-103-s3","r":"q3-103","title":"Concord among the paths of realization and the healing of the heart","text":"All schools ( المذاهب ) have experienced disagreement and division in fundamentals and branches, save the ways of the Sufis ( مذاهب الصوفية ): these, says Ibn ʿAjība, agree in their beginning and their end, for their beginning is spiritual struggle ( المجاهدة ) and their end is witnessing ( المشاهدة ). The author of al-Mabāḥith alludes to this: The schools of people stand in disagreement; The school of the Folk stands in concord. Even if they disagree over particular ways ( الطرق ) of reaching the aim, they agree concerning the end. This is unlike the people of outward inquiry ( أهل الظاهر ), whom, in Ibn ʿAjība’s characterization, one finds agreeing only on a few questions, for their method is built upon the preponderance of conjecture ( غلبة الظن ), while the method of the Folk ( القوم ) is grounded in realization through tasting and unveiling ( التحقيق ذوقاً وكشفاً ). Their hearts and spirits, likewise, are united: all are formed by compassion, tenderness, affection, harmony and purity, because they have entered Paradise—the Paradise of gnoses ( جنة المعارف )—and adopted the character traits of the inhabitants of Paradise. God says: “We shall remove whatever rancour is in their breasts, as brothers upon couches facing one another” [15:47]. [XIV-N071] Thus after spiritual opening ( الفتح ) it is said to them: Remember God’s blessing upon you, when you were enemies before being connected to the healer ( الطبيب ); He united your hearts, and by His blessing you became brothers who love one another. You were at the brink of a pit of the fire of severance and veiling ( القطيعة والحجاب ), and He rescued you from it. By such an explanation God makes His signs—that is, His self-disclosures ( تجلياته )—clear, so that you may be guided to witness His Essence in the lights of His attributes. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-103-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-103-s4","r":"q3-103","title":"","text":"He then commanded them to enjoin what is recognized as good and forbid what is reprehensible. Its connection with the preceding verses is that they remained silent when the Jews stirred discord among them, until they almost fought, and not one of them commanded restraint. God therefore warned them against that provocation, urged unity and commanded them to enjoin right and forbid wrong whenever they saw anything of the kind, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-103-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-104","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence 3:104","anchor":"unit-q3-104"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-1","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"وَلْتَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ أُمَّةٌ يَدْعُونَ إِلَى الْخَيْرِ وَيَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَأُولئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ (104)","anchor":"ar-q3-104-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-2","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"قلت: (مِنْ) : للتبعيض لأن الأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر من فُروض الكفاية إذ لا يصلح له كُلُّ أحد، أو للبيان، أي: كونوا أمة تأمرون بالمعروف، كقوله: كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ تَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ الخ، و (يأمرون بالمعروف وينْهون عن المنكر) عطف على الخبر، من عطف الخاص على العام للإيذان بفضله.","anchor":"ar-q3-104-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-3","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلْتَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ يا أمة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم أُمَّةٌ أي: طائفةً يَدْعُونَ إِلَى الْخَيْرِ، وهو كل ما فيه صلاحٌ ديني، أو دنيوى إذا كان يؤول إلى الديني، أو صلاح قلبي أو روحاني، وَيَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وهو ما يستحسنه الطبع ويرتضيه الشرع، وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وهو كل ما ينكره الطبعُ السليم والشرع المستقيم، فمن فعل ذلك فأولئك هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ المخصوصون بكمال الفلاح.","anchor":"ar-q3-104-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-4","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"روى عنه عليه الصلاة والسلام: أنه سئل مَنْ خير الناس؟ فقال: «آمرُهم بالمعروف، وأنهاهم عن المنكر، وأتقاهم لله، وأوصلهم للرحم» . وقال أيضاً: «مَنْ أمَرَ بالمَعْروفِ ونَهَى عَنِ المُنْكَرِ كان خَلِيفَةَ اللهِ في أرْضِهِ وخَلِيفَةَ رَسُولِه وخَلِيفَةَ كِتَابِه. وقال على رضي الله عنه: (أفضل الجهاد: الأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر وشنئان الفاسقين- أي بغضهم- فمن أمر بالمعروف شدَّ ظهرَ المؤمن، ومن نهى عن المنكر أرْغَمَ أنف المنافق، ومن شَنَأَ الفاسقين وغَضب لله غَضبَ الله له) . وقال أبو الدرداء: (لتأمُرُن بالمعروف، ولتنهون عن المنكر، أو ليُسلطن الله عليكم سلطاناً ظالماً، لا يُجِلُّ كبيركم، ولا يرحم صغيركم، ويدعو عليه خيارُكم فلا يستجاب لهم، ويَسْتنصِرون فلا يُنصرون، ويستغفرون فلا يغفر لهم) . وقال حذيفة: (يأتي على الناس زمان لأن تكون فيه جيفة حمار، أحب إليهم من مؤمنٍ يأمرهم بالمعروف وينهاهم عن المنكر) .","anchor":"ar-q3-104-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-5","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"وللمتصدِّي له شروط: العلم بالأحكام، ومراتب الاحْتِسَاب وكيفية إقامتها، والتمكن من القيام بها. ولذلك خاطب الحق تعالى الجميع، وطلب فعل بعضهم، إذ لا يصلح للقيام به إلا البعض، كما هو شأن فرض الكفاية، إذ هو واجب على الكل، بحيث لو تركوه لعوقبوا جميعاً، لكنه يسقط بفعل البعض.","anchor":"ar-q3-104-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-6","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"والأمر بالمعروف يكون واجباً ومندوباً، على حسب ما يأمر به، والنهي عن المنكر واجب كله لأن جميع ما أنكره الشرع حرام. وأما المكروه فليس بمنكر، فيستحب الإرشاد إلى تركه. والأظهر أن العاصي يجب أن ينهى عما يرتكبه هو لأنه يجب عليه تركه، فلا يسقط بترك أحدهما وجوب الآخر. وقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام:","anchor":"ar-q3-104-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-7","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"«مُرُوا بالمَعْرُوفِ وإنْ لَمْ تَعمَلُوا بِكُلِّهِ، وانْهَوْا عَنِ المُنْكَرِ وإنْ لم تَنْتَهُوا عنه كُلهُ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-104-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-8","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"الإشارة: (ولتكن منكم أمة) أي: طائفة ينهض حالهم ويدلُّ على الله مقالهم، يدعون إلى الخير العظيم، وهو شهود ذات السميع العليم، ويأمرون بالمعروف بالهمة العلية، وينهون عن المنكر بالحال القوية، فكلُّ من رآهم بالصفا ائتمر وانتهى، وكل من صحبهم بالوفاء أخذ حظه من الغنى بالمكيال الأوفى، إن لله رجالاً من نظر إليهم سعد سعادة لا يشقى بعدها أبداً، فهؤلاء يأمرون بالمعروف وينْهون عن المنكر بالحال دون المقال.","anchor":"ar-q3-104-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-9","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"يُحكى أن بعض الشيوخ مرَّ مع أصحابه بقوم يشربون الخمر تحت شجرة، فأراد أصحابه أن يُغيروا عليهم، فقال لهم: إن كنتم رجالاً فَغِيرُوا عليهم بحالكم دون مقالكم، فتوجهوا إلى الله بهممهم، فإذا القوم قد كسروا الأواني، وجاءوا إلى","anchor":"ar-q3-104-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-10","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"الشيخ تائبين. وكذلك قضية معروف الكرخي مع أصحاب السفينة، الذين كانوا مشتغلين باللهو واللعب، فقال له أصحابه: ادع عليهم، فقال: اللهم كما فرَّحتَهم في الدنيا ففرِّحْهُم في الآخرة، فتابوا على يده جميعاً. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-104-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-104-11","r":"q3-104","title":"3:104 · Enjoining good, collective obligation and the command of spiritual presence","text":"ثم أعاد النهى عن الفرقة، تأكيدا لذمها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-104-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-104-s1","r":"q3-104","title":"Whether “from among you” denotes a subset or the whole community","text":"I say: “From among you” ( مِنْكُمْ )—the particle min ( مِنْ )—can be partitive ( للتبعيض ), because enjoining right and forbidding wrong is among the collective obligations ( فروض الكفاية ), not every person being suited to it. Or min can be explanatory ( للبيان ): that is, “Be a community that enjoins what is right,” as in “You are the best community brought forth for humankind: you enjoin what is right ...” [3:110]. “They enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong” is coordinated with the predicate ( الخبر ), the mention of the particular after the general ( عطف الخاص على العام ) to show its special merit. [XIV-N072]","anchor":"en-q3-104-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-104-s2","r":"q3-104","title":"Calling to every form of good that leads to religious flourishing","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Let there be from among you,” O community of Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him, “a community,” that is, a party, “who call to what is good ( الخير ),” meaning whatever brings about religious wellbeing, or worldly wellbeing when it leads to religious wellbeing, or the wellbeing of heart and spirit. “They enjoin what is recognized as right ( المعروف ),” which sound disposition finds beautiful and the revealed Law approves, “and forbid what is reprehensible ( المنكر ),” which sound nature and the upright Law repudiate. Those who do so “are the ones who prosper,” especially distinguished by the perfection of success. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is reported to have been asked, “Which people are best?” and to have replied: “Those who most enjoin what is right, most forbid what is wrong, are most mindful of God, and most maintain family ties.” He is also quoted as saying: “Whoever enjoins right and forbids wrong is God’s vicegerent on His earth, the vicegerent of His Messenger, and the vicegerent of His Book.” [XIV-N073] ʿAlī, may God be pleased with him, said: “The best striving ( الجهاد ) is to enjoin right, forbid wrong, and detest the transgressors”—that is, hate them. “Whoever enjoins right strengthens the believer’s back; whoever forbids wrong humiliates the hypocrite; and whoever detests the transgressors and grows angry for God, God grows angry on his behalf.” Abū al-Dardāʾ said: “You shall surely enjoin right and forbid wrong, or God will set over you an unjust ruler who will neither honour your elders nor show mercy to your young. Your best people will pray against him without being answered, seek help without receiving it, and seek forgiveness without being forgiven.” Ḥudhayfa said: “A time will come when the corpse of a donkey will be more beloved to people than a believer who enjoins them to right and forbids them from wrong.” [Translator’s note: The chains of these cited sayings have not been individually authenticated.] [XIV-N073]","anchor":"en-q3-104-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-104-s3","r":"q3-104","title":"Capacity, knowledge and the distinction between required and recommended action","text":"The person who undertakes the duty requires qualifications: knowledge of the rulings ( العلم بالأحكام ), of the degrees of moral intervention ( مراتب الاحتساب ), of how to carry it out, and the ability to discharge it. That is why the Real addresses all but requests action from some: only a portion are fitted for it. This is the nature of a collective obligation ( فرض الكفاية ), which rests on everyone in such a way that, if all neglect it, all are liable, but whose performance by some discharges the rest. [XIV-N072] Enjoining what is right can be obligatory or recommended, depending on what is being enjoined. Forbidding what is wrong is entirely obligatory, since whatever the Law condemns in this technical sense is forbidden ( حرام ). As for what is merely disliked ( المكروه ), it is not “wrong” in that sense, so encouraging one to leave it is recommended. The stronger view, he says, is that a person who himself commits a sin must nevertheless forbid that same sin to others, because he has two duties—to desist from it and to forbid it—and neglect of one does not remove the obligation of the other. The Prophet is quoted as saying: “Command right even if you do not perform all of it; and forbid wrong even if you do not desist from all of it.” [XIV-N074]","anchor":"en-q3-104-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-104-s4","r":"q3-104","title":"Those whose state itself calls others to God","text":"“Let there be from among you a community”: a company whose spiritual state ( حال ) impels others to rise, and whose words point towards God. They summon to the greatest good, the witnessing of the Essence of the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing ( شهود ذات السميع العليم ); they enjoin right through their exalted spiritual aspiration ( الهمة العلية ) and forbid wrong through the strength of their state ( الحال القوية ). Whoever sees them in purity obeys and refrains; whoever accompanies them in fidelity obtains his full share of spiritual wealth. God has men at the sight of whom someone attains a happiness after which he shall never be wretched. Such men enjoin right and forbid wrong through their state rather than through speech ( بالحال دون المقال ). It is related that a shaykh once passed with his companions by some men drinking wine beneath a tree. His companions wished to rush upon them. He said: “If you are men, change their conduct by your state, not by your speech.” They directed their spiritual aspirations toward God and the men immediately broke their vessels and came to the shaykh in repentance. So too is the incident of Maʿrūf al-Karkhī and the people on a boat who were occupied with amusement and play. His companions told him to pray against them. He said: “O God, just as You have made them happy in this world, make them happy in the Hereafter.” All of them repented through him. Through God is success, and He is the Guide to the even way. [XIV-N075]","anchor":"en-q3-104-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-104-s5","r":"q3-104","title":"","text":"He then repeated the prohibition on division, underscoring his censure of it, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-104-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-105-109","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation 3:105–109","anchor":"unit-q3-105-109"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-1","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"وَلا تَكُونُوا كَالَّذِينَ تَفَرَّقُوا وَاخْتَلَفُوا مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ وَأُولئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذابٌ عَظِيمٌ (105) يَوْمَ تَبْيَضُّ وُجُوهٌ وَتَسْوَدُّ وُجُوهٌ فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ اسْوَدَّتْ وُجُوهُهُمْ أَكَفَرْتُمْ بَعْدَ إِيمانِكُمْ فَذُوقُوا الْعَذابَ بِما كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُونَ (106) وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ ابْيَضَّتْ وُجُوهُهُمْ فَفِي رَحْمَتِ اللَّهِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (107) تِلْكَ آياتُ اللَّهِ نَتْلُوها عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَمَا اللَّهُ يُرِيدُ ظُلْماً لِلْعالَمِينَ (108) وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ وَإِلَى اللَّهِ تُرْجَعُ الْأُمُورُ (109)","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-2","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"قلت: (يوم) : متعلق بالاستقرار في خبر (أولئك) ، أو باذكر محذوفة، وقوله: (أكفرتم) : محكي بقول محذوف جواب (أما) ، أي: فيقال لهم: أكفرتم.","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-3","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلا تَكُونُوا كاليهود والنصارى الذين (تفرقوا) في التوحيد والتنزيه، وَاخْتَلَفُوا في أحوال الآخرة. قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «افترقت اليهود على إحدى وسبعين فرقة، وافترقت النصارى على ثنتين وسبعين فرقة، وستفترق أمتي على ثلاث وسبعين فرقة، كلها في النار إلا واحدة. قيل: ومَنْ تلك الواحدة؟ قال: ما أَنَا وأَصْحابِي عَلَيْه» . وهذا الحديث أصح مما تقدم، والصحابة يروْوُن الحديث بالمعنى، فلعلَّ الأول نسي بعض الحديث. والله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-4","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"ثم إن النهي مخصوص بالتفرق في الأصول دون الفروع، لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام: «اخْتلاَفُ أُمَّتِي رَحْمَةٌ» ، ولقوله: «من اجْتَهَدَ وأصَابَ فله أجْرَانِ، ومن اجْتَهدَ وأخطَأَ فَلَهُ أجْرٌ وَاحد» .","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-5","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"ثم إن أهل الكتاب تفرقوا مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ أي: الآيات والحجج المبينة للحق الموجبة للاتفاق عليه، وَأُولئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذابٌ عَظِيمٌ، يستقر لهم هذا العذاب يَوْمَ تَبْيَضُّ وُجُوهٌ المؤمنين المتقين على التوحيد، وَتَسْوَدُّ وُجُوهٌ الكافرين المتفرقين فيه، أو تبيض وجوه المخلصين وتسود وجوه المنافقين، أو تبيض وجوه أهل السنة وتسود وجوه أهل البدعة. وبياض الوجوه وسوادها كِنَايتَان عن ظهور بهجة السرور وكآبة الخوف","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-6","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"فيه، وقيل: يُوسَم أهل الحق ببياض الوجه والصحيفة وإشراق البشرة وسعي النور بين يديه وبيمينه، وأهل الباطل بأضداد ذلك. فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ اسْوَدَّتْ وُجُوهُهُمْ فيقال لهم يومئذ: أَكَفَرْتُمْ بمحمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- بعد ظهوره، بَعْدَ إِيمانِكُمْ به قبل ظهوره، وهم اليهود أو أهل الردة، آمنوا فى حياته صلّى الله عليه وسلم وكفروا بعد موته.","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-7","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"أو جميع الكفار، آمنوا في عالم الذر وأقروا على أنفسهم، ثم كفروا في عالم الشهادة. ويقال لهم أيضا: فَذُوقُوا الْعَذابَ بسبب ما كنتم (تكفرون) .","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-8","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ ابْيَضَّتْ وُجُوهُهُمْ فَفِي رَحْمَتِ اللَّهِ أي: جَنته، هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ. وعبَّر بالرحمة عن الجنة تنبيهاً على أن المؤمن، وإنْ استغرق عمره في طاعة الله- تعالى-، لا يدخل الجنة إلا برحمة الله وفضله، وكان حق الترتيب أن يقدم حِلية المؤمنين لتقدُّم ذكرهم، لكن قصد أن يكون مطلعُ الكلام ومقطعُه حليةَ المؤمنين وثوابهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-9","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"تِلْكَ آياتُ اللَّهِ الواردة في وَعْده وَوَعِيدِه، نَتْلُوها عَلَيْكَ متلبسة بِالْحَقِّ لا شبهة فيها، فقد أعذر وأنذر، وَمَا اللَّهُ يُرِيدُ ظُلْماً لِلْعالَمِينَ إذ لا يحق عليه شيء فيظلم بنقصه، ولا يُمنع من شيء فيظلم بفعله، كما بيَّنه بقوله: وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ مُلكاً وخلقاً وعبيداً، فيجازي كلا بما وَعَدَه وأوْعَدَه، وَإِلَى اللَّهِ تُرْجَعُ الْأُمُورُ كلها فيتصرف على وفْقِ مراده وسَابق مشيئته، لاَ يُسْئَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْئَلُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-10","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"الإشارة: قد نهى الله- تعالى- أهل الجمع عن التشبه بأهل الفرق، في اختلاف قلوبهم ووجوههم وآرائهم وأنظارهم، مِن بعد ما جاءتهم الدلائل الواضحات على طلب جمع القلب على الله، والتودد في الله، وصرف النظرة في شهود الله، وأولئك المفترقون لهم عذاب عظيم، وأيّ عذاب أعظم من الحجاب؟ يوم تبيض وجوه العارفين، فتكون كالشمس الضاحية، يسرحون في الجنان حيث شاءوا، وتسود وجوه الجاهلين لما يعتريها من الندم، وسوادها باعتبار وجوه العارفين في النقص عنها، وإن كانت مُبْيَضَّةً بنور الإيمان، لكن فاتهم نور الإحسان، فيقال: أكفرتم بالخصوصية في زمانكم، بعد إيمانكم بها فيمن سلف قبلكم؟ فذوقوا عذاب القطيعة عن شهود الحبيب في كل حين، وأما الذين ابيضت وجوههم وأشرقت بنور البقاء، ففي رحمة الله، أي: جنة المعارف فِي مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ مَلِيكٍ مُقْتَدِرٍ، فقد اتضحت الطريق، وظهرت أعلام التحقيق، لكن الهداية بيد الله، كما أنَّ الأمور كلها بيده، يهدي مَن يشاء ويضل من يشاء، وَما رَبُّكَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِلْعَبِيدِ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-105-109-11","r":"q3-105-109","title":"3:105–109 · Division after proof, the illumination of faces and the mercy of salvation","text":"ثم مدح الأمة المحمدية بامتثال ما أمرها به من الأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-105-109-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-105-109-s1","r":"q3-105-109","title":"The position of “the Day” and an omitted speech formula","text":"I say: “The Day” ( يوم ) depends on the implied state of subsistence ( الاستقرار ) in the predicate ( خبر ) of “those” ( أولئك ), or on an unexpressed command “remember” ( اذكر ) with [its governing expression] omitted. As for “Did you disbelieve?” ( أكفرتم ), it is a quotation introduced by an unexpressed verb of saying that constitutes the answer to ammā ( أما ): that is, “It will be said to them: Did you disbelieve?”","anchor":"en-q3-105-109-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-105-109-s2","r":"q3-105-109","title":"Division in fundamentals versus plurality in derivative judgments","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Do not be like” the Jews and Christians, “those who split apart” concerning divine unity and God’s transcendence ( التوحيد والتنزيه ), “and differed” about the states of the Hereafter. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is cited as saying: “The Jews divided into seventy-one sects, the Christians into seventy-two, and my community will divide into seventy-three; all are in the Fire except one.” Asked which one it was, he replied: “What I and my Companions are upon.” Ibn ʿAjība says that this version is sounder than the version quoted earlier, and adds that the Companions transmitted hadith according to its meaning, so perhaps the first transmitter forgot part of it. And God knows best. [XIV-N076] He then says the prohibition concerns division over fundamentals ( الأصول ), not disagreements over derivative matters ( الفروع ), adducing the saying “Disagreement within my community is a mercy,” as well as the saying that the one who exercises legal effort ( اجتهاد ) and reaches the correct conclusion receives two rewards, while one who exercises it and errs receives one. [Translator’s note: The first saying’s status is disputed and should not be treated as an authenticated Prophetic report simply because Ibn ʿAjība quotes it.] [XIV-N077] The People of the Book divided “after clear proofs had come to them,” meaning verses and demonstrations revealing the truth and demanding agreement upon it. “For them is a mighty punishment”: this punishment shall abide for them “on the Day when some faces become white,” those of believers who were mindful of God and upheld unity; “and some faces become black,” those of unbelievers divided concerning unity. Or the whitened faces are those of the sincere ( المخلصين ), and the darkened faces those of the hypocrites ( المنافقين ); or the former are those who follow the Sunna and the latter the people of innovation. Whiteness and blackness of faces may be metonymies ( كنايتان ) for the manifest radiance of happiness and the gloom of fear. Another interpretation takes the marks literally: the people of truth are distinguished by whitened faces and records, bright complexions and light moving before them and on their right, while the people of falsehood receive the corresponding opposites. [XIV-N078] “As for those whose faces turn black,” it is said to them on that Day: “Did you disbelieve in Muḥammad,” blessings and peace be upon him, after his appearance, “after your faith” in him before his appearance? These are the Jews; or it refers to apostates ( أهل الردة ) who believed during his life and disbelieved after his death. Or it means all unbelievers: they believed and acknowledged [God] in the realm of particles ( عالم الذر ), then disbelieved in the realm of visible testimony ( عالم الشهادة ). To them it is said: “Taste the punishment for what you used to disbelieve.” “As for those whose faces become white, they will be in God’s mercy,” that is, His Garden, “abiding there forever.” He calls the Garden “mercy” to indicate that, even if a believer spends his whole life obeying God Most High, he enters the Garden only through God’s mercy and favour. One might have expected the adornment of the believers to come first because they were mentioned first, but [the passage] is designed so that both the opening and close of the discussion are concerned with the believers’ adornment and reward. “These are God’s signs,” concerning His promise and warning ( الوعد والوعيد ); “We recite them to you in truth,” without uncertainty. He has made the excuse impossible and given warning. “God does not desire injustice for the worlds,” since nothing is incumbent upon Him such that deprivation of it would wrong someone; and nothing is forbidden to Him such that His doing it would be unjust. He clarifies this by saying: “To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth,” by ownership, creation and servitude. He recompenses each according to what He has promised or threatened. “To God all affairs are returned”: He disposes them according to His will and His prior choice. “He is not questioned about what He does, but they shall be questioned” [21:23]. [XIV-N079]","anchor":"en-q3-105-109-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-105-109-s3","r":"q3-105-109","title":"The faces of realization and the pain of veiling","text":"God Most High has forbidden the people of gathering ( أهل الجمع ) to resemble the people of separation ( أهل الفرق ), in the differing of their hearts, their faces, their opinions and their ways of seeing, after clear proofs have come to them concerning gathering the heart upon God, affection for God’s sake, and directing the gaze towards the witnessing of God. For those divided people there is a great punishment—and what punishment is greater than the veil ( الحجاب )? On the Day when the faces of the knowers ( العارفين ) become white, like the brilliant sun, they roam in the gardens wherever they wish. The faces of the ignorant darken with regret. Their darkness is relative to the faces of the knowers: they may be white with the light of faith ( نور الإيمان ), but they lack the light of spiritual excellence ( نور الإحسان ). It is said to them: “Did you disbelieve in special spiritual distinction ( الخصوصية ) in your own time after believing that it existed among those before you?” Taste, then, the punishment of severance ( القطيعة ) from witnessing the Beloved at every moment. [XIV-N080] As for those whose faces become white and shine with the light of subsistence ( نور البقاء ), they are in God’s mercy: that is, the Garden of gnoses ( جنة المعارف ), “in a seat of truth, in the presence of an all-powerful Sovereign” [54:55]. The path has been made clear and the waymarks of realization manifest, but guidance is in God’s hand, just as all affairs lie in His hand. He guides whom He wills and leaves astray whom He wills. “Your Lord is not unjust to His servants” [41:46]. Through God is success.","anchor":"en-q3-105-109-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-105-109-s4","r":"q3-105-109","title":"","text":"He then praised the Muhammadan community for obeying His command to enjoin right and forbid wrong, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-105-109-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-110-112","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant 3:110–112","anchor":"unit-q3-110-112"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-1","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ تَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَتَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَتُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ ...","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-2","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"قلت: (كان) : على بابها من الدلالة على المُضِيِّ، أي: كنتم في اللوح المحفوظ، أو في علم الله، أو فيما بين الأمم المتقدمة، أو: صلة، أي: أنتم خير أمة، و (للناس) : يتعلق بأخرجت، أو بكنتم، أي: كنتم خير الناس للناس.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-3","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لأمة نبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم: كُنْتُمْ في سابق علمي خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ ظهرت لِلنَّاسِ تجيئون بهم إلى الجنة بالسلاسل. ثم بيَّن وجه فضلهم فقال: تَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَتَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَتُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وبجميع ما يجب الإيمان به.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-4","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وقد ورد في مدح هذه الأمة المحمدية أحاديث، منها: قوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «حُرِّمتْ الجنةُ على الأنبياء حتى أدخلها أنا، وحُرّمتْ الجنة على الأُمَمِ حتى تدخلها أمتي» . ومنها قوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «أمتي أمةٌ مَرْحُومَةٌ، إذَا كَانَ يَوْمُ القِيامةِ أَعطى الله كُلَّ رَجُلٍ مِن هذه الأمة رجُلاً فيقال: هذَا فِدَاؤُكَ مِنَ النَّارِ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-5","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وعن أنس قال: «خرجت مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فإذا صوت يجيىء من شِعْبِ، فقال: يا أنس: قُمْ فانظرْ ما هذا الصوت، فانطلقت فإذا برجلٍ يُصلّي إلى شجرة، ويقول: اللهم اجعلني من أمة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، الأمة المرحومة، المغفور لها، المستجاب لها، المتاب عليها، فأتيت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فأخبرته، فقال: انطلق، فقل له: إن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقرئك السلام، ويقول لك: من أنت؟ فأتيته، فأعلمته ما قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فقال: اقرأ مني السلام على رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، وقل له: أخوك الخضر يقول لك: ادع الله أن يجعلني من أمتك المرحومة المغفور لها(1)» . وقيل لعيسى بن مريم: هل بعد هذه الأمة أمة؟ قال: نعم، أمة أحمد. قيل: وما أمة أحمد؟ قال: علماء، حكماء، أبرار أتقياء، كأنهم من الفقه أنبياء، يرضون باليسير من الرزق، ويرضى الله عنهم باليسير من العمل، يدخلهم الجنة بشهادة أن لا إله إلا الله. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-6","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وليس أولها أولى بالمدح من آخرها، لقوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «أمتي كالمطر، لا يدرى أولهُ خيرٌ أو آخرُه» ؟ وفي خبر آخر عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم قال: «اشتقْتُ إلى إخواني، فقال أصحابه: نحن إخوانُك يا رسول الله، فقال: أنتم أصْحَابي، إخْواني: ناس يأتُون بعدي، يُؤمنون بي ولم يَرَوْنِي، يَوَدُّ أحدُهم لو يَرَاني بجميع ما يَمْلِكُ. يَعْدِلُ عملُ أحدهم سبعين منكم. قالوا:","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-7","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"مِنْهم يا رسول الله؟ قال: منكم. قالوا: ولِمَ ذلك يا رسول الله؟ قال: لأنكم وَجَدْتُم على الخير أعواناً، وهم لم يَجِدُوا عليه أعواناً» . أو كما قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-8","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"قلت: التفضيل باعتبار أجور الأعمال، وأما باعتبار اليقين والمعرفة، فالصحابة أفضل الخلق بعد الأنبياء- عليهم السلام- ويدل على هذا قوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «يعدل عمل أحدهم» ، ولم يقل إيمان أحدهم(2) .","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-9","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-10","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"الإشارة: كنتم يا معشر الصوفية خير أمة أخرجت للناس، تأمرون بالجمع على الله والغيبة عما سواه، وتنهونَ عن كلِّ ما يُبعد عن الله ويفرق العبدَ عن مولاه، وتؤمنون بالله وبما وعد به الله، إيمان الشهود والعيان، الذي هو مقام الإحسان. قال القشيري في رسالته: (قد جعل الله هذه الطائفة صفوة أوليائه، وفضَّلهم على الكافة من عباده بعد رسله وأنبيائه) .","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-11","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وقال الجنيد رضي الله عنه: لو نعلم أن تحت أديمِ السماء أشرف من هذا العلم الذي نتكلم فيه مع أصحابنا، لسعيت إليه ولو حبواً. هـ. وكان كثيراً ما ينشد:","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-12","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"عِلْمُ التصوفِ عِلمٌ ليس يَعْرِفُهُ ... إلاَّ أَخْو فِطْنَةِ بِالحقِّ معروفُ","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-13","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وليسَ يُبْصِرهُ مَنْ ليس يَشْهدهُ ... وكيفَ يَشْهَدُ ضوءَ الشمس مكفوفُ","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-14","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وقال الشيخ الصقلي: (كلُّ من صدَّقَ بهذا العلم فهو من الخاصة، وكل من فهمه فهو من خاصة الخاصة، وكل من عبّر به وتكلم فيه فهو من النجم الذي لا يُدرك والبحر الذي لا ينزف) . وقال في الإحياء- لمَّا تكلم على معرفة الله والعلم بالله، قال: (والرتبةُ العليا في ذلك للأنبياء، ثم للأولياء العارفين، ثم للعلماء الراسخين، ثم للصالحين) . فقد قدَّم الأولياء على العلماء. قال ابن رشد: وما قاله القشيري والغزالي متفق عليه. قال: ولا يشكُّ عاقلٌ أنَّ العارفين بالله وما يجب له من الكمال، أفضل من العارفين بأحكام الله. انظر تمامه في المعيار. وقال في المباحث:","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-15","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"حجّة من يرجّح الصُوفية ... على سواهم حُجَّةٌ قويَّة","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-16","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"هُمْ أَتْبَعُ النَّاسِ لخيرِ النَّاس ... مِنْ سَائِرِ الأَنَامِ والأُنَاس","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-17","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"ثم قال:","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-18","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"ثُمَّ بِشَيْئَيْنِ تقومُ الحُجَّه ... أنَّهمْ قَطْعاً على المَحَجَّه(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-19","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وَمَا أَتَوْا فيه بخَرْقِ الْعَادَه ... إذْ لمْ تَكُنْ لِمَنْ سِوَاهُم عَادَه","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-20","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"قَدْ رَفَضُوا الآثَامَ والعُيوب ... وطَهَّرُوا الأبدَانَ والقُلُوب","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-21","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وَبَلَغُوا حقيقَةَ الإيمَان ... وانْتَهَجُوا منَاهِجَ الإحْسَان","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-22","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"ثم دعا أهل الكتاب إلى الإيمان، وهوَّن أمرهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-23","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"... وَلَوْ آمَنَ أَهْلُ الْكِتابِ لَكانَ خَيْراً لَهُمْ مِنْهُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ وَأَكْثَرُهُمُ الْفاسِقُونَ (110) لَنْ يَضُرُّوكُمْ إِلاَّ أَذىً وَإِنْ يُقاتِلُوكُمْ يُوَلُّوكُمُ الْأَدْبارَ ثُمَّ لاَ يُنْصَرُونَ (111) ضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ أَيْنَ مَا ثُقِفُوا إِلاَّ بِحَبْلٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَحَبْلٍ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَباؤُ بِغَضَبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْمَسْكَنَةُ ذلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ كانُوا يَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ وَيَقْتُلُونَ الْأَنْبِياءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ ذلِكَ بِما عَصَوْا وَكانُوا يَعْتَدُونَ (112)","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-24","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"قلت: الاستثناء في قوله (إلا بحبل) : من أعم الأحوال، أي: ضربت عليهم الذلة في جميع الأحوال، إلا متلبسين بذمة من الله وذمة من الناس.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-25","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَوْ آمَنَ أَهْلُ الْكِتابِ إيمانا كائنا كإيمانكم، لَكانَ خَيْراً لَهُمْ مما هم عليه. وليس أهل الكتاب سواء، بل مِنْهُمُ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ كعبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه، وَأَكْثَرُهُمُ الْفاسِقُونَ المتمردون في الكفر والفسوق، فلا يهولكم أمرهم، فإنهم لَنْ يَضُرُّوكُمْ إلا ضرراً يسيراً كأذى باللسان من عيب وسب وتحريش بينكم، ولا قدرة لهم على القتال، وَإِنْ يُقاتِلُوكُمْ ينهزموا، ويُوَلُّوكُمُ الْأَدْبارَ ثُمَّ لا يُنْصَرُونَ أبداً عليكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-26","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"وهذه الآية من المُغيبات التي وافقها الواقع، إذ كان كذلك في بني قريظة والنضير وبني قينقاع وخيبر، فلم تُرْفع لهم راية أبداً، بل ضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ والخزي والهوان، أي: أحاطت بهم إحاطة البيت المضروب على أهله، أو لزمتهم لزوم الدرهم المضروب لضربه، فلا تنفك عنهم أَيْنَ ما ثُقِفُوا ووُجدوا، فلا يأمنون إِلَّا بِحَبْلٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ أي: بسبب عهد من الله، وهو عقد الذمة التي أمر الله بها، إذا أدوا الجزية للمسلمين، فلهم حرمة بسبب هذا العقد، فلا يجوز التعرض لهم في مال ولا دم ولا أهل، وَحَبْلٍ مِنَ النَّاسِ، وهو عقد الذمة التي يعقدها مع الكفار إذا كانوا تحت ذمتهم. والحاصل أن الذلة لازمة لهم(1) فلا يأمنون إلا تحت الذمة، إما من المسلمين وإما من الكفار. وَباؤُ بِغَضَبٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ أي: انقلبوا به مستحقين له، وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْمَسْكَنَةُ أي: أحاطت بهم، فاليهود في الغالب فقراء مساكين، لأن قلوبهم خاوية من اليقين، فالفقر والجزع لازم لهم، ولو ملكوا الدنيا بأجمعها.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-27","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"ذلِكَ الذل والمسكنة والبواء بالغضب بسبب أنهم كانُوا يَكْفُرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ المنزلة على رسوله، أو الدالة على توحيده، وَيَقْتُلُونَ الْأَنْبِياءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ بل ظلماً وعدواناً، ذلك الكفر بسبب عصيانهم واعتدائهم حدود الله، فإن الإصرار على الصغائر يُفضي إلى الكبائر، والإصرار على الكبائر يؤدي إلى الكفر لأن المعاصي بريد الكفر، والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-28","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"الإشارة: ولو آمن أهل العلم الظاهر بطريق الخصوص، وحطوا رؤوسهم لأهل الخصوصية لكان خيرا لهم، لتتسع عليهم دائرة العلوم، وتفتح لهم مخازن الفهوم، منهم من يقر بوجود الخصوصية، ويعجز عن حمل شروطها، وأكثرهم ينكرونها ويحتجون لأنفسهم بقول من قال: انقطعت التربية في القرن الثامن، فيموتون مصرين على الإنكار والعصيان، فلن يضركم إنكارهم أيها الفقراء، فإنهم لا قدرة لهم عليكم، للرعاية التي أحاطت بكم، إلا أذى بلسانهم، وعلى تقدير لحوق ضررهم في الظاهر، فإن الله يُغيِّبْ ألمّ ذلك عنكم في الباطن، كما شاهدناه من بعض الفقراء، وإن يُهددوكم بالقتل والجلاء، فإن الله لا يَنْصُرُهم في الغالب.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-29","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"قلت: وقد هددونا بالضرب والرفع إلى السلطان والجلاء إلى برِّ النصارى، فلم يقدروا على شيء من ذلك، وقد وقع ذلك لبعض الصوفية زيادةً في شرفهم وعزّهم، فالمنكر على الصوفية(2) لا يزال في هَمٍّ وغمٍّ وذُلٍّ ومسكنة، لخراب باطنه من نور اليقين. فإنَّ الانتقاد على الأولياء جناية واعتقادهم عناية، فإن استمر على أذاهم كان عاقبته سوء الخاتمة، فيبوء بغضب من الله بسبب اعتدائه على أولياء الله، «ومن آذى لي وليا فقد أذن بالحرب» ، رزقنا الله الأدب معهم، وأماتنا على محبتهم، آمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-110-112-30","r":"q3-110-112","title":"3:110–112 · The best community, degrees of spiritual knowledge and protection under covenant","text":"ولمّا كان من اليهود من أسلم وحسن إسلامه استثناه الله تعالى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-110-112-30"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-110-112-s1","r":"q3-110-112","title":"The force of “you were” and the beneficiaries of goodness","text":"I say: “You were” ( كُنْتُمْ ): kāna ( كان ) may retain its normal force indicating the past ( المضي ): you were [so designated] in the Preserved Tablet ( اللوح المحفوظ ), or in God’s knowledge, or among earlier peoples. Or it may be an expletive connective ( صلة ), meaning simply “You are the best community.” “For humankind” ( للنّاس ) may depend upon “brought forth” ( أخرجت ), or upon “you were” ( كنتم ), yielding “You were the best of people for people.” [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-15] ]","anchor":"en-q3-110-112-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-110-112-s2","r":"q3-110-112","title":"The virtue of the Muhammadan community","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says to the community of our Prophet Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him: “You were,” in My prior knowledge, “the best community brought forth for humankind,” leading people into Paradise even in chains. He then states the reason for their excellence: “You enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and believe in God,” and in everything it is obligatory to believe. Reports praising the Muhammadan community include the Prophet’s words, as cited here: “Paradise was withheld from the prophets until I enter it, and withheld from the communities until my community enters.” And: “My community is a community shown mercy. On the Day of Resurrection God gives each man of this community another man, and it is said: This is your ransom from the Fire.” [XIV-N081] Anas is reported as saying: “I went out with the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, and a voice was coming from a mountain pass. He said: ‘Anas, get up and find out what this voice is.’ I went, and there was a man praying toward a tree and saying: ‘O God, make me one of Muḥammad’s community, the community that receives mercy, is forgiven, is answered and whose repentance is accepted.’ I told the Prophet. He said: ‘Go and tell him that God’s Messenger sends his greeting and asks: Who are you?’ I conveyed the message. He said: ‘Send my greeting to God’s Messenger and say to him: Your brother al-Khiḍr asks you to pray that God make me a member of your community—the community shown mercy and forgiven.’” [XIV-N082] It was said to Jesus son of Mary: “Will there be a community after this one?” He answered: “Yes, the community of Aḥmad.” Asked about its character, he said: “They are scholars, wise ones, righteous and Godfearing, like prophets in their understanding of religion. They are content with a little provision, and God is content with a little work from them. He admits them into Paradise by their testimony that there is no god but God.” End of cited account. [XIV-N082] The earliest members of the community do not have an exclusive claim to praise over its later members, in view of the saying: “My community is like rain: one does not know whether its beginning is better or its end.” Another report describes the Prophet saying: “I long for my brothers.” His companions asked: “Are we not your brothers, Messenger of God?” He replied: “You are my companions. My brothers are people who will come after me, believe in me without having seen me, and one of them would desire to see me even in exchange for everything he owns. The work of one of them is equal to the work of seventy of you.” They asked: “Of them or of us?” He said: “Of you.” “Why is that, Messenger of God?” “Because you found helpers in goodness and they found no helpers in it,” or words to that effect, as Ibn ʿAjība himself qualifies the quotation. [XIV-N083] I say: This preference concerns the rewards of deeds. Regarding certainty and gnosis ( اليقين والمعرفة ), the Companions are the best of creation after the prophets, peace be upon them. The evidence is that the Prophet spoke of one person’s work being equal, not of that person’s faith being equal. And God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-110-112-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-110-112-s3","r":"q3-110-112","title":"The Sufis as a community calling to direct witnessing","text":"“You were,” O company of Sufis, “the best community brought forth for humankind”: you enjoin gathering upon God ( الجمع على الله ) and being absent to everything other than Him; you forbid anything that distances one from God and divides the servant from his Master. You believe in God and in what He promised with the faith of witnessing and direct vision ( إيمان الشهود والعيان ), the station of spiritual excellence ( مقام الإحسان ). Al-Qushayrī says in his Risāla : “God has made this company the elect among His friends and preferred them to all His servants after His messengers and prophets.” Al-Junayd said: “If we knew of a knowledge more noble, beneath the canopy of the sky, than the knowledge about which we speak with our companions, I would strive for it even if I had to crawl.” He often recited: The science of Sufism is a science known only To the discerning one who is recognized through the Real; One who does not witness it does not behold it— How should a blind man witness the sunlight? Al-Shaykh al-Ṣiqillī said: “Whoever believes this knowledge belongs to the elect ( الخاصة ); whoever understands it belongs to the elect of the elect ( خاصة الخاصة ); and whoever can express and speak of it is like a star that cannot be reached or a sea that cannot be drained.” In the Iḥyāʾ , when speaking of knowing God and the science of God ( معرفة الله والعلم بالله ), al-Ghazālī says: “The highest rank in that belongs to the prophets, then to the friends of God who know Him, then to scholars deeply established in knowledge, then to the righteous.” He thereby places the friends of God before the scholars. Ibn Rushd says, according to the source cited by Ibn ʿAjība, that what al-Qushayrī and al-Ghazālī say is agreed upon. He adds: “No rational person doubts that those who know God and what perfection must be attributed to Him are better than those who know God’s legal rulings.” Consult the complete discussion in al-Miʿyār . [XIV-N084] The author of al-Mabāḥith says: The argument that sets the Sufis above others Is a strong argument indeed. They follow, more than all other people, The best of all humankind. And then: Two further things establish the proof: That they surely follow the clear road, And what they display of extraordinary gifts, Uncustomary among other people. They have renounced sins and faults, And purified their bodies and hearts. They have attained the reality of faith And walked the pathways of spiritual excellence.","anchor":"en-q3-110-112-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-110-112-s4","r":"q3-110-112","title":"The covenant as an exception to all circumstances","text":"He then called the People of the Book to faith and made light of their power, saying: “Had [the People of the Book] believed …” I say: The exception “except by a cord” ( إلا بحبل ) is from the most general class of circumstances ( أعم الأحوال ): humiliation is laid upon them in every condition save when they are clothed in a protection granted by God and a protection granted by people.","anchor":"en-q3-110-112-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-110-112-s5","r":"q3-110-112","title":"Security, limits on harm and the cause of moral deterioration","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Had the People of the Book believed” with a belief such as yours, “it would have been better for them” than their present condition. Yet they are not all alike: “Among them are believers,” such as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his companions, “but most of them are defiantly disobedient,” rebellious in unbelief and transgression. Do not be awed by them. “They will not harm you, except by causing hurt”—slight harm from the tongue, such as reviling, insult and stirring discord among you. They have no power to fight; “if they fight you” they will be defeated and “turn their backs on you, and then will not be helped” against you. Ibn ʿAjība calls this a prediction of unseen events that subsequently matched what occurred with Banū Qurayẓa, Banū al-Naḍīr, Banū Qaynuqāʿ and Khaybar. In his account, they never raised a victorious standard. Instead, “humiliation has been laid upon them,” shame and abasement surrounding them like a tent spread over its occupants—or adhering to them like the imprint of a stamped coin—“wherever they are found.” They enjoy security only “through a cord from God,” meaning a covenant or guarantee from God, expressed in the dhimma contract ( عقد الذمة ) that God prescribed. When those under it pay the poll tax ( الجزية ), this contract safeguards them: it is forbidden to attack their property, blood or families . The other is “a cord from people,” a covenant granted by other human authorities to those residing under their protection. In sum, humiliation clings to them, and they obtain security only beneath a covenant, either from Muslims or from unbelievers. [XIV-N085] “They have incurred wrath from God,” that is, they have returned deserving it; “poverty has been laid upon them,” encircling them. Jews are generally poor and needy, because their hearts are empty of certainty; poverty and anxiety cling to them, even if they possess the entire world. [Translator’s note: This is the commentator’s historically situated polemic.] [XIV-N085] “That”—humiliation, need and incurred wrath—“is because they rejected God’s signs,” revealed to His messenger or indicating divine unity, “and killed the prophets without right,” with injustice and aggression. Their unbelief, he says, arose from disobedience and crossing God’s bounds: persistence in minor sins leads to major sins, and persistence in major sins leads to unbelief, for sins are the forerunners of unbelief. God protect us.","anchor":"en-q3-110-112-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-110-112-s6","r":"q3-110-112","title":"Hostility to the friends of God and testimony from the author’s own trials","text":"Had the people of outward learning ( أهل العلم الظاهر ) believed in the path of particular realization ( طريق الخصوص ) and humbled themselves before those endowed with special spiritual distinction ( أهل الخصوصية ), it would have been better for them. Their circle of knowledge would have widened and treasuries of understanding opened. Some acknowledge the existence of such particularity but lack the strength to bear its conditions. Most of them deny it and justify themselves by citing someone who said that spiritual training ( التربية ) ended in the eighth Islamic century; they die persisting in denial and disobedience. Yet their denial will not harm you, O spiritual poor ( الفقراء ): they have no power over you because of the protection surrounding you, apart from harm caused by their tongues. Even if visible harm reaches you, God will make you inwardly absent from its pain, as we ourselves have witnessed concerning some of the spiritual poor. If they threaten you with killing and exile, God will generally not help them achieve it. I say: They threatened to beat us, report us to the ruler, and banish us to the land of the Christians, yet they accomplished none of it. Some Sufis have indeed undergone such treatment, which only increased their honour and dignity. One who censures the Sufis, says Ibn ʿAjība, remains in distress, sorrow, humiliation and need because his inward being is ruined of the light of certainty. Criticism of God’s friends is a wrongdoing, whereas belief in them brings care. If one persists in injuring them, one will meet a bad end and incur God’s anger by wronging His friends: “Whoever harms a friend of Mine is on notice of war.” [Translator’s note: Cairo I:396 prints فقد أذن بالحرب , without a first-person verb. This is read here in the attested sense of adhina bi- , “became aware of,” rather than silently supplying ādhantuhu , “I have notified him”; see Lisān al-ʿArab , s.v. أذن .] May God grant us good manners towards them and allow us to die loving them. Amen. [XIV-N086]","anchor":"en-q3-110-112-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-110-112-s7","r":"q3-110-112","title":"","text":"Since some Jews did submit and became good Muslims, God Most High distinguished them as an exception, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-110-112-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-113-115","r":"q3-113-115","title":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people","text":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people 3:113–115","anchor":"unit-q3-113-115"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-113-115-1","r":"q3-113-115","title":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people","text":"لَيْسُوا سَواءً مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ أُمَّةٌ قائِمَةٌ يَتْلُونَ آياتِ اللَّهِ آناءَ اللَّيْلِ وَهُمْ يَسْجُدُونَ (113) يُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَيَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُسارِعُونَ فِي الْخَيْراتِ وَأُولئِكَ مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ (114) وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلَنْ تُكْفَرُوهُ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِالْمُتَّقِينَ (115)","anchor":"ar-q3-113-115-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-113-115-2","r":"q3-113-115","title":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people","text":"قلت: (قائمة) أي: مستقيمة، من أقمت العود فقام، أو قائمة بأمر الله. و (آناء الليل) : ظرف، واحده: (إنّي) ، بكسر الهمزة وسكون النون، كنحى وأنحاء، أو (إني) ، كمِعىً وأمعاء، و (لن تكفروه) أي: لن تحرموه، وعدي (كفر) إلى مفعولين لتضمنه معنى حرم أو منع.","anchor":"ar-q3-113-115-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-113-115-3","r":"q3-113-115","title":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ليس أهل الكتاب سَواءً في الكفر والعدوان، بل منهم أُمَّةٌ أي: طائفة قائِمَةٌ بالعدل مستقيمة في الدين، أو قائمة بأمر الله، أو قائمة في الصلاة يَتْلُونَ آياتِ اللَّهِ في تهجدهم آناءَ اللَّيْلِ أي: في ساعاته، وَهُمْ يَسْجُدُونَ في صلاتهم، أو في صلاة العشاء، لأن أهل الكتاب لا يصلونها، لما روى أنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أخَّرها، ثم خَرَج، فإذا الناسُ يَنْتَظُرونَها، فقال: «أبشروا فَإِنَّه لَيْسَ مِنْ أَهْل الأَرض أحدٌ يُصَلِّي في هَذِهِ السّاعَةِ غَيْرُكُم» .","anchor":"ar-q3-113-115-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-113-115-4","r":"q3-113-115","title":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people","text":"ثم وصفهم بالإيمان فقال: يُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَيَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُسارِعُونَ فِي الْخَيْراتِ، وهو عبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه ممن أسلم من اليهود، فقد وصفهم الله تعالى بخصائص لم توجد في اليهود، فإنهم منحرفون عن الحق غير متعبدين، مشركون بالله ملحدون في صفاته، يصفون اليوم الآخر بغير صفاته، مداهنون في الأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر، متباطئون عن الخيرات، بخلاف ما وصف به من أسلم منهم، وَأُولئِكَ الموصوفون بتلك الصفات مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ أي: ممن صلحت أحوالهم عند الله، واستوجبوا رضاه وثناءه، وهذه عادة الله مع خلقه، من تقرب إليه شبراً تقرب إليه ذراعاً. ولذلك قال: وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلَنْ تُكْفَرُوهُ أي: فلن تحرموا ثوابه. ولن تجحدوا جزاءه، بل يشكره لكم ويجزيكم عليه، سَمى الحرمان كفراناً كما سمى العطاء شكرا. وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِالْمُتَّقِينَ فلا يخفى عليه مقاماتهم في التقوى. وفيه إشعار بأن التقوى مبدأ الخير وأحسن الأعمال، وأن الفائزين عند الله هم أهل التقوى. رزقنا الله منها الحظ الأوفر بمنِّه. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-113-115-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-113-115-5","r":"q3-113-115","title":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people","text":"الإشارة: ليس أهل العلم سواء، بل منهم من جعله شبكةً يصطاد به الدنيا، يبيع دينه بعرض قليل، وهم علماء السوء وقضاة الجور، ومنهم من قرأه لله وعلَّمه لله، فأفنى عُمره في تعليمه وتقييده، ومنهم من صرف همته إلى جمعه وتأليفه، ومنهم من صرف همته إلى العمل به فالتحق بالعباد والزُّهاد، يَتْلُونَ آياتِ اللَّهِ آناءَ اللَّيْلِ وَهُمْ يَسْجُدُونَ ومنهم من حرره وحققه، ثم توجه إلى علم الباطن وصحب العارفين، فكان من المقربين، فهؤلاء كلهم يُسارِعُونَ فِي الْخَيْراتِ وَأُولئِكَ مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ، فيقال لهم: وما تفعلوا من خير فلن تكفروه والله عليم بالمتقين.","anchor":"ar-q3-113-115-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-113-115-6","r":"q3-113-115","title":"3:113–115 · The upright People of the Book and the successive callings of learned people","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى أضدادهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-113-115-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-113-115-s1","r":"q3-113-115","title":"The upright community, hours of night and “denying” recompense","text":"I say: “Upright” ( قائمة ) means straight or sound ( مستقيمة ), as in aqamtu al-ʿūd fa-qāma, “I set the stick straight, so it stood upright”; or it means “carrying out God’s command.” “Through the hours of the night” ( آناء الليل ) is an adverbial time expression ( ظرف ); the singular is iny ( إِنْي ), with kasra on the hamza and an unvowelled nūn, like niḥy/anḥāʾ ( نِحْي/أَنْحَاء ); or inā ( إِنًى ), like miʿā/amʿāʾ ( مِعًى/أَمْعَاء ), according to the forms transmitted here. “You shall not be denied it” ( لن تكفروه ) means “you shall not be deprived of it.” Kafara is here used with two objects ( مفعولين ) because it incorporates the meaning of “deprive” ( حرم ) or “withhold” ( منع ). [XIV-N087]","anchor":"en-q3-113-115-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-113-115-s2","r":"q3-113-115","title":"The worshippers among the People of the Book","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: The People of the Book “are not all alike” in unbelief and hostility. Rather, among them is “a community,” that is, a group, “upright,” practicing justice and steadfast in religion, or rising to fulfil God’s command, or standing in prayer, “reciting God’s signs” during their night vigil “through the hours of the night,” meaning its periods, “while they prostrate” in their prayers. Or the reference is to the night prayer ( صلاة العشاء ), which the People of the Book do not perform: it is related that the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, once delayed that prayer, then came out while the people were waiting and said, “Rejoice, for there is no one among the inhabitants of earth praying at this hour other than you.” [XIV-N088] He then describes them through faith: “They believe in God and the Last Day, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and hasten to good deeds.” They are ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his companions who accepted Islam from among the Jews. God Most High has described them with distinctive qualities not found among the Jews: the latter deviate from the truth and are not devoted to worship; they associate partners with God and deviate concerning His attributes; they describe the Last Day with qualities other than its own; they compromise in enjoining right and forbidding wrong; and they are slow to do good—unlike the description given of those among them who embraced Islam. [Translator’s note: These generalized contrasts belong to the commentator’s polemic.] “They are among the righteous”: those whose condition is sound before God, who deserve His pleasure and praise. Such is God’s practice towards His servants: when a servant draws near to Him by a handspan, He draws near by an arm’s length. [XIV-N088] Therefore He says: “Whatever good you do, you shall not be denied it.” You shall not be deprived of its reward or have its recompense refused; God will recognize it gratefully and repay you for it. Denial of recompense is called “ingratitude” ( كفران ), just as bestowal is called “gratitude” ( شكر ). “God knows those who are mindful of Him”: their stations in Godfearingness ( مقاماتهم في التقوى ) are not hidden from Him. This intimates that Godfearingness is the beginning of goodness and among the best of works, and that the successful before God are the people of Godfearingness. May God, through His bounty, grant us its fullest share. Amen.","anchor":"en-q3-113-115-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-113-115-s3","r":"q3-113-115","title":"Learning for gain, teaching, action and realization","text":"The people of learning are not all alike. Some make knowledge into a net with which to catch the world, selling their religion for a small worldly advantage: these are corrupt scholars and unjust judges. Others study knowledge for God and teach it for God, spending their lives teaching and recording it. Some devote their aspiration to gathering and composing it; others devote themselves to acting upon it and become worshippers and ascetics, “reciting God’s signs through the hours of the night while they prostrate.” Still others refine and realize it, then turn towards inward knowledge ( علم الباطن ), accompany the knowers ( العارفين ) and become among those brought near ( المقربين ). All these “hasten to good deeds and are among the righteous.” To them it is said: “Whatever good you do shall not be denied you; God knows those who are mindful of Him.”","anchor":"en-q3-113-115-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-113-115-s4","r":"q3-113-115","title":"","text":"The Real Most High then mentioned their opposites, saying:","anchor":"en-q3-113-115-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-116","r":"q3-116","title":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God","text":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God 3:116","anchor":"unit-q3-116"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-116-1","r":"q3-116","title":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَنْ تُغْنِيَ عَنْهُمْ أَمْوالُهُمْ وَلا أَوْلادُهُمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ شَيْئاً وَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (116)","anchor":"ar-q3-116-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-116-2","r":"q3-116","title":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وجحدوا ما جاء به الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم، (لن تُغني عنهم أموالُهم ولا أولادهم من) عذاب اللَّهِ شَيْئاً وَأُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ أي: مُلاَزِمُوها، كَمُلاَزَمَةِ الرجل لصاحبه، هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-116-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-116-3","r":"q3-116","title":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God","text":"الإشارة: إِنَّ الذين كفروا بالخصوصية عند أهل زمانهم، وفاتهم اقتباس أنوارهم، لن تُغني عنهم أموالُهم ولا أولادهم ولا علومهم مما فاتهم من معرفة الله شيئًا، ماذا وَجَدَ مَنْ فَقَدَ الله؟ وماذا فقد من وجد الله؟! قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-116-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-116-4","r":"q3-116","title":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God","text":"لكل شيء إذا فارقْتَهُ عِوَضٌ ... وَلَيْسَ لله إنْ فَارقَْتَ مِنْ عِوَضِ","anchor":"ar-q3-116-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-116-5","r":"q3-116","title":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God","text":"ولا طريق لمعرفة الحق المعرفة الخاصة- أعني معرفة العيان- إلا صحبة أهل الشهود والعيان، فكلُّ من أنكرهم كان غايته الحرمان، ولزمته البطالة والخذلان، وجَرَّب، ففي التجريب علم الحقائق، ومن حُرم صحبتهم لا ينفك عن نار القطيعة وعذاب الحجاب، وعنت الحرص والتعب، عائذاً بالله من ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q3-116-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-116-6","r":"q3-116","title":"3:116 · Wealth, children and the loss of direct knowledge of God","text":"ثم ضرب مثلا لأعمال الكفار، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-116-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-116-s1","r":"q3-116","title":"Possessions offer no exemption from divine judgment","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Those who disbelieve,” denying what the Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, has brought, will find that “neither their wealth nor their children will avail them anything” against God’s punishment. “They are the companions of the Fire”: they remain inseparable from it, as a man remains with his companion; “they abide therein.” [XIV-N089]","anchor":"en-q3-116-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-116-s2","r":"q3-116","title":"Denying the friends of God and losing the opportunity for witnessing","text":"Those who deny the distinctive spiritual realization ( الخصوصية ) of the people of their time, thereby missing the opportunity to receive some of their lights, will find that neither their wealth, their children, nor even their acquired sciences can compensate for the knowledge of God ( معرفة الله ) they have missed. What has the one who lost God found? And what has the one who found God lost? The poet says: For everything, once you part from it, there is a replacement; But if you part from God, there is nothing that can replace Him. There is no path to the special knowledge of the Real ( معرفة الحق المعرفة الخاصة )—by which I mean direct, first-hand knowledge ( معرفة العيان )—except through companionship with people of witnessing and direct vision ( أهل الشهود والعيان ). Thus whoever rejects them has deprivation as his ultimate lot, and idleness and abandonment cling to him. Let him put it to the test: experiment discloses the realities. Whoever is deprived of their companionship remains exposed to the fire of separation ( نار القطيعة ), the torment of veiling ( عذاب الحجاب ), and the misery of grasping effort. We seek refuge in God from that.","anchor":"en-q3-116-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-116-s3","r":"q3-116","title":"","text":"He then offered a similitude for the works of the disbelievers.","anchor":"en-q3-116-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-117","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds 3:117","anchor":"unit-q3-117"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-1","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"مَثَلُ ما يُنْفِقُونَ فِي هذِهِ الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا كَمَثَلِ رِيحٍ فِيها صِرٌّ أَصابَتْ حَرْثَ قَوْمٍ ظَلَمُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ فَأَهْلَكَتْهُ وَما ظَلَمَهُمُ اللَّهُ وَلكِنْ أَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُونَ (117)","anchor":"ar-q3-117-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-2","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"قلت: في الكلام حذف، أي: مثل تلف ما ينفقون كمثل إتلاف ريح ... الخ، و (الصر) : البرد الشديد، أو ريح فيها صوت وبرد، أو السموم الحارة.","anchor":"ar-q3-117-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-3","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: مثل ما يُنفق الكفار، قربة أو مفاخرة وسمعة، أو ما ينفق سفلة اليهود على أحبارهم، أو المنافقون رياء وخوفاً، كَمَثَلِ رِيحٍ","anchor":"ar-q3-117-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-4","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"فيها برد شديد أَصابَتْ حَرْثَ قَوْمٍ","anchor":"ar-q3-117-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-5","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"أي: زرعهم، فأتلفته وأهلكته، والمراد: تشبيه نفقتهم وأعمالهم في تلفه وضياعه وعدم الانتفاع به، بحرث كفار، ضربته ريح فيها برد فاجتاحته، فأصبح صعيداً زلقاً، ولم تبق فيه منفعة في الدنيا والآخرة، وَما ظَلَمَهُمُ اللَّهُ","anchor":"ar-q3-117-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-6","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"بأن ضيع أعمالهم من غير سبب، ولكنهم ظلموا أنفسهم بارتكاب الكفر الذي أحبط أعمالهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-117-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-7","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن لم يحقق مقام الإخلاص، ولم يصحب أهل التخليص والاختصاص، لا تنفك أعماله من علل، ولا أحواله من دخل، فأعماله فارغة خفيفة، أقل ريح تقلعها وتسقطها عن درجة الاعتبار، وما زالت العامة تقول: الصحيح يصح، والخاوي يدريه الريح. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-117-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-117-8","r":"q3-117","title":"3:117 · The wind that destroys a harvest; sincerity and the diseases of deeds","text":"ثم حذَّر الحق تعالى من مخالطة أهل التخليط، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-117-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-117-s1","r":"q3-117","title":"An implied verb of destruction and the meanings of ṣirr (صِرّ)","text":"I say: An ellipsis ( حذف ) is present in the discourse: “The likeness of the loss of what they spend is like the destruction brought about by a wind,” and so forth. The ṣirr ( الصِّرّ ) is piercing cold. Or the phrase signifies a wind containing a sound and cold; or a scorching, poisonous hot wind ( السموم الحارة ). [XIV-N090]","anchor":"en-q3-117-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-117-s2","r":"q3-117","title":"The expenditure that yields no lasting benefit","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: What the unbelievers expend, whether as a devotional offering ( قربة ) or for boasting and reputation ( مفاخرة وسمعة ); or what the lowly among the Jews expend upon their learned authorities; or what the hypocrites expend ostentatiously ( رياء ) or out of fear—is like a wind containing severe cold that strikes the cultivated land ( حَرْث ) of some people, that is, their growing crops, and ruins and destroys them. The intended comparison is between their expenditure and deeds, in their perishing, being wasted and bringing them no benefit, and the cultivation of unbelievers struck by a freezing wind that lays it waste. It becomes a smooth, bare expanse, yielding no benefit in this world or the next. God did not wrong them by letting their works go to waste without a cause: they wronged themselves by committing the unbelief that made their works fruitless. [XIV-N091]","anchor":"en-q3-117-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-117-s3","r":"q3-117","title":"Acts unpurified by sincere intention","text":"Whoever has not realized the station of sincerity ( مقام الإخلاص ) and has not accompanied the people of purification and special spiritual realization ( أهل التخليص والاختصاص ) cannot keep his works free of hidden defects ( علل ), nor his spiritual states free of adulteration ( دخل ). His works are empty and light; the slightest wind uproots them and casts them down from the rank of being taken into account. Ordinary people have long said: “What is sound stays sound; what is hollow the wind carries away.” And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q3-117-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-117-s4","r":"q3-117","title":"","text":"The Real then warned against association with people who bring about confusion and mixture.","anchor":"en-q3-117-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-118-120","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets 3:118–120","anchor":"unit-q3-118-120"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-1","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَتَّخِذُوا بِطانَةً مِنْ دُونِكُمْ لا يَأْلُونَكُمْ خَبالاً وَدُّوا ما عَنِتُّمْ قَدْ بَدَتِ الْبَغْضاءُ مِنْ أَفْواهِهِمْ وَما تُخْفِي صُدُورُهُمْ أَكْبَرُ قَدْ بَيَّنَّا لَكُمُ الْآياتِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ (118) ها أَنْتُمْ أُولاءِ تُحِبُّونَهُمْ وَلا يُحِبُّونَكُمْ وَتُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْكِتابِ كُلِّهِ وَإِذا لَقُوكُمْ قالُوا آمَنَّا وَإِذا خَلَوْا عَضُّوا عَلَيْكُمُ الْأَنامِلَ مِنَ الْغَيْظِ قُلْ مُوتُوا بِغَيْظِكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ بِذاتِ الصُّدُورِ (119) إِنْ تَمْسَسْكُمْ حَسَنَةٌ تَسُؤْهُمْ وَإِنْ تُصِبْكُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَفْرَحُوا بِها وَإِنْ تَصْبِرُوا وَتَتَّقُوا لا يَضُرُّكُمْ كَيْدُهُمْ شَيْئاً إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ مُحِيطٌ (120)","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-2","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"قلت: بطانة الرجل: خواصه الذين يطلعهم على باطنه وسره، وسميت بطانة تشبيهاً لها بالثوب الذي يلي بطنه كالشعار. قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «الأَنْصَارَ شِعَارٌ والنَّاسُ دِثَارٌ» . وهي اسم تطلق على المفرد والجمع والمذكر والمؤنث. والألو: التقصير، وأصله: أن يتعدى بالحرف، تقول: لا آلو في نصحك أي: لا أقصر فيه. ثم عدي إلى مفعولين، كقولهم: لا آلوك نصحاً، على تضمن معنى المنع أو النقص. والخبال: الفساد.","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-3","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"و (ما عنتم) : مصدرية، والعنت: التعب والمشقة، والأنامل: جمع أنملة- بضم الميم وفتحها-، والضير والضر واحد. ومضارع الأول: يضير، والثاني: يضر، وهو هنا مجزوم، وأصله: يضرُركم، نقلت حركة الراء إلى الضاد، وضمت الراء، إتباعاً لحركة الضاد طلباً للمشاكلة.","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-4","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَتَّخِذُوا بِطانَةً أي: أصدقاء وأصفياء، تطلعونهم على سركم، وهم مِنْ دُونِكُمْ ليسوا على دينكم، فإنهم لا يَأْلُونَكُمْ خَبالًا أي: لا يقصرون جهدَهم في إدخال الفساد بينكم بالتخليط والنميمة وإطلاع الكفار على عورتكم. نزلت في رجال من المسلمين، كانوا يصلون رجالاً من اليهود لما كان بينهم من القرابة والصداقة، أو في المنافقين كان يصلهم بعض المسلمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-5","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"ثم وصفهم بأوصاف توجب التنفير منهم فقال: وَدُّوا ما عَنِتُّمْ أي: تمنوا عنتكم وهلاككم وضلالكم، قَدْ بَدَتِ الْبَغْضاءُ مِنْ أَفْواهِهِمْ أي: ظهرت أمارة العداوة من أفواههم بالوقيعة في المسلمين، أو بإطلاع المشركين على عوراتهم، أو في كلامهم مع المسلمين بالغيظ، لأنهم لا يتمالكون أنفسهم لفرط بغضهم، وَما تُخْفِي","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-6","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"صُدُورُهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-7","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"من العداوة والبغضاء، أَكْبَرُ مما أظهروه، لأن ظهوره منهم ليس عن روية واختيار، بل عن غلبة غيظ واضطرار. قَدْ بَيَّنَّا لَكُمُ أيها المؤمنون الْآياتِ الدالة على مجانبة الكافرين وموالاة المؤمنين، إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ ما يبين لكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-8","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"ها أَنْتُمْ يا هؤلاء المخاطبين تُحِبُّونَهُمْ لما بينكم من المصاهرة والصداقة، وَلا يُحِبُّونَكُمْ لما بينكم من مخالفة الدين، أو تريدون لهم الإسلام وهم يريدون لكم الكفر، وأنتم تُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْكِتابِ أي: بجنس الكتب، (كله) أي: بالكتب كلها، وهم لا يؤمنون بكتابكم، فكيف تحبونهم وهم يكذبون كتابكم ورسولكم؟ وهم أيضاً ينافقونكم إِذا لَقُوكُمْ قالُوا آمَنَّا وَإِذا خَلَوْا مع أنفسهم عَضُّوا عَلَيْكُمُ الْأَنامِلَ مِنَ الْغَيْظِ لما يرون من ائتلاف المؤمنين، ولم يجدوا سبيلاً إلى التشفي فيكم، وهذه كناية عن شدة حقدهم، وإن لم يكن ثَمَّ عض في الخارج.","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-9","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"قال لهم الحق جل جلاله: قُلْ لهم يا محمد: مُوتُوا بِغَيْظِكُمْ فإنما ضرر غيظكم عليكم، أو دوموا على غيظكم حتى تموتوا عليه، فإن مادة الإسلام لا تزال تنمو حتى تهلكوا، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ بِذاتِ الصُّدُورِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-10","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"بحقيقة ما في قلوبكم من البغضاء والحَنَقَ(1) ، أو بما في القلوب من خير أو شر. هو من مقول الرسول لهم، أو من كلام الله تعالى، استئناف، أي: لا تعجب من إطلاعي إياك على أسرارهم، فإني عليم بالأخفى من ضمائرهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-11","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"ومن فرط عداوتهم أنهم إِنْ تَمْسَسْكُمْ حَسَنَةٌ كنصر وغنيمة تَسُؤْهُمْ أي: تحزنهم، وَإِنْ تُصِبْكُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ كهزيمة أو قتل أو إصابة عدو منكم او اختلاف بينكم، يَفْرَحُوا بِها، وَإِنْ تَصْبِرُوا على عداوتهم وأذاهم، وتخافوا ربكم، وَتَتَّقُوا ما نهاكم عنه، لا يَضُرُّكُمْ كَيْدُهُمْ شَيْئاً، بفضل الله وحفظه، الموعود للصابرين والمتقين، إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا. ومن كان الحق معه لا يضره شيء، إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ مُحِيطٌ لا يخفى عليه ما يعمل أهل الكفر من العداوة والحقد، فيجازيهم عليه.","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-12","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"الإشارة: لا ينبغي لأهل الخصوصية أن يتخذوا بطانة من دونهم من العامة حتى يطلعوهم على سرهم، فإن الإطلاع على السر، ولو كان غير الخصوصية، كله ضعف في العقل ووهن في الرأي، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-13","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"(من أطْلَعَ الناسَ على سره ... استحقَّ الكيَّ على جَبْهَتِه)","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-14","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"وأما سر الربوبية فإفشاؤه لغير أهله حرام، والعامة مضادون لأهل الخصوصية، لا يألونهم خبالاً في قلوبهم وتشتيتاً لفكرتهم، إذا صحبوهم يودون أن لو كانوا مثلهم في العنت وتعب الأسباب، فإذا ظهر بالفقراء نقص أو خلل","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-15","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"ظهرت البغضاء من أفواههم، وما تخفي صدورهم أكبر، فإن كنتم أيها الفقراء تحبون لهم الخير فإنهم بعكس ذلك، وإن كنتم تقرون شريعتهم فإنهم لا يؤمنون بحقيقتكم، بل ينكرونها عليكم، ومنهم من يتصف بالنفاق، إذا لقي أهل الخصوصية أظهر التصديق والمحبة، وإذا خلا مع العامة أظهر العداوة والحَنَق، وإن تمسسكم أيها الفقراء حسنة، كعز وفتح وشهود ومعرفة تَسؤْهم، وإن تصبكم سيئة كمحنة أو بلية، يفرحوا بها، وإن تصبروا على أذاهم وجفوتهم، وتتقوا شهود السوى فيهم، لا يضركم كيدهم شيئاً (إن الله بما يعملون محيط) .","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-118-120-16","r":"q3-118-120","title":"3:118–120 · Intimate confidants, the concealment of enmity and the safeguarding of spiritual secrets","text":"ولما فرغ الحق تعالى من معاتبة أهل الكتابين، شرع فى معاتبة بعض المسلمين لما وقع لهم في غزوة أحد من الفشل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-118-120-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-118-120-s1","r":"q3-118-120","title":"Biṭāna (بِطانة), alw (أَلْو), ʿanat (عَنَت), and the jussive lā yaḍurrukum","text":"I say: A man’s biṭāna ( بطانة ) comprises his intimates, whom he allows to see his inner affairs and secrets. The word is derived by comparison with the garment next to his belly—the inner garment ( شِعار ). The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said, as quoted here: “The Helpers ( الأنصار ) are the close garment ( شعار ), whereas other people are the outer covering ( دثار ).” This noun can designate an individual or a group, masculine or feminine alike. Alw ( الألو ) means failing or falling short. Ordinarily the verb is construed with a preposition: “I do not fall short in counselling you” ( لا آلو في نصحك ). Here it is made to govern two objects, as in “I will not deprive you of counsel” ( لا آلوك نصحاً ), through its implication of preventing or diminishing. Khabāl ( الخبال ) is corruption or ruin. In “what brings you hardship” ( ما عنتم ), mā ( ما ) is a particle converting the clause to a verbal-noun sense ( مصدرية ); ʿanat ( العنت ) signifies fatigue and hardship. Anāmil ( الأنامل ) is the plural of anmula ( أنملة ), pronounced with either ḍamma or fatḥa on the mīm. Ḍayr ( الضير ) and ḍurr ( الضر ) mean much the same: their imperfect verbs are respectively yaḍīru ( يضير ) and yaḍurru ( يضر ). The latter occurs here in the jussive ( مجزوم ). Its underlying form is yaḍrurkum ( يضرُركم ); the vowel of the first rāʾ is transferred to the ḍād and the remaining rāʾ is given ḍamma to agree with the ḍād's vowel, producing a phonetic harmony ( مشاكلة ). [XIV-N092]","anchor":"en-q3-118-120-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-118-120-s2","r":"q3-118-120","title":"The reported setting and exposure of concealed resentment","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “O you who believe, do not take intimate confidants ( بطانة )”—friends and chosen intimates to whom you disclose your secrets—from people outside your religious community, since “they will not spare any effort to corrupt your affairs,” striving to introduce disorder through confusion and malicious tales, and revealing your vulnerable places to unbelievers. According to one report on the occasion of revelation, it concerned Muslims who maintained close ties with certain Jewish men through kinship and friendship. According to another, it concerned hypocrites whom some Muslims associated with closely. [XIV-N093] He then describes them with qualities designed to repel such intimacy: “They wish you hardship,” meaning your suffering, ruin and misguidance. “Hatred has already appeared from their mouths”: signs of hostility have surfaced through attacks on Muslims, revelation of their vulnerabilities to the idolaters, or words of rage addressed to Muslims. The force of their hatred leaves them unable to contain themselves. “What their breasts conceal” of hostility and rancour “is greater” than what has slipped into public expression, because their spoken displays spring not from careful deliberation or free choice, but from overpowering rage. “We have made the signs clear to you,” O believers—those indicating the need to avoid unbelievers and be loyal to the faithful—“if you understand” what has been set before you. “Here you are,” those being addressed: “You love them” because of marriage connections or friendship, “and they do not love you” because of your religious differences. Alternatively, you desire Islam for them, while they desire disbelief for you. You “believe in the Book,” that is, in the category of revealed books—and “all of it,” meaning all the revealed books—while they do not believe in your Book. How, Ibn ʿAjība asks, can you love those who reject your Book and Messenger? They also dissemble in your presence: “When they meet you they say, ‘We believe,’” but “when they are alone” they “bite their fingertips in rage” at the concord they see among believers and their own inability to gain satisfaction against you. This is a figurative expression ( كناية ) for the intensity of their resentment, even if no physical biting actually occurs. The Real says to the Prophet, “Say to them, ‘Die in your rage!’” That rage can injure only yourselves—or remain in it until you die, for the strength of Islam will continue to grow until you perish. “God knows what lies in breasts”: the reality of the animosity and wrath in their hearts, or all the good and evil that hearts contain. This may be part of what the Messenger says to them; alternatively it may be God’s own renewed statement ( استئناف ): Do not be astonished that I disclosed their secrets to you, for I know even what lies more deeply hidden within them. In the excess of their hostility, “If good touches you,” such as victory or spoils, it saddens them. “If something bad befalls you,” such as defeat, death, an enemy’s attack or dissension among you, they rejoice. “But if you are patient” in the face of their hostility and injury, “and are mindful of God” and abstain from what He has forbidden, “their plot will not harm you at all,” through God’s gracious protection promised to those who patiently persevere and remain mindful. “God is with the patient”; and “God is with those who are mindful.” Whoever has the Real with him cannot be harmed by anything. “God encompasses what they do”: the deeds of the unbelievers, their hatred and hostility, do not escape His knowledge, and He will recompense them accordingly.","anchor":"en-q3-118-120-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-118-120-s3","r":"q3-118-120","title":"The discipline of confidence among the spiritually realized","text":"It does not befit the people of special realization ( أهل الخصوصية ) to choose intimates outside their company from the common people ( العامة ) and unveil their secret ( سرّ ) to them. Indeed, divulging secrets, even when they are not secrets of special realization, betrays a weak intellect and poor judgment. Hence the saying: Whoever makes his private secret known to people Deserves to be branded upon the forehead. To reveal the secret of Lordship ( سر الربوبية ) to those unfit for it, however, is forbidden. The common people stand opposed, in Ibn ʿAjība’s spiritual analogy, to the people of special realization: they do not cease to sow corruption in their hearts and disperse their focused reflection. If they accompany them, they wish that the Sufis might live as they do, in hardship and the toil of secondary causes ( تعب الأسباب ). If some deficiency or flaw appears among the spiritual poor ( الفقراء ), enmity appears in the critics’ speech, and the feelings they conceal are worse. You, spiritual poor, desire good for them, yet they desire the opposite for you. You acknowledge their adherence to the revealed Law ( شريعة ), but they do not acknowledge your spiritual reality ( حقيقة ); instead they deny it to you. Some behave hypocritically: when they meet the people of special realization they profess belief and affection, but when alone with the crowd they manifest hostility and resentment. If good touches you, O spiritual poor—honour, an opening ( فتح ), witnessing ( شهود ) or knowledge of God ( معرفة )—it distresses them; if an ordeal or calamity befalls you, they rejoice. But if you patiently endure their harshness and estrangement, and guard against the perception of anything-other-than-God ( شهود السوى ) in them, their plotting will not harm you. “God encompasses all that they do.” [XIV-N094]","anchor":"en-q3-118-120-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-118-120-s4","r":"q3-118-120","title":"","text":"Having concluded His reproach of the two People of the Book, the Real begins to rebuke some Muslims for the faltering that occurred at the Battle of Uḥud.","anchor":"en-q3-118-120-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-121-122","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle 3:121–122","anchor":"unit-q3-121-122"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-1","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"وَإِذْ غَدَوْتَ مِنْ أَهْلِكَ تُبَوِّئُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ مَقاعِدَ لِلْقِتالِ وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ (121) إِذْ هَمَّتْ طائِفَتانِ مِنْكُمْ أَنْ تَفْشَلا وَاللَّهُ وَلِيُّهُما وَعَلَى اللَّهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ (122)","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-2","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر يا محمد حين غَدَوْتَ مِنْ أَهْلِكَ من منزل عائشة، الذي نَزَلْتَ فيه بأحد، حين خرجت بها، حال كونك تُبَوِّئُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أي: تهيئ لهم، مَقاعِدَ لِلْقِتالِ أي: مواقف وأماكن يقفون فيها للحرب وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ لأقوالكم، عَلِيمٌ بإخلاصكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-3","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"قال الواقدي: خرج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم من منزل عائشة- رضي الله عنها- ماشياً على رجليه إلى أُحد، فجعل يصف أصحابه للقتال كأنما يقوم بهم القدح(1) . إن رأى صدراً خارجاً، قال: تأخر. وذلك أن المشركين نزلوا بأحد، يوم الأربعاء، فلما سمع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بنزولهم استشار أصحابه، ودعا عبد الله بن أبي بن سلول- ولم يدْعُه قط قبلها- فاستشاره، فقال عبد الله بن أبي وأكثر الأنصار: يا رسول الله أَقِمْ بالمدينة ولا تخرج إليهم، فو الله ما خرجنا منها إلى عدو قط إلا أصاب منا، ولا دخل علينا إلا أصبنا منه، فكيف وأنت فينا! فدعهم يا رسول الله، فإن أقاموا أقاموا بشر محبس، وإن دخلوا قاتلهم الرجال في وجوههم، ورماهم النساء والصبيان بالحجارة، وإن رجعوا رجعوا خاسئين. فأعجب النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم هذا الرأي، وقال بعض أصحابه: يا رسول الله اخرج بنا إلى هذه الأكْلُب(2) لا يرون أنا جَبُنَّا عنهم وضعفنا. فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «إِنِّي رأيتُ في منامِي بَقَراً تذبح، فأولتها ناساً من أصحابي يُقتلون، ورأيت في ذُبابِ سَيْفي ثلماً(3) ، فأولتها هزيمةً، ورأيت أني أدخل يدي في درع حصينة، فأولتها المدينة، فإن رأيتُمْ أن تُقيموا بالمدينة وتدعوهم فافعلوا» . فقال رجال ممن فاتهم بدر، وأكرمهم الله بالشهادة يوم أحد: اخرج بنا","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-4","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"إلى أعدائنا، وبالغوا، حتى دخل النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ولبس لأمته(1) . فلما رأوه قد لبس سلاحه ندموا، وقالوا: بئس ما صنعنا، نشير على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم والوحي يأتيه، فقاموا واعتذروا إليه. وقالوا: اصنع ما رأيت، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «لا يَنْبَغِي لنَبِي أَنْ يلبَس لأمَتَهُ فيَضَعَهَا حتَى يُقاتِلَ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-5","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"فخرج بعد صلاة الجمعة، وأصبح بشعب من أُحُد، يوم السبت للنصف من شوال، سنة ثلاث من الهجرة، ونزل في عدوة من الوادي، وجعل ظهره وعسكره إلى أحد، وسوى صفهم كما تقدم، وأمر عبد الله بن جبير على الرماة، وقال: انضحوا عنا بالنبل، لا يأتونا من خلفنا، فكان من أمر الله ما كان، على ما يأتي(2) .","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-6","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"وخرج مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم في غزوة أحد زهاء ألف، ووعدهم النصر إن صبروا، فلما بلغوا الشواط- موضع- انخزل ابنُ أُبيّ في ثلاثمائة، وقال: علام نقتل أنفسنا! فتبعهم أبو جابر السلمي، فقال: أُنشدكم الله في نبيكم وأنفسكم. فقال ابن أُبيّ: لو نعلم قتالاً لاتبعناكم، وهمت بنو حارثة وبنو سلمة بالانصراف معه، فثبتوا مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فذكرهم نعمته بقوله: إِذْ هَمَّتْ طائِفَتانِ مِنْكُمْ أَنْ تَفْشَلا وَاللَّهُ وَلِيُّهُما وناصرهما، حيث عصمهما من اتباع المنافقين، قال جابر: (ما يسرنا أنها لم تنزل، لقوله: وَاللَّهُ وَلِيُّهُما) فبنو سلمة من الخزرج، وبنو حارثة من الأوس، وَعَلَى اللَّهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ لا على غيره، إذ لا ناصر غيره.","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-7","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"الإشارة: من شأن شيوخ التربية أن يَدُلُّوا المريدين على محاربة النفوس ومقاتلتها، ويطلعوهم على دسائسها ومخادعتها، ليهيئوا لهم بذلك مقاعد لقتالها، والله مطلع على إخلاصهم ونياتهم، فمنهم من يمل ويكل، فيرجع إلى وطن عوائده، ومنهم من يصبر حتى يفوز بالغنيمة العظمى والسعادة القصوى، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-8","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"وبَالَغَوا في الجدِّ حتى مَلَّ أكثرهُم ... وعَانَقَ المجْدَ مَنْ وَافَى ومَنْ صَبَرَا","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-9","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"قال بعضهم: انتهى سير السائرين إلى الظفر بنفوسهم، فإن ظفروا بها وصلوا. هـ. ومنهم من يلحقه الملل والفشل فيهم بالانصراف والرجوع، ثم يثبته الله تعالى وينصره، فيلحق بالصابرين السابقين، وعمدة المريد في مجاهدة نفسه: التوكل على الله والاعتماد عليه دون شيء سواه «من علامة النجح في النهايات: الرجوع إلى الله في البدايات» . وَعَلَى اللَّهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-121-122-10","r":"q3-121-122","title":"3:121–122 · Uḥud: consultation, steadfastness and the guides who prepare the soul for struggle","text":"ثم ذكّر أهل أحد بما وقع لهم يوم بدر من النصر والظفر مع قلتهم ليثبتوا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-121-122-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-121-122-s1","r":"q3-121-122","title":"The dispositions at the beginning of Uḥud","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: Remember, O Muḥammad, when you went forth early from your household—from ʿĀʾisha’s lodging, where you were staying at Uḥud, having gone there with her—while you were “assigning the believers positions for battle,” arranging the positions where they would stand and fight. “God is Hearing” of your utterances and “Knowing” of your sincerity. Al-Wāqidī relates that the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, walked from ʿĀʾisha’s lodging to Uḥud and arranged the Companions for fighting as carefully as one straightens an arrow-shaft. When he saw a chest projecting out beyond the line, he said, “Step back.” The idolaters had encamped at Uḥud on Wednesday. Upon learning of their arrival, the Prophet consulted his Companions, and invited ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl for consultation—something he had not done before. Ibn Ubayy and most of the Helpers said: “Messenger of God, remain in Madīna; do not march out to them. By God, whenever we have gone out from it to meet an enemy, that enemy has inflicted losses on us; and whenever an enemy has entered it, we have inflicted losses on him. How much more so with you among us? Leave them! If they stay, they stay in a very bad place of confinement; if they enter, our men will fight them face-to-face, while our women and children cast stones at them; and if they retreat, they will go back humbled.” The Prophet approved this judgment. [XIV-N095] Other Companions urged him: “Messenger of God, lead us out against those dogs, so that they do not think we have proved cowardly or weak before them.” The Prophet replied: “I saw in my dream cattle being slaughtered, and interpreted them as men from my Companions who would be killed. I saw a chip at the point of my sword, and interpreted it as defeat. I saw myself placing my hand inside a strong coat of mail, and interpreted it as Madīna. If you think it best to remain in Madīna and leave the enemy where they are, do so.” [XIV-N096] Some men who had missed Badr, whom God would honour with martyrdom at Uḥud, insisted upon marching out against the enemy. They pressed the case until the Prophet entered and put on his coat of armour ( لأمة ). When they saw him armed they regretted their insistence, saying: “We did badly in advising the Prophet when revelation comes to him.” They stood and apologised: “Do whatever seems best to you.” The Prophet replied: “A prophet should not put on his coat of mail and then take it off until he has fought.” [XIV-N096] He departed after the Friday prayer and was at the ravine of Uḥud by Saturday, the middle of Shawwāl, in the third year after the Hijra. He took position on one side of the valley, with Uḥud behind himself and his camp, and straightened the ranks as already described. He appointed ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jubayr to command the archers, instructing them: “Drive them off from us with arrows; do not let them reach us from behind.” Then what God decreed came to pass, as will be related subsequently. About one thousand men marched out with the Prophet for Uḥud. He had promised victory if they persevered. Upon reaching al-Shawṭ, a certain location [ Translator’s note: The Cairo print spells the place-name الشواط (al-Shawāṭ). The reading al-Shawṭ (الشوط) used here is an explicit correction, supported by Ibn al-Mulaqqin’s al-Tawḍīḥ , XXI, p. 145, in its account of Uḥud.] , Ibn Ubayy withdrew with three hundred, saying: “Why should we get ourselves killed?” Abū Jābir al-Sulamī pursued the men, imploring them by God for the sake of their Prophet and themselves. Ibn Ubayy answered, “Had we known there would be a battle, we would have followed you.” The clans of Banū Ḥāritha and Banū Salama were on the verge of turning back with him, but remained firm beside the Prophet. Thus God reminded them of His grace in the verse: “When two groups among you almost lost courage, though God was their Protector”—He supported and protected the two from following the hypocrites. Jābir said: “We would not be pleased if the verse had not been revealed, because of the words ‘God was their Protector.’” Banū Salama belonged to the Khazraj and Banū Ḥāritha to the Aws. “In God let the believers put their trust,” and not in anything else, for there is no other true Helper. [XIV-N097]","anchor":"en-q3-121-122-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-121-122-s2","r":"q3-121-122","title":"A teacher maps the inward battle with the ego-self","text":"Part of the vocation of spiritual teachers ( شيوخ التربية ) is to guide disciples ( المريدين ) in struggling against their own souls ( محاربة النفوس ), and to disclose to them the soul’s hidden plots and deceptions, thereby furnishing them with battle-stations from which to confront it. God observes their sincerity and intentions. Some grow weary, become exhausted, and return to the homeland of their habitual patterns ( وطن عوائدهم ); others persevere until they win the greatest booty and supreme felicity. As the poet says: They strove with all intensity, until most grew tired; But the one who carried on and endured embraced honour. Someone said: “The travelers’ journeying ( سير السائرين ) ends with gaining the upper hand over their own souls. If they prevail over them, they arrive ( وصلوا ).” Some disciples experience weariness and faltering and contemplate withdrawing and turning back; then God makes them stand firm and grants them victory, and they catch up with those who patiently went before them. The chief resource of the disciple in struggling against his soul ( مجاهدة النفس ) is reliance upon God alone ( التوكل على الله والاعتماد عليه ). “A sign of success at the endings is returning to God at the beginnings.” “And in God let the believers put their trust.”","anchor":"en-q3-121-122-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-121-122-s3","r":"q3-121-122","title":"","text":"He then reminded the people of Uḥud of the victory granted them at Badr, despite their small numbers, to strengthen their resolve.","anchor":"en-q3-121-122-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-123","r":"q3-123","title":"3:123 · Badr and the paradox of strength through abasement","text":"3:123 · Badr and the paradox of strength through abasement 3:123","anchor":"unit-q3-123"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-123-1","r":"q3-123","title":"3:123 · Badr and the paradox of strength through abasement","text":"وَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ بِبَدْرٍ وَأَنْتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ (123)","anchor":"ar-q3-123-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-123-2","r":"q3-123","title":"3:123 · Badr and the paradox of strength through abasement","text":"قلت: (بدر) : بئر بين مكة والمدينة، كانت لرجل اسمه بدر، فسميت باسم صاحبها، وقعت فيها الغزوة التي نصر الله فيها رسوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم، فسميت الغزوة باسم المكان، وجملة: (وأنتم أذلة) : حال من الكاف، و (أذلة) : جمع ذليل، كأعزة، جمع عزيزٌ.","anchor":"ar-q3-123-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-123-3","r":"q3-123","title":"3:123 · Badr and the paradox of strength through abasement","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ في وقعة بدر وَأَنْتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ ليس معكم مراكب ولا كثرة سلاح، مع قوة عدوكم بالعُدة والعدد، فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ واثبتوا مع رسوله، وانتظروا النصر من الله كما عودكم، لَعَلَّكُمْ تكونون شاكرين، لما أنعم به عليكم من العز والنصر، فيزيدكم منه كما وعدكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-123-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-123-4","r":"q3-123","title":"3:123 · Badr and the paradox of strength through abasement","text":"الإشارة: جعل الله سبحانه وتعالى الأشياء كامنة في أضدادها، فمن أراد العز والنصر فليتحقق بالذل والمسكنة، ومن أراد الغنى فليتحقق بالفقر، ومن أراد الرفعة فليتحقق بالضعة وإسقاط المنزلة، ومن أراد القوة فليتحقق بالضعف، وهكذا: [تحقق بأوصافك يمدك بأوصافه] . فاتقوا الله يا معشر المريدين، واطلبوا الأشياء في أضدادها لتظفروا بها، واشكروا الله على ما أولاكم يزدكم من فضله ونواله.","anchor":"ar-q3-123-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-123-5","r":"q3-123","title":"3:123 · Badr and the paradox of strength through abasement","text":"ثم ذكر كيفية نصره لهم ببدر فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-123-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-123-s1","r":"q3-123","title":"The well of Badr and the circumstantial clause","text":"I say: Badr ( بدر ) is a well between Mecca and Madīna that belonged to a man named Badr, after whom the well was named. The expedition in which God gave His Messenger, blessings and peace be upon him, victory occurred at that place; the battle was accordingly named after its location. “While you were humbled” ( وَأَنْتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ ) is a circumstantial clause ( جملة حال ) referring back to the object-pronoun -kum ( الكاف ) in “He helped you.” Adhilla ( أذلة ) is the plural of dhalīl ( ذليل ), just as aʿizza ( أعزة ) is the plural of ʿazīz ( عزيز ). [XIV-N098]","anchor":"en-q3-123-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-123-s2","r":"q3-123","title":"Victory without the ordinary means of strength","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “God certainly gave you victory at Badr when you were humbled,” having neither riding animals nor much weaponry, while your enemy was strong in equipment and numbers. “So be mindful of God,” remain firm with His Messenger, and await God’s victory as He has accustomed you to do, “that you may give thanks” for the honour and triumph He has granted you, whereupon He will increase it, as He has promised.","anchor":"en-q3-123-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-123-s3","r":"q3-123","title":"Created things hidden within their opposites","text":"God, glorified and exalted, has placed things hidden within their contraries. Therefore whoever seeks honour and victory should realize abasement and destitution ( الذل والمسكنة ); whoever seeks richness should realize poverty ( الفقر ); whoever seeks elevation should realize lowliness and the laying aside of rank; and whoever seeks strength should realize weakness. And so it continues: “Realize your own attributes, and He will assist you with His attributes” ( تحقق بأوصافك يمدك بأوصافه ). O company of disciples, be mindful of God and seek things in their opposites so that you may attain them; thank God for what He has bestowed and He will increase you from His grace and generosity. [XIV-N099]","anchor":"en-q3-123-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-123-s4","r":"q3-123","title":"","text":"The author next mentions the manner in which God assisted them at Badr.","anchor":"en-q3-123-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-124-125","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor 3:124–125","anchor":"unit-q3-124-125"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-124-125-1","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"إِذْ تَقُولُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَلَنْ يَكْفِيَكُمْ أَنْ يُمِدَّكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِثَلاثَةِ آلافٍ مِنَ الْمَلائِكَةِ مُنْزَلِينَ (124) بَلى إِنْ تَصْبِرُوا وَتَتَّقُوا وَيَأْتُوكُمْ مِنْ فَوْرِهِمْ هذا يُمْدِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِخَمْسَةِ آلافٍ مِنَ الْمَلائِكَةِ مُسَوَّمِينَ (125)","anchor":"ar-q3-124-125-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-124-125-2","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"قلت: (إذ) : ظرف لنصركم، إذا قلنا: إن الإمداد يوم بدر فقط، أو بدل من (إذ غدوت) ، إذا قلنا: كان الإمداد يوم أحد بشرط الصبر، فلما لم يصبروا لم يقع. والتسويم: التعليم.","anchor":"ar-q3-124-125-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-124-125-3","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولقد نصركم الله ببدر حين كنت تَقُولُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ حين رأوا كثرة عدوهم وقلة عدتهم وعددهم: أَلَنْ يَكْفِيَكُمْ في القوة والكثرة، أَنْ يُمِدَّكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِثَلاثَةِ آلافٍ مِنَ الْمَلائِكَةِ مُنْزَلِينَ في السحاب؟ بَلى يكفيكم كما وعدكم، إِنْ تَصْبِرُوا وتثبتوا وَتَتَّقُوا الله وَيَأْتُوكُمْ مِنْ فَوْرِهِمْ أي: من سرعتهم هذا الوقت، يُمْدِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِخَمْسَةِ آلافٍ مِنَ الْمَلائِكَةِ بلا تراخ ولا تأخير، مُسَوَّمِينَ أي: مُعَلَّمين بعمائم بيض إلا جبريل، فإنه كانت عمامته صفراء. أو معلمين أنفسَهم أو خيلَهم. قيل:","anchor":"ar-q3-124-125-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-124-125-4","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"كانت مجزوزة الأذناب، وقيل: كانت بُلْقاً.","anchor":"ar-q3-124-125-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-124-125-5","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"فإن قلت: ما ذكر في الأنفال إلا ألفاً، وهنا خمسة آلاف. فالجواب: أن الله تعالى أمدهم أولاً بألف، ثم صاروا ثلاثة آلاف، ثم صاروا خمسة آلاف. قال ابن عباس: لم تقاتل الملائكة إلا يوم بدر، وفيما سوى ذلك يشهدون القتال معنا، ولا يقاتلون. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-124-125-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-124-125-6","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن توجَّه لجهاد نفسه في الله، واشتغل بذكر مولاه، أمده الله في الباطن بالأنوار والأسرار، وفي الظاهر بالملائكة الأبرار، وقد شوهد ذلك في الفقراء أصحابنا، إذا كانوا ثلاثة رآهم العامة ثلاثين، وإذا كانوا ثلاثين رأوهم ثلاثمائة، وقد كنا في سفرة سبعين، فرأونا سبعمائة على ما أخبرونا به، وَاللَّهُ يُؤَيِّدُ بِنَصْرِهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ.","anchor":"ar-q3-124-125-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-124-125-7","r":"q3-124-125","title":"3:124–125 · Angelic reinforcement at Badr and the unseen aid of spiritual endeavor","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى حكمة إمداده لهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-124-125-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-124-125-s1","r":"q3-124-125","title":"The position of idh and the meaning of taswīm","text":"I say: “When” ( إذ ) is an adverbial of time ( ظرف ) attached to “He helped you” ( نصركم ) if we consider the reinforcement to have occurred solely on the day of Badr. Alternatively, it is a substitute ( بدل ) for “when you went forth” ( إذ غدوت ) if we consider the reinforcement to have been promised at Uḥud conditional upon patience . When they failed to remain patient, it did not take place. Taswīm ( التسويم ) means marking or designating ( التعليم ). [XIV-N100]","anchor":"en-q3-124-125-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-124-125-s2","r":"q3-124-125","title":"The three and five thousand angels","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: God certainly helped you at Badr “when you said to the believers,” after they saw the many troops of the enemy and the fewness of their own equipment and numbers: “Will it not suffice you,” in strength and numbers, “that your Lord reinforce you with three thousand angels,” sent down within clouds? “Yes,” that will suffice you as He has promised, provided that “you are patient” and stand firm, “and are mindful of God,” and the enemy comes against you “at once” ( من فورهم ), meaning swiftly and at this very time, then “your Lord will reinforce you with five thousand angels” without delay or postponement, “marked out” ( مُسَوِّمِينَ ). They were marked with white turbans, except Gabriel, whose turban was yellow. Alternatively, they marked themselves or their horses. It is said that the horses had docked tails; or that they were piebald. Translator’s note: These are differing transmitted descriptions, not a single established visual account. [XIV-N101] If you ask: Why is only one thousand mentioned in Sūrat al-Anfāl, whereas here there are five thousand? The response is that God initially reinforced them with one thousand; their number then reached three thousand; and finally it rose to five thousand. Ibn ʿAbbās said: “The angels fought only on the day of Badr; on other occasions they are present at the battle with us, but do not fight.” End of the cited report. [XIV-N101]","anchor":"en-q3-124-125-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-124-125-s3","r":"q3-124-125","title":"Hidden lights, angelic support and an episode from the author’s circle","text":"Whoever turns toward struggling against his own soul for the sake of God ( جهاد النفس ), and occupies himself with the remembrance of his Master ( ذكر مولاه ), receives from God, inwardly, assistance in lights and mysteries ( الأنوار والأسرار ), and outwardly, the help of noble angels ( الملائكة الأبرار ). This, Ibn ʿAjība says, has been witnessed among the spiritual poor ( الفقراء ) of his own circle: when there were three of them, the common people saw thirty; when thirty, they saw three hundred. “We were once seventy on a journey, but people saw us as seven hundred, according to what they told us.” “And God strengthens with His help whom He wills.” [XIV-N102]","anchor":"en-q3-124-125-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-124-125-s4","r":"q3-124-125","title":"","text":"He then explains the wisdom of that reinforcement.","anchor":"en-q3-124-125-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-126-129","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence 3:126–129","anchor":"unit-q3-126-129"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-1","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"وَما جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ إِلاَّ بُشْرى لَكُمْ وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُكُمْ بِهِ وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلاَّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَكِيمِ (126) لِيَقْطَعَ طَرَفاً مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَوْ يَكْبِتَهُمْ فَيَنْقَلِبُوا خائِبِينَ (127) لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ أَوْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْهِمْ أَوْ يُعَذِّبَهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ ظالِمُونَ (128) وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ يَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (129)","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-2","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"قلت: (ليس لك من الأمر شيء) : جملة معترضة بين قوله: (أو يكبتهم) وقوله: (أو يتوب عليهم) ، أو تكون (أو) بمعنى (إلا) ، أي: ليس لك من الأمر شيء، إلا أن يتوب عليهم فتبشرهم، أو يعذبهم فتتشفى فيهم. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-3","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وما جعل الله ذلك الإمداد إلا بشارة لكم بالنصر، وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُكُمْ بِهِ فتثبتوا للقتال، وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ فهو قادر على أن ينصركم بلا واسطة، لكن أراد أن يثيبكم وينسب المزية إليكم، حيث قتلهم على أيديكم، فإن الله عزيز لا يغلب، حكيم فيما دبر وأبرم، وإنما نصركم يوم بدر لِيَقْطَعَ طَرَفاً مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بقتل بعض وأسر آخرين، فإنه قتل يومئذ سبعون، وأسر سبعون، أَوْ يَكْبِتَهُمْ أي: يحزنهم ويغيظهم، والكبت: شدة الغيظ، فَيَنْقَلِبُوا خائِبِينَ مما أملوا.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-4","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"ولما جرح- عليه الصلاة والسلام- في وجهه، وشُجَّ على قرن حاجبه، وكُسِرَت رباعيته، هَمَّ بالدعاء على الكفار، بل دعا عليهم، فأنزل الله: لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ إنما أنت رسول إليهم، مأمور بإنذارهم وجهادهم، وأمرهم بيد مالكهم، إن شاء هداهم وإن شاء عذّبهم. وإنما نهاه عن الدعاء عليهم لعلمه بأن منهم من يُسلم ويجاهد في سبيل الله، وقد كان كذلك فجُلَّهم أسلموا وجاهدوا، منهم خالد بن الوليد- سيف الله فى أرضه.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-5","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"ثم عطف على قوله: لِيَقْطَعَ طَرَفاً مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَوْ يَكْبِتَهُمْ قوله: أَوْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْهِمْ إن أسلموا أَوْ يُعَذِّبَهُمْ إن لم يسلموا، فَإِنَّهُمْ ظالِمُونَ قد استحقوا العذاب بظلمهم، والأمور كلها بيد الله، وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ خلقا وملكاً وعبيداً، يَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ غفرانه، وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشاءُ تعذيبه، ولا يجب عليه شيء، وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ لعباده، فلا تبادر بالدعاء عليهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-6","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"الإشارة: وما جعل الله التأييد الذي ينزله على أهل التجريد، حين يقابلهم بالابتلاء والتشديد، إذا أراد أن يوصلهم لصفاء التوحيد، إلا بشارة لفتحهم، ولتطمئن بمعرفته قلوبهم، فإن الامتكان على قدر الامتحان، وكل محنة تزيد مكنة، وهذه سُنة الله في أوليائه يسلط عليهم الخلق في بدايتهم، ويشدد عليهم البلاء، حتى إذا طهروا من البقايا، وكملت فيهم المزايا، كف عنهم الأذى، وانقلب الجلال جمالاً، وذلك اعتناء بهم، ونصراً لهم على أنفسهم، فإن النصر كله مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَكِيمِ. وذلك ليقطع عنهم طرفاً من الشواغل والعلائق، التي تقبضهم عن العروج إلى سماء الحقائق، فإن الروح إذا رقدت في ظل العز والجاه صعب خروجها من هذا العالم، فإذا ضيق عليها، وعكس مرادها، رحلت إلى عالم الملكوت، والأمر كله بيد الله. ليس لك أيها الفقير من الأمر شيء، إنما أنت مأمور بتحريك الأسباب(1) والله يفتح الباب. وليس لك أيها الشيخ من الأمر شيء، إنما أنت مذكر، وعلى الله البلاغ، فلا تأس على ما فاتك، ولا تفرح بما آتاك، فملكوت السموات والأرض بيد الله، يَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشاءُ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-7","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"قال القشيري: جرَّده- أي: نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم لما به عرفه عن كُلِّ غيْرٍ وسبب، حيث أخبره أنه ليس له من الأمر شيء، ثم قال: ويقال: أقامه في وقتٍ مقاماً رمى بقبضة من التراب، فأصابت جميع الوجوه، وقال: وَما رَمَيْتَ إِذْ رَمَيْتَ وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ رَمى وقال في وقت آخر: لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-8","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"يشير إلى أنهما مقامان: نيابة عن الله بالله، ونيابة الله عن عبده، والأول بقاء، والثاني فناء، قاله المحشى.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-9","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"قلت: الأول في مقام البسط، والثاني في مقام القبض، فقد قالوا: إذا بسط فلا فاقة، وإذا قبض فلا طاقة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-126-129-10","r":"q3-126-129","title":"3:126–129 · Victory from God, the limit of Prophetic control and the stations of effacement and subsistence","text":"ولما كان النصر فى الجهاد لا يكون إلا بأكل الحلال وطاعة الكبير المتعال، قدّم ذكر ذلك قبل الأمر بالقتال فى قضية أحد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-126-129-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-126-129-s1","r":"q3-126-129","title":"An inserted clause between coordinated possibilities","text":"I say: “You have no part in the matter” ( ليس لك من الأمر شيء ) is a parenthetical clause ( جملة معترضة ) inserted between “or suppress them” ( أو يكبتهم ) and “or turn toward them” ( أو يتوب عليهم ). Alternatively, the particle aw ( أو ) may carry the force of “except” ( إلا ): “You have no part in the matter, except that if He accepts their repentance you may bring them glad tidings, or if He punishes them you may take satisfaction in their punishment.” This second grammatical account is attributed to al-Bayḍāwī. [XIV-N103]","anchor":"en-q3-126-129-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-126-129-s2","r":"q3-126-129","title":"The means of victory and the Prophet’s relation to his enemies","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: God made the reinforcement only “glad tidings” of victory, so that your hearts might rest secure through it and you stand firm in battle. “Victory is only from God”: He can give you victory without any intermediary, but He desired to reward you and to ascribe distinction to you by causing the enemies to be killed at your hands. He is Mighty ( عزيز ), none can overcome Him, and Wise ( حكيم ) in what He determines and orders. He gave victory at Badr “to cut off a portion of those who disbelieve,” killing some and taking others captive—seventy, he reports, being killed that day and seventy taken prisoner—or “to suppress them,” distressing and enraging them. Kabṭ ( الكبت ) is intense rage: “so they return frustrated,” their hopes unfulfilled. When the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, was wounded in the face, cut near his eyebrow and suffered a broken front tooth, he intended to pray against the unbelievers—indeed, he prayed against them. God then revealed: “You have no part in the matter.” You are only a messenger sent to them, charged with warning them and struggling against them, while their destiny rests in the hands of their Owner. If He wills, He guides them; if He wills, He punishes them. God forbade him to call down punishment on them because He knew that some of them would accept Islam and strive in God’s way. Ibn ʿAjība says that this did happen: most entered Islam and fought in its cause, including Khālid ibn al-Walīd, “God’s sword upon His earth.” [XIV-N104] The phrase “or He turns toward them in mercy” is then coordinated with “to cut off a portion of those who disbelieve or suppress them”: He may accept their repentance if they submit, “or chastise them” if they do not, “for they are wrongdoers,” having incurred punishment through their injustice. All matters rest in God’s hands: “To God belongs whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is on the earth,” by creation, ownership and servitude. “He forgives whom He wills” to forgive “and chastises whom He wills” to chastise; nothing is incumbent upon Him. “God is Forgiving, Merciful” to His servants, so do not hasten to call down punishment on them.","anchor":"en-q3-126-129-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-126-129-s3","r":"q3-126-129","title":"Affliction as preparation for freedom from dependence","text":"The support ( التأييد ) that God sends down upon the people of detachment ( أهل التجريد ), when He confronts them with trial and hardship in order to bring them to the purity of tawḥīd ( صفاء التوحيد ), is only glad tidings of their spiritual opening ( فتح ), and serves to give their hearts repose in knowing Him. Secure establishment ( الامتكان ) comes in proportion to testing ( الامتحان ); every ordeal adds to one’s capacity to stand firm ( مكنة ). This is God’s practice with His friends: at their beginnings He grants other creatures power over them and intensifies their trials until they have been purified of their residues ( البقايا ) and their merits have reached completion. Then He restrains the harm, and Majesty ( الجلال ) turns to Beauty ( الجمال ). This is His solicitude for them and His victory for them over their own souls. All victory comes from “God, the Mighty, the Wise.” [XIV-N105] He does this “to cut off” from them some of the distractions and attachments ( الشواغل والعلائق ) that keep them from rising to the heaven of realities ( سماء الحقائق ). When the spirit lies at ease in the shade of honor and status ( العز والجاه ), it finds it hard to leave this world; when constrained and thwarted, it travels to the world of Dominion ( عالم الملكوت ). All matters are in God’s hands. You, spiritual poor one, “have no part in the matter”: you are commanded to set the means in motion, while God opens the door. You, spiritual teacher, likewise “have no part in the matter”: you only give reminder, while bringing [them] to the goal rests with God. Neither grieve over what has escaped you nor exult over what He has given you. The Dominion of the heavens and earth is God’s: “He forgives whom He wills and chastises whom He wills; God is Forgiving, Merciful.” [Translator’s note: The printed phrase وعلى الله البلاغ is retained. Balāgh can denote reaching an end or bringing something to it, as well as conveying a message (Ibn Manẓūr, Lisān al-ʿArab, root b-l-gh, II:144). The present rendering follows the immediate context: the disciple sets the means in motion, God opens the door, and the teacher gives reminder. The same idiom appears in a travel anecdote quoted by Ibn al-Jawzī, Talbīs Iblīs , I:290: “Walking is my part; bringing me there is God’s.” This is linguistic corroboration, not a claim that the anecdote is authenticated or is Ibn ʿAjība’s source. The supplied object “[them]” makes the contextual interpretation visible; no emendation of the Arabic is proposed.] Al-Qushayrī says: “He stripped him”—the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him—“of every other thing and cause, once He had made Himself known to him, telling him that he had no part in the matter.” Then he says: “It is also said that at one moment He established him in a station in which he cast a handful of dust that struck every face, and God said, ‘You did not throw when you threw, but God threw’ [Q 8:17]. At another moment He said, ‘You have no part in the matter.’” End of quotation. The glossator explains that these indicate two stations: acting as God’s deputy through God ( نيابة عن الله بالله ), and God acting in the place of His servant ( نيابة الله عن عبده ). The first is subsistence ( بقاء ), the second effacement ( فناء ), according to the gloss. I say: The first belongs to the station of expansion ( البسط ), and the second to that of contraction ( القبض ). Thus they have said: “When He expands [the heart], there is no destitution; when He contracts it, there is no power.” God Most High knows best. [XIV-N106]","anchor":"en-q3-126-129-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-126-129-s4","r":"q3-126-129","title":"","text":"Since victory in striving is attained only through consuming the lawful ( أكل الحلال ) and obedience to the Most High, he introduces these matters before returning to the command to fight in connection with Uḥud.","anchor":"en-q3-126-129-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-130-134","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān 3:130–134","anchor":"unit-q3-130-134"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-1","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَأْكُلُوا الرِّبَوا أَضْعافاً مُضاعَفَةً وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ (130) وَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكافِرِينَ (131) وَأَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَالرَّسُولَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُونَ (132) وَسارِعُوا إِلى مَغْفِرَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا السَّماواتُ وَالْأَرْضُ أُعِدَّتْ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ (133) الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ فِي السَّرَّاءِ وَالضَّرَّاءِ وَالْكاظِمِينَ الْغَيْظَ وَالْعافِينَ عَنِ النَّاسِ وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ (134)","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-2","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"قلت: الكظم هو: الكف والحبس، تقول: كظمت القربة: إذا ملأتها وسددت رأسها.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-3","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَأْكُلُوا الرِّبَوا وتزيدوا فيها إذا حلَّ الأجل أَضْعافاً مُضاعَفَةً، ولعل التخصيص بحسب الواقع، إذ كان الرجل يَحُلُّ أجلُ دَيْنِهِ، فيقول للمدين: إما أن تقضي وإما أن تزيد، فلا يزال يؤخره ويزيد في دينه حتى يستغرق مال المدين، فنُهوا عن ذلك. ورغبهم في التقوى التي هي غنى الدارين. فقال: وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فيما نهيتكم عنه، لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ في الدارين. ثم خوفهم بالنار إن لم ينتهوا، فقال: وَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكافِرِينَ، وفيه إشعار بأن النار موجودة إذ لا يُعدُّ المعدوم، وأنها بالذات معدة للكافرين، وبالعرض للعاصين.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-4","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"قال الورتجبي: في الآية إشارة إلى أن النار لم تعد للمؤمنين، ولم تخلق لهم، ولكن خوفهم بها زجراً وعظة، كالأب البار المشفق على ولده يخوفه بالأسد والسيف، وهو لا يضربه بالسيف، ولا يلقيه إلى الأسد، فهذه الآية تلطف وشفقة على عباده. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-5","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وَأَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ فيما أمر ونهى، وَالرَّسُولَ فيما شرع وسَنَّ، لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُونَ. والتعبير بلعل وعسى في أمثال هذه: دليل على عون التوصل إلى ما جعل طريقاً له.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-6","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وَسارِعُوا أي: بادروا إِلى مَغْفِرَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ كالإسلام والتوبة والإخلاص، وسائر الطاعات التي توجب المغفرة، وقرأ نافع وابن عامر بغير واو على الاستئناف. وسارعوا أيضاً إلى جَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا السَّماواتُ وَالْأَرْضُ لو وصل بعضها ببعض، وذكر العرض للمبالغة في وصفها بالسعة لأنه دون الطول. قال بعضهم: لم يُرد العَرض الذي هو ضد الطول، وإنما أراد عظمها، ومعناه: كعرض السموات السبع والأرضين السبع في ظنكم، أي: لا تدرك ببيان. أُعِدَّتْ أي: هُيِّئَتْ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ. وفيه دليل على أنَّ الجنة مخلوقة، وأنها خارجة عن هذا العالم.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-7","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"ثم وصف أهلها من المتقين بأوصاف الكمال، فقال: الَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ فِي السَّرَّاءِ وَالضَّرَّاءِ أي: في حالتي الرخاء والشدة، وفي الأحوال كلها، كما هي حالة الأسخياء، قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «الجنَّةُ دَارُ الأسخياءِ» . وقال أيضا:","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-8","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"«السَّخِيُّ قَرِيبٌ مِنَ اللهِ، قريبٌ مِنَ الجَنَّةِ، قَرِيبٌ من النَّاس، بَعِيدٌ من النَّارِ، والبَخيلُ بَعيدٌ من اللهِ، بَعِيدٌ مِنَ الجَنَّةِ، بَعِيدٌ من الناس، قَرِيبٌ من النَّارِ. ولجَاهلٌ سَخِيٌ أَحَبُ إلى اللهِ مِنَ العالمِ البخيل» . وقال أيضا صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «السّخَاء شَجَرةٌ في الجنة، أغصانها في الدنيا، من تعلق بَغُصنٍ من أغْصَانِها قادَته إلى الجنَّةِ، والبخْلُ شَجرةٌ في النَّارِ، أغصَانُها في الدُّنيا، من تعلق ببعض من أغصانها قَادَته إلى النَّارِ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-9","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وَالْكاظِمِينَ الْغَيْظَ أي: الكافين عن إمضائه مع القدرة عليه، قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «من كظم غيظا وهو يَقْدِرُ على إمْضَائِهِ مَلأَ اللهُ قَلْبَهُ أمْناً وإِيمَاناً» .","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-10","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وقال بعض الشعراء:","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-11","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وَإذَا غَضِبْتَ فَكُنْ وَقُوراً كَاظِماً ... لِلْغَيْظِ، تُبْصر مَا تَقُولُ وتَسْمَعُ","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-12","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"فَكَفَى بِهِ شَرَفاً، تَصَبُّرُ سَاعَةٍ ... يَرْضَى بِهَا عَنْكَ الإلَهُ ويَرْفَعُ(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-13","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وَالْعافِينَ عَنِ النَّاسِ أي: عمن ظلمهم، وعن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال عند ذلك: «إنَّ هؤلاءِ في أُمتي قليل، إلا مَنْ عَصَمَ الله، وقد كَانُوا كثيراً في الأمم التي مَضَت» . وعَنْ أبي هريرة: أن أبا بكر كان مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم في مجلس، فجاء رجل فوقع في أبي بكر، وهو ساكت، والنبي صلّى الله عليه وسلم يبتسم، ثم ردّ عليه أبو بكر بعضَ الرد، فغضب عليه الصلاة والسلام- وقام، فلحقه أبو بكر، وقال: يا رسول الله، شتمني وأنت تبتسم، ثم رَدَدْتُ عليه بعضَ ما قال، فغضبتَ وقُمتَ. قال: «حين كنتَ ساكتاً كان معك مَلَكٌ يردُّ عليه، فلما تكلمتَ وقع الشيطان، فلم أكُنْ لأقعدَ في مقعدْ فيه الشيطان، يا أبا بكر، ثلاثٌ حق: تعلم أنه ليس عبد يظلم مظلمة فيعفو عنها إلا أعز الله بها نصره، وليس عبد يفتح باب مسألة يريد بها كثرة إلا زاده الله قلة، وليس عبد يفتح عطية أو صلة إلا زاده الله بها كثرة» .","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-14","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ الذي أحسنوا فيما بينهم وبين الله، وفيما بينهم وبين عباد الله، و «أل» : يحتمل أن تكون للجنس، فيعم كل محسن، أو للعهد، فتكون الإشارة إلى من تقدم ذكرهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-15","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"الإشارة: كل ما يُقوي مادة الحس فهو ربا لأنه يربى الحس ويقوي مادة الغفلة، فلا ينبغي لمريد أن يضاعفه ويتعاطى أسباب تكثيره، بل ينبغي أن يفر من موارده، وهي ثلاثة: مباشرة الحس، أو الفكر فيه، أو الكلام مع أهله","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-16","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"فيه. والذي يقوي مادة المعنى ثلاثة: صحبة أهل المعنى، والفكرة في المعاني، وذكر الله بالقلب. واتقوا الله فى مباشرة الحس (لعلكم تفلحون) بالوصول إلى صفاء المعاني، واتقوا نار القطيعة التي أعدت لمنكر الخصوصية، (وأطيعوا الله والرسول) فيما ندبكم إليه، (لعلكم ترحمون) بإحياء قلوبكم وأرواحكم بأسرار المعاني، وسارعوا إلى ما يوجب تغطية مساوئكم، حتى يغطي وصفكم بوصفه، ونعتكم بنعته، فيُوصلكم بما منه إليكم، لا بما منكم إليه، فتدخلوا جنة المعارف، التي لا نهاية لفضاء شهودها، التي أعدت للمتقين السّوى، الذين يبذلون مهجهم وأموالهم في حال الجلال والجمال، (والكاظمين الغيظ) حيث ملكوا أنفسهم وأحوالهم، (والعافين عن الناس) لأن الصوفي ماله مباح ودمه هدر. وكان بعض الصوفية يقول: إذا أردتَ أن تعرفَ حال الفقير فأغضبه، وانظر إلى ما يخرج منه. وقال شيخ شيوخنا رضي الله عنه: قطب التصوف: لا تغضب ولا تُغضب. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-17","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"ولعروة بن الزبير- رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-18","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"لن يبلغَ المجدَ أقوامٌ وإنْ كَرُمُوا ... حتى يُذَلّوا وإن عَزّوا لأقوام","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-19","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"ويُشتَموا فتَرى الألوانَ مُشرِقةٌ، ... لا عَفْوَ ذُلَّ، ولكن عَفْوَ أحلام","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-20","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ الذين حازوا مقام الإحسان، فعبدوا الله بالشهود والعيان، فعم إحسانهم ذا الإساءة والإحسان والإنس والجان. قال الحسن البصري: (الإحسان: أن يعم إحسانه، ولا يكون كالشمس والريح والمطر) .","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-21","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"أي: يخص بلداً دون بلد. وقال سفيان الثوري: (ليس الإحسان أن تحسن إلى من أحسن إليك، وإنما الإحسان أن تحسن إلى مَن أساء إليك. فإن الإحسان إلى المحسن متاجرة كنقد السوق، خذ مني وهَات) . وقال السري السقطي:","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-22","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"(الإحسان: أن تُحسن وقت الإمكان، فليس في كل وقت يمكنك الإحسان) ، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-23","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"ليس في كلَّ ساعةٍ وأوان ... تَتَهَيَّأ صنائعُ الإحسان","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-24","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"فإذا أمْكَنَتْ فبادرْ إليها ... حذَراً من تعذّر الإمكان(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-25","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"وقال الورتجبي: قوله: وَسارِعُوا إِلى مَغْفِرَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ ... الخ، علم الحق- سبحانه- عِلَلَ الخلق وميلهم إلى مُنى النفوس، فدعاهم بطاعته إلى العلتين: المغفرة والجنة، ودعا الخاصة إلى نفسه، فقال: فَفِرُّوا إِلَى اللَّهِ، ثم أعْلَم أن الكل في درك امتحان الجرم، وأثبت بالآية ذنب الكل، لأنهم وإن كانوا معصومين من الزلل،","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-26","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"فذنبهم قلة معرفتهم لأقدار الحق، كما قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لو أن الله عذب الملائكة لحق منه، فقيل: إنهم معصومون، فقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: من قلة معرفتهم بربهم(1)» . ولذلك دعاهم إلى المغفرة. هـ. قال في الحاشية: وقوله: (أثبت بالآية ذنب الكل) ، يعني: شمول قوله: (يغفر لمن يشاء) مَنْ فى السموات الصادق بالملائكة، وإنما تكون المغفرة بعد ذنب، ولكنه في كل أحد على حسبه، وأما قوله: دعاهم إلى المغفرة، فكأنه من قوله: سارِعُوا إِلى مَغْفِرَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ، وأن الخطاب يعم من فى السموات أيضاً، وقد يتصور في حق الملائكة الاستنادُ لظواهر الأمور والاختلاف بينهم والاختصام، مما هو معرض للخطأ، وذلك من دواعي المغفرة، وكذلك القصور عن معرفة كنه جلال الله: نقصٌ لا يخلو منه مخلوق، لاستحالة الإحاطة به علماً، ولذلك كان الترقي في المعرفة لا حد له أبداً سرمداً. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-130-134-27","r":"q3-130-134","title":"3:130–134 · Usury, generosity, forbearance, forgiveness and the station of iḥsān","text":"ثم ذكر حال أهل اليمين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-130-134-27"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-130-134-s1","r":"q3-130-134","title":"Kaẓm (الكظم) as restraint and containment","text":"I say: Kaẓm ( الكظم ) means restraining and holding back. Thus one says, “I sealed the water-skin” ( كظمت القربة ) when one filled it and stopped up its opening.","anchor":"en-q3-130-134-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-130-134-s2","r":"q3-130-134","title":"Redoubled interest and the disposition of God-consciousness","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “O you who believe, do not consume usury” ( الرِّبا ) by increasing the debt when its due date arrives, “doubled and redoubled.” Perhaps this specification reflects the customary practice at the time: when a debt fell due, the creditor would tell the debtor, “Either settle it or add to it.” The creditor would grant repeated delays and repeatedly increase what was owing, until the debt swallowed all of the debtor’s property. They were forbidden this. God then commends mindfulness ( التقوى ), which is enrichment in both abodes: “Be mindful of God” regarding what I have forbidden you, “that you may prosper” in this world and the next. [XIV-N107] He then makes them fear the Fire if they do not desist: “Guard against the Fire prepared for the unbelievers.” This also suggests, Ibn ʿAjība argues, that the Fire already exists, since something nonexistent cannot be prepared; that it is prepared for unbelievers primarily ( بالذات ) and for sinful people incidentally ( بالعرض ). Al-Wartajbī says the verse indicates that the Fire was not prepared or created for believers , but that God has warned them with it as a deterrent and admonition, just as a kind father may frighten his son with a lion or sword without intending to strike the child with the sword or throw him to the lion. In this interpretation the verse manifests gentleness and care toward His servants. End of quotation. [XIV-N108] “Obey God” in what He commands and forbids, “and the Messenger” in what he legislates and establishes as Sunnah, “that you may receive mercy.” Forms such as laʿalla ( لعل ) and ʿasā ( عسى ), “perhaps” or “so that,” in such contexts indicate the assistance granted in reaching the end to which a path has been established.","anchor":"en-q3-130-134-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-130-134-s3","r":"q3-130-134","title":"The immensity of the Garden","text":"“Hasten” ( وسارعوا ), that is, make haste “toward forgiveness from your Lord,” such as Islam, repentance, sincerity ( الإخلاص ), and all other obedient deeds entailing forgiveness. Nāfiʿ and Ibn ʿĀmir read the command without the conjunction wāw (و), treating it as a fresh sentence ( استئناف ). And hasten toward “a Garden whose breadth is the heavens and the earth”—if the one were joined to the other. Mention of breadth, rather than length, intensifies its vastness, because breadth is less than length. Another explanation says this does not mean breadth in contrast with length, but simply extraordinary magnitude: it is as great as the seven heavens and seven earths could seem to you; its extent is beyond description. “Prepared” means made ready “for the mindful.” This, Ibn ʿAjība adds, proves that Paradise is already created and lies outside the present cosmos. [XIV-N109]","anchor":"en-q3-130-134-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-130-134-s4","r":"q3-130-134","title":"Giving in ease and adversity","text":"Then the Real describes the perfected attributes of those mindful people who will inhabit the Garden: “Those who spend in ease and hardship,” namely in prosperity and adversity and indeed in all circumstances, as is the way of the generous. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is cited as saying: “The Garden is the dwelling of the generous.” Also: “The generous person is close to God, close to the Garden, close to people and far from the Fire; the miser is far from God, far from the Garden, far from people and close to the Fire. An ignorant but generous person is dearer to God than a learned miser.” And again: “Generosity is a tree in Paradise whose branches are in the world. Whoever clings to one of its branches is led by it into Paradise. Miserliness is a tree in the Fire whose branches are in the world; whoever clings to one of those branches is led by it into the Fire.” Translator’s note: These are reports quoted by the author, with their individual degrees of authenticity still to be established. [XIV-N110] “And those who restrain their anger” ( والكاظمين الغيظ ): they desist from carrying it into effect despite being capable of doing so. He cites the Prophet as saying: “Whoever suppresses anger, while having the power to act upon it, God fills his heart with security and faith.” One poet says: When you become angry, be dignified, restraining wrath; Then you will perceive what you are saying and hearing. It is honour enough to persevere for an hour, For which God will be pleased with you and raise you high. “And those who pardon people,” meaning those who have wronged them. The Prophet is quoted as saying of such people: “In my community these are few, apart from those God has protected, though they were many among the communities that passed.” [XIV-N111] Abū Hurayra related that Abū Bakr sat in the Prophet’s company when a man came and insulted Abū Bakr. While Abū Bakr kept silent, the Prophet smiled. But when Abū Bakr responded to a portion of the abuse, the Prophet became angry and stood up. Abū Bakr followed him, saying, “Messenger of God, he insulted me while you smiled; when I answered him in part, you became angry and rose.” He replied: “While you were silent, an angel was with you answering him. When you spoke, Satan came, and I would not sit in a gathering with Satan. Abū Bakr, three things are true: no servant suffers a wrong and pardons it without God thereby strengthening His support for him; no servant opens the door of begging to increase his wealth without God increasing his want; and no servant opens the door of giving or maintaining kinship without God increasing his abundance thereby.” [XIV-N112] “God loves those who do beautiful good ( الْمُحْسِنِينَ ),” who act well in their dealings with God and with God’s servants. The definite article al- ( أل ) may be generic ( للجنس ), embracing everyone who practices iḥsān, or it may refer to a known class ( للعهد ), meaning those just described. [XIV-N113]","anchor":"en-q3-130-134-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-130-134-s5","r":"q3-130-134","title":"The multiplication of sense-life as an inward form of ribā","text":"Whatever increases the strength of sensory existence ( مادة الحس ) is, spiritually speaking, ribā : it multiplies the sensory realm and reinforces the substance of heedlessness ( مادة الغفلة ). The disciple ( المريد ) should not augment it or practise methods that cause it to grow, but should flee its three sources: direct engagement with the sensory realm, thought occupied with it, and speech about it with those devoted to it. Three things strengthen the inward order of meaning ( مادة المعنى ): companionship with those who live by inward meaning ( أهل المعنى ), reflection upon meanings ( الفكرة في المعاني ), and remembrance of God in the heart ( ذكر الله بالقلب ). [XIV-N114] Be mindful of God when engaging with the sensible, “that you may prosper” through reaching the purity of spiritual meanings. Fear the fire of separation prepared for whoever rejects the special spiritual station ( الخصوصية ). “Obey God and the Messenger” in what they have encouraged, “that you may receive mercy,” by enlivening your hearts and spirits with the mysteries of meaning. “Hasten” toward whatever veils your defects, until God’s description conceals your description and His attribute covers yours, thereby bringing you to Him through what comes from Him to you, not through what comes from you to Him. Thus you enter the Garden of direct knowledge ( جنة المعارف ), whose expanse of witnessing has no limit, prepared for those who guard against what is other than Him ( المتقين السوى ). Such people expend their very lives and property under both Majesty and Beauty ( الجلال والجمال ). They “restrain anger,” having mastered their selves and states, and “pardon people,” because, in the uncompromising ascetic idiom quoted here, “the Sufi’s property is freely available and his blood is without recompense” ( الصوفي ماله مباح ودمه هدر ). Some Sufis used to say: “If you wish to know the condition of a spiritual poor person ( حال الفقير ), anger him and see what emerges.” The shaykh of our shaykhs said: “The pivot of Sufism ( قطب التصوف ) is: do not grow angry and do not cause anger.” End of quotation. [XIV-N115] These verses are ascribed to ʿUrwa ibn al-Zubayr: People, however noble their stock, do not reach honour Until they abase themselves before others, though they were mighty; And when they are insulted, their faces remain bright— Not the pardon of weakness, but the pardon of self-command. “God loves those who do beautiful good”: those who have attained the station of spiritual excellence ( مقام الإحسان ) and worship God through witnessing and direct vision ( الشهود والعيان ). Their good reaches those who wrong them and those who treat them well, humankind and jinn alike. Al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī said: “Iḥsān is for one’s beneficence to be general, not like the sun, the wind and the rain”—meaning, as Ibn ʿAjība explains, not to favour one land and exclude another. Translator’s note: Cairo transmits a negative comparison with the sun, wind and rain, followed by Ibn ʿAjība’s gloss about favouring one land over another. An earlier version attributed to al-Ḥasan in al-Thaʿlabī’s al-Kashf wa-l-bayān (Ibn ʿĀshūr ed., first edition, 1422/2002, III:167; printed page inspected) says that beneficence should be general and not exclusive, like wind, sun and rain. This is a material difference between the two texts. The translation retains Cairo’s wording and explanatory gloss; independent manuscripts are needed to determine whether the change is authorial or arose in transmission. [XIV-N116] Sufyān al-Thawrī said: “Iḥsān is not to do good to the one who does good to you; it is to do good to the one who wrongs you. Doing good to a benefactor is commerce, like the ready money of the market: take from me and give me in return.” Al-Sarī al-Saqaṭī said: “Iḥsān is to do good when one can, for one cannot do good at every moment.” They recited: The making of deeds of kindness is not possible At every moment and in every hour; So when the opportunity presents itself, hasten to it, Lest that opportunity disappear. Al-Wartajbī said about “Hasten toward forgiveness from your Lord and a Garden ...”: the Real knows creatures’ ailments and their inclination toward what their lower selves desire, so He summoned them, through obedience to Him, toward these two aims—pardon and Paradise. He summoned the elect ( الخاصة ) to Himself, saying: “Flee to God” [Q 51:50]. He then showed that all beings lie within the ordeal of culpability. Through the verse, he attributed a fault to everyone: though some are protected from slipping, their deficiency is their inadequate recognition of the full majesty due to God. As the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, said: “Were God to punish the angels, He would be justified.” It was asked, “But they are protected from sin.” He replied, blessings and peace be upon him: “Because of how little they know their Lord.” Accordingly He called them to forgiveness. Translator’s note: The quotation and its attribution to the Prophet reproduce the author’s cited exposition. The dialogue also appears in Rūzbihān’s ʿArāʾis al-bayān (al-Mazīdī ed., 1429/2008, I:196; printed page inspected). Its modern footnote cites Ibn ʿAjība’s Baḥr (1/336), so that note supplies no independent authentication. The Cairo editor likewise reports that he did not locate the report. [XIV-N117] [Translator’s note: The Arabic repeats عِلَل and العلتين (ʿilal, “ailments,” and al-ʿillatayn, “the two motives/causes”). Rūzbihān’s fuller source passage contrasts these desired benefits with seeking God Himself and then calls seeking forgiveness a pursuit of the self’s portion ( ʿArāʾis al-bayān , al-Mazīdī ed., first edition, 1429/2008, I:196, on 3:133; printed page inspected). Thus “aims” here carries a suggestion of motives that still concern the self. The prepositions distinguish the means—obedience—from the two ends sought.] The marginal commentator explains: saying that the verse attributes a fault to all creatures refers to the inclusion, in “He forgives whom He wills,” of those in the heavens, which includes the angels. Forgiveness presupposes fault, but each creature has a deficiency appropriate to it. The summons to forgiveness is apparently taken from “Hasten toward forgiveness from your Lord,” with its address understood to include those in heaven. Even the angels may be thought of as judging by outward appearances, disagreeing and disputing, matters that allow for error and occasion forgiveness. Moreover, falling short of knowing the full measure of God’s Majesty is a shortcoming no creature can escape, for comprehending Him through knowledge is impossible. For this reason there can never, for all eternity, be a final limit to advancement in knowledge of Him ( الترقي في المعرفة ). End of marginal gloss. [XIV-N118]","anchor":"en-q3-130-134-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-130-134-s6","r":"q3-130-134","title":"","text":"He next describes the condition of the People of the Right ( أهل اليمين ).","anchor":"en-q3-130-134-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-135-136","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing 3:135–136","anchor":"unit-q3-135-136"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-1","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"وَالَّذِينَ إِذا فَعَلُوا فاحِشَةً أَوْ ظَلَمُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ ذَكَرُوا اللَّهَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا لِذُنُوبِهِمْ وَمَنْ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَلَمْ يُصِرُّوا عَلى ما فَعَلُوا وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ (135) أُولئِكَ جَزاؤُهُمْ مَغْفِرَةٌ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَجَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها وَنِعْمَ أَجْرُ الْعامِلِينَ (136)","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-2","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالَّذِينَ إِذا فَعَلُوا فاحِشَةً أي: فعلة بالغة في الفحش والقبح، كالزنى، أَوْ ظَلَمُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ بأي ذنب كان، أو فعلوا كبيرة أو صغيرة، أو الفاحشة: ما يتعدى للغير، وظلم النفس ما يخص، أو الفاحشة بالفعل، وظلم النفس بالقول، ذَكَرُوا اللَّهَ أي: عقابه وغضبه وعرضه الأكبر، أو ذَكَرُوا اللَّهَ في أنفسهم أن الله سائلهم عنه، أو كونه رقيباً عليهم، أو ذَكَرُوا اللَّهَ باللسان فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا لِذُنُوبِهِمْ بالندم والتوبة، وَمَنْ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ أي: لا أحد يغفره إلا الله، والمراد: وصفه تعالى بسعة الرحمة وعموم المغفرة، والحث على الاستغفار.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-3","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"وَلَمْ يُصِرُّوا عَلى ما فَعَلُوا أي: لم يدوموا عليها غير مستغفرين، لقوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «ما أصَرَّ مَن اسْتَغفَر، ولو عَادَ في اليَوم سَبْعِينَ مَرَةً» ، وذلك إذا صحبه الندم، وقال أيضاً: «لا كَبِيرةَ مَعَ الاستغفَار، ولا صغيرة مع","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-4","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الإصْرارِ» . قال قتادة: إياكم والإصرار، فإنما هلك المصرون الماضون قِدْماً في معاصي الله تعالى، لم يتوبوا حتى أتاهم الموت. هـ. وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ أن الإصرار يضر بهم، أو: وهم يعلمون أن لهم رباً يغفر الذنب لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «مَنْ أَذْنَبَ ذنْباً، وعَلِمَ أَنَّ له ربّاً يَغْفُرِ الذنوب، غَفَرَ له وإِنْ لمْ يسْتَغفر» . وفي الحديث القدسي يقول الله تعالى: «مِنْ علم أني ذو قدرة على المغفرة غفرتُ له ولا أبالي» . وفي بعض الكتب المنزلة:","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-5","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"«يا ابْنَ آدَمَ، إِنَّكَ ما دَعَوْتني ورَجَوْتني لأغفرن لَكَ على مَا كَانَ منكَ ولا أُبَالِي» . أو: (وهم يعلمون) أن التوبة تمحق الذنوب.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-6","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"أُولئِكَ جَزاؤُهُمْ مَغْفِرَةٌ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ تغطية لذنوبهم، وَجَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها، ولا يلزم من إعدادها للتائبين اختصاصهم بها، كما لا يلزم من إعداد النار للكفار اختصاصهم بها، ثم مدح أجر التائبين فقال: وَنِعْمَ أَجْرُ الْعامِلِينَ، وانظر هذا الفرق العظيم الذي بين المحسنين وأهل اليمين، قال في الآية الأولى: وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ وقال في هذه الآية: وَنِعْمَ أَجْرُ الْعامِلِينَ، أهل الآية الأولى من خواص الأحباب، وأهل هذه يأخذون أجرهم من وراء الباب. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى عين التحقيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-7","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الإشارة: أهل مقام الإحسان عملهم قلبي، كالسخاء والعفو وكظم الغيظ، وأهل اليمين عملهم بدني، بين طاعة ومعصية وغفلة ويقظة، إذا فعلوا فاحشة تابوا واستغفروا، وإذا فعلوا طاعة فرحوا واستبشروا، أهل مقام الإحسان غائبون عن رؤية أعمالهم ووجودهم، وأهل اليمين معتمدون على أعمالهم، إذا فعلوا طاعة قوى رجاؤهم، وإذا زلَّوا نقص رجاؤهم، أهل مقام الإحسان فانون عن أنفسهم باقون بربهم، وأهل اليمين أنفسهم موجودة وأعمالهم لديهم مشهودة، أهل مقام الإحسان محبوبون، وأهل اليمين مُحِبُّون، أهل مقام الإحسان فنيت عندهم الرسوم والأشكال، وبقي في نظرهم وجود الكبير المتعال، وأهل اليمين: الأكوان عندهم موجودة، وشموس المعارف عن قلوبهم مفقودة، أهل مقام الإحسان يعبدون الله على نعت الشهود والعيان، وأهل اليمين يعبدون الله من وراء حجاب الدليل والبرهان، أهل الدليل والبرهان عموم عند أهل الشهود والعيان.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-8","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"واعلم أن لمعرفة الشهود والعيان ثمرات ونتائج، حصرها بعضهم في إحدى عشرة خصلة:","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-9","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الأولى: الحرية، ومعناها أن يكون العارف فرداً لِفَرْدٍ، من غير أن يكون تحت رق شيء من الموجودات، لا من أغراض الدنيا ولا من أغراض الآخرة، فالحرية عبارة عن غاية التصفية والطهارة. قال بعضهم: ليس بحُرٍّ من بقي عليه من تصفية نفسه مقدار فص نواة، المكاتب عبد ما بقي عليه درهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-10","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الثانية: الوجود، وهو الفوز بحقيقة الأشياء في الأصل، وهو عبارة عن إدراك مقام تضمحل فيه الرسوم، بالاستغراق في الحقيقة الأزلية.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-11","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الثالثة: الجمع الأتم، وهو الحال الذي يقضي بقطع الإشارات، والشخوص عن الأمارات والعلامات، بعد صحة التمكين والبراءة من التلوين.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-12","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الرابعة: الصحو، وهو عبارة عن تمكين حال المشاهدة، واتصالها، مع برء الروح من لدغات الدَّهَشِ، ولا يكمل الصحو إلا بحياة الروح بوارد الجمع الدائم.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-13","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الخامسة: التحقيق، وهو الوصول إلى المعرفة بالله، التي لا تدْركُ بالحواس، لتخليص المشرب من الحق بالحق في الحق، حتى تسقط المشاهدات، وتبطل العبارات، وتفنى الإشارات.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-14","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"السادسة: البسط، ونعني به: بسط الروح باسترسال شهود المعاني عند سقوط الأواني، وفي ذلك يقول ابن الفارض:","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-15","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"فما سكَنتْ والهمَ يوماً بموضِعٍ ... كذلك لم يسكُنْ مع النغَم الغَمُّ","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-16","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"السابعة: التلبيس، وهو تغطية الأسرار بأستار الأسباب، إبقاء للحكمة وستراً عن العامة.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-17","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"الثامنة: البقاء، والمراد به الخروج عن فناء المشاهدة إلى بقاء المعرفة، من غير أفول يخل بشمس المشاهدة، ولا رجوع إلى شواهد الحس، إنما هو استصحاب الجمع مع استئناس الروح بحلاوة المعاني، فهو كبائِن دانٍ. انظر بقيتها فى [بغية السالك] . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-135-136-18","r":"q3-135-136","title":"3:135–136 · Repentance, persistence in sin and eight named fruits of spiritual witnessing","text":"ثم قوّى قلوب أهل أحد لمّا انكسرت بالهزيمة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-135-136-18"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-135-136-s1","r":"q3-135-136","title":"Indecency, wrongdoing and the refusal to persist in sin","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Those who, when they commit an indecency ( فاحشة ),” that is, an act of extreme obscenity or ugliness, such as illicit sexual intercourse ( الزنا ), “or wrong themselves,” through any sin whatsoever. This may distinguish major and minor sins; or an indecency affecting another person as against wrongdoing confined to oneself; or indecency enacted through deeds as against wrongdoing committed in speech. “They remember God”: His punishment, wrath and the Great Presentation ( العرض الأكبر ); or they call to mind that God will interrogate them, and that He observes them; or they remember God with the tongue. “Then they seek forgiveness for their sins” through remorse and repentance ( الندم والتوبة ). “And who forgives sins but God?” No one other than God forgives them. Its purpose is to describe the breadth of His mercy, the universality of His forgiveness and the encouragement to seek it. “And they do not persist in what they have done,” that is, they do not continue in it without asking forgiveness. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is quoted as saying: “One who seeks forgiveness has not persisted [in sin], even if he returns to it seventy times in a day,” provided that his seeking forgiveness is joined with remorse. Another reported saying runs: “There is no major sin in the presence of seeking forgiveness, and no minor sin in the presence of persistence.” Qatāda warned: “Beware of persistence: those who persisted before you were ruined by advancing further in disobedience to God, without repenting until death came to them.” End of quotation. [XIV-N119] “While they know” that persistence injures them; or while they know they have a Lord who forgives sin. The Prophet is quoted as saying: “Whoever commits a sin and knows that he has a Lord who forgives sins is forgiven, even if he has not expressly asked forgiveness.” A divine saying ( حديث قدسي ) is also cited: “Whoever knows that I possess the power to forgive, I forgive him and do not mind.” In some revealed books there is the declaration: “Son of Adam, so long as you call upon Me and place your hope in Me, I will surely forgive you for whatever you have done, and I do not mind.” Alternatively, “while they know” refers to their recognition that repentance erases sins. Translator’s note: The reports are transcribed here as cited; the wording, attribution and transmission of each require independent hadith review. [XIV-N120] “Their recompense is forgiveness from their Lord,” the covering over of their sins, “and Gardens beneath which rivers flow, abiding therein.” The fact that Paradise is prepared for the repentant does not mean that it is exclusively theirs, just as the preparation of the Fire for unbelievers does not mean it is exclusively theirs. He then praises the recompense of the repentant: “How excellent is the reward of those who work!” Contemplate the enormous distinction between those who practice iḥsān ( المحسنون ) and the People of the Right ( أهل اليمين ). Of the former He says, “God loves the doers of beautiful good”; of the latter, “How excellent is the reward of those who work.” The people of the first verse belong among the beloved elect ( خواص الأحباب ), whereas those of the present verse receive their reward from beyond the door. God grants success, and He guides to the very heart of verification ( عين التحقيق ). [XIV-N121]","anchor":"en-q3-135-136-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-135-136-s2","r":"q3-135-136","title":"People of spiritual excellence and People of the Right","text":"For the people of the station of iḥsān ( أهل مقام الإحسان ), work belongs principally to the heart: generosity, forgiveness and restraining anger. For the People of the Right, work belongs to the bodily life, alternating between obedience and disobedience, heedlessness and wakefulness. When they commit indecency they repent and seek forgiveness; when they obey they rejoice and take comfort. The people of iḥsān are absent from contemplating their works and their separate existence ( غائبون عن رؤية أعمالهم ووجودهم ). The People of the Right rely upon their works: when they obey, hope grows; when they slip, hope diminishes. The people of iḥsān are effaced from themselves ( فانون عن أنفسهم ), subsisting through their Lord ( باقون بربهم ); the People of the Right remain conscious of their individual selves and observe their own works. The people of iḥsān are beloved ( محبوبون ), while the People of the Right are lovers ( مُحِبُّون ). For the first, formal marks and shapes ( الرسوم والأشكال ) vanish, and they behold only the existence of the Great and Exalted One ( وجود الكبير المتعال ). For the second, the created world still stands as independently present before them and the suns of gnosis ( شموس المعارف ) are absent from their hearts. The people of iḥsān worship through witnessing and direct vision ( الشهود والعيان ); the People of the Right worship from behind the veil of demonstration and discursive argument ( الدليل والبرهان ). From the viewpoint of those who witness directly, those who have only proof and argument are counted among the generality ( العموم ). [XIV-N122]","anchor":"en-q3-135-136-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-135-136-s3","r":"q3-135-136","title":"Fruits of knowledge through witnessing: eight of eleven are given here","text":"Know that the knowledge of witnessing and direct vision ( معرفة الشهود والعيان ) bears fruits and consequences ( ثمرات ونتائج ). One author has enumerated eleven qualities ; Ibn ʿAjība states eight here and directs the reader to Bughyat al-Sālik ( بغية السالك ) for the rest. [XIV-N123] First: Freedom ( الحرية ). The knower ( العارف ) becomes a solitary servant of the One Alone ( فرداً لِفَرْد ), without falling under the bondage of any existent thing, neither worldly aims nor aims attached to the Hereafter. Freedom thus means the ultimate refinement and purification of the self ( غاية التصفية والطهارة ). Someone said: “One who still has as much left to purify in his soul as can be sucked from a date-stone is not free.” A slave buying his freedom through a manumission contract ( المكاتب ) remains a slave as long as a single dirham is outstanding. [Translator’s note: Cairo I:410 prints فص نواة (faṣṣ nawāt). The translation follows the source reading مص نواة (maṣṣ nawāt, “sucking a date-stone”), physically verified in al-Sāḥilī’s Bughyat al-sālik (al-Mazīdī ed., Beirut, 1440/2019, p. 258). The earlier Risāla of al-Qushayrī, chapter on freedom (II:372, Dār al-Maʿārif; electronic primary text), likewise has maṣṣ in a question put to al-Junayd and follows it with the manumission comparison. An electronic Bughya apparatus reports omission of maṣṣ in witness B; that apparatus is not reproduced in the 2019 edition, and no image of B has been checked. The English expands the image of the slightest remaining worldly attachment. This remains a disclosed source-based correction of Cairo, not manuscript proof of Ibn ʿAjība’s wording; faṣṣ is preserved in the Arabic transcription.] Second: Finding or realization ( الوجود ). Attainment of the reality of things in their origin ( الفوز بحقيقة الأشياء في الأصل ), namely realizing a station in which formal traces ( الرسوم ) are effaced through total immersion in the pre-eternal Reality ( الحقيقة الأزلية ). Third: Complete gathering ( الجمع الأتم ). A state that entails ceasing to indicate by signs and passing beyond visible indicators and marks ( الأمارات والعلامات ), after stable realization ( التمكين ) and freedom from variability of spiritual state ( التلوين ). Fourth: Sobriety ( الصحو ). The stabilized and enduring state of witnessing ( تمكين حال المشاهدة واتصالها ), in which the spirit is healed of the piercing shocks of bewilderment ( الدَّهَش ). Sobriety does not reach perfection unless the spirit is enlivened through the continual influx of gathering ( وارد الجمع الدائم ). Fifth: Verification ( التحقيق ). Arrival at knowledge of God that cannot be grasped through the senses: the spiritual draught is purified “from the Real, through the Real, within the Real” ( من الحق بالحق في الحق ), until acts of witnessing fall away, verbal expressions lose their hold, and indicative gestures are effaced. Sixth: Expansion ( البسط ). The freeing of the spirit through an unbroken witnessing of meanings when the containers of sense ( الأواني ) have fallen away. Ibn al-Fāriḍ says: Never has [this wine] dwelt with sorrow in one place for a day; Thus distress cannot remain where melodies sound. Seventh: Veiling or disguise ( التلبيس ). The covering of spiritual mysteries ( الأسرار ) beneath the outward veils of causes ( أستار الأسباب ), so that the wisdom of the ordering of things may remain in place and the inner matters be hidden from the common people. Eighth: Subsistence ( البقاء ). Emerging from the effacement involved in witnessing ( فناء المشاهدة ) into the abiding permanence of knowledge ( بقاء المعرفة ), without any setting that dims the sun of witnessing and without returning to the evidences of sense. Rather, it is a carrying-forward of gathering ( استصحاب الجمع ), while the spirit takes delight in the sweetness of meanings. Thus the realized person is “separate yet near” ( كبائن دانٍ ). Consult Bughyat al-Sālik for the remaining qualities. And God grants success. [XIV-N123]","anchor":"en-q3-135-136-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-135-136-s4","r":"q3-135-136","title":"","text":"He then strengthened the hearts of the people of Uḥud after they had been broken by defeat.","anchor":"en-q3-135-136-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-137-139","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat 3:137–139","anchor":"unit-q3-137-139"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-1","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ سُنَنٌ فَسِيرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ فَانْظُروا كَيْفَ كانَ عاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ (137) هذا بَيانٌ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدىً وَمَوْعِظَةٌ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ (138) وَلا تَهِنُوا وَلا تَحْزَنُوا وَأَنْتُمُ الْأَعْلَوْنَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ (139)","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-2","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"قلت: السّنن: الطرق المسلوكة، وقيل: الأمم.","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-3","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قد مضت مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ سُنَنٌ جرت على الأمم المكذبة لأنبيائها قبلكم، وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لِسُنَّةِ اللَّهِ تَبْدِيلًا، وهو إمهالي واستدراجي إياهم، حتى يبلغ الكتاب الذي أجل لهم، فإذا بلغهم أهلكتهم، وأدلتُ الأنبياء وأتباعَهم عليهم، فإذا هلكوا بقيت آثارهم دارسة، اعتباراً لمن يأتي بعدهم، فَسِيرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ وتعرفوا أخبارهم، وانظروا كَيْفَ كانَ عاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ لأنبيائهم قبلكم، فكذلك يكون شأنكم مع مَنْ كذَّبكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-4","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"هذا الذي أمرتكم به من الاعتبار، بَيانٌ لِلنَّاسِ لمن أراد أن يعتبر من الكفار، وزيادة هداية واستبصار لِلْمُتَّقِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-5","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"ثم سلاَّهم وبشرهم فقال: وَلا تَهِنُوا أي: لا تضعفوا عن قتال عدوكم بما أصابكم، وَلا تَحْزَنُوا على من قُتل منكم، وهم سبعون من الأنصار وخمسة من المهاجرين، منهم: حمزة بن عبد المطلب، ومصعب بن عمير- صاحب راية النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وعبد الله بن جحش، وعثمان بن شماس، وسعد مولى عتبة- رضى الله عنهم-.","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-6","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"أو: (لا تحزنوا) لفوات الغنيمة وَأَنْتُمُ الْأَعْلَوْنَ بأن تكون لكم العاقبة والنصر، أو: وحالكم أنكم أعلى منهم شأناً، فإنكم على الحق وقتالكم لله، وقتلاكم في الجنة، وهم على الباطل، وقتالهم للشيطان، وقتلاهم في النار، فلا تفشلوا عن الجهاد إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ فإن الإيمان يقتضي قوة القلب بالوثوق بالله والاعتماد عليه، أو: (إن كنتم مؤمنين) بما وعدتكم من العلو والنصر. والله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-7","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"الإشارة: قد خلت من قبلكم، أيها المريدون، سنن الله في أوليائه مع المنكرين عليهم من عوام عباده، فإنه أبعدهم عن ساحة حضرته، وحرمهم من سابق عنايته، حتى ماتوا على البُعد، فاندرست آثارهم وخربت ديارهم، فسيروا في الأرض وانظروا كيف كان عاقبةُ المكذِّبين لأوليائه، هذا بيان للمعتبرين، وزيادة هدى وموعظة للمتقين، فلا تهنوا أيها الفقراء وتضعفوا عن طلب الحق بالرجوع عن طريق الجد والاجتهاد، لما يصيبكم من أذى أهل العناد، وأنتم الأعلون بالنصر والتأييد، ورفع درجاتكم مع خواص أهل التوحيد، إن كنتم مؤمنين بوعد الملك المجيد، فمن طلب الله وجده، وأنجز بالوفاء موعده، لكن بعد تجرع كؤوس مرارة الصبر، ودوام الحمد والشكر، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-8","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"لا تَحْسَب المجْد تَمْراً أَنْتَ آكِلُهُ ... لَنْ تَبْلُغَ المَجْدَ حَتَّى تَلْعَقَ الصّبر(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-137-139-9","r":"q3-137-139","title":"3:137–139 · Lessons from earlier nations and strength after defeat","text":"ثم سلاهم بمشاركة المكذبين فيما أصابهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-137-139-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-137-139-s1","r":"q3-137-139","title":"Sunan (سُنَن) as paths and recurring precedents","text":"I say: Sunan ( السُّنَن ) means paths that have been trodden; according to another explanation, it refers to the nations themselves. [XIV-N124]","anchor":"en-q3-137-139-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-137-139-s2","r":"q3-137-139","title":"The fate of those who deny and the patience of those who believe","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: Before you, patterns ( سُنَن ) took their course among peoples who denied their prophets, and “you shall never find any alteration in God’s pattern” [Q 33:62]. It belongs to His way that He gives them respite, leading them on by stages ( إمهال واستدراج ), until the appointed term He has written for them comes. Once it arrives, He destroys them and grants His prophets and their followers victory over them. After their destruction, their ruins remain as an admonition to those who follow. “Journey through the land” and discover their accounts; “consider how the deniers came to their end,” those who denied their prophets before you. The same will hold in your struggle with those who deny you. “This”—the reflection I have commanded you to undertake—“is an exposition for humankind,” for those among the disbelievers who wish to draw a lesson; and it is still further “guidance and admonition for the mindful.” Then He consoled the believers and gave them glad tidings: “Do not lose heart,” meaning do not become too weak to fight your enemy on account of what has happened to you; “and do not grieve” over those killed among you. Ibn ʿAjība counts seventy Helpers and five Emigrants, naming Ḥamza ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, Muṣʿab ibn ʿUmayr (bearer of the Prophet’s standard), ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaḥsh, ʿUthmān ibn Shammās and Saʿd, the freedman of ʿUtba, may God be pleased with them. Alternatively, “do not grieve” over lost booty. “You shall be uppermost”: the final outcome and victory will be yours, or you are already above them in rank because you stand upon the truth and fight for God, your dead enter Paradise, while they stand upon falsehood and fight for Satan and their dead enter the Fire. Do not fail in your striving “if you are believers,” for faith entails a heart strengthened by trusting and relying upon God—or if you believe what I promised of elevation and victory. God knows best. [XIV-N125]","anchor":"en-q3-137-139-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-137-139-s3","r":"q3-137-139","title":"The trials of the saints and the perseverance of disciples","text":"Before you, O disciples ( المريدون ), God’s established ways took effect among His friends ( أوليائه ) and those ordinary servants who rejected them. Such people were kept far from the court of His Presence and deprived of the solicitude He had previously offered, until they died at a distance, their traces disappearing and their dwellings falling to ruin. Travel the earth and look at the fate of those who denied His friends: this is an exposition for those willing to reflect, and added guidance and admonition for the mindful. Do not grow weary, O spiritual poor ( الفقراء ), or weaken in the quest for the Real by turning back from earnestness and effort because of injuries inflicted by obstinate people. You are the higher ones through divine help, reinforcement and the elevation of your ranks among the elect of the people of tawḥīd ( خواص أهل التوحيد ), if you truly believe the promise of the Glorious King. Whoever seeks God finds Him, and He fulfils what He has pledged—but only after one has drunk the bitter cups of patience and maintained praise and gratitude. They recite: Do not suppose glory is a ripe date you merely eat; You shall not attain glory until you lick bitter patience.","anchor":"en-q3-137-139-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-137-139-s4","r":"q3-137-139","title":"","text":"He then consoled them by recalling that those who had denied them had likewise suffered injury.","anchor":"en-q3-137-139-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-140-143","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance 3:140–143","anchor":"unit-q3-140-143"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-1","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"إِنْ يَمْسَسْكُمْ قَرْحٌ فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ قَرْحٌ مِثْلُهُ وَتِلْكَ الْأَيَّامُ نُداوِلُها بَيْنَ النَّاسِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنْكُمْ شُهَداءَ وَاللَّهُ لا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ (140) وَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَمْحَقَ الْكافِرِينَ (141) أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ جاهَدُوا مِنْكُمْ وَيَعْلَمَ الصَّابِرِينَ (142) وَلَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تَمَنَّوْنَ الْمَوْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ تَلْقَوْهُ فَقَدْ رَأَيْتُمُوهُ وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ (143)","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-2","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"قلت: القرح- بالفتح والضم-: الجرح، وقيل: بالفتح: الجرح، وبالضم: ألمه ووجعه. والمداولة: المفاعلة من الدولة، وهي الغلبة، و (الأيام) : نعت أو خبر، و (نداولها) : خبر أو حال، و (ليعلم) : متعلق بمحذوف، أي: وفعل","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-3","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"ما فعل من الإدالة ليعلم، أو عطف على عِلة محذوفة، أي: نداولها ليكون كيت وكيت، وليعلم ... الخ، إيذاناً بأن العلة فيه غير واحدة، وأن ما يصيب المؤمن: فيه من المصالح ما لا يُعلم، و (يعلم الصابرين) : منصوب بأن، على أنَّ الواو للجمع.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-4","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنْ يَمْسَسْكُمْ في غزوة أحد قَرْحٌ كقتل أو جرح، فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ من أعدائكم يوم بدر قَرْحٌ مِثْلُهُ، فإن كان قُتل منكم خمسة وسبعون يوم أحد، فقد قتل منهم يوم بدر سبعون وأسُرَ سبعون. أو: فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ يوم أحد قَرْحٌ مثل ما أصابكم، فإنكم نلتم منهم وهزمتموهم، قبل أن تخالفوا أمر الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، كما نالوا منكم يومئذ. وَتِلْكَ الْأَيَّامُ نُداوِلُها بَيْنَ النَّاسِ أي: نُصرف دولتها بينهم، فنديل لهؤلاء تارة ولهؤلاء أخرى، كما قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-5","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"فَيَوْمٌ عَلَيْنَا، ويَوْمٌ لنَا، ... ويَوْمٌ نُسَاءُ، ويَوْمٌ نُسَرْ(1)","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-6","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"فقد أديل المسلمون على المشركين يوم بدر، فكانت الدولة لهم، وأديل المشركون يوم أحد. والمراد بالأيام: أيام الدنيا، أو أيام النصر والغلبة. وإنما أديل للمشركين يوم أحد ليتميز المؤمنون من المنافقين، ويظهر علمهم للناس، وليتخذ الله مِنْكُمْ شُهَداءَ حين ماتوا في الجهاد، أكرمهم الله بالشهادة، ولا تدل إدالة المشركين على أن الله يحبهم، فإن الله لا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ. وإنما أدالهم لِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أي: ليطهرهم ويصفيهم من الذنوب، وإنما أدال المسلمين على المشركين ليمحق الكافرين ويقطع دابرهم. والمحق: نقص الشيء قليلاً قليلاً.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-7","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"ثم عاتب المسلمين فقال: أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أي: ظننتم أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ جاهَدُوا مِنْكُمْ علم ظهوره، وَيَعْلَمَ الصَّابِرِينَ أي: لا تظنوا أن تدخلوا الجنة كما دخلها مَنْ قُتل منكم، ولم يقع منكم مثل ما وقع لهم من الجهاد والصبر على القتل والجرح حتى يقع العلم ظاهراً بجهادكم وصبركم.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-8","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"وَلَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ قبل خروجكم إلى الجهاد تَمَنَّوْنَ الْمَوْتَ أي: الحرب لأنه سبب الموت، وتقولون: ليت لنا يوماً مثل يوم بدر، فلقد لقيتموه وعاينتموه يوم أحد وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ من مات من إخوانكم، فما لكم حين رأيتموه جبنتم وانهزمتم؟ وهو عتاب لمن طلب الخروج يوم أحد، ثم انهزم عن الحرب، ثم تداركهم بالتوبة والعفو، على ما يأتي إن شاء الله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-9","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"الإشارة: إن يمسسكم يا معشر الفقراء قرح كحبس أو ضرب أو سجن أو حَرج أو جلاء، فقد مس العموم مثل ذلك، غير أنكم تسيرون به إلى الله تعالى لمعرفتكم فيه، وهم لا سير لهم لعدم معرفتهم، أو إن يمسسكم قرح فقد مسَّ القوم المتقدمين من أهل الخصوصية مثل ما أصابكم، ففيهم أسوة لكم، وهذه عادة الله في أوليائه، يديل عليهم حتى يتطهروا ويتخلصوا، ثم يُديل لهم، وإنما أديل عليهم أولاً ليتطهروا من البقايا وتكمل فيهم المزايا، وليعلم","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-10","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"الصادق في الطلب من الكاذب، فإن محبة الله مقرونة بالبلاء، وليتخذ منهم شهداء إن ماتوا على ذلك، كالحلاج وغيره، أو يتخذ منهم شهداء الملكوت إن صبروا حتى ظفروا بالشهود. (والله لا يحب الظالمين) أي: المؤذين لأوليائه، بل يمقتهم ويبعدهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-11","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"(وليمحص الله الذين آمنوا) بطريق الخصوص، أي: يخلصهم من بقايا الحس، سلط عليهم الناس، وليَمحق المنكرين عليهم بما يصيبهم من إيذايتهم، فإن المنكر على أهل النسبة كمن يدخل يده في الغيران(1) ، فإذا سلم من الأول والثاني، قال: لا يلحقني منهم شيء، فإذا أدخل يده في غار آخر لدغته حية فأهلكته.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-12","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"أم حسبتم يا معشر المريدين أن تدخلوا جنة المعارف، ولما يعلم الله الذين جاهدوا نفوسهم، ويعلم الصابرين على إيذاية من آذاهم، ولقد كنتم تمنون موت نفوسكم وتطلبون ما يعينكم على موتها من قبل أن تلقوا الجلال، فقد رأيتموه وعاينتموه وأنتم تنظرون ما أصاب الأولياء غيركم، فما لكم تجزعون منه وتفرون من مواطنه؟. وكان شيخ شيوخنا رضي الله عنه يقول: العجب كل العجب، ممن يطلب معرفة الله، فإذا تعرف إليه أنكره.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-13","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"وفي الحِكَم: «إذا فتح الله لك وجهة من التعرف فلا تبال معها، وإن قلَّ عملك، فإنه ما فتحها إلاَّ وهو يريد أن يتعرف إليك فيها، ألم تعلم أن التعرف هو مورده عليك، والأعمال أنت مهديها إليه، وأين ما تهديه إليه مما هو مورده عليك؟» . وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-140-143-14","r":"q3-140-143","title":"3:140–143 · The alternation of fortune, testing and the meaning of perseverance","text":"ثم وبَّخهم على ما وقع لهم من الفشل، حين سمعوا بموت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-140-143-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-140-143-s1","r":"q3-140-143","title":"Qarḥ (قَرْح), alternation of victory and the syntax of purpose","text":"I say: Qarḥ ( القرح ), pronounced with fatḥa or ḍamma, means a wound. Alternatively, with fatḥa it is a wound and with ḍamma the pain and suffering of that wound. Mudāwala ( المداولة ) is the form expressing reciprocal action ( مفاعلة ) from dawla ( دولة ), a turn of victory or mastery. “These days” ( الأيام ) may be an adjective ( نعت ) or predicate ( خبر ), while “We cause them to alternate” ( نداولها ) may be the predicate ( خبر ) or a circumstantial clause ( حال ). “So that God may know” ( وليعلم ) is attached to an omitted expression ( محذوف ): “He did what He did in turning the fortunes of war so that He might know.” Or it may be coordinated with another omitted purpose: “We cause the days to alternate in order that such-and-such may happen, and that He might know ...,” indicating that there is more than one purpose and that believers’ sufferings involve benefits not fully known to us. “And know the patient” ( ويعلم الصابرين ) is in the subjunctive ( منصوب ) through an understood an ( أن ), the wāw (و) expressing accompaniment: the two acts of knowing occur together. [XIV-N126]","anchor":"en-q3-140-143-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-140-143-s2","r":"q3-140-143","title":"The two battles and the alternating fortunes of nations","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “If a wound touches you” at Uḥud—whether through deaths or bodily injuries—“a similar wound has touched the other people,” your opponents, at Badr. If seventy-five of you were killed at Uḥud, seventy of them had been killed and seventy captured at Badr. Or it means that a similar injury touched them during Uḥud itself: at first you struck them and put them to flight, before disobeying the Messenger’s command, just as they later struck you. [XIV-N127] “These days We cause to alternate among humankind”: We turn the possession of victory among them, giving it at one time to these people and another time to those. As the poet says: One day is against us, another day is ours; One day we suffer, another day we rejoice. The Muslims prevailed at Badr, and mastery was theirs; at Uḥud the idolaters prevailed. “Days” here may mean days of worldly life generally, or more particularly days of victory and mastery. God granted the idolaters a turn at Uḥud so that the believers might be distinguished from the hypocrites and their reality become publicly evident—“so that God may know those who believe,” in the sense of their state being manifested to people—and “take from among you witnesses” ( شهداء ), those who died in holy striving and were honoured with martyrdom ( شهادة ). The idolaters’ temporary success does not prove divine love for them: “God does not love wrongdoers.” He permitted their advantage “so that God may purify those who believe,” cleansing and refining them of sins. In turn, He grants the believers power over their opponents “so that He may wipe out the disbelievers.” Maḥq ( المحق ) means the gradual diminution of a thing until it disappears. [XIV-N128] Then He admonished the Muslims: “Or did you imagine that you would enter the Garden before God knew those who strove among you,” knowledge manifest in actual events ( علم ظهوره ), “and knew those who were patient?” Do not imagine that you can enter Paradise in the way those killed among you have entered without displaying striving and steadfastness like theirs under killing and injury, until your striving and patience become apparent in the world. “Before you went out to struggle, you used to wish for death,” meaning for battle, since battle can bring death. You would say, “If only we could have a day like Badr!” Now you have encountered what you wished for and seen it at Uḥud “while you looked on” as your brothers were killed. Why did some of you lose courage and flee when you saw it? This was a reproach of those who insisted upon going out at Uḥud but then retreated from combat. Yet God subsequently restored them through repentance and pardon, as will be explained, God willing. God Most High knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-140-143-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-140-143-s3","r":"q3-140-143","title":"The testing of seekers as purification and disclosure","text":"If a wound touches you, company of the spiritual poor, whether imprisonment, beating, detention, hardship or exile, a similar affliction has touched ordinary people. But through your knowledge of God within the affliction you advance toward Him, whereas they do not journey toward Him through it because they lack that knowledge. Or the verse can mean that a similar affliction touched earlier people of special spiritual realization ( أهل الخصوصية ): their example should reassure you. This is God’s practice with His friends: He grants others the upper hand over them until they are cleansed and purified, and only thereafter grants them the upper hand. At first they are tested so that what remains of their attachments ( البقايا ) may be cleansed and their gifts completed; the sincere seeker is distinguished from the insincere, for love of God is accompanied by trial. “He takes martyrs from among you” if they die in such tribulations, like al-Ḥallāj and others; or He takes witnesses of the Dominion ( شهداء الملكوت ) from those who persevere until they attain direct witnessing ( الشهود ). “God does not love wrongdoers,” those who injure His friends: rather, He detests them and sets them far away. “So that God may purify those who believe” along the path of special realization: He gives people power over them to cleanse them of the residues of sensory attachment ( بقايا الحس ). “And He may wipe out” those who reject them by reason of the wrongs they commit against them. The author compares someone who rejects the spiritually affiliated ( أهل النسبة ) to a person who thrusts his hand into successive caves. Having emerged safe from the first two, he says, “Nothing in them can harm me”; he then reaches into a third cave, where a snake bites and kills him. [XIV-N129] “Or did you think,” disciples, “that you would enter the Garden of direct knowledge ( جنة المعارف ) before God had made manifest those among you who struggle against their own souls ( جاهدوا نفوسهم ) and those who patiently endure others’ injuries?” You formerly desired the death of your ego-selves ( موت نفوسكم ) and sought what might help to bring it about. Now you have met Majesty ( الجلال ), seen it with your own eyes and witnessed what befell other saints. Why then do you panic at it and flee the places where it appears? The shaykh of our shaykhs used to say: “How utterly astonishing is a person who asks for knowledge of God, yet when God makes Himself known to him, he rejects Him.” In the Ḥikam ( الحكم ) one reads: “When God opens for you a direction through which He makes Himself known ( وجهة من التعرف ), do not concern yourself if your work is slight. He opened it only because He wants to make Himself known to you through it. Do you not know that self-disclosure ( التعرف ) is what He brings to you, while works are what you offer Him? How incomparable are what you offer Him and what He brings to you!” And God grants success. [XIV-N130]","anchor":"en-q3-140-143-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-140-143-s4","r":"q3-140-143","title":"","text":"He then reproached them for the faltering that followed their hearing the news that the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, had died.","anchor":"en-q3-140-143-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-144-145","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die 3:144–145","anchor":"unit-q3-144-145"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-1","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"وَما مُحَمَّدٌ إِلاَّ رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ أَفَإِنْ ماتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلى أَعْقابِكُمْ وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلى عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيْئاً وَسَيَجْزِي اللَّهُ الشَّاكِرِينَ (144) وَما كانَ لِنَفْسٍ أَنْ تَمُوتَ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ كِتاباً مُؤَجَّلاً وَمَنْ يُرِدْ ثَوابَ الدُّنْيا نُؤْتِهِ مِنْها وَمَنْ يُرِدْ ثَوابَ الْآخِرَةِ نُؤْتِهِ مِنْها وَسَنَجْزِي الشَّاكِرِينَ (145)","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-2","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"قلت: (كتاباً) : مصدر، أي: كتب الموت كتاباً مؤجلاً.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-3","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَما مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ يصيبه ما أصابهم، قَدْ مضت مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ، فسيمضي كما مضوا بالموت أو القتل، أَفَإِنْ ماتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلى أَعْقابِكُمْ بعد تقرر شريعته","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-4","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"وظهور براهينه، عاتبهم على تقدير أن لو صار منهم انقلاب لو مات صلّى الله عليه وسلم أو قتل، أو على ما صدر من بعض المنافقين وهم ساكتون.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-5","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"قال أصحاب المغازي: خرج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم حتى نزل بالشعب من أحُد، في سبعمائة رجل، وأمر عبد الله بن جبيرٍ على الرماة، وهم خمسون رجلاً، وقال: انضحوا عنا بالنبل، لا يأتونا من خلفنا، لا تبرحوا مكانكم كانت لنا أو علينا، فإنا لن نزال غالبين ما ثبتُّم مكانكم، فجاءت قريش، وعلى ميمنتهم خالد بن الوليد، وعلى ميسرتهم عكرمة، ومعهم النساء. ثم انتشب القتال فقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «مَنْ يأخذ هذا السيف بحقه» ؟ فجاء رجال فمنعهم، حتى جاء أبو دُجانة، فقال: وما حقه يا رسول الله؟ قال: «تضرب به العدو حتى ينحني» ، وكان رجلاً شجاعاً يختال عند الحرب، فأخذه واعتم بعمامة حمراء، وجعل يتبختر بين الصفين، فقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إنها لمشيةٌ يبغضها الله إلاّ في هذا الموضع» .","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-6","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"ثم حمل النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وأصحابه على المشركين فهزموهم، قال الزبير: (فرأيت هنداً وصواحبها هارباتٍ مصعدات في الجبل) ، فلما نظر الرماة إلى القوم قد انكشفوا، قالوا: الغنيمة الغنيمة فقال لهم بعضهم: لا تتركوا أمر النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فلم يلتفتوا، وانطلق عامتهم، فلما رأى خالد قلة الرماة، صاح في خيله من المشركين، ثم حمل على أصحاب النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم من خلفهم، وقتل عبد الله بن جبير، واختلط الناس، فقتل بعضُهم بعضاً، ورمى عبدُ الله بن قمئة الحارثي رسولَ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بحجر، فكسر أنفه ورباعيته، وشجَّه في وجهه، وكسر البيضة(1) على رأسه، فذبَّ عنه مصعبُ بن عمير، وكان صاحب الراية، فقتله ابن قمئة وهو يرى أنه قتل النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فرجع إلى قومه، وقال: قد قتلت محمداً، وصرخ صارخ: ألا إنَّ محمداً قد مات. وقيل: إنه الشيطان، فانكفأ الناس، وجعل الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- يدعو: «إليَّ عباد الله» ، فانحاز إليه ثلاثون من الصحابة، وضموه حتى كشفوا عنه المشركين، وأصيبت يد طلحة بن عبيد الله فيبست، حين وقى بها النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، وأصيبت عين قتادة بن النعمان، حتى وقعت على وجنتيه، فردها النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مكانها، فعادت أحسن مما كانت.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-7","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"وفشا في الناس أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم مات- فقال بعض المسلمين: ليت ابنُ أُبي يأخذ لنا أماناً من أبي سفيان.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-8","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"وقال بعض المنافقين: لو كان نبيّاً ما قتل، ارجعوا إلى دينكم الأول. فقال أنس بن النضر- عمُّ أنس بن مالك: (إن كان قد قتل محمدٌ فَإِنَّ رب محمد لا يموت، وما تصنعون بالحياة بعده؟ فقاتلوا على ما قاتل عليه، حتى تموتوا على ما مات عليه) . ثم قال: اللهم إني أعتذر إليك مما صنع هؤلاء- يعني المسلمين- وأبرأ إليك مما صنع هؤلاء- يعني الكفار-، ثم شدّ سيفه وقاتل حتى قُتل، رحمة الله عليه.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-9","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"فأنزل فيما قال المنافقون: وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلى عَقِبَيْهِ بارتداده فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيْئاً وإنما يضر نفسه، وَسَيَجْزِي اللَّهُ الشَّاكِرِينَ على نعمة الإسلام بالثبات عليه، كأنس وأضرابه، وَما كانَ ينبغي لِنَفْسٍ أَنْ تَمُوتَ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ أي: بإرادته ومشيئته، أو بإذنه لملكٍ في قبض روحه، والمعنى: أنَّ لكل نفس أجلاً مسمى في علمه تعالى وقضائه، لا تستأخر عنه ساعة ولا تستقدم، بالتأخر عن القتال ولا بالإقدام عليه، وفيه تشجيعهم على القتال ووعد للرسول بحفظه وتأخر أجله فإن الله تعالى كتب أجل الموت كِتاباً مُؤَجَّلًا مؤقتاً لا يتقدم ولا يتأخر.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-10","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"ونزل في الرماة الذين خالفوا المركز للغنيمة: وَمَنْ يُرِدْ ثَوابَ الدُّنْيا نُؤْتِهِ مِنْها وَمَنْ يُرِدْ ثَوابَ الْآخِرَةِ نُؤْتِهِ مِنْها الجزاء الجليل، وَسَنَجْزِي الشَّاكِرِينَ الذين شكروا نعم الله، فلم يشغلهم شيء عن الجهاد في سبيل الله، بل كان همهم رضى الله ورسوله دون شيء سواه.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-11","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"الإشارة: ينبغي للمريد أن يستغني بالله، فلا يركن إلى شيء سواه، وتكون بصيرته نافذة حتى يغيب عن الواسطة بشهود الموسوط، فإن مات شيخه لم ينقلب على عقبيه، فإن تمكن من الشهود فقد استغنى عن كل موجود، وإن لم يتمكن نظر من يكمله، فالوقوف مع الوسائط وقوف مع النعم دون شهود المنعم، فلا يكون شاكراً للمْنعم حتى لا يحجبه عنه شيء، ولما مات- عليه الصلاة والسلام- دهشت الناس، وتحيّرت لوقوفهم مع شهود النعمة، إلاَّ الصدِّيق كان نفذ من شهود النعمة إلى شهود المُنعم، فخطب حينئذٍ على الناس، وقال: (مَنْ كانَ يَعْبُدُ مُحَمَّداً فإن مُحَمَّداً قَدْ ماتَ، ومَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ فإنَّ اللهَ حَيٌ لاَ يَمُوتِ) . ثم قرأ: وَما مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ ... إلى قوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-12","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"وَسَيَجْزِي الشَّاكِرِينَ، وهم الذين نفذوا إلى شهود المنعم، ولم يقفوا مع النعمة.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-13","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"ودخل بعض العارفين على بعض الفقراء فوجده يبكي، فقال له: ما يبكيك؟ قال: مات أستاذي، فقال له العارف: ولم جعلت أستاذك يموت؟ وهلا جعلته حيّاً لا يموت. فنبهه على نفاذ بصيرته إلى شهود المنعم دون الوقوف مع النعمة، فالشيخ الحقيقي هو الذي يغني صاحبه عنه وعن غيره، بالدلالة على ربه.","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-144-145-14","r":"q3-144-145","title":"3:144–145 · The Prophet’s mortality, the field of Uḥud and dependence upon the One who does not die","text":"ثم صبّرهم بما وقع لغيرهم قبلهم فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-144-145-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-144-145-s1","r":"q3-144-145","title":"Kitāban muʾajjalan (كِتاباً مُؤَجَّلاً)","text":"I say: “In writing, at an appointed time” ( كتاباً مؤجلاً ): kitāban ( كتاباً ) is a verbal noun ( مصدر ), meaning, “He wrote or decreed death as a writing whose time has been appointed.” [XIV-N131]","anchor":"en-q3-144-145-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-144-145-s2","r":"q3-144-145","title":"A report of death does not abolish the message","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “Muḥammad is only a messenger,” susceptible to what befell the messengers before him: “Messengers have passed away before him”; he too shall pass away as they did, through death or killing. “If he dies or is killed, will you turn back upon your heels,” after his revealed Law ( شريعة ) has been established and his proofs made manifest? God rebukes them for the possibility of an actual reversal should the Prophet die or be killed—or for the remarks already made by certain hypocrites while the others remained silent. [XIV-N132] According to the authors of the military narratives ( أصحاب المغازي ), the Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, marched to the ravine of Uḥud with seven hundred men. He appointed ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jubayr over fifty archers and instructed them: “Drive the attackers away with arrows so that they do not come upon us from behind. Do not leave your post whether we win or lose, for we shall remain victorious as long as you stay in your positions.” The Quraysh arrived, Khālid ibn al-Walīd on their right wing and ʿIkrima on their left, with women accompanying the forces. [XIV-N133] When the fighting began the Prophet asked: “Who will take this sword and discharge its right?” A number of men came, but he withheld it until Abū Dujāna approached. “What is its right, Messenger of God?” he asked. He answered: “That you strike the enemy with it until it bends.” Abū Dujāna was courageous and moved proudly in battle. Taking the sword, he wrapped a red turban around his head and strode between the two armies with a swagger. The Prophet said: “God hates such a way of walking, except in this place.” [XIV-N133] The Prophet and his Companions then charged the idolaters and put them to flight. Al-Zubayr said: “I saw Hind and her companions fleeing up the mountain.” When the archers saw the enemy retreat, they cried, “The spoils! The spoils!” Some among them warned: “Do not abandon the Prophet’s instruction!” Most paid no heed and left. Seeing that few archers remained, Khālid called his cavalry of the idolaters, charged the Muslims from the rear and killed ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jubayr. Men became entangled in the confusion and some killed others of their own side. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qamiʾa al-Ḥārithī struck the Prophet with a stone, breaking his nose and an incisor, wounding his face and breaking the helmet upon his head. Muṣʿab ibn ʿUmayr, who carried the standard, defended him, but Ibn Qamiʾa killed Muṣʿab believing he had killed the Prophet. He returned to his people crying, “I have killed Muḥammad.” Another cry spread: “Muḥammad has died!” Some said the cry came from Satan. The Muslim fighters fell back. The Messenger called, “Come to me, servants of God!” Thirty Companions rallied around him, formed a protective ring and drove off the idolaters. Ṭalḥa ibn ʿUbayd Allāh’s hand was wounded and became paralysed while protecting him; Qatāda ibn al-Nuʿmān’s eye was struck so that it fell upon his cheek. The source relates that the Prophet restored it to its place and it became better than before. [XIV-N134] The rumour of the Prophet’s death spread. Some Muslims said, “If only Ibn Ubayy could obtain for us a guarantee of safety from Abū Sufyān.” Some hypocrites said: “Had he been a prophet, he would not have been killed. Return to your former religion.” Anas ibn al-Naḍr, the uncle of Anas ibn Mālik, replied: “If Muḥammad has been killed, the Lord of Muḥammad does not die. What would you do with life after him? Fight for what he fought for, until you die upon what he died upon.” He then prayed: “God, I offer my apology for what these”—meaning the Muslims—“have done, and I dissociate myself before You from what these”—meaning the unbelievers—“have done.” He took up his sword and fought until killed. May God show him mercy. [XIV-N135] Concerning the hypocrites’ speech God revealed: “Whoever turns back upon his heels,” by abandoning his religion, “will not harm God in the least,” but will only injure himself. “God will reward the thankful,” those who thank Him for the gift of Islam by remaining steadfast, as Anas ibn al-Naḍr and others like him did. “No soul can die except by God’s permission”: through His will and volition, or through His permission to an angel charged with taking that soul. Every soul has a named term within God’s knowledge and decree; it cannot be delayed by an hour nor brought forward, either by holding back from battle or by plunging into it. This encourages steadfastness in fighting and promises preservation of the Messenger until his appointed term has elapsed. God has written death “as a writing with an appointed time”: its term neither advances nor retreats. [XIV-N136] Concerning the archers who forsook their assigned position for the sake of booty, God revealed: “Whoever desires the reward of this world, We give him some of it; and whoever desires the reward of the Hereafter, We give him some of it,” a noble recompense. “We will reward the thankful”: those who truly thank God for His gifts, letting nothing divert them from striving in His path and desiring nothing but the pleasure of God and His Messenger.","anchor":"en-q3-144-145-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-144-145-s3","r":"q3-144-145","title":"The death of a master and the independence of the disciple’s vision","text":"The disciple should seek sufficiency in God ( الاستغناء بالله ), resting upon none other than Him. His spiritual insight ( بصيرة ) should penetrate so deeply that he is absent to the intermediary ( الواسطة ) through witnessing the One mediated ( الموسوط ). If his spiritual master dies, he will not turn back upon his heels. If he is firmly established in witnessing ( الشهود ), he has become independent of every created existent. If he has not attained establishment, he seeks someone who can bring him to completion. To remain fixed on the intermediaries is to remain at the gifts without witnessing the Giver ( المنعم ). He is not fully thankful to the Giver until nothing can veil Him from him. [XIV-N137] When the Prophet died, people were stunned and bewildered because they stood at the gift and what they had witnessed of it. The Truthful One ( الصدِّيق ), however, had passed beyond witnessing the gift to witnessing the Giver. He addressed the people, saying: “Whoever worshipped Muḥammad should know that Muḥammad has died; whoever worships God should know that God is Ever-Living and does not die.” He then recited: “Muḥammad is only a messenger ...” down to “He shall reward the thankful.” These are those who pass through to the witnessing of the Giver and do not remain with the gift. [XIV-N138] One of the knowers ( العارفين ) visited a spiritual poor man ( فقير ) and found him weeping. “Why are you weeping?” he asked. “My teacher has died,” the man replied. The knower asked: “Why did you make your teacher one who dies? Why not make your teacher the Living One who does not die?” He awakened him to the need to penetrate through to the Giver rather than stopping at the gift. For the authentic spiritual teacher is the one who makes his companion independent of the teacher himself and of all others by directing him to his Lord.","anchor":"en-q3-144-145-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-144-145-s4","r":"q3-144-145","title":"","text":"He then called them to patience through the example of what earlier followers had endured.","anchor":"en-q3-144-145-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-146-148","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings 3:146–148","anchor":"unit-q3-146-148"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-1","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"وَكَأَيِّنْ مِنْ نَبِيٍّ قُتِلَ مَعَهُ رِبِّيُّونَ كَثِيرٌ فَما وَهَنُوا لِما أَصابَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَما ضَعُفُوا وَمَا اسْتَكانُوا وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الصَّابِرِينَ (146) وَما كانَ قَوْلَهُمْ إِلاَّ أَنْ قالُوا رَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لَنا ذُنُوبَنا وَإِسْرافَنا فِي أَمْرِنا وَثَبِّتْ أَقْدامَنا وَانْصُرْنا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكافِرِينَ (147) فَآتاهُمُ اللَّهُ ثَوابَ الدُّنْيا وَحُسْنَ ثَوابِ الْآخِرَةِ وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ (148)","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-2","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"قلت: (كأَيِّن) : أصله: أيْ، دخلت الكاف عليها وصارت بمعنى (كم) ، وأثبت التنوين نوناً على غير قياس، وقرأ ابن كثير: (وكائن) ، على وزن فاعل، ووجهه: أنه قلب الياء قبل الهمزة فصار: كيَاءٍ، تحركت الياء وانفتح ما قبلها فصار كائن، وهما لغتان، وقد جمع الشاعر بينهما في بيت، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-3","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"كَأيّنْ أبَدْنَا مِنْ عَدوٍّ بعِزِّنا ... وكَائِنْ أجَرْنا مِنْ ضَعيفٍ وخائِفِ","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-4","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"و (الرِبِّيون) : جمع رُبَّة، أي: الفرقة. أي: معه جموع كثيرة، وقيل: العلماء الأتقياء، وقيل: الولاة، وهو: إما مبتدأ فيوقف على (قُتل) ، أو نائب فاعل (قُتل) ، أو فاعل على من قرأ بالبناء له، و (كثير) : نعت له، كقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-5","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"وَالْمَلائِكَةُ بَعْدَ ذلِكَ ظَهِيرٌ لأن فعيلاً يخبر به عن المفرد والجمع.","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-6","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَكَأَيِّنْ وكم مِنْ نَبِيٍّ قُتِلَ في المعركة ومعه جموع كثيرة، أو ربانيون علماء أتقياء، فلم يفشلوا ولم يضعفوا، بل ثبتوا على دينهم وجهاد عدوهم، أو يقول: كثير من الأنبياء قتل معهم ربانيون كثير، أي: ماتوا في الحرب فثبت الباقون، ولم يفتروا ولم يضعفوا عن عدوهم، ويترجح الأول بما صرَخَ به الصارخ يوم أحد: إن محمدا قد مات، فضرب لهم المثل بقوله: وَكَأَيِّنْ مِنْ نَبِيٍّ قُتِلَ، ويترجح الثاني بأنه لم يقتل نبيّ قط في المحاربة.","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-7","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"أو: وَكَأَيِّنْ مِنْ نَبِيٍّ قاتَلَ أي: جاهد معه رِبِّيُّونَ كَثِيرٌ، وبعد ما قتل نبيهم أو جموعهم فَما وَهَنُوا لِما أَصابَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أي: فما فتروا، ولم ينكسر جندهم لأجل ما أصابهم من قتل نبيهم أو بعضهم، وَما ضَعُفُوا عن جهاد عدوهم ولا عن دينهم، وَمَا اسْتَكانُوا أي: خضعوا لعدوهم، من السكون لأن الخاضع يسكن لعدوه يفعل به ما يريد، فالألف إشباع زائد، أي: فما سكنوا لعدوهم بل صبروا له، وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الصَّابِرِينَ فينصرهم ويعزهم ويُعظم قدرهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-8","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"وَما كانَ قَوْلَهُمْ عند قتل نبيهم مع ثباتهم على دينه، إِلَّا أَنْ قالُوا رَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لَنا ذُنُوبَنا الصغائر، وَإِسْرافَنا فِي أَمْرِنا أي: ما تجاوزنا به الحد في أمر ذنوبنا، كالكبائر، وَثَبِّتْ أَقْدامَنا في مداحض الحرب لئلا ننهزم، وَانْصُرْنا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكافِرِينَ من أعدائنا، فَهلاَّ فعلتم مثلهم، وقلتم ذلك يا أصحاب محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-9","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"فَآتاهُمُ اللَّهُ في ثواب الاستغفار واللجوء إلى الله ثَوابَ الدُّنْيا وهو النصر والغنيمة والعز وحسن الذكر، وَحُسْنَ ثَوابِ الْآخِرَةِ وهو النعيم الذي لا يفنى ولا يبيد، وخص ثواب الآخرة بالحسن إشعاراً بفضله، وأنه المعتد به عنده، وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ الثابتين على دينهم، لأنهم أحسنوا فيما بينهم وبين ربهم بحفظ دينه، فأحبهم الله وقربهم إلى حضرته.","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-10","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"الإشارة: وكم من المريدين والأتباع مات شيخهم أو قتل، فثبتوا على طريقهم، فما فَشِلوا ولا ضعفوا، ولا خضعوا لمن يقطعهم عن ربهم، بل صبروا على السير إلى ربهم، أو الترقي في المقامات، ومن لم يرشد منهم طلب من يكمل له، (والله يحب الصابرين) ، فإذا أحبهم كان سمعهم وبصرهم، كما في الحديث. وما كان حالهم عند موت شيخهم إلا الالتجاء إلى ربهم، والاستغفار مما بقي من مساوئهم، وطلب الثبات في مواطن حرب أنفسهم، فأعطاهم الله عزّ الدنيا والآخرة، عزّ الدنيا بالإيمان والمعرفة، وعزّ الآخرة بدوام المشاهدة، فكانوا أحباب الله (والله يحب المحسنين) .","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-146-148-11","r":"q3-146-148","title":"3:146–148 · The ribbiyyūn: steadfast followers, devotion after losing one’s teacher and competing Qurʾānic readings","text":"ثم حذّرهم الله تعالى من الركون إلى عدوهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-146-148-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-146-148-s1","r":"q3-146-148","title":"Kaʾayyin (كَأَيِّن), ribbiyyūn (رِبِّيُّون), and qātala/qutila","text":"I say: Kaʾayyin ( كَأَيِّن ) originally consisted of ayy ( أي ) preceded by kāf (ك), becoming a word meaning “how many” ( كم ). Its tanwīn was established as a nūn in a way that does not follow the usual analogy ( على غير قياس ). Ibn Kathīr’s reading is kāʾin ( وكائن ), on the pattern of an active participle ( فاعل ). It can be explained by metathesis ( قلب ), the yāʾ coming before the hamza, yielding kayāʾ ( كياء ); when the yāʾ acquired a vowel and the preceding letter had fatḥa, it became kāʾin . These are two attested linguistic forms. One poet combined them in a single verse: How many an enemy ( كَأَيِّن ) we destroyed through our might, And how many a weak and fearful person ( كَائِن ) we protected. Ribbiyyūn ( الرِبِّيُّون ) is explained as the plural of rubba ( رُبَّة ), meaning a company or group; hence “many companies fought with him.” Other explanations make the word “devout, Godfearing scholars” ( العلماء الأتقياء ), or rulers ( الولاة ). The noun may be the subject ( مبتدأ ) of a new clause if one stops at a reading meaning “was killed” ( قُتِل ), or it may be the passive subject ( نائب فاعل ) of that form, or the agent/subject ( فاعل ) if one reads the verb in the active ( بالبناء للفاعل ). “Many” ( كثير ) qualifies ribbiyyūn , as in “and the angels, after that, are supporters” [Q 66:4]; a word on the pattern faʿīl can be predicated of singulars and plurals alike. [XIV-N139]","anchor":"en-q3-146-148-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-146-148-s2","r":"q3-146-148","title":"The followers of former prophets","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “How many a prophet was killed” in battle, with great companies or Godfearing scholars accompanying him, and they did not fail or grow weak. Rather, they stood firm in their faith and in their struggle against the enemy. Or the verse may be understood as: how many prophets had numerous devoted followers who were killed fighting alongside them? The survivors remained steadfast and did not grow languid or weak before the enemy. The first interpretation is strengthened by the cry heard at Uḥud that Muḥammad had died, for God set before them an exemplary contrast through “how many a prophet was killed”; the other is said to gain support from the assertion that no prophet was ever killed in open battle. [XIV-N140] Alternatively, “How many a prophet fought” means that many devoted followers struggled alongside him; even after their prophet or some of their own number were killed, “they did not lose heart because of what befell them in God’s path.” They did not slacken or lose cohesion because of their prophet’s death or the killing of some of their men; “nor did they weaken” in fighting or adhering to their religion; “nor did they submit,” meaning yield to their enemy. Ibn ʿAjība connects istakānū ( استكانوا ) with sukūn ( السكون ), the stillness of someone who submits to an opponent and lets that opponent do whatever he wishes, regarding the alif as an added prolongation. Rather, they persevered, and “God loves the patient,” granting them victory, dignity and exalted standing. “Their words,” when their prophet was killed and they had remained firm in his religion, “were nothing but: ‘Our Lord, forgive us our sins,’” meaning lesser sins, “and our excess in our affair,” the ways in which they exceeded the bounds through graver sins; “and make our feet firm” where footing slips in battle so that we do not flee; “and grant us victory over the disbelieving people,” our enemies. Why did you not do as they did and pray thus, O Companions of Muḥammad, blessings and peace be upon him? “God gave them,” in recompense for seeking forgiveness and seeking refuge in Him, “the reward of this world”: victory, booty, honour and good repute; and “the excellent reward of the Hereafter,” everlasting bliss. The latter reward is specially called excellent to mark its superiority and the weight it carries with Him. “God loves those who do beautiful good ( المحسنين ),” those who stand firm in their religion, for they treated their Lord well by safeguarding His religion, and God therefore loved them and brought them near to His Presence.","anchor":"en-q3-146-148-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-146-148-s3","r":"q3-146-148","title":"A disciple’s steadfastness after the death of a master","text":"How many disciples and followers ( المريدين والأتباع ) have had their shaykh die or be killed, yet held fast to their path! They neither lost heart nor weakened nor submitted to those who would sever them from their Lord. Instead they patiently persevered in the journey toward God ( السير إلى ربهم ) or in the ascent through stations ( الترقي في المقامات ). Whoever had not yet received complete guidance sought another to complete it. “God loves the patient”; and when He loves them, He becomes their hearing and sight, as the hadith puts it. [XIV-N141] On losing their shaykh they had no recourse but to turn toward their Lord, seek forgiveness for the faults still remaining in them, and ask to be made firm upon the battlegrounds where they fought their own souls. God accordingly gave them honour in both abodes: honour in this world through faith and gnosis ( الإيمان والمعرفة ), and honour in the next through perpetual witnessing ( دوام المشاهدة ). Thus they were among God’s beloved: “God loves those who do beautiful good.”","anchor":"en-q3-146-148-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-146-148-s4","r":"q3-146-148","title":"","text":"God then warned them not to rely upon their adversaries.","anchor":"en-q3-146-148-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-149-150","r":"q3-149-150","title":"3:149–150 · Allegiance under pressure and steadfastness in spiritual detachment","text":"3:149–150 · Allegiance under pressure and steadfastness in spiritual detachment 3:149–150","anchor":"unit-q3-149-150"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-149-150-1","r":"q3-149-150","title":"3:149–150 · Allegiance under pressure and steadfastness in spiritual detachment","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تُطِيعُوا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يَرُدُّوكُمْ عَلى أَعْقابِكُمْ فَتَنْقَلِبُوا خاسِرِينَ (149) بَلِ اللَّهُ مَوْلاكُمْ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ النَّاصِرِينَ (150)","anchor":"ar-q3-149-150-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-149-150-2","r":"q3-149-150","title":"3:149–150 · Allegiance under pressure and steadfastness in spiritual detachment","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تُطِيعُوا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وهم المنافقون، لما قالوا للمسلمين عند الهزيمة: ارجعوا إلى دينكم الأول، ولو كان نبيّاً ما قتل، يَرُدُّوكُمْ عَلى أَعْقابِكُمْ راجعين عن إيمانكم، فَتَنْقَلِبُوا خاسِرِينَ مفتونين عن دينكم، فتحبط أعمالكم فتخسروا الدنيا والآخرة، بل اثبتوا على إيمانكم، فإن الله مَوْلاكُمْ سينصركم ويعزكم، وَهُوَ خَيْرُ النَّاصِرِينَ، وقيل: إن تسكنوا إلى أبي سفيان وأشياعه وتستأمنوهم يردوكم إلى دينهم. وقيل: عام في مطاوعة الكفرة والنزول على حكمهم فإنه يجر إلى موافقتهم على دينهم، لا سيما إن طالت مدة الاستئمان.","anchor":"ar-q3-149-150-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-149-150-3","r":"q3-149-150","title":"3:149–150 · Allegiance under pressure and steadfastness in spiritual detachment","text":"قلت: وهذا هو السبب في ارتداد من بقي من المسلمين بالأندلس حتى رجعوا نصارى، هم وأولادهم، والعياذ بالله من سوء القضاء.","anchor":"ar-q3-149-150-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-149-150-4","r":"q3-149-150","title":"3:149–150 · Allegiance under pressure and steadfastness in spiritual detachment","text":"الإشارة: يا أيها المريدون- وخصوصاً المتجردين- إن تطيعوا العامة، وتركنوا إليهم، يردوكم على أعقابكم فتنقلبوا خاسرين بطلب الدنيا وتعاطي أسبابها، فتزلَّ قدمٌ بعد ثُبْوتها، وتنحط من الهمة العالية إلى الهمة السفلى، فإن الطباع تُسرق، والمرء على دين خليله، بل اثبتوا على التجريد وتحقيق التوحيد، فإن الله مولاكم (وهو خير الناصرين) فينصركم ويعزكم ويغنيكم بلا سبب، كما وعدكم وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَهُ مَخْرَجاً وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لا يَحْتَسِبُ.","anchor":"ar-q3-149-150-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-149-150-5","r":"q3-149-150","title":"3:149–150 · Allegiance under pressure and steadfastness in spiritual detachment","text":"ولّما انصرف أبو سفيان من أحد، قال: بئس ما صنعنا! قتلنا القوم ولم يبق إلا اليسير، ارجعوا حتى نستأصلهم، فألقى الله في قلبه الرعب، كما قال:","anchor":"ar-q3-149-150-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-149-150-s1","r":"q3-149-150","title":"Competing identifications of those to be obeyed","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: “O you who believe, if you obey those who disbelieve”—understood here as the hypocrites who, at the time of the defeat, said to Muslims, “Return to your former religion; if he had been a prophet, he would not have been killed”—“they will turn you back upon your heels,” away from your faith, “so you will return as losers,” seduced from your religion so that your works become futile and you lose both abodes. Rather, remain firm in faith: “God is your protecting Master ( مولاكم )”; He will grant you help and honour, “and He is the best of helpers.” According to another explanation: if you seek reassurance and protection from Abū Sufyān and his followers and rely upon them, they will bring you back to their religion. Or the wording is general: obeying unbelievers and submitting to their decisions leads to agreement with them in religion, particularly when the dependence extends over a long period. [XIV-N142] I say: This is the cause of the apostasy of the Muslims who remained in al-Andalus, until they and their children became Christians. We seek refuge in God from an evil decree. Translator’s note: This reproduces the author’s historical generalization; it is not independently verified here for every surviving Andalusi Muslim or family. [XIV-N143]","anchor":"en-q3-149-150-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-149-150-s2","r":"q3-149-150","title":"Steadfastness in tajrīd when the world calls one back","text":"O disciples, especially those who have entered detachment ( المتجردين ): if you obey the common people and rely upon them, they will turn you back upon your heels, and you will become losers through seeking worldly life and occupying yourselves with its means. A foot slips after it had been firmly planted, and high aspiration ( الهمة العالية ) sinks into the low. Natures borrow from one another ( الطباع تُسرق ); a person follows the religion or way of his intimate friend ( المرء على دين خليله ). Rather, remain firm in detachment ( التجريد ) and in realizing divine unity ( تحقيق التوحيد ), for “God is your protecting Master, and He is the best of helpers.” He will help, honour and enrich you without dependence on external means, as He has promised: “Whoever is mindful of God, He grants him a way out and provides for him from where he did not reckon” [Q 65:2–3]. [XIV-N144]","anchor":"en-q3-149-150-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-149-150-s3","r":"q3-149-150","title":"","text":"When Abū Sufyān withdrew from Uḥud, he said: “How badly we acted! We killed the men and only a few remain. Let us return and destroy them utterly.” God cast terror into his heart, as the following verse describes.","anchor":"en-q3-149-150-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-151","r":"q3-151","title":"3:151 · Terror, idolatry, and the safety of the spiritual poor","text":"3:151 · Terror, idolatry, and the safety of the spiritual poor 3:151","anchor":"unit-q3-151"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-151-1","r":"q3-151","title":"3:151 · Terror, idolatry, and the safety of the spiritual poor","text":"سَنُلْقِي فِي قُلُوبِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا الرُّعْبَ بِما أَشْرَكُوا بِاللَّهِ ما لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهِ سُلْطاناً وَمَأْواهُمُ النَّارُ وَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الظَّالِمِينَ (151)","anchor":"ar-q3-151-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-151-2","r":"q3-151","title":"3:151 · Terror, idolatry, and the safety of the spiritual poor","text":"قلت: (الرعب) : الخوف، وفيه الضم والسكون، وهكذا كل ثلاثي ساكن الوسط، كالقدس والعسر واليسر، وشبه ذلك، و (بما أشركوا) : مصدرية.","anchor":"ar-q3-151-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-151-3","r":"q3-151","title":"3:151 · Terror, idolatry, and the safety of the spiritual poor","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: سنقذف فِي قُلُوبِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا كأبي سفيان وأصحابه، الرُّعْبَ والخوف، حتى يرجعوا عنكم بلا سبب، بسبب شركهم بالله ما لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهِ سُلْطاناً ولا حجة على استحقاق العبادة، وَمَأْواهُمُ النَّارُ أي: هي مقامهم، وَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الظَّالِمِينَ أي: قبح مقامهم. ووضع الظاهر موضع المضمر للتغليظ في العلة.","anchor":"ar-q3-151-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-151-4","r":"q3-151","title":"3:151 · Terror, idolatry, and the safety of the spiritual poor","text":"الإشارة: فيها تسلية للفقراء، فإنَّ كل من هم بإذايتهم ألقى الله في قلبه الرعب، حتى لا يقدر أن يتوصل إليهم بشيء مما أمَّل فيهم، وقد رأيتهم هموا بقتلهم وضربهم وحبسهم، وسعوا في ذلك جهدهم، وعملوا في ذلك بينات على زعمهم، تُوجب قتلهم، فكفاهم الله أمرهم، وألقى الرعب في قلوبهم، فانقلبوا خائبين وماتوا ظالمين، والله ولى المتقين.","anchor":"ar-q3-151-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-151-5","r":"q3-151","title":"3:151 · Terror, idolatry, and the safety of the spiritual poor","text":"ثم ذكّرهم الله تعالى ما وعدهم من النصر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-151-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-151-s1","r":"q3-151","title":"The pronunciation of ruʿb and the causal construction","text":"I say: Ruʿb ( الرُّعْب ) is fear; its middle consonant may be pronounced with ḍamma or without a vowel ( السكون ), as with quds, ʿusr, yusr and other triliteral nouns with a vowelless middle consonant. In bimā ashrakū ( بِمَا أَشْرَكُوا ), mā is maṣdariyya ( مصدرية ), making the clause equivalent to a verbal noun.","anchor":"en-q3-151-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-151-s2","r":"q3-151","title":"Fear caused by association without authority","text":"The Real, exalted is His majesty, says: We shall cast terror and fear into the hearts of those who disbelieve, such as Abū Sufyān and his companions, so that they withdraw from you even without some outward cause. This comes because they associate with God that for whose entitlement to worship He has revealed no authority ( سلطان ) or proof ( حجة ). Their refuge and dwelling is the Fire. “How evil is the abode of the wrongdoers!” The explicit noun “wrongdoers” stands in place of the pronoun ( إظهار في موضع الإضمار ), making the reason for condemnation more forceful.","anchor":"en-q3-151-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-151-s3","r":"q3-151","title":"God's protection of the spiritual poor","text":"This offers consolation to the spiritual poor ( الفقراء ): whoever intends to injure them finds God casting fear into his heart, so that he cannot accomplish what he hoped against them. I have seen people resolve to kill, beat or imprison them, exerting themselves and fabricating what they considered evidence entailing their execution. God sufficed them against such men, cast fear into their hearts, and they returned disappointed and died as wrongdoers. God is the protecting Friend of the Godfearing.","anchor":"en-q3-151-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-151-s4","r":"q3-151","title":"","text":"Then He reminded the believers of the victory He had promised them.","anchor":"en-q3-151-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-152","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival 3:152","anchor":"unit-q3-152"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-1","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"وَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمُ اللَّهُ وَعْدَهُ إِذْ تَحُسُّونَهُمْ بِإِذْنِهِ حَتَّى إِذا فَشِلْتُمْ وَتَنازَعْتُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ وَعَصَيْتُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما أَراكُمْ ما تُحِبُّونَ مِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الدُّنْيا وَمِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الْآخِرَةَ ثُمَّ صَرَفَكُمْ عَنْهُمْ لِيَبْتَلِيَكُمْ وَلَقَدْ عَفا عَنْكُمْ وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ (152)","anchor":"ar-q3-152-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-2","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"قلت: حسَّه: إذا قتله وأبطل حسه، وجواب (إذا) : محذوف، أي: حتى إذا فشلتم وتنازعتم وعصيتم امتحناكم بالهزيمة، والواو لا ترتب، والتقدير: حتى إذا تنازعتم وعصيتم وفشلتم سلبنا النصر عنكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-152-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-3","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمُ اللَّهُ ما وعدكم من النصر لو صبرتم واتقيتم، وذلك حين كنتم تَحُسُّونَهُمْ بالسيف، وتقتلونهم حتى انهزموا هاربين، بإذنه تعالى وإرادته، حَتَّى إِذا فَشِلْتُمْ أي: جبنتم","anchor":"ar-q3-152-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-4","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"وضعف رأيكم وملتم إلى الغنيمة، وَتَنازَعْتُمْ في الثبات مع الرماة حين انهزم المشركون، فقلتم: الغنيمةَ الغنيمةَ، فما وقوفكم هنا! وقال آخرون: لا تخالفوا أمر الرسول، ثم تركتم المركز، وَعَصَيْتُمْ الرسول مِنْ بَعْدِ ما أَراكُمْ ما تُحِبُّونَ من النصر والغنيمة، امتحناكم حينئذ بالهزيمة.","anchor":"ar-q3-152-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-5","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"فمنكم مَنْ يُرِيدُ الدُّنْيا ليصرفها في الآخرة، وهم الذين خالفوا المركز وذهبوا للغنيمة، وَمِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الْآخِرَةَ صِرفاً، وهم الثابتون مع عبد الله بن جبير، محافظةً على أمر رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، ثُمَّ صَرَفَكُمْ عَنْهُمْ حين خالفتم أمر الرسول، لِيَبْتَلِيَكُمْ أي: ليختبركم، فيتبين الصابر من الجازع، والمخلص من المنافق، وَلَقَدْ عَفا عَنْكُمْ فلم يستأصلكم بعد المعصية والمخالفة، لاستحقاقكم ذلك، أو تجاوز عن ذنبكم وتفضل بالتوبة والمغفرة، وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عظيم عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ يتفضل عليهم بالمغفرة في الأحوال كلها، سواء أديل عليهم أو لهم، فإن الابتلاء أيضاً رحمة وتطهير. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-152-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-6","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"الإشارة: يقول للفقراء الذين استشرفوا على بلاد الخصوصية، ثم فشلوا ورجعوا إلى بلاد العمومية: ولقد صدقكم الله وعده في إدراك الخصوصية لو صبرتم، فإنكم حين كنتم تجاهدون نفوسكم وتحسونها بسيوف المخالفة، لمعت لكم أنوار المشاهدة، حتى إذا فشلتم وتفرقت قلوبكم، وعصيتم شيوخكم قلَّت أمدادكم، وأظلمت قلوبكم، من بعد ما رأيتم ما تحبون من مبادئ المشاهدة، فملتم إلى الدنيا الفانية، فمنكم يا معشر المنتسبين من يريد الدنيا، فصحب العارفين على حرف، وهو الذي رجع وفشل، ومنكم من يريد الآخرة وقطع يأسه من الرجوع إلى الدنيا، وهو الذي ثبت حتى ظفر، ثم صرفكم عن صحبة العارفين، يا من أراد الدنيا من المنتسبين، ليبتليكم، هل صحبتموهم لله أو لغيره، ولقد عفا عنكم وجعلكم من عوام المسلمين، ولم يسلب عنكم الإيمان عقوبة لترك صحبة العارفين. أو لقد عفا عنكم إن رجعتم إلى صحبتهم والأدب معهم، فإن الله (ذو فضل على المؤمنين) حيث لم يعاجلهم بالعقوبة. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-152-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-7","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"وقال الورتجبي: قوله: مِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الدُّنْيا، أي: منكم من وقع في بحر غنى القدم، واتصف به بنعت التمكين ورؤية النعم في شكر المنعم، كسليمان عليه السلام. ومنكم من وقع في بحر التنزيه وتقديس الأزلية، فغلب عليه القدس والطهارة، فخرج بنعت الفقر تجريداً لتوحيده وإفرادِ قدمه من الحدث، كمحمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم حيث قال: «الفقر فخري(1)» .","anchor":"ar-q3-152-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-152-8","r":"q3-152","title":"3:152 · The reversal at Uḥud: obedience, spoils and the conditions of arrival","text":"ثم بيّن وقت الذلة التي افتقرت إلى العفو، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-152-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-152-s1","r":"q3-152","title":"Ḥassa (حسّ), the suppressed answer and wāw","text":"I say: To ḥassa ( حسَّ ) someone is to kill him, abolishing his sensation ( حِسّ ). The answer ( جواب ) of idhā is omitted ( محذوف ): “until, when you lost courage, disputed and disobeyed, We tried you by defeat.” The conjunction wāw ( الواو ) does not itself specify chronological order. The sequence of events is understood as: when you disputed, disobeyed and lost courage, We withdrew victory from you.","anchor":"en-q3-152-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-152-s2","r":"q3-152","title":"The archers, the booty and divine pardon","text":"God proved truthful in His promise of victory if you remained patient and mindful of Him: you were striking down your enemies with swords, killing and routing them by His leave and will. But then your resolution weakened, your judgment faltered and you inclined towards the spoils. The archers disputed whether to stay at their station after the idolaters fled. Some cried, “The spoils! The spoils! Why remain here?” Others replied, “Do not violate the Messenger's command.” Then you abandoned your station and disobeyed the Messenger, after seeing the triumph and spoils you loved, and at that point He tried you with defeat. Among you were those seeking the world in order to employ it for the Hereafter —those who left their post for the spoils. Among you were others who desired the Hereafter without admixture: those who remained with ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jubayr in fidelity to the Messenger's command. God then turned you away from the enemy because you violated that command, to try you and disclose the patient and the distressed, the sincere and the hypocrite. Yet He pardoned you: He did not annihilate you after your disobedience and opposition, although you merited punishment; or He forgave your offence and favoured you with repentance and mercy. His bounty towards believers is immense: He favours them with forgiveness in every circumstance, whether fortune alternates against or in their favour; trial itself is mercy and purification. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-152-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-152-s3","r":"q3-152","title":"Leaving the country of particular realization for ordinary life","text":"The Real addresses the spiritual poor ( الفقراء ) who had approached the country of particular realization ( بلاد الخصوصية ) but then weakened and returned to ordinary existence ( بلاد العمومية ): God fulfilled His promise that you would attain the rank of the elect, if only you had persevered. While you struggled against the lower selves, cutting them down with the swords of contravention ( سيوف المخالفة ), the lights of witnessing ( أنوار المشاهدة ) flashed before you. But when you weakened, your hearts scattered, and you disobeyed your spiritual teachers, the reinforcements granted you diminished and your hearts darkened, after you had seen the beginnings of witnessing. You inclined to the vanishing world. Among those affiliated to the path ( المنتسبين ) is one who desires this world and accompanies realized masters only precariously, “on an edge”; he is the one who turns back. Among them is one who seeks the Hereafter and relinquishes hope of returning to worldly preoccupation; he remains until he obtains the goal. God then diverts those still seeking the world away from the company of realized masters to test whether they accompanied them for God or another motive. Yet He has pardoned you and made you ordinary Muslims, without stripping you of faith as a penalty for abandoning the realized masters. Or His forgiveness is yours when you return to their company and observe good manners ( الأدب ). God is generous towards believers and does not hasten their punishment. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q3-152-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-152-s4","r":"q3-152","title":"Rūzbihān al-Baqlī on possession and transcendence","text":"Al-Wartajbī [Rūzbihān] interprets “Some of you desire this world” as referring to those immersed in the ocean of pre-eternal richness ( غنى القدم ), established in it and seeing blessings with gratitude to their Giver, like Solomon. “And some of you desire the Hereafter” refers to those plunged in the ocean of transcendence ( التنزيه ) and the sanctification of pre-eternity ( تقديس الأزلية ), so overtaken by holiness and purity that they emerged in the guise of poverty ( الفقر ) and detachment ( التجريد ), affirming the unique pre-eternity of God apart from contingent being ( الحدث ), like Muḥammad, upon him blessings and peace, who is here quoted as saying, “Poverty is my pride [CP19] .”","anchor":"en-q3-152-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-152-s5","r":"q3-152","title":"","text":"He then specified the time of humiliation that required forgiveness.","anchor":"en-q3-152-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-153","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers 3:153","anchor":"unit-q3-153"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-1","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"إِذْ تُصْعِدُونَ وَلا تَلْوُونَ عَلى أَحَدٍ وَالرَّسُولُ يَدْعُوكُمْ فِي أُخْراكُمْ فَأَثابَكُمْ غَمًّا بِغَمٍّ لِكَيْلا تَحْزَنُوا عَلى ما فاتَكُمْ وَلا ما أَصابَكُمْ وَاللَّهُ خَبِيرٌ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ (153)","anchor":"ar-q3-153-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-2","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"قلت: (إذْ) : ظرف لعفا، أو اذكر. وأصعد: أبعد في الأرض، وصعد: في الجبل، فالإصعاد: الذهاب في الأرض المستوية، والصعود: الارتقاء في العلو. وقرئ بهما معاً لأنهما وقعا معاً، فمنهم من فرّ ذاهباً في الأرض، ومنهم من صعد إلى الجبل. و (لكيلا) : متعلق بأثابكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-153-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-3","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولقد عفا عنكم حين كنتم تُصْعِدُونَ عن نبيه- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، منهزمين عنه، تبعدون عنه، وَلا تَلْوُونَ عَلى أَحَدٍ أي: لا يلتفت بعضكم إلى بعض، ولا ينتظر بعضكم بعضاً، وَالرَّسُولُ محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم يَدْعُوكُمْ فِي أُخْراكُمْ أي: في ساقتكم، يقول: «إليَّ عباد الله، أنا رسول الله، من يكرُّ فله الجنة» ، وفيه مدح للرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم بالشجاعة والثبات، حيث وقف في آخر المنهزمين، فإن الآخر هو موقف الأبطال، والفرار فى حقه صلّى الله عليه وسلم محال.","anchor":"ar-q3-153-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-4","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"فَأَثابَكُمْ أي: فجازاكم على ذلك الفرار، غَمًّا وهو ظهور المشركين عليكم وقتل إخوانكم، بسبب غم أوصلتموه للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم بعصيانه والفرار عنه، وقدَّر ذلك لِكَيْلا تَحْزَنُوا عَلى ما فاتَكُمْ من الغنيمة، وَلا على ما أَصابَكُمْ من الجرح والهزيمة، لأن من استحق العقوبة والأدب لا يحزن على ما فاته ولا على ما أصابه إذ جريمته تستحق أكثر من ذلك، يرى ما نزل به بعض ما يستحقه، فيهون عليه أمر ما نزل به أو ما فاته من الخير.","anchor":"ar-q3-153-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-5","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"أو يقول: فَأَثابَكُمْ غَمًّا متصلاً بِغَمٍّ فالغم الأول: ما فاتهم من الظفر والغنيمة، والثاني: ما نالهم من القتل والهزيمة، أو الأول: ما أصابهم من القتل والجراح، والثاني: ما سمعوا من الإرجاف بقتل النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، وذلك ليتمرنوا على المحن والشدائد حتى لا يجزعوا من شيء. وبذلك وصفهم كعب بن زهير في لاميته، حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-q3-153-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-6","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"لاَ يَفْرَحُونَ إِذا نَالَتْ رِماحُهُمْ ... وَلَيْسُوا مجازيعاً إذا نِيلُوا","anchor":"ar-q3-153-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-7","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"فإن المتمرّن على المصائب المتعود عليها يهون عليه أمرها، فلا يحزن على ما أصابه ولا ما فاته، وَاللَّهُ خَبِيرٌ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ وبما قصدتم، فيجازيكم على ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q3-153-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-8","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"الإشارة: ما زال الدعاة إلى الله من أهل التربية النبوية يدعون الناس إلى الله، ويعرفونهم بالطريق إلى الله، يبينون لهم الطريق إلى عين التحقيق، والناس يبعدون عنهم ويفرّون منهم، وهم في أخراهم يقولون بلسان الحال أو المقال: يا عباد الله، هلم إلينا نعرفُكم بالله، وندلكم على الله، فلا يلوي إليهم أحد ولا يلتفت إليهم بشر، إلا مَن سبقت له العناية، وأراد الحق تعالى أن يوصله إلى درجة الولاية، «سبحان مَن لم يجعل الدليل على أوليائه إلا من حيث الدليل عليه، ولم يوصل إليهم إلا مَن أراد أن يوصله إليه» ، فأثابهم على الفرار غم الحجاب، متصلاً بغم الأسباب، فلا يحزنوا على ما فاتهم من المعرفة إذ لم يعرفوا قدرها، ولا على ما أصابهم من الغفلة والبطالة، إذ لم يتفطنوا لها، (والله خبير بما تعملون) يا معشر العباد، من التودد أو العناد. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-153-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-153-9","r":"q3-153","title":"3:153 · Flight from the Prophet and flight from the teachers","text":"ثم أنزل على أهل أحد الأمن والطمأنينة بعد الشدة والمحنة، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق، بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-153-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-153-s1","r":"q3-153","title":"Iṣʿād (إصعاد) and ṣuʿūd (صعود)","text":"I say: Idh ( إذ ) is a temporal adverb ( ظرف ) related to “He pardoned” or to an understood imperative “remember.” Aṣʿada ( أصعد ) means to go far across the land; ṣaʿida ( صعد ) means to ascend a mountain. Accordingly iṣʿād ( الإصعاد ) is departing over level ground, and ṣuʿūd ( الصعود ) is rising to higher ground. Both readings have been transmitted, for both occurred: some fled over the land and others climbed the mountain. Li-kay-lā ( لكيلا ) is attached to athābakum ( أثابكم ).","anchor":"en-q3-153-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-153-s2","r":"q3-153","title":"The griefs of Uḥud and the Messenger's constancy","text":"God pardoned you as you fled the Prophet, moving away in defeat, without one of you turning toward or waiting for another. Yet Muḥammad, the Messenger, was calling to you from your rear guard: “To me, servants of God! I am God's Messenger! Paradise to whoever returns to the fight!” The account praises his courage and steadfastness: he stood at the rear of the retreating men, the station of heroes; flight is inconceivable in his case. God “rewarded” you for flight with grief: the enemy gained superiority over you and your brothers were killed, because you caused grief to the Prophet through disobedience and flight. He ordained that this should befall you lest you grieve over missed booty or over wounds and defeat. One who understands that an offence deserves correction does not lament what he has lost or suffered, perceiving the affliction as less than his wrongdoing merited, and his burden becomes easier. Alternatively, He gave you grief joined to grief: first the lost victory and booty, then death and defeat; or first the deaths and wounds, then the rumours that the Prophet had been killed. It was to accustom you to trials and hardship so that you would not panic when struck. Kaʿb ibn Zuhayr described such people in his lāmiyya : They do not exult when their spears strike home, nor do they panic when they themselves are struck. One seasoned by affliction bears it lightly and is not undone by what he suffers or loses. God knows your deeds and intentions and recompenses you accordingly.","anchor":"en-q3-153-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-153-s3","r":"q3-153","title":"The call of the spiritual guides and the grief of veiling","text":"Inviters to God, bearing the inheritance of Prophetic spiritual education ( أهل التربية النبوية ), have never ceased calling people to God, teaching the way to Him and pointing them towards the very reality of realization ( عين التحقيق ). People nevertheless distance themselves and flee. The guides call behind them, by speech or by their state: “Servants of God, come to us; we shall make God known to you and guide you to Him.” No one turns to them or looks towards them except those preceded by divine solicitude ( العناية ), whom the Real intends to bring to sainthood ( الولاية ). As the saying has it: “Glory be to Him who provided no proof of His friends save what is itself proof of Him, and who brought none to them except one He wished to bring to Himself.” For fleeing them, people receive the grief of being veiled ( غم الحجاب ), added to the grief of worldly causes ( غم الأسباب ). They do not grieve over the gnosis ( المعرفة ) they missed, because they never recognized its worth, or over the heedlessness and idleness that befall them, because they do not notice them. God knows, O servants, whether your deeds proceed from affection or obstinacy. Success comes from God, the guide to the straight path.","anchor":"en-q3-153-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-153-s4","r":"q3-153","title":"","text":"God then sent security upon the people of Uḥud after their difficulty and ordeal.","anchor":"en-q3-153-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-154","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized 3:154","anchor":"unit-q3-154"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-1","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"ثُمَّ أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ الْغَمِّ أَمَنَةً نُعاساً يَغْشى طائِفَةً مِنْكُمْ وَطائِفَةٌ قَدْ أَهَمَّتْهُمْ أَنْفُسُهُمْ يَظُنُّونَ بِاللَّهِ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ ظَنَّ الْجاهِلِيَّةِ يَقُولُونَ هَلْ لَنا مِنَ الْأَمْرِ مِنْ شَيْءٍ قُلْ إِنَّ الْأَمْرَ كُلَّهُ لِلَّهِ يُخْفُونَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ ما لا يُبْدُونَ لَكَ يَقُولُونَ لَوْ كانَ لَنا مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ ما قُتِلْنا هاهُنا قُلْ لَوْ كُنْتُمْ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ لَبَرَزَ الَّذِينَ كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَتْلُ إِلى مَضاجِعِهِمْ وَلِيَبْتَلِيَ اللَّهُ ما فِي صُدُورِكُمْ وَلِيُمَحِّصَ ما فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذاتِ الصُّدُورِ (154)","anchor":"ar-q3-154-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-2","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"قلت: (نعاسا) : بدل من (أمنة) ، أو هو المفعول، و (أمنة) : حال منه، مقدمة، أو مفعول له، أي: أنزل عليكم نعاساً لأجل الأمنة، أو حال من كاف (عليكم) ، أي: أنزل عليكم حال كونكم آمنين. والأمنة: مصدر أمِن، كالعظَمة والغَلَبة.","anchor":"ar-q3-154-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-3","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ثُمَّ أَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ أيها المؤمنون مِنْ بَعْدِ الْغَمِّ الذي أصابكم بموت إخوانكم، والإرجاف بقتل نبيكم، الأمن والطمأنينة، حتى أخذكم النعاس وأنتم في الحرب. قال أبو طلحة: (غَشينَا النعاسُ ونحن في المصافّ، حتى كان السيف يسقط من يد أحدنا فيأخذه، ثم يسقط فيأخذه) . وقال الزبير رضي الله عنه: لقد رأيتني حين اشتدّ الخوف، ونحن مع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، أرسل الله- تعالى- علينا النوم، والله إني لأسمع قول معتب، والنعاس يغشاني، ما أسمعه إلا كالحلُم: (لو كان لنا من الأمر شيء ما قتلنا هاهنا) .","anchor":"ar-q3-154-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-4","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"ثم إن هذا النعاس إنما يَغْشى طائِفَةً مِنْكُمْ وهم المؤمنون، أو: هذه الأمنة إنما تغشى طائفة منكم، وأما المنافقون فقد أَهَمَّتْهُمْ أَنْفُسُهُمْ، أي: أوقعتهم في الهموم والغموم، أو ما يهمهم إلا أنفسهم، يُدبرون خلاصها","anchor":"ar-q3-154-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-5","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"ونجاتها، فقد طارت قلوبهم من الخوف، فلا يتصور في حقهم النوم، يَظُنُّونَ بِاللَّهِ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ أي: غير الظن الحق، لأنهم ظنّوا أنه لا ينصر- عليه الصلاة والسلام، وأن أمره مضمحل، أو ظنوا أنه قتل، ظنّاً كظن الجاهلية، أهل الشرك، يَقُولُونَ أي: بعضهم لبعض: هَلْ لَنا مِنَ الْأَمْرِ مِنْ شَيْءٍ أي: عُزلنا عن تدبر أنفسنا، فلم يبق لنا من الأمر من شيء. قاله ابنُ أُبي، لَما بلغه قتل الخزرج.","anchor":"ar-q3-154-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-6","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"قُلْ لهم يا محمد: إِنَّ الْأَمْرَ كُلَّهُ لِلَّهِ ليس بيد غيره شيء من التدبير والاختيار، حال كون المنافقين يُخْفُونَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ من الكفر والنفاق ما لا يُبْدُونَ لَكَ يَقُولُونَ لَوْ كانَ لَنا مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ ما قُتِلْنا هاهُنا أي: لو كان تدبيراً أو اختياراً ما خرجنا مع محمد حتى نقتل هاهنا ويقتل رؤساؤنا. قُلْ لهم يا محمد:","anchor":"ar-q3-154-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-7","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"أخرجتكم القدرة فى سلسلة المقادير، رغماً على أنفكم، فلو كُنْتُمْ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ آمنين لَبَرَزَ الَّذِينَ كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَتْلُ، ووصل أجلهم إِلى مَضاجِعِهِمْ ومصارعهم، رغماً على أنفهم، فإن الله قدَّر الأمور ودبرها في سابق أزله، لا معقب لحكمه، وإنما فعل ذلك، وأخرجكم إلى المعركة لِيَبْتَلِيَ اللَّهُ ما فِي صُدُورِكُمْ أي: يختبر ما فيها من الخير أو الشر، وَلِيُمَحِّصَ ما فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ أي: يكشف ما فيها من النفاق أو الإخلاص، فقد ظهر خبث سريرتكم ومرض قلوبكم بالنفاق الذي تمكن فيه، وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذاتِ الصُّدُورِ أي: بخفاياها قبل إظهارها. وفيه وعد ووعيد وتنبيه على أنه غني عن الابتلاء، وإنما فعل ذلك ليُميِّز المؤمنين ويُظهَر حال المنافقين. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-154-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-8","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"الإشارة: ثم أنزل عليكم أيها الواصلون المتمكنون، أو من تعلق بكم من السائرين، من بعد غم المجاهدة وتعب المراقبة أمنة في قلوبكم بالطمأنينة بشهود الله، وراحة في جوارحكم من تعب الخدمة في السير إلى الله، حتى وصلتم فنمتم في ظل الأمن والأمان، وسكنتم في جوار الكريم المنان.","anchor":"ar-q3-154-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-9","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"قال بعض العارفين: (إذا انتقلت المعاملة إلى القلوب استراحت الجوارح) ، (١) وهذه الراحة إنما تحصل للعارفين، أو من تعلق بهم من المريدين، وطائفة من غيرهم وهم المتفقرة الجاهلون، الذين لا شيخ لهم، قد أهمتهم أنفسهم، تارة تصرعهم وتارة يصرعونها، تارة تُشرق عليهم أنوارُ التوجه، فيقوى رجاؤهم في الفتح، وتارة تنقبض عنهم فيظنون بالله غير الحق، ظن الجاهلية، يقولون: هل لنا من الفتح من شيء؟.","anchor":"ar-q3-154-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-10","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"قل لهم: (إن الأمر كله لله) يوصل من يشاء ويبعد من يشاء، يخفون في أنفسهم من العيوب والخواطر الرديئة ما لا يبدون لك، فإذا طال عليهم الفتح، وغلب عليهم الفقر، ندموا على ما فاتهم من التمتع بالدنيا، يقولون: لو كان لنا من الأمر شيء ما قتلنا هاهنا بالذل والفقر والجوع، قل لهم: ذلك الذي سبق في علم الله، لا محيد لأحد عنه، ليظهر الصادق في الطلب من الكاذب، [كن صادقاً تجد مرشداً] ، فلو صدقتم في الطلب لأرشدكم إلى من يُوصلكم ويريحكم من التعب. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-154-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-154-11","r":"q3-154","title":"3:154 · Security after grief, destiny and the rest of the realized","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى علة انهزام من انهزم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-154-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-154-s1","r":"q3-154","title":"Nuʿās (نعاسًا) and amana (أمنة)","text":"I say: “Drowsiness” ( نُعاسًا ) may stand as a substitute ( بدل ) for “security” ( أمنة ), or it may be the object ( مفعول ), with amana an anticipatory circumstantial accusative ( حال مقدمة ), or an accusative of purpose ( مفعول له ): He sent down drowsiness on account of security. It can also be a circumstantial expression linked to the pronoun -kum ( كم ) in “upon you”: He sent it while you were secure. Amana is a verbal noun ( مصدر ) from amina ( أمِن ), like ʿaẓama and ghalaba .","anchor":"en-q3-154-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-154-s2","r":"q3-154","title":"Drowsiness among the believers, anxiety among the hypocrites","text":"After the grief of losing your brothers and hearing rumours of your Prophet's death, God sent you security and tranquillity, to the point that drowsiness overcame you while still drawn up in battle. Abū Ṭalḥa said that sleepiness overtook them in the ranks so that a sword would fall from a man's hand, he would retrieve it, and it would fall again. Al-Zubayr said that amid the danger God sent them sleep and he heard Muʿattib saying, “If we had any part in the matter, we would not have been killed here,” as though he heard it only in a dream. This drowsiness—or this security—overtook only one group: the believers. Another group, the hypocrites, were plunged into worry and sorrow by their own souls; or it means that they cared only for themselves, planning how to escape and survive; their hearts fluttered with fear, and sleep was impossible for them. They entertained false thoughts about God, imagining He would not help the Prophet, that his cause would perish, or that he had already been killed: the presumptions of the pagan Age of Ignorance ( ظن الجاهلية ). They asked one another whether they had any share in directing events, as though they had been deprived of all control over their own destiny. Ibn ʿAjība attributes this to Ibn Ubayy after he heard of Khazraj casualties. “Say: the affair in its entirety belongs to God.” No management ( تدبير ) or choice ( اختيار ) lies in anyone else's hands. Meanwhile they concealed their unbelief and hypocrisy, saying privately that, had the choice rested with them, they would not have marched with Muḥammad only to be killed and lose their chiefs. Say to them: divine power brought you out under the chain of decreed events ( سلسلة المقادير ), despite yourselves. Even if you had stayed secure in your houses, those appointed to die would have gone forth to their places of death ( مضاجع / مصارع ). God arranged events in His pre-eternal knowledge, and His judgment admits no reversal. He brought you to battle to make manifest what is in your breasts—good or evil—and to disclose what is in your hearts—hypocrisy or sincerity. Thus the corruption of their inner disposition and the malady of hypocrisy became visible. God knew what lay hidden before its disclosure; the verse contains promise, threat and the reminder that He has no need to learn through trial. Rather, He distinguishes believers from hypocrites and makes their conditions publicly apparent. Ibn ʿAjība cites al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q3-154-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-154-s3","r":"q3-154","title":"The composure of those who arrive and the worry of seekers without guidance","text":"After the grief of spiritual struggle ( المجاهدة ) and the labour of vigilance ( المراقبة ), God sends security into the hearts of those who have arrived and become firmly established ( الواصلون المتمكنون ), and those wayfarers attached to them: peace in witnessing God, and rest in the bodily faculties after the strain of serving Him along the path. Having arrived, they sleep beneath the shade of safety and remain at peace in the vicinity of the Generous Bestower. One gnostic says: “When dealing [with God] passes into the heart, the limbs come to rest.” Such rest belongs to realized masters and disciples connected to them. Another group, however, are ignorant people who affect spiritual poverty ( المتفقرة الجاهلون ) without a spiritual teacher. Their selves consume their attention: at times they are overcome by them; at times they overcome them. At times the lights of orientation ( أنوار التوجه ) shine, and hope of opening ( الفتح ) grows strong; at others the lights are withheld and they think false thoughts of God. They ask whether spiritual opening is possible for them. Tell them that the whole affair is God's: He brings to Himself whom He wills and keeps distant whom He wills. They conceal defects and harmful inner thoughts which they do not disclose. When opening is delayed and poverty weighs on them, they regret missing worldly ease and say, “Had we any choice, we would not have been killed here by humiliation, poverty and hunger.” Say to them: this was already in God's knowledge and none escapes it; the truthful seeker must be distinguished from the pretender. “Be truthful, and you will find a guide” ( كن صادقاً تجد مرشداً ): with sincerity He would have directed you to one who could bring you to Him and relieve the toil. God grants success and guides to the straight path.","anchor":"en-q3-154-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-154-s4","r":"q3-154","title":"","text":"Then He named the reason for the flight of those who fled.","anchor":"en-q3-154-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-155","r":"q3-155","title":"3:155 · The slip of the archers and forgiveness after withdrawing from a teacher","text":"3:155 · The slip of the archers and forgiveness after withdrawing from a teacher 3:155","anchor":"unit-q3-155"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-155-1","r":"q3-155","title":"3:155 · The slip of the archers and forgiveness after withdrawing from a teacher","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوْا مِنْكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعانِ إِنَّمَا اسْتَزَلَّهُمُ الشَّيْطانُ بِبَعْضِ ما كَسَبُوا وَلَقَدْ عَفَا اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ (155)","anchor":"ar-q3-155-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-155-2","r":"q3-155","title":"3:155 · The slip of the archers and forgiveness after withdrawing from a teacher","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوْا مِنْكُمْ وانهزموا يوم أحد يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعانِ جمع المسلمين وجمع الكفار إنما كان السبب في انهزامهم أن الشيطان اسْتَزَلَّهُمُ، أي: طلب زللهم فأطاعوه، أي: زين لهم الفرار فأطاعوه، بسبب بعض ما كَسَبُوا من الإثم، كمخالفة أمر النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، والحرص على الغنيمة، وذنوب اقترفوها قبل الجهاد، فإن المعاصي تجر بعضها بعضاً، كالطاعة، وَلَقَدْ عَفَا اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ فيما فعلوا من الفرار لتوبتهم واعتذارهم إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ للذنوب، حَلِيمٌ لا يعاجل بعقوبة المذنب كي يتوب.","anchor":"ar-q3-155-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-155-3","r":"q3-155","title":"3:155 · The slip of the archers and forgiveness after withdrawing from a teacher","text":"الإشارة: إن الذين تولوا منكم يا معشر الفقراء، ورجعوا عن صحبة الشيوخ، حين التقى في قلبهم الخصمان:","anchor":"ar-q3-155-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-155-4","r":"q3-155","title":"3:155 · The slip of the archers and forgiveness after withdrawing from a teacher","text":"خصم يرغبهم في الثبوت، وخصم يدلهم على الرجوع، ثم غلب خصم الرجوع فرجعوا، إنما استزلهم الشيطان بسوء أدبهم، فإن تابوا ورجعوا، أقبلوا عليهم، وقَبل الله توبتهم، وعفا عنهم، فإنه سبحانه غفور حليم.","anchor":"ar-q3-155-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-155-5","r":"q3-155","title":"3:155 · The slip of the archers and forgiveness after withdrawing from a teacher","text":"ثم حذّر من التشبه بالمنافقين فى ضعف اليقين، وما ينشأ عنه من مقالة الجاهلين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-155-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-155-s1","r":"q3-155","title":"The causes of the retreat and the delay of punishment","text":"Those who turned back and fled when the two armies met at Uḥud did so because Satan caused them to slip ( استزلهم ): he sought to make them stumble and they obeyed him. He adorned flight for them because of some of the sins they had committed—disobeying the Prophet, being eager for booty, or offences committed before fighting. Acts of disobedience lead to further disobedience, just as acts of obedience lead to further obedience. Yet God pardoned their flight because they repented and offered their apologies. He forgives sins and is Clement ( حليم ), not hastening a sinner's punishment, so that repentance remains possible.","anchor":"en-q3-155-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-155-s2","r":"q3-155","title":"A disciple's conflict and restoration through repentance","text":"O spiritual poor, those who turned away from accompanying their teachers did so when two adversaries met in their hearts: one inviting them to remain, another urging return to ordinary pursuits. The latter prevailed and they withdrew. Satan caused their lapse through their poor manners ( سوء الأدب ). If they repent and return to the teachers, the teachers should welcome them and God accepts their repentance and pardons them, for He is Forgiving, Clement.","anchor":"en-q3-155-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-155-s3","r":"q3-155","title":"","text":"He then warned against resembling hypocrites in weakness of certainty and the language arising from it.","anchor":"en-q3-155-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-156","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance 3:156","anchor":"unit-q3-156"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-1","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَكُونُوا كَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَقالُوا لِإِخْوانِهِمْ إِذا ضَرَبُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ أَوْ كانُوا غُزًّى لَوْ كانُوا عِنْدَنا ما ماتُوا وَما قُتِلُوا لِيَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ ذلِكَ حَسْرَةً فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ وَاللَّهُ يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ (156)","anchor":"ar-q3-156-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-2","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"قلت: (غُزّى) : جمع غازٍ، كعافٍ وعفى، وإنما وضع (إذا) موضع (إذ) لحكاية الحال.","anchor":"ar-q3-156-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-3","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَكُونُوا كَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ونافقوا، كعبد الله بن أُبي، وأصحابه، وَقالُوا لِإِخْوانِهِمْ في النسب، أو في المذهب، أي: قالوا لأجلهم أو في شأنهم، إِذا ضَرَبُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ أي: سافروا للتجارة أو غيرها فماتوا، أَوْ كانُوا غُزًّى أي: غازين فقتلوا في الغزو: لَوْ كانُوا عِنْدَنا مُقيمين ما ماتُوا وَما قُتِلُوا، وإنما نطقوا بذلك لِيَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ ذلِكَ القول الناشئ عن الاعتقاد الفاسد حَسْرَةً فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ بالاغتمام على ما فات، والتحسر على ما لم يأت، وَاللَّهُ هو يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ بلا سبب في الإقامة والسفر، فليس يمنع حذر من قدر، وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ، أيها المؤمنون بَصِيرٌ، ففيه تهديد لهم على أن يُماثلوا المنافقين في هذا الاعتقاد الفاسد، ومن قرأ بالياء فهو تهديد لهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-156-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-4","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"الإشارة: لا ينبغي للأقوياء من أهل اليقين أن يتشبهوا بضعفاء اليقين، كانوا علماء أو صالحين أو طالحين، حيث يقولون لإخوانهم إذا سافروا لأرض مخوفة أو بلد الوباء: لو جلسوا عندنا ما ماتوا وما قتلوا، وما دَرَوْا أن الله قدَّر الآجال كما قدَّر الأرزاق وجميع الشئون والأحوال، وعيَّن لها أوقاتاً محدودة في أزله، فكل مقدور يبرز في وقته، «ما من نَفَسٍ تُبديه، إلاَّ وله قَدَر فيك يمضيه» ، فما قدَّره في سابق علمه لا بد أن يكون، وما لم يقدره لا يكون، ولا تجلبه حركة ولا سكون. ولله در القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-156-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-5","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"مَا لا يقدر لا يكون بحيلة ... أبدا وما هو كائن سيكون","anchor":"ar-q3-156-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-6","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"سيكون ما هو كائن في وقته ... وَأخُو الجَهَالَةِ مُتْعَبٌ مَحْزُونُ","anchor":"ar-q3-156-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-7","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"يَجْرِي الحَريصُ ولا يَنَالُ بِحرْصِهِ ... شَيْئاً ويَحْظَى عَاجِزٌ وَمَهِينٌ","anchor":"ar-q3-156-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-8","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"فَدعَ الهُمُومَ، تَعَرَّ مِنْ أثْوابِهَا، ... إنْ كانَ عِنْدَكَ بالْقَضَاءِ يَقِينُ","anchor":"ar-q3-156-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-9","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"هَوِّنْ عَلَيْكَ وَكُنْ بِرَبِّكَ وَاثِقاً ... فأخو الحَقِيقَةِ شَأنُه التَّهْوِينُ","anchor":"ar-q3-156-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-10","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"وكان سيدنا عمر رضي الله عنه يتمثل بهذه الأبيات:","anchor":"ar-q3-156-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-11","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"فَهَوَّنْ عَلَيْكَ فَإنَّ الأُمُورَ ... بكفِّ الإلَهِ مَقَادِيرُهَا","anchor":"ar-q3-156-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-12","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"فَلَيْسَ يَأتِيكَ مَصْرُوفُهَا ... ولا عَازِبٌ عَنْكَ مَقْدُورُها","anchor":"ar-q3-156-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-13","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"وكل من لم يحقق الإيمان بالقدر لا ينفك عن الحسرة والكدر، ومن أراد النعيم المقيم فليثلج صدره ببرد الرضا والتسليم، ومن أراد الروح والريحان فعليه بجنات العرفان، وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-156-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-156-14","r":"q3-156","title":"3:156 · Death, travel, destiny and the tranquility of acceptance","text":"ثم رغّب الحق تعالى فى الموت فى الجهاد، ورجّح الموت مطلقا على الحياة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-156-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-156-s1","r":"q3-156","title":"Ghuzzā (غُزّى) and the historical present","text":"I say: Ghuzzā ( غُزّى ) is the plural of ghāzī ( غازٍ , one engaged in fighting), like ʿāfin/ʿufā . Here idhā ( إذا ) stands for idh ( إذ ) to represent a past event as if occurring before us ( حكاية الحال ).","anchor":"en-q3-156-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-156-s2","r":"q3-156","title":"False counterfactuals about travel and death","text":"Do not be like those who disbelieved and practiced hypocrisy, such as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy and his companions. They spoke concerning their brothers—brothers by kinship or creed, that is, on their behalf or about them—who had travelled for commerce or another purpose and died, or who had gone out on a campaign and been killed: “Had they stayed with us, neither death nor killing would have overtaken them.” Their utterance arises from corrupt belief ( الاعتقاد الفاسد ) and becomes a cause of remorse: grief for what has passed and regret for what never came to be. God gives life and causes death without a cause, whether one stays at home or journeys. No precaution wards off destiny ( لا يمنع حذر من قدر ). He sees your deeds, believers; the statement therefore warns you not to adopt the same mistaken notion. With the reading in the third person ( بالياء ), the threat is directed towards the hypocrites. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-156-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-156-s3","r":"q3-156","title":"The predetermined term and the release of anxiety","text":"People strong in certainty should not resemble those weak in certainty—scholars, righteous people or wrongdoers—when they say of brothers travelling to a dangerous country or one afflicted by disease: “Had they remained with us, they would neither have died nor been killed.” They fail to realize that God has determined allotted lifespans as He determined livelihood, affairs and circumstances, and appointed their times in eternity. Every decree emerges at its appointed hour. As the saying has it: “No breath do you exhale but that it contains a decree carried out in you” ( ما من نفس تبديه إلا وله قدر فيك يمضيه ). What His prior knowledge has decreed must occur; what He did not decree cannot be brought about by motion or stillness. The poet says: What is not decreed no contrivance can bring; what is to be will certainly be. What is to be will come at its appointed hour; only the ignorant are wearied and grieved. The greedy man runs but gains nothing through greed; the weak and the lowly may receive their share. So put away cares; strip off their garments, if you hold firm certainty in divine decree. Be at ease and place your trust in your Lord: the one realized in truth makes matters light. Our master ʿUmar, God be pleased with him, used to recite these lines: Make things easier upon yourself, for their measures rest in the hand of God. What He turns from you shall never reach you; what He decrees for you shall never be far away. Whoever has not realized faith in decree remains caught in remorse and distress. Whoever seeks enduring delight should cool the breast with acceptance ( الرضا ) and surrender ( التسليم ); whoever seeks ease and sweet repose should enter the gardens of gnosis ( العرفان ). Success is through God, the guide to the straight path.","anchor":"en-q3-156-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-156-s4","r":"q3-156","title":"","text":"He then encouraged them concerning death in striving, and preferred death more generally to worldly life.","anchor":"en-q3-156-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-157-158","r":"q3-157-158","title":"3:157–158 · Death in God's way and the spiritual gain of meeting Him","text":"3:157–158 · Death in God's way and the spiritual gain of meeting Him 3:157–158","anchor":"unit-q3-157-158"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-157-158-1","r":"q3-157-158","title":"3:157–158 · Death in God's way and the spiritual gain of meeting Him","text":"وَلَئِنْ قُتِلْتُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَوْ مُتُّمْ لَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرَحْمَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِمَّا يَجْمَعُونَ (157) وَلَئِنْ مُتُّمْ أَوْ قُتِلْتُمْ لَإِلَى اللَّهِ تُحْشَرُونَ (158)","anchor":"ar-q3-157-158-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-157-158-2","r":"q3-157-158","title":"3:157–158 · Death in God's way and the spiritual gain of meeting Him","text":"قلت: إذا اجتمع القسم والشرط ذكر جواب الأول وأغنى عن الثاني، فقوله: (لمغفرة) : جواب القسم، أغنى عن جواب (إن) ، والتقدير: إن قتلتم في سبيل الله غفر الله لكم، ثم سد عنه (لمغفرة..) الخ، ومن قرأ: (مِتم) بكسر الميم، فهو من: مات يمات، كهاب يهاب هِبتُ، وخاف يخاف خِفتُ، ومن قرأ بالضم: فمن مات يموت، كقال يقول قُلت.","anchor":"ar-q3-157-158-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-157-158-3","r":"q3-157-158","title":"3:157–158 · Death in God's way and the spiritual gain of meeting Him","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إن السفر والغزو ليس هما مما يجلب الموت أو يقدم الأجل، وعلى تقدير: لو وقع ذلك وحضر أجلكم فيه وقتلتم فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ بالسيف، أَوْ مُتُّمْ حتف أنفكم، لما تنالون من المغفرة والرحمة والروح والريحان خَيْرٌ مِمَّا يَجْمَعُونَ من حطام الدنيا الفانية لو لم تموتوا، وعلى أي وجه متم أو قتلتم فلا تحشرون إلا إلى الله، لا إلى أحد غيره، فيوفى جزاءكم ويعظم ثوابكم، وأما البقاء في الدنيا فلا مطمع لأحد فيه، سافر أو قعد في بيته، وقدَّم أولاً القتل على الموت وأخره ثانياً لأن الأول رتب عليه المغفرة والرحمة، وهما في حق من قتل في الجهاد أعظم ممن مات بغيره، فقدمه اعتناء به، وفي الثاني رتب عليه الحشر، وهو مستوٍ في القتل والموت، فلا مزية فيه للقتل على الموت. والله أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-157-158-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-157-158-4","r":"q3-157-158","title":"3:157–158 · Death in God's way and the spiritual gain of meeting Him","text":"الإشارة: ولئن قتلتم نفوسكم وبذلتم مهجكم في طلب محبوبكم، فظفرتم بالوصول إليه قبل موتكم، أو متم في السير قبل الوصول إلى محبوبكم، لما تنالون من كمال اليقين وشهود رب العالمين، أو من المغفرة والرحمة التي تضمكم إلى جواره، خير مما كنتم تجمعون من الدنيا قبل توجهكم إليه، فإن الموت والحشر مكتوب على كل مخلوق، فيظهر فوز المجاهدين والمتوجهين، وغبن القاعدين المتسوفين. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-157-158-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-157-158-5","r":"q3-157-158","title":"3:157–158 · Death in God's way and the spiritual gain of meeting Him","text":"ولمّا وقع ما وقع يوم أحد من مخالفة الرسول والفرار عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- لم يعاتب صلّى الله عليه وسلم أحدا، ولكن ألان لهم الكلام وعفا عنهم، كما أخبر عن ذلك الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-157-158-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-157-158-s1","r":"q3-157-158","title":"When an oath precedes a conditional","text":"I say: When an oath ( قسم ) and a condition ( شرط ) occur together, the answer to the first suffices for the second. Thus “forgiveness” ( la-maghfira , لَمَغْفِرَة ) is the answer to the oath ( جواب القسم ) and takes the place of the answer to in ( إن ): “If you are killed in God's way, God will forgive you,” with the express formula “forgiveness ... is better” standing in its place. One reading of “you die” has kasra on the mīm ( mittum , مِتُّم ), from māta/yamātu , like hāba/yahābu/hibtu and khāfa/yakhāfu/khiftu ; another has ḍamma ( muttum , مُتُّم ), from māta/yamūtu , like qāla/yaqūlu/qultu .","anchor":"en-q3-157-158-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-157-158-s2","r":"q3-157-158","title":"Why killing is named first, and why death follows","text":"Travel and battle neither cause death nor advance its appointed term. But if your term comes during striving and you are killed by the sword in God's cause—or if you die naturally—the forgiveness, mercy, repose and delight awaiting you are better than the perishable worldly gains they might have accumulated had they lived. In either case, death or killing, you are gathered to God alone, who completes your recompense and magnifies your reward. No one, traveller or stay-at-home, can hope to remain forever in the world. God places being killed before ordinary death in the first verse because forgiveness and mercy are promised in a special measure to the one killed in divine striving, so killing is advanced in honour of that promise. In the second verse, where the outcome is simply resurrection and gathering, death is named first because there is no difference between the two ways of dying with respect to that destiny. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-157-158-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-157-158-s3","r":"q3-157-158","title":"The fruit of dying to the self before bodily death","text":"If you kill your lower selves ( أنفسكم ), offering your lives in seeking the Beloved, and achieve arrival ( الوصول ) before death—or die during wayfaring ( السير ) before arriving—the perfection of certainty ( كمال اليقين ) and witnessing of the Lord of the Worlds that you attain, or the forgiveness and mercy which bring you near Him, are better than the worldly possessions gathered before you turned to Him. Death and resurrection are decreed for every creature; then the success of those who struggled and turned towards God, and the loss of those who delayed and remained behind, will become plain. Success is through God.","anchor":"en-q3-157-158-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-157-158-s4","r":"q3-157-158","title":"","text":"Despite what occurred at Uḥud—the opposition to the Messenger and the flight—he did not reproach the guilty, but addressed them gently and pardoned them, as God declares.","anchor":"en-q3-157-158-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-159","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust 3:159","anchor":"unit-q3-159"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-1","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"فَبِما رَحْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ لِنْتَ لَهُمْ وَلَوْ كُنْتَ فَظًّا غَلِيظَ الْقَلْبِ لانْفَضُّوا مِنْ حَوْلِكَ فَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ وَشاوِرْهُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ فَإِذا عَزَمْتَ فَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَوَكِّلِينَ (159)","anchor":"ar-q3-159-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-2","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"قلت: (فبما) : صلة. والفظ: الجافي، يقال: فظ فظاظةً وفظوظاً، ورجل فظ، وامرأة فظة، والفض- بغير المشالة: التفرق، ويطلق على الكسر، ومنه: لا يفضض الله فاك.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-3","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فبرحمة من الله ونعمة كنت سهلاً ليناً رفيقاً، فحين عصوا أمرك، وفروا عنك، ألنت لهم جانبك، ورفقت بهم، بل اغتممت من أجلهم مما أصابهم، وَلَوْ كُنْتَ فَظًّا جافيا سيئ الخلق غَلِيظَ الْقَلْبِ قاسيَهُ فأغلظت لهم القول، لَانْفَضُّوا مِنْ حَوْلِكَ أي: لتفرقوا عنك، ولم يسكنوا إليك، فَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ فيما يختص بك، وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ في حق ربك حتى يشفعك فيهم، وَشاوِرْهُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ الذي يصح أن يشاور فيه تطييباً لخاطرهم، ورفعاً لأقدارهم، واستخراجاً وتمهيداً لسنة المشاورة لغيرهم، وخصوصاً الأمراء.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-4","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «ما شقى عبد بمشورة، وما سعد باستغناء برأى» . وقال أيضاً: «مَا خَابَ مَن اسْتَخَارَ، وَلاَ نَدِمَ من اسْتَشَار» . وقال أيضا- عليه الصلاة والسلام- «إذَا كَانَ أُمَرَاؤُكُمْ خِيَارَكُمْ، وَأَغْنِيَاؤُكُمْ أَسخيَاءَكُمْ، وأَمرُكُم شُورَى بَيْنَكُم، فَظَهْرُ الأرْض خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ مِنْ بَطْنِهَا. وإذا كَانَ أُمَرَاؤُكُمْ شِرَارَكُمْ وأَغْنِيَاؤُكُمْ بُخَلاءَكُمْ، ولم تكن أموركم شُورَى بَيْنَكُم، فبَطْنُ الأرْضِ خَيرٌ من ظَهْرِهَا» .","anchor":"ar-q3-159-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-5","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"فَإِذا عَزَمْتَ على شيء بعد الشورى، (فتوكل على الله) أي: ثق به وكيلاً، إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَوَكِّلِينَ فينصرهم ويهديهم إلى ما فيه صلاحهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-6","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"الإشارة: ما اتصف به نبينا- عليه الصلاة والسلام- من السهولة والليونة والرفق بالأمة، اتصفت به ورثته من الأولياء العارفين، والعلماء الراسخين، ليتهيأ لهم الدعوة إلى الله، أو إلى أحكام الله، ولو كانوا فظاظاً غلاظاً لانفض الناس من حولهم، ولم يتهيأ لهم تعريف ولا تعليم، فينبغي لهم أن يعفوا ويصفحوا ويغفروا ويصبروا على جفوة الناس، ويستغفروا لهم، ويشاوروهم في أمورهم، اقتداء برسولهم، فإذا عزموا على إمضاء شيء فليتوكلوا على الله إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَوَكِّلِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-7","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"قال الجنيد- رضي الله عنه-: (التوكل أن تقبل بالكلية على ربك وتعرض عمن دونه) . وقال الثوري: أن تفني تدبيرك في تدبيره، وترضى بالله وكيلاً ومدبراً، قال الله تعالى: وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلًا. وقال ذو النون: (خُلع الأرباب، وقطع الأسباب.) وقال الخواص: قطع الخوف والرجاء مما سوى الله تعالى. وقال العرجي: رد العيش إلى يوم واحد، وإسقاط هم غد. هـ. وقال سهل: معرفة معطي أرزاق المخلوقين، ولا يصح لأحد التوكل حتى تكون عنده السماء كالصفر (١) والأرض كالحديد، لا ينزل من السماء قطر، ولا يخرج من الأرض نبات، ويعلم أن الله لا ينسى له ما ضمن من رزقه بين هذين. هـ. وقيل: هو اكتفاء العبد الذليل بالرب الجليل، كاكتفاء الخليل بالخليل، حين لم ينظر إلى عناية جبريل. وقيل لبهلول المجنون: متى يكون العبد متوكلاً؟ قال: إذا كان بالنفس غريباً بين الخلق، وبالقلب قريباً إلى الحق.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-8","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"وقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «مَنْ سَرَّهُ أنْ يَكُونَ أكْرَم النَّاسِ فَلْيَتقِ الله، ومَنْ سَرَّه أن يكُون أغنى النّاس فليكن بما في يد الله أوثق منه بما في يَده» .","anchor":"ar-q3-159-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-9","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"قال ابن جزي: التوكل هو الاعتماد على الله في تحصيل المنافع وحفظها بعد حصولها، وفي دفع المضرات ورفعها بعد وقوعها، وهو من أعلى المقامات، لوجهين: أحدهما: قوله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَوَكِّلِينَ، والآخر:","anchor":"ar-q3-159-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-10","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"الضمان الذي في قوله: وَمَنْ يَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ فَهُوَ حَسْبُهُ، وقد يكون واجباً لقوله: وَعَلَى اللَّهِ فَتَوَكَّلُوا إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ، فجعله شرطاً في الإيمان، ولظاهر قوله: وَعَلَى اللَّهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ فإن الأمر محمول على الوجوب.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-11","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"واعلم أن الناس في التوكل على ثلاث مراتب:","anchor":"ar-q3-159-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-12","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"الأولى: أن يعتمد العبد على ربه، كاعتماد الإنسان على وكيله المأمون عنده، الذي لا يشك فى نصيحته له وقيامه بمصالحه. الثانية: أن يكون العبد مع ربه كالطفل مع أمه لا يعرف سواها ولا يلجأ إِلاَّ إليها. الثالثة: أن يكون العبد مع ربه كالميت بين يدي الغاسل، قد أسلم إليه نفسه بالكلية.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-13","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"فصاحب الدرجة الأولى عنده حظ من النظر لنفسه، بخلاف صاحب الثانية. وصاحب الثانية له حظ من الاختيار، بخلاف صاحب الثالثة. وهذه الدرجات مبنية على التوحيد الخاص، الذي تكلمتُ عليه في قوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-159-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-14","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"وَإِلهُكُمْ إِلهٌ واحِدٌ، فهي تقوى بقوته وتضعف بضعفه.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-15","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"فإن قيل: هل يشترط في التوكل ترك الأسباب أم لا؟ فالجواب: أن الأسباب على ثلاثة أقسام:","anchor":"ar-q3-159-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-16","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"أحدها: سبب معلوم قطعاً قد أجراه الله، فهذا لا يجوز تركه كالأكل لرفع الجوع واللباس لرفع البرد.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-17","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"الثاني: سبب مظنون: كالتجارة وطلب المعاش، وشبه ذلك، فهذا لا يقدح فعله في التوكل، فإن التوكل من أعمال القلوب لا من أعمال البدن، ويجوز تركه لمن قوي عليه.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-18","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"والثالث: سبب موهوم بعيد، فهذا يقدح فعله في التوكل، قلت: ولعل هذا مثل طلب الكيمياء والكنوز وعلم النار والسحر، وشبه ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-19","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"ثم فوق التوكل التفويض، وهو: الاستسلام لأمر الله تعالى بالكلية، فإن المتوكل له مراد واختيار، وهو يطلب مراده في الاعتماد على ربه، وأما المفوض فليس له مراد ولا اختيار، بل أسند الاختيار إلى الله تعالى، فهو أكمل أدباً مع الله. هـ وأصله للغزالي، وسيأتي بقية الكلام عند قوله: وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْحَيِّ الَّذِي لا يَمُوتُ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-159-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-159-20","r":"q3-159","title":"3:159 · Gentleness, consultation and the three degrees of trust","text":"ولما أمر نبيّه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- بالتوكل، رغب فيه جميع عباده، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-159-20"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-159-s1","r":"q3-159","title":"Fabi-mā, faẓẓ and faḍḍ","text":"I say: The mā of fa-bi-mā ( فَبِمَا ) is additional for emphasis ( صلة ). Faẓẓ ( فظّ ) means coarse or rough; its noun forms include faẓāẓa and fuẓūẓ . A man may be called faẓẓ and a woman faẓẓa . Faḍḍ , written with ḍād (ض) rather than ẓāʾ (ظ), means dispersal, and may also mean breaking, whence the blessing “May God not break your mouth.”","anchor":"en-q3-159-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-159-s2","r":"q3-159","title":"Forgiveness, esteem and prudent decision","text":"By divine mercy and favour you were gentle, approachable and kind. When they disobeyed and fled, you still showed kindness, indeed feeling grief on their account. Had you been coarse in manners and hard-hearted, speaking harshly, they would have dispersed and found no ease with you. Pardon their wrong towards you; seek God's forgiveness for what concerns His right, so that your intercession might benefit them; and consult them in matters legitimately open to consultation. This consoles them, honours their judgment, draws counsel from them and establishes a precedent of consultation ( المشاورة ) for others, especially rulers. The Prophet, blessings and peace be upon him, is quoted as saying: “No servant is made wretched by consultation, nor happy by relying solely upon his own opinion.” He also said: “One who seeks guidance [by istikhāra] does not fail, and one who consults does not regret.” He also said: “When your rulers are the best among you, your wealthy people are the generous among you, and your affairs are settled by consultation among you, the surface of the earth is better for you than its interior. When your rulers are the worst among you, your wealthy people are the misers among you, and your affairs are not settled by consultation among you, the earth’s interior is better than its surface.” After consulting, once you resolve upon a course, trust in God as your protecting Agent ( وكيل ), who loves those exercising trust ( المتوكلين ), guides them and grants what benefits them.","anchor":"en-q3-159-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-159-s3","r":"q3-159","title":"The inheritance of Prophetic gentleness and the meaning of tawakkul","text":"The realized friends of God and firmly rooted scholars inherit our Prophet's gentleness and consideration, so that they may summon people to God or teach His rulings. If they were coarse and hard, people would scatter and neither making God known ( تعريف ) nor teaching ( تعليم ) would succeed. They must therefore pardon and forgive, bear others' harshness patiently, ask pardon on their behalf, consult them in their affairs and, when resolved, put their trust in God. Al-Junayd says: “Trust is to turn entirely to your Lord and turn away from all beneath Him.” Al-Thawrī calls it annihilating one's own management ( تدبير ) within His management and accepting God as Agent and Director of affairs. God says: “God suffices as a Trustee.” Dhū al-Nūn speaks of casting off other lords and cutting away secondary causes; al-Khawwāṣ, of severing fear and hope with regard to everything but God; al-ʿArjī, of reducing one's concern for subsistence to the present day and putting aside tomorrow's care. Sahl defines it as knowing who provides all created beings. One cannot realize trust, he says, until one could see the heavens as copper and the earth as iron—no rain descending and no growth emerging—and still know that God will not neglect the livelihood He has guaranteed. Another definition is the humble servant's sufficiency in the Majestic Lord, like Abraham's sufficiency in his intimate Friend when he did not look to Gabriel's offer. Asked when the servant trusts, Buhlūl replied: “When he is a stranger to creatures in himself, but near to the Real in his heart.” The Prophet is quoted as saying: “Whoever wishes to be the noblest of people should fear God; whoever wishes to be the richest should be more confident in what lies with God than in what lies in his own hand.” [XIV-N145]","anchor":"en-q3-159-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-159-s4","r":"q3-159","title":"Three degrees, three sorts of means and tafwīḍ beyond tawakkul","text":"Ibn Juzayy explains that tawakkul ( التوكل ) is reliance upon God in obtaining and preserving benefits, and repelling or removing harms. It is among the highest stations ( المقامات ), as God loves those who rely upon Him [Q 3:159] and guarantees sufficiency to whoever does so [Q 65:3]. It may even be obligatory, because God links it to faith [Q 5:23], and the scriptural imperative indicates an obligation. There are three degrees. First, a servant relies on the Lord as a man on a trusted attorney who can be counted upon to protect his interests. Second, he is with God like a child with its mother, knowing and seeking refuge in none besides her. Third, he is with God like a corpse before the washer of the dead, having surrendered himself wholly. The first still notices his own interest, unlike the second; the second retains something of personal choice, unlike the third. These stages rest upon particular or realized tawḥīd ( التوحيد الخاص ), previously discussed at Q 2:163, and grow or decline with its strength. Must reliance entail abandoning outward causes ( الأسباب )? No single answer applies. Causes are of three kinds. First are means known with certainty through God's established order: these may not be abandoned, like eating to relieve hunger or dressing against cold. Second are probable means, such as trading or seeking livelihood: using them does not impair trust, which belongs to the acts of the heart, not to bodily acts; someone strong enough may also leave them. Third are remote, imaginary means ( الأسباب الموهومة البعيدة ): pursuing these impairs tawakkul. Ibn ʿAjība suggests searches for alchemy, buried treasure, divinatory “knowledge of fire” or sorcery as examples. Above tawakkul lies tafwīḍ ( التفويض ), consigning the whole affair to God in utter surrender. The one who trusts still has an aim and choice, asking God to realize that aim; the one who consigns has no preference or choice, having entrusted choice itself to God. Such a person displays more complete adab ( أدب ) towards God. Ibn ʿAjība attributes the underlying account to al-Ghazālī and refers readers to Q 25:58 for further treatment. Success comes from God.","anchor":"en-q3-159-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-159-s5","r":"q3-159","title":"","text":"Having commanded His Prophet to trust, God commends that trust to all His servants.","anchor":"en-q3-159-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-160","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self 3:160","anchor":"unit-q3-160"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-160-1","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"إِنْ يَنْصُرْكُمُ اللَّهُ فَلا غالِبَ لَكُمْ وَإِنْ يَخْذُلْكُمْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَنْصُرُكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ وَعَلَى اللَّهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ (160)","anchor":"ar-q3-160-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-160-2","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: (إِنْ يَنْصُرْكُمُ اللَّهُ) كما نصركم يوم بدر، (فلا غالب لكم) من أحد من الناس، (وإن يخذلكم) كما خذلكم يوم أحد، (فمن) هذا (الذي ينصركم من بعده) تعالى، أي: فلا ناصر سواه. وهذا تنبيه على الحث على التوكل، وتحريض على ما يستوجب به النصر، وهو الاعتماد على الله، وتحذير مما يستوجب الخذلان، وهو مخالفة أمره وعصيان رسوله، أو الاعتماد على غيره، ولذلك قال: (وعلى الله فليتوكَّل المؤمنون) لِمَا علموا ألا ناصر سواه.","anchor":"ar-q3-160-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-160-3","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"الإشارة: إن ينصركم الله على مجاهدة النفوس، ودوام السير إلى حضرة القدوس، فلا غالب لكم من النفس، ولا من الناس ولا من الهوى ولا من الشيطان، وإن يخذلكم- والعياذ بالله- فمن ذا الذي ينصركم من بعد خذلانه لكم؟ فليعتمد المريد في سيره على مولاه، وليستنصر به في قطع حظوظه وهواه، فإنه لا ناصر له سواه. وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q3-160-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-160-4","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"إِذَا كَانَ عُوْنُ اللهِ لِلمَرْءِ نَاصِراً ... تَهَيَّأ لَهُ مِنْ كُلِّ صَعْبِ مُرَادُهُ","anchor":"ar-q3-160-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-160-5","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"وَإِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ عَوْنٌ مِن اللهِ للْفَتَى ... فَأَكْثَرُ مَا يَجْنِي عَلَيْهِ اجْتِهَادُهُ","anchor":"ar-q3-160-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-160-6","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-160-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-160-7","r":"q3-160","title":"3:160 · Victory, reliance and the defeat of the lower self","text":"ولما تبادرت الرماة إلى الغنيمة كما تقدم، وقع فى وهمهم أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- يحرمهم من الغنيمة، وذلك غلول لا يليق بحاله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، فنزه الله نبيه عن ذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-160-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-160-s1","r":"q3-160","title":"The conditional structure of divine assistance","text":"If God helps you, as at Badr, no human being can defeat you. If He leaves you without help, as at Uḥud, who besides Him can grant victory? There is no helper apart from Him. The verse encourages reliance ( التوكل ), and the conduct that brings help—dependence upon God—while warning against what leads to being forsaken: disobeying His command, opposing His Messenger or relying upon another. Therefore, “Upon God let the believers place their trust,” for they know no protector besides Him.","anchor":"en-q3-160-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-160-s2","r":"q3-160","title":"Seeking assistance to overcome the self","text":"If God supports you in struggling against your lower selves ( مجاهدة النفوس ) and constantly travelling towards the Presence of the Most Holy, neither self, fellow human, passion nor Satan can master you. But if He forsakes you—God preserve us—who could help after that? The disciple must depend on his Lord and ask His support in severing self-interest and passion, for no other supporter exists. As the poet says: When God's help becomes a man's supporter, all difficulty is made ready for his desire. If God's help does not support a young man, his own exertion is what harms him most. Success is through God, the guide to the straight path.","anchor":"en-q3-160-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-160-s3","r":"q3-160","title":"","text":"When the archers hastened toward the spoils, they suspected that the Prophet might deny them their share, an accusation of ghulūl ( غلول ) incompatible with Prophethood. God cleared His Prophet of it.","anchor":"en-q3-160-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-161","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets 3:161","anchor":"unit-q3-161"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-1","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"وَما كانَ لِنَبِيٍّ أَنْ يَغُلَّ وَمَنْ يَغْلُلْ يَأْتِ بِما غَلَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ ثُمَّ تُوَفَّى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لا يُظْلَمُونَ (161)","anchor":"ar-q3-161-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-2","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"قلت: الغلول: السرقة من الغنائم، فمن قرأ بفتح الياء وضم الغين، فمعناه: لا ينبغي له أن يأخذ شيئاً من الغنيمة خفية، والمراد: تبرئة رسوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام- من ذلك. ومَن قرأ بضم الياء ففيه وجهان: أحدهما:","anchor":"ar-q3-161-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-3","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"أن يكون المعنى، ما كان لنبي أن يُخان، أي: أن تخونه أُمّتُه في المغانم، وكذلك الأمراء، وإنما خص النبيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم بذلك لبشاعة ذلك مع النبيّ لأن المعاصي تعظم بحضرته، والثاني: أن يكون المعنى: ما كان لنبي أن يُنسب إلى الخيانة كقوله: فَإِنَّهُمْ لاَ يُكَذِّبُونَكَ أي: لا ينسبونك إلى الكذب.","anchor":"ar-q3-161-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-4","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ما كانَ ينبغي لِنَبِيٍّ أَنْ يَغُلَّ ويأخذ شيئاً من الغنيمة خفية لأن ذلك خيانة والنبوة تنافي ذلك، والمراد: نزاهة الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- عن ذلك، كقوله: مَا كانَ لِلَّهِ أَنْ يَتَّخِذَ","anchor":"ar-q3-161-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-5","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"مِنْ وَلَدٍ","anchor":"ar-q3-161-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-6","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"، ودفعُ ما توهمه الرماة، فقد روى أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- قال لهم لما تركوا المركز: «ألمْ أعْهَد إليكُمْ ألا تَتْركُوا المركَزَ حتَّى يأتيكُمْ أمْري؟» قالوا: تَرَكْنا بقية إخْوانِنَا وُقوفاً، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «بل ظَننْتُم أنّا نَغُلّ ولا نقْسِمُ لكُمْ» . فنزلت الآية. وقيل إنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: بعث طلائع، فغنم رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، وقسم على من معه فقط، فنزلت، فاسترجع ذلك منهم. وقيل: في قطيفة حمراء فُقدت يوم بدر، فقال المنافقون: لَعَلَّ رَسُولَ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أَخَذَهَا، فنزلت.","anchor":"ar-q3-161-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-7","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"ثم ذكر وعيد الغلول، فقال: وَمَنْ يَغْلُلْ يَأْتِ بِما غَلَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ أي: يأتي بالذي غله يحمله على رقبته، قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لا ألقى أحَدكُمْ يَوْمَ القيامة يجئ على رَقَبته بَعِيرٌ لَهُ رغاء، أو بقرة لها خُوَارٌ، أَوْ شَاةٌ تَيْعَرُ (١) .» ثم قال: «اللهُمَّ هَلْ بَلَّغْتُ؟ ثلاثاً» . كما في البخاري.","anchor":"ar-q3-161-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-8","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"ثُمَّ تُوَفَّى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ جزاء ما كَسَبَتْ تاماً، وَهُمْ لا يُظْلَمُونَ بنقص ثواب مُطيعهم، ولا يزاد على عقاب عاصيهم وكان اللائق بما قبله أن يقول: ثم يوفى ما كسب. لكنه عمم الحكم ليكون كالبرهان على المقصود والمبالغة فيه، وأنه إذا كان كل كاسب مجزياً بعمله، فالغال مع عظم جرمه بذلك أولى. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-161-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-9","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"الإشارة: ما قيل في النبي- عليه الصلاة والسلام- يقال في ورثته الكرام، كالأولياء والعلماء الأتقياء، فإنهم ورثة الأنبياء، فيُظن بهم أحسن المذاهب، ويلتمس لهم أحسن المخارج، لأن الأولياء دلّوا على معرفة الله، والعلماء دلّوا على أحكام الله، وبذلك جاءت الرسل من عند الله، فلا يظن بهم نقص ولا خلل، ولا غلول ولا دخل، فلهم قسط ونصيب من حرمة الأنبياء، ولا سيما خواص الأولياء، ومن يظن بهم نقصاً أو خللاً، ويغل قلبه على شيء من ذلك، فسيرى وباله يوم تفضح السرائر، ثُمَّ تُوَفَّى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لا يُظْلَمُونَ، فلحوم الأولياء والعلماء سموم قاتلة، وظن السوء بهم خيانة حاصلة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-161-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-161-10","r":"q3-161","title":"3:161 · The accusation of ghulūl, variant readings and the rights of prophets","text":"فاعتقاد الكمال فى الأنبياء والأولياء مستوجب لرضى الله، والانتقاد عليهم موجب لمقت الله، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق- جلت قدرته- فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-161-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-161-s1","r":"q3-161","title":"Two vocalizations of yaghulla","text":"I say: Ghulūl ( الغلول ) is secretly stealing from the war booty. Reading the verb with fatḥa on yāʾ and ḍamma on ghayn ( يَغُلَّ ) gives “It does not befit a prophet to take some booty secretly,” vindicating the Messenger. Reading ḍamma on yāʾ ( يُغَلَّ ) admits two interpretations: a prophet should not be betrayed by his community in the distribution of spoils—likewise commanders, although betrayal of a prophet is specially heinous; or a prophet should not be accused of treachery, just as “they do not call you a liar” can mean “they do not impute lying to you.”","anchor":"en-q3-161-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-161-s2","r":"q3-161","title":"Vindicating the Prophet and the warning against misappropriation","text":"It cannot befit a prophet to take spoils secretly, for it is betrayal and incompatible with prophecy. The verse vindicates the Messenger—as in God’s saying, “It is not for God to take a child” [19:35]—and removes the archers’ suspicion. It is reported that, when they abandoned the station, he said to them: “Did I not charge you not to leave the station until my order came to you?” They answered: “We left the rest of our brothers standing there.” The Prophet replied: “Rather, you thought that we would misappropriate the spoils and allot you no share.” Then the verse was revealed. Another account says that he dispatched scouts, then the Messenger of God acquired spoils and divided them only among those with him. The verse was revealed, and he recovered those spoils from them. A third locates the occasion in a missing red cloak at Badr which hypocrites insinuated that the Prophet had taken. Translator’s note: Ibn ʿAjība cites these as alternate accounts, not a single harmonized event. The verse then warns against ghulūl: whoever takes anything secretly will arrive carrying it on his neck on the Day of Resurrection. The Prophet said: “Let me not encounter any of you on the Day of Resurrection coming with a bellowing camel, a lowing cow or a bleating sheep upon his neck.” He then said, “O God, have I conveyed [the message]?” three times, as related in al-Bukhārī. Each soul then receives the full recompense for what it earned, no obedient person losing reward and no offender suffering more than is deserved. Whereas one might have expected “Then what he earned will be paid,” the verse generalizes to every soul, giving the argument greater force: if every earner is recompensed, how much more the one guilty of grave misappropriation. Ibn ʿAjība cites al-Bayḍāwī.","anchor":"en-q3-161-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-161-s3","r":"q3-161","title":"Presuming well of the inheritors of Prophets","text":"What is said of the Prophet applies in an appropriate measure to his noble heirs—the friends of God ( الأولياء ) and scrupulous scholars ( العلماء الأتقياء ). They inherit the work of prophets: the friends of God direct people to knowledge of Him, and scholars to His ordinances. One should think of them in the best ways and seek the best explanations of their conduct; one must not attribute imperfection, defect, misappropriation or corruption to them. They have a share in the reverence owed to the prophets, especially the elect among the friends of God. Whoever stores up suspicion against them will see its bitter consequence on the day secrets are exposed, for each soul is paid what it has earned. The “flesh” of the friends of God and scholars is deadly poison, and thinking ill of them is betrayal. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-161-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-161-s4","r":"q3-161","title":"","text":"Belief in the perfection of prophets and the friends of God brings God’s good pleasure, while finding fault with them brings His abhorrence.","anchor":"en-q3-161-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-162-163","r":"q3-162-163","title":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance","text":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance 3:162–163","anchor":"unit-q3-162-163"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-162-163-1","r":"q3-162-163","title":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance","text":"أَفَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ رِضْوانَ اللَّهِ كَمَنْ باءَ بِسَخَطٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَمَأْواهُ جَهَنَّمُ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيرُ (162) هُمْ دَرَجاتٌ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ (163)","anchor":"ar-q3-162-163-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-162-163-2","r":"q3-162-163","title":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: (أفمن اتبع رضوان الله) بأن اعتقد في نبيه الكمال، وأطاعه في وصف الجلال والجمال، وهم المؤمنون، حيث نزهوا نبيهم من النقائص، ومَن هَجَسَ في قلبه شيء بادر إلى التوبة، ثم اتصف بكمال الخصائص، هل يكون كَمَنْ باءَ بغضب مِنَ اللَّهِ؟ وهم المنافقون، حيث نافقوا الرسول واتهموه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- بالغلول.","anchor":"ar-q3-162-163-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-162-163-3","r":"q3-162-163","title":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance","text":"أو يقول: أَفَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ رِضْوانَ اللَّهِ بالطاعة والانقياد كَمَنْ باءَ بِسَخَطٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ بالمعاصي وسوء الاعتقاد وَمَأْواهُ جَهَنَّمُ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيرُ أي المنقلب، والفرق بين المصير والمرجع: أن المصير يجب أن يخالف الحالة الأولى، ولا كذلك المرجع. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-162-163-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-162-163-4","r":"q3-162-163","title":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance","text":"هُمْ دَرَجاتٌ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ أي: أهل الرضوان درجات متفاوتة عند الله، على قدر سعيهم في موجب الرضا، وأهل السخط درجات أيضاً، على قدر تفاوتهم في العصيان، وهو على حذف مضاف، أي: ذُوو درجات، وَاللَّهُ بَصِيرٌ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ فيجازي كلا على قدر سعيه.","anchor":"ar-q3-162-163-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-162-163-5","r":"q3-162-163","title":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance","text":"الإشارة: (أفمن اتبع رضوان الله) بتعظيم الأولياء والعلماء وأهل النسبة، كمن باء بسخط من الله بإهانة من أمر الله أن يُعظم ويُرفع، ومأواه حجاب الحس وعذاب البعد، وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيرُ، فأهل القرب درجات على قدر تقربهم إلى ربهم، وأهل البعد درجات في البعد على قدر بعدهم من ربهم، بشؤم ذنبهم وسوء أدبهم، والله بصير بأعمالهم وما احتوت عليه قلوبهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-162-163-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-162-163-6","r":"q3-162-163","title":"3:162–163 · Divine pleasure and wrath, degrees of nearness and distance","text":"ثم ذكر موجب التعظيم للرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- وهو كونه نعمة مهداة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-162-163-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-162-163-s1","r":"q3-162-163","title":"Riḍwān, sakhaṭ, maṣīr and marjiʿ","text":"Is someone who seeks God's satisfaction by believing His Prophet to be perfect and obeying him in the manifestations of both Majesty and Beauty—namely the believers, who reject blameworthy imputations and, if any such thought occurs in their hearts, immediately repent and then become endowed with the perfection of special qualities—like one who comes burdened with His wrath? The latter are the hypocrites who impugned the Messenger and suspected ghulūl. Or the contrast is broader: obedient submission versus disobedience and corrupt belief. The latter's destination is Hell, an evil end. Al-Bayḍāwī observes that maṣīr ( مصير ) implies becoming different from one's former state, unlike marjiʿ ( مرجع ), which simply means return. “They are degrees with God”: those enjoying His pleasure have differing degrees according to their striving to please Him, and those incurring wrath also differ according to their acts of rebellion. A possessed noun is understood ( حذف مضاف ): dhawū darajāt ( ذوو درجات , possessors of degrees). God sees their works and rewards or judges each accordingly.","anchor":"en-q3-162-163-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-162-163-s2","r":"q3-162-163","title":"Respect for the spiritual path and graded distance from God","text":"Can one who seeks divine pleasure by revering the friends of God, scholars and people affiliated with the path be like one who incurs wrath by insulting those whom God has ordered to be honoured? Such a person's dwelling is the veil of sensory existence ( حجاب الحس ) and the anguish of distance, an evil end. People of nearness have degrees according to their approach to their Lord; people of distance likewise differ in their remoteness, as their faults and poor manners diverge. God knows their actions and what their hearts contain.","anchor":"en-q3-162-163-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-162-163-s3","r":"q3-162-163","title":"","text":"God next explains why the Messenger should be honoured: his coming is a divinely sent favour.","anchor":"en-q3-162-163-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-164","r":"q3-164","title":"3:164 · The Messenger's three offices and the continuing masters of formation","text":"3:164 · The Messenger's three offices and the continuing masters of formation 3:164","anchor":"unit-q3-164"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-164-1","r":"q3-164","title":"3:164 · The Messenger's three offices and the continuing masters of formation","text":"لَقَدْ مَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ بَعَثَ فِيهِمْ رَسُولاً مِنْ أَنْفُسِهِمْ يَتْلُوا عَلَيْهِمْ آياتِهِ وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَإِنْ كانُوا مِنْ قَبْلُ لَفِي ضَلالٍ مُبِينٍ (164)","anchor":"ar-q3-164-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-164-2","r":"q3-164","title":"3:164 · The Messenger's three offices and the continuing masters of formation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لَقَدْ مَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ حيث بَعَثَ فِيهِمْ رَسُولًا مِنْ أَنْفُسِهِمْ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-164-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-164-3","r":"q3-164","title":"3:164 · The Messenger's three offices and the continuing masters of formation","text":"من جنسهم، أو من نسبهم، عربيّاً مثلهم ليفهموا كلامه بسهولة، ويفتخروا به على غيرهم. وتخصيص المؤمنين بالمنة، وإن كانت نعمته عامة لزيادة انتفاعهم على غيرهم لشرفهم وذكرهم به، حال كونه يَتْلُوا عَلَيْهِمْ آياتِهِ القرآن، بعد أن كانوا جاهلية لا يعرفون الوحي ولا سمعوا به، وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ أي: يطهرهم من دنس الذنوب ودرن العيوب، وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتابَ أي: القرآن، وَالْحِكْمَةَ أي: السنة، وَإِنْ كانُوا أي: وإنه، أي: الأمر والشأن كانوا مِنْ قَبْلُ بعثته لَفِي ضَلالٍ مُبِينٍ أي: ظاهر بيِّن.","anchor":"ar-q3-164-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-164-4","r":"q3-164","title":"3:164 · The Messenger's three offices and the continuing masters of formation","text":"الإشارة: لقد منّ الله على المتوجهين إليه الطالبين لمعرفته، حيث بعث لهم من يأخذ بأيديهم، ويطوي مسافة البعد عنهم، وهم شيوخ التربية، يتلون عليهم آياته الدالة على كشف الحجاب وفتح الباب، ويزكيهم من دنس العيوب المانعة لعلم الغيوب، ثم يزكيهم من درن الحس إلى مشاهدة القرب والأنس، ويعلمهم الكتاب المشتمل على عين التحقيق، والحكمة المشتملة على التشريع وبيان الطريق، فيجمعون لهم ما بين الحقيقة والشريعة، وقد كانوا قبل ذلك في ضلال مبين عن الجمع بينهما. وهذه المنّة عامة في كل زمان، إذ لا تخلو الأرض من داع يدعو إلى الله، ومن اعتقد قطعه فقد قطع منّة الله، واستعجز قدرة الله، وسد باب الرحمة في وجه عباد الله، والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q3-164-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-164-5","r":"q3-164","title":"3:164 · The Messenger's three offices and the continuing masters of formation","text":"ولما استغرب الصحابة- رضى الله عنهم- ما وقع بهم يوم أحد، مع كونهم وعدوا النصر، نبههم الحق تعالى أن ذلك منهم بشؤم مخالفتهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-164-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-164-s1","r":"q3-164","title":"Recitation, purification and instruction","text":"God bestowed a great favour upon believers by sending them a messenger from among themselves : one of their own kind, or of their own lineage, an Arab like them, so that they would readily understand his words and find distinction through him. Though his mission benefits all, the believers are singled out because they profit from it more fully and attain honour and renown through it. He recites God's signs to them—the Qurʾān—when they had lived in the Age of Ignorance without knowledge or experience of revelation. He purifies them ( يُزَكِّيهِمْ ) of the contamination of sins and defects; teaches them the Book ( الكتاب ), the Qurʾān, and Wisdom ( الحكمة ), the Sunna. Before his mission they were plainly astray. The construction “though they were ...” ( wa-in kānū ) can carry an understood matter or affair ( ضمير الشأن ).","anchor":"en-q3-164-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-164-s2","r":"q3-164","title":"The enduring favour of spiritual educators","text":"Likewise God favours those turning to Him and seeking gnosis ( معرفة ) by sending people who take them by the hand and fold away the distance separating them from Him: the spiritual educators ( شيوخ التربية ). These recite signs showing how the veil can be removed and the door opened; purify seekers of faults that impede knowledge of the Unseen, then cleanse them of attachment to sensory limitation ( درن الحس ) until they witness intimacy and nearness; and teach the Book as the locus of realized truth ( عين التحقيق ) and Wisdom as the locus of practical legislation ( التشريع ) and clarification of the road. Thus they unite spiritual Reality ( الحقيقة ) and Revealed Law ( الشريعة ), while previously their disciples were plainly astray about bringing the two together. This favour continues in every age: earth never lacks an inviter to God. Whoever says this possibility has ceased denies God's favour, treats His power as impotent and closes the gate of divine mercy against His servants—God protect us.","anchor":"en-q3-164-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-164-s3","r":"q3-164","title":"","text":"As the Companions wondered at Uḥud in view of the promised victory, God reminded them that the defeat arose through their own disobedience.","anchor":"en-q3-164-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-165","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom 3:165","anchor":"unit-q3-165"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-1","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"أَوَلَمَّا أَصابَتْكُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ قَدْ أَصَبْتُمْ مِثْلَيْها قُلْتُمْ أَنَّى هذا قُلْ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ أَنْفُسِكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (165)","anchor":"ar-q3-165-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-2","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"قلت: الهمزة- للتفريع، و (لَمَّا) : ظرف، خافضة لشرطها، منصوبة بجوابها، وهي معطوفة على محذوف، أي: أكان ما كان يوم أحد، ولمّا أصابتكم مصيبة، قلتم ما قلتم، و (قد أصبتم) : جملة حالية.","anchor":"ar-q3-165-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-3","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أحين أَصابَتْكُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ يوم أحد بقتل سبعين منكم، وقَدْ أَصَبْتُمْ مِثْلَيْها يوم بدر فقتلتم سبعين وأسرتم سبعين، قُلْتُمْ أَنَّى هذا أي: من أين أصابنا هذا البلاء وقد وعدنا النصر؟ قُلْ لهم: هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ أَنْفُسِكُمْ أي: مما اقترفته أنفسكم من مخالفة المركز، والنصر الموعود كان مشروطاً بالثبات والطاعة، فلما اختل الشرط اختل المشروط، إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ فيقدر على النصر بشرط وبغيره، لكن حكمته اقتضت وجود الأسباب والشروط لأن هذا العالم قائم بين قدرة وحكمة.","anchor":"ar-q3-165-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-4","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"أو: (قُلْ هُوَ مِنْ عِنْدِ أَنْفُسِكُمْ) باختياركم الفداء يوم بدر. رُوِيَ عن على رضي الله عنه قال: (جاء جِبْريل إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يوم بدر فقال: خيِّرْ أصْحَابَكَ في الأسارى، إن شاءوا القتل، وإن شاءوا الفداء، على أن يقتل مِنْهُمْ عاماً مقبلاً مِثْلُهمْ، قالوا: الفِدَاء ويُقْتَلُ مِنَّا.) . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-165-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-5","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"الإشارة: إذا أصاب المريد شيء من المصائب والبلايا، فلا يستغرب وقوع ذلك به، ولا يتبرم منه، فإنه في دار المصائب والفجائع، «لا تستغرب وقوع الأكدار ما دُمتَ في هذه الدار، فإنما أبرزت ما هو مستحق وصفها وواجب نعتها» . وإذا كان أصابته مصيبة في وقت، فقد أصابته نعمٌ جمة في أوقات عديدة، فليشكر الله على ما أولاه، وليصبر على ما ابتلاه، ليكون صباراً شكوراً.","anchor":"ar-q3-165-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-6","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"قال الشيخ أبو الحسن- رضي الله عنه-: (العارف هو الذي عرف إساءاته في إحسان الله إليه، وعرف شدائد الزمان في الألطاف الجارية من الله عليه، فاذكروا آلاء الله لعلكم تفلحون) . وأيضاً: كل ما يصيب المؤمن فمن كسب يده، ويعفو عن كثير.","anchor":"ar-q3-165-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-7","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"وإن كان المريد وعد بالحفظ والنصر، فقد يكون ذلك بشروط خفيت عليه، فلم تتحقق فيه، فيخلف حفظه لينفذ قدر الله فيه، وَكانَ أَمْرُ اللَّهِ قَدَراً مَقْدُوراً.","anchor":"ar-q3-165-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-165-8","r":"q3-165","title":"3:165 · The loss at Uḥud, self-accounting and the interplay of power and wisdom","text":"وليتميز الصادق من الكاذب والمخلص من المنافق، كما أشار إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-165-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-165-s1","r":"q3-165","title":"The interrogative hamza and lammā","text":"I say: The interrogative hamza ( الهمزة ) marks an inferential continuation ( tafrīʿ ). Translator’s note: Cairo I:432 prints للتفريع , “for inferential continuation,” retained here. Al-Bayḍāwī’s parallel exposition of 3:165 (II:47) instead has taqrīʿ , “rebuke,” together with taqrīr , “eliciting acknowledgement.” lammā ( لما ) is an adverb ( ظرف ), its following condition governed by it in the genitive relation and the whole governed by its answer. The expression is connected with an omitted preceding phrase: “Did what happened at Uḥud happen, and when a calamity befell you did you say what you said?” “Though you had inflicted [twice as much]” ( قد أصبتم ) is a circumstantial sentence ( جملة حالية ).","anchor":"en-q3-165-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-165-s2","r":"q3-165","title":"The conditions of the promise","text":"When seventy of you were killed at Uḥud, though at Badr you had slain seventy enemies and taken seventy prisoners, you asked, “How could this calamity have overtaken us, when victory was promised?” Say: “It comes from yourselves,” from your disobedience in abandoning the appointed post. Victory was promised on the condition of steadfast obedience ( الثبات والطاعة ); when the condition ( الشرط ) failed, so did the conditioned outcome ( المشروط ). God could give victory with or without such conditions, for He is powerful over all things, but His Wisdom ( الحكمة ) willed there should be causes and conditions: this world subsists between divine Power ( القدرة ) and Wisdom ( الحكمة ). Another explanation relates the loss to the Muslims' decision to accept ransom after Badr. ʿAlī is reported to have said that Gabriel offered them the option of killing the captives or ransoming them on condition that a corresponding number of their own be killed the following year; they chose the ransom and accepted the consequence. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-165-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-165-s3","r":"q3-165","title":"Every affliction considered against the gifts already received","text":"When calamities befall a disciple he should neither find them strange nor resent them: this is an abode marked by affliction and grief. As the Ḥikam says: “Do not be surprised that sorrows occur so long as you remain in this abode: it has only brought forth what belongs to its description and is entailed by its nature.” If he is afflicted at one time, at many other times he has received blessings beyond reckoning. Let him thank God for the gifts and remain patient in the trial: then he is one who is both patient and grateful ( صبّار شكور ). Abū al-Ḥasan says: “The gnostic knows his offences amid God's kindness towards him, and knows the severity of time amid the gracious favours flowing to him. Remember God's benefits, that you may prosper.” Whatever misfortune befalls a believer comes by what his hands have earned, yet God pardons much. Nor should one conclude that a promise of preservation was absolute when it may have concealed conditions unknown to him. Those conditions may fail, allowing the divine decree to take effect: God's command is a destiny already decreed ( قدراً مقدوراً ).","anchor":"en-q3-165-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-165-s4","r":"q3-165","title":"","text":"Thus the truthful are distinguished from the liar and the sincere from the hypocrite.","anchor":"en-q3-165-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-166-168","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor 3:166–168","anchor":"unit-q3-166-168"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-1","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"وَما أَصابَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعانِ فَبِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ (166) وَلِيَعْلَمَ الَّذِينَ نافَقُوا وَقِيلَ لَهُمْ تَعالَوْا قاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَوِ ادْفَعُوا قالُوا لَوْ نَعْلَمُ قِتالاً لاتَّبَعْناكُمْ هُمْ لِلْكُفْرِ يَوْمَئِذٍ أَقْرَبُ مِنْهُمْ لِلْإِيمانِ يَقُولُونَ بِأَفْواهِهِمْ ما لَيْسَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِما يَكْتُمُونَ (167) الَّذِينَ قالُوا لِإِخْوانِهِمْ وَقَعَدُوا لَوْ أَطاعُونا ما قُتِلُوا قُلْ فَادْرَؤُا عَنْ أَنْفُسِكُمُ الْمَوْتَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (168)","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-2","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"قلت: (وقيل لهم تعالوا) : استئناف، أو معطوف على (نافقوا) ، و (الذين قالوا لإخوانهم) : بدل من الضمير المجرور في (لهم) ، أي: وقيل للمنافقين: قاتلوا أو ادفعوا، ثم فسرهم بقوله: وهم (الذين قالوا لإخوانهم ... ) الخ. أو من الواو في (يكتمون) ، أو منصوب على الذم، أو مبتدأ، والخبر: (قل..) على من يجيز إنشاء الخبر، و (قعدوا) :","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-3","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"جملة حالية، على إضمار قد.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-4","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَما أَصابَكُمْ يا معشر المسلمين يوم أحد يَوْمَ الْتَقَى جمع المسلمين وجمع الكفار، من القتل والجرح والهزيمة، فَبِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وقضائه، لا راد لإمضائه، وَلِيَعْلَمَ علم ظهور في عالم الشهادة الْمُؤْمِنِينَ والمنافقين فيظهر إيمان هؤلاء وكفر هؤلاء، وقد ظهر نفاقهم حيث رجعوا مع عبد الله بن أبي، وكانوا ثلاثمائة.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-5","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"وذلك انَّ ابن أُبيّ كان رأيه ألا يخرج المسلمون إلى المشركين، فلما طلب الخروجَ قومٌ من المسلمين، فخرج- عليه الصلاة والسلام- كما تقدم، غضب ابن أُبيّ، وقال: أطاعهم وعصاني. فرجع، ورجع معه أصحابه، فتبعهم","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-6","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"أبو جابر عبد الله بن عمرو بن حرام، وقال لهم: ارجعوا (قاتلوا في سبيل الله أو ادفعوا) ، أي: كثروا سواد المسلمين، فقال ابنُ أُبيّ- رأس المنافقين-: ما أرى أن يكون قتالاً، ولو علمنا أن يكون قتال (لاتبعناكم) ، وكنا معكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-7","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"قال تعالى: هُمْ لِلْكُفْرِ يَوْمَئِذٍ أَقْرَبُ مِنْهُمْ لِلْإِيمانِ لظهور الكفر عليهم من كلامهم، فأمارات الكفر عليهم أكثر من أمارات الإيمان، أو: هم لأهل الكفر أقرب نصرة منهم لأهل الإيمان، لأن رجوعهم ومقالتهم تقوية للكفار عليهم وتخذيل للمسلمين، يَقُولُونَ بِأَفْواهِهِمْ ما لَيْسَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ، فهم يظهرون خلاف ما يبطنون، لا تواطئ قلوبهم ألسنتهم بالإيمان، وإضافة القول إلى الأفواه تأكيد وتغليظ، وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ منكم بِما يَكْتُمُونَ من النفاق لأنه يعلمه مفصلاً بعلم واجب، وأنتم تعلمونه مجملا بأمارات.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-8","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"وهؤلاء المنافقون هم (الذين قالوا) في شأن إخوانهم الذين قُتلوا يوم أحد: لَوْ أَطاعُونا وجلسوا في ديارهم ما قُتِلُوا، قالوا هذه المقالة وقد قعدوا عن الخروج، قُلْ لهم يا محمد: فَادْرَؤُا أي: فادفعوا عَنْ أَنْفُسِكُمُ الْمَوْتَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ أنكم تقدرون أن تدفعوا القتل عمن كتب عليه، فادفعوا عن أنفسكم الموت وأسبابه حين يبلغ أجلكم، فإنه أحرى بكم، فالقعود لا يُنجي من الموت إذا وصل الأجل، فإن أسباب الموت كثيرة، فقد يكون القعود سبباً للموت إن بلغ الأجل، وقد يكون الخروج سبباً للنجاة إن لم يبلغ. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-9","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"الإشارة: وما أصابكم يا معشر الفقراء عند توجهكم إلى الحق فارين من الخلق، حين استشرفتم على الجمع وجمع الجمع فبإذن الله فإنَّ الداخل على الله منكور، والراجع إلى الناس مبرور، وليظهر الصادق من الكاذب، فإن محبة الله مقرونة بالبلاء، والطريق الموصلة إليها محفوفة بالمكاره، مشروطة بقتل النفوس وحط الرؤوس، ودفع العلائق، والفرار من العوائق.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-10","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"فإذا قيل للعوام: قاتلوا أنفسكم في سبيل الله لتدخلوا حضرة الله، أو ادفعوا عن أنفسكم العلائق لتشرق عليكم أنوار الحقائق، قالوا: قد انقطع هذا الطريق واندرست أرباب علم التحقيق، ولو نعلم قتالاً بقي يُوصلنا إلى ربنا، كما زعمتم لاتبعناكم ودخلنا فى طريقكم. هم للكفر يومئذ أقرب للإيمان، حيث تحكموا على القدرة الأزلية، وسدوا باب الرحمة الإلهية، وإنما يقولون ذلك احتجاجاً لنفوسهم، وإبقاء على حظوظهم، وليس ذلك من خالص قلوبهم، يقولون بأفواههم ما ليس في قلوبهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-11","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"وإذا نزل بأهل النسبة نكبة أو بلية، قالوا لإخوانهم، الذين دخلوا في طريق القوم، وقد قعدوا هُم مع العوام: لو أطاعونا ولم يدخلوا في هذا الشأن، ما قتلوا أو عذبوا، فقل لهم أيها الفقير: القضاء والقدر يجري على الجميع، فادفعوا عن أنفسكم ما تكرهون، إن كنتم صادقين أن المكاره لا تصيب إلا من توجه لقتال نفسه. والله تعالى أعلم بأسرار كتابه.","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-166-168-12","r":"q3-166-168","title":"3:166–168 · The disclosure of hypocrisy and the test of the spiritual poor","text":"ولمّا قتل الشهداء يوم أحد أكرم الله أرواحهم بما يكل عنه اللسان، فقالوا: يا ليت قومنا يعلمون بما نحن فيه، كى يرغبوا فى الجهاد، فقال لهم الله تعالى: أنا أخبرهم عنكم، فأنزل الله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-166-168-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-166-168-s1","r":"q3-166-168","title":"The referent of alladhīna and the circumstantial clause","text":"I say: “And it was said to them, ‘Come ...’ ” ( وقيل لهم تعالوا ) may begin a new sentence ( استئناف ) or be coordinated with “they acted hypocritically” ( عطف ). “Those who said of their brothers” ( الذين قالوا لإخوانهم ) may be a substitute ( بدل ) for the pronoun governed by lahum ( لهم ), explaining whom the summons addressed. Alternatively it replaces the plural pronoun in yaktumūn ( يكتمون ), or is in the accusative of censure ( نصب على الذم ), or is a subject ( مبتدأ ) answered by “Say ...” as predicate ( خبر ), if one allows a performative command to serve as predicate. Wa-qaʿadū ( وقعدوا ) is a circumstantial sentence ( حال ) with an understood qad ( قد ).","anchor":"en-q3-166-168-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-166-168-s2","r":"q3-166-168","title":"The retreat of Ibn Ubayy and the limits of human control","text":"All the killing, injury and defeat at Uḥud, where the Muslim and opposing armies met, came by divine permission ( بإذن الله ) and decree, which no one can overturn. It served to disclose the believers and hypocrites, making the faith of some and the unbelief of others manifest in the world of appearance ( عالم الشهادة ), as when some three hundred withdrew with ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy. He had opposed going out to meet the idolaters, and when the Prophet went forth at the urging of others, Ibn Ubayy complained, “He listened to them and disobeyed me,” and withdrew with his followers. Abū Jābir ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥarām followed them, begging them to return: “Fight in God's way, or at least defend”—in other words, add to the visible numbers of the Muslim force. Ibn Ubayy replied that he expected no real fighting, and that if they had known there would be fighting, they would have followed. The Qurʾān says that on that day they were closer to unbelief than faith, since the signs of unbelief in their words were more numerous than those of belief. Or they were closer to helping the unbelievers than to supporting the believers, as their withdrawal emboldened the one party and discouraged the other. They speak with their mouths what their hearts do not share; specifically mentioning mouths intensifies the charge. God knows their inner hypocrisy in full and necessarily, whereas people can infer it only generally from outward signs. The same hypocrites said while sitting out the battle that their brethren would not have been killed had they stayed home. Say: if your calculations could avert a decree of death, avert your own when the appointed hour arrives. Remaining at home cannot ward off death, for its causes are many: staying may itself be the circumstance of death when the term arrives, and going out may be the circumstance of safety when it has not arrived. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-166-168-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-166-168-s3","r":"q3-166-168","title":"Trial reveals who can endure the quest for God","text":"O spiritual poor, what befalls you when turning from creatures to the Real, as you approach gathering ( الجمع ) and the gathering of gathering ( جمع الجمع ), occurs by God's permission. Whoever approaches God is the object of public censure, while one who returns to ordinary life is praised. This exposes the sincere and the false claimant: love for God is attended by trial, and the path is surrounded by hardships and requires the struggle against the lower self, the lowering of one's pride, and the release of attachments and obstacles. When ordinary people are told, “Fight your lower selves for God's sake to enter His Presence; remove attachments so the lights of realities may dawn,” they answer that the path has ended and those who possess realized knowledge are gone. “Had we known a struggle remained that could bring us to our Lord,” they claim, “we would follow you.” That day they are closer to unbelief than to faith: they limit pre-eternal divine Power and close the gate of mercy. They say this only to make excuses for themselves and preserve their worldly portions. Their mouths profess what their hearts do not contain. When people of the path suffer a calamity, those who remained among ordinary people tell their friends who entered the way, “Had they listened to us, they would not have been killed or tormented.” The disciple should reply that divine decree runs through everyone: let those critics avert unwelcome events from their own lives if they truly believe hardship touches only people striving against themselves. God knows best the secrets of His Book.","anchor":"en-q3-166-168-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-166-168-s4","r":"q3-166-168","title":"","text":"When the martyrs of Uḥud were honoured in a manner beyond speech, they wished their people could know of their state and become eager to fight in God’s way. God declared He would tell them.","anchor":"en-q3-166-168-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-169-171","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world 3:169–171","anchor":"unit-q3-169-171"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-1","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"وَلا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْواتاً بَلْ أَحْياءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ (169) فَرِحِينَ بِما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ وَيَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بِالَّذِينَ لَمْ يَلْحَقُوا بِهِمْ مِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ أَلاَّ خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (170) يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بِنِعْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَفَضْلٍ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ (171)","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-2","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"قلت: (ألّاخوف عليهم) : بدل من (الذين لم يلحقوا) ، أو مفعول لأجله، وكرر: (يستبشرون) ليذكر ما تعلق به من الفضل والنعمة، أو: الأول بحال إخوانهم، وهذا بحال أنفسهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-3","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلا تَحْسَبَنَّ أيها الرسول، أو أيها السامع، الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْواتاً بَلْ هم أَحْياءٌ لأن الله تعالى جعل أرواحهم في حواصل طير خضر، يسرحون في الجنة حيث شاءوا عند ربهم، بالكرامة والزلفى، يُرزقون من ثمار الجنة ونعيمها، فحالهم حال الأحياء في التمتع بأرزاق الجنة، بخلاف سائر الأموات من المؤمنين فإنهم لا يتمتعون بالأرزاق حتى يدخلوا الجنة. قاله ابن جزي.","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-4","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"قلت: شهداء الملكوت- وهم العارفون- أعظم قدراً من شهداء السيوف، وراجع ما تقدم في سورة البقرة (١) .","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-5","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"فَرِحِينَ بِما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ من الكرامة والزلفى والنعيم الذي لا يفنى، وَيَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بِالَّذِينَ لَمْ يَلْحَقُوا بِهِمْ مِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ أي: بإخوانهم الذي لم يُقتلوا فيلحقوا بهم من بعدهم. وتلك البشارة هي: أَلَّا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ، أو من أجل أَلَّا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-6","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"والحاصل: أنهم يستبشرون بما تبين لهم من الكرامة في الآخرة، وبحال من تركوا من خلفهم من المؤمنين، وهو أنهم إذا ماتوا أو قُتلوا، كانوا أحياء، حياة لا يدركها خوفُ وقوعِ محذور، ولا حزن فوات محبوب. فالآية تدل على أن الإنسان غير الهيكل المحسوس، بل هو جوهر مدرك بذاته، لا يفنى بخراب البدن، ولا يتوقف على وجود البدن إدراكه وتألمُه والتذاذه. ويؤيد ذلك قوله تعالى في آل فرعون: النَّارُ يُعْرَضُونَ عَلَيْها غُدُوًّا وَعَشِيًّا، وما رَوى ابنُ عباس من أنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم قال: «أرْواحُ الشهداء في أجْوافِ طَيْرِ خَضْرٍ، تَرِدُ أنْهارَ الجنّةِ، وتَأكُلُ منْ ثِمارِها، وتَأوِي إلى قَنَادِيلَ مُعلَّقةٍ في ظلِّ العَرشِ» - قال معناه البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-7","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"ولمّا ذكر استبشارهم بإخوانهم ذكر استبشارهم بما يخصهم فقال: يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بِنِعْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وهو ثواب أعمالهم الجسماني، وَفَضْلٍ وهو نعيم أرواحهم الروحاني، وهو النظر إلى وجهه الكريم، ويستبشرون أيضاً بكونه تعالى لا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، ماتوا في الجهاد أو على فرشهم، حيث حسنت سريرتهم وكرمت علانيتهم، قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «إن لله عباداً يصرفهم عن القتل والزلازل والأسقام، يطيل أعمارهم في حسن العمل، ويحسن أرزاقهم، ويحييهم في عافية، ويميتهم في عافية على الفرش، ويعطيهم منازل الشهداء» (١) . قلت: ولعلهم العارفون بالله، جعلنا الله من خواصهم، وسلك بنا مسالكهم. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-8","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"الإشارة: لا تحسبن الذين بذلوا مُهجهم، وقتلوا أنفسهم بخرق عوائدها، وعكس مراداتها، في طلب معرفة الله، حتى ماتت نفوسهم، وحييت أرواحهم بشهود محبوبهم، حياة لا موت بعدها، فلا تظن أيها السامع أنهم أموات، ولو ماتوا حسّاً، بل هم أحياء على الدوام، وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-9","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"مَوْتُ التَّقِيِّ حَيَاةٌ لا فَنَاءَ لَهَا ... قَدْ مَاتَ قَوْمٌ وَهُمْ فِي النَّاسِ أَحْيَاءُ","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-10","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"فهم عند ربهم يشاهدونه مدة بقائهم، يرزقون من ثمار المعارف وفواكه العلوم، فرحين بما أتحفهم الله به من القرب والسر المكتوم، ويستبشرون بالذين لم يلحقوا بهم في المرتبة ممن تعلق بهم، وأنهم سيصلون إلى ما وصلوا إليه من معرفة الحي القيوم، فلا يلحقهم حينئذٍ خوف ولا حزن ولا هم ولا غم، لما سكن في قلبهم من خمرة محبة الحبيب، والقرب من القريب المجيب، وفي ذلك يقول ابن الفارض:","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-11","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"وإِنْ خَطَرَتْ يوما علَى خاطِر امْرِئ ... أقَامَتْ بِهِ الأفْرَاحُ، وارتَحلَ الهمّ","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-12","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"يستبشرون بنعمة أدب العبودية، وفضل شهود أسرار عظمة الربوبية، وأن الله لا يضيع أجر المؤمنين المحبين لطريق المخصوصين، فإن طريق محبة طريق القوم عناية، والتصديق بها ولاية، وبالله التوفيق وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-169-171-13","r":"q3-169-171","title":"3:169–171 · Martyrdom, the enduring soul and the martyrs of the spiritual world","text":"ولما رجع أبو سفيان من غزوة أُحد، هو وأصحابه، حتى بلغوا الروحاء، ندم وهم بالرجوع، فبلغ ذلك رسولَ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فندب أصحابه للخروج في طلبه، وقال: «لا يخرج معنا إلا من حضر بالأمس» ، فخرج صلّى الله عليه وسلم في سبعين رجلاً حتى بلغوا حمراء الأسد- وهي على ثمانية أميال من المدينة- وكان بأصحابه القرح، فتحاملوا على أنفسهم كي لا يفوتهم الأجر، وألقى الله الرعب في قلوب المشركين، فذهبوا، فأنزل الله- تعالى- في شأن من خرج مع الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم:","anchor":"ar-q3-169-171-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-169-171-s1","r":"q3-169-171","title":"Allā khawfun ʿalayhim and yastabshirūn","text":"I say: The clause allā khawfun ʿalayhim ( ألا خوف عليهم ) may stand as a substitute ( بدل ) for “those who have not joined them,” or as an accusative of cause ( مفعول لأجله ). Yastabshirūn ( يستبشرون ) is repeated to express both the bounty and blessing associated with rejoicing; alternatively the first concerns the condition of their brothers, and the second concerns their own.","anchor":"en-q3-169-171-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-169-171-s2","r":"q3-169-171","title":"The perceiving reality beyond the body","text":"Do not think, Messenger—or any hearer—that those killed in God's way are dead. They are alive: God places their spirits in the crops of green birds that roam wherever they wish in Paradise. They dwell in God's nearness and favour and receive its fruits and delights. Thus they resemble living people in enjoyment of the provisions of Paradise, unlike other dead believers who, according to Ibn Juzayy's account, do not enjoy its provisions until they enter it. Ibn ʿAjība adds: the martyrs of the angelic or spiritual domain ( شهداء الملكوت ), the realized knowers ( العارفون ), are even higher in rank than martyrs of the sword; consult his earlier discussion in al-Baqara. They rejoice at divine generosity, nearness, and delights that do not perish, and rejoice concerning brothers left behind who have not yet been killed and joined them. The good news is that those brothers too will have neither fear nor grief; or rejoicing occurs because there will be no fear or grief. Having discovered the honour of the next life, the martyrs know that those remaining will live after death or being killed in a life without dread of threatened harm or sorrow for desired good lost. The verse therefore points, Ibn ʿAjība argues, to a distinction between the person and the perceptible bodily structure ( الهيكل المحسوس ). The person is a substance capable of perception in its own right ( جوهر مدرك بذاته ): its being does not perish with the body's dissolution, nor does its capacity to perceive, suffer or delight depend on the continuing existence of that body. He cites the Qurʾānic account of Pharaoh's people being exposed to the Fire morning and evening [Q 40:46], and Ibn ʿAbbās’s report that the Prophet said: “The spirits of martyrs are in the insides of green birds; they come to the rivers of Paradise, eat of its fruits and shelter in lamps suspended in the shade of the Throne.” He attributes the substance of the discussion to al-Bayḍāwī. Now God speaks of the gladness that concerns the martyrs themselves: “a blessing,” the bodily reward of their works ( ثواب أعمالهم الجسماني ), and “bounty,” their spiritual delight ( نعيم أرواحهم الروحاني ), which consists in gazing upon the Generous Face. They also rejoice that God does not forfeit any believer's reward, whether that believer dies on the battlefield or in bed, provided inward and outward conduct have been sound. The Prophet said: “God has servants whom He keeps from being killed, from earthquakes and from illnesses. He prolongs their lives in good works, makes their provision good, grants them life in well-being and death in well-being upon their beds, and gives them the stations of martyrs.” Ibn ʿAjība suggests they may be the realized gnostics, praying to be counted among them.","anchor":"en-q3-169-171-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-169-171-s3","r":"q3-169-171","title":"Death to customary desire and life through witnessing","text":"Do not think dead those who offered their life's essence ( مُهَجهم ) and killed their lower selves through breaking habits ( خرق العوائد ) and acting against habitual desires ( عكس المرادات ), seeking knowledge of God until their selves died and their spirits came alive through witnessing the Beloved, a life without subsequent death—even should they die bodily. As the poet says: The death of the Godfearing is a life that does not pass away; some people have died who are alive among humankind. They remain with their Lord in witnessing while they subsist, fed with the fruits of gnosis and the sciences of the heart; they rejoice in divine nearness and in the concealed secret ( السر المكتوم ). They have glad tidings concerning those connected to them who have not yet reached their degree: these too will arrive at knowledge of the Ever-Living, Self-Subsisting One. With the wine of love and nearness settled in their hearts, fear, grief, care and sorrow depart. Ibn al-Fāriḍ says: If she but passed for a day across a person's thought, joys would remain with him and cares depart. They rejoice in the grace of the manners of servanthood ( أدب العبودية ) and in the bounty of witnessing the secrets of Lordship's majesty ( أسرار عظمة الربوبية ). God does not waste the reward of believers who love the path of the elect: loving the path is itself divine solicitude, and affirming it is sainthood. Success is through God, the guide to the straight path.","anchor":"en-q3-169-171-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-169-171-s4","r":"q3-169-171","title":"","text":"When Abū Sufyān reached al-Rawḥāʾ after Uḥud, he contemplated returning; the Prophet urged his Companions to pursue him, saying: “No one is to come out with us except those who were present yesterday.” Seventy wounded men set out with him to Ḥamrāʾ al-Asad, eight miles from Medina, shouldering their injuries to obtain the reward, until God cast fear into their opponents and they withdrew. The following verses concern those who answered the call.","anchor":"en-q3-169-171-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-172","r":"q3-172","title":"3:172 · The wounded believers who answered and the unity of Reality and Law","text":"3:172 · The wounded believers who answered and the unity of Reality and Law 3:172","anchor":"unit-q3-172"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-172-1","r":"q3-172","title":"3:172 · The wounded believers who answered and the unity of Reality and Law","text":"الَّذِينَ اسْتَجابُوا لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما أَصابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا مِنْهُمْ وَاتَّقَوْا أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ (172)","anchor":"ar-q3-172-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-172-2","r":"q3-172","title":"3:172 · The wounded believers who answered and the unity of Reality and Law","text":"قلت: (الذين) : مبتدأ، وجملة (للذين أحسنوا) : خبر، أو صفة للمؤمنين قبله، أو نصب على المدح.","anchor":"ar-q3-172-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-172-3","r":"q3-172","title":"3:172 · The wounded believers who answered and the unity of Reality and Law","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الَّذِينَ اسْتَجابُوا لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ فأطاعوه فيما ندبهم إليه من اللحوق بالمشركين، إرهاباً لهم، مِنْ بَعْدِ ما أَصابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ أي: الجرح، فتحاملوا على أنفسهم حتى ذهبوا مع نبيهم، لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا مِنْهُمْ بأن فعلوا ما أُمروا به، وَاتَّقَوْا الله في مخالفة أمر رسوله، أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ يوم يقدمون عليه.","anchor":"ar-q3-172-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-172-4","r":"q3-172","title":"3:172 · The wounded believers who answered and the unity of Reality and Law","text":"الإشارة: الذين استجابوا لله فيما ندبهم من الوصول إلى حضرته، وللرسول فيما طلبهم به من اتباع سنته، فجعلوا قلوبهم محلاً لحضرته، وجوارحهم متبعة لشريعته، من بعد ما أصابهم في طلب الوصول إلى ذلك قرح وضرب وسجن وإهانة، فصبروا حتى ظفروا بالجمع بين الحقيقة والشريعة، للذين أحسنوا منهم بالثبات على السير إلى الوصول إلى الحق، واتقوا كل ما يردهم إلى شهود الفرق، أجر عظيم وخير جسيم، بالعكوف في الحضرة، والتنعم بالشهود والنظرة.","anchor":"ar-q3-172-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-172-5","r":"q3-172","title":"3:172 · The wounded believers who answered and the unity of Reality and Law","text":"ثم قال الحق تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-172-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-172-s1","r":"q3-172","title":"The position of alladhīna","text":"I say: “Those who” ( الذين ) may be the subject ( مبتدأ ), with “for those who did good” ( للذين أحسنوا ) as predicate ( خبر ); or it may qualify “believers” in the preceding verse ( صفة ); or be set in the accusative in praise ( نصب على المدح ).","anchor":"en-q3-172-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-172-s2","r":"q3-172","title":"They followed despite injury","text":"They responded to God's call and obeyed His Messenger when he urged pursuit of the idolaters to deter them, even after the wound ( القرح ) they suffered. They forced themselves onward despite injury and accompanied their Prophet. Those who acted well by carrying out the command and were mindful of God by not disobeying His Messenger possess a great reward when they come before Him.","anchor":"en-q3-172-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-172-s3","r":"q3-172","title":"Answering both the call to divine Presence and the prophetic way","text":"They respond to God by seeking arrival at His Presence ( الوصول إلى حضرته ) and to the Messenger by following his Sunna. They make their hearts an abode for that Presence and their bodily members instruments of the revealed Law ( الشريعة ). Even when seeking this conjunction brings wounds, beatings, imprisonment or humiliation, they persevere until they unite Reality and Law ( الجمع بين الحقيقة والشريعة ). Those who persist in travelling to the Real and guard against whatever returns them to the vision of mere separation ( شهود الفرق ) receive great reward: abiding in the Presence and delighting in witnessing and contemplation.","anchor":"en-q3-172-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-172-s4","r":"q3-172","title":"","text":"Then God said:","anchor":"en-q3-172-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-173-175","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude 3:173–175","anchor":"unit-q3-173-175"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-1","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"الَّذِينَ قالَ لَهُمُ النَّاسُ إِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ جَمَعُوا لَكُمْ فَاخْشَوْهُمْ فَزادَهُمْ إِيماناً وَقالُوا حَسْبُنَا اللَّهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيلُ (173) فَانْقَلَبُوا بِنِعْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَفَضْلٍ لَمْ يَمْسَسْهُمْ سُوءٌ وَاتَّبَعُوا رِضْوانَ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَظِيمٍ (174) إِنَّما ذلِكُمُ الشَّيْطانُ يُخَوِّفُ أَوْلِياءَهُ فَلا تَخافُوهُمْ وَخافُونِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ (175)","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-2","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"قلت: الموصول بدل من الموصول قبله، و (يخوف) : يتعدى إلى مفعولين للتضعيف، حذف الأول، أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-3","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"يخوفكم أولياءه من الكفار، أو حذف الثاني، أي: يخوف أولياءه القاعدين عن الخروج إلى ملاقاة العدو.","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-4","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"وهنا تفسيران: أحدهما: أن يكون من تتمة غزوة أحد، وهو الظاهر، ليتصل الكلام بما بعده، وذلك أن أبا سفيان لما هَمّ بالرجعة ليستأصل المسلمين، لقيه معبد الخزاعي، فقال له: إن محمداً خرج يطلبك في جمع لم أرَ مثله، فدخله الرعب، فلقيه ركب من عبد القيس يريد المدينة بالميرة، فقال لهم: ثبطوا محمداً عن لحوقنا، ولكم حمل بعير من الزبيب، فلما لقوا المسلمين خوفوهم، فقالوا: حَسْبُنَا اللَّهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيلُ، ومضوا حتى بلغوا حمراء الأسد ثم رجعوا، فعلى هذا:","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-5","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الَّذِينَ قالَ لَهُمُ النَّاسُ وهم ركب عبد قيس حيث قالوا للمسلمين: إِنَّ النَّاسَ يعني أبا سفيان ومن معه، قَدْ جَمَعُوا لَكُمْ ليرجعوا ليستأصلوكم فَاخْشَوْهُمْ وارجعوا إلى دياركم","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-6","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"فَزادَهُمْ ذلك إِيماناً ويقيناً وتثبيتاً في الدين، وهذا يدل على أن الإيمان يزيد وينقص، فيزيد بحسب التوجه إلى الله والتفرغ مما سواه، وينقص بحسب التوجه إلى الدنيا وشغبها، ويزيد أيضاً بالطاعة والنظر والاعتبار، وينقص بالمعصية والغفلة والاغترار.","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-7","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"ولما قال لهم الركب ذلك ليخوفهم، قالُوا حَسْبُنَا اللَّهُ أي: كافينا الله وحده، فلا نخاف غيره، وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيلُ أي: نعم من يتوكل عليه العبد، وهي كلمة يدفع بها ما يخاف ويكره، وهي الكلمة التي قالها إبراهيم حين ألقي في النار، فَانْقَلَبُوا راجعين من حمراء الأسد، متلبسين بِنِعْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وهي العافية والسلامة، وَفَضْلٍ وهي زيادة الإيمان وشدة الإيقان، لَمْ يَمْسَسْهُمْ سُوءٌ من جراحة وكيد عدو، وَاتَّبَعُوا رِضْوانَ اللَّهِ، الذي هو مناط الفوز بخير الدارين، وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَظِيمٍ فقد تفضل عليهم بالتثبيت وزيادة الإيمان، والتوفيق إلى المبادرة إلى الجهاد مع الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم الذي هو موجب الرضوان.","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-8","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"ثم حذَّرهم الحق تعالى ممن ثبّطهم عن اللحوق بالكفار، وهو ركب عبد القيس، تشبيهاً لهم بالشيطان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-9","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"إِنَّما ذلِكُمُ الشَّيْطانُ يخوفكم أولياءه من المشركين، أو يُخَوِّفُ أَوْلِياءَهُ القاعدين من المنافقين، فَلا تَخافُوهُمْ فإن أمرهم بيدي، وَخافُونِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ فإن الإيمان يقتضي إيثار خوف الله على خوف الناس.","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-10","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"التفسير الثاني: أن يكون الكلام على غزوة بدر الصغرى: وذلك أن أبا سفيان لما انصرف من أُحد نادى:","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-11","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"يا محمد، موعدنا بدرٌ لقابل، إن شئت، فقال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «إن شاء الله تعالى» ، فلما كان العام القابل، خرج أبو سفيان فى أهل مكة، حتى نزل مرّ الظهران، فأنزل الله الرعب في قلبه، وبدا له أن يرجع، فلقي نُعيم بن مسعود الأشجعي معتمراً، فقال له: ائت المدينة وأعلمهم أنّا في جمع كثير، وثبطهم عن الخروج، ولك عندي عشر من الإبل، فأتى المدينة فأخبرهم، فكره أصحابُ النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم الخروج، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «والذِي نَفْسِي بِيَدِهِ لأَخْرجَنّ، ولو وَحْدِي» .","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-12","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"فرجع الجَبان وتأهب الشجعان، فخرجوا حتى أتوا بدراً الصغرى، ورجع أبو سفيان إلى مكة، فسموا جيش السويق، ووافق المسلمون السوق ببدر، وكانت معهم تجارات، فباعوا وربحوا، وانصرف النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم إلى المدينة (١) .","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-13","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"فعلى هذا، يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الَّذِينَ اسْتَجابُوا لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ، يعني: في غزوة بدر الصغرى، لميعاد أبي سفيان، مِنْ بَعْدِ ما أَصابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ يعني: في غزوة أحد في العام الأول، لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا مِنْهُمْ بالخروج مع الرسول، وَاتَّقَوْا الله في مخالفته، أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ. الَّذِينَ قالَ لَهُمُ النَّاسُ يعني نُعَيْم بن مسعود، وأطلق عليه الناس لأنه من جنسهم، كما يقال: فلان يركب الخيل، وما يركب إلا فرساً. أو: لأنه انضم إليه","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-14","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"ناس من المدينة وأذاعوا كلامه. إِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ جَمَعُوا لَكُمْ يعني: أبا سفيان وأهل مكة لما خرج إلى مَرّ الظهران. وقوله: فَانْقَلَبُوا بِنِعْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ أي: عافية وسلامة، وَفَضْلٍ ما أصابوا من التجارة، وقوله: إِنَّما ذلِكُمُ الشَّيْطانُ يعني: نعيماً يخوفكم أَوْلِياءَهُ والباقي ظاهر.","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-15","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"الإشارة: أهل القوة من المريدين إذا قيل لهم: إن الناس قد جمعوا لكم ليردوكم أو يؤذوكم فاخشوهم، زادهم ذلك إيماناً وإيقاناً، وتحققوا أنهم على الجادة، لسلوكهم على منهاج من قبلهم أَحَسِبَ النَّاسُ أَنْ يُتْرَكُوا أَنْ يَقُولُوا آمَنَّا الآية، واكتفوا بعلم الله ونظره وبرعايته ونصره، فانقلبوا بنعمة الشهود، وفضل الترقي في عظمة الملك الودود، لم يمسسهم في باطنهم سوء ولا نقصان، واستوجبوا من الله الرضى والرضوان، وإنما ذلكم شيطان يردهم عن مقام الشهود والعيان، فلا ينبغي لهم أن يخافوا ومطلبهم مقام الإحسان، الذي تُبْذل في طلبه الأرواح والأبدان. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-173-175-16","r":"q3-173-175","title":"3:173–175 · God suffices: two historical settings and the meaning of spiritual fortitude","text":"ثم هوَّن شأن الكفار، وأمّن المسلمين من ضررهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-173-175-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-173-175-s1","r":"q3-173-175","title":"The two objects of yukhawwifu","text":"I say: The relative pronoun ( الموصول ) is a substitute ( بدل ) for the relative pronoun before it. Yukhawwifu ( يخوّف ) takes two objects ( مفعولان ) because of the causative doubling. Either the first object is omitted ( حذف الأول ): “he frightens you with his allies among the unbelievers”; or the second is omitted ( حذف الثاني ): “he frightens his allies , those who stayed behind from facing the enemy.”","anchor":"en-q3-173-175-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-173-175-s2","r":"q3-173-175","title":"Ḥamrāʾ al-Asad after Uḥud","text":"Two explanations of the historical setting are given. The first continues the account of Uḥud and, Ibn ʿAjība thinks, best connects the verses. When Abū Sufyān thought of returning to destroy the Muslims, Maʿbad al-Khuzāʿī met him and declared that Muḥammad had set out to pursue him with an assembly unmatched in size. Terror entered Abū Sufyān's heart. When a caravan of ʿAbd al-Qays travelling to Medina for provisions met him, he promised them a camel-load of raisins if they discouraged Muḥammad from further pursuit. The caravan warned the Muslims. They replied, “God suffices us and is an excellent Trustee” ( حسبنا الله ونعم الوكيل ), continued to Ḥamrāʾ al-Asad, and returned home. On this account, “the people” speaking are the ʿAbd al-Qays caravan; those said to have gathered are Abū Sufyān and his men. The warning deepened the believers' faith, certainty and steadfastness. This shows, Ibn ʿAjība says, that faith ( الإيمان ) increases and decreases: it grows through turning to God, relinquishing other preoccupations, obedience and reflection, and declines through worldly distraction, sin, heedlessness and delusion. Their words meant that God alone is sufficient and no other need be feared—words that repel feared and hated things, also spoken by Abraham when cast into the fire. They returned in good health and safety, an outward blessing ( نعمة ), and with greater faith and certainty, an additional favour ( فضل ), uninjured by their enemy and following the pleasure of God, whose bounty made their steadfastness and response to the Messenger possible. Those who tried to deter them—the ʿAbd al-Qays caravan—are likened to Satan: either Satan frightened believers with his polytheist allies, or frightened his own allies, the hypocrites who refused the campaign. Do not fear them, since their affairs are in God's hands; fear God above people if you truly believe.","anchor":"en-q3-173-175-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-173-175-s3","r":"q3-173-175","title":"The later rendezvous at lesser Badr","text":"The second interpretation places the episode in the later lesser Badr ( بدر الصغرى ). Abū Sufyān, on leaving Uḥud, called out for a meeting at Badr the following year. The Prophet replied, “God willing.” When that year came, Abū Sufyān marched from Mecca to Marr al-Ẓahrān, where fear entered his heart and he decided to return. He met Nuʿaym ibn Masʿūd al-Ashjaʿī performing the lesser pilgrimage (ʿumra), offered him ten camels to tell Medina that the Meccans had gathered in overwhelming numbers and to discourage the Muslim departure. Nuʿaym's message troubled the Companions. The Prophet declared, “By Him in whose hand is my soul, I will go out even alone.” The hesitant turned back but the courageous prepared; the Muslims reached lesser Badr while Abū Sufyān returned to Mecca with the army nicknamed “the army of meal” ( جيش السويق ). The Muslims found a market at Badr, traded profitably and returned to Medina. On this second reading, the response of Q 3:172 belongs to the later appointment, after injuries sustained at Uḥud the year before. “The people” giving warning means Nuʿaym alone—called “people” by reference to his kind, as when one says a man rides horses though he rides one horse—or those who assisted in spreading his message. The threatening “people” are Abū Sufyān's Meccans, and the “bounty” includes profit from trade. Here “Satan” means Nuʿaym, who frightens you with his allies. Ibn ʿAjība retains both alternatives.","anchor":"en-q3-173-175-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-173-175-s4","r":"q3-173-175","title":"Fear of others and the increase of the disciples’ certainty","text":"When strong disciples ( أهل القوة من المريدين ) are told that people have gathered to harm or turn them back, their faith and certainty grow, for they recognize the established path of those tested before them: “Do people imagine they will be left alone to say ‘We believe’ ... ?” [Q 29:2]. They content themselves with God's knowledge, gaze, protection and support, and return with the blessing of witnessing ( نعمة الشهود ) and the favour of advancing in the greatness of the loving King ( فضل الترقي ). Their inward selves suffer neither harm nor diminishment, and they become deserving of divine satisfaction. It is Satan who urges them to retreat from the station of direct witnessing ( مقام الشهود والعيان ). They must not fear, for their desired station is iḥsān ( مقام الإحسان ), sought at the cost of lives and bodies. Success comes from God.","anchor":"en-q3-173-175-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-173-175-s5","r":"q3-173-175","title":"","text":"God then diminished the stature of the disbelievers and assured the Muslims of safety from their harm.","anchor":"en-q3-173-175-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-176-177","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God 3:176–177","anchor":"unit-q3-176-177"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-176-177-1","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"وَلا يَحْزُنْكَ الَّذِينَ يُسارِعُونَ فِي الْكُفْرِ إِنَّهُمْ لَنْ يَضُرُّوا اللَّهَ شَيْئاً يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ أَلاَّ يَجْعَلَ لَهُمْ حَظًّا فِي الْآخِرَةِ وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ عَظِيمٌ (176) إِنَّ الَّذِينَ اشْتَرَوُا الْكُفْرَ بِالْإِيْمانِ لَنْ يَضُرُّوا اللَّهَ شَيْئاً وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ (177)","anchor":"ar-q3-176-177-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-176-177-2","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"قلت: حَزَنَ يحزُن كبلغ يبلُغ، وأحزن يُحْزِن، كأَكْرم يكرم، لغتان، والأولى أفصح.","anchor":"ar-q3-176-177-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-176-177-3","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولا يهولك شأن الَّذِينَ يُسارِعُونَ فِي الْكُفْرِ أي: يبادرون إلى الوقوع فيه، كالمنافقين أو الكفار جميعاً، فلا تخف ضررهم إِنَّهُمْ لَنْ يَضُرُّوا اللَّهَ شَيْئاً أي: لن يضروا أولياء الله، وإنما يرجع ضررهم إلى أنفسهم. يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ- بسبب ما أظهر فيهم من المسارعة إلى الكفر- أَلَّا يَجْعَلَ لَهُمْ حَظًّا فِي ثواب الْآخِرَةِ لِمَا سبق لهم من الشقاء، حتى يموتوا على الكفر. وفي ذكر الإرادة إشعار بأن كفرهم بلغ الغاية، حتى أراد أرحم الراحمين ألاَّ يكون لهم حظ من رحمته. وَلَهُمْ مع ذلك عَذابٌ عَظِيمٌ.","anchor":"ar-q3-176-177-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-176-177-4","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"ثم كرر شأنهم تأكيدا فقال: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ اشْتَرَوُا الْكُفْرَ بِالْإِيْمانِ أي: استبدلوا الإيمان الذي ينجيهم من العذاب، لو دخلوا فيه، بالكفر الذي يُوجب العذاب، لَنْ يَضُرُّوا اللَّهَ شَيْئاً وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ موجع، أو يكون في الكفار أصالة، وهذا في المرتدين، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-176-177-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-176-177-5","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"الإشارة: إنكار العوام على الخصوص لا يضرهم، ولا يغض من مرتبتهم، بل يزيدهم رفعةً وعلواً وعزّاً وقرباً، قال تعالى: لاَ تَحْسَبُوهُ شَرًّا لَكُمْ بَلْ هُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ، وسمعت شيخنا البوزيدى رضي الله عنه يقول:","anchor":"ar-q3-176-177-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-176-177-6","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"«كلامُ الناس في الولي كناموسة نفخت على جبل» . أي: لا يلحقهم من ذلك إلا ما يلحق الجبل من نفخ الناموسة، يريد الله ألا يجعل لهم من نصيب القرب شيئاً، ولهم عذاب البعد والنصب، في غم الحجاب وسوء الحساب، لا سيما من تمكن من معرفتهم، ثم استبدل صحبتهم بصحبة العوام، فلا تسأل عن حرمانه التام، والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q3-176-177-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-176-177-7","r":"q3-176-177","title":"3:176–177 · Rejection does not diminish the truth: denial and the path of God","text":"ثم لا يدل إمهال الكافرين وتمتعهم بطول الحياة على إرادة الخير لهم، بل إنما ذلك استدراج وزيادة فى الإثم، كما أشار إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-176-177-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-176-177-s1","r":"q3-176-177","title":"Two constructions of ḥuzn","text":"I say: Both ḥazana/yaḥzunu ( حَزَنَ يَحْزُنُ ), like balagha/yablughu , and aḥzana/yuḥzinu ( أَحْزَنَ يُحْزِنُ ), like akrama/yukrimu , occur; the former is more eloquent.","anchor":"en-q3-176-177-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-176-177-s2","r":"q3-176-177","title":"Neither God nor His friends can be harmed by unbelief","text":"Do not be overwhelmed by those hastening into unbelief, hypocrites or openly unbelieving people, rushing to embrace it. They cannot hurt God in the slightest—that is, they cannot harm God’s friends. Rather the damage returns to themselves. God's will is that, on account of their manifest rushing to unbelief and the misery already allotted to them, they should die in it and have no share in the next world's reward. Mentioning divine will here signals that their unbelief has reached the utmost extreme, to the point that the Most Merciful of the merciful wills that they have no share in His mercy. Beyond that deprivation awaits a great punishment. He repeats the warning for emphasis: those who exchange faith, by which they could have escaped punishment had they embraced it, for unbelief that entails punishment cannot hurt God; theirs is painful torment. Or the first verse refers to those originally unbelieving and the second to apostates ( المرتدين ). God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-176-177-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-176-177-s3","r":"q3-176-177","title":"The claims of ordinary people against the elect","text":"Denial by ordinary people ( العوام ) cannot reduce the station of the elect ( الخصوص ); rather, their attacks increase the elect in elevation, dignity and nearness. “Do not consider it evil for yourselves; rather it is good for you” [Q 24:11]. I heard our teacher al-Būzīdī say, “People's talk against a friend of God is like a gnat blowing upon a mountain.” Such an attack harms them no more than the gnat's breath harms a mountain. God wills that the deniers have no portion of nearness, and they suffer distance, weariness, veiling and a difficult reckoning, especially if they once recognized realized masters and then exchanged their company for that of ordinary people. Their deprivation is grave—God preserve us.","anchor":"en-q3-176-177-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-176-177-s4","r":"q3-176-177","title":"","text":"The respite granted to unbelievers and their enjoyment of long life do not show that God wills them good; they are only a gradual enticement ( استدراج ) and increased wrongdoing.","anchor":"en-q3-176-177-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-178","r":"q3-178","title":"3:178 · The long life that benefits or ensnares","text":"3:178 · The long life that benefits or ensnares 3:178","anchor":"unit-q3-178"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-178-1","r":"q3-178","title":"3:178 · The long life that benefits or ensnares","text":"وَلا يَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَنَّما نُمْلِي لَهُمْ خَيْرٌ لِأَنْفُسِهِمْ إِنَّما نُمْلِي لَهُمْ لِيَزْدادُوا إِثْماً وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ مُهِينٌ (178)","anchor":"ar-q3-178-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-178-2","r":"q3-178","title":"3:178 · The long life that benefits or ensnares","text":"قلت: من قرأ بالتحتية، فالذين كفروا: فاعل، و (أن) وما بعدها: سد مسد المفعولين، ومن قرأ بالفوقية فالذين: مفعول أول، و (إنما) : سد مسد الثاني، و (ما) : مصدرية، والإملال: الإمهال والتأخير. ومنه: وَاهْجُرْنِي مَلِيًّا أي: حينا طويلا.","anchor":"ar-q3-178-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-178-3","r":"q3-178","title":"3:178 · The long life that benefits or ensnares","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولا يظنن الذين كفروا أن إمهالي لهم وإمدادهم بطول الحياة، هو خير لهم، إنما نمهلهم استدراجاً لِيَزْدادُوا إثماً وعقوبة، وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ مُهِينٌ يُهينهم، ويُخزيهم يوم يُعز المؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q3-178-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-178-4","r":"q3-178","title":"3:178 · The long life that benefits or ensnares","text":"الإشارة: إمهال العبد وإطالة عمره، إن كانت أيامه مصروفةً فى الطاعة واليقظة، وزيادة المعرفة، فإطالتها خير، والبركة في العمر إنما هي بالتوفيق وزيادة المعرفة، وفي الحكم: «مَن بورك له في عمره أدرك في يسيرٍ من الزمان مالا تدركه العبارة ولا تلحقه الإشارة» . وإن كانت أيام العمر مصروفة في الغفلة والبطالة وزيادة المعصية، فالموت خير منها. وقد سُئل- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أيُّ الناس خَيْرٌ؟ قال: «مَنْ طَالَ عُمرُه وَحَسُنَ عَمَلُهُ، قيل فَأَيُّ النّاسِ شر؟ قال: مَنْ طَالَ عَمُرُهُ وَسَاءَ عَمله» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-178-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-178-5","r":"q3-178","title":"3:178 · The long life that benefits or ensnares","text":"ولمّا قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إنَّ اللهَ أطلعني على من يُؤمِنُ بي ممن يكْفُر» . قال المنافقون: نحن معه ولا يعرفنا، فأنزل الله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-178-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-178-s1","r":"q3-178","title":"The subject of yaḥsabanna","text":"I say: With the third-person reading ( بالتحتية ), “those who disbelieve” is the subject ( فاعل ), and anna with its following clause takes the place of the two required objects ( سد مسد المفعولين ). With the second-person reading ( بالفوقية ), “those who” is the first object ( مفعول أول ), while annamā takes the place of the second. Here mā is maṣdariyya ( مصدرية ). Imlāʾ ( الإملاء ) denotes granting time, deferring or giving respite, as in “Leave me for a long while” [Q 19:46]. Translator’s note: Cairo I:440 prints الإملال ( imlāl ). The translation reads الإملاء ( imlāʾ ), in accordance with the Qur’anic verb numlī and the author’s explicit gloss “granting respite and delay”; compare Lisān al-ʿArab , s.v. ملا , on amlā Allāhu lahu .","anchor":"en-q3-178-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-178-s2","r":"q3-178","title":"The danger of a respite mistaken for favour","text":"Disbelievers must not imagine that God's granting them respite and extending their lives is good for them. He gives such respite as gradual enticement ( استدراج ), so that they increase in sin and punishment. Their end is a humiliating punishment on the day believers are honoured.","anchor":"en-q3-178-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-178-s3","r":"q3-178","title":"A lifetime’s blessing is measured by realization","text":"If the servant's extended years are spent in obedience, wakefulness ( اليقظة ) and deeper gnosis, they are good. Blessing in one's life lies in divine enabling ( التوفيق ) and increase of knowledge of God. As the Ḥikam says: “One whose life is blessed can obtain in a short span of time what words cannot express and indication cannot encompass.” If life is instead spent in heedlessness, idleness and growing disobedience, death would be preferable. The Prophet is cited as saying that the best people are those whose lives are long and works good, and the worst those whose lives are long and works evil. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-178-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-178-s4","r":"q3-178","title":"","text":"When the Prophet said, “God has disclosed to me who will believe in me as distinct from those who will disbelieve,” the hypocrites said, “We are with him, yet he does not know us.” Then God revealed the following verse.","anchor":"en-q3-178-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-179","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen 3:179","anchor":"unit-q3-179"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-179-1","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"ما كانَ اللَّهُ لِيَذَرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلى ما أَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ حَتَّى يَمِيزَ الْخَبِيثَ مِنَ الطَّيِّبِ وَما كانَ اللَّهُ لِيُطْلِعَكُمْ عَلَى الْغَيْبِ وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَجْتَبِي مِنْ رُسُلِهِ مَنْ يَشاءُ فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَإِنْ تُؤْمِنُوا وَتَتَّقُوا فَلَكُمْ أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ (179)","anchor":"ar-q3-179-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-179-2","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"قلت: ماز يميز، وميّز يُمَيِّز، بمعنى واحد، لكن في ميّز معنى التكثير.","anchor":"ar-q3-179-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-179-3","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لعامة المؤمنين والمنافقين: ما كانَ اللَّهُ ليترك الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلى ما أَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ من الاختلاط، ولا يعرف مخلصكم من منافقكم، بل لا بد أن يختبركم حتى يتميز المنافق من المخلص، بالوحي أو بالتكاليف الشاقة، التي لا يصبر عليها إلا المخلصون، كبذل الأموال والأنفس في سبيل الله، ليختبر به بواطنكم، ويستدل به على عقائدكم، أو بما ظهر في غزوة أحد من الأقوال والأفعال التي تدل على الإيمان أو النفاق، وَما كانَ اللَّهُ لِيُطْلِعَكُمْ عَلَى الْغَيْبِ حتى تعرفوا ما في القلوب من كفر أو إيمان، أو تعرفوا: هل تَغْلُبون أو تُغْلَبُون. وَلكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَجْتَبِي لرسالته مَنْ يَشاءُ، فيوحي إليه ويخبره ببعض المغيبات، أو ينصب له ما يدل عليها، فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ الذي اختص بعلم الغيب الحقيقي، وآمنوا برسله الذين اختارهم لأسرار الغيوب، لا يعلمون إلا ما علَّمهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-179-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-179-4","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"رُوِيَ أن الكفرة قالوا: إن كان محمد صادقاً فليخبرنا: من يؤمن منا ومن يكفر؟ فنزلت الآية. وقيل: سببها ما تقدم من قول المنافقين، ووجه المناسبة: هو ما صَدَرَ منهم يوم أُحُد من المقالات التي ميزتهم من المؤمنين.","anchor":"ar-q3-179-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-179-5","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"وَإِنْ تُؤْمِنُوا إيماناً حقيقياً وَتَتَّقُوا النفاق والشرك فَلَكُمْ أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ عند الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-179-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-179-6","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"الإشارة: من سُنّة الله في المتوجهين إليه إذا كثروا، وظهرت فيهم دعوى القوة، أرسل الله عليهم ريح التصفية، فيثبت الصحيح، والخاوي تذروه الريح، وما كان الله ليذرهم على ما هم عليه من غير اختبار، حتى يميز الخبيث من الطيب، أي: مَنْ هِمَّتُه الله ومَنْ هِمَّتُه سواه، وما كان الله ليُطلعكم على الغيب حتى يعلموا من يثبت ممن يرجع، أو يعلموا ما يلحقهم من الجلال والجمال، وإنما ذلك خاص بالرسل عليهم السلام، وقد يُطلع على شيء من ذلك بعض خواص ورثتهم الكرام، فالواجب على المريد أن يُؤمن بالقدر المغيب، ولا يستشرف على الاطلاع عليه «استشرافُك على ما بطن فيك من العيوب، خير من استشرافك على ما حُجب عنك من الغيوب» . (وإن تؤمنوا) بمواقع القضاء والقدر، (وتتقوا) القنوط والكدر، (فلكم أجر عظيم) .","anchor":"ar-q3-179-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-179-7","r":"q3-179","title":"3:179 · Trial as disclosure: hidden sincerity and the unseen","text":"ولمّا كان البخل هو معيار المخلصين من المخلطين، ذكره بإثر تمييز المؤمنين من المنافقين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-179-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-179-s1","r":"q3-179","title":"Māza and mayyaza","text":"I say: Māza/yamīzu ( ماز يميز ) and mayyaza/yumayyizu ( ميّز يميّز ) share the sense of distinguishing, but the doubled form conveys intensity or multiplicity ( التكثير ).","anchor":"en-q3-179-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-179-s2","r":"q3-179","title":"Disclosure in action is not a grant of unrestricted foreknowledge","text":"God addresses believers and hypocrites together: He would not leave them mixed in a condition where sincere believers could not be distinguished from pretenders. He tests them until the hypocrite and sincere person become recognizable: through revelation or demands difficult enough that only the sincere persevere, such as offering property and lives in His cause. Such trials bring hidden dispositions to light and allow judgments about belief from actual deeds. The words and conduct displayed at Uḥud were just such signs. God does not disclose the unseen ( الغيب ) to all people, so that they could directly read unbelief or faith in hearts, or know in advance whether they would win or lose. He chooses whom He wills for messengership, informs them by revelation of some hidden things, or establishes indications of them. Believe in God, who alone possesses knowledge of the unseen in the true sense, and in His messengers, who learn only what He teaches them. Some unbelievers are reported to have demanded that Muḥammad name who among them would believe; another account associates the revelation with the hypocrites' challenge just mentioned. In either case the conduct at Uḥud manifested their differing conditions. If you truly believe and guard against hypocrisy and idolatry, a great reward awaits you.","anchor":"en-q3-179-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-179-s3","r":"q3-179","title":"The wind of sifting spiritual communities","text":"When the numbers of those turning to God increase and claims of spiritual strength multiply, God sends among them a wind of sifting ( ريح التصفية ): the sound person stands firm, while the empty is scattered. He does not leave them untested but distinguishes whose aspiration ( هِمّة ) is God from whose aspiration is another. The future perseverance or retreat of seekers, and the majestic ( جلال ) or beautiful ( جمال ) disclosures they will encounter, are hidden. This is reserved for the messengers; God may disclose something of it to some of their noble elect heirs. The disciple must believe in what divine decree keeps hidden instead of demanding to see it. As the Ḥikam says: “Your looking out for the defects hidden within you is better than your looking out for the unseen things withheld from you.” Faith in the workings of decree, with avoidance of despair and distress, brings the promised great reward.","anchor":"en-q3-179-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-179-s4","r":"q3-179","title":"","text":"Because miserliness is the measure distinguishing the sincere from those of mixed conduct, he mentions it immediately after distinguishing believers from hypocrites.","anchor":"en-q3-179-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-180","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self 3:180","anchor":"unit-q3-180"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-1","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"وَلا يَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ بِما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ هُوَ خَيْراً لَهُمْ بَلْ هُوَ شَرٌّ لَهُمْ سَيُطَوَّقُونَ ما بَخِلُوا بِهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ وَلِلَّهِ مِيراثُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ (180)","anchor":"ar-q3-180-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-2","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"قلت: من قرأ بالخطاب فالموصول مفعول أول، و (خيراً) : مفعول ثان، والضمير للفصل، والخطاب للرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم، ولا بد من حذف مضاف، أي: لا تحسبن بُخلَ الذين يبخلون خيراً لهم، ومن قرأ بالغيب ف- (الذين) :","anchor":"ar-q3-180-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-3","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"فاعل، والمفعول الأول محذوف، لدلالة (يبخلون) عليه، لا يحسبن البخلاء بخلهم خيراً لهم، والطوق: ما يدار بالعنق.","anchor":"ar-q3-180-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-4","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولا يظنن الَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ بِما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ من الأموال، فلم يؤدوا زكاتها، أن بخلهم خير لهم، بَلْ هُوَ شَرٌّ لَهُمْ لاستجلابه العذاب إليهم، ثم بيَّنه بقوله: سَيُطَوَّقُونَ ما بَخِلُوا بِهِ أي: يلزمون وبال ما بخلوا به إلزام الطوق للعنق، وقيل: يطوق به حقيقة، لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام:","anchor":"ar-q3-180-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-5","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"«ما من رَجُل لا يؤدي زكاة ماله إلا إذا كان يوم القيامة- مُثِّلَ له شُجَاعاً أقْرع، له زَبِيبتَان، يطوِّقُه، ثم يأخُذُ بِلْهزِمتيه- أي: شدقيه- يقول: أنا كنْزكَ، أنا مَالُكَ، ثُم تَلا هذه الآية: وَلا يَحْسَبَنَّ ... » . وقيل: يجعل يوم القيامة في أعناقهم طوقاً من نار.","anchor":"ar-q3-180-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-6","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"والمال الذي بخل به هو لله، وسيرجع لله، وَلِلَّهِ مِيراثُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ فهو الذي يرث الأرض ومن عليها، فكيف يبخل العبد بمال الله، وهو يعلم أنه يرجع لله، فيموت ويتركه لمن يسعد به! ولله درّ القائل، حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-q3-180-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-7","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"يا جَامِعَ الْمَالِ كَمْ تُضَرُّ به ... تَطْمَعُ بالله فِي الخُلُودِ معَهْ","anchor":"ar-q3-180-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-8","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"هَلْ حَمَل المالَ ميّت معه؟ ... أما تراه لِغَيْرِه جَمَعَهْ؟!","anchor":"ar-q3-180-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-9","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ لا يخفى عليه منعكم ولا إعطاؤكم، فيجازي كُلاً بعمله.","anchor":"ar-q3-180-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-10","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"الإشارة: لا يحسبن الذين يبخلون بما آتاهم الله من فضل الرئاسة والجاه، أن يبذلوها في طلب معرفة الله، وبذلها: إسقاطها وإبدالها بالخمول، والذل لله، وإسقاط المنزلة بين عباد الله، فلا يظنون أن بخلهم بذلك خير لهم، بل هو شر لهم، سيلزمون وبال ما بخلوا به يوم القيامة، حين يرون منازل المقربين كالشمس الضاحية في أعلى عليين، وهم مع عوام أهل اليمين، محجوبون عن شهود رب العالمين، إلا في وقت مخصوص وحين.","anchor":"ar-q3-180-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-180-11","r":"q3-180","title":"3:180 · Withholding wealth, reputation and the self","text":"فمن بخل بماله حشر مع الفجار، ومن بخل بنفسه وجاهه، وبذل ماله، حشر مع الأبرار، ومن بذلهما معا حشر مع المصطفين الأخيار، ومنتهى الملك لله الواحد القهار، وهو الغنى بالإطلاق. فمن وصفه بضد ذلك كان من أهل البعاد والشقاق. وإلى ذلك أشار بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-180-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-180-s1","r":"q3-180","title":"Second- and third-person readings","text":"I say: Under the second-person reading ( بالخطاب ), the relative pronoun is the first object ( مفعول أول ), khayran ( خيرًا ) the second ( مفعول ثان ), and the intervening pronoun separates them ( ضمير الفصل ); the address is to the Messenger. A possessed noun is omitted: “Do not think the miserliness of those who withhold ... is good for them.” Under the third-person reading ( بالغيب ), “those” is the subject ( فاعل ), with an understood first object indicated by “they withhold”: “Let the miserly not suppose their withholding good for them.” A ṭawq ( طوق ) is something encircling the neck.","anchor":"en-q3-180-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-180-s2","r":"q3-180","title":"Zakat, constriction and divine ownership","text":"Those who withhold the wealth God has given them and fail to pay its alms ( زكاة ) must not imagine their miserliness helps them. It draws punishment upon them. They shall be bound to the evil consequences of what they withheld, as a collar encircles a neck. Or they will literally be encircled by it: the Prophet is quoted explaining that the withholder’s wealth is represented on the Day of Resurrection as a bald venomous snake with two spots, which coils around its owner, seizes his jaws and says, “I am your hoard; I am your wealth”; then the Prophet recited the verse. Another account describes a collar of fire. All the wealth kept back belongs ultimately to God, “the inheritance of the heavens and the earth”; He survives the whole earth and those upon it. How can the servant cling to God's property, knowing he will die and leave it behind for others to enjoy? A poet asks: O gatherer of wealth, how much harm you suffer through it! By God, do you hope to remain with it forever? Did anyone dying carry wealth away? Do you not see he gathered it for another? [Translator’s note: Cairo prints bi-llāh , rendered “by God.” Its use as an oath or adjuration, and the question punctuation, are interpretive. Ibn Ḥibbān’s Rawḍat al-ʿuqalāʾ , p. 227, likewise reads bi-llāh ; al-Thaʿālibī’s Yatīmat al-dahr , V:292, has wa-llāh . These electronic primary texts also differ from Cairo in other words. The Yatīma places its version under Abū Manṣūr Naṣr b. Aḥmad b. Saʿd al-Saʿdī (entry182, V:291–292); the earlier Rawḍa introduces its version through a recitation chain ending with Mahdī b. Sābiq. These are different forms of the poem, and neither establishes the authorship of Cairo’s anonymous version or conclusively explains its bi-llāh .] God sees both what you withhold and what you give and recompenses everyone accordingly.","anchor":"en-q3-180-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-180-s3","r":"q3-180","title":"Offering social status and the burden of reputation","text":"Those who withhold the bounty of leadership, prestige and social standing ( الرئاسة والجاه ), refusing to spend it in the quest for knowledge of God, should not suppose this helps them. To spend it means to lay it aside in favour of obscurity ( الخمول ), humility before God and relinquishing rank among people. Hoarding status leads to remorse on Resurrection when they see the nearness of the elect shining like the sun in the highest stations, while they remain with ordinary people of the Right, veiled from witnessing the Lord of the Worlds except at an appointed time. Whoever withholds wealth is raised among sinners; whoever withholds self and prestige but offers wealth is raised among the righteous; whoever offers both wealth and self is raised among the chosen and elect. Dominion's final outcome belongs to the One, the Overpowering, who is absolutely free of need ( الغني بالإطلاق ). To ascribe the opposite to Him leads to estrangement and opposition, as the next verse makes clear.","anchor":"en-q3-180-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-181-183","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels 3:181–183","anchor":"unit-q3-181-183"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-1","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"لَقَدْ سَمِعَ اللَّهُ قَوْلَ الَّذِينَ قالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ فَقِيرٌ وَنَحْنُ أَغْنِياءُ سَنَكْتُبُ ما قالُوا وَقَتْلَهُمُ الْأَنْبِياءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ وَنَقُولُ ذُوقُوا عَذابَ الْحَرِيقِ (181) ذلِكَ بِما قَدَّمَتْ أَيْدِيكُمْ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ لَيْسَ بِظَلاَّمٍ لِلْعَبِيدِ (182) الَّذِينَ قالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَهِدَ إِلَيْنا أَلاَّ نُؤْمِنَ لِرَسُولٍ حَتَّى يَأْتِيَنا بِقُرْبانٍ تَأْكُلُهُ النَّارُ قُلْ قَدْ جاءَكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِنْ قَبْلِي بِالْبَيِّناتِ وَبِالَّذِي قُلْتُمْ فَلِمَ قَتَلْتُمُوهُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (183)","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-2","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"قلت: (وقتلهم) : معطوف على (ما) المفعولة أو النائبة عن الفاعل، على القراءتين رفعاً ونصباً، و (أن الله) :","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-3","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"عطف على (ما) أي: ذلك العذاب بسبب ما قدمتم وبأن الله منتفٍ عنه الظلم، فلا بد أن يعاقب المسيئ ويثيب المحسن، (الذين قالوا إِنَّ الله عهد إلينا) : صفة للذين (قالوا إِنَّ الله فَقِيرٌ) ، أو بدل منه مجرور مثله.","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-4","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لَقَدْ سَمِعَ اللَّهُ قَوْلَ اليهود الَّذِينَ قالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ فَقِيرٌ وَنَحْنُ أَغْنِياءُ وقائله: فنحاص بن عازوراء، في جماعة منهم، وذلك أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم كتب مع أبي بكر إلى يهود بنى قينقاع، يدعوهم إلى الإسلام، وإلى إقامة الصلاة وإيتاء الزكاة، وأن يقرضوا الله قرضاً حسناً، فدخل أبو بكر رضي الله عنه مِدْرَاسَهُم (١) ، فوجد خلقاً كثيراً اجتمعوا إلى فنحاص، وهو من علمائهم- ومعه حبر آخر اسمه: (أيشع) ، فقال أبو بكر لفنحاص: اتق الله وأسلم، فو الله إنك لتعلم أن محمداً رسول الله، قد جاءكم بالحق من عند الله، فأسلِمْ وصَدِّق، وأقْرِض الله قرضاً حسناً يدخلك الجنة، فقال فنحاص لعنه الله: يا أبا بكر تزعم أن ربنا يستقرضنا أموالنا، وما يستقرض إلا الفقير من الغني، ولو كان غنيّاً ما استقرض، فلطمه أبو بكر رضي الله عنه وقال: لولا ما بيننا من العهد لضربت عنقك، فشكاه إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال له: عليه الصلاة والسلام: - «ما حملك على ما فعلت؟» فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-5","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"يا رسول الله، إن عدو الله قال قولاً عظيماً، زعم أن الله فقير، وهم أغنياء، فجَحَد ما قال، فنزلت الآية تكذيبا له.","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-6","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"والمعنى: أن الله سمع مقالتهم الشنيعة، وأنه سيعاقبهم عليها، ولذلك قال: سَنَكْتُبُ ما قالُوا أي: سنسطرها عليهم في صحائف أعمالهم، أو سنحفظها في علمنا ولا نهملها، لأنها كلمة عظيمة، فيها الكفر بالله والاستهزاء بكتاب الله وتكذيب لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، ولذلك نظمت مع قتلهم الأنبياء، حيث عطفه عليه، وفيه تنبيه على أن قولهم الشنيع ليس هو أول جريمة ارتكبوها، وأن من اجترأ على قتل الأنبياء لم يستبعد أمثال هذا القول منه.","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-7","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"ثم ذكر عقابهم، فقال: وَنَقُولُ لهم يوم القيامة: ذُوقُوا عَذابَ الْحَرِيقِ أي: المُحْرِق، والذوق: يطلق على إدراك المحسوسات كالمطعومات، والمعنويات كما هنا، وذكره هنا لأن عذابهم مرتب على قولهم الناشئ عن البخل، والتهالك على المال، وغالب حاجة الإنسان إليه، لتحصيل المطاعم، ومعظم بخله للخوف من فقده.","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-8","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"ذلِكَ العذاب بسبب ما قَدَّمَتْ أَيْدِيكُمْ من قتل الأنبياء، وقولكم هذا، وسائر معاصيكم، وعبّر بالأيدي لأن غالب الأعمال بهن، وبأن اللَّهَ لَيْسَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِلْعَبِيدِ بل يجازي كلَّ عبد بما كسب من خير أو شر، فأنتم ظلمتم أنفسكم.","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-9","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"ثم إن قوماً منهم، وهو كعب بن الأشرف ومالك بن الصيف وحُيَيْ بن أخطب وفنْحَاص ووهب بن يهوذا، أتوا النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقالوا: يا محمد تزعم أن الله بعثك إلينا رسولاً، وإن الله قد عهد إلينا في التوراة، ألاَّ نؤمن لرسول يزعم أنه نبيّ حتى يأتينا بقربان تأكله النار، فإن جئتنا به صدقناك، فأنزل الله فيهم تكذيباً لهم: الَّذِينَ قالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَهِدَ إِلَيْنا في التوراة وأوصانا أَلَّا نُؤْمِنَ لِرَسُولٍ حَتَّى يَأْتِيَنا بِقُرْبانٍ كصدقة أو نسيكة، تَأْكُلُهُ النَّارُ كما كانت لأنبياء بني إسرائيل.","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-10","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"وذلك أن القرابين والغنائم كانت حراماً على بني إسرائيل، وكانوا إذا قرَّبوا قُرباناً، أو غنموا غنيمة، فتقبل منهم، ولم يُغل من الغنيمة، نزلت نار بيضاء من السماء، فتأكل ذلك القربان أو الغنيمة، فيكون ذلك علامة على القبول، وإذا لم يتقبل بقي على حاله، وهذا من تعنتهم وأباطيلهم، لأن أكل القربان لم يُوجبْ الإيمانَ إلا لكونه معجزة، وسائر المعجزات في ذلك سواء، فلذلك ردَّ عليهم بقوله: قُلْ قَدْ جاءَكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِنْ قَبْلِي بِالْبَيِّناتِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-11","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"المعجزات الواضحات، وَبِالَّذِي قُلْتُمْ من أكل النار القربان، فكذبتموهم وقتلتموهم كزكريا ويحيى وغيرهما، فَلِمَ قَتَلْتُمُوهُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في دعواكم أنه ما منعكم من الإيمان إلا عدم ظهور هذه المعجزة، فما لكم لم تؤمنوا بمن جاء بها حتى قتلتموه؟ والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-12","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"الإشارة: ما زالت خواص العامة مولعةً بالإنكار على خواص الخاصة، يسترقون السمع منهم، إذا سمعوا كلمة لم يبلغها علمُهم، وفيها ما يوجب النقص من مرتبتهم، حفظوها، وحرفوها، وأذاعوها، يريدون بذلك إطفاء نورهم،","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-13","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"وإظهار عوارهم، والله حفيظ عليهم، سيكتب ما قالوا وما قصدوا من الإنكار على أوليائه، ويقول لهم: ذوقوا عذاب البعد والحجاب. ومما يتشبثون به في الإنكار عليهم: اقتراحهم الكرامات التي كانت للأولياء قبلهم، ويقولون:","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-14","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"لانصدق بهم حتى يأتوا بما أتى به فلان وفلان، فقد كان من قبلهم يطعنون فيهم مع ظهور ذلك عليهم، كما هو سنة الله فيهم. (والله يهدي مَن يشاء إلى صراط مستقيم) .","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-181-183-15","r":"q3-181-183","title":"3:181–183 · Claims about God's poverty, rejected signs and the demand for marvels","text":"ثم سلّى الحقّ نبيه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-181-183-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-181-183-s1","r":"q3-181-183","title":"Wa-qatlahum, wa-anna Allāha and alladhīna","text":"I say: “Their killing” ( وقتلهم ) is coordinated with the object ( ما ) or what stands for the subject under the passive reading, according to the two readings in accusative and nominative. “And because God ...” ( وأن الله ) is coordinated with mā in “because of what your hands sent ahead” [3:182]: the punishment is on account of your past acts and because God is utterly removed from injustice—He necessarily recompenses the wrongdoer and the righteous. “Those who said, ‘God made a covenant ...’ ” is a modifier ( صفة ) or substitute ( بدل ) for the preceding “those who said, ‘God is poor’,” in the same genitive construction.","anchor":"en-q3-181-183-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-181-183-s2","r":"q3-181-183","title":"The taunt about a 'loan to God'","text":"God heard the words attributed to a Jewish scholar, Finḥāṣ ibn ʿĀzūrāʾ, and companions who said, “God is poor and we are rich.” According to the narrative, the Prophet sent Abū Bakr with a letter to the Jews of Banū Qaynuqāʿ, inviting them to Islam, prayer, alms and a goodly loan to God. Abū Bakr entered their study hall ( مِدْرَاس ), where many had gathered around Finḥāṣ and another scholar, Ayshaʿ. Abū Bakr said to Finḥāṣ: “Fear God and embrace Islam. By God, you know that Muḥammad is God’s Messenger and has brought you the truth from God. Embrace Islam, affirm him, and lend God a goodly loan: He will admit you to Paradise.” Finḥāṣ—God curse him—retorted that if God requested their property as a loan, He must be poor and they rich, for a rich man would not need a loan. Abū Bakr struck him and said that, were it not for their covenant, he would have struck off his head. Finḥāṣ complained to the Prophet. The Prophet asked Abū Bakr, “What prompted you to do what you did?” He replied, “Messenger of God, the enemy of God spoke an outrageous word: he claimed that God is poor and that they are rich.” Finḥāṣ denied saying it. The verse, in the report, exposed the denial.","anchor":"en-q3-181-183-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-181-183-s3","r":"q3-181-183","title":"Recording the insult and the moral argument against false claims","text":"God will write their vile utterance on their records, or preserve it in His knowledge without neglect: it contains unbelief, derision of revelation and rejection of His Messenger. It is placed alongside the killing of prophets to show that grievous crimes have preceded this one. Those who dared to kill prophets cannot be thought incapable of such utterance. On Resurrection God will tell them to taste the burning punishment. Dhawq ( الذوق , tasting) can designate apprehension of what is sensory, such as food, or of what is not literally tasted, as here. The image suits an offence issuing from miserliness and an excessive attachment to money, which people chiefly need to obtain food; most of their miserliness arises from fear of losing that money. Their punishment comes from what their hands sent ahead—prophet-killing, the blasphemous utterance and their other acts. Hands are named because most actions are carried out with them. God never wrongs servants: they have wronged themselves. A second reported deputation—Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf, Mālik ibn al-Ṣayf, Ḥuyayy ibn Akhṭab, Finḥāṣ and Wahb ibn Yahūdhā—said that their Torah required a claimant to prophecy to produce an offering devoured by heavenly fire. Such an offering might be an act of charity or a ritual sacrifice. According to the account, former Israelites were not permitted to consume sacrificial offerings or war spoils: when they presented an offering or acquired spoils, if it was accepted and none of the spoils had been misappropriated, a white fire descended from heaven and consumed that offering or those spoils as a sign of acceptance. If it was not accepted, it remained as it was. But requiring this particular marvel alone was obstinacy. Its evidential force lay simply in being a miracle ( معجزة ); other true miracles provide the same kind of proof. God therefore commanded the Messenger to reply that earlier messengers came with clear wonders including the very sign demanded , and yet were denied and killed, such as Zachariah and John: why murder them, if the absence of that sign was really the only obstacle to faith? God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-181-183-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-181-183-s4","r":"q3-181-183","title":"Concealing the station of the saints and demanding miracles","text":"Some of the outwardly accomplished among ordinary believers persist in denying the most elect ( خواص الخاصة ). They eavesdrop upon their utterances and, when they hear a saying beyond the reach of their knowledge that contains something that would diminish their standing [apparently, that of the elect], they preserve, distort and broadcast it to extinguish their light and expose their defects. God preserves the record of what they say and intend against His friends; the punishment in the allusive register is distance and veiling. One pretext for denial is demanding from present-day saints exactly the miracles attributed to earlier saints: “We shall not believe in them until they do what so-and-so did.” But earlier saints were themselves attacked even while such wonders were manifest. This is an enduring pattern. God guides whom He wills to a straight path.","anchor":"en-q3-181-183-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-181-183-s5","r":"q3-181-183","title":"","text":"God then consoled His Prophet.","anchor":"en-q3-181-183-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-184","r":"q3-184","title":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs","text":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs 3:184","anchor":"unit-q3-184"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-184-1","r":"q3-184","title":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs","text":"فَإِنْ كَذَّبُوكَ فَقَدْ كُذِّبَ رُسُلٌ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ جاؤُ بِالْبَيِّناتِ وَالزُّبُرِ وَالْكِتابِ الْمُنِيرِ (184)","anchor":"ar-q3-184-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-184-2","r":"q3-184","title":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs","text":"قلت: (الزبر) : جمع زبور، بمعنى مزبور، أي: مكتوب، من زبرت، أي: كتبت، وكل كتاب فهو زبور، وقال امرؤ القيس:","anchor":"ar-q3-184-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-184-3","r":"q3-184","title":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs","text":"لِمَنْ طَلَلٌ أبْصَرْتُهُ فَشَجَانِي ... كَخَطِّ زَبَورٍ في عَسِيبٍ يَمَانِ","anchor":"ar-q3-184-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-184-4","r":"q3-184","title":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، فى تسلية رسوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام- من تكذيب اليهود وغيرهم له: فَإِنْ كَذَّبُوكَ فليس ذلك ببدع فَقَدْ كُذِّبَتْ رُسُلٌ مثلك مِنْ قَبْلِكَ جاءوا قومهم بالمعجزات البينات، وبالكتب المنزلات، فيها مواعظ زاجرات، وَبِالْكِتابِ الْمُنِيرِ المشتمل على الأحكام الشرعيات.","anchor":"ar-q3-184-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-184-5","r":"q3-184","title":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs","text":"الإشارة: كما كُذبت الأنبياء كُذبت الأولياء، بعد أن ظهر عليهم من العلوم الباهرة والحكم الظاهرة والكرامات الواضحة، وأعظمها المعرفة، وهذه سُنَّة ماضية، ولن تجد لسنة الله تبديلا.","anchor":"ar-q3-184-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-184-6","r":"q3-184","title":"3:184 · Prophets and saints opposed despite signs","text":"وعند الله تجتمع الخصوم فيظهر المحق من المبطل، وتوفى كلُّ نفس ما أسلفتْ، وتعلم علم يقين ما أظهرت وأضمرت، كما أشار إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-184-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-184-s1","r":"q3-184","title":"Zubur (زُبُر) and mazbūr","text":"I say: Zubur ( الزُّبُر ) is the plural of zabūr , in the sense of mazbūr ( مزبور ), what has been written. It comes from zabartu , “I wrote.” Any written book can in this sense be called zabūr . Imruʾ al-Qays speaks of a ruinous dwelling: Whose traces did I see, grieving me, like script in a codex on a Yemeni palm-stalk?","anchor":"en-q3-184-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-184-s2","r":"q3-184","title":"The continuity of revelation and rejection","text":"To console the Messenger in the face of denial by Jews and others, God says that denial is not unprecedented. Messengers like him were denied before, though they came to their people with clear miracles ( البينات ), revealed scriptures ( الزبر ) containing admonitions, and an illuminating Book ( الكتاب المنير ) that conveys the rulings of the Revealed Law ( الأحكام الشرعيات ).","anchor":"en-q3-184-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-184-s3","r":"q3-184","title":"Denial as a recurrent experience of the friends of God","text":"As prophets were denied, so are God's friends ( الأولياء ) denied, even when remarkable sciences, evident wisdoms and clear gifts ( الكرامات ) appear through them, the greatest gift being knowledge of God ( المعرفة ). This is an enduring way of God which does not change. Ultimately disputants meet before Him, the truthful and false are made manifest, and everyone receives the reward or consequence of what they sent ahead, knowing for certain their public and hidden acts.","anchor":"en-q3-184-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-184-s4","r":"q3-184","title":"","text":"The next verse returns all disputants to the certainty of death.","anchor":"en-q3-184-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-185","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival 3:185","anchor":"unit-q3-185"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-1","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"كُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذائِقَةُ الْمَوْتِ وَإِنَّما تُوَفَّوْنَ أُجُورَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ فَمَنْ زُحْزِحَ عَنِ النَّارِ وَأُدْخِلَ الْجَنَّةَ فَقَدْ فازَ وَمَا الْحَياةُ الدُّنْيا إِلاَّ مَتاعُ الْغُرُورِ (185)","anchor":"ar-q3-185-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-2","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"قلت: (زحزح) : بُوعِدَ، والزحزحة: الجذب والإخراج بعجلة.","anchor":"ar-q3-185-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-3","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: كل نفس منفوسة لا بد أن تذوق حرارة الموت، وتسقى كأس المنون، وإنما توفون جزاء أعمالكم يوم القيامة، يوم قيامكم من القبور، خيراً كان أو شرًّا.","anchor":"ar-q3-185-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-4","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"قال البيضاوي: ولفظ التوفية يشعر بأنه قد يكون قبلها بعض الأجور، أي: توفية بعض الأجور، ويؤيده قوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «القَبْرُ رَوْضَةٌ مِنْ رِيَاضِ الجَنَّة، أو حُفْرة مِنْ حُفَرِ النارِ» ، فَمَنْ زُحْزِحَ أي: بُوعد عَنِ النَّارِ وَأُدْخِلَ الْجَنَّةَ فَقَدْ فازَ بالنجاة ونيل المراد، وعنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «من أحبَ أن يُزحزَحَ عن النارِ ويُدْخَل الجَنَةَ فَلتُدرِكْهُ مَنِيَّتُهُ وهو يُؤمنُ باللهِ واليَومِ الآخِرِ، ويَأتِي إلى النَاسِ ما يُحِبُّ أن يُؤْتى إِليْه» .","anchor":"ar-q3-185-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-5","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"وَمَا الْحَياةُ الدُّنْيا وزخارفها ولذاتها إِلَّا مَتاعُ الْغُرُورِ فإن الغار- وهو المُدلِّس- يظهر ما هو حسن من متاعه، ويخفي ما هو معيب، كذلك الدنيا تبتهج لطالبها، وتُظهر له حلاوتها وشهواتها، حتى تشغله عن ذكر الله وعن طاعته، فيؤثرها على آخرته، ثم يتركها أحوج ما يكون إليها، فينقلبُ نادماً متحسراً، وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-185-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-6","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"ومَنْ يحمد الدنيا لشيء يسره ... فسوف للعُسْرِ عن قَرِيبٍ يَلُومُها","anchor":"ar-q3-185-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-7","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"إذا أدبرت كانتْ على المرء حسرةً ... وإن أقبلتْ كانت كثيراً هُمُومُها","anchor":"ar-q3-185-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-8","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"الإشارة: النفس، من حيث هي، كلها تقبل الموت لمن قتلها وجاهدها، وإنما وقع التفريط من أربابها، فمن زحزحها عن نار الشهوات، وقتلها بسيوف المخالفات، حتى أدخلها جنات الحضرات، فقد فاز فوزاً عظيماً، وربح ربحاً كريما. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-185-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-185-9","r":"q3-185","title":"3:185 · Every self tastes death, and the contrast between the world and arrival","text":"ثم أمر بالصبر على فقد الأموال والإخوان، وعلى أذى اليهود والمشركين، فقال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-185-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-185-s1","r":"q3-185","title":"Zaḥzaḥa (زحزح) as removal from danger","text":"I say: Zaḥzaḥa ( زحزح ) means to remove or distance. Zaḥzaḥa ( الزحزحة ) also denotes drawing something out or away swiftly.","anchor":"en-q3-185-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-185-s2","r":"q3-185","title":"Full recompense, deception and escape","text":"Every living self must taste the heat of death and drink its cup. On the day people rise from their graves they receive the full requital of their deeds, good or evil. Al-Bayḍāwī observes that “paid in full” ( التوفية ) suggests that some payment may precede the final completion, and cites the saying that the grave may be a garden from Paradise's gardens or a pit from the Fire's pits. Whoever is drawn away from the Fire and enters Paradise has attained deliverance and the hoped-for goal. The Prophet is cited as saying that whoever would be spared the Fire and enter Paradise should meet death believing in God and the Last Day and treating others as he would wish to be treated. Worldly adornments and pleasures are only matāʿ al-ghurūr ( متاع الغرور ), the wares of deception. A deceitful seller displays whatever is attractive and hides defects. So the world presents sweetness and desire to its seeker until it distracts him from remembering and obeying God, so that he prefers it to the Hereafter; then he leaves it when he is most in need of it, and departs remorseful and sorrowing. The poet says: Whoever praises the world for something that delights him will soon condemn her when hardship comes. When she withdraws she leaves sorrow behind; when she approaches her many cares remain.","anchor":"en-q3-185-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-185-s3","r":"q3-185","title":"The death of appetite and entry into the gardens of Presence","text":"The lower self ( النفس ), considered as such, can indeed die when a seeker struggles against and overcomes it; failure lies with those responsible for its cultivation. Whoever draws it back from the fire of lusts ( نار الشهوات ), kills it with the swords of contrary discipline ( سيوف المخالفات ), and brings it into the gardens of divine Presences ( جنات الحضرات ) attains a great victory and noble profit. Success is through God.","anchor":"en-q3-185-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-185-s4","r":"q3-185","title":"","text":"God next enjoins patience at the loss of property and brethren, and at harm from the Jews and the polytheists.","anchor":"en-q3-185-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-186","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance 3:186","anchor":"unit-q3-186"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-186-1","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"لَتُبْلَوُنَّ فِي أَمْوالِكُمْ وَأَنْفُسِكُمْ وَلَتَسْمَعُنَّ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَمِنَ الَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا أَذىً كَثِيراً وَإِنْ تَصْبِرُوا وَتَتَّقُوا فَإِنَّ ذلِكَ مِنْ عَزْمِ الْأُمُورِ (186)","anchor":"ar-q3-186-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-186-2","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"قلت: أصل (تبلونَّ) : تُبلوون كتُنصرون، ثم قلبت الواو ألفاً، ثم حذفت لالتقاء الساكنين، فصار تبلون، ثم أكد بالنون، فاجتمع ثلاث نونات، حذفت نون الرفع فالتقى ساكنان الواو ونون التوكيد، فحركت الواو بالضمة المجانسة، وهى النائبة عن الفاعل.","anchor":"ar-q3-186-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-186-3","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: والله لَتُبْلَوُنَّ أي: لتختبرن فِي أَمْوالِكُمْ بما يصيبها من الآفات، وما كُلفتم به من النفقات، وَأَنْفُسِكُمْ بالقتل والجراحات، والأسر والأمراض وسائر العاهات. وَلَتَسْمَعُنَّ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا","anchor":"ar-q3-186-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-186-4","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"الْكِتابَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ","anchor":"ar-q3-186-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-186-5","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"اليهود وَمِنَ الَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا كفار مكة، أَذىً كَثِيراً كقولهم: إن الله فقير، وهجاء الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، والطعن في الدين، وإغراء الكفرة على المسلمين، أو غير ذلك من الأذى. أعْلَمهم بذلك قبل وقوعه، ليتأهبوا للصبر والاحتمال، حتى لا يروعَهم نزولها حين الإنزال. وَإِنْ تَصْبِرُوا على ذلك، وَتَتَّقُوا اللهَ فيما أمركم به، فَإِنَّ ذلِكَ مِنْ عَزْمِ الْأُمُورِ أي: من معزومات الأمور التي يجب العزم عليها، أو مما عزم الله على فعلها، وأوْجَبه على عباده. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-186-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-186-6","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"الإشارة: كل مَنْ دخل في طريق الخصوص بالصدق والعزم على الوصول، لا بد أن يُبتلى ويختبر في ماله ونفسه، ليظهر صدقه في طلبه، ولا بد أن يسمع من الناس أذى كثيراً، فإن صبر ظفر، وإن رجع خسر، وهذه سنة الله في عباده: وَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ حَتَّى نَعْلَمَ الْمُجاهِدِينَ مِنْكُمْ وَالصَّابِرِينَ وَنَبْلُوَا أَخْبارَكُمْ، قال الورتجبي: (لتبلون في أموالكم) بجمعها ومنعها والتقصير في حقوق الله فيها، (وأنفسكم) باتباع شهواتها، وترك رياضتها، وملازمتها أسباب الدنيا، وخلوها من النظر في أمر المعاد، وقيل: (لتبلون في أموالكم) بالاشتغال بها أخذاً وإعطاء. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-186-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-186-7","r":"q3-186","title":"3:186 · Trial in wealth and persons, harm from others, and the discipline of endurance","text":"ثم عاتب الحقّ تعالى اليهود، ووبّخهم على كتمان الحق وإظهار الباطل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-186-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-186-s1","r":"q3-186","title":"The reinforced passive tub-lawunna (تُبْلَوُنَّ)","text":"I say: The underlying form of tublawunna ( تُبْلَوُنَّ ) was tublawūna ( تُبْلَوُونَ ), like tunṣarūna ( تنصرون ). The wāw was changed into an alif, then elided to avoid two adjacent consonants without vowels ( التقاء الساكنين ), yielding tublawna . The emphatic nūn ( نون التوكيد ) was added, producing three nūns; the indicative nūn of the plural ( نون الرفع ) was deleted, and the remaining wāw received a ḍamma to separate the two vowelless sounds, as the consonant marking the passive plural subject ( النائبة عن الفاعل ). The analysis retains Ibn ʿAjība’s sequence of morphological operations.","anchor":"en-q3-186-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-186-s2","r":"q3-186","title":"The kinds of hardship and forewarning as preparation","text":"God swears that believers will be tried in wealth through disasters and through obligatory expenditure, and in their persons through being killed, wounds, capture, illness and other afflictions. They will hear many hurtful things from Jews, who received Scripture, and from the Meccan idolaters: the allegation that God is poor, attacks on the Prophet, criticism of the religion, incitement of unbelievers against the Muslims and other injuries. God tells them before the trials arrive so they can prepare for patience and endurance rather than being bewildered when hardship strikes. If they persevere and remain mindful of His commands, that is among matters on which resolve must be fixed ( عزم الأمور ), or what God has definitively ordained for His servants. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-186-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-186-s3","r":"q3-186","title":"The testing of the sincere entrant to the particular path","text":"Anyone who enters the path of the elect ( طريق الخصوص ) with sincerity and firm intention to arrive must be tested in wealth and self so that his sincerity becomes evident; he must also hear much injury from people. If he perseveres, he prevails; if he turns back, he loses. The Qurʾān says that believers are tried until those who strive and endure are manifested [Q 47:31]. Al-Wartajbī says that wealth is a test through acquiring it, withholding it or neglecting God's rights in it; the self is tested by obeying desires, leaving its discipline, preoccupation with worldly means and forgetting the Return. Another account holds that wealth tests one by continual occupation with receiving and disbursing it.","anchor":"en-q3-186-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-186-s4","r":"q3-186","title":"","text":"God then reproaches the concealment of truth and presentation of falsehood.","anchor":"en-q3-186-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-187","r":"q3-187","title":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank","text":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank 3:187","anchor":"unit-q3-187"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-187-1","r":"q3-187","title":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank","text":"وَإِذْ أَخَذَ اللَّهُ مِيثاقَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ لَتُبَيِّنُنَّهُ لِلنَّاسِ وَلا تَكْتُمُونَهُ فَنَبَذُوهُ وَراءَ ظُهُورِهِمْ وَاشْتَرَوْا بِهِ ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً فَبِئْسَ ما يَشْتَرُونَ (187)","anchor":"ar-q3-187-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-187-2","r":"q3-187","title":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank","text":"قلت: الضمير في (نبذوه) : يعود على الكتاب، أو الميثاق.","anchor":"ar-q3-187-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-187-3","r":"q3-187","title":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاذكر إِذْ أَخَذَ اللَّهُ مِيثاقَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ وهم اليهود، أخذ عليهم العهد ليبينن للناس ما في كتابهم من صفة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ولا يكتمونه، فنبذوا ذلك العهد أو الكتاب وَراءَ ظُهُورِهِمْ فكتموا صفته- عليه الصلاة والسلام- خوفاً من زوال رئاستهم، وَاشْتَرَوْا بذلك العهد، أي: استبدلوا به ثَمَناً قَلِيلًا من حطام الدنيا، وما كانوا يأخذونه من سفلتهم، فَبِئْسَ ما يَشْتَرُونَ، وهي تَجُر ذيلها على مَن كتم علماً سئل عنه، قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «مَنْ كَتَمَ عِلْماً عَنْ أَهْله ألجِمَ بلِجَامٍ مِنْ نار» . وعن على رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q3-187-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-187-4","r":"q3-187","title":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank","text":"(ما أخذ الله على أهل الجهل أن يتعلموا حتى أخذ على أهل العلم أن يُعلِّموا) . وقال محمد بن كعب: (لا يحل للعالم أن يسكت على علمه، ولا الجاهل أن يسكت على جهله) .","anchor":"ar-q3-187-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-187-5","r":"q3-187","title":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank","text":"الإشارة: أهل العلم إذا تحققوا بوجود الخصوصية عند ولي، وكتموا ذلك حسداً وخوفاً على زوال رئاستهم، دخلوا في وعيد الآية لأنَّ العوام تابعون لهم، فإذا كتموا أو أنكروا تبعُوهم على ذلك، فيحملون أَثْقَالَهُمْ وَأَثْقَالاً مَّعَ أَثْقَالِهِمْ، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-187-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-187-6","r":"q3-187","title":"3:187 · The scholar’s duty to disclose knowledge and the danger of rank","text":"ولما سأل- عليه الصلاة والسلام- اليهود عن شىء فى التوراة، وكتموه وأخبروه بغيره، فخرجوا وقد أروه أنهم أخبروه عما سألهم، واستحمدوا إليه ففرحوا، أنزل الله فيهم:","anchor":"ar-q3-187-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-187-s1","r":"q3-187","title":"The object of nabadhūhu (نَبَذُوهُ)","text":"I say: The pronoun in “they cast it away” ( نبذوه ) refers either to the Book ( الكتاب ) or to the covenant ( الميثاق ).","anchor":"en-q3-187-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-187-s2","r":"q3-187","title":"Learning obliges teaching","text":"Remember when God took a covenant from those given Scripture—here Ibn ʿAjība names the Jews—to explain to people what their Book said about the Prophet and not conceal it. They put the covenant or the Book behind their backs, concealing his description out of fear that their leadership might disappear. They exchanged their trust for a paltry price of perishable worldly gain and the offerings collected from those beneath them. How evil that exchange! The warning extends to anyone who conceals knowledge when asked by those entitled to receive it. The Prophet is quoted: “Whoever withholds knowledge from those entitled to it will be bridled with a bridle of fire.” ʿAlī says: “God did not command the ignorant to learn before commanding the learned to teach.” Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb declares that a scholar must not be silent about knowledge, nor an ignorant person silent about his ignorance.","anchor":"en-q3-187-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-187-s3","r":"q3-187","title":"When scholars conceal recognition of spiritual excellence","text":"When scholars recognize a saint's particular realization ( الخصوصية ), yet conceal it out of envy and fear for their leadership, they fall under the warning. Ordinary people follow them; when they conceal or deny it, followers imitate them in that. Thus they carry their own burdens along with additional burdens caused by leading others astray [cf. Q 29:13]. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-187-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-187-s4","r":"q3-187","title":"","text":"When the Prophet asked the Jews about something in the Torah, they concealed it and told him something else. They departed having made him think that they had answered his question, sought his praise and rejoiced; God then revealed the next verse concerning them.","anchor":"en-q3-187-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-188-189","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude 3:188–189","anchor":"unit-q3-188-189"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-188-189-1","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"لا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ يَفْرَحُونَ بِما أَتَوْا وَيُحِبُّونَ أَنْ يُحْمَدُوا بِما لَمْ يَفْعَلُوا فَلا تَحْسَبَنَّهُمْ بِمَفازَةٍ مِنَ الْعَذابِ وَلَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ (188) وَلِلَّهِ مُلْكُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَاللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (189)","anchor":"ar-q3-188-189-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-188-189-2","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"قلت: من قرأ بالخطاب، فالذين: مفعول أول، والثاني: محذوف، أي: بمفازة من العذاب، أو هو المذكور، و (تحسبنهم) : تأكيد للفعل الأول، ومن قرأ بالغيب فالذين: فاعل، والمفعولان: محذوفان، دلَّ عليهما ذكرُهما مع الثاني، أي: لا يحسبوا أنفسهم فائزة. (فلا تحسبنهم) : من قرأ بفتح التاء فالخطاب للرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، والفعل مبني، ومن قرأ بالياء فالخطاب للذين يفرحون، والفعل معرب، أي: لا يحسبوا أنفسهم بمفازة من العذاب. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-188-189-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-188-189-3","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لا تَحْسَبَنَّ يا محمد الَّذِينَ يَفْرَحُونَ بِما أَتَوْا أي: بما فعلوا من التدليس وكتمان الحق، وَيُحِبُّونَ أَنْ يُحْمَدُوا بِما لَمْ يَفْعَلُوا من الوفاء بالعهد، وإظهار الحق، والإخبار بالصدق، أنهم فائزون من العذاب، فلا تظنهم بِمَفازَةٍ مِنَ الْعَذابِ، بل لَهُمْ عَذابٌ أَلِيمٌ موجع، وَلِلَّهِ مُلْكُ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ إن شاء عذب وإن شاء رحم، وَاللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ فلا يعجزه من ذلك شيء، أو: لا يظن الذين يفرحون بما أتَوا، ويحبون أن يحمدوا بما لم يفعلوا، فلا يحسبون أنفسهم بمفازة من العذاب.","anchor":"ar-q3-188-189-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-188-189-4","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"وعن أبي سعيد الخدري رضي الله عنه: (أنها نزلت في المنافقين، كانوا إذا خرج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم (١) تخلَّفوا، وإذا قدم اعتذروا، فإذا قَبِل عذرهم فرحوا، وأحبُّوا أن يُحمدوا بما لم يفعلوا) . وما تقدم في التوطئة هو عن ابن عباس. وقال","anchor":"ar-q3-188-189-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-188-189-5","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"ابن حجر: ولا مانع من أن تتناول الآية كلَّ من أتى بحسنة وفَرِحَ بها فَرَحَ إعجاب، وأحب أن يحمده الناس ويثنوا عليه بما ليس فيه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-188-189-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-188-189-6","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"الإشارة: لا يظن أهل الفرق الذين يسندون الأفعال إلى أنفسهم، غائبين عن فعل ربهم، ويحبون أن يحمدهم الناس ويمدحهم بفعل غيرهم، أنهم فائزون عن عذاب الفرق، وحجاب العجب، إذ لا فاعل سوى الحق، فمن تمام نعمته عليك أن خلق فيك ونسب إليك، فإن فرح العبد بالطاعة من حيث ظهورها عليه، وهي عنوان العناية- ورأى نفسه فيها كالآلة، معزولاً عن فعلها، محمولاً بالقدرة الأزلية فيها، فلا بأس عليه، ويزيد بذلك تواضعاً وشكراً، وإن فرح بها من حيث صدورها منه، ويتبجح بها على عباد الله، فهو عين العجب، وفي الحكم: «لا تُفرحكَ الطاعة من حيث إنها صَدَرَتْ منك، وافرح بها من حيث إنها هدية من الله عليك قُلْ بِفَضْلِ اللَّهِ وَبِرَحْمَتِهِ فَبِذلِكَ فَلْيَفْرَحُوا» .","anchor":"ar-q3-188-189-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-188-189-7","r":"q3-188-189","title":"3:188–189 · Joy in self-praise, divine agency and the moral quality of gratitude","text":"ثم استدل على قدرته المفهومة من (القدير) ، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-188-189-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-188-189-s1","r":"q3-188-189","title":"The possible constructions of taḥsabanna","text":"I say: In the second-person reading ( بالخطاب ), “those who” is the first object ( مفعول أول ), and the second is omitted—“safe from punishment”—or supplied by the next clause, “do not suppose them ...,” which then reinforces the first verb. Under the third-person reading ( بالغيب ), “those who” is subject ( فاعل ) and both objects are omitted but recoverable from the repeated construction: they are not to suppose themselves saved. With fatḥa on tāʾ in fa-lā taḥsabannahum , the address is to the Messenger and the form is understood as fixed; with yāʾ , the construction concerns those who rejoice, and the verb is inflected: they must not suppose themselves safe from punishment.","anchor":"en-q3-188-189-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-188-189-s2","r":"q3-188-189","title":"Misrepresentation and undeserved praise","text":"The Prophet is told not to suppose secure from punishment those who rejoice at what they have done in concealing and falsifying the truth, while longing to be praised as if they had fulfilled the covenant, made truth plain and conveyed it honestly. They will not escape painful punishment. The entire dominion of heaven and earth belongs to God, who may punish or pardon as He wills and whose power nothing can frustrate. Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī is quoted as relating the verse to hypocrites who stayed behind when the Prophet departed, then offered excuses on his return, rejoicing when accepted and craving praise for deeds they never performed. The earlier account concerning concealment is traced to Ibn ʿAbbās. Ibn Ḥajar observes that the warning can encompass anyone who does a good deed and exults in it through self-admiration while seeking praise for qualities not possessed. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-188-189-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-188-189-s3","r":"q3-188-189","title":"Rejoicing in grace rather than claiming authorship of works","text":"People confined to separation ( أهل الفرق ) attribute deeds to their own selves, forgetting the Real's activity, and seek praise for what belongs to another Agent. They have not escaped the pain of separation or the veil of self-admiration ( حجاب العجب ): there is no agent save the Real. God's favour is complete in that He creates action within you and attributes it to you. There is no harm in joy at obedience insofar as it appears in the servant as a sign of divine solicitude ( عنوان العناية ), while the servant sees himself as an instrument ( آلة ), borne along by pre-eternal power, and sees himself removed from performing it. Such joy increases humility and gratitude. But delight in action as proceeding from oneself, coupled with boasting over others, is self-admiration itself. As the Ḥikam says: “Do not rejoice in obedience because it issued from you; rejoice because it came to you as a gift from God: ‘Say: in the bounty of God and His mercy, in that let them rejoice’ ” [Q 10:58].","anchor":"en-q3-188-189-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-188-189-s4","r":"q3-188-189","title":"","text":"He then points to the signs of the Power disclosed by the final description “powerful over all things.”","anchor":"en-q3-188-189-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-190","r":"q3-190","title":"3:190 · The signs of created change and the unity disclosed through opposites","text":"3:190 · The signs of created change and the unity disclosed through opposites 3:190","anchor":"unit-q3-190"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-190-1","r":"q3-190","title":"3:190 · The signs of created change and the unity disclosed through opposites","text":"إِنَّ فِي خَلْقِ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَاخْتِلافِ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهارِ لَآياتٍ لِأُولِي الْأَلْبابِ (190)","anchor":"ar-q3-190-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-190-2","r":"q3-190","title":"3:190 · The signs of created change and the unity disclosed through opposites","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ فِي خَلْقِ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وإظهارهما للعيان، لَدلائل واضحة على وجود الصانع، وكمال قدرته، وعلمه، لذوي العقول الكاملة الصافية، الخالصة من شوائب الحس والوهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-190-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-190-3","r":"q3-190","title":"3:190 · The signs of created change and the unity disclosed through opposites","text":"قال البيضاوي: ولعل الاقتصار على هذه الثلاثة في هذه الآية لأن مناط الاستدلال هو التغير، وهذه متعرضة لجملة أنواعه، فإنه- أي التغير- إما أن يكون في ذات الشيء، كتغير الليل والنهار، أو جزئه، كتغير الناميات بتبدل صورها، أو لخارج عنها، كتغير الأفلاك بتبدل أوضاعها، وعن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «وَيْلٌ لمن قَرَأَهَا ولَمْ يَتَفَكَرْ فِيْهَا» .","anchor":"ar-q3-190-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-190-4","r":"q3-190","title":"3:190 · The signs of created change and the unity disclosed through opposites","text":"الإشارة: الخلق هو الاختراع والإظهار، فإظهار هذه التجليات الأربعة يدل على أن الحق- تعالى- تجلى لعباده بين الضدين، بين النور والظلمة، بين القدرة والحكمة، بين الحس والمعنى، وهكذا خلق من كل زوجين اثنين، ليقع الفرار من إثنينية حسهما إلى فردية معناهما، ففرّوا إلى الله، فالسموات والنهار نورانيان، والأرض والليل ظلمانيان، ففي ذلك دلالة على وحدة المعاني، فلا تقف مع الأواني، وخُض بحر المعاني، لعلك تراني. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-190-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-190-5","r":"q3-190","title":"3:190 · The signs of created change and the unity disclosed through opposites","text":"ثم وصف أولى الألباب الذين يدركون صفاء هذه المعاني، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-190-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-190-s1","r":"q3-190","title":"From change to divine agency","text":"In the creation and manifestation of the heavens and earth are evident signs of the Creator's existence and the perfection of His power and knowledge, discernible by complete and purified intellects ( أولو الألباب ), freed from the impurities of sense ( الحس ) and imagination or estimation ( الوهم ). Al-Bayḍāwī suggests that the verse may be limited to these three because change itself supplies the basis of inference ( مناط الاستدلال ): alteration may occur in a thing's own state, like night and day; in its parts, like growing beings whose forms develop; or through something external to it, like celestial spheres changing their positions. The Prophet is quoted as warning: “Woe to one who recites this and does not reflect upon it.”","anchor":"en-q3-190-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-190-s2","r":"q3-190","title":"Power and Wisdom; the sensory vessel and its meaning","text":"Creation ( الخلق ) is origination ( الاختراع ) and manifestation ( الإظهار ). The four manifestations here—heaven, earth, night and day—show that the Real discloses Himself to servants through pairs of apparent contraries: light and darkness, Power and Wisdom ( القدرة والحكمة ), sense and meaning ( الحس والمعنى ). He creates pairs so that people may flee from the apparent twoness of their sensory appearance ( إثنينية حسهما ) to the singularity of their meaning ( فردية معناهما ): “Flee, therefore, to God” [Q 51:50]. The heavens and daytime are luminous, earth and night dark, yet their unity of meaning points beyond their differing forms. Do not stop at the vessels ( الأواني ): enter the sea of meanings ( بحر المعاني ) so that, perhaps, you may behold Me. Success comes from God.","anchor":"en-q3-190-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-190-s3","r":"q3-190","title":"","text":"God describes the people of understanding who can grasp these purified meanings.","anchor":"en-q3-190-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-191-194","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing 3:191–194","anchor":"unit-q3-191-194"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-1","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"الَّذِينَ يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ قِياماً وَقُعُوداً وَعَلى جُنُوبِهِمْ وَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِي خَلْقِ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ رَبَّنا ما خَلَقْتَ هذا باطِلاً سُبْحانَكَ فَقِنا عَذابَ النَّارِ (191) رَبَّنا إِنَّكَ مَنْ تُدْخِلِ النَّارَ فَقَدْ أَخْزَيْتَهُ وَما لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنْصارٍ (192) رَبَّنا إِنَّنا سَمِعْنا مُنادِياً يُنادِي لِلْإِيمانِ أَنْ آمِنُوا بِرَبِّكُمْ فَآمَنَّا رَبَّنا فَاغْفِرْ لَنا ذُنُوبَنا وَكَفِّرْ عَنَّا سَيِّئاتِنا وَتَوَفَّنا مَعَ الْأَبْرارِ (193) رَبَّنا وَآتِنا مَا وَعَدْتَنا عَلى رُسُلِكَ وَلا تُخْزِنا يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ إِنَّكَ لا تُخْلِفُ الْمِيعادَ (194)","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-2","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله، في وصف أولي الألباب: هم الَّذِينَ يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ قِياماً وَقُعُوداً وَعَلى جُنُوبِهِمْ، أي: يذكرونه على الدوام، قائمين وقاعدين ومضطجعين، وعنه- صلّى الله عليه وسلم-: «منْ أرادَ أن يَرْتَع في رِيَاضِ الجَنة فليُكثْر ذِكرَ الله» . وقيل: يُصلّون على الهيئات الثلاث، حسب الطاقة لقوله عليه الصلاة والسلام لعمران بن حصين، وكان مريضاً: «صَلِّ قائِماً، فإِنْ لم تستطع فقاعدا، فإن لَمْ تَستطِعْ فعلى جَنْبِكَ وتومىء إيماء» .","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-3","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"وَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِي خَلْقِ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ استدلالاً واعتباراً، وهو أفضل العبادات قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «لا عبادة كالتفكر» لأنه المخصوص بالقلب، والمقصود من الخلق، وعنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «بينَمَا رجلٌ مُسْتَلقٍ على فِرَاشهِ فَنَظَر إلى السماءِ والنُجومِ، فَقَال: أشْهدُ أن لك خالقا، اللُهمَّ اغفرْ لي، فَنَظَر اللهُ إِليه فَغَفر لَهْ» . وهذا دليل واضح على شرف علم الأصول وفضل أهله. قاله البيضاوي. وسيأتي مزيد من كلام على التفكر في الإشارة إن شاء الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-4","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"فلما تفكروا في عجائب المصنوعات، قالوا: رَبَّنا ما خَلَقْتَ هذا باطِلًا أي: عبثاً من غير حكمة، بل خلقته لحكمة بديعة، من جملتها: أن يكون مبدأ لوجود الإنسان، وسبباً لمعاشه، ودليلاً يدله على معرفتك ويحثه على طاعتك، لينال الحياة الأبدية، والسعادة السرمدية في جوارك، سُبْحانَكَ تنزيهاً لك من العبث وخلق الباطل، فَقِنا عَذابَ النَّارِ التي استحقها من أعرض عن النظر والاعتبار، وأخلّ بما يقتضيه من أحكام الواحد القهار، وَما لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنْصارٍ يمنعونهم من دخول النار. ووضع المظهر موضع المضمر للدلالة على أن ظلمهم سبب لإدخالهم النار، وانقطاع النصرة عنهم في دار البوار.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-5","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"رَبَّنا إِنَّنا سَمِعْنا مُنادِياً يُنادِي لِلْإِيمانِ، وهو الرسول العظيم الشأن، أو القرآن قائلا: أَنْ آمِنُوا بِرَبِّكُمْ ووحدوه، فأجبنا نداءه وآمنا، رَبَّنا فَاغْفِرْ لَنا ذُنُوبَنا الكبائر، وَكَفِّرْ عَنَّا سَيِّئاتِنا الصغائر، وَتَوَفَّنا مَعَ الْأَبْرارِ المصطفين الأخيار، مخصوصين بصحبتهم، معدودين في زمرتهم، وفيه تنبيه على أنهم يُحبون لقاء الله فأحب الله لقاءهم. هـ. رَبَّنا وَآتِنا مَا وَعَدْتَنا عَلى تصديق رُسُلِكَ من الثواب، أو على ألسنة","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-6","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"رسلك من الفضل والرحمة وحسن المآب، سألوا ما وُعدوا على الامتثال، لا خوفا من إخلاف الوعد، بل مخافة ألاَّ يكونوا موعودين لسوء عاقبة، أو قصور في الامتثال، أو تعبداً، أو استكانة. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-7","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"وَلا تُخْزِنا يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ أي: لا تُهِنَّا بسبب تقصيرنا، إِنَّكَ لا تُخْلِفُ الْمِيعادَ بإثابة المؤمن وإجابة الداعي، أو ميعاد البعث والحساب، وتكرير رَبَّنا للمبالغة في الابتهال، والدلالة على استقلال المطالب وعلو شأنها، ففي بعض الآثار: (من حزبه أمر فقال خمس مرات: «ربنا» ، أنجاه الله مما يخاف) (١) . قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-8","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"الإشارة: قدَّم الحق الذكر على الفكر على ترتيب السير، فإن المريد يُؤمَر أول أَمرِهِ بذكر اللسان، حتى يفضي إلى الجنان، فينتقل الذكر إلى القلب، ثم إلى الروح، وهو الفكر، ثم إلى السر، وهو الشهود والعيان، وهنا يخرس اللسان، ويغيب الإنسان في أنوار العيان، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-9","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"مَا إِنْ ذَكَرْتُكِ إلاّ هَمَّ يَلْعَنُنِي ... سِرِّي ورُوحِي وقَلْبي عِنْدَ ذِكرَاكَ","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-10","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"حَتَّى كَأَنَّ رَقيباً مِنْكَ يَهْتِفُ بِي: ... إِيَّاكَ: وَيْحَك والتَّذْكَارَ! إِيَّاكَ!","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-11","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"أَمَا تَرَى الْحقَّ قَدْ لاَحَتْ شَوَاهِدُهُ ... وَوَاصَلَ الْكُلُّ مِنْ مَعْنَاهُ مَعْنَاكَ","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-12","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"فإذا بلغ العبد هذا المقام- الذي هو مقام الإفراد- اتحدت عنده الأوراد، وصار ورداً واحداً، وهو عكوف القلب في الحضرة بين فكرة ونظرة، أو إفراد القلب بالله، وتغيبه عما سواه.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-13","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"قال في الإحياء في كتاب الأوراد: الموحد المستغرق الهم بالواحد الصمد، الذي أصبح وهمومه هم واحد، فلا يحب إلا الله، ولا يخاف إلا منه، ولا يتوقع الرزق من غيره، ولا ينظر في شيء إلا يرى الله فيه، فمن ارتفعت رتبته إلى هذه الدرجة، لم يفتقر إلى ترتيب الأوراد واختلافها، بل ورده بعد المكتوبات ورد واحد، وهو حضور القلب مع الله في كل حال، فلا يخطر بقلبه أمر، ولا يقرع سمعه قارع، ولا يلوح لنظره لائح، إلاَّ كان له فيه عبرة وفكرة ومزيد، فلا محرك ولا مسكن إلا الله. فهؤلاء جميع أحوالهم تصلح أن تكون سبباً لازديادهم، فلا تتميز عندهم عبادة عن عبادة، وهم الذين فرّوا إلى الله كما قال تعالى: فَفِرُّوا إِلَى اللَّهِ، وتحقق فيهم قوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-14","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"إِنِّي ذاهِبٌ إِلى رَبِّي، وهذه الدرجة منتهى درجة الصديقين، ولا ينبغي أن يغتر المريد بما يسمعه من ذلك، فيدعيه لنفسه، ويفتر عن وظائف عباداته، فذلك علامته ألا يحس في قلبه وسواساً، ولا يخطر بقلبه معصية، لا يزعجه هواجم الأحوال، ولا يستفزه عظائم الأشغال، وأنى تكون هذه المرتبة!. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-15","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"قلت: قوله: [لا يخطر بقلبه معصية] غير لازم لأن قلب العارف مرسى للتجليات النورانية والظلمانية، لكنها تقل ولا تسكن.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-16","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"وقال في موضع آخر: وأما عبادة ذوي الألباب فلا تجاوز ذكر الله تعالى والفكر فيه حُبّاً لجلاله وجماله، وسائر الأعمال تكون مؤكدات. قال: والعامل لأجر الجنة درجته درجة البُلْه، وإنه لينالها بعمله إذ أكثر أهل الجنة البُلْه. هـ. وقال في كتاب كيمياء السعادة: وقد غلط من ظن أن وظائف الضعفاء كوظائف الأقوياء، حتى قال بعض مشايخ الصوفية: من رآني في الابتداء، قال: صار صديقاً، ومن رآني في الانتهاء، قال: صار زنديقاً، يعني أن الابتداء يقتضي المجاهدة الظاهرة للأعين بكثرة العبادات، وفي الانتهاء يرجع العمل إلى الباطن، فيبقى القلب على الدوام في عين الشهود والحضور، وتفتر ظواهر الأعضاء، فيظن أن ذلك تهاون بالعبادة (١) ، وهيهات هيهات!!، فذلك استغراق لمخ العبادات ولبابها وغايتها، ولكن أعين الخفافيش تكل عن درك نور الشمس. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-17","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"قال شيخ شيوخنا- سيدي عبد الرحمن العارف- بعد نقل كلام القشيري في هذا المعنى: وما أشار إليه ظاهر في أن أهل القلوب لا يتعاطون كل طاعة. وإنما يتعاطون من الطاعات ما يجمعهم ولا يفرقهم. ولذلك قال الجنيد:","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-18","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"أحب للصوفي ألا يقرأ ولا يكتب لأنه أجمع لهمه، قال: وأحب للمريد ألا يشتغل بالتكسب وطلب الحديث لئلا يتغير حاله. هـ. قلت: ومن رزقه الله شيخ التربية فما عيَّنه له فهو عين ذكره، يسير به كيفما كان.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-19","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"هذا ما يتعلق بحال الذكر الذي قدَّمه الله تعالى، وأما التفكر فهو أعظم العبادات وأفضل القربات، هو عبادة العارفين ومنتهى المقربين. وفي الخبر: «تفكرُ سَاعةٍ أفضل من عبادة سبعين سنة» .","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-20","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"وقال الجنيد رضي الله عنه: أشرف المجالس وأعلاها: الجلوس مع الفكرة في ميدان التوحيد، والتنسم بنسيم المعرفة، والشرب بكأس المحبة من بحر الوداد، والنظر لحسن الظن بالله تعالى. ثم قال: يا لها من مجالس، ما أجلها، ومن شرابٍ ما ألذه، طوبى لمن رزقه. وقال القشيري رضي الله عنه: التفكر نعت كل طالب، وثمرته: الوصول بشرط العلم، فإذا سلم الفكر عن الشوائب ورد صاحبهُ على مناهل التحقيق. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-21","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"وسئلت زوجة أبي ذر عن عبادة زوجها، فقالت: كان نهاره أجمع في ناحية يتفكر. وكذلك زوجة أبي بكر قالت: كان ليله أجمع في ناحية يتفكر. وكذا زوجة أبي الدرداء، وكان سيدنا عيسى عليه السلام يقول: طوبى لمن كان قيله ذكراً وصمته تفكراً، ونظره عبرة. وقال الحسن رضي الله عنه: من لم يكن كلامه حكمة فهو لغو، ومن لم يكن سكوته تفكراً فهو سهو، ومن لم يكن نظره اعتباراً فهو لهو. هـ. وقال في الحكم: (ما نفع القلب شيء مثل عزلة يدخل بها ميدان فكرة) . وقال أيضاً: (الفكرة سِراج القلب، فإذا ذهبت فلا إضاءة له) . وقال أيضاً: (الفكرة فكرتان فكرة تصديق وإيمان، وفكرة شهود وعيان، فالأولى لأرباب الاعتبار، والثانية لأرباب الشهود والاستبصار) .","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-22","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"وفكرة الشهود والعيان هي عبادة العارفين، ولا يُحصر ثوابها في ستين ولا في سبعين، بل وقت منها يعدل أَلْفِ سنة، كما قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-23","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"كُلُّ وَقتٍ مِنْ حَبيبيِ ... قَدْرُهُ كَأَلفِ حَجّه","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-24","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"فأوقات هؤلاء كلها ليلة القدر، ومَن لم يبلغ هذا المقام فليبك على نفسه على الدوام، ومن ظفر بها ونالها حق له الهناء، وفي أمثاله قال القائل:","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-25","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"هُم الرِّجَالُ وغَبْنٌ أنْ يُقَالَ لِمَنْ ... لَمْ يَتَّصِفُ بمَعَاني وَصْفِهِمْ رَجُلُ","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-26","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"حققنا الله بمقامهم، وسقانا من منالهم، آمين.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-27","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"وقوله: رَبَّنا ما خَلَقْتَ هذا باطِلًا بل هو ثابت بإثباتك، ممحُوٌّ بأحدية ذاتك، فالباطل محال، وكل ما سواه باطل، كما قرره الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام (١) . وقوله: رَبَّنا إِنَّنا سَمِعْنا مُنادِياً يُنادِي لِلْإِيمانِ أَنْ آمِنُوا بِرَبِّكُمْ فَآمَنَّا أي: كنا في الرعيل الأول من أهل الإيمان، فجعل لنا سبيلاً إلى مقام الإحسان، رَبَّنا وَآتِنا مَا وَعَدْتَنا وهو الوصول إلى العيان. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-191-194-28","r":"q3-191-194","title":"3:191–194 · Remembrance, contemplation and the passage from intellectual signs to witnessing","text":"ثم ذكر ما أجابهم به، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-191-194-28"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-191-194-s1","r":"q3-191-194","title":"Continual dhikr and reflective reasoning","text":"Those endowed with understanding remember God continually ( الذكر ), standing, sitting and reclining. The Prophet is quoted urging abundant remembrance as grazing in Paradise's gardens. Or the verse describes prayer in the three postures permitted according to capacity, as in the Prophet's instruction to the ill ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn: pray standing if able, otherwise sitting, otherwise lying upon your side and indicating the movements. They contemplate ( يتفكرون ) the creation of heaven and earth as proof and admonition. Ibn ʿAjība calls reflection ( التفكر ) the greatest worship, citing sayings that no worship resembles it and that a man reclining on his bed looked at the sky and stars and said, “I testify that you have a Creator. O God, forgive me”; God then looked upon him and forgave him. Reflection is particular to the heart and is itself the purpose of creation. Al-Bayḍāwī sees in this testimony to the nobility of the theological sciences of principles ( علم الأصول ) and their scholars; further discussion comes in the allusion below.","anchor":"en-q3-191-194-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-191-194-s2","r":"q3-191-194","title":"Why the created order is not in vain","text":"Reflecting upon the marvels of created things, they say, “Our Lord, You did not create this in vain”—aimlessly, without Wisdom. Rather it exists for wondrous wisdom: it provides the basis for human existence and livelihood, serves as a sign leading to the knowledge of God and urges obedience, through which everlasting life and happiness in His presence may be attained. “Glory be to You!” declares His transcendence from futility. “Protect us from the Fire” which awaits those who turn away from inquiry and fail to fulfil what its conclusions demand under God's command. There are no helpers to save wrongdoers from it. Placing the explicit noun “wrongdoers” where a pronoun might stand ( إظهار في موضع الإضمار ) indicates that wrongdoing itself is the reason for punishment and loss of help. The “caller” to belief can be the noble Messenger or the Qurʾān: “Believe in your Lord, affirm His oneness.” They answer and ask forgiveness for major sins ( ذنوبنا ), the effacement of lesser misdeeds ( سيئاتنا ), and to be taken in death among the excellent and chosen ( الأبرار ), counted with them. This expresses love of meeting God and so being loved in that meeting. They ask for the reward promised to believers through acceptance of the messengers, or the mercy and beautiful return promised upon their tongues . This is not distrust of God's promise: rather it arises from fear of failing the conditions, a disastrous final outcome, insufficient fulfilment, worshipful devotion or humility. Al-Bayḍāwī mentions these readings. “Do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection” asks that their failings not bring humiliation; God does not break the promise of rewarding believers and answering supplications, or of resurrection and reckoning. Rabbanā ( رَبَّنا ) is repeated to intensify supplication and mark the separate significance of each request. An early report states: “If someone is beset by a matter and says ‘Our Lord’ five times, God delivers him from what he fears”; Ibn ʿAjība quotes it through al-Bayḍāwī. [R07-16]","anchor":"en-q3-191-194-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-191-194-s3","r":"q3-191-194","title":"The ascent of dhikr from tongue to heart, spirit and secret","text":"God sets remembrance ( الذكر ) before reflection ( الفكر ), according to the sequence of wayfaring ( ترتيب السير ). A disciple first practices remembrance by the tongue ( ذكر اللسان ) until it penetrates the inner heart ( الجنان ); then it passes to the heart ( القلب ), the spirit ( الروح ), which is the domain of contemplation, and at last the secret ( السر ), the station of witnessing and direct seeing ( الشهود والعيان ). Here the tongue falls silent and the human subject disappears amid lights of direct witnessing. A poet says: Whenever I invoke You, my secret, spirit and heart all but curse me when I remember You; as if a watchman of Yours called to me, “Beware! Woe to you—beware of recollection!” Do you not see the Real's signs now shining, and the whole, through its meaning, has joined your meaning? [Translator’s note: The Cairo print vocalizes al-kullu (“the whole”) in the nominative, making it the subject of wāṣala (“has joined”), with maʿnāka (“your meaning”) as its object. Ibn ʿAjība repeats the poem in Īqāẓ al-himam , pp. 120–121, within an account of the disappearance of awareness of the separate rememberer. The fuller discussion in Ibn ʿAbbād’s Ghayth al-mawāhib , pp. 73–74, quotes Ibn al-Bannā’s express rejection of indwelling or identity when explaining this state. These contexts support an inward account of remembrance, but do not identify the exact scope of “the whole” or the antecedent of “its meaning”; the prepositional phrase remains tentative. Al-Qushayrī’s Risāla (II:377) and al-Sulamī’s Jawāmiʿ ādāb al-ṣūfiyya preserve only the preceding two lines and cannot settle this third line. A longer, anonymous five-line version in al-Qaṣd al-mujarrad , published under Ibn ʿAṭāʾ Allāh’s name (ed. Maḥmūd Tawfīq al-Ḥakīm, Cairo, 2002, pp.119–120), adds verses about witnessing the meeting and remembrance free of uncertainty. It corroborates the difficult line and its nominative subject, but supplies no explicit gloss of its referents.] On reaching the station of singleness ( مقام الإفراد ), separate daily litanies ( الأوراد ) become a single wird : the heart remains in the Presence between thinking and looking ( فكرة ونظرة ), wholly directed to God and absent from all besides Him.","anchor":"en-q3-191-194-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-191-194-s4","r":"q3-191-194","title":"Al-Ghazālī on the realized person's wird","text":"In the Iḥyāʾ , in the Book of Litanies, al-Ghazālī describes the unifier entirely concentrated upon the One, the Eternal Refuge: all concerns become one; he loves and fears none but God, expects provision only from Him, and sees God in whatever comes before him. Such a person no longer needs a variety of arranged litanies; after obligatory prayer his continual practice is presence of heart with God. Nothing occurs, is heard or seen without becoming an occasion for reflection, admonition and growth. Since God moves and stills all things, every circumstance increases him, and no distinct form of worship is isolated from another. He has fled to God [Q 51:50] and says, “I am going to my Lord” [Q 37:99]. This is the furthest degree of the truthful ( الصديقين ). Yet, al-Ghazālī insists, a disciple must not hear this and presumptuously claim it, abandoning assigned acts of devotion. He describes its signs as freedom from distracting whispers, sinful thoughts, overwhelming changes of state and worldly distractions—and remarks how rare this rank is. Ibn ʿAjība expressly qualifies one criterion : the assertion that no thought of sin ever enters the heart is not necessary; the gnostic's heart can receive luminous and dark self-disclosures ( التجليات النورانية والظلمانية ), but the latter diminish and do not settle there. Al-Ghazālī also says elsewhere that the worship of people of understanding does not go beyond remembering God and contemplating Him in love of His Majesty and Beauty; other works reinforce these acts. Those who work for Paradise’s reward occupy the rank of the simple-hearted ( bulh ), and attain it by their works, since most of the people of Paradise are simple-hearted. In the Kīmiyāʾ al-saʿāda he warns against treating beginners' disciplines as identical with those of realized people. A Sufi teacher was once said to appear a supremely truthful one ( ṣiddīq ) at the beginning, when strenuous outward practice was evident, but a heretic at the end, when inward absorption had become dominant and outward movement less conspicuous. That is not contempt for worship, but attention to its kernel and goal; the bat's eyes cannot bear the sun. Ibn ʿAjība then cites a teaching of his teacher's teacher, Sīdī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, on the inwardly realized performing acts that gather rather than scatter their concentration. Al-Junayd reportedly preferred that the Sufi should neither read nor write, because that better gathers his purpose, and for the disciple not to be distracted by earning or collecting hadith, lest his state change. Ibn ʿAjība adds the operative qualification: whoever has been granted a teacher of spiritual formation ( شيخ التربية ) should take as his practice whatever that teacher specifically assigns; this is his very dhikr and carries him onwards, whatever it may be. [XIV-N146]","anchor":"en-q3-191-194-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-191-194-s5","r":"q3-191-194","title":"Thinking that assents and thinking that witnesses","text":"Reflection ( التفكر ) is the greatest devotional act and an exalted form of nearness, the worship of realized knowers and the limit of those drawn near. The report “An hour's reflection is better than seventy years of worship” is invoked. [Translator’s note: Its attribution requires verification.] Al-Junayd calls the noblest gathering the sitting of contemplation in the field of tawḥīd ( ميدان التوحيد ), breathing the breeze of knowledge ( المعرفة ), drinking the cup of love from the ocean of affection, and gazing with a favourable opinion of God. He then exclaims: “What gatherings—how exalted they are! What a drink—how delicious it is! Blessed is whoever is granted it.” Al-Qushayrī calls thinking a characteristic of every seeker: its fruit, when supported by knowledge and cleared of impurities, is arrival at the springs of realization ( مناهل التحقيق ). Asked about her husband’s worship, Abū Dharr’s wife said that he spent his entire day apart in contemplation; Abū Bakr’s wife said the same of his entire night, and the wife of Abū al-Dardāʾ is cited similarly. Jesus is quoted as praising a person whose speech is remembrance, silence contemplation and gaze a lesson; al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī says speech without wisdom is idle, silence without reflection heedless, and seeing without learning vain. The Ḥikam says that nothing benefits the heart like seclusion entering the field of thought; reflection is the lamp of the heart and without it the lamp gives no light; and there are two forms: reflection of affirmation and faith ( فكرة تصديق وإيمان ), for those who draw conclusions, and reflection of witnessing and immediate vision ( فكرة شهود وعيان ), for those who see directly and understand. The latter is the worship of the gnostics. Its value cannot be quantified by sixty or seventy years: Ibn ʿAjība speaks of a moment equal to a thousand years, quoting: Every moment of my Beloved is worth a thousand years. Their hours are all Laylat al-Qadr. Those still far away should lament their deficiency, while those attaining it may rejoice. Another poet says: “They are the men; it is an injustice to call a man / one who has not acquired the inward meanings of their qualities.” Ibn ʿAjība prays for realization of their state and a share in their refreshment. He concludes by returning to the verses spiritually. “You have not created this in vain”: it stands in being by Your giving it standing ( ثابت بإثباتك ), yet is effaced by the oneness of Your Essence ( ممحُوّ بأحدية ذاتك ). What is false is impossible, while everything besides Him is vain, as the Messenger—blessings and peace be upon him—affirmed. [R07-17] “We heard a caller ... and believed”: we belonged to the first company of the people of faith; He then made a way for us to the station of iḥsān. “Give us what You promised”: arrival at direct witnessing ( الوصول إلى العيان ). Success is through God.","anchor":"en-q3-191-194-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-191-194-s6","r":"q3-191-194","title":"","text":"He then recounts God's answer to their prayer.","anchor":"en-q3-191-194-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-195","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men 3:195","anchor":"unit-q3-195"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-1","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"فَاسْتَجابَ لَهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ أَنِّي لا أُضِيعُ عَمَلَ عامِلٍ مِنْكُمْ مِنْ ذَكَرٍ أَوْ أُنْثى بَعْضُكُمْ مِنْ بَعْضٍ فَالَّذِينَ هاجَرُوا وَأُخْرِجُوا مِنْ دِيارِهِمْ وَأُوذُوا فِي سَبِيلِي وَقاتَلُوا وَقُتِلُوا لَأُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّئاتِهِمْ وَلَأُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ ثَواباً مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ حُسْنُ الثَّوابِ (195)","anchor":"ar-q3-195-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-2","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"قلت: (استجاب) : أخص من أجاب، لأن استجاب مُستلزم لفعل ما طلب منه، وأجاب يصدق بالوعد، ويتعدى بنفسه وباللام، و (بعضكم من بعض) : جملة معترضة. قاله البيضاوي فانظره.","anchor":"ar-q3-195-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-3","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَاسْتَجابَ لَهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ فيما طلبوه لأنه لا يرد السؤال، ولا تخيب لديه الآمال، ولذلك قال: أَنِّي أي: بسبب أَنِّي لا أُضِيعُ عَمَلَ عامِلٍ مِنْكُمْ مِنْ ذَكَرٍ أَوْ أُنْثى لأنكم بَعْضُكُمْ مِنْ بَعْضٍ لأن الذكر من الأنثى، والأنثى من الذكر، ولأنهما من أصل واحد، ولفرط الاتصال والاتحاد والاتفاق في الدين.","anchor":"ar-q3-195-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-4","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"رُوِيَ «أَنَّ أمَّ سَلَمَة قالت: يا رسول الله، إني أَسْمَعُ الله يَذكُر الرجَالَ في الهِجْرَةِ ولم يَذكُر النساء، فنزلت. مِنْ ذَكَرٍ أَوْ أُنْثى» الخ.","anchor":"ar-q3-195-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-5","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"ثم فصل أعمال العمال، وما أعد لهم من الثواب فقال: فَالَّذِينَ هاجَرُوا دار الشرك، وفارقوا الأوطان والأصحاب والعشائر، وَأُخْرِجُوا مِنْ دِيارِهِمْ وَأُوذُوا فِي سَبِيلِي بسبب إيمانهم بالله، وَقاتَلُوا الكفار، وَقُتِلُوا أي: ماتوا في الجهاد. وقرىء بالعكس لأن الواو لا ترتب، أو قتل بعضهم، وقاتل الباقون ولم يضعفوا، لَأُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّئاتِهِمْ أي: لأمحونها، وَلَأُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ ثَواباً مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ أي: أثيبهم ثواباً من عند الله تفضلاً وإحساناً، وَاللَّهُ عِنْدَهُ حُسْنُ الثَّوابِ لا يعجزه شيء.","anchor":"ar-q3-195-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-6","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"الإشارة: لما توجهوا إليه بهممهم العلية، وعزائمهم القوية، فقرعوا بابه بدوام ذكره، والتفكر في عظمة ذاته، وجميل إحسانه وبره، وتضرعوا إليه بلسان الذل والانكسار، وحال الخضوع والاضطرار، أجابهم ففتح في وجوههم الباب، وأدخلهم في حضرته مع الأحباب، لأنه يجيب السؤال، ولا يخيب الآمال، بعد أن هاجروا الأوطان، وفارقوا العشائر والإخوان، إلا من يزيد بهم إلى الرحمن، فقاتلوا نفوسهم حتى ماتت فحييت بالوصال، إلى جوار الكبير المتعال، قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q3-195-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-7","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"إنْ تُردْ وَصْلنَا فَمَوْتكَ شَرْطٌ ... لا يَنَالُ الوِصَالَ من فيه فضله","anchor":"ar-q3-195-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-8","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"فمحا عن عين بصائرهم سيئات الأغيار، وطهَّر قلوبهم من درن الأكدار، حتى دخلوا جنة المعارف، التي لا يحيط بوصفها وصف واصف، تجري من تحتها أنهار العلوم، وتنفتح منها مخازن الفهوم، ثواباً من عند الحيّ القيوم والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-195-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-195-9","r":"q3-195","title":"3:195 · The answer to supplication and the equal recompense of women and men","text":"ولما بسط الله الدنيا على اليهود والمشركين، استدراجا، قال بعض المؤمنين: إن أعداء الله فيما نرى من الخير، وقد هلكنا من الجوع والجهد، فأنزل الله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q3-195-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-195-s1","r":"q3-195","title":"Istajāba and ajāba","text":"I say: Istajāba ( استجاب ) has a more specific sense than ajāba ( أجاب ): it implies acting upon what was requested, whereas ajāba may consist in a promise alone. The verb can govern directly or take the preposition lām ( لام ). “You belong one to another” ( بعضكم من بعض ) is a parenthetical sentence ( جملة معترضة ). Ibn ʿAjība cites al-Bayḍāwī and invites verification of the grammatical judgment.","anchor":"en-q3-195-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-195-s2","r":"q3-195","title":"No effort lost through sex or circumstance","text":"Their Lord responded to their request, for hopes are not disappointed with Him. He will not let the work of any servant be lost, male or female: each sex is born from the other, both stem from one origin, and both are joined in religion. A report states that Umm Salama asked why God spoke of men in connection with migration but not women; the verse was then revealed. The workers are specified: those who migrated from the abode of idolatry, left homeland, companions and clan, were driven from their homes and harmed on account of faith, fought disbelievers and were killed—that is, died while striving. Another reading reverses the verbs, for wāw does not necessarily establish sequence ( الواو لا ترتب ); or some were killed and the survivors went on fighting without weakening. God will efface their misdeeds, bring them into gardens with flowing streams, and bestow reward from Himself in favour and generosity. Nothing is beyond His power, and with Him is the best reward.","anchor":"en-q3-195-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-195-s3","r":"q3-195","title":"Migration from customary attachments and fighting the lower self","text":"Because they turned their high aspirations ( همم علية ) and firm resolve toward God, knocked at His gate with unceasing dhikr and reflection on His Essence's greatness and the beauty of His bounty, and entreated Him through humility, brokenness and need, He opened the gate before them and admitted them into His Presence with His beloved, for He answers those who ask and does not disappoint their hopes. They migrated from homelands and separated from kindred and companions—except those who increased their movement towards the Merciful—and fought their lower selves until these died and then came alive through union, in the presence of the Great, Most Exalted. As the poet says: If you desire union with us, your death is a condition; no one retains a portion of self and attains union. God then erased from their inward sight the evil of all otherness ( سيئات الأغيار ) and purified their hearts of troubles, until they entered the gardens of knowledge ( جنة المعارف ), indescribable in their beauty, with rivers of sciences flowing beneath and treasuries of understanding opening within. This is reward from the Living, Self-Subsisting One. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-195-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-195-s4","r":"q3-195","title":"","text":"When God extended worldly prosperity to the Jews and idolaters as a gradual drawing toward ruin ( istidrāj ), some believers said, “God’s enemies appear to us to enjoy good fortune, while we have perished from hunger and hardship.” God then revealed the next verses.","anchor":"en-q3-195-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-196-198","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness 3:196–198","anchor":"unit-q3-196-198"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-1","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"لا يَغُرَّنَّكَ تَقَلُّبُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فِي الْبِلادِ (196) مَتاعٌ قَلِيلٌ ثُمَّ مَأْواهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ وَبِئْسَ الْمِهادُ (197) لكِنِ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها نُزُلاً مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ وَما عِنْدَ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ لِلْأَبْرارِ (198)","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-2","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"قلت: النُزل- ويسكن-: ما يُقَدم للنازل من طعام وشراب وصلة، وانتصابه: على الحال من (جنات) ، والعامل فيه: الظرف، أو على المصدر المؤكد، أي: أُنزلوها نزلاً.","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-3","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لا يَغُرَّنَّكَ أيها السامع أو أيها الرسول، والمراد: تثبيته على ما كان عليه، كقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-4","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"فَلا تُطِعِ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ، أي: دُمْ على ما أنت عليه من عدم اغترارك بظاهر ما ترى عليه الكفار من البسط في الدنيا، والتقلب فيها بالتجارات والزراعات، وما هم عليه من الخصب ولين عيش، فإن ذلك مَتاعٌ قَلِيلٌ بلغة فانية، ومتعة زائلة، وظلال آفلة، وسحابة حائلة. قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «ما الدُّنْيا في الآخِرَةِ إلاَّ مِثْلُ ما يَجْعَلُ أَحَدُكُم إصْبَعَهِ في اليَمِّ، فَلْيَنْظُر بِمَ يَرْجِعَ» . فلا بد أن يرحلوا عنها قهراً، ثُمَّ مَأْواهُمْ أي: مصيرهم جَهَنَّمُ وَبِئْسَ الْمِهادُ ما مهدوا لأنفسهم.","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-5","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"والمعتبر عند الأكياس هو ما أعد الله للمتقين من الناس، قال تعالى: لكِنِ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ وخافوا عقابه، لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٌ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها، هيأ ذلك لهم وأعده نُزُلًا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ هذا النزول الذي يقدم للضيف، وأما ما أعد لهم بعد النزول فلا يعبر عنه لسان، ولذلك قال: وَما عِنْدَ اللَّهِ من النعيم الذي لا يفنى، جسماني وروحاني، خَيْرٌ لِلْأَبْرارِ مما ينقلب إليه الفجار. قيل: حقيقة البر: هو الذي لا يؤذي الذرّ.","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-6","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"الإشارة: لا يغرنك أيها الفقير ما ترى عليه أهل الدنيا من اتخاذ المنازل المشيدة، والفرش الممهدة، فإن الدنيا متاعها قليل، وعزيزها قليل، وغنيها فقير، وكبيرها حقير، واعتبر بحال نبيك- عليه الصلاة والسلام-.","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-7","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"قال أنس رضي الله عنه: دخلت على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وهُو على سَرِير مرفل بالشريط- أي: مضفور به- وتحت رَأسِهِ وسَادَةٌ من أدم، حشوها ليف، فدخل عليه عمر، وانحرف النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم انحرافة، فرأى عمر أثر الشريط في جَنْبِهِ، فَبكَى، فقال له النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «ما يُبْكِيكَ يا عمر» ؟ فقال: مَالِيَ لا أبْكِي وكِسْرى وقَيْصَرُ يعيشان فيما يعيشان فيه من الدنيا، وأنت على الحال الذي أرى، فقال له النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «يا عمر أمَا تَرْضَى أَنْ تَكُونَ لهُم الدُّنيا وَلَنا الآخرَةُ» .","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-8","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"رواه البخاري.","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-9","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"وانظر ما أعدّ الله للمتقين الأبرار، الذين صبروا قدر ساعة من نهار، فأفضوا إلى جوار الكريم الغفار فى دار القرار، وَما عِنْدَ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ لِلْأَبْرارِ، ولا سيما العارفين الكبار. قال الورتجبي: بيِّن الحق- تعالى- رفعة منزل المتقين في الجنان، ثم أبْهم لطائف العناية بقوله: وَما عِنْدَ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ لِلْأَبْرارِ أي: ما عنده من نعيم المشاهدة، ولطائف القربة، وحلاوة الوصلة، خير مما هم فيه من نعيم الجنة، وأيضاً: صرح في هذه الآية ببيان مراتب الولاية، لأنه ذكر المتقين، والتقوى: تقديس الباطن عن لوث الطبيعة، وتنزيه الأخلاق عن دنس","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-10","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"المخالفة، وذلك درجة الأول من الولاية، والأبرار أهل الاستقامة في المعرفة، وبين أن أهل التقوى في الجنة، والأبرار في الحضرة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-196-198-11","r":"q3-196-198","title":"3:196–198 · Worldly prosperity, true hospitality and the degrees of nearness","text":"ولمّا عاتب الحق تعالى، فيما تقدم، أهل الكتاب، وكان فيهم من لا يستحق العتاب لاتباعه الحق والصواب، أخرجه الحق تعالى بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q3-196-198-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-196-198-s1","r":"q3-196-198","title":"Nuzul (نُزُل) as hospitality","text":"I say: Nuzul ( النُّزُل ), also pronounced with a vowelless middle consonant, is the food, drink and gift offered to an arriving guest. Its accusative ending may make it a circumstantial expression ( حال ) relating to “gardens,” governed by the preceding locative expression ( ظرف ), or a cognate accusative ( مصدر مؤكد ): “They are welcomed with a full welcome.”","anchor":"en-q3-196-198-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-196-198-s2","r":"q3-196-198","title":"The difference between transitory abundance and lasting provision","text":"Let not the outward prosperity of unbelievers bewilder the Prophet or another hearer: their ability to travel freely, trade, farm, and enjoy comfort, abundance and ease is not a measure of ultimate success. The address confirms the Prophet in the absence of such deception, as “Do not obey those who deny” [Q 68:8] confirms an existing refusal. All such enjoyment is small and passing, provision for a short journey, shifting shade and a dissolving cloud. The Prophet is quoted saying that this world's proportion to the next is as the drop remaining on a finger dipped in the sea. Departure is inevitable; then Hell is their destination and miserable resting place. The wise instead consider what God has prepared for those who fear His punishment and are mindful of Him: gardens with rivers flowing, for everlasting residence. That is God's reception ( نُزُل ), the hospitality first presented to the guest; what He has prepared beyond that first reception cannot be expressed by the tongue. “What is with God,” bodily and spiritual delight without end, is better for the righteous than the fate of wrongdoers. It is said that true birr ( البر ) is to refrain even from injuring an ant.","anchor":"en-q3-196-198-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-196-198-s3","r":"q3-196-198","title":"The contrast with worldly kings and the divine feast","text":"O spiritual poor, be not seduced by impressive houses and richly furnished beds. The world's wares are few; its mighty are small, its wealthy poor and its eminent insignificant. Remember the Prophet's life. Anas reports entering when he lay on a simple woven bedstead with a leather cushion stuffed with palm fibre. ʿUmar entered and wept at the marks left on the Prophet's side by the weaving, contrasting his condition with the comfort enjoyed by Chosroes and Caesar. The Prophet is quoted asking whether ʿUmar was not content that they should have the world and the believers the Hereafter, a report attributed here to al-Bukhārī. Look rather at what God has prepared for the righteous who endured a brief daytime hour of striving and then attained the nearness of the Generous Forgiver in the enduring abode, above all the realized masters. Al-Wartajbī says that after clearly announcing the high rank of those mindful of God in the gardens, God leaves the subtleties of solicitude partly hidden: what is with Him—the delight of witnessing ( نعيم المشاهدة ), the graces of nearness ( لطائف القربة ) and the sweetness of union ( حلاوة الوصلة )—is better than the joys of Paradise. He also sees ranks of sainthood ( مراتب الولاية ): mindful discipline purifies the inward person of the stains of nature and protects conduct from disobedience, the first degree; the righteous ( الأبرار ) are firm in gnosis. Thus the mindful are in the Garden, whereas the fully righteous abide in the Presence.","anchor":"en-q3-196-198-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-196-198-s4","r":"q3-196-198","title":"","text":"Since some People of the Book deserved no reproach and did follow the truth, God now explicitly distinguishes them.","anchor":"en-q3-196-198-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-199","r":"q3-199","title":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love","text":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love 3:199","anchor":"unit-q3-199"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-199-1","r":"q3-199","title":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love","text":"وَإِنَّ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ لَمَنْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ وَما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْهِمْ خاشِعِينَ لِلَّهِ لا يَشْتَرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً أُولئِكَ لَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ سَرِيعُ الْحِسابِ (199)","anchor":"ar-q3-199-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-199-2","r":"q3-199","title":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنَّ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ كعبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه ممن أسلم من اليهود، لَمَنْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ إيماناً حقيقياً، وَما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ من القرآن، وَما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْهِمْ من التوراة، حال كونهم خاشِعِينَ لِلَّهِ خاضعين مخبتين وافين بالعهد، لا يَشْتَرُونَ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ ثَمَناً قَلِيلًا، كما فعل المحرفون من أحبار اليهود، أُولئِكَ لَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ أي: ما وعدوا به من تضعيف أجرهم مرتين، إِنَّ اللَّهَ سَرِيعُ الْحِسابِ فيُسرع إلى توفية أجورهم وإكرام منقلبهم لأن الله عالم بالأعمال وما تستوجبه من النوال، فلا يحتاج إلى تأمل ولا احتياط لأنه غني عن التأمل والاحتياط.","anchor":"ar-q3-199-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-199-3","r":"q3-199","title":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love","text":"وقيل: نزلت في النصارى: أربعين من نجران، واثنين وثلاثين من الحبشة، قدموا على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وأسلموا.","anchor":"ar-q3-199-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-199-4","r":"q3-199","title":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love","text":"وقيل: نزلت في النجاشي، لما نَعَاه جبريل إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فخرج- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، وصلّى عليه، فقال المنافقون: انظروا إلى هذا، يصلّي على عِلْجٍ نصراني (١)، فنزلت الآية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q3-199-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-199-5","r":"q3-199","title":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love","text":"الإشارة: قد رأينا بعض الفقهاء حصل لهم الإيمان بخصوص أهل زمانهم، فتحققوا بولايتهم، ونالوا شيئاً من محبتهم، لكن لم تساعفهم الأقدار في صحبتهم، فظهرت عليهم آثار أنوارهم، واقتبسوا شيئاً من أسرارهم، فتنوّرت سريرتهم، وكملت شريعتهم، وأظهر عليهم آثار الخشوع، وأخذوا حظّاً من التواضع والخضوع، متخلقين بالقناعة والورع، قد ذهب عن قلبهم ما ابتلى به غيرهم من الجزع والهلع، فلا جرم أن هؤلاء لهم أجرهم مرتين: أجر ما تحملوا من الشريعة لنفع العوام، وأجر ما اكتسبوا من محبة القوم «المرءُ مَع مَنْ أَحب» . وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-199-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-199-6","r":"q3-199","title":"3:199 · The faithful People of the Book and two rewards for scholarship and love","text":"ولمّا كان الصبر من الدّين كالرأس من الجسد، فلو حصل للناس دائما لم يتوجه العتاب لأحد، ختم به السورة، التي عاتب فيها جل العباد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q3-199-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-199-s1","r":"q3-199","title":"Faith, humility and rejection of worldly exchange","text":"Among the People of the Book are those like ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his companions among Jews who embraced Islam: they genuinely believe in God, the Qurʾān sent to you and the Torah given to them. They are humble, submissive and faithful to the covenant, and do not exchange God’s signs for a paltry price, as the distorters among the Jewish rabbis did. God promises them reward increased twofold. His reckoning is swift: He hastens to pay their rewards in full and honour their return, for He knows deeds and the bounty they merit, without needing deliberation or precaution. An alternative report applies the verse to Christians—forty from Najrān and thirty-two from Abyssinia—who came to the Prophet and accepted Islam. Another associates it with the Negus (al-Najāshī), whose death Gabriel informed the Prophet of; the Prophet went out to offer the funeral prayer, while the hypocrites said, “Look at this man, praying over a Christian foreign infidel ( ʿilj )!” Then the verse was revealed. [Translator’s note: Ibn ʿAjība presents these as alternative reports of the occasion of revelation.] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q3-199-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-199-s2","r":"q3-199","title":"Jurists who recognize the saints but cannot accompany them","text":"I have seen some jurists attain faith in the particularity of the friends of God of their own age ( خصوص أهل زمانهم ), recognize their sainthood and gain a measure of love for them, even though the decrees of destiny did not permit them to enter their company. Yet traces of their light appeared in these jurists, who drew something from their secrets. Their inward character was illumined and their practice of the Sacred Law perfected; signs of reverence and humility appeared, with contentment and scrupulousness ( القناعة والورع ). The anguish and panic that afflicted others had left their hearts. Such jurists have two rewards: one for carrying the burden of the Sacred Law to benefit ordinary people, and one for the love they gained for the spiritual people. “A person is with those whom he loves.” Success comes from God.","anchor":"en-q3-199-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-199-s3","r":"q3-199","title":"","text":"Patience is to religion as the head to a body: if it were constantly present in people, no reproach would be addressed to anyone. God therefore closes this sūrah, in which He has rebuked most of His servants, by commanding it.","anchor":"en-q3-199-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q3-200","r":"q3-200","title":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān","text":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān 3:200","anchor":"unit-q3-200"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-200-1","r":"q3-200","title":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اصْبِرُوا وَصابِرُوا وَرابِطُوا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ (200)","anchor":"ar-q3-200-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-200-2","r":"q3-200","title":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān","text":"قلت: المرابطة: أن يربط هؤلاء خيولهم، وهؤلاء خيولهم، إرصاداً لمن حاربهم، ثم أُطلق على كل مقيم في ثغر يدفع عمن وراءه، وإن لم يكن له مركب، إذا كان بنية الدفع عن المسلمين كان بأهله أو وحده. المدار على خلوص النية، خلاف ما قاله ابن عطية (١) ، وسيأتي صوابه (٢) في تفسير المعنى، إن شاء الله.","anchor":"ar-q3-200-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-200-3","r":"q3-200","title":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اصْبِرُوا على مشاق الطاعات، وما يصيبكم من الشدائد والأزْمَات، وعلى مجانبة المعاصي والمخالفات، وعلى شكر ما أوليتكم من مواهب العطيات وَصابِرُوا أي:","anchor":"ar-q3-200-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-200-4","r":"q3-200","title":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān","text":"غالبوا الأعداء في مواطن الصبر، والثبوت في مداحض الحرب، وَرابِطُوا أبدانكم وخيولكم في الثغور لتحفظوا المسلمين من العدو الكفور، كي تفوزوا بعظائم الأجور قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «من رَابَط يَوْماً ولَيلَة في سبيل اللهِ كان كعدل صيام شهر وقيامه، لا يفطر ولا ينفتل عن صلاته (٣) إلا لحاجة، ومن توفي في سبيل الله- أي: مرابطاً في سبيل الله- أجْرَى الله عليه أجره حتى يقضي بين أهلِ الجنَةِ وأهل النَّارِ» . ومما يلحق بالرباط: «انتظَارُ الصَّلاَةِ بَعْدَ الصَّلاَةِ» ، كما في الحديث.","anchor":"ar-q3-200-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-200-5","r":"q3-200","title":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān","text":"وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فيما يأمركم به وينهاكم عنه، لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ فلاحاً لا خسران بعده أبداً.","anchor":"ar-q3-200-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q3-200-6","r":"q3-200","title":"3:200 · The closing injunction: patience, rivalry in steadfastness and the stations of Islam, faith and iḥsān","text":"الإشارة: (يا أيها الذين آمنوا) إيمان أهل الخصوص، (اصبروا) على حفظ مراسم الشريعة، (وصابروا) على تحصيل أنوار الطريقة، (ورابطوا) قلوبكم على شهود أسرار الحقيقة، أو: اصبروا على أداء العبادة، وصابروا على تحقيق العبودية، ورابطوا في تحصيل العبودة- أي: الحرية- أو: اصبروا على تحقيق مقام الإسلام، وصابروا على دوام الإيمان، ورابطوا على العكوف في مقام الإحسان، أو: اصبروا على تخليص الطاعات، وصابروا على رفض الحظوظ والشهوات، ورابطوا أسراركم على أنوار المشاهدات، (واتقوا الله) فلا تشهدوا معه سواه، (لعلكم تفلحون) ، بتحقيق معرفة الله. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q3-200-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-200-s1","r":"q3-200","title":"Murābaṭa (مرابطة) at the frontier","text":"I say: Murābaṭa ( المرابطة ) originally referred to each of two opposing groups tethering their horses in readiness for combat. The term then extended to any person remaining in a frontier post ( ثغر ), defending those behind him even without a mount, whether with his family or alone, provided the intention is the protection of Muslims. Sincerity of intention ( خلوص النية ) is decisive; Ibn ʿAjība explicitly disagrees here with a restriction ascribed to Ibn ʿAṭiyya, promising to correct it in the exposition.","anchor":"en-q3-200-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-200-s2","r":"q3-200","title":"Four commands addressed to believers","text":"Be patient ( اصبروا ) through the labour of obedience, the difficulties and crises that touch you, abstaining from sins and violations, and giving thanks for divine gifts. Compete in perseverance ( صابروا ) against the enemy, steadfast when the field of battle is perilous. Guard the frontier ( رابطوا ), positioning your bodies and horses there to protect Muslims and win abundant reward. The Prophet is quoted saying that a day and night in frontier defence are rewarded like a month’s fasting and standing in prayer, without breaking the fast or leaving prayer except for a necessity, and that one who dies in such service continues to be rewarded until judgment. Waiting for one prayer after another is also included under the name ribāṭ , as reported in another hadith. Finally, fear God concerning what He commands and forbids, so that you attain success beyond which no loss follows.","anchor":"en-q3-200-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q3-200-s3","r":"q3-200","title":"Fourfold patience and the uniting of law, path and Reality","text":"“O you who believe,” with the faith of the elect ( إيمان أهل الخصوص ): be patient in preserving the observances of the Sacred Law ( مراسم الشريعة ); persevere in acquiring the lights of the Path ( أنوار الطريقة ); and station your hearts at the witnessing of the secrets of Reality ( شهود أسرار الحقيقة ). Or: patience is the performance of worship ( العبادة ); mutual perseverance is realization of servanthood ( العبودية ); stationing is acquisition of ʿubūda ( العبودة ), which he glosses as freedom ( الحرية ). Or: patience establishes Islam; perseverance perpetuates faith; and stationing consists in continual abiding at the station of iḥsān ( مقام الإحسان ). Or: patience is to purify deeds, perseverance to reject self-interest and desires, stationing to fix one's inward secrets upon the lights of witnessing ( أنوار المشاهدات ). Be mindful of God, and do not witness anything other than Him along with Him, so that you succeed through realized knowledge of Him ( معرفة الله ). Success is through God, the guide to the straight path.","anchor":"en-q3-200-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"intro4","r":"intro4","title":"The six matters to be safeguarded","text":"The six matters to be safeguarded intro4","anchor":"unit-intro4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro4-1","r":"intro4","title":"The six matters to be safeguarded","text":"سورة النّساء","anchor":"ar-intro4-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro4-2","r":"intro4","title":"The six matters to be safeguarded","text":"مدنية، وهى ستة عشر ألف حرف وثلاثون حرفا. وثلاثة آلاف وسبعمائة وخمس وأربعون كلمة. ومائة وستون آية. قاله الثعلبي. وقال البيضاوي: مائة وخمس وسبعون آية.","anchor":"ar-intro4-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-intro4-3","r":"intro4","title":"The six matters to be safeguarded","text":"ومضمنها: الأمر بحفظ ستة أمور: حفظ الأموال، وحفظ الأنساب، وحفظ الأبدان، وحفظ الأديان، وحفظ اللسان، وحفظ الإيمان. بعد أن قدّم الأمر بالتقوى، التي هى ملاك ذلك كله، فقال:","anchor":"ar-intro4-3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-intro4-s1","r":"intro4","title":"The scope and governing principle of Sūrat al-Nisāʾ","text":"This sūrah is Medinan. Al-Thaʿlabī says that it contains sixteen thousand and thirty letters, three thousand seven hundred and forty-five words, and one hundred and sixty verses. Al-Bayḍāwī gives one hundred and seventy-five verses. [N001] Its subject matter encompasses the injunction to safeguard six things: property ( حفظ الأموال ), lineage and kinship ( حفظ الأنساب ), bodies or lives ( حفظ الأبدان ), religion ( حفظ الأديان ), speech ( حفظ اللسان ), and faith ( حفظ الإيمان ). Before these the command to have Godfearing awareness ( التقوى ) is placed first, for it is the governing principle of them all. Thus He says:","anchor":"en-intro4-s1"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-1","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba 4:1","anchor":"unit-q4-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-1","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوا رَبَّكُمُ الَّذِي خَلَقَكُمْ مِنْ نَفْسٍ واحِدَةٍ وَخَلَقَ مِنْها زَوْجَها وَبَثَّ مِنْهُما رِجالاً كَثِيراً وَنِساءً وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ الَّذِي تَسائَلُونَ بِهِ وَالْأَرْحامَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلَيْكُمْ رَقِيباً (1)","anchor":"ar-q4-1-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-2","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"قلت: من قرأ: (والأرحامَ) بالنصب، فعطف على لفظ الجلالة، أي: اتقوا الأرحام أن تقطعوها، وقرأ حمزة بالخفض على الضمير من (به) كقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q4-1-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-3","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"فَالْيَوْمَ قَدْ بتّ تَهْجُونَا وَتَشْتُمُنَا ... فَاذْهَبْ فَمَا بِكَ والأَيَّامِ مِنْ عَجَبِ (١)","anchor":"ar-q4-1-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-4","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"وجمهور البصريين يمنعون العطف على الضمير إلا بإعادة الجار، فيقولون: مررت به وبزيد. وقال ابن مالك:","anchor":"ar-q4-1-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-5","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"ولَيْس عِنْدي لاَزمَا إذْ قَدْ أَتَى ... في النَّظْم والنَّثْر الصَّحِيح مُثْبَتَا.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-6","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"والنثر الصحيح هو ما قرأ به حمزة، وهذا هو التوجيه الصحيح، وأما من جعل الواو للقسم فبعيد.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-7","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ أي: جميع الخلق، اتقوا ربكم فيما كلفكم به، ثم بيَّن موجب التقوى فقال: الَّذِي خَلَقَكُمْ مِنْ نَفْسٍ واحِدَةٍ يعني آدم، وَخَلَقَ مِنْها زَوْجَها يعني حواء، من ضلع من أضلاعه، وَبَثَّ أي: نشر مِنْهُما رِجالًا كَثِيراً وَنِساءً أي: نشر من تلك النفس الواحدة بنين وبنات. قال البيضاوي: واكتفى بوصف الرجال بالكثرة عن وصف النساء، إذْ الحكمة تقتضي أن يكنَّ أكثر، وذكر: كَثِيراً","anchor":"ar-q4-1-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-8","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"حملاً على الجمع، وترتيب الأمر بالتقوى على هذه القصة لما فيها من الدلالة على القدرة القاهرة التي من حقها أن تُخشى والنعمة الباهرة التي توجب طاعة مولاها. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-9","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ الَّذِي تَسائَلُونَ بِهِ أي: يسأل بعضكم بعضَا فيقول: أسألك بالله العظيم، وَالْأَرْحامَ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4-1-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-10","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"واتقوا الأرحام فلا تقطعوها، فمن قطعها قطعه الله، ومن وصلها وصله الله، كما في الحديث. أو تساءلون به وبالأرحام، فيقول بعضكم لبعض: أسألك بالرحم التي بيني وبينك، أو بالقرابة التي بيني وبينك. ثم هددهم على ترك ما أمروا به فقال: إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلَيْكُمْ رَقِيباً حافظًا مطلعًا شهيدًا عليكم في كل حال.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-11","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"الإشارة: درجهم في آخر السورة في مدارج السلوك حتى زجَّهم في حضرة ملك الملوك، وأمرهم أن يتقوا ما يُخرجهم عن مشاهدة ظلمة أنوار الربوبية، ثم دلاهم في أول السورة إلى التنزل لآداب العبودية بشهود آثار القدرة الإلهية، في النشأة الأولية، ليعلَّمهم الجمع بين آداب المراقبة ودوام المشاهدة، أو بين الفناء والبقاء.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-12","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"وقد تكلم ابن جزي هنا على أحكام المراقبة، فقال: إذا تحقق العبد بهذه الآية وأمثالها، استفاد مقام المراقبة، وهو مقام شريف أصله علم وحال، ثم يثُمر حالين. أما العلم: فهو معرفة العبد بأن الله مطلع عليه، ناظر إليه في جميع أعماله، ويسمع جميع أقواله، ويعلم كل ما يخطر على باله. وأما الحال: فهو ملازمة هذا العلم بالقلب، بحيث يغلب عليه ولا يغفل عنه. ولا يكفي العلم دون هذه الحال، فإذا حصل العلم والحال كانت ثمرتهما عند أصحاب اليمين:","anchor":"ar-q4-1-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-13","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"الحياء من الله، وهو يوجب بالضرورة ترك المعاصي والجد في الطاعات، وكانت ثمرتهما عند المقربين:","anchor":"ar-q4-1-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-14","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"المشاهدة، التي توجب التعظيم والإجلال لذي الجلال.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-15","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"وإلى هاتين الثمرتين أشار الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم بقوله: «أن تعبدَ اللهَ كأنكَ تَراه فإنْ لم تكن تراه، فإنه يراك» ، فقوله:","anchor":"ar-q4-1-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-16","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"«أن تعبد الله كأنك تراه» إشارة إلى الثمرة الثانية، وهي الموجبة للتعظيم، كمن يشاهد ملكًا عظيمًا فإنه يعظمه إذ ذاك بالضرورة، وقوله: «فإن لم تكن تراه فإنه يراك» إشارة إلى الثمرة الأولى، ومعناه: إن لم تكن من أهل المشاهدة- التي هي مقام المقربين- فاعلم أنه يراك، فكن من أهل الحياء الذي هو مقام أصحاب اليمين، فلما فسر الإحسان أول مرة بالمقام الأعلى، ورأى أن كثيرا من الناس قد يعجزون عنه، تنزل منه إلى المقام الآخر.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-17","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"واعلم أن المراقبة لا تستقيم حتى تتقدم قبلها المشارطة والمرابطة، ويتأخر عنها المحاسبة والمعاتبة، فأما المشارطة فهي اشتراط العبد على نفسه التزام الطاعة، وترك المعاصي، وأما المرابطة فهي معاهدة العبد لربه على ذلك، ثم بعد المشارطة والمرابطة في أول الأمر تكون المراقبة ... الخ.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-18","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"وبعد ذلك يحاسب العبدُ نفسَه على ما اشترطه وعاهد عليه، فإن وجد نفسه قد وفَّى بما عاهد عليه الله يحمد الله، وإن وجد نفسه قد حلَ عَقد المشارطة ونقض عهد المراقبة، عاقب النفس عقابًا شديدًا بزجرها عن العودة إلى مثل ذلك، ثم عاد إلى المشارطة والمرابطة، وحافظ على المراقبة، ثم اختبر بالمحاسبة، وهكذا يكون إلى أن يلقى الله تعالى. انتهى كلامه، وهو مقتبس من الإحياء. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-1-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-1-19","r":"q4-1","title":"4:1 — One origin, kinship, vigilance and the two fruits of murāqaba","text":"ثم شرع تعالى فى الكلام على حفظ الأموال، وبدأ بأموال اليتامى، اعتناء بهم لضعفهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-1-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-1-s1","r":"q4-1","title":"The accusative and genitive readings of al-arḥām (الأرحام)","text":"I say: Whoever reads “and the ties of kinship” ( والأرحامَ ) in the accusative ( النصب ) coordinates it with the divine Name: “And guard against severing kinship ties.” Ḥamza reads it in the genitive ( الخفض ), coordinated with the pronoun in “by Him” ( به ), like the poet's verse: Today you have taken to reviling and insulting us; Go, then—for there is nothing to wonder at in you or in the days! Most Basran grammarians do not allow coordination with a governed pronoun unless the preposition ( الجار ) is repeated. Thus they say: “I passed by him and by Zayd” ( مررت به وبزيد ). But Ibn Mālik says: I do not consider it obligatory, since it has indeed been found In sound poetry and sound prose alike. The sound prose here is the reading transmitted from Ḥamza: this is the correct analysis. To take the conjunction wāw as an oath-particle ( واو القسم ) is far-fetched. [N002]","anchor":"en-q4-1-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-1-s2","r":"q4-1","title":"Creation from a single soul and the duty of kinship","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—addresses “O people,” meaning all created persons. “Be mindful of your Lord” in what He has charged you to do. He then declares why such mindfulness is incumbent: “Who created you from a single soul,” meaning Adam, “and from it created its mate,” meaning Eve, from one of his ribs, “and scattered from them many men and women”: from the single soul He brought forth sons and daughters. Al-Bayḍāwī says that men alone are explicitly qualified as numerous, without similarly qualifying women, because wisdom requires women to be more numerous; “many” agrees with the plural. The command to fear God follows this narrative because it demonstrates overwhelming power, which rightly inspires awe, and manifest beneficence, which requires obedience to its Bestower. Thus concludes his statement. “And be mindful of God, by whom you appeal to one another”: one of you says to another, “I ask you by Almighty God.” “And of kinship ties”: fear severing them, for one who severs them is cut off by God and one who maintains them is joined by Him, as stated in the report [H001] . Alternatively, you make appeals through God and the ties of kinship: “I ask you by the kinship between us,” or “by the relationship that joins us.” Then He warns them against abandoning His command: “God is ever a watcher ( رقيب ) over you”—guarding, observing, and witnessing you in every state.","anchor":"en-q4-1-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-1-s3","r":"q4-1","title":"From witnessing to servanthood; combining fanāʾ and baqāʾ","text":"At the end of the previous sūrah God led them through the ascending stations of the way ( مدارج السلوك ) until He brought them into the Presence of the King of Kings. He commanded them to guard against what removes them from witnessing the darkness of the lights of Lordship [Textual note: the Cairo text reads ẓulmat anwār al-rubūbiyya , literally “the darkness of the lights of Lordship.” The wording is preserved without emendation. A possible contextual analogy occurs in Ibn ʿAjība’s Īqāẓ al-himam , pp. 120–121: immersion in divine light removes awareness of other things, and a definition he attributes to al-Qushayrī speaks of the innermost secret’s darkening at the Remembered’s appearance. This suggests an eclipse of separate awareness, but it is not an exact gloss of the present phrase or evidence for changing its letters], and at the beginning of this sūrah brings them down again to the courtesy and disciplines of servanthood ( آداب العبودية ), through witnessing the effects of divine power in the original creation. He thereby teaches them to combine the proprieties of vigilant awareness ( المراقبة ) with continual witnessing ( المشاهدة ); or, otherwise stated, effacement and subsistence ( الفناء والبقاء ). Ibn Juzayy here discusses the principles of murāqaba . He says: Once a servant realizes this verse and others like it, he acquires the station of vigilance ( مقام المراقبة ). This noble station begins with knowledge ( علم ) and a state ( حال ), which then produce two fruits. Its knowledge is the servant's recognition that God looks upon him in all his works, hears everything he utters, and knows whatever passes through his mind. Its state consists in the heart's continually retaining that knowledge until it prevails and he does not become heedless of it. Knowledge by itself, without this state, does not suffice. Once knowledge and state are joined, their fruit among the People of the Right ( أصحاب اليمين ) is modest reverence before God ( الحياء من الله ), which necessarily brings abandonment of sins and zeal in obedience. Among those brought near ( المقربون ), their fruit is witnessing ( المشاهدة ), which necessarily produces reverence and magnification of the Lord of Majesty. The Messenger points to both fruits in his saying: “That you worship God as though you see Him; if you do not see Him, He sees you” [H002] . “That you worship God as though you see Him” designates the second fruit, producing reverence, as one who actually stands before a mighty sovereign cannot but magnify him. “If you do not see Him, He sees you” designates the first: if you are not among the people of witnessing, the station of the brought-near, know that He sees you and become one of the people of reverent shame, the station of the People of the Right. Having first explained iḥsān by the higher station, and recognizing that many may not reach it, the Prophet descended to the other station. Know also that vigilance ( المراقبة ) does not become established until stipulation with oneself ( المشارطة ) and binding covenant ( المرابطة ) precede it, and reckoning with oneself ( المحاسبة ) and reproach ( المعاتبة ) follow it. Stipulation is the servant's imposing on himself the obligation of obedience and abandonment of disobedience. Covenant is his undertaking before his Lord to do so. After stipulation and covenant at the outset come vigilance, and afterwards the servant takes account of how he has fulfilled what he stipulated and pledged. If he finds himself faithful to his covenant with God he praises God; if he has dissolved the stipulation and broken the pledge of vigilance, he disciplines his self severely, restraining it from returning to such things. Then he returns to stipulation and covenant, perseveres in vigilance, examines himself by reckoning, and continues in this way until he meets God Most High. This concludes Ibn Juzayy's words, drawn from the Iḥyāʾ . And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-1-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-1-s4","r":"q4-1","title":"","text":"The Most High then began to speak of safeguarding property, beginning with the property of orphans on account of their weakness.","anchor":"en-q4-1-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-2","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices 4:2","anchor":"unit-q4-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-1","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"وَآتُوا الْيَتامى أَمْوالَهُمْ وَلا تَتَبَدَّلُوا الْخَبِيثَ بِالطَّيِّبِ وَلا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوالَهُمْ إِلى أَمْوالِكُمْ إِنَّهُ كانَ حُوباً كَبِيراً (2)","anchor":"ar-q4-2-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-2","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"قلت: اليتيم: مَنْ فقدَ أباه، ولا يقال فيه اليتيم عُرفا إلا قبل البلوغ، وهو هنا مجاز، أي: من كان يتيمًا، والحوبُ:","anchor":"ar-q4-2-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-3","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"الإثم، ويقال فيه: حوبا، بالضم والفتح، مع الواو والألف، مصدر حاب حوبًا وحوَبا وحابا.","anchor":"ar-q4-2-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-4","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"يقول الحقْ جلّ جلاله: وَآتُوا أي: أعطوا الْيَتامى أَمْوالَهُمْ إذا بلغوا، وأُنِس منهم الرشد، وسمَّاهم يتامى بعد البلوغ اتساعًا لقرب عهدهم بالصغر، حثًا على أن يُدفع إليهم أموالهم أول بلوغهم، قبل أن يزول عنهم هذا الاسم إذا أنِسَ فيهم الرشد، ويدل على هذا ما قيل في سبب نزول الآية، وهو أن رجلاً من غطفان كان معه مال كثير لابن أخ له، فلما بلغ طلب مال أبيه، فمنعه، فنزلت الآية، فلما سمعها العم قال: أطعنا الله ورسوله، ونعوذ بالله من الحُوب الكبير. وقيل: إن العرب كانت لا تورِّث الصغار مع الكبار، فأُمِرُوا أن يورثوهم، وعلى هذا يكون اليتيم على حقيقته، فعلى الأول: الخطاب للأوصياء، وعلى الثاني: للعرب التي كانت لا تورث الصغار.","anchor":"ar-q4-2-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-5","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"ثم قال: وَلا تَتَبَدَّلُوا الْخَبِيثَ بِالطَّيِّبِ أي: لا تتبدلوا الحرام من أموالهم بالحلال من أموالكم، أو: لا تأخذوا الرفيع من أموالهم وتُعطوا الخبيث مكانها من أموالكم. كان بعضهم يبدل الشاة السمينة من مال اليتيم بالمهزولة من ماله، والدرهم الطيب بالزائف. وَلا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوالَهُمْ مضمومًا إِلى أَمْوالِكُمْ فتنفقونها معًا، مع أن اليتيم لا يأكل كالكبير، إلا إذا كان المنفَق قدَّر أكله، أو لمصلحة. إِنَّهُ أي: الأكل، كانَ حُوباً كَبِيراً أي: إثمًا عظيمًا.","anchor":"ar-q4-2-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-6","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"الإشارة: أمر الحق جل جلاله أغنياء القلوب، وهم أكابر الأولياء الراسخون في علم الغيوب، أن يَمنحوا من تعلق بهم من الفقراء والضعفاء، من الغنى بالله الذي منحهم الله، حتى لا يلتفتوا إلى سواه، وأن يَقبلوا كل من أتى إليهم من العباد، سواء كان من أهل المحبة والوداد، أو من أهل المخالفة والعناد، ولا يتبدلوا الخبيث بالطيب، بحيث","anchor":"ar-q4-2-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-7","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"يَقبلون من وجدوه طيب الأخلاق، ويردون من وجدوه خبيث الأخلاق، فإن هذا ليس من شأن أهل التربية النبوية، بل من شأنهم أن يقبلوا الناس على السوية، ويقلبوا فيهم الأعيان، فيقلبون العاصي طائعًا، والكافر مؤمنًا، والغافل ذاكرًا، والشحيح سخيًّا، والخبيث طيبًا، والمسيء محسنًا، والجاهل عارفًا، وهكذا لما عندهم من الإكسير، وهي الخمرة الأزلية، أي: التي من شأنها أن تقلب الأعيان، كما قال ابن الفارض رضي الله عنه في وصفها:","anchor":"ar-q4-2-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-8","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"تُهذبُ أخلاقَ النَّدامى فيَهْتَدي ... بها لطريقِ العزمِ مَن لا له عَزْم","anchor":"ar-q4-2-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-9","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"ويكرُمُ مَنْ لم يَعْرِف الجودَ كَفُّه ... ويحلُمُ عند الغيْظِ مَنْ لا لهُ حِلم","anchor":"ar-q4-2-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-10","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"وقوله: وَلا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوالَهُمْ إِلى أَمْوالِكُمْ يعني: حتى تتحققوا بوصول الغنى إلى قلوبهم، فإن تحققتم فخذوا ما بذلوا لكم من أموالهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-2-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-2-11","r":"q4-2","title":"4:2 — The orphan’s property and the transformation of spiritual novices","text":"ولما كان الأولياء، إذا كانت تحتهم يتيمة لها مال، وخافوا أن يدخل معهم أجنبى، تزوجها أو زوجوها من أبنائهم، حرصا على أكل مالها، ولا يقسطون لها فى صداقها، وربما أساءوا عشرتها انتظارا لموتها، فنهاهم الله عن ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q4-2-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-2-s1","r":"q4-2","title":"The orphan (يتيم) and grievous sin (حوب)","text":"I say: An orphan ( اليتيم ) is one who has lost his father; in established usage the description applies only before puberty. Here it is figurative ( مجاز ): someone who was an orphan. Ḥūb ( الحوب ) means sin. Its verbal noun ( مصدر ) is transmitted with both ḍamma and fatḥa, and with wāw or alif: ḥāba, ḥūban, ḥawban, or ḥāban.","anchor":"en-q4-2-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-2-s2","r":"q4-2","title":"Returning property promptly and without substitution","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—says: “Give the orphans their property” when they attain maturity and discernment ( الرشد ) has been perceived in them. He still calls them orphans after maturity by extended usage ( اتساع ), because their childhood is recent, and in order to hasten payment once maturity is reached and good judgment observed, rather than waiting until the designation “orphan” no longer fits. This is supported by one reported occasion of revelation: a man of Ghaṭafān held a large sum belonging to his nephew; when the nephew matured and asked for his father's property, his uncle refused, and the verse was revealed. Hearing it, the uncle said: “We obey God and His Messenger, and seek refuge with God from great sin ( الحوب الكبير ).” [N003] Others say that Arabs had prevented children from inheriting alongside adults, and were ordered to give them their inheritance. On this account “orphan” retains its primary meaning. According to the first explanation the addressees are guardians ( الأوصياء ); according to the second, Arabs who did not give children their inheritance. “Do not exchange the bad for the good”: do not substitute unlawful property taken from orphans for lawful property belonging to you; or do not take their valuable things and hand over your inferior things in exchange. Some would substitute a thin sheep of their own for a fat sheep belonging to the orphan, or a counterfeit dirham for a sound one. “Do not eat their property along with your own”: do not add their property to yours and spend the two together, while the orphan does not consume as much as an adult—except where the expenditure has been proportioned to the orphan's consumption or is for legitimate benefit. “That,” meaning such consumption, “is a great ḥūb ”: a grave sin.","anchor":"en-q4-2-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-2-s3","r":"q4-2","title":"The alchemy of spiritual education and receiving every seeker","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—commands those enriched in their hearts, the great friends of God rooted in knowledge of the unseen ( أغنياء القلوب ), to give those attached to them, including the poor and weak, of the wealth-in-God which God has granted them, until they look to none besides Him. They should receive whoever comes to them, whether belonging to love and affection or to resistance and obstinacy. They must not “exchange the bad for the good” by receiving only those they find to have good character and rejecting those of bad character. This does not belong to the people of prophetic spiritual training ( أهل التربية النبوية ). Their way is to receive people on equal terms and transform the very substances ( الأعيان ) within them: the disobedient becomes obedient, the unbeliever a believer, the heedless one a person of remembrance, the miser generous, the impure pure, the evildoer a benefactor, and the ignorant a knower of God. They possess the elixir ( الإكسير ), the primordial wine ( الخمرة الأزلية ), whose property is to transform substances, as Ibn al-Fāriḍ says in describing it: It refines the manners of the drinking companions, so that through it One without resolve is guided to the path of resolve; The hand that never knew generosity becomes open-handed, And one without forbearance becomes forbearing in anger. His words, “Do not consume their property along with your own,” mean here: wait until you have ascertained that wealth of heart has reached them. Once you have ascertained this, accept from the property they freely offer you. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-2-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-2-s4","r":"q4-2","title":"","text":"When some guardians had an orphan girl with property under their care, they might fear an outsider entering the household, so they married her themselves or to their sons to gain her property, without giving her a just bridal gift ( صداق ), and might mistreat her in expectation of her death. God prohibited this, saying:","anchor":"en-q4-2-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-3","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states 4:3","anchor":"unit-q4-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-1","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلاَّ تُقْسِطُوا فِي الْيَتامى فَانْكِحُوا ما طابَ لَكُمْ مِنَ النِّساءِ مَثْنى وَثُلاثَ وَرُباعَ فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلاَّ تَعْدِلُوا فَواحِدَةً أَوْ ما مَلَكَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ ذلِكَ أَدْنى أَلاَّ تَعُولُوا (3)","anchor":"ar-q4-3-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-2","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"قلت: «ما» من شأنها أن تقع على ما لا يعقل، وهنا وقعت على النساء لقلة عقلهن حتى التحَقْنَ بمن لا يعقل (١) و (مثْنَى وثُلاثَ ورُباع) أحوال من (ما) ممنوعة من الصرف للوصف والعدل، أي: اثنتين اثنتين، وثلاثاً ثلاثاً، وأربعًا أربعا.","anchor":"ar-q4-3-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-3","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ يا معشر الأولياء ألاَّ تعدلوا فِي الْيَتامى التي تحت حجركم إذا تزوجتم بهن طلبًا لمالهن، مع قلة جمالهن، فتهجروهن أو تسيئوا عشرتهن، فَانْكِحُوا ما طابَ لَكُمْ من غيرهن، أو: وإن خفتم ألا تقسطوا في صداقهن إذا أعجبنكم لِمَالِهنّ- الذي بيدكم- وجمالهن، فانكحوا غيرهن، ولا تنكحوهن إلا إذا أعطيتموهن صداق أمثالهن.","anchor":"ar-q4-3-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-4","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"قالت عائشة- رضى الله عنها-: (هي اليتيمة تكون في حِجر وليها، فيرغب في مالها وجمالها، ويريد أن ينكحها بأدنى صداقها، فنُهوا أن ينكحوهن إلا أن يقسطوا لهن في إكمال الصداق، وأُمِروا أن ينكحوا ما سواهن من النساء.) . رواه البخاري.","anchor":"ar-q4-3-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-5","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"وقال ابن عباس رضي الله عنه: - (إن الرجل منهم كان يتزوج العشرة وأكثر- يعني قبل التحريم- فإذا ضاق ماله أخذ من مال يتيمه) ، فقال لهم: إن خفتم ألا تقسطوا في اليتامى- أي: في أموالهن- فانكحوا ما طاب لكم من غيرهن (مَثْنى وَثُلاثَ وَرُباعَ أي: اثنتين اثنتين لكل واحدٍ، أو ثلاثاً ثلاثاً، أو أربعًا أربعًا، ولا تزيدوا، فمنع ما كان في الجاهلية من الزيادة على الأربع، وهو مُجمع عليه بنص الآية، ولا عبرة بمن جوَّز تسعًا لظاهر الآية لأن المراد التخيير بين تلك الأعداد، لا الجمع، ولو أراد الجمع لقال تسعًا، ولم يعدل عن ذلك إلى ما هو أطول منه وأقل بيانًا.","anchor":"ar-q4-3-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-6","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلَّا تَعْدِلُوا بين الاثنتين أو الثلاث أو الأربع، فاقتصروا على واحدة، أو على مَّا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ مِّن قليل أو كثير إذ لا يجب العدل بينهن، ذلِكَ الاقتصار على الواحدة أَدْنى أي: أقرب أَلَّا تَعُولُوا أي:","anchor":"ar-q4-3-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-7","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"تجوروا أو تميلوا، أو ألا تجاوزوا ما فرض عليكم من العدل، أو أدنى ألا يكثر عيالكم فتفتقروا، وهي لغة حِمْيَر. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-3-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-8","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الحق تعالى جعل أولياءه أصنافاً عديدة فمنهم من غلب عليه فيض العلوم، ومنهم من غلب عليه هجوم الأحوال، ومنهم من غلب عليه تحقيق المقامات. قال الشيخ أبو العباس المرسى رضي الله عنه: كان الجنيد رضي الله عنه قطبًا في العلوم، وكان أبو يزيد رضي الله عنه قطباً في الأحوال، وكان سهل بن عبد الله قطبًا في المقامات. هـ. أي: كل واحد غلب عليه واحد من ذلك، مع مشاركته للآخر في الباقي، فينبغي لكل واحد أن يخوض في فنِّه الذي خصَّه الله به ولا يتصدى لغيره. فقال لهم الحق- جل جلاله- من طريق الإشارة: فإن خفتم يا مَنْ غلبت عليهم الأحوال أو المقامات، أَلاَّ تُقسطوا في يتامى العلوم التي اختص بها غيركم، فانكحوا ما طاب لكم من ثيبات الأحوال وأبكار الحقائق، كثيرة أو قليلة، فإن خفتم أن تغلبكم الأحوال، أو التنزل في المقامات، ولا تعدلوا فيها، فالزموا حالة واحدة ومقامًا واحدًا، وهو المقام الذي ملكه وتحقق به، فإنه أقرب ألا ينحرف عن الاعتدال لأن كثرة الأحوال تضر بالمريد كما هو مقرر في فنه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-3-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-3-9","r":"q4-3","title":"4:3 — Justice toward orphan girls, marriage limits and restraint in spiritual states","text":"ولما أمر بالنكاح أمر ببذل الصداق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-3-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-3-s1","r":"q4-3","title":"Mā (ما), the distributive numerals and the rhetorical construction","text":"I say: The relative particle mā ( ما ) normally designates what is not rational, whereas here it refers to women. Ibn ʿAjība explains this in terms of women's alleged deficiency of intellect, as though they were assimilated to non-rational beings. “Two, three and four” ( مَثْنى وَثُلاثَ وَرُباعَ ) are circumstantial qualifiers ( أحوال ) of mā , excluded from full declension for two reasons ( ممنوعة من الصرف ): being descriptive and modified from their simple numerical form ( الوصف والعدل ). Their meaning is distributive: two by two, three by three and four by four. [N004]","anchor":"en-q4-3-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-3-s2","r":"q4-3","title":"Orphan girls, bridal gifts and the maximum of four wives","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—says: “If you fear,” guardians, “that you will not deal justly with orphan girls” under your charge by marrying them in pursuit of their wealth when you find them less beautiful, and then abandoning or ill-treating them, “marry other women who please you.” Alternatively: If you fear that you will fail to give those orphans a just bridal gift when they attract you through their property, which is already in your hands, and their beauty, marry others instead; do not marry them unless you pay a bridal gift like that given to their equals. ʿĀʾisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “This refers to an orphan girl in the custody of her guardian. He desires her wealth and beauty and wishes to marry her for less than a proper bridal gift. They were therefore prohibited from marrying such girls unless they gave the full, just bridal gift; they were commanded to marry women other than them.” Al-Bukhārī transmits the report. [H003] Ibn ʿAbbās said that previously a man might marry ten or more women; if he became short of money he would take from the property of an orphan in his care. Thus the verse prohibited that injustice. “Two, three or four” means that each man may marry two or three or four, and not more. The verse prohibits the pre-Islamic practice of exceeding four, and consensus ( الإجماع ) is established upon this limit. Those who would allow nine by treating the numbers as additive should not be heeded: the purpose is to offer alternatives, not to sum the numbers. Were addition intended, the text would simply say “nine,” rather than choosing a longer and less explicit expression. “If you fear that you will not act justly” between two, three or four wives, restrict yourselves to one, or to whatever number of enslaved women your right hands possess: he holds that the same equality requirement is not obligatory in that latter case. “That,” namely limiting oneself to one, “is nearer to your not turning aside ( تَعُولُوا ),” that is, not wronging others or inclining unjustly, or not exceeding what has been required of fairness. It can also mean, in the Ḥimyarite dialect, not burdening yourselves with a large household that brings poverty. And God knows best. [N005]","anchor":"en-q4-3-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-3-s3","r":"q4-3","title":"Each guide should remain within his gift: knowledge, states or stations","text":"Know that God Most High has given His friends differing specializations. Some are distinguished by an overflowing of sciences ( فيض العلوم ), others by an irruption of spiritual states ( هجوم الأحوال ), and yet others by the verification of spiritual stations ( تحقيق المقامات ). The shaykh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mursī said: “Al-Junayd was a pole ( قطب ) in the sciences; Abū Yazīd a pole in states; and Sahl ibn ʿAbd Allāh a pole in stations.” Each specialized in one while partaking also of the other two. Everyone should pursue the field in which God has specially gifted him, without taking responsibility for what belongs to another. Thus, by way of allusion, the Real says to those whose predominant gift is states or stations: “If you fear that you will not treat fairly the orphan girls of the sciences ( يتامى العلوم )”—the branches of knowledge specially entrusted to others—“then marry” the mature women of states and the virgin realities ( ثيبات الأحوال وأبكار الحقائق ) proper to you, whether few or many. If you fear that an excess of states or a descent among stations will overcome you and prevent balance, remain with one state and one station, the station you actually possess and have verified. That is nearer to your not deviating from equilibrium, for too many changing states can harm the seeker ( المريد ), as is explained in the discipline. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-3-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-3-s4","r":"q4-3","title":"","text":"Having commanded marriage, He then commanded the giving of the bridal gift.","anchor":"en-q4-3-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-4","r":"q4-4","title":"4:4 — Bridal gifts, willing relinquishment and the rights of the self","text":"4:4 — Bridal gifts, willing relinquishment and the rights of the self 4:4","anchor":"unit-q4-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-4-1","r":"q4-4","title":"4:4 — Bridal gifts, willing relinquishment and the rights of the self","text":"وَآتُوا النِّساءَ صَدُقاتِهِنَّ نِحْلَةً فَإِنْ طِبْنَ لَكُمْ عَنْ شَيْءٍ مِنْهُ نَفْساً فَكُلُوهُ هَنِيئاً مَرِيئاً (4)","anchor":"ar-q4-4-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-4-2","r":"q4-4","title":"4:4 — Bridal gifts, willing relinquishment and the rights of the self","text":"قلت: نِحْلَةً: مصدر من آتوهن، لأنها في معنى الإيتاء، يقال: نحله كذا نحلة ونحلا إذا أعطاه إياه عن طيب نفس بلا توقع عوض ولا حكم حاكم، والضمير في «منه» يعود على الصداق أو على «الإيتاء» ، و (نفسًا) تمييز، و (هنيئاً مريئًا) : صفتان لمصدر محذوف، أي: أكلاً هنيئًا، وهو من هَنُؤ الطعام ومَرُؤ، إذا كان سائغًا لا تنغيص فيه، وقيل الهنيء: ما يلذه الإنسان، والمريء: ما تُحمد عاقبته.","anchor":"ar-q4-4-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-4-3","r":"q4-4","title":"4:4 — Bridal gifts, willing relinquishment and the rights of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للأزواج: وَآتُوا النِّساءَ التي تزوجتموهن صَدُقاتِهِنَّ نِحْلَةً أي: عطية مُبتلة (١) ، لا مطل فيها ولا ظلم، فَإِنْ طِبْنَ لَكُمْ عَنْ شَيْءٍ من الصداق، وأعطينه لكم عن طيب أنفسهن فَكُلُوهُ هَنِيئاً لاتبعة عليكم فيه، مَرِيئاً: سائغًا حلالاً لا شبهة فيه، رُوي أن ناسًا كانوا يتحرّجون أن يقبل أحدهم من زوجته شيئًا، فنزلت. وقيل: الخطاب للأولياء، لأن بعضهم كان يأكل صداق محجورته، فأمروا أن يعطوهن صداقهن، إلا إن أعطينَهم شيئًا عن طيب أنفسهن، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-4-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-4-4","r":"q4-4","title":"4:4 — Bridal gifts, willing relinquishment and the rights of the self","text":"الإشارة: وآتوا النفوس حقوقها من الراحة وقوت البشرية، نحلة، ولا تكلفوها فوق طاقتها، فإن طبن لكم عن شيء من الأعمال أو الأحوال، بانشراح صدر ونشاط، فكلوه هنيئًا مريئاً، فإنَّ العبادة مع النشاط والفرح بالله أعظم وأقرب للدوام، وهذا في حق النفوس المطمئنة، وأما النفوس الأمارة فلا يناسبها إلا قهرية المجاهدة مع السياسة لئلا تمل، أو تقول: من أقامه الحق تعالى في حال من الأحوال أو مقام من المقامات فليلزمه، وليقم حيث أقامه الحق، ويعطيه حقه، فإن طاب وقته لحال من الأحوال فليأكله هنيئًا مريئًا. فالفقير ابن وقته، ينظر ما يبرز له فيه من رزقه، فكل ما وجد فيه قلبه فهو رزقه، فليبادر إلى أكله لئلا يفوته رزقه منه. والله تعالى أعلم بأسرار كتابه.","anchor":"ar-q4-4-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-4-5","r":"q4-4","title":"4:4 — Bridal gifts, willing relinquishment and the rights of the self","text":"ثم نهى الأوصياء عن تمكين اليتامى من أموالهم قبل الرشد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-4-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-4-s1","r":"q4-4","title":"Niḥla (نِحلة), nafsan (نفسًا) and hanīʾan marīʾan","text":"I say: Niḥla ( نِحْلَةً ) is a verbal noun ( مصدر ) governed by “give them” ( آتوهن ), since the two have the same sense: one says naḥalahu kadha niḥlatan wa-naḥlan when one gives something gladly, without expecting a return or acting under a judicial command. The pronoun in “something of it” ( منه ) refers either to the bridal gift ( الصداق ) or to the act of giving ( الإيتاء ). “Of their own souls” ( نفسًا ) is an accusative of specification ( تمييز ). “Wholesomely and agreeably” ( هنيئاً مريئًا ) are adjectives qualifying an omitted verbal noun: a wholesome eating ( أكلاً هنيئًا ). These come from the verbs describing food that is easy to swallow and brings no trouble. It is also said that hanīʾ is what gives pleasure, and marīʾ what has a praiseworthy consequence.","anchor":"en-q4-4-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-4-s2","r":"q4-4","title":"Full ownership of the bride’s gift","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—addresses husbands: give the women you have married their bridal gifts ( صَدُقاتِهِنَّ ) as an outright donation ( نِحلة ), without delay or injustice. “If they are pleased to remit to you anything of it”—from the bridal gift, willingly and freely—“then consume it with enjoyment ( هنيئًا ),” without liability, “and agreeably ( مريئًا ),” lawfully, without any suspicious element. It is reported that some people felt religious scruples about accepting anything from their wives, and this verse was revealed. Others say that the addressees are guardians, since some guardians appropriated the bridal gifts of women under their care. They are commanded to hand the gifts over to the women, unless the women willingly offer a portion. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-4-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-4-s3","r":"q4-4","title":"Giving the soul its due without making indulgence its master","text":"Give the selves ( النفوس ) their rights to rest and the sustenance proper to human embodiment, as a freely conceded gift, and do not burden them beyond what they can bear. If the selves willingly undertake some act or spiritual state with an expansive breast and activity, partake of it gladly and wholesomely. Worship undertaken with readiness and joy in God is greater and likelier to endure. This applies to tranquil selves ( النفوس المطمئنة ); as for souls that command evil ( النفوس الأمارة ), nothing fits them but the stern discipline of spiritual striving ( قهرية المجاهدة ), tempered by prudent direction lest they weary. Or the meaning is: whoever God establishes in a particular spiritual state ( حال ) or station ( مقام ) should remain there, stand where the Real has stationed him, and give that state its right. When his appointed moment ( وقته ) becomes pleasant through the arrival of some state, he should enjoy it wholesomely. The poor seeker is the son of his moment ( الفقير ابن وقته ); he observes what provision manifests for him within it. Everything in which his heart finds its nourishment is his provision; let him hasten to take it lest its apportioned benefit pass him by. God Most High knows best the secrets of His Book.","anchor":"en-q4-4-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-4-s4","r":"q4-4","title":"","text":"He then forbade guardians from putting orphans in control of their property before the attainment of sound judgment.","anchor":"en-q4-4-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-5","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets 4:5","anchor":"unit-q4-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-1","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"وَلا تُؤْتُوا السُّفَهاءَ أَمْوالَكُمُ الَّتِي جَعَلَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ قِياماً وَارْزُقُوهُمْ فِيها وَاكْسُوهُمْ وَقُولُوا لَهُمْ قَوْلاً مَعْرُوفاً (5)","anchor":"ar-q4-5-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-2","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"قلت: «قيمًا» (٢) : مصدر قام قيامًا وقيما، وأصله: قوامًا، قلبت الواو ياء.","anchor":"ar-q4-5-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-3","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للأوصياء: وَلا تُؤْتُوا السُّفَهاءَ التي تحت حضانتكم أَمْوالَكُمُ أي: أموالهم التي في أيديكم، وإنما أضاف أموال اليتامى لهم حثًا على حفظها وتنميتها كأنها مال من أموالهم، أي: ولا تمكنوا السفهاء من أموالهم التي جعلها الله في أيديكم قِياماً لمعاشهم، تقومون بها عليهم، ولكن احفظوها، واتجروا فيها، واجعلوا رزقهم وكسوتهم فيها باعتبار العادة، فإن طلبوها منكم فعدوهم وعدًا جميلاً، وَقُولُوا لَهُمْ قَوْلًا مَعْرُوفاً أي: كلامًا لينًا بأن يقول له: حتى تكبر وترشد لتصلح للتصرف فيها. وشبه ذلك. وإنما قال: (وارزقوهم فيها) دون «منها» لأن «فيها» يقتضي بقاءها بالتنمية والتجارة حتى تكون محلاً للرزق والكسوة دون «منها» ، وقيل:","anchor":"ar-q4-5-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-4","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"الخطاب للأزواج، نهاهم أن يعمدوا إلى ما خوّلهم الله من المال فيعطوه إلى نسائهم وأولادهم، ثم ينظرون إلى أيديهم. وإنما سمَّاهن سفهاء استخفافًا بعقلهن، كما عبر عنهن ب- «ما» التي لغير العاقل (١) .","anchor":"ar-q4-5-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-5","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"وروى أبو أمامة عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «إنما خُلقتْ النارُ للسفهاء- قالها ثلاثًا- ألا وإن السفهاءَ النساء إلا امرأة أطاعت قيِّمَها (٢) » . وقالت امرأة: يا رسول الله: سميتنا السفهاء! فقال: «الله تعالى سماكن في كتابه (٣)» ، يشير إلى هذه الآية. وقال أبو موسى الأشعري رضي الله عنه: (ثلاثة يَدْعُون الله فلا يُستجاب لهم: رجل كانت تحته امرأة سيئة الخلق فلم يطلقها (٤) ، ورجل كان له على رجل دين فلم يُشْهِد عليه، ورجل أعطى سفيهًا ماله، وقد قال الله تعالى: وَلا تُؤْتُوا السُّفَهاءَ أَمْوالَكُمُ.) قلت: إنما منعوا من إجابة الدعاء لتفريطهم في مراسم الشريعة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-5-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-6","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"الإشارة: لا ينبغي للشيخ أن يُطلع المريد على أسرار التوحيد، وهي أسرار المعاني التي جعلها الله تعالى قائمة بالأشياء، حتى يكمل عقله، ويتحقق أدبه، ويظهر صدقه، فإذا استعجلها قبل وقتها فليعده وعدًا قريبًا، وليقل له قولاً معروفًا، فكم من مريد استعجل الفتح قبل إبانه فعوقب بحرمانه، وكم من مريد اطلع على أسرار الحقيقة قبل كمال خدمته فطُرد أو قتل، ووقتها هو حين تبرز معه فتأخذه الحيرة، اللهم إلا أن يراه الشيخ أهلاً لحملها لرجحان عقله وكمال صدقه، فيمكنه منها قبل أن تبرز معه، ثم يربيه فيها، وهذا الذي شهدناه من أشياخنا لشدة كرمهم- رضى الله عنهم وأرضاهم- ورزقنا حسن الأدب معهم، فأطلق الحق تعالى الأموال بطريق الإشارة على أسرار المعاني، وأمر الشيوخ أن يرزقوهم منها شيئًا فشيئًا بالتدريب والتدريج، وأن يكسوهم بالشرائع، ويحتمل أن تبقى الأموال","anchor":"ar-q4-5-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-7","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"على ظاهرها، ويكون أمر الشيوخ أن يمنعوا المريدين من أخذ الأموال قبل التمكين. أشار إلى هذا الورتجبي، فانظره.","anchor":"ar-q4-5-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-5-8","r":"q4-5","title":"4:5 — Guarding the resources of the vulnerable and the gradual transmission of secrets","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى وقت دفع أموال اليتامى لهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-5-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-5-s1","r":"q4-5","title":"Qiyāman (قيامًا): property as support","text":"I say: Qiyāman ( قِيَامًا ) is the verbal noun of qāma ( قام ), also qīman ( قِيمًا ); its underlying form is qiwāman ( قوامًا ), with the wāw changed into yāʾ. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-18] ]","anchor":"en-q4-5-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-5-s2","r":"q4-5","title":"Preserving capital and providing support","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—addresses guardians: “Do not give the people without sound judgment ( السفهاء )” who are under your protection “your property,” meaning their property which is held in your hands. Their property is attributed to you to exhort you to preserve and increase it as carefully as if it were your own. Do not allow them uncontrolled access to their wealth before they are fit to manage it. God has made the property the means of sustaining their livelihoods ( قيامًا لمعاشهم ), and entrusted you with their support. Preserve it, trade with it, and make the provision of their food and clothing appropriate to customary needs. If they demand it before the proper time, promise them kindly; say with gentle speech, “When you have grown up and attained discernment ( رشد ) you will be able to handle it,” or the like. He says “provide for them in it” ( فيها ) rather than “ from it” ( منها ), because the former suggests that the wealth should remain as an ongoing source of support, preserved and increased through trade, rather than consumed as a diminishing principal. Another view holds that the address is to husbands: they are forbidden to hand over all the resources God granted them to their wives and children and then become dependent upon them. Ibn ʿAjība presents this view in terms of a dismissive estimate of women’s intellect, comparing the use of the relative particle mā in the previous verse. He transmits from Abū Umāma a report attributed to the Prophet: “The Fire was created for the foolish [CP21] ,” repeated three times, “and the foolish are women, except the woman who obeys the one responsible for her.” A woman, he says, objected: “Messenger of God, you have called us the foolish!” and he answered that God had used this designation in the Book. [H004] Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī is also reported as saying: “Three people call upon God without receiving a response: a man with a woman of bad conduct whom he does not divorce; a man who lends money without having it witnessed; and a man who places his wealth in the hands of someone incapable of sound judgment—when God has said, ‘Do not give the foolish your property.’” [H005] I say: their prayers are not granted because they have neglected the appointed requirements ( مراسم ) of the Law. God knows best. [N006]","anchor":"en-q4-5-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-5-s3","r":"q4-5","title":"The right moment to disclose metaphysical understanding","text":"A shaykh should not disclose to the disciple ( المريد ) the secrets of divine unity ( أسرار التوحيد )—the secrets of meanings that God Most High has made subsist in things—until the disciple's intellect matures, his manners ( أدب ) become sound, and his sincerity becomes manifest. If he demands those secrets before their proper time, the shaykh should promise him what is near and speak to him encouragingly. How often has the disciple who hastened an opening ( الفتح ) before its time been punished by being deprived of it! How often has one who gained insight into the secrets of Reality ( الحقيقة ) before completing the requisite service been expelled, or even killed! The time to communicate them is when they begin to disclose themselves and bring him to a state of bewilderment ( الحيرة ). There is an exception if the shaykh judges him ready to bear them through the strength of his intellect and the perfection of his sincerity. Then he can show them before they emerge of themselves, and train him within them. This is what we witnessed from our shaykhs, so generously did they give. May God be pleased with them, and grant us beautiful manners in their company. Thus the Real uses “wealth” by way of allusion for the secrets of meanings. He commands teachers to give their students something of these, little by little, through training and gradual progression ( التدريب والتدريج ), and to clothe them in the outward prescriptions of the Law ( الشرائع ). It is also possible to retain “property” in its literal sense and to read the injunction as forbidding shaykhs to let disciples acquire wealth before firm establishment ( التمكين ). Al-Wartajbī alludes to this interpretation; consult his discussion.","anchor":"en-q4-5-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-5-s4","r":"q4-5","title":"","text":"God Most High then specifies the time for handing orphans their property.","anchor":"en-q4-5-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-6","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir 4:6","anchor":"unit-q4-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-1","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"وَابْتَلُوا الْيَتامى حَتَّى إِذا بَلَغُوا النِّكاحَ فَإِنْ آنَسْتُمْ مِنْهُمْ رُشْداً فَادْفَعُوا إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوالَهُمْ وَلا تَأْكُلُوها إِسْرافاً وَبِداراً أَنْ يَكْبَرُوا وَمَنْ كانَ غَنِيًّا فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ وَمَنْ كانَ فَقِيراً فَلْيَأْكُلْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ فَإِذا دَفَعْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوالَهُمْ فَأَشْهِدُوا عَلَيْهِمْ وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ حَسِيباً (6)","anchor":"ar-q4-6-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-2","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"قلت: الابتلاء: الاختبار، و «آنس:» أبصر. والرشد هو كمال العقل بحيث يعرف مصالح نفسه وتدبير ماله من غير تبذير ولا إفساد. وإِسْرافاً وَبِداراً: حالان من «الواو» ، أو مفعولان لأجله، و (أن يكبروا) مفعول ببدارا.","anchor":"ar-q4-6-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-3","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للأوصياء: واختبروا الْيَتامى قبل البلوغ بتتبع أحوالهم في تصرفاتهم، بأن يُدفع لهم الدرهم والدرهمان، فإن ظهر عليهم حسن التصرف زادهم قليلاً قليلا، وإن ظهر عليهم التبذير كفَّ عنهم المال، حَتَّى إِذا بَلَغُوا النِّكاحَ، وهو البلوغ بعلامته، فَإِنْ آنَسْتُمْ أي: أبصرتم مِنْهُمْ رُشْداً، وهو المعرفة بمصالحه وتدبير ماله، وإن لم يكن من أهل الدين- واشترطه قوم، فَادْفَعُوا إِلَيْهِمْ حينئِذ أَمْوالَهُمْ من غير تأخير. وَلا تَأْكُلُوها إِسْرافاً وَبِداراً أَنْ يَكْبَرُوا أي: لا تأكلوها مسرفين ومبادرين كبرهم فتزول من يدكم، أو لإسرافكم ومبادرتكم كبرهم، وَمَنْ كانَ غَنِيًّا فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ عن أكلها في أجرة قيامه بها، وَمَنْ كانَ فَقِيراً فَلْيَأْكُلْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ بقدر حاجته وأجر سعيه، وعنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: أنَّ رجُلاً قال لهُ: إنَّ في حجْرِي يتَيمًا أفآكُلُ مِنْ مَالِهِ؟","anchor":"ar-q4-6-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-4","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"قال: «بالمعْرُوفِ، غَيْرَ مُتأثِّلٍ (١) مَالاً ولا وَاقٍ مَالَكَ بمَالِه» .","anchor":"ar-q4-6-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-5","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"فَإِذا دَفَعْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوالَهُمْ فَأَشْهِدُوا في قبضها منكم عَلَيْهِمْ، فإنه أنفى للتهمة وأبعدُ من الخصومة، وهو ندب، وقيل: فرض، فلا يصدق في الدفع إلا ببينة، وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ حَسِيباً أي: محاسبًا، فلا تخالفوا ما أمرتم به، ولا تجاوزوا ما حدّ لكم.","anchor":"ar-q4-6-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-6","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"وإنما قال: «حسيبًا» ولم يقل: «شهيدًا» ، مع مناسبته، تهديدًا للأوصياء لئلا يكتموا شيئًا من مال اليتامى، فإذا علموا أن الله يحاسبهم على النقير والقطمير، ويعاقبهم عليه، انزجروا عن الكتمان. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-6-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-7","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"الإشارة: ينبغي للشيخ أن يختبر المريد في معرفته وتحقيق بغيته، فإذا بلغ مبلغ الرجال وتحققت فيه أوصاف الكمال، بحيث تحقق فناؤه، وكمل بقاؤه، وتمت معرفته، فيكون تصرفه كله بالله ومن الله وإلى الله، يَفهم عن الله في كل شيء، ويأخذ النصيب من كل شيء، ولا يأخذ من نصيبه شيئًا، قد تحلَّى بحلية الورع، وزال عنه الجزع والطمع، وزال عن قلبه خوف الخلق وهَمُّ الرزق، واكتفى بنظر المَلِك الحق، يأخذ الحقيقة من معدنها، والشريعة من موضعها، فإذا تحققت فيه هذه الأمور، وأنس رشده، فليُطلقُ له التصرف في نفسه، وليأمره بتربية غيره، إن رآه أهلاً لذلك، ولا ينبغي أن يحجر عليه بعد ظهور رشده، ولا يسرف عليه في الخدمة قبل رشده، مخافة أن يزول من يده.","anchor":"ar-q4-6-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-8","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"فإن كان غنيًا عن خدمته فليستعفف عنه، وليجعل تربيته لله اقتداء بأنبياء الله. قال تعالى: قُلْ لا أَسْأَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ أَجْراً وَما أَسْأَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍ، وإن كان محتاجًا إليها فليستخدمه بالمعروف، ولا يكلفه ما يشق عليه، فإذا دفع إليه السر، وتمكن منه، وأمره بالتربية أو التذكير فليشهد له بذلك، ويوصي بخلافته عنه، كي تطمِئن القلوب بالأخذ عنه، (وَكَفَى بِاللَّهِ وَلِيّاً وَكَفَى به نصيرا) .","anchor":"ar-q4-6-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-6-9","r":"q4-6","title":"4:6 — Testing for maturity, the guardian’s expenses and the discernment of a spiritual heir","text":"ولمّا أمر الحق تعالى بحفظ أموال اليتامى أمر بحفظ أموال النساء، وذكرهن بعدهم لمشاركتهن لهم فى الضعف، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-6-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-6-s1","r":"q4-6","title":"Testing (ابتلاء), perception (إيناس) and the accusatives of cause","text":"I say: Ibtilāʾ ( الابتلاء ) means testing or examination ( الاختبار ); ānas ( آنس ) means perceived or saw ( أبصر ). Sound judgment ( الرشد ) is the completion of intellectual maturity such that a person recognizes his own interests and manages property without extravagance or corruption. “Extravagantly” ( إسرافًا ) and “in haste” ( بِدارًا ) may be circumstantial accusatives ( حالان ) describing the subject pronoun in the verb, or accusatives expressing purpose or motive ( مفعولان لأجله ). “Lest they grow up” ( أن يكبروا ) is the object of “hastening” ( بدارًا ).","anchor":"en-q4-6-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-6-s2","r":"q4-6","title":"Testing, investment and the proper use of orphan wealth","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—addresses guardians: test the orphans before they attain maturity by observing their conduct in handling wealth. Give them a dirham or two: if good management appears, increase what you entrust to them gradually; if wastefulness appears, withhold the property. “Until they reach the age of marriage,” meaning puberty as established by its legal signs; “then if you perceive sound judgment in them”—ability to understand their interests and manage property, even if they are not religiously upright ( أهل الدين ), although some made the latter a condition—“hand their wealth over to them,” without delay. “Do not consume it wastefully, hastening before they grow up”: do not consume it while being extravagant or hastening to use it up before maturity removes it from your hands; or do not consume it out of extravagant desire and eagerness before they grow. “Let the wealthy guardian abstain” from taking compensation from the wealth for administering it. “Let the poor one consume according to what is recognized as proper ( بالمعروف ),” to the extent of his need and the recompense due for his labor. A man is reported to have asked the Prophet: “I have an orphan under my care; may I eat from his property?” He replied: “According to what is right, without accumulating wealth from it, nor protecting your own property by expending his.” [H006] “When you hand their wealth over,” have witnesses attend their receipt of it from you. That removes suspicion and reduces litigation. Some take witnessing to be recommended ( ندب ), while others regard it as obligatory ( فرض ) and will not accept a guardian's assertion of payment without evidence. “God suffices as Reckoner ( حسيب )”: do not violate His commandments or exceed the limits He has set. He says “Reckoner” ( حسيب ) rather than “Witness” ( شهيد ), though the latter might seem particularly fitting, as a warning to guardians not to conceal any of the property. Once they know that God will reckon with them even over the tiniest scrap ( النقير والقطمير ), and will punish them for it, they will be deterred from concealment. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-6-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-6-s3","r":"q4-6","title":"When the teacher should release the disciple to act and to teach","text":"The spiritual teacher should test the disciple in his knowledge and in the realization of what he seeks. When he has reached maturity and the qualities of perfection become evident—his effacement ( فناؤه ) realized, his subsistence ( بقاؤه ) complete, and his knowledge of God ( معرفته ) perfected—so that his every action takes place by God, from God and toward God, he understands what comes from God in everything. He receives the allotted portion of every thing without taking for himself anything from his portion. He is adorned with scrupulous restraint ( الورع ); agitation ( الجزع ) and covetousness ( الطمع ) have passed away; fear of creatures and anxiety about livelihood have disappeared from his heart; and the regard of the True King has become sufficient for him. He takes Reality ( الحقيقة ) from its proper source and the Law ( الشريعة ) from its proper place. When these marks appear and his good judgment has been discerned, the shaykh should allow him to act for himself; indeed, if he judges him suitable, he may charge him with training others. After his maturity has become evident he should not continue to restrict him, nor demand excessive service before maturity in fear that the disciple will slip from his grasp. If the shaykh has no need of the student's service, let him abstain from it and make his training purely for God's sake, following the prophets, for the Qurʾān says, “I ask you no reward for it,” and, “I ask you no fee.” If he needs his service, let him use it only in what is fitting ( بالمعروف ), without requiring what brings hardship. When he entrusts the spiritual secret ( السرّ ) to him, the disciple becomes firmly established in it, and he charges him with teaching or reminding others, let him witness and acknowledge this, commending him as a successor ( خلافة ) so hearts may be at peace in learning from him: “God suffices as Protector, and God suffices as Helper.”","anchor":"en-q4-6-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-6-s4","r":"q4-6","title":"","text":"Having commanded the protection of orphans' wealth, the Real commands that women’s property be protected. He mentions them next on account of their shared vulnerability in the arrangements he is discussing.","anchor":"en-q4-6-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-7","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance 4:7","anchor":"unit-q4-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-1","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"لِلرِّجالِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا تَرَكَ الْوالِدانِ وَالْأَقْرَبُونَ وَلِلنِّساءِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا تَرَكَ الْوالِدانِ وَالْأَقْرَبُونَ مِمَّا قَلَّ مِنْهُ أَوْ كَثُرَ نَصِيباً مَفْرُوضاً (7)","anchor":"ar-q4-7-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-2","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"قلت: جملة مِمَّا قَلَّ.. الخ، بدل (مما ترك) ، و «نصيبًا» : مصدر مؤكد كقوله: فَرِيضَةً مِنَ اللَّهِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4-7-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-3","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"نصب لهم نصيبًا مقطوعًا، أو حال، أو على الاختصاص، أعني: نصيبًا مقطوعًا.","anchor":"ar-q4-7-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-4","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وإذا مات ميت وترك مالاً فللرجال نصيب مما ترك آباؤهم وأقاربهم، وللنساء نصيب مما ترك والدهن وأقاربهن كالإخوة والأخوات، مما ترك ذلك الميت قل أو كثر، (نصيبًا مفروضًا) واجبًا محتمًا.","anchor":"ar-q4-7-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-5","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"رُوِيَ أنَّ أَوْسَ بنَ ثَابتِ الأنْصَارِيَّ تُوفِيَّ، وتَركَ امرأة يقال لها: (أم كَحَّة) وثلاثّ بناتٍ، فأخذ ابْنَا عَمّ الميتِ المَالَ، ولم يُعْطيا المرأَة ولا بَنَاتِه شيئًا، وكان أَهلُ الجَاهلِيَّة لا يُورِّثُون النِّسَاءَ ولا الصغيرَ ولو كان ذكرًا، ويقولون:","anchor":"ar-q4-7-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-6","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"إنما يَرث مَنْ يُحارب ويَذب عن الموروث، فجاءت أمُ كحة إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وهو في مسجد الفضيخ، فقالت:","anchor":"ar-q4-7-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-7","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"يا رسول الله إن أوس بن ثابت مات، وترك بنات ثلاثًا، وأنا امرأته، وليس عندى ما أُنْفقُه عَليهنّ، وقد تَرَك أبُوهُن مالاً حسنًا، وهو عند سُويْدٍ وعَرْفَجَة، فَدَعاهُما النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فقالا: يا رسول الله ولَدُها لا يَركُب فَرسًا، ولا يَحْمِل سِلاَحًا، لا ينُكأ عَدُوًّا، فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «انْصَرِفُوا حتى أرى ما يُحدِثُ الله تعالى» ، فانْصرَفُوا. فنزلت الآية. فأثبت الله لهن في الآية حقًا، ولم يبين كم هو- فأرسل النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم إلى سُويد وعَرفجَة: «لا تُفرقا مِنْ مَال أوْسٍ شَيئًا، فَإنّ الله تعالى جَعَل لِبنَاتِه نَصِيبًا، ولم يبَّين كم هو حتى أنظُرَ ما يُنزل الله تعالى» ، فأنزل الله تعالى بعدُ: يُوصِيكُمُ اللَّهُ فِي أَوْلادِكُمْ.. إلى قوله ... الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ. فأرسل إليهما: «أن ادفعا إلى أم كحة الثُّمْن، وإلى بناته الثُّلثين، ولكما باقي المال» .","anchor":"ar-q4-7-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-8","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"الإشارة: كما جعل الله للنساء نصيبًا من الميراث الحسي جعل لهن نصيبًا من الميراث المعنوي، وهو السر، إن صحبتْ أهل السر، وكان لها أبو الروحانية، وهو الشيخ، فللرجال نصيب مما ترك لهم أشياخهم من سر الولاية، وللنساء كذلك على قدر ما سبق في القسمة الأزلية، قليلة كانت أو كثيرة، نصيبًا مفروضًا معينًا في علم الله وقدره، وقد سواهن الله تعالى مع الرجال في آية السير، فقال: إِنَّ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وَالْمُسْلِماتِ وَالْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِناتِ إلى آخر الآية، فمَنْ صار منهن مع الرجال أدرك ما أدركوا. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4-7-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-7-9","r":"q4-7","title":"4:7 — The right of women to inherit and their share in spiritual inheritance","text":"ثم أمر الورثة بالإحسان إلى من حضر معهم القسمة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-7-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-7-s1","r":"q4-7","title":"A substitutive phrase and a fixed allotted portion","text":"I say: “Whether little or much of it” ( مِمَّا قَلَّ …), etc., is a substitute ( بدل ) for “of what was left” ( مِمَّا تَرَكَ ). “An allotted share” ( نصيبًا ) is a confirming verbal noun ( مصدر مؤكّد ), like “an obligation from God” ( فريضة من الله ): He establishes for them a fixed, prescribed portion. Alternatively it is circumstantial ( حال ) or an accusative of specification ( اختصاص ): “I mean a fixed share.”","anchor":"en-q4-7-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-7-s2","r":"q4-7","title":"The inheritance rights of women and minors","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—says: when someone dies leaving property, men are entitled to a portion of what their parents and relatives have left, and women are equally entitled to a portion of what their parents and relatives—including brothers and sisters—have left, whether the estate is small or large. It is “a prescribed share,” compulsory and inescapable. It is related that Aws ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī died leaving a wife, Umm Kaḥḥa, and three daughters. His two male cousins appropriated the estate, giving neither wife nor daughters anything. In the Jāhiliyya, it is said, women and minors—even male minors—were denied inheritance on the ground that the inheritor should be someone who fights and defends the deceased's interests. Umm Kaḥḥa came to the Messenger of God in the mosque of al-Faḍīkh and said: “Messenger of God, Aws ibn Thābit has died, leaving three daughters; I am his wife and have nothing with which to maintain them. Their father left a good estate, but it is in the hands of Suwayd and ʿArfaja.” The Prophet summoned them. They replied: “Her children do not ride horses, bear weapons or injure enemies.” He said: “Depart, until I see what God Most High brings about.” According to the account, the verse then descended and established a right without yet specifying its amount. The Prophet sent word to Suwayd and ʿArfaja: “Distribute nothing from Aws's estate. God Most High has allotted a share to his daughters but has not yet declared its amount, so I shall wait to see what He reveals.” Then “God enjoins upon you concerning your children” (4:11), through “the great victory” (4:13), was revealed. He summoned them again: “Give Umm Kaḥḥa an eighth, the daughters two-thirds, and retain the remainder.” [N008]","anchor":"en-q4-7-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-7-s3","r":"q4-7","title":"The secret of sainthood is available to women","text":"Just as God gives women a portion of material inheritance, so He gives them a portion of spiritual inheritance ( الميراث المعنوي ), namely the secret ( السرّ ), when they keep company with the people of the secret and have a spiritual father ( أبو الروحانية ), the shaykh. Men receive an allotted portion of what their shaykhs leave them of the secret of sainthood ( سرّ الولاية ), and women likewise receive according to what the primordial apportioning ( القسمة الأزلية ) ordained for them, whether little or much, a share fixed in God's knowledge and decree. God has placed women alongside men in the verse concerning spiritual wayfaring: “The Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women ...” (Q 33:35). A woman who reaches their station attains what they attain. And success is through God.","anchor":"en-q4-7-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-7-s4","r":"q4-7","title":"","text":"He then commanded those receiving inheritance to show generosity toward people present at the division.","anchor":"en-q4-7-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-8","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge 4:8","anchor":"unit-q4-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-1","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"وَإِذا حَضَرَ الْقِسْمَةَ أُولُوا الْقُرْبى وَالْيَتامى وَالْمَساكِينُ فَارْزُقُوهُمْ مِنْهُ وَقُولُوا لَهُمْ قَوْلاً مَعْرُوفاً (8)","anchor":"ar-q4-8-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-2","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"قلت: الضمير في (منه) : يعود على المقسوم المفهوم من القسمة.","anchor":"ar-q4-8-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-3","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا حَضَرَ معكم في قسمة التركة ذَوو القرابة مِمَّنْ لا يرث، كالأخوال والخالات والعمات، وَالْيَتامى وَالْمَساكِينُ، فَارْزُقُوهُمْ أي: فأعطوهم شيئًا من المال المقسوم تطييبًا لقلوبهم.","anchor":"ar-q4-8-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-4","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"فإن كان المال لغيركم، أو كان الورثة غيرَ بالغين، فقولوا لهم قَوْلًا مَعْرُوفاً، بأن تُعلموهم أن المال لغيرنا، ولو كان لنا لأعطيناكم، والله يرزقنا وإياكم.","anchor":"ar-q4-8-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-5","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"واختلف في هذا الأمر، هل للندب- وهو المشهور- أو للوجوب ونسخ بآية المواريث؟ وقيل: لم يُنسخ، وهي مما تهاون الناس بها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-8-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-6","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لخواص أحبابه: إذا دارت الكؤوس بخمرة الملك القدوس، وتعاطيتم قسمتها بين أرواحكم حتى امتلأت جميعُ أشباحكم، وروت منها عُروقكم، وحضر معكم من ليس من أبناء جنسكم، ممن لا يُحل شرْب خمرتكم، فإن كان من أهل المحبة والوداد، أو من له بكم قرابة واستناد، فلا تحرموه من شراب خمرتكم، ولا من نفحات نسمتكم، فإنكم قوم لا يشقى جليسكم، فارزقوه من ثمار علومكم، واسقوه من شراب خمرتكم، وذكَّروه بالله، وقولوا له ما يدله على الله، ويوصله إلى حضرة الله، وهذا هو القول المعروف، الذي هو بالنصح موصوف.","anchor":"ar-q4-8-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-7","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"رُوِي أن أبا هريرة رضي الله عنه نادى في سوق المدينة: يا معشر التجار، اذهبوا إلى المسجد، فإنَّ تركة مُحمدٍ تقسم فيه، لتأخذوا حقكم منها مع الناس قبل أن تنفد، فذهب التُجَّارُ إلى المسجد النبوي، فوجدوه معمورًا بالناس، بعضهم يُصلي، وبعضهم يتلو، وبعضهم يذكر، وبعضهم يعلم العلم، فقالوا: يا أبا هريرة، ليس هنا ما ذكرت من قسم التركة! فقال لهم: (هذه تركة محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم، لا ما أنتم عليه من جمع الأموال) أو كما قال رضي الله عنه.","anchor":"ar-q4-8-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-8-8","r":"q4-8","title":"4:8 — Generosity at the distribution of inheritance and the legacy of knowledge","text":"ثم حثّ الأوصياء على الرفق بأولاد الناس، الذي هم فى حجرهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-8-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-8-s1","r":"q4-8","title":"The antecedent of minhu (منه)","text":"I say: The pronoun in “of it” ( منه ) returns to what is being divided ( المقسوم ), understood from the mention of division ( القسمة ).","anchor":"en-q4-8-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-8-s2","r":"q4-8","title":"Giving an appropriate portion to those present","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—says: when relatives who are not heirs—such as maternal uncles and aunts or paternal aunts—together with orphans and poor people are present as an estate is divided, “provide for them” ( فَارْزُقُوهُمْ ): give them something of the distributed wealth, bringing comfort to their hearts. If the estate belongs to others, or the heirs have not attained maturity, address the visitors kindly instead: explain that the property is not yours to give; had it belonged to you, you would have given, and God provides both for you and them. There is disagreement whether the command expresses recommendation ( الندب )—the well-known view—or obligation ( الوجوب ) later abrogated by the inheritance verses. Others deny abrogation; in their judgment this is a command many people neglect. God knows best. [N009]","anchor":"en-q4-8-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-8-s3","r":"q4-8","title":"Sharing the wine of divine knowledge without violating spiritual propriety","text":"The Real addresses the elect among His beloved: When the cups of wine of the All-Holy Sovereign ( خمرة الملك القدوس ) circulate among you, and you divide the draught between your spirits until your bodily forms are filled and your veins are drenched, and some people who are not of your own spiritual kind are present—people who do not consider drinking your wine lawful—then, if they are people of love and affection, or are connected with you, do not deprive them of your wine or the fragrant breath of your company. You are a company whose companion is not rendered wretched. Give them fruit from your sciences, let them drink from your wine, remind them of God, and speak to them in words directing them to God and bringing them to His Presence. This is the “kind word” ( القول المعروف ), characterized by sincere counsel. It is related that Abū Hurayra once called out in the market of Medina: “Traders, go to the mosque! Muḥammad's inheritance is being distributed there; go claim your share before it is exhausted.” The merchants went to the Prophet's mosque and found it filled with people praying, reciting, remembering God and teaching knowledge. “Abū Hurayra,” they protested, “we found nothing of the inheritance being distributed!” He replied: “That is Muḥammad's inheritance—not your accumulation of money,” or words to that effect. [H007]","anchor":"en-q4-8-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-8-s4","r":"q4-8","title":"","text":"Then He urged guardians to be tender with other people's children under their care.","anchor":"en-q4-8-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-9","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God 4:9","anchor":"unit-q4-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-1","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"وَلْيَخْشَ الَّذِينَ لَوْ تَرَكُوا مِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّةً ضِعافاً خافُوا عَلَيْهِمْ فَلْيَتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَلْيَقُولُوا قَوْلاً سَدِيداً (9)","anchor":"ar-q4-9-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-2","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"قلت: «لَوْ» - هنا- شرطية، تخلص للاستقبال، وجوابها: (خافُوا) ، وحذف مفعول لْيَخْشَ للعموم، فيصدق بخشية العذاب وخشية العتاب وخشية البعد عن الأحباب، على حسب حال المخاطبين بهذه الخشية.","anchor":"ar-q4-9-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-3","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للأوصياء الذين في ولايتهم أولاد الناس: وَلْيَخْشَ الذين يتولون يتامى الناس، فليحفظوا ما لهم، وليحسنوا تنميته لهم ولا يضيعوه، وليخافوا عليهم الضيعة، كما يخافون على أولادهم، فإنهم لو ماتوا وتركوا ذُرِّيَّةً ضِعافاً خافُوا عَلَيْهِمْ، فكما يخافون على أولادهم بعدهم كذلك يخافون على أولاد الناس، فَلْيَتَّقُوا اللَّهَ في شأنهم، وليحفظوا عليهم أموالهم، وليرفقوا بهم ويلاطفوهم في الكلام، كما يُحبون أن يلاطف بأولادهم، وَلْيَقُولُوا لهم قَوْلًا سَدِيداً أي: عدلاً صوابًا بالشفقة وحسن الأدب.","anchor":"ar-q4-9-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-4","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"وقيل: الخطاب لمن حضر المريض عند الإيصاء فيقولون له: قدم لنفسك، أعتق، تصدق، أعط كذا، حتى يستغرق ماله، فنهاهم الحق- تعالى- عن ذلك، وقال لهم: كما تخافون الضيعة على أولادكم بعدكم خافوا على أولاد الناس، فليتقوا الله في أمر المريض بإعطاء ماله كله، وَلْيَقُولُوا له قَوْلًا سَدِيداً: عدلاً، وهو الثلث، وقيل:","anchor":"ar-q4-9-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-5","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"للمؤمنين كلهم عند موتهم، بأن ينظروا للورثة، فلا يسرفوا في الوصية بمجاوزة الثلث. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-9-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-6","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"الإشارة: أمر الحق- جل جلاله- أهل التربية النبوية إذا خافوا على أولادهم الروحانيين أن ينقطعوا بعد موتهم، أن يمدوهم بالمدد الأبهر، ويدلوهم على الغنى الأكبر، حتى يتركوهم أغنياء بالله، قد اكتفوا عن كل أحد سواه، مخافة أن يسقطوا بعد موتهم في يد من يلعب بهم، فليتقوا الله في شأنهم، وليدلوهم على ربهم، وهو القول السديد.","anchor":"ar-q4-9-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-7","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"وينسحب حكمها على أولاد البشرية، فمن خاف على أولاده بعد موته، فليتق الله وليكثر من طاعة الله، وليحسن إلى عباد الله، في أشباحهم وأرواحهم أما أشباحهم فيُطعمهم مما خوله الله، ففي بعض الأثر عنه عليه الصلاة والسلام: «ما أحْسَنَ عَبْدٌ الصَّدَقَةَ في مَاله إلا أحْسَنَ اللهُ الخِلافَةَ عَلَى تَرِكَته» . وأما الإحسان إلى أرواحهم، فيدلهم على الله، ويرشدهم إلى طاعة الله، ويعلمهم أحكام دين الله. فمن فعل هذا تولى الله حفظ ذريته من بعده، فيعيشون في حفظ ورعاية وعز ونصر، كما هو مشاهد في أولاد الصالحين، قال تعالى: وَهُوَ يَتَوَلَّى الصَّالِحِينَ وتذكر قوله تعالى: وَكانَ أَبُوهُما صالِحاً.","anchor":"ar-q4-9-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-8","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"وقال القشيري في هذه الآية: إن الذي ينبغي للمسلم أن يدخر لعياله التقوى والصلاح، لا المال، لأنه لم يقل فليجمعوا لهم المال، وليكثروا لهم العقار والأسباب، وليخلفوا العبيد والأثاث، بل قال: فَلْيَتَّقُوا اللَّهَ فإنه يتولى الصالحين. هـ المراد منه.","anchor":"ar-q4-9-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-9-9","r":"q4-9","title":"4:9 — The moral imagination of guardians, succession and leaving children with God","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى وعيد من يأكل مال اليتيم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-9-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-9-s1","r":"q4-9","title":"Law (لو) and the omitted object of “fear”","text":"I say: Law ( لو ) here is conditional ( شرطية ) and concerns what lies ahead. Its consequent ( جوابها ) is “they would fear” ( خافوا ). The object of “let them fear” ( لْيَخْشَ ) has been omitted for generality: depending on the hearer's state, fear can concern punishment ( العذاب ), reproach ( العتاب ), or distance from the beloved ( البعد عن الأحباب ).","anchor":"en-q4-9-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-9-s2","r":"q4-9","title":"Treat an orphan as you would wish others to treat your child","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—addresses guardians of other people's children. Let them preserve their property, cultivate it for them and avoid wasting it; let them fear the children's destitution as they fear for their own children. If they themselves died leaving vulnerable children, they would fear for them; let them therefore fear for other people's children in the same fashion. “Let them be mindful of God” regarding them, protect their property, treat them gently and address them with tenderness just as they would wish their own children to be treated. “Let them speak sound words” ( قولًا سديدًا ): speech that is just and correct, shaped by compassion and good manners. Another interpretation makes the addressees those visiting a sick person who is composing a will. They urge him to free a slave, give alms, and assign this or that sum until the estate is exhausted. God prohibits such encouragement: as you would fear for your own children, fear for the children of others. Be mindful of God when urging a dying man to dispose of his whole estate; recommend instead an upright and just disposal, namely the one-third allowed for a bequest. A third view makes the address general to believers in their own approach to death: they should consider the heirs, and not overstep the one-third in making bequests. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-9-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-9-s3","r":"q4-9","title":"Preparing spiritual children for the teacher's death","text":"God—majestic is His greatness—commands the people of prophetic spiritual education ( أهل التربية النبوية ), if they fear that their spiritual children will lose their way after the teachers die, to transmit to them the resplendent spiritual assistance ( المدد الأبهر ) and guide them to the greater wealth, that they may be left enriched by God and in need of no one besides Him, lest the disciple later fall into the hands of someone who treats him as a plaything. Let teachers fear God in this and direct their children to their Lord: this is upright speech ( القول السديد ). The same principle extends to children by bodily descent. Whoever fears for his children after death should fear God, multiply acts of obedience and serve God's servants in both their bodily and spiritual dimensions. For their bodily needs he should feed them from what God has bestowed upon him. A report attributes to the Prophet: “Whenever a servant gives charity excellently from his wealth, God makes excellent provision for those left behind in his estate.” [H008] In serving their spirits, he should direct them to God, guide them to obedience and teach them the rulings of religion. Whoever does this, God takes charge of his children after him, and they live under divine protection, care, strength and succor, as may be observed among the children of the righteous. God says, “He is the Protector of the righteous” (Q 7:196), and recall His saying, “Their father was righteous” (Q 18:82). Al-Qushayrī says concerning this verse: What the Muslim should store up for his family is mindfulness of God and righteousness, not mere wealth. It does not say to accumulate property and buildings and means for them, or to leave slaves and furnishings; it says “Let them be mindful of God,” for He guards the righteous. Such is the substance of his words.","anchor":"en-q4-9-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-9-s4","r":"q4-9","title":"","text":"God then spoke of the threat against those who unjustly consume orphan property.","anchor":"en-q4-9-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-10","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority 4:10","anchor":"unit-q4-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-1","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ أَمْوالَ الْيَتامى ظُلْماً إِنَّما يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ نارًا وَسَيَصْلَوْنَ سَعِيراً (10)","anchor":"ar-q4-10-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-2","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"قلت: (ظلمًا) : تمييز، أو مفعول لأجله.","anchor":"ar-q4-10-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-3","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ أَمْوالَ الْيَتامى ظُلْماً من غير موجب شرعي، إِنَّما يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ نارًا، أي: ما يجُر إلى النار ويؤول إليها.","anchor":"ar-q4-10-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-4","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"وعن أبي برزة أنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم قال: «يبعثُ اللهُ أقوامًا من قبورهم تتأججُ أفواههم نارًا» ، فقيل: مَنْ هم يا رسول الله؟","anchor":"ar-q4-10-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-5","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"قال: «ألم تر أن الله يقول: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَأْكُلُونَ أَمْوالَ الْيَتامى ظُلْماً إِنَّما يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ نارًا وَسَيَصْلَوْنَ سَعِيراً» .","anchor":"ar-q4-10-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-6","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"أي: يحترقون في نار، وأي نار!! والصَّلْى: هو الشيّ، تقول: صليت الشيء: شويته، وأصليته وصليته، وذكر البطون مبالغة وتهجين لحالهم.","anchor":"ar-q4-10-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-7","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"الإشارة: حذَّر الحق- جل جلاله- أهل الدعوى، الذين نصبوا أنفسهم للشيخوخة، وادعوا مقام التربية، مع كونهم جهالاً بالله، محجوبين عن شهود أسرار التوحيد، أن يأخذوا أموال الضعفاء الذين تعلقوا بهم لأنهم إنما يدفعون لهم ذلك طمعًا في الوصول إلى الله. وهم ليسوا أهلاً لذلك، فإذا أكلوا ذلك فإنما يأكلون في بطونهم نارًا وسيصلون سعيرًا، وهو تكثيف الحجاب، وزيادة العنت والتعب، إن أقبل عليهم الناس فرحوا واستبشروا، وإن أدبروا عنهم حزنوا وغضبوا، فأيُّ عذاب أعظم مِنْ هذا!! فتحصَّل من أول الآية إلى آخرها، أن الحق- تعالى- أمر أهل الغنى الأكبر، وهم الذين أهلَّهم للتربية النبوية، بأن سلكوا الطريق وأشرقت عليهم شموس التحقيق على يد شيخ كامل، بالاستعفاف، ولا يأخذوا إلاّ قدر الحاجة، من أموال مّنْ انتسب إليهم، وسد الباب لأهل الدعوى، لأنه مِنْ أكْلِ أموال الناس بالباطل، لأنه يعطى على وجه لم يوجد في المعطى إليه، إلا إذا كان على وجه الصدقة المحضة، مع أنه قد يكون غير مستحق لها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-10-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-10-8","r":"q4-10","title":"4:10 — The grave sin of consuming an orphan’s estate and the abuse of spiritual authority","text":"ثم بيَّن الحقّ تعالى قسمة التركة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-10-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-10-s1","r":"q4-10","title":"The accusative ẓulman (ظلمًا)","text":"I say: “Wrongfully” ( ظلمًا ) is an accusative of specification ( تمييز ) or an accusative of purpose or cause ( مفعول لأجله ).","anchor":"en-q4-10-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-10-s2","r":"q4-10","title":"The fire concealed in wrongful consumption","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—says: “Those who consume the wealth of orphans wrongfully,” without any lawful entitlement, “consume only fire within their bellies,” meaning what inevitably draws them toward the Fire and leads to it. Abū Barza relates that the Prophet said: “God will raise a people from their graves with fire blazing from their mouths.” Asked, “Who are they, Messenger of God?” he replied: “Have you not seen that God says, ‘Those who wrongfully consume the wealth of orphans consume only fire within their bellies, and shall burn in a Blaze’?” [H009] That is, they will burn in fire—and what a fire! Ṣaly ( الصَّلْي ) is roasting. One says “I roasted the thing” ( صليت الشيء ), and the causative forms are aṣlaytuhu and ṣallaytuhu . Mentioning the bellies heightens the depiction and makes their conduct seem all the more repellent. [N010]","anchor":"en-q4-10-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-10-s3","r":"q4-10","title":"False claims to teaching and the exploitation of disciples","text":"The Real—majestic is His greatness—warns those who make false claims ( أهل الدعوى ), who establish themselves as shaykhs and claim the station of spiritual education while remaining ignorant of God and veiled from witnessing the secrets of divine unity, not to accept wealth from the weak who have attached themselves to them. Such people give their property in the hope of being brought to God. Those false teachers are unqualified for what they claim; in taking the offerings, they consume only fire in their bellies, and their end is a blazing flame—here, a thickening of the veil ( تكثيف الحجاب ) and an increase in painful labor and distress. When people turn toward them, they exult; when people turn away, they grieve and rage. What torment could exceed this? The sense of the discussion from the beginning of this group of verses to its close is thus that God commands the people of the greater wealth—those truly fitted for prophetic education because they have travelled the way and the suns of verification ( شموس التحقيق ) have shone upon them through a perfected teacher—to abstain from taking from the wealth of those who attach themselves to them, except to the measure of need. He closes the door to pretenders, for their reception of offerings amounts to consuming other people's property falsely: the gift is offered in exchange for a spiritual reality that the supposed recipient does not possess. The exception is a gift made as purely voluntary alms ( صدقة محضة ), although even then the recipient may not be worthy of receiving alms. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-10-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-10-s4","r":"q4-10","title":"","text":"He then set forth the division of inheritance.","anchor":"en-q4-10-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-11","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving 4:11","anchor":"unit-q4-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-1","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"يُوصِيكُمُ اللَّهُ فِي أَوْلادِكُمْ لِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْأُنْثَيَيْنِ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-11-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-2","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: (يوصيكم الله) أي: يأمركم ويعهد إليكم، فِي أَوْلادِكُمْ، أي: في بيان ميراثهم، ثم فصَّله فقال: لِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْأُنْثَيَيْنِ، أي يعُدُ كل ذكر بأنثيين، فإذا ترك ابنًا وبنتًا، كانت من ثلاثة، للذكر سهمان وللبنت سهم، وإذا ترك ابنًا وبنتين فله قسمتان، ولكل واحدة قسمة، وهكذا، قال ابن جزي: هذه الآية نزلت بسبب سعد بن الربيع، وقيل: بسبب جابر بن عبد الله، إذ عاده رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم في مرضه ورفَعت ما كان في الجاهلية من ترك توريث النساء والأطفال. وقيل: نُسخت الوصية للوالدين والأقربين.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-3","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"وإنما قال: «يوصيكم» بلفظ الفعل الدائم، ولم يقل: أوصاكم، تنبيهًا على نسخ ما مضى، والشروع في حكم آخر، وإنما قال: (يوصيكم) بالاسم الظاهر، أي: (الله) ولم يقل: نوصيكم، لأنه أراد تعظيم الوصية، فجاء بالاسم الذي هو أعظم الأسماء، وإنما قال: (في أولادكم) ولم يقل: في أبنائكم لأن الابن يقع على الابن من الرضاعة، وعلى ابن البنت، وعلى الابن المتبنى، وليسوا من الورثة، فإن قيل: هلاّ قال: للأنثيين مثل حظ الذَّكر، أو للأنثى","anchor":"ar-q4-11-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-4","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"نصف حظ الذَّكر؟، فالجواب، أنه بدأ بالذَّكَرِ لفضله، ولأن القصد ذكُر حظه، ولو قال للأنثيين مثل حظ الذكر لكان فيه تفضيل للإناث. هـ (١) .","anchor":"ar-q4-11-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-5","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"الإشارة: كما أوصى الله- تعالى- في أولاد البشرية، أوصى على أولاد الروحانية، ويقع التفضيل في قسمة الإمداد على حسب التعظيم والمحبة والعطف من الشيخ، فبقدر ما يقع في قلب الشيخ، يسري إليه المدد، فقد يأخذ مثل حظ رجلين أو أكثر، على حسب ما سبق في القسمة الأزلية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-6","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"ثم ذكر حكم البنات إذا انفردن، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-11-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-8","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"... فَإِنْ كُنَّ نِساءً فَوْقَ اثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُنَّ ثُلُثا مَا تَرَكَ وَإِنْ كانَتْ واحِدَةً فَلَهَا النِّصْفُ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-11-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-9","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"قلت: أنّث الضمير فى (كنّ) باعتبار الخبر، أو يعود على المتروكات، وما قاله الزمخشري بعيد. ومن قرأ (واحدةُ) بالرفع، ففاعِلُ كَانَ التامة، ومن قرأ بالنصب، فخبر كان.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-10","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فإن كان المتروك من الأولاد نِساءً ليس معهن ذكور فَوْقَ اثْنَتَيْنِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4-11-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-11","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"اثنتين فما فوق، فَلَهُنَّ ثُلُثا ما تَرَكَ، والباقي للعاصب، وأخذ ابن عباس بظاهر الآية، فأعطاهما النصف كالواحدة، والجمهور على خلافه، وأن لفظ فَوْقَ زائدة كقوله: فَاضْرِبُوا فَوْقَ الْأَعْناقِ وقيل: أخذ الثلثين بالسُنة، وإن كانَتْ بنتًا واحِدَةً فَلَهَا النِّصْفُ، والباقي للعاصب، وفيه دليل على أنَّ الابن يأخذ جميع المال إذا انفرد لأن له مثل حظ الأنثيين.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-12","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"الإشارة: انظر البنت، إذا انفردت أخذت النصف، وإذا اجتمعت مع غيرها نقص لها، كذلك أمداد الأشياخ، من انفرد عندهم وحده، أخذ أكثر مما إذا اجتمع مع غيره، لانجماع نظر الشيخ إليه، وكان شيخنا رضي الله عنه يقول له شيخه: ما زال يأتيك الرجال- أي: إخوانك من الفقراء- وكان وحده، فيقول له: الله لا يجعل أحدًا يأتي حتى نشبع.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-13","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"وكذلك أيضًا، انفراد العبد بالعبادة، في وقت الغفلة، مددها أعظم من كونه مع غيره، كالمجاهد خلف الفارين.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-14","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"وكذلك قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «طوُبَى للغُرَبَاءِ» ، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-15","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"ثم ذكر ميراث الأبوين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-11-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-16","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"... وَلِأَبَوَيْهِ لِكُلِّ واحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ مِمَّا تَرَكَ إِنْ كانَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ فَإِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُ وَلَدٌ وَوَرِثَهُ أَبَواهُ فَلِأُمِّهِ الثُّلُثُ فَإِنْ كانَ لَهُ إِخْوَةٌ فَلِأُمِّهِ السُّدُسُ مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُوصِي بِها أَوْ دَيْنٍ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-11-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-17","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"قلت: (السدس) مبتدأ، و (لأبويه) خبر، و (لكل واحد) ، بدل من (أبويه) ، ونكتة البدل إفادة أنهما لا يشتركان في السدس، ولو قال: لأبوَيْه السدس لأوهم الاشتراك.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-18","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إذا مات الولد، وترك أبويه، ف لِكُلِّ واحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ مِمَّا تَرَكَ إِنْ كانَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ ذكرًا أو أنثى، واحدًا أو متعددًا، للصلب أو ولد ابن، فكلهم يَردُّون الأبوين للسدس، فَإِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُ وَلَدٌ وَوَرِثَهُ أَبَواهُ فقط، فَلِأُمِّهِ الثُّلُثُ، والباقي للأب، فَإِنْ كانَ لَهُ إِخْوَةٌ أي: أخَوَان فأكثر، سواء كانوا أشقاء أو لأب أو لأم، أو مختلفين، فَلِأُمِّهِ السُّدُسُ، والباقي للأب، ولا شيء للأخوة معه.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-19","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"وأخذ ابن عباس بظاهر الآية، فلم يحجبها للسدس باثنين، وجعلهما كالواحد، واحتج بأن لفظ الإخوة جمع، وأقله ثلاثة، وأجيب بأن لفظ الجمع، يقع على الاثنين كقوله: وَكُنَّا لِحُكْمِهِمْ شاهِدِينَ، إِذْ تَسَوَّرُوا الْمِحْرابَ، ولقوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «الاثْنَانِ فَما فَوْقَهمَا جَمَاعَةٌ» . وهذا كله، بعد إخراج الوصية وقضاء الدين، وإنما قدّم الحق- تعالى- الوصية على الدَّين، مع كون الدّين مقدمًا في القضاء من رأس المال لأن أرباب الدّين أقوياء، بخلاف الموصى لهم، فقدمهم اعتناء بهم.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-20","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"الإشارة: الروح كالأب، والبشرية كالأم، وعقد الصحبة مع الشيخ كالولد، فإن كان الإنسان له صحبة مع شيخ التربية، يعني له ورد منه، فالبشرية والروحانية سواء، إذ كلاهما يتهذبان ويتنوران بالأدب والمعرفة الأدب للبشرية، والمعرفة للروحانية، إذا استمد بالطاعة الظاهرُ استمد الباطن، وبالعكس، وإن لم يكن عقد الصحبة موجودًا كان ميراث البشرية من الحس أقوى كميراث الأم مع فقد الولد، أو تقول: الإنسان مركب من حس ومعنى، فالحس كالأم، والمعنى كالأب، لأن المعاني قائمة بالحس، والروح تستمد منهما معًا، فهي كالولد بينهما، فإن كانت الروح حية بوجود المعرفة، استمدت منهما معًا، وإن كانت ميتة، كان استمدادها من الحس أكثر، كموت الولد في ميراث الأم.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-21","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"أو تقول: الإنسان بين قدرة وحكمة، القدرة كالأب، والحكمة كالأم، والقلب بينهما كالولد، فإِنْ وُجد القلب استمدت الروح من القدرة والحكمة، واستوى نظرها فيهما. وإن فقد القلب غلب على الروح ميراث الحكمة، كفَقْدِ","anchor":"ar-q4-11-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-22","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"الولد في ميراث الأم، وإن كان للقلب أخوة من الأنوار والأسرار يتقوى بهما فللروح من ميراث الحكمة السدس، والباقي كله للقدرة، ولا يعرف هذا إلا من حقق معرفة القدرة والحكمة، ذوقًا وكشفًا، وإلاَّ.. فليسلُم لأهل المعرفة.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-23","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-24","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى حكمة تقسيم تركة الأب والابن على ما فرض، وأن ذلك لا يعلمه إلا هو، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-11-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-25","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"... آباؤُكُمْ وَأَبْناؤُكُمْ لاَ تَدْرُونَ أَيُّهُمْ أَقْرَبُ لَكُمْ نَفْعاً فَرِيضَةً مِنَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً (11)","anchor":"ar-q4-11-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-26","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: قد بينت لكم ما يرثُ الأبُ من ابنه، وما يرث الولدُ من أبيه، ولو وكلت ذلك إليكم لأفسدتم القسمة لأنكم لا تدرون أيهم أقرب نفعًا للآخر، هل الأب أقرب نفعًا لابنه، فتعطوه الميراث كله دون ولد الميت، أو الولد أقرب نفعًا لأبيه، من الأب لابنه، فتخصونه بالإرث، ففرضتُ ميراث الأب وميراث الولد، ولم نكل ذلك إليكم. فَرِيضَةً حاصلة مِنَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيماً بمصالح العباد حَكِيماً بما فرض وقدَّر.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-27","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"وقال ابن عباس: لا تدرون أيهم أطوع لله عز وجل من الآباء والأبناء، وأرفعكم درجة يوم القيامة، لأن الله تعالى يشفع المؤمنين في بعضهم بعضًا، فيشفع الولد في والديه، إن كان أرفع درجة منهما، فيرفعهما الله إليه، ويشفع الوالدين في ولدهما، إن كانا أرفع درجة منه، فيرتفع إليهما لتقر بذلك أعينهما. هـ. بالمعنى.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-27"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-28","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"الإشارة: الإنسان لا تقوم روحانيته إلا ببشريته، وبشريته إلا بروحانيته، فلا يدري أيهما أقرب له نفعًا، لأن البشرية محل للعبودية، والروحانية محل لشهود عظمة الربوبية، ولا بد للجمع بينهما، وكذلك الحس، لا يقوم إلا بالمعنى، والمعنى لا يقوم إلا بالحس، فلا تدري أيهما أقرب نفعًا لك أيها المريد، فتؤثره، وإن كانت المعاني هي المقصودة بالسير، لكن لا تقوم إلا بوجود الحس، فلا بد من ملاحظته.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-29","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"وقال الورتجبي هنا ما نصه: أشكل الأمر من تلك الطائفتين، أيهم يبلغ درجة الولاية والمعرفة الموجبة مشاهدة الله وقربته، التي لو وقعت ذرة منها لأحد من هذه الأمة لينجو بشفاعته سبعون ألفًا بغير حساب، أي: اخدموا آباءكم وارحموا أولادكم، فربما يخرج منهم صاحب الولاية، ليشفع لكم عند الله تعالى، وحكمة الإبهام هاهنا ليشمل الرحمة والشفقة على الجمهور، لتوقع ذلك الولي الصادق. هـ. قلت: فسر الآباء والأبناء بالحسيين، وتشمل الآية أيضًا الآباء والأبناء المعنويين والروحانيين. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-11-29"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-11-30","r":"q4-11","title":"4:11 — The portions of children and parents; grammar, inheritance and spiritual giving","text":"ثم ذكر ميراث الزوج والزوجة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-11-30"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s1","r":"q4-11","title":"Shares of sons and daughters, and the report of their revelation","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: “God instructs you” ( يُوصِيكُمُ اللَّهُ ), that is, commands you and entrusts you with a charge, “concerning your children” ( فِي أَوْلَادِكُمْ ), meaning the specification of their inheritance. He then sets out the shares: “for the male the equivalent of the share of two females” ( لِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْأُنْثَيَيْنِ ). In reckoning one male as two females, if a person leaves one son and one daughter, the estate is divided into three shares: two for the son and one for the daughter. If he leaves one son and two daughters, there are two portions for him and one for each of them. The same principle applies in analogous cases. Ibn Juzayy says that this verse was revealed on account of Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ; it is also said to concern Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh when the Messenger of God visited him in his illness. It abolished the pre-Islamic practice of withholding inheritance from women and children. Some say that it abrogated the earlier testamentary provision concerning parents and close relatives. [H012]","anchor":"en-q4-11-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s2","r":"q4-11","title":"Why “He instructs you,” why “children,” and why the male is named first","text":"He said “God instructs you” ( يُوصِيكُمُ اللَّهُ ) in the form of an ongoing verb rather than “God instructed you” ( أَوْصَاكُمْ ), to call attention to the supersession of the previous ruling and the commencement of another. He used the explicit divine name “God” ( اللَّهُ ) rather than “We instruct you” ( نُوصِيكُمْ ) to magnify the importance of the injunction, bringing the greatest of the divine names. He said “concerning your children” ( فِي أَوْلَادِكُمْ ) rather than “concerning your sons” ( فِي أَبْنَائِكُمْ ), because the term “son” can also be used of a foster-son through suckling, the son of a daughter, or an adopted son, none of whom inherits on that basis alone. If someone asks why the formulation was not “the two females have the equivalent of the male’s share,” or “the female has half the male’s share,” the answer is that the male is put first because of the preference he is accorded [in this legal exposition], and because the purpose is to state his share; the reverse expression would entail preferring the females. Here ends the statement cited from Ibn Juzayy. [N100]","anchor":"en-q4-11-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s3","r":"q4-11","title":"The teacher’s attention and the distribution of spiritual support","text":"Just as God has given instructions concerning the children of bodily humanity ( أولاد البشرية ), so has He enjoined care concerning the children of spiritual parentage ( أولاد الروحانية ). Preference in distributing the flow of spiritual assistance ( الإمداد ) depends upon the degree of esteem, love and affectionate care that the shaykh has for a disciple. In proportion to the place the disciple occupies in the shaykh’s heart, assistance flows to him. He may receive the share of two men or more, according to what was established for him in the eternal allotment ( القسمة الأزلية ). And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s4","r":"q4-11","title":"","text":"He then mentioned the ruling concerning daughters where there are no sons, saying:","anchor":"en-q4-11-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s5","r":"q4-11","title":"The feminine plural, and wāḥida in the nominative or accusative","text":"I say: The pronoun in “if they are” ( كُنَّ ) is feminine by reference to the predicate, or it refers to the [female children] left behind. The explanation given by al-Zamakhsharī is far-fetched. In the reading with “one” ( وَاحِدَةُ ) in the nominative ( الرفع ), it is the subject ( فاعل ) of the complete kāna ( كان التامة ); in the accusative ( النصب ), it is the predicate ( خبر ) of kāna .","anchor":"en-q4-11-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s6","r":"q4-11","title":"Two or more daughters and the dissent of Ibn ʿAbbās","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: If the children left behind are females, with no males among them, “above two” ( فَوْقَ اثْنَتَيْنِ ), meaning two or more, “they have two-thirds of what he left,” and the residue belongs to the residuary heir ( العاصب ). Ibn ʿAbbās took the apparent sense of the verse literally, assigning two daughters one-half, as for a sole daughter. The majority disagreed with him, treating the expression “above” ( فَوْقَ ) as additional, as in “strike above the necks” ( فَاضْرِبُوا فَوْقَ الْأَعْنَاقِ ), or saying that the two-thirds share for two daughters is established by the Sunna. If the deceased leaves “one daughter” alone, “hers is half,” the remainder going to the residuary heir. This also indicates that a single son takes the entire estate when he is the only heir, since his share is the equivalent of that of two daughters.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s7","r":"q4-11","title":"Solitude in the presence of the teacher, and worship during heedlessness","text":"Consider the daughter: on her own she receives half, while, when she is joined by others, her own portion is diminished. So, too, with the spiritual gifts ( أمداد ) of the shaykhs: a person who alone enjoys their attention may receive more than when others gather with him, because the shaykh’s gaze is concentrated upon him. Our shaykh—may God be pleased with him—said that his own shaykh used to tell him, when he was alone, “Men will go on coming to you,” meaning his fellow brethren among the poor ( الفقراء ). He replied, “May God not let anyone come until we have eaten our fill.” Similarly, the assistance associated with a servant’s worship while others are heedless is greater than when he worships alongside them, just as the fighter who holds his ground behind those who flee. Likewise the Prophet said, “Glad tidings to the strangers” ( طُوبَى لِلْغُرَبَاءِ ). [H010] And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s8","r":"q4-11","title":"","text":"He then mentioned the inheritance of the parents, saying:","anchor":"en-q4-11-s8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s9","r":"q4-11","title":"A sixth for each: the function of badal","text":"I say: “The sixth” ( السُّدُسُ ) is a subject ( مبتدأ ), and “to his two parents” ( لِأَبَوَيْهِ ) is a predicate ( خبر ). “To each one of them” ( لِكُلِّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا ) is a substitute or appositional replacement ( بدل ) for “to his two parents.” The point of this substitution is to show that they do not share one sixth between them; the wording “his two parents have the sixth” could have suggested that.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s10","r":"q4-11","title":"Both parents, siblings, wills and debts","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: If a child dies leaving both parents, “to each of them a sixth of what he left, if he has a child,” male or female, one or many, directly descended or the child of a son. All of these reduce each parent’s prescribed allotment to a sixth. But “if he has no child, and his two parents inherit from him” alone, “then his mother has a third,” and the rest goes to the father. “If he has siblings” ( إِخْوَةٌ ), that is, two or more brothers or sisters—of the same father and mother, or of the father only, or mother only, or from several such categories—“then his mother has a sixth,” and the remainder goes to his father. The siblings themselves receive nothing while the father is present. Ibn ʿAbbās took the apparent expression “siblings” in its plural force, and did not reduce the mother to a sixth in the presence of two, regarding two as he would one: the minimum plural, on his view, is three. The response given is that a plural expression can be applied to two, as in the verses “And We witnessed their judgment” ( وَكُنَّا لِحُكْمِهِمْ شَاهِدِينَ ) [Q 21:78] and “when they climbed over the wall of the sanctuary” ( إِذْ تَسَوَّرُوا الْمِحْرَابَ ) [Q 38:21], and in the reported saying, “Two and more constitute a group” ( الاثنان فما فوقهما جماعة ). [H011] All this takes effect after execution of the bequest and payment of the debt. God mentions the bequest before the debt, although a debt is satisfied first from the estate, because creditors already have strong legal claims, whereas those receiving a bequest are more vulnerable, so their interest is mentioned first out of special solicitude.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s11","r":"q4-11","title":"The father as spirit, the mother as embodied humanity, and companionship as a child","text":"The spirit ( الروح ) is like the father, embodied humanity ( البشرية ) like the mother, and the bond of companionship with the shaykh like a child. If someone has a bond of companionship with a shaykh of spiritual formation ( شيخ التربية )—meaning he has a regular practice received from him ( وِرْد )—then his bodily and spiritual aspects receive equally: each is refined and illumined by proper conduct ( الأدب ) and gnosis ( المعرفة ). Conduct belongs to the bodily aspect and gnosis to the spiritual. When the outward draws assistance through obedience, the inward also receives it, and conversely. If there is no bond of companionship, bodily humanity receives a stronger inheritance from the sensory realm ( الحس ), like the mother’s greater portion when there is no child. Or say: a human being is composed of the sensory ( حس ) and the intelligible or meaningful ( معنى ). The sensory is like the mother, and meaning like the father, since meanings subsist in sensory things; the spirit draws aid from them both and thus is like their child. If the spirit is alive with gnosis, it draws from both together; but if dead, it receives more from the sensory, like the loss of a child [which increases] the mother’s inheritance. Or say: the human being stands between divine power ( القدرة ) and wisdom ( الحكمة ). Power is like the father, wisdom like the mother, and the heart like the child between them. If the heart is present, the spirit draws from both power and wisdom, and its regard toward both becomes equal. If the heart is absent, wisdom’s inheritance predominates in the spirit, just as in the mother’s inheritance when the child is absent. If the heart has brethren among lights and secrets that strengthen it, then the spirit takes a sixth from the inheritance of wisdom and the rest belongs entirely to power. This is intelligible only to one who has realized knowledge of power and wisdom by direct taste ( ذوق ) and unveiling ( كشف ). Otherwise, one should defer to the people of gnosis. And God, exalted is He, knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s12","r":"q4-11","title":"","text":"God then disclosed the wisdom in His allotment of the father’s and son’s inheritance, which He alone knows: “Your fathers and your sons…”","anchor":"en-q4-11-s12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s13","r":"q4-11","title":"Why God alone assigns the shares","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: I have explained what a father inherits from his son and what a son inherits from his father. Had I left the matter to you, you would have spoiled the division: you do not know which is closer to the other in benefit. Is the father more beneficial to his son, so you should give him the whole inheritance to the exclusion of the dead man’s child? Or is a child of greater benefit to his father than a father is to his child, so that you should reserve the inheritance for him? I therefore ordained the shares of father and son and did not leave the decision to you. An allotted portion “ordained by God” ( فَرِيضَةً مِنَ اللَّهِ ): truly God knows His servants’ interests and is wise in what He apportions and determines. Ibn ʿAbbās said: You do not know who among your parents and children is more obedient to God or more exalted in rank on the Day of Resurrection, for God permits believers to intercede for one another. A child whose station is higher than that of his parents intercedes for them and God raises them to his rank. Parents more exalted than their child likewise intercede for him, so that he is raised to them and their eyes are gladdened. Here ends the substance, paraphrased, of Ibn ʿAbbās’s statement.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s14","r":"q4-11","title":"Embodiment and spirit: neither can dispense with the other","text":"A person’s spiritual reality ( روحانية ) cannot stand without his bodily humanity ( بشرية ), nor bodily humanity without spirituality. So one does not know which of the two is nearer to him in benefit: bodily humanity is the locus for servanthood ( العبودية ), whereas spirituality is the locus for witnessing the majesty of Lordship ( الربوبية ). Both must be joined. Likewise sensory manifestation ( الحس ) cannot subsist without meaning ( المعنى ), nor meaning without sensory manifestation; you, seeker ( مريد ), do not know which is more beneficial to you so as to prefer it. Although meanings are what one journeys towards, they cannot be established without the sensory; it must therefore be attended to. Al-Wartajbī writes here, in his own words: “The question concerning these two parties has been left obscure: which of them will attain the station of sainthood ( الولاية ) and gnosis ( المعرفة ) that yields witnessing of God and nearness to Him? Were a single atom of it to fall to anyone in this community, seventy thousand might be delivered by his intercession without reckoning. In other words: serve your fathers and be tender towards your children, for from among them may emerge a person endowed with sainthood, who will intercede for you before God. The wisdom of leaving the matter unspecified here is to extend kindness and compassion throughout the community in anticipation of the true friend of God ( الولي الصادق ).” Here ends his statement. I say: He interprets fathers and sons as those related by bodily kinship, but the verse also embraces fathers and sons in meaning and in spiritual relationship. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-11-s15","r":"q4-11","title":"","text":"He then mentioned the inheritance of husbands and wives.","anchor":"en-q4-11-s15"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-12","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren 4:12","anchor":"unit-q4-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-1","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"وَلَكُمْ نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ أَزْواجُكُمْ إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُنَّ وَلَدٌ فَإِنْ كانَ لَهُنَّ وَلَدٌ فَلَكُمُ الرُّبُعُ مِمَّا تَرَكْنَ مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُوصِينَ بِها أَوْ دَيْنٍ وَلَهُنَّ الرُّبُعُ مِمَّا تَرَكْتُمْ إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَكُمْ وَلَدٌ فَإِنْ كانَ لَكُمْ وَلَدٌ فَلَهُنَّ الثُّمُنُ مِمَّا تَرَكْتُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ تُوصُونَ بِها أَوْ دَيْنٍ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-12-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-2","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَكُمْ أيها الأزواج، من ميراث أزواجكم نِصْفُ ما تركن إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُنَّ وَلَدٌ. فَإِنْ كانَ لَهُنَّ وَلَدٌ وارث، ذكرًا أو أنثى، مفردًا أو متعددًا، من بطنها أو من صلب بنيها أو بني بنيها وإن سفل، منكم أو من غيركم، فَلَكُمُ الرُّبُعُ مِمَّا تَرَكْنَ، بعد قضاء الدين وإخراج الوصية.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-3","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"وَلَهُنَّ أي: الزوجات من ميراث الزوج الرُّبُعُ مما ترك إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ له ولد لاحق، ذكرًا أو أنثى، على وزان ما تقدم في الزوجة، فَإِنْ كانَ لَكُمْ وَلَدٌ فَلَهُنَّ الثُّمُنُ تنفرد به إن كانت واحدة، ويُقسم بينهن إن تعددن، ولا ينقص لأهل السهام مما فرض الله لهم إلا ما نقصه العَوْل على مذهب الجمهور، خلافًا لابن عباس، فإنه لا يقول بالعول.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-4","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"فإن قيل: لِمَ كرر قوله: مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ مع ميراث الزوج وميراث الزوجة، ولم يذكره قبل ذلك إلا مرة واحدة في ميراث الأولاد والأبوين؟ فالجواب: أن الموروث في ميراث الزوج هو الزوجة، والموروث في ميراث الزوجة هو الزوج، فكل واحدة قضية مستقلة، فلذلك ذكر ذلك مع كل واحدة، بخلاف الأول فأن الموروث فيه واحد، ذكرَ حكم ما يرث منه أولاده وأبواه، وهي قضية واحدة، فلذلك قال فيه: مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ مرة واحدة.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-5","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"قاله ابن جزي. قال البيضاوي: فرض للرجل بحق الزواج ضِعف ما للمرأة كما في النسب، وهكذا قياس كل رجل وامرأة، إذا اشتركا في الجهة والقرب، ولا يستثنى منه إلا أولاد الأم والمعتق والمعتقة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-6","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"الإشارة: إذا ماتت النفس، ولم تبق لها بقية، وورثت الروحُ ما كان لها من العلوم الكسبية: النقلية والعقلية، وأضافته إلى مَالهَا من العلوم الوهبية، فانقلب الجميع وهبيًا، قال بعض شيوخ أشياخنا: (كنتُ أعرف أربعة عشر علمًا، فلما دخلت علم الحقيقة سرطت ذلك كله، فلم يبق إلا الكتاب والسنة) ، أو كما قال. وقال أبو سليمان الداراني:","anchor":"ar-q4-12-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-7","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"إذا اعتقدت النفوس على ترك الآثام، جالت في الملكوت، ثم عادت إلى صاحبها بطرائف العلوم، من غير أن يؤدي إليها عالم علما.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-8","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"فإن بقي للنفس بقية، نقص ميراث الروح منها، بقدر البقية، كما أن الزوج ينقص ميراثه مع الفرع، وكذلك إذا ماتت الروح بالرجوع عن طريق الجِد، ورثت النفسُ ما كان لها من العلوم الوهبية، والمعاني والأسرار القدسية، فتأكلها، وتردها نقلية حسية، بعد أن كانت وهبية ذوقية، فتتحسس المعاني، وتتكثف الأواني. والعياذ بالله من السلب بعد العطاء، إلا أن ميراث النفس من الروح أقوى، فإن بقي للروح شيء من الحياة، نقص ميراث النفس منها، كنقص الزوجة مع الفرع من ميراث الزوج، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-9","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"ثم ذكر ميراث الأخ للأخ، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-12-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-10","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"... وَإِنْ كانَ رَجُلٌ يُورَثُ كَلالَةً أَوِ امْرَأَةٌ وَلَهُ أَخٌ أَوْ أُخْتٌ فَلِكُلِّ واحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ فَإِنْ كانُوا أَكْثَرَ مِنْ ذلِكَ فَهُمْ شُرَكاءُ فِي الثُّلُثِ مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُوصى بِها أَوْ دَيْنٍ غَيْرَ مُضَارٍّ وَصِيَّةً مِنَ اللَّهِ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَلِيمٌ (12)","anchor":"ar-q4-12-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-11","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"قلت: الكلالة: انقطاع النسل، بحيث لم يبق للميت فرع ولا أصل، لا ذكر ولا أنثى، وهو مصدر من تَكَلَّلهُ النسبُ، إذا أحاط به كالإكليل، لأن ورثته أحاطوا به ولَيْسوا منه. ونظم بعضهم معنى الكلالة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-12-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-12","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"إن امرؤٌ يَسْأَلُ عن كَلاَلَة ... هو انْقِطاعُ النَّسْلِ لا مَحَالة","anchor":"ar-q4-12-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-13","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"لا والدُ يَبْقَى ولا مولوُد ... قدْ هَلَكَ الأبْنَاءُ والجُدُود","anchor":"ar-q4-12-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-14","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"فتحتمل أن تطلق هنا على الميت، أو على الورثة، أو على الوراثة، أو على القرابة أو على المال. فإن كانت على الميت، فإعرابه خبر كان، و (يورث) صفة، أو (يورث) خبر كان، و (كلالة) حال من الضمير في (يورث) ، أو «كان» تامة، و (يورث) صفة و (كلالة) حال من الضمير. وإن كانت على الورثة، فهو خبر كان، على حذف مضاف أي: ذا كلالة، وإن كانت الوِرَاثة فهو مصدر في موضع الحال، وإن كانت القرابة، فهو مفعول من أجله، أي: يورث من أجل القرابة. وإن كانت للمال، فهو مفعول ثانِ ليورث، وكل من هذه يحتمل أن تكون «كان» تامة أو ناقصة. قاله ابن جزي. و (غير مضار) ، منصوب على الحال، أو العامل فيه (يوصى) ، و (مضار) اسم فاعل، ووصية: مصدر ليوصي، أو مفعول (مضار) .","anchor":"ar-q4-12-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-15","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وإن كان الميت رجلاً أو امرأة، يُورثان كلالة، بحيث لا فرع لهما ولا أصل، قد انقطع عمود نسبهما، ولهما أخ أو أخت لأم فَلِكُلِّ واحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ. فَإِنْ كانُوا أَكْثَرَ مِنْ ذلِكَ فَهُمْ شُرَكاءُ فِي الثُّلُثِ","anchor":"ar-q4-12-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-16","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"، الذكر والأنثى سواء، لأن الإدلاء للميت بمحض الأنوثة، ومفهوم الآية: أنهما لا يرثان مع الأم والجدة، كما لا يرثان مع البنت وبنت الابن، إذ ليس حينئذٍ بكلالة، وإنما قيدنا الأخ والأخت بكونهما للأم لأن الأخ الشقيق أو للأب سيأتي في آخر السورة. والأخت تقدم أنَّ لها النصف، وأيضًا: قد قرأ سعد بن أبي وقاص، وابن مسعود: «وله أخ أو أخت لأم» .","anchor":"ar-q4-12-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-17","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"وهذا كله مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُوصى بِها أَوْ دَيْنٍ حال كونه غَيْرَ مُضَارٍّ في الوصية أو الدين، كالوصية بأكثر من الثلث، أو للوارث، أو فِرارًا منه، فإن عُلِم أنه قصد الإضرار، رد ما زاد على الثلث، واختلف في رد الثلث على قولين. قاله ابن جزي. وَصِيَّةً مِنَ اللَّهِ، أي: نوصيكم وصية، أو غير مضار وصية من الله. قال ابن عباس: (الإضرار في الوصية من الكبائر) . وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بمصالح عباده، يقسم المال على حسب المصلحة، حَلِيمٌ لا يُعاجِل بالعقوبة من خالف حدوده.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-18","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الأخوة في الشيخ كالأخوة في النسب، لأنهم يرضعون من ثدي واحدة ولبن واحد، فإن مات أحدهم، ورث أخوه المدد الذي كان يأخذه من شيخه، وكذا إذا رجع- فإنه موت- فينقلب المدد إلى أخيه، ومثاله كماء فُرِّقَ على قواديس، فإذا انسدت إحدى القواديس رجع الماء إلى الأخرى، فإن كانوا أكثر من واحد فهم شركاء في ذلك المدد، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-12-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-12-19","r":"q4-12","title":"4:12 — Spousal inheritance, the meaning of kalāla, and the shared inheritance of spiritual brethren","text":"ثم حذَّر الحق- تعالى- من مخالفة ما حدّ فى الوصايا والمواريث، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-12-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-12-s1","r":"q4-12","title":"The husband’s and wife’s prescribed shares","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: “To you,” husbands, from the inheritance of your wives, belongs “half of what they leave, if they have no child.” But if they have a child entitled to inherit, male or female, one or several—whether born directly of her or descended through sons, sons’ sons and so on, whether related to you or to another husband—“yours is a quarter of what they leave,” after the debt is discharged and the bequest executed. “And to them,” the wives, belongs “a quarter” of what the husband leaves if he has no descendant entitled to inherit, male or female, on the same basis as stated previously regarding the wife. But “if you have a child, theirs is an eighth,” which a single wife takes alone, or which several wives divide among themselves. The prescribed shares ( السهام ) are not diminished except by proportional adjustment ( العَوْل ), according to the majority school, contrary to Ibn ʿAbbās, who did not accept ʿawl ( العَوْل ). If it is asked why the clause “after any bequest” ( مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ ) is repeated for the inheritance of both husband and wife, while it was mentioned only once with the children’s and parents’ inheritance in the preceding verse, the answer is that, in the case of the husband’s inheritance, the deceased is his wife, while, in the wife’s inheritance, the deceased is her husband. Each therefore constitutes a separate legal case, and the clause appears with each. In the former case, the deceased was one person whose children’s and parents’ shares were set out together, so it was mentioned once. This is Ibn Juzayy’s explanation. Al-Bayḍāwī says: The man is assigned twice the share of a woman by virtue of marriage, as in kinship. Such is the analogy wherever a man and woman share the same cause and proximity of inheritance, except for siblings through the mother and for emancipators, male and female. Here ends his statement.","anchor":"en-q4-12-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-12-s2","r":"q4-12","title":"When the bodily self dies and acquired knowledge becomes freely bestowed","text":"When the self ( النفس ) dies and no remainder of it survives, the spirit ( الروح ) inherits what it possessed of acquired knowledge ( العلوم الكسبية ), whether transmitted ( نقلية ) or rational ( عقلية ). It joins this to its own freely bestowed knowledge ( العلوم الوهبية ), and all is transformed into something bestowed. One of our earlier masters’ masters said: “I used to know fourteen sciences. When I entered the science of Reality ( علم الحقيقة ), I swallowed all of that, until only the Book and Sunna remained”—or words to that effect. Abū Sulaymān al-Dārānī said: “When souls resolve to give up sins, they travel through the Dominion ( الملكوت ) and return to their owners bearing wondrous sciences, though no learned person transmitted knowledge to them.” If some remainder of the self subsists, the spirit’s inheritance of its knowledge decreases in proportion to that remainder, just as the husband’s share decreases when his wife leaves a descendant. Conversely, if the spirit dies by turning back from the path of earnest striving ( طريق الجدّ ), the self inherits the freely bestowed sciences, meanings and sacred mysteries that had belonged to it. It consumes them and transforms them into things transmitted and sensory after they had been freely bestowed and tasted directly. It makes meanings sensory and vessels dense. We seek God’s protection from dispossession after having received a gift ( السلب بعد العطاء ). Yet the self’s inheritance from the spirit is stronger: if something remains of the spirit’s life, the self’s share is reduced, as the wife’s inheritance from her husband decreases when he leaves a descendant. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-12-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-12-s3","r":"q4-12","title":"","text":"He then mentions the inheritance of a sibling from a sibling: “And if a man …”","anchor":"en-q4-12-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-12-s4","r":"q4-12","title":"Kalāla (الكلالة), the network of kinship and alternative syntactic analyses","text":"I say: Kalāla ( الكَلَالَة ) is the severance of the line of descent, such that the deceased has neither descendants nor ascendants, male or female. It is a verbal noun ( مصدر ) derived from the expression “kinship encircled him” ( تكلّله النسبُ ), like a wreath ( الإكليل ), because his heirs surround him rather than issuing from him. A poet gave its meaning in verse: If someone asks about kalāla, It is the severance of the line of descent, without doubt: No parent is left and no offspring, Sons and grandfathers have passed away. The expression may here denote the deceased, the heirs, the act of inheritance, kinship itself, or the property inherited. If it denotes the deceased, it is the predicate ( خبر ) of kāna ( كان ) while “is inherited from” ( يُورَثُ ) is an adjective ( صفة ). Alternatively, “is inherited from” is the predicate of kāna and kalāla is a circumstantial qualifier ( حال ) of its implicit pronoun, or kāna is complete ( تامة ), with “is inherited from” adjectival and kalāla again a circumstantial qualifier. If it denotes the heirs, it is the predicate of kāna with a suppressed annexed noun ( مضاف محذوف ): “one possessed of [the relationship of] kalāla” ( ذا كلالة ). If it denotes the inheritance, it is a verbal noun functioning as a circumstantial qualifier. If it denotes kinship, it is an accusative of cause ( مفعول لأجله )—one is inherited from by reason of the kinship. If it denotes the property, it is the second object ( مفعول ثانٍ ) of “is inherited from.” Each construction admits kāna as complete or incomplete. This is Ibn Juzayy’s grammatical analysis. The phrase “without causing injury” ( غَيْرَ مُضَارٍّ ) is accusative as a circumstantial qualifier ( حال ), or its governor ( عامل ) is “he enjoins [a bequest]” ( يُوصَى ). “One causing injury” ( مُضَارّ ) is an active participle ( اسم فاعل ). “A bequest” ( وَصِيَّةً ) is a verbal noun ( مصدر ) of “enjoins,” or the object ( مفعول ) of “causing injury.”","anchor":"en-q4-12-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-12-s5","r":"q4-12","title":"Maternal siblings, equal shares and harmful wills","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: If the deceased, a man or woman, is inherited from as a kalāla ( كَلَالَة ), with neither descendant nor ascendant—his direct line of descent having ended—and has a brother or sister through the mother , “each of them has a sixth.” But “if they are more numerous, they are partners in a third”; male and female take equal shares, because their link with the deceased runs through the maternal line alone. The implication is that they do not inherit alongside the mother or grandmother, nor alongside a daughter or son’s daughter, since the deceased is then not a kalāla in the required sense. [Source and textual note: This is a prima facie inference ( mafhūm ), not the final inheritance rule. Al-Bayḍāwī on 4:12 gives the same “mother and grandmother” wording, then adds that the implication is restricted by consensus. That qualification is absent from Cairo I:477. Mālik’s Muwaṭṭaʾ , Book of Inheritances, chapter on maternal siblings, excludes those siblings in the presence of descendants, the father or paternal grandfather, and allows them to inherit otherwise. The earlier parallel therefore explains the wording without replacing “mother and grandmother” by “father and grandfather.” The origin of Cairo’s omitted qualification remains unestablished.] We restrict brother and sister here to those related through the mother because the full or paternal brother’s inheritance will be explained at the end of the sūrah. The sister’s half-share has already been mentioned. Furthermore, Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ and Ibn Masʿūd read: “and he has a brother or sister through the mother ” ( وله أخ أو أخت لأم ). All these shares are distributed “after any bequest made or debt,” on condition that no harm is caused ( غَيْرَ مُضَارٍّ ) through bequest or debt—for example, a bequest of more than a third, an unauthorized testamentary allocation to an heir, or a contrivance designed to defeat others’ rights. Where the intention to inflict harm is known, any excess above a third is set aside; the jurists disagreed, in two reported opinions, whether the third itself should also be invalidated. This is Ibn Juzayy’s account. “A bequest from God” ( وَصِيَّةً مِنَ اللَّهِ ) means “We enjoin this upon you as an injunction,” or means “without violating an injunction from God.” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “Causing harm in a bequest is one of the grave sins.” God knows what serves His servants’ welfare, apportions wealth accordingly, and is Forbearing ( حَلِيمٌ ): He does not immediately inflict punishment upon those who violate His bounds.","anchor":"en-q4-12-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-12-s6","r":"q4-12","title":"Brethren under the same teacher share spiritual nourishment","text":"Know that brotherhood through the shaykh ( الأخوة في الشيخ ) is like brotherhood through kinship, for they suckle at one breast and drink one milk. If one of them dies, his brother inherits the spiritual provision ( المدد ) he used to receive from their teacher. Likewise if a disciple turns back [from the path]—which is a kind of death—the influx is diverted to his brother. It resembles water divided among conduits ( القواديس ): if one conduit is blocked, the water flows towards the others. If there are several spiritual brethren, they become partners in that spiritual influx. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-12-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-12-s7","r":"q4-12","title":"","text":"Then the Real—exalted is He—warned against transgressing the limits He had established for bequests and inheritances.","anchor":"en-q4-12-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-13-14","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline 4:13–14","anchor":"unit-q4-13-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-13-14-1","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"تِلْكَ حُدُودُ اللَّهِ وَمَنْ يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ يُدْخِلْهُ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها وَذلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ (13) وَمَنْ يَعْصِ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَيَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَهُ يُدْخِلْهُ نارًا خالِداً فِيها وَلَهُ عَذابٌ مُهِينٌ (14)","anchor":"ar-q4-13-14-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-13-14-2","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"قلت: توحيد الضمير في (نُدخله) (١) مراعاة للفظ (من) . وجمع الحال في (خالدين) مراعاة للمعنى.","anchor":"ar-q4-13-14-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-13-14-3","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"و (خالدين) و (خالدًا) : حال مقدرة من ضمير (نُدخله) ، كقولك: مررت برجل معه صقر صائداً به غدًا، وليسا صفتين لجنات ونارًا، وإلا لوجب إبراز الضمير لأنهما جرتا على غير مَنْ هما له.","anchor":"ar-q4-13-14-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-13-14-4","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: تِلْكَ الأحكام التي شرعناها لكم في أمر الوصايا والمواريث، هي حُدُودُ اللَّهِ حدَّها لكم لتقفوا معها ولا تتعدوها وَمَنْ يُطِعِ اللَّهَ فيما أمر به وحدّه، وَرَسُولَهُ فيما شرَّعه وسنّه نُدْخِلْهُ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها. وَذلِكَ هو الْفَوْزُ أي: الفلاح الْعَظِيمُ، وَمَنْ يَعْصِ اللَّهَ فيما أمر ونهى، وَرَسُولَهُ فيما شرعه، وَيَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَهُ التي حدها، فتجاوز إلى متابعة هواه، نُدْخِلْهُ نارًا خالِداً فِيها وَلَهُ عَذابٌ مُهِينٌ. وهذا إذا أنكر مشروعيتها فيكون كافرًا، وإلاَّ كان عاصيًا في حكم المشيئة، ومذهب أهل السنة أنه لا يخلد، وحملوا الآية على الكافر، أو عبارة عن طول المدة، كما في قاتل النفس. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-13-14-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-13-14-5","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"الإشارة: قد حدَّ الحق- جل جلاله- لأهل الشريعة الظاهرة حدودًا قام ببيانها العلماء، وحدَّ لأهل الحقيقة- وهي سر الولاية- حدودًا، قام بها الأولياء، فمن قام بحدود الشريعة الظاهرة كان من المؤمنين الصالحين، ومن تعداها كان من العاصين الظالمين، ومن قام بحدود الحقيقة الباطنية، وصحب أهلها كان من المحسنين العارفين المقربين، ودخل جنة المعارف، ومن تعدَّ حدود الحقيقة، أو لم يصحب أهلها كان من عوام أهل اليمين، وله عذاب الحجاب في غم الحساب، وقال في الحاشية: في حد حدوده إشارة للعبودية، في إخراج كل عن نظره واختياره، ثم انقياده وذلته لحكم ربه، والوقوف عند حدوده.","anchor":"ar-q4-13-14-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-13-14-6","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"وقال الورتجبي: قيل: (تلك حدود الله) أي: الإظهار من الأحوال للمريدين على حسب طاقتهم لها، فإن التعدي فيها يهلكهم، وقال أبو عثمان: ما هلك امرؤ لزم حده ولم يتعد طوره. هـ. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q4-13-14-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-13-14-7","r":"q4-13-14","title":"4:13–14 — The limits of the revealed law and the bounds of spiritual discipline","text":"ولمّا فرغ الحق تعالى من الأمر بحفظ الأموال، شرع فى الكلام على حفظ الأنساب، وقدّم الكلام أولا على الزنى إذ به تختلط الأنساب، ويختل نظام حفظها، ثم تكلم بعد على النكاح وما يحرم من النساء وما يحل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-13-14-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-13-14-s1","r":"q4-13-14","title":"Agreement with man (مَن) and prospective circumstantial qualifiers","text":"I say: The singular pronoun in “We admit him” ( نُدْخِلْهُ ) observes the grammatical form of “whoever” ( مَنْ ). The plural circumstantial form “abiding” ( خَالِدِينَ ) observes its sense, since it includes a multitude of persons. The forms “abiding” ( خَالِدِينَ ) and “abiding” ( خَالِدًا ) are prospective circumstantial qualifiers ( حال مقدرة ) of the object pronoun in “We admit him,” like saying, “I passed a man with a falcon, who will be hunting with it tomorrow.” They are not adjectives of “gardens” ( جَنَّات ) and “fire” ( نَارًا ): were they adjectives predicated of something other than their grammatical possessor, the pronoun would have to be made explicit. [Reading note: the Cairo verse headings print yudkhilhu , “He admits him,” while this grammatical discussion and the following exposition quote nudkhilhu , “We admit him.” The Cairo editor attributes the nūn reading to Nāfiʿ and Ibn ʿĀmir, and the yāʾ reading to the other readers. The verse translation follows its displayed heading; the translations of the grammatical discussion and exposition follow the forms they actually quote.]","anchor":"en-q4-13-14-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-13-14-s2","r":"q4-13-14","title":"Obedience, disobedience, and the duration of punishment","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: The ordinances We have established for you concerning bequests and inheritance “are the limits of God” ( حُدُودُ اللَّهِ ), which He marked out for you so that you should stand by them and not transgress them. “Whoever obeys God” in what He commands and limits, “and His Messenger” in what he legislates and establishes by his Sunna, “We will admit him to gardens beneath which rivers flow, abiding therein.” “That is the great triumph” ( الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ ), the supreme success. But “whoever disobeys God” in what He commands or forbids, “and His Messenger” in what he legislates, “and transgresses His limits,” departing from those bounds to pursue desire, “We will admit him to a fire, abiding therein; and for him is a humiliating punishment.” This everlasting punishment applies where the transgressor rejects the legitimacy of the injunctions and thereby becomes an unbeliever. Otherwise he is a sinner subject to the divine will ( المشيئة ). According to the doctrine of the People of the Sunna ( أهل السنة ), he does not remain eternally in the Fire; they interpret the verse as applying to the unbeliever, or take the term to indicate a very long stay, as in the verse concerning the murderer. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-13-14-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-13-14-s3","r":"q4-13-14","title":"The limits of outward law and of inner spiritual realization","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—has established limits for the people of the outward Law ( الشريعة الظاهرة ), which the scholars ( العلماء ) have undertaken to clarify. He has likewise established limits for the people of inward Reality ( الحقيقة ), which is the secret of sainthood ( سر الولاية ), and the Friends of God ( الأولياء ) undertake to maintain them. Whoever observes the limits of outward Law belongs among the righteous believers; whoever exceeds them belongs among sinners and wrongdoers. Whoever observes the bounds of inward Reality and keeps company with its people belongs among the spiritually excellent, the knowers drawn near ( المحسنين العارفين المقربين ), and enters the Garden of gnoses ( جنة المعارف ). Whoever transgresses the bounds of Reality, or fails to accompany its people, belongs to the ordinary People of the Right ( عوام أهل اليمين ) and suffers the punishment of veiling ( عذاب الحجاب ) amid the distress of reckoning. The marginal commentary says: In the designation of His limits lies an indication of servanthood ( العبودية ): removing every person from self-regard and autonomous choosing, then submitting with humility to the judgment of his Lord and stopping at His bounds. Al-Wartajbī says: It has been said that “those are God’s limits” means the states which are made manifest to seekers ( المريدين ) according to their capacity to bear them; to overstep those capacities destroys them. Abū ʿUthmān said: “No one has perished who kept to his limit and did not exceed his station.” Here ends the quotation. God grants success and guides to the even path.","anchor":"en-q4-13-14-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-13-14-s4","r":"q4-13-14","title":"","text":"Having completed the command to preserve property, the Real now begins His discussion of the preservation of lineage ( حفظ الأنساب ). He first treats illicit intercourse because it confuses descent and disrupts its protection, then speaks of marriage and of those women who are prohibited or permitted in it.","anchor":"en-q4-13-14-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-15-16","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self 4:15–16","anchor":"unit-q4-15-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-1","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"وَاللاَّتِي يَأْتِينَ الْفاحِشَةَ مِنْ نِسائِكُمْ فَاسْتَشْهِدُوا عَلَيْهِنَّ أَرْبَعَةً مِنْكُمْ فَإِنْ شَهِدُوا فَأَمْسِكُوهُنَّ فِي الْبُيُوتِ حَتَّى يَتَوَفَّاهُنَّ الْمَوْتُ أَوْ يَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ لَهُنَّ سَبِيلاً (15) وَالَّذانِ يَأْتِيانِها مِنْكُمْ فَآذُوهُما فَإِنْ تابا وَأَصْلَحا فَأَعْرِضُوا عَنْهُما إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ تَوَّاباً رَحِيماً (16)","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-2","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالنساء اللَّاتِي يَأْتِينَ الْفاحِشَةَ أي: الزنى، سُمِّيَ فاحشة لفُحش قبحه وبشاعة فعله شرعًا، مِنْ نِسائِكُمْ المسلمات، فَاسْتَشْهِدُوا عَلَيْهِنَّ أي: اطلبوا مَنْ رَمَاهُنَّ بذلك أن يُشْهِدوا","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-3","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"عَلَيْهِنَّ أَرْبَعَةً مِنْكُمْ، أي: من عدول المؤمنين يرونهما كالمرود في المكحلة، وإنما جعلوا أربعة مبالغة في الستر على المؤمن، أو ليكون على كل واحد اثنان، فَإِنْ شَهِدُوا عليهن بذلك فَأَمْسِكُوهُنَّ فِي الْبُيُوتِ، واجعلوه سجنًا لهن حَتَّى يَتَوَفَّاهُنَّ الْمَوْتُ أي: يستوفي أجلّهن الموتُ، أو يتوفاهن ملك الموت، أَوْ يَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ لَهُنَّ سَبِيلًا كتعيين الحد المخلّص من السجن، وكان هذا في أول الإسلام ثم نسخ بما في سورة النور من الحدود، ويحتمل أن يراد التوصية بإمساكهن بعد أن يُجلدن كي لا يَعُدْن إلى الزنى بسبب الخروج والتعرض للرجال.","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-4","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"واكتفى بذكر حدِّهن، بما في سورة النور، وهذا الإمساك كان خاصًا بالنساء بدليل قوله وَالَّذانِ يَأْتِيانِها مِنْكُمْ أي: الزاني والزانية منكم، (فآذوهما) بالتوبيخ والتقريع- (فإن تابا وأصلحا فأعرضوا عنهما) أي:","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-5","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"اقطعوا عنهما الأذى، أو أعرِضوا عنهما بالإغماض عن ذكر مساوئهما.","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-6","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"قيل: إن هذه الآية سابقة على الأولى نزولاً، وكان عقوبة الزنى الأذى ثم الحبس ثم الجلد، وقيل، الحبس في المساحقات، والإيذاء في اللواطين، وما في سورة النور في الزناة. والذي يظهر. أن الحكم كان في أول الإسلام في الزنا: الإمساك للنساء في البيوت بعد الإيذاء بالتوبيخ، فتُمسك في بيتها حتى تموت، أو يجعل الله لها سبيلاً بالتزوج بمن يعفها عنه. والإيذاء للرجال بالتعيير والتقريع والتحجيم حتى تتحقق توبته، ثم نسخ ذلك كله بالحدود، وهو جَلْد البكر مائة وتغريبه عامًا ورجم المحصن. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-7","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"الإشارة: ينبغي للعبد، إذا طَغَتْ عليه نفسُه، وأرادت ارتكاب الفواحش، أن يستشهد عليها الحفظة، الذين يحفظون عليه تلك المعاصي، فإن لم تستحِ، فليعاقبها بالحبس في سجن الجوع والخلوة والصمت، حتى تموت عن تلك الشهوات، أو يجعل الله لها طريقًا بالوصول إلى شيخ يُغيِّبه عنها، أو بوارد قوي مِن خوف مُزعج أو شوق مقلق، فإن تابت وأصلحت، أعرض عنها واشتغل بذكر الله، ثم يغيب عما سواه. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-15-16-8","r":"q4-15-16","title":"4:15–16 — Early discipline for sexual offences and the purification of the self","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى وقت التوبة التي تقبل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-15-16-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-15-16-s1","r":"q4-15-16","title":"Four witnesses, seclusion and subsequent penal provisions","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: “Those women who commit indecency” ( الْفَاحِشَةَ ), that is, unlawful sexual intercourse ( الزنا ), so called because of its extreme moral repulsiveness and the gravity of its prohibition in the Sacred Law, “from among your women”—Muslim women—“summon four witnesses to testify against them.” Require those who accuse them to produce four upright believers who witnessed the act unmistakably, as [the classical legal simile says] the kohl-stick entering its container. Four witnesses are required as an exceptional protection of the believer’s reputation and privacy, or so that the proof may consist of two witnesses for each party. “If they testify” to that effect, “then confine the women in houses”: make the houses their places of imprisonment “until death takes them,” completing their lifespan, or the Angel of Death takes them, “or God appoints some way for them” ( سَبِيلًا ), such as a specified fixed penalty ( حدّ ) which releases them from confinement. That was the early rule of Islam, subsequently abrogated by the prescribed penalties in Sūrat al-Nūr. It is also possible to understand the verse as recommending confinement even after flogging, so that the women do not return to illicit relations through going outside and meeting men. Their fixed penalty is then left to the verse of al-Nūr. Confinement was specifically mentioned for women, as is clear from the following words, “The two who commit it among you,” meaning [on his interpretation] the man and woman who commit fornication: “inflict a penalty upon them,” by admonition and reproach. “If they repent and amend themselves, turn away from them”: stop imposing reproach, or refrain from recalling and disclosing their past wrongdoing. Some say that the second verse was revealed before the first: the succession of punishments for fornication was then admonition, confinement, and finally flogging. Others apply confinement to women engaging in same-sex acts and admonition to men engaging in same-sex acts, leaving the provisions in Sūrat al-Nūr for illicit intercourse. What appears to Ibn ʿAjība to have been the earliest ruling concerning fornication is that women were confined to their homes after admonition until death, or until God provided them a way through marriage to someone who would keep them chaste; and that men were subjected to reproach, public condemnation and [social] restraint until their repentance became manifest. All this was then abrogated by the fixed penalties: one hundred lashes and one year of exile for an unmarried offender, and stoning for an offender previously married in the relevant legal sense ( المحصن ). And God knows best. [N110]","anchor":"en-q4-15-16-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-15-16-s2","r":"q4-15-16","title":"Confine destructive desires, not the body itself","text":"When the servant’s self ( النفس ) grows rebellious and wishes to perpetrate indecencies, he should call upon the recording guardians ( الحفظة )—those who register his misdeeds—to testify against it. If it is still unashamed, he should discipline it by confining it in the prison of hunger, spiritual seclusion ( الخلوة ) and silence until it dies to those desires, or until God creates a path for it through the servant’s reaching a shaykh who makes him absent from his self, or by a powerful spiritual arrival ( وارد ) of disturbing fear or unsettling longing. If the self repents and is reformed, he should cease his reproach of it and occupy himself in remembrance of God ( الذكر ), until he is absent from everything besides Him. And God grants success.","anchor":"en-q4-15-16-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-15-16-s3","r":"q4-15-16","title":"","text":"Then the Real mentions the time at which repentance is accepted.","anchor":"en-q4-15-16-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-17-18","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers 4:17–18","anchor":"unit-q4-17-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-1","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللَّهِ لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السُّوءَ بِجَهالَةٍ ثُمَّ يَتُوبُونَ مِنْ قَرِيبٍ فَأُولئِكَ يَتُوبُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً (17) وَلَيْسَتِ التَّوْبَةُ لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السَّيِّئاتِ حَتَّى إِذا حَضَرَ أَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قالَ إِنِّي تُبْتُ الْآنَ وَلا الَّذِينَ يَمُوتُونَ وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ أُولئِكَ أَعْتَدْنا لَهُمْ عَذاباً أَلِيماً (18)","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-2","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ التي يُستحق عَلَى اللَّهِ قبولُها فضلاً وإحسانًا هي لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السُّوءَ أي: المعاصي متلبسين بِجَهالَةٍ أي: سفاهة وجهل وسوء أدب، فكل من اشتغل بالمعصية فهو جاهل بالله، قد انتزع منه الإيمان حتى يفرغ، وإن كان عالمًا بكونها معصية، ثُمَّ يَتُوبُونَ بعد تلك المعصية مِنْ قَرِيبٍ أي: من زمن قريب، وهو قبل حضور الموت لقوله بعدُ: حَتَّى إِذا حَضَرَ أَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ، وقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «إن الله يقبلُ توبةَّ العبْدِ مَا لمْ يُغَرْغِرُ» وإنما جعله قريبًا لأن الدنيا سريعة الزوال، متاعها قليل وزمانها قريب، فَأُولئِكَ يَتُوبُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ تصديقاً لوعده المتقدم، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً بإخلاصهم التوبة، حَكِيماً في ترك معاقبة التائب، إذ الحكمة هي وضع الشيء في محله.","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-3","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"وعن الحسن: قال: قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «لما أُهبط إبليسُ قال: وعزتك وعظمتك لا أفارق ابنَ آدم حتى تفارقَ روحُه جسدَه، قال الله تعالى: وعزتي وعظمتي لا أحجب التوبة عن عبدي حتى يغرغر بها» . وعن أبي سعيد الخدري أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: «إنّ الشيطانَ قال: وعزتِك لا أبرح أُغوى عبادكَ، ما دامتْ أرواحهم في أجسادهم. قال الله تعالى: وعزتي وجلالي وارتفاع مكاني لا أزال أغفر لهم ما استغفروني» .","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-4","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"قال ابن جزي: وإذا تاب العبد توبة صحيحة بشروطها، فيقطع بقبول توبته عند جمهور العلماء. وقال أبو المعالي: يغلب ذلك على الظن ولا يقطع. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-5","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"وَلَيْسَتِ التَّوْبَةُ مقبولة لِلَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السَّيِّئاتِ حَتَّى إِذا حَضَرَ أَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ أي: بلغت الحلقوم قالَ إِنِّي تُبْتُ الْآنَ وَلَا الَّذِينَ يَمُوتُونَ وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ فلا توبة لهم، أُولئِكَ أَعْتَدْنا أي: أعددنا وهيأنا لَهُمْ عَذاباً أَلِيماً، قال البيضاوي: سوَّى الحقُ تعالى بين من سوَّف التوبة إلى حضور الموت من الفسقة، وبين مَن مات على الكفر في نفي التوبة للمبالغة في عدم الاعتداد بها في تلك الحالة، وكأنه يقول: توبة هؤلاء وعدم توبة هؤلاء سواء. وقيل: المراد بالذين يعملون السوء: عصاة المؤمنين، وبالذين يعملون السيئات: المنافقون لتضاعف كفرهم، وبالذين يموتون: الكفار. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-6","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"الإشارة: توبة العوام ليست كتوبة الخواص، إنَّ الله يمهل العوام ترغيبًا لهم في الرجوع، ويُعاقب الخواص على التأخير على قدر مقامهم في القرب من الحضرة، فكلما عظُم القربُ عظمت المحاسبة على ترك المراقبة، منهم من يسامح له في لحظة، ومنهم في ساعة، ومنهم في ساعتين، على قدر المقام، ثم يُعاتبهم ويردهم إلى الحضرة.","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-7","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"وقال شيخ شيوخنا سيدي عبد الرحمن الفاسي في حاشيته: إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللَّهِ أي: إنما الهداية بعد الذلة، على الله لأنه الذي يُخلص من قَهْره بكرمه الفياض وبرحمته التي غلبت غضبه، كما قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-8","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"كَتَبَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلى نَفْسِهِ الرَّحْمَةَ، ونبه على وقوع الذنب بهم قهرًا، ثم تداركهم بالهداية والإنابة، فضلاً على علمه بتربيتهم وتدريجهم لمعرفته بالعلم والحكمة بقوله: وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-17-18-9","r":"q4-17-18","title":"4:17–18 — Repentance before death and the different accountability of ordinary and advanced seekers","text":"ثم شرع فى أحكام النكاح، وبدأ بالعضل لأنه يتعذر معه العقد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-17-18-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-17-18-s1","r":"q4-17-18","title":"Wrongdoing in ignorance and the point at which repentance is barred","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: “God’s acceptance of repentance” ( إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللَّهِ )—the repentance whose acceptance God has graciously undertaken, as a favor and kindness—is for those who do evil, that is, acts of disobedience, “in ignorance” ( بِجَهَالَةٍ ), in the sense of foolishness, lack of discernment, and failure in proper conduct. Everyone engaged in wrongdoing is in that moment ignorant of God; faith has been withdrawn from him until he ceases, even if he knows that what he does is a sin. “Then they repent soon afterward” ( مِنْ قَرِيبٍ ), meaning before the onset of death, as clarified by the later words “until death comes to one of them.” The Prophet said, “God accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he has not begun to gasp at death” ( إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَقْبَلُ تَوْبَةَ الْعَبْدِ مَا لَمْ يُغَرْغِرْ ). [H013] The verse describes that interval as “near” because this world passes swiftly: its goods are few and its lifetime short. “Those are the ones to whom God turns in mercy,” fulfilling His earlier promise; He knows the sincerity of their repentance and is wise in not punishing the repentant, for wisdom is to put each thing in its right place. A narration attributed through al-Ḥasan says that the Prophet reported: When Iblīs was brought down, he said, “By Your might and majesty, I shall not leave the son of Adam until his spirit leaves his body.” God said: “By My might and majesty, I shall not withhold repentance from My servant until he reaches the death-rattle.” [H014] And from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, the Prophet is reported to have said: “The Devil said, ‘By Your might, I shall not cease misleading Your servants as long as their souls are in their bodies.’ God—exalted is He—said, ‘By My might and majesty and the loftiness of My station, I shall continue forgiving them so long as they seek forgiveness from Me.’” [H015] Ibn Juzayy says: When the servant repents with genuine repentance, fulfilling its conditions, most scholars hold that he can be certain of its acceptance. Abū al-Maʿālī held instead that acceptance is strongly probable, rather than certain. Here ends the quotation.","anchor":"en-q4-17-18-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-17-18-s2","r":"q4-17-18","title":"Repentance deferred until the death-rattle","text":"“Repentance is not accepted” for those who persist in sinful deeds “until, when death comes to one of them,” that is, when it reaches his throat, “he says, ‘Now I have repented,’” nor for those who “die while unbelievers.” For these no repentance remains; “We have prepared for them a painful punishment.” Al-Bayḍāwī says: God equates those who delay repentance until the presence of death, although sinful believers, with those who die in unbelief, in negating the acceptance of repentance, to emphasize how little such last-minute repentance counts at that point—as though the one’s repentance and the other’s lack of it are alike. Another interpretation understands those who do “wrong” as disobedient believers, those who persist in “evil deeds” as hypocrites on account of the doubling of their unbelief, and those who die as unbelievers as unbelievers openly so. Here ends the quotation.","anchor":"en-q4-17-18-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-17-18-s3","r":"q4-17-18","title":"Repentance in proportion to one’s degree of nearness","text":"Repentance among ordinary people ( توبة العوام ) is not like repentance among the elect ( توبة الخواص ). God grants respite to the ordinary to encourage them to return, but calls the elect to account for delay in proportion to their station of proximity to the divine Presence ( الحضرة ). The greater the nearness, the greater the reckoning for neglecting watchfulness ( المراقبة ): some are indulged for an instant, others for an hour, still others for two hours, according to their station; then they are reproached and returned to the Presence. Our masters’ master, Sīdī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Fāsī, says in his marginal commentary concerning “repentance is upon God” ( إِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللَّهِ ): This means that guidance after abasement belongs to God, for it is He who releases people from His irresistible power ( قهر ) through abundant generosity and through His mercy that prevails over His wrath, as He says, “Your Lord has prescribed mercy upon Himself” ( كَتَبَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ الرَّحْمَةَ ) [Q 6:54]. The expression draws attention to how sin overtakes them under overpowering circumstances, after which He reaches them with guidance and penitence, as a grace arising from His knowledge of how to educate them and bring them by degrees into knowing Him. Hence His words, “God is Knowing, Wise.” Here ends the note.","anchor":"en-q4-17-18-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-17-18-s4","r":"q4-17-18","title":"","text":"He then begins the rules governing marriage, starting with unjust obstruction ( العَضْل ), because it prevents the contract from being concluded.","anchor":"en-q4-17-18-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-19","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self 4:19","anchor":"unit-q4-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-1","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ أَنْ تَرِثُوا النِّساءَ كَرْهاً وَلا تَعْضُلُوهُنَّ لِتَذْهَبُوا بِبَعْضِ مَآ آتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ إِلاَّ أَنْ يَأْتِينَ بِفاحِشَةٍ مُبَيِّنَةٍ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-19-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-2","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"قلت: أصل العضل: التضييق، يقال: عضلَت الدجاجة ببيضها إذا ضاقت، ثم أُطلق عُرفًا على منع المرأة من التزوج.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-3","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا يحل لكم أن تمنعوا النساء من النكاح لترثوا ما لهن كَرْهاً. قال ابن عباس: كانوا في الجاهلية إذا مات الرجل، وله امرأة، كان قريبه من عصبته أحق بها من نفسها ومن غيره، فإن شاء تزوجها من غير صداق، إلا الصداق الأول الذي أصدقها الميت، وإن شاء زوّجها غيره وأخذ صداقها ولم يُعطها شيئًا، وإن شاء عَضَلهَا وضيَّق عليها لتفتدى منه بما ورثت من الميت، أو تموت فيرثُها، وإن ذهبت إلى أهلها قبل أن يُلقِيَ وليُّ زوجها ثوبَه عليها فهي أحق بنفسها. فكانوا على ذلك في أول الإسلام، حتى توفي أبو قَيس بن الأَسْلتَ الأنصاري، وترك امرأته «كبشة بنت معن الأنصارية» ، فقام ابنٌ له من غيرها فطرح ثوبه عليها، ثم تركها ولم يقربها، ولم ينفق عليها، يضارّها لتفتدى منه، فأتت إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقالت: يا رسول الله إن أبا قيس تُوفي ووَرِثَ نكاحي ابنُه، وقد أضرَّ بي وطوّل عليّ، فلا هو ينفق عليّ ولا يدخل بي، ولا يخلي سبيلي، فقال لها النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «اقعدي في بيتك حتى يأتَي فيك أمرُ الله» . قالت: فانصرفتُ وسمعت بذلك النساءُ في المدينة فأتين النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وهو في مسجد الفضيخ، فقلن: يا رسول الله: ما نحن إلا كهيئة كبشة، غير أنه لا ينكحنا الأبناء، ونكَحَنا أبناء العَم، فنزلت الآية. فمعنى الآية على هذا: لا يحل لكم أن تجعلوا النساء يُورثن عن الرجال كما يُورث المال.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-4","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"وقيل: الخطاب للأزواج الذين يمسكون المرأة في العصمة ليرثوا مالها، من غير غبطة بها، وإنما يمسكها انتظارًا لموتها، وقيل: الخطاب للأولياء الذين يمنعون ولياتهم من التزوج ليرثوهن دون الزوج.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-5","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"وَلا يحل لكم أيضًا أيها الأزواج أن تَعْضُلُوهُنَّ، أي: تحبسوهن من غير حاجة لكم فيهن لِتَذْهَبُوا بِبَعْضِ ما آتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ من الصداق افتداء فيه بإضراره. قال ابن عباس رضي الله عنه: (هي أيضًا في الأزواج الذين","anchor":"ar-q4-19-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-6","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"يمسكون المرأة ويُسيئُون عشرتها حتى تفتدى بصداقها) ، إِلَّا أَنْ يَأْتِينَ بِفاحِشَةٍ مُبَيِّنَةٍ، كالنشوز وسوء العشرة وعدم العفة، فيحل له حينئِذ حبسها حتى تفتدى منه بصداقها، فيأخذه خلعًا على مذهب مالك. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-7","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"الإشارة: لا يحل للمريد أن يُضيق على نفسه تضييقاً يُفضي إلى العطب، فالنفس كالبهيمة: علفها واستخدامها، وقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لا يكن أحدكم كالمنبت، لا أرضا قطع ولا ظهرًا أبقى» .","anchor":"ar-q4-19-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-8","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"فبعض الناس يسمعون أن من ضيَّق على نفسه أورثته العلوم، فيضيق عليها تضييقًا فاحشًا ليرث ذلك منها كرهًا، وإنما يمنعها من شهواتها الزائدة على قيام البنية، إلا أن تأتي بفاحشة مبينة، بحيث تطغى عليها، فيضيق عليها بما لا يُفضي إلى الهلاك، وهذا كله إنما ينفعه إذا صح مِلْكُه لها بالعقد الصحيح من الشيخ الكامل، وإلاَّ كان تعبه باطلاً، كمن يريد أن يرى امرأة غيره أو دابة غيره. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-9","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"ثم أمر الحق تعالى بحسن العشرة مع النساء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-19-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-10","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"... وَعاشِرُوهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ فَإِنْ كَرِهْتُمُوهُنَّ فَعَسى أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئاً وَيَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ فِيهِ خَيْراً كَثِيراً (19)","anchor":"ar-q4-19-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-11","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وعاشروا النساء بِالْمَعْرُوفِ بأن تلاطفوهن في المقال وتجملوا معهن في الفعال، أو يَتَزَيَّنُ لها كما تتزين له. قال الورتجبي: كونوا في معاشرتهن في مقام الأنس وروح المحبة، وفرح العشق حين أنتم مخصوصون بالتمكين والاستقامة والولاية، فإن معاشرة النساء لا تليق إلا في المستأنس بالله، كالنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم وجميع المستأنسين من الأولياء والأبدال، حيث أخبر صلّى الله عليه وسلم عن كمال مقام أُنْسِه بالله ورؤيته لجمال مشاهدته حيث قال: «حُبِّبَ إلي من دنياكم ثَلاث: الطيب، والنساء، وجُعلت قرة عيني في الصلاة. (١)»","anchor":"ar-q4-19-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-12","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"ثم قال: عن ذي النون: المستأنس بالله يستأنس بكل شيء مليح ووجه صبيح، وبكل صوت طيب وبكل رائحة طيبة. ثم قال: عن ابن المبارك: العشرة الصحيحة: ما لا يورثك الندم عاجلاً ولا آجلاً، وقال أبو حفص: المعاشرة بالمعروف: حسن الخلق مع العيال فيما ساءك. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-13","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"فَإِنْ كَرِهْتُمُوهُنَّ فاصبروا فَعَسى أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئاً وَيَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ فِيهِ خَيْراً كَثِيراً إما ولدًا صالحًا أو عاقبة حسنة في الدين. قال ابن عمر: إن الرجل يستخير الله فيخار له فيسخط على ربه، فلا يلبث أن ينظر في العاقبة فإذا هو قد خير له. هـ. حكى أن أبا الإمام مالك رضي الله عنه تزوج امرأة فدخل عليها فوجدها سوداء، فبقي متفكرًا","anchor":"ar-q4-19-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-14","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"ولم يقربها، فقالت له: هل استخرت ربك؟ فقال: نعم، فقالت: أتَتَّهمُ ربك، فدخل بها، فحملت بالإمام مالك صاحب المذهب. وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم: «لا يَفْرك مؤمنٌ مؤمنة- أي لا يُبْغِضها- إن سخط منها خُلقَا رضي منها آخر» . قال الورتجبي: قيل: غيب عنك العواقب لئلا تسكن إلى مألوف، ولا تفر من مكروه.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-15","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"الإشارة: إذا طهرت النفس من البقايا، وكملت فيها المزايا، وانقادت بكليتها إلى مولاها، وجب الإحسان إليها والصلح معها ومعاشرتها بالمعروف، فإنما تجب مجاهدتها ما دامت كافرة فإذا أسلمت وانقادت وجب محبتها والإحسان إليها. فإن كرهتها في حال اعوجاجها فجاهدتها ورضتها حتى استقامت كان في عاقبة ذلك خيرٌ كثير، وعادت تأتي إليك بالعلوم اللدنية تشاهد فيها أسرارًا ربانية.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-16","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"قال الورتجبي: كل أمر من الله- سبحانه- جاء على مخالفة النفس امتحانًا واختبارًا، والنفس كارهة في العبودية فإذا ألزمت عليها حقوق الله بنعت الرياضة والمجاهدة واستقامت في عبودية الله، أول ما يطلع على قلبك أنوار جنان القرب والمشاهدة، قال الله تعالى: وَنَهَى النَّفْسَ عَنِ الْهَوى، فَإِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ هِيَ الْمَأْوى، وفى أجواف ظلام المجاهدة للعارفين شموس المجاهدات وأقمار المكاشفات. هـ. المراد منه.","anchor":"ar-q4-19-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-19-17","r":"q4-19","title":"4:19 — Women’s rights in marriage; reciprocal kindness and gentleness toward the disciplined self","text":"فإذا لم يصبر العبد على أذى زوجته، وأراد فراقها، فلا بد أن يؤدى إليها صداقها، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحق جل جلاله، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-19-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s1","r":"q4-19","title":"The derivation of ʿaḍl (العَضْل)","text":"I say: The root meaning of ʿaḍl ( العَضْل ) is constraint or making a thing narrow. One says that a hen is ʿaḍilat bi-bayḍihā ( عضلت ببيضها ) when it cannot pass its egg because of constriction. In conventional usage the word came to refer to preventing a woman from marrying.","anchor":"en-q4-19-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s2","r":"q4-19","title":"The Qurʾānic prohibition of treating widows as property","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: “O believers, it is not lawful for you to prevent women from marrying in order to inherit what they own, against their will.” Ibn ʿAbbās relates that in the age of ignorance, when a man died leaving a wife, a male relative from his agnatic family ( عصبته ) regarded himself as more entitled to her than she was to herself or anyone else. If he wished he married her without a new bridal payment ( صداق ), beyond what the deceased had given her. If he wished he married her to another and took her bridal payment for himself; or he impeded and constrained her, so that she would redeem herself with the property inherited from the deceased, or eventually die and leave him her wealth. If she escaped to her family before her deceased husband’s relative cast his garment over her, she was entitled to decide for herself. Ibn ʿAjība relates that this custom persisted into the earliest Islamic period until Abū Qays ibn al-Aslat al-Anṣārī died, leaving his widow Kabsha bint Maʿn al-Anṣāriyya. A son of his from another wife cast his garment over Kabsha and then abandoned her, not consummating a marriage or providing maintenance, so that she might be compelled to purchase her freedom from him. She came to the Prophet and said: “Messenger of God, Abū Qays has died and his son has inherited control of my marriage. He has harmed and delayed me; he neither supports me nor cohabits with me, nor will he let me go.” The Prophet is reported to have replied: “Stay in your house until God makes His command regarding you.” Women in Medina learned of this and came to the Prophet while he was in the Mosque of al-Fuḍaykh, saying: “Our situation is like Kabsha’s, except that it is not sons who marry us but cousins.” Then the verse was revealed. [H016] On this interpretation the verse means: You are not permitted to treat women as possessions inherited from men as money is inherited. A second explanation addresses husbands who keep wives within the marriage bond solely in hope of inheriting their money when they die, without finding any affection or benefit in the marriage. A third addresses guardians who prevent female wards from marrying to ensure that their wealth comes to the guardian rather than to their eventual husbands.","anchor":"en-q4-19-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s3","r":"q4-19","title":"Forbidding coercion to recover the dower; the specified exception","text":"Nor is it lawful for husbands to “constrain” their wives, retaining them without wishing to fulfil their marital rights, “so as to take away part of what you gave them,” meaning the bridal gift ( الصداق ), by harming them until they surrender it in return for release. Ibn ʿAbbās says that this, too, concerns husbands who keep their wives while mistreating them until they offer the bridal gift to free themselves. “Unless they commit a manifest indecency” ( فَاحِشَةٍ مُبَيِّنَةٍ ), such as rebellious misconduct ( النشوز ), abusive behaviour or unchastity, in which case, on the Mālikī view Ibn ʿAjība records, a husband may constrain her until she redeems herself by a return of the bridal gift in a divorce by compensation ( خُلْع ). God knows best. [N115]","anchor":"en-q4-19-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s4","r":"q4-19","title":"The self requires nourishment as well as spiritual training","text":"The seeker ( المريد ) must not constrict his own self ( النفس ) so harshly that he brings it to destruction. The self is like a working animal: feed it and make use of its service. The Prophet is reported as saying, “Let none of you be like the traveler whose mount collapses: he neither traverses the land nor preserves his mount.” [H017] Some people hear that one who constrains his self will inherit knowledge from it, and therefore impose such severe hardship upon it that they seek to seize that knowledge by force. The right course is only to prevent desires exceeding what is required for the body’s continued existence ( قيام البنية ). If the self commits a manifest indecency, growing excessively rebellious, it may be restrained, but never to a degree that leads to destruction. All this benefits the disciple only if his ownership and discipline of the self are established by a sound contract with a complete shaykh ( الشيخ الكامل ); without that, the toil is vain, like a person seeking to see another’s wife or riding animal. [Textual note: Cairo prints يرى, “see.” The point of this analogy is difficult in that wording; “possess” is not what the printed verb says, and no alternative reading is independently attested.] And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-19-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s5","r":"q4-19","title":"","text":"The Real then commanded good companionship with women, saying: “Live with them in the recognized manner …”","anchor":"en-q4-19-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s6","r":"q4-19","title":"Good companionship (المعاشرة بالمعروف)","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: “Live with women in the recognized good manner” ( وَعَاشِرُوهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ ), by speaking gently to them and treating them kindly in your conduct; or by adorning yourself for your wife just as she adorns herself for you. Al-Wartajbī comments: In living with your wives, dwell in intimacy ( الأنس ), the spirit of love and the joy of ardent affection once you have been singled out for establishment ( التمكين ), uprightness ( الاستقامة ) and sainthood ( الولاية ). The companionship of women is proper to the one intimate with God, like the Prophet and all the saints ( الأولياء ) and substitutes ( الأبدال ) intimate with Him. For the Prophet disclosed the perfection of his intimacy with God and his vision of the beauty of witnessing ( المشاهدة ) when he said: “Of your world, three things have been made beloved to me: perfume, women; and the coolness of my eye was placed in prayer.” [H018] Al-Wartajbī further transmits from Dhū al-Nūn that a person intimate with God finds delight in every beautiful thing and pleasing face, every fine voice and agreeable scent. From Ibn al-Mubārak he gives: “Good companionship is that which causes no remorse, either immediately or in the future.” Abū Ḥafṣ says: “Living together in the recognized good manner means showing good character towards one’s family even in what displeases one.” Here ends his report. “If you dislike them,” bear patiently: “It may be that you dislike something and God places much good in it,” perhaps a righteous child or a good outcome for your religion. Ibn ʿUmar says: A man asks God to choose what is best for him, and God chooses; he is then displeased with his Lord, but before long he sees the outcome and discovers that what was chosen was best for him. Here ends his statement. A story is told that the father of Imām Mālik married a woman, entered to meet her and found her dark-skinned. He remained thoughtful and did not approach her. She asked: “Did you seek your Lord’s guidance ( استخارة )?” He replied, “Yes.” She said: “Do you suspect your Lord?” He then consummated the marriage, and she conceived Imām Mālik, the founder of the school. [N116] The Prophet said, “Let no believing man despise a believing woman: if one trait of hers displeases him, another will please him” ( لَا يَفْرَكْ مُؤْمِنٌ مُؤْمِنَةً ...). [H019] Al-Wartajbī transmits an anonymous saying: “Future outcomes are concealed from you so that you will not rest complacently in what is familiar nor flee everything disliked.”","anchor":"en-q4-19-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s7","r":"q4-19","title":"When the self becomes obedient, reconcile with it","text":"When the self has been purified of its remnants, its virtues perfected, and it submits entirely to its Master, it becomes necessary to treat it with kindness, make peace with it and live with it in the recognized good manner. Its struggle and discipline ( مجاهدة ) are required only while it remains unbelieving; when it has submitted in Islam and become obedient, love and kindness towards it become incumbent. If, while still crooked, you dislike it and struggle to train it until it grows upright, its final state will bring much good; it will return bearing divinely bestowed knowledge ( العلوم اللدنية ), and you will behold lordly mysteries within it. Al-Wartajbī says: Every command of God which runs contrary to the self is an examination and trial. The self dislikes servanthood ( العبودية ); but if you impose upon it God’s rights through spiritual training ( الرياضة ) and struggle ( المجاهدة ), until it grows upright in His service, the first thing to dawn upon the heart is the lights of the gardens of nearness and witnessing. God says, “And forbade the self its caprice: the Garden shall be its dwelling” ( وَنَهَى النَّفْسَ عَنِ الْهَوَى فَإِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ هِيَ الْمَأْوَى ) [Q 79:40–41]. In the inward depths of the darkness of struggling, the knowers behold suns of spiritual combat and moons of unveiling [XV-N001] ( المكاشفات ). Here ends the substance of his remarks.","anchor":"en-q4-19-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-19-s8","r":"q4-19","title":"","text":"If the husband cannot bear the harm he finds in living with his wife and wishes to separate, he must nonetheless pay her the bridal gift, as the Real indicates in the following verse.","anchor":"en-q4-19-s8"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-20-21","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation 4:20–21","anchor":"unit-q4-20-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-1","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"وَإِنْ أَرَدْتُمُ اسْتِبْدالَ زَوْجٍ مَكانَ زَوْجٍ وَآتَيْتُمْ إِحْداهُنَّ قِنْطاراً فَلا تَأْخُذُوا مِنْهُ شَيْئاً أَتَأْخُذُونَهُ بُهْتاناً وَإِثْماً مُبِيناً (20) وَكَيْفَ تَأْخُذُونَهُ وَقَدْ أَفْضى بَعْضُكُمْ إِلى بَعْضٍ وَأَخَذْنَ مِنْكُمْ مِيثاقاً غَلِيظاً (21)","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-2","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"قلت: «بهتانًا» : حال، أو على إسقاط الخافض.","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-3","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنْ أَرَدْتُمُ أن تبدلوا زوجًا مَكانَ زَوْجٍ أخرى بأن تُطلقوا الأولى وتتزوجوا غيرها، وقد كنتم أعطيتم إِحْداهُنَّ قِنْطاراً أو أقل أو أكثر، فَلا تَأْخُذُوا مِنْهُ شَيْئاً بل أدوه لها كاملاً. ثم وبَّخهم على ما كانوا يفعلون في الجاهلية، فقال: أَتَأْخُذُونَهُ بُهْتاناً وَإِثْماً مُبِيناً، أي: مباهتين وآثمين، أو بالبهتان والإثم الظاهر، والبهتان: الكذب الذي يبهت المكذوب عليه، رُوي أن الرجل كان إذا أراد أن يتزوج امرأة","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-4","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"جديدة، بهت التي عنده بفاحشة حتى يلجئها إلى الافتداء منه بما أعطاها ليصرفه في تزوج الجديدة، فَنُهُوا عن ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-5","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"ثم استعظم ذلك فقال: وَكَيْفَ تَأْخُذُونَهُ وَقَدْ أَفْضى بَعْضُكُمْ إِلى بَعْضٍ بالمماسة والجماع حتى تقرر الصداق واستحقته بذلك، وقد أَخَذْنَ مِنْكُمْ مِيثاقاً غَلِيظاً وهو حسن الصحبة، أو الإمساك بالمعروف والتسريح بالإحسان، أو تمكينها نفسها منه، فإنها ما مكنته إلا لوفاء العهد في الصداق ودوام العشرة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-6","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"الإشارة: إذا كان العبد مشتغلاً بجمع دنياه، عاكفًا على حظوظه وهواه، ثم استبدل مكان ذلك الانقطاع إلى مولاه والاشتغال بذكر الله، حتى أفضى إلى شهود أنوار قدسه وسناه، فلا ينبغي أن يرجع إلى شيء خرج عنه لله.","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-7","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"ولا يلتفت إلى ما ترك من أمر دنياه، فإن الرجوع في الشيء من شيم اللئام وليس من شأن الكرام، وتأمل ما قاله الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-8","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"إذا انْصَرَفَتْ نفسي عن الشيء لم تكن ... إليه بوجهِ آخرَ الدهرِ تُقبِلُ","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-9","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"وكيف تأخذُ ما خرجت عنه لله، وقد أفضيت إلى شهود أنوار جماله وسُكْنَى حماه، فاتحد عندك كل الوجود، وكل شيء عن عين بصيرتك مفقود، بعد أن أخذ عليك مواثيق العهود، ألا ترجع إلى ما كان يقطعك عن حضرة الشهود، وبالله التوفيق. وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-20-21-10","r":"q4-20-21","title":"4:20–21 — Return of the bridal gift, the solemn marital covenant, and fidelity to spiritual renunciation","text":"ثم شرع يتكلم على ما يحرم من النساء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-20-21-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-20-21-s1","r":"q4-20-21","title":"Buhtānan (بُهْتَانًا) as a circumstantial qualifier or an omitted prepositional construction","text":"I say: “By slander” ( بُهْتَانًا ) is accusative as a circumstantial qualifier ( حال ), or because a preposition has been omitted ( على إسقاط الخافض ).","anchor":"en-q4-20-21-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-20-21-s2","r":"q4-20-21","title":"The bridal payment cannot be recaptured by an invented accusation","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: “If you wish to exchange one wife in place of another,” divorcing the first to marry someone else, and you have given one of your wives a qinṭār ( قِنْطَارًا )—a great quantity of property—or less or more, “do not take any part of it back”; pay it to her in full. He then rebukes practices of the age of ignorance: “Would you take it by slander and manifest sin?”—that is, acting as slanderers and sinners, or using open calumny and wrongdoing. Buhtān ( بُهْتَان ) is a lie that astonishes or confounds the falsely accused. It is related that when a man wanted to marry a new wife he would accuse his existing wife falsely of indecency, forcing her to pay him compensation from the bridal gift he had given her, which he would use to finance the new marriage. The Qurʾān forbade this. The divine address magnifies the wrong: “How could you take it, when you have come intimately into one another’s presence?” ( وَقَدْ أَفْضَى بَعْضُكُمْ إِلَى بَعْضٍ ), by touching and marital intercourse, through which the bridal gift is confirmed and the wife’s entitlement completed. “And they have taken from you a solemn covenant” ( مِيثَاقًا غَلِيظًا ): this may mean the duty of good companionship; or retaining the wife with recognized kindness and separating with graciousness; or her giving herself to him, which she did only trusting in the fulfilment of the promised bridal gift and continued companionship. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-20-21-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-20-21-s3","r":"q4-20-21","title":"Do not reclaim what you relinquished for God","text":"If a servant was formerly occupied gathering worldly possessions and immersed in his own shares and desires, then exchanged all that for withdrawal to his Master and remembrance of God ( ذكر الله ), until he came to witness the lights of divine sanctity and radiance, he should not return to anything he relinquished for God. He should not glance back towards worldly matters he abandoned: returning to what one has renounced is a mark of the ignoble, not the generous. Consider the poet’s words: When my soul has turned away from a thing, It never turns its face back toward that thing, throughout time. How could you seize again what you gave up for God after attaining the witnessing of the lights of His Beauty and dwelling in His protected precinct? All existence has become unified for you in that vision, and everything has vanished from the sight of your inner eye, after He took solemn covenants from you never to return to what once barred you from the Presence of witnessing ( حضرة الشهود ). God grants success and guides to the straight way.","anchor":"en-q4-20-21-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-20-21-s4","r":"q4-20-21","title":"","text":"He now begins explaining which women are prohibited in marriage.","anchor":"en-q4-20-21-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-22","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh 4:22","anchor":"unit-q4-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-1","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"وَلا تَنْكِحُوا ما نَكَحَ آباؤُكُمْ مِنَ النِّساءِ إِلاَّ مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ إِنَّهُ كانَ فاحِشَةً وَمَقْتاً وَساءَ سَبِيلاً (22)","anchor":"ar-q4-22-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-2","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"قلت: أوقع «ما» على ما يعقل لقلة عقل النساء، كما تقدم (١) ، أو مصدرية، والاستثناء منقطع أو متصل على وجه المبالغة في التحريم، أي لا تنكحوا ما نكح آباؤكم إِلاَّ مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ لآبائكم إن قدرتم عليه، فهو كقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q4-22-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-3","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"لاَ عَيْبَ فِيهِمْ غَيْرَ أَنَّ سُيُوفَهُمْ ... بِهِنَّ فُلُولٌ مِنْ قِرَاعِ الْكَتَائِبِ (٢)","anchor":"ar-q4-22-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-4","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولا تتزوجوا ما تزوج به آباؤُكُمْ مِنَ النِّساءِ بالعقد في الحرائر والوطء في الإماء، إِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ فإن الله قد عفا عنكم بعد فسخه وردَّه، إِنَّهُ كانَ فاحِشَةً عظيمة عند الله،","anchor":"ar-q4-22-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-5","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"ما أحله لأحد من الأمم قبلكم، وَمَقْتاً أي: ممقوتًا فاعله عند الله وعند ذوي المروءات من عباد الله، وكان يسمى ولد الرجل من امرأة أبيه مَقيتًا ومقتيًا. وَساءَ سَبِيلًا، وبئس طريقًا لمن يريد أن يسلكه بعد التحريم.","anchor":"ar-q4-22-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-6","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"فالمراد بالنكاح في الآية: العقد، فعلى هذا لا تحرم المرأة على الولد إذا زنا بها أبوه على المشهور، قال في الرسالة:","anchor":"ar-q4-22-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-7","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"ولا يحرم بالزنا حلال. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-22-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-8","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"الإشارة: ما جرى في آباء البشرية يجري في آباء الروحانية من طريق الأدب لا من طريق الشرع، فلا ينبغي للمريد أن يتزوج بامرأة شيخه، مات عنها أو طلقها، فإن ذلك قبيح ومقت عند أرباب الأدب، وأما بنت الشيخ فإن قدر على القيام بتعظيمها فلا بأس، وقد تزوج سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه- بنت سيدنا رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، لكن السلامة في الترك أكثر.","anchor":"ar-q4-22-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-9","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"وهنا إشارة أخرى أرق، وهي أن يشير بالنساء إلى الأحوال، فلا ينبغي للفقير أن يتعاطى أحوال الشيخ، ويفعل مثله. فإن الشيخ في مقام وهو في مقام، فإذا رجع الشيخ إلى الأسباب وتعاطى العلويات، فلا يقتدى به. إلا أن يدرك مقامه، وكان شيخ شيخنا يقول: (لا تقتدوا بالأشياخ في أفعالهم، وإنما اقتدوا بهم في أقوالهم، فإن أقوالهم لكم ولهم، وأفعالهم خاصة بهم) . إِلاَّ مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ لهم من الأحوال في حال سيرهم، فخذوها وسيروا من حيث ساروا، حتى تدركوا ما أدركوا، وافعلوا ما شئتم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-22-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-22-10","r":"q4-22","title":"4:22 — Marriage to a father’s former wife and the boundaries of imitating a shaykh","text":"ثم ذكر بقية المحرمات، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-22-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-22-s1","r":"q4-22","title":"Mā for persons; the exceptional phrase illā mā qad salaf","text":"I say: “What” ( مَا ) is applied here to rational beings, and Ibn ʿAjība again explains it—following his earlier discussion—as owing to women’s alleged deficient intellect; or it may be a particle introducing a verbal noun ( مصدرية ). The exception ( الاستثناء ) may be disconnected ( منقطع ), or connected by way of rhetorical exaggeration: “Do not marry those your fathers married, except whatever marriages of theirs lie in the past, if you could do so”; compare the poet: They have no defect—except that their swords Are nicked from striking ranks of fighters. Here a supposed exception serves to intensify the prohibition rather than remove it. [N121]","anchor":"en-q4-22-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-22-s2","r":"q4-22","title":"A father’s wife is prohibited to the son","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: Do not marry any woman whom your fathers have married, whether by valid contract ( العقد ) where free women are concerned or by sexual access ( الوطء ) in the historical case of women held in bondage, “except what has already passed,” which God has forgiven you after it was dissolved and annulled. “It was an indecency” ( فَاحِشَةً ), exceedingly grave before God, and not permitted, he says, to any previous community; “and an abomination” ( مَقْتًا ), whose perpetrator is detested before God and among people of honour. A man born from a union with his father’s wife was known as maqīt ( مَقِيت ) or maqtī ( مَقْتِي ). “And an evil path” indeed for anyone choosing it after the prohibition. On this reading “marriage” ( النِّكَاح ) means the contract. It follows, according to the predominant doctrine Ibn ʿAjība reports, that if the father committed illicit intercourse with a woman this does not by itself render her forbidden in marriage to the son. As the Risāla says, “An unlawful act does not render lawful [relations] forbidden” ( ولا يحرم بالزنا حلال ). Here ends his report. [N122]","anchor":"en-q4-22-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-22-s3","r":"q4-22","title":"The etiquette of the shaykh is not identical with a legal prohibition","text":"What holds of fathers by bodily descent has a parallel among spiritual fathers ( آباء الروحانية ), by way of spiritual etiquette ( الأدب ), not by way of the revealed law ( لا من طريق الشرع ). A disciple should not marry the widow or former wife of his shaykh; such conduct is regarded as offensive and blameworthy by those concerned with proper spiritual etiquette. With the shaykh’s daughter there is no objection, provided he can fulfil the duty of honouring her. Our master ʿAlī married the daughter of the Messenger of God, yet safety is more likely in refraining. A subtler indication reads “women” ( النساء ) as spiritual states ( الأحوال ). The poor seeker ( الفقير ) should not claim or imitate his shaykh’s states as though those states were his own: the shaykh occupies one station and he another. If a shaykh returns to ordinary means ( الأسباب ), or engages with elevated matters, the disciple should not imitate him until he has reached a comparable station. Our shaykh’s shaykh used to say: “Do not imitate the shaykhs in their acts; imitate them in their words. Their words are for you and for them, but their acts are particular to them.” “Except what is past,” meaning the states the masters passed through during their own spiritual journeying ( السير ): take up those stages and journey from where they began until you have reached what they reached; then do as you wish. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-22-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-22-s4","r":"q4-22","title":"","text":"He then mentioned the remaining prohibited relationships.","anchor":"en-q4-22-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-23","r":"q4-23","title":"4:23 — Prohibited degrees of kinship, fosterage and affinity","text":"4:23 — Prohibited degrees of kinship, fosterage and affinity 4:23","anchor":"unit-q4-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-23-1","r":"q4-23","title":"4:23 — Prohibited degrees of kinship, fosterage and affinity","text":"حُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ أُمَّهاتُكُمْ وَبَناتُكُمْ وَأَخَواتُكُمْ وَعَمَّاتُكُمْ وَخالاتُكُمْ وَبَناتُ الْأَخِ وَبَناتُ الْأُخْتِ وَأُمَّهاتُكُمُ اللاَّتِي أَرْضَعْنَكُمْ وَأَخَواتُكُمْ مِنَ الرَّضاعَةِ وَأُمَّهاتُ نِسائِكُمْ وَرَبائِبُكُمُ اللاَّتِي فِي حُجُورِكُمْ مِنْ نِسائِكُمُ اللاَّتِي دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فَإِنْ لَمْ تَكُونُوا دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَحَلائِلُ أَبْنائِكُمُ الَّذِينَ مِنْ أَصْلابِكُمْ وَأَنْ تَجْمَعُوا بَيْنَ الْأُخْتَيْنِ إِلاَّ مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً (23)","anchor":"ar-q4-23-1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-23-s1","r":"q4-23","title":"Kitāba Allāhi ʿalaykum as the confirming verbal noun","text":"I say: “God’s ordinance upon you” ( كِتَابَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ ) is an emphatic verbal noun ( مصدر مؤكد ): “God has written this prescription upon you as an ordinance” ( كتب الله ذلك كتابًا ); or it may be a construction of direct exhortation ( الإغراء ).","anchor":"en-q4-23-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-23-s2","r":"q4-23","title":"Women prohibited through descent","text":"The Real—majestic is His glory—says: Several classes of women are prohibited to you in marriage, whether by blood relationship ( النسب ), suckling ( الرضاع ), or marriage affinity ( المصاهرة ). Those prohibited by descent include “your mothers,” meaning one’s own mother and the maternal and paternal grandmothers however high the line ascends; “your daughters,” meaning one’s daughter, son’s daughter and daughter’s daughter however far the line descends; “your sisters,” including full sisters, sisters by the father and sisters by the mother; “your paternal aunts,” including the father’s sisters and grandfathers’ sisters of every higher generation, full or half-sisters; “your maternal aunts,” the mother’s or grandmothers’ sisters of every higher generation, full or half-sisters; “your brother’s daughters,” daughters of full or paternal brothers and of their descendants; and “your sisters’ daughters,” including daughters and further descendants of full sisters and maternal or paternal half-sisters. The governing principle is that a man cannot marry his ancestors however high, his descendants however low, the descendants of his own parents however low, or the first generation of descendants of any ancestor higher than his parents [i.e. his aunts].","anchor":"en-q4-23-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-23-s3","r":"q4-23","title":"Prohibition arising through suckling","text":"He then lists what is prohibited by suckling: “Your mothers who suckled you and your sisters through suckling.” God names two classes in the verse, while the Sunna establishes that every category prohibited by blood is likewise prohibited by suckling. The Prophet said: “What is prohibited through suckling is what is prohibited through lineage” ( يَحْرُمُ مِنَ الرَّضَاعِ مَا يَحْرُمُ مِنَ النَّسَبِ ). [H020] Accordingly, the seven categories are: foster-mother, foster-daughter, foster-sister, foster-paternal aunt, foster-maternal aunt, foster-niece through a brother and foster-niece through a sister.","anchor":"en-q4-23-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-23-s4","r":"q4-23","title":"Affinity: mothers-in-law, stepdaughters and daughters-in-law","text":"He then speaks of the women forbidden by marriage affinity: “Your wives’ mothers.” The prohibition on a father’s wife has been mentioned, and that of a son’s wife follows. “Your stepdaughters who are in your care, from wives with whom you have consummated marriage”: the mention of being “in your care” is not a restrictive condition on the majority interpretation, but corresponds to what most often occurs. The daughter is prohibited whether she grew up in his household or not. ʿAlī is reported to have permitted marrying such a stepdaughter if she had not been brought up under the husband’s care. The phrase “with whom you have consummated marriage” ( اللَّاتِي دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ ) is, however, operative by consensus as reported here: if a man merely contracts marriage with a woman but does not consummate it, he may divorce her and marry her daughter. Hence the words: “If you have not consummated marriage with them, there is no blame upon you” in marrying the daughters. [N124] “And the wives of your sons,” that is, a woman with whom a son has contracted a marriage and to whom he thereby becomes lawfully married. She becomes prohibited to the father by the contract alone. In sum, a father’s wife, a son’s wife and a wife’s mother become prohibited by the contract, whereas the wife’s daughter becomes prohibited only upon consummation with her mother. Contracting marriage with the daughter prohibits her mother; consummation with the mother prohibits the daughter. “Those [sons] who come from your loins” excludes a woman divorced by an adopted son from this particular prohibition, as in the account of Zayd and the Messenger of God.","anchor":"en-q4-23-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-23-s5","r":"q4-23","title":"Combining two sisters","text":"“And [it is forbidden] to join two sisters” in marriage, whether full sisters or paternal or maternal half-sisters. This applies to marriage. In the historical institution of ownership of enslaved women without intercourse, no such objection was raised; regarding intercourse with two sisters under that institution, Mālik, al-Shāfiʿī and Abū Ḥanīfa forbade it, while Ibn ʿAjība reports the Ẓāhirīs as permitting it. “Except what has already passed,” meaning what happened in the age of ignorance, has been forgiven. “Truly God is Forgiving, Merciful.” [N125] Ibn ʿAbbās says: The Arabs had treated as forbidden all the unions prohibited by the Sacred Law, except a father’s wife and the simultaneous marriage of two sisters; that is why the divine speech specifically says “except what has already passed” in these two cases.","anchor":"en-q4-23-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-24","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift 4:24","anchor":"unit-q4-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-1","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"وَالْمُحْصَناتُ مِنَ النِّساءِ إِلاَّ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ كِتابَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-24-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-2","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"قلت: «كتاب الله عليكم» : مصدر مؤكد. أي: كتب الله ذلك كتاباً، أو على الإغراء.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-3","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: حُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ من النساء أصنافٌ: منها بالنسب ومنها بالرضاع ومنها بالمصاهرة: فأما التي تحرم بالنسب فهي أُمَّهاتُكُمْ، وهي الأم، والجدة من الأم ومن الأب ما عَلَوْن، وَبَناتُكُمْ وهي البنت وبنت الابن، وبنت البنت ما سفلن، وَأَخَواتُكُمْ وهي الأخت الشقيقة والتي للأب والأخت للأم، (وعماتكم) وهي أخت الوالد وأخت الجد ما علت، شقيقة أو لأب أو لأم، وَخالاتُكُمْ وهي أخت الأم وأخت الجدة ما علت، شقيقة أو لأب أو لأم، وَبَناتُ الْأَخِ الشقيق، أو للأب، وما تناسل منهم. وَبَناتُ الْأُخْتِ، فيدخل كل ما تناسل من الأخت الشقيقة أو للأب أو للأم.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-4","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"والضابط في ذلك: أنه يحرم على الرجل أصوله وإن علت، وفصوله وإن سفلت، وفصول أبويه ما سفلت، وأول فصل من كل أصل متقدم على أبويه.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-5","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"ثم ذكر ما يحرم بالرضاع، فقال: وَأُمَّهاتُكُمُ اللَّاتِي أَرْضَعْنَكُمْ وَأَخَواتُكُمْ مِنَ الرَّضاعَةِ ذكر تعالى صنفين، وحرمت السُّنَّةُ كل ما يحرم من النسب. قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «يَحْرُمُ مِنَ الرَّضَاعِ مَا يَحْرُمُ مِنَ النَّسَبِ» فيدخل الأصناف السبعة، وهي الأم من الرضاع والبنت والأخت والعمة والخالة وبنت الأخ وبنت الأخت.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-6","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"ثم ذكر ما يحرم بالمصاهرة، فقال: وَأُمَّهاتُ نِسائِكُمْ، وتقدمت زوجة الأب، وسيأتي حليلة الابن، وَرَبائِبُكُمُ اللَّاتِي فِي حُجُورِكُمْ مِنْ نِسائِكُمُ لا مفهوم لهذا القيد، لكنه جرى مجرى الغالب، فهي محرمة، كانت في حجره أم لا، على قول الجمهور، ورُوي عن علي رضي الله عنه أنه أجاز نكاحها إن لم تكن في حجره. وأما قوله:","anchor":"ar-q4-24-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-7","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"اللَّاتِي دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فهو معتبر إجماعًا، فلو عقد على المرأة ولم يدخل بها، فله طلاقها ويأخذ ابنتها، ولذلك قال: فَإِنْ لَمْ تَكُونُوا دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ أن تَنكحوهن.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-8","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"وَحَلائِلُ أَبْنائِكُمُ وهي التي عقد عليها الابن فحلت له، فتحرم على الأب بمجرد العقد. والحاصل: أن زوجة الأب وزوجة الابن وأم الزوجة يحرمن بالعقد، وأما بنت المرأة فلا تحرم إلا بالدخول بأمها، فالعقد على البنات يُحرم الأمهات، والدخول بالأمهات يُحرم البنات. وقوله تعالى: الَّذِينَ مِنْ أَصْلابِكُمْ احترز به من زوجة المتبنِّي فلا تحرم حليلته، كقضية زيد مع رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-9","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"وَأَنْ تَجْمَعُوا بَيْنَ الْأُخْتَيْنِ، شقيقتين أو للأب أو للأم، وهذا في النكاح، وأما في الملك دون الوطء فلا بأس، أما في الوطء فمنعه مالك والشافعي وأبو حنيفة، وأجازه الظاهرية، إِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ أي: في الجاهلية، فقد عفا عنكم، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً، قال ابن عباس: (كانت العرب تُحرم كل ما حرمت الشريعة إلا امرأة الأب والجمع بين الأختين، فلذلك ذكر الحق تعالى: إِلَّا ما قَدْ سَلَفَ فيهما.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-10","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"وَحرم الله تعالى- الْمُحْصَناتُ مِنَ النِّساءِ وهُنَّ اللاتي في عصمة أزواجهن، فلا يحل نكاحهن ما دُمْنَ في عصمة الزوج، إِلَّا مَّا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ مِّن الغنيمة، فإذا سُبيت الكافرة، ولها زوج، جاز لمن ملكها أن يطأها بالملك بعد الاستبراء، قال في المختصر: وهدم السبيْ النكاحَ، إلا أن تُسبى وتُسلْم في عدتها فهو أحق بها، وقد بعث رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم جيشًا إلى أَوْطَاس، فأصابوا سبيًا من العدو، ولهن أزواج من المشركين فتأثموا من غشيانهن، فنزلت الآية مُبيحة لذلك، كِتابَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ أي: كتب الله ذلك عليكم كتاباً، وهو ما حرّم في الآية من النساء.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-11","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الإنسان لا يصير كاملاً عارفًا حتى يولد ثلاث مرات بعد الأم الحسية، أولها: خروجه من بطن حب الدنيا الدنية، ثم من الغفلة والشهوات الجسمانية، ثم من ضيق الأكوان الظلمانية، إلى فضاء المشاهدة والمعاينة، وقال بعض الأولياء: (ليس منا من لم يولد مرتين) : فاعتبر الأولى والثالثة، فإذا خرج الإنسان من هذه البطون حرَّم الله عليه نكاحها والرجوع إليها.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-12","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"وكذا يحرم عليه الرجوع إلى ما تولد منه من الزلات، والأحوال الظلمانية، وما كان ألفه وتواخى معه من البطالات والمألوفات، وما وجد عليه أسلافه من التعصبات والحميات والرئاسات، ولا فرق بين ما واجهه من ذلك من قبل الآباء والأمهات، وكذلك ما ارتضع من ثدي الشهوات من لِبان الغفلة، وتراكم الأَكِنَّات (١) ، فليبادر إلى تحريمها، وفطام نفسه عنها، قبل تحكمها، كما قال البوصيري رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q4-24-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-13","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"والنَّفْسُ كالطِّفلِ إنْ تُهْمِلْهُ شَبَّ ... عَلَى حُبِّ الرَّضاعِ وإنْ تَفْطِمْهُ يَنْفَطِم","anchor":"ar-q4-24-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-14","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"وكذا يحرم عليه، صحبة من ارتضع معه في هذا الثدي قبل الفطام من الأخوة والأخوات، وكذا أمهات الخطايا، وهي حب الدنيا والرياسة والجاه، وكذلك حرمت عليكم ربائب العلائق والعوائق، لتدخلوا بلاد الحقائق، فإن لم تكونوا من أهل الحقائق فلا جناح عليكم إذ كنتم من عوام الخلائق، وكذلك يحرم عليكم ما حل لأبناء جنسكم من تعاطي الأسباب والاشتغال بها عن خدمة رب الأرباب، وأن تجمعوا بين حب الدنيا ومحبة المولى. قال الشافعي رضي الله عنه: (من ادَّعى أنه جمَعَ بين حب الدنيا وحب خالقها، فقد كذب) .","anchor":"ar-q4-24-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-15","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"إِلاَّ مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ في أيام البطالة، وكذا يحرم على المريد المتجرد المستشرف على المعاني تعاطى العلوم الظاهرة، التي دخل بها أهل الظاهر وافتضوا بكارتها- إلا ما ملكه قبل التجريد، فلا يضره إن غاب عنها في أسرار التوحيد، والله تعالى أعلم بأسرار غيبه.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-16","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى ما يحلّ من النساء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-24-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-17","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"... وَأَحَلَّ لَكُمْ مَّا وَراءَ ذلِكُمْ أَنْ تَبْتَغُوا بِأَمْوالِكُمْ مُحْصِنِينَ غَيْرَ مُسافِحِينَ فَمَا اسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِهِ مِنْهُنَّ فَآتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ فَرِيضَةً وَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيما تَراضَيْتُمْ بِهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ الْفَرِيضَةِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً (24)","anchor":"ar-q4-24-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-18","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"قلت: «وأَحَلَّ» عطف على الفعل العامل في «كتاب الله عليكم» أي: كتب الله عليكم تحريم ما ذكر، وأحل ما سوى ذلك. ومن قرأ بالبناء للمفعول فعطف على «حُرمت» . و (أن تبتغوا) مفعول لأجله، أي: إرادة أن تبتغوا. أو بدل من (وراء ذلكم) . و (محصنين) حال من الواو. والسفاح: الزنا، من السفح وهو الصب، لأنه يصب المنيّ في غير مَحِلَّهُ.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-19","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَأَحَلَّ لَكُمْ أن تتزوجوا من النساء ما سوى ذلكم المحرمات، وما سوى ما حرمته السنة بالرضاع، كما تقدم، والجمع بين المرأة وعمتها، وبين المرأة وخالتها، فقد حرَمتْه السُنة، وإنما أحل لكم نكاح النساء إرادة أن تطلبوا بأموالكم الحلال، فتصرفوها في مهور النساء.. حال كونكم مُحْصِنِينَ. أي: أعفة متحصنين بها من الحرام، غَيْرَ مُسافِحِينَ أي: غير زناة، تصبون الماء في غير موضعه، فَمَا اسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِهِ مِنْهُنَّ أي: من تمتعتم به من المنكوحات فَآتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ أي: مهورهن، لأن المهر في مقابلة الاستمتاع فَرِيضَةً، أي: مفروضة مقدرة، لا جَهْلَ فيها ولا إبهام، وَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيما تَراضَيْتُمْ بِهِ من زيادة على المهر المشروط، أو نقص منه، مِنْ بَعْدِ الْفَرِيضَةِ، التي وقع العقد عليها، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيماً بمصالح خلقه، حَكِيماً فيما شرع من الأحكام.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-20","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"وقيل قوله: فَمَا اسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِهِ ... إلى آخره. نزل في نكاح المتعة، التي كانت ثلاثة أيام في فتح مكة، ثم نُسِخَ بما روى عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أنه أباحه، ثم أصبح يقول: «أيُّهَا النَّاسِ، إِنِّي كُنْتُ أمرتكم بالاسِتْمْتَاعِ مِنَ هذه النَّساء، ألا إنَّ اللهَ حَرَمَ ذَلِكَ إلىَ يَوْمِ القِيَامةِ» . وهو النكاح المؤقت بوقت معلوم، سُمي به لأن الغرض منه مجرد الاستمتاع. وتمتعها بما يُعطى لها. وجوَّزه ابن عباس رضي الله عنه ثم رجع عنه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-21","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"الإشارة: يقول الحق جلّ جلاله من طريق الإشارة: إذا خرجتم من بطن الشهوات، ورفضتم ما كنتم عليه من العوائد والمألوفات، وزهدتم فيما يشغل فكرتكم من العلوم الرسميات، حل لكم ما وراء ذلكم من العلوم اللدنية","anchor":"ar-q4-24-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-22","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"والأسرار الربانية، التي هي وراء طور العقول ولا تدرك بالطروس (١) ولا بالنقول، وإليها أشار ابن الفارض رضي الله عنه حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-q4-24-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-23","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"ولا تكُ مِمَنْ طَيّشَتْهُ طروسه ... بحيثُ استخفت عقَلَهُ واستفزّتِ","anchor":"ar-q4-24-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-24","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"فَثمَ وراء النّقلِ عِلْمٌ يَدِقُّ عن ... مَدارِكِ غايات العقولِ السليمةِ","anchor":"ar-q4-24-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-25","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"تَلَقيْتُه منّي وعني أَخَذْتهُ ... ونفسي كانت من عَطاءٍ مُمدَّةِ","anchor":"ar-q4-24-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-26","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"أردنا منكم أن تبتغوا ببذل أموالكم ومُهجكم تلك العلوم المقدسة، والأسرار المطهرة، متحصنين من دنس الحس والهوى، غير مباشرين لنجاسة الدنيا، ولا مصطحبين مع أهلها، لتتمتعوا بشهود أسرارنا، وأنوار قدسنا، فما استمتعتم به من ذلك، فصونوه عن غير أهله، ولا جناح عليكم فيما تراضيتم به من إعطائه لأهله، من بعد حفظه عمن لا يستحقه، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-24-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-24-27","r":"q4-24","title":"4:24 — Marriage impediments, the inward severance of attachments, and the bridal gift","text":"ثم ذكر حكم من عجز عن صداق الحرة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-24-27"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-24-s1","r":"q4-24","title":"The prohibition concerning married women","text":"God also prohibited al-muḥṣanāt (المحصنات) among women: that is, women bound by marriage to their husbands. It is therefore not lawful to marry them while the marriage bond remains in force, “except those whom your right hands possess” from the spoils of war. Thus, when a non-Muslim woman is captured while she has a husband, the person who becomes her owner, according to the rule Ibn ʿAjība is describing, may have intercourse with her by reason of ownership after istibrāʾ (الاستبراء), the ascertainment that her womb is free [from a previous pregnancy]. In the Mukhtaṣar it is said: “Captivity annuls marriage—except that, if she is captured and embraces Islam during her waiting period ( ʿidda , العدة), he [her previous husband] has the prior claim to her.” [N127] The Messenger of God, blessings and peace upon him, sent an army to Awṭās. They took captive women from the enemy who had husbands among the polytheists. The Muslims felt religious scruple ( taʾaththum , التأثم) about intercourse with them, and this verse was revealed permitting it [under the legal conditions understood by the commentator]. [H021] “God’s ordinance upon you” means that God prescribed this for you as an ordinance: the prohibition of the women named in the verse.","anchor":"en-q4-24-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-24-s2","r":"q4-24","title":"the three births and the renunciation of former attachments","text":"Know that a human being does not become a perfected knower ( ʿārif kāmil , عارف كامل) until he is born three times after his birth from his bodily mother. The first is his emergence from the womb of love for this lowly world; then [he emerges] from heedlessness and bodily appetites; then from the narrowness of the darkened created orders ( al-akwān al-ẓulmāniyya , الأكوان الظلمانية), into the open expanse of witnessing and direct vision ( al-mushāhada wa-l-muʿāyana , المشاهدة والمعاينة). One of the saints said: “One who has not been born twice is not of us.” Here he counted the first and the third [of the births just described]. When a person has emerged from these wombs, God has made it forbidden for him to “marry” them or return to them. [N128] In the same way, returning to the lapses and dark states born from him is forbidden for him; likewise the vain pursuits and customary attachments with which he had formerly made himself intimate and brotherly, and the partisanships, heated loyalties and claims to eminence in which he found his forebears established. There is no difference here between what confronts him through the fathers and what confronts him through the mothers. So too with what he has suckled from the breast of appetites—the milk of heedlessness—and with the veils ( akinna , أكنة) that have accumulated over him: let him hasten to prohibit such things to himself and wean his soul from them before they gain mastery over it. As al-Būṣīrī, may God be pleased with him, said: The soul is like a child: neglect it, and it will grow up loving to suckle; wean it, and it will be weaned. Likewise forbidden to him is the companionship of the brothers and sisters who suckled alongside him from that breast before weaning. The “mothers of sins,” too, are love of this world, command, and standing among people ( al-jāh , الجاه). Likewise the “stepdaughters” of entanglements and obstacles ( al-ʿalāʾiq wa-l-ʿawāʾiq , العلائق والعوائق) have been forbidden to you, so that you may enter the lands of realities ( al-ḥaqāʾiq , الحقائق). If you are not among the people of realities, however, there is no blame upon you, for you belong to the ordinary company of created beings. Equally forbidden to [the advanced seeker] are occupations with worldly means ( al-asbāb , الأسباب)—though permissible for people of his own kind—when they distract him from serving the Lord of lords, and also the combining of love of the world with love of the Master. Al-Shāfiʿī, may God be pleased with him, is reported to have said: “Whoever claims to have joined love of the world with love of its Creator has lied.” [N129] “Except what has gone before” during the days of idle distraction. Similarly, a seeker ( murīd ) who has become detached ( mutajarrid , متجرد) and is looking toward the inward meanings must not busy himself with the exoteric sciences which the people of the outward have entered and whose virginity they have taken—except what he acquired before detachment: such knowledge does not harm him if he becomes absent from it in the secrets of divine unity ( asrār al-tawḥīd , أسرار التوحيد). God knows best the secrets of His Unseen.","anchor":"en-q4-24-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-24-s3","r":"q4-24","title":"","text":"He then speaks of the women who are lawful to marry","anchor":"en-q4-24-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-24-s4","r":"q4-24","title":"The grammar of “made lawful,” seeking with wealth, and chastity","text":"“And made lawful to you …” I say: Ibn ʿAjība first construes “and made lawful” in an active reading, wa-aḥalla (وأَحَلَّ), as coordinated ( ʿaṭf , عطف) with the unexpressed verb governing “God’s ordinance upon you” : that is, God prescribed the prohibition of those mentioned and made lawful what lies beyond them. In the passive reading wa-uḥilla (وأُحِلَّ), the verb is instead coordinated with “prohibited [to you]” ( ḥurrimat , حرمت). [N142] “That you should seek” ( an tabtaghū , أن تبتغوا) is an object of purpose ( mafʿūl li-ajlih , مفعول لأجله)—“with the intention that you seek”—or a substitute ( badal , بدل) for “beyond these” . “In chastity” ( muḥṣinīn , محصنين) is a circumstantial accusative ( ḥāl , حال) relating to the plural pronoun. Sifāḥ (السفاح) is fornication, derived from safḥ (السفح), “pouring out,” because semen is poured where it does not belong.","anchor":"en-q4-24-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-24-s5","r":"q4-24","title":"Lawful marriage, dowers, and the question of temporary marriage","text":"The Real—majestic is His majesty—says: “And made lawful to you what lies beyond these” : marrying women other than those listed as prohibited, apart also from the prohibitions established by the Sunna through suckling, as mentioned earlier, and the prohibition of combining marriage to a woman and her paternal aunt, or to a woman and her maternal aunt. These the Sunna has prohibited. [H031] God permitted the marriage of women in order that you might seek what is lawful through your wealth, devoting it to women’s bridal gifts ( muhūr , مهور), while being “chaste” ( muḥṣinīn ): preserving your modesty and securing yourselves by marriage against what is forbidden, “not fornicators” ( musāfiḥīn , مسافحين), who cast their water where it does not belong. “So for those of them with whom you have enjoyed [marital intimacy], give them their wages as an obligation” : that is, give the women you have married their bridal gifts, for the bridal gift corresponds to marital enjoyment; it is an obligatory, stipulated amount, neither unknown nor ambiguous. “There is no blame upon you in what you mutually agree upon after the obligation” : in an increase above the contractually stipulated bridal gift or a reduction of it, after the amount upon which the marriage contract was made. “God has ever been Knowing” of His creatures’ welfare and “Wise” in the rulings He has prescribed. Another view says that “So for those of them with whom you have enjoyed …” to the end was revealed concerning nikāḥ al-mutʿa (نكاح المتعة), the fixed-term marriage said to have been permitted for three days at the conquest of Mecca and then abrogated ( nusikha , نُسخ). This is supported by what is transmitted of the Prophet, blessings and peace upon him: having permitted it, he then said the following morning, “People! I had allowed you to seek temporary enjoyment with these women, but God has forbidden this until the Day of Resurrection.” [H022] It is a marriage stipulated for a known time, called mutʿa because the object is enjoyment alone, together with the woman’s enjoyment of what she is given. Ibn ʿAbbās permitted it and then, according to this report, withdrew his permission. God knows best. [N130]","anchor":"en-q4-24-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-24-s6","r":"q4-24","title":"knowledge beyond discursive transmission","text":"The Real—majestic is His majesty—says by way of allusion: When you have emerged from the womb of appetites, abandoned your previous habits and familiar attachments, and renounced the conventional, formally transmitted sciences ( al-ʿulūm al-rasmiyyāt , العلوم الرسميات) that preoccupy your thought, then there becomes lawful for you what lies beyond them: the God-given sciences ( al-ʿulūm al-ladunniyya , العلوم اللدنية) and lordly secrets ( al-asrār al-rabbāniyya , الأسرار الربانية), which transcend the reach of discursive intellects and cannot be grasped from written pages ( ṭurūs , طروس) or transmitted reports ( nuqūl , نقول). Ibn al-Fāriḍ, may God be pleased with him, alluded to these when he said: Be not among those whom their pages have made giddy, so that they have unsettled their intellect and swept it away. For beyond transmission there is knowledge too subtle for the furthest comprehension of sound intellects. I received it from myself and took it from myself, while my soul was sustained by a gift. We wished you, through the expenditure of your wealth and your very lives ( muhaj , مهج), to seek those holy sciences and purified secrets, safeguarding yourselves against the taint of sense perception ( al-ḥiss , الحس) and caprice ( al-hawā , الهوى), neither touching the impurity of the world nor keeping company with its people, so that you may delight in witnessing Our secrets and the lights of Our holiness. Whatever you have enjoyed of these, guard it from those unworthy of it; yet there is no blame upon you in mutually agreeing to give it to those worthy of it, once you have protected it from those who have no rightful claim. And God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-24-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-24-s7","r":"q4-24","title":"","text":"He then gives the ruling concerning someone unable to afford the bridal gift of a free woman","anchor":"en-q4-24-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-25-28","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation 4:25–28","anchor":"unit-q4-25-28"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-1","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"وَمَنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ مِنْكُمْ طَوْلاً أَنْ يَنْكِحَ الْمُحْصَناتِ الْمُؤْمِناتِ فَمِنْ مَّا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ مِنْ فَتَياتِكُمُ الْمُؤْمِناتِ وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِإِيمانِكُمْ بَعْضُكُمْ مِنْ بَعْضٍ فَانْكِحُوهُنَّ بِإِذْنِ أَهْلِهِنَّ وَآتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ مُحْصَناتٍ غَيْرَ مُسافِحاتٍ وَلا مُتَّخِذاتِ أَخْدانٍ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-2","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"قلت: الطول: الغنى والسعة، ويطلق على العلو، مصدر طال طَوْلاً، وهو مفعول «يستطع» أو مصدر له- لتقارب معناهما، و (أن ينكح) بدل منه على الأول، أو مفعول به على الثاني، أي: لأن ينكح، و (محصنات غير مسافحات) ، حالان، والعامل فيه: (أنكحوهن) ، والخدن: الخليل.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-3","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعْ مِنْكُمْ طَوْلًا أي: لم يجد غنى يقدر به على نكاح الْمُحْصَناتُ، أي: الحرائر الْمُؤْمِناتِ، فليتزوج مِّن مَّا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ، من الإماء المؤمنات دون الكافرات، فإن أظهرت الإيمان فاكتفوا بذلك، وعلم الباطن لا يعلمه إلا الله، وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِإِيمانِكُمْ فلا يمنعكم من نكاحهن خوف المعرة، فإنما أنتم جنس واحد، ودينكم واحد، بَعْضُكُمْ مِنْ بَعْضٍ فلا تستنكفوا من نكاحهن،","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-4","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"فَانْكِحُوهُنَّ بِإِذْنِ أَهْلِهِنَّ، أي أربابهن، حتى يعقدوا لكم نكاحهن، وَآتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ: أي: مهورهن، وهن أحق به دون ساداتهن، على مذهب مالك، بِالْمَعْرُوفِ من غير مطل، ولا نقص، على ما تقتضيه السنة. حال كونهن مُحْصَناتٍ أي: عفيفات غَيْرَ مُسافِحاتٍ أي: غير زانيات وَلا مُتَّخِذاتِ أَخْدانٍ. أي: أصحاب يزنون بهن. وكان في الجاهلية مِن النساء مَنْ تتخذ صاحبًا واحدًا تزني معه خاصة، ومنها من لا ترد يد لامس.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-5","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"قال ابنُ جزي: مذهب مالك وأكثر أصحابه أنه لا يجوز للحر نكاح الأمة إلا بشرطين: أحدهما: عدم الطول وهو ألاَّ يجد ما يتزوج به حُرة، والآخر: خوف العنت وهو الزنا. لقوله بعد هذا: ذلِكَ لِمَنْ خَشِيَ الْعَنَتَ مِنْكُمْ، وأجاز ابن القاسم نكاحهن دون الشرطين، على القول بأن دليل الخطاب لا يُعتبر، واتفقوا على اشتراط الإسلام في الأمة، لقوله: مِنْ فَتَياتِكُمُ الْمُؤْمِناتِ إلا أهل العراق فلم يشترطوه. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-6","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"الإشارة: فمن لم يستطع أن ينكح أبكار الحقائق، لكونه لم يقدر أن يدفع عن قلبه الشواغل والعلائق، فليتنزل لنكاح العلوم الرسمية والأعمال الحسية، بأخذها من أربابها، ويحصنها بالإخلاص في أخذها، ويقوم بحقها بقدر الإمكان، وهو بذلها لأهلها، والصبر على نشرها، والله لا يضيع أجرَ من أحسن عملاً، فإن صح قصده، وخلص عمله، قيض الله له وليًا من أوليائه يغنيه بالله، حتى يصير من الأغنياء به، فيتأهل لنكاح الحرائر، ويلتحق بأولياء الله الأكابر، (وَمَا ذلك على الله بعزيز) .","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-7","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"قال الشيخ أبو الحسن الشاذلى رضي الله عنه لما تكلم على ثمرات المحبة- قال: فترى النفس مائلة لطاعته، والعقل متحصنا بمعرفته (١) ، والروح مأخوذة في حضرته، والسر مغمورا في مشاهدته، والعبد يستزيد [من حبه ] (٢) فيُزاد ويفاتح بما هو أعذب من لذيذ مناجاته، فيكسي حلل التقريب على بساط القربة، ويمس أبكار الحقائق وثيبات العلوم. هـ. فعلم الحقائق أبكار، وما يوصل إليه من علوم الطريقة ثيبات حرائر، وما سواها من علوم الرسوم إماء بالنسبة إلى غيرها، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-8","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"ثم ذكر حدَّ الأمَةِ إذا زنت، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-10","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"... فَإِذا أُحْصِنَّ فَإِنْ أَتَيْنَ بِفاحِشَةٍ فَعَلَيْهِنَّ نِصْفُ مَا عَلَى الْمُحْصَناتِ مِنَ الْعَذابِ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-11","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"قلت: أحصن الرجل- بفتح الهمزة وضمها-: صار محصنًا بالفتح والكسر، وهذا مما اتحد فيه البناء للفاعل والمفعول. وقيل بالفتح، معناه: أسلم، وبالضم: تزوج.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-12","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إن الإماء إذا تزوجن فَإِنْ أَتَيْنَ بِفاحِشَةٍ، وهو الزنا، فعليهن نصف ما على الحرة من الحد، وهو خمسون، لأن حد البكر مائة. ويفهم منه أنها لا ترجم لأن الرجم لا يتبعض. وكذلك الذكور من العبيد عليهم نصف الحدود كلها، ولا رجم عليهم، وسمَى الحد عذابًا، كقوله: وَلْيَشْهَدْ عَذابَهُما طائِفَةٌ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-13","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"الإشارة: بقدر ما يعلو المقام يُشدد العقاب، وبقدر ما يحصل من القرب يُطلَب الآداب، فليست المعصية في البعد كالمعصية في القرب، وليس يُطلب من البعيد ما يُطلب من القريب، وانظر إلى أزواج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم حيث قال تعالى لهن: يَا نِساءَ النَّبِيِّ مَنْ يَأْتِ مِنْكُنَّ بِفاحِشَةٍ مُبَيِّنَةٍ يُضاعَفْ لَهَا الْعَذابُ ضِعْفَيْنِ. وما ذلك إلا لحظوتهن وشدة قربهن من الله. ولذلك كان لا يدخل الحضرة إلا أهل الآداب والتهذيب، بعد التدريج والتدريب، وتأمل قضيةَ الجنيد، حيث قيل له في المنام: مثلُك لا يُرضى منه هذا، حيث خطر على قلبه الاعتراض على السائل، غير أن المقربين يعاتبون، ويردون إلى الحضرة، وأهلُ البُعد يزيدون بُعداً، ولكن لا يشعرون، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-14","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"ثم ذكر شرط تزوج الأمة لعادم الطَوْل، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-15","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"... ذلِكَ لِمَنْ خَشِيَ الْعَنَتَ مِنْكُمْ وَأَنْ تَصْبِرُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ (25) يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ وَيَهْدِيَكُمْ سُنَنَ الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَيَتُوبَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ (26) وَاللَّهُ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَيُرِيدُ الَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ الشَّهَواتِ أَنْ تَمِيلُوا مَيْلاً عَظِيماً (27) يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ أَنْ يُخَفِّفَ عَنْكُمْ وَخُلِقَ الْإِنْسانُ ضَعِيفاً (28)","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-16","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"قلت: العنت: المشقة والضرر، ولا ضرر أعظم من مواقعة الإثم، ولا سيما بأفحش الفواحش وهو الزنا، (يريد الله ليبين لكم) ، أي: لأن يُبين، واللام زائدة في المفعول، لتأكيد معنى الاستقبال اللازم للإرادة.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-17","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ذلِكَ أي: نكاح الإماء إنما أبَحْتُهُ لمن خشي الوقوع في الزنا، الذي هو أقبح الفواحش، فنكاح الأمةُ، وإرقاق الولد يباع في الأسواق أخف من الزنا. وَأَنْ تَصْبِرُوا عن نكاحهن، مع التعفف عن الزنا، خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ لئلا يرق أولادكم. وعن أنس قال: سمعت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: «من أراد أن يَلْقَى اللهَ طَاهِرًا مُطَهَّرًا فَلْيَتَزَوَّج الْحَرائِر» وقال أبو هريرة: سمعته صلّى الله عليه وسلم يقول: «الحَرَائِر صَلاحُ البَيْتَ، والإماء هلاك البيت (١) » .","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-18","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ لكم فيما سلف من المخالفة، رَحِيمٌ بكم، حيث رخَّص لكم عند خوف الإثم نكاحَ الأمَة، يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ شرائع دينكم، ومصالح أموركم، وَيَهْدِيَكُمْ سُنَنَ الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ أي: مناهج مَنْ تقدمكم من أهل الرشد، كالأنبياء والصالحين، لتسلكوا مناهجهم، كحفظ الأموال والأنساب، وتحريم الأمهات والبنات والأخوات، فإنهن محرمات على من قبلكم، وَيَتُوبَ عَلَيْكُمْ أي: يغفر ذنوبكم الماضية، أو يرشدكم إلى التوبة، أو يمنعكم من المعاصي بالعصمة. وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بما أسلفتم وما تستقبلونه من أفعالكم، حَكِيمٌ بما دبر وأبرم.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-19","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"وَاللَّهُ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْكُمْ كرره توطئة لقوله: وَيُرِيدُ الَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ الشَّهَواتِ أَنْ تَمِيلُوا عن الحق مَيْلًا عَظِيماً بموافقتهم على اتباع الشهوات واستحلال المحرمات، وكأنه تعالى يقول: إنا نريد توبتكم ورشدكم، والذين يتبعون الشهوات يريدون ميلكم وإضلالكم، والمراد بهم الزناة لأنهم يودون أن يكون الناس كلهم زناة، وأمَّا من تعاطى شهوة النكاح في الحلال، فإنه متبع للحق لا لهم، وقد قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-:","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-20","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"«تَنَاكَحُوا تَنَاسَلُوا، فَإنِّي مُبَاهِ بِكُمُ الأممَ يَوم القِيَامة» . وقد كان سيدنا علي- كرّم الله وجهه- أزهدَ الصحابة، وكان له أربع حرائر وسبعُ جواري سُرِّيَّاتٍ، وقيل: سبع عشرة، وقيل: المراد بهم اليهود والنصارى، لأن اليهود يُحلون الأقارب من الأب وبنات الأخ وبنات الأخت. وقيل: المجوس.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-21","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ أَنْ يُخَفِّفَ عَنْكُمْ فلذلك شرع لكم الشريعة الحنيفية السمحة السهلة، ورخص لكم عند المضايق في نكاح الأمة. وَخُلِقَ الْإِنْسانُ ضَعِيفاً في كل شيء، لأنه خُلق من ضعف، ويؤول إلى ضعف، أسير جَوعة، صريع شبعة، وخصوصًا عن شهوة النساء، فإنه لا يصبر عن الجماع، ولا يكون في شيء أضعفَ منه في أمر النساء، وعن عبادة ابن الصامت رضي الله عنه أنه قال: (ألا تروني أني لا أقوم إلا رفدًا (١) ، ولا آكل إلا ما لُيِّن لي، وقد مات صاحبي- يعني ذكره- منذ زمان، وما يسرني أني خلوت بامرأة لا تحل لي، وأن لي ما تطلع عليه الشمس، مخافة أن يأتيني الشيطان فيحركه، على أنه لا سمع له ولا بصر.) .","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-22","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"قال ابن عباس: ثماني آيات في سورة النساء، هي خير لهذه الأمة مما طلعت عليه الشمس وغربت، يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ، وَاللَّهُ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْكُمْ، يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ أَنْ يُخَفِّفَ عَنْكُمْ، إِنْ تَجْتَنِبُوا كَبائِرَ مَا تُنْهَوْنَ عَنْهُ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-23","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"الآية، إِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَغْفِرُ أَنْ يُشْرَكَ بِهِ.... الآية، إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقالَ ذَرَّةٍ ... ، وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ سُوءاً أَوْ يَظْلِمْ نَفْسَهُ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-24","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"الآية، مَّا يَفْعَلُ اللَّهُ بِعَذابِكُمْ ... الآية. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-25","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"الإشارة: إنما ينزل المريد إلى العلوم الرسمية، أو الأعمال الحسية، إذا خشي الانمحاق أو الاصطلام في بحر الحقائق، وإن صبر وتماسك، حتى يتقوى على حمل أعبائها، فهو خير له، لأن الرجوع إلى الحس، لا يؤمن من","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-26","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"الحبس، والله غفور لمن تنزل لعلة ما تقدم، رحيم حين جعل له الرخصة، يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ سلوك الطريق إلى عين التحقيق، ويهديكم طرق الوصول، كما هدى مَنْ قبلكم، ويتوب فيما خطر ببالكم، من الفترة أو الوقفة، والله يريد أن يتعطف عليكم، لترجعوا إليه بكليتكم. وأهل الغفلة المنهمكون في الشهوات، يريدون ميلكم عن طريق الوصول إلى حضرة ربكم، يريد الله أن يخفف عنكم، فلا يُحملكم من الواردات إلا ما تطيقه طاقتكم، لأنكم ضعفاء إلا إن قوَّاكُم. اللهم قونا على ما نريد، وأيدنا فيما تريد، إِنك على كل شيءٍ قدير.","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-26"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-25-28-27","r":"q4-25-28","title":"4:25–28 — Marriage under constraint, the degrees of knowledge, and divine accommodation","text":"ولمّا ذكر ما يتعلق بحفظ أموال اليتامى وأموال النساء، وانجر الكلام إلى ما يتعلق بهن من حدودهن، وما يحل وما يحرم منهن، ذكر ما بقي من حفظ أموال الرجال، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-25-28-27"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s1","r":"q4-25-28","title":"Means, syntactic objects, circumstance, and companionship","text":"I say: Ṭawl (الطول) means wealth and ample means; it can also mean exaltedness. It is a verbal noun ( maṣdar , مصدر) of ṭāla ṭawlan . It functions either as the direct object ( mafʿūl , مفعول) of “is able” or as a cognate verbal noun ( maṣdar ), since the meanings are closely related. “To marry” ( an yankiḥa , أن ينكح) is, on the first analysis, a substitute ( badal , بدل) for that object, or, on the second, the direct object—“[has the means] to marry.” “Chaste, not fornicators” are two circumstantial accusatives ( ḥālān , حالان), governed by “marry them” ( ankiḥūhunna , أنكحوهن). And khidn (الخدن) means a lover or intimate companion.","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s2","r":"q4-25-28","title":"Marriage to an enslaved woman and the diversity of legal conditions","text":"The Real—majestic is His majesty—says: “Whoever among you lacks the means” , namely, does not possess the wealth that would enable him to marry “chaste believing women” , that is, free believing women, may marry from among “those whom your right hands possess, of your believing young women” : enslaved believing women, but not unbelieving ones. If one of these women makes an outward profession of faith, that is sufficient: knowledge of the inward state belongs to God alone, for “God knows best your faith.” Nor should fear of social disgrace deter you from marrying them, for you are of one kind and of one religion: “You are one of another.” Do not be too proud to marry them. “Marry them with the permission of their people” means with the consent of their owners, who conclude the marriage contract for you. “Give them their bridal gifts” ( ujūrahunna , أجورهن), which, in Mālik’s school as presented here, belong more properly to the women themselves rather than to their masters, “in the recognized manner” ( bi-l-maʿrūf , بالمعروف): without delaying payment or diminishing it, as required by the Sunna. They are to be “chaste” ( muḥṣanāt , محصنات), that is, modest, “not fornicators” , and “not taking secret lovers” ( akhdān , أخدان), namely, companions with whom they commit fornication. In pre-Islamic times, some women took one exclusive partner for illicit intercourse, while others rejected no man who approached them. Ibn Juzayy says: “According to Mālik and most of his companions, a free man may marry an enslaved woman only on two conditions. One is the absence of means ( ʿadam al-ṭawl , عدم الطول)—that he lack enough to marry a free woman. The other is fear of hardship ( khawf al-ʿanat , خوف العنت), namely fornication, because of what follows: ‘That is for one among you who fears hardship.’ Ibn al-Qāsim allowed their marriage even in the absence of both conditions, on the view that the dalīl al-khiṭāb (دليل الخطاب)—inference from what a statement leaves unsaid—is not legally probative. They agreed upon requiring that the enslaved woman be Muslim, on the strength of ‘of your believing young women’ , except the jurists of Iraq, who did not impose that condition.” End of quotation. [N131]","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s3","r":"q4-25-28","title":"the “virgins” of reality and formal learning","text":"Whoever is unable to marry the virgins of spiritual realities ( abkār al-ḥaqāʾiq , أبكار الحقائق), because he cannot drive distractions and attachments ( shawāghil wa-ʿalāʾiq , شواغل وعلائق) from his heart, should descend to the marriage of formal sciences ( al-ʿulūm al-rasmiyya , العلوم الرسمية) and sense-based acts ( al-aʿmāl al-ḥissiyya , الأعمال الحسية). He should receive these from their masters, protect his acquisition of them with sincerity ( ikhlāṣ , إخلاص), fulfil their rights to the extent he can by sharing them with those qualified for them, and patiently disseminate them. God does not waste the reward of anyone who acts well. If his intention is sound and his action sincere, God will appoint for him one of His friends ( walī , ولي) who enriches him through God, until he becomes among those rich through Him. Then he will become qualified to marry free women and will join the great friends of God. “And that is not difficult for God.” When Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan al-Shādhilī, may God be pleased with him, spoke about the fruits of love, he said: “You will see the soul inclined toward His obedience, the intellect fortified by knowledge of Him, the spirit taken up into His Presence, and the secret immersed in witnessing Him. The servant seeks an increase [in love] and receives an increase; he is opened to what is sweeter than the delight of intimate conversation with Him; he is clothed in the robes of nearness upon the carpet of nearness; and he touches the virgins of realities and the previously married women of the sciences.” End of quotation. Thus the knowledge of realities is “virgins”; the sciences of the Path that lead to them are “free, previously married women”; and the remaining formal disciplines are, by comparison, “enslaved women.” God knows best. [N132]","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s4","r":"q4-25-28","title":"","text":"He then describes the penalty concerning the enslaved woman who commits fornication","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s5","r":"q4-25-28","title":"Different readings of the verb “protected by marriage”","text":"I say: Aḥṣana al-rajul (أحصن الرجل), with either fatḥa or ḍamma on the initial hamza, means that the man became muḥṣan (محصن), with either fatḥa or kasra [in that derived form]; in this instance the active and passive constructions ( al-bināʾ li-l-fāʿil wa-l-mafʿūl , البناء للفاعل والمفعول) coincide. According to another account, the form with fatḥa signifies embracing Islam, while that with ḍamma signifies marrying.","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s6","r":"q4-25-28","title":"The juristic rule on the reduced penalty","text":"The Real—majestic is His majesty—says: If enslaved women are married, then “if they commit an indecency” ( fāḥisha , فاحشة)—fornication—their prescribed punishment is half of that imposed upon a free woman: fifty [lashes], because the punishment of an unmarried [free] person is one hundred. One may also infer that they do not undergo stoning, since stoning admits of no division into halves. Likewise enslaved males receive half of the prescribed penalties, and there is no stoning for them. God calls the prescribed penalty “chastisement” ( ʿadhāb , عذاب), as in “Let a group of believers witness their chastisement” [Q 24:2]. [N133]","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s7","r":"q4-25-28","title":"the closer the station, the finer the discipline","text":"As rank ( maqām , مقام) rises, punishment becomes more severe; as nearness increases, good comportment ( ādāb , آداب) is required more strictly. A lapse far from God is not like a lapse in nearness, and what is expected of someone far away is not what is expected of someone close. Consider the wives of the Prophet, blessings and peace upon him, to whom God said: “O wives of the Prophet, whoever among you commits a manifest indecency shall have her chastisement doubled” [Q 33:30]. This is only because of their favor and extraordinary nearness to God. Therefore none enters the Presence ( al-ḥaḍra , الحضرة) except those of comportment and refinement, after gradual education and training. Reflect on the case of al-Junayd: he was told in a dream, “Such a thing cannot be accepted from someone like you,” after the thought of objecting to a petitioner had crossed his heart. Yet those drawn near are reproved and brought back into the Presence, while those remote become still more remote without perceiving it. God knows best. [N134]","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s8","r":"q4-25-28","title":"","text":"He next returns to the condition for marrying an enslaved woman when means are lacking","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s9","r":"q4-25-28","title":"The term ʿanat and the purpose-lām in “God wishes to clarify”","text":"I say: ʿAnat (العنت) means hardship and harm; no harm is greater than falling into sin, especially the gravest sexual indecency, fornication. “God desires to explain to you” ( yurīdu Allāhu li-yubayyina lakum , يريد الله ليبين لكم) means “so that He may explain”; the lām is an additional particle ( lām zāʾida , لام زائدة) in an object construction, reinforcing the prospective sense that necessarily belongs to intending.","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s10","r":"q4-25-28","title":"Fear of fornication, patience, and reports about marriage","text":"The Real—majestic is His majesty—says: “That” —the marriage of enslaved women—“is for whoever among you fears hardship”: I have only permitted it for one who fears falling into fornication, the vilest of indecencies. Under the historical law being described, the marriage of an enslaved woman, with the prospect that her child would also enter slavery and be sold in the markets, is treated as less harmful than fornication. “But that you should remain patient is better for you” : refrain from such a marriage while abstaining from fornication, so that your children do not become enslaved. [N135] Anas said: “I heard the Prophet, blessings and peace upon him, say, ‘Whoever wishes to meet God pure and purified, let him marry free women.’” Abū Hurayra said: “I heard him say, ‘Free women are the well-being of the household, and enslaved women the destruction of the household.’” [Translator’s note: Both reports are transmitted in the tradition literature, but neither may safely be treated as an authenticated Prophetic saying.] [H023] [H024] “And God is Forgiving” toward you for whatever contravention has passed; “Merciful” to you because He granted a dispensation ( rukhṣa , رخصة) to marry an enslaved woman when you fear sin. “God desires to make clear to you” the ordinances of your religion and the welfare of your affairs, “and to guide you to the ways of those who came before you” , the paths of the rightly guided—prophets and righteous people—so that you follow their ways: protecting property and descent, and prohibiting marriage to mothers, daughters and sisters, just as these were prohibited to those before you. “And to turn to you” means to forgive your past sins, or guide you to repentance, or preserve you from disobedience through protection ( ʿiṣma , عصمة). “God is Knowing” of all your past and future acts and “Wise” in what He disposes and determines. “God desires to turn toward you” is repeated to prepare for the contrast “while those who follow desires wish you to incline tremendously” , away from truth, so that you conform to them in pursuit of appetites and treating forbidden acts as lawful. It is as though God says: We wish your repentance and right guidance; those who follow appetites desire your deviation and ruin. He means fornicators, who would like everyone to be like themselves. As for someone who satisfies sexual desire in a lawful marriage, he follows the truth and not them. The Prophet, blessings and peace upon him, is reported to have said: “Marry and beget children; I will boast of your numbers before the nations on the Day of Resurrection.” [H025] Our master ʿAlī—may God ennoble his face—was among the most ascetic of the Companions, yet he had four free wives and seven women kept as concubines; another report gives seventeen. Another interpretation takes “those who follow appetites” as Jews and Christians, on the ground that Jews permit marriage within certain close relations, such as paternal relatives and brothers’ and sisters’ daughters; still another says that it means the Magians. [Translator’s note: These are Ibn ʿAjība’s transmitted identifications, not a definition established by the verse itself.] [N136] “God desires to lighten things for you” : He accordingly ordained the easy, broad and upright religious law ( al-sharīʿa al-ḥanīfiyya al-samḥa al-sahla , الشريعة الحنيفية السمحة السهلة), and in circumstances of pressure He allowed the dispensation of marrying an enslaved woman. “The human being was created weak” in every respect. He was created in weakness and will return to weakness; a single bout of hunger enslaves him, and a full meal can strike him down. Particularly in matters of sexual desire, he is unable to endure indefinitely without intercourse; in no matter, says the author, is a man weaker than with respect to women. ʿUbāda b. al-Ṣāmit, may God be pleased with him, reportedly said: “Do you not see that I can stand only with support, and eat only what has been softened for me? My companion”—meaning his male organ—“has been dead for some time. Yet it would not please me to be alone with a woman not lawful to me, even if I possessed everything upon which the sun rises, for fear that Satan should come and stir it, though it has neither hearing nor sight.” [N137] Ibn ʿAbbās said: “There are eight verses in Sūrat al-Nisāʾ better for this community than everything upon which the sun rises and sets”: “God desires to explain to you” [4:26], “God desires to turn toward you” [4:27], “God desires to lighten things for you” [4:28], “If you avoid the grave sins you are forbidden” [4:31], “God does not forgive the association of partners with Him” [4:48], “God does not wrong [anyone] by so much as an atom’s weight” [4:40], “Whoever does evil or wrongs his own soul” [4:110], and “What would God gain from punishing you?” [4:147]. End of report. [N138]","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s11","r":"q4-25-28","title":"overload, concession, and return to the path","text":"The disciple ( murīd , مريد) descends to the formal sciences or sensible activities only if he fears being blotted out ( inmiḥāq , انمحاق) or overwhelmed ( iṣṭilām , اصطلام) in the sea of realities. If he can remain patient and hold firm until strengthened to carry its burdens, that is better for him, because after returning to sensible experience ( al-ḥiss , الحس) there is no certainty that he will not be detained there ( al-ḥabs , الحبس). Yet God is Forgiving to one who descends for the reason just given, Merciful in having established the dispensation for him. “God desires to explain to you” the journey of the Path ( sulūk al-ṭarīq , سلوك الطريق) toward the very reality of realization ( ʿayn al-taḥqīq , عين التحقيق), and guide you along the roads of arrival ( ṭuruq al-wuṣūl , طرق الوصول), as He guided those before you; He forgives the pause or stagnation ( fatra aw waqfa , فترة أو وقفة) that might cross your mind, and He seeks to turn tenderly toward you so that you return to Him with your entire being. But the heedless who are submerged in appetites wish you to deviate from the way of arrival into your Lord’s Presence. God wishes to lighten your burden: He will not lay upon you spiritual visitations ( wāridāt , واردات) beyond what your strength can bear, for you are weak unless He strengthens you. O God, strengthen us for what we desire and support us in what You desire; You have power over all things.","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-25-28-s12","r":"q4-25-28","title":"","text":"After speaking of protecting the estates of orphans and women, and being led into the legal boundaries concerning women, he now resumes the protection of people’s property","anchor":"en-q4-25-28-s12"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-29-30","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction 4:29–30","anchor":"unit-q4-29-30"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-1","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوالَكُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ بِالْباطِلِ إِلاَّ أَنْ تَكُونَ تِجارَةٌ عَنْ تَراضٍ مِنْكُمْ ...","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-2","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"قلت: الاستثناء منقطع، وكان تامة لمن رفَع، وناقصة لمن نصب، واسمها: ضمير الأموال، على حذف مضاف، إلاَّ أن تكون الأموال أموالَ تجارة.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-3","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوالَكُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ بِالْباطِلِ الذي لا تُجوزه الشريعة، كالربا والقمار، والغصب والسرقة، والخيانة والكهانة والسحر وغير ذلك. إِلَّا أَنْ تَكُونَ، أي: لكن إن وجدت تِجارَةً صحيحة عَنْ تَراضٍ مِنْكُمْ أي: اتفاق منكم على البيع، وبه استدلت المالكية على انعقاد البيع بالعقد ولو لم يحصل تفرق بالأبدان.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-4","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"وقال الشافعي: إنما يتم بالتفرق بالأبدان، لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام: «البَيِّعَان بالخِيَار مَا لَمْ يتَفَرَّقَا» . وحمله مالك على التفرق بالكلام، وقال أكثر المفسرين: التخيير، هو أن يُخير كلُ واحد منهما صاحبه بعد عقد البيع. وقد ابتاع عمرو ابن جرير فرسًا، ثم خَيَّر صاحبه بعد البيع، ثم قال: سمعت أبا هريرة يقول: البيع عن تراض. قال البيضاوي:","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-5","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"وتخصيص التجارة من الوجوه التي يحل بها انتقال مال الغير، لأنها أغلب وأوفق لذوي المروءات، ويجوز أن يُراد بها الانتقال مطلقًا. وقيل: المقصود بالنهي: صرف المال فيما لا يرضاه الله تعالى، وبالتجارة: صرفه فيما يرضى. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-6","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"الإشارة: لا تصرفوا أموالكم ولا أحوالكم في غير ما يُقربكم إلى الحق فإن ما سوى الحق كله باطل، كما قال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-7","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"ألا كل شيء ما خلا الله باطل ... وكل نعيم لا محالة زائل (١)","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-8","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"إلا أن يكون صرفه في تجارة رابحة، تقربكم من الحبيب، وتجلبُكم إلى حضرة القريب، فتلك تجارة رابحة وصفقة نافعة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-9","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"ثم تكلم على بعض ما يتعلق بحفظ الأبدان، وسيأتي تمامه في قوله: (وَمَا كَانَ لمؤمن ... ) إلى آخر الآيات، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-10","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"... وَلا تَقْتُلُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيماً (29) وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ عُدْواناً وَظُلْماً فَسَوْفَ نُصْلِيهِ نَاراً وَكانَ ذلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ يَسِيراً (30)","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-11","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلا تَقْتُلُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ، بالخنق أو بالنخع (١) أو بالجرح، الذي يؤدي إلى الموت، أو بالإلقاء إلى التهلكة. وعن عمرو بن العاص رضي الله عنه قال: (بعثني رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم في غَزوة ذَات السَّلاَسِلِ، فأجنَبتُ في لَيْلَة بَارِدَة، فَأشْفَقْتُ على نفسي وصَليْتُ بأصحَابِي صَلاة الصُبح بالتيمم. فلَمّا قَدِمتُ ذَكَرتُ ذلك لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فقال: «يا عَمرُو صلَّيتَ بأصحَابِكَ وأنت جُنُب؟» قلت: نعم يا رسول الله، أشفقت إن اغتسلتُ أن أهلك، فذكرت قوله تعالى: لا تَقْتُلُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيماً، فضحك النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، ولم يقل شيئاً) .","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-12","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"أو: ولا تقتلوا إخوانكم في الإسلام، فإن المؤمنين كنفس واحدة. قال البيضاوي: جمع في التوصية بين حفظ النفس والمال- الذي هو شقيقها من حيث إنه سبب قوامها- استبقاء لهم. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-13","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"وإنما نهاكم عن قتل أنفسكم رأفة، ورحمة بكم، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيماً، فقد أمر بني إسرائيل بقتل أنفسهم، وأنتم نهاكم عنه. وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ القتل. أو جميع ما سبق من المحرمات عُدْواناً وَظُلْماً، أي:","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-14","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"إفراطًا في التجاوز عن الحد، وإتيانًا بما لا يستحق، أو تعديًا على الغير وظلمًا على النفس، بتعريضها للعقاب، فَسَوْفَ نُصْلِيهِ نارًا أي: نحرقه ونشويه فيها. وَكانَ ذلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ يَسِيراً.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-15","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «مَن قَتَل نفسَهُ بِشَيءٍ عذب به في نار جهنم خَالِدًا مُخَلَّدًا فِيهَا» وهو تغليظ، أو لمن استحل ذلك. وهذا الوعيد الذي ذكره الحق هنا في قتل الإنسان بيده، أهون مما ذكره في قتل الغير، الذي يأتي، لأنه زاد هناك الغضب واللعنة والعذاب العظيم، أما قول ابن عطية: إنه أجمع المفسرون أن هذه الآية في قتل بعضهم بعضًا، فليس بصحيح، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-16","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"الإشارة: ولا تقتلوا أنفسكم باتباع الشهوات وتراكم الغفلات، فإنه يفوتها الحياة الحقيقية. وقال الفضيل بن عياض رضي الله عنه: (لا تغفلوا عن حظ أنفسكم، فمن غفل عن حظ نفسه، فكأنما قتلها) . وحظ النفس هو تزكيتها وتحليتها بالكمالات، أو قُوتها من العلم اليقين، والمعرفة وصحة التمكين، والمراد بالنفس هنا الروح، وأما ما اصطلحت عليه الصوفية من أن النفس يجب قتلها، فإن مرادهم بذلك النفس الأمارة، فإن الروح ما دامت مُظلمة بالمعاصي والهوى سُميت نفساً، فإذا تطهرت وتزكت سميت روحًا. وهو المراد هنا. سماها نفسًا باعتبار ما كانت عليه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-29-30-17","r":"q4-29-30","title":"4:29–30 — Trading by consent, preservation of life, and the spiritual meaning of self-destruction","text":"ثم إن قتل النفس من الكبائر، فمن اجتنبه مع غيره من الكبائر غفرت له الصغائر، كما أشار إلى ذلك ترغيبا فى اجتناب ما ذكر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4-29-30-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-29-30-s1","r":"q4-29-30","title":"The disconnected exception and the two analyses of kāna","text":"I say: The exception ( al-istithnāʾ , الاستثناء) is disconnected ( munqaṭiʿ , منقطع), meaning “but [let there be] trade.” In the reading with the nominative ( rafʿ , رفع), “be” ( kāna , كان) is complete ( tāmma , تامة), meaning “occur”; in the accusative reading ( naṣb , نصب), it is incomplete ( nāqiṣa , ناقصة), with a pronoun referring to property as its subject after supplying an omitted construct: “except that the property be property of trade.”","anchor":"en-q4-29-30-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-29-30-s2","r":"q4-29-30","title":"Unlawful enrichment, lawful trading, and disagreement over the option to rescind","text":"The Real—majestic is His majesty—says: “O you who believe, do not consume one another’s property unlawfully” ( bi-l-bāṭil , بالباطل): by any means the religious law does not permit, such as usury, gambling, violent appropriation, theft, betrayal of trust, divination, sorcery, and the like. “Except that there be trade by mutual consent among you” : that is, rather, when a valid commercial transaction occurs through mutual agreement on the sale. The Mālikīs draw from this the conclusion that a sale is constituted by the contract even before the two parties physically separate. Al-Shāfiʿī says that the sale is completed only once the parties separate physically, relying on the Prophet’s saying, blessings and peace upon him: “The seller and buyer retain their option [to annul the contract] so long as they have not separated.” [H026] Mālik interprets “separation” as separation of speech [the ending of negotiation]. According to most exegetes, the “option” ( takhyīr , تخيير) means each party formally offering the other a choice once the contract is concluded. ʿAmr b. Jarīr reportedly bought a horse and then gave his counterpart the choice after the sale, saying: “I heard Abū Hurayra say that trade must be by mutual consent.” Al-Bayḍāwī says: “Trade is singled out among the means by which another’s property may lawfully pass [to one] because it is the most common, and most fitting for people of dignity. It is also possible that ‘trade’ is intended to mean transfer [of property] in general.” Another interpretation takes the prohibition as forbidding spending wealth on what God does not approve, and “trade” as spending it on what He does approve. End of quotation. [N139]","anchor":"en-q4-29-30-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-29-30-s3","r":"q4-29-30","title":"the profitable exchange","text":"Do not expend your wealth—or your spiritual states ( aḥwāl , أحوال)—on anything that does not draw you nearer to the Real ( al-Ḥaqq , الحق), for everything besides the Real is vain. As the poet said: Truly everything apart from God is vain; and every delight will surely vanish. There is an exception when the expenditure becomes profitable trade, bringing you near to the Beloved and drawing you into the Presence of the Near One: that is a profitable trade and a beneficial bargain. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-29-30-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-29-30-s4","r":"q4-29-30","title":"","text":"He then turns to one aspect of preserving bodily life, a topic completed later in the discussion of “It is not for a believer …”","anchor":"en-q4-29-30-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-29-30-s5","r":"q4-29-30","title":"The prohibition on killing oneself and the precedent of ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ","text":"“Do not kill yourselves” by strangling, severing the spinal cord, or inflicting a wound that brings death; nor by throwing yourselves into destruction. ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ, may God be pleased with him, reported: “The Messenger of God sent me on the expedition to Dhāt al-Salāsil. I became ritually impure on a cold night; fearing for my life [if I washed], I performed tayammum (التيمم) and led my companions in the dawn prayer. When I returned I mentioned this to the Messenger of God. He said, ‘ʿAmr, did you lead them in prayer while you were in a state of major ritual impurity?’ I said, ‘Yes, Messenger of God. I feared that washing would destroy me, and I remembered the saying of God: Do not kill yourselves. God has indeed been merciful to you. ’ The Prophet laughed and said nothing.” [H027] Alternatively, “Do not kill yourselves” can mean: do not kill your brothers in Islam, for the believers are like one soul. Al-Bayḍāwī says that by joining the preservation of life and wealth, which is its companion because life depends on it, God enjoins the continued safety of both. End of quotation. It is only out of kindness and mercy that God has forbidden you to kill yourselves: “God has ever been Merciful to you.” He commanded the Children of Israel to kill themselves [in a particular account], whereas He forbade it to you. “Whoever does that” —meaning the killing, or all the prohibited acts just mentioned— “in aggression and wrongdoing” : that is, excessive transgression of a limit and doing what one has no right to do, or trespassing against another while wronging oneself by exposing oneself to punishment, “We shall soon expose him to a Fire” , that is, burn and roast him in it. “And that is easy for God.” The Prophet, blessings and peace upon him, is reported to have said: “Whoever kills himself by something will be punished by it in the Fire of Hell, remaining there forever.” [H028] This is a threat expressed with extraordinary severity, or, Ibn ʿAjība says, it applies to someone who declares the act lawful. The warning given here for killing oneself, he observes, is lighter than the warning later given for killing another human being, where wrath, the curse, and a tremendous punishment are added. As for Ibn ʿAṭiyya’s assertion that the exegetes unanimously agreed that this verse refers to killing one another, Ibn ʿAjība says that assertion is not correct. God knows best. [N140]","anchor":"en-q4-29-30-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-29-30-s6","r":"q4-29-30","title":"preserving the soul’s real life","text":"Do not kill your souls by following appetites and allowing heedlessness to accumulate over you, for these deprive the soul of true life. Al-Fuḍayl b. ʿIyāḍ, may God be pleased with him, said: “Do not be heedless of your soul’s portion; one who neglects his soul’s portion is as if he had killed it.” The soul’s portion is its purification ( tazkiya , تزكية) and adornment with perfections, or its nourishment with certain knowledge ( ʿilm al-yaqīn , علم اليقين), gnosis ( maʿrifa , معرفة), and sound establishment ( tamkīn , تمكين). By “soul” here [the author] means spirit ( rūḥ , روح). When Sufis say that the soul must be “killed,” they intend the commanding soul ( al-nafs al-ammāra , النفس الأمارة). So long as the spirit remains darkened by sins and caprice it is called nafs (نفس); when purified and refined it is called rūḥ (روح). This is the sense intended here: the verse calls it nafs in view of what it had previously been. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4-29-30-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-29-30-s7","r":"q4-29-30","title":"","text":"Killing oneself is one of the grave sins; avoidance of the grave sins brings forgiveness of lesser ones","anchor":"en-q4-29-30-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4-31","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence 4:31","anchor":"unit-q4-31"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-1","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"إِنْ تَجْتَنِبُوا كَبائِرَ مَا تُنْهَوْنَ عَنْهُ نُكَفِّرْ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّئاتِكُمْ وَنُدْخِلْكُمْ مُدْخَلاً كَرِيماً (31)","anchor":"ar-q4-31-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-2","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"قلت: المدخل- بالضم: مصدر، بمعنى الإدخال، وبالفتح: المكان، ويحتمل المصدر.","anchor":"ar-q4-31-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-3","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إن تجتنبوا كبائر الذنوب التي تُنهون عنها نُكَفِّرْ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّئاتِكُمْ الصغائر وَنُدْخِلْكُمْ مُدْخَلًا كَرِيماً وهو الجنة، أو إدخالاً مصحوبًا بالكرامة والتعظيم، واختلف في الكبائر، هل تعرف بالعد أو بالحد؟ فقيل: سبع، وقيل: سبعون، وقيل: سبعمائة، وقيل: كل معصية فهى كبيرة. وعنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «اجتَنِبُوا السَّبعَ المُوبِقَاتِ: الإشراك باللهِ، والسَّحرَ، وقَتلَ النَّفس بغير حقها، وأكل الرّبا، وأكلَ مَالِ اليَتِيمِ، والفرار مِن الزَّحفِ، ورَمي المُحصنَاتٍ الغَافِلاتِ المُؤمِنَاتِ» .","anchor":"ar-q4-31-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-4","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"قال ابن جزي: لا شك أن هذه مِنَ الكبائر لنص الشارع عليها، وزاد بعضهم عليها أشياء ورد النص عليها في الحديث أنها من الكبائر، منها عقوق الوالدين، وشهادة الزور، واليمين الغموس، والزنا، والسرقة، وشرب الخمر، والنهبة، والقنوط من رحمة الله، والأمن من مكر الله، ومنع ابن السبيل الماء، والإلحاد في البيت الحرام، والنميمة، وترك التحرّز من البول، والغلول، واستطالة الرجل في عرض أخيه، والجور في الحكم.","anchor":"ar-q4-31-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-5","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"وقيل في حدّها: كل جريمة تؤذن بقلة الدين ورقة الديانة، وقيل: ذنوب الظاهر صغائر، وذنوب الباطن كبائر.","anchor":"ar-q4-31-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-6","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"وقيل: كل ما فيه حق الغير فهو كبائر، وما كان بينك وبين الله تعالى صغائر، واحتج هذا بقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «يُنَادِي يومَ القيامة مناد من بُطنان العرش (١) : يا أمّة أحمد، أن الله تعالى يقول: أمَّا ما كان لي قِبلَكُمُ فقد وهبتهُ لكم، وبقيت التباعات، فتواهبوها، وادخلوا الجنة» .","anchor":"ar-q4-31-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-7","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"الإشارة: كل ما يُبعد العبد عن حضرة ربه فهو من أكبر الكبائر، فمن اجتنب ذلك واتقى كلَّ ما يشغله عن الله أدخله الله مدخلاً كريمًا، وهو حضرة الشهود والتلذذ برؤية المعبود، والترقي في أسرار الحبيب الودود. قال الورتجبي: قال أبو تراب: أمر الله باجتناب الكبائر، وهي الدعاوى الفاسدة، والإشارات الباطلة، وإطلاق اللفظ بغير الحقيقة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4-31-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4-31-8","r":"q4-31","title":"4:31 — Major sins, lesser sins, and nearness to the Divine Presence","text":"ولما قسّم الله المواريث على ما تقدم، قال بعض النساء: ليتنا استوينا مع الرجال، أو يكون لنا سهمان لأننا أحوج منهم، فأنزل الله:","anchor":"ar-q4-31-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-31-s1","r":"q4-31","title":"The two forms and senses of mudkhal","text":"I say: Mudkhal (مدخل), with ḍamma on the mīm, is a verbal noun ( maṣdar , مصدر) meaning “causing to enter” ( idkhāl , إدخال); with fatḥa it denotes the place of entry, although it can also be a verbal noun.","anchor":"en-q4-31-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-31-s2","r":"q4-31","title":"How the major sins are enumerated—or defined","text":"The Real—majestic is His majesty—says: “If you avoid the grave sins of what you are forbidden” , the major sins ( kabāʾir al-dhunūb , كبائر الذنوب), “We shall efface your evil deeds” , that is, your minor sins, “and admit you through a noble entrance” : into the Garden, or through an act of admission attended by honor and magnification. There is disagreement about grave sins: are they known by enumerating ( ʿadd , عد) them or by defining their limit ( ḥadd , حد)? Some say seven, others seventy, others seven hundred; others again say that every act of disobedience is grave. The Prophet, blessings and peace upon him, said: “Avoid the seven destructive sins” ( al-sabʿ al-mūbiqāt , السبع الموبقات): associating others with God, sorcery, killing a life without right, taking usury, consuming an orphan’s wealth, fleeing the advance of battle, and slandering chaste, unsuspecting believing women. [H029] Ibn Juzayy says: “These are undoubtedly among the grave sins, for the Lawgiver expressly named them. Others add matters explicitly called grave sins in hadith: disobedience to parents, false witness, the oath that plunges one into wrongdoing ( al-yamīn al-ghamūs , اليمين الغموس), fornication, theft, drinking wine, plunder, despair of God’s mercy, feeling secure from God’s plan, refusing a traveler access to water, profaning the Sacred House, tale-bearing, failing to safeguard oneself from urine, embezzlement of communal spoils ( ghulūl , غلول), violating one’s brother’s reputation, and ruling unjustly.” Another definition is any offence indicating diminished religious seriousness and weakened religious commitment. Another says outward sins are minor and inward sins are grave. Another says every offence involving another person’s right is grave, while what remains between a servant and God is minor. Its proponents cite a report attributed to the Prophet: “On the Day of Resurrection a caller from within the Throne will proclaim: ‘Community of Aḥmad! God says: As for the claims I had against you, I have granted them to you; claims belonging to others remain, so grant them freely to one another, and enter the Garden.’” [Translator’s note: This report is weak and is presented as an argument cited by a particular group, not an authenticated foundation for cancelling the rights of injured persons.] [H030] [N141]","anchor":"en-q4-31-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-31-s3","r":"q4-31","title":"the greatest sin is whatever bars the Presence","text":"Everything that drives the servant away from his Lord’s Presence is among the greatest grave sins. Whoever avoids it and guards against everything that distracts him from God is admitted by God through a noble entrance: the Presence of witnessing ( ḥaḍrat al-shuhūd , حضرة الشهود), delight in beholding the Worshipped One, and advancing in the secrets of the Beloved, the All-Loving. Al-Wartajbī says: “Abū Turāb said: God commanded the avoidance of grave sins, and these are corrupt pretensions, false allusions, and the utterance of words without their reality.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q4-31-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4-31-s4","r":"q4-31","title":"","text":"After God divided inheritances, some women reportedly wished to have the same portions as men, or two portions because of their greater need. At this point Ibn ʿAjība introduces the following verse, Q 4:32.","anchor":"en-q4-31-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_32","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God 4:32","anchor":"unit-q4_32"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-1","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"وَلا تَتَمَنَّوْا مَا فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ بِهِ بَعْضَكُمْ عَلى بَعْضٍ لِلرِّجالِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا اكْتَسَبُوا وَلِلنِّساءِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا اكْتَسَبْنَ وَسْئَلُوا اللَّهَ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيماً (32)","anchor":"ar-q4_32-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-2","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلا تَتَمَنَّوْا مَا فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ بِهِ من الميراث (١) بَعْضَكُمْ عَلى بَعْضٍ، كتضعيف الذكر على الأنثى، فللرجال نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا اكْتَسَبُوا أي: مما أصابوا وأحرزوا في القسمة، وَلِلنِّساءِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا اكْتَسَبْنَ منه، قلَّ أو كثر، فلتقنع بما قسم الله لها، ولا تعترض على أحكام الشريعة، ولكن سْئَلُوا اللَّهَ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ يُعطكم من غير الميراث، هكذا فسرها ابن عباس.","anchor":"ar-q4_32-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-3","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"وقال مجاهد: قالت أُم سلمة: يغزو الرجال ولا نغزو، فليتنا رجال نغزو، ونبلغ ما يبلغ الرجال. فنزلت. فيكون المعنى: وَلاَ تَتَمَنَّوْاْ مَا فَضَّلَ الله به الرجال على النساء كالغزو وغيره، فللرجال نصيب مما اكتسبوا من ثواب الجهاد وسائر أعمالهم، (وللنساء نصيب مما اكتسبن) من طاعة أزواجهن وحفظ فروجهن وسائر بقية أعمالهن.","anchor":"ar-q4_32-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-4","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"والتحقيق أنها عامة في جميع المراتب الدينية والدنيوية لأن ذلك ذريعة إلى التحاسد والتعادي، ومعربة عن عدم الرضا بما قسم الله له، وإلى التشهي لحصول الشيء له من غير طلب، وهو مذموم لأن تمنّي ما لم يقدر له، معارضة لحِكمة القدر، وتمنّي ما قدر له بكسب، بطالة وتضييع حظ، وتمنّي ما قدر له بغير كسب، ضياع ومحال، قاله البيضاوي. فللرجال نصيب من أجل ما اكتسبوا من الأعمال، وتحملوا من المشاق، فيعطيهم الله على قدر ما اكتسبوا وَلِلنِّساءِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا اكْتَسَبْنَ كذلك، فلا فائدة في تمني ما للناس، ولكن (اسألوا الله من فضله) يُعطكم مثله، أو أكثر من خزائنه التي لا تنفد. إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيماً وهو يعلم ما يستحقه","anchor":"ar-q4_32-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-5","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"كل إنسان، فيُفَضِّل من شاء بما شاء عن علم وبيان، ومناسبة الآية حينئِذ لما قبلها: أن تجنب الكبائر فضل من الله ونعمة، وهو أفضل ممن يقع فيها، لكن لا ينبغي تمني ذلك من غير عمل، ولكن يسأل الله من فضلِهِ حتى يُلحقه بأهل العصمة. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_32-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-6","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"الإشارة: قد وقع التفضيل في مقامات الأولياء كالأنبياء، لكن لا ينبغي تعيين الفاضل من المفضول، لِما يؤدي إليه من التنقيص فيؤدي إلى الغيبة، والتفضيل يقع بزيادة اليقين وصحة التمكين، والترقي في أنوار التوحيد وأسرار التفريد. ويكون أيضًا بهداية الخلق على يده، وظهور إحسانه ورفده، فإذا رأى العبدُ أنه لم يبلغ إلى مقام غيره فلا يتمنى ذلك المقام بعينه، فقد يكون مقامه عند الله في علمه أعظم، وقد يكون أدون، فيُسيء الأدب، فالخير كله في العبودية والرضى بأحكام الربوبية، فللأقوياء نصيب مما اكتسبوا بالقوة والمجاهدة التي خلق الله فيهم، حكمةً وفضلاً، وللضعفاء نصيب مما اكتسبوا قسمة وعدلاً، ولكن يسأل الله من فضله العظيم، فإن الله بكل شيء عليم، فقد يُعطى بلا سبب ويُبَلِّغ بلا تعب.","anchor":"ar-q4_32-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-7","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «سَلُوا الله مِن فَضلِهِ فَإنَّ اللهَ يُحِبُ أن يُسألَ» . وفي حديث آخر: «مَن لَم يَسألِ اللهَ يَغضَب عَلَيهِ» . وقال الورتجبي: أمر بالسؤال ونهى عن التمني لأن السؤال افتقار، والتمني، اختيار. هـ. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_32-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_32-8","r":"q4_32","title":"4:32 · Allotted gifts, work, and the stations of the friends of God","text":"ثم تكلم على ميراث الحليف على ما كان في أول الإسلام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_32-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_32-s1","r":"q4_32","title":"Inheritance and the limits of comparison","text":"The Real, majestic is His glory, says: Do not wish for what God has bestowed upon some of you beyond others in inheritance, such as the male receiving twice the female’s share. “Men have a share of what they have earned” means what they have received and taken possession of in the division; women too have a share of what they receive from it, whether small or great. Let each be content with what God has allotted to her rather than objecting to the rulings of the Sacred Law. Instead, “ask God of His bounty”: He may grant you something other than inheritance. Ibn ʿAbbās explained the verse in this way.","anchor":"en-q4_32-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_32-s2","r":"q4_32","title":"The reported circumstances of revelation","text":"Mujāhid, however, related that Umm Salama said: “Men go out on military expeditions while we do not. If only we were men, so that we could fight and attain what the men attain.” Then the verse was sent down. On this reading, its meaning is: Do not desire the advantages God has assigned to men over women, such as participation in battle and similar matters. Men have the reward of their military striving and other works, and women have the reward of obedience to their husbands, guarding their chastity, and the rest of their works.","anchor":"en-q4_32-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_32-s3","r":"q4_32","title":"A general teaching about all worldly and religious ranks","text":"The more exact determination (التحقيق) is that the verse is general, embracing every rank in religion and worldly affairs. Wishing for another’s allotted rank can lead to envy and hostility; it betrays dissatisfaction with what God has apportioned and a desire to obtain something without seeking its proper means. That is blameworthy. To wish for what has not been decreed for oneself is to challenge the wisdom of the decree (حكمة القدر). To wish for what has been decreed through work while neglecting the work is idleness and the squandering of one’s opportunity. To wish for what has been decreed independently of work is a futile loss of effort. Al-Bayḍāwī makes this observation. Thus men obtain a portion on account of the deeds they perform and the hardships they undergo, and God grants them according to what they earn; women likewise have a portion according to their deeds. There is no benefit in coveting what belongs to others. Ask God of His inexhaustible bounty, and He can give you the like of it or more. “God has knowledge of everything”: He knows what each person merits and favours whom He wills with what He wills, in knowledge and discernment. The verse is connected to the preceding discussion as follows: abstaining from grave sins is itself God’s grace and favour, and those who avoid them are better off than those who fall into them. One should not merely wish for such a condition without acting; one should ask God of His bounty that He may join one to those He preserves. And through God comes success.","anchor":"en-q4_32-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_32-s4","r":"q4_32","title":"Different degrees of sainthood without disparagement","text":"Degrees of excellence exist among the stations of God’s friends, as they do among the prophets. Yet one should not insist on ranking this saint above that one: the resulting disparagement can lead to backbiting (الغيبة). Distinction may arise through an increase in certainty (اليقين), the soundness of established realization (التمكين), progression through the lights of divine oneness (أنوار التوحيد) and the mysteries of singularization (أسرار التفريد), through guiding others by one’s hand, or through manifest generosity and benefit. When someone observes that he has not attained the station of another, he should not wish for that precise station. His own degree may be greater in God’s knowledge, or less; such wishing may therefore violate proper comportment (الأدب). The entire good lies in servanthood (العبودية) and contentment with the ordinances of Lordship (الربوبية). The strong have a share of what they have gained through the strength and spiritual struggle (المجاهدة) God created in them as wisdom and grace; the weak have a share of what they have gained by divine allotment and justice. Let all ask of God’s vast bounty, for He knows every thing. He may bestow without apparent means and bring a person to arrival without toil.","anchor":"en-q4_32-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_32-s5","r":"q4_32","title":"Asking, rather than choosing one’s portion","text":"A report attributed to the Prophet, blessings and peace upon him, says: “Ask God of His bounty, for God loves to be asked.” [H032] Another states: “Whoever does not ask God, He becomes angry with him.” [H033] Al-Wartajbī says: “He commands asking and forbids wishing, because asking is confession of poverty (افتقار), while wishing is an act of choosing (اختيار).” End of quotation. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_32-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_32-s6","r":"q4_32","title":"","text":"He then spoke of the inheritance of an ally, as this had existed at the beginning of Islam.","anchor":"en-q4_32-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_33","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance 4:33","anchor":"unit-q4_33"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-1","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"وَلِكُلٍّ جَعَلْنا مَوالِيَ مِمَّا تَرَكَ الْوالِدانِ وَالْأَقْرَبُونَ وَالَّذِينَ عَقَدَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ فَآتُوهُمْ نَصِيبَهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيداً (33)","anchor":"ar-q4_33-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-2","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"قلت: التنوين في «كل» : للعوض، و «مما ترك» بيان للمعوض منه، أي: ولكل مال مما ترك الوالدان والأقربون جعلنا موالي، أي: ورثة، وهم الذرية والعصبة يرثون من ذلك المال، والوالدان على هذا فاعل، ويحتمل أن يكون مبتدأ والتنوين عوض عن الميت الموروث، أي: ولكل ميت جعلنا ورثة يرثون مما ترك ذلك الميت، وهم الوالدان والأقربون فيوقف على (ترك) ، و (مما) يتعلق بمحذوف، و (الذين) مبتدأ، و (فآتوهم) خبر، دخلت الفاء لما في المبتدأ من العموم.","anchor":"ar-q4_33-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-3","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولكل ميت جعلنا ورثة يرثون مِمَّا تَرَكَ ذلك الميت، وهم الْوالِدانِ وَالْأَقْرَبُونَ، أو لكل تركة جعلنا لها مَوالِيَ أي: ورثة يرثون مما ترك الوالدان والأقربون، وَالَّذِينَ عَقَدَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ وهم موالي الحِلف، كانوا يتحالفون في الجاهلية على النصرة والمؤازرة، يقول الرجل لآخر: دمي دمك،","anchor":"ar-q4_33-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-4","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"وهدمي هدمك، وثأري ثأرك. فيضرب بعضهم على يد الآخر في عقد ذلك الحلف. فلذلك قال: عَقَدَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ فكان في أول الإسلام يرث من حليفه السدس، وإليه أشار بقوله: فَآتُوهُمْ نَصِيبَهُمْ، ثم نسخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_33-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-5","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"وقيل: نزلت في المؤاخاة التي آخى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بين المهاجرين والأنصار، فكان يرث السدس، ثم نُسخ بقوله: وَأُولُوا الْأَرْحامِ بَعْضُهُمْ أَوْلى بِبَعْضٍ فِي كِتابِ اللَّهِ. وعن أبي حنيفة: لو أسلم رجل على يد رجل وتعاقدا على أن يتعاقلا ويتوارثا صح وورث. وقال ابن عباس: آتوهم نصيبهم من النصرة التي تعاقدوا عليها، فيُوفي لهم بها، فلا نسخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_33-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-6","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيداً، هو تهديد لمن تعدى الحدود، ونقض العهود. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_33-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-7","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"الإشارة: ولكل زمان جعلنا أولياء كبراء، يرثون مما ترك أشياخهم من خصوصية الولاية وسر العناية، إلى يوم القيامة فالأرض لا تخلو ممن يقوم بالحجة ويظهر المحجة، فيقال لهم: والذين عقدت أيمانكم في الصحبة معكم، فظهر صدقهم، وبانت خدمتهم، فآتوهم نصيبهم مما خصكم الله به من سر الولاية ولطف العناية، (إِن الله كان على كل شيء شهيدًا) ، لا يخفى عليه مَن يستحق الخلافة ويرث سرَ الولاية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_33-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_33-8","r":"q4_33","title":"4:33 · Heirs, contractual alliances, and the inheritance of spiritual guidance","text":"ثم بيّن حكمة تفضيل الرجال على النساء فى المواريث وغيرها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_33-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_33-s1","r":"q4_33","title":"The substitution in kull, and two readings of the syntax","text":"I say: The tanwīn (التنوين) of “each” (كُلٍّ) stands in place of an omitted term (للعوض); “of what was left” (مِمَّا تَرَكَ) explains what that omitted term represents. Thus: “For every property left by parents and relatives, We appointed heirs (مَوَالِي),” namely children and agnatic relatives (العصبة), who inherit from that property. On this analysis “the parents” (الوالدان) is the subject (فاعل) of “left.” Alternatively, “the parents” (الوالدان) may be construed as the subject of a nominal sentence (مبتدأ), while the tanwīn stands in for “the deceased person”: “For every deceased person We appointed heirs who inherit what that deceased person leaves”; those heirs are the parents and near relatives. In that case one pauses after “left” (ترك), and “from what” (مما) depends upon an omitted expression (محذوف). “Those with whom your right hands have contracted” (الذين عقدت أيمانكم) is a subject (مبتدأ), and “give them their share” (فآتوهم نصيبهم) its predicate (خبر). The fāʾ (الفاء) enters the predicate because of the generality expressed by the subject.","anchor":"en-q4_33-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_33-s2","r":"q4_33","title":"Allies, the first inheritance rule, and its reported replacement","text":"The Real, majestic is His glory, says: For every deceased person We have appointed inheritors from what that deceased person leaves, namely parents and near relatives. Or: every estate has its own heirs, who inherit what parents and kin leave. “As for those with whom your right hands have contracted” (الذين عقدت أيمانكم), these are the allies joined by a pact (موالي الحلف). In the Age of Ignorance they formed compacts of mutual protection and assistance. A man might say to another, “My blood is your blood, my injury your injury, and my vengeance your vengeance.” They would then clasp or strike one another’s hands in concluding the pact; hence the reference to what their “right hands have contracted.” At the beginning of Islam an ally inherited a sixth from his fellow ally; “give them their share” referred to that provision, which was later abrogated (نُسخ).","anchor":"en-q4_33-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_33-s3","r":"q4_33","title":"Brotherhood between emigrants and helpers; a contrary account","text":"It is also said that the verse came concerning the brotherhood (المؤاخاة) established by the Messenger of God between the Emigrants (المهاجرين) and Helpers (الأنصار): one would inherit a sixth through that bond, until this was abrogated by “Relatives are nearer to one another in God’s Book” [Q 8:75]. According to a report from Abū Ḥanīfa, if a man became Muslim at another man’s hand and the two contracted to bear indemnity and inherit from one another, this was valid and they inherited. Ibn ʿAbbās, however, explained “give them their share” as referring to the support due under their mutual undertaking, which must still be fulfilled; on this interpretation there is no abrogation. The exegetical report of Ibn ʿAbbās has a close transmitted parallel in al-Bukhārī [H034] . “God is witness over everything” warns against transgressing prescribed bounds or breaking undertakings. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_33-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_33-s4","r":"q4_33","title":"The inheritance of walāya and the trust placed in disciples","text":"In every age We have appointed great friends of God who inherit from their teachers the special grace of sainthood (خصوصية الولاية) and the mystery of divine solicitude (سر العناية) until the Resurrection. The earth is never without someone who establishes the proof and discloses the clear way. To those who have bound themselves to you through companionship (الصحبة), whose sincerity and service have become manifest, give a share of the mystery of sainthood and the kindness of divine solicitude that God has specially granted you. “God is witness over everything”: He knows who merits succession (الخلافة) and inherits the mystery of sainthood. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_33-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_33-s5","r":"q4_33","title":"","text":"He then explains the rationale given for the preference of men over women in inheritance and other matters.","anchor":"en-q4_33-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_34","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self 4:34","anchor":"unit-q4_34"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-1","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"الرِّجالُ قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النِّساءِ بِما فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ بَعْضَهُمْ عَلى بَعْضٍ وَبِما أَنْفَقُوا مِنْ أَمْوالِهِمْ فَالصَّالِحاتُ قانِتاتٌ حافِظاتٌ لِلْغَيْبِ بِما حَفِظَ اللَّهُ وَاللاَّتِي تَخافُونَ نُشُوزَهُنَّ فَعِظُوهُنَّ وَاهْجُرُوهُنَّ فِي الْمَضاجِعِ وَاضْرِبُوهُنَّ فَإِنْ أَطَعْنَكُمْ فَلا تَبْغُوا عَلَيْهِنَّ سَبِيلاً إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيراً (34)","anchor":"ar-q4_34-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-2","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"قلت: (فالصالحات) مبتدأ، وما بعده إخبار عنه، وأتى بالفاء المؤذنة بالسببية والتفريع، وكأنه تعالى يقول:","anchor":"ar-q4_34-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-3","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"الرجال قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النسآء، فمن كانت صالحة قام عليها بما تستحقه من حسن المعاشرة، ومن كانت ناشزة عاملها بما تستحقه من الوعظ وغيره. وكل ما هنا من لفظ (ما) فهي مصدرية. إلا ما قرأ به أبو جعفر: [بما حفظ الله] ، بالنصب، فهي عنده موصولة اسمية، أي: بالأمر الذي حفظ الله وهو طاعتها لله فحفظها بذلك، وقيل إنها مصدرية. انظر الثعلبي.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-4","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الرِّجالُ قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النِّساءِ أي: قائمون عليهن قيام الولاة على الرعية، في التأديب والإنفاق والتعليم، ذلك لأمرين: أحدهما وهبي، والآخر كسبي فالوهبي: هو تفضيل الله لهم على","anchor":"ar-q4_34-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-5","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"النساء بكمال العقل وحسن التدبير ومزيد القوة في الأعمال والطاعات، ولذلك خُصوا بالنبوة، والإمامة، والولاية، وإقامة الشعائر، والشهادة، في مجامع القضايا، ووجوب الجهاد والجمعة ونحوهما، والتعصيب، وزيادة السهم في الميراث، والاستبداد بالطلاق. والكسبي هو: (بما أنفقوا من أموالهم) في مهورهن، ونفقتهن، وكسوتهن.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-6","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"فيجب على الزوج أن يقوم بالعدل في أمر نسائه، فالمرأة الصالحة القانتة، أي: المطيعة لزوجها ولله تعالى، الحافظة للغيب، أي: لما غاب عن زوجها من مال بيته وفرجها وسر زوجها، حفظت ذلك بحفظ الله، أي: بما جعل الله فيها من الأمانة والحفظ، وبما ربط على قلبها من الديانة، أو بحفظها حق الله، فلما حفظت حقوق الله حفظها الله بعصمته، لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «احفَظَ اللهَ يَحفَظكَ» . فمن كانت على هذا الوصف من النساء فيجب على الزوج حُسن القيام بها، ومقابلتها في القيام بما قابلته من الإحسان، وعنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «خير النساء امرأةٌ إن نَظَرتَ إلَيهَا سَرَّتكَ، وإن أمرتها أطَاعَتكَ، وإن غبت عنها حفظتك في مَالِها ونَفسِهَا» . وتلا هذه الآية.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-7","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"وأما النساء التي تَخافُونَ أي: تتيقنون نُشُوزَهُنَّ أي: ترفعهن عن طاعة أزواجهن وعصيانهن، فَعِظُوهُنَّ بالقول، فإن لم ينفع فاهجروهن في المضاجع، أي: لا تدخلوا معهن في لحاف، أو لا تجامعوهن، فإن لم ينفع فاضربوهن ضربًا غير مؤلم ولا شائن. قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «عَلِّق السَّوطَ حَيثُ يَرَاهُ أهلُ البيت» . وعن أسماء بنت أبي بكر- رضى الله عنهما- قالت: (كنتُ رابعَ نسوة عند الزبير بن العوام، فإذا غضب على إحدانا، ضربها بعود المِشجب، حتى ينكسر) . والمشجب: أعواد مركبة يجعل عليها الثياب.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-8","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"فَإِنْ أَطَعْنَكُمْ يا معشر الأزواج، أو عقدن التوبة مما مضى، فَلا تَبْغُوا عَلَيْهِنَّ سَبِيلًا أي: لا تطلبوا عليهن طريقًا تجعلونه سبيلاً لإيذائهن، بل اجعلوا ما كان منها من النشوز كأن لم يكن، (فإنَّ التَّائِبَ مِن الذَّنبِ كَمَن لا ذَنَب لَهُ) . وقال ابن عُيَيْنَة: أي لا تكلفوهن بحبكم. هـ. وقال الورتجبي: إذا حصل منهن صورة طاعة الرجال فلا يطلب منهن موافقة الطباع، فإن ذلك منازعة للقدر. قال تعالى: لاَ تَبْدِيلَ لِخَلْقِ اللَّهِ، وذكر حديث: «الأروَاح جُنودٌ مُجنَّدةٌ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_34-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-9","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"ثم هدد الأزواج فقال: إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيراً فاحذروه، فإنه أقدر عليكم منكم على من تحت ولايتكم، أو: إنه على علو شأنه، يتجاوز عن سيئاتكم، فأنتم أولى بالعفو عن نسائكم، أو: أنه يتعالى ويَكبر أن يظلم أحدًا أو يُنقص حقه.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-10","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"وسبب نزول الآية: أن سَعدَ بنَ الرَّبِيع، وَكَانَ مِن النُقَبَاءِ، لَطَمَ امرأته حَبيبَةَ بِنتَ زَيدِ بن أبي زُهَيرِ، وكانت نَشَزَتَ عَليهِ، فَانطَلَقَ أبُوُها معَهَا إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال: أفرَشتُهُ كَرِيمَتِي فَلَطَمَها، فقال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-:","anchor":"ar-q4_34-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-11","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"لِتقتَصَّ مِنهُ، فَانصرَفَت لتقتصّ منه، فقال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: ارجعوا، هذا جِبرِيلُ أتَاني وأنزَلَ الله هَذِهِ الآية: الرِّجالُ قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النِّساءِ إلى آخرها، فقال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «أَرَدنَا أمرًا، وأرَادَ اللهُ أمرًا، والَّذِي أرَاد اللهُ خَير» فرفع القِصَاص. وقيل: نزلت في غيره ممن وقع له مثل هذا من النشوز. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-12","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"الإشارة: الرجال الأقوياء قوامون على نفوسهم قهارون لها، بفضل القوة التي مكنهم الله منها، وبما أنفقوا عليها من المجاهدات والرياضات، فهم ينظرون إليها ويتهمونها في كل حين، فإن صلحت وأطاعت وانقادت لما يراد منها من أحكام العبودية، والقيام بوظائف الربوبية، عاملوها بالإكرام والإجمال، ورفعوا عنها الآداب والنكال، وإن نشزت وترفعت أدبوها وهجروها عن مواطن شهواتها ومضاجع نومها، وضربوها على قدر لجاجها وغفلتها.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-13","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"وكان الشيخ أبو يزيد يأخذ قبضة من القضبان ويذهب إلى خلوته، فكلما غفلت ضربها، حتى يكسرها كلها، وكان بعض أصحابنا يأخذ خشبة ويذهب إلى خلوته، فكلما غفل ضرب رأسه بها، حتى يأتي رأسُه كلَّه مفلول.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-14","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"وبلغني أن بعض أصحابنا كان يُدخل في لحمة رجله سكيناً كلما غفل قلبه، وهذا إغراق، وخير الأمور أوسطها.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-15","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_34-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_34-16","r":"q4_34","title":"4:34 · Marital responsibility, contested disciplinary reports, and spiritual mastery of the self","text":"ولمّا تكلم على حكم المرأة الطائعة والناشزة، تكلم على ما إذا أشكل الأمر، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_34-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_34-s1","r":"q4_34","title":"The subject al-ṣāliḥāt; causation; a variant reading","text":"I say: “The upright women” (الصالحات) is a subject (مبتدأ), and what follows gives information about it (خبر). The prefixed fāʾ (الفاء) indicates consequence and derivation (السببية والتفريع), as though He were saying: Men are charged with responsibility for women; whoever is upright is to receive the good treatment she deserves, and whoever is recalcitrant is dealt with through admonition and the other measures indicated. Every mā (ما) in the verse is verbal-noun forming (مصدرية), except on Abū Jaʿfar’s reading “by what has safeguarded God [His rights]” (بما حفظ الله), where “God” is in the accusative; here mā is understood as a nominal relative (موصولة اسمية): through that which safeguards God [His rights], namely her obedience to God, by which He in turn protects her. It has also been analysed as a maṣdariyya. Consult al-Thaʿlabī.","anchor":"en-q4_34-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_34-s2","r":"q4_34","title":"Two grounds of household responsibility in Ibn ʿAjība’s account","text":"The Real, majestic is His glory, says: “Men are charged with responsibility for women”—that is, they stand in relation to them as governors to those in their care with respect to discipline, expenditure and teaching. Ibn ʿAjība describes two grounds for this in the social and legal order he expounds: one bestowed (وهبي) and the other acquired (كسبي). Under the former he places what he considers the greater strength, planning and discernment of men in works and acts of worship, and the historically male offices of prophecy, leadership, public guardianship, certain acts of worship, testimony in judicial proceedings, military obligation, Friday prayer, agnatic inheritance, larger inheritance shares and unilateral pronouncement of divorce. The acquired ground is “what they spend of their wealth” in dowries (المهور), maintenance (النفقة), and clothing. A husband is therefore obliged to discharge his dealings with his wives justly (بالعدل). An upright woman (صالحة) devoted in obedience (قانتة)—to God and, within the account being given, to her husband—guards in his absence his household property, her chastity and his confidence. God has preserved her by giving her trustworthiness and constancy and by fixing religion firmly in her heart. Or, because she preserves God’s right, God protects her: as the Prophet is quoted as saying, “Be mindful of God and He will guard you.” [H035]","anchor":"en-q4_34-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_34-s3","r":"q4_34","title":"Reciprocal good treatment, nushūz and its limits","text":"Such a wife, Ibn ʿAjība says, is owed good conduct by her husband: he must respond to her beneficence with equally good care. He cites the report, “The best woman is she who pleases you when you look at her, obeys when you instruct her, and in your absence safeguards you in respect of her property and herself.” [H036] He says that the Prophet then recited this verse. Regarding women whose nushūz (نشوز)—rising up in disobedience against the husband—is feared or, on one interpretation, known, Ibn ʿAjība glosses the successive expressions as verbal admonition (وعظ), if that proves ineffective, withdrawal in the sleeping place (هجر في المضاجع), that is not sharing the cover or refraining from intercourse, and, if that too proves ineffective, finally ḍarb (ضرب), which he constrains as a blow that is neither painful nor disfiguring (غير مؤلم ولا شائن). He quotes, “Hang the whip where the household can see it” [H037] , and relates from Asmāʾ daughter of Abū Bakr an account of al-Zubayr striking one of his four wives with a wooden clothes-rack rod until it broke [R002] . [Translator’s note: the latter is a report about al-Zubayr, not a saying attributed here to the Prophet.] “If they obey you”—or resolve to repent of what has passed—“do not seek a way against them”: do not look for a pretext to injure them. Treat any preceding nushūz as though it had not occurred; “one who repents of sin is like one without sin” [H038] . Ibn ʿUyayna explained that husbands are not to demand that their wives love them. Al-Wartajbī likewise says that when the outward form of compliance occurs, requiring their inward natural dispositions to match one’s own would be a quarrel with providence. He cites “There is no changing God’s creation” [Q 30:30] and the report “Souls are like enlisted companies” [H039] . Finally, “God is exalted, great” is a warning to husbands: He has greater power over you than you possess over those in your care; despite His greatness He overlooks your faults, and you have still stronger reason to pardon theirs. Or the verse teaches that God is too great and exalted to wrong anyone or withhold anyone’s due.","anchor":"en-q4_34-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_34-s4","r":"q4_34","title":"A reported occasion of revelation—its evidential limits","text":"As the occasion of revelation Ibn ʿAjība relates a story that Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ, one of the Medinan representatives, slapped his wife Ḥabība bint Zayd ibn Abī Zuhayr after a dispute. Her father accompanied her to the Messenger of God and said, “I gave him my precious daughter as wife, and he has slapped her!” The Prophet is reported first to have said that she should take equivalent retaliation; they departed, but he called them back and stated that Gabriel had brought the verse “Men are charged with responsibility for women.” He is then reported to have said, “We intended one thing and God intended another; what God intended is better,” whereupon the retaliation was abandoned. A second account attributes the occasion to another similar marital dispute. [Translator’s note: These transmitted narratives are not verified Prophetic hadith with secure isnāds ; the core story is found in early tafsīr reports, several of which are disconnected.] [R003] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_34-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_34-s5","r":"q4_34","title":"The strong wayfarer governs the lower self","text":"Strong men, in the inward meaning, are those who stand firmly over their lower selves (نفوس), mastering them through the strength God enables and through the spiritual struggles (المجاهدات) and disciplines (الرياضات) they expend. They watch and question the self at every moment. If it becomes upright, obeying and yielding to the demands of servanthood (أحكام العبودية) and carrying out the obligations that proceed from Lordship (وظائف الربوبية), they treat it honourably and graciously and release it from severity and chastisement. If it rebels and exalts itself, they train it, remove it from the places of its desires and repose, and impose correction proportionate to its obstinacy and heedlessness. Ibn ʿAjība then transmits accounts of exceptional ascetic practices: Abū Yazīd, he says, would enter seclusion with a handful of twigs and strike himself when inattentive until he had broken them all; one of the author’s companions took a wooden implement into seclusion and struck his own head whenever his attention lapsed, until his whole head was battered. He also relates having been informed of a person who injured his own leg with a knife during distraction. Ibn ʿAjība himself rejects the excess , stating: “This is going to extremes (إغراق); the best of matters is their middle course.” [Translator’s note: these anecdotes are historical claims in the source, not practical instructions to the reader.] Through God comes success.","anchor":"en-q4_34-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_34-s6","r":"q4_34","title":"","text":"After addressing the compliant wife and one described as rebellious, he turns to cases in which the matter is disputed or unclear.","anchor":"en-q4_34-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_35","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit 4:35","anchor":"unit-q4_35"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-1","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ شِقاقَ بَيْنِهِما فَابْعَثُوا حَكَماً مِنْ أَهْلِهِ وَحَكَماً مِنْ أَهْلِها إِنْ يُرِيدا إِصْلاحاً يُوَفِّقِ اللَّهُ بَيْنَهُما إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيماً خَبِيراً (35)","anchor":"ar-q4_35-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-2","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"قلت: الشقاق: المخالفة والمساورة، وأضيف إلى الظرف توسعًا كقوله: بَلْ مَكْرُ اللَّيْلِ، والأصل: شقاقًا بينهما، والضمير في (يُريدا) للحكمين، وفي (بينهما) للزوجين، وقيل: للحكمين معًا، وقيل: للزوجين معًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_35-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-3","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنْ خِفْتُمْ يا معشر الحكام، أي علمتم خلافَا بين الزوجين ومشارة، ولم تدروا الظالم من المظلوم، فَابْعَثُوا رجلين أمينين يحكمان بينهما، يكون أحدهما من أهله والآخر من أهلها، لأن الأقارب أعرف ببواطن الأحوال، وأطلب للإصلاح، فإن بعثهما الحاكمُ أجنبيين صح، وكذا إن أقامهما الزوجان.","anchor":"ar-q4_35-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-4","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"وما اتفق عليه الحكمان لزم الزوجين من خُلع أو طلاق أو وفاق. وقال أبو حنيفة: ليس لهما التطليق إلاَّ أن يجعل لهما، وإذا اختلفا لم يلزم شيء، ويستأنفان الحكم، قال ابن جُزَي: ومشهور مذهب مالك: أن الحاكم هو الذي يبعث","anchor":"ar-q4_35-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-5","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"الحكمين، وقيل: الزوجان، وجرت عادة القضاء أن يبعثوا امرأة أمينة ولا يبعثوا الحكمين، قال بعض العلماء: هو تغيير للقرآن والسنة الجارية. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_35-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-6","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"فإن بُعِث الحكمان، فإن أرادا إصلاحًا بين الزوجين، واتفقا عليه، وفق الله بينهما ببركة قصدهما، وفيه تنبيه على أن من أصلح نيته فيما يتحراه أصلح الله مبتغاه. إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلِيماً خَبِيراً بما في الظواهر والبواطن، فيعلم كيف يرفع الشقاق ويوقع الوفاق.","anchor":"ar-q4_35-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-7","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"الإشارة: وإن خفتم، أيها الشيوخ، على صاحبكم منازعة النفس والروح فكانت النفس تجمح به إلى أسفل سافلين، بمتابعة هواها وعصيان مولاها، والروح تجنح به إلى أعلى عليين، بجهاد هواها ومشاهدة مولاها، فابعثوا له واردين قويين، إما شوق مقلق يرحل الروح إلى مولاها، أو خوف مزعج يزجر النفس عن هواها. فإن أراد الله بذلك العبد إصلاحًا لحاله أرسلهما معًا متفقين على تخليصه وارتفاعه، فيتقدم الخوف المزعج ويستدركه الشوق المقلق، فيلتحق بأهل التحقيق من أهل التوفيق، وما ذلك على الله بعزيز، وفي الحكم: «لا يُخرِج الشهوةَ من القلب إلا خوف مُزعج، أو شوقٍ مقلق» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_35-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_35-8","r":"q4_35","title":"4:35 · Two arbiters, reconciliation and the dialogue of soul and spirit","text":"ولما فرغ الحق جل جلاله من الكلام على حفظ الأموال، وحفظ الأنساب، وبعض حفظ الأبدان، شرع يتكلم على حفظ الأديان، وما يتعلق بذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_35-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_35-s1","r":"q4_35","title":"Shiqāq, ellipsis and the referents of the pronouns","text":"I say: Shiqāq (الشقاق) signifies opposition and conflict. Its annexation to an adverbial expression (إضافة إلى الظرف) is an extension of usage, like “the plotting of the night” (مكر الليل); the underlying wording would be “a rupture between them.” The dual pronoun in “if they both desire” (إن يريدا) refers to the two arbiters, whereas that in “He will reconcile between them” (بينهما) refers to husband and wife. Some apply both pronouns to the arbiters; others apply both to the spouses.","anchor":"en-q4_35-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_35-s2","r":"q4_35","title":"Appointment and powers of the two arbitrators","text":"The Real, majestic is His glory, says: If you, the authorities (الحكام), perceive a dispute between the spouses and cannot tell oppressor from wronged party, appoint two trustworthy men to adjudicate between them, one from his family and one from hers. Relatives generally know their inner circumstances better and are more eager to effect reconciliation. It remains valid if a magistrate appoints two outsiders, and likewise if the spouses themselves appoint the pair. What the two arbiters agree upon, whether khulʿ (خلع), divorce (طلاق), or accommodation, binds the couple according to the view presented here. Abū Ḥanīfa, by contrast, holds that they cannot effect divorce unless authorized to do so. If the arbiters disagree, nothing binds the spouses and the adjudication must be undertaken afresh. Ibn Juzayy says: “The well-known position in Mālik’s school is that the magistrate appoints the two arbiters, though another opinion assigns that appointment to the spouses. In judicial practice a trustworthy woman is sometimes sent instead of the two arbiters; some scholars called this a change to the Qurʾān and the established sunna.” End of quotation.","anchor":"en-q4_35-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_35-s3","r":"q4_35","title":"Right intention and divine help in reconciliation","text":"When the two arbiters are appointed and sincerely seek reconciliation, God brings harmony between the spouses through the blessing of their intention. This points to a general principle: whoever makes his intention sound in what he pursues, God makes the goal of his pursuit sound. “God is knowing, fully aware”: He knows outward states and inward thoughts and knows how to lift the estrangement and establish concord.","anchor":"en-q4_35-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_35-s4","r":"q4_35","title":"Fear and longing as arbiters between the lower soul and the spirit","text":"If, spiritual teachers, you fear conflict between the lower soul (النفس) and the spirit (الروح) in a companion—when the soul races towards the lowest depths by following its passion and disobeying its Lord, while the spirit rises towards the highest heights by striving against passion and witnessing its Master—send powerful inward arrivals of two kinds (واردان): either a disquieting yearning (شوق مقلق) that draws the spirit toward its Master, or an unsettling fear (خوف مزعج) that restrains the lower soul from its passion. If God intends reform for the servant, He sends both in harmony for the servant’s liberation and ascent. Fear comes first, disturbing the soul and curbing it; longing then catches up, so that the servant joins the people of realization (أهل التحقيق) and divine enabling (أهل التوفيق). This is no great matter for God. As a saying in the Ḥikam has it: “Nothing drives desire from the heart except a fear that unsettles or a longing that disquiets.” [A035] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_35-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_35-s5","r":"q4_35","title":"","text":"After discussing the preservation of wealth, lineage, and some matters of bodily security, the Real begins to discuss the preservation of religion and what pertains to it.","anchor":"en-q4_35-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_36","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd 4:36","anchor":"unit-q4_36"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-1","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"وَاعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ وَلا تُشْرِكُوا بِهِ شَيْئاً وَبِالْوالِدَيْنِ إِحْساناً وَبِذِي الْقُرْبى وَالْيَتامى وَالْمَساكِينِ وَالْجارِ ذِي الْقُرْبى وَالْجارِ الْجُنُبِ وَالصَّاحِبِ بِالْجَنْبِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ وَما مَلَكَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كانَ مُخْتالاً فَخُوراً (36)","anchor":"ar-q4_36-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-2","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"قلت: الجُنب- بالضم-: البعيد، يقال فيه: جُنُب وأجنب وأجنبي، وسمي الجُنبُ جُنُبًا لأنه يبعد من المسجد وعن الصلاة وعن التلاوة، و (مختال) اسم فاعل، وأصله: مختيل، بالكسر، من الخُيَلاَء وهو التكبر.","anchor":"ar-q4_36-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-3","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَاعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ أي: وَحِّدُوه وأطيعوه وَلا تُشْرِكُوا بِهِ شَيْئاً جليًا أو خفيًا في اعتقادكم أو في عبادتكم، فمن قصد الحج والتجارة، فقد أشرك مع الله في عبادته، وأحسنوا بالوالدين إحسانًا حسنًا، وهو برهما والقيام بحقهما، وَبِذِي الْقُرْبى، أي: القرابة في النسب، أو الدين وَالْيَتامى لضعف حالهم، وَالْمَساكِينِ لقلة ما بيدهم، وقد شكى بعض الناس قساوة قلبه، فقال له عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إن أردتَ أن يلين قلبُك، فأطعم المسكين وامسح رأس اليتيم، وأطعمه» .","anchor":"ar-q4_36-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-4","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"وَالْجارِ ذِي الْقُرْبى الذي قّرُب جواره أو نسبه، وَالْجارِ الْجُنُبِ الذي بَعُد مكانه أو نسبه، وحَدَّد بعضُهم الجوار بأربعين دارًا من كل ناحية. وقال ابن عباس: الجار ذي القربى: الجار الذي بينك وبينه قرابة، والجار الجنب: الجار من قوم آخرين. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_36-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-5","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"قيل يا رسول الله: ما حق الجار على الجار قال: «إن دعاك أجبتَه، وإن أصابته فاقةٌ عُدتَ عليه، وإن استقرضك أقرضته، وإن أصابه خير هنأته، وإن مرض عدته، وإن أصابته مصيبة عزيته، وإن توفي شهدت جنازته، ولا تستعل عليه بالبنيان لتحجب عنه الريح إلا بإذنه، ولا تؤذه بقُتار قدرك- أي: بخارها- إلا أن تغرف له منها، وإن ابتعت فاكهة فأهد له منها، فإن لم تفعل فأدخلها سرًا، ولا يخرج ولدك منها بشيء فيغيظ ولده» ثم قال: «الجيران ثلاثة: فَجَارٌ له ثلاثة حقوق: حق الجوَارِ، وحق القرابة، وحق الإسلام، وجار له حقان: حق الجِوَار، وحق الإسلام، وجَارٌ له حق واحد: وهو المشرك من أهل الكتاب» .","anchor":"ar-q4_36-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-6","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"وَالصَّاحِبِ بِالْجَنْبِ، وهو الرفيق في أمر حسن، كتعلم وتصرف وصناعة وسفر، فإنه صحبك بجنبك، وعن عليّ- كرّم الله وجهه- (أنها الزّوجة) ، فيتأكد في حقها الإحسان زيادة على المعاشرة بالمعروف، قال بعضهم: أول قدم في الولاية كف الأذى وحمل الجفا، ومعيار ذلك حسن معاشرة الأهل والولد، وقال- عليه الصلاة السلام-: «خَيرُكُمْ خَيْرُكُمْ لِنسَائِه، وأنَا خَيْرُكُمْ لِنسَائِي» . وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ، وهو الضيف أو المسافر لغرابته، وَما مَلَكَتْ أَيْمانُكُمْ، من الإماء والعبيد، وكَانَ آخر كلام النبي- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «الصلاةَ الصَلاةَ وَمَا مَلَكتْ أيمانُكُمْ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_36-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-7","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كانَ مُخْتالًا أي: متكبراً، يأنف عن أقاربه وجيرانه وأصحابه ولا يلتفت إليهم، فَخُوراً يتفاخر عليهم بماله وجاهه، وما خوله الله من نعمه، فهو جدير أن تسلب منه.","anchor":"ar-q4_36-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-8","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"الإشارة: واعبدوا الله، أي: بالقيام بوظائف العبودية، ومشاهدة عظمة الربوبية، وقال بعض الحكماء:","anchor":"ar-q4_36-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-9","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"العبودية: ترك الاختيار، وملازمة الذل والافتقار. وقيل: العبودية أربعة أشياء: الوفاء بالعهود، والحفظ للحدود، والرضا بالموجود، والصبر على المفقود، وعنوان ذلك صفاء التوحيد، ولذلك قال: وَلا تُشْرِكُوا بِهِ شَيْئاً أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_36-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-10","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"لا تَرَوْا معه غيره، كما قال القائل:","anchor":"ar-q4_36-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-11","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"مُذْ عَرفْتُ الإِلَهَ لَمْ أَرَ غَيْراً ... وكَذا الْغَيْرُ عندنا ممْنُوعُ","anchor":"ar-q4_36-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-12","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"وقال آخر: (لو كلفت أن أرى غيره، لم أستطع، فإنه لا غير معه حتى أشهده) . فإذا حصلت العبودية في الظاهر، وتحقق التوحيد في الباطن، ظهرت عليه مكارم الأخلاق فيُحسن إلى الأقارب والأجانب، ويجود عليهم","anchor":"ar-q4_36-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-13","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"بالحس والمعنى، لأن الفتوة من شأن أهل التوحيد، ومن شيم أهل التجريد، كما هو معلوم من حالهم، نفعنا الله بذكرهم، وخرطنا في سلكهم. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q4_36-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-14","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"قال الورتجبي: «الوالدين» : مشايخ المعرفة. ثم نقل عن الجنيد، أنه قال: أمرني أبي أمرًا، وأمرني السري أمرًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_36-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-15","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"فقدمت أمر السري على أمر أبي، وكل ما وجدت فهو من بركاته. هـ. وذوو القربى هم الأخوة في الشيخ، واليتامى: من قصدهم من المتفقرة الجاهلة، والمساكين: ضعفاء اليقين من العامة، أمر الله تعالى أهل الخصوصية بالإحسان إليهم والبرور بهم، وهو أن يقرهم في طريقهم، ويحوشهم إلى ربهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_36-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-16","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"والجار ذي القربى وهو جارك في السكنى وأخوك في النسبة، فيستحق عليك زيادة الإحسان. والجار الجنب: من جاورك من العوام فتنصحه وترشده، والصاحب بالجنب: من رافقك في أمر من العوام، كَسَفَرٍ وغيره، وابن السبيل:","anchor":"ar-q4_36-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-17","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"من نزل بأهل الخصوصية من الأضياف، فلهم حق الضيافة عليهم حسًّا ومعنًى، وما ملكت أيمانكم: مالكم تصرف عليهم من الأهل والبنين والإماء والعبيد، فتقربونهم إلى حضرة الملك المجيد. ثم أمرهم بالتواضع والإقبال على الخاص والعام. فقال: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كانَ مُخْتالًا فَخُوراً. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_36-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_36-18","r":"q4_36","title":"4:36 · The rights of parents, neighbours and dependants; service as an expression of tawḥīd","text":"ثم بيّن حال أضداد هؤلاء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_36-18"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_36-s1","r":"q4_36","title":"Junub and mukhtāl: lexical and morphological explanations","text":"I say: Junub (الجُنُب), with ḍamma, means “distant.” One may say junub, ajnab, or ajnabī. A person in a state of major ritual impurity is called junub , it is said, because he remains away from the mosque, prayer, and Qurʾānic recitation. Mukhtāl (مختال, arrogant or vainglorious) is an active participle (اسم فاعل). Its underlying form is mukhtayil (مختيل) from khuyalāʾ (الخيلاء), pride.","anchor":"en-q4_36-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_36-s2","r":"q4_36","title":"The divine rights and kindness to parents and vulnerable people","text":"The Real, majestic is His glory, says: “Worship God”: affirm His oneness (وحّدوه) and obey Him. “Do not associate anything with Him,” openly or covertly, in creed or worship. Ibn ʿAjība gives as an example a person intending pilgrimage and commerce simultaneously: on the rigorous interpretation of purity of intention presented here, such a person mixes another aim into his worship. “Show kindness to parents” means to honour them and fulfil their claims; to relatives, by blood or in religion; to orphans, on account of the weakness of their state; and to the poor, because of their scarce resources. It is reported that someone complained of a hard heart to the Prophet, who replied, “If you wish your heart to soften, feed the needy, stroke the head of an orphan, and feed him.” [H041] [Source note: The Aḥmad 7576 route located in the source register passes through an unnamed intermediary. This is a limitation of that chain, not a verdict on every parallel. The additional words “and feed him” in Ibn ʿAjība’s quotation are not present in that short Aḥmad wording.]","anchor":"en-q4_36-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_36-s3","r":"q4_36","title":"Near and distant neighbours and the long catalogue of obligations","text":"“The near neighbour” is one whose dwelling or kinship is close; “the distant neighbour” is one whose place or ancestry is further away. Some defined neighbourhood as extending forty houses in every direction. Ibn ʿAbbās said that the near neighbour is the one connected to you by kin, while the distant neighbour belongs to another group. When someone asked the Messenger of God about a neighbour’s rights, Ibn ʿAjība quotes an extended report: “If he invites you, accept his invitation; if he falls into need, provide for him; if he seeks a loan, lend to him; if good comes to him, congratulate him; if he becomes sick, visit him; if misfortune befalls him, console him; if he dies, attend his funeral. Do not raise your building above his so as to deprive him of the breeze without his permission. Do not distress him with the smell of your cooking unless you give him a portion. If you buy fruit, give some to him; otherwise bring it indoors discreetly, and do not let your child carry it out in sight of his child so as to provoke longing.” He then quotes its classification of neighbours according to three, two, or one right: the Muslim neighbour who is also a relative, the Muslim neighbour, and a polytheist neighbour from the People of the Book. [H042] Translator’s source note. The extended version is transmitted through a route whose narrators Suwayd b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, ʿUthmān b. ʿAṭāʾ and his father are criticized by al-Bayhaqī; al-Dhahabī also identifies weaknesses in this route and a disconnection in a separate Muʿādh version. The shorter report in al-Bukhārī 6014 supports the general duty towards neighbours [H048] .","anchor":"en-q4_36-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_36-s4","r":"q4_36","title":"Companions, spouses, travellers, and historically dependent persons","text":"“The companion at one’s side” (الصاحب بالجنب) is anyone accompanying one in a good undertaking: learning, work, a craft, or a journey. ʿAlī interpreted this expression as “the wife”; then the call to excellence towards her is especially emphatic, in addition to the command to associate with her honourably. Someone said: “The first step upon the path of sainthood is to withhold harm and to bear harshness; the test is one’s good conduct towards spouse and children.” The Prophet is quoted as saying, “The best of you are those best to their wives, and I am the best of you to my wives.” [H043] “The wayfarer” is a traveller or guest who is a stranger in the place. “Those whom your right hands possess” denotes female and male slaves within historical slaveholding institutions. Ibn ʿAjība adds a last injunction attributed to the Prophet: “Prayer, prayer—and those whom your right hands possess!” [H044] [Source note: Ibn Mājah 2698 transmits the last-words frame and the injunction, with “prayer” stated once. Source attribution does not by itself establish the strength of this particular chain or its separate parallels.] “God does not love the arrogant, boastful person”: one who disdains relatives, neighbours and companions and pays no attention to them, and boasts over them about wealth, office, and God’s gifts, exposes himself to the withdrawal of those gifts.","anchor":"en-q4_36-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_36-s5","r":"q4_36","title":"Servanthood as poverty, trust and purified intention","text":"“Worship God” means to carry out the functions of servanthood (وظائف العبودية) while witnessing the majesty of Lordship (عظمة الربوبية). Some sages said: “Servanthood is relinquishing personal choice, adhering to humility, and acknowledging need.” Another definition gives four components: fulfilment of covenants, preservation of limits, contentment with what is present, and patience concerning what is absent. The mark that gathers these is the purity of the realization of oneness (صفاء التوحيد). Thus “associate nothing with Him” means: do not see any other alongside Him. As a poet said: “Since I knew the Godhead, I have seen no other; / Indeed, for us any ‘other’ is ruled out.” Someone else said: “If I were commanded to behold something other than Him, I could not, for there is no other alongside Him for me to witness.” Once servanthood is established outwardly and oneness inwardly realized, noble character appears in the servant. He does good to relatives and strangers and gives to them both materially and spiritually, because generosity of soul (الفتوة) is a characteristic of the people of oneness and of spiritual detachment (التجريد). May God benefit us through their remembrance and number us among them. Amen.","anchor":"en-q4_36-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_36-s6","r":"q4_36","title":"Parents and neighbours as metaphors for relationships of spiritual training","text":"Al-Wartajbī explains “parents” as the teachers of divine knowledge. He transmits from al-Junayd: “My father gave me one command and al-Sarrī gave me another. I put al-Sarrī’s command before my father’s, and everything I have found has come through its blessing.” Kin are one’s brothers in the spiritual guide. Orphans are those untrained, needy seekers who approach them; the poor are the people of weak certainty among the generality. God has commanded those granted special realization (أهل الخصوصية) to treat them with beneficence: to confirm them in their path and gather them toward their Lord. The near neighbour is someone who lives next to you and is joined to you in spiritual affiliation; an additional share of good conduct is owed him. The distant neighbour is an ordinary person living nearby: advise and guide him. The companion at one’s side is an ordinary person accompanying you in travel or another affair. The wayfarer is a guest staying with the people of special realization; such a guest has rights of hospitality, material and spiritual. “Those whom your right hands possess” signifies, in the author’s social order, the family members, children, and persons under one’s care whom one can affect; bring them near to the Presence of the glorious King. Finally, humility and openness towards both the special and the general is demanded by “God does not love the arrogant, boastful.” God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_36-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_36-s7","r":"q4_36","title":"","text":"He then describes those who behave in the contrary way.","anchor":"en-q4_36-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_037","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity 4:37–39","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_037"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-1","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"الَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ وَيَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبُخْلِ وَيَكْتُمُونَ ما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ وَأَعْتَدْنا لِلْكافِرِينَ عَذاباً مُهِيناً (37) وَالَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ رِئاءَ النَّاسِ وَلا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَلا بِالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَمَنْ يَكُنِ الشَّيْطانُ لَهُ قَرِيناً فَساءَ قَرِيناً (38) وَماذا عَلَيْهِمْ لَوْ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَأَنْفَقُوا مِمَّا رَزَقَهُمُ اللَّهُ وَكانَ اللَّهُ بِهِمْ عَلِيماً (39)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-2","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"قلت: (الذين) بدل مِن: «مَن كان» ، أو منصوب على الذم، أو مرفوع عليه، أي: هم. أو مبتدأ حُذف خبره، أي: نعذبهم عذابًا مُهينًا، أو أحقاء بكل ملامة، و (الذين ينفقون) : عطف على الأولى، أو مبتدأ حُذف خبره، أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-3","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"الشيطان قرينهم. والبخل فيه لغتان: البُخل والبَخَل بحركتين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-4","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: الَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ بأموالهم على أقاربهم وجيرانهم، وَيَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبُخْلِ وَيَكْتُمُونَ ما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ من الغنى، فيظهرون القلة والعيلة، أو يكتمون العلم بصفة النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، هم أحقاء بكل لوم وعتاب. وَأَعْتَدْنا لِلْكافِرِينَ منهم عَذاباً مُهِيناً يُهينهم ويُخزيهم، نزلت في اليهود، كانوا يقولون","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-5","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"للأنصار: لا تنفقوا أموالكم، فإنا نخشى عليكم الفقر، وكتموا صفته- عليه الصلاة والسلام-. ووضع الظاهر موضع المضمر وكأنه يقول: وأعتدنا لهم، إشعارًا بأن مَن هذا شأنه فهو كافر بنعمة الله تعالى، ومن كفر بنعمة الله وأهانها استحق عذابًا مهينًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-6","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"وَالَّذِينَ يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوالَهُمْ رِئاءَ النَّاسِ طلبا لمدحهم وخوفًا من ذمهم، وَلا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَلا بِالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ، يتحرّون بإنفاقهم مراضيه، فالشيطان قرينهم لا يفارقهم، وَمَنْ يَكُنِ الشَّيْطانُ لَهُ قَرِيناً فَساءَ قَرِيناً، فلمّا كان الشيطان قرينهم زين لهم التهالك على الأموال والرياء في الأعمال، وإنما أشرك أهل الرياء مع البخلاء في الوعيد من حيث إنهما طَرَفَا تفريط وإفراط، وهما سواء في القبح واستجلاب الذم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-7","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"وَماذا عَلَيْهِمْ لَوْ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَأَنْفَقُوا مِمَّا رَزَقَهُمُ اللَّهُ أي: لا ملامة عليهم ولا تبعة تحيق بهم لو أخلصوا الإيمان وأنفقوا مما رزقهم الكريم المنان. قال البيضاوي: وفيه تنبيه على أن المدعو إلى أمر لا ضرر فيه ينبغي أن يُجيب إليه احتياطاً، فكيف إذا تضمن المنافع. وإنما قدم الإيمان هاهنا وأخره في الآية الأخرى: لأن القصد بذكره هنا التخصيص، وثَم التقليل. هـ. وَكانَ اللَّهُ بِهِمْ عَلِيماً لا يخفى عليه شيء من أمورهم وقصدهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-8","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"الإشارة: قال بعض الصوفية: (مِن أقبح كل قبيح صوفي شحيح) ، فالصوفية العارفون- رضى الله عنهم- الذين هم صفوة العباد متخلقون بأضداد ما وسم به الحق- تعالى- أهل العناد، فهم يجودون بأنفسهم وما خصهم الله به من العلوم اللدنية والأسرار القدسية، على من يستحقه من أهل التخلية والتحلية، ويأمرون الناس بالسخاء ومكارم الأخلاق، ويتحدثون بما منحهم الملك الخلاق، ويظهرون الغنى بالله والاكتفاء به عن كل ما سواه، وإذا بذلوا أموالهم أعطوها لله وبالله ومن الله وإلى الله وابتغاء مرضاة الله، هجم عليهم اليقين، وتمكنوا من شهود رب العالمين، فلا يقرب ساحتهم الشيطان، ولا يرون في الدارين إلا الملك الديان، تحبهم ملائكة الرحمن، ويحن إليهم الإنس والجان. نفعنا الله بمحبتهم، وخرطنا في مسلكهم، آمين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_037-9","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"4:37–39 · Miserliness, ostentation, and sincerity","text":"ثم رغّب الحق- تعالى- فى الإنفاق مع الإخلاص، الذي هو عنوان الدين الخاص، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_037-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_037-s1","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"Language and construction (qultu)","text":"“Those who” ( alladhīna ) may be a substitute ( badal ) for “whoever was” ( man kāna ) in the preceding verse; alternatively it is in the accusative of censure ( naṣb ʿalā l-dhamm ) or nominative of censure, with an understood “they are.” It may also be an initial subject ( mubtadaʾ ) whose predicate has been omitted: “We shall punish them with a humiliating punishment,” or “they deserve every reproach.” “And those who spend” is coordinated with the first relative phrase, or begins a further sentence with an omitted predicate: “Satan is their companion.” The Arabic noun for miserliness is pronounced both bukhl and bakhal (with both vowels sounded in the latter form).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_037-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_037-s2","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"The outward interpretation (yaqūlu l-Ḥaqq)","text":"God—majestic and exalted is He—speaks of those who withhold their wealth from their relatives and neighbours, tell others to be miserly, and conceal the abundance He has given them, making themselves appear poor and needy. Alternatively, they conceal their knowledge of the Prophet's description, God bless him and grant him peace. Such people deserve reproach on every account. “We have prepared for the unbelievers among them a humiliating punishment”: one that disgraces and abases them. The passage was revealed concerning Jews who, according to the account cited here, advised the Anṣār not to spend because they feared poverty for them, and concealed the Prophet's description. God places the explicit word “unbelievers” where a pronoun, “them,” might have stood; this indicates that one who acts in this way has denied God's blessing, and whoever denies and dishonours His blessing deserves a humiliating punishment. Those who spend “to be seen by people” seek their praise and fear their blame; they do not believe in God or the Last Day [so as to] seek His good pleasure through their expenditure. [Source and textual note: Al-Bayḍāwī and Abū al-Suʿūd on 4:38 explicitly connect this phrase to belief with li-yataḥarraw , “so as to seek”: genuine belief would direct expenditure toward God’s pleasure. Cairo I:504 instead prints yataḥarrawna without that connective. The bracketed words recover the relation supported by both earlier texts; “His” remains divine, and no assertion that ostentatious spending pleases God is intended. This is a disclosed explanatory supply, not a claim that Cairo prints the connective.] Satan is the companion who does not leave them. He beautifies for them a ruinous attachment to wealth and ostentation ( riyāʾ ) in their works. Ibn ʿAjība says that the ostentatious are joined to the miserly in the warning because they occupy the two opposite extremes of falling short and going too far ( tafrīṭ and ifrāṭ ): alike in their ugliness and in provoking blame. “What harm would there have been to them had they believed in God and the Last Day and spent from what God had provided them?” Had they made their faith sincere and given of what the Generous Bestower had provided, no blame or harmful consequence would attach to them. Al-Bayḍāwī remarks that a person invited to something entailing no harm ought prudently to accept it—how much more when it entails benefits. He also explains the different ordering of belief in this passage and another: here belief is mentioned first to mark specification, there later to give [the reason]. [Textual note: Cairo I:504 attributes al-taqlīl , “diminution,” to al-Bayḍāwī. His commentary on 4:39 instead reads al-taʿlīl , “giving the reason”: the preceding verse’s unbelief explains the ostentation. The bracketed rendering follows the checked earlier source; the different Cairo word is expressly recorded.] “God has always known them well”: nothing of their deeds or intentions escapes Him.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_037-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_037-s3","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"(al-ishāra)","text":"A Sufi once said, “Among the ugliest of all ugly things is a miserly Sufi.” The Sufis who know God, the elect of His servants, have acquired the qualities opposite to those with which God describes obstinate people. They give generously of themselves and of the divinely bestowed knowledges ( ʿulūm laduniyya ) and holy mysteries ( asrār qudsiyya ) entrusted to them, to those ready to receive them through emptying themselves of vices ( takhliya ) and adorning themselves with virtues ( taḥliya ). They summon people to liberality and noble character, speak of the gifts granted by the Creator, and show themselves rich through God and sufficient with Him against everything else. When they give their wealth, they give it for God, by God, from God, toward God, seeking His good pleasure. Certainty ( yaqīn ) has overtaken them, and they are established in witnessing ( shuhūd ) the Lord of the worlds. Thus Satan cannot approach their precinct; in either abode they behold only the Sovereign, the Judge. The angels of the Merciful love them; human beings and jinn long for them. May God profit us through love for them and enroll us in their way. Amen.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_037-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_037-s4","r":"q4_cont_037","title":"","text":"God now encourages expenditure joined to sincerity, the distinguishing mark of the way of the elect.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_037-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_040","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense 4:40","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_040"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_040-1","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقالَ ذَرَّةٍ وَإِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُضاعِفْها وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَدُنْهُ أَجْراً عَظِيماً (40)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_040-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_040-2","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"قلت: الذرة: النملة الصغيرة الحمراء. وتطلق على جزء من أجزاء الهباء. ومن نَصَب (حسنة) فَخَبَرُ كان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_040-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_040-3","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"وأُنث الضمير باعتبار الخبر. أو لإضافة مثقال إلى ذرة، فاكتسب التأنيث، ومن رفع فهي تامة، وحذف نونها على غير قياس، تشبيهًا لها بحروف العلة. وضاعف وضعّف بمعنى واحد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_040-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_040-4","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَظْلِمُ أحدًا بحيث ينقص من ثواب عمله، أو يزيد فى عقاب ما يستحقه، ولو مثقال ذرة. بل يجازي كلاً على قدر عمله. فإن كان صالحًا، ولو صغر قدره، عظم أجره. وَإِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُضاعِفْها بعشر أمثالها إلى سبعمائة إلى أضعاف كثيرة، بحسب الإخلاص. قال أبو هريرة رضي الله عنه: سمعت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول: «إنَّ اللهَ يُعْطِي المُؤمنَ عَلى الحَسَنة ألفي ألف حَسَنة» ، ثم تلا إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقالَ ذَرَّةٍ الآية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_040-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_040-5","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَدُنْهُ أَجْراً عَظِيماً، وخيرًا جسيمًا، فضلاً منه وإحسانا. قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «إنَّ الله لا يَظْلِمُ المُؤمنَ حَسنةً، بل يُثاب عَلَيها الرزْقَ فِي الدُنيَا ويجزيه بها في الآخِرَةِ. والكَافِر يعطيه بها في الدُّنيَا، فإذا كان يوم القيامة لم يكُن لَهُ حَسَنةٌ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_040-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_040-6","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"الإشارة: كما أنَّ الحق تعالى لا يظلم طالبي الأجور، بل يضاعف لهم في زيادة الحور والقصور، كذلك لا يبخس طالبي القرب والحضور، ورفع الحُجب والستور. بل كلما فعلوا من أنواع المجاهدات ضاعف لهم أنوار المشاهدات. وكلما نقص لهم من الحس- ولو مثقال ذرة- زادهم في المعنى قَدْرَهُ وأكثر شهودًا ونظرة. وكلما يقهر النفس ولو مقدار الفتيل، شربوا مقداره وأكثر من خمرة الجليل، وهذا كله مع صحبة المشايخ أهل التربية، وإلاَّ فلا تزيده مجاهدته إلا حَجبًا وبعدًا عن الخصوصية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_040-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_040-7","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"4:40 · The smallest good deed and its immeasurable recompense","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى الموطن الذي تظهر فيه مقادير الأعمال، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_040-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_040-s1","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"Language and readings (qultu)","text":"A dharra is a tiny red ant; the word is also used for a particle of dust in the air. In the reading in which ḥasana (“good deed”) is accusative, it is the predicate of kāna (“be”), and the feminine pronoun is accounted for either by this predicate or by the genitive construction “weight of a dharra ,” which lends feminine agreement to the phrase. In the nominative reading, kāna is complete, meaning “exist”; the dropping of its final nūn is irregular and likened to the elision of a weak letter. The two verb forms ḍāʿafa and ḍaʿʿafa both mean “to multiply.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_040-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_040-s2","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"","text":"God does not wrong anyone by diminishing the reward for an action or increasing the punishment beyond what is deserved, even to the weight of a minute particle. Rather, He recompenses each according to what has been done. If the deed is righteous, however small, its recompense becomes great. He may multiply it tenfold, seven hundredfold, and many times beyond that according to the measure of sincerity. Abū Hurayra is cited as saying that he heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: “God gives the believer, for one good deed, two million good deeds,” and then recite the verse beginning “God does not wrong anyone by an atom's weight.” “And He grants, from His own presence, a tremendous reward”: a great good bestowed as sheer favour and beneficence. Ibn ʿAjība also quotes the Prophet: “God does not wrong a believer regarding a single good deed: he is provided for on account of it in this world and rewarded for it in the Hereafter. The unbeliever receives [the recompense of] his good deed in this world, so when the Day of Resurrection comes there is no good deed left for him.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_040-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_040-s3","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"","text":"Just as God neither wrongs those who seek rewards nor fails to multiply the recompense that brings the ḥūr and the palaces of Paradise, so He does not diminish the portion of those who seek nearness ( qurb ), presence ( ḥuḍūr ), and the lifting of veils and coverings. For every kind of spiritual striving ( mujāhada ) He multiplies the lights of direct witnessing ( mushāhada ). Whenever they lose so much as a particle of the sensible world ( ḥiss ), He increases their inward meaning ( maʿnā ), indeed by more than its measure, through further witnessing and insight. Every time they subdue the lower soul ( nafs ), even by the measure of a thread, they drink that measure and more of the wine of the Majestic One. All this, however, is with the companionship ( ṣuḥba ) of the masters of spiritual training ( mashāyikh ahl al-tarbiya ); without it, a person's striving only adds to his veils and distance from the special proximity of God ( khuṣūṣiyya ). God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_040-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_040-s4","r":"q4_cont_040","title":"","text":"God next mentions the place where the true measures of deeds will become manifest.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_040-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_041","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection 4:41–42","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_041"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_041-1","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"فَكَيْفَ إِذا جِئْنا مِنْ كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ بِشَهِيدٍ وَجِئْنا بِكَ عَلى هؤُلاءِ شَهِيداً (41) يَوْمَئِذٍ يَوَدُّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَعَصَوُا الرَّسُولَ لَوْ تُسَوَّى بِهِمُ الْأَرْضُ وَلا يَكْتُمُونَ اللَّهَ حَدِيثاً (42)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_041-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_041-2","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"قلت: (كيف) إذا كان الكلام بعدها تامًا أُعربت حالاً، كقولك: كيف جاء زيد؟ وإذا كان ناقصًا، كانت خبرًا، كقولك: كيف زيد؟ وهي هنا خبر، أي: كيف الأمر إذا ... الخ. وهي مبنية لتضمنها معنى الاستفهام، والعامل في (إذا) مضمون المبتدأ، أو الخبر، أي: كيف يستقر الأمر أو يكون إذا جئنا؟ ومن قرأ (تَسوّى) بالشد، فأصله تتسوى، أدغمت الأولى في الثانية، ومن قرأ (لو تُسوّى) بالبناء للمفعول فحذف الثانية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_041-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_041-3","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَكَيْفَ يكون حال هؤلاء الكفرة واليهود إِذا قامت القيامة وجِئْنا مِنْ كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ بِشَهِيدٍ يشهد عليها بخيرها وشرها، وهو نبيهم الذي أرسل إليهم، وَجِئْنا بِكَ أنت يا محمد عَلى هؤُلاءِ الأمة التي بعثت إليهم شَهِيداً عليهم، أو على صدق هؤلاء الشهداء شهيدًا، تشهد على صدق رسالتهم وتبليغهم؟ لعلمك بعقائدهم واستجماع شرعك مجامع قواعدهم، وقيل: عَلى هؤُلاءِ الكفرة المستفهم عن حالهم،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_041-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_041-4","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"وقيل: على المؤمنين لقوله: لِتَكُونُوا شُهَداءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيداً. يَوْمَئِذٍ يَوَدُّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَعَصَوُا الرَّسُولَ أي: الذين جمعوا بين الكفر والعصيان يتمنون أن تُسَوَّى بِهِمُ الْأَرْضُ فيكونون ترابًا لما يرون من هول المطلع، فإذا شهدت عليهم الرسل بالكفر قالوا: وَاللَّهِ رَبِّنا مَا كُنَّا مُشْرِكِينَ، فيُنطق ألسنتهم وأيديهم وأرجلهم بشركهم فيفتضحون وَلا يَكْتُمُونَ اللَّهَ حَدِيثاً واحدًا، لأنهم كلما هموا بالكتمان شهدت عليهم جوارحهم بالكفر والعصيان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_041-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_041-5","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"وقيل: إن القيامة مواطن، في موطن لا يتكلمون ولا تسمع إلا همسًا، وفي موطن يتكلمون ويقولون: واللهِ رَبِّنَا مَا كُنَّا مشركين، إلى غير ذلك من اختلاف أحوالهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_041-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_041-6","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"الإشارة: لا بد أن يحصل الندم لمن فاته صحبة أهل الخصوصية، حتى مات محجوباً عن مشاهدة أسرار الربوبية، لا سيما إذا انضم إليهم كفرهم بخصوصيتهم والإنكار عليهم، وذلك حين يكشف له عن مقامهم البهي وحالهم السني، مصاحبين للمقربين في جوار الأنبياء والمرسلين، وهو في مقام أهل اليمين، ثم يعاتب على ما أسر عليه من الكبائر، وهي معاصي القلوب والضمائر، وهذا إذا مات على الإسلام، وإلا فالإنكار على الأولياء شُؤمُه سوء الخاتمة. والعياذ بالله من ذلك. وقد تقدم أن العارفين بالله يشهدون على العلماء، والعلماء يشهدون على العموم، ونبينا- عليه الصلاة والسلام- يزكي من يحتاج إلى التزكية. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_041-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_041-7","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"4:41–42 · Witnesses at the Resurrection","text":"ثم تكلم على عماد الدين وهى الصلاة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_041-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_041-s1","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"Grammar and readings (qultu)","text":"When what follows the interrogative kayfa (“how?”) forms a complete proposition, it is parsed as a circumstantial accusative ( ḥāl ), as in “How did Zayd come?” When the proposition is incomplete, it is the predicate ( khabar ), as in “How is Zayd?” It is a predicate here: “How will the matter be when ...?” Its form is indeclinable because it contains the sense of interrogation. The governing element of idhā (“when”) is the meaning implied by the subject or predicate: “How will the matter stand or occur when We bring [the witnesses]?” In the doubled reading tassawwā , the original is tatasawwā , with “the first assimilated into the second”; in the passive reading tusawwā , “the second has been omitted.” [XV-N002]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_041-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_041-s2","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"","text":"What will become of the unbelievers and the Jews whom the passage addresses when the Resurrection occurs, when We bring from each community a witness to its good and evil deeds—the prophet sent to that community—and bring you, Muḥammad, as a witness over the people to whom you were sent? Alternatively, you witness the truthfulness of the other witnesses, that they did deliver their messages, through your knowledge of their teachings and because your revealed law gathers together their fundamental principles. It is also said that “these” means the unbelievers whose circumstances are being questioned, or else the believers, as in “that you may be witnesses over humankind and that the Messenger may be a witness over you” [Q 2:143]. On that Day those who joined unbelief to disobedience will wish the earth were level with them and they became dust, because of the terror confronting them. When the messengers bear witness against them, they will say, “By God, our Lord, we were not idolaters” [Q 6:23]. But their tongues, hands and feet are made to speak of their idolatry and expose them. Not a single statement can be concealed from God: whenever they intend concealment, their own limbs testify to unbelief and disobedience. Another explanation is that the Resurrection has distinct stations: at one there is no speaking, and nothing is heard but a whisper; at another they speak, saying, “By God, our Lord, we were not idolaters,” and so on. This explains the apparently different descriptions of their condition. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_041-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_041-s3","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"","text":"Remorse is unavoidable for one who dies without having enjoyed the company of the people of special spiritual election ( ahl al-khuṣūṣiyya ), veiled from witnessing the mysteries of divine lordship ( asrār al-rubūbiyya ). The remorse is particularly acute if they compounded this deprivation by rejecting the special station of those people and denouncing them. At the unveiling of their luminous rank and elevated state, they are seen in the company of those brought near, beside the prophets and messengers, whereas the others remain in the station of the People of the Right. The latter are reproached for what they hid of great sins—the sins of hearts and inner consciences. [Textual note: Cairo I:506 prints أسر عليه , with sīn , here provisionally rendered as concealment. The familiar أصر عليه would mean “persisted in it.” Ibn ʿAjība himself speaks at I:550, on 4:97–99, of “persistence in diseases of the heart” as among the gravest sins. That parallel strengthens the latter interpretation contextually, but does not attest a different letter in this sentence; the local reading remains unresolved.] That is if they die in Islam; otherwise, Ibn ʿAjība warns, hostility to God's friends can carry the ill omen of a bad ending. God protect us from it. It has already been stated that those who know God bear witness concerning the scholars, and the scholars concerning the generality of people, while the Prophet, peace be upon him, confirms whoever is in need of confirmation. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_041-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_041-s4","r":"q4_cont_041","title":"","text":"The exposition turns to prayer, the pillar on which religion rests.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_041-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_043","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution 4:43","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_043"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-1","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَقْرَبُوا الصَّلاةَ وَأَنْتُمْ سُكارى حَتَّى تَعْلَمُوا ما تَقُولُونَ وَلا جُنُباً إِلاَّ عابِرِي سَبِيلٍ حَتَّى تَغْتَسِلُوا وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ مَرْضى أَوْ عَلى سَفَرٍ أَوْ جاءَ أَحَدٌ مِنْكُمْ مِنَ الْغائِطِ أَوْ لامَسْتُمُ النِّساءَ فَلَمْ تَجِدُوا ماءً فَتَيَمَّمُوا صَعِيداً طَيِّباً فَامْسَحُوا بِوُجُوهِكُمْ وَأَيْدِيكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَفُوًّا غَفُوراً (43)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-2","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"قلت: جملة (وأنتم سكارى) : حال، وسكارى: جمع سكران، ويجمع على سَكارى بالفتح، وسكْرى بالسكون، و (لا جُنُبًا) عطف على جملة الحال، و (جُنب) يستوي فيه الواحد والاثنان والجماعة والمذكر والمؤنث، لأنه يجري مجرى المصدر، فلا يُثنى ولا يُجمع. و (إلا عابري) مستثنى من عام الأحوال، وأصل الغائط: الموضع المنخفض من الأرض، ثم أطلق على الواقع فيه مما يخرج من الإنسان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-3","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَقْرَبُوا الصَّلاةَ وَأَنْتُمْ سُكارى: لا تقوموا إليها وأنتم سكارى من خمر، أو غلبة نوم، أو شدة غفلة، حَتَّى تَعْلَمُوا ما تَقُولُونَ في صلاتكم، وتتدبروا ما تقرءون فيها، فالصلاة من غير حضور خاوية، وعند الخصوص باطلة، رُوِي أن عبد الرحمن بن عَوف صنَع مأدبة، ودَعَا إليها نفرًا من الصحابة، حين كانت الخمر مباحة، فأكلوا وشربوا حتى ثَمِلُوا، وجاء وقت صلاة المغرب، فتقدم أحدهم ليصلي بهم، فقرأ: أعبدُ ما تعبدون- من غير نفي- فنزلت الآية قبل تحريم الخمر، ثم حرمت بآية المائدة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-4","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"ولا تقربوها حالة جنابتكم في أي حال كان، إِلَّا عابِرِي سَبِيلٍ أي: في وقت سفركم، حيث لم تجدوا ماءً، بدليل ما يأتي، فيتيمم ويقرب الصلاة وهو جنب، وفيه دليل أن التيمم لا يرفع الحدث، قيل المراد بالصلاة مواضعها، وهي المساجد فلا يدخلها الجنب إلا مارًا، وبه قال الشافعي- رضى الله عنه- وقال أبو حنيفة: لا يجوز المرور، إلاَّ إذا كان فيه الماء والطريق. وقال مالك: لا يدخل إلا بالتيمم ولا يمر به أصلاً.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-5","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"فلا تقربوا الصلاة وأنتم جنب حَتَّى تَغْتَسِلُوا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-6","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ مَرْضى تخافون ضرر الماء، أو زيادته، أو تأخر برء، أو منع الوصول إلى الماء، أَوْ عَلى سَفَرٍ لم تجدوه فيه، أَوْ كنتم في الحضر مُحدِثِين حيث جاءَ أَحَدٌ مِنْكُمْ مِنَ الْغائِطِ، أو البول، أو بغيره من الأحداث، أَوْ لامَسْتُمُ النِّساءَ أي: مست بشرتكم بشرتهن، بقصد اللذة أو عند وجدانها، وبه قال مالك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-7","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"وقال الشافعي: ينقض مطلقًا، قصد أم لا، وجد أم لا، ولو بميتة، وقال أبو حنيفة: إن كانت ملامسة فاحشة بحيث يحصل الانتشار نقضت، وإلا فلا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-8","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"وقال ابن عباس والحسن البصري ومحمد بن الحسن: لا تنقض الملامسة مطلقًا، ويقاس على اللمس سائر نواقض الأسباب، فتحصَّل أن «أو» تبقى على أصلها من التقسيم، فتكون الآية نصًا في تيمم الحاضر الصحيح، وبه قال مالك، ولا يعيد. وقال الشافعي: يُصلي بالتيمم ويُعيد، وقال أبو حنيفة: لا يُصلي حتى يجد الماء، ومن قال: «أو» بمعنى الواو فخروج عن الأصل بلا داع.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-9","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"ثم قيّد التيمم في هذه الأحوال بفقد الماء، فقال: فَلَمْ تَجِدُوا ماء كافيًا، أو لم تقدروا على استعماله، فَتَيَمَّمُوا أي: اقصدوا صَعِيداً طَيِّباً أي: طاهرا، وهو ما صعد على وجه الأرض من جنسها كتراب، وهو الأفضل، وثلج وخضخاض (١) وحجر ومدر، لا شجر وحشيش ومعدن ذهب وفضة، وما التحق بالعقاقير، كشب، وملح، وكبريت، وغاسول (٢) وشبهه، فلا يجوز. وقال أبو حنيفة: بكل شيء من الأرض وما اتصل بها كشجر","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-10","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"وكحل، وزرنيخ، وشب ونورة، وجص، وجوهر، إلا منخالة الذهب والفضة والرصاص. وقال الشافعي: لا يجوز إلا بالتراب المنبت خاصة، وبه فسر الطيب، واشترط علوق التراب بيده، ولم يشترطه غيره.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-11","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"ثم علّم الكيفية فقال: فَامْسَحُوا بِوُجُوهِكُمْ وَأَيْدِيكُمْ. قال مالك: اليد اسم للكف بدليل قطع السارق منه، فجعل المسح إلى المرفق سنة. وقال الشافعي: فرض، قياسًا على الوضوء، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَفُوًّا غَفُوراً فلذلك يسَّر عليكم ورخص لكم في التيمم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-12","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"الإشارة: يا أيها الذين آمنوا لا تقربوا صلاة الحضرة القدسية، وأنتم سكارى بحب الدنيا الدنية، حتى يذهب عنكم سُكر حبها، وتعلموا ما تقولون في مناجاة خالقها، ولا جنبًا من جنابة الغفلة، إلا ما يمر بالخواطر على سبيل الندرة والقلة، حتى تغتسلوا بماء الغيب، الذي يحصل به طهارة الجنان، ويغيب المتطهر به عن رؤية الأكوان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-13","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"وإليه أشار ابن العربي الحاتمي: كما في طبقات الشعراني، ونسبها غيرُه للجنيد- رضى الله عنهم أجمعين- وهو الأصح، بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-14","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"تَوَضَّأ بماءِ الغَيبِ إن كُنتَ ذا سِرٍّ ... وإلاَّ تَيَمَّم بالصَّعِيدِ أو الصَّخر","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-15","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"وقَدِّم إمَامًا كُنتَ أنتَ إمَامَه ... وصَلِّ صلاة الظُّهرِ فى أول العصر","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-16","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"فَهَذِي صَلاةُ العَارِفينَ بربّهِم ... فإن كنت منهم فانضح البرِّ بالبَحر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-17","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"أي: إن لم تقدر على الطهارة الأصلية وهي الغيبة عن الأحداث الكونية، فاقصد العبادة الحسية، وقَّدم الشريعة أو من قام بها من أهل التربية النبوية أمامك، بعد أن كان يطلبك قبل أن تعرفه، واجمع ظُهر الشريعة لعصر الحقيقة، فهذه صلاة العارفين، فإن كنت منهم فانضح بَرَّ ظاهرك بحقيقة باطنك، فما كمن في غيب السرائر ظهر في شهادة الظواهر. لهذا أشار تعالى بقوله: (وإن كنتم مرضى) بحب الهوى، (أو على سفر) في عجلة شغل الدنيا، أو جاء أحد منكم من غائط الحس، أو لامستم العلوم الرسمية، وانطبع صُورُ خيالها في قلوبكم، ولم تجدوا من يسقيكم ماء الغيب، وهي الخمرة الأزلية، فاقصدوا الأعمال الحسية، فلعلها توصلكم إلى الأعمال الباطنية، (إن الله كان عفوًا غفورًا) ، وفي الحِكَم: «كيف يشرق قلبٌ صورُ الأكوان منطبعة في مرآته؟ أم كيف يرحل إلى الله وهو مُكَبَّل بشهواته، أم كيف يطمع أن يدخل حضرة الله وهو لم يتطهر من جنابة غفلاته؟ أم كيف يرجو أن يفهم دقائق الأسرار وهو لم يتب من هفواته؟» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_043-18","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"4:43 · Intoxication, major impurity, and dry ablution","text":"ثم نبه الحق تعالى على عداوة اليهود، وأنّ من شأنهم إذا سمعوا عليكم مثل ما وقع من تحريف الآية الذي صدر من المصلى فى حال السكر فرحوا بذلك، فحذّر المؤمنين من العود لمثل ذلك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_043-18"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_043-s1","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"Grammar and language (qultu)","text":"“While you are intoxicated” ( wa-antum sukārā ) is a circumstantial clause ( ḥāl ). Sukārā is a plural of sakrān (“intoxicated”); alternative plural forms are sakārā , with initial fatḥa, and sakrā , with sukūn on the kāf. “Nor [being] junub ” is coordinated with the circumstantial phrase. Junub , a person in major ritual impurity, is unchanged for singular, dual and plural, masculine and feminine, because it behaves like a verbal noun ( maṣdar ) rather than an ordinary adjective. “Except those passing along a way” is an exception from all the possible circumstances. Ghāʾiṭ first meant a low place in the ground and came to mean what is expelled there by a person.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_043-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_043-s2","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"","text":"Do not rise for prayer in a state of drunkenness through wine, overpowering sleep, or profound heedlessness; wait until you know what you say in it and reflect on what you recite. Prayer without presence ( ḥuḍūr ) is empty, and for the elect, Ibn ʿAjība says, it is invalid [in the spiritual sense]. It is related that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf held a feast and invited several Companions when wine was still permitted. They ate and drank until drunk. When the time for sunset prayer came, one of them led the others but recited “I worship what you worship,” omitting the negation. The verse was revealed before wine was prohibited outright; the prohibition subsequently came in Sūrat al-Māʾida. Nor are you to approach the prayer in a state of janāba until you wash, except as travellers without water, as explained by the following words; such a traveller performs tayammum and prays despite remaining in major impurity. This, Ibn ʿAjība argues, indicates that tayammum does not itself remove the state of ritual impurity. Another interpretation takes “prayer” here to mean its places—the mosques—so a person in janāba may pass through a mosque without remaining there. This is attributed to al-Shāfiʿī. Abū Ḥanīfa does not permit passage except when water and the way to it are within the mosque. Mālik does not permit entry or passage at all, except entry after tayammum . Thus the instruction is not to approach prayer in major impurity until washing has been performed. “If you are ill”: ill such that water may cause injury, worsen an illness, delay recovery, or cannot be reached. “Or on a journey”: travelling and unable to find water. “Or one of you has come from the privy”: this includes the need to purify after urination or another cause of minor ritual impurity. “Or you have touched women”: according to Mālik's view, when your skin has met theirs with an intention of pleasure or when pleasure occurs. Al-Shāfiʿī holds that skin contact invalidates ablution absolutely, whether intended or not and whether pleasure occurs or not, even with a dead woman. In the view presented here as Abū Ḥanīfa's, intimate contact that produces an erection invalidates it. Ibn ʿAbbās, al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī and Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan are reported here as holding that mere touching does not invalidate ablution at all. The other causes of ritual impurity can be assimilated to touching in this legal discussion. The disjunctive aw (“or”) should therefore retain its ordinary force of differentiating situations. On this reading the verse expressly permits a healthy person at home to perform tayammum when no water is available. Mālik holds that he need not repeat the prayer; al-Shāfiʿī holds that he prays with tayammum and later repeats it; and Abū Ḥanīfa, as represented here, holds that he waits to pray until finding water. Making aw mean “and” would abandon the ordinary linguistic meaning without necessity. The subsequent clause restricts tayammum in these conditions to absence of sufficient water or inability to use it. Fa-tayammamū means “direct yourselves toward” clean ṣaʿīd : something pure that rises to the earth's surface and belongs to its substance. Ibn ʿAjība lists soil (which is preferable), snow, mud, stone, and clods of earth. [Textual note: “mud” renders خضخاض in this purification context; compare the Mālikī Mudawwana , I:148, on الطين الخضخاض. The Cairo editor instead glosses the word as a thin black tar used to coat mangy camels. That editorial gloss is distinguished here from the contextual body translation.] He excludes trees, grasses, gold and silver minerals, and substances resembling compounded drugs, such as alum, salt, sulphur, and ghāsūl [a cleansing plant], or similar materials. He reports Abū Ḥanīfa as permitting tayammum with everything of the earth and things joined to it, naming trees, kohl, orpiment, alum, lime, gypsum and minerals, but excluding sifted particles of gold, silver and lead. Al-Shāfiʿī permits only earth capable of supporting plant growth, interpreting “pure” in this way, and requires dust to adhere to the hand; the others do not make that condition. “Wipe your faces and your hands.” Mālik takes yad (“hand”) here to mean the palm, citing the extent of the hand at which a thief's hand is cut, and therefore regards wiping to the elbows as recommended ( sunna ). Al-Shāfiʿī regards it as obligatory, by analogy with ablution in water. “God is Pardoning, Forgiving”: this is why He has facilitated purification and given the dispensation of tayammum .","anchor":"en-q4_cont_043-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_043-s3","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"","text":"O believers, do not approach the prayer of the holy divine Presence ( ṣalāt al-ḥaḍra al-qudsiyya ) while drunk with love for this paltry world, until its intoxication has left you and you know what you are saying in your intimate address ( munājāt ) to its Creator. Neither approach in the janāba of heedlessness, except for passing thoughts that come only rarely, until you wash with the water of the Unseen ( māʾ al-ghayb ), through which the heart is purified and one who washes with it becomes absent from the vision of created beings ( al-akwān ). To this is related a poem that al-Shaʿrānī's Ṭabaqāt attributes to Ibn al-ʿArabī al-Ḥātimī, although others attribute it—and Ibn ʿAjība considers this more accurate—to al-Junayd: Wash for prayer with the water of the Unseen, if you possess a secret; otherwise perform tayammum with soil or rock. Set before you an imam whose imam you yourself once were, and pray the noon prayer at the beginning of the afternoon. Such is the prayer of those who know their Lord; if you are among them, sprinkle the land with the sea. That is, if you cannot attain the original purification—absence from created events—turn to outward, perceptible worship. Set the revealed law ( sharīʿa ), or one who bears it through prophetic spiritual training, before you as imam, though before you knew him he once sought you out. Join the noon ( ẓuhr ) of the revealed law to the afternoon ( ʿaṣr ) of spiritual reality ( ḥaqīqa ). This is the prayer of those who know God. If you are among them, pour the ocean of your inner reality over the land of your outward form, so that what lay hidden in the inward secrets appears in the visible outward world. The same meaning is indicated in the rest of the verse. “If you are ill” with the love of passions ( hawā ), “or travelling” in the haste of worldly occupation, or someone comes from the ghāʾiṭ of sensory entanglement ( ḥiss ), or you have touched the formal disciplines ( ʿulūm rasmiyya ) and their imagined forms have become impressed on your hearts, and you find no one to offer you the water of the Unseen—the pre-eternal wine—then aim at outward works: perhaps they will lead you to inward works. “God is Pardoning, Forgiving.” In the Ḥikam [of Ibn ʿAṭāʾ Allāh] it is asked: “How can a heart shine when the forms of created things are imprinted upon its mirror? How can it journey to God while bound in the chains of its appetites? How can it hope to enter God's Presence without having cleansed itself of the major impurity of its heedlessness? How can it hope to grasp the subtleties of the secrets without repenting of its slips?”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_043-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_043-s4","r":"q4_cont_043","title":"","text":"God warns of the hostility of those among the Jews who rejoice on hearing believers make mistakes comparable to the distortion of recitation just mentioned. The warning follows in the next passage.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_043-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_044","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection 4:44–45","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_044"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_044-1","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيباً مِنَ الْكِتابِ يَشْتَرُونَ الضَّلالَةَ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَضِلُّوا السَّبِيلَ (44) وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِأَعْدائِكُمْ وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَلِيًّا وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ نَصِيراً (45)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_044-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_044-2","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"قلت: دخلت الباء على الفاعل في (كفى بالله) ، لتضمنه معنى اكتف بالله وكيلاً.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_044-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_044-3","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أَلَمْ تَرَ يا محمد، أو يا مَن يسمع، ببصرك أو بقلبك، إِلَى حال الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيباً يسيرًا مِنَ علم الْكِتابِ أي: التوراة، وهم أحبار اليهود، يَشْتَرُونَ الضَّلالَةَ بالهدى، أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_044-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_044-4","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"يستبدلونها بها بعد تمكنهم منها عادة، وَيُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَضِلُّوا السَّبِيلَ أي: الطريق الموصلة إلى الحق، أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_044-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_044-5","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"يتمنون انحرافكم عنها، فإذا سمعوا عنكم ما يحرفكم عنها فرحوا واستبشروا، لأنهم انحرفوا عنها فحرفوا كتابهم وبدلوا، فتمنوا أن تكونوا مثلهم، فاحذروا ما يتوقع منكم أعداؤكم، فإن الله أعلم بهم منكم، فسيكفيكم الله أمرهم، فثقوا به وتوكلوا عليه، فكفى بالله وليًا وكفى بالله نصيرًا، فسيتولى أمركم وينصركم على من عاداكم. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_044-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_044-6","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"الإشارة: من شأن أهل الإنكار، ولا سيما من سلف له في أسلافه رياسة أو إظهار، إذا سمعوا بأهل النسبة وقع لهم شيء من الأكدار، فرحوا واستبشروا، وودوا لو حادوا كلهم عن سبيل الحق، والله مطلع على أسرارهم، وكاف بأسهم وشرهم، (وكفى بالله وليًا) لأوليائه ونصيرًا لأحبابه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_044-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_044-7","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"4:44–45 · Those who purchase error and God's protection","text":"ثم بيّنهم، أو ذكر حال فريق منهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_044-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_044-s1","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"","text":"The preposition bi- enters the grammatical subject in kafā bi-llāhi (“God suffices”), because the expression also implies “I deem God sufficient as my protector” ( aktafi bi-llāhi wakīlan ).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_044-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_044-s2","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"","text":"Have you not considered, Muḥammad—or anyone who hears—with bodily sight or inward vision the condition of those given a little of the knowledge of the Book, namely the Torah? They are the Jewish scholars whom Ibn ʿAjība has been discussing. They buy error in place of guidance, replacing guidance with error after they had ordinarily been capable of retaining guidance. They wish that you would stray from the road leading to the Real ( al-Ḥaqq ). When they hear of a happening that might divert you from that road they rejoice, for they themselves diverted from it, altered their Book, and substituted other things for its contents; they would like you to become like them. Take care, then, of what your enemies anticipate from you. God knows them better than you do, and He will suffice you against their designs. Trust Him and place your reliance on Him ( tawakkul ). “God suffices as protector, and God suffices as helper”: He will take charge of your affairs and grant you victory over your opponents. From God comes success ( tawfīq ).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_044-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_044-s3","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"","text":"Those who denounce the spiritual path ( ahl al-inkār )—especially if their forebears enjoyed positions of eminence or public recognition—are apt to rejoice when they hear that distress has befallen the people of authentic spiritual connection ( ahl al-nisba ). They would like every one of them to deviate from the path of the Real. But God sees what is secret in them and is sufficient against their might and harm. God suffices as a protector for His friends ( awliyāʾ ) and a helper for His beloved ones. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_044-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_044-s4","r":"q4_cont_044","title":"","text":"The passage next describes these opponents more specifically, or speaks of a party among them.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_044-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_046","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab 4:46","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_046"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-1","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"مِنَ الَّذِينَ هادُوا يُحَرِّفُونَ الْكَلِمَ عَنْ مَواضِعِهِ وَيَقُولُونَ سَمِعْنا وَعَصَيْنا وَاسْمَعْ غَيْرَ مُسْمَعٍ وَراعِنا لَيًّا بِأَلْسِنَتِهِمْ وَطَعْناً فِي الدِّينِ وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ قالُوا سَمِعْنا وَأَطَعْنا وَاسْمَعْ وَانْظُرْنا لَكانَ خَيْراً لَهُمْ وَأَقْوَمَ وَلكِنْ لَعَنَهُمُ اللَّهُ بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَلا يُؤْمِنُونَ إِلاَّ قَلِيلاً (46)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-2","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"قلت: (من الذين هادوا) : خبر عن محذوف، أي: منهم قوم يحرفون، أو بيان للذين قبله، أو متعلق بأعدائكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-3","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: من اليهود قوم تمردوا في الكفر وهم أحبارهم، يُحَرِّفُونَ الْكَلِمَ وهو التوراة عَنْ مَواضِعِهِ أي: يميلونه عن مواضعه التي وضعه الله فيها، بإزالة لفظه أو تأويله. وقال ابن عباس:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-4","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"(لا يقدر أحد أن يُحرّف كلام الله ولكن يفسرونه على غير وجهه) ، وَيَقُولُونَ لمن دعاهم إليه، وهو","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-5","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم: سَمِعْنا قولك، وَعَصَيْنا أمرك، وَاسْمَعْ منا غَيْرَ مُسْمَعٍ قولك، أي: لا نلتفت إليه، أو دعاء بالصمم: أي: لا سمعت، أو غير مسمع منا مكروهًا، نفاقًا، ويقولون له مكان انظرنا: راعِنا قاصدين بذلك الشتم والسخرية، من الرعونة، وقد كان الصحابة يخاطبون به الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- ومعناه:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-6","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"انظرنا. أو راعنا بقلبك، فوجد اليهود بها سبيلاً إلى الشتم، فنهاهم الله عن ذلك، وبقيت اليهود تقولها شتماً واستهزاءً لَيًّا بِأَلْسِنَتِهِمْ، أي: فَتلاً لها عن معناها، من الانتظار إلى ما قصدوا من رَميِه بالرُّعُونة، وَطَعْناً فِي الدِّينِ أي: استهزاء به، وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ قالُوا سَمِعْنا وَأَطَعْنا مكان سمعنا وعصينا، وَاسْمَعْ منا فقط، مكان: واسمع غير مسمع، وَانْظُرْنا مكان راعنا، لَكانَ قولهم ذلك خَيْراً لَهُمْ وَأَقْوَمَ وأعدل، وَلكِنْ لَعَنَهُمُ اللَّهُ أي: طردهم وأبعدهم بسبب كفرهم، فَلا يُؤْمِنُونَ إِلَّا إيمانًا قَلِيلًا لا يعبأ به وهو الإيمان بالبعض والكفر بالبعض من الآيات والرسل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-7","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"الإشارة: والله ما ربح من ربح، إلا بالأدب والتعظيم، وما خسر من خسر إلا من فقدهما. قال بعضهم:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-8","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"«اجعل عَمَلك مِلحًا، وأدبك دقيقا» . وآداب الظاهر عنوان آداب الباطن، ويظهر الأدب في حسن الخطاب، ورد الجواب، وفي حسن الأفعال، وظهور محاسن الخلال. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_046-9","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"4:46 · Distorting words and the necessity of adab","text":"ثم دعاهم إلى الإيمان بعد أن وسمهم بالعصيان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_046-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_046-s1","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"","text":"“From those who are Jews” ( min alladhīna hādū ) can be the predicate of an omitted subject—“among them are people who distort”—or can explain the persons described in the previous verse, or can depend on “your enemies.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_046-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_046-s2","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"","text":"Ibn ʿAjība says that among the Jews are people, especially their scholars, who rebel in unbelief and distort the words of the Torah from the places in which God established them. They do so either by removing their wording or by interpreting them inappropriately. He quotes Ibn ʿAbbās: “No one can alter God's words, but they explain them contrary to their true meaning.” When the Messenger, peace be upon him, calls them to the truth, they say, “We heard your statement and disobeyed your command.” They say, “Hear us, while not being made to hear”: either “We will pay no attention to what you say,” or as an imprecation for deafness, “May you not hear!” Alternatively it can outwardly mean “Hear, with nothing unpleasant said to you,” as a hypocritical appearance of courtesy. They also say rāʿinā instead of “look upon us” ( unẓurnā ), intending abuse and ridicule by associating the word with ruʿūna —foolishness or boorishness. The Companions had addressed the Messenger with rāʿinā in the sense “take notice of us,” or “attend to us with your heart.” The Jews then found in the expression an opportunity to insult him; God prohibited the Companions from using it, while those who mocked continued to use it as an insult. “Twisting their tongues” means turning the word away from the intended meaning of seeking attention to their own suggestion of foolishness; “attacking the religion” means making it an object of ridicule. Had they said “We heard and we obeyed,” instead of “We heard and we disobeyed,” simply “Hear” instead of “Hear, without being made to hear,” and “Look upon us” instead of rāʿinā , their speech would have been better, more just, and more upright. Instead, their unbelief caused them to be driven away from divine mercy. “They believe only a little” signifies a belief of no account: accepting some verses and messengers while rejecting others. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_046-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_046-s3","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"","text":"By God, no one who has attained success has done so except by adab —propriety, reverence, and giving others their due—and honouring what deserves honour. No one who has suffered spiritual loss has done so except through lacking these. Someone said: “Make your actions the salt and your adab the flour.” The outward manners ( ādāb al-ẓāhir ) reveal the inward manners ( ādāb al-bāṭin ). Adab appears in gracious speech, an appropriate answer, excellent actions, and the manifestation of beautiful character. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_046-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_046-s4","r":"q4_cont_046","title":"","text":"Having described their disobedience, God summons them to belief.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_046-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_047","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection","text":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection 4:47","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_047"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_047-1","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ آمِنُوا بِما نَزَّلْنا مُصَدِّقاً لِما مَعَكُمْ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ نَطْمِسَ وُجُوهاً فَنَرُدَّها عَلى أَدْبارِها أَوْ نَلْعَنَهُمْ كَما لَعَنَّا أَصْحابَ السَّبْتِ وَكانَ أَمْرُ اللَّهِ مَفْعُولاً (47)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_047-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_047-2","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ مِن اليهود آمِنُوا بِما نَزَّلْنا من القرآن مُصَدِّقاً لِما مَعَكُمْ من التوراة مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ نَطْمِسَ وُجُوهاً أي: نغير صُورها ونمحو تخطيط أشكالها، فلا تبقى عين ولا أنف ولا حاجب، فَنَرُدَّها عَلى هيئة أَدْبارِها من الأقفاء، أو ننكسها إلى ورائها في الدنيا، أَوْ نَلْعَنَهُمْ أي: نخزيهم بالمسخ، كَما لَعَنَّا أَصْحابَ السَّبْتِ، فمسخناهم قردة وخنازير، وَكانَ أَمْرُ اللَّهِ مَفْعُولًا، لا مرد له، ولعله كان مشروطاً بعدم إيمان بعضهم، أو يراد بطمس الوجوه ما يكسوها من الذلة والصغار. ويراد باللعن حقيقته، أي: نلعنهم على لسانك كما لُعنوا على لسان داوود وعيسى بن مريم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_047-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_047-3","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection","text":"وهذه الآية كانت سبب إسلام كعب الأحبار، سمعها من بعض الصحابة فأسلم في زمن عمر بن الخطاب رضي الله عنه. والمسخ جائز على هذه الأمة، كما وقع فى الأمم السابقة، بدليل ما في كتاب الأشربة من البخاري أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: «ليكوننَّ من أمَّتي أقوام يَستحلُّون الحِر والحَريرَ، والخمر والمعازف، ولينزلنَّ أقوام إلى جَنِب علَمِ، يَروحُ عليهم بسارحة لهم يأتيهم لحاجة، فيقولون: ارجع إلينا غَدًا، فيُبيَّتُهم الله، ويضع عليهم العَلَم، ويَمسَخُ آخرين قِردَة وخنازيرَ إلى يوم القيامة» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_047-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_047-4","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection","text":"الإشارة: حملة الشريعة يخاطبون بالإيمان بأهل الحقيقة، لأنها لبها وصفاؤها، فإن امتنعوا من الإيمان بها ومن الإذعان لأهلها، طمس الله وجوه قلوبهم، وملأها خوفًا وجزعًا وحبًا للدنيا، وردها على أدبارها، فلا تفهم أسرارَ الكتاب ولا تفقه إشارة الخطاب، فإن قصّروا عن حقوق الشريعة، وغيَّروا أحكامها مُسخوا قردة وخنازير. وفي نوادر الأصول بسنده إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: «تَكُونُ فِي أُمَّتي قزَعةٌ (١) ، فَيَصيرُ النَّاسُ إلى عُلَمَائِهِمْ، فإذا هُم قِردَةٌ وخَنَازِيرُ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_047-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_047-5","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection","text":"قال الترمذي الحكيم: فالمسخ: تغيير الخلقة عن جهتها، فإنما حل بهم المسخ لأنهم غيَّروا الحق عن جهته، وحرفوا الكلم عن مواضعه، فمسخوا عن أعين الخلق، وقلوبُهم عن رؤية الحق. فمسخ الله صورهم وبدَّل خِلقتهم، كما بدلوا الحق باطلاً. هـ. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_047-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_047-6","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"4:47 · Recognising revelation and the dangers of rejection","text":"ولمَّا دعاهم إلى الإيمان، أخبرهم أنهم إن داموا على الكفر لا مطمع لهم فى الغفران، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_047-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_047-s1","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"","text":"God addresses those of the Jews who possess the Scripture: believe in the Qurʾān We have sent down, which confirms the Torah you possess, before We efface faces, removing their outlines so that eyes, nose and brows no longer remain, and make them resemble the backs of heads. Or He could turn the faces round to the back in this world. Alternatively He could disgrace them by bodily transformation, as happened, according to the interpretation given here, to the people of the Sabbath who were changed into apes and swine. God's command cannot be repelled. Perhaps the warning was conditional on none of them coming to believe. Or “effacement of faces” can signify the humiliation and abasement that comes over them, and the curse can mean its literal sense: they would be cursed by the Prophet's tongue as others were cursed through David and Jesus son of Mary. Ibn ʿAjība relates that hearing this verse from certain Companions occasioned the conversion of Kaʿb al-Aḥbār in the time of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. He adds that bodily transformation remains possible within this community, citing a report in the Book of Drinks in al-Bukhārī. The Prophet says: “There will indeed be people of my community who regard as lawful illicit sexual intercourse, silk, wine and musical instruments. People will lodge beside a mountain, and someone will come to them in the evening with their grazing herd, asking for something he needs, and they will say, ‘Come back tomorrow.’ God will destroy them by night and bring the mountain down on them, and He will transform others into apes and swine until the Day of Resurrection.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_047-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_047-s2","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"","text":"Bearers of the outward religious law ( ḥamalat al-sharīʿa ) are called to acknowledge the people of inner reality ( ahl al-ḥaqīqa ), since ḥaqīqa is the kernel and purified essence of sharīʿa . If they refuse to believe in this inward knowledge and submit to its people, God effaces the faces of their hearts, fills them with fear, agitation and love of the world, and turns them backwards. They can no longer understand the secrets of the Book or comprehend the allusions ( ishārāt ) in revelation. If they also fail in the rights of the outward law and alter its rulings, they are transformed into apes and swine. Ibn ʿAjība cites Nawādir al-uṣūl , with its chain to the Prophet: “A small cloud [ qazaʿa ] will arise in my community, and the people will resort to their scholars, only to find them apes and swine.” [Textual note: the Cairo editor reports فزعة (with initial fāʾ , “a fright” or “an alarm”) in the source copies, but prints qazaʿa from al-Suyūṭī’s al-Jāmiʿ al-kabīr and Kanz al-ʿummāl , glossing it as a piece of cloud. The translation above preserves that printed reading.] He then quotes al-Ḥakīm al-Tirmidhī: Transformation ( maskh ) is a change of form away from its proper configuration. It befell them because they changed the truth from its proper position and distorted words away from their places. They became transformed in the sight of creatures, while their hearts were [transformed] away from beholding the Real. God changed their outward forms, just as they had changed the truth into falsehood. Here ends the citation. [Translator’s source note: The cited Nawādir al-uṣūl , II:196, principle 150, reads فمسخوا قلوب الخلق وأعينهم عن رؤية الحق : “they transformed people’s hearts and eyes, turning them away from seeing the truth.” The scholars are the agents of this inward distortion, which explains their ensuing outward transformation. Cairo’s wording, translated above, changes that construction. This comparison identifies a consequential source variant; it does not establish which wording Ibn ʿAjība wrote.] With God lies success.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_047-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_047-s3","r":"q4_cont_047","title":"","text":"After calling them to faith, God tells them that if they persist in unbelief they have no claim to forgiveness.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_047-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_048","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"4:48 · The unforgiven association and hidden shirk","text":"4:48 · The unforgiven association and hidden shirk 4:48","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_048"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_048-1","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"4:48 · The unforgiven association and hidden shirk","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَغْفِرُ أَنْ يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذلِكَ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ وَمَنْ يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدِ افْتَرى إِثْماً عَظِيماً (48)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_048-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_048-2","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"4:48 · The unforgiven association and hidden shirk","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَغْفِرُ أَنْ يُشْرَكَ بِهِ لأنه بتَّ الحكم على خلود عذابه، لأن الله تعالى غيور لا أحد أغير منه. كما في الحديث، ومن عادة الملوك إذا خرج أحدٌ من رعيته ونصر غيره لا يقبل منه إلا الرجوع أو الموت. ولا شفاعة تنفع فيه غير الرجوع عنه، وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذلِكَ الشرك لِمَنْ يَشاءُ من الكبائر والصغائر. تاب أم لا. فالعصاة إذا لم يتوبوا في مشيئة الله، وَمَنْ يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدِ افْتَرى إِثْماً عَظِيماً ارتكب ما تستحقر دونه الآثام. وهو إشارة إلى المعنى الفارق بينه وبين سائر الذنوب، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_048-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_048-3","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"4:48 · The unforgiven association and hidden shirk","text":"الإشارة: ولما رأت الصوفية أن الشرك لا يُغفر، ولا يُسمح في شيء منه، جليًا أو خفيًا، حققوا إخلاصهم، ودققوا معاملتهم مع ربهم، وفتشوا على قلوبهم، هل بقي فيها شيء من محبة غير مولاهم، أو خوفٌ من شيء دونه، وطهروا توحيدهم من نسبة التأثير لشيء من الكائنات، فتوجهوا إلى الله في إزالة ذلك عنهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_048-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_048-4","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"4:48 · The unforgiven association and hidden shirk","text":"قال بعضهم: شربتُ لبنًا فأصابني انتفاخ، فقلت ضرني ذلك اللبن، فلما كنت ذات يوم أتلو، وبلغت هذه الآية قلت: يا رب أنا لا أشرك بك شيئًا، فقال لي هاتفٌ: ولا يوم اللبن، فبادرت إلى التوبة. أ. هـ. بالمعنى. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_048-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_048-5","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"4:48 · The unforgiven association and hidden shirk","text":"ثم عاتبهم على تزكية أنفسهم بالدعوى، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_048-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_048-s1","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"","text":"God does not forgive the setting-up of partners ( shirk ) beside Him, for He has definitively ruled that its punishment abides. God is jealous in His majesty; none is more jealous than He, as the ḥadīth says. By the custom of rulers, if a subject leaves his own sovereign and supports another, only return or death is accepted; no intercession then benefits him unless he abandons his disloyalty. But God forgives whatever is below shirk —grave as well as lesser sins—to whomsoever He wills, whether the sinner has repented or not. Thus disobedient believers who do not repent stand within God's will. “Whoever associates a partner with God has fabricated a tremendous sin”: such a person has committed an offence before which other sins seem small. This points to the essential distinction between shirk and other sins. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_048-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_048-s2","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"","text":"The Sufis saw that no amount of shirk , whether manifest ( jalī ) or hidden ( khafī ), could be excused [in the strict spiritual demand for perfect sincerity]. So they sought to make their sincerity ( ikhlāṣ ) complete and refined their dealings with their Lord. They searched their own hearts to discover whether any love remained for other than their Master or any fear of something below Him. They purified their affirmation of unity ( tawḥīd ) from attributing efficacy ( taʾthīr ) to any created being, turning to God to remove this from them. Someone related: “I drank milk and developed a swelling, so I said, ‘That milk harmed me.’ One day, while reciting, I came upon this verse and said, ‘My Lord, I associate nothing with You.’ Then an unseen caller said to me, ‘Not even on the day of the milk?’ I hastened to repent.” The story is reported here by sense rather than verbatim ( bi-l-maʿnā ). God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_048-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_048-s3","r":"q4_cont_048","title":"","text":"God next reproaches them for claiming purity on their own behalf.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_048-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_049","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs","text":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs 4:49–50","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_049"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_049-1","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ يُزَكُّونَ أَنْفُسَهُمْ بَلِ اللَّهُ يُزَكِّي مَنْ يَشاءُ وَلا يُظْلَمُونَ فَتِيلاً (49) انْظُرْ كَيْفَ يَفْتَرُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ وَكَفى بِهِ إِثْماً مُبِيناً (50)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_049-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_049-2","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أَلَمْ تَرَ يا محمد إِلَى الَّذِينَ يُزَكُّونَ أَنْفُسَهُمْ، وهم اليهود، قالوا: نَحنُ أبنَاءُ اللهِ وَأحبَّاؤُه، وقيل: طائفة منهم، أتَوا بأطفَالِهِم إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقالوا: هَل عَلَى هؤُلآءِ ذَنبٌ؟ قال: «لآ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_049-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_049-3","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs","text":"قَالوُا: واللهِ مَا نَحنُ إلا كَهَيئَتِهِم، مَا عَمِلنَا بالنّهَارِ يُكَفَّر عَنَّا باللَّيلِ، وما عملنا باللَّيلِ يُكَفَّر عَنَّا بالنّهَارِ، فنزلت فيهم الآية. وفي معناهم: من زكى نفسه وأثنى عليها قبل معرفتها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_049-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_049-4","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs","text":"بَلِ اللَّهُ يُزَكِّي مَنْ يَشاءُ لأنه العالم بخفيات النفوس وكمائنها، وما انطوت عليه من قبيح أو حسن، فيزكي من يستحق التزكية، ويفضح المُدَّعِين، وَلا يُظْلَمُونَ فَتِيلًا، وهو الخيط الذي في شق النواة، يضرب مثلاً لحقارة الشيء، فإن الله لا يظلم مثقال ذرة، انْظُرْ كَيْفَ يَفْتَرُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ الْكَذِبَ في زعمهم أنهم أبناء الله، أو أنهم مغفور لهم، وَكَفى بِهِ أي: بالافتراء، إِثْماً مُبِيناً أي: ظاهرًا لا يخفى على أحد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_049-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_049-5","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs","text":"الإشارة: قال بعض الصوفية: للنفس من النقائص ما لله من الكمالات، فلا ينبغي للعبد أن يُزكي نفسه، ولو بلغ فيها من التطهير ما بلغ، ولا يرضى عنها ولو عملت من الأعمال ما عملت. قال أبو سليمان الداراني: لي أربعون سنة وأنا مُتَّهِمٌ لنفسي. وفي الحِكَم: «أصل كل معصيةٍ وغفلةٍ وشهوةٍ: الرضا عن النفس، وأصلُ كل طاعةٍ ويقظةٍ وعفةٍ: عدمُ الرضا منك عنها، ولأن تصحب جاهلاً لا يرضى عن نفسه خير من أن تصحب عالماً يرضى عن نفسه فأيُّ علمٍ لعالمٍ يرضى عن نفسه؟! وأيّ جهل لجاهل لا يرضى عن نفسه؟!» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_049-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_049-6","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"4:49–50 · Self-praise and the discipline of distrust of the nafs","text":"ثم وبخهم على سجودهم للأصنام. وشهادتهم لأهل الكفر بأنهم أهدى من أهل الإسلام، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_049-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_049-s1","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"","text":"God addresses Muḥammad concerning those who praise themselves as pure. Ibn ʿAjība identifies them as Jews who said, “We are God's children and His beloved.” It is also related that a group of them came to the Messenger with their children and asked, “Do these have any sin?” “No,” he answered. They then said, “By God, we are just like them: what we do in the daytime is expiated at night, and what we do at night is expiated by day.” The verse was said to have been revealed about them. Its sense extends to anyone who praises or declares the lower soul pure before truly knowing it. “Rather, God purifies whom He wills,” for He alone knows the concealed places and hidden stores of souls, and what ugly or beautiful dispositions they contain. He purifies those deserving purification and exposes pretenders. “They are not wronged by a fatīl ”: the fatīl is the fine thread in the cleft of a date-stone, proverbial for something negligible. God does not wrong anyone by an atom's weight. “Look how they invent a lie against God”: by claiming to be God's children or to have guaranteed forgiveness. Such fabrication is sufficient as a plain, manifest sin.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_049-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_049-s2","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"","text":"A Sufi said that the lower soul ( nafs ) has as many deficiencies as God has perfections. A servant therefore must not proclaim the purity of the nafs , however far its purification has progressed, nor be satisfied with it, however many actions it has performed. Abū Sulaymān al-Dārānī said: “For forty years I have held my own nafs suspect.” In the Ḥikam it is said: “The root of every act of disobedience, every heedlessness and every desire is being satisfied with oneself. The root of every obedience, wakefulness and chastity is not being satisfied with oneself. It is better that you accompany an ignorant person dissatisfied with himself than a scholar satisfied with himself. What knowledge does a scholar who is satisfied with himself possess? And what ignorance does an ignorant person dissatisfied with himself possess?”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_049-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_049-s3","r":"q4_cont_049","title":"","text":"God rebukes those who prostrated before idols and testified that people of unbelief were better guided than the people of Islam.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_049-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_051","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis 4:51–52","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_051"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-1","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيباً مِنَ الْكِتابِ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْجِبْتِ وَالطَّاغُوتِ وَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا هؤُلاءِ أَهْدى مِنَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا سَبِيلاً (51) أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ لَعَنَهُمُ اللَّهُ وَمَنْ يَلْعَنِ اللَّهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُ نَصِيراً (52)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-2","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"قلت: الجبت في الأصل: اسم صنم، فاستعمل في كل ما عُبد من دون الله، والطاغوت: كل باطل من معبود أو غيره، أو الجبت: السحر، والطاغوت: الساحر، وبالجملة: هو كل ما عُبد أو أطيع من دون الله، وقال الجوهري:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-3","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"الجبت: اسم لكل صنم ولكل عاصٍ ولكل ساحر وكل مُضِلّ، والطاغوت: الشيطان، وأصله: طغيوت، فعلوت، من الطغيان، ثم قلب فصار طيَغوت، ثم قلبت الياء ألفًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-4","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا نَصِيباً مِنَ علم الْكِتابِ، وهم أحبار اليهود يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْجِبْتِ وَالطَّاغُوتِ يقرون بصحة عبادتهما، وَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا هؤُلاءِ الكفرة أَهْدى مِنَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا طريقًا، نزلت في اليهود- لعنهم الله-: كانوا يقولون: إن عبادة الأصنام أرضى عند الله مما يدعو إليه محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم، وقيل: في حُيي بن أخطب وكعب بن الأشرف، خرجا في سبعين راكبًا إلى مكة يُحالفون قريشًا على محاربة رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بعد وقعة أُحد، وينقضون العهد الذي كان بينهم وبين رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فنزل كَعبُ على أبي سفيان، فأحسن مثواه، ونزلت اليهود في دور قريش. فقال أهل مكة: أنتم أهل كتاب، ومحمدٌ صاحب كتاب، ولا نأمن أن يكون هذا مكيدة منكم، فإن أردتم أن نخرج معكم فاسجدوا لهذين الصنمين، وآمنوا بهما، ففعلوا، فذلك قوله تعالى: يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْجِبْتِ وَالطَّاغُوتِ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-5","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"ثم قال أبو سفيان لكعب: إنك امرؤ تقرأ الكتاب وتعلم، ونحن أميون لا نعلم، فأيُّنا أهدى سبيلاً وأقرب إلى الحق، نحن أو محمد؟ قال كعب: اعرضوا عليَّ دينَكم، فقال أبو سفيان: نحن ننحر للحجيج الكومَاءَ- أي: العظيمة- من النوق- ونسقي الماء، ونَقري الضيف، ونفك العاني، ونصل الرحم، ونعمر بيت ربنا، ونطوف به، ونحن أهل الحرم، ومحمدٌ فارقَ دينَ آبائه، وقطع الرحم وفارق الحرم، فقال كعب: أنتم والله أهدى سبيلاً. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-6","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ لَعَنَهُمُ اللَّهُ وأبعدهم وأسحقهم، وَمَنْ يَلْعَنِ اللَّهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُ نَصِيراً ينصره من عذاب الله. فقد قُتل هؤلاء كلهم شر قتلة، وذهبوا إلى الهاوية. عائذاً بالله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-7","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"الإشارة: قال الورتجبي: وبَّخ الله تعالى أهل ظاهر العلم الذين اختاروا الرياسة، وأنكروا على أهل الولاية، وآثروا صحبة المخالفين، يقبلون هواجس نفَوسهم التي هي الجبت، ويخطون على آثار الطاغوت، التي هي إبليس. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-8","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"قلت: وينسحب التوبيخ على من فضّل أهل الظاهر على أهل الباطن، وفضَّل العلماء على الأولياء، ويقولون:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-9","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"هم أهدى منهم سبيلاً. هيهات! بينهم من البَون ما بين السماء والأرض.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-10","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"والكلام إنما هو في التفضيل بين العارفين بالله، الذين جمعوا بين الفناء والبقاء، وبين العلماء والأتقياء. وأما العُبَّاد والزهاد والصالحون فلا شك أن العلماء الأتقياء أفضل منهم، وإليهم أشار صلّى الله عليه وسلم بقوله: «فَضلُ العَالِمِ على العابِد كَفَضِلِي عَلَى أدناكُم» . وكذلك الأحاديث التي وردت في تفضيل العلماء. وأما العارفون بالله فهم أعظم العلماء، لأن علمهم متعلق بذات الله كشفًا وذوقًا، وعلماء الظاهر علمهم متعلق بأحكام الله. مفرقُون عن الله، بل هم أشد حجابًا من غيرهم عن الله. قال بعض الأولياء: أشد الناس حجابًا عن الله: العلماء ثم العباد ثم الزهاد. هـ. لأن حلاوة ما هم فيه تمنعهم عن الانتقال عنه، وقد تقدم الكلام عند قوله: كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ (١) بأبلغ من هذا. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_051-11","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"4:51–52 · Jibt, ṭāghūt, and the contrast between scholarship and gnosis","text":"ثم ردّ الحق تعالى على اليهود، حيث ادعوا أن الملك سيصير إليهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_051-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_051-s1","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"Lexical discussion (qultu)","text":"Jibt originally designated an idol; it was then applied to everything worshipped apart from God. Ṭāghūt names any false object of worship or other false authority. Alternatively, jibt is sorcery and ṭāghūt a sorcerer. Generally it means whatever is worshipped or obeyed in defiance of God. Al-Jawharī says that jibt is a name for any idol, transgressor, sorcerer, or one who misguides. Ṭāghūt is Satan; in its derivation the original ṭaghyūt is built on the faʿalūt pattern from ṭughyān (transgression), undergoes transposition to ṭayghūt , and then changes the yāʾ into an alif .","anchor":"en-q4_cont_051-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_051-s2","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"","text":"“Have you not considered those granted a portion of the knowledge of the Book”—that is, the scholars of the Jews—“who believe in jibt and ṭāghūt ”: they concede the validity of worshipping them. They tell unbelievers that they are more rightly guided than those who believe. Ibn ʿAjība reports that the verse was revealed about Jews who preferred idol worship to the religion proclaimed by Muḥammad. Another account names Ḥuyayy ibn Akhṭab and Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf. After Uḥud they travelled to Mecca with seventy riders, intending an alliance with Quraysh against the Messenger and breaking their earlier agreement with him. Kaʿb stayed with Abū Sufyān, who hosted him generously, and the other Jews stayed in Quraysh's houses. The Meccans said: “You are people of Scripture, and Muḥammad is a man of Scripture. We cannot know that you are not deceiving us. If you wish us to march with you, prostrate yourselves to these two idols and acknowledge them.” They did so, says the report, and this is what is meant by “They believe in jibt and ṭāghūt .” Abū Sufyān then said to Kaʿb: “You read the Scripture and possess knowledge; we are unlettered. Which of us is nearer the truth and better guided: ourselves or Muḥammad?” Kaʿb asked them to describe their religion. Abū Sufyān replied: “We slaughter large, well-fleshed camels for the pilgrims, supply water, honour guests, release captives, maintain kinship bonds, tend the House of our Lord, and circumambulate it; we are the people of the Sacred Precinct. Muḥammad has departed from his ancestors' religion, severed ties of kinship, and departed from the Precinct.” Kaʿb is reported to have answered: “By God, you are better guided.” Thus ends the narrative. “These are the ones whom God has cursed”: God has removed them far from His mercy. “Whoever God curses will have no helper” against His punishment. Ibn ʿAjība adds that these persons died violent deaths and descended into perdition. He seeks refuge in God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_051-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_051-s3","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"","text":"Al-Wartajbī writes that God reproached people whose knowledge remains merely outward, who chose worldly leadership, rejected the people of sanctity ( ahl al-wilāya ), preferred the fellowship of their opponents, and followed the impulses of their lower souls—their jibt —and the tracks of their ṭāghūt , Satan. Here ends his statement. Ibn ʿAjība adds that the reproach extends to those who prefer the outward people ( ahl al-ẓāhir ) to the inward people ( ahl al-bāṭin ) and rank scholars above the friends of God ( awliyāʾ ), saying “These are better guided.” Far from it, he exclaims: the distance between them is like that between earth and heaven. He carefully specifies that the comparison is between knowers of God ( ʿārifūn bi-llāh ) who unite effacement ( fanāʾ ) and subsistence ( baqāʾ ), on the one side, and scholars and the God-fearing on the other. As for ordinary worshippers, ascetics and righteous people, he has no doubt that God-fearing scholars are superior to them. He cites the prophetic saying: “The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is as my superiority over the least of you,” together with other reports favouring the learned. Those who know God, however, are the greatest scholars, because their knowledge concerns God's very Essence through unveiling ( kashf ) and tasting ( dhawq ), whereas the scholars of the outward disciplines know God's rulings. Their attention is dispersed away from God ( mufarraqūn ʿan Allāh ); indeed, he says, they are more veiled from God than others. A saintly person reportedly said: “The people most veiled from God are first the scholars, then the worshippers, then the ascetics,” because delight in their present achievements prevents them from moving beyond them. Ibn ʿAjība refers readers to his earlier discussion of “You were the best community brought forth for humankind” [Q 3:110]. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_051-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_051-s4","r":"q4_cont_051","title":"","text":"The next verse replies to the claim that political rule will pass to these opponents.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_051-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_053","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self","text":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self 4:53","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_053"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_053-1","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self","text":"أَمْ لَهُمْ نَصِيبٌ مِنَ الْمُلْكِ فَإِذاً لا يُؤْتُونَ النَّاسَ نَقِيراً (53)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_053-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_053-2","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self","text":"قلت: «أم» : منقطعة، بمعنى بل، والهمزة للإنكار، وهو إنكار وجحدٌ لما زعمت اليهود من أنَّ المُلكَ سيصيرُ لهم، و (إذًا) إن فُصل بينها وبين المضارع ب- «لا» ففيها الإهمال والإعمال، وقد قرئ: (وإذًا لا يلبثوا) ، والنقير:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_053-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_053-3","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self","text":"النقرة التي في ظهر النواة، وهو هنا كناية عن نهاية بخلهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_053-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_053-4","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله منكرا على اليهود: أيحصل لهم نَصِيبٌ مِنَ الْمُلْكِ والرياسة؟ هيهات، لا يكون هذا أبدًا، فكيف يكون لهم الملك وهم أبخل الناس؟. فإذا أُوتوا شيئًا من الملك لا يُعطون الناس نقيرًا، فما بالك بأكثر، والملك والنصر لا يكونان إلا لأجل الكرم والجود والشجاعة، وإصابة الرأي وحسن التدبير، وهم بعداء من هذه المكارم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_053-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_053-5","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self","text":"الإشارة: لا يُمكن اللهُ من العز والنصر والتصرف الظاهر أو الباطن إلا أهل السخاء والجود، فمن جاد بمالِهِ حتى لا يبالي كم أعطى ولا لمن أعطى، مكّنه الله من العز والتصرف الحسي، ومن جاد بنفسه وجاهه، وبذلهما في مرضاة ربه، مكّنه الله من العز والنصر والتصرف المعنوي يتصرف بهمته في الوجود بأسره، من عرشه إلى فرشه، ويدوم عزه ونصره إلى أبد الأبد. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_053-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_053-6","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"4:53 · Sovereignty, stinginess, and the gifts of the self","text":"ولمّا كان الحسد والبخل رذيلتين متناهيتين فى الذم وصفهم الحق- تعالى- أيضا به (١) ، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_053-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_053-s1","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"","text":"Am is disconnected ( munqaṭiʿa ), equivalent to “rather,” with the interrogative hamza expressing rejection. It denies the claim—attributed here to Jews—that sovereignty will become theirs. When idhan is separated from a present-tense verb by lā , both operation and non-operation of the particle are allowed; the reading wa-idhan lā yalbathū is cited by way of comparison. A naqīr is the little pit on the back of a date-stone; it serves here as an image of the smallest possible gift, exposing extreme miserliness.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_053-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_053-s2","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"","text":"Ibn ʿAjība paraphrases the divine reproach: Could they obtain any part of dominion or public authority? Far from it! Such a thing will never happen, he writes in this polemical context. How, he asks, can power be theirs when they are so miserly? Even given a share of sovereignty, they would not bestow a naqīr upon other people, let alone something greater. In Ibn ʿAjība's moral argument, political authority and victory depend on generosity, open-handedness, courage, sound judgment and good government: he portrays the people criticized in the verse as lacking these virtues.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_053-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_053-s3","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"","text":"God grants strength, victory and the power to act ( taṣarruf ), outwardly or inwardly, only to the generous. One who gives freely of his wealth without being concerned about how much he gives or to whom is enabled to enjoy outward honour and effective action ( taṣarruf ḥissī ). One who gives away his own self and standing ( nafs and jāh ) and expends both in pursuit of his Lord's good pleasure is granted spiritual dignity, victory and inward effective action ( taṣarruf maʿnawī ): his spiritual aspiration ( himma ) acts throughout existence, from the Throne to the earth beneath it. His honour and victory endure perpetually. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_053-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_053-s4","r":"q4_cont_053","title":"","text":"As envy and miserliness are two especially blameworthy vices, the exposition proceeds to reproach envy as well.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_053-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_054","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment 4:54–57","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_054"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-1","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"أَمْ يَحْسُدُونَ النَّاسَ عَلى ما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ فَقَدْ آتَيْنا آلَ إِبْراهِيمَ الْكِتابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَآتَيْناهُمْ مُلْكاً عَظِيماً (54) فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ آمَنَ بِهِ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ صَدَّ عَنْهُ وَكَفى بِجَهَنَّمَ سَعِيراً (55) إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآياتِنا سَوْفَ نُصْلِيهِمْ ناراً كُلَّما نَضِجَتْ جُلُودُهُمْ بَدَّلْناهُمْ جُلُوداً غَيْرَها لِيَذُوقُوا الْعَذابَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَزِيزاً حَكِيماً (56) وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها أَبَداً لَهُمْ فِيها أَزْواجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ وَنُدْخِلُهُمْ ظِلاًّ ظَلِيلاً (57)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-2","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"قلت: (أم) بمعنى بل، و (سعيرًا) تمييز.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-3","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله توبيخًا لليهود على الحسد: أَمْ يَحْسُدُونَ النَّاسَ، أي: العرب حيث انتقلت النبوة إليهم، وقد كانت في أسلافهم، عَلى ما آتاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ، وهو ظهور النبوة فيهم، أو رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم لأنه اجتمع فيه ما افترق في سائر الناس، حسدوه على ما آتاه الله من فضله، من النبوة وغيرها، وقالوا- لعنهم الله-: ماله همٌّ إلا النساء، ولو كان نبيًا لشغله أمر النبوة عن النساء.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-4","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"فكَّذبهم الله- تعالى- وردَّ عليهم بقوله: فَقَدْ آتَيْنا آلَ إِبْراهِيمَ وهم: يوسف وداود وسليمان، الْكِتابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ أي: النبوّة، وَآتَيْناهُمْ مُلْكاً عَظِيماً، فقد اجتمع لداود عليه السلام مائة امرأة. ولسليمان- عليه السلام- ألف امرأة: ثلاثمائة مهيرة، - أي بالمهر- وسبعمائة سرية، فقال لهم- عليه الصلاة والسلام- حين نزلت الآية: ألف امرأة عند رجل، ومائة امرأة عند آخر، أكثر من تسع نسوة، فسكتوا (٢) .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-5","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"فَمِنْهُمْ أي: اليهود، مَنْ آمَنَ بِهِ أي: بمحمد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- كعبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه، وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ صَدَّ عَنْهُ أي: أعرض عنه، أو: من آل إبراهيم من آمن بإبراهيم، ومنهم من صدّ عنه، ولم يكن في ذلك توهين لقدر إبراهيم، فكذلك لا يُوهن كفرُ هؤلاء أمرَك، أو: من أسلافهم من آمن بما أُوتي آل إبراهيم من الكتاب والحكمة والمُلك، ومنهم مَن صدّ عنه، كما فعلوا مع سليمان وغيره. وَكَفى بِجَهَنَّمَ سَعِيراً لمن كفر بما جاء به أحد من الرسل، أي: فإن لم يُعاجَلوا بالعقوبة فقد كفاهم ما أعد لهم من سعير جهنم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-6","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"ثم بيَّن مآل مَن كفر، فقال: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآياتِنا المنزلة على رسلنا، أو الدالة على وحدانيتنا، سَوْفَ نُصْلِيهِمْ نارًا أي: نحرقهم بها ونشويهم، كُلَّما نَضِجَتْ جُلُودُهُمْ أي: لانت واحترقت بَدَّلْناهُمْ جُلُوداً غَيْرَها، قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «تُبدَّلُ في ساعةٍ مائةَ مَرَّة» . وقال الحسن: (تأكلهم النارُ في كل يوم سبعين ألف مرة، كلما أكلتهم وأنضجتهم قيل لهم: عودوا فيعودون كما كانوا) . وقال مجاهد: (ما بين جلده ولحمه دود، لها جلبة- أي حركة- وهرير كجلبة حمر الوحش) . رَوى أبو هريرة رضي الله عنه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قال: «غلظٌ جِلدِ الكَافِرِ اثنَانٍ وأربعَونَ ذرَاعًا، وضِرسه مِثلُ أحُد» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-7","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"وإنما بدلت جلودهم لِيَذُوقُوا ألم الْعَذابَ، أي: يدوم لهم ذلك بخلق جلد آخر مكانه، والعذاب في الحقيقة للنفس العاصية لا لآلة إدراكها، فلا محذور، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَزِيزاً لا يمتنع عليه ما يريد، حَكِيماً يعاقب على قدر حكمته.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-8","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"ثم ذكر مقابل هؤلاء فقال: وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها أَبَداً لَهُمْ فِيها أَزْواجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ مما يستقذر وَنُدْخِلُهُمْ ظِلًّا ظَلِيلًا أي: دائمًا لا تنسخه شمس، ولا يصحبه برد. قدَّم وعيد الكفار على وعد المؤمنين، لأن الكلام فيهم، وذكر المؤمنين بالعرض. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-9","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"الإشارة: الحسد خلق مذموم، لا يتطهر منه إلا الصديقون، وكل من بقي فيه بقية من الحسد لا يشم رائحة المعرفة، إذ لو عرف الله لم يجد من يحسد، وقد قيل: الحسود لا يسود. وفي الحديث عنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم أنه قال: «الحَسدُ يأكُلُ الحسنَاتِ كما تأكلُ النَّارُ الحَطَبَ» . وقال سفيان: (بلغني إنَّ الله تبارك وتعالى يقول: الحاسدُ عدو نعمتي، غيرُ راضٍ بقسمتي التي قسمت بين عبادي) . وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-10","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"ألاَ قُل لمَن كانَ لي حَاسِدًا ... أتدري على مَن أسَأتَ الأدَب","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-11","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"أسَأتَ على اللهِ في فِعلِه ... إذا أنتَ لم تَرضَ لي مَا وَهَب","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-12","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"جَزَاؤُكَ منه الزيادةُ لي ... وألاَّ تَنَالَ الذِي تَطَّلِب","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-13","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"وقال آخر:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-14","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"إن تحسُدُوني فإني غيرُ لائمكم ... قَبَلى من الناسِ أهل الفضلِ قّد حُسِدُوا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-15","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"فَدَامَ لي وَلَهُم ما كَانَ بي وبهم ... وماتَ أكثَرُنا غيظًا بما يَجِدُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-16","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"ثم إن الحسود لا تزول عداواته، ولا تنفع مداواته، وهو ظالم يشتكي كأنه مظلوم. ولقد صدق القائل:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-17","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"كلُ العَدَاوةِ قد تُرجىَ إزالتُها ... إلا عداوة مَن عَادَاكَ مِن حَسَدٍ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-18","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"وقال حكيم الشعراء:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-19","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"وأظلمُ خَلقِ اللهِ مَن بَاتَ حَاسِدًا ... لِمَن بَاتَ في نَعمَائِه يَتَقَلَّبُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-20","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"وقال آخر:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-21","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"إني لأرحمُ حاسِدِيَّ لفرطِ ما ... ضَمَّت صُدُوُرُهُم مِن الأوغَارِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-22","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"نَظَرُوا صنيعَ اللهِ فيّ فَعُيُونهُم ... في جَنَّةٍ وقَلوبُهُم في نارِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-23","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"قال بعض الحكماء: (الحاسدُ يضرُّ نفسه ثلاث مضرات: إحداها: اكتساب الذنوب لأن الحسد حرام. الثانية:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-24","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"سوء الأدب مع الله- تعالى- فإنَّ حقيقة الحسد: كراهية إنعام الله على غيره، واعتراض على الله في فعله. الثالثة:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-25","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"تألم قلبه وكثرة همه وغمه) . عافانا الله من ذلك كله، فالحاسد لا ينفك عن نار الحجاب وغم الحساب، والمتطهر منه يدخل جنة الرضى والتسليم في جوار الحبيب، وهو محل الراحة والأمن في الدارين، وهو الظل الظليل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_054-26","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"4:54–57 · Envy, divine favour, fire, and the shelter of contentment","text":"ولما كان حفظ نظام الدين لا يقوم إلا بالجهاد، ولا ينتظم الجهاد إلا بنصب الإمام، تكلم الحق- جل جلاله- على ما يتعلق بالأمراء، ثم بعد ذلك يتكلم على الجهاد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_054-26"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_054-s1","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"","text":"The particle am here has the force of “rather,” and saʿīran (“blazing fire”) is a specification ( tamyīz ).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_054-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_054-s2","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"","text":"In rebuking envy, God says: Do they envy “people”—that is, the Arabs, to whom prophethood has now come after being among the ancestors of those addressed—for the bounty He has given them? The bounty is the manifestation of prophethood among them. Or “people” can mean the Messenger himself, peace be upon him, in whom have been gathered qualities that are separately distributed among other people. According to the story Ibn ʿAjība transmits, his opponents envied him for the prophethood and other favours God had bestowed and said, disparagingly: “He has no concern but women; if he were a prophet, the labour of prophethood would occupy him rather than women.” God contradicts them: “We gave the House of Abraham”—Ibn ʿAjība names Joseph, David and Solomon—“the Book and wisdom,” which he here explains as prophethood, “and bestowed upon them a mighty dominion.” He then relates numerical claims that David had one hundred women, and Solomon one thousand: three hundred wives married with a dower ( mahīra ) and seven hundred concubines. He reports the Prophet as answering those critics, when the verse descended, by comparing these numbers with his nine wives, after which they fell silent. [Translator’s note: The numerical claims belong to reports cited in the commentator's argument; their historical accuracy is unestablished.] “Among them”—meaning the Jews—“are those who believe in him,” namely Muḥammad, such as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his companions, and others who turn away from him. Alternatively, the pronouns concern the House of Abraham: some believed in Abraham, others rejected him; just as this did not diminish Abraham's standing, their rejection does not diminish your mission. A third interpretation contrasts earlier people who accepted the Book, wisdom and kingship given to Abraham's family with others who rejected them, as they had rejected Solomon and others. “Hell is sufficient as a blazing fire” for those who reject what any messenger brings. If their punishment is not hastened in the present world, the fire reserved for them is sufficient. God then describes the end of those who reject His revealed signs or the signs of His unity. “We shall make them enter fire”: that is, burn and roast them. “Whenever their skins are consumed,” softened and burned, “We replace them with other skins.” Ibn ʿAjība quotes a saying attributed to the Prophet that they are changed a hundred times in an hour. Al-Ḥasan is cited as saying that the fire consumes them seventy thousand times a day; every time it consumes and cooks them, they are told to return and return as they were. Mujāhid is cited as describing worms between skin and flesh, in commotion and growling like wild asses. From Abū Hurayra Ibn ʿAjība transmits the prophetic report: “The thickness of an unbeliever's skin will be forty-two cubits, and his molar tooth like Uḥud.” The replacement of skins makes the pain endure, by creating other skin in the place of what was consumed. The actual subject of punishment, he observes, is the disobedient soul and not the instrument through which it perceives; therefore he sees no difficulty in this replacement. God is “Mighty”: none can prevent Him from acting as He wills; and “Wise”: He punishes in accordance with His wisdom. God then contrasts the destiny of the believers. Those who believe and act rightly enter gardens with flowing rivers and abide there for ever; their spouses are purified of everything repellent; and they enjoy a shade that is perpetual, never removed by sunshine and never accompanied by cold. The warning to unbelievers comes first because they are the immediate subject of the discourse, while the believers are mentioned by contrast. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_054-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_054-s3","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"","text":"Envy ( ḥasad ) is a blameworthy disposition from which only the most truthful ( ṣiddīqūn ) become completely purified. Anyone in whom a trace of envy remains cannot smell the fragrance of true knowing ( maʿrifa ). Had the person known God, there would be no object of envy left to him. The saying goes: “The envious person never rises to leadership” ( al-ḥasūd lā yasūd ). Ibn ʿAjība quotes as a prophetic saying: “Envy consumes good deeds as fire consumes firewood.” Sufyān also reports that it reached him that God says: “The envious person is an enemy of My blessing, dissatisfied with the portion I have divided among My servants.” Poets have said: Say to one who envies me: Do you know against whom you have offended in courtesy? You have offended against God in His act, since you disapprove of what He has given me. Your recompense from Him is an increase for me, and that you will not obtain what you seek. And another: If you envy me, I do not blame you: before my time, those of excellence were envied. May what is in me and in them remain with each of us; and may the greater number of us die from the anger they feel. [Translator’s note: The poet wishes that his merit and their envy should persist, as al-Fārisī explains in his commentary on the Ḥamāsa , p. 224. Al-Marzūqī, Sharḥ Dīwān al-Ḥamāsa , I:294, takes “the greater number of us” as the enviers, who are many against one. Another grammatical construal of aktharunā ghayẓan is “the one of us most enraged.” The wish and the parties’ different conditions are clear; the latter construction is not treated here as uniquely determined.] Enmity born from envy cannot be removed and is not benefited by treatment: the envious person oppresses another yet complains as though oppressed. A poet rightly said: Every hostility may admit the hope of removal, except the hostility of one who opposes you out of envy. And a master of poets said: The most unjust of God's creatures is one who lies awake in envy of a person who lies surrounded by His blessings. And another: I pity my enviers for all the rancour their breasts contain. They saw God's handiwork in me: their eyes were in a garden, while their hearts were in a fire. A wise person said that the envious inflicts three kinds of injury on himself. First, he accumulates sins, for envy is forbidden. Second, he violates adab toward God, since envy is essentially dislike of God's giving blessings to someone else and an objection to the divine act. Third, he suffers pain of heart, recurring distress and sorrow. May God protect us from all this. The envious person remains in the fire of veiling ( nār al-ḥijāb ) and the anguish of accounting ( ghamm al-ḥisāb ). The one purified of envy enters the garden of contentment ( riḍā ) and surrender ( taslīm ) in the neighbourhood of the Beloved: the place of rest and security in both abodes, the “abundant shade” of the verse. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_054-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_054-s4","r":"q4_cont_054","title":"","text":"Since the order of religion cannot be maintained without struggle ( jihād ), and such struggle cannot be organized without appointing an imam, God turns first to what concerns rulers, and then later speaks of struggle.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_054-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_058","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge 4:58","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_058"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-1","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَنْ تُؤَدُّوا الْأَماناتِ إِلى أَهْلِها وَإِذا حَكَمْتُمْ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ أَنْ تَحْكُمُوا بِالْعَدْلِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ نِعِمَّا يَعِظُكُمْ بِهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ سَمِيعاً بَصِيراً (58)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-2","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"قلت: «ما» في (نِعِمَّا) تمييز أو فاعل، والمخصوص محذوف، أي نعم شيئًا شيء يعظكم به، أو نعم الذي يعظكم به ذلك الأمر، وهو رد الأمانات والعدل في الحكومات.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-3","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"قال زيد بن أسلم وشهر بن حوشب: نزلت الآية في شأن الأمراء. هـ قلت: وإن نزلت في شأن عثمان بن طلحة- سَادِن الكَعبَةِ فهي عامة. والمخاطب بذلك أولاً الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم وهو سيد الأمراء، أمره الحق- تعالى- أن يرد المفاتح إلى عثمان، وذلك أن عثمان أغلق باب الكعبة يوم فتح مكة، وأبى أن يدفعها إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ليدخل","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-4","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"الكعبة، وقال: لو عَلمِتُ أنه رَسُول الله (١) ما منعتُهُ، فَلَوى عَلِيٌّ يده، وأخذها مِنهُ، فدخل رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وصَلّى رَكعَتينِ، فلما خَرَجَ سألُه العباس أن يُعطيه المفتَاح، وَيَجمَعَ له السِّدَانَةَ والسِّقَايةَ، فأمره اللهُ- تعالى- أن يرده إليه، فأمر عَلِيًّا بأن يَرُدَّه وَيَعتَذِر إليه، وكان ذلك سببًا لإسلام عثمان، ونزل الأمر بأن السِّدَانَة في أولاده أبدًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-5","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ، يا معشر الأمراء، أن تردوا الْأَماناتِ إِلى أَهْلِها من أنفسكم، أو من رعيتكم فتُنصفوا المظلوم من الظالم، حتى يؤدي ما ائتُمن عليه من دَينٍ، أو وديعة، أو غصب، أو سرقة، أو غير ذلك من حقوق العباد، بعضهم من بعض، وأن تؤدوا الزكاة إلى من يستحقها، وتصرفوا بيت المال فيمن يستحقه، لا تظلموا أهلها، ولا تضيعوا منها شيئاً في غير مستحقها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-6","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"وَيأمركم إِذا حَكَمْتُمْ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ أَنْ تَحْكُمُوا بِالْعَدْلِ في من يَنفُذُ عليه حكمُكُم، إِنَّ اللَّهَ نِعِمَّا يَعِظُكُمْ بِهِ أي: إن الله يعظكم بأمر نعم ما هو، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ سَمِيعاً بَصِيراً لا يخفى عليه أحكامكم، ولا ما أخفيتم من أمانات غيركم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-7","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"الإشارة: أمر الحق- جل جلاله- شيوخ التربية أن يؤدوا السر إلى من يستحقه من الفقراء، إذا تحققوا أهليتهم له، بحيث تخلوا عن الرذائل، كالحسد والكبر وغيرهما، وتحلوا بالفضائل، كسلامة الصدر وسخاوة النفوس وحسن الخلق، وغير ذلك من أوصاف الكمال، فإن تحققوا بالتخلية والتحلية، استحقوا الاطلاع على أسرار الربوبية، التي هي أمانات عند أهل الخصوصية، وأمرهم أن يحكموا بين الفقراء بالعدل، فيمدوا كلاً على قدر صِدقِه وخِدمَتِه، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_058-8","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"4:58 · The trust of government and the trust of spiritual knowledge","text":"ثم أمر الحق تعالى بطاعة الأمراء الذين أمرهم بالعدل وأداء الأمانة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_058-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_058-s1","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"","text":"In the expression niʿimmā (“excellent indeed is what ...”), mā may be a specifying accusative ( tamyīz ) or the grammatical subject, while what is specially commended is unexpressed. Thus it is either “excellent is the thing with which He admonishes you” or “excellent is that with which He admonishes you: namely, this command.” The commanded good is the restoration of trusts and equity in adjudication.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_058-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_058-s2","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"Occasion and scope","text":"Zayd ibn Aslam and Shahr ibn Ḥawshab are cited as saying that the verse concerns rulers. Ibn ʿAjība adds that even if its occasion was ʿUthmān ibn Ṭalḥa, custodian ( sādin ) of the Kaʿba, it is general in scope. The one first addressed is the Messenger, peace be upon him, the foremost of rulers. God commanded him to return the keys to ʿUthmān. Ibn ʿAjība relates that at the conquest of Mecca ʿUthmān had locked the Kaʿba's door and refused to hand over the keys so the Messenger might enter, saying, “Had I known he was God's Messenger, I would not have prevented him.” ʿAlī then twisted his arm and took the keys. The Messenger entered and prayed two cycles. When he emerged, al-ʿAbbās requested the keys, so that custody of the Kaʿba ( sidāna ) and the provision of water to pilgrims ( siqāya ) might be combined in him. God commanded that the keys be returned to their holder; the Prophet ordered ʿAlī to return them and apologise. The incident became the occasion of ʿUthmān's embracing Islam, and the guardianship, according to this account, was assigned to his descendants perpetually.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_058-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_058-s3","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"","text":"God commands rulers to restore what has been entrusted to its rightful owners, whether among themselves or among their subjects. They must give redress to the oppressed against the oppressor, until the rights of people are discharged: a loan or debt, a deposit, goods seized by force or theft, or other claims among human beings. They must give zakāt to its lawful recipients and distribute the public treasury ( bayt al-māl ) to those entitled to it, neither wronging its beneficiaries nor diverting any of it to an undeserving purpose. They must judge with equity those who are subject to their jurisdiction. “God admonishes you most excellently”: His command is indeed excellent advice. God is All-Hearing and All-Seeing: none of their judgments nor any trusts they have concealed can escape Him.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_058-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_058-s4","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"","text":"God likewise commands the teachers of spiritual training ( shuyūkh al-tarbiya ) to hand over the secret ( sirr ) to those fuqarāʾ [disciples of the path] entitled to it, when the teachers have become certain of their readiness ( ahliyya ). This occurs when the aspirants have emptied themselves of vices such as envy and pride and have adorned themselves with the virtues: purity of heart, generous souls, good character, and other marks of completeness. Once takhliya and taḥliya have been realized in them, they become qualified to receive the secrets of lordship ( asrār al-rubūbiyya ), held in trust by the people of special spiritual election. Teachers must also judge justly between the fuqarāʾ , extending to each the measure of help appropriate to his truthfulness ( ṣidq ) and service ( khidma ). God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_058-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_058-s5","r":"q4_cont_058","title":"","text":"After commanding rulers to be just and to return trusts, God commands obedience to those rulers.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_058-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_059","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh 4:59","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_059"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-1","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُوا الرَّسُولَ وَأُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنْكُمْ فَإِنْ تَنازَعْتُمْ فِي شَيْءٍ فَرُدُّوهُ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ ذلِكَ خَيْرٌ وَأَحْسَنُ تَأْوِيلاً (59)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-2","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"أعاد العامل في قوله: (وأطيعوا الرسول) ، إشارة إلى استقلال الرسول بالطاعة، ولم يُعده في أُولِي الْأَمْرِ إشارة إلى أنه يوجد منهم من لا تجب طاعته، ثم بيّنه بقوله: فَإِنْ تَنازَعْتُمْ فِي شَيْءٍ كأنه قيل: فإن لم يعملوا بالحق فلا تطيعوهم، وردوا ما تخالفتم فيه إلى حكم الله ورسوله. قاله الطيبي، وسيأتي تحريرُ ذلك إن شاء الله تعالى.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-3","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ فيما أمركم به ونهاكم عنه، وَأَطِيعُوا الرَّسُولَ كذلك. وَأُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنْكُمْ أي: مَن ولي أمرَكم. من وُلاَةِ العدل كالخلفاء والأمراء بعدهم، تجب طاعتهم فيما أمَروُا به من الطاعة دون المعصية إلا لخوف هرج. قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «إنَّمَا الطَّاعَةُ فِي المَعرُوف» ، فإن لم يعدل: وجبت طاعته خوفًا من الفتنة. وهذا هو الأصح. لقوله- عليه الصلاة والسلام-:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-4","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"«سَيَليكم ولاة، فيليكم البَرُّ ببره، والفاجر بفجوره، فاستمعوا لهم، وأطيعوا في كل ما وافق الحق، فصلوا وراءهم، فإن أحسنوا فلهم، وإن أساءوا فلكم وعليهم» . رواه أبو هريرة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-5","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"وفي حديث آخر: «لا أن تَروا كُفرًا بَوَاحًا، لكم عليه من اللهِ بُرهَانٌ» . أي: فيجب عزلهم. وقال أيضا صلّى الله عليه وسلم لما سأله أبو وائل فقال: يا رسول الله أرأيت إن كان علينا أمراء يمنعوننا حقنا ويسألون حقهم؟. فقال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «اسمَعُوا وأطِيعُوا، فَإنَّ عليهم ما حُمِّلُوا وَعَليكُم ما حُملتم» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-6","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"وقال جابر بن عبد الله والحسن والضحاك ومجاهد: أولو الأمر هم الفقهاء والعلماء، أهل الدين والفضل، يُعلَّمون الناس معالم دينهم، ويأمرون بالمعروف وينْهون عن المنكر، دليله. قوله تعالى: وَلَوْ رَدُّوهُ إِلَى الرَّسُولِ وَإِلى أُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنْهُمْ ... الآية. قال أبو الأسود: ليس شيء أعز من العلم، الملوك حُكَّام على الناس، والعلماء حُكَّام على الملوك. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-7","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"فَإِنْ تَنازَعْتُمْ أنتم وأولو الأمر، أو بعضكم مع بعض- أي: اختلفتم في حكم شيء من أمر الدين فلم تعلموا حكمه، فَرُدُّوهُ إِلَى اللَّهِ أي: إلى كتاب الله، وَإلى الرَّسُولَ في زمانه، أو سنته بعد موته، فإن لم يوجد بالنص فبالقياس. فالأحكام ثلاثة: مثبت بالكتاب، ومثبت بالسنة، ومثبت بالرد إليهما على وجه القياس. وعن إبراهيم بن يسار قال: قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «اعملُوا بالقرآن: أحلُّوا حَلاَلهُ، وحرَّمُوا حرامَهُ، وآمنوا بِه ولا تكفُروا بشيءٍ منهُ، وما اشتبه عليكُم فردُّوه إلي الله تعالى وإلى أولى العِلم من بَعدي، كيما يُخبرُونكم به» ، ثم قال: «وليَسعُكُم القرآن وما فيهِ من البَيَانِ فإنه شافعٌ مشفَّعٌ، وما حِلٌ مُصدَّقَّ (١) وأن له بكل حَرفٍ نُورًا يومَ القِيَاَمَة» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-8","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"فردوا الأحكام إليه وإلى الرسول، إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فإن الإيمان يُوجِبُ ذلك. ذلِكَ الرد خَيْرٌ لكم وَأَحْسَنُ تَأْوِيلًا من تأويلكم بالرأي من غير رد، وأحسن عاقبة ومآلاً، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-9","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"الإشارة: أولو الأمر عند الصوفية، هم شيوخ التربية العارفون بالله، فيجب على المريدين طاعتهم في المنشط والمكره، وفي كل ما أمروا به، فمن خالف أو قال: «لِمَ» لَم يفلح أبدًا، ويكفي الإشارة عن التصريح عند الحذاق أهل الاعتناء، فإن تعارض أمر الأمراء وأمر الشيوخ، قدَّم أمر الشيخ إلا لفتنة فادحة، فإن الشيخ يأمر بطاعتهم أيضًا لما يؤدي من الهرج بالفقراء، فإن تنازعتم يا معشر الفقراء، في شيء من علم الشريعة أو الطريقة، فردوه إلى الكتاب والسُّنة. قال الجنيد رضي الله عنه: طريقتنا هذه مؤيدة بالكتاب والسنة، فمن لم يقرأ القرآن ويتعلم الحديث لا يُقتدى به في هذا الشأن. هـ. ويكفي المهم من ذلك، وهو ما يتوقف عليه أمر عبادته. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_059-10","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"4:59 · Obedience, juristic reasoning, and the authority of the shaykh","text":"ثم ذكر الحق تعالى من أعرض عن حكم الله ورسوله، ورضى بحكم غيرهما، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_059-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_059-s1","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"Grammar and principle of interpretation","text":"The governing verb “obey” is repeated before “the Messenger,” marking his independent right to obedience. It is not repeated before “those entrusted with authority,” indicating that there may be among them persons whose commands are not binding. This is then clarified by “If you dispute about anything,” as though the verse said: if they do not act in accordance with the truth, do not obey them in that matter; return the point of disagreement to the judgment of God and His Messenger. Ibn ʿAjība attributes this explanation to al-Ṭībī and promises to elaborate it.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_059-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_059-s2","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"","text":"O believers, obey God in what He commands and forbids, and obey His Messenger likewise. “And those in authority among you” means those who administer your affairs, including just governors such as the caliphs and rulers who followed them. They must be obeyed in commands entailing obedience to God, not in sins, although Ibn ʿAjība makes an exception concerning the fear of civil disorder ( harj ). He adds that if a ruler does not act justly, obedience remains required for fear of sedition ( fitna ), and calls this the sounder position. The Prophet said: “Obedience is only in what is right” ( innamā l-ṭāʿatu fī l-maʿrūf ). He also quotes a report attributed to Abū Hurayra: “Governors will rule you: the virtuous will govern through their virtue and the wicked through their wickedness. Listen to them and obey them in everything that accords with the truth; pray behind them. If they do well, the benefit is theirs; if they do wrong, it is for you [the merit of your proper conduct] and against them [the sin].” Another ḥadīth says: “Unless you see manifest unbelief ( kufr bawāḥ ) for which you have a proof from God.” [Textual note: Cairo I:519 prints لا أن تروا, whereas the report in Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī , nos. 7055–7056, reads إلا أن تروا (“unless you see”). The English follows the latter reading here; the apparent omission in the Cairo print is expressly disclosed.] Ibn ʿAjība glosses this as requiring the removal of such rulers. He further quotes a question which the Cairo text attributes to Abū Wāʾil: “Messenger of God, what if we have rulers who withhold our rights but demand their own?” The Prophet replies: “Listen and obey; they bear the burden entrusted to them, and you bear the burden entrusted to you.” [Source note: Muslim 1846a names Salama b. Yazīd al-Juʿfī as the questioner, in a report transmitted through ʿAlqama b. Wāʾil from his father; 1846b explicitly assigns the reply to the Prophet. Al-Thaʿlabī on 4:59 likewise gives ʿAlqama’s report from his father, but leaves the questioner unnamed. This earlier tafsīr parallel separates narrator from questioner and supports Muslim’s report structure. Cairo’s Abū Wāʾil is retained as its own attribution; the exact origin of that different name is unestablished.] Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḍaḥḥāk and Mujāhid are also reported as holding that ulū l-amr signifies the jurists and scholars, people of religion and excellence, who teach the foundations of faith, command what is right and forbid what is wrong. The proof offered is “If they had referred it to the Messenger and to those in authority among them ...” [Q 4:83]. Abū l-Aswad remarked: “Nothing is dearer than knowledge. Kings judge their peoples, and scholars judge kings.” “If you dispute”—whether between yourselves and rulers or amongst yourselves—over the ruling of a matter of religion, and you do not know what its judgment is, “refer it to God,” that is, to God's Book, and “the Messenger,” either to him during his lifetime or to his sunna after his death. If there is no explicit text, one returns it by analogy ( qiyās ). Rules therefore fall into three classes: established by the Book, established by the sunna , and established by being referred to both through a valid qiyās . Ibn ʿAjība then cites from Ibrāhīm ibn Yasār a saying attributed to the Prophet: “Act according to the Qurʾān: deem lawful its lawful things, deem unlawful its forbidden things, believe in it, and reject none of it. Whatever is unclear to you, refer to God Most High and to those who possess knowledge after me, so that they may inform you of it.” The continuation reads: “Let the Qurʾān and the clarification within it suffice you, for it is an intercessor whose intercession is granted, an accuser whose testimony is accepted, and for every letter of it there is a light on the Day of Resurrection.” [Translator’s source note: An earlier close parallel in al-Thaʿlabī, al-Kashf wa-l-bayān , III:337, under Q4:59, introduces this report through “Abū al-Malīḥ al-Hudhalī, from Maʿqil ibn Yasār” ( أبو المليح الهذلي عن معقل بن يسار ). Cairo instead names Ibrāhīm ibn Yasār. The parallel locates the report but does not establish which attribution Ibn ʿAjība wrote or authenticate the transmitted saying.] Refer the rulings, then, to God and the Messenger “if you believe in God and the Last Day,” for faith itself demands this. Such referral is better for you and “more excellent in taʾwīl ”—better than applying your own interpretation without reference to revelation, and better in final consequence and issue. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_059-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_059-s3","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"","text":"For the Sufis, those charged with authority ( ulū l-amr ) are the spiritual masters who know God ( shuyūkh al-tarbiya al-ʿārifūn bi-llāh ). Aspirants ( murīdūn ) are obliged, within the discipline of the path, to obey them in ease and hardship and in everything they instruct. Ibn ʿAjība says that one who objects or asks “Why?” does not prosper, and that for perceptive aspirants a gesture suffices without a fully explicit command. If a command of rulers conflicts with a command of the shaykhs, the disciple, according to Ibn ʿAjība, gives precedence to the shaykh, except when doing so would occasion a grave public disturbance: the shaykh himself then commands obedience to rulers to avoid disorder affecting the fuqarāʾ . Should you, people of the path, dispute about a question of outward law ( sharīʿa ) or the inner way ( ṭarīqa ), refer it to the Book and the sunna . Al-Junayd said: “This path of ours is supported by the Book and the sunna . Whoever has not read the Qurʾān and learned the ḥadīth is not to be followed in this affair.” For each person, the essential portion is what his acts of worship require. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_059-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_059-s4","r":"q4_cont_059","title":"","text":"God next speaks of those who turn away from His and His Messenger's judgment and consent to judgment by another.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_059-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_060","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition 4:60–63","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_060"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-1","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ يَزْعُمُونَ أَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ وَما أُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ يُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يَتَحاكَمُوا إِلَى الطَّاغُوتِ وَقَدْ أُمِرُوا أَنْ يَكْفُرُوا بِهِ وَيُرِيدُ الشَّيْطانُ أَنْ يُضِلَّهُمْ ضَلالاً بَعِيداً (60) وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُمْ تَعالَوْا إِلى ما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ وَإِلَى الرَّسُولِ رَأَيْتَ الْمُنافِقِينَ يَصُدُّونَ عَنْكَ صُدُوداً (61) فَكَيْفَ إِذا أَصابَتْهُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ بِما قَدَّمَتْ أَيْدِيهِمْ ثُمَّ جاؤُكَ يَحْلِفُونَ بِاللَّهِ إِنْ أَرَدْنا إِلاَّ إِحْساناً وَتَوْفِيقاً (62) أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ يَعْلَمُ اللَّهُ ما فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ فَأَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَعِظْهُمْ وَقُلْ لَهُمْ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ قَوْلاً بَلِيغاً (63)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-2","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"قلت: (رأيت المنافقين) ، وضع الظاهر موضع المضمر تسجيلاً عليهم بالنفاق وذمًا لهم به. وكان القياس: رأيتهم، و (صدودًا) : مصدر، أو اسم مصدر الذي هو الصد، والفرق بينه وبين المصدر: أن المصدر اسم للمعنى الذي هو الحدث، واسم المصدر اسم للفظ المحسوس، و (يحلفون) حال. و (في أنفسهم) يتعلق بقُل، وقيل ببليغًا. وهو ضعيف لأن الصفات لا يتقدم عليها معمولها، اللهم إلا أن يتوسع في الظروف.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-3","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أَلَمْ تَرَ يا محمد إِلَى الَّذِينَ يَزْعُمُونَ أَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ وَما أُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ وهم المنافقون، يُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يَتَحاكَمُوا إِلَى الطَّاغُوتِ، كعب بن الأشرف لفرط طغيانه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-4","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"وفي معناه كل من يحكم بالباطل، وَقَدْ أُمِرُوا أَنْ يَكْفُرُوا بِهِ، ويؤمنوا بالله ويرضوا بحكمه. وَيُرِيدُ الشَّيْطانُ أَنْ يُضِلَّهُمْ ضَلالًا بَعِيداً، بأن يصرفهم عن حكم الله ورسوله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-5","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"قال ابن عباس: إنَّ منافقًا خَاصَمَ يَهُودِيًّا فَدَعَاهُ اليهوديّ إلى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، ودعاه المنافق إلى كعب بن الأشْرَف، ثم اختصما إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، فحكم لليهودي بالحق فلم يرض المنافق، وقال: نتحاكم إلى عُمَر، فقال اليهودي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-6","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"نعم فذهبا إلى عمر رضي الله عنه فقال اليهودي: قضى لي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فلم يرض بقضائه وخاصم إليك. فقال عمر للمنافق: أكذلك؟. قال: نعم، فقال: على رسلكما حتى أخرج إليكما، فدخل وأخذ سيفه فخرج، فضرب به عنق المنافق حتى برد (١) ، وقال: هكذا أقضي لمن لم يرضَ بقضاء الله ورسوله، فنزلت الآية.. وقال جبريل عليه السلام: إن عمر فرّق بين الحق والباطل. فسُمي الفاروق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-7","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"وَإِذا قِيلَ لَهُمْ تَعالَوْا إِلى ما أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ وَإِلَى الرَّسُولِ رَأَيْتَ الْمُنافِقِينَ أي: بعضَهم، يَصُدُّونَ عَنْكَ غير راضين بحكمك صُدُوداً عظيمًا. فَكَيْفَ يكون حالهم إِذا أَصابَتْهُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ كقتل عمر المنافقَ، بسبب ما قدمت أَيْدِيهِمْ من عدم الرضى بحكم الله، ثُمَّ جاؤُكَ يطلبون ديّة صاحبهم، يَحْلِفُونَ بِاللَّهِ إِنْ أَرَدْنا بالانصراف إلى عمر إِلَّا إِحْساناً منه بالخصمين، وَتَوْفِيقاً بينهما، قطعًا للنزاع بينهما، قال تعالى: أُولئِكَ الَّذِينَ يَعْلَمُ اللَّهُ ما فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ من النفاق، فلا يغني عنهم الكتمان والحلف الكاذب من الله شيئًا، أو يعلم الله ما في قلوبهم من الطمع في الدية، فَأَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ، أي: عن قبول معذرتهم ولا تمكنهم من طمعهم، وَقُلْ لَهُمْ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ، أي: خاليًا بهم قَوْلًا بَلِيغاً يبلغ إلى قلوبهم، ويؤثر فيهم، لينزجروا عن طلب دم صاحبهم، وإنما أمر أن يعظهم خاليا بهم لأن النصح في ذلك أنجح، وأقرب للقبول، ولذلك قيل: من نصحك وَحدَكَ فقد نصحك، ومن نصحك مع الناس فقد فضحك. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-8","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"الإشارة: كل من دخل تحت ولاية شيخ التربية، وجب أن يرد حكوماته كلها إليه، ويرضى بما قضى عليه، وترى بعض الفقراء يزعمون أنهم في تربية الشيخ وتحت أحكامه، ثم يتحاكمون إلى حُكام الجور وقضاة الزمان في أمر الدنيا وما يرجع إليها، فهؤلاء قد ضلوا ضلالاً بعيدًا. إلا أن يتوبوا ويُصلحوا ما أفسدوا، بإصلاح قلب الشيخ حتى يجبر كسرهم، فالمريد الصادق لا يصل إلى الحاكم، ولو ذهب ماله كله. فإن كان ولا بد. فليوكل عنه فى ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-9","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"فكيف إذا أصابت هؤلاء مصيبة وهي ظلمة القلب، وفتنة الدنيا بسبب ما قدمت أيديهم من تخطى حكم شيخهم إلى حُكم غيره، ثم جاؤوك يحلفون بالله ما أردنا إلا إحسانًا وهو حفظ مالنا، وتوفيقًا بيننا وبين خصمنا، فيجب على الشيخ أن يُعرض عن عتابهم ويذكرهم حتى يتوبوا،. فإن تابوا فإن الله غفور رحيم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_060-10","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"4:60–63 · Appeal to false judgment, repentance, and private admonition","text":"ثم أعاد الأمر بطاعة الرسول وتحكيمه فى جميع الأمور ترهيبا وترغيبا، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_060-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_060-s1","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"Language and construction (*qultu*)","text":"In “you see the hypocrites” the explicit noun replaces the pronoun one might have expected, “you see them”; it brands them with hypocrisy and censures them for it. Ṣudūdan (“turning away”) is either a verbal noun ( maṣdar ) or what the grammarians call an ism al-maṣdar , corresponding to ṣadd ; Ibn ʿAjība distinguishes the verbal noun as naming the event or meaning and the ism al-maṣdar as naming its perceptible verbal expression. Yaḥlifūna (“swearing”) is circumstantial ( ḥāl ). The phrase fī anfusihim (“within themselves,” or “concerning their very selves”) is related syntactically to “say.” A proposed attachment to balīghan (“penetrating”) is weak, because a dependent of an attributive expression should not ordinarily precede it, except under a broader allowance for adverbial expressions.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_060-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_060-s2","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"The outward interpretation (*yaqūlu l-Ḥaqq*)","text":"God—exalted is His majesty—addresses Muḥammad: Have you not observed those hypocrites who merely claim faith in the revelation given to you and the books revealed before you? They nevertheless seek the judgment of the ṭāghūt : here Ibn ʿAjība identifies him as Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf because of the magnitude of his transgression. The expression includes, by extension, everyone who judges according to falsehood. Yet these people were commanded to disown false authority, believe in God, and accept His judgment. Satan wishes to deflect them from the judgment of God and His Messenger into a remote error. Ibn ʿAjība then relates an account attributed to Ibn ʿAbbās. A hypocrite and a Jewish man were in dispute. The Jewish litigant proposed that the Prophet decide their case, while the hypocrite proposed Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf. They nevertheless went to the Messenger, who gave judgment in favour of the Jewish man, according to what was right. The hypocrite refused to accept it and proposed that they appeal to ʿUmar. The Jewish man agreed. On hearing that the Messenger had already judged and that the hypocrite rejected the decision, ʿUmar asked the latter whether it was so. When he answered yes, ʿUmar told them to wait, entered his house, took up his sword, and—according to this transmitted story —struck off the hypocrite's head, saying, “Thus do I judge one who will not accept God's and His Messenger's judgment.” The story associates the descent of the verses with this event and relates that Gabriel described ʿUmar as the one who distinguished truth from falsehood, whence the epithet al-Fārūq . [Translator’s note: This is an exegetical report, not an established ruling or an authorization of private violence.] [Translator’s note: Its transmission requires the separate historical scrutiny recorded in the notes.] When they are summoned to God's revelation and the Messenger, some of these hypocrites avert themselves, refusing his judgment. What will become of them if misfortune strikes them—in the account just recited, the killing of their companion—as a consequence of rejecting the divine decision? They then come asking compensation for their companion, swearing that in going to ʿUmar they wanted only kindness to both litigants and reconciliation between them, so as to settle the dispute. But God knows the hypocrisy within their hearts; alternatively He knows their desire for blood compensation. Their concealment and false oaths cannot avail them before Him. Therefore the Messenger is told neither to accept their excuses nor permit them to obtain what they covet. He is to admonish them and speak to them privately, with words that reach the heart and restrain them from pursuing the claim. Privacy makes advice more effective and easier to accept. Hence the maxim: “Whoever counsels you when you are alone has counselled you; whoever counsels you before people has exposed you to shame.” God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_060-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_060-s3","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"(*al-ishāra*)","text":"Whoever has placed himself under the spiritual authority ( wilāya ) of a shaykh of training ( shaykh al-tarbiya ) should, within that relationship, refer his disputes and affairs to him and accept his direction. Ibn ʿAjība criticizes certain fuqarāʾ who profess to be under a shaykh's training but then turn to the unjust rulers and judges of their time over worldly affairs and related matters. He says that they have strayed far astray, unless they repent and repair the harm by reconciling the shaykh's heart with them, so that he may mend their fracture. He says that the truthful aspirant will not go to a judge even if all his wealth is lost; if recourse is absolutely unavoidable, he should appoint a representative. [Translator’s note: This states Ibn ʿAjība's demanding counsel on discipleship, not a substitute for legal rights or a general rule barring access to justice.] If such aspirants experience the calamity of a darkened heart and entanglement in worldly turmoil because they have crossed from their shaykh's ruling to another's, they may come insisting that they intended only to safeguard their property and reconcile with their opponent. The shaykh should refrain from reproach and instead remind them so that they repent. If they do repent, God is Forgiving, Merciful.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_060-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_060-s4","r":"q4_cont_060","title":"","text":"The command to obey the Messenger and seek his judgment in all affairs is repeated, combining warning with encouragement.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_060-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_064","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience 4:64–68","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_064"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-1","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"وَما أَرْسَلْنا مِنْ رَسُولٍ إِلاَّ لِيُطاعَ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ إِذْ ظَلَمُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ جاؤُكَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا اللَّهَ وَاسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمُ الرَّسُولُ لَوَجَدُوا اللَّهَ تَوَّاباً رَحِيماً (64) فَلا وَرَبِّكَ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ حَتَّى يُحَكِّمُوكَ فِيما شَجَرَ بَيْنَهُمْ ثُمَّ لا يَجِدُوا فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ حَرَجاً مِمَّا قَضَيْتَ وَيُسَلِّمُوا تَسْلِيماً (65) وَلَوْ أَنَّا كَتَبْنا عَلَيْهِمْ أَنِ اقْتُلُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ أَوِ اخْرُجُوا مِنْ دِيارِكُمْ ما فَعَلُوهُ إِلاَّ قَلِيلٌ مِنْهُمْ وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ فَعَلُوا ما يُوعَظُونَ بِهِ لَكانَ خَيْراً لَهُمْ وَأَشَدَّ تَثْبِيتاً (66) وَإِذاً لَآتَيْناهُمْ مِنْ لَدُنَّا أَجْراً عَظِيماً (67) وَلَهَدَيْناهُمْ صِراطاً مُسْتَقِيماً (68)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-2","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"قلت: (توابًا رحيمًا) مفعولا (وَجَدَ) إن كانت علمية، أو (توابًا) حال، و (رحيمًا) بدل منه، أو حال من ضميره إن فسرت بصادف.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-3","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَما أَرْسَلْنا مِنْ رَسُولٍ من لدن آدم إلى زمانك، إِلَّا لِيُطاعَ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وأمره بطاعته، فمن لم يطعه ولم يرض بأحكامه فهو كافر به. وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ أي: المنافقون حين ظَلَمُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ بالترافع إلى غيرك، والتحاكم إلى الطاغوت جاؤُكَ تائبين فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا اللَّهَ بالتوبة، وَاسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمُ الرَّسُولُ حين اعتذروا إليه حتى انتصب لهم شفيعًا، لَوَجَدُوا اللَّهَ أي: تحققوا كونه تَوَّاباً رَحِيماً، قابلاً لتوبتهم متفضلاً عليهم بالرحمة والغفران. وإنما عدل عن الخطاب في قوله: وَاسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمُ الرَّسُولُ ولم يقل: واستغفرت لهم، تفخيمًا لشأنه، وتنبيهًا على أن من حق الرسول أن يقبل اعتذار التائبين، وإن عَظُم جُرمُهم، ويشفع لهم، ومن جلالة منصبه أن يشفع في عظائم الذنوب وكبائرها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-4","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"ثم أقسم بربوبيته على نفي إيمان من لم يرض بحكم رسوله، فقال: فَلا وَرَبِّكَ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ إيمانًا حقيقيًا حَتَّى يُحَكِّمُوكَ أي: يترافعوا إليك، راضين بحكمك، فِيما شَجَرَ بَيْنَهُمْ أي: اختلط بينهم واختلفوا فيه ثُمَّ لا يَجِدُوا فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ حَرَجاً أي: ضيقًا وشكًا مِمَّا قَضَيْتَ، بل تنشرح صدورهم لحكمك لأنه حق من عند الله. وَيُسَلِّمُوا لأمرك تَسْلِيماً. أي: ينقادوا لأمرك ظاهرًا وباطنًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-5","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"وَلَوْ أَنَّا كَتَبْنا عَلَيْهِمْ أَنِ اقْتُلُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ، توبة من ذنوبكم، كما كتبناه على بني إسرائيل، أو في الجهاد في سبيل الله، أَوِ اخْرُجُوا مِنْ دِيارِكُمْ كما خرج بنو إسرائيل حين أمرناهم بالهجرة من مصر، ما فَعَلُوهُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-6","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"إِلَّا قَلِيلٌ مِنْهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-7","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"وهم المخلصون. قال أبو بكر الصديق رضي الله عنه: (لو كتب ذلك علينا لكنت أنا أول خارج) . قال ثابت بن قيس بن شماس: (لو أمرني رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أن أقتل نفسي لفعلت) . وكذلك قال عُمر وعمارُ بن ياسر وابنُ مسعود وناس من أصحاب رسول الله صلّى الله عليه وسلم: لو أمرنا لفعلنا. فبلغ ذلك النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال: «إنَّ مِن أُمَّتِي رِجَالاً:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-8","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"الإيمَانُ في قُلُوبِهِم أثبَتُ مِنَ الجِبَالِ الرَّوَاسِي» . فهؤلاء من القليل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-9","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"وسبب نزول قوله: فَلا وَرَبِّكَ.. الخ: قضية الزُّبَيرِ مع حَاطِب في شرَاج الحَرَّة (١) ، كَانَا يسقيانِ به النّخل، فتخاصما إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال عليه السلام: «اسقِ يا زُبيرُ وأرسِل إلى جارِكَ» ، فقال حَاطبُ: لأن كَان ابن عمتك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-10","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"فقال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «اسقِ يا زُبيرُ، واحِبِس الماءَ حتَّى يبلغ الجدر (٢) واستوف حقك» . وقيل: نزلت في اليهودي مع المنافق المتقدم، وهو أليق بالسياق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-11","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ فَعَلُوا ما يُوعَظُونَ بِهِ من طاعة الرسول، والرضى بحكمه، لَكانَ خَيْراً لَهُمْ في آجلهم وعاجلهم، وَأَشَدَّ تَثْبِيتاً في دينهم وقوة في إيمانهم، أو تثبيتًا لثواب أعمالهم، وَإِذاً لو فعلوا ذلك لَآتَيْناهُمْ مِنْ لَدُنَّا أَجْراً عَظِيماً وَلَهَدَيْناهُمْ صِراطاً مُسْتَقِيماً يصلون بسلوكه إلى حضرة القدس، ودوام الأنس، ويفتح لهم أسرار العلوم، ومخازن الفهوم، قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «من عَمِلَ بِمَا عَلِمَ أَوْرَثَهُ اللهُ علمَ مَا لم يعلم» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-12","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"الإشارة: كما أمر الله بطاعة رسوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم في حياته، أمر بطاعة ورثته بعد مماته، وهم العلماء الأتقياء الذين يعدلون في الأحكام، والأولياء العارفون الذين يحكمون بوحي الإلهام، فالعلماء حُكَّام على العموم، والأولياء حكام على الخصوص، أعني من تعلق بهم من أهل الإرادة، فمن لم يرض بحكم العلماء، ووجد في نفسه حرجًا مما قضوا به عليه، ففيه شعبة من النفاق، وخصلة من المنافقين. ومن لم يرض بحكم الأولياء فقد خرج من دائرتهم، ومن عُش تربيتهم، لأن حكم الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- وحكم ورثته هو حكم الله، ومن لم يرض بحكم الله خرج عن دائرة الإيمان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-13","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"فلا يَكمُلُ إيمَانُ العَبدِ حتَّى لا يجد في نفسه حرجًا من أحكام الله، القهرية والتكليفية، ويسلم لما يبرز من عنصر القدرة الأزلية، كيفما كان، فقرًا أو غنى، ذلاً أو عزًا، منعًا أو عطاء، قبضًا أو بسطًا، مرضًا أو صحة، إلى غير ذلك من اختلاف المقادير. ويرضى بذلك ظاهرَا وباطنًا، وينسلخ من تدبيره واختياره إلى اختيار مولاه فهو أعلم بمصالحه، وأرحم به من أمه وأبيه: وبالله التوفيق. وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_064-14","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"4:64–68 · Prophetic judgment, inward surrender, and the fruit of obedience","text":"ثم وعد المطيعين وعدا جميلا، وخيرا جزيلا، ترغيبا فى امتثال ما أُمر به من طاعة الرسول، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_064-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_064-s1","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"","text":"If wajada (“find”) is treated as a verb of cognition, the sense is “they would have known God to be accepting of repentance and merciful.” [Grammatical and textual note: On this analysis Allāh is the first object, with acceptance of repentance and mercy predicated of Him. Cairo I:522 instead calls tawwāban and raḥīman “the two objects” of wajada , a faulty formula because it leaves the already expressed first object, Allāh , unaccounted for. The explanatory English follows the contrast made explicit by al-Bayḍāwī and al-ʿUkbarī on 4:64; it does not claim to reproduce a corrected Arabic witness.] If wajada means to encounter or come upon, tawwāban is circumstantial, while raḥīman is either substitutive ( badal ) or another circumstance tied to the relevant pronoun.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_064-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_064-s2","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"","text":"From Adam's day to Muḥammad's, God has sent no messenger but that the messenger should be obeyed by His leave and command. Ibn ʿAjība says that one who rejects a messenger's authority and refuses his judgments thereby rejects him. Had the hypocrites come repentantly to the Messenger after wronging themselves by seeking another tribunal and appealing to the ṭāghūt , and had they asked God's pardon while the Messenger sought forgiveness on their behalf, they would have experienced God's readiness to receive repentance and His mercy. The verse speaks of “the Messenger” rather than simply “you”—“had you asked forgiveness for them”—to magnify his station, and to indicate that he should receive the apology of sincere penitents, however grave their offence, and intercede for them. That he may intercede in matters of the greatest sins belongs to the dignity of his office. God then swears by His Lordship that those who refuse the Messenger's judgment do not possess faith in its true sense. They must bring their disputes to him, willingly accept what he rules, and experience neither inward narrowness nor doubt about it; rather their breasts should expand at his decision, for it is truth from God. Their surrender must be outward and inward together. If they had been charged to kill themselves by way of repentance, as the children of Israel were charged in the episode invoked here—or to risk their lives in striving in God's way—or ordered to abandon their homes, as Israel was ordered to migrate from Egypt, only a few, the sincerely devoted, would have complied. Abū Bakr is reported to have said that had emigration been enjoined he would have been the first to leave. Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās is said to have declared that if the Messenger ordered him to kill himself, he would obey. Similar expressions of resolve are attributed to ʿUmar, ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir, Ibn Masʿūd, and other Companions. When this reached the Prophet, the account reports him saying that some men of his community have faith in their hearts firmer than immovable mountains. Ibn ʿAjība counts them among the “few.” [Translator’s note: These extraordinary hypothetical declarations belong to the account's rhetorical illustration of obedience; they are not instructions addressed to the reader.] Concerning the occasion of verse 65, he recounts the dispute of al-Zubayr with Ḥāṭib over irrigation channels in the stony ground ( shirāj al-ḥarra ). They watered date palms from the same supply. The Messenger first said, “Water, Zubayr, then release [the water] to your neighbour.” The neighbour retorted that this was because al-Zubayr was the son of the Messenger's paternal aunt. The Prophet then told al-Zubayr to water fully, holding back the flow until it reached the boundary banks ( judur ), and thus to take his complete due. Another report links the verse to the Jewish litigant and hypocrite discussed above, which Ibn ʿAjība judges more fitting to the immediate sequence. [Translator’s note: The irrigation report’s sound core and Ibn ʿAjība’s identification of its other litigant are distinct questions.] If the people had practised the exhortation to obey the Messenger and accept his judgment, it would have been better for their affairs in this world and the next, firmer for their religion and stronger for their faith; alternatively, it would have secured the reward for their works. In that event God would bestow immense reward from His own presence and guide them on the straight road, leading them to the holy Presence and continual intimacy, opening to them the mysteries of the sciences and treasuries of understanding. Ibn ʿAjība cites the saying ascribed to the Prophet, “Whoever acts according to what he knows, God bequeaths to him knowledge of what he did not know.” [Source note: Abū Nuʿaym, Ḥilyat al-awliyāʾ X:14–15, explains that a saying transmitted from Jesus through a Successor was mistakenly attributed to the Prophet and furnished with a chain. He rejects that chain as a basis for attributing it through Aḥmad b. Ḥanbal. This criticism concerns that attribution and chain; it does not decide the maxim’s use by Sufi teachers.] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_064-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_064-s3","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"","text":"Just as God commanded obedience to His Messenger during his lifetime, He has commanded obedience after the Prophet's passing to his heirs: God-fearing scholars who exercise justice in judgments and the saints who know God and judge through inspired understanding ( waḥy al-ilhām ). The scholars judge for the community at large; the saints judge concerning their particular disciples and those who voluntarily attach themselves to their training. Whoever resists the just decision of learned authorities and feels inward constriction has a trait of hypocrisy. Whoever rejects the direction of the saints withdraws from their circle and from the sphere of their training. For, Ibn ʿAjība says, the judgment of the Messenger and that of his heirs is God's judgment; whoever does not accept God's judgment has departed from the circle of faith. Faith reaches perfection only when a servant ceases to find constriction in the workings of God's determinations, whether irresistible ( qahriyya ) or prescriptive ( taklīfiyya ), and submits to whatever manifests from eternal power: poverty or wealth, humiliation or honour, withholding or gift, contraction ( qabḍ ) or expansion ( basṭ ), illness or health, and the remaining variations of destiny. To accept them both outwardly and inwardly is to surrender the management ( tadbīr ) of one's affairs and one's self-directed choosing ( ikhtiyār ) to the choice of one's Master, who knows the servant's true good more fully and is more merciful to him than his mother or father. God grants success and guides to the even road.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_064-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_064-s4","r":"q4_cont_064","title":"","text":"God next promises the obedient a splendid reward to encourage them in obedience to the Messenger.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_064-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_069","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship 4:69–70","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_069"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-1","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"وَمَنْ يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَالرَّسُولَ فَأُولئِكَ مَعَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنَ النَّبِيِّينَ وَالصِّدِّيقِينَ وَالشُّهَداءِ وَالصَّالِحِينَ وَحَسُنَ أُولئِكَ رَفِيقاً (69) ذلِكَ الْفَضْلُ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ عَلِيماً (70)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-2","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"قلت: «رفيقاً» : تمييز لما في (حَسُن) من معنى التعجب أو المدح، ولم يجمع لأن فعيلا يُحمل على الواحد والجمع، أو لأنه أريد حسن كل واحد منهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-3","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَالرَّسُولَ ويرضى بأحكامهما ويمتثل أمرهما ويجتنب نهيهما، فَأُولئِكَ مَعَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ، وهم أكرم الخلق عند الله وأعظمهم قدرًا مِنَ النَّبِيِّينَ والمرسلين وَالصِّدِّيقِينَ وهم من كثر صدقهم وتصديقهم وعظم يقينهم وهم الأولياء العارفون بالله، وَالشُّهَداءِ الذين ماتوا جهادًا في سبيل الله، وَالصَّالِحِينَ وهم العلماء الأتقياء، ومن صلح حاله من عامة المسلمين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-4","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"قال البيضاوي: قسمهم أربعة أقسام، بحسب منازلهم في العلم والعمل، وحث كافة الناس على ألاَّ يتأخروا عنهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-5","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"وهم: الأنبياء الفائزون بكمال العلم والعمل، المتجاوزون حد الكمال إلى درجة التكميل. ثم الصديقون الذين صعِدت نفوسهم تارة بمراقي النظر في الحجج والآيات، وأخرى بمعارج التصفية والرياضات إلى أوج العرفان، حتى اطلعوا على الأشياء وأخبروا عنها على ما هي عليها. ثم الشهداء الذين أدى بهم الحرص على الطاعة والجد في إظهار الحق، حتى بذلوا مُهَجَهُم في إعلاء كلمة الله، ثم الصالحون الذين صرفوا أعمارهم في طاعته، وأحوالهم في مرضاته. ولك أن تقول: المُنعَمُ عليهم هم العارفون بالله، وهؤلاء إما أن يكونوا بالغين درجة العيان، أو واقفين في مقام الاستدلال والبرهان، والأولون إما أن ينالوا مع العيان القرب، بحيث يكونون كمن يرى الشيء قريبًا، وهم الأنبياء، أو لا، فيكونون كمن يرى الشيء بعيدًا، وهم الصديقون، والآخرون إما أن يكون عرفانهم بالبراهين القاطعة، وهم العلماء الراسخون الذين هم شهداء الله في أرضه. وإما أن يكون بأمارات وإقناعات تطمئن إليها نفوسهم، وهم الصالحون. انتهى كلامه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-6","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"وفيه نظر من وجهين: أحدهما: أنه أطلق على أهل الاستدلال أنهم عارفون، ولا يقال عند الصوفية فيه عارف، حتى يترقى عن مقام الاستدلال، وإلا فهو عالم فقط، والثاني: أنه جعل الصديقين بمنزلة من يرى الشيء بعيدًا،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-7","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"وأهل الفناء لم يبق لهم بُعدٌ، بل غابوا في القرب حتى امتحى اسمهم ورسمهم. فأيُّ بينونة وأيُّ بُعد يبقى للعارف؟","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-8","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"لولا فقدان الذوق، ولكن لكلِّ فنِ أربابُه، وسيأتي في الإشارة تحقيق ذلك إن شاء الله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-9","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"ثم قال جلّ جلاله: وَحَسُنَ أُولئِكَ رَفِيقاً أي: ما أحسنهم رفقًا في الفراديس العُلى، فهم يتمتعون فيها برؤيتهم وزيارتهم والحضور معهم، وإن كانوا أعلى منهم، فلا يلزم من كونه معهم أن تستوي درجته معهم، قال في الحاشية: وتعقل مرافقة من دون النبي في المدانات من حاله وكشفه، بحيث لا يحجب عنه، وإن كان لا مطمع له في منزلته، واعتبر برؤية البصائر له وعدم غيبته عنهم وأنسهم به والاستفادة منه، وروى عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أنه قال: «يزور الأعلَون من أهل الجنة الأسفلين، ولا يزور الأسفلون الأعلين، إلا من كان يزور في الله في الدنيا، فذلك يزور فى الجنة حيث شاء» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-10","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"رُوِيَ أن ثَوبَانَ مَولى رَسُول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أتاه يومًا وَقَد تَغَيَّر وَجهُهُ وَنَحَلَ جِسمُهُ، فسأله عليه الصلاة والسلام عن حاله، فقال: ما بي وَجَعٌ، غَيرَ أنِّي إذَا لَمْ أرَكَ اشتقْتُ إليك، واستَوحَشتُ وَحشةً شَدِيدَةً حَتَى ألقَاكَ، ثمَّ ذَكَرتُ الآخِرَةَ فخفت ألا أرَاكَ هُنَاكَ لأني عرفت أنكَ تُرفَعُ مَعَ النَّبِيِّينَ. وإن دخلتُ الجَنَّة، كُنتُ في مَنزلٍ أدون مِن مَنزِلكَ، وإن لَم أدخُلِ الجَنَّةَ فّذَلكَ حَرِيّ ألا أرَاكَ أبَدًا. فنزلت الآية وَمَنْ يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَالرَّسُولَ ... الخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-11","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"ذلِكَ الْفَضْلُ مِنَ اللَّهِ إشارة إلى ما للمطيعين من الأجور، ومزيد القرب والحضور، وأنه فضل تفضل على عباده، وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ عَلِيماً بمقادير الأعمال والمقامات، فيُجازى كُلاًّ على حسب مقامه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-12","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الطاعة التي توجب المعية الحسية في النعيم الحسي الجسماني هي الطاعة الظاهرة الحسية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-13","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"والطاعة التي توجب المعية المعنوية في النعيم الروحاني هي الطاعة الباطنية القلبية. فالمعية الحسية صاحبها مفروق، والمعية المعنوية صاحبها مجموع، لا يغيب عن حبيبه لحظة. هؤلاء هم الصديقون المقربون. وفوقهم الأنبياء، وتحتهم الشهداء والصالحون.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-14","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"وبيان ذلك أن العلم بالله تعالى: إما أن يكون عن كشف الحجاب وانقشاع السحاب، أعني سحاب الأثر، وهم أهل الشهود والعيان. وإما أن يكون من وراء الحجاب، يأخذون أجرهم من وراء الباب، يستدلون بالآثار على المؤثر. وهم أهل الدليل والبرهان. والأولون إما أن يرتقوا إلى مكافحة الوحي ورؤية الملائكة الكرام. وهم الأنبياء والرسل- عليهم الصلاة والسلام-، وإما أن يقصروا عن درجة الوحي ويكون لهم وحي إلهام، وهم الصديقون أهل الحال والمقام، فقد اشتركوا في مقام العيانِ. لكن مقام الحضرة فضاؤه واسع، والترقي في معارج أسرار التوحيد غير","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-15","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"متناهٍ، فحيث انتهى قدم الولي ابتدأ ترقي النبي، وأما أهل الحجاب فإما أن يكون علمهم بالله بالبراهين القطعية والدلائل السمعية، وهم العلماء الراسخون، وهو مقام الشهداء، وإما أن يكون علمهم بالرياضات والمجاهدات وتواتر الكرامات، وهم العباد والزهاد. وهو مقام الصالحين، ويلتحق بهم عوام المسلمين، لأن كل مقام من هذه المقامات فيه درجات ومقامات لا يحصرها إلا العالم بها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_069-16","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"4:69–70 · Prophets, truthful ones, martyrs, and the degrees of companionship","text":"ثم رغّب في الجهاد الذي هو المقصود، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_069-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_069-s1","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"","text":"Rafīqan (“as companion”) is a specification ( tamyīz ) explaining the commendatory or exclamatory force of ḥasuna . The singular is used with reference to several people because the adjective faʿīl may be applied to singular and plural alike; alternatively the intention is to commend each of them individually.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_069-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_069-s2","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"","text":"Those who obey God and the Messenger, accept their judgments, carry out their commands and shun their prohibitions, will be among God's most honoured creatures, those upon whom He has bestowed grace. These are the prophets and messengers; the ṣiddīqūn , whose truthfulness, affirmation of truth and certainty have become great—identified here with the saints who know God; the martyrs ( shuhadāʾ ) who have died fighting in God's path; and the righteous ( ṣāliḥūn ), including devout scholars and the upright among Muslims generally. Al-Bayḍāwī, whom Ibn ʿAjība quotes at length, divides them into four groups in correspondence with their stations of knowledge and action, urging everyone not to lag behind. The prophets possess perfection in both knowledge and practice, and pass beyond the attainment of perfection in themselves to perfecting others. Next come the ṣiddīqūn , whose souls rise toward the summit of knowing: at one time ascending by examination of arguments and signs, at another by purification and spiritual exercises, until they perceive things and give account of them as they are. Then come the martyrs, whose ardour for obedience and striving to manifest the truth leads them to offer their very lives to exalt God's word. Finally come the righteous, who devote their years to His obedience and their circumstances to what pleases Him. [Translator’s source note: Bayḍāwī’s Anwār al-tanzīl , II:83, under Q4:69, reads وأموالهم في مرضاته , “and their wealth to what pleases Him.” Cairo instead prints وأحوالهم , “and their circumstances,” retained above. The cited source therefore differs in meaning at this word; it does not by itself establish Ibn ʿAjība’s intended wording.] Al-Bayḍāwī offers another classification: those favoured are people who know God, and their knowing occurs either by reaching immediate vision ( ʿiyān ) or while remaining in inference and demonstration ( istidlāl and burhān ). Those who behold directly may have, in addition, an intimate nearness analogous to seeing something close at hand: these are the prophets. Or they may be like a person who sees from a distance: these are the ṣiddīqūn . Those who remain with proofs may know through decisive demonstrations, and thus are deeply rooted scholars, God's witnesses on earth; or through indications and persuasive reasons in which their souls rest, and thus are the righteous. Here ends the cited discourse. Ibn ʿAjība raises two objections . First, al-Bayḍāwī applies the name ʿārif —one possessing realized knowledge—to those who have knowledge through inference, while Sufis reserve it for those who pass beyond mere inference; otherwise the person is an ʿālim , a scholar. Second, he locates the ṣiddīqūn among those seeing from afar. But, says Ibn ʿAjība, people of self-effacement ( fanāʾ ) no longer experience remoteness: they have become lost in nearness, to the point that their name and trace are effaced. What distance or separation can remain to the knower? He remarks that this mistake comes from lacking direct taste ( dhawq ), and each discipline has its own masters. He promises further clarification in the ishāra . “How excellent are these companions” in the lofty paradises! Those who accompany them enjoy seeing, visiting and being present with them even when the companions occupy higher degrees. Sharing company need not mean equality of rank. The marginal commentary adds that even one below a prophet's station may have a sort of companionship through nearness to his inward state and unveiling without being veiled from him, though he cannot aspire to the prophet's own degree. It adduces the illumination, intimacy and profit obtained by others when they inwardly perceive him. Ibn ʿAjība transmits a report that those of the higher ranks in Paradise visit the lower, but not the reverse, except that one who visited another for God's sake in this life may visit where he wishes in Paradise. The transmission of this specific report remains to be examined. He also narrates that Thawbān, the Prophet's freedman, came to him one day with changed countenance and a wasted body. Asked what was wrong, he replied that he was not physically ill: when he could not see the Prophet he felt an overwhelming longing and estrangement until they met again. He then thought of the hereafter and feared that, while the Prophet would be elevated among the prophets, he himself would either enter Paradise on a lower level or not enter it at all, and so might never see him again. The verse “Whoever obeys God and the Messenger…” was then revealed, according to the report. “This is the favour of God”: the expression includes the recompense promised to the obedient and the further gifts of nearness ( qurb ) and presence ( ḥuḍūr ). It is bestowed freely by God. He knows the degrees of works and stations and recompenses each according to his place. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_069-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_069-s3","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"","text":"Outward, bodily obedience brings sensory companionship in the bodily bliss of Paradise; inward obedience of the heart brings spiritual companionship in spiritual felicity. The one whose companionship remains merely sensory experiences separation ( farq ), while the possessor of inward companionship is gathered in unity ( jamʿ ) and never absent from the Beloved for a moment. These are the ṣiddīqūn , the brought-near; above them stand the prophets, below them the martyrs and righteous. Knowledge of God arises either through the removal of the veil and dispersal of the cloud—the cloud of created effects ( athar )—and these are the people of direct witnessing ( shuhūd ) and vision ( ʿiyān ); or from behind the veil, where seekers receive their reward beyond the doorway, proceeding from effects to the One who acts ( muʾaththir ) through evidence and demonstration. Those of the first class may attain the direct address of revelation and sight of the noble angels: these are the prophets and messengers. Others stop short of prophetic revelation, yet receive inspiration ( ilhām ): these are the ṣiddīqūn , people of spiritual states and established stations ( aḥwāl and maqāmāt ). Both share the station of direct vision, but the expanse of the Presence is immeasurable, and ascent through the mysteries of divine unity has no end. Where the saint's foot comes to rest, the prophet's ascent begins. Those behind the veil know God either through decisive demonstrations and scriptural evidences: these are the rooted scholars, corresponding in this inner classification to the station of witnesses ( shuhadāʾ ); or through discipline ( riyāḍa ), struggle ( mujāhada ) and repeated extraordinary graces ( karāmāt ): these are the worshippers and renunciants, the station of the righteous. Ordinary Muslims are joined to the latter class, for within each named station are innumerable degrees and lesser stations known fully only to the One who knows them. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_069-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_069-s4","r":"q4_cont_069","title":"","text":"The discourse now encourages striving in God's way, the immediate subject toward which the preceding directions have been leading.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_069-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_071","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity 4:71–74","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_071"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-1","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا خُذُوا حِذْرَكُمْ فَانْفِرُوا ثُباتٍ أَوِ انْفِرُوا جَمِيعاً (71) وَإِنَّ مِنْكُمْ لَمَنْ لَيُبَطِّئَنَّ فَإِنْ أَصابَتْكُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ قالَ قَدْ أَنْعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيَّ إِذْ لَمْ أَكُنْ مَعَهُمْ شَهِيداً (72) وَلَئِنْ أَصابَكُمْ فَضْلٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ لَيَقُولَنَّ كَأَنْ لَمْ تَكُنْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُ مَوَدَّةٌ يا لَيْتَنِي كُنْتُ مَعَهُمْ فَأَفُوزَ فَوْزاً عَظِيماً (73) فَلْيُقاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ الَّذِينَ يَشْرُونَ الْحَياةَ الدُّنْيا بِالْآخِرَةِ وَمَنْ يُقاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَيُقْتَلْ أَوْ يَغْلِبْ فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيهِ أَجْراً عَظِيماً (74)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-2","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"قلت: الحِذر والحَذَر واحد، كالشِّبه والشِّبَه، وبَطُأ يستعمل لازمًا بمعنى ثقل، ومتعديًا- بالتضعيف- أي: بطَّأ غيره، و (لَمَن ليبطئن) اللام الأولى للابتداء، والثانية للقسم، أي: وإنَّ منكم- أُقسم بالله- لمن ليبطئن. وجملة:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-3","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"(كأن لم يكن) : اعتراضية بين القول والمقول، تنبيهًا على ضعف عقيدتهم، وأن قولهم هذا قولُ من لا مواصلة بينكم وبينه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-4","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا تأهبوا واستعدوا لجهاد الأعداء، وخُذُوا حِذْرَكُمْ منهم بالعُدَّةِ والعَدَد، وَلاَ تُلْقُواْ بِأَيْدِيكُمْ إِلَى التهلكة، ولا حجة فيه للقدرية لأن هذا من الأسباب التي ستر الله بها أسرار القدرة. وقد قال لنبيّه- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: قُلْ لَنْ يُصِيبَنا إِلَّا ما كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَنا وقال- عليه الصلاة السلام-:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-5","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"«اعقلها وتوكل» . وفي ذلك طمأنينة للقلوب التي لم تطمئن وتشريعًا للضعفاء، فإذا تأهبتم واستعددتم فَانْفِرُوا أي: اخرجوا إلى الجهاد ثُباتٍ أي: جماعات متفرقة، سرية بعد سرية، أَوِ انْفِرُوا جَمِيعاً أي: مجتمعين مع نبيكم، أو مع أميركم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-6","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"وَإِنَّ مِنْكُمْ يا معشر المسلمين لَمَنْ لَيُبَطِّئَنَّ الناس عن الجهاد، أو ليتثاقلن ويتخلفن عنه، وهو عبد الله بن أبي المنافق، وأشباهه من المنافقين، فَإِنْ أَصابَتْكُمْ مُصِيبَةٌ كقتل أو هزيمة قالَ قَدْ أَنْعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيَّ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-7","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"حين تخلفت إِذْ لَمْ أَكُنْ مَعَهُمْ شَهِيداً فيصيبني ما أصابهم. وَلَئِنْ أَصابَكُمْ فَضْلٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ، كنصر وغنيمة، لَيَقُولَنَّ لفرط عداوته: يا لَيْتَنِي كُنْتُ مَعَهُمْ فَأَفُوزَ فَوْزاً عَظِيماً، بالمال والعز. كأن ذلك المنافق، لم يكن بينكم وبينه مودة ولا مواصلة أصلاً، حيث يتربص الدوائر، يفرح بمصيبتكم ويتحسر بعزكم ونصركم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-8","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"فإن تثاقل هذا عن القتال أو بطَّأ غيره، فَلْيُقاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أهلُ الإخلاص والإيمان الَّذِينَ يَشْرُونَ، أي: يبيعون الْحَياةَ الدُّنْيا بِالْآخِرَةِ، فيؤثرون الآخرة الباقية على الدنيا الفانية، وَمَنْ يُقاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ لإعلاء كلمة الله فَيُقْتَلْ شهيدًا أَوْ يَغْلِبْ عدوه وينصره الله فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيهِ أَجْراً عَظِيماً، وإنما قال تعالى: فَيُقْتَلْ أَوْ يَغْلِبْ تنبيهًا على أن المجاهد ينبغي أن يثبت في المعركة، حتى يعز نفسه بالشهادة، أو الدين بالظفر والنصر. وألا يكون قصده بالذات القتل، بل إعلاء الحق وإعزاز الدين. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-9","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"الإشارة: يا أيها الذين آمنوا إيمان الخصوص خذوا حذركم من خدع النفوس، لئلا تعوقكم عن حضرة القدوس، فانفروا إلى جهادها ثُباتٍ أو جماعة «فإن يد الله مع الجماعة» ، فالصحبة عند الصوفية شرط مؤكد وأمر محتم. والله ما أفلح مَن أفلح إلا بصحبة مَن أفلح، فالنفس الحية لا تموت مع الأحياء، وإنما تموت مع الأموات، فهي كالحوت ما دامت في البحر مع الحيتان لا تموت أبدًا، فإذا أخرجتها وعزلتها عن أبناء جنسها ماتت سريعًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-10","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"كما قال شيخنا رضي الله عنه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-11","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"وإن من نفوسكم لمن ليبطئنكم عن السير إلى حضرة قدسكم، تفر من مواطن الشدة والمحن، وفى ذلك حياتها لو تعقل وتفطن، فإن أصابتكم- أهل النسبة- نكبة، أو تعرف من التعرفات، ولم يصادفها فى ذلك الوقت شىء من تلك النكبات، قال: قد أنعم الله علىّ إذ لم أكن معهم شهيدًا، ولئن أصابكم بعد ذلك فضل من الله كنفحات ربانية وخمرات أزلية، قالت: يا ليتني كنتُ معهم فأفوز كما فازوا، فليجاهد نفسه في سبيل الله من أراد الظفر بحضرة الله، يقدمها إلى المكاره، وهو كل ما يثقل عليها، ويجنبها الشهوات، وهو كل ما يخف عليها، هكذا يسير معها ويقاتلها، حتى يموت أو يغلبها ويظفر بها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-12","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"قال بعض المشايخ: انتهى سير السائرين إلى الظفر بنفوسهم. فإن ظفروا بها وصلوا. هـ. وحينئذ تذهب عنه المتاعب والأنكاد، وتصير الأزمنة كلها عنده مواسم وأعياد، ويقال له حينئذ:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-13","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"لك الدهر طوع والأنام عبيد ... فعش كل يوم من أيامك عيد","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-14","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"ويقال له أيضا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-15","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"بَدَا لَكَ سِرٌّ طَالَ عَنْكَ اكْتتَامُهُ ... وَلاَحَ صَبَاحُ كُنْتَ أنْتَ ظَلاَمُهُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-16","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"فَأنْتَ حِجَابُ القَلْبِ عَنْ سِرِّ غَيبهِ ... وَلَوْلاَكَ لَمْ يُطْبَعْ عليه ختامه","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-17","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"إذا غِبْتَ عَنْهُ حَلَّ فِيهِ وَطَنَّبَتْ (١) ... عَلَى مَوْكبِ الكَشْفِ المصُونِ خِيَامُهُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-18","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"وَجَاء حَدِيثٌ لا يُمَلُّ سَمَاعُهُ ... شَهِيٌّ إليْنَا نَثْرُهُ وَنِظَامُهُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-19","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"إذَا سَمِعَتْهُ النَّفْسُ طَابَ نَعِيمُهَا ... وَزَالَ عَنِ القَلْبِ المُعَنَّى غرامه (٢)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_071-20","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"4:71–74 · Vigilance, the reluctant self, and the struggle for sincerity","text":"ثم عاتب العباد على عدم النهوض إلى الجهاد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_071-20"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_071-s1","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"Language (*qultu*)","text":"The words ḥidhr and ḥadhar (“caution”) are variants, like shibh and shabah . The verb baṭuʾa is intransitive, “to be slow, heavy”; the doubled form baṭṭaʾa is transitive, “to delay another.” In la-man la-yubaṭṭiʾanna the first lām emphasizes the opening of the statement, while the second indicates an oath: “Among you—by God, I swear—is one who will certainly cause delay.” The phrase ka-an lam yakun baynakum wa-baynahu mawadda (“as though there had never been any affection between you and him”) is parenthetic between the verb “he will say” and the saying reported, drawing attention to the shallowness of his attachment to the believers.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_071-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_071-s2","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"","text":"God tells believers to prepare themselves for the struggle against their enemies, taking every precaution of equipment and numbers rather than casting themselves to destruction. The text, says Ibn ʿAjība, offers no proof for the view he attributes to the Qadarites, because precaution is one of the causes with which God veils the mysteries of divine power. The Prophet himself was told that nothing would befall the believers except what God had decreed, and the saying “Tie it and place your trust [in God]” brings tranquillity to hearts not yet at rest and gives a practical ordinance to those whose faith is weak. Having prepared, believers may go forth in separate units, expedition following expedition ( thubāt ), or together with the Prophet or their commander. Among those outwardly counted with Muslims, however, were the hypocrite ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubayy and others of his kind. Such a person either holds others back from fighting or becomes sluggish and declines to go. If killing or defeat befalls the believers, he rejoices that God spared him by keeping him away from the battle. If they receive victory and spoils, he regrets not being there, wishing for the wealth and worldly honour they gained. Despite the affection he professes, his conduct is that of an estranged enemy: he waits for calamities to strike them, delights in their adversity, and grieves at their success. If such a person hangs back or hinders others, the people of genuine faith and sincerity should be the ones to struggle in God's way. They “sell the life of this world for the hereafter,” preferring what endures to what passes away. Whoever contends to make God's word uppermost, whether he is killed as a martyr or God grants him victory, receives a mighty reward. Ibn ʿAjība, following al-Bayḍāwī, draws attention to the wording “is killed or prevails”: the participant must remain steadfast, honouring himself through martyrdom if it occurs, or honouring the religion through victory. His immediate purpose should not be his own death, but the manifestation of the truth and the honour of the religion.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_071-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_071-s3","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"","text":"“O you who believe with the faith of the elect, take precautions against the deceits of your lower souls ( nufūs ), lest they prevent you from reaching the holy Presence. Go forth against them in detachments or together.” He adduces the saying that God's hand is with the community, emphasizing the condition of companionship ( ṣuḥba ) in Sufi training. The people of the path say that no one attains success without keeping company with someone who has attained it. A living ego-self does not die while living among ego-selves; it dies in the company of those who are themselves dead to selfishness. A fish remains alive while still in the water with other fish, but if removed from its element it quickly dies. Ibn ʿAjība says this image came from his own shaykh. Within each of you is a self that delays departure toward the sanctity of the Presence. It flees places of hardship and trial, although there, if it understood, lies its true life. When members of the path meet a reversal or a severe manifestation of divine dealing ( taʿarruf ), while that self has escaped it, it congratulates itself on having been spared. If later the people of the path receive divine breaths ( nafaḥāt rabbāniyya ) and the wine-like delights of eternity, it wishes it had joined them and attained their success. Whoever desires victory in reaching the Presence should set his soul to endure what it dislikes and withhold from it the desires it finds easy. He proceeds in this struggle until he dies or conquers the ego and so obtains mastery over it. A shaykh said that the course of wayfarers ends in victory over their lower selves: when they conquer those selves, they arrive. Burdens and afflictions then depart, and every season becomes a festival. Ibn ʿAjība cites verses: Time becomes obedient to you and humankind your servants; live each day of your days as a feast. And further poetry: A secret has appeared to you whose concealment from you endured so long; a dawn has gleamed whose darkness you yourself had been. You are the veil upon the heart, concealing the mystery of its unseen; but for you, its seal would never have been impressed upon it. When you vanish from the heart, the secret settles in it, and its tents are pitched above the guarded procession of unveiling. Then comes a discourse never wearisome to hear, lovely to us in its prose and its measured verse. When the soul hears it, its delight becomes sweet, and the afflicted heart is relieved of its consuming passion.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_071-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_071-s4","r":"q4_cont_071","title":"","text":"God next reproves the servants for not rising to the defence of the weak.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_071-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_075","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self 4:75","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_075"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-1","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"وَما لَكُمْ لا تُقاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَالْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ مِنَ الرِّجالِ وَالنِّساءِ وَالْوِلْدانِ الَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنا أَخْرِجْنا مِنْ هذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ الظَّالِمِ أَهْلُها وَاجْعَلْ لَنا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا وَاجْعَلْ لَنا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ نَصِيراً (75)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-2","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"قلت: (ما) مبتدأ. و (لكم) خبر. و (لا تقاتلون) حال، و (المستضعفين) عطف على اسم الجلالة، أي: أي شيء حصل لكم حال كونكم غير مجاهدين في سبيل الله وفي تخليص المستضعفين؟ و (الظالم) نعت للقرية، وإنما ذُكَّر ولم يؤنث، لأنه أسند إلى المذكر، واسم الفاعل إذا جرى على غير مَن هُوَ لَهُ أجرى مجرى الفعل، فيذكر ويؤنث باعتبار الفاعل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-3","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَما لَكُمْ يا معشر المسلمين لا تُقاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، وفي تخليص إخوانكم الْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ بمكة، الذين حبسهم العدو أو أسرهم ومنعهم من الهجرة مِنَ الرِّجالِ وَالنِّساءِ وَالْوِلْدانِ، فهم في أيديهم مغللون ممتحنون. قال البيضاوي: وإنما ذكر الولدان مبالغة في الحث وتنبيهًا على تناهي ظلم المشركين بحيث بلغ أذاهم الصبيان، وأن دعوتهم أجيبت بسبب مشاركتهم في الدعاء، حتى تشاركوا في استنزال الرحمة واستدفاع البلية. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-4","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"ثم ذكر دعاءهم فقال: الَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنا أَخْرِجْنا مِنْ هذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ أي: مكة الظَّالِمِ أَهْلُها بالشرك والطغيان حتى تعدى إلى النساء والصبيان. وَاجْعَلْ لَنا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا يصوننا عن أذاهم، وَنَصِيراً يمنعنا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-5","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"من التخلف عن الهجرة إلى رسولك صلّى الله عليه وسلم، فاستجاب الله دعاءهم بأن يسَّر لبعضهم الخروج إلى المدينة، وجعل لمن بقي منهم أعظم ولي وناصر، بفتح مكة على نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم، فتولاهم ونصرهم، واستعمل عليهم عتَّاب بن أسيد، فحماهم وأعزهم حتى صاروا أعزاء أهلها، كما هي عادته سبحانه في إجابة دعاء المضطرين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-6","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"الإشارة: ما لكم يا معشر العِباد، وخصوصًا المريدين من أهل الجد والاجتهاد، لا تجاهدون نفوسكم في طريق الوصول إلى الله، كي تنالوا بذلك مشاهدة جماله وسناه، وتخلصوا ما كمن في نفوسكم من الأسرار، وما احتوت عليه من العلوم والأنوار. فإن قرية البشرية قد احتوت عليها وأسرتها بظلمات شهواتها، واستضعفتها بتراكم غفلتها وتكثيف حجاب حسها. فمن جاهدها استخلص جواهر تلك العلوم والأسرار مِن صَدَفِها. وفي ذلك يقول ابن البنا في مباحثه:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-7","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"وَلَمْ تزل كُلُّ النُّفُوسِ الأحيا ... عَلاَّمة درَّاكة للأشيَا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-8","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"وَإِنَّمَا تَعُوقُها الأبدَان ... وَالأَنْفُسُ النُّزَّعُ والشَّيطَان","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-9","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"فكلُّ مَن أذاقهم جهادَه ... أظهرَ لِلْقَاعِدِ خَرقَ الْعَادَهْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-10","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"وقال أيضًا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-11","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"وَهِيَ مِن النفوس في كُمُون ... كما يكون الحَبُّ في الغُصُون.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-12","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"فالرجال: الأسرار والأنوار، والنساء: العلوم والأذكار، والولدان: الحكم بنات الأفكار. فكل هؤلاء مستضعفون تحت قهر البشرية الظالم أهلها. من الأنفس النزع والشياطين المغوية، فكل من جاهد هؤلاء القواطع أظهر تلك العلوم والأنوار السواطع، واستخلص رُوحه من أسر حجاب الأكوان، وأفضى إلى فضاء الشهود والعيان. وبالله التوفيق. وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_075-13","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"4:75 · The oppressed and the spiritual treasures held captive within the self","text":"ثم حثّ أولياءه من أهل الإيمان أن يقاتلوا أولياء الشيطان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_075-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_075-s1","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"","text":"The interrogative mā is the initial nominal subject ( mubtadaʾ ); lakum (“with you”) is its predicate ( khabar ); “while you do not fight” is a circumstance ( ḥāl ). “The oppressed” ( al-mustaḍʿafīn ) is coordinated with the divine name, in the sense: what has befallen you that you do not struggle in God's way and for the deliverance of the oppressed? The adjective al-ẓālim (“unjust”) qualifies “town” ( qarya ) but stands in the masculine because its grammatical agent is the masculine noun ahl (“its inhabitants”). When an active participle is predicated through a noun other than its actual agent it behaves like a verb, agreeing in gender by reference to the agent.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_075-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_075-s2","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"","text":"God asks the Muslims why they do not fight in His way and liberate their weak brothers and sisters left in Mecca. Those people have been detained or captured by enemies and prevented from migrating; they include men, women, and children, bound and tormented in their hands. Al-Bayḍāwī says that naming the children intensifies the appeal and indicates how far the idolaters' wrongdoing reached, even harming children. It also shows that the oppressed people's prayer was answered because the children joined in it, so that all shared in asking for mercy to descend and for affliction to be averted. Those oppressed people cry: “Our Lord, bring us forth from this town”—Mecca—“whose inhabitants are unjust” through idolatry and aggression, reaching even women and children. “Appoint for us a protector” who will safeguard us from their harm, and a “helper” to free us from being held back from migration to Your Messenger. God answered by opening a way for some to leave for Medina. For those who remained, He ultimately appointed the greatest protector and helper through the conquest of Mecca granted to His Prophet. The Prophet supported them and placed ʿAttāb ibn Asīd in authority over them. He protected and honoured them until they became honoured members of the city. Such, Ibn ʿAjība says, is God's custom in answering the supplications of people in dire need.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_075-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_075-s3","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"","text":"Why, he asks the worshippers—and especially striving aspirants ( murīdūn )—do you not contend against your own selves on the path of arrival at God, so that you may behold His beauty and radiance, and rescue the secrets concealed within you and the knowledge and lights which the self contains? The “town of corporeal humanity” ( qaryat al-bashariyya ) has captured these treasures, shrouding them beneath the darkness of its appetites, weakening them through layers of heedlessness and the thick veil of sensible appearance ( ḥiss ). Whoever contends against it extracts the jewels of knowledge and spiritual mysteries from their shell. He cites Ibn al-Bannāʾ's Mabāḥith : All living souls have ever been knowing, endowed with discernment of the things; it is bodies that hinder them, and souls that pull backward, and Satan. Whoever gives them the taste of his struggle shows even the one who sat still a breach in ordinary habit. And another of Ibn al-Bannāʾ's couplets: These [knowledges] lie concealed within the souls, as kernels lie concealed within branches. In this allusion, the men are spiritual mysteries and lights ( asrār and anwār ); the women are branches of knowledge and remembrances ( ʿulūm and adhkār ); and the children are wisdoms born as daughters of reflection ( ḥikam banāt al-afkār ). All are oppressed beneath the coercion of the human self, whose inhabitants are unjust—the regressive souls and tempting devils. Whoever struggles against these obstructing influences makes the sciences and bright lights emerge, frees the spirit from imprisonment within the veil of created beings, and reaches the open space of witnessing and direct vision. God guides to the even path.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_075-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_075-s4","r":"q4_cont_075","title":"","text":"Believers are next urged to strive against the allies of Satan.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_075-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_076","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"4:76 · Fighting for God rather than for the *ṭāghūt*: the test of intention","text":"4:76 · Fighting for God rather than for the *ṭāghūt*: the test of intention 4:76","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_076"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_076-1","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"4:76 · Fighting for God rather than for the *ṭāghūt*: the test of intention","text":"الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا يُقاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يُقاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ الطَّاغُوتِ فَقاتِلُوا أَوْلِياءَ الشَّيْطانِ إِنَّ كَيْدَ الشَّيْطانِ كانَ ضَعِيفاً (76)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_076-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_076-2","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"4:76 · Fighting for God rather than for the *ṭāghūt*: the test of intention","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في مدح المخلصين: الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا يُقاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، وابتغاء مرضات الله، وإعلاء لكلمة الله، وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا، من أهل مكة وغيرهم، يُقاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ الطَّاغُوتِ وهو","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_076-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_076-3","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"4:76 · Fighting for God rather than for the *ṭāghūt*: the test of intention","text":"الشيطان، فَقاتِلُوا يا أولياء الله أَوْلِياءَ الشَّيْطانِ ولا يهولكم كيده إِنَّ كَيْدَ الشَّيْطانِ كانَ ضَعِيفاً، وكيد الله للكافرين كان قويًا متينًا، فلا تخافوا أولياءه، فإنهم اعتمدوا على أضعف شيء وأوهنه، وأنتم اعتمدتم على أقوى شيء وأمتَنِه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_076-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_076-4","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"4:76 · Fighting for God rather than for the *ṭāghūt*: the test of intention","text":"الإشارة: كل ما سوى الله طاغوت، فمن قصد بجهاده أو عمله رضى الله والوصول إلى حضرته دون شيء سواه، كان من أولياء الله، ومن قصد بجهاده أو أعماله حظًا دنيويًا أو أخرويًا خرج من دائرة الولاية، فإما أن يكون مع عامة أهل الإيمان، أو من أولياء الشيطان. قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «إنَّما الأعمَالُ بالنيات، وإنما لكلّ امرئ مَا نَوَى، فمن كانَت هجرَتُه إلى الله ورسولِه فهجرتُه إلى اللهْ ورسولِه، ومن كانت هجرتُه إلى دُنيا يُصيبهُا أو امرأةٍ ينكِحُها، فهجرتُه إلى ما هَاجَرَ إليه» . وقال في الحِكَم: «لا ترحل من كَونٍ إلى كَونٍ، فتكون كحمار الرحى، يسير والذي ارتحل منه هو الذي ارتحل إليه، ولكن ارحل من الأكوانِ إلى المُكَوِّنِ، وَأَنَّ إِلى رَبِّكَ الْمُنْتَهى» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_076-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_076-5","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"4:76 · Fighting for God rather than for the *ṭāghūt*: the test of intention","text":"ثم عاتب الحقّ جل جلاله قوما طلبوا فرض الجهاد، فلما فرض عليهم خطر ببالهم شىء من طبع البشر، الذي هو الخوف من الموت، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_076-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_076-s1","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"","text":"God praises the sincere believers who fight seeking His good pleasure and to exalt His word. The unbelievers—among the people of Mecca and elsewhere—fight for the ṭāghūt , identified here as Satan. Thus the allies of God should resist the allies of Satan and not be overawed by Satan's plans. His device is weak, whereas God's counteraction against unbelievers is powerful and unshakable. The allies of Satan rest their hopes on what is weakest and most frail; the believers have placed their dependence on what is strongest and most enduring.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_076-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_076-s2","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"","text":"Everything other than God is a ṭāghūt . One whose struggle or other acts aim at God's pleasure and arrival in His Presence, without seeking anything besides Him, belongs to the friends of God ( awliyāʾ Allāh ). One whose fighting or work aims instead at some worldly gain—or even at a self-regarding reward in the hereafter—has left the circle of the elect saintly station and belongs either among believers at large or among those whose allegiance is to Satan, according to his intention. [Translator’s note: The description is a searching critique of spiritual motivation, not a declaration that all ordinary hopes for reward amount legally to unbelief.] Ibn ʿAjība cites the Prophet's saying: “Works are only according to intentions, and each person has only what he intended. So whoever's migration was to God and His Messenger, his migration is to God and His Messenger; and whoever's migration was to a worldly thing he would obtain or a woman he would marry, his migration is to that for which he migrated.” He also quotes Ibn ʿAṭāʾ Allāh's Ḥikam : “Do not journey from one created being ( kawn ) to another, lest you be like the mill-donkey: it goes on walking while the place it left is the very place to which it comes. Instead journey from created things ( akwān ) to their Originator ( al-Mukawwin ): ‘To your Lord is the final destination’ [Q 53:42].”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_076-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_076-s3","r":"q4_cont_076","title":"","text":"God then reproves those who had sought the imposition of fighting but, when it was prescribed, experienced the human temperament's fear of death.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_076-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_077","r":"q4_cont_077","title":"4:77 · When the command to fight comes: human fear and the smallness of this world","text":"4:77 · When the command to fight comes: human fear and the smallness of this world 4:77","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_077"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_077-1","r":"q4_cont_077","title":"4:77 · When the command to fight comes: human fear and the smallness of this world","text":"أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ قِيلَ لَهُمْ كُفُّوا أَيْدِيَكُمْ وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكاةَ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتالُ إِذا فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ يَخْشَوْنَ النَّاسَ كَخَشْيَةِ اللَّهِ أَوْ أَشَدَّ خَشْيَةً وَقالُوا رَبَّنا لِمَ كَتَبْتَ عَلَيْنَا الْقِتالَ لَوْلا أَخَّرْتَنا إِلى أَجَلٍ قَرِيبٍ قُلْ مَتاعُ الدُّنْيا قَلِيلٌ وَالْآخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِمَنِ اتَّقى وَلا تُظْلَمُونَ فَتِيلاً (77)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_077-1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_077-s1","r":"q4_cont_077","title":"","text":"Aw ashadda (“or more intense”) is coordinated with the comparative kāf which stands in the place of an implied verbal noun: “a fear like fear of God, or a greater fear.” Here the verbal noun is in a genitive construction with its object; the underlying meaning is “as they fear God.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_077-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_077-s2","r":"q4_cont_077","title":"","text":"God points out a group who had eagerly requested that the Prophet make fighting obligatory for them. They had then been told, through the Messenger, to keep their hands from fighting until it was commanded and to occupy themselves with their current duties of prayer and almsgiving. But when battle was actually enjoined, fear entered their hearts. Some now feared being killed by enemy people as intensely as they feared God's punishment—or more. They inwardly cried out, “Why has fighting been commanded at this very time? Could You not postpone it for a little while, so that we may enjoy our lives, or until our appointed deaths arrive?” Ibn ʿAjība introduces an interpretive caution: if these verses concern the Companions, it seems to him that the words were thoughts passing through their hearts , not objections they pronounced aloud. If they concern hypocrites, however, it is possible they spoke them explicitly. God replies that this world's enjoyment is little, its livelihood abject, and its term near, whereas the hereafter is better and longer-lasting for the one who is God-fearing. They will return to their Master, who will honour their dwelling and give them the full reward of their actions. Not a fatīl , the fine fibre or thread of a date-stone, will be subtracted from their reward; nor will their allotted lifespans be diminished whether they fight or remain seated.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_077-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_077-s3","r":"q4_cont_077","title":"Interpretive continuation","text":"The commentary extends directly into the opening of verse 78, where Ibn ʿAjība supplies both an account of its occasion and the spiritual application of this earlier reproach. The next unit keeps this original textual sequence rather than inventing a separate ishāra in verse 77.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_077-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_078","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet 4:78","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_078"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-1","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"أَيْنَما تَكُونُوا يُدْرِكْكُمُ الْمَوْتُ وَلَوْ كُنْتُمْ فِي بُرُوجٍ مُشَيَّدَةٍ ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-2","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"قلت: (أو أشد) عطف على الكاف النائبة عن المصدر، أي: خشيةً مثل خشية الله أو أشد، وهو من إضافة المصدر إلى المفعول، أي: مثل خشيتهم الله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-3","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أَلَمْ تَرَ يا محمد إِلَى الَّذِينَ طلبوا منك فرضَ الجهاد حرصًا على أن يجاهدوا، فقيل لهم على لسان الرسول: كُفُّوا أَيْدِيَكُمْ عنه إلى أوَانِ فَرضِه، واشتغلوا بما أُمِرتم به من إقامة الصلاة وإيتاء الزكاة، فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتالُ دخلهم الخوف إِذا فَرِيقٌ مِنْهُمْ يَخْشَوْنَ النَّاسَ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-4","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"الكفار، أن يقتلوهم مثل خشية عقاب اللَّهِ أو أشد خشية منه. وَقالُوا رَبَّنا لِمَ كَتَبْتَ عَلَيْنَا الْقِتالَ في هذا الوقت لَوْلا: هلاّ أَخَّرْتَنا إِلى أَجَلٍ قَرِيبٍ نتمتع فيه بحياتنا أو إلى أن نموت بآجالنا. قلت: والظاهر أنهم قالوا ذلك في نفوسهم، خواطر خطرت لهم، ولم يفوهوا به، إن نزلت فى الصحابة- رضي الله عنهم-، وإن كانت في المنافقين فيمكن أن ينطقوا بها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-5","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"قُلْ مَتاعُ الدُّنْيا قَلِيلٌ وعيشها ذليل، وأجلها قريب، وَالْآخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِمَنِ اتَّقى، وحياتها خير وأبقى، وسَتَقدُمون على مولاكم، فيكرم مثواكم، ويوفيكم جزاء أعمالكم، وَلا تُظْلَمُونَ فَتِيلًا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-6","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"من ثواب أعمالكم، ولا تنقصون من أيام أعماركم، جاهدتم أو قعدتم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-8","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"أَيْنَما تَكُونُوا يُدْرِكْكُمُ الْمَوْتُ عند انقضاء آجالكم، وَلَوْ كُنْتُمْ فِي بُرُوجٍ مُشَيَّدَةٍ عالية محصنة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-9","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"فإن كان الموت لا بد منه ففي الجهاد أفضل، لأنه حياة لا موتَ بعده. قال الكلبي: نزلت في قوم من الصحابة، منهم: عبد الرحمن بن عوف، والمِقدادُ وقُدامة بن مَظعون وغيرهم، كانوا يُؤذَونَ بمكة، ويستأذنون النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم في القتال، فيقول لهم: كفوا أيديكم حتى يُؤذن فيه لكم، فلما هاجروا إلى المدينة وأُمروا به، كرهه بعضهم كراهية الطبع البشري، فخطر ببالهم شيءٌ مما حكى الله عنهم. فلما كانوا في عين العناية ومحل القرب والهداية عوقبوا على تلك الخواطر، ولو كان غيرهم من أهل البُعد لسُومح له في ذلك، وقيل: نزلت في قوم من المؤمنين أُمروا بالجهاد فنافقوا من الجُبن، وتخلفوا عن الجهاد، وهذا أليق بما بعده من قوله: إِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ حَسَنَةٌ. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-10","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"الإشارة: نرى بعض الفقراء يبطشون إلى مقام التجريد ومجاهدة نفوسهم قبل كمال يقينهم، فإذا أُمِروا بذلك، ورأوا ميادين الحروب واشتعال نيران قتل النفوس، وأمروا بالصبر على المكاره، من مواجهة الإنكار ولحوق الذل والافتقار، جبنوا وكلَّوا ورجعوا القهقرى، فيقال لهم: متاعُ الدنيا قليل وعزيزها ذليل، وغنيها فقير، وكبيرها حقير، وما تنالون من الله في جزاء مجاهدتكم خيرٌ وأبقى، ولا تُظلمون فتيلاً من مجاهدتكم لنفوسكم، فلو صبرتم لفزتم بالوصول إلى حضرة ربكم، فلما جبُنتُم ورجعتم، كان جزاؤكم الحرمان، عما ظفر به أهل العرفان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-11","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"وفي مثل هؤلاء يقول ابن الفارض رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-12","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"تعرّضَ قومٌ للغرامِ وأعرَضوا ... بجانبهم عن صحّتي فيه واعتلّوا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-13","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"رضوا بالأماني، وابُتُلوا بحظُوظهم ... وخاضوا بحارَ الحبّ، دعوى، فما ابتلّوا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-14","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"فهُم في السُّرى لم يَبرَحوا من مكانهم ... وما ظَعَنوا في السير عنه، وقد كلَّوا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-15","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"ثم حكى مقالتهم الدالة على نفاقهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_078-16","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"4:78 · Death cannot be evaded; good and bad fortune ascribed to the Prophet","text":"... وَإِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ حَسَنَةٌ يَقُولُوا هذِهِ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ وَإِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَقُولُوا هذِهِ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ قُلْ كُلٌّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ فَمالِ هؤُلاءِ الْقَوْمِ لا يَكادُونَ يَفْقَهُونَ حَدِيثاً (78)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_078-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_078-s1","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"The outward interpretation, continuing 4:77","text":"Death will meet people at the expiration of their appointed terms, even if they fortify themselves in high and defended towers. Since death is unavoidable, the commentary says, dying in God's path is preferable: it is a life after which there is no death. Al-Kalbī reports that the earlier reproach concerned certain Companions, among them ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, al-Miqdād and Qudāma ibn Maẓʿūn. They suffered mistreatment in Mecca and asked permission to fight, but the Prophet instructed them to restrain their hands until permission came. After the emigration to Medina and the subsequent command, some felt a natural human aversion to fighting, and thoughts of the kind mentioned in the verse passed through their minds. Because they occupied, says Ibn ʿAjība, a place of divine care and closeness, even those thoughts met with rebuke; others further away would have been excused them. Another report says the verses concern believers whose cowardice led them to behave hypocritically and refuse the struggle. Ibn ʿAjība thinks this reading better suits the subsequent reference to those who attribute misfortune to the Prophet. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_078-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_078-s2","r":"q4_cont_078","title":", arising from 4:77","text":"Some fuqarāʾ strive eagerly for tajrīd —stripping away worldly attachments—and combat with their selves before their certainty is fully formed. When they are actually directed to that way and see the battlefields and the fires of slaying egoic desires, and are called to patience under painful things—being criticized, shamed, brought low and reduced to poverty—they grow timid and exhausted and retreat. To them it is said: The world is little; its honoured person is abased, its wealthy person is poor, its great person is insignificant. What God grants as recompense for struggling against oneself is better and more lasting. Not a thread's weight of their striving will be lost. Had they remained patient, they would have arrived in the Presence of their Lord; having retreated in cowardice, their recompense is exclusion from what the people of realized knowing attain. Ibn ʿAjība quotes Ibn al-Fāriḍ: Some exposed themselves to love, then turned aside from my health in it, and made excuses. They were content with mere wishes and were tried by their own shares; they crossed the seas of love in claim—yet never became wet. On the night journey they never left their place; they did not depart from it upon the road, for they grew weary. Translator’s note: Al-Būrīnī, in his commentary on this poem ( Sharḥ Dīwān Ibn al-Fāriḍ , II:161–162), explains “my health” as steadfastness in love, and iʿtallū as offering reasons for turning away. The verb also means “fell ill,” allowing a possible play on health and illness.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_078-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_078-s3","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"The outward interpretation, concerning the remainder of 4:78","text":"God now reports a saying that exposes the hypocrites. If they encounter prosperity, abundant crops and manifest blessings, they say that these come from God directly. But if they suffer drought, hunger, deaths or killing, they tell the Messenger that this is due to the ill omen of his arrival and the arrival of his Companions. Ibn ʿAjība attributes a similar accusation to some Jews of Medina: since Muḥammad entered the city, they allegedly said, its fruit diminished and prices rose. The commentator answers indignantly that its fruit rather flourished, prices became favourable, its lights shone and its mysteries appeared. The Prophet had prayed for Medina for blessings like those Abraham prayed for Mecca, and several times as much. Ibn ʿAjība says its blessings have continued to arrive, sensible and spiritual, until the Day of Resurrection. Other peoples used the same language about their prophets: Ṣāliḥ's people claimed an evil omen from him and his companions [Q 27:47], and Pharaoh's people took bad events as omens from Moses and his followers [Q 7:131]. The Qurʾān declares that earlier messengers were subjected to comparable accusations [cf. Q 41:43]. “Say: All is from God”: the good comes by His generosity and the adverse by His justice. Those who fail to understand this are reproved as being like cattle, or more straying still; they do not comprehend or ponder the Qurʾānic address. Were they to reflect, they would recognise God as Creator and determiner of everything.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_078-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_078-s4","r":"q4_cont_078","title":"Transition to 4:79","text":"Ibn ʿAjība then distinguishes the metaphysical statement that all is from God from an adab of speech: attribute perfections directly to God, but attribute deficiencies to the baleful effects of one's sins. He begins expounding “Whatever good befalls you is from God” and notes that a servant's obedience could never adequately repay even one divine blessing. He cites the Prophet: “None of you will enter Paradise by his deed.” When asked, “Not even you, Messenger of God?” he replied, “Not even I, unless God enfolds me in His mercy.” The remainder of this explanation continues with verse 79 in the next unit.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_078-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_079","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger 4:79–80","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_079"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-1","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"مَّآ أَصابَكَ مِنْ حَسَنَةٍ فَمِنَ اللَّهِ وَما أَصابَكَ مِنْ سَيِّئَةٍ فَمِنْ نَفْسِكَ ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-2","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في وصف أهل النفاق: وإنهم إن تُصِبْهُمْ حَسَنَةٌ كخصب ورخاء ونعمة ظاهرة، قالوا: هذِهِ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ، ونسبوها إلى الله بلا واسطة، وَإِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ كقحط وجوع وموت وقتل، قالوا للرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: هذِهِ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ بشؤم قدومك أنت وأصحابك، كما قالت اليهود- لعنهم الله-: منذ دخل محمدٌ المدينة نقصت ثمارها وغلت أسعارها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-3","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"قلت: بل زكت ثمارها، ورخصت أسعارها، وأشرقت أنوارها، ولاحت أسرارها، وقد دعا صلّى الله عليه وسلم للمدينة بمثل ما دعا إبراهيمُ لمكة، وأضعاف ذلك، فما زالت الخيرات تترادف إليها حسًا ومعنى إلى يوم القيامة، وهذه المقالة قد صدرت ممن كان قبلهم فقد قالوا لسيدنا صالح عليه السلام: قالُوا اطَّيَّرْنا بِكَ وَبِمَنْ مَعَكَ، وقال تعالى: وَإِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَطَّيَّرُوا بِمُوسى وَمَنْ مَعَهُ، مَّا يُقالُ لَكَ إِلَّا مَا قَدْ قِيلَ لِلرُّسُلِ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ. قال تعالى مكذبًا لهم: قُلْ كُلٌّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ الحسنة بفضله، والسيئة بعدله. ثم عيرهم بالجهل فقال: فَمالِ هؤُلاءِ الْقَوْمِ لا يَكادُونَ يَفْقَهُونَ حَدِيثاً فهُم كالبهائم أو أضل سبيلاً، أو لا يفقهون القرآن ويتدبرون حديثه، ولو تدبروا لعلموا أن الكل من عند الله، وأنه خالق كل شيء، المقدَّر لكل شيء.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-4","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"ثم علَّمنا الأدب بنسبة الكمالات إليه سبحانه بلا واسطة، ونسبة النقائص إلى شؤم ذنوبنا، فقال: مَّآ أَصابَكَ مِنْ حَسَنَةٍ أي: نعمة فَمِنَ اللَّهِ فضلاً وإحسانًا، وأما طاعة العبد فلا تفي بشكر نعمة واحدة، ولذلك قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «لَن يَدخلَ أحدُكُمُ الجنةَ بعملهِ» ، قيل: ولا أنتَ يا رسول الله؟ قال: «ولا أَنَا، إِلاَّ أنْ يتغمدنى الله برحمته» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-6","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"وَما أَصابَكَ أيها الإنسان مِنْ سَيِّئَةٍ أي: بلية فَمِنْ نَفْسِكَ أي: شؤم ذنبك، وعنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أنه قال: «ما من خَدشٍ بعُود ولا اختلاج عرق ولا غيره إلا بذنب، وما يعفو الله عنه أكثرُ» . فلا ينافي قوله: قُلْ كُلٌّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ فإن الكل منه إيجاداً واختراعًا، غير أن الحسنة إحسانٌ، والسيئة مُجَازاة وانتقام. كما قالت عائشة- رضى الله عنها-: «مَا مِن مُسلمٍ يُصيبه وَصَبٌ ولا نَصَبٌ، حتى الشوكة يُشَاكها، وحتى انقطاع شِسع نَعلهِ، إلا بذنب، وما يعفو الله عنه أكثر» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-7","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"وفي مصحف ابن مسعود: (قالوا مَّآ أَصَابَكَ مِنْ حَسَنَةٍ فمن الله) الآية، فتكون حينئٍذ من مقالة المنافقين، والآيتان كما ترى لا حجة فيها للمعتزلة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-8","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"الإشارة: ثلاث خصال لا ينجو منها إلا القليل كما في الحديث: الطيرة، والحسد، والظن. فقال- عليه الصلاة السلام: «إذا تَطَيَّرتَ فامضِ، وإذا حسدتَ فلا تبغ، وإذا ظننت فلا تُحَقّق» . فيتأكد على المريد أن يتطهر من هذه الخصال، ويصفي مشربه من التوحيد، فلا يرى في الوجود إلا مولاه، ولا ينسب التأثير إلى شيء سواه، إذا رأى نعمة به أو بغيره، قال: من الله، وإذا رأى مصيبة كذلك تأدب مع الله، فيعتقد في قلبه أنها من قَدَرِ الله، يقول:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-9","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"قُلْ كُلٌّ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ، وينسب النقص إلى نفسه وهواه، فالنفس والشيطان مناديل الحضرة، تمسح فيهما أوساخ الأقدار، وَرَبُّكَ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشاءُ وَيَخْتارُ. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-10","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"ثم شَهِدَ جلّ جلاله لرسوله بالرسالة، تحريضًا على تعظيمه وحثًا على طاعته، وترهيبًا من سوء الأدب معه، كما صدر من المنافقين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-11","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"... وَأَرْسَلْناكَ لِلنَّاسِ رَسُولاً وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ شَهِيداً (79) مَنْ يُطِعِ الرَّسُولَ فَقَدْ أَطاعَ اللَّهَ وَمَنْ تَوَلَّى فَما أَرْسَلْناكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيظاً (80)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-12","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"قلت: إن تعلق الجار بالفعل كان (رسولاً) حال مؤكدة، وإن تعلق بالاسم كان حالاً مؤسسة تفيد العموم أي أرسلناك رسولاً للناس جميعًا، و (حفيظًا) حال من الكاف.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-13","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَأَرْسَلْناكَ يا محمد لِلنَّاسِ رَسُولًا تعلمهم التوحيد وتدلهم على الأدب، فالتوحيد محله البواطن، فلا يرى الفعل إلا من الله، والأدب محله الظواهر فينسب بلسانه النقص إلى نفسه وهواه. وإذا شهد الحق- جلّ جلاله- لرسوله بالرسالة أغْنَى عن غيره، وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ شَهِيداً. وشهادة الحق له بالمعجزات الواضحات، والبراهين القطعيات، والدلائل السمعيات، فإذا ثبتت رسالته وجب على الناس طاعته، ولذلك قال: مَنْ يُطِعِ الرَّسُولَ فَقَدْ أَطاعَ اللَّهَ لأنه مُبلغ عن الله لا ينطق عن الهوى. رُوِي أنه صلّى الله عليه وسلم قال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-14","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"«مَن أطَاعَنِي فَقَد أطَاعَ الله، ومَن أحبَني فقَد أحبَ الله» فقال بعض المنافقين: ما يريد هذا الرجل إلا أن نتخذه ربًّا، كما اتخذت النصارى عيسى. فنزل: مَنْ يُطِعِ الرَّسُولَ فَقَدْ أَطاعَ اللَّهَ وَمَنْ تَوَلَّى وأعرض فَما أَرْسَلْناكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيظاً تَحفَظُ عليهم أعمالهم، وتحاسبهم عليها، إنما عليك البلاغ وعلينا الحساب.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-15","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"الإشارة: كما شهد الحق- جل جلاله- لرسله بالرسالة، بما أظهر لهم من المعجزات، شهد لأوليائه بالولاية بما منحهم من الكرامات. والمراد بالكرامة: هي تحقيق العرفان، ومعرفة الذوق والوجدان، واستقامة الظواهر والبواطن، وتهذيب الأخلاق وهداية الناس على يديه إلى العليم الخلاق، فهذه الكرامة المعتبرة عند المحققين، فمن أطاعهم فقد أطاع الله، ومن أعرض عنهم فقد أعرض عن معرفة الله، ومن أحبهم فقد أحب الله، ومن أبغضهم فقد أبغض الله لأنهم نور من أنوار الله، وعين من عيون الله، إذ لم يبق فيهم بقية مما سوى الله، أقدامهم على قدم رسول الله، «إِنَّ الذين يُبَايِعُونَكَ إنما يبايعون الله» . فافهم، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_079-16","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"4:79–80 · Divine causality, the ethics of attribution, and obeying the Messenger","text":"ثم ذكر أحوال أهل النفاق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_079-16"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_079-s1","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"The outward interpretation, continuing from 4:78","text":"Whatever adversity ( sayyiʾa ) comes upon a person, says Ibn ʿAjība, is due to his own self: the baleful consequence of sin. He cites a report attributed to the Prophet saying that even a scratch from a stick, a twitching vein, or another minor affliction occurs because of a sin, while God forgives much more. This does not contradict “Say: All is from God” [4:78]. Every event comes from God in the sense of being brought into existence and originated ( ījād and ikhtirāʿ ); yet good is His beneficence, whereas the adverse is requital and chastisement. He also attributes to ʿĀʾisha a report that no Muslim suffers fatigue, illness, the prick of a thorn, or even the snapping of a sandal-strap except through some sin, while God forgives far more. [Translator’s note: The specific extensions in these two attributions require comparison with their transmitted witnesses.] Ibn ʿAjība notes a wording attributed to the codex of Ibn Masʿūd, adding “They said” at the start of “Whatever good befalls you is from God.” On that reported reading, the sentence is understood as continuing the speech of the hypocrites. [Translator’s note: This is cited as an early exegetical reading, not presented as part of the standard transmitted Qurʾānic text.] Neither this verse nor the preceding, he insists, furnishes an argument for the Muʿtazilites as against his theological account of divine creation. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_079-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_079-s2","r":"q4_cont_079","title":", concerning attribution and purification","text":"Ibn ʿAjība mentions the report that only a few escape three traits: taking evil omens ( ṭiyara ), envy ( ḥasad ) and suspicion ( ẓann ). In its cited form the Prophet advises: “If you take an omen, proceed; if you envy, do not transgress; if you suspect, do not investigate [as if it were certainty].” The aspirant must cleanse himself of these habits and purify the drink of his tawḥīd. He sees only his Lord in being, attributing no efficacy to anything besides Him. Seeing a blessing in himself or another, he says, “It is from God.” Seeing calamity, he still holds inwardly that it comes by God's decree, as the Qurʾān says, “All is from God,” while in speech he courteously attributes deficiency to his own self and passions. The self and Satan, in Ibn ʿAjība's bold image, are the “cloths of the Presence” upon which the stains of decreed contingencies are wiped. “Your Lord creates what He wills and chooses” [Q 28:68]. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_079-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_079-s3","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"Grammar, now on the Messenger (*qultu*)","text":"The Exalted One then bears witness to His Messenger’s mission, urging reverence for him and obedience to him, and warning against discourtesy toward him such as the hypocrites displayed. If the prepositional phrase “to humankind” depends on the verb “We sent,” the word “messenger” ( rasūlan ) is a confirming circumstantial accusative ( ḥāl muʾakkida ). If it depends instead on “messenger,” it is an establishing circumstance ( ḥāl muʾassisa ) which expresses universality: We sent you as messenger to all humankind . “Keeper” ( ḥafīẓan ) is a circumstance of the second-person object-pronoun.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_079-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_079-s4","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"The outward interpretation, concerning 4:79b–80","text":"God has sent Muḥammad to humankind to teach divine unity and guide people into proper comportment ( adab ). The inward place of tawḥīd is the heart: it recognises action as coming only from God. The outward place of adab is conduct and speech: the servant assigns imperfection to his own self and its cravings. God's testimony to the Messenger's mission suffices without anyone else's endorsement—“God suffices as witness”—a testimony given by clear miracles, decisive demonstrations and transmitted proofs. Once the mission is established, people are bound to obey him. Whoever obeys the Messenger obeys God, for he transmits God's command and does not speak by mere caprice. Ibn ʿAjība reports the saying: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed God; whoever loves me has loved God,” and a polemical anecdote in which hypocrites objected that the Messenger sought to be made a lord like Jesus among Christians. The revelation replied that obedience to him is obedience to God. But the one who turns away is not entrusted to the Messenger as a keeper of every deed and its reckoning: his commission is to convey, whereas the account belongs to God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_079-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_079-s5","r":"q4_cont_079","title":", concerning 4:80","text":"As God testified to the mission of His messengers through miracles ( muʿjizāt ), so, says Ibn ʿAjība, He testifies to the sanctity ( wilāya ) of His friends through extraordinary graces ( karāmāt ). The karāma that matters to those of realization is the attainment of knowing God ( ʿirfān ) through experience and taste ( dhawq and wijdān ), the uprightness of outward and inward conduct, the refinement of character, and the guidance of people through a saint toward the All-Knowing Creator. These, rather than wonders for their own sake, constitute the grace esteemed by the accomplished. Whoever obeys them has obeyed God; to turn away from them is to turn away from knowing God. Whoever loves them has loved God, and whoever hates them has hated God, because they are a light among God’s lights and an eye among God’s eyes: no trace of anything other than God remains in them. Their footsteps follow the footsteps of the Messenger. Ibn ʿAjība adduces [Q 48:10], “Those who pledge allegiance to you pledge allegiance only to God,” and closes: Understand. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_079-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_079-s6","r":"q4_cont_079","title":"","text":"The discourse returns to the conduct of hypocrites.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_079-s6"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_081","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"4:81 · Profession of obedience and secret contradiction","text":"4:81 · Profession of obedience and secret contradiction 4:81","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_081"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_081-1","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"4:81 · Profession of obedience and secret contradiction","text":"وَيَقُولُونَ طاعَةٌ فَإِذا بَرَزُوا مِنْ عِنْدِكَ بَيَّتَ طائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ غَيْرَ الَّذِي تَقُولُ وَاللَّهُ يَكْتُبُ ما يُبَيِّتُونَ فَأَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلاً (81)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_081-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_081-2","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"4:81 · Profession of obedience and secret contradiction","text":"قلت: (طاعة) : خبر، أي: أمرنا طاعة، وأصله النصب على المصدر، ورُفِعَ للدلالة على الثبوت، وبيَّتَ الشيء: دبَّره ليلاً وأضمره في نفسه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_081-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_081-3","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"4:81 · Profession of obedience and secret contradiction","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في شأن المنافقين: وَيَقُولُونَ لك إذا حضروا معك: أمرنا وشأننا طاعَةٌ لك فيما تأمرنا به، فَإِذا بَرَزُوا أي: خرجوا مِنْ عِنْدِكَ بَيَّتَ طائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ أي: دبَّرت ليلاً وأخفت من النفاق غَيْرَ الَّذِي تَقُولُ لك من قبول الإيمان وإظهار الطاعة، أو زوَّرت خلاف ما قلتَ لها من الأمر بالطاعة، وَاللَّهُ يَكْتُبُ ما يُبَيِّتُونَ أي: يُثبِتُه في صحائفهم فيجازيهم عليه، فَأَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ ولا تبال بهم، وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ يكفك شرهم، وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلًا عليهم، فسينتقم لك منهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_081-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_081-4","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"4:81 · Profession of obedience and secret contradiction","text":"الإشارة: هذه الخصلة موجودة في بعض العوام إذا حضروا مع أهل الخصوصية أظهروا الطاعة والإقرار، وإذا خرجوا عنهم بيَّتوا الانتقاد والإنكار، فلا يليق إلا الإعراض عنهم، والغيبة في الله عنهم، فإن الله يكفي شرهم بكفالته وحفظه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_081-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_081-5","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"4:81 · Profession of obedience and secret contradiction","text":"ثم دلّهم على ما فيه دواء مرض قلوبهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_081-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_081-s1","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"","text":"Ṭāʿa (“obedience”) stands in the nominative as a predicate, its implied subject being “our affair”: “Our business is obedience.” Its underlying form could have been an accusative verbal noun, ṭāʿatan , but the nominative suggests permanence and established character. To bayyata something is to devise it at night and conceal it inwardly.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_081-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_081-s2","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"","text":"The hypocrites say, when they sit with the Messenger, that their affair is complete obedience to whatever he commands. But once they leave him, a faction arranges matters secretly at night and conceals hypocrisy contrary to its outward declaration of faith and acceptance of obedience. Or they distort and fabricate something different from the command he had given them. God writes down their nocturnal designs in their scrolls and will recompense them for them. The Messenger should turn aside from them, pay them no heed and trust in God, who will suffice against their malice. God is enough as trustee ( wakīl ), and will exact a reckoning on his behalf.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_081-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_081-s3","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"","text":"Ibn ʿAjība finds an analogous trait among some ordinary people. In the company of people distinguished by spiritual realization they display agreement and obedience; on leaving they secretly prepare criticism and repudiation. The appropriate response is not to struggle with them, but to turn aside and become absent in God from concern over them. God's care and protection will suffice against their harm. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_081-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_081-s4","r":"q4_cont_081","title":"","text":"The Qurʾān now directs such people to a remedy for the disease of their hearts.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_081-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_082","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"4:82 · Contemplating the Qurʾān and the unveiling of meaning","text":"4:82 · Contemplating the Qurʾān and the unveiling of meaning 4:82","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_082"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_082-1","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"4:82 · Contemplating the Qurʾān and the unveiling of meaning","text":"أَفَلا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ الْقُرْآنَ وَلَوْ كانَ مِنْ عِنْدِ غَيْرِ اللَّهِ لَوَجَدُوا فِيهِ اخْتِلافاً كَثِيراً (82)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_082-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_082-2","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"4:82 · Contemplating the Qurʾān and the unveiling of meaning","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: أفلا يتدبر هؤلاء المنافقون الْقُرْآنَ، وينظرون ما فيه من البلاغة والبيان، ويتبصّرون في معاني علومه وأسراره، ويطلعون على عجائب قصصه وأخباره، وتَوافُق آياتهِ وأحكامه، حتى يتحققوا أنه ليس من طوق البشر، وإنما هو من عند الله الواحد القهار، وَلَوْ كانَ مِنْ عِنْدِ غَيْرِ اللَّهِ لَوَجَدُوا فِيهِ اخْتِلافاً كَثِيراً بَين أحكامه وآياته، من تَفَاوتِ اللفظ وتناقض المعنى، وكَون بعضه فصيحًا، وبعضه ركيكًا، وبعضه تصعب معارضته وبعضه تسهل، وبعضه توافق أخباره المستقبلة للواقع، وبعضه لا يوافق، وبعضه يوافق العقل، وبعضه لا يوافقه، على ما دلّ عليه الاستقراء من أن كلام البشر، إذا طال، قطعًا يوجد فيه شيء من الخلل والتناقض.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_082-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_082-3","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"4:82 · Contemplating the Qurʾān and the unveiling of meaning","text":"قال البيضاوي: ولعل ذكره للتنبيه على أن اختلاف ما سبق من الأحكام ليس للتناقض في الحكم، بل لاختلاف الأحوال من الحكم والمصالح. هـ. قال ابن جزي: وإن عَرَضَت لأحدٍ شبهةٌ وظن اختلافًا في شيء من القرآن، فالواجب أن يَتَّهِمَ نظره، ويسأل أهل العلم ويطالع تآليفهم، حتى يعلم أن ذلك ليس باختلاف. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_082-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_082-4","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"4:82 · Contemplating the Qurʾān and the unveiling of meaning","text":"الإشارة: تدبر القرآن على حسب صفاء الجنان، فبقدر ما يتطهر القلب من حب الدنيا والهوى تتجلى فيه أسرار كلام المولى، وبقدر ما يتراكم في مرآة قلبه من صور الأكوان، ينحجب عن أسرار معاني القرآن ولو كان من أكابر علماء اللسان. فلما كان القرآن هو دواء لمرض القلوب، أمر الله المنافقين بالتدبر فى معانيه لعل ذلك المرض ينقلع عن قلوبهم، لكن الأقفال التي على القلوب مَنَعَت القلوبَ من فهم كلام علام الغيوب، فحلاوة كلام الله لا يذوقها إلا أهل التجريد، الخائضون في تيار بحار التوحيد، الذين صَفَت قلوبُهم من الأغيار، وتطهرت من الأكدار، يتمتعون أولاً بحلاوة الكلام، ثم يتمتعون ثانيا بحلاوة شهود المتكلم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_082-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_082-5","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"4:82 · Contemplating the Qurʾān and the unveiling of meaning","text":"ومن مساوئ المنافقين إفشاء أسرار المؤمنين، كما قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_082-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_082-s1","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"","text":"Why do these hypocrites not reflect on ( yatadabbarūn ) the Qurʾān—its eloquence and lucidity, the sciences and mysteries contained in its meanings, the wonders of its narratives and accounts, and the concord of its verses and judgments? Attentive study would disclose that such a discourse lies beyond human capacity and is from God, the One, the Overpowering. Had it originated from another than God, its laws and verses would reveal frequent conflict: inequalities of diction, contradictions of meaning, some parts eloquent and others poor, some passages difficult to imitate and others easy, some predictions agreeing with subsequent events and others failing, some assertions agreeing with reason and others not. Human discourse, when extended long enough, is bound, as induction shows, to exhibit faults or inconsistencies. Al-Bayḍāwī adds that the verse may be intended to show that differences among the judgments previously mentioned do not indicate contradictory legislation; they arise from differences in circumstances, with their respective purposes of wisdom ( ḥikam ) and benefits ( maṣāliḥ ). Ibn Juzayy says that if someone encounters a troubling question and supposes some disagreement exists within the Qurʾān, he should first suspect his own reading, consult people of knowledge and examine their works until he understands that the appearance is not an actual contradiction. Here end the cited observations.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_082-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_082-s2","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"","text":"The capacity to ponder the Qurʾān corresponds to the cleanness of the heart ( ṣafāʾ al-janān ). In the measure that the heart is purified of love of the world and passionate inclination ( hawā ), the mysteries of the Lord's speech are disclosed within it. In the measure that images of created things accumulate upon the heart's mirror, the deeper significations of the Qurʾān are hidden from it—even if its possessor is among the greatest experts in the Arabic language. Because the Qurʾān is a medicine for diseased hearts, the hypocrites are commanded to contemplate its meanings in the hope that their disease may be uprooted. Yet the locks upon their hearts have kept them from understanding the speech of the Knower of all unseen things. Only people of tajrīd , whose hearts have been emptied of other-than-God ( aghyār ) and cleansed of clouding impurities ( akdār ), who have plunged into the streaming seas of divine unity ( tawḥīd ), taste the sweetness of God's words. First they enjoy the sweetness of the speech ( kalām ); then they enjoy the sweetness of witnessing the One who speaks ( al-Mutakallim ). God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_082-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_082-s3","r":"q4_cont_082","title":"","text":"Among the blameworthy acts of the hypocrites is the disclosure of the believers' secrets.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_082-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_083","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge 4:83","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_083"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-1","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"وَإِذا جاءَهُمْ أَمْرٌ مِنَ الْأَمْنِ أَوِ الْخَوْفِ أَذاعُوا بِهِ وَلَوْ رَدُّوهُ إِلَى الرَّسُولِ وَإِلى أُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنْهُمْ لَعَلِمَهُ الَّذِينَ يَسْتَنْبِطُونَهُ مِنْهُمْ ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-2","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"قلت: استنبط الشيء: استخرجه من غيره، وأصل الاستنباط: إخراج النبط، وهو الماء، يخرج من البئر أول ما يحفر، والجار في (منهم) : إما بيان للموصول، أي: لعلم المستنبطون الذين هم أولوا الأمر، أو يتعلق ب (علم) ، أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-3","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"لعلمه الذين يستخرجونه إلى الناس من أولي الأمر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-4","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: في ذمّ المنافقين أو ضعفة المسلمين: وَإِذا جاءَهُمْ أَمْرٌ أي: خبر عن السرايا الذين توجهوا للغزو، من نصر وغنيمة وأمن أو خوف، وقتل وهزيمة، أَذاعُوا بِهِ أي: تحدثوا به، وأشهروه، وأرجفوا به قبل أن يصل إلى الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- وأكابر الصحابة، الذين هم أولو الأمر وأهل البصائر، فيعرفون كيف يتحدثون به.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-5","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"ولو ردوا ذلك إِلَى الرَّسُولِ وأخبروه به سرًا، أو سكتوا حتى يصل إليه، أو يردوه إِلى أُولِي الْأَمْرِ من أكابر الصحابة، لعلمه الذين يستخرجونه إلى الناس مِنْهُمْ، فينقلونه على وجهه، ويعرفون كيف يتحدثون به من غير إرجاف ولا تخويف، أو لَعَلِمَهُ الَّذِينَ يَسْتَنْبِطُونَهُ وهم أولو الأمر أولاً، ثم يعلم الناس، فلا يكون فيه إرجاف ولا سوء أدب. أو: وإذا جاءهم أمر من وحي السماء: من تخويف أو تأمين، أذاعوا به قبل أن يظهره الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، ولو سكتوا وردوا ذلك إلى الرسول حتى يتحدث به للناس، ويظهره أولو الأمر من أكابر أصحابه، لعلمه الذين يستخرجون ذلك الوحي من أصله، وهو الرسول- عليه الصلاة السلام- وأكابر أصحابه، كما فعل عمر رضي الله عنه: إذ سمع أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم طلق نساءه، فدخل عليه فقال: أطلقت نساءك؟ قال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-6","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"«لا» ، فقام على باب المسجد، فقال: إن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم لم يطلق نساءه، فأنزل الله هذه القصة، قال: وأنا الذي استنبطته. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-7","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"الإشارة: قالت الحكماء: قلوب الأحرار قبور الأسرار، وهذه الخصلة التي ذمَّها الله تعالى تُوجد في كثير من العوام مهما سمعوا خبرًا: خيرًا أو شرًا، بادروا إلى إفشائه، ولا سيما إذا سمعوه على أهل النسبة أو أهل الخصوصية، وقد تُوجد في بعض الفقراء، وهي غفلة ونوع من الفضول، فالفقير الصادق غائب عن أخبار الزمان وأهله، وقد ترك الناسَ وما هم فيه، وقد تغلب عليه الغيبة في الله حتى تغيب عنه الأيام، وأما الفقير الذي يتسمع الأخبار ويبحث عنها فلا نسبة له في الفقر، إلا اسم بلا مسمى، وقد ترى بعض الفقراء، يبلّغ مساوئ إخوانه إلى المشايخ، وهو سبب الطرد، والعياذ بالله. وقد كان صلّى الله عليه وسلم يقول: «لا تبلغونى مساوئ أصحابي (١)» لأن ذلك يسؤوهم، والخير كله في إدخال السرور على قلوب المشايخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-8","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"وتنسحب الآية على مَن يُفشِيِ أسرار الربوبية، ويُطلع الفقراء علَى الحقيقة، ولو ردوا ذلك إلى شيخهم حتى يكون هو الذي يطلعهم لكان أحسن، لأن الحقيقة إذا أُخِذَت من الشيخ كان فيها سر كبير، بخلاف ما إذا أُخِذّت من غيره، إلاَّ إذا كان مأذونا له في ذلك فكأنه هو. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-9","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"وقال الورتجبي: قال أبو سعيد الخراز: إن له عبادًا يدخل عليهم الخلل، ولولا ذلك لفسدوا وتعطلوا، وذلك أنهم بَلَغُوا من العلم غاية، صاروا إلى علم المجهول، الذي لم ينصُّه كتاب، ولا جاء به خبر، لكن العقلاء العارفون، يحتجون له من الكتاب والسنة، بحسن استنباطهم ومعرفتهم، قال الله تعالى: لَعَلِمَهُ الَّذِينَ يَسْتَنْبِطُونَهُ مِنْهُمْ. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-10","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"قلت: ومعنى كلامه: أن الله- تعالى- أشغل علماء الظاهر بتقرير علم الفرق، ولولا اشتغالهم بذلك لتعطلوا وتبطلوا، إذ لا قدرة لهم على عمل القلوب من الفكرة والنظرة، لكن العارفون يقرون لهم ذلك، ويحتجون لهم بما في نشر العلم من الأجور، من الكتاب والسنة، لأنهم قاموا بنظام علم الحكمة ورفعوا علم الشريعة، ولولا قيامهم بذلك لتعين على أهل الباطن، فتتشوش عليهم قلوبهم، وكان شيخ شيوخنا سيدي علي الجمل العمراني رضي الله عنه يقول:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-11","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"جزاهم الله عنا خيرًا رفعوا لنا علم الشريعة، نحن نغرق في البحر، ثم نرفع رأسنا فنرى العلم قائمًا، ثم نرجع إلى البحر. هـ. بالمعنى، والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-12","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"ثم إن الهداية بيد الله، قوم أقامهم في الفرق، وقوم هداهم إلى الجمع، كما قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-13","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"... وَلَوْلا فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ لاتَّبَعْتُمُ الشَّيْطانَ إِلاَّ قَلِيلاً (83)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-14","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لولا أن الله تفضل عليكم ورحمكم بنبي الرحمة، وأنقذكم من متابعة الشيطان وعبادة الأوثان، لبقيتم على كفركم وضلالكم، ولا تبعتم الشيطان فيما يأمركم به من الكفر والعصيان، إلا قليلاً ممن اهتدى قبل بعثته، كقس بن ساعدة، وزيد بن نفيل، وورقة بن نوفل، رزقهم الله كمال العقل فنظروا وتفكروا بعقولهم فوجدوا الله واعتزلوا ما كان يعبد آباؤهم وإخوانهم. أما قس فاعتزل قومه، وعبد الله وحده، وكان يخطب على الناس ويأمرهم بالتوحيد، ويعيب عليهم عبادة الأصنام. وعاش سبعمائة عام. وأما زيدٌ فتعلق بالحنيفية، دين إبراهيم، حتى مات قبل البعثة. وأما ورقة- فأخذ بدين النصرانية التي لم تُغَيَّر، وأدرك أول البعثة، وآمن بالرسول قبل أن يُؤمر بالإنذار. قال- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «رأيتُه في الجنة عليه ثيابُ خُضر» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-15","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-16","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"الإشارة: لولا فضل الله عليكم بأن بعث لكم مَن يدلكم على الله ويعرفكم بالله، ورحمته بأن أخرجكم من ضيق الفرق، إلى فضاء الجمع، لا تبعتم الفرق علمًا وعملاً، لكن الله تعالى بفضله ورحمته غيبكم عن شهود الفرق بشهود الملك الحق. إلاّ فرقًا قليلاً تقيمون به رسم العبودية، وتظهرون به الآداب مع الربوبية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-17","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"قال الورتجبي: الفضل والرحمة منه للعموم، ومحبته للخصوص، الذين هم مستثنون بقوله: «إلا قليلاً» . هـ. قال القشيري: وَلَوْلا فَضْلُ اللَّهِ مع أوليائه لهاموا في كل وادٍ من التفرقة كأشكالهم في الوقت. هـ. فَخَصَّ الإشارة بالأولياء، وعليه فقوله: إِلَّا قَلِيلًا أي: إلا تفرقة قليلة تعرض لهم، تربيةً لهم، وإبقاء لرسمهم ومناطِ تكليفهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-18","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"والله تعالى أعلم. قاله في الحاشية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_083-19","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"4:83 · News, *istinbāṭ*, the guarding of secrets, and the complementarity of knowledge","text":"ولا يظهر هذا كله إلا بالجهاد الأكبر والأصغر، كما قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_083-19"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_083-s1","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"Language and construction (*qultu*)","text":"Istinbaṭa means to extract or draw something out of another thing. The underlying image is taking out nabaṭ —water issuing from a well when it is first dug. The phrase “from among them” ( minhum ) may explain the relative pronoun: “those who could extract it, namely the holders of authority.” Alternatively it depends on “would have known”: the people who draw the information out for others would have known it from the holders of authority .","anchor":"en-q4_cont_083-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_083-s2","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"The outward interpretation: broadcasting without discernment","text":"God censures hypocrites, or weaker Muslims, who receive news of military detachments that have gone out on campaigns: tidings of victory, booty and safety, or of danger, killing and defeat. Immediately they publicize the information, spreading alarming rumours before it has reached the Messenger and the senior Companions. These people of discernment ( ahl al-baṣāʾir ), who are holders of authority ( ulū l-amr ), know when and how such matters should be communicated. Had the news-bearers reported it privately to the Prophet, or kept silence until it came to him, or referred it to the senior Companions, those capable of drawing its real significance from the reports would have known what to convey. They would have communicated it in its proper form, without spreading rumour or frightening people. Alternatively the verse means that these competent authorities would first establish its meaning and only then tell the public, so that neither intimidation nor lack of propriety would result. There is another possible reference. News may come from heavenly revelation, bearing warning or reassurance, and be circulated before the Prophet himself has announced it. Had people kept silent and left it to the Messenger to proclaim, and to the leading Companions to explain, those able to derive its meaning from its source—the Messenger and his senior companions—would have known and communicated it properly. Ibn ʿAjība offers the incident of ʿUmar: on hearing that the Prophet had divorced his wives, he entered and asked, “Have you divorced your wives?” The Prophet replied, “No.” ʿUmar then stood at the mosque entrance and announced that the Messenger had not divorced them. He connected the revelation of this verse to that event and said, “I was the one who drew it out ( istanbaṭtuhu ).” God knows best. Translator’s source note: The central first-person narrative, including the direct question, public announcement and connection with 4:83, is preserved in Muslim 1479a. This source identification is an editorial observation.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_083-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_083-s3","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"the grave of secrets","text":"The sages say, “The hearts of free people are the graves of secrets” ( qulūb al-aḥrār qubūr al-asrār ). The fault reproved here is widespread: some people, hearing something favourable or unfavourable, hasten to disclose it—especially when the story touches those affiliated with a spiritual way ( ahl al-nisba ) or those specially favoured ( ahl al-khuṣūṣiyya ). It may also arise among the fuqarāʾ . Ibn ʿAjība calls it heedlessness and a needless curiosity ( fuḍūl ). The truthful faqīr does not occupy himself with the passing reports of his time or with its people. He has left the people to whatever occupies them; absence in God may become so powerful that even the days pass beyond his notice. Someone who continually listens out for news and hunts it down possesses only the name of spiritual poverty without its reality. Some fuqarāʾ , he continues, bring their brothers' defects to the ears of their shaykhs, which can lead to expulsion from their company—God protect us. He quotes the Prophet as saying, “Do not bring me reports of the bad acts of my Companions,” because such news grieves the hearer. There is great good in bringing joy to the hearts of spiritual teachers. [Source note: Al-Tirmidhī 3896 transmits a longer report from Ibn Masʿūd containing the request, calls his route gharīb , and notes an additional intermediary in al-Walīd b. Abī Thawr’s transmission. Cairo’s “Do not bring me reports of the bad acts of my Companions” is an abbreviated wording.] The verse applies also to those who expose secrets of divine lordship ( asrār al-rubūbiyya ) and disclose to the fuqarāʾ matters of the inner reality ( ḥaqīqa ). It is better to refer the matter to the shaykh and let him disclose it. When ḥaqīqa is received from a teacher, a profound secret accompanies that transmission; this is not the case when it comes from someone else, except where that person has received the teacher's authorization ( idhn ), so that he acts, as it were, in his place. God knows best. Al-Wartajbī, al-Kharrāz, and knowledge beyond the formulated report. Ibn ʿAjība then quotes Rūzbihān al-Wartajbī, who quotes Abū Saʿīd al-Kharrāz: God has servants upon whom a defect or disturbance enters; without it they would become spoiled and remain idle. They have reached an extreme degree in knowledge and arrived at knowledge of what is not formulated in a revealed book or transmitted account ( ʿilm al-majhūl ), but discerning knowers can still argue for it from the Book and sunna through subtle derivation ( ḥusn al-istinbāṭ ) and realized understanding. Al-Kharrāz invokes “those who draw it out among them would know it” [4:83]. Ibn ʿAjība comments upon this as follows. God has occupied the scholars of outward learning ( ʿulamāʾ al-ẓāhir ) with establishing the science of differentiation ( ʿilm al-farq ). Without that occupation they would become idle, for, in his characterization, they do not possess the ability to practise the inward work of hearts—reflection ( fikra ) and contemplative looking ( naẓra ). Yet the knowers recognise and justify their undertaking by the scriptural rewards attached to teaching and disseminating knowledge. These scholars maintain the ordering of the science of wisdom ( ʿilm al-ḥikma ) and keep the banner of the sharīʿa upright. Were they not to do it, the people of inward knowing would have to perform that task, and their hearts would become disturbed by it. Ibn ʿAjība recalls the approximate words of the teacher of his teachers, Sīdī ʿAlī al-Jamal al-ʿImrānī: “May God reward them on our behalf with goodness! They have held high for us the banner of the sharīʿa . We plunge into the sea, and then raise our heads and see that the banner is still standing, then return to the sea.” He expressly says that he reports the sense, not a verbatim quotation. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_083-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_083-s4","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"","text":"Guidance belongs to God. He establishes some in differentiation ( farq ) and guides others into gathered unity ( jamʿ ).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_083-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_083-s5","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"God’s bounty and those guided before the mission","text":"“Were it not for God's bounty…” If God had not bestowed upon the community the Prophet of mercy, rescuing people from the pursuit of Satan and the worship of idols, they would have remained in unbelief and wandering and continued following Satan in unbelief and sin. The exception, in one outward explanation, concerns a small number who found guidance before the prophetic mission: Quss ibn Sāʿida, Zayd ibn Nufayl and Waraqa ibn Nawfal. God endowed them with exceptional understanding, so they reasoned and reflected until they recognised God and kept apart from what their families worshipped. Ibn ʿAjība relates that Quss withdrew from his people, worshipped God alone, preached divine unity and reproved idol-worship, and that he lived seven hundred years . Translator’s note: The seven-hundred-year figure is the author’s transmitted historical claim; it has not been independently corroborated. Zayd adhered to the ḥanīfiyya , the religion of Abraham, until he died before the mission. Waraqa, in Ibn ʿAjība's description, followed an uncorrupted Christianity, lived to the start of the mission and believed in the Messenger before he was ordered to issue public warning. Ibn ʿAjība cites the Prophet as saying that he saw Waraqa in Paradise dressed in green garments. Translator’s source note: The green garments occur in Ibn Abī Shayba, al-Muṣannaf 37710, in a mursal narrative from Abū Maysara. A related version in al-Bayhaqī’s Dalāʾil II:158 has silk garments and is explicitly called disconnected by its compiler. Al-Tirmidhī 2288 gives white garments through a different route, which he calls gharīb while criticizing a transmitter. These witnesses establish the source history without warranting a change to Cairo’s green.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_083-s5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_083-s6","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"on bounty and unity","text":"Were it not for God's bounty in sending you someone who points you toward Him and makes Him known, and His mercy in leading you out of the narrowness of differentiation into the openness of gathering ( faḍāʾ al-jamʿ ), you would follow separation in both knowledge and action. But through His bounty and mercy He has concealed the differentiated appearances from your vision by granting you witnessing of the True King. Only a little farq remains by which you maintain the visible form of servanthood ( rasm al-ʿubūdiyya ) and preserve due propriety before lordship ( adab maʿa l-rubūbiyya ). Al-Wartajbī says that divine bounty and mercy extend to people in general, while God's special love belongs to the elect—the “few” exempted in the verse. Al-Qushayrī says that but for divine bounty God's friends would wander through every valley of dispersion like others in their own day. He thus construes the verse allusively with regard to the saints. On this reading “except a few” means the small amount of differentiated awareness that overtakes them for their training, safeguarding their outward human form and preserving the locus on which legal responsibility ( taklīf ) rests. Ibn ʿAjība notes that this last interpretation comes from the marginal commentary. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_083-s6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_083-s7","r":"q4_cont_083","title":"","text":"These realizations become manifest only through the greater and lesser struggles ( al-jihād al-akbar wa-l-aṣghar ), the subject of the next verses.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_083-s7"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_084","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings 4:84–86","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_084"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-1","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"فَقاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ لا تُكَلَّفُ إِلاَّ نَفْسَكَ وَحَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَسَى اللَّهُ أَنْ يَكُفَّ بَأْسَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَاللَّهُ أَشَدُّ بَأْساً وَأَشَدُّ تَنْكِيلاً (84) مَنْ يَشْفَعْ شَفاعَةً حَسَنَةً يَكُنْ لَهُ نَصِيبٌ مِنْها وَمَنْ يَشْفَعْ شَفاعَةً سَيِّئَةً يَكُنْ لَهُ كِفْلٌ مِنْها وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُقِيتاً (85) وَإِذا حُيِّيتُمْ بِتَحِيَّةٍ فَحَيُّوا بِأَحْسَنَ مِنْها أَوْ رُدُّوها إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ حَسِيباً (86)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-2","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"قلت: (نفسك) : مفعول ثانٍ، والأول نائب، أي: لا يكلفك الله إلا نفسك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-3","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَقاتِلْ يا محمد فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ولو وَحدَكَ إن تثبطوا عن الجهاد، لا نكلفك إلا أمر نفسك، وَلكن حَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ على الجهاد، إذ ما عليك إلا التحريض. فجاهدوا حتى تكون كلمة الله هي العليا. عَسَى اللَّهُ أَنْ يَكُفَّ بجهادكم بَأْسَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ويبطل دينهم الفاسد. وَاللَّهُ أَشَدُّ بَأْساً منهم وَأَشَدُّ تَنْكِيلًا أي: تعذيبًا لهم. وقد حقَّق الله ذلك ففتح الله على نبيه قبائل العرب، فلم يبق فيهم مشرك، ثم فتح على الصحابة سائر البلاد، وهدى الله بهم جميع العباد، إلا من فرّ من الكفار إلى شواهق الجبال.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-4","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"وإنما أمرتك بالتحريض على الجهاد لأن الدَّالُّ عَلَى الخَيْرِ كَفَاعِلِه، وذلك كالشفاعة بين الناس ودلالتهم على إصلاح ذات البين، فمن يَشْفَعْ شَفاعَةً حَسَنَةً بأن ينفع المشفوع له، بدفع ضرر أو جلب نفع، ابتغاء وجه الله، يَكُنْ لَهُ نَصِيبٌ مِنْها، أي: حظ كبير من الثواب لأنه دل المشفوع عنده على الخير، وأوصل النفع إلى المشفوع له، فله من الأجر مثل ما لهما، ومنها: الدعاء بظهر الغيب، فقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «مَن دعا لمسلمٍ بظَهرِ الغَيبِ استُجيب له، وقال له الملك: لك مِثلُ ذَلِكَ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-5","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"وَمَنْ يَشْفَعْ شَفاعَةً سَيِّئَةً، يريد بها فسادًا بين الناس كنميمة وزور وإحداث بدعة، يَكُنْ لَهُ كِفْلٌ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-6","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"نصيب مِنْها أي: من وِزرها، وفي الحديث: «مَن سنَّ سُنةَ حسنة، فله أجرُهَا وأجرُ مَن عمل بها إلى يَومِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-7","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"القيامَةِ، ومن سنَّ سُنَّة سَيِّئةً فعليه وزرُهَا وَوِزرُ من عمل بها إلى يَوم القيامَةِ» . وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُقِيتاً أي: مقتدرًا من أقات على الشيء: إذَا قدر عليه، أو شهيدًا حافظَا فيجازي على قدر الأعمال.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-8","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"ومن هذا أيضًا: السلام، فإنه سبب في ثواب الرد، لذلك ذكره الحق في سلك الدلالة على الخير فقال: وَإِذا حُيِّيتُمْ بِتَحِيَّةٍ فَحَيُّوا بِأَحْسَنَ مِنْها بأن تقولوا: وعليكم السلام والرحمة والبركة، أَوْ رُدُّوها بأن تقولوا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-9","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"وعليكم السلام.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-10","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"وفي الخبر: «مَن قَالَ لأخيه المسلم: السَّلامُ علَيكُم، كتب الله له عَشرُ حَسنات، فإن قال: السَّلامُ عليكُم ورحمَةُ الله، كتب الله له عِشرين حَسنة، فإن قال: وَبَرَكَاتُه، كتب الله ثَلاثين» ، وكذلك لمن ردّ، فإن اقتصر على السلام، فعشر، وهكذا.. فإن ذكرَ المسلم الرحمةَ والبركةَ، قال الرادُّ: وعليكم، فقط، إذ لم يبق ما يزاد، ورد السلام واجب على الكفاية، حيث يكون مشروعًا، فلا يرد في الخطبة، وقراءة القرآن، والذكر والتفكر، والاعتبار، ونظرة الشهود والاستبصار، لأنه يفتر ويشوش، وفي الحمام إذا كانوا عراة، وفي حال الجماع والأكل والشرب وغيرها من المسائل المستثناة. وقد نظمه بعضهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-11","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"رَدُّ السَّلآم واجبٌ إلا على ... مَن في الصَّلاةِ أو بأكل شُغلا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-12","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"أو شُربٍ أو قراءةٍ أو أدعِيه ... أو ذكرٍ أو خُطبةٍ أو تَلبِيه","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-13","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"والسلام من تحية أهل الإسلام، خاصٌّ بهم. لذلك استغرب الخضر- عليه السلام- سلام سَيدنا موسى عليه السلام فقال له: «وأنَّى بأرضِكَ السَّلامُ» ، وكذلك خليل الله إبراهيم عليه السلام، إنما أنكر الملائكة حيث سلموا عليه بتحية أهل الإسلام لأنه كان بين أظهر قوم كفار، أما سلام أبي ذر على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بتحية أهل الإسلام، قبل أن يسلم، فلعله سمعه من بعض الصحابة قبل أن يسلم، أو إلهام من الله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-14","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَلى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ حَسِيباً يحاسبكم على التحية وغيرها. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-15","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"الإشارة: فجاهد أيها الإنسان نفسك في سبيل الله، لا تكلف إلا إصلاحها وتزكيتها، وحرض من يسمع قولك من المؤمنين على جهاد أنفسهم، عسى الله أن يكف عنهم القواطع والعلائق، فيتأهلون لإشراق قلوبهم بأنوار الحقائق، فإن الله لا يغلبه شيء، فمن ذكّر عبادَ الله، ودسهم إلى حضرة الله كان حظه كبيرًا عند الله. ومن دلهم على غير الله فقد غشهم وكان مُهانًا عند الله، وإذا وقع السلام على الفقراء فإن كانوا سالكين غير مشتغلين بالذكر","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-16","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"وجب عليهم الرد بأحسن، وإذا كانوا ذاكرين أو متفكرين أو سكارى في شهود الحبيب سقط عنهم السلام، وكذلك إذا سلم عليهم اختبارًا وتعنيتًا لم يجب الرد. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_084-17","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"4:84–86 · Striving, intercession, and the ethics of returning greetings","text":"ولما ذكر أمر الحساب ذكر وقته، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_084-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_084-s1","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"","text":"Nafsaka (“yourself”) is a second object, while the first functions as the deputy subject of the passive verb, understood as “you”. The underlying sense is: “God charges you with none but your own self.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_084-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_084-s2","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"The outward interpretation: duty and encouraging others","text":"God tells Muḥammad to fight in His way even alone if others hang back from the struggle: he has been charged with the duty pertaining to his own self. He should nevertheless encourage the believers, for encouragement is what is incumbent upon him with regard to them. Their struggle aims to make God's word uppermost. God may thereby ward off the power of the unbelievers and overturn the false religion to which they cling. God is stronger in warfare and sterner in chastisement than any opponent. Ibn ʿAjība sees this promise fulfilled in the Prophet's triumph over the tribes of Arabia, the disappearance of idolatry from among them, and the later extension of Muslim rule by the Companions across other lands, guiding inhabitants except those he says withdrew to inaccessible mountain heights. [Translator’s note: These are the commentator's retrospective historical generalizations, not a critical survey of the conquests.] The command to encourage others is joined to the maxim that “one who directs to good is like the one who does it.” Such direction includes beneficial intercession between people and guidance toward the restoration of good relations. Whoever intercedes well on someone's behalf—in order to avert harm or secure a benefit, seeking God's face—receives a substantial share of reward, for he has directed the person addressed toward good and conveyed benefit to the beneficiary. In recompense he receives a reward like theirs. Another instance is supplication for an absent person; Ibn ʿAjība quotes a report that one who prays for a Muslim in his absence is answered, and an angel says, “And the like of that for you.” Whoever makes a bad intercession, conversely, intending corruption among people through malicious tale-bearing, false witness or the institution of blameworthy innovation, receives a kifl , a portion of the resulting burden. Ibn ʿAjība cites the prophetic saying that one who introduces a good precedent ( sunna ḥasana ) receives its recompense and that of those who act upon it until the Resurrection, while one who initiates an evil precedent bears its burden and that of those who follow it. God's being muqīt over everything may mean that He has power over it (from aqāta , “to be able”), or that He watches and preserves it, recompensing actions in due measure. Greetings as an instance of good mediation. Peaceful greeting becomes an occasion for the reward earned by the one who responds; therefore it is mentioned alongside directing people to good. When greeted, one may reply with a more complete formula, “And upon you be peace, God's mercy and His blessing,” or with one equivalent to the original, “And upon you be peace.” Ibn ʿAjība quotes a report according to which “Peace be upon you” brings ten good deeds, adding “and God's mercy” brings twenty, and adding “and His blessings” brings thirty. The responder receives equivalent recompense. When the first speaker has already mentioned both mercy and blessing, Ibn ʿAjība's suggested response is simply “And upon you,” since no further element remains to add. He says that answering the greeting is a collective obligation ( farḍ ʿalā l-kifāya ) where the greeting is legally appropriate. He lists occasions in which, in his account of the law and Sufi propriety, a reply is not due: during a sermon, Qurʾān recitation, remembrance, reflection, spiritual consideration or contemplative witnessing (because a greeting would interrupt or unsettle the person); in a bathhouse when people are undressed; during sexual intercourse, eating or drinking; and other exceptional cases. He quotes instructional verse: Returning peace is obligatory—save for one engaged in prayer, or occupied with eating, or drinking, reciting, supplicating, remembering, preaching, or reciting the talbiya . [Translator’s note: These are Ibn ʿAjība's stated exemptions ; their scope differs among jurists and is not offered here as a settled universal legal ruling.] He describes salām as the distinctive greeting of the people of Islam. Thus, he says, al-Khiḍr was surprised when Moses greeted him with peace and asked, “How does peace come to be in your land?” Likewise, he explains Abraham's surprise at the angels' greeting by reference to the unbelieving people among whom he lived. As for Abū Dharr greeting the Prophet in this Islamic manner before he himself became Muslim, Ibn ʿAjība suggests that he heard the expression from some Companions or received it through divine prompting. “God is Reckoner over all things”: He calls people to account concerning greetings and every other matter. With God is success.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_084-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_084-s3","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"","text":"“Strive, O human being, against your own self in God's way. You are responsible for its reformation and purification, and should encourage believers who hear you to contend with their selves.” God may then remove their impediments ( qawāṭiʿ ) and entangling attachments ( ʿalāʾiq ), preparing their hearts to shine with the lights of the realities ( anwār al-ḥaqāʾiq ), for nothing can overcome God. Whoever recalls God's servants to Him and conveys them toward His Presence acquires a great share with God; one who directs them away from God betrays their trust and is abased. If a greeting is offered to members of the Sufi way, those engaged in ordinary travelling along the path ( sālikūn ) and not occupied with remembrance should answer in a better form. If they are absorbed in remembrance, contemplation, or spiritual intoxication in witnessing the Beloved, Ibn ʿAjība holds that an answering greeting is not required. Nor, he says, is a response required when the greeting is given to test, provoke or torment them. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_084-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_084-s4","r":"q4_cont_084","title":"","text":"Having spoken of reckoning ( ḥisāb ), the Qurʾān turns to the appointed time of reckoning.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_084-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_087","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention","text":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention 4:87","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_087"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_087-1","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention","text":"اللَّهُ لاَ إِلهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ لَيَجْمَعَنَّكُمْ إِلى يَوْمِ الْقِيامَةِ لا رَيْبَ فِيهِ وَمَنْ أَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللَّهِ حَدِيثاً (87)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_087-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_087-2","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention","text":"قلت: (الله) : مبتدأ، و (لا إله) : خبر، أو اعتراض، و (ليجمعنكم) : خبر، وهو أوفق بالسياق، و (لا ريب فيه) حال، أو صفة لمصدر، أي: جمعًا لا ريب فيه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_087-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_087-3","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: اللَّهُ لاَ إِلهَ إِلَّا هُوَ أي: لا مستحق للعبادة إلا هو، والله لَيَجْمَعَنَّكُمْ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_087-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_087-4","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention","text":"ليحشرنكم من قبوركم إِلى يَوْمِ الْقِيامَةِ للحساب الذي وعدكم به، لا شك فيه، فهو وعد صادق، وَمَنْ أَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللَّهِ حَدِيثاً، أي: لا أحدَ أصدقُ من الله حديثًا، لأن الكذب نقص، وهو على الله محال.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_087-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_087-5","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention","text":"الإشارة: الحق تعالى واحد في ملكه، فلا يذوق وحدانيته إلا من كان واحدًا في قصده وهمه، فكل من وحَّد قلبه وقصده وهمته في طلبه، وانجمع بكليته إليه، جمعه الله لحضرته، ونعَّمه بشهود ذاته، وعداً حقاً وقولاً صدقاً، لا ريب فيه ولا اشتباه، إذ لا أحدَ أصدق من الله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_087-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_087-6","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"4:87 · The gathering on the Last Day and the unity of the seeker's intention","text":"ثم رجع إلى الكلام مع المنافقين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_087-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_087-s1","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"","text":"“God” ( Allāh ) is an initial subject ( mubtadaʾ ), with “there is no god” ( lā ilāha ) as predicate ( khabar ). Alternatively the declaration of divine unity is parenthetic, and “He will certainly gather you” ( la-yajmaʿannakum ) is the predicate; this more closely suits the context. “There is no doubt in it” ( lā rayba fīhi ) is either a circumstance ( ḥāl ) or an adjective qualifying an unexpressed verbal noun: “a gathering in which there is no doubt.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_087-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_087-s2","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"","text":"God alone deserves worship. By God, He will certainly raise you out of your graves and assemble you on the Day of Resurrection to face the accounting He has promised. There is no doubt about that day or His promise, for the promise is true. Who could speak more truthfully than God? No one, because lying is a defect, and defect is impossible of God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_087-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_087-s3","r":"q4_cont_087","title":"","text":"The True ( al-Ḥaqq ) is one in His kingdom, and no one tastes His oneness except a person who becomes single in his aim and spiritual concern. Whoever gathers his heart, intention ( qaṣd ) and spiritual aspiration ( himma ) into a single pursuit of God, turning his entire being toward Him, God gathers him into His Presence and favours him with the witnessing of His Essence ( shuhūd dhātihi ). This is His real promise and truthful word, free from doubt and ambiguity. None is truer in speech than God. Ibn ʿAjība next returns to the matter of the hypocrites.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_087-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_088","r":"q4_cont_088","title":"4:88 · Disagreement over the hypocrites","text":"4:88 · Disagreement over the hypocrites 4:88","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_088"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_088-1","r":"q4_cont_088","title":"4:88 · Disagreement over the hypocrites","text":"فَما لَكُمْ فِي الْمُنافِقِينَ فِئَتَيْنِ وَاللَّهُ أَرْكَسَهُمْ بِما كَسَبُوا أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَهْدُوا مَنْ أَضَلَّ اللَّهُ وَمَنْ يُضْلِلِ اللَّهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُ سَبِيلاً (88)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_088-1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_088-s1","r":"q4_cont_088","title":"","text":"I say: fiʾatayn (“two parties”) is a circumstantial accusative ( ḥāl ); its governing expression is the implicit idea of being or remaining conveyed by the preceding prepositional phrase. To arkasa something is to turn it upside down or throw it back. God, exalted is His majesty, reproaches the Companions for dividing into two groups over the status of certain hypocrites, instead of agreeing concerning their unbelief. God had cast those people back into unbelief after they had displayed Islam, as the consequence of their sins. Do you propose to guide people whose wretched destiny God already knew? Whoever God leads astray will find no way to guidance. Ibn ʿAbbās is cited as saying that the verse concerned people in Mecca who claimed to have embraced Islam but did not emigrate. When some journeyed to Syria on business, Muslims differed: should they be killed and their merchandise taken because they had not emigrated, or spared because they professed belief? Another report concerns men who embraced Islam but found Medina unhealthy. They asked permission to return to the desert, and, once away, travelled on until they joined the polytheists; Muslims then disputed their religious status. [Translator’s note: These are reported occasions of revelation, not independent conclusions concerning contemporary persons.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_088-s1"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_089","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties 4:89–90","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_089"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-1","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"وَدُّوا لَوْ تَكْفُرُونَ كَما كَفَرُوا فَتَكُونُونَ سَواءً ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-2","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"قلت: (فئتين) : حال، والعامل فيه: الاستقرار في الجر، وأركس الشيء: نكَّسه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-3","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله معاتبًا الصحابة حين اختلفوا في إسلام بعض المنافقين، فقال: فَما لَكُمْ افترقتم فِي شأن الْمُنافِقِينَ فرقتين، ولم تتفقوا على كفرهم، والحالة أن الله- تعالى- أَرْكَسَهُمْ، أي: نكَّسهم وردهم إلى الكفر بعد أن أظهروا الإسلام بسبب ما كسبوا من الآثام. أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَهْدُوا مَنْ أَضَلَّ اللَّهُ، وسبق لهم الشقاء في علم الله؟ ومَن يُضللِ اللهُ فلن تجد له طريقاً إلى الهدى. قال ابن عباس- رضى الله عنهما-: (نزلت في قوم كانوا بمكة من المشركين، فزعموا أنهم آمنوا ولم يهاجروا، ثم سافر قوم منهم بتجارات إلى الشام، فاختلف","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-4","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"المسلمون، هل يقتلونهم ليغنموا تجارتهم، لأنهم لم يهاجروا، أو يتركونهم لأنهم مؤمنون؟) . وقيل: في قوم أسلموا ثم اجتَوَوا المدينة (1) ، واستأذنوا رسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم في الخروج إلى البدو، فلما خَرَجُوا لم يزالُوا راحلين مَرحلةً حتى لحقُوا بالمُشركين، فاختلف المسلمون فى إسلامهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-6","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"ثم حكم بكفرهم فقال وَدُّوا لَوْ تَكْفُرُونَ أي: يتمنون كفركم كَما كَفَرُوا فَتَكُونُونَ معهم سَواءً في الضلال والكفر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-7","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"الإشارة: مَنْ دخل في طريق المخصوصين الأبرار، ثم لم تساعده رياح الأقدار، فلا ينبغي الكلام فيه، ولا الخوض في شأنه، لأن أمره بيد ربه، (من يهده الله فلا مضل له) ، ومن يضلل فلا ناصر له. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-8","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"ثم نهى عن مُوَالاَتهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-9","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"... فَلا تَتَّخِذُوا مِنْهُمْ أَوْلِياءَ حَتَّى يُهاجِرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَخُذُوهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوهُمْ حَيْثُ وَجَدْتُمُوهُمْ وَلا تَتَّخِذُوا مِنْهُمْ وَلِيًّا وَلا نَصِيراً (89) إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ يَصِلُونَ إِلى قَوْمٍ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِيثاقٌ أَوْ جاؤُكُمْ حَصِرَتْ صُدُورُهُمْ أَنْ يُقاتِلُوكُمْ أَوْ يُقاتِلُوا قَوْمَهُمْ وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَسَلَّطَهُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ فَلَقاتَلُوكُمْ فَإِنِ اعْتَزَلُوكُمْ فَلَمْ يُقاتِلُوكُمْ وَأَلْقَوْا إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ فَما جَعَلَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سَبِيلاً (90)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-10","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"قلت: (حَصِرت) : أي: ضاقت، والجملة حال من الواو، بدليل قراءة يعقوب (حَصِرَةً) .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-11","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فَلا تَتَّخِذُوا من هؤلاء الكفرة أَوْلِياءَ وأصدقاء حتى يتحقق إيمانهم، بأن يهاجروا من دار الكفر إلى دار الإسلام فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وابتغاء مرضات الله، لا لحرف دنيوي، فَإِنْ تَوَلَّوْا عن إظهار الإيمان بالهجرة فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، فَخُذُوهُمْ أسارى وَاقْتُلُوهُمْ حَيْثُ وَجَدْتُمُوهُمْ كسائر الكفرة، وجانبوهم وَلا تَتَّخِذُوا مِنْهُمْ وَلِيًّا وَلا نَصِيراً أي: لا تستعينوا بهم في جهادكم، إِلَّا الَّذِينَ يَصِلُونَ إِلى قَوْمٍ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ عهد، ومِيثاقٌ أي: مهادنة، فلهم حكم المُعَاهَدِين الذين وصلوا إليهم، ودخلوا معهم في الصلح، فلا تقتلوهم ولا تأسروهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-12","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"وكانت خزاعة وادعت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وعقدت معه الصلح، فجاء بنو مدلج فدخلوا معهم في الصلح، فنهى الله عن قتالهم ماداموا معهم، فالقوم الذين بين المسلمين وبينهم ميثاق هم خزاعة، والذين وصلوا إليهم هم بنو مدلج.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-13","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"فالاستثناء على هذا منقطع، لأن بني مدلج حينئٍذ كانت مظهرة للكفر لا منافقة، ويحتمل أن يكون متصلاً، أي: إلا الذين يصلون منهم ... الخ، فتأمل. وكان هذا في أول الإسلام، ثم نسخ بقوله: فَاقْتُلُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ حَيْثُ وَجَدْتُمُوهُمْ الآية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-14","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"ثم ذكر قومًا آخرين نهى عن قتالهم، فقال: أَوْ جاؤُكُمْ أي: إلّا قوما جاءوكم، قد حَصِرَتْ صُدُورُهُمْ أي: ضاقت عن أَنْ يُقاتِلُوكُمْ أَوْ يُقاتِلُوا قَوْمَهُمْ يعني أنهم كرهوا قتالهم، وكرهوا قتال قومهم الكفار، فلا تقتلوهم أيضًا، لأن الله كفَّ شرهم عنكم، وَلَوْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَسَلَّطَهُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ بأن قوَّى قلوبهم وأزال رعبهم فَلَقاتَلُوكُمْ ولم يكفّوا عنكم، فَإِنِ اعْتَزَلُوكُمْ ولم يتعرّضوا لكم وَأَلْقَوْا إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ أي: الاستسلام والانقياد فَما جَعَلَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سَبِيلًا أي: طريقًا إلى قتالهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-15","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"الإشارة: نهى الله تعالى عن مساكنة النفوس وموالاتها، حتى تهاجر عن مواطن شهواتها إلى حضرة ربها، فإن تولت عن الهجرة وألِفَت البطالةَ والغفلة فليأخذها ليقتلها حيثما ظهرت صورتها، ولا يسكن إليها أبدًا أو يواليها، إلاَّ إن وصلت إلى حضرة الشيخ، وأمره بالرفق بها، أو كفت عن طغيانها، أو كفى الله أمرها بجذبٍ أخرجها عن عوائدها، أو واردٍ قوَّى دفع شهواتها، فإنه يأتي من حضرة قهّار، لا يصادم شيئاً إلا دمغه، وهذه عناية من الرحمن، ولو شاء الله تعالى لسلطها على الإنسان يرخى لها العنان، فتجمح به في ضَحضَاح النيران، فإن كفت النفس عن شهواتها، وانقادت إلى حضرة ربها، فما لأحدٍ عليها من سبيل، وقد دخلت في حمى الملك الجليل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-16","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_089-17","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"4:89–90 · Emigration, hostility, and protected parties","text":"ثم ذكر صنفا آخر من المنافقين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_089-17"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_089-s1","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"Running commentary","text":"Continuation of the previous exposition. God describes those persons as wishing that the believers would become unbelievers like themselves, thus becoming their equals in error and unbelief.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_089-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_089-s2","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"to the previous verse","text":"Whoever entered the path of the specially chosen and righteous but was not helped by the winds of decree should not become the subject of speculative talk or intrusive inquiry. His case rests with his Lord: no one can misguide a person God guides, and no one can assist a person left astray. God gives success and directs to the straight path.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_089-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_089-s3","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"","text":"I say: ḥaṣirat means that their breasts were constricted. The sentence is circumstantial ( ḥāl ) in relation to the plural pronoun. This is corroborated by Yaʿqūb's reading ḥaṣiratan in adjectival form, “constricted.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_089-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_089-s4","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"","text":"God prohibits taking the people just described as close allies and protectors before their faith is manifest in emigration from the abode of unbelief to the abode of Islam, for God's sake rather than for a worldly advantage. If they turn away from manifesting faith through emigration in God’s way, Ibn ʿAjība explains the command as: ‘Take them captive and kill them wherever you find them, like the other unbelievers.’ He adds that they are to be shunned. They are not to be relied upon as helpers in the believers' military expeditions. Yet people who attach themselves to a party with whom Muslims have a treaty share the protections of those bound by the treaty: they are neither to be killed nor taken captive. He identifies the treaty partners in one report as Khuzāʿa, with whom the Prophet made a peace agreement, and those joining them as Banū Mudlij. The command not to fight the latter held while they remained protected by that agreement. On this account the grammatical exception is disconnected ( istithnāʾ munqaṭiʿ ), since Banū Mudlij were openly unbelievers, not the hypocrites first mentioned. Alternatively it is connected, referring to those among the first group who joined a treaty-bound people. Ibn ʿAjība adds the traditional exegetical claim that the early rule was later abrogated by the verse “Kill the polytheists wherever you find them” (9:5). [Translator’s note: This is a report of his exegetical position; it is not an unrestricted legal instruction, and the conditions and debates over abrogation require independent juristic examination.] A second protected class consists of people who come unwilling either to fight the Muslims or to fight their own kin. Their hearts recoil from both engagements. They too are not to be fought, for God has restrained the harm they might otherwise have done. Had He removed their fear and strengthened their resolve, they could have fought. But if they keep apart, refrain from hostilities and offer peaceful submission or a peace agreement, there is no legitimate cause to attack them.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_089-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_089-s5","r":"q4_cont_089","title":"","text":"The prohibition can also be applied to intimate accommodation of one's lower soul ( nafs ), until it emigrates from the dwelling places of its desires to the Presence of its Lord. If it turns away from this emigration and becomes accustomed to idleness and heedlessness, Ibn ʿAjība enjoins seizing and slaying it wherever its form appears, never settling with it or befriending it. Yet if it reaches the spiritual master's presence and he directs gentleness toward it, if it desists from tyranny, or if a divine attraction ( jadhb ) or incoming spiritual impulse ( wārid ) drives it out of its habits and repels its appetites, it should no longer be treated in that manner. Such help proceeds from the Presence of the All-Subduer: it strikes nothing without crushing it. This is care from the All-Merciful. Were God to give the soul unrestricted power, it would bolt toward the shallows of the Fire. Once it restrains its passions and yields to its Lord, no one has a cause against it: it has entered the sanctuary of the Sovereign. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_089-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_091","r":"q4_cont_091","title":"4:91 · Those who seek protection from both sides","text":"4:91 · Those who seek protection from both sides 4:91","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_091"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_091-1","r":"q4_cont_091","title":"4:91 · Those who seek protection from both sides","text":"سَتَجِدُونَ آخَرِينَ يُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يَأْمَنُوكُمْ وَيَأْمَنُوا قَوْمَهُمْ كُلَّما رُدُّوا إِلَى الْفِتْنَةِ أُرْكِسُوا فِيها فَإِنْ لَمْ يَعْتَزِلُوكُمْ وَيُلْقُوا إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ وَيَكُفُّوا أَيْدِيَهُمْ فَخُذُوهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوهُمْ حَيْثُ ثَقِفْتُمُوهُمْ وَأُولئِكُمْ جَعَلْنا لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطاناً مُبِيناً (91)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_091-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_091-2","r":"q4_cont_091","title":"4:91 · Those who seek protection from both sides","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: سَتَجِدُونَ قوماً آخَرِينَ منافقين، وهم أسد وغطفان، قَدِمُوا المدينة، وأظهروا الإسلام نفاقًا ورياء إذا لقوا النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قالوا: إنا على دينك، يريدون الأمن، إذا لقوا قومهم، وقالوا لأحدهم: لماذا أسلمت، ومن تعبد؟ فيقول: لهذا القرد ولهذا العقرب والخنفساء، يُرِيدُونَ بإظهار الإسلام أَنْ يَأْمَنُوكُمْ وَيَأْمَنُوا قَوْمَهُمْ، كُلَّما رُدُّوا إِلَى الْفِتْنَةِ أُرْكِسُوا فِيها، أي: كلما دُعُوا إلى الكفر رَجَعُوا إليه أقبحَ رد، فَإِنْ لَمْ يَعْتَزِلُوكُمْ وَيُلْقُوا إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ أي: ولم يلقوا إليكم المسالمة والصلح، ولم يَكُفُّوا أَيْدِيَهُمْ بأن تعرضوا لكم فَخُذُوهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوهُمْ حَيْثُ ثَقِفْتُمُوهُمْ أي: وجدتموهم، وَأُولئِكُمْ جَعَلْنا لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطاناً، أي: تسلطاً مُبِيناً ظاهرًا، لظهور كفرهم وثبوت عداوتهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_091-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_091-3","r":"q4_cont_091","title":"4:91 · Those who seek protection from both sides","text":"الإشارة: النفوس على ثلاثة أقسام: قسم مطلقة العنان في الجرائم والعصيان، وهي النفوس الأمارة، وإليها الإشارة بالآية قبلها، والله أعلم. وقسم مذبذبة تارة تظهر الطاعة والإذعان، تريد أن يأمنها صاحبها، وتارة ترجع إلى الغي والعصيان، مهما دعيت إلى فتنة وقعت فيها، فإن لم تنته عن ذلك، وتكف عن غيها، فالواجب جهادها وقتلها حتى تنقاد بالكلية إلى ربها، وأما النفس المطمئنة فلا كلام معها لتحقق إسلامها، فالواجب الكف عنها وحبها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_091-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_091-4","r":"q4_cont_091","title":"4:91 · Those who seek protection from both sides","text":"ولما فرغ من حفظ الأديان تكلم على بقية حفظ الأبدان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_091-4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_091-s1","r":"q4_cont_091","title":"","text":"God speaks of another class of hypocrites, identified in the report as men of Asad and Ghaṭafān. On coming to Medina they professed Islam and told the Prophet they followed his religion, seeking security. On returning to their kin, when asked why and whom they worshipped, one answered derisively that he worshipped a monkey, a scorpion and a beetle. Such persons sought safety with both sides. Each time they were summoned to unbelief they plunged into it more shamefully. If they refuse separation from hostilities, decline to offer peace and do not restrain their hands from attacking, the text commands, “Seize them and kill them wherever you find them,” and states that clear authority has been granted against them, because their unbelief is manifest and their hostility established. [Translator’s note: This interpretation is Ibn ʿAjība's description of the passage's historical combatants.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_091-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_091-s2","r":"q4_cont_091","title":"","text":"Lower souls fall into three classes. Some are wholly unrestrained in crime and disobedience—the commanding soul ( al-nafs al-ammāra ), alluded to by the preceding verses. Others vacillate: they display obedience and submission to reassure their possessor, then return to error and disobedience whenever temptation calls. So long as they refuse to desist, Ibn ʿAjība declares struggle against them and their “slaying” obligatory until they yield wholly to their Lord. As for the soul at peace ( al-nafs al-muṭmaʾinna ), there is no conflict with it: its submission has become real, and it must be left alone and loved. Having treated the safeguarding of religion, the commentary next turns to the safeguarding of human lives.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_091-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_092","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation 4:92","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_092"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-1","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"وَما كانَ لِمُؤْمِنٍ أَنْ يَقْتُلَ مُؤْمِناً إِلاَّ خَطَأً وَمَنْ قَتَلَ مُؤْمِناً خَطَأً فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُؤْمِنَةٍ وَدِيَةٌ مُسَلَّمَةٌ إِلى أَهْلِهِ إِلاَّ أَنْ يَصَّدَّقُوا فَإِنْ كانَ مِنْ قَوْمٍ عَدُوٍّ لَكُمْ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُؤْمِنَةٍ وَإِنْ كانَ مِنْ قَوْمٍ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِيثاقٌ فَدِيَةٌ مُسَلَّمَةٌ إِلى أَهْلِهِ وَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُؤْمِنَةٍ فَمَنْ لَمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتابِعَيْنِ تَوْبَةً مِنَ اللَّهِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً (92)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-2","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"قلت: (وما كان لمؤمن) النفي هنا بمعنى النهي، كقوله: وَما كانَ لَكُمْ أَنْ تُؤْذُوا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، و (إلا خطًأ) : استثناء منقطع، و (خطأ) : حال، أو مفعول من أجله، أو صفة لمصدر محذوف، أي: لا يحل له أن يقتل مؤمنًا في حال من الأحوال، لكن إن وقع خطأ فحكمه ما يأتي. وقيل: متصل. انظر ابن جزي. أو: إلا قتلا خطأ، و (إلا أن يصدقوا) : حال، أي: إلا حال تصدقهم، و (توبة) : مفعول من أجله، أي: شرع ذلك لأجل التوبة. أو، مصدر، أي: تاب عليكم توبة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-3","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَما كانَ ينبغي لِمُؤْمِنٍ أَنْ يَقْتُلَ مُؤْمِناً مثله، أي: هو حرام عليه، إِلَّا أن يقتله خَطَأً بأن ظنه كافرًا، أو رمى غيرَه فصادفه. والآية نزلت بسبب قتل عياش بن ربيعة للحارث بن زيد، وكان الحارث يعذبه على الإسلام، ثم أسلم الحارث، وهاجر، ولم يعلم عياشُ بإسلامه، فقتله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-4","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"ثم ذكر حُكمه فقال: وَمَنْ قَتَلَ مُؤْمِناً خَطَأً فَتَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ أي: فعليه تحرير رقبة مُؤْمِنَةٍ سالمة من العيوب، ليس فيها شوب حرية، تكون من مال القاتل، وَدِيَةٌ مُسَلَّمَةٌ أي: مدفوعة إِلى أَهْلِهِ وهي على العاقلة كما بيّن الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام-، وهي عند مالك: مائة من الإبل على أهل الإبل، وألف دينار شرعية على أهل الذهب، واثنا عشر ألف درهم، على أهل الوَرِق، مقسطة على ثلاث سنين، فإن لم تكن العاقلة فعلى بيت المال، وتقسم على أهله، على حسب المواريث، إلا أن يتصدقوا بالدية على القاتل فتسقط، أي: تسمح فيها الورثة أو القتيل قبل موته.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-5","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"فَإِنْ كانَ المقتول مِنْ قَوْمٍ عَدُوٍّ لَكُمْ أي: محاربين لكم، وَهُوَ أي: المقتول مُؤْمِنٌ فعلى القاتل تَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُؤْمِنَةٍ ولا دية لأنهم محاربون فيتقووا بها على المسلمين، ورأى مالك أن الدية في هذا واجبة لبيت المال، وَإِنْ كانَ المقتول مؤمنًا وهو مِنْ قَوْمٍ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِيثاقٌ أي: عقد الصلح أو الذمة، فعلى القاتل دِيَةٌ مُسَلَّمَةٌ إِلى أَهْلِهِ، وعليه أيضًا تَحْرِيرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُؤْمِنَةٍ كفارة لخطئه. فإن كان غير مؤمن فلا كفارة فيه. وفيه نصف دية المسلم، فَمَنْ لَمْ يَجِدْ الرقبة، أو لم يقدر عليها فعليه فَصِيامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتابِعَيْنِ عوضًا من العتق، جعل الله ذلك تَوْبَةً مِنَ اللَّهِ على القاتل لتفريطه. وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً بما فرض، حَكِيماً فيما قدَّر ودبَّر. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-6","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الحق- جلّ جلاله- قد رغَّب في إحياء النفوس، حسًا ومعنًى، ونهى عن قتلها حسًا ومعنًى، وما ذلك إلا لخصوص محبة له فيها، ومزيد اعتناء له بشأنها فليس في الوجود أعز عند الله من مظهر هذا الآدمي إن استقام في العبودية لربه، فهو قلب الوجود، ومن أجله ظهر كل موجود، وهو المنظور إليه من هذا العالم السفلي، والمقصود بالخطاب التكليفي: جزئي وكلي، فهو المقصود من بيت القصيد، وهو المحبوب إليه، دون سائر العبيد، قال تعالى: وَاصْطَنَعْتُكَ لِنَفْسِي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-7","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"ومعنى إحيائها حسًّا: إنقاذها من الهلاك الحسّي، ومعنى إحيائها معنى: إنقاذها من الهلاك المعنوي كالجهل والغفلة، حتى تحيا بالعلم والإيمان واليقظة، ومعنى قتلها حسًا: إهلاكها، ومعنى قتلها معنًى: إيقاعها في المعاصي والكفر وحملها على ذلك، وكذلك إهانتها وذلها، ولذلك قال عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «لَعنُ المُؤمن كَقَتَلهِ» . فأمر من قتله خطًأ أن يحيى نفسا أخرى فى مقابلتها بإخراجها من موت إهانة الرق، فإن لم يقدر، فليحى نفسه بقتل صولتها بالجوع حتى تنكسر، فتحيا بالتوبة واليقظة، ويُجبر كسر أهل المقتول بالدية المسلّمة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_092-8","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"4:92 · Unintentional killing and compensation","text":"هذا كله فى تفريطه وقلة حزمه حتى قتل خطأ، وأما إن قتله عمدا، فأشار إليه الحقّ جلّ جلاله بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_092-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_092-s1","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"","text":"I say: “It is not for a believer” uses formal negation with the force of prohibition, as in “It is not for you to hurt the Messenger of God.” “Except by mistake” can be a disconnected exception ( istithnāʾ munqaṭiʿ ): killing a believer is not permitted in any circumstance, but where it accidentally happens the following ruling applies. Khaṭaʾan can be parsed as a circumstantial expression, an accusative of cause, or the qualification of a suppressed verbal noun; some construe the exception as connected—compare Ibn Juzayy—or supply “except a killing committed by mistake.” “Unless they remit it” describes the circumstance of voluntary renunciation. Tawbatan can express purpose (“to bring about repentance”) or be a verbal noun (“He turned toward you in repentance”).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_092-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_092-s2","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"","text":"God forbids one believer to kill another. Mistaken killing may occur when someone takes a believer to be an unbeliever or a projectile meant for someone else strikes the believer. Ibn ʿAjība relates the verse to ʿAyyāsh ibn Rabīʿa's killing of al-Ḥārith ibn Zayd: al-Ḥārith had formerly tormented him for accepting Islam, then himself converted and emigrated, but ʿAyyāsh did not know of the conversion. For unintentional killing, the killer must emancipate a believing slave free of disqualifying defects and of any partial freedom, at his own expense. Blood-money ( diya ) is delivered to the family and borne by the ʿāqila , the kin-group financially responsible for accidental homicide, as clarified in the Prophetic practice. Ibn ʿAjība records the Mālikī calculation as one hundred camels for camel owners, a thousand legally reckoned gold dinars for those using gold, or twelve thousand silver dirhams for those using silver, distributed over three years. If there is no ʿāqila , the public treasury bears the amount. The recipients share according to inheritance shares unless the heirs, or the victim before dying, freely remit it to the killer, in which case it lapses. If the slain believer belongs to a hostile people, emancipation remains obligatory but, on one account, no blood-money is paid to the enemy, since it could strengthen them militarily; Mālik is reported to require its payment instead to the public treasury. If a believing victim is from a treaty-bound community, both compensation to the family and emancipation are due. Ibn ʿAjība also distinguishes the case of a nonbelieving victim in such a community, for whom he does not require the same expiation and assigns half the compensation of a Muslim according to the school position he reports. If a believing slave is unavailable or unaffordable, the substitute is two consecutive months of fasting. God instituted this as repentance for the killer's neglect of due caution; He knows what He has imposed and judges wisely. [Translator’s note: These are historical legal positions; their application depends upon the relevant legal jurisdiction and juristic conditions.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_092-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_092-s3","r":"q4_cont_092","title":"","text":"God encourages reviving souls both outwardly and inwardly, and forbids killing them in either respect. This is because of His particular love for human souls and His special care for them. Nothing in existence is dearer to God than this human manifestation when the human being stands upright in servanthood to his Lord. He is the heart of existence; for his sake every existent has appeared. He is the one regarded in this lower world and the intended addressee of the religious charge, particular and general. He is the very point of it all, the one beloved to God above the rest of His servants. “I have fashioned you for Myself” (20:41) is cited. To give sensory life is to save from bodily destruction; to give inward life is to rescue from ignorance and heedlessness so that one lives by knowledge, faith and awakening. Bodily killing is to destroy the person; inward killing is to draw someone into sins or unbelief or to humiliate and abase them. The Prophet's reported saying “Cursing a believer is like killing him” illustrates this dignity. The one who kills unintentionally is therefore told to restore life to another human being by liberating that person from the humiliation of slavery. If incapable of this, one revives one's own spiritual life by bringing its arrogance low through hunger, so that repentance and watchfulness renew it. The financial compensation also repairs the distress of the bereaved family. Such provisions answer the negligence and want of care that led to the accidental killing. Deliberate murder receives the much more severe warning of the next verse.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_092-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_093","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning 4:93","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_093"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-1","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"وَمَنْ يَقْتُلْ مُؤْمِناً مُتَعَمِّداً فَجَزاؤُهُ جَهَنَّمُ خالِداً فِيها وَغَضِبَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَلَعَنَهُ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُ عَذاباً عَظِيماً (93)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-2","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ يَقْتُلْ مُؤْمِناً مُتَعَمِّداً مستحلاً لقتله فَجَزاؤُهُ جَهَنَّمُ خالِداً فِيها وَغَضِبَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَلَعَنَهُ أي: طرده وَأَعَدَّ لَهُ عَذاباً عَظِيماً، وقولُنا: مستحلاً لقتله، هو أحد الأجوبة عن شبهة المعتزلة القائلين بتخليد عصاة المؤمنين في النار. ومن جُملتهم: قاتل النفس.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-3","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"ومذهب أهل السنة: أنه لا يخلد إلا الكافر، ويؤيد هذا الجواب سبب نزول الآية، لأنها نزلت في كافر، وهو (مَقِيس بن ضُبَابة الكناني) وَجَدَ أخَاه هشامًا قَتَيلاً في بني النجار- وكان مُسلمًا- فذكر ذلك للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم فأرسَل مَعهُ رجلاً من بني فهرِ، وقال له: «ائت بني النّجار، وقُل لهم: إن عَلمتُم قاتِل هِشَامٍ فادفَعُوهُ لمقيس يَقتَصُّ مِنه، وإن لم تَعلمُوا فادفَعُوا إليه الدَّيةَ» . فقالوا: سمعًا وطاعة، لم نَعلَم قاتِله، فجمعوا مائة من الإبل، فأخذها، ثم انصرفا راجعَين إلى المدينة، فوسوس إليه الشيطان، وقال: أيَّ شيء صَنَعتَ؟ تَقبلُ ديةَ أخيكَ فتكونُ عليك سُبَّة، اقتل الرجلَ الذِي مَعكَ فتكُونَ نفسٌ مكانَ نَفسٍ وفَضلُ الدِّيَة، فَقَتَلَه وأخذ الدِّية، فنزلت فيه الآية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-4","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"أو يكون الخلود عبارة عن طول المكث، والجمهور على قبول توبته، خلافًا لابن عباس، ونُقِل عنه أيضًا قبولها، ولعله تعالى استغنى عن ذكر التوبة هنا اكتفاء بذكرها في الفرقان، حيث قال: وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ يَلْقَ أَثاماً ثم قال: إِلَّا مَنْ تابَ. وأما من قال: إن تلك منسوخة بهذه فليس بصحيح لأن النسخ لا يكون في الأخبار. أو فجزاؤه إن جُوزِي، ولا بِدع في خلف الوعيد لقوله: وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذلِكَ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ لأن الوعيد","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-5","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"مشروط بعدم العفو، لدلائل منفصلة اقتضت ذلك كما هو مشروط بعدم التوبة أيضًا، والحاصل: أن الوعد لا يخلف لأنه من باب الامتنان، والوعيد يصح إخلافه بالعفو والغفران، كما في بعض الأخبار عن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-6","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"«مَن وَعَدَه الله- عز وجل- على عملٍ ثوابًا فهو منجزه له لا محالة، ومَن أوعَدَه على عمل عقابًا فهو بالخيار، إن شاءَ عَفَا عنه، وإن شاء عَاقَبه» . هـ. ذكره في القوت.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-7","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"فَتَحَصَّل أن القاتل لا يُخلَّد على المشهور إلاَّ إذا كان مستحلاً، وهذا أيضًا ما لم يقتص منه، وأما إذا اقتُص منه فالصحيح أنه يسقط عنه العقاب لقول النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «مَن أصَابَ ذَنبًا فعُوقِبَ به في الدنيا فهو له كَفَّارَةٌ» . وبه قال الجمهور، وكذلك إذا سَامَحَهُ ورثةُ الدم لأنه حق ورثوه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-8","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"الإشارة: الإيمان محله القلوب، فالقلب هو المتصف بالإيمان حقيقة. فالمؤمن الحقيقي هو القلب، فمن قتله بتتبع الشهوات، وتراكم الغفلات، فجزاؤه نار القطيعة في سجن الأكوان، والبعد عن عرفان الشهود والعيان، وفي الحِكَم: «سبب العذاب وجود الحجاب، وإتمام النعيم بالنظر إلى وجهه الكريم» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_093-9","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"4:93 · Deliberate murder and its warning","text":"ثم إن اللسان ترجمان القلب، فمن أظهر الإيمان حرم التعرض له، كما أشار إلى ذلك الحقّ جلّ جلاله بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_093-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_093-s1","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"Outward interpretation and the theological dispute","text":"Ibn ʿAjība adds the qualification “regarding his killing as lawful” ( mustaḥillan li-qatlihi ). This supplies one Sunni answer to the Muʿtazilite inference that a believer guilty of grave sin, including murder, must abide eternally in Hell. In the Sunni position he describes, none except an unbeliever remains there forever. He supports this answer with the verse’s occasion of revelation, saying that it concerned an unbeliever, Miqyās ibn Ḍubāba al-Kinānī. Finding his brother Hishām murdered among Banū al-Najjār, Miqyās complained to the Prophet. A messenger was sent with him, directing the clan to surrender the known murderer for retaliation, or, if the killer was unknown, to pay blood-money. They said they did not know the perpetrator and paid a hundred camels. On the return journey, Satan suggested to Miqyās that accepting compensation would bring disgrace; Miqyās killed the accompanying messenger and kept the camels. The verse is said to have been revealed concerning this deed. Another explanation takes “abiding” to mean a very long sojourn rather than eternity. The majority, says Ibn ʿAjība, accept the murderer's repentance, contrary to one reported position of Ibn ʿAbbās, from whom acceptance of repentance is also transmitted. He proposes that repentance was not repeated here because it was already mentioned in al-Furqān (25:68–70), where a threat is followed by “except those who repent.” The assertion that this earlier passage has been abrogated by the present verse is, in his account, unsound because abrogation does not apply to straightforward reports. Or the expression may mean “that will be his recompense if he is recompensed with it .” God's waiving a threatened punishment by pardon is not impossible, for “He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills” (4:48). Threats of punishment presuppose the absence of pardon or repentance. A promise of beneficence is fulfilled, but a threatened penalty may be remitted by mercy. Ibn ʿAjība cites a reported Prophetic saying, attributed through al-Qūt , that God necessarily fulfils a promised reward but may either forgive or punish where He has threatened punishment. [Translator’s note: The source and strength of this particular wording require checking.] He concludes that, on the well-known view, the murderer is not eternally punished unless he has declared the killing lawful. He adds that worldly retaliation, when carried out, is understood by the majority to expiate the crime, adducing the Prophetic teaching that punishment suffered in this life is an expiation. He says the same applies when the heirs entitled to retaliation pardon him, because it is a right they have inherited.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_093-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_093-s2","r":"q4_cont_093","title":"","text":"Faith is properly the quality of the heart: the heart, in its reality, is the true believer. To kill the heart by the pursuit of passions and the accumulation of heedlessness merits the fire of separation, imprisonment within the created world and remoteness from direct recognition and witnessing. The Ḥikam is cited: the existence of a veil is the cause of torment, while bliss is completed by looking upon the face of the Generous One. The tongue translates the heart; hence outward profession of faith deserves protection, as the next verse makes clear.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_093-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_094","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action 4:94","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_094"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-1","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَتَبَيَّنُوا وَلا تَقُولُوا لِمَنْ أَلْقى إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ لَسْتَ مُؤْمِناً تَبْتَغُونَ عَرَضَ الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا فَعِنْدَ اللَّهِ مَغانِمُ كَثِيرَةٌ كَذلِكَ كُنْتُمْ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَمَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكُمْ فَتَبَيَّنُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيراً (94)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-2","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"قلت: (السَّلم) بالقصر: الانقياد والاستسلام، وبالمد: التحية. وجملة (تبتغون) : حال من الواو، مشعرة بما هو الحامل على العجلة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-3","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذا ضَرَبْتُمْ أي: سافرتم وسرتم تجاهدون فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ، فَتَبَيَّنُوا الأمور وتثبتوا فيها ولا تعجلوا، فإن العجلة من الشيطان، وَلا تَقُولُوا لِمَنْ أَلْقى إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ أي: الانقياد والاستسلام، أو سلَّم عليكم تحية الإسلام، لَسْتَ مُؤْمِناً إنما فعلت ذلك متعوذًا خائفًا، فتقتلونه طمعًا في ماله، تَبْتَغُونَ عَرَضَ الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا وحطامها الفاني، فَعِنْدَ اللَّهِ مَغانِمُ كَثِيرَةٌ وَعَدَكُم بها، لم تقدروا الآن عليها، فاصبروا وازهدوا فيما تَشُكُّون فيه حتى يأتيكم ما لا شبهة فيه، كَذلِكَ كُنْتُمْ مِنْ قَبْلُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-4","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"هذه الحال، كنتم تخفون إسلامكم خوفًا من قومكم، فَمَنَّ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكُمْ بالعز والنصر والاشتهار، فَتَبَيَّنُوا وتثبتوا ولا تعَجلَوا، وافعلوا بالداخلين في الإسلام كما فعل اللهُ بكم، حيث حفظكم وعصمكم، ولا تبادروا إلى قتلهم ظنًا بأنهم إنما دخلوا فيه اتقاء وخوفًا، فإن إبقاء ألف كافر أهون عند الله من قتل مؤمن، وتكريره تأكيد لتعظيم الأمر. ثم هدَّدهم بقوله إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيراً مطلعًا على قصدكم، فلا تتهافتوا في القتل، واحتاطوا فيه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-5","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"رُوِي أن سريةً لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم غزت أهل فَدَك فهربوا، وبقي مرداسُ ثقًة بإسلامه، لأنه كان مسلمًا وحده، فلما رأى الخيلَ ألجأ غَنَمه إلى عاقول من الجبل (1) ، وصعد عليه، فلما تلاحقوا وكَبَّروا، كَبَّر ونزل يقول: لا إله إلا الله محمد رسول الله، السلام عليكم، فقتله أسامةُ، واستاق غنمه، فنزلت الآية. فلما أخبر- عليه الصلاة والسلام- وَجِدَ وجدًا شديدًا، وقال لأسامة: «كيف بلا إله إلا الله إذا جاءت يوم القيامة؟!» قالها ثلاثًا، حتى قال أسامة: ليتني لم أكن أسلمتُ إلا يومئٍذ، ثم استغفرَ له بعدُ، وقال له: «اعتق رقبة» ، وقيل: نزلت في المقداد، مرَّ برجل في غنمه فأراد قتله، فقال: لا إله إلا الله، فقتله وظفر بأهله وماله، وقيل: القاتل: مُحلِّم بن جَثَامة، والمقتول: عامرُ بن الأضبط. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-6","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"الإشارة: يستفاد من الآية: الترغيب في خَصلتين ممدوحتين وخصوصًا عند الصوفية:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-7","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"الأولى: التأني في الأمور والرزانة والطمأنينة، وعدم العجلة والخفة والطيش. وفي الحديث: «من تَأنَّى أصابَ أو كادَ، ومَن استعجَّلَ أخطَأ أو كَادَ» . ولا يُقدم على أمر حتى يعلم حكم الله فيه، ويفهم عن الله أنه مراد الله في ذلك الوقت.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-8","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"والثانية: حُسْن الظن بعباد الله كافة، واعتقاد الخير فيهم، وعدم البحث عما اشتمل عليه بواطنهم، فقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «أُمِرتُ أن أحكم بالظواهر والله يتولى السرائر» (2) وقال لأسامة: «هلاّ شققت عن قلبه» ، حين قَتَلَ مَن قال: لا إله إلا الله، أو لغيره. وفي الحديث: «خصلتان ليس فوقهما شيء من الخير: حُسْن الظنِّ بالله، وحُسْن الظن بعباد الله، وخصلتان ليس فوقهما من الشر شيء: سوء الظن بالله، وسوء الظن بعباد الله» . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_094-9","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"4:94 · Discernment before taking action","text":"ولما نهى عن العجلة نهّضهم إلى الجهاد لئلا يتوهم أنها مذمومة حتى فى الجهاد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_094-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_094-s1","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"","text":"I say: salam or silm without lengthening denotes yielding and submission; salām with a long vowel means the greeting of peace. “Seeking” ( tabtaghūna ) forms a circumstantial clause exposing the motive that might prompt hasty action.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_094-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_094-s2","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"","text":"When travelling for struggle in God's way, the believers must scrutinise the facts and establish them instead of rushing to judgment, for haste is from Satan. Whoever manifests peaceful submission or offers the Islamic greeting must not be dismissed as an unbeliever merely suspected of speaking out of fear; otherwise the listener may kill him in desire for his goods, that perishing merchandise of worldly life. God has promised many lawful benefits not presently within reach; wait for what is free of suspicion instead of grabbing at doubtful spoils. Believers too once concealed their conversion out of fear of their own people; God then granted them dignity, victory and public recognition. Accordingly, they should extend protection to new entrants just as God protected them. He adds: “Sparing a thousand unbelievers is less grave in God’s sight than killing one believer.” Repeating the command to verify underscores the gravity of the matter. He knows hidden intentions and cautions against rash killing. Ibn ʿAjība relates an expedition against Fadak: the people fled, but Mirdās, a Muslim, stayed with his sheep, trusting in his religion. Seeing cavalry approach, he led his flock into a bend in the mountain and climbed above it. When the soldiers pronounced takbīr , he did likewise, came down proclaiming the two testimonies and greeted them. In the report, Usāma killed him and took his sheep. The Prophet was deeply distressed and asked three times, “What will you do with ‘There is no god but God’ when it comes on the Day of Resurrection?” Usāma wished his conversion had occurred only after that event. The account adds a prayer for forgiveness and an instruction to emancipate a slave. Another account says the verse concerned al-Miqdād: he passed a man among his sheep and intended to kill him; the man said, “There is no god but God,” but al-Miqdād killed him and took possession of his family and property. Another report names the killer as Muḥallim ibn Jaththāma and the victim as ʿĀmir ibn al-Aḍbaṭ. [Translator’s note: The accounts differ in their chains and details.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_094-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_094-s3","r":"q4_cont_094","title":"","text":"Two praised dispositions are drawn out, especially for Sufis. First, deliberation, gravity, tranquillity and freedom from haste, fickleness and impulsiveness. A reported saying has it that the deliberate person is right, or nearly so, while the hasty person errs, or nearly so. Do not undertake a matter before understanding God's ruling concerning it and discerning what God wills of you at that moment. Second, cultivate good opinion of all God's servants. Assume the best rather than probing their inner secrets. Ibn ʿAjība quotes the Prophet as saying, “I have been commanded to judge by outward appearances, while God takes charge of the inner secrets.” The Prophet is reported to have asked Usāma—or, Ibn ʿAjība adds, someone else— “Did you split open his heart?” Ibn ʿAjība additionally transmits the saying that nothing exceeds good opinion of God and of God's servants in goodness, or exceeds bad opinion of them in evil. [Translator’s note: Its Prophetic attribution also requires independent verification.] God knows best. The next passage urges active striving lest the warning against precipitancy be misunderstood as a rejection of decisive effort.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_094-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_095","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain 4:95–96","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_095"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-1","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"لا يَسْتَوِي الْقاعِدُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ غَيْرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ وَالْمُجاهِدُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ بِأَمْوالِهِمْ وَأَنْفُسِهِمْ فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ الْمُجاهِدِينَ بِأَمْوالِهِمْ وَأَنْفُسِهِمْ عَلَى الْقاعِدِينَ دَرَجَةً وَكُلاًّ وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْحُسْنى وَفَضَّلَ اللَّهُ الْمُجاهِدِينَ عَلَى الْقاعِدِينَ أَجْراً عَظِيماً (95) دَرَجاتٍ مِنْهُ وَمَغْفِرَةً وَرَحْمَةً وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً (96)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-2","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"قلت: (من المؤمنين) : حال من (القاعدين) ، و (غير) بالرفع: صفة للقاعدين، وبالنصب: حال، وبالجر: بدل من المؤمنين، و (درجة) : نصب على إسقاط الخافض، أو على المصدر، لأنه متضمن معنى التفضيل، أو على الحال، أي: ذوي درجة. و (أجرًا عظيمًا) : مصدر لفضَّل، لأنه بمعنى أجرًا، أو مفعول ثان لفضَّل، لأنه بمعنى أعطى، أي: أعطاهم زيادة على القاعدين أجرًا عظيمًا، و (درجات) وما بعده، كل واحد بدل من (أجرًا) ، و (درجات) : نصب على المصدر، كقولك: ضربته أسواطًا، و (أجرًا) : حال، تقدمت عليها لأنها نكرة، و (مغفرة ورحمة) : على المصدر بإضمار فعلهما.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-3","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله ترغيبًا في الجهاد: لا يَسْتَوِي الْقاعِدُونَ عن الجهاد مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ مع المجاهدين في سبيل الله في الدرجة والأجر العظيم. ولما نزلت أتى ابنُ أم مكتوم وعبد الله بن جحش، وهما أعميان فقالا: يا رسول الله ذكرَ الله فضيلةَ المجاهدين على القاعدين، وحالُنا على ما ترى، ونحن نشتهي الجهاد، فهل من رخصة؟ فأنزل الله: غَيْرُ أُولِي الضَّرَرِ، فجعل لهم من الأجر ما جعل للمجاهدين لزمانتهم وحسن نياتهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-4","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"ثم ذكر فضل مَن خرج على من قعد لعذٍر فقال: فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ الْمُجاهِدِينَ بِأَمْوالِهِمْ، مواساة للمجاهدين، وَأَنْفُسِهِمْ ببذلها في سبيل رب العالمين، عَلَى الْقاعِدِينَ لعذر، دَرَجَةً واحدة، لمزيد مشقة السفر والغزو والخطر بالنفس للموت، وَكُلًّا من القاعدين لعلة والمجاهدين في سبيل الله، وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْحُسْنى أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-5","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"المثوبة الحسنى، وهي الجنة. وَفَضَّلَ اللَّهُ الْمُجاهِدِينَ عَلَى الْقاعِدِينَ من غير عذر أَجْراً عَظِيماً وخيرًا جسيمًا. وفي البخاري: «إنَّ لله مائة درجة أعدّها الله للمجاهدين في سبيلِ الله، ما بينَ الدَرجتين كَمَا بَيْنَ السَّماءِ والأرضِ» . الحديث. ثم بيَّنها بقوله دَرَجاتٍ مِنْهُ أي: من فضله وإحسانه، وَمَغْفِرَةً لذنوبه، وَرَحْمَةً تُقرِّبه إلى ربه، وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفُوراً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-6","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"لِما عسى أن يفرط منه، رَحِيماً بما وعدَ له.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-7","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"الإشارة: لا يستوي القاعد مع حظوظه وهواه، مشتغلاً بتربية جاهه وماله وتحصيل مُناه، غافلاً عن السير إلى حضرة مولاه، مع الذي سلَّ سيفَ العزم في جهاد نفسه وهواه، وبذل مهجته وجاهد نفسه في طلب رضاه، حتى وصل إلى شهود أنوار جماله وسناه، هيهات هيهات، لا يستوي الأحياء مع الأموات، فإن قعد مع نفسه لعذر يُظهره، مع محبته لطريق القوم وإقراره لأهل الخصوصية، فقد فضَّل الله عليه المجاهدين لنفوسهم بدرجة الشهود ومعرفة العيان للملك الودود، وإن قعد لغير عذر مع الإنكار لأهل الخصوصية، فقد فضَّل الله عليه المجاهدين أجرًا عظيمًا، درجات منه بالترقي أبدًا، ومغفرة ورحمة، وفي البيضاوي: التفضيل بدرجة في جهاد الكفار، وبدرجات في جهاد النفس لأنه الأكبر للحديث. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_095-8","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"4:95–96 · Those who strive and those who remain","text":"ثم ذكر حكم من تخلف عن الهجرة والجهاد حتى مات، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_095-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_095-s1","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"","text":"I say: “Among the believers” is circumstantial in relation to those who remain behind. Ghayr (“apart from”) may be nominative, as an adjective of “those remaining”; accusative, as a ḥāl ; or genitive, as a substitute ( badal ) for “believers.” Darajatan (“a degree”) may depend on an omitted preposition, express the meaning of the verbal action of preferring, or describe persons possessing a degree. Ajran ʿaẓīman (“a mighty recompense”) may be a verbal equivalent of “preferred,” or its second object when it means “granted”; “degrees,” “forgiveness” and “mercy” are each construed as a substitute ( badal ) for “recompense”. He offers further possibilities, including an accusative of verbal action ( mafʿūl muṭlaq ), a circumstantial expression placed before its referent because that referent is indefinite, and supplied verbal nouns for forgiveness and mercy.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_095-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_095-s2","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"","text":"In encouraging struggle, God denies that those who sit out fighting and those who expend property and life for His cause possess equal degrees or recompense. Ibn ʿAjība reports that, upon revelation of the initial wording, the two blind men Ibn Umm Maktūm and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaḥsh came to the Prophet, desiring to strive but asking what concession their condition allowed. “Except those suffering injury or disability” was then revealed; on account of their inability and sincere intention they were awarded the recompense of those who strove. The striving combatant gives possessions to help other combatants and offers his life in God's way. He excels the one staying behind for a genuine excuse by one degree on account of fatigue, travel and risk of death. Both such categories have been promised Paradise. Those who stay behind without an excuse are contrasted with combatants who receive a vastly greater reward. Ibn ʿAjība cites the report in al-Bukhārī of one hundred degrees God has prepared for those who strive in His way, separated like heaven and earth. These degrees issue from His generosity; forgiveness removes sins, and mercy brings one near to Him.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_095-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_095-s3","r":"q4_cont_095","title":"","text":"The person content to sit with personal pleasures and inclinations, increasing position and wealth and pursuing private hopes while neglecting the journey to his Lord, is not equal to the one who draws the sword of determination against the lower soul and submits his life to the search for divine acceptance until he witnesses the lights of divine beauty. The living and the dead cannot be equal. One detained by genuine incapacity but loving the path and acknowledging its special people is beneath those who struggle against their souls by one degree—that of direct witnessing and immediate knowledge of the Loving Sovereign. Someone staying away without excuse while denying the people of the special way is separated by many degrees from those who keep advancing, with forgiveness and mercy. Ibn ʿAjība reports from al-Bayḍāwī a distinction between a degree for outward struggle and degrees for the greater struggle against the soul, as explained by a cited tradition. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_095-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_097","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration 4:97–99","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_097"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-1","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَفَّاهُمُ الْمَلائِكَةُ ظالِمِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ قالُوا فِيمَ كُنْتُمْ قالُوا كُنَّا مُسْتَضْعَفِينَ فِي الْأَرْضِ قالُوا أَلَمْ تَكُنْ أَرْضُ اللَّهِ واسِعَةً فَتُهاجِرُوا فِيها فَأُولئِكَ مَأْواهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ وَساءَتْ مَصِيراً (97) إِلاَّ الْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ مِنَ الرِّجالِ وَالنِّساءِ وَالْوِلْدانِ لا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ حِيلَةً وَلا يَهْتَدُونَ سَبِيلاً (98) فَأُولئِكَ عَسَى اللَّهُ أَنْ يَعْفُوَ عَنْهُمْ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَفُوًّا غَفُوراً (99)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-2","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"يقول الحق جلَ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تتوفاهم الْمَلائِكَةُ أي: ملك الموت وأعوانه، يعني: تَقبِضُ أرواحهم، ظالِمِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ بترك الهجرة ومرافقة الكفرة، قالُوا أي: الملائكة في توبيخهم: فِيمَ كُنْتُمْ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-3","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"في أي شيء كنتم من أمر دينكم: أعلى الشك أو اليقين؟ أو: في أي بلد كنتم: في دار الكفر أو الإسلام؟ قالُوا كُنَّا مُسْتَضْعَفِينَ فِي الْأَرْضِ فعجزنا عن الهجرة وإظهار الدين خوفًا من المشركين، قالُوا أي: الملائكة تكذيبًا لهم وتبكيتًا: أَلَمْ تَكُنْ أَرْضُ اللَّهِ واسِعَةً فَتُهاجِرُوا فِيها إلى قطر آخر، كما فعل المهاجرون إلى الحبشة والمدينة، لكن حبستكم أموالُكم، وعزَّت عليكم أنفسكم، فَأُولئِكَ مَأْواهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ لتركهم الهجرة الواجبة في ذلك الوقت، ومساعدتهم الكفار على غزو المسلمين، وَساءَتْ مَصِيراً أي: قبحت مصيرا جهنم التي يصيرون إليها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-4","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"نزلت في ناس من أهل مكة تكلموا بالإسلام ولم يُهاجروا، فخرجوا يوم بدر مع المشركين فرأوا قلةَ المسلمين، فقالوا: غرَّ هؤلاء دينُهم، فقُتِلوا، فضربت الملائكة وجوههم وأدبارهم، كما يأتي، فلا تجوز الإقامة تحت حكم الكفر مع الاستطاعة، بل تجب الهجرة، ولا عذر في المقام، وإن منعه مانعٌ فلا يكون راضيًا بحاله مطمئنَ النفس بذلك، وإلا عمَّهُ البلاءُ، كما وقع لأهل الأندلس، حتى صار أولادُهم كفارًا والعياذ بالله، وكذلك لا تجوز الإقامة في موضعٍ تغلبُ فيه المعاصي وترك الدين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-5","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"قال البيضاوي: في الآية دليل على وجوب الهجرة من موضع لا يتمكن فيه الرجل من إقامة دينه، وعن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «من فرَّ بدينه من أرض، ولو كان شبرًا من الأرض، استَوجَبَ الجنة، وكان رفيقَ إبراهيم ومحمد- عليهما الصلاة والسلام» (1) . قلت: ويدخل فيه- على طريق الخصوص- من فرّ من موضع تكثر فيه الشهوات والعوائد، أو تكثر فيه العلائق والشواغل، إلى موضع يقلُّ فيه ذلك، طلبًا لصفاء قلبه ومعرفة ربه، بل هو أولى، ويكون رفيقاً لهما في حضرة القدس عند مليك مقتدر. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-6","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"ثم استثنى مَن تَحَقَّق إسلامُه وحبسه العذر، فقال: إِلَّا الْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ مِنَ الرِّجالِ وَالنِّساءِ وَالْوِلْدانِ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-7","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"المماليك والصبيان، وفيه إشعار بأنهم على صدد وجوب الهجرة، فإنهم إذا بلغوا وقدروا على الهجرة، فلا محيص عنها، وأن قومهم يجب أن يهاجروا بهم متى أمكنت الهجرة. قال ابن عباس- رضى الله عنهما-: «كنت أنا وأبى وأُمي ممن استثنى الله بهذه الآية» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-8","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"ثم وصفهم بقوله: لا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ حِيلَةً أي: قوة على ما يتوقف عليه السفر، من ركوب أو غيره، وَلا يَهْتَدُونَ سَبِيلًا أي: لا يعرفون طريقًا، ولا يجدون دليلاً، فَأُولئِكَ عَسَى اللَّهُ أَنْ يَعْفُوَ عَنْهُمْ. وعبَّر بحرف الرجاء إيذانًا بأنّ تركَ الهجرة أمرٌ خطير، حتى إن المضطر من حقه أن لا يأمن، ويترصد الفرصة، ويُعلِّقُ بها قلبه، وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً فيعفو ويغفر لمن غلبه العذر. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-9","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"الإشارة: كل مَن لم يتغلغل في علم الباطن، مات ظالمًا لنفسه، أي: باخسًا لها لما فوَّتها من لذيذ الشهود، ومعرفة الملك المعبود، ولا يخلو باطنه من الإصرار على أمراض القلوب، التي هي من أكبر الذنوب، فإذا توفته الملائكة على هذه الحالة، قالت له: فيم كنتَ حتَّى لم تهاجر إلى من يُطهرك من العيوب، ويوصلك إلى حضرة علام الغيوب؟ فيقول: كنتُ من المستضعفين في علم اليقين، ولم أقدر على صحبة أهل عين اليقين وحق اليقين حَبَسَنَي عنهم حُبُّ الأوطان، ومرافقة النساء والولدان. فيقال لهُ: ألم تكن أرض الله واسعة فتهاجر فيها إلى من يخلصك من الحجاب، وينفي عنك الشك والارتياب؟ فلا جرم أن مأواه سجن الأكوان، وحرمان الشهود والعيان، إلاَّ من أقر بوجود ضعفه، واضطر إلى مولاه في تخليصه من نفسه، فعسى ربه أن يعطف عليه، فيوصله إلى عارف من أوليائه، حتى يلتحق بأحبابه وأصفيائه. وما ذلك على الله بعزيز.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_097-10","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"4:97–99 · The oppressed and emigration","text":"ثم رغّب فى الهجرة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_097-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_097-s1","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"","text":"The angels here are the angel of death and his assistants, taking the souls of people who had wronged themselves by neglecting emigration and remaining in the company of unbelievers. “What were you in?” may question the state of their religion—doubt or certainty—or the land in which they stayed, a land of unbelief or Islam. They plead that fear of the polytheists prevented outward profession of their faith and escape. The angels reply reproachfully: God's earth is broad; others emigrated to Abyssinia and Medina. Attachment to possessions and self-preservation kept these people behind. In the initial historical circumstances, says Ibn ʿAjība, they incurred the warning because they failed to make a then-obligatory emigration and assisted unbelievers against Muslims. He recounts that the verse concerned Meccans who spoke of accepting Islam but had not emigrated. They went with the polytheists to Badr and, seeing how few the Muslims were, remarked that religion had deceived them; they were killed, and the angels struck their faces and backs, as explained elsewhere. He concludes that residing under the rule of unbelief is impermissible when one is able to leave: emigration is obligatory, with no excuse for remaining. One prevented by an impediment ought not become content with the inability, but remain ready to leave. Otherwise, he says, affliction will encompass him, as happened to the people of Andalusia until their children became unbelievers, and extends the objection to settings where wrongdoing and neglect of religion predominate. Al-Bayḍāwī is cited for the obligation to migrate from any place where one cannot establish one's religious practice. Ibn ʿAjība transmits a reported saying that one who flees a land for the sake of religion, even a short distance, earns Paradise and the companionship of Abraham and Muḥammad. [Translator’s note: Its isnād is not verified here.] In a special inward sense, this includes moving from a place of excessive appetites, habitual attachments and distracting relationships to one more favourable for purification of the heart and knowledge of the Lord. The inward migrant hopes for companionship with the prophets in the sanctuary of divine nearness. The exception is for those demonstrably weak or powerless: men, women and children, including enslaved persons and minors in the commentary's social setting. Ibn ʿAjība adds that reaching maturity and acquiring ability makes emigration incumbent when its original conditions obtain, and that the responsible families should take the vulnerable with them when possible. Ibn ʿAbbās is reported to have identified himself and his parents as among those excepted. Such persons lack the resources and physical capacity for travel or cannot find a route or a guide. The word “perhaps” attached to divine pardon, Ibn ʿAjība says, reminds even the excused that the obligation is grave: they should wait attentively for an opening. “God has always been Forgiving, Merciful”: He pardons and forgives those overcome by an excuse. [Textual note: Cairo I:550 gives ghafūran raḥīman , “Forgiving, Merciful,” here, whereas the Q4:99 verse block at I:549 correctly has ʿafuwwan ghafūran , “Pardoning, Forgiving.” The former wording also ends Q4:100, printed next. The difference is retained as a feature of the exposition; it is not presented as a variant Qurʾānic reading, and its origin has not been established.] [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-19] ]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_097-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_097-s2","r":"q4_cont_097","title":"","text":"One who never penetrated inward knowledge dies having wronged the soul by depriving it of the delight of direct witnessing and recognition of the Worshipped Sovereign. His inward being is not free from persistence in diseases of the heart, which are among the greatest sins. At death the angels ask why this person did not emigrate to a guide able to remove defects and bring him to the Presence of the Knower of the Unseen. He says he was weak in the knowledge of certainty ( ʿilm al-yaqīn ) and could not accompany people of the eye or truth of certainty ( ʿayn al-yaqīn , ḥaqq al-yaqīn ): love of native country, wife and children detained him. The reply is that God's earth was broad enough to seek one who would remove the veil and dispel uncertainty. Thus his home is the prison of created forms and deprivation of direct witnessing, except for one who recognises his weakness and urgently implores his Master for deliverance from his self: his Lord may then have compassion on him and bring him to a knower among His saints, so that he may join His beloved and elect. Such a thing is not difficult for God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_097-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_100","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God 4:100","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_100"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-1","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"وَمَنْ يُهاجِرْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ يَجِدْ فِي الْأَرْضِ مُراغَماً كَثِيراً وَسَعَةً وَمَنْ يَخْرُجْ مِنْ بَيْتِهِ مُهاجِراً إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ ثُمَّ يُدْرِكْهُ الْمَوْتُ فَقَدْ وَقَعَ أَجْرُهُ عَلَى اللَّهِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً (100)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-2","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"قلت: المراغَم: المهرب والمذهب. قاله في القاموس. وقال البيضاوي: يجد متحولاً، من الرغام وهو التراب.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-3","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"وقيل: طريقًا يراغم قومه بسلوكه فيها، أي: يفارقهم على رغم أنوفهم، وهو أيضًا من الرغام.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-4","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ يُهاجِرْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ لإعلاء كلمة الله وإقامة دينه، يَجِدْ فِي الْأَرْضِ فضاءً كثيرًا، ومتحولاً كبيرًا يتحول إليه، وسعة بدلاً من ضيق ما كان فيه، من قهر العدو ومنعه من إظهار دينه، أو سعةٌ في الرزق، وبسطًا في المعيشة، فلا عذر له في المقام في مكان مُضَيَّقٍ عليه فيه في أمر دينه، وَمَنْ يَخْرُجْ مِنْ بَيْتِهِ مُهاجِراً إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وجهادٍ في سبيله، ثُمَّ يُدْرِكْهُ الْمَوْتُ قبل وصوله فقد ثبت أجرُه، ووجب على الله- وجوب امتنان- أن يبلغه قصده بعد موته، وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفُوراً لِما سلف له من عدم المبادرة، رَحِيماً به، حيث بلَّغه مأمولَه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-5","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"نزلت في جُندع بن ضَمرة، وكان شيخًا كبيرًا مريضًا، فلما سمع ما نزل في شأن الهجرة قال: والله ما أنا ممن استثنى الله، ولي مال يُبِلغني المدينة، والله لا أبيتُ الليلة بمكة، اخرجُوا بي، فخرجوا به على سريره حتى أتوا به التنعيم، فأدركه الموت بها، فَصفَّق بيمينه على شماله، وقال: اللهم هذه لك وهذه لرسولك، أُبايعك على مَا بَايَعَك عليه رسولك، فمات حَمِيدًا. فقال الصحابة: لو وافَى المدينةَ، كان أتم أجرًا، وضحك المشركون، وقالوا: ما أدرك ما طلب. فنزلت: وَمَنْ يَخْرُجْ مِنْ بَيْتِهِ.. الخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-6","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"وقيل: نزلت في خالد بن حزام، فإنه هاجر إلى أرض الحبشة، فنهشته حيَّةٌ في الطريق، فمات قبل أن يصل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-7","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"الإشارة: ومن يهاجر من وطن حظوظه وهواه، طلبًا للوصول إلى حضرة مولاه، يجد في أرض نفسه متسعًا للعلوم، ومفتاحًا لمخازن الفهوم، وسعة الفضاء والشهود، حتى ينطوي في عين بصيرته كلُّ موجود، ويتحقق بشهود واجب الوجود. ومن يخرج من بيت نفسه وسجن هيكله إلى طلب الوصول إلى الله ورسوله، ثم يُدركه الموت قبل التمكين، فقد وقع أجره على الله، وبلَّغه الله ما كان قَصَدَه وتمناه، فيُحشر مع الصديقين أهلِ الرسوخ والتمكين، التي تلي درجتُهم درجةَ النبيين، وكذلك من مات في طلب العلم الظاهر ولم يدركه في حياته، حشِر مع العلماء، قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «من جاءَه أجله وهو يطلبُ العلمَ لم يكن بينه وبين النبيين إلا درجةٌ واحدة» . قلت:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-8","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"وهذه الدرجة التي بينه وبين النبوة هي درجة الصديقين المتقدمة قبله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-9","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"وكل من مات في طلب شيء من الخير، أدركه بعد موته بحسن نيته، كما في الأحاديث النبوية، قال القشيري: المهاجر في الحقيقة، من هاجر نفسه وهواه، ولا يصح ذلك إلا بانسلاخه عن جميع مراداته وقصوده،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-10","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"فمن قصَده- أي قصد الحق تعالى- ثم أدركه الأجلُ قبل وصوله، فلا ينزل إلا بساحات وصله، ولا يكون محط رفقته إلا مكان قربه. هـ. وفي بعض الآثار: الهجرة هجرتان: هجرة صُغرى، وهجرة كبرى، فالصغرى: انتقال الأجسام مِن وطنٍ غير مرضي إلى وطن مرضي، والكبرى: انتقال النفوس من مألوفاتها وحظوظها إلى معرفة ربها وحقوقها. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_100-11","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"4:100 · The reward of leaving for God","text":"ثم ذكر ما يتعلق بالسفر من قصر وغيره، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_100-11"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_100-s1","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"","text":"I say: Murāgham means an escape or destination, according to al-Qāmūs . Al-Bayḍāwī explains it as a place to which one can transfer, connecting it with rughām , dust. It can also mean a road taken in defiance of one's people, separating from them to their vexation.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_100-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_100-s2","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"","text":"One who emigrates to exalt God's word and uphold religion finds abundant room for movement, relief from the constraints of hostile rule and prevention of religious practice, and perhaps enlarged livelihood. He therefore has no excuse for remaining in a place where his religious life is constrained. If someone sets out from home intending emigration to God and His Messenger and struggle for His cause, but dies before reaching the destination, the reward has nevertheless been established. God, through His free beneficence—not through a compulsion upon Him—grants the person the intended end, forgives the delay that preceded departure, and shows mercy by fulfilling the hope. Ibn ʿAjība relates a report about the elderly, sick Jundaʿ ibn Ḍamra. Hearing the revelation about emigration, he swore that he was not among the excused, had sufficient means to reach Medina, and would not pass another night in Mecca. He was carried on a bed as far as al-Tanʿīm, where death overtook him. He struck one hand upon the other, declaring, “O God, this is for You and this is for Your Messenger; I pledge to You what Your Messenger pledged.” Some Companions said he would have received a fuller reward had he arrived; polytheists mocked his failure to reach his goal. The verse was revealed, according to this report. Another account concerns Khālid ibn Ḥizām, bitten by a snake on the way to Abyssinia and dying before arrival.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_100-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_100-s3","r":"q4_cont_100","title":"","text":"One who emigrates from the homeland of personal self-indulgence and appetite toward the Presence of the Lord finds in the land of the soul spaciousness for sciences, keys to treasures of understanding and expanses of witnessing, until all existing things are encompassed in inner insight and the Necessary Existent is witnessed. One who departs from the house of the lower soul and the prison of bodily form in search of God and His Messenger but dies before reaching established mastery ( tamkīn ) still has the reward with God; the person is raised with the firmly established ṣiddīqūn , whose station follows that of the prophets. Likewise the seeker of outward religious knowledge who dies before completing its acquisition is raised with the scholars. Ibn ʿAjība cites a saying that only one rank separates a person dying in pursuit of knowledge from the prophets, and identifies that rank as the ṣiddīqūn . [Translator’s note: The transmission requires source criticism.] A sincere person who dies in pursuit of any good attains the intended reward after death through the excellence of intention. Al-Qushayrī says that the true emigrant leaves behind the lower self and its appetites, which requires the shedding of all one's private aims. One whose aim is God and who dies before reaching Him arrives at nothing but the courtyards of union and the resting-place of nearness. Some inherited reports distinguish a lesser emigration—bodily removal from a displeasing home to a pleasing one—from a greater emigration: the soul's transfer from familiar habits and selfish claims to knowledge of its Lord and its own rights. [Textual note: the Cairo text reads ḥuqūqihā , “its rights,” with a feminine pronoun referring back to the soul. This preserves the printed wording; the source does not read “His rights.”] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_100-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_101","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road 4:101","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_101"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-1","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"وَإِذا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُناحٌ أَنْ تَقْصُرُوا مِنَ الصَّلاةِ إِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَنْ يَفْتِنَكُمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا إِنَّ الْكافِرِينَ كانُوا لَكُمْ عَدُوًّا مُبِيناً (101)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-2","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ، أي: سافرتم للجهاد أو غيره من السفر المباح، أو المطلوب، فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُناحٌ أَنْ تَقْصُرُوا مِنَ الصَّلاةِ الرباعية إلى ركعتين، ونفيُ الجُناح يقتضي أنها رُخصة، وبه قال الشافعي، ويؤيده أنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أتمّ في السفر، وأن عائشة- رضى الله عنها- قالت:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-3","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"يا رسول الله قَصَرْتَ وأتممْتُ، وصُمْتُ وأفطرتَ؟ فقال: «أحسنت (1) يا عائشة» . وأوجبه أبو حنيفة لقول عمر رضي الله عنه: (السفر ركعتان تمام غير قصر، على لسان نبيكم) . ولقول عائشة: (أول ما فرضت الصلاة ركعتان، فأقرت صلاة السفر، وزيدت في الحضر) .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-4","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"وقال مالك رضي الله عنه: القصر سنة لكونه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- دام عليه في كل سفر، ولم يتُم إلا مرةً لبيان الجواز.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-5","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"وقوله تعالى: إِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَنْ يَفْتِنَكُمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ظاهره أن الخوف شرط في القصر، وبه قالت عائشة وعثمان- رضى الله عنهما-، والجمهور على عدم شرطه، وإنما ذكره الحق- تعالى- لكونه غالبًا في ذلك الوقت، فلا يعتبر مفهومه، أو يؤخذ القصر في الأمن من السُّنة. ويؤيد هذا حديثُ يَعلى بن أمِية، قلت لعمر بن الخطاب: إن الله يقول: إِنْ خِفْتُمْ، وقد أمن الناس؟. فقال: عجبتُ مما تعجبتَ منه. فسألت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال: «صدقة تصدّق بها الله علَيكم، فاقبلوا صدَقته» . وقد ثبت أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم قصر الصلاة وهو آمن.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-6","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"وليس في الآية ما يدل على تحديد المسافة التي تُقصَرُ فيها الصلاةُ، بل ذَكَرَ مطلقَ السفر، ولذلك أجاز الظاهرية القصر في كل سفر، طال أو قصر. ومذهب مالك والشافعي: أن المسافة أربعة بُردُ، واحتجوا بآثار عن ابن عمر وابن عباس. وقال أبو حنيفة: ستة بُرُد، وكذلك لم يقيد الحقُّ السفرَ بمباح ولا غيره، ولذلك أجاز أبو حنيفة القصر","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-7","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"في كل سفر. ومنعه مالك في سفر المعصية. ومنعه ابن حنبل في المعصية والمباح. والمراد بالفتنة في قوله: إِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَنْ يَفْتِنَكُمُ: الجهاد والتعرض لما يُكره، وعداوة الكفار معلومة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-8","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"الإشارة: وإذا ضربتم في ميادين النفوس، وتحقق سيرُكم إلى حضرة القدوس، فلا جناح عليكم أن تقتصروا على المهم من الصلاة الحسية، وتدوموا على الصلاة القلبية، التي هي العكوف في الحضرة القدسية، إن خفتم أن تشغلكم عن الشهود حلاوةُ المعاملة الحسية. قال بعض العارفين: اتقوا حلاوة المعاملة، فإنها سموم قاتلة. وكذلك قال القطب ابن مشيش في المقامات كالرضا، والتسليم: أخاف أن تشغلني حلاوتها عن الله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_101-9","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"4:101 · Shortening prayer on the road","text":"ثم ذكر صلاة الخوف، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_101-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_101-s1","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"Outward interpretation and the law of travel","text":"This permission applies to journeying for struggle or another permissible or praiseworthy purpose. The four-cycle prayers may be shortened to two cycles. The absence of blame suggests a concession ( rukhṣa ), says Ibn ʿAjība, who attributes this view to al-Shāfiʿī. He cites reports that the Prophet at times completed prayer while travelling, and a report in which ʿĀʾisha says she completed while he shortened and fasted while he broke his fast; the Prophet responded approvingly. Abū Ḥanīfa, on the other hand, is said to make shortening obligatory, supported by ʿUmar's statement that the travelling prayer is two complete cycles rather than a truncated prayer, and by ʿĀʾisha's report that prayer was first imposed in two cycles, retained as such in travel and increased at home. Mālik treats shortening as a Sunna because of the Prophet's consistent travel practice, allowing that he completed once to demonstrate permissibility. [Translator’s note: These reports and their legal uses are reproduced as Ibn ʿAjība gives them; the claimed reports about completion and the school formulations require independent detailed checking before normative reliance.] The wording “if you fear” appears to make danger a condition. Ibn ʿAjība attributes this view to ʿĀʾisha and ʿUthmān, but says the majority do not require fear: it was mentioned because it commonly accompanied journeys at the time, or else the permission under conditions of safety is taken from the Sunna. Yaʿlā ibn Umayya asked ʿUmar why shortening persisted after people had become safe, given the condition in the verse; ʿUmar had asked the Prophet the same question and received the reply: “It is a charity God has bestowed upon you, so accept His charity.” The Prophet also shortened while secure. The verse gives no numerical limit on the distance: it speaks simply of travel. Thus the Ẓāhirīs permit shortening on every journey however short or long. Mālik and al-Shāfiʿī prescribe four burud , adducing reports from Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās; Abū Ḥanīfa is reported here to prescribe six burud . Nor does the wording restrict the journey to one free of sin. Thus Abū Ḥanīfa permits shortening on any journey; Mālik denies it for travel undertaken to commit a sin, and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal is reported to disallow it both for sinful and merely permissible travel. In the clause about causing fitna , the feared trial means conflict and other hostile harm.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_101-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_101-s2","r":"q4_cont_101","title":"","text":"When you traverse the fields of your own soul and journey toward the Most Holy Presence, there is no blame in restricting yourselves to the essential part of sensory prayer while persisting in the prayer of the heart, which is dwelling in the sacred Presence—if you fear that the sweetness of outward observance could distract you from witnessing. A knower said, “Beware the sweetness of devotional practice, for it is a deadly poison.” Ibn Mashīsh is cited as saying, even concerning spiritual stations such as contentment and surrender, “I fear their sweetness will distract me from God.” [Translator’s note: This is mystical application, not a legal licence to omit prescribed acts of worship.] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_101-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_102","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger 4:102","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_102"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-1","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"وَإِذا كُنْتَ فِيهِمْ فَأَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلاةَ فَلْتَقُمْ طائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ مَعَكَ وَلْيَأْخُذُوا أَسْلِحَتَهُمْ فَإِذا سَجَدُوا فَلْيَكُونُوا مِنْ وَرائِكُمْ وَلْتَأْتِ طائِفَةٌ أُخْرى لَمْ يُصَلُّوا فَلْيُصَلُّوا مَعَكَ وَلْيَأْخُذُوا حِذْرَهُمْ وَأَسْلِحَتَهُمْ وَدَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ تَغْفُلُونَ عَنْ أَسْلِحَتِكُمْ وَأَمْتِعَتِكُمْ فَيَمِيلُونَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَيْلَةً واحِدَةً وَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِنْ كانَ بِكُمْ أَذىً مِنْ مَطَرٍ أَوْ كُنْتُمْ مَرْضى أَنْ تَضَعُوا أَسْلِحَتَكُمْ وَخُذُوا حِذْرَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ أَعَدَّ لِلْكافِرِينَ عَذاباً مُهِيناً (102)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-2","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِذا كُنْتَ فِيهِمْ أيها الرسول فَأَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلاةَ، أي: صلاة الخوف، وكذلك الأمراء النائبون عنه، فَلْتَقُمْ طائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ مَعَكَ، وطائفة تقف وجَاهَ العدو للحراسة، وَلْيَأْخُذُوا أَسْلِحَتَهُمْ أي: المصلون معك، فَإِذا سَجَدُوا فَلْيَكُونُوا أي: الطائفة الحارسة مِنْ وَرائِكُمْ، فإذا صلَّت نصفَ الصلاة مع الإمام، قضت في صلبه ما بقي لها وذهبت تحرس.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-3","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"وَلْتَأْتِ طائِفَةٌ أُخْرى لَمْ يُصَلُّوا فَلْيُصَلُّوا مَعَكَ النصف الباقي، فإذا سلمتَ، قضوا ما بقي لهم، فإذا كانت ثنائية: صلَّى بالأولى ركعةَ، وَثَبَتَ قائمًا ساكتًا أو قارئًا، ثم تصلي من صلت معه ركعة وتسلم، وتأتي الثانية فتكبر، فيُصلِي بها ركعةً ويسلم وتقضي ركعة. واذا كانت رباعية، أو ثلاثية صلى بالأولى ركعتين، ثم تقوم الأولى فتصلي ما بقي لها وتسلم وتأتي الثانية فتكبر وتصلي معه ما بقي له، ثم تقضي ما بقي لها. هكذا قاله مالك والشافعي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-4","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"وقال أبو حنيفة: يصلي بالأولى ركعة، ثم تتأخر وهي في الصلاة، وتأتي الثانية فيصلي بها ركعة، فإذا سلَّم ذهبت مكان الأولى قبل سَلاَمها، فتأتي الأولى فتصلي ركعة ثم تسلم، وتأتي الثانية فتصلي ركعة ثم تسلم. وفي","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-5","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"صلاة الخوف عشرة أقوال على حسب الأحاديث النبوية، لأنها تعدّدت منه صلّى الله عليه وسلم، فكل واحد أخذ بحديث، وما قاله مالك والشافعي هو الذي فعله- عليه الصلاة والسلام- في غزوة ذات الرقاع.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-6","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"ثم أمر الطائفة الحارسة بأخذ السلاح، والحذر من العدو فقال: وَلْيَأْخُذُوا حِذْرَهُمْ وَأَسْلِحَتَهُمْ، ثم ذكر عِلَّةَ الحذر فقال: وَدَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ تَغْفُلُونَ عَنْ أَسْلِحَتِكُمْ وَأَمْتِعَتِكُمْ فَيَمِيلُونَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَيْلَةً واحِدَةً أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-7","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"تمنوا أن ينالوا منكم غرة، فيشدون عليكم شدة واحدة فيستأصلونكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-8","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"رُوِي أن المشركين لما رأوا المسلمين صلوا صلاة الظهر ندموا أن لو كانوا أغاروا عليهم في الصلاة، ثم قالوا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-9","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"دعوهم فإن لهم صلاة هي إليهم أحب من آبائهم وأبنائهم- يعنون صلاة العصر-، فلما قام النبي- عليه الصلاة والسلام- لصلاة العصر نزل جبريلُ بصلاة الخوف.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-10","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"ثم رخَّص لهم في وضع السلاح، لعذرٍ فقال: وَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْكُمْ أي: لا إثم إِنْ كانَ بِكُمْ أَذىً مِنْ مَطَرٍ أَوْ كُنْتُمْ مَرْضى أَنْ تَضَعُوا أَسْلِحَتَكُمْ وَخُذُوا حِذْرَكُمْ منهم بالحراسة. رُوي أنها نزلت في عبد الرحمن بن عوف، مَرِضَ فوضع سلاحه، فعنَّفه أصحابُه، فنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-11","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"ثم هوَّن شأن الكفار بعد أن أمر بالحذر منهم فقال: إِنَّ اللَّهَ أَعَدَّ لِلْكافِرِينَ عَذاباً مُهِيناً في الدنيا والآخرة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-12","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"قال البيضاوي: وعد المؤمنين بالنصرة على الكفار، بعد الأمر بالحذر، ليقوي قلوبهم، وليعلموا أن الأمر بالحذر ليس لضعفهم وغلبة عدوهم، بل إن الواجب أن يحافظوا في الأمور على مراسم التيقظ والتدبير. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-13","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"الإشارة: إذا كنت في جند الأنوار، وأحدَقَت بك حضرة الأسرار، ثم نزلتَ إلى سماء الحقوق أو أرض الحظوظ فلتقم طائفة من تلك الأنوار معك، لتحرسك من جيش الأغيار وجند الأكدار، حتى يكون رجوعُك إلى الآثار مصحوبًا بكسوة الأنوار وحلية الاستبصار، فيكون رجوعك إليها بالله لا بنفسك، فإذا سجد القلبُ في الحضرة كانت تلك الأنوار من ورائه والأسرار من أمامه، وَاللَّهُ مِنْ وَرائِهِمْ مُحِيطٌ، ولتأت طائفة أخرى لم تصل هذه الصلاة لأنها لم تبلغ هذا المقام، فلتصل معك اقتباسًا لأنوارك، لكن تأخذ حذرها وتستعد من خواطر الأشغال، كي لا تميل عليهم فتفتنهم عن الحضور مع الكبير المتعال، فإن كان مريض القلب بالهوى وسائر العلل، فلا يكلف من الحضور إلا ما يطيقه، لأن القط لا يكلف بحمل الجمل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_102-14","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"4:102 · The prayer performed under danger","text":"ثم ذكر ما يعين على الحضور، ويتحصن به من العدو الكفور وهو ذكر الله، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_102-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_102-s1","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"","text":"The instruction to the Prophet concerns the prayer of fear ( ṣalāt al-khawf ) and applies also, says Ibn ʿAjība, to the leaders who act in his place. One detachment joins the imām while another faces the enemy on guard. The praying group carries weapons. Once its portion of prayer is concluded, it completes the remainder under the imām's continuing prayer and moves out to guard. The second group comes and joins him for the remaining portion and completes its own prayer when he pronounces the closing salutation. In the two-cycle prayer the leader performs a first cycle with one group, then remains standing—silent or reciting—while they complete a cycle and finish; the second group joins and performs one cycle with the leader, who concludes, and they complete their last cycle. In prayers of three or four cycles the leader performs two cycles with the first group; they finish the remainder, move to guard, and the second group joins the leader for the remaining cycles, completing any cycles they still owe. Ibn ʿAjība attributes this to Mālik and al-Shāfiʿī. Abū Ḥanīfa's transmitted procedure differs: the first group prays one cycle and retreats while still in prayer, the second joins for the next and moves back after the imām's salutation, and each group subsequently returns to complete its unperformed cycle. Ten views of the fear-prayer are reported, reflecting different Prophetic implementations and traditions. The Mālikī-Shāfiʿī form, he says, was practised in the expedition of Dhāt al-Riqāʿ. Both detachments must remain cautious, for their enemies would seize any moment when Muslims abandoned equipment or watchfulness and attack as one. A report says the polytheists regretted not assaulting them during the noon prayer and waited for the afternoon prayer, which Muslims loved especially; Gabriel then brought the revelation describing prayer under threat. If rain, sickness or a similar impediment causes harm, the arms may be laid aside, but vigilance and guarding remain required. Another report associates this concession with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who put down his arms while ill and was rebuked until the verse was revealed. God's promise of humiliating punishment for unbelievers, al-Bayḍāwī observes, follows the command to take precautions in order to strengthen believers' hearts: vigilance is not a confession of weakness but the proper observance of intelligent preparation.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_102-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_102-s2","r":"q4_cont_102","title":"","text":"If you are among the troops of lights, enveloped by the Presence of mysteries, and descend again to the heaven of duties or the earth of ordinary satisfactions, let a detachment of those spiritual lights remain with you, guarding against the army of distractions and the troops of sorrows. Thus your return to created effects remains clothed in illumination and insight, and you return through God , not through self-reliance. When the heart prostrates before the Presence, the lights are behind it and the mysteries ahead, while “God encompasses them from behind” (85:20). Other people have not yet experienced this prayer because they have not attained the station: let them join you in order to partake of its illumination, while guarding against thoughts and worldly preoccupations which could disrupt their presence before the Exalted. One whose heart is sick with appetite or other ailments is only charged with the degree of inward presence he can bear; the cat is not required to carry the camel's load. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_102-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_103","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"4:103 · Prayer, remembrance and appointed times","text":"4:103 · Prayer, remembrance and appointed times 4:103","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_103"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_103-1","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"4:103 · Prayer, remembrance and appointed times","text":"فَإِذا قَضَيْتُمُ الصَّلاةَ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ قِياماً وَقُعُوداً وَعَلى جُنُوبِكُمْ فَإِذَا اطْمَأْنَنْتُمْ فَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ إِنَّ الصَّلاةَ كانَتْ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ كِتاباً مَوْقُوتاً (103)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_103-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_103-2","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"4:103 · Prayer, remembrance and appointed times","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فإذا فرغتم من الصلاة فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ في جميع أحوالكم قِياماً وَقُعُوداً وَعَلى جُنُوبِكُمْ إن أردتم حراسة قلوبكم، والنصر على عدوكم، أو إذا أردتم قضاءَ الصلوات وأداء فرضها، وأنتم في المعركة، فصلوا كما أمكنكم، قِياماً راجلين أو على خيولكم إيماءً، وحلَّ للضرورة حينئٍذ مشى وركض وطعن وعدم توجه، وإمساك ملطخ، وتنبيهٌ وتحذيرٌ، هذا للصحيح، وَقُعُوداً وَعَلى جُنُوبِكُمْ، للمريض أو الجريح، هكذا قال جمهور الفقهاء في صلاة المسايفة (1) . وقال أبو حنيفة: لا يصلي المحارب حتى يطمئن.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_103-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_103-3","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"4:103 · Prayer, remembrance and appointed times","text":"فَإِذَا اطْمَأْنَنْتُمْ وذهب الخوفُ عنكم فَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ على هيأتها المعلومة، واحفظوا أركانها وشروطها، وأُتوا بها تامة، إِنَّ الصَّلاةَ كانَتْ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ كِتاباً مَوْقُوتاً أي: فرضًا محدود الأوقات، لا يجوز إخراجها عن وقتها في شيء من الأحوال. قال البيضاوي: وهذا دليل على أن المراد بالذكر الصلاة، وأنها واجبة الأداء، حال المسايفة، والاضطراب في المعركة، وتعليلٌ للأمر بالإتيان بها، كيف أمكن.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_103-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_103-4","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"4:103 · Prayer, remembrance and appointed times","text":"الإشارة: إذا فرغتم من الصلاة الحسية، فاستغرقوا أحوالكم في الصلاة القلبية، حتى تطمئن قلوبكم في الحضرة القدسية، فإذا اطمأننتم في الحضرة، فأقيموا صلاة الشهود والنظرة، وهي الصلاة الدائمة، قال تعالى: الَّذِينَ هُمْ عَلى صَلاتِهِمْ دائِمُونَ. وقال الورتجبي: إذا كنتم في حالةِ التمكين وامتلأتم من أنوار ذكره، فينبغي أن تخرجوا من أبواب الرخص، والاستراحة في سعة الروح، وترجعوا إلى مقام الصلاة، فإن آخر سيركم في ربوبيتي: أول بدايتكم فى عبوديتى. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_103-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_103-5","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"4:103 · Prayer, remembrance and appointed times","text":"ثم حذرهم من الوهن فى أمر الجهاد، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_103-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_103-s1","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"","text":"After completing prayer, remember God in every bodily state to protect your hearts and receive help against adversaries. Or, if in the heat of battle you need to fulfil prescribed prayer, perform it as possible: standing on foot or mounted, gesturing as necessary. In extreme necessity walking, running, thrusting, facing away from the qibla, holding stained equipment and giving urgent warnings may be permitted. The healthy pray as they can; the wounded or sick may pray seated or upon their sides. Ibn ʿAjība attributes this account of prayer during direct combat ( ṣalāt al-musāyafa ) to most jurists; Abū Ḥanīfa is reported to postpone such prayer until safety returns. Once the danger has passed, the prescribed form, conditions and pillars of prayer are to be observed completely. Prayer is a timed obligation ( kitāban mawqūtan ) and may not be taken outside its time in any circumstances. Al-Bayḍāwī takes the context to show that “remembrance” here can mean prayer itself, and that even amid actual hand-to-hand conflict it is to be performed by whatever means are possible.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_103-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_103-s2","r":"q4_cont_103","title":"","text":"On finishing the bodily prayer, immerse your states in the prayer of the heart until your hearts become settled in the sacred Presence. Then establish the prayer of witnessing and direct vision, the unceasing prayer: “Those who remain constant in their prayer” (70:23). Al-Wartajbī says that when you are established in spiritual mastery, filled with the lights of God's remembrance, you should leave behind the mere conveniences of concessions and resting in spiritual expansiveness and return to the station of prayer. He ends in the divine first person: “The end of your journey in My Lordship is the first beginning of your servanthood to Me.” God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_103-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_104","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve","text":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve 4:104","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_104"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_104-1","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve","text":"وَلا تَهِنُوا فِي ابْتِغاءِ الْقَوْمِ إِنْ تَكُونُوا تَأْلَمُونَ فَإِنَّهُمْ يَأْلَمُونَ كَما تَأْلَمُونَ وَتَرْجُونَ مِنَ اللَّهِ ما لا يَرْجُونَ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً (104)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_104-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_104-2","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve","text":"قلت: الوهن: الفشل والضعف.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_104-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_104-3","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ولا تضعفوا في طلب الْقَوْمِ، أي: الكفار، فتجاهدوهم في سبيل الله، فإن الحرب دائرة بينهم وبينكم، قد أصابهم مثل ما أصابكم، فإن تَكُونُوا تَأْلَمُونَ، أي: تتوجعون من الجراح، فَإِنَّهُمْ يَأْلَمُونَ كَما تَأْلَمُونَ، وأنتم ترجون من الله النصر والعز في الدنيا، والدرجات العلا في الآخرة، وهم لا يرجون","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_104-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_104-4","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve","text":"ذلك، فحقكم أن تكونوا أصبر وأرغب في الجهاد منهم، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً بأعمالكم وضمائركم، حَكِيماً فيما يأمركم به وينهاكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_104-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_104-5","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve","text":"الإشارة: لا تهنوا عن طلب الظفر بنفوسكم، ولا تفشلوا عن السير إلى حضرة ربكم، فإن كنتم تألمون حال محاربتها ومخالفة شهواتها، فإنها تألم مثلكم، ما دامت لم ترتض في حضرة ربكم، فإذا ارتاضَت وتحلت صار المُر عندها حلوًا، وذلك إنما يكون بعد موتها وحياتها، فدوموا على سياستها ورياضتها، فإنكم ترجون من الله الوصول، وبلوغ المأمول، وهي ترجو الرجوع إلى المألوفات وركوب العادات، فاعكسوا مُراداتها، حتى تطمئن في حضرة ربها، فتأمن غوائلها، فليس بعد الوصول رجوع، ولا إلى العوائد نزوع، والله غالب على أمره.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_104-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_104-6","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"4:104 · Do not lose resolve","text":"ثم ذكر ما يتعلق بحفظ اللسان، وهو الأمر الخامس من مضمون السورة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_104-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_104-s1","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"","text":"I say: wahn means failure, feebleness and weakness. Do not flag in pursuing the enemy in the circumstances of the conflict. The suffering and injuries of war fall on both parties. If wounds cause you pain, they too are in pain; yet you seek victory and honour in this life and exalted ranks in the next, hopes not shared by them. Believers should therefore show greater patience and resolve. God knows actions and motives and acts with wisdom in what He commands and forbids.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_104-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_104-s2","r":"q4_cont_104","title":"","text":"Do not grow weary in overcoming your lower souls or abandon the journey toward your Lord. Opposition to the appetites of the soul pains you, but it pains the soul too while it has not yet been disciplined in the divine Presence. When trained and beautified, what was bitter becomes sweet—after its figurative death and revived life. Continue its management and discipline: your hope is arrival at God, while its own inclination is toward familiar habits and indulgences. Reverse its wishes until it becomes peaceful in its Lord's Presence and its dangers no longer threaten. After true arrival there is no reverting to habitual self-indulgence. God prevails in His affair. The exposition next turns to guarding the tongue, the fifth theme treated in the sūrah.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_104-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_105","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation 4:105–109","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_105"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-1","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"إِنَّا أَنْزَلْنا إِلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ بِالْحَقِّ لِتَحْكُمَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِما أَراكَ اللَّهُ وَلا تَكُنْ لِلْخائِنِينَ خَصِيماً (105) وَاسْتَغْفِرِ اللَّهَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً (106) وَلا تُجادِلْ عَنِ الَّذِينَ يَخْتانُونَ أَنْفُسَهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كانَ خَوَّاناً أَثِيماً (107) يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَلا يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَهُوَ مَعَهُمْ إِذْ يُبَيِّتُونَ ما لا يَرْضى مِنَ الْقَوْلِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ مُحِيطاً (108) ها أَنْتُمْ هؤُلاءِ جادَلْتُمْ عَنْهُمْ فِي الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا فَمَنْ يُجادِلُ اللَّهَ عَنْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ أَمْ مَنْ يَكُونُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكِيلاً (109)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-2","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"قلت: أرى، هنا عرفانية، لا علمية، فلذلك لم تتعد إلى ثلاثة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-3","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله لنبيه- عليه الصلاة والسلام- حين همَّ أن يخاصم عن طُعمَة بن أبَيرِق، وذلك أنه سرق درعًا من جاره قتادة بن النعمان، في جراب دقيق، فجعل الدقيق يسقط من خرق فيه، وخبَّأها عند يهودي، فالتمس الدرع عند طعمة، فلم توجد، وحلف ما أخذها، وما له بها علم، فتركوه واتبعوا أثر الدقيق حتى انتهى إلى منزل اليهودي فأخذوها، فقال اليهودي: دَفَعَهَا إليَّ طُعمَة، وشهد له ناس من اليهود، فقال رهط طعمة من بني ظفر: انطلقوا بنا إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فنسأله أن يجادل عن صاحبنا، وقالوا: إن لم يفعل هلك وافتضح، وبرئ اليهودي، فهمَّ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم اعتماداً على ظاهر الأمر، ولم يكن له علم بالواقعة، فنزلت الآية:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-4","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"إِنَّا أَنْزَلْنا إِلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ بِالْحَقِّ أي: ملتبسًا بالحق لِتَحْكُمَ بما فيه من الحق بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بسبب ما أَراكَ أي: عَرَّفك اللَّهُ بالوحي، أو بالاجتهاد، ففيه دليل على إثبات القياس، وبه قال الجمهور. وفي اجتهاد الأنبياء خلاف. وَلا تَكُنْ لِلْخائِنِينَ خَصِيماً أي: عنهم للبرآء، أو لأجلِهم والذَّبَّ عنهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-5","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"وَاسْتَغْفِرِ اللَّهَ مما هممت به، إِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً، وفيه دليل على منع الوكالة عن الذمي، وبه قال ابن شعبان. وقال ابن عات: لعله أراد الندب. وقال مالك بن دينار: كفى بالمرء خيانة أن يكون أمينًا للخونة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-6","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"والوكالة من الأمانة، والمصطفى- عليه الصلاة والسلام- لم يقصد شيئًا من ذلك، ولا علم له بالواقعة، لولا أطلعَه تعالى، فلا نقص في اهتمامه، ولا درك (1) يلحقه. وبالجملة، فالآية خرجت مخرج التعريف بحقيقة الأمر في النازلة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-7","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"ثم نهاه عن الذبّ عنهم، فقال: وَلا تُجادِلْ عَنِ الَّذِينَ يَخْتانُونَ أَنْفُسَهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-8","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"وهم رهط ابن أبيرق السارق، قال السهيلي: هم بِشر وبشير ومُبشر وأُسَير، إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كانَ خَوَّاناً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-9","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"أي: كثير الخيانة، أَثِيماً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-10","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-11","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"مصرًا عليها، رُوِي أن طعمة هرب إلى مكة، وارتدَّ، ونَقَبَ حائطًا بها ليسرق أهله، فسقط الحائط عليه فقتله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-12","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"ويستفاد من الآية امتناع الجدال عمن عُلِمَت خيانتُه بالأحرى، أو كان مظنة الخيانة، كالكافر ونحوه. وكذا قال ابن العربي في أحكام القرآن في هذه الآية: إن النيابة عن المبطل المتهم في الخصومة لا تجوز، بدليل الآية. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-13","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"ثم فَضحَ سرهم، فقال: يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ النَّاسِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-14","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"أي: يستترون منهم، وَلا يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ اللَّهِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-15","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"وهو أحق أن يستحيا منه ويُخاف وَهُوَ مَعَهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-16","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"لا يخفى عليه شيء، فلا طريق للنجاة إلا تَركُ ما يستُقبح، ويؤاخذ عليه سرًا وجهرًا. إِذْ يُبَيِّتُونَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-17","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"أي: يدبرون ويُزَوِّرُون ما لا يَرْضى مِنَ الْقَوْلِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-18","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"من رمي البريء، والحلف الكاذب، وشهادة الزور، وَكانَ اللَّهُ بِما يَعْمَلُونَ مُحِيطاً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-19","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"لا يفوته شيء، ها أَنْتُمْ هؤُلاءِ جادَلْتُمْ عَنْهُمْ فِي الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-20","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"ودفعتم عنهم المعرة، فَمَنْ يُجادِلُ اللَّهَ عَنْهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-21","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"أي: مَن يُدافُع عنهم عذابه يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ، أَمْ مَنْ يَكُونُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكِيلًا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-22","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"يحميهم من عقاب الله، حين تُفضَح السرائر، ولا تنفع الأصحاب ولا العشائر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-23","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"الإشارة: في الآية عتاب للقضاة والولاة إذا ظهرت صورة الحق بأمارات وقرائن، ثم تجمدوا على ظاهر الشريعة، حمية أو رشوة، فإن القضاء جُلّه فِراسة، وفيها عتاب لشيوخ التربية، إذا ظهر لهم عيب في المريد ستروه عليه حيَاء أو شفقة، ولذلك قالوا: شيخ التربية لا تليق به الشفقة، غير أنه لا يُعيَّن، بل يذكر في الجملة، وصاحب العيب يفهم نفسه، وفيها عتاب للفقراء إذا راقبوا الناس، وأظهروا لهم ما يُحبون، وأخفوا عنهم ما لا يرضون، لقوله-","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-24","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"سبحانه-: يَسْتَخْفُونَ مِنَ النَّاسِ ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-25","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"الآية، بل ينبغي أن يكونوا بالعكس من هذا، قال بعضهم: إن الذين تكرهون مني، هو الذي يشتهيه قلبي. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-25"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_105-26","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"4:105–109 · Justice and the treachery accusation","text":"ثم حضّهم على التوبة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_105-26"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_105-s1","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"","text":"I say: arā in “what God has shown you” means to acquaint someone with or make something known ( ʿirfāniyya ), not the construction denoting learned knowledge that takes three objects. Hence it does not govern three objects here. Reported occasion. God addresses the Prophet when he was about to defend Ṭuʿma ibn Ubayriq. The report says Ṭuʿma stole a coat of mail belonging to his neighbour Qatāda ibn al-Nuʿmān, which was in a sack of flour. Flour trickled through a tear and marked the route. He concealed the armour in a Jewish man's house. When searched, Ṭuʿma swore he neither possessed nor knew of it. The flour trail led to the Jewish man's home. The latter said Ṭuʿma had entrusted him with the armour, and other Jews testified to it. Ṭuʿma's clan, Banū Ẓafar, asked the Prophet to defend their man, asserting that otherwise he would be disgraced and the Jewish man vindicated. Relying on appearances and not knowing the actual events, the Prophet considered speaking on his behalf. Then the revelation came.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_105-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_105-s2","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"","text":"The Book was sent enveloped in truth so the Prophet could judge justly through what God makes known to him, whether by revelation or juridical effort ( ijtihād ). Ibn ʿAjība sees support here for analogy ( qiyās ) as recognised by the majority, although the exercise of independent judgment by prophets is itself disputed. “Do not be a disputant for traitors” means do not contend against the innocent for their sake or undertake their defence. “Ask forgiveness” concerns what had been contemplated, not a knowingly unjust judgment. He takes the verse as evidence that representing a protected non-Muslim is prohibited, as Ibn Shaʿbān also held, and records Ibn ʿĀt’s suggestion that Ibn Shaʿbān may have intended abstention as a recommendation, and Mālik ibn Dīnār's saying that being the trusted agent of traitors is itself sufficient treachery. Advocacy is a trust. Nevertheless the Chosen Prophet did not knowingly intend treachery or comprehend the hidden facts until God revealed them; his initial wish to help, resting on the apparent evidence, does not detract from his station or entail liability. The verse discloses the actual circumstances of the dispute. The people who “betray themselves” are Ṭuʿma's associates, identified by al-Suhaylī as Bishr, Bashīr, Mubashshir and Usayr. God does not love one repeatedly deceitful and persistent in sin. Ibn ʿAjība transmits that Ṭuʿma later fled to Mecca, apostasised and tried to burgle another house through its wall, which collapsed upon and killed him. From the verse Ibn ʿAjība infers, all the more, a prohibition on arguing for someone whose treachery is known, or who is an object of suspicion of treachery, such as an unbeliever and the like. He cites Ibn al-ʿArabī’s Aḥkām al-Qurʾān : “Representing a party in the wrong who is suspected in the dispute is not permissible, as evidenced by this verse.” People ashamed before their neighbours yet unashamed before God behave irrationally, since God is ever with them and knows what is hidden. Escape from His judgment comes only by abandoning what deserves censure inwardly and outwardly. To “devise words by night” means plotting false accusation of an innocent person, perjury and fabricated testimony. God encompasses their acts. They may have defended their associates in this world and concealed their disgrace, but no defender can protect them from judgment when concealed intentions are exposed and neither kinship nor friendship can avail them.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_105-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_105-s3","r":"q4_cont_105","title":"","text":"The verses reproach judges and governors who discern signs and evidence pointing toward justice but rigidly cling to superficial legal appearance out of partisanship or bribery: judgment, says Ibn ʿAjība, relies considerably upon penetrating discernment ( firāsa ). They also admonish masters of formation who detect a defect in a disciple but conceal it out of embarrassment or pity. Hence their saying, “Pity does not befit a master of formation ( shaykh al-tarbiya ).” Yet the failing should be described generally without publicly naming the disciple, who recognises the admonition. Finally the verses censure Sufi poor ( fuqarāʾ ) who monitor people's approval, displaying what others like while hiding what would displease them. Instead, they should do the reverse of this. One of the people of the path said, “What you dislike in me is precisely what my heart desires.” God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_105-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_110","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy 4:110","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_110"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-1","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ سُوءاً أَوْ يَظْلِمْ نَفْسَهُ ثُمَّ يَسْتَغْفِرِ اللَّهَ يَجِدِ اللَّهَ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً (110)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-2","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ سُوءاً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-3","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"أي: ذنبًا قبيحًا يسوءُ به غيره، أَوْ يَظْلِمْ نَفْسَهُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-4","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"بذنب يختص به، أو من يعمل سوءًا بذنبٍ غيرِ الشرك، أو يظلم نفسه بالشرك، أو من يعمل سوءًا بالكبيرة، أو يظلم نفسه بالصغيرة، ثُمَّ يَسْتَغْفِرِ اللَّهَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-5","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"بالتوبة يَجِدِ اللَّهَ غَفُوراً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-6","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"لذنوبه رَحِيماً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-7","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"بقبول توبته، وفيه حث لطُعمَة وقومِه على التوبة والاستغفار.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-8","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"الإشارة: ومن يعمل سوءًا بالميل إلى الهوى، أو يظلم نفسه بالالتفات إلى السوى، أو من يعمل سوءًا بالهفوات والخطرات، أو يظلم نفسه بالغفلات والفترات، أو من يعمل سوءًا بالوقوف مع الكرامات وحلاوة الطاعات، أو يظلم نفسه بالقناعة من الترقي في الدرجات والمقامات، ثم يستغفر الله من حينه يجد الله غفورًا رحيمًا، حيث لم يُخرِجهُ من حضرته، ولم يتركه مع غفلته.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_110-9","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"4:110 · Repentance and mercy","text":"ثم عاتب رهط السارق على رميهم الغير بالسرقة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_110-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_110-s1","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"","text":"Evil may refer to a shameful sin that harms someone else, while wronging oneself denotes a private transgression. Alternatively evil can mean a sin other than associationism and wronging the soul can mean associationism; or evil denotes a major sin and self-wrong a lesser sin. Whoever then seeks forgiveness through repentance finds God forgiving sins and merciful in accepting repentance. The wording urges Ṭuʿma and his associates to repent.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_110-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_110-s2","r":"q4_cont_110","title":"","text":"Whoever commits wrong by inclining to appetite, or wrongs the soul by turning to what is other than God ( siwā ); whoever stumbles in fleeting thoughts or falls into prolonged inattentiveness; whoever stops at extraordinary spiritual graces ( karāmāt ) or the sweetness of devotions, or wrongs himself by contentment with his present rank and refusal to advance through the stations—then immediately seeks pardon, finds God forgiving and merciful. He has not cast that person from His Presence or abandoned him to heedlessness.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_110-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_111","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing 4:111–112","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_111"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-1","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"وَمَنْ يَكْسِبْ إِثْماً فَإِنَّما يَكْسِبُهُ عَلى نَفْسِهِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً (111) وَمَنْ يَكْسِبْ خَطِيئَةً أَوْ إِثْماً ثُمَّ يَرْمِ بِهِ بَرِيئاً فَقَدِ احْتَمَلَ بُهْتاناً وَإِثْماً مُبِيناً (112)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-2","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ يَكْسِبْ إِثْماً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-3","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"كسرقة أو يمين فاجرة، أو رمى غيره بجريمة، فَإِنَّما يَكْسِبُهُ عَلى نَفْسِهِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-4","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"لا يتعدى ضررها إلى غيره، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-5","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"بسرائر عباده حَكِيماً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-6","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"في إمهالهم وسترهم، وَمَنْ يَكْسِبْ خَطِيئَةً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-7","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"أي: جريمة تتعدى إلى ضرر غيره، أَوْ إِثْماً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-8","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"يختص بنفسه، ثُمَّ يَرْمِ بِهِ بَرِيئاً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-9","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"منه، كما رمى طُعمَةُ زيدًا اليهوديِّ، فَقَدِ احْتَمَلَ بُهْتاناً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-10","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"وهو أن يبهت الرجل بما لم يفعل، وَإِثْماً مُبِيناً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-11","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"أي: ذنبًا ظاهرًا، لا يخفى قبحه وبشاعته.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-12","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"الإشارة: الإثم: ما حاك في الصدر وتلجلج فيه، ولم ينشرح إليه الصدر، وضده البر وهو ما ينشرح إليه الصدر ويطمئن إليه القلب، فكل من فعل شيئًا قد تلجلج قلبه منه ولم يقبله نقص من نوره، وأظلم قلبه منه، وإليه","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-13","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"الإشارة بقوله: (ومن يكسب إثمًا..) الآية، أي: فإنما يُسَوِّدُ به نور نفسه وروحه، ومن تلبَّس بذنب أو عيب، ثم يرم به غيرَه من باب سُوءِ الظن (فقد احتمل بهتانًا وإثمًا مبينًا) لأن الواجب على المريد السائر أن يشهد الصفاء من غيره، ويُقصر النقصَ على نفسه، والواصل يرى الكمال في كل شيء لمعرفته في كل شيء. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_111-14","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"4:111–112 · The burden of wrongdoing","text":"ثم شهد لرسوله بالهداية والعناية، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_111-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_111-s1","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"","text":"Theft, false oaths and laying a crime upon another are sins whose liability returns to the perpetrator. God knows the inward secrets of His servants and is wise in granting respite and concealing their faults. A “fault” ( khaṭīʾa ) may be an offence injuring another, whereas “sin” ( ithm ) can name wrongdoing confined to its perpetrator. If the guilty person then accuses an innocent person, as Ṭuʿma accused the Jewish man Zayd, he carries a buhtān : a slander which stuns the accused with a deed he never committed. He thereby bears an obviously abominable sin.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_111-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_111-s2","r":"q4_cont_111","title":"","text":"Sin is what troubles the breast, remains unsettled there and meets no inward acceptance; its opposite, birr (righteous goodness), expands the breast and brings the heart peace. One who undertakes an action rejected by the inward conscience darkens the light of the soul and spirit. If he then projects his own defect upon another through suspicion, he compounds wrongdoing with false accusation. The traveller on the path should see purity in other people and locate the shortcoming in himself. The one who has arrived ( wāṣil ) sees perfection everywhere because the One truly recognised is seen through everything. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_111-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_113","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction 4:113","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_113"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-1","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"وَلَوْلا فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَتُهُ لَهَمَّتْ طائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ أَنْ يُضِلُّوكَ وَما يُضِلُّونَ إِلاَّ أَنْفُسَهُمْ وَما يَضُرُّونَكَ مِنْ شَيْءٍ وَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَكَ ما لَمْ تَكُنْ تَعْلَمُ وَكانَ فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكَ عَظِيماً (113)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-2","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"قلت: الجارّ في قوله: (من شيء) ، في موضع نصب على المصدر، أي: لا يضرونك شيئًا من الضرر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-3","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَوْلا فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-4","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"بالعصمة ورحمته بالعناية، لَهَمَّتْ طائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-5","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"وهم رهط السارق أَنْ يُضِلُّوكَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-6","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"عن القضاء بالحق، مع علمهم بالقصة، لكن سبقت العناية، وحفت الرعاية، فلم تخرج من عين الهداية. وليس المراد نفي همهم لأنه وقع، إنما المراد نفي تأثيره فيه، وَما يُضِلُّونَ إِلَّا أَنْفُسَهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-7","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"لعوده عليهم، وَما يَضُرُّونَكَ مِنْ شَيْءٍ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-8","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"لأن الله عصمك، وما خطر ببالك من المجادلة عنهم، كان اعتمادًا منك على ظاهر الأمر، وإنما أُمرتَ أن تحكم بالظواهر، والله يتولى السرائر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-9","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"وَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتابَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-10","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"أي: القرآن، وَالْحِكْمَةَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-11","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"ما نطقتَ به من الحِكَم، وَعَلَّمَكَ ما لَمْ تَكُنْ تَعْلَمُ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-12","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"من خفيات الأمور، التي لم تطلع عليها، أو من أمور الدين والأحكام، وَكانَ فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكَ عَظِيماً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-13","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"ولا فضل أعظم من النبوة، لا سيما وقد فضَّله على كافة الخلق وأرسله إلى كافة الناس، وهدى الله على يديه ما لم يَهدِ على يدِ أحد من الأنبياء قبله، إلى غير ذلك من الفضائل التي تفوت الحصر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-14","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"الإشارة: لولا أن الله تفضل على أوليائه بسابق العناية، وحفَّت بهم منه الكلاءة والرعاية، لأضلتهم العموم عن عين التحقيق، ولأتلفتهم القواطع عن سلوك الطريق، لكن مَن سبقت له العناية لا يصيبه سهمُ الجناية، فثبَّتَ أقدامهم على سير الطريق، حتى أظهر لهم معالم التحقيق، فكشف عن قلوبهم رين الحجاب، حتى فهموا أسرار الكتاب، ونبع من قلوبهم ينابيع الحِكَم والأسرار، واطلعوا على علوم لم يُحِط بها كتاب ولا دفتر، فحازوا في الدارين خيرًا جسيمًا، وكان فضل الله عليهم عظيمًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_113-15","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"4:113 · Divine protection and instruction","text":"ولما ظهرت السرقة على طعمة، كثر فى شأنه التناجي والخوض فيما لا يعني، فنهاهم الحقّ عن ذلك فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_113-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_113-s1","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"","text":"I say: the expression “in anything” ( min shayʾ ) has the syntactic force of an accusative verbal noun, “not the least amount of harm.” God's grace upon the Prophet consists in safeguarding from error ( ʿiṣma ) and His mercy in providential care. The thief's associates, although aware of the events, tried to divert judgment from the truth. God's prior care prevented their plan from affecting the Prophet. The verse does not deny that they intended deception; it denies that the intention achieved its effect. Their error returns upon themselves. The contemplated defence rested only on the apparent circumstances, which is what the Prophet is charged to judge; God knows the inner realities. The Book is the Qurʾān, wisdom includes the wisdom voiced by the Prophet, and what was taught includes hidden matters and ordinances not previously known. Among the immeasurable divine favours upon him, none is greater than prophethood, above all when accompanied by his pre-eminence among creation, universal mission and the guidance God brought about through him as He had not through any prophet before him.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_113-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_113-s2","r":"q4_cont_113","title":"","text":"Without the prior divine grace and protection surrounding God's saints, ordinary society would turn them from direct verification and attachments would destroy their progress along the path. When divine care precedes a person, the arrow of wrongdoing does not strike him. God makes their feet firm until landmarks of realised knowledge appear, removes the tarnish of veils from their hearts, opens to them the secrets of the Book, and causes fountains of wisdom and mystery to spring from them. They become acquainted with sciences not encompassed by book or register. Thus they acquire great good in both worlds; God's favour toward them is immense. After Ṭuʿma's theft became known, the text turns to the excessive whispering about his affair.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_113-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_114","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation 4:114","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_114"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-1","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"لا خَيْرَ فِي كَثِيرٍ مِنْ نَجْواهُمْ إِلاَّ مَنْ أَمَرَ بِصَدَقَةٍ أَوْ مَعْرُوفٍ أَوْ إِصْلاحٍ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ ابْتِغاءَ مَرْضاتِ اللَّهِ فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيهِ أَجْراً عَظِيماً (114)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-2","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"قلت: إن كان المراد بالنجوى الكلام الخفي فالاستثناء منقطع، وقد يكون متصلاً على حذف مضاف أي: إلا نجوى مَن أمر ... الخ. وإن كان المراد بالنجوى الجماعة المتناجين، فالاستثناء متصل. قاله ابن جزي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-3","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله محرّضًا على الصمت: لا خَيْرَ فِي كَثِيرٍ مما يتناجون به في شأن السارق أو غيره، بل لا خير في الكلام بأسره إِلَّا مَنْ أَمَرَ بِصَدَقَةٍ واجبة أو تطوعية، فله مثل أجره، أَوْ مَعْرُوفٍ وهو: ما يستحسنه الشرع، ويوافقه العقل، كالقرض، وإغاثة الملهوف، وتعليم الجاهل، وإرشاد الضال، وغير ذلك من أنواع المعروف. أو أمر بإصلاح بَيْنَ النَّاسِ، أي: إصلاح ذات البين، كإصلاح بين طعمة واليهودي وغيرهما.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-4","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"قال مجاهد: (هي عامة للناس) ، يريد أنه لا خير فيما يتناجى فيه الناس، ويخوضون فيه من الحديث، إلا ما كان من أعمال الخير.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-5","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ أي: الصدقة، والمعروف والإصلاح، ابْتِغاءَ مَرْضاتِ اللَّهِ أي: مُخلصًا لله فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيهِ أَجْراً عَظِيماً وخيرًا جسيمًا. قال البيضاوي: بَنَى الكلامَ على الأمر، ورتَّب الجزاء على الفعل، ليدل على أنه لما دخل الآمر في زمرة الخَيّرين كان الفاعل أدخل فيهم، وأن العمدة والغرض هو الفعل، واعتبار الأمر من حيث إنه وصلة إليه. وقيد الفعل بأن يكون لطلب مرضاة الله لأن الأعمال بالنيات، وإن من فعل خيرًا رياء وسمعة، لم يستحق بها من الله أجرًا، ووصف الأجر بالعظم تنبيهًا على حقارة مافات في جنبه من أغراض الدنيا. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-6","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"الإشارة: في الآية حثٌّ على الصمت، وهو ركن قوي في طريق التصوف، وهو أحد الأركان الأربعة التي هي: العزلة والجوع والسهر، فهذه طريق أهل البداية، ومن لا بداية له لا نهاية له، وقالوا: بقدر ما يصمت اللسان يعمر الجنان، وبقدر ما كان يتكلم اللسان يخرب الجنان. وقالوا أيضًا: إذا كثر العلمُ قلَّ الكلام، وإذا قل العلم كثر الكلام. وقالوا أيضًا: من عرف الله كَلَّ لسانهُ. وقيل لبعض العلماء: هل العلم فيما سلف أكثر، أو اليوم أكثر؟ قال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-7","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"العلم فيما سلف أكثر، والكلامُ اليومَ أكثر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-8","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"وفي قوله: وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذلِكَ.. إشارة إلى أن العمل أشرف من العلم بلا عمل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_114-9","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"4:114 · Private talk, charity and reconciliation","text":"ثم نزل فى شأن طعمة، لما هرب وارتد مشركا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_114-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_114-s1","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"","text":"If najwā denotes whispered speech, the exception “except one who commands...” is grammatically disconnected unless a noun is understood: “except the confidential speech of someone who commands...” If it denotes the company of whisperers, the exception is connected. This is Ibn Juzayy's observation.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_114-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_114-s2","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"","text":"God encourages silence. There is no good in much of their private talk about the thief or others; indeed, Ibn ʿAjība says, there is no good in speech as a whole except when one enjoins charity, obligatory or voluntary, recognised right action ( maʿrūf ), or reconciliation. One who enjoins charity has a reward equal to that of its giver. Maʿrūf is what the revealed law approves and sound reason recognises, such as lending, rescuing someone in distress, educating the ignorant or guiding the lost. Reconciling those in conflict includes the dispute involving Ṭuʿma and the Jewish man. Mujāhid is cited for interpreting the verse universally, addressing conversations among all people. Whoever actually performs charity, beneficence or peacemaking, seeking God's satisfaction with sincerity, receives an abundant reward. Al-Bayḍāwī notes the rhetoric: the verse praises commanding good yet attaches the reward to doing it. The one who enjoins good is included among the good, but the performer merits that description even more; commanding is important because it leads to action. Seeking God's pleasure is made a condition because actions are judged by intentions. A deed performed for display or reputation does not earn this divine reward. Calling that reward tremendous draws attention to how paltry worldly objectives are beside it.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_114-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_114-s3","r":"q4_cont_114","title":"","text":"Silence is a strong pillar of Sufi formation and one of its four disciplines, joined by solitude, hunger and vigil. These mark the way of beginners; one without a beginning will have no completion. They say that the garden of the heart is cultivated as the tongue becomes quiet and is devastated as speech proliferates. As knowledge increases, talk decreases; with less knowledge, words abound. Whoever knows God finds the tongue exhausted before Him. Asked whether there had been more knowledge in former times or now, a scholar replied, “Knowledge was more abundant before, but speech is more abundant today.” The phrase “whoever does this” also indicates the superiority of action over learning that never produces practice. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_114-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_115","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers 4:115–116","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_115"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-1","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"وَمَنْ يُشاقِقِ الرَّسُولَ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ الْهُدى وَيَتَّبِعْ غَيْرَ سَبِيلِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ نُوَلِّهِ ما تَوَلَّى وَنُصْلِهِ جَهَنَّمَ وَساءَتْ مَصِيراً (115) إِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَغْفِرُ أَنْ يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذلِكَ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ وَمَنْ يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلالاً بَعِيداً (116)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-2","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"قلت: المشاقة: المخالفة والمباعدة، كأنَّ كل واحد من المتخالفين في شق غير شقّ الآخر.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-3","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ يخالف الرَّسُولَ ويتباعد عنه مِنْ بَعْدِ ما تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ الْهُدى أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-4","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"بعد ما تحقق أنه على الهدى بالوقوف على المعجزات، فيترك طريق الحق وَيَتَّبِعْ غَيْرَ سَبِيلِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أي: يسلك غير ما هم عليه، من اعتقاد أو عمل. نُوَلِّهِ ما تَوَلَّى أي: نتركه مع ما تولى، ونجعله وليًّا له، ونُخَلِّي بينه وبين ما اختاره من الضلالة، وَنُصْلِهِ جَهَنَّمَ أي: ندخله فيها، ونشويه بها، وَساءَتْ مَصِيراً أي: قبحت مصيرا جهنم التي يصير إليها. والآية تَدُل على حرمة مخالفة الإجماع، لأن الله رتَّب الوعيد الشديد على مشاقة الرسول، واتباع غير سبيل المؤمنين، وكل منهما محرم، وإذا كان اتباع غير سبيلهم محرمًا كان اتباع سبيلهم واجبًا، انظر البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-5","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"ثم نزل في طُعمة لما ارتد مشركًا: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَغْفِرُ أَنْ يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذلِكَ لِمَنْ يَشاءُ وقيل: كرر للتأكيد تقبيحًا لشأن الشرك، وقيل: أتى شيخ إلى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال: إني شيخ منهمك في الذنوب إلا أني لم أشرك بالله شيئًا منذ عرفتُه وآمنتُ به، ولم أتخذ من دونه وليًا، ولم أوقع المعاصي جرأة، وما توهمت طرفة عين أني أُعجز الله هربًا، وإني لنادم تائب، فما ترى حالي عند الله؟ فنزلت. وَمَنْ يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ، فَقَدْ ضَلَّ عن الحق ضَلالًا بَعِيداً لأن الشّرك أقبح أنواع الضلالة، وأبعدها عن الثواب والاستقامة، وإنما ذكر في الآية الأولى. فَقَدِ افْتَرى لأنها متصلة بقصة أهل الكتاب، ومنشأ شركهم نوع افتراء، وهو دعوى الشيء على الله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-6","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-7","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"الإشارة: كل من خالف شيخه، وسلك طريقًا غير طريقه ولاه الله ما تولى، واستدرجه من حيث لا يشعر، وقد تؤخر العقوبة عنه فيقول: لو كان هذا فيه سوء أدب مع الله، لقطع الإمداد وأوجب البعاد، وقد يقطع عنه من حيث لا يشعر، ولو لم يكن إلا وتخليته وما يريد. وبالجملة: فالخروج عن مشايخ التربية والانتقال عنهم، ولو إلى من هو أكمل في زعمه، بعد ما ظهر له الفتح والهداية على يديه طردٌ وبعدٌ، وإفساد لبذرة الإرادة، فلا نتيجة له أصلاً. والله تعالى أعلم. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_115-8","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"4:115–116 · Opposing the Messenger and the believers","text":"ثم قبّح شأن الشرك، وشنّع قبحه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_115-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_115-s1","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"","text":"I say: mushāqqa is opposition and estrangement, as if the two opponents occupied different sides ( shiqq ) of a division. Whoever departs from the Messenger after recognising his guidance through his miracles, and follows beliefs or conduct contrary to the believers' path, is left to the allegiance he selected and to the misguidance he embraced. Ibn ʿAjība, following al-Bayḍāwī, treats the two prohibited acts—opposing the Messenger and following a different communal path—as evidence that violating authoritative consensus ( ijmāʿ ) is forbidden, and consequently that the believers' agreed path is binding. The next verse is also said to have been revealed concerning Ṭuʿma after his apostasy, or to repeat the condemnation of associationism for emphasis. Another report concerns an old man who asked the Prophet about long-standing sin, explaining that he had never associated partners with God, had never relied on another patron, had not sinned in deliberate defiance, had always known he could not elude God, and was repentant. The verse was revealed, according to this report. Associationism constitutes the furthest departure from truth and rectitude. Al-Bayḍāwī explains that the earlier use of “fabricated a monstrous lie” fits the preceding controversy with the People of the Book, whose particular error involved making a claim about God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_115-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_115-s2","r":"q4_cont_115","title":"","text":"Whoever opposes his shaykh and follows a path other than his, God leaves him to what he has chosen and gradually draws him toward ruin without his noticing. A person may suppose that continuing spiritual gifts prove no error of conduct occurred, even though the gifts have been cut off without his awareness—or even though he is simply being left alone to his desires. In Ibn ʿAjība’s account, leaving a master through whom openings and guidance have appeared, even for another imagined to be more perfect, is expulsion and estrangement, corrupts the seed of aspiration, and yields no result at all. [Translator’s note: this claim concerns Ibn ʿAjība’s school of discipleship and should be distinguished from the independent juristic limits of a teacher’s authority.] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_115-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_117","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises 4:117–121","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_117"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-1","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"إِنْ يَدْعُونَ مِنْ دُونِهِ إِلاَّ إِناثاً وَإِنْ يَدْعُونَ إِلاَّ شَيْطاناً مَرِيداً (117) لَعَنَهُ اللَّهُ وَقالَ لَأَتَّخِذَنَّ مِنْ عِبادِكَ نَصِيباً مَفْرُوضاً (118) وَلَأُضِلَّنَّهُمْ وَلَأُمَنِّيَنَّهُمْ وَلَآمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُبَتِّكُنَّ آذانَ الْأَنْعامِ وَلَآمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُغَيِّرُنَّ خَلْقَ اللَّهِ وَمَنْ يَتَّخِذِ الشَّيْطانَ وَلِيًّا مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ فَقَدْ خَسِرَ خُسْراناً مُبِيناً (119) يَعِدُهُمْ وَيُمَنِّيهِمْ وَما يَعِدُهُمُ الشَّيْطانُ إِلاَّ غُرُوراً (120) أُولئِكَ مَأْواهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ وَلا يَجِدُونَ عَنْها مَحِيصاً (121)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-2","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"قلت: المَرِيد والمارد هو الذي لا يعلق بخير، وأصل التركيب للملابسة، ومنه: صرح ممرَّد، وغلام أمرد، وشجرة مردى، أي: سقط ورقها. قاله البيضاوي. هـ. وقيل: المريد: الشديد العاتي، الخارج عن الطاعة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-3","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنْ يَدْعُونَ: ما يعبدون مِنْ دُونِهِ تعالى إِلَّا إِناثاً، كاللات والعزى ومناة، فإن ألفاظها مؤنثة عندهم، أو لأنها جوامد لا تعقل، فهي منفعلة لا فاعلة، ومن حق المعبود أن يكون فاعلاً غير منفعل، أو يريد الملائكة لأنهم كانوا يعبدونها، ويزعمون أنها بنات الله، وما يعبدون في الحقيقة إِلَّا شَيْطاناً مَرِيداً عاصيًا، لأنه هو الذي أمرهم بها، وأغراهم عليها، وكان يكلمهم من أجوافها.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-4","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"ثم وصفه بأوصاف تُوجب التنفير عنه فقال: لَعَنَهُ اللَّهُ أي: أبعده من رحمته، وَقالَ لَأَتَّخِذَنَّ مِنْ عِبادِكَ نَصِيباً مَفْرُوضاً أي: مقطوعًا فرضته لنفسي، من قولهم: فرض له في العطاء، أي: قطع، وَلَأُضِلَّنَّهُمْ عن الحق وَلَأُمَنِّيَنَّهُمْ الأماني الباطلة، كطول الحياة، وألاَّ بعث ولا عقاب، وَلَآمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُبَتِّكُنَّ آذانَ الْأَنْعامِ أي: يشقونها لتحريم ما أحل الله، وهي عبارة عما كانت العرب تفعل بالبحائر والسوائب، وإشارة إلى تحريم كل ما أحل الله، ونقص كل ما خلق الله كاملاً بالفعل أو بالقوة، وَلَآمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُغَيِّرُنَّ خَلْقَ اللَّهِ، صورة، أو صفة، فيندرج فيه خصاء العبيد والوشم، والتنمص- وهو نتف الحاجب-.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-5","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"زاد البيضاوي: واللواط، والمساحقة، وعبادة الشمس والقمر، وتغيير فطرة الله التي هي الإسلام، واستعمال الجوارح والقوى فيما لا يعود على النفس كمالاً ولا يوجب لها من الله زلفى. وعموم اللفظ يقتضي منع الخِصاء مطلقًا، لكن الفقهاء رخصوا في خصاء البهائم للحاجة، والجُمل الأربع حكاية عما ذكره الشيطان نطقًا، أو أتاه فعلاً. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-6","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"ثم حذّر منه فقال: وَمَنْ يَتَّخِذِ الشَّيْطانَ وَلِيًّا مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ باتباعه فيما أمره به دون ما أمر الله به، فَقَدْ خَسِرَ خُسْراناً مُبِيناً واضحًا حيث ضيع رأس ماله، وأبدل بمكانه من الجنة مكانه من النار. يَعِدُهُمْ أي: الشيطان، أمورًا لا تُنجز لهم، وَيُمَنِّيهِمْ أماني لا تعطى لهم، وَما يَعِدُهُمُ أي: الشَّيْطانُ إِلَّا غُرُوراً، وهو إظهار النفع فيما فيه الضرر، فكان يوسوس لهم أنهم على الحق وأنهم أولى بالجنة، إلى غير ذلك من أنواع الغرور، أُولئِكَ المغرورون مَأْواهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ أي: هي منزلهم ومقامهم، وَلا يَجِدُونَ عَنْها مَحِيصاً أي: مهربًا ولا معدلاً. من حاص يحيص: إذا عدل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-7","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"الإشارة: ما أحببتَ شيئاً إلا كنت له عبدًا، فاحذر أن تكون ممن يعبد من دون الله إناثًا، إن كنت تحب نفسك، وتؤثر هواها على حق مولاها، أو تكون عبد المرأة أو الخميصة (1) أو البهيمة، أو غير ذلك من الشهوات التي أنت تحبها، واحذر أيضًا أن تكون من نصيب الشيطان بإيحاشك إلى الكريم المنان، وفي الحِكَم:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-8","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"«إذا علمت أن الشيطان لا يغفل عنك، فلا تغفل أنت عمن ناصيتك بيده» . فاشتغل بمحبة الحبيب، يكفيك عداوة العدو، فاتخذ الله وليًا وصاحبًا، ودع الشيطان جانبًا، غِب عن الشيطان باستغراقك في حضرة العِيان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-9","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_117-10","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"4:117–121 · False objects of devotion and Satan’s promises","text":"ثم ذكر ضد أهل الشرك، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_117-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_117-s1","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"","text":"I say: marīd or mārid can describe something to which no good adheres. The root’s basic sense is [smoothness], with the examples of a smooth palace, a beardless youth and a tree whose leaves have fallen; this is attributed to al-Bayḍāwī. [Translator’s textual note: Cairo I:562 prints li-l-mulābasa , “association” or “intermingling,” as does the checked electronic text of al-Bayḍāwī. Abū al-Suʿūd on 4:117 explicitly has li-l-malāsa , “smoothness,” beside the same palace and bare-tree examples. Those examples and the exact earlier parallel establish the intended lexical explanation. The bracketed English adopts it openly; it does not claim that Cairo or an independently checked manuscript of Ibn ʿAjība prints the corrected word. See source check XII-S062.] Another explanation is defiant and intensely rebellious, departing from obedience.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_117-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_117-s2","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"","text":"The female entities invoked apart from God may be idols named with feminine nouns—al-Lāt, al-ʿUzzā and Manāt—or lifeless objects capable only of being acted upon, whereas divinity demands an agent, not something passively acted upon. Or the verse may mean the angels, falsely regarded by their worshippers as divine daughters. In reality such worship answers Satan, who encouraged it and, in some reports, spoke from the interior of the idols. God cursed Satan, distancing him from mercy. Satan claimed an allotted share of servants, resolved to mislead them and promised false hopes of long life, denial of resurrection or immunity from judgment. His command to slit livestock ears refers to the custom of marking baḥīra and sāʾiba animals and prohibiting what God permitted. By extension it refers to wrongfully forbidding permitted things and damaging an integrity God created, whether actually realised or latent. “Changing God's creation” may concern bodily alteration or change of attributes. Ibn ʿAjība lists castration of slaves, tattooing and plucking eyebrows; al-Bayḍāwī adds sodomy ( liwāṭ ) and female same-sex sexual activity ( musāḥaqa ), worship of the sun and moon, replacing the primordial disposition ( fiṭra ) of Islam, and employing limbs and capacities in ways that bring the soul no perfection or divine nearness. Although the verse's generality seems to prohibit castration, jurists made an exception for castrating animals where a recognised need existed. The four clauses reporting Satan's resolutions may recount words actually spoken or deeds through which the intentions were expressed. To take Satan as a protecting companion by obeying his commands in preference to God's is a manifest loss: the person forfeits the capital of life and substitutes a place in Hell for the promised place in Paradise. Satan makes promises he cannot fulfil, arouses desires for things never to be given, and disguises harm as benefit, including the delusion that his followers are right and best entitled to Paradise. Such people will find no turning away ( maḥīṣ ) from the consequence; ḥāṣa means to turn aside.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_117-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_117-s3","r":"q4_cont_117","title":"","text":"Whatever you love, you become its slave. Beware of serving “female idols” in the sense of loving the lower soul and preferring its appetite to the Lord's claim. Likewise do not become the slave of a woman, a fine garment, an animal, or any other object of appetite that you love. Nor yield to Satan's efforts to make you estranged from the Most Generous. The Ḥikam warns: “When you know that Satan does not neglect you, do not neglect the One who holds your forelock.” Occupy yourself with love of the Beloved: it suffices against the enmity of the enemy. Take God as intimate patron and companion, put Satan aside and become absent from his suggestions through immersion in the Presence of direct witnessing. God gives success.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_117-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_122","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"4:122 · The promise to believers","text":"4:122 · The promise to believers 4:122","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_122"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_122-1","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"4:122 · The promise to believers","text":"وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها أَبَداً وَعْدَ اللَّهِ حَقًّا وَمَنْ أَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللَّهِ قِيلاً (122)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_122-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_122-2","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"4:122 · The promise to believers","text":"قلت: (وعد اللهِ) مصدر، مؤكد لنفسه، أي: وعدهم وعدًا، و (حقًا) مؤكد لغيره، أي: لمضمون الجملة قبله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_122-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_122-3","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"4:122 · The promise to believers","text":"انظر البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_122-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_122-4","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"4:122 · The promise to believers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بالله ووحدوه، وَعَمِلُوا الأعمال الصَّالِحاتِ التي كلفوا بها سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ خالِدِينَ فِيها أَبَداً وعدهم بذلك وعدًا حقًا، وَمَنْ أَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللَّهِ قِيلًا أي: لا أحدَ أصدقُ من الله في قوله. والمقصود من الآية معارضة المواعيد الشيطانية الكاذبة لقرنائه، بوعد الله الصادق لأوليائه، ترغيبًا في تحصيل أسبابه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_122-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_122-5","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"4:122 · The promise to believers","text":"الإشارة: والذين جمعوا بين توحيد عظمة الربوبية والقيام بوظائف العبودية سندخلهم جنةَ المعارف، تجري من تحتها أنهار العلوم، خالدين فيها أبدًا، وعداً حقاً وقولاً صدقاً. ومن أصدق من الله قيلا؟","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_122-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_122-6","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"4:122 · The promise to believers","text":"وهذا الوعد لا ينال بالأمانى مع البطالة والتواني وإنما ينال بالأعمال الصالحة والمقاصد الخالصة، كما قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_122-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_122-s1","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"","text":"I say: waʿda llāhi is a confirming verbal noun reinforcing its own action—“He promised them a promise.” Ḥaqqan confirms the substance of the preceding statement, as al-Bayḍāwī explains. Those who profess God's unity and perform the works imposed upon them are admitted to eternal gardens. No speech is more truthful than God's. The verse counterposes God's dependable promise to His intimates against the false promises Satan offers his associates, and encourages attaining the means of that promise.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_122-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_122-s2","r":"q4_cont_122","title":"","text":"Those who unite recognition of the oneness of majestic Lordship ( rubūbiyya ) with the actual duties of servanthood ( ʿubūdiyya ) will enter the garden of direct knowledges ( jannat al-maʿārif ), beneath which flow rivers of sciences, abiding there in enduring felicity. The promise is true, but it is not obtained through fantasies joined to idleness: it is acquired through upright works and purified intentions, as the following verse makes plain.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_122-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_123","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability 4:123","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_123"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-1","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"لَيْسَ بِأَمانِيِّكُمْ وَلا أَمانِيِّ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ مَنْ يَعْمَلْ سُوءاً يُجْزَ بِهِ وَلا يَجِدْ لَهُ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَلِيًّا وَلا نَصِيراً (123)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-2","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"قلت: اسم ليس ضمير الأمر، أي: ليس الأمر بأمانيكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-3","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لَيْسَ هذا الوعد الذي ذكرت لأهل الإيمان يُنَال بِأَمانِيِّكُمْ أي: تمنيكم أيها المسلمون، ولا بأماني أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ، أي: لا يكون ما تتمنون ولا ما يتمنى أهل الكتاب، بل يحكم الله بين عباده ويجازيهم بأعمالهم. رُوِي أن المسلمين وأهل الكتاب تفاخروا، فقال أهل الكتاب: نبينا قبل نبيكم، وكتابنا قبل كتابكم، ونحن أولى بالله منكم، وقال المسلمون: نحن أولى منكم، نبينا خاتم النبيين، وكتابنا يقضي على الكتب المتقدمة، فنزلت. وقيل: الخطاب مع المشركين، وهو قولهم: لا جنة ولا نار، أو قولهم: إن كان الأمر كما يزعم هؤلاء لنكونن خيرًا منهم وأحسن حالاً.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-4","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"وأماني أهل الكتاب: قولهم لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ إِلَّا أَيَّاماً مَعْدُوداتٍ ولَنْ يَدْخُلَ الْجَنَّةَ إِلَّا مَنْ كانَ هُوداً أَوْ نَصارى ثم قرر ذلك فقال: مَنْ يَعْمَلْ سُوءاً يُجْزَ بِهِ عاجلاً أو آجلاً لِما رُوِي أنه لمّا نزلت قال أبو بكر:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-5","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"من ينجو مع هذا يا رسول الله، إن كنا مجزيين بكل سوء عملناه؟ فقال له- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «أما تحزن؟","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-6","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"أما تمرض؟ أما يصيبك اللأواء (1)؟ قال: بلى يا رسول الله، قال: هو ذلك» . فكل من عمل سوءًا جوزي به، وَلا يَجِدْ لَهُ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَلِيًّا يليه ويدفع عنه، وَلا نَصِيراً ينصره ويمنعه من عذاب الله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-7","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"الإشارة: لا تُنال المراتب بالأماني الكاذبة والدعاوي الفارغة، وإنما تنال بالهمم العالية، والمجاهدات القوية، إنما تنال المقامات العالية بالأعمال الصالحة، والأحوال الصافية، وأنشدوا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-8","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"بقدر الكدّ تُكتَسَبُ المَعَالِي ... من أراد العز سهر الليالي","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-9","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"تُرِيدُ العزَّ ثُم تَنَامُ ليلاً ... يَغُوصُ البحر مَن طَلَبَ اللآلي","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_123-10","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"4:123 · Merit, religion and accountability","text":"ولمّا نزل قوله تعالى: لَيْسَ بِأَمانِيِّكُمْ وَلا أَمانِيِّ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ ... الآية. قال أهل الكتاب: نحن وأنتم سواء، فأنزل الله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_123-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_123-s1","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"","text":"I say: the suppressed subject of laysa is “the matter,” so the sense is: “the matter is not governed by your wishes.” The promise given to believers is not attained by the Muslims' hopes alone or by those of the People of the Book. God will judge between servants by deeds. A report tells of mutual boasting: the People of the Book argued their prophets and scriptures preceded those of Muslims; Muslims claimed precedence because their Prophet was the Seal and their Book confirmed and governed earlier books. Another interpretation addresses polytheists who denied Paradise and Hell, or who imagined they would fare better than believers should the hereafter prove true. The People of the Book's wishful claims include that the Fire would touch them only briefly and that Paradise was reserved for Jews or Christians. Wrongdoing must be accounted for, whether now or later. Abū Bakr is reported to have feared, when the verse was revealed, that no one could be saved if every wrong brought retribution. The Prophet reminded him that sorrow, sickness and life's severe difficulties themselves answer part of that account. Outside God no guardian or helper can repel His judgment.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_123-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_123-s2","r":"q4_cont_123","title":"","text":"High stations cannot be reached by empty wishing and boasts. They require lofty aspiration ( himam ), vigorous spiritual exertion ( mujāhada ), good works and purified states. Verses are recited: Sublimity is won in proportion to the toil; whoever seeks honour spends the nights awake. You desire exaltation, yet sleep through the night— the seeker of pearls must dive into the sea. According to the report, the People of the Book responded that Muslims and themselves had been made equal; the following verse then makes the distinctive requirements of belief and work clear.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_123-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_124","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden 4:124–126","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_124"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-1","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ مِنَ الصَّالِحاتِ مِنْ ذَكَرٍ أَوْ أُنْثى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَأُولئِكَ يَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ وَلا يُظْلَمُونَ نَقِيراً (124) وَمَنْ أَحْسَنُ دِيناً مِمَّنْ أَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهُ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ وَاتَّبَعَ مِلَّةَ إِبْراهِيمَ حَنِيفاً وَاتَّخَذَ اللَّهُ إِبْراهِيمَ خَلِيلاً (125) وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُحِيطاً (126)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-2","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"قلت: (من ذَكَرٍ أو أنثى) : حال من الضمير في (يعمل) ، وكذا قوله: وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ و (حنيفًا) ، حال من (إبراهيم) لأنه جزء ما أضيف إليه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-3","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ شيئاً مَنْ الأعمال الصَّالِحاتِ وهو المهم من المكلف به، إذ لا طاقة للبشر على الإتيان بكلها. حال كون العامل مِنْ ذَكَرٍ أَوْ أُنْثى إذ النساء شقائق الرجال في طلب الأعمال، والحالة أن العامل مُؤْمِنٌ لأن الإيمان شرط في قبول الأعمال، فلا ثواب على عمل ليس معه إيمان.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-4","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"ثم ذكر الجواب فقال: فَأُولئِكَ يَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ أي: يتصفون بالدخول، أو يُدخلهم الله الجنة، وَلا يُظْلَمُونَ أي: لا ينقصون من ثواب أعمالهم نَقِيراً أي: مقداره، وهو النقرة في ظهر النواة. قال البيضاوي: وإذا لم ينقص ثواب المطيع فبالأحرى ألا يزيد في عقاب العاصي، لأن المجازي أرحَمُ الراحمين. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-5","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"وَمَنْ أَحْسَنُ دِيناً مِمَّنْ أَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهُ لِلَّهِ أي: لا أحد أحسن دينًا ممن انقاد بكليته إلى مولاه وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ أي: موحد أحسَنَ فيما بينه وبين الله، وفيما بينه وبين عباد الله، وَاتَّبَعَ مِلَّةَ إِبْراهِيمَ حَنِيفاً بأن دخل في الدين المحمدي الذي هو موافق لملة إبراهيم بل هو عينه، فمن ادعى أنه على ملة إبراهيم ولم يدخل فيه فقد كذب.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-6","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"ثم ذكر ما يحث على اتباع ملته، فقال: وَاتَّخَذَ اللَّهُ إِبْراهِيمَ خَلِيلًا أي: اصطفاه وخصه بكرامة تشبه كرامة الخليل عند خليله، وإنما أعاد ذكره ولم يضمر تفخيمًا له وتنصيصًا على أنه الممدوح، وسمي خليلاً لأنه قد تخللت محبة الله في جميع أجزائه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-7","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"رُوِي أن إبراهيم عليه السلام كان يضيف الناس، حتى كان يسمى أبا الضيفان، وكان منزله على ظهر الطريق، فأصاب الناسَ سَنَةٌ، جهدوا فيها، فحشد الناسُ إلى باب إبراهيم، يطلبون الطعامَ، وكانت الميرة كل سنة تصله من صديق له بمصر، فبعث غلمانه بالإبل إلى الخليل الذي له بمصر يسأله الميرة، فقال لغلمانه: لو كان إبراهيم يريد لنفسه احتملت له ذلك، ولكنه يريد للأضياف، وقد أصابنا ما أصاب الناس، فرجع الرسل إليه، ومرّوا ببطحاء لينة، فملأوا منها الغرائر حياء من الناس، وأتوا إبراهيم فأخبروه، فاهتم إبراهيم لمكان الناس ببابه، فنام، وكانت سارة نائمة فاستيقظت، وقالت: سبحان الله! أما جاء الغلمان؟ فقالوا: بلى، فقامت إلى الغرائر فإذا فيها أجود الحوّارى- أي: الخالص من الدقيق- فخبزوا وأطعموا؟ فاستيقظ إبراهيم، وشم رائحة الخبز، فقال: يا سارة، من أين هذا؟","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-8","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"فقالت: من عند خليلك المصري، فقال: هذا من عند خليلي الله- عز وجل-، فحينئذ سماه الله خليلاً (1) .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-9","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"قال الزجاج: ومعنى الخليل: الذي ليس في محبته خلل، أو لأنه ردَّ خلَته، أي: فقره إلى الله مخلصًا. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-10","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ مُلكاً وخلقا وعبيدا، فالملك له، والعبيد عبيده، يختار ما يشاء كما يشاء من خلة ومحبة وخدمة، وَكانَ اللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُحِيطاً علمًا وقدرة، فيجازي كلا على قدر سعيه وقصده. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-11","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"الإشارة: على قدر المجاهدة والمكابدة تكون المعاينة والمشاهدة، على قدر البدايات تكون النهايات، من أشرقت بدايته أشرقت نهايته، والجزاء على العمل يكون على قدر الهمم، فمن عمل لجنة الزخارف مُتع بها، ومن عمل لجنة المعارف تنعم بها، وَلا يَظْلِمُ رَبُّكَ أَحَداً، فمن انقاد بكليته إلى مولاه فلا أحد أحسن منه عند الله، ومن تمسك بالملة الحنيفية، وهي الانقطاع إلى الله بالكلية- فقد استمسك بالعروة الوثقى، وكان في أعلى ذروة أهل التقى، من تخلق بخلق الحبيب كان أقربُ إلى الله من كل قريب. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_124-12","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"4:124–126 · Faithful works and the Garden","text":"ومما يتعلق بحفظ اللسان الفتوى بما يطابق الحق، ولذلك ذكره بعد الأمر بالحكم بالعدل، وما بينهما اعتراض انجرّ الكلام إليه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_124-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_124-s1","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"","text":"I say: “Male or female” and “being a believer” are circumstantial expressions qualifying the performer; ḥanīfan is circumstantial concerning Abraham, since the annexed noun (“way”) is a part of that to which it is annexed (Abraham). Whoever performs some of the righteous deeds—namely, the important duties imposed upon him, since a human being cannot accomplish every such action—whether male or female, enters the promise equally: women are the counterparts of men in works. Faith is the condition for the acceptance of these deeds. Those who act in faith enter Paradise, whether the verb is construed as their doing so or God admitting them. They are deprived of no amount of reward, not even the naqīr , the tiny indentation on a date-stone. Al-Bayḍāwī observes that if the obedient do not lose the least of their reward, sinners will still less have their punishment increased unjustly, for the Rewarder is the Most Merciful. The finest religion belongs to one who yields the whole self to the Lord, practices excellence ( iḥsān ) through divine unity and behaves rightly both toward God and toward His servants, and follows the upright religion of Abraham. In Ibn ʿAjība's presentation this is achieved by entering the Muḥammadan religion, which accords with Abraham’s religion—indeed, is that very religion; anyone who claims to follow Abraham’s religion but has not entered it has, he says, lied. God took Abraham as khalīl : He selected him and singled him out for an honour resembling that of an intimate friend with his friend. Repeating Abraham's proper name magnifies him and identifies the one praised. He is called khalīl because love of God permeated every part of his being. Ibn ʿAjība reports that Abraham was known as the father of guests because his home stood beside a road and he fed travellers. In a famine crowds came to his door. Every year a friend in Egypt normally sent him supplies. Abraham sent servants with camels, but the Egyptian friend replied that even he lacked provisions: he would help Abraham personally but could not feed all of Abraham's guests. Ashamed to return with empty sacks, the servants filled them with soft sand as they passed through a valley. Abraham learned their news and worried about his hungry visitors, then slept. Sarah awoke and said, “Glory be to God! Have the servants not arrived?” They replied, “Yes.” She went to the sacks and found in them the purest white flour. They baked bread and fed the guests. Abraham awoke and smelled bread. Told it had come from his Egyptian friend, he answered, “It is from my intimate Friend, God.” It was then, the report says, that God named him His intimate friend. [Cairo editor’s note: citing Ibn Kathīr, the editor questions this story’s authenticity and occurrence. At most, he says, it is an Israelite report, neither affirmed nor denied. Abraham was called God’s intimate friend because of his intense love for God, expressed in obedience that God loves and approves.] Al-Zajjāj explains khalīl either as one whose love has no flaw ( khalal ) or one who refers his need ( khalla ) wholly and sincerely to God. Since all heavens and earth are God's created possessions and servants, He chooses whom He wills for love, intimacy and service. His knowledge and power encompass all things and He recompenses every intention and striving.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_124-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_124-s2","r":"q4_cont_124","title":"","text":"Direct vision corresponds to the measure of struggle and hardship; endings correspond to beginnings. A beginning radiant with sincere aspiration leads to a radiant end. Reward is proportioned to aspiration ( himma ): one who works for a garden of outward delights enjoys it, and one who works for the garden of divine knowledges enjoys that; God wrongs no one. No one is finer than the person entirely surrendered to the Lord. One clinging to Abraham's upright way, understood inwardly as total severance from everything but God, grasps the firmest handle and reaches a summit of reverent godliness. Whoever takes on the Beloved's moral qualities becomes nearer to God than any other who is near. God gives success. Giving a fatwā in accord with the truth is one of the matters concerning guarding the tongue. It is therefore mentioned after the command to judge justly; the intervening discussion is a digression into which the discourse was drawn.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_124-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_127","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women 4:127","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_127"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-1","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"وَيَسْتَفْتُونَكَ فِي النِّساءِ قُلِ اللَّهُ يُفْتِيكُمْ فِيهِنَّ وَما يُتْلى عَلَيْكُمْ فِي الْكِتابِ فِي يَتامَى النِّساءِ اللاَّتِي لا تُؤْتُونَهُنَّ ما كُتِبَ لَهُنَّ وَتَرْغَبُونَ أَنْ تَنْكِحُوهُنَّ وَالْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ مِنَ الْوِلْدانِ وَأَنْ تَقُومُوا لِلْيَتامى بِالْقِسْطِ وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِهِ عَلِيماً (127)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-2","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"قلت: و (ما يتلى) : عطف على (الله) ، أي: يفتيكم الله، والمتلو عليكم في الكتاب، أي: في القرآن. وَتَرْغَبُونَ أَنْ تَنْكِحُوهُنَّ حذف الجار، وهو في أو عن، ليصدق النهي بالراغب فيها إذا كانت جميلة، والراغب عنها إذا كانت دميمة، والْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ عطف على (يتامى النساء) أي: والذي يتلى في المستضعفين من الولدان، وهو قوله تعالى: يُوصِيكُمُ اللَّهُ ... الخ، أو على الضمير في (فيهن) أي: يفتيكم فيهن وفي المستضعفين، و (أن تقوموا) عطف على (المستضعفين) ، أو منصوب بمحذوف، أي: ويأمركم أن تقوموا ... الخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-3","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَيَسْتَفْتُونَكَ يا محمد فِي شأن النِّساءِ من الميراث وغيره، قُلِ اللَّهُ يُفْتِيكُمْ فِيهِنَّ، فيأمركم أن تعطوهن حقهن من الميراث، وَيفتيكم أيضًا فيهن ما يُتْلى عَلَيْكُمْ فِي الْكِتابِ في أول السورة إذ قال: لِلرِّجالِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا اكْتَسَبُوا وَلِلنِّساءِ نَصِيبٌ مِمَّا اكْتَسَبْنَ ثم بيَّنه في تقسيم الميراث في يُوصِيكُمُ اللَّهُ فِي أَوْلادِكُمْ، وقال في اليتامى: وَآتُوا الْيَتامى أَمْوالَهُمْ وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَلَّا تُقْسِطُوا فِي الْيَتامى ... الآية، فقد أفتاكم في اليتامى اللَّاتِي لا تُؤْتُونَهُنَّ ما كُتِبَ لَهُنَّ من الصداق وَتَرْغَبُونَ أَنْ تَنْكِحُوهُنَّ بدون صداق مثلهن، فأمركم أن تنكحوا غيرهن، ولا تنكحوهن إلا أن تقسطوا لهن في الصداق، إذا كانت جميلة، أو لها مال، أو ترغبون عن نكاحهن إذا كانت دميمة، فتعضلوهن لترثوهن، فلا تفعلوا ذلك، بل تزوجوها أو زوجوها، وكانوا في الجاهلية، إذا كانت اليتيمة ذات مال وجمال، رغبوا فيها وتزوجوها بدون صداقها، وإن كانت دميمة ولا مال لها رغبوا عنها وعضلوها، أو زوجوها غيرهم. فنهى الله تعالى الفريقين معا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-4","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"وَيفتيكم أيضًا في الْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ مِنَ الْوِلْدانِ وهم الصغار، أن تعطوهم حقهم من الميراث مع الكبار، وكانوا لا يورثونهم، رُوِي أن عُيينة بن حصن أتى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال: أُخبرنا أنك تورث النساء والصبيان، وإنما كنا نورث من يشهد القتال ويحوز الغنيمة؟ فقال له صلّى الله عليه وسلم: «كذا أُمِرتُ» ، فنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-5","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"وَيفتيكم أيضًا ويأمركم أَنْ تَقُومُوا لِلْيَتامى بِالْقِسْطِ أي: العدل. وهو خطاب للأئمة أن ينظروا لهم بالمصلحة ويستوثقوا حقوقهم، ويحتاطوا لهم في أمورهم كلها. ثم وعدهم بالثواب على ذلك فقال: وَما تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِهِ عَلِيماً، فيجازيكم على قدر إحسانكم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-6","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"الإشارة: يستفتونك عن نساء العلوم الرسمية، وعن يتامى العلوم القلبية، وهن نتائج الأفكار، وهي العلوم اللدنية، والأسرار الربانية التي هي من علوم الحقيقة، ولا تليق إلا بالمستضعفين عند الخليقة، وفى الخبر: «ألا أُخبِركُم بأهل الجَنَّة؟ هو كل ضَعيفٍ متضعَّف، لو أقسمَ على اللهِ لأبرَّهُ في قَسمه» . أو كما قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم. قل الله يفتيكم فيهن فيأمركم أن تأخذوا من العلوم الرسمية ما تتقنون به عبادة ربكم، وترغبوا في علم الطريقة، التي هي علم","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-7","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"القلوب، ما تحققون به عبوديتكم، ومن نتائج الأفكار ما تُشاهدون به عظمة ربكم، ويأمركم أن تقوموا بالعدل فى جميع شئونكم، فتعطوا الشريعة حقها والطريقة حقها، وتحفظوا أسرار الحقيقة عن غير مستحقها، والله لا يضيع أجر المحسنين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_127-8","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"4:127 · Justice toward orphan women","text":"ثم أمر بالصلح بين الزوجين عند خوف النشوز، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_127-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_127-s1","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"","text":"I say: “What is recited to you” ( mā yutlā ) is coordinated with “God”: God gives the ruling, as does what is recited in the Book. The preposition governing targhabūna an tankiḥūhunna (“you desire to marry them”) has been omitted and can be either fī or ʿan , so that it condemns both wishing to marry an attractive orphan at an unfair dower and declining to marry an unattractive one while obstructing her marriage. “The helpless children” can be coordinated with “orphan girls” in the preceding reference, pointing to “God instructs you concerning your children” (4:11), or to the pronoun in “concerning them.” “That you act justly” can be coordinated with the same object or depend upon an omitted expression meaning “and He commands you to deal justly.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_127-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_127-s2","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"","text":"People ask the Prophet for rulings on women's inheritance and other rights. God commands granting them their rightful shares, already specified earlier in the sūrah, including provisions on the wealth of orphans, marriage of wards and children's inheritance. Guardians must not withhold the dower prescribed for orphan girls and then marry them for less than the dower customarily owing to their peers. If the guardian wishes to marry a beautiful, wealthy orphan, justice requires giving her a suitable dower, otherwise marrying someone else. If he refuses to marry a girl because she is considered unattractive, he may not obstruct her marriage to others in order to inherit her property. In pre-Islamic practice, says Ibn ʿAjība, guardians sought attractive and wealthy orphans without appropriate dowers, while neglecting and obstructing those without beauty or means. Both practices are prohibited. The helpless children too must be given inheritance shares along with adults, although people had formerly withheld inheritance from minors. He transmits that ʿUyayna ibn Ḥiṣn objected to children and women inheriting when custom had rewarded only those who could fight and gather booty; the Prophet replied that this was what he had been commanded. God also addresses the leaders ( al-aʾimma ), commanding them to administer orphans’ affairs with justice, protect their rights and take precautions for them in all their affairs. God knows the good they perform and rewards them accordingly.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_127-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_127-s3","r":"q4_cont_127","title":"","text":"The question can be understood as concerning the “feminine” forms of formal sciences and the “orphan” fruits of the heart, arising from contemplation: divinely granted inward knowledge ( ʿilm ladunnī ) and lordly secrets of the science of reality ( ḥaqīqa ). These are fitting only for those deemed weak among created beings. The saying is cited that the people of Paradise include a weak, despised person whose oath God would fulfil. The response directs the seeker to acquire from formal sciences what is needed to perform worship correctly, to desire the science of the path ( ṭarīqa ) that concerns the heart and establishes servanthood, and to seek from contemplative insights what reveals the Lord's majesty. Justice requires giving the revealed law ( sharīʿa ) its right, the path its right, and guarding the secrets of reality from those unfit to receive them. God does not squander the reward of those who excel.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_127-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_128","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice 4:128","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_128"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-1","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"وَإِنِ امْرَأَةٌ خافَتْ مِنْ بَعْلِها نُشُوزاً أَوْ إِعْراضاً فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما أَنْ يُصْلِحا بَيْنَهُما صُلْحاً وَالصُّلْحُ خَيْرٌ وَأُحْضِرَتِ الْأَنْفُسُ الشُّحَّ وَإِنْ تُحْسِنُوا وَتَتَّقُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيراً (128)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-2","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"قلت: امرأة: فاعل بفعل يُفسره ما بعده، وأصل (يَصَّالِحَا) : يتصالحا، فأدغمت، و (صُلحًا) مصدر. وقرأ الكوفيون: يُصلحا من الرباعي، فتنصب صُلحًا على المفعول به، أو المصدر، و (بينهما) ظرف، أو حال منه، وجملة (الصلح خير) : معترضة، وكذا: وَأُحْضِرَتِ الْأَنْفُسُ الشُّحَّ، ولذلك اغتفر عدم تجانسهما.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-3","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنِ امْرَأَةٌ خافَتْ وتوقعت من زوجها نُشُوزاً أي: ترفعًا عن صحبتها، وتجافيًا عنها، كراهية لها، ومنعًا لحقوقها، أَوْ إِعْراضاً عنها، بأن يترك مجالستها، ومحادثتها، فَلا جُناحَ عَلَيْهِما أن يتصالحا بَيْنَهُما صُلْحاً بأن تحط له من مهرها، أو من قسمها مع ضرتها، أو تهب له شيئًا تستميله به.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-4","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"نزلت في سعد بن الربيع، تزوج على امرأته شابةً، وآثرها عليها. وقيل: في رجل كبرت امرأته، وله معها أولاد، فأراد طلاقها ليتزوج، فقالت له: دعني على أولادي، وأقسم لي في كل شهرين أو أكثر، أو لا تقسم. فذكر ذلك للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم فقال له: «قد سمع الله ما تقول، فإن شاء أجابك» ، فنزلت. وقيل: نزلت في سودة زوج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، لما كبرت، أراد- عليه الصلاة والسلام- أن يُفارقها، فقالت: أمسكني في نسائك ولا تقسم لي، فقد وهبتُ نوبتي لعائشة، فإني أريد أن أُبعث في نسائك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-5","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"ثم رغَّب في الصلح فقال: وَالصُّلْحُ خَيْرٌ من المفارقة، أو من سوء العشرة والخصومة، أو خير في نفسه، ولا يكون إلا مع ترك بعض حق النفس من أحد الخصمين، فلذلك ثقل على النفس فشحت به، وإليه أشار بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-6","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"وَأُحْضِرَتِ الْأَنْفُسُ الشُّحَّ أي: جعلته حاضرًا لديها لا يفارقها، لأنها مطبوعة عليه، فالمرأة لا تكاد تسمح للزوج من حقها، ولا تسخو بشيء تعطيه لزوجها، والزوج لا يكاد يصبر على إمساكها وإحسان عشرتها إذا كَرِهها،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-7","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"وَإِنْ تُحْسِنُوا العشرة وَتَتَّقُوا النشوز والإعراض ونقص حق المرأة مع كراهة الطبع لها، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيراً لا يخفى عليه إحسانكم ولا نشوزكم، فيجازي كُلاًّ بعمله، وفي بعض الأثر: «من صبر على أذى زوجته أعطاه الله ثواب أيوب عليه السلام» . وكذلك المرأة. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-8","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن النفس كالمرأة حين يتزوجها الرجل، فإنها إذا رأت من زوجها الجد في أموره والانقباض عنها، هابته وانقادت لأمره، وإذا رأت منه الليونة والسيولة استخفت بأمره وركبته، وسقطت هيبته من قلبها، فإذا أمرها ونهاها لم تحتفل بأمره، وكذلك النفس إذا رأت من المريد الجد في بدايته والصولة عليها، هابته وانقادت لأمره وكانت له سميعة مطيعة، وإذا رأت منه الرخو والسهولة معها، ركبته وصعب عليه انقيادها وجهادها، فإذا صال عليها وقهرها فأرادت الصلح معه على أن يسامحها في بعض الأمور، وتساعفه فيما يُريد منها، فلا جناح عليهما أن يصالحا بينهما صلحًا، والصلح خير، فإن دوام التشديد قد يفضي إلى الملل، وإن تحسنوا معها بعد معرفتها، وتتقوا الله في سياستها ورياضتها حتى ترد بكم إلى حضرة ربها، فإن الله كان بما تعملون خبيرا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_128-9","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"4:128 · Marital reconciliation and avarice","text":"ثم أمر بالعدل بين النساء، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_128-9"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_128-s1","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"","text":"I say: imraʾa is the subject of an understood verb explained by the verb following. The original form of “reconcile” ( yaṣṣālaḥā ) is yataṣālaḥā , with assimilation; ṣulḥan is a verbal noun. The Kūfan reading yuṣliḥā is the causative fourth form, in which ṣulḥan may be an object or an accusative of action. “Between them” can be adverbial or circumstantial. “Reconciliation is better” and “avarice has been made present to souls” are parenthetic clauses; hence their different formal constructions cause no difficulty.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_128-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_128-s2","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"","text":"A wife may expect nushūz , an aloofness that refuses intimate companionship or neglects her rights because her husband dislikes her, or iʿrāḍ , turning away from her in visits or conversation. They may establish an agreed settlement: for example, she may freely waive part of a dower or a share of alternating nights with another wife, or offer something intended to renew their relationship. Ibn ʿAjība reports several occasions of revelation: Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ is said to have favoured a younger woman he married over an existing wife. Another report concerns an older mother who asked not to be divorced, but to remain with her children and receive an occasional night or none. When this was mentioned to the Prophet, he said, “God has heard what you say; if He wills, He will answer you.” The verse was then revealed, according to the report. A further report concerns Sawda: when she grew old, the Prophet wished to separate from her, but she asked to remain among his wives and, according to the account, gave her allotted turn to ʿĀʾisha, saying that she wished to be raised at the Resurrection among his wives. Reconciliation is better than separation, acrimony or continual hostile cohabitation, and has intrinsic goodness. It can occur only when one of the disputants relinquishes some personal right, which is why the soul finds it burdensome and clings to that right. A wife may not readily surrender claims, and a husband who dislikes her may struggle to maintain kind companionship. God's command nevertheless requires goodness in marital treatment and watchfulness against rejection, neglect and deficient performance of the wife's rights, despite personal aversion. God sees generosity as well as injustice and recompenses accordingly. Ibn ʿAjība also cites an edifying report promising a reward like Job's to one who endures a spouse's hurt. [Translator’s note: the precise attribution of this report has not been verified here.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_128-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_128-s3","r":"q4_cont_128","title":"","text":"Know that the lower soul is like a woman when a man marries her. If she sees her husband earnest in his affairs and reserved toward her, she stands in awe of him and obeys his command. If she sees softness and pliancy in him, she makes light of his command and gains the upper hand over him; awe of him falls from her heart, and she pays no heed to his commands and prohibitions. Likewise, when the lower soul sees the novice’s earnestness at the beginning and his forcefulness toward it, it stands in awe of him and listens and obeys. If it sees laxness and leniency in him, it gains the upper hand, and making it obey and struggling against it become difficult. If, after he has assailed and subdued it, it wants to make peace with him on condition that he indulges it in certain matters and it accommodates him in what he wants from it, there is no blame in their making peace, and peace is better: continued severity may lead to weariness. Once you know it, deal well with it and fear God in managing and training it until it brings you into the Presence of its Lord. [Translator’s note: this paragraph applies a marital analogy to training the lower soul; it does not formulate a legal ruling on marital conduct.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_128-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_129","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation","text":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation 4:129","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_129"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_129-1","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation","text":"وَلَنْ تَسْتَطِيعُوا أَنْ تَعْدِلُوا بَيْنَ النِّساءِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتُمْ فَلا تَمِيلُوا كُلَّ الْمَيْلِ فَتَذَرُوها كَالْمُعَلَّقَةِ وَإِنْ تُصْلِحُوا وَتَتَّقُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً (129)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_129-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_129-2","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَنْ تَسْتَطِيعُوا، يا معشر الأزواج، أَنْ تَعْدِلُوا بَيْنَ النِّساءِ العدل الكامل التام في الأقوال والأفعال والنفقة والكسوة والمحبة، وَلَوْ حَرَصْتُمْ على ذلك لضعف حالكم، وقد خففت عنكم، وأسقطت الحرج عنكم، فلا يجب العدل في البيت فقط، وكان صلّى الله عليه وسلم يَقسِمُ بين نِسَائِه فيعِدلُ ويقُولُ: «اللهمَّ هذه قسمتي فِيمَا أملِك، فلا تُؤاخِذني فيمَا لا أملِكُ» ، يعني: ميل القلب، وكان عمر رضي الله عنه يقول: (اللهم قلبي فلا أملكُه، وأما سوى ذلك فإني أرجو أن أعدل) ، وأما الوطء فلا يجب العدل فيه، إلا أن تتحرك شهوته، فيكف لتتوفر لذته للأخرى.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_129-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_129-3","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation","text":"فَلا تَمِيلُوا إلى المرغوب فيها لجمالها أو شبابها، كُلَّ الْمَيْلِ بالنفقة والكسوة والإقبال عليها، وتَدَعُوا الأخرى كَالْمُعَلَّقَةِ التي ليست ذات بعل ولا مطلقة، كأنها محبوسة مسجونة، وعن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «مَن كانت له أمَرأتانِ يَميلُ معَ إحدَاهما، جَاء يومَ القِيَامَةِ، وأحَدُ شِقّيه مَائِلٌ» ، وَإِنْ تُصْلِحُوا ما كنتم تفسدون في أمورهن بالعدل بينهن، وَتَتَّقُوا الجور فيما يستقبل، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً، يغفر لكم ما مضى من ميلكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_129-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_129-4","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation","text":"الإشارة: من شأن العبودية: الضعف والعجز، فلا يستطيع العبد أن يقوم بالأمور التي كلف بها على العدل والتمام، ولو حرص كل الحرص، وجدَّ كل الجد، فلا يليق به إلا التحقق بوصفه والرجوع إلى ربه، فيأتي بما يستطيع ولا يحرص على مالا يستطيع، فلا يميل إلى الدعة والكسل كل الميل، ولا يحرص على مالا طاقة له به كل الحرص، فإن التعقيد ليس من شأن أهل التوحيد، بل من شأنهم مساعفة الأقدار، والسكون تحت أحكام الواحد القهار، فلا تميلوا إلى التعمق والتشديد كل الميل، فتتركوا أنفسكم كالمُعلَّقة، أي: المسجونة، وهذا من شأن أهل الحجاب، يُحبسون في المقامات والأحوال، تشغلهم حلاوة ذلك عن الله تعالى. فإذا فقدوا ذلك الحال أو المقام سلبوا وأفلسوا. وأهل الغنى بالله لا يقفون مع حال ولا مقام، هم مع مولاهم، وكل ما يبرز من عنصر القدرة قبلوه، وتلونوا بلونه، وهذا مقام التلوين بعد التمكين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_129-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_129-5","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation","text":"وفي إشارة أخرى: اعلم أن القدرة والحكمة كالزوجين للقلب، يقيم عند هذه مدة، وعند هذه أخرى، فإذا أقام عند الحكمة كان في مقام العبودية من جهل وغفلة وضعف وذلة، وإذا أقام عند القدرة كان في مقام شهود الربوبية فيكون في علم ويقظة وقوة وعزة. ولا قدرة له على العدل بينهما، فلا يميل إلى إحداهما كل الميل بل يسير بينهما، ويعطي كل ذي حق حقه، بأن يعرف فضلهما، ويسير بكل واحد منهما. وإن تصلحوا قلوبكم وتتقوا ما يشغلكم عن ربكم، فإن الله كان غفورًا رحيمًا يغفر لكم ميلكم إلى إحدى الجهتين والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_129-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_129-6","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"4:129 · Equity between wives and human limitation","text":"فإذا تعذر الإصلاح بين الزوجين، وأراد الفراق ففى الله الغنى عن كل شيء، كما أشار إلى ذلك بقوله:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_129-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_129-s1","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"","text":"Husbands cannot achieve absolute equality in speech, actions, spending, clothing and inward affection, no matter how they strive, because of the weakness of the human condition. He then says, in the divine first person, “I have lightened [the requirement] for you and removed hardship from you,” followed in the printed text by, “Equality in the house alone is not obligatory.” [Textual note: Cairo I:569 reads فلا يجب العدل في البيت فقط . Besides “house,” bayt can mean spending the night: Lisān al-ʿArab , II:16, lists it among the verbal nouns of bāta . The following account of dividing turns among wives makes that sense plausible here. It does not settle the scope of “not” and “only,” however. Earlier parallels in Ibn Juzayy and al-Bayḍāwī explain the concession for unattainable perfect equality but do not supply this disputed clause.] Ibn ʿAjība cites the reported supplication of the Prophet when distributing his turns among his wives: “O God, this is my division concerning what I control; do not hold me to account for what I do not control,” meaning the heart's leaning. ʿUmar is quoted similarly: the heart is not his to command, but in other affairs he hopes to act justly. Ibn ʿAjība says absolute equality in intercourse is not imposed, though a husband must not deliberately reserve all his sensual energy for one wife to the neglect of another. Do not incline so completely toward a favoured younger or more attractive wife in clothing, maintenance and attention that the other is left “suspended”—not enjoying actual married companionship, yet not divorced and free to form a new household. The Prophet is reported to warn that the man who shows unjust partiality toward one of two wives will appear on the Day of Resurrection with one side inclined. If husbands correct previous unfairness and abstain from injustice in future, God is merciful and forgives what has passed.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_129-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_129-s2","r":"q4_cont_129","title":"capacity and moderation","text":"Weakness and incapacity are among the essential marks of servanthood. However diligent a person becomes, complete perfection in all responsibilities is beyond him. He should recognise his proper condition, return to the Lord and do what is within capacity, without surrendering entirely to laziness or trying to accomplish what he has no power to bear. Excessive self-imposed complication is not the way of the people of divine unity; they consent to decrees and rest beneath the judgment of the irresistible One. Do not incline wholly to spiritual severity, leaving the soul suspended and imprisoned. The veiled can become detained within spiritual stations and states, distracted from God by their sweetness; losing those states then leaves them bereft. Those enriched through God do not stop with any state or station: whatever the divine power unfolds, they receive it and assume its appropriate colour. This is talwīn —responsive change—after tamkīn , spiritual establishment. Another spiritual allusion. Divine power ( qudra ) and wisdom ( ḥikma ) are like two spouses to the heart, which dwells for a time with one and then with the other. With wisdom it is in the station of servanthood, marked by ignorance, heedlessness, weakness and lowliness; with power it witnesses lordship, characterised by knowledge, awakening, strength and dignity. The human being cannot deal equally with the two, yet should not abandon one wholly for the other. Both must be recognised and given their appropriate rights. If you purify your hearts and remain attentive to what distracts from the Lord, He forgives your leaning toward one of the two sides. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_129-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_130","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency 4:130","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_130"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_130-1","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"وَإِنْ يَتَفَرَّقا يُغْنِ اللَّهُ كُلاًّ مِنْ سَعَتِهِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ واسِعاً حَكِيماً (130) وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_130-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_130-2","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنْ يَتَفَرَّقا أي: يفارق كل واحد منهما صاحبه، يُغْنِ اللَّهُ كل واحد منهما عن صاحبه، ببدل أو سُلُو يقوم بأمره من رزق أو غيره، من سعة غناه وكمال قدرته، وَكانَ اللَّهُ واسِعاً بقدرته حَكِيماً أي: متقنًا في أحكامه وأفعاله. ثم بيَّن معنى سعته فقال: وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ أي: كل ما استقر فيهما فهو تحت حكمه ومشيئته، قائمًا بحفظه وتدبيره، يعطي كل واحد ما يقوم بأمره ويغنيه عن غيره. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_130-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_130-3","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الروح ما دامت مسجونة تحت قهر البشرية، محجوبةً عن شهود معاني الربوبية، كانت فقيرة جائعة متعطشة، تتعشق إلى الأكوان وتفتقر إليها، وتقف معها، فإذا فارقت البشرية وانطلقت من سجن هيكلها،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_130-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_130-4","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"وخرجت فكرتها من سجن الأكوان، أغناها الله بشهود ذاته، وأفضت إلى سعة فضاء الشهود والعيان، وملكت جميع الأكوان، «أنت مع الأكوان ما لم تشهد المكون، فإذا شهدت المكون كانت الأكوان معك» ، وكذلك البشرية يغنيها الله عن تعب الخدمة وتستريح في ظل المعرفة، فلما تفرقا أغنى الله كلاًّ من سعة فضله وجوده، لأنه واسع العطاء والجود، حكيم في تدبير إمداد كل موجود.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_130-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_130-6","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"وفي قوله: وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ إشارة إلى أنَّ مَن كان بالله، ووصل إلى شهود ذاته، ملَّكه الله ما في السموات وما في الأرض، فيكون خليفة الله في ملكه، (وما ذلك على الله بعزيز) .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_130-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_130-7","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"ولمّا جرى الكلام على شأن النساء، وهن حبائل الشيطان، تشغل فتنتهن عن ذكر الرحمن، حذَّر الحق تعالى من فتنتهن، كما هو عادته تعالى في كتابه عند ذكرهن، وأمر بالتقوى التي هي حصن من كل فتنة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_130-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_130-8","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"4:130 · Separation and God’s sufficiency","text":"... وَلَقَدْ وَصَّيْنَا الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتابَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَإِيَّاكُمْ أَنِ اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَإِنْ تَكْفُرُوا فَإِنَّ لِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَنِيًّا حَمِيداً (131)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_130-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_130-s1","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"","text":"If husband and wife separate, God will make each independent of the other by another suitable partner, consolation or sustaining provision from His boundless generosity. He is vast in power and precise in every ordinance and deed. The following declaration that everything in the heavens and earth belongs to Him explains the source of that abundance: every creature lives under His will, protection and governance. He gives each whatever is necessary to sustain them and frees them from dependence upon another. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_130-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_130-s2","r":"q4_cont_130","title":"","text":"So long as the spirit remains imprisoned beneath the domination of bodily human nature and veiled from the witnessing of lordship, it remains hungry, thirsty and needy, attaching itself passionately to created objects. When it separates from that tyranny and departs from the prison of bodily form, its reflective faculty leaves the imprisonment of created appearances. God makes it wealthy through the witnessing of His Essence, granting it the ample space of direct vision and presence. It comes to possess all created things. It is said: “You are with created things as long as you do not witness their Creator; once you witness the Creator, created things are with you.” God also frees bodily nature from the fatigue of service, and it rests in the shade of knowledge. Through that separation each receives sufficiency out of God's bounty, for He is boundless in generosity and wise in arranging provision for every existent.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_130-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_131","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness 4:131–133","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_131"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-1","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"وَلِلَّهِ مَا فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلاً (132) إِنْ يَشَأْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ وَيَأْتِ بِآخَرِينَ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلى ذلِكَ قَدِيراً (133)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-2","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"قلت: (من قبلكم) : يتعلق بأوتوا أو بوصينا، و (إياكم) : عطف على الذين، و (أن اتقوا) : على حذف الجار، أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-3","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"بأن اتقوا، أو مفسرة لأن التوصية في معنى القول، و (إن تكفروا) على حذف القول، أي: وقلنا لهم ولكم: وإن تكفروا ... الخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-4","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَلَقَدْ وَصَّيْنَا الأمم المتقدمة الذين أنزلنا عليهم الْكِتابَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ كأهل التوراة والإنجيل والزبور، وغيرهم من الأمم، ووصيناكم أنتم أَنِ اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ بأن تمتثلوا أوامره، وتجتنبوا نواهيَه، ظاهرًا وباطنًا، وقلنا لهم ولكم: وَإِنْ تَكْفُرُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عَنِ كفركم وشكركم فقد استقر له ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ مُلكاً وعبيدًا، فله فيهما من الملائكة من هو أطوع منكم، فلا يتضرر بكفركم، كما لا ينتفع بشكركم وتقواكم، وإنما أوصاكم رحمًة بكم، لا لحاجة إليكم، ثم قرر ذلك بقوله: وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَنِيًّا حَمِيداً أي: غنيًا عن الخلق وعبادتهم، محمودًا في ذاته، حُمِد أو لم يُحمد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-5","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"وَلِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ كرره ثالثًا للدلالة على كونه غنيًا حميدًا، فإن جميع المخلوقات تدل بحاجتها على غناه، وبما أفاض عليها من الوجود، وأنواع الخصائص والكمالات على كونه حميدًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-6","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"قاله البيضاوي. وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلًا أي: حافظًا ومجيرًا لمن تعلق به من أهل السموات والأرض. إِنْ يَشَأْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إن لم تتقوه، ويأت بقوم آخرين، هم أطوع منكم وأتقى، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلى ذلِكَ قَدِيراً أي: بليغ القدرة لا يعجزه مُراد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-7","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"قال البيضاوي: وهذا- أي قوله: (إن يشأ يذهبكم..) - أيضًا تقرير لغناه وقدرته، وتهديد لمن كفر وخالف أمره، وقيل: هو خطاب لمن خالف الرسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم من العرب، وهو معنى قوله: وَإِنْ تَتَوَلَّوْا يَسْتَبْدِلْ قَوْماً غَيْرَكُمْ لما رُوي: أنها لمّا نزلت ضرب رسول صلّى الله عليه وسلم يدَه على ظهر سَلمَان وقال: «إنّهم قَومُ هذا» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-8","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"الإشارة: التقوى أساس الطريق ومنهاج أهل التحقيق، عليها سلك السائرون، وبها وصل الواصلون، قد وصَّى بها الحق تعالى المتقدمين والمتأخرين، وبها قرّب المقربين وشرّف المكرمين. ولها خَمسُ درجاتٍ: أن يتقي العبد الكفر وذلك بمقام الإسلام، وأن يتقي المعاصي والمحرمات وهو: مقام التوبة، وأن يتقي الشبهات وهو مقام الورع، وأن يتقي المباحات، وهو مقام الزهد، وأن يتقي شهود السَّوى والحس وهو مقام المشاهدة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-9","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"ولها فضائل مستنبطة من القرآن، وهي خمس عشرة: الهداية لقوله تعالى: هُدىً لِلْمُتَّقِينَ، والنصرة لقوله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا، والولاية لقوله: وَاللَّهُ وَلِيُّ الْمُتَّقِينَ والمحبة لقوله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِينَ، وتنوير القلب لقوله: يَآ أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تَتَّقُوا اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَكُمْ فُرْقاناً، والمخرج من الغم والرزق من حيث لا يحتسب، لقوله: وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَهُ مَخْرَجاً، وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لا يَحْتَسِبُ، وتيسير الأمور لقوله: وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَهُ مِنْ أَمْرِهِ يُسْراً وغفران الذنوب وإعظام الأجر لقوله: وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يُكَفِّرْ عَنْهُ سَيِّئاتِهِ وَيُعْظِمْ لَهُ أَجْراً، وتقبل الأعمال لقوله: إِنَّما يَتَقَبَّلُ اللَّهُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِينَ والفلاح لقوله: وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ والبشرى لقوله: لَهُمُ الْبُشْرى فِي الْحَياةِ الدُّنْيا وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-10","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"، ودخول الجنة لقوله: إِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنَّاتِ النَّعِيمِ، والنجاة من النار لقوله: ثُمَّ نُنَجِّي الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا. هـ. من ابن جزي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-11","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"ومما ينسب للقطب ابن مشيش رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-12","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"عليكَ بتقوى الله في السرِّ والجهرِ ... ذا شئتَ توفيقَا إلى سُبُلِ الخيرِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-13","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"لأن التُّقى أصلٌ إلى البِرَّ كلَّه ... فخُذه تَفُز بكلِّ نوعٍ من البرّ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-14","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"وخيرُ جميعِ الزاد ما قال ربُّنا فَكُن ... يا أخي للهِ مُمتَثِل الأمر","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_131-15","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"4:131–133 · The imperative of reverent awareness","text":"ولمّا قرر أن الملك كله بيده، رغّب الناس فى رفع حوائجهم إليه، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_131-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_131-s1","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"Abiding through God","text":"Ibn ʿAjība finds an allusion in “To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth”: whoever abides through God and attains the witnessing of His Essence, God gives him dominion over whatever is in the heavens and the earth, and he becomes God’s deputy in His kingdom. “That is not difficult for God.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_131-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_131-s2","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"","text":"After speaking of women, whom he calls “Satan’s snares,” Ibn ʿAjība says that their temptation distracts from remembrance of the All-Merciful. He says that God therefore warns against their temptation, as is His custom in His Book whenever He mentions them. [Translator’s note: this description of women belongs to the historical source’s ascetic rhetoric.] God then commands taqwā , the protection against every trial.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_131-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_131-s3","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"The construction of the instruction","text":"I say: “before you” may attach either to “were given” or to “We instructed”; “and you” is coordinated with “those.” “To fear God” may have an omitted governing preposition, or an may introduce what the instruction consists in. “If you disbelieve” follows an understood “We said to them and to you.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_131-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_131-s4","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"","text":"All preceding communities entrusted with revelation—the communities of Torah, Gospel and Psalms, and others—were instructed, as Muslims are now, to obey God's commands and avoid His prohibitions inwardly and outwardly. They are told that He has no need for either their unbelief or thanksgiving. All heavens and earth and obedient angels already belong to Him. Their denial does not diminish Him and their gratitude does not increase Him: the instruction proceeds from mercy for their welfare, not from divine need. “Self-Sufficient, Praiseworthy” means entirely independent of creation and intrinsically deserving praise, whether anyone praises Him or not. The repetition of the ownership of heavens and earth for a third time, al-Bayḍāwī explains, strengthens both attributes: the neediness of creatures demonstrates His sufficiency, while the existence and particular perfections He bestows disclose why He is praised. As Wakīl , He protects those who entrust themselves to Him. If human beings resist the demand for taqwā , He can replace them with another people more devoted and obedient. Al-Bayḍāwī sees a further proof of God's sufficiency and power and a warning to those who deny His command. One interpretation addresses Arabs opposing the Prophet, alongside “If you turn away, He will replace you with another people” (47:38). Ibn ʿAjība cites the report that the Prophet placed his hand on Salmān's back and said, “These are that man's people.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_131-s4"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_131-s5","r":"q4_cont_131","title":"the degrees of *taqwā*","text":"God-consciousness is the foundation of the path and the method of those who realise the truth. Through it wayfarers travel and people of arrival reach their goal; God enjoined it upon earlier and later communities and by it brought His chosen servants near. It has five degrees: guarding against unbelief, the station of Islam; guarding against prohibited deeds, the station of repentance; guarding against doubtful matters, the station of scrupulousness ( waraʿ ); guarding against permissible things, the station of renunciation ( zuhd ); and guarding against witnessing what is other than God and sensory appearances, the station of witnessing ( mushāhada ). He enumerates fifteen virtues associated with taqwā from Qurʾānic verses (following Ibn Juzayy): guidance (2:2); divine help and victory (16:128); God's protective friendship (45:19); divine love (3:76); illumination and discernment ( furqān , 8:29); an exit from distress and provision from unexpected sources (65:2–3); ease in difficult affairs (65:4); removal of sins and augmentation of reward (65:5); acceptance of good works (5:27); success (5:100); glad tidings in this life and the next (10:64); gardens of bliss (68:34); and salvation from the Fire (19:72). [Translator’s note: the count of fifteen separates the paired effects—relief from distress and unexpected provision, and forgiveness of sins and enlargement of reward—rather than counting the cited verses.] A poem attributed to Ibn Mashīsh is then cited: Hold fast to God-consciousness in secret and in public, if you desire success upon the pathways of the good; reverent care is the root of every act of righteousness, so grasp it and obtain each kind of excellence. The best provision is that which our Lord declared: my brother, therefore, obey God's command. Since all sovereignty belongs to Him, the next verse encourages people to take their needs directly to Him.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_131-s5"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_134","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"4:134 · Reward in this world and the next","text":"4:134 · Reward in this world and the next 4:134","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_134"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_134-1","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"4:134 · Reward in this world and the next","text":"مَنْ كانَ يُرِيدُ ثَوابَ الدُّنْيا فَعِنْدَ اللَّهِ ثَوابُ الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ سَمِيعاً بَصِيراً (134)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_134-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_134-2","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"4:134 · Reward in this world and the next","text":"قلت: (من) : شرطية، وجوابها محذوف دل عليه الكلام، أي: مَن كان يريد ثواب الدنيا فليطلبه منه، فعند الله ثواب الدنيا والآخرة، أو من كان يريد ثواب الدنيا فلا يقتصر عليه خاصة، فعند الله ثواب الدنيا والآخرة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_134-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_134-3","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"4:134 · Reward in this world and the next","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: مَنْ كانَ يُرِيدُ ثَوابَ الدُّنْيا والتوسع فيها، فليطلبه منا فعند الله ثواب الدارين، أو من كان يريد ثواب الدنيا، فليطلب مع ذلك ثوابَ الآخرة أيضًا، وليقل: رَبَّنا آتِنا فِي الدُّنْيا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً فَعِنْدَ اللَّهِ ثَوابُ الدُّنْيا وَالْآخِرَةِ، فيعطيهما معًا لمن طلبهما، والثاني أنهض من الأول، وأكملُ منهما من أعرض عنهما وطلب مولاه، وَكانَ اللَّهُ سَمِيعاً بَصِيراً، لا يخفى عليه مقاصد خلقه، فيعطي كُلاًّ على حسب قصده.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_134-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_134-4","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"4:134 · Reward in this world and the next","text":"الإشارة: الهمم ثلاثة: همة دنية تعلقت بالدنيا الدنية، وهمة متوسطة تعلقت بنعيم الآخرة، وهمة عالية تعلقت بالكبير المتعال. والله تعالى يرزق العبد على قدر همته، وبالهمم ترفع المقادير أو تسقط، فمن كانت همته دنية كان دَنيًا خسيسًا، ومن كانت همته متوسطة كان قدره متوسطًا، رحل من كون إلى كون، كحمار الرحا، يسير، والذي ارتحل منه هو الذي عاد إليه، ومن كانت همته عالية كان عالي المقدار، كبير الشأن، حاز الكونين بما فيهما، وزاد مشاهدة خالقهما. جعلنا الله منهم بمنِّه وكرمه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_134-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_134-5","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"4:134 · Reward in this world and the next","text":"ولما أمر بالعدل بين النساء أمر بالعدل فى الأحكام كلها، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_134-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_134-s1","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"","text":"I say: man is conditional, with its answer omitted but made clear by what follows: whoever desires worldly reward should ask for it from God, since He possesses both worlds; or one seeking worldly recompense should not confine the aspiration to that alone, since the reward of both worlds is with God. A person who desires worldly ease should seek it from God, or better should also seek the hereafter, praying “Our Lord, grant us good in the world and good in the hereafter” (2:201). God gives both together to whoever seeks them. The second understanding is more uplifting than the first. More complete than either is the person who turns away from both and seeks the Lord Himself. God hears and sees the intentions of creatures and bestows what accords with their purposes.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_134-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_134-s2","r":"q4_cont_134","title":"","text":"Aspirations ( himam ) are three: lowly aspiration attached to the lower world; middle aspiration seeking the delights of the hereafter; and high aspiration directed to the Most High. God provides to a servant in proportion to the scope of aspiration, and through aspiration stations rise or fall. Whoever desires the lowest is correspondingly low in rank. The middle aspirant passes from one created condition to another, like a mill-donkey turning around its wheel and arriving again at the same place. A person of lofty aspiration rises high, attains what both worlds contain, and in addition receives vision of their Creator. May God make us among them through bounty and generosity. The commentary next extends the demand for justice from marriage to all judgments.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_134-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_135","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice 4:135","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_135"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-1","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُونُوا قَوَّامِينَ بِالْقِسْطِ شُهَداءَ لِلَّهِ وَلَوْ عَلى أَنْفُسِكُمْ أَوِ الْوالِدَيْنِ وَالْأَقْرَبِينَ إِنْ يَكُنْ غَنِيًّا أَوْ فَقِيراً فَاللَّهُ أَوْلى بِهِما فَلا تَتَّبِعُوا الْهَوى أَنْ تَعْدِلُوا وَإِنْ تَلْوُوا أَوْ تُعْرِضُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيراً (135)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-2","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"قلت: (شهداء) : خبر ثان لكان، أو حال، (فالله أولى) : علة للجواب أي: إن يكن المشهود عليه غنيًا عليه فلا تمتنعوا من الشهادة عليه تعظيمًا له، وإن يكن فقيرًا فلا تمتنعوا من الشهادة عليه إشفاقًا عليه، فإن الله أولى بالغني والفقير منكم، والضمير في (بهما) راجع إلى مادل عليه المذكور، وهو جنسا الغني والفقير، لا إليه وإلا لوحّد لأن «أو» لأحد الشيئين. و (أن تعدلوا) : مفعول من أجله، ومن قرأ: تلوا- بضم اللام- فقد نقل ضم الواو إلى اللام وحذف أحد الواوين، وقيل: من الولاية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-3","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُونُوا قَوَّامِينَ بِالْقِسْطِ أي: مجتهدين في إقامة العدل مواظبين على الحكم به، وكونوا شُهَداءَ لِلَّهِ بالحق تقيمون شهادتكم لوجه الله، وابتغاء مرضاته، بلا طمع أجر ولا عوض، وهذا إن تعينت عليه، ولم يكن في تحملها مشقة، وإلا أُبيح له أجر تعبه، فأدوا شهاداتكم وَلَوْ كانت عَلى أَنْفُسِكُمْ بأن تقروا بالحق الذي عليها، لأن الشهادة بيان الحق، سواء كان عليها أو على غيرها، أَوِ كانت الشهادة على الْوالِدَيْنِ وَالْأَقْرَبِينَ، فلا تمنعكم الشفقة والتعظيم من إقامة الشهادة عليهما، وأحرى غيرهما من الأجانب، إِنْ يَكُنْ المشهود عليه غَنِيًّا أَوْ فَقِيراً فلا تميلوا عن الشهادة بالحق عليهما، تعظيمًا للغني أو شفقة للفقير، فإن الله أَوْلى بِهِما وبالنظر لهما، فلو لم تكن الشهادة عليهما صلاحًا لهما ما شرعها، فَلا تَتَّبِعُوا الْهَوى فتميلوا مع الغني أو الفقير، فقد نهيتكم إرادة أَنْ تَعْدِلُوا في أحكامكم، فتكونوا عدولاً، أو كراهية أن تعدلوا عن الحق أي: تميلوا، وَإِنْ تَلْوُوا ألسنتكم عن شهادة الحق أو حكومة العدل أَوْ تُعْرِضُوا عن أدائها فتكتموها فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ بِما تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيراً، فيجازي الكاتم والمؤدي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-4","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"قال صلّى الله عليه وسلم عند نزولها: «مَن كانَ يؤمن بالله واليوم الآخر فليُقِم شهادتَه على من كانت، ومن كان يؤمن بالله واليوم الآخر، فلا يَجحَد حَقًا هو عليه، وليؤُده عَفوّا، ولا يلجئه إلى السُلطان وخصوُمتِه، ليقتطع بها حقه، وأيما رجل خَاصَمَ إليَّ فقضَيتُ له على أخِيِه بحقٍ ليس له عليه، فلا يأخُذُه، فإنَما أقَطَعُ له قطعةً مِنَ النَارِ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-5","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"الإشارة: قد أمر الحق تعالى عباده بإقامة العدل في الأمور كلها، ونهى عن مراقبة الخلق في الأشياء كلها، فيتأكد على المريد ألاَّ يراقب أحدًا من الخلق وإنما يراقب الملك الحق، فيكون قويًا في الحق، يقيمه على نفسه وغيره، فلا تجتمع مراقبة الحق مع مراقبة الخلق، من راقب الحق غاب عن الناس، ومن راقب الناس غاب عن الحق، وعاش مغمومًا من الخلق، ولله در القائل حيث قال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-6","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"من رَاقَبَ الناسَ مات غما ... وفاز باللذات الجَسُور","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-7","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"وكان شيخ شيخنا رضي الله عنه يقول: (مراقبةُ الخلقِ عند أهل الظاهر شيءٌ كبير، وعدم المراقبة عند الباطن أمر كبير) . فإقامة العدل على النفس ألاَّ يتركها تميل إلى الرخص والتأويلات، وإقامته على الوالدين تذكيرهما بالله ودلالتهما على الله بلطف ولين، وإقامته على الأقربين بنصحهم وإرشادهم إلى ما فيه صلاحهم، كانوا أغنياء أو فقراء، وإقامته على الأجانب كذلك. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_135-8","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"4:135 · Testimony, impartiality, and justice","text":"ولما فرغ مما يتعلق بحفظ اللسان، تكلم على حفظ الإيمان، وهو الأمر السادس مما تضمنته السورة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_135-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_135-s1","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"","text":"I say: shuhadāʾ may be a second predicate of “be” or a circumstantial expression. “God has a greater claim” supplies the reason: do not avoid testimony against the wealthy out of reverence or the poor out of pity, for God is more concerned for each than you are. The dual pronoun in “both” refers to the two classes of rich and poor, not simply to a singular person connected by “or,” which would require a singular pronoun. “That you act justly” is an expression of purpose, understood either as desire for justice or as aversion to deviating from the truth. The reading talū , with a ḍamma on the lām , is explained by transferring the wāw ’s ḍamma to the lām and deleting one of the two wāw s; alternatively it derives from wilāya , exercising a governing charge.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_135-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_135-s2","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"","text":"God commands persistence and strenuous commitment to equitable judgment. Witnesses are to give truthful testimony for God's pleasure, not for a gift or material return. This applies when giving the testimony is incumbent on that particular person and undertaking it causes no hardship; otherwise, compensation for his trouble is permitted. Even against themselves they must acknowledge debts or other facts, since testimony communicates the truth whether the fact favours the speaker or not. Filial respect and compassion must not prevent evidence against parents or relatives; still less should deference to strangers. Wealth must not awe the witness, and poverty must not lead to the suppression of truth through indulgent pity. God knows what benefits each and has instituted lawful testimony for their welfare. Do not follow passion by favouring either party. Twisting the tongue to deform testimony or turning away and suppressing it is known to God, who recompenses both the witness and the concealer. Ibn ʿAjība reports that, when this verse was revealed, the Prophet said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him give his testimony against whomever it concerns. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day must not deny a right owed by him; let him discharge it willingly, without forcing the claimant to appeal to the ruler and contest the matter in order to recover his right. Any man who brings a case before me, and for whom I award a right against his brother that is not owed to him, must not take it: I am only allotting him a piece of Fire.” [Translator’s note: the final warning resembles the well-attested tradition concerning a judgment that awards another person’s right and thereby gives the recipient a piece of Fire; the combined wording as quoted warrants separate authentication.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_135-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_135-s3","r":"q4_cont_135","title":"","text":"Justice must be upheld in every matter, and concern for human approval must be abandoned. The seeker should watch the Real Sovereign rather than make people his audience, exercising firmness in truth against himself and others. Vigilance toward the Real does not coexist with vigilance toward created beings. Whoever watches the Real becomes absent from preoccupation with people; whoever watches people becomes absent from God and lives distressed by their opinions. The poet says: The watcher of people's judgments dies of grief; the courageous one wins the joys of life. Ibn ʿAjība reports his grand-shaykh’s aphorism: “Vigilance toward created beings is a great matter for the people of the outward; absence of that vigilance is a great matter for the people of the inward.” Justice toward the self means not allowing it to incline toward concessions and interpretations; toward parents it means gentle remembrance and guidance to God; toward kin and strangers it means sincere advice for their true welfare, whether they are wealthy or poor. God gives success. With this treatment of the tongue complete, the next topic is safeguarding faith, the sixth theme contained in the sūrah.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_135-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_136","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures 4:136","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_136"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_136-1","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا آمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَالْكِتابِ الَّذِي نَزَّلَ عَلى رَسُولِهِ وَالْكِتابِ الَّذِي أَنْزَلَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلالاً بَعِيداً (136)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_136-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_136-2","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: مخاطبًا من أسلم من اليهود- وهو عبد الله بن سَلاَم وأسَد وأسيد ابنا كَعبٍ، وثَعلبة بن قَيسٍ، وسلّام بن أخت عبد الله بن سلام، وسلمة ابن أخيه ويامين- قالوا يا رسول الله، نؤمن بك وبكتابك وبموسى والتوراة وعُزَّير، ونكفُرُ بما سِوَاهُ من الكُتب؟ فقال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: «آمِنُوا بالله ورسوله محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم وبكتابه القرآن، وبكل كتاب قبله» ، فَنزلت الآية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_136-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_136-3","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"فقال لهم جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بمحمد، بعد أن آمنوا بموسى آمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَالْكِتابِ الَّذِي نَزَّلَ عَلى رَسُولِهِ القرآن وَالْكِتابِ الَّذِي أَنْزَلَ مِنْ قَبْلُ أي: جنس الكتاب، فتدخل الكتب المتقدمة كلها، وَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِاللَّهِ وَمَلائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ أي: ومن يكفر بشيء من ذلك فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلالًا بَعِيداً أي: أخطأ خطًأ بعيدًا لا يكاد يعود إلى الطريق، فلما نزلت قالوا: يا رسول الله إنا نؤمن بالجميع، ولا نفرق بين أحد منهم، كما فرقت اليهود والنصارى.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_136-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_136-4","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"وقيل: الخطاب للمنافقين، أي: يا أيها الذين آمنوا بألسنتهم آمِنُوا بقلوبكم، كما آمنتم بألسنتكم، وقيل: للمؤمنين، أي: دُوموا على إيمانكم، وأثبتوا عليه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_136-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_136-5","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"الإشارة: أمر الحق جل جلاله، أهل الإيمان أن يجددوا إيمانهم، فيثبتوا على ما هو حاصل، ويسترشدوا إلى ما ليس بحاصل، فإن أنوار الإيمان تتزايد وتترادف على القلوب بحسب التصفية والنظر، وبقدر الطاعة والتقرب، فلا يزال العبد يتقرب إلى الله، وأنوار التوجه تتوارد عليه، حتى تشرق عليه أنوار المواجهة وهي أنوار الشهود، فشروق الأنوار على قدر صفاء الأسرار، وورود الإمداد على حسب الاستعداد، فبقدر التفرغ من الأغيار ترد على","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_136-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_136-6","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"القلوب المواهب والأسرار، وهذا كله لمن صحب العارفين وأخذ عنهم، وملّك زمام نفسه لهم، وإلا فحَسبُه الإيمان بالغيب، ولو عمل ما عمل، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_136-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_136-7","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"4:136 · Belief and revealed scriptures","text":"ثم ذكر وعيد مَن ارتد عن الإيمان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_136-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_136-s1","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"","text":"Ibn ʿAjība reports an occasion involving certain Jews who embraced Islam, naming ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām, Asad and Usayd sons of Kaʿb, Thaʿlaba ibn Qays, Sallām, the son of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām’s sister, Salama, the son of his brother, and Yāmīn. They professed belief in Muḥammad, the Qurʾān, Moses, Torah and Ezra, but asked whether they could reject the remaining revealed books. The Prophet, according to the account, commanded them to believe in God, Muḥammad, the Qurʾān and all scriptures revealed before it. The verse then instructed those who had accepted Muḥammad after Moses to affirm the entire genus of revealed scripture without dividing God's messengers into accepted and rejected. The report says they affirmed belief in all without distinction, unlike those Jews and Christians who divided the prophetic succession. Another explanation addresses hypocrites: you have professed belief with your tongues; now believe sincerely in your hearts. A further interpretation speaks to believers themselves: continue steadfastly in the faith already received. Whoever rejects any of these has gone so far astray that he scarcely returns to the path.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_136-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_136-s2","r":"q4_cont_136","title":"","text":"The call to believe commands the renewal and deepening of faith. Maintain what you already possess and seek instruction in what has not yet been realised. The lights of faith increase in succession upon hearts in proportion to their purification, contemplation, obedience and approach to God. As the servant draws nearer, the lights of tawajjuh (turning toward God) arrive until the lights of muwājaha (direct encounter), the lights of witnessing, shine forth. The appearance of lights corresponds to purification of inward secrets; spiritual aid ( imdād ) descends according to readiness ( istiʿdād ). As attention withdraws from what is other than God, gifts and mysteries are bestowed upon the heart. All of this belongs to one who accompanies the knowers, learns from them and places the reins of his soul in their hands; otherwise he must content himself with faith in the unseen, whatever deeds he performs. God gives success.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_136-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_137","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy 4:137–139","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_137"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_137-1","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا ثُمَّ آمَنُوا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا ثُمَّ ازْدادُوا كُفْراً لَمْ يَكُنِ اللَّهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ سَبِيلاً (137) بَشِّرِ الْمُنافِقِينَ بِأَنَّ لَهُمْ عَذاباً أَلِيماً (138) الَّذِينَ يَتَّخِذُونَ الْكافِرِينَ أَوْلِياءَ مِنْ دُونِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَيَبْتَغُونَ عِنْدَهُمُ الْعِزَّةَ فَإِنَّ الْعِزَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعاً (139)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_137-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_137-2","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا ثم تكرر منهم الإيمان والكفر، ثم أصروا على الكفر وهم المنافقون، لَمْ يَكُنِ اللَّهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ لمَا سبق لهم من الشقاء، أو إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بموسى ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا بعبادة العجل ثُمَّ آمَنُوا حين تابوا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا بعيسى ثُمَّ ازْدادُوا كُفْراً بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، لَمْ يَكُنِ اللَّهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ، وهم اليهود، والأول أظهر لأن الكلام بعده في المنافقين، فقال تعالى في شأنهم: لَمْ يَكُنِ اللَّهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ سَبِيلًا أي: طريقاً توصلهم إلى الحق، إذ يُستبعد منهم أن يتوبوا، فإن قلوبهم أشربت الكفر، وبصائرهم عميت، لا ينفع علاجها، لا أنهم لو أخلصوا الإيمان لم ينفعهم، وقد يكون إضلالهم عقابًا لسوء أفعالهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_137-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_137-3","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"ثم ذكر وعيدهم فقال: بَشِّرِ الْمُنافِقِينَ بِأَنَّ لَهُمْ عَذاباً أَلِيماً. وهم الَّذِينَ يَتَّخِذُونَ الْكافِرِينَ أَوْلِياءَ أي: أحبابًا وأصدقاء مِنْ دُونِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، وقد كان الكفار قبل ظهور الإسلام لهم الصولة والجاه، فطلب المنافقون أن ينالوا بولايتهم ومصادقتهم العزّ منهم، فردَّ الله عليهم بقوله: أَيَبْتَغُونَ عِنْدَهُمُ الْعِزَّةَ بولايتهم؟ فَإِنَّ الْعِزَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعاً ولرسوله ولأوليائه، ولا عزة لغيره إذ لا يعبأ بعزة لا تدوم ويعقبها الذل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_137-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_137-4","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"الإشارة: من كان ضعيفَ الاعتقاد في أهل الخصوصية، ضعيفَ التصديق، تراه تارة يدخل وتارة يخرج، وتارة يصدق وتارة ينكر، لا يُرجى فلاحُه في طريق الخصوص، فإن ضم إلى ذلك صحبة أهل الإنكار وولايتهم، فبشره بالخيبة والخسران، فإن تعزز بعزهم أعقبه الذل والهوان، والعياذ بالله من الخذلان، فالعز إنما يكون بعز التوحيد والإيمان، وعزة المعرفة والإحسان، وبصحبة أهل العرفان، الذين تعززوا بعز الرحمن، فمن تعزز بعز يفنى مات عزه، ومن تعزز بعز يبقى دام عزه، والشبكة التي يصطاد بها العزّ هو الذل لله، يظهره بين عباد الله. قال بعضهم: والله ما رأيتُ العزّ إلاَّ في الذل. وقال الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_137-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_137-5","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"تذلَّلْ لمَن تَهْوَى لِتَكْسِبَ عِزةً ... فكم عزةٍ قد نالها المرء بالذّلّ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_137-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_137-6","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_137-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_137-7","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"4:137–139 · Repeated disbelief and hypocrisy","text":"ثم نهى عن صحبة أهل الخوض، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_137-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_137-s1","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"","text":"One reading concerns hypocrites who alternate profession of faith and unbelief, eventually persisting in denial. God will not forgive them because wretchedness has already been allotted to them. Another interpretation concerns Jews: they believed in Moses, disbelieved through worship of the calf, repented and believed again, rejected Jesus, and increased unbelief by rejecting Muḥammad. Ibn ʿAjība prefers the first in view of the verses about hypocrisy that follow. The denial of forgiveness and guidance is explained by how unlikely their repentance is: their hearts are imbued with unbelief and their inner sight is blind, beyond treatment. It does not mean that sincere faith, were they to embrace it, would not benefit them. God’s leading them astray may also be a punishment for their evil deeds. The hypocrites sought intimate protection from unbelievers rather than believers because, before the visible rise of Islam, those unbelievers held power and prestige. The hope was to acquire dignity by association. God rebukes such dependence: all lasting dignity belongs to Him, His Messenger and those attached to Him. Dignity that ends in humiliation is unworthy of the name.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_137-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_137-s2","r":"q4_cont_137","title":"","text":"One whose confidence in the people of special spiritual knowledge is weak alternates between entering their company and leaving, believing them one moment and denying them the next. Success for such a person in the special path is not to be hoped for. Joining those who reject its people makes the failure worse. If a person borrows prestige from opponents of the friends of God, abasement follows. Dignity comes from divine unity, faith, inward recognition and excellence, and companionship of knowers honoured by the Merciful. Borrowed dignity dies when its source perishes; divine dignity endures. The net with which honour is caught is humility before God, displayed among God’s servants. One person said, “By God, I have only seen honour in abasement.” A poet says: Humble yourself before the one you love and acquire honour; how much dignity has one obtained by humble surrender!","anchor":"en-q4_cont_137-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_140","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps 4:140–141","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_140"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-1","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"وَقَدْ نَزَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِي الْكِتابِ أَنْ إِذا سَمِعْتُمْ آياتِ اللَّهِ يُكْفَرُ بِها وَيُسْتَهْزَأُ بِها فَلا تَقْعُدُوا مَعَهُمْ حَتَّى يَخُوضُوا فِي حَدِيثٍ غَيْرِهِ إِنَّكُمْ إِذاً مِثْلُهُمْ ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-2","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"قلت: (أن) مخففة: نافية، فاعل نزّل، و (يكفر) و (يُستهزأ) ، حالان من الآيات، وضمير (معهم) : يعود على الكفار المفهوم من (يكفر) ، وضمير (غيره) يعود على الكفر والاستهزاء، وهما شيء واحد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-3","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في التحذير من مجالسة أهل الكفر والمعاصي: وَقَدْ نَزَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ يا معشر المسلمين في القرآن في سورة الأنعام، أنه إِذا سَمِعْتُمْ آياتِ اللَّهِ حال كونها يُكْفَرُ بِها، وَيُسْتَهْزَأُ بِها، فَلا تَقْعُدُوا مَعَهُمْ بل قوموا عنهم، إن لم تقدروا أن تنكروا عليهم، والآية التي في سورة الأنعام قوله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-4","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"وَإِذا رَأَيْتَ الَّذِينَ يَخُوضُونَ فِي آياتِنا فَأَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ حَتَّى يَخُوضُوا فِي حَدِيثٍ غَيْرِهِ الآية. فما داموا في الخوض فاعرضوا عنهم حتى يخوضوا في حديث غير الخوض، فإن جلستم معهم في حال الخوض فإنكم إِذاً مِثْلُهُمْ في الإثم، إن لم ترضوا، أو في الكفر، إن رضيتم بخوضهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-5","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"نزلت في قوم من المنافقين كانوا يجلسون إلى أحبار اليهود، فيسخرون من القرآن، ويكذبون به ويحرفونه، فنهى المسلمين عن مجالستهم، قال ابن عباس: ودخل في هذه الآية كُلُّ مُحدِث في الدين ومُبتدعٍ إلى يوم القيامة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-6","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"الإشارة: أولياء الله آيات من آيات الله: فمن استهزأ بهم فقد استوجب المقت من الله، وكل موطن يقع فيه الإنكار عليهم أو الغض من مرتبتهم، يجب الفرار منه، لأنه موطن الغضب ومحل الهلاك والعَطب، فإن لحوم الأولياء سموم قاتلة، واللعنة على من يقع فيهم حاصلة، فمن جلس مع أهل الخوض من غير عذر، كان من الخائضين، ومن فرّ منهم كان من الناجين، ومن أنكر على من يقع فيهم كان من المجاهدين. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-7","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"ثم ذكر وعيد الخائضين ومن رضي بخوضهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-8","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"... إِنَّ اللَّهَ جامِعُ الْمُنافِقِينَ وَالْكافِرِينَ فِي جَهَنَّمَ جَمِيعاً (140) الَّذِينَ يَتَرَبَّصُونَ بِكُمْ فَإِنْ كانَ لَكُمْ فَتْحٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ قالُوا أَلَمْ نَكُنْ مَعَكُمْ وَإِنْ كانَ لِلْكافِرِينَ نَصِيبٌ قالُوا أَلَمْ نَسْتَحْوِذْ عَلَيْكُمْ وَنَمْنَعْكُمْ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ فَاللَّهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ وَلَنْ يَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ لِلْكافِرِينَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ سَبِيلاً (141)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-9","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"قلت: (الذين) : صفة المنافقين، أو نصب على الذم، و (نستحوذ) : نغلب، استحوذ: غلب، جاء على أصله، ولم يُعلّ كاستعاذ والقياس: استحاذ، يستحيذ، كاستعاذ يستعيذ، لكنه صحح تنبيهًا على الأصل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-10","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ سيجمع الْمُنافِقِينَ وَالْكافِرِينَ، أي: الخائضين والقاعدين معهم، فِي جَهَنَّمَ جَمِيعاً خالدين فيها. الَّذِينَ يَتَرَبَّصُونَ بِكُمْ أي: ينتظرون بكم الدوائر، أي: ما يدور به الزمان والدهر عليكم، وهم المنافقون، فَإِنْ كانَ لَكُمْ فَتْحٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ كالنصر والغنيمة قالُوا للمؤمنين: أَلَمْ نَكُنْ مَعَكُمْ على دينكم، فأعطونا مما غنمتم، وَإِنْ كانَ لِلْكافِرِينَ نَصِيبٌ دولة أو ظهور على المسلمين، قالُوا لهم: أَلَمْ نَسْتَحْوِذْ عَلَيْكُمْ أي: نغلبكم ونتمكن من قتلكم، وأبقينا عليكم فمنعناكم من قتل المسلمين لكم، بأن خذلناهم بتخييل ما ضعُفت به عزيمتهم عليكم، وتوانينا في مظاهرتهم عليكم، فأشركُونا مما أصبتم. وإنما سمي ظفر المسلمين فتحًا، وظفر الكافرين نصيبًا لخسة حظه، فإنه حظ دنياوي، استدراجًا ومكرًا، بخلاف ظفر المسلمين، فإنه إظهار الدين، وإعانة بالغنيمة للمسلمين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-11","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"فَاللَّهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ فيدخل أهل الحق الجنة، ويدخل أهل الخوض النار، وَلَنْ يَجْعَلَ اللَّهُ لِلْكافِرِينَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ سَبِيلًا أي: حجة، أو غلبة في الدنيا والآخرة، وفيه دليل على عدم صحة ملك الكافر للمسلم، فيباع عليه إن اشتراه، ويفسخ نكاحه إن تزوج مسلمة. والله تعالى أعلم الإشارة: (المرء مع مَن أحب) من أحب قوما حشر معهم، فمن أحب أهل الخوض حُشر مع الخائضين، ومن أحب أهل الصفا حشر مع المخلصين، وإن كان مذبذبًا يميل مع كل ريح حشر مع المخلطين، وهو من خف عقله وضعف يقينه، إن رأى بأهل النسبة من الفقراء عزًا ونصرًا وفتحًا انحاز إليهم، وقال: ألم نكن معكم، وإن رأى لأهل الإنكار من العوام صولة وغلبة رجع إليهم، وقال: ألم نستحوذ عليكم ونمنعكم من دعاء الصالحين عليكم، فما لهذا عند الله من خلاق. وفي الحديث: «ذو الوجهين لا يكون عند الله وجيهًا» . فالله يحكم بينهم يوم القيامة، فيرفع أهل الصفا مع المقربين، ويسقط أهل الخوض مع الخائضين، وليس لأهل الخوض من أهل الإنكار سبيل ولا حجة على أهل الصفا من الأبرار، إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا وَالَّذِينَ هُمْ مُحْسِنُونَ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_140-12","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"4:140–141 · The company one keeps","text":"ثم ذكر أحوالهم الشنيعة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_140-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_140-s1","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"","text":"I say: an is “lightened”; Cairo then prints the difficult words نافية، فاعل نزل , literally “negative; the subject of نزل .” [Translator’s textual note: The heading reads active nazzala , “He has revealed,” while the gloss is inconsistent as printed. Al-Bayḍāwī on 4:140 explicitly distinguishes ʿĀṣim’s active reading from the others’ passive reading, calls an lightened, and makes its clause stand as the passive subject. That documented analysis explains the proposed conjecture نائبة فاعل , “standing as the passive subject.” It does not establish that these were Ibn ʿAjība’s own words: Cairo prints neither that phrase nor a passive verb in the heading. Both difficulties remain disclosed; the text is not recast as an analysis of explanatory an . See source check XII-S063.] The verbal expressions “denied” and “mocked” describe the circumstances of the divine verses. The pronoun “them” refers to those who deny, implied by the passive verb; “other than it” refers to the combined activity of disbelief and mockery. Later “those who wait” is an adjective describing hypocrites or is accusative as an expression of censure. Nastaḥwidh means “we gain mastery,” retaining an older verbal form whose consonantal pattern did not undergo the expected phonological alteration, as istaʿādha normally does.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_140-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_140-s2","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"","text":"Muslims had already been instructed in al-Anʿām (6:68) to turn aside from people indulging in the derision of divine signs. If unable to denounce it, they should leave the conversation until it changes. If you sit with them while they engage in that talk, you are like them in sin if you do not approve of it, or in unbelief if you do approve of it. The verse is said to concern hypocrites who sat with Jewish scholars mocking and distorting the Qurʾān. Ibn ʿAbbās says that this verse includes everyone who introduces a novelty in religion and every innovator until the Day of Resurrection. God will gather those who engage in derisive talk and those who sit with them together in Hell, where they will abide. Hypocrites, meanwhile, wait for reversals in Muslim fortunes. If believers gain victory and spoils, they demand a share on the ground of their professed membership. If opponents gain ground, they claim to have spared them, weakened the Muslims' resolve through deception, and were slow to support the believers against them, and demand reward from the other side. The text calls Muslim success a fatḥ , an opening, but unbelievers' momentary success only a naṣīb , a worldly portion: Ibn ʿAjība treats the former as the strengthening of true religion and the latter as a paltry worldly share, involving gradual enticement to ruin and a stratagem. Ultimately God decides the dispute, admitting the people of truth into the Garden and the deliberate mockers into punishment. He interprets “no way” as no proof or dominance in this world or the next and additionally deduces historical juristic rules forbidding non-Muslim ownership of a Muslim slave and requiring the sale of such a slave if acquired, as well as dissolving his marriage if he marries a Muslim woman. [Translator’s note: these are juristic deductions recorded in this historical commentary.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_140-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_140-s3","r":"q4_cont_140","title":"","text":"God's saints are among His signs. In Ibn ʿAjība’s spiritual application, anyone who derides them has made himself deserving of God’s abhorrence. It is obligatory to flee any place where they are repudiated or their rank is disparaged, for it is a place of wrath, destruction and ruin. He says, “The flesh of the saints is a deadly poison, and the curse falls upon those who disparage them.” Remaining without excuse makes one a participant; departing protects one; speaking against the slander is a kind of struggle. “A person is with those whom he loves”: love of contentious mockers joins them, love of the pure joins the sincere, and opportunistic vacillation attaches one to confused companions. Such a weakly grounded person joins Sufi poor ( fuqarāʾ ) when their recognition brings influence and falls back among their deniers when the latter hold power. Such a person has no share with God. The hadith says, “A two-faced man is not esteemed before God.” God raises the people of purity with those brought near, and brings the mockers to the consequences of their acts. Those denying the people of purity have no genuine argument against them. “God is with those who are reverently mindful and excel” (16:128).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_140-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_142","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance 4:142–143","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_142"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-1","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"إِنَّ الْمُنافِقِينَ يُخادِعُونَ اللَّهَ وَهُوَ خادِعُهُمْ وَإِذا قامُوا إِلَى الصَّلاةِ قامُوا كُسالى يُراؤُنَ النَّاسَ وَلا يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ إِلاَّ قَلِيلاً (142) مُذَبْذَبِينَ بَيْنَ ذلِكَ لآَ إِلى هؤُلاءِ وَلا إِلى هؤُلاءِ وَمَنْ يُضْلِلِ اللَّهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُ سَبِيلاً (143)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-2","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"قلت: جملة: (ولا يذكرون الله) حال من واو (يُراءون) ، وكذلك (مذبذبين) أي: يراءون حال كونهم غير ذاكرين مذبذبين، أو منصوب على الذم، والمذبذب: المضطرب المتردد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-3","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الْمُنافِقِينَ يُخادِعُونَ اللَّهَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-4","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"بإظهار الإيمان وإخفاء الكفر، وَهُوَ خادِعُهُمْ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-5","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"، أي: مجازيهم على خداعهم بأن يظهر لهم يوم القيامة نورًا يمشون به على الصراط، كما يعطي المؤمنين، فإذا مضوا به طفئ نورهم وبقي نور المؤمنين، فينادونهم: انْظُرُونا نَقْتَبِسْ مِنْ نُورِكُمْ قِيلَ ارْجِعُوا وَراءَكُمْ فَالْتَمِسُوا نُوراً، فيتهافتون في النار. فسمي هذه العقوبة خداعًا تسمية للعقوبة باسم الذنب.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-6","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"وكانوا إِذا قامُوا إِلَى الصَّلاةِ قامُوا كُسالى","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-7","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"أي: متثاقلين، لا يريدون بها وجه الله، فإن رءاهم أحد، صلوا، وإلاَّ انصرفوا، فلم يصلوا، يُراؤُنَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-8","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"بأعمالهم النَّاسَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-9","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"أي: المؤمنين، وَلا يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-10","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"لأن المرائى لا يذكر إلا بحضرة الناس، وهو أقل أحواله، أو لا يذكرونه في صلاتهم إلا قليلاً، لأنهم لا يذكرون إلا التكبير والتسليم، وقال ابن عباس: إنما ذلك لأنهم يفعلونها رياءً وسمعةً، ولو أرادوا بذلك وجه الله تعالى لكان كثيرًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-11","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"وقال قتادة: إنما قل ذكرهم، لأنه لم يُقبل، فكل ما رُدَّ من العمل فهو قليل، وكل ما قُبل فهو كثير.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-12","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"وكانوا أيضًا مُذَبْذَبِينَ أي: مترددين ومتحيرين بين الكفر والإيمان، لا إِلى هؤُلاءِ وَلا إِلى هؤُلاءِ أي: لا صائرين إلى المؤمنين ولا إلى الكافرين. قال قتادة: ما هم بمؤمنين مخلصين، ولا مشركين مُصَرِّحين بالشرك، هكذا سبق في علم الله، وَمَنْ يُضْلِلِ اللَّهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُ سَبِيلًا أي: طريقًا إلى الهدى، ومثله قوله تعالى: وَمَنْ لَمْ يَجْعَلِ اللَّهُ لَهُ نُوراً فَما لَهُ مِنْ نُورٍ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-13","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"الإشارة: كل من أحب أن يَرى الناسُ محاسنَ أعماله وأحواله، ففيه شعبة من النفاق وشعبة من الرياء، وعلامة المرائي: تزيين ظاهره وتخريب باطنه، يتزين للناس بحسن أعماله وأحواله، يراقب الناس ولا يراقب الله، وكان بعضُ الحكماء يقول: يقول الله- تعالى-: «يا مُرائي: أمرُ من ترائي بيد من تعصيه» . فمثل هذا أعماله كلها قليلة، ولو كثرت في الحس كالجبال الرواسي، وأعمال المخلصين كلها كثيرة ولو قلَّت في الحس، وأعمال المرائين كلها قليلة ولو كثرت في الحس. قال في القوت: وَصَفَ اللهُ تعالى ذكر المنافقين بالقلة، لكونه غير خالص، كما قيل في تفسير قوله تعالى: ذِكْراً كَثِيراً أي: خالصًا، فسمي الخالص كثيرا. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-14","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"قوله تعالى: مُذَبْذَبِينَ بَيْنَ ذلِكَ: هذه صفة أهل الدعوى، المستشرفين على الحقيقة بالعلم، ليسوا من الخصوص ولا من العموم، مترددين بين الفريقين، ومن يضلل الله عن طريق التحقيق، فلن تجد له سبيلا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_142-15","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"4:142–143 · Hypocrisy in prayer and remembrance","text":"ثم نهى المؤمنين عن موالاة الكفار لئلا يتشبهوا بالمنافقين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_142-15"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_142-s1","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"","text":"I say: “They remember God only a little” is circumstantial to the subject of “they display themselves,” as is “wavering”: they make a show while not truly remembering, suspended between alternatives. Alternatively “wavering” may be accusative in censure. Mudhadhdhab denotes one disturbed, oscillating and unable to settle.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_142-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_142-s2","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"","text":"The hypocrites profess faith and conceal unbelief. God is said to “deceive” them in the sense of a corresponding punishment, named after their act: in the hereafter they are shown a light to walk by upon the bridge, as the faithful are; when they move on, the hypocrites' light is extinguished while the believers' light remains, and they call for light before falling into punishment (cf. 57:13). They undertake prayer lazily because God is not their intention. If watched, they pray; if unseen, they abandon it. They seek reputation by their actions and remember God only when observed, which occupies the smaller part of their time. Or remembrance within their prayer is slight, restricted to the opening and closing formulas without inward attention. Ibn ʿAbbās says their act is designed for display and reputation: if performed for God it would be much remembrance. Qatāda says rejected remembrance is small no matter how abundant its appearance; accepted remembrance is great even if externally slight. Such hypocrites oscillate between denial and faith, genuine believers and open polytheists, at ease with neither. God has known their state, and whoever is left astray has no other guide, like the verse, “Whoever God gives no light has no light” (24:40).","anchor":"en-q4_cont_142-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_142-s3","r":"q4_cont_142","title":"","text":"A desire that people should admire one's good deeds or spiritual states contains a branch of hypocrisy and ostentation ( riyāʾ ). Its mark is decorating the outward appearance while neglecting the inner state, attending to people rather than God. One of the sages used to say, “God Most High says: ‘You who show off, the affairs of those before whom you show off are in the hands of the One you disobey.’” All his outwardly gigantic deeds are inwardly small; the sincere person's little work is great. Al-Qūt is cited for understanding abundant remembrance as pure remembrance, for sincerity makes it abundant. “Wavering” also describes mere claimants to realisation who glimpse inward truth intellectually but belong fully neither to the special people nor to ordinary religious society. Without divine guidance onto the path of actual verification ( taḥqīq ), they have no way to its goal.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_142-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_144","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons","text":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons 4:144","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_144"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_144-1","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons","text":"يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَتَّخِذُوا الْكافِرِينَ أَوْلِياءَ مِنْ دُونِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَجْعَلُوا لِلَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ سُلْطاناً مُبِيناً (144)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_144-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_144-2","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons","text":"قلت: اتخذ، يتعدّى إلى مفعولين، و (من دون) : حال.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_144-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_144-3","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تتشبهوا بالمنافقين فتتخذوا الْكافِرِينَ أَوْلِياءَ وأصدقاء مِنْ دُونِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ لأن الله أعزكم بالإيمان والنصر، فلا تطلبوا العز من أحد سواه، أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَجْعَلُوا لِلَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ سُلْطاناً مُبِيناً أي: حجة واضحة على تعذيبكم وسببًا في عقابكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_144-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_144-4","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons","text":"الإشارة: قد تقدم في كثير من الإشارات النهي عن موالاة أهل الإنكار على الأولياء، وعن مخالطة أهل الدنيا وصحبتهم، فإن ذلك حجة واضحة على الرجوع إليهم ومصانعتهم، وهو عين النفاق عند المخلصين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_144-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_144-5","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_144-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_144-6","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"4:144 · Taking unbelief as patrons","text":"ثم ذكر وعيد المنافقين، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_144-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_144-s1","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"","text":"I say: ittakhadha governs two objects, and “instead of” is circumstantial. Do not imitate the hypocrites by seeking protection and friendship through enemies of the believing community, as though worldly power were the source of dignity. God has already ennobled believers through faith and victory. Such a choice would provide manifest evidence for their censure and punishment.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_144-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_144-s2","r":"q4_cont_144","title":"","text":"Ibn ʿAjība reiterates his warning against alliance with those who denounce God's saints and immersion in companionship devoted to worldly ambition. This is clear evidence of returning to them and ingratiating oneself with them; for sincere seekers that split allegiance is a form of inward hypocrisy. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_144-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_145","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance 4:145–147","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_145"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-1","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"إِنَّ الْمُنافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرْكِ الْأَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ نَصِيراً (145) إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ تابُوا وَأَصْلَحُوا وَاعْتَصَمُوا بِاللَّهِ وَأَخْلَصُوا دِينَهُمْ لِلَّهِ فَأُولئِكَ مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَسَوْفَ يُؤْتِ اللَّهُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَجْراً عَظِيماً (146) مَّا يَفْعَلُ اللَّهُ بِعَذابِكُمْ إِنْ شَكَرْتُمْ وَآمَنْتُمْ وَكانَ اللَّهُ شاكِراً عَلِيماً (147)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-2","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"قلت: الدَّرَك: والدَّرْك لغتان، كالظَّعَن والظَّعْن، والنَّهَر والنَّهْر، والنَّشَر والنَّشْر، وهي الطبقة السفلى، وسميت طبقاتهم دركات لأنها مُتداركة متتابعة، وهي ضد الدرجات، فالدرجات للعلو، والدركات للسفل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-3","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الْمُنافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرْكِ الْأَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ أي: في الطبقة السفلى في قَعر جهنم لأنهم أخبث الكفرة، حيث ضموا إلى الكفر الاستهزاء بالإسلام وخداع المسلمين. قال ابن مسعود رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-4","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"(هم في توابيت من النار مقفلة عليهم في النار، مطبقة عليهم) . وعن ابن عمر رضي الله عنه: (إن أشدُّ الناس عذاباً يومَ القيامة ثلاثة: المنافقون، ومن كفر من أصحاب المائدة، وآل فرعون لقوله: إِنَّ الْمُنافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرْكِ الْأَسْفَلِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-5","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"مِنَ النَّارِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-6","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"وقال في أصحاب المائدة: فَإِنِّي أُعَذِّبُهُ عَذاباً لآ أُعَذِّبُهُ أَحَداً مِنَ الْعالَمِينَ. وقال: أَدْخِلُوا آلَ فِرْعَوْنَ أَشَدَّ الْعَذابِ، وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ نَصِيراً يمنعهم من ذلك العذاب. إِلَّا الَّذِينَ تابُوا عن النفاق وَأَصْلَحُوا ما أفسدوا في سرائرهم وأعمالهم في حال النفاق، وَاعْتَصَمُوا بِاللَّهِ أي: وثقوا به وتمسكوا به، دون أحد سواه، وَأَخْلَصُوا دِينَهُمْ لِلَّهِ لا يريدون بطاعته إلا وجه الله، لا رياء ولا سمعة فَأُولئِكَ مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ في الدين. قال الفرَّاء: من المؤمنين، وقال العتبي: حاد عن كلامهم غيظًا عليهم، ولم يقل هم المؤمنون. هـ. قلت:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-7","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"إنما قال: مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ولم يقل: منهم، لأنَّ التخلص من النفاق صعب، ولا يكون من المؤمنين، حتى يتخلص من جميع شعبه، وهو عزيز، وقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «ثلاث من كن فيه فهُوَ مُنَافقٌ، وإن صَامَ وصلَّى وزَعم أنه مُسلمٌ، من إذا حدَّثَ كَذَبَ، وإذا وعد أخلف، وإذا ائُتمِنَ خَانَ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-8","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"وَسَوْفَ يُؤْتِ اللَّهُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ المخلصين أَجْراً عَظِيماً فيساهُمونَهم فيه إن تابوا وأصلحوا، فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عَنِ عذابهم، ولذلك قال: مَّا يَفْعَلُ اللَّهُ بِعَذابِكُمْ إِنْ شَكَرْتُمْ وَآمَنْتُمْ أي: لا حاجة له في عذابكم، فلا يشفى به غيظًا ولا يدفع به ضررًا، أو يستجلب به نفعًا لأنه غنيَّ عن المنافع، وإنما يعاقب المصر بكفره، لأن إصراره عليه كسوء المزاج يؤدي إلى مرض، فإن زال بالإيمان والشكر، ونقَّى منه قلبه، تخلص من تبعته. وإنما قدم الشكر لأن الناظر يدرك النعم أولاً فيشكر شكرًا مبهمًا، ثم يمعن النظر حتى يعرف المنعم فيؤمن به. قاله البيضاوي. وقال الثعلبي: فيه تقديم وتأخير، أي إن آمنتم وشكرتم، لأن الشكر لا ينفع مع عدم الإيمان. وَكانَ اللَّهُ شاكِراً لأعمال عباده، يقبل اليسير ويعطي الكثير، عَلِيماً بحقيقة شكرهم وإيمانهم، ومقدار أعمالهم، فيضاعفها على قدر تخليصها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-9","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"الإشارة: لا شيء أصعب على النفس من الإخلاص كلما اجتهد العبد في قطع الرياء نبت على لون آخر، فلا يتطهر العبد منها إلا بتحقيق الفناء والغيبة عن السوى بالكلية. كما قال الششترى رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-10","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"طهِّر العَينَ بالمَدامِعِ سَكبًا ... مِن شُهُودِ السَّوى تَزُل كلُّ عِلَّه","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-11","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"قال بعضهم: [لا ينبت الإخلاص في القلب حتى يَسقط من عين الناس، ويُسقط الناسَ من عينه] . والإخلاص من أعمال القلوب، فلا يطَّلع عليه إلا علام الغيوب. فلا يجوز أن يحكم على أحد بالرياء بمجرد ما يرى عليه من الإظهار، وقد تدخل الرياء مع الإسرار، وتتخلص من القلب مع الإظهار، وفي الحكم: «ربما دخل الرياءُ عليك حيث لا ينظر الخلق إليك» . فإذا تخلص العبد من دقائق الرياء، وأصلح ما بينه وبين الله، واعتصم به دون شيء سواه، كان مع المخلصين المقربين فيكون عمله موفورًا، وسعيه مشكورًا. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-12","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"وقد تكلم في الإحياء على هذه الآية فقال: إنما كان المنافقون في الدرك الأسفل لأنهم جحدوا بعد العلم، وإنما تضاعف عذاب العالم في معصيته لأنه عَصَى عن علم. قلت: وافهم منه قوله صلّى الله عليه وسلم في أبي طالب: «وَلَولاَ أنَا لَكَانَ فِي الدَّركِ الأسفلَ مِنَ النَّارِ» . وذلك لإعراضه مع العلم. وقال في الإحياء أيضًا: شدَّد أمر المنافقين لأن الكافر كفرَ وأظهَرَ، والمنافق كفر وستر، فكان ستره لكفره كفرًا آخر، لأنه استخف بنظر الله إلى قلبه، وعظَّم أمر المخلوقين. هـ. والحاصل: أن التشديد في الرياء والنفاق لِمَا في ذلك من تعظيم نظر الخلق على نظر الخالق، فكان أعظمَ من الكفر الصريح. هـ. من الحاشية.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_145-13","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"4:145–147 · The lowest depth and the opening of repentance","text":"ومن علامة تصفية الباطن من الرياء والنفاق تلبس الظاهر بأحسن الأخلاق، ولذلك ذكره بِأَثَره، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_145-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_145-s1","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"","text":"I say: darak and dark are two vocalisations, like ẓaʿan/ẓaʿn , nahar/nahr , and nashar/nashr . Darakāt are the successive descending layers, in contrast with rising darajāt . Hypocrites occupy the lowest depth because their denial was compounded by ridicule and deliberate deception of believers. Ibn Masʿūd is reported to describe them as locked in coffins of Fire. Ibn ʿUmar is quoted: “The three kinds of people punished most severely on the Day of Resurrection are the hypocrites, those of the People of the Table who disbelieved, and Pharaoh’s people,” citing: “The hypocrites are in the lowest depth of the Fire” [4:145]; concerning the People of the Table, “I shall punish him with a punishment with which I punish no other being” [5:115]; and “Admit Pharaoh’s people to the severest punishment” [40:46]. [Translator’s note: These descriptions of the unseen are presented in the source as reports.] The exception is real. Those who repent of hypocrisy, correct outward deeds and inward dispositions, trust in and attach themselves to God alone, and purify worship of ostentation and the wish for reputation, are joined to believers. Al-Farrāʾ takes “with the believers” as meaning “among the believers,” while al-ʿUtbī supposes the wording deliberately avoids saying “they are believers” to indicate God's displeasure. Ibn ʿAjība responds: “He says ‘with the believers,’ not ‘from among them,’ because escape from hypocrisy is difficult. One does not belong among the believers until freed from all its branches, and this is rare.” He cites the familiar Prophetic warning about lying when speaking, breaking promises and betraying trusts, even if a person fasts, prays and asserts Islam. Sincere people receive great reward, and the repentant share in it. God has no need to inflict punishment for personal gratification, since He is not harmed by sin or benefited by worship. Persisting in disbelief produces a spiritual disease; faith and thanksgiving cure it. Al-Bayḍāwī explains that gratitude precedes faith in the verse because a person first experiences benefits and offers rudimentary gratitude, then reflects until recognising the Giver. Al-Thaʿlabī instead takes the sequence as transposed: belief precedes gratitude, since gratitude without faith brings no saving benefit. God is Shākir , accepting slight deeds and repaying them many times over, and ʿAlīm , knowing the true degree of sincerity.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_145-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_145-s2","r":"q4_cont_145","title":"","text":"No vice is harder for the self to uproot than ostentation: cut it back in one guise and it returns in another. It is fully purified only by effacement ( fanāʾ ) and complete absence from what is other than God. Ibn ʿAjība quotes al-Shushtarī: With flowing tears, cleanse the eye of witnessing all else: every sickness departs. A saying holds that sincerity never grows in the heart until one falls from people's gaze and lets people fall from one's own. Sincerity belongs to inward actions, whose reality is known to the Knower of the Unseen alone. Accordingly no one should simply declare another person ostentatious because a devotional act has been made visible. Ostentation can be present in secrecy and absent from public action. The Ḥikam warns that ostentation may enter even where no creature sees one. When the seeker is purified of its finer traces, restores the relationship with God and takes refuge in Him alone, he joins the sincerely devoted brought-near; his acts are valued and his endeavour gratefully received. The marginal commentary cites the Iḥyāʾ and comments upon it. The hypocrites' lowest depth reflects denial after knowledge: the scholar's sin is aggravated because it knowingly violates what he understands. The marginal commentator connects this with the reported statement that, without the Prophet's intercession, Abū Ṭālib would have been in the lowest depth, on account of his refusal despite recognition. He also reports al-Ghazālī's explanation that open denial is one evil but concealed denial adds another, because the hypocrite values the judgment of people more than God's awareness of the heart. The severity of ostentation and hypocrisy thus concerns elevating human observation above divine observation; it is therefore graver than open unbelief. Here ends the material from the marginal commentary.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_145-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_148","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon 4:148–149","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_148"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-1","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"لا يُحِبُّ اللَّهُ الْجَهْرَ بِالسُّوءِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ إِلاَّ مَنْ ظُلِمَ وَكانَ اللَّهُ سَمِيعاً عَلِيماً (148) إِنْ تُبْدُوا خَيْراً أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ أَوْ تَعْفُوا عَنْ سُوءٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَفُوًّا قَدِيراً (149)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-2","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"قلت: (إلا من ظلم) : استثناء منقطع، أي: لكن من ظلم فلا بأس أن يشكو بظالمه ويدعو عليه، وليس المراد أن الله يحب ذلك منه، إذ العفو أحسن كما يقوله بعد، وقرئ: (إلا من ظَلَم) بالبناء للفاعل، أي: ولكن الظالم يفعل مالا يحبه الله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-3","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"يقول الحق جلَ جلاله: لا يُحِبُّ اللَّهُ الْجَهْرَ أي: الإجهار بِالسُّوءِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ لأنه مِن فِعل أهل الجفاء والجهل إِلَّا مَنْ ظُلِمَ فلا بأس أن يجهر بالدعاء على ظالمه، أو بالشكوى به. نظيرها: وَلَمَنِ انْتَصَرَ بَعْدَ ظُلْمِهِ فَأُولئِكَ مَا عَلَيْهِمْ مِنْ سَبِيلٍ. قال مجاهد: هذا في الضيف النازل إذا لم يُضَف ومُنِع حقه، أو أُسِيءَ قِراه، فقد رخص له أن يذكر ما صُنعَ به. وزَعَم أن ضيفا تضيّف قوما فأساءوا قراه، فاشتكاهم، فنزلت الآية رخصة في شكواه. وَكانَ اللَّهُ سَمِيعاً لدعاء المظلوم، ورده على الظالم، فلا يحتاج إلى جهره، عَلِيماً بالظالم فيعاقبه على قدر جرمه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-4","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"ثم رغَّب في العفو فقال: إِنْ تُبْدُوا خَيْراً: طاعة وبرًا كحسن الخلق ولين الجانب، أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-5","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"تفعلوه سرًا، أَوْ تَعْفُوا عَنْ سُوءٍ بأن لا تؤاخذوا به من أساء إليكم، وهذا هو المقصود بالذكر، وإنما ذُكِرَ إبداءُ الخير وإخفاؤُه سببًا ووسيلة لذكره، ولذلك رتب عليه فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كانَ عَفُوًّا قَدِيراً أي: كثير العفو عن العُصاة، مع كمال قدرته على الانتقام، فأنتم أولى بذلك، وهو حث للمظلوم على العفو، بعد ما رخَّص له في الانتصار، حملاً على مكارم الأخلاق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-6","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن الباطن إذا كمل تطهيره وتحقق تنويره ظهر أثر ذلك على الظاهر من مكارم الأخلاق، ولين الجانب، وحسن الخطاب، وترك العتاب، فما كمن في غيب السرائر ظهر في شهادة الظواهر وما كمَن فيك ظَهَرَ على فيك، وهذه أخلاق الصوفية- رضى الله عنهم وأرضاهم- وبذلك وصفهم القائل فيهم، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-7","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"هيْنُون ليْنُون أيسَارٌ بنو يَسَرٍ ... سُوَّاسُ مَكرُمَةِ أبناءُ أيسَارِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-8","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"لا يَنطقُون بغيرِ الحقِّ إن نطقُوا ... ولا يُمَاروُنَ إن مارَوُا بإكثَارِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-9","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"مَن تَلق مِنهُم تَقُل هذاك سَيِّدهُم ... مِثلُ النُّجُومِ التي يُهدَى بها السَّارِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-10","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"ومن شأن الحضرة التهذيب والتأديب، فلا يبقى معها لغو ولا تأثيم، لأنها جنة معجلة، قال تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-11","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"لاَ يَسْمَعُونَ فِيها لَغْواً وَلا تَأْثِيماً إِلَّا قِيلًا سَلاماً سَلاماً.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-12","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"وأيضَا أهل الحضرة حصل لهم القرب من الحبيب، فهم في حضرة القريب على بساط القرب على الدوام، ولا يتصور منهم الجهر بالكلام، وهم في حضرة الملك العلاَّم. قال تعالى: وَخَشَعَتِ الْأَصْواتُ لِلرَّحْمنِ فَلا تَسْمَعُ إِلَّا هَمْساً، فرفعُ الصوت عند الصوفية مذموم شنيع، يدل على بُعد صاحبه كيف ما كان، وتأمل قضية الصِّدِّيق حيث قال له- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «مالك تقرأ سرًا؟» فقال: (إن الذي نناجيه ليس ببعيد) . أو كما قال، وإنما قال له صلى الله عليه وسلم: «ارفع قليلاً» إخراجًا له عن مُراده، تربية له. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_148-13","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"4:148–149 · Wronged speech and divine pardon","text":"ولما قدّم أقبح الكفر، وهو كفر المنافقين، ذكر ما يليه، وهو كفر اليهود، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_148-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_148-s1","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"","text":"I say: “Except one wronged” is a disconnected exception: the one who suffers injustice is permitted to complain against or pray against the wrongdoer, but this does not mean God positively loves such speech, since forgiveness is better, as the next verse shows. In a variant reading ẓalama is active—“except the one who wronged”—that is, the offender engages in speech displeasing to God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_148-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_148-s2","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"","text":"God does not approve of crying out in evil words, an act of coarseness and ignorance. A person who has been oppressed may publicly complain or invoke judgment against the oppressor; 42:41 similarly excuses proportionate self-defence. Mujāhid applies it to a guest denied appropriate hospitality or badly treated, who may recount the treatment received. A report attributes its revelation to such a guest's complaint. God hears the prayer of the oppressed and his response to the oppressor —so raised speech is unnecessary—and knows the oppressor, whom He punishes in proportion to his wrongdoing. Yet the highest response is pardon. Showing goodness openly through virtue, gentleness and obedience, or performing it secretly, are valuable, but the point of the passage is pardon of the person who has wronged you. These other kinds of goodness prepare its mention. God is repeatedly forgiving, although possessed of perfect power to avenge; people should imitate that moral generosity. Thus, after granting the oppressed permission to protest, He encourages the more excellent character of pardon.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_148-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_148-s3","r":"q4_cont_148","title":"","text":"Once inward purification and illumination are established, the outward character displays generosity, softness, gracious speech and an end to reproach. What lies in inward secrecy becomes manifest in outward conduct: what is hidden within appears upon the tongue. Ibn ʿAjība cites these lines about them: Easy and gentle, generous, sons of ease; stewards of noble deeds, sons of the generous. When they speak, they speak only truth; nor, when they dispute, do they dispute at length. Whomever you meet among them, you say, “That is their chief,” like the stars by which the night traveller is guided. The divine Presence educates and refines: no empty or sinful speech remains there, like the Paradise where only “Peace, peace” is heard (56:25–26). Those continuously near the Beloved stand in the audience of the Most High; loud self-assertion does not fit that station. God says, “Voices are humbled before the All-Merciful, so you hear only a whisper” [20:108]. Among the Sufis, raising the voice is reprehensible and ugly, indicating the speaker’s remoteness whatever his condition. When the Prophet asked Abū Bakr why he recited so quietly, he is reported to have answered, “The One I address is not far away.” The Prophet instructed him to raise the voice a little, which Ibn ʿAjība interprets as training him not to become attached to his own chosen manner. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_148-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_150","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers 4:150–151","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_150"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_150-1","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يُفَرِّقُوا بَيْنَ اللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَيَقُولُونَ نُؤْمِنُ بِبَعْضٍ وَنَكْفُرُ بِبَعْضٍ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يَتَّخِذُوا بَيْنَ ذلِكَ سَبِيلاً (150) أُولئِكَ هُمُ الْكافِرُونَ حَقًّا وَأَعْتَدْنا لِلْكافِرِينَ عَذاباً مُهِيناً (151)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_150-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_150-2","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"قلت: (حقًا) : مصدر مؤكد للجملة، أو صفة لمصدر الكافرين، أي: كفروا كفرًا محققًا يقينًا. وأصل (أعتدنا) :","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_150-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_150-3","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"أعددنا، أبدلت الدال تاء لقرب المخرج.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_150-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_150-4","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يُفَرِّقُوا بَيْنَ اللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ بأن يؤمنوا بالله ويكفروا برسله، وَيَقُولُونَ نُؤْمِنُ بِبَعْضٍ الأنبياء وَنَكْفُرُ بِبَعْضٍ، كاليهود، آمنوا بموسى","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_150-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_150-5","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"وعُزير والتوراة، وكفروا بعيسى ومحمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم، وَيُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يَتَّخِذُوا بَيْنَ ذلِكَ سَبِيلًا، أي: طريقًا وسطًا بين الإيمان والكفر، ولا واسطة، إذ الحق لا يختلف، فإن الإيمان بالله إنما يتم برسله وتصديقهم فيما بلغوا عنه، تفصيلاً وإجمالاً، فالكافر بالبعض كالكافر بالكل في الضلال. ولذلك حكم عليهم بصريح الكفر فقال: أُولئِكَ هُمُ الْكافِرُونَ حَقًّا أي: هم الكاملون في الكفر حقيقة، وإنما أكد كفرهم لأنهم تحكموا على الله، واتخذوا إلههم هواهم، حيث جعلوا الاختيار لهم دون الله، وفي ذلك منازعة للقدر، وتعطيل له، وهو كفر وشرك، ثم ذكر وعيدهم فقال: وَأَعْتَدْنا أي: هيأنا لِلْكافِرِينَ منهم عَذاباً مُهِيناً أي: يخزيهم ويهينهم، حين يُكرِّم أولياءَه ويرفع أقدارهم. جعلنا الله منهم. آمين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_150-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_150-6","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"الإشارة: الأولياء على قَدم الأنبياء، فمن فرق بينهم حرم بركةَ جميعهم، ومن صدَّق بجميعهم وعَظَّمَهم اقتبس من أنوارهم كلهم، والله- تعالى- غيور على أوليائه، كما كان غيورًا على أنبيائه، فطرد من فرَّق بينهم، فكذلك يطرد من يقع في بعض أوليائه ويعظم البعض، لأن البعض هو الكل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_150-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_150-7","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"4:150–151 · Refusing to distinguish between messengers","text":"ثم ذكر من لم يفرق، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_150-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_150-s1","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"","text":"I say: ḥaqqan is an emphatic verbal noun reinforcing the whole judgment or qualifying an understood noun: they have disbelieved with real, certain unbelief. Aʿtadnā was originally aʿdadnā , the first dāl being replaced by tāʾ because their places of articulation are close. Those who affirm God but reject His messengers attempt an incoherent separation; the verse speaks especially, in Ibn ʿAjība's exposition, of Jews accepting Moses, Ezra and Torah but rejecting Jesus and Muḥammad. Such people seek an imagined middle way between belief and denial. Yet belief in God is completed by accepting the messengers and what they authentically communicate, each in the proper degree, in detail or generally. Denial of one legitimate messenger undermines the whole principle. He interprets the emphatic judgment as censuring those who made their own preferences an authority over God's choice, effectively treating whim as a deity and disputing divine decree. A humiliating punishment is contrasted with God's honouring and elevating of His friends. He prays that God include us with the latter.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_150-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_150-s2","r":"q4_cont_150","title":"","text":"Saints follow in the footsteps of prophets. Ibn ʿAjība carries the verse over analogically: one who makes distinctions among the friends of God loses the blessing of their company, whereas one who respects them all receives illumination from each. God is jealous for His friends, as for His prophets. As He drove away those who distinguished between His prophets, so He drives away someone who disparages some of His saints while exalting others, for the part is the whole. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_150-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_152","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers","text":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers 4:152","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_152"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_152-1","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers","text":"وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَلَمْ يُفَرِّقُوا بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ أُولئِكَ سَوْفَ نُؤْتِيهِمْ أُجُورَهُمْ وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفُوراً رَحِيماً (152)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_152-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_152-2","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers","text":"قلت: (بين) : من الأمور النسبية، فلا بد أن تدخل على متعدد، تقول: جلست بين فلان وفلان، وإنما دخلت هنا على (أحد) لأنه يقتضي متعددًا لعمومه، لأنه وقع في سياق النفي. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_152-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_152-3","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ وما يجب له من الكمالات، (ورسله) وما يجب لهم كذلك، وَلَمْ يُفَرِّقُوا بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ بأن آمنوا بجميعهم، وصدقوا بكل ما جاءوا به من عند ربهم، أُولئِكَ سَوْفَ نُؤْتِيهِمْ [١] أُجُورَهُمْ الموعودة لهم، بأن نُجِلَّ مقدارهم، ونرفع مقامهم، ونُبوئهم في جنات النعيم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_152-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_152-4","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers","text":"وتصديره بسوف لتأكيد الوعد والدلالة على أنه كائن لا محالة وإن تأخر وقته، ولما كان العبد لا يخلو من نقص، رفع الخوف عنهم بقوله: وَكانَ اللَّهُ غَفُوراً لِما فرط منهم رَحِيماً بهم بتضعيف حسناتهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_152-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_152-5","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers","text":"الإشارة: والذين صدقوا بأولياء الله، وعظموا جميعهم، واقتبسوا من أنوارهم كلهم، أولئك سوف نؤتيهم أجورهم، بأن أُنعمهم في جنات المعارف في دار الدنيا، فإن ماتوا أسكنّاهم فى الفراديس العُلَى (في مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عند مليك مقتدر) . والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_152-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_152-6","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"4:152 · Those who believe in all messengers","text":"ثم ذكر مساوئ اليهود فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_152-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_152-s1","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"","text":"I say: bayna (“between”) normally implies more than one referent, but here it governs “any one” ( aḥad ) because that word occurs in a negative context and therefore signifies the whole plurality. This is al-Bayḍāwī's explanation.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_152-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_152-s2","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"","text":"Those who affirm God's due perfections and the truthful mission and rank of His messengers without excluding one of them, believing what each communicated from the Lord, are promised a reward that raises and honours them in the gardens of bliss. The particle sawfa emphasises the promised reward's certainty, even if its appearance lies in the future. Because no servant is free of shortcomings, the verse adds that God is Forgiving of what they have neglected and Merciful in multiplying their good deeds.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_152-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_152-s3","r":"q4_cont_152","title":"","text":"Those who acknowledge all genuine saints, honour them and benefit from their several illuminations receive their portion too. They will enjoy the gardens of divine knowledge in this world and, upon death, be placed in the high gardens, “in an abode of truth with a Sovereign fully powerful” (54:55). God knows best. The next passage returns to the People of the Book.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_152-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_153","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs 4:153–154","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_153"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-1","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"يَسْئَلُكَ أَهْلُ الْكِتابِ أَنْ تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْهِمْ كِتاباً مِنَ السَّماءِ فَقَدْ سَأَلُوا مُوسى أَكْبَرَ مِنْ ذلِكَ فَقالُوا أَرِنَا اللَّهَ جَهْرَةً فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّاعِقَةُ بِظُلْمِهِمْ ثُمَّ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ فَعَفَوْنا عَنْ ذلِكَ وَآتَيْنا مُوسى سُلْطاناً مُبِيناً (153) وَرَفَعْنا فَوْقَهُمُ الطُّورَ بِمِيثاقِهِمْ وَقُلْنا لَهُمُ ادْخُلُوا الْبابَ سُجَّداً وَقُلْنا لَهُمْ لا تَعْدُوا فِي السَّبْتِ وَأَخَذْنا مِنْهُمْ مِيثاقاً غَلِيظاً (154)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-2","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"قلت: من قرأ: (لا تعدوا) بالسكون، فماضيه: عدا، ومن قرأ بتشديد الدال، فماضيه اعتَدى، وأصله: لا تعتدوا، فنُقلت حركة التاء إلى العين وأدغمت التاء في الدال، ومن قرأ بالاختلاس أشار إلى الأصل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-3","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يَسْئَلُكَ أَهْلُ الْكِتابِ، وهم أحبار اليهود، أَنْ تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْهِمْ كِتاباً مِنَ السَّماءِ جملة واحدة، كما نزل التوراة، أو كتابًا بخطَّ سماوي على ألواح كما كانت التوراة، والسائل هو كعب بن الأشرف وفنحاص بن عازوراء وغيرهم، قالوا للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم: (إن كنت نبيًا فأتنا بكتاب من السماء جملةً، كما أتى به موسى) ، قال تعالى في الرد عليهم: فَقَدْ سَأَلُوا مُوسى أَكْبَرَ مِنْ ذلِكَ وهو رؤية ذات الحقّ- تعالى- جهرًا حسًا. والمعنى: إن استعظمت ما سألوا منك فقد وقع منهم ما هو أعظم من ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-4","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"وهذا السؤال، وإن كان من آبائهم، أُسند إليهم لأنهم كانوا آخذين بمذهبهم تابعين لهديهم، فما اقترحوا عليك ليس بأول جهالاتهم وتشغيبهم بل عُرفُهُم راسخٌ في ذلك، فلا تستغرب ما وقع منهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-5","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"ثم فسر سؤالهم بقوله: فَقالُوا أَرِنَا اللَّهَ جَهْرَةً أي: عيانًا في الحس، فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّاعِقَةُ، بأن جاءت نار من السماء فأهلكتهم، فماتوا ثم بُعثوا بدعوة موسى عليه السلام وذلك بسبب ظلمهم. وهو تعنتهم وسؤالهم لما استحيل في تلك الحال التي كانوا عليها. وذلك لا يقتضي امتناع الرؤية مطلقًا. وسيأتي في الإشارة تحرير ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-6","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"ثُمَّ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ مِنْ بَعْدِ ما جاءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّناتُ على وحدانيته تعالى. وهذه جناية أخرى اقترفها أيضًا أوائلهم، فَعَفَوْنا عَنْ ذلِكَ حين تابوا، ولم نعاجلهم بالعقوبة، وَآتَيْنا مُوسى سُلْطاناً مُبِيناً أي: تسلطًا ظاهرًا عليهم، حين أمرهم أن يقتلوا أنفسهم، توبة من اتخاذهم العجل إلهًا، وحجة واضحة على نبوته كالآيات التسع.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-7","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"وَرَفَعْنا فَوْقَهُمُ الطُّورَ حين امتنعوا من قبول أحكام التوراة، بسبب ميثاقهم الذي أخذناه عليهم، وهو التزام أحكام التوراة، وقلنا لهم على لسان موسى: ادْخُلُوا الْبابَ سُجَّداً أي: باب بيت المقدس، فدخلوا يزحفون على استاههم عنادًا واستهزاءً، وقلنا لهم: لا تَعْدُوا فِي السَّبْتِ على لسان داود عليه السلام، فاعتدوا فيه بالاصطياد، فمسخناهم قردةً وخنازير، وَأَخَذْنا مِنْهُمْ مِيثاقاً غَلِيظاً على ذلك كله، فنقضوا جميع ذلك، أو ميثاقًا غليظًا في التوراة لئن أدركوك ليؤمنن بك، وليبينن صفتك للناس، فنقضوا وكتموا. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-8","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"الإشارة: اقتراح الآيات وطلب الكرامات من الأولياء، سنة ماضية، لأنهم على قدم الأنبياء- عليهم السلام- ما يقال لهم إلا ما قيل للأنبياء قبلهم، فلا تكاد تجد أحدًا يصدق بولي حتى تظهر عليه الكرامة، وهو جهل كبير لأن الكرامة قد تظهر على من لم تكمل له استقامة، وقد تكون استدراجًا ومكرًا. وأيُّ كرامة أعظم من العلوم اللدنية والأخلاق النبوية؟ كما قال شيخنا رضي الله عنه. وقد ظهرت الكرامات على المتقدمين ولم ينقطع الإنكار عليهم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-9","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"واعلم أن طلب الرؤية في الدنيا ليس بممتنع، وإنما عاقب الله بني إسرائيل على طلبها لأنهم طلبوها قبل إبانها، طلبوها من غير اتصاف بشروط حصولها، وهو كمال التهذيب والتطهير من دنس الحس، فمن كمل تهذيبه وتحقق تطهيره حصل له شهود الحق، حتى لو كُلف أن يشهد غيره لم يستطع، وذلك حين تستولي البصيرة على البصر، فيشهد البصر ما كانت تشهده البصيرة، وذلك بعد كمال فتحها. ولذلك قال في الحِكَم: «شعاعُ البصيرة يشهدك قرب الحق منك، وعين البصيرة يشهدك عدمك لوجوده، وحق البصيرة يشهدك وجود الحق» ... الخ كلامه. وهذه المشاهدة لا تحصل إلا لمن اتصل بشيخ التربية، وإلا فلا مطمع فيها. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_153-10","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"4:153–154 · Scripture, Israel and the demand for signs","text":"ثم ذكر عقوبة اليهود حيث نقضوا العهود، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_153-10"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_153-s1","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"","text":"I say: one reading of lā taʿdū has a quiescent consonant and derives from ʿadā . Another doubles the dāl , deriving from iʿtadā : the original lā taʿtadū underwent a transfer of vowel and assimilation. A reading with an incompletely pronounced vowel preserves an indication of that origin.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_153-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_153-s2","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"","text":"Certain Jewish religious leaders, named as Kaʿb ibn al-Ashraf and Finḥāṣ ibn ʿĀzūrāʾ, demanded that Muḥammad produce a complete heavenly book at once, or written celestial tablets as those associated with Moses. God responds that previous generations had demanded something more extraordinary: direct sensible vision of the divine Essence. The acts of their ancestors are addressed to these later claimants because they had adopted their inherited posture and participated in its defiance. Their rejection should not surprise the Prophet. Their forebears said, “Show us God openly,” seeking a sensory manifestation for which they had not been prepared. The thunderbolt, described as fire from heaven, destroyed them, and they were restored to life in response to Moses' supplication. Ibn ʿAjība insists this punishment does not mean the vision of God is altogether impossible; their request was untimely and wrong in its circumstances. Those forebears then worshipped the calf after proofs of divine unity had come. God accepted repentance and pardoned, bestowing on Moses manifest authority over them and evident proofs of prophecy, including the nine signs. Moses’ manifest authority over them is illustrated by his command that they kill themselves in repentance for taking the calf as a god. God raised Mount Sinai above them when they resisted the Torah's stipulations, obliging them through solemn covenant. They were told to enter the gate of the sacred city bowing, but in the traditional account they entered dragging themselves on their buttocks in obstinacy and mockery. They were forbidden to violate the Sabbath, through David, but transgressed by fishing; the text recalls the traditional narrative of punishment by transformation into apes and swine. A weighty covenant encompassed all these commands, which they broke; alternatively it included a stipulation that, should they live to meet Muḥammad, they would recognise and proclaim his traits, but they concealed them.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_153-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_153-s3","r":"q4_cont_153","title":"","text":"Demand for signs and extraordinary miracles from saints is an old pattern. Saints walk in the prophets' footsteps and encounter analogous objections. People are often reluctant to acknowledge a saint without a karāma ; yet extraordinary phenomena do not by themselves prove an established uprightness ( istiqāma ). A marvel can occur before a person is perfected, and can even be a trial or a deceptive elevation ( istidrāj ). Ibn ʿAjība quotes his shaykh: what miracle is greater than divinely granted knowledge ( ʿulūm ladunniyya ) and Prophetic virtues? Miracles appeared with earlier saints and did not end opposition to them. The desire to behold God during this life is not, in Ibn ʿAjība's inward interpretation, absolutely excluded. The Israelites were punished because they demanded it before its proper season, without the requisite perfection of training and purification from the defilement of sensory perception. When insight has been completely purified, it witnesses the Real so fully that it cannot be forced to witness anything other than Him. The inward eye comes to govern the outward eye, and the latter witnesses what the inward eye had first perceived. The Ḥikam is cited for three gradations: the ray of insight shows God's nearness; the eye of insight witnesses one's own non-existence before His existence; and the truth of insight witnesses the existence of the Real. Such witnessing is attained only by someone who has attached himself to a shaykh of spiritual training; otherwise there is no hope of it. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_153-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_155","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah 4:155–158","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_155"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-1","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"فَبِما نَقْضِهِمْ مِيثاقَهُمْ وَكُفْرِهِمْ بِآياتِ اللَّهِ وَقَتْلِهِمُ الْأَنْبِياءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ وَقَوْلِهِمْ قُلُوبُنا غُلْفٌ بَلْ طَبَعَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْها بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَلا يُؤْمِنُونَ إِلاَّ قَلِيلاً (155) وَبِكُفْرِهِمْ وَقَوْلِهِمْ عَلى مَرْيَمَ بُهْتاناً عَظِيماً (156) وَقَوْلِهِمْ إِنَّا قَتَلْنَا الْمَسِيحَ عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَما قَتَلُوهُ وَما صَلَبُوهُ وَلكِنْ شُبِّهَ لَهُمْ وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ لَفِي شَكٍّ مِنْهُ ما لَهُمْ بِهِ مِنْ عِلْمٍ إِلاَّ اتِّباعَ الظَّنِّ وَما قَتَلُوهُ يَقِيناً (157) بَلْ رَفَعَهُ اللَّهُ إِلَيْهِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَزِيزاً حَكِيماً (158)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-2","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"قلت: (فبما) : صلة زيدت للتأكيد، و (نقضهم) : مصدر مجرور بالباء، وهي متعلقة بالفعل المحذوف، أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-3","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"بسبب نقضهم فَعَلنا بهم ما فعلنا، أو بقوله: (حرَمنا عليهم) ، ويكون (فبظلم) على هذا بدلاً من قوله: (فبما نقضهم) ، فيكون التحريم بسبب النقض، وما عطف عليه. والاستثناء في قوله: (إلا اتباع الظن) منقطع إذ العلم يناقض الظن.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-4","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فلما أخذنا على بني إسرائيل العهد والميثاق خالفوا ونقضوا، ففعلنا بهم ما فعلنا، بسبب نقضهم ميثاقهم، أو بسبب نقضهم وكفرهم حَرَّمْنا عَلَيْهِمْ طَيِّباتٍ أُحِلَّتْ لَهُمْ، وبسبب كفرهم أيضًا بِآياتِ اللَّهِ القرآن، أو بما في كتبهم، وَقَتْلِهِمُ الْأَنْبِياءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ وَقَوْلِهِمْ قُلُوبُنا غُلْفٌ أي: مغلفة لا تفقه ما تقول.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-5","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"قال تعالى في الرد عليهم: بَلْ طَبَعَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْها بِكُفْرِهِمْ، فجعلها محجوبة عن العلم، بأن خذلها ومنعها التوفيق للتدبر في الآيات والتذكر بالمواعظ، فَلا يُؤْمِنُونَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا منهم كعبد الله بن سلام وأصحابه، أو إيمانًا قليلاً لا عبرة به لنقصانه، وَبِكُفْرِهِمْ أيضًا بعيسى عاقبناهم وطبعنا على قلوبهم، وَقَوْلِهِمْ عَلى مَرْيَمَ بُهْتاناً عَظِيماً أي: نسبتها للزنى وبقولهم: إِنَّا قَتَلْنَا الْمَسِيحَ عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أي بزعمه، ويحتمل أنهم قالوه استهزاء، ونظيره: إِنَّ رَسُولَكُمُ الَّذِي أُرْسِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ لَمَجْنُونٌ، أو يكون استئنافًا من الله بمدحه، أو وضعًا للذكر الحسن موضع قولهم القبيح. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-6","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"ثم رد الله تعالى عليهم فقال: وَما قَتَلُوهُ وَما صَلَبُوهُ وَلكِنْ شُبِّهَ لَهُمْ، رُوِي أنَّ رهطاً من اليهود سبوه هو وأمه، فدعا عليهم، فمُسخوا قردة وخنازير، فاجتمعت اليهود على قتله، فقال لهم: يا معشر اليهود، إن الله يبغضكم، فغضبوا وثاروا ليقتلوه، فبعث الله تعالى جبريل فأدخله خوخة فيها كُوة في سقفها، ورفعه الله إلى السماء من تلك الكوة، فأمر اليهود رجلاً منهم يقال له: طيطانوس، أن يدخل الخوخة ويقتله، فلما دخل الخوخة، لم ير عيسى، فألقى الله تعالى شبه عيسى عليه، فلما أبطأ عليهم دخلوا عليه، فظنوه عيسى، فقتلوه وصلبوه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-7","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"وقال قتادة: ذكر لنا أن عيسى عليه السلام قال لأصحابه: أيكم يقذف عليه شبهي فيقتل؟ فقال رجل: أنا يا رسول الله، فقتل ذلك الرجل، ورفع عيسى عليه السلام، وكساه الريش وألبسه النور، وقطع عنه لذة المطعم والمشرب وصار مع الملائكة، فهو معهم في السماء إنسيًّا ملكيًّا، أرضيًّا سماويًّا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-8","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ اخْتَلَفُوا فِيهِ لَفِي شَكٍّ مِنْهُ فقال بعض اليهود: إن كان هذا عيسى فأين صاحبنا؟ وإن كان صاحبنا فأين عيسى؟ ويقال: إن الله تعالى ألقى شبه وجه عيسى على صاحبهم، ولم يلق عليه شبه جسده، فلما","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-9","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"قتلوه ونظروا إليه، فقالوا: الوجه وجه عيسى والجسد جسد صاحبنا. ما لَهُمْ بِهِ مِنْ عِلْمٍ إِلَّا اتِّباعَ الظَّنِّ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-10","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"لا علم لهم بقتله، لكن يتبعون الظن فقط. وَما قَتَلُوهُ قتلاً يَقِيناً كما زعموا بقولهم: إنا قتلنا المسيح، بَلْ رَفَعَهُ اللَّهُ إِلَيْهِ فهو في السماء الثانية مع يحيى عليها السلام، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَزِيزاً حَكِيماً أي: قويًا بالنقمة على اليهود، حكيمًا فيما حكم عليهم من اللعنة والغضب. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-11","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"الإشارة: نقضُ عهود الشيوخ من أسباب المقت والبعد عن الله، وكذلك الإنكار عليهم والطعن فيهم، وكذلك البعد عن وعظهم وتذكيرهم، وضد هذا من موجبات القرب والحب من الله، كحفظ حرمتهم، والوقوف مع أوامرهم، والذب عنهم حين تهتك حرمتهم، والدنو منهم، والسعي في خدمتهم. وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_155-12","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"4:155–158 · Covenant, transgression, and the Messiah","text":"ثم ذكر نزول عيسى فى آخر الزمان، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_155-12"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_155-s1","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"","text":"I say: mā in fa-bi-mā naqḍihim strengthens the expression. “Their breaking” is a verbal noun governed by bi- and related either to a suppressed verb—“because they broke the covenant, We dealt with them as We did”—or to the later “We prohibited good things for them”; in the latter parsing the “because of the wrongdoing” of 4:160 restates the cause, with the prohibitions following covenant-breaking and its associated offences. “Except following conjecture” is a disconnected exception because genuine knowledge and conjecture are opposed.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_155-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_155-s2","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"","text":"Israel's former commitments were broken, so consequences followed. Ibn ʿAjība includes the later removal of previously permitted good things, the denial of divine signs in Scripture or Qurʾān, the unjust killing of prophets, and the claim “Our hearts are wrapped,” as though unable to receive the Prophet's message. God answers that their continued denial has veiled the hearts from understanding and withheld success in contemplating signs and accepting admonition. “Few believe” may refer to a minority such as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and his associates; alternatively it means a meagre faith too deficient to count. He also cites rejection of Jesus, the monstrous accusation of sexual misconduct made against Mary, and the boast of killing Jesus, called “the Messenger of God” either mockingly by the speakers or by God as an insertion honouring Jesus amid their words, as al-Bayḍāwī explains. In Ibn ʿAjība's theological telling, God decisively denies that they killed or crucified Jesus. He recounts one narrative in which hostile Jews insulted Jesus and his mother; after Jesus prayed against them, they were transformed into apes and swine, and the Jews assembled to kill him. He told them, “Company of Jews, God hates you.” They became angry and rose to kill him. Gabriel led Jesus into an enclosure with an opening in its roof, through which God lifted him. An attacker named Ṭīṭānūs was sent inside; God caused him to resemble Jesus, and when the others entered they mistook him for Jesus and killed and crucified him. A different account attributed to Qatāda reports that Jesus asked his companions who would receive his resemblance and be killed; a volunteer accepted, Jesus was raised, clothed in feathers and in light [Translator’s note: The close earlier version in al-Thaʿlabī’s commentary, III:410, also places him among angels circling the Throne. This context supports “feathers” for rīsh ; “fine apparel” remains a lexical alternative. This preference concerns the narrative’s wording, not its historical authenticity.] , and deprived of the pleasure of food and drink, living among angels in heaven, human and angelic, earthly and heavenly. Those who disputed about the death were uncertain. Some wondered how the figure could be Jesus if their companion was missing, or their companion if Jesus had escaped. Another report says only the substitute's face, not his body, resembled Jesus, provoking their suspicion. They followed conjecture, not certainty. God, says Ibn ʿAjība, raised Jesus to heaven, where the commentator places him in the second heaven with John. God is mighty in His vengeance upon the Jews and wise in His judgment of curse and anger upon them. [Translator’s note: The competing substitution accounts are transmitted exegetical narratives. Their historical particulars are additional to the Qurʾānic phrase shubbiha lahum , “it was made to appear so to them.”]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_155-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_155-s3","r":"q4_cont_155","title":"","text":"Breaking commitments made to spiritual guides is among the causes of God’s abhorrence and of distance from Him, as can hostile denunciation of them and refusal of their admonitions. The contrary acts—respecting their dignity, abiding by their commands, defending them against slander, maintaining proper nearness and serving appropriately—are portrayed as means to proximity and love. [Translator’s note: This is Ibn ʿAjība’s application of the passage to spiritual formation. It does not establish prophetic infallibility or unlimited immunity for human teachers.] God gives success.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_155-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_159","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus","text":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus 4:159","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_159"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_159-1","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus","text":"وَإِنْ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ إِلاَّ لَيُؤْمِنَنَّ بِهِ قَبْلَ مَوْتِهِ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ يَكُونُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيداً (159)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_159-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_159-2","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنْ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتابِ أي: ما من يهودي ولا نصراني، أي: الموجودين حين نزوله إِلَّا لَيُؤْمِنَنَّ بعيسى قَبْلَ مَوْتِهِ أي: عيسى، وذلك حين نزوله من السماء، رُوِيَ أنه ينزل من السماء حين يخرج الدجال فيهلكه، ولا يبقى أحد من أهل الكتاب إلا ويؤمن به، حتى تكون الملة واحدة، وهي ملة الإسلام، وتقع الأمنة حتى يرتع الأسود مع الإبل، والنمور مع البقر، والذئاب مع الغنم، ويلعب الصبيان بالحيات، ويلبث في الأرض أربعين سنة، ثم يتوفّى ويصلى عليه المسلمون ويدفنونه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_159-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_159-3","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus","text":"وقيل الضمير فى (به) إلى عيسى، وفي (موته) إلى الكتابي، أي: وإن من أهل الكتاب أحد إلا ليؤمنن بعيسى بأنه عبد الله ورسوله، قَبْلَ مَوْتِهِ أي: قبل خروج نفس ذلك الكتابي إذا عاين الملك، فلا ينفعه حينئذ إيمانه، لأن كل من نزل به الموت لم تخرج نفسه حتى يتبين له الحق من الباطل. ويؤيد هذا قراءة من قرأ: ليُؤمنُنَّ به قبل موتهم بضم النون، لأن (أحدًا) في معنى الجمع، وهذا كالوعيد لهم والتحريض على معاجلة الإيمان به من قبل أن يُضطر إليه ولم ينفعه إيمانه، وَيَوْمَ الْقِيامَةِ يَكُونُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيداً يشهد على اليهود بالتكذيب، وعلى النصارى بأنهم دعوه ابن الله. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_159-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_159-4","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus","text":"الإشارة: عند الموت تتحقق الحقائق، ويتميز الحق من الباطل، ويحصل الندم، ولا ينفع حين تزل القدم، فالمطلوب المبادرة بتحقيق الإيمان، وتحصيل مقام العرفان، قبل أن يسقط إلى جنبه، فينفرد رهينًا في قبره بذنبه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_159-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_159-5","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_159-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_159-6","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"4:159 · The People of the Book and Jesus","text":"ثم ذكر وبال ظلمهم وعدوانهم فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_159-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_159-s1","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"","text":"On the first reading, every Jew and Christian living at Jesus' descent will believe in him before Jesus' death. Ibn ʿAjība transmits a traditional account in which Jesus descends when the Antichrist appears, destroys him, and all the surviving People of the Book recognise Jesus, leaving one religious community of Islam. Peace becomes so complete that lions graze with camels, leopards with cattle and wolves with sheep, while children safely play with snakes. Jesus remains for forty years, dies, receives the Muslim funeral prayer and is buried. [Translator’s note: The timescale and illustrative details belong to the report quoted by the commentator.] A second reading makes “his death” refer to each member of the People of the Book rather than Jesus: every such person will acknowledge before their own death that Jesus is God's servant and messenger, upon seeing the angel of death and learning truth from error. This final compulsory recognition, Ibn ʿAjība says, cannot replace faith freely attained earlier. He mentions a reading in which the pronoun denotes the plurality of those dying, and understands the passage as warning them to believe before death. On the Day of Resurrection Jesus will bear witness that some denied him and others ascribed divine sonship to him.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_159-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_159-s2","r":"q4_cont_159","title":"","text":"Death exposes realities and distinguishes truth from error, often bringing remorse when the opportunity for purposeful change has passed. The aim is to attain established faith and inward recognition ( ʿirfān ) now, before the foot slips and the person is left alone, held in pledge in his grave by his sin. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_159-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_160","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"4:160–161 · Wrongdoing, usury and forbidden things","text":"4:160–161 · Wrongdoing, usury and forbidden things 4:160–161","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_160"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_160-1","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"4:160–161 · Wrongdoing, usury and forbidden things","text":"فَبِظُلْمٍ مِنَ الَّذِينَ هادُوا حَرَّمْنا عَلَيْهِمْ طَيِّباتٍ أُحِلَّتْ لَهُمْ وَبِصَدِّهِمْ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ كَثِيراً (160) وَأَخْذِهِمُ الرِّبَوا وَقَدْ نُهُوا عَنْهُ وَأَكْلِهِمْ أَمْوالَ النَّاسِ بِالْباطِلِ وَأَعْتَدْنا لِلْكافِرِينَ مِنْهُمْ عَذاباً أَلِيماً (161)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_160-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_160-2","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"4:160–161 · Wrongdoing, usury and forbidden things","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: فبسبب ظلم مِنَ الَّذِينَ هادُوا وهو نقضهم الميثاق، وكفرهم بآيات الله، وقتلهم الأنبياء، حَرَّمْنا عَلَيْهِمْ طَيِّباتٍ كانت أُحِلَّتْ لَهُمْ كالشحوم، وكل ذي ظفر، وغير ذلك من لذيذ الطيبات، وكانوا كلما ارتكبوا كبيرة حرّم عليهم شيئًا من الطيّبات، وحرّمنا ذلك أيضًا عليهم بِصَدِّهِمْ عن طريق اللَّهِ صدًّا كَثِيراً، أي: بإعراضهم عنه إعراضًا كثيرًا، أو بصدهم عنه ناسًا كثيرًا كانوا يُخَذِّلونَهُم عن الدخول في دين الله، وبأخذهم الربا وَقَدْ نُهُوا عَنْهُ، فهو محرم عليهم وعلى الأمة المحمدية، وبأكلهم أَمْوالَ النَّاسِ بِالْباطِلِ كالرشوة وما كانوا يأخذونه من عوامهم، وَأَعْتَدْنا لِلْكافِرِينَ مِنْهُمْ بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلم عَذاباً أَلِيماً، دون من تاب وآمن به.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_160-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_160-3","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"4:160–161 · Wrongdoing, usury and forbidden things","text":"الإشارة: اعلم أن كل غفلة ومعصية وسوء أدب يحرم مرتكبه بسببه من لذيذ الطاعات وحلاوة المشاهدات على قدره، شعر أو لم يشعر، وقد يبعده من الحضرة وهو لا يشعر، مكرًا واستدراجًا، فإذا أصر عليه سلب من مقام الولاية بالكلية، ولا يزال ينقص إيمانه شيئًا فشيئًا، حتى يتفلت منه، والعياذ بالله، وإذا بادر بالتوبة رجى قبوله، وكل يقظة وطاعة وحسن أدب يوجب لصاحبه الزلفى والقرب من الحضرة، ويزيده في حلاوة المعاملة والمشاهدة على قدره، فلا يزال يتقرب إليه بنوافل الخيرات، حتى يحبه فيتولاه، فيكون سمعه وبصره، كما في الحديث.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_160-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_160-4","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"4:160–161 · Wrongdoing, usury and forbidden things","text":"وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_160-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_160-5","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"4:160–161 · Wrongdoing, usury and forbidden things","text":"ثم استثنى من تاب من اليهود، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_160-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_160-s1","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"","text":"Because of covenant-breaking, denial of God's signs and the murder of prophets, Ibn ʿAjība says, food formerly permitted was prohibited to the Children of Israel: kinds of fat, clawed animals and other desirable foods. In his account, whenever they committed a grave sin, He prohibited some good thing to them. They also turned from the divine way themselves or obstructed many other people from entering it, accepted usury ( ribā ) despite its prohibition in their own dispensation, and took wealth unjustly through bribes and illegitimate demands upon ordinary people. Usury is prohibited in the Muḥammadan dispensation as well. The punishment falls upon those who persist in denial, not those who repent and truly believe.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_160-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_160-s2","r":"q4_cont_160","title":"","text":"Every heedlessness, sin and breach of spiritual courtesy ( sūʾ al-adab ) deprives its perpetrator, to a corresponding degree, of the sweetness of worship and the delights of witnessing, whether the person notices or not. One may be distanced from divine presence without realising it, in an imperceptible spiritual trial. If he persists, he is stripped of the station of protecting friendship ( wilāya ) altogether, and his faith continues to weaken little by little until it escapes him. God preserve us. Immediate repentance offers hope of restoration. Conversely, every awakening, obedient act and refinement of conduct brings a person nearer and increases the sweetness of devotional work and direct vision. By supererogatory good deeds a servant draws near until God loves him and becomes his hearing and sight, as the famous divine saying relates. God gives success.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_160-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_162","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge","text":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge 4:162","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_162"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_162-1","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge","text":"لكِنِ الرَّاسِخُونَ فِي الْعِلْمِ مِنْهُمْ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ وَما أُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ وَالْمُقِيمِينَ الصَّلاةَ وَالْمُؤْتُونَ الزَّكاةَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ أُولئِكَ سَنُؤْتِيهِمْ أَجْراً عَظِيماً (162)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_162-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_162-2","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge","text":"قلت: والمؤمنون عطف على الراسخين، و (يؤمنون) : حال منهم. و (المقيمين) : نصب على المدح، لأن العرب إذا تطاولت في مدح شيء أو ذمه خالفوا بين إعراب أوله وأوسطه، نظيره: وَالْمُوفُونَ بِعَهْدِهِمْ إِذا عاهَدُوا وَالصَّابِرِينَ. وقالت عائشة رضي الله عنها: هو لحن من الكُتَّاب [١] ، وفي مصحف ابن مسعود: (والمقيمون) بالرفع على الأصل.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_162-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_162-3","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: ليس أهل الكتاب كلهم كما ذكرنا، لكِنِ الرَّاسِخُونَ فِي الْعِلْمِ مِنْهُمْ كعبد الله ابن سلام، ومخيريق، وغيرهما ممن له علم بالكتب المتقدمة، وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ منهم بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، من عوامهم حال كونهم يُؤْمِنُونَ بِما أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ وَما أُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ أي: يؤمنون إيمانًا كاملاً بلا تفريق، وأخص الْمُقِيمِينَ الصَّلاةَ، المتقنين لها، الْمُؤْتُونَ الزَّكاةَ المفروضة، وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ منهم بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ، على صفة ما جاء به القرآن من البعث بالأجسام والحساب وغير ذلك مما هو مقرر في السنة، أُولئِكَ سَنُؤْتِيهِمْ أَجْراً عَظِيماً، فتكون الآية كلها في أهل الكتاب.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_162-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_162-4","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge","text":"أو يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: لكِنِ الرَّاسِخُونَ فِي الْعِلْمِ من أهل الكتاب، وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ بمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، من العرب، وَالْمُقِيمِينَ الصَّلاةَ منهم، وَالْمُؤْتُونَ الزَّكاةَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ أُولئِكَ سَنُؤْتِيهِمْ أَجْراً عَظِيماً.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_162-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_162-5","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge","text":"الإشارة: كل من تحقّقت توبته بعد عصيانه، وظهرت يقظته بعد غفلاته، ورسخ في العلم بالله وبصفاته وأسمائه التحق بالسابقين، وحشر مع المقربين، وكان ممن أوتي أجرًا عظيمًا وخيرًا جسيمًا، والحمد لله رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_162-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_162-6","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"4:162 · Those grounded in knowledge","text":"ثم أجاب أهل الكتاب عن سؤالهم أن ينزل عليهم كتابًا من السماء فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_162-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_162-s1","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"","text":"I say: “The believers” is coordinated with “those firmly rooted in knowledge”; “they believe” is circumstantial. Al-muqīmīn (“those who establish prayer”) is in the accusative to express praise ( naṣb ʿalā l-madḥ ). Arabs sometimes depart from a repeated case construction in an extended encomium or censure, as in the Qurʾānic switch in 2:177. Ibn ʿAjība reports a statement attributed to ʿĀʾisha regarding an error by scribes, while noting that Ibn Masʿūd's codex is reported to read the expected nominative al-muqīmūn . [Translator’s note: These are reports of textual history; the received reading is accusative.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_162-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_162-s2","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"","text":"Not every person among the People of the Book belongs to the earlier condemned classes. Some have deep familiarity with earlier Scripture, such as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām and Mukhayrīq, and others in the same communities sincerely accept Muḥammad. They believe in what was sent to him and in preceding revelations without dividing the messengers, establish prayer properly, pay obligatory alms, and accept bodily resurrection and judgment and the doctrinal matters transmitted by the Qurʾān and Sunna. They receive abundant recompense. On another parsing “those rooted in knowledge” denotes learned people of earlier Scripture while “the believers” refers to believing Arabs, with the other qualifications describing the latter.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_162-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_162-s3","r":"q4_cont_162","title":"","text":"Whoever truly repents of past disobedience, wakes from heedlessness and becomes firmly grounded in knowledge of God, His attributes and His names, is joined to those who have preceded on the spiritual path and raised with the brought-near. Such people receive a tremendous reward. Praise belongs to God, Lord of the worlds. The next passage answers the demand for a book descending whole from heaven.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_162-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_163","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation 4:163–165","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_163"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-1","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"إِنَّا أَوْحَيْنا إِلَيْكَ كَما أَوْحَيْنا إِلى نُوحٍ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ وَأَوْحَيْنا إِلى إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْباطِ وَعِيسى وَأَيُّوبَ وَيُونُسَ وَهارُونَ وَسُلَيْمانَ وَآتَيْنا داوُدَ زَبُوراً (163) وَرُسُلاً قَدْ قَصَصْناهُمْ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَرُسُلاً لَمْ نَقْصُصْهُمْ عَلَيْكَ وَكَلَّمَ اللَّهُ مُوسى تَكْلِيماً (164) رُسُلاً مُبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنْذِرِينَ لِئَلاَّ يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَى اللَّهِ حُجَّةٌ بَعْدَ الرُّسُلِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَزِيزاً حَكِيماً (165)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-2","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"قلت: من قرأ (زبورًا) بالفتح، فالمراد به كتاب الزبور، ومن قرأ بالضم، فجمع «زِبر» بكسر الزاي وسكون الباء، بمعنى مزبورًا، أي: مكتوبًا، أي: آتينا داود كتبًا متعددة، و (رسلاً) : منصوب بمحذوف دل عليه «أوحينا» ، أي: أرسلنا رسلاً، أو يفسره ما بعده، أي: قصصنا عليك رسلاً، و (رسلاً مبشرين) : منصوب على البدل، أو على المدح، أو بإضمار أرسلنا، أو على الحال الموطئة لما بعده، كقولك: مررت بزيد رجلاً صالحاً.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-3","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّا أَوْحَيْنا إِلَيْكَ يا محمد كَما أَوْحَيْنا إِلى نُوحٍ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ ولم يكن ينزل عليهم الكتاب جملة واحدة، كما سألك أهل الكتاب تعنيتًا، بل كان ينزل عليهم الوحي شيئًا فشيئًا، فأمرك كأمرهم. وقدَّم نوحًا عليه السلام لأنه أبو البشر بعد آدم، وأول نبي من أنبياء الشريعة، وأول نذير على الشرك، وأول رسول عُذبت أمته بدعوته، وأطول الأنبياء عُمرًا، وجُعلت معجزته في نفسه، فإنه عمَّر ألف سنة، ولم تنقص له سن، ولم تنقص له قوة، ولم تشب له شعرة، ولم يبالغ أحد في تأخير الدعوة ما بالغ هو عليه السلام، ولم يصبر أحدٌ على أذى قومه ما صبر هو، كان يُشتم ويُضرب حتى يغمى عليه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-4","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"ثم قال تعالى: وَأَوْحَيْنا إِلى إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْماعِيلَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْباطِ أي: الأحفاد، وهم أنبياء بني إسرائيل، وَعِيسى وَأَيُّوبَ وَيُونُسَ وَهارُونَ وَسُلَيْمانَ، وإنما خصهم بالذكر مع اشتمال النبيين عليهم تعظيمًا لهم، فإن إبراهيم أولُ أُولي العزم منهم، وآخرهم عيسى عليه السلام، والباقون أشراف الأنبياء ومشاهيرهم، وَآتَيْنا داوُدَ زَبُوراً أي: كتاب الزبور، أو زُبورًا أي: صحفًا متعددة، وأرسلنا رُسُلًا قَدْ قَصَصْناهُمْ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ أي: من قبل هذه السورة، أو قبل هذا اليوم، وَرُسُلًا لَمْ نَقْصُصْهُمْ عَلَيْكَ، وفي الحديث:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-5","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"«عددُهم ثلاثمائة وأربعة عشر» ، وَكَلَّمَ اللَّهُ مُوسى تَكْلِيماً حقيقيًا، خُصَّ به من بين الأنبياء، وزاد نبينا محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم بالرؤية مع الكلام.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-6","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"قال الورتجبي: بادر موسى عليه السلام من بين الأنبياء لسؤال الرؤية، فأوقفه الحق في مقام سماع كلامه، ومنعه من مشاهدة رؤيته صرفًا، وتحمل نبينا محمد صلّى الله عليه وسلم أثقال السر بمطايا أسراره، ولم يسأل مشاهدة الحق جهرًا بالانبساط، فأوصله الله إلى مقام مشاهدته، ثم أسمعه كلامه بلا واسطة ولا حجاب. قال تعالى: فَأَوْحى إِلى عَبْدِهِ مَآ أَوْحى مَا كَذَبَ الْفُؤادُ ما رَأى","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-7","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":". هـ. وقال ابن عطية: كلامه تعالى لموسى دون تكييف ولا تحديد، وكما أنَّ الله تعالى موجود لا كالموجودات معلوم لا كالمعلومات، فكذلك كلامه لا كالكلام. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-8","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"ثم ذكر حكمة إرسال الرسل فقال: أرسلنا رُسُلًا مُبَشِّرِينَ وَمُنْذِرِينَ لِئَلَّا يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَى اللَّهِ حُجَّةٌ بَعْدَ بعث الرُّسُلِ فيقولون: لولا أَرْسَلْتَ إِلَيْنَا رَسُولاً ينبهنا ويعلمنا ما جهلنا من أمر توحيدك والقيام بعبوديتك،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-9","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"فقطع عذر العباد ببعث الرسل، وقامت الحجة عليهم، وفى الحديث عنه- عليه الصلاة والسلام-: «مَا أحدٌ أغيرَ مِنَ الله، ولذلكَ حرَّم الفواحِشَ ما ظهر منها وما بَطَنَ، وما أحدٌ أحبَّ إليهِ المدحُ من الله، ولذلكَ مدَحَ نفسَهُ، وما أحَدٌ أحبَّ إليهِ العذرُ مِنَ الله تعالى، ولذلِكَ أرسَلَ الرسل وأنزَلَ الكُتبَ» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-10","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَزِيزاً لا يغلب، فلا يجب عليه شيء، حَكِيماً فيما دبر من النبوة، وخص كل نبي بنوع من الوحي والإعجاز على ما يليق به في زمانه. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-11","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"الإشارة: علماءُ هذه الأمة كأنبياء بني إسرائيل، العارفون منهم كالرسل منهم، قال ابن الفارض رضي الله عنه:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-12","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"فَعَالِمُنَا منهم نبي، ومَن دَعَا ... إلى الحقِّ منّا قَامَ بالرسليّة [١]","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-13","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"وعارِفنا في وقتِنا الأحمَديُّ من ... أولي العزمِ منهم آخِذٌ بالعَزِيمَة","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-14","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"فإنهم يشاركونهم في وحي الإلهام، ويحصل لهم المكالمة مع المشاهدة، فيسمعون من الحق كما ينطقون به. كما قال الششتري:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-14"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-15","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"أنَا بالله أنطق ... ومن الله أسمَع","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-15"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-16","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"فتارة يسمعون كلامه بالوسائط، وتارة من غير الوسائط، يعرف هذا أهل الفن من أهل الذوق، وشأن مَن لم يَبلُغ مقامهم: التسليم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-16"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-17","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"إن لم ترَ الهلالَ فسَلِّم ... لأناس رَأوه بالأبصَارِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-17"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-18","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"وفي الورتجبي: وإن الله تعالى إذا أراد أن يُسمع كلامه أحدًا من الأنبياء والأولياء يعطيه سمعًا من أسماعه، فيسمع به كلامه، كما حكى- عليه الصلاة والسلام- عنه- تعالى-، قال: (فإذا أحببتُه كنت سمعه....) ، الحديث.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-18"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-19","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"أسمعه كلامه، وليس هناك الحروف والأصوات، بل أسمعه بحرف القدرة وصوت الأزلية، الذي هو منزه عن همهمة الأنفاس وخطرات الوسواس، وليس في ولاية الأزل من رسوم أهل الآجال شيء، حتى هناك السامع والمسمع واحد من حيث المحبة، لا من حيث الجمع والتفرقة. انتهى كلامه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-19"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-20","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"واعلم أن أهل الجمع لا يشهدون إلا متكلمًا واحدًا، قد انتفى من نظرهم التعدد والاثنينية، غير أنهم يفرقون بين كلام القدرة وكلام الحكمة، كلام القدرة يبرز من غير اختيار، بل يكون المتكلم به مأخوذًا عنه، غائبًا عن اختياره،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-20"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-21","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"وكلام الحكمة معه ضرب من الاختيار، وقد يسمعون كلام القدرة من الهواتف الغيبية، ومن الجمادات على وجه الكرامة، وكله بحرف وصوت. نعم ما يقع من الهواتف القلبية والتجليات الباطنية، قد يكون بلا حرف ولا صوت، وقد تحصل لهم المكالمة بالإشارة بلا صوت ولا حرف، فقوله: (بل أسمعه بحرف القدرة وصوت الأزلية ... ) الخ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-21"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-22","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"إن أراد به التجليات الباطنية فمسلَّم، لكن ظاهره أن كلام الحق الذي يُسمعه لأنبيائه وأوليائه محصور في ذلك، وأنه لا يكون إلا بلا حرف ولا صوت. وليس كذلك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-22"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-23","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"وقوله: (وليس في ولاية الأزل من رسوم أهل الآجال شيء) الخ، معناه: لم يبق في ولاية أهل مشاهدة الأزل من رسوم الحوادث شيء. قلت: لكنهم يثبتونها حكمةً، ويمحونها قدرةً ومشاهدة، ولا يلزم من محوها عدم صدور الكلام منها بالحرف والصوت فإن البشرية لا تطيق سماع كلام الحق بلا واسطة الحكمة، كما هو معلوم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-23"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-24","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-24"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_163-25","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"4:163–165 · The continuity of prophetic revelation","text":"ثم شهد لرسوله بالوحى والرسالة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_163-25"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_163-s1","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"","text":"I say: those reading zabūran with an open initial vowel refer to the Psalter as one book, whereas zubūran , with a rounded vowel, is understood as the plural of zibr —something written—thus implying several writings given to David. “Messengers” in the accusative may depend upon a suppressed verb indicated by “We revealed,” i.e. “We sent messengers,” or be explained by “We have narrated to you.” “Messengers bearing good news” can be appositional, accusative in praise, governed by an implicit “We sent,” or a preparatory circumstantial qualification for the words that follow, as when one says, “I passed Zayd, a righteous man.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_163-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_163-s2","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"","text":"God's revelation to Muḥammad resembles His revelation to Noah and later prophets; their scriptures did not necessarily descend as completed books at a single instant, despite the People of the Book's challenge. Revelation came piece by piece. Noah is named first, says Ibn ʿAjība, because he was humanity's ancestor after Adam, the first prophet of revealed law and the first to warn against associating partners with God, the first messenger whose community was punished in response to his prayer, and the prophet of exceptional longevity and patience. His very longevity was miraculous: Ibn ʿAjība transmits the description of a thousand-year life without loss of teeth, strength or hair colour, and of great endurance under insults and blows from his people. Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob and the asbāṭ (the Israelite tribal descendants), Jesus, Job, Jonah, Aaron and Solomon are named with special honour though all belong to the wider prophetic class. Abraham is described as the first of their prophets of firm resolve ( ulū l-ʿazm ) and Jesus as the last; the others are distinguished and famous. God gave David the Psalter or written leaves. Many messengers have been narrated already, while others remain unnamed; a report is quoted assigning them a number of 314. [Translator’s note: This number is presented as a transmitted report.] God spoke to Moses with actual divine address. Ibn ʿAjība understands this as a special distinction of Moses and adds that Muḥammad received both speech and vision. Al-Wartajbī's inward comparison says Moses hastened to request vision and was held at the station of hearing His speech and barred from unalloyed witnessing of His vision, whereas Muḥammad patiently bore the weight of spiritual secrets without demanding a public manifestation and was brought to witnessing and to speech heard without a mediating veil. He cites the verses of Sūrat al-Najm: “He revealed to His servant what He revealed; the heart did not falsify what it saw” (53:10–11). Ibn ʿAṭiyya affirms God’s speech to Moses without assigning it a modality or limit: God exists without resembling existents, is known without resembling known things, and speaks without His speech resembling created speech. Messengers announce good and warn of evil, removing people's plea that they were never told about divine unity and the responsibilities of servanthood. Ibn ʿAjība cites the Prophetic report: “No one is more jealous than God, and for this reason He forbids indecencies, outward and inward. No one loves praise more than God, and for this reason He praises Himself. No one loves an excuse more than God Most High, and for this reason He sends messengers and reveals books.” God is mighty and under no external compulsion; His wisdom determines the forms of prophethood, revelation and miraculous sign appropriate for each messenger's time.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_163-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_163-s3","r":"q4_cont_163","title":"inspiration, divine address and witnessing","text":"The scholars of this community are compared analogically to Israel's prophets, and among them the knowers of God ( ʿārifūn ) to the messengers, because they guide people toward truth. [Translator’s note: This analogy does not confer new prophethood or legislative revelation.] Ibn al-Fāriḍ says: Our scholar is a prophet among them, and whoever calls to the Real from among us discharges the messenger’s task. Our gnostic in this Aḥmadan age of ours is among their people of firm resolve, holding fast to resolute purpose. They share with the prophets in the revelation of inspiration ( waḥy al-ilhām ) and can, according to the Sufi testimony he records, experience inward divine address joined to witnessing. Al-Shushtarī sings: Through God I speak; from God I hear. Some hearing comes through intermediaries and some without them, understood by those who have tasted these states. Those without experience are asked not to deny reflexively: If you do not see the crescent, accept the word of those who have seen it with their own eyes. Al-Wartajbī says that when God wills a prophet or saint to hear divine speech He grants the person a hearing from His hearings, as in the divine saying “When I love him, I become his hearing...” He lets him hear His speech: there are no letters or sounds there. Rather, He lets him hear through the “letter of power” and the “voice of eternity,” which is beyond the murmuring of breaths and the stirrings of insinuation. He also speaks of the unity of the hearer and the One who makes him hear in the aspect of love, not from the standpoint of gathering and separation ( jamʿ wa-tafriqa ). Ibn ʿAjība then adds an important qualification rather than merely repeating al-Wartajbī. People of gathered vision ( jamʿ ) witness but one true Speaker, multiplicity and duality having vanished from their vision. Nonetheless they distinguish the discourse of divine power ( kalām al-qudra ) from the discourse of wisdom ( kalām al-ḥikma ). Speech of power bursts forth without the human speaker's discretionary control, as the speaker is seized in a state beyond ordinary choice; speech of wisdom accompanies an exercise of agency. Those in such states may, as a karāma , hear the speech of power through extraordinary unseen voices or inanimate things, in ways involving audible letters and sounds. Inward prompts arising in the heart and hidden divine disclosures can also be wordless and soundless, or communicable through indication alone. Accordingly Ibn ʿAjība accepts al-Wartajbī's account where it concerns purely inward disclosures, but disputes any suggestion that all speech God allows His prophets and saints to hear must be without letters or sounds. The statement that nothing belonging to the temporal world remains within the “realm of eternity” means, for Ibn ʿAjība, that no traces of temporally originated things remain in the realm of those who witness eternity. They remain affirmed at the level of divine wisdom while effaced in the vision of divine power. Such effacement does not prevent human speech from being uttered and heard with letters and sounds: human nature cannot bear hearing the speech of the Real without the mediation of wisdom. God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_163-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_166","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation","text":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation 4:166","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_166"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_166-1","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation","text":"لكِنِ اللَّهُ يَشْهَدُ بِما أَنْزَلَ إِلَيْكَ أَنْزَلَهُ بِعِلْمِهِ وَالْمَلائِكَةُ يَشْهَدُونَ وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ شَهِيداً (166)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_166-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_166-2","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation","text":"قلت: (لكن) : حرف استدراك، وهو عن مفهوم ما تقدم، وكأنه قال: إنهم لا يشهدون بوحينا إليك. لكن الله يشهد بذلك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_166-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_166-3","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في الرد على اليهود لما قالوا للنبى صلّى الله عليه وسلم: لا نشهد لك بما أوحى إليك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_166-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_166-4","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation","text":"فقال تعالى: لكِنِ اللَّهُ يَشْهَدُ بِما أَنْزَلَ إِلَيْكَ إن لم يشهدوا به، أَنْزَلَهُ بِعِلْمِهِ أي: متلبسًا بعلمه الخاص به، وهو العلم بتأليفه على نظم يعجز عنه كل بليغ. أو متلبسًا بعلمه الذي يحتاج الناس إليه في معاشهم ومعادهم. أو بعلمه المتعلق بمن يستأهل نزول الكتب إليه، وَالْمَلائِكَةُ أيضًا يشهدون بذلك. وفيه تنبيه على أن الملائكة يودُّون أن يعلم الناس صحة دعوى النبوة، على وجه يستغني عن النظر والتأمل، وهذا النوع من خواص الملك، ولا سبيل للإنسان إلى العلم بأمثال ذلك، سوى التفكر والنظر، فلو أتى هؤلاء بالنظر الصحيح لعرفوا نبوتك، وشهدوا بها كما عرفت الملائكة وشهدوا. قاله البيضاوي، وقد يخلق الله العلم في قلب الإنسان من غير تفكر ولا نظر، بل هداية من المالك القدير. وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ شَهِيداً لرسوله عن شهادة غيره.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_166-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_166-5","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation","text":"الإشارة: كما شهد الحق تعالى لرسوله بالنبوة والرسالة، شهد لمن كان على قدمه من ورثته الخاصة بالولاية والخصوصية، وهم الأولياء العارفون بالله، وشهادته لهم بما أظهر عليهم من العلوم اللدنية والأسرار الربانية، وبما أتحفهم به من الأخلاق النبوية والمحاسن البهية، وبما أظهر على أيديهم من الكرامات الظاهرة مع الاستقامة الشرعية، لكن لا يدرك هذه الشهادة إلا مَن سبقت له العناية، وكان له حظ فى الولاية. «سبحان مَن لم يجعل الدليل على أوليائه إلا من حيث الدليل عليه! ولم يوصل إليه إلاّ مَن أراد أن يوصله إليه» وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_166-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_166-6","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"4:166 · God’s witness to the revelation","text":"ثم ذكر وعيد من أعرض عن هذه الشهادة، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_166-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_166-s1","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"","text":"I say: lākin marks a correction of what the previous discourse implies—as if it said, “They refuse to acknowledge your revelation; yet God acknowledges it.” The Prophet's opponents among certain Jews are reported to have said they would not testify that revelation had come to him. If they withhold their acknowledgment, God's own testimony and that of the angels suffice. “With His knowledge” may mean that the Qurʾān embodies a special divine knowledge, including an inimitably ordered composition beyond any eloquent human capacity; or that it provides knowledge people need for life and the hereafter; or that it was revealed with God's knowledge of the person fit to receive Scripture. The angels’ testimony indicates that they wish people to know the truth of the claim to prophethood in a way that dispenses with reflection and deliberation. [XV-N003] This kind of knowledge is characteristic of angels. Al-Bayḍāwī says that human beings have no way to know such matters except through thought and reflection: had these opponents reasoned correctly, they would have recognized your prophethood and testified to it, as the angels recognized it and testified. Ibn ʿAjība adds that God can also create knowledge in a human heart directly, without preceding argument, through free guidance. God's testimony is enough without anyone else's assent.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_166-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_166-s2","r":"q4_cont_166","title":"","text":"Just as God bears witness to the Messenger's prophethood, He bears witness to the special heirs of the Messenger who attain sanctity and recognition of God. The signs are divinely given sciences, profound inward secrets, luminous Prophetic manners, fine moral qualities, and extraordinary graces accompanied by fidelity to the revealed law. Such testimony is recognised only by those granted a share of prior divine care. Ibn ʿAjība cites the Ḥikam : “Glory to the One who made the evidence of His saints none other than the evidence of Himself, and who leads to Him none except whom He wishes to lead.” God gives success.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_166-s2"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_167","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"4:167–169 · Disbelief, obstruction and distant wandering","text":"4:167–169 · Disbelief, obstruction and distant wandering 4:167–169","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_167"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_167-1","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"4:167–169 · Disbelief, obstruction and distant wandering","text":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَصَدُّوا عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ قَدْ ضَلُّوا ضَلالاً بَعِيداً (167) إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَظَلَمُوا لَمْ يَكُنِ اللَّهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ طَرِيقاً (168) إِلاَّ طَرِيقَ جَهَنَّمَ خالِدِينَ فِيها أَبَداً وَكانَ ذلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ يَسِيراً (169)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_167-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_167-2","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"4:167–169 · Disbelief, obstruction and distant wandering","text":"قلت: (خالدين) : حال مقدرة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_167-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_167-3","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"4:167–169 · Disbelief, obstruction and distant wandering","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بما أنزلت على رسولنا من اليهود أو غيرهم، وَصَدُّوا الناس عن طريق الله الموصلة إليه، قَدْ ضَلُّوا ضَلالًا بَعِيداً لأنهم جمعوا بين الضلال والإضلال، ولأن المضل يكون أغرق في الضلال وأبعد عن الانقلاع. إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَظَلَمُوا الناس بصدهم عما فيه صلاحهم وخلاصهم، أو ظلموا رسول الله بإنكار نبوته وكتمان صفته، أو ظلموا أنفسهم بالانهماك في الكفر، لَمْ يَكُنِ اللَّهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ طَرِيقاً، إِلَّا طَرِيقَ جَهَنَّمَ خالِدِينَ فِيها أَبَداً، فجرى حكمه السابق ووعده الصادق على أن مَن مات على الكفر مخلد في النار، وَكانَ ذلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ يَسِيراً لا يصعب عليه ولا يتعاظمه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_167-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_167-4","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"4:167–169 · Disbelief, obstruction and distant wandering","text":"الإشارة: إِنَّ الذين كفروا بالخصوصية وأنكروا على أهلها، وصدوا الناس عن القصد إليها والدخول في حزبها قد ضلوا عن طريق الوصول ضلالاً بعيدًا، إذ لا وصول إلى الله إلا على يد أولياء الله لأنهم باب الحضرة، فلا بد من الأدب معهم والخضوع لهم. إن الذين كفروا بأولياء الله، وظلموا أنفسهم حيث حرموها الوصول، وتركوها في أودية الخواطر تَجُول، لم يكن الله ليستر مساوئهم ويقدس سرائرهم، ولا ليهديهم طريق المشاهدة ولا كيفية المجاهدة، وإنما يمكنهم من طريق التعب والنصب حتى يلقوا الله بقلب سقيم، والعياذ بالله.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_167-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_167-5","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"4:167–169 · Disbelief, obstruction and distant wandering","text":"ولما قرر أمر النبوة، وبيّن الطريق الموصل إلى العلم بها، وأوعد من أنكرها، خاطب الناس بالدعوة إليها فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_167-5"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_167-s1","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"","text":"I say: khālidīn (“abiding”) is a circumstantial accusative ( ḥāl muqaddara ), a condition anticipated with reference to their future abode.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_167-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_167-s2","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"","text":"God, exalted is His majesty, says: Those who disbelieve in what He sent down upon His Messenger, whether Jews or others, and obstruct people from God's path, which leads to Him, have gone far astray. Their error is grave because they combine going astray themselves with causing others to go astray. One who misguides is more deeply immersed in error and further from casting it off. Those who disbelieve and commit injustice may be understood as wronging other people by barring them from what would set them right and save them; or as wronging the Messenger by denying his prophethood and concealing the descriptions identifying him; or as wronging themselves through immersion in disbelief. God does not forgive them or guide them to a path other than that of Hell, where they remain for ever. His preceding judgment and truthful promise concern the one who dies in disbelief : it is that condition at death that Ibn ʿAjība explicitly specifies when he speaks of abiding in the Fire. Such judgment is neither difficult nor imposing for God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_167-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_167-s3","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"","text":"Those who deny the khuṣūṣiyya —the special spiritual distinction of the friends of God ( awliyāʾ )—condemn those who possess it, and obstruct others from seeking or entering their company have strayed far from the path of arrival ( wuṣūl ). Ibn ʿAjība says that there is no arrival at God except at the hands of God’s saints, for they are the door to the Divine Presence ( bāb al-ḥaḍra ), and approach to them requires courtesy ( adab ) and humility. [Translator’s note: This is his Sufi application of the verse, not a replacement of its outward subject.] Those who reject God's friends thereby wrong themselves and deprive themselves of arrival, leaving their hearts wandering through the valleys of passing thoughts ( khawāṭir ). They are not brought to the covering of faults, the sanctification of inward secrets, the path of direct witnessing ( mushāhada ), or knowledge of spiritual striving ( mujāhada ). Instead they remain on the way of exhaustion and toil, until they encounter God with an ailing heart. God is the refuge from such a condition.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_167-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_167-s4","r":"q4_cont_167","title":"","text":"After establishing the matter of prophethood, showing the way by which it is known and warning those who deny it, Ibn ʿAjība says the discourse turns to a universal summons to believe in the Messenger.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_167-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_170","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons 4:170","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_170"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-1","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جاءَكُمُ الرَّسُولُ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ فَآمِنُوا خَيْراً لَكُمْ وَإِنْ تَكْفُرُوا فَإِنَّ لِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً حَكِيماً (170)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-2","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"قلت: (فآمنوا خيرًا لكم) ، و (انتهوا خيرًا لكم) : قال سيبويه: هو منصوب بفعل مضمر، تقديره: وائتوا خيرًا لكم، وقال الخليل: منصوب بآمنوا وبانتهوا على المعنى. أي: اقصدوا. وقال الفراء: صفة لمصدر، أي: آمنوا إيمانًا خيرًا لكم. وقال بعض الكوفيين: هو خبر كان المحذوفة، وتقديره: ليكن الإيمان خيرًا لكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-3","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"قلت: وهو أظهر من جهة المعنى، وإن منعه البصريون، قالوا: لأنَّ (كان) لا تحذف مع اسمها إلا في مواضع مخصوصة، قال ابن مالك:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-4","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"ويحذفونها ويُبقُون الخبَر ... وبَعدَ إن، ولو، كثِيرًا ذا اشتَهر","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-5","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"ولعل هذا الموضع أتى على غير المشهور تنبيهًا على الجواز.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-6","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جاءَكُمُ الرَّسُولُ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وهو محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم، فَآمِنُوا به يكن خَيْراً لَكُمْ مما أنتم فيه من الضلال، وَإِنْ تَكْفُرُوا فَإِنَّ لِلَّهِ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وما تركبتا منه، ملكًا وخلقًا وعبيدًا، فهو غني عنكم، لا يتضرر بكفركم، كما لا ينتفع بإيمانكم، وَكانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيماً بأحوالكم، حَكِيماً فيما دبر لكم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-7","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"الإشارة: الذي جاء به الرسول- عليه الصلاة والسلام- هو إتقان مقام الإسلام، وتصحيح مقام الإيمان، الذي من أركانه: الإيمان بالقدر خيره وشره، حلوه ومره، وتحقيق مقام الإحسان الذي هو مقام الشهود والعيان، ولا يكمل هذا إلا بصحبة أهل العرفان، الذين صححوا مقام الفناء، وخرجوا إلى البقاء، خاضوا بحار التوحيد، وانفردوا بأسرار التفريد، ورسخ فيهم مقام الرضى والتسليم، فتلقوا المقادير كلها بقلب سليم، فمن لم يصحبهم ويتأدب بآدابهم بقي إيمانه ناقصًا، وحقه العتاب، فكأن الحق- تعالى- يقول على لسان الإشارة: قد جاءكم وليي، وهو خليفة رسولي، فآمنوا بخصوصيته، وأذعنوا لأمره وتربيته، يكن خيرًا لكم مما أنتم فيه من المساوئ والأمراض، لئلا تلقوني بقلب سقيم، وبالله التوفيق.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_170-8","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"4:170 · The Messenger and the universal summons","text":"ثم خص أهل الكتاب بالخطاب والعتاب، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_170-8"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_170-s1","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"","text":"I say: the expressions fa-āminū khayran lakum (“so believe—it is better for you”) and, in the next verse, intahū khayran lakum (“desist—it is better for you”) present a problem concerning the accusative khayran . Sībawayh explains it through an omitted verb: “come to that which is better for you.” Al-Khalīl connects the accusative with the command “believe” or “desist” through its sense: “seek/aim at what is better.” Al-Farrāʾ takes it as an adjective of an understood verbal noun: “believe with a believing better for you.” Certain Kūfan grammarians make it the predicate of an elided kāna : “let belief be better for you.” Ibn ʿAjība calls the last interpretation the clearest in meaning, though the Baṣrans object that kāna is not normally omitted with its subject except under specified conditions. He adduces Ibn Mālik's grammatical verse: “They omit it, leaving the predicate; after in and law , this is well known.” Perhaps the construction here departs from what is most familiar in order to signal the possibility of such ellipsis. [Translator’s note: The discussion records competing grammatical accounts; Ibn ʿAjība gives his preference above.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_170-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_170-s2","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"","text":"God's Messenger, Muḥammad—God bless him and give him peace—has come bearing truth from the Lord. Belief in him would be better than the error in which his hearers presently stand. If they choose denial, everything contained in and constituted by the heavens and the earth belongs to God in ownership, creation and servanthood. God needs nothing from them: their unbelief does not injure Him, just as their faith does not benefit Him. He knows their conditions and is wise in what He ordains for them.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_170-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_170-s3","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"","text":"What the Messenger brought includes the perfecting of the station of islām , the rectification of the station of īmān —among whose foundations is belief in destiny, its good and evil, its sweet and bitter—and the realisation of the station of iḥsān , which is the station of beholding and direct witnessing ( shuhūd wa-ʿiyān ). The full realisation of this, says Ibn ʿAjība, requires companionship with the people of experiential knowledge ( ahl al-ʿirfān ). They have rectified the station of passing away ( fanāʾ ) and emerged into abiding ( baqāʾ ); they have ventured into the seas of unity ( tawḥīd ) and become singularly devoted to the secrets of making-one ( tafrīd ). The stations of contentment and surrender ( riḍā wa-taslīm ) have become firm within them, so that they meet every divine apportionment with an unharmed heart. Without keeping company with them and being formed by their manners, a person's faith remains, in Ibn ʿAjība's assessment, incomplete and liable to admonition. He then reformulates the Qurʾānic address in the language of allusion , as though God were saying, “My friend, the successor to My Messenger, has come to you: acknowledge his particular spiritual distinction, yield to his direction and training; that would be better for you than the defects and illnesses in which you live, lest you encounter Me with an unsound heart.” [Translator’s note: This is an analogical Sufi application, not an assertion that a saint possesses the Messenger’s legislative status.] Success comes through God.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_170-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_170-s4","r":"q4_cont_170","title":"","text":"Having addressed all people, the Qurʾān next addresses and admonishes the People of the Book in particular.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_170-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_171","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit 4:171","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_171"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-1","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ لا تَغْلُوا فِي دِينِكُمْ وَلا تَقُولُوا عَلَى اللَّهِ إِلاَّ الْحَقَّ إِنَّمَا الْمَسِيحُ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ وَكَلِمَتُهُ أَلْقاها إِلى مَرْيَمَ وَرُوحٌ مِنْهُ فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَلا تَقُولُوا ثَلاثَةٌ انْتَهُوا خَيْراً لَكُمْ إِنَّمَا اللَّهُ إِلهٌ واحِدٌ سُبْحانَهُ أَنْ يَكُونَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ لَهُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلاً (171)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-2","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"قلت: أصل الغلو: مجاوزة الحد في كل شيء، يقال: غلا بالجارية لحمها وعظمها، إذا أسرعت إلى الشباب فجاوزت لداتها أي: أقرانها، تغلو غلوًا.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-3","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في عتاب النصارى- بدليل ما بعده: يا أَهْلَ الْكِتابِ الإنجيل لا تَغْلُوا فِي دِينِكُمْ فتجاوزوا الحد فيه باعتقادكم في عيسى أنه الله، أو ابن الله، قصدوا تعظيمه فغلوا وأفرطوا، وَلا تَقُولُوا عَلَى اللَّهِ إِلَّا الْحَقَّ، وهو تنزيه عن الصاحبة والولد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-4","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"ثم بيَّن الحق فيه فقال: إِنَّمَا الْمَسِيحُ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، لا كما قالت اليهود: ليس برسول، ولا كما قالت النصارى: إنه الله، أو ابن الله، وإنما هو عبد الله ورسوله، وَكَلِمَتُهُ أَلْقاها إِلى مَرْيَمَ أي:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-5","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"أوصلها إليها وحصلها فيها، وهي كلمة: كن. فَتَكَوّنَ بها في رحم أمه فسمى بها، وَرُوحٌ مِنْهُ وهو نفخ جبريل في جيبها فحملت بذلك النفخ، وسمي النفخ روحًا لأنه ريح يخرج عن الروح، فكانت روحه صادرة من روح القدس، كما قال فى آدم: نَفَخْتُ فِيهِ مِنْ رُوحِي، وقد قال: إِنَّ مَثَلَ عِيسى عِنْدَ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ آدَمَ، فنفخ جبريل في الحقيقة لما كان بأمر الله صار هو نفخ الحق لأن الواسطة محذوفة عند المحققين، فلذلك أضاف روحه إليه كروح آدم عليه السّلام.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-6","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ أي: وحدوا الله في إلوهيته، وَلا تَقُولُوا ثَلاثَةٌ أي: الآلهة ثلاثة: الله، والمسيح، ومريم، انْتَهُوا عن التثليث يكن خَيْراً لَكُمْ إِنَّمَا اللَّهُ إِلهٌ واحِدٌ في ذاته وصفاته وأفعاله، سُبْحانَهُ أي: تنزيهاً له أن يكون له ولد، لأنه لا يجانس ولا يتطرقه الفناء، لَهُ ما فِي السَّماواتِ وَما فِي الْأَرْضِ، مُلكاً وخلقا وعبيدا، والعبودية تنافي البُنوة، وَكَفى بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلًا فلا يحتاج إلى ولد لأن الولد يكون وكيلاً عن أبيه وخليفته، والله تعالى قائم بحفظ الأشياء كافٍ لها، مستغن عمن يعينه أو يخلفه لوجوب بقائه وغناه.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-7","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"واعلم أن النصارى انقسموا على أربع فرق: نسطورية، ويعقوبية، وملكانية، ومرقوسية، ومنهم نصارى نجران، فالنسطورية، قالوا في عيسى هو ابن الله، واليعقوبية، والملكانية، قالوا هو الله، والمرقوسية قالوا: هو ثالث ثلاثة، وكلهم ضالون.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-8","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"الإشارة: الغلو كله مذموم، وخير الأمور أوساطها، وقد قال عليه الصلاة والسلام: «لا تطروني كما أطرت النّصارى عيسى بن مَريم، ولكن قولوا: عَبدُ اللهِ وَرَسُوله» ، ويرخص للفقير أن يتغالى في مدح شيخه، ما لم يخرجه عن طوره، أو ينتقص غيره بمدحه، وفي الإشارة حث على حفظ مقام التوحيد، وتنزيهه تعالى عن الأضداد والأنداد. وفي ذلك يقول الشاعر:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-9","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"أرَبٌّ وعَبدٌ ونَفى ضِدٍ ... قلتُ لَهُ: لَيسَ ذَاكَ عِندِي","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-10","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"فَقَالَ ما عِندَكُم؟ فقُلنَا: ... وُجُودُ فَقدٍ وفَقدُ وُجد","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-11","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"فإثبات العبودية مستقلة تضاد الربوبية، ولذلك أنكرها الشاعر، أي: أثبت ربًا وعبدًا، وأنت تقول بنفي الضد عنه وفي الحكم: «الأكوان ثابتة بإثباته ممحوة بأحدية ذاته» .","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-12","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"ولما قالت نصارى نجران للنبي صلّى الله عليه وسلم: إنك تعيب صاحبنا؟ فقال- عليه الصلاة والسلام- ومن صاحبكم؟ قالوا:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_171-13","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"4:171 · Jesus as messenger, Word, and spirit","text":"عيسى. قال: وأي شيء أقول؟ قالوا: تقول إنه عبد الله. قال لهم- عليه الصلاة والسلام- «ليس بعارٍ أن يكون عيسى عبدا لله» ، أنزل الله تعالى:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_171-13"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_171-s1","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"","text":"I say: the root of ghulūw is passing beyond the limit in anything. The Arabs say that a young girl has rapidly advanced in flesh and bone beyond those of her age when she has quickly attained adolescence and outstripped her contemporaries; the verb is ghalā–yaghlū–ghulūwan . The grammatical explanation of khayran lakum (“better for you”) was given under the preceding verse.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_171-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_171-s2","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"","text":"The rebuke is addressed, in view of what follows, to Christians among the People of the Gospel. They are forbidden to exaggerate religion by transgressing its bounds and regarding Jesus as God or the son of God: intending to honour him, they carried their praise beyond its proper limit. They are not to say anything about God except the truth, which includes proclaiming Him exalted above a consort and offspring. The Messiah, Jesus son of Mary, is God's messenger—not, as Ibn ʿAjība reports the Jewish denial, one who is no messenger, and not, as he describes the Christian affirmation, God or God's son. He is God's servant and messenger. He is God's Word cast to Mary: the divine command “Be!” was conveyed and realised within her, and through it he was formed in her womb; for this reason he is designated the Word. He is a “spirit from Him” through Gabriel's breathing into the opening of Mary's garment, through which she conceived. The breath is called rūḥ , as a moving breath issuing from a living spirit, and Jesus' spirit is connected with the Holy Spirit's breath. Ibn ʿAjība invokes the parallel with Adam: “I breathed into him of My Spirit,” and “The likeness of Jesus with God is as the likeness of Adam.” In reality, since Gabriel breathed by God's command, the action may be ascribed to God Himself: for those with realised vision the intermediary is effaced in relation to the divine originating command. It is thus in this respect that Jesus' spirit, like Adam's, is attributed to God. [Translator’s note: This language is not being understood here as establishing shared divinity.] “Believe in God and His messengers” means maintaining the uniqueness of God in His deity. “Do not say ‘Three’” excludes a plurality of gods. Here Ibn ʿAjība paraphrases the three as God, the Messiah and Mary, then insists upon divine unity of essence, attributes and acts. [Translator’s note: This is Ibn ʿAjība’s polemical representation of Christian doctrine; it does not describe the Nicene formulation of Father, Son and Holy Spirit.] God is free from having a child: nothing shares His genus, extinction cannot touch Him, and everything in heaven and earth belongs to Him as creation, property and servants. Servanthood is inconsistent with the sonship Ibn ʿAjība has in view. God needs no heir or representative, whereas a human son may succeed or act for a father; God Himself maintains all things and needs neither helper nor successor because He necessarily endures and is absolutely independent. Ibn ʿAjība inserts a historical taxonomy, dividing Christians into Nestorians, Jacobites, Melkites and “Marqūsites,” adding the Christians of Najrān. He ascribes to Nestorians a formulation of Jesus as son of God, to Jacobites and Melkites his being God, and to “Marqūsites” the assertion that he is the third of three; he judges them all in error. [Translator’s note: These labels and formulations are the author’s assertions; their accuracy as descriptions of the named communities’ historical doctrines is unestablished.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_171-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_171-s3","r":"q4_cont_171","title":"","text":"All excess is blameworthy, for the best of matters is the middle way. Ibn ʿAjība cites the Prophetic instruction: “Do not exaggerate in praising me as the Christians exaggerated in praising Jesus son of Mary; rather say, ‘God's servant and messenger.’” A Sufi disciple ( faqīr ) may be allowed elevated language in praising his shaykh only so long as it does not remove the shaykh from his true created station or demean others through the praise. The deeper purpose is to guard the station of divine unity and to proclaim God beyond opposites and rivals. A poet says: “A Lord and a servant, and denial of an opposite? / I said to him: ‘That is not my view.’ / He asked: ‘What do you hold?’ We replied: / ‘The existence of loss, and the loss of existence.’” If independent and self-subsisting creaturely being were posited over against Lordship, that would establish an opposite to it; that is what the poet rejects. Ibn ʿAjība cites the Ḥikam : “Created things subsist through His establishing them and are effaced through the oneness of His Essence.” [Translator’s note: This is understood here as concerning creaturely dependence in the vision of divine unity; the distinction governing religious obligation and practice is not being denied.] A narrative follows: when the Christians of Najrān reportedly protested that the Prophet disparaged their master Jesus, he asked whom they meant. Told that it was Jesus and that they objected to his calling Jesus the servant of God, he replied, “It is no dishonour that Jesus be a servant of God.” Ibn ʿAjība introduces the next verse as revealed in this connection. [Translator’s note: The narrative is reproduced as a report in the commentary; its chain and historical circumstances are unestablished.]","anchor":"en-q4_cont_171-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_172","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks 4:172–173","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_172"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-1","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"لَنْ يَسْتَنْكِفَ الْمَسِيحُ أَنْ يَكُونَ عَبْداً لِلَّهِ وَلا الْمَلائِكَةُ الْمُقَرَّبُونَ وَمَنْ يَسْتَنْكِفْ عَنْ عِبادَتِهِ وَيَسْتَكْبِرْ فَسَيَحْشُرُهُمْ إِلَيْهِ جَمِيعاً (172) فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ فَيُوَفِّيهِمْ أُجُورَهُمْ وَيَزِيدُهُمْ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ اسْتَنْكَفُوا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوا فَيُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذاباً أَلِيماً وَلا يَجِدُونَ لَهُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَلِيًّا وَلا نَصِيراً (173)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-2","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"قلت: أصل الاستنكاف: التنحية، من قولهم: نكفت الدمع إذا نحيته بإصبعك كي لا يُرى أثره عليك، ثم أُطلق على الأنفة، والاستكبار دون الاستنكاف، ولذا عطف عليه لأن الاستنكاف لا يستعمل إلا حيث لا استحقاق، بخلاف الاستكبار فإنه يكون باستحقاق. قاله البيضاوي.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-3","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله في الرد على النصارى: لَنْ يَسْتَنْكِفَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-4","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"أي: لن يأنفْ الْمَسِيحُ أَنْ يَكُونَ عَبْداً لِلَّهِ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-5","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"فإن عبوديته لله شرف يتباهى بها، وإنما المذلة والاستنكاف في عبوديته لغيره، وَلَا الْمَلائِكَةُ الْمُقَرَّبُونَ","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-6","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"لا يستنكفون أيضًا أن يكونوا عبيدًا لله، بل ما كانوا مكرمين إلا بعبوديتهم لله، واحتج بالآية مَن فَضَّل الملائكة على الأنبياء، لأن المعطوف يقتضي أن يكون أرفع درجة من المعطوف عليه، حتى يكون عدم استنكاف الملائكة كالدليل على عدم استنكاف المسيح.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-7","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"والجواب: أن عطف الملائكة إنما أريد به التكثير والمبالغة، كقولهم: أصبح الأمير اليوم لا يخالفه رئيس ولا مرؤوس، والرئيس أفضل من المرءوس، والتحقيق في المسألة أنَّ الأنبياء والرسل أفضل من خواص الملائكة كالمقربين، وخواص الملائكة- وهم المقربون- أفضل من خواص البشر كالأولياء، وخواص البشر أفضل من عوام الملائكة، وعوام الملائكة أفضل من عوام البشر، ولذلك قيل: من غلب عقله على هواه، كان كالملائكة أو أفضل، ومن غلَب هواه على عقله، كان كالبهائم أو أضل. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-7"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-8","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"ثم ذكر وعيد من استنكف عن عبوديته- تعالى- فقال: وَمَنْ يَسْتَنْكِفْ عَنْ عِبادَتِهِ وَيَسْتَكْبِرْ فَسَيَحْشُرُهُمْ إِلَيْهِ جَمِيعاً","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-8"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-9","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"فيجازيهم فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ ولم يستنكفوا عن عبادته فَيُوَفِّيهِمْ أُجُورَهُمْ وَيَزِيدُهُمْ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ مالا عين رأت ولا أُذن سمعت، ولا خطر على قلب بشر، وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ اسْتَنْكَفُوا عن عبوديته وَاسْتَكْبَرُوا عن عبادته فَيُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذاباً أَلِيماً أي: مُوجعًا، وهو النار، وقال القشيري: العذاب الأليم: هو ألا يصلوا إليه أبدًا بعد ما عرفوا جلاله، إذ صارت معرفتهم ضرورية- أي قهرية- فحسراتهم حينئذ على ما فاتهم أشدُّ عقوبة لهم. هـ. وَلا يَجِدُونَ لَهُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَلِيًّا وَلا نَصِيراً.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-9"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-10","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"فإن قلت: هذا التفصيل أعم من المفصل، لأن الحشر إنما ذكر للمتكبرين والتفصيل أعم، فالجواب: أن عموم المفصل يفهم من قوة الكلام، فكأنه قال: فسيحشرهم للمجازاة يوم يجازي عباده جميعًا، فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا ...","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-10"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-11","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"الخ، نظيره: قولك: جمع الأمير كافة مملكته، فأما العلماء فأكرمهم، وأما الطغاة فقطعهم. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-11"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-12","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"الإشارة: العبودية أشرف الحالات وأرفع المقامات، بها شرف من شرف، وارتفع من ارتفع، عند الله، وما خاطب الله أحباءه إلا بالعبودية، فقال تعالى: سُبْحانَ الَّذِي أَسْرى بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا، وقال: وَاذْكُرْ عِبادَنا إِبْراهِيمَ وَإِسْحاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ، وَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنا داوُدَ، وَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنا أَيُّوبَ، نِعْمَ الْعَبْدُ إِنَّهُ أَوَّابٌ ... إلى غير ذلك.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-12"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-13","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"وأوصاف العبودية أربعة: الذل، والفقر، والضعف والجهل. ومقابلها من أوصاف الربوبية أربعة: العز، والغنى والقوة والعلم، فبقدر ما يظهر العبد من أوصاف العبودية يمده الحق من أوصاف الربوبية، فبقدر ما يظهر العبد من الذل يمده من العز، وبقدر ما يظهر من الفقر يمده بالغنى، وبقدر ما يظهر من الضعف يمده من القوة، وبقدر ما يظهر من الجهل يمده من العلم، تحقق بوصفك يُمدك بوصفه، ولا يتحقق ظهور هذه الأوصاف إلا بين عباده لتمتحق بذلك أوصاف النفس.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-13"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_172-14","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"4:172–173 · Servanthood, angels, and its four marks","text":"ثم دعا الكل إلى كتابه والإيمان برسوله، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_172-14"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_172-s1","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"","text":"I say: istinkāf , “refusing out of disdain,” originally refers to moving something away: one says nakaftu l-damʿ , “I wiped away the tears with my finger,” so that their trace could not be seen. It subsequently denotes proud distaste. Al-Bayḍāwī says istikbār (self-exaltation) is less intense than istinkāf , which is why it is conjoined to it. Istinkāf is used only where there is no entitlement, whereas istikbār may occur where there is entitlement. These are al-Bayḍāwī's lexical distinctions as cited by Ibn ʿAjība.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_172-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_172-s2","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"","text":"Against those who exalt Jesus beyond servanthood, God declares that the Messiah never recoils from being God's servant. Indeed, his servanthood is the honour in which he may glory; humiliation would be servitude to someone other than God. Neither do the angels brought near recoil from such servanthood: their dignity is rooted precisely in serving Him. Some theologians invoked the coordination of the angels after Jesus in this verse to argue that angels are superior to prophets: they said an additional member in such a construction should signify a higher rank, so that the angels' lack of disdain confirms all the more strongly that Jesus cannot disdain servanthood. Ibn ʿAjība responds that the conjunction may instead serve amplification and generalisation. One says, ‘Today neither chief nor subordinate disobeys the prince,’ even though the chief has the higher rank; the conjunction does not entail a ranking of its second member above its first. He then gives what he considers the sound ranking: prophets and messengers outrank the specially favoured or “near” angels; these special angels outrank specially favoured humans, the saints; such humans outrank ordinary angels, who outrank ordinary humanity. Thus one who subordinates appetite to intellect may be like the angels or above them, whereas one in whom appetite dominates intellect may be like cattle or further astray. Ibn ʿAjība ends the comparison with “God knows best.” [Translator’s note: This theological ordering is reported from the commentary; a universal consensus is unestablished.] God warns the one who rejects servanthood arrogantly that all will be gathered for divine recompense. Those whose belief expresses itself in sound works, and who do not recoil from His worship, receive their wages in full, with an increase of grace beyond what eye has seen, ear heard or mind conceived. Those who reject worship through disdain and arrogance receive a painful punishment, understood in the outward commentary as the Fire; no protecting ally or helper will then be found apart from God. Al-Qushayrī offers an inward elaboration: for such people an even more painful punishment is never to arrive in God's Presence after His majesty has become known to them by an unavoidable, overpowering knowledge. Their regrets over what they have missed are then their most severe punishment. Ibn ʿAjība raises a grammatical and argumentative objection. The threat of being gathered initially concerns the arrogant, but the subsequent distribution of recompense covers all people, including the believers. He replies that the wider scope is already implicit in the force of the statement: they will be gathered for recompense on the day when God recompenses all His servants. Thus a ruler may assemble his whole kingdom, honouring the scholars and cutting the tyrants off. [Translator’s note: Cairo I:598 prints fa-qaṭaʿahum , “so he cut them off,” without specifying the punitive act. Al-Zamakhsharī on 4:173 offers a related illustrative contrast: an imam rewards those who did not rebel and punishes those who did. It explains the distribution of recompense between two groups; it does not establish the exact physical or political act intended by Ibn ʿAjība’s different verb. The translation therefore preserves that lack of specification.] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_172-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_172-s3","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"the four marks of servanthood","text":"ʿUbūdiyya (servanthood) is the most noble condition and the highest station: through it the honoured become honourable and the exalted are raised. God addresses His beloved servants only by their servanthood: “Glory to Him who carried His servant by night,” “Remember Our servants Abraham, Isaac and Jacob,” “Remember Our servant David,” and “Remember Our servant Job—what an excellent servant; he ever turns back,” among other examples. Ibn ʿAjība names four qualities of servanthood: abasement ( dhull ), poverty ( faqr ), weakness ( ḍaʿf ) and ignorance ( jahl ) . Opposed to them are four predicates of Lordship: dignity or might ( ʿizz ), riches or freedom from need ( ghināʾ ), strength ( quwwa ) and knowledge ( ʿilm ). In the measure that a servant manifests the qualities of servanthood, the Real supplies him from the qualities of Lordship: to the acknowledgment of abasement, dignity; to poverty, sufficiency; to weakness, power; and to ignorance, knowledge. “Realise your proper description, and He will support you with His description.” The manifestation of these qualities, he adds, is realised only among God’s servants , so that the attributes of the ego may thereby be effaced.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_172-s3"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_172-s4","r":"q4_cont_172","title":"","text":"The discourse turns from the dignity of servanthood to a universal invitation to God's scripture and His Messenger.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_172-s4"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_174","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path","text":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path 4:174–175","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_174"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_174-1","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path","text":"يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جاءَكُمْ بُرْهانٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وَأَنْزَلْنا إِلَيْكُمْ نُوراً مُبِيناً (174) فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَاعْتَصَمُوا بِهِ فَسَيُدْخِلُهُمْ فِي رَحْمَةٍ مِنْهُ وَفَضْلٍ وَيَهْدِيهِمْ إِلَيْهِ صِراطاً مُسْتَقِيماً (175)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_174-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_174-2","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جاءَكُمْ بُرْهانٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ وهو الرسول عليه الصلاة والسلام وما اقترن به من المعجزات الواضحات، وَأَنْزَلْنا إِلَيْكُمْ على لسانه نُوراً مُبِيناً وهو القرآن. أو جاءكم برهان من ربكم: المعجزات الظاهرة، وَأَنْزَلْنا إِلَيْكُمْ نُوراً مُبِيناً: القرآن العظيم، أي: جاءكم دليل العقل وشواهد النقل، فلم يبق لكم عذر ولا علة.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_174-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_174-3","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path","text":"فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ أي: وحدوه في ربوبيته، وَاعْتَصَمُوا أي: تمسكوا بدينه أو بكتابه، فَسَيُدْخِلُهُمْ فِي رَحْمَةٍ مِنْهُ وهي الجنة، وَفَضْلٍ: النظر لوجهه الكريم، قال البيضاوي: فِي رَحْمَةٍ أي: ثواب قدّره بإزاء إيمانه وعمله، رحمة منه، لا قضاء لحق واجب، وفضل إحسان زائد عليهما. هـ. وقال القشيري: سيحفظ عليهم إيمانهم في المآل عند التوفي، كما أكرمهم به وبالعرفان في الحال. هـ. وَيَهْدِيهِمْ إِلَيْهِ أي: إلى الوصول إليه، صِراطاً مُسْتَقِيماً أي: يبيّن لهم الوصول إليه، وهو طريق السير الذي لا عوج فيه العلم والعمل والحال، وقال البيضاوي: هو الإسلام والطاعة في الدنيا، وطريق الجنة في الآخرة. هـ.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_174-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_174-4","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path","text":"الإشارة: قد جاءكم من يُعرفكم بالله، ويدلكم على الله، وهم أولياء الله، ببرهان واضح لا يخفى إلا على من كان خفاشيًا، وأنزلنا إليكم من سر قُدسنا، وبحر جبروتنا، نورًا مبينًا، تُشاهدون فيه أسرار الذات وأنوار الصفات، وهو ما ظهر من التجليات من القبضة الأولية المحمدية، فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَاعْتَصَمُوا بِهِ في حال سيرهم إليه فَسَيُدْخِلُهُمْ فِي رَحْمَةٍ مِنْهُ وهي حضرة القدس، (وفضل) وهو الترقي في أسرار المعارف إلى مالا نهاية له،","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_174-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_174-5","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path","text":"ويهديهم إلى الوصول إليه، وهو شهوده في ذلك النور، طريقا مستقيما توصل إليه في أقرب زمان. ولعل الآية فيها تقديم وتأخير، أي: فسيهديهم إليه طريقًا مستقيمًا يسيرون فيه، حتى يصلوا إليه، ثم يدخلهم في رحمة حضرته، وفضل زيادة معرفته. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_174-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_174-6","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"4:174–175 · Proof, manifest light and the straight path","text":"ثم ختم السورة بميراث الكلالة، لأن آخر أحوال الإنسان الموت فيورث ماله، وكان المناسب ذكر يوصيكم هنا، لكنه أدرجه فى حفظ الأموال لكونه أنسب، فقال:","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_174-6"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_174-s1","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"","text":"The burhān (proof) may be the Messenger—God bless him and grant him peace—together with his evident miracles, while the manifest nūr (light) sent down through his tongue is the Qurʾān. Alternatively the proof refers particularly to the outward miracles, the manifest light to the mighty Qurʾān. Both rational indication and the attestations of transmission ( dalīl al-ʿaql wa-shawāhid al-naql ) have come; no valid excuse or pretext remains for rejecting them. Those who affirm God's uniqueness in Lordship and cling to His religion or His Book will be brought into mercy from Him. Ibn ʿAjība identifies this mercy with the Garden and the additional “bounty” with the vision of His generous Face. He quotes al-Bayḍāwī: mercy is the recompense appointed for belief and deeds, but it is bestowed as mercy, not the settlement of some debt or right binding on God. Bounty is a further divine beneficence over and above the appointed recompense. Al-Qushayrī takes the promised favour to include God's preserving their faith at the time of death, just as He honours them now with belief and intimate knowledge ( ʿirfān ). “He will guide them to Himself” promises arrival and shows the way of approach. The straight path without crookedness is the path of journeying comprising knowledge, work and inward condition ( ʿilm, ʿamal, ḥāl ). Al-Bayḍāwī explains it as Islam and obedience in this life and the route to Paradise in the hereafter.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_174-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_174-s2","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"","text":"Those who show the way to knowing God and indicate the route to Him are God's friends, the awliyāʾ . They bear a proof clear to those fit to perceive it, though hidden, says Ibn ʿAjība, to someone with the sight of a bat. From the secret of holiness and the ocean of divine power ( jabarūt ) there descends a manifest light wherein the secrets of the divine Essence and the lights of the divine attributes are witnessed. This light is what has appeared of the self-disclosures ( tajalliyāt ) from the first Muḥammadan grasp ( al-qabḍa al-awwaliyya al-muḥammadiyya ). Those who believe and hold fast while journeying toward God will be admitted to the mercy of the holy Presence ( ḥaḍrat al-quds ) and to an additional bounty: perpetual progress in the endless mysteries of spiritual knowledge ( maʿārif ). They are guided into arrival through beholding Him within the light, by a straight path that brings them to Him in the shortest time. Ibn ʿAjība suggests a possible inversion in the order of expression: perhaps the intended sequence is that God guides them first upon a straight way, so that they travel it and arrive; thereafter He admits them into the mercy of His Presence and the bounty of increased knowledge. He offers this tentatively: “God knows best.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_174-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_174-s3","r":"q4_cont_174","title":"","text":"The chapter ends with the inheritance of kalāla , because death is the last condition of a human life, after which property passes to heirs. Ibn ʿAjība observes that “God instructs you concerning your children” could appropriately have been mentioned here, but was included in the discussion of preserving property because that was more fitting.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_174-s3"},{"kind":"passage","id":"q4_cont_176","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession 4:176","anchor":"unit-q4_cont_176"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_176-1","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"يَسْتَفْتُونَكَ قُلِ اللَّهُ يُفْتِيكُمْ فِي الْكَلالَةِ إِنِ امْرُؤٌ هَلَكَ لَيْسَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ وَلَهُ أُخْتٌ فَلَها نِصْفُ ما تَرَكَ وَهُوَ يَرِثُها إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَها وَلَدٌ فَإِنْ كانَتَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُمَا الثُّلُثانِ مِمَّا تَرَكَ وَإِنْ كانُوا إِخْوَةً رِجالاً وَنِساءً فَلِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْأُنْثَيَيْنِ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ أَنْ تَضِلُّوا وَاللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (176)","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_176-1"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_176-2","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"قلت: (في الكلالة) ، يتعلق بيفتيكم، ويستفتونك، فيكون من باب التنازع، وأعمل الثاني على اختيار البصريين، وعمل الأول في الضمير المجرور حذف، أي: يستفتونك فيها، أو عمل الأول وحذف ضمير الثاني، أو يكون يستفتونك مقطوعًا فيوقف عليه، أو حُذف متعلقه لدلالة الجواب عليه، أي: يستفتونك في الكلالة، وهو أظهر، وتقدم تفسير الكلالة [١] ، إِنِ امْرُؤٌ هَلَكَ: ارتفع بفعل مضمر عند البصريين، من باب الاشتغال في المرفوع.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_176-2"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_176-3","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"يقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يَسْتَفْتُونَكَ في الكلالة، والمستفتِي هو جابر بن عبد الله، كان مريضًا فعاده رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فقال: يا رسول الله. إني كلالة، فكيف أصنع في مالي؟ فنزلت، وهي آخر ما نزل من الأحكام.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_176-3"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_176-4","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"قُلِ اللَّهُ يُفْتِيكُمْ فِي الْكَلالَةِ، ثم بيَّن الفتوى فيها فقال: إِنِ امْرُؤٌ هَلَكَ لَيْسَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ ولا والد، بل انقطع نسبه من الجهتين، وَلَهُ أُخْتٌ شقيقة أو لأب فَلَها نِصْفُ ما تَرَكَ والباقي للعصبة، ولا ميراث لها مع الأب أو الابن، وَهُوَ يَرِثُها إن ماتت ولم يكن لها ولد ولا والد.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_176-4"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_176-5","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"فإن استقل فله المال، وإن كان معه ذو سهم أخذ الباقي، فَإِنْ كانَتَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فأكثر شقائق فَلَهُمَا الثُّلُثانِ مِمَّا تَرَكَ، وإن كانت شقيقة مع الأب أخذت الشقيقة النصف، والتي لأب السدس تكملة الثلثين، وإن كانت لأب","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_176-5"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_176-6","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"مع الشقيقتين فلا شيء لها، وَإِنْ كانُوا إِخْوَةً رِجالًا وَنِساءً شقائق، مات أخوهم، فَلِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْأُنْثَيَيْنِ، ولا شيء للأخوة لأب من الشقائق. يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ الحق، كراهية أَنْ تَضِلُّوا، وَاللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ فهو عالم بمصالح العباد في المحيا والممات. اللهم أحينا حياة طيبة وأمتنا موتة حسنة، في عافية وستر جميل، يا أرحم الراحمين، يا رب العالمين.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_176-6"},{"kind":"arabic","id":"ar-q4_cont_176-7","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"4:176 · The inheritance of kalāla; spiritual succession","text":"الإشارة: الكلالة من الأولياء، هو الذي مات ولم يخلف ولدًا يرث حاله، فإن لم تكن له تلاميذ، فإن كان له أخ يقارب حاله، ورثه، وقد يرث سره أخته في النسبة، لكن لا تستوجب ذلك كله لحكمة الله تعالى. يشير إليه قوله تعالى: فَلَها نِصْفُ ما تَرَكَ، وإن ترك إخوة في الشيخ اقتسموا سره كله، كلٌ على قدر صِدقه، والنساء الصادقات شقائق الرجال في نيل أسرار الولاية. وقد تقدم أول السورة أن مدد الشيخ كنهر أو كبحر يصب في القواديس، فإذا انسدت قادوس انتقل ماؤها إلى الأُخرى. والله تعالى أعلم.","anchor":"ar-q4_cont_176-7"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_176-s1","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"","text":"I say: the phrase fī l-kalāla (“concerning kalāla ”) can relate to both yastaftūnaka (“they seek a ruling from you”) and yuftīkum (“He gives you a ruling”), making the construction an instance of grammatical tanāzuʿ , two governors competing over a complement. On the preferred Baṣran construction the second verb exercises government while the pronominal complement required by the first is omitted: the sense is “they seek a ruling from you about it .” Alternatively, the first verb may govern and the second omit its pronoun; or “They seek a ruling from you” may stand as a complete expression with a pause; or the relation to the first may simply be understood from the answer. The last, that they are asking about kalāla , appears most straightforward to Ibn ʿAjība. He refers back to his earlier explanation of the term. In in imruʾun halaka (“if a man dies”), the nominative imruʾun is analysed by Baṣran grammarians through a suppressed verb in a construction resembling ishtighāl , anticipation of the expressed verb by an omitted governing expression.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_176-s1"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_176-s2","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"","text":"The inquirer, Ibn ʿAjība says, was Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who fell ill and received a visit from the Messenger—God bless him and grant him peace. He said, “Messenger of God, I am a kalāla : how should I dispose of my property?” The verse was revealed, and Ibn ʿAjība calls it the last of the legal rulings to be revealed. [Translator’s note: The central episode of Jābir’s illness and inheritance question is attested in al-Bukhārī 6743 and Muslim 1616a; Muslim explicitly cites 4:176. Separately, al-Bukhārī 4605 transmits al-Barāʾ’s statement that 4:176 was the final verse revealed. The latter is a Companion’s chronological report; it does not establish agreement among all transmitted chronologies. See source checks XII-S033–034.] God gives the requested determination: if a man dies without a child or father , so that his direct line is absent in both directions, but has one full sister or paternal half-sister, she receives half his estate; the rest belongs to the legally entitled residuary agnates ( ʿaṣaba ). She inherits nothing in the presence of a father or son. Conversely, a brother inherits his sister's estate if she dies without a child or father. If there is no other share-holder, he takes all; if someone has a prescribed portion ( dhū sahm ), he takes what remains. If there are two or more full sisters, they share two-thirds of the estate. Where there is one full sister and one sister through the father, the full sister receives one-half and the paternal half-sister one-sixth, completing two-thirds. [Translator’s note: The printed text reads شقيقة مع الأب , literally ‘a full sister with the father.’ This translation supplies ‘a sister through’ before ‘the father,’ as indicated by the following allocation to ‘the one through the father’; the supplied wording is not what the copytext prints. Mālik’s Muwaṭṭaʾ , Book of Inheritances, chapter on paternal siblings, confirms the stated allocation: a sole full sister receives half and the paternal sister or sisters receive the complementary sixth. This confirms the legal case, not an independently attested correction of Ibn ʿAjība’s wording.] A paternal half-sister does not inherit in the case envisaged when two full sisters have already taken the two-thirds. If the deceased leaves full brothers and sisters, the male receives twice the portion of the female. Ibn ʿAjība then says that paternal half-siblings have no portion where full brothers and sisters take priority in the case described. [Translator’s note: The copytext prints من الشقائق , literally ‘from/of the full siblings.’ The English understands this as referring to their presence in the preceding case; it does not reproduce an explicit printed ‘with.’ Mālik’s Muwaṭṭaʾ , Book of Inheritances, chapter on paternal siblings, confirms that a male full sibling excludes the paternal siblings in this case. The likely sense is thus supported, but مع الشقائق (“with the full siblings”) remains a conjectural replacement of the printed preposition, not an independently verified authorial reading.] [Translator’s note: These statements are Ibn ʿAjība’s compact explanation of particular cases. Their application in actual estates requires the complete roster of heirs, precise kinship, impediments, residuary relationships and the legal school’s detailed rules.] The conclusion says God makes the truth manifest so that people may not go astray, for He knows the welfare of servants in life and after death. Ibn ʿAjība concludes with a supplication: “O God, grant us a good life and a good death, in well-being and under Your gracious covering, O Most Merciful of the merciful, Lord of the worlds.”","anchor":"en-q4_cont_176-s2"},{"kind":"english","id":"en-q4_cont_176-s3","r":"q4_cont_176","title":"heirs to the saintly secret","text":"Among the awliyāʾ , the one who dies as kalāla is the saint who leaves no spiritual child to inherit his inward condition: he has no disciples in whom the state has been transmitted. If he has a spiritual brother close to his own station, the brother inherits it. A “sister” in the spiritual affiliation ( nisba ) can also inherit some of his secret; according to God’s wisdom, she is not entitled to all of it; Ibn ʿAjība points to the Qurʾānic allotment of half as indicating this. When he leaves fellow disciples who are brothers in allegiance to the same shaykh, they divide his entire spiritual secret, each according to the sincerity ( ṣidq ) with which he receives it. Sincere women, Ibn ʿAjība expressly says, are the counterparts of sincere men in their capacity to attain the mysteries of sainthood ( wilāya ). He recalls the image introduced earlier in the sūra: the spiritual aid ( madad ) of the shaykh resembles a river, or a sea, pouring into water channels; when one channel becomes blocked, its flow passes to another. [Translator’s note: The legal ending is thus interpreted as an image of the transmission of spiritual realisation.] God knows best.","anchor":"en-q4_cont_176-s3"}];
